अङ्गद|अंगद|अंगदं|अङ्गदं|अङ्गदः
अङ्गद अङ्ग-द (vb. 3. दा).<BR> I. n. A bracelet.<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्गद|चित्राङ्गदः
चित्र- + अङ्गद चित्र- + अङ्गद, 1. adj. adorned with splendid or variegated bracelets. 2. m. a proper name. 3. f. दा, a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन|अंगन|अंगनं|अङ्गनं
अङ्गन अङ्ग् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A passage.<BR> 2. A court.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाङ्गन|रणांगन
रण- + अङ्गन रण- + अङ्गन, n. a field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गना|अंगना
अङ्गना अङ्गना (cf. अङ्ग), f.<BR> 1. A beautiful woman.<BR> 2. A woman in general.<BR> 3. The female of any animal.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाङ्गना|कुलांगना
कुल- + अङ्गना कुल- + अङ्गना, f. a chaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गना|वरांगना
वर- + अङ्गना वर- + अङ्गना, f. a lovely woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरुह|अंगरुह
अङ्गरुह अङ्ग-रुह् + अ, n. Hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविद्या|अंगविद्या
अङ्गविद्या अङ्ग-विद्या, f.<BR> 1. Such learning as is comprehended under the title अङ्ग, viz. pronunciation, grammar, prosody, explanation of obscure terms, description of religious rites, and astronomy, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 6.<BR> 2. Palmistry, Man. 6, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहीनत्व
अङ्गहीनत्व अङ्ग-हीन + त्व (vb. 2. हा), n. Defect of some limb; Man. 11, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गार|अंगार|अंगारं|अंगारः|अङ्गारः
