अङ्गारक|अंगारक|अंगारकं|अंगारकः|अङ्गारकः
अङ्गारक अङ्गार + क, m.<BR> 1. The planet Mars.<BR> 2. The name of a king.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गारक
स- + अङ्गारक स- + अङ्गारक, adj. attended by the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिन्|अंगिन्
अङ्गिन् अङ्गिन्, i. e. अङ्ग + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Having limbs.<BR> 2. Having expedients.<BR> 3. Chief.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गिन्
चतुर्- + अङ्गिन् चतुर्- + अङ्गिन्, (i. e. चतुरङ्ग + इन्), adj., f. इणी, consisting of four parts (Bhāg. P. 1, 10, 32, इनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिरस्|अंगिरस्
अङ्गिरस् अङ्गिरस्, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, or saint.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसोमाङ्गिरस्
तृण-सोम- + अङ्गिरस् तृण-सोम- + अङ्गिरस्, m. one of the seven priests attending a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकरण|अंगीकरण|अंगीकरणं
अङ्गीकरण अङ्गीकरण, i. e. 2. अङ्ग-कृ + अन, n. Agreement, consent, Vedāntas. in Chr. 213, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकार|अंगीकार|अंगीकारः|अङ्गीकारः
अङ्गीकार अङ्गीकार, i. e. 2. अङ्ग-कृ + अ, m. Agreement, Vedāntas. in Chr. 213, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरीयक|अंगुरीयक|अंगुरीयकं|अङ्गुरीयकं
अङ्गुरीयक अङ्गुरीयक = अङ्गुलीयक (q. cf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुल|अंगुल|अंगुलः|अङ्गुलः
अङ्गुल अङ्गुल (from a lost base, अङ्गु) m.<BR> 1. A finger's breadth as a linear measure.<BR> 2. A substitute for अङ्गुलि at the end of many comp. words: e. g. दशाङ्गुल, i. e. दशन्-, adj. Ten fingers long, Man. 8, 271.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुल|पंचांगुल|पञ्चाङ्गुलः
पञ्चाङ्गुल पञ्चाङ्गुल, i. e. पञ्चन्-, m. The castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलक
ऽअङ्गुलक -अङ्गुल + क, a substitute for अङ्गुल at the end of comp. words: षोडशाङ्गुलक, i. e. षोडशन्-, adj. Of sixteen fingers' breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलि|अंगुलि|अंगुलिः|अङ्गुलिः
अङ्गुलि and अङ्गुली अङ्गुली̆, f. A finger.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताङ्गुलि|लताङ्गुलिः
लता- + अङ्गुलि लता- + अङ्गुलि, f. a branch serving instead of a finger, Śiś. 9, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्र|अंगुलित्र
अङ्गुलित्र अङ्गुलि-त्र (vb. त्रा), n. A piece of leather or thin iron, worn by archers to prevent the fingers being injured by the bowstring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्रवन्त्|अङ्गुलित्रवत्
अङ्गुलित्रवन्त् अङ्गुलित्र + वन्त्, adj. Protected by the अङ्गुलित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीय|अंगुलीय|अंगुलीयं|अङ्गुलीयः
अङ्गुलीय अङ्गुलीय, i. e. अङ्गुलि + ईय, n. A finger-ring.<BR> --Cf. Lat. annulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीयक|अंगुलीयक|अंगुलीयकं|अङ्गुलीयकं
अङ्गुलीयक अङ्गुलीय + क, n. A finger-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठः|अङ्गुष्ठः
अङ्गुष्ठ अङ्गुष्ठ, i. e. अङ्गु-स्थ (cf. अङ्गुल), m.<BR> 1. The thumb.<BR> 2. The great toe.<BR> 3. A thumb's breadth as a measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्|अंघ्
† अङ्घ् अङ्घ्, i. 1. Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To begin moving.<BR> 3. To begin.<BR> 4. To hasten.<BR> 5. To blame.<BR> 6. To despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रि|अंघ्रि|अङ्घ्रिः
अङ्घ्रि अङ्घ्रि (akin to जङ्घा from जङ्घन्, the frequent. of हन्; the initial consonant is lost, as e. g. in इनक्ष् for निनस्क्ष् and others, and न् is changed to र्, as in पीवर् + ई fem. of पीवन्), m.<BR> 1. A foot.<BR> 2. The root of a tree.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णाङ्घ्रि|शीर्णांघ्रि|शीर्णाङ्घ्रिः
शीर्ण- + अङ्घ्रि शीर्ण- + अङ्घ्रि (vb. शॄ), m. Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचल|अचलः
अचल अ-चल.<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Immovable.<BR> 2. Steady, Pañc. 202, 19.<BR> II. m. A mountain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचल|कुलाचलः
कुल- + अचल कुल- + अचल, m. a principal mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनाचल|तुहिनाचलः
तुहिन- + अचल तुहिन- + अचल, m. Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाचल
महा- + अचल महा- + अचल, m. a great mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ अच्छ (akin to 1. अक्ष), adj., f. छा. Transparent, clear, Megh. 52.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
सु- + अच्छ सु- + अच्छ, adj. 1. transparent, 2. pure. 3. white. 4. healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्
अज् अज्, i. 1, Par., in the Vedas also Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To drive; to direct, Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. 1, 112, 16. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a " target="_blank">Page0008-a + 40</a>]<BR> --With the prepos. उद् उद्, To drive out, Chr. 297, 12 = Rigv. 1, 112, 12.<BR> --Cf. ἄγω, πράσσω (πραγ-ϳω); Lat. ago, igitur (for agitur); O.N. aka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
1. अज अ-ज, adj., f. जा. Unborn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
2. अज अज.<BR> 1. m. A he-goat.<BR> 2. f. जा. A she-goat.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. αἶξ of which the base is ἀγ + ι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाज|वनाजः
वन- + अज वन- + अज, m. a wild goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगर|अजगरः
अजगर अजगर, i. e. अज-गॄ + अ, m. A large serpent, Boa constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननि|अजननिः
अजननि अ-जन् + अनि, f. Privation of birth, used as imprecation, Pañc. i. d. 355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य|अजर्य्य|अजर्य्यं
अजर्य अ-जर्य (vb. जॄ), n. Friendship, Ragh. 18, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र अ-जस् + र, adj., f. रा. Continual. acc. रम्, adv. Continually, always, Man. 1, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात अ-जात (vb. जन्), adj., f. ता.<BR> 1. Unborn.<BR> 2. As former part of comp. adj., Not having, e. g. अजात-व्यञ्जन, adj. beardless.<BR> अजात-शत्रु. 1. Having no enemies. 2. One with whom nobody can contend; epithet and name of Yudhiṣṭhira and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाविक
अजाविक अजाविक, i. e. अज-अवि + क, n. sing. Goats and sheep, Man. 8, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिन|अजिनं
अजिन अजिन (perhaps derived from 2 अज), n. The hide of any animal, particularly of the black antelope, used as a covering, Man. 2, 64, as purse, Daśak. 191, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाजिन
कृष्ण- + अजिन कृष्ण- + अजिन, n. the hide of the black antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर अज् + इर, n. A court, Pañc. 138, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाजिर
रण- + अजिर रण- + अजिर, n. a field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मग|अजिह्मगः
अजिह्मग अ-जिह्म-ग.<BR> I. adj. Advancing in a straight path, Man. 6, 31.<BR> II. m. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्त|अजीगर्तः|अजीगर्त्त
अजीगर्त अजीगर्त, m. The name of a Ṛṣi or saint, Man. 10, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्णिन्
अजीर्णिन् अजीर्णिन्, i. e. अ-जीर्ण + इन् (vb. जॄ), adj. Suffering from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जुका अज्जुका, f.<BR> 1. A courtesan (Mṛcch. 27, 2, Prākṛ.; in the Ssk. translation अज्जू).<BR> 2. (in Prākṛ. अज्जू, and in the Ssk. translation अज्जुका, Śāk. p. 105, 3.) A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञता
अज्ञता अ-ज्ञ + ता, f. Ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्मन्
अज्मन् अज् + मन्, n. Battle, Chr. 297, 17 = Rigv. 1, 112, 17.<BR> --Cf. Lat. agmen; -αγμα in κάταγμα, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र|अज्रः
अज्र अज् + र, m. A field.<BR> --Cf. ἀγρός; Lat. ager; Goth. akrs; A.S. acer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च्|अंच्
अञ्च् अञ्च् (cf. अङ्क), i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To ask.<BR> 3. To speak indistiṅctly.<BR> 4. To bend, to curve, Nal. 12, 45.<BR> 5. To honour, Ragh. 9, 24.<BR> 6. i. 10 (rather Caus.). To make clear, to manifest, Gīt. 10, 11.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To rise, Rājat. 5, 362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चन
अञ्चन अञ्च् + अन, n. Bending, curving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चल|अंचलं|अंचलः|अञ्चलः
अञ्चल अञ्च् + अल, m. The end or border of a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्ज्|अंज्
अञ्ज् अञ्ज्, ii. 7, अनज्, अञ्ज्, Par. (Ved. also Ātm.). To cause to shine by smearing with greasy substances.<BR> 1. To anoint, to smear, Man. 5, 25.<BR> 2. To adorn, Chr. 294, 1 = Rigv. 1, 92, 1.<BR> 3. To make clear.<BR> 4. To be beautiful.<BR> 5. † To go.<BR> --Caus. To anoint, Man. 4, 44.<BR> --† i. 10. To shine.<BR> --With the prepos. अभि अभि. 1. To anoint, Man. 4, 44. 2. To pollute, Śāk. d. 108.<BR> --With वि वि. 1. Ātm. To dress one's self, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. 1, 64, 4. 2. To make clear, MBh. 2, 2122.<BR> व्यक्त. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a " target="_blank">Page0009-a + 45</a>] manifest, clear, Rām. 3, 73, 12.<BR> acc. sing. तम्, adv. to be sure, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR> acc. sing. तम्, adv. indistinctly, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 21.<BR> n. the primary Being, Ragh. 13, 60.<BR> --Caus. 1. To make discernible, Man. 1, 6. 2. To betray, Man. 10, 58. 3. To show, Rājat. 5, 107.<BR> व्यञ्जित, discerned, Man. 9, 36.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, 1. To discern clearly, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 23. 2. To reveal.<BR> अभिव्यक्त + म्, adv. evidently, Nal. 17, 8.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To adorn, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. 1, 64, 1.<BR> --Cf. Lat. unguere; O.H.G. anko, butter; and ἀγ in ἀγλαός, ἀγάλλω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं|अव्यक्तः
अ-व्यक्त अ-व्यक्त, adj. 1. invisible, Man. 1, 6. 2. imperceptible, Rām. 1, 70, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अंजनः|अञ्जनः
अञ्जन अञ्ज् + अन.<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Anointing, Man. 4, 152.<BR> 2. A collyrium or application to the eyelashes to darken and improve them, Man. 2, 178.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The elephant of the west or southwest quarter.<BR> 2. The name of a mountain.<BR> 3. A particular plant, Pañc. 10, 7.<BR> III. f. ना. The name of a female monkey, the mother of Hanumant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्जन|निरंजन|निरञ्जनः
निरञ्जन निरञ्जन, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ना, artless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाञ्जन|रसाञ्जनं
रस- + अञ्जन रस- + अञ्जन, n. a particular sort of collyrium, Śiś. 9, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलि|अंजलिः|अञ्जलिः
अञ्जलि अञ्जलि, m.<BR> 1. The cavity formed by putting the hands together and hollowing the palms, Man. 4, 63.<BR> 2. This cavity as measure: two handfuls.<BR> 3. Putting the hands together and raising them to the forehead, as humble salutation of inferiors to their superiors.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्जलि|उदंजलि
उद्- + अञ्जलि उद्- + अञ्जलि, adj. with uplifted hands, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाञ्जलि|कर्णांजलि|कर्णाञ्जलिः
कर्ण- + अञ्जलि कर्ण- + अञ्जलि, m. the auditory passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलि|कृतांजलि|कृताञ्जलिः
कृत- + अञ्जलि कृत- + अञ्जलि, adj. with humble salutation, Man. 4, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाञ्जलि|जलांजलि|जलाञ्जलिः
जल- + अञ्जलि जल- + अञ्जलि, m. 1. two handfuls of water in honour of a deceased relation. 2. farewell, resignation: जलाञ्जलिं दत्त्वा दुःकाय च सुखाय च, ‘having completely renounced sorrow and joy,’ Rājat. 4, 284. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b " target="_blank">Page0009-b + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माञ्जलि|ब्रह्मांजलि|ब्रह्माञ्जलिः
ब्रह्माञ्जलि ब्रह्माञ्जलि, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. 1. joining both hands together whilst reading the Vedas, Man. 2, 71. 2. paying obeisance to the spiritual preceptor at the beginning or end of a lecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसा|अंजसा
अञ्जसा अञ्जसा (instr. sing. of the Ved. अञ्ज् + अस्, n. Smoothness, slip), adv.<BR> 1. Straightforward, directly, Man. 2, 244.<BR> 2. Instantly, Vikr. d. 48.<BR> 3. Truly, Man. 8, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जि|अंजि|अञ्जिः
अञ्जि अञ्ज् + इ, m.<BR> 1. An ornament, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. 1, 64, 4.<BR> 2. The penis: cf. Lat. inguen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्
अट् अट्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 1586), To roam, with the loc. and acc. MBh. 1, 1031; Daśak. in Chr. 179, 6.<BR> --With the preposition परि परि, To wander about, Pañc. 55, 1.<BR> पुर्यटित, n. Wandering about, Pañc. 70, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटन|अटनं
अटन अट् + अन, n. Rambling, Man. 9, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाटन|भिक्षाटनं|भिक्षाटनः
भिक्षा- + अटन भिक्षा- + अटन, n. wandering about for begging alms, Pañc. 116, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनि|अटनिः
अटनि and अटनी अटनी̆, f. The notched extremity of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवी
अटवी अटवी (vb. अट्), f. A wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट्
† अट्ट् अट्ट्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To transgress.<BR> 2. To kill.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट अट्ट, m.<BR> 1. A room on the top of a house, a sollar.<BR> 2. A tower, Rām. 5, 56, 142.<BR> 3. As former part of some comp. words, High, lofty, loud. (cf. the next.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टपतिभागाख्य
अट्टपतिभागाख्य अट्टपतिभागाख्य, i. e. अट्ट-पति-भाग-आख्य, adj. Called the part of the great king, name of a government office, Rājat. 5, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहास|अट्टहासः
अट्टहास अट्ट-हास, m. A horse-laugh. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a " target="_blank">Page0010-a + 39</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्टहासम्
स-अट्टहास + म् स-अट्टहास + म्, adv. with a horse-laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाल|अट्टालः
अट्टाल अट्टाल (derived from अट्ट), m. A room on the top of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालक|अट्टालकः
अट्टालक अट्टाल + क, m. A tower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्या
अट्या अट् + या, f. Wandering about.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाट्या
वृथा- + अट्या वृथा- + अट्या, f. strolling about, Man. 7, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठ्
† अठ् अठ्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्
† अड् अड्, i. 1, Par. To strive or endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्ड्
† अड्ड् अड्ड्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To attack.<BR> 2. To connect.<BR> 3. To meditate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्
† अण् अण्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --i. 4, Ātm. To breathe (cf. अन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिमन्
अणिमन् अणिमन्, i. e. अणु + इमन्, m. Subtility; the superhuman power of making one's self infinitely small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणु|अणुः
अणु अणु.<BR> I. adj., f. णु and ण्वी.<BR> 1. Small, minute; अण्व् अपि, the least, Man. 3, 51.<BR> 2. Subtile, Hariv. 1241. Comparat. अणियंस्, very soft, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 22.<BR> II. m. An atom, Bhāṣāp. 35.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाणु|परमाणुः
परम- + अणु परम- + अणु, m. an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुत्व
अणुत्व अणु + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Smallness.<BR> 2. Condition of being an atom, Bhāṣāp. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुमात्रिक
अणुमात्रिक अणुमात्रिक, i. e. अणु-मात्र + इक, adj. Composed of atoms, Man. 1, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ठ्|अंठ्
† अण्ठ् अण्ठ्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ड|अंडं|अण्डं|अंडः|अण्डः
अण्ड अण्ड, n.<BR> 1. An egg.<BR> 2. A testicle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माण्ड|ब्रह्मांड|ब्रह्माण्डं
ब्रह्माण्ड ब्रह्माण्ड, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, n. the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाण्ड|मेषांड|मेषाण्डः
मेष- + अण्ड मेष- + अण्ड, m. Indra; see पूत्यण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डक|अंडकः|अण्डकः
अण्डक अण्ड + क, n.<BR> 1. A bird's egg.<BR> 2. An egg in general, Śiś. 9, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डज|अण्डजः
अण्डज अण्ड-ज.<BR> I. adj. Oviparous, Man. 1, 44.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bird.<BR> 2. A fish.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाण्डज|कालांडज|कालाण्डजः
काल- + अण्डज काल- + अण्डज, m. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्|अन्त्|अंत्
अत् अत्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To move continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतदर्ह|अतदर्हं
अतदर्ह अ-तद्-अर्ह, adj. Not deserving that, Rām. 2, 13, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रित|अतंद्रित
अतन्द्रित अतन्द्रित, i. e. अ-तन्द्रा + इत, adj., f. ता. Unwearied, not remiss. Man. 2, 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्क
अतपस्क अ-तपस् + क, adj. Impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस् अ + तस् (cf. इदम्), adv.<BR> 1. abl. of इदम्, From this, Man. 2, 213.<BR> 2. From this place.<BR> 3. From this time, then, now, Man. 5, 26.<BR> 4. From this reason, therefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति अति.<BR> I. adv. Over, exceedingly in a high degree, much. Comparat. अति + तराम्, very much, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217 10.<BR> II. prepos. with the acc. Over beyond, more than.<BR> III. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. Former part of compound nouns and adverbs, implying<BR> 1. Exceedingly, much, very: e. g. अति-गुरु, adj. very heavy; अति-काय, adj. having a very large body, gigantic<BR> 2. Too muc: e. g. अति-प्रणय, n. exorbitant love, Daśak. in Chr. 18, 10; अत्यश्नन्त्, i. e. अति- (vb. 2. अश्), adj. eating too much.<BR> 3. Surpassing the object denoted by the following part the comp. These comps. are generally: a) adj. e. g. अतीन्द्रिय, i. e. अति-, surpassing the senses, transcendental. b) adv., e. g. अति-मात्र + म् exceeding extraordinarily.<BR> --Cf. ἔτι; Lat. at in atavus, and et.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम|अतिक्रमः
अतिक्रम अति-क्रम् + अ, m. Transgression (of time), Pañc. 55, 5.<BR> 2. Violation, Man. 11, 120. Offence.<BR> 4. Irreverence, Man. 3, 63. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a " target="_blank">Page0011-a + 40</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरतिक्रम|दुरतिक्रमः
दुरतिक्रम दुरतिक्रम, i. e. दुस्-, adj. 1. hard to be overcome, unconquerable, Man. 11, 238. 2. difficult of accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमण|अतिक्रमणं
अतिक्रमण अतिक्रमण, i. e. अति-क्रम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Overstepping (of a boundary), Yājñ. 2, 155.<BR> 2. Transgression (of time), Pañc. i. d. 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमिन्
अतिक्रमिन् अति-क्रम् + इन्, adj., f. इणी. One who violates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग
ऽअतिग -अति-ग, adj.<BR> 1. Surpassing, (सर्व-लोक-,) Rām. 2, 19, 33.<BR> 2. Piercing, (देह-,) Ragh. 12, 48.<BR> --Cf. वयोतिग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथि|अतिथिः
अतिथि अतिथि (vb. अत्), m.<BR> 1. A guest.<BR> 2. The name of a king.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशातिथि|देशातिथिः
देश- + अतिथि देश- + अतिथि, m. a foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिग्व|अतिथिग्वः
अतिथिग्व अतिथिग्व, m. A name of Divodāsa, Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथित्व
अतिथित्व अतिथि + त्व, n. Hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिधर्मिन्
अतिथिधर्मिन् अतिथिधर्मिन्, i. e. अतिथि-धर्म + इन्, adj. Having the character of a guest, as guest, Man. 3, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदर्शिन्
अतिदर्शिन् अतिदर्शिन्, i. e. अति-दृश् + इन्, adj., f. नी. Seeing very far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेश|अतिदेशः
अतिदेश अतिदेश, i. e. अति-दिश् + अ, m. Extension, as e. g. of the signification of a word by analogy, Bhāṣāp. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिर्वसुत्व
अतिनिर्वसुत्व अतिनिर्वसुत्व, i. e. अति-निस्-वसु + त्व, n. Excessive poverty, Rājat. 6, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्ति|अतिपत्तिः
अतिपत्ति अति-पत् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Lapse (of time).<BR> 2. Unsuitableness, Yājñ. 2, 169 (देश-काल-अतिपत्तौ, ‘should time or place not permit’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात|अतिपातः
अतिपात अतिपात, i. e. अति-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Neglect, Śāk. 7, 10.<BR> 2. Hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातिन्
अतिपातिन् अतिपातिन्, i. e. अति-पत् + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b " target="_blank">Page0011-b + 38</a>] adj.<BR> 1. Outrunning.<BR> 2. Acute (as a disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभाव
अतिभाव अतिभाव, i. e. अति-भू + अ, m. Overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानिता
अतिमानिता अतिमानिता, i. e. अति-मानिन् + ता, f. Excessive self-conceit, Bhag. 16, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्त|अतिमुक्तः
अतिमुक्त अति-मुक्त (vb. मुच्), m. A large creeper, Gaertnera racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्तक|अतिमुक्तकः
अतिमुक्तक अतिमुक्त + क, m. The name of several plants, as Dalbergia ougeinensis, Gaertnera racemosa, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियश
अतियश अतियश, see यशस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्तता
अतिरिक्तता अति-रिक्त + ता (vb. रिच्), f. Excess, MBh. 2, 2270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेक|अतिरेकः
अतिरेक अतिरेक, i. e. अति-रिच् + अ, m. Excess, high degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलुब्धता
अतिलुब्धता अति-लुब्ध + ता (vb. लुभ्), f. Excessive greediness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलोभता
अतिलोभता अति-लोभ + ता, f. Excessive greediness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्तनं|अतिवर्त्तन
अतिवर्तन अतिवर्तन, i. e. अति-वृत् + अन, n. Remission (of a fine), Man. 8, 290.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तिन्|अतिवर्त्तिन्
अतिवर्तिन् अतिवर्तिन्, i. e. अति-वृत् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Crossing, passing over.<BR> 2. Not caring, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 8.<BR> 3. Offending, Rām. 4, 16, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाद|अतिवादः
अतिवाद अतिवाद, i. e. अति-वद् + अ, m. A reproachful speech, Man. 6, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाह्य
अतिवाह्य अति-वाह्य (vb. वह्), n. Passing (as time), Böhtl. Chr. 217, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृत्ति|अतिवृत्तिः
अतिवृत्ति अति-वृत् + ति, f. Trespass, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशय|अतिशयः
अतिशय अतिशय, i. e. अति-शी + अ, m.<BR> 1. Excellence.<BR> 2. Excess, Śiś. 9, 77.<BR> 3. Plenty, Vikr. d. 157.<BR> 4. As former [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a " target="_blank">Page0012-a + 40</a>] part of comp. words: 1. In a high degree, great, Pañc. 239, 14. 2. Violent.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरतिशय|निरतिशयः
निरतिशय निरतिशय, i. e. निस्-, adj. not to be surpassed, greatest, Pañc. i. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिशय
स- + अतिशय स- + अतिशय, adj. most excellent, Man. 9, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयिन्
अतिशयिन् अतिशयिन्, i. e. अतिशय + इन्, adj., f. नी. Most excellent, Vikr. d. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायिन्
अतिशायिन् अतिशायिन्, i. e. अति-शी + इन्, adj. Surpassing, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसमीपता
अतिसमीपता अति-समीप + ता, f. Too close proximity, Śiś. 9, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्ग|अतिसर्गः
अतिसर्ग अतिसर्ग, i. e. अति-सृज् + अ, m. Granting (of a wish), Rām. 4, 52, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसार|अतिसारः
अतिसार and अतीसार अती̆सार, i. e. अति-सृ + अ, m. Diarrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतीन्द्रिय अतीन्द्रिय, i. e. अति-इन्द्रिय.<BR> I. adj. Surpassing the senses, transcendental, Bhāṣāp. 57.<BR> II. n. Mind, Man. 1, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव अतीव, i. e. अति-इव, adv.<BR> 1. Much, very.<BR> 2. Indeed, Śāk. d. 137, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्तिता
अतृप्तिता अ-तृप्ति + ता. f. Insatiableness, Śiś. 9, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोर्थम्
अतोर्थम् अतोर्थम्, i. e. अतस्-अर्थ + म्, adv. To that end, Rām. 3, 8, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता अत्ता, f. A mother, Mṛcch. 27, 2. (Prākṛ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ अत्तृ, i. e. अद् + तृ, m. One who eats, Man. 5, 30; (a king) who swallows up the possessions of his people, Man. 8, 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्य|अत्यः
अत्य अत् + य, m. A horse, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. 1, 64, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त अत्यन्त, i. e. अति-अन्त, adj., f. ता.<BR> 1. Excessive, very large.<BR> 2. Endless, perpetual, Man. 5, 46; eternal. acc. sing. तम्, adv. 1. very much. 2. for ever, Man. 9, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय अत्यय, i. e. अति-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Passing away, lapse (of time), Man. 8, 145.<BR> 2. Death.<BR> 3. Danger, Man. 5, 27.<BR> 4. Transgression, crime, fault, Man. 8, 243; दाप्यो ऽष्टगुणम् अत्ययम्, ‘he shall be fined eight times the amount of the defraudation,’ Man. 8, 400.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनत्यय
अन्- + अत्यय अन्- + अत्यय, adj. imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालात्यय|कालात्ययः
काल- + अत्यय काल- + अत्यय, m. lapse of time, Man. 8, 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलात्यय|जलात्ययः
जल- + अत्यय जल- + अत्यय, m. the end of the rainy season, i. e. autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्यय|तपात्ययः
तप- + अत्यय तप- + अत्यय, m. 1. the end of the hot season, i. e. the rainy season. 2. the end of the heat, i. e. sunset, Śāk. d. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरत्यय
दुरत्यय दुरत्यय, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. या, 1. hard to be crossed (as a river), MBh. 4, 1970. 2. hard to be attained, 13, 4880. 3. unfathomable, Rām. 3, 71, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत्यय
निरत्यय निरत्यय, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. या, 1. free from danger. 2. infallible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्यय|महात्ययः
महा- + अत्यय महा- + अत्यय, 1. m. great pain, Chr. 11, 15. 2. adj. very pernicious, Chr. 22, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहात्यय
सु-महा- + अत्यय सु-महा- + अत्यय, adj. very dangerous, Chr. 37, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थम्
अत्यर्थम् अत्यर्थम्, i. e. अति-अर्थ + म्, adv. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र अ + त्र (cf. इदम्), adv.<BR> 1. = the loc. of इदम्, In this, Śāk. d. 59.<BR> 2. Here, therein, Man. 3, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रत्य
अत्रत्य अत्र + त्य, adj. Of this place, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि अत्रि, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, or saint, Man. 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन् अत्रिन् (for अत्त्रिन्, vb. अद्), adj. A demon, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. 1, 85, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ अ + थ (probably for अथा, Ved. cf. इदम्), adv.<BR> 1. Then, Nal. 17, 35.<BR> 2. Now, at the beginning of works and parts of works.<BR> 3. But, Nal. 22, 13.<BR> 4. In conditional sentences: If, अथ तान् नानु गच्छामि गमिष्यामि यमक्षयम्, ‘if I do not follow them, I shall go to the house of death,’ Rām. 2, 60, 3.<BR> --With following उ, (अथो): 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a " target="_blank">Page0013-a + 43</a>] afterwards, then, Chr. 56, 11. 2. and, Man. 2, 430. 3. even, Chr. 3, 1; and 23, 28.<BR> --With following अपि, nevertheless, Rām. 2, 29, 7.<BR> --With following वा: 1. or also, or, Man. 2, 219. Pañc. i, d. 399, वाथ instead of वाथ वा (cf. Pañc. iii, d. 36. अथो वा, Man. 3, 202). 2. or even, Bhartṛ. 2, 10. 3. but no, Śāk. 60, 18. 4. it is particularly used to introduce sentences: for, Pañc. 26, 14.<BR> --With following किम्: yes, well (in dialogue, cf. τί μήν).<BR> --Cf. Lat. at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वन्|अथर्व्वन्
अथर्वन् अथर्वन् (borrowed from the Zend. आथ्र-वन्, derived from आतर्, ‘fire’), m.<BR> 1. A priest.<BR> 2. The name of a Ṛṣi, or saint.<BR> 3. The Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरस|अथर्वांगिरस|अथर्वाङ्गिरसः
अथर्वाङ्गिरस अथर्वाङ्गिरस, i. e. अथर्वन्-अङ्गिरस् + अ.<BR> 1. adj., f. सी. Revealed to Atharvan and Angiras, Man. 11, 33.<BR> 2. sing and pl. The hymns of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वी
अथर्वी अथर्वी, f. (probably from अथर्वन्), The wife of a priest(?), Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. 1, 112, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो अथो, see अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद् अद्, ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm. Nal. 12, 35). To eat, Man. 2, 53; to devour, 4, 28.<BR> स्वदित, i. e. सु-अदित, n. Well eaten, a term used after presenting food (‘muc good may it do you!’), Man. 3, 251; 254.<BR> अद्य, Eatable, Pañc. iv. d. 79 (perhaps it ought to be changed to आद्य, the regular form).<BR> --Cf. ἔδω; Lat. edere; Goth. itan; A.S. etan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
ऽअद् -अद्, latter part of comp. words. One who eats, cf. क्रव्याद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन|अदनं
अदन अद् + अन, n. Eating, Man. 11, 64.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलादन|फलादनः
फल- + अदन फल- + अदन, m. a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्भित्व
अदम्भित्व अदम्भित्व, i. e. अ-दम्भिन् + त्व, n. Sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्
अदस् अदस्, pronoun, nom. sing. m. and f. असौ, nom. and acc. sing. n. अदस्; the bases of the remaining cases are अमु, अमू, and अमी. That, you, Man. 10, 128. It is preceded by the relative pronoun, He-who, Man. 1, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिक
अदायिक अदायिक, i. e. अ-दाय + इक, adj. For which there are no heirs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
अदिति अ-दिति, f. The name of a female deity, Chr. 298, 25 = Rigv. 1, 112, 25; the mother of the gods, Rām. 3, 20, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्यता
अदृश्यता अ-दृश्य + ता (vb. दृश्), f. Invisibility, Bhartṛ. 1, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेशकाल|अदेशकालः
अदेशकाल अ-देश-काल, s. A wrong place and wrong time, Bhag. 17, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत अद्भुत.<BR> I. adj., f. ता. Surprising, wonderful; superl. अद्भुत + तम, most surprising.<BR> II. n. A strange phenomenon, Man. 4, 118; a prodigy.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यद्भुत
अत्यद्भुत अत्यद्भुत, i. e. अति-, adj. very surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाद्भुत
महा- + अद्भुत महा- + अद्भुत adj. very surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य अद्य, Ved. also अद्या, i. e. अ-दिव् + आ (cf. इदम्), adv.<BR> 1. To-day.<BR> 2. Now.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ho-die; ἤδη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन अद्य + तन, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Of to-day, Pañc. 5, 6.<BR> 2. Of this time, a contemporary, Rājat. 5, 100. ‘The Hriṣīkeśa (i. e. an idol of Viṣṇu) of Suyya, reposing in meditation on the bank, may be adored by any contemporary who comes near the temple of Sundarī.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनीय
अद्यतनीय अद्यतनीय, i. e. अद्यतन + ईय, adj., f. या. Of to-day, Pañc. 169, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यूति
अद्यूति अद्यूति, i. e. अ-दिव् + ति, adj. Eager, Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. 1, 112, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रि|अद्रिः
अद्रि अद्रि, m.<BR> 1. A stone, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. 1, 88, 3.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. A cloud, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. 1, 85, 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a " target="_blank">Page0014-a + 42</a>]<BR> 4. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताद्रि|अस्ताद्रिः
अस्त- + अद्रि अस्त- + अद्रि, m. the mountain called अस्त (q. cf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाद्रि|कुलाद्रिः
कुल- + अद्रि कुल- + अद्रि, m. a principal mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषाराद्रि|तुषाराद्रिः
तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रलेय- + अद्रि तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रालेय- + अद्रि, m. Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनाद्रि|तुहिनाद्रिः
तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रलेय- + अद्रि तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रालेय- + अद्रि, m. Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेयाद्रि|प्रालेयाद्रिः
तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रलेय- + अद्रि तुषार-, तुहिन- and प्रालेय- + अद्रि, m. Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसारमय
अद्रिसारमय अद्रि-सार + मय, adj. f. यी. Made of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयत्व
अद्वयत्व अ-द्वय + त्व, n. Absence of duality.<BR> त्व + तस्, adv. In consequence of there being no duality, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 23 (i. e. because he knows that there is no duality, that all is one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वारतस्
अद्वारतस् अ-द्वार + तस्, adv. By any other aperture than the door, MBh. 13, 4750.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषरागिन्
अद्वेषरागिन् अद्वेषरागिन्, i. e. अ-द्वेष-राग + इन्, adj. Exempt from hatred and affection, Man. 2, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष्टृत्व
अद्वेष्टृत्व अ-द्वेष्टृ + त्व, n. Inoffensiveness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध|अधः
अध अ + ध (cf. अधस्), a particle. There, then, Lass. Anth. 98, 14 = Rigv. 5, 9, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम अधम (an old superlative, akin to अधस्), adj., f. मा. Extremely low, Man. 6, 65. In Karmadhāraya compounds it is generally the latter part: e. g. द्विज-, m. the meanest of twice-born men, Man. 3, 140; नर-, m. the lowest of mortals, Man. 10, 26; पाप-, m. the lowest of the wicked; पार्थिव-, m. the meanest of kings; पुरुष-, m. the vilest of men; शशक-, m. the vilest of hares.<BR> --Cf. Lat. infimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्ण|अधमर्णः
अधमर्ण अधमर्ण, i. e. अधम-ऋण, m. A debtor, Man. 8, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिक|अधमर्णिकः
अधमर्णिक अधमर्णिक, i. e. अधमर्ण + इक, m. A debtor, Man. 8, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर अधर (an old comparative, akin to अधस्).<BR> I. adj., f. रा. Lower, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b " target="_blank">Page0014-b + 45</a>] inferior.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The lower lip Śāk. 102, 10.<BR> 2. The lip in general, Śiś. 9, 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. inferus; Goth. undar; A.S. under; probably ἔνεροι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिताधर
खण्डित- + अधर खण्डित- + अधर, adj., f. रा, with bitten lips, Pañc. 46, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरोष्ठ
अधरोष्ठ अधरोष्ठ, and अधरौष्ठ अधरौष्ठ, i. e. अधर-ओष्ठ, m.<BR> 1. The lower lip, Suśr. 1, 114, 19.<BR> 2. The lower and the upper lips, the lips, Pañc. 45, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिसंवृताधरोष्ठ
अङ्गुलि-सम्-वृत- + अधरोष्ठ अङ्गुलि-सम्-वृत- + अधरोष्ठ, adj. the lips of which are covered with the finger, Śāk. d. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बफलाधरोष्ठ
विम्ब-फल- + अधरोष्ठ विम्ब-फल- + अधरोष्ठ, adj., f. ष्ठी, having lips like the Bimba fruit, Rām. 5, 28, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस् अ + धस् (cf. इदम्).<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Underneath.<BR> 2. Low, Man. 11, 224.<BR> 3. Down, Pañc. i. d. 214; to hell, Man. 7, 53.<BR> II. prepos. Under, with the gen., Man. 2, 59, and abl. Pañc. 115, 25.<BR> III. doubled: अधोधस्, i. e. अधस्-अधस्, adv.<BR> 1. Lower and lower, Man. 7, 53.<BR> 2. One below the other.<BR> --Cf. ἔνθεν, and see अधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तात्
अधस्तात् अधस्-तात् (the latter part is the original abl. of तद्).<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Underneath, below.<BR> 2. Down, downward, Man. 4, 54; to hell, 194.<BR> II. prepos. Under, with the gen.<BR> III. latter part of comp. adv. Under, Pañc. 141, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि अ + धि (cf. इदम्).<BR> I. adv. Above, on high, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. 1, 85, 2.<BR> II. prepos. Over, on with the abl., Chr. 287, 7 = Rigv. 1, 48, 7.<BR> III. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. Former part of compounded nouns and adverbs, implying:<BR> 1. Over, cf. अधिज्य<BR> 2. Chief, cf. अधिराज.<BR> 3. Before, cf. aध्यक्ष.<BR> 4. Relative to, cf. अधियज्ञ.<BR> 5. On, cf. अधिजानु.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक|अधिकं|अधिकः
अधिक अधि + क, adj.<BR> 1. Exceeding, Man. 3, 49; greater, Rām. 4, 9, 9; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a " target="_blank">Page0015-a + 46</a>] stronger, Pañc. ii. d. 29; more than, with the abl., Man. 9, 154; higher than, with the abl., Bhag. 6, 46; dearer, Rām. 2, 45, 32, Gorr.<BR> 2. Surpassing, Man. 11, 185; chief, Hit. pr. d. 48; highest, Bhartṛ. 2, 17.<BR> 3. Having an addition, अधिकं मासम्, ‘a month and more,’ Rām. 3, 15, 27.<BR> 4. Too much, Rām. 6, 16, 78.<BR> --acc. sing. कम्, adv. 1. Much, exceedingly. 2. More; with the abl., Rājat. 5, 419.<BR> --Comparat. अधिक + तर, Better than, Śāk. 100, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR> 1. exceeding, e. g.<BR> 2. exceeded by, particularly after numerals, e. g. वर्षे...राजन्यबन्धोर् द्वाविंशे, वैश्यस्य द्व्यधिके ततह्, ‘in the twenty-second year for a soldier, for a merchant two years later than that,’ Man. 2, 65. नवतिं नवाधिकाम्, ninety-nine, Ragh. 3, 69.<BR> 3. doubled:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाधिक
एक- + अधिक एक- + अधिक, adj. exceeding one, i. e. two, Man. 9, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदानाधिक
सर्व-दान- + अधिक सर्व-दान- + अधिक, adj. better than any gift, Yājñ. 1, 334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाधिक
प्राण- + अधिक प्राण- + अधिक, adj. dearer than life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षशताधिक
वर्ष-शत- + अधिक वर्ष-शत- + अधिक, adj. longer than a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधिक
वयोधिक वयोधिक, i. e. वयस्-अधिक, adj. advanced in age, Man. 4, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाधिक
अधिकाधिक अधिकाधिक, adj. outbidding each other, Rājat. 5, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण|अधिकरणं
अधिकरण अधिकरण, i. e. अधि-कृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Substance, substratum, or site.<BR> 2. Court of justice, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरण|धर्माधिकरणः|धर्म्माधिकरण|धर्म्माधिकरणं|धर्म्माधिकरणः
धर्म- + अधिकरण धर्म- + अधिकरण, n. 1. administration of justice, Pañc. 97, 1. 2. A court of justice, Pañc. 96, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामाधिकरण
राम- + अधिकरण राम- + अधिकरण, adj. relating to Rāma, Rām. 2, 15, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाधिकरण
समान- + अधिकरण समान- + अधिकरण,<BR> I. n. generic property.<BR> II. adj. contained in the same subject or category.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार|अधिकारः
अधिकार and अधीकार अधी̆कार, i. e. अधि-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Superintendence, Vikr. d. 42.<BR> 2. Administration.<BR> 3. Office, Pañc. 63, 23.<BR> 4. Office of a king.<BR> 5. Right, title, Man. 2, 16.<BR> 6. Topic, main point.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

