अनेकैकत्वबुद्धि
अनेकैकत्वबुद्धि अन्-एक-एक + त्व-बुद्धि, f. Comprehension of manifold unities, Bhāṣāp. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेहस्
अनेहस् अनेहस्, i. e. अन्-ईह् + अस् (anom.).<BR> I. adj. Without a rival.<BR> II. m. (nom. sing., हा) Time, Rājat. 5, 405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त|अनैकांत
अनैकान्त अनैकान्त, i. e. अन्-एक-अन्त + अ, adj. Going astray (one of the five forms of fallacious middle term), Bhāṣāp. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकह|अनोकहः
अनोकह अन्-ओक-ह (vb. 2. हा), m. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोंकृत
अनोंकृत अनोंकृत, i. e. अन्-ॐ-कृत, adj. Not accompanied by the mystical syllable ॐ, Man. 2, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्|अत्|अंत्
† अन्त् अन्त्, i. 1, Par. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त अन्त, m.<BR> 1. End, Nal. 22, 4.<BR> 2. Boundary, Rām. 3, 15, 16.<BR> 3. Limit, Rām. 3, 1, 23.<BR> 4. Border, Rām. 4, 6, 16.<BR> 5. Proximity, Man. 4, 116.<BR> 6. Death, Rām. 5, 87, 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. andi; A.S. ende; Lat. uls instead of ultis; see अन्तर, अन्तिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अन्- + अन्त अन्- + अन्त,<BR> I. adj. endless, Man. 3, 275.<BR> II. m. 1. a name of Viṣṇu. 2. Śeṣa, the chief of the Nāgas, or serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्त|अपरान्तः
अपर- + अन्त अपर- + अन्त, m. 1. the western extremity. 2. pl. the name of a people. 3. completion. 4. death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकान्त|उदकांत|उदकान्तः
उदक- + अन्त उदक- + अन्त, m. the bank of a river, Śāk. 54, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतदन्त
एतद्- + अन्त एतद्- + अन्त, adj., f. ता, ending in this, Man. 1, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्त|कल्पांत|कल्पान्तः
कल्प- + अन्त कल्प- + अन्त, m. the end of a Kalpa-period, the destruction, the end of the world, Dev. 1, 49; Hit. i, d. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृत- + अन्त कृत- + अन्त,<BR> I. adj., f. ता, deciding, Bhāg. P. 9, 6, 13.<BR> II. m. 1. fate, Rām. 1, 41, 1. 2. a name of the God of Death, Hit. 9, 6. 3. a proved doctrine, Bhag. 18, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्त|केशांत|केशान्तः
केश- + अन्त केश- + अन्त, m. 1. the end of the hair, Rām. 6, 8, 2. 2. a tuft of hair, Pañc. 245, 12. 3. hair, Rām. 5, 35, 21. 4. the ceremony of cutting the hair, Man. 2, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतान्त|गतांत
गत- + अन्त गत- + अन्त, adj. whose end is near, Rām. 2, 12, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्मान्त|घर्मांत|घर्मान्तः|घर्म्मान्त|घर्म्मान्तः
घर्म- + अन्त घर्म- + अन्त, m. the end of the hot season, Megh. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन जन m. an uninhabited country, Suśr. 1, 204, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदन्त|तदंत
तद्- + अन्त तद्- + अन्त, adj. finding its end thereby, Hit. i. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्त|दिगंत|दिगन्तः
दिश्- + अन्त दिश्- + अन्त,<BR> I. m. the end of the world, Kir. 5, 1.<BR> II. adj. dwelling at the end of the world, MBh. 10, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टान्त|दिष्टांत|दिष्टान्तः
दिष्ट- + अन्त दिष्ट- + अन्त, m. (vb. दिश्) death, Rām. 2, 111, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्त|दृष्टांत|दृष्टान्तः
दृष्ट- + अन्त दृष्ट- + अन्त, m. (n. Rām. 2, 109, 37 Gorr.) 1. a prototype, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a " target="_blank">Page0027-a + 42</a>] Hariv. 5298. 2. an example, Hit. ii, d. 97. 3. comparison, Chr. 9, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञान्त|यज्ञान्तः
यज्ञ- + अन्त यज्ञ- + अन्त, m. a supplementary sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगान्त|युगांत|युगान्तः
युग- + अन्त युग- + अन्त, m. 1. the end of an age. 2. a destruction of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकारान्त
स्वीकार- + अन्त स्वीकार- + अन्त, adj. 1. agreed to. 2. consequent upon a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुर|अन्तःपुरं
अन्तःपुर अन्तःपुर, i. e. अन्तर्-पुर, n.<BR> 1. The palace of a king, Rām. 2, 14, 28.<BR> 2. The female apartments, the gyneceum, Man. 7, 221.<BR> 3. The wives of a king. Sing. Nal. 17, 31, and plur. Śāk. 30, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्थ|अन्तःस्थः
अन्तःस्थ अन्तःस्थ, i. e. अन्तर्-स्थ (vb. स्था), adj., f. था, Being in the interior, Kathās. 16, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक अन्त + क.<BR> I. adj., f. का, Causing death, Rām. 3, 46, 9.<BR> II. m. A name of the god of Death, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1520.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तक|अनंतक
अन्- + अन्तक अन्- + अन्तक, adj. endless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तक|कालांतक|कालान्तकः
काल- + अन्तक काल- + अन्तक, m. the god of Death, Rām. 6, 67, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदन्तक
जगदन्तक जगदन्तक, i. e. जगत्-, m. the destroyer of the world, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषान्तक|विषांतक|विषान्तकः
विष- + अन्तक विष- + अन्तक, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर
अन्तकर अन्त-कर, adj., f. री, Causing death, Rām. 5, 94, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकृत्
अन्तकृत् अन्त-कृ + त्.<BR> I. adj. Causing the end.<BR> II. m. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तग|अन्तगः
अन्तग अन्त-ग (vb. गम्), adj., f. गा.<BR> 1. Going to the end.<BR> 2. Thoroughly conversant in, Man. 3, 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ततस्
अन्ततस् अन्त + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. With the end or extremity, Man. 2, 62.<BR> 2. At the end, lastly, Man. 3, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर् अन्तर्.<BR> I. adv. Within, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 119; Vikr. d. 8.<BR> II. prep. Within, with gen. Bhag. 13, 15.<BR> III. Combined and compounded with some verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. Former and latter part of compound [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b " target="_blank">Page0027-b + 46</a>] nouns implying the interior; e. g. अन्तः-करण, the internal sense (cf. करण); अम्भोन्तर्, i. e. अम्भस्-अन्तर् in the water, Yājñ. 1, 149.<BR> जन्तान्तर्, between the teeth, Man. 5, 141.<BR> --Cf. Lat. inter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर अन्तर.<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Other, Rām. 5, 56, 57.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The interior, Pañc. ii. d. 42; the main substance, Pañc. 167, 6.<BR> 2. Interval, Man. 2, 17.<BR> एतस्मिन्न् अन्तरे, In the mean while, Rām. 1, 24, 24.<BR> एकान्तर, adj. With one class between, Man. 10, 13.<BR> द्वि-एक-, adj. With one or two classes between, Man. 10, 7.<BR> काल-, n. Lapse of time, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1264.<BR> --Loc. अन्तरे, Between, Rājat. 5, 152.<BR> 3. A hole, Rām. 3, 35, 84.<BR> 4. Distance, Rām. 2, 49, 1.<BR> 5. Difference, Rām. 3, 53, 56.<BR> 6. Opportunity, Rām. 1, 46, 23.<BR> 7. A weak side, Rām. 6, 18, 46.<BR> 8. A surety, Pañc. 213, 24; see अन्तरेण.<BR> 9. When latter part of compound words it may be translated very often by adjectives, e. g. ‘other,’ दिश्- and देश-, n. A foreign country, Rājat. 6, 16; Man. 5, 78.<BR> स्थान-, n. Another place, Hit. 25, 9. ‘Special,’ कारण-, A special reason, Nal. 13, 59; Rām. 4, 9, 28. ‘Suitable,’ e. g. काल-, A suitable time, Pañc. iii. d. 236. ‘Relative to,’ मद्-, Relative to myself, Rām. 2, 90, 16 (cf. 92, 21 Gorr.)<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. interus, interior, alter, and ulterior, ultra (see अन्त and अन्तिम); Goth. anthar; A.S. other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसान्तर
दिवस- + अन्तर दिवस- + अन्तर, adj. one day old, MBh. 11, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर|सांतर|सान्तरं
स- + अन्तर स- + अन्तर, adj. with interstices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनान्तर|स्तनांतर|स्तनान्तरं
स्तन- + अन्तर स्तन- + अन्तर, n. the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतस्
अन्तरतस् अन्तर + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. From the interior, Śiś. 9, 19.<BR> 2. Within (in his heart), Rām. 3, 62, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरा|अंतरा
अन्तरा अन्तरा (old instr. sing. of अन्तर cf. अन्तरेण).<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Amidst, Chr. 14, 17.<BR> 2. Between, Rām. 5, 34, 5.<BR> 3. In the interval, i. e. between morning and evening, Man. 2, 56.<BR> 4. For some [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a " target="_blank">Page0028-a + 41</a>] time, Rām. 3, 8, 13.<BR> 5. Therein, Man. 10, 174.<BR> 6. On the way, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 17.<BR> 7. Near, Rām. 2, 57, 13.<BR> II. prep.<BR> 1. Between, with loc., Rām. 2, 40, 44, and acc., Rām. 2, 92, 12.<BR> 2. Without.<BR> --Cf. अन्तरेण, ἄτερ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरात्मन्य
अन्तरात्मन्य अन्तर्-आत्मन् + य, adj. Internal, Man. 12, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराय|अंतरायः|अन्तरायः
अन्तराय अन्तराय, i. e. अन्तर्-इ + अ, m. Obstacle, Śiś. 9, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराल|अंतरालं|अन्तरालं
अन्तराल अन्तराल, i. e. अन्तर्-आलि, n. Interval, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17; Śiś. 9, 2. loc. ले, While, Pañc. 55, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तराल
स- + अन्तराल स- + अन्तराल, adj., separated, distinct from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष|अंतरिक्षं|अन्तरिक्षं
अन्तरिक्ष अन्तरिक्ष and अन्तरीक्ष अन्तरीक्ष, i. e. अन्तर्-ईक्ष् + अ, n. The sky, Chr. 41, 21; 30, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीक्षग
अन्तरीक्षग अन्तरीक्ष-ग (vb. गम्).<BR> I. adj. Moving in the air, Rām. 5, 27, 11.<BR> II. m. A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीय|अंतरीयं|अन्तरीयं
अन्तरीय अन्तरीय, i. e. अन्तर + ईय, n. A lower garment, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरेण अन्तरेण (instr. of अन्तर), prep. with acc.<BR> 1. Between, Śiś. 3, 3.<BR> 2. During, Mālav. 67, 21.<BR> 3. Except, Rām. 3, 25, 1.<BR> 4. Without, Rām. 3, 71, 13.<BR> 5. Regarding, Śāk. 59, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दशाह
अन्तर्दशाह अन्तर्दशाह, i. e. अन्तर्-दशन्-अहन्, n. An interval of ten days, Man. 5, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धान|अन्तर्द्धानं|अंतर्धानं
अन्तर्धान अन्तर्धान, i. e. अन्तर्-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Disappearance; with इ or गम्, to disappear, Rām. 6, 19, 39.<BR> 2. Invisibility, Rām. 6, 19, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः|अन्तर्भावः
अन्तर्भाव अन्तर्भाव, i. e. अन्तर्-भू + अ, m. Inclusion, being included, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामिन्
अन्तर्यामिन् अन्तर्यामिन् i. e. अन्तर्-यम् + इन्, m. The soul, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वंशिक|अन्तर्वंशिकः
अन्तर्वंशिक अन्तर्वंशिक, i. e. अन्तर्-वंश + इक, m. A superintendent of a gyneceum, Pañc. 156, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वन्त्|अन्तर्वत्
अन्तर्वन्त् अन्तर् + वन्त्, adj., f. वत्नी (ved. वती). A pregnant woman, Rājat. 5, 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवन्त्|अन्तवत्|अंतवत्
अन्तवन्त् अन्त + वन्त्, adj., f. वती. Having an end, perishable, Bhag. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक अन्ति + क (from the ved. anti = ἀντί, cf. ἄντα, ἄντην; Lat. ante; Goth. and, e. g. in and-hafjan, to answer; N.H.G. ant-, ent-, e. g. in ant-worten, ent-gegnen), n. Vicinity, Rājat. 5, 57.<BR> --abl. कात्. Near, with acc. Rām. 3, 9, 11. From, with gen. Man. 9, 174.<BR> --loc. के. Close to, Nal. 1, 25. In presence of, Man. 2, 202.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्तिक
केश- + अन्तिक केश- + अन्तिक, i. e. केशान्त + इक, reaching to the hair, Man. 2, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणान्तिक
ग्रहण- + अन्तिक ग्रहण- + अन्तिक, i. e. ग्रहणान्त + इक, lasting till the comprehension, Man. 3, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तिकम्|जनांतिकम्
जनान्तिकम् जनान्तिकम्, i. e. जन-अन्तिक + म्, adv. whispering, speaking aside, Śāk. 13, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
अन्तिम अन्तिम (ved. अन्तम), adj., f. मा. Last, Hit. Pr. d. 12.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ultimus and intimus; see अन्त and अन्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासिन्
अन्तेवासिन् अन्तेवासिन्, i. e. अन्त + इ-वस् + इन्, m. A pupil, Man. 4, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अन्त्य अन्त्य, i. e. अन्त + य.<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Last, Man. 11, 213. With दशा, State of extremity, Pañc. 70, 5.<BR> 2. Lowest, Pañc. iv. d. 76. Of a very low class, Man. 12, 59.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Cāṇḍāla, Man. 2, 238.<BR> 2. One of a barbarous nation, Man. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यज|अन्त्यजः
अन्त्यज अन्त्य-ज (vb. जन्).<BR> I. adj., f. जा, Born in the lowest class, Man. 8, 385.<BR> II. m. A man of the lowest tribe, Pañc. i. d. 452.<BR> III. f. जा, A woman of the lowest class, Man. 11, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजातिता
अन्त्यजातिता अन्त्य-जाति + ता, f. The lowest of human conditions, Man. 12, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायिन्
अन्त्यावसायिन् अन्त्यावसायिन्, i. e. अन्त्य-अव-सो + इन्, m. A man of a degraded tribe; the son of a Niṣādī woman by a Cāṇḍāla, Man. 10, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्र|अंत्रं|अन्त्रं
अन्त्र अन्त्र (for अन्तर, cf. ἔντερον; Lat. interiora), n. An intestine (mostly used in the plur.), Rām. 5, 25, 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रान्त्र|क्षुद्रांत्र|क्षुद्रान्त्रं|क्षुद्रान्त्रः
क्षुद्र- + अन्त्र क्षुद्र- + अन्त्र, n. the entrails which are nearer to the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलान्त्र|स्थूलांत्र
स्थूल- + अन्त्र स्थूल- + अन्त्र, n. those which are near the anus, Yājñ. 3, 94; 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्द्|अंद्
† अन्द् अन्द्, i. 1, Par. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलन|अंदोलनं
अन्दोलन अन्दोलन, i. e. अन्दोलय + अन, n. Swinging, Rājat. 5, 356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलय
† अन्दोलय अन्दोलय (a denomin. derived from *अन्दोल, based on *अन्दुल्, an anomalous frequent. of दुल् for *दन्दुल्, cf. अङ्घ्रि). To swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्|अंध्
अन्ध् अन्ध्, i. 10, Par. (rather denomin. of अन्ध)<BR> 1. † To be blind.<BR> 2. To make blind, to obstruct the sight, Śiś. 9, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध अन्ध, adj., f. धा.<BR> 1. Blind, Pañc. 291, 11.<BR> 2. Obstructing the sight, Man. 8, 94.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवान्ध|दिवांध|दिवान्धः
दिवा- + अन्ध दिवा- + अन्ध, m. An owl, Pañc. 158, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धक|अंधक|अन्धकः
अन्धक अन्ध + क.<BR> I. adj., f. धिका, Blind.<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकार|अन्धकारः
अन्धकार अन्ध + कार, m. and n. Darkness, Man. 4, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकारमय
अन्धकारमय अन्धकार + मय, adj., f. यी. Dark, Kathās. 4, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धता
अन्धता अन्ध + ता, f. and अन्धत्व अन्ध + त्व, n. Blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
अन्धस् अन्धस्, n. The sacrificial food (ved.), Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अंध्रः|अन्ध्रः
अन्ध्र अन्ध्र, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people.<BR> 2. A man of a low caste, son of a Vaideha by a Kārāvara woman, Man. 10, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न|अन्नं|अन्नः
अन्न अन्न, i. e. अद् + न, n.<BR> 1. Food, Man. 3, 182.<BR> 2. Corn, Man. 3, 76.<BR> 3. Boiled rice, Man. 3, 82.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. annona.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्न
कृत- + अन्न कृत- + अन्न, n. dressed food, Man. 9, 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवान्न
देव- + अन्न देव- + अन्न, n. food offered to gods, Man. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यन्न
दधि- + अन्न दधि- + अन्न, n. rice with curdled milk, Yājñ. 1, 288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यायान्न|पर्य्यायान्न
पर्याय- + अन्न पर्याय- + अन्न, n. food prepared for another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टान्न|मिष्टान्नं
मिष्ट- + अन्न मिष्ट- + अन्न, n. a mixture of sugar and acids, etc., eaten with bread or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजान्न|राजान्नं
राजान्न राजान्न, i. e. राजन्-, n. a sort of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद
अन्नद अन्न-द (vb. दा), adj., f. दा. Giving food, Man. 4, 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नमय अन्न + मय, adj., f. यी. Consisting of food in a metaphysical sense, i. e. of the essence of the elementary creation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद|अन्नादः
अन्नाद अन्नाद, i. e. अन्न-अद् + अ, adj., f. दी. Eating food, Man. 8, 317 (one who eats food given to him by a killer of a Brāhmaṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद्य
अन्नाद्य अन्नाद्य, i. e. अन्न-आद्य.<BR> 1. (the latter part being the ptcple. of the fut. pass. of अद्), n. Proper food, Man. 3, 82.<BR> 2. (the latter part being the adj. आद्य), Dressed rice, etc., Man. 3, 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य अन्य, adj., f. या, n. यद्.<BR> 1. Other, Man. 8, 17.<BR> 2. Different, Hit. i. d. 121.<BR> 3. with abl. Other than, Rājat. 5, 178. (नान्यः शङ्करवर्मणः, no other than Śaṅkaravarman).<BR> 4. One, Pañc. 80, 16.<BR> 5. plur. The others, i. e. the rest, Böhtl. Chr. 219, 161.<BR> 6. acc. sing., n. यद्. Besides, else, Pañc. 55, 9.<BR> --Comparat. अन्यतर, f. रा. n. रद्, Either of two, Man. 2, 111.<BR> --Superl. अन्यतम, f. मा, Any one of more than two, Man. 11, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. alius; ἄνευ, ἄνις, ἄλλος; Goth. alja-, alis, alja, probably also alls; A.S. eall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अन्- + अन्य अन्- + अन्य, adj., f. या, fixed on one object, Bhag. 9, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्
अन्यतस् अन्य + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. From another, Man. 4, 33.<BR> 2. On the contrary, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a " target="_blank">Page0030-a + 41</a>] Pañc. i. d. 109.<BR> 3. To another place, Man. 2, 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यता
अन्यता अन्य + ता, f. Difference, Śiś. 4, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यता
अन्- + अन्यता अन्- + अन्यता, f. identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र अन्य + त्र, adv.<BR> 1. Elsewhere<BR> 2. On another occasion, Man. 5, 41.<BR> 3. To another subject, Man. 2, 168.<BR> 4. With abl., except, without, Bhag. 8, 9.<BR> --Cf. Goth. aljathrô; Lat. aliter; ἀλλότριος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा अन्य + था, adv.<BR> 1. In another manner, differently. अन्यथा कृ, To change, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 717.<BR> 2. Otherwise, else, Man. 8, 144.<BR> 3. Untruly, Rām. 4, 21, 15.<BR> 4. Wrongly, illegally, Man. 9, 234.<BR> 5. In an opposite way, Pañc. 206, 14; with कृ, To deny.<BR> --Cf. Lat. aliuta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा अन्य + दा, adv.<BR> 1. At another time.<BR> 2. Once, Pañc. 234, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीय
अन्यदीय अन्यदीय, i. e. अन्य + द् + ईय, adj. f. या.<BR> 1. Belonging to another.<BR> 2. Being in others, Daśak. 187, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमातृज|अन्यमातृजः
अन्यमातृज अन्य-मातृ-ज (vb. जन्), m. A half-brother, born by another mother, Yājñ. 2, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यस्त्रीग|अन्यस्त्रीगः
अन्यस्त्रीग अन्य-स्त्री-ग (vb. गम्), m. An adulterer, Man. 8, 386.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश|अन्यादृशः
अन्यादृश अन्यादृश, i. e. अन्य-दृश् + अ, adj., f. शी, Looking different. Lass. 72, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनाधिक
अन्यूनाधिक अन्यूनाधिक, i. e. अ-न्यून-अधिक, adj., f. का. Neither too little nor too much, Rām. 6, 16, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्
अन्येद्युस् अन्येद्युस्, i. e. अन्य + इ-द्यु + अस्, adv.<BR> 1. On the following day, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 9.<BR> 2. Once, Pañc. 68, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्य|अन्योदर्यः|अन्योदर्य्य|अन्योदर्य्यः
अन्योदर्य अन्योदर्य, i. e. अन्य-उदर + य, m. A half-brother, having the same father but another mother, Yājñ. 2, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य अन्योन्य, i. e. अन्य + स्-अन्य, adj.<BR> 1. Each other, Man. 7, 89.<BR> 2. Mutual, Man. 9, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्
अन्वक् अन्वक्, i. e. अनु-अञ्च्, acc. sing. n.<BR> I. adv. Behind, Śiś. 9, 76.<BR> II. prep. with acc. After, Ragh. 2, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय अन्वय, i. e. अनु-इ + अ, m<BR> 1. Following.<BR> 2. Connection.<BR> 3. The affirmative connection between the major and middle terms, Bhāṣāp. 141.<BR> 4. Male descendants, Yājñ. 2, 117.<BR> 5. Lineage, Ragh. 1, 9. Race, Rājat. 5, 151. Family, Rājat. 5, 41.<BR> 6. Succession, inheritance in अन्वयागत, Inherited, Pañc. 16, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्वय|दुरन्वयः
दुस्- + अन्वय दुस्- + अन्वय, adj. 1. hard to be pursued, Rām. 2, 92, 13 Gorr. 2. hard to be performed, MBh. 13, 5854. 3. not easy to be conceived, Bhāg. P. 7, 6, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्वय
निस्- + अन्वय निस्- + अन्वय, adj. 1. in absence (cf. अन्वयवन्त्), Man. 8, 332. 2. without descendants, Rājat. 2, 81. 3. not related, Man. 8, 198.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
स- + अन्वय स- + अन्वय, adj. 1. related, Man. 8, 331. 2. in connection with family. 3. with all the family, Pañc. 45, 6. 4. in order or regular succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयवन्त्|अन्वयवत्
अन्वयवन्त् अन्वय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, In presence, Man. 8, 332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन् अन्वयिन्, i. e. अन्वय + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Connected with, Bhāṣāp. 73.<BR> 2. Belonging to a race, Rājat. 5, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थ
अन्वर्थ अन्वर्थ, i. e. अनु-अर्थ.<BR> I. adj., f. था, Clear.<BR> II. adv. थम्, Literally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववाय|अन्ववायः
अन्ववाय अन्ववाय, i. e. अनु-अव-इ + अ, m. Race, Sund. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्षा
अन्ववेक्षा अन्ववेक्षा, i. e. अनु-अव-ईक्ष् + आ, f. Regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका अन्वष्टका, i. e. अनु-अष्टका<BR> I. The ninth day of the latter half of the months Pauṣa, Māgha, and Phālguna (and according to another authority, also of the Agrahāyaṇa), Man. 4, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम् अन्वहम्, i. e. अनु-अह + म्, adv. Every day, Man. 2, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेय|अन्वाधेयं
अन्वाधेय अन्वाधेय, i. e. अनु-आ-धेय (vb. धा), n. A woman's property, consisting in what she has received after her marriage from her husband's or her father's families, Man. 9, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयक|अन्वाधेयकं
अन्वाधेयक अन्वाधेय + क, n. = अन्वाधेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य अन्वाहार्य, i. e. अनु-आ-हार्य (vb. हृ), n. The monthly Śrāddha or funeral repast in honour of the manes, held on the day of new noon, Man. 3, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यक|अन्वाहार्य्यक|अन्वाहार्य्यकं
अन्वाहार्यक अन्वाहार्य + क, n. = अन्वाहार्य, in पिण्ड- (properly, the oblation offered after the funeral cakes), Man. 3, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष|अन्वेषः
अन्वेष अन्वेष, i. e. अनु- 2. इष् + अ, m. Searching, Śāk. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषक
अन्वेषक अन्वेषक, i. e. अनु- 2. इष् + अक, adj., f. इका, One who searches, Rām. 4, 61, 12. Who explores, Rājat. 5, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषण|अन्वेषणं
अन्वेषण अन्वेषण, i. e. अनु- 2. इष् + अन, n. and f. णा, Searching, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषिन्
अन्वेषिन् अन्वेषिन्, i. e. अनु- 2. इष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Searching, Rājat. 5, 463.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितान्वेषिन्
हित- + अन्वेषिन् हित- + अन्वेषिन्, adj. seeking another's welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष्टृ
अन्वेष्टृ अन्वेष्टृ, i. e. अनु- 2. इष् + तृ, m. A searcher, Nal. 16, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप् अप्, f., in the classical literature plur.: N.V. आपस्,<BR> I. अद्भिस्, D.A. अद्भ्यस्. Water, Man. 1, 8. अद्भिर् दा, To give and confirm the gift by pouring water, Man. 9, 168.<BR> --Cf. Lat. aqua, amnis; Goth. ahva; A.S. ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
1. अप अप.<BR> I. adv. (ved.) Away. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b " target="_blank">Page0031-b + 40</a>]<BR> II. prep. with abl. Away from, without (very seldom).<BR> III. combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. former part of compounded nouns and adverbs, implying: Loss, negation, privation, wrong, bad, unnatural.<BR> --Cf. ἀπό; Lat. ab; Goth. and A.S. af.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
2. ऽअप -अप् + अ, a substitute for अप्, when latter part of a comp. word, e. g. शुष्क-, adj. Of which the water is dried up, Rām. 2, 72, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अपकर्तृ अपकर्तृ, i. e. अप-कृ + तृ, m. An injurer, Hit. iii. d. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्ष|अपकर्षः
अपकर्ष अपकर्ष, i. e. अप-कृष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Deterioration.<BR> 2. Sinking, Man. 10, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षक
अपकर्षक अपकर्षक, i. e. अप-क्रिष् + अक, adj. Deteriorating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षण
अपकर्षण अपकर्षण, i. e. अप-कृष्-अन.<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Removing, Rām. 1, 29, 18.<BR> II. n. Removal, Yājñ. 1, 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकार|अपकारः
अपकार अपकार, i. e. अप-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Injury.<BR> 2. Malice, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारता
अपकारता अपकार + ता, f. An injurious action, Nal. 21, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारिन् अपकारिन्, i. e. अप-कृ + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Mischievous, Man. 11, 31; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 687.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत्य
अपकृत्य अप-कृत्य, n. Injury, Pañc. 255, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमण|अपक्रमणं
अपक्रमण अपक्रमण, i. e. अप-क्रम् + अन, n. Going away, Rām. 2, 34, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया अप-क्रिया, f.<BR> 1. A wrong (unseasonable) act, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 890.<BR> 2. Wrong manner, Śiś. 9, 68.<BR> --Cf. अनपक्रिया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोश|अपक्रोशः
अपक्रोश अपक्रोश, i. e. अप-क्रुश् + अ [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a " target="_blank">Page0032-a + 39</a>] m. Reviling, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 21 (ib. 20, read पार्थिवं मिथो).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्वता
अपक्वता अ-पक्व + ता, f. Immaturity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम|अपगमः
अपगम अप-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going away, Megh. 71.<BR> 2. Separation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 643.<BR> 3. Passing away (of time), Kathās. 21, 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगर्जित
अपगर्जित अप-गर्जित (vb. गर्ज्), adj. Without thundering, Kathās. 19, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचमान
अपचमान अ-पचमान (vb. पच्, ptcple. pres. Ātm.), adj. One who by his mode of life is prevented from dressing his food, as a student, a mendicant, and a heretic, Man. 4, 32 (Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचय|अपचयः
अपचय अपचय, i. e. अप-चि + अ m. Decrease, Hit. iii. d. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायिन्
ऽअपचायिन् -अपचायिन्, i. e. अप-चि + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Decreasing in, MBh. 3, 11157.<BR> 2. Honouring, MBh. 13, 6705.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचार|अपचारः
अपचार अपचार, i. e. अप-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Death, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 20.<BR> 2. Trespass, fault, Śāk. 110, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् अपचारिन्, i. e. अप-चर् + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Deviating from, Hariv. 1014 (corr. ˚चारिणः).<BR> 2. Adulterous, Man. 8, 317.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचिति|अपचितिः
अपचिति अप-चि + ति, f.<BR> 1. Honour, Rām. 2, 74, 26.<BR> 2. Expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय अपच्छाय, i. e. अप-छाय (cf. छाया), adj. Shadowless, Pañc. ii. d. 108 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजिहीर्षु
अपजिहीर्षु अपजिहीर्षु, i. e. अप-जिहीर्ष, desid. of हृ + उ, adj. Desirous of taking away, Rājat. 5, 426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी अपटी, f. A screen of cloth; see क्षेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डितता
अपण्डितता अ-पण्डित + ता, f. Foolishness, Bhartṛ. 2, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्य|अपत्यं
अपत्य अप + त्य, n. Offspring, Man. 5, 161. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b " target="_blank">Page0032-b + 41</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्य
अन्- + अपत्य अन्- + अपत्य, adj., f. या, childless, without offspring, Man. 9, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्नापत्य
विपन्न- + अपत्य विपन्न- + अपत्य (vb. पद्), adj. f. या, having lost a child by abortment, Rājat. 5, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्य|सापत्यः
स- + अपत्य स- + अपत्य, adj. having progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यता
ऽअपत्यता -अपत्य + ता, f. State of having offspring, Man. 3, 16.<BR> अन्-, Having no offspring, childlessness, Śāk. 90, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपा
अपत्रपा अप-त्रप् + आ, f. Bashfulness, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपत्रप
निस्- + अपत्रप निस्- + अपत्रप, adj., f. पा, impudent, Rām. 4, 30, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश|अपदेशः
अपदेश अपदेश, i. e. अप-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Stating, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 14.<BR> 2. Denunciation, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 13.<BR> 3. Pretext, Man. 4, 198.<BR> अपदेशैस्, Artfully, Man. 8, 182.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापदेशम्
स-अपदेश + म् स-अपदेश + म्, adv. under a pretext, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेशिन्
ऽअपदेशिन् -अपदेश् + इन् in राजपुत्र-, adj. Disguised as (Rājputs) Kathās. 24, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदोषता
अपदोषता अप-दोष + ता, f. Faultlessness, Śiś. 9, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यान|अपध्यानं
अपध्यान अपध्यान, i. e. अप-ध्यै + अन, n.<BR> 1. Disregard, MBh. 1, 8457.<BR> 2. Hurting, Hariv. 9058 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसज|अपध्वंसजः
अपध्वंसज अप-ध्वंस् + अ-ज (vb. जन्), m. The offspring of a father inferior in caste to the mother, Man. 10, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयन|अपनयनं
अपनयन अपनयन, i. e. अप-नी + अन, n. Removing, Rām. 3, 64, 11; 1, 46, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्ति|अपनुत्तिः
अपनुत्ति अपनुत्ति, i. e. अप-नुद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Removing.<BR> 2. Expiation, Man. 11, 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुद
ऽअपनुद अप-नुद् + अ, adj., f. दा. Removing, Rām. 2, 1, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुनुत्सु
अपनुनुत्सु अपनुनुत्सु, i. e. अप-नुनुत्स, desider. of नुद् + उ, adj. Desirous of removing, Man. 11, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोद|अपनोदः
अपनोद अपनोद, i. e. अप-नुद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Removal.<BR> 2. Expiation, Man. 11, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदन|अपनोदनं
अपनोदन अपनोदन, i. e. अप-नुद् + अन.<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Removing, Man. 11, 215.<BR> II. n. Expiation, Man. 11, 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अपपात्र अप-पात्र, adj. Deprived of vessels, Man. 10, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपादत्र
अपपादत्र i. e. अप-पाद-त्र (vb. त्रा), adj. Without shoes, Rājat. 5, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश|अपभ्रंशः
अपभ्रंश अप-भ्रंश् + अ, m. Incorrect language, Rājat. 5, 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्द|अपमर्दः|अपमर्द्द
अपमर्द अपमर्द, i. e. अप-मृद् + अ, m. Dirt, Rām. 3, 2, 3.<BR> --Cf. Lat. merda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्श|अपमर्शः
अपमर्श अपमर्श, i. e. अप-मृश् + अ, m. Touch, Śāk. d. 116, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान|अपमानं|अपमानः
अपमान अपमान, i. e. अप-मन् + अ, m., n.<BR> 1. Disrespect, Rām. 1, 12, 14.<BR> 2. Token of disrespect, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानिन्
अपमानिन् अपमानिन्, i. e. अप-मन् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Disregarding, despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्ग|अपमार्गः
अपमार्ग अपमार्ग, i. e.<BR> I. अप-मृज् + अ, m. Cleansing, Śiś. 9, 36.<BR> II. अप-मार्ग, m. A sideway, Pañc. 169, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयान|अपयानं
अपयान अपयान, i. e. अप-या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going away, Śiś. 9, 84.<BR> 2. Retreat, flight, Rām. 3, 40, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर<BR> I. अप + र, adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Posterior, Man. 3, 278; with सन्ध्या, Evening-twilight, Man. 4, 93.<BR> 2. Following, Rām. 2, 65, 1.<BR> 3. Western, Śiś. 9, 1.<BR> 4. Other, Pañc. 55, 13. acc. रम्, adv. Moreover, Pañc. 71, 1.<BR> II. अ-पर, adj.<BR> 1. Inferior, Bhag. 7, 5.<BR> 2. Relative, Bhāṣāp. 7; 9.<BR> 3. Modern, Man. 9, 99.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. afar, after; N.H.G. aber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वापर|पूर्व्वापर
पूर्व- + अपर पूर्व- + अपर,<BR> I. adj. 1. being before and behind. 2. prior and subsequent.<BR> II. n. sing. 1. east and west. 2. connexion, Man. 8, 56 (Proof, and thing to be proved, Ragh.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरता
अपरता अपर + ता, f.<BR> 1. Relative ness.<BR> 2. Condition of being less extensive, Bhāṣāp. 8.<BR> 3. Shortness of distance and time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्र
अपरत्र अपर + त्र, adv. In another place, Rām. 3, 15, 26; 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्व|अपरत्वं
अपरत्व अपर + त्व, n. Shortness of distance and time, Bhāṣāp. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्वक
अपरत्वक अपरत्व + क, n. = अपरता, Bhāṣāp. 3; 85, Shortness of distance and time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरथा
अपरथा अपर-था, adv. Otherwise, Śiś. 9, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्परसंभूत|अपरस्परसम्भूत
अपरस्परसंभूत अपरस्परसंभूत, i. e. अ-परस्पर-सम्-भूत (vb. भू), adj. Not sprung up in a successive order, Bhag. 16, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध|अपराधः
अपराध अप-राध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Transgression, Ragh. 1, 6.<BR> 2. Offence, Pañc. 40, 23.<BR> 3. Crime, Rām. 2, 58, 22.<BR> 4. Injury, Rām. 6, 33, 21.<BR> 5. अपराध + तस्, adv. By the fault, Man. 8, 408.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपराध|निरपराधः
निस्- + अपराध निस्- + अपराध, adj. innocent, Pañc. 198, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
स- + अपराध स- + अपराध, adj. guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधकृत्
अपराधकृत् अपराध-कृत्, adj. One who has committed a crime, sinful, Śiś. 9, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अपराधिन् अप-राध् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Offending, Rām. 5, 91, 8. An offender, Yājñ. 2, 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्तक|अपरान्तकः
अपरान्तक अपरान्तक, i. e. अपर-अन्त + क.<BR> I. m. The name of a people.<BR> II. n. A song conducive to final liberation, Yājñ. 3, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरावर्तिन्|अपरावर्त्तिन्
अपरावर्तिन् अपरावर्तिन्, i. e. अ-परा-वृत् + इन्, adj. Not turning the back, not flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपराह्ण अपराह्ण, i. e. अपर-अह्न, m., n.<BR> 1. The afternoon, Man. 3, 255.<BR> 2. Evening, Chr. 34, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहारवन्त्
अपरिहारवन्त् अ-परिहार + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Unavoidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेद्युस्
अपरेद्युस् अपरेद्युस्, i. e. अपर + इ-दिव् + अस्, adv. The following day, Rām. 1, 9, 52; Nal. 13, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलताभवन
अपलताभवन अप-लता-भवन, adj., f. ना, Without arbours, Kir. 5, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग अपवर्ग, i. e. अप-वृज् + अ, m. Completion; the delivery of the soul from the body; final beatitude, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्गद
अपवर्गद अपवर्ग-द (vb. दा), adj., f. दा, Giving final beatitude, Rājat. 5, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तन|अपवर्तनं|अपवर्त्तन
अपवर्तन अपवर्तन, i. e. अप-वृत् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Removing.<BR> 2. Depriving one of, Man. 9, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाद|अपवादः
अपवाद अपवाद, i. e. अप-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Refutation of an erroneous imputation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 24.<BR> 2. Insulting, Man. 4, 239.<BR> 3. Blame, Pañc. 37, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादिन्
अपवादिन् अपवादिन्, i. e. अप-वद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Blaming, Śāk. 23, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितक
अपवारितक अप-वारित + क (vb. वृ), adj., instr. केन, Apart, Mṛcch. 23, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहन|अपवाहनं
अपवाहन अपवाहन, i. e. अप-वह् + अन (vb. वह्), n. Removal, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेध|अपवेधः
अपवेध अपवेध, i. e. अप-व्यध् + अ, m. Boring improperly, Man. 9, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशङ्कम्|अपशंकम्
अपशङ्कम् अप-शङ्क + म् (see शङ्का), adv. Fearless, Śiś. 4, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्
अपस् अपस्, Ved. (akin to आप्)<BR> I. n. Work, Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. i. 85, 9.<BR> II. adj. Active, diligent, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. opus; Ved. अपस्य = Lat. operari; ποιέω for ποσίεω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपस्
सु- + अपस् सु- + अपस्, adj. making beautiful works, Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. 1, 85, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसद|अपसदः
अपसद अप-सद्-अ, m.<BR> 1. A degraded one, Man. 10, 10.<BR> 2. A contemptible individual; in this signification, it is generally the latter part of a comp., e. g. गज-, m. A contemptible elephant, Pañc. 80, 21; वानर-, m. A contemptible monkey, Rām. 6, 83, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरण|अपसरणं
अपसरण अपसरण, i. e. अप-सृ + अन, n. Retreating, Pañc. 152, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर्प अपसर्प, i. e. अप-सृप् + अ, m. A spy, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पण|अपसर्पणं
अपसर्पण अपसर्पण, i. e. अप-सृप् + अन, n. Retreating, Rām. 6, 92, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यवन्त्|अपसव्यवत्
अपसव्यवन्त् अप-सव्य + वन्त्, adj. With the sacrificial cord over the right shoulder (cf. सव्य), Yājñ. 1, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसार|अपसारः
अपसार अपसार, i. e. अप-सृ + अ, m. An outlet, Pañc. 171, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कर|अपस्करः
अपस्कर अपस्कर, i. e. अप-कृ + अ, m. Excrements, Lass. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नान|अपस्नानं
अपस्नान अपस्नान, i. e. अप-स्ना + अन, n. Water which had been used for bathing, Man. 4, 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मार|अपस्मारः
अपस्मार अपस्मार, i. e. अप-स्मृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Epilepsy.<BR> 2. Madness, Bhartṛ. 1, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारिन्
अपस्मारिन् अपस्मारिन् i. e. अपस्मार + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Subject to epilepsy, Man. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह
ऽअपह -अप-ह (vb. हन्), adj., f. हा,<BR> 1. Removing, Rām. 3, 79, 44; Kir. 5, 22.<BR> 2. Destroying, Rājat. 5, 179.<BR> 3. Curing, Suśr. 2, 408, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषापह|विषापहः
विष- + अपह विष- + अपह, adj. antidotal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरण|अपहरणं
अपहरण अपहरण, i. e. अप-हृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Taking away, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 21.<BR> 2. Stealing, Man. 9, 293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहर्तृ|अपहर्त्तृ
अपहर्तृ अपहर्तृ, i. e. अप-हृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, n.<BR> 1. One who takes away, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a " target="_blank">Page0035-a + 42</a>] thief, Man. 9, 275.<BR> 2. One who withholds another's property, Man. 8, 190.<BR> 3. Removing, expiating, Man. 11, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहार|अपहारः
अपहार अपहार, i. e. अप-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Taking away.<BR> 2. Concealment, Śāk. 13, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारक|अपहारकः
अपहारक अपहारक, i. e. अप-हृ + अक.<BR> I. adj., f. इका, Taking away, stealing, Man. 9, 256.<BR> II. m. A thief, Man. 4, 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारिन्
अपहारिन् अपहारिन्, i. e. अप-हृ + इन्.<BR> I. adj., f. इणी, Taking away; ravishing, Man. 2, 88.<BR> II. m. A thief, Pañc. 33, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नव|अपह्नवः
अपह्नव अपह्नव, i. e. अप-ह्नु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Denying, Man. 8, 52.<BR> 2. Concealment, Kathās. 10, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरिष्णु
अपाकरिष्णु अपाकरिष्णु, i. e. अप-आ-कृ + इष्णु, adj. Surpassing, Bhartṛ. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्ग|अपांग|अपाङ्गः
अपाङ्ग अपाङ्ग, i. e. अप-अङ्ग, m. The outer corner of the eye, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 15.<BR> --In comp. adj. the fem. terminates in गी and गा, Rām. 5, 38, 7; 2, 30, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लापाङ्ग|शुक्लापांग|शुक्लापाङ्गः
शुक्ल- + अपाङ्ग शुक्ल- + अपाङ्ग, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रकृत्या
अपात्रकृत्या अ-पात्र-कृत्या, f. An action by which a person becomes unworthy of receiving a present, Man. 11, 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रीकरण|अपात्रीकरणं
अपात्रीकरण अपात्रीकरण, i. e. अ-पात्र-कृ + अन, n. Causing a person to become unworthy of receiving a present, Man. 11, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान|अपानं|अपानः
अपान अपान, i. e. अप-अन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. One of the five vital airs, that which goes downwards, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 10.<BR> 2. The anus (cf. अन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाय|अपायः
अपाय अपाय, i. e. अप-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going away.<BR> 2. Disappearance.<BR> 3. Diminution, Man. 1, 70.<BR> 4. End, Rājat. 5, 98.<BR> 5. Trespass, injury.<BR> 6. Loss.<BR> 7. Danger.<BR> 8. Calamity. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-b " target="_blank">Page0035-b + 46</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकापाय|एकापायः
एक- + अपाय एक- + अपाय, adj. diminished by one, Man. 1, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपाय
निस्- + अपाय निस्- + अपाय, adj. 1. imperishable, MBh. 12, 8003. 2. infallible, MBh. 3, 2178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापाय
स- + अपाय स- + अपाय, adj. dangerous, Pañc. 192, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थक
अपार्थक अपार्थक, i. e. अप-अर्थ + क, adj. f. थिका, Useless, Man. 8, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रय|अपाश्रयः
अपाश्रय अपाश्रय, i. e. अप-आ-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Refuge, support, Man. 9, 335.<BR> 2. An awning spread over a court, Rām. 5, 11, 19.<BR> 3. The head, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 20 (Sch. Wils. p. 90).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपि
अपि अपि (properly, Thereto, on, by, cf. ἐπί; Lat. ob)<BR> I. part.<BR> 1. Moreover, also, Man. 8, 274; 1, 119.<BR> 2. Even, Man. 2, 150.<BR> 3. Still, Śāk. d. 29.<BR> 4. Though, Śāk. d. 68.<BR> 5. With preceding यदि, Although, Man. 9, 145.<BR> 6. With तथा, Even thus, nevertheless, Śāk. 99, 8.<BR> 7. With तद्, Nevertheless, Bhartṛ. 1, 28.<BR> 8. Only, Pañc. Pr. d. 9.<BR> 9. All together, after numerals and words used in a similar signification, Man. 1, 107 (All four), Man. 2, 14 (after उभौ, both); Man. 3, 193 (all together); Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1047 (after च्तानि, all these); Pañc. 108, 14 (after अपरम्, Every other subject).<BR> 10. A part. of interrogation, Rām. 5, 33, 34.<BR> 11. A part of desire, O that! Man. 3, 274.<BR> 12. With following नाम (base नामन्), Perhaps, Mṛcch. 174, 3. O that! Vikr.<BR> 13. Following the interrogat. pron. किम् or its derivatives:<BR> a. It makes them indefinite, को ऽपि (i. e. कस् अपि), Somebody, Bhartṛ. 3, 99 (cf. Lat. quispiam for quis-pi-jam).<BR> b. Signifies: Even, Kathās. 4, 55.<BR> c. Violently, Megh. 110.<BR> 14. Preceding किं चिद् becomes more indefinite, Man. 3, 14.<BR> II. conjunct.<BR> 1. And also, Man. 1, 115.<BR> 2. And, Man. 4, 55.<BR> 3. अपि-अपि, ‘as well as,’ Hit. i. d. 159; from the one part--from the other part, Pañc. 113, 8; 9; अपि-च, Man. 5, 23.<BR> 4. But, Man. 8, 267.<BR> 5. But also, Pañc. 155, 25. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a " target="_blank">Page0036-a + 42</a>]<BR> III. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. Former part of comp. nouns implying ‘near to,’ ‘joined to.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधान|अपिधानं
अपिधान अपिधान, i. e. अपि-धा + अन, n. A cover.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापिधान
शिला- + अपिधान शिला- + अपिधान, adj., f. ना, covered by stones, Rām. 3, 76, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप|अपूपः
अपूप अपूप, m. A cake, Man. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वता|अपूर्व्वता
अपूर्वता अ-पूर्व + ता, f. and अपूर्वत्व अ-पूर्व + त्व, n. Condition of having no antecedent, i. e. acquiring an understanding of the ओन्ल्य् रेअल् बेइन्ग् from no other authority than the Vedic texts, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 10 cf. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षा
अपेक्षा अपेक्षा, i. e. अप-ईक्ष् + अ f.<BR> 1. Consideration, Pañc. 40, 16.<BR> 2. Regard.<BR> 3. Care, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 6.<BR> 4. Expectation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 9.<BR> 5. Reference, relation, ib. 208, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्ष|अनपेक्षं
अन्-अपेक्ष अन्-अपेक्ष, adj., f. क्षा. 1. Regardless. 2. Without desire, Bhag. 12, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्षा
निस्- + अपेक्षा निस्- + अपेक्षा,<BR> I. f. indifference, Rām. 2, 116, 5 Gorr.<BR> II. adj. 1. Regardless, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 19. 2. Without desire, indifferent, Man. 6, 41.<BR> III. क्षम्, adv. 1. Without having any regard. Daśak. in Chr. 192, 22. 2. Accidentally, Pañc. 264, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितत्व
अपेक्षितत्व अपेक्षितत्व, i. e. अप-ईक्षित + त्व, (vb. ईक्ष्), n. Consideration, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षिन्
अपेक्षिन् अपेक्षिन्, i. e. अप-ईक्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Regarding.<BR> 2. Expecting, Rājat. 5, 296.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्षिन्
अन्- + अपेक्षिन् अन्- + अपेक्षिन्, disregarding, Rām. 4, 28, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घापेक्षिन्
दीर्घ- + अपेक्षिन् दीर्घ- + अपेक्षिन्, i. e. दीर्घापेक्षा + इन्, adj. patient, enduring, MBh. 7, 5467.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्षिन्
निस्- + अपेक्षिन् निस्- + अपेक्षिन्, adj. indifferent, ib. 13, 6169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्ड|अपोगंडः|अपोगण्डः
अपोगण्ड अपोगण्ड, adj. Not under sixteen years of age, Man. 8, 148 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह|अपोहः
अपोह अपोह, i. e. अप-ऊह् + अ, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b " target="_blank">Page0036-b + 40</a>] Disconnecting reasoning, MBh. 13, 6725.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहन|अपोहनं
अपोहन अपोहन, i. e. अप-वह् + अन, n. Removal, Bhag. 15, 15 (of recollection and knowledge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्चर|अप्चरः
अप्चर अप्-चर, adj., f. रा, Living in water, Man. 7, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्वन्त्|अप्नस्वत्
अप्नस्वन्त् अप्नस् + वन्त् (अप्नस्, ved.), adj. Efficacious, Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. i. 112, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यय|अप्ययः
अप्यय अप्यय, i. e. अपि-इ + अ, m. Absorption.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेशप्रभवाप्यय
लोक-ईश-प्रभव- + अप्यय लोक-ईश-प्रभव- + अप्यय, adj. owing both origin and end to the guardians of the world, Man. 5, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजस्
अप्रजस् अप्रजस्, i. e. probably अ-प्र-जन् + अस्, adj. Childless, Rām. 1, 14, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं|अप्रतिरथः
अप्रतिरथ अ-प्रति-रथ (cf. the next), m. A leader in combat, Śāk. d. 95; 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिवीर्य|अप्रतिवीर्य्य
अप्रतिवीर्य अ-प्रति-वीर्य (अ-प्रति is a ved. word, Irresistible), adj. Of irresistible strength, Rām. 4, 35, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञता
अप्राज्ञता अ-प्राज्ञ-ता, f. Ignorance, Man. 4, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस् अप्सरस्, i. e. अप्-सृ + अस्, f. The name of female divinities; in the classical poetry the courtesans of paradise.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाप्सरस्
पञ्चाप्सरस् पञ्चाप्सरस्, i. e. पञ्चन्-, n. the name of a pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधक
अबाधक अ-बाध + क (see बाधा) adj., f. का, Unobstructed, Kathās. 26, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ज|अब्जः
अब्ज अब्ज, i. e. अप्-ज (vb. जन्),<BR> I. adj., f. जा, Born or produced in or by water, Man. 5, 112.<BR> II. n. A lotus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाब्ज|नीलाब्जं
नील- + अब्ज नील- + अब्ज, n. a blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्द|अब्दः
अब्द अब्द, i. e. अप्-द (vb. दा) m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. A year, Rājat. 5, 291.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्राब्द
कृच्छ्र- + अब्द कृच्छ्र- + अब्द, m. a year of penance, Man. 11, 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्द
त्रि- + अब्द त्रि- + अब्द, n. Three years, Man. 8, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धि|अब्धिः
अब्धि अब्धि, i. e. अप्-धा (cf. निधि), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a " target="_blank">Page0037-a + 41</a>] m. The occan, Kathās. 12, 113.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धि|क्षीराब्धिः
क्षीर- + अब्धि क्षीर- + अब्धि, m. the sea of milk, Kathās. 22, 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभि
अभि अभि (Towards, to).<BR> I. adv. On, Chr. 295, 10 = Rigv. i. 92, 10.<BR> II. prep. with acc. To, Ved. Chr. 287, 7 = Rigv. i. 48, 7; over, Chr. 292, 5 = Rigv. i. 86, 5.<BR> III. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> IV. Former part of compounded nouns and adverbs implying Towards, in presence of, very, cf. e. g. अभिताम्र; Quite, cf. अभिनव.<BR> --Cf. Goth. bî. The original form of this indeclinable was probably अम्भि = Gr. ἀμϕί; Lat. amb in amb-ire; O.H.G. umbi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक|अभिकः
अभिक अभि-क (vb. कम्) adj., f. का, Libidinous, Ragh. 19, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षा|अभिकांक्षा
अभिकाङ्क्षा अभि-काङ्क्ष् + आ, f. Desire, Rām. 3, 48, 15 (स्वर्गम् अभिकङ्क्षा, Desire of getting into heaven, with accus. like its verbal base).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षिन्|अभिकांक्षिन्
अभिकाङ्क्षिन् अभि-काङ्क्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Desiring, Chr. 7, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाम
अभिकाम अभिकाम, i. e. अभि-कम् + अ.<BR> I. m. Love.<BR> II. adj., f. मा, Loving, Rām. 1, 77, 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिकाम
स- + अभिकाम स- + अभिकाम, adj. loving, Nal. 24, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाल
अभिकाल अभिकाल, m. The name of a town, Rām. 2, 68, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम|अभिक्रमः
अभिक्रम अभि-क्रम् + अ, m. An undertaking, Bhag. 2, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या अभि-ख्या, f. Beauty, Megh. 78.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकोद्रेचिताभिख्य
अधिक-उद्-रेचित-अभिख्य अधिक-उद्-रेचित-अभिख्य, adj. exceedingly beautiful, Rājat. 5, 365.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाभिख्य|हंसाभिख्यं
हंस- + अभिख्य हंस- + अभिख्य, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांश्वभिख्य|हिमांश्वभिख्यं
हिमांशु- + अभिख्य हिमांशु- + अभिख्य, i. e. हिम-अंशु-, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम|अभिगमः
अभिगम अभि-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Approaching.<BR> 2. A visit, Megh. 50.<BR> 3. Sexual intercourse, Yājñ. 2, 291.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमन|अभिगमनं
अभिगमन अभि-गम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b " target="_blank">Page0037-b + 41</a>] Approaching.<BR> 2. Mounting, Kathās. 20, 154.<BR> 3. Sexual intercourse, Pañc. Pr. d. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभिगामिन् अभिगामिन्, i. e. अभि-गम् + इन् adj., f. नी, Approaching (for sexual intercourse), Man. 3, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभिघात अभिघात, i. e. अभि-हन् Caus. + अ, m.<BR> 1. Striking, Bhāṣāp. 117; Kir. 5, 42.<BR> 2. Hurting, affliction. Man. 12, 77.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राभिघात|वप्राभिघातः
वप्र- + अभिघात वप्र- + अभिघात, m. butting at a bank or mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातिन्
अभिघातिन् अभिघातिन्, i. e. अभि-हन्, Caus. + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Striking.<BR> 2. Hostile, Hit. iv. d. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचार|अभिचारः
अभिचार अभिचार, i. e. अभि-चर् + अ, m. Incantation, making charms for mischievous purposes, Man. 11, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजन|अभिजनः
अभिजन अभि-जन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Race, Rām. 3, 48, 18.<BR> 2. Family, Rām. 5, 87, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनन
अभिजनन अभि-जन् + अन, n. Production, Häberl. 524, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनवन्त्|अभिजनवत्
अभिजनवन्त् अभिजन + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Noble, Śāk. d. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजित्
अभिजित् अभि-जि + त्,<BR> I. m. The name of a sacrifice, Man. 11, 74.<BR> II. n. The name of the eighth Indian hour (मुहूर्त, comprising 48 minutes) of the day, (i. e. 24 minutes before and 24 minutes after midday), Rām. 6, 112, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञ|अभिज्ञः
अभिज्ञ अभि-ज्ञ (vb. ज्ञा), adj., f. ज्ञा, Knowing, conversant with, Rājat. 5, 383.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिज्ञ|अनभिज्ञः
अन्- + अभिज्ञ अन्- + अभिज्ञ, adj. ignorant, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञता
अभिज्ञता अभिज्ञ + ता, f. Knowledge, Ragh. 7, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञान|अभिज्ञानं
अभिज्ञान अभिज्ञान, i. e. अभि-ज्ञा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Remembrance, Rām. 5, 68, 1.<BR> 2. Recognition, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 12.<BR> 3. A token of remembrance, Rām. 2, 100, 6.<BR> 4. A sign by which [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a " target="_blank">Page0038-a + 40</a>] one proves himself to be a trustee, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितस्
अभितस् अभि + तस्, adv. and prep. with acc.<BR> 1. On both sides, Bhartṛ. 1, 80; Rām. 2, 45, 4.<BR> 2. From every side, round about, Rām. 2, 94, 20.<BR> 3. Near, Kir. 5, 14; also with gen. Rām. 1, 33, 22.<BR> 4. Completely, Kir. 5, 11.<BR> 5. Towards, in presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताप|अभितापः
अभिताप अभि-ताप, m.<BR> 1. Extreme heat, Śiś. 9, 1.<BR> 2. Great pain, Sāv. 5, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताम्र
अभिताम्र अभि-ताम्र, adj., f. रा, Very red, Kathās. 14, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितिग्मरश्मि
अभितिग्मरश्मि अभि-तिग्म-रश्मि, adv. Towards the sun, Śiś. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदर्शन|अभिदर्शनं
अभिदर्शन अभिदर्शन, i. e. अभि-दृश् + अन, n. Sight, Man. 9, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदूति
अभिदूति अभिदूति, i. e. अभि-दूती (cf. दूत), adv. To a female messenger, Śiś. 9, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रोह|अभिद्रोहः
अभिद्रोह अभिद्रोह, i. e. अभि-द्रुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Injury, Rām. 1, 26, 20.<BR> 2. Contumely, Man. 8, 271.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिद्रोह
अन्- + अभिद्रोह अन्- + अभिद्रोह, m. tenderness, Kathās. 13, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा अभि-धा, f.<BR> 1. A name, Rājat. 5, 379.<BR> 2. The primary sense of a word.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरवर्माभिध
शूरवर्माभिध शूरवर्माभिध, i. e. शूरवर्मन्-, adj. called Śūravarman, Rājat. 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधान|अभिधानं
अभिधान अभिधान, i. e. अभि-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. A name, Kathās. 7, 112.<BR> 2. A word.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुय्याभिधान
सुय्या- + अभिधान सुय्या- + अभिधान, adj., f. ना, called Suyyā, Rājat. 5, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिन्
अभिधायिन् अभिधायिन्, i. e. अभि-धा + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Speaking, Rām. 5, 14, 41.<BR> 2. Teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावक|अभिधावकः
अभिधावक अभि-धाव् + अक, adj. Running towards, hastening, Yājñ. 2, 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यान|अभिध्यानं
अभिध्यान अभिध्यान, i. e. अभि-ध्यै + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b " target="_blank">Page0038-b + 40</a>] n. Desire, covetousness, Man. 12, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्द|अभिनंद|अभिनन्दः
अभिनन्द अभि-नन्द् + अ, m., or f. दा, Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दिन्|अभिनंदिन्
अभिनन्दिन् अभि-नन्द् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Praising, Rām. 5, 59, 11.<BR> 2. Delighting, Rām. 3, 79, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनम्र
अभिनम्र अभि-नम्र, adj., f. रा, Bent, Ragh. 13, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनय|अभिनयः
अभिनय अभिनय, i. e. अभि-नी + अ, m. Dramatic performance, Vikr. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनव|अभिनवः
अभिनव अभि-नव, adj., f. वा, Quite new, Rājat. 5, 1.<BR> 2. Fresh, Bhartṛ. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनासिकाविवरम्
अभिनासिकाविवरम् अभि-नासिका-विवर + म्, adv. To the nostril, Śiś. 9, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेश|अभिनिवेशः
अभिनिवेश अभिनिवेश, i. e. अभि-नि-विश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Inclination, Vikr. 35, 13.<BR> 2. Adhering, Man. 12, 5.<BR> 3. Tenacity.<BR> 4. Determined resolution.<BR> समुपजाताभिनिवेशम्, i. e. सम्-उप-जात-अभिनिवेश + म्, adv. After having taken a determined resolution, Prab. 67, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशवन्त्
अभिनिवेशवन्त् अभिनिवेश + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Adhering, Yājñ. 3, 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशिन्
अभिनिवेशिन् अभिनिवेशिन्, i. e. अभिनिवेश + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Adhering.<BR> 2. Persevering, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपीतत्व
अभिपीतत्व अभि-पीत + त्व (vb. 1. पा), n. Condition of being saturated, MBh. 12, 12844.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपुष्प
अभिपुष्प अभि-पुष्प, adj. Covered with flowers, Rām. 6, 93, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राय|अभिप्रायः
अभिप्राय अभिप्राय, i. e. अभि-प्र-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Intention, Pañc. i. d. 366; wish, Rām. 3, 28, 31.<BR> 2. Opinion, Pañc. 150, 25.<BR> 3. Consideration, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 13 sqq.<BR> समष्टि-अभिप्रायेण, when taken collectively.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिप्राय
स- + अभिप्राय स- + अभिप्राय, adj. resolute, Pañc. 122, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेप्सु
अभिप्रेप्सु अभिप्रेप्सु, i. e. अभि-प्र-ईप्स, desider. of आप् + उ, adj. Ardently desiring, Man. 8, 344.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभर्तृ
अभिभर्तृ अभि-भर्तृ, adv. In the presence of the husband, Śiś. 9, 77; on the husband, ib. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभव|अभिभवः
अभिभव अभिभव, i. e. अभि-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. The being overpowered, Śāk. d. 40. 2. Defeat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिभव
निस्- + अभिभव निस्- + अभिभव, adj., not surpassable, Bhartṛ. 2, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवन|अभिभवनं
अभिभवन अभिभवन, i. e. अभि-भू + अन, n. The being overpowered, Man. 6, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाविन्
अभिभाविन् अभिभाविन्, i. e. अभि-भू + इन्, adj. Overpowering, Ragh. 1, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषण|अभिभाषणं
अभिभाषण अभिभाषण, i. e. अभि-भाष् + अन, n. Allocution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषिन्
अभिभाषिन् अभि-भाष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Addressing, Rām. 3, 49, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति अभि-भू + ति, f. Defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनस्
ऽअभिमनस् -अभि-मनस्, adj. Wishing for, Rām. 5, 38, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तृ|अभिमंतृ
अभिमन्तृ अभि-मन् + तृ, m. One who refers existing objects to one's own self, Man. 1, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभिमन्त्रण अभिमन्त्रण, i. e. अभि-मन्त्र् + अन, n. Consecration, Yājñ. 1, 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्द|अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्द अभिमर्द, i. e. अभि-मृद् + अ, m. Oppression, invasion, Draup. 6, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दन|अभिमर्द्दन
अभिमर्दन अभिमर्दन, i. e. अभि-मृद् + अन.<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Oppressing.<BR> II. n. Oppression, Rām. 6, 95, 8; invasion, 6, 100, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दिन्
अभिमर्दिन् अभिमर्दिन्, i. e. अभि-मृद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्श|अभिमर्शः
अभिमर्श अभिमर्श, i. e. अभि-मृश् + अ, m. Touching improperly, Śāk. d. 116. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b " target="_blank">Page0039-b + 41</a>] Sometimes it is written incorrectly with ष् instead of श्, Man. 8, 352.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शक
अभिमर्शक अभिमर्शक, i. e. अभि-म्रिश् + अक, adj. Touching improperly.<BR> --With ष् instead of श् (see the last), Rām. 1, 7, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शन|अभिमर्शनं
अभिमर्शन अभिमर्शन, i. e. अभि-मृश्-अन, n. Touching improperly, Yājñ. 2, 284. Also incorrectly (see the last) with षण instead of शन, Rām. 6, 66, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शिन्
अभिमर्शिन् अभिमर्शिन्, i. e. अभि-मृश्-इन्, adj., f. नी, Courting, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्ष|अभिमर्षः
अभिमर्ष, -मर्षक, -मर्षण See अभिमर्श, -मर्शक, -मर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमातिन्
अभिमातिन् अभिमातिन्, i. e. अभि-मन् + ति + इन्, m. An enemy, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभिमान अभिमान, i. e. अभि-मन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Referring existing objects to one's own self, egotism, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 2.<BR> 2. Self-conceit, pride, Bhartṛ. 3, 4.<BR> 3. Love, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिमान
निस्- + अभिमान निस्- + अभिमान, adj. exempt from pride, Bhāg. P. 5, 15, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिमान
स- + अभिमान स- + अभिमान, adj. proud, Rājat. 5, 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानवन्त्|अभिमानवत्
अभिमानवन्त् अभिमान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानित्व
ऽअभिमानित्व अभिमानित्व, i. e. अभिमानिन् + त्व, n. State of one who refers existing objects to his own self, egotism, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन् अभिमानिन्, i. e. अभिमान + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Proud, Rām. 3, 37, 16.<BR> 2. Fancying, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 12 (नरेन्द्राभिमानिन्, having the fancy of being a physician).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख अभि-मुख, adj., f. खा or खी.<BR> 1. Facing, fronting, Rām. 1, 71, 18: with acc. Directed towards. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a " target="_blank">Page0040-a + 41</a>] Rām. 2, 1, 34; towards, Bhag. 11, 28; opposite, Rām. 5, 71, 9.<BR> 2. Near, Vikr. d. 28.<BR> 3. Ready for, Ragh. 5, 29.<BR> 4. Favourable, Rām. 2, 109, 23. Acc. खम्, adv. Opposite to, Man. 2, 193; towards, Pañc. 40, 17; to, Rām. 1, 45, 48; near, Megh. 69. Loc. खे, adv. Opposite, Rām. 6, 19, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननाभिमुख
कानन- + अभिमुख कानन- + अभिमुख, adv. to the wood, Pañc. 63, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाभिमुख
दक्षिणा- + अभिमुख दक्षिणा- + अभिमुख, adj. turned to the south, Man. 4, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाचना
अभियाचना अभि-याच् + अना, f. A request, at the end of the comp. adj. सत्य-अभियाचन, Fulfilling the requests (which are directed to him), Rām. 2, 55, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातृ
अभियातृ अभि-या + तृ, m. An aggressor, Rām. 2, 1, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियान|अभियानं
अभियान अभियान, i. e. अभि-या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Approaching.<BR> 2. Aggression, Chr. 53, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायिन्
अभियायिन् अभियायिन्, i. e. अभि-या + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Approaching, Rām. 6, 16, 56.<BR> 2. Assaulting, Ragh. 12, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभियोक्तृ अभियोक्तृ, i. e. अभि-युज् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. An enemy.<BR> 2. A plaintiff. Man. 8, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग|अभियोगः
अभियोग अभियोग, i. e. अभि-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Exertion, Rām. 5, 51, 16.<BR> 2. Attack.<BR> 3. A charge, Yājñ. 2, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभियोगिन् अभियोगिन्, i. e. अभि-युज् + इन्, adj. Accusing, a plaintiff, Yājñ. 2, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षितृ
अभिरक्षितृ अभि-रक्ष् + इतृ, m. A protector, Man. 7, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरति|अभिरतिः
अभिरति अभिरति, i. e. अभि-रम् + ति, f. Delight, Hit. i. d. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभिराम अभिराम, i. e. अभि-रम् + अ, adj., f. मा, Charming, delighting Rām. 3, 49, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचि|अभिरुचिः
अभिरुचि अभि-रुच् + इ, f. Delight, desire, Bhartṛ. 2, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचिर
अभिरुचिर अभि-रुचिर, adj., f. रा, Very beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप अभि-रूप, adj., f. पा.<BR> 1. Suitable.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Man. 9, 88.<BR> 3. Learned, Man. 3, 144.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिरूप
अन्- + अभिरूप अन्- + अभिरूप, adj. ugly, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्ष्यम्
अभिलक्ष्यम् अभि-लक्ष्य + म्, adv. Towards the mark, Rām. 2, 63, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलङ्घन|अभिलंघन|अभिलंघनं
अभिलङ्घन अभि-लङ्घ् + अन, n. Jumping over, Rām. 5, 53, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाष|अभिलाषः
अभिलाष अभिलाष, i. e. अभि-लष् + अ, m. Desire, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिलाष
निस्- + अभिलाष निस्- + अभिलाष, adj. indifferent, Śāk. d. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिलाष
स- + अभिलाष स- + अभिलाष, adj., f. षा, eager, Dev. 1, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिलाषम्
साभिलाष + म् साभिलाष + म्, adv. passionately, Śāk. 33, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषक
अभिलाषक अभिलाषक, i. e. अभि-लष् + अक, adj. Desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषिन्
अभिलाषिन् अभिलाषिन्, i. e. अभि-लष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Desirous, Śāk. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषुक|अभिलाषुकः
अभिलाषुक अभिलाषुक, i. e. अभि-लष् + उक, adj., f. का, Desiring (with acc.), Kir. 11, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवदन|अभिवदनं
अभिवदन अभि-वद् + अन, n. Address, allocution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्दन|अभिवंदनं
अभिवन्दन अभि-वन्द् + अन, n. Respectful salutation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपादाभिवन्दन
कृत-पाद- + अभिवन्दन कृत-पाद- + अभिवन्दन, adj., f. ना, literally, having performed a respectful salutation of the feet, i. e. having made a respectful salutation, Kathās. 22, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्तिन्|अभिवर्त्तिन्
अभिवर्तिन् अभिवर्तिन्, i. e. अभि-वृत् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Approaching, Rām. 6, 88, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्षण|अभिवर्षणं
अभिवर्षण अभिवर्षण, i. e. अभि-वृष् + अन, n. Raining upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्षिन्
अभिवर्षिन् अभिवर्षिन्, i. e. अभि-वृष्-इन्, adj., f. इणी, Throwing upon, Rām. 1, 28, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद|अभिवादः
अभिवाद अभिवाद, i. e. अभि-वद् + अ, m. Salutation, Man. 2, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभिवादक अभिवादक, i. e. अभि-वद् + अक, adj., f. दिका, Greeting, Nal. 21, 24 (भवन्तम् अभिवादकह्, in order to salute you).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादन|अभिवादनं
अभिवादन अभिवादन, i. e. अभि-वद् + अन, n. Respectful salutation, Man. 2, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाह्य
अभिवाह्य अभिवाह्य, i. e. अभि-वह् + य, n. Offering, Man. 1, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृद्धि|अभिवृद्धिः
अभिवृद्धि अभिवृद्धि, i. e. अभि-वृध् + ति, f. Growth, exaltation, Man. 7, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्ति|अभिव्यक्तिः
अभिव्यक्ति अभिव्यक्ति, i. e. अभि-वि-अञ्ज् + ति, f. Manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यञ्जक|अभिव्यंजक
अभिव्यञ्जक अभिव्यञ्जक, i. e. अभि-वि-अञ्ज् + अक, adj. Manifesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसन|अभिशंसनं
अभिशंसन अभि-शंस् + अन, n. Slandering Man. 8, 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसिन्
अभिशंसिन् अभि-शंस् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Slandering, Yājñ. 3, 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्का|अभिशंका
अभिशङ्का अभि-शङ्क् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Suspecting, Rām. 6, 66, 26.<BR> 2. Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तक
अभिशस्तक अभि-शस्त + क (vb. शंस्), adj.<BR> 1. Accused, Yājñ. 1, 223.<BR> 2. Inflicted, imprecated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ति|अभिशस्तिः
अभिशस्ति अभिशस्ति, i. e. अभि-शंस् + ति, f. Defamation, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशान्त्व|अभिशांत्वः|अभिशान्त्वः
अभिशान्त्व अभि-शान्त्व् + अ, m. Conciliating manner, Rām. 5, 56, 44 (written with स् instead of श्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशाप|अभिशापः
अभिशाप अभिशाप, i. e. अभि-शप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A curse, Rām. 3, 8, 12.<BR> 2. A heavy charge.<BR> 3. Calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषङ्ग|अभिषंग|अभिषंगः|अभिषङ्गः
अभिषङ्ग अभिषङ्ग, i. e. अभि-सञ्ज्+ अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b " target="_blank">Page0041-b + 40</a>] m.<BR> 1. Attachment.<BR> 2. An oath, Chr. 53, 23.<BR> 3. A curse.<BR> 4. Defeat, Ragh. 2, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक|अभिषेकः
अभिषेक अभिषेक, i. e. अभि-सिच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sprinkling with water, inauguration of a king, Pañc. iii. d. 267.<BR> 2. The water used for an inauguration.<BR> 3. Ablution, Śāk. 50, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचन|अभिषेचनं
अभिषेचन अभिषेचन, i. e. अभि-सिच् + अन, n. Inauguration of a king, Rām. 3, 53, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टव|अभिष्टवः
अभिष्टव अभिष्टव, i. e. अभि-स्तु + अ, m. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्द|अभिष्यंदः|अभिष्यन्दः
अभिष्यन्द अभिष्यन्द, i. e. अभि-स्यन्द् + अ, m. Great increase, Ragh. 15, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्वङ्ग|अभिष्वंग|अभिष्वंगः|अभिष्वङ्गः
अभिष्वङ्ग अभिष्वङ्ग, i. e. अभि-स्वञ्ज् + अ, m. Attachment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिष्वङ्ग|अनभिष्वंग
अन्- + अभिष्वङ्ग अन्- + अभिष्वङ्ग, adj. without attachment, Bhag. 13, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंश्रय|अभिसंश्रयः
अभिसंश्रय अभिसंश्रय, i. e. अभि-सम्-श्रि + अ, m. Refuge, Rām. 4, 54, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंदेह|अभिसन्देह|अभिसंदेहः
अभिसंदेह अभिसंदेह, i. e. अभि-सम्-दिह् + अ, m. The organ of generation, Chr. 58, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधक|अभिसन्धक|अभिसंधकः
अभिसंधक अभिसंधक, i. e. अभि-सम्-ध + क (vb. धा), m. A calumniator, Man. 4, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधा|अभिसन्धा
अभिसंधा अभि-सं-धा, f. Promise.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याभिसंध
सत्याभिसंध सत्याभिसंध, i. e. सत्य-, adj. one who keeps his promises true, Rām. 1, 6, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधान|अभिसन्धान|अभिसंधानं|अभिसन्धानं
अभिसंधान अभि-सं-धा + न, n.<BR> 1. Promise.<BR> 2. Deceiving. Ragh. 17, 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याभिसंधान
सत्य- + अभिसंधान सत्य- + अभिसंधान, adj., f. ना, keeping one's promises true, Rām. 5, 31, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधि|अभिसन्धि|अभिसंधिः|अभिसन्धिः
अभिसंधि अभिसंधि, i. e. अभि-सम्धा (cf. निधि), m. Intention, Pañc. 200, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधित
अभिसंधित अभिसंधित, see धा with अभि-सम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबन्ध|अभिसम्बन्ध|अभिसंबंधः|अभिसंबन्धः
अभिसंबन्ध अभिसंबन्ध, i. e. अभि-सम्-बन्ध् + अ, m. Union, Man. 5, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर|अभिसरः
अभिसर अभिसर, i. e. अभि-सृ + अ, m. Companion, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 1; 201, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरण|अभिसरणं
अभिसरण अभिसरण, i. e. अभि-सृ + अन, n. An amorous visit, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ग|अभिसर्गः
अभिसर्ग अभिसर्ग, i. e. अभि-सृज् + अ, m. Creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसान्त्व|अभिसांत्वः|अभिसान्त्वः
अभिसान्त्व अभिसान्त्व, see अभिशान्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसार|अभिसारः
अभिसार अभिसार, i. e. अभि-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A lover's appointment, a rendezvous.<BR> 2. An attack, Rām. 6, 9, 19.<BR> 3. plur. The name of a people.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहाभिसार|लोहाभिसारः
लोह- + अभिसार लोह- + अभिसार, m. lustration of arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभिसारिका अभिसारिका, i. e. अभि-सृ-अक, f. A woman who goes to a rendezvous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसेवन|अभिसेवनं
अभिसेवन अभि-सेव् + अन, n. Indulgence, habitual practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरण|अभिहरणं
अभिहरण अभिहरण, i. e. अभि-हृ + अन, n. Conveying, Ragh. 11, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहार|अभिहारः
अभिहार अभिहार, i. e. अभि-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Seizing.<BR> 2. Robbing.<BR> 3. Attack.<BR> 4. Arming.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाभिहार
लोक- + अभिहार लोक- + अभिहार, m. lustration of arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्णम्
अभीक्ष्णम् अभीक्ष्णम्, i. e. probably अभि-ईक्षण + म् (cf. क्षण), adv.<BR> 1. Every moment, continually.<BR> 2. Repeatedly.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभीक्ष्णम्
अन्- + अभीक्ष्णम् अन्- + अभीक्ष्णम्, adv. seldom, Rām. 2, 71, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्णशस्
अभीक्ष्णशस् अभीक्ष्ण + शस्, adv. Continually, Rām. 2, 46, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीतवत्
अभीतवत् अ-भीत + वत्, adv. Like a fearless one, Rām. 6, 28, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सु
अभीप्सु अभीप्सु, i. e. अभि-ईप्स, desider. of आप् + उ, adj. Desiring, Nal. 5, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान अभीमान = अभिमान. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b " target="_blank">Page0042-b + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभीमान
निस्- + अभीमान निस्- + अभीमान, adj., f. ना, 1. devoid of egotism, MBh. 7, 2019. 2. devoid of pride, MBh. 4, 14668.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशाप|अभीशापः
अभीशाप अभीशाप, अभिशाप, Yājñ. 2, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशु|अभीशुः
अभीशु अभीशु, i. e. अभि-ईश् + उ, m. A bridle, Śāk. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग्घन्
अभोग्घन् अभोग्घन्, i. e. अ-भुज्-हन्, adj. Slaying those who do not feed (the gods), i. e. who do not sacrifice, impious, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. 1, 64, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंग|अभ्यंगः|अभ्यङ्गः
अभ्यङ्ग अभ्यङ्ग, i. e. अबि-अञ्ज् + अ, m. Unction, Man. 2, 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यञ्जन|अभ्यंजन|अभ्यंजनं|अभ्यञ्जनं
अभ्यञ्जन अभ्यञ्जन, i. e. अभि-अञ्ज् + अन, n. Anointing, Man. 10, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक अभ्यधिक, i. e. अभि-अधिक, adj., Exceeding, preeminent, Rām. 5, 82, 13. Superior, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 2. Acc. कम्, adv. Exceedingly, Rām. 5, 73, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा अभ्यनुज्ञा, i. e. अभि-अनु-ज्ञा, f. Permission.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यनुज्ञा
अन्- + अभ्यनुज्ञा अन्- + अभ्यनुज्ञा, f. want of permission, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 7 (without the permission of the father).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभ्यनुज्ञ
कृत- + अभ्यनुज्ञ कृत- + अभ्यनुज्ञ, adj., f. ज्ञा, having received the permission to withdraw, dismissed, Rām. 5, 76, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञान|अभ्यनुज्ञानं
अभ्यनुज्ञान अभ्यनुज्ञान, i. e. अभि-अनु-ज्ञा + अन, n. Assent, Rām. 1, 3, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर अभ्यन्तर, i. e. अभि-अन्तर.<BR> I. adj., f. रा,<BR> 1. Interior, Kathās. 4, 51. Being within, Rām. 6, 112, 43 (in the town). Belonging to, Man. 3, 154.<BR> 2. Conversant in, Rām. 6, 5, 19.<BR> 3. Intimate, Pañc. i. d. 290 (perhaps to be read आभ्य्˚).<BR> 4. Secret, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 9.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The interior, the space within. Bhag. 5, 27.<BR> 2. An interval, Pañc. 5, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरीकरण|अभ्यंतरीकरणं
अभ्यन्तरीकरण अभ्यन्तरीकरण, i. e. अभ्यन्तर-कृ + अन, n. Initiation. Daśak. in Chr. 180, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्चन|अभ्यर्चनं|अभ्यर्च्चन
अभ्यर्चन अभ्यर्चन, i. e. अभि-अर्च् + अन, n. Worship, Man. 2, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण्ण|अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं
अभ्यर्ण्ण अभ्यर्ण्ण, i. e. अभि-अर्न्ण (vb. अर्द्).<BR> I. adj., f. णा, Near.<BR> II. n. Proximity, Rājat. 5, 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थना
अभ्यर्थना अभ्यर्थना, i. e. अभि-अर्थ् + अन, f. Request, Sāv. 4, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थिन्
अभ्यर्थिन् अभ्यर्थिन्, i. e. अभि-अर्थ् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हणीयता
अभ्यर्हणीयता अभ्यर्हणीयता, i. e. अभि-अर्हणीय + ता (vb. अर्ह्), f. Great venerableness, Man. 9, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्यवहार अभ्यवहार, i. e. अभि-अव-हृ + अ, m. Eating, Man. 6, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्य|अभ्यवहार्य्य
अभ्यवहार्य अभ्यवहार्य, i. e. अभ्यवहार + य, adj. Fit to be taken as food, eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसन|अभ्यसनं
अभ्यसन अभ्यसन, i. e. अभि- 2. अस् + अन, n. Study, Bhag. 17, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यसन
अन्- + अभ्यसन अन्- + अभ्यसन, n. laziness, Rām. 5, 19, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक अभ्यसूयक, i. e. अभि-असूय + अक, adj. Detracting, a detractor, Bhag. 16, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूया
अभ्यसूया अभ्यसूया, i. e. अभि-असूय + अ, f.<BR> 1. Detraction, envy.<BR> 2. Wrath, Megh. 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
स- + अभ्यसूय स- + अभ्यसूय, adj. envious, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम|अभ्यागमः
अभ्यागम अभ्यागम, i. e. अभि-आ-गम् + अ, m. A visit, Ragh. 16, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमन|अभ्यागमनं
अभ्यागमन अभ्यागमन, i. e. अभि-आ-गम् + अन, n. Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघात|अभ्याघातः
अभ्याघात अभ्याघात, i. e. अभि-आ-हन्, Caus. + अ, m. Assault (by robbers), Man. 9, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश अभ्याश, i. e. अभि- 1. अश् + अ, often written अभ्यास (q. cf.) but incorrectly.<BR> I. adj., f. शा, Near, Kumāras. 6, 2.<BR> II. n. Proximity, Rām. 4, 59, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्यास अभ्यास, i. e. अभि- 2. अस् + अ (cf. अभ्याश), m.<BR> 1. Repetition, Man. 12, 74. Repetition of words, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 8; 9.<BR> 2. Repeated practice, Rājat. 5, 164; 439. Use, Yājñ. 3, 68.<BR> 3. Reading, Man. 4, 148. Study, Pañc. 220, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षण|अभ्युक्षणं
अभ्युक्षण अभ्युक्षण, i. e. अभि-उक्ष् + अन, n. Sprinkling, Ragh. 16, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थान|अभ्युत्थानं
अभ्युत्थान अभ्युत्थान, i. e. अभि-उद्-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rising, Rām. 6, 72, 65.<BR> 2. Rising from one's seat as mark of respect, Pañc. ii. d. 65.<BR> 3. Origin, Bhag. 4, 7.<BR> 4. Elevation, dignity, Ragh. 4, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पतन|अभ्युत्पतनं
अभ्युत्पतन अभ्युत्पतन, i. e. अभि-उद्-पत् + अन, n. Assault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय अभ्युदय, i. e. अभि-उद्-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Prosperity, Bhartṛ. 2, 53. Wealth, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 19.<BR> 2. A festival, Man. 9, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयिन्
अभ्युदयिन् अभ्युदयिन्, i. e. अभि-उद्-इ + इन्, adj., f. नी, Arising, impending, Rājat. 5, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गम|अभ्युद्गमः
अभ्युद्गम अभ्युद्गम, i. e. अभि-उद्-गम् + अ, m. Rising from one's seat as mark of respect, Kathās. 24, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम|अभ्युपगमः
अभ्युपगम अभ्युपगम, i. e. अभि-उप-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Arrival.<BR> 2. Assenting, agreement, Man. 9, 53.<BR> 3. Admitting to be true, Mālav. 15, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्ति|अभ्युपपत्तिः
अभ्युपपत्ति अभ्युपपत्ति, i. e. अभि-उप-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Defence, Man. 8, 112.<BR> 2. Protection, Daśak. in Chr. 179 19.<BR> 3. Assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाय|अभ्युपायः
अभ्युपाय अभ्युपाय, i. e. अभि-उप-इ + अ, m. An expedient, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 3; 191, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्
अभ्र् अभ्र्, i. 1, Par. To roam (probably for बभ्र्, a mutilated redupl. of भ्रम् cf. अन्दोलय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र अभ्र (akin to अम्भस्), n.<BR> 1. A cloud, especially a rain-cloud, Man. 4, 104.<BR> 2. Atmosphere, Pañc. i. d. 209. Heaven, Śiś. 9, 3.<BR> --Cf. अम्भस्, ὄμβρος; Lat. imber, and probably umbra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह अभ्रंलिह, i. e. अभ्र + म्-लिह् + अ.<BR> I. adj., f. हा, Touching the clouds, very lofty, Megh. 65.<BR> II. m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशक
अभ्रावकाशक अभ्रावकाशक, i. e. अभ्र-अवकाश + क, adj. Uncovered (see the next), Rām. 1, 63, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिक
अभ्रावकाशिक अभ्रावकाशिक, i. e. अभ्र-अवकाश + इक, adj. Having the clouds for shelter, uncovered, Man. 6, 23 (read आभ्रा˚ आभ्रा˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिन्
अभ्रावकाशिन् अभ्रावकाशिन्, i. e. अभ्र-अवकाश + इन्, Uncovered (see the last), Rām. 3, 10, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रि|अभ्रिः
अभ्रि अभ्रि, f. A sharp pointed stick, Man. 11, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रित
अभ्रित अभ्रित, i. e. अभ्र + इत, adj., f. ता, Clouded, Ragh. 3, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् अम्, i. 1, Par., with prep. also Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To sound.<BR> --<BR> I. 10, Par. To be ill (ved.). The original notion was ‘to be hard, strong, powerful.’<BR> --Cf. अंस, आम, and many ved. significations and derivatives; Lat. emo, properly ‘to take,’ demo; περιημεκτέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रक|अमंत्रक
अमन्त्रक अ-मन्त्र + क, adj., f. रिका, Not accompanied by a मन्त्र or vedic verse, Man. 2, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम अ-मम (the latter part is the gen. sing. of the pronoun of the first person, in the sense of a possessive pronoun), adj., f. मा, Devoid of selfish affection, Man. 6, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर अमर, i. e. अ-मृ + अ.<BR> I. adj., f. रा and री, Immortal, Man. 2, 148; Rām. 1, 34, 16.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A god, Man. 7, 72.<BR> 2. The name of a Marut and of a mountain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरामर|धरामरः
धरा- + अमर धरा- + अमर, m. a Brāhmaṇa, Mārk. P. 26, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर
स- + अमर स- + अमर, adj. with the gods, Rām. 3, 53, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरत्व|अमरत्वं
अमरत्व अमर + त्व, n. Immortality, Arj. 3, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोकता
अमरलोकता अमर-लोक + ता, f. The happiness of the world of gods, Man. 2, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरावती अमरावती, i. e. अमर + वन्त् + ई. The capital of Indra, Rām. 3, 53, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यत्व
अमर्त्यत्व अ-मर्त्य + त्व, n. Immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षिन्
अमर्षिन् अमर्षिन्, i. e. अ-मृष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Unable to endure, impatient, Draup. 7, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलय
अमलय अमलय, a denom. derived from अ-मल, Par. To make white, Kir. 5, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्य|अमात्यः
अमात्य अमा + त्य (the basis signifies in the Vedas ‘in the house’).<BR> I. adj. Being in the house.<BR> II. m. (A companion of the king) A minister, Rājat. 5, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्य|महामात्यः
महा- + अमात्य महा- + अमात्य, m. a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामात्य
स- + अमात्य स- + अमात्य, adj. with the ministers, Chr. 18, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजनामात्य
स-जनामात्य स-जनामात्य, i. e. -जन-अमात्य, adj. together with people and ministers, Chr. 53, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानन|अमाननं
अमानन अमानन, i. e. अ-मन् + अन, n. Disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानित्व|अमानित्वं
अमानित्व अमानित्व, i. e. अ-मानिन् + त्व, n. Humility, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावासी
अमावासी अमावासी, and अमावास्या अमावास्या, i. e. अमा (cf. अमात्य) -वास + य, f. The day of the conjunction of the sun and moon, the day of the new moon, Man. 4, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रता
अमित्रता अ-मित्र + ता, f. Enmity, Pañc. ii. d. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्राय
अमित्राय अमित्राय, a denom. derived from अ-मित्र by य, Ātm. To behave like an enemy, Bhartṛ. 3, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीव|अमीवं|अमीवः
अमीव अम् + ईव, n. Pain, Rām. 3, 59, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक अमु + क (cf. अदस्), adj., f. का, Instead of a proper name, Mr. so and so, Yājñ. 2, 86 sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतस्
अमुतस् अमु + तस् (cf. अदस्), adv.<BR> 1. = abl. of अदस्, From that, from him, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 8.<BR> 2. From thence, from the other world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र अमु + त्र (cf. अदस्), adv.<BR> 1. There, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 14.<BR> 2. In the other world, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत अ-मृत.<BR> I. adj., f. ता, Immortal, Bhag. 14, 27.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A god.<BR> 2. The soul.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. The beverage of the gods, nectar.<BR> 2. A medicine preventing old age, prolonging life, and awakening the dead, Lass. 33, 20.<BR> 3. A medicament; nectar and medicament, Śiś. 9, 36.<BR> 4. The residue of sacrificial food, Man. 3, 285.<BR> 5. Unsolicited alms, Man. 4, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἄμβροτος, ἀμβροσία.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवामृत
गव- + अमृत गव- + अमृत, n. अमृत, consisting of rays, MBh. 3, 17351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतत्व|अमृतत्वं
अमृतत्व अमृत + त्व, n. Immortality, Man. 6, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमय
अमृतमय अमृत + मय, adj., f. यी, Like nectar, Pañc. 206, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतलतिका
अमृतलतिका अमृतलतिका, i. e. अमृत-लता + क, f. A small creeper as beautiful as nectar (denoting a beautiful woman), Śrut. (Br.) 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रुत्
अमृतस्रुत् अमृत-स्रु + त्, adj. Shedding nectar, Śiś. 5, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताय
अमृताय अमृताय denom. derived from अमृत by य, Ātm. To be like nectar, Ragh. 2, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्|अंब्
† अम्ब् अम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go; Ātm. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर|अंबर|अंबरं|अम्बरं|अम्बरः
अम्बर अम्बर (akin to अम्भस्, cf. स्तम्भ् and स्तम्ब).<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sky, Rām. 3, 55, 9.<BR> 2. Cloth, Rām. 3, 55, 5. Sky and garment, Śiś. 9, 7.<BR> II. m. plur. The name of a people.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरम्बर
निस्- + अम्बर निस्- + अम्बर, adj., f. रा, naked, MBh. 12, 7775.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्बर|मदांबर|मदाम्बरः
मद- + अम्बर मद- + अम्बर, m. an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अंबष्ठः|अम्बष्ठः
अम्बष्ठ अम्बष्ठ, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1189.<BR> 2. The offspring of a Brāhmaṇa father and a Vaiśyā mother, Man. 10, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बा अम्बा (voc. sing. अम्ब; in the Veda also अम्बे).<BR> 1. f. A mother, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 855.<BR> 2. A proper name, Chr. 4, 10.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. amma and ama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बालिका|अंबालिका
अम्बालिका अम्बालिका, and अम्बिका अम्बिका (akin to अम्बा), f. Proper names, Chr. 4, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बु|अंबु
अम्बु अम्बु (akin to अम्भस्, cf. अम्बर), n. Water, Pañc. iii. d. 33.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्माम्बु|घर्मांबु|घर्म्माम्बु
घर्म- + अम्बु घर्म- + अम्बु, n. sweat, Suśr. 2, 343, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलाम्बु|तिलांबु
तिल- + अम्बु तिल- + अम्बु, n. water with sesame, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरम्बु|निरंबु
निस्- + अम्बु निस्- + अम्बु, adj. abstaining from water, Bhāg. P. 7, 3, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुज|अम्बुजं|अम्बुजः
अम्बुज अम्बु-ज (vb. जन्).<BR> I. adj., f. जा, Born in water, Rām. 4, 25, 24.<BR> II. n. A lotus, Rām. 5, 13, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुजस्थ
अम्बुजस्थ अम्बुज-स्थ (vb. स्था), adj., f. था, Sitting on a lotus, Ṛt. 6, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुद|अम्बुदः
अम्बुद अम्बु-द (vb. दा), m. A cloud, Ṛt. 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुधर
अम्बुधर अम्बु-धर, m. A cloud, Rām. 5, 16, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुधि|अम्बुधिः
अम्बुधि अम्बुधि, i. e. अम्बु-धा (cf. निधि), m. The occan, Rājat. 5, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a " target="_blank">Page0046-a + 39</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराम्बुधि
क्षार- + अम्बुधि क्षार- + अम्बुधि, m. the salt ocean, Bhartṛ. 2, 6 (Häb.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराम्बुधि
क्षीर- + अम्बुधि क्षीर- + अम्बुधि, m. he sea of milk, Kathās. 17, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमुच्
अम्बुमुच् अम्बु-मुच्, m. A cloud, Kir. 5, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुरुह|अम्बुरुहः
अम्बुरुह अम्बु-रुह् + अ, n. A lotus, Kir. 5, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाम्बुरुह
हेम- + अम्बुरुह हेम- + अम्बुरुह, n. a golden lotus, Ṛt. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भ्|अंभ्
† अम्भ् अम्भ्, i. 1, Ātm. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्|अंभस्
अम्भस् अम्भस्, n. Water, Bhartṛ. 2, 91; Śiś. 9, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदम्भस्|उदंभस्
उद्- + अम्भस् उद्- + अम्भस्, adj. abounding in water, Ragh. 4, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्माम्भस्|घर्मांभस्
घर्म- + अम्भस् घर्म- + अम्भस्, n. sweat, Śāk. d. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणाम्भस्|लवणांभस्
लवण- + अम्भस् लवण- + अम्भस्, n. the sea of salt water, Matsyop. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोज|अम्भोजं|अम्भोजः
अम्भोज अम्भोज, i. e. अम्भस्-ज (vb. जन्), n. A lotus flower, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1447.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाम्भोज|हेमांभोज
हेम- + अम्भोज हेम- + अम्भोज, n. a golden lotus flower, Megh. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजिनी|अंभोजिनी
अम्भोजिनी अम्भोजिनी, i. e. अम्भोज + इन् + ई, f. An assemblage of lotus flowers, Bhartṛ. 2, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोद|अम्भोदः
अम्भोद अम्भोद, i. e. अम्भस्-द (vb. दा), m. A cloud, Rām. 5, 40, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधर|अम्भोधरः
अम्भोधर अम्भोधर, i. e. अम्भस्-धर, m. A cloud, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधि|अम्भोधिः
अम्भोधि अम्भोधि, i. e. अम्भस्-धा (cf. निधि), m. The ocean, Kathās. 19, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोरुह्
अम्भोरुह् अम्भोरुह्, and अम्भोरुह अम्भोरुह, i. e. अम्भस्-रुह् and रुह् + अ, n. A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्मय|अम्मयं
अम्मय अम्मय, i. e. अप् + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of water, watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ल|अम्लं|अम्लः
अम्ल अम्ल, m. Sourness, Rām. 5, 14, 45; Man. 5, 114 (acids). Perhaps from vb. अम्.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ăm + ârus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय्
अय् अय्, see इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय अय, i. e. इ + अ. m.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. Good luck. Ragh. 4, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन अयन, i. e. इ + अन, n.<BR> 1. A place of motion, Man. 1, 10.<BR> 2. A road.<BR> 3. A line, Bhag. 1, 11.<BR> 4. The half year, i. e. the sun's road north and south of the equator, Man. 4, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरायण|उत्तरायणं
उत्तरा- + अयन उत्तरा- + अयन, Man. 6, 10; and उदगयन, i. e. उदञ्च्-, Man. 1, 67, n. the half of the year in which the sun is to the north of the equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायन|दक्षिणायनं
दक्षिणा- + अयन दक्षिणा- + अयन,<BR> I. n. the half of the year when the sun moves to the south of the equator, Man. 1, 67.<BR> II. adj. lying on the course of the sun to the south of the equator, Bhāg. P. 5, 23, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतायन
गीत- + अयन गीत- + अयन, n. a procession accompanied by hymns, Bhāg. P. 4, 4, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणायन
गुण- + अयन गुण- + अयन, adj. walking the path of virtue, Bhāg. P. 4, 21, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तायन|वार्तायन|वार्त्तायनः
वार्त्ता- + अयन वार्त्ता- + अयन, m. a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयवन्त्|अयवत्
अयवन्त् अय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Happy, Kir. 5, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्
अयस् अयस् (probably अ-यम् + अस्), n. Iron.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. aes; Goth. eis + arn; A.S. isern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णायस्
कृष्ण- + अयस् कृष्ण- + अयस्, n. iron, MBh. 13, 6225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कान्त|अयस्कान्तः
अयस्कान्त अयस्-कान्त (vb. कम्), m. A loadstone, Ragh. 17, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्मय
अयस्मय अयस् + मय, adj., f. यी, Of iron, Arj. 10, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अया
अया अया, Ved. (old instr. sing of इदम्) Thus, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4; but in this passage rather for अयास्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयास्
अयास् अयास्, i. e. अ-यस्, adj. Indefatigable (?), Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयि
अयि अयि,<BR> 1. A vocative particle, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 16.<BR> 2. An interrogative particle, Pañc. 38, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अयुज् अ-युज्, adj. Odd, Man. 3, 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतशस्
अयुतशस् अ-युत + शस्, adv. Ten thousand-fold, Indr. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये अये, interj. Oh! Ah!<BR> 1. Of surprise, Vikr. 11, 3.<BR> 2. Of calling, Bhartṛ. 3, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगव|अयोगवः
अयोगव अयोगव, m. An आयोगवी woman (? cf. आयोगव), Man. 10, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिज|अयोनिजः
अयोनिज अ-योनि-ज (vb. जन्), adj. Not born in the natural way, Ragh. 11, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिजत्व
अयोनिजत्व अयोनिज + त्व, n. A supernatural birth, Rājat. 5, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमय
अयोमय अयोमय, i. e. अयस् + मय, adj., f. यी, Iron, Man. 11, 103 (read तल्पे, instead of तप्ते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर अर, i. e. ऋ + अ, m. The spoke of a wheel, Śāk. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्ट|अरघट्टः
अरघट्ट अर-घट्ट् + अ, m. A wheel or a machine for raising water from a well, Pañc. 209, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणि|अरणिः
अरणि and -णी अरणी̆, f. Wood used for kindling a fire by attrition, Pañc. i. d. 247; Rām. 2, 104, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्य|अरण्यं|अरण्यः
अरण्य अरण्य, n. A forest.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मारण्य|धर्म्मारण्य|धर्म्मारण्यं
धर्म- + अरण्य धर्म- + अरण्य, n. 1. a grove where ascetics live, Śāk. 14, 1. 2. The name of a forest, MBh. 13, 7655.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारण्य|महारण्यं
मह- + अरण्य मह- + अरण्य, a large forest, Rām. 3, 52, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यक|अरण्यकं
अरण्यक अरण्य + क, n. A forest, Yājñ. 3, 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानी अरण्यानी, i. e. अरण्य + ई, f. A large forest, Hit. 17, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति अरति (vb. ऋ?), m.<BR> 1. A disposer, Lass. 101, 4 = Rigv. 7, 16, 1.<BR> 2. अ-रति, f. Pain, Kir. 5, 31.<BR> --Cf. ὑπηρέτης.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि अरत्नि (vb. ऋ; the aff. contains the verb तन्), m.<BR> 1. The elbow, Draup. 9, 5.<BR> 2. A cubit of the middle length from the elbow to the tip of the little finger, Rām. 4, 40, 43.<BR> --Cf. Goth. arms; Lat. armus, arma; ὠλένη; Lat. ulna; O.H.G. elina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निक|अरत्निकः
अरत्निक अरत्नि + क, m. The elbow, Yājñ. 3, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द अरविन्द, n. A lotus, Ragh. 1, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक अराजक, i. e. अ-राजन् + क, adj. Without a king, Man. 7, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्यप्रसूतितस्
अराजन्यप्रसूतितस् अ-राजन्य-प्रसूति + तस्, adv. From one who is not born in the military caste, Man. 4, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल अराल, adj., f. ला, Crooked, Rām. 5, 28, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि अरि, m.<BR> 1. probably अ-रा (+ इ?) An enemy, Pañc. i. d. 267.<BR> 2. ऋ + इ, A wheel, Pañc. i. d. 324.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवारि|दानवारिः
दानव- + अरि दानव- + अरि, m. an enemy of the Dānavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीय
अरिक्थीय अरिक्थीय, i. e. अ-रिक्थ + ईय, adj., f. या, Incapable of inheriting, Man. 9, 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र अरित्र, i. e. ऋ + त्र, n. A rudder.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. ruodar; ἐρέτης = Ved. अरितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिंदम|अरिन्दम|अरिन्दमः
अरिंदम अरिंदम, i. e. अरि + म्-दम् + अ, adj. Victorious, Chr. 21, 14; 31, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट अ-रिष्ट (vb. रिष्).<BR> I. adj., f. टा, Unhurt, Chr. 298, 25 = Rigv. i. 112, 25; Draup. 7, 20.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The soap berry plant, Sapindus saponaria, Yājñ. 1, 186.<BR> 2. The nimb tree, Melia azadaracta, Rām. 2, 94, 9.<BR> 3. A woman's apartment, the lying in chamber, Ragh. 3, 15; the female apartments, the gyneceum, Rām. 2, 42, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टक|अरिष्टकः
अरिष्टक अरिष्ट + क, m. The soap berry plant, Sapindus saponaria, Man. 5, 120 (its pounded fruits).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टनेमिन्
अरिष्टनेमिन् अरिष्टनेमिन् (= अ-रिष्ट-नेमि), m. A proper name, Rām. 5, 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण अरुण (akin to अरुस्, cf. अरुष). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a " target="_blank">Page0048-a + 39</a>]<BR> I. adj., f. णा and णी, Tawny, dark red, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 88, 2; Rām. 3, 5, 7.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The dawn, Man. 10, 33.<BR> 2. The sun, Śāk. d. 31 (परिणत-, The setting sun).<BR> 3. A proper name, Dev. 11, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणता
अरुणता अरुण + ता, f. Tawny (the colour), Śiś. 9, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणप्सु
अरुणप्सु अरुण-प्सु (the latter part perhaps भास् + उ), adj. Tawny, Chr. 288, 1 = Rigv. i. 49, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणित
अरुणित अरुणित, i. e. अरुण + इत, adj., f. ता, Made red, Ṛt. 6, 5; Śiś. 6, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुंतुद|अरुन्तुद|अरुन्तुदः
अरुंतुद अरुंतुद, i. e. अरु + म्-तुद् + अ (cf. अरुस्), adj.<BR> 1. Wounding, Prab. 31, 16.<BR> 2. Causing pain, Prab. 93, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती अ-रुन्धती (vb. रुध्), f.<BR> 1. The wife of Vaśiṣṭha, Rām. 1, 10, 37.<BR> 2. An asterism, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष|अरुषं|अरुषः
अरुष अरुष, i. e. अरुस् + अ.<BR> I. adj., f. षी, Tawny, Chr. 294, 1 = Rigv. 1, 92, 1.<BR> II. m. A dark red cloud, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. 1, 85, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुस्
अरुस् अरुस्, n. A wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरे
अरे अरे, interj. of calling to inferiors, sirrah! Prab. 24, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेपस्
अरेपस् अरेपस्, i. e. अ-रिप् (= लिप्) + अस्, adj. Spotless, pure from sin, Chr. 290, 2 = Rigv. i. 64, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिता
अरोगिता अरोगिता, i. e. अ-रोगिन् + ता, f. Health, Hit. Pr. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग्यता
अरोग्यता अरोग्यता, i. e. अ-रोग + य + ता, f. Health, Rām. 2, 70, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क्
† अर्क् अर्क्, i. 10, Par. (rather a denom. derived from अर्क).<BR> 1. To praise.<BR> 2. To heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क अर्क, i. e. अर्च् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b " target="_blank">Page0048-b + 43</a>] ray of light, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2.<BR> 2. The sun, Chr. 36, 22.<BR> 3. Swallowwort, Asclepias gigantea, Śāk. d. 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्क|जलार्कः
जल- + अर्क जल- + अर्क, the reflexion of the sun in water, Bhāg. P. 3, 27, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालार्क|बालार्कः
बाल- + अर्क बाल- + अर्क, m. the rising sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्क
स- + अर्क स- + अर्क, adj. with the sun, sunny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्क
सु- + अर्क सु- + अर्क, adj. flashing beautifully, Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 50, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल|अर्गलं|अर्गलः
अर्गल अर्गल, m., f. ला, and n. A wooden bolt, or pin for fastening a door, Kathās. 4, 56; Pañc. 105, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्गल|अनर्गलं
अन्- + अर्गल अन्- + अर्गल, adj. unrestrained, Ragh. 3, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्गल|निरर्गलः
निस्- + अर्गल निस्- + अर्गल, 1. adj. unrestrained, MBh. 3, 16601. 2. acc. लम्, adv. without constraint, Rājat. 3, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलित
अर्गलित अर्गलित. i. e. अर्गल + इत, adj. Shut by a pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्
अर्घ् अर्घ्, i. 1, Par. To be worth, Pañc. i. d. 88.<BR> --Cf. अर्ह्, ἄρχω, ὄρχαμος, ἄρχομαι, ἄργμα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ अर्घ् + अ (vb. अर्घ् or अर्ह्), m. and n.<BR> 1. Price, cost, Man. 8, 398.<BR> 2. A mode of worship, or reverence, consisting in an oblation of rice, etc., with water or, of water only, Sāv. 3, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ|अनर्घः
अन्- + अर्घ अन्- + अर्घ,<BR> I. m. n. wrong price, Yājñ. 2, 250.<BR> II. adj. priceless, inestimable, Kathās. 24, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घ|महार्घं|महार्घः
महा- + अर्घ महा- + अर्घ, adj. of great value, Kathās. 21, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घतस्
अर्घतस् अर्घ + तस्, adv. Under the real value, Bhartṛ. 2, 12 (this is the true reading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य अर्घ्य, i. e. अर्घ + य.<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Deserving worship, Yājñ. 1, 357.<BR> 2. Deserving to be entertained, ib. 1, 110.<BR> II. n. A respectful oblation to gods or venerable men, consisting of rice, durva grass, flowers, etc., with water, or of water only, Yājñ. 1, 289.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्य
अन्- + अर्घ्य अन्- + अर्घ्य, adj. invaluable, Kathās. 3, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् अर्च्, i. 1 and 10, Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To beam, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2; to shine, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a " target="_blank">Page0049-a + 39</a>].<BR> 2. To worship, to honour, Man. 3, 93. To offer respectfully, Man. 4, 235.<BR> अन्-अर्चित, Given without due honour, Man. 4, 213.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To worship, Man. 8, 391.<BR> अभ्यर्चित, with gen. Rājat. 5, 101.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To worship, Yājñ. 1, 179.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Causal, To return a respectful salutation, with acc. Rām. 2, 71, 31.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To honour, Rām. 2, 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक अर्च् + अक. adj. Worshipping, Man. 11, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन अर्च् + अन, n. Worship, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा अर्च् + आ, f. Worship, Chr. 56, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चि|अर्चिः|अर्च्चिः
अर्चि अर्च् + इ, m. Flame, Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13; Ragh. 12, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्चि
स- + अर्चि स- + अर्चि, adj. flaming, Rām. 4, 10, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चितृ
अर्चितृ अर्च्-इतृ, m. A worshipper, Rām. 5, 32, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मन्त्|अर्चिष्मत्
अर्चिष्मन्त् अर्चिष्मन्त्, i. e. अर्चिस् + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Beaming, flaming, Vikr. d. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् अर्च् + इस्, f. and n.<BR> 1. A ray of light, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 92, 5.<BR> 2. Flame, Rām. 5, 75, 6; 6, 36, 117.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणार्चिस्
अरुण- + अर्चिस् अरुण- + अर्चिस्, m. the sun, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्चिस्|उदर्च्चिस्
उद्- + अर्चिस् उद्- + अर्चिस्, adj. radiant, Ragh. 7, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तार्चिस्|शान्तार्च्चिस्
शान्त- + अर्चिस् शान्त- + अर्चिस् (vb. शम्), adj. extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तार्चिस्|सप्तार्च्चिस्
सप्तार्चिस् सप्तार्चिस्, i. e. सप्तन्-, m. 1. fire. 2. the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्छ्
अर्छ् अर्छ्, see ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
1. अर्ज् अर्ज्, i. 1, and 10, Par. To earn, to acquire, MBh. 11, 193; Indr. 3, 7 (Ātm.).<BR> स्व-अर्जित and स्वयम्-अर्जित, adj. Acquired by one's own efforts, Rām. 1, 43, 11; Man. 9, 209.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, To acquire, Man. 9, 208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
2. अर्ज् अर्ज्, i. 10, Par. To work, to prepare.<BR> --With the prepositions समुप सम्-उप, To prepare, Chr. 14, 21 (read तत् तु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जन|अर्जनं|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जन अर्ज् + अन, n. Earning, acquisition, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन अर्ज्-उन (from a lost vb. akin to राज्).<BR> I. adj., f. नी, White, Chr. 288, 3 = Rigv. i. 49, 3.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A tree, Terminalia Arjuna, Rām. 3, 19, 13.<BR> 2. The name of the third son of Pāṇḍu, Indr. 1, 10.<BR> III. f. नी, The dawn, Rām. 2, 114, 14.<BR> --Cf. ἀργεννός, ἄργυρος; Lat. argentum; the base of these forms is अर्ज् + वन्त्: cf. also ἀργός, ἄργιλος, ἀργής, Ἀργυννίς; see रञ्ज्, रजत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव अर्णव (from अर्ण, ved. by aff. व for वन्त्), m. The ocean, Rām. 4, 9, 38.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्णव|महार्णवः
महा- + अर्णव महा- + अर्णव, m. the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणार्णव
लवण- + अर्णव लवण- + अर्णव, m. the sea of salt water, Rām. 1, 1, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्वतवनार्णव
स-पर्वत-वन- + अर्णव स-पर्वत-वन- + अर्णव, adj., f. वा (viz. पृथिवी, earth), with its mountains, forests, and seas, Rām. 1, 16, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्ति|अर्ति|अर्तिः|अर्त्तिः
अर्त्ति अर्त्ति, i. e. अर्द् + ति, f. Pain, Kathās. 13, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्
अर्थ् अर्थ्, i. 10 (rather a denom. derived from अर्थ) Ātm. To ask, to request; with two acc. Daśak. in Chr. 199, 15. त्वाम् तम् इमम् अर्थम् अर्थयते, He asks this from thee, Pass. Kathās. 22, 52. तैर् एवार्थ्यमानस्, Being requested by them.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To ask, to request, Prab. 109, 18, with two acc.; Par., with acc. and loc. Kathās. 26, 148. त्वाम् भर्तृत्वे ऽभ्य् अर्थयिष्यति, She will ask thee to become her husband.<BR> अभ्यर्थित, Asked, Man. 2, 189. n. Desire, Yājñ. 2, 88.<BR> --With कद् कद्.<BR> 1. To treat ill, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 591.<BR> 2. To reproach, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 15.<BR> 3. To torment, Kathās. 18, 243.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a " target="_blank">Page0050-a + 45</a>] प्र प्र, To request, Pañc. 255, 22; प्रार्थयान instead of प्रार्थयमान, Rām. 2, 25, 31; with inf. किम् इदं प्रार्थितं कर्तुम्, What is this which you intend to do? Nal. 19, 15; Par. Rām. 3, 40, 6; Pañc. 96, 5.<BR> तत्प्रार्थित, i. e. तद्-, adj. Requested by him, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 8.<BR> --Pass. प्रार्थ्य, To be desired, ib. 184, 17.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To wish, Rām. 2, 11, 3.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To request, MBh. 5, 18.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To challenge, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 25.<BR> --With सम् सम् (rather a denom. derived from समर्थ),<BR> 1. To prepare, Rām. 4, 26, 25 (Par.); Chr. 55, 7.<BR> 2. To consider, Rām. 6, 101, 17.<BR> 3. To expect, Vikr. 20, 9.<BR> 4. To interpret, Śāk. d. 67.<BR> 5. To judge, Pañc. 185, 2.<BR> 6. To approve, Pañc. 71, 25 (Par.).<BR> 7. To determine, Rām. 2, 20, 26 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ अर्थ, i. e. ऋ + थ, m.<BR> 1. Desire; विवाह-, a marriage suit.<BR> 2. Aim; सिद्ध-, one who has obtained his aim, Chr. 62, 60.<BR> 3. Advantage, Bhartṛ. 2, 40.<BR> 4. Business, Man. 2, 67.<BR> 5. Wealth, Pañc. i. d. 197; worldly prosperity, Man. 12, 38 (one of the three aims of men; the two others are काम, pleasure, and धर्म, virtue); money, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 19.<BR> 6. Cause, Man. 2, 213.<BR> 7. Thing, Man. 8, 170.<BR> 8. Meaning, Man. 3, 186; true sense, Man. 1, 3; thought, word, Śāk. d. 164.<BR> 9. In law: A suit, an action.<BR> 10. The acc. अर्थम् is used as an adverb, but almost always at the end of a compound word, implying, ‘for,’ ‘on account of,’ e. g. यज्ञ-सिद्धि-अर्थम्, For the performance of sacrifices, Man. 1, 23. The dat. अर्थाय, and loc. अर्थे, may be also used at the end of a compound word, or may govern the genitive. Abl. अर्थात्, ‘to wit,’ ‘namely,’ Sch. Śāk. d. 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यर्थम्
इति-अर्थ + म् इति-अर्थ + म्, adv. to this end, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियार्थ|इन्द्रियार्थः
इन्द्रिय- + अर्थ इन्द्रिय- + अर्थ, m. an object [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-b " target="_blank">Page0050-b + 45</a>] of sense, Man. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतदर्थम्
एतद्-अर्थ + म् एतद्-अर्थ + म्, therefore, Pañc. i. d. 330; in order, Rām. 2, 52, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थ
किम्- + अर्थ किम्- + अर्थ, adj. with what aim, Chr. 57, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थम्
किम्-अर्थ + म् किम्-अर्थ + म् adv. why, to what end, Nal. 22, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थ|कृतार्थः
कृत- + अर्थ कृत- + अर्थ, adj. having attained one's end, satisfied, Rām. 4, 34, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहार्थ|गृहार्थः
गृह- + अर्थ गृह- + अर्थ, m. the business of the house, Man. 2, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थम्
तद्-अर्थ + म् तद्-अर्थ + म्, adv. therefore, Rām. 1, 73, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थ|निरर्थः
निरर्थ निरर्थ, i. e. निस्-,<BR> I. m. nonsense.<BR> II. adj. 1. purposeless. 2. poor. 3. unmeaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितार्थ
निश्चितार्थ निश्चितार्थ, i. e. निस्-चित-, (vb. चि), adj. completely resolved, Rām. 4, 42, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
पर- + अर्थ पर- + अर्थ, m. 1. great importance. 2. the interests of another. 3. sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थ|परमार्थः
परम- + अर्थ परम- + अर्थ, m. 1. the most sublime truth. 2. the whole truth. 3. reality. 4. earnest, Śāk. d. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषार्थ|पुरुषार्थः
पुरुष- + अर्थ पुरुष- + अर्थ, m. 1. the object or aim of man. 2. human exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्थ|भूतार्थः
भूत- + अर्थ भूत- + अर्थ, m. an element of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्थ
महा- + अर्थ महा- + अर्थ,<BR> I. m. a principal object.<BR> II. adj. 1. significant. 2. dignified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञार्थ
यज्ञ- + अर्थ यज्ञ- + अर्थ, adj. serving for a sacrifice, Bhag. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थ|यथार्थं
यथा- + अर्थ यथा- + अर्थ, adj. 1. according to the sense. 2. proper, right, थम्, adv. suitably, properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथार्थ
अ-यथा- + अर्थ अ-यथा- + अर्थ, adj. not true, Śāk. d. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदर्थम्
यद्-अर्थ + म् यद्-अर्थ + म्, adv. for what reason, Chr. 3, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावदर्थ
यावदर्थ यावदर्थ, i. e. यावन्त्-,<BR> I. adj. as much as may be useful, Man. 2, 182.<BR> II. adv. थम्, as much as may be useful, ib. 2, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थ|स्वार्थः
स्व- + अर्थ स्व- + अर्थ,<BR> I. adj. 1. having one's own object. 2. having a literal meaning. 3. pleonastic.<BR> II. m. 1. property. 2. own object. 3. own interest, Bhartṛ. 2, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर
अर्थकर अर्थ-कर, adj., f. री, Useful, Hit. Pr. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृत्
अर्थकृत् अर्थ-कृ + त्, adj. Useful, Indr. 5, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थघ्न
अर्थघ्न अर्थ-घ्न, adj., f. नी, Prodigal, Man. 9, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थजात
अर्थजात अर्थ-जात (vb. जन्), n.<BR> 1. Money's worth, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 16.<BR> 2. Financial affairs, Śāk. 90, 13 (Prākṛ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतस्
अर्थतस् अर्थ-तस्, adv. Truly, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थद
अर्थद अर्थ-द (vb. दा), adj.<BR> 1. Useful, Kathās. 17, 122.<BR> 2. Liberal, Man. 2, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना अर्थ् + अना, f. A request, Naiṣ. 5, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थवत् अर्थ + वत्, adv. According to the object, Man. 5, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवन्त्|अर्थवत्
अर्थवन्त् अर्थ + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Wealthy, Hit. i. d. 175. 2. Significant, full of meaning, Rām. 1, 14, 35.<BR> 3. True, Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्थवन्त्|महार्थवत्
महा- + अर्थवन्त् महा- + अर्थवन्त्, adj. very dignified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिता
अर्थिता अर्थिता, i. e. अर्थिन् + ता, f.<BR> 1. Desire, Man. 9, 203.<BR> 2. Begging, Hit. i. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित्व|अर्थित्वं
अर्थित्व अर्थित्व, i. e. अर्थिन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Condition of one who implores, Megh. 6.<BR> 2. Request, Mālav. 40, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थित्व
अन्- + अर्थित्व अन्- + अर्थित्व, n. Absence of desire, disdain, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 87 (Pañc. i. d. 158).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् अर्थिन्, i. e. अर्थ + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Full of desire, Rām. 1, 48, 18; with instr. भार्यया चार्थी, Longing after a wife, Rām. 3, 24, 4.<BR> वधेन ममार्थी, Desiring my death, Böhtl. Chr. 114, 27.<BR> 2. A beggar, Bhartṛ. 2, 36; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 20.<BR> 3. A plaintiff, Man. 8, 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायार्थिन्
छाया- + अर्थिन् छाया- + अर्थिन्, adj. desiring shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्थिन्
धन- + अर्थिन् धन- + अर्थिन्, adj. greedy for money, Man. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रार्थिन्
पुत्र- + अर्थिन् पुत्र- + अर्थिन्, adj. wishing for a son, Man. 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलार्थिन्
बल- + अर्थिन् बल- + अर्थिन्, adj. desiring power, Man. 2, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यार्थिन्
भार्या- + अर्थिन् भार्या- + अर्थिन्, adj. desiring a wife, Chr. 6, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धार्थिन्
युद्ध- + अर्थिन् युद्ध- + अर्थिन्, adj. seeking war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणार्थिन्
शरण- + अर्थिन् शरण- + अर्थिन्, adj. depending on others for protection, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितार्थिन्
हित- + अर्थिन् हित- + अर्थिन्, adj. seeking another's welfare, Rām. 3, 48, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिसात्
अर्थिसात् अर्थिसात्, i. e. अर्थिन् + सात्, adv. (Given) to mendicants, Rājat. 5, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीय
ऽअर्थीय -अर्थीय, i. e. -अर्थ + ईय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b " target="_blank">Page0051-b + 42</a>] adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Fit for, susceptible of, e. g. यातना-, susceptible of torment, Man. 12, 16.<BR> 2. Referring to, e. g. धर्म-, referring to duty, MBh. 1, 600.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थेप्सुता
अर्थेप्सुता अर्थेप्सुता, i. e. अर्थ-ईप्स, ईप्स, desid. of आप् + उ + ता, f. Desire of wealth, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य अर्थ्य, i. e. अर्थ + य, adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Proper, Rām. 6, 92, 77.<BR> 2. Wealthy.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमार्थ्य
हेम- + अर्थ्य हेम- + अर्थ्य, adj. abounding in gold, Pañc. i. d. 377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् अर्द्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To go.<BR> 2. To beg, Ragh. 5, 17.<BR> --i. 1 and 10, Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To kill, Rām. 1, 16, 30.<BR> 2. To hurt; to wound, Pañc. 221, 13.<BR> 3. To afflict; to vex, Rām. 3, 14, 11; 53, 27.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति. To press violently, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 115.<BR> --With अभि अभि. To press; to afflict, Rām. 2, 21, 55; cf. अभ्यर्ण्ण.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति. To press in return, Rām. 6, 92, 52.<BR> --With वि वि. To press.<BR> अ-व्यर्ण्ण. Not pressed, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 19.<BR> --With सम् सम्. To wound, MBh. 3, 761.<BR> --Cf. perhaps ἀρδ in ἄρδις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्दनः|अर्द्दन
ऽअर्दन -अर्द् + अन, adj. Killing, Rām. 1, 54, 17.<BR> कैटभ- and जन-, m. Names of Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 18; Bhartṛ. 3, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध अर्ध, i. e. ऋध् + अ.<BR> I. adj., f. धा. Half, halved, Lass. 22, 2.<BR> --Often former part of comp. words: -पण, Half a paṇa, Man. 8, 404. -अक्त, Half spoken, Pañc. 77, 2. -दगध, Half burnt, Pañc. 98, 1.<BR> --When before cardinal numerals it denotes:<BR> 1. A half more, e. g. -त्रयोदशन्, thirteen and a half, Yājñ. 2, 265.<BR> 2. A half of the following number more, e. g. -शत, hundred and fifty, Man. 8, 331.<BR> 3. Division of the following number, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a " target="_blank">Page0052-a + 42</a>] -पञ्चाशत्, twenty-five, Man. 8, 268.<BR> --When an ordinal follows a half is added, e. g. -तृतीय, three and a half, Rām. 2, 92, 10.<BR> --When it follows a cardinal numeral, this numeral is divided, e. g. दशार्ध, i. e. दशन्-, Five, Man. 1, 24.<BR> II. n. A half, Man. 8, 296.<BR> III. m. A part, e. g. जघन-, the rear of an army, MBh. 5, 5162. पश्च-, The hind-part, Śāk. d. 7. पूर्व-, The former part, Bhartṛ. 2, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रार्ध|चंद्रार्ध|चन्द्रार्धः
चन्द्र- + अर्ध चन्द्र- + अर्ध, m. The half-moon, Rām. 1, 28, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धचन्द्र|अर्द्धचन्द्रः|अर्धचन्द्रः
अर्धचन्द्र अर्ध-चन्द्र, m.<BR> 1. A half-moon, Rām. 3, 49, 35.<BR> --Cf. अर्ध-भाषर.<BR> 2. An arrow with a head like a half-moon, Rām. 3, 34, 30; cf. 6, 36, 77.<BR> 3. The hand bent into a semicircle or the shape of a claw, as for the purpose of seizing or clutching any thing. अर्धचन्द्रं दा. To seize one by the neck, Pañc. 63, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभाज्
अर्धभाज् अर्धभाज्, i. e. अर्ध-भज्, adj. Getting a half of, Man. 8, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभास्कर|अर्धभास्करः
अर्धभास्कर अर्ध भास्कर, m. Noon, Rām. 3, 55, 33 (अर्धचन्द्र-, loc. At noon on the day of the halfmoon, i. e. on the eighth day of the month).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धरात्रार्धदिवस|अर्धरात्रार्धदिवसः
अर्धरात्रार्धदिवस अर्धरात्रार्धदिवस, i. e. अर्ध-रात्र-अर्ध-दिवस, m. The equinox, Rām. 3, 55, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिक|अर्धिकः
अर्धिक अर्धिक, i. e. अर्ध + इक, adj., f. की, Amounting to the half, Yājñ. 2, 296.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्धिक
तद्- + अर्धिक तद्- + अर्धिक, adj. half that (time), Man. 3, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिन्
अर्धिन् अर्धिन्, i. e. अर्ध + इन्, adj., f. नी, Entitled to a half, Man. 8, 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोरुक|अर्द्धोरुकं
अर्धोरुक अर्धोरुक, i. e. अर्ध-ऊरु + क, n. A petticoat, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पण|अर्पणं
अर्पण अर्पण, i. e. ऋ, Caus. + अन, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b " target="_blank">Page0052-b + 40</a>]<BR> 1. Offering, Rām. 4, 28, 22.<BR> 2. Returning, Hit. 72, 19.<BR> 3. Putting on, Ragh. 2, 35.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवार्पण
देव- + अर्पण देव- + अर्पण, adj. receiving sacrifices(?), MBh. 13, 4202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्
† अर्ब् अर्ब्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुद|अर्बुदं|अर्बुदः|अर्ब्बुद|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्बुद अर्बुद.<BR> I. m., n.<BR> 1. The shape of the fœtus in the second month after the conception, Yājñ. 3, 75.<BR> 2. A hundred millions, Rām. 5, 29, 3.<BR> II. m. The name of a mountain, Rām. 6, 2, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ अर्भ, adj. Small.<BR> --Cf. अर्भक; ὀρϕός; Lat. orbus; Goth. arbja; A.S. orf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक अर्भ + क, m.<BR> 1. A child, Ragh. 3, 21.<BR> 2. The young of any animal, Śāk. d. 14, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य|अर्यः|अर्य्य|अर्य्यः
अर्य अर्य, m., f. या and यी, A man or woman of the third caste, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यमन्|अर्य्यमन्
अर्यमन् अर्यमन्, m.<BR> 1. The name of a deity, Rām. 2, 25, 8.<BR> 2. The chief of the Pitṛs, or Manes, Bhag. 10, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्
† अर्व् अर्व्, i. 1, Par. To kill, or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वन्|अर्व्वन्
अर्वन् अर्वन् and अर्वन्त् अर्वन्त्, m. वती, f. A horse, Lass. 102, 3 = Rigv. 7, 102, 2.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. armentum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाक्कालिकता
अर्वाक्कालिकता अर्वाक्कालिकता, i. e. अर्वाञ्च्-काल + इक + ता, f. Modern date, Man. 12, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाञ्च्|अर्वांच्
अर्वाञ्च् अर्वाञ्च्, i. e. अर्व-अञ्च् (the former part is still questionable), adj., f. वाची; n. अर्वाक्, adv.<BR> 1. Towards, Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR> 2. Before, till, with abl., Man. 5, 59. Within, Yājñ. 2, 173. अर्वाक् संवत्सरात्, Until one year has elapsed, Man. 8, 30.<BR> 3. Near, Śāk. d. 40 v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस्
अर्शस् अर्शस्, probably ऋष् + अस् (with श् instead of ष्), n. Hæmorrhoids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस|अर्शसः
अर्शस अर्शस् + अ, adj., f. सा. Subject to hæmorrhoids, Man. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्
अर्ह् अर्ह् (ह् for घ्, cf. अर्घ्), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Hiḍ. 1, 36).<BR> 1. To deserve, with the acc., Man. 2, 208 (मानम्, honour); Man. 8, 323 (वधम्, death); 8, 194 (दण्डम्, a fine); 8, 267 (शतम्...दण्डम्, a fine of hundred पणस्); 8, 139 (पञ्चकं शतम्, with ellipsis of दण्ड, he must pay five in the hundred).<BR> 2. To be entitled to, with the inf., Man. 8, 147.<BR> 3. To be obliged to, with the acc., Śāk. d. 66; with the inf., Man. 8, 155; Naiṣ. 5, 112 (कर्तुम् अर्हति, must be done).<BR> 4. To undergo, Man. 8, 145; Rām. 6, 103, 20.<BR> 5. To be worthy, to be equal to, with the acc., Man. 3, 131.<BR> 6. To be able, with the inf., Bhag. 2, 17.<BR> 7. i. 1, and i. 10, Par. To worship or to honour.<BR> 8. The second persons of i. 1, joined with an inf. represent a respectful form of the imperative, वक्तुम् अर्हसि, Say (literally, Be pleased to say, cf. the Lat. dignor, with the inf.), Man. 1, 3.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभ्यर्हित. Fit, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह अर्ह् + अ, adj., f. का.<BR> 1. Deserving, with the acc., Rām. 1, 53, 12; subject to, Man. 8, 240.<BR> --With the inf., Bhag. 1, 37 (नार्हा वयं कन्तुम्, we ought not to be killed).<BR> 2. Entitled to, with the acc., Man. 9, 144; with the inf., Rām. 4, 36, 17.<BR> 3. Worth; महा-, of great value, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 16.<BR> 4. Fit, suitable, Pañc. 152, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह
अन्- + अर्ह अन्- + अर्ह, adj. 1. not deserving, Draup. 9, 7. 2. unworthy, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजार्ह|पूजार्हः
पूजा- + अर्ह पूजा- + अर्ह, adj. worthy of reverence, Man. 9, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियार्ह|प्रियार्हः
प्रिय- + अर्ह प्रिय- + अर्ह, adj. deserving love, amiable, Kir. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानार्ह
मान- + अर्ह मान- + अर्ह, adj. entitled to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b " target="_blank">Page0053-b + 39</a>] respect, Man. 2, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्ह|राजार्हं
राजार्ह राजार्ह, i. e. राजन्-, adj. royal, suitable to, or fit for a king, Rām. 3, 49, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कारार्ह
सत्कार- + अर्ह सत्कार- + अर्ह, adj. deserving hospitality, Nal. 9, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखार्ह
सुख- + अर्ह सुख- + अर्ह, adj. deserving pleasure, Rām. 3, 52, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हण|अर्हणं
अर्हण अर्हण, i. e. अर्ह् + अन.<BR> I. n. A token of respect, Man. 3, 54.<BR> II. f. णा, Worship, adoration, Pañc. 236, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्व
अर्हत्व अर्ह + त्व, n. Worthiness, Kathās. 2, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हन्त्|अर्हत्
अर्हन्त् अर्हन्त् (ptcple. of the pres. of अर्ह्), f. हती, Venerable, Śāk. d. 112.<BR> --Superlat. अर्कत्तम, Most venerable, Man. 3, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्
† अल् अल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To adorn.<BR> 2. To be able.<BR> 3. To prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक|अलकं|अलकः
अलक अलक.<BR> I. m. and n. A curl, Ṛt. 6, 6.<BR> II. f. का, The capital of Kuvera, Megh. 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतालक|लतालकः
लता- + अलक लता- + अलक, m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकनन्दा
अलकनन्दा अलकनन्दा, f. The name of a river, and surname of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्त|अलक्तः
अलक्त अलक्त (cf. लक्तक), m. Lac, the red animal dye so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तक|अलक्तकः
अलक्तक अलक्त + क, m. Lac (see the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्यजन्मता
अलक्ष्यजन्मता अलक्ष्यजन्मता, i. e. अ-लक्ष्य-जन्मन् + ता. f. Insignificant birth, Kumāras. 5, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकरण|अलङ्करण|अलंकरणं|अलङ्करणं
अलंकरण अलंकरण, i. e. अलम्-कृ + अन, n. Ornament, Bhartṛ. 2, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकार|अलङ्कार|अलंकारः|अलङ्कारः
अलंकार अलंकार, i. e. अलम्-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Trimming, Rām. 2, 40, 13.<BR> 2. Ornament, trinkets, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकारक
अलंकारक अलंकार + क, m. Ornament, Man. 7, 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकृति|अलङ्कृति|अलंकृतिः
अलंकृति अलंकृति, i. e. अलम्-कृ + ति, f. Ornament, Amar. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज्जाकर
अलज्जाकर अ-लज्जा-कर, adj. Not disgracing, Pañc. v. d. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्
अलम् अलम् (i. e. ऋ + अ + म्, cf. Ved. अरम्, ἄρα, ἀρι-, ἐρι-, ἄρω), adv.<BR> 1. Fit, able, with loc., Rām. 3, 47, 6; with inf., Rām. 2, 39, 28.<BR> 2. Adequate, Megh. 54; with inf., Kir. 5, 17; Daśak. in Chr. 194, 3.<BR> 3. Enough, with dat. Man. 11, 76; with inf., Śiś. 9, 87.<BR> 4. No more, implying prohibition, no, not; with instr., Daśak. 187, 14 (शुचालम्, cease to lament); with inf., Mṛcch. 45, 6 (अलं सुप्तजनं प्रबोधयितुम्, do not awake the sleeping man); with absolutive, Rām. 2, 28, 5 (अलं वनं गत्वा, do not go to the forest).<BR> 5. Abundant, powerfully, Rām. 5, 3, 21; Rājat. 5, 377.<BR> 6. See कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्क|अलर्कः
अलर्क अलर्क, m.<BR> 1. A fabulous animal, MBh. 12, 87.<BR> 2. The proper name of a prince, Rām. 2, 12, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस|अलसः
अलस अ-लस् + अ, adj., f. सा.<BR> 1. Weary.<BR> 2. Slack, Ṛt. 6, 12.<BR> 3. Sleepy, Rājat. 5, 408.<BR> 4. Lazy, Pañc. iii. d. 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालस
स- + अलस स- + अलस, adj. languid, Ṛt. 6, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलात|अलातं|अलातः
अलात अलात, n. A firebrand, Rām. 3, 24, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबु|अलाबुः
अलाबु अलाबु, f. A long gourd, a gourd-bottle, Man. 6, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबुमय
अलाबुमय अलाबु + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of a gourd, Yājñ. 3, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलि|अलिः
अलि अलि, m. A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिञ्जर|अलिंजर|अलिंजरः|अलिञ्जरः
अलिञ्जर अलिञ्जर, m. An earthen water jar, Matsyop. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्
अलिन् अलिन्, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिनी
अलिनी अलिनी, f. A swarm of bees (?), Bhartṛ. 1, 5: perhaps ought to be [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b " target="_blank">Page0054-b + 42</a>] read अलिनाम् or अलिनो, from अलिन् अलिन्, m. A large black bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्द|अलिंदः|अलिन्दः
अलिन्द अलिन्द, m.<BR> 1. A terrace, Śāk. 62, 14.<BR> 2. The name of a people, MBh. 6, 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक|अलीकं
अलीक अलीक.<BR> I. adj., f. का, False, Amar. 23.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Any thing displeasing, Rām. 2, 52, 25.<BR> 2. Falsehood, Pañc. 259, 4.<BR> 3. Smallness, Pañc. i. d. 205 (smallness and falsehood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेपक|अलेपकः
अलेपक अ-लेप + क, adj., f. पका and पिका, Spotless, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक्य
अलोक्य अलोक्य, i. e. अ-लोक + य, adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Extraordinary.<BR> 2. Obstructing the progress to heaven, Man. 2, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोमक
अलोमक अ-लोम + क, adj., f. मिका (ved. also मका). Having no hair, Man. 3, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुत्व
अलोलुत्व अलोलुत्व (probably for अ-लोलुप + त्व), n. Absence of covetousness, Bhag. 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्प|अल्पं|अल्पः
अल्प अल्प, adj. f. पा.<BR> 1. Little, small, Rām. 5, 35, 31; Man. 3, 55; अल्पेन, For a small price, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 18.<BR> 2. Insignificant, Ragh. 2, 47.<BR> 3. Of no great value, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 6 (cf. नय).<BR> 4. Short, Pañc. Pr. d. 10.<BR> 5. Feeble, Kathās. 24, 136. Comparative, अल्पीयंस्, Man. 8, 36, and अल्पतर.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल्प
अन्- + अल्प अन्- + अल्प, adj., 1. great, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 8. 2. numerous, 187, 5. 3. much, Kathās. 18, 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाल्प
अल्प-अल्प अल्प-अल्प, adj. very little, Man. 7, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्प|स्वल्पः
सु- + अल्प सु- + अल्प, adj. 1. very small, Bhartṛ. 2, 23; स्वल्पेन, for a very short time, Man. 2, 134. 2. very few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पक|अल्पकः
अल्पक अल्प-क, adj., f. इका, Small, Man. 3, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पता
अल्पता अल्प + ता, f. and अल्पत्व अल्प + त्व, n. Minuteness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पदुःखता
अल्पदुःखता अल्प-दुःख + ता, f. Having little pain, Arj. 10, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशस्
अल्पशस् अल्प-शस्, adv. In a small degree, Man. 12, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पित
अल्पित अल्पित, i. e. अल्प + इत, adj., f. ता, Diminished, Naiṣ. 1, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्
अव् अव्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To please, to satisfy, Ragh. 11, 75.<BR> 2. To be pleased, ved.<BR> 3. To desire, Ragh. 1, 65.<BR> 4. To take care, ved.<BR> 5. To protect, Chr. 291, 13 = Rigv. i. 64, 13; Śāk. d. 1.<BR> 6. † To move.<BR> 7. † To excite affection, or be lovely.<BR> 8. † To know, or apprehend.<BR> 9. † To own (v. r. to be able).<BR> 10. † To obey.<BR> 11. † To act.<BR> 12. † To shine.<BR> 13. † To obtain.<BR> 14. † To embrace.<BR> 15. † To kill or hurt.<BR> 16. † To take (v. r. to burn).<BR> 17. † To be (v. r. to divide).<BR> 18. † To grow.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ऊत.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, To help. Chr. 288, 2 = Rigv. i. 49, 2; Chr. 296, 5 = Rigv. i. 112, 5.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To satisfy, Chr. 297, 18 = Rigv. i. 112, 18.<BR> --Cf. ἄω; Lat. avere and uti (an old denominat.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव अव, a prefix. Away, off, down.<BR> I. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> II. Former part of compounded nouns.<BR> --Cf. αὐ- in αὐερύω, αὖ, αὖτε; Lat. autem, aut.<BR> --This prefix is based on a pronoun अव, which is preserved in the Zend language, and in the former part of the compounded pronoun αὐ-τός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर|अवकरः
अवकर अवकर, i. e. अव-कॄ + अ, m. Sweepings, Bhartṛ. suppl. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्त|अवकर्तः
अवकर्त अवकर्त, i. e. अव-कृत् + अ, m. A chip, Nal. 10, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तन|अवकर्तनं|अवकर्त्तन
अवकर्तन अवकर्तन, i. e. अव-कृत् + अन, n. Cutting off, Nal. 10, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश|अवकाशः
अवकाश अव-काश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Space, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b " target="_blank">Page0055-b + 40</a>] room, Man. 3, 207.<BR> 2. Interval.<BR> 3. Opportunity, Rām. 5, 9, 28; Pañc. iii. d. 263 (264), cf. विषय.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवकाश
निस्- + अवकाश निस्- + अवकाश, adj. having no room for moving freely, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलभावकाश
सुलभ- + अवकाश सुलभ- + अवकाश, adj. f. शा, getting easily the opportunity (of appearing), Śāk. d. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशद
ऽअवकाशद -अवकाश-द (vb. दा), m. One who gives shelter, Man. 9, 271; 278.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
