अवगूहन|अवगूहनं
अवगूहन अवगूहन, i. e. अव-गुह्, Caus. + अन, n. Embracing. Prab. 57, 11 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह|अवग्रहः
अवग्रह अव-ग्रह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstacle.<BR> 2. Drought, Ragh. 11, 29.<BR> 3. Contempt, Rām. 5, 44, 18.<BR> 4. Nature, original temperament, Mālav. 70, d. 89. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0056-a " target="_blank">Page0056-a + 39</a>] (affection).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवग्रह
दुस्- + अवग्रह दुस्- + अवग्रह, adj. 1. hard to be stopped, Kām. Nītis. 8, 66. 2. disagreeable, Bhāg. P. 4, 19, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवग्रह|निरवग्रहः
निस्- + अवग्रह निस्- + अवग्रह, adj. 1. without any obstacle, MBh. 4, 436. 2. irresistible, Rājat. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्टन|अवघट्टनं
