सेवावलम्ब
सेवा- + अवलम्ब सेवा- + अवलम्ब, adj. depending on the service of..., Bhartṛ. 1, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तावलम्ब|हस्तावलम्बः
हस्त- + अवलम्ब हस्त- + अवलम्ब, adj. supported by the hand of..., Vikr. 11, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बन|अवलंबनं|अवलम्बनं
अवलम्बन अव-लम्ब् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Supporting one's self, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 24.<BR> 2. A prop or support, Śāk. d. 100.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलम्बन|अनवलंबन
अन्- + अवलम्बन अन्- + अवलम्बन, n. not supporting one's self, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करावलम्बन
कर- + अवलम्बन कर- + अवलम्बन, n. taking hold with the hand, Śiś. 9, 82; Hit. 41, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बिन्|अवलंबिन्
अवलम्बिन् अव-लम्ब् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Hanging down.<BR> 2. Hanging, Mṛcch. 46, 7.<BR> 3. Supporting one's self, Śāk. 62, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्ज्ववलम्बिन्
रज्जु- + अवलम्बिन् रज्जु- + अवलम्बिन्, adj. hanging by a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्तता
अवलिप्तता अव-लिप्त + ता, f., and अवलिप्तत्व अव-लिप्त + त्व, n. Pride, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुञ्चन|अवलुंचन|अवलुंचनं
अवलुञ्चन अव-लुञ्च् + अन, n. Pulling out, Rām. 6, 98, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठन|अवलुंठनं|अवलुण्ठनं
अवलुण्ठन अव-लुण्ठ् + अन, n. Robbing, Kathās. 22, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुम्पन|अवलुंपनं
अवलुम्पन अवलुम्पन, i. e. अव-लुप् + अन, n. Leaping away, Lass. 48, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेप|अवलेपः
अवलेप अवलेप, i. e. अव-लिप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Anointing.<BR> 2. Pride, Vikr. 5, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलेप
अन्- + अवलेप अन्- + अवलेप, adj. without anointing and without pride, Śiś. 9, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेप
स- + अवलेप स- + अवलेप, adj. Proud, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपन|अवलेपनं
अवलेपन अवलेपन, i. e. अव-लिप् + अन, n. Haughtiness, Rām. 1, 44, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक|अवलोकः
अवलोक अव-लोक् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sight, Śiś. 9, 71.<BR> 2. Observation, Vikr. 38, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकक
अवलोकक अव-लोक् + अक, m. A spy, Rām. 6, 101, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकन|अवलोकनं
अवलोकन अव-लोक् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sight.<BR> 2. Observation.<BR> 3. A glance, Ragh. 10, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकयितृ
अवलोकयितृ अवलोकयितृ, i. e. अव-लोक्, Caus. + तृ, m. An observer, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेष|अवशेषः
अवशेष अवशेष, i. e. अव-शिष् + अ, m. Residue.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धावशेष
अर्ध- + अवशेष अर्ध- + अवशेष, adj. of which a half is left, Rām. 5, 14, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पावशेष
अल्प- + अवशेष अल्प- + अवशेष, adj. of which few are left, Rām. 3, 32, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेष
निस्- + अवशेष निस्- + अवशेष, adj. without a residue, whole, Rām. 3, 16, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
स- + अवशेष स- + अवशेष, adj. 1. leaving a residue. 2. imperfect. 3. remaining, सावशेष-बन्धन, adj. still bound, Pañc. 109, 17. 4. till, मृद्-भाण्ड-, adj. exclusive of the earthen pots, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यम्
अवश्यम् अवश्यम्, i. e. अ-वश + य + म्, adv.<BR> 1. Certainly.<BR> 2. Inevitably, Man. 12, 68; necessarily. When compounded with a participle of fut. pass. the final म् is dropped, e. g. अवश्य-करणीय, to be done necessarily, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्याय|अवश्यायः
अवश्याय अवश्याय, i. e. अव-श्यै + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hoar-frost, Rām. 3, 22, 21.<BR> 2. Dew, MBh. 12, 5334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भः
अवष्टम्भ अवष्टम्भ, i. e. अव-स्तम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Relying on, Pañc. 20, 20. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b " target="_blank">Page0059-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. Self-confidence, Pañc. 246, 19.<BR> 3. Gold.<BR> --Comp.<BR> acc. सावष्टम्भम्, adv. courageously, Kathās. 25, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भ|सावष्टंभ
स- + अवष्टम्भ स- + अवष्टम्भ, adj. full of self-confidence, Pañc. i. d. 215;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भन|अवष्टंभनं
अवष्टम्भन अवष्टम्भन, i. e. अव-स्तम्भ् + अन, n. Supporting one's self on, being supported by, Pañc. 233, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भमय|अवष्टंभमय
अवष्टम्भमय अवष्टम्भ + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Ragh. 3, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्
अवस् अव् + अस्, n. Protection, Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 48, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका अव-सक्थि + का, f. A cloth drawn round the knees and loins of a person sitting on his hams, Man. 4, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर|अवसरः
अवसर अवसर, i. e. अव-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Opportunity, Śiś. 9, 41; Rājat. 5, 36.<BR> 2. The right time, Kir. 5, 16; with inf., Śāk. 12, 11.<BR> 3. Turn, Pañc. 55, 4 (शशकस्यावसरः समायातः, The turn of the hare came).<BR> 4. Use, Kathās. 6, 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसर|अनवसरः
अन्- + अवसर अन्- + अवसर,<BR> I. m. wrong time, Mṛcch. 102, 8.<BR> II. adj. unseasonable, Hit. 53, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वावसरम्
सर्वावसर + म् सर्वावसर + म्, i. e. सर्व-, adv. on every occasion, Lass. 2, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अवसाद अवसाद, i. e. अव-सद्-अ, m.<BR> 1. Sitting down.<BR> 2. Exhaustion,<BR> 3. Lassitude, want of energy.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवसाद
निस्- + अवसाद निस्- + अवसाद, adj. cheerful, Gīt. 11, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक अवसादक, i. e. अव-सद्, Caus. + अक, adj. Bringing down, impairing, Rām. 4, 26, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
अवसान अवसान, i. e. अव-सो + अन, n.<BR> 1. Termination, end, Śiś. 9, 19; Daśak. in Chr. 201, 4.<BR> 2. Death, Pañc. ii. d. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानिक
अवसानिक अवसानिक, i. e. अवसान + इक, adj., f. इका, Concluding, Rām. 2, 56, 25 (perhaps the masc. must be read -सानक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेक|अवसेकः
अवसेक अवसेक, i. e. अव-सिएह् + अ, m. Sprinkling, Mṛcch. 47, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेचन|अवसेचनं
अवसेचन अवसेचन, i. e. अव-सिच् + अन, n. Water used for washing, Man. 4, 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्द|अवस्कंदः|अवस्कन्दः
अवस्कन्द अव-स्कन्द् + अ, m. Assault, Pañc. iii. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दिन्|अवस्कंदिन्
अवस्कन्दिन् अव-स्कन्द् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Assailing, Mahāv. 72, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कर|अवस्करः
अवस्कर अवस्कर, i. e. अव-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Ordure, Rājat. 5, 406.<BR> 2. The privy, Rājat. 5, 412.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्त्रता
अवस्त्रता अ-वस्त्र + ता, f. Nakedness, Nal. 10, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्था
अवस्था अव-स्था, f.<BR> 1. State, Pañc. 44, 1.<BR> 2. Condition, Rām. 3, 44, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदवस्थ
तद्- + अवस्थ तद्- + अवस्थ, adj., f. था, being in this state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावस्थ
अन्त्य- + अवस्थ अन्त्य- + अवस्थ, adj. being in the lowest condition, Pañc. iv. d. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावस्थ
कृत- + अवस्थ कृत- + अवस्थ, adj. brought into court, Man. 8, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थान|अवस्थानं
अवस्थान अवस्थान, i. e. अव-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Standing-place, Rām. 5, 15, 8.<BR> 2. Position, Pañc. 9, 14.<BR> 3. State, Pañc. 107, 8.<BR> 4. Abiding, Pañc. 19, 5; duration, Rājat. 5, 278.<BR> 5. Perseverance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थान|अनवस्थानः
अन्- + अवस्थान अन्- + अवस्थान,<BR> I. n. unsteadiness, mobility.<BR> II. adj. unsteady.<BR> III. m. wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापन|अवस्थापनं
अवस्थापन अवस्थापन, i. e. अव-स्था, Caus. + अन, n. Setting out for sale, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थिति|अवस्थितिः
अवस्थिति अवस्थिति, i. e. अव-स्था + ति, f. A bode, Kathās. 9, 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थिति|अनवस्थितिः
अन्- + अवस्थिति अन्- + अवस्थिति, f. unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार|अवहारः
अवहार अवहार, i. e. अव-हृ + अ, m. Suspension of fighting, Chr. 37, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहास|अवहासः
अवहास अवहास, i. e. अव-हस् + अ, m. Jest, Bhag. 11, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेल|अवहेलं|अवहेलः
अवहेल अवहेल, i. e. अव-हेड् + अ, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b " target="_blank">Page0060-b + 40</a>] and f. ला, Contempt.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
स- + अवहेल स- + अवहेल, adj. despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्च्|अवांच्
अवाञ्च् अवाञ्च्, i. e. अव-अञ्च्, adj., f. वाची, Downward, headlong, Man. 3, 249; acc. ntr. अवाक्, adv. Downwards, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 10; headlong, Man. 8, 75.<BR> --Cf. οὐκ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तर|अवांतर|अवान्तरं
अवान्तर अवान्तर, i. e. अव-अन्तर, adj. Included, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्ति|अवाप्तिः
अवाप्ति अवाप्ति, i. e. अव-आप् + ति, f. Acquisition, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अवि अवि, m. A sheep; f. an ewe, Man. 3, 6.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ovis; οἶς; O.H.G. awi; A.S. eav; Goth. avistr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकता
अविवेकता अ-विवेक + ता, f. Want of discrimination or judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषयीकरण|अविषयीकरणं
अविषयीकरण अविषयीकरण, i. e. अ-विषय-कृ + अन, n. The non-acquiring of an understanding, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 9; 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षण|अवेक्षणं
अवेक्षण अवेक्षण, i. e. अव-ईक्ष् + अन, n. Attention, care, Ragh. 14, 85.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षण|अनवेक्षणं
अन्- + अवेक्षण अन्- + अवेक्षण, n. want of attention, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षा
अवेक्षा अवेक्षा, i. e. अव-ईक्ष् + आ, f. Careful attention, Man. 7, 101.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षा
अन्- + अवेक्षा अन्- + अवेक्षा, f. Want of attention, Man. 7, 111 (instr. rashly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववेक्ष
सु- + अवेक्ष सु- + अवेक्ष, adj. well taken care of, Rām. 5, 75, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षिन्
अवेक्षिन् अवेक्षिन्, i. e. अव-ईक्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Looking, Pañc. i. d. 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथि|अव्यथिः
अव्यथि अ-व्यथ् + इ, adj. Fearless, Chr. 296, 6 = Rigv. 1, 112, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रतिक
अव्रतिक अव्रतिक, i. e. अ-व्रत + इक, adj. One who neglects his religious duties, Indr. 2, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्
1. अश् अश्, ii. 5, अश्नु. Ātm.<BR> 1. To pervade, to occupy, Yājñ. 1, 260.<BR> 2. To attain, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 2; ved. ii. 2, Par. Chr. 294, 8 = Rigv. i. 92, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a " target="_blank">Page0061-a + 40</a>]<BR> 3. † To heap or crowd.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, To attain, Man. 6, 82.<BR> --With वि वि, To pervade, Ragh. 4, 15.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To attain, Man. 2, 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्
2. अश् अश्, ii. 9, अश्ना, नी, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm. MBh. 3, 14686)<BR> 1. To eat, Man. 1, 95.<BR> अन्-अश्नान, Not eating, Chr. 57, 23.<BR> 2. To enjoy, Bhag. 9, 20.<BR> --Caus. To cause to eat, Man. 3, 83.<BR> अन्-आशित, Not satiated, Rām. 5, 17, 34.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To eat before another, MBh. 3, 14686.<BR> --With उप उप.<BR> 1. To eat up, to consume, Dev. 5, 61.<BR> 2. To enjoy, Rām. 1, 62, 6.<BR> उपाश्नीयात्, instead of ˚श्नीय्˚, on account of the metre, MBh. 12, 3266.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To enjoy, MBh. 3, 12631.<BR> --With परि परि, To eat, MBh. 3, 13354.<BR> --With प्र प्र.<BR> 1. To begin eating, Rām. 3, 63, 28.<BR> 2. To take in the mouth only, Man. 2, 62.<BR> 3. To eat, Man. 5, 103.<BR> 4. To drink, Chr. 47, 39 (Ātm.).<BR> 5. To enjoy one's self, MBh. 3, 8083 (Ātm.).<BR> --Caus. To cause to eat or devour, Kathās. 9, 10; Man. 3, 260.<BR> प्राशित, n. An oblation to the Pitṛs, or Manes, Man. 3, 73; 74.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To eat, Pañc. iv. d. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशंकुसुक
अशंकुसुक अशंकुसुक, Firm, Man. 6, 43; see संकसुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन|अशनं|अशनः
अशन 2. अश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Eating, Pañc. 236, 22.<BR> 2. Food, Man. 3, 59.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यशन
अति- + अशन अति- + अशन, n. excess of eating, Man. 2, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशन|अध्यशनं
अधि- + अशन अधि- + अशन, n. Eating too often.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशन|अनशनं
अन्- + अशन अन्- + अशन,<BR> I. adj. consisting in abstinence, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 20.<BR> II. n. 1. hunger, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 9. 2. fasting, Rājat. 5, 428 (plur.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निस्- + अशन निस्- + अशन, adj. abstaining from food, Hariv. 2539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलफलाशन
मूल-फल- + अशन मूल-फल- + अशन, n. feeding on roots and fruits, Man. 6, 75. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b " target="_blank">Page0061-b + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशन|पिशिताशनः
पिशित- + अशन पिशित- + अशन, n. eating flesh, Śāk. d. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशन
स- + अशन स- + अशन, adj. consisting of nourishment, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविरशन|हविरशनः
हविस्- + अशन हविस्- + अशन, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशन|हुताशनः
हुत- + अशन हुत- + अशन (vb. कु), m. 1. fire. 2. the deity of fire. 3. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनि|अशनिः
अशनि 1. अश् + अनि, f. (seldom m. Rām. 3, 4, 45) and अशनी 1. अश् + अनी, f. (Chr. 40, 12) Indra's thunderbolt, Ragh. 3, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्क
अशिरस्क अ-शिरस् + क, adj. Headless, Draup. 8, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशिरता
अशिशिरता अ-शिशिर + ता, f. Heat, Megh. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अशीत अशीत, i. e. अशीति + अ, ord. num. Eightieth.<BR> एक-, Eighty-first, MBh. i. adhy. 81.<BR> त्रि-, Eighty-third, adhy. 83.<BR> द्वि-, Eighty-second, adhy. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीति|अशीतिः
अशीति अशीति (cf. अष्टन्), card. num., f. Eighty, with genitive of the numbered objects, Man. 11, 220; in the same case, Rām. 2, 32, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाशीति|एकाशीतिः
एक- + अशीति एक- + अशीति, eighty-one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशीति|पंचाशीति|पञ्चाशीतिः
पञ्चाशीति पञ्चाशीति, i. e. पञ्चन्-, eighty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिक
अशीतिक अशीति + क, adj. Measuring eighty, Rām. 5, 6, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतितम
अशीतितम अशीति + तम, ord. num. f. मी. Eightieth.<BR> एक-, Eighty-first.<BR> त्रि-, Eighty-third.<BR> नव(न्)-, Eightyninth.<BR> पञ्च(न्)-, Eighty-fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषतस्
अशेषतस् अ-शेष + तस्, adv. Entirely, Man. 1, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषय
अशेषय अशेषय (a denom. derived from अ-शेष). To complete, Kumāras. 7, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोक|अशोकं|अशोकः
अशोक अ-शोक.<BR> I. adj. Free from sorrow, Nal. 12, 107.<BR> II. m. A shrub, Jonesia Asoka, Ṛt. 6, 16.<BR> III. n. An asoka-flower, Ṛt. 6, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाशोक
नील- + अशोक नील- + अशोक, m. an asoka with blue flowers, Rām. 3, 17, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
अश्मन् अश् + मन् (see vb. शो), m. A stone.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. the next and ἄκμων; also ved. अश्न, stone, and Goth. auhns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताश्मन्
अ-सित- + अश्मन् अ-सित- + अश्मन्, m. an emerald, Kir. 5, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्मन्
महा- + अश्मन् महा- + अश्मन्, m. a ruby, Kir. 5, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a " target="_blank">Page0062-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्याश्मन्|सूर्य्याश्मन्
सूर्य- + अश्मन् सूर्य- + अश्मन्, m. the sun-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताश्मन्
हरित- + अश्मन् हरित- + अश्मन्, n. 1. blue vitriol. 2. a turquoise; an emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्तक|अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मन्तक अश् + मन्त् + अक (see the last), n. A stove, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ममय
अश्ममय अश्ममय, i. e. अश्मन् + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of stone, Man. 5, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मसारमय
अश्मसारमय अश्मसारमय, i. e. अश्मन्-सार + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of iron, Rām. 4, 22, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मान्तक
अश्मान्तक अश्मान्तक, The name of a plant, Man. 2, 43 (probably = अश्मन्तक, m. A species of Oxalis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र अश् + र (see vb. शो).<BR> I. A substitute for अश्रि, when latter part of comp. adj., implying An angle, e. g. चतुर्-, adj. Quadrangular, regular, Kumāras. 1, 32 (written with स् instead of श्).<BR> II. n. A tear, Kathās. 13, 126; Man. 3, 229 (with स् instead of श्).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. the next, and ἄκρος, ἄκρα; Lat. acer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्र
स- + अश्र स- + अश्र, adj. weeping, Megh. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रि|अश्रिः
अश्रि अश् + रि (see vb. शो), f.<BR> 1. Edge, Kumāras. 2, 20.<BR> 2. A corner, an angle, Rām. 1, 13, 28.<BR> --Cf. ὄκρις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रु
अश्रु अश् + रु (see vb. शो), n. A tear, Rām. 2, 48, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्रु
उद्- + अश्रु उद्- + अश्रु, adj. shedding tears, Ragh. 12, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुतवत्
अश्रुतवत् अ-श्रु + त + वत्, adv. As if not heard, Rājat. 5, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लीक
अश्लीक अश्लीक, i. e. अ-श्री + क (ल् for र्), adj. Bringing misfortune, Man. 4, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व|अश्वः
अश्व अश् + व (see vb. शो).<BR> I. m. A horse, Man. 7, 96.<BR> II. f. वा, A mare, Rājat. 5, 415.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. equus; ἴκκος, ἴππος; Goth. aihvs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्व|अनश्वः
अन्- + अश्व अन्- + अश्व, m. one who is not a horse, Pañc. iv. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियाश्व
इन्द्रिय- + अश्व इन्द्रिय- + अश्व, m., plur. the horse-like organs of sense, Kir. 5, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाश्व
गव- + अश्व गव- + अश्व, n. bulls and horses, MBh. 1, 3654.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजाश्व
वीज- + अश्व वीज- + अश्व, m. a stallion, Rājat. 5, 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदश्व
वृहदश्व वृहदश्व, i. e. वृ-कन्त्-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b " target="_blank">Page0062-b + 41</a>] m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्व
स- + अश्व स- + अश्व, adj. with horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताश्व|सप्ताश्वः
सप्ताश्व सप्ताश्व, i. e. सप्तन्-, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश्व
हत- + अश्व हत- + अश्व (vb. हन्), adj. having the horses killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वक्रन्द|अश्वक्रन्दः
अश्वक्रन्द अश्व-क्रन्द् + अ, m. The name of a bird, MBh. 1, 1488.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर अश्व + तर.<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A mule, Rām. 2, 91, 53.<BR> 2. One of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent race, MBh. 1, 1555.<BR> II. f. तरी.<BR> 1. A female mule.<BR> 2. Probably the name of a kind of serpent, which, according to a popular opinion, used to die when pregnant with or bringing forth young, Rām. 3, 49, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थ|अश्वत्थः
अश्वत्थ अश्वत्थ, m. The holy figtree, Ficus religiosa, Bhag. 15, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थामन्
अश्वत्थामन् अश्वत्थामन्, i. e. अश्व-स्था + मन्, m. A proper name, Bhag. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेधिक|अश्वमेधिकः
अश्वमेधिक अश्वमेधिक, i. e. अश्व-मेध + इक, adj. Referring to the sacrifice of a horse, MBh. 1, 354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वयुज्
अश्वयुज् अश्व-युज्, adj. On which horses are put, Rām. 5, 27, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववार|अश्ववारः
अश्ववार अश्ववार, i. e. अश्व-वृ + अ, m. A horseman, Rām. 5, 73, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तनिक
अश्वस्तनिक अश्वस्तनिक, i. e. अ-श्वस् + तन + इक, adj. Not having for tomorrow, Man. 4, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वावन्त्|अश्वावत्
अश्वावन्त् अश्वावन्त्, i. e. अश्व + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in horses, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन् अश्विन्, i. e. अश्व + इन्, m., du. Two deities, Rām. 1, 24, 8.<BR> --Cf. the Dioscuri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्य|अश्व्यः
अश्व्य अश्व्य, i. e. अश्व + य, m. A patronymic: a son of Aśva, Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. i. 112, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्
† अष् अष्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a " target="_blank">Page0063-a + 41</a>] go.<BR> 2. To take.<BR> 3. To shine (v. r. अस्, cf. 3. अस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक अष्टक, i. e. अष्टन् + क.<BR> I. adj. Eight-fold, Man. 7, 48.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. The eighth day after the full moon, Man. 4, 113; especially those on which the Pitṛs or Manes are worshipped.<BR> 2. Worship of the Pitṛs, Rām. 2, 108, 14.<BR> III. n. An octad, a collection of eight things.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यष्टक
त्रि- + अष्टक त्रि- + अष्टक, n. a kind of vessel, Suśr. 1, 171, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाष्टक
अष्टाष्टक अष्टाष्टक, i. e. अष्टन्-, n. sixty-four (arts), Rām. 3, 53, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतय
अष्टतय अष्टतय, i. e. अष्टन् + तय, n. A complex of eight, Lass. 89, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टधा अष्टधा, i. e. अष्टन् + धा, adv. Eight-fold, Bhag. 7, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन् अष्टन्, i. e. अश् + तन् (cf. अशीति; the vb. is doubtful), card. num., adj. Eight, Hiḍ. 2, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ὀκτώ = अष्टौ; Lat. octo; Goth. ahtau; A.S. ëhta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यष्टन्
त्रि- + अष्टन् त्रि- + अष्टन्, Twentyfour, Man. 9, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम अष्टम, i. e. अष्टन् + म.<BR> I. ord. num., f. मी, Eighth, Man. 2, 36.<BR> II. m. An eighth, Man. 10, 120.<BR> III. f. मी, The eighth day of a lunar half month, Rājat. 5, 327; 412.<BR> --Cf. Lat. octavus; ὄγδοος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमक
अष्टमक अष्टम + क, adj. Eighth, Yājñ. 2, 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टा
अष्टा अष्टा, a substitute of अष्टन् in the former part of many comp. words, especially before numerals, e. g. अष्टा-दशन्, Eighteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादश
अष्टादश अष्टा-दश, ord. num., f. शी, Eighteenth, Chr. 51, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टादशन् अष्टा-दशन्, card. num. adj. Eighteen, Man. 8, 3.<BR> --Cf. Lat. octodecim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापद|अष्टापदं|अष्टापदः
अष्टापद अष्टा-पद.<BR> I. n. A board for draughts, dice, etc., Hariv. 6752.<BR> II. m. and n. Gold, Kumāras. 7, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापाद्य
अष्टापाद्य अष्टापाद्य, i. e. अष्टा-पाद + य, adj. Eight-fold, Man. 8, 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ट्रा
अष्ट्रा अष्ट्रा, i. e. अश् + त्र (vb. शो, cf. Lat. incitare), f. A goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला अष्ठीला (probably from अस्थि), f.<BR> 1. A kernel, MBh. 3, 10629.<BR> 2. A ball, MBh. 1, 4494.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
1. अस् अस्, ii. 2, Par. (Ātm. when combined with वि-अति and as auxiliary vb.; e. g. सृष्टाः स्मके, MBh. 13, 13).<BR> 1. To exist, Bhag. 2, 12.<BR> 2. To be, Man. 1, 5; with an adv., MBh. 3, 4041; with participles, Man. 8, 94. अस्ति, So it is, Śāk. 14, 16. अस्ति, Once, Pañc. 132, 22. With न, Not, it implies very often ‘to be lost,’ e. g. MBh. 3, 10284.<BR> 3. With a gen. To belong. कस्यासि, Whose are you, Nal. 12, 118. सन्ति मे, I have, Man. 8, 87. तवास्मि, I am thy captive, Man. 7, 91.<BR> 4. With a dat. To suffice, Man. 11, 85.<BR> 5. With a loc. or with प्रति, To be affected against, Śāk. 17, 13; 14.<BR> सन्त्, participle of the present (cf. Lat. præ-sens), 1. Being, Hit. i. d. 75. 2. Being in the true sense of the word, Right, Bhāṣāp. 138. 3. Virtuous, Chr. 8, 22. 4. Steady, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 10. 5. Venerable, Rājat. 5, 79. 6. Excellent, Kir. 5, 9. fem. सती, A virtuous wife, Lass. 41, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --superl. सत् + तम, adj., f. मा, Most excellent.<BR> --In comp. words of the Karmadhār. class it forms the latter part, e. g. द्विज-सत्तम, 1. A Brāhmaṇa, Man. 1, 33. 2. A most excellent Brāhmaṇa, Chr. 15, 30. ब्राह्मण-, m. Chr. 22, 15; भरत-, 25, 55; भारत-, 40, 17; भृगु-, 45, 11; मृग-, Rām. 3, 49, 25; रथ-, Chr. 63, 64; राजसत्तम, i. e. राजन्-, 53, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-सन्त्, adj. wicked, Pañc. i. d. 182; heretic, Man. 11, 65.<BR> अ-सती, f. an unchaste woman, Pañc. 185, 15.<BR> अ-सत्, n. non-entity, Man. 1, 11. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0064-a " target="_blank">Page0064-a + 41</a>]<BR> --With the prepositions व्यति वि-अति, Ātm. To outweigh, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 35.<BR> --With आविस् आविस्, To be visible, to appear, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 17 (corr. आविर् आसीत्).<BR> --With उप उप, To be near, Chr. 12, 2.<BR> --With प्रादुस् प्रादुस्,<BR> 1. To be conspicuous, Man. 1, 6.<BR> 2. To appear, Chr. 13, 6.<BR> 3. To spring up, Chr. 31, 10.<BR> --Cf. εἰμί, e. g. ἐστί = अस्ति; Lat. sum, est; Goth. im, ist; A.S. ëom, is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासती
महा-सती महा-सती, a very virtuous wife, Pañc. 38, 12. n. सत्, Entity, Man. 1, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
2. अस् अस्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To throw, Rām. 2, 67, 18.<BR> 2. To leave, Kathās. 6, 141. Aor. आस्थम्, Ragh. 12, 23. Part. of the perf. pass. अस्त (असित, Rām. 4, 13, 54).<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To surpass, Rām. 2, 23, 37.<BR> --With व्यति वि-अति, To cross, Man. 2, 72.<BR> --With अप अप.<BR> 1. To drive away, Amar. 2.<BR> 2. To put off, Nalod. 3, 8.<BR> 3. To lay aside, Rām. 2, 32, 30.<BR> 4. To leave, Pañc. Pr. d. 10. Absolutive अपास्य, Except, Hit. iii. d. 139.<BR> --With अभि अभि, also Ātm. Man. 4, 149; sometimes i. 1, Par. Man. 11, 106.<BR> 1. To discharge (an arrow), MBh. 1, 5497.<BR> 2. To do repeatedly; to repeat, Man. 2, 79.<BR> 3. To practise, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 1.<BR> 4. To study, Pañc. 244, 1.<BR> --With उद् उद्.<BR> 1. To east upward, MBh. 3, 430.<BR> 2. To lift up, Śāk. 34, 1; to raise, Śiś. 9, 74.<BR> --With पर्युद् परि-उद्, To heap round about, MBh. 2, 1805.<BR> --With व्युद् वि-उद्, To cast off, Bhag. 18, 51.<BR> --With नि नि, also i. 1 Par. Man. 6, 46.<BR> 1. To cast down, Rām. 3, 58, 2; to put down, Chr. 27, 12.<BR> 2. To resign, Rām. 2, 46, 20.<BR> 3. To put on, Rām. 2, 28, 27; Daśak. in Chr. 189, 6.<BR> 4. To support, Śāk. d. 161.<BR> 5. To put in, Bhartṛ. 2, 77; to settle, Yājñ. 2, 186; to appoint, MBh. 12, 4336.<BR> 6. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0064-b " target="_blank">Page0064-b + 42</a>] To intrust, Rām. 3, 51, 18.<BR> --Comp. partic.<BR> --Caus., to cause to put down, Chr. 43, 31.<BR> --With उपनि उप-नि.<BR> 1. To put near, Rām. 4, 4, 17.<BR> 2. To intrust, MBh. 3, 11551.<BR> 3. To prove, Hit. 120, 5.<BR> 4. To hint, Śāk. 65, 15.<BR> --Comp. partic.<BR> अन्-उपन्यस्त, unproved, Yājñ. 2, 19.<BR> --With समुपनि सम्-उप-नि, To prove, Hit. 103, 3.<BR> --With परिनि परि-नि, To stretch, Kathās. 6, 121.<BR> --With प्रतिनि प्रति-नि, To put down for every one, Rām. 2, 40, 16.<BR> --With विनि विनि,<BR> 1. To put off and down, Pañc. 230, 18.<BR> 2. To put down, Nal. 24, 45.<BR> 3. To divide, Rām. 1, 13, 28.<BR> 4. To direct, Rām. 2, 60, 7.<BR> 5. To put in, Pañc. 236, 9.<BR> --Comp. partic.<BR> सु-वि-न्यस्त, well arranged, Rām. 5, 13, 37.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि,<BR> 1. To put down, MBh. 3, 16708.<BR> 2. To abandon, Man. 6, 95; to abandon all worldly concerns, i. e. to become an anchorite, Man. 6, 94.<BR> 3. To put together, Rām. 3, 35, 63.<BR> 4. To put on, MBh. 3, 740.<BR> 5. To intrust, Rām. 4, 28, 5.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To throw out, to expel, Śiś. 9, 62; Ṛt. 6, 23; Rām. 3, 75, 24.<BR> 2. To drive back, Rām. 3, 42, 42; to send back, Śiś. 9, 33.<BR> 3. To destroy, Hit. i. d. 63.<BR> --With परा परा, To leave, Kir. 5, 27.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To spread, Kir. 5, 34.<BR> 2. To put around, MBh. 2, 1898.<BR> 3. To turn round, Kumāras. 3, 68.<BR> 4. To surround, Kumāras. 1, 45; to enchase, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 23.<BR> 5. To turn over, Man. 11, 183.<BR> 6. To turn away. Bhartṛ. 3, 29.<BR> --Caus. to cause to drop, Ragh. 13, 28.<BR> --With विपरि वि-परि, To invert, Mṛcch. 115, 4.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a " target="_blank">Page0065-a + 42</a>] throw, Man. 11, 73.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To separate, Man. 7, 159; Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 3; to divide, MBh. 1, 4263; pf. विव्यास, MBh. 1, 2212, instead of व्या-स, as if the combined व्यस् was a simple vb. व्यस्त, different, Prab. 97, 19; MBh. 3, 17052.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To unite, Man. 7, 57; Vedāntas. 205, 3.<BR> समस्त. 1. United, Man. 3, 85. 2. All, Rājat. 5, 62. 3. Whole, Pañc. 69, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> यावत्समस्त, i. e. यावन्त्-, large as it is, Pañc. 31, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रन्यस्त
चित्र-न्यस्त चित्र-न्यस्त, adj. painted, MBh. 9, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्यस्त
सु-न्यस्त सु-न्यस्त, gracefully reposing, Rām. 5, 14, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
† 3. अस् अस्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To take.<BR> 3. To shine (v. r. अष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्
असन् असन्, see असृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन|असनं|असनः
असन 2. अस् + अन.<BR> I. n. Discharging (as arrows), Chr. 297, 21 = Rigv. i. 112, 21.<BR> II. m. The name of a tree, Terminalia alata tomentosa, Rām. 2, 94, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वसन
इषु- + असन इषु- + असन, n. a bow, Ragh. 11, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरासन|शरासनं
शर- + असन शर- + असन, n. a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्ज
असमञ्ज असमञ्ज and असमञ्जस् असमञ्जस्, m. A proper name, Rām. 1, 39, 16; 1, 40, 16 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायित्व
असमवायित्व असमवायित्व, i. e. अ-समवायिन् + त्व, n. Condition of not being in an intimate relation, Bhāṣāp. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तिक|असमावृत्तिकः
असमावृत्तिक असमावृत्तिक, i. e. अ-सम्-आवृत्त + इक (? see वृत्), m. A student before he has completed his studies, Man. 11, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असि|असिः
असि असि, m. A sword, Rām. 3, 50, 2.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ensis; ἄορ, cf. अक्षन् = अक्षि, and πῖαρ = पीवन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असु|असुः
असु असु, i. e. 1. अस् + उ, m. plur.<BR> 1. The five vital breaths, or airs of the body (cf. Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 9).<BR> 2. Life, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतासु
गत- + असु गत- + असु (vb. गम्), adj. lifeless, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगतासु
अ-गत- + असु अ-गत- + असु, adj. living, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर असुर, i. e. 1. अस् + उर,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b " target="_blank">Page0065-b + 43</a>] Eternal, Chr. 290, 2 = Rigv. i. 64, 2.<BR> II. m. An Asura, or demon, Kir. 5, 30.<BR> III. f. री, A female Asura, or demon, MBh. 3, 12203.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवासुर
देव- + असुर देव- + असुर,<BR> I. m. pl. the gods and the demons, Rām. 1, 45, 27.<BR> II. adj. 1. referring to the gods and the demons, Rām. 1, 34, 8 Gorr. 2. n. elliptically (supply युद्ध), the war between the gods and the demons, Rām. 3, 53, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असू
असू अ-सू, adj. Sterile, Chr. 296, 3 = Rigv. i. 112, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूय
असूय असूय (an old denom. based on 2. अस्), Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To detract, scorn, MBh. 4, 99.<BR> 2. To reprove, Rājat. 5, 196.<BR> 3. To be angry, Mālav. 51, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. असूयय, To chastise, Nal. 14, 17.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To blame, Sāv. 5, 90.<BR> असूयाम्, instead of असूयेयम्, MBh. 1, 4377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयन्त्|अनसूयत्
अन्-असूयन्त् अन्-असूयन्त्, free from a spirit of detraction, Bhag. 3, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयक|असूयकः
असूयक असूयक, i. e. असूय + अक, adj., f. यिका, A scorner, Man. 2, 114.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अन्- + असूयक अन्- + असूयक (i. e. अनसूय + क, see असूया), adj. free from a spirit of detraction, Nal. 12, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया असूया, i. e. असूय + अ, f.<BR> 1. Detraction, Man. 7, 48.<BR> 2. Ill-will, Rām. 4, 14, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूय
अन्-असूय अन्-असूय,<BR> I. adj. free from a spirit of detraction, Man. 4, 158.<BR> II. f. या, a proper name, Śāk. 9, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासूया
स- + असूया स- + असूया, adv. angrily, Vikr. 30, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज् असृज्, i. e. असर्-, for 1. अस् + अन्, which is the base of several cases, -ज् (vb. जन्), n. Blood, Pañc. 21, 12.<BR> --With असन्, cf. Lat. san + ies; with असर्; Lat. assir; ἔαρ; with *असन्-ज्; Lat. sanguis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त 1. अस् + त,<BR> I. n. Home.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Sun-set, Pañc. iii. d. 187; Śiś. 9, 5. The acc. sing. अस्तम्, combined like a prefix, with इ, गम्, या, implies, To set, Daśak. 184, 1.<BR> 2. The western mountain, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a " target="_blank">Page0066-a + 41</a>] behind which the sun is supposed to set, Rām. 4, 37, 4.<BR> IV. n. Death, Kathās. 13, 74; Rājat. 5, 126.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यास्त|सूर्य्यास्त|सूर्य्यास्तं
सूर्य- + अस्त सूर्य- + अस्त, n. sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमन|अस्तमनं
अस्तमन अस्तमन (a syncope of अस्तम्-अयन), n. Sun-set, Pañc. ii. d. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमय|अस्तमयः
अस्तमय अस्तमय, i. e. अस्तम्-इ + अ, m. Sun-set, Kir. 5, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृ
अस्तृ 2. अस् + तृ, m. A shooter, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्र|अस्त्रं
अस्त्र 2. अस् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. A missile weapon, Śāk. 94, 10; an arrow, Vikr. d. 18.<BR> 2. A bow, Arj. 8, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वस्त्र
इषु- + अस्त्र इषु- + अस्त्र, n. the art of discharging arrows, Chr. 22, 16; 51, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमास्त्र|कुसुमास्त्रः
कुसुम- + अस्त्र कुसुम- + अस्त्र, m. the god of Love, Ragh. 7, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्त्र
कृत- + अस्त्र कृत- + अस्त्र, adj. conversant with the use of missile weapons, MBh. 3, 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डास्त्र
दण्ड- + अस्त्र दण्ड- + अस्त्र, n. the name of a fabulous weapon, Rām. 1, 56, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्त्र
महा- + अस्त्र महा- + अस्त्र, n. a great missile weapon, Chr. 44, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्
अस्थन् अस्थन्, see अस्थि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि अस्थि; several cases have अस्थन् as their base, n.<BR> 1. A bone, Bhartṛ. 2, 9.<BR> 2. A kernel, seed, Man. 4, 78.<BR> --Cf. ὀστέον; Lat. os, gen. ossis, for ostis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिक
अस्थिक अस्थि + क,<BR> 1. n. A small bone, Bhartṛ. 2, 23.<BR> 2. A substitute for अस्थि, when latter part of comp. adj., e. g. अन्-, Boneless, Yājñ. 3, 275.<BR> दृढ-गुल्फ-शिरा-, adj. Having strong ancles, nerves, and bones, Rām. 5, 32, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिदन्तमय
अस्थिदन्तमय अस्थि-दन्त + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of bones and ivory, Man. 5, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमन्त्|अस्थिमत्
अस्थिमन्त् अस्थि + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Having bones, Man. 11, 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमय
अस्थिमय अस्थि-मय, adj., f. यी, Full of bones, Rājat. 5, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद् अस्मद्, First person. pronoun, I; nom. sing. अहम्, plur. वयम्; the bases of the other cases are, म, आव, न, अस्म.<BR> --Cf. ἐγώ, ἐμοῦ, μοῦ, νῶϊ, ἄμμες; Lat. ego, me, nos; Goth. ik, mis, veis, unsis; A.S. ic, më, vit, unc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय अस्मद् + ईय, adj., f. या, Our, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मयु
अस्मयु अस्मयु, i. e. *अस्मय (a denominat. of अस्मद् by य) + उ, adj. Favourable to us, Lass. p. 100, 8 = Rigv. vii. 15, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यवामीय|अस्यवामीयं
अस्यवामीय अस्य वाम् + ईय, n. The Vedic hymn beginning with the words अस्य वाम् (Rigv. i. 164), Man. 11, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्र|अस्रं|अस्रः
अस्र अस्र, see अश्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
1. अह् अह् (ह् for घ्; cf. Lat. adag + ium, ajo for agjo, nego; Goth. aikan), forms only 2. sing. and du., and 3. sing. du., and plur. of the redupl. pf.<BR> 1. To say, speak, Man. 9, 47.<BR> 2. To specify, Man. 8, 122.<BR> 3. To call, MBh. 3, 16065.<BR> 4. To pronounce, Man. 9, 44.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To pronounce, Man. 9, 45.<BR> 2. To say, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 8.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer. Hit. 10, 2.<BR> --Cf. ἦ = आह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
† 2. अह् अह्, ii. 5, अह्नु, Par. To pervade, or occupy (v. r. अड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
1. अह अह, a particle; Certainly, Chr. 287, 4 = Rigv. i. 48, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
2. ऽअह -अह, a substitute for अहन्, when part of compound words. Day, e. g. अघ-, n. A day of impurity, Man. 5, 84.<BR> अनिर्दशाह, i. e. अ-निस्-दशन्-, adj. f. हा, Not out of the ten days (of impurity which follow birth or death), Man. 8, 242.<BR> एकादशाह, i. e. एकादशन्-अह, adj. Lasting eleven days, MBh. 13, 4938.<BR> एकाह, i. e. एक-अह, m. One day, Man. 5, 59.<BR> कतिपयाह, i. e. कतिपय-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a " target="_blank">Page0067-a + 42</a>] Some day, Chr. 52, 19 (sing); Pañc. 9, 6 (plur.).<BR> क्षपाह, i. e. क्षपा-, A day and night, Man. 1, 68.<BR> त्रि-,<BR> I. n. Three days, Man. 4, 110.<BR> II. adj. Lasting three days, Rām. 1, 13, 43.<BR> दशाह, i. e. दशन्-, n. An interval of ten days, Man. 5, 59.<BR> पञ्चाह, i. e. पञ्चन्-, n. A period of five days, Kathās. 41, 26.<BR> पुण्य-, n. A holy day, Chr. 25, 20.<BR> सप्ताह, i. e. सप्तन्-, n. Seven days, a week.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंकार|अहङ्कार|अहङ्कारः
अहंकार अहंकार, i. e. अहम्-कार, m.<BR> 1. Conceiving objects with the notion that they refer to one's own self, egotism, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 3.<BR> 2. Pride, Rām. 4, 6, 22.<BR> 3. Self-conceit, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 4; arrogance, Rājat. 5, 234.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहंकार|निरहङ्कार
निस्- + अहंकार निस्- + अहंकार, adj. free from selfishness, MBh. 15, 882.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंकृत|अहङ्कृत
अहंकृत अहंकृत, i. e. अहम्-कृत, adj.<BR> 1. Selfish, Bhag. 18, 17.<BR> 2. Proud, Yājñ. 3, 151.<BR> 3. Arrogant, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहंकृत
अन्- + अहंकृत अन्- + अहंकृत, adj. not arrogant, Man. 9, 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहंकृत
निस्- + अहंकृत निस्- + अहंकृत, adj. 1. Impersonal, Bhāg. P. 6, 16, 8. 2. Not selfish, Bhāg. P. 3, 32, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंकृति|अहङ्कृति|अहङ्कृतिः
अहंकृति अहंकृति, i. e. अहम्-कृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Selfishness, Bhartṛ. 3, 95.<BR> 2. Pride, Rājat. 5, 481.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् अहन्; several cases have as their base अहस्, which is used also as former part of compound words, n. A day, Śiś. 9, 23. Ved. अहा for अहानि, Chr. 289, 7 = Rigv. i. 50, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्
अहम् अहम् (see अस्मद्). Former part of many compound words, implying the first person, e. g. अहंकार, see above; अहम्-पूर्व, see पूर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्पति|अहर्पतिः
अहर्पति अहर्पति, i. e. अहन्-पति, m. The sun, Ragh. 10, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्या
अहल्या अहल्या, f. The wife of Gautama, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहह
अहह अहह, interj.<BR> 1. of surprise, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b " target="_blank">Page0067-b + 39</a>] Bhartṛ. 2, 28;<BR> 2. of pain, Bhartṛ. 2, 29;<BR> 3. of pleasure, Vikr. 65, 11;<BR> 4. of calling, Hit. 12, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्यत्व|अहार्य्यत्व
अहार्यत्व अ-हार्य + त्व (vb. हृ), n. Condition of not being easily taken away, Hit. Pr. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि अहि, i. e. probably *अंह् + इ (cf. अंहस्), A snake, Kir. 5, 47.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἔχις; Lat. anguis; probably also ὄϕις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहि|अन्धाहिः
अन्ध- + अहि अन्ध- + अहि, m. a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिर्ब्रध्न
अहिर्ब्रध्न अहिर्ब्रध्न, i. e. अहि + स्-ब्रध्न, m. The name of a Rudra or deity, MBh. 5, 3899.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन अहीन, m. The name of a sacrifice, Man. 11, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो अहो, interj.<BR> 1. of calling, Pañc. 45, 12;<BR> 2. of grief, Pañc. 21, 3;<BR> 3. of regret, Śāk. d. 35;<BR> 4. of contempt, Pañc. Pr. d. 8;<BR> 5. of surprise, Pañc. 76, 24;<BR> 6. of praise, Hit. 17, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र अहोरात्र, i. e. अहन्-रात्र, m. and n. A day of twenty-four hours or thirty मुहूर्तस्, Man. 1, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्न|अह्नः
ऽअह्न -अह्न, i. e. अहन् + अ, A substitute for अहन् in the latter part of some compound words, e. g. पराह्न and पराहन्, i. e. पर-, m. The afternoon.<BR> पूर्व-, and प्र-, m. The forenoon, Man. 2, 256.<BR> मध्य-, m. Noon, Lass. 73, 18.<BR> साय-, m. Evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय अह्नाय, (properly dat. sing. of the preceding), adv. Soon, Ragh. 5, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
1. आ आ, interj. of reminiscence. Ah! Prab. 46, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
2. आ आ.<BR> I. prep.<BR> 1. With abl., implying:<BR> a. Limit inceptive: From, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a " target="_blank">Page0068-a + 42</a>] Chr. 295, 17 = Rigv. i. 92, 17; Daśak. in Chr. 195, 17.<BR> b. Limit conclusive: Until, with abl., Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR> 2. With loc., On, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4; In, Chr. 297, 17 = Rigv. 1, 112, 17.<BR> II. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> III. Former part of compounded nouns and adverbs: signifying<BR> 1. From, e. g. आ-कुमार + म्, adv. From (my) youth, MBh. 3, 1403.<BR> 2. Up to, till, e. g. आ-गोपाल, adj. Reaching up to the herdsmen, MBh. 2, 531. आ-मरण + म्, adv. Till death, Pañc. i. d. 44. Compounded adverbs of this kind, when they are former part of a compound word, drop the final म्, e. g. आ-योजन-सु-गन्धि, adj. Spreading fragrance as far as a yojana, MBh. 1, 6965.<BR> 3. A little, as former part of adj. or participles, e. g. आ-पीत, adj. Yellowish, Rām. 2, 76, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकत्थन|आकत्थनं
आकत्थन आ-कत्थ् + अन, adj. Boasting, Rām. 6, 3, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प|आकंपः|आकम्पः
आकम्प आ-कम्प् + अ, m. Shaking, Rām. 3, 62, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकम्प
अन्- + आकम्प अन्- + आकम्प, adj. unshakeable, Vikr. d. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर|आकरः
आकर आकर, i. e. आ-कॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A multitude, Rām. 5, 17, 18.<BR> 2. A mine, Man. 7, 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाकर|कुसुमाकरः
कुसुम- + आकर कुसुम- + आकर, m. spring (literally, Having plenty of flowers), Bhag. 10, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माकर|पद्माकरः
पद्म- + आकर पद्म- + आकर, m. a pond abounding in lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाकर|रत्नाकरः
रत्न- + आकर रत्न- + आकर, m. 1. the ocean. 2. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिन्
आकरिन् अकरिन्, i. e. आकर + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Born in mines, Kir. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णन|आकर्णनं
आकर्णन आकर्णन, i. e. आकर्णय + अन, n. Hearing, Kathās. 16, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णय
आकर्णय आकर्णय, a denominative derived from आ-कर्ण, Par. To hear, Pañc. 19, 10.<BR> --With the prepos. सम् सम्, To perceive, Pañc. 19, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ष|आकर्षः
आकर्ष आकर्ष, i. e. आ-कृष् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b " target="_blank">Page0068-b + 42</a>] m.<BR> 1. Attraction, Prab. 61, 16.<BR> 2. Playing with dice, MBh. 2, 2110.<BR> 3. A proper name, MBh. 2, 1270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आकर्षण आकर्षण, i. e. आ-कृष् + अन, n. Attracting, drawing near, drawing on, MBh. 1, 7109.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलीनाकर्षण
खलीन- + आकर्षण खलीन- + आकर्षण, pulling of a bridle, Pañc. 258, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्प|आकल्पः
आकल्प आकल्प, i. e. आ-कॢप् + अ, m. Ornament, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकस्मिक|आकस्मिकं
आकस्मिक आकस्मिक, i. e. अ-कस्मात्, abl. of किम् + इक, adj., f. की, Sudden, Rājat. 5, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षा|आकांक्षा
आकाङ्क्षा आ-काङ्क्ष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Wish, Amar. 41.<BR> 2. A necessary supply, Bhāṣāp. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षिन्|आकांक्षिन्
ऽआकाङ्क्षिन् -आ-काङ्क्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Desiring, Rām. 1, 20, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकाङ्क्षिन्
निराकाङ्क्षिन् निराकाङ्क्षिन्, i. e. निस्-, adj. devoid of desire, MBh. 14, 537.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकार|आकारः
आकार आकार, i. e. आ-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Form, Śāk. 103, 18.<BR> 2. Countenance, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जाफलसमाकार
गुञ्जा-फल-सम-आकार गुञ्जा-फल-सम-आकार, adj. like the fruit of the guñjā, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधाकार
द्विधा- + आकार द्विधा- + आकार, adj., of two kinds, Pañc. iii. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निस्- + आकार निस्- + आकार, adj. 1. deprived of one's natural form, Rām. 2, 124, 24 Gorr. 2. disguised, MBh. 1, 5787. 3. unassuming, ib. 5, 1395.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाकार|वृथाकारः
वृथा- + आकार वृथा- + आकार, m. a vain, or useless appearance, Pañc. i. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारण|आकारणं
आकारण आकारण, i. e. आ-कृ, Caus. + अन, n. Calling up, Pañc. 227, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवन्त्|आकारवत्
आकारवन्त् आकार + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Embodied, Kathās. 17, 50.<BR> 2. Well-shaped, Nal. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिक|आकालिकं
आकालिक आकालिक, adj., f. का, i. e.<BR> I. अ-काल + इक, Unseasonable, Kumāras. 3, 34.<BR> II. आ-काल + इक, What must be deferred till the same time next day, Man. 4, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश|आकाशं|आकाशः
आकाश आ-काश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. The fifth element, æther, Man. 1, 75.<BR> 2. Sky. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a " target="_blank">Page0069-a + 41</a>] Pañc. 47, 14.<BR> 3. The open air, Man. 3, 90; Nal. 14, 10.<BR> 4. The loc. sing. शे denotes in dramatic language that which is spoken off the stage, Mṛcch. 32, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकाश
निस्- + आकाश निस्- + आकाश, adj. filled, Rām. 5, 64, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशग|आकाशगः
आकाशग आकाश-ग (vb. गम्).<BR> I. adj., f. गा, Moving in or through the sky, Rām. 2, 33, 8; 1, 38, 7.<BR> II. m. A bird, Chr. 41, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिंचन्य
आकिंचन्य आकिंचन्य, i. e. अ-किम्-चन + य, n. Poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चन|आकुंचनं|आकुञ्चनं
आकुञ्चन आ-कुञ्च् + अन, n. Bending together, Bhāṣāp. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल आकुल, i. e. probably आ-कॄ + अ, adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Crowded.<BR> 2. Fully occupied.<BR> 3. Confounded.<BR> 4. Distressed.<BR> 5. Perplexed.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अन्- + आकुल अन्- + आकुल, adj., composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्याकुल|पर्य्याकुल
परि- + आकुल परि- + आकुल, adj. 1. full of. 2. confused. 3. agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुल
सम्- + आकुल सम्- + आकुल, adj. 1. agitated, bewildered, confused. 2. crowded, thronged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलता
आकुलता आकुल + ता, f. Disturbance, MBh. 3, 401.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलत्व|आकुलत्वं
आकुलत्व आकुल + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Crowd, MBh. 3, 13711.<BR> 2. Disturbance, Bhartṛ. 1, 17.<BR> 3. Commotion, Śiś. 9, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलय
आकुलय आकुलय (a denomin. derived from आकुल), Par. To disturb, Pañc. 129, 18.<BR> आकुलित, Distressed, Rām. 2, 98, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूत|आकूतं
आकूत आ-कू + त (vb. कू, has no correspondent signification, but cf. κο in ἔκομεν, κών, κοέω, κοᾷ, κοάσαι, ἐκοάϑη and ἀκούω), n. Intention, Amar. 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
स- + आकूत स- + आकूत, adj. 1. intentional, Lass. 83, 2. 2. significant. 3. wanton. Acc. तम्, adv. intentionally, Kathās. 6, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूति|आकूतिः
आकूति आ-कू + ति (see the last), f. Intention, MBh. 3, 15539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृति|आकृतिः
आकृति आ-कृ + ति, f. Form, Śāk. d. 19; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b " target="_blank">Page0069-b + 42</a>] figure, Hiḍ. 2, 2; appearance, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
निस्- + आकृति निस्- + आकृति,<BR> I. adj. 1. shapeless, Hariv. 12090. 2. ugly, Mārk. P. 8, 83. 3. one who disregards his religious duties, Man. 3, 154. 4. annihilating, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 4.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनाकृति
वामन- + आकृति वामन- + आकृति, adj. dwarf-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिमन्त्|आकृतिमत्
आकृतिमन्त् आकृति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Embodied, Kathās. 10, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टि|आकृष्टिः
आकृष्टि आकृष्टि, i. e. आ-कृष् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Drawing, Amar. 1.<BR> 2. Attraction, Hit. i. d. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्द|आक्रंदः|आक्रन्दः
आक्रन्द आ-क्रन्द् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Calling loud, Man. 8, 292.<BR> 2. Cry of lamentation, Kathās. 10, 94.<BR> 3. A king, whose kingdom lies next but one, Man. 7, 207; cf. Kām. Nītis. viii. 17; 43; 46; sqq.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रन्द
अन्- + आक्रन्द अन्- + आक्रन्द, adj., f. दा, not crying, MBh. 1, 6568.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रन्दम्
दुराक्रन्दम् दुराक्रन्दम्, i. e. दुस्-आक्रन्द + म्, adv. miserably, Pañc. iv. d. 31 (thus to be read).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दन|आक्रंदनं
आक्रन्दन आ-क्रन्द् + अन, n. Crying, lamenting, Pañc. 145, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दिन्|आक्रंदिन्
आक्रन्दिन् आ-क्रन्द् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Calling lamentably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रम|आक्रमः
आक्रम आ-क्रम् + अ, m. Beginning, Kathās. 25, 64.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रम
दुस्- + आक्रम दुस्- + आक्रम, adj. 1. difficult to be attained, MBh. 7, 8861. 2. difficult to be attacked, Rām. 1, 23, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमण|आक्रमणं
आक्रमण आक्रमण, i. e. आ-क्रम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Ascending, Rām. 2, 31, 5.<BR> 2. Increase.<BR> 3. Entering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्ति|आक्रांतिः|आक्रान्तिः
आक्रान्ति आक्रान्ति, i. e. आ-क्रम् + ति, f. Ascending, Kathās. 22, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड|आक्रीडः
आक्रीड आ-क्रीड् + अ.<BR> I. m. and n. A royal garden, Rām. 5, 9, 10; MBh. 3, 10823.<BR> II. m. Sport.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाक्रीड|देवाक्रीडः
देव- + आक्रीड देव- + आक्रीड, m. a play-ground of the gods, Hariv. 6980.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोश|आक्रोशः
आक्रोश आक्रोश. i. e. आ-क्रुश् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a " target="_blank">Page0070-a + 41</a>] m.<BR> 1. Abuse, Yājñ. 2, 302.<BR> 2. A curse.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रोशम्
दुराक्रोशम् दुराक्रोशम्, i. e. दुस्-आक्रोश + म्, adv. with terrible curses, Rām. 4, 9, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोष्टृ
आक्रोष्टृ आक्रोष्टृ, i. e. आ-क्रुश् + तृ, m. An abuser, MBh. 1, 3557.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेप|आक्षेपः
आक्षेप आक्षेप, i. e. आ-क्षिप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Convulsion, Kumāras. 7, 95.<BR> 2. Putting on, Kumāran, 17.<BR> 3. Throwing away.<BR> 4. Reproach, Bhartṛ. 2, 59; blame, Bhartṛ. 3, 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराक्षेप|शराक्षेपः
शर- + आक्षेप शर- + आक्षेप, m. a flight of arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षेपम्
स-आक्षेप + म् स-आक्षेप + म्, adv. revilingly, Pañc. 24, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डल|आखंडलः|आखण्डलः
आखण्डल आ-खण्ड् + अल, m. A name of Indra, Śāk. d. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखु|आखुः
आखु आखु, i. e. आ-खन् + उ, m. A rat, a mouse.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाखु|वनाखुः
वन- + आखु वन- + आखु, m. A hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेट|आखेटः
आखेट आखेट, m. Hunting, Kathās. 15, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटक|आखेटकः
आखेटक आखेट + क, m.<BR> 1. A hunter, Pañc. i. d. 432.<BR> 2. Hunting, Kathās. 9, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या आ-ख्या, f. A name, Śāk. 105, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयाख्य
उदय-आख्य उदय-आख्य, adj. called Udaya, Böhtl. Chr. 228, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमाख्य
किम्- + आख्य किम्- + आख्य, adj. how called, Śāk. 104, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाब्दाख्य
दशाब्द- + आख्य दशाब्द- + आख्य, i. e. दशन्-अब्द-, adj. declared to be of ten years, Man. 2, 134 (i. e. a citizen may be considered as equal to another citizen who is ten years older or younger than himself).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्याति|आख्यातिः
आख्याति आ-ख्या + ति, f.<BR> 1. A tale, a report.<BR> 2. Appellation, Kathās. 18, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यान|आख्यानं
आख्यान आख्यान, i. e. आ-ख्या + अन, n.<BR> 1. A tale.<BR> 2. A legend, Nal. 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानक|आख्यानकं
आख्यानक आख्यान + क, n. A little tale, Pañc. 72, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यापन
आख्यापन आख्यापन, i. e. आ-ख्या, Caus. + अन, n. Invitation to give a report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिका
आख्यायिका आख्यायिका, i. e. आ-ख्या + अक, f. A tale, MBh. 2, 453, with short final on account of the metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिन्
आख्यायिन् आख्यायिन्, i. e. आ-ख्या + इन्, adj., f. नी, Reporting, Śāk. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगति|आगतिः
आगति आगति, i. e. आ-गम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Arrival, Śiś. 9, 43.<BR> 2. Concern, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 9 (that you have something to do with the theft).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतागति
गत- + आगति गत- + आगति, f. literally, coming and going, i. e. origin and disappearance, Rām. 2, 110, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत्व
आगत्व आ-ग + त्व (vb. गम्), n. Concern, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 4 (तद्-आगत्वेन चाहम् अपदेश्यह्, And you will denounce that I have to do with that; चा˚ must be read instead of ना˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आगन्तु आगन्तु, i. e. आ-गम् + तु, adj.<BR> 1. One who arrives, Hit. 18, 2.<BR> 2. Incidental, adventitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक आगन्तु + क.<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Arriving.<BR> 2. Incidental.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A stranger, Hit. 70, 12.<BR> 2. An estray (Jur.), Yājñ. 2, 163.<BR> 3. A vagabond, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम|आगमं|आगमः
आगम आ-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Arrival, Rām. 2, 25, 19.<BR> 2. Occurrence, Yājñ. 2, 92.<BR> 3. Stream, Man. 8, 252.<BR> 4. Afflux of wealth, Bhartṛ. 2, 39.<BR> 5. Report, Yājñ. 2, 212.<BR> 6. Knowledge, Rām. 6, 4, 30.<BR> 7. Art, Mālav. 15, d. 16.<BR> 8. Sacred science, Kir. 5, 22.<BR> 9. A work on sacred science, Kir. 5, 18.<BR> 10. A precept, MBh. 3, 1163.<BR> 11. A legal title, Man. 8, 202.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अन्- + आगम अन्- + आगम, m. not returning, MBh. 3, 8868.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थागम|अर्थागमः
अर्थ- + आगम अर्थ- + आगम, m. revenue, Hit. Pr. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदागम|जलदागमः
जलद- + आगम जलद- + आगम, m. the approach of the rainy season, Nal. 21, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनागम|दिनागमः
दिन- + आगम दिन- + आगम, m. daybreak, Hariv. 4287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरागम|दुरागमः
दुस्- + आगम दुस्- + आगम, m. illegal afflux of wealth, MBh. 5, 1513.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनागम
धन- + आगम धन- + आगम, m. afflux of wealth, Man. 8, 347.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मागम|धर्मागमः
धर्म- + आगम धर्म- + आगम, m. a code of law, Mārk. P. 23, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पागम|पुष्पागमः
पुष्प- + आगम पुष्प- + आगम, m. spring, Ṛt. 6, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमागम|हिमागमः
हिम- + आगम हिम- + आगम, m. winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमन|आगमनं
आगमन आ-गम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Coming, arrival, Nal. 3, 21.<BR> 2. Origin, Rām. 4, 2, 29.<BR> 3. Sexual intercourse, Rājat. 5, 399.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागमन
अन्- + आगमन अन्- + आगमन, m. non-returning, Pañc. 89, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनतस्
आगमनतस् आगमन + तस्. adv. In consequence of the arrival, Indr. 5, 23 (thus to be read).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमवन्त्|आगमवत्
आगमवन्त् आगम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having sexual intercourse. MBh. 1, 3025.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमापायिन् आगमापायिन्, i. e. आगम-अपाय + इन्, adj. Coming and going, Bhag. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् आगस्, n. Crime, Man. 9, 241; fault, Śiś. 9, 60; sin, Ragh. 2, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागस्
अन्- + आगस् अन्- + आगस्, adj. faultless. Brāhmaṇav. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागस्
कृत- + आगस् कृत- + आगस्, adj. guilty, Amar. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतागस्
अ-कृत- + आगस् अ-कृत- + आगस्, adj. innocent, Rām. 1, 7, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागस्
निस्- + आगस् निस्- + आगस्, adj. innocent, Rājat. 5, 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्य|आगस्त्यः
आगस्त्य आगस्त्य, i. e. अगस्ति + य or अगस्त्य + अ, adj. Referring to Agasti, or Agastya, MBh. 1, 442.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आगामिन् आगामिन्, i. e. आ-गम् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Arriving.<BR> 2. Future, next, Pañc. 169, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगार|आगारं
आगार आगार (perhaps अगार + अ), n. A house, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यागार|अग्न्यागारः
अग्नि- + आगार अग्नि- + आगार, m. a building for keeping the sacred fire, Man. 4, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरागार
अन्तर्- + आगार अन्तर्- + आगार, m. a private chamber, Yājñ. 2, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागार|आयुधागारं
आयुध- + आगार आयुध- + आगार, n. an arsenal, Man. 9, 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटागार|कूटागारं
कूट- + आगार कूट- + आगार, n. an apartment on the top of a house, Rām. 5, 12, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशागार|कोशागारः
कोश- + आगार कोश- + आगार, or कोष-, m. and n. a treasury, Rām. 6, 111, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठागार
कोष्ठ- + आगार कोष्ठ- + आगार, m. and n. a treasury, Man. 9, 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकागार|कौतुकागारः
कौतुक- + आगार कौतुक- + आगार, m., n. a nuptial apartment, Kumāras. 7, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भागार|गर्भागारं
गर्भ- + आगार गर्भ- + आगार, the sanctuary of a temple, Kathās. 7, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवागार|देवागारः
देव- + आगार देव- + आगार, and देवता-, m. a temple, Rām. 2, 71, 36; Man. 9, 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षागार|प्रेक्षागारः
प्रेक्षा- + आगार प्रेक्षा- + आगार, a temporary structure consisting of stalls for spectators.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनागार|बंधनागार|बन्धनागारः
बन्धन- + आगार बन्धन- + आगार, a jail, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b " target="_blank">Page0071-b + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डागार|भांडागार|भाण्डागारः
भाण्ड- + आगार भाण्ड- + आगार,<BR> I. m. a store-room.<BR> II. n. a treasury, Rājat. 5, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तागार|मुक्तागारं|मुक्तागारः
मुक्ता- + आगार मुक्ता- + आगार, n. the pearl oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरव
आगुरव आगुरव, i. e. अगुरु + अ, adj., f. वी, Produced by agallochum, Śiś. 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र आग्नीध्र, i. e. अग्नि-इन्ध् + र + अ, m. A priest (who kindles the sacrificial fire?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय आग्नेय, i. e. अग्नि + एय.<BR> I. adj., f. यी, Belonging or relating to fire or the deity of fire, Man. 9, 310.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयण|आग्रयणं|आग्रयणः
आग्रयण आग्रयण (from अग्र).<BR> I. n. Offering of new grain, MBh. 3, 14188, and in the vedic literature; in the classic books it is spelled आग्रायण, e. g. Rām. 3, 22, 6; Yājñ. 1, 25; Man. 6, 10, Lois.<BR> II. m. A name of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह|आग्रहः
आग्रह आ-ग्रह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Favour, Kumāras. 5, 7.<BR> 2. Pertinacity, Śukasapt. 6; 8; Kathās. 25, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराग्रह|दुराग्रहः
दुस्- + आग्रह दुस्- + आग्रह, m. blameable pertinacity, Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहिका
आग्रहिका आ-ग्रह् + इका, f. (of अक) Help, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायण
आग्रायण आग्रायण, see आग्रयण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघात|आघातः
आघात आघात, i. e. आ-हन्, Caus. + अ, m.<BR> 1. Beating, Rājat. 5, 417.<BR> 2. A stroke, Bhartṛ. 2, 83.<BR> 3. A cast, Rājat. 5, 463.<BR> 4. A gust, Rājat. 5, 330.<BR> 5. Killing, Bhartṛ. 2, 60 (read प्राणा˚).<BR> 6. A slaughter-house, Mṛcch. 161, 11.<BR> 7. An execution-place, Hit. iv. d. 64.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाघात|तटाघातः
तट- + आघात तट- + आघात, m. butting at a bank or mound, Kumāras. 2, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाघात|पक्षाघातः
पक्ष- + आघात पक्ष- + आघात, m. Hemiplegy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराघात|शराघातः
शर- + आघात शर- + आघात, m. shooting with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणि|आघृणिः
आघृणि आघृणि, i. e. आ-घृ + नि, adj. Radiant, Lass. 99, 5 (read पूषन्न्-आघृणे) = Rigv. iii. 62, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषणा
आघोषणा आघोषणा, i. e. आ-घुष् + अन, f. A proclamation, Pañc. 261, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राणतस्
आघ्राणतस् आघ्राणतस्, i. e. आ-घ्रा + अन + तस्, adv. By smelling, Kathās. 13, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आङ्ग आङ्ग, i. e. 3. अङ्ग + अ adj., f. गी, An inhabitant of Anga, MBh. 1, 3772.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गारक
आङ्गारक आङ्गारक, i. e. अङ्गार + क, n. A multitude of firebrands, Pañc. iii. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आङ्गिरस आङ्गिरस, i. e. अङ्गिरस् + अ, patronym., f. सी, A descendant of Angiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमन|आचमनं
आचमन आ-चम् + अन, n. Rinsing the mouth, Yājñ. 1, 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण|आचरणं
आचरण आचरण, i. e. आ-चर् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Arrival, Chr. 287, 3 = Rigv. i. 48, 3.<BR> 2. Conduct, MBh. 15, 312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम|आचामः
आचाम आचाम, i. e. आ-चम् + अ, m. The water or scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार|आचारः
आचार आचार, i. e. आ-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rule of conduct, Man. 2, 69.<BR> 2. Good custom, good conduct, Sāv. 6, 16.<BR> 3. Conduct, Rām. 6, 10, 24.<BR> 4. Sacred usage, Ragh. 2, 10.<BR> 5. Use, Śāk. d. 100.<BR> 6. Rule. MBh. 3, 166.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचार|दक्षिणाचारः
दक्षिण- + आचार दक्षिण- + आचार, adj. conducting one's self honestly, MBh. 4, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखाचार
दुःख- + आचार दुःख- + आचार, adj., f. रा, one who is difficult to dead with, MBh. 4, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचार|दुराचारः
दुस्- + आचार दुस्- + आचार,<BR> I. m. bad conduct, ib. 12, 4539.<BR> II. adj., f. रा, following bad customs, Man. 4, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाचार
काम- + आचार काम- + आचार, adj. following one's own will, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचार|सदाचारः
सदाचार सदाचार i. e. सन्त्- (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), m. 1. approved usage, Man. 2, 18. 2. virtuous conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारतस्
आचारतस् आचार + तस्, adv. From immemorial custom. Man. 1, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवन्त्|आचारवत्
आचारवन्त् आचार + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b " target="_blank">Page0072-b + 40</a>] Virtuous, Rām. 5, 21, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचारवन्त्|सदाचारवत्
सदाचार + वन्त् सदाचार + वन्त्, i. e. सन्त्- (see आचार), adj. one who observes the approved usages, Man. 4, 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य|आचार्यः|आचार्य्य|आचार्य्यः
आचार्य आचार्य, i. e. आचार + य, m. A spiritual guide or teacher; he who invests the student with the sacrificial thread and instructs him in the Vedas, etc., Man. 2, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचार्य|कुलाचार्यः|कुलाचार्य्य|कुलाचार्य्यः
कुल- + आचार्य कुल- + आचार्य, m. a family priest, Bhāg. P. 9, 1, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्याचार्य|नाट्याचार्यः
नाट्य- + आचार्य नाट्य- + आचार्य, m. a dancing master, Mṛcch. 49, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यक|आचार्य्यक
आचार्यक आचार्य + क, n. in नाट्य-, Teaching the scenic art, i. e. dancing and acting, Pañc. iii. d. 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यता
आचार्यता आचार्य + ता, f., and आचार्यत्व आचार्य + त्व, n. The condition of a teacher, Chr. 28, 32; Śiś. 9, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यवन्त्|आचार्यवत्
आचार्यवन्त् आचार्य + वन्त्, adj. Having a teacher, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद|आच्छादः|आछाद
आच्छाद आच्छाद, i. e. आ-छद् + अ, m. Cloth, Man. 7, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादकत्व
आच्छादकत्व आच्छादक + त्व, i. e. आ-छद् + अक + त्व, n. Covering, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादन|आच्छादनं|आछादन
आच्छादन आच्छादन, i. e. आ-छद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Covering, Pañc. 22, 17.<BR> 2. Cloth, Man. 3, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादिन्
आच्छादिन् आच्छादिन्, i. e. आ-छद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Covering, Śāk. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज|आजं|आजः
आज आज, i. e. 2. अज + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Coming from goats.<BR> 2. Made of goat's flesh, Rām. 2, 91, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजनन|आजननं
आजनन आ-जन् + अन, n., and आजाति आजाति, i. e. आ-जन् + ति, f., New birth, transmigration, MBh. 1, 4561; Man. 4, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानेय|आजानेयः
आजानेय आजानेय, i. e. आ-जन् + इ + एय,<BR> I. adj. f. यी, Of good race, MBh. 2, 1733.<BR> II. m. A horse of good breed, Draup. 7, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजि|आजिः
आजि आजि, i. e. अज् + इ, f. and m.<BR> 1. Battle, Arj. 10, 74.<BR> 2. Level ground, field of battle, Chr. 36, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिहीर्षु
आजिहीर्षु आजिहीर्षु, i. e. आ-जिहीर्ष, desider. of हृ + उ, adj. Desiring to fetch, with acc., MBh. 3, 11078.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव|आजीवः
आजीव आ-जीव् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Livelihood, MBh. 14, 956.<BR> 2. Profession, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गाजीव|रंगाजीव|रङ्गाजीवः
रङ्ग- + आजीव रङ्ग- + आजीव, m. 1. a painter. 2. an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याजीव|स्त्र्याजीवः
स्त्री- + आजीव स्त्री- + आजीव, m. one who subsists by (the harlotry of) a wife, Man. 11, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवन|आजीवनं
आजीवन आ-जीव् + अन, n. Livelihood, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्य
आजीव्य आजीव्य, i. e. आजीव + य,<BR> I. adj. Granting livelihood, MBh. 14, 1330.<BR> II. n. Provisions, MBh. 3, 8452.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाजीव्य
सु- + आजीव्य सु- + आजीव्य, adj. yielding an easy subsistence, Man. 7, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञत्व
ऽआज्ञत्व -आज्ञत्व in अ-खण्डित-, i. e. अ-खण्डित-आज्ञ, from आज्ञा, + त्व, n. The whole authority, Rājat. 6, 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा आ-ज्ञा, f.<BR> 1. An order, Rājat. 5, 3.<BR> 2. Authority, Bhartṛ. 2, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाज्ञा
अन्- + आज्ञा अन्- + आज्ञा, f. want of assent, Man. 9, 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकर|आज्ञाकरः
आज्ञाकर आज्ञा-कर, m., f. री, A servant, Śāk. 110, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकरत्व
आज्ञाकरत्व आज्ञाकर + त्व, n. The office of a servant, Vikr. d. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्य|आज्यं
आज्य आज्य, i. e. आ-अञ्ज् + य, n. Butter in a liquid state, which is poured on a sacrificial fire.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराज्य
वर- + आज्य वर- + आज्य, n. choicest liquid butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यप
आज्यप आज्य-प (vb. 1. पा), m. The Pitṛs or Manes of the Vaiśyas, Man. 3, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यभुज्
आज्यभुज् आज्य-भुज्, m. A name of Agni, Rām. 3, 20, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्छ्|आंछ्
आञ्छ् आञ्छ्, i. 1, Par. To stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जन|आंजन|आञ्जनः
आञ्जन आञ्जन, i. e. आ-अञ्ज् + अन, n. and f. नी, Ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविक|आटविकः
आटविक आटविक, i. e. अटवि + इक, m.<BR> 1. One who lives in forests, MBh. 3, 15255.<BR> 2. A forest keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोप|आटोपः
आटोप आटोप, m.<BR> 1. Inflation.<BR> 2. Pride, Pañc. i. d. 229; 46, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
स- + आटोप स- + आटोप, adj. 1. swollen, big, Pañc. 93, 8. 2. Proud. Acc. पम्, adv. arrogantly, proudly, Hit. 58, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बर|आडंबरः|आडम्बरः
आडम्बर आडम्बर, m. A drum, Rām. 5, 13, 51 (where erroneously is read आडम्पर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढक|आढकं|आढकः
आढक आढक (a transformation of अर्ध + क), m. n. A measure of grain, equal to 7 lb. 11 oz. avoirdupois, Hit. Pr. d. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य आढ्य, i. e. probably a transformation of ऋध् + अ + य. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Wealthy, Chr. 61, 38.<BR> 2. A bounding in.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाढ्य
रत्न- + आढ्य रत्न- + आढ्य, adj. abounding in jewels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यता
आढ्यता आढ्य + ता, f. Wealth, Rājat. 5, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्
आत् आत् (the regular abl. sing. n. of the pronoun इदम्) adv. Then, Chr. 293, 5 = Rigv. i. 87, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्क|आतंक|आतंकः|आतङ्कः
आतङ्क आतङ्क, i. e. आ-तञ्च् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sickness, Yājñ. 3, 245.<BR> 2. Affliction, Vikr. 41, 20.<BR> 3. Agitation, fear.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टातङ्कम्|नष्टातंकम्
नष्ट-आतङ्क + म् नष्ट-आतङ्क + म्, adv. fearless, Śāk. d. 14 n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरातङ्क|निरातंक|निरातङ्कः
निस्- + आतङ्क निस्- + आतङ्क, adj. 1. without ailment, Dev. 12, 30. 2. not causing ailment, MBh. 2, 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन् आततायिन्, i. e. आ-तत (vb. तन्) + विन् (य् instead of व् as in कियन्त् for किम् + वन्त्),<BR> I. adj. Assailing, Chr. 3, 1.<BR> II. m. A felon, a murderer, a thief, Man. 8, 350.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आतप आ-तप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sunshine, Pañc. ii. d. 136.<BR> 2. Heat of the sun, Śāk. 31, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अन्- + आतप अन्- + आतप, adj. shadowy, Bhartṛ. 2, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालातप|बालातपः
बाल- + आतप बाल- + आतप, m. the rays of the rising sun, Man. 4, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यातप|सूर्यातपः
सूर्य- + आतप सूर्य- + आतप, m. sunshine, Pañc. 121, 13; heat of the sun, Ṛt. 1, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्र|आतपत्रं
आतपत्र आतप-त्र (vb. त्रा), n. A parasol, Kir. 5, 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छीलीन्ध्रातपत्र
उच्छीलीन्ध्र- + आतपत्र उच्छीलीन्ध्र- + आतपत्र, i. e. उद्-शिलीन्ध्र-, adj., f. रा, having raised mushrooms instead of parasols, Megh. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवन्त्|आतपवत्
आतपवन्त् आतप + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Irradiated by the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय आतिथेय, i. e. अतिथि + एय,<BR> I. adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Proper for a guest, Śāk. 7, 11.<BR> 2. Hospitable, Ragh. 12, 25.<BR> II. n. Hospitality, Man. 3, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य आतिथ्य, i. e. अतिथि + य, n. Hospitable salutation, Chr. 13, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरैक्य|आतिरैक्यं
आतिरैक्य आतिरैक्य, i. e. अतिरेक + य, n. Having some redundant member, Man. 11, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर आतुर, adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Diseased, Rām. 3, 55, 36.<BR> 2. Wounded, Rām. 3, 50, 19.<BR> 3. Agitated by a morbid desire; प्रधर्षयितुम् आतुरः, Desirous to violate her, Nal. 11, 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अन्- + आतुर अन्- + आतुर, adj. 1. free from illness, Man. 2, 187. 2. indefatigable, Ragh. 1, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगन्ध|आत्तगन्धः
आत्तगन्ध आत्त-गन्ध, i. e. आ-दत्त- (vb. दा), adj. Strangled, Śāk. 93, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्म
ऽआत्म -आत्म, A substitute for आत्मन् when latter part of compound words, e. g. प्रत्यय-, adj. Trustworthy, Rām. 2, 109, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मक
ऽआत्मक -आत्मक, i. e. आत्मन् + क, adj., f. मिका, A substitute for आत्मन्, when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. अष्टादशात्मक, i. e. अष्टा-दशन्-आत्मक, adj. Eighteenfold, Rām. 1, 13, 30. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b " target="_blank">Page0074-b + 45</a>]<BR> उभय-, adj. Having the nature of both, Man. 2, 92.<BR> करुण-, adj. Compassionate, Rām. 1, 10, 6.<BR> काल-, adj. Governed by fate, MBh. 13, 52 sqq.<BR> दाह-, adj. Easily flashing up, Śāk. d. 40.<BR> विषय-, adj. Sensual, Man. 2, 29.<BR> सदसद्-, i. e. सन्त्-अ-सन्त्- (cf. vb. 1. अस्), adj. Having the nature of entity and non-entity, Man. 1, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकाम
आत्मकाम आत्मकाम, i. e. आत्मन्-कम् + अ, adj., f. मा, Selfish, Rām. 2, 70, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकीय
आत्मकीय आत्मकीय, i. e. आत्मन् + क + ईय, adj. Own, MBh. 1, 4712.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज|आत्मजः
आत्मज आत्मज, i. e. आत्मन्-ज (vb. जन्),<BR> I. m. A son, Man. 7, 14.<BR> II. f. जा, A daughter, Rām. 1, 1, 69.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मज|धर्मात्मजः
धर्म- + आत्मज धर्म- + आत्मज, m. epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira, Lass. 15, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दात्मज|नंदात्मज|नन्दात्मजः
नन्द- + आत्मज नन्द- + आत्मज,<BR> I. m. a name of Kṛṣṇa, Gīt. 8, 11.<BR> II. f. जा, a name of Durgā, MBh. 4, 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणात्मज|वरुणात्मजः
वरुण- + आत्मज वरुण- + आत्मज, f. जा, spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञ|आत्मज्ञः
आत्मज्ञ आत्मज्ञ, i. e. आत्मन्-ज्ञ (vb. ज्ञा), adj., f. ञा, Knowing the Supreme Being, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मज्ञ
अन्- + आत्मज्ञ अन्- + आत्मज्ञ, adj. foolish, Śāk. 78, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन् आत्मन्, i. e. probably *अवा (= वा) + त्मन् (cf. ἀϋτμήν, ἀϋτμή, ἀτμή, ἀτμός), m.<BR> 1. Breath.<BR> 2. The soul. Bhāṣāp. 97.<BR> 3. One's own self, Man. 4, 254.<BR> 4. Self, own; used, but only in the sing., as reflective pronoun of all the three persons, e. g. दर्शयात्मानम्, Show thyself, Nal. 11, 8. गोपायन्ति कुलस्त्रियः आत्मानम् आत्मना, Virtuous wives protect themselves by means of themselves, Nal. 18, 8.<BR> 5. The instr. sing. compounded with following ordinal numbers denotes one's self as making up the number, e. g. आत्मना-सप्तम, Himself as the seventh, i. e. he with six.<BR> 6. The body.<BR> 7. Intellect, understanding.<BR> 8. The soul of the universe, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 4.<BR> 9. The initial आ when preceded by ए or ओ is sometimes in vedic and epic writings irregularly [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-a " target="_blank">Page0075-a + 47</a>] dropped, e. g. Draup. 5, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> I. When latter part it denotes often, 1. nature, mind, e. g. कृत-, adj. whose mind is improved, Pañc. ii. d. 15.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. atum; A.S. aedhm, and see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतात्मन्
अ-कृत- + आत्मन् अ-कृत- + आत्मन्, adj. whose mind is not improved, Man. 6, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितात्मन्
जित- + आत्मन् जित- + आत्मन्, adj. one who has subdued his mind, who restrains himself, Pañc. 131, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितात्मन्
अ-जित- + आत्मन् अ-जित- + आत्मन्, adj. one who has not subdued his mind, Man. 7, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतात्मन्
प्रीत- + आत्मन् प्रीत- + आत्मन्, adj. with an affectionate mind, Man. 1, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तात्मन्
शान्त- + आत्मन् शान्त- + आत्मन् (vb. शम्), adj. with a tranquil mind, Man. 1, 52. 2. natural disposition, e. g. कर्मात्मन्, i. e. कर्मन्-, adj. having a natural disposition for action, Man. 2, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मन्
काम- + आत्मन् काम- + आत्मन्, adj. voluptuous, Man. 7, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलात्मन्
चल- + आत्मन् चल- + आत्मन्, adj. unsteady, Rām. 4, 55, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मन्|धर्म्मात्मन्
धर्म- + आत्मन् धर्म- + आत्मन्, adj. just, Rām. 1, 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापात्मन्
पाप- + आत्मन् पाप- + आत्मन्, adj. wicked, Pañc. 37, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्मन्
महा- + आत्मन् महा- + आत्मन्, adj. magnanimous, Pañc. ii. d. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रात्मन्
सूत्र- + आत्मन् सूत्र- + आत्मन्, m. having the nature of a thread, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरात्मन्
अन्तर्- + आत्मन् अन्तर्- + आत्मन्, m. the soul, Rājat. 5, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलात्मन्
केवल- + आत्मन् केवल- + आत्मन्, m. being the absolute unity, Kumāras. 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरात्मन्
चतुर्- + आत्मन् चतुर्- + आत्मन्, adj. having four faces, Rājat. 5, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायात्मन्
छाया- + आत्मन् छाया- + आत्मन्, m. an image, Megh. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदात्मन्
जगत्- + आत्मन् जगत्- + आत्मन्, m. the soul of the world, Rām. 6, 82, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवात्मन्
जीव- + आत्मन् जीव- + आत्मन्, m. the individual soul, Bhāg. P. 6, 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्मन्
दत्त- + आत्मन् दत्त- + आत्मन्, (vb. दा), adj. one who has given himself (as a son to another), Yājñ. 2, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशात्मन्
द्वादशात्मन् द्वादशात्मन्, i. e. द्वादशन्-, adj. appearing in twelve forms, MBh. 3, 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमात्मन्
परम- + आत्मन् परम- + आत्मन्, m. the universal soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितात्मन्
भावित- + आत्मन् भावित- + आत्मन् (vb. भू), adj. 1. intent upon. 2. having obtained (the union with) the universal soul, Pañc. iii. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतात्मन्
भूत- + आत्मन् भूत- + आत्मन्, m. 1. the elementary or vital principle. 2. the body. 3. Brahman. 4. Śiva. 5. war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दात्मन्|मंदात्मन्
मन्द- + आत्मन् मन्द- + आत्मन्, adj. dull, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वात्मन्
विश्व- + आत्मन् विश्व- + आत्मन्, m. the soul of the universe, a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं|आत्मनीनः
आत्मनीन आत्मन् + ईन, adj.<BR> 1. Appropriate.<BR> 2. Suitable (as diet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभू
आत्मभू आत्मभू, i. e. आत्मन्-भू, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b " target="_blank">Page0075-b + 41</a>] adj. Self-existing, epithet of Brahman, Śāk. d. 186; of Viṣṇu, Śiva and Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूत|आत्मभूतः
आत्मभूत आत्मभूत, i. e. आत्मन्-भूत (vb. भू), adj. Attached to one's person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मंभरि|आत्मम्भरि|आत्मम्भरिः
आत्मंभरि आत्मंभरि, i. e. आत्मन्-भृ + इ, adj. Selfishly voracious, Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मंभरित्व
आत्मंभरित्व आत्मंभरि + त्व, n. Selfishness, Kathās. 26, 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्ता
आत्मवत्ता आत्मवत्ता, i. e. आत्मवन्त् + ता, f. Self-control, Man. 11, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवन्त्|आत्मवत्
आत्मवन्त् आत्मवन्त्, i. e. आत्मन् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. One who has subdued his senses; endowed with selfcontrol, Rām. 3, 51, 44.<BR> 2. Sensible, Man. 5, 43.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मवन्त्|अनात्मवत्
अन्- + आत्मवन्त् अन्- + आत्मवन्त्, adj. one who has no self-control, Nal. 20, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्
आत्मसात् आत्मसात्, i. e. आत्मन्-सात् (cf. अग्निसात्), adv.<BR> 1. In one's mind, Man. 6, 25.<BR> 2. On one's self, Yājñ. 3, 54.<BR> 3. Under one's self, MBh. 3, 493.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीभाव|आत्मीभावः
आत्मीभाव आत्मीभाव, i. e. आत्मन्-भू + अ, m. Becoming the universal soul, Bhartṛ. 3, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीय|आत्मीयः
आत्मीय आत्मीय, i. e. आत्मन् + ईय,<BR> I. adj., f. या, Own, poss. pron. of the refl. of all the three persons, Hit. 52, 16; Pañc. 63, 23.<BR> II. m. A friend, Bhartṛ. 2, 47.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मीय
अन्- + आत्मीय अन्- + आत्मीय, adj. not belonging to one's self, Pañc. 132, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिक|आत्यंतिक
आत्यन्तिक आत्यन्तिक, i. e. अत्यन्त + इक, adj., f. की, Continual, Man. 2, 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिक
आत्ययिक आत्ययिक, i. e. अत्यय + इक, adj. What must be done instantly, Man. 7, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेय|आत्रेयः
आत्रेय आत्रेय, i. e. अत्रि + एय.<BR> I. patronym., f. यी, A descendant of Atri, MBh. 3, 971.<BR> II. f. यी, A woman who has bathed after temporary uncleanness, Man. 11, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वण|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्वण आथर्वण, i. e. अथर्वन् + अ, adj., f. णी, Belonging to the Atharvaveda, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद
ऽआद -आद, i. e.<BR> I. अद् + अ, adj., f. दी, Eating, e. g. पुरुषाद, i. e. पुरुष-, Eating men. पृष्ठ-मांस-, m. A backbiter, a slanderer. मानुष-मांस-, Eating men's flesh, Hiḍ. 2, 2.<BR> II. आ-द (vb. दा), adj. Taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदक
ऽआदक -आदक, i. e. अद् + अक, adj. Eating, e. g. पुरुष-, Eating men, Hiḍ. 2, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर आदर, i. e. आ-द्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Regard, Kumāras. 6, 13.<BR> 2. Concern, Pañc. iii. d. 262.<BR> 3. Care, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 10.<BR> 4. Love, Pañc. iv. d. 7 (आदरात्, passionately).<BR> 5. Interest, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 8.<BR> 6. Respect, Kir. 5, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादर
अति- + आदर अति- + आदर, m. excessive regard, Pañc. i. d. 463.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अन्- + आदर अन्- + आदर, m. carelessness, Pañc. 202, 5, Bhartṛ. 2, 28 (राइ, easily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादर
स- + आदर स- + आदर, adj., f. रा. 1. impassioned, Ṛt. 6, 14. 2. respectful, Kathās. 2, 67. Acc. sing. रम्, adv. considerately, Pañc. 33, 16; respectfully, Pañc. 71, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर्श आदर्श, i. e. आ-दृश् + अ, and आदर्शक आदर्श + क, m. A mirror, Bhag. 3, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदातृ
आदातृ आ-दा + तृ, m. A receiver, Man. 4, 193.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादातृ
अन्- + आदातृ अन्- + आदातृ, m. a nonreceiver, Man. 6, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
आदान आदान, i. e. आ-दा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Seizing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 20. Seizure, Kumāras. 5, 11; Man. 7, 204.<BR> 2. Taking, receiving, Man. 11, 15. Receipt, Rājat. 5, 265.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनादान
अध्ययन- + आदान अध्ययन- + आदान, n. learning the Veda, Man. 11, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादान
निस्- + आदान निस्- + आदान, adj. not taking, MBh. 3, 8501.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसादान|रसादानं
रस- + आदान रस- + आदान, n. drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादान
सु- + आदान सु- + आदान, n. taking with justice, Man. 8, 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदानवन्त्|आदानवत्
आदानवन्त् आदान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Taking away, MBh. 3, 8501.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायिन्
आदायिन् आदायिन्, i. e. आ-दा + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Taking, MBh. 12, 5969 (अ-सम्-मत-, taking without assent, a thief).<BR> 2. Robbing, Man. 7, 123.<BR> 3. Bringing, Rājat. 5, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि आदि, i. e. आद्य, with इ for य,<BR> 1. m. Beginning, Man. 1, 8; 4, 25.<BR> 2. indecl. First, MBh. 2, 2008.<BR> --Comp.<BR> When latter part of a comp. adj. 1. having first, beginning with, e. g. Man. 3, 205, दैव-आदि-अन्त, beginning and ending with an offering to the gods. 2. other, et-cetera, e. g. Man. 1, 58, मरीचि-आदीन् मुनीन्, Marīci and the other Munis (properly, as before ‘The Munis beginning with Marīci’); Man. 3, 104, अन्न-आदि-दायिन्, giving food, etc. 3. the like, Man. 9, 260, एवम्-आदीन्...कण्टकान्, these and the like thorny weeds. 4. more, e. g. Man. 8, 407, गर्भिणी द्विमासादिह्. a woman who is pregnant two months or more. These adj. when without subst. are neuters: e. g. Nal. 13, 43, एवम्-आदीनि...विलप्य, lamenting thus and similarly; Hit. 12, 16, अतो ऽहं ब्रवीमि कङ्कणस्य तु लोभेनेत्य्-आदि, therefore I say, कङ्कणस्य et-cetera, i. e. the verse beginning with कङ्कणस्य तु लोभेन. Man. 8, 31, the masc. is used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिक
ऽआदिक -आदि + क, adj., f. का, a substitute for आदि as latter part of a compound adj., e. g. Man. 2, 143, अग्नि-ष्टोम-आदिकान् मखान्, the agniṣṭoma and the other sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितस्
आदितस् आदि + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. From the beginning, Chr. 11, 22.<BR> 2. First, Man. 1, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदर्शनादितस्
राम-दर्शन-आदितस् राम-दर्शन-आदितस्, after having seen Rāma, Rām. 1, 51, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य आदित्य, i. e. अदिति + य, m.<BR> 1. The name of a class of deities, sons of Aditi, Man. 3, 284.<BR> 2. The sun, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 24.<BR> 3. A deity in general, MBh. 18, 215.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादित्य
अति- + आदित्य अति- + आदित्य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a " target="_blank">Page0077-a + 39</a>] adj. surpassing the sun, Megh. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धादित्य
सु-गन्ध- + आदित्य सु-गन्ध- + आदित्य, m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आदित्सु आदित्सु, i. e. आ-दित्स, desid. of दा + उ, adj. Desirous to take, Hit. ii. d. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिन्
ऽआदिन् -आदिन्, i. e. अद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Eating, e. g. एकान्न-, i. e. एक-अन्न-, adj. Eating the food of one person only, Man. 2, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम आदि + म, adj., f. मा, First, Bhāṣāp. 20; 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिमन्त्|आदिमत्
आदिमन्त् आदि + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Having a beginning, Yājñ. 3, 183.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिमन्त्|अनादिमत्
अन्- + आदिमन्त् अन्- + आदिमन्त्, adj. without any beginning, Bhag. 13, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्
आदिश् आ-दिश्, f. Advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन् आदिष्टिन्, i. e. आ-दिष्ट + इन् (vb. दिश्), m. A student, Man. 5, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपक
आदीपक आ-दीप् + अक, m. An incendiary, MBh. 12, 3215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आदेश आदेश, i. e. आ-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Report, tidings, Yājñ. 2, 304.<BR> 2. Instruction, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 15.<BR> 3. Order, Rām. 3, 53, 29.<BR> 4. Prediction, Man. 9, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशक
आदेशक आदेशक, i. e. आ-दिश् + अक, adj. Announcing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवादेशक|शिवादेशकः
शिव- + आदेशक शिव- + आदेशक, m. a fortuneteller, Mālav. 69, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशतस्
आदेशतस् आदेश + तस्, adv. According to a command, Pañc. ii. d. 199 (with the gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशन|आदेशनं
आदेशन आदेशन, i. e. आ-दिश् + अन, n. Performance, Man. 2, 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आदेशिन् आदेशिन्, i. e. आ-दिश् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Commanding, Ragh. 4, 68 (कपोल-पाटल-, Commanding paleness to the cheeks of..., i. e. frightening).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य आद्य, i. e. आत् + य for ईय (cf. तर्य = तुरीय, वस्यंस् = वसियंस्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b " target="_blank">Page0077-b + 42</a>] etc.), adj., f. या.<BR> 1. First, Man. 7, 92.<BR> 2. Preeminent, MBh. 1, 8130.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्याद्य
आद्य-आद्य आद्य-आद्य, each preceding, Man. 1, 20. Like आदि (q. cf.), other, et-cetera, e. g. अन्न-, adj. food, etc., Pañc. i. d. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तवन्त्|आद्यन्तवत्
आद्यन्तवन्त् आद्यन्तवन्त्, i. e. आदि-अन्त + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having beginning and end, Bhag. 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्रिसार
आद्रिसार आद्रिसार, i. e. अद्रि-सार (see सार) + अ, adj. Of iron, Rām. 6, 18, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमन|आधमनं
आधमन आधमन, i. e. आ-ध्मा + अन, n. A pledge, Man. 8, 165.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाधमन|योगाधमनं
योग- + आधमन योग- + आधमन, n. a fraudulent pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधान|आधानं
आधान आधान, i. e. आ-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Adding, Man. 2, 176. 2. Preparing the holy fire, MBh. 3, 8194.<BR> 3. Lighting the nuptial fire, Man. 5, 186.<BR> 4. Conception, Megh. 3.<BR> 5. Pledging, Yājñ. 2, 238.<BR> 6. Using, Ragh. 1, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाधान|गर्भाधानं
गर्भ- + आधान गर्भ- + आधान, n. a ceremony performed previous to conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषाधान
पुरीष- + आधान पुरीष- + आधान, n. the strait-gut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधायक
आधायक आधायक, i. e. आ-धा + अक, adj. Bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आधार आधार, i. e. आ-धृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A prop, support, Rām. 5, 3, 77; Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 4.<BR> 2. A canal, Yājñ. 3, 144.<BR> 3. A basin round the foot of a tree, Śāk. d. 14.<BR> 4. A dike, Ragh. 5, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाधार|जलाधारः
जल- + आधार जल- + आधार, or तोय-, m. a reservoir of water, Yājñ. 3, 144; Śāk. d. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
आधि आधि, n., i. e.<BR> I. आ-धा (cf. निधि), A pledge, Man. 8, 143.<BR> II. आ-ध्यै, Mental agony, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्य|आधिक्यं
आधिक्य आधिक्य, i. e. अधिक + य, n.<BR> 1. Excess, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 19.<BR> 2. Preeminence, Rām. 5, 90, 24.<BR> 3. Superiority, Man. 7, 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक आधिदैविक, i. e. अधि-देव + इक, adj. Treating of the deities, Man. 6, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्य|आधिपत्यं
आधिपत्य आधिपत्य i. e. अधिपति + य, n. Sovereign dominion, Man. 12, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिवेदनिक|आधिवेदनिकं
आधिवेदनिक आधिवेदनिक, i. e. अधि-वेदन + इक, n. Property given to a first wife upon marrying a second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधोरण|आधोरणः
आधोरण आधोरण, i. e. आ-धोर् + अन, m. The driver of an elephant, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यात्मिक|आध्यात्मिकं
आध्यात्मिक आध्यात्मिक, i. e. अधि-आत्मन् + इक, adj., f. का and की, Referring to or treating of the universal soul; sacred, Man. 2, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वनिक
आध्वनिक आध्वनिक, i. e. अध्वन् + इक, adj. Travelling, MBh. 1, 3031.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक|आनकः
आनक आनक. m. A drum, Bhag. i, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानक|शतानकं
शत- + आनक शत- + आनक, m. a cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनडुह
आनडुह आनडुह, i. e. अनडुह् + अ, adj. Coming from a bull (as its flesh or hide).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनति|आनतिः
आनति आनति, i. e. आ-नम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Bowing, Amar. 22. Salutation, Kathās. 23, 17.<BR> 2. Homage, Rājat. 5, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन|आननं
आनन आनन, i. e. अन् + अन, n.<BR> 1. The mouth; the face, Ṛt. 6, 30.<BR> 2. A point, Rām. 6, 79, 69.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरानन|चतुराननः
चतुर्- + आनन चतुर्- + आनन, adj. having four faces, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानन|दशाननः
दशानन दशानन, i. e. दशन्-, adj. epithet of Rāvaṇa, Rām. 3, 39, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागानन|नागाननः
नाग- + आनन नाग- + आनन, m. a peacock, Pañc. i. d. 175 (perhaps to be changed to नागाशन, i. e. नाग-अशन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चानन|पंचानन|पञ्चाननः
पञ्चानन पञ्चानन, i. e. पञ्चन्-, 1. Śiva. 2. used at the end of names of scholars, Chr. 234, 6. 3. f. नी, perhaps a name of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन
महा- + आनन महा- + आनन, adj. having a great mouth, Hiḍ. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहसानन
सु-हस- + आनन सु-हस- + आनन, adj. having a cheerfully smiling face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्तर्य|आनंतर्यं|आनन्तर्य्य
आनन्तर्य आनन्तर्य, i. e. अन्-अन्तर + य, n. Absence of an interval, Man. 10, 28. Instr. येण, Instantly, Rām. 4, 23, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्त्य|आनंत्यं
आनन्त्य आनन्त्य, i. e. अनन्त + य, n. Eternity, Man. 3, 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द|आनंदः|आनन्दः
आनन्द आ-नन्द् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Joy, Rām. 1, 1, 17.<BR> 2. Sensual pleasure, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 20.<BR> 3. Happiness, bliss, ib. 202, 3; 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरानन्द
निस्- + आनन्द निस्- + आनन्द, adj., f. दा, joyless, Rām. 2, 47, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमानन्द|परमानन्दः
परम- + आनन्द परम- + आनन्द, m. 1. the highest bliss. 2. the universal soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दक|आनंदक
आनन्दक आ-नन्द् + अक, adj. Delighting, Hit. i. d. 204 v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दन|आनंदन|आनन्दनं
आनन्दन आ-नन्द् + अन, n. Delight, Hit. i. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमय|आनंदमय|आनन्दमयः
आनन्दमय आनन्द + मय, adj., f. यी, Full of joy or happiness, Kathās. 23, 85; Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दयितृ|आनंदयितृ
आनन्दयितृ आनन्दयितृ, i. e. आ-नन्द्, Caus. + तृ, m., f. त्री, n. Giving pleasure, Ragh. 14, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिन्|आनंदिन्
आनन्दिन् आनन्दिन्, i. e. आनन्द + इन्, adj., f. नी, Joyful, Rām. 6, 11, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयन|आनयनं
आनयन आनयन, i. e. आ-नी + अन, n.<BR> 1. Bringing near, Rām. 1, 12, 27.<BR> 2. Escorting, Śāk. 48, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्त|आनर्त्तः
आनर्त आनर्त, m., pl. The name of a people and their country (also sing.), Rām. 4, 43, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाथ्य|आनाथ्यं
आनाथ्य आनाथ्य, i. e. अ-नाथ + य, n. Want of protection, Kathās. 3, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय|आनायः
आनाय आनाय, i. e. आ-नी + अ, m. A net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनायिन्
आनायिन् आनायिन्, i. e. आनाय + इन्, m. A fisher, Ragh. 16, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाह|आनाहः
आनाह आनाह, i. e. आ-नह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstruction.<BR> 2. Length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीति|आनीतिः
आनीति आ-नी + ति, f. Bringing near, Rām. 1, 8, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूल्य|आनुकूल्यं
आनुकूल्य आनुकूल्य, i. e. अनुकूल + य, n.<BR> 1. Suitability, Yājñ. 1, 74.<BR> 2. Compliance with (gen.), Rājat. 5, 132.<BR> 3. Favour, Kathās. 19, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व|आनुपूर्वं|आनुपूर्व्व
आनुपूर्व आनुपूर्व, i. e. अनुपूर्व + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a " target="_blank">Page0079-a + 39</a>]<BR> I. n. Regular succession, order, Man. 2, 41.<BR> II. f. र्वी, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्य|आनुपूर्व्यं
आनुपूर्व्य आनुपूर्व्य, i. e. अनुपूर्व + य, n. and fem. वी, Regular succession, order, Man. 9, 149; Rām. 3, 70, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्य
आनुलोम्य आनुलोम्य, i. e. अनु-लोम + य, n. Direct or natural order, Man. 10, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुवेश्य|आनुवेश्यः
आनुवेश्य आनुवेश्य, i. e. अनु-वेश + य, m. A neighbour who lives next but one, Man. 8, 392.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषक्
आनुषक् आनुषक्, i. e. अनु-सङ्ज्, adv. Continually, Lass. 98, 7 = Rigv. v. 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषङ्गिक|आनुषंगिक
आनुषङ्गिक आनुषङ्गिक, i. e. अनु-षङ्ग + इक, adj. Connected, adherent, accustomed to live (there), Pañc. 10, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूप|आनूपः
आनूप आनूप, i. e. अनूप + अ.<BR> I. adj. Watery, marshy.<BR> II. m. Any animal frequenting marshy places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्य|आनृण्यं
आनृण्य आनृण्य, i. e. अन्-ऋण + य, n. Freedom from debt; acc. with गम्, to pay, Man. 4, 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्यता
आनृण्यता आनृण्य + ता, f. Freedom from debt, Rām. 2, 24, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस्य|आनृशंस्यं
आनृशंस्य आनृशंस्य, i. e. अ-नृशंस + य, n. Mildness, Man. 8, 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर|आंतर
आन्तर आन्तर, i. e. अन्तर + अ, m. A subject, MBh. 12, 3346; 3913.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरिक्ष|आंतरिक्ष
आन्तरिक्ष आन्तरिक्ष and आन्तरीक्ष आन्तरीक्ष, i. e. अन्तरी̆क्ष + अ, adj. Proceeding from the air or sky; airy, MBh. 2, 1636; Rām. 2, 25, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलन|आंदोलनं|आन्दोलनं
आन्दोलन आन्दोलन = अन्दोलन, n. A swinging motion, Caurap. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्य|आंध्यं
आन्ध्य आन्ध्य, i. e. अन्ध + य, n. Blindness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वाहिक
आन्वाहिक आन्वाहिक, i. e. अन्वहम् + इक, adj., f. की, Daily, Man. 3, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्
आप् आप्, i. 1 and 10; ii. 5, आप्नु, Par. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-b " target="_blank">Page0079-b + 44</a>] (in ved. and epic writings also Ātm., MBh. 14, 597. Originally also ăप्; cf. the ved. desiderative अप् + स; Lat. ăpiscor, ops, opto, cœpi, copia; πρέπειν i. e. originally προ-έπειν).<BR> 1. To attain, Ragh. 8, 24.<BR> 2. To incur, Man. 8, 188.<BR> 3. To obtain, Man. 1, 63.<BR> आप्त (cf. Lat. aptus).<BR> 1. Fit, Ragh. 3, 12.<BR> 2. Trusted, Man. 7, 80; just, 8, 63.<BR> 3. Near, Man. 5, 101; a friend, ib. 8, 64.<BR> 4. Large, Man. 7, 79.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Desid. ईप्स, To desire to obtain, MBh. 1, 1090.<BR> ईप्सित.<BR> 1. Desired, Nal. 3, 2.<BR> 2. Loved, Nal. 1, 4.<BR> 3. Ordained, Man. 2, 48. n. A wish, Kathās. 22, 170.<BR> --Comp.<BR> यथा-ईप्सित, adj. as desired, Sund. 4, 5; acc. तम्, adv. 1. According to one's wish. 2. Willingly. 3. Independently.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, desid. To desire, Man. 5, 136; with infin., Chr. 11, 14.<BR> --With अव अव.<BR> 1. To attain, Kathās. 1, 27.<BR> 2. To meet, Kathās. 3, 46.<BR> 3. To obtain, Vikr. d. 105.<BR> अन्-अवाप्त, adj. Not obtained, Man. 9, 209.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव, To recover, Śiś. 5, 40.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव.<BR> 1. To meet, Rām. 4, 44, 71.<BR> 2. To incur, Chr. 23, 20.<BR> 3. To obtain, Rām. 3, 55, 40.<BR> --With परि परि, To cease, MBh. 15, 1073.<BR> पर्याप्त.<BR> 1. Adequate, Bhag. 1, 10.<BR> 2. Sufficient, Man. 11, 7.<BR> 3. Enough (no more), Chr. 42, 13.<BR> 4. Full, Kumāras. 7, 26.<BR> 5. Many, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 10.<BR> 6. Large, Man. 3, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-पर्याप्त, adj. inadequate; with infin., Rām. 3, 51, 7.<BR> अति-, adj. excessive, Ragh. 15, 18.<BR> सु-, adj. well finished, Man. 7, 76.<BR> अ-पर्याप्तवन्त्, adj. unable, Ragh. 16, 28.<BR> --Desid.<BR> 1. To demand, Man. 8, 161.<BR> 2. To desire, MBh. 1, 5515; Ātm., MBh. 2, 563.<BR> 3. To take care, MBh. 3, 17327.<BR> 4. To defend, MBh. 4, 480.<BR> --With प्र प्र.<BR> 1. To reach, Rām. 3, 22, 37. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-a " target="_blank">Page0080-a + 43</a>] attain, Rājat. 5, 57.<BR> 2. To meet, Pañc. i. d. 328.<BR> 3. To incur, Man. 8, 355.<BR> 4. To obtain, Man. 3, 277.<BR> 5. To get in, Man. 11, 263.<BR> 6. To find, Yājñ. 3, 142; Rājat. 5, 406.<BR> प्राप्त.<BR> 1. Proper, right, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 4.<BR> 2. Having obtained, Man. 7, 2.<BR> अस्तं प्राप्त, Dead, Kathās. 13, 74.<BR> 3. Having arrived, Nal. 23, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-प्राप्त, adj. 1. not finished, pending, Yājñ. 2, 243. 2. not of age, Man. 9, 88. 3. not obtained, Bhāṣāp. 114.<BR> क्रम-, adj. obtained by succession, Nal. 12, 49.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --ptcple. of the fut. pass., दुष्प्राप्य, i. e. दुस्-प्राप्य, adj. difficult to be attained, Rām. 4, 17, 44.<BR> --Caus. प्रापय.<BR> 1. To bring, Rām. 4, 62, 19.<BR> 2. To cause to obtain, MBh. 2, 171.<BR> 3. To appoint, Rājat. 5, 424.<BR> 4. To give, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 15.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र.<BR> 1. To recover, Rām. 1, 1, 80.<BR> 2. To find, Chr. 70, 54.<BR> 3. To incur, Chr. 54, 11.<BR> 4. To imitate, Ragh. 4, 22.<BR> 5. To arrive, Rām. 3, 75, 2.<BR> अनुप्राप्त, Having attained, MBh. 1, 5874; come, Rām. 3, 27, 9.<BR> --With समनुप्र सम्-अनु-प्र.<BR> 1. To attain, Rām. 2, 52, 76.<BR> 2. To obtain, MBh. 2, 1616.<BR> समनुप्राप्त, Having attained, Rām. 3, 30, 1.<BR> --With उपप्र उप-प्र, To come near, Rām. 3, 75, 17 (the ptcple. of the pf. pass. in active signification).<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र.<BR> 1. To attain, Rām. 6, 109, 1.<BR> 2. To obtain, Man. 12, 74.<BR> संप्राप्त, Having arrived, Man. 3, 99.<BR> अ-संप्राप्य, Without touching, Chr. 40, 17.<BR> --With अनुसंप्र अनु-सम्-प्र, To attain, Rām. 3, 68, 7.<BR> अनुसंप्राप्त, Having arrived, Rām. 2, 65, 11.<BR> --With अभिसंप्र अभि-सम्-प्र.<BR> 1. To attain, Rām. 2, 55, 21.<BR> 2. To obtain, Rām. 4, 3, 27.<BR> अभिसंप्राप्त, Having arrived, MBh. 3, 11366.<BR> --With उपसंप्र उप-सम्-प्र, To attain, MBh. 3, 2337. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b " target="_blank">Page0080-b + 42</a>]<BR> उपसंप्राप्त.<BR> 1. Having incurred, MBh. 1, 5188.<BR> 2. Come, MBh. 3, 14378.<BR> --With वि वि.<BR> 1. To pervade, MBh. 12, 124.<BR> 2. To occupy, Bhag. 10, 16.<BR> 3. To fill, Chr. 33, 5.<BR> व्याप्त, That which has inherent properties, e. g. smoke, as invariably accompanied by fire, Bhāṣāp. 67.<BR> व्याप्य, n. That which is invariably accompanied by something else, as smoke by fire; the sign or middle term in an inference.<BR> --Absol. अ-व्याप्य, Not having pervaded, Bhāṣāp. 26.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To obtain, Rām. 3, 2, 28.<BR> समाप्त, Finished, Rām. 3, 49, 27.<BR> --Caus. To finish, Man. 8, 420.<BR> --Desid. To desire, Rām. 3, 5, 22.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, To bring to a full conclusion, Bhag. 4, 33.<BR> परि-समाप्त, Sufficient, Śāk. d. 105.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. uobjan, and see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अन्-आप्त अन्-आप्त, unapt, Man. 8, 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप आप, m. One of the eight deities, called Vasus, MBh. 3, 14208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा आपगा, i. e. अप् + अ-ग (vb. गम्), f.<BR> 1. A river, Rājat. 5, 140.<BR> 2. The name of a river, MBh. 3, 6038.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापगा
सुर- + आपगा सुर- + आपगा, f. the Ganges, Kir. 5, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगेय|आपगेयः
आपगेय आपगेय, i. e. आपगा + एय, patronym. m. The son of a river, a surname of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 2, 1340, and Bhīṣma, Chr. 15, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपण|आपणः
आपण आ-पण् + अ, m. A market, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरापण|अन्तरापणः
अन्तर्- + आपण अन्तर्- + आपण, m., the interior part of a market, Rām. 1, 5, 8 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतन|आपतनं
आपतन आ-पत् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Happening.<BR> 2. Appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्ति|आपत्तिः
आपत्ति आपत्ति, i. e. आ-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Undergoing, obtaining.<BR> 2. Misfortune, Lass. 30, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापत्ति|अर्थापत्तिः
अर्थ- + आपत्ति अर्थ- + आपत्ति, f. presumption (the fifth प्रमाण of the Pūrva and Uttara mīmānsā), Bhāṣāp. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथी
आपथी आपथी (probably आ-पथ + ई). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a " target="_blank">Page0081-a + 39</a>] An impediment on a road(?), Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् आ-पद्, f.<BR> 1. Calamity, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 14.<BR> 2. Necessity, Man. 9, 82.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापद्
अन्- + आपद् अन्- + आपद्, f. absence of misfortune, Man. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरापद्
निस्- + आपद् निस्- + आपद्,<BR> I. f. absence of misfortune, MBh. 12, 9671.<BR> II. adj. free from calamity, Ragh. 1, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात आपात, i. e. आ-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Attack, Arj. 7, 10.<BR> 2. Running on, Man. 11, 9; running in, Yājñ. 3, 154.<BR> 3. Throwing down, Megh. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाततस्
आपाततस् आपात + तस्, adv. Instantly, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातिन्
आपातिन् आपातिन्, i. e. आ-पत्-इन्, adj. f. नी, Happening, Kathās. 18, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपान|आपानं
आपान आपान, i. e. आ-पा + अन, n.<BR> 1. A banquet, MBh. 1, 620.<BR> 2. A place for drinking, Rām. 1, 3, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आपीड आ-पीड् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Squeezing.<BR> 2. A chaplet tied on the crown of the head, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलापीड
गल- + आपीड गल- + आपीड, m. strangling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजापीड|भुजापीडः
भुज- + आपीड भुज- + आपीड, m. clasping or enfolding in the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आपीडित आपीडित, i. e. आपीड + इत, adj. Adorned with chaplets, Nal. 12, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरण
आपूरण आपूरण, i. e. आ-पूर् + अन, n. Filling, Pañc. 96, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमय
आपोमय आपोमय, i. e. आपस् (plur. of अप्) + मय, adj. Consisting of water, MBh. 1, 6859.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोशान|आपोशानः
आपोशान आपोशान, i. e. अपो ऽशान + अ, n. The name of a prayer beginning with the words अपो ऽशान, Yājñ. 1, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ति|आप्तिः
आप्ति आप् + ति, f. Acquisition, Pañc. ii. d. 49.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्ति|अनाप्तिः
अन्- + आप्ति अन्- + आप्ति, f. non-effecting of a purpose, Man. 9, 290.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन आ-प्याय् + अन.<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Causing corpulency.<BR> 2. Causing wellbeing.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Satisfying, Man. 3, 211.<BR> 2. Advancement, Man. 3, 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवन|आप्लवनं
आप्लवन आप्लवन, i. e. आ-प्लु + अन, n. Bathing, MBh. 1, 1814; v. r. Man. 5, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध|आबंधः|आबन्धः
आबन्ध आ-बन्ध् + अ, m. A tie or bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्धन|आबंधनं
आबन्धन आ-बन्ध् + अन, n. Girding round, Rām. 2, 23, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाध|आबाधः
आबाध आ-बाध् + अ, m. Injury, Man. 4, 51.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाबाध
अन्- + आबाध अन्- + आबाध, adj. unobstructed, Rām. 3, 44, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराबाध|दुराबाधः
दुस्- + आबाध दुस्- + आबाध, adj. irresistible, MBh. 13, 724.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराबाध|निराबाधः
निस्- + आबाध निस्- + आबाध, adj. 1. unmolested, Hiḍ. 4, 12. 2. not injuring, Hariv. 11811.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्दिक
आब्दिक आब्दिक, i. e. अब्द + इक, adj. Yearly, Man. 7, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्त्रिंशदाब्दिक
षष्-त्रिंशत्- + आब्दिक षष्-त्रिंशत्- + आब्दिक, adj. lasting thirty-six years, Man. 3, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरण|आभरणं
आभरण आभरण, i. e. आ-भृ + अन, n. Ornaments, as jewels, etc., Rām. 3, 55, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्ताभरण
तप्त- + आभरण तप्त- + आभरण, n. an ornament made of refined gold, Rām. 3, 58, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा आ-भा, f.<BR> 1. Splendour, light, Pañc. iv. d. 58.<BR> 2. When latter part of a compound adj., often Like; e. g. Rām. 3, 55, 28, गिरि-शृङ्ग-आभ, Like the peak of a mountain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राभ|वज्राभः
वज्र- + आभ वज्र- + आभ,<BR> I. adj. like a diamond.<BR> II. m. a precious opal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष|आभाषः
आभाष आ-भाष् + अ, m., and आभाषण आभाषण, i. e. आ-भाष् + अन n. Addressing, speaking to, Rām. 3, 26, 12; Rājat. 5, 462.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् आ-भास्, f. Light, MBh. 3, 10980.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास|आभासः
आभास आ-भास् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Splendour, Rām. 6, 77, 17.<BR> 2. Light, Vedāntas. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a " target="_blank">Page0082-a + 41</a>] in Chr. 219, 11.<BR> 3. Appearance, Kathās. 12, 16.<BR> 4. Semblance, Bhāṣāp. 70.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाभास|रसाभासः
रस- + आभास रस- + आभास, m. the semblance of sentiment, as e. g., a sentiment attributed to an irrational animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वाभास|हेत्वाभासः
हेतु- + आभास हेतु- + आभास, m. fallacious reason or middle term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्य|आभिजात्यं
आभिजात्य आभिजात्य, i. e. अभि-जात (vb. जन्) + य, n. Nobility, Rām. 2, 35, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्य|आभिमुख्यं
आभिमुख्य आभिमुख्य, i. e. अभि-मुख + य, n. Front, direction towards, Pañc. i. d. 370 (with या, to attack).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिषेचनिक
आभिषेचनिक आभिषेचनिक, i. e. अभिषेचन + इक, adj., f. की, Referring or serving to the inauguration of a king, Rām. 6, 112, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीर|आभीरः
आभीर आभीर, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1192.<BR> 2. The offspring of a Brāhmaṇa by an Ambaṣṭha woman, Man. 10, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील आ-भी + ल, adj. Terrible, MBh. 3, 388.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू आ-भू, adj. Helping, Chr. 290, 1, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 1; 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोग|आभोगः
आभोग आभोग, i. e. आ-भुज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Crookedness, MBh. 3, 9957; vault, Rām. 2, 65, 3; roundness, Megh. 89.<BR> 2. Fullness, plenty, Śāk. 8, 1.<BR> 3. The expanded hood of the Cobra capella, MBh. 16, 118.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाभोग|स्तनाभोगः
स्तन- + आभोग स्तन- + आभोग, m. a man with a breast like a woman's.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यन्तर|आभ्यंतर|आभ्यन्तरः
आभ्यन्तर आभ्यन्तर, i. e. अभ्यन्तर + अ, adj. Interior, MBh. 2, 202.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाभ्यन्तर|गणाभ्यंतर|गणाभ्यन्तरः
गण- + आभ्यन्तर गण- + आभ्यन्तर, m. the member of a corporation, MBh. 3, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक आभ्यासिक (with स् for श्), i. e. अभ्याश + इक, adj. Standing near together, MBh. 1, 7577.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
ऽआभ्युदयिक -आभ्युदयिक, i. e. अभ्युदय + इक, adj. Causing prosperity, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b " target="_blank">Page0082-b + 41</a>] increase, Man. 12, 88.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभ्युदयिक
अन्- + आभ्युदयिक अन्- + आभ्युदयिक, Not causing prosperity, Mṛcch. 111, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्
आम् आम्, A particle of reminiscence: Ah! Vikr. 38, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम आम, i. e. अम् + अ, adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Raw, undressed, Man. 4, 223.<BR> 2. Unbaked (as a pot), Pañc. iii. d. 13.<BR> --Cf. ὠμός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रण|आमंत्रणं|आमन्त्रणं
आमन्त्रण आमन्त्रण, i. e. आ-मन्त्र् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Calling, addressing.<BR> 2. Invitation, Pañc. 34, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमय|आमयं|आमयः
आमय आमय, i. e. अम्, Caus. + अ (anomal.), m. Sickness, Rājat. 5, 209.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अन्- + आमय अन्- + आमय,<BR> I. adj. 1. healthy, Draup. 4, 10. 2. being in a good condition, Rām. 2, 72, 52. 3. unharmed, Rām. 1, 44, 58.<BR> II. n. health, Śāk. 64, 23; wellbeing, Rām. 2, 89, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामय|निरामयः
निस्- + आमय निस्- + आमय,<BR> I. adj. 1. healthy, Indr. 3, 8. 2. full, Hariv. 3639. 3. pure, Rām. 1, 62, 18.<BR> II. n. health, Rām. 1, 41, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामय
स- + आमय स- + आमय, adj. sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयावित्व
आमयावित्व आमयावित्व, i. e. आमयाविन् + त्व, n. Dyspepsia, Man. 11, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन् आमयाविन्, i. e. आमय + विन्, adj., f. नी, Subject to dyspepsia, Man. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्त|आमरणांत
आमरणान्त आमरणान्त, i. e. आ-मरण-अन्त, adj. Lasting till death, Hit. i. d. 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्तिक|आमरणांतिक
आमरणान्तिक आमरणान्तिक, i. e. आमरणान्त + इक, adj. Lasting till death, Man. 9, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्द|आमर्दः
आमर्द आमर्द, i. e. आ-मृद् + अ, m. Pulling (as of hair), Śāk. d. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दिन्|आमर्द्दिन्
आमर्दिन् आमर्दिन्, i. e. आ-मृद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Destroying, Rām. 4, 14, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्ष|आमर्षः
आमर्ष आमर्ष = अ-मर्ष in निस्-आमर्ष, = निस्-अमर्ष, Devoid of energy, Rām. 2, 10, 14 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलक|आमलकं|आमलकः
आमलक आमलक, m., f. की, and n. Emblic myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष|आमिषं
आमिष आमिष, m. and n. Flesh, Pañc. i. d. 449.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गामिष
खड्ग- + आमिष खड्ग- + आमिष, n. the flesh of a rhinoceros, Man. 3, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामिष
निस्- + आमिष निस्- + आमिष, adj. 1. fleshless, Bhartṛ. 2, 9. 2. free of covetousness, Man. 6, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषता
आमिषता आमिष + ता, f. and आमिषत्व आमिष + त्व, n. Being an object of covetousness, Ragh. 12, 11; Daśak. 194, 6 Wils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुख|आमुखं
आमुख आ-मुख, n. Prelude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्मिक
आमुष्मिक आमुष्मिक, i. e. अमुष्मिन्, loc. sing. of अदस्, + इक, adj., f. की, Belonging to the next life, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोक्षण
आमोक्षण आमोक्षण, i. e. आ-मोक्ष् + अन (v. r.), n. Binding on, Rām. 2, 23, 39, Schl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचन|आमोचनं
आमोचन आमोचन, i. e. आ-मुच् + अन, n. Binding on, Rām. 2, 20, 43 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद आमोद, i. e. आ-मुद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Pleasure, Kir. 5, 26.<BR> 2. A fragrancy, strong smell, Ṛt. 6, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद
स- + आमोद स- + आमोद, adj. fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
ऽआमोदिन् -आमोदिन्, i. e. आ-मुद् + इन्, adj. Smelling, Rājat. 5, 357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नाय|आम्नायः
आम्नाय आम्नाय, i. e. आ-म्ना + अ, m.<BR> 1. Holy tradition, Man. 7, 80.<BR> 2. A Veda, Daśak. 140, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराम्नाय
दुस्- + आम्नाय दुस्- + आम्नाय, adj. hard to be transmitted, MBh. 14, 1441.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भस|आंभस
आम्भस आम्भस, i. e. अम्भस् + अ, adj. Full of water, Matsyop. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्र|आम्रः
आम्र आम्र, m. The mango tree, Mangifera indica, Nal. 12, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्र|राजाम्रः
राजाम्र राजाम्र, i. e. राजन्-, m. a superior sort of mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रात|आम्रातः
आम्रात आम्रात (derived from the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b " target="_blank">Page0083-b + 41</a>] last), and आम्रातक आम्रात + क, m. The hog-plum, Spondias mangifera, Rām. 3, 17, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आय|आयः
आय आय, i. e. आ-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Gain, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 219.<BR> 2. Revenue, Man. 8, 419.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतन|आयतनं
आयतन आयतन, i. e. आ-यत् + अन n.<BR> 1. A place, Cāṇ. 32.<BR> 2. A seat, Man. 6, 77; Pañc. 32, 23.<BR> 3. An outhouse, Yājñ. 2, 154.<BR> 4. An altar, Pañc. 199, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायतन|देवायतनं
देव- + आयतन देव- + आयतन and देवता-, n. a temple, Man. 4, 46; 8, 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयति|आयतिः
आयति आयति, i. e. आ-यम् + ति, and, on account of the metre, f. ती, Rām. 3, 44, 11.<BR> 1. Dignity, Kathās. 24, 119; Rājat. 5, 189.<BR> 2. Future time, Man. 4, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तता
आयत्तता आ-यत्त + ता (vb. यत्) f., Dependence, Dev. 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस आयस, i. e. अयस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी, Of iron, Man. 8, 315;<BR> II. n. Iron, Yājñ. 1, 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाग|आयागः
आयाग आयाग, i. e. आ-यज् + अ, m. A sacrificial gift, Rām. 1, 33, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयान|आयानं
आयान आयान, i. e. आ-या + अन, n. Coming near, MBh. 3, 11029 (p. 570).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाम|आयामः
आयाम आयाम, i. e. आ-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Stopping, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 14.<BR> 2. Oppression, Rājat. 5, 165 (perhaps is to be read आयास, q. cf.).<BR> 3. Length, Rām. 1, 40, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामवन्त्|आयामवत्
आयामवन्त् आयाम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, and आयामिन् आयामिन्, i. e. आयाम + इन्, adj., f. नी, Long, Vikr. d. 4; Daśak. in Chr. 200, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयास|आयासः
आयास आयास, i. e. आ-यस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Effort, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 997.<BR> 2. Fatigue, Rām. 3, 55, 17.<BR> 3. Trouble, Śāk. d. 37.<BR> 4. Oppression, Rājat. 5, 174 (Chr. 261, 191, read आयासो).<BR> 5. Weariness, Rām. 6, 7, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अन्- + आयास अन्- + आयास, adj. easy, Śāk. 22, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासक
आयासक आयासक, i. e. आ-यस् Caus. + अक, adj., f. इका, Causing fatigue, Bhartṛ. 3, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आयासिन् आयासिन्, i. e. आयास + इन्, adj., f. नी, Endeavouring, Śāk. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुःशेषता
आयुःशेषता आयुःशेषता, i. e. आयुस्-शेष + ता, f. Condition of having saved only the life, Pañc. 127, 3 (I came off scarcely alive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध|आयुधं|आयुधः
आयुध आ-युध् + अ, n., A weapon, Man. 7, 93.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रायुध|इन्द्रायुधं|इन्द्रायुधः
इन्द्र- + आयुध इन्द्र- + आयुध n. the rainbow, Man. 4, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रायुध
स-इन्द्र- + आयुध स-इन्द्र- + आयुध, adj. with a rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदायुध
उद्- + आयुध उद्- + आयुध, adj. with raised weapons, Chr. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमायुध|कुसुमायुधः
कुसुम- + आयुध कुसुम- + आयुध, m. the god of love, Ṛt. 6, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रायुध|चक्रायुधः
चक्र- + आयुध चक्र- + आयुध, m. a name of Viṣṇu, Rām. 6, 102, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशायुध|त्रिदशायुधं
त्रिदश- + आयुध त्रिदश- + आयुध, n. the rainbow, Ragh. 9, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायुध
निस्- + आयुध निस्- + आयुध, adj., f. धा, disarmed, Man. 7, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुध
स- + आयुध स- + आयुध, adj. armed, Pañc. 44, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलायुध|हलायुधः
हल- + आयुध हल- + आयुध, m. Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक आयुधिक, i. e. आयुध + इक, and आयुधिन् आयुधिन्, i. e. आयुध + इन्, m. A warrior, MBh. 16, 212; Rām. 2, 53, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधीय आयुधीय, i. e. आयुध + ईय, adj. Military, Man. 7, 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदमय
आयुर्वेदमय आयुर्वेदमय, i. e. अयुस्-वेद + मय, adj. Containing the Ayurveda (see वेद), Rām. 1, 45, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष|आयुषं
ऽआयुष -आयुष, i. e. आयुस् + अ, A substitute for आयुस् when latter part of compound words: e. g. चिर-, adj. Long living, Pañc. 245, 35; पुरुष-, n. The duration of a man's life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्काम
आयुष्काम आयुष्काम, i. e. आयुस्-कम् + अ, adj. Desirous of long life, Man. 9, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्मन्त्|आयुष्मत्
आयुष्मन्त् आयुष्मन्त्, i. e. आयुस् + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Long-lived, Man. 2, 152. Used in dramas as an honorific address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य आयुष्य, i. e. आयुस् + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या, Procuring long life, Man. 1, 106.<BR> II. n. Long life, Man. 2, 52.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुष्य
अन्- + आयुष्य अन्- + आयुष्य, adj. prejudicial to long life, Man. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस् आयुस्, n. Life, Man. 1, 84.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. αἰές, αἰεί, αἰών; Lat. aevum; Goth. aivs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पायुस्
अल्प- + आयुस् अल्प- + आयुस्, adj. short-lived, Man. 4, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणायुस्
क्षीण- + आयुस् क्षीण- + आयुस् (vb. क्षि), adj. lifeless, Sāv. 2, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतायुस्
गत- + आयुस् गत- + आयुस्, adj. 1. lifeless, Pañc. 101, 23. 2. whose life is forfeited, Rām. 6, 1, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुस्
दीर्घ- + आयुस् दीर्घ- + आयुस्, adj. 1. long. lived, Rām. 1, 6, 18. 2. wished to be long-lived, Rām. 3, 1, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितायुस्
परि-मित- + आयुस् परि-मित- + आयुस् (vb. मा), adj. short-lived, Rām. 3, 55, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतायुस्
शत- + आयुस् शत- + आयुस्, m. a man a hundred years old, Lass. 32, 18; an old man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोग|आयोगः
आयोग आयोग, i. e. आ-युज् + अ, m. Presenting with flowers, perfumes, Rām. 5, 17, 15 (भ्रमर-, A present of flowers made to the bees).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगव|आयोगवः
आयोगव आयोगव, m., f. वी, Offspring of a Śūdra by a Vaiśya woman, Man. 10, 12; 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधन|आयोधनं
आयोधन आयोधन, i. e. आ-युध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Battle, Ragh. 5, 71.<BR> 2. A field of battle, Draup. 8, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष आ-रक्ष् + अ, m. Guard, protection, Man. 3, 204; Rām. 5, 75, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षक|आरक्षकः
आरक्षक आ-रक्ष् + अक, and आरक्षिक आरक्षिक, i. e. आ-रक्ष + इक(?), m. A policeman, Pañc. 129, 5; Daśak. in Chr. 195, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्ट|आरट्टः
आरट्ट आरट्ट (a dialectical change of आ̆-राष्ट्र), m. pl. The name of a people and country, MBh. 8, 2056.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्टज|आरट्टजः
आरट्टज आरट्ट-ज (vb. जन्), adj. Born in Āraṭṭa, Rām. 5, 12, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण|आरणं
आरण आरण, An abyss, Chr. 296, 6 = Rigv. i. 112, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य आरण्य, i. e. अरण्य + अ, adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Living in forests, MBh. 1, 3637.<BR> 2. Growing in forests, MBh. 1, 6658; wild, Man. 10, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक आरण्य + क,<BR> I. adj. Referring to forests, MBh. 15, 532; produced in forests, Rām. 2, 36, 6.<BR> II. m. An anchorite, Śāk. d. 46.<BR> III. n. The name of a book, Man. 4, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्धि|आरब्धिः
आरब्धि आरब्धि, i. e. आ-रभ् + ति, f. An enterprise, Rājat. 5, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भ|आरंभः|आरम्भः
आरम्भ आरम्भ, i. e. आ-रभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A beginning, Megh. 37.<BR> 2. Exertion, effort, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 22.<BR> 3. An enterprise, Rām. 4, 30, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रारम्भ|चित्रारंभ|चित्रारम्भः
