इज्या
इज्या इज्या, i. e. यज् + या, f. Sacrifice, Man. 1, 89.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेज्य
भूत-इज्य भूत-इज्य, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a " target="_blank">Page0099-a + 43</a>] one who makes oblations to the Bhūtas, Bhag. 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्
इट् इट्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा इडा (akin to ईड्), f.<BR> 1. Refreshment, ved. Chr. 288, 16 = Rigv. i. 48, 16 (written इऌअ).<BR> 2. Oblations to the deities, MBh. 2, 1304.<BR> 3. Speech, Hariv. 14036.<BR> 4. Earth, MBh. 3, 14750.<BR> 5. The wife of Budha, MBh. 1, 3141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर इ-तर (from the pronominal base इ, see इदम्), adj., f. रा, n. रद् (ved. रम्, cf. Lat. iterum),<BR> 1. Other, Man. 1, 70; इतर-इतरैर् अथ वा इतरैः, By these or those, MBh. 2, 2503.<BR> 2. Contrary, e. g. विजयाय इतराय वा, To victory or defeat, MBh. 1, 4092.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --When the latter part of a comp. word it signifies,<BR> I. negation of the former part, e. g. द्विज-, m. one who is not a Brāhmaṇa, Ragh. 9, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतर|इतरेतरं
इतर-इतर इतर-इतर, adj., used generally only in the oblique cases of the sing., 1. mutual, with each another, Pañc. ii. d. 136. 2. several Man. 3, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेतर|नरेतरः
नर- + इतर नर- + इतर, m. 1. a superhuman being, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 9. 2. an animal, 3, 13, 49.<BR> II. the contrary, e. g. दक्षिण-, adj. left, Kumāras. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषेतर
परुष- + इतर परुष- + इतर, adj. mild, Ragh. 5, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्येतर
सभ्य- + इतर सभ्य- + इतर, adj. vulgar, Bhartṛ. 3, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येतर
सव्य- + इतर सव्य- + इतर, adj. right, Ragh. 12, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजेतर
सहज- + इतर सहज- + इतर, adj. not innate, accidental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितेतर|सितेतरः
सित- + इतर सित- + इतर, adj. black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरतस्
इतरतस् इतर + तस्, adv., Repeated; इतरतश् चेतरतः, Hither and thither, Rām. 2, 105, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरथा
इतरथा इतर + था, adv. Else, Śiś. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतरतस्
इतरेतरतस् इतरेतरतस्, i. e. इतर-इतर + तस्, adv. One from the other. MBh. 1, 7403.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस् इ + तस् (from the pronominal base इ, see इदम्),<BR> I. = the abl. of इदम्, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 2 (from this person, i. e. from myself); Hiḍ. 1, 5, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-b " target="_blank">Page0099-b + 45</a>] than this, i. e. than<BR> I.<BR> II. adv.<BR> 1. From hence, from this place, Rām. 3, 54, 28; from this time, MBh. 3, 204; therefore, Rām. 5, 81, 45.<BR> 2. Hither, Rām. 5, 13, 9; Ragh. 2, 34, against myself.<BR> 3. इतस्-इतस्, Here--there, Śāk. 29, 20; इतश्चेतश् च, Here and there, Pañc. 20, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति इति (probably a case of an original इ + त्य, see इदम्), adv.<BR> 1. Thus, Man. 2, 237.<BR> 2. It is used in quoting words or thoughts of one's self or some other: Man. 2, 129, तां ब्रूयाद् भवतीति, He may address her thus (i. e. by the word), भवति; Chr. 4, 15, अवोचम्...भीष्मः शान्तनवः कन्या करतीति, I spoke thus: ‘Bhīṣma the son of Śāntanu robs the girls,’ i. e.<BR> I. rob, etc.; Nal. 16, 9, तर्कयाम् आस भैमीति, he thought thus: ‘she is the daughter of Bhīma’; Nal. 20, 14, न हि जानामि भवेद् एवं न वेति, I do not know (thus): may it be so or not, i. e. I do not know if it be thus or not. Generally words expressing ‘to say,’ or ‘to think,’ are wanting, e. g. Pañc. 68, 25, अकुतो पि भयम् इति, ‘There is no danger from any quarter’ thus (thinking); Nal. 14, 14, न त्वां विद्युर् जना इति, ‘People will not know thee’ thus (thinking). Sometimes is added कृत्वा or ह, e. g. MBh. 1, 1522, सखेति कृत्वा, Thinking you are my friend, Man. 9, 45.<BR> 3. It often follows a question without expressing a distinct meaning, e. g. Hit. 53, 18.<BR> 4. It is used to denote the conclusion of a book or chapter, Rām. 1, end.<BR> 5. With preceding किम्, Why, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्तव्यता|इतिकर्त्तव्यता
इतिकर्तव्यता इति-कर्तव्य + ता, इति-कार्यता इति-कार्य + ता, and इतिकृत्यता इति-कृत्य + ता (vb. कृ), f. Business, Sāv. 3, 7; MBh. 3, 10031; 1, 7929.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहास|इतिहासः
इतिहास इतिहास, i. e. इति-ह-आस (the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a " target="_blank">Page0100-a + 41</a>] last part is the third sing. of the pf. of 1. अस्) m. Traditional account, a legend, Man. 3, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्
इत्थम् इत्थम्, i. e. इद् + थम्, adv. Thus, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्था
इत्था इत्था, i. e. इद् + था, adv. Thus, Chr. 295, 17 = Rigv. 1, 92, 17.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् इ + द् (properly the acc. n. of the pronominal base इ = Lat. id; Goth. ita; O.H.G. iz), a ved. part. laying a stress upon the preceding word, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् इ + द्-अम्, pron. sbst. and adj. The bases of the declension are अ m. and n., आ f., इ n. ई f., इ-म m. and n. इ-मा f., अ-न m. and n. अ-ना f., and ए-न m. and n. ए-ना f. This, Man. 2, 163; Nal. 7, 17 (16). Combined with other pronouns it may be translated Here, e. g. with the first psn., Chr. 24, 44, अयं गच्छामि, Here I go; with तद्, Rām. 5, 13, 31; with यद्, Hiḍ. 3, 19; with किम्, Hit. 18, 11.<BR> --Cf. Lat. is, ea, id; Goth. is, ita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीम्
इदानीम् इदानीम्, i. e. इ + दा + न + ई + म् (इदा ved., and, properly then, cf. ἰδέ), adv.<BR> 1. Now, Ṛt. 6, 29.<BR> 2. Presently, Śāk. 94, 2.<BR> --Cf. Lat. idoneus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म इध्म, i. e. इन्ध् + म, m. Fuel, Rām. 3, 21, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्|इंद्
† इन्द् इन्द्, i. 1, Par. To have supreme power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवर|इंदीवर|इंदीवरं|इन्दीवरं
इन्दीवर इन्दीवर, n. and. m. The blue lotus, Nymphæa cærulea, Indr. 1, 8; Daśak. in Chr. 199, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दु|इंदुः|इन्दुः
इन्दु इन्दु, m. The moon, Rām. 3, 50, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबालेन्दु
अ-बाल- + इन्दु अ-बाल- + इन्दु, m. the full moon, Ragh. 6, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनेन्दु
वदन- + इन्दु वदन- + इन्दु, m. a moon-like face, Śiś. 9, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्र|इंद्रः|इन्द्रः
इन्द्र इन्द्र, m.<BR> 1. The name of a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b " target="_blank">Page0100-b + 45</a>] deity, originally the supreme go of the Hindus. Rām. 1, 1, 83.<BR> 2. First, a king, especially as latter part of comp. words, e. g. खग-, m. The king of the birds, Pañc. i. d. 356; गज-, m. A huge elephant, Nal. 12, 54 (40); जन-, m. A king (of the people), Rām. 2, 100, 14.<BR> तृण-, m. The palmyra tree, MBh. 13, 6861.<BR> देव-, m. Indra, Arj. 4, 5.<BR> नग-, m. The Himālaya, Ragh. 2, 28.<BR> नर-, m.<BR> 1. A king, Man. 9, 253.<BR> 2. A physician, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 12.<BR> महा-, m.<BR> 1. Indra.<BR> 2. A range of mountains, the northern part of the Ghats.<BR> मृग-, m. A lion.<BR> यक्ष-, m. Kuvera, the god of wealth.<BR> राक्षस-, m. Rāvaṇa, the king of the Rākṣasas, or demons, Rām. 3, 55, 35.<BR> राजेन्द्र, i. e. राजन्-, m. An emperor, a powerful king, Chr. 41, 5.<BR> सुर-, m. Indra, Bhartṛ. 2, 11.<BR> स-, adj. With Indra, Rām. 3, 51, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकोषक|इन्द्रकोषकः
इन्द्रकोषक इन्द्र-कोष + क, m. A projection of the roof of a house forming a kind of balcony, Rām. 5, 9, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी इन्द्राणी, i. e. इन्द्र + ई, f. The wife of Indra, MBh. 1, 7351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय इन्द्रिय, i. e. इन्द्र + इय, n.<BR> 1. Power, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 83, 2.<BR> 2. Semen virile, Man. 4, 220.<BR> 3. An organ of sense, Man. 1, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिन्द्रिय|अन्तरिंद्रिय
अन्तर्- + इन्द्रिय अन्तर्- + इन्द्रिय, n. the internal sense, i. e. the faculty of thinking. Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मेन्द्रिय|कर्मेंद्रिय|कर्म्मेन्द्रिय|कर्म्मेन्द्रियं
कर्मेन्द्रिय कर्मेन्द्रिय, i. e. कर्मन्-, n. an organ of action, e. g. the hand, foot, etc., Man. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रिय|जितेंद्रिय|जितेन्द्रियः
जित- + इन्द्रिय जित- + इन्द्रिय, adj. one who has subdued his senses, Rām. 3, 49, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिन्द्रिय|निरिंद्रिय|निरिन्द्रियः
निस्- + इन्द्रिय निस्- + इन्द्रिय, adj., f. या, 1. having lost the use of a limb, Man. 9, 201. 2. powerless, Man. 9, 18 (? see Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धीन्द्रिय|बुद्धींद्रिय|बुद्धीन्द्रियं
बुद्धि- + इन्द्रिय बुद्धि- + इन्द्रिय (or ज्ङान-), n. an organ of perception and intellect, as the mind, eye, ear, etc., Man. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रिय
स- + इन्द्रिय स- + इन्द्रिय, adj. with the organs of sense, Man. 1, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध्|इंध्
इन्ध् इन्ध्, ii. 7, Ātm., pf. ईधे,<BR> 1. To kindle; pass. इध्य, MBh. 3, 10821; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a " target="_blank">Page0101-a + 41</a>] ptcple. pf. इद्ध, Man. 8, 215.<BR> 2. To shine.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, To kindle, MBh. 3, 10658.<BR> --Cf. ἰθαρός, αἴθω, αἰθήρ; Lat. aestus; O.H.G. eit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन|इंधन|इन्धनं
इन्धन इन्ध् + अन, n. Fuel, Man. 7, 118.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीन्धन|अग्नीन्धनं|अग्नीन्धनः
अग्नि- + इन्धन अग्नि- + इन्धन, n. kindling a sacrificial fire, Man. 2, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिन्धन|अबिंधनः|अबिन्धनः
अप्- + इन्धन अप्- + इन्धन, adj. having water for fuel, Ragh. 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धनवन्त्|इन्धनवत्
इन्धनवन्त् इन्धन + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessed of fuel, Rām. 5, 75, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्व्
इन्व् इन्व्, i. 1, Par. (properly इ, ii. 5 इ + नु, which form is in the Vedas the base of the pres.),<BR> 1. To pervade.<BR> 2. To please.<BR> 3. To satisfy. In the Veda especially: to further.<BR> --Cf. ἀνύω for αἰνύω, cf. γάνυμαι under जु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ इभ, m. An elephant, Rājat. 5, 315.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धेभ|गंधेभ|गन्धेभः
गन्ध- + इभ गन्ध- + इभ, m. a kind of elephant, Rājat. 1, 300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलगन्धेभ
जल-गन्ध- + इभ जल-गन्ध- + इभ, m. a kind of elephant, or a गन्धेभ (see the preceding) living in water, Rājat. 5, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगिभ|दिगिभः
दिगिभ दिगिभ, i. e. दिश्-, m. an elephant of a quarter or point of the compass, one of eight attached to the north, north-east, etc., supporting the globe, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य इभ्य-, i. e. इभ + य, adj., f. या, Wealthy, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 19.<BR> --Cf. probably ἴϕιος, ἴϕθιμος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्ता
इयत्ता इयत्ता, i. e. इयन्त् + ता, f. Quantity, Ragh. 6, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयन्त्|इयत्
इयन्त् इयन्त्, i. e. इ + वन्त्, cf. ved. ई-वन्त्, with य् for व्, adj., f. यती.<BR> 1. So much, Kathās. 4, 95.<BR> 2. So large, Kathās. 12, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा इरा, f.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. The name of an Apsaras, MBh. 2, 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण|इरिणं|इरिणः
इरिण इरिण, i. e. इरा + इन् + अ, n. Barren soil, Man. 3, 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्
इल् इल्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To sleep.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-b " target="_blank">Page0101-b + 44</a>] To go, Hariv. 620.<BR> 3. † To throw; in this signification also i. 10, Par.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
ऽइव -इव, i. e. curtailed इ + वत् (see इदम्), indecl.<BR> 1. Like, Man. 2, 79.<BR> 2. In some way, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 14.<BR> 3. Almost, Nal. 17, 12.<BR> 4. Scarcely, Chr. 36, 15.<BR> 5. With न, Not very, Nal. 25, 19.<BR> 6. With किम्, Indeed, Śāk. 97, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
1. इष् इष्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To throw, ved.<BR> 2. To go.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To search, Daśak. in Chr. 192 10, (cf. 2. इष्).<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To throw, Rām. 3, 35, 46.<BR> 2. To direct, Śāk. d. 35.<BR> 3. To send, Rām. 3, 64, 7.<BR> 4. To make known, Rām. 1, 71, 17; प्रेषित, Banished, Rām. 2, 68, 8; m. A messenger, Śāk. 29, 12.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, Caus. To send after, Rām. 4, 37, 10.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To throw, Chr. 30, 7.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To send, MBh. 2, 1179.<BR> 2. To send away, Rām. 4, 56, 17.<BR> --Cf. ἴημι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
2. इष् इष्, i. 6, Par. (base of the pres. impf. imprt. and potent. इच्छ, but cf. अनु-),<BR> 1. To wish, Sāv. 5, 100; Yājñ. 1, 130.<BR> 2. To cherish, Man. 2, 159.<BR> 3. To chose, Man. 8, 384.<BR> 4. To approve, Man. 8, 366. Pass., To be fixed or determined, Bhāṣāp. 12; Yājñ. 3, 18; Man. 8, 322.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --part. of the pres. अन्-इच्छन्त्,<BR> 1. Not desiring, Rām. 5, 24, 8.<BR> 2. Unwilling, Pañc. 55, 4.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass., इष्ट, Desired, good. Nal. 1, 1. m. A lover, Śāk. d. 78.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-इष्ट, 1. disagreeable, Rām. 3, 14, 23. 2. disapproved. Man. 9, 319. 3. wicked, Hit. i. d. 5. n. evil occurrence, Kathās. 18, 86.<BR> यथा-इष्ट + म्, adv. 1. according to one's wish, Bhartṛ. 2, 81. 2. carelessly, Man. 2, 198.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. एष्टव्य (anomal.), Desirable, MBh. 3, 8075; n. wish, MBh. 14, 1600.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a " target="_blank">Page0102-a + 40</a>] the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To search, Man. 6, 84; with इष as base of the present, etc., MBh. 3, 15753.<BR> 2. To try Man. 8, 190.<BR> 3. To ask, Man. 4, 33.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass., दुस्-, Difficult to be searched through, Rām. 4, 86, 6.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To search, Pañc. 214, 19.<BR> 2. To expect, Pañc. 182, 24.<BR> --With पर्यनु परि-अनु, To search, MBh. 1, 1668.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To search through, Rām. 3, 66, 1.<BR> --With अभि अभि, अभीष्ट,<BR> 1. Desired, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 4.<BR> 2. Agreeable, Pañc. 77, 24.<BR> --With आ आ, एष्टव्य (anomal.), Desirable, MBh. 3, 8075; n. Wish, MBh. 14, 1600.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, पर्येष्टव्य (see the last), To be searched, MBh. 9, 229.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To receive, Sāv. 3, 12.<BR> 2. To obey, Rām. 1, 34, 30.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To assent, Rām. 1, 52, 13.<BR> --Cf. ἰότης, perhaps ἵμερος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
3. इष् इष्, ii. 9, इष्णा, Par.<BR> 1. † To repeat an act.<BR> 2. ved. To further, Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. i. 112, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
4. इष् इष्, f. A desirable object, comfort, Chr. 288, 15 = Rigv. i. 48, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीका
इषीका 1. इष् + ईका, f. Reed, MBh. 1, 4332.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरेषीका
शर- + इषीका शर- + इषीका, f. an arrow, Rām. 2, 104, 43, Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषु|इषुः
इषु 1. इष् + उ, m. and f. An arrow.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἰός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमेषु|कुसुमेषुः
कुसुम- + इषु कुसुम- + इषु, m. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेषु|पंचेषु|पञ्चेषुः
पञ्चेषु पञ्चेषु, i. e. पञ्चन्-, m. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पेषु|पुष्पेषुः
पुष्प- + इषु पुष्प- + इषु, m. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधि|इषुधिः
इषुधि इषुधि, i. e. इषु-धा (see निधि), m. and f. A quiver.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेषुधि
महा- + इषुधि महा- + इषुधि, a great quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका इष्टका, f. A brick, Rājat. 5, 463.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टतस्
इष्टतस् इष्ट + तस् (vb. 2. इष्), adv. According to one's wish, Rām. 1, 34, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टाकृत
इष्टाकृत इष्टाकृत, i. e. इष्ट-आ(?)-कृत, n. The name of a sacrifice, MBh. 3, 10513.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्त|इष्टापूर्तं|इष्टापूर्त्त|इष्टापूर्त्तं
इष्टापूर्त इष्टापूर्त, i. e. इष्ट-आ-पूर्त (vb. यज् and पॄ), n. Sacrifices and pious works, Rām. 1, 23, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
इष्टि इष्टि, f.<BR> I. 2. इष् + ति, Wish.<BR> II. यज् + ति,<BR> 1. Sacrificing, Chr. 296, 1 = Rigv. i. 112, 1.<BR> 2. Sacrifice. Man. 4, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातेष्टि|जातेष्टिः
जात- + इष्टि जात- + इष्टि (vb. जन्), f. a sacrifice on the birth of a child, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका इष्टिका = इष्टका, MBh. 14, 2633.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्मिन्
इष्मिन् 1. इष् + मिन्, adj. Hastening, Chr. 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 87, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वास|इष्वासं|इष्वासः
इष्वास इष्वास, i. e. इषु- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. An archer, Rām. 1, 1, 12.<BR> 2. A bow, Rām. 3, 49, 48.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेष्वास|महेष्वासः
महा- + इष्वास महा- + इष्वास, m. an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह इह, i. e. इ + ध, which appears still in the Vedas, cf. इदम्, adv.<BR> 1. In this case, Man. 5, 55.<BR> 2. Here, Man. 9, 8; in this world, Man. 3, 181.<BR> 3. Hither, Chr. 13, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहत्य
इहत्य इह + त्य, adj. Of this place, Kathās. 13, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इळा
इळा इऌआ, see इदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई ई, see इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्
ईक्ष् ईक्ष् (like अक्ष् in 1. अक्ष, a desider. of a lost vb., see अक्ष), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 15, 826).<BR> 1. To look, Kathās. 25, 148. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0103-a " target="_blank">Page0103-a + 42</a>] To behold, Śiś. 9, 61. To perceive, Bhag. 6, 29.<BR> 2. To mind, Kumāras. 5, 82; ईक्षित, n. A look, Śāk. d. 44.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To suspect, Hit. iv. d. 101 (सत्ये प्य् अपायम् अधीक्षते, Suspects injury even in truth).<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To see, Rām. 5, 42, 6.<BR> 2. To mind, Pañc. v. d. 61. To pay regard to, Kathās. 17, 12.<BR> 3. To intend, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 13.<BR> 4. To require, Bhāṣāp. 63.<BR> 5. To expect, Bhartṛ. 3, 66.<BR> अन्-अपेक्षित, adj.<BR> 1. Not minded, Man. 8, 309; unregarded, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 3.<BR> 2. Regardless, Prab. 34, 15.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप,<BR> 1. To look back, Rām. 2, 86, 22.<BR> 2. To mind, Ragh. 19, 6.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To look at, MBh. 1, 5923; Rām. 3, 50, 11 (अवेक्ष्य-अवेक्ष्य, ever pursuing with his eyes).<BR> 2. To perceive, Rām. 2, 45, 5.<BR> 3. To consider, Man. 7, 10.<BR> 4. To mind, MBh. 2, 2158; to regard, Rām. 6, 7, 48.<BR> दुस्-अवेक्षित, n. An unsuitable look, MBh. 3, 14669.<BR> सु-अव्च्क्षित, adj. Well pondered, Rām. 4, 31, 5.<BR> --With अन्वव अनु-अव,<BR> 1. To look at, Rām. 1, 64, 9.<BR> 2. To look round, Rām. 5, 16, 38.<BR> 3. To perceive, Rām. 1, 3, 5.<BR> 4. To reflect, Man. 6, 65.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, To look at, MBh. 2, 2686.<BR> --With न्यव नि-अव, To ponder, MBh. 12, 4975.<BR> --With निरव निस्-अव, To perceive, Mṛcch. 86, 1.<BR> --With पर्यव परि-अव, To regard(?), MBh. 14, 636.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव,<BR> 1. To look at, Rām. 2, 39, 1.<BR> 2. To inspect one after the other, Śāk. 80, 21.<BR> 3. To mind, Rām. 2, 32, 34.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव,<BR> 1. To look at, Ṛt. 6, 17; to behold, MBh. 4, 218.<BR> 2. To consider, Rām. 2, 78, 4.<BR> 3. To reflect, Rām. 1, 50, 10.<BR> 4. To pay regard to, Rām. 4, 19, 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0103-b " target="_blank">Page0103-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To look up to, Rām. 5, 30, 12.<BR> 2. To look at, Man. 4, 77.<BR> 3. To see, Rām. 2, 22, 7.<BR> 4. To wait, Man. 9, 90; to expect, Rām. 6, 109, 5.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To look at, Rām. 6, 11, 2.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, To look at, Rām. 2, 9, 19.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To look, Rām. 3, 73, 3.<BR> 2. To perceive, Rām. 5, 2, 1.<BR> 3. To look up to one, Chr. 3, 7.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To look at, Nal. 22, 5.<BR> 2. To pay regard to, Chr. 55, 5.<BR> 3. To examine, Rām. 4, 29, 29.<BR> 4. To descry, Rām. 5, 29, 4.<BR> 5. To overlook, Pañc. 66, 11; Rām. 2, 23, 16; to disregard, Rājat. 5, 47; to neglect, Rām. 4, 17, 5.<BR> 6. To let escape, Man. 8, 344.<BR> --With अभ्युप अभि-उप, To forsake, MBh. 16, 160.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To neglect, MBh. 2, 1960.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To behold, MBh. 2, 2463.<BR> 2. To look at, Man. 4, 38.<BR> 3. To look about, Pañc. iv. d. 63, 64 (pass. on account of the metre).<BR> 4. To perceive, Kathās. 2, 19.<BR> 5. To consider, Rām. 5, 84, 5.<BR> --With संनिस् सम्-निस्, To perceive, Rām. 2, 21, 55.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To look round, Rām. 5, 17, 2.<BR> 2. To examine, Man. 9, 14<BR> 3. To perceive, Rājat. 5, 109.<BR> अ-परीक्षित, adj. Inconsiderate, Lass. 15, 5; foolish, Lass. 14, 20.<BR> --See कु-; सु-, adj. Well considered, Pañc. v. d. 16.<BR> दुष्परीक्ष्य, i. e. दुस्-परीक्ष्य, adj. Difficult to be examined, MBh. 3, 12481.<BR> --Comp.<BR> absol. अ-परीक्ष्य, Without due consideration, Pañc. v. d. 16.<BR> --Caus. परीक्षय, To cause to be examined, Man. 7, 194.<BR>--With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To look at, Rām. 2, 97, 13.<BR> 2. To suffer patiently, MBh. 3, 526.<BR> 3. To perceive, Pañc. 23, 11.<BR> प्रेक्षित n. A look, Daśak. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-a " target="_blank">Page0104-a + 40</a>] in Chr. 190, 15.<BR> प्रेक्षणीय, Worthy to be looked at, Indr. 5, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुष्प्रेक्षणीय and दुष्प्रेक्ष्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be looked at, MBh. 1, 2112; Rām. 3, 30, 35.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, To see, Draup. 5, 23.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र,<BR> 1. To look at, Draup. 8, 39.<BR> 2. To perceive, MBh. 3, 888.<BR> --With उत्प्र उद्-प्र,<BR> 1. To look up to, Rām. 5, 85, 5 (उत्प्रेक्ष्यामस्, ii. 2, Par.).<BR> 2. To perceive, Amar. 38.<BR> --With उपप्र उप-प्र, To overlook, MBh. 1, 3022.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To look in different directions, Rām. 3, 52, 3.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To behold, Bhag. 6, 13.<BR> 2. To perceive, Chr. 22, 21.<BR> 3. To consider, Man. 7, 127.<BR> --With अभिसंप्र अभि-सम्-प्र, To behold, MBh. 1, 3011.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To wait, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 15; To expect, MBh. 3, 1726.<BR> 2. To endure, Man. 9, 77.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-प्रतीक्षमाण, adj. Not expecting, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 1.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To wait, MBh. 1, 2903; Rām. 3, 52, 37; literally: do not dwell here waiting, i. e. do not stay here a moment; to expect, Rām. 1, 73, 13.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To look, Man. 2, 192; pass. to appear, Vikr. d. 132.<BR> 2. To consider, Man. 7, 140.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वीक्षित, n. A look, Ṛt. 6, 11, v. r.<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि,<BR> 1. To look at, MBh. 4, 1235.<BR> 2. To examine, Rām. 5, 19, 34.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि,<BR> 1. To look at, Man. 7, 6.<BR> 2. To perceive, Rām. 3, 53, 62.<BR> 3. To consider, MBh. 15, 379 (read -वीक्षते).<BR> --With उद्वि उद्-वि,<BR> 1. To look up, Amar. 24.<BR> 2. To look to, Śāk. d. 161.<BR> 3. To consider, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b " target="_blank">Page0104-b + 40</a>] Pañc. i. d. 265.<BR> --With समुद्वि सम्-उद्-वि,<BR> 1. To look at, Rām. 3, 4, 34.<BR> 2. To perceive, MBh. 3, 12425.<BR> --With उपवि उप-वि, To look at, Rām. 2, 58, 32.<BR> --With प्रतिवि प्रति-वि, To perceive, Rām. 1, 15, 26.<BR> दुष्प्रतिवीक्षणीय and दुष्प्रतिवीक्ष्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Difficult to be looked at, MBh. 6, 137; Rām. 2, 23, 3.<BR> --With संवि सम्-वि, To perceive, Rām. 5, 46, 10.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To look to, Man. 6, 68.<BR> 2. To behold, Rām. 3, 52, 11; to perceive, Hiḍ. 4, 26.<BR> 3. To mind, Rām. 2, 61, 12.<BR> 4. To consider, Man. 7, 26.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अ-समीक्षित, adj. Unperceived, Rām. 5, 81, 8; of the fut. pass. दुस्-समीक्ष्य, adj. Difficult to be looked at, MBh. 7, 1928.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To perceive, Rām. 2, 100, 39.<BR> --With प्रसम् प्र-सम्,<BR> 1. To see, Man. 7, 214.<BR> 2. To perceive, Rām. 3, 52, 52.<BR> 3. To consider, Man. 5, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षण|ईक्षणं
ईक्षण ईक्षण, i. e. ईक्ष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sight, Kathās. 18, 300.<BR> 2. Care, Man. 7, 141; superintendence, Man. 9, 11.<BR> 3. The eye, Hiḍ. 3, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितेक्षण
अ-सित- + ईक्षण अ-सित- + ईक्षण, adj., f. णा, black-eyed, Rām. 3, 52, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरेक्षण
मदिरा- + ईक्षण मदिरा- + ईक्षण, f. णा, a fascinating woman, Śāk. d. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिक|ईक्षणिकः
ईक्षणिक ईक्षणिक, i. e. ईक्षण + इक, m., f. का, A fortune-teller, Man. 9, 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षितृ
ईक्षितृ ईक्षितृ, i. e. ईक्ष् + तृ, m. An inspector, Man. 8, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख्
† ईख् ईख्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईङ्ख्|ईंख्
ईङ्ख् ईङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To vacillate.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To tremble, Bhartṛ. 1, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज्
† ईज् ईज् and ईञ्ज् ईञ्ज्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् ईड् (a change of इष्ट्, a denominative based on 2. इष्), ii. 2, Ātm. and † i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To implore, Chr. 296, 1 = Rigv. i. 112, 1.<BR> 2. To praise, Rām. 3, 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति ई + ति, f. Calamity, MBh. 3, 11258.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीति
निस्- + ईति निस्- + ईति, adj. free from calamities, Ragh. 1, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ता
ईदृक्ता ईदृक्ता, i. e. ईदृश् + ता, f. Quality, Ragh. 13, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष ईदृक्ष, i. e. इद्-दृश् + स (see इदम्), adj. Such, Kathās. 25, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश्
ईदृश् ईदृश्, i. e. इद्-दृश् (see the last), adj. Such, Kathās. 25, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश|ईदृशः
ईदृश ईदृश, i. e. इद्-दृश् + अ (see ईद्रिक्ष), adj., f. शी, Such, Pañc. 206, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृशक
ईदृशक ईदृश + क, adj. Such, MBh. 2, 1644.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सा
ईप्सा ईप्सा, i. e. ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + अ, f. Desire, MBh. 14, 1025.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेप्सा
यथा- + ईप्सा यथा- + ईप्सा, fem., instr. sing., according to one's desire, MBh. 3, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु ईप्सु, i. e. ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + उ, adj. Desiring, Man. 2, 61.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मेप्सु
धर्म- + ईप्सु धर्म- + ईप्सु, adj. anxious to perform one's duty, Man. 10, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईम्
ईम् ईम् (an old acc. of ई, f. of इ, see इदम्), a ved. part. which lays a stress upon the preceding word, Chr. 292, 11 = Rigv. i. 85, 11 (cf. ῑ́ν in οὑτοσῑ́ν, also ved. ई = ῑ́ in οὑτοσ-ῑ́, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् ईर् (akin to ऋ), ii. 2, Ātm. († i. 1 and 10, Par.)<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To shake, to throw.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To move, MBh. 13, 1839.<BR> 2. To throw, MBh. 3, 709.<BR> 3. To excite, Rām. 5, 11, 8.<BR> 4. To utter (a sound), MBh. 1, 4565; to pronounce, MBh. 14, 941.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, ptcple. of the pf. pass. उदिर्ण,<BR> 1. Excited MBh. 3, 973.<BR> 2. Lofty, MBh. 1, 5138. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b " target="_blank">Page0105-b + 40</a>]<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To lift up, Rām. 2, 57, 3.<BR> 2. To throw, Rām. 1, 55, 22.<BR> 3. To excite, Rām. 2, 93, 14.<BR> 4. To cause, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 23.<BR> 5. To utter Man. 2, 161.<BR> 6. To speak, Lass. 73, 8.<BR> 7. To show, Kumāras. 2, 6.<BR> 8. उदीरित् अ Quick, Prab. 14, 14.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, Caus. To utter, MBh. 1, 2170.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुदीर्ण, Excited, Rām. 4, 43, 69.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To raise, Chr. 29, 29.<BR> 2. To throw, Rām. 1, 56, 15.<BR> 3. To excite, MBh. 3, 5073.<BR> 4. To utter, Kathās. 24, 41.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To move, Ragh. 15, 23.<BR> 2. To turn, Śāk. d. 35, v. r.<BR> 3. To push on, Rājat. 5, 329; 330.<BR> 4. To send, Rām. 3, 50, 23.<BR> 5. To excite, Megh. 71.<BR> 6. To ask, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 1.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus. To push forward, Pañc. 222, 2.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus.<BR> 1. To move, Rām. 5, 16, 45.<BR> 2. To lift up, MBh. 3, 12185.<BR> 3. To utter, Rām. 4, 6, 21.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, Caus. To move, MBh. 10, 579.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण ईरिण (cf. इरिण), n. A desert, MBh. 13, 7257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
† ईर्क्ष्य् ईर्क्ष्य्, i. 1, Par. To envy (cf. ईर्ष्य्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा ईर्षा, i. e. ईर्ष्य् + अ, f. Envy, jealousy, Rām. 4, 24, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षित
ईर्षित ईर्षित, ptcple. of the pf. pass., and ईर्षितव्य ईर्षितव्य, ptcple. of the fut. pass. of ईर्ष्य्, Hit. i. d. 107 v. r.; Prab. 49, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षु
ईर्षु ईर्षु, i. e. ईर्ष्य् + उ, adj. Envious, Hit. i. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य् ईर्ष्य् (probably ईर्ष्य, and originally an anomal. frequentat. of रिष्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To envy, Hit. i. d. 167, v. r.<BR> 2. To be jealous, Prab. 49, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्या
ईर्ष्या ईर्ष्य् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Envy, Man. 7, 48.<BR> 2. Jealousy, Bhartṛ. 1, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेर्ष्यम्
