उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उपस्थ उप-स्थ (vb. स्था), m. and n.<BR> 1. The lap (ved.).<BR> 2. The male or female organs of generation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πόσθη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथोपस्थ|रथोपस्थः
रथ- + उपस्थ रथ- + उपस्थ, m. and n. the carioteer's seat for driving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थान|उपस्थानं
उपस्थान उपस्थान, i. e. उप-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Waiting on, Rām. 4, 44, 111; Vikr. 5, 5.<BR> 2. Being at one's command, Yājñ. 3, 160.<BR> 3. Assembly, MBh. 2, 1757.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थान|अनुपस्थानं
अन्- + उपस्थान अन्- + उपस्थान, n. want of compliance, Rām. 6, 72, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेह|उपस्नेहः
उपस्नेह उपस्नेह, i. e. उप-स्निक् + अ, m. Humectation, Rām. 5, 75, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शन|उपस्पर्शनं
उपस्पर्शन उपस्पर्शन, i. e. उप-स्पृश् + अन, n. Bathing, MBh. 3, 8053.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वेद|उपस्वेदः
उपस्वेद उपस्वेद, i. e. उप-स्विद् + अ, m. Moisture; in the comp. word स-, adj. Moistened, MBh. 1, 1033.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्तृ|उपहर्त्तृ
उपहर्तृ उपहर्तृ, i. e. उप-हृ + तृ, m. One who serves (meat), Man. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्तिका
उपहस्तिका -उपहस्तिका, i. e. उप-हस्त + क, f. A box, Daśak. 135, ult..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार|उपहारः
उपहार उपहार, i. e. उप-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A complimentary present to a superior, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 6.<BR> 2. Exultation (which comprehends laughter, dance, song, bowing, recital of prayer, etc.), Daśak. in Chr. 181, 20 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास|उपहासः
उपहास उपहास, i. e. उप-हस् + अ, m. Sneering, Ragh. 12, 37.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपहासम्
सोपहासम् सोपहासम्, i. e. स-उपहास + म्, adv. Sneeringly, Pañc. 227, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्यता
उपहास्यता उप-हास्य + ता (vb. हस्), f. Derision, Ragh. 1, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वर|उपह्वरं|उपह्वरः
उपह्वर उपह्वर, i. e. उप-ह्वृ + अ<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A slope, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 87, 2.<BR> II. loc. sing. रे,<BR> 1. Near, Arj. 1, 5.<BR> 2. Privately, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 1; 192, 7; 193, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु उपांशु, i. e. उप-अंशु,<BR> I. m. A low muttered prayer, Man. 2, 8.<BR> II. adv. Secretly, MBh. 3, 17309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्मन्|उपाकर्म्मन्
