मानसौकस्
मानस- + ओकस् मानस- + ओकस्, m. the wild swan or goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनौकस्
वन- + ओकस् वन- + ओकस्,<BR> I. adj. living in woods, Chr. 25, 61.<BR> II. m. 1. an anchorite, Chr. 11, 18. 2. a wild beast, Rām. 3, 49, 39. 3. a monkey, 6, 26, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्योकस्|वार्य्योकस्
वारि- + ओकस् वारि- + ओकस्, m. a leech, Man. 7, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासौकस्
वास- + ओकस् वास- + ओकस्, n. the private apartments; a sleeping-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलौकस्
विल- + ओकस् विल- + ओकस्, m. any animal living in holes, Man. 10, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गौकस्
स्वर्ग- + ओकस् स्वर्ग- + ओकस्, m. a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख्
† ओख् ओख्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be dry (cf. उष्, ष् is often changed to ख्).<BR> 2. To be able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघ|ओघः
ओघ ओघ, i. e. probably वह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A stream, Man. 9, 54.<BR> 2. A multitude, MBh. 1, 4448.<BR> 3. Density, Śiś. 9, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरौघ|शरौघः
शर- + ओघ शर- + ओघ, m. a multitude of arrows, Chr. 34, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वौघ|सर्वौघः|सर्व्वौघ|सर्व्वौघः
सर्व- + ओघ सर्व- + ओघ, m. 1. assembling a complete army. 2. great speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघवन्त्|ओघवत्
ओघवन्त् ओघ + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Rapid, MBh. 3, 10538.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 13, 121.<BR> III. f. वती, A proper name, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओंकार|ओङ्कार|ओंकारः|ओङ्कारः
ओंकार ओंकार, i. e. ॐ-कृ + अ, n.<BR> 1. The holy syllable ॐ, Man. 2, 75.<BR> 2. Thanksgiving, Rājat. 5, 134.<BR> 3. Grumbling, Pañc. 158, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्
† ओज् ओज्, i. 1, and i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To be strong.<BR> 2. To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस् ओजस्, i. e. वज् + अस्,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Strength, Matsyop. 2.<BR> 2. Light, splendour, Man. 12, 18.<BR> II. ओजसा (instr.), adv. Powerfully, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4; courageously, Rām. 3, 53, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. augus in augus + tus, and αὐγή, -αὐγες in ἀνταυγής, ές.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितौजस्
अमितौजस् अमितौजस्, i. e. अ-मित- (vb. मा), adj. all-mighty, Man. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस्
महौजस् महौजस्, i. e. महा-, adj. eminent in power, Man. 1, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्विन्
ओजस्विन् ओजस् + विन्, adj., f. नी, Strong, MBh. 14, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्र|ओड्रः
ओड्र ओड्र, m. pl. The name of a people and their country, now Orissa, Man. 10, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्
† ओण् ओण्, i. 1, Par. To take away (probably a form of अर्ण् for अर्णु, i. e. ऋ ii. 5, cf. ἄρνυμαι).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदती
ओदती ओदती (fem. of a ptcple. of उद् = उन्द्), f. The dawn, Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदन|ओदनं|ओदनः
ओदन ओदन, i. e. उद् (= उन्द्) + अन, m. and n.<BR> 1. A pap, see comp.<BR> 2. Boiled rice, Man. 8, 329.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरौदन|क्षीरौदनः
क्षीरौदन क्षीरौदन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a " target="_blank">Page0146-a + 43</a>] i. e. क्षीर-, m. rice boiled with milk, MBh. 13, 947.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडोदन
गुडोदन गुडोदन (sic instead of ˚डौ˚), i. e. गुड-, boiled rice with sugar, MBh. 13, 6162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलौदन|तिलौदनं|तिलौदनः
तिल- + ओदन तिल- + ओदन, n. a dish of rice, milk, and sesamum, Rām. 2, 69, 10 (तिलोदन instead of ˚लौ˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्योदन
दधि- + ओदन दधि- + ओदन, m. a mess prepared of curds, Yājñ. 1, 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसभूतोदन
मांस-भूतोदन मांस-भूतोदन (instead of ˚तौ˚), i. e. -भूत-, a dish of rice and meat(?), Rām. 2, 52, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्योदन|शाल्योदनः
शालि- + ओदन शालि- + ओदन, boiled rice, Bhartṛ. 2, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम् ॐ, ind. A mystic word prefacing all prayers, Pañc. 33, 11; used at the commencement and end of holy recitations, Man. 2, 74; 73; and writings, Man.; used to commence respectful salutations, and on other occasions, e. g. Man. 2, 75; and the subject of many mystical speculations, Man. 2, 79; 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्यावन्त्|ओम्यावत्
ओम्यावन्त् ओम्यावन्त्, i. e. अव् + मन् + य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Agreeable, Chr. 296, 7 = Rigv. i. 112, 7; kind, Chr. 297, 20 = Rigv. i. 112, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलण्ड्|ओलंड्
ओलण्ड् ओलण्ड्, see लण्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधि|ओषधिः
ओषधि and धी ओषधी̆, i. e. उष् + अ-धा (cf. निधि), f.<BR> 1. A plant, Man. 1, 46.<BR> 2. A medicinal herb, Caurap. 47.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषधि|महौषधिः
महौषधि महौषधि, i. e. महा-, f. a kind of sensitive plant, Mimosa pudica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधिज|ओषधिजः
ओषधिज ओषधि-ज (vb. जन्), adj. Produced from plants, Kir. 5, 14 (i. e. a phosphorescent light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ|ओष्ठः
ओष्ठ ओष्ठ, i. e. probably अव-स्थ (vb. स्था), m.<BR> 1. The lip, Man. 8, 282.<BR> 2. The upper lip, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 46. In comp. words a preceding अ may be dropped, and the fem. of a comp. adj. may end in ठा or ठी, e. g. रुचिर-दन्तौष्ठी, Having beautiful teeth and lips, Rām. 3, 52, 16.<BR> बिम्बोष्ठ, adj. Having bimba-like lips, Kathās. 4, 8.<BR> संदष्टौष्ठ, i. e. सम्-दष्ट-ओष्ठ [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b " target="_blank">Page0146-b + 37</a>] (vb. दंश्), adj. Biting the lips, MBh. 3, 427.<BR> स्फुरदोष्ठ, i. e. स्फुरन्त्-ओष्ठ, adj., f. ठी, With trembling lips, Indr. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थ्य
औक्थ्य औक्थ्य, i. e. उक्थ + य, n. A complex of hymns(?), MBh. 3, 10686.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औग्र्य|औग्र्यं
औग्र्य औग्र्य, i. e. उग्र + य, n. Formidableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कण्ठ्य|औत्कंठ्यं
औत्कण्ठ्य औत्कण्ठ्य, i. e. उत्कण्ठा + य, n. Desire, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कण्ठ्यवन्त्|औत्कण्ठ्यवत्
औत्कण्ठ्यवन्त् औत्कण्ठ्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Desirous, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तमि|औत्तमिः
औत्तमि औत्तमि, i. e. उत्तम + इ, patron. m. The name of a Manu, Man. 1, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तर
औत्तर औत्तर (? if correct it would be उत्तर + अ), adj. Inhabiting the north, MBh. 3, 10546 (probably it must be corrected यत्रोत्त्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तानपाद|औत्तानपादः
औत्तानपाद औत्तानपाद, and -पादि -पादि, i. e. उत्तान-पाद (a proper name) + अ or इ, patron. m. Dhruva or the polar star, MBh. 13, 195; Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पत्तिक
औत्पत्तिक औत्पत्तिक, i. e. उत्पत्ति + इक, adj. Innate, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पातिक
औत्पातिक औत्पातिक, i. e. उत्पात + इक, adj., f. की, Prodigious, Rām. 5, 52, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सुक्य|औत्सुक्यं
औत्सुक्य औत्सुक्य, i. e. उत्सुक + य,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Perturbation, Rām. 3, 1, 4.<BR> 2. Desire, MBh. 3, 114.<BR> II. instr. येन, adverbially, Quickly, Pañc. 35, 9; 95, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दौत्सुक्य|मंदौत्सुक्य
मन्द- + औत्सुक्य मन्द- + औत्सुक्य, adj. having no great desire, Śāk. 18, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्सुक्य
स- + औत्सुक्य स- + औत्सुक्य, adj., f. या, full of desire, Pañc. 185, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदक
औदक औदक, i. e. उदक + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Referring to water, Man. 3, 215.<BR> 2. Aquatic, Man. 1, 44; 6, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदञ्चन|औदंचन
औदञ्चन औदञ्चन, i. e. उदञ्चन + अ, adj. Contained in a tub, Bhāg. P. 8, 24, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदरिक|औदरिकः
औदरिक औदरिक, i. e. उदर + इक, adj., f. की, Gluttonous, Vikr. 39, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदर्य|औदर्यः|औदर्य्य
औदर्य औदर्य, i. e. उदर + य, adj. Being in the womb, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदार्य|औदार्यं|औदार्य्य|औदार्य्यं
औदार्य औदार्य, i. e. उदार + य, n.<BR> 1. Excellence, Nal. 16, 17.<BR> 2. Dignity, Rām. 3, 18, 25.<BR> 3. Generosity, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदासीन्य|औदासीन्यं
औदासीन्य औदासीन्य, i. e. उद्-आसीन + य (vb. आस्), and औदास्य औदास्य, i. e. उद्-आस् + अ + य, n. Indifference, apathy, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 17; Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदुम्बर|औदुंबर|औदुम्बरः
औदुम्बर औदुम्बर, i. e. उदुम्बर + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री, Made of Udumbara wood, Man. 2, 45.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1869.<BR> III. f. री, A branch of the Udumbara tree, Rām. 1, 4, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धारिक
औद्धारिक औद्धारिक, i. e. उद्धार + इक, adj. Deducted, Man. 9, 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्वाहिक|औद्वाहिकं
औद्वाहिक औद्वाहिक, i. e. उद्वाह + इक, adj. Received on account of marriage, Man. 9, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपधर्म्य|औपधर्म्यं
