स- + कटुक स- + कटुक, adj. Harsh, MBh. 2, 1551.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुता
कटुता कटु + ता, f. Wickedness, Hariv. 1022.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोदक
कटोदक कटोदक, i. e. कट-उदक, n. Obsequies of a deceased person, Bhāg. P. 7, 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ्
† कठ् कठ् (a form of कष्ट् in कष्ट), i. 1, Par. To live in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ कठ, m. The name of a sage, MBh. 1, 962.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिन|कठिनं|कठिनः
कठिन कठिन, perhaps for कष्ट + इन (cf. कठ्),<BR> I. adj., f. ना.<BR> 1. Hard, solid, Pañc. 190, 16; Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> 2. Cruel, Kathās. 19, 89.<BR> II. f. नी, Chalk, Pañc. Pr. 7.<BR> III. n. A pat, MBh. 3, 8484.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनता
कठिनता कठिन + ता, f., and कठिनत्व कठिन + त्व, n. Hardness, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोर|कठोरः
कठोर कठोर, i. e. probably कष्ट + वर् (for वन्) + अ (cf. कठिन), adj.<BR> 1. Hard, solid, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 15.<BR> 2. Full grown, Mṛcch. 115, 13.<BR> 3. Sharp, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 3.<BR> 4. Violent, Pañc. 93, 1.<BR> 5. Loud, Pañc. 248, 17.<BR> 6. Hard-hearted, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्
† कड् कड्, i. 1 and 6, Par. To be glad.<BR> --i. 6, Par. To eat.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To remove the husk of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्ड्
† कड्ड् कड्ड्, i. 1, Par. To be rough (a dialectical form of कष्ट्; cf. कठ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्
† कण् कण्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To cry as in distress.<BR> 3. To go.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To wink, to cover the eye with the lids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण कण,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Grain, Hit. 9, 14; broken rice, Man. 11, 92; also the fine red powder which adheres to the rice berry beneath the husk.<BR> 2. A drop, Bhartṛ. 3, 15; spray, Śāk. d. 55.<BR> 3. A spark, Pañc. 93, 3.<BR> 4. A little bit, Prab. 29, 13.<BR> II. f. णा, Long pepper, Suśr. 2, 418, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारकण|तुषारकणः
तुषार-, तुहिन- + कण तुषार-, तुहिन- + कण, m. a flake of snow, Kathās. 19, 50; Amar. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनकण|तुहिनकणः
तुषार-, तुहिन- + कण तुषार-, तुहिन- + कण, m. a flake of snow, Kathās. 19, 50; Amar. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणप|कणपः
कणप कणप, m. A kind of spear, MBh. 1, 8257; with न् instead of ण्, MBh. 3, 810.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणभ|कणभः
कणभ कणभ, m. A kind of fly (an autumn fly ?), Suśr. 2, 258, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणशस्
कणशस् कण + शस्, adv. In small pieces, Kumāras. 4, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाद|कणादः
कणाद कणाद, m. The name of a sage, the founder of the Vaiśeṣika or atomic school of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणान्नता
कणान्नता कणान्नता, i. e. कण-अन्न + ता, f. Eating broken rice, Man. 11, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिक|कणिकः
कणिक कणिक, i. e. कण + इक,<BR> I. m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b " target="_blank">Page0152-b + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Seed, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 33.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 1, 5544.<BR> II. f. का, A drop, Megh. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ट्|कंट्
† कण्ट् कण्ट्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टक|कंटक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कण्टक कण्टक (the base कण्ट् is a dialect. form of कृन्त् (originally कर्न्त्), the base of the present, etc. of कृत्), m.<BR> 1. A thorn, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 183.<BR> 2. A sharp bone, Man. 8, 95.<BR> 3. An enemy, Pañc. 176, 8; a wicked person, Man. 9, 252; 253.<BR> 4. Stinging pain, Suśr. 1, 93, 4.<BR> 5. Obstacle, Hit. iii. d. 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकण्टक
अ- + कण्टक अ- + कण्टक, adj., f. इका, free from thorns, i. e. obstacles, Rām. 2, 46, 29; from danger, 2, 81, 6; from harm, 3, 53, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरकण्टक
अमर- + कण्टक अमर- + कण्टक, n. the name of the eastern table-land of the Vindhya mountain, Rām. 2, 73, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक|निष्कण्टकः
निष्कण्टक निष्कण्टक, i. e. निस्-, adj. = अकण्टक, MBh. 4, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जकण्टक|भूर्जकंटक|भूर्जकण्टकः
भूर्ज- + कण्टक भूर्ज- + कण्टक, m. the son of an outcast Brāhmaṇa, Man. 10, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकण्टक|सकंटक|सकण्टकः
स- + कण्टक स- + कण्टक, adj. thorny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकित|कंटकित
कण्टकित कण्टकित, i. e. कण्टक + इत, adj., f. ता.<BR> 1. Thorny, Draup. 1, 14.<BR> 2. With bristling hair (a sign of pleasure or love, according to the Hindus), Rājat. 5, 2; Śāk. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिन्|कंटकिन्
कण्टकिन् कण्टकिन्, i. e. कण्टक + इन्, adj., f. नी. Thorny, MBh. 1, 2851.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्|कंठ्
† कण्ठ् कण्ठ्, i. 1, Par., Ātm., i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To grieve.<BR> 2. To desire, to long for.<BR> --Cf. उत्कण्ठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ|कंठ|कंठं|कंठः|कण्ठः
कण्ठ कण्ठ (probably a dial. form of *कन्धर, for कन्धर), m.<BR> 1. The neck, Rām. 2, 66, 32 Gorr.<BR> 2. The throat, Mṛcch. 128, 20; Man. 11, 205.<BR> 3. Voice, MBh. 3, 829.<BR> 4. Proximity, Pañc. 247, 14.<BR> 5. The proper name of a Ṛṣi, Rām. 4, 18, 11.<BR> --When latter part of a comp. adj., f. ठी and ठा, e. g. अश्रु- adj. With tears in the throat, i. e. the voice interrupted by tears, Rām. 2, 74, 28; f. ठी, Daśak. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a " target="_blank">Page0153-a + 43</a>] in Chr. 191, 3.<BR> निष्क-,<BR> I. adj., f. ठी, Wearing a golden ornament on the neck, MBh. 3, 14694.<BR> II. m. A golden ornament of the neck, 13, 4928.<BR> नील-,<BR> I. adj. With a blue throat, MBh. 10, 454.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A peacock, Megh. 77.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva, Rām. 5, 89, 41.<BR> III. f. ठी, A peahen, 5, 11, 23.<BR> मुक्त-कण्ठ + म् (vb. मुच्), adv. Aloud, as shouting or crying.<BR> शिति-, m.<BR> 1. A peacock.<BR> 2. A gallinule.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> श्री-, m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> सन्न- (vb. सद्), adj. Choked, scarcely able to articulate.<BR> सूत्र-, m.<BR> 1. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 2. A wagtail.<BR> 3. A dove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीरव|कंठीरव|कण्ठीरवः
कण्ठीरव कण्ठीरव, i. e. कण्ठी- (f. of कण्ठ with the same signification) रु + अ, m. A lion, Pañc. iii. d. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्य|कंठ्य|कण्ठ्यः
कण्ठ्य कण्ठ्य, i. e. कण्ठ + य, adj.<BR> 1. Being at the throat.<BR> 2. Salutary to the throat.<BR> 3. Guttural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्|कंड्
† कण्ड् कण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm. To be glad.<BR> --i. 1 and i. 10, Par. To remove the husk of grain.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To preserve.<BR> --Cf. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डन|कंडन|कंडनं|कण्डनं
कण्डन कण्ड् + अन,<BR> I. n. The chaff, Suśr. 1, 38, 4.<BR> II. f. नी, A mortar, Man. 3, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डु|कंडु|कंडुः|कण्डुः
कण्डु,<BR> I. कण्डु, and, usually, कण्डू कण्डू, f. The itch, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 13.<BR> II. कण्डु, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, Rām. 2, 21, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूति|कंडूति|कंडूतिः|कण्डूतिः
कण्डूति कण्डूति, i. e. कण्डूय + ति, f. Wantonness, Rājat. 5, 281.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूय
कण्डूय कण्डूय, a denominative derived from कण्डु, Par. (Ātm. MBh. 13, 5023).<BR> 1. To scratch, MBh. 1, 5932.<BR> 2. To rub, Śāk. d. 144.<BR> 3. To stroke, Man. 4, 82.<BR> खर-कण्डूयित, n. (proverbially) Scratching with a thorn for ‘doing an absurd action,’ MBh. 3, 1329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयन|कंडूयन|कण्डूयनं
कण्डूयन कण्डूयन, i. e. कण्दूय + अन, n.<BR> 1. Itching, Bhāg. P. 8, 7, 10.<BR> 2. Scratching, 3, 31, 26.<BR> 3. Stroking, Vikr. d. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक|कण्डूयनकः
कण्डूयनक कण्डूयन + क, adj. Titillating, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयितृ|कंडूयितृ
कण्डूयितृ कण्डूयितृ, i. e. कण्डूय + तृ, m., f. तॄ, n. Who or what rubs, Ragh. 13, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व कण्व, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, MBh. 1, 2874. Superl. कण्व + तम, The first of the Kaṇva tribe, Chr. 287, 4 = Rigv. i. 48, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कतक कतक, m. The nut plant, Strychnos potatorum, which clears water, Man. 6, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम क + तम, superl. of किम्, pron. n. ˚मद्. Who, what, which of many, MBh. 1, 4312; of two, 13, 3044.<BR> --With न and अपि, Not the least, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर क + तर, compar. of किम्, pron. n. ˚रद्, Who, what, which of two, MBh. 1, 3645; of many, Vikr. 5, 14.<BR> --Cf. Lat. uter for cuter (ubi: alicubi), utrum; κότερον, ὁ-πότερος; Goth. hvathar; A.S. hvädher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति कति, i. e. क, base of किम् + ति, pron.<BR> 1. How many, Rām. 5, 73, 2.<BR> 2. Some, Pañc. 171, 2; usually with following चिद्, Pañc. 87, 22; with अपि, Amar. 25.<BR> 3. A proper name, Hariv. 1461.<BR> --Cf. Lat. quot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिधा
कतिधा कति + धा, adv. In how many ways, Bhāg. P. 3, 6, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कतिपय कतिपय (from कति), adj., f. या and यी, Some, Pañc. 9, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ्
कत्थ् कत्थ्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To boast, Chr. 24, 39.<BR> 2. To praise, Rām. 3, 55, 8.<BR> 3. To blame, Bhāg. P. 8, 7, 33. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a " target="_blank">Page0154-a + 42</a>]<BR> --With the prep. वि वि,<BR> 1. To boast, Rām. 6, 36, 42.<BR> 2. To disparage, MBh. 4, 1299.<BR> --Caus. To humble, Draup. 9, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थन
कत्थन कत्थ् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Boasting, a boaster, Rām. 1, 6, 10.<BR> II. n. Boasting, Rām. 3, 35, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्र्
† कत्र् कत्र्, see कर्त्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्
कथ् कथ्, i. 10, Par., in epic poetry also Ātm. (probably a denomin. of कथम्).<BR> 1. To tell, MBh. 1, 2206; Ātm. ib. 3, 13180; to tell of, with the acc., Śāk. 7, 18.<BR> 2. To announce, MBh. 14, 144.<BR> 3. To declare, Man. 7, 157.<BR> 4. To command, Pañc. 57, 22; Vikr. d. 7.<BR> 5. To converse, Rām. 2, 57, 1; Brāhmaṇ. 1, 11.<BR> --Pass. To be called, Hit. Pr. d. 32.<BR> --Anomalous ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. कथयान, MBh. 2, 1906.<BR> कथित, n. Talk, Śāk. 33, 3.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, To announce, Rām. 5, 1, 93.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To tell, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 13.<BR> 2. To explain, MBh. 3, 14000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक कथ् + अक, adj. Telling, Śāntiś. 2, 27. m. A narrator, MBh. 1, 7778.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन कथ् + अन, n. Relating, Bhartṛ. 2, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् क + थ + म् (cf. किम्), adv.<BR> 1. In what manner, Nal. 3, 10.<BR> 2. How, Śāk. 14, 13; Man. 5, 2.<BR> 3. What, Śāk. 94, 1 (कथं माम् एवोद्दिशति, What! dares he defy me?).<BR> 4. Whence, Śāk. 98, 23.<BR> --With following अपि,<BR> 1. By some means, by accident, Pañc. 127, 25; 261, 13.<BR> 2. A little, Śāk. d. 73.<BR> 3. Slowly, with difficulty, Pañc. 236, 7.<BR> 4. कथंकथम् अपि, Not without great pain, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 11.<BR> --With following नु,<BR> 1. How now? Nal. 17, 20 (19).<BR> 2. How much more? [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b " target="_blank">Page0154-b + 44</a>] Śāk. d. 81; with न, How much less? Rām. 1, 33, 9.<BR> --With following चन,<BR> 1. In any manner, Man. 5, 143; with न, In no manner, never, Man. 4, 11.<BR> 2. Not without difficulty, Rām. 1, 67, 4.<BR> 3. कथंकथम् चन, A little, Vikr. 29, 15.<BR> --With following चिद्,<BR> 1. A little, Śāk. 65, 1.<BR> 2. Scarcely, Rām. 3, 24, 20.<BR> 3. With difficulty, Pañc. 9, 5; MBh. 13, 2797.<BR> कथं चिद् अपि, Even a little, Man. 3, 190; Scarcely, Rām. 6, 99, 50.<BR> कथं चिद्--न, In no way, Rām. 5, 75, 7.<BR> न कथं चिद् अपि, Never, Chr. 19, 4.<BR> न कथं चिद्--न, By all means, Arj. 10, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकथम्
यथा-कथ + म् यथा-कथ + म्, adv. with following चिद्, by all means, Man. 11, 220 (221).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
कथा कथ् + आ, f.<BR> 1. A tale, Rām. 1, 2, 38.<BR> 2. A speech, discourse, Man. 3, 231; Śāk. d. 76.<BR> 3. Mention, Nal. 21, 33.<BR> 4. With preceding का (fem. of किम्), and a following loc., or प्रति with acc., No question, out of the question, Ragh. 10, 29 (you are out of the question); in a protasis, Śāk. d. 52, का कथा वाणसंधाने, There is no need to fix the arrow to the bow; in an apodosis, Kathās. 4, 123, how much less?<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकथा
धर्म- + कथा धर्म- + कथा, f. a conversation concerning law or duty, Pañc. 117, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकथा
पुरा- + कथा पुरा- + कथा, f. a tale of past ages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथा|संकथा
सम्- + कथा सम्- + कथा, f. conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानक|कथानकं
कथानक कथ् + आन + क, n. A little tale, Lass. 15, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथामय
कथामय कथा + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of tales, Kathās. 8, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथावशेषता
कथावशेषता कथावशेषता, i. e. कथा-अवशेष + ता, f. Condition of one of whom nothing but the mention is left, i. e. death, Prab. 83, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् क + द् (the old nom. acc. sing. n. of किम्; cf. Lat. quod; O.H.G. huaz; A.S. hvät).<BR> 1. With following चिद् कच्चिद् कच् चिद्, particle of interrogation, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a " target="_blank">Page0155-a + 40</a>] Perhaps, Nal. 4, 24.<BR> 2. As former part of compound nouns, Bad, e. g. कद्-अन्न, n. Bad food, Bhāg. P. 5, 9, 9.<BR> कद्-अपत्य, adj. Having a bad offspring, 4, 13, 43.<BR> कद्-इन्द्रिय, n. pl. The paltry organs of sense, 8, 3, 28.<BR> 3. Combined with vb. दा, To blame, 7, 5, 28; with अर्थ्, q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् कद्, or † कन्द् कन्द्, or † क्रन्द् क्रन्द्, or † क्लन्द् क्लन्द्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. † To be confused.<BR> 2. † To confound.<BR> 3. To kill; चकाद, Rām. 6, 65, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन|कदनं
कदन कद् + अन, n. Killing, Rām. 6, 65, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्ब|कदंब|कदम्बं|कदंबः|कदम्बः
कदम्ब कदम्ब,<BR> I. m. A tree, Nauclea cadamba (its flower, when fullblown, is covered with projecting anthers), Rām. 5, 74, 4; Kir. 5, 9.<BR> II. n. Plenty, Śāk. 87, 15 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बक|कदंबक|कदम्बकं|कदंबकः|कदम्बकः
कदम्बक कदम्ब + क, n. Plenty, Śāk. d. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थ्
कदर्थ् कदर्थ्, see अर्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थ|कदर्थः
कदर्थ कदर्थ, see कदर्थी under कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थन
कदर्थन कदर्थन. i. e. कद्-अर्थ् + अन, n. and f. ना, Tormenting, Daśak. 169, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य|कदर्यः|कदर्य्य|कदर्य्यः
कदर्य कद्-अर्य, adj., f. या, Avaricious, Man. 4, 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदल|कदलः
कदल कदल,<BR> I. m. and f. ली, The plaintain tree, Musa sapientum, Megh. 75.<BR> II. f. ली, A kind of deer, MBh. 2, 1743.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलिका
कदलिका कदलिका, i. e. कदली + क, f. The plaintain tree, Prab. 65, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदा
कदा क + दा (see किम्), adv. At what time, Nal. 22, 7. With following चन,<BR> 1. Once, some time; preceded by न, Never, Man. 2, 58.<BR> 2. Perhaps, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b " target="_blank">Page0155-b + 40</a>] Pañc. 22, 10. With following चिद्, Once, Brāhmaṇ. 1, 2; preceded by न, Never, Man. 4, 74.<BR> 3. Followed by अपि, and preceded by न, Never, Hit. 58, 12.<BR> --Cf. Lat. quando, quandoque = काद चिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रू
कद्रू कद्रू, f. The wife of Kaśyapa and mother of the serpent race, MBh. 1, 1074.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्
कन् कन्, i. 1, Par. (perhaps proceeded from कम्, q. cf., by कम् + ना, ii. 9, cf. रण्).<BR> 1. To love, to be satisfied, etc. (ved.).<BR> 2. † To shine.<BR> 3. † To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनक|कनकं|कनकः
कनक कन् + अक, n. Gold, Ṛt. 6, 28; 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकमय
कनकमय कनक + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Pañc. 235, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनप|कनपः
कनप कनप, see कणप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ कनिष्ठ, superl. of अल्प and युवन्, f. ष्ठा.<BR> 1. Smallest, very small, Rām. 3, 51, 7.<BR> 2. Youngest, Man. 9, 113.<BR> 3. with and without अङ्गुलि, f. The little finger, Yājñ. 1, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठिका
कनिष्ठिका कनिष्ठिका, i. e. कणिष्ठ + क, f. The little finger, MBh. 13, 5059.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयंस्
कनीयंस् कनीयंस्,<BR> I. comparative of अल्प and युवन्, f. यसी, Very small, Pañc. 16, 7.<BR> II. m. A younger brother, Rām. 1, 26, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस|कनीयसं
कनीयस कनीयस, i. e. कनीयंस् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Smaller, MBh. 13, 2560.<BR> 2. Younger, MBh. 1, 3518.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्था|कंथा
कन्था कन्था, f. A patched cloth, Bhartṛ. 3, 16.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. cento(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द्|कंद्
† कन्द् कन्द्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To call.<BR> 2. To cry or shed tears.<BR> --Cf. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द|कंद|कंदं|कन्दं|कंदः|कन्दः
कन्द कन्द, m. A bulbous root, Pañc. ii. d. 161.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकन्द|महाकंद|महाकन्दः
महा- + कन्द महा- + कन्द, m. 1. garlic. 2. a sort of yam. 3. a plant, Hingtsha repens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्द|रक्तकंद|रक्तकन्दः
रक्त- + कन्द रक्त- + कन्द, m. 1. coral. 2. a sort of onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दट|कंदट|कन्दटं
कन्दट कन्दट, n. The white esculent water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दद
कन्दद कन्द-द (vb. दा), adj. One who makes roots (?), MBh. 12, 10403.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर|कंदर|कंदरं|कन्दरं|कंदरः|कन्दरः
कन्दर कन्दर (probably क + म्, old nom. and acc. n. of किम्, -दॄ + अ), m., f. ॠ, and n. A cave, Pañc. 93, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दरवन्त्|कन्दरवत्
कन्दरवन्त् कन्दर + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abundant in caves, Rām. 3, 21, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्प|कंदर्प|कंदर्पः|कन्दर्पः
कन्दर्प कन्दर्प (probably कम्, see कन्दर, -दृप् + अ), m.<BR> 1. A name of the god of love, Rām. 1, 25, 10.<BR> 2. Love, MBh. 1, 7920.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दल|कंदल|कंदलं|कन्दलं|कंदलः|कन्दलः
कन्दल कन्दल (perhaps कम्, see the last, and दल), n.<BR> 1. The flower of the कन्दली (q. cf.), Bhartṛ. 1, 43.<BR> 2. A new shoot.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्दल|रक्तकंदल|रक्तकन्दलः
रक्त- + कन्दल रक्त- + कन्दल, रत्न-, and हेम-, m. coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दली|कंदली
कन्दली कन्दली, see the last, f. The plaintain tree, Musa sapientum, Vikr. d. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलिन्
कन्दलिन् कन्दलिन्, i. e. कन्दल + इन्, adj., f. नी, Abundant in new shoots, Bhartṛ. 1, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दु|कंदुः|कन्दुः
कन्दु कन्दु, m. f. An iron pan, Mālav. 24, 21 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुक|कंदुक|कंदुकं|कंदुकः|कन्दुकः
कन्दुक कन्दुक,<BR> I. m. A ball for playing with, Bhartṛ. 2, 83.<BR> II. n. A pillow, Bhartṛ. 3, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धर|कंधर|कंधरः|कन्धरः
कन्धर कन्धर [i. e. कम् (see कन्दर), according to the grammarians, Head, -धृ + अ], m., and f. रा, The neck, Yājñ. 2, 220.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्धर|उत्कंधर|उत्कन्धरं
उत्कन्धर उत्कन्धर, i. e. उद्-, adj., f. रा (cf. Kathās. 20, 8), with raised neck, Pañc. 249, 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-b " target="_blank">Page0156-b + 38</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकन्धर|दशकंधर|दशकन्धरः
