सकर्मन्|सकर्म्मन्
स- + कर्मन् स- + कर्मन्, adj. 1. performing any act. 2. following the same business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जकर्मन्
सज्ज- + कर्मन् सज्ज- + कर्मन्, n. preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर्मन्|सुकर्म्मन्
सु- + कर्मन् सु- + कर्मन्,<BR> I. adj. 1. one who performs beautiful works, Rājat. 5, 115. 2. virtuous. 11. m. the artist of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनकर्मन्|हीनकर्म्मन्
हीन- + कर्मन् हीन- + कर्मन्, adj. neglecting religious acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनाशा|कर्म्मनाशा
कर्मनाशा कर्मनाशा, i. e. कर्मन्-नश् + अ, f. The name of a river, the water of which destroys religious merit, Bhāṣāp. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ममय|कर्म्ममय
कर्ममय कर्ममय, i. e. कर्मन् + मय, adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Produced by action, MBh. 3, 129.<BR> 2. Having the nature of action, MBh. 14, 1456.<BR> 3. Active, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्गः
कर्मरङ्ग कर्मरङ्ग, m. A plant, Averrhoa carambola, Lin., Rām. 3, 17, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवन्त्|कर्मवत्
कर्मवन्त् कर्मवन्त्, i. e. कर्मन् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Working, MBh. 3, 1263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्त|कर्मांत|कर्मान्तः|कर्म्मान्त|कर्म्मान्तः
कर्मान्त कर्मान्त, i. e. कर्मन्-अन्त, m.<BR> 1. Business, Rām. 5, 12, 39; Man. 8, 419 (public affairs).<BR> 2. Cultivated land, Man. 7, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तर|कर्मांतर|कर्म्मान्तर
कर्मान्तर कर्मान्तर, i. e. कर्मन्-अन्तर, n. A pause in the performance of sacred actions, Rām. 1, 13, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तिक|कर्मांतिक|कर्मान्तिकः|कर्म्मान्तिक
कर्मान्तिक कर्मान्तिक, i. e. कर्मान्त + इक, m. A workman, Rām. 1, 12, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मार|कर्मारः|कर्म्मार|कर्म्मारः
कर्मार कर्मार (base कर्मन्), m. A blacksmith, Man. 4, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिन्|कर्म्मिन्
कर्मिन् कर्मिन्, i. e. कर्मन् + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Attached to worldly action, Bhag. 6, 46.<BR> 2. When latter part of a compound word, the aff. इन् generally belongs to the whole compound, not to कर्मन् alone, e. g. अन्-आर्य-कर्मिन् is अनार्यकर्मन् + इन्, adj. Doing the work of an Anārya, Man. 10, 73.<BR> पाप-कर्मिन् is पापकर्मन् + इन्, m. A sinner, MBh. 18, 51.<BR> पुण्यवाग्बुद्धिकर्मिन्, is पुण्य-वाच्-बुद्धि-कर्मन् + इन्, adj. Pure in word, mind, and action, MBh. 17, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्
† कर्व् कर्व्, i. 1, Par. To be proud.<BR> --Cf. गर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वट|कर्वटः|कर्व्वट|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्वट कर्वट,<BR> I. m. and n. A market town, Yājñ. 2, 167.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a country or people, MBh. 2, 1098.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शन|कर्शनः
कर्शन कर्शन, i. e. कृश् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Causing to grow lean, Suśr. 1, 189, 1.<BR> II. m. Fire, MBh. 13, 6307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष कर्ष, i. e. कृष् + अ,<BR> I. m. Dragging, Yājñ. 2, 217.<BR> II. m. and n. A certain weight, equal to 16 māṣas, about 280 troy grains, Suśr. 2, 175, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक कर्षक, i. e. कृष् + अक, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b " target="_blank">Page0166-b + 43</a>] A cultivator, one who lives by tillage, Yājñ. 2, 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण कर्षण, i. e. कृष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Bringing, Śāk. 69, 15, v. r.<BR> 2. Tormenting, Man. 7, 112.<BR> 3. Bending (a bow), Ragh. 11, 46.<BR> 4. Tillage, Man. 4, 5.<BR> 5. Cultivated land, MBh. 3, 10082.<BR> 6. At the end of a compound adj. Overpowering, e. g. शत्रु-, Overpowering his enemies, Rām. 4, 38, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन् कर्षिन्, i. e. कृष् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Dragging, Mṛcch. 96, 6.<BR> 2. Attracting, Ragh. 19, 11.<BR> II. m. A cultivator, Kathās. 18, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षू
कर्षू कर्षू, i. e. कृष् + उ, f. A furrow, an incision, Suśr. 2, 33, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि क + र्हि (see किम्), adv. At what time; with following चिद्, At any time, Nal. 24, 22; with a negation, Never, e. g. न कर्हि चिद्, Man. 2, 4. With following अपि, Sometimes, Bhāg. P. 5, 17, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
† 1. कल् कल्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To count.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
2. कल् कल् (akin to कृ), 1. 10, in three forms, कलय, कलापय, and कालय, Par. (कालय Ātm. Rām. 4, 18, 28): कलय,<BR> 1. To impel, Kathās. 18, 90; कालय, to drive, MBh. 4, 1007, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 1.<BR> कलित, Incited by, Śiś. 9, 59; greedy of, Rām. 5, 83, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, कलय,<BR> 1. To shake, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a " target="_blank">Page0167-a + 42</a>] MBh. 1, 2853.<BR> 2. To catch, Śiś. 9, 72.<BR> 3. To fasten, Kathās. 20, 52; Śiś. 9, 45.<BR> 4. To surrender, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 2.<BR> 5. To regard, Prab. 5, 5.<BR> 6. To perceive, Hit. 38, 10.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, कलय, To enumerate one by one, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 10.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> I. कलय, To loosen, to deliver, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 26; उत्कलित,<BR> 1. Opened, Pañc. 184, 18 (where काल्˚ must be changed to कल्˚).<BR> 2. Joyful, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 34.<BR> II. कलापय, To beg for dismission, Pañc. 244, 25.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> I. कालय, To pursue, MBh. 15, 1060.<BR> II. कलय, To reckon, Śiś. 8, 9. To perceive, Naiṣ. 2, 54.<BR> --With प्र प्र, कालय,<BR> 1. To drive onwards, MBh. 1, 7178.<BR> 2. To pursue, 3, 10778.<BR> --With सम् सम्, कालय,<BR> 1. To drive, Hariv. 1191.<BR> 2. To put to flight, MBh. 4, 1981.<BR> --Cf. Lat. celer, cello, procella; κέλλω, ὀκέλλω, κέλης, κέλομαι, κελεύω, κολετράω; O.H.G. halôn, holôn, holên.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यकलित|धैर्य्यकलित
धैर्य- + कलित धैर्य- + कलित, adj. steady, calm.<BR> 2. कालय, To drive onwards, MBh. 1, 6690; to pursue, Rām. 4, 18, 28.<BR> 3. कालय, To provoke, Rām. 3, 41, 26.<BR> 4. etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलय
कलय कलय, To bear, Gīt. 1, 16.<BR> 5. To perform, Bhartṛ. 3, 20.<BR> 6. To put in, to fasten, Gīt. 12, 26.<BR> 7. To utter, Gīt. 11, 9.<BR> 8. To endow, Śiś. 9, 59.<BR> 9. To reckon, Bhartṛ. 2, 37.<BR> 10. To perceive, Śiś. 9, 83.<BR> 11. To consider, Śiś. 9, 58.<BR> 12. † To go: cf. उद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल कल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला,<BR> 1. Dumb (ved.).<BR> 2. Low, Brāhmaṇ. 3, 21; soft, Śāk. d. 85; Ṛt. 6, 29.<BR> कलम्, adv. Softly, Rām. 1, 19, 10.<BR> 3. Indistinct, confused, Megh. 31.<BR> 4. Uttering a low sound, Vikr. d. 119.<BR> II. m. A kind of Pitṛs or Manes, MBh. 2, 463.<BR> III. Often in compound words after अश्रु and वाष्प, adj. Indistinct on account of tears, Rām. 2, 106, 33; 2, 34, 53.<BR> वाष्प-कल + म्, adv. MBh. 3, 10839.<BR> वाष्प-कला, f. A torrent of tears, Bhāg. P. 3, 22, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकल|मदकलः
मद- + कल मद- + कल, 1. adj. speaking like a drunken person. 2. m. an elephant in rut; see कला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकल|कलकलः
कलकल कल-कल, m.<BR> 1. A confused noise, Rām. 3, 34, 34.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10378.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्क|कलंक|कलंकः|कलङ्कः
कलङ्क कलङ्क (probably an anomalous [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b " target="_blank">Page0167-b + 41</a>] compound, कल-अङ्क), m.<BR> 1. A spot, Rām. 6, 86, 42.<BR> 2. The rust of iron, Ragh. 13, 15.<BR> 3. Defamation, Pañc. 46, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. काल; κελαινός, κηλίς, κηλάς; Lat. cāligo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकलङ्क|हरिणकलंक|हरिणकलङ्कः
हरिण- + कलङ्क हरिण- + कलङ्क, m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कय
कलङ्कय कलङ्कय, a denom. derived from the last, Par. To disgrace, Daśak. 124, 1.<BR> कलङ्कित,<BR> 1. Painted, Bhartṛ. 1, 9.<BR> 2. Disgraced, Kathās. 12, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्र|कलत्रं
कलत्र कलत्र, n. A wife, Bhartṛ. 2, 58.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलत्र
स- + कलत्र स- + कलत्र, adj. with his wife, Pañc. 46, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्रवन्त्|कलत्रवत्
कलत्रवन्त् कलत्र + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Having a wife, Mṛcch. 67, 3.<BR> 2. With his wives, Rājat. 5, 427.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्रिन्
कलत्रिन् कलत्रिन्, i. e. कलत्र + इन्, adj. Having a wife.<BR> वसुमत्या नृपाः कलत्रिणः, Kings are wedded to the earth, i. e. the earth is the wife of kings, Ragh. 8, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौत|कलधौतं
कलधौत कल-धौत,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Gold, Gīt. 8, 4.<BR> 2. Silver, Śiś. 4, 41.<BR> II. adj. Golden, Rām. 3, 60, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन कलन (cf. कलङ्क),<BR> I. n. A spot, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 2.<BR> II. f. ना, Subjection, Ānandal. 29.<BR> III. As latter part of a comp., Bhartṛ. 3, 72, causing, perhaps to be corrected to करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभ|कलभः
कलभ कलभ (cf. करभ), m.<BR> 1. A young elephant, Pañc. 159, 16.<BR> 2. A young camel, Pañc. 229, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम|कलमः
कलम कलम, m. A kind of rice Rām. 5, 74, 11.<BR> --Cf. κάλαμος; Lat. calamus; O.H.G. halm; A.S. haelme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविंकः|कलविङ्कः
कलविङ्क कलविङ्क, m. A sparrow, Man. 5, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलश|कलशः
कलश कलश, or कलस कलस,<BR> I. m. (and f. शी, and n.), A water-pot, a cup, Pañc. 252, 10; i. d. 225; designation [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a " target="_blank">Page0168-a + 44</a>] of the ocean when churned, MBh. 1, 1149.<BR> II. f. शी,<BR> 1. A plant, Hemionitis cordifolia, Roxb., Suśr. 1, 139, 15.<BR> 2. The name of a holy place, MBh. 3, 650.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलह|कलहं|कलहः
कलह कलह, m. and n. Quarrel, MBh. 2, 1780.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कलह|वाक्कलहः
वाक्कलह वाक्कलह, i. e. वाच्-, m. a contest about words, Prab. 55, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्ककलह|शुष्ककलहः
शुष्क- + कलह शुष्क- + कलह, m. a quarrel about trifles, Pañc. 171, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलह
स- + कलह स- + कलह, adj. quarreling, Kir. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहंस|कलहंसः
कलहंस कल-हंस, m., f. सी, A kind of duck or goose, Rām. 2, 82, 9; Kir. 5, 13; Ragh. 8, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहाय
कलहाय कलहाय, a denom. derived from कलह by य, To quarrel, Pañc. 207, 22 (Par.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कला
कला कला, i. e. कॄ + अ, f.<BR> 1. A small part, Man. 8, 36.<BR> 2. A part, Man. 2, 86.<BR> 3. The sixteenth part of the moon's disc, Hit. pr. d. 1.<BR> 4. Interest on capital, Śiś. 9, 32 (at the same time, a sixteenth part of the moon's disc).<BR> 5. A division of time, Man. 1, 64.<BR> 6. One of the seven elements of the human body, as blood, etc., Suśr. 1, 326, 13.<BR> 7. One of the sixty-four mechanical or elegant arts, Rām. 1, 9, 8; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 7; 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निष्कल निष्कल, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ला, 1. undivided, MBh. 13, 1044. 2. maimed, infirm, MBh. 3, 13851.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
स-कल स-कल, adj. f. ला, 1. whole, Vikr. d. 95. 2. all, Pañc. 53, 21; 55, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाप|कलापः
कलाप कला-प (vb. 2. पा), m.<BR> 1. A bundle, MBh. 3, 10772.<BR> 2. A string, Kumāras. 1, 43 (of pearls).<BR> 3. A band (of belts, laces, etc., worn by women round the waist). Ṛt. 3, 20; Bhartṛ. 1, 56.<BR> 4. Totality, Bhāg. P. 9, 4, 21; perfection, Pañc. v. d. 23.<BR> 5. A quiver, MBh. 3, 11454.<BR> 6. A peacock's tail, Pañc. ii. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापक|कलापकं|कलापकः
कलापक कलाप + क, m.<BR> 1. A string, MBh. 3, 10055.<BR> 2. A band, Śiś. 9, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापवन्त्
कलापवन्त् कलाप + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, MBh. 1, 1957 in ततायुध-, i. e. तत-आयुध- (vb. तन्), the aff. वन्त् belongs to the whole comp., Wearing a strung bow and a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापशस्
कलापशस् कलाप + शस्, adv. (Made) into bundles, MBh. 13, 4509.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापिन्
कलापिन् कलापिन्, i. e. कलाप + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Wearing a quiver, MBh. 4, 141 (the aff. इन् belongs to the whole comp.).<BR> 2. With its tail spread out, MBh. 3, 11585 (a peacock).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A peacock, Pañc. ii. d. 85.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाभृत्
कलाभृत् कला-भृ + त्, m. An artist, Man. 2, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाय|कलायः
कलाय कलाय, m.<BR> 1. Peas, MBh. 13, 5469.<BR> 2. An unknown plant, Śiś. 13, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलावन्त्|कलावत्
कलावन्त् कला + वन्त्,<BR> I. m. The moon, Kumāras. 5, 71.<BR> II. f. वती, A proper name, Kathās. 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलि|कलिः
कलि कलि, i. e. कॄ + इ, m.<BR> 1. A die (ved.).<BR> 2. The game at dice personified, Nal. 6, 14.<BR> 3. The fourth age of the world, Man. 9, 302.<BR> 4. Quarrel, MBh. 3, 12282; Hit. iii. d. 47.<BR> 5. A very wicked king, MBh. 12, 361; 363.<BR> 6. The name of an inferior deity, MBh. 1, 2552.<BR> 7. A proper name, Chr. 297, 15 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका कलिका, i. e. कला + क, f.<BR> 1. The sixteenth part of the moon's disc, Bhartṛ. 3, 1.<BR> 2. A bud, Ṛt. 6, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्ग|कलिंग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिङ्ग कलिङ्ग, m. pl. The name of a people and their country, Rām. 2, 71, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्द|कलिंद|कलिंदः|कलिन्दः
कलिन्द कलिन्द,<BR> I. m. The name of a mountain, on which the Yamunā rises, Gīt. 3, 2; Rām. 2, 71, 6.<BR> II. f. कलिन्दी, Rām. 2, 55, 4; 12; 13; it must be corrected to काल्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिल|कलिलः
कलिल कलिल (vb. कॄ)<BR> I. adj., f. ला, Filled, MBh. 1, 3717.<BR> II. n. Confusion, Bhag. 2, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुष|कलुषं|कलुषः
कलुष कलुष (cf. कलङ्क and कल्मष),<BR> I. adj., f. षा.<BR> 1. Turbid, Vikr. d. 8.<BR> 2. Impure, Man. 10, 57.<BR> 3. Choked, Śāk. d. 81.<BR> 4. Unable, Ragh. 5, 64.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Dirt, Ṛt. 3, 22.<BR> 2. Impurity, Rām. 2, 97, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषाय
कलुषाय कलुषाय, a denom. derived from the last by य, Ātm. To become turbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवर|कलेवरं|कलेवरः
कलेवर कलेवर, n. The body, Bhag. 8, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कलेवर
दुष्कलेवर दुष्क˚, i. e. दुस्-, n. the vile body, Bhāg. P. 5, 19, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क कल्क, m. (and n.)<BR> 1. Sediment, Yājñ. 1, 276.<BR> 2. Paste, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13.<BR> 3. Foulness, MBh. 1, 268.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकल्क|तिलकल्कः
