कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य कल्य (i. e. कृ + य, cf. कल्याण, of which the lingual ण् proves that the original form was कर्याण, cf. also καιρός)<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Healthy, MBh. 2, 1974.<BR> 2. Ready, MBh. 1, 865.<BR> II. n. Dawn, MBh. 1, 6304.<BR> III. कल्य + म्, adv. At break of day, MBh. 1, 6304.<BR> कल्यम्-कल्यम्, Every morning, Rām. 4, 44, 112.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकल्यम्
अति-कल्यम् अति-कल्यम्, adv. too early in the morning, Man. 4, 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यपाल|कल्यपालः
कल्यपाल कल्यपाल, see कल्प-पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यवर्त|कल्यवर्तः|कल्यवर्त्त|कल्यवर्त्तः
कल्यवर्त कल्यवर्त, m.<BR> 1. कल्य-वृत् + अ, Breakfast.<BR> 2. A trifle, Mṛcch. 34, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण कल्याण (cf. कल्य),<BR> I. adj., f. (ना, and) णी.<BR> 1. Prosperous, Nal. 12, 92.<BR> 2. Blessed, Man. 8, 91; Nal. 8, 10.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Prosperity, welfare, Man. 3, 60.<BR> 2. A virtuous action, Rām. 2, 54, 29.<BR> 3. An entertainment, Man. 8, 392.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

