कल्लोलिनी
कल्लोलिनी कल्लोलिनी, i. e. कल्लोल + इन् + ई, f. A river, Prab. 73, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हण
कल्हण कल्हण, m. The name of the author of the Rājatarangiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्
† कव् कव्, see कब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
कवऽ कव-, i. e. क-व (cf. किम् and क्व). Former part of comp. words, denoting inferiority, cf. कवोष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवक|कवकं|कवकः
कवक कवक, n. A mushroom, Man. 5, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवच|कवचं|कवचः
कवच कवच, m. and n. Mail, Rām. 3, 50, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकवच|नारीकवचः
नारी- + कवच नारी- + कवच, adj. having wives as a coat of mail, protected by wives, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातकवच|निवातकवचः
निवात- + कवच निवात- + कवच, (wearing an impenetrable coat of mail), m. a class of demons, Arj. 5, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकवच
स- + कवच स- + कवच, adj. clad in armour, mailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचिन्
कवचिन् कवचिन्, i. e. कवच + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Mailed, Rām. 3, 56, 30.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 1, 2738.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवन्ध
कवन्ध कवन्ध, see कबन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कवर कवर, m., f. री, and n. A braid of hair, Amar. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभृत्
कवरीभृत् कवरी-भृ + त्, in नव-चन्द्रिका-कुसुम-तमः-हव्˚, adj. Wearing darkness (i. e. black) like a braid of hair, adorned with the young moon as with fresh flowers, Śiś. 9, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवल|कवलं|कवलः
कवल कवल (cf. कवि, iii.), m.<BR> 1. A mouthful, Bhartṛ. 2, 22; a morsel, Rām. 2, 41, 9.<BR> 2. Water for rinsing the mouth, Suśr. 1, 39, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित कवलित, i. e. कवल + इत, adj. Devoured, Pañc. 213, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट कवाट, टी = कपाट, ती, q. cf., Rām. 2, 71, 34 (and at the end of a comp. adj. कवाटक, Kathās. 19, 24).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि कवि, i. e. कू + इ,<BR> I. adj. Wise (ved.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A wise man, Man. 7, 49.<BR> 2. A poet, Rājat. 5, 203.<BR> 3. A proper name, MBh. 13, 4123.<BR> III. f. The bit of a bridle, Rām. 1, 53, 18 (cf. कवल).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κοας in εὐρυκόας Λαο-κόων, i. e. Λαϝο-κόϝων, and कू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकवि
सु- + कवि सु- + कवि, m. an excellent [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a " target="_blank">Page0171-a + 39</a>] poet, Rājat. 5, 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविता
कविता कवि + ता, f. Poetry, Rām. Pr. 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकविता
सु- + कविता सु- + कविता, f. excellent poetical talent, Bhartṛ. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवित्व
कवित्व कवि + त्व, n. Poetic art, Lass. 5, 18; pl. Daśak. 196, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
कवोष्ण कवोष्ण, i. e. कव-उष्ण, adj. Slightly warm, Ragh. 1, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्य|कव्यं|कव्यः
कव्य कव्य, i. e. कवि + य, n. An oblation to deceased ancestors (the wise men of old), Man. 1, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्
† कश् कश्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --Cf. कंस्, कस्, छष् and शश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश|कशः
कश कश, m., and f. आ, A whip, MBh. 3, 13268; 13272; also कषा कष, Rām. 3, 30, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु कशिपु, m. and n. A cushion, Bhāg. P. 2, 2, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपु|हिरण्यकशिपुः
हिरण्य- + कशिपु हिरण्य- + कशिपु, m. a Daitya, or demon, slain by Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशेरु कशेरु; also कसेरु कसेरु, m. and f. (रू) and n. A kind of grass, Suśr. 1, 377, 18; 2, 223, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुक|कशेरुकं|कशेरुकः
कशेरुक कशेरु + क; also कसेरुक कसेरुक, m., and f. (का) and n. A kind of grass, Suśr. 1, 156, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशोजू
कशोजू कशोजू, i. e. कशस्-जू, adj. Hastening to the water (passing a river?), Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल कश्मल,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. Fainting, Chr. 31, 15; 35, 4.<BR> 2. Pusillanimity, MBh. 1, 2060.<BR> 3. Weakness, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 15.<BR> II. adj., f. ला, Dirty, Lass. 75, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीर|कश्मीरः
कश्मीर कश्मीर, m. The name of a country, Cashmere, Rājat. 1, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यप|कश्यपः
कश्यप कश्यप, m. The name of a Muni, or sage, Man. 9, 129.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकश्यप|भूकश्यपः
भू- + कश्यप भू- + कश्यप, m. a name of Vasudeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्
कष् कष् (probably a dialectical form of कर्ष्, vb. कृष्).<BR> 1. i. 1, Par., Ātm. To scratch, to itch, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 13 (कषाण, anomalous, or ii. 2).<BR> 2. i. 1, Par. To injure, to destroy, Prab. 90, 3.<BR> --Cf. छष्, व्रूस्, and शश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष कष् + अ, m. The touch-stone, Mṛcch. 48, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण कषण, i. e. कष् + अन, n. Rubbing, Kir. 5, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषा
कषा कषा, see कश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाय|कषायः
कषाय कषाय (probably vb. कृष्),<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Being of an astringent taste, MBh. 14, 1411.<BR> 2. Fragrant, Megh. 32.<BR> 3. Red, subst. m. and n., red colour, Yājñ. 1, 272; MBh. 14, 1263; of a colour composed of red and yellow, Mṛcch. 113, 3.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. An astringent juice, Man. 11, 153.<BR> 2. A decoction, Suśr. 2, 175, 9.<BR> 3. Ointment, MBh. 13, 5970.<BR> 4. Dirt, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 45; impurity, 4, 22, 20.<BR> 5. Stupor, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्कषाय
अ-निष्कषाय अ-निष्कषाय, i. e. अ-निस्-, adj. full of impure passions, MBh. 12, 568.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायित
कषायित कषायित, i. e. कषाय + इत, adj. Coloured. Prab. 102, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्ट|कष्टं|कष्टः
कष्ट कष्ट, i. e. कष् + त,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bad, Rām. 3, 51, 23; comparat. worse, Man. 7, 53.<BR> 2. Miserable, Bhartṛ. 2, 22.<BR> 3. Heavy, Yājñ. 3, 29.<BR> 4. Severe, Man. 12, 78.<BR> 5. Dangerous, Man. 7, 186; 210.<BR> 6. Pernicious, Man. 7, 50.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A blameable action, Rām. 1, 2, 32.<BR> 2. Misfortune, Hit. 72, 15.<BR> 3. Misery, Pañc. 123, 22. Acc. कष्टम्, adv. Woe! Rām. 3, 79, 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकष्ट
अधि- + कष्ट अधि- + कष्ट, n. excessive misery, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्
कस् कस् (or कश् कश्), i. 1, Par. To go, Nal. 2, 2.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, Caus. To turn out, Pañc. 127, 16 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a " target="_blank">Page0172-a + 39</a>] (with श् instead of स्); 224, 5.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. दन्त-निष्काशित, Hit. 91, 16, showing his teeth (perhaps from काश्, q. cf.).<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To cause to open, Ghaṭ. 19.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To burst, Suśr. 1, 247, 12.<BR> 2. To open as a flower, Mālat. 15, 3.<BR> 3. To rejoice, Bhartṛ. 2, 71.<BR> --Caus. To cause to blow, Bhartṛ. 2, 65 (श् for स्).<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि, To blossom, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 17.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To blow, Śiś. 11, 63.<BR> --Cf. कंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरु|कसेरुः
कसेरु कसेरु, and कसेरुक कसेरुक, see कशेरु and कशेरुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिका
कस्तूरिका कस्तूरिका, and कस्तूरी कस्तूरी, f. Musk, Pañc. 47, 8; Śṛṅgārat. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्मात्
कस्मात् कस्मात् (abl. sing. n. of किम्), adv. Why, on what account, Rām. 1, 9, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकस्मात्
अ- + कस्मात् अ- + कस्मात्, adv. 1. without a cause, Hit. i. d. 102. 2. instantly, Hit. 18, 2. 3. Suddenly, Sāv. 6, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्लार|कह्लारं
कह्लार कह्लार, n. The white esculent water-lily, Ṛt. 3, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

का
काऽ का- (see किम्), former part of comp. words, Bad.<BR> --Cf. e. g. कापथ, कापुरुष, क्ôष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्
† कांस् कांस् = काश्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्य|कांस्यं|कांस्यः
कांस्य कांस्य, i. e. कंस + य,<BR> I. adj. Made of brass, Man. 4, 65.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Brass, Man. 5, 114.<BR> 2. A drinking vessel, MBh. 2, 1751.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक|काकं|काकः
काक काक (onomatop.),<BR> I. m., A crow, Man. 7, 21.<BR> II. f. की.<BR> 1. A female crow, Pañc. 52, 23.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 3, 14396.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकाक|भूकाकः
भू- + काक भू- + काक, m. a small kind of heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीय
काकतालीय काकतालीय, i. e. काक-ताल + ईय, adj. literally, Resembling [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b " target="_blank">Page0172-b + 40</a>] the crow and the palmyra tree, an unknown fable, and denoting,<BR> 1. Inconsiderate, Rām. 3, 45, 17.<BR> ˚यम्, adv. By accident, MBh. 12, 6596.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीयवत्
काकतालीयवत् काकतालीय + वत्, adv. By accident, Hit. Pr. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरुक काकरुक (perhaps काक-रु + क), and काकरूक काकरूक, adj., f. का, Timid, Pañc. 9, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलि|काकलिः
काकलि and काकली काकली̆ (cf. कल), f.<BR> 1. A soft sound, Ṛt. 1, 8; Bhartṛ. 1, 35.<BR> 2. काकली, A dog-whistle, used for trying whether one be asleep or awake, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाण्डक
काकाण्डक काकाण्डक, i. e. काक-अण्ड + क, The name of an unknown plant, MBh. 3, 12880.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणी
काकिणी काकिणी, and काकिनी काकिनी (perhaps काक + इन् + ई), f. A small coin, a quarter of a Paṇa, Pañc. ii. d. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकु|काकुः
काकु काकु, f. Change of voice in fear, grief, etc.; Vikr. d. 42, अस्माकम्...प्रतिदिनम् इयम्...सेवाकाकुपरिणतिर् अभूत्, My lot is to be obliged by my office to use every day another voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थ|काकुत्स्थः
काकुत्स्थ काकुत्स्थ, i. e. ककुत्स्थ + अ, patron. A descendant of Kakutstha, Rām. 1, 23, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोल|काकोलं|काकोलः
काकोल काकोल (cf. काक),<BR> I. m. A raven, Man. 5, 14.<BR> II. n. A division of the infernal regions, or hell, Yājñ. 3, 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोलूकीय
काकोलूकीय काकोलूकीय, i. e. काक-उलूक + ईय, n. The war of the crows and owls, Pañc. 148, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवत
काक्षीवत काक्षीवत, i. e. कक्षीवन्त् + अ, patron., f. ती, A descendant of Kakṣīvant, MBh. 1, 4695.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवन्त्|काक्षीवत्
काक्षीवन्त् काक्षीवन्त् = कक्षीवन्त्, MBh. 1, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्ष्|कांक्ष्
काङ्क्ष् काङ्क्ष् (an old desider. of कम्, *कङ्कंस्, by intermediate कङ्कस्), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 13, 769).<BR> 1. To wish, Bhag. 12, 17.<BR> 2. To desire, Rām. 4, 17, 18.<BR> 3. To wait for, MBh. 3, 414.<BR> 4. To attend to (with the dat.), Rām. 2, 25, 43.<BR> काङ्क्षित, n. Desire, Rām. 5, 29, 9.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To desire, MBh. 2, 2135 (Ātm.).<BR> --With अभि अभि, To desire, Rām. 2, 49, 15.<BR> --Caus. To desire, MBh. 3, 12457.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To desire, MBh. 1, 4286.<BR> 2. To strive for, Yājñ. 1, 153.<BR> 3. To seek (with the gen.), Man. 2, 162.<BR> 4. To turn towards, Man. 3, 258.<BR> 5. To want, Man. 10, 121.<BR> 6. To expect, Rām. 2, 5, 19.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To expect, MBh. 12, 4870 (Ātm.); to wait for, 4, 734 (Ātm.).<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To desire, MBh. 4, 1664.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To desire, Suśr. 1, 52, 6.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To long for, Rām. 2, 112, 12 (Ātm.).<BR> --With वि वि, To intend, Hariv. 13136.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Goth. huhru; A.S. hungor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षा|कांक्षा
काङ्क्षा काङ्क्ष् + आ, f. Desire, Nal. 16, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षिता
काङ्क्षिता काङ्क्षिता, i. e. काङ्क्षिन् + ता, f. Desire, Rām. 2, 34, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षिन्|कांक्षिन्
काङ्क्षिन् काङ्क्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Desiring (with acc.), Rām. 2, 110, 20.<BR> 2. Expecting, Rām. 5, 33, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच काच, m.<BR> 1. Glass, Pañc. i. d. 87.<BR> 2. A disease of the eyes, Suśr. 2, 305, 4 sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्च्|कांच्
† काञ्च् काञ्च्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To shine.<BR> 2. To bind.<BR> --Cf. कच्क्, कञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चन|कांचन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
काञ्चन काञ्चन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Gold. Man. 2, 239.<BR> 2. Wealth, Bhartṛ. 2, 33.<BR> II. adj., f. नी, Golden, Man. 5, 112; Rām. 3, 52, 21.<BR> III. m. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 15, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनमय
काञ्चनमय काञ्चन + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Pañc. 236, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनवर्मन्
काञ्चनवर्मन् काञ्चन-वर्मन्, m. A substitute for the proper name Hiranyavarman, Chr. 53, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनीय|कांचनीय
काञ्चनीय काञ्चनीय, i. e. काञ्चन + ईय, adj., f. या, Golden, MBh. 13, 5039.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चि|कांचि|कांचिः|काञ्चिः
काञ्चि काञ्चि, m. pl.<BR> 1. The name of a people, MBh. 1, 6684.<BR> 2. see काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्ची|कांची
काञ्ची काञ्ची, f. A woman's zone or girdle, usually adorned by small bells, Rām. 5, 10, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकरावलम्बनविमुक्तगलत्कलकाञ्चि
स्व-कर-अवलम्बन-वि-मुक्त-गलत्-कल-काञ्चि स्व-कर-अवलम्बन-वि-मुक्त-गलत्-कल-काञ्चि, adv. so that her girdle fell down with a sound when loosened by his taking hold of it with his hand, Śiś. 9, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जिक|कांजिक|कांजिकं|काञ्जिकं
काञ्जिक काञ्जिक, n. Sour gruel, Suśr. 1, 34, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन्य|काठिन्यं
काठिन्य काठिन्य, i. e. कठिन + य, n.<BR> 1. Hardness, Śāk. d. 58.<BR> 2. Firmness, Rājat. 5, 440.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण|काणः
काण काण (probably a syncope of एक-अक्स्हन् + अ by intermediate काक्ष्ण; cf. Lat. cocles, i. e. *coclo + vit, see शष्प), adj., f. णा.<BR> 1. One-eyed, monoculous, Man. 3, 155.<BR> 2. Perforated, Pañc. ii. d. 74.<BR> 3. Blind, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 20; Hit. Pr. d. 11; Bhartṛ. 3, 5 (used of a worn-out coin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेलीमातृ
काणेलीमातृ काणेली-मातृ, m. An abusive word; according to glosses: A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a " target="_blank">Page0174-a + 43</a>] son of an unmarried woman, Mṛcch. 14, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः|काण्डः
काण्ड काण्ड, m. and n.<BR> 1. The part of a plant from one joint to another (ved.).<BR> 2. A slip, Man. 1, 46.<BR> 3. A stalk, Rām. 2, 91, 15.<BR> 4. A switch, Rām. 2, 89, 19 (97, 24 Gorr.).<BR> 5. An arrow, Hit. 85, 5.<BR> 6. The section of a book, Bhāg. P. 4, 24, 9; Rām. (title of the first, of the second book, etc.); e. g. आरण्यक-, The section comprising the sojourn in the forest (title of the third book).<BR> 7. A bone, Suśr. 2, 31, 5.<BR> 8. A multitude, Mālav. d. 43; Rām. 1, 30, 15 (corr. काण्ड for कण्ड).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्ड|अकांड
अ- + काण्ड अ- + काण्ड, adj., f. डा. 1. unjust, Rājat. 4, 655. 2. sudden, Hit. iv. d. 82; loc. डे, suddenly, Śāk. d. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाकाण्ड
जङ्घा- + काण्ड जङ्घा- + काण्ड, a stalk-like leg, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकाण्ड
दन्त- + काण्ड दन्त- + काण्ड, a stemlike tusk, 188, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर कातर, i. e. कतर + अ (properly, irresolute), adj., f. रा, Timid, Rām. 4, 9, 103; disheartened, Śāk. 56, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकातर
अ- + कातर अ- + कातर, adj. resolute, courageous, Rām. 3, 19, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकातर
स- + कातर स- + कातर, adj. cowardly, Nal. 13, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरता
कातरता कातर + ता, f., and कातरत्व कातर + त्व, n. Fear, Śāk. d. 59; Pañc. 216, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर्य|कातर्यं
कातर्य कातर्य, i. e. कातर + य, n. Fear, Rām. 4, 9, 100; apprehension (care), Ragh. 17, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायन|कात्यायनः
कात्यायन कात्यायन, i. e. कति, or कात्य + आयन,<BR> I. patron., f. नी, A descendant of कति or कात्य, used as proper name, Rām. 2, 67, 2.<BR> II. f. नी, A name of Durgā, Dev. 8, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः|कादम्बः
कादम्ब कादम्ब,<BR> I. m. A kind of goose, Rām. 3, 78, 27.<BR> II. i. e. कदम्ब + अ, n. The flower of the Nauclea cadamba, Roxb., Ragh. 13, 27.<BR> --Cf. perhaps, Lat. columba; κόλυμβος; O.H.G. tûba; A.S. dûua.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरी|कादंबरी
कादम्बरी कादम्बरी (for कादम्ब-वारि), f.<BR> 1. The rain-water which collects in the hollow of the tree Nauclea cadamba when the flowers are in perfection, and which is supposed to be impregnated with their honey, Hariv. 5417.<BR> 2. A spirituous liquor, Śāk. 76, 6 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 3. A proper name, Sāh. D. 79, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काद्रवेय|काद्रवेयः
काद्रवेय काद्रवेय, i. e. कद्रू + एय, metron. m. A serpent, MBh. 1, 2549.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानक|कानकं
कानक कानक, i. e. कनक + अ, adj. Golden, Suśr. 1, 99, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानन|काननं
कानन कानन, n.<BR> 1. A forest, Hiḍ. 1, 42.<BR> 2. A grove, Rām. 3, 68, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडाकानन
क्रीडा- + कानन क्रीडा- + कानन, n. a grove, Bhartṛ. 3, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकानन|मणिकाननं
मणि- + कानन मणि- + कानन, n. 1. a wood abounding in jewels. 2. the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीन|कानीनः
कानीन कानीन, i. e. कनीन (ved. young) + अ (cf. कन्या), adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. A son, a daughter, of an unmarried woman, Man. 9, 172.<BR> 2. Serviceable for the pupil of the eye, Suśr. 2, 353, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तक
कान्तक कान्त + क (see कम्), m. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तत्व
कान्तत्व कान्त + त्व (vb. कम्), n. Charm, grace, MBh. 3, 14437.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताय
कान्ताय कान्ताय, a denominative derived from कान्त (vb. कम्) by य, Ātm. To play the lover, Bhartṛ. 1, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः|कान्तारः
कान्तार कान्तार, m. and n.<BR> 1. A large forest, Rām. 2, 28, 6.<BR> 2. Wilderness, Rām. 4, 44, 27.<BR> 3. A difficult road, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारक|कांतारकः|कान्तारकः
कान्तारक कान्तार + क, m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ति|कांति|कांतिः|कान्तिः
कान्ति कान्ति, i. e. कम् + ति, f. Beauty, Indr. 5, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यकान्ति|सूर्यकांति|सूर्यकान्तिः|सूर्य्यकान्ति|सूर्य्यकान्तिः
सूर्य- + कान्ति सूर्य- + कान्ति, f. 1. sunshine. 2. the flower of the sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिमत्ता
कान्तिमत्ता कान्तिमत्ता, i. e. कान्तिमन्त् + ता, f. Beauty, Kumāras. 4, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिमन्त्|कान्तिमत्|कांतिमत्
कान्तिमन्त् कान्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Beautiful, Rām. 4, 44, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांदिश्
कांदिश् कांदिश्, i. e. काम् (acc. sing. f. of किम्) -दिश् (based on an acc. कां दिशम्, literally ‘to what quarter’), adj. Fugitive, MBh. 12, 6320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांदिशीक|कान्दिशीक|कान्दिशीकः
कांदिशीक कांदिश् + ईक, adj. Fugitive, Śukas. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुब्ज|कान्यकुब्जं|कान्यकुब्जः
कान्यकुब्ज कान्यकुब्ज, i. e. कन्यकुब्ज + अ, n. The name of a city, the modern Canouj, Pañc. 244, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथ|कापथः
कापथ का-पथ, m. A bad road, Rām. 2, 108, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल कापाल, i. e. कपाल + अ, adj. Made of skulls, Rām. 1, 56, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापालिक कापालिक, i. e. कपाल + इक,<BR> 1. m. A follower of a certain Śaiva sect, Bhartṛ. 1, 64.<BR> II. adj. Practised by a Kāpalika, Prab. 57, 12.<BR> --Cf. कपालिक 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिन्
कापालिन् कापालिन्, m.<BR> 1. = कपालिन्<BR> III. MBh. 13, 1217 (perhaps with lengthened अ on account of the metre).<BR> 2. A proper name, Hariv. 9196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल कापिल, i. e. कपिल + अ, adj. Referring or peculiar to Kapila, Rām. 1, 41, 3; MBh. 12, 12218.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिलेय
कापिलेय कापिलेय, i. e. कपिल + एय, m. A descendant of Kapila, MBh. 12, 7886.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायन|कापिशायनं
कापिशायन कापिशायन, n. A spirituous liquor, Śiś. 10, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष का-पुरुष,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A contemptible man, Pañc. i. d. 21.<BR> 2. A coward Rām. 6, 89, 5.<BR> II. adj. Cowardly, Rām. 6, 88, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय कापेय, i. e. कपि + एय, adj., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b " target="_blank">Page0175-b + 45</a>] f. यी, Peculiar to monkeys, Rām. 6, 111, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत कापोत, i. e. कपोत + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती, peculiar to pigeons, MBh. 3, 15408.<BR> II. f. ती, The name of a plant, Suśr. 2, 173, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम|कामं|कामः
काम काम, i. e. कम् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Wish, Rām. 2, 90, 23.<BR> 2. Desire, Indr. 5, 61.<BR> 3. Love, Man. 2, 94; 214.<BR> 4. Intention, Man. 9, 248.<BR> 5. A desired object, Man. 9, 304.<BR> 6. The god of love, Indr. 5, 49.<BR> II. acc. कामम्, adv.<BR> 1. At one's pleasure, Man. 2, 189.<BR> 2. Willingly, MBh. 3, 298; Ragh. 12, 75.<BR> 3. With following न, Rather than, Hit. i. d. 125; Man. 9, 89.<BR> 4. Indeed, Śāk. 26, 16.<BR> 5. Only, Rām. 5, 94, 21.<BR> III. When the latter part of a comp. adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Desiring, Man. 2, 37.<BR> 2. Loving, Rām. 3, 55, 29.<BR> 3. An infin. ending in तुम् drops its final before it; cf. कर्तुकाम.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाम
अ- + काम अ- + काम, adj., f. मा, exempt from desire, Man. 2, 4.<BR> 2. unwilling, without one's consent, Man. 8, 364.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थ- + काम अर्थ- + काम,<BR> I. m. du. wealth and pleasure, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 24.<BR> II. adj. desiring wealth, Nal. 17, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काम
निष्काम निष्काम, i. e. निस्-, adj. disinterested, Man. 12, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्काम
पुंस्- + काम पुंस्- + काम, adj., f. मा, wishing for a lover or husband, Hiḍ. 3, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकाम
प्रिय- + काम प्रिय- + काम, adj. benevolent, Brāhmaṇ. 2, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुकाम
बन्धु- + काम बन्धु- + काम, adj. one who loves his kinsmen, Brāhmaṇ. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकामम्
यथा-काम + म् यथा-काम + म्, adv. at pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतकाम
वीत- + काम वीत- + काम, i. e. वि-इत-, adj. free from desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाम|सकामः
स- + काम स- + काम,<BR> I. adj. 1. one who has attained his desire, Rām. 3, 52, 52. 2. being in love, Ṛt. 6, 2.<BR> II. -मम्, adv. 1. with pleasure, Pañc. 44, 9. 2. indeed, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 4 (for aught I care).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नकाम
स्वप्न- + काम स्वप्न- + काम, adj. wishing to sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम
हित- + काम हित- + काम, adj., wishing well to, friendly to, Pañc. i. d. 360.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकार|कामकारः
कामकार काम-कार, m. Free will, Rām. 3, 66, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकारतस्
कामकारतस् कामकार + तस्, adv. Voluntarily, Man. 11, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामग
कामग काम-ग (vb. गम्),<BR> I. adj., f. गा,<BR> 1. Coming by one's own free will, Nal. 18, 23.<BR> 2. Going as one lists, Rām. 3, 48, 5.<BR> II. f. गा, A lascivious woman, Yājñ. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगम
कामगम काम-गम् + अ, adj., f. मा, Going as one lists, Rām. 5, 13, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वकामगम
सर्व- + कामगम सर्व- + कामगम, yielding every desired object, MBh. 13, 357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचर
कामचर काम-चर् + अ, adj. One who comes by his own free will. MBh. 4, 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचरत्व
