कालिन्द|कालिंद
कालिन्द कालिन्द, i. e. कलिन्द + अ,<BR> I. n. A water melon, Suśr. 1, 156, 21.<BR> II. f. दी.<BR> 1. A proper name, Rām. 1, 70, 33.<BR> 2. The Yamunā, Pañc. 25, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकालिन्दी
यम-कालिन्दी यम-कालिन्दी, f. The wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन् कालिमन्, i. e. 2. काल + इमन्, m. Blackness, Śiś. 4, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
कालिय कालिय, i. e. 2. काल + इय, m. The name of a Nāga, MBh. 1, 1551.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
ऽकालीन -कालीन, i. e. 1. काल + ईन, latter part of compound words derived from nouns ending in काल, adj. Referring to the time of, e. g. उत्पत्तिकालीन, i. e. उत्पत्ति-काल + ईन, adj. At the time of production, Bhāṣāp. 77.<BR> समान-, adj. Occurring or produced at the same period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
कालीय कालीय, i. e. 2. काल + ईय, n. A dark kind of sandal, Suśr. 2, 120, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयक|कालीयकं|कालीयकः
कालीयक कालीय + क,<BR> I. n. A dark kind of sandal, Rām. 6, 96, 3.<BR> II. m. The name of a Nāga, MBh. 1, 1555.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालुष्य|कालुष्यं
कालुष्य कालुष्य, i. e. कलुष + य, n.<BR> 1. Foulness, Kathās. 19, 95.<BR> 2. Unfairness, Rājat. 5, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
कालेय कालेय, i. e. 2. काल + एय,<BR> I. n. A dark kind of sandal, Kumāras. 7, 9.<BR> II. m. The name of a tribe of Daityas, MBh. 3, 8719; 8769.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयक|कालेयकं|कालेयकः
कालेयक कालेय + क,<BR> I. n. A yellow fragrant wood, Suśr. 1, 146, 3.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One of the interior parts of the body not yet identified, Suśr. 1, 208, 3.<BR> 2. A kind of jaundice, Suśr. 2, 469, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य काल्य, i. e. कल्य + अ, n. Dawn, Rām. 2, 34, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेरी
कावेरी कावेरी, f. The name of a river, MBh. 2, 372.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य काव्य, i. e. कवि + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या, Coming from old sages, MBh. 2, 2097.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A class of Pitṛs or Manes, Man. 3, 199.<BR> 2. patron. Surname of Uśanas, MBh. 1, 3188.<BR> III. m. A bard, MBh. 2, 453.<BR> IV. n. A poem, Rām. 1, 2, 38.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाव्य|महाकाव्यं
महा- + काव्य महा- + काव्य, n. a classical poem, Chr. 170, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् काश्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.), † i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To be visible, Rām. 3, 29, 8.<BR> 2. To shine MBh. 1, 7008.<BR> काशित, Resplendent, Rām. 6, 26, 48.<BR> --With the prepos. उद् उद्, To shine, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 2.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, Caus. To reveal, MBh. 14, 1283.<BR> --With निस् निस्, cf. कस्.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To be visible, MBh. 3, 9990.<BR> 2. To appear, Rām. 6, 20, 10.<BR> 3. To shine, MBh. 3, 13750.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, Śāk. 12, 11; Rām. 4, 42, 14.<BR> 2. To illumine, MBh. 4, 232.<BR> 3. To make known, Lass. 3, 9.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To shine, Rām. 5, 73, 6.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To appear, MBh. 3, 13982.<BR> 2. To shine, Rām. 5, 5, 23.<BR> --Caus. To discover, MBh. 1, 87.<BR> --With वि वि, To appear, Rām. 5, 40, 10.<BR> --Caus. To illumine, MBh. 1, 7856.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To appear, Rām. 2, 65, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश काश् + अ, m. and n. A species of grass, Saccharum spontaneum, Rām. 2, 28, 22. When the latter part of a comp. adj., f. शा, e. g. कुसुमित-नव-, adj., f. शा, Covered with fresh blossoming Kāśa, Ṛt. 3, 28.<BR> --Cf. कास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशमय
काशमय काश + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of Kāśa-grass, Bhāg. P. 3, 22, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि काशि,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A proper name, Hariv. 1734.<BR> 2. The king of Kāśi, Chr. 19, 6.<BR> 3. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 13, 1949.<BR> II. f. शि and शी.<BR> 1. The name of Benares, Rām. 1, 12, 22.<BR> 2. शी, A proper name, Hariv. 9204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
ऽकाशिन् -काश् + इन्, adj., f. नी, latter part of comp. adj. Shining like, e. g. मत्त-, Like one delighted, charming, Rām. 5, 18, 37.<BR> 2. Shining on account of, e. g. जय- and जित-, On account of victory, victorious, proud on account of triumphs, Bhāg. P. 4, 10, 15; Chr. 16, 12.<BR> --Cf. कासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिष्णु
काशिष्णु काश् + इष्णु, adj. Resplendent, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशेय
काशेय काशेय, i. e. काशि + एय,<BR> I. m. A son of Kāśi, Hariv. 1734.<BR> II. f. यी, A daughter of Kāśi, MBh. 1, 3785.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मरी
काश्मरी काश्मरी, i. e. काश् + मन् + ई, f. A plant, Gmelina arborea, Rām. 2, 94, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मर्य|काश्मर्यः|काश्मर्य्य|काश्मर्य्यः
काश्मर्य काश्मर्य, i. e. काश् + मन् + य, m. A plant, Gmelina arborea, MBh. 13, 2773.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर|काश्मीरं|काश्मीरः
काश्मीर काश्मीर, i. e. कश्मीर + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री.<BR> 1. Trained in Cashmere, MBh. 4, 254 (a horse).<BR> 2. An inhabitant of Cashmere, MBh. 3, 5032.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A king of Cashmere, Mudrār. 18, 17.<BR> 2. Cashmere, Rām. 4, 43, 32.<BR> III. n. Saffron, Bhartṛ. 1, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरक
काश्मीरक काश्मीर + क, adj. Belonging to Cashmere, MBh. 2, 1025 (the inhabitants); 2, 1271 (the king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरिक
काश्मीरिक काश्मीरिक, i. e. का̆श्मिर + इक, adj. Referring to Cashmere, Chr. 245, l. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्य|काश्यं
काश्य काश्य, i. e. काशि + य, adj., and f. या.<BR> 1. Belonging to the Kāśis; a king of the Kāśis, MBh. 1, 4128.<BR> 2. f. A daughter of the king of the Kāśis, MBh. 1, 3829.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यप|काश्यपं|काश्यपः
काश्यप काश्यप, i. e. कश्यप + अ, f. पी.<BR> I. adj. Belonging to Kaśyapa, MBh. 13, 7237.<BR> II. patron. m. A descendant of Kaśyapa, Rām. 1, 9, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपेय|काश्यपेयः
काश्यपेय काश्यपेय, i. e. कश्यप + एय, patron. m. A name of the Ādityas, MBh. 13, 7094; of the sun, 1, 1247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषाय
काषाय काषाय, i. e. कषाय + अ, adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Red, Sāv. 3, 18.<BR> 2. s. A red cloth, Rām. 3, 52, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठ|काष्ठं
काष्ठ काष्ठ,<BR> I. n. A piece of wood, Man. 8, 372.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 2, 415.<BR> काष्ठा, q. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डकाष्ठ|दंडकाष्ठ
दण्ड- + काष्ठ दण्ड- + काष्ठ, n. a wooden staff, Śāk. 21, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकाष्ठ|दंतकाष्ठ|दन्तकाष्ठं
