कुण्ड्|कुंड्
† कुण्ड् कुण्ड्, i. 1, Par. To maim (?).<BR> --i. 1, Ātm. To heat.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुण्ड कुण्ड,<BR> I. m., f. डी, and n. A pitcher, a jar, a water pot, MBh. 3, 14311.<BR> II. m. and n. A basin of water, MBh. 13, 4816; Rām. 4, 26, 4.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A hole in the ground for receiving and preserving consecrated fire, MBh. 3, 8216.<BR> 2. A vessel for holding coals, Rām. 5, 10, 16.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. A son of an [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0193-a " target="_blank">Page0193-a + 42</a>] adulteress born before the death of the husband, Man. 3, 156; 174.<BR> 2. The name of a Nāga or serpent, MBh. 1, 4828.<BR> 3. A name of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10358.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतकुण्ड
