कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः|कुन्दः
कुन्द कुन्द,<BR> I. m. and n. A kind of jasmine, Jasminum multiflorum, or pubescens, Megh. 48.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Viṣṇu, MBh. 13, 7036.<BR> 2. The name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द्र्
† कुन्द्र् कुन्द्र्, i. 10, Par. To speak falsely, to lie.<BR> --Cf. कुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्
1. कुप् कुप्, i. 4, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To become excited, Suśr. 2, 184, 11.<BR> 2. To be angry, Man. 3, 229. With dat. gen. and acc., Of the person with whom one is angry, Pañc. 23, 22; Rām. 4, 19, 24; 1, 49, 7.<BR> कुपित, Enraged, Man. 9, 313. With उपरि and gen. (enraged against us), Pañc. 73, 15.<BR> अ-कुप्य, adj. Not liable to become angry, MBh. 15, 821.<BR> --Caus. कोपय,<BR> 1. To excite, Suśr. 2, 204, 3.<BR> 2. To provoke, MBh. 2, 2140. Ātm. To provoke against one's own self, MBh. 2, 2187. Anomalous कोपयीत for कोपयेत, कोपिष्ठास् for चूकुपथास्, कोपयान for कोपयमान, MBh. 1, 5790; 2, 2188; 3, 1956.<BR> 3. To be angry, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 11.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि,<BR> 1. To be much excited, MBh. 1, 1186.<BR> 2. To be very angry, MBh. 13, 2101.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To excite violently, MBh. 14, 469.<BR> 2. To provoke violently, MBh. 13, 7403.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To become agitated, Suśr. 2, 396, 4; MBh. 13, 14508.<BR> प्रकुपित, Very angry, Pañc. 163, 5.<BR> नातिप्रकुपित, Rather indifferent, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a " target="_blank">Page0195-a + 43</a>] Daśak. in Chr. 194, 11. Anomalous प्रकुप्त, Vikr. d. 130.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To excite, MBh. 14, 465.<BR> 2. To provoke, Man. 9, 313.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To become angry, MBh. 3, 1093.<BR> --Caus. To provoke, MBh. 4, 1845.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cupio = कुप्यामि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्
† 2. कुप् कुप्, i. 10, Par. To speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्य|कुप्यं
कुप्य कुप् + य,<BR> I. n. (and ऽकुप्यक -कुप्य + क as latter part of a comp.), Any metal except gold and silver, Man. 7, 96.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Rājat. 6, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज कुब्ज, i. e. कुभ्-ज (vb. जन्, cf. कुम्भ), adj., f. जा.<BR> 1. Hump-backed, Pañc. 261, 12.<BR> 2. Crooked, Pañc. ii. d. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जक|कुब्जकः
कुब्जक कुब्ज + क,<BR> I. adj. Humpbacked, Pañc. v. d. 77.<BR> II. m. An aquatic plant, Trapa bispinosa, Man. 8, 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार्
† कुमार् कुमार्, i. 10 (rather a denom. derived from the next), Par. To play as a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार कुमार, i. e. कु-मृ + अ (vb. मृ in its original signification, To be weak),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A child (ved.).<BR> 2. A boy, Man. 7, 152.<BR> 3. A youth, Ragh. 3, 40.<BR> 4. When compounded, often: Young, as latter part, Śāk. 27, 15; Ragh. 3, 40; as former part, Man. 3, 159. From early youth.<BR> 5. A young prince, Ragh. 12, 41.<BR> 6. A name of Skanda, the god of war, Suśr. 2, 394, 10.<BR> 7. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1870.<BR> II. f. री.<BR> 1. A girl, Man. 3, 54.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 1, 3796.<BR> 3. The name of a river, MBh. 6, 343.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुमार|राजकुमारः
राजकुमार राजकुमार, i. e. राजन्-, m. a prince, Lass. 7, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्कुमार|सनत्कुमारः
सनत्कुमार सनत्क्˚, i. e. सनद्-, m. one of the four sons of Brahman, and eldest of the progenitors of mankind. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b " target="_blank">Page0195-b + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुमार|सुकुमारः
सु- + कुमार सु- + कुमार,<BR> I. adj. 1. soft, smooth. 2. youthful. 3. delicate.<BR> II. m., and f. रा, names of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारक|कुमारकः
कुमारक कुमार + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A boy, Śāk. 50, 1.<BR> 2. A youth, Bhāg. P. 3, 3, 24.<BR> 3. The name of a Nāga or serpent, MBh. 1, 2154.<BR> II. f. रिका, A girl, Pañc. 184, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारत्व
कुमारत्व कुमार + त्व, n. Youth, Ragh. 17, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारसू
कुमारसू कुमार-सू, m. A name of Agni, MBh. 2, 1148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमाल्
† कुमाल् कुमाल् = कुमार् (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद् कु-मुद्, n. The esculent white water-lily, Nymphæa esculenta, Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद|कुमुदं|कुमुदः
कुमुद कु-मुद् + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. The white esculent water-lily, Nymphæa esculenta, Pañc. 50, 10.<BR> II. m. The name of a Nāga or serpent, MBh. 1, 1560; of a celestial being, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 39; of a monkey, Rām. 4, 39, 37; of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 16, 12; of a man, Rājat. 5, 422.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनी
कुमुदिनी कुमुदिनी, i. e. कुमुद + इन् + ई, f. A group of lotus flowers, Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्वन्त्|कुमुद्वत्
कुमुद्वन्त् कुमुद् + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Abounding in lotusses, Ragh. 4, 19.<BR> II. f. वती,<BR> 1. A group of lotus flowers, Śāk. d. 65.<BR> 2. A plant, Menyanthes indica, Suśr. 2, 251, 18.<BR> 3. A proper name, Ragh. 16, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्प्
† कुम्प् कुम्प्, i. 10, Par., v. r. of कुम्ब्, i. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्ब्
† कुम्ब् कुम्ब्, i. 1, and i. 10 (cf. the last and the next), To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ्
† कुम्भ् कुम्भ्, i. 10, Par., v. r. of कुम्ब्.<BR> --Cf. the last and the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ|कुंभ|कुम्भं|कुंभः|कुम्भः
कुम्भ कुम्भ् + अ (the vb. कुम्भ्, कुभ्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-a " target="_blank">Page0196-a + 47</a>] from which this noun is derived, is lost in the corresponding signification, but cf. कुब्ज, κυϕός, κύϕων, κῦϕος; Engl. hump; O.H.G. hofar; Lat. cŭbitus, the elbow, lying, etc., cŭbare, concumbere, etc.; and at the end of this article. From these and other instances, we may infer that the original signification of the vb. कुभ् was ‘to be crooked’),<BR> I. m., and f. भी.<BR> 1. A pot, Man. 11, 186; MBh. 18, 84.<BR> 2. A measure of grain, equal to twenty droṇas, Man. 8, 320; 4, 7.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. dual, The two frontal globes of an elephant, which swell in the rutting season, Pañc. i. d. 351.<BR> 2. The paramour of a harlot, Śṛṅgārat. 9.<BR> 3. The name of a Dānava, MBh. 1, 2527; of a Rākṣasa, Rām. 5, 79, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --When latter part of a comp. adj. the fem. is भा, e. g. वारि-पूरित-कुम्भ, adj., f. भा, Bearing jars filled with water, Kathās. 18, 339.<BR> --Cf. κῡϕος, a vessel, κύϕελλον, κυψέλη, κύβος, κύβιτον, κύβη, κύμβος, κύμβαχος, etc.; Goth. hups; O.H.G. huf; A.S. hipe; O.H.G. hufila, ‘a cheek,’ hûfo and hauf, a multitude, heap; cf. supra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकुम्भ
अग्नि- + कुम्भ अग्नि- + कुम्भ, m. a fire pot, MBh. 13, 5490 (he will get [in hell] a fire pot, in order to be burnt therein; cf. कुम्भी-पाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमकुम्भ|आमकुम्भः
आम- + कुम्भ आम- + कुम्भ, m. an unburnt earthen pot, Pañc. iii. d. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकुम्भ|उदकुंभ|उदकुम्भः
उदकुम्भ उदकुम्भ, i. e. उदन्-, m. a water pot, Man. 2, 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचकुम्भ|कुचकुम्भः
कुच- + कुम्भ कुच- + कुम्भ, m. a bosom like the frontal globes of an elephant, Śṛṅgārat. 9 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकुम्भ|तप्तकुम्भः
तप्त- + कुम्भ तप्त- + कुम्भ, m. the name of a hell, Mārk. P. 12, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकुम्भ|भद्रकुंभ|भद्रकुम्भः
भद्र- + कुम्भ भद्र- + कुम्भ, m. a golden jar filled with water from a holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुम्भ|वातकुंभ|वातकुम्भः
वात- + कुम्भ वात- + कुम्भ, m. the part of an elephant's forehead below the frontal globes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकुम्भ|शतकुंभ|शतकुम्भः
शत- + कुम्भ शत- + कुम्भ,<BR> I. m. the name of a mountain.<BR> II. n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भक|कुंभक|कुंभकः|कुम्भकः
कुम्भक कुम्भ + क,<BR> I. m. A religious exercise, closing the nostrils and mouth so as to suspend breathing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 18.<BR> II. f. भिका, A small pot, Kathās. 6, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकार|कुंभकार|कुम्भकारः
कुम्भकार कुम्भ-कार, m. A potter, Pañc. 217, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकारिका
कुम्भकारिका कुम्भकारिका, i. e. कुम्भ-कारक, f. The wife of a potter, Kathās. 21, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिल|कुंभिल|कुंभिलः|कुम्भिलः
कुम्भिल कुम्भिल (akin to कुम्भ), m. A thief, Śāk. 13, 2 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीर|कुंभीर|कुंभीरः|कुम्भीरः
