कुरुविन्द|कुरुविंद|कुरुविंदं|कुरुविन्दं|कुरुविंदः|कुरुविन्दः
कुरुविन्द कुरुविन्द, m.<BR> 1. The name of several plants, a kind of barley, Suśr. 1, 197, 1.<BR> 2. A ruby, Śiś. 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्कुट|कुर्कुटः
कुर्कुट कुर्कुट, m. Rubbish (?), Pañc. iii. d. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्कुर|कुर्कुरः|कुर्क्कुर
कुर्कुर कुर्कुर (onomatop.), also कुक्कुर कुक्कुर and कुकुर कुकुर, m. A dog, Pañc. ii. d. 97; Hit. 50, 3. कुकुर, also, The proper name of a prince, MBh. 13, 7679; and a people, Rām. 4, 41, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्द्
कुर्द् कुर्द्, i. 1, कूर्द, Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To hop, Hariv. 8398.<BR> 2. † To play.<BR> --Caus. of the frequent. चोकूर्दय, To invite to hop, Hariv. 8403 (चुकूर्दयद्भिः, read चोकूर्द्˚).<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To hop briskly, Hariv. 8404.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To jump aloft, Pañc. 124, 7.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To jump on, Pañc. 118, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्पासक|कुर्पासकः
कुर्पासक कुर्पास + क, m. A bodice, Ṛt. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्
† कुल् कुल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To accumulate.<BR> 2. To be of kin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल कुल, n.<BR> 1. A herd, Rām. 4, 40, 24; a flock, Ṛt. 1, 23; Pañc. 82, 20.<BR> 2. A multitude, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 33.<BR> 3. A caste. Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 43.<BR> 4. Family, Man. 2, 34.<BR> 5. A house, Man. 7, 82.<BR> 6. A grange, holding as much land as can be tilled by two ploughs, each drawn by six bulls, Man. 7, 119.<BR> 7. Noble lineage, Man. 7, 54.<BR> 8. An inspector of causes, Man. 8, 169 (? Kull.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपकुल
अनुरूप- + कुल अनुरूप- + कुल, adj., f. ला, being of a suitable family, Rām. 3, 35, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःकुल
