देवकुल|देवकुलं
देव- + कुल देव- + कुल, n. a temple, Mṛcch. 30, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुल
निष्कुल निष्कुल, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ला, having no kindred, Man. 8, 28; with कृ, to exterminate one's family, Rām. 4, 26, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकुल
नीच- + कुल नीच- + कुल, n. a low family, Mṛcch. 83, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुल
राजकुल राजकुल, i. e. राजन्-,<BR> I. n. 1. the court of a king, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 18. 2. a court of justice, Pañc. 96, 20. 3. a royal race.<BR> II. m. a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

