कुलीन|कुलीनः
कुलीन कुलीन, i. e. कुल + ईन, adj., f. ना.<BR> 1. Being of a good family, Man. 7, 210.<BR> 2. Of noble breed, Rām. 5, 12, 31.<BR> 3. Latter part of a comp. adj. Belonging to a race or family of; the aff. ईन belongs to the whole comp., e. g. तद्-, adj. Belonging to the same (i. e. his) race, Chr. 25, 53.<BR> महाराज-, adj., f. ना, Belonging to a race of great kings, Rām. 2, 88, 3.<BR> अ-, adj. Sprung from a low family, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 404.<BR> दुष्कुलीन, i. e. दुस्-कुल + ईन, adj. Sprung from a low family, Rām. 3, 23, 15.<BR> सत्कुलीन, i. e. सन्त्-कुल + ईन (vb. अस्), adj. Well born, nobly descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

