कृण्व्
† कृण्व् कृण्व्, ii. 5 (base of the pres. कृणु), Par.<BR> 1. To do (see 1. कृ ii. 5, ved.).<BR> 2. To injure (see 2. कॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
1. कृत् कृत्, i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 17212; and i. 1, MBh. 3, 11383), base of the pres., etc., कृन्त.<BR> 1. To cut, MBh. 1, 3641.<BR> 2. To cut off, Rām. 3, 75, 4.<BR> 3. To cut down, Pañc. 250, 6.<BR> 4. To cut out, Man. 4, 172; to extract, Man. 8, 12.<BR> 5. To kill, MBh. 1, 5593.<BR> --Caus. To cut, Pañc. 143, 13.<BR> --With the prepositions समधि सम्-अधि, To cut in addition, MBh. 3, 13294.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To cut one by one, MBh. 13, 2906.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To cut off, Suśr. 2, 237, 15.<BR> 2. To destroy, MBh. 1, 6810.<BR> --Caus. To order a gash to be made on, Man. 8, 281.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To cut out, 11, 104 (105).<BR> 2. To pull out, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 2.<BR> 3. To cut to pieces, Ragh. 12, 49.<BR> --With नि नि, To cut down, Rām. 3, 33, 36.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To cut off, Rām. 3, 31, 48.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To cut out, to separate, MBh. 3, 8846.<BR> 2. To cut down, 1, 2835.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To cut wholly, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0211-a " target="_blank">Page0211-a + 42</a>] Rām. 6, 39, 21.<BR> 2. To exclude, Man. 4, 219.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To cut to pieces, MBh. 3, 11383 (i. 1).<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To rend, Rām. 3, 56, 39.<BR> 2. To divide, Nal. 10, 17 (i. 1).<BR> --Caus. To rend, Pañc. 91, 5.<BR> --With सम्, To cut in pieces, Rām. 3, 25, 6.<BR> --Cf. Lat. curtus; Goth. giltha, grinda-, dis-skreitan; κερσ in ἀκερσεκόμης, and कर्त्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
2. कृत् कृत्, ii. 7.<BR> 1. To spin, (ved.).<BR> 2. † To surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
3. ऽकृत् -कृत्, i. e. 1. कृ + त्, latter part of comp. adj.<BR> 1. Making, e. g. क्षेत्रकर्मकृत्, i. e. क्षेत्र-कर्मन्-, m. A husbandman, Kathās. 20, 11; चित्र-, m. A painter, Kathās. 5, 28; जन्मकृत्, i. e. जन्मन्-, m. A father, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 7; दिन- and दिवस-, m. The sun, MBh. 3, 192; 7, 2935; सु-कृत-, Performing virtuous acts, Man. 3, 37.<BR> 2. Causing, सर्व-भूत-, Causing, or the cause of, all beings, Man. 1, 18; अन्त-, 1. adj. causing death, Rām. 3, 67, 19; 2. death, 5, 23, 17.<BR> 3. Agent of all actions signified by the vb. 1. कृ, e. g. बहु-पत्नी-, Marrying many wives, Brāhmaṇ. 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक 1. कृ + त + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Adopted, MBh. 13, 2630.<BR> 2. Feigned, Pañc. 188, 5.<BR> 3. False, MBh. 13, 2607.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 24, 47.<BR> III. कम्, acc. sing. n., adv. Feignedly, Śiś. 9, 83.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

