अर्थकृत्य
अर्थ- + कृत्य अर्थ- + कृत्य, n. a useful act, Rām. 4, 38, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत्य
असत्- + कृत्य असत्- + कृत्य, i. e. अ-सन्त्- (vb. 1. अस्), adj. one who has acted wickedly, Rājat. 5, 300. See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्य|कृतकृत्यः
कृत- + कृत्य कृत- + कृत्य,<BR> I. n. 1. what has been done and what must be done. 2. fulfilled intention, MBh. 4, 882.<BR> II. adj., f. या, satisfied, Rām. 1, 1, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकृत्य
गृह- + कृत्य गृह- + कृत्य, n. domestic affairs, Rājat. 5, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकृत्य
भूति- + कृत्य भूति- + कृत्य, n. any ceremony of a festive character, as marriage, Man. 8, 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रकृत्य
शीघ्र- + कृत्य शीघ्र- + कृत्य, adj., f. य, what must be done quickly, Pañc. iii. d. 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यका
कृत्यका कृत्य + का, f. A witch, Nal. 13, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यवन्त्|कृत्यवत्
कृत्यवन्त् कृत्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Occupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम कृ + त्रिम,<BR> I. adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Factitious, the reverse of what is natural, Pañc. 110, 16.<BR> 2. Feigned, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 5 (cf. आर्ति).<BR> 3. Adopted, Man. 9, 169.<BR> 4. False, Yājñ. 2, 247.<BR> II. m. An adopted son, Man. 9, 159. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b " target="_blank">Page0212-b + 41</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्रिम|अकृत्रिमं
अ- + कृत्रिम अ- + कृत्रिम, adj. Candid, Hit. i. d. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वस्
ऽकृत्वस् -कृ + त्वस्, adv. forming multiplicative numerals from numerals and other words, e. g. सहस्र-, adv. A thousand times, Man. 2, 79.<BR> तावत्कृत्वस्, i. e. तावन्त्-, adv. So many times, Man. 5, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्न|कृत्स्नं|कृत्स्नः
कृत्स्न कृत्स्न, adj.<BR> 1. Whole, Man. 1, 105.<BR> 2. All, Rām. 4, 43, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नशस्
कृत्स्नशस् कृत्स्न + शस्, adv. Completely, Man. 7, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तन|कृंतन|कृंतनं|कृन्तनं
कृन्तन कृन्तन, i. e. कृत् + अन, n. Cutting, Bhāg. P. 6, 2, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप्
कृप् कृप्, i. 10, Par. कृपय,<BR> 1. To pity, Bhāg. P. 8, 7, 40.<BR> 2. † To be weak.<BR> --Cf. क्रप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप कृप, m., and f. पी, Proper names, MBh. 1, 2436.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण|कृपणः
कृपण कृपण, i. e. कृप् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णा.<BR> 1. Miserable, Rām. 4, 21, 19.<BR> 2. Lamenting, Megh. 5.<BR> 3. Avaricious, Hit. i. d. 152.<BR> II. n. Misery, MBh. 2, 2348.<BR> III. णम्, acc. sing. n., adv. Miserably, Pañc. iii. d. 183.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृपण
स-कृपण स-कृपण, adj. miserable, Śāntiś. 4, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणत्व
कृपणत्व कृपण + त्व, n. Wretchedness, MBh. 2, 1361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपा
कृपा कृप् + आ, f. Compassion, MBh. 2, 2294.<BR> कृपां कृ, To have compassion, Draup. 9, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृपम्
स-कृप + म् स-कृप + म्, adv. compassionately, Śāntiś. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाण|कृपाणः
कृपाण कृपाण, i. e. कृप् (cf. Lat. carpo, discerpo) + आन, m. A sword, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाय
कृपाय कृपाय, a denomin. derived from कृपा by य, Ātm. To pity, MBh. 13, 2330; कृपायीत, anomal. for ˚येत, 1, 5597.<BR> कृपायित, n. Lamentation, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a " target="_blank">Page0213-a + 39</a>] MBh. 3, 337.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To pity, MBh. 3, 329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपालु|कृपालुः
कृपालु कृपा + लु, adj. Compassionate, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 17; 187, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपावन्त्|कृपावत्
कृपावन्त् कृपा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Compassionate, Kumāras. 5, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमि|कृमिः
कृमि कृमि, also क्रिमि क्रिमि, i. e. ह्वृ + मि,<BR> I. m. A worm, an insect in general, Man. 1, 40; Suśr. 2, 509, 11 sqq.<BR> II. m. and f. Proper names, Hariv. 2002; 1675.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vermis; Goth. vaurms; ἕλμινς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिक|कृमिकः
कृमिक कृमि + क, m. A small worm, MBh. 1, 1800.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिज|कृमिजं
कृमिज कृमि-ज (vb. जन्), adj. Produced by a worm, Pañc. i. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिल
कृमिल कृमि + ल, adj., f. ला, Wormy, Suśr. 1, 191, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश्
कृश् कृश्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To become thin (ved.).<BR> 2. To make thin.<BR> --Caus. कर्शय, To cause to become thin, Suśr. 2, 196, 6.<BR> कर्शित, Emaciated, Rām. 1, 54, 2.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, Caus. To cause to become thin, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 25.<BR> --Cf. κολέκ + ανος, κολόκανος, κολοσσός for κολοκϳος; Lat. gracilis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश कृश् + अ, adj., f. शा.<BR> 1. Thin, emaciated, Suśr. 1, 53, 17.<BR> 2. Weak, Hit. i. d. 196; Man. 7, 208.<BR> 3. Poor, Man. 4, 184.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृश
अ- + कृश अ- + कृश, adj. great, Kir. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृश
अति- + कृश अति- + कृश, adj. very thin, Rām. 5, 10, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशता
कृशता कृश + ता, f., and कृशत्व कृश + त्व, n. Meagerness, MBh. 2, 1933; Pañc. i. d. 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानु|कृशानुः
कृशानु कृश् + आनु, m.<BR> 1. A name of fire, Bhartṛ. 2, 67.<BR> 2. A proper name, Chr. 297, 21 = Rigv. i. 112, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्व
कृशाश्व कृशाश्व, i. e. कृश-अश्व, m. A proper name, Rām. 1, 23, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्
कृष् कृष्, i. 1, Par. (in epie poetry also Ātm., e. g. MBh. 1, 6289),<BR> 1. To draw, MBh. 1, 6468; Ragh. 9, 27 (an arrow to the ear).<BR> 2. To draw (a bow), Ragh. 5, 20.<BR> 3. To drag along, MBh. 1, 6001.<BR> 4. To lead, Chr. 54, 14 (Ātm.).<BR> 5. To bear, MBh. 13, 4580.<BR> 6. To tear, MBh. 1, 5992.<BR> 7. To allure, Lass. 85, 2.<BR> 8. To subdue, Man. 2, 215.<BR> 9. To attain, MBh. 3, 66.<BR> 10. i. 1, Par., and i. 6, Par., Ātm., To draw furrows, to plough, Rām. 3, 4, 12 (i. 1); Yājñ. 2, 150 (i. 6, कृषाण, anom. instead of कृषमाण).<BR> 11. To walk, MBh. 3, 16021.<BR> कृष्ट,<BR> 1. Drawn, Śāk. d. 131.<BR> 2. Ploughed, Pañc. i. d. 53.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Absol. कृष्य, instead of कृष्ट्वा, Chr. 40, 10.<BR> --Caus. कर्षय,<BR> 1. To drag, Mṛcch. 16, 25.<BR> 2. To pluck out, MBh. 3, 2307.<BR> 3. To distress, Man. 2, 24.<BR> 4. To oppress, Man. 7, 111.<BR> --All the following are inflected after i. 1: With the prep. अनु अनु, To drag after one's self Rām. 1, 54, 1 (Ātm.).<BR> --Caus. अनुकर्षित, Occupied, MBh. 13, 7281.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To draw away, MBh. 3, 10615; Rām. 6, 72, 68 (Ātm.).<BR> 2. To remove, Rām. 5, 71, 5.<BR> 3. To deduct, Suśr. 2, 40, 8.<BR> 4. To put aside, Nal. 17, 33.<BR> 5. To draw (a bow), MBh. 4, 1909.<BR> 6. To humble, MBh. 13, 2186.<BR> अपकृष्ट,<BR> 1. Lost, Nal. 9, 33.<BR> 2. Inferior, Man. 5, 163.<BR> --Causal, To remove, MBh. 1, 6205.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप,<BR> 1. To drag away, Rām. 6, 88, 2.<BR> 2. To cast off, MBh. 1 5104.<BR> 3. To remove, Nal. 24, 41.<BR> 4. To atone, Man. 11, 210.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To subdue, MBh. 3, 15064.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To draw away, Śāk. d. 173. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-a " target="_blank">Page0214-a + 41</a>]<BR> 2. To cast off, MBh. 13, 5007 (reflective pass.).<BR> 3. To remove, MBh. 2, 207.<BR> 4. To draw down, Suśr. 2, 291, 1.<BR> अवकृष्त, Inferior, Man. 8, 177.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव, To alienate, MBh. 13, 1642.<BR> --With आ आ.<BR> 1. To draw near. Hit. i. d. 102.<BR> 2. To draw (a sword), Mṛcch. 132, 5; (a bow) Śāk. d. 54.<BR> 3. To draw on, Śāk. 5, 5.<BR> 4. To drag along, Śāk. d. 32.<BR> 5. To allure, Hit. 41, 14.<BR> 6. To cast off, MBh. 2, 2291.<BR> 7. To draw out, Lass. 22, 7.<BR> 8. To take from, Hit. pr. d. 8; to withdraw, Rājat. 5, 69.<BR> --Caus. To draw near, Ṛt. 5, 11; to fetch, Pañc. 32, 17.<BR> --With अपा अप-आ, To remove, Rām. 2, 17, 9.<BR> --With व्यपा वि-अप-आ, To remove, MBh. 2, 2290.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, To drag about, MBh. 18, 9.<BR> --With व्या,<BR> 1. To cast off, Rām. 5, 54, 15.<BR> 2. To remove, Prab. 37, 7.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To drag near, MBh. 3, 10494; to fetch, Amar. 76.<BR> 2. To take out (with abl.), Pañc. 40, 16.<BR> --Caus. To carry along, Pañc. 74, 23.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To raise, Bhāg. P. 5, 6, 10 (pass. to rise).<BR> 2. To take out, MBh. 1, 7869.<BR> 3. To cast off, MBh. 2, 1810.<BR> 4. To draw (a bow), MBh. 4, 1635.<BR> उत्कृष्ट,<BR> 1. Excessive, Rām. 3, 41, 5.<BR> 2. Superior, Man. 5, 163.<BR> 3. Distinguished, Man. 3, 132.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To raise, MBh. 1, 3613.<BR> --With उप उप, To draw near, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 22.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To draw near, Rām. 2, 89, 10.<BR> --With नि नि, To sink into (a river), MBh. 1, 3616.<BR> निकृष्ट, Low, base, MBh. 1, 3067. n. Vicinity, Suśr. 1, 94, 4.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि; संनिकृष्ट, Near, Rām. 3, 21, 5. n. Vicinity, Śāk. 23, 23.<BR> ˚टम्, adv. Near, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b " target="_blank">Page0214-b + 40</a>] Kumāras. 3, 2.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To draw out, MBh. 3, 16763.<BR> 2. To tear, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 21; to dissolve, Rājat. 6, 272.<BR> --Caus. To destroy, Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 19.<BR> --With परा परा,<BR> 1. To draw away, MBh. 2, 2227.<BR> 2. To blame, MBh. 13, 2102.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To drag about, Rām. 2, 97, 30.<BR> 2. To carry about with one, MBh. 17, 104.<BR> 3. To lead, Rām. 6, 2, 28.<BR> --Caus. To torment, Rām. 1, 8, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To drag away, MBh. 3, 12787.<BR> 2. To draw (a bow), MBh. 4, 1959.<BR> 3. To agitate, Rām. 5, 70, 11.<BR> 4. To lead, Rām. 6, 2, 44.<BR> प्रकृष्ट,<BR> 1. Long, Nal. 12, 111.<BR> 2. Well to do, Man. 7, 170.<BR> 3. Excellent, Pañc. 191, 16.<BR> 4. Violent, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 4.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To conquer, MBh. 1, 7197.<BR> विप्रकृष्ट, Distant, Pañc. 127, 17.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To draw (a bow), Rām. 3, 34, 3; (an arrow) Rām. 6, 70, 39.<BR> 2. To drag about, Rām. 2, 78, 16.<BR> 3. To draw out, Bhartṛ. 1, 84 (to catch).<BR> 4. To withdraw, Rājat. 5, 90.<BR> विकृष्ट, Long, Rām. 2, 68, 21.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To drag along, Rām. 5, 63, 19.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ac-cerso.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकृष्ट|इन्द्रकृष्टः
इन्द्र- + कृष्ट इन्द्र- + कृष्ट, adj. growing without culture, MBh. 2, 1831.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फालकृष्ट|फालकृष्टः
फाल- + कृष्ट फाल- + कृष्ट, n. 1. tilled ground, Man. 4, 46. 2. produced by cultivation, 6, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषक|कृषकः
कृषक कृष् + अक, m. A husbandman, Cāṇ. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषि|कृषिः
कृषि कृष् + इ (कृषी कृषी, MBh. 1, 7207), f.<BR> 1. Ploughing, Lass. 76, 18.<BR> 2. Agriculture, Man. 1, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषीवल|कृषीवलः
कृषीवल कृषी + वल, m. A husbandman, Man. 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टज
कृष्टज कृष्ट-ज, adj. Cultivated, Man. 11, 144 (145).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
कृष्ण कृष्ण, i. e. कृष् + न (the origin of the signification is dubious).<BR> I. adj., f. णा.<BR> 1. Black, or dark blue, Rām. 3, 55, 5.<BR> 2. With or without [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a " target="_blank">Page0215-a + 41</a>] पक्ष, m. The dark half of a month, from the full moon to that of the new moon, Man. 1, 66; 6, 20.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. कृष्ण, The most celebrated incarnation of Viṣṇu, MBh. 14, 1589.<BR> 2. The black antelope, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 20.<BR> III. f. णा.<BR> 1. A name of Durgā, MBh. 4, 184.<BR> 2. The name of several plants, Suśr. 1, 162, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृष्ण
अति- + कृष्ण अति- + कृष्ण, adj. very black, Pañc. 104, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णता
कृष्णता कृष्ण + ता, f., and कृष्णत्व कृष्ण + त्व, n. Blackness, Suśr. 1, 33, 20; MBh. 1, 4236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णल|कृष्णलः
कृष्णल कृष्ण + ल, m. and n. The berry of the plant Guñja, used as a weight; a coin of this weight, Man. 8, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलक|कृष्णलकः
ऽकृष्णलक -कृष्णल + क, substitute for the last when latter part of a comp. adj., पञ्चकृष्णलक, i. e. पञ्चन्-, Comprising five कृष्णलस्, Man. 8, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाजिनिन्
कृष्णाजिनिन् कृष्णाजिनिन्, i. e. कृष्ण-अजिन + इन्, adj., f. नी, Covered with the hide of the black antelope, MBh. 14, 2113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाय
कृष्णाय कृष्णाय, a denom. derived from कृष्ण by य, Ātm. To blacken, Hit. i. d. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णायस्
कृष्णायस् कृष्णायस्, i. e. कृष्ण-अयस्, and कृष्णायस कृष्णायस् + अ, n. Iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृसर|कृसरः
कृसर कृसर, m. A dish consisting of sesamum and grain, Man. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
1. कॄ कॄ, i. 6, किर, Par.<BR> 1. To pour out, Amar. 11.<BR> 2. To cast, MBh. 14, 1898.<BR> 3. To cover, Rām. 5, 42, 10.<BR> कीर्ण,<BR> 1. Scattered, Rām. 5, 16, 17.<BR> 2. Dishevelled, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 15.<BR> 3. Covered, Pañc. i. d. 239.<BR> --With the prepositions व्यति वि-अति, To scatter, MBh. 4, 830.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To cover, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-b " target="_blank">Page0215-b + 38</a>] MBh. 1, 4340.<BR> --With अप अप, which forms also अपस्किर, Ātm. To rake (as a bird for pleasure), Uttararāmac. p. 31, 1.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To cover, MBh. 13, 2655.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To diffuse, Man. 6, 48.<BR> 2. To cast off, MBh. 2, 2289.<BR> 3. To leave, MBh. 1, 3057.<BR> 4. To cover, Rām. 2, 43, 13. Ātm. and reflect. pass.,<BR> 1. To spread, MBh. 3, 12306.<BR> 2. To vanish, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 19.<BR> --With अन्वव अनु-अव, To scatter about, Yājñ. 1, 230.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be scattered about, MBh. 13, 4291 (read कारयेत्).<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, To cover, Rām. 2, 33, 19.<BR> --With पर्यव परि-अव, To cover round about, MBh. 3, 13596.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, To cover, Bhāg. P. 8, 18, 10.<BR> --With आ आ, आकीर्ण,<BR> 1. Crowded, Arj. 6, 7.<BR> 2. Frequented, Man. 6, 51.<BR> 3. Confused, Rājat. 5, 321.<BR> --With अपा अप-आ, To repudiate, MBh. 1, 2851.<BR> --With अवा अव-आ, To cover, Rām. 2, 42, 14 Gorr. (Schl. v. r.).<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, व्याकीर्ण, Dishevelled, Pañc. i. d. 207.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To cover, Rām. 1, 6, 24.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To throw up, Rām. 6, 90, 26.<BR> 2. To dig up, MBh. 1, 5813.<BR> 3. To engrave, Vikr. d. 43.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To pierce, Ragh. 1, 4.<BR> --With उप उप, To cover, MBh. 3, 11886.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि,<BR> 1. To cast down, Rām. 6, 8, 19.<BR> 2. To leave, Kumāras. 4, 6.<BR> 3. विनिकीर्ण, Crowded, Rām. 4, 41, 33.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, संनिकिर्ण, Stretched out, Megh. 87.<BR> --With परा परा, To leave, MBh. 4, 1369.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-a " target="_blank">Page0216-a + 41</a>] surround, MBh. 4, 585.<BR> 2. To deliver, Ragh. 18, 32.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To scatter, Rām. 2, 76, 15.<BR> 2. To spring up, Rām. 1, 9, 19.<BR> 3. Pass. (anom. कीर्येत्, with the termination of the Par.), To vanish, MBh. 3, 14767.<BR> प्रकीर्ण,<BR> 1. Dishevelled, MBh. 3, 11755.<BR> 2. Squandered, Lass. 74, 17.<BR> 3. Public, MBh. 13, 6735.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, विप्रकीर्ण,<BR> 1. Scattered, Rām. 5, 14, 53.<BR> 2. Dishevelled, MBh. 3, 401.<BR> 3. Extended, MBh. 3, 730.<BR> --With प्रतिस् प्रतिस्, instead of प्रति प्रति, To injure (cf. 2. कॄ), Śiś. 1, 47.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To scatter, Hit. 9, 14.<BR> 2. To cover, Man. 3, 234.<BR> 3. To blame, Rām. 2, 12, 73.<BR> विकीर्ण,<BR> 1. Dishevelled, Kumāras. 4, 4.<BR> 2. Split, Rām. 3, 34, 25.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To scatter, MBh. 4, 298.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To mix, MBh. 13, 6232.<BR> 2. To confound, MBh. 3, 13736.<BR> संकीर्ण,<BR> 1. Crowded, MBh. 1, 7675.<BR> 2. Mixed, Man. 1, 116.<BR> 3. Impure, Yājñ. 3, 310.<BR> --Cf. कल्, शकृत्; and Lat. cribrum, cerno, procerus; κρίνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
† 2. कॄ कॄ, also कृ कृ, ii. 5 and 9, Par., Ātm. To injure, to kill.<BR> --Cf. 1. कॄ with प्रतिस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
† 3. कॄ कॄ, i. 10, Ātm. To know (? v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄत्
कॄत् कॄत्, i. 10, कीर्तय (rather a denomin. derived from कीर्ति), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm. MBh. 1, 1549),<BR> 1. To celebrate, Man. 3, 221.<BR> 2. To propound, Man. 10, 131.<BR> 3. To pronounce, Man. 2, 124.<BR> 4. To say, Man. 2, 203.<BR> 5. To call, Man. 10, 19. Anom. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. कीर्तयान, MBh. 13, 7661.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To mention, Rām. 1, 14, 22.<BR> 2. To repeat, Bhāg. P. 8, 4, 15.<BR> 3. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-b " target="_blank">Page0216-b + 43</a>] proclaim, MBh. 3, 13259.<BR> 4. To propound. MBh. 2, 994.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To tell, MBh. 14, 2066.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To glorify, Ragh. 10, 33.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To proclaim, Man. 11, 122.<BR> 2. To propound, MBh. 13, 12802.<BR> 3. To glorify, MBh. 13, 7160.<BR> 4. To pronounce, Man. 1, 92.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, To particularise, Suśr. 2, 268, 21.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To propound, Man. 2, 95.<BR> 2. To call, Man. 2, 21.<BR> 3. To approve, Pañc. iv. d. 37.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To mention, MBh. 13, 4926.<BR> 2. To pronounce, Bhag. 18, 4.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To celebrate, Man. 3, 221.<BR> 2. To proclaim, Rām. 4, 59, 3.<BR> 3. To mention, Chr. 13, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्
कॢप् कॢप्, i. 1, कल्प, Ātm.<BR> 1. To prosper, Man. 4, 15.<BR> 2. To be fit, to be qualified for; with the loc. Rām. 2, 62, 26 Gorr.; 5, 37, 30; with the dat. Man. 3, 266; to become qualified, Man. 7, 22; Megh. 56 (प्राप्तये, to attain).<BR> 3. To fall to one's lot, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 12.<BR> 4. To serve (with the dat.), Man. 8, 353.<BR> 5. To resolve upon, Pañc. 150, 24.<BR> 6. To create, Bhāg. P. 3, 7, 25.<BR> क्लिप्त,<BR> 1. Well arranged, MBh. 3, 790.<BR> 2. Fixed, Man. 3, 69.<BR> 3. Made, Bhāg. P. 6, 10, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus., कल्पय, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To put in suitable order.<BR> कल्पित, Fixed in proportion, Yājñ. 2, 244.<BR> प्रथम-कल्पित, put at the head, Man. 9, 166.<BR> 2. To make fit for something, MBh. 8, 9912.<BR> 3. To approve, Rām. 2, 61, 17.<BR> 4. To show, MBh. 1, 58.<BR> 6. To design, Rām. 2, 52, 100; to determine, Man. 7, 125; Daśak. in Chr. 189, 1.<BR> 7. To consider, Rām. 2, 23, 33.<BR> 8. To form, Ragh. 8, 46; Bhāg. P. 8, 9, 26; to make, Rām. 2, 98, 29; MBh. 1, 700 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0217-a " target="_blank">Page0217-a + 42</a>] (वृत्तिम्, To live on, with the instr.).<BR> 9. To create, Man. 5, 28; Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 42.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, Caus., श्रद्धाम्, To give faith, Rām. 5, 56, 15.<BR> अनुकल्पित, Accompanied, MBh. 13, 2150.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, Caus., To assume, MBh. 3, 9964.<BR> --With अभि अभि, Caus., To arrange, Rām. 2, 54, 17.<BR> --With अव अव, To be fit (with the dat.), Bhāg. P. 6, 7, 18.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To be suitable, Bhāg. P. 6, 18, 42.<BR> 2. To serve, Rām. 5, 25, 21.<BR> उपकॢप्त,<BR> 1. Prepared for use, Man. 8, 333; prepared, MBh. 1, 4098.<BR> 2. Produced, Bhāg. P. 5, 16, 2.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To prepare, Rām. 1, 12, 29.<BR> 2. To fit out, MBh. 1, 4098.<BR> 3. To design for (with the dat.), Yājñ. 1, 109.<BR> 4. To place, Bhāg. P. 5, 23, 5; 1, 9, 32.<BR> 5. To communicate, Bhāg. P. 5, 3, 9.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, Caus. To prepare, Rām. 2, 50, 29.<BR> --With परि परि, परिकॢप्त, Existing, MBh. 13, 2831.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To decide, Man. 12, 110.<BR> 2. To determine, MBh. 13, 2689.<BR> 3. To perform, Yājñ. 1, 346.<BR> 4. To make, Kathās. 15, 173; Man. 9, 152 (दशधा, To distribute into ten parts).<BR> 5. To invite, MBh. 13, 1596.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रकॢप्त, Prepared, Kathās. 18, 366.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To prepare, 3, 264.<BR> 2. To further, Rām. 2, 31, 24.<BR> 3. To allot, Man. 7, 135.<BR> 4. To establish, Man. 8, 46.<BR> 5. To design, Bhāg. P. 4, 18, 20.<BR> 6. To make, Nal. 25, 5; Amar. 73 (अश्रु, To shed tears).<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus. To ordain, MBh. 3, 14110.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To change, MBh. 3, 697.<BR> 2. To be doubtful, Pañc. i. d. 385; to doubt, Pañc. i. d. 87.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To prepare in a different way, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 38.<BR> 2. To devise, Śāk. d. 51.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0217-b " target="_blank">Page0217-b + 40</a>] To doubt, Prab. 106, 7.<BR> 4. To presume, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To desire; अ-संकॢप्त, Not desired, MBh. 14, 1277.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To desire, Man. 2, 5.<BR> 2. To determine, MBh. 14, 4349.<BR> 3. To fancy, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 1.<BR> 4. To perform obsequies, Rām. 2, 72, 53.<BR> --With उपसम् उप-सम्, उपसंकॢप्त, Put on, Bhāg. P. 4, 9, 54.<BR> --Caus. To place, MBh. 16, 199.<BR> --Cf. Lat. corpus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

