गद्
1. गद् गद्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 13, 1138),<BR> 1. To recite, MBh. 3, 2642.<BR> 2. To speak, Rām. 4, 5, 31; to speak to, with acc. of the person and of the object, Rām. 2, 36, 1.<BR> गदित, Reckoned up, MBh. 3, 13425. n. Speech, Śāk. d. 81, v. r.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass., गद्य, n. A prosaic composition, MBh. 3, 966.<BR> --Desid. जिगदिष, To desire to speak, MBh. 12, 1604.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि,<BR> 1. To declare, MBh. 1, 4223.<BR> 2. To speak, Rām. 2, 40, 10. Pass. To be named, MBh. 1, 5308.<BR> निगदित, n. Speech, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 5.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer, MBh. 13, 5887.<BR> --With वि वि, विगदित, Spread, Rām. 2, 35, 15.<BR> --Cf. Goth. quithan; Engl. quoth; perhaps also βάζω (cf. गद्गद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदित
