गन्धि|गंधि
ऽगन्धि -गन्धि, A substitute for गन्ध, when the latter part of a comp. e. g. उत्पल-, adj. Smelling like lotus flowers, Rām. 5, 5, 12.<BR> उद्-, adj. Fragrant, Ragh. 16, 47.<BR> त्रि-सु-, n. The three perfumes, Suśr. 2, 483, 9.<BR> दुस्-, adj. Having no agreeable smell, Man. 6, 76.<BR> पुण्य-, adj. Having a fragrant smell, Chr. 34, 6.<BR> पूति-, adj. Stinking, MBh. 2, 2138.<BR> वि-, adj. Having a disagreeable smell, Bhartṛ. 2, 9.<BR> सु-,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fragrant.<BR> 2. Virtuous.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A perfume.<BR> 2. A fragrant sort of mango.<BR> III. n. The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिक|गंधिक|गन्धिकः
ऽगन्धिक -गन्धि + क, latter part of a comp.<BR> 1. Smelling,<BR> 2. Having only the smell of, e. g. भ्रातृ-, adj. Being a brother only nominally, not really, MBh. 3, 16111.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुगन्धिक
त्रि-सु- + गन्धिक त्रि-सु- + गन्धिक, n. the three perfumes, Suśr. 2, 493, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिन्|गंधिन्
गन्धिन् गन्धिन्, i. e. गन्ध + इन्, adj., f. नी, Fragrant, MBh. 14, 1398. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0252-b " target="_blank">Page0252-b + 45</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिन्
