गालोडय
गालोडय गालोडय, a denomin. (akin to the Caus. of गल्), Ātm. To examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह्
गाह् गाह् (akin to गभ् in गभीर and गाध् in गाध), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 13, 3795). With acc. and loc.<BR> 1. To dive into, Rām. 3, 76, 33.<BR> 2. To enter, Rām. 2, 52, 95.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. गाहित, with the sense of the act., MBh. 3, 8772.<BR> II. गाढ,<BR> 1. Used for bathing in, Ragh. 9, 72.<BR> 2. Accessible, open, Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 40.<BR> 3. Fast, tight, Rām. 4, 15, 20.<BR> 4. Vehement, Amar. 36; Megh. 81. ढम्, adv.<BR> 1. Strongly, fast, Mārk. P. 16, 25; Rām. 2, 31, 2.<BR> 2. Vehemently, Rām. 1, 9, 47.<BR> 3. Heavily, Chr. 35, 7.<BR> 4. Much, Rām. 2, 57, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव (sometimes व without its initial),<BR> 1. To dive into, Rām. 1, 2, 8.<BR> 2. To bathe, MBh. 3, 8649.<BR> 3. To betake one's self, Vikr. 62, 15. अवगाहित and अवगाढ, Used for bathing in, MBh. 3, 8230; 8236. अवगाढ,<BR> 1. Immersed, Rām. 2, 59, 28.<BR> 2. Deeply [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0263-b " target="_blank">Page0263-b + 41</a>] impressed, Śāk. d. 56.<BR> 3. Vanished, MBh. 4, 2238.<BR> 4. Stagnating, Suśr. 1, 353, 3.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To let bathe, Suśr. 2, 192, 11.<BR> 2. To bathe, Suśr. 2, 550, 11.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To dive, MBh. 1, 7285.<BR> 2. To break in, MBh. 4, 1984.<BR> 3. To sink down, to begin (as nightfall), MBh. 3, 16820.<BR> --With उद् उद् in उद्गाढ, Excessive, Prab. 67, 9.<BR> --With उप उप, To break in, Rām. 6, 31, 29.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To dive into, MBh. 14, 1392.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To dive into, Rām. 2, 48, 8.<BR> 2. To enter, Ragh. 14, 30.<BR> 3. To betake one's self to, MBh. 3, 11343.<BR> 4. To fall (as night; see वि-अव), MBh. 5, 7246. विगाढ,<BR> 1. Bathed, Rām. 5, 7, 39.<BR> 2. Used for bathing, Rām. 5, 74, 31.<BR> 3. Having penetrated, MBh. 4, 2072.<BR> 4. Fallen (as night; see वि-अव), MBh. 3, 1821.<BR> 5. Having taken place, MBh. 5, 2776.<BR> 6. Much, exceeding.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass., दुर्विगाह्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj.<BR> 1. Difficult to be sounded, MBh. 13, 1840.<BR> 2. Difficult to be passed, Hariv. 13670.<BR> 3. Difficult to be accomplished, Rām. 5, 51, 23.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To enter, Rām. 6, 16, 2.<BR> --Cf. βαθύς, βῆσσα for βηθ-ια, βένθος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाढ
दुस्-गाढ दुस्-गाढ, unfathomable, Hariv. 17484.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहन|गाहनं
