गेहिन् गेहिन्, i. e. गेह + इन्,<BR> I. m. A householder (cf. गृहिन्).<BR> II. f. इनी, The wife of a householder, Megh. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गै
गै गै, i. 1, गाय (in epic poetry गान्ति, instead of गायन्ति, from the original form of the vb. गा), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 1, 62, 20).<BR> 1. To sing, Man. 4, 64.<BR> 2. To teach, Bhāg. P. 4, 21, 40 (3 pl. Aor. अगुस्).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. गीत, Sung, Śāk. 4, 11. n. A song, Arj. 4, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. गेय, n. A song, Indr. 5, 27.<BR> --Caus. गापय,<BR> 1. To cause to sing, Kathās. 12, 31.<BR> 2. To cause to praise, Bhāg. P. 6, 17, 3. Frequent. जेगीय, To sing aloud, MBh. 12, 12200.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To sing in harmony with (with acc.), Gīt. 1, 39.<BR> 2. To accompany with singing, MBh. 1, 7913.<BR> 3. To sing, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0271-b " target="_blank">Page0271-b + 40</a>] Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 60. Pass. अनु-गीय, To be spoken of in songs, MBh. 12, 4211.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To sing, Rām. 1, 4, 24. अभिगीत, Filled with song, Rām. 6, 15, 11.<BR> --With अव अव, in अवगीत, Detested, Kir. 2, 7.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To sing, Bhāg. P. 7, 4, 39.<BR> 2. To celebrate by song, Ragh. 2, 12. उद्गीत, Filled with song, MBh. 3, 1533. n. song, MBh. 1, 6569.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To begin to sing, Prab. 80, 3.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To sing before somebody (with the acc. of the pson.), MBh. 1, 4809; उपगीयन्त्, anomalous ptcple. of the pres. pass. MBh. 15, 883.<BR> 2. To fill with song, MBh. 3, 11606.<BR> 3. To celebrate by song, Rām. 4, 44, 57.<BR> 4. To sing, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 41. उपगीत Singing in the vicinity, Śiś. 4, 57.<BR> --With नि नि, निगीत, Canted, Man. 9, 19.<BR> --With परि परि, To sing round a person, MBh. 6, 75.<BR> 2. To celebrate by song, MBh. 13, 4095.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To sing, Rām. 1, 4, 31. प्रगीत,<BR> 1. Filled with song, Rām. 1, 9, 17.<BR> 2. Singing, Kathās. 16, 85.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To sing, MBh. 8, 1836.<BR> --With वि वि, विगीत,<BR> 1. Inconsistent, contradictory, Man. 8, 53.<BR> 2. Abused.<BR> 3. Ill sung (i. e. गीत, with वि).<BR> --With सम् सम्, To celebrate by song, Bhāg. P. 3, 22, 23. संगीत, n.<BR> 1. A concert, Megh. 57.<BR> 2. Science of music and dancing, Lass. 67, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्गगीत
उपाङ्ग-गीत उपाङ्ग-गीत, n. a kind of song (perhaps of lascivious purport), Rājat. 5, 381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवद्गीता
