गोचर|गोचरः
गोचर गो-चर, m.<BR> 1. Pasture ground; in अद्भुत-, adj. Having excellent pasture ground, Rām. 4, 44, 80.<BR> 2. Stay, abode; used only as latter part of comp. adj., e. g. वन-, Inhabiting woods, Man. 8, 259; आकाश-, Moving in the air, Rām. 5, 3, 35. शरीरान्तर-, Being in the body, Rām. 6, 101, 30; यौवन-, Being in one's youth, MBh. 1, 3168.<BR> 3. Reach, province; हर्तुर् याति न गोचरम्, Comes not within the reach of a robber, i. e. cannot be robbed, Bhartṛ. 2, 49; वाण-, m. The reach of an arrow-shot, MBh. 1, 2833; अ-वाङ्-मनस-, adj. Within the reach neither of speech nor thought, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 3.<BR> 4. The range of the eyes, MBh. 7, 5616.<BR> 5. An object of sense, as sound, shape, etc., Bhag. 13, 5.<BR> 6. An object of devotion, MBh. 13, 4349.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचनगोचर|लोचनगोचरः
लोचन- + गोचर लोचन- + गोचर,<BR> I. m. the range of the eyes, horizon, Pañc. v. d. 82.<BR> II. adj. accessible to the eyes, Bhartṛ. 1, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोचनगोचर
