चुञ्चु|चुंचु|चुञ्चुः
चुञ्चु चुञ्चु,<BR> I. m. The name of a mixed class, Man. 10, 48.<BR> II. as latter part of comp. words, Renowned, known; see चञ्चु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्
† चुट् चुट्, i. 6 and 10, Par. To cut.<BR> --i. 1 and 10, Par. To become small (cf. चुट्ट्, of which it is a v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्ट्
† चुट्ट् चुट्ट्, i. 10, Par. To become [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b " target="_blank">Page0308-b + 40</a>] small (probably a dialectical form of a denomin. derived from क्षुद्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्
† चुड् चुड्, or बुड् बुड्, i. 6, Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्ड्
† चुड्ड् चुड्ड्, i. 1, Par. To dally, to wanton (or to guess, to act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्
† चुण् चुण्, i. 6, Par. To cut, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्ट्|चुंट्
† चुण्ट् चुण्ट्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To cut.<BR> --i. 1, Par. To become small.<BR> --Cf. चुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्टा|चुंटा
चुण्टा चुण्टा and टी, f. A well, Suśr. 1, 169, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्ठ्
† चुण्ठ् चुण्ठ्, i. 10, Par. To hurt, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्ड्|चुंड्
† चुण्ड् चुण्ड्, i. 1, Par. To become small (cf. चुट्).<BR> --i. 10, Par. To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत्
† चुत् चुत्, v. r. of च्युत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुद्
चुद् चुद् (for primitive श्चुद्, cf. च्यु), in the Vedas, i. 1, Par., Ātm. To speed. In classical language, i. 10, Par. (also Ātm. MBh. 13, 578), or rather Caus.<BR> 1. To push on, Arj. 4, 37.<BR> 2. To impel, MBh. 1, 5986.<BR> 3. To order, Draup. 8, 1.<BR> 4. To ask, MBh. 13, 578.<BR> 5. To ordain, Man. 2, 165.<BR> 6. To mention, Man. 3, 26.<BR> 7. To lay a stress upon, Śiś. 9, 16 (न चोद्यम् अदस्, It is not to be wondered at).<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. चोद्य, n. A question, MBh. 5, 1653.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus.<BR> 1. To impel, Chr. 4, 17.<BR> 2. To order, Rājat. 3, 67.<BR> 3. To announce, MBh. 3, 11396.<BR> 4. To inquire, MBh. 1, 2913.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus.<BR> 1. To wield, Hariv. 15892.<BR> 2. To impel, MBh. 14, 2387.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To push on, MBh. 3, 12095.<BR> 2. To impel, Rām. 3, 28, 42.<BR> 3. To command, Man. 2, 291.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a " target="_blank">Page0309-a + 37</a>] To ask, Man. 4, 248.<BR> 5. To proclaim, Man. 3, 228.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, Caus. To impel, MBh. 1, 575.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To wield, MBh. 7, 559.<BR> 2. To push on, to impel, MBh. 3, 12109; 1, 4875.<BR> 3. To invite, Rām. 1, 4, 32.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. To push on, to impel, Rām. 3, 28, 40. प्रतिचोदित, One who has turned himself against (with the acc.), Rām. 4, 61, 48.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus.<BR> 1. To wield, MBh. 3, 12238.<BR> 2. To push on, to impel, MBh. 3, 756; Rām. 2, 40, 40.<BR> 3. To further, Rām. 6, 95, 59.<BR> --Cf. Goth. skiutan; A.S. sceótan; O.H.G. sciozan; probably σπεύδειν; Lat. studere; perhaps Goth. giutan: A.S. geotan.<BR> --Cf. च्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुन्द्
चुन्द् चुन्द्, see बुन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुप्
1. चुप् चुप्, i. 1, Par. To move, MBh. 3, 10648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुप्
2. चुप् चुप्, see छुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्ब्|चुंब्
1. चुम्ब् चुम्ब्, i. 1, and 10, Par. (i. 1, Ātm., Pañc. iv. d. 7), To kiss Ṛt. 6, 14.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be kissed, Daśak. 49, 9.<BR> --With परि परि, to kiss warmly, Amar. 77. परिचुम्बित, Closesurrounded, Caurap. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्ब्|चुंब्
† 2. चुम्ब् चुम्ब्, i. 10, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बक|चुंबक|चुंबकः|चुम्बकः
चुम्बक 1. चुम्ब् + अक, m. A loadstone, Prab. 108, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बन|चुंबन|चुंबनं|चुम्बनं
चुम्बन चुम्ब् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Kissing, Pañc. 263, 5.<BR> 2. Kiss, Rājat. 5, 383.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बिन्|चुंबिन्
चुम्बिन् चुम्ब् + इन्, adj. Kissing, Caurap. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुर्
चुर् चुर्. i. 10, चोरय, † i. 1, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b " target="_blank">Page0309-b + 42</a>] Par.<BR> 1. To steal, Man. 8, 333.<BR> 2. To steal from, Hariv. 11146.<BR> --Cf. चोर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्
† चुल् चुल्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To rise.<BR> 2. To let down, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्प्|चुलुंप्
† चुलुम्प् चुलुम्प्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To rock.<BR> 2. To break(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल्
† चुल्ल् चुल्ल्, i. 1, Par. To dally, to wanton (or, to guess, to act), v. r.<BR> --Cf. चुड्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ली
चुल्ली चुल्ली, f. A fire-place, Man. 3, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूचुक|चूचुकं
चूचुक चूचुक (cf. चूष्), n.<BR> 1. A nipple, Suśr. 1, 349, 17.<BR> 2. The breast, Rām. 6, 23, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूड|चूडः
चूड चूड,<BR> I. m. or n. The ceremony of cutting the hair.<BR> II. f. डा.<BR> 1. A single lock of hair left on the crown of the head at the ceremony of tonsure.<BR> 2. The hair.<BR> 3. The ceremony of cutting the hair.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतचूड|कृतचूडः
कृत-चूड कृत-चूड, adj. one whose head has been shorn, Man. 5, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रचूड|चंद्रचूड|चन्द्रचूडः
चन्द्र- + चूड चन्द्र- + चूड, m. a name of Śiva, ताम्र-,<BR> I. adj. having a red cock's comb.<BR> II. m. 1. a cock. 2. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचूड
पञ्चचूड पञ्चचूड, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. adj. having five tufts of hair.<BR> II. f. डा, the name of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करचूड
पुष्कर- + चूड पुष्कर- + चूड, m. the name of one of the four elephants who are supposed to support the world, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णचूड|स्वर्णचूडः
स्वर्ण- + चूड स्वर्ण- + चूड, m. 1. a cock. 2. the blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडक|चूडकः
ऽचूडक -चूडक, A substitute for -चूदा, when the latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. निर्वृत्त-, i. e. निस्- (vb. वृत्), adj. One whose head has been shorn, Man. 5, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाल|चूडालं
चूडाल चूडा + ल, adj., f. ला, Having a tuft of hair on the crown of the head, MBh. 10, 288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूण्
† चूण् चूण्, i. 10, Par. To contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूत|चूतः
चूत चूत, m. The mango, Mangifera indica, Rām. 3, 79, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्
† चूर् चूर्, i. 4, Ātm. To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण्
चूर्ण् चूर्ण्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par.<BR> 1. To grind, Suśr. 2, 56, 3.<BR> 2. To crush, MBh. 3, 12133.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To powder, to cover with a ground substance, Suśr. 1, 46, 14; MBh. 8, 456.<BR> 2. To cover, MBh. 2, 813.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To crush, MBh. 8, 4665.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To grind, MBh. 1, 4773.<BR> 2. To crush, Rām. 6, 87, 23.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To grind, Suśr. 1, 162, 19.<BR> 2. To crush, MBh. 7, 1394; Rājat. 5, 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण चूर्ण (an old ptcple. pf. pass. akin to चर्व्), m. and n. Any pulverulent or minute division of substance.<BR> 1. Flour, Pañc. 121, 11.<BR> 2. Dust, MBh. 3, 10972.<BR> 3. Powder, MBh. 6, 5764.<BR> 4. Aromatic powder, Megh. 69.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगचूर्ण
योग- + चूर्ण योग- + चूर्ण, m. or n. magical powder, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागचूर्ण|रागचूर्णः
राग- + चूर्ण राग- + चूर्ण, m. 1. a name of Kāma. 2. red lead. 3. the red powder thrown over one another by the Hindus, at the festival called Holi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णक|चूर्णकं|चूर्णकः
चूर्णक चूर्ण + क, n. Aromatic powder, Suśr. 2, 392, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णता
चूर्णता चूर्ण + ता, f. State of powder, Rājat. 5, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णशस्
चूर्णशस् चूर्ण + शस्, adv. Into powder, MBh. 1, 3225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिका
चूर्णिका चूर्णिका, i. e. चूर्ण + क, f. A sort of pastry, Lass. 11, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिन्
चूलिन् चूलिन्, i. e. चूडा + इन्,<BR> 1. adj. Having a crest, Hariv. 2495; 4440.<BR> 2. m. A proper name, Rām. 1, 34, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्
चूष् चूष्, i. 1. Par.<BR> 1. To suck.<BR> 2. pass. To fester (of wounds), Suśr. 1, 103, 17.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. चूष्य, To be sucked, Pañc. 61, 13.<BR> --Caus. To suck up, Suśr. 2, 33, 16.<BR> --With the prep सम् सम्, pass. To boil up, Suśr. 2, 486, 10.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. sûgere, succus; A.S. súcan; O.H.G. sûgan (cf. चक्ष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृत्
चृत् चृत्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To connect together.<BR> 2. To kill.<BR> --Cf. छृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृप्
† चृप् चृप्, i. 1, and 10, Par. To light, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेट|चेटः
चेट चेट, m. f. टी, A slave, a servant, Kathās. 6, 127; Rām. 2, 91, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटक|चेटकः
चेटक चेट + क, m., f. टिका, A slave, a servant, Bhartṛ. 1, 91; Kathās. 4, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतन|चेतनः
चेतन चेतन, i. e. 1. चित् + अन,<BR> I. m. A sentient being, Megh. 5.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. Consciousness, Bhāg. P. 4, 21, 34.<BR> 2. Recollection, Pañc. 35, 11. (˚नां लब्ध्वा, After having recovered his senses).<BR> 3. Intellect, Man. 9, 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतन|अचेतनः
अ- + चेतन अ- + चेतन, adj., f. ना. 1. insensible, Bhartṛ. 2, 30. 2. unconscious of one's self, Nal. 13, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेतन
निस्- + चेतन निस्- + चेतन, adj. 1. unreasonable, Rām. 2, 41, 6. 2. unconscious of one's self, Pañc. 146, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतन
वि- + चेतन वि- + चेतन, adj. unconscious, senseless, lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतन
स- + चेतन स- + चेतन, adj. recovering one's senses, Pañc. 43, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनावन्त्|चेतनावत्
चेतनावन्त् चेतना + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Sentient, MBh. 14, 529.<BR> 2. Discreet, MBh. 12, 2449.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयितृ
चेतयितृ चेतयितृ, i. e. 1. चित्, Caus., + तृ, m. A perceiver, MBh. 12, 7693.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस् चेतस्, i. e. 1. चित् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Intellect, Nal. 11, 24.<BR> 2. Consciousness, MBh. 7, 6935.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतस्
अ- + चेतस् अ- + चेतस्, adj. unconscious of one's self, Chr. 31, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचेतस्
दुष्ट- + चेतस् दुष्ट- + चेतस्, adj. malevolent, Man. 3, 225. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a " target="_blank">Page0311-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्
निस् निस्, adj. senseless, Rām. 2, 77, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दचेतस्|मंदचेतस्
मन्द- + चेतस् मन्द- + चेतस्, adj. fainting, Chr. 29, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतस्
वि- + चेतस् वि- + चेतस्, adj. 1. stupid. 2. perplexed, unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलचेतस्
व्याकुल- + चेतस् व्याकुल- + चेतस्, adj. bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतस्
स- + चेतस् स- + चेतस्, adj. intelligent, Bhāṣāp. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतिष्ठ
चेतिष्ठ चेतिष्ठ, superl. of 1. चित् + तृ, adj. Wisest, Lass. 101, 3 = Rigv. vii. 16, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतोमन्त्|चेतोमत्
चेतोमन्त् चेतोमन्त्, i. e. चेतस् + मन्त्, adj. Living, MBh. 3, 8676.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेद्
चेद् चेद्, i. e. च-इद्, a particle.<BR> 1. Even, MBh. 1, 2403.<BR> 2. If, Man. 7, 25.<BR> 3. With preceding नो it forms usually a short sentence, which must be completed by the preceding words, e. g. भवता मौनव्रतेन स्थातव्यम् नो चेत् तव काष्ठात् पातो भविष्यति, You must be silent, if not you will fall from the stick, Pañc. 76, 20.<BR> 4. With preceding न sometimes, That not, Rām. 5, 80, 24.<BR> 5. With preceding इति and following न, viz. इति चेन् न, a common form of concluding an opponent's objection, and proceeding to answer it.<BR> --Cf. probably वै᳓.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदि|चेदिः
चेदि चेदि, m. pl. The name of a people, Nal. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्
† चेल् चेल्, i. 1, Par. To move.<BR> --Cf. चल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल चेल, n. Cloth, Man. 11, 166; raiment, Man. 4, 216.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचेल|कुचेलः
कु- + चेल कु- + चेल, n. coarse vesture, Man. 6, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेल
स- + चेल स- + चेल, adj. clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्ल्
चेल्ल् चेल्ल्, v. r. of चेल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट्
चेष्ट् चेष्ट्, i. 1, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To struggle, to move in convulsions, MBh. 3, 2542.<BR> 2. To stir, Matsyop. 22.<BR> 3. To strive, MBh. 6, 3642.<BR> 4. To perform, MBh. 13, 4676.<BR> 5. To act, Bhag. 3, 13.<BR> 6. To frequent, Ragh. 9, 51. Ptcple of the pf. pass. चेष्टित, n.<BR> 1. Motion, gesture, Man. 8, 25.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b " target="_blank">Page0311-b + 42</a>] Action, Man. 2, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To cause to move, MBh. 3, 13981.<BR> 2. To impel, Rām. 6, 94, 24.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To strive too much, Hit. i. d. 170.<BR> --With आ आ, To perform, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 1.<BR> --With परि परि, To welter, Rām. 4, 19, 32.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To stretch, MBh. 7, 3168.<BR> 2. To struggle against, Draup. 9, 3.<BR> 3. To move in convulsions, Rām. 2, 77, 20.<BR> 4. To surround, Hariv. 10200.<BR> 5. To move, Rām. 3, 54, 10.<BR> 6. To struggle, Rām. 2, 66, 21.<BR> 7. To act, Man. 8, 334. विचेष्टित, n.<BR> 1. Action, Pañc. 95, 16.<BR> 2. Evil or malicious act (i. e. चेष्टित, with वि).<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To shrink up, MBh. 7, 3168.<BR> 2. To crowd together (from fear), MBh. 5, 1855.<BR> 3. To strive, MBh. 3, 2923.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चेष्ट्
दुस्- + चेष्ट् दुस्- + चेष्ट्, n. acting perversely, Bhartṛ. 1, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट|चेष्टं
चेष्ट चेष्ट् + अ,<BR> I. n. and f. टा.<BR> 1. Motion, Kathās. 23, 84.<BR> 2. Gesture, Man. 7, 63; 8, 26.<BR> 3. Action, Hariv. 5939; Man. 4, 63.<BR> II. f. टा, Acting, activity, Man. 1, 65.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मचेष्टा|कर्म्मचेष्टा
कर्मचेष्टा कर्मचेष्टा, i. e. कर्मन्-, f. 1. acting, business, Man. 1, 66. 2. action, Nal. 23, 18 (16, read कर्मचेष्टाभि˚). 3. exertion, Rām. 2, 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्ट|निश्चेष्टः
निश्चेष्ट निश्चेष्ट, i. e. निस्-, adj. deprived of motion, Rām. 2, 45, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेष्ट|सचेष्टः
स- + चेष्ट स- + चेष्ट,<BR> I. adj. making effort, active.<BR> II. m. the mango, Mangifera indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टन|चेष्टनं
चेष्टन चेष्ट् + अन, n. Motion, Man. 12, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टयितृ
चेष्टयितृ चेष्टयितृ, i. e. चेष्ट्, Caus., + त्रि, m. The being who causes motion, MBh. 12, 1181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टावन्त्|चेष्टावत्
चेष्टावन्त् चेष्टा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Moveable, Suśr. 1, 340, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्य|चैतन्यं|चैतन्यः
चैतन्य चैतन्य, i. e. चेतन + य, n.<BR> 1. Intellect. Yājñ. 3, 81.<BR> 2. Consciousness, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a " target="_blank">Page0312-a + 41</a>] Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 18.<BR> 3. Soul, spirit, MBh. 14, 529.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्त
चैत्त चैत्त, i. e. चित्त + अ, adj. Belonging to the dominion of thought, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य चैत्य,<BR> I. probably चिति + य, m. The individual soul, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 61.<BR> II. चिता + य, m. and n.<BR> 1. A tomb, MBh. 12, 914.<BR> 2. An altar, Rām. 1, 13, 30.<BR> 3. A religious building, Rām. 5, 17, 20.<BR> 4. A sacred tree; a religious fig-tree growing in a village, or near it, and held in veneration by the villagers, Hiḍ. 1, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामचैत्य|ग्रामचैत्यः
ग्राम- + चैत्य ग्राम- + चैत्य, m. a sacred tree growing in a village, Megh. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्र|चैत्रं|चैत्रः
चैत्र चैत्र, i. e. चित्र and चित्रा + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Made of a tree called citra, MBh. 7, 76.<BR> II. m. The name of a month, March--April, Man. 7, 182.<BR> III. f. त्री, The day of the full-moon in this month, MBh. 12, 3691.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ|चैत्ररथं
चैत्ररथ चैत्ररथ, i. e. चित्र-रथ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Treating of the Gandharva Citraratha, MBh. 1, 313.<BR> II. patron. m. and f. थी, A descendant of Citraratha, MBh. 1, 3740; Hariv. 712.<BR> III. n. The name of a forest, Rām. 1, 28, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैल|चैलः
चैल चैल, cf. चेल, n.<BR> 1. Cloth, Man. 5, 119.<BR> 2. Raiment, Man. 5, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलधाव|चैलधावः
चैलधाव चैल-धाव् + अ, m. A washer, Yājñ. 1, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलाशक|चैलाशकः
चैलाशक चैलाशक, i. e. चैल-आशक (vb. अश् + अक), m. The name of a demon, Man. 12, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोक्ष|चोक्षः
चोक्ष चोक्ष (cf. चौक्ष), adj. Clean, pure, Man. 3, 207; MBh. 12, 2708.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदक|चोदकः
चोदक चोदक, i. e. चुद् + अक, adj. Impelling, calling, MBh. 13, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदन
चोदन चोदन, i. e. चुद् + अन, n. and f. ना.<BR> 1. Inciting, invitation, MBh. 13, 41; Bhag. 18, 18.<BR> 2. Command, Man. 2, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदयितृ
चोदयितृ चोदयितृ, i. e. चुद्, Caus., + तृ, m., f. त्री, n. Inciting, an inciter, Kumāras. 3, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोर|चोरः
चोर चोर, i. e. चुर् + अ, m. A thief, Chr. 53, 1.<BR> --Cf. ϕώρ; Lat. fur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरितक|चोरितकं
चोरितक चोरित + क (vb. चुर्), n. A stolen object, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोल|चोलः
चोल चोल, and चोलक चोल + क, m. pl. The name of a people, Rām. 4, 41, 18; Kathās. 19, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष|चोषः
चोष चोष (cf. चूष्), m. Burning (of diseases), Suśr. 1, 37, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष्य|चोष्यं
चोष्य चोष्य (cf. चूष्, of which it is an anomalous ptcle. fut. pass.), adj. What is to be sucked, Rām. 1, 52, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष|चौक्षं
चौक्ष चौक्ष, i. e. चुक्षा (Washing? Grammar.) + अ, adj. Clean, MBh. 12, 4315.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष्य
चौक्ष्य चौक्ष्य = the last, MBh. 12, 7049.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौड
चौड चौड, i. e. चूडा + अ, n. The ceremony of cutting the hair, Man. 2, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर|चौरः
चौर चौर, i. e. चुरा, Theft (Grammar.) + अ, m.<BR> 1. A thief, Man. 4, 118.<BR> 2. The robber of a heart; in the title, चौर-पञ्चाशिका, The fifty strophes of a robber of a heart.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिचौर|भित्तिचौरः
भित्ति- + चौर भित्ति- + चौर and वन्दि-, m. a housebreaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचौर|स्त्रीचौरः
स्त्री- + चौर स्त्री- + चौर, m. a libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरिका
चौरिका चौरिका, i. e. चौर + क, f.<BR> 1. Theft, Pañc. v. d. 41.<BR> 2. Fraud, Pañc. 199, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्य|चौर्यं|चौर्य्य|चौर्य्यं
चौर्य चौर्य, i. e. चौर + य, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a " target="_blank">Page0313-a + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Theft, Man. 9, 276.<BR> 2. Fraud, Hariv. 15163.<BR> 3. Stealth, Pañc. i. d. 190 (चौर्य-रत, literally, enjoyment of love by stealth, i. e. adultery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्यक|चौर्यकं
चौर्यक चौर्य + क, n. Theft, MBh. 12, 8501.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौल
चौल चौल, i. e. चूडा + अ, n. The ceremony of cutting the hair, Ragh. 3, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवन|च्यवनं|च्यवनः
च्यवन च्यवन, i. e. च्यु + अन,<BR> I. m. The name of a Ṛṣi, MBh. 1, 870.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Motion, Suśr. 1, 48, 12.<BR> 2. Loss, Bhāg. P. 8, 20, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावन
च्यावन च्यावन, i. e. च्यु, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj. Felling, MBh. 8, 1506.<BR> II. n. Expelling, Hariv. 1512.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
1. च्यु च्यु (for original श्च्यु, cf. श्च्युत्), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.),<BR> 1. To move (ved.).<BR> 2. To depart, Rām. 2, 72, 5.<BR> 3. To fly, Rām. 3, 33, 16.<BR> 4. (with abl.), To swerve, MBh. 2, 2357; Man. 7, 98 (अस्माद् धर्मान् न च्यवेत क्षत्रियः, From this law a king must never depart).<BR> 5. To become deprived, to lose (with the abl.), Man. 3, 140.<BR> 6. To fall, Rām. 5, 13, 31.<BR> 7. To perish, Man. 12, 96.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अ-च्युत,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Unshakeable, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4; firm, MBh. 1, 7770.<BR> 2. Imperishable, Chr. 51, 18.<BR> II. m. A name of Viṣṇu, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 20.<BR> --Caus. च्यावय,<BR> 1. To expel, MBh. 3, 15920.<BR> 2. To cause to fall, MBh. 13, 324.<BR> 3. To deprive (with two acc.), Rām. 2, 53, 7.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि,<BR> 1. To fly, MBh. 7, 5220.<BR> 2. To swerve, Rām. 4, 16, 20.<BR> 3. To become deprived, to lose, Rām. 4, 16, 8.<BR> 4. To escape, Mārk. P. 15, 38.<BR> 5. To come down, MBh. 3, 11614.<BR> 6. To surround, MBh. 7, 6449.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To depart, Man. 9, 273.<BR> 2. To proceed, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b " target="_blank">Page0313-b + 40</a>] Rām. 4, 44, 47.<BR> 3. To fall, Rām. 2, 91, 21.<BR> 4. To become deprived, Rām. 3, 53, 22. अ-प्रच्युत, adj. Not swerving, Man. 12, 116.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To shake, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 3.<BR> 2. To expel, Pañc. 86, 13.<BR> 3. To cause to fall, MBh. 7, 1717.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To fall asunder, Bhāg. P. 8, 12, 21; to split, Rām. 3, 35, 53.<BR> 2. To depart, Man. 9, 273. अ-विच्युत, Unperishable, Yājñ. 1, 212. ˚तम्, adv. Faultless, Yājñ. 3, 112.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To remove, MBh. 7, 7515.<BR> --Cf. σεύω, ἔσσευον, etc.; Goth. skevjan, skura, vinthi-skauro; A.S. scur; Engl. shower; O.H.G. spuon; A.S. spëovan; O.H.G. spua + t, spuatôn; A.S. spaedan; see चुद्; χέω; Lat. jacere (Causal = च्यावय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
† 2. च्यु च्यु, i. 10, Par. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत्
च्युत् च्युत् (cf. च्यु and श्च्युत्), i. 1, Par. To drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युति|च्युतिः
च्युति च्यु + ति, f.<BR> 1. Departing, MBh. 1, 4169.<BR> 2. Not doing one's duty, Bhartṛ. suppl. 10.<BR> 3. Perishing, Kumāras. 3, 10.<BR> 4. Flowing out, Pañc. i. d. 371.<BR> 5. Fall, Bhartṛ. 3, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भच्युति|गर्भच्युतिः
गर्भ- + च्युति गर्भ- + च्युति, f. abortion, Hit. Pr. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस्
† च्युस् च्युस्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To laugh.<BR> 2. To leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगल|छगलं|छगलः
छगल छगल, m. A goat, Suśr. 1, 203, 19. f ती, A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा छटा, f.<BR> 1. A lump, a mass, Kathās. 25, 274.<BR> 2. An assemblage, a multitude, Śiś. 1, 47.<BR> 3. Light, splendour, Prab. 65, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्र
छत्त्र छत्त्र, i. e. छद् + त्र, usually written छत्र छत्र,<BR> I. n. A parasol, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a " target="_blank">Page0314-a + 41</a>] Man. 2, 178; one of the insignia of a king, Rājat. 5, 18.<BR> II. f. रा, The name of a plant, Suśr. 2, 170, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. castrum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्त्र
अहिच्छत्त्र अहिच्छत्त्र, i. e. अहि-, m. the name of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रधारत्व
छत्त्रधारत्व छत्त्र-धार + त्व, n. The office of bearing the royal parasol, Pañc. 63, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रवन्त्|छत्रवत्
छत्त्रवन्त् छत्त्र + वन्त्,<BR> 1. adj., f. वती, Having a parasol, Suśr. 1, 30, 2.<BR> 2. f. वती, The name of a town or country, MBh. 1, 6348.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्राक
छत्त्राक छत्त्राक, i. e. छत्र + आक, n. A mushroom, Man. 5, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रिन्
छत्त्रिन् छत्त्रिन्, i. e. छत्त्र + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Having a parasol, Rām. 1, 31, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
1. छद् छद्, i. 10, छादय, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm. Rām. 4, 58, 7); † i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 1, 8245.<BR> 2. To conceal, Rām. 5, 90, 16.<BR> 3. To eclipse, Pañc. i. d. 319. Anomalous ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. छादयान, MBh. 6, 2430.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> 1. छादित, Kathās. 17, 44.<BR> 2. छन्न, Rām. 1, 74, 16; ˚नम्, adv. Secretly, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 10; tacitly, Man. 9, 98; n. A hiding-place, Hariv. 8686.<BR> --With the prep. समभि सम्-अभि, To cover, MBh. 12, 255.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 1, 5421.<BR> 2. To leave unlighted, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 30. अवच्छन्न, Filled, MBh. 12, 5835.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव,<BR> 1. To cover, Hariv. 6444.<BR> 2. To obscure, MBh. 6, 94.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To cover, Rām. 1, 13, 29.<BR> 2. To obscure, MBh. 4, 1853.<BR> 3. To clothe, Man. 3, 27.<BR> 4. To put on, MBh. 2, 789.<BR> 5. To conceal, Hit. 22, 1.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 3, 12179.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b " target="_blank">Page0314-b + 41</a>] veil, MBh. 3, 15670.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To unclothe, Rām. 2, 91, 51.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 1, 5005.<BR> 2. To conceal, Man. 8, 249.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To cover, Pañc. 144, 23.<BR> 2. To disguise, Rām. 1, 9, 9.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 2, 2626.<BR> 2. To obscure, MBh. 1, 4416.<BR> 3. To conceal, Chr. 51, 5.<BR> 4. To disguise, Man. 4, 198. प्रच्छन्न, Secret, Man. 5, 107. ˚नम्, adv.<BR> 1. Privately, Man. 9, 228.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To cover, Pañc. 224, 4.<BR> 2. To endow, MBh. 3, 1268.<BR> 3. To obscure, MBh. 7, 6129.<BR> 4. To disguise, Rām. 3, 51, 27.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To cover, Rām. 2, 93, 3.<BR> 2. To obscure, MBh. 1, 8235.<BR> 3. To conceal, MBh. 13, 2606.<BR> --Cf. Goth. skadus, shadow; σκήνη (for σκαδ-νη), σκότος, which show that the primitive form of छद् was स्कद्; cf. also Lat. castrum, and छाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुच्छन्न
सु- + छन्न सु- + छन्न, adj. well-concealed, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
† 2. छद् छद्, i. 1, Par. To make strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
ऽछद् -छद्, Latter part of comp. adj. Covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद छद् + अ, m. A cover, Mṛcch. 15, 19.<BR> 2. A leaf, Pañc. ii. d. 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरच्छद|उत्तरच्छदः
उत्तर- + छद उत्तर- + छद, 1. a cover, MBh. 13, 746. 2. a coverlet, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनच्छद
घन- + छद घन- + छद, adj. covered by clouds, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छद|तनुच्छदः
तनु- + छद तनु- + छद, 1. adj. covering the body, Rām. 4, 63, 2. 2. m. a coat of mail, MBh. 12, 4424.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तच्छद|दंतच्छद|दन्तच्छदः
दन्त- + छद दन्त- + छद and दशन-, m. a lip, Ṛt. 4, 12; Rām. 5, 45, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्छद
दुस्- + छद दुस्- + छद, adj. ill-covering, Rām. 2, 32, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदछद|रदच्छद|रदच्छदः
रद- + छद रद- + छद and रदन-, m. a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितछद|सितच्छद|सितच्छदः
सित- + छद सित- + छद, m. a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदन|छदनं
छदन छद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Covering, a cover, Rām. 2, 56, 32.<BR> 2. A wing, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a " target="_blank">Page0315-a + 41</a>] MBh. 3, 11595.<BR> 3. A leaf, Suśr. 1, 305, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदि|छदिः
छदि छद् + इ, The cover of a carriage, Bhāg. P. 3, 21, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिस्
छदिस् छद् + इस्, n. A roof, Kathās. 2, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन् छद् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. Disguise, Rām. 3, 53, 28.<BR> 2. Hypocrisy, Rām. 4, 16, 16.<BR> 3. Fraud, Man. 4, 199.<BR> 4. Pretext, Megh. 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटच्छद्मन्
कूट- + छद्मन् कूट- + छद्मन्, m. a rogue, Pañc. i. d. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मिन्
ऽछद्मिन् -छद्मिन्, i. e. छद्मन् + इन्, adj. Latter part of comp. adj. Disguised as, MBh. 3, 16957.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छनच्छन्
छनच्छन् छनच्छन्, i. e. repeated छनत् before इति, A word imitative of the sound of falling drops, Amar. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द्|छंद्
छन्द् छन्द्, i. 1 and 10, Par. (ved. also छदय, Par., Ātm.).<BR> --i. 1.<BR> 1. To appear (ved.).<BR> 2. To please.<BR> --i. 10, or rather Caus.<BR> 1. To wait on, Rām. 2, 97, 1; Chr. 48, 8.<BR> 2. To present (especially with वरेण), Rām. 6, 4, 43.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, i. 1, To desire, MBh. 12, 7378.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus.<BR> 1. To wait on, Ragh. 5, 58.<BR> 2. To seduce, Prab. 101, 10.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To wait on, to present, MBh. 3, 13507.<BR> --Cf. Lat. spons, spontis for spond + ti, spondeo; σπένδειν.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द|छंद|छन्दः
छन्द छन्द् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Flattering, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Appearance, Hariv. 8359.<BR> 2. Wish, Rām. 2, 9, 7.<BR> 3. Will, Yājñ. 2, 195.<BR> 4. Self-help, Man. 8, 176.<BR> 5. Power, MBh. 12, 1820.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छन्द
अ- + छन्द अ- + छन्द, m. unwillingness, Hariv. 8557 (against the will).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परछन्द|परच्छन्द|परच्छंद|परच्छन्दः
पर- + छन्द पर- + छन्द, m. dependence, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वछन्द|स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्दः
स्व- + छन्द स्व- + छन्द,<BR> I. m. 1. one's own will, Hit. i. d. 62. 2. independence, Rām. 1, 34, 28. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b " target="_blank">Page0315-b + 39</a>]<BR> II. adj. 1. independent, Rām. 1, 36, 17. 2. following one's own will, Hit. ii. d. 135. 3. spontaneous. 4. uncultivated.<BR> III. ˚दम्, adv. by one's own will, Yājñ. 2, 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दतस्
छन्दतस् छन्द + तस्, adv. By one's own will, Yājñ. 3, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्|छंदस्
छन्दस् छन्द् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Pleasure, MBh. 12, 7376.<BR> 2. A holy hymn, MBh. 5, 1224.<BR> 3. The Vedas, MBh. 12, 12933.<BR> 4. Poetical metre, Bhag. 10, 35.<BR> 5. Metrics, Pañc. ii. d. 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छन्दस्|निश्छंदस्
निश्-छन्दस् निश्-छन्दस्, i. e. निस्-, adj. where the Vedas are not studied, Man. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्कृत|छंदस्कृत
छन्दस्कृत छन्दस्-कृत (vb. कृ), n. The metrical part of the Vedas, Man. 4, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोग|छंदोग|छन्दोगः
छन्दोग छन्दोग, i. e. छन्दस्-ग (vb. गै), m. A chanter of the Sāma-Veda, Man. 3, 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोमय
छन्दोमय छन्दोमय, i. e. छन्दस् + मय, adj., f. यी, Having the Vedas as one's substance, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्
† छम् छम्, i. 1, Par. To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमच्छमित
छमच्छमित छमच्छमित, n. i. e. repeated छमत्, an imitative sound, + इत, n. Crackling, Mārk. P. 8, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्प्|छंप्
† छम्प् छम्प्, i. 10, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द्
छर्द् छर्द्, i. 10, Par. To vomit, see छृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दि|छर्दिः|छर्द्दि|छर्द्दिः
छर्दि छर्दि, i. e. छृद् + इ, f. Nausea, vomiting, Suśr. 1, 108, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
छर्दिस् छर्दिस्, n. A secure habitation, Chr. 288, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल|छलं|छलः
छल छल (cf. vb. स्खल्),<BR> 1. Fraud, Rām. 4, 57, 10.<BR> 2. Artful management, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a " target="_blank">Page0316-a + 40</a>] Man. 8, 49.<BR> 3. Pretext, Śiś. 9, 48.<BR> 4. Intention, Mārk. P. 25, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलक
छलक छलक (cf. vb. स्खल्), adj. sbst. Deceiving, a deceiver, Hariv. 11476.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलन|छलनं
छलन छलन (cf. vb. स्खल्), n. Deceiving, MBh. 6, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलय
छलय छलय (a denominative derived from छल), Par. To deceive, MBh. 3, 15560. Anomalous infinitive, छलितुम्, Rām. 6, 86, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिक|छलिकं
छलिक छलिक, n. A kind of song, Mālav. 16, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छवि|छविः
छवि छवि (cf. vb. स्कु), f.<BR> 1. Hide, skin, Hariv. 15709.<BR> 2. Colour, Ṛt. 6, 20.<BR> 3. Beauty, Ragh. 9, 34.<BR> 4. Splendour, Śiś. 9, 3.<BR> --Cf. Goth. skauns, gutha-skaunei; A.S. sceone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छष्
† छष् छष् (v. r. कश् and कष्), i. 1, Par., Ātm. To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग छाग (cf. छगल),<BR> I. m. A goat, Man. 3, 269.<BR> II. adj. Produced from a goat, or a she-goat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनछाग|वनच्छाग|वनच्छागः
वन- + छाग वन- + छाग, m. 1. a wild goat. 2. a hog, Yājñ. 1, 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागमय
छागमय छाग + मय, adj., f. यी, Resembling a goat, MBh. 3, 14399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल छागल, i. e. छगल + अ,<BR> I. adj. Produced from a goat, or a shegoat, Suśr. 2, 12, 18.<BR> II. m. A goat, Rām. 6, 19, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्र
छात्त्र छात्त्र, i. e. छत्त्र + अ,<BR> I. m. A pupil, Pañc. 34, 25.<BR> II. n. A kind of honey, Suśr. 1, 185, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्रता
छात्त्रता छात्त्र + ता, f. Apprenticeship. ˚तां व्रज्, To become a pupil, Pañc. 33, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादन|छादनं|छादनः
छादन छादन, i. e. छद् + अन. n.<BR> 1. Covering, raiment, MBh. 1, 3685. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b " target="_blank">Page0316-b + 43</a>]<BR> 2. A means of concealing, Bhartṛ. 2, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक छाद्मिक, i. e. छद्मन् + इक, adj. Fraudulent, Man. 4, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दस|छांदस|छान्दसः
छान्दस छान्दस, i. e. छन्दस् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Referring, or referable, to the Vedas (vedic), Hariv. 12284.<BR> 2. Conversant with the Vedas, Kathās. 18, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोग्य|छान्दोग्यं
छान्दोग्य छान्दोग्य i. e. छन्दोग + य, n. The name of a Brāhmaṇa and Upaniṣad, belonging to the vedic literature, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाय|छायः
छाय छाय,<BR> I. m. Shadowing, MBh. 12, 10374.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. Shade, Rām. 2, 45, 23; Man. 4, 51.<BR> 2. Reflected image, Man. 5, 133.<BR> 3. Reflected light, splendour, Megh. 36.<BR> 4. Colour, Vikr. d. 146.<BR> 5. When latter part of a comp. subst. noun, it becomes very often neuter, e. g. Ragh. 12, 50; Man. 3, 274 (प्राक्छाये [i. e. प्राञ्च्-] कुञ्जरस्य, When the shadow of an elephant falls to the east).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. σκιά.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकच्छाय
एक- + छाय एक- + छाय, adj. quite dark, MBh. 4, 1878.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छाय|विच्छायं|विच्छायः|विछाय
वि- + छाय वि- + छाय,<BR> I. adj. shadowless.<BR> II. n. the shadow of a flock of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षच्छाय|वृक्षच्छायं
वृक्ष- + छाय वृक्ष- + छाय,<BR> I. f. या, the shadow of a single tree.<BR> II. n. the shade of many trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायावन्त्|छायावत्
छायावन्त् छाया + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Shadowy, Rām. 2, 94, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालिक्य
छालिक्य छालिक्य, i. e. छलिक + य, n. A kind of song, Hariv. 8449.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् छिद्, ii. 7, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To cut, Man. 4, 69.<BR> 2. To lop off, Man. 9, 276.<BR> 3. To wound, Man. 3, 33.<BR> 4. To break, Man. 9, 276.<BR> 5. To interrupt, Hariv. 16258.<BR> 6. To destroy, Rām. 3, 70, 20.<BR> 7. To remove, MBh. 1, 6890. With ऋणम्, To discharge, Rājat. 6, 16.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. दुश्छिन्न, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Cut out, or extracted wrongly. MBh. 12,5307 (a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0317-a " target="_blank">Page0317-a + 42</a>] thorn).<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-च्छेद्य, adj. Not to be cut down, MBh. 1, 93.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10. छेदय,<BR> 1. To lop off, MBh. 7, 5954.<BR> 2. To order to be lopped off, Man. 8, 283.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, अवच्छिन्न, Confined, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 13; अन्-अवच्छिन्न, adj. Unbounded, Bhartṛ. 2, 1.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To cut off, MBh. 7, 1166.<BR> 2. To separate, Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 45.<BR> 3. To resolve, Bhāg. P. 1, 19, 7. अ-व्यवच्छिन्न, adj. Uninterrupted, Hariv. 3580.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To pull off, MBh. 12, 9377.<BR> 2. To cut, MBh. 1, 5936.<BR> 3. To break, Bhāg. P. 3, 21, 18.<BR> 4. To remove, MBh. 3, 11710.<BR> 5. To tear away, Pañc. 222, 4.<BR> 6. To rob, MBh. 4, 2147.<BR> 7. To draw, Daśak. 117, 4.<BR> 8. To disregard, Rām. 2, 24, 33.<BR> --With अवा अव-आ, To deliver, Vikr. d. 15.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, To snatch away, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 24.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To snatch away, Rām. 6, 8, 17.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To root out, MBh. 7, 139; to exterminate, MBh. 1, 6811.<BR> 2. To cut off, Mālat. 151, 6.<BR> 3. To stop, MBh. 1, 4891.<BR> 4. pass. To be deficient, Man. 3, 101.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. दुरुच्छेद्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Difficult to be exterminated, Prab. 93, 12. सुखोच्छेद्य, i. e. सुख-, adj. To be exterminated easily, Pañc. iii. d. 25.<BR> --Caus. or i. 10, To exterminate, Pañc. 55, 12.<BR> --With व्युद् वि-उद्, pass., with the terminations of the Par. (i. e. i. 4),<BR> 1. To become extinct, MBh. 12, 3923.<BR> 2. To cease, MBh. 1, 6188. अ-व्युच्छिन्न, adj. Uninterrupted, Vikr. d. 110.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To exterminate, Pañc. iii. d. 57.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To cut [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0317-b " target="_blank">Page0317-b + 42</a>] off, MBh. 3, 2593.<BR> 2. To wound, Rām. 3, 32, 26.<BR> 3. To limit, Ragh. 6, 77.<BR> 4. To weigh duly, Pañc. 161, 24.<BR> 5. To be assured, Ragh. 15, 51. परिच्छिन्न, Limited, small, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 1. अ-परिच्छेद्य, adj. Boundless, Ragh. 10, 29.<BR> --With विपरि वि-परि, To destroy completely, MBh. 5, 4513.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To cut, Rām. 2, 87, 9 Gorr.<BR> 2. To cut to pieces, Hariv. 13580.<BR> 3. To withdraw, MBh. 12, 9770.<BR> --Caus. To order to be lopped off, MBh. 12, 686.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To cut to pieces, Hariv. 13613.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To retort by cutting to pieces, MBh. 7, 4848.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To tear asunder, Hariv. 8530.<BR> 2. To interrupt, Bhartṛ. 1, 95; Daśak. in Chr. 179, 16 (अ-विच्छिन्न-पातम्, Without rising again).<BR> 3. To separate, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 20.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To cut, MBh. 1, 2242.<BR> 2. To cut to pieces, MBh. 5, 2909.<BR> 3. To cut off, MBh. 7, 7918.<BR> 4. To pierce, MBh. 4, 2004.<BR> 4. To destroy, to remove, Bhag. 4, 11.<BR> 5. To decide (a question), Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 52.<BR> --Cf. σκίδνημι, κίδναμαι, σκοῖδος, κοῖδος, σκινδάλαμος, σκεδάννυμι (for σκειδανϳυμι), σχίζω, σχίδη, σχίνδαλμος, σχέδη, etc.; Lat. scindo, caedo (Causal); Goth. skaidan; A.S. sceádan; O.H.G. sceit, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
ऽछिद् -छिद्, latter part of comp. adj.<BR> 1. Cutting, piercing, e. g. MBh. 7, 4656; Rām. 5, 37, 10.<BR> 2. Destroying, MBh. 5, 1809.<BR> 3. Removing, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्छिद्
दुश्चिद् दुश्चिद्, i. e. दुस्-, difficult to be destroyed, Kām. Nītis. 14, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर छिद् + उर, adj., f. रा, What may be torn easily, Ragh. 16, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र्
† छिद्र् छिद्र्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To perforate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र छिद् + र,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Perforated, Rām. 1, 73, 20.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A gap, Man. 8, 239.<BR> 2. A defect, Pañc. 40, 12.<BR> 3. An opening, Suśr. 1, 54, 16; an entry, Bhāg. P. 5, 6, 4.<BR> 4. A weak point, Pañc. i. d. 366; a vulnerable part, Man. 7, 105.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छिद्र|अच्छिद्रं|अछिद्र
अ-च्छिद्र अ-च्छिद्र,<BR> I. n. uninterruptedness, Rām. 4, 43, 25.<BR> II. adj. 1. unhurt, Rām. 6, 23, 16. 2. uninterrupted, Rām. 1, 40, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छिद्र
निश्छिद्र निश्छिद्र, i. e. निस्-, adj. without holes, and without weak points, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रता
छिद्रता छिद्र + ता, f. The quality of giving space, MBh. 12, 9137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रदातृत्व
छिद्रदातृत्व छिद्र-दातृ + त्व, n. The quality of giving space, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रात्मन्
छिद्रात्मन् छिद्रात्मन्, i. e. छिद्र-आत्मन्, m. One who shows his weak points, MBh. 12, 11345.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रिन्
छिद्रिन् छिद्रिन्, i. e. छिद्र + इन्, adj. Hollow, Suśr. 1, 304, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुच्छुन्दर|छुच्छुन्दरः|छुछुंदर|छुछुन्दर|छुछुंदरः
छुच्छुन्दर छुच्छुन्दर, and ˚रि रि, m. The musk rat, Suśr. 2, 279, 4; Man. 12, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुट्
† छुट् छुट्, i. 6 and 10, Par. To cut, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड्
† छुड् छुड्, i. 6, Par. To cover, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप्
† छुप् छुप्, or चुप् चुप्, i. 6, Par. To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुर्
छुर् छुर् (a form of क्षुर्), To cut.<BR> --Caus. छोरय and छुरय, To inlay with, Kathās. 24, 1.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, Caus. To scratch, Kathās. 17, 33.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b " target="_blank">Page0318-b + 41</a>] To inlay with, Kumāras. 1, 56.<BR> 2. To paint, Vikr. d. 136.<BR> 3. To cover, Caurap. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरिका
छुरिका छुरिका (a form of क्षुरिका), f. A knife, Kathās. 12, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छूरिका
छूरिका छूरिका, f. The nostril, Man. 8, 325.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृद्
छृद् छृद्, ii. 7, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. † To shine.<BR> 2. To vomit.<BR> 3. † To play.<BR> छृद्, or छृत् छृत्, or छृप् छृप्, i. 1 and 10, † To kindle.<BR> --Caus. To vomit, MBh. 5, 3493 (3492).<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, Caus. To vomit, Suśr. 1, 276, 14.<BR> --Cf. σκόρδον and σκόροδον, perhaps also σκορδινέομαι and σκορδύλος, κορδύλος, etc.; Goth. spai-skuldrs; Lat. screare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृप्
† छृप् छृप्, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तृ
छेत्तृ छेत्तृ, i. e. छिद् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A wood-cutter, Hit. i. d. 52.<BR> 2. One who removes, Hit. i. d. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद छेद, i. e. छिद् + अ,<BR> I. adj. One who cuts away, Man. 9, 44.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A slice, a piece, Ragh. 12, 100; Megh. 11.<BR> 2. Cutting, Pañc. 108, 11.<BR> 3. Cutting off, Man. 8, 368.<BR> 4. Destruction, MBh. 13, 1637.<BR> 5. Dissipation, Śāk. d. 38.<BR> 6. Ceasing, Vikr. d. 76.<BR> 7. Want, Śāk. 91, 12.<BR> 8. Limit, Yājñ. 1, 319.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिच्छेद|भक्तिच्छेदः
भक्ति- + छेद भक्ति- + छेद, m. certain streaks on the forehead, nose, cheeks, breast, and arms, which denote a follower of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्छेद
स- + छेद स- + छेद, adj. interrupted, Lass. 21, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुच्छेद|स्थाणुच्छेदः|स्थाणुछेद
स्थाणु- + छेद स्थाणु- + छेद, m. one who cuts away the trunks of trees, Man. 9, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदन|छेदनं
छेदन छेदन, i. e. छिद् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cutting, destroying, MBh. 1, 1498.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Cutting, Man. 12, 75.<BR> 2. Lopping off, Man. 8, 280.<BR> 3. Removing, MBh. 3, 12700.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदिन्
छेदिन् छेदिन्, i. e. छिद् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. One who splits, Man. 4, 71.<BR> 2. Removing, Śāk. 35, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छो
छो छो, i. 4, छ्य, Par. To cut.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, Caus. To scarify, प्रच्छित, Suśr. 2, 247, 19; cf. 1, 33, 18 (प्र-च्छयित्वा, sic!)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ्यु
† छ्यु छ्यु, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ऽज -ज (vb. जन्), latter part of comp. words, m., f. जा, and n.<BR> 1. Born, son, daughter, e. g. गूढ- (vb. गुह्), Born secretly. m. A son of concealed birth, Yājñ. 2, 129. धृतराष्ट्र-जा, f. A daughter of Dhṛtarāṣṭra, MBh. 14, 2285. आत्मज, i. e. आत्मन्-, A son, Hit. 41, 21. जघन्य-, adj. Youngest, MBh. 1, 804. देह-, m. A son, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 3. पूर्व-, m. pl. Ancestors, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 7.<BR> 2. Produced, Man. 1, 87; Bhāṣāp. 62.<BR> 3. Caused, Nal. 4, 13.<BR> --Cf. also धर्म-,<BR> I. adj. Begotten from a sense of duty, Man. 9, 107.<BR> II. m. Son of Dharma, a name of Arjuna, Bhāg. P. 3, 3, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंस्
† जंस् जंस्, i. 10 (and 1?) Par. To protect, to deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्
1. जक्ष् जक्ष् (i. e. जघस्, vb. घस् reduplicated), ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To eat, Bhāg. P. 4, 17, 23.<BR> 2. To be hungry, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 17.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. जग्ध, Man. 5, 125.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To devour, MBh. 11, 479.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्
2. जक्ष् जक्ष् (i. e. जहस्, vb. हस् reduplicated), ii. 2, Par. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्
जगत् जगत् (i. e. an old ptcple. of the pres. of vb. गम्, ii. 3),<BR> I. adj. Moveable, MBh. 12, 12465.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Race [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b " target="_blank">Page0319-b + 42</a>] of men, Man. 7, 22.<BR> 2. The world, Man. 1, 52; dual, जगती, Heaven and earth, Kir. 5, 20.<BR> III. f. ती,<BR> 1. The earth, Man. 1, 100.<BR> 2. The world, Rām. 2, 69, 11.<BR> 3. The name of a metre, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 45.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगत्
अ-जगत् अ-जगत्, adj. immoveable, MBh. 12, 12465.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजगत्
त्रि-जगत् त्रि-जगत्, n. the three worlds, heaven, earth, and the lower regions, Lass. 5, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदायु|जगदायुः
जगदायु जगदायु, and जगदायुस् जगदायुस्, i. e. जगत्-, m. Containing the life of the world, MBh. 3, 11193; 12, 13569.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्मय
जगन्मय जगन्मय, i. e. जगत् + मय, adj. Containing the universe, Hariv. 3762.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगल|जगलः
जगल जगल, probably a reduplicated form of 2. गॄ, + अ, m. An intoxicating beverage, Suśr. 1, 189, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्धि|जग्धिः
जग्धि जग्धि, i. e. जक्ष् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Eating, Man. 5, 31.<BR> 2. Food, Man. 3, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि जग्मि, i. e. reduplicated गम्, + इ, adj. Hastening, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन|जघनं
जघन जघन, i. e. reduplicated हन् + अ, n. and m.<BR> 1. The pudenda, Hariv. 8625.<BR> 2. The buttocks, Rām. 5, 18, 11.<BR> 3. The rear-guard of an army, MBh. 3, 16284.<BR> --Cf. κοχώνη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनिन्
जघनिन् जघनिन्, i. e. जघन + इन्, adj., f. नी, Having large buttocks, Hariv. 9547.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्य|जघन्यः
जघन्य जघन्य, i. e. जघन + य, adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Last, MBh. 3, 1366.<BR> 2. Late, MBh. 12, 4794.<BR> 3. Shortest, Suśr. 1, 125, 5.<BR> 4. Indifferent, Suśr. 1, 95, 14.<BR> 5. Lowest, Man. 8, 270; Pañc. iii. d. 218.<BR> 6. Comparat. जघन्यतर, Lower, MBh. 14, 1137.<BR> 7. ˚यम्, adv. At last, MBh. 3, 905.<BR> 8. loc. ये, adverbially, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a " target="_blank">Page0320-a + 39</a>] At last, MBh. 3, 1303; Behind, Hariv. 3087.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्यतस्
जघन्यतस् जघन्य + तस्, adv. At last, Rām. 5, 40, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्क्ष्
† जङ्क्ष् जङ्क्ष्, v. r. of क्षञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गम|जंगम|जङ्गमः
जङ्गम जङ्गम् + अ (frequentat. of गम्), adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Moveable, Man. 1, 41; patrolling, Man. 9, 266.<BR> 2. Living, MBh. 1, 5019.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गमत्व
जङ्गमत्व जङ्गम + त्व, n. Mobility, MBh. 14, 654.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गल|जंगल|जङ्गलं|जङ्गलः
जङ्गल जङ्गल् + अ (frequentat. of गल्? cf. ग्लै), adj. Dry, desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घा|जंघा
जङ्घा जङ्घा, i. e. reduplicated हन् + अ, fem. The leg, Suśr. 1, 348, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालजङ्घ
ताल- + जङ्घ ताल- + जङ्घ, 1. adj. long-legged, Rām. 5, 12, 35.<BR> 2. m. The name of a people, Rām. 1, 70, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजङ्घ|सुजंघ
सु- + जङ्घ सु- + जङ्घ, adj., f. घा, having a beautiful leg, Śrut. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाल|जंघाल|जङ्घालः
जङ्घाल जङ्घा + ल, m. A rapid walker, Suśr. 1, 200, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्
† जज् जज्, i. 1, Par. To fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्ज्|जंज्
जञ्ज् जञ्ज्, i. 1, Par. To fight(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट्
† जट् जट्, i. 1, Par. To be entangled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट
जट जट,<BR> I. m. = f. (see<BR> II.), Hariv. 9551.<BR> II. f. टा,<BR> 1. The hair matted, as worn by the god Śiva and by ascetics; the long hair occasionally clotted together and brought over the head, so as to project like a horn from the forehead, or allowed to fall carelessly over the back and shoulders, Man. 6, 6.<BR> 2. A braid, MBh. 3, 16137.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजट|त्रिजटः
त्रि-जट त्रि-जट,<BR> I. adj. wearing three braids, MBh. 3, 16137.<BR> II. m. 1. a name of Śiva, 12, 10357. 2. a proper name, Rām. 2, 32, 28.<BR> III. f. टा, a proper name, Rām. 3, 41, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाजट
शिखा- + जट शिखा- + जट, adj. one who wears a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b " target="_blank">Page0320-b + 42</a>] lock of hair in a knot on the top of the head, Man. 2, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाजिनिन्
जटाजिनिन् जटाजिनिन्, i. e. जटा-अजिन + इन्, adj. Wearing matted hair and the hide of an antelope, MBh. 1, 4917.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायु|जटायुः
जटायु जटायु and जटायुस् जटायुस्, m. A fabulous vulture, Rām. 1, 1, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाल|जटालः
जटाल जटा + ल, and जटालक जटाल + क, adj., f. ला, इका, Wearing matted hair, Hariv. 10594; Mārk. P. 8, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिन्
जटिन् जटिन्, i. e. जटा + इन्, adj. Wearing matted hair, Man. 11, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिल|जटिलः
जटिल जटिल, i. e. जटा + इल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Having matted or entangled hair, Man. 2, 219; MBh. 3, 16257.<BR> 2. Entangled, Bhāg. P. 3, 33, 14.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. A proper name, MBh. 1, 7265.<BR> 2. The name of several plants, e. g. Suśr. 1, 71, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलीभाव|जटिलीभावः
जटिलीभाव जटिलीभाव, i. e. जटिल-भू + अ, m. Clotting, Suśr. 1, 272, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठर|जठरं|जठरः
जठर जठर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Hard, Śāntiś. 4, 13.<BR> 2. Old, Śiś. 4, 29(?).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The belly, Pañc. i. d. 27.<BR> 2. The womb, Bhāg. P. 3, 33, 4.<BR> 3. The interior, Rām. 3, 41, 26.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. venter; γαστήρ; Goth. qvithra and in-kiltho.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जड|जडं|जडः
जड जड (probably for original जल, to which the Grammar. give the same signification; Lat. gĕlu gelidus; Goth. kald; A.S. ceald; cf. जत), adj.<BR> 1. Cold, Pañc. i. d. 353.<BR> 2. Rigid, immoveable, Rām. 6, 6, 1.<BR> 3. Material, irrational, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 22.<BR> 4. Dimmed, Śāk. d. 81.<BR> 5. Unfeeling, apathetic, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 10.<BR> 6. Stupid, Bhāg. P. 5, 9, 8.<BR> 7. Dumb, Man. 2, 110.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजड
अ-जड अ-जड, m. not an idiot, Man. 8, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडता
जडता जड + ता, f.<BR> 1. Apathy, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a " target="_blank">Page0321-a + 44</a>] Sāh. D. 175.<BR> 2. Stupidity, Mārk. P. 10, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडत्व|जडत्वं
जडत्व जड + त्व, n. Stupidity, Rājat. 6, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडिमन्
जडिमन् जडिमन्, i. e. जड + इमन्, m. Stupidity, Rājat. 4, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतु|जतुः
जतु जतु, m. Lac, the red animal dye, MBh. 1, 5725.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाजतु
शिला- + जतु शिला- + जतु, n. 1. bitumen. 2. red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्रु
जत्रु जत्रु, m. and n. The collarbone, MBh. 3, 713.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्
जन् जन्, ii. 3, Par.; i. 4, जाय, Ātm. (ved. also i. 1, Par.),<BR> I. Transitive,<BR> 1. To bring forth, MBh. 1, 2770.<BR> 2. To produce, Bhāg. 5, 7, 12.<BR> II. Intransitive, i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 12, 7751).<BR> 1. To be born, Man. 3, 39.<BR> 2. To be produced, Man. 3, 76.<BR> 3. To be caused, MBh. 3, 16748.<BR> 4. To grow, Man. 9, 38.<BR> 5. To be born again (by transmigration of the soul), Hit. Pr. 13.<BR> 6. To fall to one's share, Pañc. ii. d. 3.<BR> 7. To become, MBh. 3, 4083.<BR> 8. To be, Śrut. 19. 25.<BR> 9. To take place, Lass. 11, 5.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. act. जज्ञिवंस् and जातवन्त्, Born, Bhāg. P. 4, 23, 2; Chr. 24, 40; of the pass. जात,<BR> 1. Born, Rām. 1, 1, 26.<BR> 2. Old, MBh. 8, 3389.<BR> 3. Grown, Man. 9, 40.<BR> 4. Sprung up, Rām. 1, 9, 27.<BR> 5. Happened, Hit. 9, 7.<BR> 6. Become, Śāk. d. 60.<BR> 7. As former part of a comp. adj. very often, Having, e. g. जात-दन्त, adj. Having teeth, Man. 5, 70. The same signification it has also sometimes as latter part, e. g. दन्त-जात, adj. Having teeth, Man. 5, 58.<BR> 8. m. A son, Pañc. i. d. 32.<BR> 9. n.<BR> a. Class, MBh. 15, 215;<BR> b. Kind, MBh. 13, 7241;<BR> c. A multitude of objects of the same genus, MBh. 4, 143; 12, 1500.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. जनय (also Ātm., MBh. 1, 3104; Hit. i. d. 133),<BR> 1. To beget, Man. 3, 17.<BR> 2. To bring forth, Man. 9, 172.<BR> 3. To produce, Man. 12, 119.<BR> 4. To cause, Pañc. v. d. 47.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिजात, Superior by birth (to the parents), Pañc. i. d. 442.<BR> --With अधि अधि, To be born, Ragh. 18, 23.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To be born afterwards, Man. 9, 134.<BR> 2. To be born similar to (with the acc.), Ragh. 6, 78. अनुजात,<BR> 1. Similar by birth (to his parents), Pañc. i. d. 442.<BR> 2. After teething(?) Man. 5, 53.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To be born similar to (with the acc.), Rām. 2, 35, 26.<BR> --With अप अप, अप-जात, Inferior (to his parents), Pañc. i. d. 442.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To be born (predestinated) to, Bhag. 16, 3; with महीम्, To be born to rule the earth, MBh. 5, 4342.<BR> 2. To be born, Man. 2, 147.<BR> 3. To be produced, Bhag. 2, 62.<BR> 4. To be born again (by transmigration of the soul), Bhag. 6, 41.<BR> 5. To spring up again, MBh. 1, 3514.<BR> 6. To become, Rām. 4, 44, 77. अभि-जात,<BR> 1. Inherited, MBh. 5, 1357.<BR> 2. Of noble family, Rām. 5, 11, 21.<BR> 3. Well-bred, Bhartṛ. 2, 48.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To spring up, Rām. 1, 39, 24.<BR> --With अव अव, Caus. To bring forth, Hit. Pr. n. d. 12, 13.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To be born again, Man. 2, 249.<BR> 2. To be produced, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 17. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-a " target="_blank">Page0322-a + 43</a>]<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To be added, MBh. 4, 1608.<BR> 2. To be born, Man. 1, 45.<BR> 3. To spring up, Man. 12, 73.<BR> 4. To appear, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 15.<BR> 5. To be born again, Bhag. 14, 2.<BR> 6. To be, Hit. i. d. 115. उपजात, as former part of comp. adj., Having, Hit. 42, 6.<BR> --Caus. To cause, Prab. 29, 15.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप,<BR> 1. To spring up, Rām. 2, 75, 41.<BR> 2. To be born again, MBh. 13, 6722; cf. अभिनिवेश.<BR> --Caus. To produce, Ṛt. 2, 28.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To bring forth, Chr. 50, 14.<BR> 2. To be born, Man. 10, 9.<BR> 3. To be produced, Hit. i. d. 24.<BR> 4. To be born again, MBh. 13, 5509.<BR> 5. To propagate, Man. 10, 64. प्रजाता, f. A woman who has borne a child, MBh. 1, 3046.<BR> --With अपप्र अप-प्र, To abort, Suśr. 2, 398, 21. अपप्रजाता, f. A woman who has miscarried, Suśr. 2, 398, 21.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To spring up, Pañc. i. d. 69.<BR> 2. To appear, Rām. 6, 90, 32.<BR> 3. To exist, Pañc. i. d. 452.<BR> 4. To be born again, MBh. 13, 5459.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To spring up anew, MBh. 6, 2651.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To bring forth, Rām. 1, 70, 35.<BR> 2. To be born, Rām. 1, 16, 20.<BR> 3. To spring up, Rām. 1, 68, 8.<BR> 4. To be changed to, to become, MBh. 5, 7368. विजात, Base born, of mixed origin (rather जात with वि); f. ता, The mother of children, a matron.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To bring forth, Rām. 3, 20, 27.<BR> 2. To be born, Rām. 1, 70, 27.<BR> 3. To grow, Nal. 24, 52.<BR> 4. To be produced, MBh. 3, 17684.<BR> 5. To rise, Man. 8, 172.<BR> 6. To happen, Rājat. 5, 180.<BR> 7. To become, Pañc. 32, 9.<BR> 8. To pass, Pañc. 242, 14. संजात, as former part of comp. adj. often, Having, Kathās. 4, 26.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To beget, MBh. 1, 3135.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b " target="_blank">Page0322-b + 45</a>] bring forth, Rām. 3, 20, 13.<BR> 3. To build, MBh. 1, 4995.<BR> 4. To produce, Pañc. 188, 10.<BR> 5. To cause, Rām. 2, 95, 5.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To be produced, Hariv. 13778.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्, To be produced, Rām. 2, 22, 7.<BR> --Cf. γίγνομαι, γένεσις, γονή, γνήσιος, τηλύ-γετος, νη-γάτεος, νεο-γνός, γυνή, etc.; Lat. gigno, genus, germen (cf. जन्मन्); Goth. keinan, us-kijan, niu-klahs, kuni, qvino; A.S. cyn; O.H.G. kind; A.S. cild; see जनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अ-जात अ-जात, see separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजात
एक- + जात एक- + जात, adj. 1. having the same father, Man. 9, 148. 2. having the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-b " target="_blank">Page0321-b + 42</a>] same parents, Man. 9, 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलजात
कुल- + जात कुल- + जात, adj. descending from a noble family, Rām. 1, 71, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरजात
चिर- + जात चिर- + जात, adj. old, MBh. 3, 13334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जात|दुर्जातं|दुर्ज्जात
दुस्- + जात दुस्- + जात, 1. miserable, MBh. 12, 8120. 2. wicked, Rājat. 1, 356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाजात|यथाजातः
यथा- + जात यथा- + जात, adj. foolish, a fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजात
सु- + जात सु- + जात, adj. of high birth, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य जन्य, see separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन जन्-अ, m.<BR> 1. Creature, MBh. 3, 1204.<BR> 2. Man collectively, men, Rām. 1, 6, 7; Man. 4, 108; with आयुधीय, Armed men, 7, 222; crowd, Rām. 6, 101, 33.<BR> 3. Man individually, a person, Draup. 3, 5; Man. 11, 241.<BR> 4. This person, Nal. 10, 10.<BR> 5. With the msc. of the pronoun इदम्,<BR> I. Śāk. 85, 16.<BR> 6. The name of a division of the world, the residence of deified mortals, Bhāg. P. 3, 11, 31.<BR> 7. It is often used as latter part of comp. words, especially in signification<BR> 2 and<BR> 3; e. g. प्रेष्य-, m. The whole set of menial servants, Man. 7, 125; शिशु-, m. sing. pl. Children, Pañc. 95, 17; दास-, m. A slave, Vikr. d. 54.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अ- + जन अ- + जन, adj. deserted, Rām. 2, 92, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरजन
अन्तःपुर- + जन अन्तःपुर- + जन, i. e. अन्तर्-पुर-, m. the women of a gyneceum, Rām. 1, 10, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्जन|असज्जनः
अ-सज्जन अ-सज्जन, i. e. -सन्त्-जन, m. a wicked person, Rām. 2, 39, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलजन|कुलजनः
कुल- + जन कुल- + जन, m. a person of a noble family, Mṛcch. 120, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुजन|गुरुजनः
गुरु- + जन गुरु- + जन, m. a venerable person, as one's parents or spiritual teacher, Bhartṛ. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामबालजन
ग्राम-बाल- + जन ग्राम-बाल- + जन, m. young peasants, Lass. 11, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलाजन|चपलाजनः
चपला- + जन चपला- + जन, m. an unsteady woman, and the goddess of fortune, Śiś. 9, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्जन|तिर्यग्जनः
तिर्यग्जन तिर्यग्जन, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-, m. an animal, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासजन|दासजनः
दास- + जन दास- + जन, m. the household servants, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जन|दुर्जनः
दुस्- + जन दुस्- + जन, m. a mischief-making person, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a " target="_blank">Page0323-a + 45</a>] Man. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजन|पंचजन|पञ्चजनः
पञ्चजन पञ्चजन, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. m. 1. the five higher classes of beings (gods, men, Gandharvas with the Apsaras, serpents, and manes). 2. mankind. 3. the name of a demon, and of others.<BR> II. f. नी, a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजन|पुण्यजनः
पुण्य- + जन पुण्य- + जन, m. pl. a kind of good demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्जन|पृथग्जनः
पृथग्जन पृथग्जन, i. e. पृथक्-, m. 1. low people, Man. 7, 137. 2. an ignorant man. 3. a sinner, a wicked man. 4. pl. children of one father by different mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजन|पौरजनः
पौर- + जन पौर- + जन, m. a citizen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजन|महाजनः
महा- + जन महा- + जन, m. 1. a preeminent man, a virtuous man. 2. a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
वि- + जन वि- + जन, adj. lonely, private; loc. ˚ने, privately, Pañc. 58, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजन
विश्व- + जन विश्व- + जन, m. all men, mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजन|सुजनः
सु- + जन सु- + जन, m. 1. a virtuous man. 2. a benevolent one. 3. the charioteer of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजन|स्वजनः
स्व- + जन स्व- + जन, m. 1. a kinsman. 2. family, Bhartṛ. 2, 19; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक जन् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Causing, MBh. 4, 1456.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A father, Pañc. v. d. 19.<BR> 2. A producer, Bhāṣāp. 44.<BR> 3. A proper name, Rām. 1, 1, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. kuning; A.S. cyning, king; ϝάναξ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाजनक|यमुनाजनकः
यमुना- + जनक यमुना- + जनक, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकता
जनकता जनक + ता, f.<BR> 1. Causing, Sāh. D. 2, 5.<BR> 2. Paternity, Kathās. 17, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनता
जनता जन + ता, f.<BR> 1. Mankind, Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 8.<BR> 2. Household servants, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 24.<BR> 3. Subjects, Kathās. 18, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनता
सु- + जनता सु- + जनता, f. 1. goodness. 2. benevolence.<BR> 3. a number of respectable persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन जन् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Bringing forth, Man. 9, 81.<BR> 2. Causing, MBh. 1, 1183.<BR> II. f. नी, A mother, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 20.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Child-birth, Man. 5, 61.<BR> 2. Producing, production, Rām. 1, 23, 17.<BR> 3. Existence, Śāk. d. 99.<BR> --Comp.<BR> see कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजननी
स्त्री-जननी स्त्री-जननी, a woman who brings forth only daughters, Man. 9, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ जनयितृ, i. e. जन्, Caus., + तृ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A progenitor, Rām. 2, 111, 11.<BR> 2. A father, Man. 9, 142.<BR> II. f. त्री, A mother, Rājat. 3, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयिष्णु|जनयिष्णुः
जनयिष्णु जनयिष्णु, i. e. जन्, Caus., + इष्णु, m. A progenitor, MBh. 9, 2222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्
जनस् जन् + अस्, n. indecl. One of the seven worlds beyond the महर्-लोक, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनि|जनिः
जनि जन् + इ, f.<BR> 1. A woman, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1.<BR> 2. Birth-place, Hariv. 11979.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितृ
जनितृ जनितृ, i. e. जन् + तृ,<BR> I. m. A father, Pañc. i. d. 9.<BR> II. f. त्री, A mother, MBh. 3, 10498.<BR> --Cf. Lat. genitor, genitrix; γενετήρ, γενέτωρ, γενέτειρα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्र|जनित्रं
जनित्र जनित्र, i. e. जनितृ + अ, n. Birth-place, MBh. 5, 2580.<BR> --Cf. γενέθλη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिष्य
जनिष्य जनिष्य (mutilated जनिष्यन्त्, ptcple. of the fut. Par.), adj. Future, Rām. 3, 66, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः|जन्तुः
जन्तु जन् + तु, m.<BR> 1. A creature, Man. 3, 77.<BR> 2. A man, Man. 4, 240.<BR> 3. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 22, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटीजन्तु
कर्कटी- + जन्तु कर्कटी- + जन्तु, m. the offspring of a crab, Cāṇ. 56 in Berl. Monatsb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्तु|जलजंतु|जलजन्तुः
जल- + जन्तु जल- + जन्तु, m. an aquatic animal, Hit. i. d. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुमन्त्|जन्तुमत्
जन्तुमन्त् जन्तु + मन्त्, adj. Full of reptiles, Mārk. P. 32, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन् जन् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. Birth, Man. 1, 42.<BR> 2. Production, Rām. 3, 20, 31.<BR> 3. Sowing, planting, Kumāras. 5, 60.<BR> 4. Appearance, Yājñ. 3, 23.<BR> 5. Existence, Man. 5, 38.<BR> 6. A father, Śāk. d. 177.<BR> 7. Creature, Chr. 289, 7 = Rigv. i. 50, 7.<BR> 8. Manner, Chr. 293, 5 = Rigv. i. 87, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. germen; O.H.G. chîmo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजन्मन्
अग्र- + जन्मन् अग्र- + जन्मन्, m. a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 2, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजन्मन्
अन्त्य- + जन्मन् अन्त्य- + जन्मन्, adj. of the lowest tribe, Man. 10, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजजन्मन्
अम्भोज- + जन्मन् अम्भोज- + जन्मन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a " target="_blank">Page0324-a + 43</a>] m. a name of Brahman, Lass. 66, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजन्मन्
आत्मजन्मन् आत्मजन्मन्, i. e. आत्मन्-,<BR> I. n. the birth of a son, Kumāras. 6, 28.<BR> II. m. a son, Ragh. 1, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरु|ऊरुः
ऊरु ऊरु, m. = और्व, Mālav. 71, d. 92. See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भजन्मन्|कुंभजन्मन्
कुम्भ- + जन्मन् कुम्भ- + जन्मन्, m. a name of Agastya, Ragh. 12, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तजन्मन्
चित्त- + जन्मन् चित्त- + जन्मन्, m. the god of love, Daśak. 106, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजन्मन्
द्वि- + जन्मन् द्वि- + जन्मन्, m. a man of either of the three first classes, especially a Brāhmaṇa (cf. द्विज), Man. 2, 26; Rājat. 4, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मन्
पुनर्- + जन्मन् पुनर्- + जन्मन्, n. Palingenesia (by transmigration of the soul), Bhag. 8, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वजन्मन्
पूर्व- + जन्मन् पूर्व- + जन्मन्,<BR> I. n. a former existence.<BR> II. m. an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मजन्मन्
ब्रह्मजन्मन् ब्रह्मजन्मन्, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, n. 1. second or spiritual birth, Man. 2, 146. 2. investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
वि- + जन्मन् वि- + जन्मन्,<BR> I. adj. born by a paramour (ŚKD.).<BR> II. m. the son of an outcaste Vaiśya, Man. 10, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरजन्मन्
शर- + जन्मन् शर- + जन्मन्, m. Kārtikeya, the god of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पजन्मन्|सङ्कल्पजन्मन्
संकल्प- + जन्मन् संकल्प- + जन्मन्, m. Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजन्मन्
सरोजन्मन् सरोज्˚, i. e. सरस्-, n. a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तर|जन्मांतर|जन्मान्तरं
जन्मान्तर जन्मान्तर, i. e. जन्मन्-अन्तर, n.<BR> 1. A preceding existence, MBh. 3, 2564.<BR> 2. A future existence, Pañc. ii. d. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तरीय|जन्मांतरीय
जन्मान्तरीय जन्मान्तरीय, i. e. जन्मान्तर + ईय, adj. Performed in a preceding existence, Rājat. 6, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन् जन्मिन्, i. e. जन्मन् + इन्, m. A creature, Pañc. i. d. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य जन्य,<BR> A. ptcple. of the fut. pass. of जन्,<BR> 1. To be born, Bhāṣāp. 44.<BR> 2. Produced, Bhāṣāp. 110.<BR> 3. n. The body, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 31.<BR> B. i. e. जन + य,<BR> I. m. The friend of a bridegroom, MBh. 1, 7203.<BR> II. f. या, A bridesmaid, Ragh. 6, 30.<BR> III. n. War, combat, MBh. 5, 3195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्
जप् जप् (a form of जल्प्), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., MBh. 13, 750).<BR> 1. To speak low, to murmur (prayers), Man. 2, 78.<BR> 2. To pray to in a low voice, MBh. 13, 750. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b " target="_blank">Page0324-b + 37</a>]<BR> 3. To invoke murmuring, Bhāg. P. 4, 7, 29.<BR> --Ptcple. of the future pass. जप्य and जाप्य, n. A low prayer, Man. 2, 87; Bhāg. P. 8, 3, 1.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To pray low afterwards, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 29.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To charm, Rām. 2, 25, 36.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To whisper to, Rām. 1, 9, 38.<BR> 2. To bring over to one's party, Man. 7, 197.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To recite in a low tone, MBh. 3, 13432.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To report, MBh. 4, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप जप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Muttering prayers, Man. 3, 74.<BR> 2. A prayer, Rām. 1, 25, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपन|जपनं
जपन जप् + अन, n. Muttering prayers, MBh. 12, 7157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपा
जपा जपा, f. The China rose, Kir. 5, 8; Śiś. 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपिन्
जपिन् जप् + इन्, adj. Muttering prayers, Yājñ. 3, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जबा
जबा जबा, Megh. 37 = जवा, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ् जभ्, and जम्भ् जम्भ्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To gape, to yawn.<BR> 2. To destroy, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 26.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, जम्भय, Par. To destroy; cf. यभ्.<BR> --Cf. A.S. geapan, to gape; and see गभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्
जम् जम्, i. 1, Par. To eat.<BR> --Frequent. To chew, anomal. जाजम्, MBh. 13, 4495.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्नि|जमदग्निः
जमदग्नि जमदग्नि, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, MBh. 1, 2611.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बाल|जंबाल|जंबालः|जम्बालः
जम्बाल जम्बाल, m. Mud, Rājat. 5, 94.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजम्बाल|सजंबाल|सजम्बालः
स- + जम्बाल स- + जम्बाल, adj. Muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बु|जंबु|जम्बुः
जम्बु जम्बु, and जम्बू जम्बू, f.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a " target="_blank">Page0325-a + 42</a>] A fruit tree, the rose apple, Eugenia jambu, MBh. 1, 7587; Pañc. 205, 5.<BR> 2. The name of a division of the world, comprising India (cf. द्वीप), Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 32.<BR> 3. The name of a fabulous river, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजम्बू|भूजंबू
भू-जम्बू भू-जम्बू, f. 1. wheat. 2. the fruit of the Flacourtia sapida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुक|जंबुक|जंबुकः|जम्बुकः
जम्बुक जम्बुक, m. A jackal, Pañc. 35, 2. f. का, A female jackal, Pañc. iv. d. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूल|जंबूल|जम्बूलः
जम्बूल जम्बूल, m. A fragrant plant, Pandanus odoratissimus, Hariv. 5371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ्|जंभ्
जम्भ् जम्भ्, see जभ् and यभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ जम्भ, i. e. जभ् + अ,<BR> I. m., f. भा, and n.<BR> 1. The jaws, the teeth, a tooth (ved.).<BR> 2. Cracking, explaining, MBh. 5, 2474.<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR> --Cf. γαμϕηλαί, γόμϕιος; A.S. geaflas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भक|जंभक|जम्भकः
जम्भक जम्भ् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bruising, Rām. 1, 30, 9.<BR> 2. Cracking, explaining, MBh. 5, 2470.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of certain demons, Rām. 1, 31, 4 Gorr.<BR> 2. The name of a spell, Rām. 1, 31, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भन|जंभनं
जम्भन जम्भ् + अन, adj., f. नी, Bruising, MBh. 6, 807.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय जय, i. e. जि + अ,<BR> I. latter part of comp. adj. Conquering.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Victory, Man. 7, 183.<BR> 2. Conquest, Bhāg. P. 5, 19, 22.<BR> 3. Resigning, resignation, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 5.<BR> 4. A name of the sun, MBh. 3, 154.<BR> 5. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 8, 13, 22.<BR> III. f. या, A name of Durgā, MBh. 4, 194.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अ- + जय अ- + जय, m. defeat, Bhag. 2, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुब्जय
ककुब्जय ककुब्जय, i. e. ककुभ्-, m. the conquest of the world, Rājat. 5, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जय|दुर्जयः|दुर्ज्जय
दुस्- + जय दुस्- + जय,<BR> I. adj., f. या, difficult to be conquered. Rām. 6, 75, 51.<BR> II. m. 1. the name of a race of demons, Śāk. 95, 4. 2. a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b " target="_blank">Page0325-b + 41</a>] proper name, Rām. 3, 29, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्जय
सु-दुस्- + जय सु-दुस्- + जय, adj. very difficult to be overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्कजया
रक्क- + जया रक्क- + जय, f. या, the name of an idol, Rājat. 5, 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन्त|जयंत|जयंतः|जयन्तः
जयन्त जयन्त, i. e. जयन्त्, ptcple. pres. of जि, + अ,<BR> I. m. A proper name, Śāk. d. 161.<BR> II. f. ती.<BR> 1. The name of a river, MBh. 3, 5089.<BR> 2. The name of a country, Rājat. 8, 655.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवन्त्|जयवत्
जयवन्त् जय + वन्त्, adj. Victorious, MBh. 6, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयितृ
जयितृ जयितृ, i. e. जि + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Victorious, MBh. 12, 3753.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन् जयिन्, i. e. जि + इन्, adj. and sbst.<BR> 1. Conquering, a conqueror, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 38.<BR> 2. Victorious, MBh. 9, 1676.<BR> 3. The winning party in a law-suit, Yājñ. 2, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिष्णु
जयिष्णु जयिष्णु i. e. जि + इष्णु, adj. Victorious, MBh. 7, 1480.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ जरठ (vb. जॄ), adj. Old, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण जरण, i. e. जॄ + अन, adj.<BR> 1. Old (ved.).<BR> 2. Digestive, Suśr. 1, 155, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरतिका
जरतिका जरतिका, i. e. जरती (fem. of the ptcple. pres. of जॄ) + क, f. A contemptible old woman, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरद्गव|जरद्गवः
जरद्गव जरद्गव, i. e. जरन्त्-गव (vb. जॄ), m.<BR> 1. An old ox, Pañc. ii. d. 169.<BR> 2. A proper name, Hit. i. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरस्
जरस् जरस्, i. e. जॄ + अस्, and जरा जरा, i. e. जॄ + आ; जरस् is optionally the base of the cases of which the terminations begin with a vowel, f.<BR> 1. Old age, Man. 6, 62; Daśak. in Chr. 189, 13; Bhāg. P. 3, 2, 3.<BR> 2. Digestion, Rām. 3, 53, 59.<BR> 3. A proper name, MBh. 2, 715.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अ-जर अ-जर, adj. ever young, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. i. 64, 3 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a " target="_blank">Page0326-a + 39</a>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरस्
अ-जरस् अ-जरस्, adj. not to be worn out by use, MBh. 13, 5862.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरस
ऽजरस -जरस् + अ, a substitute for जरस्, when the latter part of a comp. adv., also of the adj. वीतजन्मजरस, i. e. वि-इत-जन्मन्-जरस, Not subject to birth or old age, Kir. 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायु|जरायुः
जरायु जरायु, i. e. जरा + यु, n. m. f. The after-birth, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायुज|जरायुजः
जरायुज जरायु-ज, adj., f. जा, Born from the womb, as man and other animals, Man. 1, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरावन्त्|जरावत्
जरावन्त् जरा-वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Old, Hariv. 1621.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च्
† जर्च् जर्च्, also जर्छ् जर्छ्, v. r., i. 1 and 6, Par.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज्
जर्ज् जर्ज्, † i. 1 and 6, Par.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To abuse, v. r.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. जर्जित, Mangled, Pañc. 160, 4; cf. जर्जरित, which is perhaps to be read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर जर्जर, i. e. reduplicated जॄ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Decayed, Lass. 7, 9.<BR> 2. Ragged, Mṛcch. 49, 11.<BR> 3. Broken, Pañc. 117, 6.<BR> 4. Crushed, MBh. 3, 16049.<BR> 5. Torn asunder, disunited, Rājat. 2, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरत्व
जर्जरत्व जर्जर + त्व, n. Decay, Mṛcch. 65, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरित
जर्जरित जर्जरित, i. e. जर्जर + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Mangled, Hariv. 4676.<BR> 2. Weakened, MBh. 3, 10353.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्झ्
† जर्झ् जर्झ्, v. r. of जर्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्स्
† जर्त्स् जर्त्स्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To abuse.<BR> 3. To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्
† 1. जल् जल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be wealthy, or to cover; or to be blunt, or sharp.<BR> --i. 10, जालय, To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्
2. जल् जल् (a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To turn into water, Śatr. 14, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल जल (cf. जड),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Water, Man. 4, 46.<BR> 2. A fragrant plant, Suśr. 2, 275, 19.<BR> II. f. ला, The name of a river, MBh. 3, 10556.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजल
अति- + जल अति- + जल, adj., f. ला, abounding in water, Rām. 4, 44, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धजल|गंधजल
गन्ध- + जल गन्ध- + जल, f. ला, fragrant water, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रजल
नेत्र- + जल नेत्र- + जल, n. tears, Rām. 5, 25, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीजल|रजनीजलं
रजनी- + जल रजनी- + जल, n. frost, hoarfrost, dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजल
स- + जल स- + जल, adj. humid, Megh. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलचर|जलचरः
जलचर जल-चर, n. An aquatic animal, Pañc. 50, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलज|जलजं|जलजः
जलज जल-ज,<BR> I. adj., f. जा.<BR> 1. Water-born, Hariv. 3621.<BR> 2. Existing in water, MBh. 2, 94.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An aquatic animal, Rām. 5, 5, 30.<BR> 2. A fish, Rām. 2, 61, 22.<BR> 3. A shell, Hariv. 10936.<BR> III. n. A lotus, MBh. 2, 1813.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजकुसुमयोनि
जलजकुसुमयोनि जलज-कुसुम-योनि, m. A name of Brahman, MBh. 8, 4647.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलद|जलदः
जलद जल-द, m.<BR> 1. A cloud, Kir. 5, 48.<BR> 2. The name of a वर्ष, or division of the known continent, MBh. 6, 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधर|जलधरः
जलधर जल-धर, m. A cloud, Bhāṣāp. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधि|जलधिः
जलधि जलधि, i. e. जल-धा (cf. निधि), m. The ocean, Śiś. 9, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमय
जलमय जल + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of water, Kathās. 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमुच्
जलमुच् जल-मुच्, m. A cloud, Megh. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवन्त्|जलवत्
जलवन्त् जल + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in water, MBh. 12, 3694.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलस्थाय|जलस्थायः
जलस्थाय जलस्थाय, जल-स्था + अ, m. A pond, MBh. 12, 4893.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाय
जलाय जलाय (a denomin. derived from जल), Ātm. To turn into water, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाशय|जलाशयं|जलाशयः
जलाशय जलाशय,<BR> I. i. e. जल-आ-शी + अ, adj. Reposing in water, MBh. 3, 11123.<BR> II. for जड-आशय (which is perhaps to be read), adj. Stupid, Kathās. 6, 58.<BR> III. i. e. जल-आशय, m.<BR> 1. A reservoir of water, Hariv. 3820.<BR> 2. A pond, Man. 4, 129.<BR> 3. A sea, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाश्रय|जलाश्रयः
जलाश्रय जलाश्रय, i. e. जल-आश्रय, m. A pond, Pañc. 76, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलूका
जलूका जलूका, i. e. anomal. for जल-ओक, f. A leech.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणजलूका
तृण- + जलूका तृण- + जलूका, f. a caterpillar, Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेचर|जलेचरः
जलेचर जलेचर, i. e. जल + इ-चर,<BR> I. adj., f. री, Living in water, Rām. 4, 50, 18.<BR> II. m. An aquatic animal, Rām. 4, 51, 39.<BR> III. f. री, The female of an aquatic animal, MBh. 1, 7852.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेशय|जलेशयः
जलेशय जलेशय, i. e. जल + इ-शी + अ,<BR> I. adj. Living in water, MBh. 1, 1365.<BR> II. m. Epithet of Viṣṇu, Hariv. 14348.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौक
जलौक जलौक, i. e. जल-ओक, m. and f. का, A leech, Suśr. 1, 112, 6; 1, 39, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौकस्
जलौकस् जलौकस्, i. e. जल-ओकस्,<BR> 1. adj. and sbst. Living in water, an aquatic animal, MBh. 13, 2650.<BR> 2. f. A leech, Suśr. 1, 28, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प्
जल्प् जल्प्, (akin to or rather old Causal of, 1. गॄ), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Hariv. 1173),<BR> 1. To speak, Pañc. 35, 10.<BR> 2. To speak with or of (with the acc.), Lass. 41, 18; MBh. 4, 864. जल्पित, n. Talk, Pañc. 133, 5.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To speak afterwards, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 58.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To address, Rām. 4, 2, 16.<BR> 2. To accompany [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b " target="_blank">Page0327-b + 40</a>] by words, MBh. 12, 3189.<BR> 3. To advise, MBh. 7, 3033.<BR> 4. To determine, MBh. 4, 711.<BR> --With उप उप, उपजल्पित, n. Talk, Rām. 2, 60, 14.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To prate, MBh. 5, 1125.<BR> 2. To speak of (with the acc.), Hariv. 11301.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To speak, Pañc. i. d. 300.<BR> 2. To chatter, Pañc. i. d. 437.<BR> 3. To proclaim, MBh. 13, 3686.<BR> प्रजल्पित, Having begun to speak, Kumāras. 1, 46; n. Words, Hiḍ. 1, 22.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer, Rām. 3, 75, 2.<BR> --With वि वि, To utter, Śāk. d. 51.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To converse, Rām. 1, 74, 20.<BR> 2. To speak, Rām. 5, 89, 21. संजल्पित, n. Words, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प जल्प् + अ, m. and n.<BR> 1. Words, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 17.<BR> 2. Prate. MBh. 1, 566.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पक
जल्पक जल्प् + अक, adj. sbst. Chattering, a chatterer, Bhartṛ. 2, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पन|जल्पनं
जल्पन जल्प् + अन, n. Speaking, Pañc. i. d. 193.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पितृ
जल्पितृ जल्प् + इतृ, m., f. त्री, n. Speaking, Rām. 5, 36, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पिन्
जल्पिन् जल्प् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Speaking, MBh. 5, 2038.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव जव, i. e. जू + अ,<BR> I. m. Quickness, Chr. 297, 21 = Rigv. i. 112, 21; MBh. 3, 10891.<BR> II. f. जवा = जपा, The China rose, Rām. 5, 3, 48.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजव|अतिजवः
अति- + जव अति- + जव, m. excessive quickness, Pañc. ii. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजव|मनोजवः
मनोजव मनोजव, i. e. मनस्-,<BR> I. adj. 1. swift as thought. 2. quick in thought, 3. fatherly, parental.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजव|महाजवः
महा- + जव महा- + जव, adj. very fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
जवन जवन, i. e. जू + अन,<BR> I. adj. f. नी, Quick, Kir. 5, 7.<BR> II. n. Quickness, MBh. 4, 1414.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0327-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस्
जवस् जवस्, i. e. जू + अस्, n. Speed, velocity.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजवस्
सु- + जवस् सु- + जवस्, adj. quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिका
जवनिका जवनिका (= यवनिका), f. A curtain, Hariv. 4648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन्
जविन् जविन्, i. e. जू + इन्, adj. Swift, Yājñ. 2, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष्
† जष् जष्, i. 1, Par. To kill; to wound, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्
जस् जस्, i. 1, Ātm. (ved); i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To be exhausted, Chr. 296, 6 = Rigv. i. 112, 6.<BR> 2. i. 4, Par. † To liberate.<BR> 3. i. 1(?) and 10, or Caus., जासय, To kill, to strike, † to slight.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, Caus. or i. 10, To root out (with gen.), Śiś. 1, 37.<BR> --Cf. Goth. qvistjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नु|जह्नुः
जह्नु जह्नु, m. The name of a king who adopted the river Gaṅgā as his daughter, Rām. 1, 44, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर|जागरः
जागर जागर, i. e. जागृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Waking, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 3.<BR> 2. A vision, Yājñ. 3, 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरण|जागरणं
जागरण जागरण, i. e. जागृ + अन, n. Waking, Pañc. 27, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिष्णु
जागरिष्णु जागरिष्णु, i. e. जागृ + इष्णु, adj. Wakeful, Suśr. 1, 121, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरूक|जागरूकः
जागरूक जागरूक, i. e. जागृ + ऊक, adj. Watchful, Ragh. 14, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृ
जागृ जागृ, ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also i. 1, जागर, MBh. 12, 7823; anomalous जागृमि, 12, 6518),<BR> 1. To wake, Rām. 2, 63, 4.<BR> 2. To watch over (with the loc.), Ragh. 8, 23; with the acc., Caurap. 35.<BR> 3. To be roused, Hit. 50, 14.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. जाग्रत्, n. Waking, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 13. Anomalous ptcple. of the pres. Ātm., जाग्रमाण, MBh. 13, 1274.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass., जागरित, One who has [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b " target="_blank">Page0328-b + 43</a>] waked, Suśr. 1, 357, 18. n. Waking, Suśr. 1, 330, 8; Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 22. जागरितवन्त्, One who has waked, Suśr. 1, 330, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass., जागर्तव्य, n. Necessity of waking, MBh. 1, 5925; anomalous जागृतव्य, MBh. 13, 2746.<BR> --Caus. जागरय, To rouse, Hit. 50, 4; ved. Aor. sing. 3, अजीगर्, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To wake near to somebody, Rām. 2, 50, 36.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To lie in wait (with the gen.), MBh. 9, 1463.<BR> --Cf. ἐγείρω, ἔγρομαι; perhaps also Lat. vigil, vigilare; and Goth. vakan; A.S. wácian; O.H.G. wachar; A.S. waccor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाघनी
जाघनी जाघनी, i. e. जघन + अ + ई, f. The tail, MBh. 12, 5375; Man. 10, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गल|जांगल|जाङ्गलं|जाङ्गलः
जाङ्गल जाङ्गल, i. e. जङ्गल + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Dry, even and productive (country), Man. 7, 69.<BR> 2. Existing in such a country, Suśr. 1, 184, 12.<BR> 3. Belonging to game which lives in such a country, Suśr. 1, 72, 2.<BR> II. n. Game, Suśr. 2, 342, 21.<BR> III. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 5, 2127.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुजाङ्गल|कुरुजांगल
कुरु- + जाङ्गल कुरु- + जाङ्गल, 1. n. the name of a country, Rām. 2, 68, 13. 2. m. pl. the name of its inhabitants, MBh. 3, 356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटासुरि|जाटासुरिः
जाटासुरि जाटासुरि, i. e. जटासुर (the name of a demon), + इ, patronym., MBh. 7, 7856.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठर|जाठरः
जाठर जाठर, i. e. जठर + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री,<BR> 1. Of the belly, Mārk. P. 2, 37.<BR> 2. With अग्नि,<BR> a. The digestive power, Suśr. 1, 128, 18.<BR> b. Hunger, Pañc. ii. d. 193.<BR> II. m. A child, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्य|जाड्यं
जाड्य जाड्य, i. e. जड + य, n.<BR> 1. Want of sensation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 17.<BR> 2. Stupidity, Bhartṛ. 2, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक जात + क, (vb. जन्)<BR> I. m. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a " target="_blank">Page0329-a + 43</a>] son, Man. 9, 143 (in जार-, Begotten by an adulterer).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A ceremony on the birth of a child, MBh. 1, 949.<BR> 2. Astrological calculation of a nativity, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूपमय
जातरूपमय जात-रूप + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Rām. 3, 48, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदस्
जातवेदस् जात-वेदस्, and जातवेद जातवेद (Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 13), m.<BR> 1. The producer of wealth(?), Chr. 289, 1 = Rigv. i. 50, 1.<BR> 2. Fire, Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदसी
जातवेदसी जातवेदसी, i. e. जातवेदस् + अ + ई, f. A name of Durgā, MBh. 6, 802.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाति|जातिः
जाति जाति, i. e. जन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Birth, Man. 2, 148.<BR> 2. Existence, life, Man. 4, 148.<BR> 3. State, Man. 3, 15.<BR> 4. Tribe, Man. 1, 118.<BR> 5. Kind, genus, MBh. 4, 45; Pañc. 203, 3.<BR> 6. Species, Man. 1, 48.<BR> 7. Also जाती जाती, Great flowered jasmine, Hariv. 7891. जाती जाती, also The nutmeg-tree, Suśr. 1, 132, 20; nutmeg.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. gens; A.S. cynd; Engl. kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाति|अजातिः
अ-जाति अ-जाति, f. another sort, Yājñ. 2, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजाति|एकजातिः
एक- + जाति एक- + जाति, 1. adj. having only one birth, Man. 10, 4. 2. belonging to the same kind, Suśr. 2, 289, 12.<BR> II. m. a Śūdra, Man. 8, 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जाति|दुर्जातिः|दुर्ज्जाति
दुस्- + जाति दुस्- + जाति, 1. f. misfortune, Mālav. d. 86. 2. adj. wicked, MBh. 5, 1944.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाति|द्विजातिः
द्वि- + जाति द्वि- + जाति, m. a man of either of the three first classes, especially a Brāhmaṇa (cf. द्विज), Man. 10, 4; Bhāg. P. 6, 11, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वजाति|पूर्वजातिः
पूर्व- + जाति पूर्व- + जाति, f. a former existence, Kathās. 27, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजाति
मृग- + जाति मृग- + जाति, f. pl. the deer species, Draup. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजाति|सजातिः
स- + जाति स- + जाति, adj. being of the same class, Man. 9, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनजाति|हीनजातिः
हीन- + जाति हीन- + जाति (vb. हा), adj. being of the lowest class, Man. 3, 15; degraded, outcaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमन्त्|जातिमत्
जातिमन्त् जाति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, High-born, Rām. 2, 75, 21 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मरता
जातिस्मरता जाति-स्मर + ता, f., and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मरत्व
जातिस्मरत्व जाति-स्मर + त्व, n. Remembrance of a former existence, MBh. 3, 160; 8107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाती
जाती जाती, see जाति<BR> 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
ऽजातीय -जातीय, i. e. जाति + ईय, adj. Belonging to a caste, Man. 11, 162; or kind, Pañc. 190, 21; or genus, Pañc. 76, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जातीय
दुस्- + जातीय दुस्- + जातीय, wicked, Hariv. 4239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
वि- + जातीय वि- + जातीय, adj. 1. of mixed origin. 2. of a different cast. 3. of a different kind, dissimilar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजातीय|सजातीयः
स- + जातीय स- + जातीय, adj. 1. of the same tribe. 2. of the same species. 3. like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजातीय
समान- + जातीय समान- + जातीय, adj. of the same caste or species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजातीय
स्व- + जातीय स्व- + जातीय, adj. of one's own tribe, caste, species, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु जातु, i. e. जन् + तु, adv.<BR> 1. Ever, MBh. 5, 7071.<BR> 2. Perhaps, MBh. 12, 6739.<BR> 3. Once, Kathās. 6, 89.<BR> 4. With preceding न, Never, Man. 2, 94.<BR> 5. With preceding न, and following चिद्, Nevermore, never, MBh. 1, 1936.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष जातुष, i. e. जतुस् (= जतु) + अ, adj., f. षी, Made of lac, Pañc. i. d. 120; painted with lac, MBh. 1, 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य जात्य, i. e. जाति + य, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to a tribe, Rām. 2, 50, 18.<BR> 2. Belonging to a family, Man. 10, 5.<BR> 3. Of a noble race, Rām. 2, 45, 14.<BR> 4. True, Rām. 2, 9, 40. स्व-, adj. Belonging to one's own species, Pañc. 71, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकी
जानकी जानकी, i. e. जनक + अ + ई, patron. The daughter of Janaka, i. e. Sitā, Rām. 3, 51, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपद|जानपदः
जानपद जानपद, i. e. जन-पद + अ,<BR> I. m. An inhabitant of a country, a subject, Yājñ. 2, 36.<BR> II. adj.<BR> 1. Living in the country, Rām. 2, 50, 4.<BR> 2. Referring to districts, Man. 8, 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजानपद
पौर- + जानपद पौर- + जानपद, m. The inhabitants of the town and of the country, MBh. 1, 2828.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदिक
जानपदिक जानपदिक, i. e. जनपद + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a " target="_blank">Page0330-a + 41</a>] adj. Concerning a realm, MBh. 11, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानार्दन
जानार्दन जानार्दन, i. e. जनार्दन + अ, patronym. A descendant of Janārdana, MBh. 3, 723.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानि
ऽजानि -जानि, i. e. जन् + इ, latter part of comp. adj. Wife, e. g. अन्-अन्य-, Having no other wife, Ragh. 15, 61. वित्त-, adj. Having married (vb. विद्), Chr. 297, 15 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR> --Cf. Goth. quens; A.S. cwen; Engl. queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु जानु (for original जन्वन्त्), n. and m. The knee, Suśr. 1, 348, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. γόνυ γούνατος (for γόνϝατος); Lat. genu; Goth. kniu; A.S. cneow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्जानु
अन्तर्- + जानु अन्तर्- + जानु, adj. and adv. Having (the hands) between the knees, Yājñ. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजानु
इन्द्र- + जानु इन्द्र- + जानु, m. A proper name, Rām. 4, 39, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुविजानु
जानु-वि- + जानु जानु-वि- + जानु, n. Joining and disjoining the legs, a mode of fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतजानु|संहतजानुः
संहत- + जानु संहत- + जानु (vb. हन्), adj. knock-kneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप|जापः
जाप जाप, i. e. जप् + अ, m. A prayer, Rām. 1, 31, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजाप|कर्णजापः
कर्ण- + जाप कर्ण- + जाप, m. Tale-bearing, Pañc. i. d. 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक जापक, i. e. जप् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Muttering prayers, MBh. 12, 7153.<BR> 2. Produced by prayer, MBh. 12, 7249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापिन्
जापिन् जापिन्, i. e. जप् + इन्, adj. Reciting in a low tone, Yājñ. 3, 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्नेय
जामदग्नेय जामदग्नेय, i. e. जमदग्नि + एय, patron. A descendant of Jamadagni, Rām. 1, 74, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्य|जामदग्न्यः
जामदग्न्य जामदग्न्य, i. e. जमदग्नि + य,<BR> I. adj. Referring to Jamadagni, MBh. 1, 332.<BR> II. patron. A descendant of Jamadagni, Rām. 1, 74, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामा
जामा जामा (from *जम् = γαμ in γαμέω, an older form of यम्, by the aff. अ; cf. the next), f. A daughter-in-law, MBh. 13, 2474.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ जामातृ (from *जम्, cf. the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b " target="_blank">Page0330-b + 41</a>] last and यामातृ, by the aff. तृ), m. A son-in-law, Rām. 1, 8, 26.<BR> --Cf. γαμβρός for γαμρός; Lat. gener for gem + ros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृक|जामातृकः
जामातृक जामातृ + क, adj. Belonging to a son-in-law, Pañc. 46, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृत्व
जामातृत्व जामातृ + त्व, n. Condition of being a son-in-law, Pañc. 48, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि जामि (from *जम्, cf. जामा, but in the signification which appears in Lat. gem-ini and Sskt. यम, Twin, a pair),<BR> I. adj. and sbst. Brother and sister; related (ved.).<BR> II. also जामी जामी, f.<BR> 1. A female relation, Man. 3, 57.<BR> 2. A sister, Yājñ. 1, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्र|जामित्रं
जामित्र जामित्र, The seventh house in Astrology, Kumāras. 7, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बव|जांबव|जांबवं|जाम्बवं
जाम्बव जाम्बव, i. e.<BR> I. जम्बु + अ,<BR> 1. adj. Coming from the Jambu-tree, Suśr. 1, 190, 5.<BR> 2. n. The fruit of the Jambu-tree, 1, 73, 17.<BR> II. = जाम्बवन्त्, A proper name, Rām. 5, 1, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवन्त्|जाम्बवत्|जांबवत्
जाम्बवन्त् जाम्बवन्त्, m. A proper name, Rām. 4, 25, 33. f. वती, A proper name, MBh. 3, 670.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुक
जाम्बुक जाम्बुक, i. e. जम्बुक + अ, adj. Proceeding from a jackal, MBh. 12, 5779.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुनद
जाम्बुनद and जाम्बूनद जाम्बू̆नद, i. e. जम्बू̆-नदी + अ,<BR> I. adj. Coming from the river Jambu, epithet of a peculiar kind of gold, MBh. 6, 279.<BR> II. n. Gold, Rām. 3, 49, 9.<BR> III. adj., f. दी, Golden, Rām. 5, 7, 19.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. A proper name, MBh. 1, 3745.<BR> 2. The name of a mountain, MBh. 3, 10835.<BR> V. f. दी, The name of a river, MBh. 6, 338.<BR> VI. n.<BR> 1. A golden ornament, Śiś. 4, 66.<BR> 2. The name of a sea, MBh. 5, 3843.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुनदमय
जाम्बुनदमय and जाम्बूनदमय [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a " target="_blank">Page0331-a + 39</a>] जाम्बू̆नद + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Pañc. 175, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायन्तेय|जायन्तेयः
जायन्तेय जायन्तेय, i. e. जयन्ती + एय, metronym. A son of Jayantī, Bhāg. P. 5, 4, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया जाया, i. e. जन् + या, f. A spouse, Man. 9, 8.<BR> --Cf. Lat. gaja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायात्व
जायात्व जाया + त्व, n. The condition of a जाया, the name जाया, Man. 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायिन्
ऽजायिन् -जायिन्, i. e. जि + इन्, adj. Conquering, MBh. 3, 1383.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार|जारः
जार जार, i. e. जॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A lover, Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR> 2. A paramour, an adulterer, Yājñ. 2, 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारज|जारजः
जारज जार-ज, m. A son begotten by an adulteress, Pañc. Pr. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारता
जारता जार + ता, f. Adultery, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारासंधि
जारासंधि जारासंधि, i. e. जरासंध, a proper name, + इ, patronym. A descendant of Jarāsaṃdha, MBh. 2, 966.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारूथी
जारूथी जारूथी, f. The name of a river, Rām. 6, 109, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारूथ्य
जारूथ्य जारूथ्य, m. A kind of sacrifice, Rām. 6, 113, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार्यक
जार्यक जार्यक, m. A certain animal, Rājat. 5, 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल|जालं|जालः
जाल जाल, n.<BR> 1. A net, Pañc. 78, 14.<BR> 2. A coat of mail, MBh. 6, 725.<BR> 3. A lattice, Rām. 3, 61, 13.<BR> 4. A window, Man. 8, 132.<BR> 5. A dense multitude, Rām. 1, 28, 23.<BR> 6. A webmembrane between the fingers, Śāk. d. 175.<BR> 7. A disease of the eye, Suśr. 2, 311, 6.<BR> 8. Magic, illusion, Kathās. 24, 199.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजाल|इन्द्रजालं
इन्द्र- + जाल इन्द्र- + जाल, n. 1. magic, Kathās. 22, 12. 2. illusion, Vedāntas. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b " target="_blank">Page0331-b + 41</a>] in Chr. 218, 20. 3. the name of a weapon, MBh. 3, 14995.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तजाल
ध्वान्त- + जाल ध्वान्त- + जाल, n. deep darkness, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताजाल
मुक्ता- + जाल मुक्ता- + जाल, n. a string of pearls, Megh. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुजाल|विन्दुजालं
विन्दु- + जाल विन्दु- + जाल, n. coloured marks on as elephant's face or trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालक|जालकं|जालकः
जालक जाल + क,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A net, Pañc. iii. d. 179.<BR> 2. (m?) A window, Śiś. 9, 39.<BR> 3. A bud, Megh. 96.<BR> II. m. The name of a tree, Bhāg. P. 8, 2, 18.<BR> III. f. लिका.<BR> 1. A net.<BR> 2. A coat of mail, Rām. 3, 28, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपाद|जालपादः
जालपाद जाल-पाद, m. A webfooted bird, Man. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपादभुज
जालपादभुज जाल-पाद-भुज, adj. Having a web-membrane on the feet and the hands, MBh. 12, 13339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालवन्त्|जालवत्
जालवन्त् जाल + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Having a net, Suśr. 1, 87, 16.<BR> 2. Covered with a coat of mail, MBh. 6, 747.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म जाल्म, m. and f. मी.<BR> 1. Wicked, Vikr. 5, 14.<BR> 2. Contemptible, MBh. 5, 4518.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मक
जाल्मक जाल्म + क, adj. Wicked, MBh. 7, 9023.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्य
जाल्य जाल्य, i. e. जाल + य, adj. Exposed to nets, MBh. 12, 10417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नव
जाह्नव जाह्नव, i. e. जह्नु + अ, patron. A descendant of Jahnu, Bhāg. P. 9, 22, 9. f. वी, A name of the Gaṅgā, Kir. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवीय
जाह्नवीय जाह्नवीय, i. e. जाह्नवी + ईय, adj. Belonging to the Gaṅgā, MBh. 13, 1857.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि जि (akin to ज्या, q. cf.), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 15193). red. pf. जिगाय; ptcple. जिगीवान्, etc.<BR> 1. To overpower, to conquer, Pañc. i. d. 375; Man. 4, 181.<BR> 2. To be victorious, Śāk. 23, 11.<BR> 3. To win, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-a " target="_blank">Page0332-a + 42</a>] MBh. 3, 2229.<BR> 4. To win something from somebody (with two accs.), Daśak. in Chr. 186, 3.<BR> 5. To restrain, Man. 7, 22.<BR> 6. To excel, MBh. 2, 2577. Anomal. potent. जय्यात्, MBh. 4, 1604. Anomal. pf. परा-जयाम् आस, Hariv. 13946. Anomal. Aor. अजैष्ट, MBh. 1, 6378. Anomal. fut. जयिष्यसि, Rām. 1, 29, 3. Anomal. potent. of the pass. जीयेयम्, MBh. 7, 2702.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अ-जित,<BR> 1. adj. Unsubdued.<BR> 2. m. Viṣṇu.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass.,<BR> 1. अ-जेय, and<BR> 2. अ-जय्य, adj. Unconquerable, Chr. 44, 6; Rām. 2, 11, 7.<BR> --Caus. जापय; anomal. Aor. अजीजयत्, MBh. 7, 2280; see वि.<BR> --Desid. जिगीष, Par. and Ātm. To desire to conquer, MBh. 2, 1140; Pañc. i. d. 409.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To subdue, MBh. 12, 3124.<BR> --Desid. To desire to subdue, MBh. 5, 1274.<BR> --With अभि अभि, अभिजित, m. The leading star of the twenty-second Nakṣatra, or lunar asterism.<BR> --Desid.<BR> 1. To desire to gain, MBh. 12, 8465.<BR> 2. To assail, Suśr. 1, 122, 3.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To extort, MBh. 1, 7765. अवजित्य, Forcibly, Man. 11, 80.<BR> 2. To conquer, MBh. 4, 1118.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To overcome in play, MBh. 3, 2589.<BR> 2. To conquer, MBh. 1, 7658.<BR> 3. To gain, निर्जित, run up, Man. 8, 154.<BR> --With अभिनिस् अभि-निस्, To overpower, MBh. 14, 2220.<BR> --With परिनिस् परि-निस्, To conquer, MBh. 4, 2251.<BR> --With प्रतिनिस् प्रति-निस्, To rescind, Rām. 2, 26, 22.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्,<BR> 1. To overpower, Man. 11, 205.<BR> 2. To conquer, MBh. 3, 1883.<BR> --With परा परा, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 2, 2141),<BR> 1. To succumb, to be defeated, MBh. 4, 1604 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b " target="_blank">Page0332-b + 42</a>] (anomal. potent. जय्यात्).<BR> 2. To lose, MBh. 2, 2141.<BR> 3. To overpower, Rām. 3, 36, 13; to defeat in a law suit, Yājñ. 2, 75; पराजित, Condemned (by law), Man. 8, 58; to defeat in play, MBh. 2, 2171.<BR> अ-परा-जित, m. A poisonous insect, Suśr. 2, 289, 14. f. ता, The northeastern quarter, Man. 6, 31.<BR> --With परि परि, To overpower, MBh. 5, 712.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To overpower, MBh. 7, 70.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To defeat (in game), MBh. 7, 1357.<BR> --Desid. To desire to conquer, MBh. 7, 4376.<BR> --With वि वि, Ātm. (also Par., e. g. Man. 2, 232),<BR> 1. To be victorious, Pañc. 184, 1.<BR> 2. To conquer, MBh. 2, 992.<BR> 3. To defeat (in play), Nal. 26, 22.<BR> 4. To overcome; in विजितासन, i. e. विजित-आसन, adj. Indifferent concerning one's seat, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 8.<BR> --Caus. To conquer (anomal. Aor. अजीजयत्), MBh. 7, 2280.<BR> --Desid. To desire to conquer, Hariv. 8828.<BR> --Cf. Goth. ga-geigan (Frequent.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषु
जिगमिषु जिगमिषु, i. e. जिगमिष, desid. of गम्, + उ, adj. Being about to go, Rām. 2, 21, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा जिगीषा, i. e. जिगीष, desid. of जि, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wish to overcome, Chr. 31, 20.<BR> 2. Wish to win, Kathās. 21, 81.<BR> 3. Wish to attain, MBh. 3, 13360.<BR> 4. Emulation, Chr. 28, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुजिगीष
गुरु-जिगीष गुरु-जिगीष, adj. wishing to surpass, emulating the venerable, Kathās. 21, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु जिगीषु, i. e. जिगीष (see the last), + उ, adj.<BR> 1. Desiring to conquer, MBh. 1, 6845.<BR> 2. Desiring to excel, Rām. 1, 13, 21.<BR> 3. Ambitious, Kathās. 4, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषुता
जिगीषुता जिगीषु + ता, f. Emulation, Kathās. 18, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसा
जिघांसा जिघांसा, i. e. जिघांस, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a " target="_blank">Page0333-a + 40</a>] desider. of हन्, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Intention to kill, Man. 11, 206.<BR> 2. Intention to destroy, Bhāg. P. 4, 19, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसिन्
जिघांसिन् जिघांसिन्, i. e. जिघाम्स (see the last), + इन्, adj. Desiring to kill, Rām. 6, 77, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसु|जिघांसुः
जिघांसु जिघांसु, i. e. जिघांस (see the last), + उ, adj.<BR> 1. Desiring to kill, Bhāg. P. 7, 1, 41.<BR> 2. Desiring to destroy, Suśr. 1, 71, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षा
जिघृक्षा जिघृक्षा, i. e. जिघृक्ष, desider. of ग्रह्, + अ, f. Desire to seize, MBh. 7, 794.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषा
जिजीविषा जिजीविषा, i. e. जिजीविष, desider. of जीव्, + अ, f. Desire to live, MBh. 8, 1790.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषु
जिजीविषु जिजीविषु, i. e. जिजीविष (see the last), + उ, adj. Wishing to live, Man. 4, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासन
जिज्ञासन जिज्ञासन, i. e. जिज्ञास, desider of ज्ञा, + अन, n. Wish to know, examination, Kathās. 5, 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासा
जिज्ञासा जिज्ञासा, i. e. जिज्ञास (see the last), + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wish to know, Rām. 1, 50, 23.<BR> 2. Wish to test, Rām. 4, 8, 6.<BR> 3. Examination, MBh. 2, 1158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्
ऽजित् -जि + त्, latter part of comp. words, Victorious, conquering, e. g. कैटभ-, m. A name of Viṣṇu (slayer of the demon Kaiṭabha), Śiś. 9, 30. युद्ध-, adj. Victorious in battle, Draup. 9, 11. स्वर्-, The name of a kind of sacrifice, Man. 11, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन जि + न, n. A name of Buddha. Pañc. 236, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्व्
जिन्व् जिन्व् (originally जि + नु, ii. 5; cf. γάνυμαι for γαι + νυμαι; akin to दिव्, जीव्, and जू), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be brisk (ved.).<BR> 2. To further (ved.).<BR> 3. To help, Chr. 296, 1; 6, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 1 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b " target="_blank">Page0333-b + 40</a>]; 6; 9.<BR> 4. To love, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR> --† i. 10, To speak (? v. r.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम्
† जिम् जिम्, i. 1, Par. To eat, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
† जिरि जिरि, ii. 5, जिरिणु, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्
† जिष् जिष्, i. 1, Par. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्णु|जिष्णुः
जिष्णु जिष्णु, i. e. जि + स्नु,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Overpowering, MBh. 6, 5352.<BR> 2. Victorious, Rājat. 5, 136.<BR> 3. Excelling, Bhartṛ. 1, 5.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Viṣṇu, MBh. 5, 2571.<BR> 2. Of Arjuna, MBh. 3, 425.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजिष्णु
स- + जिष्णु स- + जिष्णु, adj. with Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहासा
जिहासा जिहासा, i. e. जिहास, desider. of हा, + अ, f. Wish to resign, Bhāg. P. 5, 5, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहासु
जिहासु जिहासु, i. e. जिहास (see the last), + उ, adj. Wishing to resign, Bhāg. P. 5, 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षा
जिहीर्षा जिहीर्षा, i. e. जिहीर्ष, desider. of हृ, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wish to take, to seize, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 25.<BR> 3. Wish to remove, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षु
जिहीर्षु जिहीर्षु, i. e. जिहीर्ष (see the last), + उ, adj.<BR> 1. Wishing to fetch, to rob, Daśak. 1, 36; MBh. 7, 8980.<BR> 2. Wishing to remove, Rājat. 5, 401.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म जिह्म (probably akin to ह्वृ, for primitive जिह्वृ, i. e. redupl. ह्वृ, + अ), adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Oblique, Chr. 292, 11 = Rigv. i. 85, 11.<BR> 2. Squinting, Suśr. 2, 349, 3.<BR> 3. Crooked, fallacious, Rām. 5, 89, 69.<BR> 4. ˚मम्, adv. Astray, MBh. 5, 7361.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अ- + जिह्म अ- + जिह्म,<BR> I. adj. candid, Yājñ. 1, 123.<BR> II. m. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
वि- + जिह्म वि- + जिह्म, adj. 1. crooked. 2. dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मग|जिह्मगः
जिह्मग जिह्म-ग, m. A snake, MBh. 1, 982.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मता
जिह्मता जिह्म + ता, f. Falsehood, Rām. 2, 43, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मित
जिह्मित जिह्मित, i. e. जिह्म + इत, adj. Crooked, Mṛcch. 143, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्व|जिह्वं|जिह्वः
जिह्व जिह्व, i. e. जिह्वे (a redupl. form of ह्वे, for primitive ध्वे), + अ,<BR> I. m. and f. वा, The tongue, Hariv. 6326; Man. 2, 90.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. lingua for dingua; Goth. tuggo (based on an older redupl. दुह्व; cf. vedic जुहू); A.S. tunge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्व|अधिजिह्वः
अधि- + जिह्व अधि- + जिह्व, m. a tumour on the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजिह्व|दीर्घजिह्वः
दीर्घ- + जिह्व दीर्घ- + जिह्व, m. the name of a Dānava, MBh. 1, 2538. f. वा, the name of a female Rākṣasa, Rām. 1, 28, 18 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्व|द्विजिह्वः
द्वि- + जिह्व द्वि- + जिह्व,<BR> I. adj. 1. having two tongues, MBh. 1, 1543. 2. treacherous, Pañc. i. d. 74.<BR> II. m. a snake, Rām. 2, 42, 2 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तजिह्व|सप्तजिह्वः
सप्तजिह्व सप्तज्˚, i. e. सप्तन्-, m. Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरजिह्व|स्थिरजिह्वः
स्थिर- + जिह्व स्थिर- + जिह्व, m. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वक
ऽजिह्वक -जिह्व + क, a substitute for जिह्वा when the latter part of comp. adj., e. g. अ-, adj., f. का, Without a tongue, MBh. 3, 16137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन जीन,<BR> I. ptcple. pf. pass. of ज्या.<BR> II. n. A leathern pouch, Man. 11, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूत|जीमूतः
जीमूत जीमूत (probably akin to जिह्म, for जिह्म + वन्त् + अ), m. A cloud, Rām. 2, 92, 32.<BR> 2. A name of the sun, MBh. 3, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर जीर (akin to जि in जिन्व्, and जी in जिव्),<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Driving, Chr. 287, 3 = Rigv. i. 48, 3.<BR> II. m. Cumin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरक|जीरकः
जीरक जीर + क, m. Cumin seed, Suśr. 1, 218, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णता
जीर्णता जीर्ण + ता (cf. जॄ), f. Frailty, Mṛcch. 48, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्
जीव् जीव्, i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., MBh. 1, 5913).<BR> 1. To live, Man. 2, 235.<BR> 2. To return to life, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 51.<BR> 3. To maintain one's self, Man. 10, 112; with the instr. 3, 152; with the loc. MBh. 5, 1059.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-जीवन्त्, Unable to subsist, Man. 10, 81.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-b " target="_blank">Page0334-b + 44</a>] pass. जीवित,<BR> 1. Living, Ragh. 12, 75.<BR> 2. Revived, Pañc. 221, 8.<BR> 3. Enlivened, Rām. 5, 66, 24. n.<BR> 1. Life, Man. 6, 45.<BR> 2. Livelihood, Hit. i. d. 85.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, n. death.<BR> अन्-अपेक्षित- (vb. ईक्ष्), adj. regardless of life, Kathās. 18, 374.<BR> स-, adj. still living, Rājat. 5, 58.<BR> हत- (vb. हन्),<BR> I. adj. desponding.<BR> II. n. despair.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. जीव्य, n. Life, Hariv. 14376.<BR> II. जीवितव्य, n.<BR> 1. Possibility of living, Pañc. 76, 13.<BR> 2. Life, Pañc. 221, 6.<BR> III. जीवनीय, n. Epithet of milk; perhaps, Just milked, still warm, Suśr. 1, 175, 14.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. जीवय (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 16230),<BR> 1. To revive, MBh. 1, 1995.<BR> 2. To let live, MBh. 3, 870.<BR> 3. To bring up, MBh. 1, 6152.<BR> II. जीवापय, To revive, Lass. 18, 8.<BR> --Desid. जिजीविष,<BR> 1. To wish to live, MBh. 4, 615.<BR> 2. To gain one's livelihood, Man. 10, 121.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To imitate the life of (with the acc.), Ragh. 19, 15.<BR> 2. To live in conformance with, Rām. 6, 5, 7.<BR> 3. To live for (with the acc.) MBh. 8, 3388.<BR> 4. To maintain one's self by (with the acc.) Rām. 5, 2, 35.<BR> --Caus. जीवय, To revive, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 9.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To maintain one's self by (with the acc.), MBh. 5, 4536.<BR> 2. To use, Yājñ. 2, 67.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To return to life, MBh. 12, 5675.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To live as chief, MBh. 5, 4538.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, To return to life, Kathās. 10, 97.<BR> --Caus. To revive, Pañc. 244, 2.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To maintain one's self by (with the acc.), Man. 9, 105.<BR> 2. To apply to one's own use, Man. 3, 52.<BR> 3. To gain, Man. 4, 200.<BR> 4. To practise, Bhāg. P. 7, 13, 7. उपजीव्य, That by which one maintains one's self, Yājñ. 2, 227. n. Livelihood, Rām. 2, 37, 25. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a " target="_blank">Page0335-a + 41</a>]<BR> --With वि वि, To return to life, MBh. 1, 2002.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To live, MBh. 3, 3054.<BR> 2. To return to life, Draup. 9, 4.<BR> --Caus. जीवय,<BR> 1. To animate, Man. 1, 57.<BR> 2. To revive, Rām. 4, 51, 20.<BR> 3. To preserve, Rājat. 2, 28.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्, To return to life, Rām. 5, 28, 16.<BR> --Cf. βίος, βίοτος (= जीवथ), βείομαι, βιόμεσθα, etc.; Lat. vivo; Goth. quivs; A.S. cwic; Goth. ga-quivjan, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव जीव् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Living, MBh. 13, 31.<BR> 2. Causing life, Bhāg. P. 9, 21, 13.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Creature, MBh. 13, 13828.<BR> 2. Life, Rām. 5, 3, 74.<BR> III. m. The individual soul, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. βίος; Lat. vivus; Goth. qvivs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जीव
दुस्- + जीव दुस्- + जीव,<BR> I. adj. difficult to live, Rām. 2, 57, 20.<BR> II. n. hard life, Rām. 2, 105, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जीव|निर्ज्जीवः
निस्- + जीव निस्- + जीव,<BR> I. death, Kathās. 17, 15.<BR> II. adj., f. वा, lifeless, dead, MBh. 7, 1954.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजीव
सु- + जीव सु- + जीव, n. easy life, Rām. 2, 105, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक जीव् + अक,<BR> I. latter part of comp. adj. Maintaining one's self by, MBh. 13, 6455.<BR> II. m. A medicinal plant, considered as one of the eight principal drugs, Suśr. 1, 59, 16.<BR> III. f. विका,<BR> 1. Life, Man. 4, 11.<BR> 2. A means of subsistence, Man. 10, 76; Bhāg. P. 7, 13, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गजीवक|रंगजीवक|रङ्गजीवकः
रङ्ग- + जीवक रङ्ग- + जीवक, m.<BR> 1. a painter.<BR> 2. an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवजीवक|जीवजीवकः
जीवजीवक जीवजीवक, m. A kind of bird, Man. 12, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवंजीव|जीवञ्जीव|जीवञ्जीवः
जीवंजीव जीवंजीव, i. e. जीव + म्-जीव, and जीवंजीविक जीवंजीविक, i. e. जीव + म्-जीव + इक, m. A kind of pheasant, MBh. 3, 8702.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ जीव् + अथ, m. Life.<BR> --Cf. βίοτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन जीव् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Animating, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-b " target="_blank">Page0335-b + 41</a>] enlivening, MBh. 1, 3241.<BR> II. n. Life, Rām. 4, 19, 19.<BR> 2. Subsistence, Man. 11, 76.<BR> 3. A means of subsistence, MBh. 3, 13724.<BR> 4. Revivification, Rām. 6, 105.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवन
अ- + जीवन अ- + जीवन, n. death, Rām. 2, 38, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासजीवन
दास- + जीवन दास- + जीवन, adj. living by slavish work, Man. 10, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजीवन|धर्मजीवनः|धर्म्मजीवन
