तन्त्रिन्|तंत्रिन्
तन्त्रिन् तन्त्रिन्, i. e. तन्त्र + इन्, m. A soldier, Rājat. 5, 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्री|तंत्री
तन्त्री तन्त्री, see तन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्
तन्द् तन्द्, i. 1 (or 6), Ātm. To slacken (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रा|तंद्रा
तन्द्रा तन्द्रा, i. e. तन्द् + र, f.<BR> 1. Lassitude, Suśr. 1, 13, 8.<BR> 2. Want of energy, MBh. 14, 874; Hit. i. d. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रालु|तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तन्द्रालु तन्द्रा + लु, adj. Weary, Suśr. 2, 403, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तंद्रिः|तन्द्रिः
तन्द्रि तन्द् + रि,<BR> I. m. or n. Fatigue, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 40.<BR> II. f. री, The same, Rām. 2, 80, 24 Gorr.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्री
अ-तन्द्री अ-तन्द्री, and निस्-तन्द्रि, adj. unwearied, indefatigable, MBh. 12, 12585, Rām. 2, 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिता
तन्द्रिता तन्द्रिता, i. e. तन्द्रिन् + ता, Lassitude, MBh. 12, 10512.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिन्|तंद्रिन्
तन्द्रिन् तन्द्रिन्, i. e. तन्द्रा + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Lazy, MBh. 12, 7740.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रिन्|अतंद्रिन्
अ- + तन्द्रिन् अ- + तन्द्रिन्, adj. 1. without remissness, Man. 3, 279. 2. unwearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय तन्मय, i. e. तद् + मय, adj. Having the essence of him, her, it, that, MBh. 3, 1143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मयता
तन्मयता तन्मय + ता, f. and तन्मयत्व तन्मय + त्व, n. Identity with him, her, it, that, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 2; MBh. 5, 1622.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्र|तन्मात्रं
तन्मात्र तन्मात्र, i. e. तद्-मात्र,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. That only, Pañc. i. d. 284.<BR> 2. An atom, or rudimentary element, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 19.<BR> II. adj. Consisting of atoms, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्रता
तन्मात्रता तन्मात्र + ता, f. and तन्मात्रत्व तन्मात्र + त्व, n. The condition [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-b " target="_blank">Page0352-b + 45</a>] of being an atom, or rudimentary principle, Mārk. P. 45, 46, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
1. तप् तप्, i. 1. Par. (also Ātm. MBh. 1, 8414), i. 4, Ātm. or pass. (also Par. MBh. 1, 3165).<BR> I. i. 1,<BR> 1. To warm, to heat, Rām. 1, 14, 17.<BR> 2. To be warm, MBh. 2, 1333.<BR> 3. To shine, Śāk. d. 111; to illuminate, Bhag. 11, 19.<BR> 4. To burn up, to consume, Bhāg. P. 7, 3, 4.<BR> 5. To give pain, MBh. 1, 3323.<BR> II. i. 1, and i. 4, or pass.,<BR> 1. To suffer pain, MBh. 8, 1794; MBh. 1, 6217; 1, 3165,<BR> 2. To mortify one's flesh, Rām. 1, 58, 1, and 4 Gorr.; usually with तपस्, To do penance, Man. 2, 167; 166.<BR> III. i. 4, To become warm, Lass. 12, 19 (with the termination of the Par.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तप्त,<BR> 1. Hot, Man. 8, 272.<BR> 2. Molten, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 6, 13.<BR> 3. also तपित, Refined, MBh. 3, 1722; Hariv. 13035.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. तपनीय, n. Gold, Rām. 6, 70, 41. तप्य, Doing religious penance, MBh. 12, 10381 (cf. 13, 750).<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, Par. and Ātm., तापय, Par.<BR> 1. To warm, to heat, MBh. 12, 5536; to burn, Rām. 6, 11, 44.<BR> 2. To torment, Rām. 5, 32, 36; by mortification, Chr. 46, 23.<BR> 3. To mortify one's flesh, MBh. 3, 8199. Anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. तापयान, MBh. 15, 855.<BR>--Frequentat. तातप्य, To suffer violent pain, Rām. 1, 11, 8.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, i. 1, To heat excessively, Rām. 3, 12, 8. अतितप्त, Very afflicted, Rām. 3, 66, 26.<BR> --Caus. To heat excessively, MBh. 14, 506.<BR> --With अनु अनु, i. 4. or pass. To suffer pain, MBh. 3, 13720.<BR> --i. 1, and 4,<BR> 1. To repent, MBh. 5, 1822; Rām. 2, 42, 11.<BR> 2. To grieve, to long for (with the acc.), MBh. 11, 182; 7, 2195. अनु-तप्त, Hot, Suśr. 2, 181, 14.<BR> --Caus. To cause to grieve, Ragh. 8, 88.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, i. 4, or pass. To repent, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0353-a " target="_blank">Page0353-a + 41</a>] MBh. 13, 5335.<BR> --With अभि अभि, i. 4, or pass., To suffer pain, Rām. 2, 62, 5; Kathās. 21, 72; MBh. 7, 6555 (with the termination of the Par.). अभितप्त,<BR> 1. Heated, Bhāg. P. 3, 6, 11.<BR> 2. Illuminated, Ṛt. 4, 14.<BR> 3. Tormented, MBh. 6, 5771.<BR> --Caus. To torment, MBh. 7, 1417.<BR> --With अव अव, Caus. To illuminate, MBh. 5, 7162.<BR> --With आ आ, i. 4, or pass.<BR> 1. To suffer pain, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 13.<BR> 2. To mortify one's flesh, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 8. आतप्त, Refined, Hariv. 15769.<BR> --With उद्, i. 1, To torment, Śiś. 9, 67; to afflict, Rājat. 3, 183; उत्तप्त, Nealed, purged by fire, Rājat. 4, 368; उत्तप्त ताम्र, Pure copper.<BR> --Caus. To warm, MBh. 12, 11884.<BR> --With उप उप, i. 4, or pass. To become hot, MBh. 3, 71; to suffer pain, Suśr. 1, 21, 16. उपतप्त, Hot, Rām. 2, 59, 9.<BR> --Caus. To torment, to mortify, MBh. 3, 10708.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, i. 4, or pass. To suffer pain, MBh. 2, 856.<BR> --With निस् निस्, of which the स् becomes ष्, i. 1, To purify, MBh. 7, 9458. निष्टप्त,<BR> 1. Singed, MBh. 1, 8215.<BR> 2. Warmed, MBh. 13, 1796.<BR> 3. Roasted, Rām. 2, 97, 2.<BR> 4. Refined, MBh. 6, 228.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, विनिष्टप्त, Well roasted, Rām. 3, 76, 10.<BR> --With परि परि, i. 1,<BR> 1. To set on fire, Rām. 3, 35, 15.<BR> 2. i. 1, and i. 4, or pass. To suffer pain, Rām. 2, 66, 7; MBh. 3, 9916; 14, 1070 (with the termination of the Par.).<BR> 3. i. 4, or pass. To mortify one's flesh, MBh. 1, 4784.<BR> --Caus. To torment, Rām. 5, 86, 9.<BR> --With विपरि वि-परि, i. 4, or pass. To suffer much pain, Rām. 2, 19, 3, Gorr.<BR> --With पश्चात् पश्चात्, i. 4, or pass. To repent, MBh. 8, 1795.<BR> --With प्र [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0353-b " target="_blank">Page0353-b + 43</a>] प्र, i. 1, To heat, Bhag. 11, 30; to burn, MBh. 3, 881; to roast, Rām. 2, 91, 65.<BR> 2. To shine, MBh. 13, 2125.<BR> 3. To illuminate, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 30.<BR> 4. To suffer pain, Rām. 2, 12, 1.<BR> 5. To mortify one's flesh, Rām. 1, 67, 8.<BR> 6. To torment, MBh. 6, 5567.<BR> --i. 4, or pass. To suffer pain, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 21.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To warm, Man. 4, 53; to heat, Mārk. P. 14, 60.<BR> 2. To illuminate, Rām. 4, 60, 16.<BR> 3. To set on fire.<BR> 4. To torment, MBh. 4, 550; 6, 3103. Anomalous प्रतापिता (fut. i) instead of प्रतापयिता, MBh. 8, 1971.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, अभिप्रतप्त,<BR> 1. Dried, Suśr. 1, 158, 12.<BR> 2. Tormented, Rām. 2, 21, 54.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, संप्रतप्त, Suffering, Suśr. 1, 70, 17.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, प्र-वितप्त, Tormented, Kām. Nītis. 15, 9.<BR> --With सम् सम्, i. 1, To repent, MBh. 7, 4731.<BR> --i. 4, or pass.<BR> 1. To suffer pain, Bhartṛ. 2, 84.<BR> 2. To mortify one's flesh, Rām. 1, 63, 26. संतप्त,<BR> 1. Heated, Rām. 4, 44, 26.<BR> 2. Molten, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 32, 10.<BR> 3. Dried, Rām. 2, 85, 17.<BR> 4. Tormented, Ṛt. 1, 27.<BR> 5. संतप्त-वक्षस्, Shortbreathed. Suśr. 2, 447, 7.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To warm, Hit. i. d. 81.<BR> 2. To burn, MBh. 1, 1270.<BR> 3. To set on fire, MBh. 13, 3998.<BR> 4. To torment by heat, Bhartṛ. 2, 86; to torment, Pañc. iii. d. 244.<BR> --With अतिसम् अति-सम्, अतिसंतप्त, Much afflicted, Rām. 3, 68, 15.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, अभिसंतप्त, Tormented, Rām. 4, 57, 13.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, To suffer pain, Rām. 4, 21, 11.<BR> --Cf. τέϕρα, Τέμπεα; Lat. tepeo; probably A.S. tháfian (to suffer, to allow), concerning the signification cf. Sskr. क्षम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
† 2. तप् तप्, i. 4, Ātm. To govern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप तप् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Illuminating.<BR> 2. Tormenting, e. g. परंतप.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Heat, Pañc. 121, 13.<BR> 2. The hot season, Śiś. 1, 66.<BR> 3. Penance, Hariv. 15434.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतप
सु- + तप सु- + तप, adj. having accomplished great religious austerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन तप् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Warming, shining, Rām. 6, 79, 57.<BR> 2. Tormenting, MBh. 12, 10381.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Rām. 1, 16, 11.<BR> 2. The name of a hell, Man. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीयमय
तपनीयमय तपनीय + मय (vb. तप्), adj., f. यी, Golden, MBh. 7, 4389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस् तप् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Fire, Man. 6, 23.<BR> 2. Penance, mortification, religious austerity, devotion, Man. 1, 33.<BR> 3. The name of a month, January--February, Suśr. 1, 19, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्
अ- + तपस् अ- + तपस्, adj. one who does not practise austerities, Man. 4, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतपस्
दीर्घ- + तपस् दीर्घ- + तपस्, adj. practising longlasting austerities, Rām. 1, 59, 11 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतपस्|पंचतपस्
पञ्चतपस् पञ्चतपस्, i. e. पञ्चन्-, adj. sitting exposed to five fires, i. e. four blazing around him with the sun above, Man. 6, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातपस्
महा- + तपस् महा- + तपस्, or सु-तपस्, adj. one who has practised great religious austerities, Chr. 39, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहातपस्
सु-महा- + तपस् सु-महा- + तपस्, adj. one who has practised very great religious austerities, Chr. 11, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
1. तपस्य तपस्य, a denominat. derived from तपस् by य, Par. To mortify one's flesh, Bhag. 9, 27; Kir. 5, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
2. तपस्य तपस् + य,<BR> I. m. The name of a month, February--March, Suśr. 1, 19, 8.<BR> II. n. Religious penance, MBh. 13, 445.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विता
तपस्विता तपस्विता, i. e. तपस्विन् + ता, f. Religious penance, MBh. 13, 2896.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विन्
तपस्विन् तपस् + विन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Distressed, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 48.<BR> 2. Devout, Man. 4, 162.<BR> II. m. An ascetic, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b " target="_blank">Page0354-b + 40</a>] one engaged in the practice of rigorous and devout penance, Bhag. 6, 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितपस्विन्
अति- + तपस्विन् अति- + तपस्विन्, exceedingly devout, Chr. 25, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपिष्णु
तपिष्णु तप् + इष्णु, adj. Burning, MBh. 12, 11726.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपीयंस्
तपीयंस् तप् + ईयंस्, comparat. of तपस्विन्, A most rigorous ascetic, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमय|तपोमयः
तपोमय तपोमय, i. e. तपस् + मय, adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Consisting in religious penance, Bhāg. P. 2, 4, 19.<BR> 2. Devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवन्त्|तपोवत्
तपोवन्त् तपोवन्त्, i. e. anomalous, तपस् + वन्त्, adj. Practising religious austerities, devout, MBh. 12, 8548.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तृ
तप्तृ तप् + तृ, m. One who heats, MBh. 1, 8414.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्
तम् तम्, i. 4, ताम्य, Par. (also Ātm., Rām. 2, 63, 50),<BR> 1. To become breathless, Suśr. 1, 120, 16.<BR> 2. To breathe with difficulty, Rājat. 5, 344.<BR> 3. To become exhausted, Rām. 2, 52, 25.<BR> 4. To be distressed, Amar. 7.<BR> 5. To become staring, immoveable, Amar. 3.<BR> 6. To choke (ved.).<BR> 7. † To desire.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तान्त, Distressed, Kathās. 24, 65.<BR> --Caus. तमय.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To become breathless, Rām. 2, 63, 50.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To become breathless, Rām. 2, 65, 45 Gorr.<BR> 2. To be distressed, Rājat. 6, 124.<BR> --With नि नि in नितान्त, Excessive, much, Pañc. i. d. 139. ˚त + म्, adv. Much, excessively, Rājat. 4, 634; violently, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 15.<BR> --With परि परि, To gasp. Suśr. 2, 447, 7.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To become breathless, Suśr. 1, 121, 1.<BR> 2. To become exhausted, MBh. 12, 12241.<BR> 3. To be beside one's self, Rām. 2, 12, 105.<BR> --With सम् सम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a " target="_blank">Page0355-a + 42</a>] To become exhausted, Gīt. 4, 21.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. temere, con-tumax, temetum, abs-temius; perhaps O.H.G. damf, damfjan, an old Causal (to choke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम तम = इष्टतम in Kirāt. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमक|तमकः
तमक तम् + अक, m. A kind of asthma, Suśr. 1, 159, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस् तम् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Darkness, Hit. pr. 16.<BR> 2. The gloom of hell, Man. 4, 242.<BR> 3. The name of a hell, Mārk. P. 12, 10.<BR> 4. = Rāhu, or the personified ascending node, Rām. 2, 63, 2.<BR> 5. One of the three guṇas, or qualities incident to creation, the property of darkness, whence proceed folly, ignorance, stupidity, worldly delusion, etc., Man. 12, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. demar; A.S. dim, thystre; Lat. tenebrae.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतमस्
दीर्घ- + तमस् दीर्घ- + तमस्, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, MBh. 2, 293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस तमस् + अ,<BR> I. n. a substitute for तमस्, when the latter part of a comp. word, e. g. सम्-, n. Intense darkness, Śiś. 9, 22.<BR> II. f. सा, The name of a river, Rām. 1, 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्क
ऽतमस्क -तमस् + क, a substitute for तमस्, when latter part of a comp. adj., Bhāg. P. 7, 1, 11. निस्-, adj. Free from darkness, Śāk. d. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्विन्
तमस्विन् तमस् + विन्,<BR> I. adj. f. नी, Dark.<BR> II. f. नी, Night, MBh. 4, 732.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाल|तमालं|तमालः
तमाल तमाल, i. e. तम् + अ + आल, m. The name of a dark-coloured tree, Xanthochymus pictorius Roxb., Rām. 3, 21, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालक|तमालकं|तमालकः
तमालक तमाल + क, m. and n. = तमाल, Rām. 2, 91, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र तमिस्र, i. e. तमस् + र,<BR> I. n. Darkness, a dark night, MBh. 4, 710.<BR> II. f. रा, A night without moon or star, Ragh. 5, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतमिस्र
अ- + तमिस्र अ- + तमिस्र, adj. without darkness, Śiś. 9, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमी
तमी तमी, i. e. तम् + अ + ई, f. Night, Śiś. 9, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोघ्न|तमोघ्नः
तमोघ्न तमोघ्न, i. e. तमस्-घ्न, m. The sun, MBh. 3, 193.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद्
तमोनुद् तमोनुद्, i. e. तमस्-नुद्,<BR> I. adj. Removing darkness, MBh. 13, 7298.<BR> II. m. Light, नष्ट- (vb. नश्), adj. Dark, Rām. 5, 32, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद|तमोनुदः
तमोनुद तमोनुद, i. e. तमस्-नुद् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. दा, Removing darkness, Man. 1, 6.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun, MBh. 3, 11892.<BR> 2. The moon, Ragh. 3, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोपह|तमोपहः
तमोपह तमोपह, i. e. तमस्-अप-ह (vb. हन्), adj. Removing darkness, Kir. 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभूत
तमोभूत तमोभूत, i. e. तमस्-भूत (vb. भू), adj.<BR> 1. Dark, involved in darkness, Man. 1, 5.<BR> 2. Foolish, Man. 12, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमय|तमोमयः
तमोमय तमोमय, i. e. तमस् + मय,<BR> I. adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Consisting of darkness, Bhāg. P. 3, 22, 19.<BR> 2. Involved in darkness, Rājat. 4, 583.<BR> II. m. Wrath, Mārk. P. 47, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोवन्त्|तमोवत्
तमोवन्त् तमोवन्त्, i. e. anomal. तमस् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Dark, Rām. 4, 44, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्ब्
† तम्ब् तम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय्
तय् तय् (originally an anomal. pass. of तन्, cf. ताय्), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. † To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर तर, i. e. तॄ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Conquering, MBh. 12, 10380.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Passage, crossing, Man. 8, 407.<BR> 2. Freight, Man. 8, 406.<BR> 3. A certain spell for banishing demons, Rām. 1, 30, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तर
दुस्- + तर दुस्- + तर, adj., f. रा. 1. hard to be crossed or traversed, Rām. 2, 28, 9; Man. 4, 242. 2. hard to be overcome, Rām. 3, 2, 46. 3. irresistible, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 32. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a " target="_blank">Page0356-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतर
अ-सु- + तर अ-सु- + तर, adj. hard to be surmounted, Kir. 5, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0355-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्षु|तरक्षुः
तरक्षु तरक्षु, m. A hyena, Rām. 2, 94, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग्|तरंग्
तरङ्ग् तरङ्ग्, a denomin. derived from the next, Par. To move to and fro, Gīt. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
तरङ्ग तरङ्ग, i. e. तर + म् + ग, m.<BR> 1. A wave, Pañc. 263, 20; signifying a section of a book, Kathās.<BR> 2. The gallop of a horse, Gīt. 12, 20.<BR> 3. Moving to and fro, Hariv. 4298.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंग|उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्गं
उद्- + तरङ्ग उद्- + तरङ्ग, adj. with high waves, Ragh. 7, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गित|तरंगित
तरङ्गित तरङ्गित, i. e. तरङ्ग + इत,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Wavy, MBh. 6, 3851.<BR> 2. Overflowing, Kathās. 18, 223.<BR> II. n. Moving to and fro, Gīt. 3, 13. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गिन्|तरंगिन्
तरङ्गिन् तरङ्गिन्, i. e. तरङ्ग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Wavy, Rām. 2, 71, 2.<BR> 2. Unsteady, Gīt. 5, 19.<BR> II. f. इणी, A river, Bhartṛ. 3, 65.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतरङ्गिणी|राजतरंगिणी
राज-तरङ्गिणी राज-तरङ्गिणी, i. e. राजन्-, f. title of a historical poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तरण तरण, i. e. तॄ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Passing over, crossing, Rām. 6, 11, 4.<BR> 2. Overcoming, MBh. 1, 6054.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तरण
दुस्- + तरण दुस्- + तरण, adj., f. णी, difficult to be crossed, MBh. 8, 3905.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपतरण
प्रतीप- + तरण प्रतीप- + तरण, n. crossing over (literally, crossing against the stream), Vikr. d. 24 (read उह्यमानस्य, instead of उद्यमानस्य, which would be the ptcple. pres. pass. of उन्द्; cf. Lenz. App. cr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणि|तरणिः
तरणि तरणि, i. e. तॄ + अनि,<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Overcoming, Hariv. 14078.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 30.<BR> 2. (? or f.), A boat, Prab. 83, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्समन्दीय
तरत्समन्दीय तरत्समन्दीय, i. e. तरत् स मन्दी + इय, n. A hymn of the Rigveda (9, 58), beginning तरत् स मन्दी, Man. 11, 253.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल तरल, i. e. तॄ + अल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Trembling, tremulous, MBh. 1, 1234; 4, 269.<BR> 2. Sparkling, Śāk. d. 25.<BR> 3. Fickle, Rājat. 3, 515.<BR> II. m. The central gem of a necklace, MBh. 8, 4913.<BR> III. f. ला, Spirituous liquor, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 75, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलता
तरलता तरल + ता, f. Sprightliness, Pañc. i. d. 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलय
तरलय तरलय, a denomin. derived from तरल, Par.<BR> 1. To cause to tremble, Amar. 87.<BR> 2. To move to and fro, Gīt. 12, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस् तरस्, i. e. तॄ + अस्,<BR> 1. Speed (ved.).<BR> 2. Energy, Rām. 5, 77, 18.<BR> 3. Strength, Ragh. 11, 77. Instr. ˚सा, adv. Speedily, Hiḍ. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्विन्
तरस्विन् तरस् + विन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Swift, energetic, Bhāg. P. 8, 20, 31; MBh. 1, 2546.<BR> 2. Bold, Śāk. 90, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तराम्
तराम् + तराम्, acc. sing. f. of the aff. तर, is joined to indeclinables, i. e. verbs and adverbs in the signification of a comparative, Pañc. i. d. 368.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरि|तरिः
तरि and तरी तरी̆, i. e. तॄ + ई̆, f. A boat, MBh. 1, 4014; 4228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिक|तरिकः
तरिक तरिक, i. e. तर + इक, m. A ferry-man, Yājñ. 2, 263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरित्र|तरित्रं
तरित्र तरित्र, i. e. तॄ + त्र, n. A boat, MBh. 5, 2436.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
तरु तरु, i. e. तॄ + उ (for original तर् + वन्), m. A tree, Rām. 6, 82, 115.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. termes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पतरु|कल्पतरुः
कल्प- + तरु कल्प- + तरु, m. a fabulous tree fulfilling all wishes, Pañc. v. d. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातरु|छायातरुः
छाया- + तरु छाया- + तरु, m. a shady tree, Megh. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितरु
प्रति- + तरु प्रति- + तरु, adv. at every tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखातरु|शिखातरुः
शिखा- + तरु शिखा- + तरु, m. a lampstand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुण|तरुणं|तरुणः
तरुण तरुण, i. e. तॄ + वन् + अ (cf. the last),<BR> I. adj., f. णी.<BR> 1. Young, MBh. 4, 1108.<BR> 2. Fresh, Suśr. 1, 191, 8.<BR> 3. Vivid, Bhartṛ. 3, 86.<BR> 4. Beginning, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-a " target="_blank">Page0357-a + 42</a>] Suśr. 2, 52, 16.<BR> II. m. A young man, Pañc. i. d. 11.<BR> III. f. णी, A young woman, Rām. 3, 59, 1; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 22.<BR> IV. n. Cartilage, Suśr. 1, 35, 1.<BR> --Cf. τέρην, τέρεινα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणाय
तरुणाय तरुणाय, a denomin. derived from the last by य, Ātm.<BR> 1. To become young, Hariv. 4745.<BR> 2. To remain young, Pañc. v. d. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुता
तरुता तरु + ता, f. Condition of a tree, being a tree, Mārk. P. 31, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्
तर्क् तर्क्, i. 10, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm, Hariv. 11402),<BR> 1. To suppose, Rām. 5, 18, 22.<BR> 2. To utter one's supposition, Śāk. 83, 5, v. r.<BR> 3. To find out, Kathās. 26, 18; Nal. 11, 36.<BR> 4. To reflect, MBh. 3, 1723.<BR> 5. To bear in mind, MBh. 5, 1895.<BR> 6. To intend, MBh. 3, 1894.<BR> 7. † To shine or speak.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तर्कित, n. Supposition, Hariv. 9467. अ-, adj. Unexpected, Hariv. 4467.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. तर्कणीय, To be suspected, MBh. 5, 1093.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To suppose, Bhāg. P. 1, 18, 32.<BR> 2. To bear in mind, MBh. 3, 1722.<BR> --With परि परि, To reflect, Rām. 5, 30, 18. अ-परितर्कित, adj.<BR> 1. Not examined, Rām. 2, 109, 16.<BR> 2. Unexpected, Hariv. 4500.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To search, to investigate, MBh. 12, 6687. अ-प्रतर्क्य, adj. Undiscoverable by reason, inconceivable, Man. 1, 5.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To think, Hariv. 13804.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To suppose, Pañc. 35, 5.<BR> 2. To guess, MBh. 1, 3571.<BR> 3. To take for, Suśr. 1, 298, 17.<BR> 4. To reflect, Rām. 5, 35, 39.<BR> 5. To infer, Kathās. 7, 67. अ-वितर्कित, adj. Not anticipated, Rām. 2, 69, 21. दुर्वि-तर्क्य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b " target="_blank">Page0357-b + 40</a>] i. e. दुस्-, adj. Hard to be imagined, Bhāg. P. 7, 10, 53.<BR> --With संवि सम्-वि, To reflect, MBh. 4, 234.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To take for, MBh. 1, 6540.<BR> --Cf. ἀ-τρεκής, probably also ἄ-τρακτος (cf. तर्कु); Lat. torquere, torcular, torques, torvus; O.H.G. drajan; N.G. drehen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अ-तर्क्य अ-तर्क्य, and निस्-, adj. incomprehensible, Bhāg. P. 3, 33, 3; MBh. 12, 11299.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क तर्क् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Supposition, Rām. 5, 71, 12.<BR> 2. Consideration, Pañc. iii. d. 258.<BR> 3. Logical reasoning, logic, Man. 12, 106; MBh. 2, 453.<BR> 4. A philosophical system, Prab. 86, 14.<BR> II. f. का, Logical reasoning, MBh. 4, 892.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतर्क|कुतर्कः
कु- + तर्क कु- + तर्क, and दुस्-, m. wrong reasoning, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 22; 6, 9, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कक|तर्ककः
तर्कक तर्क + क, adj. Poor(?), MBh. 12, 1537.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किन्
तर्किन् तर्किन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. i. e. तर्क् + इन्, Supposing, Śāk. 103, 19.<BR> 2. i. e. तर्क + इन्, Skilled in speculation, Man. 12, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कु|तर्कुः
तर्कु तर्क् + उ, m.(?), A spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुट|तर्कुटं
तर्कुट तर्क् + उट,<BR> I. n. Spinning.<BR> II. f. टी, A distaff, a spindle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रतर्कुटी
सूत्र- + तर्कुटी सूत्र- + तर्कुट, f. टी, A distaff, a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्
तर्ज् तर्ज्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 7, 6131),<BR> 1. To menace, Rām. 2, 96, 26.<BR> 2. To blame, MBh. 8, 1543.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. To menace, Ragh. 12, 41.<BR> 2. To blame, Hariv. 11166.<BR> 3. To terrify, Rām. 6, 98, 31.<BR> 4. To ridicule, MBh. 5, 2485. तर्जित, n. Menacing, Rām. 5, 66, 22.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To menace, Rām. 3, 55, 32.<BR> 2. To blame, Ṛt. 5, 6, v. r.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, The same, MBh. 7, 7176.<BR> --With परि परि, To menace, Rām. 5, 42, 9.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To menace, Bhāg. P. 8, 11, 30.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a " target="_blank">Page0358-a + 40</a>] blame, Ṛt. 5, 6.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To menace, Rām. 3, 68, 43.<BR> 2. To blame. Rām. 4, 61, 26.<BR> --Cf. A.S. threagan (to chide); O.H.G. drawjan; N.G. drohen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जन|तर्जनं|तर्ज्जन|तर्ज्जनं
तर्जन तर्ज् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Menacing, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 20.<BR> 2. Blaming, Rām. 5, 66, 3.<BR> 3. Terrifying, MBh. 3, 12569.<BR> II. f. ना, Menacing, Sāh. D. 66, 11.<BR> III. f. नी, The forefinger, Kathās. 17, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णक|तर्णकः
तर्णक तर्णक, probably akin to तरुण, m. A calf, Rājat. 5, 431.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द्
तर्द् तर्द्, i. 1, Par. To kill; see तृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पण|तर्पणं
तर्पण तर्पण, i. e. तृप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Satisfaction given or received, Kathās. 26, 236; MBh. 14, 673.<BR> 2. An oblation to the deities or Manes, Yājñ. 1, 46; Man. 3, 70.<BR> 3. Pleasing, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 27.<BR> 4. A sweetmeat(?), MBh. 18, 269.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पण|अपतर्पणं
अप- + तर्पण अप- + तर्पण, n. fasting (in sickness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पण|घ्राणतर्पणः
घ्राण-तर्पण घ्राण-तर्पण, 1. adj. smelling sweetly, Hariv. 3710. 2. n. perfume, Rām. 2, 94, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतर्पण|पितृतर्पणं
पितृ- + तर्पण पितृ- + तर्पण, n. oblation to the Manes, Man. 2, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब्
† तर्ब् तर्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष|तर्षः
तर्ष तर्ष, i. e. तृष् + अ, m. Thirst, desire, MBh. 12, 4296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षण|तर्षणं
तर्षण तर्षण, i. e. तृष् + अन, n. Desiring, Bhāg. P. 3, 25, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षुल
ऽतर्षुल -तर्षुल, i. e. तृष् + उल, in अ-तर्षुल + म्, adv. Without desire, MBh. 12, 7762.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हि
तर्हि त + र्हि, see तद् (probably for तत्र-हि), adv.<BR> 1. At that time, Bhāg. P. 1, 8, 12.<BR> 2. Then, therefore, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्
† तल् तल्, i. 1 and 10. To fulfil a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल तल, m. and n.<BR> 1. Surface, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-b " target="_blank">Page0358-b + 45</a>] MBh. 3, 2412.<BR> 2. Bottom, Rām. 5, 13, 11.<BR> 3. Without a special signification, as latter part of many comp. words, e. g. नभस्-तल = नभस्, Heaven, Bhāg. P. 2, 1, 27.<BR> 4. The palm, Arj. 3, 40; often compounded with a word denoting hand, e. g. पाणि-तल, MBh. 13, 5013.<BR> 5. Sole of the foot, Rām. 5, 13, 47; usually compounded with a word signifying foot, e. g. पाद-तल, MBh. 13, 7444.<BR> 6. That which is under or below anything, under, Hit. 43, 21; Mṛcch. 34, 11; Man. 2, 59 (अङ्गुष्ठमूलस्य तले, Under the root of the thumb).<BR> 7. (also f. ला), A leathern fence worn by archers on the left arm, MBh. 6, 621 (तलबद्ध = बद्धतल, Having put on a leathern fence, etc., cf. तलत्र), Rām. 2, 87, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अ- + तल अ- + तल, n. the name of a hell, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तल
अधस्- + तल अधस्- + तल, m. or n. that which is under anything, Pañc. 187, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतल|करतलः
कर- + तल कर- + तल, m. or n. the palm, Rām. 2, 66, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलातल|तलातलं
तलातल तलातल, i. e. तल-अ-तल, n. the name of a hell, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतल
पाद- + तल पाद- + तल, n. the sole of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतल
भू- + तल भू- + तल, n. the earth, Pañc. 43, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातल|महातलं
महा- + तल महा- + तल, n. the name of a hell, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीतल
मही- + तल मही- + तल, m. or n. the earth, Rām. 3, 52, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसातल|रसातलं
रसा- + तल रसा- + तल, n. 1. the lowest of the seven hells, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 2. 2. the lower regions, Bhartṛ. 2, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटतल
वट- + तल वट- + तल, under a fig-tree, Pañc. 9, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितल|वितलं
वि- + तल वि- + तल, n. one of the seven hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षतल
वृक्ष- + तल वृक्ष- + तल, n. the foot of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलातल
शिला- + तल शिला- + तल, n. the surface of a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतल|सुतलः
सु- + तल सु- + तल, m. one of the hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ततल
हस्त- + तल हस्त- + तल, m. 1. the palm of the hand. 2. the hand. 3. the tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलतस्
तलतस् तल + तस्, adv. From the bottom, Śiś. 9, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलत्र
तलत्र तल + त्र (vb. त्रा), n. A leathern fence worn by archers on the left arm, MBh. 6, 1673.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतलत्र
स- + तलत्र स- + तलत्र, adj. with leathern fences, MBh. 8, 616.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन्
तलिन् तलिन्, i. e. तल + इन्, adj., f. नी, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a " target="_blank">Page0359-a + 37</a>] Wearing the leathern fence of the archers (see तल,<BR> 7), MBh. 5, 5367.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्प|तल्पं|तल्पः
तल्प तल्प, m. and n.<BR> 1. A bed, Man. 3, 3.<BR> 2. A turret, MBh. 1, 7577.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्प|गुरुतल्पः
गुरु- + तल्प गुरु- + तल्प, m. one who violates the bed of his guru, i. e. of his father or teacher, Man. 9, 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पक|तल्पकः
तल्पक तल्प + क, m. One who makes beds, Kām. Nītis. 12, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पज
तल्पज तल्प-ज, adj. Brought forth in the marriage-bed, Man. 9, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्
तवस् तवस्, i. e. तु + अस्, adj. Strong, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतवस्
स्व- + तवस् स्व- + तवस्, adj. possessed of own or innate strength, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविषी
तविषी तविषी, i. e. तवस् + अ + ई, f. Strength, Chr. 290, 5 = Rigv. i. 64, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्
† तस् तस्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To wane,<BR> 2. To cast, v. r.<BR> 3. To cast aloft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्कर|तस्करः
तस्कर तस्-कर (probably for अतस्-), m. A thief, Man. 4, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करता
तस्करता तस्कर + ता, f., and तस्करत्व तस्कर + त्व, n. Theft, Ragh. 1, 27; Daśak. in Chr. 193, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्थु
तस्थु तस्थु (from तस्थुस्, the weak form of the ptcple. pf. Par. of स्था), adj. Immoveable, Bhāg. P. 7, 7, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड ताड, i. e. तड् + अ, adj. Striking, Man. 10, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडन|ताडनं
ताडन ताडन, i. e. तड् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. ना, Striking, Rām. 1, 30, 17 Gorr.<BR> II. n. (The act of) striking, Yājñ. 1, 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयितृ
ताडयितृ ताडयितृ, i. e. तड् + तृ, m. One who strikes, Yājñ. 2, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडाग
ताडाग ताडाग, i. e. तडाग + अ, adj. Being in ponds, Suśr. 1, 170, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|तांडवः|ताण्डवः
ताण्डव ताण्डव, m. and n. Frantic dancing, Caurap. 7; Rājat. 5, 380.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवित|तांडवित
ताण्डवित ताण्डवित, i. e. ताण्डव + इत, adj. Dancing, fluttering, Prab. 21, 10; frowning, 85, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात|तातः
तात तात, m.<BR> 1. voc. sing. Dear; a caressing word used by parents addressing their children, MBh. 1, 4728; by teachers addressing their pupils, Rām. 1, 2, 7; by children addressing their fathers, MBh. 1, 6796.<BR> 2. A father, Rām. 2, 53, 10.<BR> --Cf. तत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कर्म्य
तात्कर्म्य तात्कर्म्य, i. e. तद्-कर्मन् + य, n. Homogeneousness of occupation, Sāh. D. 13, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक तात्कालिक, i. e. तद्-काल + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Lasting a time of equal length, MBh. 12, 12785.<BR> 2. Instantly appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य|तात्पर्यं|तात्पर्य्य|तात्पर्य्यं
तात्पर्य तात्पर्य, i. e. तद्-पर + य, n.<BR> 1. Purport, Bhāṣāp. 83.<BR> 2. Aim, Bhartṛ. Suppl. 19.<BR> 3. Object, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्य|तादात्म्यं
तादात्म्य तादात्म्य, i. e. तद्-आत्मन् + य, n. Identity, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृक्ष|तादृक्षः
तादृक्ष तादृक्ष, i. e. तद्-दृश् + स, adj. Such one, Rājat. 4, 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश्
तादृश् तादृश्, i. e. तद्-दृश्, adj.<BR> 1. Such one, Rājat. 5, 425.<BR> 2. Equal, Pañc. 38, 15; 19.<BR> --Cf. Lat. talis, and see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश|तादृशः
तादृश तादृश, i. e. तद्-दृश् + अ, adj., f. शी.<BR> 1. Such like, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 13.<BR> 2. Such one, Man. 5, 34.<BR> 3. Equal, Bhāg. P. 4, 27, 14.<BR> 5. With preceding यादृश, Indiscriminate, Pañc. i. d. 435; compounded, MBh. 13, 5847.<BR> --Cf. τηλίκος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान|तानं|तानः
तान तान, i. e. तन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A thread, Suśr. 1, 93, 17.<BR> 2. A musical [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a " target="_blank">Page0360-a + 42</a>] tone, MBh. 2, 133.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. τόνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतान|एकतानः
एक- + तान एक- + तान, 1. adj. turning one's attention wholly upon an object, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 8. 2. m. attention directed only to one object, Bhāg. P. 4, 20, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानव|तानवं
तानव तानव, i. e. तनु + अ, n.<BR> 1. Meagerness, Rājat. 4, 25.<BR> 2. Smallness, Bhartṛ. 1, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव|तांतव
तान्तव तान्तव, i. e. तन्तु + अ, n. Woven cloth, Man. 9, 329.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणतान्तव
शण- + तान्तव शण- + तान्तव, adj., f. वी, woven of hemp, Man. 2, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्र
तान्त्र तान्त्र, i. e. तन्त्री + अ, n. Instrumental music, Rām. 1, 3, 70 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तान्त्रिक तान्त्रिक, i. e. तन्त्र + इक,<BR> I. m. One versed in a system, Bhāṣāp. 148.<BR> II. adj. Taught in a work of the Tantra-class, Bhāg. P. 8, 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप ताप, i. e. तप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Heat, Man. 12, 76.<BR> 2. Pain, MBh. 1, 4405.<BR> 3. Sorrow, Rām. 2, 22, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्ताप|पश्चात्तापः
पश्चात्- + ताप पश्चात्- + ताप, m. repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्य|तापत्यः
तापत्य तापत्य, i. e. तपती, a proper name, + य,<BR> 1. adj. Relating to Tapatī, MBh. 1, 387.<BR> 2. metronym. A descendant of Tapatī, MBh. 1, 6505.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन तापन, i. e. तप्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Tormenting, MBh. 1, 1178.<BR> II. m. The sun, MBh. 5, 1739.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Heating, Suśr. 1, 151, 13.<BR> 2. Mortifying, MBh. 13, 1098.<BR> 3. The name of a hell, Yājñ. 3, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय तापनीय, i. e. तपनीय (vb. तप्) + अ, adj. Golden, MBh. 1, 8188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस तापस, i. e. तपस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी.<BR> 1. Performing penance, a practiser of religious austerities, an ascetic, Man. 6, 27; MBh. 1, 3006.<BR> 2. Referring to religious penance, Rām. 2, 52, 5 Gorr.<BR> II. m. A sort of sugar-cane, Suśr. 1, 186, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटतापस|कपटतापसः
कपट- + तापस कपट- + तापस, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b " target="_blank">Page0360-b + 42</a>] a feigned ascetic, Kathās. 24, 208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतापस
कु- + तापस कु- + तापस, m. and f., सी, a wicked ascetic, Kathās. 13, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस्य|तापस्यं
तापस्य तापस्य, i. e. तापस + य, n. The condition of an ascetic, Man. 1, 114; Chr. 45, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छ|तापिच्छः
तापिच्छ तापिच्छ, m. A tree, Xanthochymus pictorius Roxb., Gīt. 11, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरस|तामरसं
तामरस तामरस,<BR> I. n. A lotus, Rām. 3, 76, 14.<BR> II. f. सी, A pond full of lotus flowers, MBh. 4, 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस तामस, i. e. तमस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी.<BR> 1. Belonging to the dark गुण, or quality, MBh. 12, 33.<BR> 2. Immersed in darkness, Man. 12, 40.<BR> 3. Referring to the Manu Tāmasa (see<BR> II.), Bhāg. P. 8, 1, 28.<BR> II. m. The name of a Manu, Man. 1, 62.<BR> III. f. सी, Night, Rājat. 1, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्र|तामिस्रं|तामिस्रः
तामिस्र तामिस्र, i. e. तमिस्र + अ,<BR> I. adj. With and without पक्ष, The dark half of the month, from full-moon to new-moon, MBh. 3, 11813.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Wrath, MBh. 14, 1019.<BR> 2. The name of a hell, Man. 4, 88.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिस्र|अन्धतामिस्रं|अन्धतामिस्रः
अन्ध- + तामिस्र अन्ध- + तामिस्र, n. the name of a hell, Man. 4, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूल|तांबूल|तांबूलं|ताम्बूलं
ताम्बूल ताम्बूल, n. and f. ली, Betel, Piper betel, Lin. Suśr. 1, 223, 2; Bhartṛ. 1, 48.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासताम्बूल|वासतांबूल
वास- + ताम्बूल वास- + ताम्बूल, n. betel mixed with fragrant substances, Daśak. 88, n. 2 Wils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिकः
ताम्बूलिक ताम्बूलिक, i. e. ताम्बूल + इक, m. A seller of betel, Rām. 2, 90, 23 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र ताम्र (vb. तम्, cf. तमस्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. f. रा, Of a coppery-red colour, Rām. 2, 34, 13.<BR> 2. f. री, Of copper, Rām. 3, 21, 17.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Copper, Man. 5, 114.<BR> 2. A sort of sandal, Rām. 2, 83, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रक|ताम्रकं
ताम्रक ताम्र + क, n. Copper, Yājñ. 1, 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकुट
ताम्रकुट ताम्र + कुट, see कुत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रत्व
ताम्रत्व ताम्र + त्व, n. Coppery-red (the colour), Rām. 5, 85, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमय
ताम्रमय ताम्र + मय, adj., f. यी, Coppery, Pañc. 241, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिक|ताम्रिकः
ताम्रिक ताम्रिक, i. e. ताम्र + इक, adj. Of copper, Man. 8, 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय्
† ताय् ताय्, i. 1, Ātm. (properly pass. of तन्),<BR> 1. To spread.<BR> 2. To protest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार|तारं|तारः
तार तार,<BR> A. i. e. तॄ + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Saving, MBh. 13, 6986.<BR> 2. Piercing, Mṛcch. 44, 10; ˚र + म्, adv. Sounding loud, 92, 13.<BR> II. m. and n. A shrill loud sound, MBh. 7, 6737.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A pearl, Gīt. 11, 25.<BR> 2. A proper name, Rām. 1, 3, 24.<BR> B. (for original स्तार, cf. 3. स्तृ),<BR> I. (m.), f. रा (and n.),<BR> 1. A star, Rām. 1, 35, 16.<BR> 2. The pupil of the eye, Ṛt. 6, 31.<BR> II. f. रा,<BR> 1. A certain meteor, perhaps a shootingstar, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 32, 1.<BR> C. f. रा.<BR> 1. The knowledge which arises from reasoning in regard to the principles, the conditions of intellect, the elemental creation, Tattvas. 41 Ball.<BR> 2. The name of deities, MBh. 5, 3972; of a monkey, Rām. 1, 1, 67.<BR> D. n. Silver, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तार
दुस्- + तार दुस्- + तार, adj. difficult to be crossed or overcome, MBh. 6, 2337; Bhāg. P. 6, 14, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक|तारकं|तारकः
तारक तारक,<BR> I. i. e. तॄ + अक, adj., f. रिका,<BR> 1. Bringing over, Rām. 2, 97, 23 Gorr.<BR> 2. Saving, Prab. 25, 17.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 6, 4249.<BR> III. f. रका, and n.<BR> 1. A star (see तार<BR> B.), Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 11; MBh. 5, 5390.<BR> 2. The pupil of the eye, Rām. 3, 52, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकामय
तारकामय तारका + मय (तारका = तारा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b " target="_blank">Page0361-b + 40</a>] proper name), adj., f. यी, On account of Tārā, MBh. 2, 939.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकित|तारकितं
तारकित तारकित, i. e. तारका + इत, adj. Starry, bestarred, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारण|तारणः
तारण तारण, i. e. तॄ + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Saving, Hariv. 7022.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Crossing, passing over, Mṛcch. 146, 25.<BR> 2. Overcoming, MBh. 4, 135.<BR> 3. Saving, MBh. 1, 1050.<BR> 4. An implement of sacrifice(?), MBh. 14, 2668.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारणेय|तारणेयः
तारणेय तारणेय, patronym. MBh. 1, 6363.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारतम्य|तारतम्यं
तारतम्य तारतम्य, i. e. तर-तम, the affixes of the comparative and superlative, + य, n. More or less, proportion, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 2.<BR> 2. State or condition, Mṛcch. 157, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारिक तारिक, i. e. तॄ + इक, n. Toll for passage, Man. 8, 407.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिन्
तारिन् तारिन्, i. e. तॄ + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Saving, MBh. 6, 797.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण्य|तारुण्यं
तारुण्य तारुण्य, i. e. तरुण + य, n. Youth, Pañc. i. d. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्किक|तार्किकः|तार्क्किक
तार्किक तार्किक, i. e. तर्क + इक, m. A dialectician, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष|तार्क्षः
तार्क्ष तार्क्ष, m.<BR> 1. A kind of bird, Suśr. 1, 334, 11.<BR> 2. A kind of plant, 2, 498, 19.<BR> 3. A name of Kaśyapa, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 2.<BR> 4. erroneously instead of तार्क्ष्य, e. g. Hariv. 6966.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्य|तार्क्ष्यं|तार्क्ष्यः
तार्क्ष्य तार्क्ष्य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A fabulous being, sometimes fancied as a horse, sometimes as a bird, MBh. 1, 2548. identical with Garuḍa, Hariv. 7460.<BR> 2. A bird(?), Suśr. 2, 162, 4.<BR> 3. A kind of antidote, Suśr. 2, 275, 21.<BR> II. n. A certain medicine, Suśr. 2, 69, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्ण|तार्णः
तार्ण तार्ण, i. e. तृण + अ, adj. Made of grass, MBh. 1, 996.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीय|तार्त्तीय
तार्तीय तार्तीय, i. e. तृतीय + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to the third, Bhāg. P. 3, 6, 29.<BR> 2. Third, 8, 19, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताल|तालं|तालः
ताल ताल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The palmyra tree, or fan palm, Borassus flabelliformis, Rām. 1, 1, 64; used as banner, MBh. 6, 1811.<BR> 2. Slapping or clapping the hands together, Megh. 77; often compounded with a word denoting hand, MBh. 13, 1397.<BR> 3. Slapping together in general, Ragh. 9, 71.<BR> 4. Musical measure, Pañc. v. d. 43; MBh. 13, 995.<BR> 5. A sort of cymbal, Pañc. 20, 8.<BR> II. n. The fruit of the palmyra tree, Hariv. 3711.<BR> III. f. लि, The name of a tree. Corypha taliera Roxb., Rām. 4, 43, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरताल
अपर- + ताल अपर- + ताल, m. the name of a country, Rām. 2, 68, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकताल|एकतालः
एक-ताल एक-ताल, adj. endowed with one tree, Ragh. 15, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यताल|कांस्यतालः
कांस्य- + ताल कांस्य- + ताल, m. a cymbal, Rājat. 5, 464.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलताल|तलतालः
तल- + ताल तल- + ताल, m. slapping the hands together, MBh. 3, 12379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्ताल|मनस्तालः
मनस्- + ताल मनस्- + ताल, m. the lion of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतताली
सु-रत- + ताली सु-रत- + ताल (see रम्), f. ली, 1. a female messenger, a gobetween. 2. a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालावचरण
तालावचरण तालावचरण, i. e. तील-अव-चर् + अन, m. A dancer, Rājat. 3, 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिक|तालिकः
तालिक तालिक, i. e. ताल + इक,<BR> I. m. Slapping the hands together, Pañc. ii. d. 137.<BR> II. f. का, The palm, Hariv. 9920.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिन्
तालिन् तालिन्, i. e. ताल + इन्, adj. Provided with cymbals, MBh. 13, 1172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीयक
तालीयक तालीयक, i. e. ताल + ईय + क, A cymbal, Rām. 5, 13, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालु
तालु तालु, n. and m. and तालूषक तालूषक, The palate, Ṛt. 1, 11; MBh. 14, 568; Yājñ. 3, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावक
तावक तावक, i. e. तव, gen. sing. of युष्मद्, + अक, possess. pron., f. कि, Thine, Rām. 3, 13, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावद्धा
तावद्धा तावद्धा, i. e. तावन्त् + धा, adv. So many times, Ragh. 12, 45, Calc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावन्त्|तावत्
तावन्त् तावन्त्, i. e. तद् + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., correl. of यावन्त्, Man. 8, 155; of यथा, Nal. 20, 24.<BR> 1. So much, Man. 9, 249.<BR> 2. So long, Man. 1, 72.<BR> 3. Just so many, Man. 1, 64.<BR> 4. So manifold, Ragh. 12, 45 (v. r.).<BR> 5. Compounded with numerals, As much, e. g. द्विस्-, Twice as much, MBh. 4, 289.<BR> II. ˚वत्, acc. ntr., adv.<BR> A. combined with a correlative,<BR> 1. So much, Rām. 1, 53, 21.<BR> 2. So long, Man. 2, 235; combined with यावत् न, As long as not, Till, Hit. pr. 39; sometimes also without न, Man. 8, 27.<BR> 3. In that time, then, Lass. 5, 11.<BR> B. Without a correlative,<BR> 1. Meanwhile, MBh. 13, 2727.<BR> 2. For a while, Man. 4, 174.<BR> 3. At first, Hit. 45, 1.<BR> 4. Just, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 22.<BR> 5. With मा, Not for heaven's sake, Śāk. 66, 22.<BR> 6. With न, Not yet, MBh. 1, 1273; not at all, Rām. 6, 5, 4.<BR> 7. Indeed, Rām. 5, 49, 2.<BR> 8. Even, Rām. 5, 49, 27.<BR> 9. Only Man. 3, 53.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. τῆμος = तावत्, also τέως, ταῦς, τηΰσιος (= तावत् + य); Lat. tantus (for tāvant + o).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विस्तावन्त्
द्विस्- + तावन्त् द्विस्- + तावन्त्, twice as much, Hariv. 6927.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तास्कर्य|तास्कर्यं|तास्कर्य्य
तास्कर्य तास्कर्य, i. e. तस्कर + य, n. Theft, Man. 9, 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्
† तिक् तिक्, i. 1, Ātm. To go. ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To assail.<BR> 3. To seek to injure.<BR> 4. To challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तक|तिक्तकः
तिक्तक तिक्त + क (vb. तिज्),<BR> I. adj. Bitter, Suśr. 1, 215, 21.<BR> II. m. or n. An object of bitter taste, Suśr. 2, 136, 2.<BR> III. m. The name of several plants; Trichosanthes dioica Roxb., etc.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुतिक्तक|कटुतिक्तकः
कटु- + तिक्तक कटु- + तिक्तक, m. the name of two plants, Gentiana cherayta Roxb., Cannabis sativa, Lin.; (Rām. 2, 28, 21, Gorr., Pungent or disagreeable Trichosanthes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्
† तिग् तिग्, ii. 5 = तिक्, ii. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म तिग्म, i. e. तिज् + म, adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Sharp, MBh. 6, 3187.<BR> 2. Hot, Rām. 4, 44, 26.<BR> 3. Passionate, MBh. 13, 1161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मग
तिग्मग तिग्म + ग, adj. Flying swiftly, Rām. 3, 34, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिघ्
† तिघ् तिघ्, ii. 5, Par. To kill,<BR> --Cf. स्तिघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिङ्गुद
तिङ्गुद तिङ्गुद, Nal. 12, 3, read तिन्दुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिज्
तिज् तिज्, i. 1, Par., Ātm. To be sharp (ved.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तिक्त, Bitter, Pañc. 61, 11.<BR> --Caus. तेजय,<BR> 1. To sharpen, MBh. 5, 7169.<BR> 2. To stir up, Rām. 3, 31, 36.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. सु-तेजित, adj. Well-pointed, Chr. 30, 7. Desider. तितिक्ष, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 1, 3560), To endure, to suffer, Man. 6, 47.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, Caus. To stir up, Kathās. 18, 91.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To stir up, MBh. 5, 2742.<BR> --Cf. probably στίζω, στίγμα, etc.; Lat. stimulus for stig + mulus, instigo, instinguere; Goth. stiggqvan; A.S. stician, to sting; तिज् has lost the initial स्, as तार<BR> B., and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितउ|तितउः
तितउ तितü (i. e. probably reduplicated तन् + उ, cf. τιταίνω for τιτανϳω), m. A sieve, Cāṇ. 108 in Berl. Monatsb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षा
तितिक्षा तितिक्षा, i. e. तितिक्ष, desider. of तिज्, + आ, f.<BR> 1. Suffering, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 17; Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 24.<BR> 2. Patience, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षु|तितिक्षुः
तितिक्षु तितिक्षु, i. e. तितिक्ष, see the last, + उ, adj. Patient, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षु
तितीर्षु तितीर्षु, i. e. तितीर्ष, desider. of तॄ, + उ, adj.<BR> 1. Desiring to cross, Rām. 2, 52, 68.<BR> 2. Desiring to attain, MBh. 1, 4647.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिर|तित्तिरः
तित्तिर तित्तिर, and तित्तिरि तित्तिरि (based on an imitative sound), m. The francoline partridge, MBh. 5, 267; Man. 11, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरिक|तित्तिरिकः
तित्तिरिक तित्तिरि + क, m. The francoline partridge, MBh. 9, 2587.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथि|तिथिः
तिथि तिथि, m. and f., also तिथी, f. A lunar day, (1/30) of a whole lunation, Man. 2, 30; MBh. 13, 4238.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तिथि
दुस्- + तिथि दुस्- + तिथि, an inauspicious lunar day, MBh. 12, 6735.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनिश|तिनिशः
तिनिश तिनिश, m. A tree, Dalbergia ougeinensis Roxb., Rām. 3, 17, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुक|तिंदुक|तिंदुकं|तिन्दुकं|तिंदुकः|तिन्दुकः
तिन्दुक तिन्दुक, m. and f. की, A tree, Diospyros embryopteris Pers., Rām. 2, 94, 8; Suśr. 2, 25, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिप्
† तिप् तिप्, i. 1, Par. To drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम्
तिम् तिम्, i. 4, Par. To become wet, Hit. 79, 5 Seramp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तिमित, Unmoved, Rām. 5, 1, 26.<BR> --Cf. स्तिम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमि|तिमिः
तिमि तिम् + इ, m.<BR> 1. A large fish, MBh. 1, 1222.<BR> 2. A whale, Ragh. 13, 10.<BR> 3. A fish in general, Kathās. 5, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिंगिल|तिमिङ्गिल|तिमिंगिलः|तिमिङ्गिलः
तिमिंगिल तिमिंगिल, i. e. तिमि + म् -2 गॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A large fabulous fish, MBh. 1, 1208.<BR> 2. The name of a people and their prince, MBh. 2, 1172.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमितिमिंगिल
तिमि- + तिमिंगिल तिमि- + तिमिंगिल, m. a large fabulous fish, MBh. 3, 12081.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिर|तिमिरं|तिमिरः
तिमिर तिमिर (akin to तमस्, perhaps for original तम् + इर),<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Dark, Rām. 6, 16, 104.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Darkness, Rām. 2, 28, 18.<BR> 2. A class of diseases of the eye, Suśr. 1, 32, 4.<BR> 3. A certain plant, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 54, 11.<BR> III. n. The name of a town, Rām. 4, 40, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तिमिर
निस्- + तिमिर निस्- + तिमिर, and वि-, adj. clear, MBh. 12, 6817; Indr. 1, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिरय
तिमिरय तिमिरय, a denomin. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a " target="_blank">Page0364-a + 38</a>] derived from the last, Par. To darken, Hit. 103, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिश
तिमिश तिमिश, probably to be corrected to तिनिश, Rām. 2, 94, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमीर
तिमीर तिमीर, m. A certain tree, Rām. 3, 21, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरय
तिरय तिरय, a denomin. derived from तिरस्, Par.<BR> 1. To stop, Mālat. 21, 6.<BR> 2. To restrain, to conquer, Prab. 41, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्च्
तिरश्च् तिरश्च्, see तिर्यञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चीन
तिरश्चीन तिरश्चीन, i. e. तिरस्-अञ्च् + ईन, adj. Oblique, awry, Bhāg. P. 3, 18, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरश्चीन
आ- + तिरश्चीन आ- + तिरश्चीन, adv. a little athwart, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्
तिरस् तिरस् (for original तरस्), i. e. तॄ + अस्,<BR> 1. adv. Awry, Mārk. P. 17, 3.<BR> 2. prepos. Over, through, etc. (ved.); see कृ, धा, and भू.<BR> --Cf. Lat. trans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कर
तिरस्कर तिरस्-कर, adj., f. री, Surpassing, Bhāg. P. 1, 10, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्करिन्
तिरस्करिन् तिरस्करिन्, i. e. तिरस्-कृ + इन्,<BR> I. m. A curtain, Rām. 2, 15, 20.<BR> II. f. इणी.<BR> 1. The same, Mālav. d. 22.<BR> 2. A hiding veil, Vikr. 27, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कार|तिरस्कारः
तिरस्कार तिरस्-कार, m. Abuse, Hit. 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्क्रिया
तिरस्क्रिया तिरस्-क्रिया, f. Disrespect, Pañc. i. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीट|तिरीटं|तिरीटः
तिरीट तिरीट (perhaps for original तिरीत्र, i. e. तॄ + त्र),<BR> 1. n. A diadem.<BR> 2. m. A tree, Symplocos racemosa Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीटक
तिरीटक तिरीट + क, m. A kind of bird, Rām. 3, 78, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोधान|तिरोधानं
तिरोधान तिरोधान, i. e. तिरस्-धान, n. Disappearance, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोभवितृ
तिरोभवितृ तिरोभवितृ, i. e. तिरस्-भवितृ, m. f. त्री, n. Disappearing, Bhāg. P. 3, 27, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहय
तिरोहय तिरोहय, a denominative derived from a lost तिरोध (see धा with तिरस्), with ह् for ध्, To conceal, Chr. 52, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहितता
तिरोहितता तिरोहितता, i. e. तिरस्-हित (vb. धा) + ता, f. Disappearance, Kathās. 21, 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यक्ता
तिर्यक्ता तिर्यक्ता, i. e. तिर्यञ्च् + ता, f. and तिर्यक्त्व तिर्यक्त्व, i. e. तिर्यञ्च् + त्व, n. The nature of beasts, Rājat. 3, 448; Man. 12, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग
तिर्यग तिर्यग, on account of the metre for तिर्यग्ग, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-ग, m. A quadruped, MBh. 13, 5755.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यगीक्ष
तिर्यगीक्ष तिर्यगीक्ष, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-ईक्ष् + अ, adj. Looking at sideways, MBh. 12, 6575.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्ग|तिर्यग्गः
तिर्यग्ग तिर्यग्ग, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-ग, adj.<BR> 1. Moving crookedly, Rām. 2, 12, 6 Gorr.<BR> 2. Moving horizontally, Suśr. 1, 43, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्ज|तिर्य्यग्ज
तिर्यग्ज तिर्यग्ज, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-ज, adj. Brought forth by animals, Man. 10, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्योन|तिर्यग्योनः
तिर्यग्योन तिर्यग्योन, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-योनि + अ, m. An animal, Man. 7, 149, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यञ्च्|तिर्य्यञ्च्
तिर्यञ्च् तिर्यञ्च्, i. e. तिरस्-अञ्च् (the final स् is dropped, as often, and अ is changed to ई, as before अस्, कृ, भू, cf. विश्वद्र्यञ्च्, सम्यञ्च्).<BR> I. adj., f. तिरश्ची, i. e. तिरस्-अञ्च् + ई, Horizontal (ved.).<BR> II. acc. sing. n. ˚यक्, adv.<BR> 1. Over, Man. 8, 291 (cf. आ-गम्).<BR> 2. Horizontally, MBh. 2, 1396.<BR> 3. Sideways, Rām. 2, 23, 5.<BR> III. m. and n.<BR> 1. An animal, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 34.<BR> 2. An amphibious animal, Man. 5, 40. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a " target="_blank">Page0365-a + 39</a>]<BR> --Cf. Goth. thairh, thairko; A.S. thurh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्
1. तिल् तिल्, i. 6 and 10, Par. To be greasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्
† 2. तिल् तिल्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल तिल, m.<BR> 1. Sesame, a plant, Sesamum indicum, Lin., Man. 3, 210.<BR> 2. Its seed, which gives a good oil, Pañc. ii. d. 68.<BR> 3. A very small piece, Rājat. 4, 328.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलक|तिलकं|तिलकः
तिलक तिल + क, m. (and n.).<BR> 1. The name of a tree, Rām. 2, 91, 48.<BR> 2. A freckle, a mole, Kathās. 5, 32.<BR> 3. A mark made on the forehead and between the eyebrows, either as an ornament or as a sectarial distinction, Rām. 3, 22, 8.<BR> 4. Ornament, Rājat. 1, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकित
तिलकित तिलकित, i. e. तिलक + इत, adj. Adorned, Rājat. 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णिक
तिलपर्णिक तिलपर्णिक, i. e. तिल-पर्णी + क,<BR> I. f. का, Red sanders, Pterocarpus santalinus, Lin., Suśr. 1, 215, 5.<BR> II. n. क, Its wood, 2, 285, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णी|तिलपर्ण्णी
तिलपर्णी तिलपर्णी, i. e. तिल-पर्ण + ई, f. Red sanders (see the last), Suśr. 1, 146, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपीड|तिलपीडः
तिलपीड तिल-पीड् + अ, m. An oilgrinder, MBh. 12, 6481.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलशस्
तिलशस् तिल + शस्, adv. (Broken) to pieces as small as seeds of sesame, Rām. 3, 35, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलोत्तमा
तिलोत्तमा तिलोत्तमा, i. e. तिल-उत्तम, f. The name of an Apsaras, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्ल्
† तिल्ल् तिल्ल्, i. 1, Par. To go, v. r. for तिल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्वक|तिल्वकः
तिल्वक तिल्वक, m. A tree, Symplocos racemosa Roxb., Suśr. 1, 32, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्य|तिष्यः
तिष्य तिष्य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a Nakṣatra, or lunar mansion, containing three stars, of which one is δ Cancri, MBh. 3, 13099.<BR> II. n. The Kali yuga, i. e. fourth or present age, MBh. 6, 387.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिसृ
तिसृ तिसृ, see त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्
† तीक् तीक्, i. 1, Ātm. To go, see तिक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण तीक्ष्ण, i. e. तिज् + स्न,<BR> I. adj., f. णा,<BR> 1. Sharp, Rām. 1, 44, 22.<BR> 2. Hot, Ṛt. 1, 18; flashing, Rām. 5, 29, 14.<BR> 3. Energetic, Chr. 49, 14.<BR> 4. Of a pungent taste, Bhag. 17, 9.<BR> 5. Harsh, Man. 7, 140.<BR> 6. Subtle, Śiś. 2, 109.<BR> II. n. Harsh speech, Rām. 2, 35, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीक्ष्ण|सुतीक्ष्णः
सु- + तीक्ष्ण सु- + तीक्ष्ण, adj. very sharp, Ṛt. 6, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णता
तीक्ष्णता तीक्ष्ण + ता, f. Sharpness, Rām. 3, 19, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीम्
† तीम् तीम्, i. 4, Par. = तिम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्
तीर् तीर्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To get through or over, to finish, to settle, Man. 9, 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर तीर (for original तार), i. e. तॄ + आ, n. A shore, a bank, Man. 3, 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरज|तीरजः
तीरज तीर-ज,<BR> I. adj. Grown on a shore, MBh. 5, 2052.<BR> II. m. A tree grown on a shore, Rām. 2, 91, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ|तीर्थं|तीर्थः
तीर्थ तीर्थ, i. e. तॄ + थ, m. and n.<BR> 1. Stairs of a landing-place, a descent, Bhāg. P. 9, 19, 4.<BR> 2. A bathing-place, Rām. 1, 2, 6.<BR> 3. A place of pilgrimage, Man. 8, 356; Rājat. 5, 304.<BR> 4. A holy place, Man. 11, 196.<BR> 5. The right or holy moment, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 44; 1, 12, 14.<BR> 6. Opportunity, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 4.<BR> 7. Instruction, Kir. 2, 3.<BR> 8. A sacred preceptor, MBh. 5, 4212.<BR> 9. Certain lines or parts of the hand, Man. 2, 58.<BR> 10. A venerable object, Bhāg. P. 4, 20, 4.<BR> 11. A venerable person, MBh. 13, 5356; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a " target="_blank">Page0366-a + 41</a>] Daśak. in Chr. 182, 20.<BR> 12. Certain persons of a king's court, MBh. 2, 171; तीर्थतम, see separately.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्तीर्थ
अप्सरस्- + तीर्थ अप्सरस्- + तीर्थ, n. the name of a locality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तीर्थ
दुस्- + तीर्थ दुस्- + तीर्थ, adj., f. था, difficult to be crossed, Chr. 47, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ|सतीर्थः
स- + तीर्थ स- + तीर्थ, m. a fellow student, सोम-, n. a place of pilgrimage in the west of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थक|तीर्थकः
तीर्थक तीर्थ + क,<BR> I. adj. Holy, Bhāg. P. 1, 19, 32.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकर|तीर्थकरः
तीर्थकर तीर्थ-कर,<BR> I. adj. Saving, MBh. 13, 7023.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थतम
तीर्थतम तीर्थ + तम, n.<BR> 1. A holier place of pilgrimage, MBh. 3, 7018.<BR> 2. A holiest object of veneration, Bhāg. P. 5, 24, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थवन्त्|तीर्थवत्
तीर्थवन्त् तीर्थ + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in holy bathing-places, Rām. 3, 68, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थीकरण
तीर्थीकरण तीर्थीकरण, i. e. तीर्थ-कृ + अन, adj. Hallowing, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्
† तीव् तीव्, i. 1, Par. To become fat.<BR> --Cf. तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्र|तीव्रं|तीव्रः
तीव्र तीव्र, probably तिज् + वन् + अ, (with र् for न्, cf. तिग्म and तीक्ष्ण), adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Sharp, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> 2. Hot, Bhartṛ. 3, 19; flashing, Rām. 3, 62, 11.<BR> 3. Violent, MBh. 7, 6893; deep (of darkness), Arj. 8, 13.<BR> 4. Bad, MBh. 1, 3097.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रता
तीव्रता तीव्र + ता, f. Heat; in अ-, moderate temperature, Rājat. 1, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
1. तु तु, ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To be powerful (ved.).<BR> 2. † To increase.<BR> 3. † To go.<BR> 4. † To hurt.<BR> --Cf. τύλος; Lat. tumor, tumere, tumulus, tuber, tueri, totus; Goth. thiuda, thiuth, thiuthjan; A.S. theod, people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
2. तु तु, a particle (akin to त्व, a ved. pron., Some, one, another, etc.).<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b " target="_blank">Page0366-b + 41</a>] But, Man. 1, 109.<BR> 2. Preceded by अपि, But rather, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 17; by किम्, Nevertheless, MBh. 1, 1916.<BR> 3. Or, Man. 11, 201.<BR> 4. And, Man. 2, 22.<BR> 5. तु--तु, Indeed--but, Hit. i. d. 32.<BR> 6. Often without a special signification, Man. 7, 95.<BR> 7. Sometimes erroneously for नु, Brāhmaṇ. 3, 17 (where the Calc. ed. has नु).<BR> --Cf. perhaps τοί.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुखार|तुखारः
तुखार तुखार, m. pl. The name of a people, Rām. 4, 44, 14; also written तुषार तुषार, Rām. 1, 56, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगा
तुगा तुगा and तुगाक्षीरी तुगा-क्षीरी, f. The manna of bambus, Suśr. 2, 504, 7; 1, 140, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग तुङ्ग, i. e. तुञ्ज् + अ.<BR> I. adj., f. गा, Prominent, Bhāg. P. 1, 19, 27; high, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. a mountain, Rām. 4, 44, 20.<BR> 2. Culmination, Varāh. Bṛh. 1, 13.<BR> 3. Height, Bhāg. P. 3, 3, 1.<BR> 4. A tree, Bottleria tinctoria Roxb., Suśr. 2, 78, 19.<BR> 5. A proper name, Rājat. 6, 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गक|तुङ्गकः
तुङ्गक तुङ्ग + क, n. The name of a holy forest, MBh. 3, 8195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गिन्|तुंगिन्
तुङ्गिन् तुङ्गिन्, i. e. तुङ्ग + इन्, adj., f. नी, Lofty, Pañc. ii. d. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छ|तुच्छं|तुच्छः
तुच्छ तुच्छ, adj. Void, vain, Prab. 76, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छय
तुच्छय तुच्छय, a denomin. derived from the last by अय, Par. To make poor, Mṛcch. 178, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
तुज् तुज्, and तुञ्ज् तुञ्ज्, † i. 1, Par.; ved., i. 6 (and तुञ्ज्, once i. 1) Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To strike, to push.<BR> 2. तुञ्ज्, † To protect, or to be strong.<BR> --i. 10, तोजय and तुञ्जय,<BR> 1. † To be strong.<BR> 2. To strike.<BR> 3. To abide.<BR> 4. To give, or to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुञ्जीन
तुञ्जीन तुञ्जीन, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुट्
† तुट् तुट्, i. 6, Par. To quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्
† तुड् तुड् (a form of तृद्, based on तर्द्), i. 1 and 6, Par. To split (v. r. to procure, to destroy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्ड्
† तुड्ड् तुड्ड्, i. 1, Par. To disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्
तुण् तुण्, i. 6, Par. To curve, to bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड्|तुंड्
तुण्ड् तुण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm. To split.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To jut out, Suśr. 1, 100, 12 (probably a denomin. derived from the following word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड|तुंड|तुंडं|तुण्डं|तुण्डः
तुण्ड तुण्ड, a form of तुन्द् + र, n.<BR> 1. Beak, MBh. 1, 1474.<BR> 2. Snout, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 31.<BR> 3. The name of a Rākṣasa or demon, MBh. 3, 16372.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कतुण्ड
कङ्क- + तुण्ड कङ्क- + तुण्ड, m. the name of a Rākṣasa or demon, Rām. 6, 84, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतुण्ड|सिंहतुंड|सिंहतुण्डः
सिंह- + तुण्ड सिंह- + तुण्ड, m. a kind of fish, Man. 5, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ्
† तुत्थ् तुत्थ्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ तुत्थ, n. Blue vitriol, Suśr. 2, 13, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद्
तुद् तुद्, i. 6, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To strike, Rām. 2, 36, 14.<BR> 2. To sting, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 27.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तुन्न.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To push on, Man. 4, 68. आतोद्य, n. A musical instrument, Kathās. 23, 83.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To sting, Suśr. 1, 61, 18.<BR> --With परि परि, To stamp to pieces, MBh. 5, 2747.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To strike, MBh. 8, 4187.<BR> --Caus. तोदय, To push on, MBh. 13, 2795.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To sting, Yājñ. 3, 53.<BR> 2. To strike, MBh. 8, 2729.<BR> 3. To scratch, Rām. 5, 68, 7.<BR> --With मस् सम्, To sting, MBh. 9, 3067.<BR> --Cf. तुन्द्, Lat. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b " target="_blank">Page0367-b + 40</a>] tundo, tussis; Τυδεύς, Τυνδαρεύς; the initial स् in Goth. stautan is original and dropped in Sskt., etc.; A.S. a-stintan, to blunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्द्
तुन्द् तुन्द्,<BR> 1. = तुद्, ved.<BR> 2. † i. 1, Par. To be active, v. r. of त्रन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नवाय|तुन्नवायः
तुन्नवाय तुन्न-वाय, i. e. तुन्न (vb. तुद्), -वे + अ, m. A tailor, Man. 4, 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुप्
† तुप् तुप्, and † तुफ् तुफ्, तुम्प् तुम्प्, † तुम्फ् तुम्फ्, i. 1, and 6, Par. To hurt. तुम्प्, i. 10, v. r. of तुम्ब्.<BR> --Cf. τύπτω, τυπή, τύμπανον; Lat. stupeo; see तुद्, and cf. स्तुम्प्, in the Gaṇa pāraskarādi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ्
तुभ् तुभ्, † i. 1, Ātm. and † i. 4, Par., ii. 9, Par. To kill. to hurt.<BR> --Cf. स्तुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुल|तुमुलं|तुमुलः
तुमुल तुमुल, and sometimes तुमल तुमल (probably vb. तु),<BR> I. adj., f. ला,<BR> 1. Noisy, Rām. 1, 26, 6; तुमल, MBh. 7, 6670.<BR> 2. Tumultuous, Hariv. 9609.<BR> 3. Excited, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 23.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Tumultuous combat, melée, MBh. 2, 2688.<BR> 2. Tumult, MBh. 6, 1642; तुमल, 7, 6661.<BR> --Cf. Lat. tumultus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्प्|तुंप्
तुम्प् तुम्प्, and † तुम्फ् तुम्फ्, see तुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब्|तुंब्
† तुम्ब् तुम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To torment.<BR> --i. 10, To be invisible, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब|तुंब|तुंबः|तुम्बः
तुम्ब तुम्ब, m. and f. बी, A long gourd, Lagenaria vulgaris, Rām. 1, 39, 7 Ser.; Suśr. 1, 183, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरु|तुंबुरु|तुंबुरुः|तुम्बुरुः
तुम्बुरु तुम्बुरु,<BR> I. m. The name of a Gandharva, Rām. 3, 8, 12.<BR> II. n. The fruit of Diospyros embryopteris Pers., Suśr. 2, 43, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्
तुर् तुर्, i. 6, Par., Ātm.; ii. 3, Par. To hasten (ved.).<BR> --Cf. तूर्, तॄ, and त्वर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्
तुर् तुर्, adj. Hastening, a warrior Chr. 296, 4 = Rigv. i. 112, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरग|तुरगः
तुरग तुर + -ग,<BR> 1. m. A horse, Pañc. i. d. 314.<BR> 2. f. गी, A mare, Śatr. 14, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरंग|तुरङ्ग|तुरंगः|तुरङ्गः
तुरंग तुरंग, i. e. तुर् + अ + म्-ग, m. A horse, Pañc. i. d. 314.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरंगम|तुरङ्गम|तुरंगमः|तुरङ्गमः
तुरंगम तुरंगम, i. e. तुर् + अ + म्-गम् + अ,<BR> 1. m. A horse, Rām. 2, 45, 14.<BR> 2. f. मी, A mare, MBh. 4, 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरायण|तुरायणं|तुरायणः
तुरायण तुरायण, n. The name of a certain sacrifice or vow, MBh. 13, 4940.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरासाह्
तुरासाह् तुरासाह्, i. e. तुर-सह्, in the nomin. voc. sing., and dat. abl. du. and pl., and loc. pl., स् becomes ष्, e. g. nom. sing. तुराषाट् तुराषाट्, m. A name of Indra, Bhāg. P. 8, 11, 26; of Viṣṇu, Hariv. 14114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय तुरीय, i. e. चतुर् + ईय (the intermediate form was probably क्तुरीय),<BR> 1. ord. number, fem. या, Fourth, Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 3.<BR> 2. adj. and n. Fourth part, a quarter, Man. 11, 126; 4, 202.<BR> 3. n. The fourth state of the student of the Vedānta philosophy, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयक
तुरीयक तुरीय + क, adj. Fourth part, Yājñ. 2, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरुष्क|तुरुष्कः
तुरुष्क तुरुष्क, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, Rājat. 5, 152.<BR> 2. Olibanum, the resin of the Boswellia serrata Stackh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य|तुर्य्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य तुर्य, i. e. चतुर् + य (see तुरीय),<BR> 1. ord. number, Fourth, Bhāg. P. 4, 3, 9.<BR> 2. n. A quarter, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व्
तुर्व् तुर्व्, i. 1, तूर्व, Par.<BR> 1. To overcome (ved.).<BR> 2. † To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वसु|तुर्व्वसु|तुर्व्वसुः
तुर्वसु तुर्वसु, m. A proper name, MBh. 1, 3159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वीति
तुर्वीति तुर्वीति, m. A proper name, Chr. 298, 23 = Rigv. i. 112, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्
तुल् तुल् (akin to तॄ), i. 10, तोलय and तुलय, Par. (also Ātm. Rām. 4, 9, 100), † i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To lift, Rām. 3, 4, 44.<BR> 2. To weigh, MBh. 3, 10588.<BR> 3. To ponder, MBh. 12, 2394.<BR> 4. To suspect, Mṛcch. 33, 5.<BR> 5. To compare, Bhāg. P. 5, 5, 23.<BR> 6. To equal, Megh. 65.<BR> 7. To attain, Ragh. 13, 75.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To lift, Rām. 1, 34, 10 Gorr.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To weigh, together, MBh. 13, 2607.<BR> --Cf. Lat. tollo, tuli, latum (for tlatum); ταλάω, τάλας, τλῆσις, τάνταλος (Frequent.), ἀντλέω (for ταντλέω, Frequent.), ὄτλος, τέλος (office), τέλλω, ἐντολή, τόλμα, τάλαντον; Goth. thulan; A.S. tholian, thyldian, athylgian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलन|तुलनं
तुलन तुल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Lifting, Mṛcch. 146, 25.<BR> 2. Taxing, 50, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसिका
तुलसिका तुलसिका, i. e. तुलसी + क, and तुलसी तुलसी, f. A small shrub, held in veneration by the Hindus, holy basil, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 19; 1, 19, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुला
तुला तुल् + आ, f.<BR> 1. A balance, Man. 8, 403.<BR> 2. Weight, MBh. 3, 10385.<BR> 3. The beam of a balance, MBh. 12, 9350.<BR> 4. Equality, Ragh. 19, 50; Megh. 93.<BR> 5. The sign of the zodiac, Libra, Pañc. i. d. 375.<BR> 6. A measure or weight of gold and silver = 100 palas, MBh. 14, 1929.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अ-तुल अ-तुल, adj., f. ला, incomparable, Rām. 5, 13, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटतुला
कूट- + तुला कूट- + तुला, f. a wrong balance, Pañc. 7, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य तुल्य, i. e. तुला + य, adj., f. या,<BR> 1. Equal, Brāhmaṇ. 1, 31; with the gen. Rām. 1, 7, 17; and the instr. Man. 4, 86.<BR> 2. Indifferent, Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 24.<BR> 3. Being of the same class, Man. 8, 364.<BR> 4. ˚यम्, adv. Equally, Rām. 6, 90, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासतुल्य
मास- + तुल्य मास- + तुल्य, adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a " target="_blank">Page0369-a + 42</a>] या, equal to the number of months, Man. 5, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरतुल्य
शरीर- + तुल्य शरीर- + तुल्य, adj. dear as one's person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यता
तुल्यता तुल्य + ता, f. and तुल्यत्व तुल्य + त्व, n. Equality, Rām. 1, 4, 7 Gorr.; Prab. 27, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यशस्
तुल्यशस् तुल्य + शस्, adv. In equal parts, Suśr. 2, 327, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवर|तुवरः
तुवर तुवर, i. e. तु-वन् + अ, with र् for न्, adj. Astringent, Suśr. 1, 179, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुविद्युम्न
तुविद्युम्न तुवि-द्युम्न (तुवि is तु + इ, ved. Much), adj. Wealthy, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुश्
तुश् तुश्, i. 1, Ātm. To sprinkle (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्
तुष् तुष्, i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., or refl. pass., Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 8).<BR> 1. To be calmed (properly, to be silent, cf. तूष्णीम्), MBh. 3, 1109.<BR> 2. To be satisfied, Man. 2, 228.<BR> 3. To be content, Hit. i. d. 134.<BR> 4. To be pleased, Man. 3, 207; with the gen., MBh. 1, 8361; with the dat., Kathās. 24, 195; with the instr., MBh. 4, 291; with the loc., Pañc. iii. d. 155.<BR> 5. To satisfy, MBh. 1, 4198.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तुष्ट, Content, satisfied, pleased, MBh. 4, 291.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. तुष्य, Easily to be satisfied, Hariv. 14882.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To appease, MBh. 5, 7391.<BR> 2. To satisfy, Mārk. P. 26, 37.<BR> 3. To gladden, Pañc. 38, 3. Anomalous absolutive, तोष्य, MBh. 1, 160.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि,<BR> 1. To be completely satisfied, Bhāg. P. 6, 18, 67; Rām. 2, 2, 33.<BR> 2. To be much pleased, Bhartṛ. 2, 2.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To satisfy completely, Rām. 6, 104, 28.<BR> 2. To flatter, Pañc. 38, 22.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To satisfy, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 1.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To be content, MBh. 12, 6283.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To be calmed, Bhartṛ. 3, 4.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b " target="_blank">Page0369-b + 41</a>] To be satisfied, content, MBh. 13, 220.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. संतुष्ट, Easy to be satisfied, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 277.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To appease, Pañc. 101, 11.<BR> 2. To please, to gladden, MBh. 3, 13685.<BR> --Cf. Lat. taceo; Goth. thahan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुष्ट
अ- + तुष्ट अ- + तुष्ट, adj. unsatiable, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंतुष्ट
दुस्-संतुष्ट दुस्-संतुष्ट, adj. discontented, Hit. i. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतुष्ट
सु- + तुष्ट सु- + तुष्ट, easily satisfied, Pañc. i. d. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष तुष, m. The husk of grain, especially rice, Man. 4, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषार|तुषारः
तुषार तुष् + आर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Cold, Naiṣ. 3, 93.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Mist, MBh. 9, 3632.<BR> 2. Thin rain, Ragh. 2, 13.<BR> 3. Dew, Śāk. d. 115.<BR> 4. Hoar frost, Ṛt. 4, 1.<BR> 5. Snow, Megh. 53.<BR> 6. see तुखार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषित|तुषितः
तुषित तुषित (originally ptcple. of the pf. pass. of तुष्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. pl. A class of subordinate deities, MBh. 13, 1371.<BR> 2. Epithet of Viṣṇu, MBh. 12, 12864.<BR> II. f. ता, A proper name, Bhāg. P. 8, 1, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टि|तुष्टिः
तुष्टि तुष्टि, i. e. तुष् + ति, f. Satisfaction, Man. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस्
† तुस् तुस्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुह्
† तुह् तुह्, i. 1, Par. To hurt, to give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिन|तुहिनं
तुहिन तुहिन (cf. तुषार), n.<BR> 1. Mist, Prab. 13, 13.<BR> 2. Dew, Ṛt. 4, 7.<BR> 3. Snow, Rājat. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूड्
† तूड् तूड्, i. 1, Par. To split.<BR> --Cf. तुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण्
† तूण् तूण्, i. 10, Par. To shrink.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण तूण, and तूणि तूणि,<BR> I. m. and f. णी, A quiver, Hariv. 15940; Rām. 1, 48, 3; 2, 31, 30.<BR> II. f. णी, A disease of the nerves, Suśr. 1, 232, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णतूण
पूर्ण- + तूण पूर्ण- + तूण, adj. full quivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणवन्त्|तूणवत्
तूणवन्त् तूण + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Provided with a quiver, MBh. 3, 8486.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिन्
तूणिन् तूणिन्, i. e. तूण + इन्, adj. Provided with quivers, Rām. 6, 76, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणीर|तूणीरं|तूणीरः
तूणीर तूणी + र (see तूण), m. and n. A quiver, MBh. 7, 1271; MBh. 6, 2288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणीरवन्त्|तूणीरवत्
तूणीरवन्त् तूणीर + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Provided with a quiver, Hariv. 15154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
† तूर् तूर्, i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go quick.<BR> 2. To hurt, see तुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
तूर् तूर्, f. Swiftness, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य|तूर्यं|तूर्यः|तूर्य्य|तूर्य्यं
तूर्य तूर्य,<BR> I. = तुर्य, Rājat. 2, 91.<BR> II. m. and n. Any musical instrument, Man. 7, 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्यमय
