तृणवन्त्|तृणवत्
तृणवन्त् तृण + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in grass, MBh. 12, 3694.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाङ्कु
तृणाङ्कु तृणाङ्कु, m. The name of a Ṛṣi, Rām. 4, 41, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय तृतीय, i. e. त्रि + तीय, f. या<BR> 1. ordinal number, Third, Man. 2, 35.<BR> 2. adj. A third part, Man. 6, 33.<BR> 3. ˚यम्, adv. Thirdly, Man. 8, 129.<BR> --Cf. Goth. thridja; A.S. thridda; Lat. tertius; τρίτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयक
तृतीयक तृतीय + क, adj. Tertian, Suśr. 2, 405, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिन्
तृतीयिन् तृतीयिन्, i. e. तृतीय + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Being of the third rank.<BR> 2. Entitled to a third part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृद्
तृद् तृद्, ii. 7, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To cleave (ved.).<BR> 2. To kill, to destroy, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-a " target="_blank">Page0371-a + 41</a>] Hariv. 7621.<BR> 3. † To disregard (or, to eat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृन्
तृन् तृन्, see तृण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्
तृप् तृप् (i. 1, Par., MBh. 14, 1040), i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 1781), † i. 6, Par. ii. 5, तृप्नु (ved. तृप्णु), Par., and तृम्प् तृम्प्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To become satiate, Kathās. 26, 237.<BR> 2. To be satisfied, Man. 3, 267.<BR> 3. To enjoy, Man. 4, 251. With gen. instr. and loc., MBh. 3, 336; Hit. ii. d. 164; MBh. 4, 2320.<BR> 4. † To kindle.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तृप्त, Satisfied, Bhartṛ. 2, 82; MBh. 3, 2247.<BR> --Caus. तर्पय, Par. (and Ātm., MBh. 12, 5542),<BR> 1. To satisfy, Kathās. 26, 237; Chr. 292, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 11; Man. 3, 283.<BR> 2. To gladden, to exhilarate, Bhāg. P. 7, 2, 8.<BR> 3. † To kindle. Anomalous ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. तर्पयान (with न् instead of ण्), MBh. 14, 291.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To become satisfied, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 13.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To be satisfied after (with abl.), MBh. 13, 1922.<BR> --With अप अप, Caus. To cause to hunger, Suśr. 2, 43, 1.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To be satisfied, MBh. 5, 3604.<BR> 2. To enjoy, Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 1.<BR> --Caus. To satisfy, Rām. 1, 54, 5 Gorr.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To satisfy completely, MBh. 3, 8537.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To satisfy, Pañc. 217, 6.<BR> --With वि वि, To be satisfied, Bhāg. P. 1, 1, 19; Rām. 4, 35, 9.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To satisfy, MBh. 3, 946.<BR> --Cf. τέρπω; Lat. torpor, torpere; Goth. tharf (primitively ‘to satisfy,’ then ‘to be of use,’ cf. O.H.G. bidarbi; and finally ‘to be necessary’), thrafstjan; A.S. thearf; O.H.G. trôstjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ति|तृप्तिः
तृप्ति तृप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Satiating, Bhag. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b " target="_blank">Page0371-b + 41</a>] 10, 18.<BR> 2. Satisfaction, Man. 3, 271.<BR> 3. Disgust, Suśr. 1, 90, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृप्ति
अति- + तृप्ति अति- + तृप्ति, f. over-satisfaction, Yājñ. 1, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफ्
† तृफ् तृफ् and तृम्फ् तृम्फ्, i. 6, Par. = तृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्प्|तृंप्
तृम्प् तृम्प् and † तृम्फ् तृम्फ्, see तृप्, तृफ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
1. तृष् तृष्, i. 4, Par. To thirst.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तृषित.<BR> 1. Thirsty, MBh. 3, 101.<BR> 2. Desirous, Rām. 2, 104, 1.<BR> 3. Greedy, Ṛt. 1, 18.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. durst; A.S. thurst; Goth. thaursjan, thairsan, thaursus; A.S. thyrr; τέρσομαι, ταρσός, τρασιά; Lat. torrere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
2. तृष् तृष्, f. Thirst, MBh. 14, 1605.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्
मृग- + तृष् मृग- + तृष्, f. mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्
स- + तृष् स- + तृष्, adj. 1. thirsty. 2. greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषा
तृषा तृष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Thirst, Pañc. 81, 22.<BR> 2. Desire, Hit. i. d. 133.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृषा
मृग- + तृषा मृग- + तृषा, f. mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णज्
तृष्णज् तृष्णज्, i. e. तृष् + न-ज, adj. Thirsty, Chr. 289, 11 = Rigv. i. 85, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णा
तृष्णा तृष्णा, i. e. तृष् + न, f.<BR> 1. Thirst, Man. 8, 67.<BR> 2. Desire, Bhartṛ. 2, 70.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृष्णा
अति- + तृष्णा अति- + तृष्णा, f. excess of covetousness, Man. 7, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृष्ण
अति-तृष्ण अति-तृष्ण, adj. very thirsty, Ragh. 2, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्णा
मृग- + तृष्णा मृग- + तृष्णा, f. mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्णा
वि- + तृष्णा वि- + तृष्णा, adj. free from desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्णम्
स-तृष्ण + म् स-तृष्ण + म्, adv. with desire, Śāk. d. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णालु
तृष्णालु तृष्णा + लु, adj. Very thirsty, Suśr. 2, 383, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह्
तृह् तृह्, ii. 7, त्रिणेह्, तृंह्, Par. To crush (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ तॄ, i. 1, Par. (sometimes also Ātm., MBh. 1, 6184).<BR> 1. To pass over, Man. 4, 194; to cross, Man. 4, 77.<BR> 2. To hasten, Śāk. d. 8, v. r.<BR> 3. To accomplish, Rām. 6, 100, 14.<BR> 4. To fulfil, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0372-a " target="_blank">Page0372-a + 44</a>] Rām. 2, 25, 41.<BR> 5. To overcome, MBh. 2, 669.<BR> 6. To conquer, Rām. 2, 53, 26.<BR> 7. To be saved, MBh. 14, 44.<BR> 8. To save, MBh. 1, 8369.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. तीर्ण,<BR> 1. Passed over, Prab. 92, 15.<BR> 2. Having passed over, Rām. 2, 55, 22; 5, 15, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple of the fut. pass. तर्तव्य, MBh. 7, 4706. तार्य, n. Toll at a ferry, Man. 8, 405.<BR> --Infin. तरीतुम्, Rām. 4, 44, 77; तरितुम्, Rām. 5, 74, 18; तर्तुम्, MBh. 1, 6142.<BR> --Caus. तारय,<BR> 1. To bring over, MBh. 1, 5853.<BR> 2. To save, MBh. 5, 1470; to release, Man. 4, 228. Desider. तितीर्ष, To desire to pass over, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 40.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति,<BR> 1. To cross, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 21.<BR> 2. To attain, Hit. iv. d. 85; Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 20.<BR> 3. To overcome, MBh. 12, 4053. Desider. To desire to overcome, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 3.<BR> --With व्यति वि-अति, To overcome, Bhag. 2, 52.<BR> --With अनु अनु, pass. तीर्य, To lay down, MBh. 7, 8721.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To attain, MBh. 7, 280.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To descend, Rām. 2, 45, 17; used especially of deities who descend from heaven to be born as men, MBh. 1, 2509.<BR> 2. To betake one's-self, MBh. 3, 10015.<BR> 3. To overcome, Kathās. 24, 194.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to descend, MBh. 1, 4327; 3, 9917; to lead down, Rām. 2, 103, 23; to lead to, MBh. 5, 4395.<BR> 2. To take off, Rām. 4, 19, 29.<BR> 3. To introduce, Rājat. 5, 32.<BR> 4. To perform, Rājat. 2, 58.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, Caus. To cause to descend, MBh. 1, 4326.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To get out, MBh. 3, 211; to get out of water, MBh. 1, 6750.<BR> 2. To descend, Lass. 5, 7.<BR> 3. To pass over, MBh. 2, 795.<BR> 4. To overcome, Hariv. 14227.<BR> 5. To abandon, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0372-b " target="_blank">Page0372-b + 43</a>] MBh. 3, 2042. उत्तीर्ण, Learned, MBh. 4, 1408.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To fetch out, Rām. 4, 52, 15.<BR> 2. To vomit, Man. 11, 160.<BR> 3. To save, to deliver, MBh. 3, 8306; Rām. 1, 43, 4 Gorr.<BR> 4. To cause to descend, Pañc. 187, 13.<BR> 5. To take off, Lass. 22, 3.<BR> 6. To bring over, Pañc. 226, 15. Desider. To wish to cross, MBh. 15, 1878.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To pass over, Rājat. 3, 71.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्,<BR> 1. To get again out (as from water), Rām. 2, 111, 37.<BR> 2. To betake one's-self, Rām. 2, 103, 28.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To get out, Yājñ. 3, 7.<BR> 2. To be saved, MBh. 13, 6676.<BR> 3. To pass over, Rājat. 3, 344.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To be saved, MBh. 3, 15561.<BR> 2. To pass over, Bhartṛ. 3, 5.<BR> 3. To pass, MBh. 13, 5155.<BR> 4. To accomplish, Lass. 4, 2.<BR> 5. To overcome, MBh. 12, 1566.<BR> 6. To expiate, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 30.<BR> 7. To settle, Yājñ. 2, 9.<BR> --Caus. To release, Man. 3, 98. Desider. To desire to pass over, Bhāg. P. 1, 1, 22.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To pass over, MBh. 4, 1546.<BR> 2. To propagate, MBh. 3, 8149.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To extend, MBh. 3, 8647.<BR> 2. To persuade, Kathās. 26, 243.<BR> 3. To deceive, Mṛcch. 82, 2.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To deceive, Śatr. 10, 121.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To cross, Ragh. 6, 77.<BR> 2. To grant, MBh. 1, 4498; to favour with (with acc.), Pañc. 127, 21; to allow, MBh. 3, 1681.<BR> 3. To give (as medicine), Suśr. 2, 337, 9.<BR> 4. To give away, Bhartṛ. 3, 86.<BR> 5. To perform, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 24; to fight (a battle), Rājat. 5, 135.<BR> 6. To produce, Kir. 5, 31.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To cross, MBh. 1, 5887.<BR> 2. To overcome, MBh. 12, 11161.<BR> 3. To attain, Rām. 5, 35, 5.<BR> 4. To be saved, Rājat. 4, 528.<BR> 5. To save, MBh. 13, 4155.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a " target="_blank">Page0373-a + 44</a>] bring over, Rām. 2, 89, 8.<BR> 2. To save, Man. 9, 139.<BR> 3. To persuade, MBh. 14, 2310.<BR> 4. To deceive, Kām. Nītis. 14, 4.<BR> --Cf. τερέω τέρετρον τορός, τόρος, τορέω, τορεύω, τιτράω, τετραίνω, τρῆμα, τρῦμα, τιτρώσκω, τρῶμα, τέλος (end), τέλλω (to rise), τηρέω (Causal), τρῡτάνη (i. e. ταρ + ῡταν + ο cf. ved. तरूतृ and तुल्), etc.: Lat. terminus; cf. तुल्, त्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तीर्ण
दुस्- + तीर्ण दुस्- + तीर्ण, adj., f. णा, 1. difficult to be crossed, MBh. 5, 7368. 2. impenetrable, Rām. 5, 76, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज्
† तेज् तेज्, i. 1, Par. To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन तेजन, i. e. तिज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Kindling, Suśr. 2, 140, 10.<BR> 2. A point, MBh. 6, 3187.<BR> 3. A bambu.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निज्वलिततेजन
अग्नि-ज्वलित- + तेजन अग्नि-ज्वलित- + तेजन, adj. the points of which are blazing with fire, Man. 7, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्
तेजस् तेजस्, i. e. तिज् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Sharpness (ved.).<BR> 2. Splendour, Bhag. 10, 30.<BR> 3. Flame, Man. 11, 246.<BR> 4. Light, MBh. 2, 1395; Śāk. d. 77 (the sun and the moon).<BR> 5. Beauty, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 3.<BR> 6. Strength, Man. 9, 321.<BR> 7. Violence, MBh. 3, 1031.<BR> 8. Dignity, Man. 9, 303; glory, Man. 7, 5.<BR> 9. A venerable person or object, MBh. 13, 5017; a renowned person, Chr. 24, 40.<BR> 10. Semen virile, Rām. 1, 37, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिततेजस्
अ-मित- + तेजस् अ-मित- + तेजस् (vb. मा), adj. of boundless splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मतेजस्
तिग्म- + तेजस् तिग्म- + तेजस्, adj. 1. very sharp, Rām. 4, 7, 21. 2. very violent, MBh. 13, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तेजस्
निस्- + तेजस् निस्- + तेजस्, adj. devoid of energy, MBh. 10, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातेजस्
महा- + तेजस् महा- + तेजस्,<BR> I. adj. 1. very bright. 2. very vigorous.<BR> II. m. 1. fire. 2. a name of the god of war. 3. a demigod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मतेजस्
ब्रह्मतेजस् ब्रह्मतेजस्, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, n. Brahmanical virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसतेजस्
मांस- + तेजस् मांस- + तेजस्, n. marrow or serum of the flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानतेजस्
समान- + तेजस् समान- + तेजस्, adj. equal in glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतेजस्
सु- + तेजस् सु- + तेजस्, adj. 1. sharp-edged. 2. very bright. 3. potent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस
ऽतेजस -तेजस् + अ, a substitute for तेजस् when latter part of a compound word, e. g. MBh. 3, 8681.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्काम
तेजस्काम तेजस्-काम, adj. One who desires manly strength, Man. 4, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्त्व
