त्वन्मय
त्वन्मय त्वन्मय, i. e. त्वद् + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of thee, Hariv. 2585.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वर्
त्वर् त्वर्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Rām. 2, 19, 16), To make haste, Rām. 3, 78, 20.<BR> --Ptcple. of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b " target="_blank">Page0381-b + 41</a>] the pf. pass.<BR> I. त्वरित,<BR> 1. Hastening. Rām. 1, 67, 24.<BR> 2. Swift, Pañc. iii. d. 102. ˚तम्, adv. Swifty, Rām. 1, 42, 23.<BR> II. तूर्ण, ˚णम्, adv. Quickly, Pañc. 167, 16.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. त्वरणीय, Where there needs haste, MBh. 7, 5842.<BR> --Caus. त्ररय, To cause to hasten, MBh. 7, 1584.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To hasten very much, MBh. 12, 5003.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To make haste, Rām. 6, 33, 4.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To hasten, MBh. 6, 3776.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To make haste, Rām. 2, 30, 43.<BR> --Caus. To cause to hasten, MBh. 7, 955.<BR> --Cf. तुर्; तॄ, θόρνυμι, θοῦρος. θρώσκω; Lat. red-am-truare, probably ἀ-θύρω, τύρβη; Lat. turba; θόρυβος; probably A.S. a-thwerian (to move, or to shake together).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरा
त्वरा त्वर् + आ, f. Haste, Rām. 2, 46, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्वरा
अ- + त्वरा अ- + त्वरा, f. absence of precipitate haste, Man. 3, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वर|सत्वरं
स-त्वर स-त्वर, adj. hastening, Chr. 28, 18; quick. ˚रम्, adv. Quickly, Pañc. 46, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरावन्त्|त्वरावत्
त्वरावन्त् त्वरा + वन्त्, adj., f. वति, Quick, MBh. 3, 16207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टि|त्वष्टिः
त्वष्टि त्वष्टि, i. e. त्वक्ष् + ति, f. The profession of a carpenter, Man. 10, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टृ
त्वष्टृ त्वष्टृ, i. e. त्वक्ष् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A carpenter (ved.).<BR> 2. The name of a deity, the artist of the gods, Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. i. 85, 9; MBh. 4, 1178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वादृश्
त्वादृश् त्वादृश्, i. e. त्वद्-दृश्, adj. Resembling thee, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वादृश
त्वादृश त्वादृश, i. e. त्वद्-दृश् + अ, adj., f. शि, Resembling thee, Rām. 4, 16, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाष्ट्र|त्वाष्ट्रः
त्वाष्ट्र त्वाष्ट्र, i. e. त्वष्टृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Referring to or made by Tvaṣṭṛ, Rām. 1, 29, 19.<BR> II. m. The name of an Asura or demon, MBh. 5, 504 = Vṛtra, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a " target="_blank">Page0382-a + 37</a>] Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 17.<BR> III. f. री, The daughter of Tvaṣṭṛ, and wife of Sūrya, MBh. 1, 2599.<BR> IV. n. The power of Tvaṣtṛ, Bhāg. P. 8, 11, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
1. त्विष् त्विष्, i. 1, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To be excited (ved.).<BR> 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
2. त्विष् त्विष्, f.<BR> 1. Light, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 23.<BR> 2. Splendour, Arj. 10, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषसंदृश्
त्वेषसंदृश् त्वेषसंदृश्, i. e. त्वेष (ved.) -सम्-दृश् adj. Of a splendid aspect, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सर्
त्सर् त्सर्, i. 1, Par. To sneak, to steal upon (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्सरु त्सरु, m. The hilt of a sword, MBh. 10, 461.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सारुक
त्सारुक त्सारुक, i. e. त्सरु + क, adj. Skilled in sword-fight, MBh. 1, 5271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थक्कियक
थक्कियक थक्कियक, m. A proper name, Rājat. 4, 493.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुड्
† थुड् थुड्, i. 6, Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुर्व्
† थुर्व् थुर्व्, i. 1, थूर्व, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
ऽद -द, latter part of compound words,<BR> I. (vb. 1. दा), Giving, e. g. अश्व-, adj. Giving a horse, Man. 4, 231. गो-<BR> 1. adj. Giving cattle, Man. 4, 231.<BR> 2. f. दा, The name of a river, Ragh. 13, 35 (अनु-गोद + म्, compounded adverb, Along the Godā). जन्मद, i. e. जन्मन्-, m. A father, Śāk. d. 177, v. r. सहस्र-, adj. Giving, or one who has given, a thousand (cows), Man. 3, 186.<BR> II. (vb. 2. दा),<BR> 1. Destroying, cf. e. g. अनल-, adj. Quenching fire. मान-, adj. Destroying arrogance (or from<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b " target="_blank">Page0382-b + 41</a>] pride-inspiring), Chr. 38, 15.<BR> III. (vb. 3. दा), Binding; cf. अङ्गद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
1. दंश् दंश् (in epic poetry also दश् दश्, MBh. 1, 1605), i. 1, दश, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 1798), To bite, MBh. 1, 843.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दष्ट, Man. 11, 199.<BR> 2. † To see (cf. दंस्, the Prākṛt form of दृश्).<BR> --Caus. To cause to be bitten, MBh. 1, 2243.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. † To bite.<BR> 2. † To see.<BR> --Frequent. Caus. दन्दशय, To cause to be bitten violently, Daśak. 11, 14.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To bite, MBh. 11, 638.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To bite through, MBh. 6, 1798.<BR> --With परि परि, To bite violently, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 27.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To bite through, MBh. 1, 3362.<BR> 2. To wedge in, Suśr. 1, 101, 5.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To bite, Bhāg. P. 6, 2, 15.<BR> 2. To press together, MBh. 1, 6274; to crush, Śāk. d. 66. संदष्ट,<BR> 1. Bound, Śāk. d. 170.<BR> 2. Tight, Ragh. 16, 65.<BR> --Cf. δάκνω, δάκος, ὀδαγμός, ὀδάζω, ὀδακτάζω, ὀδαξέω, etc., δάκρυ; Lat. lacruma, perhaps lacero; Goth. tagr; A.S. taeher; O.H.G. zanga; A.S. tang; O.H.G. zangar, mordacitas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
† 2. दंश् दंश्, i. 1 and 10. To speak or shine; cf. दंस् and the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश दंश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Biting, Gīt. 10, 11.<BR> 2. Bite, Mālav. 47, 4.<BR> 3. A tooth, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 3.<BR> 4. A gad-fly, Man. 12, 62.<BR> 5. A coat of mail, Bhāg. P. 3, 18, 9.<BR> 6. A proper name, MBh. 12, 93.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकदंश|वृकदंशः
वृक- + दंश वृक- + दंश, m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषदंश|वृषदंशः
वृष-दंश् + अ वृष-दंश् + अ, m. a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक दंश् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Biting.<BR> II. m. A gadfly.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशक|सदंशकः
स- + दंशक स- + दंशक,<BR> I. adj. having teeth.<BR> II. m. a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन दंश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Biting, MBh. 14, 754.<BR> 2. Coat of mail, 8, 2848.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित दंशित, i. e. दंश + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Mailed, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 33; armed, Bhāg. P. 9, 1, 24.<BR> 2. Protected, MBh. 7, 4202.<BR> 3. Close together, MBh. 4, 1329.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदंशित
सु- + दंशित सु- + दंशित, adj. Very close, Chr. 32, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्र
दंष्ट्र दंष्ट्र, i. e. दंश् + त्र, n. and f. रा, A tusk, a large tooth, Rām. 4, 39, 11; Pañc. 55, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोदंष्ट्र
अयस्- + दंष्ट्र अयस्- + दंष्ट्र, adj. with iron teeth, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 88, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्र|तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रः
तीक्ष्ण- + दंष्ट्र तीक्ष्ण- + दंष्ट्र, adj. having sharp teeth, Hiḍ. 2, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदंष्ट्र
पुष्प- + दंष्ट्र पुष्प- + दंष्ट्र, m. the name of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरदंष्ट्र|स्थिरदंष्ट्रः
स्थिर- + दंष्ट्र स्थिर- + दंष्ट्र, m. 1. A snake. 2. Viṣṇu in the boar avatāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन् दंष्ट्रिन्, i. e. दंष्ट्र + इन्, m. Any animal having teeth, Man. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंस्
† दंस् दंस् (cf. दंश् and the Prākṛt form of दृश्), and दस् दस्, i. 1, Par. and i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. To bite.<BR> 2. To see. दंस् दंस्, i. 1(?) and 10, Par. To speak or to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसस्
दंसस् दंसस्, n. A work, an action (ved.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदंसस्
सु- + दंसस् सु- + दंसस्, adj. performing splendid actions, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंह्
† दंह् दंह्, i. 10. To shine, to burn.<BR> --Cf. दह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दकोदर
दकोदर दकोदर, i. e. दक (for उदक), -उदर, n. A dropsical belly, Suśr. 1, 92, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष्
दक्ष् दक्ष्, i. 1, Par. ved. To act in a satisfying manner.<BR> --Ātm.<BR> 1. To be strong, Lass. 101, 15 (read दक्षते) = Rigv. vii. 16, 6, ved.<BR> 2. † To increase.<BR> 3. To act quickly.<BR> 4. To go or move.<BR> 5. † To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष दक्ष् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. षा.<BR> 1. Clever, able, Man. 7, 61; 5, 150.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b " target="_blank">Page0383-b + 44</a>] Suitable, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 44.<BR> II. m. One of the Prajāpatis, sons of Brahman, Man. 9, 128; MBh. 1, 2574.<BR> --Cf. दक्षिण; δεξιός, δεξιτερός; Lat. dexter; Goth. taihsvs. O.H.G. zeso.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षता
दक्षता दक्ष + ता, f. Cleverness, Sāh. D. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण दक्षिण, i. e. दक्ष् + इन,<BR> I. adj., f. णा.<BR> 1. Clever, Śatr. 14, 56.<BR> 2. Right (not left), Rām. 2, 52, 86; with परि-इ, To walk round a person or thing, keeping the right hand towards them, Bhāg. P. 4, 12, 25; with कृ, To show one's reverence in this manner, 1, 14, 13.<BR> 3. South, southern, Man. 3, 258.<BR> 4. Upright, honest, MBh. 4, 167.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. The right side, Rām. 2, 92, 13.<BR> 2. South, Nal. 9, 23.<BR> III. f. णा.<BR> 1. A good milch cow (ved.).<BR> 2. Legitimate possession(?), Man. 8, 349.<BR> 3. A present to Brāhmaṇas, as a sacrificial fee, Man. 8, 207.<BR> 4. Fee, MBh. 5, 3779.<BR> 5. Gift, Man. 3, 141.<BR> IV. दक्षिणेन, instr. adv.<BR> 1. Southward, Bhāg. P. 5, 17, 9.<BR> 2. To the right hand, 5, 21, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अ-दक्षिण अ-दक्षिण, adj. 1. left, Rām. 6, 29, 10. 2. foolish, 3, 24, 13. 3. devoid of presents, Pañc. ii. d. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदक्षिणा
अ-भय-दक्षिणा अ-भय-दक्षिणा, f. promise of security, Man. 4, 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वदक्षिण
पूर्व- + दक्षिण पूर्व- + दक्षिण, adj. south-eastern, Mārk. P. 58, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणदक्षिणा
प्राण-दक्षिणा प्राण-दक्षिणा, f. with दा, to give one his life, Pañc. 231, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिदक्षिण|भूरिदक्षिणः
भूरि-दक्षिण भूरि-दक्षिण, adj. one who makes large presents to Brāhmaṇas upon solemn or sacrificial occasions, Nal. 12, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदक्षिण
स-दक्षिण स-दक्षिण, adj. accompanied by presents, Rājat. 5, 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतस्
दक्षिणतस् दक्षिण + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. To the right hand, MBh. 3, 14549.<BR> 2. Southward, Man. 3, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा दक्षिणा (old instr. sing. of दक्षिण), adv. To the right hand, southward.<BR> --Cf. दक्षिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावन्त्|दक्षिणावत्
दक्षिणावन्त् दक्षिणा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in presents, MBh. 1, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय दक्षिणीय, i. e. दक्षिणा + ईय, adj. Worthy to be honored with presents, Hariv. 2780.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धृ
दग्धृ दग्धृ, i. e. दह् + तृ, m. f. ध्री, n. Consuming by fire, Mālav. d. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्
दघ् दघ्, i. 4, Par. To attain (ved.). ii. 5, Par. To hurt; to protect.<BR> --Cf. ταχύς, δέχομαι; Goth. tekan (to take); Lat. tango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्न
ऽदघ्न -दघ् + न, latter part of comp. adj. Reaching to, e. g. स्तन-, to the breast, Hariv. 8324. अश्व-, adj. Of a horse's height, Rām. 1, 13, 28 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दङ्घ्|दंघ्
† दङ्घ् दङ्घ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To quit.<BR> 2. To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दच्छद|दच्छदः
दच्छद दच्छद, i. e. दन्त्-छद, m. The lip, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्|दंड्
दण्ड् दण्ड्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par.<BR> 1. To chastise, to punish, Man. 8, 132.<BR> 2. To amerce (with two accus.), 9, 234.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass., दण्ड्य, Guilty, Man. 7, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड्य|अदंड्य
अ-दण्ड्य अ-दण्ड्य, 1. not to be punished, Man. 8, 335. 2. innocent, 8, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड दण्ड (a form of दन्त्र, i. e. दम् + त्र), m. and n.<BR> 1. A staff, Man. 8, 280.<BR> 2. Often compounded with preceding words signifying arm, thigh, trunk, e. g. बाहु-, An arm as hard as a staff, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 11.<BR> 3. A stem, MBh. 2, 2390.<BR> 4. A handle, MBh. 2, 38.<BR> 4. The staff of a banner, MBh. 2, 2079.<BR> 5. m. A long measure, a pole of four cubits, Mārk. P. 49, 39.<BR> 6. A staff as symbol of royal power, the sceptre of justice, etc., MBh. 12, 4485 sqq. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b " target="_blank">Page0384-b + 45</a>]<BR> 7. Symbol of energetic power, Man. 7, 102 (नित्यम् उद्यतदण्ड, Ever with raised staff, i. e. ever ready to use violence); military power, Man. 7, 101; force of arms, 7, 107.<BR> 8. Violence, Man. 8, 72.<BR> 9. An army, Man. 9, 294.<BR> 10. Punishment of all kind, corporal and amercement, Man. 7, 22; 8, 274; personified, Mārk. P. 50, 26.<BR> 11. The name of an attendant of the sun, MBh. 3, 198.<BR> 12. A proper name, MBh. 1, 2681.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्ड|उद्दंड|उद्दण्डः
उद्- + दण्ड उद्- + दण्ड, adj. with raised staff, Hit. ii. d. 28; stem, Ragh. 16, 46; arm, Prab. 81, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदण्ड|खरदंड|खरदण्डं
खर- + दण्ड खर- + दण्ड, n. A lotus, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदंड|त्रिदण्डः
त्रि- + दण्ड त्रि- + दण्ड, n. 1. the three staves of a religious mendicant joined together, MBh. 12, 12007. 2. three kinds of self-command (in thought, word, and deed), Man. 12, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदण्ड|धनदंड|धनदण्डः
धन- + दण्ड धन- + दण्ड, m. an amercement, Man. 8, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दंड|धिग्दण्डः
धिक्- + दण्ड धिक्- + दण्ड, m. a harsh reproof, Man. 8, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदण्ड|मनोदंड|मनोदण्डः
मनस्- + दण्ड मनस्- + दण्ड, m. control over the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादण्ड|महादण्डः
महा- + दण्ड महा- + दण्ड, m. heavy punishment, Chr. 61, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनिर्धूतदण्ड
राजनिर्धूत- + दण्ड राजनिर्धूत- + दण्ड, i. e. राजन्-निस्- (vb. धू), adj. punished by the king, Man. 8, 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दण्ड|वाग्दंड|वाग्दण्डः
वाग्दण्ड वाग्दण्ड, i. e. वाच्-, m. 1. reprimand, Man. 8, 129. 2. restraint, or control of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणदण्ड|वाणदण्डः
वाण- + दण्ड वाण- + दण्ड, m. a weaver's loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणादण्ड|वीणादंड|वीणादण्डः
वीणा- + दण्ड वीणा- + दण्ड, the neck of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डक|दंडक|दंडकः|दण्डकः
दण्डक दण्ड + क, m. and n.<BR> 1. The staff of a banner, MBh. 7, 1569.<BR> 2. also f. का, The name of a great forest in the Dekhan, Rām. 1, 1, 39; Mahāv. 65, 11.<BR> 3. m. pl. The name of the inhabitants of this locality, and of the locality itself, MBh. 13, 7223; Rām. 2, 21, 63.<BR> 4. m. A proper name, Hariv. 637.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डक
त्रि- + दण्डक त्रि- + दण्डक, n. the three staves of a religious mendicant, MBh. 12, 11870.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डन|दंडन|दंडनं
दण्डन दण्ड् + अन, n. Chastising, Kām. Nītis. 13, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाशक|दण्डपाशकः
दण्डपाशक दण्ड-पाश + क, A policeman (? perhaps -पाशिक), Pañc. 129, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवन्त्|दण्डवत्|दंडवत्
दण्डवन्त् दण्ड + वन्त्, adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a " target="_blank">Page0385-a + 39</a>] वती, One who has a great army, Kām. Nītis. 13, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिक|दंडिक|दंडिकः|दण्डिकः
दण्डिक दण्डिक, i. e. दण्ड + इक, adj. One who chastises, MBh. 6, 439.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिन्|दंडिन्
दण्डिन् दण्डिन्, i. e. दण्ड + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Bearing a staff, Man. 6, 52.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Epithet of Yama, Kām. Nītis. 2, 36.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 1, 2738.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डिन्|त्रिदंडिन्
त्रि- + दण्डिन् त्रि- + दण्डिन्, i. e. त्रि-दण्ड + इन्, m. 1. an ascetic, Yājñ. 3, 85. 2. one who has command over the three seats of action (mind, speech, and body), Man. 12, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक दत्त + क (vb. दा), adj., with पुत्र, Given to be adopted as a son, Yājñ. 2, 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ति|दत्तिः
दत्ति दत्ति, i. e. दा + ति (from the reduplicated form दद्), f. Offering, Ragh. 8, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्रिम|दत्त्रिमः
दत्रिम दत्रिम (rather दत्त्रिम, i. e. दद्, see दत्ति, + त्र + इम), adj. Received by donation, Man. 9, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्
दद् दद् (proceeded from दा, ii. 3; cf. ved. red. pf. ददद् + आते, etc.), i. 1, Ātm. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रु|दद्रुः
दद्रु दद्रु, i. e. a reduplicated form of दॄ + उ, m. and f. रू, A kind of cutaneous eruption, Suśr. 1, 31, 17; 2, 66, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्
दध् दध् (proceeded from धा, ii. 3),<BR> 1. To hold.<BR> 2. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधन्
दधन् दधन्, see दधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधि
दधि दधि, from a reduplicated form of धे, n. (the base for many of the cases is दधन्), Curdled milk, Man. 2, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच|दधीचः
दधीच दधीच, i. e. दध्यञ्च् + अ, also दधीचि दधीचि, and दध्यञ्च् दधि-अञ्च्, m. The name of a Muni [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b " target="_blank">Page0385-b + 44</a>] or sage (originally of the sun), MBh. 3, 8695; 12, 10288; Bhāg. P. 6, 11, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनु|दनुः
दनु दनु, m. and f. Proper names, Rām. 3, 75, 24; 2, 30, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुज|दनुजः
दनुज दनु-ज, m. A Dānava or demon, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्|दत्
दन्त् दन्त् (probably ptcple. of the pres. of अद्; cf. ὀδούς, ὀδόντος),<BR> 1. m., without nom. voc., acc. sing., and du., and nom. and voc. pl., A tooth, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 39.<BR> 2. Often latter part of comp. words, e. g. उभयतोदन्त्, i. e. उभयतस्-, adj. Having two rows of teeth, Man. 1, 39 (43, anomalous nom. pl.). एकतस्-, adj. Having but one row of teeth, Man. 5, 18. कर-पाद-, m. A hand, a foot, or a tooth, Yājñ. 2, 219. सु-, adj. f. दती, Having handsome teeth.<BR> --Cf. Lat. dens, and the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त|दंत|दंतः|दन्तः
दन्त दन्त् + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. A tooth, Man. 4, 69; Rām. 6, 82, 28.<BR> II. f. ती, A medicinal plant, Croton polyandrum Roxb., Suśr. 1, 139, 18.<BR> III. When latter part of comp. adj., the fem. ends in ता, Kathās. 21, 29, and ती, MBh. 9, 2649.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. tunthus; A.S. todh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशादन्त|ईशादन्तः
ईशा- + दन्त ईशा- + दन्त, or ईषा-, adj. having tusks like the pole of a carriage (i. e. an elephant), Rām. 5, 12, 31; MBh. 2, 1877.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दन्त|चतुर्दंत|चतुर्दन्तः|चतुर्द्दन्त|चतुर्द्दन्तः
चतुर्- + दन्त चतुर्- + दन्त, m. the name of an elephant, Pañc. 159, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्त|नागदंत|नागदन्तः
नाग- + दन्त नाग- + दन्त,<BR> I. m. 1. ivory, MBh. 12, 3630. 2. a pin projecting from a wall, and used to hang things upon, Pañc. 116, 19.<BR> II. f. ता, the name of an Apsaras, Rām. 2, 91, 17.<BR> III. f. ती, a plant, Tiaridium indicum Lehm., Suśr. 1, 138, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदन्त|पुष्पदंत|पुष्पदन्तः
पुष्प- + दन्त पुष्प- + दन्त,<BR> I. m. 1. the name of a Gandharva and other beings. 2. du. the sun and the moon, Śatr. 14, 225.<BR> II. f. ती, the name of a female Rākṣasa.<BR> III. n. the name of a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदन्त|राजदन्तः
राजदन्त राजद्˚, i. e. राजन्-, m. an upper and fore-tooth, applied to the two middle ones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिदन्त|हस्तिदंत|हस्तिदन्तं|हस्तिदन्तः
हस्तिदन्त हस्तिद्˚, i. e. हस्तिन्-,<BR> I. m. a pin projecting from a wall, and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a " target="_blank">Page0386-a + 39</a>] used to hang things upon.<BR> II. n. ivory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तक|दंतक|दन्तकः
ऽदन्तक -दन्त + क, a substitute for दन्त when latter part of comp. words, e. g. कृमि-, m. Caries of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 93, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तक|नागदंतक|नागदन्तकः
नाग- + दन्तक नाग- + दन्तक, m. 1. ivory, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 52, 62. 2. a pin projecting from a wall, and used to hang things upon, Hit. 27, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमय|दंतमय
दन्तमय दन्त + मय, adj., f. यी, Of ivory, Man. 5, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवेष्टक
दन्तवेष्टक दन्त-वेष्ट + क, m. A tumour in the gum, Suśr. 1, 303, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तादन्ति|दंतादंति
दन्तादन्ति दन्तादन्ति, i. e. दन्त-दन्त + इ, adv. Biting one another, MBh. 8, 2377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिदन्तमय
दन्तिदन्तमय दन्तिदन्तमय, i. e. दन्तिन्-दन्त + मय, adj., f. यी, Of ivory, MBh. 8, 1021.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिन्|दंतिन्
दन्तिन् दन्तिन्, i. e. दन्त + इन्, m. An elephant, Hit. i. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिल
दन्तिल दन्तिल, m. A proper name, Pañc. 26, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुर|दंतुर|दन्तुरः
दन्तुर दन्तुर, i. e. दन्त + उर, adj., f. रा, Having large or projecting teeth, Kathās. 20, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुरित|दंतुरित
दन्तुरित दन्तुरित i. e. दन्तुर + इत, adj. Having projecting teeth, Gīt. 1, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दशूक|दंदशूक|दन्दशूकः
दन्दशूक दन्दश् + ऊक (Frequent. of दंश्), + ऊक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Mordacious, MBh. 1, 1199.<BR> 2. Mischievous, MBh. 5, 1254.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A snake, Yājñ. 3, 197.<BR> 2. A kind of snake, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 27.<BR> 3. The name of a hell, 5, 26, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्व्
† दन्व् दन्व्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्
दभ् दभ्, and दम्भ् दम्भ्, i. 1, दभ, ii. 5, दभ्नु, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt (ved.).<BR> 2. To deceive.<BR> --Comp. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b " target="_blank">Page0386-b + 43</a>] ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-दाभ्य, Not to be checked, Bhāg. P. 4, 23, 4.<BR> --† i. 10, दाभय, and दम्भय, Par. To send, to impel.<BR> --† दम्भय, Ātm. To gather.<BR> --Cf. probably θάμβος, ἔταϕον, τέθηπα; O.H.G. tepjan or depjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभीति
दभीति दभीति, m. A proper name, Chr. 298, 23 = Rigv. i. 112, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र दभ् + र, adj. Little, insignificant, Bhāg. P. 6, 7, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदभ्र|अदभ्रः
अ- + दभ्र अ- + दभ्र, adj. Great, Bhāg. P. 8, 3, 19. Excellent, 1, 15, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम् दम्, i. 4, दाम्य, Par.<BR> 1. To be tamed.<BR> 2. To tame, MBh. 7, 2379.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दान्त, Tamed, MBh. 3, 15704. m.<BR> 1. A steer, a young bullock, Rājat. 5, 432.<BR> 2. One who has subdued his passions, calm, Man. 4, 35.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. दम्य,<BR> 1. To be tamed for labour, Man. 8, 146.<BR> 2. m. A steer, a young bullock, MBh. 12, 6590.<BR> --Caus. दमय,<BR> 1. To subdue, MBh. 1, 2995.<BR> 2. To break, Rājat. 4, 265.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To subdue, MBh. 12, 6596.<BR> --Cf. δάμνημι, δαμνάω, δαμάω (= ved. दमायामि; Lat. domare), δμώς; Lat. damnare, damnum; Goth. ga-timan; O.H.G. zeman, zam; A.S. tam, tamian; Lat. densus; δασύς, etc., cf. दम्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्दान्तः|दुर्द्दान्त
दुस्- + दान्त दुस्- + दान्त, adj. unruly, MBh. 13, 1534.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम दम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Self-command, Man. 4, 246.<BR> 2. A fine, Man. 9, 230.<BR> 3. Punishment, chastisement, Man. 9, 284; Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 20.<BR> 4. The name of a Ṛṣi, MBh. 13, 1762.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. दम्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दम
दुस्- + दम दुस्- + दम, 1. adj. difficult to be tamed, MBh. 12, 3310. 2. m. a proper name, Hariv. 1951.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदम
सु- + दम सु- + दम, adj. easy to be subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमक|दमकः
दमक दम् + अक, adj. Taming, a tamer, Man. 3, 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन दम् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Subduing, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a " target="_blank">Page0387-a + 40</a>] Bhartṛ. 3, 47.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Subduing, Bhartṛ. 2, 52.<BR> 2. Chastising, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 14.<BR> III. m. A proper name, Nal. 1, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदमन|सर्व्वदमन|सर्व्वदमनः
सर्व- + दमन सर्व- + दमन,<BR> I. adj. all-subduing.<BR> II. m. Bharata, the son of Śakuntalā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनक|दमनकः
दमनक दमन + क, m. A proper name, Pañc. 9, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयन्ती|दमयंती
दमयन्ती दमयन्ती, fem. of the pres. ptcple. of the Causal of दम्, A proper name, Nal. 1, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयितृ
दमयितृ दमयितृ, i. e. दम्, Caus., + तृ, m. A chastiser, MBh. 13, 7041.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिन्
दमिन् दमिन्, i. e. दम + इन्, adj. One who has subdued his passions, MBh. 3, 5016.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदमिनी
काम-दमिन् + ई काम-दमिन् + ई, f. a proper name, Pañc. 185, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्पति|दंपति
दम्पति दम्पति, probably दंस् (= δῶ and δες) -पति (= ποτης), m. The master of the house; dual ती, The master and the mistress; husband and wife, Man. 3, 116; a couple, Pañc. 225, 22.<BR> --Cf. δεσπότης, δόμος (= ved. दम), δέμω; Lat. domus; Goth. timrjan; A.S. timber, timbrian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ्|दंभ्
दम्भ् दम्भ्, see दभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ दम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Deceit, Pañc. i. d. 222.<BR> 2. Feigning, Rājat. 6, 195.<BR> 3. Arrogance, Mārk. P. 34, 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्भ|अदंभ|अदम्भः
अ- + दम्भ अ- + दम्भ, 1. m. sincerity, Rām. 2, 86, 2. 2. adj. sincere, Hariv. 4137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतदम्भ|वीतदम्भः
वीत- + दम्भ वीत- + दम्भ, i. e. वि-इत-, adj. humble, not proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भक|दंभक
दम्भक दम्भ् + अक, adj. Deluding, Man. 4, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भन|दंभन|दंभनं
दम्भन दम्भ् + अन, n. Deceit, Man. 4, 198.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भिन्|दंभिन्
दम्भिन् दम्भिन्, i. e. दम्भ + इन्, m. A deceiver, Pañc. iv. d. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय्
दय् दय्, i. 1, Ātm. (also Par. Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 42).<BR> 1. To allot (ved.). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b " target="_blank">Page0387-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. To have compassion, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 2; with the gen., 195, 10.<BR> 3. To destroy (ved.).<BR> 4. † To move.<BR> 5. † To protect.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दयित, Dear, Rām. 1, 1, 26. m. A lover, a husband, Śāk. 58, 7, C. f. ता, A mistress, a woman, Śiś. 9, 70.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δαίομαι, δαίνυμι, δαῖς, 2. दा and दे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रदयिता
समुद्र- + दयिता समुद्र- + दयिता, f. ता, a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदयित
सु- + दयित सु- + दयित, adj. very dear, Chr. 38, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दया
दया दय् + आ, f. Compassion, Bhag. 16, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदयम्
अ-दय + म् अ-दय + म्, adv. passionately, Vikr. d. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दय|निर्द्दयः
निर्दय निर्दय, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. या. 1. unmerciful, cruel, Pañc. 176, 10. 2. passionate, Rājat. 5, 281. 3. not treated with affection, Man. 9, 239. ˚यम्, adv. passionately, Hit. i. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतदया
भूत- + दया भूत- + दया, f. compassion for living creatures, MBh. 14, 2841.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदय
स- + दय स- + दय, adj. 1. compassionate. 2. benevolent. ˚यम्-, adv. softly, Śāk. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
दयालु दया + लु, adj. Compassionate, Pañc. iii. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालुत्व
दयालुत्व दयालु + त्व, n. Compassion, Kām. Nītis. 3, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयावन्त्|दयावत्
दयावन्त् दया + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Compassionate, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर|दरं|दरः
दर दर, i. e.<BR> A. दॄ + अ,<BR> I. m., f. री, and n. A cave, Rām. 2, 96, 4; MBh. 1, 4651.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Cavity, Bhartṛ. 3, 24.<BR> 2. A shell, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 1.<BR> B. दृ + अ, m. and n. Fear, MBh. 5, 4622.<BR> C. adj. and indecl., A little, Sāh. D. 41, 18; Gīt. 1, 35.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर
स- + दर स- + दर, adj. fearful, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद्
दरद् दरद् and दरद दरद, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, Rājat. 5, 152; Man. 10, 44.<BR> 2. दरद, The king of the Daradas, Hariv. 4969.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्र|दरिद्रः
दरिद्र दरिद्र, (derived from an old frequentat. of द्रा), adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Strolling (ved.).<BR> 2. Poor, Man. 9, 230.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रता
दरिद्रता दरिद्र + ता, f. and दरिद्रत्व दरिद्र + त्व, n. Poverty, Bhartṛ. 2, 87; Rājat. 2, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रा
दरिद्रा दरिद्रा, see द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरी
दरी दरी, see दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरीवन्त्|दरीवत्
दरीवन्त् दरी + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in caves, Rām. 4, 49, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दर|दर्दरः|दर्द्दरः
दर्दर दर्दर् + अ (anomal. frequent. of दॄ), m. The name of a mountain, Rām. 2, 91, 24, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुर|दर्दुरः|दर्द्दुर|दर्द्दुरं|दर्द्दुरः
दर्दुर दर्दुर् + अ (anomal. frequent. of दॄ), m.<BR> 1. A frog, Man. 12, 64.<BR> 2. A flute, Bhāg. P. 1, 10, 15.<BR> 3. The name of a mountain, Rām. 5, 34, 7.<BR> 4. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपदर्दुर
कूप- + दर्दुर कूप- + दर्दुर, m. A frog living in a well, Pañc. i. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्प|दर्पः
दर्प दर्प, i. e. दृप् + अ, m. Arrogance, Rām. 1, 56, 3; pride, Hit. 28, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदर्प
अति- + दर्प अति- + दर्प, 1. m. excessive arrogance, Cāṇ. 50. 2. the name of a snake, Pañc. 170, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नदर्प
भग्न- + दर्प भग्न- + दर्प (vb. भञ्ज्), adj. humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर्प
स- + दर्प स- + दर्प, adj. lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिद्धदर्प
सम्-इद्ध- + दर्प सम्-इद्ध- + दर्प (vb. इन्ध्), adj. inflamed with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पण|दर्पणं|दर्पणः
दर्पण दर्पण, i. e. दृप् + अन, m. A mirror, Megh. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पिन्
दर्पिन् दर्पिन्, i. e. दर्प + इन्, adj. Insolent, Hariv. 15606.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भ|दर्भः
दर्भ दर्भ, i. e. दृभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Kuśa, or sacrificial grass, Man. 3, 216.<BR> 2. Another kind of grass, Suśr. 1, 137, 19.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. zurft (zurba); A.S. turf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भमय
दर्भमय दर्भ + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of Darbha grass, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वि|दर्विः|दर्व्विः
दर्वि and दर्वी दर्वी̆, i. e. दॄ + वी̆,<BR> 1. A spoon, MBh. 2, 1945.<BR> 2. The expanded hood of a snake (see the next). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b " target="_blank">Page0388-b + 44</a>]<BR> 3. The name of a country, MBh. 6, 362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वीकर|दर्वीकरः|दर्व्वीकरः
दर्वीकर दर्वी-कर, n. A kind of snake, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श दर्श, i. e. दृश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. The new moon, Ragh. 18, 34.<BR> 2. The day of the conjunction, Man. 3, 282.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्श|आत्मदर्शः
आत्मदर्श आत्मदर्श, i. e. आत्मन्-, m. a mirror, Ragh. 7, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर्श|दुर्द्दर्श
दुस्- + दर्श दुस्- + दर्श, adj., f. शा, 1. difficult to be beheld, Bhag. 11, 52. 2. disgusting, MBh. 1, 3471.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्दर्श|सुदुर्द्दर्श
सु-दुस्- + दर्श सु-दुस्- + दर्श, adj. very difficult to be beheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शक|दर्शकः
दर्शक दर्शक, i. e.<BR> A. दृश् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Looking, seeing, a spectator, MBh. 13, 5907.<BR> 2. Searching, MBh. 1, 5559.<BR> B. दृश्, Causal, + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Showing, causing to be seen, Mṛcch. 65, 4; Man. 8, 284.<BR> 2. Explaining, Hit. Pr. d. 9, v. r.<BR> C. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 6, 361.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदर्शक
पार- + दर्शक पार- + दर्शक, adj. showing the opposite bank or shore, Bhāg. P. 1, 13, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शत|दर्शतः
दर्शत दर्शत, ved. ptcple. of the fut. pass. of दृश्, Visible, Chr. 289, 4 = Rigv. i. 50, 4; Chr. 290, 9 = 1, 64, 9.<BR> --Cf. δυς-δέρκετος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शन|दर्शनं
दर्शन दर्शन, i. e. दृश् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Looking on, Ragh. 11, 93, v. r.<BR> 2. Knowing, MBh. 13, 3254.<BR> 3. Teaching, MBh. 1, 583.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Seeing, Suśr. 2, 158, 10. आदित्य-, Exposure to the sun, Mṛcch. 47, 5.<BR> 2. Sight, MBh. 13, 961; Śāk. 18, 18; a vision, Rām. 5, 27, 8; a dream, Hariv. 1285.<BR> 3. Adoration, Kathās. 3, 8.<BR> 4. Appearance, Man. 2, 101; with the vbs. इ and या, To become visible, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 34; with दा, To show one's self, Gīt. 3, 9.<BR> 5. Review, Yājñ. 1, 328; inspection, Man. 8, 9.<BR> 6. Knowledge, Man. 6, 74.<BR> 7. Opinion, Kām. Nītis. 2, 6.<BR> 8. Precept, MBh. 14, 2700.<BR> 9. Doctrine, Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 8.<BR> 10. A philosophical system, Lass. 29, 7.<BR> 11. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a " target="_blank">Page0389-a + 45</a>] Intention, Rām. 1, 58, 18.<BR> 12. An eye, Śāk. d. 81.<BR> 13. A mirror, Megh. 59, v. r.<BR> 14. Showing, Lass. 87, 3.<BR> 15. Producing, Yājñ. 2, 170.<BR> 16. abl. दर्शनात्, From, Ragh. 12, 60.<BR> III. f. नी, Epithet of Durgā, Hariv. 10238.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शन|अदर्शनं
अ- + दर्शन अ- + दर्शन,<BR> I. n. 1. not seeing, Rām. 5, 53, 6. 2. neglect, Man. 10, 43. 3. disappearance, Rām. 3, 50, 11; with गम्, to disappear, Pañc. 137, 21; with नी, to cause to disappear, Rām. 5, 22, 2.<BR> II. adj. invisible, Arj. 8, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छिद्रदर्शन
अच्छिद्र- + दर्शन अच्छिद्र- + दर्शन, i. e. अ-छिद्र-, adj., f. ना, faultless, MBh. 6, 384.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतदर्शन
अद्भुत- + दर्शन अद्भुत- + दर्शन, adj. wonderfully handsome, Nal. 12, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिदर्शन
अन्-अति- + दर्शन अन्-अति- + दर्शन. n. not seeing too often, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्शन
आत्मदर्शन आत्मदर्शन, i. e. आत्मन्-, n. seeing one's self, Yājñ. 3, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यदर्शन
तुल्य- + दर्शन तुल्य- + दर्शन, adj. indifferent, Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारदर्शन
दार- + दर्शन दार- + दर्शन, n. interview with a woman, Cāṇ. 22, in Berl. Monatsb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर्शन
दुस्- + दर्शन दुस्- + दर्शन, adj. 1. difficult to be seen, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 34. 2. disgusting, Suśr. 1, 260, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शन|दूरदर्शनः
दूर- + दर्शन दूर- + दर्शन, adj. hardly to be seen, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदर्शन
पार- + दर्शन पार- + दर्शन, adj. seeing the opposite bank or shore, Bhāg. P. 9, 4, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शन|पुण्यदर्शनः
पुण्य- + दर्शन पुण्य- + दर्शन, adj. f. ना, of beautiful aspect, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शन|भालदर्शनं|भालदर्शनः
भाल- + दर्शन भाल- + दर्शन, n. red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदर्शन|सुदर्शनं|सुदर्शनः
सु- + दर्शन सु- + दर्शन,<BR> I. adj. handsome.<BR> II. m. 1. The discus of Viṣṇu. 2. a vulture. 3. Mount Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितुकाम
दर्शयितुकाम दर्शयितुकाम, i. e. दर्शयितुम्, inf. of the Causal of द्रिश्, -काम, adj. Wishing to show, Vikr. 29, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितृ
दर्शयितृ दर्शयितृ, i. e. द्रिश्, Caus., + तृ, m. One who shows, MBh. 6, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शिन्
दर्शिन् दर्शिन्, i. e. दृश् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Looking; सम-, Looking indifferently on every object, Bhag. 5, 18.<BR> 2. Knowing, Man. 3, 212; दिव्य-, Knowing celestial things, MBh. 15, 566.<BR> 3. Having seen, Kathās. 25, 297.<BR> 4. Showing, Rām. 2, 75, 12.<BR> 5. Teaching, MBh. 1, 522.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रदर्शिन्
छिद्र- + दर्शिन् छिद्र- + दर्शिन्, adj. perceiving weak points, Hariv. 1265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदर्शिन्
दीर्घ- + दर्शिन् दीर्घ- + दर्शिन्, adj. far-seeing, provident, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b " target="_blank">Page0389-b + 42</a>] Pañc. 194, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शिन्
दूर- + दर्शिन् दूर- + दर्शिन्, far-seeing, wise, Rām. 5, 87, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदर्शिन्
देव- + दर्शिन् देव- + दर्शिन्, adj. frequenting the gods, Rām. 5, 30, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारदर्शिन्
द्वार- + दर्शिन् द्वार- + दर्शिन्, m. a porter, Rām. 2, 41, 25 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदर्शिन्
विधि- + दर्शिन् विधि- + दर्शिन्, m. a priest whose business at a sacrifice is to see that everything is done according to the rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदर्शिन्
सम- + दर्शिन् सम- + दर्शिन्, adj. impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदर्शिन्
सूक्ष्म- + दर्शिन् सूक्ष्म- + दर्शिन्, adj. acute. intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शिवंस्
दर्शिवंस् दर्शिवंस् (an anomalous ptcple. pf. act. of दृश्), only nom. sing. वान्,<BR> 1. Having seen, MBh. 8, 1756.<BR> 2. Knowing, 1, 6157.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदर्शिवंस्
दीर्घ- + दर्शिवंस् दीर्घ- + दर्शिवंस्, provident, MBh. 5, 4380.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्
दल् दल् (akin to दॄ), i. 1, Par. To burst, Lass. 66, 15.<BR> --Caus. दा̆लय, To cause to burst, Suśr. 1, 262, 9, दलित,<BR> 1. Burst, MBh. 8, 4633.<BR> 2. Split, wounded, Prab. 87, 13.<BR> 3. Destroyed, Prab. 116, 6.<BR> 4. Visible, Prab. 40, 10.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To burst, Suśr. 2, 166, 6.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus. To divide, MBh. 12, 7349.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To burst, Naiṣ. 4, 88.<BR> 2. To rend, Rām. 2, 87, 10 Gorr. विदलित, Crushed, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संदलित, Pierced, Lass. 73, 12.<BR> --Cf. दॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल दल् + अ,<BR> I. n. A part, Suśr. 2, 357, 4 (अण्ड-, an egg-shell; वेणु-, a small shoot of a cane, Man. 8, 299).<BR> 2. A half, Suśr. 1, 25, 2.<BR> 3. A leaf, Rām. 2, 46, 14.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 3, 13178.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदल
द्वि- + दल द्वि- + दल, adj. broken, Hariv. 15522.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलन|दलनं
दलन दल् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Tearing, Bhāg. P. 7, 10, 59.<BR> II. n. Breaking, crushing, Gīt. 5, 2; Rājat. 3, 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलशस्
दलशस् दल + शस्, adv. In pieces, Kathās. 19, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव दव, i. e. दु + अ, m. A forest conflagration, Bhāg. P. 8, 6, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दविष्ठ|दविष्ठः
दविष्ठ दविष्ठ, superl. दवीयंस् दवीयंस्, comparat. of दूर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दश
दश दश,<BR> 1. instead of दशन्, Ten, MBh. 3, 15649.<BR> 2. = दशम when latter part of a comp. numeral; cf. अष्टादश, द्वादश, त्रिदश.<BR> नव-दश, i. e. नवन्-, f. शी, Nineteenth.<BR> पञ्चदश, i. e. पञ्चन्-, f. शी,<BR> 1. Fifteenth.<BR> 2. f. शी, The fifteenth day of a half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशक
दशक दशक, i. e. दशन् + क, adj. Containing ten, Man. 6, 92.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतदशक
शत- + दशक शत- + दशक, ten per cent., Yājñ. 2, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशत्
दशत् दशत्, f. (cf. दशन्), An aggregate of ten, a decade, Man. 8, 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशति|दशतिः
दशति दशति (cf. दशन्), f. A hundred, MBh. 1, 1081.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशधा
दशधा दशधा, i. e. दशन् + धा, adv. In ten parts, Man. 9, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन्
दशन् दशन्, cardinal number,<BR> 1. Ten, MBh. 3, 10677.<BR> 2. Ten bad qualities, Hariv. 744.<BR> --Cf. δέκα; Goth. taihun and -tigu in tvaim-tigum; A.S. tên, -tig; Lat. decem; cf. दश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन|दशनं|दशनः
दशन दशन, i. e. दंश् + अन, n. A tooth, Pañc. 52, 8; when latter part of a comp. adj., the fem. ends in ना, Man. 3, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रदशन|वज्रदशनः
वज्र- + दशन वज्र- + दशन, m. a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम दशम, i. e. दशन् + म,<BR> I. ordinal number, f. मी, Tenth, Chr. 47, 38.<BR> II. f. मी,<BR> 1. The tenth day of the half month, Man. 3, 276.<BR> 2. The tenth decade of human life, Man. 2, 137.<BR> III. n. A tenth part, Man. 8, 33.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. decimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदशम
त्रयो- + दशम त्रयो- + दशम, Thirteenth, Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशम
द्वा- + दशम द्वा- + दशम, twelfth, MBh. 1, 6597.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमास्य
दशमास्य दशमास्य, i. e. दशन्-मास + य, adj. Of ten months, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीस्थ|दशमीस्थः
दशमीस्थ दशमी-स्थ (cf. दशम), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b " target="_blank">Page0390-b + 39</a>] adj. Above ninety years old, Man. 2, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशलक्षणक|दशलक्षणकः
दशलक्षणक दशलक्षणक, i. e. दशन्-लक्षण + क, adj. Ten-fold, Man. 6, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशा
दशा दशा, i. e. दंश् + अ, f.<BR> 1. The skirt, or the ends of a garment, Man. 3, 44; Mṛcch. 26, 17.<BR> 2. The wick of a lamp, Bhartṛ. 3, 1.<BR> 3. Condition, state of life, Rām. 3, 75, 59.<BR> 4. State, Kathās. 7, 113.<BR> 5. Period, age, Hit. 10, 19; Hariv. 4394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ण|दशार्णः
दशार्ण दशार्ण, m.<BR> 1. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 1, 4449.<BR> 2. Their king, Chr. 60, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्णक
दशार्णक दशार्णक, read दाश्˚, Chr. 52, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ह|दशार्हः
दशार्ह दशार्ह,<BR> 1. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 3, 769.<BR> 2. m. A proper name, Hariv. 1991.<BR> 3. A name of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 13, 7003.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशिन्
दशिन् दशिन्, i. e. दशन् + इन्, m. A lord of ten towns, Man. 7, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेरक|दशेरकः
दशेरक दशेरक, i. e. दंश् + एर + क, m.<BR> 1. A young camel, MBh. 8, 1852.<BR> 2. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 7, 397.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेश|दशेशः
दशेश दशेश, i. e. दशन्-ईश, m. A lord of ten towns, Man. 7, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्
दस् दस्, i. 4, Par. To become exhausted (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्यु|दस्युः
दस्यु दस्यु, m.<BR> 1. A ruffian, a thief, Man. 7, 143.<BR> 2. The name of one of the mixed classes, Man. 5, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्युसात्
दस्युसात् दस्यु + सात्, adv. In the hand of ruffians, MBh. 12, 2554.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्र|दस्रं|दस्रः
दस्र दस्र, adj.<BR> 1. Helping(?), Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR> 2. The name of one of the Aśvins, MBh. 1, 723.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्
दह् दह् (originally दघ्), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 5, 33, 38; also i. 4, MBh. 4, 799),<BR> 1. To consume by fire, MBh. 8, 116.<BR> 2. To destroy, Man. 7, 9.<BR> 3. To give pain, Pañc. pr. d. 4; Pass. To suffer pain, MBh. 3, 2483.<BR> 4. Pass. To burn, MBh. 1, 8330. Passive, with the terminations of the Par., MBh. 1, 2061; 8210.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दग्ध,<BR> 1. Consumed by fire, Man. 8, 189.<BR> 2. Pained, Ṛt. 1, 10.<BR> 3. Cunning, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 15.<BR> 4. n. Cauterising, Suśr. 1, 33, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. दाहय,<BR> 1. To cause to be burned, Man. 5, 167.<BR> 2. To cause to be roasted, Hariv. 15523. Desider. दिधक्ष (also Ātm., Rām. 2, 12, 106), To wish to consume by fire, to be about to consume, MBh. 1, 1244; Rām. 2, 97, 17 Frequent.<BR> 1. दन्दह्, दन्दह्य, To destroy completely, Hariv. 8726; Śiś. 2, 11.<BR> 2. दन्दह्य, To be consumed completely by fire, Bhāg. P. 2, 2, 26; by grief, Pañc. 58, 2.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To burn excessively, Suśr. 2, 47, 19.<BR> 2. To press hard, MBh. 6, 5238.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To consume completely by fire, Rām. 2, 63, 41.<BR> --With अप अप, To burn away, MBh. 12, 7705.<BR> --With अव अव, To burn away, Suśr. 2, 35, 10.<BR> --With उप उप, To set on fire, MBh. 3, 546.<BR> --With नि नि, To consume by fire, MBh. 1, 4454.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To consume by fire, Man. 11, 246.<BR> 2. To destroy, Rām. 1, 54, 22.<BR> --Caus. To order to set on fire, Rājat. 6, 171.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-b " target="_blank">Page0391-b + 42</a>]<BR> 1. To consume by fire, MBh. 1, 5307.<BR> 2. To destroy completely, MBh. 5, 5769.<BR> --With परि परि, To consume by fire, Suśr. 1, 155, 22. Pass. To burn, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 29.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, i. 4, To be consumed by fire, MBh. 3, 10067.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To consume by fire, MBh. 1, 2120.<BR> 2. To destroy, Rām. 2, 24, 8. Pass. To be consumed by fire, MBh. 2, 2689.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To consume by fire, MBh. 1, 5796.<BR> 2. To destroy, 9, 3526.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, i. 4, To be consumed by fire, MBh. 8, 2750.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To cauterise, Suśr. 1, 100, 21.<BR> 2. To consume by fire, MBh. 8, 464. Pass.<BR> 1. To be consumed by fire, Rām. 4, 60, 20.<BR> 2. To burn (as a wound), Suśr. 1, 103, 19.<BR> 3. To be consumed by grief, MBh. 12, 52.<BR> 4. To puff one's self up, Rām. 2, 6, 12 Gorr. विदग्ध,<BR> 1. Inflamed, Suśr. 2, 5, 21.<BR> 2. Digested, Suśr. 2, 110, 14; 118, 15.<BR> 3. Corrupt, Suśr. 2, 369, 18.<BR> 4. Clever, MBh. 4, 745.<BR> 5. Well-bred, Vikr. 3, 12.<BR> 6. Intriguing, Bhartṛ. 1, 97.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. uncultivated, foolish, Pañc. i. d. 180.<BR> दुस्-, adj. 1. puffed up, Bhartṛ. 2, 3. 2. stupid, Prab. 27, 8.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To destroy, Rām. 1, 77, 12 Gorr. Pass.<BR> 1. To burn, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 8.<BR> 2. To grieve, Ragh. 14, 56 Calc.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be consumed by fire, MBh. 1, 4954.<BR> --Cf. probably τήγανον; Lat. lignum; O.H.G. tâht or dâht; perhaps Goth. dags; A.S. daeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदग्ध
अग्नि- + दग्ध अग्नि- + दग्ध, 1. adj. burned with fire. 2. m. a class of Pitṛs or Manes, Man. 3, 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्निदग्ध
अन्-अग्नि- + दग्ध अन्-अग्नि- + दग्ध, m. another class of Pitṛs, Man. 3, 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहन|दहनं|दहनः
दहन दह् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Consuming by fire, Hariv. 2522.<BR> 2. Destroying, Bhartṛ. 1, 70.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Fire, Bhartṛ. 2, 29.<BR> 2. The deity of fire, MBh. 1, 8360.<BR> 3. One of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0392-a " target="_blank">Page0392-a + 46</a>] Rudras, MBh. 1, 2567.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Consuming by fire, Ragh. 8, 20.<BR> 2. Burning, Bhāṣāp. 156.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवदहन|दवदहनः
दव- + दहन दव- + दहन, n. The fire of a forest conflagration, Bhāg. P. 5, 8, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहर|दहरं|दहरः
दहर दहर, and दह्र दह्र (forms of दभ्र),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Small, subtile.<BR> II. The cavity of the heart, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
1. दा दा, ii. 3, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To give, Man. 3, 31.<BR> 2. To grant, to bestow, Hariv. 5709; Hit. pr. d. 2.<BR> 3. To marry, MBh. 1, 6526.<BR> 4. To sell, with the instr. of the price, Rām. 1, 53, 8.<BR> 5. To deliver, Man. 8, 234.<BR> 6. To return, Man. 8, 222.<BR> 7. To pay, Man. 8, 154.<BR> 8. With तलम्, or तलान्, To shake hands, Hariv. 15741; MBh. 3, 14819.<BR> 9. To offer, Man. 9, 136.<BR> 10. To communicate, to teach, Man. 2, 114.<BR> 11. With आत्मानम्, To sacrifice one's self, Kathās. 22, 227.<BR> 12. With many words it has the signification of Doing, performing, Caurap. 35; with अनुयात्राम्, To accompany, Kathās. 18, 197; with तालम्, To beat the time, MBh. 1, 5939.<BR> 13. To cause, Rām. 2, 53, 21.<BR> 14. To allow, MBh. 1, 1528 (with infin.).<BR> 15. To put, Mṛcch. 139, 8; cf. अर्धचन्द्र.<BR> 16. With शारम्, To draw, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 24.<BR> 17. With अर्गलम्, To bolt, Kathās. 4, 60.<BR> 18. To turn, Kathās. 16, 40; MBh. 12, 2526.<BR> 19. To add, Pañc. ii. d. 148.<BR> --Anomalous 1. sing. pr. par. दद्मि, MBh. 12, 10466; 3. sing. ददति, 3, 13422; 3. pl. ददन्ति, 13, 3148; 3. sing. impf. अददत्, 2, 1880; 2. sing. imptive. दद, 9, 2442; Ātm. ददस्व, 1, 3482; cf. दद्.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दत्त, m.<BR> 1. A given son, Man. 9, 159.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> 3. n. Giving Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-देय, What [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0392-b " target="_blank">Page0392-b + 44</a>] ought not to be given, Chr. 57, 26. Comp. absol. अ-दत्त्वा, Without being given, Rājat. 5, 195.<BR> --Caus. दापय,<BR> 1. To cause to be given, Rām. 2, 32, 19.<BR> 2. To oblige to pay, Man. 7, 127.<BR> 3. To oblige to return, Yājñ. 2, 269.<BR> 4. To procure, Pañc. 26, 1.<BR> 5. To cause to be performed, Kathās. 5, 112.<BR> 6. To cause to utter, Hariv. 15782.<BR> 7. To cause to be put on, MBh. 1, 5724. Desider. दित्स, To wish to give, MBh. 1, 5119.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To leave(?), MBh. 7, 9499.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To give, MBh. 3, 13309.<BR> --With आ आ, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 2, 2637),<BR> 1. To take, Man. 4, 223.<BR> 2. To receive, Man. 2, 238; with गर्भम्, To become pregnant, Draup. 5, 9 (and To rob).<BR> 3. To take away, Man. 7, 124.<BR> 4. To impair, Man. 4, 218.<BR> 5. To carry with one's self, Man. 9, 92.<BR> 6. To seize, MBh. 4, 1113.<BR> 7. To perceive, MBh. 14, 675.<BR> 8. To agree, Rām. 2, 90, 16.<BR> 9. To undergo, Bhāg. P. 2, 3, 15.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. आत्त,<BR> 1. Seized, MBh. 6, 5592.<BR> 2. Robbed, Rām. 2, 61, 18.<BR> 3. Undertaken, Kathās. 21, 142.<BR> II. आ-दत्त, Taken away, Hariv. 11811. आदेय,<BR> 1. What ought to be received, Man. 8, 171.<BR> 2. To be approved, Rājat. 5, 274. अन्-आदेय, What ought not to be taken, ib.<BR> --Absol. आदाय, very often With, Rām. 3, 42, 30. Desider. To be about to seize, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 11.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ, Ātm. (Par., Hariv. 14602),<BR> 1. To take away, MBh. 1, 3558.<BR> 2. To put on, Hariv. 13086.<BR> 3. To begin, MBh. 5, 3384.<BR> --With उदा उद्-आ, उदात्त, Prominent, Rām. 2, 100, 10; Prab. 97, 1. m. The acute accent. n. An ornament (in rhetoric), Sāh. D. 752.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, m. The grave accent.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, Ātm.<BR> 1. To receive, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0393-a " target="_blank">Page0393-a + 41</a>] MBh. 3, 8537.<BR> 2. To acquire, Mārk. P. 21, 93.<BR> 3. To take away, MBh. 3, 8599.<BR> 4. To take, MBh. 3, 1553.<BR> 5. To gather, Rām. 3, 13, 18.<BR> 6. To assume, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 10.<BR> 7. To consider, MBh. 12, 427.<BR> 8. To begin, Rām. 5, 81, 32.<BR> --Absol. उपादाय,<BR> 1. With, MBh. 3, 3028.<BR> 2. Inclusively, Rām. 2, 92, 6.<BR> 3. By means of, MBh. 4, 1775. Desider. To wish to acquire, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 7 (Par.).<BR> --With अभ्युपा अभि-उप-आ, To gather, MBh. 12, 167.<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ,<BR> 1. To take, Rām. 2, 25, 25.<BR> 2. To acquire, Mārk. P. 21, 95.<BR> 3. To rob, MBh. 3, 11676.<BR> 4. To collect, Rām. 2, 32, 35 Gorr.<BR> 4. To put on, MBh. 1, 6974.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, Ātm.<BR> 1. To take off, Suśr. 2, 36, 2.<BR> 2. To seize, MBh. 5, 1940.<BR> 3. To learn, MBh. 12, 3256.<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ, To deliver, MBh. 1, 4899.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, Ātm.<BR> 1. To get back, MBh. 12, 7415.<BR> 2. To take back, to rescind, MBh. 1, 785.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, Par.<BR> 1. To open wide, Hariv. 16003.<BR> 2. To gape, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 14.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. व्यात्त, and anomalous व्यादित, Wide-opened, MBh. 3, 2024; 2, 946.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> I. Par.<BR> 1. To give, Hariv. 16367.<BR> 2. To return, Bhāg. P. 9, 17, 15.<BR> II. Ātm. (also Par., Bhāg. P. 8, 10, 43),<BR> 1. To take up, Man. 6, 4.<BR> 2. To take away, Man. 3, 219.<BR> 3. To seize, Rām. 3, 32, 5.<BR> 4. To begin, MBh. 5, 26.<BR> 5. To take to mind, Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 24.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To snatch away, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 39.<BR> --With उप उप, To give, Rām. 1, 50, 9 Gorr.<BR> --With कद् कद्, To reproach, Bhāg. P. 7, 5, 28.<BR> --With परा परा, To exclude, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0393-b " target="_blank">Page0393-b + 41</a>]<BR> --With परि परि, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To deliver, Man. 9, 327.<BR> 2. To grant, Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 50.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be delivered, MBh. 15, 445.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Par. (Ātm., Naiṣ. 6, 95),<BR> 1. To give, Man. 9, 118; to communicate, MBh. 1, 103.<BR> 2. To grant, Rām. 1, 62, 26.<BR> 3. To give in marriage, Man. 8, 204.<BR> 4. To sell, Pañc. i. d. 17.<BR> 5. To pay, Yājñ. 2, 90.<BR> 6. To make good, Man. 8, 232.<BR> 7. To put, Yājñ. 1, 236.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्रत्त and प्रदत्त, Given, etc., Pañc. 25, 4; 63, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-प्रत्त, adj. of which nothing is given away before (eating it), Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 18.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To compel to return, Yājñ. 2, 270.<BR> 2. To cause to put in, MBh. 1, 5723. Desider. To wish to give in marriage, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 6.<BR> --With प्रतिप्र प्रति-प्र, To return, MBh. 5, 5525.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To deliver, Rām. 2, 32, 23.<BR> 2. To grant, MBh. 1, 3346.<BR> 3. To give in marriage, Hariv. 11006 (p. 790).<BR> --Caus. To order to be given, Rām. 2, 32, 16.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To return, Chr. 58, 6.<BR> 2. To give, MBh. 7, 6976.<BR> --Caus. To cause to repay, Yājñ. 2, 61.<BR> --With वि वि, to divide, Rām. 1, 13, 39 Gorr.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To grant, MBh. 7, 2618.<BR> --Cf. δίδωμι, δωτήρ, δοτήρ, δάνος, δαπάνη (Caus.); Lat. dare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयम्- + दत्त स्वयम्- + दत्त, adj. self-given. m. a child who has given himself to adoptive parents, Man. 9, 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
2. दा दा, ii. 2 Par., and दो दो, i. 4, द्य, Par. To cut.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दित, Cut off, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 23.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To cut off, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 31.<BR> --With वि वि, To cut, to destroy, Hariv. 8435 (anomal. absolut. वि-दित्य).<BR> --Cf. दय्; δατήρ, δασμός, δάπτω (Caus.), δεῖπνον; Lat. daps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
† 3. दा दा, i. 4, द्य, To bind (ved.).<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, ptcple. of the pf. pass. संदित, Tied, Hariv. 3674.<BR> --Cf. δίδημι, δέμα, δετός, perhaps also δέω, δεσμός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष
दाक्ष दाक्ष, i. e. दक्ष + अ,<BR> I. adj. Referring to Dakṣa, Hariv. 7444.<BR> II. m. or n. South, Man. 6, 10 (with अयन, The sacrifice ordained for the winter solstice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण|दाक्षायणः
दाक्षायण दाक्षायण, i. e. दक्ष + आयन,<BR> I. patronym., f. णी, A descendant of Dakṣa, Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 2; Śāk. 101, 7.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The posterity of Dakṣa, Bhāg. P. 4, c. 1.<BR> 2. Gold, or a gold ornament; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणिन्
दाक्षायणिन् दाक्षायणिन्, i. e. दाक्षायण + इन्, adj., f. नी, Wearing gold ornaments, Yājñ. 1, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण्य|दाक्षायण्यः
दाक्षायण्य दाक्षायण्य, i. e. दाक्षायणी + य, m. The son of Dākṣāyaṇī, MBh. 13, 6831.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्य|दाक्षिणात्यः
दाक्षिणात्य दाक्षिणात्य, i. e. दक्षिणा + त्य + अ,<BR> I. adj. Southern, MBh. 1, 4690; Pañc. 3, 9.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. pl. The nations of the south, Rām. 2, 82, 7.<BR> 2. The south, Hariv. 6200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
दाक्षिण्य दाक्षिण्य, i. e. दक्षिण + य, n.<BR> 1. Politeness, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 17.<BR> 2. Kindness, Bhartṛ. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष्य|दाक्ष्यं
दाक्ष्य दाक्ष्य, i. e. दक्ष + य, n. Ability, skill, Man. 10, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम|दाडिमः
दाडिम दाडिम, m. The pomegranate tree (n. the fruit), Rām. 3, 7, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढिका
दाढिका दाढिका (a form of दंष्तृका, i. e. दंष्त्रा + क), f. The beard, Man. 8, 283.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिक|दांडिक|दांडिकः|दाण्डिकः
दाण्डिक दाण्डिक, i. e. दण्ड + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b " target="_blank">Page0394-b + 42</a>] adj., f. की, Punishing; m. A chastiser, MBh. 12, 2135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातुकाम
दातुकाम दातुकाम, i. e. दातुम्, infin. of 1. दा, -काम, adj. Wishing to make a present, Pañc. ii. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
दातृ दा + तृ, m., f. त्री, n.<BR> 1. A donor, a giver, Man. 11, 9; Rām. 4, 20, 4.<BR> 2. Giving in marriage, Man. 3, 172.<BR> 3. Communicating, Man. 2, 146.<BR> 4. A creditor, Man. 8, 161.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δωτήρ; Lat. dator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदातृ
अ- + दातृ अ- + दातृ, m. 1. one who gives no present, Man. 11, 15. 2. one who is not obliged to pay, Man. 8, 161. क्षीर-दात्री, f. yielding milk, MBh. 13, 4919.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृता
दातृता दातृ + ता, f., and दातृत्व दातृ + त्व, n. Liberality, Rājat. 3, 197; Hariv. 14414.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यूह|दात्यूहः
दात्यूह दात्यूह, m. A gallinule, Rām. 2, 56, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्र|दात्रं
दात्र 2. दा + त्र, n. A kind of sickle, Rām. 2, 87, 9 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाद|दादः
