दानवेय|दानवेयः
दानवेय दानवेय, i. e. दानु + एय (see दानव), m. = Dānava, a demon, MBh. 8, 3692.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिक
ऽदानिक -दानिक, i. e. -दान + इक, adj. Referring to a gift, e. g. उदक-, Referring to an oblation to deceased ancestors, MBh. 1, 589. वर-, Caused by the grant of a favour, Rām. 2, 115, 7 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिन्
दानिन् दानिन्, i. e. दान + इन्, adj., f. नी, Liberal, Bhāg. P. 7, 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त दान्त, i. e.<BR> I. दन्त + अ, adj. Of ivory, Rājat. 5, 12. 21.<BR> II. Ptcple. pf. pass. of दम्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्तिक|दांतिक
