दार्दुर दार्दुर, i. e. दर्दुर + अ, adj., f. री, and दार्दुरिक दार्दुरिक, i. e. दर्दुर + इक, f. का, Referring to a frog, Hariv. 4162; Bhāg. P. 2, 3, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व|दार्वं
दार्व दार्व, i. e. दारु + अ (anomal.),<BR> I. adj., f. वी, Wooden, Bhāg. P. 5, 12, 6.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 1026.<BR> III. f. वी, The name of several plants, Curcuma zantorhiza, Suśr. 2, 23, 14, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वाघाट|दार्वाघाटः|दार्व्वाघाट|दार्व्वाघाटः
दार्वाघाट दार्वाघाट, i. e. दारु-आघाट = आघात, m. The woodpecker, MBh. 10, 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्श
दार्श दार्श, i. e. दर्श + अ, m. The sacrifice to be performed at the conjunction of the moon, Man. 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालन|दालनं
दालन दालन, i. e. दल् + अन, n. Crumbling off (of the teeth), Suśr. 2, 132, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिम|दालिमः
दालिम दालिम = दाडिम, Amar. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्भ्य|दाल्भ्यः
दाल्भ्य दाल्भ्य, i. e. दल्भ, the name of a Ṛṣi, + य, patronym. A descendant of Dalbha, MBh. 2, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाव|दावः
दाव दाव, i. e. दु + अ, m.<BR> 1. A forest conflagration, MBh. 3, 2608.<BR> 2. A forest, MBh. 1, 8088.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावदहनज्वालाकलापाय
दावदहनज्वालाकलापाय दावदहनज्वालाकलापाय, i. e. दाव-दहन-ज्वाला-कलाप + य, a denomin. Ātm. To resemble the stream of flames of a burning forest, Gīt. 4, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्
दाश् दाश्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To worship, Chr. 292, 6 = Rigv. i. 86, 6.<BR> 2. To make oblations.<BR> 3. To bestow.<BR> 4. † ii. 5, Par. To hurt.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. act. ददाशिवंस्, Chr. 297, 20 = Rigv. i. 112, 20, and दाश्वंस्, 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12.<BR> 1. Pious.<BR> 2. Bestowing, Bhāg. P. 8, 22, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश दाश, written also दास दास,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A fisherman, MBh. 1, 4012.<BR> 2. A boatman, MBh. 1, 5875; Man. 8, 408 (with स्).<BR> 3. The son of a Niṣāda by an Āgoyava-woman, Man. 10, 34 (with स्).<BR> II. f. शी, A fisher-maid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथ|दाशरथः
दाशरथ दाशरथ, i. e.<BR> I. दशरथ, a proper name, + अ.<BR> 1. patronym. A descendant of Daśaratha, Rām. 5, 80, 23.<BR> 2. adj. Belonging to Daśaratha, Hariv. 4167.<BR> II. दशन्-रथ + अ, adj. Ten carriages broad, MBh. 12, 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथि|दाशरथिः
दाशरथि दाशरथि, i. e. दशरथ, see the last, + इ, patronym. A descendant of Daśaratha, Rām. 1, 3, 11; 6, 19, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्णक
दाशार्णक दाशार्णक, i. e. दशार्न + अ + क, adj. णिका, Referring to the Daśārṇas, e. g., with नृप, The king of the Daśārṇas, Chr. 52, 11; with धात्री, A female servant of this people, Chr. 52, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्ह|दाशार्हः
दाशार्ह दाशार्ह, i. e. दशार्ह + अ,<BR> 1. adj., f. ही, Belonging to Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 2, 84.<BR> 2. m. A name of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 2, 1223.<BR> 3. m. pl. Daśārhas, the people, MBh. 1, 7513.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्हक
दाशार्हक दाशार्ह + क, m. pl. = Daśārhas, the people, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेय|दाशेयः
दाशेय दाशेय, written also दासेय दासेय, i. e. दाशी + एय, m. and f. यी, The son, the daughter, of a fisherwoman, MBh. 1, 4015; Chr. 5, 1 (with स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्वंस्
दाश्वंस् दाश्वंस्, see दाश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास दास, i. e. probably दम् + स,<BR> I. m. A slave, a servant, Man. 4, 253; 8, 416.<BR> II. f. सी, A female slave, a servant-maid, Man. 9, 48.<BR> --Cf. दाश.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदास|अदासः
अ- + दास अ- + दास, m. not being a slave, Man. 10, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डदास|दंडदास|दण्डदासः
दण्ड- + दास दण्ड- + दास, m. one enslaved by punishment, Man. 8, 415.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीदास
दासी- + दास दासी- + दास, n. sing. and m. pl. male and female slaves, MBh. 13, 2950; 2, 2510.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0397-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदास|भक्तदासः
