दिव्
1. दिव् दिव्, i. 4, दीव्य, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm. MBh. 4, 533),<BR> 1. To play at dice, MBh. 3, 2260.<BR> 2. To play, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 2.<BR> 3. With the instrumental and dat. of the stake, MBh. 2, 2061; 4, 533.<BR> 4. To shine, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 22.<BR> 5. † To praise.<BR> 6. † To be glad.<BR> 7. † To be mad.<BR> 8. † To be sleepy.<BR> 9. † To desire.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. द्यूत, n.<BR> 1. Gaming with inanimate things, Man. 9, 221.<BR> 2. Game at dice, Nal. 9, 2.<BR> 3. Battle, MBh. 7, 1350.<BR> 4. The prize of a combat, MBh. 7, 3996.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. देवितव्य, To be played at dice, MBh. 2, 2493. n. Game at dice, 5, 894.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To lose at play, MBh. 2, 2041.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To play, MBh. 8, 4210.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0399-b " target="_blank">Page0399-b + 41</a>] throw dice in one's turn, MBh. 5, 137.<BR> --With वि वि, To lose at play, MBh. 2, 2384.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्यूत
