दिश्
1. दिश् दिश्, i. 6, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To show, to produce, Man. 8, 57.<BR> 2. To denote, Rām. 3, 30, 14.<BR> 3. To give, Ṛt. 6, 34.<BR> 4. To command, Kir. 5, 28.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दिष्ट.<BR> 1. Shown, Bhaṭṭik. 2, 32.<BR> 2. Determined, MBh. 3, 8847; with गति, Death, Rām. 2, 30, 40. n.<BR> 1. Command, Bhāg. P. 4, 28, 1.<BR> 2. Fate, MBh. 14, 1551.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. देशय,<BR> 1. To point out, Rām. 3, 78, 13.<BR> 2. To order, MBh. 4, 670.<BR> 3. To govern, Rām. 2, 61, 34 Gorr.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति,<BR> 1. To assign to, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 19.<BR> 2. To promise, 4, 9, 26.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To order, Rām. 6, 89, 21.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. एकानुदिष्ट, i. e. एक-, n. obsequies to a single ancestor, Man. 4, 111.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To state, Man. 8, 54.<BR> 2. To denounce, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 4.<BR> 3. To pretend, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 19.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप,<BR> 1. To design, MBh. 3, 16189.<BR> 2. To name, Bhāg. P. 5, 4, 9.<BR> 3. To name falsely, Rām. 3, 54, 24.<BR> 4. To pretend, MBh. 13, 1458.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To aim at, MBh. 7, 1234.<BR> 2. To assign to, Rām. 4, 41, 7.<BR> 3. To mark, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 7.<BR> 4. To show, Bhāg. P. 8, 32, 5.<BR> 5. To teach, Man. 4, 80.<BR> 6. To design, Bhāg. P. 8, 22, 4.<BR> 7. To order, prescribe, Rām. 5, 38, 19; Man. 11, 192 (193).<BR> 8. To banish, Kathās. 2, 19.<BR> 9. To undertake, Rām. 2, 52, 65 (a vow).<BR> 10. To try, MBh. 3, 11986. आदिष्ट, n. Command, Lass. 67, 13.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To point out, Mṛcch. 138, 4.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To assign to, MBh. 1, 7239.<BR> 2. To declare, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 29.<BR> 3. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0401-a " target="_blank">Page0401-a + 43</a>] order, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 7.<BR> --With निरा निस्-आ, To pay, Man. 8, 162.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ,<BR> 1. To prescribe, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 22.<BR> 2. To advise, Rām. 5, 81, 4.<BR> 3. To report again, MBh. 3, 14717.<BR> 4. To summon, Hit. 71, 16.<BR> 5. To countermand, Vikr. 56, 1.<BR> 6. To decline, Śāk. 73, 3.<BR> 7. To overcome, MBh. 14, 2460.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ,<BR> 1. To assign to, MBh. 14, 1921.<BR> 2. To teach, Prab. 107, 5.<BR> 3. To order, MBh. 1, 7689.<BR> 4. To declare, Mālav. 69, 13 v. r.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To assign to, Man. 1, 91.<BR> 2. To declare, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 1.<BR> 3. To teach, Kām. Nītis. 15, 2.<BR> 4. To determine, Rām. 1, 8, 14.<BR> 5. To order, Arj. 3, 10.<BR> --Caus. To order, Pañc. 171, 8.<BR> --With प्रतिसमा प्रति-सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To answer, Daśak. 124, 3.<BR> 2. To order, Rām. 5, 24, 35.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To point out, Rām. 2, 56, 4.<BR> 2. To defy, Śāk. 94, 1.<BR> 3. To predict, Śāk. 71, 11.<BR> 4. To denote, Mārk. P. 26, 17.<BR> 5. To teach, Bhartṛ. 2, 54.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. एक-उद्दिष्ट, n. Obsequies to a single ancestor, Man. 4, 110.<BR> --Absol. उद्दिश्य,<BR> 1. Against, on, Rām. 3, 50, 17.<BR> 2. To, Rām. 1, 33, 17; 3, 2, 14.<BR> 3. For, Rām. 1, 13, 31.<BR> 4. In remembrance of, Rājat. 5, 120.<BR> 5. On account of, Kathās. 2, 17.<BR> 6. In the name of, Rām. 1, 80, 21 Gorr.<BR> 7. Referring to, Bhartṛ. 1, 56. Repeated उद्-दिश्योद्दिश्य, To one (this)--to another (that), MBh. 15, 414.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To mention, Man. 5, 17.<BR> 2. To name, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 47, 52.<BR> --Absol. समुद् अ,<BR> 1. Against, on, MBh. 1, 4573.<BR> 2. For, MBh. 4, 742; Rām. 2, 15, 34 Gorr.<BR> 3. In remembrance of, MBh. 15, 1094.<BR> 4. With regard to, MBh. 1, 489.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To point out, Rām. 2, 55, 2 Gorr. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0401-b " target="_blank">Page0401-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. To teach, Chr. 22, 16.<BR> 3. To advise, Hit. 57, 1.<BR> 4. To mention, Man. 3, 14.<BR> 5. To name, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 9.<BR> 6. To ordain, Man. 2, 190.<BR> 7. To govern, Kumāras. 1, 2.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. काल-अत्यय-उपदिष्ट, Produced too late, the designation of an argument which, however plausible, is precluded by higher evidence, Bhāṣāp. 70.<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, To teach in one's turn, Mālav. d. 5.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप,<BR> 1. To point out, MBh. 3, 2328.<BR> 2. To assign to, Rām. 3, 45, 18.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To point to, Śāk. 63, 10.<BR> 2. To assign to, Rām. 1, 15, 18 Gorr.<BR> 3. To declare, Man. 3, 199.<BR> 4. To denounce, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 23.<BR> 5. To determine, Bhāg. P. 7, 6, 22.<BR> 6. To mention, Man. 7, 144; with परिगणनया, To number, Megh. 22.<BR> 7. To order, Man. 11, 146.<BR> 8. To advise, Hit. iii. d. 39. अ-निर्दिष्ट, adj. Allowed (by the Veda), Man. 5, 11.<BR> --With अभिनिस् अभि-निस्,<BR> 1. To point to, Rām. 3, 63, 15.<BR> 2. To determine, MBh. 12, 6991.<BR> 3. To call, Man. 10, 20.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्,<BR> 1. To direct, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 8.<BR> 2. To determine, Bhāg. P. 7, 11, 35.<BR> 3. To declare, Yājñ. 2, 111.<BR> 4. To order, Rām. 5, 37, 32.<BR> --With परि परि, परिदिष्ट, Known, MBh. 3, 12497.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 3, 2209.<BR> 2. To declare, Bhag. 8, 28.<BR> 3. To ordain, MBh. 12, 7050.<BR> 4. To impel, Rām. 3, 66, 9.<BR> 5. To assign to, Rām. 1, 14, 13.<BR> 6. To grant, MBh. 1, 6472 (i. 4, Par.).<BR> --Caus. To impel, MBh. 3, 2727.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, Caus. To impel, Rām. 2, 32, 6.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. To teach, MBh. 12, 13943.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To assign [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a " target="_blank">Page0402-a + 43</a>] to, Rām. 1, 22, 29.<BR> 2. To promise, Yājñ. 2, 232.<BR> 3. To declare, MBh. 5, 7534.<BR> 4. To order, Rām. 2, 52, 59.<BR> --Caus. To invite to speak, MBh. 14, 458.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्,<BR> 1. To give an order in one's turn, Rām. 6, 98, 37.<BR> 2. To give an order, MBh. 1, 748.<BR> --Cf. δείκνυμι, δείκελος, δίκη, δικεῖν, δίκτυον, δειδίσκομαι (frequent. with inchoat. σκ for δειδικ + σκ), δίσκος; Lat. in-dicare, ju-dex, dicere, perhaps dignus (but cf. यशस्); Goth. teihan; A.S. tihian, tihhan; O.H.G. zeigôn; A.S. taecan; probably Goth. taikns; A.S. tácn, tácen, taecan; O.H.G. zît (for zig + ti); A.S. tiid, tíd; O.H.G. zeinjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वदिश्|पूर्व्वदिश्
पूर्व- + दिश् पूर्व- + दिश्, n. fate, Bhāg. P. 6, 17, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0400-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
2. दिश् दिश्, f.<BR> 1. A region, or quarter, or point of the compass, Pañc. ii. d. 64.<BR> 2. pl. The parts of the earth, Sund. 2, 26.<BR> 3. pl. Different directions, Rām. 1, 55, 22; 2, 106, 27; repeated तिशो-दिशस् (The one) hither--(the other) thither, Pañc. 129, 20; also sing. (but with सर्वतस्), Nal. 16, 5.<BR> 4. There are variously reckoned four, eight, or ten quarters of the world, Kathās. 15, 137; Man. 1, 13; MBh. 1, 729.<BR> 5. The number ten, Śrut. 36.<BR> 6. A foreign country, Yājñ. 2, 254.<BR> 7. The name of a river, MBh. 6, 327.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिश्
वि- + दिश् वि- + दिश्, f. an intermediate point of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश|दिशः
ऽदिश -दिश् + अ, a substitute for दिश् when latter part of comp. adv.; see यथादिशम्, यथाभीष्टदिशम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशा
दिशा दिश् + आ, f. A quarter or point of the compass, MBh. 4, 1716.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशोभाग
दिशोभाग दिशोभाग, i. e. दिश् + अस्-भाग, adj. One who betakes himself to his heels, Pañc. 232, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टि|दिष्टिः
दिष्टि दिष्टि, i. e. दिश् + ति, f. used only in the instr. दिष्ट्या, implying joy or auspiciousness, Thank heaven ! Sāv. 6, 23.<BR> --Cf. दिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह्
दिह् दिह्, ii. 2, Par., Ātm. To smear.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दिग्ध,<BR> 1. Smeared, Man. 3, 132.<BR> 2. Anointed, Rām. 3, 42, 39. m. A poisoned arrow, Man. 7, 90; Rām. 2, 114, 33 Gorr.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, आदिग्ध,<BR> 1. Smeared, MBh. 6, 4384.<BR> 2. Anointed, 7, 4386.<BR> --With उप उप, उपदिग्ध, Overlaid, Suśr. 2, 376, 11.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To smear, Bhag. 2, 5.<BR> 2. To anoint, Suśr. 1, 42, 19.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To smear, MBh. 8, 3161.<BR> 2. To cover, Vikr. d. 43. Pass. To be dubious, Rām. 5, 18, 17. संदिग्ध,<BR> 1. Poisoned (?), Daśak. in Chr. 197, 2.<BR> 2. Indistinct, MBh. 1, 6565.<BR> 3. Dubious, uncertain, Pañc. i. d. 196.<BR> 4. Desponding, Rām. 1, 66, 25. अ-संदिग्ध + म्, adv. Undoubtedly, Pañc. 241, 8. निस्-संदिग्ध, adj. Certain, MBh. 13, 3528. ˚धम्, adv. Undoubtedly, MBh. 12, 7809.<BR> --Cf. τείχος, τοῖχος; Lat. tingere; θιγγάνω; Lat. fingo, figulus; O.H.G. ziagal; A.S. tigel, tigul; Goth. deigaṇ, ga-dikis, daigs; A.S. díc, deag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
1. दी दी (cf. डी), i. 4, Par. To soar, to fly (ved.).<BR> --Cf. probably δίνη, δινέω, perhaps δίω, δίεμαι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
2. दी दी, anomal. ii. 3, दीदी, Par., Ātm. To shine (ved.).<BR> --Cf. δέαται, δέατο, probably also δῆλος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
3. दी दी, i. 4, Ātm. To waste, to go to ruin.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दीन,<BR> 1. Scanty (ved.).<BR> 2. Afflicted, wretched, Man. 9, 238.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीन
अ-दीन अ-दीन, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदीन
परिदीन परिदीन, much afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदीनम्
स-दीन + म् स-दीन + म्, adv. lamentably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्ष्
दीक्ष् दीक्ष् (originally a desider. of दक्ष्), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To hallow one's self, to prepare one's self for a sacred act.<BR> 2. † To be shaved.<BR> 3. † To perform a sacrifice.<BR> 4. † To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a " target="_blank">Page0403-a + 43</a>] initiate.<BR> 5. † To restrain one's self.<BR> 6. † To declare a vow.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दीक्षित,<BR> 1. Prepared for a sacrifice, Man. 8, 360.<BR> 2. Initiated, MBh. 13, 918.<BR> 3. Ready, MBh. 2, 2514.<BR> --Caus. दीक्षय,<BR> 1. To initiate, Par. and Ātm., MBh. 14, 2110; 2, 1247.<BR> 2. To determine, MBh. 5, 5648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षण|दीक्षणं
दीक्षण दीक्षण, i. e. दीक्ष् + अन, n. Consecration, MBh. 14, 2092.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षा
दीक्षा दीक्ष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Consecration, MBh. 1, 8135.<BR> 2. Undergoing religious observances, engaging in a course of austerities, Rām. 1, 32, 4.<BR> 3. Religious observances, Man. 6, 29.<BR> 4. Devotion, Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथादीक्षम्
यथा-दीक्ष + म् यथा-दीक्ष + म्, adv. according to the religious observances, MBh. 14, 1270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधिति|दीधितिः
दीधिति दीधिति, i. e. दीधी + ति, f.<BR> 1. A ray of light, a sun or moonbeam, MBh. 3, 188; Prab. 94, 6.<BR> 2. Light, Pañc. i. d. 369; Mārk. P. 18, 19.<BR> 3. Splendour (?), Bhartṛ. 2, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितदीधिति|सितदीधितिः
सित- + दीधिति सित- + दीधिति and हिम-, m. the moon, Śiś. 9, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधी
दीधी दीधी (akin to दी), ii. 2, Ātm. To shine (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनकम्
दीनकम् दीन + क + म् (see 3. दी), adv. Miserably, Arj. 10, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनार|दीनारः
दीनार दीनार (borrowed from δηνάριον), m. A coin, Pañc. 174, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्
दीप् दीप् (originally a Causal of दी), i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 3, 13984).<BR> 1. To blaze, Rām. 5, 50, 5.<BR> 2. To shine, MBh. 5, 7322. दीप्त,<BR> 1. Blazing, Bhag. 11, 17.<BR> 2. Hot, Man. 3, 133.<BR> 3. Radiant, MBh. 5, 7040.<BR> 4. Illuminated by the sun, opposite to the sun, inauspicious, Draup. 6, 3; Hariv. 9702.<BR> 5. Clear, MBh. 3, 16603.<BR> --Caus. दीपय,<BR> 1. To kindle, Bhag. 4, 27.<BR> 2. To excite, Śiś. 9, 42.<BR> 3. To illuminate, Kir. 5, 2.<BR> 4. To make illustrious, MBh. 5, 1069. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-b " target="_blank">Page0403-b + 40</a>]<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अदीपित, Not illuminated, Kir. 5, 48.<BR> --Frequent. देदीप्य (Par., MBh. 7, 8138),<BR> 1. To be all in flame, MBh. 3, 15588.<BR> 2. To be very radiant, MBh. 3, 2146.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिदीप्त (rather दीप्त with अति), Blazing violently, Rām. 5, 50, 8.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To shine towards, Hariv. 7501.<BR> --With आ आ, आदीप्त,<BR> 1. Blazing, Ṛt. 6, 19.<BR> 2. Burning, MBh. 15, 1081.<BR> --Caus. To kindle, Rām. 2, 89, 16.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, Caus. To illuminate completely, MBh. 7, 7296.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To kindle, Hariv. 5521.<BR> 2. To excite, Bhāg. P. 8, 7, 11.<BR> 3. To illuminate, Mārk. P. 49, 11.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, Caus. To inflame, Rām. 4, 26, 14.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus. To kindle, set on fire, MBh. 3, 10230; 1, 5828.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To boil up, MBh. 12, 2036 (Par.).<BR> 2. To be completely radiant, MBh. 7, 2237.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रदीप्त,<BR> 1. Blazing, Rām. 1, 54, 22.<BR> 2. Kindled (as anger), MBh. 3, 2374.<BR> 3. Shining, Ṛt. 1, 27.<BR> 4. Illuminated, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 9.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To set on fire, kindle, MBh. 1, 5600; 13, 4037. 2. To inflame, Rām. 3, 69, 21.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, संप्रदीप्त, Blazing, Rām. 5, 52, 13.<BR> --Caus. To kindle, MBh. 7, 7237.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रतिदीप्त, Flaming towards, Hariv. 13155.<BR> --With वि वि, To shine, MBh. 7, 7322; विदीप्त, Shining, MBh. 12, 8332.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To illuminate, MBh. 8, 1488.<BR> 2. To inflame, Bhāg. P. 9, 4, 46.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, Caus. To set on fire, MBh. 14, 2033.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To blaze, Hariv. 3539; संदीप्त,<BR> 1. Burning, Bhartṛ. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a " target="_blank">Page0404-a + 43</a>] 3. 26.<BR> 2. Flaming, MBh. 5, 7205.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To kindle, set on fire, Pañc. 97, 25; MBh. 1, 8366.<BR> 2. To excite, MBh. 5, 2801.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप|दीपः
दीप दीप् + अ, m. A lamp, Bhag. 6, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणदीप
निर्वाण- + दीप निर्वाण- + दीप, m. an extinguished lamp, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1610.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपदीप
नृप- + दीप नृप- + दीप, m. a king like a lamp, Pañc. i. d. 251.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपक|दीपकं|दीपकः
दीपक दीप् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Inflaming, Pañc. iii. d. 27.<BR> 2. Illuminating, Pañc. 190, 2.<BR> II. m. A lamp, Bhartṛ. 1, 55.<BR> III. f. पिका, A lamp, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वरीदीपक
शर्वरी- + दीपक शर्वरी- + दीपक, m. the lamp of the night (epithet of the moon), Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2968.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपन|दीपनं|दीपनः
दीपन दीप् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Inflaming, MBh. 1, 8455.<BR> 2. Exciting, Ṛt. 1, 3.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Setting on fire, Pañc. 194, 12.<BR> 2. Burning, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 21.<BR> 3. Exciting, or promoting digestion, Suśr. 1, 152, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलदीपन
अनल- + दीपन अनल- + दीपन, adj. promoting digestion, Suśr. 1, 200, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीय|दीपनीयः
दीपनीय दीपनीय, i. e. दीपन + ईय, adj. Promoting digestion, Suśr. 1, 177, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ति|दीप्तिः
दीप्ति दीप् + ति, f. Splendour, Rām. 1, 7, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहदीप्ति|गृहदीप्तिः
गृह- + दीप्ति गृह- + दीप्ति, f. being the splendour of the house, Man. 9, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिमन्त्|दीप्तिमत्
दीप्तिमन्त् दीप्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Radiant, Indr. 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्र|दीप्रः
दीप्र दीप् + र, adj. Shining, Kathās. 25, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घ|दीर्घं|दीर्घः
दीर्घ दीर्घ, i. e. दृह् (for original दर्घ्), + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. घा Long, applied either to space or time, Rām. 5, 17, 28; 3, 68, 36; ˚घम्, adv. 2, 62, 3; comparat. दीर्घतर, Pañc. 209, 1; and द्राघीयंस्; superl. दीर्घतम, Bhāg. P. 7, 5, 44, and द्राघिष्ठ.<BR> II. m. A long vessel, Man. 2, 33.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δολιχός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदीर्घ|सुदीर्घः
सु- + दीर्घ सु- + दीर्घ, adj. very long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घता
दीर्घता दीर्घ + ता, f., and दीर्घत्व दीर्घ + त्व, n. Length, Suśr. 1, 117, 18; Bhāg. P. 7, 7, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदर्शिता
दीर्घदर्शिता दीर्घदर्शिता, i. e. दीर्घ-दर्शिन् + ता, and दीर्घदर्शित्व दीर्घदर्शित्व, i. e. दीर्घ-दर्शिन् + त्व, n. Longsightedness, providence, Kām. Nītis. 8, 10; 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसंध्यत्व|दीर्घसन्ध्यत्व
दीर्घसंध्यत्व दीर्घ-संध्य + त्व (see संध्या), n. The continued repetition of the twilight prayer, Man. 4, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रता
दीर्घसूत्रता दीर्घ-सूत्र + ता, f. Irresolution, dilatoriness. MBh. 2, 241.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घसूत्रता
अ- + दीर्घसूत्रता अ- + दीर्घसूत्रता, f. Resoluteness, Kām. Nītis. 8, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रिन्
