दुष्टर दुष्टर, i. e. दुस्-तॄ + अ, adj. Unconquerable, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टि|दुष्टिः
दुष्टि दुष्टि, i. e. दुष् + ति, f. Corruptness, Suśr. 1, 253, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रज्ञत्व
दुष्प्रज्ञत्व दुष्प्रज्ञत्व, i. e. दुस्-प्रज्ञ + त्व, n. Stupidity, Prab. 108, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रतर
दुष्प्रतर दुष्प्रतर, i. e. दुस्-प्र-तृ + अ, adj., f. रा, Difficult to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्ष
दुष्प्रधर्ष दुष्प्रधर्ष and दुष्प्रधर्षण दुष्प्रधर्षण, i. e. दुस्-प्र-धृष् + अ or अन, adj., f. षा, णा, Difficult to be attacked, Rām. 6, 95, 12; 5, 72, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसह
दुष्प्रसह दुष्प्रसह, i. e. दुस्-प्र-सह् + अ, adj., f. हा.<BR> 1. Difficult to be supported, irresistible, Ragh. 3, 58.<BR> 2. Terrible, MBh. 12, 3094.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसाह
दुष्प्रसाह दुष्प्रसाह, = the last, with आ on account of the metre, Arj. 3, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप
दुष्प्राप दुष्प्राप, i. e. दुस्-प्र-आप्-अ, adj., f. पा, Difficult to be attained, MBh. 4, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रेक्ष
दुष्प्रेक्ष दुष्प्रेक्ष, i. e. दुस्-प्र-ईक्ष् + अ, adj., f. षा, Difficult to be looked at, Rām. 3, 17, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्मन्त|दुष्मन्तः
दुष्मन्त दुष्मन्त, or दुष्यन्त दुष्-यन्त, or दुष्वन्त दुष्वन्त, m. The name of a prince, the husband of Śakuntalā, MBh. 1, 2801; Hariv. 1701; Rām. 2, 116, 29 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्
दुस् दुस् (cf. दुष्), a prefix implying:<BR> 1. Bad, wicked, contemptible, e. g. दुर्वाच्, A bad speech, abuse (see वाच्); दुर्जन, A wicked person (see जन); दुर्बुद्धि, Having a contemptible intellect, i. e. stupid (see बुद्धि).<BR> 2. Wrong, e. g. दुस्तर्क (see तर्क).<BR> 3. Inauspicious, e. g. दुस्तिथि (see तिथि).<BR> 4. Difficult, e. g. दुष्प्रेक्ष.<BR> --Cf. δυς; Goth. tus in tuz-verjan; O.H.G. zur-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्त्यज
दुस्त्यज दुस्-त्यज् + अ, adj., f. जा, Difficult to be abandoned or resigned, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 48; MBh. 1, 3513.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्त्यज|सुदुस्त्यजः
सु- + दुस्त्यज सु- + दुस्त्यज, to be risked very unwillingly, Chr. 33, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्
1. दुह् दुह् (originally दुघ्, cf. दुघ), ii. 2, and i. 4.<BR> I. Par.<BR> 1. To milk, Man. 8, 231; Bhāg. P. 4, 17, 7; to milk out (with two accs.), 4, 18, 18.<BR> 2. To enjoy, Ragh. 1, 26.<BR> 3. To practise from interested motives, MBh. 3, 1165.<BR> 4. To draw something out of anything (with two accs.), MBh. 12, 3305; with acc. and abl., Man. 1, 23.<BR> II. Ātm.<BR> 1. To yield milk or other desired objects, MBh. 1, 6658; 6657 (also i. 4, Par., Bhāg. P. i, 14, 19). Anomal. 3 pl. of the red. pf. दुदूहुस्, on account of the metre, Bhāg. P. 5, 15, 9.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दुग्ध,<BR> 1. Milked. Hariv. 79.<BR> 2. Impoverished, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 16.<BR> 3. Collected, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 12. n. Milk. Bhartṛ. 2, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. दोहय,<BR> 1. To cause to yield milk or other desired objects, Bhāg. P. 4, 18, 15.<BR> 2. To produce, Man. 2, 77. Desider. दुधुक्ष, To wish to milk or to enjoy, Bhartṛ. 2, 38.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To milk out, to produce, MBh. 2, 76.<BR> 2. To withdraw, Kathās. 16, 83.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To milk, to enjoy, MBh. 12, 4384. (i. 4. Par.)<BR> --Cf. Goth. tiuhan; A.S. teon, teoge; O.H.G. ziuhan; Lat. duco; O.H.G. ziug (gaziug), zaugjan; τεῦχος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तदुग्ध
वित्त- + दुग्ध वित्त- + दुग्ध, n. wealth like milk (as if it were milk), Pañc. i. d. 249. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a " target="_blank">Page0410-a + 39</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्
† 2. दुह् दुह्, i. 1, Par. To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह
ऽदुह -दुह् + अ, adj. Yielding (cf. कामदुह).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुहा
दुस्- + दुहा दुस्- + दुह, adj., f. हा, difficult to be milked, MBh. 5, 1128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहितृ
दुहितृ दुहितृ, i. e. दुह् + तृ, f. A daughter, Man. 2, 215. Anomal. acc. pl. दुहितरस्, Rām. 3, 20, 28.<BR> --Abstract. त्व त्व, n. Rām. 1, 44, 38.<BR> --Cf. θυγάτηρ; Goth. dauhtar; A.S. dohtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू दू = 1. du.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दूऽ दू-, for दुस्, before following र्; cf. दूरक्ष्य under रक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत|दूतः
दूत दूत,<BR> I. m. A messenger, an envoy, Man. 3, 163.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघदूत
मेघ- + दूत मेघ- + दूत, The Cloud-messenger, a poem by Kālidāsa.<BR> II. f. ति and ति.<BR> 1. A female messenger, Nal. 21, 35.<BR> 2. A procuress, Lass. 8, 17; Vikr. d. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नदूती
प्रश्न-दूती प्रश्न-दूती, f. a riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतक|दूतकः
दूतक दूत + क,<BR> I. m. A messenger, MBh. 3, 15438.<BR> II. f. तिका.<BR> 1. A procuress, Lass. 24, 14.<BR> 2. A betrayer, Rājat. 6, 362.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदूतक|यमदूतकः
यम- + दूतक यम- + दूतक, m. 1. a messenger of Yama. 2. a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतत्व
दूतत्व दूत + त्व, n. Condition of an envoy, Pañc. 24, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतीत्व
दूतीत्व दूती + त्व, f. Condition of a procuress, Lass. 44, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत्य|दूत्यं
दूत्य दूत्य, i. e. दूत + य, n., also f. या, A message, Hariv. 6180; Kathās. 13, 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर|दूरं
दूर दूर, adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Distant, remote, Kathās. 16, 47.<BR> 2. Long, MBh. 9, 1738.<BR> --Comparat. दवीयंस्, Bhartṛ. 1, 68; superl. दविष्ठ, Rājat. 4, 365.<BR> --Acc. ˚रम्, adv.<BR> 1. Far, Rām. 1, 1, 28.<BR> 2. High, Hit. 27, 19.<BR> 3. Deep, Hariv. 14084.<BR> 4. In a high degree, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 7.<BR> --Instr. ˚रेण, adv. Far, Bhartṛ. 1, 80.<BR> --Abl. ˚रात्, adv.<BR> 1. From afar, Man. 2, 186.<BR> 2. Far from (with abl.), Man. 4, 151.<BR> 3. In a remote degree, Man. 3, 130 (Kull.)<BR> --Loc. ˚रे.<BR> 1. Far, Śāk. d. 9.<BR> 2. Far away, MBh. 9, 1737. दूरतरे, Far from (with abl.), Man. 11, 128 (129).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूर
अ- + दूर अ- + दूर, adj. near, Lass. 41, 7; abl ˚रात्, adv. near, Rām. 3, 50, 15; with gen., 2, 92, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूर
अति-, ˚रम् अति-, ˚रम्, adv. very far, Pañc. 105, 4; ˚रेण and ˚रे, adv. the same, Pañc. 51, 15; Rām. 3, 17, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूरम्
अति-, ˚रम् अति-, ˚रम्, adv. very far, Pañc. 105, 4; ˚रेण and ˚रे, adv. the same, Pañc. 51, 15; Rām. 3, 17, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियद्दूर
कियद्-दूर कियद्-दूर, i. e. कियन्त्-, adj., acc. ˚रम्, not very far, some little way, Pañc. 229, 20; loc. s. रे, how far, Pañc. 52, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूर|विदूरः
वि- + दूर वि- + दूर,<BR> I. adj. very far.<BR> II. m. the name of a mountain (विदूराद्रि i. e. विदूर-अद्रि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अ-वि अ-वि, adj. not very far; ˚रात्, adv. near, Rām. 3, 48, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदूर
सु- + दूर सु- + दूर, adj. very distant; ˚रम्, adv. in a very high degree, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरग
दूरग दूर-ग, adj. Being far, Rājat. 5, 320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरतस्
दूरतस् दूर + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. From afar, Rām. 1, 48, 9.<BR> 2. Aloof from, Man. 4, 73.<BR> 3. Far, Rām. 3, 60, 31; Pañc. i. d. 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूरतस्
अ- + दूरतस् अ- + दूरतस्, adv. near, Rām. 3, 9, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरत्व
दूरत्व दूर + त्व, n. Distance, Bhāṣāp. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरूढत्व
दूरूढत्व दूरूढत्व, i. e. दुस्-रूढ + त्व [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a " target="_blank">Page0411-a + 42</a>] (vb. रुह्), n. Bad cicatrisation, Suśr. 2, 12, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेचर
दूरेचर दूरे-चर, i. e. दूर + इ-चर, adj. Distant, Kām. Nītis. 8, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेयम
दूरेयम दूरे-यम, i. e. दूर + इ-यम, adj. One from whom the god of death is far removed, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्वा|दूर्व्वा
दूर्वा दूर्वा, f. A kind of milletgrass, Panicum dactylon, MBh. 3, 9984.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्वावन्त्|दूर्वावत्
दूर्वावन्त् दूर्वा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Joined with dūrvā grass, Kathās. 7, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष
ऽदूष -दूष, i. e. दुष्, Caus., + अ, latter part of comp. adj., Defiling; in पञ्क्ति- (a company), MBh. 13, 1274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषक|दूषकः
दूषक दूषक, i. e. दुष्, Caus., + अक,<BR> I. adj., f. षिका.<BR> 1. Defiling, MBh. 12, 1236 (sinful); one who defiles, Rām. 2, 75, 38.<BR> 2. Disfiguring, Suśr. 1, 295, 19.<BR> 3. Seducing, Man. 3, 164; 9, 232 (sowing dissensions, Kull.).<BR> 4. Hurting, Hariv. 3206.<BR> 5. Trespassing, Rām. 4, 37, 13.<BR> II. f. षिका.<BR> 1. Concretion on the eyes, Man. 5, 135.<BR> 2. A kind of rice, Suśr. 1, 195, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषण|दूषणः
दूषण दूषण, i. e. दुष्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णी.<BR> 1. Defiling, disgracing, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 13.<BR> 2. Hurting, Rām. 2, 109, 7.<BR> II. m. The name of a Rākṣasa or demon, Rām. 1, 1, 45.<BR> III. f. णा, The name of a deity, Bhāg. P. 5, 15, 13.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Defiling, Man. 9, 286; 11, 61.<BR> 2. Hurting, Man. 7, 48 (unjust seizure).<BR> 3. Seducing, Man. 2, 213.<BR> 4. Calumniating, Kathās. 24, 227.<BR> 5. Fault, Man. 9, 13; Bhartṛ. 2, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषयितृ
दूषयितृ दूषयितृ, i. e. दुष्, Caus., + तृ, One who deflowers, Mārk. P. 31, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिन्
दूषिन् दूषिन्, i. e. दुष्, Caus., + इन्, adj. f. इणी, Polluting, MBh. 3, 11158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृ
1. दृ दृ, i. 6, द्रिय, Ātm. (in epie poetry also Par., MBh. 13, 7411).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ,<BR> 1. To consider, Kām. Nītis. 5, 67.<BR> 2. To respect, Man. 2, 234.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. आदृत,<BR> 1. Respectful, Rām. 5, 25, 56.<BR> 2. Careful, Pañc. iii. d. 243.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With अत्या अति-आ, To regard carefully, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 21.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, समादृत, Very respectful, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 5.<BR> --Cf. probably A.S. dyre, deorling, perhaps also draed, dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अन्- + आदृत अन्- + आदृत, acc. adv. without any regard, Rām. 1, 59, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादृत
अत्यादृत अत्यादृत,<BR> 1. Very respectful, Dev. 4, 15.<BR> 2. Much cared for, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृ
† 2. दृ दृ, ii. 5, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृ
† 3. दृ दृ, i. 1, and i. 10, Par. To fear.<BR> --Cf. दॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृंह्
दृंह् दृंह्, i. 1, and i. 4, Par., Ātm. To fasten (ved.). To be fastened (ved.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दृढ,<BR> 1. Hard, firm, Rām. 2, 56, 14; Hit. 21, 20; Hariv. 7329.<BR> 2. Reliable, MBh. 3, 2646.<BR> 3. Violent, MBh. 13, 1972.<BR> 4. Great, MBh. 1, 7636. Compar. द्रढीयंस्, superl. द्रढिष्ठ. Acc. ˚ढम्, adv.<BR> 1. Tightly, Prab. 12, 3.<BR> 2. Much, Arj. 8, 1.<BR> 3. Well, Mālav. 11, 8.<BR> 4. Incessantly, MBh. 4, 314. Ved. frequent. दादृह्, To be excessively firm, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10.<BR> --Cf. τραχύς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढ|दृढं|दृढः
दृढ दृढ, see दृंह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढता
दृढता दृढ + ता, f. and दृढत्व दृढ + त्व, n. Firmness, Prab. 13, 17; Pañc. i. d. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढीकरण|दृढीकरणं
दृढीकरण दृढीकरण, n. and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढीकार|दृढीकारः
दृढीकार दृढीकार, i. e. दृढी-कृ + अन or अ, m. Confirmation, Rām. 2, 90, 21; MBh. 12, 7307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृति|दृतिः
दृति दृति, i. e. दृ + ती, f. A leather bag for holding liquids, Man. 2, 99.<BR> --Cf. δέρω, δείρω, δέρμα; O.H.G. gi-zelt, pelles, zelt; A.S. teld, tentorium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्
1. दृप् दृप्, i. 4, Par. To be mad or extravagant, arrogant, Gīt. 9, 11. दृप्त,<BR> 1. Wild, Rām. 1, 15, 7.<BR> 2. Arrogant, MBh. 1, 162. Compar. दृप्ततर, Excessively arrogant, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 12.<BR> --Caus. दर्पय,<BR> 1. To make mad, Kathās. 20, 64.<BR> 2. To make arrogant or proud, Pañc. iii. d. 244.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. दर्पित,<BR> 1. Wild, Bhartṛ. 3, 73.<BR> 2. Proud, Man. 8, 371.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिदृप्त (rather दृप्त with अति), Excessively arrogant, Kathās. 20, 65.<BR> --Cf. probably δόρπον, a banquet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्
† 2. दृप् दृप्, दृफ् दृफ्, दृम्फ् दृम्फ्, i. 6, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्
† 3. दृप् दृप्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृफ्
दृफ् दृफ्, see 2. दृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृभ्
1. दृभ् दृभ्, i. 6, Par. and † i. 1 and 10, Par. To string, to bind.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, To compose, Naiṣ. 9, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृभ्
† 2. दृभ् दृभ्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्प्|दृंप्
† दृम्प् दृम्प्, i. 10 Ātm. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फ्|दृंफ्
दृम्फ् दृम्फ्, see 2. दृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
1. दृश् दृश्, i. 1, पश्य (for original स्पश् + य, i. 4, forms the pres. impfct. imptive. and potent.), Par. (also Ātm., MBh. 1, 2896; 2830),<BR> 1. To see, Rām. 2, 64, 59.<BR> 2. To behold, look at, Man. 4, 44.<BR> 3. To be a spectator, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-b " target="_blank">Page0412-b + 48</a>] Man. 7, 92; to look on something (without being able to prevent it), Rām. 1, 54, 18.<BR> 4. To wait on, Lass. 2, 14.<BR> 5. To inspect, Man. 7, 120.<BR> 6. To live to see, Rām. 1, 1, 88.<BR> 7. To discover, Man. 8, 38.<BR> 8. To search, MBh. 4, 1172.<BR> 9. To learn, Rām. 1, 13, 7.<BR> 10. To know, Rām. 1, 57, 20.<BR> 11. To decide, Pañc. 165, 7. Passive also with the terminations of the Par., e. g. MBh. 2, 2345.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-दृश्यन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Invisible, Sund. 2, 19.<BR> 2. fem. न्ती A proper name, MBh. 1, 6757.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. द्रिष्ट,<BR> 1. Seen, etc.<BR> 2. Treated, Pañc. 85, 1.<BR> 3. Experienced, Rām. 3, 47, 18.<BR> 4. Devised, Nal. 4, 19.<BR> 5. Determined, MBh. 13, 11784.<BR> 6. Declared, Man. 9, 249.<BR> 7. Acknowledged, Man. 8, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-,<BR> I. adj. 1. not seen before, Rām. 5, 43, 10. 2. unperceived, Man. 5, 127. 3. not approved, Man. 8, 153.<BR> II. n. fate, Bhāṣāp. 160; Pañc. v. d. 27. See कु-.<BR> दुस्-, adj. unrighteously decided, Yājñ. 2, 305.<BR> सु-, adj. looked at eagerly, Rām. 1, 17, 23.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. दर्शनीय,<BR> 1. Visible, Rām. 1, 67, 6.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Pañc. iv. d. 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, n. invisibility, Pañc. 138, 40.<BR> II. दृश्य,<BR> 1. Visible, Rām. 4, 40, 64.<BR> 2. To be looked at, Bhartṛ. 1, 86.<BR> 3. Worth to be looked at, Ragh. 6, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. invisible, Rām. 1, 17, 33. 2. ugly, Arj. 10, 66.<BR> III. द्रष्टव्य,<BR> 1. To be seen, etc., MBh. 13, 1404.<BR> 2. Visible, Bhartṛ. 1, 7.<BR> --Caus. दर्शय,<BR> 1. To cause to see, to show (with two accus., or acc. and gen., and acc. and dat.), Rām. 3, 61, 5; Man. 4, 59; Rām. 2, 31, 33.<BR> 2. To point out, Śāk. 12, 19.<BR> 3. To confess, Rājat. 5, 124.<BR> 4. To produce, Man. 8, 158.<BR> 5. To pay, 8, 155.<BR> 6. To prove, 8, 225.<BR> 7. To show one's self, MBh. 1, 4709 (Ātm.); 1, 6561 (Par.). Anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. दर्शयान, MBh. 1, 17. Desider. दिदृक्ष, To wish to see, Bhāg. P. 4, 3, 11.<BR> --Ptcple. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0413-a " target="_blank">Page0413-a + 41</a>] pf. pass. दिदृक्षित, n. Wish to see, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 31.<BR> --With the prep. अनु,<BR> 1. To look afterwards, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 60.<BR> 2. To see, Man. 3, 176.<BR> 3. To look on, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 23.<BR> 4. To regard, to honour, MBh. 15, 679.<BR> 5. To perceive, MBh. 6, 5456.<BR> 6. To know, Bhag. 13, 30.<BR> 7. To find, MBh. 9, 2986.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, Rām. 2, 49, 12.<BR> 2. To teach, Rām. 2, 100, 1.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु,<BR> 1. To look after, Bhāg. P. 5, 21, 9.<BR> 2. To consider, MBh. 1, 5037.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप, pass. To be visible, MBh. 7, 8136.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To look at, MBh. 3, 9982.<BR> 2. To regard, Rām. 2, 30, 2 Gorr.<BR> 3. To perceive, MBh. 1, 5002.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 14, 2151.<BR> 2. To show one's self, MBh. 1, 7740.<BR> --With अव अव, To infer, Bhāg. P. 3, 27, 12.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. To show, Ragh. 4, 38.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To see distinctly, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 6.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To foresee, Megh. 23.<BR> 2. To perceive, Megh. 102.<BR> --Caus. To show one's self, Vikr. 11, 6.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To look on, MBh. 1, 8440.<BR> 2. To perceive, Bhāg. P. 4, 10, 13.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, Hit. 38, 15.<BR> 2. To pretend, Kathās. 19, 75.<BR> --With नि नि, Caus.<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 12, 13222.<BR> 2. To point out, Śāk. 100, 9, v. r.<BR> 3. To enter, Rājat. 1, 18.<BR> 4. To teach, MBh. 12, 2154.<BR> 5. To appear to somebody (acc.), Hariv. 1559.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, Caus. To show, Rām. 4, 63, 15.<BR> --With परि प्रि,<BR> 1. To look at, MBh. 12, 6576.<BR> 2. To frequent, MBh. 15, 1014.<BR> 3. To Rām. 2, 91, 2 Gorr.<BR> 4. To consider Prab. 71, 6.<BR> 5. To search, MBh. 1, 6222.<BR> 6. To know, MBh. 3, 224. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0413-b " target="_blank">Page0413-b + 43</a>]<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To foresee, Bhag.<BR> 2. To be intelligent, MBh. 7, 1057.<BR> 3. To see before one's self, Rām. 1, 60, 27 Gorr.<BR> 4. To see, Man. 8, 85; pass. To appear, Brāhmaṇ. 2, 6.<BR> 5. To behold, Bhag. 11, 49.<BR> 6. To learn, MBh. 9, 1550.<BR> 7. To know, Rām. 5, 3, 63.<BR> 8. To judge, MBh. 3, 1082.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, Rām. 4, 27, 21.<BR> 2. To describe, Man. 10, 40.<BR> 3. To explain, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 10.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To see, MBh. 3, 15050; pass. To appear, Rām. 2, 52, 80 Gorr.<BR> 2. To perceive, Rām. 1, 3, 4.<BR> 3. To consider, MBh. 5, 795.<BR> 4. To know, Rām. 5, 70, 3.<BR> 5. To judge, MBh. 12, 410.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 9, 3280.<BR> 2. To declare, MBh. 6, 571.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To behold, MBh. 3, 12005; pass. To appear, MBh. 5, 4679.<BR> 2. To know, MBh. 5, 2021.<BR> 3. To experience, MBh. 12, 12548.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To discern, to recognise, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 48.<BR> 2. To perceive, Bhāg. P. 9, 8, 22; pass. To appear, Rām. 1, 13, 14 Gorr.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 4, 1844.<BR> 2. To teach, Rām. 2, 29, 7.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To behold, Rām. 2, 54, 3; pass. To appear, Arj. 1, 3.<BR> 2. To recognise, Yājñ. 3, 64.<BR> 3. To look on something (without preventing it), Man. 7, 143.<BR> 4. To review (soldiers), Man. 7, 222.<BR> 5. To regard, MBh. 2, 2623.<BR> 6. To consider, Man. 8, 10.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To show, MBh. 13, 3505.<BR> 2. To represent, Rājat. 6, 244.<BR> 3. To show one's self to somebody (acc.), MBh. 12, 12882.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्, To ponder one by one, MBh. 12, 12024.<BR> --Cf. स्पश and स्पष्ट; O.H.G. spehôn, to spy; Lat. species, conspicio, specto; σκέπτομαι, σκέψις, σκοπός, etc., δέρκω, ἔδρακον, δέδορκα, δράκος, ὑπόδραξ, ὑπόδρα, δράκων, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a " target="_blank">Page0414-a + 41</a>] etc.; O.H.G. in auga-zorht (= दृश् + त, ptcple. of the pf. pass.), A.S. torht; O.H.G. zorhtjan, manifestare; also, with फ़् for ह्, zorft, zorftjan; Goth. ga-tarhjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
2. दृश् दृश्,<BR> I. adj., latter part of comp. adj.<BR> 1. Seeing, e. g. सर्व- Seeing everything, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 9.<BR> 2. Knowing, Bhāg. P. 8, 8, 34.<BR> II. f. 1. Sight, Bhāg. P. 1, 4, 18.<BR> 2. Perception, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 5.<BR> 3. The eye, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यदृश्
दिव्य- + दृश् दिव्य- + दृश्,<BR> I. adj. knowing the celestial phenomena, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 5, 13.<BR> II. m. An astrologer, 54, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदृश्
भाल- + दृश् भाल- + दृश्, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगदृश्
मृग- + दृश् मृग- + दृश्,<BR> I. adj. having eyes like an antelope.<BR> II. f. a woman, Rājat. 5, 481.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगीदृश्
मृगी- + दृश् मृगी- + दृश्, adj. having eyes like a female antelope. Rājat. 5, 375 (a woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदृश्
सम- + दृश् सम- + दृश्, adj. equable, Lass. 6, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदृश्
सु- + दृश् सु- + दृश्,<BR> I. adj. having beautiful eyes.<BR> II. f. a pretty woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशि|दृशिः
दृशि दृश् + इ, f.<BR> 1. Intuition, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 5.<BR> 2. The eye, Bhāg. P. 5, 2, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यत्व
दृश्यत्व दृश्य + त्व (vb. दृश्), n. Visibility, Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्वन्
ऽदृश्वन् -दृश् + वन्, latter part of comp. adj. Conversant with, Kām. Nītis. 1, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्
दृषद् दृषद्, f. A rock, a large stone, especially a mill-stone, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्वती
दृषद्वती दृषद्वती, i. e. दृषद् + वन्त् + ई, f.<BR> 1. The name of a river, Man. 2, 17.<BR> 2. A proper name, Hariv. 1473.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टनष्टता
दृष्टनष्टता दृष्ट-नष्ट + ता (vb. दृश् and 2. नश्), f. Disappearance after having been scarcely seen, Rājat. 4, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्ततस्
दृष्टान्ततस् दृष्टान्ततस्, i. e. दृष्ट-अन्त + त, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-b " target="_blank">Page0414-b + 43</a>] As a precedent, MBh. 13, 2506; 2, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टि|दृष्टिः
दृष्टि दृष्टि, i. e. दृश् + अ f.<BR> 1. Looking at, Rām. 5, 14, 57.<BR> 2. Sight, Pañc. iii. d. 195.<BR> 3. Intelligence, Bhāg. P. 1, 4, 5.<BR> 4. The eye, Mṛcch. 48, 23.<BR> 5. The pupil of the eye, Suśr. 1, 126, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0414-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टि|अदृष्टिः
