देवत्रा
देवत्रा देव + त्रा, adv. Among the gods. Chr. 289, 10 = Rigv. i. 50, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवत्व|देवत्वं
देवत्व देव + त्व, n. The state of deities, Man. 12, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरदेवत्व
नर- + देवत्व नर- + देवत्व, i. e. नर-देव + त्व, n. royalty, Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्त|देवदत्तः
देवदत्त देव-दत्त (vb. दा),<BR> I. adj. Given by the gods, Man. 9, 95.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The conch of Arjuna, Arj. 5, 24.<BR> 2. One of the vital airs, that which is exhaled in yawning, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 16.<BR> 3. A proper name used to denote a person in general, Pañc. 36, 2; Vedāntas. 213, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदारुमय
देवदारुमय देव-दारु + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of Devadāru wood, Rām. 1, 13, 23 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन|देवनं|देवनः
देवन देवन, i. e. दिव् + अन, n. Game at dice, MBh. 2, 2033.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमय
देवमय देव + मय, adj., f. यी, Containing the gods, Hariv. 2798.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर|देवरः
देवर देवर, m. i. e.<BR> 1. देवृ + अ, A husband's brother, but especially his younger brother, Man. 3, 55.<BR> 2. दिव् + अर, A lover, Bhāg. P. 4, 26, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलक|देवलकः
देवलक देव + ल + क, m. A Brāhmaṇa of inferior order, who subsists upon the offerings made to the images which he attends, Man. 3, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसात्
देवसात् देव + सात्, adv. To a god or gods (e. g. turned), MBh. 7, 8687.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवहू
देवहू देवहू, i. e. देव-ह्वे, adj. Invoking the gods, a designation of the left ear, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवापि|देवापिः
देवापि देवापि, m. The name of a Ṛṣi or sage, MBh. 1, 3750.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवितृ
देवितृ देवितृ, i. e. दिव् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A dice-player, MBh. 2, 2005.<BR> 2. A gamester, MBh. 4, 496.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविन्
देविन् देविन्, i. e. दिव् + इन्, adj. A dice-player, a gamester, MBh. 3, 15204; 5, 895.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीक
देवीक देवी + क (see देव), A substitute for देवी when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. स-, With the queen, Kathās. 18, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीत्व
देवीत्व देवी + त्व, n. The dignity,<BR> 1. of a goddess, Kathās. 12, 163;<BR> 2. of a queen, 17, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवृ
देवृ देवृ, m. A husband's brother, but especially his younger brother.<BR> --Cf. δαήρ; Lat. levir; O.H.G. zeihur; A.S. tacur, tacor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेशय|देवेशयः
देवेशय देवेशय, i. e. देव + इ-शी + अ, adj. Reposing in a god, MBh. 12, 12864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश|देशः
देश देश, i. e. दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A place, Man. 2, 222.<BR> 2. A part, a side, Kathās. 18, 280.<BR> 3. A country, Rām. 1, 61, 10.<BR> 4. When latter part of comp. words, often without a special signification, e. g. कण्ठ-देश = कण्ठ, Kathās. 17, 81; नितम्ब-, Ṛt. 1, 6; Rām. 1, 55, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश|अदेशः
अ- + देश अ- + देश, m.<BR> 1. an improper place, Hit. iv. d. 45. 2. a place which ought not to be touched, Man. 8, 358.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदेश|एकदेशः
एक- + देश एक- + देश, m. 1. one place, Pañc. 21, 13. 2. one part, Man. 2, 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूदेश
तनू- + देश तनू- + देश, m. a part of the body, Bhāg. P. 7, 13, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्देश|दिग्देशः
दिश्- + देश दिश्- + देश, pl. a country in this or that direction, distant countries, Hit. 9, 4; cf. Rājat. 4, 417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेश|परदेशः
पर- + देश पर- + देश, m. a foreign country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वदेश|पूर्वदेशः|पूर्व्वदेश|पूर्व्वदेशः
पूर्व- + देश पूर्व- + देश, m. the eastern country, MBh. 2, 1856.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदेश|मध्यदेशः
मध्य- + देश मध्य- + देश, m. the middle region, a part of India, Man. 2, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेश|विदेशः
वि- + देश वि- + देश, m. 1. a foreign country, abroad. 2. any place away from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेश|सदेशः
स- + देश स- + देश, adj. 1. near. 2. of the same country or place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0416-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशक|देशकः
देशक देशक, i. e. दिश् + अक, adj. Showing, teaching, Mārk. P. 19, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशज
देशज देश-ज, and देशजात देश-जात (vb. जन्), adj. Of genuine descent, born in the country whence comes the best kind (e. g. of horses, or elephants), Hariv. 6927; Rām. 1, 54, 21 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशना
देशना देशना, दिश्, Caus., + अन, f. Instruction, doctrine, Śatr. 14, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशान्तरिन्
देशान्तरिन् देशान्तरिन्, i. e. देश-अन्तर + इन्, adj. subst. m. Foreign, a foreigner, Śatr. 10, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिक|देशिकः
देशिक देशिक, i. e. देश + इक, m.<BR> 1. A guide, MBh. 7, 143.<BR> 2. A teacher, 13, 6847.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिनी
देशिनी देशिनी, i. e. दिश् + इन् + ई, f. The index or forefinger, Yājñ. 1, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशीय
देशीय देशीय, i. e. देश + ईय, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to a country or province.<BR> 2. Latter part of comp. adj. Bordering, being about, e. g. पञ्च(न्)-वर्ष + क-, About five years old, MBh. 12, 1119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्य|देश्यं|देश्यः
देश्य देश्य, i. e. देश + य,<BR> 1. adj. subst. A witness, Man. 8, 52.<BR> 2. adj. Belonging to a country, Rājat. 3, 9.<BR> 3. adj. Of genuine descent, Rām. 2, 72, 23 Gorr. (cf. देशज).<BR> 4. adj. Being almost, e. g. शिशु-, Being almost still a child, Rājat. 5, 220.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश्य
अ- + देश्य अ- + देश्य, adj. one who has not been present at a place, Man. 8, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्देश्य
तद्- + देश्य तद्- + देश्य, adj. being of the same country, MBh. 12, 6305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानादेश्य
नाना- + देश्य नाना- + देश्य, adj. belonging to or coming from several countries, MBh. 1, 5221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देष्टृ
देष्टृ देष्टृ, i. e. दिश् + तृ, m. One who shows, Bhāg. P. 6, 7, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देह|देहं|देहः
देह देह, i. e. दिह् + अ, m. and n. The body, Man. 6, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वदेह|ऊर्ध्वदेहः
ऊर्ध्व- + देह ऊर्ध्व- + देह, n. obsequies, Rām. 2, 90, 37 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वदेह|पूर्व्वदेह
पूर्व- + देह पूर्व- + देह, m. a former existence, Hariv. 9153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहंभर
देहंभर देहंभर, i. e. देह + म्-भृ + अ, adj. Minding only one's own body, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहली
देहली देहली, i. e. दिह् + अल + ई, f. The threshold of a door, or a raised terrace in front of it, Megh. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहवन्त्|देहवत्
देहवन्त् देह + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Embodied, Rām. 6, 90, 44.<BR> II. m. A living creature, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहिन्
देहिन् देहिन्, i. e. देह + इन्,<BR> I. adj. subst. Embodied, a creature having a body, Man. 1, 30.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A man, Bhartṛ. 2, 18.<BR> 2. The soul, Bhag. 2, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दै
दै दै, i. 1, Par. To purify.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, ptcple. of the pf. pass. अवदात,<BR> 1. Pure, Lass. 67, 3.<BR> 2. White or yellow, Sāv. 5, 8.<BR> 3. Dazzling white, MBh. 5, 1794.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव, pass. To spread, shining with clear light, Daśak. 55, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैतेय|दैतेयः
दैतेय दैतेय, i. e. दिति + एय,<BR> 1. m An Asura or demon, Rām. 1, 45, 38.<BR> 2. adj., f. यी, Referring, belonging to the Asuras, MBh. 12, 7544.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैतेय
अ- + दैतेय अ- + दैतेय, m. a god, Hariv. 11139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्य|दैत्यः
दैत्य दैत्य, i. e. दिति + य, m. An Asura or demon, Man. 12, 48; Rām. 1, 30, 20 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैन्य|दैन्यं
दैन्य दैन्य, i. e. दीन (see 3. दी) + य, n.<BR> 1. Affliction, Rām. 6, 89, 17.<BR> 2. Humbleness, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR> 3. Miserable state, Megh. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैर्घ्य|दैर्घ्यं
दैर्घ्य दैर्घ्य, i. e. दीर्घ + य, n. Length, MBh. 6, 427.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव|दैवं|दैवः
दैव दैव, i. e. देव + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. वी.<BR> 1. Divine, Man. 1, 67.<BR> 2. (with and without विवाह), m. One of the forms of marriage, the gift of a daughter at a sacrifice to the officiating priest, Man. 3, 21; 9, 196.<BR> 3. n. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0418-a " target="_blank">Page0418-a + 42</a>] part of the hand sacred to the gods (the tips of the fingers), Man. 2, 59.<BR> 4. Royal, Rājat. 5, 205.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Deity, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 4.<BR> 2. An oblation to the gods, Man. 3, 18.<BR> 3. Divine power, destiny, fate, Man. 3, 166; Hit. pr. d. 32; Daśak. in Chr. 187, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदैव|अधिदैवं
अधि- + दैव अधि- + दैव, n. 1. the supreme deity, Bhag. 8, 4. 2. a tutelary deity, Śāk. 7, 10, v. r. कुल-, n. 1. the fortune of a family, Bhāg. P. 9, 5, 9. 2. the deity of a family, 9, 9, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दैव|दुर्द्दैव
दुस्- + दैव दुस्- + दैव, n. misfortune, Lass. 74, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवक|दैवकः
