दोष|दोषः
दोष दोष, i. e. दुष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Defect, blemish, Hariv. 2108; Man. 8, 205.<BR> 2. Fault, vice, MBh. 5, 1048.<BR> 3. Damage, Yājñ. 2, 256.<BR> 4. Sin, Man. 5, 3.<BR> 5. Crime, Man. 9, 262.<BR> 6. Reproach, Rām. 2, 101, 32 Gorr.; दोषेण [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0419-a " target="_blank">Page0419-a + 42</a>] गम्, To accuse, Chr. 16, 14.<BR> 7. Detrimental operation, Kathās. 13, 35.<BR> 8. Effect, Rām. 3, 79, 25.<BR> 9. Disorder of the humours of the body, or defect in the functions of bile, phlegm, and wind, Suśr. 2, 562, 4.<BR> 10. The humours of the body, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 4.<BR> 11. Evening, darkness, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δειελός, δείλη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0418-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

