द्यु|द्युः
1. द्यु द्यु, ii. 2, Par. To attack.<BR> --Cf. दिव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यु|द्युः
2. द्यु द्यु, the base of many cases and derivatives of 3. दिव्, and its substitute when former part of a comp. word, e. g. द्यु-चर, m. An inhabitant of the heaven, Hariv. 7497. द्यु-जय, m. Attainment of heaven, Bhāg. P. 5, 19, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत्
1. द्युत् द्युत् (originally a denomin.. probably of द्युति), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 12, 8129), To shine, MBh. 3, 1745.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To illuminate, MBh. 4, 2031.<BR> 2. To hint, Sāh. D. 20, 2.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To illuminate, Ragh. 6, 36.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To beam, Hariv. 15701.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To illuminate, Prab. 86, 11.<BR> 2. To make glorious, Ragh. 10, 81.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To shine, Prab. 115, 2.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To illuminate, Prab. 116, 1.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To flash, MBh. 3, 180.<BR> 2. To illuminate, MBh. 12, 8063.<BR> --Caus. To illuminate, MBh. 1, 1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत्
2. द्युत् द्युत्, f. Splendour, MBh. 1, 6406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0421-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युति|द्युतिः
