द्रव|द्रवः
द्रव द्रव, i. e. द्रु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Running (ved.).<BR> 2. Liquid, Hariv. 12333.<BR> 3. n. A liquid substance, Man. 5, 115.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Quick motion, Hariv. 11430.<BR> 2. Flight, 12567.<BR> 3. Fluidity, Bhāṣāp. 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतद्रव|अमृतद्रवः
अमृत- + द्रव अमृत- + द्रव, adj., f. वा, flowing with Amṛta (and medicaments), Śiś. 9, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवता
द्रवता द्रव + ता, f. Wetness, Śiś. 9, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवत्व|द्रवत्वं
द्रवत्व द्रव + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Fluidity, Bhāṣāp. 153 (˚त्व + क in 30).<BR> 2. Fusibility, Hit. i. d. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविड|द्रविडः
द्रविड द्रविड, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, MBh. 14, 832.<BR> 2. The son of a Vrātya or degraded Kṣatriya, Man. 10, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविण|द्रविणं
द्रविण द्रविण (akin to द्रव्य and probably to 3. द्रु),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Wealth, Man. 7, 136.<BR> 2. Money, Rājat. 5, 167.<BR> 3. Strength, Rām. 1, 16, 15.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. pl. Wealth, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 12.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 1, 2585.<BR> 3. The name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 15.<BR> 4. The name of the inhabitants of a Varṣa or division of the world, 5, 20, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणवन्त्|द्रविणवत्
द्रविणवन्त् द्रविण + वन्त्, adj. Strong, MBh. 5, 3889.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्य|द्रव्यं
द्रव्य द्रव्य (probably akin to 3. द्रु), n.<BR> 1. Object, thing, Man. 1, 113; 8, 34.<BR> 2. Substance, Bhāṣāp. 1.<BR> 3. Property, Man. 4, 114.<BR> 4. A fit object.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्य|अद्रव्यं
अ- + द्रव्य अ- + द्रव्य, n. a worthless object, Hit. pr. d. 43; Mālav. 14, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्य|अपद्रव्यं
अप- + द्रव्य अप- + द्रव्य, n. any bad substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्रव्य
निस्- + द्रव्य निस्- + द्रव्य, adj. 1. immaterial, MBh. 12, 11350. 2. poor, Rām. 5, 33, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताद्रव्य
सीता- + द्रव्य सीता- + द्रव्य, n. pl. implements of husbandry, Man. 9, 293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यत्व
द्रव्यत्व द्रव्य + त्व, n. Substantiality, Bhāṣāp. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यमय
द्रव्यमय द्रव्य + मय, adj., f. यी, Substantial, Bhāg. P. 4, 14, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यवन्त्|द्रव्यवत्
द्रव्यवन्त् द्रव्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Wealthy, Rām. 2, 49, 26 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टुकाम
द्रष्टुकाम द्रष्टुकाम, i. e. द्रष्टुम् (infinitive of दृश्) -काम, adj. Desirous of seeing, Sund. 3, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टुशक्य
द्रष्टुशक्य द्रष्टुशक्य, Indr. 2, 6, read द्रष्तुं शक्य, MBh. 3, 1761.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टृ
द्रष्टृ द्रष्टृ, i. e. द्रिश् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. One who sees, MBh. 3, 12623.<BR> 2. One who decides, Yājñ. 2, 202.<BR> 3. A judge, Mṛcch. 137, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टृत्व
द्रष्टृत्व द्रष्टृ + त्व, n. The faculty of seeing, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रा
1. द्रा द्रा, ii. 2. Par. To run.<BR> --Caus. द्रापय. Anomal. frequent. दरिद्रा, To be in distress, to be poor, Hit. ii. d. 2.<BR> --Cf. διδράσκω, ἔδραν, δραπέτης (from the Causal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रा
2. द्रा द्रा, ii. 2, and द्रै द्रै, i. 1, द्रा + य (properly द्रा, i. 4), Par. (also Ātm. Mṛcch. 116, 10), To sleep.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, To fall asleep, MBh. 13, 7568; 7418.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. निद्राण, Sleeping, Rājat. 2, 165.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. traum; O.S. drôm; O.H.G. denomin. traumjan; O.S. drômjan, to dream; Lat. dormire (a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a " target="_blank">Page0423-a + 40</a>] denomin. based on dor + mo), δαρθάνω, ἔδαρθον and ἔδραθον (also a denomin. based on δαρ + tvan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0422-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्
द्राक् द्राक्, i. e. 1. द्रा-अञ्च्, acc. sing. ntr. adv. Soon, instantly, Pañc. 4, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्षा
द्राक्षा द्राक्षा, f.<BR> 1. A vine, Hariv. 6407.<BR> 2. A grape, Gīt. 12, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राख्
† द्राख् द्राख्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To become dry.<BR> 2. To be sufficient; cf. ध्राख्.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. trukan; A.S. drig, dryg, drí.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघ्
† द्राघ् द्राघ्, i. 1, Ātm. (probably a denomin. derived from दीर्घ, comparat. द्राघीयंस्, etc.),<BR> 1. To lengthen.<BR> 2. To exert one's self, to be tired.<BR> 3. To be able.<BR> 4. To torment.<BR> 5. To stroll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघय
द्राघय द्राघय, a denomin. derived from दीर्घ, comparat. द्राघीयंस्, Par.<BR> 1. To extend, Rājat. 4, 513.<BR> 2. To lengthen, Bhaṭṭ. 18, 33.<BR> 3. To tarry, Rām. 2, 109, 14 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिष्ठ|द्राघिष्ठः
द्राघिष्ठ द्राघिष्ठ, and द्राघीयंस् द्राघीयंस्, see दीर्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राड्
द्राड् द्राड्, i. 1, Ātm. To divide, to split.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, Caus. To split, Śatr. 14, 44 (perhaps faulty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावण|द्रावणं
द्रावण द्रावण, i. e. द्रु, Caus. + अन,<BR> I. adj. Putting to flight, MBh. 8, 1523.<BR> II. n. Putting to flight, Hariv. 7583.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविड|द्राविडः
द्राविड द्राविड, i. e. द्रविड + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. डी, Belonging to the Draviḍas, MBh. 8, 454.<BR> II. m. pl. = Draviḍa, MBh. 1, 6683.<BR> III. f. डी, Cardamom, Suśr. 1, 142, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राह्
† द्राह् द्राह्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To wake.<BR> 2. To cast down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
1. द्रु द्रु (akin to द्रम्, 1. द्रा), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., MBh. 6, 4710),<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-b " target="_blank">Page0423-b + 40</a>] To run, MBh. 8, 3014.<BR> 2. To attack, MBh. 1, 5478.<BR> 3. To melt, Lass. 24, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. द्रुत,<BR> 1. Swift, MBh. 13, 1839<BR> 2. Flown, Ṛt. 1, 20.<BR> 3. Running away, Bhāg. P. 4, 17, 14.<BR> 4. Molten, Śiś. 9, 9. ˚तम्, adv. Instantly, Man. 9, 272. Comparat. द्रुत + तर + म्, adv. As quickly as possible, Pañc. 25, 15.<BR> --Caus. द्रावय, To put to flight, MBh. 4, 1082. Anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. द्रावयाण, MBh. 6, 5199.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To pursue, Bhāg. P. 4, 19, 16. अनुद्रुत,<BR> 1. Pursued, Ragh. 3, 38.<BR> 2. Accompanied, Rām. 2, 65, 26.<BR> 3. Pursuing, Bhāg. P. 3, 18, 7.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To pursue, MBh. 10, 657; to follow, 14, 636.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To run on, MBh. 1, 6000.<BR> 2. To attack, Arj. 7, 1.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि,<BR> 1. To assail, MBh. 6, 1953.<BR> 2. To infest, MBh. 18, 46. समभिद्रुत + म्, adv. Quickly, 12, 6402.<BR> --With आ आ, To hasten on, MBh. 3, 248.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, To pursue, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 17.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, To hasten on round about, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 13.<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ,<BR> 1. To run away, MBh. 1, 2843.<BR> 2. To escape, 1, 6127.<BR> --With संप्रा सम्-प्र-आ, To run away, MBh. 9, 1675 (perhaps only सम्-प्र).<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To assail, MBh. 7, 5292.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To assail, MBh. 2, 815.<BR> --With उप उप, To assail, Pañc. 147, 1. उपद्रुत,<BR> 1. Assailed, Hariv. 1151.<BR> 2. Distressed, Rām. 2, 48, 22.<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, To rush on, Pañc. 226, 23.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप,<BR> 1. To run on, MBh. 3, 10993.<BR> 2. To assail, Rām. 4, 48, 29.<BR> --With परा [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-a " target="_blank">Page0424-a + 41</a>] परा. To run away, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 18.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To press on, Arj. 6, 8.<BR> 2. To run away, MBh. 3, 8749.<BR> 3. To hasten to, Rām. 1, 20, 6.<BR> 4. To attain, Brāhmaṇ. 1, 19. प्रद्रुत, Run away, Rām. 2, 97, 9.<BR> --Caus. To put to flight, MBh. 8, 2424.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To assail, MBh. 9, 398.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र,<BR> 1. To run in different directions, to disperse, Rām. 2, 102, 1 Gorr.<BR> 2. To run away, MBh. 3, 861. विप्रद्रुत, Run away, MBh. 3, 675.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To run away, MBh. 3, 239.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To run to, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 17.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To run in different directions, MBh. 3, 2549.<BR> 2. To run away, MBh. 4, 163.<BR> 3. To burst, MBh. 13, 7472. विद्रुत,<BR> 1. Run in different directions, Sund. 4, 20.<BR> 2. Run away, Draup. 8, 35.<BR> 3. Burst, Man. 7, 3.<BR> 4. Dissolved, i. e. destroyed, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 49.<BR> 5. Unsteady, Pañc. 203, 3.<BR> --Caus. To put to flight, MBh. 1, 6680.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि,<BR> 1. To assail, MBh. 6, 1776.<BR> 2. To run away, MBh. 6, 4614.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, प्रविद्रुत, Run away, MBh. 7, 4865.<BR> --Cf. Lat. gruere in in-gruere etc., and ruere; probably O.H.G. triufan; A.S. driopan (an old Causal); O.H.G. trofo; A.S. dropa; O.H.G. trauf, traufi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0423-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
2. द्रु द्रु, ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt.<BR> 2. † To repent, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
3. द्रु द्रु. i. e. दृ + उ,<BR> I. m. and n. Wood, Man. 7, 131.<BR> II. m. A tree.<BR> --Cf. δρῦς, δρύτη, δροίτη; Got. triu; A.S. tre, a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुड्
† द्रुड् द्रुड्. i. 1 and 6. Par. To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुण्
† द्रुण् द्रुण्. i. e. Par.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b " target="_blank">Page0424-b + 42</a>] make crooked.<BR> 2. To go.<BR> 3. To hurt; cf. 2. द्रु and द्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुपद|द्रुपदः
द्रुपद द्रुपद, m. The name of a king, Man. 1, 2453.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुम|द्रुमः
द्रुम 3. द्रु + म, m.<BR> 1. A tree, Man. 9, 255.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 1, 227.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δρῡμός, δρῡ̆μά.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पद्रुम|कल्पद्रुमः
कल्प- + द्रुम कल्प- + द्रुम, m. a fabulous tree fulfilling all wishes, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामद्रुम|ग्रामद्रुमः
ग्राम- + द्रुम ग्राम- + द्रुम and चैत्य-, m. a sacred tree growing in a village or near it, and held in veneration by the villagers, Hiḍ. 1, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाद्रुम|छायाद्रुमः
छाया- + द्रुम छाया- + द्रुम, m. very shady tree, Śāk. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्वतवनद्रुम
स-पर्वत-वन- + द्रुम स-पर्वत-वन- + द्रुम, adj. with (its) mountains, forests, and trees, Chr. 40, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमवन्त्|द्रुमवत्
द्रुमवन्त् द्रुम-वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Woody, MBh. 7, 782.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमाय
द्रुमाय द्रुमाय, a denomin. derived from द्रुम by य, Ātm. To pass for a tree, Hit. i. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह्
1. द्रुह् द्रुह्, i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 75, 22),<BR> 1. To hurt, Rām. 2, 25, 17.<BR> 2. To seek to injure or to grieve, Man. 2, 144. With the dat., Bhāg. P. 4, 4, 15; with the gen., Rām. 2, 99, 23 Gorr.; with the loc., Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 21; and with the acc., MBh. 2, 2107.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. द्रुग्ध, Wished to be injured, Rājat. 5, 298.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To hurt, Bhāg. P. 4, 20, 3.<BR> 2. To seek to hurt, Pañc. i. d. 270, with the dat. and acc. अभिद्रुग्ध, Seeking to injure, MBh. 5, 2160.<BR> --With वि वि, To insult, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 41.<BR> --Cf. Goth. driugan (द् instead of त् on account of the following र्), dulgs; O.H.G. triugan (see द्रोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुग्ध
अ-द्रुग्ध अ-द्रुग्ध, adj. innoccnt, MBh. 5, 715.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह्
2. द्रुह् द्रुह्,<BR> 1. m. An injurer, MBh. 7, 6512.<BR> 2. Latter part of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a " target="_blank">Page0425-a + 41</a>] adj., Injuring, having injured, e. g. गर्भ-भर्तृ-, f. A woman who has caused an abortion or stricken her husband, Man. 5, 90. मित्र-, n. An injurer of his friend, Man. 3, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0424-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रू
द्रू द्रू, ii. 9, Par. To go, to hurt.<BR> --Cf. 2. द्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक्
द्रेक् द्रेक्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To increase (?).<BR> 3. To show pride (?).<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, To begin to neigh, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रै
द्रै द्रै, see 2. द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोग्धृ
द्रोग्धृ द्रोग्धृ, i. e. द्रुह् + तृ, m. An injurer, MBh. 5, 2124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोण|द्रोणः
द्रोण द्रोण, probably द्रु + वन् (त्) + अ,<BR> I. n. A wooden tub, MBh. 1, 5105.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. A measure of capacity, = आढक, Man. 7, 126.<BR> 2. A cloud abounding in water, Mṛcch. 163, 8.<BR> III. m. A proper name, the military preceptor of the Pāṇḍus and Kurus, MBh. 1, 2434.<BR> IV. f. णी.<BR> 1. A wooden tub, Hariv. 3866.<BR> 2. A valley, Bhāg. P. 4, 10, 5; Rājat. 5, 141.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहद्रोण
सह-द्रोण सह-द्रोण, adj. with Droṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानद्रोणी
स्नान-द्रोणी स्नान-द्रोणी, f. a bathing-tub, Rājat. 5, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणमय
द्रोणमय द्रोण + मय, adj. Full of Droṇas (द्रोण<BR> III.), MBh. 7, 936.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोह|द्रोहः
द्रोह द्रोह, i. e. द्रुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Injury, Pañc. 45, 25.<BR> 2. Insidious wounding, Man. 7, 48.<BR> 3. Perfidy, Rājat. 4, 410.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोह|अद्रोहः
अ- + द्रोह अ- + द्रोह, n. 1. absence of injury, Man. 4, 2. 2. kindness, Sāv. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्रोह
निस्- + द्रोह निस्- + द्रोह, adj. 1. not hostile, Rājat. 1, 362. 2. innocent, 5, 208. 3. Well disposed, 6, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहिन्
द्रोहिन् द्रोहिन्, i. e.<BR> I. द्रुह् + इन्, latter part of comp. adj. Injuring, Rām. 3, 16, 34.<BR> II. द्रोह + इन्, adj. Perfidious, Rājat. 1, 1362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौणायनि|द्रौणायनिः
द्रौणायनि द्रौणायनि, i. e. द्रोण + आयनि, and द्राणि द्रौणि, i. e. द्रोण + इ, patron. A son of Droṇa, MBh. 1, 7019; 4, 1150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौणिक|द्रौणिकः
द्रौणिक द्रौणिक, i. e. द्रोण + इक,<BR> I. adj., f. की, Containing a Droṇa (see द्रोण<BR> II.), e. g. पञ्चद्रौणिक, i. e. पञ्चन्-द्रोण + इक, Containing five Droṇas, MBh. 2, 2091.<BR> II. (m. or n.), A field which may be sown with a Droṇa of grain, Kathās. 3, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौपद
द्रौपद द्रौपद, i. e. द्रुपद + अ, patron., f. दी, The daughter of Drupada, the common wife of the five Pāṇḍu princes, MBh. 1, 2791.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौपदेय|द्रौपदेयः
द्रौपदेय द्रौपदेय, i. e. द्रौपदि + एय, metronym. A son of Draupadī, MBh. 1, 429.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वंद्व|द्वन्द्व|द्वंद्वं|द्वन्द्वं|द्वन्द्वः
द्वंद्व द्वंद्व, i. e. द्व + म्-द्व (+ म्, old sing. ntr. of द्वि, twice repeated), n. A pair, a couple, Megh. 46.<BR> 2. A pair of opposite things, as heat and cold, Man. 1, 26.<BR> 3. Quarrel, contest, MBh. 12, 7557.<BR> 4. A duel, MBh. 5, 7083.<BR> 5. Doubt, MBh. 1, 1867.<BR> 6. A class of comp. words, Bhag. 10, 33. Acc. sing. ˚द्वम्, and instr. ˚द्वेन, adv. Two by two. Hariv. 3754; Bhāg. P. 8, 10, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्वंद्व|निर्द्वन्द्व
निस्- + द्वंद्व निस्- + द्वंद्व, adj. 1. indifferent in regard to the opposite pairs, as pleasure and pain, etc. (cf. Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 17), Bhag. 2, 45. 2. independent, MBh. 12, 489. 3. free from jealousy, MBh. 3, 14734. 4. uncontested, MBh. 4, 889.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वंद्वचर|द्वन्द्वचर|द्वन्द्वचरः
द्वंद्वचर द्वंद्व-चर, m. The ruddy goose, Anas casarca Gm., Ragh. 8, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वंद्वशस्
द्वंद्वशस् द्वंद्व + शस्, adv. Two by two, Rām. 2, 103, 11 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0425-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वंद्विन्
द्वंद्विन् द्वंद्विन्, i. e. द्वंद्व + इन्, adj. Contradictory, Prab. 86, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वय|द्वयं
द्वय द्वय, i. e. द्वि + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. यी, Of two different sorts, Bhartṛ. 2, 25.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A pair, Yājñ. 1, 59.<BR> 2. Two things, Bhartṛ. 1, 53.<BR> 3. Both, MBh. 12, 6552.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δοιός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अ- + द्वय अ- + द्वय, adj. without a second, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वा
द्वाऽ द्वा. (old nom. du. of द्वि), former part in comp. numerals, Two, e. g. द्वा-चत्वारिंशत्, Forty-two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थ|द्वाःस्थः
द्वाःस्थ द्वाःस्थ, i. e. द्वार्-स्थ,<BR> I. adj. Standing at the door, Rām. 2, 71, 30.<BR> II. m. A porter, Rām. 6, 8, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादश|द्वादशः
द्वादश द्वा-दश,<BR> I. ordin. numb., f. शी, Twelfth, Man. 2, 36; 7, 130.<BR> II. f. शी, The twelfth day of the half-month, Kathās. 26, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशक
द्वादशक द्वादश + क, adj.<BR> 1. Twelfth, MBh. 12, 11955.<BR> 2. Amounting to twelve, Man. 8, 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशधा
द्वादशधा द्वादशधा, i. e. द्वादशन् + धा, adv. Twelve fold, Bhāg. P. 5, 22, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशन्
द्वादशन् द्वा-दशन्, numeral, Twelve, Man. 5, 134.<BR> --Cf. δυώδεκα, δώδεκα; Lat. duodecim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशिक
द्वादशिक द्वादशिक, i. e. द्वादशन् + इक, adj. Taking place on the twelfth day of the half-month, Rām. 2, 86, 1 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वापर|द्वापरं|द्वापरः
द्वापर द्वा-पर, n.<BR> 1. The die which is marked with two points, MBh. 4, 1578.<BR> 2. The third of the four युगस् or great periods, Man. 9, 391.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार्
द्वार् द्वार् (vb. द्वृ), f.<BR> 1. A door, a gate, Man. 3, 88.<BR> 2. Opportunity, Mṛcch. 138, 1.<BR> 3. A means; instr, द्वारा, as latter part of comp. words, By, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार|द्वारं
द्वार द्वार, i. e. द्वृ + अ, n.<BR> 1. A door, a gate, Man. 9, 289.<BR> 2. A way, MBh. 7, 1526.<BR> 3. A means, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 1; instr. द्वारेण, as latter part of comp. words,<BR> 1. By, Pañc. i. d. 52.<BR> 2. By means of, Pañc. 166, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. θύρα, θαιρός; Lat. foras, foris, fores; Goth. daur; A.S. duru, dyr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वार|अद्वारं
अ- + द्वार अ- + द्वार, n. any other entrance than the door, Man. 4, 73; not a door, MBh. 13, 4749.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाद्वार|गंगाद्वार
गङ्गा- + द्वार गङ्गा- + द्वार, n. the locality where the Gaṅgā, leaving the mountains, enters the plains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलद्वार
गल- + द्वार गल- + द्वार, n. the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिद्वार
गिरि- + द्वार गिरि- + द्वार, n. a mountain-pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वार|पक्षद्वारं
पक्ष- + द्वार पक्ष- + द्वार, n. a side-door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृद्द्वार|शकृद्द्वारं
शकृद्द्वार शकृद्द्व्˚, i. e. शकृत्-, n. the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहद्वार|सिंहद्वारं
सिंह- + द्वार सिंह- + द्वार, n. a gate, especially the chief gate of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारक|द्वारकः
द्वारक द्वार + क,<BR> I. n. A gate, MBh. 12, 2639.<BR> II. f. का, The name of Kṛṣṇa's residence, MBh. 1, 7899.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारता
द्वारता द्वार + ता, f. Access, Ragh. 11, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारवती
द्वारवती द्वारवती, i. e. अवर + वन्त् + ई, f. The name of Kṛṣṇa's residence, Rām. 4, 43, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारस्थ|द्वारस्थः
द्वारस्थ द्वार-स्थ,<BR> I. adj., f. था, Standing at the door, Pañc. 198, 11.<BR> II. m. A perter, Pañc. 15, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारिक|द्वारिकः
द्वारिक द्वारिक, i. e. द्वार + इक, and द्वारिन् द्वारिन्, i. e. द्वर + इन्, m. A porter, Pañc. iii. d. 85; MBh. 1, 4906.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वि|द्विः
द्वि द्वि, the base of the declension is द्व, m. n.; द्वा, f.; du. numeral,<BR> 1. Two.<BR> 2. Both, Rām. 6, 95, 44.<BR> --Cf. δύο, δυάκις,, etc., δεύτερος, δί-τυλος, διά, δίζω; Lat. duo, bi-farius, dubius, duellum, bellum, dis-; Goth. tvai; A.S. tvá, twi-, tweogan; Goth. tveifljan, tvi-standan, dis-dailjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विक|द्विकं|द्विकः
द्विक द्वि + क,<BR> I. adj. Increased by [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0427-a " target="_blank">Page0427-a + 39</a>] two, Man. 8, 141 (two in the hundred).<BR> II. (n.) A pair, Rājat. 1, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0426-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

