द्वैधीभाव द्वैधीभाव, i. e. द्वैध-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Duality, MBh. 14, 809.<BR> 2. Doubt, MBh. 7, 1211.<BR> 3. Uncertainty, Śāk. 15, 11.<BR> 4. Duplicity, Pañc. iii. d. 59.<BR> 5. Division of an army, Man. 7, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध्य|द्वैध्यं
द्वैध्य द्वैध्य, i. e. द्विधा + य, n. Duplicity.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैध्य
अ- + द्वैध्य अ- + द्वैध्य, adj. sincere, Kām. Nītis. 4, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपक्ष|द्वैपक्षं
द्वैपक्ष द्वैपक्ष, i. e. द्वि-पक्ष + अ, n. Two parties, MBh. 8, 4432.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपायन|द्वैपायनः
द्वैपायन द्वैपायन, i. e.<BR> 1. द्वीप + आयन, m. A name of Vyāsa, MBh. 1, 2416.<BR> 2. द्वैपायन + अ, adj. Referring to Vyāsa, MBh. 9, 1743.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातुर|द्वैमातुरः
द्वैमातुर द्वैमातुर, i. e. द्वि-मातृ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Having different mothers, Rājat. 4, 355.<BR> 2. Having another mother, 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरथ|द्वैरथं|द्वैरथः
द्वैरथ द्वैरथ, i. e. द्वि-रथ + अ,<BR> I. adj. combined with युद्ध, and subst. n. without युद्ध, A single fight in chariots, Rām. 6, 86, 27; MBh. 4, 1061.<BR> II. m. An adversary, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैराज्य|द्वैराज्यं
द्वैराज्य द्वैराज्य, i. e. द्वि-राजन् + य. n. A dominion divided between two princes, Mālav. 69, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैविध्य|द्वैविध्यं
द्वैविध्य द्वैविध्य, i. e. द्वि-विध + य (see विधा), n.<BR> 1. Duality, twofold character, Bhāṣāp. 141.<BR> 2. Duplicity, MBh. 15, 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्क्
† धक्क् धक्क्, i. 10, Par. To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धट|धटः
धट धट (probably a dialectical form of धर्तृ, based on the nom. sing. धर्ता), m. The scale of a balance, Mit. 140, 1, below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धण्
† धण् धण्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --Cf. ध्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्
1. धन् धन् (cf. धन्व्), f. †, Par.<BR> 1. To put in motion (ved.).<BR> 2. † To bear or produce grains, etc.<BR> --Caus. धनय, To put in motion, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्
2. धन् धन्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --Cf. ध्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन धन, n.<BR> 1. Property of any description, chattels, Man. 8, 201.<BR> 2. A gift, Man. 3, 138.<BR> 3. Gold, money, Man. 3, 6; Rām. 1, 5, 5.<BR> 4. Abundance in, Man. 2, 155.<BR> 5. Cattle, Hariv. 3886.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably εῦ-θενής.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन
अ- + धन अ- + धन, adj., f. ना. 1. having no property, Man. 8, 416. 2. poor, Rām. 1, 15, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धन
अन्तर्- + धन अन्तर्- + धन, n. an inward treasure, Bhartṛ. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्धन|अलंधन
अलम्- + धन अलम्- + धन, adj. having a sufficient property, Man. 8, 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पधन
अल्प- + धन अल्प- + धन, adj. possessing little wealth, Man. 3, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याधन
कन्या- + धन कन्या- + धन, n. dowry, Rām. 1, 74, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधन|गोधनं|गोधनः
गो- + धन गो- + धन, n. 1. property in cattle, MBh. 4, 1504. 2. a station of cowherds, Rām. 2, 32, 42 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोधन|तपोधनः
तपोधन तपोधन, i. e. तपस्-, adj., f. ना. 1. devout; subst. m. an ascetic, Man. 11, 241. 2. Consisting in devotion, MBh. 13, 2727.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धन|निर्धनः
निस्- + धन निस्- + धन, adj. poor, Bhartṛ. 2, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महा
महा महा,<BR> I. adj. 1. rich. 2. valuable.<BR> II. n. 1. (ved.) battle, Chr. 297, 17 = Rigv. i. 112, 17. 2. gold. 3. incense. 4. costly raiment. 5. agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याधन|विद्याधनं
विद्या- + धन विद्या- + धन, n. property acquired by learning, Man. 9, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधन
सत्य- + धन सत्य- + धन, adj. sincere, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a " target="_blank">Page0430-a + 40</a>] virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन
सु- + धन सु- + धन, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतधन
हृत- + धन हृत- + धन (vb. हृ), adj. spoiled of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनंजय|धनञ्जय|धनंजयः|धनञ्जयः
धनंजय धनंजय, धन + म्-जि + अ,<BR> I. adj. Conquering booty, MBh. 9, 2665.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One of the five vital airs, that which is supposed to fatten, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 16.<BR> 2. A name of Arjuna, MBh. 1, 2444.<BR> 3. One of the Nāgas or infernal serpents, MBh. 1, 1550.<BR> 4. A proper name, MBh. 2, 1238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनद|धनदः
धनद धन-द,<BR> I. adj. Liberal, Kām. Nītis. 3, 23.<BR> II. m. A name of Kuvera, Rām. 3, 39, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनवन्त्|धनवत्
धनवन्त् धन + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Wealthy, Man. 3, 40.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. dives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसा
धनसा धनसा i. e. धन-सन्, Conquering booty, Chr. 296, 7 = Rigv. i. 112, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्थ
धनस्थ धन-स्थ, adj. Wealthy, MBh. 12, 3331.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्पृत्
धनस्पृत् धन-स्पृ + त्, adj. Conquering booty, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाय
धनाय धनाय, a denomin. derived from धन by य, Par., Ātm. To be desirous of (with gen.), MBh. 5, 4510.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिक|धनिकः
धनिक धनिक i. e. धन + इक,<BR> I. adj. Wealthy, Pañc. 229, 1.<BR> II. m. A creditor, Man. 8, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिन्
धनिन् धनिन् i. e. धन + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Wealthy, Man. 8, 179.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A creditor, Man. 8, 61.<BR> 2. An owner, Man. 8, 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठा
धनिष्ठा धनिष्ठा, f. The name of a Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, MBh. 13, 4266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनु|धनुः
धनु धनु (a curtailed form of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b " target="_blank">Page0430-b + 41</a>] धनुस्), m.<BR> 1. A bow, Hit. pr. d. 22.<BR> 2. A measure of length, MBh. 8, 4224.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधनु
स- + धनु स- + धनु, adj. with a bow (in his hand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्क
ऽधनुष्क -धनुष्क, i. e. धनुस् + क, a substitute for धनुस् when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. स-, adj. Having a bow or bows, MBh. 2, 2699.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्मत्ता
धनुष्मत्ता धनुष्मत्ता i. e. धनुस् + मन्त् + ता, f. Archery, Bhartṛ. 1, 13 (thus to be read).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्मन्त्|धनुष्मत्
धनुष्मन्त् धनुष्मन्त् i. e. धनुस् + मन्त्,<BR> I. adj. Bearing a bow, Draup. 2, 8.<BR> II. m. An archer, Pañc. i. d. 219.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधनुष्मन्त्|महाधनुष्मत्
महा- + धनुष्मन्त् महा- + धनुष्मन्त्, m. a mighty archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस् धनुस् i. e. probably हन् + वन्त् (akin to धन्वन्),<BR> I. adj. Armed with a bow, MBh. 7, 9536.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A bow, Man. 3, 160.<BR> 2. A measure of length, Man. 8, 237.<BR> 3. The sign Sagittarius.<BR> 4. A desert, Man. 7, 70 (cf. धन्वन्).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रधनुस्
इन्द्र- + धनुस् इन्द्र- + धनुस् and सुर-पति-, n. the rainbow, Man. 1, 38; Megh. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पधनुस्
पुष्प- + धनुस् पुष्प- + धनुस्, m. a name of the god of love, Śiś. 9, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधनुस्
स- + धनुस् स- + धनुस्, adj. armed with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य धन्य i. e. धन + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bringing wealth, Man. 4, 19.<BR> 2. Auspicious, MBh. 8, 3606.<BR> 3. Fortunate, MBh. 13, 937.<BR> II. m. A kind of spell, Rām. 1, 31, 8 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यता
धन्यता धन्य + ता, f. Fortunate condition, MBh. 3, 3078.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यंमन्य
धन्यंमन्य धन्यंमन्य i. e. धन्य + म्-मन् + य, adj. Thinking one's self fortunate, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व्
धन्व् धन्व् (akin to धन् and to धा̆व्), i. 1, Par. To run, to flow (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व|धन्वं|धन्वः
धन्व धन्व (a curtailed form of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a " target="_blank">Page0431-a + 42</a>] धन्वन्), n. A bow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियधन्व|प्रियधन्वः
प्रिय- + धन्व प्रिय- + धन्व, adj. bow-loving, MBh. 7, 9596.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् धन्वन्,<BR> I. (a curtailed form of धन्वन्त्, cf. धनुस्), n. A bow; in the classic language almost always latter part of comp. adj. or sbst. derived from adjectives, e. g. उद्यत- (vb. यम्), adj. With raised bow, Rām. 2, 91, 10 Gorr. कुसुम-, पुष्प-, m. Kāma, the god of love (properly, adj. Having a bow made of flowers), Prab. 72, 11. गाण्डीव-, m. A name of Arjuna, Megh. 49.<BR> II. m. and n. A country scantily supplied with water, a desert, Man. 7, 70 (v. r.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन्वन्
सु- + धन्वन् सु- + धन्वन्, m. 1. an archer. 2. the son of an outcast Vaiśya, Man. 10, 23. 3. Viśvakarman, the artist of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः|धन्वन्तरिः
धन्वन्तरि धन्वन्तरि, m.<BR> 1. A name of the sun, MBh. 3, 155.<BR> 2. The physician of the gods, who was produced at the churning of the ocean, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वायन
धन्वायन धन्वायन, in भीम-धन्वायनी, f. Armed with frightful bows, MBh. 5, 7633; probably to be changed to -धन्वायिनी, i. e. भीम-धन्वन् + विन् + ई (with य् for व्, VS. 16, 22).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन् धन्विन्, i. e. धन्वन् + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Armed with a bow, MBh. 4, 1639.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An archer, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 21.<BR> 2. The sign Sagittarius, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 5, 41.<BR> 3. A name of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10361.<BR> 4. A proper name, Hariv. 429.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्
धम् धम्, see ध्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम|धमः
ऽधम -धम् + अ (vb. ध्मा), latter part of comp. adj., Blowing, melting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनि|धमनिः
धमनि and नी धम् + अनी̆ (vb. धमा), f. A vein, MBh. 1, 5936.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्ल|धम्मिल्लः
धम्मिल्ल धम्मिल्ल, m. Braided and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b " target="_blank">Page0431-b + 46</a>] ornamented hair tied round the head, Rājat. 5, 356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर|धरः
धर धर, i. e. धृ + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Bearing, especially latter part of comp. adj., e. g. Arj. 6, 10.<BR> 2. Preserving, MBh. 6, 3005.<BR> 3. Possessed of, Rām. 1, 9, 27.<BR> 4. Observing, Pañc. 187, 12.<BR> II. m. The name of a वसु, MBh. 1, 2582.<BR> III. f. रा, The earth, Man. 6, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाधर|गदाधरः
गदा- + धर गदा- + धर, m. a name of Kṛṣṇa, Bhāg. P. 1, 8, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भधरा
गर्भ- + धरा गर्भ- + धर, adj., f. रा, pregnant, MBh. 3, 12864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीधर|जगतीधरः
जगती- + धर जगती- + धर, m. a mountain, Kir. 5, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाधर|जटाधरः
जटा- + धर जटा- + धर, 1. adj. wearing matted hair (cf. जटा) Rām. 2, 86, 22; an ascetic, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 7. 2. epithet of Śiva, MBh. 3, 1625.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधर|तोयधरः
तोय- + धर तोय- + धर, adj. containing water, Rām. 2, 93, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधर|दंडधर|दण्डधरः
दण्ड- + धर दण्ड- + धर,<BR> I. adj. 1. having a mast, Rām. 2, 97, 17. 2. holding a rod as symbol of justice, chastising, Man. 9, 245; MBh. 12, 694.<BR> II. m. 1. a king, Ragh. 9, 3. 2. a judge, Daśak. 111, 12. 3. epithet of Yama, Rājat. 4, 655.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डव्रतधर
दण्ड-व्रत- + धर दण्ड-व्रत- + धर, adj. punishing, Bhāg. P. 4, 13, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः|दुर्धरः
दुस्- + धर दुस्- + धर, adj., f. रा. 1. difficult to be borne, MBh. 5, 4403. 2. hard to be supported, Hariv. 8293. 3. hard to be managed, Man. 7, 28. 4. hard to be kept in remembrance, MBh. 13, 3618.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस् धनुस्, adj. sbst. armed with a bow, an archer, Man. 7, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीधर|धरणीधरः
धरणी- + धर धरणी- + धर,<BR> I. adj. holding the earth, MBh. 13, 6159.<BR> II. m. 1. a mountain, Rām. 6, 16, 4. 2. a king, Rājat. 3, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराधर|धराधरः
धरा- + धर धरा- + धर,<BR> I. adj. holding, supporting the earth, MBh. 13, 6860.<BR> II. m. a mountain, Rām. 3, 35, 24; धारा-, m. a cloud, MBh. 4, 2039.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षधर|पक्षधरः
पक्ष- + धर पक्ष- + धर,<BR> I. adj. Siding with, MBh. 1, 7507.<BR> II. m. a bird, Hariv. 11852.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशधर|पाशधरः
पाश- + धर पाश- + धर, m. (holding a noose), a name of Varuṇa, Hariv. 4808.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाधर
माया- + धर माया- + धर, adj. fraudulent, Rām. 3, 49, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमन्त्रधर|राजमन्त्रधरः
राज-मन्त्र- + धर राज-मन्त्र- + धर, i. e. राजन्-मन्त्र-, m. a king's counsellor, Hariv. 4137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलधर|हलधरः
हल- + धर हल- + धर,<BR> I. adj. holding a plough.<BR> II. m. Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरण|धरणं|धरणः
धरण धरण, i. e. धृ + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Preserving, Hariv. 9643.<BR> II. f. णी, and धरणि धरणि, The earth, Rām. 2, 42, 2; 1, 44, 17.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Supporting, Kumāras. 1, 17.<BR> 2. Support, Hariv. 12823.<BR> 3. A weight of ten Palas, Man. 8, 135; 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणि|धरणिः
धरणि धरणि, see the last (<BR> II.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरित्री
धरित्री धरित्री, i. e. धृ + तृ + ई, f.<BR> 1. A supporter, Hariv. 7419.<BR> 2. The earth, Bhartṛ. 2, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिमन्
धरिमन् धरिमन्, i. e. धृ + इमन्, m. Weight, Man. 8, 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्तृ|धर्त्तृ
धर्तृ धर्तृ, i. e. धृ + तृ, m. A preserver, Lass. 98, 11 = Rigv. v. 9, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्म|धर्म्मः
धर्म धर्म (a curtailed form of धर्मन्, q. cf.), m. and n.<BR> 1. Virtue, Hit. i. d. 59.<BR> 2. Merit, Bhāṣāp. 160.<BR> 3. Right, Man. 1, 26.<BR> 4. Law, Man. 1, 114; 2, 12.<BR> 5. Duty, Man. 6, 92.<BR> 6. Justice, Man. 7, 18.<BR> 7. Character, quality, MBh. 12, 7850.<BR> 8. Resemblance, Rām. 2, 123, 14 Gorr. (धर्मात्, Like).<BR> 9. A sacrifice, MBh. 14, 2623.<BR> 10. Personified justice, Rām. 1, 1, 19.<BR> 11. = Yama, the judge of the dead, Hiḍ. 1, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म|अधर्मः|अधर्म्म|अधर्म्मः
अ- + धर्म अ- + धर्म, m. 1. wrong, Man. 1, 26. 2. unjust way, Man. 2, 111. 3. demerit, Bhāṣāp. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिधर्म|अतिथिधर्मः
अतिथि- + धर्म अतिथि- + धर्म, m. 1. the duty of hospitality, Pañc. 35, 17. 2. the character of a guest, Man. 3, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधर्म|अरण्यधर्मः|अरण्यधर्म्म
अरण्य- + धर्म अरण्य- + धर्म, m. the customs of beasts, Pañc. 31, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्धर्म|आपद्धर्मः|आपद्धर्म्म
आपद्- + धर्म आपद्- + धर्म, m. the duties and dispensations in time of distress, Man. 1, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालधर्म|कालधर्मः|कालधर्म्म|कालधर्म्मः
काल- + धर्म काल- + धर्म, m. death, Rām. 1, 43, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधर्म|कुलधर्मः|कुलधर्म्म|कुलधर्म्मः
कुल- + धर्म कुल- + धर्म, m. the customs of families, Man. 1, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटधर्म
कूट- + धर्म कूट- + धर्म, adj. where falsehood passes for right, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधर्म|गोधर्मः|गोधर्म्म
गो- + धर्म गो- + धर्म, m. 1. law concerning cattle, MBh. 1, 4195. 2. public sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यधर्म|ग्राम्यधर्मः|ग्राम्यधर्म्म|ग्राम्यधर्म्मः
ग्राम्य- + धर्म ग्राम्य- + धर्म, 1. m. the customs of tame animals (or of persons living in a village ?), Pañc. 31, 6. 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b " target="_blank">Page0432-b + 44</a>] public sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मधर्म
छद्मन्- + धर्म छद्मन्- + धर्म, m. hypocrisy, Rām. 4, 16, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिधर्म|जातिधर्मः|जातिधर्म्म
जाति- + धर्म जाति- + धर्म, m. the customs of tribes, Man. 1, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर्म
दुस्- + धर्म दुस्- + धर्म, adj. following bad customs, MBh. 8, 2066.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुधर्म|पशुधर्मः|पशुधर्म्म
पशु- + धर्म पशु- + धर्म, m. 1. manner of treating cattle, Pañc. 34, 16. 2. a custom fit only for beasts, Man. 9, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिधर्म|पाणिधर्मः|पाणिधर्म्म
पाणि- + धर्म पाणि- + धर्म, m. the form of marriage, MBh. 1, 3379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धधर्म
युद्ध- + धर्म युद्ध- + धर्म, m. the law of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषधर्म|विशेषधर्मः|विशेषधर्म्म
विशेष- + धर्म विशेष- + धर्म, m. peculiar or different duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधर्म|सत्यधर्मः
सत्य- + धर्म सत्य- + धर्म, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षाद्धर्म
साक्षात्- + धर्म साक्षात्- + धर्म, m. the living law, Man. 2, 12 (cf. 2, 237).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधर्म|सुधर्म्म|सुधर्म्मः
सु- + धर्म सु- + धर्म, f. मा and मी, a council of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म|स्त्रीधर्मः|स्त्रीधर्म्म|स्त्रीधर्म्मः
स्त्री- + धर्म स्त्री- + धर्म, m. 1. law concerning women, Man. 1, 114. 2. duty of women. 3. Menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म|स्वधर्मः|स्वधर्म्म|स्वधर्म्मः
स्व- + धर्म स्व- + धर्म, m. 1. that which is due to somebody, one's right, Chr. 21, 8. 2. one's duty, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 4. 3. peculiar duty or occupation. 4. peculiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मतस्|धर्म्मतस्
धर्मतस् धर्म + तस्, adv. By right, Man. 1, 93.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रधर्मतस्
पुत्र- + धर्मतस् पुत्र- + धर्मतस्, adv. by the ceremonies used on the birth of a son, Chr. 55, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मन्|धर्म्मन्
धर्मन् धर्मन्, i. e. धृ + मन्,<BR> 1. n. in ved. language = धर्म.<BR> 2. in the later language hardly ever used except as a substitute for धर्म, when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. विदित-, adj. Knowing one's duty, Śāk. 40, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालधर्मन्|कालधर्म्मन्
काल- + धर्मन् काल- + धर्मन्, n. death, Hariv. 4761.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रधर्मन्
क्षत्र- + धर्मन् क्षत्र- + धर्मन्, adj. fulfilling the duty of a warrior, Chr. 30, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यधर्मन्|मनुष्यधर्म्मन्
मनुष्य- + धर्मन् मनुष्य- + धर्मन्, m. Kuvera, the god of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दादिधर्मन्
शब्दादि- + धर्मन् शब्दादि- + धर्मन्, i. e. शब्द-आदि-, n. quality of sound, etc., Bhāg. P. 3, 32, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मन्|सधर्म्मन्
स- + धर्मन् स- + धर्मन्, adj. 1. equal in respect of duty, Man. 10, 41. 2. of the same caste, performing like duties. 3. of the same properties. 4. Like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममय|धर्म्ममय
धर्ममय धर्म + मय, adj. Consisting of virtue, MBh. 1, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवन्त्|धर्मवत्|धर्म्मवत्
धर्मवन्त् धर्म + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Virtuous, Rām. 5, 3, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मस्थ|धर्मस्थः
धर्मस्थ धर्म-स्थ, m. A judge, Man. 8, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मता
धर्मात्मता धर्मात्मता, i. e. धर्म-आत्मन् + ता, f. Justice, Rām. 4, 55, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणिक|धर्माधिकरणिकः
धर्माधिकरणिक धर्माधिकरणिक, i. e. धर्म-अधिकरण + इक, m. A judge, Pañc. 97, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मित्व
धर्मित्व धर्मित्व, i. e. धर्मिन् + त्व, n. Virtue, Kām. Nītis. 8, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिन्|धर्म्मिन्
धर्मिन् धर्मिन्, i. e. धर्म + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> I. Virtuous, MBh. 7, 1663.<BR> II. Having special qualities, Hariv. 10948.<BR> III. Latter part of comp. adj.<BR> 1. Following the law of (Bhagavant), Bhāg. P. 4, 23, 10.<BR> 2. Bound by the law of (the twice born), Man. 10, 41.<BR> 3. Following the habits of (beasts), MBh. 1, 3480.<BR> 4. Having the nature of (perishableness), Ragh. 8, 10.<BR> 5. Having duties (to each other), MBh. 14, 708.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मिन्|सधर्म्मिन्
स- + धर्मिन् स- + धर्मिन्,<BR> I. adj. Observing the same customs or laws.<BR> II. f. इणी, A wife wedded according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्मिणी|स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी
स्त्री- + धर्मिणी स्त्री- + धर्मिन्, i. e. स्त्री-धर्म + इन्, f. इणी, A woman during menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठः|धर्म्मिष्ठ
धर्मिष्ठ धर्मिष्ठ, superl. of धर्मवन्त्, f. ठा.<BR> 1. Performing all duties, Man. 3, 40.<BR> 2. Very virtuous, Bhāg. P. 9, 16, 15.<BR> 3. Completely harmonising with law, Rām. 2, 26, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मिष्ठ|अधर्म्मिष्ठ
अ- + धर्मिष्ठ अ- + धर्मिष्ठ, adj. 1. unjust, Rām. 2, 23, 13. 2. very wicked, MBh. 1, 4579.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठता
धर्मिष्ठता धर्मिष्ठ + ता, f. Supreme virtuousness, MBh. 1, 2987.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्य|धर्म्म्यः
धर्म्य धर्म्य, i. e. धर्म + य, adj.<BR> 1. Conformable to law, legal, Man. 3, 22; 9, 111.<BR> 2. Loving justice, just, Rām. 2, 21, 49; 50.<BR> 3. Legitimate (as a wife), Rām. 3, 4, 7.<BR> 4. Latter part of comp. words, Having the quality of (that), Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्य
अ- + धर्म्य अ- + धर्म्य, adj. 1. illegal, Man. 3, 25. 2. unjust, Rām. 1, 27, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ष|धर्षः
धर्ष धर्ष, i. e. धृष् + अ, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b " target="_blank">Page0433-b + 42</a>] Arrogance, MBh. 1, 7040.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर्ष
दुस्- + धर्ष दुस्- + धर्ष, adj. 1. difficult to be injured or attacked, Nal. 11, 36; Rām. 6, 16, 58. 2. dangerous, Hariv. 2327. 3. horrible, MBh. 14, 1849.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षक|धर्षकः
धर्षक धर्षक, i. e. धृष् + अक, adj. Assailing, Hariv. 8844.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षण|धर्षणं
धर्षण धर्षण, i. e. धृष् + अन, n. and f. णा, Disrespect, contumely, abuse, Rām. 6, 38, 21; MBh. 1, 6502; Pañc. 255, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर्षण
दुस्- + धर्षण दुस्- + धर्षण, adj. difficult to be attacked, Rām. 4, 9, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिन्
धर्षिन् धर्षिन्, i. e. धृष् + इन्, adj. Ill-treating, Hariv. 8213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव्
धव् धव्, i. 1, Ātm. To run, (ved.).<BR> --Cf. θέω, θεύσομαι, θοός, βοη-θέω, νω-θής.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव धव, m.<BR> 1. A man, Pañc. ii. d. 109.<BR> 2. A husband, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 20.<BR> 3. A lord, Hariv. 14952.<BR> 4. A shrub, Grislea tomentosa Roxb., Rām. 1, 26, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाधव|मेनाधवः
मेना- + धव मेना- + धव, m. Himālaya, the personified mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधव
वि- + धव वि- + धव, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधवा
स-धवा स-धवा, f. a wife whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवल|धवलः
धवल धव् + अल (cf. 2. धाव्), adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Dazzling white, Kathās. 25, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधवल
अति- + धवल अति- + धवल, adj. very white, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलित
धवलित धवलित, i. e. धवल + इत, adj. Made dazzling white, Bhartṛ. 3, 85.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधवलित
सुधा- + धवलित सुधा- + धवलित, adj. whitewashed, plastered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलिमन्
धवलिमन् धवलिमन्, i. e. धवल + इमन्, m. White (the colour), Śiś. 4, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा धा, ii. 3, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To put, MBh. 5, 1075; Hit. ii. d. 163; pass. To be contained, MBh. 12, 8933.<BR> 2. With मनस् or मतिम्, often To resolve, Rām. 1, 9, 40, 11, 1; to fix the mind on, Man. 12, 23.<BR> 3. To grant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0434-a " target="_blank">Page0434-a + 46</a>] confer, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14 (ved. धत्तन for धत्त), MBh. 7, 5267; Man. 1, 29.<BR> 4. To generate, Bhāg. P. 9, 6, 38.<BR> 5. To undertake, Rājat. 1, 295.<BR> 6. To put on, Ṛt. 6, 13.<BR> 7. To carry, bear, Ragh. 3, 1; Ṛt. 6, 16.<BR> 8. To nourish, Chr. 295, 13 = Rigv. i. 92, 13 (ved. धामके, conj. of the Aor.).<BR> 9. To preserve, Ragh. 1, 26.<BR> 10. Ātm. To get, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 23.<BR> 11. Ātm. To undergo, Hariv. 531.<BR> 12. Ātm. To show, Hit. pr. d. 41. Anomal. impf. अदधन्, MBh. 3, 12706. Anomal. Aor. धीमकि (ved.), Bhāg. P. 6, 16, 18. Anomal. (or rather false) ptcple. of the pf. Par. f. दध्युषी (for दधुषी), Rām. 2, 16, 20 (= 2, 13, 19 Gorr., where v. r.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. pass. धीयमान, One whose mind is directed to, Hariv. 1854 (अ-धर्मे, to injustice).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. धित (ved. and) Hariv. 7799, Resolved.<BR> II. हित,<BR> 1. Fit, suitable, Chr. 10, 5.<BR> 2. Salutary, Man. 4, 35; most beneficial, Man. 7, 57.<BR> 3. Worthy, Pañc. i. d. 358.<BR> 4. Friendly, agreeable, Man. 2, 108. m. A friend, MBh. 12, 5471. n.<BR> 1. Well-being, Rām. 3, 53, 12; also pl. Bhartṛ. 2, 65.<BR> 2. A good, a benefit, Rājat. 5, 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. धेय, To be produced, MBh. 12, 13108.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, Ātm. To conquer, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2.<BR> --With अन्तर् अन्तर्,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 4, 1683.<BR> 2. To cause to disappear, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 35.<BR> 3. To eclipse, MBh. 1, 5519.<BR> 4. especially pass. To disappear, Bhāg. P. 3, 2, 11; MBh. 4, 1042.<BR> 5. To receive [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0434-b " target="_blank">Page0434-b + 42</a>] in one's self, contain, Ragh. 15, 81; MBh. 12, 12747. अन्तर्हित,<BR> 1. Covered, Rām. 2, 9, 18.<BR> 2. Hidden, Śāk. 9, 18, v. r.<BR> 3. Disappeared, Chr. 39, 19.<BR> --With अपि अपि and पि पि,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 1, 5863; 4, 1453.<BR> 2. To shut, MBh. 3, 12089.<BR> 3. To make invisible, Vikr. d. 72.<BR> 4. pass. To disappear, MBh. 12, 8932.<BR> 5. To hinder, Rām. 5, 29, 16.<BR> --Caus. To cause to shut, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 29.<BR> --With अन्वपि अनु-अपि, pass. To disappear after somebody (acc.), Bhāg. P. 3, 11, 28.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To invade, MBh. 2, 1090.<BR> 2. Ātm. To take back, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 30.<BR> 3. To name, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 10.<BR> 4. To declare, Man. 1, 42.<BR> 5. To speak, Rām. 2, 123, 15 Gorr. (with acc., Rām. 6, 12, 7). अभिहित, Called, Man. 3, 141.<BR> --With प्रत्यभि प्रति-अभि,<BR> 1. To take back, Bhāg. P. 3, 7, 4.<BR> 2. To answer, 4, 3, 15.<BR> 3. To approve, MBh. 5, 7459.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To address, Kathās. 25, 93.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To put, MBh. 1, 4503.<BR> 2. To fix one's attention on something, Śāntiś. 3, 11. अवहित,<BR> 1. Shut, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 32.<BR> 2. Attentive, Prab. 33, 2.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, अभ्यवहित, Allayed, Rām. 2, 40, 33.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव, To separate, Rām. 2, 114, 13 Gorr.; pass. To separate one's self, Śāntiś. 3, 11. व्यवहित,<BR> 1. Stopped, Śāk. 71, 18.<BR> 2. Covered, Śiś. 9, 26.<BR> 3. Hostile, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 36.<BR> --With संव्यव सम्-वि-अव, अ-संव्यवहित + म्, adv. Immediately, Bhāg. P. 5, 6, 6.<BR> --With आ आ, usually Ātm.<BR> 1. To put, Rām. 5, 31, 1.<BR> 2. To generate, MBh. 3, 8639; 16637; to produce, Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 34; to perform, MBh. 3, 2600.<BR> 3. To instil, MBh. 1, 6157.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0435-a " target="_blank">Page0435-a + 44</a>] To direct, MBh. 5, 4172.<BR> 5. With मतिम्, मनस्, चित्तम्, often To resolve, Rām. 1, 18, 7.<BR> 6. To employ, Śāk. 3, 13.<BR> 7. To put on, Śāk. d. 36.<BR> 8. To hold, Man. 11, 104.<BR> 9. To pawn, Nārada in Mit. 268, 2.<BR> 10. To confer, MBh. 1, 7735.<BR> 11. Ātm. To