गिरि- + धातु गिरि- + धातु, m. the constituent parts of a mountain, as minerals, etc., Rām. 2, 63, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरिकधातु
गैरिक- + धातु गैरिक- + धातु, m. = गैरिक, q. v. Rām. 5, 5, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातु|त्रिधातुः
त्रि- + धातु त्रि- + धातु, adj. threefold, Chr. 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधातु|महाधातुः
महा- + धातु महा- + धातु, m. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तधातु|रक्तधातुः
रक्त- + धातु रक्त- + धातु, m. 1. red chalk. 2. copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाधातु|शिलाधातुः
शिला- + धातु शिला- + धातु, m. 1. chalk. 2. red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यधातु|सौम्यधातुः
सौम्य- + धातु सौम्य- + धातु, m. phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमत्ता
धातुमत्ता धातुमत्ता, i. e. धातु-मन्त् + ता, f. Abundance in metals, Kumāras. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमन्त्|धातुमत्
धातुमन्त् धातु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Having clements, Bhāg. P. 2, 8, 7.<BR> 2. Abounding in metals, Rām. 2, 94, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरिकधातुमन्त्
गैरिक-धातु + मन्त् गैरिक-धातु + मन्त्, adj. abounding in red chalk, MBh. 3, 826.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृ
धातृ धा + तृ, m.<BR> 1. The creator, Ragh. 13, 6.<BR> 2. A bearer, Hariv. 11851.<BR> 3. A preserver, MBh. 1, 1722.<BR> 4. One of the Ādityas, MBh. 1, 2523.<BR> 5. A name of Brahman, Man. 5, 30.<BR> 6. A son of Brahman, MBh. 1, 2614.<BR> 7. An adulterer, Daśak. 191, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. con-ditor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्धातृ
जगत्- + धातृ जगत्- + धातृ,<BR> I. m. a name of Brahman.<BR> II. f. धात्री, a name of Sarasvatī, Mārk. P. 23, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्री
धात्री धात्री, i. e. धे + तृ + ई, f.<BR> 1. A mother, Yājñ. 3, 82.<BR> 2. A nurse, Rām. 1, 40, 18 Gorr.<BR> 3. A waitingwoman, Chr. 52, 15.<BR> 4. The earth, MBh. 11, 215.<BR> 5. Emblica officinalis Gaertn., Myrobalane, Suśr. 1, 162, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रेयिका
धात्रेयिका धात्रेयिका, i. e. धात्री + एय + क, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b " target="_blank">Page0438-b + 41</a>] f. A foster-sister, Draup. 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान|धानं
धान धान, i. e.धा + अन, f. नी, latter part of comp. words implying especially the place of the preceding notion, e. g. जीव-धानी, f. The seat of living creatures, epithet of the earth, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 30. मत्स्य-धानी, f. A fish-basket. यम-धानी, f. The residence of the god of death, Bhartṛ. 3, 51. यातु-धान, m. A Rākṣasa or demon. राज-धान, n. and -धानी, f. i. e. राजन्-, A capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाना
धाना धाना, i. e. probably धा + अना, f. pl. Grain, Bhāg. P. 6, 15, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्क|धानुष्कः
धानुष्क धानुष्क, i. e. धनुस् + क + अ, m. An archer, MBh. 6, 756.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्य|धान्यं
धान्य धान्य, i. e. धाना + य, n. Corn, Man. 2, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुधान्य
कु- + धान्य कु- + धान्य, n. a kind of corn, Suśr. 1, 196, 21 sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनधान्य
धन- + धान्य धन- + धान्य, n. a kind of spell, Rām. 1, 30, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यक|धान्यकं|धान्यकः
धान्यक धान्य + क,<BR> 1. A substitute for धान्य in the latter part of a comp. word. कुम्भी-, adj. Having vessels full of corn, Man. 4, 7 (sufficing for one year, Kull.). कुशूल-, adj. Having granaries full of corn (sufficing for three years, Kull.), ib. बहु-, adj. Abounding in corn, MBh. 2, 1187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवन्त्|धान्यवत्
धान्यवन्त् धान्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having much corn, MBh. 12, 3526.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन
धान्वन धान्वन, i. e. धन्वन् + अ, adj. Situated in a desert, Kām. Nītis. 4, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन्तर
धान्वन्तर धान्वन्तर and धान्वन्तर्य धान्वन्तर्य, i. e. धन्वन्तरि + अ or य, adj.<BR> 1. Referring to Dhanvantari (the incarnation of Viṣṇu as Dhanvantari), Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 17.<BR> 2. Sacred to the sun, MBh. 13, 4660.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाम
धाम धाम (akin to धामन्), m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a " target="_blank">Page0439-a + 45</a>] pl. The name of a class of superhuman beings, MBh. 13, 15446.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन् धा + मन्, n.<BR> 1. An abode, MBh. 1, 3602.<BR> 2. State, Prab. 17, 15.<BR> 3. A host, Chr. 292, 11, and 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 11; 87, 6.<BR> 4. Dignity, Ragh. 11, 85.<BR> 5. Light, splendour, Prab. 26, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. θέμα; A.S.-dóm, as affix of abstracts, properly ‘state.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्मधामन्|अघर्म्मधामन्
अ-घर्म- + धामन् अ-घर्म- + धामन्, m. the moon, Śiś. 9, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधामन्
त्रि- + धामन् त्रि- + धामन्,<BR> I. adj. referring to the three worlds, MBh. 13, 7376.<BR> II. m. a name of Viṣṇu, MBh. 12, 1508.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिधामन्
रुचि- + धामन् रुचि- + धामन्, adj. the abode of whom is light, epithet of the sun, Śiś. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतधामन्
श्वेत- + धामन् श्वेत- + धामन्, m. 1. the moon. 2. camphor. 3. cuttle-fish bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणधामन्
हरिण- + धामन् हरिण- + धामन्, m. the moon, Rājat. 5, 482.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार धार, i. e.<BR> I. धृ + अ, latter part of comp. words, Holding, bearing, e. g. छत्त्र-, m. The bearer of the royal parasol, Pañc. 156, 22; दण्ड-, adj. Holding the staff, as symbol of judicature, Rājat. 4, 108.<BR> II. धारा + अ.<BR> 1. adj. Coming down in a shower, Suśr. 1, 170, 1.<BR> 2. m. A shower, Hariv. 6333.<BR> --Cf. धारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक धारक, i. e. धृ + अक,<BR> I. latter part of comp. adj., Bearing, MBh. 1, 1691. नामधारक, i. e. नामन्-, adj. Being something only nominally, not really, Pañc. ii. d. 91.<BR> II. m. A trunk or box (for keeping clothes), Suśr. 2, 55, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण धारण, i. e. धृ + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णी.<BR> 1. Preserving, MBh. 12, 12751.<BR> 2. Keeping in remembrance, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 46.<BR> 3. Having the shape, MBh. 13, 739.<BR> II. f. णा.<BR> 1. Bearing, MBh. 7, 1912.<BR> 2. Supporting, Rām. 2, 109, 25 Gorr.<BR> 3. Suppression, Bhāg. P. 4, 4, 26.<BR> 4. Mental retention, MBh. 1, 1010.<BR> 5. Keeping the mind collected, the breath suspended, and all natural wants restrained; steady [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b " target="_blank">Page0439-b + 45</a>] immoveable abstraction, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 19.<BR> 6. A settled rule, Man. 4, 38.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Holding, bearing, Kumāras. 7, 68; MBh. 3, 9946.<BR> 2. Maintaining, Yājñ. 3, 174.<BR> 3. Observance, Man. 10, 3.<BR> 4. Mental retention, MBh. 15, 756.<BR> 5. Possession, Man. 1, 93.<BR> 6. Fixing one's mind on one object, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 19.<BR> 7. Restraining, or rather stopping, the senses, MBh. 3, 13939.<BR> 8. Enduring, Rām. 1, 38, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भधारण
गर्भ- + धारण गर्भ- + धारण, n. pregnancy, MBh. 3, 10449.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रधारण
छत्त्र- + धारण छत्त्र- + धारण, n. carrying an umbrella, Man. 2, 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधारण
तुला- + धारण तुला- + धारण, n. weighing, Yājñ. 2, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधारण
दण्ड- + धारण दण्ड- + धारण, n. punishment, Rām. 4, 17, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधारण
देह- + धारण देह- + धारण, n. 1. bearing a body, MBh. 5, 3693. 2. life, MBh. 5, 7258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तधारण|हस्तधारणं
हस्त- + धारण हस्त- + धारण, n. warding off a blow, resisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणक|धारणकः
धारणक धारण + क,<BR> I. latter part of comp. adj., Containing, MBh. 12, 6889.<BR> II. m. A debtor, Yājñ. 2, 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधारणक
अ- + धारणक अ- + धारणक, adj. unsupportable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणामय
धारणामय धारणा + मय, adj., f. यी, depending on abstraction, Bhāg. P. 4, 18, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयितृ
धारयितृ धारयितृ, i. e. धृ, Caus., + तृ, m.<BR> 1. One who bears, Rām. 1, 44, 23 Gorr.<BR> 2. One who restrains, MBh. 5, 3391.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारा
धारा धारा (akin to धा̆व्,), f.<BR> 1. A torrent, MBh. 6, 5785.<BR> 2. A river, Hariv. 8325.<BR> 3. A shower, Mṛcch. 76, 15.<BR> 4. A drop, Mṛcch. 91, 4; Bhartṛ. 2, 89.<BR> 5. A multitude, Rām. 6, 88, 3.<BR> 6. pl. A horse's pace, as the trot, canter, etc., Śiś. 5, 60.<BR> 7. The sharp edge of a sword or any cutting instrument, Rām. 2, 23, 35.<BR> 8. The circumference of a wheel, Ragh. 13, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरधार|क्षुरधारः
क्षुर-धार क्षुर-धार, 1. adj. as sharp as a razor, MBh. 4, 168. 2. (m. or n.) a sharp instrument, MBh. 4, 2063.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतधार
कृत-धार कृत-धार, adj. sharpened, MBh. 7, 3090.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरधार
खर-धार खर-धार, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a " target="_blank">Page0440-a + 43</a>] having a rough or jagged edge, Suśr. 1, 27, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्धार
तिर्यग्धार तिर्यग्धार, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-, adj. having sharp sides, MBh. 7, 1875.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णधार|तीक्ष्णधारः
तीक्ष्ण-धार तीक्ष्ण-धार, 1. adj. having a sharp edge, MBh. 1, 786. 2. m. a sword, MBh. 12, 6203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावन्त्|धारावत्
धारावन्त् धारा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Edged, Kām. Nītis. 11, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन् धारिन्, i. e. धृ + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Bearing, MBh. 13, 4350.<BR> 2. Having, Ragh. 12, 41.<BR> 3. Knowing, Kathās. 13, 20.<BR> 4. Maintaining, MBh. 1, 2596.<BR> 5. Keeping. न्यास-, A depositary, Man. 8, 196.<BR> 6. Retaining (what one has read), Man. 12, 103.<BR> 7. Observing, Rām. 3, 1, 35.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थाधारिन्|कंथाधारिन्
कन्था- + धारिन् कन्था- + धारिन्, adj. wearing a patched cloth, Bhartṛ. 2, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाधारिन्
जटा- + धारिन् जटा- + धारिन्, adj. wearing matted hair (see जटा), Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधारिन्
दण्ड- + धारिन् दण्ड- + धारिन्, adj. chastising, Bhāg. P. 6, 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रधारिन्
मन्त्र- + धारिन् मन्त्र- + धारिन्, adj. sbst. a counsellor, MBh. 5, 926.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वधारिन्
विश्व- + धारिन् विश्व- + धारिन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी, all-sustaining.<BR> II. m. a deity.<BR> III. f. इणी, the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्तराष्ट्र धार्तराष्ट्र, i. e. धृतराष्ट्र + अ,<BR> I. adj. f. री.<BR> I. Referring, belonging to Dhṛtarāṣṭra, MBh. 8, 176.<BR> II. patronym. A son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra, MBh. 1, 2726.<BR> III. m. A sort of goose with black legs and bill, Hariv. 8585.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म|धार्म्म
धार्म धार्म, i. e. धर्म + अ, adj., f. मी, Belonging to the god of justice, MBh. 1, 2426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक धार्मिक, i. e. धर्म + इक, adj., f. की, Just, performing all duties, virtuous, Man. 2, 109.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधार्मिक|अधार्म्मिक|अधार्म्मिकः
अ- + धार्मिक अ- + धार्मिक, adj. 1. unobservant of one's duties, Man. 4, 61. 2. where the duties are neglected, Man. 4, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिकता
धार्मिकता धार्मिक + ता, f. Justice, Kām. Nītis. 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट
धार्ष्ट धार्ष्ट i. e. धृष्ट + अ, patronym. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-b " target="_blank">Page0440-b + 39</a>] Descending from Dhṛṣṭa, Bhāg. P. 9, 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
1. धाव् धाव् (cf. धव्, धन्व्), i. 1, Par., Ātm.<BR> 1. To flow, Hariv. 14516.<BR> 2. To run, Man. 8, 314.<BR> 3. To run to (acc.), MBh. 3, 2543.<BR> 4. To move, Rājat. 4, 425.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धावित, Beginning to run, Kathās. 3, 52.<BR> --Caus. धावय,<BR> 1. To cause to run, to push on, Pañc. 223, 12.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To stream through, Suśr. 1, 43, 8.<BR> 2. To spread over, Rām. 2, 109, 13 Gorr.<BR> 3. To run after, Rām. 2, 25, 8 Gorr.<BR> 4. To pursue, Bhāg. P. 4, 11, 20.<BR> 5. To come to one's assistance (acc.), MBh. 3, 2384.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To pursue, MBh. 8, 4086.<BR> --With अन्तर् अन्तर्, To run among, Bhāg. P. 3, 32, 37.<BR> --With अप अप, To deviate, to vary, Man. 8, 54.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To run to (acc.), Rām. 4, 41, 24.<BR> 2. To come to assistance, Man. 9, 274.<BR> --With प्रत्यभि प्रत्-अभि, To run to (acc.), Rām. 2, 82, 13 Gorr.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To run to, MBh. 6, 3119.<BR> 2. To fly against Rām. 6, 34, 23.<BR> --With व्यव वि-आव,<BR> 1. To run away, MBh. 12, 10599.<BR> 2. To separate, Rām. 2, 105, 25.<BR> --With आ आ, To run near, to rush upon, Bhāg. P. 8, 10, 39.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, To run to (acc.), Bhāg. P. 7, 13, 28.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To run near, Hariv. 14566.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To run near, Rām. 1, 28, 16.<BR> 2. To run to, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 6.<BR> 3. To fly for refuge to (acc.), Bhāg. P. 4, 7, 38.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To run near, MBh. 3, 2097.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To run out, Hariv. 11020.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-a " target="_blank">Page0441-a + 41</a>] परि परि,<BR> 1. To flow about, Chr. 47, 40.<BR> 2. To stream through, Suśr. 1, 91, 5.<BR> 3. To run about, Pañc. 62, 23.<BR> 4. To drive about, MBh. 4, 302.<BR> 5. With मृगयाम्, To hunt, Rām. 5, 30, 8.<BR> 6. To run round, Bhāg. P. 5, 22, 2.<BR> 7. To run through, Rām. 6, 11, 38.<BR> 8. To pursue, Pañc. 106, 7.<BR> --Caus. To surround, MBh. 14, 828.<BR> --With विपरि वि-परि,<BR> 1. To run to and fro, Rām. 5, 36, 38.<BR> 2. To run through, Hariv. 4105.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To flow away, Suśr. 1, 81, 9.<BR> 2. To run away, MBh. 3, 2548.<BR> 3. To run, Man. 4, 38.<BR> 4. To run to, MBh. 4, 428.<BR> 5. To spread, MBh. 1, 6400. प्रधावित, Run away, Rām. 6, 79, 37.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, To pursue, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 16.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To run asunder, MBh. 8, 3036.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To run away, MBh. 5, 5148.<BR> 2. To run to, Bhāg. P. 3, 7, 15.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To assail, Rām. 6, 13, 26.<BR> --With वि वि, To run through, Rām. 5, 16, 14.<BR> --With परिवि परि-वि, To run through, Rām. 5, 29, 22.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To run together, MBh. 3, 8879.<BR> 2. To assail, Hariv. 5617.<BR> 3. To run to, MBh. 12, 10670.<BR> --Cf. धर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
2. धाव् धाव्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To cleanse, to wash, Śiś. 17, 8.<BR> 2. To rub into one's person, Suśr. 2, 344, 14.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धौत,<BR> 1. Cleansed, washed, MBh. 1, 3641; Daśak. in Chr. 188, 22.<BR> 2. Polished, MBh. 9, 1079.<BR> 3. Resplendent, Kathā. 11, 31.<BR> 4. Pure, Śāk. d. 132.<BR> 5. Washed away, Śṛṅgārat. 7.<BR> 6. n. Washing, Cāṇ. 76, in Berl. Monatsb.<BR> --Caus. To wash, Man. 4, 65.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्,<BR> 1. निर्धौत, Washed away, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b " target="_blank">Page0441-b + 40</a>] Śiś. 8, 51.<BR> 2. Cleansed, Ragh. 5, 70.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To wash, MBh. 3, 14024.<BR> --With वि वि, To wash away, Śiś. 8, 50. विधौत. Cleansed, Śiś. 8, 70.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. tau; A.S. deaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक धाव् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Running, Rām. 2, 32, 22 Gorr.<BR> 2. Washing, Rām. 2, 38, 13, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
धावन धाव् + अन, n.<BR> 1. An attack, Rājat. 1, 114.<BR> 2. Rubbing, Man. 4, 152.<BR> 3. Washing, Rām. 1, 9, 57 Gorr.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तधावन|दंतधावन|दन्तधावनं|दन्तधावनः
दन्त- + धावन दन्त- + धावन, n. 1. cleansing the teeth, Pañc. 47, 23. 2. a small piece of wood for cleansing the teeth, Rām. 2, 91, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिलाचन्दनधावन
मनःशिला-चन्दन- + धावन मनःशिला-चन्दन- + धावन, n. a preparation made of red arsenic and sandal, Rām. 6, 96, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावितृ
धावितृ धावितृ, i. e. 1. धाव् + त्रि, m. A runner, MBh. 11, 760.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाविन्
धाविन् 1. धाव् + इन्, adj. Running, Kathās. 22, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
† धि धि, i. 6, Par. To hold (akin to धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
ऽधि -धि (vb. धा, form of an old ptcple., धन्त्, cf. ऊधन्, पयोधस् and पयोधि), latter part of comp. nouns, The receptacle for keeping that which the preceding part denotes; cf. e. g. अम्बु-धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् धिक्, an interjection:<BR> 1. of dissatis-faction, Pie, Brāhmaṇ. 1, 35.<BR> 2. of reproach, Shame, Pañc. 38, 12. With nom., voc., acc. (Draup. 9, 21). gen. (Rām. 6, 95, 40).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कार|धिक्कारः
धिक्कार धिक्-कार, m. Contempt, Bhāg. P. 4, 14, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष्
† धिक्ष् धिक्ष् (properly a desiderat. of दह्), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To kindle.<BR> 2. To be weary.<BR> 3. To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वण|धिग्वणः
धिग्वण धिग्वण (probably a dialectical [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a " target="_blank">Page0442-a + 41</a>] form of धिक्-वर्ण), m. The son of a Brāhmaṇa and an Āyogava-woman, MBh. 10, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0441-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिन्व्
धिन्व् धिन्व् (properly धि. i. 5), ii. 5, धिनु, Par.<BR> 1. To satisfy (ved.).<BR> 2. To please, Prab. 55, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियावसु
धियावसु धियावसु, i. e. धी + आ-वसु, adj. Granting wealth on account of devotion, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
† धिष् धिष्, ii. 3, Par. To emit sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण धिषण,<BR> I. n. An abode, a seat, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 33.<BR> II. f. णा,<BR> 1. Intellect, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 47.<BR> 2. The name of one of the wives of the gods, MBh. 9, 2516.<BR> 3. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्य
धिष्ठ्य धिष्ठ्य, n. A seat, an abode, Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 6 (probably to be changed to धिष्ण्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्यप
धिष्ठ्यप धिष्ठ्य-प, m. A cherisher of the world, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य धिष्ण्य (i. e. probably धा + स्न + य),<BR> I. m. A fireplace, Bhāg. P. 8, 15, 9.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. An abode, a seat, Bhāg. P. 8, 3, 27; MBh. 3, 17090. A meteor, MBh. 5, 7272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
† धी धी, i. 4, Ātm. (properly pass. of धा), To hold, to disregard, or to accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी धी, (vb. ध्यै), f.<BR> 1. Knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 45; Man. 6, 92.<BR> 2. Intellect, mind, Man. 12, 122.<BR> 3. Devotion, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 88, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारधी
उदार- + धी उदार- + धी, adj. high-minded, Chr. 44, 6. Cf. कु-, पर-द्रोह-कर्मन्-, adj. injuring another in deed or in thought, Man. 2, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुधी
साधु- + धी साधु- + धी,<BR> I. adj. well-disposed.<BR> II. f. a wife's or husband's mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधी
सु- + धी सु- + धी, m. 1. an intelligent, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b " target="_blank">Page0442-b + 39</a>] wise man. 2. a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितधी
स्थित- + धी स्थित- + धी, adj. calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमन्त्|धीमत्
धीमन्त् धी + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Sensible, wise, Man. 1, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर धीर, i. e.<BR> I. धृ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Lasting, Cāṭ. 7.<BR> 2. Firm, resolute, Hariv. 3755; Bhartṛ. 2, 72; Hit. i. d. 167; courageous, Kathās. 18, 297.<BR> 3. Solemn, grave, Bhartṛ. 2, 26.<BR> 4. Deep (as a sound), Ragh. 16, 13.<BR> II. धी + र, adj. Sensible, wise, MBh. 5, 1076; Rām. 3, 19 13; Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. i. 64, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरता
धीरता धीर + ता, f. (and धीरत्व धीर + त्व, n.),<BR> 1. Firmness, Ragh. 8, 43.<BR> 2. Courage, Pañc. 129, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीरता
अ- + धीरता अ- + धीरता, f. pusillanimity, Prab. 15, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर धीवर,<BR> 1. m. A fisherman, MBh. 2, 784.<BR> 2. f. री, A fisherman's wife, Kathās. 26, 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु धु, see धू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् धुक्ष्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To kindle.<BR> 2. To be weary.<BR> 3. To live.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To animate, MBh. 13, 3677.<BR> 2. To inflame, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 10.<BR> --Caus. To kindle, to animate, MBh. 1, 5628.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि धुनि, i. e. ध्वन् + इ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Roaring, Chr. 290, 5 = Rigv. i. 64, 5.<BR> 2. f. also धुनी धुनी, A river, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युधुनि|द्युधुनिः
द्यु-धुनि द्यु-धुनि, f. a name of the Gaṅgā, Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धु
धुन्धु धुन्धु, m. The name of an Asura or demon, Hariv. 672.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् धुर् (vb. धृ), f. (m., MBh. 13, 2876).<BR> 1. A yoke, Mṛcch. 63, 10.<BR> 2. A burthen, a load, MBh. 1, 741; 5, 2799.<BR> 3. The fore-part of the pole where the yoke is fixed, MBh. 3, 13310. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a " target="_blank">Page0443-a + 41</a>]<BR> 4. Place of honour, the head, Ragh. 14, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0442-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर|धुरः
धुर धुर, i. e. धृ + अ,<BR> I. m. A yoke, MBh. 7, 3675.<BR> II. m. and f. धुरा धुरा, A burthen, MBh. 13, 4879; Pañc. 26, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्यधुरा
अग्र्य-धुरा अग्र्य-धुरा, f. the fore-part of the pole, Pañc. 8, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरंधर|धुरन्धर|धुरन्धरः
धुरंधर धुरंधर, i. e. धुर् + अम्-धर,<BR> 1. adj.<BR> 1. Able to bear a burthen, MBh. 3, 12724.<BR> 2. Bearing patiently a burthen, MBh. 5, 1077.<BR> 3. Helping, Hit. i. d. 181.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A beast of burthen, Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 17.<BR> 2. A chief, MBh. 13, 6275.<BR> 3. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 6, 349.<BR> 4. The name of a Rākṣasa or demon, Rām. 6, 32, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण धुरीण, i. e. धुर् + ईन, m. A chief, Pañc. 187, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य धुर् + य (sometimes written धूर्य धूर्य),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Able to bear a burthen, MBh. 13, 3518.<BR> 2. Being at the head, MBh. 4, 1074.<BR> 3. Best, MBh. 3, 13309.<BR> II. m. A beast of burthen, Man. 4, 67.<BR> III. n. The fore-part of the pole, Rām. 6, 92, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधुर्य|कुलधुर्यः|कुलधुर्य्य
कुल-धुर्य कुल-धुर्य,<BR> I. adj. able to bear the burthen of a family, Ragh. 7, 68.<BR> II. m. the chief of a family, MBh. 3, 11826.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्
धुर्व् धुर्व् (akin to ध्वृ), i. 1, धार्व, Par.<BR> 1. To bend (ved.).<BR> 2. To hurt<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू धू and धु धु, ii. 5, धू̆नु, ii. 9, धुना, नी, Par. Ātm., and i. 6, धुव, Par.<BR> 1. To shake, Megh. 63.<BR> 2. To shake out, to remove, Bhāg. P. 2, 8, 5.<BR> 3. To blow (as wind), MBh. 3, 2733.<BR> 4. To shake off, MBh. 5, 1588.<BR> 5. To struggle, to resist, Pañc. i. d. 42. Anomal. potent. धुनेत्, MBh. 13, 5006. Pass. with the terminations of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-b " target="_blank">Page0443-b + 42</a>] Par., Sāv. 4, 29.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धूत and धुत,<BR> 1. Shaken, Rām. 3, 58, 37; 5, 16, 17.<BR> 2. Removed, Rām. 1, 31, 13; 1, 29, 11 Gorr.<BR> --Frequent. दोधू and दोधूय,<BR> 1. To shake violently, MBh. 12, 8564.<BR> 2. To move violently to and fro, MBh. 12, 8563.<BR> 3. To be shaken violently, Bhāg. P. 8, 24, 36.<BR> --Caus. धूनय, To shake, MBh. 3, 444.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To shake off, to remove, MBh. 3, 2033.<BR> 2. To refuse, Vikr. d. 130. अवधूत,<BR> 1. Cast off, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 19.<BR> 2. Removed, dispersed, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 32.<BR> 3. Disregarded, Vikr. d. 46.<BR> 4. Sent back, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 21.<BR> 5. One who has shaken off every terrestrial bond, an ascetic, Rājat. 1, 112.<BR> 6. Shaken, Man. 5, 125.<BR> 7. Struck, Rām. 6, 82, 62.<BR> 8. n. Thrusting off, MBh. 4, 352.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To shake, Man. 3, 229.<BR> --With व्यव व्य्-अव,<BR> 1. To shake off, to remove, Hariv. 11076.<BR> 2. To abuse, MBh. 2, 2231. व्यवधूत, Indifferent in regard of life, MBh. 6, 150.<BR> --With आ आ, To shake, Ragh. 16, 36. आधूत,<BR> 1. Shaken, Rām. 2, 104, 9 Gorr.<BR> 2. Troubled, Rām. 1, 65, 3.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To move to and fro, Śāk. d. 22.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To shake, Rām. 1, 33, 13 Gorr.<BR> --With उअ,<BR> 1. To rouse, Rām. 1, 28, 14.<BR> 2. To shake, Rām. 2, 95, 8.<BR> 3. To blow, Ragh. 7, 45.<BR> 4. To raise, Rām. 6, 92, 60.<BR> 5. To shake off, Bhāg. P. 8, 19, 38.<BR> 6. To dash out, Hariv. 4315. उद्धूत and उद्धुत, Loud, Hariv. 4718; 9608.<BR> --Comp.<BR> पाद-उद्धीत, n. Kicking with the foot, MBh. 4, 353.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To rouse, MBh. 1, 1336.<BR> 2. To shake, MBh. 1, 3846.<BR> --With नि नि, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-a " target="_blank">Page0444-a + 40</a>] To move to and fro, Hariv. 14650. (probably to be changed into वि-).<BR> --With निस् निस्, To shake off, Rām. 2, 95, 10.<BR> 2. To remove, Bhag. 5, 17.<BR> 3. To disown, Yājñ. 2, 71.<BR> 4. To shake, Hariv. 6238.<BR> 5. To torment, Rām. 5, 2, 26. निर्धूत, Deprived, Hariv. 3531.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्,<BR> 1. To shake off. Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 4.<BR> 2. To expel, Rām. 6, 16, 89.<BR> 3. To move to and fro, Rām. 2, 20, 4 Gorr.<BR> --With प्रविनिस् प्र-वि-निस्, To fling to, MBh. 12, 13417.<BR> --With परि परि, To shake to and fro, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 33.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To blow away = to destroy, MBh. 13, 1800.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To move to and fro, to shake, Rām. 2, 23, 4; MBh. 1, 7035.<BR> 2. To blow, MBh. 2, 1132.<BR> 3. To excite, Sāv. 4, 29 (anomal. ptcple. of the pres. pass. विधूयन्त्).<BR> 4. To remove, Rām. 3, 30, 18.<BR> 5. To disperse, Rām. 1, 54, 6.<BR> 6. To drive away, Kathās. 4, 108.<BR> 7. To shake off, Man. 6, 85.<BR> --Caus. To press hard, MBh. 12, 4361.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To drive away, Hariv. 10492.<BR> --Cf. θύω, θυίω, θύνω, θυνάω, θύελλα, θυεία, θυΐα, θύσσω, αἰθύσσω, θυάω; Lat. suffire, fimus; Iceland. dyja; perhaps Goth. dauns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यधूत
विर्य- + धूत वीर्य- + धूत, adj. surpassed in prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0443-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूति|धूतिः
धूति धू + ति, m. One who shakes, Chr. 290, 5 = Rigv. i. 64, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनन|धूननं|धूननः
धूनन धूनन, i. e. धू, Caus., + अन, n. Shaking, Rājat. 6, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् धूप्, i. 1, धूपाय, and i. 10, धूपय, Par.<BR> 1. To fumigate, Suśr. 1, 16, 9.<BR> 2. To perfume, Rām. 1, 10, 30; Śiś. 4, 52.<BR> 3. i. 10, Par. † To speak, or to shine.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To perfume, Rām. 2, 83, 16 Gorr.<BR> --With उप उप, To fumigate, Rām. 5, 14, 7. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b " target="_blank">Page0444-b + 41</a>]<BR> 2. To fill with smoke, MBh. 1, 815.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To perfume, MBh. 12, 1389.<BR> --Cf. τύϕω, θύψω, τῦϕος, τυϕεδανός, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप धूप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Incense, Rām. 1, 5, 15.<BR> 2. The aromatic vapour that proceeds from the burning of incense, Vikr. d. 43.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकधूप|वृकधूपः
वृक- + धूप वृक- + धूप, and वृक्ष-, m. 1. compounded perfume. 2. turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपक|धूपकः
धूपक i. e.<BR> I. धूप + क, A substitute for धूप, as latter part of comp. adj., e. g. स-धूपक, Filled with incense, Rām. 1, 73, 20.<BR> II. धूप् + अक, m. A preparer of perfumes, Rām. 2, 83, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपन|धूपनं|धूपनः
धूपन धूप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Fumigation, Suśr. 1, 133, 12.<BR> 2. Perfuming, MBh. 13, 4749.<BR> 3. Perfume, incense, Man. 7, 219.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपधूपन|सूपधूपनं
सूप- + धूपन सूप- + धूपन, n. assafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिक|धूपिकः
धूपिक धूपिक, i. e. धूप + इक, m. = धूपक<BR> II. Rām. 2, 90, 14 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम|धूमः
धूम धूम (vb. धू, or ध्मा), m. Smoke, Man. 4, 69.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. fumus; θυμός (originally breath), cf. ध्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूम
वि- + धूम वि- + धूम, adj. smokeless; loc. ˚मे, at the time when there is no smoke in the kitchen, Man. 6, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमक
धूमक धूम + क,<BR> I. a substitute for धूम as latter part of comp. adj., e. g. स-, adj. Covered with smoke, Suśr. 2, 318, 7.<BR> II. f. मिका, Smoke, Kathās. 8, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूममय
धूममय धूम + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of vapours, MBh. 5, 4059.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमय
धूमय धूमय, a denomin. derived from धूम by अय, To cover with vapours, to eclipse, Rām. 5, 21, 9.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, प्रधूमित, Covered with smoke, Ragh. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमवत्त्व
धूमवत्त्व धूमवत्त्व, i. e. धूम-वन्त् + त्व, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a " target="_blank">Page0445-a + 40</a>] n. Condition of having smoke, Bhāṣāp. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमवन्त्|धूमवत्
धूमवन्त् धुम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Smoking, Tarkasaṃgr. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाय
धूमाय धूमाय, a denomin. derived from धूम by य, Par., Ātm. To smoke, MBh. 3, 1319.<BR> 2. To be covered with smoke, Chr. 41, 21.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धूमयित, n. Smoking, MBh. 5, 4508.<BR> --Caus. धूमायय, To cause to be covered with smoke, MBh. 3, 1545.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र धूम्र, i. e. धूम + र (or rather an old धूमन् + अ, with र् for न्),<BR> I. adj., f. रा,<BR> 1. Of a smoky colour.<BR> 2. Black red, MBh. 1, 2033.<BR> 3. Gray, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 24.<BR> 4. Obscured, Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 48.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Rām. 4, 33, 14.<BR> III. f. रा, A proper name, MBh. 1, 2583.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्
† धूर् धूर्, i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To hurt.<BR> 2. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्जटि|धूर्जटिः|धूर्ज्जटि
धूर्जटि धूर्जटि (curtailed from धूर्जटिन्), and धूर्जटिन् धूर्जटिन्, i. e. धुर्-जटा + इन्, m. A name of Śiva, MBh. 7, 9621.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्त|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त धूर्त (properly ptcple. pf. pass. of ध्वृ), adj., f. ता, Fraudulent, knavish, a rogue, Pañc. 33, 4.<BR> 2. Gaming at dice, a gamester, Rām. 5, 13, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधूर्त|अक्षधूर्तः|अक्षधूर्त्त|अक्षधूर्त्तः
अक्ष- + धूर्त अक्ष- + धूर्त, m. A dice-player, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 17; 196, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तक|धूर्तकः|धूर्त्तक|धूर्त्तकः
धूर्तक धूर्त + क, m.<BR> 1. A cheat, MBh. 5, 1519.<BR> 2. The name of a Nāga or infernal serpent, MBh. 1, 2154.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगधूर्तक|मृगधूर्तकः|मृगधूर्त्तक|मृगधूर्त्तकः
मृग- + धूर्तक मृग- + धूर्तक, m. A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तता|धूर्त्तता
धूर्तता धूर्त + ता, f. Shrewdness, Bhartṛ. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलि|धूलिः
धूलि धूलि, i. e. धू + लि, or perhaps ध्वंस् + लि, f. Dust, Pañc. 215, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूश्
† धूश् धूश् (= धूष्, q. cf.), i. 10, Par. To make splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूष्
धूष् धूष् (perhaps a dialectical form of धृष् for हृष्), i. 10, Par. To make splendid.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, उद्धूषित, Having the hairs (of the body) standing on end (out of joy), embellished, Pañc. 190, 21.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोद्धूषित, Having the hairs standing on end (on account of chill), Pañc. 94, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूषरत्व
धूषरत्व धूषरत्व, read धूसरत्व, Lass. 72, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्
† धूस् धूस् (a dialectical form of धूष्, q. cf.), i. 10, Par. To make splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसर|धूसरः
धूसर धूसर, i. e. ध्वंस् + अर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Gray (like dust), Ragh. 5, 42.<BR> II. f. रा, A small shrub, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 76, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमधूसर
क्रम- + धूसर क्रम- + धूसर, adj. having become by degrees gray (like dust), Ragh. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरक
धूसरक धूसर + क, m. A proper name, Pañc. 214, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरत्व
धूसरत्व धूसर + त्व, n. Paleness, Lass. 72, 11 (see धूषरत्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ धृ, i. 1, Par., Ātm.; i. 6, ध्रिय, Ātm. (also Par., Hariv. 9693).<BR> 1. To bear, to carry, Rām. 1, 38, 11 Gorr.; Man. 4, 66; with गर्भम्, To be pregnant, MBh. 5, 7399; with दण्डम् and दमम्, To punish, Rām. 4, 17, 24; Bhāg. P. 1, 18, 41.<BR> 2. To maintain, Rām. 2, 109, 46 Gorr.; with आत्मानम्, जीवितम्, प्राणान्, शरीरम्, गात्रम्, देहम्, To endure, or to continue to live, Rām. 6, 82, 119.<BR> 3. To support, Man. 9, 311 (Ātm.).<BR> 4. i. 4, and pass. To exist, Bhag. 7, 5; to live, Man. 3, 220; with the termination of the Par., MBh. 3, 11293.<BR> 5. With मनस्, मतिम्, बुद्धिम्, To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0446-a " target="_blank">Page0446-a + 48</a>] direct one's attention to, MBh. 2, 541; to resolve, Hariv. 8261.<BR> 6. With and without तुलया, To weigh, MBh. 3, 10585; 1, 266.<BR> 7. With समये, To bring to an agreement, Pañc. 24, 25.<BR> 8. With अन्तरे, To give as surety, to pledge, Pañc. 223, 24.<BR> 9. To stop, MBh. 7, 619.<BR> 10. To retain, Pañc. 55, 23.<BR> 11. To resist, Pañc. ii. d. 150.<BR> 12. To have, MBh. 2, 81.<BR> 13. To keep, Hit. 68, 13. धृत,<BR> 1. Carried, Śāk. d. 103.<BR> 2. Worn, used, Man. 4, 66.<BR> 3. Held, Lass. 7, 5.<BR> 4. Weighed, Man. 8, 135 (सम-धृत, Of equal weight).<BR> 5. Maintained, Bhāg. P. 3, 3, 17.<BR> 6. Observed, Rām. 2, 18, 47 Gorr.<BR> 7. Firm, MBh. 5, 7337.<BR> 8. Kept, Pañc. 229, 6.<BR> 9. Ready, MBh. 5, 1446; resolved, 2108.<BR> 10. धृतम्, adv. Slowly, solemnly, Pañc. 158, 2.<BR> 11. n. A mode of fighting, Hariv. 15979. धृतवन्त्, Resolved, Kathās. 12, 49.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. शिरोधरणीय, i. e. शिरस्-, adj. To be borne on the head, i. e. to be venerated, Lass. 67, 14.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, धारय, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To bear, MBh. 13, 5007.<BR> 2. With दण्डम्, To punish, Man. 11, 21.<BR> 3. To hold, Rām. 1, 123, 14 Gorr.<BR> 4. With तुलया, To weigh, MBh. 3, 13293.<BR> 5. To continue to live, Chr. 46, 21.<BR> 6. To support, MBh. 14, 710.<BR> 7. To keep, MBh. 3, 11980; to possess, Rām. 1, 26, 25; Man. 5, 96.<BR> 8. To practise, Yājñ. 3, 201.<BR> 9. With आत्मानम्, मनस्, To direct one's attention to, Yājñ. 3, 201.<BR> 10. With and without मनसा, To keep in remembrance, MBh. 13, 4455; Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 75.<BR> 11. With शिरसा, मूर्ध्नि, To honour, Mṛcch. 19, 3.<BR> 12. To hold in, Śāk. 8, 11.<BR> 13. To endure, Rām. 3, 35, 39.<BR> 14. To contain, Hariv. 6567.<BR> 15. To recover, Rām. 1, 48, 33.<BR> 16. To assign to, Hariv. 2091.<BR> 17. To owe to, MBh. 12, 7286. Anomal. potent. धारयित, MBh. 13, 5007; anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. धारयाण, 6, 4600.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धारित, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0446-b " target="_blank">Page0446-b + 41</a>]<BR> 1. Borne, MBh. 3, 11169.<BR> 2. Maintained, Vikr. d. 38.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-धार्य,<BR> 1. Not to be borne, Rām. 4, 16, 31; Man. 3, 79.<BR> 2. Not to be stemmed, MBh. 13, 2161. दुस्-,<BR> 1. Difficult to be supported, MBh. 3, 9941.<BR> 2. Difficult to be kept in remembrance, 13, 4483.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To endure, MBh. 6, 5063. With प्रानान्, To continue to live, MBh. 3, 16221.<BR> --With अव अव, अवधृत, Perceived, MBh. 13, 3544.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To know exactly, Rājat. 3, 179.<BR> 2. To consider, MBh. 14, 1977.<BR> 3. To perceive, MBh. 3, 11210.<BR> 4. (Caus. of the Caus.), To communicate, Kathās. 14, 7. अवधार्य, What ought to be considered, Bhartṛ. 2, 97. अन्-अवधारणीय, Not to be known exactly, Ragh. 13, 5.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. To keep, Rām. 4, 20, 16; to keep in remembrance, Kathās. 2, 37.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To draw out, Rām. 4, 22, 21.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To support, MBh. 4, 1765.<BR> 2. To consider, MBh. 1, 7805.<BR> 3. To perceive, Bhāg. P. 1, 8, 11.<BR> --With नि नि, Caus. To keep, Bhāg. P. 3, 2, 22.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To verify, Śiś. 9, 20.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To bear, MBh. 3, 10907.<BR> --With प्र प्र. To direct to; with मनस्. To resolve, MBh. 8, 4336.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To inflict a punishment, MBh. 12, 9569.<BR> 2. To keep in remembrance, 5, 4120.<BR> 3. To reflect, 1, 3581.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To deliver, MBh. 3, 11741.<BR> 2. To direct; with बुद्धिम्, To resolve, 3, 8772.<BR> 3. To consider, to reflect, Pañc. 8, 14.<BR> --With वि वि, To bear. Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 13. विधृत,<BR> 1. Separated, MBh. 13, 7070.<BR> 2. Spread, Caurap. 16.<BR> 3. Par from, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a " target="_blank">Page0447-a + 43</a>] Hariv. 4253.<BR> 4. Retained, stopped, Amar. 85.<BR> 5. Borne, MBh. 14, 1654; with शिरसा, Borne on the head, and Honoured, Pañc. i. d. 94.<BR> 6. Maintained, Bhartṛ. 3, 58.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-विधृत, unrestrained, MBh. 1, 243.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To dispose, MBh. 1, 5549.<BR> 2. To act, 12, 3809.<BR> 3. To withhold, Rām. 2, 13, 3.<BR> 4. To stop, MBh. 3, 676.<BR> 5. To have, 9, 2476.<BR> 6. To direct, with मनस्, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 30.<BR> 7. To protect, 7, 5, 7.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To observe, Rām. 4, 29, 34.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To hold, Pañc. i. d. 93.<BR> 2. To bear, Rām. 2, 62, 15 Gorr.<BR> 3. To possess, MBh. 1, 6383.<BR> 4. To observe, Bhāg. P. 2, 1, 21.<BR> 5. To direct, with मनस्, 2, 38.<BR> 6. To keep in remembrance, Pañc. v. d. 78.<BR> 7. To restrain, Rām. 2, 21, 47; MBh. 6, 3397.<BR> 8. To endure, Rām. 2, 63, 38; to sustain, Man. 3, 79.<BR> 9. To exist, Mārk. P. 8, 52.<BR> --Cf. θράομαι, θρᾶνος, θρῆνυς, θέλω, ἐθέλω, θρόνος; Lat. firmus, fre + tus (partly based on ध्रा for धृ; cf. e. g. पृ and प्रा); probably A.S. dragan, dreogan; O.H.G. tragan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृक्
ऽधृक् -धृक्, latter part of comp. words, and only in the nom. sing. (probably a form of धृ + त्),<BR> 1. Bearing, Rām. 1, 6, 9.<BR> 2. Sustaining, MBh. 12, 10432.<BR> 3. Old, 3, 12597.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधृक्
दण्ड- + धृक् दण्ड- + धृक्, adj. ruling, Bhāg. P. 4, 21, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधृक्
देह- + धृक् देह- + धृक्, m. Air, wind, Suśr. 1, 250, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज्
† धृज् धृज्, and धृञ्ज् धृञ्ज्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --Cf. ध्रज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
ऽधृत् -धृ + त्, latter part of comp. words, Bearing, Hariv. 6766.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराष्ट्र|धृतराष्ट्रः
धृतराष्ट्र धृत-राष्ट्र, m.<BR> 1. The father of Duryodhana and uncle of the Pāṇḍu princes, MBh. 1, 95.<BR> 2. A frequent proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृति|धृतिः
धृति धृ + ति,<BR> I. f.<BR> 1. Holding, MBh. 7, 4540 (धृतिं कृ, To keep ground). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-b " target="_blank">Page0447-b + 44</a>]<BR> 2. Steadiness, Nal. 6, 10.<BR> 3. Content, Man. 10, 116.<BR> 4. Satisfaction, Kir. 5, 35.<BR> 5. personified, MBh. 1, 2794.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of a deity, MBh. 13, 4355.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृति|अधृतिः
अ- + धृति अ- + धृति, f. 1. uneasiness. 2. discontent, Man. 12, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माधृति|क्ष्माधृतिः
क्ष्मा- + धृति क्ष्मा- + धृति, m. a king and a mountain, Rājat. 5, 476.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधृति|शतधृतिः
शत- + धृति शत- + धृति, m. 1. Indra. 2. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमन्त्|धृतिमत्
धृतिमन्त् धृति + मन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Firm, Man. 7, 210.<BR> 2. Content, MBh. 13, 3054.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Agni, 3, 14188.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> III. f. मती, The name of a river, 6, 339.<BR> IV. n. The name of a division of the world, 6, 454.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमय
