धृष्
धृष् धृष्, i. 1; ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. To be courageous, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 81.<BR> 2. To dare, MBh. 1, 3573.<BR> 3. pass. To be subdued, Pañc. 265, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. धृष्ट.<BR> 1. Bold, MBh. 5, 1831.<BR> 2. Impudent, Bhartṛ. 2, 48; Daśak. in Chr. 198, 2.<BR> 3. n. The name of a spell, Rām. 1, 30, 4.<BR> 4. m. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. धृष्य, To be attacked, MBh. 12, 8176.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-धृष्य, 1. unassailable, MBh. 1, 5054. 2. unconquerable, Rām. 5, 42, 4.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10.<BR> 1. To lay hands on, to offend, MBh. 1, 2346.<BR> 2. To hurt, Hariv. 3153.<BR> 3. To violate, MBh. 5, 373.<BR> 4. To overcome, 3, 2149.<BR> 5. † To rain, v. r. अ-धर्षित, adj. Unassailable, Rām. 4, 15, 3. धर्षणीय, To be conquered easily, MBh. 5, 1472. अ-, adj. Unconquerable, Hariv. 4368.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To overpower, MBh. 14, 47.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अन्-आधृष्य, Unassailable, Chr. 27, 11.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To aggrieve, Yājñ. 2, 5.<BR> 2. To provoke, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a " target="_blank">Page0448-a + 41</a>] Hariv. 10295.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus. To animate, MBh. 5, 2357.<BR> --With परि परि, To pounce upon, MBh. 14, 1684.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To lay hands on, Rām. 3, 62, 18.<BR> 2. To overcome, 5, 58, 15; to lay waste, 5, 63, 5.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-प्रद्कृष्य, adj. Unconquerable, Pañc. 161, 14. दुष्-प्रधृष्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj.<BR> 1. Unapproachable, MBh. 6, 612.<BR> 2. Difficult to be overpowered, Rām. 6, 36, 24.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To assail, Rām. 3, 14, 12.<BR> 2. To violate, MBh. 13, 2291.<BR> 3. To overcome, 13, 2890.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus. To hurt, MBh. 12, 4998.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus.<BR> 1. To violate, Hariv. 4616.<BR> 2. To trouble, MBh. 12, 10541.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To violate, Hariv. 9937.<BR> --Cf. θάρσος, θράσος,, etc., ϕάρυμος, ϕαρυνός; Lat. fortis; Goth. ga-dars; O.H.G. gaturst; A.S. dear, thu dearst, thu dors + test, dyrstig, thrist, bold, etc.; to dare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अ-धृष्ट अ-धृष्ट, timid, Pañc. iii. d. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0447-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टत्व
धृष्टत्व धृष्ट + त्व, n. Impudence, Pañc. 27, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु धृष्णु, i. e. धृष् + नु,<BR> I. adj. Courageous, bold, Chr. 294, 1 = Rigv. i. 92, 1; MBh. 14, 2098.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 1, 3140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णुत्व
धृष्णुत्व धृष्णु + त्व, n. Boldness, MBh. 1, 6406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धॄ
† धॄ धॄ, ii. 9, धृणा, Par. To grow old, v. r. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे धे, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To suck, to drink, MBh. 7, 2276; Man. 4, 59.<BR> 2. To suck in, to absorb, Prab. 40, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनु|धेनुः
धेनु धे + नु, f.<BR> 1. A milch cow, one that has lately calved, Man. 11, 137.<BR> 2. The earth, MBh. 13, 3165.<BR> 3. Gift, MBh. 3, 12727; in this signification the word is used especially as [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b " target="_blank">Page0448-b + 43</a>] latter part of comp. words, e. g. तिल, MBh. 13, 3286; घृत-, 3523, etc., which imply that sesame, ghee, etc., are given instead of a milch cow, a milch cow being the usual present given to a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनु|असिधेनुः
असि- + धेनु असि- + धेनु, f. a knife; Daśak. in Chr. 198, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामधेनु|कामधेनुः
काम- + धेनु काम- + धेनु, f. cow that yields every wish, Kathās. 17, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिधेनु|क्षितिधेनुः
क्षिति- + धेनु क्षिति- + धेनु, f. the cow-like earth, Bhartṛ. 2, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुक|धेनुकः
धेनुक धेनु + क,<BR> I. m. The name of a demon, MBh. 5, 4410.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. A milch cow, 3, 13035.<BR> 2. A present (cf. धेनु<BR> 3), 3, 8065.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य|धैर्यं|धैर्य्य|धैर्य्यं
धैर्य धैर्य, i. e. धीर + य, n.<BR> 1. Gravity, Hariv. 8408.<BR> 2. Firmness, constancy, MBh. 3, 17381; Rām. 2, 63, 47.<BR> 3. Courage, Pañc. 21, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य|अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य्यः
अ- + धैर्य अ- + धैर्य, n. perturbation of mind, Man. 12, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यवन्त्|धैर्यवत्
धैर्यवन्त् धैर्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with constancy, Rām. 4, 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर्
† धोर् धोर्, i. 1, Par. To be quick, to have a good pace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौन्धुमार
धौन्धुमार धौन्धुमार, i. e. धुन्धु-मार + अ, adj. Referring to Dhundhumāra, MBh. 1, 468.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा ध्मा, i. 1, धम, Par.<BR> 1. To blow (as breath, wind), MBh. 14, 1732; Suśr. 1, 332, 11.<BR> 2. To produce sound by blowing, MBh. 2, 1925.<BR> 3. To excite fire by blowing, 2, 2483.<BR> 4. To melt, Man. 6, 71.<BR> 5. To throw, MBh. 5, 7209. Anomal. fut. धमिष्यन्ति, Rām. 3, 62, 7. Pass.<BR> 1. ध्माय, in epic poetry also with the terminations of the Par., MBh. 2, 1756.<BR> 2. In epic poetry also धम्य, 3, 16825; also with the terminations of the Par. 14, 1738.<BR> --Caus. ध्मापय.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ध्मापित, Turned to ashes, Suśr. 1, 46, 16.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, To blow away, Rām. 1, 42, 26 Gorr. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a " target="_blank">Page0449-a + 39</a>]<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To blow a wind instrument, Hariv. 15853.<BR> 2. To blow up; pass. To be filled with air, to swell, MBh. 12, 3555; Suśr. 1, 62, 1; also Par. 290, 10.<BR> --Caus. To blow up, to cause to swell, Suśr. 1, 374, 5.<BR> --With अत्या अति-आ, To gasp violently for breath, Suśr. 1, 38, 12.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, To blow a wind instrument, MBh. 7, 3096.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To blow a wind instrument, MBh. 2, 1925.<BR> 2. To sound, Hariv. 15854.<BR> --With उप उप, To excite fire by blowing, Man. 4, 53.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To blow out of something, Suśr. 1, 100, 5.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To blow away, i. e. to destroy, MBh. 2, 1028.<BR> 2. To blow into something, MBh. 14, 78.<BR> 3. To blow a wind instrument, MBh. 3, 789.<BR> --Caus. To blow a wind instrument, MBh. 3, 633.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To blow asunder, i. e. to disperse, MBh. 1, 5462; i. e. to destroy, Rām. 2, 80, 8.<BR> --Cf. θυμός, perhaps σμώνη, σμῶδιξ; O.H.G. tunst, perhaps A.S. dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माङ्क्ष्|ध्मांक्ष्
† ध्माङ्क्ष् ध्माङ्क्ष्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To crow.<BR> 2. To desire.<BR> --Cf. ध्राङ्क्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातृ
ध्यातृ ध्यातृ, i. e. ध्यै + तृ, m. One who reflects, who meditates, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान ध्यान, i. e. ध्यै + अन, n.<BR> 1. Religious, pious meditation, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 13; Bhag. 12, 12; Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 15.<BR> 2. Intuition, Rām. 1, 9, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानवन्त्|ध्यानवत्
ध्यानवन्त् ध्यान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Applying one's self to religious meditation, MBh. 12, 7170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यानिक ध्यानिक, i. e. ध्यान + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-b " target="_blank">Page0449-b + 41</a>] adj. Proceeding from pious meditation, Man. 6, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिन्
ध्यानिन् ध्यानिन्, i. e. ध्यान + इन्, adj., f. नी = ध्यानवन्त्, MBh. 13, 1016.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम ध्याम, n. A fragrant grass, Suśr. 1, 103, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै ध्यै (probably akin to अधि-या, but cf. also दीधी, दीदी), i. 1, ध्याय (in epic poetry also ध्या, ii. 2, e. g. ध्याहि, MBh. 3, 13210), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 13, 1994).<BR> 1. To contemplate, MBh. 2, 2563.<BR> 2. To think of, 5, 47; to meditate on, 3, 224.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ध्यात, Thought of, Bhartṛ. 3, 46.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To meditate on, MBh. 1, 3464.<BR> 2. To think of, 12, 9666 (with gen.).<BR> 3. To reflect, Rām. 1, 2, 20 (अनुध्यात्वा, instead of ˚ध्याय). अनुध्यात,<BR> 1. Thought of, MBh. 7, 2180.<BR> 2. Absorbed in meditation, 12, 4678.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु-,<BR> 1. To think of, MBh. 13, 968.<BR> 2. To think, 12, 6644.<BR> --With अप अप, To disregard, MBh. 7, 2076.<BR> 2. To hurt, 3, 13656.<BR> --With समप सम्-अप, To hurt, MBh. 3, 13655 (Ātm.).<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To desire, Yājñ. 3, 134.<BR> 2. To think of, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 44.<BR> 3. To meditate, to be absorbed in meditation, Man. 1, 8.<BR> 4. To curse (?), MBh. 13, 2144 (अभि-ध्यासुस्, 4. Aor. without augment in the sense of an imperat., cf. 2143).<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To reflect, MBh. 5, 2217.<BR> 2. To desire, Suśr. 1, 323, 15.<BR> --With अव अव, To disregard, Bhāg. P. 5, 4, 9.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To wish that something may happen to another (gen.), MBh. 13, 4900.<BR> 2. To be absorbed in meditation, Bhāg. P. 9, 14, 43.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To meditate [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a " target="_blank">Page0450-a + 38</a>] on, Hariv. 14823.<BR> --With उप उप, To think of, MBh. 1, 3847; (Hariv. 7453, read अपध्यातो).<BR> --With नि नि, To be absorbed in meditation, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 44.<BR> --With अभिनि अह्हि-नि, To attend to (acc.), Rām. 1, 28, 7.<BR> --With प्रणि प्र-नि, To direct one's attention to (acc.), Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 3.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To muse ver (acc.), Rājat. 1, 279.<BR> 2. To reflect, Rām. 6, 31, 2.<BR> --With परि परि, To muse, Rām. 2, 37, 13 Gorr. (परी on account of the metre).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To reflect, MBh. 1, 7013.<BR> 2. To think of (acc. and प्रति), Hariv. 10381.<BR> 3. To devise, MBh. 5, 3882.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To reflect, MBh. 3, 1411.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To devise, MBh. 5, 3880.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To reflect, MBh. 2, 8.<BR> --Cf. θεάω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्र
ऽध्र -ध्र for धर, f. ध्री, latter part of comp. words, e. g. मही-ध्र, m. A mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज्
ध्रज् ध्रज्, and † ध्रञ्ज् ध्रञ्ज्, i. 1, Par. To glide (as wind, birds, etc.), ved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण्
† ध्रण् ध्रण्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --Cf. ध्वन्; Goth. drunjus; θρῆνος, τενθρηδών (Frequent.), ἀνθρηδών; A.S. dran, a drone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस्
† ध्रस् ध्रस्, ii. 9, and i. 10. Par.<BR> 1. To glean.<BR> 2. To cast upward.<BR> --Cf. उध्रस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख्
† ध्राख् ध्राख्, i. 1, Par. = द्राख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ्
† ध्राघ् ध्राघ्, i. 1, Ātm. = द्राघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राङ्क्ष्|ध्रांक्ष्
† ध्राङ्क्ष् ध्राङ्क्ष्, i. 1, Par. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b " target="_blank">Page0450-b + 42</a>]<BR> 1. To crow.<BR> 2. To desire.<BR> --Cf. ध्माङ्क्ष्, ध्वाङ्क्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड्
† ध्राड् ध्राड्, i. 1, Ātm. To divide, to split.<BR> --Cf. द्राड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज्
† ध्रिज् ध्रिज्, i. 1, Par. To move.<BR> --Cf. ध्रज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु ध्रु, i. 1 and 6, Par.<BR> 1. To stand firm.<BR> 2. To go.<BR> 3. To know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव्
† ध्रुव् ध्रुव्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To stand firm.<BR> 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव ध्रुव (akin to धृ),<BR> I. adj., f. वा.<BR> I. Firm, stable, MBh. 1, 808; Rām. 1, 60, 17.<BR> 2. Permanent, Nal. 6, 11.<BR> 3. Fixed (as a day), MBh. 14, 1888.<BR> 4. Certain, Man. 7, 169.<BR> II. m. The polar star, MBh. 8, 2105; personified as son of Uttānapāda and grandson of Manu, 13, 195.<BR> 2. A name of Viṣṇu, 2, 1510.<BR> 3. The name of a Vasu, 1, 2528, and others.<BR> III. n. Permanence, Hariv. 3959.<BR> IV. adv. ˚वम्, Certainly, Man. 12, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. ga-triuwi; Goth. triggvs; A.S. treowe, for truwian; perhaps Lat. durus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अ- + ध्रुव अ- + ध्रुव, adj. 1. perishable, Rām. 3, 61, 34. 2. uncertain, 5, 37, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवच्युत्
ध्रुवच्युत् ध्रुव-च्यु + त्, adj. Felling what in firm, Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक्
† ध्रेक् ध्रेक्, i. 1, Ātm. = द्रेक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
† ध्रै ध्रै, i. 1, Par. To be satisfied.<BR> --Cf. perhaps τρέϕω, θρέψις, τρόϕις, ταρϕύς (= Caus. ध्रापय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस्
ध्वंस् ध्वंस्, base of the pass. and some other forms, ध्वस्, i. 1, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 1, 3596).<BR> 1. To fall to pieces, to perish, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 55.<BR> 2. To go away, MBh. 3, 12525.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ध्वस्त,<BR> 1. Fallen, Rām. 3, 58, 38.<BR> 2. Lost, 1, 58, 10.<BR> 3. Hurt, 6, 20, 22.<BR> 4. Disappeared 5, 21, 12.<BR> 5. Covered, MBh. 10, 662.<BR> --Caus. ध्वंसय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-a " target="_blank">Page0451-a + 40</a>]<BR> 1. To fell, Rām. 5, 63, 23.<BR> 2. To destroy, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 18.<BR> 3. To interrupt, Rām. 2, 60, 15.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप,<BR> 1. To go away, Hariv. 720.<BR> 2. To cause to go away, MBh. 1, 5596. अपध्वस्त, Reviled, miserable, Mṛcch. 124, 3 (crazed, Wils.).<BR> --With अभि अभि, To attack, MBh. 5, 3230.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus. To cover, MBh. 13, 4817.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To cover, Rām. 2, 42, 10.<BR> --With उप उप, pass. To be attacked, Suśr. 1, 21, 14.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, विनिध्वस्त, Destroyed, Rām. 2, 125, 13 Gorr.<BR> --With परि परि, परिध्वस्त,<BR> 1. Destroyed, Rām. 2, 33, 18.<BR> 2. Covered, 2, 41, 11 Gorr.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रध्वस्त, Perished, Bhartṛ. 3, 26.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to fall, MBh. 7, 1387.<BR> 2. To destroy, 1529.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रति-ध्वस्त,<BR> 1. Afflicted, MBh. 12, 3606.<BR> 2. Left (?), 3717.<BR> --With वि वि, To crumble down, MBh. 12, 7978.<BR> 2. To disperse, 5, 5877. विध्वस्त,<BR> 1. Fallen, 3, 2668.<BR> 2. Fallen to pieces, Rām. 2, 114, 6.<BR> 3. Destroyed, MBh. 1, 7675.<BR> 4. Whirled up, Rām. 6, 19, 12.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To break to pieces, MBh. 1, 8282.<BR> 2. To crush, 3, 16501.<BR> 3. To destroy, Rām. 5, 26, 37.<BR> 4. To hurt, 3, 53, 51.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, प्रविध्वस्त,<BR> 1. Thrown away, Rām. 6, 22, 26.<BR> 2. Struck, Hariv. 10627.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. vastus, vastare; O.H.G. wôsti; A.S. weste; Goth. driusan; A.S. dreosan, dysi, dyselic, dysig, dysian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस ध्वंस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Destruction, Prab. 82, 14.<BR> 2. Loss, Pañc. i. d. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन ध्वंस् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Destroying, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b " target="_blank">Page0451-b + 44</a>] MBh. 5, 5316.<BR> II. n. Destruction, Rām. 6, 38, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन् ध्वंस् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Perishing, Bhartṛ. 3, 35.<BR> 2. Destroying, Hariv. 4627.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज्
† ध्वज् ध्वज्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. vagus, vagari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज ध्वज, m. and n.<BR> 1. A flag or banner, Rām. 2, 67, 26.<BR> 2. A mark, a symbol, MBh. 1, 1511.<BR> 3. A distiller's flag, Man. 4, 85.<BR> 4. The penis, Suśr. 2, 114, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पताकध्वज
उद्-पताक-ध्वज उद्-पताक-ध्वज, adj. with raised flags and banners, Rājat. 5, 465.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिध्वज|कपिध्वजः
कपि- + ध्वज कपि- + ध्वज, m. a name of Arjuna, Bhag. 1, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशध्वज|कुशध्वजः
कुश- + ध्वज कुश- + ध्वज, m. a proper name, Rām. 1, 71, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडध्वज|गरुडध्वजः
गरुड- + ध्वज गरुड- + ध्वज, m. a name of Viṣṇu, MBh. 2, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृषध्वज
गो-वृष- + ध्वज गो-वृष- + ध्वज, m. a name of Śiva, Arj. 3, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालाध्वज|ज्वालाध्वजः
ज्वाला- + ध्वज ज्वाला- + ध्वज, m. fire, Rājat. 4, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालध्वज|तालध्वजः
ताल- + ध्वज ताल- + ध्वज, m. 1. a name of Balarāma, MBh. 9, 2139. 2. the name of a mountain, Śatr. 1, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिध्वज|तिमिध्वजः
तिमि- + ध्वज तिमि- + ध्वज, epithet of the demon Śambara, Rām. 2, 8, 12 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मध्वज|धर्मध्वजः
धर्म- + ध्वज धर्म- + ध्वज, 1. adj. one who displays the flag of virtue, a hypocrite, Bhāg. P. 3, 32, 39. 2. m. a proper name, 9, 13, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारध्वज
पार- + ध्वज पार- + ध्वज, m. pl. standards come from an opposite shore (i. e. from Ceylon), Rājat. 3, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरध्वज|मकरध्वजः
मकर- + ध्वज मकर- + ध्वज, m. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषध्वज|महिषध्वजः
महिष- + ध्वज महिष- + ध्वज, m. Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभध्वज|वृषभध्वजः
वृषभ- + ध्वज वृषभ- + ध्वज, m. a name of Śiva, Chr. 48, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरध्वज|सीरध्वजः
सीर- + ध्वज सीर- + ध्वज, m. Janaka, Mahāv. 5, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराध्वज|सुराध्वजः
सुरा- + ध्वज सुरा- + ध्वज, n. a tavern flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वज|स्मरध्वजं|स्मरध्वजः
स्मर- + ध्वज स्मर- + ध्वज,<BR> I. m. 1. any musical instrument. 2. a fabulous fish, the makara. 3. the penis.<BR> II. f. जा, bright moonlight.<BR> III. n. the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजवन्त्|ध्वजवत्
ध्वजवन्त् ध्वज + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Adorned with flags, Rām. 1, 5, 17.<BR> 2. Branded, Yājñ. 3, 243.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ensign, MBh. 9, 3302.<BR> 2. A distiller or seller of spirits, Man. 4, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिक|ध्वजिकः
ध्वजिक ध्वजिक, i. e. ध्वजिन् + क, adj. One who displays the flag of virtue, a hypocrite, Man. 13, 7594.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन् ध्वजिन्, i. e. ध्वज + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Furnished with, or bearing, a flag, Rām. 3, 28, 32; Man. 11, 92.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ensign, MBh. 1, 7765.<BR> 2. A distiller or seller of spirits, Yājñ. 1, 141.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मध्वजिन्|धर्म्मध्वजिन्
धर्म- + ध्वजिन् धर्म- + ध्वजिन्, i. e. धर्म-ध्वज + इन्, m. one who displays the flag of virtue, a hypocrite, Man. 4, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वञ्ज्
† ध्वञ्ज् ध्वञ्ज्, i. 1, Par. = ध्वज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण्
† ध्वण् ध्वण्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
1. ध्वन् ध्वन्, Par. To cover one's self.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ध्वान्त, n. Darkness, Rām. 2, 21, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
2. ध्वन् ध्वन्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To produce a sound, to roar, Ṛt. 1, 25.<BR> 2. To buzz, Rājat. 5, 315.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ध्वनित, n.<BR> 1. Sound, Megh. 43.<BR> 2. Thunder, Kir. 5, 12.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, ध्वा̆नय, To cause to sound, to strike, Śatr. 14, 223.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To sound, to hiss, Śiś. 20, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To resound, 17, 31.<BR> --Cf. A.S. dynan, dyne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनि|ध्वनिः
ध्वनि ध्वन् + इ, m.<BR> 1. Sound, Man. 4, 123.<BR> 2. Figurative style, Sāh. D. 5, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहध्वनि|सिंहध्वनिः
सिंह- + ध्वनि सिंह- + ध्वनि, m. 1. the roar of a lion. 2. war-cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसन्ति
ध्वसन्ति ध्वसन्ति, m. A proper name, Chr. 298, 23 = Rigv. i. 112, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्ति|ध्वस्तिः
ध्वस्ति ध्वस्ति, i. e. ध्वंस् + ति, f. One of the four states of a Yogin, that in which all the consequences of actions cease, Mārk. P. 39, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष्|ध्वांक्ष्
† ध्वाङ्क्ष् ध्वाङ्क्ष्, i. 1, Par. = ध्राङ्क्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वांक्षः|ध्वाङ्क्षः
ध्वाङ्क्ष ध्वाङ्क्ष, m. A crow, Brāhmaṇ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान|ध्वानः
ध्वान ध्वान, i. e. ध्वन् + अ, m. Murmuring, sound, Prab. 73, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
ध्वान्त ध्वान्त, see 1. ध्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ ध्वृ, i. 1. Par. To bend, to fell; cf. ह्वृ.<BR> --Cf. probably A.S. thwer; O.H.G. dweran, gadwor, twarôn, dwerh; A.S. thweorh, thwir, thwur; Goth. dvals; A.S. dwelian, dol, dweorg, for-dwilman; θόλος, θάλαμος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्व्रण्
† ध्व्रण् ध्व्रण्, i. 1, Par. = ध्रण्, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न न, a particle,<BR> 1. Not, MBh. 3, 362.<BR> 2. When repeated in the same sentence it implies a very strong affirmation, Absolutely, Arj. 10, 17.<BR> 3. Lest (with a potential), Rām. 2, 63, 41.<BR> 4. Often in the beginning of comp. words, e. g. नातिदूर, i. e. न-अति-दूर, adj. Not very distant, Hiḍ. 1, 51.<BR> 5. ved. Like, just as, Chr. 294, 5, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 5; 4.<BR> --Cf. Goth. ne, nei; A.S. ná; O.H.G. ni; Lat. ne in nonne; νη-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंश्
नंश् नंश्, see नश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिंचन
नकिंचन नकिंचन, i. e. न-किम्-च-न, adj. Beggarly, MBh. 5, 4522.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिस्
नकिस् न-कि + स् (the latter part is an old nom. sing. msc. of कि, cf. किम् and Lat. quis), a particle, Not, never, Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुल|नकुलः
नकुल नकुल, m.<BR> 1. The Bengal mungoose, Viverra ichneumon, MBh. 12, 444.<BR> 2. f. ली, Its female, 16, 41.<BR> 3. The name of the fourth of the five Pāṇḍu princes, 1, 2445.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क्
† नक्क् नक्क्, i. 10, Par. To kill, to annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त नक्त,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Night, Bhāg. P. 5, 22, 5.<BR> 2. Eating only by night, Yājñ. 3, 319.<BR> II. ˚तम्, adv. By night, Man. 6, 19.<BR> --Cf. Lat. nox, noctu; Goth. nahts; A.S. naht, niht; νύξ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तंचर|नक्तञ्चर|नक्तञ्चरः
नक्तंचर नक्तंचर, i. e. नक्त + म्-चर, m., f. री, A goblin, a demon, Rām. 5, 11, 9; Kathās. 25, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तंचर्या
नक्तंचर्या नक्तंचर्या, i. e. नक्त + म्-चर्या, f. Wandering by night, MBh. 12, 10575.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तंचारिन्
नक्तंचारिन् नक्तंचारिन्, i. e. नक्त + म्-चारिन्, adj. Walking by night, Man. 3, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तंदिन
नक्तंदिन नक्तंदिन, i. e. नक्त + म्-दिन,<BR> 1. n. sing. Day and night, Mālav. d. 88.<BR> 2. ˚नम्, adv. By day and by night, Pañc. 32, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमाल|नक्तमालः
नक्तमाल नक्तमाल, m. A tree, Pongamia glabra Vent., Rām. 3, 79, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्र|नक्रं|नक्रः
नक्र नक्र, m. A crocodile, Man. 1, 44.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रनक्र|वक्रनक्रः
वक्र- + नक्र वक्र- + नक्र, m.<BR> 1. A parrot.<BR> 2. A depraved man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ष्
नक्ष् नक्ष्, (akin to 1. नश्), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm.), To approach, to attain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्र|नक्षत्रं
नक्षत्र नक्षत्र, n.<BR> 1. A star, Man. 1, 24.<BR> 2. An asterism in the moon's path or lunar mansion; they are regarded as wives of the moon and daughters of Dakṣa, Hariv. 104; MBh. 13, 3256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रिन्
नक्षत्रिन् नक्षत्रिन्, i. e. नक्षत्र + इन्, adj. Epithet of Viṣṇu (containing the stars?), MBh. 13, 6996.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख्
† नख् नख्, i. 4 and i. 1, Par., and नङ्ख् नङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख नख,<BR> I. m. and n. A nail of a finger or of a toe, Man. 4, 35.<BR> II. n. and f. खी, A certain perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. nagal; A.S. naegel; ὄνυξ, ὀνύχιον; Lat. ungula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रनख
अग्र- + नख अग्र- + नख, the point of a nail, Rām. 2, 9, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनख|पंचनख|पञ्चनखः
पञ्चनख पञ्चनख, i. e. पञ्चन्-, m. a beast having five claws, Man. 5, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्पनखा|सूर्प्पनखा
सूर्प- + नखा सूर्प- + नखा, f. खा, the sister of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनख|हस्तिनखः
हस्तिनख हस्तिनख, i. e. हस्तिन्-, n. a sort of covered way, covering the access [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b " target="_blank">Page0453-b + 41</a>] to the gate of a fort or town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखर|नखरं|नखरः
नखर नख + र,<BR> I. adj. Shaped like a claw, MBh. 6, 693.<BR> II. (m. or n.),<BR> 1. A knife, 7, 1318.<BR> 2. A fingernail, a claw, Caurap. 15; Pañc. 91, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखानखि
नखानखि नखानखि, i. e. नख-नख + इ, adv. Scratching one another, MBh. 8, 2377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखायुधत्व
नखायुधत्व नखायुध + त्व, i. e. नख-आयुध + त्व, n. Being a beast using its nails or claws as its weapon, Pañc. 71, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखिन्
नखिन् नखिन्, i. e. नख + इन्, m. A beast with nails or claws, Cāṇ. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग|नगः
नग न-ग,<BR> I. adj. Immoveable, MBh. 12, 5730 (?).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mountain, Rām. 6, 83, 1.<BR> 2. A tree, Man. 8, 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगर|नगरं
नगर नग + र, n. and f. री, A town, Man. 4, 107.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्नगर
अन्तर्-नगर अन्तर्-नगर, n. a palace, Rām. 5, 11, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिनगर
काशि-नगर काशि-नगर, n. the city of the Kāśis = Benares, Chr. 11, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्वनगर|गंधर्वनगर
गन्धर्व-नगर गन्धर्व-नगर, n. 1. the city of the Gandharvas, MBh. 2, 1043. 2. the fata morgana, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भनगरी
विदर्भ-नगरी विदर्भ-नगरी, f. the city of the Vidarbhas, Nal. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखानगर|शाखानगरं
शाखा- + नगर शाखा- + नगर, n. a suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनगर
स्व- + नगर स्व- + नगर, n. own or native town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगराय
नगराय नगरय, a denomin. derived from नगर by य, Ātm. To look like a town, MBh. 9, 2162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीय
नगरीय नगरीय, i. e. नगर + ईय, adj. Belonging to a town, Lass. 75, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगवन्त्|नगवत्
नगवन्त् नग + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in trees, Rām. 5, 9, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न नग्न,<BR> I. adj., f. ना, Naked, Man. 4, 45.<BR> II. f. ना, A girl before menstruation, Pañc. iii. d. 217.<BR> --Cf. Goth. naqvadei; A.S. nacud, nacod, genacian; Lat. nudus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नक|नग्नकः
नग्नक नग्न + क,<BR> I. m. A naked mendicant, Pañc. 236, 4.<BR> II. f. निका, A girl before menstruation, Pañc. iii. d. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नजित्
नग्नजित् नग्न-जि + त्,<BR> I. m. The name of a prince, MBh. 1, 2439.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नत्व
नग्नत्व नग्न + त्व, n. Nakedness, Hit. pr. d. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नङ्ख्
नङ्ख् नङ्ख्, see नख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज्
† नज् नज्, i. 6, Ātm. To be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्
नट् नट् (a form of नर्त्, vb. नृत्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To dance, Gīt. 4, 9.<BR> 2. To injure.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10,<BR> 1. To dance, to represent as an actor, to act, Śāk. 6, 11.<BR> 2. † To fall.<BR> 3. † To speak or shine.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. नाटित, n. Representing, Śāk. 43, 4, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट नट (a form of नर्त),<BR> 1. m. A mime, MBh. 1, 6940.<BR> 2. f. टी, An actress, Śāk. 3, 9.<BR> 3. m. A tree, Caloranthes indica, Jonesia asoca, Rām. 5, 74, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानट|महानटः
महा- + नट महा- + नट, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटता
नटता नट + ता, f. The state of an actor, Hariv. 8692.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटन|नटनं
नटन नट् + अन, n. Dancing, Pañc. iii. d. 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्
† नड् नड्, i. 10, Par. To fall.<BR> --Cf. नट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड नड, probably a form of नर्त, m. (and n.), Reed.<BR> --Cf. नल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वल|नड्वलः
नड्वल नड्वल, i. e. नड + वल, n. A reed-bed, MBh. 5, 707.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमंहस्
नतमंहस् नतमंहस्, i. e. न तमंहस्, The beginning of a holy text, Man. 11, 251.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नताङ्ग
नताङ्ग नताङ्ग, i. e. नत-अङ्ग (vb. नम्),<BR> I. adj., f. गी, Bent.<BR> II. f. गी, A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नति|नतिः
नति नति, i. e. नम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. A bow, a courtesy, Kathās. 9, 18.<BR> 2. Modest behaviour, Navar. 3 in Haeb. Anth. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् नद् (probably a form of नर्द्), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm. MBh. 2, 1925), To sound, to roar, MBh. 3, 2855. Frequently with the acc. of a noun expressing sound, e. g. शब्दम्, To utter a sound, MBh. 3, 15655.<BR> --Caus. नादय, To cause to resound, to fill with noise, Rām. 1, 28, 5. Anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. नादयान, MBh. 6, 2269. नादित, n. Sound, 1, 7650. Frequent.<BR> 1. नानद्, To roar, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8; MBh. 7, 882.<BR> 2. नानद्य, To make a great noise, 7, 887.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To sound against (with acc.), Rām. 2, 111, 53 Gorr. (to rise to).<BR> --Caus. To cause to resound, to fill with noise, MBh. 5, 5169.<BR> --With व्यनु वि-अनु, Caus. To fill with noise, Bhag. 1, 19.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To sound against, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 2 (to answer).<BR> 2. To roar, Hariv. 11042 (p. 791).<BR> --Caus. To fill with noise, 13859. अभिनादित, Re-echoed, 4582.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. To fill with noise, MBh. 3, 789.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To roar, MBh. 7, 6814.<BR> 2. To bray, Pañc. 248, 17.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To roar, Hariv. 6754.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To roar, Hariv. 13167.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus. To fill with noise, Rām. 2, 28, 10.<BR> --With नि नि.<BR> 1. To resound, Pañc. 158, 5.<BR> 2. To sing, Rām. 2, 65, 2.<BR> 3. To cry, Ragh. 5, 75.<BR> --Caus. To fill with noise, MBh. 1, 119. निनादित, n. Sound, Rām. 1, 73, 36.<BR> --With परि परि, To cry aloud, MBh. 6, 3256.<BR> --With प्र प्र, णद् णद्, To begin to sound, to roar, MBh. 2, 1925; 3, 2859. प्रणदित, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a " target="_blank">Page0455-a + 42</a>] Buzzing, Śiś. 9, 71.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, Caus. To fill with noise, Rām. 5, 12, 45.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To cry, Rām. 5, 1, 87.<BR> --Caus. To fill with a cry, Rām. 4, 29, 15.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer with a cry, or with cries, Rām. 3, 24, 30; (with acc.) Rājat. 4, 285; MBh. 6, 4518.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To fill with cries, Hariv. 4179.<BR> 2. To cry aloud, MBh. 3, 14057.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To resound, Rām. 4, 9, 44.<BR> 3. To cry, 3, 30, 6.<BR> 3. To roar, MBh. 1, 6002.<BR> 4. To cry round about somebody (acc.), 11, 599.<BR> 5. To fill with cries, Hariv. 8097.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to sound, or to cry, Bhāg. P. 8, 8, 13; Ghaṭ. 10.<BR> 2. To fill with noise, MBh. 1, 1187.<BR> 3. To sound aloud, Rām. 6, 11, 23.<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि, Caus. To fill completely with noise, Rām. 2, 103, 48.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, To cry aloud, Rām. 6, 37, 37.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To roar, MBh. 7, 8127.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to resound, MBh. 1, 2896.<BR> 2. To cry aloud, MBh. 7, 8386.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद नद् + अ,<BR> I. m. A river, MBh. 1, 8730. A male river, Man. 6, 90.<BR> II. f. दी, A river, 3, 9; a female river, 6, 90.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिणदी
गिरि-णदी गिरि-णदी, i. e. गिरि-नदी, f. a mountain stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनदी
देव-नदी देव-नदी, f. A holy river, Man. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनदी
द्यु-नदी द्यु-नदी, f. a name of the Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगनदी
नग-नदी नग-नदी, f. the name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनद|पंचनद|पञ्चनदः
पञ्चनद पञ्चनद, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. n. 1. the country which is now called Panjāb. 2. the name of a river.<BR> II. m. 1. pl. the inhabitants of the Panjāb. 2. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानदी
महा-नदी महा-नदी, f. a great river, Rājat. 5, 98; = Gaṅgā, Chr. 26, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्नदी
स्वर्- + नदी स्वर्- + नद, f. the Gaṅgā of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदिका
नदिका नदिका, i. e. नदि + क, f. See क-नदिका, s. v. कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीज|नदीजं|नदीजः
नदीज नदी-ज,<BR> I. Born near a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-b " target="_blank">Page0455-b + 42</a>] river, epithet of horses, Rām. 1, 6, 24 Gorr.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Epithet of Bhīṣma, the son of the Gaṅgā, MBh. 4, 1294.<BR> 2. Antimony, Suśr. 2, 340, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीष्ण|नदीष्णः
नदीष्ण नदीष्ण, i. e. नदी-स्न (vb. स्ना), adj. Versed in, Ragh. 16, 75.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनदीष्ण
अति- + नदीष्ण अति- + नदीष्ण, Much versed in, Daśak. 180, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु न-नु, a particle of interrogation.<BR> 1. Not (Lat. nonne), MBh. 13, 313.<BR> 2. with an imperat. Do, Śiś. 9, 61.<BR> 3. Then, Mṛcch. 174, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्|नंद्
नन्द् नन्द् (probably for ननद्, a reduplicated form of नद्), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., Rām. 2, 84, 4), To be pleased, Rām. 1, 10, 28.<BR> --Caus. नन्दय, To gladden, Rām. 4, 22, 6.<BR> --With the prep. अभी,<BR> 1. To be pleased, Bhag. 2, 57.<BR> 2. To be pleased with (acc.), Man. 6, 45.<BR> 3. To desire, MBh. 13, 6655.<BR> 4. To salute, Pañc. 57, 18; with न, sometimes To receive unkindly, MBh. 14, 134.<BR> 5. To take leave from (acc.), MBh. 1, 5751.<BR> 6. To approve, Rām. 4, 10, 33; Śāk. d. 71.<BR> 7. To acknowledge, Man. 8, 54.<BR> 8. With न; sometimes To refuse. MBh. 5, 7505.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. अभिनन्दनिय, अभि-नन्द्य, To be rejoiced at. Śāk. 63, 18; 27, 6.<BR> --Caus. To exhilarate, Rām. 2, 107, 10.<BR> --With प्रत्यभि प्रति-अभि, To return a salutation. MBh. 13, 7721.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To congratulate, Kathās. 21, 148.<BR> --With आ आ, To be pleased, Gīt. 11, 10.<BR> --Caus. To gratify, Yājñ. 1, 355.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To gratify very mac, MBh. 15, 522.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To salute. MBh. 5, 1806.<BR> 2. To salute in one's turn, Man. 7, 146.<BR> 3. To show one's satisfaction, MBh. 13, 426.<BR> 4. To favour, Kumāras. 7, 87.<BR> 5. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a " target="_blank">Page0456-a + 44</a>] receive joyfully, MBh. 1, 7253.<BR> 6. With न, To refuse, 3673. अ-प्रति-नन्दित, Disowned, Bhāg. 4, 4, 8.<BR> --Caus. To gratify, MBh. 3, 16444.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To welcome joyfully, 10, 475.<BR> --With वि वि, To be pleased, 3, 2607 (Ātm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द|नंद|नंदः|नन्दः
नन्द नन्द् + अ,<BR> I. m. One of Yudhiṣṭhira's drums, MBh. 7, 1032.<BR> 2. A name of Viṣṇu, 13, 7005.<BR> 3. A proper name (especially of the foster father of Kṛṣṇa and Durgā), 4, 179; 1, 2731.<BR> 4. The name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 21.<BR> II. f. दा.<BR> 1. A proper name, MBh. 1, 2597.<BR> 2. The name of a river, 7818.<BR> III. f. दी, A tree, Cedrela toona Roxb., Suśr. 1, 219, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्द|सनन्दः
स- + नन्द स- + नन्द, m. one of the four sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनन्द|सुनन्दं|सुनन्दः
सु- + नन्द सु- + नन्द,<BR> I. adj. delighting.<BR> II. f. दा, 1. Umā. 2. a woman.<BR> III. n. the club of Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक नन्द् + अक,<BR> I. adj. in देवता-स्तव-, Gladdening the deities by praises, MBh. 13, 7662.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of Kṛṣṇa's sword, MBh. 5, 4427.<BR> 2. A proper name, 1, 6983.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिन्|नंदकिन्
नन्दकिन् नन्दकिन्, i. e. नन्दक + इन्, m. A name of Viṣnu (possessed of the sword नन्दक), MBh. 13, 7056.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नन्दन नन्द् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. ना, Gladdening, MBh. 3, 11073.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son, Yājñ. 1, 274.<BR> 2. Epithet of Viṣṇu and Śiva, MBh. 13, 7005; 1189.<BR> 3. A certain plant, Suśr. 2, 251, 19.<BR> 4. A proper name, MBh. 9, 2540.<BR> 5. The name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 21.<BR> III. n. The pleasure-ground of the gods, especially of Indra, Indr. 2, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कनन्दन|अर्कनन्दनः
अर्क- + नन्दन अर्क- + नन्दन, m. the planet Saturn, Pañc. i. d. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपनन्दन|काश्यपनंदन|काश्यपनन्दनः
काश्यप- + नन्दन काश्यप- + नन्दन, m. pl. the children of Kāśyapa, a name of the gods, MBh. 13, 3330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुनन्दन|कुरुनन्दनः
कुरु- + नन्दन कुरु- + नन्दन, m. a descendant of Kuru, Chr. 22, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनन्दन|कुलनंदन
कुल- + नन्दन कुल- + नन्दन, adj., f. ना, being an honour to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b " target="_blank">Page0456-b + 41</a>] a family, Pañc. 187, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीनन्दन
नलिनी- + नन्दन नलिनी- + नन्दन, n. a garden of Kuvera, Rām. 3, 36, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुनन्दन|भृगुनंदन|भृगुनन्दनः
भृगु- + नन्दन भृगु- + नन्दन, m. the son of Bhṛgu, i. e. Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनन्दन|रघुनन्दनः
रघु- + नन्दन रघु- + नन्दन, m. Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनक|नंदनकः|नन्दनकः
नन्दनक नन्दन + क, a substitute for नन्दन when latter part of a comp. word, MBh. 3, 10856.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः|नन्दिः
नन्दि नन्द् + इ,<BR> I. m.<BR> I. Epithet of Viṣṇu and Śiva, MBh. 13, 7015; 1189.<BR> 2. A proper name, 13, 872.<BR> II. f. (and m. and n.) Joy, MBh. 5, 4600; personified, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन् नन्द् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Liking, MBh. 6, 16.<BR> 2. Gladdening, 13, 4708.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son, Mṛcch. 47, 21.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 12, 10223.<BR> III. f. नी,<BR> 1. A daughter, 14, 1841.<BR> 2. The name of a fabulous cow, 1, 3923.<BR> 3. A proper name, 9, 2623.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपात्
नपात् न-पा + त्, नप्तृ नप्तृ (i. e. न-पा + तृ),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A grandson, Man. 4, 173.<BR> 2. A proper name, MBh. 13, 4362.<BR> II. f. नप्ती नप्ती (i. e. न-पात् + ई), A granddaughter, Chr. 289, 9 = Rigv. i. 50, 9, where the horses are denoted as granddaughters of the chariot.<BR> --Cf. Lat. nepos, neptis; O.H.G. nefo; A.S. nefa; O.H.G. nift; Goth. nithjis, nithjo; ἀ-νεψιός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंस|नपुंसः
नपुंस न-पुंस् + अ, m. An eunuch, MBh. 13, 901.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसक|नपुंसकं|नपुंसकः
नपुंसक नपुंस + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Neither man nor woman.<BR> 2. Of neuter gender.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An eunuch, MBh. 4, 1190.<BR> 2. A coward, Pañc. i. d. 364.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्ती
नप्ती नप्ती and नप्तृ नप्तृ, see नपात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् नभ्, i. 1, Ātm. † i. 4, ii. 9, Par.<BR> 1. To burst.<BR> 2. To injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ नभ, m. A proper name, Hariv. 823.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभग
नभग नभग, m. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 8, 13, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःश्रित्
नभःश्रित् नभःश्रित्, i. e. नभस्-श्रि + त्, adj. Reaching to, or attaining heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चर|नभश्चरः
नभश्चर नभश्चर, i. e. नभस्-चर,<BR> I. adj. Moving in the sky, Rām. 3, 49, 45.<BR> II. m. A deity, Ragh. 18, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस् नभस्, n.<BR> 1. Sky, atmosphere, Man. 4, 37.<BR> 2. du. Heaven and earth, MBh. 12, 13240.<BR> 3. Æther as one of the five elements, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 12.<BR> 4. (n. and m.) The name of a month of the rainy season (July--August), Ragh. 12, 29.<BR> --Cf. νέϕος, δνόϕος, ἰο-δνεϕής, γνόϕος, νεϕέλη; Lat. nubes, nebula; O.H.G. nibul; A.S. ge-nip, a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य नभस् + य, m. The name of a month of the rainy season, Hariv. 8781.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्वन्त्|नभस्वत्
नभस्वन्त् नभस् + वन्त्,<BR> 1. m. Wind, Ṛt. 2, 27.<BR> 2. f. वती, A proper name, Bhāg. P. 4, 24, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्
नम् नम्, i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., MBh. 3, 1200, especially when intransitive),<BR> 1. To bow to (with dat., gen. and acc.), Chr. 287, 8 = Rigv. i. 48, 8 (नानाम, ved. pf. red.); Bhāg. P. 4, 9, 47; MBh. 10, 495; Hariv. 10235.<BR> 2. To bow, Bhartṛ. 3, 61.<BR> 3. To submit, Kām. Nītis. 8, 55.<BR> 4. To sink, Mṛcch. 85, 11.<BR> 5. To bend, Suśr. 1, 254, 7.<BR> 6. † To sound.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. नत,<BR> 1. Inclined to (with acc. and gen.), Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 40.<BR> 2. Cast down, Pañc. 46, 5; Rājat. 5, 372 (read एका नतमुखी).<BR> 3. Bent, curved, Rām. 2, 96, 15; crooked, Vikr. d. 95.<BR> 4. Sunk in (not prominent), Kumāras. 1, 38.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. नमनीय, To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-b " target="_blank">Page0457-b + 42</a>] be bowed to, Bhāg. P. 3, 21, 21.<BR> --Caus. ना̆मय,<BR> 1. To cause to bow, Ragh. 8, 9.<BR> 2. To curve, bend, Pañc. i. d. 430; (as a bow), MBh. 3, 3039.<BR> 3. To cause to sink in, Hariv. 3754.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-नाम्य, adj. Not to be curved, or bent, Pañc. i. d. 430; MBh. 5, 1335.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To bow to, Indr. 2, 19.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To bow, Bhāg. P. 5, 25, 4.<BR> 2. To stoop, MBh. 1, 5336 (anomal red. pf. ननामिरे). अवनत,<BR> 1. Stooping, MBh. 3, 1776.<BR> 2. Bent, crooked, Rām. 2, 56, 7; Kumāras. 5, 86.<BR> 3. Sunk in (not prominent), Rām. 6, 23, 12.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to bow, Hariv. 3586.<BR> 2. To bend (a bow), MBh. 8, 4606.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, Caus. To bend downward, MBh. 3, 10062.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To bow, Rām. 2, 25, 38.<BR> 2. To bow to (acc.), Bhāg. P. 8, 23, 3. आनत,<BR> 1. Stooping, Hariv. 6344.<BR> 2. Stooping to (with acc.), Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 2.<BR> 3. Submissive, Man. 7, 69.<BR> 4. Bent, MBh. 1, 1667.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To bend downward, 5561.<BR> 2. To subdue, 4, 967.<BR> 3. To bend (a bow), 1, 7088.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To rise, Pañc. ii. d. 98.<BR> 2. To erect, to raise, Pañc. i. d. 407. उन्नत,<BR> 1. Erected, upright. Hit. 76, 6; raised, Draup. 5, 1.<BR> 2. High, Kir. 5, 15.<BR> 3. Sublime, Pañc. 24, 17.<BR> 4. Prominent, Mṛcch. 144, 18.<BR> 5. Vaulted, Bhartṛ. 1, 41.<BR> --Caus. To raise Rām. 5, 30, 12.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, अभ्युन्नत, Elevated, Śāk. d. 56.<BR> --With समभ्युद् सम्-अभि-उद्, समभ्युन्नत, Risen, Mṛcch. 76, 20.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोन्नत,<BR> 1. Very elevated, Pañc. 118, 9.<BR> 2. Superior, i. d. 387.<BR> --Caus. To erect, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 3.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुन्नत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-a " target="_blank">Page0458-a + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Upright, Hit. 76, 6.<BR> 2. High, Rājat. 5, 38.<BR> 3. Sublime, Kām. Nītis. 1, 64.<BR> 4. Prominent, Rām. 3, 52, 30.<BR> 5. Vaulted, Amar. 51.<BR> --Caus. To raise, Śāk. 40, 16.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To fall to one's share (with dat. and gen.), Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 14.<BR> 2. To present one with (acc. of the person and instr. of the object), 6, 19, 16. उपनत,<BR> 1. One who has submitted to somebody, MBh. 1, 5623.<BR> 2. Approached, Ragh. 10, 40.<BR> 3. Near, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 18.<BR> 4. Due, 4, 27, 25.<BR> --With निस् निस् णम् णम्, न्त्र्णत, Prominent, MBh. 7, 7894.<BR> --With परि परि णम् णम्,<BR> 1. To stoop (as an elephant about to strike with his tusks), Śiś. 18, 27.<BR> 2. To turn aside, Bhartṛ. 1, 4.<BR> 3. To change into (instr.), Kir. 13, 44.<BR> 4. To be digested, Pañc. 232, 7.<BR> 5. To grow old, Kir. 5, 37. परिणत,<BR> 1. Changed into (instr.), Megh. 46.<BR> 2. Ripe, MBh. 5, 1109.<BR> 3. Advanced, Pañc. 197, 18. m. An elephant stooping to strike with his tusks, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 17.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To ripen, Hariv. 2957.<BR> 2. To pass, MBh. 6, 3847.<BR> 3. To stoop, MBh. 8, 1143.<BR> --With प्र प्र णम् णम्,<BR> 1. To bow, Man. 2, 197.<BR> 2. To bow to, Man. 8, 23. प्रणत,<BR> 1. Bowing, Man. 11, 195.<BR> 2. Bowing to (with gen. and acc.), MBh. 4, 202; Rām. 1, 52, 1.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To order to bow to, Kumāras. 7, 27.<BR> 2. To bend, Mālav. d. 47.<BR> 3. To give. respectfully, Amar. 82.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र,<BR> 1. To bow, Rām. 1, 18, 5 Gorr.<BR> 2. To bow to, 2, 100, 37 Gorr. अभिप्रणत, 1, 70, 5 Gorr.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To bow to, Rām. 2, 112, 23.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To bow, MBh. 3, 2929.<BR> 2. To bend, Bhartṛ. 1, 66. विनत,<BR> 1. Sunk down, drooping, Śāk. d. 58; cast down. Brāhmaṇ. 1, 13.<BR> 2. Bent, Rām. 3, 50, 2.<BR> 3. Stooping, Ghaṭ. 18. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b " target="_blank">Page0458-b + 40</a>] f. ता,<BR> 1. A sort of basket.<BR> 2. The wife of Kaśyapa and mother of Araṇa and Garuḍa.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To bend down, MBh. 3, 15588.<BR> 2. To bend, 4, 394; (a bow), 1, 5436.<BR> 3. To incline, Amar. 81.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To bow, Rām. 2, 72, 30.<BR> 2. To bow to, MBh. 5, 1130.<BR> 3. To submit to, Ragh. 18, 33. संनत,<BR> 1. Bent, Rām. 3, 16, 5.<BR> 2. Curved, Kumāras. 1, 34.<BR> 3. Stooping, Indr. 1, 10.<BR> 4. Bowed to, Bhāg. P. 7, 4, 32.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To bend, MBh. 12, 10675.<BR> 2. To cause to sink, Bhāg. P. 8, 18, 20.<BR> --Cf. νέμω; Goth. and A.S. niman (originally, to subdue); perhaps A.S. ge-nedhan (cf. नत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनत
त्रि-नत त्रि-नत, bent at three places (as a bow), Rām. 6, 20, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस् नम् + अस्, n. Bowing, adoration, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 41; Rām. 1, 52, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कर्तृ
नमस्कर्तृ नमस्-कर्तृ, m. One who adores (the gods), MBh. 13, 6706.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कार|नमस्कारः
नमस्कार नमस्-कार, m. and नमस्क्रिया नमस्-क्रिया, f. Adoration, Nal. 5, 16; MBh. 15, 954.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नमस्कार
निस्-नमस्कार निस्-नमस्कार, adj. 1. respecting nobody, Rām. 2, 24, 24. 2. respected by nobody, Man. 9, 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य नमस्य, a denomin. derived from नमस् by य, Par. (Ātm. MBh. 13, 5129). To adore, MBh. 2, 234.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, The same, Hariv. 7769.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य नमस् + य, adj., or ptcple. of the fut. pass. of नमस्य, What ought to be adored, MBh. 13, 2142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्विन्
नमस्विन् नमस् + विन्, adj. Respectful, Lass. 102, 7 = Rigv. vii. 14, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचि|नमुचिः
नमुचि न-मुच् + इ, m. The name of a demon subdued by Indra, MBh. 1, 2530.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्ब्
† नम्ब् नम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र नम् + र, adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Bent, Bhartṛ. 2, 62.<BR> 2. Bowed, Bhāg. P. 6, 17, 16.<BR> 3. Crooked, Ṛt. 6, 10.<BR> 4. Addicted, Kathās. 17, 56.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
वि- + नम्र वि- + नम्र, adj. 1. bent, bowed. 2. humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रता
नम्रता नम्र + ता, f.<BR> 1. Bowing, Rājat. 5, 223.<BR> 2. Respect, Bhartṛ. 2, 52.<BR> 3. Humbleness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रत्व|नम्रत्वं
नम्रत्व नम्र + त्व, n. Humility, Bhartṛ. 2, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय्
† नय् नय्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To protect.<BR> --Cf. नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय नय, i. e. नी + अ, m.<BR> 1. Leading, Rām. 2, 1, 21.<BR> 2. Conduct, Hariv. 7346; way of life, Kathās. 20, 191.<BR> 3. Prudent conduct, Bhartṛ. 2, 19.<BR> 4. Prudence, Bhāg. P. 3, 7, 9; Daśak. in Chr. 198, 6 (read त्वन्नय एवात्र भूयान्, Thy prudence is here of greater weight).<BR> 5. Policy, Man. 7, 159.<BR> 6. Design, Pañc. i. d. 358.<BR> 7. Philosophical system, Bhāṣāp. 16.<BR> 8. Prudent conduct personified as son of Dharma by Kriyā, Mārk. P. 50, 26.<BR> 9. A proper name, Hariv. 489.<BR> --Comp.<BR> cf. अनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनय|अपनयः
अप- + नय अप- + नय, m. bad policy, Rām. 4, 40, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नय|दुर्नयः
दुस्- + नय दुस्- + नय (written sometimes दुर्णय दुर्णय instead of दुर्नय दुर्नय), m. bad conduct, MBh. 1, 4379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनय|राजनयः
राज-नय राज-नय, i. e. राजन्-, m. policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनय|सुनयः
सु- + नय सु- + नय, m. 1. good conduct. 2. policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयन|नयनं
नयन नयन, i. e. नी + अन, n.<BR> 1. Leading, MBh. 12, 458.<BR> 2. Ruling, 1, 2580.<BR> 3. Leading to, Śāk. 71, 14.<BR> 4. Bringing, Pañc. 174, 19.<BR> 5. The eye, Rām. 1, 59, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनयन|त्रिनयनः
त्रि- + नयन त्रि- + नयन, त्रिणयन त्रिणयन and त्रिनयन, adj. having three eyes, epithet of Śiva, Megh. 53; MBh. 14, 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमनयन|विषमनयनः
विषम- + नयन विषम- + नयन, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रुनयन
साश्रु- + नयन साश्रु- + नयन, i. e. स-अश्रु-, adj., f. ना, the eyes filled with tears, Chr. 7, 21. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b " target="_blank">Page0459-b + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनयन|सुनयनः
सु- + नयन सु- + नयन,<BR> I. m. a deer.<BR> II. f. ना, a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयवन्त्|नयवत्
नयवन्त् नय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Versed in policy, Rām. 5, 81, 14.<BR> 2. Prudent, Kir. 5, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर|नरं|नरः
नर नर, i. e. नृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A man; pl. Men, Man. 1, 96.<BR> 2. The Eternal, the divine imperishable spirit pervading the universe, Man. 1, 10.<BR> 3. pl. Certain fabulous beings, MBh. 2, 396.<BR> 4. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 8, 1, 27.<BR> --Cf. Lat. Nero, Neriene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरक|नरकं|नरकः
नरक नरक, m.<BR> 1. Hell, the infernal regions, Man. 2, 116.<BR> 2. The name of a demon, MBh. 1, 2537.<BR> 3. The name of a country, MBh. 2, 578.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानरक|महानरकः
महा- + नरक महा- + नरक, m. the name of a hell, Man. 4, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकाय
नरकाय नरकय, a denomin. derived from नरक by the aff. य, Ātm. To resemble hell, Mārk. P. 8, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरता
नरता नर + ता, f. Human condition, Bhāg. P. 7, 14, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त|नर्तः|नर्त्त
ऽनर्त -नर्त, i. e. नृत् + अ, adj. Dancing, MBh. 13, 1164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तक|नर्तकः|नर्त्तक|नर्त्तकः
नर्तक नर्तक, i. e. नृत् + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A dancer, Rām. 1, 12, 7.<BR> 2. A dancing-master, MBh. 4, 305.<BR> II. f. की, A female dancer, Ragh. 19, 14.<BR> III. adj. Causing to dance, Sāh. D. 74, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनर्तक|हरिणनर्तकः|हरिणनर्त्तक|हरिणनर्त्तकः
हरिण- + नर्तक हरिण- + नर्तक, m. a Kiṃnara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तन|नर्तनः|नर्त्तन|नर्त्तनं
नर्तन नर्तन, i. e. नृत् + अन.<BR> I. m. A dancer, MBh. 4, 1217.<BR> II. n. Dancing, Man. 2, 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तयितृ
नर्तयितृ नर्तयितृ, i. e. नृत्, Caus., + तृ, m. A dancing-master, Mālav. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्
नर्द् नर्द्, i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., Hariv. 11936), To roar, MBh. 1, 4114. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a " target="_blank">Page0460-a + 39</a>]<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. नर्दित,<BR> 1. n. Roaring, Rām. 4, 8, 38.<BR> 2. m. The name of one of the dice, Mṛcch. 33, 10.<BR> --Frequent. नानर्द्, To sound aloud, Hariv. 8064 (anomal. Ātm. नानर्दमान).<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To roar at, MBh. 6, 2738.<BR> --With आ आ, आनर्दित, n. Roaring, Rām. 2, 42, 20.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To greet with roaring, crying, MBh. 8, 1806.<BR> 2. To roar for, 12, 5777.<BR> --With वि वि, To roar, MBh. 8, 2468.<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि, To answer with roaring, Hariv. 14559.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्ब्
† नर्ब् नर्ब्, i. 1, Par. = नम्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मद|नर्मदः|नर्म्मद|नर्म्मदः
नर्मद नर्मद, i. e. नर्मन्-द,<BR> 1. adj. Causing pleasure, Somad. Nal. 128.<BR> 2. f. दा, The name of a river, the modern Nerbudda, MBh. 2, 371; personified, 15, 550.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मन्|नर्म्मन्
नर्मन् नर्मन्, probably नर्द् + मन्, n. Jest, sport, MBh. 1, 1000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मय
नर्मय नर्मय, a denomin. derived from नर्मन् by अय, Par. To exhilarate by jesting, Kām. Nītis. 7, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य नर्य, i. e. नर + य,<BR> 1. adj. Manly (ved.).<BR> 2. A proper name (?), Chr. 296, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्
† नल् नल्, i. 1, Par. To smell; to bind (?).<BR> --i. 10, Par. To speak, or to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल नल (for नड, q. cf.), m.<BR> 1. A kind of reed, Amphidonax karka Lindl., MBh. 6, 4898.<BR> 2. A proper name, Hariv. 823; the hero of the episode Nala and Damayantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलद|नलदं
नलद नलद,<BR> 1. n. (and f. दा), The Indian spikenard, Nardostachys jatamansi, Suśr. 1, 140, 20.<BR> 2. n. The root of the Andropogon muricatus, Kir. 5, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिन|नलिनं|नलिनः
नलिन नलिन, i. e. नल + इन,<BR> I. n. A lotus flower, MBh. 7, 1299.<BR> II. f. नी,<BR> 1. A lotus, Nelumbium speciosum, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR> 2. An assemblage of lotus flowers, Vikr. d. 5.<BR> 3. A pond in which the lotus grows or may grow, Draup. 6, 2.<BR> 4. A branch of the heavenly Ganges, Hariv. 3502.<BR> 5. A mystical name of one of the nostrils, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 48.<BR> 6. A proper name, 9, 21, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

