नल्व|नल्वः
नल्व नल्व, perhaps नत + व, cf. नड्वल, m. A furlong, a distance measured by four hundred (?) cubits, Rām. 6, 82, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव नव (akin to the particle नु, cf. नूतन),<BR> I. adj., f. वा.<BR> 1. New, Man. 11, 186.<BR> 2. Fresh, Bhartṛ. 1, 7.<BR> 3. Young, MBh. 4, 410.<BR> 3. ˚वम्, adv. Just, Mṛcch. 108, 7.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Hariv. 1677.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. novus; νέος; Goth. nivjis; A.S. niwe, neow, niwa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

