1. नश् नश्, i. 1, Par. To attain (ved.).<BR> --Cf. Lat. nanciscor, and 2. नश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
2. नश् नश् (the base of many forms is नंश्), i. 4, Par. (also Ātm., Rām. 5, 27, 24, and i. 1, Par. and Ātm., MBh. 13, 3083; 7, 685.),<BR> 1. To be lost, Man. 8, 32.<BR> 2. To disappear, Man. 8, 247.<BR> 3. To escape, MBh. 5, 2736.<BR> 4. To go away, Rām. 5, 27, 24.<BR> 5. To perish, Man. 4, 52.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. नष्ट,<BR> 1. Lost, Śāk. d. 167.<BR> 2. Invisible, Rām. 3, 50, 7; disappeared, MBh. 3, 2690.<BR> 3. Destroyed, MBh. 1, 3147.<BR> 4. Dead, Man. 8, 166.<BR> --Caus. नाशय,<BR> 1. To cause to disappear, Rām. 1, 55, 20.<BR> 2. To efface, Man. 11, 245.<BR> 3. To destroy, Rām. 5, 63, 8; Man. 2, 55.<BR> 4. To violate, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 10.<BR> 5. To extinguish, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 20.<BR> 6. To lose, Pañc. i. d. 23.<BR> 7. To disappear, MBh. 5, 862.<BR> --With the prep. व्यप वि-अप, Caus. To remove, MBh. 5, 7090.<BR> --With अव अव, To disappear, 4, 1728.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निर्नष्ट, Disappeared, Rājat. 1, 83. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-a " target="_blank">Page0462-a + 41</a>]<BR> --With प्र प्र णश् णश्, except where ś is changed to ष्, e. g. प्र-नष्ट,<BR> 1. To be lost, Man. 8, 149.<BR> 2. To disappear, Bhag. 1, 40. प्रनष्ट (sometimes erroneously प्रणष्ट),<BR> 1. Perished, Rājat. 5, 211.<BR> 2. Disappeared, Man. 8, 30.<BR> 3. Escaped, Pañc. 89, 20.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to disappear, MBh. 7, 327.<BR> 2. To cause to be lost, Hit. iv. d. 9 (to leave unrewarded).<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र,<BR> 1. To disappear, MBh. 3, 5027.<BR> 2. To be lost, 13, 3212. विप्रनष्ट,<BR> 1. Disappeared, MBh. 4, 877.<BR> 2. Lost, 1, 4802.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To be lost, MBh. 3, 13781. सम्प्रनष्ट, Disappeared, 2847.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To disappear, Man. 11, 263.<BR> 2. To perish, 2, 163. विनष्ट,<BR> 1. Lost, Mālav. 9, 3.<BR> 2. Utterly ruined or spoiled, Man. 7, 41; 2, 64.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To destroy, 7, 19.<BR> 2. To kill, Pañc. 71, 24.<BR> 3. To perish (Aor.), Rām. 2, 110, 30.<BR> --Desid. of the Caus. विनाशयिषित, without reduplication; read rather निनाश्˚, Sought to be destroyed, Daśak. 112, 3, below.<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि, To perish afterward, or together with, MBh. 12, 3400.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To perish, Rām. 1, 56, 27 Gorr.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संनष्ट, Perished, Rām. 5, 51, 13.<BR> --Cf. 1. नश्, The original signification of 1. and 2. नश्, has been probably, To hasten (cf. Lat. per-nix); then on the one side, To overtake, to attain (1. नश्); on the other, To hasten out of view, to disappear, to vanish, to perish (2. नश्).<BR> --Cf. νέκυς, νεκρός, etc.; Lat. per-nicies, necare, nocere, ve-nenum (for ve-nec + num); Goth. naus (for nahu + s = νέκυς), navis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर 2. नश् + वर, adj., f. री, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b " target="_blank">Page0462-b + 41</a>] Perishable, Kathās. 19, 50.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वर|अनश्वरं
अ- + नश्वर अ- + नश्वर, adj. imperishable, Bhartṛ. 3, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वरत्व
नश्वरत्व नश्वर + त्व, n. Perishableness, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टि|नष्टिः
नष्टि नष्टि, i. e. नश् + ति, f. Ruin, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् नस्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. † To be crooked.<BR> 2. To go to, to join (ved.).<BR> --Cf. νέομαι (? perhaps = ved. नु), νίσσομαι (for νεσϳομαι), νόστος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् नस् see नासा and अस्मद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस
ऽनस -नस् + अ, a substitute for नासा, when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. उन्नस, i. e. उद्-, adj. Having a prominent nose, Bhāg. P. 8, 8, 42. गो-,<BR> 1. m. A large kind of snake, Suśr. 2, 265, 12.<BR> 2. f. सा, The nose of a cow, 2, 171, 7.<BR> 3. f. सी, A certain plant, 2, 170, 1. वि-, adj. Noseless. सु-, adj. Handsomenosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तक|नस्तकं
नस्तक नस् + त + क, m. A hole bored through the bridge of the nose of cattle for draught, MBh. 12, 9377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्ततस्
नस्ततस् नस् + त + तस्, adv. Out of the nose, MBh. 4, 2227.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तस्
नस्तस् नस् + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. Out of the nose, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 11.<BR> 2. In the nose, Suśr. 2, 297, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य नस् + य, n.<BR> 1. A sternutatory, Suśr. 2, 235, 21. 2. f. या, A nosebridle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ननस्य
छिन्न-नस्य छिन्न-नस्य, adj. with broken nose-bridle, Yājñ. 2, 299.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्योत|नस्योतः
नस्योत नस्योत, i. e. नस् + इ-आ-उत (vb. वे), adj.<BR> 1. Led by a string through the septum of the nose, MBh. 3, 1142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह्
नह् नह् (for original नध्), i. 4, Par., Ātm. (also i. 1 or 6, MBh. 1, 1460),<BR> 1. To bind, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 38.<BR> 2. Ātm. To arm one's self, MBh. 4, 1016.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. नद्ध,<BR> 1. Tied, Rām. 4, 12, 19.<BR> 2. Bound, Rām. 5, 14, 15.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-a " target="_blank">Page0463-a + 41</a>] Covered, Hariv. 8799.<BR> 4. Joined, Rām. 4, 13, 13.<BR> 5. Laid in, MBh. 2, 1915.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, To untie, MBh. 3, 13309.<BR> --With अपि अपि, or पि पि,<BR> 1. To fasten, MBh. 4, 301; 13, 2352.<BR> 2. To squeeze, Śāk. d. 18.<BR> 3. To cover, Rām. 5, 18, 4. पिनद्ध, Striped, MBh. 13, 976 (इन्द्रायुधपिनद्धाङ्ग, of which the body was adorned by a rainbow, viz. a cloud).<BR> --With अव अव, अवनद्ध, Covered, Man. 6, 76.<BR> --With आ आ, Ātm. To be obstructed, Suśr. 2, 369, 10. आनद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound, MBh. 6, 5525.<BR> 2. Obstructed, Suśr. 2, 373, 21<BR> 3. Covered, 1, 22, 3.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, व्यानद्ध, Striped (cf. अपि), Hariv. 6884.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To press out, Suśr. 1, 301, 9.<BR> 2. To come out, MBh. 3, 11016 (p. 570). उन्नद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound upward, Ragh. 18, 50.<BR> 2. Raised, Bhāg. P. 4, 11, 4.<BR> 3. Unfettered, 4, 27, 4.<BR> 4. Proud, 4, 14, 4.<BR> 5. Arrogant, 7, 10, 26.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुन्नद्ध,<BR> 1. Unfettered, Bhāg. P. 4, 17, 33.<BR> 2. Pressed out, Suśr. 1, 280, 20.<BR> 3. Excessive, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 3.<BR> 4. Conceited, MBh. 5, 1000.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With उप उप, उपनद्ध, Laid in, Bhāg. P. 8, 15, 6.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be dressed (as a wound), Suśr. 2, 109, 18.<BR> --With परि परि णह् णह्,<BR> 1. To span, MBh. 1, 1406.<BR> 2. To surround, Ṛt. 6, 25. परिणद्ध, Large, Ragh. 3, 34.<BR> --With पि पि, see अपि.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To fasten, Bhāg. P. 8, 12, 21.<BR> 2. To dress, MBh. 4, 1220.<BR> 3. To put on, MBh. 218, 7; 3, 14958.<BR> 4. To prepare for, Bhartṛ. 2, 6. संनद्ध,<BR> 1. Tied together, Rājat. 4, 543.<BR> 2. Fastened, MBh. 15, 627.<BR> 3. Bordering, Rām. 1, 38, 21. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b " target="_blank">Page0463-b + 42</a>]<BR> 4. Armed, MBh. 2, 2463.<BR> 5. Accoutred, Hariv. 6402.<BR> 6. Ready, Rājat. 1, 77.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, अभिसंनद्ध, Armed, MBh. 3, 14883.<BR> --Cf. Lat. nexus, nectere, nere; νέω, νήθω; O.H.G. nâhan, nâwan; Goth. nêthla; A.S. naedl; Goth. nehv, nehva, nehvis; A.S. neah, nearra, neahst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमुन्नद्ध
अ- + समुन्नद्ध अ- + समुन्नद्ध, adj. modest, 5, 1010.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि न-हि, adv.<BR> 1. For not (non enim), Man. 3, 168.<BR> 2. Not at all, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 23.<BR> 3. न--नहि, Certainly not, Pañc. translation by Benfey, T. i. p. 465, n. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष|नहुषः
नहुष नहुष, m. The name of an ancient king, Man. 7, 41; of a Nāga, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक नाक, n.<BR> 1. Heaven, MBh. 13, 4882.<BR> 2. The mystical name of a weapon, MBh. 5, 3490.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनाक
त्रि- + नाक त्रि- + नाक, n. the three heavens, Bhāg. P. 6, 13, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकपृष्ठ्य
नाकपृष्ठ्य नाकपृष्ठ्य, i. e. नाक-पृष्ठ + य, adj. Being in the highest heaven, Rām. 3, 9, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन् नाकिन्, i. e. नाक + इन्, m. A god, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुल|नाकुलः
नाकुल नाकुल, i. e. नकुल + अ,<BR> I. adj. Ichneumon-like, Suśr. 2, 305, 21.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 6, 2084.<BR> III. f. ली, The ichneumon plant, Suśr. 2, 297, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुलि
नाकुलि नाकुलि, i. e. नकुल + इ. patronym. A descendant of Nakula, MBh. 1, 2451.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग नाग, i. e. नग + अ, 1. m.<BR> 1. A serpent, especially the name of fabulous serpents, having a human face and inhabiting Pātāla, or the infernal regions, Rām. 2, 25, 30; Man. 1, 37.<BR> 2. An elephant, Rām. 1, 6, 22.<BR> 3. A small tree, Mesua Roxburghii Wight., Suśr. 1, 171, 7.<BR> 4. One of the five vital airs, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a " target="_blank">Page0464-a + 41</a>] Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 15.<BR> 5. A proper name, Hariv. 11537.<BR> 6. The name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 16, 27.<BR> II. f. गी, A female elephant, Suśr. 1, 178, 1.<BR> III. adj., f. गी.<BR> 1. Consisting of serpents, MBh. 8, 2586.<BR> 2. Produced from an elephant, Suśr. 1, 194, 1.<BR> IV. f. गा, A proper name, Rājat. 7, 293.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्नाग|दिङ्नागः
दिङ्नाग दिङ्नाग, i. e. दिश्-, m. an elephant supposed to support a quarter of the world, Megh. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुनाग|शिशुनागः
शिशु- + नाग शिशु- + नाग, m. a kind of Rākṣasa or demon, Rām. 3, 76, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमय
नागमय नाग + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting in elephants, Hariv. 9379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर नागर, i. e. नगर + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to a town, MBh. 1, 5682; m. A citizen, Rām. 1, 17, 34.<BR> 2. Referring to a town, MBh. 2, 256.<BR> 3. Polite, Śāk. 94, 10 C.<BR> II. f. री, A crafty woman, Uddhavadūta 16 in Haeb. Anth. 351.<BR> III. n. Dry ginger, Suśr. 1, 161, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनागरी
देव-नागरी देव-नागरी, f. the name of the character proper to Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक नागर + क, m. The chief of a town, Śāk. 73, 1, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरिक
नागरिक नागरिक, i. e. नगर + इक,<BR> I. adj. Inhabiting a town, Sch. ad Śāk. d. 51.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A citizen, Vikr. 77, 12.<BR> 2. Polite, Śāk. 60, 2.<BR> 2. A superintendent of the police, Daśak. 195, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवन्त्|नागवत्
नागवन्त् नाग + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Consisting in elephants, MBh. 5, 5703.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागिन्
नागिन् नागिन्, i. e. नाग + इन्, adj. Surrounded by serpents, Hariv. 14844.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग्नजित
नाग्नजित नाग्नजित, i. e. नग्नजित् + अ, patronym. f. ती, A descendant of Nagnajit, Bhāg. P. 3, 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटक|नाटकं|नाटकः
नाटक नाटक, i. e. नट् + अक,<BR> I. m. A mime, Rām. 1, 5, 18.<BR> II. n. A drama, Rām. 2, 69, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटितक|नाटितकं
नाटितक नाटित + क (vb. नट्), n. A gesture, Śāk. 73, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्य|नाट्यं|नाट्यः
नाट्य नाट्य, i. e. नट + य, n.<BR> 1. The art of acting or dancing, scenic art, Bhāg. P. 4, 15, 19.<BR> 2. Mimical representation, Mṛcch. 88, 4.<BR> 3. The attire of an actor, Bhāg. P. 1, 8, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिका
नाडिका नाडिका, i. e. नाडी + क, f.<BR> 1. A measure of time, (1/60) of a sidereal day, an Indian hour, Bhāg. P. 3, 11, 3.<BR> 2. A measure of length, half a daṇḍa, Mārk. P. 49, 39.<BR> 3. An Indian clock, Kām. Nītis. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडी
नाडी नाडी, i. e. नड + अ + ई, also<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडि|नाडिः
नाडि नाडि (Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 11), f.<BR> 1. The stalk or culm of any plant.<BR> 2. Any tubular organ of the body, as an artery, a vein, an intestine, etc., MBh. 3, 13974; Ragh. 10, 59 (the rays of the sun, supposed to be hollow).<BR> 3. A fistulous sore, Suśr. 1, 284, 11.<BR> 4. = नाडिका 1, Sūryas. 1, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भनाडी
गर्भ-नाडी गर्भ-नाडी, f. the navel-string, Suśr. 1, 368, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणक|नाणकं
नाणक नाणक, n. A coin, Yājñ. 2, 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ्
नाथ् नाथ्, and नाध् नाध् (akin to नम्), i. 1, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 3, 12630). To beg, MBh. 12, 1365 (with gen. of the object, MBh. 3, 12630).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ नाथ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A protector, MBh. 12, 2292.<BR> 2. A master, a lord, Pañc. v. d. 90; Rām. 1, 76, 19.<BR> 3. A husband, Ragh. 12, 75.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अ- + नाथ अ- + नाथ, adj., f. था, having no protector, helpless, Rām. 6, 23, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनाथ|कालनाथः
काल- + नाथ काल- + नाथ, m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10368.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनाथ|कुनाथः
कु- + नाथ कु- + नाथ, 1. m. a bad protector, Bhāg. P. 9, 14, 28. 2. adj. having a bad guide, 5, 14, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीनाथ|गौरीनाथः
गौरी- + नाथ गौरी- + नाथ, m. a name of Śiva, Bhartṛ. 3, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूनाथ|चमूनाथः
चमू- + नाथ चमू- + नाथ, m. a commander of an army, Bhāg. P. 4, 26, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदेकनाथ
जगत्-एक- + नाथ जगत्-एक- + नाथ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a " target="_blank">Page0465-a + 43</a>] m. monarch of the world, Ragh. 5, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथ|जगन्नाथः
जगन्नाथ जगन्नाथ, i. e. जगत्-, m. a name of Viṣṇu or कृष्ण, MBh. 2, 729.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितनाथ|जीवितनाथः
जीवित- + नाथ जीवित- + नाथ, m. a husband, Kumāras. 4, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनाथ|धर्मनाथः
धर्म- + नाथ धर्म- + नाथ, m. a legitimate lord, Rām. 5, 33, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रनाथ|नक्षत्रनाथः
नक्षत्र- + नाथ नक्षत्र- + नाथ, m. the moon, Hariv. 16033.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरनाथ
नर- + नाथ नर- + नाथ, m. a king, Rām. 2, 68, 55 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिनाथ
नाकि(न्)- + नाथ नाकि(न्)- + नाथ, m. a name of Indra, Śatr. 2, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानाथ|प्रजानाथः
प्रजा- + नाथ प्रजा- + नाथ, m. a king, Rājat. 5, 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणनाथ|प्राणनाथः
प्राण- + नाथ प्राण- + नाथ, m. a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिनाथ|भूमिनाथः
भूमि- + नाथ भूमि- + नाथ, m. a king, Lass. 14, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदुनाथ|यदुनाथः
यदु- + नाथ यदु- + नाथ, m. a name of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनाथ|रघुनाथः
रघु- + नाथ रघु- + नाथ, m. Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीचयनाथ
रजनी-चय- + नाथ रजनी-चय- + नाथ, m. the moon, Hit. ii. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वनाथ|विश्वनाथः
विश्व- + नाथ विश्व- + नाथ, m. 1. a name of Śiva. 2. a proper name, Chr. p. 234, 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथ
स- + नाथ स- + नाथ,<BR> I. adj. endowed, Pañc. 76, 18.<BR> II. f. था, a woman whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथत्व
नाथत्व नाथ + त्व, n. The dignity of a protector, Rām. 2, 81, 2 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवन्त्|नाथवत्
नाथवन्त् नाथ + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Having a protector, Rām. 1, 62, 12.<BR> 2. Having a husband, 5, 37, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथाय
नाथाय नाथाय, a denomin. derived from नाथ with य, Par. To grant, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथिन्
नाथिन् नाथिन्, i. e. नाथ + इन्, adj., f. नी, Having a protector, Rām. 1, 78, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद|नादः
नाद नाद, i. e. नद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Roaring, Rām. 4, 29, 12.<BR> 2. Sound, cry, MBh. 4, 1885; 14, 2694.<BR> 3. A semicircle representing the nasal sound, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 53.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमनाद|भीमनादः
भीम- + नाद भीम- + नाद, m. a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानाद|महानादः
महा- + नाद महा- + नाद, m. 1. a loud cry. 2. an elephant, 3. a lion. 4. a camel. 5. the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनाद|मेघनादः
मेघ- + नाद मेघ- + नाद, m. 1. Varuṇa. 2. a son of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनाद|सिंहनादः
सिंह- + नाद सिंह- + नाद, m. war cry, Pañc. 5, 4 (signifying principal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन् नादिन्, i. e. नद् or नाद + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Sounding, sounding aloud, Hariv. 8069; MBh. 2, 987.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Hariv. 12941.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय नादेय, i. e. नदी + एय,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Coming from a river, Suśr. 1, 170, 11.<BR> 2. Aquatic, Rām. 4, 39, 12.<BR> II. n. A sort of salt, Suśr. 2, 326, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध्
नाध् नाध्, see नात्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना नाना, adv. Different, Bhāg. P. 1, 2, 32. Often in the beginning of comp. words, Of different classes, Man. 9, 148; various, 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानात्व
नानात्व नाना + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Difference, MBh. 2, 137.<BR> 2. Manifoldness, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दी|नांदी
नान्दी नान्दी, i. e. नन्द् + अ + ई, f.<BR> 1. Joy, MBh. 4, 2189.<BR> 2. A prayer at the opening of a drama, Mṛcch. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित|नापितः
नापित नापित, based on the nom. sing. स्नापिता, i. e. स्नाप्, curtailed Causal of स्ना, + तृ.<BR> 1. m. A barber, Man. 4, 253.<BR> 2. f. ति, The wife of a barber, Pañc. 37, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ
नाभ नाभ,<BR> I. a substitute for नाभि, when latter part of a comp. adj. or of a noun based on an adj., e. g. अब्ज- and पद्म- (Having a lotus in his navel), m. A name of Viṣṇu. पद्म-नाभ also,<BR> 1. A proper name.<BR> 2. A kind of spell. सु-, adj.<BR> 1. Having a handsome nave, MBh. 10, 625.<BR> 2. Having a beautiful centre, Rām. 1, 33, 12. काल-, m. The name of an Asura or demon and others. कुश-, m. A proper name, Rām. 1, 34, 3. त्रि-, m. A name of Viṣṇu (holding the three worlds in his navel), Bhāg. P. 8, 17, 26. दृध-, m. The name of a spell, Rām. 1, 30, 5. पुष्कर-, m. A name of Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 48. वत्स-, m. a particular poisonous tree.<BR> II. m. Epithet of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10364.<BR> III. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभाग|नाभागः
नाभाग नाभाग (cf. नभग), m. A proper name. MBh. 1, 3140; Rām. 1, 70, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभागि
नाभागि नाभागि, i. e. नाभाग + इ, patronym. A son of Nābhāga, MBh. 12, 993.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि नाभि (नभ् + इ ?), f. (also नाभी नाभी), and m.<BR> 1. The navel, Man. 1, 92.<BR> 2. The nave of a wheel, MBh. 1, 726.<BR> 3. Centre, Bhāg. P. 5, 16, 7.<BR> 4. Chief, Ragh. 18, 19.<BR> 5. Musk, Megh. 53.<BR> 6. (m. ?) The musk animal, Bhāg. P. 3, 21, 44.<BR> 7. m. A proper name, 5, 2, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. nafu, nafela; ὀμϕαλός; Lat. umbilicus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णनाभि|ऊर्णनाभिः
ऊर्ण- + नाभि ऊर्ण- + नाभि, m. a spider, 2, 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रनाभि|चक्रनाभिः
चक्र- + नाभि चक्र- + नाभि, f. the nave of a wheel, Suśr. 1, 354, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाभि
निस्- + नाभि निस्- + नाभि, adj. not reaching to the navel, Kumāras. 7, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनाभि|मृगनाभिः
मृग- + नाभि मृग- + नाभि, m. musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसनाभि|विसनाभिः
विस- + नाभि विस- + नाभि, m. a quantity of lotusses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धनाभि|वृद्धनाभिः
वृद्ध- + नाभि वृद्ध- + नाभि, adj. corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभि|सनाभिः
स- + नाभि स- + नाभि,<BR> I. adj. 1. uterine, Man. 9, 192. 2. like, resembling. 3. affectionate.<BR> II. m. 1. an uterine brother. 2. a paternal kinsman, Man. 5, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिक
नाभिक नाभि + क, a substitute for नाभि at the end of comp. adj., MBh. 12, 8946.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य नाभ्य, i. e. नाभि + य, adj.<BR> 1. Proceeding from the navel, Bhāg. P. 3, 4, 13.<BR> 3. Epithet of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10364.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभ्य|सनाभ्यः
स- + नाभ्य स- + नाभ्य, m. a relation as far as the seventh degree, Man. 5, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम नाम, see नामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामक
नामक नामक, i. e. नामन् + क, a substitute for नामन् at the end of comp. adj., f. मिका, e. g. चन्द्र-सरस्-, Called Candrasaras, Pañc. 159, 20. पर्वत-नामिका, f. Having the name of a mountain, Man. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामतस्
नामतस् नामतस्, i. e. नामन् + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. = the abl. of नामन्, Bhāg. P. 5, 12, 8.<BR> 2. By name, together with the name, Man. 8, 255.<BR> 3. With respect to the name, Śāk. 104, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेय|नामधेयं
नामधेय नामधेय, i. e. नामन् + धेय [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b " target="_blank">Page0466-b + 46</a>] (vb. धा), n.<BR> 1. A name, Man. 2, 123.<BR> 2. A title, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 56.<BR> 3. The ceremony of giving a name to a child, Man. 2, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंनामधेय
पुंनामधेय पुंनामधेय, i. e. पुंस्-, m. one of the male sex, Rām. 5, 35, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेयतस्
नामधेयतस् नामधेय + तस्, adv. By name, Rām. 4, 62, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन् नामन्, i. e. ज्ञा + मन्,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A name, Man. 2, 128.<BR> 2. Only the name (opposed to the reality), 157.<BR> II. acc. sing. नाम, adv.<BR> 1. By name, Man. 3, 127.<BR> 2. Indeed, of course, 8, 335.<BR> 3. Perhaps, Rām. 2, 85, 18 Gorr.<BR> 4. It is often preceded,<BR> a. by an interrogative pronoun, Then, Rām. 2, 15, 20 Gorr.;<BR> b. by अपि, Perhaps, 2, 97, 6 Gorr. Of course, Śāk. 93, 5, v. r.; would that;<BR> c. by मा, Perhaps (I hope not), Mṛcch. 54, 24;<BR> d. by ननु Certainly, Rām. 4, 24, 37.<BR> 5. With an imperative, No matter, Mṛcch. 75, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> when latter part of a comp. adj. the fem. ends -नाम्नी, Man. 3, 9; or -नामन्, Rām. 1, 6, 25; or -नामा, 2, 109, 47 Gorr.<BR> --Cf. Lat. nomen, co-gnomen, nam, quis-nam (cf. quem-nam = कं नाम), nem-pe (cf. नाम अपि); ὄνομα (for ὀ + γνομα), ὀνομαίνω (for ὀνομαν + ϳω); Goth. namo; A.S. nama, nemnan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अ- + नामन् अ- + नामन्, adj. not named, not declared, Man. 12, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रनामन्
उष्ट्र- + नामन् उष्ट्र- + नामन्, adj. called camel, Pañc. 68, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतनामन्
गृहीत- + नामन् गृहीत- + नामन् (vb. ग्रह्), adj. called, Nal. 12, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुस्- + नामन् दुस्- + नामन्, n. hæmorrhoids, Suśr. 1, 177, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृनामन्
पितृ- + नामन् पितृ- + नामन्, adj. called after his father's name, Cāṇ. 79 in Berl. Monatsb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृनामन्
मातृ- + नामन् मातृ- + नामन्, adj. called after his mother's name, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालनामन्
श्याल- + नामन् श्याल- + नामन्, adj. called after the name of his brother-in-law, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनामन्
सु- + नामन् सु- + नामन्, adj., f. म्नी, well-named, MBh. 1, 1053.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनामन्
स्त्री- + नामन् स्त्री- + नामन्, adj. having a female name, Chr. 63, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक नायक, i. e. नी + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A guide, Rām. 2, 64, 33.<BR> 2. A chief, Bhāg. P. 4, 7, 22.<BR> 3. A general, Rām. 3, 33, 14.<BR> 4. A husband, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 20.<BR> 5. A lover, Śāk. 15, 12.<BR> 6. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a " target="_blank">Page0467-a + 43</a>] central gem of a necklace, Vāsav. 17, 1.<BR> 7. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 158.<BR> II. f. यिका, A mistress, Lass. 24, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायक
अ- + नायक अ- + नायक, adj., f. का, deprived of or wanting a guide, a commander, a ruler, Rām. 2, 14, 52; 79, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनायक
कु-नायक कु-नायक, adj. having a bad guide, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनीनायक|कुमुदिनीनायकः
कुमुदिनी- + नायक कुमुदिनी- + नायक, m. the moon, Hit. 9, 5. -गण-, m. 1. the chief of the retinue of a god, Bhāg. P. 5, 17, 3. 2. the god Gaṇeśa, MBh. 1, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रनायक|चक्रनायकः
चक्र- + नायक चक्र- + नायक, m. the chief of a division of an army, Rājat. 2, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनायक|दंडनायक|दण्डनायकः
दण्ड- + नायक दण्ड- + नायक, m.<BR> I. a judge, Hit. 66, 6. 2. the commander of a division of an army, Rājat. 7, 969.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनायिका
भूत-नायिका भूत-नायिका, f. Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकत्व
नायकत्व नायक-त्व, n. Chieftainship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार नार,<BR> 1. i. e. नृ or नर + अ, adj. Belonging to a man, Man. 5, 87.<BR> II. m. Water (cf. नीर, νηρός, Νηρεύς), Man. 1, 10.<BR> III. f. नारी नारी, i. e. नृ + ई,<BR> 1. A woman, Man. 1, 32.<BR> 2. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 5, 2, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनारी
कुल-नारी कुल-नारी, f. a virtuous woman, Hit. i. d. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यनारी
दिव्य-नारी दिव्य-नारी, f. an Apsaras, Rām. 2, 91, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशनारी
प्रकाश-नारी प्रकाश-नारी, f. a harlot, Mṛcch. 46, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक नारक, i. e. नरक + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. की, Infernal, hellish, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 30.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An inhabitant of the infernal regions, 2, 10, 41.<BR> 2. Hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिन् नारकिन्, i. e. नारक + इन्, m. An inhabitant of hell, Prab. 46, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारंगः|नारङ्गः
नारङ्ग नारङ्ग, m. An orange tree, Suśr. 1, 209, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारद|नारदः
नारद नारद, m. A Devarṣi, i. e. a celestial Ṛṣi; in epic poetry the messenger of the gods, MBh. 1, 2048.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंह|नारसिंहः
नारसिंह नारसिंह, i. e. नर-सिंह + अ, adj., f. ही, Referring, belonging, etc., to Viṣṇu in his incarnation as man-lion, MBh. 3, 15837.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराच|नाराचः
नाराच नाराच (perhaps नर-अञ्च् + अ), m. A kind of arrow, MBh. 1, 5522.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण नारायण, probably नर + आयन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The first living being, identified with Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 7, 9447; Man. 1, 10.<BR> 2. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 24.<BR> II. adj. Referring, belonging to Nārāyaṇa. MBh. 1, 337.<BR> III. f. णी, patronym. name of Indrasenā, MBh. 4, 651.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणमय
नारायणमय नारायण + मय, adj. Consisting of Nārāyaṇa, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणीय
नारायणीय नारायणीय, i. e. नारायण + ईय, adj. Referring to Nārāyaṇa, MBh. 12, 13422.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेर|नारिकेरः
नारिकेर नारिकेर, and नारिकेल नारिकेल, m. The cocoa-nut, Suśr. 2, 108, 9; Rām. 3, 39, 12.<BR> --Cf. नालिकेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी नारी, see नार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीक
नारीक नारी + क, a substitute for नारी at the end of comp. adj., Rām. 2, 109, 22 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीमय
नारीमय नारी + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting in wives, Bhartṛ. 1, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाल|नालं|नालः
नाल नाल, i. e. नल + अ,<BR> I. adj. Consisting of reed, Bhāg. P. 6, 11, 8.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A hollow or tubular stalk, especially the stalk of the water-lily, MBh. 2, 88.<BR> 2. A tubular vessel of the body, Prab. 55, 5.<BR> 3. A handle, MBh. 9, 909.<BR> III. f. ला, The name of a river, MBh. 6, 339.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाला
नाभि-नाला नाभि-नाला, f. the navelstring, Ragh. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रनाल|यंत्रनाल
यन्त्र-नाल यन्त्र-नाल, n. a pipe (of a well), Mārk. P. 39, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालाय
नालाय नालाय, a denomin. derived from नाल with य, ptcple. of the pf. pass. नालायित, Representing the handle of an axe, Bhāg. P. 7, 5, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेर|नालिकेरः
नालिकेर नालिकेर, and नालिकेल नालिकेल, m. The cocoa-nut, Suśr. 2, 175, 2; 1, 213, 3.<BR> --Cf. नारिकेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिनी
नालिनी नालिनी, i. e. नाल + इन् + ई, f. A mystical name of one of the nostrils, Bhāg. P. 4, 29, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीक|नालीकः
नालीक नालीक, i. e. नाल + ईक, m. A kind of arrow, Rām. 3, 31, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावनीत
नावनीत नावनीत, i. e. नवनीत + अ, adj. Mild, Chr. 43, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविक|नाविकः
नाविक नाविक, i. e. नौ + इक, m. The helmsman of a vessel, a pilot, Rām. 2, 52, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
नाव्य नाव्य, i. e. नौ + य, adj.<BR> 1. Navigable, Ragh. 4, 31.<BR> 2. Accessible to a ship, MBh. 3, 10027.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश|नाशः
नाश नाश, i. e. 2. नश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Loss, Bhartṛ. 2, 35.<BR> 2. Disappearance, Rām. 2, 47, 13.<BR> 3. Destruction, Yājñ. 1, 339.<BR> 4. Death, 63.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनाश
अर्थ- + नाश अर्थ- + नाश, m. ruin of wealth, Cāṇ. 80 in Berl. Monatsb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तनाश|चित्तनाशः
