विघ्ननाशक|विघ्ननाशकः
विघ्न- + नाशक विघ्न- + नाशक, m. Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशन
नाशन नाशन, i. e. 2. नश्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी<BR> 1. Destroying, MBh. 13, 2194; Man. 8, 127.<BR> 2. Removing, MBh. 2, 426.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Destruction, Mārk. P. 24, 36.<BR> 2. Removal, MBh. 7, 5120.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्वनाशन|कृतपूर्व्वनाशन
कृत-पूर्व- + नाशन कृत-पूर्व- + नाशन, n. ungratefulness, Hit. 27, 16, n. भूत-,<BR> I. m. 1. marking nut plant, Semicarpus anacardium. 2. mustard.<BR> II. n. the Eleocarpus seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यनाशन|मत्स्यनाशनः
मत्स्य- + नाशन मत्स्य- + नाशन, m. an osprey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशिन्
नाशिन् नाशिन्, i. e. 2. नश्, or नाश + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Perishable, Prab. 100, 11.<BR> 2. Removing, Hariv. 10239.<BR> 3. Destroying, Rām. 6, 80, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशिन्
अ- + नाशिन् अ- + नाशिन्, adj. 1. not being lost, Man. 8, 185. 2. not perishing, Bhag. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्टिक|नाष्टिकः
नाष्टिक नाष्टिक, i. e. नष्ट (vb. 2. नश्) + इक, m. The former owner who has lost a chattel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्
† नास् नास्, i. 1, Ātm. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासत्य
नासत्य नासत्य, i. e. न-अ-सत्य,<BR> I. m. du. A name of the Aśvins, MBh. 12, 7583.<BR> II. adj. Referring to the Nāsatyas, 12, 13491.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासा
नासा नासा, the base of some cases and derivatives is नस्, f. The nose, Man. 8, 125.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. nasa; A.S. nase; Lat. nâsus, nâris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णनासा
कर्ण-नासा कर्ण-नासा, f. the ears and the nose, Rām. 3, 24, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्नास
तिर्यग्नास तिर्यग्नास, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-, adj. having a wry nose, 5, 17, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागनासा
नाग-नासा नाग-नासा, f. the trunk of an elephant, 5, 22, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

