नितम्बिन् नितम्बिन्, i. e. नितम्ब + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Latter part of comp. adj. Having buttocks, e. g. चारु-पीन-नितम्ब + इन्, Having beautiful big buttocks, Mārk. P. 17, 20.<BR> 2. Having beautiful buttocks, Mālav. d. 24.<BR> 3. Having beautiful slopes, Rājat. 2, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितराम्
नितराम् नि + तराम्, comparative of नि.<BR> 1. Continually, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 11.<BR> 2. Excessively, Rām. 3, 1, 2.<BR> 3. At all events, Bhartṛ. 1, 95.<BR> --Cf. A.S. nidher; O.H.G. nidar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य नि + त्य, adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Constant, perpetual, Man. 2, 206; 58 (नित्यकालम्, adv. At all times).<BR> 2. Eternal, Man. 1, 11.<BR> 3. Essential, regular, 11, 203; Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 11. 4.<BR> 4. ˚यम्, adv. Perpetually, constantly, Man. 1, 108.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अ- + नित्य अ- + नित्य, adj. 1. perishable, 6, 77. 2. occasional, 7, 199. 3. inconstant. Rām. 2, 4, 26; uncertain, 5, 29, 31. 4. ˚यम्, adv. not perpetually, Man. 3, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनित्य
आत्मनित्य आत्मनित्य, i. e. आत्मन्-, adj. best-beloved, MBh. 1, 6080.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनित्य
तपो-नित्य तपो-नित्य, i. e. तपस्-, adj. practising perpetually religious austerities, 14, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यता
नित्यता नित्य + ता, f.<BR> 1. Perpetuity, Bhāṣāp. 101.<BR> 2. Perseverance, in धर्म-नित्य + ता, MBh. 3, 12531.<BR> 3. Necessity, Mārk. P. 30, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यता
अ- + नित्यता अ- + नित्यता, f. perishableness, Bhartṛ. 3, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यत्व|नित्यत्वं
नित्यत्व नित्य + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Perpetuity, eternity, Bhāg. P. 3, 27, 17.<BR> 2. Perseverance, in अध्यात्मज्ञान-नित्य + त्व, Bhag. 13, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यत्व
अ- + नित्यत्व अ- + नित्यत्व, n. 1. transitoriness, Pānch. iii. d. 21. 2. fickleness, Rām. 4, 32, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदा
नित्यदा नित्य + दा, adv. Perpetually, Indr. 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यमय
नित्यमय नित्य + मय, adj., f. यी, Eternal, MBh. 12, 8948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशस्
नित्यशस् नित्य + शस्, adv. Constantly, Man. 2, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
1. निद् निद्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. (only ved. and very seldom), and निन्द् निन्द् (perhaps originally vb. नद्, with the prep. नि), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 7, 2601), To blame, MBh. 2, 2275. निन्दित,<BR> 1. Reprehended, Man. 3, 47.<BR> 2. Reprehensible, 42.<BR> 3. Despised, 3, 165.<BR> 4. Forbidden, 11, 44.<BR> 5. Inauspicious, 182.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> 1. अ-निन्द्य, adj. blameless, Man. 3, 42.<BR> 2. अ-नेद्य, adj. blameless, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, To blame violently, MBh. 5, 40.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To blame, 3, 15656.<BR> --With वि वि, To blame, 3, 13700.<BR> --Cf. ὄνειδος, etc., λοίδορος, etc.; Goth. ga-naitjan, naiteins; O.H.G. neizjan; A.S. naetan, naeting; probably also Goth. neith; A.S. nidh, ge-nidhle (hatred).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्य
अ- + निन्द्य अ- + निन्द्य, adj. blameless, Man. 3, 42. निन्द्य, 1. reprehensible, Man. 3, 42. 2. forbidden, 3, 50. 3. disgraceful, 11, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
† 2. निद् निद्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. To be near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
निदर्शक निदर्शक, i. e. नि-दृश् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Seeing, MBh. 12, 7472.<BR> 2. Announcing, 3, 13086.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन निदर्शन, i. e. नि-दृश् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Showing, Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 1.<BR> 2. Announcing, Hariv. 12815.<BR> 3. Teaching, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 33.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Seeing, sight, MBh. 9, 62.<BR> 2. Evidence, Man. 11, 45.<BR> 3. Example, 9, 20; MBh. 8, 1882.<BR> 4. Foreboding, Hariv. 9885.<BR> 5. Prognostic, MBh. 5, 1235.<BR> 6. Symptom, 12, 11718.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शिन्
निदर्शिन् निदर्शिन्, i. e. नि-दृश् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Knowing, MBh. 14, 1406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघ|निदाघः
निदाघ निदाघ, i. e. नि-दह् + अ, m. The hot season, MBh. 3, 12539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदान|निदानं
निदान निदान, i. e. नि-३. दा + अन, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0473-a " target="_blank">Page0473-a + 41</a>]<BR> 1. A first cause, Ragh. 3, 1.<BR> 2. The causes of disease, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धिका
