निश
ऽनिश -निश (cf. निशा), in अ-निश + म्, adv. (Without rest) continually, Śiś. 9, 61. अहर्-निश, n. A whole day, comprising a day and a night, Man. 1, 74. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0484-a " target="_blank">Page0484-a + 40</a>] दिवा-निश + म्, adv. Day and night, Man. 7, 44. निशा-निश + म्, adv. Constantly, MBh. 3, 12343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ नि-शठ,<BR> I. adj. Candid, Bhāg. P. 6, 7, 15.<BR> II. m. A proper name, MBh. 1, 7915.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशब्द
निशब्द नि-शब्द, adj. Silent, Kir. 8, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा निशा, probably from नि-शी, (cf. निशिथ), f.<BR> 1. Night, Man. 11, 223.<BR> 2. A dream, MBh. 5, 7252.<BR> 3. Turmeric, Curcuma, Suśr. 2, 208, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिशा
