नॄ
† नॄ नॄ, ii. 9, नृणा, Par. To lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजक|नेजकः
नेजक नेजक, i. e. निज् + अक, m. A washerman, Man. 8, 396.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजन|नेजनं
नेजन नेजन, i. e. निज् + अन, n. Washing, MBh. 7, 8530.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतृ
नेतृ नेतृ, i. e. नी + तृ, m., f. त्री, and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b " target="_blank">Page0493-b + 42</a>] n.<BR> 1. One who guides or leads, Man. 7, 17.<BR> 2. One who leads to, MBh. 3, 954.<BR> 3. With दण्डस्य, One who inflicts punishment, Man. 7, 25.<BR> 4. The hero of a drama, Sāh. D. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्र|नेत्रं
नेत्र नेत्र, i. e. नी + त्र,<BR> I. A substitute for नेतृ when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. भवन्नेत्र, i. e. भवन्त्-, Having thee as commander, MBh. 7, 3702.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The eye, Man. 4, 44.<BR> 2. The string of a churning rope, MBh. 1, 1124.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्मनेत्र|अयुग्मनेत्रः
अ-युग्म- + नेत्र अ-युग्म- + नेत्र, and त्रि-, m. a name of Śiva, Kumāras. 3, 51; MBh. 12, 10357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रनेत्र|सहस्रनेत्रः
सहस्र- + नेत्र सहस्र- + नेत्र, adj. possessed of a thousand eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनेत्र
परि- + नेत्र परि- + नेत्र,<BR> I. m. an owl.<BR> II. n. the white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेद्
नेद् नेद्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To blame (cf. निद्).<BR> 2. † To be near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठ|नेदिष्ठं
नेदिष्ठ नेदिष्ठ, superl. (from नेद for नद्ध, ptcple. of the pf. pass. of नह्; cf. Goth. nehva; A.S. neah), Very near, nearest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदीयंस्
नेदीयंस् नेदीयंस्, comparat. of the last (q. cf.), Nearer, as near as possible, Rājat. 4, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपथ्य|नेपथ्यं
नेपथ्य नेपथ्य n.<BR> 1. Ornament, attire, Ragh. 6, 6.<BR> 2. The attire of an actor, Śāk. 3, 6.<BR> 3. The tiring room of a stage, the part behind the scenes, Śāk. 8, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमि|नेमिः
नेमि नेमि, i. e. नम् (with ए instead of being reduplicated), + इ, f.<BR> 1. The circumference of a wheel, MBh. 3, 15489.<BR> 2. Circumference, e. g. समुद्र-नेम्, adj. Surrounded by the ocean, MBh. 1, 1585.<BR> 3. Edge, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टनेमि|अरिष्टनेमिः
अ-रिष्ट- + नेमि अ-रिष्ट- + नेमि, m. a proper name, 3, 20, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमि|कालनेमिः
काल- + नेमि काल- + नेमि, 1. f. the name of a weapon, Hariv. 2640.<BR> 2. m. the name of a demon, Śāk. 95, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्
† नेष् नेष्, i. 1. Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयस
नैःश्रेयस नैःश्रेयस, i. e. निस्-श्रेयस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी, Leading to future beatitude, Man. 9, 334.<BR> II. n. The name of a fabulous forest, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयसिक
नैःश्रेयसिक नैःश्रेयसिक, i. e. नैः-श्रेयस + इक, adj. Leading to future beatitude, Man. 12, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्नेह्य
नैःस्नेह्य नैःस्नेह्य, i. e. निस्-स्नेह + य, n. Want of affection, Man. 9, 15 (read नैःस्न्˚ instead of नैस्न्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
नैक नैक, i. e. न-एक, adj., f. का.<BR> 1. Many a, Mārk. P. 28, 29.<BR> 2. pl. Many, Nal. 12, 109.<BR> 3. Manifold, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 15.<BR> 4. Including several matters, Yājñ. 2, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकधा
नैकधा नैक + धा (or rather न-एकधा), adv.<BR> 1. In many parts, Rām. 6, 77, 12.<BR> 2. To many directions, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकशस्
नैकशस् नैक + शस् (or rather न-एकशस्), adv. Repeatedly, Rām. 3, 36, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकशस्त्रमय
नैकशस्त्रमय नैक-शस्त्र + मय, adj. Consisting of many missiles, Rām. 6, 91, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकृतिक
नैकृतिक नैकृतिक, i. e. निकृति + क, adj. Fallacious, Man. 4, 196 (read नैकृ˚, instead of निष्कृ˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगम|नैगमः
नैगम नैगम, i. e. निगम + अ,<BR> I. adj. Referring to the Vedas (vedic), Bhāg. P. 3, 7, 38.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A means, MBh. 12, 3685.<BR> 2. A trader, Yājñ. 2, 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यक
नैत्यक नैत्यक, and नैत्यिकं नैत्यिक, i. e. नित्य + क or इक, adj. What must be done constantly or regularly (opposed to नैमित्तिक), Man. 2, 105; 8, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदाघ|नैदाघः
नैदाघ नैदाघ, and नैदाघिक नैदाघिक, i. e. निदाघ + अ, or इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b " target="_blank">Page0494-b + 39</a>] adj. Belonging to the hot season, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदेशिक|नैदेशिकः
नैदेशिक नैदेशिक, i. e. निदेश + इक, m. A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैधन
नैधन नैधन, i. e. निधन + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Referring to death, Hariv. 4900.<BR> 2. Perishable, 2124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण|नैपुणं
नैपुण नैपुण, i. e. निपुण + अ, n.<BR> 1. Dexterity, MBh. 13, 1378.<BR> 2. Skill, experience, Rājat. 4, 354.<BR> 3. Strictness, Man. 10, 85.<BR> 4. Completion. Bhāg. P. 3, 25, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण्य|नैपुण्यं
नैपुण्य नैपुण्य, i. e. निपुण + य, n.<BR> 1. Cleverness, Sāv. 3, 21.<BR> 2. Artfulness, Pañc. 121, 16.<BR> 3. Exactness, Rām. 3, 75, 70.<BR> 4. Completion, Man. 4, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं|नैमित्तिकः
नैमित्तिक नैमित्तिक, i. e. निमित्त + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Occasional, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 21.<BR> 2. Dependent on an external cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिष
नैमिष नैमिष, n. The name of a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषीय|नैमिषीयः
नैमिषीय नैमिषीय, i. e. नैमिष + ईय, adj. Referring to the Naimiṣa forest, MBh. 9, 2161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषेय|नैमिषेयः
नैमिषेय नैमिषेय, i. e. नैमिष + एय, adj. Living in the Naimiṣa forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिक
नैयमिक नैयमिक, i. e. नियम + इक, adj. Conformable to a (religious) precept, Bhāg. P. 5, 8, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयायिक|नैयायिकः
नैयायिक नैयायिक, i. e. न्याय + इक, m. A logician, a follower of the Nyāya philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरन्तर्य|नैरंतर्य|नैरंतर्यं|नैरन्तर्य्य|नैरन्तर्य्यं
नैरन्तर्य नैरन्तर्य, i. e. निस्-अन्तर + य, Absence of interruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरर्थ्य|नैरर्थ्यं
नैरर्थ्य नैरर्थ्य, i. e. निस्-अर्थ + य, n. Senselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैराश्य|नैराश्यं
नैराश्य नैराश्य, i. e. निस्-आश + य (cf. आशा), n. Hopelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्त|नैरुक्तं|नैरुक्तः
नैरुक्त नैरुक्त, i. e. निरुक्ति + अ,<BR> I. adj. Explained etymologically MBh. 13, 4485.<BR> II. m. One who is conversant with etymological interpretation, Man. 12, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत|नैरृतः
नैरृत नैरृत, i. e. निरृति + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती.<BR> 1. Southwestern, Man. 11, 104.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son of Nirṛti, i. e. a Rākṣasa or demon, Ragh. 12, 43.<BR> 2. pl. The name of a people.<BR> III. adj. Belonging to the Rākṣasas or demons, MBh. 12, 6132.<BR> IV. f. ती, A name of Durgā, Dev. 5, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गुण्य|नैर्गुण्यं
