नैर्मल्य|नैर्मल्यं|नैर्म्मल्यं
नैर्मल्य नैर्मल्य, i. e. निस्-मल + य, n. Purity, MBh. 7, 9264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्लज्ज्य|नैर्लज्ज्यं
नैर्लज्ज्य नैर्लज्ज्य, i. e. निस्-लज्ज + य (see लज्जा), n. Impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैल्य|नैल्यं
नैल्य नैल्य, i. e. नील + य, n. Darkblue (the colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैविड्य|नैविड्यं
नैविड्य नैविड्य, i. e. निविड + य, n. Denseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश|नैशं
नैश नैश, i. e. निशा + अ, adj., f. शी, Nocturnal, Man. 2, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशाकर
नैशाकर नैशाकर, i. e. निशाकर + अ, m. Caused by the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशिक|नैशिकं
नैशिक नैशिक, i. e. निशा + इक, adj., f. की, Obtained in one night, Man. 5, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चिन्त्य
नैश्चिन्त्य नैश्चिन्त्य, i. e. निस्-चिन्त + य (see चिन्ता), n. Freedom from care, Bhartṛ. 3, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध|नैषधः
नैषध नैषध, i. e. निषध + अ,<BR> 1. m.<BR> 1. A prince of the Niṣadhas, a designation of Nala.<BR> 2. pl. = Niṣadhas (the people).<BR> II. n. The name of a poem treating of Nala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषाद
नैषाद नैषाद, i. e. निषाद + अ,<BR> 1. adj. Belonging to the Niṣādas<BR> 2. m. pl. Niṣādas (the people).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषादि
नैषादि नैषादि, i. e. निषाद + इ, m. A prince of the Niṣādas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्म्य|नैष्कर्म्यं
नैष्कर्म्य नैष्कर्म्य, i. e. निस्-कर्मन् + य, n. Abandoning action, inactivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कृतिक
नैष्कृतिक नैष्कृतिक, see नैकृतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक नैष्ठिक, i. e. निष्ठा + इक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Final, MBh. 17, 21.<BR> 2. Decided, Rām. 6, 21, 28.<BR> 3. Accomplished, MBh. 13, 758.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmana who remains always in the condition of a religious student, observing the vow of chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठुर्य|नैष्ठुर्यं|नैष्ठुर्य्य
नैष्ठुर्य नैष्ठुर्य, i. e. निष्ठुर + य, n. Coarseness, Hit. i. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्फल्य
नैष्फल्य नैष्फल्य, i. e. निस्-फल + य, n. Want of fruit or effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्गिक|नैसर्गिकः
नैसर्गिक नैसर्गिक, i. e. निसर्ग + इक, adj., f. की, Innate, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 660.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्नेह्य
नैस्नेह्य नैस्नेह्य, see नैःस्नेह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नो
नो नो, i. e. न-उ, a particle.<BR> 1. Nor, Suśr. 2, 461, 18.<BR> 2. Not, Pañc. i. d. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदन|नोदनं
नोदन नोदन, i. e. नुद् + अन, n. Removing, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदिन्
नोदिन् नोदिन्, i. e. नुद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधस्
नोधस् नोधस्, m. The name of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधा
नोधा नोधा (= नवधा), adv. In nine parts, Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ नौ,<BR> I. see अस्मद्.<BR> II. probably स्ना + व, f. A ship, a boat.<BR> --Cf. ναῦς; Lat. navis; O.H.G. nacho; A.S. naca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौक
नौक नौ + क,<BR> I. a substitute for नौ when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. भिन्न- (vb. भिद्), adj. Wrecked.<BR> II. f. का, A small vessel, a boat, Rām. 1, 9, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कार|न्यक्कारः
न्यक्कार न्यक्कार, i. e. न्यञ्च्-कार, m.<BR> 1. Humiliation.<BR> 2. Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावयितृ
न्यग्भावयितृ न्यग्भावयितृ, i. e. न्यञ्च्-भू, Caus., + तृ, m., f. त्री, n. One who humbles, Daśak. 180, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोध|न्यग्रोधः
न्यग्रोध न्यग्रोध, i. e. न्यञ्च्-रुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. The Indian fig-tree, Ficus indica, Man. 8, 246.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कु|न्यंकु|न्यंकुः|न्यङ्कुः
न्यङ्कु न्यङ्कु (probably नि-अञ्च् + उ), n. A kind of antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
न्यञ्च् न्यञ्च्, i. e. नि-अञ्च्,<BR> I. adj., f. नीची, Downward.<BR> II. न्यक्, acc. n. adv., Humbly, MBh. 5, 1426; see कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यन्त|न्यन्तः
न्यन्त न्यन्त, i. e. नि-अन्त (m. or n.). Proximity, Rām. 2, 68, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्बुद|न्यर्बुदं
न्यर्बुद न्यर्बुद, i. e. नि-अर्बुद, n. A hundred millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय|न्यायः
न्याय न्याय, i. e. नि-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rule.<BR> 2. Method, manner, Man. 8, 310; Daśak. in Chr. 193, 13.<BR> 3. Suitable manner, propriety, Man. 5, 140.<BR> 4. A lawful act, 189, 15.<BR> 5. A lawsuit, Pañc. 97, 2.<BR> 6. Judgment, iii. d. 89.<BR> 7. A syllogism, Prab. 111, 8.<BR> 8. The Nyāya doctrine, consisting principally in logic.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अ- + न्याय अ- + न्याय, m. an unlawful act, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 15; acc. n. ˚यम्, adv. improperly, Rām. 3, 51, 34. यथा-न्याय + म्, adv. suitably, duly, Man. 3, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायवन्त्|न्यायवत्
न्यायवन्त् न्याय + वन्त्, adj. Behaving properly, Rām. 5, 11, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय्य|न्याय्यं
न्याय्य न्याय्य, i. e. न्याय + य, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b " target="_blank">Page0496-b + 39</a>]<BR> 1. Fit.<BR> 2. Right, Man. 2, 152.<BR> 3. Just, 9, 202.<BR> 4. An infinitive governed by न्याय्य has sometimes the signification of a passive, Rām. 2, 21, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्यास न्यास, i. e. नि- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Planting (as the foot), Rām. 5, 31, 60.<BR> 2. Striking in, seizing with, Ragh. 12, 73.<BR> 3. Seizing with one's claws, MBh. 12, 552.<BR> 4. Putting on, Kathās. 8, 15.<BR> 5. Writing down, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 170.<BR> 6. Laying aside, Vikr. 87, 2; Bhag. 18, 2.<BR> 7. A deposit, Yājñ. 2, 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणन्यास|चरणन्यासः
चरण- + न्यास चरण- + न्यास, m. trace of a foot, Megh. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासिन्
न्यासिन् न्यासिन्, i. e. न्यस + इन्, adj. subst. One who has abandoned all worldly concerns, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं|न्युब्जः
न्युब्ज न्युब्ज, i. e. नि-उब्ज, adj. One who lies on his face, MBh. 5, 7244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यून|न्यूनं
न्यून न्यून, i. e. नि-ऊन, adj., f. ना.<BR> 1. Defective, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 21.<BR> 2. Wanting, MBh. 3, 4057; अर्थ-, Poor.<BR> 3. Smaller, Yājñ. 2, 116; less, Man. 8, 203.<BR> 4. Low, MBh. 13, 6616.<BR> 5. Inferior, MBh. 1, 5592.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनता
न्यूनता न्यून + ता, f. Inferiority, MBh. 8, 774.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
ऽप -प, latter part of a comp. adj. or subst. derived from adj.<BR> I. (vb. 1. पा), Drinking, cf. पाद-प, properly, Drinking by means of the foot, i. e. a tree.<BR> II. (vb. 2. पा),<BR> 1. Guarding, e. g. द्वार-प, m. properly, Guarding a door, i. e. a doorkeeper.<BR> 2. Ruling, e. g. क्षिति-प, m. properly, Ruling the earth, = a king; दशप, i. e. दशन्-प, m. A governor of ten villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंश्
† पंश् पंश्, and पंस् पंस्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कण|पक्कणः
पक्कण पक्कण, m. The but of a Cāṇḍāla, or one of the outcast tribes, Kāśīkh. 12, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति पक्ति, i. e. पच् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Cooking, Man. 9, 11.<BR> 2. Digestion, 12, 120.<BR> 3. Ripening, development, MBh. 12, 9745 (read पक्ति instead of पङ्क्ति).<BR> 4. Dignity, Suśr. 1, 51, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तृ
पक्तृ पक्तृ, i. e. पच् + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Cooking, a cook, MBh. 12, 10935.<BR> 2. Promoting digestion, Suśr. 1, 189, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्व|पक्वं
पक्व पक्व, i. e. पच् + व. It is used as ptcple. of the pf. pass. of पच्, f. वा.<BR> 1. Cooked, Man. 4, 223.<BR> 2. Baked (as a brick, a pot), Yājñ. 1, 197.<BR> 3. Mature, Hit. i. d. 144.<BR> 4. Grey (as hair), Lass. Anth. 80, 17.<BR> 5. Accomplished, perfect.<BR> 6. On the eve of decay, Bhāg. P. 4, 28, 38.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πέπων (from which we may infer that पक्व is curtailed पक्वन्), πεπανός, with ρ for ν, curtailed in δρυπεπής, δρύπεψ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अ- + पक्व अ- + पक्व, adj. 1. uncooked. 2. unbaked (as a pot). 3. indigested. 4. immature. 5. imperfect, MBh. 12, 8440.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिपक्व
अन्-अति-पक्व अन्-अति-पक्व, adj. rather immature (figuratively), Daśak. in Chr. 195, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपक्व
काल- + पक्व काल- + पक्व, adj. matured by time, Man. 6, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वण
पक्वण पक्वण = पक्कण, MBh. 12, 5330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वापक्वा
पक्वापक्वा पक्वापक्वा, a sound imitative of the ery of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्
† पक्ष् पक्ष्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To seize; cf. पश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष पक्ष, m.<BR> 1. A wing; also n., Mārk. P. 9, 15.<BR> 2. The feathers of an arrow.<BR> 3. A flank, a side, Ragh. 5, 72.<BR> 4. Half.<BR> 5. The half of a lunar [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-b " target="_blank">Page0497-b + 46</a>] month, comprising fifteen days, Man. 1, 66.<BR> 6. Party, Rām. 2, 18, 13 Gorr. (he who sides with Bharata).<BR> 7. A partisan, Vikr. d. 16.<BR> 8. A friend, Hariv. 3013.<BR> 9. A class, a host, a troop, MBh. 13, 3315; Hariv. 7124.<BR> 10. Place, condition, Rām. 6, 99, 32.<BR> 11. Alternative, Ragh. 4, 10.<BR> 12. Opinion, MBh. 2, 2266.<BR> 13. The subject of an inference, Bhāṣāp. 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps παξ in ἅπαξ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातपक्ष
अ-जात- + पक्ष अ-जात- + पक्ष (vb. जन्), adj. having not yet wings, Rām. 5, 11, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपक्ष|काकपक्षः
काक- + पक्ष काक- + पक्ष, m. the side locks of the head of boys and youths, Rām. 1, 21, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपक्ष|कृष्णपक्षः
कृष्ण- + पक्ष कृष्ण- + पक्ष, m. the dark half of the month, the fifteen days during which the moon is in the wane, Man. 3, 276.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपक्ष|केशपक्षः
केश- + पक्ष केश- + पक्ष, m. a tuft of hair, MBh. 4, 1114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपक्ष
त्रि- + पक्ष त्रि- + पक्ष (m. or n.), three fortnights, Man. 8, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वपक्ष|पूर्वपक्षः|पूर्व्वपक्ष|पूर्व्वपक्षः
पूर्व- + पक्ष पूर्व- + पक्ष, m. 1. the first half of a lunar month, Man. 3, 278. 2. the opponent's proposition, a primā facie assertion. 3. action at law, Yājñ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपक्ष|भूमिपक्षः
भूमि- + पक्ष भूमि- + पक्ष, m. a swift horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापक्ष|महापक्षः
महा- + पक्ष महा- + पक्ष, adj. having a great family, Man. 8, 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
वि- + पक्ष वि- + पक्ष,<BR> I. adj. opposed, inimical.<BR> II. m. 1. an enemy, Pañc. 171, 10. 2. an opponent, a disputant. 3. a negative instance (साध्याभाववान्), Bhāṣāp. 72; one in which the major term is not found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुपक्ष|शत्रुपक्षः
शत्रु- + पक्ष शत्रु- + पक्ष, m. an enemy, Hit. 53, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपक्ष|शुक्लपक्षः
शुक्ल- + पक्ष शुक्ल- + पक्ष, m. the light half of the month, from new to full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपक्ष|सपक्षः
स- + पक्ष स- + पक्ष,<BR> I. adj. 1. winged. 2. having a side or party.<BR> II. m. a similar instance, one in which the major term is found (साध्यवान्), Bhāṣāp. 72.<BR> III. m. a partisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपक्ष|स्वपक्षः
स्व- + पक्ष स्व- + पक्ष, m. a friend, Pañc. iii. d. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षक|पक्षकः
पक्षक पक्ष + क,<BR> I. m. A side, Śiś. 11, 7.<BR> II. A substitute for पक्ष when latter part of a comp. adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षगम
पक्षगम पक्ष-गम, and पक्षंगम पक्षंगम, i. e. पक्ष + म्-गम, Moving by means of wings, flying, Rām. 5, 56, 45; 4, 43, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षता
पक्षता पक्ष + ता, f. Alliance, MBh. 2, 2665.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षति|पक्षतिः
पक्षति पक्ष + ति, f. The root of a wing, Rājat. 1, 374.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवन्त्|पक्षवत्
पक्षवन्त् पक्ष + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Winged, Rām. 4, 63, 5.<BR> 2. Of a noble extraction, MBh. 13, 2965.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षशस्
पक्षशस् पक्ष + शस्, adv. By, or for fortnights, MBh. 13, 5659.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षि
पक्षि पक्षि, i. e. curtailed पक्षिन्, m. A bird, MBh. 12, 9306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिन्
पक्षिन् पक्षिन्, i. e. पक्ष + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Winged (figuratively).<BR> 2. Siding with; in कृष्ण-पक्ष + इन्, Hariv. 4559.<BR> 3. fem. with रात्रि (a night), accompanied by the foregoing and following day, Man. 4, 97.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bird, Man. 1, 44.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1183.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. fugl; A.S. fugul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपक्षिन्
जल- + पक्षिन् जल- + पक्षिन्, m. a water-fowl, Pañc. 159, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिमृगता
पक्षिमृगता पक्षिमृगता, i. e. पक्षिन्-मृग + ता, f. The form of a bird or beast, Man. 12, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षीय
पक्षीय पक्षीय, i. e. पक्ष + ईय, in कृष्ण-पक्ष + ईय, adj. Siding with Kṛṣṇa, Hariv. 3748.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मन्
पक्ष्मन् पक्ष्मन् (akin to पक्ष), n. An eye-lash, Suśr. 1, 115, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पक्ष्मन्
उद्- + पक्ष्मन् उद्- + पक्ष्मन्, adj. whose eye-lids are elevated, Śāk. d. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मल
पक्ष्मल पक्ष्मल, i. e. पक्ष्मन् + अ, with ल् for न्, adj.<BR> 1. Having long eye-lashes, Kathās. 18, 14.<BR> 2. Hairy, Śiś. 4, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क|पंक|पंकं|पंकः|पङ्कः
पङ्क पङ्क, m. Mud, mire, clay, Man. 4, 191.<BR> 2. Ointment, Ṛt. 1, 6; Rām. 3, 53, 57 (mire and ointment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कज|पंकज|पङ्कजं|पङ्कजः
पङ्कज पङ्क-ज,<BR> 1. m. A lotus [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b " target="_blank">Page0498-b + 40</a>] flower, Śāk. d. 124.<BR> 2. f. जी, A name of Durgā, MBh. 4, 188.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपङ्कज
स- + पङ्कज स- + पङ्कज, adj., f. जा, abounding in lotus flowers, Rām. 3, 68, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कवन्त्|पङ्कवत्
पङ्कवन्त् पङ्क + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Muddy, Rām. 2, 28, 9 (15 Gorr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किन्|पंकिन्
पङ्किन् पङ्किन्, i. e. पङ्क + इन्, latter part of comp. adj. Muddy, MBh. 3, 2959. मांस-शोणित-पङ्क + इन्, Filled instead of mire with flesh and blood, MBh. 8, 2551.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किल|पंकिल|पङ्किलः
पङ्किल पङ्किल, i. e. पङ्क + इल, adj., f. ला, Muddy, MBh. 8, 4005.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्केरुह|पंकेरुह|पङ्केरुहं|पङ्केरुहः
पङ्केरुह पङ्केरुह, i. e. पङ्क + इ-रुह् + अ, m. A lotus flower, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्ति|पंक्ति|पंक्तिः|पङ्क्तिः
पङ्क्ति and पङ्क्ती पङ्क्ती̆ (akin to पञ्चन्), f. The number five, πεντάς, समर-बाण-, The five arrows of the god of love, Rājat. 3, 525.<BR> 2. A sort of metre, consisting of four times ten syllables.<BR> 3. The number ten, Ragh. 12, 99.<BR> 4. A line, a row, Pañc. 182, 16.<BR> 5. A multitude, a flock, Mārk. P. 43, 9.<BR> 6. A company, Man. 3, 183.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदपङ्क्ति|पदपंक्ति|पदपङ्क्तिः
पद- + पङ्क्ति पद- + पङ्क्ति, a line of footsteps, Śāk. d. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गु|पंगु|पङ्गुः
पङ्गु पङ्गु, perhaps anomal. comp. अप-अङ्ग + उ, adj., f. गू and ग्वी, Lame, Suśr. 1, 89, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुक|पंगुक
पङ्गुक पङ्गु + क, adj. Lame, MBh. 12, 2135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुता
पङ्गुता पङ्गु + ता, f. Lameness, Man. 11, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुल|पंगुल|पङ्गुलः
पङ्गुल पङ्गु + ल,<BR> 1. adj. Lame.<BR> 2. Lameness, Suśr. 1, 360, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्
1. पच् पच्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To cook, to bake, Man. 3, 118.<BR> 2. To roast, 7, 20.<BR> 3. pass. To be inflamed, 9, 231.<BR> 4. To melt, Hariv. 5525.<BR> 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-a " target="_blank">Page0499-a + 42</a>] To digest, Suśr. 1, 78, 5.<BR> 6. To ripen. Ragh. 11, 50 (figurat.).<BR> 7. To conduct something to its end, Rām. 6, 8, 16.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the present Ātm. अ-पचमान, adj. One who does not prepare food for himself, a religious mendicant, Man. 4, 32. Anomalous पचान, MBh. 3, 13239. Pass. with the termination of the Par., 5, 3792.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पक्व (see s. v.).<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. कृष्ट-पच्य, adj. Sown or ripening after ploughing, cultivated, Bhāg. P. 7, 12, 18.<BR> --Caus. पाचय,<BR> 1. To cause to be dressed, MBh. 3, 104.<BR> 2. To cure, Suśr. 1, 155, 20. Frequent. पापच् and पापच्य,<BR> 1. To roast, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 27.<BR> 2. To burn violently (figur., to be much afflicted), 4, 3, 21.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To ripen softly, 8, 5, 35.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To boil up, Suśr. 1, 149, 11.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To heat, Suśr. 2, 67, 2.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To cook, Pañc. 199, 10.<BR> 2. To roast, Hariv. 6079.<BR> 3. To mature, Hariv. 4875.<BR> 4. To conduct something to its end, MBh. 12, 8306.<BR> --Caus. To mature by cooking, Suśr. 1, 230, 15.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To use to cook, Rām. 3, 76, 24.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To develope, Suśr. 1, 322, 6.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To dissolve by cooking, Suśr. 1, 32, 20.<BR> 2. To roast, MBh. 13, 6122.<BR> 3. To digest, MBh. 14, 570.<BR> 4. To ripen, Ragh. 17, 53.<BR> --Caus. To dissolve by cooking.<BR> --Cf. Lat. coquere (for poquere by assimilation), culina (for cuclina); πέπτω, πέσσω, πόπανον, probably also ὀπτός, and ἕψω, ἕψημα, ἑϕθός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्
† 2. पच् पच् and पञ्च् पञ्च्, 1 Ātm. (Par.), To make evident. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b " target="_blank">Page0499-b + 41</a>] पञ्च्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To state fully.<BR> 2. To spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
ऽपच -पच् + अ, latter part of comp. adj. Cooking, baking, roasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचन|पचनं|पचनः
पचन पच् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Cooking, Suśr. 1, 31, 13.<BR> 2. Ripening, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 40.<BR> 3. Becoming entirely cooked, MBh. 9, 2780.<BR> 4. A frying-pan Suśr. 2, 158, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्च्|पंच्
पञ्च् पञ्च्, see 2. पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्च|पंच
ऽपञ्च -पञ्च (see पञ्चन्); in चतुःपञ्च, i. e. चतुर्-, adj. Four or five, Rājat. 6, 326.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चक|पंचक|पञ्चकं|पञ्चकः
पञ्चक पञ्चक, i. e. पञ्चन् + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Consisting of five, Man. 2, 92.<BR> 2. With शत, Five in the hundred, Man. 8, 139.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The number five, πεντάς शत-, Five hundred, Pañc. 134, 16.<BR> 2. A collection of five, Bhāg. P. 3, 11, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चक
पञ्चपञ्चक पञ्चप्˚, i. e. पञ्चन्-, n. the twenty-five (principles of the Sāṅkhya philosophy), Rām. 3, 53, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृत्वस्|पंचकृत्वस्
पञ्चकृत्वस् पञ्चकृत्वस्, i. e. पञ्चन्-कृत्वस्, adv. Five times, Suśr. 1, 365, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चता|पंचता
पञ्चता पञ्चता, i. e. पञ्चन् + ता, f.<BR> 1. Quintuple amount, Man. 8, 151.<BR> 2. Death (properly, Solution of the body into its five elements), Kathās. 10, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्व|पंचत्व|पंचत्वं|पञ्चत्वं
पञ्चत्व पञ्चत्व, i. e. पञ्चन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. The five elements, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 41.<BR> 2. Death (see पञ्चता), Hariv. 1139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशधा
पञ्चदशधा पञ्चदशधा, i. e. पञ्चदशन् + धा, adv. In fifteen parts, Mārk. P. 78, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशन्|पंचदशन्
पञ्चदशन् पञ्चदशन्, i. e. पञ्चन्-दशन्, numer. adj. Fifteen, Man. 10, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशाहिक
पञ्चदशाहिक पञ्चदशाहिक, i. e. पञ्चदशन्-अह + इक, adj. Lasting fifteen days, Yājñ. 3, 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चधा|पंचधा
पञ्चधा पञ्चधा, i. e. पञ्चन् + धा, adv. In five parts, five-fold, Yājñ. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चन्|पंचन्
पञ्चन् पञ्चन्, numer. adj. Five, Man. 2, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपुष्पमय
पञ्चपुष्पमय पञ्चपुष्पमय, i. e. पञ्चन्-पुष्प + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of five flowers, Kathās. 34, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चम|पंचम|पञ्चमं|पञ्चमः
पञ्चम पञ्चम, i. e. पञ्चन् + म,<BR> I. ordinal number, f. मी, Fifth, Man. 2, 37.<BR> II. acc. n. मम्, adv. Fifthly, Man. 8, 125.<BR> III. with अंश, A fifth part, Man. 9, 164.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. One of the seven musical notes, originally the fifth, afterwards the seventh, MBh. 14, 1419.<BR> 2. One of the modes of music, Gīt. 10, 13.<BR> V. f. मी.<BR> 1. The fifth day of the half month, Hariv. 10241.<BR> 2. The name of a river, MBh. 6, 333.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपञ्चम
अर्ध- + पञ्चम अर्ध- + पञ्चम, adj. four and a half, Man. 4, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमक
पञ्चमक पञ्चम + क, adj. Fifth, Śrut. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमय
पञ्चमय पञ्चमय, i. e. पञ्चन् + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of five (clements), Mārk. P. 37, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवट|पञ्चवटः
पञ्चवट पञ्चवट, i. e. पञ्चन्-वट, n. and f. टी, The name of a locality near the Godāvarī, Rām. 1, 3, 18 (13 Gorr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्षीय|पंचवर्षीय
पञ्चवर्षीय पञ्चवर्षीय, i. e. पञ्चन्-वर्ष + ईय, adj. Five years old, Śatr. 11, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंशक
पञ्चविंशक पञ्चविंशक, i. e. पञ्चन्-विंश + क, adj.<BR> 1. Twenty-fifth, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 15.<BR> 2. Twenty-five (years old), Rām. iii. p. 469.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंशतिका|पंचविंशतिका
पञ्चविंशतिका पञ्चविंशतिका, i. e. पञ्चन्-विंशति + क, fem.; in वेताल-, Twenty-five tales of a Vetāla; the title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशस्|पंचशस्
पञ्चशस् पञ्चशस्, i. e. पञ्चन् + शस्, adv. Five by five, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चष|पंचष
पञ्चष पञ्चष, i. e. पञ्चन्-षष्, adj. Five or six, Rājat. 5, 333.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चा
पञ्चा पञ्च् + आ, f. Spreading; in चञ्चत्पञ्च, i. e. चञ्चन्त्-, adj. Shaking in all its parts, Utt. Rāmac. 120, 3 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाग्नित्व
पञ्चाग्नित्व पञ्चाग्नित्व, i. e. पञ्चन्-अग्नि + त्व, n. An aggregate of five fires (or passions), Kathās. 28, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाल|पंचाल|पञ्चालः
पञ्चाल पञ्चाल, m.<BR> 1. pl. The name of a people and their country, Man. 2, 19.<BR> 2. A prince of the Pañcālas, MBh. 12, 13262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चालक
पञ्चालक पञ्चाल + क,<BR> I. adj. Referring to the Pañcālas; with राजन्, A prince of the Pañcālas, MBh. 5, 7504 (perhaps to be changed to पाञ्चा-लक).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. pl. = The Pañcālas, Bhāg. P. 9, 22, 3.<BR> 2. A certain poisonous insect, Suśr. 2, 288, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाश|पंचाश
पञ्चाश पञ्चाश (cf. पञ्चाशत्), ordinal number, fem. शी, Fiftieth, Chr. 73, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपञ्चाश
एक- + पञ्चाश एक- + पञ्चाश, fifty-first, Chr. 76, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वापञ्चाश|द्वापंचाश
द्वा- + पञ्चाश द्वा- + पञ्चाश and द्वि-, fifty-second, Rām. 4, 52; Chr. 81, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपञ्चाश|त्रिपंचाश
त्रि- + पञ्चाश त्रि- + पञ्चाश, fifty-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःपञ्चाश
चतुःपञ्चाश चतुःपञ्चाश, i. e. चतुर्-, fifty-fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चाश|पंचपंचाश
पञ्चपञ्चाश पञ्चपञ्चाश, i. e. पञ्चन्-, fiftyfifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्|पंचाशत्
पञ्चाशत् पञ्चाशत्, i. e. पञ्चा-दशन्ति (cf. चत्वारिंशत्), numeral, f. Fifty, Man. 8, 297.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πεντήκοντα; Lat. quinquâginta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वापञ्चाशत्|द्वापंचाशत्
द्वा- + पञ्चाशत् द्वा- + पञ्चाशत् and द्वि-, fifty-two, Hariv. 13076; MBh. 2, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःपञ्चाशत्|चतुःपंचाशत्
चतुःपञ्चाशत् चतुःपञ्चाशत्, i. e. चतुर्-, fiftyfour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशति|पंचाशति|पंचाशतिः|पञ्चाशतिः
पञ्चाशति पञ्चाशति, i. e. पञ्चा-दशन्ति (see the preceding), numeral, f. Fifty, Rājat. 5, 71 (आ is perhaps only a mistake; when shortened, we have पञ्चशती, Five hundred).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्क
पञ्चाशत्क पञ्चाशत् + क, adj. Fifty years old, Kām. Nītis. 7, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्तम
पञ्चाशत्तम पञ्चाशत् + तम, ordinal number, f. मी, Fiftieth, MBh. 9, 50.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपञ्चाशत्तम
एक- + पञ्चाशत्तम एक- + पञ्चाशत्तम, fifty-first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपञ्चाशत्तम
त्रि- + पञ्चाशत्तम त्रि- + पञ्चाशत्तम, fiftythird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशद्धा
पञ्चाशद्धा पञ्चाशद्धा, i. e. पञ्चाशत् + धा adv. In fifty parts, Rām. 1, 48, 1 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जर|पंजर|पंजरं|पञ्जरं|पञ्जरः
पञ्जर पञ्जर, n.<BR> 1. A cage, MBh. 12, 3061.<BR> 2. A skeleton, Prab. 71, 1. (Probably akin to पज् in vedic पज्र, पाजस्; cf. πήγνυμι, πάγη; Lat. pango).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जरक|पंजरकं|पंजरकः|पञ्जरकः
पञ्जरक पञ्जर + क, m. or n. A cage, Pañc. iii. d. 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्
पट् पट्, † i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR> --i. 10, पाटय,<BR> 1. † To speak, or to shine.<BR> 2. To split, to divide, MBh. 3, 16747; 882.<BR> 3. To break, to breach, Mṛcch. 47, 16.<BR> 4. To tear, Kathās. 20, 21.<BR> 5. To pluck out, 28, 21.<BR> 6. To cause to be torn up, Yājñ. 2, 94.<BR> 7. † i. 10, पटय, To string, to surround.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, पाटय, To split, Suśr. 1, 32, 12.<BR> --With आ आ, पाटय, To split, Suśr. 2, 22, 19.<BR> --With उद् उद्, पाटय,<BR> 1. To tear out, Man. 4, 69.<BR> 2. To slit up, Rājat. 5, 432.<BR> 3. To open, Pañc. 222, 5.<BR> 4. To destroy, Rām. 6, 88, 19.<BR> 5. To remove, 6, 37, 87.<BR> 6. To dethrone, Rājat. 5, 298.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, पाटय,<BR> 1. To tear out, Rām. 5, 39, 23.<BR> 2. To draw out, Dev. 2, 20.<BR> 3. To dethrone, Rājat. 5, 286. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b " target="_blank">Page0501-b + 43</a>]<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, पाटय, To split, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 16.<BR> --With वि वि, पाटय,<BR> 1. To split, MBh. 12, 591.<BR> 2. To tear, Hariv. 4310.<BR> 3. To uproot, Rājat. 5, 477.<BR> 4. To open, 3, 482 (to bring on).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट|पटं|पटः
पट पट (probably for पत्र), m. and f. टी, and n.<BR> 1. Woven cloth, MBh. 1, 806.<BR> 2. Cloth, Rām. 5, 49, 5.<BR> 3. A piece of cloth, MBh. 1, 4376.<BR> 4. Garment, 5421.<BR> 5. (cf. पट्ट), A table, a plate (for painting and writing), Yājñ. 1, 297.<BR> 6. f. टी, The curtain of a stage.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णपट|ऊर्णपटः
ऊर्ण- + पट ऊर्ण- + पट, m. a spider, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपट|कांडपट|काण्डपटः
काण्ड- + पट काण्ड- + पट, m. a curtain, Daśak. 122, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपट|कुपटः
कु- + पट कु- + पट,<BR> I. m. and n. a plain garment, Bhāg. P. 5, 9, 11.<BR> II. m. the name of a Dānava or demon, MBh. 1, 2534.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपट|चित्रपटः
चित्र- + पट चित्र- + पट, m. or n. a picture, Kathās. 5, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजपट|ध्वजपटः
ध्वज- + पट ध्वज- + पट, m. a flag, a standard, Vikr. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदपट|प्रच्छदपटः
प्रच्छद- + पट प्रच्छद- + पट, and प्रच्छादन-, m. a cover, a blanket, Pañc. 62, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखपट|मुखपटः
मुख- + पट मुख- + पट, m. or n. a veil, Megh. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तोत्तरपट
स्रस्तोत्तर- + पट स्रस्तोत्तर- + पट, i. e. स्रस्त-उत्तर- (vb. स्रंस्), adj. with the upper garment loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटच्चर|पटच्चरं|पटच्चरः
पटच्चर पटच्चर, i. e. पटत् (from पट्, an imitative sound, perhaps of sneaking) -चर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A thief, MBh. 1, 6996.<BR> 2. pl. The name of a people, MBh. 2, 590.<BR> II. n. Old cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटभाक्ष
