पतिंवरा
पतिंवरा पतिंवरा, i. e. पति + म्-वृ + अ, adj. One who chooses her husband herself, Ragh. 6, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिक
ऽपतिक -पति + क, A substitute for पति when latter part of a comp. adj., Man. 9, 68 (प्र-मीत-, f. a widow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्व|पतित्वं
पतित्व पति + त्व, m. Matrimony, marriage, MBh. 3, 2140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिधर्मतस्
पतिधर्मतस् पति-धर्म + तस्, adv. = abl. पति-धर्म, m. The duty to a husband, Chr. 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिधर्मवती
पतिधर्मवती पतिधर्मवती, i. e. पति-धर्म + वन्त् + इ, adj., f. Fulfilling the duties of a wife, MBh. 4, 279.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिन्
पतिन् पतिन् = पति, MBh. 12, 8883.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवत्नी
पतिवत्नी पतिवत्नी, i. e. पति + वन्त् + ई (by metathesis पतिवत्नी, instead of the later पतिवती), f. A married woman, Ragh. 15, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तङ्ग
पत्तङ्ग पत्तङ्ग (for पत्राङ्ग, q. cf.), (n. and) m. Red sanders, Suśr. 1, 46, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तन|पत्तनं
पत्तन पत्तन, i. e. पद् + तन (cf. Lat. op-pidum), n. A town, Mālav. 13, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ति|पत्तिः
पत्ति पत्ति, i. e. पद् + ति (probably for तन्, see पति), m.<BR> 1. A pedestrian.<BR> 2. A foot-soldier, MBh. 5, 5164.<BR> 3. The name of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्त्र
पत्त्र पत्त्र, see पत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नि
पत्नि पत्नि, see पत्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नी
पत्नी पत्नी, and sometimes पत्नि पत्नि, i. e. पतन् (see पति) + ई, f. A wife, Man. 2, 129.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πότνια, δές-ποινα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपत्नी
एक- + पत्नी एक- + पत्नी, f. 1. only one wife, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 53. 2. the wife of one man only, a chaste wife, Man. 5, 158. 3. pl. the several wives of one husband, Man. 9, 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपत्नी
गुरु- + पत्नी गुरु- + पत्नी, f. a mother-in-law, 9, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपत्नी
देव- + पत्नी देव- + पत्नी, f. the wife of a god, Kathās. 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपत्नी|धर्म्मपत्नी
धर्म- + पत्नी धर्म- + पत्नी, f. a lawful wife, Man. 3, 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नी
स- + पत्नी स- + पत्नी, f. a wife whose husband has other wives, Chr. 55, 2; Pañc. i. d. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीक
ऽपत्नीक -पत्नी + क, a substitute for पत्नी when latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. बहु-, Having many wives, Śāk. 90, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीत्व
पत्नीत्व पत्नी + त्व, n. Matrimony, Mārk. P. 50, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्र|पत्त्रं|पत्रं
पत्र पत् + र, n. (perhaps पत् + त्र, but cf. O.H.G. fedara; A.S. feher; and πτερόν for πετρόν).<BR> 1. The wing of a bird.<BR> 2. The feather of an arrow, Rām. 3, 35, 87.<BR> 3. A vehicle in general, as a horse, a camel, a car, Man. 9, 219.<BR> 4. A leaf, Man. 4, 49.<BR> 5. The leaf of the Laurus cassia(?).<BR> 6. A leaf prepared for writing on, paper, Śāk. 81, 2.<BR> 7. A letter. Śāk. 90, 8.<BR> 8. A document, Pañc. i. d. 451.<BR> 9. A thin piece of metal, Suśr. 2, 74, 21.<BR> 10. Lines and signs painted in the faces by means of musk and other fragrant substances, Ragh. 13, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. supra O.H.G. fedara; πτερόν, also πτέρις, πτίλον, πτίλος, and πέτρος (cf. पत्रिन्<BR> 3; in the old poetical language clouds and rocks are identified, and the clouds considered as wings of the mountains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपत्र|अर्कपत्रः
अर्क- + पत्र अर्क- + पत्र, m. Calotropis gigantea; n. its leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
कङ्क- + पत्र कङ्क- + पत्र,<BR> I. n. the feather of a heron, Rām. 4, 7, 22.<BR> II. m. an arrow, Rām. 6, 28, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्र|करपत्रं
कर- + पत्र कर- + पत्र, n. a saw, Hit. 49, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पत्र|त्वक्पत्रं
त्वक्-पत्र त्वक्-पत्र, i. e. त्रच्-, n. woody cassia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपत्र|दंतपत्र|दन्तपत्रं
दन्त- + पत्र दन्त- + पत्र, n. a kind of ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्र
निष्-पत्र निष्-पत्र, i. e. निस्-, adj. leafless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जपत्र|भूर्जपत्रः|भूर्ज्जपत्र|भूर्ज्जपत्रः
भूर्ज- + पत्र भूर्ज- + पत्र, m. a kind of birch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्र|युगपत्रः
युग- + पत्र युग- + पत्र, m. mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपत्र|शतपत्रं|शतपत्रः
शत- + पत्र शत- + पत्र,<BR> I. n. a lotus flower, Rām. 2, 60, 15 Gorr.<BR> II. m. 1. a peacock. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b " target="_blank">Page0508-b + 44</a>] 2. a parrot. 3. a woodpecker. 4. the Indian crane.<BR> III. f. रा, a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पत्र|सत्पत्रं
सत्पत्र सत्प्˚, i. e. सन्त्- (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), n. the new leaf of a waterlily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छपत्र|स्वच्छपत्रं
स्वच्छ- + पत्र स्वच्छ- + पत्र, i. e. सु-अच्छ-, n. talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रक|पत्रकं
पत्रक पत्र + क,<BR> 1. A substitute for पत्र when latter part of a comp. adj. f. त्रिका.<BR> 2. f. त्रिका, A document, a letter, Śāk. 90, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपत्रक|कर्णपत्रकः|कर्ण्णपत्रक
कर्ण-पत्रक कर्ण-पत्रक, m. the lobe of the car, Yājñ. 3, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्रक|युगपत्रकः
युग- + पत्रक युग- + पत्रक, m. mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्ग|पत्रांग|पत्राङ्गं
पत्राङ्ग पत्राङ्ग, i. e. पत्र-अन्ग, n. Red sanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रिन्
पत्रिन् पत्रिन्, i. e. पत्र + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणि.<BR> 1. Winged, Hariv. 5470.<BR> 2. Feathered, MBh. 3, 709.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bird, Śāk. 78, 19.<BR> 2. An arrow, Kathās. 33, 203.<BR> 3. A mountain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्रिन्|कंकपत्रिन्
कङ्क- + पत्रिन् कङ्क- + पत्रिन्, m. an arrow, MBh. 4, 1804.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपत्रिन्
पुष्प- + पत्रिन् पुष्प- + पत्रिन्, adj. having flowers for arrows, Kumāras. 4, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्
1. पथ् पथ्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --† i. 10, पाथय, To throw (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्
2. पथ् पथ्, see पथिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ|पथः
पथ पथ,<BR> 1. m. Way, reach, Rām. 3, 56, 3.<BR> 2. Latter part of comp. words = पथिन्, A way, a road. अ-, m. A wrong way. अपत्य-, m. The vulva. अर्ध-, m. The half of a way. आर्य-, m. The road of the honourable ones. उत्तरा- and उदक्पथ, i. e. उदञ्च्-, m. The northern country. कुसिद-, m. An usurious way, Man. 8, 152. जल-, m. A sea voyage. त्रि-, n. Heaven, earth, and the infernal regions. दक्षिणा-, m. The southern country. दर्शन-, m. Sight. दिक्पथ, i. e. दिश्-, m. The road of the country, Rājat. 5, 341. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a " target="_blank">Page0509-a + 44</a>] दृक्पथ, i. e. दृश्-, m. Sight, Vikr. d. 95. धर्म-, m. The road of virtue. धूम-, m. A sacrifice, Bhāg. P. 4, 4, 10. नक्षत्र-, m. The starred heaven. नयन-, m. Sight, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 1. पाषण्ड-, m. The way of the heretics, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 6. बणिक्पथ, i. e. बणिज्-, m. Trade, Man. 1, 90. रोमराजि-, i. e. रोमन्-राजि- (m.), A line of hair extending to the navel; in तनुरोम-राजिपथ, The waist, Śiś. 9, 22. वि-, m. A bad road. श्री-, m. A highway. सत्प्˚, i. e. सन्त्- (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), m.<BR> 1. A good road.<BR> 2. Correct conduct. सु-,<BR> I. adj. Having good roads, Lass. 97, 2 (था, ved. for थानि).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A good road.<BR> 2. Good conduct.<BR> --Cf. πάτος; A.S. padh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिक|पथिकः
पथिक पथिक, i. e. पथ + इक, m. A traveller, Pañc. 245, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिन्
पथिन् पथिन्, for पन्थन् (cf. परिपन्थिन्), which is the base of some cases, the bases of some others is पथ्, the nom. and voc. sing. पन्थास्, m.<BR> 1. A road, a way, Megh. 28.<BR> 2. The name of a hell, Man. 4, 90.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pons, pontis, and perhaps ponto, pontonis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपथिन्
अर्ध- + पथिन् अर्ध- + पथिन्, m. the half of a way, Pañc. 134, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपथिन्
धर्म- + पथिन् धर्म- + पथिन्, m. the road of virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपथिन्
सह- + पथिन् सह- + पथिन्, m. a fellow-traveller, Rām. 3, 53, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्य|पथ्यं|पथ्यः
पथ्य पथ्य, i. e. पथ + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या, Furthering, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 448. Fit, suitable, salutary, Pañc. 69, 17.<BR> II. f. या, Yellow myrobalan, Terminalia chebula.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अ- + पथ्य अ- + पथ्य, adj. unfit, unwholesome, Yājñ. 3, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्
1. पद् पद्, i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.),<BR> 1. To fall (ved.).<BR> 2. To go to (acc.), MBh. 1, 4288.<BR> 3. To obtain, MBh. 9, 2847.<BR> 4. To observe, 7, 16.<BR> --Caus. पादय; i. 10, † पदय, To go.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-b " target="_blank">Page0509-b + 43</a>] follow, MBh. 1, 6710.<BR> 2. To court, MBh. 1, 4180.<BR> 3. To resort to, Rām. 2, 45, 4.<BR> 4. To fall down, MBh. 7, 3361.<BR> 5. To find out, Bhāg. P. 4, 17, 12.<BR> 6. To be deprived of, to lose (with abl.), MBh. 12, 4653.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To obtain, Hariv. 11210.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To come near, to approach, MBh. 1, 8105.<BR> 2. To come to (acc. and loc.), 13, 4375.<BR> 3. To worship, Śiś. 9, 27.<BR> 4. To come to one's assistance (acc.), MBh. 6, 4043; to assist, 1, 1981.<BR> 5. To seize, to catch, Rām. 5, 41, 24.<BR> 6. To assail, MBh. 8, 3047.<BR> 7. To attain, Man. 1, 30.<BR> 8. To accept, Rām. 2, 36, 12.<BR> 9. To apply one's self to, Rām. 2, 63, 1.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि,<BR> 1. To come to, to attain, MBh. 1, 5515.<BR> 2. To come on, MBh. 3, 12539.<BR> 3. To answer, 10441.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To fall down.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. केश-किट-अवपन्न, On which lice have fallen, Man. 4, 207.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To come near, Bhāg. P. 5, 8, 25.<BR> 2. To enter, Rām. 6, 16, 21.<BR> 3. To fall into, Man. 10, 104.<BR> 4. To undergo, Prab. 33, 8.<BR> 5. To become unfortunate, Rām. 2, 53, 13.<BR> 6. To be, Mālav. 14, 23.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. आपन्न,<BR> 1. Unfortunate.<BR> 2. Having obtained, Bhāg. P. 9, 16, 37.<BR> 3. Obtained, Rām. 2, 43, 31 Gorr.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To put somebody into a certain state or condition; मृत्युम् आपादित, Killed, Rām. 2, 73, 5.<BR> 2. To ruin somebody, Vikr. 33, 2.<BR> 3. To procure, MBh. 1, 7873.<BR> 4. To produce, to cause, Rām. 2, 74, 5.<BR> 5. To make, to change into, Daśak. 183, 2.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-अ, To return. प्रत्यापन्न, Returned, Bhāg. P. 8, 11, 48.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To perish, MBh. 7, 3008 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0510-a " target="_blank">Page0510-a + 42</a>]<BR> व्यापन्न,<BR> 1. Fallen into disorder.<BR> 2. Spoiled.<BR> 3. Failed, Suśr. 1, 21, 9.<BR> 4. Dead.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, alive, Megh. 10.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To injure, Suśr. 1, 21, 11.<BR> 2. To ruin, to destroy, MBh. 1, 1607.<BR> 3. To kill, Pañc. 22, 15.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To assail, MBh. 5, 2002.<BR> 2. To undergo, MBh. 13, 411; to begin, Rām. 6, 92, 4.<BR> समापन्न,<BR> 1. Come.<BR> 2. Endowed with, MBh. 2, 2588.<BR> --With अभिसमा अह्बि-सम्-आ, To undergo, to begin, Rām. 2, 12, 1.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To spring up, to rise, Man. 1, 70.<BR> 2. To be brought forth, 9, 170.<BR> 3. To become, 4, 228.<BR> उत्पन्न,<BR> 1. Brought forth.<BR> 2. Complete, Yājñ. 2, 157.<BR> 3. Ready, MBh. 12, 4913. गूढोत्पन्न, i. e. गूढ- (vb. गुह्), Secretly born, i. e. one whose father is unknown, Man. 9, 159.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To produce, Pañc. 132, 4; to bring forth, Man. 9, 175.<BR> 2. To cause to be shed, Man. 4, 167.<BR> 3. To procure, 2, 148.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोत्पन्न, Developed, Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 4.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, प्रत्युत्पन्न,<BR> 1. Present, MBh. 12, 8278.<BR> 2. Ready, Śāk. 67, 23.<BR> --With व्युद् वि-उद्, To become clear in (its) etymological relation, Śiś. 10, 23.<BR> व्युत्पन्न, Learned, versed, Bhartṛ. Suppl. 18.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To produce, to cause, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 33.<BR> 2. To explain etymologically.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, (समु सम्-उ, MBh. 12, 946, on account of the metre, see Caus.),<BR> 1. To spring up, to arise, Pañc. iii. d. 214.<BR> 2. To be brought forth, Man. 10, 66.<BR> 3. To come Rām. 2, 29, 11.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To produce Mārk. P. 17, 6.<BR> 2. To cause, Rājat. 5, 6.<BR> 3. To expect, MBh. 12, 4912 (समुपादयेत्).<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To come to, Pañc. 9, 5.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0510-b " target="_blank">Page0510-b + 45</a>] attain (acc. and dat.), Bhag. 13, 18.<BR> 3. To undergo, Rām. 2, 72, 50.<BR> 4. To take place, Man. 9, 121.<BR> 5. To appear, Mārk. P. 49, 4.<BR> 6. To be suitable, Śāk. 15, 6.<BR> 7. To spring up, MBh. 14, 455.<BR> उपपन्न,<BR> 1. Present.<BR> 2. Suitable.<BR> 3. Endowed, provided with.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, unnatural, Śāk. 111, 1.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To induce to get, Rām. 5, 57, 12.<BR> 2. To give, Man. 9, 73.<BR> 3. To accomplish, Rām. 2, 50, 10 Gorr.<BR> 4. To make suitable, to prepare, Man. 9, 36.<BR> 5. To provide with.<BR> 6. To make, to declare, Prab. 111, 17.<BR> 7. To select, Man. 3, 206.<BR> 8. To argue, Rām. 5, 18, 22.<BR> --With अभ्युप अभि-उप,<BR> 1. To come to one's assistance, MBh. 10, 608.<BR> 2. To come for receiving assistance, Rām. 3, 14, 7.<BR> 3. To provide with, MBh. 2, 187.<BR> अभ्युपपन्न,<BR> 1. Sprung up; in -वत्सल, adj. Affectionate, Mṛcch. 108, 5.<BR> 2. Admitted.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To be accomplished, MBh. 2, 779.<BR> --Caus. To prepare, Rām. 5, 14, 45.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निष्पद् निष्पद्,<BR> 1. To spring up, to arise.<BR> 2. To ripen, Man. 9, 247.<BR> निष्पन्न,<BR> 1. Sprung up, Rām. 5, 2, 32.<BR> 2. Descended, Rām. 1, 6, 23.<BR> 3. Accomplished, Rājat. 4, 234.<BR> 4. Ready.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to ripen, Kathās. 20, 87.<BR> 2. To accomplish, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 43.<BR> 3. To prepare, Lass. Anth. 17, 17.<BR> 4. To perform, Rājat. 5, 21.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To enter, Man. 4, 77.<BR> 2. To begin, 4, 60.<BR> 3. To attain, Bhāg. P. 3, 6, 22.<BR> 4. To come to, Ragh. 12, 68.<BR> 5. To come for receiving assistance, Rām. 1, 57, 16.<BR> 6. To embrace (the doctrine of Jina), Rājat. 1, 102.<BR> 7. To fall down, MBh. 1, 1183.<BR> 8. To undergo, Yājñ. 1, 132.<BR> 9. To be going on, to succeed, MBh. 13, 3527.<BR> 10. To admit, Yājñ. 2, 40.<BR> 11. प्र-पन्न, Provided, Śāk. d. 1. Desider. प्र-पित्स, To be a bout to begin, Daśak. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0511-a " target="_blank">Page0511-a + 44</a>] 114, 10.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र,<BR> 1. To enter one after another, MBh. 3, 6772.<BR> 2. To enter, Suśr. 1, 258, 7.<BR> 3. To appear, MBh. 13, 7363.<BR> 4. To follow, Bhag. 9, 21.<BR> 5. To comply with (acc.), Rām. 5, 28, 5.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र,<BR> 1. To hasten to, MBh. 1, 1182.<BR> 2. To begin, MBh. 3, 1209.<BR> 3. अभिप्रपन्न, Come for assistance, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 20.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To set out on, to begin, Hariv. 5289.<BR> 2. To enter, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 2.<BR> 3. To turn to somebody, especially for assistance, Hariv. 11685.<BR> 4. To succeed, Pañc. ii. d. 137.<BR> 5. संप्रपन्न, Endowed, Caurap. 43.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To go to, to enter, Rām. 2, 33, 21.<BR> 2. To come to, MBh. 1, 5918.<BR> 3. To return, Man. 6, 74.<BR> 4. To obtain, Man. 7, 40.<BR> 5. To receive, Rām. 1, 39, 15 Gorr.<BR> 6. To recover, Man. 2, 120.<BR> 7. To perceive, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 57.<BR> 8. To learn, MBh. 5, 6027.<BR> 9. To consider.<BR> 10. To comply with, Pañc. 129, 4.<BR> 11. To avow, Śāk. d. 119.<BR> 12. To promise, Kathās. 1, 45.<BR> 13. To give, Rām. 2, 1, 8.<BR> 14. To act, MBh. 1, 1936.<BR> 15. To perform, MBh. 2, 1420.<BR> 16. To make, MBh. 4, 703.<BR> 17. To restore, Man. 8, 183.<BR> 18. प्रतिपन्न, Offered, Mālav. d. 48; admitted; acting; conversant with, MBh. 2, 1949.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To lead to, MBh. 3, 2852.<BR> 2. To procure, MBh. 1, 3417.<BR> 3. To bestow on, Man. 11, 4.<BR> 4. To deliver, 9, 190.<BR> 5. To install, Rām. 1, 1, 68.<BR> 6. To cause, Rām. 4, 22, 20.<BR> 7. To prepare.<BR> 8. To teach, Man. 8, 391.<BR> 9. To consider, Pañc. 169, 22.<BR> --With विप्रति वि-प्रति,<BR> 1. To go in different directions.<BR> 2. To waver, MBh. 5, 4276.<BR> 3. विप्रतिपन्न, Opposite, Rām. 2, 109, 1.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति,<BR> 1. To attain, Suśr. 1, 267, 13.<BR> 2. To approach, MBh. 14, 946.<BR> 3. To befull, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0511-b " target="_blank">Page0511-b + 44</a>] Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 164.<BR> 4. To recover, Rām. 3, 73, 16.<BR> 5. To receive, Hariv. 12201.<BR> 6. To agree, MBh. 5, 2706.<BR> 7. To consider, Kumāras. 5, 37.<BR> 8. To perform, MBh. 13, 3629.<BR> --Caus. To grant, MBh. 3, 12759.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. Not to turn out well, Rām. 2, 23, 18.<BR> 2. To perish, Rām. 2, 64, 68.<BR> 3. To miscarry.<BR> 4. विपन्न, Weakened, unfortunate.<BR> --Caus. To kill, Rājat. 2, 79.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To succeed, MBh. 14, 154.<BR> 2. To amount to (acc.), Hariv. 15082.<BR> 3. To become, MBh. 1, 2995.<BR> 4. To be brought forth, MBh. 1, 3143.<BR> 5. To get, to obtain (with instr., loc., and acc.), Mālav. d. 52; Bhag. 13, 30; Rām. 3, 54, 12.<BR> सम्पन्न,<BR> 1. Endowed with.<BR> 2. Accomplished.<BR> 3. Conversant with. n. Sweetmeats(?), Pañc. iv. d. 81.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To convey, to procure, MBh. 13, 2867.<BR> 2. To cause to succeed, to bring about, Bhartṛ. 2, 59.<BR> 3. To perform, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 14.<BR> 4. To prepare, Rām. 3, 28, 27.<BR> 5. To complete, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 35.<BR> 6. To turn into, Kathās. 37, 114.<BR> 7. To endow with, MBh. 6, 2304.<BR> 8. To attain, Rām. 5, 3, 40.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, अभिसंपन्न, Composed, Utt. Rāmac. 135, 6.<BR> --With उपसम् उप-सम्, To attain, MBh. 11, 363.<BR> उपसंपन्न,<BR> 1. Conversant with.<BR> 2. Endowed with.<BR> 3. Diseased, Man. 5, 81.<BR> --Caus. To convey, to procure.<BR> --Cf. 3. पद्; πηδάω, ὀπαδός; perhaps Goth. finthan; A.S. findan; the anomalous reflex of Sskr. द् may have been caused by न्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

