परिसंख्या|परिसङ्ख्या
परिसंख्या परिसंख्या, i. e. परि-सम्-ख्या,<BR> 1. Full number, totality, Man. 1, 72.<BR> 2. Number.<BR> 3. Full enumeration (leaving nothing unsaid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसंख्यान|परिसङ्ख्यान|परिसंख्यानं
परिसंख्यान परिसंख्यान, i. e. परि-सम्-ख्या + अन, n.<BR> 1. = the preceding 1, 2, 3.<BR> 2. Just examination, Yājñ. 3, 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमूहन|परिसमूहनं
परिसमूहन परि-सम्-ऊह् + अन, n. Sweeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर|परिसरः
परिसर परिसर, i. e. परि-सृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Encompassing, Megh. 68.<BR> II. m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b " target="_blank">Page0529-b + 39</a>]<BR> 1. Border, Pañc. 25, 3.<BR> 2. Proximity, Vikr. d. 119.<BR> 3. Standing-place, Suśr. 2, 166, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदावरीपरिसर
गोदावरी- + परिसर गोदावरी- + परिसर, adj. being near the Godāvarī, Utt. Rāmac. 56, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्पण|परिसर्पणं
परिसर्पण परिसर्पण, i. e. परि-सृप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Creeping, Mṛcch. 46, 13.<BR> 2. Walking about.<BR> 3. Running to and fro, Mṛcch. 15, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्पिन्
परिसर्पिन् परिसर्पिन्, i. e. परि-सृप् + इन्, adj. Moving about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसान्त्वन
परिसान्त्वन परि-सान्त्व् + अन, n. Consoling, Utt. Rāmac. 5, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसाधन
परिसाधन परि-साध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Performing.<BR> 2. Settling, Man. 8, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्द|परिस्कंद|परिस्कन्दः
परिस्कन्द परि-स्कन्द् + अ, m. A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तर|परिस्तरः
परिस्तर परिस्तर, i. e. परि-स्तृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A layer.<BR> 2. A cover(?), MBh. 5, 5246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तोम|परिस्तोमः
परिस्तोम परि-स्तोम, m. (n. MBh. 6, 2287), A cover, a bolster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्द|परिस्पंद|परिस्पंदः|परिस्पन्दः
परिस्पन्द परि-स्पन्द् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Motion, Bhāṣāp. 122.<BR> 2. Attention to, MBh. 13, 6438.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पर्धिन्
परिस्पर्धिन् परि-स्पर्ध् + इन्, adj. Emulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्यन्द|परिस्यंद|परिस्यंदः|परिस्यन्दः
परिस्यन्द परि-स्यन्द् + अ, m. Flow, stream (figuratively), Bhartṛ. 1, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रव|परिस्रवः
परिस्रव परिस्रव, i. e. परि-स्रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. A river, a torrent, MBh. 7, 6437.<BR> 2. Birth (of a child), Rām. 1, 38, 26 (erroneously परिश्रव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहर्षण
परिहर्षण परिहर्षण, i. e. परि-हृष्, Caus., + अन, adj., f. णी, Causing much pleasure, MBh. 9, 582.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहाटक
परिहाटक परि-हाटक, n. A ring worn on the arms or legs, MBh. 4, 453.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहाणि|परिहाणिः
परिहाणि परिहाणि, i. e. परि-हा + नि, f. Decreasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहार|परिहारः
परिहार and परीहार परी̆हार, i. e. परि-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Avoiding, MBh. 12, 848.<BR> 2. Escaping, Hariv. 577.<BR> 3. Abandoning, Vikr. 32, 15.<BR> 4. Removing.<BR> 5. Reserve, MBh. 13, 5116.<BR> 6. Concealment, Śāk. 39, 9 (ed. Will.).<BR> 7. Leaving out.<BR> 8. Largess, Man. 7, 201.<BR> 9. A space round a town or village left for pasture, Man. 8, 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहारिन्
परिहारिन् परिहारिन्, i. e. परि-हृ + इन्, adj. Avoiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहास|परिहासः
परिहास and परीहास परी̆हास, i. e. परि-हस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Jest, Vikr. 13, 1; pleasantry, Nal. 11, 8.<BR> 2. Deriding, mocking, Pañc. iii. d. 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षक|परीक्षकः
परीक्षक परीक्षक, i. e. परि-ईक्ष् + अक, m. An examiner, one who knows well, Pañc. i. d. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षण|परीक्षणं
परीक्षण परीक्षण, i. e. परि-ईक्ष् + अन, n. and f. णा, Examination, Man. 1, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षा
परीक्षा परीक्षा, i. e. परि-ईक्ष् + अ, f. Examination, test, Man. 9, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परीक्ष
निष्परीक्ष निष्परीक्ष, i. e. निस्-, adj. not examining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षित्
परीक्षित् परीक्षित्, see परिक्षित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षिन्
परीक्षिन् परीक्षिन्, i. e. परि-ईक्ष् + इन्, m. An examiner, Yājñ. 2, 241.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणाह|परीणाहः
परीणाह परीणाह, परीताप परी-ताप, परीतोष परीतोष, परीदाह परीदाह, परीधान परीधान, परीपाक परीपाक, see परिण˚ परिणाह, etc., with इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीप्सा
परीप्सा परीप्सा, i. e. परि-ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + अ, f. Wish to obtain, to maintain, to preserve, Bhāg. P. 9, 4, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीप्सु
परीप्सु परीप्सु, i. e. परि-ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + उ, adj. Wishing to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b " target="_blank">Page0530-b + 41</a>] maintain, to preserve, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीमाण|परीमाणं
परीमाण परीमाण, परीवर्त परी-वर्त, परीवाद परीवाद, परीवाह परीवाह, परीहार परीहार, परीहास परीहास, see परिमा˚ परिमा˚, etc., with इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुत्
परुत् परुत्, i. e. पर-वत् (a word occurring only in compounds, cf. संवत्), adv., Last year.<BR> --Cf. πέρυσι, πέρυτις, ἔτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुष|परुषं
परुष परुष, i. e. परुस् + अ, adj., f. षा.<BR> 1. Knotty, huge, Vikr. d. 142.<BR> 2. Variegated, spotted.<BR> 3. Soiled, Rām. 2, 71, 34.<BR> 4. Rough, rugged, Rājat. 4, 308.<BR> 5. Harsh, MBh. 1, 7090.<BR> 6. Severe, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1314.<BR> 7. Coarse, Yājñ. 1, 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषित
परुषित परुषित, i. e. परुष + इत, adj., Used roughly, Hit. i. d. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुस्
परुस् परुस्, i. e. पॄ + वन्त् (cf. पर्वन् and पर्वत), n. The knot or joint of a plant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपरुस्
त्रि- + परुस् त्रि- + परुस्, m. a surname of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्ष|परोक्षं|परोक्षः
परोक्ष परोक्ष, i. e. परस्-अक्ष,<BR> I. adj., f. षा.<BR> 1. Being beyond sight, invisible, imperceptible, Bhāg. P. 2, 1, 12.<BR> 2. Unknown, strange, Śāk. 108, 17.<BR> II. क्षम्, acc. and loc. क्षे,<BR> 1. In one's absence, Man. 2, 199.<BR> 2. Imperceptibly, Pañc. 46, 7.<BR> 3. Surreptitiously, 112, 22.<BR> III. m. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्ष
अ- + परोक्ष अ- + परोक्ष,<BR> I. adj. not imperceptible, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 24 (although not [quite] imperceptible, [nevertheless] perceivable only by one's self).<BR> II. क्षम्, adv. in one's view. Hence the denominative अपरोक्षय, to make visible, MBh. 1, 781.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षता
परोक्षता परोक्ष + ता, f. Obscurity, MBh. 3, 2820.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षत्व
परोक्षत्व परोक्ष + त्व, n. Want of perceptibility, Vedāntas. in Chr. 213, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकारित्व
परोपकारित्व परोपकारित्व, i. e. पर-उपकारिन् + त्व, n. Supporting others, Bhartṛ. Suppl. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्कटिन्|पर्क्कटिन्
पर्कटिन् पर्कटिन्, m., and पर्कटी पर्कटी, f. The waved-leaf fig tree, Ficus infectoria, Hit. 38, 10, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्जन्य|पर्जन्यः|पर्ज्जन्य|पर्ज्जन्यः
पर्जन्य पर्जन्य (and incorrectly पर्यन्य पर्यन्य), probably स्फुर्ज्, for old स्पर्ज्, + अन + य, m.<BR> 1. A rainthreatening cloud, Ragh. 17, 15.<BR> 2. Rain, Bhag. 3, 14.<BR> 3. The deity of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण्
† पर्ण् पर्ण्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from पर्ण), Par. To be green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण पर्ण, perhaps पॄ + न,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A wing.<BR> 2. A feather, MBh. 1, 1517.<BR> 3. A leaf, Nal. 16, 12.<BR> II. m. A tree, Butea frondosa Roxb.<BR> III. f. णी, An aquatic plant, Pistia stratiotes Lin.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. farn; A.S. fearn; perhaps Πάρνης, Παρνασός, Παρνασσός; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-b " target="_blank">Page0531-b + 39</a>] perhaps Lat. penna (but cf. पत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वपर्ण|अश्वपर्ण्ण
अश्व- + पर्ण अश्व- + पर्ण, adj. having horses serving for wings, Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 88, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपर्ण|ऋतुपर्णः
ऋतु- + पर्ण ऋतु- + पर्ण, m. a proper name, Nal. 8, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपर्णी
ताम्र-पर्णी ताम्र-पर्णी, f. 1. the name of a river. 2. the name of a town in Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपर्ण|श्रीपर्णं
श्री- + पर्ण श्री- + पर्ण,<BR> I. n. 1. a lotus. 2. a tree, Premna spinosa.<BR> II. f. णी, the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपर्णी
सप्तपर्णी सप्तप्˚, i. e. सप्तन्-,<BR> I. adj. seven-leaved.<BR> II. m. a tree, Alstonia scholaris, Lass. Anth. 25, 14.<BR> III. n. a sort of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्ण|सुपर्णः
सु- + पर्ण सु- + पर्ण,<BR> I. m. 1. Garuḍa. 2. a cock.<BR> II. f. णा and णी, 1. a number of lotusses. 2. the mother of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्ण|त्रिसुपर्णः
त्रि-सु- + पर्ण त्रि-सु- + पर्ण, adj. conversant with hymns called trisuparṇa, Man. 3, 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपपर्णी
सूप- + पर्णी सूप- + पर्ण, f. णी, a sort of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णवन्त्|पर्णवत्
पर्णवन्त् पर्ण + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in leaves, Kathās. 30, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णिन्
पर्णिन् पर्णिन्, i. e. पर्ण + इन्,<BR> I. m. A tree, MBh. 12, 5858.<BR> II. f. इनी.<BR> 1. A certain plant.<BR> 2. The name of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णोटज|पर्णोटजं
पर्णोटज पर्णोटज, i. e. पर्ण-उटज, n. A hut of leaves, Utt. Rāmac. 46, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्
† पर्द् पर्द्, i. 1, Ātm. To fart.<BR> --Cf. πέρδω, ἔπαρδον, πορδή; O.H.G. ferzan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ब्
