पर्वत पर्वत, i. e. पर्वन्त् (the original form of पर्वन्) + अ, m.<BR> 1. A mountain, Megh. 23.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपर्वत|अग्निपर्वतः|अग्निपर्व्वत
अग्नि- + पर्वत अग्नि- + पर्वत, m. a volcano. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a " target="_blank">Page0533-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपर्वत
अमर- + पर्वत अमर- + पर्वत, and इन्द्र-, m. names of mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपर्वत
उत्तर- + पर्वत उत्तर- + पर्वत, m. the northern ridge of mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुपर्वत|जम्बुपर्वतः
जम्बु- + पर्वत जम्बु- + पर्वत, m. = जम्बु<BR> 2. वर्ष-, m. A mountainous range supposed to separate the Varṣas, or divisions of the globe, from each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वतीय|पर्व्वतीय|पर्व्वतीयः
पर्वतीय पर्वतीय, i. e. पर्वत + ईय, adj. Referring to a mountain, growing on, ruling over, a mountain, Hariv. 2668.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्वतीय
अ- + पर्वतीय अ- + पर्वतीय, adj. situated in a plain, Rām. 4, 44, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वन्|पर्व्वन्
पर्वन् पर्वन्, i. e. पॄ + वन्त् (cf. परुस् and पर्वत), n.<BR> 1. A knot, a joint in a cane or plant in general, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 413.<BR> 2. A joint of the body, Śāk. d. 80.<BR> 3. A limb, Vikr. d. 112.<BR> 4. A section, a division, especially of a book, MBh. i. ii. etc.<BR> 5. The days of the four periodic changes of the moon, particularly the days of conjunction and opposition, Man. 3, 45.<BR> 6. The sacrifice performed at these days.<BR> 7. A festival.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्वन्
अ- + पर्वन् अ- + पर्वन्, n. a day which is not पर्वन् (see<BR> 5 and<BR> 7) सु-, m. 1. a bamboo. 2. an arrow. 3. =<BR> 5 and<BR> 7. 4. a deity. 5. smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्विणी
पर्विणी पर्विणी, i. e. पर्वन् + इन् + ई, f. A festival, Rājat. 4, 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ष्
† पर्ष् पर्ष्, or वर्ष् वर्ष्, स्पर्ष् स्पर्ष्, i. 1, Ātm. To grow wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्
पर्षद् पर्षद् = परिषद् (q. cf.), f. An assembly, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्
† पल् पल्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR> --i. 10, पालय, see 2. पा.<BR> --Cf. πάλλω; Lat. pello (both Caus.); O.H.G. fallan; A.S. feallan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल पल, n.<BR> 1. A weight = 4 karṣas, Man. 8, 135.<BR> 2. Flesh, Yājñ. 3, 215.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपल
दश(न्)- + पल दश(न्)- + पल, n. ten palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलल|पललं|पललः
पलल पलल, n. (and m.).<BR> 1. Pounded [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b " target="_blank">Page0533-b + 40</a>] sesamum, Hariv. 7362.<BR> 2. Mire, mud, Rām. 5, 87, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाण्डु|पलांडु|पलाण्डुः
पलाण्डु पलाण्डु, m. and n. An onion, Man. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाय्
पलाय् पलाय्, see vb. इ, with the prep. पला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायन|पलायनं
पलायन पलायन, i. e. पला (for परा) -इ + अन, n. Flight, running away, Pañc. 63, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायिन्
पलायिन् पलायिन्, i. e. पला (for परा) -इ + इन्, adj. Running away, showing the heels, MBh. 12, 3719.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाल|पलालं|पलालः
पलाल पलाल,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. Straw, Man. 5, 122.<BR> 2. The stalk of Sorghum.<BR> II. f. ला, A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाश|पलाशं|पलाशः
पलाश पलाश,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A leaf.<BR> 2. Foliage, MBh. 3, 1400.<BR> II. m. A tree bearing red blossoms, Butea frondosa.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपलाश
स- + पलाश स- + पलाश, adj., f. शा, together with a Butea frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशिन्
पलाशिन् पलाशिन्, i. e. पलाश + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Leafy, MBh. 1, 1775.<BR> II. m. The name of a town.<BR> III. f. नी, The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिक
ऽपलिक -पलिक, i. e. -पल + इक, latter part of comp. adj. preceded by numerals, Weighing (so many) palas, Yājñ. 2, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलित|पलितं|पलितः
पलित पलित,<BR> I. adj., f. इक्नी (and ता), Grey, MBh. 7, 5089.<BR> II. n. Grey hair, Man. 6, 2.<BR> --Cf. πελιδνός, πελιός, πελός, πελλός, πολιός; Lat. pullus, pallidus. pallere; O.H.G. falw; A.S. fealo, falu, fealwe, falewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलितिन्
पलितिन् पलितिन्, i. e. पलित + इन् adj. Grey-haired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्पूल्
पल्पूल् पल्पूल् (perhaps an old anomal. frequent. of पल्; cf. चर्, चञ्चूर्य, फल् पम्फुल्, तॄ, ved. तर्तुर्, etc.), i. 10, Par., ved.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a " target="_blank">Page0534-a + 38</a>] tan.<BR> 2. To cleanse.<BR>† पल्यूल् पल्यूल्, and † पल्युल् पल्युल्, † वल्यूल् वल्यूल्, † वल्युल् वल्युल्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To purify.<BR> 2. To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल्
† पल्ल् पल्ल्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लल
पल्लल पल्लल, see पल्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लव|पल्लवं|पल्लवः
पल्लव पल्लव, probably for original पर्ण + वन्त्,<BR> 1. m. and n. A sprout, a shoot, Śāk. d. 34.<BR> 2. m. pl. The name of a people.<BR> 3. The red dye of lac; cf. पल्लवित.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुकपल्लव
अंशुक- + पल्लव अंशुक- + पल्लव, m. and. n. a scarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपल्लव|करपल्लवः
कर- + पल्लव कर- + पल्लव and पाणि-, m. and n. the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपल्लव
स- + पल्लव स- + पल्लव, adj. together with shoots, Ṛt. 6, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवय
पल्लवय पल्लवय, a denomin. derived from पल्लव with अय, Par.<BR> 1. To get new shoots, Häberl. Anth. 233, 6.<BR> 2. To extend, Gīt. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवित|पल्लवितं|पल्लवितः
पल्लवित पल्लवित, i. e. पल्लव + इत, and पल्लविन् पल्लविन्, i. e. पल्लव + इन् adj.<BR> 1. Having young shoots, Kumāras. 3, 54.<BR> 2. Possessing the red dye of lac, Vikr. d. 141 (प्रभा-, having its own radiance instead of the red dye).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वल|पल्वलं
पल्वल पल्वल, sometimes incorrectly पल्लल पल्लल, akin to पलित (cf. O.H.G. falw), n. (and m.), A small pond, Pañc. 142, 13.<BR> --Cf. Lat. palus; πηλός, perhaps A.S. pol, pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव्
† पव् पव्, i. 1, Ātm. To go (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव|पवं|पवः
पव पव, i. e. पू + अ, n. Cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवन|पवनं|पवनः
पवन पवन, i. e. पू + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Wind, air, Śāk. d. 55.<BR> 2. A potter's kiln, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 117.<BR> 3. A proper name.<BR> II. m. (or n.) The sacred fire. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b " target="_blank">Page0534-b + 41</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपवन|दंतपवन
दन्त- + पवन दन्त- + पवन, n. A small piece of wood for cleaning the teeth with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमान|पवमानः
पवमान पवमान (properly ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. of पू, i. 1), m.<BR> 1. Wind, Ragh. 8, 9.<BR> 2. Agni, the deified fire.<BR> 3. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवि|पविः
पवि पवि, m.<BR> 1. The iron band of a wheel (ved.).<BR> 2. The thunderbolt of Indra, Śatr. 14, 219. Perhaps akin to Lat. pavire, puvire; παίω, πταίω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्र|पवित्रं|पवित्रः
पवित्र पवित्र, i. e. पू + त्र,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A means of purifying, Man. 11, 85.<BR> 2. Sacrificial grass, Man. 2, 75.<BR> 3. Prayer, Man. 11, 225.<BR> II. m. pl. The name of a class of deities.<BR> III. f. त्रा, The name of a river.<BR> IV. adj., f. त्रा.<BR> 1. Purifying, Rām. 1, 1, 94.<BR> 2. Pure, Man. 3, 235.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवित्र|अपवित्रं
अ- + पवित्र अ- + पवित्र, adj. Impure, Pañc. 169, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रक|पवित्रकं|पवित्रकः
पवित्रक पवित्र + क,<BR> I. n. The vessel in which an Argha or oblation is presented(?), Yājñ. 1, 250.<BR> II. As latter part of comp. adj., a substitute for पवित्र.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपवित्रक
स- + पवित्रक स- + पवित्रक, adj. Containing sacrificial grass, Yājñ. 1, 230.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रता
पवित्रता पवित्र + ता, f., and पवित्रत्व पवित्र + त्व, n. Purity, Utt. Rāmac. 168, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रय
पवित्रय पवित्रय, a denomin. derived from पवित्र with अय, Par. To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रिन्
पवित्रिन् पवित्रिन्, i. e. पवित्र + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Purifying, MBh. 1, 1543.<BR> 2. Pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्
पश् पश्, i. 10 पाशय, Par. To bind. पाशित, Bound, Hariv. 3536.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, ptcple. of the pf. pass. अवपाशित, Bound, Rām. 3, 59, 18; cf. दृश्, and स्पश्.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. fahan; A.S. fón with feng; O.H.G. fahan with fang, fôgjan; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a " target="_blank">Page0535-a + 42</a>] A.S. fegan; Goth. fahjan; O.H.G. gafagjan; A.S. ge-fegan; Lat. pac in paciscor, dispesco for dis-pec + sco, compesco.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशव्य|पशव्यं
पशव्य पशव्य, i. e. पश्व् + य, adj.<BR> 1. Fit for cattle.<BR> 2. Brutish, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 42, with काम, sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशु|पशुः
पशु पश् + उ, m.<BR> 1. Cattle (viz. neatcattle, horses, goats, sheep, asses, and dogs), Man. 10, 48.<BR> 2. A beast, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 304.<BR> 3. An animal to be immolated, Rām. 1, 61, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. faihu; A.S. feoh; Lat. pecus, pecoris and pecudis; probably also πῶϋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपशु|घृतपशुः
घृत- + पशु घृत- + पशु, m. the image of a beast formed with clarified butter, Man. 5, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपशु|देवपशुः
देव- + पशु देव- + पशु, m. cattle consecrated to a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरपशु|नरपशुः
नर- + पशु नर- + पशु, and पुरुष-, m. a beast-like man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपशु|नृपशुः
नृ- + पशु नृ- + पशु, m. a man destinated to be immolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपशु|पिष्टपशुः
पिष्ट- + पशु पिष्ट- + पशु (vb. पिष्), m. the image of a beast formed with dough, Man. 5, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुता
पशुता पशु + ता, f.<BR> 1. The condition of cattle, Man. 3, 104.<BR> 2. The condition of an animal destined to be immolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुत्व
पशुत्व पशु + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Bestiality, Prab. 59, 11.<BR> 2. The condition of an animal destined to be immolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुमन्त्|पशुमत्
पशुमन्त् पशु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Abounding in cattle, MBh. 2, 798.<BR> 2. Possessing many flocks, 4, 1162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुमारक
पशुमारक पशु-मार + क, adj. Accompanied by immolation of animals, Bhāg. P. 4, 27, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुसमाम्नायिक
पशुसमाम्नायिक पशुसमाम्नायिक, i. e. पशु-समाम्नाय + इक, adj. Read of in the books on animal sacrifices, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्
पश्चात् पश्चात्, abl. sing. of the ved. adj. पश्च, i. e. अपस् (= अप)-अञ्च् + अ (cf. तिरश्चीन),<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b " target="_blank">Page0535-b + 42</a>] Behind, Man. 2, 196.<BR> 2. From behind, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1235.<BR> 3. After, afterwards, Man. 8, 164.<BR> 4. Backwards, Yājñ. 2, 299.<BR> 5. Westward, Megh. 16.<BR> II. prep. with gen. and abl. After, Man. 3, 116.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. postid-ea, post; akin is also pone for pos-ne, perhaps ὀπίσσω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्तापिन्
पश्चात्तापिन् पश्चात्तापिन्, i. e. पश्चात्-ताप + इन्, adj. Repenting, Yājñ. 3, 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चार्ध|पश्चार्द्धः|पश्चार्धः
पश्चार्ध पश्चार्ध, i. e. पश्च (cf. पश्चात्) -अर्ध, m. Hind-part, Śāk. d. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिम|पश्चिमं
पश्चिम पश्चिम, i. e. पश्च (cf. पश्चात्) + इम, adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Hinder, last; with संध्या, The evening twilight, Man. 2, 101; with क्रिया, Obsequies.<BR> 2. Western, west, Man. 2, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्चिम
अ- + पश्चिम अ- + पश्चिम, adj. 1. last. 2. extreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपश्चिम
दक्षिण- + पश्चिम दक्षिण- + पश्चिम, adj. south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिमतस्
पश्चिमतस् पश्चिम + तस्, adv. From behind, MBh. 4, 2108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष्
† पष् पष्, i. 1, Par. Ātm., v. r. of स्पश्, q. cf. i. 10, पषय, Par.<BR> 1. To bind.<BR> 2. To hinder.<BR> 3. To touch.<BR> 4. To go (v. r. पश्).<BR> --i. 10, पाषय, Par. To bind (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्
† पस् पस्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. v. r. of स्पश्, q. cf. i. 10, Par. पासय, To bind (v. r.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लव
पह्लव पह्लव, n. The name of a people, the Persians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
1. पा पा, i. 1, base of the pres. पिब, पिव, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm.),<BR> 1. To drink, Man. 4, 63.<BR> 2. with रजस्, To quaff dust, Man. 11, 110.<BR> 3. To enjoy, e. g. with चक्षुषा, Megh. 16.<BR> 4. (figuratively) To swallow up, Pañc. iii. d. 233.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass., पीत,<BR> 1. Drunk.<BR> 2. Enjoyed.<BR> 3. Swallowed up, squandered away, Rājat. 5, 421. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0536-a " target="_blank">Page0536-a + 41</a>]<BR> 4. Having drunk, Kathās. 39, 57.<BR> 5. Filled.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass., पेय, Drinkable.<BR> I. n. Drink, beverage, Pañc. 47, 8 (at the end of a comp. adj., नाना-प्रकार-वस्त्र-पुष्प-भक्ष्य-पेय, Accompanied by garments, flowers, food, and drink of different kinds).<BR> II. f. या, Rice gruel. पानीय, Drinkable. n.<BR> 1. Beverage.<BR> 2. Water, Man. 8, 326.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. पायय, To cause to drink, MBh. 1, 192. Desider. पिपास, To desire to drink, MBh. 7, 705.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass., पिपासित, Thirsty, 3, 17247. Frequentat. पेपीय,<BR> 1. To drink repeatedly or greedily.<BR> 2. To be drunk greedily (pass., probably to be corrected to पेपीय्य). Bhāg. P. 5, 8, 1; Hariv. 8798.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, Caus. To cause to drink plenty of (acc.).<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To drink after or afterwards, Ragh. 8, 67.<BR> 2. To drink of, Rām. 2, 104, 5 Gorr.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To drink of.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To drink up, Rām. 3, 55, 9.<BR> 2. To drink.<BR> 3. To imbibe (figuratively) with one's ears, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 49.<BR> --Caus. To cause to imbibe, Bhāg. P. 1, 18, 12.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To imbibe, Kām. Nītis. 12, 48.<BR> 2. To press, to impoverish, MBh. 12, 3307.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To sip in, Rām. 2, 95, 18.<BR> 2. To drink.<BR> 3. To absorb, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 6.<BR> --Caus. To cause to sip in, Bhāg. P. 8, 2, 25.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निष्पीत, Dried up, Rām. 2, 62, 17 Gorr.<BR> --With परि परि, To drink up, Ṛt. 3, 6. परिपीत, Imbibed.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To begin to drink.<BR> 2. To drink.<BR> 3. To enjoy, Rām. 2, 45, 5.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To cause to drink, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 26. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0536-b " target="_blank">Page0536-b + 41</a>]<BR> --Cf. Lat. bibo, potare, poculum, etc.; πέπωκα, πῶθι, ποτός, ποταμόσ, πίνω (cf. पिन्व्), πιπίσκω, πιστός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेय|अपेयं
अ- + पेय अ- + पेय, adj. not drinkable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
2. पा पा, ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To guard, MBh. 14, 514.<BR> 2. To preserve, Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 15.<BR> 3. To beware of (with abl.), MBh. 1, 3417.<BR> 4. To govern.<BR> --Caus. and पल्, पाल्, i. 10, पालय (properly, a denomin. derived from पाल),<BR> 1. To protect, Rām. 1, 45, 29.<BR> 2. To guard as guardian, Rājat. 5, 227.<BR> 3. To cherish, Māl. 48, 19.<BR> 4. To govern, Pañc. i. d. 253.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. निधि-पालित, m. A proper name. वसु-, m. A proper name.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be guarded, Man. 8, 27.<BR> 2. To observe, MBh. 2, 2509; to maintain, Hariv. 3762.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, Caus.<BR> 1. To observe, MBh. 12, 476.<BR> 2. To keep, Rām. 2, 26, 27.<BR> --With अभि अभि, Caus. To assist, MBh. 3, 8472.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, Caus. To govern, Hariv. 5233.<BR> --With नि नि, To protect, Rām. 5, 81, 22.<BR> --Caus. To govern, Rām. 1, 6, 29 Gorr.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To protect, MBh. 1, 8413.<BR> 2. To maintain, Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 36.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To protect, to guard, to govern.<BR> 2. To maintain, to keep, Chr. 3, 5.<BR> 3. To expect, to wait, Rām. 2, 70, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To beware of (with abl.), Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 17.<BR> --Caus. To protect.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus.<BR> 1. To protect, MBh. 1, 4080.<BR> 2. To maintain, to observe, 1, 3521.<BR> 3. To expect, to wait, Śāk. 9, 4.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, Caus. To wait.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. Caus. To protect, MBh. 12, 2667.<BR> 2. To maintain, to keep, MBh. 3, 15249.<BR> 3. To overcome, MBh. 4, 2321. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a " target="_blank">Page0537-a + 43</a>] 2. पा is akin to 1. पा; the link between the signification To drink and To protect is formed by the signification To nourish.<BR> --Cf. πάομαι, πῶμα, akin is also πατέομαι; Goth. fôdjan; A.S. foda; Lat. pasco, pabulum; βόσκω, ποιμήν.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु पांशु and पांशुल पांशुल, see पांसु, पांसुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांसन पांसन, latter part of comp. adj., f. नी (and ना), Disgracing, Hiḍ. 1, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसव
पांसव पांसव, i. e. पांसु + अ, adj. Consisting of dust, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसु|पांसुः
पांसु पांसु, and पांशु पांशु, m.<BR> 1. Dust, Man. 4, 102.<BR> 2. A particle of dust, Man. 4, 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुक
पांसुक पांसु + क, m., pl. Dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुल|पांसुलः
पांसुल पांसु + ल, and पांशुल पांशुल, adj.<BR> 1. Dusty, covered with dust, Rām. 2, 43, 30 Gorr.<BR> 2. Disgraced, Śāk. d. 125.<BR> 3. Disgracing(?), Rām. 5, 88, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपांसुल|वनपांसुलः
वन- + पांसुल वन- + पांसुल, m. a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक पाक, i. e. पच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Cooking, baking, MBh. 3, 15551.<BR> 2. Food, Man. 3, 104.<BR> 3. Burning (as pots, bricks), 5, 122.<BR> 4. Digestion.<BR> 5. Ripening, maturing, Vikr. d. 90.<BR> 6. The appearance of the consequences, e. g. of an action, Pañc. 129, 13.<BR> 7. Fulfilling, accomplishment.<BR> 8. Inflammation.<BR> 9. The name of a demon.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मपाक|कर्मपाकः
कर्म(न्)- + पाक कर्म(न्)- + पाक, m. the requital for actions done in a former existence, Pañc. i. d. 417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंपाक|किम्पाक|किम्पाकः
किंपाक किंपाक, i. e. किम्-, m. a kind of cucumber; n. its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीपाक|कुंभीपाक|कुम्भीपाकः
कुम्भी- + पाक कुम्भी- + पाक, m. sing. and pl. the name of a hell in which the wicked are baked like potters' vessels, Man. 12, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपाक
पुनःपाक पुनःपाक, i. e. पुनर्-, m. repeated burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःपाक
पुरस्- + पाक पुरस्- + पाक, adj. of which the fulfilment is imminent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यपाक|हव्यपाकः
हव्य- + पाक हव्य- + पाक (vb. हु), m. 1. an oblation [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b " target="_blank">Page0537-b + 39</a>] dressed for the gods. 2. the vessel it is prepared in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकज|पाकजं
पाकज पाक-ज, adj. Produced by maturing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकज
अ- + पाकज अ- + पाकज, adj. not produced by maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकजत्व
पाकजत्व पाकज + त्व. n. Capability of being affected by contact with fire, Bhāṣāp. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासन|पाकशासनः
पाकशासन पाक-शासन, m. A name of Indra, Vikr. 89, 1 (chastiser of पाक, see पाक<BR> 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासनि|पाकशासनिः
पाकशासनि पाकशासनि, i. e. पाक-शासन + इ, patronym., m. A son of Indra, a surname of Arjuna, Johns. Sel. 17, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिन्
पाकिन् पाकिन्, i. e. पच् + इन्, latter part of comp. adj., f. नि, Maturing, being digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम पाकिम, i. e. पाक + इम, adj. Prepared by cooking, baking, or evaporation (as salt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य पाक्य, i. e. पाक + य, adj., n. A kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक पाक्षिक, i. e. पक्ष + इक, adj., f. की, Belonging to a fortnight, MBh. 14, 2513.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्तेय|पांक्तेय
पाङ्क्तेय पाङ्क्तेय, and पाङ्क्त्य पाङ्क्त्य, i. e. पङ्क्ति + एय or य, adj. Worthy to belong to a respectable society, Man. 3, 176.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्तेय|अपांक्तेय
अ- + पाङ्क्तेय अ- + पाङ्क्तेय, adj. inadmissible into society, Man. 3, 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक पाचक, i. e. पच् + अक,<BR> I. adj., f. चिका.<BR> 1. Cooking, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1787.<BR> 2. Effecting digestion.<BR> II. m., f. चिका, A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन पाचन, i. e. पच् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Digestive.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A warm cataplasm.<BR> 2. A digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन
पाञ्चजन पाञ्चजन, i. e. पञ्चन्-जन + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a " target="_blank">Page0538-a + 40</a>] patronym., m. and f. नी, A son or daughter of Pañcajana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पांचजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्यः
पाञ्चजन्य पाञ्चजन्य, i. e. पञ्चन्-जन + य, m.<BR> 1. Kṛṣṇa's conch, Bhag. 1, 15.<BR> 2. The name of a part of Jambu-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश्य|पांचदश्यं
पाञ्चदश्य पाञ्चदश्य, i. e. पञ्च-दशी + य (cf. दश), adj. Used at the fifteenth day of a half month, Bhāg. P. 6, 4, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनख
पाञ्चनख पाञ्चनख, i. e. पञ्चन्-नख + अ, adj. Made of the skin of an animal with five claws, MBh. 4, 1338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनद|पांचनद|पाञ्चनदः
पाञ्चनद पाञ्चनद, i. e. पञ्चन्-नद + अ,<BR> I. adj. Observed in Pañcanada, i. e. the Panjab.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A prince of Pañcanada.<BR> 2. pl. The inhabitants of Pañcanada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चभौतिक|पांचभौतिक
पाञ्चभौतिक पाञ्चभौतिक, i. e. पञ्चन्-भूत + इक, adj. Consisting of the five elements, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयज्ञिक|पांचयज्ञिक
पाञ्चयज्ञिक पाञ्चयज्ञिक, i. e. पञ्चन्-यज्ञ + इक, adj. Belonging to the five sacrifices, Man. 3, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पाञ्चाल पाञ्चाल, i. e. पञ्चाल + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. लि, Belonging to, referring to, ruling over, etc., the Pañcālas.<BR> II. m. pl. The Pañcālas.<BR> III. f. ली, A surname of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालक|पांचालक|पाञ्चालकः
पाञ्चालक पाञ्चाल + क, adj., f. लिका, Belonging to the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालेय|पाञ्चालेयः
पाञ्चालेय पाञ्चालेय, i. e. पञ्चाल + एय, m. A prince of the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल्य|पाञ्चाल्यः
पाञ्चाल्य पाञ्चाल्य, i. e. पञ्चाल + य,<BR> I. adj. Belonging to the Pañcālas.<BR> II. m. A prince of the Pañcālas, Johns. Sel. 5, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटक|पाटकः
पाटक पाटक, i. e. पट् + अक, m. One who divides, Hariv. 9767.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटच्चर|पाटच्चरः
पाटच्चर पाटच्चर, i. e. पटच्चर + अ, m. A thief, a robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटन|पाटनं
पाटन पाटन, i. e. पट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Ripping up, slitting up, Mārk. P. 14, 88.<BR> 2. Opening, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल पाटल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Of a pale red colour, Ragh. 7, 24.<BR> 2. Pallid, Śāk. d. 182.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Pale red, rose colour, Ragh. 4, 68.<BR> 2. A kind of rice ripening in the rains.<BR> 3. A proper name.<BR> 4. The tree of trumpet flower, Bignonia suaveolens.<BR> III. f. ला, The tree and its flower.<BR> IV. n. Its flower, Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटापाटल
सटा-पाटल सटा-पाटल, m. the red mane of a lion, Rājat. 5, 332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलि|पाटलिः
पाटलि पाटलि,<BR> I. m. and f., and पाटली पाटली, f.<BR> 1. Trumpet flower, Bignonia suaveolens.<BR> II. पाटली, f.<BR> 1. The name of a tree.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिमन्
पाटलिमन् पाटलिमन्, i. e. पाटल + इमन्, m. Pale red, rose colour, Prab. 85, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटव|पाटवं
पाटव पाटव, i. e. पटु + अ, n.<BR> 1. Sharpness, energy.<BR> 2. Cleverness, dexterity, Hit. pr. d. 2.<BR> 3. Quickness, precipitation, Kathās. 5, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ|पाठः
पाठ पाठ, i. e. पठ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Reading, recital, Kathās. 2, 36.<BR> 2. A text.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिपाठ|वन्दिपाठः
वन्दिपाठ वन्दिपाठ, i. e. वन्दिन्-, m. a panegyric, an eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक|पाठकः
पाठक पाठक, i. e. पठ् + अक, m.<BR> 1. A student, one who is conversant with a science, Pañc. 165, 2.<BR> 2. A preceptor.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपाठक|धर्मपाठकः|धर्म्मपाठक
