पाण्डवीय|पांडवीय
पाण्डवीय पाण्डवीय, i. e. पाण्डव + ईय, adj. Relating to the five Pāṇḍavas, MBh. 5, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पांडवेयः|पाण्डवेयः
पाण्डवेय पाण्डवेय, i. e. पाण्डु + एय,<BR> I. patronym. A descendant of Pāṇḍu.<BR> II. m. A partisan of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR> III. adj. Belonging to, connected with, the five Pāṇḍavas(?), MBh. 8, 1634.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डित्य|पांडित्य|पांडित्यं|पाण्डित्यं
पाण्डित्य पाण्डित्य, i. e. पण्डित + य, n.<BR> 1. Scholarship, learning, MBh. 5, 917.<BR> 2. Wisdom, prudence, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1735.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डु|पांडु|पाण्डुः
पाण्डु पाण्डु,<BR> I. adj. Pale, white, yellowish white, Śāk. d. 80.<BR> II. m. The name of a sovereign, father of Yudhiṣṭhira, and the other four Pāṇḍavas.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपाण्डु
पुष्प- + पाण्डु पुष्प- + पाण्डु, m. a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डु|विपांडु
वि- + पाण्डु वि- + पाण्डु, adj. pale, Śiś. 9, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुक|पांडुकः|पाण्डुकः
पाण्डुक पाण्डु + क, m. The jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकिन्|पांडुकिन्
पाण्डुकिन् पाण्डुकिन्, i. e. पाण्डुक + इन्, adj. Jaundiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुता
पाण्डुता पाण्डु + ता, f., and पाण्डुत्व पाण्डु + त्व, n. Paleness, Megh. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुर|पांडुर
पाण्डुर पाण्डु + र,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Of a yellowish white colour, white, pale, Bhāg. P. 8, 8, 8.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाण्डुर
आ- + पाण्डुर आ- + पाण्डुर, adj. a little pale, Amar. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डुर
वि- + पाण्डुर वि- + पाण्डुर, adj. pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरता
पाण्डुरता पाण्डुर + ता, f. White colour, Pañc. 253, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्य|पांड्य|पाण्ड्यः
पाण्ड्य पाण्ड्य, m.<BR> 1. pl. The name [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a " target="_blank">Page0540-a + 44</a>] of a people and its country.<BR> 2. A prince of the Pāṇḍyas.<BR> 3. The name of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
पात पात, i. e. पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Flying, MBh. 8, 1898.<BR> 2. Manner of flying, 3, 10646.<BR> 3. Throwing one's self, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> 4. Falling.<BR> 5. A cast.<BR> 6. A stroke. खड्ग-, A stroke with the sword, Kathās. 27, 50.<BR> 7. Case, Lass. 43, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पात|असृक्पातः
असृक्पात असृक्पात, i. e. असृज्-, m. drops of blood, Man. 8, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलपात
कूल- + पात कूल- + पात, m. falling from the bank (of a river), Rām. 2, 103, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपात|गर्भपातः
गर्भ- + पात गर्भ- + पात, m. miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपात|चरणपातः
चरण- + पात चरण- + पात, m. 1. laying one's self at another's feet, Pañc. 113, 2. 2. a kick, Hariv. 13607.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपात|दूरपातः
दूर- + पात दूर- + पात,<BR> I. m. flying far.<BR> II. adj. shooting from afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्पात|दृक्पातः
दृक्पात दृक्पात, i. e. दृश्-, and दृष्टि-, m. a glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारापात|धारापातः
धारा- + पात धारा- + पात, m. a shower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपात|पक्षपातः
पक्ष- + पात पक्ष- + पात, m. 1. siding with somebody, MBh. 1, 5347. 2. partiality, Bhartṛ. 1, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षपात
वि-पक्ष- + पात वि-पक्ष- + पात, m. indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापात|महापातः
महा- + पात महा- + पात, adj. falling with great force (as an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मपात|वर्त्मपातः
वर्त्म(न्)- + पात वर्त्म(न्)- + पात, m. aberration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणपात
वाण- + पात वाण- + पात, m. an arrow-shot, as a measure of distance, Chr. 27, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनपात|विलोचनपातः
विलोचन- + पात विलोचन- + पात, m. a glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातक|पातकं|पातकः
पातक पातक, i. e. पत्, Caus., + अक, m. and n. Sin, crime, Man. 8, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन् पातकिन्, i. e. पातक + इन्, adj., f. नी, Wicked, a criminal, Mṛcch. 154, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापातकिन्
महा- + पातकिन् महा- + पातकिन्, adj. offending, or an offender, in the highest degree, Man. 9, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्ग|पातंग
पातङ्ग पातङ्ग, i. e. पतंग + अ, adj., f. गी, Peculiar to a grasshopper Rājat. 8, 469.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन पातन, i. e. पत्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj. नी, Cutting down, MBh. 1, 6560.<BR> II. n. Causing to fall, Man. 5, 130; with दण्डस्य, Chastising, Man. 7, 51; with गर्भस्य, Causing a miscarriage.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपातन|दंडपातन
दण्ड- + पातन दण्ड- + पातन, n. chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपातन
दूर- + पातन दूर- + पातन, n. throwing missiles from afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाताल|पातालं|पातालः
पाताल पाताल, i. e. perhaps पात-आलय, n.<BR> 1. One of the seven hells, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 3.<BR> 2. The regions under the earth, and the abode of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिन्
पातिन् पातिन्, i. e. पत् + इन्, and पात + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Flying, MBh. 8, 1911.<BR> 2. Falling, Kathās. 19, 29.<BR> 3. Causing to fall.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपातिन्
एक- + पातिन् एक- + पातिन्, adj. fallen on a sudden, MBh. 1, 3032.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपातिन्
दण्ड- + पातिन् दण्ड- + पातिन्, adj. inflicting punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपातिन्
दूर- + पातिन् दूर- + पातिन्, adj. 1. flying far. 2. making wide ways. 3. Throwing missiles over a great distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेषुपातिन्
दूर-इषु- + पातिन् दूर-इषु- + पातिन्, adj. shooting arrows over large distances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिन्
पक्ष- + पातिन् पक्ष- + पातिन्, adj. siding with, partial, Mālav. 13, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठपातिन्
पृष्ठ- + पातिन् पृष्ठ- + पातिन्, adj. following, Rājat. 6, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक पातुक, i. e. पत् + उक, adj. Disposed to fall, MBh. 12, 3444.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
पातृ पा + तृ, m.<BR> 1. One who drinks, MBh. 10, 287.<BR> 2. A protector, Hariv. 14617.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pôtor; ποτήρ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
पात्य पात्य, i. e. पति + य, n. Dominion, MBh. 12, 9517.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
पात्र पा + त्र,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A vessel in general, a plate, a cup, etc., Man. 5, 116.<BR> 2. A receptacle, Kām. Nītis. 5, 90.<BR> 3. The bed of a river, Rām. 2, 73, 2 Gorr.<BR> 4. A person worthy of receiving gifts, Bhartṛ. 2, 80.<BR> 5. A king's counsellor or minister, Rājat. 5, 304.<BR> 6. The persons of a drama, Vikr. 3, 9.<BR> II. f. त्री.<BR> 1. A vessel, a plate, MBh. 1, 7215.<BR> 2. A name of Durgā.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. fôdr; perhaps Lat. patera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्र|अपात्रं
अ- + पात्र अ- + पात्र, n. a person not worthy of receiving gifts, Bhag. 17, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपात्र
उद(न्)- + पात्र उद(न्)- + पात्र, n. a pot of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोशपात्र
उपक्रोश- + पात्र उपक्रोश- + पात्र, n. an object of blame, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपात्र
ताम्र- + पात्र ताम्र- + पात्र, n. a copper vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुपात्र
दारु- + पात्र दारु- + पात्र, n. a wooden bowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपात्र
दूर- + पात्र दूर- + पात्र, adj. having a wide bed (as a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपपात्र
धूप- + पात्र धूप- + पात्र, n. a box for keeping incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपात्र
पिण्ड- + पात्र पिण्ड- + पात्र, n. 1. the vessel in which cakes are offered to the Manes. 2. alms (properly, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a " target="_blank">Page0541-a + 40</a>] the pot for receiving food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णपात्र|पूर्णपात्रं
पूर्ण- + पात्र पूर्ण- + पात्र, m. and n. 1. a full cup. 2. a measure of 256 handfulls of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपात्र
प्रसाद- + पात्र प्रसाद- + पात्र, n. an object of favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानपात्र|यानपात्रं
यान- + पात्र यान- + पात्र, n. a ship, a boat, Pañc. 262, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासपात्र
विश्वास- + पात्र विश्वास- + पात्र, n. a confidential agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपात्र|सुपात्रं
सु- + पात्र सु- + पात्र, n. 1. an earthen vessel. 2. a very fit or respectable person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रता
पात्रता पात्र + ता, f., and पात्रत्व पात्र + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Condition of being a receptacle, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1249.<BR> 2. Condition of being worthy, Yājñ. 1, 200; Hit. pr. d. 6, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रय
पात्रय पात्रय, a denomin. derived from पात्र with अय, Par. To use as drinking vessel, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1754.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक पात्रिक, i. e. पात्र + इक, n. and f. की, A vessel, a cup, MBh. 12, 8327; Bhāg. P. 8, 18, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन् पात्रिन्, i. e. पात्र + इन्, adj. Having a vessel, Man. 6, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस् पा + थस्, n. Water, Kathās. 27, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेय|पाथेयं
पाथेय पाथेय, i. e. पथिन् + एय, n. Provisions for a journey, Vikr. d. 94.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाथेय
अ- + पाथेय अ- + पाथेय, adj. without provisions for a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोज|पाथोजं
पाथोज पाथोज, i. e. पाथस्-ज, n. A lotus, Rājat. 4, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधर|पाथोधरः
पाथोधर पाथोधर, i. e. पाथस्-धर, m. A cloud, Rājat. 3, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधि|पाथोधिः
पाथोधि पाथोधि, i. e. पाथस्-धा (see पयोधि), m. The ocean, Rājat. 3, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्
पाद् पाद्, see 3. पद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद|पादः
पाद पाद, i. e. 1. पद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A foot.<BR> 2. The bottom (of a bag), Man. 2, 99.<BR> 3. The foot of a mountain, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b " target="_blank">Page0541-b + 44</a>] Megh. 19.<BR> 4. A hill at the foot of a mountain, Śāk. d. 145.<BR> 5. The root of a tree.<BR> 6. A ray, a beam, Pañc. i. d. 372.<BR> 7. A quarter, Man. 8, 18.<BR> 8. The fourth part of a śloka or strophe, Man. 2, 77.<BR> 9. The quadrant of a circle.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. fôtus; A.S. fót.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपाद
अधःपाद अधःपाद, i. e. अधस्-, m. the sole of the feet, Pañc. 165, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद|अष्टपादः
अष्ट(न्)- + पाद अष्ट(न्)- + पाद, adj. having eight feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपाद|एकपादः
एक- + पाद एक- + पाद,<BR> I. adj., f. दा. 1. one-footed. 2. using only one foot.<BR> II. m. the name of a fabulous people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपाद
गुरु- + पाद गुरु- + पाद, m. the feet of a guru, i. e. of the parents or of the spiritual teacher, instead of गुरु, Bhartṛ. 2, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रपाद|चंद्रपाद|चन्द्रपादः
चन्द्र- + पाद चन्द्र- + पाद, m. a moonbeam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपाद
जल- + पाद जल- + पाद (rather जाल-), m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपाद|जालपादः
जाल- + पाद जाल- + पाद, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपाद
देव- + पाद देव- + पाद, m. pl. the feet of a king, instead of a king, Pañc. 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपाद|द्विपादः
द्वि- + पाद द्वि- + पाद, adj., f. दी, biped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपाद|रक्तपादः
रक्त- + पाद रक्त- + पाद, m. a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपाद|शीर्णपादः
शीर्ण- + पाद शीर्ण- + पाद, m. Yama (having shrivelled feet in consequence of a curse of his mother; cf. probably the devil with his horse's foot).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपाद|स्थूलपादः
स्थूल- + पाद स्थूल- + पाद, m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपाद|हंसपादं
हंस- + पाद हंस- + पाद,<BR> I. m. vermilion.<BR> II. f. दी, a particular shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादक
पादक पाद + क, a substitute for पाद when latter part of a comp. adj., f. दिका, e. g. त्रि-, Three-footed, Rām. 5, 17, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतस्
पादतस् पाद + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. Out of the feet, Man. 1, 31.<BR> 2. At the foot (of one's bed), Man. 4, 54.<BR> 3. = In the south-west, Man. 3, 89.<BR> 4. By degrees (हीन, Each in succession is lower in rank than the preceding), Kām. Nītis. 12, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप|पादपः
पादप पाद-प (vb. 1. पा), m. A tree, Man. 8, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादभाज्
पादभाज् पादभाज्, i. e. पाद-भज्, adj. Possessing a fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरक्ष|पादरक्षः
पादरक्ष पाद-रक्ष् + अ, m. A footguard, Draup. 8, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवन्त्|पादवत्
पादवन्त् पाद + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessed of feet, Rām. 2, 107, 19 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशस्
पादशस् पाद + शस्, adv.<BR> 1. Foot by foot, Man. 1, 82.<BR> 2. By a fourth, Man. 1, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात|पादातं|पादातः
पादात पादात, i. e. पाद-अत् + अ,<BR> I. m. A foot-soldier.<BR> II. n. Foot, infantry, MBh. 12, 3672.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथपादात
स-रथ- + पादात स-रथ- + पादात, adj. with chariots and infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्त|पादांत|पादान्तः
पादान्त पादान्त, i. e. पाद-अन्त, m. End of the feet; loc. ते, Near the feet, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 752.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्तर|पादांतर
पादान्तर पादान्तर, i. e. पाद-अन्तर, n. The interval of a step; loc. रे, After having made a step, Śāk. 16, 1, Chezy. (cf. पदान्तर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिक
पादिक पादिक, i. e. पाद + इक, adj. Amounting to a quarter, Man. 3, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपादिक
अर्ध- + पादिक अर्ध- + पादिक, adj. Consisting in the loss of half of one foot, 8, 325.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन्
पादिन् पादिन्, i. e. पाद + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Having feet.<BR> 2. Entitled to a fourth part or share, Man. 8, 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुका
पादुका पादुका, i. e. पद् + उ + क, f. A shoe, Rām. 2, 115, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपादुक
स-पादुक स-पादुक, adj. With sandals, Rām. 3, 52, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकृत्
पादुकृत् and पादूकृत् पादू̆कृत्, i. e. पद् + उ-कृ + त्, m. A shoemaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्म|पाद्मः
पाद्म पाद्म, i. e. पद्म + अ, adj. Referring to, treating of, the lotus, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्य|पाद्यं
पाद्य पाद्य, i. e. पाद् or पाद + य,<BR> I. adj. Referring or belonging to the feet.<BR> II. n. Water for cleaning the feet, Indr. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
पान पान, i. e. 1. पा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Drinking, Pañc. 184, 18.<BR> 2. Enjoying, Lass. 25, 11.<BR> 3. Beverage, Man. 3, 227.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपान|वीरपानं
वीर-पान वीर-पान and -पाण, n. the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b " target="_blank">Page0542-b + 41</a>] drink of warriors, taken for refreshment or to elevate courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपान|सहपानं
सह- + पान सह- + पान, n. drinking together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानक|पानकं
पानक पान + क, m. and n. Beverage, MBh. 15, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिक|पानिकः
पानिक पानिक, i. e. पान + इक, m. A seller of liquors, Rām. 2, 90, 16 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्थ|पांथ|पांथः|पान्थः
पान्थ पान्थ, i. e. पन्थन् + अ (see पथिन्), m. A traveller, Pañc. 117, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्नग
पान्नग पान्नग, i. e. पन्नग + अ, adj. Consisting of snakes, Hariv. 9387.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप|पापं|पापः
पाप पाप,<BR> I. adj., f. पा and पी, comparat. पापतर, पापीयंस्, and पापीयस्तर, MBh. 13, 2213; superl. पापतम, पापिष्ठ, पापिष्ठतर, MBh. 7, 8734, and पापिष्ठतम, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 9.<BR> 1. Wicked, sinful, Chr. 61, 46; 9, 43.<BR> 2. Inauspicious.<BR> 3. पापिष्ठतम, with abl., Worse, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 9.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Wickedness, Rām. 3, 51, 36.<BR> 2. Evil, 3, 54, 27.<BR> 3. Crime, Pañc. i. d. 321.<BR> 4. Sin, Chr. 30, 37.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably, Lat. pejor (for pepjor), pessimus, peccare, perhaps κακός, κακίων, κάκιστος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाप|अपापः
अ- + पाप अ- + पाप, adj. innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपाप|उपपापं
उप- + पाप उप- + पाप, n. a crime of the third degree, Yājñ. 3, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतपाप
धूत- + पाप धूत- + पाप (vb. धू), adj. free from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाप
निष्पाप निष्पाप, i. e. निस्-, adj. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापाप|महापापं
महा- + पाप महा- + पाप, n. a sin of the highest degree. Yājñ. 3, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापक|पापकं|पापकः
पापक पाप + क,<BR> I. adj., f. की and पिका, Wicked, Indr. 5, 61.<BR> II. m. A rascal, MBh. 5, 1270.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Evil, 1, 3016.<BR> 2. Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकृत्
पापकृत् पाप-कृ + त्, adj. sbst. Wicked, sinful, a villain, Rām. 3, 50, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापर्द्धि
पापर्द्धि पापर्द्धि, i. e. पाप-ऋद्धि, f. Hunting. Pañc. 120, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापलोक्य
पापलोक्य पापलोक्य, i. e. पाप-लोक + य, adj., f. या, Belonging to hell, infernal, MBh. 1, 3558.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापहन्
पापहन् पाप-हन्, adj. Destroying sin, Man. 7, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिन्
पापिन् पापिन्, i. e. पाप + इन्, adj. Wicked, sinful, a sinner, Rājat. 5, 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिष्ठतम
पापिष्ठतम पापिष्ठ + तम, see पाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीय
पापीय पापीय = पापीयंस्, see पाप, Worse, MBh. 2, 2123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीयस्त्व
पापीयस्त्व पापीयस्त्व, i. e. पापीयंस् + त्व (see पाप), n. Sinfulness, Rājat. 5, 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप्मन्
पाप्मन् पाप्मन्, i. e. पाप + मन्, m.<BR> 1. Evil.<BR> 2. Sin, wickedness. Man. 11, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन्
पामन् पामन्, n. and f. मा, Cutaneous eruption, herpes, scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामर|पामरः
पामर पामर, i. e. पामन् + अ, with र् for न्, adj. Base, wicked, Rājat. 5, 400.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायना
पायना पायना, i. e. 1. पा, Caus. + अन, f. Causing to drink, moistening, Suśr. 1, 27, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायस|पायसः
पायस पायस, i. e. पयस् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of milk.<BR> II. m. and n. Food made of milk, Man. 3, 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायिन्
पायिन् पायिन्, i. e. 1. पा + इन्, latter part of comp. adj. Drinking, Vikr. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायु|पायुः
पायु पायु, m. The anus, Man. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्
पार् पार्, i. 10, see 1. पृ, Caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार पार, i. e. 1. पृ + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. The further or opposite bank of a river or sea, Rām. 3, 54, 14; figuratively with gen. The totality of the object denoted by the gen., e. g. तमसस्, The whole darkness, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6. कारणानाम्, All the tortures, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 16.<BR> 2. End, Yājñ. 1, 51.<BR> II. m. Quicksilver.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अ- + पार अ- + पार, adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b " target="_blank">Page0543-b + 41</a>] रा, boundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पार
दुष्पार दुष्पार, i. e. दुस्-पॄ + अ, adj. 1. difficult to be sailed across. 2. difficult to be overcome. 3. difficult to be performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपार|दूरपारः
दूर- + पार दूर- + पार,<BR> I. adj. the opposite bank of which is very distant, broad. 2. difficult to be obtained.<BR> II. m. a broad river, difficult to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पार
निष्पार निष्पार, i. e. निस्-, adj. boundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्य|पारक्यं|पारक्यः
पारक्य पारक्य, i. e. पर + क + य, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to another, Man. 10, 97.<BR> 2. Hostile. m. An enemy, Hit. 109, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग|पारगः
पारग पार-ग, adj.<BR> 1. Crossing MBh. 2, 2418.<BR> 2. Intending to cross, 4, 451.<BR> 3. Accomplishing, Rām. 3, 53, 8.<BR> 4. Having studied, knowing, Pañc. 155, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपारग|वेदपारगः
वेद- + पारग वेद- + पारग, adj. sbst. skilled in the Vedas, Chr. 60, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग्रामिक
पारग्रामिक पारग्रामिक, i. e. पर-ग्राम + इक, adj., f. की, Hostile, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 24 (पारग्रामिकं विधिम् आ चिकीर्ष, To prepare for hostility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारजायिक|पारजायिकः
पारजायिक पारजायिक, i. e. पर-जाया + इक, adj. sbst. An adulterer, MBh. 12, 2512.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
पारण पारण, i. e. पॄ + अन,<BR> I. adj. Saving, Hariv. 7941.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Fulfilling, MBh. 7, 2907.<BR> 2. Reading, studying, MBh. 18, 212.<BR> III. n. and f. णा,<BR> 1. with and without व्रत, Concluding a fast, eating or drinking after a fast, Kathās. 21, 146.<BR> 2. Breakfast, Kathās. 23, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत|पारतः
पारत पारत (cf. पार), m. Quicksilver, Kathās. 37, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्र्य|पारतंत्र्य|पारतंत्र्यं|पारतन्त्र्यं
पारतन्त्र्य पारतन्त्र्य, i. e. पर-अन्त्र + य, n. Dependence, MBh. 5, 1725.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्रिक|पारत्रिकं
पारत्रिक पारत्रिक, i. e. परत्र + इक, adj. Relating to the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्र्य|पारत्र्यं
पारत्र्य पारत्र्य, i. e. परत्र + य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a " target="_blank">Page0544-a + 41</a>] adj. Relating to the next world, Man. 2, 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारद|पारदः
पारद पारद, m.<BR> 1. Quicksilver (cf. पारत).<BR> 2. pl. The name of a people, the Parthians, Man. 10, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिक|पारदारिकः
पारदारिक पारदारिक, i. e. पर-दार + इक, adj. sbst. Having sexual intercourse with another's wife, an adulterer, Kathās. 19, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदार्य|पारदार्यं|पारदार्य्य
पारदार्य पारदार्य, i. e. पर-दार + य, n. Adultery, Man. 11, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्य|पारदेश्यः
पारदेश्य पारदेश्य, i. e. पर-देश + य, adj. Belonging to, or coming from, a foreign country, Yājñ. 2, 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्य|पारमहंस्यं
पारमहंस्य पारमहंस्य, i. e. परम-हंस + य,<BR> I. adj. Relating to the परमहंसस्, or religious men who have subdued all their senses by abstract meditation, Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 4.<BR> II. n. Most sublime asceticism or meditation (see the following).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्यपरि
पारमहंस्यपरि पारमहंस्य-परि, adv. Relating to the most sublime meditation or speculation, Bhāg. P. 4, 21, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमार्थिक|पारमार्थिकः
पारमार्थिक पारमार्थिक, i. e. परम-अर्थ + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Real.<BR> 2. Loving right, Pañc. i. d. 389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेश्वर
पारमेश्वर पारमेश्वर, i. e. परम-ईश्वर + अ, adj. Referring to, coming from, the supreme lord, Śiva, etc., Kathās. 6, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेष्ठ्य|पारमेष्ठ्यं
पारमेष्ठ्य पारमेष्ठ्य, i. e. परमेष्ठिन् + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Referring to the supreme lord, Brahman, etc., MBh. 1, 7682.<BR> 2. Referring to a king, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 38 (n. the royal insignia).<BR> II. n. Highest position, 2, 2, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य|पारंपर्य|पारंपर्यं|पारम्पर्य्य|पारम्पर्य्यं
पारम्पर्य पारम्पर्य, i. e. परंपर + य, n. Hereditary succession, tradition, Man. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
पारयिष्णु पारयिष्णु, i. e. 1. पृ, Caus. + इष्णु, adj.<BR> 1. Accomplishing.<BR> 2. Victorious, MBh. 12, 3749.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलोक्य
पारलोक्य पारलोक्य, i. e. पर-लोक + य, adj. Referring to the next world, MBh. 5, 778.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिक
पारलौकिक पारलौकिक, i. e. पर-लोक + इक, adj. Referring to the next world, MBh. 3, 12616.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवर्ग्य
पारवर्ग्य पारवर्ग्य, i. e. पर-वर्ग + य. Siding with the enemy, MBh. 2, 2131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारशव पारशव, i. e. परशु + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. Iron.<BR> II. adj., f. वी, Of iron, MBh. 4, 1011.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. pl. The name of a people (v. r. पारसव).<BR> 2. The son of a Śūdra woman by a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 9, 178.<BR> 3. A bastard, f. वी (पारसव, and वी with स्), MBh. 1, 4361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसव
पारसव पारसव. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारहंस्य
पारहंस्य पारहंस्य, i. e. पर-हंस + य, adj. Relating to an ascetic who has subdued all his senses (cf. पारमहंस्य), Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापत|पारापतः
पारापत पारापत, and पारावत पारावत, m. A pigeon, Vikr. d. 43; Pañc. 157, 3 (with व्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायण|पारायणं
पारायण पारायण, i. e. पार-अयन, n.<BR> 1. Study, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 10.<BR> 2. Totality, MBh. 13, 2701; Utt. Rāmac. 98, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावत|पारावतः
पारावत पारावत, m.<BR> 1. See पारापत.<BR> 2. A kind of snake.<BR> 3. A tree, Diospyros embryopteris Pers. (n. its fruit).<BR> 4. pl. A class of deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावर्य
पारावर्य पारावर्य, i. e. पर-अवर + य, n. Totality; instr. येण, Completely, MBh. 11, 655.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावार|पारावारं|पारावारः
पारावार पारावार, i. e. पार-अवार (from अव, being on this side, Gramm. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0545-a " target="_blank">Page0545-a + 40</a>] ved.)<BR> 1. The opposite bank or shore, and that on this side, MBh. 5, 1017.<BR> 2. m. The sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर्य|पाराशर्यः|पाराशर्य्य|पाराशर्य्यः
पाराशर्य पाराशर्य, i. e. पराशर + य, patronym. A son of Parāśara, i. e. Vyāsa, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिक्षित|पारिक्षितः
पारिक्षित पारिक्षित, i. e. परिक्षित् + अ, patronym. A descendant of Parikṣit, i. e. Janamejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजात|पारिजातः
पारिजात पारिजात, i. e. परि-जात (vb. जन्), + अ, m.<BR> 1. A tree of paradise, Hariv. 7168.<BR> 2. The coral tree, Erythrina indica Lam.<BR> 3. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजातक|पारिजातकः
