पार्ष्णिग्रह पार्ष्णि-ग्रह, adj. Seizing from behind, Bhāg. P. 8, 2, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पार्ष्णिग्रह
दुष्पार्ष्णिग्रह दुष्पार्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. having a dangerous enemy in the rear, Kām. Nītis. 13, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्राह|पार्ष्णिग्राहः
पार्ष्णिग्राह पार्ष्णि-ग्राह, m. An enemy in the rear, Man. 7, 207.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पार्ष्णिग्राह
दुष्पार्ष्णिग्राह दुष्पार्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. having a dangerous enemy in the rear, Kām. Nītis. 13, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्
पाल् पाल्, see 2. पा, Caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल 2. पा + ल, m. One who guards [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b " target="_blank">Page0547-b + 46</a>] or protects, Rām. 1, 42, 15 Gorr.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाल
अङ्क- + पाल अङ्क- + पाल, f. ली, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तपाल|अन्तपालः
अन्त- + पाल अन्त- + पाल, m. 1. a guard of the frontiers. 2. a guard of the rear of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपाल|अवनिपालः
अवनि- + पाल अवनि- + पाल, m. a king, Bhag. 11, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानपाल|उद्यानपालः
उद्यान- + पाल उद्यान- + पाल, m. the inspector of a garden, a gardener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पपाल|कल्पपालः
कल्प- + पाल कल्प- + पाल, m. 1. a protector of the holy precepts or institutes. 2. a distiller or seller of spirituous liquors, Rājat. 5, 205 (where कल्य- is to be changed to कल्प-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टपाल
कोट्ट- + पाल कोट्ट- + पाल, m. the governor of a fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपाल|क्षितिपालः
क्षिति- + पाल क्षिति- + पाल, m. a king, Ragh. 2, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रपाल|क्षेत्रपालः
क्षेत्र- + पाल क्षेत्र- + पाल, m. 1. a field-guard, Pañc. 224, 5. 2. the tutelary deity of a field, 174, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मापाल|क्ष्मापालः
क्ष्मा- + पाल क्ष्मा- + पाल, m. a king, Rājat. 5, 319.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहपाल|गृहपालः
गृह- + पाल गृह- + पाल, m. 1. a castle-ward. 2. a dog, Bhāg. P. 1, 13, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाल|गोपालः
गो- + पाल गो- + पाल,<BR> I. m. 1. a cowherd, Man. 4, 251. 2. a king, Pañc. i. d. 249. 3. a proper name.<BR> II. f. ली, a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यपाल|चैत्यपालः
चैत्य- + पाल चैत्य- + पाल, m. the watchman of a sanctuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीपाल
जगती- + पाल जगती- + पाल, m. a king, Hit. ii. d. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पाल|दिक्पालः
दिक्पाल दिक्पाल, i. e. दिश्-, and दिशा-, m. the guardian deity of a quarter of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारपाल|द्वारपालः
द्वार- + पाल द्वार- + पाल, m. a door-keeper, a porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपाल|धर्मपालः
धर्म- + पाल धर्म- + पाल, m. 1. the guardian of law. 2. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपाल|पशुपालः
पशु- + पाल पशु- + पाल, m. 1. a herdsman. 2. pl. the name of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापाल|प्रजापालः
प्रजा- + पाल प्रजा- + पाल, भू-, भूमि, and मही-, m. a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपाल|भोगपालः
भोग- + पाल भोग- + पाल, m. a groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपाल|लोकपालः
लोक- + पाल लोक- + पाल, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाल
वि- + पाल वि- + पाल, adj. having no keeper, Man. 8, 240; unguarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपाल|शिशुपालः
शिशु- + पाल शिशु- + पाल, m. the name of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक|पालकः
पालक पाल + क, m.<BR> 1. A guardian, Rājat. 5, 263.<BR> 2. A protector, Mārk. P. 61, 66.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. bubulcus (with गोपालक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालिका
कुल-पालिका कुल-पालिका, f. a proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालक|गोपालकः
गो- + पालक गो- + पालक,<BR> I. m. 1. a cowherd. 2. a proper name.<BR> II. f. लिका, the wife of a cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपालक|दंडपालक|दण्डपालकः
दण्ड- + पालक दण्ड- + पालक, m. the chief of the police, Mṛcch. 117, 19 v. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन पाल् + अन, i. e. पा, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Guarding, fostering, Mārk. P. 76, 23.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Preserving, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a " target="_blank">Page0548-a + 41</a>] guarding, Man. 7, 88; nourishing.<BR> 2. Maintaining, keeping, MBh. 1, 327.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ पालयितृ, i. e. 2. पा, Caus., + तृ, m. A protector, MBh. 1, 2107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश पालाश, i. e. पलाश + अ, adj., f. शी, Made of the wood of the Palāśatree, Man. 2, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालि|पालिः
पालि पालि, and पाली पाली, f.<BR> 1. The tip of the ear, Gīt. 3, 13.<BR> 2. The edge of a sword or any other cutting instrument.<BR> 3. A line or row, Gīt. 6, 10.<BR> 4. A raised bank, a dike, Rājat. 5, 106 (ली).<BR> 5. A boundary, a margin, Bhartṛ. 3, 24 (ली).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाली|अंकपाली
अङ्क-पाली अङ्क-पाली, f. embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्
पालिन् पालिन्, i. e. 2. पा, Caus., + इन्, adj., f. नी, Protecting, Bhāg. P. 3, 21, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक पावक, i. e. पू + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to Agni, Utt. Rāmac. 142, 12.<BR> 2. Pure.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Fire, or its deified personification, Man. 2, 187.<BR> 2. A kind of Ṛṣi.<BR> 3. Name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकि|पावकिः
पावकि पावकि, i. e. पावक + इ, patronym., m. A son of fire, i. e. Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन पावन, i. e. पू + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Purifying, Man. 2, 26.<BR> 2. Pure, Rām. 1, 27, 17.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> III. f. नी, The name of a river.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Purifying, Man. 11, 85.<BR> 2. A means of purifying, 11, 177.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिपावन|पंक्तिपावन|पङ्क्तिपावनः
पङ्क्ति- + पावन पङ्क्ति- + पावन, adj. purifying a company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमानी
पावमानी पावमानी, i. e. पवमान (vb. पू), + अ + ई, f. The name of hymns referring to the preparation of the सोम, Man. 5, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावर|पावरः
पावर पावर, a corrupt form of द्वापर, The die which is marked with two points, Mṛcch. 33, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश|पाशः
पाश पाश, i. e. पश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A tie, a string, a chain, a fetter, MBh. 1, 6749.<BR> 2. A string for fastening tamed animals.<BR> 3. A net or noose for catching birds, Hit. 21, 10.<BR> 4. A noose as principal attribute of Varuṇa, Rām. 3, 54, 9 (cf. the Vedas).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपाश|कर्णपाशः
कर्ण- + पाश कर्ण- + पाश, m. a handsome ear, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटपाश|कूटपाशः
कूट- + पाश कूट- + पाश, m. a net for catching deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपाश|केशपाशः
केश- + पाश केश- + पाश, m. much or flowing hair, a tuft of hair, Vikr. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपाश
धर्म- + पाश धर्म- + पाश, m. the noose of the god of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपाश|नागपाशः
नाग- + पाश नाग- + पाश, m. a special kind of noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपाश|पशुपाशः
पशु- + पाश पशु- + पाश, m. the fetter which enchains the soul, i. e. the external world, Prab. 59, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश
वि- + पाश वि- + पाश, adj. deprived of his noose, Rām. 3, 54, 97; unfettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशन|पाशनं
पाशन पाशन, i. e. पश् + अन (m. or n.), A noose, MBh. 7, 5923.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशभृत्
पाशभृत् पाश-भृ + त्, m. (holding a noose), Varuṇa, Ragh. 2, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव पाशव, i. e. पशु + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Come from animals, animal, Nal. 23, 10.<BR> 2. Used by animals, beastly, Lass. 11, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशवन्त्|पाशवत्
पाशवन्त् पाश + वन्त्, adj. Possessed of a noose, MBh. 7, 3136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन् पाशिन्, i. e. पाश + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Having a noose, MBh. 8, 1998.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Varuṇa.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत पाशुपत, i. e. पशु-पति + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती, Belonging or referring to Śiva.<BR> II. m. A follower or worshipper of Śiva in one of his forms as the supreme deity of the Hindu triad, Rājat. 5, 403.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्य|पाशुपाल्यं
पाशुपाल्य पाशुपाल्य, i. e. पशु-पाल + य, n. The business of a grazier rearing and keeping cattle, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्त्य
पाश्चात्त्य पाश्चात्त्य, i. e. पश्चात् + त्य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a " target="_blank">Page0549-a + 39</a>] adj.<BR> 1. Last, posterior, Pañc. ed. orn. 49, 15.<BR> 2. Western, Ragh. 4, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्ड|पाषंड|पाषण्डः
पाषण्ड पाषण्ड,<BR> I. m. n. Heresy, Man. 5, 90.<BR> II. adj. Heretical, MBh. 12, 11284.<BR> III. m. A heretic, Prab. 21, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डिन्|पाषंडिन्
पाषण्डिन् पाषण्डिन्, i. e. पाषण्ड + इन्, m. A heretic, Man. 4, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाण|पाषाणः
पाषाण पाषाण, m. A stone, Yājñ. 2, 298.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषपाषाण|कषपाषाणः
कष- + पाषाण कष- + पाषाण, and निकष-, m. a touchstone, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1940.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पि
† 1. पि पि, i. 6, पिय, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पि
2. पि पि, sometimes for अपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंस्
† पिंस् पिंस्, i. 10 and 1, Par. To speak or to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक|पिकः
पिक पिक,<BR> 1. m. The Indian cuckoo, Cuculus indicus, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 857.<BR> 2. f. की, The female.<BR>//Probably for primitive स्पि + क, cf. σπίζω.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pîcus, pîca; O.H.G. speh, speht; σίττη for σπίττη or ψίττη, σίττακος, ψίττακος, ϕίττακ for σϕίττα (the π is aspirated by the influence of the preceding σ), ϕιττάκη, βίττακος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्ग|पिंग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिङ्ग पिङ्ग, i. e. पिञ्ज् + अ, adj., f. गा.<BR> 1. Of a tawny colour, Pañc. 182, 18.<BR> 2. Yellow, Vikr. d. 157.<BR> 3. Red, Hiḍ. 2, 2 (cf. पिङ्गाक्ष).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिङ्ग|एकपिंग|एकपिङ्गः
एक- + पिङ्ग एक- + पिङ्ग, m. a name of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतपिङ्ग|श्वेतपिंग|श्वेतपिङ्गः
श्वेत- + पिङ्ग श्वेत- + पिङ्ग, m. a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गल|पिंगल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिङ्गल पिङ्ग + ल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Of a tawny colour, brown, Ragh. 12, 71; yellowish.<BR> 2. Red-eyed, Man. 3, 8 (Kull.).<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR> III. f. ला, A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिङ्गल
कृष्ण- + पिङ्गल कृष्ण- + पिङ्गल, adj., f. ला, of a fuscous colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलिका|पिंगलिका
पिङ्गलिका पिङ्गलिका, i. e. पिन्गल + क, f. A kind of bee, Suśr. 2, 290, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलित|पिंगलित
पिङ्गलित पिङ्गलित, i. e. पिङ्गल + इत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b " target="_blank">Page0549-b + 40</a>] adj. Grown of a tawny colour, Kathās. 21, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाक्ष|पिंगाक्ष|पिङ्गाक्षः
पिङ्गाक्ष पिङ्गाक्ष, i. e. पिङ्ग-अक्ष,<BR> I. adj., f. क्षी, Red-eyed, Hiḍ. 2, 2.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A monkey, Rām. 5, 5, 23.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> III. f. क्षी, The name of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचु|पिचुः
पिचु पिचु, m.<BR> 1. Cotton, Suśr. 1, 60, 16.<BR> 2. The name of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमर्द|पिचुमर्दः|पिचुमर्द्द|पिचुमर्द्दः
पिचुमर्द पिचुमर्द, see -मन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुल|पिचुलः
पिचुल पिचु + ल, m.<BR> 1. Tamarix indica.<BR> 2. Cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्च्
† पिच्च् पिच्च्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To cut, to divide.<BR> --Cf. पिछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ पिच्छ,<BR> I. m. A tail.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A feather of the tail, Pañc. 175, 9; especially of a peacock.<BR> 2. A crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिका
पिच्छिका पिच्छिका, i. e. पिच्छा + क, f. A bunch of feathers of a peacock's tail, Kathās. 30, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिल|पिच्छिलं|पिच्छिलः
पिच्छिल पिच्छिल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, Slimy, lubricous, Mārk. P. 10, 9.<BR> II. f. ला, The name of several plants.<BR> --Cf. πίσσα; Lat. pix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिछ्|पिच्छ्
† पिछ् पिछ्, i. 10, Par. To cut, to divide.<BR> --i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To inflict pain.<BR> 2. To obstruct, to hinder.<BR> --Cf. मिछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज्|पिंज्
† 1. पिञ्ज् पिञ्ज्, ii. 2, Ātm.<BR> 1. To dye or colour (probably अपि-अञ्ज्, cf. Lat. pingere).<BR> 2. To join.<BR> 3. To adore.<BR> 4. To sound inarticulately.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To kill or injure.<BR> 2. To be strong.<BR> 3. To give or take.<BR> 4. To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज्|पिंज्
† 2. पिञ्ज् पिञ्ज्, i. 10 and 1, Par.<BR> 1. To speak or shine.<BR> 2. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज|पिंज|पिञ्जं|पिञ्जः
पिञ्ज पिञ्ज, adj. Disturbed.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्ज
उत्पिञ्ज उत्पिञ्ज, i. e. उद्-, Insurrection(?), Rājat. 3, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जर|पिंजर|पिञ्जरं|पिञ्जरः
पिञ्जर पिञ्ज् + अर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a " target="_blank">Page0550-a + 40</a>] Yellow or tawny, reddish-yellow, Mṛcch. 48, 11.<BR> II. n. Gold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिञ्जर|आपिंजर|आपिञ्जरं
आ- + पिञ्जर आ- + पिञ्जर, adj., f. रा, reddish, Ragh. 16, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपिञ्जर
परि- + पिञ्जर परि- + पिञ्जर, adj. brown-red, Kām. Nītis. 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जल|पिंजल|पिञ्जलं|पिञ्जलः
पिञ्जल पिञ्ज + ल adj. Disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जलक
पिञ्जलक पिञ्जल + क in उत्पिञ्जलक, i. e. उद्-, adj. Full of disturbance, MBh. 7, 1048.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्
† पिट् पिट्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट पिट,<BR> I. m. A basket.<BR> II. n. A roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटक|पिटकं|पिटकः
पिटक पिट + क, m., f. का, and n.<BR> 1. A basket, Hariv. 14578.<BR> 2. A boil.<BR> 3. An ornament on Indra's banner, MBh. 1, 2354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ्
† पिठ् पिठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt.<BR> 2. To feel pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठर|पिठरं|पिठरः
पिठर पिठर<BR> I. m. and f. री, and n. A pot, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1782; a pan.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A kind of fire, Hariv. 10467.<BR> 2. The name of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठरक|पिठरकं|पिठरकः
पिठरक पिठर + क, A pot, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 729.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिडक|पिडकः
पिडक पिडक, m. (n. ?). A small boil, a pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड्|पिंड्
पिण्ड् पिण्ड्, probably akin to पिष्, i. 1, Ātm., and i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To accumulate.<BR> 2. To assemble. पिण्डित,<BR> 1. Gathered, Kathās. 26, 283; collected, MBh. 10, 622; massy, solid, close.<BR> 2. Multiplied, MBh. 7, 4746.<BR> 3. Thick.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To heap together, MBh. 10, 8310. संपिण्डित, Clenched, united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड|पिंड|पिण्डं|पिण्डः
पिण्ड पिण्ड, probably akin to पिष्,<BR> I. m., f. डी, and n.<BR> 1. A lump, Pañc. 136, 2; a heap, a cluster, a quantity, Kathās. 4, 81.<BR> 2. A ball, a globe, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-b " target="_blank">Page0550-b + 47</a>] little button, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 19.<BR> II. m. n.<BR> 1. A mouthful, or roundish lump of food, Man. 11, 216.<BR> 2. Food.<BR> 3. Livelihood, means of living, MBh. 1, 4148.<BR> 4. Alms, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 15.<BR> 5. The body.<BR> 6. An object, Bhāṣāp. 123.<BR> 7. An oblation to deceased ancestors, as a ball or lump of meat, or rice mixed up with milk, curds, flowers, etc., and offered to the manes at the several Śrāddhas by the nearest surviving relations; the funeral cake, Man. 3, 215.<BR> III. f. डी, A plant, Jonesia aśoka, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 10; cf. 184, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पिण्ड|पृथक्पिण्डः
पृथक्- + पिण्ड पृथक्- + पिण्ड, m. a relation who offers the oblations to the Manes separately, Man. 5, 78 (Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपिण्ड
सह- + पिण्ड सह- + पिण्ड (Man. 3, 248), and स-, m. a kinsman, especially one connected by the offering of the funeral cake to either or all of the manes of the father, grandfather, and great-grandfather, and their wives respectively, as sprung from them in directly collateral lines; the relationship stops with every fourth person. The following are enumerated as स-पिण्डस्: the son, son's son, and son's grandson; widow, daughter, and daughter's son; the father, the mother, the brother, brother's son, and brother's grandson; father's daughter's son; paternal grandfather; paternal grandmother; paternal grandfather's brother, brother's son, and grandson; and lastly, the great-grandfather's daughter's son. Other enumerations extend the connection of Sapiṇḍas to seven persons, both in an ascending or descending line; cf. Man. 2, 247; 3, 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिण्ड|असपिंड
अ-सपिण्ड अ-सपिण्ड, adj., f. डा, Not descended from a relation within the sixth degree, Man. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डक|पिंडक|पिंडकं|पिण्डकं|पिंडकः|पिण्डकः
पिण्डक पिण्ड + क,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A lump, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 11.<BR> 2. A lump of food, Hariv. 14740.<BR> 3. The frontal globes of an elephant in rut, MBh. 1, 5471.<BR> II. f. डिका, A fleshy part of the body, Yājñ. 3, 97; as the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a " target="_blank">Page0551-a + 41</a>] calf, MBh. 14, 2582.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमस्तकपिण्डक
भिन्न-मस्तक-पिण्डक भिन्न-मस्तक-पिण्डक, and -पिण्डिक (from the fem. पिण्डिका), adj. (an elephant) whose frontal globes are open, MBh. 1, 5471; 7, 4564.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डतस्
पिण्डतस् पिण्ड + तस्, adv. Of a lump, Hit. Pr. d. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डत्व
पिण्डत्व पिण्ड + त्व, n. State of a mass, density; figuratively, Kathās. 11, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डद|पिंडद|पिण्डदः
पिण्डद पिण्ड-द, adj., f. दा.<BR> 1. Who or what gives the funeral cake to deceased ancestors, Yājñ. 2, 132.<BR> 2. Giving a mouthful of food, Bhartṛ. 2, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डन|पिंडन|पिंडनं|पिण्डनः
पिण्डन पिण्ड् + अन, n. Forming globes, taking a globular form (as water), Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमय
पिण्डमय पिण्ड + मय, adj. Consisting of a lump (of clay), Mṛcch. 47, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डवत्
पिण्डवत् पिण्ड + वत्, adv. Like a ball.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयःपिण्डवत्
अयस्- + पिण्डवत् अयस्- + पिण्डवत्, Like a ball of iron, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्याक|पिण्याकं|पिण्याकः
पिण्याक पिण्याक (probably from पिष्, cf. पुण्य), m.<BR> 1. The sediments of seed, etc., ground for oil, oil-cake, Man. 11, 92.<BR> 2. Assafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितापुत्र
पितापुत्र पितापुत्र, i. e. पितृ, nom. sing., + पुत्र, m. du. Father and son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितामह|पितामहः
पितामह पितामह, i. e. पितृ, nom. sing., -मह (for महन्त्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A paternal grandfather, Man. 3, 221.<BR> 2. pl. Ancestors, Chr. 43, 21.<BR> 3. A name of Brahman.<BR> II. f. ही, A paternal grandmother, Kathās. 30, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वपितामह|पूर्वपितामहः
पूर्व- + पितामह पूर्व- + पितामह, m. an ancestor, Kathās. 21, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपितामह|लोकपितामहः
लोक- + पितामह लोक- + पितामह, m. the great forefather of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितु|पितुः
पितु पितु, i. e. 1. पा + तु, m. Drink.<BR> --Cf. Lat. potus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृ
पितृ पितृ, i. e. 2. पा + तृ, m. (acc. pl. पितरस्, MBh. 3, 12924),<BR> 1. A father, Man. 2, 145.<BR> 2. du. Mother and father, parents, Śāk. 109, 9.<BR> 3. pl.<BR> a. Paternal ancestors, Man. 2, 159.<BR> b. The Manes, or the deceased and deified progenitors of mankind, Man. 3, 194, etc.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pater; πατήρ; Goth. fadar; A.S. faeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकपितृ
अन्-एक- + पितृ अन्-एक- + पितृ, adj., descended from different fathers (viz. grandsons), Yājñ. 2, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितृ
कु- + पितृ कु- + पितृ, m. a wicked father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपितृ
स्व- + पितृ स्व- + पितृ, m. pl. one's ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक|पितृकं
पितृक i. e. पितृ + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Paternal.<BR> 2. Ancestral.<BR> II. A substitute for पितृ, when latter part of comp. adj., Yājñ. 2, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृत्व
पितृत्व पितृ + त्व, n. Paternity, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 966.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपैतामह
पितृपैतामह पितृ-पैतामह,<BR> I. adj., f. ही, Inherited by the father from the grandfather, Sāv. 7, 7.<BR> II. m. pl. Father and ancestors, Manes, Pañc. 89, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपैतामहिक
पितृपैतामहिक पितृपैतामहिक, i. e. पितृपैतामह + इक, adj. Inherited by the father from the grandfather, Pañc. 78, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमन्त्|पितृमत्
पितृमन्त् पितृ + मन्त्, adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Having a father, MBh. 1, 6578.<BR> 2. Accompanied by the Manes, Mārk. P. 31, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्य|पितृव्यः
पितृव्य पितृ + व्य, m. A paternal uncle, Man. 2, 130.<BR> --Cf. Lat. patruus; πατρυιός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृष्वसृ
पितृष्वसृ पितृष्वसृ, i. e. पितृ-स्वसृ, f. A father's sister, Man. 2, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृष्वस्रीय|पितृष्वस्रीयः
पितृष्वस्रीय पितृष्वस्रीय, and पितृस्वस्रीय पितृस्वस्रीय, i. e. पित्रि-स्वसृ + ईय, m., f. या, A paternal aunt's son or daughter, MBh. 1, 4382.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृहन्
पितृहन् पितृ-हन्, m. A parricide, Rājat. 5, 447.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृहू
पितृहू पितृहू, i. e. पितृ-ह्वे, f. The right car, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्त|पित्तं
पित्त पित्त, n. Bile, MBh. 6, 3736.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासारक्तपित्त
नासा-रक्त- + पित्त नासा-रक्त- + पित्त, n. bleeding of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्र्य|पित्र्यं|पित्र्यः
पित्र्य पित्र्य, i. e. पितृ + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Paternal, Man. 9, 92.<BR> 2. Referring, devoted, to the Manes, 2, 59.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Worship of the Manes.<BR> 2. The lunar mansion Maghā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधान|पिधानं
पिधान पिधान, i. e. अपि-धा + अन (m.), n.<BR> 1. Covering, shutting, Mālav. d. 32.<BR> 2. A lid, a covering, Mārk. P. 50, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधानवन्त्|पिधानवत्
पिधानवन्त् पिधान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Covered with a lid, Rājat. 5, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधायकता
पिधायकता पिधायकता, i. e. अपि-धा + अक + ता, f. The act of covering, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनद्धक
पिनद्धक पिनद्धक, i. e. अपि-नद्ध (vb. नह्) + क, adj., f. धिका, Dressed, clothed, Hariv. 11164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाक|पिनाकं|पिनाकः
पिनाक पिनाक, m. and n.<BR> 1. A staff, MBh. 5, 5259.<BR> 2. The bow of Śiva, 13, 849.<BR> 3. The club of Śiva, 6, 2797.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकभृत्
पिनाकभृत् पिनाक-भृ + त्, m. A name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकि
पिनाकि पिनाकि, i. e. curtailed पिनाकिन्, m. A name of Śiva, MBh. 2, 1642.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकिन्
पिनाकिन् पिनाकिन्, i. e. पिनाक + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Armed with a पिनाक (a bow?), MBh. 6, 684.<BR> II. m. A name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्व्
पिन्व् पिन्व्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To sprinkle, to wet.<BR> 2. To cause to abound, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 6. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b " target="_blank">Page0552-b + 39</a>]<BR> 3. To cause to abound in milk, Chr. 296, 3 = Rigv. i. 112, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषु|पिपतिषुः
पिपतिषु पिपतिषु, i. e. पिपतिष, desider. of पत्, + उ, adj. Being about to fall, MBh. 3, 15471.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासा
पिपासा पिपासा, i. e. पिपास, desider. of 1. पा, + अ, f. Thirst, Nal. 10, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासावन्त्|पिपासावत्
पिपासावन्त् पिपासा + वन्त्, adj. Thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासु|पिपासुः
पिपासु पिपासु, i. e. पिपास, desider. of 1. पा, + उ, adj. Thirsty, Rām. 5, 19, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपील|पिपीलः
पिपील पिपील (perhaps redupl. पीड् + अ), m. An ant, MBh. 5, 5668.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलक|पिपीलकः
पिपीलक पिपील + क, m., f. लिका, An ant, MBh. 13, 5476.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलिक|पिपीलिकः
पिपीलिक पिपीलिक, i. e. पिपील + इक,<BR> I. m. An ant, MBh. 2, 1860.<BR> II. n. Gold carried by ants, MBh. 2, 1860 (cf. Herod. iii. 102).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पल|पिप्पलं|पिप्पलः
पिप्पल पिप्पल,<BR> I. m. The holy fig-tree, Ficus religiosa.<BR> II. f. ली, Long pepper.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. The fruit of the Ficus religiosa.<BR> 2. Sensual enjoyment, Bhāg. P. 3, 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्रीषु
पिप्रीषु पिप्रीषु, i. e. पिप्रीष, desider. of प्री, + उ, adj. Wishing to delight, MBh. 7, 6855.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्लु|पिप्लुः
पिप्लु पिप्लु, i. e. perhaps अपि-प्लु, m. A freckle, a mark, a mole, Nal. 17, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपिप्लु|मृगपिप्लुः
मृग- + पिप्लु मृग- + पिप्लु, m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पियाल|पियालः
पियाल पियाल, for original प्रियाल (q. cf.), m. A tree, Buchanania latifolia Roxb. n. Its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्
† पिल् पिल्, i. 10, Par. To throw, to cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलु|पिलुः
पिलु and पीलु पी̆लु, m. A certain tree; cf. पैलव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिव्
पिव् पिव्, see 1. प<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश्
पिश् पिश्, i. 6, पिंश, Par.<BR> 1. To adorn.<BR> 2. To form.<BR> --Cf. ποικίλος; Goth. faihu; O.H.G. fêh; A.S. faeger, fah, fag, fagian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश पिश् + अ, m. A deer, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्ग|पिशंग|पिशङ्गः
पिशङ्ग पिशङ्ग (vb. पिश्), adj., f. गी and गा, Of a tawny, or brown, or reddish colour, Kathās. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाच|पिशाचः
पिशाच पिशाच (cf. पिशुन), perhaps पिश-अञ्च् + अ,<BR> 1. m. A fiend, a malevolent being, Man. 1, 37.<BR> 2. f. ची, A female demon.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिशाच
स- + पिशाच स- + पिशाच, adj. together with Piśācas, Rām. 3, 53, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचक
पिशाचक पिशाच + क,<BR> 1. m. A fiend.<BR> 2. f. चिका, A female demon.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशापिशाचिका
आशा-पिशाचिका आशा-पिशाचिका, f. a demon like alluring and deceiving hope, Pañc. 252, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशित|पिशितं
पिशित पिश् + इत (cf. पिशङ्ग), n. Flesh, MBh. 4, 770.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन पिश् + उन,<BR> I. adj., f. ना.<BR> 1. Malignant, mischievous, Pañc. i. d. 1.<BR> 2. Betraying, Vikr. d. 32.<BR> 3. Backbiting, Pañc. i. d. 339.<BR> 4. Wicked, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 300.<BR> 5. Unkind, Hit. 56, 16.<BR> 6. One who excites hopes and disappoints them (ŚKD. sub रागारु).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A backbiter, Man. 4, 213.<BR> 2. A spy, an informer, 3, 161.<BR> III. n. Sycophancy, MBh. 14, 1025.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनता
पिशुनता पिशुन + ता, f. Backbiting, sycophancy, Bhartṛ. 2, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनय
पिशुनय पिशुनय, a denomin. derived from पिशुन with अय, Par. To betray, Śāk. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्
पिष् पिष्, ii. 7, पिनष्, पिंष्, Par.<BR> 1. To grind, to pound, MBh. 4, 632.<BR> 2. To bruise, to destroy (with gen.), Śiś. 1, 40. In epic poetry anomal. imperf. अपिंषत्, potent. पिषेयम्.<BR> --Ptcple. of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b " target="_blank">Page0553-b + 41</a>] the pf. pass. पिष्ट, n. The flour or meal of anything that is ground. न पिनष्टि पिष्टम्, He does not grind flour, i. e. he does no useless work, Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 24.<BR> --Caus. पेषय, To grind, to pound, MBh. 1, 3223.<BR> --† i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To injure.<BR> 2. To be strong.<BR> 3. To dwell.<BR> 4. To give, or take.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To grind.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To bruise, MBh. 3, 457.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To grind, to bruise, to crush, MBh. 2, 2377.<BR> 2. To rub together, MBh. 1, 5922 (the hands); 4, 465 (to gnash the teeth).<BR> --Caus. To destroy, Prab. 36, 11, v. r.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्,<BR> 1. To bruise, Hiḍ. 4, 35.<BR> 2. To rub together, Rām. 3, 55, 1.<BR> --With परि परि, To strike, Rām. 3, 51, 30.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To crush, Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 266.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To bruise, to destroy in one's turn, MBh. 12, 5206.<BR> 2. To grind, to bruise, MBh. 4, 361.<BR> 3. To rub together, 1, 2004.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To bruise, to destroy, Rām. 1, 45, 48.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pinso, pistor, pistillum, pistrinum, pistura, pîla, pîlum, pîlus; πτίσσω, πτίσμα, πίσος, πίσσος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टप|पिष्टपं|पिष्टपः
पिष्टप पिष्टप, n. and m. A world, a division of the universe, Man. 4, 231.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टप|त्रिपिष्टपं
त्रि- + पिष्टप त्रि- + पिष्टप, n. the mansion of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टमय
पिष्टमय पिष्ट + मय (vb. पिष्), adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Made of flour, MBh. 13, 5499.<BR> 2. Mixed with flour, MBh. 13, 6228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्
पिस् पिस्, i. 4, † i. 1, and पेस् पेस्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. पेसय,<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To injure or hurt.<BR> 3. To be strong.<BR> 4. To give or take.<BR> 5. To dwell.<BR> --Cf. पिष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्पृक्षु
पिस्पृक्षु पिस्पृक्षु, i. e. पिस्पृक्ष, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a " target="_blank">Page0554-a + 42</a>] desider. of स्पृश्, + उ, adj. Being about to touch (viz. water, i. e.) to make one's ablution, MBh. 12, 8338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी पी, i. 4, Ātm. (originally pass. of 1. पा), To drink.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To drink, MBh. 3, 13611.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठ|पीठं
पीठ पीठ n. and m.<BR> 1. A stool, a seat, a chair, MBh. 5, 1399; a bench.<BR> 2. A base or pedestal, Rājat. 2, 126.<BR> 3. The seat of a deity, an altar, Rājat. 5, 46; 473.<BR> 4. A kind of ornament, Hariv. 8063.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठ|पादपीठं|पादपीठः
पाद- + पीठ पाद- + पीठ, m. a footstool, Vikr. d. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपीठ|पूगपीठं|पूगपीठः
पूग- + पीठ पूग- + पीठ, n. a spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपीठ
भद्र- + पीठ भद्र- + पीठ, a throne, Vikr. 87, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गपीठ
रङ्ग- + पीठ रङ्ग- + पीठ, n. a place for dancing, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठक|पीठकं|पीठकः
पीठक पीठ + क,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A chair, a bench.<BR> 2. A saddle(?), MBh. 1, 3486.<BR> II. f. ठिका.<BR> 1. A bench.<BR> 2. The section of a literary work, Daśak. 48, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठग
पीठग पीठ-ग, adj. Lame (moving by means of a small car), MBh. 3, 871.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठमर्द|पीठमर्दः|पीठमर्द्द|पीठमर्द्दः
पीठमर्द पीठमर्द, i. e. पीठ-मृद् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Mounted on horses(?), MBh. 4, 674.<BR> 2. Very impudent, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 13(?).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The companion of a hero.<BR> 2. A dancing master of courtesans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठसर्प
पीठसर्प पीठ-सर्प, i. e. पीठ-सृप् + अ, adj. sbst. Lame, a cripple (cf. पीठग), MBh. 3, 1397.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्
पीड् पीड् (perhaps akin to पिष्), Ātm. To be squeezed (ved.).<BR> --Caus. or i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To squeeze, Bhartṛ. 2, 5.<BR> 2. To give pain, to afflict, Man. 5, 50.<BR> 3. To oppress, Chr. 30, 38.<BR> 4. To cover, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 14.<BR> 5. To hurt, MBh. 1, 7798.<BR> 6. To remove, Man. 1, 51.<BR> 7. To eclipse (in astrology).<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To press bard, Rām. 1, 68, 20 Gorr. अभि-पीडित, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-b " target="_blank">Page0554-b + 41</a>]<BR> 1. Trodden, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 33.<BR> 2. Afflicted, MBh. 3, 2490.<BR> 3. Oppressed, Chr. 40, 19.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, Caus. To crush, Hariv. 2936.<BR> --With अव अव, Caus.<BR> 1. To press down, MBh. 1, 6292.<BR> 2. To strike down, MBh. 14, 1944.<BR> 3. To oppose, 4, 1455. अवपीडित, Pressed, Mārk. P. 37, 18.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus.<BR> 1. To press hard, to give pain, MBh. 3, 12121.<BR> 2. To oppress. आपीडित, Adorned, MBh. 3, 2501 (rather आपीद + इत).<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To press on, Kumāras. 1, 40.<BR> 2. To tuck up, MBh. 3, 426.<BR> 3. To squeeze out, Suśr. 2, 47, 5.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus.<BR> 1. To afflict, Man. 8, 67.<BR> 2. To lay waste, Man. 7, 195.<BR> 3. To eclipse, Rām. 5, 73, 57.<BR> --With नि नि, Caus.<BR> 1. To press, Rām. 2, 25, 42 Gorr.<BR> 2. To impress, Rām. 1, 44, 1.<BR> 3. To embrace, Ragh. 2, 23.<BR> 4. To torment, MBh. 2, 6106.<BR> 5. with दण्डेन, To punish, to correct, Man. 7, 23.<BR> 6. with दन्तैस् and दन्तान्, To gnash the teeth, Pañc. 249, 7; 259, 10.<BR> --With अभिनि अभि-नि, Caus.<BR> 1. To squeeze, MBh. 3, 14759.<BR> 2. To torment, 1, 7009.<BR> --With उपनि उप-नि, Caus. To oppress, Chr. 58, 1.<BR> --With निस् निस्, Caus.<BR> 1. To squeeze out, Pañc. i. d. 161 (read निष्पी˚ instead of निपी˚, also i. d. 209).<BR> 2. To squeeze hard, MBh. 8, 1256; to compress, Rājat. 5, 88; to knock at (the door), Rām. 4, 9, 61.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus.<BR> 1. To press, to compress, Suśr. 1, 16, 6.<BR> 2. To embrace, Hit. 65, 12.<BR> 3. To torment violently, Pañc. 88, 4.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To press, MBh. 6, 3907.<BR> 2. To press hard, to oppress, MBh. 1, 5892.<BR> 3. To torment violently, Lass. 54, 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a " target="_blank">Page0555-a + 40</a>]<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To oppress, Rām. 2, 22, 23.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus.<BR> 1. To press, Rām. 5, 62, 11.<BR> 2. To press hard, MBh. 4, 980.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus.<BR> 1. To compress, Caurap. 3.<BR> 2. To press hard, to torment, Rām. 4, 21, 37.<BR> 3. To restrain, MBh. 13, 5893.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडन|पीडनं
पीडन पीड् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Pressing, squeezing, Rām. 5, 15, 29.<BR> 2. Inflicting pain, distressing, 2, 22, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपीडन
ग्रह- + पीडन ग्रह- + पीडन, n. pain, distress caused by an eclipse, Bhartṛ. 2, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडा
पीडा पीड् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Pain, anguish, suffering, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 753.<BR> 2. Infraction, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपीडा
ग्रह- + पीडा ग्रह- + पीडा, f. pain, distress caused by an eclipse, Dev. 12, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत पीत, adj., f. ता, Of a yellow colour, Rām. 2, 94, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आ- + पीत आ- + पीत, adj. yellowish, Rām. 2, 76, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतक|पीतकं|पीतकः
पीतक पीत + क,<BR> I. adj., f. तिका, Of a yellow colour, Rām. 6, 82, 60.<BR> II. f. तिका, Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतता
पीतता पीत + ता, f. Yellowness, yellow (the colour), Bhāṣāp. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीति|पीतिः
पीति पीति, i. e. 1. पा + ति, f. Drinking, a drink.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीति|सपीतिः
स- + पीति स- + पीति, f. drinking together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपीति|सोमपीतिः
सोम- + पीति सोम- + पीति, f. drinking the Soma juice, Chr. 288, 12 = Rigv. i. 48, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ|पीथं|पीथः
पीथ पीथ, i. e. 1. पा + थ,<BR> I. m. A drink.<BR> II. n. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपीथ|गोपीथं|गोपीथः
गो-पीथ गो-पीथ, i. e. 2. पा + थ, m. protection, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथिन्
पीथिन् i. e. पीथ + इन्; in कोश-पिथिन्, adj. Squandering away the treasury, Rājat. 5, 422; सोम-, m. Drinking the Soma juice, Utt. Rāmac. 7, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनता
पीनता पीन + ता (vb. प्यै), f. Fatness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2735.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनस|पीनसः
पीनस पीनस, probably अपि-नस् (= नासा) + अ, m.<BR> 1. Cold affecting the nose.<BR> 2. Catarrh, cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूष्
पीयूष् पीयूष्, a denomin. derived from पीयूष, Par. To turn into nectar, Śatr. 14, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूष|पीयूषं|पीयूषः
पीयूष पीयूष, probably पीवस् (ved. grease, cf. पीवन्), + अ,<BR> 1. n. The food or beverage of the gods, nectar, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 838.<BR> 2. m. and n. The milk of a cow during the first seven days after calving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषवर्षाय
पीयूषवर्षाय पीयूषवर्षाय, a denomin. derived from पीयूष-वर्ष with य, Ātm. To turn into a shower of nectar, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पील्
† पील् पील्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To impede, to obstruct.<BR> 2. To become stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलु|पीलुः
पीलु पीलु, perhaps पिष् + लु, m.<BR> 1. An elephant.<BR> 2. An arrow.<BR> 3. A tree, Careya arborea Roxb. n. Its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीव्
† पीव् पीव्, i. 1, Par. To be fat or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवन्
पीवन् पीवन्, i. e. probably प्यै (or पी, पा) + वन्, cf. the next,<BR> I. adj., f. ved. वरी.<BR> 1. Fat, large.<BR> 2. Strong.<BR> II. f. वरी, A proper name.<BR> --Cf. πίων, πίειρα, Πιερία (= पीवरी), πῖαρ, etc.; Lat. pinguis, pĭgere, pĭger.<BR> --Cf. प्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवन्त्|पीवत्
पीवन्त् पीवन्त्, original form of the last, Fat, MBh. 1, 700.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवर|पीवरः
पीवर पीवर, i. e. पीवन् + अ, with र् instead of n. adj., f. रा and री.<BR> 1. Fat, large, MBh. 5, 5437.<BR> 2. Dense, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवरत्व
पीवरत्व पीवर + त्व, n. Largeness, heaviness, Lass. 72, 10 (of deep sighs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवत्
पुंवत् पुंवत्, i. e. पुंस् + वत्, adv. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a " target="_blank">Page0556-a + 40</a>]<BR> 1. As a man, Ragh. 6, 20.<BR> 2. As on the birth of a male, Chr. 51, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चली
पुंश्चली पुंश्चली, i. e. पुंश्-चल् + अ + ई, adj. and sbst., f. A harlot, an unchaste woman, Man. 4, 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चलीय
पुंश्चलीय पुंश्चलीय, i. e. पुंश्चली + ईय, m. The son of a harlot, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1536.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्
1. पुंस् पुंस्, i. 10, Par. To grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्
2. पुंस् पुंस्, i. e. probably अपि-मन् + त्, the base of some cases is पुमांस्, पुम्, the nom. sing. पुमान्, voc. sing. पुमन्, m.<BR> 1. A man or male, Man. 2, 29.<BR> 2. A servant, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 38.<BR> 3. The soul, 7, 1, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्
अ- + पुंस् अ- + पुंस् and न-, m. an eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुंसी
सु-पुंस् + ई सु-पुंस् + ई, f. (a woman) having a good husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंस्
स्त्री- + पुंस् स्त्री- + पुंस्, m. one who has been changed from a female into a male, Chr. 50, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंसवन|पुंसवनं
पुंसवन पुंसवन, i. e. पुंस्-सवन, adj.<BR> 1. Causing the birth of a male child, Bhāg. P. 9, 6, 28.<BR> 2. n. with or without व्रत, A religious and domestic festival, held on the mother's perceiving the first signs of a living conception, Bhāg. P. 6, 19, 1.<BR> II. n. Fœtus, 5, 24, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्त्व|पुंस्त्वं
पुंस्त्व पुंस् + त्व, n. Virility, manhood, Yājñ. 1, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्त्व|अपुंस्त्वं
अ- + पुंस्त्व अ- + पुंस्त्व, n. being an eunuch, Indr. 5, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कश|पुक्कशः
पुक्कश पुक्कश, and पुक्कस पुक्कस, m. A mixed tribe; the offspring of a Niṣāda by a Śūdra female, Man. 10, 18. f. शी, सी, A female of this tribe, Man. 10, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कस|पुक्कसः
पुक्कस पुक्कस, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्ख|पुंख|पुंखं|पुंखः|पुङ्खः
पुङ्ख पुङ्ख, m. The lower part of an arrow, containing the feathers and the shaft, Śāk. d. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्खित|पुंखित
पुङ्खित पुङ्खित, i. e. पुङ्ख + इत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b " target="_blank">Page0556-b + 41</a>] adj. Endowed with the पुङ्ख (see the last), Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 774.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गव|पुंगव|पुङ्गवः
पुङ्गव पुङ्गव, i. e. पुंस्-गव,<BR> 1. m. A bull Hariv. 3796.<BR> 2. As latter part of comp. words, Excellent, e. g. गज-, m. A pre-eminent elephant, Bhartṛ. 2, 26. नर-, m. An excellent warrior, Chr. 21, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छ|पुच्छं|पुच्छः
पुच्छ पुच्छ, m. and n.<BR> 1. A tail, Draup. 5, 8.<BR> 2. The hinder part, MBh. 7, 206.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably πῡγή, perhaps πύματος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपुच्छ
काल- + पुच्छ काल- + पुच्छ, m. a certain animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुच्छ|गोपुच्छः
गो- + पुच्छ गो- + पुच्छ, 1. m. and n. a cow's tail. 2. m. a kind of monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिपुच्छ
दधि- + पुच्छ दधि- + पुच्छ, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तपुच्छ|हस्तपुच्छं
हस्त- + पुच्छ हस्त- + पुच्छ, n. the hand below the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुछ्|पुच्छ्
† पुछ् पुछ्, v. r. of युछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्ज|पुंज|पुंजः|पुञ्जः
पुञ्ज पुञ्ज, m.<BR> 1. A heap, a mass, MBh. 3, 9957.<BR> 2. A quantity, Mark. P. 8, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जय
पुञ्जय पुञ्जय, a denomin. derived from the last with अय, To heap. पुञ्जित, Heaped, Utt. Rāmac. 126, 2; put together, Rājat. 3, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जशस्
पुञ्जशस् पुञ्ज + शस्, adv. In heaps, MBh. 2, 1860.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट्
पुट् पुट्, i. 6, Par. † To embrace.<BR> --† i. 1, Par. To grind, to pound (v. r.).<BR> --† i. 10, पुटय, Par. To fasten, to bind together.<BR> --† i. 10, पोटय, Par.<BR> 1. To speak or shine.<BR> 2. To reduce to powder, to grind.<BR> 3. To be small.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, pass. To peel, to lose the skin, Suśr. 1, 302, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट|पुटं|पुटः
पुट पुट, m., f. टी, and n.<BR> 1. A concavity.<BR> 2. A cup or concavity made of a leaf folded or doubled, MBh. 9, 2827.<BR> 3. A shallow cup or receptacle, as the hollow of the hand, Pañc. 44, 24.<BR> 4. A vessel, or basket made of leaves, Man. 6, 28.<BR> 5. A cover, a covering, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a " target="_blank">Page0557-a + 41</a>] Utt. Rāmac. 50, 8.<BR> 6. A cloth worn to cover the privities.<BR> II. m. A horse's hoof.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरपुट
अधर- + पुट अधर- + पुट and ओष्ठ-, m. or n. the cup-like lips, Śṛṅgārat. 7; Śāk. d. 182 (in a comp. adj. having pale-red cup-like lips).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलिपुट
कृत-अञ्जलि- + पुट कृत-अञ्जलि- + पुट, adj. putting the hands together, Rām. 1, 9, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनपुट
नयन- + पुट नयन- + पुट, an eyelid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासापुट|नासापुटः
नासा- + पुट नासा- + पुट, m. the nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपुट|पक्षपुटः
पक्ष- + पुट पक्ष- + पुट, m. a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुट|भांडपुट|भाण्डपुटः
भाण्ड- + पुट भाण्ड- + पुट, m. a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रपुट|मूत्रपुटं
मूत्र- + पुट मूत्र- + पुट, n. the lower belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटक|पुटकं
पुटक पुट + क, n. and f. टिका (Pañc. 265, 5),<BR> 1. A concavity.<BR> 2. A bag or vessel or concavity made of a leaf doubled over in a funnel-like shape, Rājat. 1, 213.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणपुटक
घ्राण- + पुटक घ्राण- + पुटक, m. the nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट्ट्
† पुट्ट् पुट्ट्, i. 10, Par. To be small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुड्
† पुड् पुड्, also बुड् बुड्, and मुड् मुड्, i. 6, Par. To emit, to leave.<BR> --Cf. 2. मुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्
† पुण् पुण्, i. 6, Par. To be pure or virtuous, to do a pious or holy act.<BR> --Cf. पूल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ट्|पुंट्
† पुण्ट् पुण्ट्(?), i. 10, Par. To speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्|पुंड्
† पुण्ड् पुण्ड्, see 2. मुट् and मुण्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीक|पुंडरीक|पुंडरीकं|पुण्डरीकं|पुण्डरीकः
पुण्डरीक पुण्डरीक,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. The white lotus flower.<BR> 2. A lotus in general, Rām. 2, 95, 3 Gorr.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A kind of sacrifice, MBh. 3, 1133.<BR> 2. A kind of rice.<BR> 3. A kind of leprosy.<BR> 4. The elephant of the south-east quarter, Ragh. 18, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीयक|पुण्डरीयकं
पुण्डरीयक पुण्डरीयक, m. The name of a divine being, MBh. 13, 4359.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्र|पुंड्र|पुंड्रः|पुण्ड्रः
पुण्ड्र पुण्ड्र, m.<BR> 1. pl. The name of a people and their country, the greater part of Bengal and part of Behar.<BR> 2. A kind of sugar-cane.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b " target="_blank">Page0557-b + 42</a>] (and n.), A mark or line made on the forehead with sandal.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्र|त्रिपुंड्र|त्रिपुण्ड्रं
त्रि- + पुण्ड्र त्रि- + पुण्ड्र, n. three horizontal marks made across the forehead, especially by the followers of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रक|पुंड्रक|पुंड्रकः|पुण्ड्रकः
पुण्ड्रक पुण्ड्र + क, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people = Puṇḍra, Man. 10, 44.<BR> 2. A sort of sugar-cane.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतत्रिपुण्ड्रक
कृत-त्रि- + पुण्ड्रक कृत-त्रि- + पुण्ड्रक, adj. provided with the three horizontal marks (see the last), Hariv. 15426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्य|पुण्यं
पुण्य पुण्य, probably from पुष्,<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Beautiful, Nal. 12, 37.<BR> 2. Pure, Man. 9, 186; virtuous, Man. 2, 106.<BR> 3. Fragrant, Chr. 37, 6.<BR> 4. Producing bliss, propitious, Man. 2, 30.<BR> 5. Holy; festival, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 5.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Virtue, Indr. 2, 4.<BR> 2. A good or meritorious act, Rājat. 5, 72.<BR> 3. Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यक|पुण्यकं|पुण्यकः
पुण्यक पुण्य + क, n.<BR> 1. A festival, MBh. 15, 407.<BR> 2. A ceremony performed by a woman in order to keep the love of her husband and to get a son, 1, 817.<BR> 3. The observance of this ceremony, 1, 760.<BR> 4. The presents given to the woman on this occasion, Hariv. 7654 (m., corr. perhaps इदं for इमं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकृत्
पुण्यकृत् पुण्य-कृ + त्, adj. Virtuous, pious, Bhag. 6, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यता
पुण्यता पुण्य + ता, f., and पुण्यत्व पुण्य + त्व, n. Purity, holiness, MBh. 1, 557.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदुह्
पुण्यदुह् पुण्य-दुह्, adj. Yielding bliss, MBh. 7, 2181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभरित
पुण्यभरित पुण्यभरित, i. e. पुण्य-भर + इत, adj. Abounding in holiness or bliss, Śatr. 1, 297.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यवन्त्|पुण्यवत्
पुण्यवन्त् पुण्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Virtuous, Mārk. P. 20, 23.<BR> 2. Wellfated, Hit. 14, 21; with abl. Happier, Hit. i. d. 38, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याह|पुण्याहं
पुण्याह पुण्याह, i. e. पुण्य + अह. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a " target="_blank">Page0558-a + 45</a>] n. A good or happy day; with वाचय, To wish somebody a happy day, MBh. 2, 1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्
पुत् पुत्, A hell (to which the childless are condemned), Man. 9, 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तिका
पुत्तिका पुत्तिका, f.<BR> 1. A termite, Man. 4, 238.<BR> 2. A kind of bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्र|पुत्त्रः|पुत्रः
पुत्र पुत्र, perhaps पू + त्र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A son, Man. 9, 138.<BR> 2. du. Two sons.<BR> 3. A son and a daughter, Nal. 23, 26.<BR> 4. pl. Children, young ones, MBh. 12, 3306.<BR> II. f. त्री, A daughter, Pañc. 190, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्र|अपुत्रः
अ- + पुत्र अ- + पुत्र, adj., f. रा, sonless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यपुत्र|आर्यपुत्रः|आर्य्यपुत्त्रः|आर्य्यपुत्र
आर्य- + पुत्र आर्य- + पुत्र, m. the son of an Ārya, used to denote: 1. a prince, Rām. 6, 8, 38. 2. the son of an elder brother, 2, 23, 26. 3. a husband (by his wife), 3, 49, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपुत्र|कुलपुत्रः
कुल- + पुत्र कुल- + पुत्र, m. the son of a respectable family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिपुत्र|गाधिपुत्रः
गाधि- + पुत्र गाधि- + पुत्र, m. the son of Gādhi, i. e. Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणपुत्र
तरुण- + पुत्र तरुण- + पुत्र, adj., f. रा, having young ones, Rām. 3, 53, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपुत्र
जीव- + पुत्र जीव- + पुत्र, adj. one of whom a son or children are alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्याःपुत्र
दास्यास्- + पुत्र दास्यास्- + पुत्र (gen. sing. of दासी, see दास), m. the son of a female slave, a contemptible person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरापुत्र|धरापुत्रः
धरा- + पुत्र धरा- + पुत्र, m. the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपुत्री
नन्द-पुत्री नन्द-पुत्री, f. a name of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापुत्र
निशा- + पुत्र निशा- + पुत्र, m. pl. a class of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्र
पाटलि- + पुत्र पाटलि- + पुत्र, n. the name of a town, the Palibothra of the ancients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पुत्र|मरुत्पुत्त्रः|मरुत्पुत्रः
मरुत्- + पुत्र मरुत्- + पुत्र, m. Bhīmasena, the second of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुत्र|राजपुत्त्रः|राजपुत्रः
राजपुत्र राजपुत्र, i. e. राजन्-,<BR> I. m. 1. the son of a king. 2. a man of the military tribe. 3. a soldier. 4. the planet Mercury.<BR> II. f. त्री. 1. a princess. 2. a woman of the Kṣatriya tribe. 3. a kind of brass. 4. the musk shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुत्र|लक्ष्मीपुत्त्रः|लक्ष्मीपुत्रः
लक्ष्मी- + पुत्र लक्ष्मी- + पुत्र, m. 1. Kāma. 2. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापुत्र|शिलापुत्त्रः|शिलापुत्रः
शिला- + पुत्र शिला- + पुत्र, m. a muller or roller for grinding condiments on a flat stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुत्र
स- + पुत्र स- + पुत्र, adj. together with (his) son, Rājat. 5, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुत्र|सत्पुत्त्रः|सत्पुत्रः
सत्पुत्र सत्प्˚, i. e. सन्त्-, adj. having sons living, Man. 9, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यपुत्र|सूर्यपुत्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्त्र|सूर्य्यपुत्त्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्र
सूर्य- + पुत्र सूर्य- + पुत्र,<BR> I. m. 1. Varuṇa. 2. Saturn, Pañc. i. d. 238. 3. Yama.<BR> II. f. री. 1. lightning. 2. the Yamunā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रक|पुत्त्रकः|पुत्रकः
पुत्रक पुत्र + क,<BR> I. m. A son, Man. 2, 151.<BR> II. f. त्रिका and त्रका.<BR> 1. A daughter, Pañc. 190, 2.<BR> 2. A daughter appointed to raise issue for her father, Man. 9, 127.<BR> 3. A doll, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 635.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रक|अपुत्रकः
अ- + पुत्रक अ- + पुत्रक, adj. sonless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्रक|कृत्रिमपुत्रकः
कृत्रिम- + पुत्रक कृत्रिम- + पुत्रक, m. and f. त्रिका, a doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्रक
पाटलि- + पुत्रक पाटलि- + पुत्रक, n. the name of a town, the Palibothra of the ancients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुत्रक|मुनिपुत्त्रकः|मुनिपुत्रकः
मुनि- + पुत्रक मुनि- + पुत्रक, m. a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रपुत्रिका
वस्त्र-पुत्रिका वस्त्र-पुत्रिका, f. a doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रता
पुत्रता पुत्र + ता, f., and पुत्रत्व पुत्र + त्व, n. The state of a son, Rām. 1, 20, 1 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रवत्|पुत्रवन्त्
पुत्रवत् पुत्र + वत्, adv. As on the birth of a son, Chr. 50, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रवन्त्|पुत्रवत्
पुत्रवन्त् पुत्र + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having a son or sons, or children, Man. 9, 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिन्
पुत्रिन् पुत्रिन्, i. e. पुत्र + इन्, adj., f. इणी, The same, Man. 9, 182; Vikr. d. 152.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुत्रिन्
स- + पुत्रिन् स- + पुत्रिन्, adj. with one's sons, Hariv. 11842.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिय
पुत्रिय पुत्रिय, i. e. पुत्र + इय, adj., f. या, Referring to a son, procuring a son, Rām. 1, 15, 2 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रीय|पुत्त्रीयं
पुत्रीय पुत्रीय, i. e. पुत्र + इय, adj., f. या, Relating to a son or child, procuring a son, Rām. 1, 14, 1 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ्
1. पुथ् पुथ्, i. 4, Par. To hurt, to kill.<BR> --Caus. पोथय.<BR> 1. To kill, MBh. 4, 727.<BR> 2. To bruise, 4, 643.<BR> 3. To overpower (sound), Kathās. 34, 257. पोथित, Annihilated, MBh. 4, 795.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To crush, Hariv. 3347.<BR> --With अव अव, Caus. The same, Hariv. 5611.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. The same.<BR> --With नि नि, Caus. To strike down, Hariv. 4525.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. To push on, Rām. 6, 25, 7.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus. To bruise, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a " target="_blank">Page0559-a + 40</a>] Dev. 2, 57.<BR> --With सम् सम्, The same, MBh. 7, 1935.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ्
† 2. पुथ् पुथ्, i. 10, Par. To speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गल|पुद्गलः
पुद्गल पुद्गल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, Beautiful, Mārk. P. 99, 57.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The body, Hit. i. d. 41 (read पुद्गले).<BR> 2. The soul.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्
पुनर् पुनर्, adv.<BR> 1. Back, Chr. 8, 27.<BR> 2. Again, Man. 2, 120.<BR> 3. In an opposite way, Pañc. 263, 15.<BR> 4. But, Nal. 17, 15; on the contrary.<BR> 5. Nevertheless, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1964.<BR> 6. With preceding किम्,<BR> a. How much more, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 504.<BR> b. How much less, Pañc. i. d. 452.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुनर्
पुनः-पुनर् पुनः-पुनर्, i. e. पुनर्-, adv. 1. repeatedly, Man. 1, 28. 2. again and again, Utt. Rāmac. 82, 12; every day, Chr. 295, 10 = Rigv. i. 92, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरर्थिता
पुनरर्थिता पुनरर्थिता, i. e. पुनर्-अर्थिन् + ता, f. Renewed begging, Bhāg. P. 5, 19, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्ति|पुनरुक्तिः
पुनरुक्ति पुनर्-उक्ति, f.<BR> 1. Tautology.<BR> 2. A useless word, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 462.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भू
पुनर्भू पुनर्-भू,<BR> I. adj., n. भु, Reborn, regenerated.<BR> II. f. A virgin widow remarried, Yājñ. 1, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्थ्
† पुन्थ् पुन्थ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt.<BR> 2. To give pain.<BR> 3. To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नाग|पुंनाग|पुन्नागः
पुन्नाग पुन्नाग, m.<BR> 1. i. e. पुंस्-नाग, A pre-eminent man.<BR> 2. A white elephant.<BR> 3. A tree, from the flowers of which is prepared a yellowish dye, Rottleria tinctoria.<BR> 4. A white lotus.<BR> 5. Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नामन्|पुंनामन्
पुन्नामन् पुन्नामन्, i. e.<BR> 1. पुंस्-नामन्, adj. Having a male name.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b " target="_blank">Page0559-b + 43</a>] पुत्-नामन्, adj. called पुत् (q. cf.), Man. 9, 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्पुट
पुप्पुट पुप्पुट, m. The name of a disease, a swelling at the palate or the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुस|पुप्फुसः
पुप्फुस पुप्फुस, and फुप्पुस फुप्फुस, m. The lungs.<BR> --Cf. ϕῦσα, ϕυσάω, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुम्
पुम् पुम्, and पुमांस् पुमांस्, see पुंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
1. पुर् पुर् (probably vb. पॄ), f.<BR> 1. A town, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 12.<BR> 2. The body, 2, 10, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुर्
त्रि- + पुर् त्रि- + पुर्, f. pl. three forts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
† 2. पुर् पुर्, i. 6, Par. To go at the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर पुर, i. e. probably पॄ + अ,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A fortified town, Man. 7, 70.<BR> 2. A town, 8, 386.<BR> 3. The town, κατ̕ ἐξοχήν i. e. Pāṭaliputra.<BR> 4. An abode, Bhāg. P. 5, 11, 9.<BR> 5. An upper story.<BR> 6. The body, Bhāg. P. 5, 11, 5.<BR> 7. A kind of Cyperus.<BR> 8. Skin.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A sort of resin, Bdellium.<BR> 2. The name of a demon.<BR> III. f. रा, A perfume.<BR> IV. f. री (also रि).<BR> 1. A town, Megh. 31.<BR> 2. The body, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πόλις, πτόλις, perhaps also πύργος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपुरी
अङ्ग-पुरी अङ्ग-पुरी, f. the capital of the Aṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपुर
अमर-पुर अमर-पुर, n. and -पुरी, f. the residence of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिपुर
अवन्ति- + पुर अवन्ति- + पुर, n. the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापुर
कन्या-पुर कन्या-पुर, n. a gynæceum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनपुर
काञ्चन-पुर काञ्चन-पुर, n. the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिपुरी
काशि-पुरी काशि-पुरी, f. the capital of the Kāśis, i. e. Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारीपुर
कुमारी-पुर कुमारी-पुर, n. a gynæceum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमपुर|कुसुमपुरं
कुसुम-पुर कुसुम-पुर, n. a surname of Pāṭaliputra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपुर
गज-पुर गज-पुर, n. a name of Hāstinapura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्वपुर|गंधर्वपुर
गन्धर्व-पुर गन्धर्व-पुर, n. a mirage, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुर|गोपुरं
गो- + पुर गो- + पुर, n. 1. a town-gate, Rām. 5, 27, 20. 2. a gate in general, Kir. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डरद्वारगोपुर
पाण्डर-द्वार-गो- + पुर पाण्डर-द्वार-गो- + पुर, adj. f. रा, having white doors and towngates, Rām. 5, 9, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं|त्रिपुरः
त्रि-पुर त्रि-पुर,<BR> I. n. three [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a " target="_blank">Page0560-a + 43</a>] forts.<BR> II. m. the name of a demon.<BR> III. f. रा. 1. the name of a town. 2. a form of Durgā.<BR> IV. f. री, the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुर|दशपुरं
दश(न्)-पुर दश(न्)-पुर, n. the name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुर
देव-पुर देव-पुर, n. the residence of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपुर|नागपुरं
नाग-पुर नाग-पुर, n. a name of Hāstinapura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपुर
पञ्च(न्)-पुर पञ्च(न्)-पुर, n., परिहास-पुर, n., and फल-पुर, n., names of towns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुरी
महा-पुरी महा-पुरी, f. a great town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मपुर
रुक्म- + पुर रुक्म- + पुर, n. the name of a fabulous town, Pañc. 84, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापुर|शाखापुरं
शाखा- + पुर शाखा- + पुर, n. a suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरपुर
शूर- + पुर शूर- + पुर, n. the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यपुर
हिरण्य- + पुर हिरण्य- + पुर, n. the town of the Asuras, Arj. 10, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःसर|पुरःसरः
पुरःसर पुरःसर, i. e. पुरस्-सृ + अ, adj., f. री, and sbst.<BR> 1. One who goes first or before, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 27; a leader, a preceder, MBh. 4, 630; Śāk. d. 77.<BR> 2. When latter part of a comp. adj. the fem. ends in रा, Preceded by, attended with, with; e. g. प्रिय-आख्यान-, adj. Preceded by agreeable news, i. e. with agreeable news, Rām. 1, 10, 31 Gorr.<BR> 3. रम्, adv. Preceded by, with; e. g. प्रणिपात-पुरःसरम्, With a prostration, Mārk. P. 77, 30 (laying herself at his feet); after, Pañc. 16, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरग
पुरग पुरग, i. e. probably पुरस्-ग, adj. Inclined to, Mārk. P. 64, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरजित्
पुरजित् पुर-जि + त्, m.<BR> 1. A name of Śiva.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंजन|पुरञ्जन|पुरंजनः|पुरञ्जनः
पुरंजन पुरंजन, i. e. पुर + म्-जन् + अ,<BR> I. m. The soul, personified as a king, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 9 sqq.<BR> II. f. नी, The intellect, personified as his queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंजय|पुरञ्जय|पुरञ्जयः
पुरंजय पुरंजय, i. e. पुर + म्-जि + अ, m. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुरंजय
पर- + पुरंजय पर- + पुरंजय, adj. conquering the enemy's towns, Nal. 20, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरट|पुरटं
पुरट पुरट, n. Gold, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतस्
पुरतस् पुर + तस् (cf. पुरा), adv.<BR> 1. Before, in front (with gen.), Rām. 2, 39, 6.<BR> 2. Forward, Vikr. 65, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंदर|पुरन्दर|पुरन्दरं|पुरंदरः|पुरन्दरः
पुरंदर पुरंदर, i. e. पुर + म्-दॄ + अ, m. Destroyer of castles, a name of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंधि
पुरंधि पुरंधि,<BR> I. f. Understanding, wisdom.<BR> II. adj. Intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंध्रि|पुरन्ध्रि|पुरंध्रिः|पुरन्ध्रिः
पुरंध्रि and पुरंध्री पुरंध्री̆, i. e. पुर + म्-धृ + ई, and the final shortened, f. A respectable matron, Ragh. 7, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्चरणता
पुरश्चरणता पुरश्चरणता, i. e. पुरस्-चरण + ता, f. Preparation, MBh. 12, 13206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्
पुरस् पुर + स् (cf. पुरा),<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Forward.<BR> 2. Before, in front, in presence, Śāk. 29, 1; Pañc. i. d. 135.<BR> 3. First, Śāk. d. 33.<BR> 4. Eastward, from the east, MBh. 7, 2349.<BR> II. prep. with the gen., Before, Megh. 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πάρος, πρόσθε, πρόσθιος, etc., perhaps πρες, in πρέσβυς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतःपुरस्
दक्षिणतस्-पुरस् दक्षिणतस्-पुरस्, adv. south-eastward, MBh. 2, 1120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कार|पुरस्कारः
पुरस्कार पुरस्-कार, m.<BR> 1. Preference, Mālav. 19, 6.<BR> 2. Deference, Rām. 1, 80, 11 Gorr.<BR> 3. As latter part of comp. adj. Preceded by, joined with; e. g. सुरा-सव-, adj. Together with spirituous liquors, MBh. 13, 4737.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्क्रिया
पुरस्क्रिया पुरस्-क्रिया, f. Deference, Ragh. 4, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्तात्
पुरस्तात् पुरस्-तात् (तात्, an old abl. of तद्),<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Before, in front, Bhag. 11, 40.<BR> 2. First, preceding, Rām. 2, 80, 5.<BR> 3. Forward, Vikr. 31, 4.<BR> 4. Formerly, MBh. 1, 735.<BR> 5. Eastward, in the east, from the east, Megh. 15.<BR> II. prep. with gen. and abl. Before, Hit. 8, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरा
पुरा पुरा (old instrum. sing. of a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a " target="_blank">Page0561-a + 42</a>] base पुर, for पर, cf. पुरस्; उ is changed to अ by the influence of the preceding प्);<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Formerly, Man. 1, 119.<BR> 2. Of old, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1231.<BR> 3. With न, Never, MBh. 9, 1806.<BR> 4. First.<BR> 5. Soon.<BR> II. prep. with abl., Before, Arj. 4, 20.<BR> --Cf. πάροι (old loc.) in πάροιθε, παροίτερος, πάλαι (old dat.), παλαιός, etc.; perhaps also πέλας with πλησίος, etc.; Goth. faura and faur; A.S. for, fora-, fore-; Lat. por-, e. g. in por-tendere, and probably also prō-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण पुराण, i. e. पुरा + न,<BR> I. adj., f. (णा and) णी.<BR> 1. Primeval, Man. 5, 23.<BR> 2. Old, ancient. Mālav. 4, 2.<BR> 3. Aged, Vikr. d. 9; worn out.<BR> II. n. A tale of past ages; old history, legends; a sacred work treating for the most part of the creation, the destruction and renovation of worlds, the genealogy of gods, etc. There are eighteen acknowledged Purāṇas.<BR> III. m. A coin of a certain weight, Man. 8, 136.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुराण
निष्पुराण निष्पुराण, i. e. निस्-, adj. New, unheard of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातन|पुरातनः
पुरातन पुरा + तन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Old, ancient, Man. 3, 213.<BR> II. n. An old tale, Rām. 1, 45, 13.<BR> --Cf. Lat. (regarding the form) prôtenus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराराति|पुरारातिः
पुराराति पुराराति, and पुरारि पुरारि, i. e. पुर-अराति and -अरि, m. Names of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराविद्
पुराविद् पुरा-विद्, adj. Knowing the past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरि|पुरिः
पुरि पुरि, and पुरी पुरी, see पुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीतत्
पुरीतत् पुरीतत्, probably पुर् + इ -तन् + त्, n.<BR> 1. An entrail near the heart.<BR> 2. The entrails in general, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीष|पुरीषं
पुरीष पुरीष (akin to पॄ),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Fæces, excrements, Man. 5, 138.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b " target="_blank">Page0561-b + 41</a>] The remains of food (in a pot), Bhāg. P. 5, 9, 12.<BR> II. f. षी (perhaps f. of पुरीष्य), The name of a religious ceremony, 3, 12, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषण|पुरीषणः
पुरीषण पुरीषण, i. e. पुरीषय (a denomin. derived from पुरीष with the aff. अय) + अन, n.<BR> 1. Evacuation of excrements.<BR> 2. Fæces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषाधान
पुरीषाधान पुरीष-आ:धान, n. The strait-gut, Yājñ. 3, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषम|पुरीषमः
पुरीषम पुरीषम (akin to पुरीष), m. The black kidney bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीष्य
पुरीष्य पुरीष्य, adj. Epithet of fire.<BR> --Cf. पुरीष, f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरु|पुरुः
पुरु पुरु, in the Veda also पूरु, i. e. पॄ + उ<BR> I. adj., f. पुर्वी.<BR> 1. Much, many.<BR> 2. Exceeding. adv. Very, exceedingly.<BR> II. also पूरु, m. The name of an old prince, Śāk. 7, 4.<BR> --Cf. πολύ; Goth. filu; A.S. fela, feala; comparat. πλεῖον; Lat. plus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुकुत्स
पुरुकुत्स पुरु-कुत्स, m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंशक|पुरुदंशकः
पुरुदंशक पुरु-दंश् + अक, m. A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंशस्
पुरुदंशस् पुरु-दंश् + अस्, m., nom. sing. शा, A name of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुधा
पुरुधा पुरु + धा, adv. Manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुष|पुरुषः
पुरुष पुरुष, and sometimes पूरुष,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A man generally or individually, a male, mankind, Man. 1, 32.<BR> 2. Punishment personified, Man. 7, 17.<BR> 3. An attendant, a functionary, 8, 43.<BR> 4. The first man, Hariv. 51.<BR> 5. The soul, Yājñ. 3, 194.<BR> 6. The universal soul, the supreme Being, Mārk. P. 26, 21; Man. 1, 11.<BR> 7. A principle, Man. 1, 19.<BR> 8. A tree, Rottleria tinctoria.<BR> 9. A proper name.<BR> II. f. षी, A female, Bhāg. P. 5, 24, 17.<BR> III. n.(?). A name of the mountain Meru.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-a " target="_blank">Page0562-a + 44</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपुरुष|अदृष्टपुरुषः
अ-दृष्ट- + पुरुष अ-दृष्ट- + पुरुष (vb. दृश्), adj. (viz. संधि), a kind of alliance where one party alone settles for the other, on the condition that the enemy has to disburse the expenses of the expedition, Hit. iv. d. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरपूरुष|अन्तरपूरुषः
अन्तर-पूरुष अन्तर-पूरुष, m. the soul, Man. 8, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुष|आदिपुरुषः
आदि-पुरुष आदि-पुरुष, m. the first man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिपुरुष
उपरि- + पुरुष उपरि- + पुरुष, m. a rider, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपुरुष|एकपुरुषः
एक- + पुरुष एक- + पुरुष,<BR> I. m. the one universal soul, Vikr. d. 1.<BR> II. adj. consisting only of one person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंपुरुष|किम्पुरुष|किम्पुरुषः
किंपुरुष किंपुरुष, i. e. किम्-, m. 1. a class of horse-faced beings belonging to the suite of Kuvera, Kumāras. 1, 11. 2. one of the portions into which the world is divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपुरुष|कुलपुरुषः
कुल- + पुरुष कुल- + पुरुष, m. a polite man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपुरुष|गूढपुरुषः
गूढ- + पुरुष गूढ- + पुरुष (vb. गुह्), m. a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुष|तुलापुरुषः
तुला- + पुरुष तुला- + पुरुष, m. 1. a person weighed in a balance, i. e. a present of gold or other precious things of equal weight. 2. the name of a penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकारिपुरुष
धर्माधिकारिपुरुष धर्माधिकारिपुरुष, i. e. धर्म-अधि-कारिन्-, m. a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुष|निष्पुरुषः
निष्पुरुष निष्पुरुष, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. not having produced male children, Man. 3, 7. 2. devoid of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिपुरुष|प्रकृतिपुरुषः
प्रकृति- + पुरुष प्रकृति- + पुरुष, m. a minister, Megh. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपुरुष|प्रमाणपुरुषः
प्रमाण- + पुरुष प्रमाण- + पुरुष, m. an arbitrator, Hit. 116, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलपुरुष|मूलपुरुषः
मूल- + पुरुष मूल- + पुरुष, m. the last male of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिकपुरुष
रक्षिक- + पुरुष रक्षिक- + पुरुष, m. a policeman, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुरुष
राज(न्)- + पुरुष राज(न्)- + पुरुष, m. 1. a servant of the king. 2. A guard, a watchman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुरुष|सत्पुरुषः
सत्पुरुष सत्पुरुष, i. e. सन्त्-, m. an honest man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषक|पुरुषकं|पुरुषकः
पुरुषक पुरुष + क, n. Rearing as a horse, standing like a man on two feet, Śiś. 5, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकार|पुरुषकारः
पुरुषकार पुरुष-कार, m.<BR> 1. Any act of man, care, Man. 8, 232.<BR> 2. The exertion of man (opposite to fate), Yājñ. 1, 348.<BR> 3. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषता
पुरुषता पुरुष + ता, f., and पुरुषत्व पुरुष + त्व, n. Manhood, MBh. 13, 552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषन्ति
पुरुषन्ति पुरुषन्ति, m. A proper [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b " target="_blank">Page0562-b + 42</a>] name, Chr. 298, 23 = Rigv. 1, 112, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषशीर्षक|पुरुषशीर्षकः
पुरुषशीर्षक पुरुष-शीर्ष + क (m. n.?), The name of a thief's instrument, Daśak. 71, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषादत्व
पुरुषादत्व पुरुषादत्व, i. e. पुरुष-आद + त्व, n. State or condition of a man-eater, or demon, MBh. 13, 326.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषान्तर|पुरुषांतर
पुरुषान्तर पुरुषान्तर, i. e. पुरुष-अन्तर,<BR> I. n. A following generation, Mārk. P. 118, 31.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Man (opposed to deities), Vikr. d. 35.<BR> 2. A treaty by which is stipulated that the affairs of the one shall be settled by warriors selected from both parties, Kām. Nītis. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाय
पुरुषाय पुरुषाय, a denomin. derived from पुरुष with य, Ātm. To behave like a man, MBh. 12, 8102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूरवस्
पुरूरवस् पुरूरवस्, m. The name of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूवसु
पुरूवसु पुरूवसु, i. e. पुरु-वसु, adj. Abounding in riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोग|पुरोगः
पुरोग पुरोग, and पुरोगम पुरोगम, i. e. पुरस्-ग and -गम,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Going before, preceding, Nal. 4, 20.<BR> 2. Chief, Ragh. 6, 55.<BR> II. m. A leader, MBh. 3, 2522.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपुरोगम
अग्नि-पुरोगम अग्नि-पुरोगम, adj. led by Agni, Nal. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिपुरोग
प्रीति-पुरोग प्रीति-पुरोग, adj. accompanied by love, friendly, MBh. 12, 10935.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिष्ठिरपुरोगम
युधिष्ठिर-पुरोगम युधिष्ठिर-पुरोगम, adj. having Yudhiṣṭhira as leader, led on by Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोजन्मता
पुरोजन्मता पुरोजन्मता, i. e. पुरस्-जन्मन् + ता, f. Priority of birth, Ragh. 16, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश|पुरोडाशः
पुरोडाश पुरोडाश, i. e. पुरस्-दाश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A kind of cake made of rice meal, offered in oblations to the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a " target="_blank">Page0563-a + 40</a>] gods, Man. 6, 11.<BR> 2. An oblation to deities, Man. 5, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाशीय
पुरोडाशीय पुरोडाशीय, i. e. पुरोडाश + ईय, adj., f. या, Relating to the sacrificial cakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोध
पुरोध पुरोध = पुरोधस्, MBh. 3, 10635.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधस्
पुरोधस् पुरोधस्, i. e. पुरस् and vb. धा, m. The family or domestic priest of a prince, Śāk. 71, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधिका
पुरोधिका पुरोधिका (probably पुरस्-धा + इका), f. A favourite wife, Hariv. 7817.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहित|पुरोहितः
पुरोहित पुरोहित, see धा with पुरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्व्
† पुर्व्, पूर्व् पू̆र्व्, and पूर्ब् पूर्ब्, i. 1, Par. To fill (cf. पॄ).<BR> --i. 10, Par. To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्
† पुल् पुल्, i. 1, and 6, and 10, Par. To be great or large, to be lofty or high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल पुल,<BR> I. adj. Extensive.<BR> II. m. Erection of the hairs of the body, considered as proof of exquisite delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलक|पुलकं|पुलकः
पुलक पुल + क, m.<BR> 1. Erection of the hairs of the body, considered as occasioned by pleasure, Vikr. d. 57.<BR> 2. Flaw or defect in a gem.<BR> 3. A ball of bread and sweetmeats with which elephants are fed.<BR> 4. An insect of any class affecting animals whether externally or internally.<BR> 5. A kind of esculent plant, MBh. 13, 4363.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलक
वि- + पुलक वि- + पुलक, adj. free from horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकय
पुलकय पुलकय, a denomin. derived from पुलक with अय, Par. To have or feel one's hairs of the body erect by pleasure, Gīt. 11, 10.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पुलकित, rather पुलक + इत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b " target="_blank">Page0563-b + 41</a>] adj. Having the hairs of the body erect, Hit. 16, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्त्य|पुलस्त्यः
पुलस्त्य पुलस्त्य, i. e. पुरस् + त्य, m. The name of one of the seven Ṛṣis and mental sons of Brahman, Rām. 3, 53, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलह|पुलहः
पुलह पुलह, m. The name of one of the seven Ṛṣis and mental sons of Brahman, Man. 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाक|पुलाकं|पुलाकः
पुलाक पुलाक, m. and n.<BR> 1. Shrivelled, or blighted, or empty grain.<BR> 2. Bad grain, Man. 10, 125.<BR> 3. A lump of boiled rice.<BR> 4. Abridgement.<BR> 5. Celerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन|पुलिनं|पुलिनः
पुलिन पुलिन, m. and n.<BR> 1. An alluvial formation, a small island, MBh. 4, 395.<BR> 2. The bank of a river, Pañc. 226, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्द|पुलिंद|पुलिंदः|पुलिन्दः
पुलिन्द पुलिन्द, m.<BR> 1. pl. The name of a barbarian tribe.<BR> 2. One belonging to this tribe, Pañc. 120, 8.<BR> 3. A prince of the Pulindas, MBh. 2, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्दक|पुलिंदक|पुलिंदकः|पुलिन्दकः
पुलिन्दक पुलिन्द + क, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोम
पुलोम पुलोम,<BR> I. m. = पुलोमन्, Rām. 4, 39, 7.<BR> II. f. मा, The wife of Kaśyapa (Viṣṇu P. 148).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमजा
पुलोमजा पुलोमजा, i. e. पुलोमन्-ज. f. Śacī, the wife of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमन्
पुलोमन् पुलोमन्, m. The name of an Asura (ŚKD.), or Dānava (VP. 147), father-in-law of Indra, by whom he was slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्
पुष् पुष्, ii. 9, Par.<BR> 1. To nourish, MBh. 3, 13639.<BR> 2. To cherish, Pañc. 238, 7.<BR> 3. To manage, Bhartṛ. 2, 38.<BR> 4. To augment, Rājat. 5, 159.<BR> --i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To thrive, to prosper, Chr. 291, 13 = Rigv. i. 64, 13.<BR> 2. To enjoy, Ragh. 18, 32.<BR> 3. To possess, Ragh. 16, 58.<BR> 4. To exhibit, Man. 9, 37.<BR> 5. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-a " target="_blank">Page0564-a + 43</a>] unfold, Śāk. d. 18.<BR> 6. To support, to maintain, Rām. 4, 61, 24.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पुष्ट,<BR> 1. Nourished.<BR> 2. Well-fed, strong, Chr. 4, 18.<BR> 3. Eminent, Man. 4, 231.<BR> 4. Loud, Hariv. 14063.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be nourished, Śāk. 107, 7.<BR> --Caus. or i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To nourish, Lass. 99, 3 = Rigv. v. 9, 7. To cherish, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1890.<BR> --Cf.<BR> 2. व्युष्.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिपुष्ट, Very strong, Pañc. iii. d. 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> न-, adj. rather insignificant, paltry, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 14.<BR> --With परि परि, परिपुष्ट,<BR> 1. Cherished.<BR> 2. Abounding in.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be cherished or managed, Bhartṛ. 2, 38.<BR> 2. To cherish, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2602.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To nourish, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 10.<BR> --With वि वि, विपुष्ट, Ill-fed, low, Pañc. i. d. 313 (rather पुष्ट, with वि).<BR> --With सम् सम्, ii. 9, To increase, Bhartṛ. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्ट
अ-पुष्ट अ-पुष्ट, adj. deficient, Sāh. D. 7, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपुष्ट|अन्यपुष्टः
अन्य- + पुष्ट अन्य- + पुष्ट, m. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिपुष्ट|बलिपुष्टः
बलि- + पुष्ट बलि- + पुष्ट, m. a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष
पुष पुष् + अ, in ग्रह-, m. The sun (nourishing the planets by its light). f. षा, The name of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कर|पुष्करं|पुष्करः
पुष्कर पुष्कर (probably पुष्-कृ + अ).<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. The sky, heaven, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1770.<BR> 3. The blue lotus flower, MBh. 1, 4704.<BR> 4. The tip of an elephant's trunk, Pañc. 80, 8.<BR> 5. The skin of a drum, Ragh. 17, 11.<BR> 6. A drug, Costus speciosus.<BR> 7. The name of a celebrated place of pilgrimage.<BR> 8. The blade of a sword.<BR> 9. The sheath of a sword.<BR> 10. (also m.), One of the seven great Dvīpas, or divisions of the world.<BR> 11. An arrow.<BR> 12. The art or science of dancing.<BR> 13. War, battle.<BR> 14. Intoxication.<BR> 15. A cage.<BR> 16. A part.<BR> II. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b " target="_blank">Page0564-b + 42</a>] m.<BR> 1. A pond or lake.<BR> 2. A drum, a kettle-drum, Megh. 67.<BR> 3. One of the principal clouds, that which occasions dearth.<BR> 4. The Indian crane.<BR> 5. A sort of snake.<BR> 6. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुष्कर
त्रि- + पुष्कर त्रि- + पुष्कर, pl. three holy ponds, Ragh. 18, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कराय
पुष्कराय पुष्कराय, a denomin. derived from पुष्कर with य, Ātm. To represent a drum, Daśarūp. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करावती
पुष्करावती पुष्करावती, i. e. पुष्कर + वन्त् + ई, f. The name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करावर्तक|पुष्करावर्तकः|पुष्करावर्त्तक
पुष्करावर्तक पुष्करावर्तक, i. e. पुष्कर-आवर्त + क, m. A certain kind of cloud, Megh. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करिन्
पुष्करिन् पुष्करिन्, i. e. पुष्कर + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी, Abounding in lotus flowers, Rām. 3, 76, 5.<BR> II. m. An elephant.<BR> III. f. इणी, A pool where the lotus does or may grow, Arj. 4, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कल|पुष्कलं|पुष्कलः
पुष्कल पुष्कल (= पुष्कर, with ल् for र्),<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Excellent, Man. 8, 81; best.<BR> 2. Good, salutary.<BR> 3. Much, Rām. 1, 71, 2 Gorr.; many, Bhag. 11, 21; with following न, More than, Man. 3, 129.<BR> 4. Complete.<BR> 5. Loud, MBh. 7, 578.<BR> II. m. A kind of drum, MBh. 6, 1631.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A certain measure.<BR> 2. Alms to the extent of four mouthfuls of food.<BR> 3. The name of a holy place.<BR> 4. A proper name.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुष्कल
सु- + पुष्कल सु- + पुष्कल, adj. Very copious, MBh. 9, 2146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कलक|पुष्कलकः
पुष्कलक पुष्कल + क, m.<BR> 1. The musk deer.<BR> 2. A pin, a bolt.<BR> 3. A Bauddha mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कलावती
पुष्कलावती पुष्कलावती, = पुष्करावती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टि|पुष्टिः
पुष्टि पुष्टि, i. e. पुष् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Thriving, increase, Pañc. 215, 2.<BR> 2. Vegetation, Man. 9, 37.<BR> 3. Prosperity, Pañc. i. d. 246.<BR> 4. Nourishment, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a " target="_blank">Page0565-a + 44</a>] Man. 2, 32.<BR> 5. One of the divine mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिका
पुष्टिका पुष्टि + का, f. An oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिद|पुष्टिदः
पुष्टिद पुष्टि + द,<BR> I. adj. Yielding prosperity, Hariv. 833.<BR> II. m. A class of Manes, Mārk. P. 96, 45.<BR> III. f. दा, The name of a plant, Physalis flexuosa Lin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प्
पुष्प् पुष्प् (rather an anomal. denomin. derived from पुष्प), i. 4, Par. To flower, to blossom, Hariv. 12799 (also i. 1, Mālatīm. 153, 5; Hariv. 7874).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पुष्पित (rather पुष्प + इत), Flowered, in flower. f. ता, A woman during menstruation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुष्पित
सु- + पुष्पित सु- + पुष्पित, adj. blossoming beautifully, Rām. 3, 55, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णपुष्पित
सुवर्ण- + पुष्पित सुवर्ण- + पुष्पित, adj. having gold instead of flowers, Pañc. i. d. 51 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3284).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प पुष् + प,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A flower, Nal. 13, 3.<BR> 2. The menses, Mārk. P. 51, 42.<BR> 3. The vehicle or car of Kuvera.<BR> 4. A disease of the eyes, albugo.<BR> 5. A topaz, Rām. 2, 94, 6 (cf. पुष्प-राग).<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR> III. f. पा, The capital of Karṇa.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्प|अपुष्पः
अ- + पुष्प अ- + पुष्प, adj., f. पा, without flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्प|अभ्रपुष्पं|अभ्रपुष्पः
अभ्र- + पुष्प अभ्र- + पुष्प, n. 1. water. 2. a flower in the air, i. e. anything non-existent. 3. the ratan, Calamus rotang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खपुष्प
ख- + पुष्प ख- + पुष्प, n. a sky-flower, a nonentity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपुष्प|गंधपुष्प|गन्धपुष्पः
गन्ध- + पुष्प गन्ध- + पुष्प,<BR> I. n. a fragrant flower.<BR> II. m. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपुष्प
जीव- + पुष्प जीव- + पुष्प,<BR> I. n. 1. the flower of life, denoting a certain plant and the head. 2. the name of two plants.<BR> II. f. पा, the name of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भपुष्प
दर्भ- + पुष्प दर्भ- + पुष्प, m. 1. a kind of snake. 2. a certain insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपुष्प|नागपुष्पः
नाग- + पुष्प नाग- + पुष्प, m. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुष्प|भाण्डपुष्पः
भाण्ड- + पुष्प भाण्ड- + पुष्प, m. a sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुष्प|लक्ष्मीपुष्पः
लक्ष्मी- + पुष्प लक्ष्मी- + पुष्प, m. a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषपुष्प|विषपुष्पं|विषपुष्पः
विष- + पुष्प विष- + पुष्प, n. the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपुष्प|वीजपुष्पं
वीज- + पुष्प वीज- + पुष्प, n. 1. common citron. 2. a thorny plant, Vangueria spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खपुष्पी
शङ्ख-पुष्पी शङ्ख-पुष्पी, f. a sort of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b " target="_blank">Page0565-b + 40</a>] grass, Andropogon aciculatum, Man. 11, 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुष्प
स- + पुष्प स- + पुष्प, adj. endowed with blossoms, Ṛt. 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुष्प|सुपुष्पं|सुपुष्पः
सु- + पुष्प सु- + पुष्प, m., f. पा, and n. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रपुष्प|सूत्रपुष्पः
सूत्र- + पुष्प सूत्र- + पुष्प, m. the cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पक|पुष्पकं
पुष्पक पुष्प + क,<BR> I. m. A kind of snake, Suśr. 2, 265, 20.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The chariot of Kuvera, Rām. 3, 36, 15.<BR> 2. A bracelet of diamonds or jewels.<BR> 3. A cup or vessel of iron.<BR> 4. Green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पध|पुष्पधः
पुष्पध पुष्प-ध, m. The offspring of an outcaste Brāhmaṇa, Man. 10, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पंधय|पुष्पन्धय|पुष्पंधयः|पुष्पन्धयः
पुष्पंधय पुष्पंधय, i. e. पुष्प + म्-धे + अ, m. A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमय
पुष्पमय पुष्पमय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of flowers, Rām. 5, 5, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलिह्
पुष्पलिह् पुष्प-लिह्, m. A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवत्|पुष्पवन्त्
पुष्पवत् पुष्प + वत्, adv. Like a flower or flowers, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1876.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवन्त्|पुष्पवत्
पुष्पवन्त् पुष्प + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Having flowers, MBh. 6, 529.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A proper name.<BR> 2. du. The sun and the moon.<BR> III. f. वती.<BR> 1. A woman during menstruation.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाकर
पुष्पाकर पुष्पाकर, i. e. पुष्प-आकर, adj. Abounding in flowers, Vikr. d. 9 (with मास, i. e. Spring).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिन्
पुष्पिन् पुष्पिन्, i. e. पुष्प + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Bearing flowers, blossoming, Man. 1, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पेषु|पुष्पेषुः
पुष्पेषु पुष्पेषु, i. e. पुष्प-इषु, m. Kāma, the god of love (properly, Having flowers for arrows.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्य|पुष्यः
पुष्य पुष् + य, m.<BR> 1. The eighth lunar asterism.<BR> 2. The name of a month, Dec.--Jan.<BR> 3. The fourth age, Kaliyuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्
पुस् पुस्, see व्युष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त्
† पुस्त् पुस्त्, i. 10, Par.<BR> I. To bind.<BR> II. (also बुस्त् बुस्त्), i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To respect.<BR> 2. To disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त पुस्त,<BR> I. m. and n. A book.<BR> II. n. Working in clay, modelling, Kathās. 34, 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तक|पुस्तकं|पुस्तकः
पुस्तक पुस्त + क, m. and n. A book, a manuscript, Pañc. 127, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तमय
पुस्तमय पुस्त + मय, adj., f. यी, Wrought in clay, modelled, Suśr. 1, 29, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू पू, ii. 9, पुना, पुनी, Par. Ātm. i. 1, Ātm. (Par. Bhag. 10, 31); i. 4, Ātm., properly Passive. To purify, Man. 1, 105; to make pure, 8, 311.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पूत,<BR> 1. Purified, pure.<BR> 2. Cleaned.<BR> 3. Threshed, winnowed.<BR> 4. Foul smelling, stinking (cf. पूति and पूय्). n. Truth.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. पावय, To cause to be purified, to purify, Man. 3, 183.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पावित, Purified, 2, 75.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, निष्-पू, To purify, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 18.<BR> --With परि परि, परिपूत,<BR> 1. Purified completely, Mṛcch. 159, 2.<BR> 2. Threshed (winnowed?), Man. 8, 331.<BR> --With वि वि, To purify, MBh. 2, 1150.<BR> --Cf. Lat. purus, pŭtus, putare (cf. the vedic use of पू), pius, ex-piare, piaculum, punio, poena; ποινή, ἄποινα, νηποινῆ; Goth. fon (fire, cf. पावक), probably for favan; with र् for न्; O.H.G. fiur; A.S. fyr; πῦρ, πυρός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूत
अ- + पूत अ- + पूत, adj. impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपूत
शस्त्र- + पूत शस्त्र- + पूत, adj. purified by arms, absolved from guilt by dying in the field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूग|पूगं|पूगः
पूग पूग,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A heap, Arj. 3, 32.<BR> 2. A multitude, MBh. 5, 1085. pl. A number of persons, Man. 3, 152.<BR> 3. The betel-nut tree (Areca faufel).<BR> II. n. The fruit of the last.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपूग
काल- + पूग काल- + पूग, m. lapse of long time, MBh. 2, 1329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्
पूज् पूज्, i. 10, Par. (also Ātm., Hit. ii. d. 36, and in epic poetry, i. 1, MBh. 3, 1005).<BR> 1. To honour, to reverence, MBh. 1, 6038; Pañc. i. d. 146 (Ātm.).<BR> 2. To regard, Yājñ. 2, 14. (Ptcple. of the pf. pass. Anomalous potential पूजयीत, MBh. 3, 1070). पूजित,<BR> 1. Frequented, Arj. 4, 55.<BR> 2. Recommended.<BR> 3. Acknowledged, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3174.<BR> 4. Endowed, Rām. 2, 26, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To honour one after the other, Rām. 2, 99, 9 Gorr.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To honour, Rām. 1, 1, 83.<BR> 2. To value highly, MBh. 1, 17.<BR> 3. To approve, Rām. 2, 76, 12. अभिपूजित,<BR> 1. Offered after humble reverences, Man. 6, 58(?).<BR> 2. Agreeable, Rām. 1, 52, 23.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To honour, MBh. 4, 98.<BR> --With परि परि, To honour much, Śiś. 1, 14.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, The same, MBh. 13, 2110.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To honour especially, Pañc. i. d. 164; MBh. 6, 3790 (प्रपूजिरे without reduplication; probably it is to be changed to पुपूजिरे); 13, 914.<BR> 2. To approve, MBh. 8, 3244.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To show honour, Hariv. 16223.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To return a salutation, Rām. 1, 26, 4.<BR> 2. To salute in one's turn, Man. 1, 1.<BR> 3. To approve, Rām. 1, 11, 10.<BR> 4. To honour, Man. 3, 58.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To honour, to salute with reverence, Rām. 2, 70, 6.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To honour, Man. 2, 210.<BR> 2. To esteem highly, MBh. 3, 1110.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To honour, MBh. 1, 6376.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूजित
सु-पूजित सु-पूजित, adj. much honoured, Chr. 62, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजक|पूजकः
पूजक पूज् + अक, adj., f. जिका, Worshipping, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a " target="_blank">Page0567-a + 39</a>] MBh. 2, 454; honouring, a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजन|पूजनं
पूजन पूज् + अन,<BR> I. n. Honouring, worshipping, Man. 4, 152.<BR> II. f. नी, The name of a female bird (in a legend).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिपूजन|अतिथिपूजनं
अतिथि-पूजन अतिथि-पूजन, n. receiving guests with honour, Man. 3, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितृ
पूजयितृ पूजयितृ, i. e. पूज्, Caus., + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Worshipping, a worshipper, MBh. 13, 7517.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजा
पूजा पूज् + आ, f., Worshipping, honouring, respect, adoration, Kathās. 4, 43; Vikr. 45, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपूजा
अग्र- + पूजा अग्र- + पूजा, f. first oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिपूजा
अतिथि- + पूजा अतिथि- + पूजा, f. receiving guests with honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तपूज
त्यक्त-पूज त्यक्त-पूज (vb. त्यज्), adj. abandoning the worship, Rājat. 5, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्यता
पूज्यता पूज्य + ता (vb. पूज्), f., and पूज्यत्व पूज्य + त्व, n. Venerableness, MBh. 2, 1386.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूण्
† पूण् पूण्, see पूल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्
पूत् पूत्, a sound imitative of blowing, Pañc. 93, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतना
पूतना पूतना,<BR> 1. Yellow myrobalan, Terminalia Chebula.<BR> 2. The name of a female demon causing a certain disease of children, and killed by Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
पूति पूति,<BR> A. i. e. पू + ति, f.<BR> 1. Purification.<BR> B. i. e. पूय् + ति,<BR> I. adj. Putrid, stinking, MBh. 12, 3606.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Pus matter.<BR> 2. Civet.<BR> --Cf. Lat. putidus; see पूय्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिक|पूतिकं|पूतिकः
पूतिक पूति + क,<BR> I. adj. Putrid, stinking, MBh. 4, 173.<BR> II. m. Grey bonduc, Guilandina Bonduc Lin.<BR> III. f. का, A civet or pole-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतित्व
पूतित्व पूति + त्व, n. Stinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवक्त्रता
पूतिवक्त्रता पूति-वक्त्र + ता, f. Condition [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b " target="_blank">Page0567-b + 41</a>] of having stinking breath, Man. 11, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्यण्ड|पूत्यंड|पूत्यण्डः
पूत्यण्ड पूत्यण्ड, i. e. पूति-अण्ड, m. A kind of insect, cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1808.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूप|पूपः
पूप पूप, m. A cake, Rām. 1, 54, 3 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपालिक
पूपालिक पूपालिक, i. e. पूप + आल + इक, m., and f. का, A cake, Suśr. 2, 511, 14; 155, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय्
पूय् पूय्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To become putrid, to stink.<BR> 2. To putrefy.<BR> 3. To be dissolved. पूत, see पू.<BR> --Cf. Goth. fûls, and A.S. fúl; πύϊον, πῦον, πῦος, πυόω, etc., πύθω, πυθεδών, etc.; Lat. pŭter, putris, putrescere, pŭdere, repudium, repudiare, probably also fœtor, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय पूय् + अ, m. and n. Pus, matter, Man. 3, 180.<BR> --Cf. πύϊον, πῦον, πῦος; Lat. pus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयन|पूयनं
पूयन पूय् + अन, n. Pus, discharge from a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयभुज्
पूयभुज् पूय-भुज्, adj. Eating purulent carcasses, Man. 12, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयोद|पूयोदः
पूयोद पूयोद, i. e. पूय-उद (cf. उदक), m. The name of a hell, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्
पूर् पूर्, see पॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर पूर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Filling, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 7.<BR> 2. A large quantity of water, Ragh. 3, 17.<BR> 3. A cake, Rām. 2, 100, 64 Gorr.<BR> 4. Drawing in breath through the nose, a religious practice, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 9.<BR> 5. The healing or cleansing of ulcers.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर
अ-पूर अ-पूर, adj. not to be satisfied, unquenchable, Bhāg. P. 7, 13, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपूर
अति- + पूर अति- + पूर, m. large stream, Utt. Rāmac. 68, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपूर|कर्णपूरः|कर्ण्णपूर
कर्ण- + पूर कर्ण- + पूर, m. 1. an ornament of the ear, Utt. Rāmac. 62, 13. 2. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपूर
काम- + पूर काम- + पूर, adj. Fulfilling wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपूर|घृतपूरः
घृत- + पूर घृत- + पूर, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a " target="_blank">Page0568-a + 41</a>] m. a sweetmeat composed of flour, butter, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपूर|जलपूरः
जल- + पूर जल- + पूर, m. a bed full of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पूर
दुष्पूर दुष्पूर, adj., f. रा, difficult to be filled or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपूर
पाणि- + पूर पाणि- + पूर, adj. filling the hand, Yājñ. 3, 320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूर|फलपूरः
फल- + पूर फल- + पूर, m. common citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूर|सुपूरः
सु- + पूर सु- + पूर,<BR> I. adj. easy to be filled, Pañc. i. d. 31.<BR> II. m. a sort of lime or citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरक|पूरकः
पूरक पूर् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Filling.<BR> 2. Filling up, Man. 9, 289.<BR> 3. Satisfying, MBh. 1, 75.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Closing the right nostril, and drawing up air through the left, a religious observance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 17.<BR> 2. A citron (Citrus medica).<BR> 3. The final obsequial cake.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूरक|फलपूरकः
फल- + पूरक फल- + पूरक, m. a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरण|पूरणं|पूरणः
पूरण पूरण, i. e. पूर् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णि, Filling, Hariv. 7441.<BR> II. n. Act of filling, Ragh. 9, 73; completing, satisfying, Mālav. d. 73.<BR> 2. Drawing (a bow), MBh. 16, 271.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A dyke.<BR> 2. The ocean.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्तापूरण
गर्ता- + पूरण गर्ता- + पूरण, n. Filling up a hole, Pañc. 96, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयितृ
पूरयितृ पूरयितृ, i. e. पूर्, i. 10, + तृ, m., f. त्रि, n. One who fills up, who satisfies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिक|पूरिकः
पूरिक पूरिक, i. e. पूर + इक, m., and f. का, A sort of cake, MBh. 7, 2309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिन्
ऽपूरिन् -पूर् + इन्, adj. Filling, MBh. 8, 4669.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरु
पूरु पूरु, पूरुष पूरुष, see पुरु, पुरुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णक|पूर्णकः
पूर्णक पूर्ण + क (vb. पृ),<BR> I. adj. Filled, full, MBh. 7, 2199.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A certain tree, Rām. 3, 79, 38.<BR> 2. The blue jay.<BR> III. f. निका, A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णता
पूर्णता पूर्ण + ता (vb. पॄ), f. Plenty, Megh. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णत्व
पूर्णत्व पूर्ण + त्व (vb. पॄ). n. Being full of. Kathās. 16, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णपात्रमय
पूर्णपात्रमय पूर्ण-पात्र + मय (cf. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b " target="_blank">Page0568-b + 43</a>] पात्र), adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Consisting in a पूर्ण-पात्र, MBh. 12, 2306.<BR> 2. Concerning full cups. Kathās. 23, 84 (? Brockh., Consisting in a poem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमा
पूर्णमा पूर्णमा, and पूर्णिमा पूर्णिमा, i. e. पूर्ण and curtailed मास, f. The night or day of full moon, Rājat. 5, 156; Pañc. 74, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्
पूर्ब् पूर्ब्, see पुर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब|पूर्ब्ब|पूर्ब्बः
पूर्ब पूर्ब, see पूर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्भिद्य
पूर्भिद्य पूर्भिद्य, i. e. पुर्-भिद् + य n. The destruction of castles, war, Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्
पूर्व् पूर्व्, see पुर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व|पूर्वः|पूर्व्व|पूर्व्वः
पूर्व पूर्व, i. e. पुर + व (see पुरा), also पार्ब, adj., f. वा (बा).<BR> 1. Fore, Śāk. d. 37.<BR> 2. Former, prior, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 905.<BR> 3. First, Man. 1, 10.<BR> 4. Lowest, Man. 8, 120.<BR> 5. Eastern, Man. 2, 22.<BR> II. adv. वम्.<BR> 1. Before, Chr. 3, 2; first, Pañc. 51, 18.<BR> 2. Formerly, Chr. 16, 20.<BR> 3. Immemorially, Man. 9, 87.<BR> III. पूर्वेण, instr. adv. To the east, Rām. 2, 70, 11.<BR> IV. An ancestor, Pañc. iii. d. 216; Man. 3, 220.<BR> V. f. वा, The cast.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. पूर्वेद्युस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व|अपूर्वः|अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व्वं
अ- + पूर्व अ- + पूर्व, adj. 1. new, Pañc. ii. d. 16; unknown, 68, 13. 2. incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपूर्व|अदृष्टपूर्व्व
अ-दृष्ट- + पूर्व अ-दृष्ट- + पूर्व (vb. दृश्),<BR> I. adj. not seen before, Rām. 5, 54, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यपूर्व
अद्य- + पूर्व अद्य- + पूर्व, adv. till to-day, Rām. 1, 32, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयप्रश्नपूर्वम्
अन्-आमय-प्रश्न- + पूर्वम् अन्-आमय-प्रश्न- + पूर्वम्, adv. after having inquired for a person's health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपूर्व
अन्य- + पूर्व अन्य- + पूर्व, f. वा, a woman previously promised to one and married to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधपूर्वम्
अ-बोध- + पूर्वम् अ-बोध- + पूर्वम्, adv. without having perceived before, Śāk. d. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्व|अहंपूर्व
अहम्- + पूर्व अहम्- + पूर्व, adj. desiring to be the first, Rām. 2, 12, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्दपूर्वम्
त्रि-अब्द- + पूर्वम् त्रि-अब्द- + पूर्वम्, adv. less than three years, Man. 2, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्व
दक्षिण- + पूर्व दक्षिण- + पूर्व, adj., f. वा, south-eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्वा|परपूर्व्वा
पर- + पूर्वा पर- + पूर्व, f. a woman formerly married, having belonged formerly to another man, Chr. 6, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वपूर्व
पूर्व-पूर्व पूर्व-पूर्व,<BR> I. adj. every preceding one.<BR> II. m. pl. ancestors, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-a " target="_blank">Page0569-a + 44</a>] MBh. 3, 12408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्व
भूत- + पूर्व भूत- + पूर्व, adj. prior; ˚वम्, adv. formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतपूर्व
अ-भूत- + पूर्व अ-भूत- + पूर्व, adj. not having existed before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपूर्व
मृदु- + पूर्व मृदु- + पूर्व, adj. mild, friendly. adv. mildly, gently at first, Rām. 2, 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथापूर्वम्
यथा-पूर्वम् यथा-पूर्वम्, adv. 1. as before, Pañc. 36, 18. 2. formerly. 3. in order or succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखिपूर्व
सखि- + पूर्व सखि- + पूर्व, adj. more excellent than a friend, MBh. 1, 5142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपूर्व|स्त्रीपूर्वः|स्त्रीपूर्व्वः
स्त्री- + पूर्व स्त्री- + पूर्व, one who has been before a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितपूर्व
स्मित- + पूर्व स्मित- + पूर्व, adv. smiling first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वक|पूर्वकः|पूर्व्वक
पूर्वक पूर्व + क,<BR> I. adj., f. विका.<BR> 1. Prior, before, preceding, MBh. 12, 13697.<BR> 2. First, Rām. 1, 70, 21.<BR> 3. As latter part of comp. adj. often, Accompanied by, Man. 2, 78.<BR> II. कम्, adv.<BR> 1. With, Man. 2, 128.<BR> 2. Conformable to, 2, 173.<BR> III. m. An ancestor, Hariv. 5176.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यपूर्विका
अन्-अन्य-पूर्विका अन्-अन्य-पूर्विका, f. a woman who had no other husband before, Yājñ. 1, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्विका|अहंपूर्विका|अहम्पूर्व्विका
अहम्-पूर्विका अहम्-पूर्विका, f. emulation for precedence, Kir. 14, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

