पूर्वाह्ण पूर्वाह्ण, i. e. पूर्व-अहन् + अ, m. The forenoon, Man. 4, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वाह्णिक
पूर्वाह्णिक पूर्वाह्णिक, i. e. पूर्वाह्ण + इक, f. की, Belonging to the forenoon, in the forenoon, MBh. 13, 1573.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्विक
पूर्विक in स्त्री-, i. e. स्त्री-पूर्व + इक, adj. One who has been at first a female, Chr. 63, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्विन्
पूर्विन् पूर्विन्, adj., f. इणी, Done by ancestors.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्विन्
अ-पूर्विन् अ-पूर्विन्, adj. doing what has not been done by the ancestors, MBh. 12, 10796; स्त्रीपूर्विन्, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वेद्युस्|पूर्व्वेद्युस्
पूर्वेद्युस् पूर्वेद्युस्, i. e. पूर्व + इ-दिव् + अस्, adv.<BR> 1. A former day, yesterday, Man. 3, 187.<BR> 2. The morning.<BR> --Cf. प्रातर् and πρώϊ-ζος, πρώϊζα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वोत्पन्नत्व
पूर्वोत्पन्नत्व पूर्वोत्पन्नत्व, i. e. पूर्व-उद्-पन्न (vb. पद्), + त्व, n. Condition of anterior existence, Bhāṣāp. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल्
† पूल् पूल्, i. 1, Par. To accumulate.<BR> --i. 10 (or पूण् पूण्, or पुण् पुण्), Par. To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष्
† पूष् पूष्, i. 1, Par. To nourish.<BR> --Cf. पुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषन्
पूषन् पूषन्, i. e. पुष् + अन्, m.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a " target="_blank">Page0570-a + 42</a>] The name of a vedic deity.<BR> 2. One of the Ādityas, MBh. 1, 2523.<BR> 3. The sun, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 461.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
1. पृ पृ, ii. 3, पिपृ (पीपृ, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 41), Par. † ii. 9, पृणा, णी, Par.<BR> 1. To bring over (ved.).<BR> 2. To protect, Bhāg. P. 7, 9, 41. (<BR> 3. To fill, see पॄ).<BR> --Caus. and पार्, i. 10, पारय,<BR> 1. To accomplish, Rām. 2, 55, 19.<BR> 2. To keep one's ground, MBh. 9, 1074.<BR> 3. To live, Man. 9, 178.<BR> 4. To be able, Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 4.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To maintain, Bhāg. P. 3, 18, 12.<BR> --Caus. To save from (abl.), 3, 25, 40.<BR> --Cf. पर and πείρω, πεῖρα, πόρος, πορεύς, ἄπορος, ἀπορέω, πορίζω, πορσύνω, πορθμός, παρών, πειράτης, πεπαρεῖν; Lat. par, peritus, ex-pertus, ex-perior, parere, partus, parare, portus, porta, portare; Goth. farjan; O.H.G. and A.S. faran; O.H.G. furt; A.S. fyrd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
2. पृ पृ, i. 6, प्रिय, Ātm. To be busy or active.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, ptcple. of the pf. pass. आपृत, Occupied, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 10.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To be busy, occupied with. व्यापृत, Occupied, Rām. 2, 39, 14; affected with, Lass. 94, 10.<BR> --Caus. To occupy, Ragh. 6, 19.<BR> --Cf. πέρ-νημι (see पण्), περνάω, πιπράσκω, ἔμπορος, πόρνος, νη (cf. पण्य-स्त्री), ἐμπολάω, πωλέω, πρίαμαι (old pass.); O.H.G. feil, feili.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
3. पृ पृ, ii. 5, पृणु, Par. To be pleased with.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To be attached to, Bhāg. P. 5, 5, 4 (cf. प्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ति|पृक्तिः
पृक्ति पृक्ति, i. e. पृच् + ति, f. Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्
पृच् पृच्, ii. 7, Par., and ii. 2, Ātm., and पृञ्च् पृञ्च्, ii. 2, Ātm.<BR> 1. To mix.<BR> 2. To unite, Rājat. 4, 1.<BR> 3. To fill, MBh. 1, 3659.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. पृक्त,<BR> 1. Touched.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b " target="_blank">Page0570-b + 38</a>] Touching.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनुपृक्त, Mixed.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संपृक्त,<BR> 1. Mixed.<BR> 2. United, Man. 9, 322; near to, Vikr. d. 142.<BR> --Cf. probably πλέκω, πόρκος; Lat. plicare, plecto; Goth. flahta; O.H.G. flehtan; also A.S. folgian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छक|पृच्छकः
पृच्छक पृच्छक, i. e. प्रछ् + अक, adj. Inquiring, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1819.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छा
पृच्छा पृच्छा, i. e. प्रछ् + अ, f. Asking a question, inquiring, Śāk. 104, 23 v. r.; question, Pañc. i. d. 438.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृज्
† पृज् पृज्, and पृञ्ज पृञ्ज्, ii. 2, Ātm. v. r. of पृच्, ii. 2, and पृञ्च्, and of पिञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृञ्च्
† पृञ्च् पृञ्च्, see पृच्; पृञ्ज् पृन्ज्, see पृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृड्
† पृड् पृड्, i. 6, Par. To delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृण्
पृण् पृण्, i. 6, To fill.<BR> --Cf. पॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृत्
पृत् पृत्, see पृतना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतना
पृतना पृतना, f., the base of many cases is पृत्.<BR> 1. Battle, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR> 2. An army, MBh. 1, 291.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनानी
पृतनानी पृतना-नी, m. The commander of an army, MBh. 7, 1464.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्या
पृतन्या पृतन्या, i. e. पृतना + य, f. An army, Bhāg. P. 8, 15, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्
† पृथ् पृथ्, or प्रथ् प्रथ्, i. 10, Par. To throw or cast, to extend (cf. प्रथ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्
पृथक् पृथक्,<BR> I. adv. Separately, severally, Draup. 6, 1.<BR> II. prep. (with acc., instr., abl.), Without, except.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. pars, partis, privus, privare; perhaps ϕάρσος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पृथक्
पृथक्-पृथक् पृथक्-पृथक्, separately, Man. 3, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्त्व|पृथक्त्वं
पृथक्त्व पृथक् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Individuality, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a " target="_blank">Page0571-a + 39</a>] Bhag. 9, 15.<BR> 2. Separation, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 28; separateness. पृथक्त्वेन, Singly, one by one, MBh. 14, 1058.<BR> 3. Severality, Bhāṣāp. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथा
पृथा पृथा, f. Kunti, one of the wives of Paṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथि
पृथि पृथि, m. A proper name, Chr. 297, 15 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी पृथिवी, i. e. पृथ्वी, f. of पृथु.<BR> 1. The earth personified, Man. 2, 225.<BR> 2. Earth as an element, Prab. 27, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवींजय
पृथिवींजय पृथिवींजय, i. e. पृथिवी + म्-जि + अ, m. A prince, MBh. 2, 364.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीभुज्
पृथिवीभुज् पृथिवी-भुज्, m. A king, Vikr. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीमय
पृथिवीमय पृथिवी + मय, adj., f. यी, Earthen, MBh. 12, 1452.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीरुह|पृथिवीरुहः
पृथिवीरुह पृथिवी-रुह् + अ, m. A plant, a tree, Hariv. 11445.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु पृथु, i. e. प्रथ् + उ,<BR> I. adj., f. थु and थ्वी, comparat. पृथुतर and प्रथीयस्, superl. पृथुतम and प्रथिष्ठ, Large, great, Megh. 47.<BR> II. m. The name of a king and of others.<BR> III. f. थ्वी, The earth, Pañc. i. d. 51.<BR> IV. f. थु and थ्वी, A pungent seed, Nigella Indica.<BR> --Cf. Goth. braids; A.S. brád; πλατύς; Lat. lātus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुक|पृथुकं|पृथुकः
पृथुक पृथुक, perhaps प्रथ् + उक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Rice or grain flattened.<BR> 2. A child, a boy, Śiś. 3, 30.<BR> 3. The young of any animal.<BR> II. f. का, A girl.<BR> --Cf. probably πόρταξ, πόρτις, perhaps παρθένος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुता
पृथुता पृथु + ता, f., and पृथुत्व पृथु + त्व, n. Largeness, greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुल|पृथुलं
पृथुल पृथु + ल, adj., f. ला, Large, great, Śiś. 10, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीदण्डपालता
पृथ्वीदण्डपालता पृथ्वी-दण्ड-पाल + ता, f. The office of a chief of the police, Mṛcch. 177, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृदाकु|पृदाकुः
पृदाकु पृदाकु (vb. पर्द्?) m., f. कू.<BR> 1. A snake, MBh. 3, 12190.<BR> 2. A scorpion.<BR> 3. A tiger.<BR> 4. A leopard.<BR> 5. An elephant.<BR> 6. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि पृश्नि,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Of variegated colour.<BR> 2. Delicate, feeble.<BR> 3. Thin, small, short.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A proper name.<BR> 2. A tribe of Ṛṣis.<BR> III. f.<BR> 1. A ray of light.<BR> 2. The mother of the Maruts.<BR> 3. A kind of fruit. पृश्नी, Pistia stratistes Lin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निगु
पृश्निगु पृश्निगु, i. e. पृश्नि-गो, m. A proper name, Chr. 296, 7 = Rigv. i. 112, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निमातृ
पृश्निमातृ पृश्नि-मातृ, adj. Brought forth by Pṛśni, epithet of the Maruts, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्
† पृष् पृष्, (akin to प्रुष्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sprinkle.<BR> 2. To hurt.<BR> 3. To vex.<BR> 4. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत|पृषतः
पृषत पृषत i. e. पृषन्त् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Speckled.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A drop, Rām. 3, 32, 4.<BR> 2. A spot.<BR> 3. The porcine deer, 2, 93, 2.<BR> 3. The father of Drupada, Chr. 51, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्क|पृषत्कः
पृषत्क पृषत्क, i. e. पृषन्त् + क, m. An arrow, Rām. 3, 18, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदश्व|पृषदश्वः
पृषदश्व पृषदश्व, i. e. पृषन्त् + अश्व,<BR> I. adj. Riding on antelopes, epithet of the Maruts, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The God of air, or wind divinely personified.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदाज्य|पृषदाज्यं
पृषदाज्य पृषदाज्य, i. e. पृषन्त्-आज्य, n. Clarified butter mixed with curds, forming an oblation, Rām. 6, 96, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषद्वल|पृषद्वलः
पृषद्वल पृषद्वल, i. e. पृषन्त् + वल, m. The vehicle of the god of wind (cf. पृषदश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषन्त्|पृषत्
पृषन्त् पृषन्त् (properly, ptcple. pres. of पृष्),<BR> I. adj., f. अती, Speckled (ved.).<BR> II. n. A drop of water, Hariv. 3586.<BR> III. m. The porcine deer, Rām. 3, 76, 12.<BR> IV. f. षती, Its female, MBh. 7, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषन्ति|पृषंति|पृषंतिः|पृषन्तिः
पृषन्ति पृषन्त् + इ, m. A drop of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषाकरा
पृषाकरा पृषाकरा, i. e. probably पृष, for पृषन्त्, -आकर, f. A small stone, used as weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोदर|पृषोदरः
पृषोदर पृषोदर, i. e. probably पृष, for पृषन्त्, -उदर, adj. Having the belly speckled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोद्यान|पृषोद्यानं
पृषोद्यान पृषोद्यान, i. e. probably पृष, for पृषन्त्, -उद्यान, n. A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ|पृष्ठं
पृष्ठ पृष्ठ, perhaps प्र-स्थ, n.<BR> 1. The back, Man. 4, 72; with दा, To incline deeply, Rājat. 4, 135.<BR> 2. The rear, the hinder-part of anything. ष्ठे and ष्ठेन, from behind, Mārk. P. 23, 5; Vikr. 47, 12.<BR> 3. The surface or superficies, Man. 7, 147; terrace, Vikr. 38, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपृष्ठ|कांडपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठं|काण्डपृष्ठः
काण्ड- + पृष्ठ काण्ड- + पृष्ठ, 1. m. a soldier, MBh. 13, 1593. 2. the husband of a Vaiśya female. 3. the bow of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिपृष्ठ|गिरिपृष्ठः
गिरि- + पृष्ठ गिरि- + पृष्ठ, n. the top of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपृष्ठ|त्रिपृष्ठः
त्रि- + पृष्ठ त्रि- + पृष्ठ, n. the highest heaven, Bhāg. P. 1, 19, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहपृष्ठ|लोहपृष्ठः
लोह- + पृष्ठ लोह- + पृष्ठ, m. a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यपृष्ठ
हर्म्य- + पृष्ठ हर्म्य- + पृष्ठ, n. the upper room of a palace, Vikr. 38, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठक|पृष्ठकं
पृष्ठक पृष्ठ + क, n. The back. पृष्ठके हृ, To postpone, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 138 v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतस्
पृष्ठतस् पृष्ठ + तस्, adv. and prep. (with the gen.).<BR> 1. Behind, at the back of, Rām. 2, 30, 11; with गम्, To follow, Pañc. 9, 1; to pursue, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b " target="_blank">Page0572-b + 43</a>] 172, 17.<BR> 2. On the back, Man. 8, 300.<BR> 3. Backward, Rām. 5, 49, 33.<BR> 4. Secretly, MBh. 13, 5046.<BR> 5. With कृ, To postpone, to renounce, MBh. 1, 6694.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांसादन|पृष्ठमांसादनं
पृष्ठमांसादन पृष्ठमांसादन, i. e. पृष्ठ-माम्स-अद् + अन, n. Backbiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठानुग
पृष्ठानुग पॄष्ठानुग, i. e. पृष्ठ-अनुग, adj. Following, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2493.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ्य|पृष्ठ्यं|पृष्ठ्यः
पृष्ठ्य पृष्ठ्य, i. e. पृष्ठ + य, m., f. A pack-horse or riding-horse, MBh. 1, 8011.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पॄ
पॄ पॄ, ii. 9, पृणा, पृणी, Par. (whence a new verb पृण् पृण्, i. 6, Par. Ātm.); hither also पृ पृ, ii. 3, and पूर् पूर्, i. 4, Ātm. (properly passive; in epic poetry also Par. and ii. 2).<BR> 1. To fill.<BR> 2. To collect, Bhāg. P. 3, 32, 1.<BR> 3. To satisfy.<BR> 4. पूर्, i. 4, Ātm., To be filled, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 945.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. पूर्ण,<BR> 1. Filled, full, Nal. 23, 11.<BR> 2. Complete, entire, Rām. 1, 54, 12.<BR> 3. Satisfied, Rām. 1, 10, 34.<BR> 4. Strong, able.<BR> 5. Selfish.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. and पृ पॄ, i. 10, पारय, Par. and पूर् पूर्, i. 10, पूरय, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To fill, Hariv. 6456.<BR> 2. To intensify (a sound), MBh. 10, 412.<BR> 3. To blow (a wind instrument), Rām. 6, 37, 39.<BR> 4. To draw (a bow), 1, 34, 10 Gorr.<BR> 5. To draw (an arrow to the ear), 6, 79, 16.<BR> 6. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-a " target="_blank">Page0573-a + 41</a>] fulfil, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 587.<BR> 7. To cover, 6, 86, 36.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-पूर्य, adj. Not to be satisfied, insatiable, MBh. 12, 514.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, i. 4, To swell, to rise, MBh. 6, 4783 (Par.).<BR> --With अनु अनु, पूरय, To accomplish, Gīt. 1, 25.<BR> --With अभि अभि, i. 4, To be filled, MBh. 12, 6502. अभिपूर्ण, Full, full of. पूरय,<BR> 1. To fill, Rām. 5, 56, 111.<BR> 2. To load, Kathās. 44, 47.<BR> 3. To cover, MBh. 6, 1721.<BR> 4. To present with, Hariv. 6556.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, पूरय, To fill, MBh. 3, 10723.<BR> --With अव अव, अव-पूर्ण. Full of, Hariv. 11993.<BR> --With आ आ, i. 4,<BR> 1. To be filled, MBh. 1, 1302.<BR> 2. To increase, Kathās. 27, 8.<BR> 3. To abound, Hit. ii. d. 72. आपूर्ण, Satisfied, MBh. 14, 627. पूरय,<BR> 1. To fill, Bhag. 11, 30.<BR> 2. To blow (a wind instrument), Rām. 6, 75, 11.<BR> 3. To cover, Rām. 3, 32, 15.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, i. 4, To be filled, MBh. 1, 2472. समापूर्ण, Complete, entire. पूरय, To draw (a bow), Rām. 1, 34, 9 Gorr.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निष्पूर्त, Poured out, MBh. 7, 2239.<BR> --With परि परि, i. 4, To be filled, Rājat. 4, 109. परिपूर्ण,<BR> 1. Full, filled.<BR> 2. Covered.<BR> 3. Satisfied.<BR> 4. Wealthy, Pañc. v. d. 10.<BR> 5. Being at the summit of (his) power, i. d. 370.<BR> 6. Very intelligent, Rām. 3, 52, 52. पूरय,<BR> 1. To fill, MBh. 5, 7523.<BR> 2. To complete, to enjoy entirely, Gīt. 2, 16.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, सम्परिपूर्ण,<BR> 1. Filled.<BR> 2. Accomplished, MBh. 3, 15641.<BR> --With पि पि, instead of अपि, ii. 3, To fulfil, Bhāg. P. 4, 19, 38.<BR> --With प्र प्र, i. 4, To be filled, Hit i. d. 62. पूरय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b " target="_blank">Page0573-b + 39</a>]<BR> 1. To fill.<BR> 2. To cause to grow wealthy, Mṛcch. 178, 4.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, i. 4, To be filled, MBh. 15, 678.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रतिपूर्ण, Full, full of, Hariv. 5654. पूरय,<BR> 1. To fill, MBh. 14, 2122.<BR> 2. To satisfy, MBh. 13, 4442.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संपूर्ण,<BR> 1. Full, full of, Rām. 6, 96, 12.<BR> 2. Plentiful, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 779.<BR> 3. Fulfilled, Śāk. 106, 3; complete, Man. 1, 109. पूरय,<BR> 1. To fill, Kathās. 2, 83.<BR> 2. To satisfy, 22, 12.<BR> --Cf. πίμπλημι and प्रा; Goth. and A.S. full = पूर्ण; Goth. fulljan; A.S. fyllan; Lat. multus = पूर्त + स्; Lat. populus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णपूर्ण
आ-कर्ण- + पूर्ण आ-कर्ण- + पूर्ण, adj. drawn to the ear (as the string of a bow), MBh. 4, 1096.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापूर्ण|कलापूर्णः|कलापूर्ण्ण
कला- + पूर्ण कला- + पूर्ण, 1. adj. equal to the sixteenth part of, MBh. 4, 1299. 2. m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपूर्ण|वीजपूर्णः
वीज- + पूर्ण वीज- + पूर्ण, m. common citron, or a large kind of lime.<BR> II. पूर्त,<BR> 1. Filled, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 32; full.<BR> 2. Complete; with धर्म-, An act of pious liberality (see n.).<BR> 3. Covered. n. An act of pious liberality, as digging a well, etc., Man. 4, 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचक|पेचकः
पेचक पेचक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An owl, Rām. 6, 27, 31.<BR> 2. The root of an elephant's tail.<BR> 3. A bed.<BR> 4. A louse.<BR> 5. A cloud.<BR> II. f. चिका, A kind of owl, Rām. 6, 7, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेट|पेटः
पेट पेट, m., and f. टा and टी. A basket, bag, Pañc. 126, 2; 127, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटक|पेटकं|पेटकः
पेटक पेट + क<BR> I. m. and n.(?), A basket for holding clothes, books, etc., Vikr. 78, 7.<BR> II. f. टिका, A box, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 4.<BR> III. n. Multitude, Kathās. 34, 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेडा
पेडा पेडा, f. A basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेण्
पेण् पेण्, see पैण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेत्व|पेत्वं|पेत्वः
पेत्व पेत्व, i. e. पी + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Nectar.<BR> 2. Clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेब्
पेब् पेब्, see पेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूष|पेयूषं|पेयूषः
पेयूष पेयूष (= पीयूष, q. cf.), m. and n.<BR> 1. The milk of a cow which has calved within seven days, Man. 5, 6.<BR> 2. Fresh butter.<BR> 3. Nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरा
पेरा पेरा, f. A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
पेरु पेरु, m.<BR> 1. The ocean.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल्
† पेल् पेल्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलव|पेलवं
पेलव पेलव, adj., f. वा.<BR> 1. Delicate, Śāk. d. 70 (too delicate).<BR> 2. Thin, slender.<BR> 3. Soft, tender, Kathās. 21, 97.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेलव|परिपेलवं
परि- + पेलव परि- + पेलव,<BR> I. adj. 1. very small. 2. very delicate.<BR> II. n. a fragrant grass, Cyperus rotundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेव्
† पेव् पेव्, and प्लेव् प्लेव्, and पेव् पेब्, i. 1, Ātm. To serve, to attend on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशल|पेशलः
पेशल पेशल, i. e. पिश् + अल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Beautiful, Megh. 75.<BR> 2. Soft, tender, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 650.<BR> 3. Dexterous, 889.<BR> 4. Crafty.<BR> II. n. Beauty, Bhāg. P. 1, 10, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ποικίλος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपेशल
अति- + पेशल अति- + पेशल, adj. very crafty, Hit. ii. d. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्
पेशस् पेशस्, i. e. पिश् + अस्, n. An ornament, Chr. 294, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वपेशस्
विश्व- + पेशस् विश्व- + पेशस्, adj. containing all that is beautiful, Chr. 288, 16 = Rigv. i. 48, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपेशस्
सु- + पेशस् सु- + पेशस्, adj. very splendid, Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्कृत्
पेशस्कृत् पेशस्-कृ + त्, m.<BR> I. The hand, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 54.<BR> II. A kind of insect, 7, 1, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशिका
पेशिका पेशिका, i. e. पेशी + क, f. The peel of a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशी पेशी (cf. पिशित), f.<BR> 1. A ball or piece of flesh or meat, MBh. 1, 4494.<BR> 2. The fœtus directly after conception, 12, 11968.<BR> 3. A muscle, Yājñ. 3, 100.<BR> 4. The peel of a fruit.<BR> 5. A kind of drum, MBh. 6, 1535.<BR> 6. An egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्
† पेष् पेष्, or येष् येष्, i. 1, Ātm. To exert one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष|पेषः
