प्रतिनव प्रति-नव, adj. New, young, fresh, recent, Megh. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाग
प्रतिनाग प्रति-नाग, m. A hostile elephant, MBh. 8, 498.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाद|प्रतिनादः
प्रतिनाद प्रतिनाद, i. e. प्रति-नद् + अ, m. Echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधि|प्रतिनिधिः
प्रतिनिधि प्रतिनिधि, i. e. प्रति-नि-धा (see निधि), m.<BR> 1. A substitute, Man. 9, 180.<BR> 2. An image, likeness, Ragh. 5, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिपात|प्रतिनिपातः
प्रतिनिपात प्रतिनिपात, i. e. प्रति-नि-पत् + अ, m. Falling down, MBh. 7, 8591.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवर्तन|प्रतिनिवर्तनं|प्रतिनिवर्त्तन
प्रतिनिवर्तन प्रतिनिवर्तन, i. e. प्रति-नि-वृत्, + अन n. Turning back, return, Rām. 5, 1, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवारण
प्रतिनिवारण प्रतिनिवारण, i. e. प्रति-नि-वृ + अन, n. Keeping off, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिशम्
प्रतिनिशम् प्रति-निश + म् (निशा), adv. Every night, Kathās. 3, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्ष|प्रतिपक्षः
प्रतिपक्ष प्रति-पक्ष, m.<BR> 1. Opposite part, MBh. 8, 4409.<BR> 2. Opposition.<BR> 3. An opponent, an adversary, Pañc. ed. orn. 56, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रतिपक्ष|सत्प्रतिपक्षः
सत्प्रतिपक्ष सत्प्रतिपक्ष, i. e. सन्त्- (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), m. a contradictory premiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्षता
प्रतिपक्षता प्रतिपक्ष + ता, f. Opposition, obstacle, Bhāg. P. 5, 8, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्षवादित्व
प्रतिपक्षवादित्व प्रतिपक्षवादित्व, i. e. प्रतिपक्ष-वादिन् + त्व, n. Doubledealing, deceitful talk, Mālav. 57, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्षित
प्रतिपक्षित प्रतिपक्ष + इत, adj., f. ता, Nullified by a contradictory premiss (one of the five kinds of fallacious middle-term), Bhāṣāp. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्ति|प्रतिपत्तिः
प्रतिपत्ति प्रतिपत्ति, i. e. प्रति-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Obtaining, acquirement, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2801.<BR> 2. Perception, 1747.<BR> 3. Knowledge, Ragh. 8, 4.<BR> 4. Acknowledgment, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2159.<BR> 5. Admitting, Yājñ. 2, 283.<BR> 6. Proceeding, acting, MBh. 13, 2461.<BR> 7. A means, Mālav. 48, 6.<BR> 8. Respectful behaviour, honouring, worshipping, Pañc. 117, 12; MBh. 7, 7467.<BR> 9. Giving, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2659.<BR> 10. Causing, Kām. Nītis. 1, 40.<BR> 11. Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिमन्त्|प्रतिपत्तिमत्
प्रतिपत्तिमन्त् प्रतिपत्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Intelligent, Rām. 2, 1, 13 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपथम्
प्रतिपथम् प्रति-पथ + म्, adv. Along the way, straight-way(?), Rājat. 5, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् प्रति-पद्, f.<BR> 1. The first day of a lunar fortnight, the first of the moon's increase or wane, especially that of its increase, Rām. 2, 122, 28 Gorr.<BR> 2. Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदम्
प्रतिपदम् प्रति-पद + म्, adv.<BR> 1. At every step, Kathās. 19, 84.<BR> 2. Everywhere, 23, 79.<BR> 3. Place for place, at their several places, Prab. 44, 9 (Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाण|प्रतिपाणः
प्रतिपाण प्रतिपाण, i. e. प्रति-पण् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A counter-pledge, the thing staked against another, Nal. 9, 2.<BR> 2. Revenge at play, Nal. 26, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपात्रम्
प्रतिपात्रम् प्रति-पात्र-म्, adv. Every actor, Śāk. 3, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादक|प्रतिपादकः
प्रतिपादक प्रतिपादक, i. e. प्रति-पद्, Caus., + अह, adj. Illustrating, explanatory, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपादक
अ- + प्रतिपादक अ- + प्रतिपादक, adj. not forwarding, MBh. 12, 1212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादन|प्रतिपादनं
प्रतिपादन प्रतिपादन, i. e. प्रति-पद्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Causing to attain, Rām. 6, 69, 33.<BR> 2. Bringing back, 3, 76, 1.<BR> 3. Giving back, returning, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b " target="_blank">Page0592-b + 40</a>] MBh. 3, 13349.<BR> 4. Producing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 16.<BR> 5. Repetition, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 8.<BR> 6. Giving, gift, donation, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 20.<BR> 7. Teaching.<BR> 8. Beginning, MBh. 12, 5332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादपम्
प्रतिपादपम् प्रति-पादप + म्, adv. Tree for tree, in every tree, Vikr. 21, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रणाम|प्रतिप्रणामः
प्रतिप्रणाम प्रतिप्रणाम, i. e. प्रति-प्र-नम् + अ, m. Saluting in one's turn, Rājat. 5, 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रयाण|प्रतिप्रयाणं
प्रतिप्रयाण प्रतिप्रयाण, i. e. प्रति-प्र-या + अन, n. Return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसव|प्रतिप्रसवः
प्रतिप्रसव प्रति-प्रसव, m. Precept for an act which under other circumstances is forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफल|प्रतिफलं|प्रतिफलः
प्रतिफल प्रति-फल् + अ, and प्रति-फलन प्रति-फल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A reflection, a reflected image, Ānandal. 62.<BR> 2. A requital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्ध|प्रतिबंध|प्रतिबंधः|प्रतिबन्धः
प्रतिबन्ध प्रति-बन्ध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstacle, Mālav. 10, d. 9; Śāk. 23, 13.<BR> 2. Blocking up, Hariv. 5512.<BR> 3. Connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबंधक|प्रतिबन्धकः
प्रतिबन्धक प्रति-बन्ध् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Impeding, obstructing, Bhāṣāp. 146.<BR> II. m. A branch.<BR> III. At the end of comp. adj. = प्रतिबन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धवन्त्|प्रतिबन्धवत्
प्रतिबन्धवन्त् प्रतिबन्ध + वन्त्, adj. Beset with obstacles, difficult to be obtained, Mālav. 28, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धिता
प्रतिबन्धिता प्रतिबन्धिता, i. e. प्रति-बन्ध् + इन् + ता, f. State of checking, impeding, Vikr. 84, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबल|प्रतिबलः
प्रतिबल प्रति-बल, adj.<BR> 1. Able, adequate, Rām. 4, 9, 52.<BR> 2. Of equal strength, Hiḍ. 3, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबल
अ- + प्रतिबल अ- + प्रतिबल, adj. of incomparable strength, Rām. 6, 70, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्ब|प्रतिबिंब|प्रतिबिम्बः
प्रतिबिम्ब प्रतिबिम्ब, or प्रतिविम्ब प्रतिविम्ब, n. A reflection, Śiś. 9, 18; a reflected image, Hit. 68, 9; an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बित|प्रतिबिंबित
प्रतिबिम्बित प्रतिबिम्बित, i. e. प्रति-बिम्ब + इत, adj. Reflected, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोध|प्रतिबोधः
प्रतिबोध प्रतिबोध, i. e. प्रति-बुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Waking, awaking.<BR> 2. Instructing, admonishing, Lass. 38, 13.<BR> 3. Knowledge, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधन
प्रतिबोधन प्रतिबोधन, i. e. प्रति-बुध् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Awakening, Bhāg. P. 3, 8, 14.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Awaking, MBh. 12, 901.<BR> 2. Awakening, Rām. 6, 37, 38.<BR> 3. Instructing, Bhāg. P. 8, 24, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधवन्त्|प्रतिबोधवत्
प्रतिबोधवन्त् प्रतिबोध + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessed of understanding, Śāk. d. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभय|प्रतिभयं
प्रतिभय प्रति-भय, adj. Terrible, Pañc. ii. d. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा प्रति-भा, f.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. Understanding, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 15; Matsyop. 52 (corr. प्रतिभास्य).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नप्रतिभ
उत्पन्न- + प्रतिभ उत्पन्न- + प्रतिभ, i. e. उद्-पन्न- (vb. पद्), adj., f. भा, alert in mind, Pañc. 199, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभ|निष्प्रतिभः
निष्प्रतिभ निष्प्र्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. भा, deprived of splendour, Hariv. 4422.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाग|प्रतिभागः
प्रतिभाग प्रति-भाग, m. A small daily present, Man. 8, 307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान|प्रतिभानं
प्रतिभान प्रतिभान, i. e. प्रति-भा + अन, n. Understanding, Hariv. 1219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानवन्त्|प्रतिभानवत्
प्रतिभानवन्त् प्रतिभान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with presence of mind, Hit. iii. d. 19, M.M.; Indr. 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावन्त्|प्रतिभावत्
प्रतिभावन्त् प्रतिभा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with presence of mind, Kathās. 4, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभास|प्रतिभासः
प्रतिभास प्रति-भास, m. Reflection, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभू
प्रतिभू प्रति-भू, m. A surety, a sponsor, Pañc. 88, 11; Man. 7, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा प्रति-मा, f., and प्रतिमान [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b " target="_blank">Page0593-b + 43</a>] प्रतिमान, i. e. प्रति-मा + अन, n.<BR> 1. A resemblance, a figure, Hit. ii. d. 149.<BR> 2. An idol, Man. 9, 285.<BR> 3. The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिम
अ-प्रतिम अ-प्रतिम, adj., f. मा, incomparable, Pañc. iii. d. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताप्रतिमा
देवता-प्रतिमा देवता-प्रतिमा, f. Image of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पितपलाशप्रतिम
पुष्पित-पलाश- + प्रतिम पुष्पित-पलाश- + प्रतिम, adj. Resembling a Butea frondosa full of flowers, Pañc. 91, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुख
प्रतिमुख प्रति-मुख,<BR> I. adj. Being in front, Rām. 6, 90, 11.<BR> II. ˚खम्, adv.<BR> 1. In front, Megh. 18, n.<BR> 2. Against, Man. 8, 291.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातन|प्रतियातनं
प्रतियातन प्रतियातन, i. e. प्रति-यत् + अन.<BR> I. n. Requital, MBh. 8, 4635.<BR> II. f. ना, An image, Ragh. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोग|प्रतियोगः
प्रतियोग प्रति-योग, m.<BR> 1. Opposition.<BR> 2. Existing as the counterpart of anything, Kathās. 19, 84 (an antidote).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिन्
प्रतियोगिन् प्रतियोगिन्, i. e. प्रति-युज् + इन्, and प्रतियोग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Who or what impedes.<BR> 2. Connected.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An opponent.<BR> 2. A counterpart.<BR> 3. Any thing or object depending upon another and not existing without it.<BR> 4. The counter-entity of a negation, i. e. that thing of which there is a negation. (Cf. अ-, adj., Bhāṣāp. 68; the meaning is, that in a true व्याप्ति the middle term is always found with the major, and this latter cannot be incapable of being found where the middle term is, i. e. in the minor term.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोद्धृ
प्रतियोद्धृ प्रतियोद्धृ, i. e. प्रति-युध् + तृ, m. Able to oppose, Sund. 4, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरव|प्रतिरवः
प्रतिरव प्रति-रव, i. e. प्रति-रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Echo, Pañc. 193, 23.<BR> 2. Answering aloud, quarrel, 183, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरात्रम्
प्रतिरात्रम् प्रति-रात्र + म्, adv. Every night, Hit. 90, 10, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरूप|प्रतिरूपं
प्रतिरूप प्रति-रूप,<BR> I. adj. Suitable, Utt. Rāmac. 130, 14.<BR> II. n. A picture.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूप
अ- + प्रतिरूप अ- + प्रतिरूप, adj., f. पा. 1. incomparable, Rām. 3, 52, 6. 2. unsuitable, 3, 51, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरूपक|प्रतिरूपकं
ऽप्रतिरूपक -प्रतिरूप + क, latter part of comp. adj., f. पिका, Resembling, counterfeiting, Man. 11, 9; Śāk. 16, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोद्धृ
प्रतिरोद्धृ प्रतिरोद्धृ, i. e. प्रति-रुध् + तृ, m., f. ध्री, and n.<BR> 1. Who or what hinders, opposes, an opposer, Man. 3, 153.<BR> 2. One who recovers, Man. 11, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोध|प्रतिरोधः
प्रतिरोध प्रतिरोध, i. e. प्रति-रुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Impediment, opposition.<BR> 2. Siege, blockade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधक|प्रतिरोधकः
प्रतिरोधक प्रतिरोधक, i. e. प्रति-रुध् + अक, m.<BR> 1. An opponent.<BR> 2. A thief, Mālav. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधन|प्रतिरोधनं
प्रतिरोधन प्रतिरोधन, i. e. प्रति-रुध् + अन, n. Hindering, obstructing, Man. 9, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधिन्
प्रतिरोधिन् प्रतिरोधिन्, i. e. प्रति-रुध् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Impeding.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An opponent.<BR> 2. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलम्भ|प्रतिलंभः|प्रतिलम्भः
प्रतिलम्भ प्रतिलम्भ, i. e. प्रति-लभ् + अ, m. Obtaining, Lass. 89, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोम|प्रतिलोमः
प्रतिलोम प्रतिलोम, i. e. प्रति-लोमन्, adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Inverted. contrary to the natural order (regarding the intermixture of castes, where the mother is of a higher caste than the father), Man. 10, 25.<BR> 2. Left.<BR> 3. Low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोमज|प्रतिलोमजः
प्रतिलोमज प्रतिलोम-ज, adj. Born in the inverse order of the castes (cf. प्रतिलोम), Man. 10, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोमतस्
प्रतिलोमतस् प्रतिलोम + तस्, adv. Against the grain, invertedly, Pañc. iii. d. 230; because the order of the castes was inverted, Man. 10, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचन|प्रतिवचनं
प्रतिवचन and प्रतिवचस् प्रति-वच् + अन or अस्, n. An answer, Vikr. 58, 16; Pañc. 117, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवसथ|प्रतिवसथः
प्रतिवसथ प्रति-वस् + अथ, m. A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्य|प्रतिवाक्यं
प्रतिवाक्य प्रति-वाक्य, n. An answer, Nal. 22, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवात|प्रतिवातः
प्रतिवात प्रति-वात, m. The wind that blows in front. ते, loc. To the leeward, Man. 3, 203. तम्, adv. Against the wind, Pañc. iii. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारण|प्रतिवारणं|प्रतिवारणः
प्रतिवारण प्रतिवारण, i. e. प्रति-वृ + अन,<BR> I. adj. Keeping off, MBh. 12, 6165.<BR> II. n. Keeping off, Chr. 32, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रतिवारण
दुष्प्रतिवारण दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be kept off, Rām. 3, 31, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासिन्
प्रतिवासिन् प्रतिवासिन्, i. e. प्रति-वस् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Neighbouring, a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधान|प्रतिविधानं
प्रतिविधान प्रतिविधान i. e. प्रति-वि-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Arrangement against something, prevention, Pañc. 148, 20; help, 260, 24.<BR> 2. Arrangement.<BR> 3. Subsidiary ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविम्ब|प्रतिविंब|प्रतिविम्बं|प्रतिविम्बः
प्रतिविम्ब प्रतिविम्ब, see प्रतिबिम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश|प्रतिवेशः
प्रतिवेश प्रतिवेश, m., and प्रतिवेश्मन् प्रतिवेश्मन्, n. i. e. प्रति-विश् + अ or मन्. A neighbouring house or neighbourhood, Pañc. ap. Weber, Ind. St. iii. 372, 2 (मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशिन्
प्रतिवेशिन् प्रतिवेशिन्, i. e. प्रतिवेश + इन्, adj., f. नी, Neighbouring, a neighbour, Lass. 76, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूह|प्रतिव्यूहः
प्रतिव्यूह प्रति-व्यूह, m.<BR> 1. Arraying an army against an enemy. MBh. 6, 2073.<BR> 2. A multitude, Hariv. 3605.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशब्द|प्रतिशब्दः
प्रतिशब्द प्रति-शब्द, m. Echo, Pañc. 57, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशम|प्रतिशमः
प्रतिशम प्रति-शम् + अ, m. Cessation, deliverance, Chr. 57, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्या
प्रतिश्या प्रतिश्या, f., and पतिश्याय प्रतिश्याय, m., i. e. प्रति-श्यै, without aff., and with aff. अ, Catarrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रय|प्रतिश्रयः
प्रतिश्रय प्रतिश्रय, i. e. प्रति-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Assistance. MBh. 3, 8828.<BR> 2. An asylum, Pañc. i. d. 282.<BR> 3. Habitation, Nal. 24, 6; Man. 10, 36 (वहिस्-ग्राम-, adj. Living without the town).<BR> 4. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रव|प्रतिश्रवः
प्रतिश्रव प्रतिश्रव, i. e. प्रति-श्रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. A promise, Rājat. 5, 132.<BR> 2. An assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवण|प्रतिश्रवणं
प्रतिश्रवण प्रतिश्रवण, i. e. प्रति-श्रु + अन, n.<BR> 1. Promising.<BR> 2. Listening to, Man. 2, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत्
प्रतिश्रुत् प्रति-श्रु + त्, f.<BR> 1. Echo, Ragh. 13, 40.<BR> 2. Promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेद्धृ
प्रतिषेद्धृ प्रतिषेद्धृ, i. e. प्रति-सिध् + तृ, m., f. ध्री, n. Who or what keeps off, opposes, prevents, Rām. 1, 22, 9 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेध|प्रतिषेधः
प्रतिषेध प्रतिषेध, i. e. प्रति-सिध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Keeping off, Man. 9, 266.<BR> 2. Avoiding. Utt. Rāmac. 125, 4.<BR> 3. Prohibition, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधन|प्रतिषेधनं
प्रतिषेधन प्रतिषेधन, i. e. प्रति-सिध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Keeping off. preventing, Chr. 56, 13.<BR> 2. Prohibition, Man. 10, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्क|प्रतिष्कः
प्रतिष्क प्रतिष्क, probably curtailed प्रतिष्कश, m. An emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कश|प्रतिष्कशः
प्रतिष्कश प्रतिष्कश (प्रति and akin to काश्), m.<BR> 1. A spy, an emissary.<BR> 2. A companion.<BR> 3. A leader.<BR> 4. A leather thong, a whip (cf. कश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टम्भ|प्रतिष्टंभ|प्रतिष्टंभः|प्रतिष्टम्भः
प्रतिष्टम्भ प्रतिष्टम्भ, i. e. प्रति-स्तम्भ् + अ, m. Obstacle, impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठा
प्रतिष्ठा प्रतिष्ठा, i. e. प्रति-स्था, f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b " target="_blank">Page0595-b + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Place, Bhag. 14, 27.<BR> 2. A firm standing, staying, Bhag. 2, 70.<BR> 3. Quiet, Vikr. d. 42.<BR> 4. The earth.<BR> 5. Accomplishment, completion.<BR> 6. Fame, celebrity, Rājat. 5, 28; Utt. Rāmac. 131, 7.<BR> 7. Pre-eminence, MBh. 12, 6690.<BR> 8. Erecting the image of a deity, Rājat. 1, 124.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठ|अप्रतिष्ठः
अ-प्रतिष्ठ अ-प्रतिष्ठ, adj. 1. without stability, Bhag. 16, 8. 2. perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मप्रतिष्ठा
जन्मप्रतिष्ठा जन्मप्रतिष्ठा, i. e. जन्मन्-, f. a mother, Śāk. 83, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्ठा
सु- + प्रतिष्ठा सु- + प्रतिष्ठा,<BR> I. f. 1. erection (as of a temple), consecration. 2. fame.<BR> II. adj., f. ठा, famous, Nal. 12, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठान|प्रतिष्ठानं
प्रतिष्ठान प्रतिष्ठान, i. e. प्रति-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. A firm standing, Johns. Sel. 93, 50.<BR> 2. Base, Rām. 1, 5, 12 Gorr.<BR> 3. The same of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहार|प्रतिसंहारः
प्रतिसंहार प्रतिसंहार, i. e. प्रति-सम्-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Taking back, MBh. 10, 698.<BR> 2. Resigning, 12, 7161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधान|प्रतिसन्धान|प्रतिसंधानं
प्रतिसंधान प्रतिसंधान, i. e. प्रति-सम्-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Joining again, a remedy, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 10.<BR> 2. Suppressing of feeling for a time.<BR> 3. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमाधान|प्रतिसमाधानं
प्रतिसमाधान प्रतिसमाधान, i. e. प्रति-सम्-आ-धा + अन, n. A remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर|प्रतिसरः
प्रतिसर प्रतिसर, i. e. प्रति-सृ + अ,<BR> I. m. f. n. A servant, dependent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The rear of an army.<BR> 2. A garland.<BR> 3. A bracelet, Kir. 5, 33.<BR> 4. A string worn round the hand at nuptials, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 5.<BR> 5. Ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर्ग|प्रतिसर्गः
प्रतिसर्ग प्रति-सर्ग, m.<BR> 1. Secondary creation, or the creation of the world by Brahman and other divine beings.<BR> 2. The portion of a Purāṇa which treats of the destruction and renovation of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसान्धानिक|प्रतिसांधानिक|प्रतिसांधानिकः|प्रतिसान्धानिकः
प्रतिसान्धानिक प्रतिसान्धानिक, i. e. प्रतिसंधान + इक, m. A bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारण|प्रतिसारणं
प्रतिसारण प्रतिसारण, i. e. प्रति-स्रि, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a " target="_blank">Page0596-a + 40</a>] Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Repelling.<BR> 2. Applying remedies to a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्य|प्रतिसूर्यः|प्रतिसूर्य्य|प्रतिसूर्य्यः
प्रतिसूर्य प्रति-सूर्य, and प्रतिसूर्यक प्रति-सूर्य + क, m.<BR> 1. A mock sun, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 3, 37; 36, 1.<BR> 2. A lizard, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 7 (क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्कन्ध
प्रतिस्कन्ध प्रति-स्कन्ध, Hit. iv. d. 122, read स्कन्ध-स्कन्ध, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पन्दन|प्रतिस्पंदन|प्रतिस्पंदनं
प्रतिस्पन्दन प्रति-स्पन्द् + अन, n. Throbbing, vibration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्धा
प्रतिस्पर्धा प्रति-स्पर्धा, f. Emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहति|प्रतिहतिः
प्रतिहति प्रतिहति, i. e. प्रति-हन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Repulse, rebound, Śiś. 9, 49.<BR> 2. Disappointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहरण|प्रतिहरणं
प्रतिहरण प्रतिहरण, i. e. प्रति-हृ + अन, n. Avoiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहस्त|प्रतिहस्तः
प्रतिहस्त प्रति-हस्त, and प्रतिहस्तक प्रति-हस्त + ह, m. A substitute, Hit. ii. d. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहस्तिन्
प्रतिहस्तिन् प्रतिहस्तिन्, m. The keeper of a neighbouring brothel (? perhaps, a rival), Daśak. in Chr. 180, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहार|प्रतिहारः
प्रतिहार and प्रतीहार प्रती̆हार, i. e. प्रति-हृ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A door.<BR> 2. A door-keeper, Hit. 89, 2 (ई); a chamberlain, Kathās. 18, 194 (ई).<BR> 3. A juggler.<BR> II. f. री, A female doorkeeper, Utt. Rāmac. 25, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक|प्रतीकः
प्रतीक प्रतीक, i. e. प्रत्यञ्च् + अ, m.<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Contrary.<BR> 2. Inverted.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A limb.<BR> 2. A part.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतीक|सुप्रतीकः
सु- + प्रतीक सु- + प्रतीक,<BR> I. adj., f. का. 1. handsome-faced, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6. 2. handsome.<BR> II. m. 1. Śiva. 2. Kāma. 3. the elephant of the south-east(?) quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकार|प्रतीकारः
प्रतीकार प्रतीकार, and प्रतीकाश प्रतीकाश, see प्रतिक्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षा
प्रतीक्षा प्रतीक्षा, i. e. प्रति-ईक्ष् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b " target="_blank">Page0596-b + 38</a>] f.<BR> 1. Looking to.<BR> 2. Regard.<BR> 3. Expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षिन्
प्रतीक्षिन् प्रतीक्षिन्, i. e. प्रति-ईक्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Waiting for, Rājat. 5, 405; expecting, Nal. 17, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघात|प्रतीघातः
प्रतीघात प्रतीघात, see प्रतिघ्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीन|प्रतीचीनं
प्रतीचीन प्रतीचीन, and प्रतीच्य प्रतीच्य, i. e. प्रत्यञ्च् + ईन, or य, adj. Western, Rām. 2, 82, 7 (च्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्छक|प्रतीच्छकः
प्रतीच्छक प्रतीच्छक, i. e. प्रति-इष् (cf. the base of the pres. इच्छ), + अक, m. A receiver, Man. 4, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीति|प्रतीतिः
प्रतीति प्रतीति, i. e. प्रति-इ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 113.<BR> 2. Conviction, Śāk. d. 190.<BR> 3. Notoriety.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीति|अप्रतीतिः
अ- + प्रतीति अ- + प्रतीति, f. the not being understood, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीनाह|प्रतीनाहः
प्रतीनाह प्रतीनाह, i. e. प्रति-नह् + अ, m. Obstruction; in नासा-, m. Obstruction of the nose, Suśr. 2, 370, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीप|प्रतीपं|प्रतीपः
प्रतीप प्रतीप, i. e. प्रति-आप् + अ, adj., f. पा.<BR> 1. Backward.<BR> 2. Retrograde, Pañc. iii. d. 7.<BR> 3. Contradictory, opposite, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396.<BR> 4. Refractory, Hit. ii. d. 173; disobedient.<BR> 5. Adverse, Man. 4, 206; against the stream, Vikr. d. 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतीप
निष्प्रतीप निष्प्र्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. going straight forward, unconcerned, MBh. 4, 933.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीमान
प्रतीमान प्रतीमान, i. e. प्रति-मा + अन, n. A measure for gold, etc. (goldweights, etc.), Man. 8, 403.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहार|प्रतीहारः
प्रतीहार प्रतीहार, see प्रतिह्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहारता
प्रतीहारता प्रतीहार + ता, f., and प्रतीहारत्व प्रतीहार + त्व, n. The office of a door-keeper or chamberlain, Pañc. 63, 23; Rājat. 5, 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुद|प्रतुदः
प्रतुद प्र-तुद् + अ, m. A bird of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a " target="_blank">Page0597-a + 40</a>] game, one that kills with his beak, Man. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टिद
प्रतुष्टिद प्रतुष्टिद, i. e. प्र-तुष्टि-द (vb. दा), adj. Giving pleasure, Pañc. i. d. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोद|प्रतोदः
प्रतोद प्रतोद, i. e. प्र-तुद् + अ, m. A goad, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 16; Man. 3, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोली
प्रतोली प्रतोली, f. A high street, Rām. 2, 87, 22 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्त|प्रत्तं
प्रत्त प्रत्त, i. e. प्र-दत्त, vb. दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्न|प्रत्नः
प्रत्न प्र + त्न, adj., f. ना, Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष प्रत्यक्ष, i. e. प्रति-अक्ष,<BR> I. adj., f. क्षा.<BR> 1. Being before one's eyes, visible, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 9; Hit. iii. d. 24.<BR> 2. Present.<BR> 3. Perceptible, evident, Hit. 85, 21 (˚क्षी-कृत, made evident).<BR> II. क्षम्, adv. In the presence, Pañc. 216, 3; publicly, iii. d. 93.<BR> III. instr. क्षेण, At sight, Hit. i. d. 98, M.M.; evidently, Hit. 106, 12.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Perception, Bhāṣāp. 51.<BR> 2. Superintendence, Man. 9, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्ष|अप्रत्यक्षः
अ- + प्रत्यक्ष अ- + प्रत्यक्ष, adj. 1. not seen by one's own eyes Man. 8, 95. 2. unknown, Rām. 4, 9, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षता
प्रत्यक्षता प्रत्यक्ष + ता, f. Visibility, Pañc. 256, 10 (˚तया, visibly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षय
प्रत्यक्षय प्रत्यक्षय, a denomin. derived from प्रत्यक्ष with अय, To make visible, Mālav. 20, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्र|प्रत्यग्रः
प्रत्यग्र प्रत्यग्र, i. e. प्रति-अग्र, adj. New, fresh, Vikr. d. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्ग|प्रत्यंग|प्रत्यङ्गं
प्रत्यङ्ग प्रत्यङ्ग, i. e. प्रति-अङ्ग,<BR> I. n. A minor member of the body, as the chin, nose, etc.<BR> II. गम्, adv.<BR> 1. Limb by limb, Pañc. 183, 21.<BR> 2. Each part, Man. 8, 208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्च्|प्रत्यंच्
प्रत्यञ्च् प्रत्यञ्च्, i. e. प्रति-अञ्च्,<BR> I. adj., f. तीची.<BR> 1. Proceeding to, Chr. 289, 5 = Rigv. i. 50, 5.<BR> 2. Behind, following [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b " target="_blank">Page0597-b + 41</a>] in time or place.<BR> 3. West, western.<BR> 4. Inward, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 24; 17; 211, 22; 210, 12.<BR> II. यक्, adv. with abl.<BR> 1. Behind, following in time or place.<BR> 2. To the west, Man. 2, 21.<BR> III. f. तीची, The west quarter, Draup. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनन्तर|प्रत्यनंतर
प्रत्यनन्तर प्रत्यनन्तर, i. e. प्रति-अन्-अन्तर, adj. Next, Man. 10, 81. m. The next heir, Man. 8, 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनीक|प्रत्यनीकः
प्रत्यनीक प्रत्यनीक, i. e. प्रति-अनीक,<BR> I. adj. sbst. Hostile, an enemy, Bhāg. P. 5, 24, 30.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A hostile army, MBh. 7, 1986.<BR> 2. Enmity, 6, 571.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यन्तर
प्रत्यन्तर प्रत्यन्तर, i. e. प्रति-अन्तर, adj. Near, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 5 (is it to be changed to प्रत्यनन्तरी? cf. प्रत्यनन्तर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञा
प्रत्यभिज्ञा प्रत्यभिज्ञा, f., and प्रत्यभिज्ञान प्रत्यभिज्ञान, n., i. e. प्रति-अभि-ज्ञा, without aff. and with अन, Recognition Bhāṣāp. 159 (ज्ञा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवाद|प्रत्यभिवादः
प्रत्यभिवाद प्रत्यभिवाद, i. e. प्रति + अभि-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Returning a salute.<BR> 2. The benediction of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यय|प्रत्ययः
प्रत्यय प्रत्यय, i. e. प्रति-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Knowledge, Utt. Rāmac. 162, 6.<BR> 2. Ascertainment, certainty, proof, Pañc. iii. d. 91; 64, 12.<BR> 3. Decisive sentence, Pañc. 165, 4.<BR> 4. Usage, practice.<BR> 5. Truth, belief, Utt. Rāmac. 116, 1; confidence, Kathās. 49, 122; dependence on (loc.), Pañc. i. d. 373.<BR> 6. Oath, ordeal, Man. 8, 178.<BR> 7. Instrument, means of agency.<BR> 8. A helpmate.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यय|अप्रत्ययः
अ- + प्रत्यय अ- + प्रत्यय,<BR> I. m. mistrust, Pañc. i. d. 204.<BR> II. adj. not confiding, Śāk. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययित|प्रत्ययितः
प्रत्ययित प्रत्ययित, i. e. प्रत्यय + इत, adj. Trusted, trusting, Pañc. 216, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययिन्
प्रत्ययिन् प्रत्ययिन्, i. e. प्रत्यय + इन्, adj. Trustworthy, Rām. 6, 5, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिन्
प्रत्यर्थिन् प्रत्यर्थिन्, i. e. प्रति-अर्थिन्, m. A defendant, Man. 8, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवभास
ऽप्रत्यवभास -प्रत्यवभास, i. e. प्रति-अव-भास् + अ, in आकस्मिक-, adj., f. सा, Appearing on a sudden, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्श|प्रत्यवमर्शः
प्रत्यवमर्श प्रत्यवमर्श, i. e. प्रति-अव-मृश् + अ, m. Meditation on, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्ष|प्रत्यवमर्षः
प्रत्यवमर्ष प्रत्यवमर्ष, i. e. प्रति-अव-मृष् + अ, m. Return and continuation, Hariv. 1203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवर
प्रत्यवर प्रत्यवर, i. e. प्रति-अवर, adj. Lower, less valued, Man. 10, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसान|प्रत्यवसानं
प्रत्यवसान प्रत्यवसान, i. e. प्रति-अव-सो + अन, n. Eating, Pāṇ. 1, 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवाय|प्रत्यवायः
प्रत्यवाय प्रत्यवाय, i. e. प्रति-अव-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Decrease, Bhag. 2, 40.<BR> 2. Disappearance.<BR> 3. Disappointment, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 10.<BR> 4. Reverse, contrary course, Man. 4, 245.<BR> 5. Disadvantage, Prab. 12, 13.<BR> 6. Sin, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षा
प्रत्यवेक्षा प्रत्यवेक्षा, i. e. प्रति-अव-ईक्ष् + अ, f.<BR> 1. Attention, Rājat. 5, 168 (‘having directed his mind to stealing,’ read मुषे instead of मुखे).<BR> 2. Management, 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यहम्
प्रत्यहम् प्रत्यहम्, i. e. प्रति-अह + म्, adv. Day by day, Pañc. 191, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यान|प्रत्याख्यानं
प्रत्याख्यान प्रत्याख्यान, i. e. प्रति-आ-ख्या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rejection.<BR> 2. Refusing, Hit. i. d. 12, M.M.; denial.<BR> 3. Reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादर्श
प्रत्यादर्श प्रत्यादर्श, i. e. प्रति-आ-दृश् + अ, m. An image, Pañc. iii. d. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादेश|प्रत्यादेशः
प्रत्यादेश प्रत्यादेश, i. e. प्रति-आ-दिश् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b " target="_blank">Page0598-b + 40</a>] m.<BR> 1. Rejection, repudiation, Śāk. d. 183.<BR> 2. Refusal, abstemiousness, Megh. 93.<BR> 3. Eclipsing, Daśak. 138, 3.<BR> 4. Prevention, Man. 8, 344.<BR> 5. Informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानयन|प्रत्यानयनं
प्रत्यानयन प्रत्यानयन, i. e. प्रति-आ-नी + अन, n. Bringing back, Vikr. 5, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याशा
प्रत्याशा प्रत्याशा, i. e. प्रति-आशा, f.<BR> 1. Desire (ŚKD.), Daśak. 195, 18.<BR> 2. Hope, expectation, Vikr. 40, 17 (स-प्रत्याश + म्, Full of expectation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासर|प्रत्यासरः
प्रत्यासर and प्रत्यासार प्रत्यासा̆र, i. e. प्रति-आ-सृ + अ, m. The rear of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरण|प्रत्याहरणं
प्रत्याहरण प्रत्याहरण, n., and प्रत्याहार प्रत्याहार, m., i. e. प्रति-आ-हृ + अन or अ.<BR> 1. Taking back.<BR> 2. Recovering, Vikr. 11, 15.<BR> 3. Restraining the organs of sense, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 18; Man. 6, 72.<BR> 4. Withholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रम|प्रत्युत्क्रमः
प्रत्युत्क्रम प्रत्युत्क्रम, m., and प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति, f., i. e. प्रति-उद्-क्रम् + अ or ति.<BR> 1. Beginning.<BR> 2. Effort.<BR> 3. Setting out to assail an enemy.<BR> 4. Declaration of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्तर|प्रत्युत्तरं
प्रत्युत्तर प्रत्युत्तर, i. e. प्रति-उत्तर, n.<BR> 1. A reply to an answer.<BR> 2. An answer, Hit. 64, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थान|प्रत्युत्थानं
प्रत्युत्थान प्रत्युत्थान, i. e. प्रति-उद्-स्था + अन, n. Rising from a seat as a mark of respect, Pañc. 117, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गम|प्रत्युद्गमः
प्रत्युद्गम प्रत्युद्गम, m., and प्रत्युद्गमन प्रत्युद्गमन, n., i. e. प्रति-उद्-गम् + अ or अन.<BR> 1. Rising from a seat as a mark of respect.<BR> 2. Going to meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धरण|प्रत्युद्धरणं
प्रत्युद्धरण प्रत्युद्धरण, i. e. प्रति-उद्-हृ + अन, n. Recovering, reobtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकार|प्रत्युपकारः
प्रत्युपकार प्रत्युपकार, i. e. प्रति-उप-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Service in return, Pañc. 207, 17.<BR> 2. Requital, Rājat. 5, 190.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःप्रत्युपकार|पुनःप्रत्युपकारः
पुनःप्रत्युपकार पुनःप्र्˚, i. e. पुनर्-, m. requital, Pañc. i. d. 384.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपमान|प्रत्युपमानं
प्रत्युपमान प्रत्युपमान, i. e. प्रति-उपमान, n. A counter-comparison, Vikr. d. 22 (उपमानस्यापि, of every comparison, i. e. incomparable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युष|प्रत्युषः
प्रत्युष and प्रत्यूष प्रत्यू̆ष, i. e. प्रति-उषस्, m. Morning, dawn, Pañc 40, 13 (उ); 27, 5 (ऊ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषस्
प्रत्यूषस् प्रत्यूषस्, i. e. प्रति-उषस्, n. Morning, dawn, Lass. 57, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूह|प्रत्यूहः
प्रत्यूह प्रत्यूह, प्रति-ऊह् + अ, m. Obstacle, Hit. ii. d. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्येकम्
प्रत्येकम् प्रत्येकम्, i. e. प्रति-एक + म्, adv. One by one, Prab. 44, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्वक्षस्
प्रत्वक्षस् प्र-त्वक्षस् (ved.), adj. Possessed of great energy, Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 87, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथ्
प्रथ् प्रथ्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To be extended, to spread, Chr. 295, 12 = Rigv. i. 92, 12 (ved. ptcple. of the pres. प्रथान).<BR> 2. To be unfolded, Rājat. 5, 366.<BR> 3. To be famous, Rām. 2, 61, 2.<BR> --Caus. प्रथय,<BR> 1. To extend, Bhartṛ. 2, 37.<BR> 2. To show, Kir. 5, 3.<BR> 3. (and i. 10 प्राथय?) To praise, Rām. 1, 4, 1; cf. पृथ्.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्रथित, Renowned, Rām. 3, 53, 12.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, विप्रथित, Spread, MBh. 2, 2667.<BR> --Caus. To praise, MBh. 3, 10277.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. interpretari, perhaps Goth. frathjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम प्र + थ + म,<BR> I. ordinal number, f. मा.<BR> 1. First, Hit. 77, 1, M.M.; prior, Vikr. 14, 6.<BR> 2. Chief, excellent, Śāk. 99, 23.<BR> II. मम्, adv.<BR> 1. First, Vikr. d. 132.<BR> 2. Previously, Vikr. d. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमतस्
प्रथमतस् प्रथम + तस्, adv. First, Bhāṣāp. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथा
प्रथा प्रथ् + आ, f. Fame, celebrity, Rājat. 5, 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिति|प्रथितिः
प्रथिति प्रथिति, i. e. प्रथ् + ति, f. Celebrity, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमन्
प्रथिमन् प्रथिमन्, i. e. पृथु + इमन्, m. Greatness, Ragh. 18, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिष्ठ|प्रथिष्ठः
प्रथिष्ठ प्रथिष्ठ, प्रथीयंस् प्रथीयंस्, see पृथु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुक|प्रथुकः
प्रथुक प्रथुक (cf. पृथुक), m. The young of any animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद|प्रदः
प्रद प्र-द (vb. दा),<BR> I. adj. sbst. Giving, Vikr. d. 9; a giver, Rājat. 5, 162.<BR> II. f. दा, A gift.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यप्रद
पुण्य- + प्रद पुण्य- + प्रद, adj. meritorious, Hariv. 351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं|प्रदक्षिणः
प्रदक्षिण प्र-दक्षिण,<BR> I. adj., f. णा, Being at the right hand, Man. 4, 39.<BR> II. m., f. णा, and n. Reverential salutation by circumambulating a person or object, keeping the right side towards them, Pañc. 236, 8.<BR> III. णम्, adv.<BR> 1. From left to right, Man. 2, 48.<BR> 2. Proceeding from the east in a southern direction, 3, 87.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रदक्षिणम्
अभि-प्रदक्षि-णम् अभि-प्रदक्षि-णम्, adv. From left to right, Rām. 1, 15, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणसव्य
प्रदक्षिणसव्य प्र-दक्षिण-सव्य, adj. Having the right hand next to the left of the adversary (watching for an opportunity of striking a blow at the unguarded side).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर|प्रदरः
प्रदर प्रदर, i. e. प्र-दॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Scattering, MBh. 12, 3715 (an army).<BR> 2. A cleft, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 6.<BR> 3. Fracture.<BR> 4. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शक|प्रदर्शकः
प्रदर्शक प्रदर्शक, i. e. प्र-दृश् + अक, m. A teacher, MBh. 2, 1452.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदल|प्रदलः
प्रदल प्रदल (= प्रदर), m. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदातृ
प्रदातृ प्र-दा + तृ, m. A giver, Rājat. 5, 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदान|प्रदानं
प्रदान प्रदान, i. e. प्र-दा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Giving, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 17.<BR> 2. Gift, Pañc. 184, 2; delivery 101, 11.<BR> 3. Giving in marriage, marriage, Śāk. d. 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दप्रदान
अवस्कन्द- + प्रदान अवस्कन्द- + प्रदान, n. Giving the opportunity of being surprised, Pañc. iii. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायिन्
प्रदायिन् प्रदायिन्, i. e. प्र-दा + इन्, adj. sbst. Giving, a giver, Man. 3, 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् प्र-दिश्, f. Intermediate point of the compass, or half-quarter, as north-east, Matsyop. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप|प्रदीपः
प्रदीप प्र-दीप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A lamp, Hit. i. d. 167, M.M.<BR> 2. Splendour, Śāk. 7, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपन|प्रदीपनः
प्रदीपन प्र-दीप् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Inflaming, Suśr. 1, 177, 10.<BR> II. m. A kind of poison.<BR> III. n. Kindling, Rām. 5, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्ति|प्रदीप्तिः
प्रदीप्ति प्र-दीप् + ति, f. Light, lustre, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्तिमन्त्|प्रदीप्तिमत्
प्रदीप्तिमन्त् प्रदीप्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मति, Radiant, luminous, Johns. Sel. 94, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेश|प्रदेशः
प्रदेश प्रदेश, i. e. प्र-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A place, Pañc. 118, 14; part, 134, 20 (पृष्ठ-प्रदेशे, from behind).<BR> 2. A country, Pañc. 159, 21.<BR> 3. A foreign country.<BR> 4. A short span, measured from the tip of the thumb to that of the forefinger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशन|प्रदेशनं
प्रदेशन प्रदेशन, i. e. प्र-दिश् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A present.<BR> 2. A bribe.<BR> II. f. नी, The forefinger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशस्थ
प्रदेशस्थ प्रदेश-स्थ, adj. Situated in a district, Rājat. 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशिनी
प्रदेशिनी प्रदेशिनी, i. e. प्र-दिश् + इन् + ई, f. The forefinger, Rājat. 5, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेह|प्रदेहः
प्रदेह प्रदेह, i. e. प्र-दिह् + अ, m. Unguent, unction, Suśr. 1, 42, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोष|प्रदोषः
प्रदोष प्र-दोष, m.<BR> 1. Offence.<BR> 2. Evening, the first part of the night, Pañc. 186, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीप्रदोष
ग्रहणी- + प्रदोष ग्रहणी- + प्रदोष, m. Diarrhœa, Suśr. 2, 186, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्न|प्रद्युम्नः
प्रद्युम्न प्र-द्युम्न, m. The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योत|प्रद्योतः
प्रद्योत प्र-द्योत, m.<BR> 1. A ray of light.<BR> 2. Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधन|प्रधनं
प्रधन प्र-धन (see निधन), n.<BR> 1. Tearing, destroying, Megh. 49; destruction, Utt. Rāmac. 119, 7.<BR> 2. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधान|प्रधानं|प्रधानः
प्रधान प्रधान, i. e. प्र-धा + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Nature, MBh. 13, 1009.<BR> 2. The Supreme God.<BR> 3. Intellect.<BR> 4. Chief, Hit. 49, 18; principal (only sing.), excellent, Pañc. 156, 15.<BR> 5. The first companion of a king, his minister, his confidant, etc.<BR> II. adj. Chief, principal, Pañc. i. d. 324; Hit. 60, 22; Bhartṛ. 2, 99.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधान|अप्रधानं
अ- + प्रधान अ- + प्रधान, adj. not principal, not minister, subordinate, inferior, Hit. 51, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्प्रधान
तद्- + प्रधान तद्- + प्रधान, adj. having her (viz. his wife) as chief, i. e. performed principally with her assistance, Man. 3, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रधान|धर्म्मप्रधान
धर्म- + प्रधान धर्म- + प्रधान, adj. loving justice, Man. 4, 243.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रधान
निष्प्रधान निष्प्र्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. deprived of one's chief, Rām. 2, 111, 16 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाप्रधानम्
यथा-प्रधान + म् यथा-प्रधान + म्, adv. according to their chiefs, represented by their chiefs, Johns. Sel. 46, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धसत्त्वप्रधान
विशुद्ध-सत्त्व- + प्रधान विशुद्ध-सत्त्व- + प्रधान, adj., f. ना, having the nature of pure goodness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानतस्
प्रधानतस् प्रधान + तस्, adv. According to superiority, Man. 9, 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानता
प्रधानता प्रधान + ता, f.<BR> 1. Condition of a thing's nature, latter part of comp. words; e. g. स्व-प्रधान + ता The character of one's own nature, Vedāntas in Chr. 206, 12.<BR> 2. Supremacy. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a " target="_blank">Page0601-a + 39</a>] excellence, Rām. 3, 49, 12.<BR> 3. Ministership, Hit. 52, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधानता
अ-प्रधान + ता अ-प्रधान + ता, f. the condition of not being minister, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधि|प्रधिः
प्रधि प्रधि, i. e. प्र-धा (cf. निधि), m. The periphery of a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्यान|प्रध्यानं
प्रध्यान प्रध्यान, i. e. प्र-ध्यै + अन, n.<BR> 1. Thinking.<BR> 2. Thought, Johns. Sel. 92, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनप्तृ
प्रनप्तृ प्र-नप्तृ, m. A great grandson.<BR> --Cf. Lat. prŏnepos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिघातन|प्रनिघातनं
प्रनिघातन प्रनिघातन, i. e. प्र-नि-हन्, Caus., + अन, n. Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्च|प्रपंच|प्रपंचः|प्रपञ्चः
प्रपञ्च प्रपञ्च, m.<BR> 1. Extent.<BR> 2. Development, analysis, Bhāṣāp. 126.<BR> 3. Prolixity.<BR> 4. Heap.<BR> 5. Error.<BR> 6. Delusion, deceit, Pañc. 256, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपद|प्रपदं
प्रपद प्र-पद, n. The point of the foot, the tip of the toes, Draup. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायन|प्रपलायनं
प्रपलायन प्र-पलायन, n. Flight, Pañc. i. d. 362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपा
प्रपा प्र-पा, f. A cistern, Man. 8, 319.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाठक|प्रपाठकः
प्रपाठक प्रपाठक, i. e. प्र-पठ् + अ + क, m. A chapter, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणि|प्रपाणिः
प्रपाणि प्र-पाणि, m. The palm of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपात|प्रपातः
प्रपात प्र-पात, m.<BR> 1. A precipice, Śāk. d. 137.<BR> 2. A bank, Ragh. 2, 26.<BR> 3. A cascade.<BR> 4. Flying forward, Pañc. ii. d. 57.<BR> 5. Hastening away, Kathās. 43, 264.<BR> 6. Throwing one's self, Pañc. iii. d. 238.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिप्रपात|गिरिप्रपातः
गिरि- + प्रपात गिरि- + प्रपात, m. a precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्रपात|जलप्रपातः
जल- + प्रपात जल- + प्रपात, m. A cascade, Rām. 2, 94, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपावन|प्रपावनं
प्रपावन प्रपा-वन, n. A grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामह|प्रपितामहः
प्रपितामह प्र-पितामह,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A paternal great-grandfather, Bhag. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b " target="_blank">Page0601-b + 42</a>] 11, 39.<BR> 2. pl. Ancestors, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 5.<BR> 3. A name of Brahman.<BR> II. f. ही, A paternal great-grandmother.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रपितामह|वृद्धप्रपितामहः
वृद्ध- + प्रपितामह वृद्ध- + प्रपितामह,<BR> I. m. a paternal great-greatgrandfather.<BR> II. f. ही, a paternal great-great-grandmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपित्सु
प्रपित्सु प्रपित्सु, i. e. प्र-पित्स, desider. of पत्, + उ, adj. Being about to descend, to alight, Śiś. 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरण|प्रपूरणं
प्रपूरण प्रपूरण, i. e. प्र-पूर् + अन (see पृ), n. The drawing of a bowstring, Rām. 1, 60, 10 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्र|प्रपौत्रः
प्रपौत्र प्र-पौत्र,<BR> 1. and ˚त्रक त्र + क, m. A great-grandson, Kathās. 9, 7, Yājñ. 1, 78.<BR> 2. f. त्री, A great-granddaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्ध|प्रबंध|प्रबंधः|प्रबन्धः
प्रबन्ध प्र-बन्ध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Uninterrupted connexion.<BR> 2. Continuous application, Hit. 47, 3, M.M.; action.<BR> 3. A connected narrative, composition, Utt. Rāmac. 112, 5.<BR> 4. A literary production, Mālav. 3, 2 bel.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रबन्ध|अतिप्रबंधः|अतिप्रबन्धः
अति- + प्रबन्ध अति- + प्रबन्ध, m. Uninterruptedness, Ragh. 3, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटप्रबन्ध|कपटप्रबंध|कपटप्रबन्धः
कपट- + प्रबन्ध कपट- + प्रबन्ध, m. A fraudulent design, Hit. 21, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टरसप्रबन्ध
दृष्ट-रस- + प्रबन्ध दृष्ट-रस- + प्रबन्ध, adj. one who has seen dramas, Vikr. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबल|प्रबलः
प्रबल प्र-बल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Prevailing, Hiḍ. 4, 46; strong, Ṛt. 1, 24; powerful.<BR> 2. Violent, Vikr. d. 81.<BR> 3. Much, Rājat. 5, 68.<BR> II. m. A sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाल|प्रबालं|प्रबालः
प्रबाल प्र-बाल, m. and n.<BR> 1. Coral, Rām. 3, 49, 4.<BR> 2. A sprout, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 18.<BR> 3. A new leaf.<BR> 4. The bridge of a lute, through which the strings are drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोध|प्रबोधः
प्रबोध प्रबोध, i. e. प्र-बुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Waking, Hit. iii. d. 142; vigilance.<BR> 2. Awaking either from sleep or ignorance, Pañc. 37, 20.<BR> 3. Knowledge, intellect.<BR> 4. Awakening, Rām. 6, 37, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधन|प्रबोधनं
प्रबोधन प्रबोधन, i. e. प्र-बुध्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Awakening, Pañc. 4, 13; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a " target="_blank">Page0602-a + 43</a>] recalling to life, Utt. Rāmac. 460, 10.<BR> 2. Instructing, Pañc. 4, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्जन|प्रभंजन|प्रभंजनं|प्रभञ्जनः
प्रभञ्जन प्र-भञ्ज् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Breaking down.<BR> II. m. Air or wind, Hit. ii. d. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्रभव प्रभव, i. e. प्र-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Generative cause, the root of existence, origin, Draup. 2, 5; Bhag. 7, 6.<BR> 2. The father.<BR> 3. The mother.<BR> 4. The place of receiving existence, birth-place.<BR> 5. Birth.<BR> 6. Strength, superiority.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरप्रभव|अन्तरप्रभवः
अन्तर- + प्रभव अन्तर- + प्रभव, m. a mixed class produced by the intermixture of different castes, Man. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्पुण्यप्रभव
प्राञ्च्-पुण्य- + प्रभव प्राञ्च्-पुण्य- + प्रभव, adj. caused by the merits of a former existence, Pañc. iii. d. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषिप्रभव
विद्वेषिप्रभव विद्वेषिप्र्˚, i. e. विद्वेषिन्-, adj. proceeding from an enemy, Pañc. i. d. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणिप्रभव|स्पर्शमणिप्रभवं
स्पर्श-मणि- + प्रभव स्पर्श-मणि- + प्रभव, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवितृ
प्रभवितृ प्रभवितृ, i. e. प्र-भू + तृ, m. A mighty one, Bhartṛ. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्रभविष्णु प्रभविष्णु, i. e. प्र-भू + इष्णु,<BR> I. adj. Mighty, pre-eminent, Bhag. 13, 16.<BR> II. m. A master, a lord, Śāk. 24, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा प्र-भा, f.<BR> 1. Light, Rām. 3, 53, 47.<BR> 2. Radiance, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1155; splendour, Vikr. d. 125.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरप्रभा
अ-चिर-प्रभा अ-चिर-प्रभा, f. lightning, Vikr. d. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रभ
आत्मप्रभ आत्मप्रभ, i. e. आत्मन्-, adj. enlightened by themselves, Indr. 1, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभ|निष्प्रभः
निष्प्रभ निष्प्रभ, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. भा, deprived of light or radiance, MBh. 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातमप्रभा
महातमप्रभा महातमप्रभा, i. e. महा-तम- (for तमस्), f. the lowermost hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समप्रभ
सम-प्रभ सम-प्रभ, adj., f. भा, of equal splendour, Lass. 51, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभा
सु- + प्रभा सु- + प्रभा, adj. splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकर|प्रभाकरः
प्रभाकर प्रभा-कर, m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR> 3. Fire.<BR> 4. A proper name = Kumārilasvāmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाव|प्रभावः
प्रभाव प्रभाव, i. e. प्र-भू + अ. m.<BR> 1. Power, Vikr. 73, 4; Pañc. 29, 20.<BR> 2. Celestial power, Vikr. d. 30.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b " target="_blank">Page0602-b + 42</a>] Dignity.<BR> 4. Majesty.<BR> 5. Magnanimity, high spirit, Pañc. 29, 15. (गत-, adj. humbled).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंप्रभाव
किंप्रभाव किंप्रभाव, i. e. किम्-, adj. possessed of how large a power, Pañc. 258, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाप्रभाव
तथा- + प्रभाव तथा- + प्रभाव, adj. possessed of such a power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावत्व
ऽप्रभावत्व -प्रभाव + त्व, in अल्प-, n. Small ability, Hit. iv. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावन्त्|प्रभावत्
प्रभावन्त् प्रभा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Luminous, splendid, Pañc. i. d. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु प्र-भु (vb. भू),<BR> I. adj., f. भ्वी and भु.<BR> 1. Strong.<BR> 2. Able; with gen., Man. 11, 30; with inf., Mālav. d. 9.<BR> 3. Eternal, Sund. 1, 19.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A master, a lord, Vikr. 12, 8; Bhartṛ. 2, 12; a husband, Śṛṅgārat. 2.<BR> 2. A name of Viṣṇu, cf. Johns. Sel. 51, 111.<BR> 3. Sound.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभु
अ- + प्रभु अ- + प्रभु, adj. unable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्प्रभु|किंप्रभु|किम्प्रभुः
किम्- + प्रभु किम्- + प्रभु, m. A bad master, Hit. ii. d. 31 (read किंप्रभु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकप्रभु
चम्पक- + प्रभु चम्पक- + प्रभु, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्प्रभु|जगत्प्रभुः
जगत्- + प्रभु जगत्- + प्रभु, m. the lord of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुता
प्रभुता प्रभु + ता, f. Power, Śāk. d. 122; supremacy, sovereignty, tyranny, Vikr. d. 89; स्व-प्रभुतया, arbitrarily, Pañc. 26, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुत्व|प्रभुत्वं
प्रभुत्व प्रभु + त्व, n. Sovereignty, Pañc. 63, 17; power, Hit. Pr. d. 11, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभुत्व
अ- + प्रभुत्व अ- + प्रभुत्व, n. weakness, Pañc. 69, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतता
प्रभूतता प्र-भूत + ता, f., and प्रभूतत्व प्र-भूत + त्व, n. Plenty, Pañc. 171, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्रभूष्णु प्रभूष्णु, i. e. प्र-भू + स्नु, adj. Strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृति|प्रभृतिः
प्रभृति प्र-भृ + ति (originally, Beginning), ind. with abl. Beginning and continuing from, since, Pañc. 264, 5; Man. 9, 68. It is usually the latter part of comp. nouns implying, And those of the same kind (as the former part), the remainder, others, etc.; e. g. बृहस्पति-, m. The planet Jupiter [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a " target="_blank">Page0603-a + 42</a>] and the other planets, Bhartṛ. 2, 27, cf. Pañc. 157, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यप्रभृति
अद्य- + प्रभृति अद्य- + प्रभृति, adv. from to-day, Chr. 61, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततःप्रभृति
ततस्- + प्रभृति ततस्- + प्रभृति, adv. from that time, Hit. 57, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेद|प्रभेदः
प्रभेद प्रभेद, i. e. प्र-भिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Division, cutting through, Bhartṛ. 3, 23.<BR> 2. Difference, Bhāṣāp. 51.<BR> 3. Kind, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टक|प्रभ्रष्टकं
प्रभ्रष्टक प्र-भ्रष्ट + क (vb. भ्रंश्), n. A chaplet of flowers suspended from the middle lock of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ|प्रमथः
प्रमथ प्र-मथ् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. An attendant on Śiva, MBh. 13, 983.<BR> II. f. था, Terminalia chebula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथन|प्रमथनं
प्रमथन प्र-मथ् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Paining, MBh. 1, 2793.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Killing.<BR> 2. Paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्रमद प्र-मद् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. दा.<BR> 1. Mad, intoxicated.<BR> 2. Impassioned.<BR> II. m. Joy.<BR> III. f. A handsome woman, a woman, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 20; Pañc. iii. d. 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमय|प्रमयः
प्रमय प्रमय, i. e. प्र-मी + अ, m. Death, Rājat. 4, 708.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा प्र-मा, f. True perception, true knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 125.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमा
अ- + प्रमा अ- + प्रमा, f. wrong knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 125. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाण|प्रमाणं|प्रमाणः
प्रमाण प्रमाण, i. e. प्र-म + अन, n.<BR> 1. Measure, Pañc. i. d. 371; a scale, Hit. i. d. 12, M.M.; analogy, Hit. 110, 12; quantity, power, Pañc. 75, 22.<BR> 2. Authority.<BR> 3. Decision, a decider, Śāk. 61, 8; Pañc. 30, 18; 34, 10.<BR> 4. A work of sacred authority.<BR> 5. Proof, Pañc. iii. d. 93; evidence.<BR> 6. Cause.<BR> 7. Principal.<BR> 8. A title of Viṣṇu.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रमाण
अति- + प्रमाण अति- + प्रमाण, adj. of exceeding largeness, Rām. 5, 54, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रमाण
अनु- + प्रमाण अनु- + प्रमाण, adj. suitable, Suśr. 2, 7, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणतस्
प्रमाणतस् प्रमाण + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. With respect to measure, Man. 2, 46. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b " target="_blank">Page0603-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. Agreeably to measure.<BR> 3. According to authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणय
प्रमाणय प्रमाणय, a denomin. derived from प्रमाण with अय, Par.<BR> 1. To receive as authority, Hit. i. d. 9, M.M.<BR> 2. To prove, Rājat. 5, 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामह|प्रमातामहः
प्रमातामह प्र-मातामह,<BR> 1. m. A maternal great-grandfather.<BR> 2. f. ही, A maternal great-grandmother.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रमातामह|वृद्धप्रमातामहः
वृद्ध- + प्रमातामह वृद्ध- + प्रमातामह,<BR> I. m. a maternal great-great-grandfather.<BR> II. f. ही, a maternal great-great-grandmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्रमातृ प्र-मा + तृ, m. One who knows well, an authority, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमात्व
प्रमात्व प्रमा + त्व, n. The state of true knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथ|प्रमाथः
प्रमाथ प्रमाथ, i. e. प्र-मथ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Paining, torturing.<BR> 2. Violence.<BR> 3. Carrying off forcibly (ŚKD.), Draup. title.<BR> 4. Killing, Utt. Rāmac. 120, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्रमाथिन् प्रमाथिन्, i. e. प्र-मथ् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Agitating, MBh. 12, 9040.<BR> 2. Afflicting, torturing, ib. 3, 16435.<BR> 3. Killing, destroying, a destroyer, Chr. 34, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद|प्रमादः
प्रमाद प्रमाद, i. e. प्र-मद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Intoxication.<BR> 2. Insanity, distraction, Utt. Rāmac. 51, 5.<BR> 3. Inadvertence, carelessness, Pañc. iii. d. 243.<BR> 4. Distress, Utt. Rāmac. 61, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाद|अप्रमादः
अ- + प्रमाद अ- + प्रमाद,<BR> I. m. carefulness, Rām. 2, 85, 14.<BR> II. adj. careful, 3, 49, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका प्रमादिका, i. e. प्रमादिन् + क, f. A deflowered girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन् प्रमादिन्, i. e. प्रमाद + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Intoxicated.<BR> 2. Insane.<BR> 3. Careless, Pañc. i. d. 20; imprudent, Vikr. 30, 14; Hit. ii. d. 173.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादिन्
अ- + प्रमादिन् अ- + प्रमादिन्, adj. careful, vigilant, Man. 2, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापण|प्रमापणं
प्रमापण प्रमापण, i. e.<BR> A. प्र-मी, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj. Killing, Yājñ. 2, 279.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Killing.<BR> 2. Slaughter, Man. 11, 140.<BR> B. प्र-मे, Caus., + अन, n. Change, MBh. 12, 13252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिति|प्रमितिः
प्रमिति प्रमिति, i. e. प्र-मा + ति, f.<BR> 1. Measure.<BR> 2. True knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्रमीला प्र-मील् + आ, f. Lassitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुख|प्रमुखं|प्रमुखः
प्रमुख प्र-मुख, adj., f. खा.<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. First, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 6.<BR> 2. Chief, Hit. iii. d. 83.<BR> 3. Best.<BR> II. n. Mouth, Johns. Sel. 15, 55 (cf. p. 39, n.).<BR> III. खे, loc., adverbially.<BR> 1. In presence, Śāk. d. 181.<BR> 2. In front, Chr. 30, 5.<BR> IV. खतस्, adv. At the head, Johns. Sel. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोक्ष|प्रमोक्षः
प्रमोक्ष प्र-मोक्ष, m. The liberation of the soul from the body and exemption from transmigration, eternal happiness, Brāhmaṇ. 2, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोचन|प्रमोचनं
प्रमोचन प्रमोचन, i. e. प्र-मुच् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Liberating, MBh. 3, 8031.<BR> II. n. Liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोद|प्रमोदः
प्रमोद प्रमोद, i. e. प्र-मुद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hilarity, Man. 3, 61; joy, Vikr. d. 153.<BR> 2. Fragrance, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदन|प्रमोदनं|प्रमोदनः
प्रमोदन प्रमोदन, i. e. प्र-मुद् + अन, n. Hilarity, Lass. 87, 8 (स-प्र-मोदन + म्, adv. Cheerfully).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोह|प्रमोहः
प्रमोह प्रमोह, i. e. प्र-मुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Fascination.<BR> 2. Fainting, insensibility, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 6.<BR> 3. Confusion, Draup. 6, 20 (-चित्त, adj. bewildered in mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लोचा
प्रम्लोचा प्रम्लोचा, i. e. प्र-म्लुच् + अ, f. One of the Apsaras, Lass. 50, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयज्यु
प्रयज्यु प्र-यज् + यु, adj. To be worshipped especially, Chr. 292, 7 = Rigv. i. 86, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्न|प्रयत्नः
प्रयत्न प्र-यत्न, m.<BR> 1. Persevering [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b " target="_blank">Page0604-b + 41</a>] exertion, effort, Vikr. d. 143.<BR> 2. Great care, Man. 3, 79.<BR> 3. Difficulty, Śāk. 5, 11 (scarcely).<BR> 4. Articulation of sound, Pāṇ. 1, 1, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्न|अप्रयत्नः
अ- + प्रयत्न अ- + प्रयत्न, adj. not solicitous, Man. 6, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयत्न
निष्प्रयत्न निष्प्रयत्न, i. e. निस्-, adj. abstaining from any exertion, Hariv. 2514.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नतस्
प्रयत्नतस् प्रयत्न + तस्, adv. With great care, Man. 3, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नवन्त्|प्रयत्नवत्
प्रयत्नवन्त् प्रयत्न + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Taking great care, Pañc. iii. d. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् प्रयस्, i. e. प्री + अस्, n. Sacrifice, Chr. 292, 7 = Rigv. i. 86, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाग|प्रयागः
प्रयाग प्रयाग, i. e. प्र-यज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sacrifice.<BR> 2. A celebrated place of pilgrimage, the confluence of the Gangā and Yamunā, Chr. 46, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाण|प्रयाणं
प्रयाण प्रयाण, i. e. प्र-या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going forth, march, Pañc. 8, 19.<BR> 2. Going, Hit. iv. d. 80.<BR> 3. Attack, Pañc. 232, 16; invasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयास|प्रयासः
प्रयास प्रयास, i. e. प्र-यस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Labour, fatigue, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 11.<BR> 2. Effort, Pañc. 82, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्ति|प्रयुक्तिः
प्रयुक्ति प्रयुक्ति, i. e. प्र-युज् + ति, f. Object, Utt. Rāmac. 124, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत|प्रयुतं
प्रयुत प्र-युत (vb. यु), n. A million, Chr. 33, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तृ
प्रयोक्तृ प्रयोक्तृ, i. e. प्र-युज् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. Creator, Utt. Rāmac. 89, 2.<BR> 2. A mime, Ragh. 19, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोग|प्रयोगः
प्रयोग प्रयोग, i. e. प्र-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Throwing missiles, Arj. 5, 6.<BR> 2. Application, employment, Pañc. i. d. 205; use, Śiś. 9, 79.<BR> 3. Example, comparison.<BR> 4. Lending money at interest, Man. 10, 115.<BR> 5. Appointing.<BR> 6. Ceremonial form, course of proceeding.<BR> 7. Device, contrivance,<BR> 8. Act, action, practice, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 10.<BR> 9. Dramatic performance, Vikr. d. 36. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a " target="_blank">Page0605-a + 42</a>]<BR> 10. Affair, matter.<BR> 11. Cause, motive, occasion, object.<BR> 12. Consequence, result.<BR> 13. Magic, magical rites.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रयोग|अर्थप्रयोगः
अर्थ- + प्रयोग अर्थ- + प्रयोग, m. lending money, Cāṇ. 22 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रयोग|विधिप्रयोगः
विधि- + प्रयोग विधि- + प्रयोग, m. acting in conformity to a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयोग|सुप्रयोगः
सु- + प्रयोग सु- + प्रयोग, m. 1. approximation. 2. dexterity, expertness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगतस्
प्रयोगतस् प्रयोग + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. By employing, Hit. iii. d. 60.<BR> 2. According to.<BR> 3. Actually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजक|प्रयोजकः
प्रयोजक प्रयोजक, i. e. प्र-युज् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who or what causes.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An author, Yājñ. 1, 5.<BR> 2. A creditor, 2, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजन|प्रयोजनं
प्रयोजन प्रयोजन, i. e. प्र-युज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Cause, Vikr. 80, 11; motive, Pañc. 107, 10.<BR> 2. Purpose, design, Pañc. 58, 2; 240, 15.<BR> 3. Use, Pañc. 5, 5; need, Hit. 54, 20; profit, Pañc. 88, 10; interest, 114, 22.<BR> 4. Means of attaining, Man. 7, 100.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयोजन
अ- + प्रयोजन अ- + प्रयोजन, and निस्-, adj. 1. not induced by motives, MBh. 13, 2025 (निष्प्˚). 2. useless, Hit. 105, 19 (निष्प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानार्थप्रयोजन
समान-अर्थ- + प्रयोजन समान-अर्थ- + प्रयोजन, adj. depending on equal interests, Hit. iv. d. 110 (read ˚नः, cf. Kām. Nītis. 4, 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररक्षण|प्ररक्षणं
प्ररक्षण प्ररक्षण, i. e. प्र-रक्ष् + अन, n. Guarding, Pañc. iii. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोह|प्ररोहः
प्ररोह प्ररोह, i. e. प्र-रुह् + अ, m. A shoot, Vikr. d. 157; a branch, Pañc. 259, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहिन्
प्ररोहिन् प्ररोहिन्, i. e. प्र-रुह् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Sprouting, Man. 1, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपन|प्रलपनं
प्रलपन प्र-लप् + अन, n. Prattling, peaking, Pañc. 163, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्ब|प्रलंब|प्रलम्बः
प्रलम्ब प्र-लम्ब् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Hanging down, pendulous, Lass. 4, 19.<BR> 2. Prominent, Johns. Sel. 55, 142.<BR> 3. Dilatory, slow.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Hanging on or from.<BR> 2. The new shoot or bud of a creeping plant.<BR> 3. A branch. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b " target="_blank">Page0605-b + 41</a>]<BR> 4. A garland of flowers worn round the neck.<BR> 5. The name of a demon killed by Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्भ|प्रलंभ|प्रलंभः|प्रलम्भः
प्रलम्भ प्रलम्भ, i. e. प्र-लभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obtaining, Rām. 5, 68, 43.<BR> 2. Fraud.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलम्भ|सुप्रलम्भः
सु- + प्रलम्भ सु- + प्रलम्भ, adj. easy of attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलय|प्रलयः
प्रलय प्रलय, i. e. प्र-ली + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dissolution,<BR> 2. Destruction, Utt. Rāmac. 83, 10; Hit. ii. d. 175.<BR> 3. End, Pañc. 265, 11.<BR> 4. Death.<BR> 5. The destruction of the world, Hit. 47, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रलय|महाप्रलयः
महा- + प्रलय महा- + प्रलय, m. 1. a destruction of the world occurring after every period of 4,320,000,000 years. 2. a total destruction of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलाप|प्रलापः
प्रलाप प्रलाप, i. e. प्र-लप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Prattlement, useless speech, Utt. Rāmac. 84, 1.<BR> 2. Lamentation, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 6; Pañc. 213, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलाप|सुप्रलापः
सु- + प्रलाप सु- + प्रलाप, m. eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिन्
प्रलापिन् प्रलापिन्, i. e. प्र-लप् + इन्, adj. Prattling, Nal. 26, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीनता
प्रलीनता प्र-लीन + ता (vb. ली), f.<BR> 1. Destruction.<BR> 2. The end of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठन|प्रलोठनं
प्रलोठन प्रलोठन, i. e. प्र-लुठ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rolling on the ground.<BR> 2. Tossing (as of the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभ|प्रलोभः
प्रलोभ प्रलोभ, i. e. प्र-लुभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Allurement, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 37.<BR> 2. Greediness, Pañc. i. d. 462.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभन|प्रलोभनं
प्रलोभन प्रलोभन, i. e. प्र-लुभ्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Allurement, Sund. 3, 20.<BR> 2. Seducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तृ
प्रवक्तृ प्रवक्तृ, i. e. प्र-वच् + तृ, m. A teacher, a propounder, Man. 3, 180; 4, 162.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवक्तृ
अ- + प्रवक्तृ अ- + प्रवक्तृ, m. one who does not instruct, Pañc. iii. d. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचन|प्रवचनं|प्रवचनः
प्रवचन प्र-वच् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Eloquence, Hit. ii. d. 26.<BR> 2. Teaching.<BR> 3. A holy treatise, Man. 3, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवण|प्रवणः
प्रवण प्रवण (akin to प्रक्व),<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a " target="_blank">Page0606-a + 42</a>] adj.<BR> 1. Declining.<BR> 2. Bent.<BR> 3. Curved.<BR> 4. Inclined to, Kathās. 3, 54; Lass. 77, 3; endowed with.<BR> 5. Swift, Ṛt. 1, 24 v. r.<BR> 6. Ready (with infin.), MBh. 1, 2187.<BR> II. m. A place where four roads meet.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणा- + प्रवण दक्षिणा- + प्रवण, adj. with a declivity towards the south, Man. 3, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवपण|प्रवपणं
प्रवपण प्रवपण, i. e. प्र-वप् + अन, n. Sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयण|प्रवयणं
प्रवयण प्रवयण, i. e. प्र-वी + अन, n. A goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयस्
प्रवयस् प्र-वयस्,<BR> I. adj. Aged, Utt. Rāmac. 106, 6.<BR> II. m. An old man, Ragh. 8, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर|प्रवरं|प्रवरः
प्रवर प्रवर, i. e. प्र-वर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा, Best, Indr. 5, 20; exalted, Pañc. 3, 10; Man. 3, 167; chief, Man. 9, 67.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Muni who contributes to the credit of a particular family (गोत्र).<BR> 2. One of the forty-nine gotras, as opposed to the eight principal, Āśval. S. ap. M. Müller, Anc. Sskr. Lit. 380. n. 1.; cf. Weber, Berl. Handschriften, p. 59, 60; Kusumāñj. 3, 19.<BR> III. n. A family.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खप्रवर
शङ्ख- + प्रवर शङ्ख- + प्रवर, m. or n. an excellent conch, Chr. 25, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग|प्रवर्गः
प्रवर्ग प्र-वर्ग, m. Sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग्य|प्रवर्ग्यः
प्रवर्ग्य प्रवर्ग्य, i. e. प्रवर्ग + य, m. A very holy sacrifice, Bhāg. P. 5, 3, 2; MBh. 3, 13027.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्तक प्रवर्तक, i. e. प्र-वृत् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Inciting, stimulating.<BR> 2. One who causes.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An instigator, Man. 12, 4.<BR> 2. An author, a founder, Bhāg. P. 9, 17, 4; Hariv. 4135.<BR> III. n. The entrance of the first person of the drama at the close of the introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तन|प्रवर्तनं|प्रवर्त्तन|प्रवर्त्तनं
प्रवर्तन प्रवर्तन, i. e. प्र-वृत् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going forward, Rām. 6, 92, 4.<BR> 2. Engaging in, Man. 11, 63. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b " target="_blank">Page0606-b + 39</a>]<BR> 3. Beginning.<BR> 4. Activity.<BR> 5. Stimulating, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 6.<BR> 6. Directing.<BR> 7. Informing.<BR> 8. Revolving.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तन|अप्रवर्तनं|अप्रवर्त्तन
अ- + प्रवर्तन अ- + प्रवर्तन, n. abstaining from (with loc.), Hit. i. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तिन्
प्रवर्तिन् प्रवर्तिन्, i. e. प्र-वृत् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Acting, moving, in प्रतिकूल-, adj. Acting and moving in a contrary or perverse way, Chr. 94, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ष|प्रवर्षः
प्रवर्ष प्रवर्ष, i. e. प्र-वृष् + अ, adj. Raining fast, Pañc. 93, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षण|प्रवर्षणं
प्रवर्षण प्रवर्षण, i. e. प्र-वृष् + अन, adj. Raining, MBh. 3, 10012.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ह|प्रवर्हः
प्रवर्ह प्रवर्ह, i. e. प्र-वृह् + अ, adj. Chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवलाकिन्
प्रवलाकिन् प्रवलाकिन्, m.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसन|प्रवसनं
प्रवसन प्र-वस् + अन, n. Sojourn abroad, Hit. i. d. 113, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह|प्रवहः
प्रवह प्र-वह् + अ, m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहण|प्रवहणं
प्रवहण प्रवहण, i. e. प्र-वह् + अन, n. A covered car, a litter or carriage for women, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लि|प्रवह्लिः
प्रवह्लि प्रवह्लि, and प्रवह्लिका प्रवह्लि + का, f. A riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणी
प्रवाणी प्रवाणी, i. e. प्र-वे + न + इ, f. A weaver's shuttle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाणि
निष्-प्रवाणि निष्-प्रवाणि, i. e. निस्-, adj. Quite new, Daśak. 62, 1 bel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवात
प्रवात प्र-वात, m.<BR> 1. A breeze, Śāk. 32, 16; Kathās. 20, 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाद|प्रवादः
प्रवाद प्रवाद, i. e. प्र-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rumour, report, Hit. 19, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. A proverb, Pañc. 174, 1.<BR> 3. Speaking, discourse.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रवाद|लोकप्रवादः
लोक- + प्रवाद लोक- + प्रवाद, m. common report or saying, Lass. 12, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवापिन्
प्रवापिन् प्रवापिन्, i. e. प्र-वप् + इन्, m. A sower, one who sows seed, Man. 9, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवास|प्रवासः
प्रवास प्रवास, i. e. प्र-वस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Living away from home, a temporary foreign residence, Vikr. 61, 17 (cf. मनस); far away, d. 135.<BR> 2. A journey, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासन|प्रवासनं
प्रवासन प्रवासन, i. e. प्र-वस्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Banishment, Man. 7, 125.<BR> 2. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासिन्
प्रवासिन् प्रवासिन्, i. e. प्र-वस् + इन्.<BR> 1. adj. sbst. Living away from home, Hit. i. d. 138, M.M. (चिर-, long exiled).<BR> 2. A traveller, Ṛt. 6, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाह|प्रवाहः
प्रवाह प्रवाह, i. e. प्र-वह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Stream, Vikr. d. 49.<BR> 2. A torrent, Pañc. 38, 20.<BR> 3. A pond.<BR> 4. A swift horse.<BR> 5. Occupation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिप्रवाह|वारिप्रवाहः
वारि- + प्रवाह वारि- + प्रवाह, m. a cascade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहक|प्रवाहकः
प्रवाहक प्रवाहक, i. e. प्र-वह् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who or what carries well.<BR> II. m. A demon.<BR> III. f. हिका, Diarrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्याति|प्रविख्यातिः
प्रविख्याति प्र-वि-ख्या + ति, f. Celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारण|प्रविदारणं
प्रविदारण प्रविदारण, i. e. प्र-वि-दॄ + अन, n.<BR> I. Tearing.<BR> 2. Bursting.<BR> 3. War, battle.<BR> 4. Tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभाग|प्रविभागः
प्रविभाग प्रविभाग, i. e. प्र-वि-भज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Division, Man. 1, 66.<BR> 2. A part, Utt. Rāmac. 110, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवाद|प्रविवादः
प्रविवाद प्र-विवाद, m. Quarrel, Lass. 18, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्लेष|प्रविश्लेषः
प्रविश्लेष प्रविश्लेष, i. e. प्र-वि-श्लिष् + अ, m. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीण|प्रवीणः
प्रवीण प्र-वीण (cf. वीणा), adj. Skilful, clever, Lass. 39, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीणता
प्रवीणता प्रवीण + ता, f. Cleverness, Hit. Pr. d. 41, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीर|प्रवीरः
प्रवीर प्र-वीर,<BR> I. adj. Excellent, bravest, Hit. iii. d. 70.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b " target="_blank">Page0607-b + 41</a>] hero, Utt. Rāmac. 122, 4.<BR> 2. A chief, Rām. 3, 49, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्ति|प्रवृत्तिः
प्रवृत्ति प्र-वृत् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Action, Hit. 17, 5 (engaging); occupation, doing, Man. 5, 31; Daśak. 186, 13; activity, Bhāṣāp. 148.<BR> 2. Perseverance.<BR> 3. Practice, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 10.<BR> 4. Tidings, Vikr. 57, 18; report, d. 102; utterance, Śāk. d. 21; Ragh. 12, 60.<BR> 5. Continuous flow, Vikr. d. 110.<BR> 6. The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples when in rut.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रवृत्ति
दुष्प्रवृत्ति दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, f. ill-tidings, Ragh. 12, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहप्रवृत्ति|स्नेहप्रवृत्तिः
स्नेह- + प्रवृत्ति स्नेह- + प्रवृत्ति, f. love, Śāk. d. 92, 58, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्धि|प्रवृद्धिः
प्रवृद्धि प्रवृद्धि, i. e. प्र-वृध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Growing, Ragh. 13, 71.<BR> 2. Elevation, prosperity, Rājat. 5, 388.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक|प्रवेकः
प्रवेक प्रवेक, i. e. प्र-विच् + अ, adj. Chief, principal.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिप्रवेक|मणिप्रवेकः
मणि- + प्रवेक मणि- + प्रवेक, most excellent jewels, Rām. 3, 52, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्रवेणी प्रवेणी, see वेणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेदिन्
प्रवेदिन् प्रवेदिन्, i. e. प्र-विद् + इन्, adj. Well-knowing, Man. 9, 267.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपन|प्रवेपनं
प्रवेपन प्र-वेप् + अन, n. Shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेरित
प्रवेरित प्रवेरित, i. e. प्र-व (for अव), -ईरित (vb. ईर्), ptcple. pf. pass. Thrown, Lass. ed. 2, p. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश|प्रवेशः
प्रवेश प्रवेश, i. e. प्र-विश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Entering, Pañc. 33, 6.<BR> 2. Entrance, Vikr. 20, 8.<BR> 3. Intentness on an object.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रवेश
दुष्प्रवेश दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. शा, difficult to be entered, Rām. 3, 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशक|प्रवेशकः
प्रवेशक प्रवेशक, i. e. प्र-विश् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who or what enters.<BR> II. m. An interlude, Śāk. 76, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशन|प्रवेशनं
प्रवेशन प्रवेशन, i. e. प्र-विश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Entering, entrance.<BR> 2. The principal door of a house.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निप्रवेशन
अग्नि- + प्रवेशन अग्नि- + प्रवेशन, n. ascending a funeral pile, Kathās. 18, 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्ट|प्रवेष्टः
प्रवेष्ट प्रवेष्ट, m.<BR> 1. An arm.<BR> 2. The fleshy part on the back of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्टृत्व
प्रवेष्टृत्व प्रवेष्टृत्व, i. e. प्र-विश् + तृ + त्व, n. Condition of one who enters, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्या
प्रव्रज्या प्र-व्रज् + या, f.<BR> 1. Emigrating, Rām. 6, 8, 27.<BR> 2. Wandering about as a religious mendicant, Chr. 10 8; Man. 5, 89 (in a dress not authorised by the Vedas, cf. Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजन|प्रव्राजनं
प्रव्राजन प्रव्राजन, i. e. प्र-व्रज्, Caus., + अन, n. Banishment, Rām. 3, 53, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसन|प्रशंसनं
प्रशंसन प्र-शंस् + अन, n. Praising, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसा
प्रशंसा प्र-शंस् + आ, f. Praise, applause, Man. 10, 127; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्त्वन्
प्रशत्त्वन् प्रशत्त्वन्, i. e. प्र-शद् + त्वन्,<BR> I. m. The ocean.<BR> II. f. वरी, A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम|प्रशमः
प्रशम प्र-शम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Quiet, end, Pañc. iii. d. 3, 21.<BR> 2. Tranquillising, removing, Śiś. 9, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन प्र-शम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Tranquillising, pacifying, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 4.<BR> 2. Securing, Man. 7, 56.<BR> 3. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्ति|प्रशस्तिः
प्रशस्ति प्रशस्ति, i. e. प्र-शंस् + ति, f. Praise, Lass. 98, 16 = Rigv. v. 9, 6; Utt. Rāmac. 156, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखा
प्रशाखा प्र-शाखा, and प्रशास्विका प्रशाखिका, i. e. प्रशाखा + क, f. A small branch or twig, Rām. 5, 29, 21; Nal. 20, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्ति|प्रशांति|प्रशांतिः|प्रशान्तिः
प्रशान्ति प्रशान्ति, i. e. प्र-शम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Calm, tranquillity, moral or physical, Pañc. 123, 21.<BR> 2. Removal, iii. d. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासन|प्रशासनं
प्रशासन प्र-शास् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Governing.<BR> 2. Dominion, Chr. 296, 3 = Rigv. i. 112, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासितृ
प्रशासितृ प्र-शास् + इतृ, m. A governor, master, Pañc. v. d. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्तृ
प्रशास्तृ प्र-शास् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A king, Nal. 12, 51.<BR> 2. A governor.<BR> 3. A kind of priest, Pañc. 156, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्चोतन|प्रश्चोतनं
प्रश्चोतन प्र-श्चोत् + अन, n. Sprinkling, Utt. Rāmac. 58, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्न|प्रश्नः
प्रश्न प्रश्न, i. e. प्रछ् + न, m. A question, Pañc. 149, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलप्रश्न|कुशलप्रश्नः
कुशल- + प्रश्न कुशल- + प्रश्न, m. Inquiring after another's welfare, Utt. Rāmac. 70, 6; Lass. 10, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रय|प्रश्रयः
प्रश्रय प्रश्रय, i. e. प्र-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Affection, love, Pañc. ii. d. 2.<BR> 2. Affectionate behaviour.<BR> 3. Civility, modesty, Indr. 2, 21.<BR> 4. Respect, Utt. Rāmac. 152, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रश्रयम्
स-प्रश्रय + म् स-प्रश्रय + म्, adv. affectionately, Pañc. 25, 25; 33, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लथ|प्रश्लथः
प्रश्लथ प्र-श्लथ् + अ, adj. Flaccid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठ|प्रष्ठः
प्रष्ठ प्रष्ठ, i. e. प्र-स्थ,<BR> I. adj. One who goes first.<BR> II. m. A leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्
† प्रस् प्रस्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To extend.<BR> 2. To bring forth (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्ति|प्रसक्तिः
प्रसक्ति प्रसक्ति, i. e. प्र-सञ्ज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Connexion.<BR> 2. Attachment.<BR> 3. Perseverance, activity, Kir. 5, 50.<BR> 4. Energy.<BR> 5. Practicableness, Rājat. 6, 154.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्ति|अप्रसक्तिः
अ- + प्रसक्ति अ- + प्रसक्ति, f. absence of attachment, Man. 1, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसक्ति|अतिप्रसक्तिः
अति- + प्रसक्ति अति- + प्रसक्ति, f. excessive attachment, Man. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्यान
प्रसंख्यान प्रसंख्यान, i. e. प्र-सम्-ख्या + अन, n. Meditation, Kumāras. 3, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्ग|प्रसंग|प्रसंगः|प्रसङ्गः
प्रसङ्ग प्रसङ्ग, i. e. प्र-सञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Association, union, Pañc. i. d. 218.<BR> 2. Attachment, Man. 2, 93; 4, 186; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a " target="_blank">Page0609-a + 41</a>] illicit gratification, Man. 9, 5; 4, 15 (an art which pleases the senses).<BR> 3. Connected reasoning.<BR> 4. Conjuncture, occasion, Pañc. 117, 10; time, Rājat. 5, 276.<BR> 5. Insertion, introduction.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसङ्ग|अतिप्रसंग|अतिप्रसंगः|अतिप्रसङ्गः
अति- + प्रसङ्ग अति- + प्रसङ्ग, m. 1. excessive attachment, Pañc. i. d. 201. 2. asserting too much, Utt. Rāmac. 135, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसंग|कथाप्रसङ्गः
कथा- + प्रसङ्ग कथा- + प्रसङ्ग, m. conversation, Hit. 61, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मदोषप्रसङ्ग
धर्म-दोष- + प्रसङ्ग धर्म-दोष- + प्रसङ्ग, m. a sinful attachment to duty, Rām. 2, 23, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रसङ्ग
विधि- + प्रसङ्ग विधि- + प्रसङ्ग, m. application of, or acting upon, a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गवन्त्|प्रसङ्गवत्
प्रसङ्गवन्त् प्रसङ्ग + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Occasional, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गिन्|प्रसंगिन्
प्रसङ्गिन् प्रसङ्गिन्, i. e. प्रसङ्ग + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Attached to, Ṛt. 6, 1.<BR> 2. Occasional.<BR> 3. Subordinate, MBh. 5, 1442.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभम्
प्रसभम् प्र-सभ + म् (probably vb. सह्), adv.<BR> 1. Forcibly, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1917; Vikr. d. 19; violently, Śāk. d. 5.<BR> 2. Exceedingly, importunately, Johns. Sel. 5, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर|प्रसरः
प्रसर प्रसर, i. e. प्र-सृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Who or what proceeds.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Going forward, Śāk. d. 28.<BR> 2. Spreading.<BR> 3. A multitude.<BR> 4. Battle.<BR> 5. An iron arrow.<BR> 6. Space, room, Hit. i. d. 185, M.M.; Megh. 93.<BR> 7. Occasion.<BR> 8. Affectionate solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरण|प्रसरणं
प्रसरण प्रसरण, i. e. प्र-सृ + अन, n., and f. णी and णि.<BR> 1. Going forth.<BR> 2. Spreading over the country to forage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव|प्रसवः
प्रसव प्रसव, i. e. प्र-सू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Bringing forth, Pañc. 75, 23; being in labour, 228, 14.<BR> 2. Offspring, Man. 3, 22; 9, 55.<BR> 3. Blossom.<BR> 4. Fruit, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवितृ
प्रसवितृ प्रसवितृ, i. e. प्र-सू̆ + तृ.<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A father.<BR> 2. Forefather, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 1.<BR> II. f. त्रि, A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह|प्रसहः
प्रसह प्र-सह् + अ, m. A beast or bird of prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहन|प्रसहनः
प्रसहन प्र-सह् + अन,<BR> I. m. A beast or bird of prey.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Enduring.<BR> 2. Overcoming.<BR> 3. Embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाद|प्रसादः
प्रसाद प्रसाद, i. e. प्र-सद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Clearness, Vikr. d. 8.<BR> 2. Perspicuity.<BR> 3. Calmness (of mind), Vikr. d. 147.<BR> 4. Favour, Vikr. d. 54.<BR> 5. Kind behaviour, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1372.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसाद
दुष्प्रसाद दुष्प्रसाद, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be pacified, MBh. 1, 1679.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिप्रसाद|दृष्टिप्रसादः
दृष्टि- + प्रसाद दृष्टि- + प्रसाद, m. favour of looking at, Hit. 88, 6, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रसाद
स- + प्रसाद स- + प्रसाद, adj. propitious, Pañc. 85, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रसाद|सुप्रसादः
सु- + प्रसाद सु- + प्रसाद,<BR> I. adj. kind.<BR> II. m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादक
प्रसादक प्रसादक, i. e. प्र-सद्, Caus., + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Making clear, purifying, Man. 6, 67.<BR> 2. Exhilarating Rām. 3, 55, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादन|प्रसादनं|प्रसादनः
प्रसादन प्रसादन, i. e. प्र-सद्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Exhilarating, Indr. 2, 31.<BR> II. f. ना, Worship.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसादन
दुष्प्रसादन दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be pacified, Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधन|प्रसाधनं|प्रसाधनः
प्रसाधन प्र-साध् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Dressing, Man. 10, 32; 2, 211 (decking the hair).<BR> 2. Dress, embellishment, accomplishment, Vikr. d. 22.<BR> 3. Accomplishing, adorning, Mālav. 62, 23; anointing the body, Man. 7, 220; 4, 152.<BR> II. m., f. नी, and n. A comb.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसाधन
दुष्प्रसाधन दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be dealt with, MBh. 11, 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसार|प्रसारः
प्रसार प्रसार, i. e. प्र-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going about, spreading.<BR> 2. Going to forage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारण|प्रसारणं
प्रसारण प्रसारण, i. e. प्र-सृ, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. n. Extending, Bhāṣāp. 5.<BR> II. f. णी.<BR> 1. Surrounding an enemy.<BR> 2. The dispersion of an army for collecting forage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारिन्
प्रसारिन् प्रसारिन्, i. e. प्र-सृ + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a " target="_blank">Page0610-a + 41</a>] adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Breaking forth, Śāk. d. 61.<BR> 2. Going along.<BR> 3. Spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धि|प्रसिद्धिः
प्रसिद्धि प्रसिद्धि, i. e. प्र-सिध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Accomplishment, Man. 4, 3.<BR> 2. Ornament.<BR> 3. Fame.<BR> 4. Notoriety.<BR> 5. Name. Hit. 83, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू प्र-सू, f.<BR> 1. A mother, Śiś. 9, 14.<BR> 2. A mare.<BR> 3. A spreading creeper.<BR> 4. The plantain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिप्रसू
मसि- + प्रसू मसि- + प्रसू, f. an inkstand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूति|प्रसूतिः
प्रसूति प्र-सू + ति, f.<BR> 1. Bringing forth (as young).<BR> 2. Birth, Man. 4, 84 (अ-राजन्य-प्रसूति + तस्, from one who is not born in the Kṣatriya caste); springing up, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 4.<BR> 3. Offspring, Man. 9, 6; Vikr. 78, 21; Pañc. 74, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका प्रसूतिका, i. e. प्र-सूत + क. f. A woman who has had a child, or who has been recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृति|प्रसृतिः
प्रसृति प्र-सृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. The palm of the hand hollowed.<BR> 2. A handful, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेक|प्रसेकः
प्रसेक प्रसेक, i. e. प्र-सिच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sprinkling.<BR> 2. Oozing, dropping, Ṛt. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कण्व|प्रस्कण्वः
प्रस्कण्व प्रस्कण्व, m. The name of a Vedic poet, Chr. 287, 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तर|प्रस्तरः
प्रस्तर प्रस्तर, i. e. प्र-स्तॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A handful or bundle of Kuśa grass used at sacrifices.<BR> 2. A plain, level, Rām. 3, 79, 5; Man. 2, 204.<BR> 3. A stone or rock, Utt. Rāmac. 71, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तार|प्रस्तारः
प्रस्तार प्रस्तार, i. e. प्र-स्तॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A bed.<BR> 2. A thicket or wood, overgrown with grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्ताव|प्रस्तावः
प्रस्ताव प्रस्ताव, i. e. प्र-स्तु + अ, m.<BR> 1. An introductory eulogium, introduction, Hit. 13, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. Beginning, Śāk. 101, 9.<BR> 3. Opportunity, Hit. 52, 16; Pañc. 158, 19 (loc. opportunely). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b " target="_blank">Page0610-b + 41</a>]<BR> 4. Turn, Pañc. 55, 16.<BR> 5. Treating a subject, Pañc. ii. d. 176.<BR> 6. A chapter.<BR> 7. Report. Hit. 120, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावना
प्रस्तावना प्रस्तावना, i. e. प्र-स्तु, Caus., + अन, f.<BR> 1. Causing to be praised, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 14.<BR> 2. A dramatic prelude, prologue, Vikr. 4, 8.<BR> 3. Commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ प्र-स्थ (vb. स्था),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Who goes on a journey.<BR> 2. Expanding.<BR> 3. Solid.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Tableland on the top of a mountain, Sund. 4, 6.<BR> 2. A measure of quantity.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रस्थ|इंद्रप्रस्थ|इन्द्रप्रस्थं
इन्द्र- + प्रस्थ इन्द्र- + प्रस्थ, n. (m.), the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयप्रस्थ|उदयप्रस्थः
उदय- + प्रस्थ उदय- + प्रस्थ, the table-land on the top of the mountain, behind which the sun rises, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डवप्रस्थ|खांडवप्रस्थ|खाण्डवप्रस्थः
खाण्डव- + प्रस्थ खाण्डव- + प्रस्थ, m. the name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमप्रस्थ|हिमप्रस्थः
हिम- + प्रस्थ हिम- + प्रस्थ, m. the Himālaya mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थान|प्रस्थानं
प्रस्थान प्रस्थान, i. e. प्र-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Departing, Megh. 42.<BR> 2. March of an assailant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रस्थान
महा- + प्रस्थान महा- + प्रस्थान, n. Death, Hariv. 11070.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानिक
प्रस्थानिक प्रस्थानिक, Sund. 2, 2; read प्रास्थ्˚, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थायिन्
प्रस्थायिन् प्रस्थायिन्, i. e. प्र-स्था + इन्, adj. Preparing to go, or to depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नव|प्रस्नवः
प्रस्नव प्रस्नव, i. e. प्र-स्नु + अ, m. Dropping, stream, Vikr. d. 150 (v. r., cf. प्रस्नुत-स्तन); Utt. Rāmac. 153, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फोटन|प्रस्फोटनं
प्रस्फोटन प्रस्फोटन, i. e. प्र-स्फुट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Expanding, opening.<BR> 2. Striking.<BR> 3. Winnowing corn.<BR> 4. A winnowing basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रव|प्रस्रवः
प्रस्रव प्रस्रव, i. e. प्र-स्रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Oozing, dropping, Johns. Sel. 14, 47; Vikr. d. 150 (v. r. प्रस्नव, q. cf.).<BR> 2. The flowing of milk, Man. 5, 130.<BR> 3. Urine, MBh. 1, 6683.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रवण|प्रस्रवणं|प्रस्रवणः
प्रस्रवण प्रस्रवण, i. e. प्र-स्रु + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Washing away of rocks. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a " target="_blank">Page0611-a + 40</a>]<BR> 2. Oozing, Nal. 13, 7.<BR> 3. A cascade Man. 4, 203 (Kull.); spring, Indr. 1, 25; 27.<BR> 4. A pool of water, formed by dripping of springs.<BR> 5. A pure stream, Johns. Sel. 9, 9.<BR> 6. Sweat, perspiration.<BR> II. m. The name of a range of mountains, Rām. 3, 55, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्राव|प्रस्रावः
प्रस्राव प्रस्राव, i. e. प्र-स्रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Flowing, dropping.<BR> 2. Urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वाप|प्रस्वापः
प्रस्वाप प्रस्वाप, i. e. प्र-स्वप् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Epithet of a weapon (causing to sleep), Chr. 38, 12.<BR> II. m. Falling asleep, Bhāg. P. 6, 16, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेद|प्रस्वेदः
प्रस्वेद प्रस्वेद, i. e. प्र-स्विद् + अ, m. Excessive perspiration, Lass. 28, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर|प्रहरः
प्रहर प्रहर, i. e. प्र-हृ + अ, m., and प्रहरक प्रहर + क, A watch, or a division comprising about three hours, Lass. 29, 9; Pañc. 237, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरण|प्रहरणं
प्रहरण प्रहरण, i. e. प्र-हृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Striking, pecking, Pañc. 146, 14; biting, 147, 2.<BR> 2. A weapon, Hariv. 13745.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्तृ|प्रहर्त्तृ
प्रहर्तृ प्रहर्तृ, i. e. प्र-हृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. One who strikes, a combatant, a shooter, Vikr. 78, 13.<BR> 2. One who attacks, Pañc. 149, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्ष|प्रहर्षः
प्रहर्ष प्रहर्ष, i. e. प्र-हृष् + अ, m. Joy, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 11; merriness, Sund. 1, 29; Vikr. 58, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसन|प्रहसनं
प्रहसन प्र-हस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Hearty laughter, laughter, Utt. Rāmac. 91, 7.<BR> 2. Mirth.<BR> 3. Scoffing, sarcasm, Hit. i. d. 107.<BR> 4. A comedy, Lass. 67, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणि|प्रहाणिः
प्रहाणि प्रहाणि, i. e. प्र-हा + नि, f. Disappearance, Mārk. P. 58, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहार|प्रहारः
प्रहार प्रहार, i. e. प्र-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Striking, Pañc. 245, 12; pecking, Hit. 107, 19; killing.<BR> 2. A stroke, Man. 4, 83; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b " target="_blank">Page0611-b + 40</a>] a shot (of an arrow), Pañc. 141, 10; a kick, 215, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलप्रहार|तलप्रहारः
तल- + प्रहार तल- + प्रहार, m. a stroke with the palm of the hand or claw, Pañc. 215, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रहार|पादप्रहारः
पाद- + प्रहार पाद- + प्रहार, m. a kick, Rām. 4, 9, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारिन्
प्रहारिन् प्रहारिन्, i. e. प्र-हृ + इन्, adj. sbst. Striking, a warrior, a hero, Mālav. 69, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहास|प्रहासः
प्रहास प्रहास, i. e. प्र-हस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Loud laughter.<BR> 2. An actor.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहि|प्रहिः
प्रहि प्रहि, m. A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेला
प्रहेला प्र-हेल् + आ, f. Wantonness, carelessness, Pañc. ii. d. 48 (˚लया, with a jump(?), cf. हेला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलि|प्रहेलिः
प्रहेलि प्र-हेल् + इ, f. An enigma, a riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लाद|प्रह्लादः
प्रह्लाद प्र-ह्लाद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Joy, pleasure.<BR> 2. The name of a Daitya, Arj. 8, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादन
प्रह्लादन प्र-ह्लाद् + अन, adj., f. नी, Rejoicing, refreshing, MBh. 14, 2045.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्व|प्रह्वः
प्रह्व प्रह्व, probably curtailed प्रह्वर, i. e. प्र-ह्वृ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Bowed. stooping, Arj. 1, 5.<BR> 2. Intent upon.<BR> 3. Propitious, Kathās. 46, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रा
प्रा प्रा (akin to पॄ for पर् + आ), ii. 2, Par. To fill.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्राण, Full.<BR> --Cf. πλῆμα, πλήρης, πληρότης, πλήθω, πλῆθος, πλέθρον, πλοῦτος, etc.; Lat. plenus (= प्राण), implere, etc., plebes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशु|प्रांशुः
प्रांशु प्रांशु, adj.<BR> 1. Tall, Johns. Sel. 15, 53; lofty, Ragh. 15, 19.<BR> 2. Long, Śāk. d. 49.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रांशु
अति- + प्रांशु अति- + प्रांशु, adj. very tall, Prab. 21, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्
प्राक् प्राक्, see प्राञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकषिक|प्राकषिकः
प्राकषिक प्राकषिक, i. e. प्र-आ-कष् + इक, m. A dancer, one who gets his livelihood from the wives of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाम्य|प्राकाम्यं
प्राकाम्य प्राकाम्य, i. e. प्रकाम + य, n. The faculty to perform what one lists, a magical power, Lass. 3, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकार|प्राकारः
प्राकार प्राकार, i. e. प्र-कृ + अ + अ, m. An inclosure, a surrounding wall, Pañc. iii. d. 48; Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17; Man. 9, 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाश्य|प्राकाश्यं
प्राकाश्य प्राकाश्य, i. e. प्रकाश + य, n.<BR> 1. Clearness, brightness.<BR> 2. Celebrity, Pañc. i. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृत|प्राकृतः
प्राकृत प्राकृत, i. e. प्रकृति + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती.<BR> 1. Natural.<BR> 2. Material.<BR> 3. Low, Man. 8, 336.<BR> 4. Common, Pañc. 25, 2.<BR> II. n. A peculiar dialect, or rather some peculiar dialects akin to the Sanskrit language used particularly in dramatic compositions.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्राकृत
अति- + प्राकृत अति- + प्राकृत, adj. supernatural, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन प्राक्तन, i. e. प्राञ्च् + तन, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Old.<BR> 2. Prior, former, Pañc. iii. d. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागभाव|प्रागभावः
प्रागभाव प्रागभाव, i. e. प्राक्-अ-भाव, m. The non-existence (of any effect) previous to production, Bhāṣāp. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्य|प्रागल्भ्यं
प्रागल्भ्य प्रागल्भ्य, i. e. प्रगल्भ + य, n.<BR> 1. Confidence, boldness.<BR> 2. Arrogance.<BR> 3. Pride, Lass. 67, 17.<BR> 4. Rank, proficiency, Pañc. 31, 5; 112, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुण|प्राघुणः
प्राघुण (a dialectical form of प्राघूर्ण, see the next), m. A guest, Pañc. iii. d. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघूर्णक|प्राघूर्णकः
प्राघूर्णक प्राघूर्णक (Pañc. 117, 10), and प्राघूर्णिक प्राघूर्णिक (ŚKD.), i. e. प्र-घूर्ण् + अ + क or इक (cf. प्राघुण), m. A guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्गण|प्रांगण|प्रांगणं|प्राङ्गणं
प्राङ्गण प्राङ्गण, n.<BR> 1. A sort of drum.<BR> 2. and प्राङ्गन प्राङ्गन, (i. e. प्र-अङ्गन), A court, Hit. 50, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्गनतस्
प्राङ्गनतस् प्राङ्गन-तस्, (see the last), adv. Near the court, Rājat. 5, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन प्राचीन, i. e. प्राञ्च् + ईन, adj.<BR> 1. Former, old.<BR> 2. Eastern, east.<BR> 3. Left, not right, Man. 2, 63 (Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचुर्य|प्राचुर्यं
प्राचुर्य प्राचुर्य, i. e. प्रचुर + य, n. Plenty, Pañc. 253, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतस|प्राचेतसः
प्राचेतस प्राचेतस, i. e. प्रचेतस् + अ, patronym. A descendant of Pracetas, i. e.<BR> 1. Vālmīki, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 10.<BR> 2. The ten sons of Prācīnavarhis<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य प्राच्य, i. e. प्राञ्च् + य, adj. Eastern, Mārk. P. 57, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राछ्|प्राच्छ्
प्राछ् प्राछ् (vb. प्रछ्), m. An inquirer, see प्राड्विवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजक|प्राजकः
प्राजक प्राजक, i. e. प्र-अज् + अक, m. A driver, Man. 8, 293; 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य प्राजापत्य, i. e. प्रजापति + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Coming from, belonging to, Prajāpati, Chr. 38, 12; Pañc. i. d. 239.<BR> 2. Belonging to the Prajāpatis, Man. 4, 182.<BR> 3. With and without विधि, a form of marriage, Man. 3, 30.<BR> 4. With or without कृच्छ्र, A sort of penance, Man. 11, 105; 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञ|प्राज्ञः
प्राज्ञ प्राज्ञ, i. e. प्रज्ञा + अ,<BR> I. adj. Wise, Pañc. i. d. 129.<BR> II. m. A learned man, Man. 2, 123.<BR> III. f. ज्ञा, Knowledge.<BR> IV. f. ज्ञी and ज्ञा, A clever woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्य|प्राज्यं
प्राज्य प्राज्य (vb. अज्). adj.<BR> 1. Much, Śāk. d. 193.<BR> 2. Lofty, Rājat. 5, 347.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्च्|प्रांच्
प्राञ्च् प्राञ्च्, i. e. प्र-अञ्च्,<BR> I. adj., f. आची.<BR> 1. Former, Pañc. 49, 1; prior.<BR> 2. Before, in front.<BR> 3. Eastern, east.<BR> II. प्राक् (acc. sing. n.), adv.<BR> 1. First.<BR> 2. Before, Rājat. 5, 45; 338; formerly, Pañc. 217, 3.<BR> 3. In front, Utt. Rāmac. 56, 11 (so that she cannot see); Hit. i. d. 80, M.M.<BR> 4. Past.<BR> 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a " target="_blank">Page0613-a + 41</a>] Eastern.<BR> 6. At dawn.<BR> III. f. आची, The east, Draup. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जल|प्रांजल|प्राञ्जलः
प्राञ्जल प्राञ्जल, adj.<BR> 1. Straight.<BR> 2. Honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलता
प्राञ्जलता प्राञ्जल + ता, f. Straightness, Pañc. 263, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलि|प्रांजलि
प्राञ्जलि प्राञ्जलि, i. e. प्र-अञ्जलि, adj. Putting the hands together to the forehead, as a mark of respect, Vikr. 45, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राड्विवाक|प्राड्विवाकः
प्राड्विवाक प्राड्विवाक, i. e. प्राछ्-वि-वच् + अ, m. A judge, Man. 8, 79; 181; 9, 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण|प्राणः
प्राण प्राण, i. e. प्र-अन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Breath, Vikr. d. 1.<BR> 2. Air, wind.<BR> 3. A vital organ, Man. 4, 143.<BR> 4. One of the five vital airs, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 9.<BR> 5. The Supreme Spirit, ib. 208, 3.<BR> 6. A name of Brahman.<BR> 7. pl. Life, Hit. i. d. 11, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably ϕρήν, ϕρένες, ϕρόνιμος, ϕρόντις, ϕρονέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्राणम्
अति-प्राण + म् अति-प्राण + म्, adv. more than life, Pañc. 220, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रप्राण
कृच्छ्र- + प्राण कृच्छ्र- + प्राण, adj. supporting life with difficulty, Rām. 4, 9, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्राण
गत- + प्राण गत- + प्राण, adj. dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्राण
निष्प्राण निष्प्र्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. dead. 2. exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिप्राणा
पति- + प्राणा पति- + प्राण, adj., f. णा, living in, or for, one's husband, Pañc. iii. d. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्राण|महाप्राणः
महा- + प्राण महा- + प्राण, m. a raven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिप्राण
यष्टि- + प्राण यष्टि- + प्राण, adj. out of breath, Johns. Sel. 21, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणथ|प्राणथः
प्राणथ प्राणथ, i. e. प्र-अन् + अथ, adj. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन|प्राणनं|प्राणनः
प्राणन प्राणन, i. e. प्र-अन् + अन,<BR> I. n. Breathing, Chr. 288, 10 = Rigv. i. 48, 10.<BR> II. m. The throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन्त|प्राणंत|प्राणंतः|प्राणन्तः
प्राणन्त प्राणन्त् + अ (vb. अन्),<BR> I. m. Wind.<BR> II. f. ती, Hiccough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमय
प्राणमय प्राण + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting in breath or life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणवन्त्|प्राणवत्
प्राणवन्त् प्राण + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with life, Śāk. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिन्
प्राणिन् प्राणिन्, i. e. प्राण + इन्, adj. sbst., f. नी, Living, a living being, Man. 4, 117, Pañc. iii. d. 140.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राणिन्
अ- + प्राणिन् अ- + प्राणिन्, adj. inanimate, Man. 4, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणीत्य|प्राणीत्यं
प्राणीत्य प्राणीत्य, i. e. प्र-नीत + य, n. Debt (or प्रामीत्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्
प्रातर् प्रातर्, i. e. a curtailed case of प्रा (probably akin to पुरा = प्र) + तर, adv. In the morning, at dawn, Kathās. 22, 100; early, Hit. 15, 2, M.M. Doubled, प्रातःप्रातर्, adv. Every morning, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 17.<BR> --With प्रा cf. O.H.G. frô, fruo; πρωΐ; see पूर्वेद्युस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभाव्य|प्रातिभाव्यं
प्रातिभाव्य प्रातिभाव्य, i. e. प्रति-भू + य, n. Surety, Man. 8, 159.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रातिभाव्य
दर्शन- + प्रातिभाव्य दर्शन- + प्रातिभाव्य, n. Surety for appearing, 8, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोम्य|प्रातिलोम्यं
प्रातिलोम्य प्रातिलोम्य, i. e. प्रति-लोम + य, n. Inverted order, Man. 10, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्य|प्रातिवेश्यः
प्रातिवेश्य प्रातिवेश्य, i. e. प्रतिवेश + य, and प्रातिवेश्यक प्रातिवेश्य + क, m. A next-door neighbour, a neighbour, Man. 8, 392; Pañc. 164, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिस्विक|प्रातिस्विकं
प्रातिस्विक प्रातिस्विक, i. e. प्रति-स्व + इक, adj. Own, peculiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमकल्पिक|प्राथमकल्पिकः
प्राथमकल्पिक प्राथमकल्पिक, i. e. प्रथम-कल्प + इक, m.<BR> 1. One who has begun the perusal of the Veda.<BR> 2. A student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमिक|प्राथमिकः
प्राथमिक प्राथमिक, i. e. प्रथम + इक, adj. First, initial, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भाव|प्रादुर्भावः
प्रादुर्भाव प्रादुर्भाव, i. e. प्रादुस्-भू + अ, m. Appearance, manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्य|प्रादुष्यं
प्रादुष्य प्रादुष्य, i. e. प्रादुस् + य, n. Manifestation, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुस्
प्रादुस् प्रादुस्, adv. and prep. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a " target="_blank">Page0614-a + 39</a>] combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives.<BR> 1. Arising, coming to light.<BR> 2. Visible, manifestly.<BR> 3. Existent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेश|प्रादेशः
प्रादेश प्रादेश, i. e. प्रदेश + अ, m.<BR> 1. The span of the thumb and forefinger.<BR> 2. Place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशन|प्रादेशनं
प्रादेशन प्रादेशन, i. e. प्र-आ-दिश् + अन, n. Offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिक|प्रादेशिकः
प्रादेशिक प्रादेशिक, i. e. प्रदेश + इक, adj. Limited, Bhāṣāp. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधनिक|प्राधनिकं
प्राधनिक प्राधनिक, i. e. प्रधन + इक (n. ?), A weapon, Bhāg. P. 3, 8, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्य|प्राधान्यं
प्राधान्य प्राधान्य, i. e. प्रधान + य, n. Prevalence, supremacy, Hit. ii. d. 75 (तद्-, abl. When these rule).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्व|प्राध्वं|प्राध्वः
प्राध्व adj.<BR> 1. प्राध्व, i. e. प्र-अद्वन्, Being on a journey.<BR> 2. Bent.<BR> 3. Inclined, friendly (ŚKD.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्त|प्रांत|प्रांतः|प्रान्तः
प्रान्त प्रान्त, i. e. प्र-अन्त, m.<BR> 1. Edge.<BR> 2. Border, cheek, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 4.<BR> 3. End, Vikr. d. 4; Pañc. 197, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तर|प्रांतर|प्रांतरं|प्रान्तरं
प्रान्तर प्रान्तर, i. e. प्र-अन्तर, n.<BR> 1. A long unshaded lonesome road, Hit. 121, 2.<BR> 2. A forest, Hit. 85, 3.<BR> 3. A hollow tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्
ऽप्राप् -प्राप्, i. e. प्र-आप्, adj. Obtaining, Megh. 45 (कुवलय-दल-, Else adorned with lotus leaves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापण|प्रापणं
प्रापण प्रापण, i. e. प्र-आप् + अन, n. Attainment, Man. 2, 95.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रापण
दुष्प्रापण दुष्प्र्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be attained, Bhāg. P. 8, 3, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणिक|प्रापणिकः
प्रापणिक प्रापणिक, i. e. प्र-आ-पण् + इक, m. A trader, a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तव्यमर्थ
प्राप्तव्यमर्थ प्राप्तव्य + म्-अर्थ, m. A surname, proceeded from its owner [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b " target="_blank">Page0614-b + 43</a>] saying ever प्राप्तव्यम् अर्थम्, etc., Pañc. 130, 15; cf. 127, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्ति|प्राप्तिः
प्राप्ति प्राप्ति, i. e. प्र-आप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Coming, taking place, Pañc. 119, 5 (कुतस् ते ब्राह्मण-भोजन-, Whence can you afford to entertain a Brāhmaṇa?).<BR> 2. Taking possession, obtaining, Kathās. 4, 105; Bhāṣāp. 114.<BR> 3. The power of obtaining every thing, one of the eight superhuman faculties, Lass. 3, 19.<BR> 4. Obtaining by actions done in a former existence, Pañc. ii. d. 132.<BR> 5. Gain, Hit. 101, 10.<BR> 6. Fortune, MBh. 14, 1337.<BR> 7. Successful termination of a plot.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्ति|अप्राप्तिः
अ- + प्राप्ति अ- + प्राप्ति, f. 1. non-attainment. 2. not taking place. 3. not being justified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मप्राप्ति
अकर्मप्राप्ति अकर्मप्राप्ति, i. e. अ-कर्मन्-, f. acquisition without being deserved by actions done in a former existence, Pañc. 132, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाप्राप्ति
यथा- + प्राप्ति यथा- + प्राप्ति, adj. as justified, suitable, Hit. 100, 5 (cf. प्राप्त, i. e. प्र-आप्त, proper, right; perhaps with Schlegel, corr. यथाप्राप्ति, adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबल्य|प्राबल्यं
प्राबल्य प्राबल्य, i. e. प्रबल + य, n.<BR> 1. Predominance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 20.<BR> 2. Power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधक|प्राबोधकः
प्राबोधक प्राबोधक, or प्रावोधिक प्राबोधिक (vv. rr.), i. e. प्रबोध + क or इक, m. Dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभवत्य|प्राभवत्यं
प्राभवत्य प्राभवत्य, i. e. प्र-भ-वन्त् (vb. भू), + य, n. Authority, Man. 8, 412.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभाकर|प्राभाकरः
प्राभाकर प्राभाकर, i. e. प्रभा-कर + अ, m. pl. The followers of Prabhākara, one of the sects of the Pūrva Mīmānsā school, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभातिक
प्राभातिक प्राभातिक, i. e. प्र-भात (vb. भा), + इक, adj. Matutinal, Pañc. i. d. 353.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृत|प्राभृतं
प्राभृत प्राभृत, i. e. प्र-भृत + अ, n. A present, an offering, Kathās. 22, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाणिक|प्रामाणिकः
प्रामाणिक प्रामाणिक, i. e. प्रमाण + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Proceeding from some evidence.<BR> 2. Being of authority.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A chief.<BR> 2. A learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्य|प्रामाण्यं
प्रामाण्य प्रामाण्य, i. e. प्रमाण + य, n.<BR> 1. Proof, Bhāṣāp. 139.<BR> 2. Authority.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाण्य|अप्रामाण्यं
अ- + प्रामाण्य अ- + प्रामाण्य, n. want of authority, irrelevancy, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्यतस्
प्रामाण्यतस् प्रामाण्य + तस्, adv. According to (the) authority, Man. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामोदिक
प्रामोदिक प्रामोदिक, i. e. प्रमोद + इक, adj. Affording pleasure, Utt. Rāmac. 152, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राय|प्रायः
1. प्राय प्राय, i. e. प्रा + अ or य (cf. प्रायस्), or प्र-इ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Exceeding, much, abundant, Pañc. 163, 23 (or a Bahuvr.)<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Quantity, plenty, Man. 7, 69.<BR> 2. A banquet, a feast, Man. 3, 264(?).<BR> 3. येण, instr.<BR> a. Generally, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR> b. How much more, Ṛt. 6, 23.<BR> c. Likely, Hit. 16, 6, M.M.<BR> 4. As latter part of comp. adj.<BR> a. Almost; e. g. गत-, adj. Almost past, MBh. 4, 376. सम्-आ-गत-, Almost approached, very near, Hit. 97, 14.<BR> b. Like, resembling; e. g. अमृत-, Like nectar, Pañc. 206, 6; 194, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धक्षत्रियप्राय
प्र-सिद्ध-क्षत्रिय- + प्राय प्र-सिद्ध-क्षत्रिय- + प्राय, adj. consisting for the most part of renowned Kṣatriyas, Hit. iii. d. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियप्राय|प्रियप्रायं
प्रिय- + प्राय प्रिय- + प्राय, adj. very kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तजनप्राय
सुप्त-जन- + प्राय सुप्त-जन- + प्राय, adj. almost everybody being asleep, Johns. Sel. 60, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाप्राय
हिंसा- + प्राय हिंसा- + प्राय, adj., f. या, abundant in injury (to living beings), Man. 10, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राय|प्रायः
2. प्राय प्राय, i. e. प्र-इ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Death.<BR> 2. Fasting to death, Pañc. 50, 15.<BR> 3. Age.<BR> II. n. Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायण|प्रायणं
प्रायण प्रायण, i. e. प्र-इ + अन, n. Death, Man. 9, 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायशस्
प्रायशस् 1. प्राय + शस्, adv. Usually, for the most part. Hit. i. d. 201, M.M.; Man. 12, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्त|प्रायश्चित्तं
प्रायश्चित्त प्रायश्चित्त, i. e. प्रायस्-चित्त, n.<BR> 1. Penance, Man. 2, 221; Pañc. i. d. 307.<BR> 2. Expiation, Man. 9, 236; Pañc. 207, 17.<BR> 3. Punishment, Hit. ii. d. 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तीय
प्रायश्चित्तीय प्रायश्चित्तीय, a denomin. derived from प्रायश्-चित्त with य, Ātm. To be obliged to perform an expiatory penance, Man. 11, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तीयता
प्रायश्चित्तीयता प्रायश्चित्तीयता, i. e. प्रयस्चित्त + ईय + ता, f. Condition of one who is obliged to perform a penance, Man. 11, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायस्
प्रायस् प्रायस् (probably acc. sing. n. of an old comparat. of पुरु = πλεῖον; Lat. plus), adv.<BR> 1. Frequently, Pañc. iv. d. 7; commonly, v. d. 19.<BR> 2. Probably, MBh. 12, 4989.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्धि|प्रारब्धिः
प्रारब्धि प्रारब्धि, i. e. प्र-आ-रभ् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Beginning.<BR> 2. A rope for binding an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारम्भ|प्रारंभ|प्रारंभः|प्रारम्भः
प्रारम्भ प्रारम्भ, i. e. प्र-आ-रभ् + अ, m. Beginning, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थक|प्रार्थकः
प्रार्थक प्रार्थक, i. e. प्र-अर्थ् + अक, adj. One who sues for, woos, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1448.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थन|प्रार्थनं
प्रार्थन प्रार्थन, i. e. प्र-अर्थ् + अन, n., and f. ना.<BR> 1. Asking, Pañc. 169, 7; demand, Pañc. 5, 5.<BR> 2. Desire, wish, Vikr. 50, 5; wishing for, Śāk. 15, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बितप्रार्थन
आ-लम्बित- + प्रार्थन आ-लम्बित- + प्रार्थन, adj. one whose desire is supported, Vikr. d. 38 (अञ्जसा अभिभवितुम्, to be attained quickly, i. e. one who may hope to attain his desire quickly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफलप्रार्थन
स-फल- + प्रार्थन स-फल- + प्रार्थन, adj. one who has attained his desire, Vikr. d. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितृ
प्रार्थयितृ प्रार्थयितृ, i. e. प्र-अर्थ्, i. 10, + तृ, m.<BR> 1. One who solicits, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a " target="_blank">Page0616-a + 40</a>] Hit. i. d. 115, M.M.<BR> 2. A wooer, Śāk. 21, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्ब|प्रालंब|प्रालम्बं|प्रालम्बः
प्रालम्ब प्रालम्ब, i. e. प्र-आ-लम्ब् + अ, n. A garland hanging down from the neck to the breast, Ragh. 6, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
प्रालेय प्रालेय, i. e. प्रलय + अ (anomal.), n. Snow, hail, Pañc. i. d. 353 (cf. लेश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
प्रालेय प्रालेय, a denomin. derived from प्रालेय, Par. To play the part of hail, Lass. 67, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरण|प्रावरणं
प्रावरण प्रावरण, i. e. प्र-आ-वृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. An upper garment, Pañc. 97, 18 (धौत-, adj. Dressed in a white garment); Rājat. 4, 669.<BR> 2. Any covering.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णप्रावरण
कर्ण- + प्रावरण कर्ण- + प्रावरण, 1. adj., f. णा, using the ears as a cloak, Rām. 5, 17, 34. 2. m. pl. the name of a fabulous people, MBh. 2, 1170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावार|प्रावारः
प्रावार प्रावार, i. e. प्र-आ-वृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. An upper garment, a garment, MBh. 2, 1733.<BR> 2. A cover, MBh. 3, 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावितृ
प्रावितृ प्रावितृ, i. e. प्र-अव् + तृ, m. A protector, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावीण्य|प्रावीण्यं
प्रावीण्य प्रावीण्य, i. e. प्रवीण + य, n. Skilfulness, accurate knowledge, Utt. Rāmac. 110, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृति|प्रावृतिः
प्रावृति प्रा-वृति, i. e. प्र-आ-वृ + ति, f. An inclosure, a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्
प्रावृष् प्रावृष्, i. e. प्र-वृष्, and प्रावृषा प्रावृषा, i. e. प्र-वृष् + अ, f. The rainy season, the months Śrāvaṇa and Bhādra, about July and August, Hiḍ. 2, 1; Pañc. 118, 22 (ष्); Megh. 113 (षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेण्य|प्रावृषेण्यः
प्रावृषेण्य प्रावृषेण्य, i. e. प्रा-वृष् + एन्य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Referring to the rainy season, Vikr. 56, 9; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1915 (a cloud).<BR> 2. Produced in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b " target="_blank">Page0616-b + 40</a>] the rains.<BR> 3. Much.<BR> II. m. The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेण्य|प्रावेण्यं
प्रावेण्य प्रावेण्य, i. e. प्र-वेणी̆ + य, n. A texture made of hairs, Rām. 3, 49, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशिक
प्रावेशिक प्रावेशिक, i. e. प्रवेश + इक, adj., f. की, Referring to the entrance, Vikr. 51, 3 (cf. Sch. added. Calc. p. 76).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्रज्य|प्राव्रज्यं
प्राव्रज्य प्राव्रज्य, i. e. प्रव्रज्या + अ, n. Wandering as a religious mendicant, Chr. 9, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
ऽप्राश् -प्राश् (vb. प्रछ्, cf. प्राछ्), adj. Asking; in शब्द-प्राश्, adj. Inquiring after (the meaning of) a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश|प्राशः
प्राश प्राश, i. e. प्र- 2. अश् + अ, m. Eating, Man. 11, 143.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमप्राश
धूम- + प्राश धूम- + प्राश, adj. feeding only on smoke, MBh. 13, 646.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशन|प्राशनं
प्राशन प्राशन, i. e. प्र- 2. अश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Causing to eat, Man. 2, 29.<BR> 2. Eating, Man. 5, 144.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्राशन|अन्नप्राशनं
अन्न- + प्राशन अन्न- + प्राशन, n. the first feeding of a child with rice, a religious ceremony taking place in the sixth month after his birth, Man. 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित्र|प्राशित्रं
प्राशित्र प्राशित्र, प्र- 2. अश् + त्र, n. The part of a sacrifice to be eaten by a Brāhmaṇa (Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 35, the vessel containing the part of the Brāhmaṇa, Burnouf).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्निक|प्राश्निकः
प्राश्निक प्राश्निक, i. e. प्रश्न + इक, m.<BR> 1. An inquirer.<BR> 2. An examiner, Mālav. 11, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास|प्रासः
प्रास प्रास, i. e. प्र- 2. अस् + अ, m. A bearded dart, MBh. 7, 559.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासक|प्रासकः
प्रासक प्रासक, i. e. प्र- 2. अस् + अ, m. A die, dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग|प्रासंग|प्रासंगः|प्रासङ्गः
प्रासङ्ग प्रासङ्ग, i. e. प्र-आ-सञ्ज् + अ, m. A yoke for cattle, MBh. 13, 3270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्गिक|प्रासंगिक
प्रासङ्गिक प्रासङ्गिक, i. e. प्रसङ्ग + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a " target="_blank">Page0617-a + 42</a>] adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Belonging to any connexion, connected, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 17.<BR> 2. Inherent.<BR> 3. Incidental, episodical, Rājat. 5, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग्य|प्रासंग्य|प्रासंग्यः|प्रासङ्ग्यः
प्रासङ्ग्य प्रासङ्ग्य, i. e. प्रासङ्ग + य, adj. Yoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाद|प्रासादः
प्रासाद प्रासाद, i. e. प्र- (आ-?) सद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A palace, Pañc. 256, 3.<BR> 2. A temple, Pañc. 10, 8; Rām. 5, 38, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक प्रासिक, i. e. प्रास + इक, adj. Armed with a spear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थानिक
प्रास्थानिक प्रास्थानिक, i. e. प्र-स्थान + इक, adj. Referring to a journey, Rām. 2, 25, 16 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहुण|प्राहुणः
प्राहुण प्राहुण, (a form of प्राघुण), m. A guest, Kathās. 45, 269; 311.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहुणक
प्राहुणक प्राहुण + क, f. णिका, A guest, Kathās. 45, 267; 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतन|प्राह्णेतनः
प्राह्णेतन प्राह्णेतन, i. e. प्र-अह्न + इ + तन, adj., f. नी, Belonging to the forenoon, matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय प्रिय, i. e. प्री + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. या, comparat. प्रियतर and प्रेयंस्, superl. प्रियतम and प्रेष्ठ, Beloved, dear, Pañc. i. d. 205; agreeable, Śāk. 112, 15. प्रेयंस्, Much beloved, Kathās. 26, 283; Lass. 68, 4.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A husband, Bhāg. P. 4, 3, 6.<BR> 2. A lover, Pañc. i. d. 205.<BR> 3. A sort of deer.<BR> 4. A sort of drug.<BR> III. f. A wife or mistress.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Love, Rājat. 5, 47; sake, Chr. 22, 18.<BR> 2. A service, Vikr. 11, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ϕίλος, ϕιλίων; Lat. filius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अ- + प्रिय अ- + प्रिय,<BR> I. adj. unkind, offensive, Man. 5, 156.<BR> II. m. an enemy, Man. 6, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रप्रिय
पुत्र- + प्रिय पुत्र- + प्रिय, m. a kind of bird, MBh. 3, 9927.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणप्रिय|प्राणप्रियः
प्राण- + प्रिय प्राण- + प्रिय, adj. as dear as life, Lass. 8, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्राणप्रिय
अति-प्राण- + प्रिय अति-प्राण- + प्रिय, adj. dearer than life, Pañc. 220, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाप्रिय
प्रियाप्रिय प्रियाप्रिय, i. e. प्रिय-अ-, adj. agreeable and disagreeable, Hit. i. d. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुप्रिय|मरुप्रियः
मरु- + प्रिय मरु- + प्रिय, m. a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनप्रिय|यवनप्रियं
यवन- + प्रिय यवन- + प्रिय, m. black pepper. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b " target="_blank">Page0617-b + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणप्रिय|रणप्रियं|रणप्रियः
रण- + प्रिय रण- + प्रिय, 1. adj. warlike. 2. m. a hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमाप्रिय|रमाप्रियं|रमाप्रियः
रमा- + प्रिय रमा- + प्रिय, n. the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविप्रिय|रविप्रियं|रविप्रियः
रवि- + प्रिय रवि- + प्रिय, n. 1. the red lotus. 2. copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रिय|वनप्रियं|वनप्रियः
वन- + प्रिय वन- + प्रिय, m. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
वि- + प्रिय वि- + प्रिय,<BR> I. adj. disagreeable, Rājat. 5, 210.<BR> II. n. offence, transgression, Rām. 3, 55, 17; hostility, Pañc. i. d. 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वप्रिय|सर्व्वप्रिय|सर्व्वप्रियः
सर्व- + प्रिय सर्व- + प्रिय, adj. 1. generally beloved. 2. generally friendly, loving all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रिय|सुप्रियः
सु- + प्रिय सु- + प्रिय, adj. agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरप्रिय|सुरप्रियः
सुर- + प्रिय सुर- + प्रिय, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पतिसुरतप्रिया
वृहस्पति-सु-रत- + प्रिया वृहस्पति-सु-रत- + प्रिय (vb. रम्), f. या, a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहप्रिय|स्नेहप्रियः
स्नेह- + प्रिय स्नेह- + प्रिय, m. a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयप्रिय|हयप्रियः
हय- + प्रिय हय- + प्रिय, m. barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रिय|हरिप्रियं|हरिप्रियः
हरि- + प्रिय हरि- + प्रिय,<BR> I. m. 1. Śiva. 2. a foot. 3. armour.<BR> II. f. या, Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंवद|प्रियंवदः
प्रियंवद प्रियंवद, i. e. प्रिय + म्-वद् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Speaking what is agreeable, Hit. iii. d. 103.<BR> 2. Sweet speaking, Indr. 4, 11.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Ragh. 3, 53.<BR> III. f. दा, A proper name, Śāk. 10, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियक|प्रियकः
प्रियक प्रिय + क, m.<BR> 1. The name of several plants.<BR> 2. A kind of deer.<BR> 3. A bee.<BR> 4. A certain bird, MBh. 3, 11576.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकार
प्रियकार प्रिय-कार, and प्रियंकर प्रियंकर, i. e. प्रिय + म्-कर, adj.<BR> 1. Acting kindly, Sund. 1, 5.<BR> 2. Amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकृत्
प्रियकृत् प्रिय-कृ + त्, adj. sbst. Doing a kindness, a friend, Johns. Sel. 18, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंकर|प्रियङ्कर|प्रियङ्करः
प्रियंकर प्रियंकर, see प्रियकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंगु|प्रियङ्गु|प्रियंगुः|प्रियङ्गुः
प्रियंगु प्रियंगु, m.<BR> 1. A medicinal plant and perfume.<BR> 2. Panick seed, Panicum italicum.<BR> 3. Black mustard seed.<BR> 4. Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियता
प्रियता प्रिय + ता, f.<BR> 1. Being beloved, Man. 5, 50.<BR> 2. Love, Rājat. 5, 351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाल|प्रियालः
प्रियाल प्रियाल (akin to प्रिय), m. A tree, commonly Piyal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री प्री, ii. 9, प्रीणा, प्रीणी. and i. 1: † i. 10, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To please to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a " target="_blank">Page0618-a + 43</a>] delight, Bhartṛ. 2, 71; Rājat. 5, 280.<BR> 2. † To love. Pass. and i. 4, Ātm. (properly pass.),<BR> 1. To be pleased, MBh. 1, 1070; with the termination of the Par., MBh. 3, 15025 (and loc.).<BR> 2. To be satisfied, to assent, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 19.<BR> 3. To love, Rām. 6, 10, 23.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. प्रीत.<BR> 1. Beloved, Rām. 3, 49, 11.<BR> 2. Pleased, delighted, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 21.<BR> 3. Satisfied, Chr. 28, 17.<BR> 4. Kind.<BR> II. प्रीण,<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. प्रीणय (properly a denomin. derived from प्रीण), To delight, MBh. 1, 6414. प्रीणित, Pleased, Pañc. 198, 21.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, i. 4, Ātm. To be pleased, Rām. 2, 45, 22 Gorr. (= Schl. 2, 48, 18, where erroneously प्रियेत with short इ).<BR> --Cf. ἐϕιλάμην, प्रिय and प्रीति; Goth. frijon, frijônds, friathva, freis; A.S. fréfrian, freónd, freo, frio, frige, fridh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रीत
सु-प्रीत सु-प्रीत, adj., well pleased, very happy, Johns. Sel. 5, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीति|प्रीतिः
प्रीति प्री + ति, f.<BR> 1. Joy, Pañc. ii. d. 71; gratification, Hit. i. d. 96, M.M.<BR> 2. Love, Pañc. i. d. 317; Kathās. 99, 100.<BR> 3. Peaceable way, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR> 4. The wife of Kāma, or Cupid.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. fridh, fredho; O.H.G. fridu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपमरस
निरुपम-रस निरुपम-रस, i. e. निस्-उपम-रस-, f. unparalleled delight, Bhartṛ. 2, 9 (thus to be read).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमन्त्|प्रीतिमत्
प्रीतिमन्त् प्रीति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Affectionate, Lass. 66, 1.<BR> 2. Joyful, Chr. 60, 30.<BR> 3. Content, voluntary, Chr. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रु
प्रु प्रु, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्
प्रुष् प्रुष्, i. 1, Par. (i. e. probably प्र-उष्), To burn, to consume by fire. ii. 9 (i. e. probably प्र-उक्ष्), प्रुष्णा, प्रुष्णि, Par.<BR> 1. To sprinkle.<BR> 2. † To be wet.<BR> 3. † To fill.<BR> --Cf. perhaps περι-ϕλύω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्व|प्रुष्वः
प्रुष्व प्रुष् + व,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The rainy season.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> II. f. वा, A drop of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्वाय
प्रुष्वाय प्रुष्वाय, a denomin. derived from प्रुष्वा with य, Ātm. To dribble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षक|प्रेक्षकः
प्रेक्षक प्रेक्षक, i. e. प्र-ईक्ष् + अक, adj., f. इका, and sbst. Looking at, a spectator, Chr. 26, 63; Utt. Rāmac. 162, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षण|प्रेक्षणं
प्रेक्षण प्रेक्षण, i. e. प्र-ईक्ष् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. णा, Seeing, looking at, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212; looking wantonly, Man. 2, 179.<BR> 2. Seeing, visiting, Śāk. 18, 16 (Prākṛ.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The eye.<BR> 2. A public spectacle, Man. 9, 264.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यक्प्रेक्षण
तिर्यक्- + प्रेक्षण तिर्यक्- + प्रेक्षण (see तिर्यञ्च्), adj. looking sideways, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षा
प्रेक्षा प्रेक्षा, i. e. प्र-ईक्ष् + अ, f.<BR> 1. Seeing, Johns. Sel. 9, 11.<BR> 2. Seeing a play or entertainment of dancing, etc., Man. 9, 48.<BR> 3. Any public spectacle.<BR> 4. Consideration, Hariv. 6462; intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षावन्त्|प्रेक्षावत्
प्रेक्षावन्त् प्रेक्षा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षिन्
प्रेक्षिन् प्रेक्षिन्, i. e. प्र-ईक्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Seeing, Rām. 3, 52, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यक्प्रेक्षिन्
तिर्यक्- + प्रेक्षिन् तिर्यक्- + प्रेक्षिन् (see तिर्यञ्च्), adj. looking sideways, MBh. 2, 2164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खा|प्रेंखा
प्रेङ्खा प्रेङ्खा, i. e. प्र-ईङ्ख् + अ, f.<BR> 1. A swing, a hammock.<BR> 2. Dancing.<BR> 3. A horse's pace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोल्|प्रेंखोल्
प्रेङ्खोल् प्रेङ्खोल्, i. 10 (properly a denomin. akin to प्र-ईङ्ख्), To swing, Pañc. rec. orn. प्रेङ्खोलित, Swung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलन|प्रेंखोलनं|प्रेङ्खोलनं
प्रेङ्खोलन प्रेङ्खोल् + अन, n. A swing, a hammock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेणि
प्रेणि प्रेणि, i. e. प्री + नि, m. One who delights by praises, Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. i. 112, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सु
प्रेप्सु प्रेप्सु, i. e. प्र-ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + उ, adj. Desirous of obtaining, desiring, Man. 5, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन् प्रेमन्, i. e.<BR> I. प्री + मन् (and प्रिय + इमन्), n., Lass. 56, 16, and m. Love, Megh. 45; kindness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 187; 3337.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Indra.<BR> 2. Wind.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रेमन्
स्थित- + प्रेमन् स्थित- + प्रेमन्, m. a faithful friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्टप्रेमन्
प्रकृष्ट- + प्रेमन् प्रकृष्ट- + प्रेमन्, f. मा, exceedingly loving, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयंस्
प्रेयंस् प्रेयंस्, see प्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरण|प्रेरणं
प्रेरण प्रेरण, i. e. प्र-ईर् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sending, directing.<BR> 2. Ordering.<BR> 3. Passion.<BR> II. f. णा, Instigation, Hit. 88, 4; Rājat. 5, 478.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्त्वन्
प्रेर्त्वन् प्रेर्त्वन्, i. e. प्र-ईर् + त्वन्,<BR> I. m. The ocean.<BR> II. f. वरी, A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्
† प्रेष् प्रेष् (? or ह्रेष् ह्रेष्), i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषण|प्रेषणं
प्रेषण प्रेषण, i. e. प्र- 1. इष् + अन, n. Sending, despatching, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 7; errand, Lass. 30, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ प्रेष्ठ, see प्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्य|प्रेष्यः
प्रेष्य प्रेष्य, i. e. प्र- 1. इष्, Caus., + य, m. A servant, Chr. 52, 17; a slave, Man. 3, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामप्रेष्य|ग्रामप्रेष्यः
ग्राम- + प्रेष्य ग्राम- + प्रेष्य, m. the public servant of a town, MBh. 12, 2359; cf. Man. 3, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्यता
प्रेष्यता i. e. प्रेष्य + ता, f. Slavery, service, Man. 12, 70; Pañc. iii. d. 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैण्
प्रैण् प्रैण्, see पैण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष|प्रैषः
प्रैष प्रैष, i. e. प्र- 1. 2. इष् + अ.<BR> 1. Order.<BR> 2. Sorrow.<BR> 3. Frenzy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष्य|प्रैष्यः
प्रैष्य प्रैष्य, i. e. प्रेष्य + अ,<BR> I. m., f. या, A servant.<BR> II. n. Condition of a servant, Man. 2, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षण|प्रोक्षणं
प्रोक्षण प्रोक्षण, i. e. प्र-उक्ष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sprinkling with water, Man. 5, 115.<BR> 2. Immolation of victims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चण्ड|प्रोच्चंड
प्रोच्चण्ड प्रोच्चण्ड, i. e. प्र-उद्-चण्ड, adj. Horrible, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चैस्
प्रोच्चैस् प्रोच्चैस्, i. e. प्र-उच्चैस् (cf. उच्च), adv. Very loud, Pañc. 78, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झन|प्रोज्झनं
प्रोज्झन प्रोज्झन, i. e. प्र-उज्झ् + अन, n. Leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कट
प्रोत्कट प्रोत्कट, i. e. प्र-उत्कट, adj. Favourite(?), Pañc. 156, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कर्ष|प्रोत्कर्षः
प्रोत्कर्ष प्रोत्कर्ष, i. e. प्र-उत्कर्ष, m. Pre-eminence, Utt. Rāmac. 134, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहन|प्रोत्साहनं
प्रोत्साहन प्रोत्साहन, i. e. प्र-उद्-सह्, Caus., + अन, n. Instigating, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ्
प्रोथ् प्रोथ्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To neigh, to snort.<BR> 2. To be able (cf. प्रोथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ प्रोथ, i. e.<BR> I. प्रोथ् + अ (perhaps प्र-उद्-स्थ, vb. स्था; in this case the vb. प्रोथ् would be an old denomin., but cf. N.H.G. prusten), m. and n. The nose of a horse, Nal. 13, 20; of a hog, Arj. 3, 19.<BR> II. (for प्रोत्थ, i. e. प्र-उद्-स्थ), adj.<BR> 1. Travelling, a traveller.<BR> 2. Notorious.<BR> 3. Fixed.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The loins or hips.<BR> 2. The womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपद|प्रोष्ठपदः
प्रोष्ठपद प्रोष्ठपद, m. The month Bhādra, August--September.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ण
प्रोष्ण प्रोष्ण, i. e. प्र-उष्ण, adj. Very hot, Pañc. iii. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह|प्रोहः
प्रोह प्रोह, i. e. प्र-ऊह् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Skilful.<BR> 2. A reasoner.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An elephant's foot.<BR> 2. A joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढ|प्रौढं
प्रौढ प्रौढ, see प्र-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढि|प्रौढिः
प्रौढि प्रौढि, f., i. e.<BR> I. प्र-वह् + ति.<BR> 1. Increase, Kathās. 14, 63.<BR> 2. Elevation, Kathās. 21, 103 (in speech).<BR> 3. Enterprize, confident or audacious [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a " target="_blank">Page0620-a + 41</a>] exertion.<BR> II. प्र-ऊह् + ति, Investigation, discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठपद|प्रौष्ठपदः
प्रौष्ठपद प्रौष्ठपद, i. e. प्रोष्थपद + अ.<BR> 1. m. The month Bhādra, August--September.<BR> 2. f. दी, Full moon in Bhādra, Man. 4, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष्
† प्लक्ष् प्लक्ष्, v. r. of भक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष प्लक्ष, m.<BR> 1. The holy figtree, Ficus religiosa, Nal. 12, 4.<BR> 2. The waved-leaf fig-tree, Ficus infectoria.<BR> 3. Another tree, Hibiscus populneoides.<BR> 4. One of the seven Dvīpas or divisions of the world.<BR> 5. A side door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लब्
† प्लब् प्लब्, and प्लब् प्लव्, i. 1, Ātm. To go; cf. प्लु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव प्लव, i. e. प्लु + अ,<BR> I. adj. Leaping, jumping.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Jumping.<BR> 2. Swimming, Bhartṛ. i. 19 (cf. Böhtl. Roth. Sskr. Wörterbuch. s. v. पुलकय्).<BR> 3. A raft, a boat, Pañc. ii. d. 42.<BR> 4. A frog.<BR> 5. A monkey.<BR> 6. A sort of duck, Man. 5, 12.<BR> 7. A declivity or shelving ground.<BR> 8. A sort of basket or snare for catching fish.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πλόος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मप्लव
अश्म(न्)- + प्लव अश्म(न्)- + प्लव, m. a boat of stone, Man. 4, 190. See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्प्लव|मरुत्प्लवः
मरुत्- + प्लव मरुत्- + प्लव, m. a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवक|प्लवकः
प्लवक प्लवक, i. e. प्लु + अक, m. A tumbler, a man who walks on the edge of a sword, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवग|प्लवगः
प्लवग प्लव-ग (vb. गम्), m.<BR> 1. A monkey, Rām. 5, 58, 13.<BR> 2. A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवंग|प्लवङ्ग|प्लवंगः|प्लवङ्गः
प्लवंग प्लवंग, i. e. प्लव + म्-ग (vb. गम्), m.<BR> 1. A monkey.<BR> 2. A deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवंगम|प्लवङ्गम|प्लवंगमः|प्लवङ्गमः
प्लवंगम प्लवंगम, i. e. प्लव + म्-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A monkey, Man. 7, 72; Utt. Rāmac. 3, 4.<BR> 2. A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवन|प्लवनः
प्लवन प्लवन, i. e. प्लु + अन, n.<BR> 1. Jumping.<BR> 2. Swimming.<BR> 3. Inclining, MBh. 12, 1454.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशप्लवन
कुश- + प्लवन कुश- + प्लवन, n. the name of a holy place, MBh. 3, 8179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिह्
† प्लिह् प्लिह्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहन्
प्लिहन् and प्लीहन् प्ली̆हन्, m., and प्लीहा प्लीहा (ŚKD.), f.<BR> 1. The spleen, Yājñ. 3, 94 (ई).<BR> 2. Its disease.<BR> --Cf. σπλήν, probably σπλάγχνα; Lat. lien.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ली
† प्ली प्ली, or ल्वी ल्वी, ii. 9, प्लिना, प्लिनी, ल्विना, ल्विनी, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहन्
प्लीहन् प्लीहन् and प्लीहा प्लीहा, see प्लिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लु
प्लु प्लु, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To swim, Rām. 2, 69, 9.<BR> 2. To navigate, MBh. 3, 12782.<BR> 3. To fly, 3, 11767.<BR> 4. To jump, Śāk. d. 7; Rām. 5, 2, 34 (प्लवन्त्, ptcple. of the pres. Par., perhaps A monkey).<BR> 5. To jump over (with acc.), Rām. 1, 1, 70.<BR> 6. To blow, MBh. 3, 11070.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्लुत.<BR> 1. Bathed, Chr. 46, 25; wet, Pañc. 206, 24.<BR> 2. Jumped.<BR> 3. Lengthened to three moras, Man. 2, 125. n.<BR> 1. Leaping, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 12.<BR> 2. Bounding, Lass. 27, 1; capering, one of a horse's paces. Frequent. पोप्लूय, To swim swiftly, Rām. 2, 95, 10.<BR> --Caus. प्लावय,<BR> 1. To inundate, Rājat. 5, 269.<BR> 2. To sprinkle, Pañc. 208, 12.<BR> 3. Ātm. To bathe, Rām. 1, 44, 56.<BR> 4. To cause to stagger. प्लावित, Moistened, Pañc. 122, 24; covered (with blood), 237, 17.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभिप्लुत,<BR> 1. Overflowed.<BR> 2. Attacked, Hit. iv. d. 87 (v. r. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 936).<BR> 3. Labouring, Man. 4, 41.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To cover, MBh. 3, 2016. समभिप्लुत, Overwhelmed, labouring, Man. 4, 42.<BR> --With अव अव, To spring down, MBh. 4, 1260.<BR> 2. To deviate, 2, 1452.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To bathe, Man. 5, 77.<BR> 2. To wash, MBh. 3, 8514.<BR> 3. To swim near, 8. 12098.<BR> 4. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-a " target="_blank">Page0621-a + 43</a>] leap on, Johns. Sel. 31, 50. आप्लुत,<BR> 1. Bathed, Johns. Sel. 41, 49.<BR> 2. Wetted, Pañc. 238, 23; 160, 4 (covered, viz. with blood).<BR> 3. Covered, MBh. 3, 10693. m. An initiated householder. n. Bathing.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to bathe, MBh. 1, 7334.<BR> 2. Ātm. To bathe (गात्राणि, one's own limbs), Chr. 46, 29.<BR> 3. To sprinkle, Man. 3, 244.<BR> 4. To inundate, Man. 11, 97.<BR> 5. To cause to move, to excite, Rām. 1, 16, 24.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, समाप्लुत,<BR> 1. Drenched, drowned.<BR> 2. Filled, MBh. 3, 2172.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To leap up, Pañc. 117, 1.<BR> 2. To spring on, Man. 8, 236. उत्प्लुत, Jumped upon, approached suddenly.<BR> --With उप उप, उपप्लुत,<BR> 1. Wet.<BR> 2. Covered, Rām. 2, 7, 16.<BR> 3. Assailed, Man. 4, 118.<BR> 4. Distressed, MBh. 3, 2025.<BR> 5. Eclipsed.<BR> 6. Marked by prodigies.<BR> --With परि परि, To fluctuate, throb, Utt. Rāmac. 171, 5. परिप्लुत,<BR> 1. Circumfused, Chr. 30, 37.<BR> 2. Bathed.<BR> 3. Immersed.<BR> --With अभिपरि अभि-परि, अभिपरि-प्लुत,<BR> 1. Overflowed.<BR> 2. Filled, Rām. 1, 73, 27.<BR> 3. Agitated, Chr. 17, 29.<BR> --With वि वि, To fluctuate, Hit. iii. d. 2. विप्लुत,<BR> 1. Immersed, Rājat. 5, 20.<BR> 2. Mixed.<BR> 3. Having had sexual intercourse, Man. 8, 377.<BR> 4. Interrupted, Chr. 7, 21; troubled, Chr. 35, 7.<BR> 5. Depraved, false, Utt. Rāmac. 104, 7.<BR> 6. Devastated, destroyed, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. to divulge, to profane, Man. 11, 198.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To flow together, Utt. Rāmac. 97, 14.<BR> 2. To fluctuate, Utt. Rāmac. 155, 9. संप्लुत, Overspread, Johns. Sel. 60, 188.<BR> --Caus. To inundate, Rām. 1, 44, 35.<BR> --Cf. πλέω, πλεύσομαι, πλύνω, πύελος [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b " target="_blank">Page0621-b + 37</a>] probably λούω; Lat. pluere, plorare, fluere, probably lavare; O.H.G. flawjan, fluz; A.S. fleot; O.H.G. fliuzan; A.S. fleowan, aet-flowan, fleotan; O.H.G. flot; A.S. flód, also fleógan, fliógan, and fleón, flión.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लुत
अ- + प्लुत अ- + प्लुत, adj. uninterrupted, without intermission, Man. 2, 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्लुत
भय- + प्लुत भय- + प्लुत, adj. panic-struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुक्षि|प्लुक्षिः
प्लुक्षि प्लुक्षि (cf. 1. प्लुष्), m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
1. प्लुष् प्लुष्, i. 1 and 4, Par. To burn (cf. प्रुष्). प्लुष्ट, Rām. 2, 79, 20; Utt. Rāmac. 15, 5.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To consume with fire; उत्प्लुष्ट, Ṛt. 1, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
2. प्लुष् प्लुष्, ii. 9, Par.<BR> 1. † To be wet.<BR> 2. † To sprinkle.<BR> 3. † To fill.<BR> 4. To burn (cf. प्रुष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुस्
† प्लुस् प्लुस्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To burn.<BR> 2. To share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लेव्
† प्लेव् प्लेव्, see पेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोष|प्लोषः
प्लोष प्लोष, i. e. प्लुष् + अ, m. Burning, Rājat. 4, 316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा प्सा (sprung from भस् + आ by dropping अ), ii. 2, Par. To eat.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्सात, Eaten.<BR> --Cf. ὄψον.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सान|प्सानं
प्सान प्सान, i. e. प्सा + अन, n. Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्क्
फक्क् फक्क्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To creep, to move slowly.<BR> 2. † To act wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्किका
फक्किका फक्किका, f.<BR> 1. An assertion to be proved.<BR> 2. A sophism.<BR> 3. Fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट्
फट् फट्, A mystical syllable, Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट|फटः
फट फट (probably स्फट् + अ),<BR> I. m., and f. टा, The expanded hood or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a " target="_blank">Page0622-a + 43</a>] neck of the cobra di capello, or snake, Pañc. iii. d. 83; i. d. 229.<BR> II. f. टा.<BR> 1. A tooth.<BR> 2. A cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्
फण् फण्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --Caus. फणय,<BR> 1. To cause to go.<BR> 2. To produce easily (cf. फाण्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण फण, m., and f. णा, The expanded hood or neck of the cobra di capello, or snake in general, Pañc. i. d. 107; Śāk. d. 158; Bhartṛ. 2, 28 (णा).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्फण
अवाक्फण अवाक्फ्˚, i. e. अवाञ्च्-, adj. with downcast neck, Ṛt. 1, 13 v. r. गो-फणा, f. a concave bandage for the chin, nose, etc., Suśr. 1, 65, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणभृत्
फणभृत् फण-भृ + त्, फणवन्त् फण + वन्त्, and फणिन् फणिन्, i. e. फण + इन्, m. A snake, Kir. 5, 11 (˚भृत्); 27 (वन्त्); Pañc. i. d. 175 (˚णिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्ड|फंडः|फण्डः
फण्ड फण्ड, m. The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर्फरीक|फर्फरीकः
फर्फरीक फर्फरीक,<BR> I. m. The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Sweetness.<BR> 2. A shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्
फल् फल् (sprung from original स्पर्, cf. स्फर्, स्फुर्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To burst, MBh. 3, 1654.<BR> 2. To disappear (as if by bursting), MBh. 13, 7472.<BR> 3. To produce, Hit. ii. d. 132.<BR> 4. To bear fruit, figuratively, Man. 1, 84; to fall to one's share, Hit. 54, 18; to befall, Hit. iii. d. 21 (साधुषु, the good ones).<BR> 5. To be fruitful, Bhartṛ. 2, 38.<BR> 6. To be useful, 2, 98.<BR> 7. Impersonal pass. फलितम् (supply अस्ति), Fruit is borne, produced, Hit. 21, 13.<BR> 8. † To go.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. फलित (or फल + इत),<BR> 1. Fruitful, bearing fruit, Hit. 47, 3, M.M.<BR> 2. Successful, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 1.<BR> II. फुल्ल (instead of फल् + न),<BR> 1. Blown, expanded as a flower, Ṛt. 6, 6; Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> 2. Opened (as the eyes, with [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b " target="_blank">Page0622-b + 44</a>] pleasure), smiling.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, उत्फुल्ल,<BR> 1. Blown, as a flower, Kir. 5, 39.<BR> 2. Expanded (as the eyes, with fear), Rām. 3, 50, 15; (with surprise, with joy), Hit. 51, 10, M.M.; Indr. 2, 26.<BR> --Caus. फालय, To open, MBh. 1, 5977.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोत्फुल्ल, Blown, as a flower, Ṛt. 6, 34.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रफुल्ल,<BR> 1. Blown, as a flower, Ṛt. 6, 1.<BR> 2. Smiling.<BR> 3. Shining.<BR> 4. Glad.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To bound against, to be reflected, Śiś. 9, 37. प्रतिफलित,<BR> 1. Reflected.<BR> 2. Requited.<BR> --Cf. probably ὄϕελος, ὀϕέλλω; Lat. flos; A.S. blowan; Goth. bloma; A.S. bloma, blostma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल|फलं|फलः
फल फल् + अ, n.<BR> 1. Fruit, Utt. Rāmac. 33, 8.<BR> 2. Revenue, Hit. iv. d. 121.<BR> 3. Consequence, Chr. 9, 43.<BR> 4. Result, Hit. iv. d. 98 (संख्या-मात्रम्, consisting only in the number, i. e. by reckoning four you have nothing but the number, really there is only one).<BR> 5. Fulfilment of an omen, Śāk. d. 15.<BR> 6. Gain, Bhartṛ. 2, 18.<BR> 7. Reward.<BR> 8. A shield.<BR> 9. The blade of a sword or knife, the head of an arrow, Daśak. 197, 2(?).<BR> 10. A ploughshare.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अ- + फल अ- + फल, adj., f. ला. 1. Without fruit, Rām. 4, 59, 12. 2. unproductive, Man. 2, 158; figurat. 234. 3. unprofitable, prejudicial, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मफल
कर्म(न्)- + फल कर्म(न्)- + फल, n. retribution for actions, Man. 11, 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टफल
कृष्ट- + फल कृष्ट- + फल, n. the value of the crop, Yājñ. 2, 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणफल
क्षीण- + फल क्षीण- + फल, (vb. क्षि), adj. fruitless, Pañc. ii. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिफल
त्रि- + फल त्रि- + फल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, endowed with three fruits, Kām. Nītis. 8, 42.<BR> II. f. ला, the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फल|निष्फलः
निष्फल निष्फ्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ला. 1. without fruit, Rām. 4, 48, 6. 2. fruitless, useless, Man. 3, 144. 3. unproductive, Pañc. 174, 19. 4. irrelevant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यफल|पुण्यफलः
पुण्य- + फल पुण्य- + फल, n. reward of virtue or meritorious works [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a " target="_blank">Page0623-a + 45</a>] Man. 3, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःफल
पुरःफल पुरःफ्˚, i. e. पुरस्-, adj. of which the fruit is coming on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्फल|मरुत्फलं
मरुत्- + फल मरुत्- + फल, n. hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाफल|महाफलः
महा- + फल महा- + फल,<BR> I. n. a great fruit, Bhartṛ. 2, 86.<BR> II. m. a fruit-tree, Aegle marmelos.<BR> III. f. ला, a bitter gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दफल
मन्द- + फल मन्द- + फल, adj., f. ला, bearing scanty fruit, Lass. 35, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताफल|मुक्ताफलं
मुक्ता- + फल मुक्ता- + फल, n. 1. a pearl, Pañc. pr. d. 9. 2. camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाफलम्
यथा-फल + म् यथा-फल + म्, when bearing fruit, Pañc. i. d. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
वि- + फल वि- + फल, adj. vain, fruitless useless Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1395.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिफल|शारिफलं
शारि- + फल शारि- + फल, n. a chequered cloth or fable for playing draughts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीफल|श्रीफलः
श्री- + फल श्री- + फल, 1. m. a fruit-tree, Aegle marmelos. 2. (n.) the fruit of the Vilva, Man. 5, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफल|सफलं
स- + फल स- + फल, adj. 1. bearing fruit, Hit. i. d. 10, M.M.; rewarded, Vikr. 10, 9; fulfilled, Vikr. d. 27. 2. yielding a profit. 3. blessed, Rājat. 5, 373.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुफल|सुफलः
सु- + फल सु- + फल,<BR> I. adj. bearing good fruit.<BR> II. m., and f. ला, the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलक|फलकं|फलकः
फलक फल + क,<BR> I. (m. and) n.<BR> 1. A board, Man. 8, 396.<BR> 2. A bench, Man. 2, 204 (Kull.).<BR> 3. A layer, a base, Megh. 77 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. का, Having a base of crystal).<BR> 4. Surface, Bhartṛ. 2, 28.<BR> 5. A shield.<BR> 6. A leaf for writing on, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13 (? a small table).<BR> 7. The bone of the forehead.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The buttocks.<BR> 2. The receptacle of the seed = core; in गण्ड-, a core-like, or core-representing cheek, Śiś. 9, 47 (at the end of a comp. adj. Having cheeks instead of cores).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रफलक|चित्रफलकः
चित्र- + फलक चित्र- + फलक, n. a table with a likeness, a picture, Śāk. 85, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाफलक
शिला- + फलक शिला- + फलक, n. a layer or table of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपाकान्त
फलपाकान्त फलपाकान्त, i. e. फल-पाक + अन्त,<BR> I. adj., f. ता, Perishing when the fruit is mature, Man. 1, 46.<BR> II. f. ता, An annual plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलमुद्गरिका
फलमुद्गरिका फलमुद्गरिका, i. e. फल-मुद्गर + क, f. A sort of date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलवन्त्|फलवत्
फलवन्त् फल + वन्त्, adj. वति, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b " target="_blank">Page0623-b + 40</a>] Bearing fruit, Man. 1, 47; fruitful, Hit. pr. 43, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलस|फलसः
फलस फल-स, m. The jack or bread-fruit-tree<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन्
फलिन् फलिन्, i. e. फल + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Having fruits, Cāṇ. 21 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408; bearing fruit, Man. 1, 47.<BR> II. m. A tree, MBh. 14, 498.<BR> III. f. नी.<BR> 1. = Priyaṅgu.<BR> 2. A potherb, Echites dichotoma.<BR> 3. A flower, Celosia cristata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन|फलिनः
फलिन फलिन् + अ, adj. Bearing fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्क|फल्कः
फल्क फल्क, adj., explained by विशोधिताङ्क, which may be विशोधित-अङ्क, or शोधित-अङ्क with वि.<BR> --Cf. perhaps ϕολκός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गु|फल्गुः
फल्गु फल्गु, i. e. स्फुर्ज् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Pithless, sapless.<BR> 2. Vain, worthless, Pañc. pr. d. 10.<BR> 3. Weak, Hit. iii. d. 79.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. The opposite-leaved fig-tree.<BR> 2. The spring season.<BR> 3. Falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुता
फल्गुता फल्गु + ता, f., and फल्गुत्व फल्गु + त्व, n. Vainness, Bhartṛ. 2, 9.<BR> --Cf. सारफल्गुत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुन|फल्गुनः
फल्गुन फल्गु + न,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The month Phālguna.<BR> 2. A name of Arjuna.<BR> II. f. नी, du. or pl. The eleventh and twelfth lunar asterisms, distinguished as former, पूर्व, and latter, उत्तर; see फाल्गुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुनक
फल्गुनक फल्गुन + क, m.<BR> 1. Name of a people, Mārk. P. 58, 36.<BR> 2. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 472.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्य|फल्यं
फल्य फल्य, i. e. फल + य, n. A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाण्ट|फांट|फाण्टं|फाण्टः
फाण्ट फाण्ट, i. e. फण्, Caus., + त,<BR> I. ptcple. of the pf. pass. of the causal of फण्, Readily or easily prepared.<BR> II. m. Diluted decoction<BR> III. n. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a " target="_blank">Page0624-a + 41</a>] first particle of butter that are prepared by churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाण्ड|फांडं
फाण्ड फाण्ड (cf. फण्ड), n. The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल|फालं|फालः
फाल फाल, i. e. फल् + अ,<BR> I. m. n. The share of a plough, Man. 4, 46; 6, 16.<BR> II. m. A name of Śiva and Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुन|फाल्गुनः
फाल्गुन फाल्गुन, i. e. फल्गुन + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A month, February--March, Rājat. 5, 221.<BR> 2. A name of Arjuna, Johns. Sel. 13, 43.<BR> 3. A sort of tree, Pentaptera arjuna.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. The day of full moon in the month Phālguna.<BR> 2. The name of the eleventh and twelfth lunar asterisms, distinguished by the epithet former, पूर्व, and latter, उत्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुट|फुटः
फुट फुट, probably स्फुट् + अ, m., f. टा, and n. The expanded hood or neck of a snake, Pañc. 174, 11 (त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्
फुत् फुत्, indecl.<BR> 1. The expression of disregard.<BR> 2. Imitative sound, implying the boiling of water, etc. (see कृ, and cf. फूत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कार|फुत्कारः
फुत्कार फुत्-कार,<BR> I. adj. Disdainful, arrogant.<BR> II. m. The sound of bubbling (see फूत्कार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुप्फुस|फुप्फुसः
फुप्फुस फुप्फुस, see पुप्फुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल्
† फुल्ल् फुल्ल् (cf. फल्), i. 1, Par. To blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्
फूत् फूत् = फुत्,<BR> 1. Imitative sound of blowing, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1184.<BR> 2. Crying aloud, expression of indignation, anger, Pañc. 35, 11; 82, 18; 193, 11; Vetālap. xviii. MS. (see कृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कर्तुमनस्
फूत्कर्तुमनस् फूत्कर्तुमनस्, i. e. फूत्-कर्तुम्-मनस्, adj. Intending to cry aloud, to rage, Pañc. 40, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कार
फूत्कार फूत्-कार, m.<BR> 1. Blowing, hissing, Kathās. 22, 183.<BR> 2. Crying aloud, 13, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेन|फेनः
फेन फेन, probably akin to स्फाय्, m.<BR> 1. Froth, foam, Vikr. d. 115.<BR> 2. Moisture, Man. 3, 19.<BR> 3. Vapour.<BR> 4. Cuttle-fish bone.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. fam, foeman; Lat. spuma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अ- + फेन अ- + फेन, adj. not frothy, Man. 2, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनल|फेनलः
फेनल फेन + ल, फेनवन्त् फेन + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Frothy, foamy, Arj. 6, 2 (वन्त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाय
फेनाय फेनाय, a denomin. derived from फेन with य (Par.), Ātm. To froth, to foam, MBh. 6, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिन्
फेनिन् फेनिन्, i. e. फेन + इन्, फेनिल फेनिल, i. e. फेन + इल, adj. Frothy, foamy, Hiḍ. 2, 11 (निन्); Ragh. 13, 2 (निल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेर|फेरः
फेर फेर, and फेरु फेरु, m. A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरव|फेरवः
फेरव फेरव, i. e. फेरु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fraudulent.<BR> 2. Malicious.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A jackal, Mālat. 79, 17.<BR> 2. A Rākṣasa, Kathās. 47, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरु|फेरुः
फेरु फेरु, see फेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल्
† फेल् फेल्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल|फेलं
फेल फेल, n., फेला फेला, f., फेलि and फेली फेली̆, फेलिका फेलि + का, f. Orts, leavings of a meal, or droppings from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंह्
† बंह् बंह्, or वंह् वंह् (cf. बृह्), i. 1, Ātm. To grow or increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिष्ठ|बंहिष्ठः
बंहिष्ठ बंहिष्ठ, बंहीयंस् बंहीयंस्, see बहुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुल|बकुलः
बकुल बकुल, see वकुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बट्
बट् बट्, see वट्; बठ् बथ्, see वठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवा
बडवा बडवा and वडवा, f.<BR> 1. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a " target="_blank">Page0625-a + 38</a>] mare, Pañc. 252, 16; Utt. Rāmac. 123, 1.<BR> 2. The nymph Aśvinī, or the personified asterism which is designated by a horse's head, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 11.<BR> 3. A female slave, Rājat. 5, 280 (cf. -अनल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण्
बण् बण्, see त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्वह|बणिग्वहः
बणिग्वह बणिग्वह, i. e. बणिज्-वह् + अ, n. A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्
बणिज् बणिज्, and वणिज् वणिज्, i. e. पणि (ved. A merchant), -ज (vb. जन्), m. A merchant, Hit. 62, 9, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतबणिज्
पोत- + बणिज् पोत- + बणिज्, m. a seafaring merchant, Hit. 63, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्य|बणिज्यं
बणिज्य बणिज् + य, n., and f. या, Trade, traffic (probably erroneously for बाणिज्य, q. cf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्
† बद् बद्, पद् पद्, बन्द् बन्द्, i. 1, Par. To be steady or firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर बदर,<BR> I. m., and f. री (and वदरि), The jujube, Zizyphus jujuba or scandens, Nal. 12, 5 (व्).<BR> II. m. The seed of the cotton pod.<BR> III. f. रा and री, Cotton.<BR> IV. f. रा.<BR> 1. A plant, Mimosa octandra.<BR> 2. A medicinal drug.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. The fruit of the jujube.<BR> 2. The pod of the cotton.<BR> --Cf. वदरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिका
बदरिका बदरिका(?), i. e. बदरी + क (see the last), f. The jujube, Hit. i. d. 93, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्
बध् बध्,<BR> 1. See हन्.<BR> 2. See बन्ध्.<BR> 3. See बीभत्स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध बध, बधक बधक, see वध, वधक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधत्र
बधत्र 1. बध् + अत्र, n. A weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर बधिर, probably बन्ध् + इर, adj. Deaf, Pañc. v. d. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरता
बधिरता बधिर + ता f. Deafness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 831.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधूयु
बधूयु बधूयु, see वधूयु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्य
बध्य बध्य. see हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यता
बध्यता बध्य + ता, see वध्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्र|बध्रं
बध्र बध्र,<BR> I. n. Lead.<BR> II. (i. e. बन्ध् + र), f. री, A thong, MBh. 1, 1406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्
बन् बन्, see वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्|बंध्
बन्ध् बन्ध्, ii. 9, बध्ना, बध्नी, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Chr. 27, 2).<BR> 1. To bind, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 14; with अञ्जलिम्, to put one's hands together, etc. (see अञ्जलि,<BR> 3), Vikr. 58, 12; सेतुना गङ्गाम्, To bridge over the Ganges, MBh. 3, 10727; to overpower, Pañc. i. d. 128; to preclude, Pañc. i. d. 350.<BR> 2. To fasten, Matsyop. 47.<BR> 3. To bind on, MBh. 3, 12066.<BR> 4. To put on, Rām. 2, 37, 12; Ātm., Chr. 27, 2.<BR> 5. To fix on (as the inclination), Man. 5, 47.<BR> 6. To catch, Hit. i. d. 46.<BR> 7. To gain, get, Vikr. d. 27 (धृतिम्, satisfaction).<BR> 8. To bear (as fruit), Ragh. 12, 69.<BR> 9. To punish, Hit. ii. d. 63.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. बद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound.<BR> 2. Fixed, Vikr. 54, 4; firmly rooted, Rājat. 5, 377.<BR> 3. Directed, Pañc. i. d. 350.<BR> 4. Got, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 5. Inlaid, Megh. 77.<BR> 6. Checked, suppressed, Utt. Rāmac. 125, 1; Daśak. in. Chr. 187, 10.<BR> 7. Withheld.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. fut. pass. अ-बध्य, adj. what may not be checked, Pañc. i. d. 413.<BR> --Caus. बन्धय,<BR> 1. To cause to be bound, endowed, Ragh. 12, 7.<BR> 2. To cause to be embanked, Rājat. 5, 90.<BR> --i. 10, and † बध् बध्, i. 10, To bind, Rām. 2, 84, 4.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To unite, Rām. 1, 72, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-a " target="_blank">Page0626-a + 42</a>]<BR> 2. To hold together, Hit. i. d. 94, M.M.<BR> 3. To set on, Utt. Rāmac. 82, 12 (Premacandra Tark˚, to confound).<BR> 4. To continue, MBh. 3, 2562.<BR> 5. To follow, Śāk. 101, 20. अनुबद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound to.<BR> 2. Connected, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 1 (-अर्थ, adj. Wealthy).<BR> 3. Pressed, Mālav. 44, 14.<BR> --With अपि अपि, अपिबद्ध, Connected, fastened.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To fasten, Rām. 2, 96, 31.<BR> 2. To put on, Rām. 3, 50, 3. आबद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound on, Kir. 5, 33 (-वेपथु, adj. Trembling).<BR> 2. Joined, Rājat. 5, 92; Daśak. in Chr. 199, 14.<BR> 3. Put on, Megh. 9.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To fasten, Pañc. 135, 5; MBh. 3, 10030; to fix, Vikr. d. 118.<BR> 2. To fetter, Man. 6, 74.<BR> 3. To impose, Vikr. d. 36.<BR> 4. To catch, Pañc. 105, 9; and, To gain, i. d. 18.<BR> 5. To gain, i. d. 18.<BR> 6. To record, Man. 8, 255.<BR> 7. To destroy, MBh. 4, 982. निबद्ध,<BR> 1. Bound, Utt. Rāmac. 143, 2 (covered).<BR> 2. Connected, Man. 4, 155; made, Pañc. 211, 5.<BR> 3. Fixed upon.<BR> 4. Checked.<BR> 5. Restricted.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. not called upon as witness, Man. 8, 76 (Kull.).<BR> --With उपनि उप-नि, उपनिबद्ध, Composed, Utt. Rāmac. 162, 13.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निर्बद्ध, Pressed hard, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 3.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. निर्बन्धनीय, n. Quarrel(?), Hariv. 7267.<BR> --With परि परि, परिबद्ध, Obstructed, Rām. 2, 58, 11.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To bind, Pañc. iii. d. 269. प्रबद्ध, Bound, fastened, Pañc. 89, 10.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To disclaim, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 6.<BR> 2. To obstruct, Ragh. 1, 80 (79).<BR> 3. To enchase, Pañc. i. d. 85. प्रतिबद्ध,<BR> 1. Obstructed.<BR> 2. Opposed.<BR> 3. Set, inlaid, bestudded, Śiś. 9, 8.<BR> 4. Bound, connected with, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b " target="_blank">Page0626-b + 45</a>] Hit. iii. d. 128.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संबद्ध,<BR> 1. Connected with.<BR> 2. Endowed with.<BR> 3. Bound.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. one who has received no mandate, being without authority, Man. 8, 163. 2. unconnected. 3. incoherent. 4. inept, Śāk. d. 16.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्, अनुसंबद्ध, Accompanied, Johns. Sel. 23, 123.<BR> --Cf. Goth. and A.S. bindan; A.S. bonda, baend, baest; Goth. fastan; O.H.G. fasti; A.S. faest; Lat. patibulum (cf. रुधिर), pendĕre, pendêre, pondus, etc., probably filum, funis (for fid + lum, fud-nis); mani-festus; πεῖσμα (for πενθ + ματ), πενθερός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अ- + बद्ध अ- + बद्ध, adj. inept. Nal. 26, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध|बंध|बंधः|बन्धः
बन्ध बन्ध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Binding. Pañc. 248, 12; laying (snares), Pañc. 114, 11.<BR> 2. Holding in fetters, Man. 8, 310.<BR> 3. The body.<BR> 4. Building, Rājat. 5, 114.<BR> 5. Forming, 344.<BR> 6. Agreement, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 19; union, Pañc. 60, 19.<BR> 7. A tie, Vikr. d. 85; fetter, knot, Hit. i. d. 49, M.M.<BR> 8. A pledge, a deposit.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कबन्ध|अङ्कबन्धः
अङ्क- + बन्ध अङ्क- + बन्ध, m. branding with a dishonouring mark, Yājñ. 2, 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबन्ध|अर्थबन्धः
अर्थ- + बन्ध अर्थ- + बन्ध, m. a text, Śāk. d. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितार्थबन्ध
ललित-अर्थ- + बन्ध ललित-अर्थ- + बन्ध, adj. composed in verses treating of love, Vikr. d. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वबन्ध|अश्वबन्धः
अश्व-बन्ध् + अ अश्व-बन्ध् + अ, m. a groom, Rām. 2, 91, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाबन्ध|आशाबन्धः
आशा- + बन्ध आशा- + बन्ध, m. 1. confidence, Megh. 10. 2. a spider's web, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनबन्ध
आसन- + बन्ध आसन- + बन्ध, m. sitting down, Ragh. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशबन्ध|केशबंध|केशबन्धः
केश- + बन्ध केश- + बन्ध, m. a hair fillet, Bhāg. P. 8, 12, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबन्ध|दशबन्धः
दश-बन्ध दश-बन्ध, i. e. दशन्-, m. a fine amounting to the tenth part, Man. 8, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुबन्ध|पशुबन्धः
पशु- + बन्ध पशु- + बन्ध, m. immolation of an animal, MBh. 3, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिबन्ध|पाणिबंध|पाणिबन्धः
पाणि- + बन्ध पाणि- + बन्ध, m. union of the hands (as in marriage), MBh. 12, 9516.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादबन्ध
पाद- + बन्ध पाद- + बन्ध, m. a chain for the feet, MBh. 8, 2586.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्ध|पाशबंध|पाशबन्धः
पाश- + बन्ध पाश- + बन्ध, m. a net or noose, Hit. i. d. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिबन्ध|मणिबंध|मणिबन्धः
मणि- + बन्ध मणि- + बन्ध, m. the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागबन्ध|रागबन्धः
राग- + बन्ध राग- + बन्ध, m. true connection of the rāgas, Mālav. d. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सबन्ध
वत्स- + बन्ध वत्स- + बन्ध, adj., f. धा, anxious for (her) calf, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबन्ध|सुबंध|सुबन्धः
सु- + बन्ध सु- + बन्ध,<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a " target="_blank">Page0627-a + 43</a>] adj. well-secured.<BR> II. m. Sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुबन्ध|सेतुबंध|सेतुबन्धः
सेतु- + बन्ध सेतु- + बन्ध, m. 1. a dike, Rājat. 5, 92. 2. the ridge of rocks between the Coromandel coast and Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धक|बंधक|बन्धकं|बंधकः|बन्धकः
बन्धक बन्ध् + अक,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Binding.<BR> 2. Barter.<BR> II. m. A pledge.<BR> III. f. की.<BR> 1. An unchaste woman, Pañc. i. d. 197.<BR> 2. A barren woman.<BR> 3. A she elephant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबन्धक|नागबंधक|नागबन्धकः
नाग- + बन्धक नाग- + बन्धक, m. an elephant-hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्धक|पाशबंधक|पाशबन्धकः
पाश- + बन्धक पाश- + बन्धक, m. a birdcatcher, Pañc. iii. d. 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धन|बंधन|बन्धनं
बन्धन बन्ध् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Binding, Pañc. ii. d. 20; Hit. iii. d. 21 (of the ocean, by a bridge), fastening, Hit. i. d. 29, M.M.; catching, Pañc. 114, 6.<BR> 2. Confining, Hit. 34, 3, M.M. (जाल-, by a net).<BR> 3. A prison, Man. 9, 288.<BR> 4. A rope for tying cattle.<BR> II. m., f. ना or नी, and n. The instrument of tying, holding together, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 12; tic, Pañc. v. d. 19; string, Hit. 77, 1, M.M. (स्नायु-, made of a sinew); a rope, a thread, Pañc. iv. d. 78; a chain, snare, Pañc. ii. d. 19; stem, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौबन्धन
नौ- + बन्धन नौ- + बन्धन, n. the name of the highest top of the Himālaya, Matsyop. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्धन|पाशबंधन
पाश- + बन्धन पाश- + बन्धन,<BR> I. n. a snare, Bhāg. P. 9, 16, 31.<BR> II. adj. caught in a snare, Kathās. 13, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिबन्धन|मणिबंधन
मणि- + बन्धन मणि- + बन्धन, n. the wrist, Śāk. d. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितपदबन्धन
ललित-पद- + बन्धन ललित-पद- + बन्धन, n. a composition in verses treating of love, Śāk. 36, 16 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेषबन्धन
स-अवशेष- + बन्धन स-अवशेष- + बन्धन, adj. still bound, Pañc. 109, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्यबन्धन
सा-मर्थ्य- + बन्धन सा-मर्थ्य- + बन्धन, adj. cemented by power, Johns. Sel. 5, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धमय
बन्धमय बन्धमय, see श्लोक-बन्धमय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धिन्
ऽबन्धिन् -बन्धिन्, i. e. बन्ध्, and बन्ध + इन्, adj., f. नी, Fettered, Vikr. d. 147. मत्स्य-, m. A fisher, Pañc. 247, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धु|बंधु|बंधुः|बन्धुः
बन्धु बन्ध् + उ, m.<BR> 1. A kinsman, Pañc. iii. d. 182.<BR> 2. Kindred, Man. 2, 136; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b " target="_blank">Page0627-b + 43</a>] 3, 148 (maternal cousin, Kull.).<BR> 3. A friend, Hit. i. d. 30, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धु|अबंधु
अ- + बन्धु अ- + बन्धु, adj. having no friends, Pañc. i. d. 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रबन्धु|क्षत्त्रबन्धुः|क्षत्रबंधु|क्षत्रबन्धुः
क्षत्र- + बन्धु क्षत्र- + बन्धु, m. 1. a Kṣatriya, Man. 2, 38. 2. a mere, a base Kṣatriya, Bhāg. P. 1, 16, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मबन्धु|ब्रह्मबंधु|ब्रह्मबन्धुः
ब्रह्मबन्धु ब्रह्मबन्धु, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. 1. a Brāhmaṇa. 2. a base Brāhmaṇa, a term of abuse, Mālav. 39, 13; 58, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यबन्धु|राजन्यबन्धुः
राजन्य- + बन्धु राजन्य- + बन्धु, m. a Kṣatriya, Man. 2, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तबन्धु|वसंतबंधु|वसन्तबन्धुः
वसन्त- + बन्धु वसन्त- + बन्धु, m. the god of love, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुर|बंधुर|बन्धुरं|बन्धुरः
बन्धुर बन्धुर (partly vb. बन्ध्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Uneven, undulating, Ragh. 13, 47.<BR> 2. Bent, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 23.<BR> 3. Pleasing, handsome, Śāk. d. 140.<BR> 4. Deaf.<BR> 5. Injurious.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A goose.<BR> 2. A crane.<BR> III. f. रा, A prostitute.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. A diadem.<BR> 2. The dregs of oil.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. वन्धुर and A.S. bendan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धुर
अ- + बन्धुर अ- + बन्धुर, adj. straight, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूर|बंधूर|बन्धूरः
बन्धूर बन्धूर, adj.<BR> 1. Bent.<BR> 2. Handsome (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्य|बंध्य|बन्ध्यः
बन्ध्य बन्ध्य, i. e. बन्ध् + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Barren, Hit. pr. d. 15, M.M.<BR> 2. Confined.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. A childless woman.<BR> 2. A barren cow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्य|अबन्ध्यः
अ- + बन्ध्य अ- + बन्ध्य, adj. 1. fruitful, Megh. 11, s. v.; having a result, not vain, Vikr. d. 21. 2. happy, Vikr. d. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्र्
बभ्र् बभ्र् (sprung from बभ्रम्, i. e. reduplicated भ्रम्), or वभ्र् वभ्र्, i. 1, Par. To go, to go astray, Hit. 82, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रु|बभ्रुः
बभ्रु बभ्रु,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Large.<BR> 2. Tawny.<BR> 3. Bald-headed through disease.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu, Śiva, fire.<BR> 2. A large ichneumon.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A tawny or brown colour.<BR> 2. Any object of that colour; e. g. a tawny (red-) haired man, Man. 4, 130.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. brûn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रुश
बभ्रुश बभ्रु + श, adj. Tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्ब्|बंब्
बम्ब् बम्ब्, see बर्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्जह
बर्जह बर्जह, m. or n. An udder, Chr. 294, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्|बर्ब्ब्
† बर्ब् बर्ब्, बम्ब् बम्ब्, मर्ब् मर्ब्, and मम्ब् मम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्बर|बर्बरः|बर्ब्बर
बर्बर बर्बर (borrowed from the Greek βάρϐαρος, cf. वर्वर), m. A block head, Hit. 50, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह्
बर्ह् बर्ह्, or वर्ह् वर्ह्, i. 1, Ātm. †<BR> 1. To be pre-eminent.<BR> 2. † To speak.<BR> 3. To kill.<BR> 4. † To give, or to cover.<BR> --i. 10, †<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To kill, to hurt.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, i. 10, To destroy, to remove, Śiś. 1, 29.<BR> --Cf. वर्ह्, वल्ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह बर्ह. and वर्ह वर्ह, m. and n.<BR> 1. A peacock's tail, Megh. 15. 45.<BR> 2. A leaf.<BR> 3. Retinue.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रबर्ह|चित्रबर्हः
चित्र- + बर्ह चित्र- + बर्ह, 1. m. a peacock, MBh. 2, 2103. 2. a proper name, 5, 3597.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिण|बर्हिणः
बर्हिण बर्हिण, and वर्हिण वर्हिण, i. e. बर्हिन् + अ, m. A peacock, Vikr. d. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिन्
बर्हिन् बर्हिन्, and वर्हिन् वर्हिन्, i. e. बर्ह + इन्, m. A peacock, Draup. 8, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रबर्हिन्
चित्र- + बर्हिन् चित्र- + बर्हिन्, adj. having a variegated peacock's tail, MBh. 13, 4206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिषद्
बर्हिषद् बर्हिषद्, i. e. बर्हिस्-सद्, m. The name of a class of Pitṛs, Man. 3, 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिस्
बर्हिस् बर्हिस्, or वर्हिस् वर्हिस्,<BR> I. n. A layer, a seat of sacred grass, Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 6.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Sacrificial grass.<BR> 2. Sacrifice, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 5.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. Lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्
† बल् बल्. i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To live.<BR> 2. To hoard grain.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b " target="_blank">Page0628-b + 45</a>] बालय (Caus.), To nourish.<BR> II. बलय, To live.<BR> --Cf. भल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल बल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Baladeva.<BR> 2. A crow, Chr. 24, 45.<BR> 3. A demon.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Strength, Hit. i. d. 191, M.M.; power, Pañc. 44, 14.<BR> 2. An army, Hit. iv. d. 32.<BR> 3. Bulkiness.<BR> 4. The body.<BR> 5. Rigour, violence; abl. बलात्, Forcibly, Vikr. 33, 2 (as if it was your intention); without, or against one's will, Chr. 77, 11; Pañc. 27, 10.<BR> III. f. ला, A plant, Sida cordifolia.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अ- + बल अ- + बल,<BR> I. n. weakness, Rām. 1, 7, 12.<BR> II. adj., f. ला, weak, Pañc. i. d. 387.<BR> III. m. a proper name.<BR> IV. f. ला, a woman, Megh. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाबल
बलाबल बलाबल, i. e. बल-अ-बल, n. strength and weakness, Hit. iii. d. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबल|अतिबलः
अति- + बल अति- + बल,<BR> I. adj., excessively strong, Rām. 3, 20, 37.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR> III. f. ला, 1. the name of a spell, Rām. 1, 24, 12. 2. a plant, Sida cordifolia. 3. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघबल
अ-मोघ- + बल अ-मोघ- + बल, adj. of unfailing power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्बल|किंबल
किम्- + बल किम्- + बल, adj. possessed of what a power, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गबल
तुङ्ग- + बल तुङ्ग- + बल, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बल|दुर्ब्बल|दुर्ब्बलः
दुर्बल दुर्बल, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. ला. 1. weak, feeble, Pañc. i. d. 128. 2. without a prepuce, Man. 3, 151(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबल|नागबलः
नाग- + बल नाग- + बल, 1. m. a name of Bhīmasena. 2. f. ला, a shrub, Uraria lagopodioides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदुर्बल
परि-दुस्- + बल परि-दुस्- + बल, adj. very weak, Rām. 3, 63, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबल|महाबलं|महाबलः
महा- + बल महा- + बल,<BR> I. adj. very strong, powerful, Hit. 89, 22.<BR> II. m. air, wind.<BR> III. n. lead.<BR> IV. f. ला, a sort of Sida with yellow flowers, S. rhombifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाबलम्
यथा-बल + म् यथा-बल + म्, adv. to the utmost of one's power, Johns. Sel. 48, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्बल
वृहद्बल वृहद्ब्˚, i. e. वृहन्त्-, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबल|सबलः
स- + बल स- + बल, adj. 1. powerful, strong, Pañc. i. d. 267. 2. with (his) army, Chr. 54, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहाबल
सु-महा- + बल सु-महा- + बल, adj. very strong, Chr. 54, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेव|बलदेवः
बलदेव बलदेव, m.<BR> 1. Air, wind.<BR> 2. The elder brother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभिद्
बलभिद् बल-भिद्, m. Indra (the slayer of बल), Bhartṛ. 2, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलय
बलय बलय, see वलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवन्त्|बलवत्
बलवन्त् बल + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, comparat. बलीयंस्, superl. बलिष्ठ, strong, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 5; powerful, Chr. 35, 7; heavy, Vikr. 50, 8. बलीयंस्, Stronger, Pañc. iii. d. 7; बलीयस् + तर, much stronger, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 191. बलवत्, acc. sing. n., adv.<BR> 1. Much, Vikr. 7, 9.<BR> 2. Well, Śāk. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाक|बलाकः
बलाक बलाक, see वलाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाकिन्
बलाकिन् बलाकिन्, i. e. बलाक + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Having cranes, Ragh. 11, 15.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Johns. Sel. 42, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्कार|बलात्कारः
बलात्कार बलात्कार, i. e. बल + अत् (abl. of बल), -कार, m. Violence, Śāk. d. 173; Lass. 24, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहक|बलाहकः
बलाहक बलाहक, also वला˚ वला˚, m.<BR> 1. A cloud, MBh. 1, 1289; Śiś. 4, 54.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. A Nāga.<BR> 4. A demon, Draup. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलि|बलिः
बलि बलि (also वलि),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A religious offering, Pañc. 199, 13.<BR> 2. Presentation of food to all created beings; it consists in throwing a small parcel of the offering into the open air, Hit. ii. d. 41.<BR> 3. Fragments of food left at an oblation, or a meal, Pañc. 114, 5.<BR> 4. The sacrifice of an animal, sacrifice in general, Lass. 31, 7.<BR> 5. An animal, or one which is fit for an oblation.<BR> 6. Tax, royal revenue, Man. 7, 80; 9, 254; Pañc. 130, 17.<BR> 7. The handle of a fly-flapper, Megh. 36.<BR> 8. A king of the Daityas, also महाबलि, Johns. Sel. 95, 65; Pañc. iii. d. 268.<BR> II. f., also बली, and वलि.<BR> 1. A wrinkle.<BR> 2. The fold of skin upon the upper part of the belly, especially in females, Man. 6, 2; MBh. 1, 3467 (ई).<BR> 3. The ridge of a thatch.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलि|गृहबलिः
गृह-बलि गृह-बलि, m. a domestic sacrifice, Man. 3, 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबली
त्रि-बली त्रि-बली, or -वली, f. three folds of skin [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b " target="_blank">Page0629-b + 40</a>] on the abdomen, Bhartṛ. 1, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबलि|सबलिः
स-बलि स-बलि,<BR> I. adj. endowed with (royal) revenues, Pañc. 130, 17.<BR> II. m. evening twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपुष्पबलि
स-पुष्प- + बलि स-पुष्प- + बलि, adj. filled with offerings, surrounded by flowers, Vikr. d. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्
बलिन् बलिन्, i. e. बल + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Strong, Pañc. i. d. 128.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bull.<BR> 2. A camel.<BR> 3. A hog.<BR> 4. A name of Balarāma.<BR> 5. A sort of pulse, Phaseolus radiatus.<BR> 6. A sort of jasmine.<BR> III. f. नी, Sida cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन|बलिनः
बलिन बलि + न, and बलिभ बलि + भ, adj. Wrinkled, shrivelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिष्ठ|बलिष्ठः
बलिष्ठ बलिष्ठ, and बलीयंस् बलीयंस्, see बलवन्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीयस्त्व
बलीयस्त्व बलीयस्त्व, i. e. बलीयंस् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. State of being very powerful, Hit. iv. d. 42.<BR> 2. Excessive strength, Hit. iv. d. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीवर्द|बलीवर्दः|बलीवर्द्द|बलीवर्द्दः
बलीवर्द बलीवर्द, m. An ox (cf. बलिन्), Pañc. i. d. 311.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीवर्ध
बलीवर्ध बलीवर्ध, Hit. 57, 17 (corr. बलीवर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्ह्
† बल्ह् बल्ह्, or वल्ह् वल्ह्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To hurt.<BR> 3. To give, or to cover.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR> --Cf. बर्ह् and वल्ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बष्
बष् बष्, see वष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बस्
बस् बस्, see 3. वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहिस्
बहिस् बहिस्, see वहिस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहु
बहु बहु, adj., f. हु and ह्वी, comparat. बहु + तर, Utt. Rāmac. 13, 13, and भूयंस्, i. e. बहु + ईयम्स्, superl. भूयिष्ठ, i. e. भूयंस् + थ.<BR> 1. Much, Hit. 82, 5, M.M.; many, Hit. ii. d. 35.<BR> 2. Large, great.<BR> 3. बहुना, with किम्, In short, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 10. Comparat.<BR> I. भूयंस्.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a " target="_blank">Page0630-a + 41</a>] More, largest, Utt. Rāmac. 89, 4.<BR> 2. Greater part, Śāk. d. 7.<BR> 3. Stronger, Vikr. 65, 12.<BR> 4. More important, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 6. यस्, acc. sing. n., adv.<BR> 1. Repeatedly.<BR> 2. Again, Pañc. i. d. 184; Vikr. d. 94.<BR> 3. With following अपि, Again, Pañc. 24, 12; anew, Rājat. 5, 296.<BR> 4. Doubled, भूयोभूयस्, Repeatedly, Pañc. 37, 25. भूयसा, instr. sing. n. Generally, Utt. Rāmac. 128, 1.<BR> II. बहुतर + म्, adv. with following स्तोकम्, More than, Śāk. d. 7. Superl. भूयिष्ठ,<BR> 1. Very rich, Śāk. 3, 11.<BR> 2. Very many.<BR> 3. Almost all, Vikr. d. 8. adv. ˚ठम्, For the greatest part, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूयिष्ठ
अ-भूयिष्ठ अ-भूयिष्ठ, adj. scanty, Hit. iii. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तभूयिष्ठ
समाप्त-भूयिष्ठ समाप्त-भूयिष्ठ, adj. having the greater part finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबहु
सु-बहु सु-बहु, adj. very much, Chr. 28, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुक|बहुकः
बहुक बहुक, m.<BR> 1. A crab.<BR> 2. The digger of a tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुकुसुमित
बहुकुसुमित बहुकुसुमित, i. e. बहु-कुसुम + इत, adj. Full of blossoms, Vikr. d. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतस्
बहुतस् बहु + तस्, adv. From or by much, or many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतिथ|बहुतिथः
बहुतिथ बहु + तिथ, adj., f. थी.<BR> 1. Manifold, manieth.<BR> 2. Very long, Nal. 13, 2.<BR> 3. ˚थम्, adv. A very long time, Chr. 57, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्र
बहुत्र बहु + त्र, adv. In many ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्व|बहुत्वं
बहुत्व बहु + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Multitude, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 997.<BR> 2. Majority, Man. 8, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधनत्व
बहुधनत्व बहु-धन + त्व, n. Wealth, Śāk. 90, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधा
बहुधा बहु + धा, adv.<BR> 1. In many ways, Ṛt. 6, 10.<BR> 2. Manifoldly, Chr. 33, 4; Pañc. iii. d. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपत्नीकृत्
बहुपत्नीकृत् बहु-पत्नी-कृ + त्, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b " target="_blank">Page0630-b + 41</a>] One who marries many wives, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुल|बहुलं|बहुलः
बहुल बहु + ल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, comparat. बंहीयंस्, superl. बंहिष्ठ.<BR> 1. Manifold.<BR> 2. Much, Bhartṛ. 2, 29; numerous, Pañc. ii. d. 8; abundant, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 13; exceeding, ib. 69, 2 (thus to be read).<BR> 3. Abounding in, Man. 4, 60; Hit. i. d. 183, M.M.; Chr. 47, 41.<BR> 4. Variously applicable (a rule).<BR> 5. Black, Ragh. 11, 15.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Agni.<BR> 2. The dark half of a month.<BR> III. f. ला, pl. The Pleiades.<BR> IV. n. The sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशस्
बहुशस् बहु + शस्, adv.<BR> 1. Abundantly, Pañc. iii. d. 183.<BR> 2. Repeatedly, Śāk. d. 22; Vikr. d. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाड्
† बाड् बाड्, or वाड् वाड्, i. 1, Ātm. To bathe, to dive and emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडव|बाडवं|बाडवः
बाडव बाडव (also वाडव), i. e. बडवा + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 2. Submarine fire, Pañc. iv. d. 26.<BR> II. n. A stud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाण|बाणः
बाण बाण, see वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिजिक|बाणिजिकः
बाणिजिक बाणिजिक, i. e. बणिज् + इक, m. A trader, Man. 3, 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिज्य|बाणिज्यं
बाणिज्य बाणिज्य, i. e. बणिज् + य, n. Trade, Hit. 46, 14 (˚येन, for traffic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादर|बादरं|बादरः
बादर बादर, i. e. बदरा + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of cotton.<BR> II. m. The cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्
बाध् बाध्, or वाध् वाध् (akin to बध्, see हन्), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To repel, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 92, 5.<BR> 2. To oppose.<BR> 3. To remove, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 7.<BR> 4. To annoy, Hit. 57, 5; to grieve, Man. 10, 129; Pañc. 31, 10; pass. To suffer, ii. d. 95.<BR> 5. To torment, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2220 (= Hit. ii. d. 102, but cf. 1. 1.).<BR> 6. To damage, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a " target="_blank">Page0631-a + 41</a>] the pf. pass. बाधित,<BR> 1. Obstructed.<BR> 2. Pained.<BR> 3. Self-refuted, contradictory, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 7.<BR> --Caus. To annoy, Rām. 1, 14, 15.<BR> --With अधि अधि, To annoy, MBh. 1, 5693.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To pain, Rājat. 5, 442.<BR> --With अप अप, To repel, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3.<BR> --With आ आ, To restrain, Śāk. Chezy. 58, 10.<BR> --With परि परि, To annoy, MBh. 3, 8743; to importune, Śāk. d. 184.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To repel, MBh. 2, 1648.<BR> 2. To throw down, Pañc. i. d. 183.<BR> 3. To destroy, i. d. 455.<BR> 4. To annoy, Rām. 2, 53, 15.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To repel, Rām. 2, 52, 46.<BR> 2. To restrain, MBh. 3, 1081.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध बाध् + अ, or वाध वाध,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Opposing.<BR> 2. Being precluded by superior evidence (one of the five forms of fallacious middle term), Bhāṣāp. 77.<BR> 3. Annoyance.<BR> 4. Damage, Yājñ. 2, 156.<BR> 5. Danger, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3136.<BR> II. f. धा.<BR> 1. Refutation.<BR> 2. Annoyance, affliction, pain, Gīt. 1, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अ-बाध अ-बाध, adj. 1. Not harassed, Nal. 12, 104 (by fear). 2. and अबाध + क, free, Kathās. 26, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोकबाध
पर-लोक- + बाध पर-लोक- + बाध, f. loss of paradise, Pañc. 167, 8 (cf. my transl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणबाध
प्राण-बाध प्राण-बाध, m. extreme peril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनबाध
मदन- + बाध मदन- + बाध, f. pain of love, Vikr. 41, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध|सबाधः
स- + बाध स- + बाध, adj. 1. painful. 2. oppressive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधन|बाधनं
बाधन बाध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Opposing.<BR> 2. Refutation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 11.<BR> 3. Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधितत्व
बाधितत्व बाधित + त्व, n. Condition of being contradicted, refuted, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धकिनेय|बांधकिनेय|बांधकिनेयः|बान्धकिनेयः
बान्धकिनेय बान्धकिनेय, i. e. बन्धकी + इन् + एय, m. A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धव|बांधव|बांधवः|बान्धवः
बान्धव बान्धव, i. e. बन्धु + अ, m.<BR> 1. A relation, a kinsman, Pañc. iii. d. 141; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b " target="_blank">Page0631-b + 44</a>] Hit. i. d. 71, M.M.; Man. 4, 179 (a maternal relation, Kull.).<BR> 2. A friend, Hit. i. d. 72, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अ- + बान्धव अ- + बान्धव, adj. without kinsmen or friends, Rājat. 5, 23; 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतबान्धव
हत- + बान्धव हत- + बान्धव (vb. हन्), adj. without relations, Cāṇ. 6 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, p. 407.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल|बालं|बालः
बाल बाल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Young, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 2. Ignorant, Pañc. 169, 16.<BR> II. m., and f. ला.<BR> 1. A child (till sixteen years of age), Pañc. iv. d. 41; 219, 3; a foolish boy, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR> 2. A colt.<BR> 3. A five years' old elephant.<BR> 4. A tail, Man. 8, 234.<BR> 5. An elephant's or horse's tail, Rājat. 5, 386.<BR> 6. Hair.<BR> III. m. and n. A perfume, Andropogon schoenanthus.<BR> IV. f. ला.<BR> 1. A woman, Lass. 59, 10.<BR> 2. Small cardamoms.<BR> V. f. ली, A sort of earring.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बाल
दुस्- + बाल दुस्- + बाल, Man. 3, 151 v. r. The signification is questionable; Medātithi gives, bald-pated, or red-haired, or without a prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालक|बालकं|बालकः
बालक बाल + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A boy, a child, Pañc. 238, 20; a young one, 49, 18; young, Pañc. i. d. 372 (just risen, viz. the sun).<BR> 2. A foot.<BR> 3. The tail of a horse or elephant.<BR> 4. A finger ring.<BR> 5. A perfume.<BR> II. f. लिका.<BR> 1. A female infant.<BR> 2. A woman, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR> 3. Sand (perhaps erroneously for बालुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालखिल्य|बालखिल्यः
बालखिल्य बाल-खिल्य (ved.), m. A divine personage of the size of the thumb, sixty thousand of whom were produced from the hair of Brahman's body, MBh. 13, 442; Sund. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालधि|बालधिः
बालधि बालधि, i. e. बाल-धा (see निधि), m. A hairy tail, Man. 4, 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रबालधि|वक्रबालधिः
वक्र- + बालधि वक्र- + बालधि, m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालि|बालिः
बालि बालि, and बालिन् बालिन्, i. e. बाल + इन्, m. A monkey, the son of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश|बालिशं|बालिशः
बालिश बालिश, derived from बाल, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a " target="_blank">Page0632-a + 39</a>]<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Young.<BR> 2. Ignorant, foolish, Man. 3, 176; Pañc. i. d. 338.<BR> 3. Careless.<BR> II. n. A pillow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबालिश
अ- + बालिश अ- + बालिश, adj. wise, Hit. iv. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिशता
बालिशता बालिश + ता, f. Childishness, foolishness, Utt. Rāmac. 147, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश्य|बालिश्यं
बालिश्य बालिश्य, i. e. बालिश + य, n.<BR> 1. Youth.<BR> 2. Folly, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 8.<BR> 3. Thoughtlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुक|बालुकं|बालुकः
बालुक बालुक, cf. बाल,<BR> I. m. A drug and perfume.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. Sand, Man. 8, 250; 12, 76; Pañc. 105, 8.<BR> 2. Powder, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13.<BR> 3. Camphor.<BR> 4. and ˚की की, also बालुङ्की बालुङ्की, बालुङ्गिका बालुङ्गिका, बालुङ्गी बालुङ्गी, A sort of cucumber.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तबालुक|तप्तबालुकः
तप्त-बालुक तप्त-बालुक, adj. covered with hot sand, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तबालुक
रक्त-बालुक रक्त-बालुक, n. red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालेय|बालेयः
बालेय बालेय, i. e. बाल + एय,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fit for a child.<BR> 2. Soft.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ass.<BR> 2. A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल्य|बाल्यं
बाल्य बाल्य, i. e. बाल + य, n.<BR> 1. Childhood, Pañc. 219, 14.<BR> 2. Youth, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 1.<BR> 3. Foolishness, Draup. 5, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाष्प|बाष्पं|बाष्पः
बाष्प बाष्प, see वाष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह्
बाह् बाह्, see वाह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह|बाहः
बाह बाह,<BR> I. m., and f. हा, The arm.<BR> II. m. A horse (vb. वह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहु|बाहुः
बाहु बाहु, m. The arm, Vikr. d. 50.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πῆχυς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बाहु
उद्- + बाहु उद्- + बाहु, and ऊर्ध्व-, adj. having the arms lifted up, Ragh. 1, 3; Pañc. 165, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्बाहु|चतुर्बाहुः
चतुर्- + बाहु चतुर्- + बाहु, 1. adj. having four arms, Pañc. 251, 24. 2. m. Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 8, 17, 4; Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घबाहु
दीर्घ- + बाहु दीर्घ- + बाहु, 1. adj. long-armed, Rām. 3, 74, 20. 2. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुबाहु
पृथु- + बाहु पृथु- + बाहु, adj. lustyarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबाहु|महाबाहुः
महा- + बाहु महा- + बाहु, and सु-महा-, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b " target="_blank">Page0632-b + 40</a>] having long arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबाहु|सुबाहुः
सु- + बाहु सु- + बाहु,<BR> I. adj. powerful, Chr. 3, 2; very powerful, 39, 7; epithet of Rāvaṇa, Utt. Rāmac. 103, 2.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Johns. Sel. 27, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुक|बाहुकः
बाहुक बाहु + क,<BR> I. adj. Servile, a servant.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A monkey.<BR> 2. also वाहुक वाहुक, The name of Nala after his change of form, Nal. 15, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुगुण्य|बाहुगुण्यं
बाहुगुण्य बाहुगुण्य, i. e. बहु-गुण + य, n. Excess, Man. 7, 71 (instr. येन, Exceedingly)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुमय
बाहुमय बाहु + मय, adj., f. यी, Made with the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल|बाहुलं|बाहुलः
बाहुल बाहुल,<BR> I. i. e. बहुल + अ, m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. The month Kārttika.<BR> II. i. e. बाहु + ल, n. Mail worn on the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल्य|बाहुल्यं
बाहुल्य बाहुल्य, i. e. बहुल + य, n. Plenty, Hit. 47, 5, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह्य|बाह्यः
बाह्य बाह्य, see वाह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिट्
† बिट् बिट्, विट्, विट्, विड् विड्, and हिट् हिट्, i. 1, Par. To curse, to swear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिन्द्|बिंद्
† बिन्द् बिन्द्, or भिन्द् भिन्द्, i. 1, Par. To divide; cf. भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्ब|बिंब|बिंबं|बिम्बं|बिंबः|बिम्बः
बिम्ब बिम्ब, or विम्ब,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. The disk of the sun or moon, Pañc. 162, 23.<BR> 2. A reflected form, an image, Megh. 48.<BR> 3. Reflection, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 18.<BR> 4. The gourd of the Momordica monadelpha.<BR> II. n., and f. बा or बी, A cucurbitaceous plant with red fruit, Momordica monadelpha, Pañc. i. d. 225.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्कबिम्बम्
अभि-अर्क-बिम्ब + म् अभि-अर्क-बिम्ब + म्, adv. towards the orb of the sun, Śāk. d. 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुबिम्ब
इन्दु- + बिम्ब इन्दु- + बिम्ब, n. or m. the disk of the moon, Vikr. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बबिम्ब|नितंबबिंब
नितम्ब- + बिम्ब नितम्ब- + बिम्ब, n. the rounding of the buttocks, Ṛt. 6, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाङ्गश्रोणिविम्बा
रथ-अङ्ग-श्रोणि-विम्ब रथ-अङ्ग-श्रोणि-विम्ब, adj., f. बा, having buttocks [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a " target="_blank">Page0633-a + 39</a>] like the part (half) of a wheel, i. e. semicircular, Vikr. d. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तबिम्ब|हस्तबिम्बं
हस्त- + बिम्ब हस्त- + बिम्ब, n. perfuming the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बित|बिंबित
बिम्बित बिम्बित, i. e. बिम्ब + इत, also विम्बित, adj.<BR> 1. Reflected, Rājat. 5, 343.<BR> 2. Pictured.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बित|प्रतिबिंबित
प्रति- + बिम्बित प्रति- + बिम्बित, adj. reflected, Utt. Rāmac. 109, 5; Lass. 73, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बोष्ठ
बिम्बोष्ठ बिम्बोष्ठ, and बिम्भौष्ठ बिम्बौष्ठ, or विम्ब्˚, i. e. बिम्ब-ओष्ठ,<BR> I. m. A bimba-like lip, i. e. red as the Bimba fruit, Kathās. 4, 8 (corr. p. 146 A, 2 bel.).<BR> II. adj., f. ठा and ठी, Having lips like the Bimba fruit, redlipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्
† बिल् बिल्, i. 6, Par., and i. 10, Par., also भिल् भिल्, To break, to divide; cf. भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल|बिलं|बिलः
बिल बिल, see विल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिश्
† बिश् बिश्, and बेश् बेश्, i. 6, Par. To go(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिस्
† बिस् बिस्, i. 4, Par. To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीज|बीजं|बीजः
बीज बीज, see वीज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभ्
† बीभ् बीभ्, or चीभ् चिभ्, i. 1, Ātm. To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
1. बीभत्स बीभत्स, an anomal. desider. probably of बाध्, Ātm. To be angry, to detest, Utt. Rāmac. 6, 6 (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
2. बीभत्स बीभत्स, i. e. बीभत्स + अ,<BR> I. m. Disgust, abhorrence.<BR> II. adj.<BR> 1. Loathing, detesting.<BR> 2. Loathful, Utt. Rāmac. 99, 9; Pañc. iii. d. 112.<BR> 3. Mischievous, cruel.<BR> 4. Envious.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबीभत्स
अति- + बीभत्स अति- + बीभत्स,<BR> I. m. grudge, envy, Rām. 3, 1, 21<BR> II. adj. exceedingly loathful, cruel, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्सु|बीभत्सुः
बीभत्सु बीभत्सु, i. e. बीभत्स + उ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b " target="_blank">Page0633-b + 43</a>] adj. Envious, emulous, Arj. 3, 1 (read बिभ्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क्
बुक्क् बुक्क्, i. 1 and † 10, Par.<BR> 1. To sound, to bark, Pañc. rec. orn.<BR> 2. † i. 10, To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क बुक्क,<BR> I. m. A goat.<BR> II. m., f. का and की, and n. The heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुङ्ग्
बुङ्ग् बुङ्ग्, see वुङ्ग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुट्
† बुट् बुट्, i. 10 and 1, Par. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुड्
बुड् बुड्, see चुड् and पुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्
बुद् बुद्, see बुन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धि|बुद्धिः
बुद्धि बुद्धि, i. e. बुध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Understanding, Bhāṣāp. 50; Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 24; Pañc. 81, 5.<BR> 2. Reflexion, Rām. 3, 48, 14.<BR> 3. Intellect, Pañc. i. d. 219.<BR> 4. Mind, Pañc. i. d. 87; Chr. 5, 8.<BR> 5. Thought, Rām. 3, 48, 14; intention, Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR> 6. Knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 165.<BR> 7. Opinion, Hit. 81, 14 (व्याघ्र-, mistaking him for a tiger).<BR> 8. Presence of mind, Pañc. ii. d. 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. πύστις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धि|अबुद्धिः
अ- + बुद्धि अ- + बुद्धि,<BR> I. f. foolishness, Rām. 4, 1, 23.<BR> II. adj. foolish, Man. 3, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमनुष्यबुद्धि
अति-मनुष्य- + बुद्धि अति-मनुष्य- + बुद्धि, adj. having a more than human intellect, Johns. Sel. 54, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षाबुद्धि|अपेक्षाबुद्धिः
अपेक्षा- + बुद्धि अपेक्षा- + बुद्धि, f. that operation of the mind by which we count things one by one, which produces द्वित्व, etc., Bhāṣāp. 106. See कु. कृत-, adj. 1. one who knows his duty, Man. 1, 97. 2. resolved, Vikr. 86, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रबुद्धि|क्षुद्रबुद्धिः
क्षुद्र- + बुद्धि क्षुद्र- + बुद्धि, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुद्धि
दुर्बुद्धि दुर्ब्˚ i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. f. foolishness, MBh. 5, 4890.<BR> II. adj. perverse, foolish MBh. 4, 416; Hiḍ. 1, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टबुद्धि
दुष्ट- + बुद्धि दुष्ट- + बुद्धि (vb. दुष्), adj. ill-minded, Pañc. 22, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहबुद्धि|द्रोहबुद्धिः
द्रोह- + बुद्धि द्रोह- + बुद्धि,<BR> I. adj. treacherous, Pañc. 58, 8.<BR> II. f. treachery, 58, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबुद्धि
धर्म- + बुद्धि धर्म- + बुद्धि,<BR> I. adj. virtuous.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बुद्धि
निर्बुद्धि निर्ब्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. deprived of reason, Hit. i. d. 133, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापबुद्धि
पाप- + बुद्धि पाप- + बुद्धि, 1. adj. evil-minded. 2. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदबुद्धि
भेद- + बुद्धि भेद- + बुद्धि, f. distinction, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a " target="_blank">Page0634-a + 45</a>] Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दबुद्धि|मंदबुद्धि
मन्द- + बुद्धि मन्द- + बुद्धि, adj. stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्दबुद्धि
सु-मन्द- + बुद्धि सु-मन्द- + बुद्धि, adj. very disheartened, Chr. 41, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबुद्धि
महा- + बुद्धि महा- + बुद्धि, adj. endowed with much intellect, Pañc. 4, 22; very sensible (ironically, Chr. 6, 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतबुद्धि
विकृत- + बुद्धि विकृत- + बुद्धि, adj. ill-minded, Hit. 73, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतविरुद्धबुद्धि
वीत-विरुद्ध- + बुद्धि वीत-विरुद्ध- + बुद्धि, i. e. वि-इत-वि-रुद्ध- (vb. रुध्), adj. peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबुद्धि
सु- + बुद्धि सु- + बुद्धि, adj. intelligent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धितस्
बुद्धितस् बुद्धि + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. = abl. of बुद्धि, Bhāṣāp. 121.<BR> 2. By the mind, Rām. 6, 95, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिमन्त्|बुद्धिमत्
बुद्धिमन्त् बुद्धि + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Endowed with understanding, Man. 1, 96; intelligent, Pañc. iii. d. 40; wise, Pañc. i. d. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्बुद|बुद्बुदः
बुद्बुद बुद्बुद, m. A bubble, Utt. Rāmac. 88, 3; Pañc. 203, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्
बुध् बुध्, i. 1, Par. Ātm., i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 1, 5053); originally, To fathom, to penetrate (cf. ved. बुध् + न, Depth, ground; A.S. bytne, botm; βυθός; Lat. fundus).<BR> 1. To understand, Hit. i. d. 92 (pass.).<BR> 2. To know, MBh. 1, 5148 (i. 4).<BR> 3. To think, Hit. i. d. 3.<BR> 4. To perceive, MBh. 3, 2893 (i. 4); Lass. 55, 12 (Ātm.); 14 (Par.).<BR> 5. To admonish, Pañc. i. d. 176, (बोद्धव्य, in the sense of बोधयितव्य).<BR> 6. i. 4, To recover one's senses, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 57.<BR> 7. i. 4, To awake, Rām. 1, 46, 19; pass., Pañc. 183, 2; Śiś. 9, 24.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. बुद्ध,<BR> 1. Known, understood.<BR> 2. Knowing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 5. m.<BR> 1. A sage.<BR> 2. The founder of the Bauddha religion.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अश्व-बुध्य, adj. cognoscible, distinguished by horses, Chr. 294, 7 = Rigv. i. 92, 7.<BR> --Caus. बोधय,<BR> 1. To cause to know (with two acc.), to inform, MBh. 2, 2506.<BR> 2. To advise, 3, 12774.<BR> 3. To admonish, 1, 5785.<BR> 4. To awaken, Pañc. i. d. 351; MBh. 1, 5959.<BR> 5. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-b " target="_blank">Page0634-b + 42</a>] expand (as a flower), Śāk. d. 124. बोधित, Brought to consciousness, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 14.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To learn, MBh. 3, 14779.<BR> 2. To know, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17.<BR> 3. To remember, MBh. 1, 4874.<BR> 4. To awake, 1, 5024.<BR> --Caus. To cause to remember, Śāk. 4, 16. अनुबोधित, Informed or convinced by reflection.<BR> --With अव अव, i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To know, MBh. 2, 1371.<BR> 2. To perceive, Man. 8, 53.<BR> 3. To awake, Rām. 2, 72, 50, ed. Ser.<BR> --Caus. To inform, MBh. 1, 5811.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, i. 4, Ātm. To know, to perceive, Rām. 2, 9, 31.<BR> --With नि नि, i. 1,<BR> 1. To learn, Man. 1, 119.<BR> 2. To hear, MBh. 3, 311.<BR> 3. To know, 3, 2443.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. i. 1, To awaken, MBh. 3, 10635.<BR> 2. i. 4, To awake, Hit. iii. d. 142; Kathās. 3, 65. प्रबुद्ध,<BR> 1. Wise, Pañc. 4, 22.<BR> 2. Wakened, awakened, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 12; awake, Hit. 14, 7, M.M.<BR> 3. Expanded.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to know, to inform, to admonish, Pañc. 121, 10; Ragh. 3, 68; to instruct, Hit. i. d. 53, M.M.<BR> 2. To awaken, Rām. 2, 56, 1. प्रबोधित,<BR> 1. Instructed.<BR> 2. Aroused.<BR> --With वि-प्र वि-प्र, विप्रबुद्ध, Awakened, aroused, Megh. 110.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, i. 4, To awake, Man. 1, 74. प्रतिबुद्ध,<BR> 1. Known.<BR> 2. Wakened, awake.<BR> 3. Exalted.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To inform, Ragh. 1, 75.<BR> 2. To admonish, to instruct, Pañc. 87, 24.<BR> 3. To charge one with, Rām. 2, 52, 35.<BR> 4. To awaken, Śāk. d. 143. प्रतिबोधित,<BR> 1. Instructed.<BR> 2. Awakened.<BR> --With वि वि, i. 4, To awake, MBh. 2, 162. विबुद्ध,<BR> 1. Awake.<BR> 2. Opened (as a flower), Mālav. d. 60.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To awaken.<BR> 2. To instruct, Daśak. 181, 17.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a " target="_blank">Page0635-a + 41</a>] सम् सम्, i. 4,<BR> 1. To know, MBh. 1, 2498.<BR> 2. To be wise, 2, 2187 (Par.).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to agree, Pañc. 101, 11.<BR> 2. To exhort, Pañc. 84, 1; to admonish, Pañc. 103, 2.<BR> 3. With परस्परम्, To come to an explanation with each other, Pañc. 101, 11.<BR> 4. To ask, MBh. 1, 3521.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्, प्रतिसंबुद्ध, Recovered, MBh. 3, 12519.<BR> --Cf. πυθμήν, πυνθάνομαι, πεύθομαι; Lat. puteus (cf. रुधिर and बन्ध्), putare; Goth. biudan; A.S. beodan, boda, bodian, bodare, and look to the beginning of this article.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्
अ- + बुध् अ- + बुध्, adj. foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध|बुधः
बुध बुध् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Wise, Pañc. i. d. 427.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Budha, the son of the moon and regent of the planet Mercury.<BR> 2. A proper name, Vikr. d. 159.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध
अ- + बुध अ- + बुध, adj. foolish, Hit. ii. d. 23; Rājat. 5, 380.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुध
दुर्बुध दुर्ब्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. foolish, MBh. 11, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधान|बुधानः
बुधान बुधान (properly a ptcple. pres. of बुध्, following ii. 2), m. A spiritual guide or teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्न|बुध्नः
बुध्न बुध् + न, m.<BR> 1. The root of a tree.<BR> 2. Śiva; see बुध्.<BR> --Cf. probably A.S. bytne, the bottom of a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्द्|बुंद्
बुन्द् बुन्द्, or † चुन्द् चुन्द्, also † बुद् बुद्, बुन्ध् बुन्ध्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To perceive.<BR> 2. † To reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्ध्|बुंध्
† बुन्ध् बुन्ध्, i. 10, Par. To bind; cf. बुन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षा
बुभुक्षा बुभुक्षा, i. e. बुभुक्ष, desider. of भुज्, + अ, f. Desire of eating, Hit. 77, 1, M.M.; Hunger, Pañc. 114, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षित|बुभुक्षितः
बुभुक्षित बुभुक्षित, i. e. बुभुह्षा + इत, adj. Hungry, starving, Pañc. 114, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षु
बुभुक्षु बुभुक्षु, i. e. बुभुक्ष, desider. of भुज्, + उ, adj. Wishing to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सा
बुभुत्सा बुभुत्सा, i. e. बुभुत्स, desider. of बुध्, + अ, f. Wishing to know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सु
बुभुत्सु बुभुत्सु, i. e. बुभुत्स, desider. of बुध्, + उ, adj. Desirous of knowing, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुल्
† बुल् बुल्, i. 10, Par. To sink, to dive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुलि|बुलिः
बुलि बुलि, f. The vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्
बुस् बुस्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To effund.<BR> 2. † To distribute (cf. 2. व्युष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त्
बुस्त् बुस्त्, see पुस्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृंह्
बृंह् बृंह्, and बृह् बृह्, see वृंह्, वृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहन्त्|बृहत्
बृहन्त् बृहन्त्, and वृहन्त् वृहन्त् (originally ptcple. pres. of बृह्),<BR> I. adj., f. हती.<BR> 1. Large, great, Pañc. 175, 9.<BR> 2. Much.<BR> II. f. अती.<BR> 1. A wrapper, a mantle.<BR> 2. A reservoir, a place containing water.<BR> 3. A large lute.<BR> 4. The name of two plants.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. bairgahei; A.S. beorh, beorg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पति|बृहस्पतिः
बृहस्पति बृह् + अस्-पति, and बृहस्पति वृहस्पति, m.<BR> 1. A deity, originally The lord of prayer, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 12.<BR> 2. The regent of the planet Jupiter and preceptor of the gods, Bhartṛ. 2, 27.<BR> 3. The name of a saint and lawgiver, Pañc. i. d. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बॄ
बॄ बॄ, see वॄ; बेश् बेश्, see बिश्; and बेह् बेह्, see वेह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध|बोधः
बोध बोध, i. e. बुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Knowledge, Bhāṣāp. 140.<BR> 2. Intellect, wisdom.<BR> 3. Arousing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अ- + बोध अ- + बोध,<BR> I. m. stupidity, Bhartṛ. 3, 2.<BR> II. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a " target="_blank">Page0636-a + 41</a>] adj. ignorant, Cāṇ. 35 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबोध|आत्मबोधः
आत्मबोध आत्मबोध, i. e. आत्मन्-,<BR> I. m. knowledge of the universal soul, Häberl. Anth. 489.<BR> II. adj. endowed with the knowledge of the universal soul, Bhartṛ. 1, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ब्˚
दुर्ब्˚ दुर्ब्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be understood, or penetrated, Rām. 4, 17, 6; Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबोध|सुबोधः
सु- + बोध सु- + बोध,<BR> I. adj. 1. easily taught. 2. of easy apprehension.<BR> II. m. 1. waking. 2. knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधक|बोधकः
बोधक बोधक, i. e. बुध्, Caus., + अक,<BR> I. adj. Causing to know, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 1.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A teacher.<BR> 2. A spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधन|बोधनं|बोधनः
बोधन बोधन, i. e. बुध् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. नी.<BR> 1. Knowledge, Ragh. 9, 49.<BR> 2. Teaching.<BR> 3. Arousing, Śiś. 9, 24.<BR> II. n. Burning incense.<BR> III. m. The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधि|बोधिः
बोधि बोधि, i. e. बुध् + इ,<BR> I. adj. Wise, learned.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Intellect.<BR> 2. The holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्ध|बौद्धं|बौद्धः
बौद्ध बौद्ध, i. e. बुद्ध + अ, m. A follower of the Bauddha religion, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौध|बौधः
बौध बौध, i. e. बुध + अ, patronym. A son of Budha = Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्युस्
ब्युस् ब्युस्, see 2. व्युष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रण्
ब्रण् ब्रण्, see व्रण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्न|ब्रध्नः
ब्रध्न ब्रध्न, perhaps वृध् + न, m.<BR> 1. The root of a tree.<BR> 2. A son.<BR> 3. The body.<BR> 4. The sun, Man. 4, 231.<BR> 5. Śiva, Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मक
ऽब्रह्मक -ब्रह्मक, i. e. ब्रह्मन् + क, at the end of a comp. adj. instead of ब्रह्मन्, in स-, adj. With Brahman, Utt. Rāmac. 174, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघातक|ब्रह्मघातकः
ब्रह्मघातक ब्रह्मघातक, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-घातक, and ब्रह्मघ्न ब्रह्मघ्न, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b " target="_blank">Page0636-b + 43</a>] i. e. ब्रह्मन्-घ्न, m. The slayer of a Brāhmaṇa, Pañc. ii. d. 115. iv. d. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघोष|ब्रह्मघोषः
ब्रह्मघोष ब्रह्मघोष, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-घोष, m. The word of Brahman, the Vedas, Utt. Rāmac. 145, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्य|ब्रह्मण्यः
ब्रह्मण्य ब्रह्मण्य, i. e. ब्रह्मन् + य, adj.<BR> 1. Relating or connected with Brahman or a Brāhmaṇa; fit for a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 2. Pious, Nal. 1, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मण्य|अब्रह्मण्यं
अ- + ब्रह्मण्य अ- + ब्रह्मण्य,<BR> I. adj. 1. not fit for a Brāhmaṇa. 2. hostile to the Brāhmaṇas.<BR> II. n. 1. wickedness, a wicked act, Pañc. 101, 1. 2. an exclamation of distress, alas! woe! Pañc. 82, 18; murder, Kathās. 4, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मत्व|ब्रह्मत्वं
ब्रह्मत्व ब्रह्मत्व, i. e. ब्रह्मन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Identification with, or state of, Brahman, MBh. 13, 1361.<BR> 2. Godhead.<BR> 3. The rank of a Brāhmaṇa, Johns. Sel. 23, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मद|ब्रह्मदः
ब्रह्मद ब्रह्मद, and ब्रह्मदातृ i. e. ब्रह्मन्-द (vb. दा), or -दातृ, m. A spiritual teacher, Man. 2, 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदायहर
ब्रह्मदायहर ब्रह्मदायहर, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-दाय-हृ + अ, adj. One who receives the gift of holy science, Man. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन् ब्रह्मन्, probably बृह् + मन्,<BR> I. n. Prayer, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 88, 4.<BR> 2. The practice of austere devotion.<BR> 3. Chastity, Śāk. 14, 12.<BR> 4. The Vedas or scripture, Man. 1, 23.<BR> 5. The Brāhmaṇas, or theological part of the Veda, Man. 4, 100.<BR> 6. Holy knowledge.<BR> 7. The brahmanical caste, Man. 9, 320.<BR> 8. The divine cause and essence of the world, the unknown God.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Brāhmaṇa, a priest (originally possessed of, or performing, powerful prayer), Chr. 15, 5.<BR> 2. Brahman, the first deity of the Hindu triad, and the operative creator of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a " target="_blank">Page0637-a + 40</a>] world, Man. 1, 9; 50; Utt. Rāmac. 36, 12 (वागात्मन्, i. e. वाच्-, adj. whose soul is speech).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मन्
अ- + ब्रह्मन् अ- + ब्रह्मन्, adj. without Brāhmaṇas, Man. 9, 322.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाब्रह्मन्
महा- + ब्रह्मन् महा- + ब्रह्मन्, m. a great, mighty Brāhmaṇa, Chr. 20, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दब्रह्मन्
शब्द- + ब्रह्मन् शब्द- + ब्रह्मन्, n. holy writ, Veda, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 3; cf. 36, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुब्रह्मन्
सु- + ब्रह्मन् सु- + ब्रह्मन्, adj. endowed with beautiful prayers, Lass. 101, 6 = Rigv. vii. 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयोनिस्थ
ब्रह्मयोनिस्थ ब्रह्मयोनिस्थ, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-योनि-स्थ, adj. Intent on the means of attaining holy knowledge, Man. 10, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्चस|ब्रह्मवर्च्चस|ब्रह्मवर्च्चसं
ब्रह्मवर्चस ब्रह्मवर्चस, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-वर्चस् + अ, n.<BR> 1. Holiness, Man. 2, 37; 4, 94.<BR> 2. The superhuman power of a Brāhmaṇa, Śāk. 81, 16 (ironically).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवित्त्व
ब्रह्मवित्त्व ब्रह्मवित्त्व, i. e. ब्रह्मविद् + त्व, n. The state of one who knows the nature of the Supreme Spirit, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविद्
ब्रह्मविद् ब्रह्मविद्, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-विद्, m. One who knows the Supreme Spirit; a wise one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माञ्जलिकृत
ब्रह्माञ्जलिकृत ब्रह्माञ्जलिकृत, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-अञ्जलि-कृत, adj. Having joined together the hands, as token of homage, Man. 2, 70; cf. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माधिगमिक
ब्रह्माधिगमिक ब्रह्माधिगमिक, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-अधिगम + इक, adj. Proceeding from the study of the scripture, Man. 2, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोज्झता
ब्रह्मोज्झता ब्रह्मोज्झता, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-उज्झ् + अ + ता, f. Neglecting or forgetting the Veda, Man. 11, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोद्य|ब्रह्मोद्यं
ब्रह्मोद्य ब्रह्मोद्य, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-वद् + य, adj., f. या, Speaking or treating of holy knowledge, Man. 3, 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म ब्राह्म, i. e. ब्रह्मन् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. मी.<BR> 1. Relating to the Brāhmaṇas, brahmanical, Johns. Sel. 33, 67; deposited with the sacerdotal class, Man. 7, 82.<BR> 2. Relating to holy knowledge.<BR> 3. Relating to study, scriptural, Man. 3, 157.<BR> 4. Prescribed by the Veda, 7, 2.<BR> 5. Relating to Brahman, 1, 68.<BR> 6. Fit for a divine state, 2, 28.<BR> 7. Epithet of a weapon, Chr. 40, 15.<BR> 8. also sbst. m. The name of the first nuptial form, Man. 3, 27, and 21.<BR> 9. Relating, sacred to Brāhmī, the goddess of speech, 4, 92.<BR> II. m. Nārada, the son of Brahman.<BR> III. f. मी.<BR> 1. A wife espoused according to the Brāhma form, Man. 3, 37.<BR> 2. The goddess of speech, the wife of Brahman.<BR> 3. The moon plant (Asclepias acida).<BR> IV. n. The part of the hand under the root of the thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण ब्राह्मण, i. e. ब्रह्मन् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Relating to, becoming a Brāhmaṇa, brahmanical, Johns. Sel. 38, 27.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa, a man of the first caste, Pañc. 220, 24.<BR> III. f. णी.<BR> 1. A woman of the brahmanical tribe.<BR> 2. The wife of a Brāhmaṇa, Pañc. 118, 25.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. An assemblage of Brāhmaṇas.<BR> 2. The theological portion of the Vedas, Pāṇ. 2, 3, 60, Sch.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्राह्मण|अब्राह्मणः
अ- + ब्राह्मण अ- + ब्राह्मण, 1. m. one who is not a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 2, 241. 2. adj. without Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोब्राह्मण
गो- + ब्राह्मण गो- + ब्राह्मण, a cow and a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 5, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणब्रुव|ब्राह्मणब्रुवः
ब्राह्मणब्रुव ब्राह्मणब्रुव, i. e. ब्राह्मण-ब्रू + अ, m. A wicked Brāhmaṇa, Man. 7, 85; Chr. 24, 38 (read -ब्रुव instead of -ब्रुवम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्य|ब्राह्मण्यः
ब्राह्मण्य ब्राह्मण्य, i. e. ब्राह्मण (cr ब्रह्मन्), + य,<BR> I. m. The planet Saturn.<BR> II. n. Brahmanhood, priestly character, Man. 11, 97; the dignity of a Brāhmaṇa, Pañc. i. d. 76.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-a " target="_blank">Page0638-a + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वब्राह्मण्या
स्व-ब्राह्मण्या स्व-ब्राह्मण्या, f. a sort of text, Man. 9, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्य|ब्राह्म्यं
ब्राह्म्य ब्राह्म्य, i. e. ब्रह्मन् or ब्राह्म, + य,<BR> I. adj. with and without हुत, n. One of the five sacraments, the worship or veneration of Brāhmaṇas, Man. 3, 73, 74.<BR> II. n. Astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रू
ब्रू ब्रू, ii. 2, Par. Ātm., used only in the pres., imperf., imperat. and potent. All other forms are supplied by वच्, and the redupl. pf., partly also by 1. अह्.<BR> 1. To speak, Man. 1, 1.<BR> 2. To speak to, with dat. and acc., 1, 60.<BR> 3. To answer, 8, 94.<BR> 4. With अन्यथा, To decide wrongly, to give a wrong sentence (in a law suit), Pañc. iii. d. 108. In epic poetry, anomal. 1. sing. present, ब्रूमि, Rām. 2, 19, 4; imperf. अब्रुवम्, even in Daśak. in Chr. 185, 11.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To abuse, MBh. 3, 15640.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To pronounce, MBh. 1, 176.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To declare, MBh. 1, 838.<BR> 2. To recite, Man. 10, 1.<BR> 3. To tell, MBh. 3, 16678.<BR> 4. To speak, 3, 10487.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer, MBh. 3, 2737.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To explain, MBh. 1, 4245.<BR> 2. To speak at variance, Man. 8, 194.<BR> 3. To say what is false, 8, 13; to declare falsely, 8, 75.<BR> 4. To decide unjustly, 8, 390.<BR> 5. To speak, MBh. 3, 2990.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्ली
ब्ली ब्ली (ved.), व्ली व्ली, ii. 9, ब्लिना, व्लिना, नी, ved. ब्लीना, व्लीना, नी, Par.<BR> 1. To select.<BR> 2. † To hold.<BR> 3. † To maintain.<BR> 4. † To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ भ (vb. भा),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A star, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 14.<BR> 2. A lunar asterism. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b " target="_blank">Page0638-b + 43</a>]<BR> 3. A planet.<BR> II. m. A name of the planet Venus.<BR> III. f. भा, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्त|भक्तं|भक्तः
भक्त भक्त, i. e. ptcple. pf. pass. of भज् (in the signification To cook, cf. also भक्ष्), n.<BR> 1. Food, Man. 9, 271.<BR> 2. Boiled rice.<BR> 3. A meal, Man. 11, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्त
एक- + भक्त एक- + भक्त, n. eating only once a day, MBh. 13, 5146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थभक्त
चतुर्थ- + भक्त चतुर्थ- + भक्त, n. eating only the fourth meal (leaving out three), i. e. eating only every second day, MBh. 13, 5145; cf. भज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकर|भक्तकरः
भक्तकर भक्त-कर, m. Factitious incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ति|भक्तिः
भक्ति भक्ति, i. e. भज् and भञ्ज् + ति,<BR> 1. Worship, Vikr. d. 1; service.<BR> 2. Devotion, Hit. iii. d. 65.<BR> 3. Attachment, Pañc. i. d. 326.<BR> 4. Faith, Pañc. 71, 4; belief, Śāṇḍilyas. ed. Ballantyne, 76 sqq.<BR> 5. Fracture, breaking, Megh. 61.<BR> 6. In भक्ति-छेद, Megh. 19, see छेद.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रभक्ति|क्षेत्रभक्तिः
क्षेत्र- + भक्ति क्षेत्र- + भक्ति, f. partition of a field, Pāṇ. 5, 1, 46, Sch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्भक्ति|दृग्भक्तिः
दृग्भक्ति दृग्भक्ति, i. e. दृश्-, f. a side look, an amorous look, Lass. 66, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिभाज्
भक्तिभाज् भक्तिभाज्, i. e. भक्ति-भज्, adj. Devout, Pañc. 236, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिमन्त्|भक्तिमत्
भक्तिमन्त् भक्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. ती, Devoted, faithful, Pañc. pr. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्
भक्ष् भक्ष्, akin to भज् and भञ्ज्, i. 1, Par. Ātm., and i. 10, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm.),<BR> 1. To devour, Man. 5, 50.<BR> 2. To eat, MBh. 3, 1741.<BR> 3. To enjoy, Pañc. 137, 20.<BR> 4. To bite, Pañc. 62, 23; Kathās. 4, 69.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. भक्ष्य, Eatable, allowed to be eaten, Man. 1, 113. n.<BR> 1. Food, Pañc. 199, 13.<BR> 2. Dainty food, Man. 9, 268; 3, 227.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a " target="_blank">Page0639-a + 43</a>] सम् सम्, To devour, MBh. 3, 422.<BR> --Cf. ϕαγεῖν, perhaps ϕακός, ϕάσηλος; Lat. fames, perhaps bacca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्य|अभक्ष्यं
अ- + भक्ष्य अ- + भक्ष्य, adj. unfit, or not allowed, to be eaten, Man. 1, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभक्ष्य|सर्व्वभक्ष्य
सर्व- + भक्ष्य सर्व- + भक्ष्य, adj. 1. eating anything (a child). 2. omnivorous. Desider. of i. 10, बिभक्षयिष, To desire to devour, MBh. 1, 5951.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष|भक्षः
भक्ष भक्ष् + अ,<BR> I. m., f. षा, and n. (Pañc. rec. orn.), Eating food, Pañc. 53, 23.<BR> II. latter part of comp. adj. Devouring, Man. 9, 314 v. r.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्ष|वायुभक्षः
वायु- + भक्ष वायु- + भक्ष,<BR> I. adj., f. षा. 1. feeding on air, Johns. Sel. 51, 1. 2. fasting, Chr. 46, 20.<BR> II. m. 1. an ascetic. 2. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभक्ष|सर्वभक्षः|सर्व्वभक्ष
सर्व- + भक्ष सर्व- + भक्ष,<BR> I. adj. omnivorous, eating all things, Hit. ii. d. 173.<BR> II. f. षा, a female goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षक|भक्षकः
भक्षक भक्ष् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Voracious.<BR> 2. Eating, feeding on, Hit. 75, 8.<BR> 3. A feeder, Hit. i. d. 54, M.M.<BR> II. f. षिका, A meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षण|भक्षणं
भक्षण भक्षण, i. e. भक्ष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Eating, Pañc. 114, 10; being eaten, 88, 25.<BR> 2. Enjoying, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्षण|वायुभक्षणः
वायु- + भक्षण वायु- + भक्षण, n. fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षिन्
ऽभक्षिन् -भक्ष् + इन्, adj. Eating; in सर्व-, adj. Eating all kinds of food, Pañc. i. d. 472.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग|भगं|भगः
भग भग, i. e. भज् and भञ्ज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Divine power.<BR> 2. Fortune.<BR> 3. Virtue.<BR> 4. Beauty.<BR> 5. Pudendum muliebre, Rājat. 5, 282.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. ga-bigs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भग
दुर्भग दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. गा. 1. difficult to be obtained, Rājat. 4, 113. 2. unfortunate, Hit. i. d. 17, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभग|सुभगः
सु- + भग सु- + भग,<BR> I. adj., f. गा. 1. fortunate, Chr. 287, 7 = Rigv. i. 48, 7. 2. beautiful, Vikr. d. 123; lovely, Śāk. d. 3; charming, d. 57. 3. beloved, amiable, Man. 2, 129.<BR> II. m. 1. the Aśoka tree. 2. the Champaca, Micelia campaka.<BR> III. f. गा. 1. a favourite woman. 2. a respectable mother. 3. the name of several plants.<BR> IV. n. fortune, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदत्त|भगदत्तः
भगदत्त भग-दत्त (vb. दा), m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगनेत्र
भगनेत्र भग-नेत्र, m. The name of a demon, Johns. Sel. 97, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवन्त्|भगवत्
भगवन्त् भग + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Adorable, Man. 1, 6; Vikr. 31, 18; 85, 21; respectable, worshipful (used in address), Chr. 17, 27; Pañc. 80, 13.<BR> II. f. वती, A name of Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाल|भगालं
भगाल भगाल, n. The human skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगालिन्
भगालिन् भगालिन्, i. e. भगाल + इन्, m. A name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनी
भगिनी भगिनी, i. e. भग + इन् + ई, f.<BR> 1. A sister, Pañc. 214, 25; 222, 9.<BR> 2. A woman in general.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभगिनी
धर्म- + भगिनी धर्म- + भगिनी, f. 1. a woman on whom the rank of a sister is bestowed, Kathās. 4, 96; cf. Pañc. 222, 9. 2. a Bauddha nun, Mṛcch. 134, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथ|भगीरथः
भगीरथ भगीरथ, m. A king whose austerities brought Gaṅgā, the river, from heaven; called her father, Rām. 1, 44, 8 sqq. Gorr.; Utt. Rāmac. 167, 10; Chr. 24, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोस्
भगोस् भगोस्, an old voc. sing. of भगवन्त्, indecl. A particle used as respectful address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्क्तृ
भङ्क्तृ भङ्क्तृ, i. e. भञ्ज् + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Breaking, one who breaks down, Man. 9, 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग|भंग|भंगः|भङ्गः
भङ्ग भङ्ग, i. e. भञ्ज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Breaking, Pañc. iii. d. 16.<BR> 2. A fissure, a broken piece, Vikr. d. 107 (a branch).<BR> 3. Interruption, Pañc. 8, 19; obstacle, Vikr. 12, 17.<BR> 4. Repudiation.<BR> 5. Defeat, discomfiture, destruction, Hit. 100, 3; ruin, Lass. 76, 18.<BR> 6. Disappointment, neglect, Hit. ii. d. 52.<BR> 7. Fear, Pañc. 219, 18; iv. d. 43.<BR> 8. Curving, Śāk. d. 7; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a " target="_blank">Page0640-a + 45</a>] knitting (the brow), Utt. Rāmac. 138, 3.<BR> 9. Fraud.<BR> 10. A wave.<BR> 11. A water-course.<BR> 12. Disease.<BR> II. f. गा Hemp.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभङ्ग|असुभंग|असुभङ्गः
असु- + भङ्ग असु- + भङ्ग, m. danger of life, Bhartṛ. 2, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहभङ्ग
उत्साह- + भङ्ग उत्साह- + भङ्ग, m. destroying, breaking one's courage, Hit. 94, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभङ्ग|गृहभंग|गृहभङ्गः
गृह- + भङ्ग गृह- + भङ्ग, m. loss of a wife, Pañc. 225, 17 (cf. iii. d. 152).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डभङ्ग|दंडभंग|दण्डभङ्गः
दण्ड- + भङ्ग दण्ड- + भङ्ग, m. hinderance of punishment, Bhāg. P. 6, 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तभङ्ग
दन्त- + भङ्ग दन्त- + भङ्ग, m. splitting, breaking of teeth, Pañc. i. d. 418.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भङ्ग
दुर्भङ्ग दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be loosened, Hariv. 1138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रभङ्ग|पत्रभंग|पत्रभङ्गः
पत्र- + भङ्ग पत्र- + भङ्ग, m., and f. गी̆, strokes and lines drawn on the face with fragrant pigments of sandal, musk, etc., Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 622 (ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पभङ्ग
पुष्प- + भङ्ग पुष्प- + भङ्ग, m. treading on flowers, Nal. 25, 7 (Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठभङ्ग|पृष्ठभङ्गः
पृष्ठ- + भङ्ग पृष्ठ- + भङ्ग, m. a sort of fighting, MBh. 2, 908.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतभङ्ग|पोतभंग|पोतभङ्गः
पोत- + भङ्ग पोत- + भङ्ग, m. shipwreck, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1072.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयभङ्ग|प्रणयभंग|प्रणयभङ्गः
प्रणय- + भङ्ग प्रणय- + भङ्ग, m. faithlessness, Vikr. d. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूभङ्ग|भ्रूभंग|भ्रूभङ्गः
भ्रू- + भङ्ग भ्रू- + भङ्ग, m. a frown, Vikr. d. 115; Rājat. 5, 398.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्रूभङ्गम्
स-भ्रू-भङ्ग + म् स-भ्रू-भङ्ग + म्, adv. knitting the brows, Śāk. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभङ्ग|सारभङ्गः
सार- + भङ्ग सार- + भङ्ग,<BR> I. adj. void of pith, substance, strength.<BR> II. m. destroying vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिताभङ्ग
हिता- + भङ्ग हिता- + भङ्ग, m. breaking of a dike, Man. 9, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गि|भंगि|भंगिः|भङ्गिः
भङ्गि and भङ्गी भङ्गी, i. e. भञ्ज् + अ + इ, f.<BR> 1. Fracture.<BR> 2. Separation, interval, Lass. 83, 1; step, degree, Ragh. 13, 69.<BR> 3. Incurvation, Lass. 87, 16.<BR> 4. Current, Rājat. 2, 131.<BR> 5. figurat. Modesty, Kathās. 21, 103.<BR> 6. Fraud, pretext, Kathās. 3, 53.<BR> 7. A wave, Ragh. 16, 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रभङ्गि|पत्रभंगि|पत्रभङ्गिः
पत्र- + भङ्गि पत्र- + भङ्गि, see s. v. भङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिन्|भंगिन्
भङ्गिन् भङ्गिन्, i. e. भङ्ग + इन्, adj., f. नी, Frail, perishable, Lass. 42, 18; Bhartṛ. 2, 88 (क्षण-, in a moment; v., and better r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुर|भंगुर|भङ्गुरः
भङ्गुर भङ्गुर, i. e. भञ्ज् + उर,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Crooked, Bhartṛ. 3, 36.<BR> 2. Frail, perishable, Pañc. 165, 17; vanishing, Hit. i. d. 186, M.M.<BR> 3. Fraudulent, Lass. 84, 9.<BR> II. m. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-b " target="_blank">Page0640-b + 43</a>] bend of a river.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभङ्गुर|अभंगुर
अ- + भङ्गुर अ- + भङ्गुर, adj. 1. unbroken. 2. undisturbed, Rājat. 5, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग्य|भंग्यं|भङ्ग्यं
भङ्ग्य भङ्ग्य, i. e. भङ्गा + य, n. A field of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भज्
भज् भज्, i. I, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To divide, Man. 9, 104.<BR> 2. To obtain as one's share, to obtain, Man. 10, 59 (Ātm.); to get, Śāk. d. 167; Pañc. 69, 4 (Par.).<BR> 3. To take, MBh. 4, 237 (Ātm.); to embrace, Śāk. d. 107 (Ātm.); to love, Lass. 44, 7.<BR> 4. To go to, Rām. 1, 16, 28; with दिशस्, To run away, MBh. 3, 11113.<BR> 5. To take possession of, Man. 1, 28.<BR> 6. To possess, to have, Man. 5, 148.<BR> 7. To enjoy carnally, to love, Man. 9, 70.<BR> 8. To make advances, Man. 8, 365.<BR> 9. To serve, to worship, MBh. 3, 16004.<BR> 10. Ātm. To favour, Pañc. i. d. 41.<BR> 11. To practise, Man. 4, 204.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भक्त,<BR> 1. Attached, devoted, Hit. ii. d. 74; believing; तद्-, believing in him, Rāmatap. Up. 1, 94.<BR> 2. Served.<BR> 3. Dressed, cooked. m. A follower, a votary; cf. also s. v. भक्त.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus., with दिशस्, To put one to flight, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 80.<BR> --† i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To give.<BR> 2. To dress, or cook.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, To exclude, Man. 9, 207.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To return to (acc.), Daśak. in Chr. 193, 5 (anomal. भजिष्यति).<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To distribute, to divide, Man. 9, 164.<BR> 2. To put up severally, Vikr. d. 43.<BR> 3. To distinguish, Rām. 2, 67, 31. विभक्त, Attached, Śāk. d. 107; Vikr. d. 160.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To divide, MBh. 3, 16147. प्रविभक्त,<BR> 1. Formerly distributed, Śāk. d. 165.<BR> 2. Divided, Man. 8, 166.<BR> --With संवि सम् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a " target="_blank">Page0641-a + 42</a>] -वि,<BR> 1. To make one partake of something, Rājat. 5, 109.<BR> 2. To divide, Pañc. 217, 12. संविभक्त, Divided, parted.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be divided, MBh. 3, 12683.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. famulus, familia; Goth. anda-bahti, and bahtjan; also ϕώγω, ϕώγνυμι, and A.S. bacan; O.H.G. bachan (but see पच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्त
एक- + भक्त एक- + भक्त, adj. kept by one master, Man. 8, 363.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यभक्त|सूर्यभक्तः|सूर्य्यभक्त|सूर्य्यभक्तः
सूर्य- + भक्त सूर्य- + भक्त,<BR> I. adj. worshipping the sun.<BR> II. m. a flower, Pentapetes phoenicea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजन|भजनं
भजन भज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sharing.<BR> 2. Possession.<BR> 3. Service, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्ज्|भंज्
भञ्ज् भञ्ज्, ii. 7, भनज्, भञ्ज्, Par.<BR> 1. To split, Rām. 1, 67, 17.<BR> 2. To break, Pañc. i. d. 148; to destroy, MBh. 3, 10990.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भग्न.<BR> 1. Broken, Pañc. 36, 12; torn.<BR> 2. Defeated, Bhartṛ. 2, 85; Rājat. 5, 340.<BR> 3. Disheartened, Chr. 5, 23; Pañc. iv. d. 43.<BR> 4. Disappointed, Bhartṛ. 2, 82.<BR> 5. Extinct, Man. 8, 148.<BR> 6. Disregarded, humbled;<BR> --† i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To break down, MBh. 1, 7081.<BR> --With नि नि, To break, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 117.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, विनिर्भग्न, Broken down, MBh. 3, 12477.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To break down, MBh. 3, 11121. The original form has been probably भ्रञ्ज्.<BR> --Cf. Lat. frango; Goth. brikan; A.S. bracan, brecan; ῥαγή, ῥήγνυμι, ῥηγμίν.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जन|भंजन|भञ्जनं|भञ्जनः
भञ्जन भञ्ज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Breaking, destroying.<BR> 2. Afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्
† भट् भट्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To hive.<BR> 2. To nourish.<BR> 3. To speak.<BR> --Caus. of 1. 2. भाटय, of 3. भटय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट|भटः
भट भट (a form of भृत, based on भर्त), m.<BR> 1. A soldier.<BR> 2. An outcaste of a particular tribe.<BR> 3. A goblin.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारभट|चारभटः
चार- + भट चार- + भट, m. a soldier, Bhartṛ. 1, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभट
भू- + भट भू- + भट, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभट|महाभटः
महा- + भट महा- + भट, m. a great warrior, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 27. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b " target="_blank">Page0641-b + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्भट|वार्भटः
वार्- + भट वार्- + भट, m. an alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभट|सुभटः
सु- + भट सु- + भट, m. a warrior (cf. भट्ट), Pañc. iii. d. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभट|स्वभटः
स्व- + भट स्व- + भट, m. 1. one's own soldier, Hit. 104, 17. 2. a life-guardian(?), Hit. iii. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्ट|भट्टः
भट्ट भट्ट (a dialectical form based on भर्ता, nom. sing. of भर्तृ), m.<BR> 1. A philosopher, a learned man, Rājat. 5, 66.<BR> 2. An enemy.<BR> 3. Authority.<BR> 4. Best.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभट्ट|सुभट्टः
सु- + भट्ट सु- + भट्ट, m.a very learned man, or perhaps rather a distinguished warrior, Lass. 29, 1 (in the latter case read सुभट, see भट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टार|भट्टारः
भट्टार भट्टार (probably a dialectical form sprung from भर्तृ, and based on भर्तारम्, etc.), adj. Venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारक|भट्टारकः
भट्टारक भट्टार + क,<BR> I. adj., f. रिका, Venerable, Lass. 13, 18.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Sir, Mālav. 28, 4.<BR> 2. The sun(?), Hit. 48, 3, M.M.<BR> III. f. रिका, Lady, tutelar deity, Lass. 31, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भडिल|भडिलः
भडिल भडिल, m.<BR> 1. An attendant.<BR> 2. A hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्
भण् भण् (a dialectical form based on भाष् + णा, i. e. भाष् ii. 9), i. 1, Par. To speak, Lass. 21, 3. भणित, Spoken, Pañc. 128, 5; sounded.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 38. प्रतिभणित, Answered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ट्
† भण्ट् भण्ट्, i. 10, Par. To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ड्|भंड्
† भण्ड् भण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To upbraid; to reprove.<BR> 2. To jest.<BR> 3. To deride.<BR> 4. To speak.<BR> --i. 10 or 1, Par. To be, and to make fortunate; to do an auspicious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डन|भंडन|भंडनं|भण्डनं
भण्डन भण्डन, n.<BR> 1. Armour.<BR> 2. Battle.<BR> 3. Evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डि|भंडि|भंडिः|भण्डिः
भण्डि and भण्डी भण्डी̆, f.<BR> 1. A wave.<BR> 2. A plant, Rubia manjith Roxb.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभण्डी
त्रि-भण्डी त्रि-भण्डी̆, f. a plant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a " target="_blank">Page0642-a + 44</a>] Convolvulus turpethum, Suśr. 1, 161, 21; 2, 70, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभण्डि
त्रि-भण्डि त्रि-भण्डी̆, f. a plant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a " target="_blank">Page0642-a + 44</a>] Convolvulus turpethum, Suśr. 1, 161, 21; 2, 70, 1.<BR>त्रि-भण्डी त्रि-भण्डी̆, f. a plant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a " target="_blank">Page0642-a + 44</a>] Convolvulus turpethum, Suśr. 1, 161, 21; 2, 70, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिल|भंडिल|भण्डिलः
भण्डिल भण्डिल (probably a dialectical form, akin to भद्र),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fortunate.<BR> 2. A messenger.<BR> II. m. A tree, Mimosa sirisha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदन्त|भदंत|भदंतः|भदन्तः
भदन्त भदन्त, m. A Bauddha mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदाक|भदाकः
भदाक भदाक (cf. भन्द्), adj. Auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्र|भद्रं|भद्रः
भद्र भद् + र (cf. भन्द्),<BR> I. adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Excellent, best, Vikr. 27, 10; Pañc. 146, 17.<BR> 2. Worthy, dear, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 11.<BR> 3. Pious.<BR> 4. Happy, Vikr. d. 163; propitious, Hit. 22, 5, M.M.<BR> 5. Comparat. भद्रतर, Better, Hit. 80, 5.<BR> II. भद्र + म्, adv. Well, happy.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Prosperity, Pañc. iii. d. 191; hail. Hit. 83, 10, M.M.<BR> 2. Happiness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212.<BR> 3. (with the dat. of the second person), A polite address, especially accompanying an advice, an objection, or expression of a different opinion; if you please, Rām. 3, 53, 2; Chr. 12, 3; 10, 5; with all respect for you, Chr. 11, 13; I beg your pardon, Rām. 3, 52, 37.<BR> 4. Gold.<BR> 5. Iron or steel.<BR> 6. A fragrant grass, Cyperus, Ṛt. 1, 17 v. r.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. A wagtail.<BR> 3. A bull.<BR> 4. A heap.<BR> 5. A fortune-teller, an impostor, Man. 9, 258.<BR> V. f. रा.<BR> 1. The Ganges of heaven.<BR> 2. A name of the second, seventh, and twelfth days of the lunar fortnight.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. bats, bat + izo, bat + ista; A.S. bet; O.H.G. baz; Goth. ga-bat + non, bot + a, bot + jan; A.S. bót; Lat. fastus (for fad-tus), fastigium, fastidium, festivus (but festus belongs rather to भाष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभद्र
अ- + भद्र अ- + भद्र, adj. distressed, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भद्र|चतुर्भद्रं
चतुर्- + भद्र चतुर्- + भद्र, n. sing. four good things, Hit. i. d. 158, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गभद्र|तुंगभद्र|तुङ्गभद्रः
तुङ्ग- + भद्र तुङ्ग- + भद्र, 1. m. an elephant in rut. 2. f. रा, a river in Mysore, Bhāg. P. 5, 19, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्र|बलभद्रः
बल- + भद्र बल- + भद्र,<BR> I. m. 1. Baladeva. 2. Ananta, the great serpent. 3. a strong man.<BR> II. f. रा, a young girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभद्र|मणिभद्रः
मणि- + भद्र मणि- + भद्र, m. a name of Kuvera, Nal. 12, 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोभद्र|सर्वतोभद्रः|सर्व्वतोभद्र|सर्व्वतोभद्रं|सर्व्वतोभद्रः
सर्वतोभद्र सर्वतोभ्˚, i. e. सर्वतस्-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b " target="_blank">Page0642-b + 44</a>]<BR> I. adj. everywhere auspicious.<BR> II. m. and n. a temple or palace of a square form, with an entrance opposite to each point of the compass.<BR> III. m. 1. the carriage of Viṣṇu. 2. a form of military array. 3. a bambu. 4. the Nimb tree.<BR> IV. f. द्रा. 1. an actress. 2. the name of two plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्र|रामभद्रः
राम- + भद्र राम- + भद्र, m. (auspicious Rāma), a surname of Rāma, Utt. Rāmac. 38, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्र|सुभद्रः
सु- + भद्र सु- + भद्र,<BR> I. adj. propitious, fortunate, Ṛt. 1, 17 v. r.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu.<BR> III. f. रा, The sister of जगन्नाथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रक|भद्रकं|भद्रकः
भद्रक भद्र + क, adj., f. रिका.<BR> 1. Beautiful, agreeable.<BR> 2. Respectable, worthy, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 1.<BR> 3. Good, Man. 9, 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रंकर|भद्रङ्कर|भद्रङ्करः
भद्रंकर भद्रंकर, i. e. भद्र + म्-कर, adj., f. री, Propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्द्|भंद्
† भन्द् भन्द्, 1. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To be fortunate.<BR> 2. To make fortunate.<BR> 3. To worship.<BR> 4. To be excellent.<BR> 5. To be glad.<BR> 6. To exhilarate.<BR> 7. To shine.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To make fortunate; cf. भद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भय|भयं|भयः
भय भय, i. e. भी + अ, n.<BR> 1. Fear, Pañc. v. d. 67.<BR> 2. Fright, Pañc. 242, 21.<BR> 3. Danger, Pañc. ii. d. 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभय|अभयं|अभयः
अ- + भय अ- + भय,<BR> I. n. 1. safety, Hit. i. d. 104, M.M. 2. protection from danger, Man. 4, 247. 3. the name of a Dvīpa, or division of the world. 4. a fragrant grass, Andropogon muricatum.<BR> II. adj., f. या, fearless, Bhartṛ. 3, 32.<BR> III. m. 1. epithet of Śiva. 2. a proper name.<BR> IV. f. या, a plant, Terminalia citrina, Suśr. 1, 139, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुतोभय|अकुतोभयः
अकुतोभय अकुतोभय, i. e. अ-कुतस्-, adj. having nothing to fear from any part, Pañc. 107, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातभय
अ-जात- + भय अ-जात- + भय, adj. fearless, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a " target="_blank">Page0643-a + 44</a>] Pañc. i. d. 352.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभय
अप- + भय अप- + भय, adj. fearless, Ragh. 3, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भय|निर्भयः
निर्भय निर्भ्˚, i. e. निस्-,<BR> I. adj., f. या. 1. fearless, Pañc. 111, 25. 2. free from danger, Man. 9, 255.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गभय
भङ्ग- + भय भङ्ग- + भय, Pañc. i. d. 357 (भङ्गभयाद् दिवः, from fear that (else) heaven would break down).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतभय|वीतभयः
वीत- + भय वीत- + भय, i. e. वि-इत-, adj. fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभय
स- + भय स- + भय, adj. fearful, Pañc. 45, 8. ˚यम्, adv. with fear, Hit. 85, 3, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयंकर|भयङ्कर|भयङ्करं|भयंकरः
भयंकर भयंकर, i. e. भय + म्-कर, adj., f. री, Terrific, Hit. i. d. 88, M.M.; formidable, Pañc. iii. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद
भयद भय-द (vb. दा), adj. Terrific, Pañc. i. d. 350.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानक|भयानकः
भयानक भयानक, properly an old anomal. ptcple. pres. Ātm. of भी, viz. भयान + क,<BR> I. adj. Frightful, formidable, Bhag. 11, 27; Utt. Rāmac. 43, 12.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sentiment of terror, as excited by poetical composition.<BR> 2. A tiger.<BR> 3. Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर|भरः
भर भर, i. e. भृ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A load, Lass. 88, 2; Vikr. d. 42; 52; with भुवस्, ἄχθος ἀρούρας i. e. a dead mass.<BR> 2. With कृ, To make a load, to support one's self, Hit. 47, 3.<BR> 3. Plenty, Śiś. 9, 47.<BR> 4. Much, excessive, Bhartṛ. 2, 68.<BR> 5. A measure of value of two thousand Palas.<BR> II. adj. Who or what supports.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. -fer; A.S. -bora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभर|अतिभरः
अति- + भर अति- + भर, m. excessive heaviness, Śiś. 9, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृतभर
अप-हृत- + भर अप-हृत- + भर, adj., unburthened, Vikr. d. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भर
दुर्भर दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. रा, 1. difficult to be borne, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 8. 2. difficult to be maintained, Pañc. iii. d. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर|निर्भरं|निर्भरः
निर्भर निर्भ्˚, i. e. निस्-,<BR> I. adj., f. रा. 1. excessive, violent, ardent, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396. 2. deep (as sleep), Hit. 85, 8. 3. latter part of comp. adj. full of, Pañc. 259, 3; Kathās. 6, 126.<BR> II. ˚रम्, adv. much, excessively, Hit. 86, 8; 10; Hit. 50, 2 (deeply).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभर
सु- + भर सु- + भर, adj. 1. heavily burthened. 2. heavy, Chr. 296, 2 = Rigv. i. 112, 2 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b " target="_blank">Page0643-b + 39</a>]. 3. f. रा, perhaps a proper name, Chr. 297, 20 = Rigv. i. 112, 20 (Sch. nourishing, viz. food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरट|भरटः
भरट भरट, m. A potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण|भरणं|भरणः
भरण भरण, i. e. भृ + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Bearing, Pañc. 257, 23; supporting, Śāk. d. 192.<BR> 2. Nourishing, Hit. ii. d. 42.<BR> 3. Wages, hire.<BR> II. f. णी.<BR> 1. The name of the second lunar asterism.<BR> 2. A creeper, commonly Ghoshā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः|भरण्डः
भरण्ड भरण्ड (vb. भ्रि). m. A master, a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्य|भरण्यं
भरण्य भरण्य (for भरणीय, ptcple. of the fut. pass. of भृ), n. Wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत|भरतः
भरत भरत, i. e. भरन्त्, ptcple. pres. of भृ, + अ (cf. Śāk. d. 192), m.<BR> 1. The name of several princes, and of a sage, the inventor of dramatic composition, Vikr. d. 36; Utt. Rāmac. 111, 4.<BR> 2. pl. The descendants of Bharata, Chr. 3, 1.<BR> 3. An actor, a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरथ|भरथः
भरथ भरथ, m. A deity presiding over one of the regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाज|भरद्वाजः
भरद्वाज भरद्वाज, i. e. भरन्त्, ptcple. pres. of भृ, -वाज, m. The name of a Muni, Johns. Sel. 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
भरित भरित, i. e. भर + इत, adj. Filled, MBh. 2, 2061.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिमन्
भरिमन् or भरीमन् भरी̆मन् (vb. भृ, or भर, + इमन्), m. A household, a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरु|भरुः
भरु भरु, i. e. भृ + उ, m.<BR> 1. Gold.<BR> 2. A lord.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुज|भरुजः
भरुज भरु-ज, m. A small sort of jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुटक|भरुटकं
भरुटक भरुटक (vb. भृ), n. Fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग|भर्गः
भर्ग भर्ग, i. e. भ्राज्, or भृज्, + अ, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गस्
भर्गस् भर्गस्, i. e. भ्राज्, or भृज्, + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Light, Lass. 99, 11 = Rigv. iii. 62, 10.<BR> 2. A name of Brahman.<BR> --Cf. A.S. baelch, superbia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृ|भर्त्तृ
भर्तृ भर्तृ, i. e. भृ + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. One who contains, Śiś. 9, 17.<BR> 2. A cherisher, Bhag. 9, 18.<BR> 3. A protector.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A lord, Vikr. d. 36; master, d. 155.<BR> 2. A commander, Man. 7, 94.<BR> 3. A husband, Hit. i. d. 196, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याभर्तृ|कन्याभर्त्तृ
कन्या- + भर्तृ कन्या- + भर्तृ, m. epithet of the god of war, MBh. 3, 14633.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणभर्तृ|गणभर्त्तृ
गण- + भर्तृ गण- + भर्तृ, m. epithet of Śiva, Kir. 5, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीभर्तृ
जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ, m. a king, Rām. 2, 103, 17; Rājat. 5, 69. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभर्तृ
जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ, m. a king, Rām. 2, 103, 17; Rājat. 5, 69. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभर्तृ|महीभर्त्तृ
जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ जगती-, भू-, मही- + भर्तृ, m. a king, Rām. 2, 103, 17; Rājat. 5, 69. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुभर्तृ
पशु- + भर्तृ पशु- + भर्तृ, m. epithet of Śiva, MBh. 13, 620.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिभर्तृ
रुचि- + भर्तृ रुचि- + भर्तृ, m. bearer of light and cherisher of love, Śiś. 9, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गभर्तृ|स्वर्गभर्त्तृ
स्वर्ग- + भर्तृ स्वर्ग- + भर्तृ, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृक
ऽभर्तृक -भर्तृ + क, latter part of comp. words, which are, or were originally adj.; e. g. प्रोषित- (ptcple. of the pf. pass. of प्र-वस्), f. का, A woman whose husband is absent, Ṛt. 6, 9. स-, f. का, A woman whose husband is alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृघ्नत्व
भर्तृघ्नत्व भर्तृ-घ्न + त्व, n. Injuring one's master, MBh. 2, 2123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृत्व
भर्तृत्व भर्तृ + त्व, n. Husbandship, Kathās. 26, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृमन्त्
भर्तृमन्त् भर्तृ + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Married, Śāk. d. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृहरि|भर्तृहरिः|भर्त्तृहरि|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्तृहरि भर्तृ-हरि, m. The name of a prince and poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स्
भर्त्स् भर्त्स्, i. 10, Ātm. (also Par.).<BR> 1. To menace, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 14.<BR> 2. To blame, to abuse, MBh. 4, 357.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भर्त्सित, Blamed, Pañc. i. d. 170. n. Menace, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 21.<BR> --With the prep. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b " target="_blank">Page0644-b + 38</a>] अभि अभि, To menace, Rām. 1, 28, 13. अभिभर्त्सित, Terrified, MBh. 3, 10921.<BR> --With अव अव, To deter, Chr. 26, 66 (read ˚भर्त्स्-अयत्).<BR> --With नि नि, To menace, Pañc. 220, 2 (probably corr. निर्भ्˚).<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To menace, Pañc. 84, 18; MBh. 1, 4190.<BR> 2. To blame, Utt. Rāmac. 174, 6; Chr. 60, 32.<BR> 3. To abuse, Hit. 64, 22.<BR> --With अभि-निस् अभि-निस्, To blame, Rām. 2, 78, 19.<BR> --With परि परि, To menace, MBh. 3, 16008.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To reproach, to blame, Rām. 2, 75, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सन|भर्त्सनं
भर्त्सन भर्त्स् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Threat.<BR> 2. Reproach, curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ब्
भर्ब् भर्ब्, भर्भ् भर्भ्, see भर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मन्|भर्म्मन्
भर्मन् भर्मन्, i. e. भृ + मन्, n.<BR> 1. Wages, hire.<BR> 2. Gold.<BR> 3. A coin, a piece of money.<BR> 4. The navel.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भभर्मन्|गर्भभर्म्मन्
गर्भ- + भर्मन् गर्भ- + भर्मन्, n. cherishing of a child, Ragh. 3, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्व्
भर्व् भर्व्, and † भर्भ् भर्भ्, or † भर्ब् भर्ब्, i. 1, Far.<BR> 1. To injure (ved.).<BR> 2. † To eat.<BR> --With the second signification and the form भर्ब् cf. ϕέρβω, ϕορβή; Lat. herba; with the first and भर्व् Goth. balvjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्
भल् भल्, and बल् बल्, † i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To describe.<BR> 2. To kill, to hurt.<BR> 3. To give.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. To describe, to see, to behold (ved.); with the prep. नि, Chānd. Up. 452; and Prākṛ. with निस्, Mālav. 5, 9.<BR> 2. † to throw up.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, To hear, Naiṣ. 6, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल्
† भल्ल् भल्ल्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To describe.<BR> 2. To kill.<BR> 3. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल भल्ल,<BR> I. m. A bear.<BR> II. m. and n. A kind of arrow, Chr. 29, 27.<BR> III. f. लि.<BR> 1. An arrow with a crescent-shaped head.<BR> 2. The marking nut plant, Semicarpus Anacardium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लक|भल्लकः
भल्लक भल्ल + क, भल्लुक and भल्लूक भल्लू̆क, m. A bear, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 1 (लू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातक|भल्लातकः
भल्लातक भल्ल्äतक (cf. भल्ल), m., and f. की, The marking nut plant, Lass. 52, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव भव, i. e. भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Being, existing, Sāv. 3, 10.<BR> 2. Birth, Śāk. d. 186; Megh. 46 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 3. Origin, Ragh. 3, 14 (at the end of a comp. adj. Arising; त्वद्-वियोग-, Arising from absence from thee, Vikr. d. 133).<BR> 4. The place or means of being.<BR> 5. Welfare.<BR> 6. Excellence, Pañc. v. d. 12.<BR> 7. The world, Hit. iii. d. 140.<BR> 8. A god.<BR> 9. Śiva, Kir. 5, 29; Rudra, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव|अभवः
अ- + भव अ- + भव, m. 1. nonexistence, Sāv. 3, 10. 2. cessation of existence, Rām. 3, 69, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यभव
अरण्य- + भव अरण्य- + भव, adj. growing in a forest, without culture, Pañc. ii. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभव
आत्मभव आत्मभव, i. e. आत्मन्-,<BR> I. m. the existence of one's self, Nal. 5, 37.<BR> II. adj. attracted by one's self, Rām. 2, 64, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभव|आदिभवः
आदि- + भव आदि- + भव, adj. who is the first being, Ragh. 13, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाग्भव
दुर्वाग्भव दुर्वाग्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-वाच्-, m. abusing, MBh. 13, 2258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भव|पुनर्भवः
पुनर्भव पुनर्भ्˚, i. e. पुनर्-, m. regeneration, MBh. 1, 251; transmigration, Śāk. d. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभव|मघाभवः
मघा- + भव मघा- + भव, m. the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय भवदीय, i. e. भवन्त् + ईय, adj. Thine, yours, Pañc. 135, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन|भवनं|भवनः
भवन भवन, i. e. भू + अन, n.<BR> 1. Nature.<BR> 2. A dwelling, house, Pañc. ii. d. 17; a palace, Pañc. iii. d. 236.<BR> 3. A temple, Rājat. 5, 100.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भभवन
गर्भ- + भवन गर्भ- + भवन, n. a sanctuary, Mālat. 13, 3 (below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभवन|देवभवनं
देव- + भवन देव- + भवन, n. a temple, Kathās. 6, 75. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b " target="_blank">Page0645-b + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीभवन
देवी- + भवन देवी- + भवन, n. a temple of Durgā, Kathās. 18, 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्त्|भवत्
भवन्त् भवन्त्, properly ptcple. pres. of भू, m., and f. अती, Lord, lady, used as respectful term of address instead of the second personal pronoun, Thou, You, Vikr. 9, 6; Pañc. 107, 8; but taking the verb in the third person, Pañc. 109, 1; pl., Vikr. 3, 9; f., 9, 6; pl., 5, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ϕώς, ϕωτός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रभवन्त्|अत्रभवत्
अत्र- + भवन्त् अत्र- + भवन्त्, adj., f. अति, respectable, Kir. 11, 18.<BR> II. m., f. अती, used to denote in a respectful manner third persons who are present, Śāk. 16, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रभवन्त्|तत्रभवत्
तत्र- + भवन्त् तत्र- + भवन्त्, m., f. अती, used to denote in a respectful manner persons who are absent, Śāk. 9, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्त|भवंत|भवंतः|भवन्तः
भवन्त भवन्त् + अ, m. Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृश्
भवादृश् भवादृश्, and भवादृश भवादृश, i. e. भरन्त्-दृश् or दृश् + अ, adj. Like you, your like, Pañc. ii. d. 185; Hit. iii. d. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानी
भवानी भवानी, i. e. भव + ई, f. The wife of Śiva, Kir. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्यता
भवितव्यता भवितव्य + ता (vb. भू), f.<BR> 1. Necessity of coming into existence, of taking place, Pañc. ii. d. 11; 133.<BR> 2. Fate, Vikr. 36, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितृ
भवितृ भवितृ, i. e. भू + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Actually being.<BR> 2. Being about to become.<BR> 3. Wellbeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविल|भविलः
भविल भविल, i. e. भू + इल, adj. Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्य|भविष्यः
भविष्य भविष्य, curtailed भविष्यन्त्, ptcple. fut. of भू, adj., f. या, Future, Pañc. i. d. 103.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्भविष्य
यद्- + भविष्य यद्- + भविष्य, m. a proper name, Pañc. 77, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष्
भष् भष्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 2, 1425).<BR> 1. To bark, MBh. 1, 5249.<BR> 2. To bark at, to reproach malevolently, to rail, 3, 15641; cf. भाष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष|भषः
भष भष् + अ, m. A dog. f. षी, A bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषक|भषकः
भषक भष + क, m. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्
भस् भस्, ii. 3, Par.<BR> 1. To eat.<BR> 2. To shine.<BR> 3. † To blame. भसित, see s. v.; cf. प्सा and भा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद्
भसद् भसद्, f.<BR> 1. Pudendum muliebre.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. A month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन्त|भसंत|भसंतः|भसन्तः
भसन्त भसन्त, m. Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसित|भसितं
भसित भसित, n. Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रका
भस्त्रका भस्त्रका, see भस्त्राका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रा
भस्त्रा भस्त्रा, f.<BR> 1. A bellows, Pañc. iii. d. 97.<BR> 2. A bag, Pañc. 265, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्राका
भस्त्राका भस्त्राका, भस्त्रका भस्त्रका, भस्त्रिका भस्त्रिका, i. e. भस्त्रा + क or इक, f.<BR> 1. A bellows.<BR> 2. भस्त्रिका, A bag, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 2 (चर्म-रत्न-, a most wonderful leather bag).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मक|भस्मकं
भस्मक भस्मक, n.<BR> 1. A disease of the eyes, indistinctness of vision.<BR> 2. (i. e. भस् + मन् + क), Morbid appetite with general decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मन्
भस्मन् भस्मन् (cf. भसित), n. Ashes, Hit. ii. d. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मसात्
भस्मसात् भस्मसात्, i. e. भस्मन् + सात्, adv. Completely into ashes; with नी and कृ, To reduce to ashes, Pañc. 38, 18; 186, 14; Utt. Rāmac. 74, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मी
भस्मी भस्मी, see कृ and भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
1. भा भा, ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To shine, Kir. 5, 20.<BR> 2. To appear, Rājat. 5, 94.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भात, Bright. n. Morning.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To shine from every part, Ghaṭ. 10. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b " target="_blank">Page0646-b + 41</a>]<BR> --With अव अव, To shine, MBh. 3, 10094.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To shine forth, Chr. 288, 9 = Rigv. i. 48, 9.<BR> 2. To illuminate, Chr. 289, 4 = Rigv. i. 50, 4.<BR> 3. To shine, Rām. i. 15, 19.<BR> 4. To appear, Vikr. d. 142; MBh. 3, 13701.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To shine forth, Man. 1, 7.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To shine forth, Man. 5, 44.<BR> 2. To proceed, Man. 2, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To begin to shine, Rām. 1, 45, 5.<BR> 2. To shine forth, MBh. 3, 10054. प्रभात, Begun to become clear, Rām. 2, 6, 10. n. Daybreak, morning, Pañc. 246, 16; loc. ते, tomorrow, 119, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To appear, MBh. 3, 10055.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To shine, Ghaṭ. 15.<BR> 2. To appear, Vikr. d. 23; Chr. 41, 23.<BR> 3. To please, Pañc. 78, 12; 151, 1; Vikr. 43, 17 (with acc.)<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To appear, MBh. 1, 8095.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To shine, Vikr. d. 44; Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6.<BR> 2. To appear, Lass. 75, 2. विभात, Become manifest, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 5. n. Daybreak.<BR> --Cf. ϕῶς, ϕωτός, ϕανός, ϕαλός, ἐμϕατικός, ἀμϕαδόν; probably, ϕοῖβος (for ϕοβ + ιος, from the Caus. भापय), ϕάος (for ϕαϝος), ϕαέθω, ϕαίνω (for ϕαϝέσνω), ϕαίδιμος, etc.; Lat. focus, februus (from the Causal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्प्रभात
तत्प्रभात तत्प्र्˚, i. e. तद्-, loc. the following morning, Lass. 12, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभात|सुप्रभातं
सु- + प्रभात सु- + भा, adj. enlightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
2. भा भा,<BR> I. f.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. Splendour.<BR> II. m. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग|भागः
भाग भाग, i. e. भज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A portion, part, Pañc. i. d. 447; side, Vikr. d. 26; Utt. Rāmac. 42, 12.<BR> 2. Fortune, fate, Utt. Rāmac. 38, 9.<BR> 3. A division of time, the 30th part [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a " target="_blank">Page0647-a + 45</a>] of a zodiacal sign.<BR> 4. A degree, the 360th part of the circumference of a great circle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग
अ- + भाग अ- + भाग, adj. deprived of one's share, Man. 9, 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभाग|अग्रभागः
अग्र- + भाग अग्र- + भाग, m. fore or top part, Śāk. 141, 10 Chezy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभाग|अधोभागः
अधोभाग अधोभ्˚, i. e. अधस्-, m. 1. the lower part, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 18; Pañc. 76, 23 (under). 2. the lower part of the body, Suśr. 1, 208, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभाग|अर्धभागः
अर्ध- + भाग अर्ध- + भाग, m. 1. half, Kumāras. 5, 50. 2. a part, Ragh. 7, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिभाग|अशीतिभागः
अशीति- + भाग अशीति- + भाग, m. an 80th part, Man. 8, 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भाग|चतुर्भागः
चतुर्- + भाग चतुर्- + भाग, m. a 4th part, Man. 8, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभाग|त्रिभागः
त्रि- + भाग त्रि- + भाग, m. a 3rd part, Hariv. 8887.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायभाग|दायभागः
दाय- + भाग दाय- + भाग, m. partition of heritage, Man. 9, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्भाग|दिग्भागः
दिग्भाग दिग्भ्˚, i. e. दिश्-, m. region, quarter, Pañc. 106, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नभाग
निम्न- + भाग निम्न- + भाग, m. a deep place, Rām. 2, 80, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग|परभागः
पर- + भाग पर- + भाग, m. 1. supremacy, Pañc. i. d. 375. 2. highest degree, Kathās. 1, 47 (cf. दिव्य-मानुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादभाग|पादभागः
पाद- + भाग पाद- + भाग, f. a fourth part, MBh. 2, 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभाग|पुरोभागः
पुरोभाग पुरोभाग, i. e. पुरस्-,<BR> I. m. 1. obtrusiveness, Hariv. 7338. 2. envy, Mālav. d. 19.<BR> II. adj., f. गा, obtrusive, Śāk. 70, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाग
महा- + भाग महा- + भाग, adj. 1. eminent. 2. virtuous in a high degree, Chr. 9, 41; 24, 47; Utt. Rāmac. 38, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभाग|यज्ञभागः
यज्ञ- + भाग यज्ञ- + भाग, m. a deity, Śāk. d. 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभाग|शेषभागः
शेष- + भाग शेष- + भाग, m. the remaining or last part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भाग|षड्भागः
षड्भाग षड्भाग, i. e. षष्-, m. a sixth part, Pañc. i. d. 391.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागधेय|भागधेयं|भागधेयः
भागधेय भाग-धेय (vb. धा),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A heir.<BR> 2. Royal revenue.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Portion, Man. 3, 245.<BR> 2. Fate, fortune, happiness, Vikr. 55, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागशस्
भागशस् भाग + शस्, adv. Part for part, MBh. 2, 211; Man. 12, 22 (Jones: In the order of their natural distribution.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिन्
भागिन् भागिन्, i. e. भज् and भाग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Who or what shares.<BR> 2. One who partakes, Man. 3, 143; Pañc. 16, 2.<BR> 3. Undergoing, suffering, Pañc. 29, 9; 68, 23.<BR> 4. An [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b " target="_blank">Page0647-b + 42</a>] owner, Man. 9, 48.<BR> 5. Consisting of parts.<BR> II. m. A co-heir.<BR> III. f. नी, Co-heiress.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखभागिन्
दुःख- + भागिन् दुःख- + भागिन्, adj. suffering pain, Hit. i. d. 24, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभागिन्
धर्म- + भागिन् धर्म- + भागिन्, adj., f. नी, virtuous, Hit. iii. d. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभागिन्
पुरोभागिन् पुरोभागिन्, i. e. पुरस्- (cf. पुरोभाग under भाग), adj., f. गिणी, 1. obtrusive, Śāk. 70, 14 v. r. 2. envious, censorious, Rājat. 6, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दभागिन्
मन्द- + भागिन् मन्द- + भागिन्, adj. unhappy, Utt. Rāmac. 79, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिनेय|भागिनेयः
भागिनेय भागिनेय, i. e. भगिनी + एय,<BR> I. m. A sister's son, Pañc. 231, 20.<BR> II. यी, A sister's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीरथी
भागीरथी भागीरथी, i. e. भगिरथ + अ + ई, f. The Ganges. Hit. 3, 3, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्य|भाग्यं
भाग्य भाग्य, i. e. भाग + य, n.<BR> 1. Merit and demerit acquired in former existences, fate, fortune, Vikr. 63, 19.<BR> 2. Merit, Bhartṛ. 2, 94.<BR> 3. Happiness, Hit. pr. d. 5, M.M.<BR> 4. instr. येन, Happily, Hit. 17, 4, M.M.<BR> 5. Sensual pleasure, Rājat. 5, 385.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग्य
अ- + भाग्य अ- + भाग्य, adj. unfortunate, Pañc. 197, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग्य
पर- + भाग्य पर- + भाग्य n. another's property, Hit. i. d. 24, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दभाग्य|मंदभाग्य
मन्द- + भाग्य मन्द- + भाग्य, adj. unhappy, Vikr. 32, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाग्य
महा- + भाग्य महा- + भाग्य, n. great luck, happiness, Sāv. 1, 1; Man. 11, 244 (Jones: Transcendent excellence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्यवन्त्|भाग्यवत्
भाग्यवन्त् भाग्य + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Abounding in merits.<BR> 2. Happy, Pañc. 201, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गासुरि
भाङ्गासुरि भाङ्गासुरि, m. A proper name, Nal. 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गीन|भांगीन|भांगीनं|भाङ्गीनं
भाङ्गीन भाङ्गीन, i. e. भङ्गा + ईन, n. A field of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
† 1. भाज् भाज्, i. 10, Par. To divide; cf. भज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
2. ऽभाज् -भाज्, (vb. भज्), latter part of comp. adj. One who possesses or obtains; e. g. अर्ध- adj. Obtaining or entitled to a half, Man. 8, 239. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a " target="_blank">Page0648-a + 43</a>] नृप-मान-, Obtaining royal honour, Man. 2, 139. विभाग-, m. Entitled to a portion of a property already distributed, as a son born after the distribution of his father's property. वियोग-, adj. Suffering separation, cf. also Pañc. i. d. 196; 147, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजन|भाजनं
भाजन भाजन, भज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Any vessel, as a pot or cup, Hit. pr. d. 8, M.M.; figuratively, Pañc. ii. d. 194 (a vessel of love and confidence, a person on whom one may depend).<BR> 2. A fit person.<BR> 3. Sharing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपभाजन
दीप- + भाजन दीप- + भाजन n. a lamp, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजनत्व
भाजनत्व भाजन + त्व, n. Condition of being a vessel, i. e. a fit object, Mālav. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटक|भाटकं|भाटकः
भाटक भाटक, i. e. probably भट + क, m. Price, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाट्ट|भाट्टः
भाट्ट भाट्ट, i. e. भट्ट + अ, m. A follower of Kumārila Bhaṭṭa, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्ड|भांड|भांडं|भाण्डं|भाण्डः
भाण्ड भाण्ड, n.<BR> 1. Any vessel, a pot, a cup, Pañc. 96, 18; Hit. 85, 14.<BR> 2. Any implement or utensil, Sāv. 3, 1.<BR> 3. The capital, principal of a merchant.<BR> 4. Goods, wares, Pañc. 7, 17 (देश-अन्तर-भाण्ड-आनयन, n. Exporting wares to foreign countries), i. d. 19.<BR> 5. An ornament, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 2.<BR> 6. Any musical instrument, Man. 10, 49.<BR> 7. The bed of a river.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरभाण्ड|क्षुरभांड|क्षुरभाण्डं
क्षुर- + भाण्ड क्षुर- + भाण्ड, n. a razorcase, Hit. 64, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभाण्ड
भिन्न- + भाण्ड भिन्न- + भाण्ड (vb. भिद्), n. 1. a potsherd. 2. a broken vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाण्ड
महा- + भाण्ड महा- + भाण्ड, n. a great vessel, Pañc. 62, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभाण्ड|सारभाण्डं
सार- + भाण्ड सार- + भाण्ड, n. 1. a natural vessel, as the bag or skin in which musk is sold. 2. a bale of goods, Pañc. 8, 14. 3. implements, Mālav. 44, 1 (Prākṛ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डायन
भाण्डायन भाण्डायन, n. A proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 91, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिक|भांडिक|भांडिकः|भाण्डिकः
भाण्डिक भाण्डिक, i. e. भाण्ड + इक, m. A musician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिल|भांडिल|भांडिलः|भाण्डिलः
भाण्डिल भाण्डिल, i. e. भाण्ड + इल, m. A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भातु|भातुः
भातु भा + तु, m. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्र|भाद्रः
भाद्र भाद्र, i. e. भद्र + अ, m. The name of a month, August--September.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमातुर|भाद्रमातुरः
भाद्रमातुर भाद्रमातुर, i. e. भद्र-मातृ + अ, m. The son of a virtuous wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान|भानं
भान भान, i. e. भा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Appearance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 3.<BR> 2. Perception, Bhāṣāp. 65.<BR> --Cf. ϕανός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानतस्
भानतस् भान + तस्, adv. In consequence of the appearance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानवन्त्|भानवत्
भानवन्त् भान + वन्त्, adj. Endowed with the appearance, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानु|भानुः
भानु भा + नु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A ray of light, Chr. 288, 9 = Rigv. i. 48, 9.<BR> 2. Light.<BR> 3. The sun, Pañc. 134, 17.<BR> 4. A sovereign, a master.<BR> II. f. A handsome woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रभानु|चित्रभानुः
चित्र- + भानु चित्र- + भानु,<BR> I. adj. resplendent, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7.<BR> II. m. fire, MBh. 1, 2036.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्भानु|वृहद्भानुः
वृहद्-भानु वृहद्-भानु, i. e. वृहन्त्-, m. a name of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानु|स्वर्भानुः
स्वर्- + भानु स्वर्- + भानु, m. Rāhu, the ascending node, Chr. 36, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुमन्त्|भानुमत्
भानुमन्त् भानु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Luminous, splendid.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Draup. 7, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम्
भाम् भाम् (rather a denomin. derived from भाम), i. 1, Ātm., and i. 10, Par. To be angry or wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
भाम भा + म,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. Passion, wrath.<BR> 4. A sister's husband.<BR> II. f. मा. A passionate [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a " target="_blank">Page0649-a + 42</a>] woman.<BR> --Cf. probably A.S. beam, a sun-beam, beamian, to shine (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
भामिन् भामिन्, i. e. भाम + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Passionate, Ragh. 8, 28.<BR> II. f. नी, A passionate woman, often used, as a term of endearment, in the same sense as मानिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार|भारः
भार भार, i. e. भृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Carrying burthens, Pañc. i. d. 312.<BR> 2. Weight, a burthen, Pañc. 52, 4; figurat., Pañc. 31, 3 (of government); v. d. 4.<BR> 3. A great weight, Pañc. 99, 25.<BR> 4. A weight of gold equal to two thousand Palas.<BR> 5. A yoke.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभार|अतिभारः
अति- + भार अति- + भार, m. 1. a too great burthen, Pañc. i. d. 22. 2. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठभार|काष्ठभारः
काष्ठ- + भार काष्ठ- + भार, m. a load of wood, Hariv. 4356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भभार
गर्भ- + भार गर्भ- + भार, m. the burthen of being with child, Kathās. 26, 216. अर्ह-, m. 1. the circumference of a peacock's tail, Megh. 102. 2. the tuft of a peacock's feathers at the shaft of a lance or the handle of a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारक|भारकः
भारक भार + क, m. A load, Man. 11, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारण्ड|भारंड|भारंडः|भारण्डः
भारण्ड भारण्ड, भारुण्ड भारुण्ड, भेरण्ड भेरण्ड (m.), The name of a fabulous bird, see Pañc. 263, 19; cf. my translation, 535, n. 1437. f. दी, Its female, Pañc. 264, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत भारत, i. e. भरत + अ,<BR> I. patronym. A descendant of Bharata, Hit. iv. d. 86.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An actor.<BR> 2. A name of fire.<BR> III. f. ती.<BR> 1. Speech, Chr. 53, 1.<BR> 2. Dramatic recitation.<BR> 3. The goddess of speech, Pañc. ii. d. 16.<BR> 4. A quail.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. India proper.<BR> 2. A great epic poem, also महाभारत महा-, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाज|भारद्वाजं|भारद्वाजः
भारद्वाज भारद्वाज, i. e. भरद्वाज + अ,<BR> I. patronym., m.<BR> 1. Epithet of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b " target="_blank">Page0649-b + 39</a>] Droṇa.<BR> 2. One of the seven Ṛṣis.<BR> 3. Agastya.<BR> 4. The son of Vṛhaspati.<BR> II. m. A skylark, Pañc. 157, 3, Wild cotton.<BR> IV. n. A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारव|भारवं
भारव भारव, n. A bowstring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवि|भारविः
भारवि भारवि, m. The name of a poet, Chr. 170, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारि|भारिः
भारि भारि, m. A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक भारिक, i. e. भार + इक, m. A porter, Rājat. 5, 204 (treasurer; cf. 176 and my Chr. p. 315, n. ad 176. I propose to read भौरिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिन्
भारिन् भारिन्, i. e. भार + इन्, m. A porter, Man. 2, 138; Kathās. 22, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारुण्ड
भारुण्ड भारुण्ड, see भारण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गव|भार्गवः
भार्गव भार्गव, i. e. भृगु + अ, patronym.<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A descendant of Bhṛgu.<BR> 2. Epithet of Paraśurāma, Johns. Sel. 4, 22; Utt. Rāmac. 13, 10.<BR> 3. A name of Śukra, regent of Venus.<BR> 4. An archer.<BR> 5. An elephant.<BR> 6. A proper name, Johns. Sel. 60, 189.<BR> II. f. वी.<BR> 1. Pārvatī.<BR> 2. Lakṣmī.<BR> 3. Bent grass, Panicum dactylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्या|भार्य्या
भार्या भार्या, properly ptcple. fut. pass. of भृ, f. A wife, Pañc. 137, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभार्या
कु- + भार्या कु- + भार्या,<BR> I. f. a wicked wife, Mārk. P. 21, 73.<BR> II. कु-भार्य, adj. having a wicked wife, Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभार्य
स-भार्य स-भार्य, adj. with (his) wife, Rām. 3, 55, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्याट|भार्य्याट|भार्य्याटः
भार्याट भार्याट, m. A man who lets out his wife for prostitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यात्व|भार्य्यात्व
भार्यात्व भार्या + त्व, f. State of a female, Man. 12, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल|भालं
भाल भाल, m.<BR> 1. The forehead, Bhartṛ. 2, 48.<BR> 2. i. e. भा + ल, Lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालु|भालुः
भालु भा + लु, m. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालूक|भालूकः
भालूक भालूक, m. A bear (cf. भल्लक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव|भावः
भाव भाव, i. e. भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. State, Hit. pr. d. 28, M.M.; Vikr. d. 115 (नदी-भावेन परिणत, changed into a river).<BR> 2. Property, Pañc. iv. d. 62; nature, Nal. 10, 15.<BR> 3. Meaning, Man. 2, 124.<BR> 4. Purpose, Man. 4, 234; intention, Vikr. d. 102 (Sch.).<BR> 5. Mind, Pañc. i. d. 317; heart, Rām. 3, 24, 11; Chr. 18, 35.<BR> 6. Emotion, passion, as an object of poetry, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 11; (of music? Pañc. v. d. 44); love, Vikr. d. 72; Lass. 58, 16 (read हुर्वन्त्या भाव˚).<BR> 7. Gesture.<BR> 8. Corporeal expression of amorous sentiments.<BR> 9. A being.<BR> 10. Substance, Bhāṣāp. 13; thing, object, Utt. Rāmac. 74, 9.<BR> 11. The world.<BR> 12. Superhuman power.<BR> 13. The Supreme Being, Man. 4, 234.<BR> 14. A learned man.<BR> 15. Venerable, master, Vikr. 3, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव|अभावः
अ- + भाव अ- + भाव, m. 1. absence, Man. 8, 259; Hit. i. d. 118, M.M. 2. nonexistence; अभाव + तस्, adv. in consequence of the non-existence, Bhāṣāp. 113. 3. death, Kathās. 18, 270. 4. destruction, Rām. 5, 27, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्यभाव
अ-बध्य- + भाव अ-बध्य- + भाव, adj. state of being inviolable, Hit. iii. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाराधेयभाव|आधाराधेयभावः
आधार-आ-धेय- + भाव आधार-आ-धेय- + भाव (vb. धा), m. state or relation of the receptacle and the object received, Hit. iii. d. 12 (instr. because it [viz. the mirror] can receive [reflect] only in proportion to its greatness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यभाव|आर्यभावः
आर्य- + भाव आर्य- + भाव, m. honest behaviour, Rām. 1, 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभाव|एकभावः
एक- + भाव एक- + भाव,<BR> I. m. 1. same state, Hit. ii. d. 151. 2. simplicity (opposite to duplicity), candour, Pañc. iii. d. 61.<BR> II. adj. unchanged, MBh. 13, 3677.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याभाव
कन्या- + भाव कन्या- + भाव, m. virginity, MBh. 1, 2405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतभाव
कृत- + भाव कृत- + भाव, adj. resolute, Rām. 6, 70, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभाव
तनु- + भाव तनु- + भाव, m. scantiness, Śāk. d. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासभाव|दासभावः
दास- + भाव दास- + भाव, m. slavery, Draup. 9, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नीतभाव
दुर्नीत- + भाव दुर्नीत- + भाव, i. e. दुस्-, m. foolish behaviour, Chr. 8, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरभाव
दूर- + भाव दूर- + भाव, m. distance, Megh. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहभाव|द्रोहभावः
द्रोह- + भाव द्रोह- + भाव, m. malignance, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b " target="_blank">Page0650-b + 44</a>] Man. 9, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वभाव|द्वंद्वभाव|द्वन्द्वभावः
द्वन्द्व- + भाव द्वन्द्व- + भाव, m. discord, Ṛt. 1, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भाव|पुनर्भावः
पुनर्- + भाव पुनर्- + भाव, m. regeneration, Prab. 108, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्भाव|पृथग्भावः
पृथग्भाव पृथग्भाव, i. e. पृथक्-, m. 1. separateness. 2. difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तभाव|प्राप्तभावः
प्राप्त- + भाव प्राप्त- + भाव, i. e. प्र-आप्त,<BR> I. adj. 1. of a good disposition. 2. wise. 3. handsome.<BR> II. m. a bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालभाव|बालभावः
बाल- + भाव बाल- + भाव, m. youth, Pañc. 182, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धभाव|वृद्धभावः
वृद्ध- + भाव वृद्ध- + भाव, m. old age, Pañc. 50, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भाव|सद्भावः
सद्भाव सद्भाव, i. e. सन्त्-, m. 1. the property of being, entity. 2. truth, Lass. 57, 7. 3. the property of goodness, kindness, Megh. 18, n. 4. honesty, Hit. iv. d. 103. 5. merit, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1880; a pure or holy disposition. 6. amiability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभाव|सर्वभावः|सर्व्वभाव
सर्व- + भाव सर्व- + भाव, m. one's whole being, Hit. ii. d. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुभाव|साधुभावः
साधु- + भाव साधु- + भाव, m. goodness, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाव|स्वभावः
स्व- + भाव स्व- + भाव, m. 1. nature, natural disposition, Rām. 3, 51, 33; Hit. i. d. 19, M.M. 2. purpose, Johns. Sel. 46, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वभाव|स्त्रीस्वभावः
स्त्री-स्व- + भाव स्त्री-स्व- + भाव, m. 1. female nature. 2. an eunuch, attendant on women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिभाव|स्थायिभावः
स्थायिभाव स्थायिघ्˚, i. e. स्थायिन्-, m. 1. fixed condition. 2. A passion or feeling, as object of poetical description, viz. desire, mirth, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावज|भावजः
भावज भाव-ज, m. Love, Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावतस्
भावतस् भाव + तस्, in ज्ञाति-, adv. By being a relation, Hit. ii. d. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत्क भावत्क, i. e. भवन्त् + क, adj., f. की, Thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावन|भावनं|भावनः
भावन भावन, i. e. भू, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A creator, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 11.<BR> 2. A founder.<BR> II. n., and f. ना.<BR> 1. Causing to be.<BR> 2. Mental perception, Bhāṣāp. 31; Pañc. v. d. 91 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2119; the success of an advice, etc., depends on the manner in which it is mentally received, faithfully believed, etc.).<BR> 3. Recollection, Utt. Rāmac. 25, 13.<BR> 4. Imagination, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 6.<BR> 5. Meditation, Bhag. 2, 66.<BR> 6. Observing.<BR> 7. Decorating with flowers, etc. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a " target="_blank">Page0651-a + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावन
न्यग्भावन न्यग्भावन, i. e. न्यञ्च्-, n. 1. contempt. 2. humbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषभावना
विशेष- + भावना विशेष- + भावना, f. reflecting on, or perceiving, differences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्र|भावित्रं
भावित्र भावित्र (vb. भू), n. The universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन् भाविन्, adj. f. नी, i. e.<BR> I. भू + इन्, Future, Vikr. 87, 1; what will be, Daśak. in. Chr. 186, 24; what will fall at one's share, Pañc. iv. d. 73.<BR> II. भा + विन्.<BR> 1. Beautiful, Rām. 3, 53, 39.<BR> 2. f. नी, A distinguished woman, a wanton woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यभाविन्
अवश्यभाविन् अवश्यभ्˚, i. e. अवश्यम्-, adj. what will be inevitably, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाभाविन्
तथा- + भाविन् तथा- + भाविन्, adj. destined to become really, Śāk. 111, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भाविन्
पुनर्- + भाविन् पुनर्- + भाविन्, adj. possible to be undone, Chr. 22, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक भावुक, i. e. भू + उक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Actually being.<BR> 2. Happy.<BR> 3. Latter part of comp. adj. Becoming.<BR> II. m. A sister's husband.<BR> III. n. Happiness. See शुभंभ्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् भाष्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Chr. 27, 1).<BR> 1. To speak, Man. 8, 216.<BR> 2. To speak to (acc.), Rām. 2, 78, 19.<BR> 3. To address, MBh. 3, 2747.<BR> 4. To describe, Man. 4, 255. भाषित, n. Speech, Pañc. i. d. 356.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To speak distinctly, Man. 3, 30.<BR> 2. To confess, Man. 11, 228.<BR> --With अप अप, To revile, Kumāras. 5, 83.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To address, Man. 2, 128.<BR> 2. To speak to (with instr.), Man. 4, 57.<BR> 3. To declare loudly, Man. 11, 103.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To converse, MBh. 3, 12697.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To address, MBh. 1, 74. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b " target="_blank">Page0651-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. To speak, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396.<BR> 3. To exclaim, Dev. 2, 36.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To address, MBh. 3, 15169.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. दुःख-व्याभाषित, adj. Difficult to be pronounced, MBh. 13, 4485.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To address, MBh. 1, 4198.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To declare, Utt. Rāmac. 130, 5.<BR> 2. To persuade, MBh. 1, 4287.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To speak, Rām. 3, 51, 25.<BR> 2. To address, MBh. 3, 2599. प्रभाषित, n. Speech, Nal. 8, 11.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To speak, MBh. 5, 41.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To answer, MBh. 3, 2524.<BR> 2. To address, Rām. 1, 8, 29; Pañc. 193, 13.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To converse, Chr. 56, 18; to converse with (instr.), Man. 8, 55.<BR> 2. To have sexual intercourse with, Hit. 64, 12 (with acc.).<BR> 3. To greet, Hit. 14, 20.<BR> 4. To speak. MBh. 1, 5190; to say, Hit. 57, 6 (read संभाषते. The sense is: It is true he is anxious, else he would not have said to me, etc.). भाष् is probably akin to भा.<BR> --Cf. Lat. fastus, nefastus, nefarius, festus, feriæ, hariolus, fas, nefas, fari; ϕημί, ϕάσις, ϕατός, ϕήμη, ϕωνή; akin are ϕθέγγομαι, ϕθέγμα (but cf. भञ्ज्, i. 10); A.S. bannan, abannan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाषित|सुभाषितः
सु- + भाषित सु- + भाषित,<BR> I. adj. 1. well spoken. 2. and n. well discoursing. Pañc. 31, 4, ii. d. 177.<BR> II. n. 1. eloquence. 2. a good advice(?), Man. 2, 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषण|भाषणं
भाषण भाषण, i. e. भाष् + अन, n. Speech, Lass. 8, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा भाष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Speech, Chr. 220, 1. 1.<BR> 2. Language, Pañc. i. d. 445.<BR> 3. Vernacular speech, Lass. 39, 11; MBh. 2, 2040.<BR> 4. Speech exposing the plaint in a law-suit, Lass. 90, 3; Pañc. 167, 6(?).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशभाषा
देश-भाषा देश-भाषा, f. the language of a country, MBh. 9, 2605.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
वि-भाषा वि-भाषा, indecl. alternatively, either of two ways, optionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिन्
भाषिन् भाष् + इन्, adj., f. षिणी, Speaking, Pañc. 184, 4; Rājat. 5, 61. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a " target="_blank">Page0652-a + 41</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भाषिन्
दुस्- + भाषिन् दुस्- + भाषिन्, adj. abusing, MBh. 5, 751.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वभाषिन्|पूर्व्वभाषिन्
पूर्व- + भाषिन् पूर्व- + भाषिन्, adj. speaking first, making advances, Rām. 2, 1, 7 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुभाषिन्
मृदु- + भाषिन् मृदु- + भाषिन्, adj. speaking sweetly, Vikr. d. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
1. भास् भास् (akin to भा, probably a denomin.), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 1, 4852).<BR> 1. To shine, MBh. 3, 12299.<BR> 2. To appear, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 4.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To illuminate, Bhagav. 15, 6.<BR> 2. To make evident, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 22.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To shine, Rām. 1, 35, 16.<BR> 2. To appear, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 12.<BR> --Caus. To illuminate, Śiś. 9, 37.<BR> --With आ आ, To shine, MBh. 2, 1313.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To beautify, Ragh. 7, 16.<BR> 2. To honour, Bhartṛ. 2, 49.<BR> --With नि नि, To seem likely.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To shine, MBh. 3, 17090.<BR> 2. To seem likely.<BR> --Caus. To illuminate, MBh. 1, 6532.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To reflect, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 15.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To shine agreeably, Rām. 2, 30, 10.<BR> 2. To shine, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 88; 595.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
2. भास् भास्, f.<BR> 1. Light, Ṛt. 6, 33.<BR> 2. A ray of light, Rājat. 5, 343.<BR> 3. Splendour, Pañc. i. d. 213.<BR> 4. Image, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38.<BR> 5. Wish.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरभास्
अ-चिर- + भास् अ-चिर- + भास्, f. lightning, Śāk. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्कभास्
शशाङ्क- + भास् शशाङ्क- + भास्, adj. shining like the moon, Ṛt. 6, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास भास् + अ,<BR> I. m., and f. सा, Light.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A vulture, Man. 11, 135; Pañc. 157, 3(?).<BR> 2. A cock.<BR> 3. A sort of water-fowl.<BR> 4. A station of cowherds.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मभास|पद्मभासः
पद्म- + भास पद्म- + भास, m. a name of Viṣṇu, Hariv. 14119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषभासा
पूषभासा पूषभासा, i. e. पूषन्-, f. The capital of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासक|भासकः
भासक भास् + अक, adj. Making evident, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासता
भासता भास + ता, f. Condition of a vulture, Man. 11, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्त|भासंत|भासन्तः
भासन्त भासन्त् + अ (vb. भास्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Shining.<BR> 2. Beautiful.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR> 3. A kind of water-fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासिन्
भासिन् भास् + इन्, adj. Shining, Hariv. 985.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुर|भासुरं|भासुरः
भासुर भासुर (= भास्वर),<BR> I. adj. Shining, Bhartṛ. 2, 27.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Crystal.<BR> 2. A hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुरक
भासुरक भासुर + क, m. A proper name, Pañc. 53, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुरत्व
भासुरत्व भासुर + त्व, n. Splendour, Mālav. d. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्कर भास्-कर,<BR> I. adj. Resplendent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Pañc. 190, 4.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR> 3. A hero.<BR> III. n. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्यत्व
भास्यत्व भास्य + त्व (vb. भास्), n. Condition of appearing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वन्त्|भास्वत्
भास्वन्त् भास् + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Shining, Man. 1, 77; radiant, Chr. 294, 7 = Rigv. i. 92, 7.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. The sun, Pañc. iii. d. 77.<BR> 3. A hero.<BR> III. f. वती, The city of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वर|भास्वरं|भास्वरः
भास्वर भास्वर, i. e. भास्वन् (curtailed ˚वन्त्), + अ (with र् for न्),<BR> I. adj. Shining, Bhāṣāp. 40; radiant.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. A day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष्
भिक्ष् भिक्ष् (for बिभक्ष्, desider. of भज्), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 3, 16986).<BR> 1. To beg, Man. 2, 184.<BR> 2. To solicit from, Man. 2, 50 (acc.); 11, 24 (abl.).<BR> 3. † To obtain.<BR> 4. † To fail of obtaining.<BR> 5. † To be distressed.<BR> 6. † To solicit anything through covetousness(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षा
भिक्षा भिक्ष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Begging, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a " target="_blank">Page0653-a + 42</a>] Pañc. 116, 17.<BR> 2. Alms., Pañc. 116, 19.<BR> 3. Begged food, Man. 2, 50.<BR> 4. Hire.<BR> 5. Service.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भिक्ष|दुर्भिक्षं
दुर्भिक्ष दुर्भिक्ष, i. e. दुस्-, n.<BR> 1. Famine, Pañc. 114, 4.<BR> 2. Want of provisions, Hiḍ. iii. d. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभिक्ष|सुभिक्षः
सुभिक्ष सुभिक्ष, i. e. सु-, n. abundance of food, Rājat. 5, 116; Pañc. iv. d. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाक|भिक्षाकः
भिक्षाक भिक्षा + क, m., and f. की, A mendicant, Rājat. 6, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षु|भिक्षुः
भिक्षु भिक्ष् + उ, m.<BR> 1. A mendicant; one who subsists only upon alms, Pañc. v. d. 55.<BR> 2. A religious mendicant, Hit. iii. d. 104.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतभिक्षु|श्वेतभिक्षुः
श्वेत- + भिक्षु श्वेत- + भिक्षु, a sort of mendicant, Pañc. iii. d. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुक|भिक्षुकः
भिक्षुक भिक्षु + क, m., and f. की, A beggar, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभिक्षुक|धर्मभिक्षुकः|धर्म्मभिक्षुक
धर्म- + भिक्षुक धर्म- + भिक्षुक, m. a virtuous mendicant, Man. 11, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यभिक्षुक|शाक्यभिक्षुकः
शाक्य- + भिक्षुक शाक्य- + भिक्षुक, f. की, a Bauddha nun, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिण्ड|भिण्डः
भिण्ड<BR> I. m. A shrub.<BR> II. f. दा, A kind of shrub (ŚKD.), Pañc. i. d. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त|भित्तं
भित्त भित्त, i. e. भिद् + त, n. A part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्ति|भित्तिः
भित्ति भित्ति, i. e. भिद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Breaking.<BR> 2. A thing broken or divided.<BR> 3. A fissure, Bhartṛ. 2, 31.<BR> 4. A fragment, Kir. 5, 8.<BR> 5. A defect.<BR> 6. Opportunity.<BR> 7. An asylum.<BR> 8. A wall of earth or masonry, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17; Mālav. 50, 6.<BR> 9. A place, Śiś. 9, 75.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभित्ति|सुधाभित्तिः
सुधा- + भित्ति सुधा- + भित्ति f. a plastered wall, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिका
भित्तिका भित्ति + का, f.<BR> 1. A wall.<BR> 2. A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
1. भिद् भिद्, ii. 7, भिनद्, भिन्द्, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To break, Rām. 2, 80, 17; to destroy, Pañc. i. d. 112.<BR> 2. To tear up, Pañc. 230, 16.<BR> 3. To pierce, Rām. 3, 50, 18; pass. to be afflicted, Pañc. i. d. 436.<BR> 4. To divide, Pañc. i. d. 115; to disjoin, Man. 7, 66.<BR> 5. To betray, 7, 50.<BR> 6. Pass. To differ, Śiś. 9, 46.<BR> 7. Pass. To split, Cāṇ. 21 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 406. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-b " target="_blank">Page0653-b + 45</a>]<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भिन्न,<BR> 1. Broken, split, cloven, Rājat. 5, 260.<BR> 2. Divide, Rājat. 5, 176.<BR> 3. Disunited, Hit. iv. d. 39 (दान-, on account of gifts).<BR> 4. Distinguished, other, different (दिनस्य पूर्वार्धपरार्धभिन्नछाया, the shade of the day different in the morning and in the afternoon, Pañc. ii. d. 38).<BR> 5. Separated, detached, without (also as former part of comp. adj.), Pañc. i. d. 212; Megh. 82; Bhāṣāp. 133.<BR> 6. Blown, opened.<BR> 7. Performed with great strides, Vikr. d. 80 (भिन्न-गति, adj. Going quickly, cf. गति-भेद).<BR> 8. Neglected, deviated from.<BR> 9. Connected, joined, mixed, Megh. 60. m. A flaw in a jewel. n.<BR> 1. A bit, a portion.<BR> 2. (in arithmetic), A fraction.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. भेद्य.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-भेद्य, adj. 1. impenetrable, Rām. 6, 79, 65. 2. indestructible. n. a diamond.<BR> दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be broken or divided, Hit. i. d. 21, M.M.<BR> सुची-, 1. to be pierced by a needle. 2. palpable. 3. very dense (viz. darkness), Hit. 98, 22.<BR> II. भिद्य, m. a river.<BR> --Caus. भेदय,<BR> 1. To divide, to cleave, Rām. 1, 16, 23.<BR> 2. To perplex, Rām. 1, 64, 7.<BR> 3. To disunite, MBh. 1, 7399.<BR> 4. To remove, to overcome, MBh. 1, 5592.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिभिन in नातिभिन्न, Wholly like, Śāk. 27, 18.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To break afterward, MBh. 2, 2483.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To divide, to pierce through, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 7.<BR> 2. Pass. To break forth, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 5. उद्भिन्न,<BR> 1. Opened, burst, Ragh. 13, 21.<BR> 2. Budded.<BR> 3. Destroyed, Lass. 64, 1.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोद्भिन्न,<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-a " target="_blank">Page0654-a + 43</a>] Breaking forth, Śāk. 128, 18 Chezy.<BR> 2. Standing erect, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To divide, to cleave, Rām. 3, 55, 10; to open, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> 2. To break down, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 1.<BR> 3. To put out (one's eyes), MBh. 3, 10328.<BR> 4. To pierce, Vikr. d. 144; Rām. 2, 35, 4.<BR> 5. To destroy, Hit. ii. d. 21.<BR> 6. To betray, to divulge, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 8. निर्-भिन,<BR> 1. Pierced, Vikr. d. 150.<BR> 2. Undistinguished, equal (rather भिन्न with निस्).<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. निर्भेद्य,<BR> 1. Not disappointed, Rām. 6, 91, 26.<BR> 2. Without fissures, Kām. Nītis. 11, 66 (rather भेद्य with निस्).<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, To cleave, MBh. 3, 8551.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रभिन्न,<BR> 1. Pierced, Sund. 2, 20.<BR> 2. Well cut, detached, Johns. Sel. 54, 134; severed. m. A furious elephant (cf. Johns. 1. 1.).<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To disown, Śiś. 9, 58.<BR> 2. To pierce, Draup. 6, 15.<BR> 3. To reproach, Ragh. 19, 22.<BR> 4. To betray, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 22. प्रतिभिन्न,<BR> 1. Pierced.<BR> 2. Separated.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To cleave, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10.<BR> 2. To pierce, MBh. 3, 709. विभिन्न,<BR> 1. Pierced, wounded.<BR> 2. Broken.<BR> 3. Scattered, moved to and fro, Vikr. d. 85.<BR> 4. Mixed, Kir. 5, 34.<BR> 5. Various.<BR> 6. Disappointed.<BR> 7. Bewildered.<BR> --Caus. To alienate, Rām. 2, 7, 18.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संभिन्न,<BR> 1. Divided.<BR> 2. Shaken.<BR> 3. Combined, united.<BR> --Cf. Lat. findo, finis (for fid + nis); Goth. beitan; A.S. bitan (with batan, Caus. to cause to bite, to bait); Goth. baitar; A.S. biter; O.H.G. biz, bizzo, fiza, etc.; ϕείδομαι, ϕιτρός (for ϕιδ + τρος), and probably ϕῑμός (for ϕιδ-μός).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्
अ- + भिद् अ- + भिद्, adj. 1. unhurt, Ragh. 17, 12. 2. undivided. 3. not different, unchanged, Śāk. d. 14; equal, identical, Prab. 9, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
2. भिद् भिद्,<BR> I. adj. Who or what [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b " target="_blank">Page0654-b + 36</a>] breaks, divides, destroys; cf. बलभिद्.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Difference, kind.<BR> 2. Breaking, dividing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाभिद्
यमुना- + भिद् यमुना- + भिद्, m. Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदक|भिदकं|भिदकः
भिदक भिद् + अक,<BR> I. m. A sword.<BR> II. n. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदा
भिदा भिद् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Tearing, cleaving, Kir. 5, 43.<BR> 2. Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदि|भिदिः
भिदि भिद् + इ, m., भिदिर भिद् + इर, n., भिदु भिद् + उ, m., and भिद्र भिद् + र, n. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुर|भिदुरं|भिदुरः
भिदुर भिद् + उर,<BR> I. adj. Brittle.<BR> II. n. Thunderbolt; Pañc. i. d. 241 corr. पिठरु, see my translation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्द्
भिन्द् भिन्द्, see बिन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नक|भिन्नकः
भिन्नक भिन्न + क (vb. भिद्), m.<BR> 1. A Bauddha.<BR> 2. A musical mode, Vikr. 56, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदेशत्व
भिन्नदेशत्व भिन्न-देश + त्व, n. Condition of being widely distant, Śāk. d. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवृत्तिता
भिन्नवृत्तिता भिन्न-वृत्ति + ता, f. Omission of prescribed acts, Man. 12, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिया
भिया भिया, i. e. भी + अ, f. Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्
भिल् भिल्, see बिल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्ल|भिल्लः
भिल्ल भिल्ल, m. A barbarian of a particular tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषग्जित|भिषग्जितं
भिषग्जित भिषग्जित, i. e. भिषज् + जित (vb. जि), n. A medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्
भिषज् भिषज्, i. e. अभि-सञ्ज्, m. A physician, Pañc. 156, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
1. भी भी, ii. 3; i. 1, ved. (and † i. 10?), Par. (ved., and in epic poetry also Ātm., Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8; MBh. 3, 16289).<BR> 1. To fear, Rām. 1, 59, 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a " target="_blank">Page0655-a + 44</a>]<BR> 2. To be afraid of, with abl., Man. 4, 191; with gen., Rām. 1, 1, 4; with acc., Lass. 51, 7. Anomal. aor. sing.<BR> 2. भैस्, Chr. 36, 16.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भीत, Frightened, Pañc. i. d. 364; fearful, Chr. 19, 14; timid, Chr. 54, 11; afraid of, Cāṇ. 96 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 413. n. Fear.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. भायय.<BR> 2. भापय, Ātm.<BR> 3. भीषय, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 1, 185), To terrify, MBh. 8, 1791. भिषित, Terrified, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 15.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, निर्भित, adj. fearless, Rām. 2, 27, 17 (rather भीत, n. Fear, with निस्).<BR> --With प्र प्र, To fear in a high degree, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 2. (वि वि, in वि-भीत, adj. Fearless, is compounded rather with भीत).<BR> --Cf. ϕέβομαι, ϕόβος (ϕεβ = भाप् in the Caus. भापय), and probably ϕάψ; O.H.G. bibên; A.S. bifian, beofian (old frequent.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अ- + भीत अ- + भीत, adj. fearless, Rām. 2, 60, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीत|दिवाभीतः
दिवा- + भीत दिवा- + भीत, m. 1. an owl, Kumāras. 1, 12. 2. a thief. 3. any flower, the petals of which close in the daytime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीत
महा- + भीत महा- + भीत, 1. adj. very timid. 2. f. ता, a sort of sensitive plant, Mimosa pudica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभीत
सु- + भीत सु- + भीत, adj. much afraid, Pañc. i. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
2. भी भी, f. Fear, Pañc. i. d. 125.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अ- + भी अ- + भी, and अप-, adj. fearless, Rām. 5, 14, 12; Draup. 8, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीति|भीतिः
भीति भी + ति, f.<BR> 1. Fear, Bhartṛ. 2, 72; Hit. ii. d. 54 (दोष-, of committing faults).<BR> 2. Trembling.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीति|दिवाभीतिः
दिवा- + भीति दिवा- + भीति, m. an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीम|भीमं|भीमः
भीम भी + म,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fearful, horrid, Rām. 3, 50, 27; Bhartṛ. 2, 72. 3. Terrifying, Utt. Rāmac. 139, 18.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. One of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR> III. f. मा.<BR> 1. Durgā.<BR> 2. A whip.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Horror.<BR> 2. Danger.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीम|महाभीमः
महा- + भीम महा- + भीम, 1. a name of Śāntanu. 2. one of Śiva's chamberlains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमसेन|भीमसेनः
भीमसेन भीमसेन (cf. सेन), m. The second of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरु|भीरुः
भीरु भी + रु,<BR> I. adj., f. रु or रू, Timid, Pañc. iii. d. 25.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A jackal.<BR> 2. A tiger.<BR> III. f. रु or रू.<BR> 1. A timid woman, Vikr. d. 5.<BR> 2. A plant, Asparagus racemosa.<BR> 3. A sort of prickly nightshade.<BR> 4. A centipede.<BR> 5. A goat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अ- + भीरु अ- + भीरु, 1. adj. fearless, Man. 7, 190. 2. f. रू̆, a plant, Asparagus racemosa, Suśr. 2, 223, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायभीरु
अध्यवसाय- + भीरु अध्यवसाय- + भीरु, adj. afraid of exertion, Hit. i. d. 167, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुक|भीरुकं|भीरुकः
भीरुक भीरु + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Afraid, Śāk. 30, 6 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 2. Timid, a coward, Hit. iv. d. 30.<BR> 3. Formidable.<BR> II. m. An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुता
भीरुता भीरु + ता, f. Fear, timidity. Hit. i. d. 118, M.M.; Vikr. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुत्व|भीरुत्वं
भीरुत्व भीरु + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Fear, timidity, Pañc. i. d. 118; 205.<BR> 2. The nature of a tiger, Pañc. i. d. 205 (at the same time in the first signification).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुमय
भीरुमय भीरु + मय, adj., f. यि, Terrible, Hit. 116, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु भी + लु, and भीलुक भीलु + क, adj. Timid, Hit. iv. d. 30 (क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषण|भीषणः
भीषण भीषण, i. e. भि, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. णा.<BR> 1. Horrible, Pañc. 174, 11.<BR> 2. Awful, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 8.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sentiment of horror, as the object of poetical composition.<BR> 2. The olibanum tree, Boswellia thurifera.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Horror, the property that excites fear.<BR> 2. An object of horror, Man. 3, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभीषण
अति- + भीषण अति- + भीषण, adj. very terrific, Hit. ii. d. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषा
भीषा भीषा, i. e. भी, Caus., + अ, f. Terrifying, intimidation, Man. 8, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्म|भीष्मं|भीष्मः
भीष्म भीष्म, i. e. भी, Caus., + म,<BR> I. adj. Frightful, terrific.<BR> II. n. Horror. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a " target="_blank">Page0656-a + 44</a>]<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The sentiment of horror, as the object of poetical composition.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. An imp, a goblin.<BR> 4. The grand-uncle of the Pāṇḍus, son of the Gaṅgā, Chr. 19, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीष्म|महाभीष्मः
महा- + भीष्म महा- + भीष्म, m. a name of Śāntanu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मक|भीष्मकः
भीष्मक भीष्म + क, m. The contemptible Bhīṣma, Chr. 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्ति|भुक्तिः
भुक्ति भुक्ति, i. e. 2. भुज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Fating, Pañc. 133, 2.<BR> 2. Food, Rājat. 5, 170.<BR> 3. Fruition.<BR> 4. Possession, Man. 8, 252; Pañc. iii. d. 93; iv. d. 76 (but cf. also Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 125).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
1. भुज् भुज्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To bend, to make crooked.<BR> 2. Pass. To incline one's self, Hit. iv. d. 28.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भुग्न,<BR> 1. Bent, crooked.<BR> 2. Bending, stooping.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, अवभुग्न, Crooked, MBh. 1, 5801.<BR> --Cf. Goth. biugan; A.S. bigan, búgan; O.H.G. baug; A.S. beág, beagrian; O.H.G. bogo; A.S. bóga; O.H.G. elin-bogo; A.S. elnboga, elboga; O.H.G. buoc, bûh; ϕεύγειν, ϕυγή; Lat. fugio, fuga; cf. A.S. bi-bugan, To flee away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभुज्
आ- + भुज् आ- + भुज्, adj. slightly inflexed, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
2. भुज् (akin to the preceding; cf. भज् and भञ्ज्), ii. 7, भुनज्, भुञ्ज्, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To eat and drink, Man. 2, 53; Nal. 13, 68; Rām. 3, 53, 7.<BR> 2. To enjoy (regularly, Ātm.), MBh. 3, 2167.<BR> 3. To endure, Megh. 1.<BR> 4. To govern, to possess (regularly, Par.), Man. 7, 148 (Ātm.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भुक्त,<BR> 1. Eaten.<BR> 2. Possessed, Pañc. iii. d. 93.<BR> 3. Eating, having eaten, Pañc. iv. d. 75; n. Food.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. भोग्य, To be enjoyed, Pañc. i. d. 133. n.<BR> 1. Enjoyment, Śāk. d. 47.<BR> 2. Wealth.<BR> 3. Grain. f. या, A whore.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-,<BR> I. adj. what cannot be enjoyed.<BR> II. n. absence of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-b " target="_blank">Page0656-b + 44</a>] enjoyment, Megh. 111.<BR> सु-, adj. to be enjoyed easily, Pañc. iv. d. 84.<BR> II. भोज्य, To be eaten, edible. n.<BR> 1. Food, meal, Hit. 76, 7, M.M.; milky messes, Man. 3, 227 (Kull.).<BR> 2. Gratification, Man. 9, 268.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj.<BR> 1. prohibited as food, Pañc. 121, 16. 2. a person whose food must not be eaten, Man. 4, 221.<BR> कु-, n. bad food, Cāṇ. 30 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 409. Desider. बुभुक्ष,<BR> 1. To wish to eat, MBh. 1, 8087.<BR> 2. To wish to govern, or to possess, 1, 5667.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. भोजय, To cause to eat, to invite, to give food, Man. 3, 106; 151; 8, 392; to treat, to entertain, Pañc. 26, 20.<BR> II. भुञ्जापय, To cause to eat, Lass. 12, 4.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To dispose of, Hit. 130, 4.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To receive the reward of, Man. 4, 240; Pañc. 259, 15.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To eat, to drink, Rām. 2, 30, 16; Ragh. 1, 68 (67).<BR> 2. To enjoy, Hit. i. d. 112, M.M.<BR> 3. To have a reward of, Man. 12, 8.<BR> 4. To appropriate, 4, 202.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. उपभोग्य, To be enjoyed, what may be eaten, Pañc. 86, 23. n. An object of enjoyment, MBh. 1, 2346.<BR> II. उपभोज्य, Edible, serving for food, MBh. 14, 2552.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To eat, Mṛcch. 297, 12 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To enjoy, Kir. 5, 5.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To govern, Chr. 287, 5 = Rigv. i. 48, 5.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To enjoy, Hit. ii. d. 167; Rājat. 5, 283. अ-संभोज्य, m. One with whom nobody is allowed to eat, Man. 9, 238.<BR> --Caus. भोजय, To cause to eat, to treat, MBh. 3, 12672.<BR> --Cf. Lat. fungi; Goth. bugjan; A.S. bycgan, to buy (originally, to possess one's self of something); Goth. biuhts, biuhti. As भ्रञ्ज् for भञ्ज्, the original form was probably भ्रुञ्ज्, cf. Lat. frux, frugis, fruor, fructus, frustum, frustra, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a " target="_blank">Page0657-a + 42</a>] frutex; Goth. bruks, brûkjan; O.H.G. brûhan; A.S. brúcan, bryce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभुक्त
कु- + भुक्त कु- + भुक्त, n. bad food, Lass. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
3. ऽभुज् 2. -भुज्, latter part of comp. nouns.<BR> 1. Eating, e. g. शेष-, adj. Eating the rest, Man. 3, 117.<BR> 2. Enjoying, governing; e. g. क्षिति-, m. A king, Bhartṛ. 3, 78. क्षिति-लव-, m. A small prince, Bhartṛ. 3, 100. क्ष्मा-, गो-, जगती-, m. A king, Rājat. 5, 50; 6; 2, 44. देह-, m. Epithet of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1067. धरा-, पृथिवी-, m. A king, Rājat. 2, 7. बलि-, m. A crow. भू-, भूमी̆-, मही-, m. A king, Bhartṛ. 2, 47; Śṛṅgārat. 5; Rājat. 5, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज|भुजः
भुज 1. भुज् + अ, m., and f. जा.<BR> 1. The arm, Pañc. 215, 7.<BR> 2. The hand, Hiḍ. 1, 2.<BR> 3. The proboscis of an elephant, Draup. 8, 21.<BR> 4. A bending.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिभुज
ऊर्मि- + भुज ऊर्मि- + भुज, m. an arm-like wave, i. e. a wave instead of an arm, Śiś. 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भुज|चतुर्भुजः
चतुर्- + भुज चतुर्- + भुज,<BR> I. four arms, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 35.<BR> II. adj., f. जा, having four arms, 4, 12, 20.<BR> III. m. the name of a Dānava, Hariv. 12934.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभुज
महा- + भुज महा- + भुज, adj. having great, powerful arms, Rām. 3, 55, 4; Indr. 5, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजग|भुजगः
भुजग 1. भुज् + अ-ग, m. A snake, Kir. 5, 4. f. गी, A female snake, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजंग|भुजङ्ग|भुजंगः|भुजङ्गः
भुजंग भुजंग, 1. भुज् + अ + म्-ग,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A snake, Bhartṛ. 2, 4; Vikr. 25, 20.<BR> 2. A catamite, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 10.<BR> II. f. गी, A female snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजंगम|भुजङ्गम|भुजंगमः|भुजङ्गमः
भुजंगम भुजंगम, i. e. 1. भुज् + अ + म्-गम् + अ, m. A snake, Pañc. 174, 11; Bhartṛ. 2, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाकण्ट|भुजाकंट|भुजाकण्टः
भुजाकण्ट भुजा-कण्ट (cf. कण्टक), m. A finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजान्तर|भुजांतर|भुजान्तरं
भुजान्तर भुजान्तर, i. e. भुज-अन्तर, n. The breast, Vikr. d. 112 (अल्प-, adj., f. रा, Having a small chest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजि|भुजिः
भुजि 2. भुज् + इ, m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजिष्य|भुजिष्यः
भुजिष्य भुज् + इष्य,<BR> I. m., and f. या, A servant, Nal. 13, 55.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An independent man.<BR> 2. A string worn round the wrist.<BR> III. f. या, A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यु|भुज्युः
भुज्यु 2. भुज् + यु, m.<BR> 1. Eating.<BR> 2. A vessel(?).<BR> 3. A proper name, Chr. 296, 6 = Rigv. i. 112, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुञ्जापय
भुञ्जापय भुञ्जापय, see 2. भुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुण्ड्|भुंड्
† भुण्ड् भुण्ड्, and हुण्ड् हुण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To support.<BR> 2. To select.<BR> 3. To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरण्य
भुरण्य भुरण्य (a ved. denomin. from ved. भुरण, based on भुर् = Lat. fur-ere), Par. To be active, Chr. 289, 6 = Rigv. i. 50, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरिज्
भुरिज् भुरिज्, f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन|भुवनं
भुवन भुवन, i. e. ब्नु + अन, n.<BR> 1. A being, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. i. 64, 3; creature, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8.<BR> 2. The world, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.<BR> 3. Man, mankind.<BR> 4. Heaven.<BR> 5. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुवन|त्रिभुवनं
त्रि- + भुवन त्रि- + भुवन, n. the three worlds, heaven, sky, and earth; or heaven, earth, and the lower regions, Bhartṛ. 1, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन्यु|भुवन्युः
भुवन्यु भुवन्यु (akin to भुवन), m.<BR> 1. A master, a lord.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवर्लोक|भुवर्लोकः
भुवर्लोक भुवर्लोक, i. e. भुवस्-लोक, m. The space between the earth and the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवस्
भुवस् भुवस्, i. e. भु + अस्, indecl. The sky, the atmosphere, Man. 2, 76; Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुविस्
भुविस् भुविस् (vb. भू), m.(?) The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुशुण्डी|भुशुंडी
भुशुण्डी भुशुण्डी, f. A weapon, apparently a kind of fire-arms, MBh. 3, 643.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
1. भू भू, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0658-a " target="_blank">Page0658-a + 47</a>] become, Man. 1, 9; with अन्यथा, To be changed, to fail, Pañc. 187, 1; न जातु अन्यथा, To be unalterable, Chr. 50, 6.<BR> 2. To spring up, Bhag. 14, 17.<BR> 3. To be MBh. 2, 150; auxiliary verb, Rām. 1, 41, 3; with अग्रे, To precede, Pañc. 215, 13.<BR> 4. To behave, Pañc. iii. d. 61.<BR> 5. To take place, Pañc. 4, 15; to be possible, Pañc. 33, 6; to be asked, Man. 12, 108.<BR> 6. With dat. To serve to, to cause; e. g. विनाशाय, Causes destruction, MBh. 3, 12312; संगमाय, To unite, Vikr. d. 129.<BR> 7. With gen. To belong to; e. g. धनं भविष्यति मे, I shall have wealth; to fall to one's share, Hit. iii. d. 104; to befall, Hit. pr. d. 28, M.M.<BR> 8. With loc. To be occupied with, MBh. 5, 205; Pañc. iii. d. 258 (भविष्यन्त्, Who will be occupied, i. e. who begins).<BR> 9. To live, to exist, MBh. 3, 2372.<BR> 10. With न, To perish. Pañc. 164, 13; MBh. 1, 2781.<BR> 11. With पुनर्, To marry a second time, Man. 9, 175.<BR> 12. To obtain (with acc.), MBh. 1, 5366.<BR> 13. Impersonal pass. with instr., literally, It is existed by = exists; e. g. यैर् च्व भूमिपालैर् भविष्यते, literally, ‘by whom will be existed kings,’ i. e. ‘who were to be kings,’ Rājat. 5, 418.<BR> 14. भवतु, imperat.<BR> 3. sing. a May be, but, Śāk. 64, 8. b. Stop, Śāk. 12, 12. c. Well, Vikr. 4, 2. d. No matter, Śāk. 7, 17; 9, 18. ved. conjunctive of the aor. भुवत्, Lass. 99, 3 = Rigv. v. 9, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भूत.<BR> 1. Been, become, Arj. 3, 28; Pañc. ii. d. 2 (भू-तार-भूतो ऽपरः, Become, or being, a second Saviour of the world).<BR> 2. Being, Pañc. i. d. 324; consisting of, Hit. 114, 22 (शक्तु- perhaps to be read शक्तु-पूर्णः).<BR> 3. Gone, past, former, Pañc. iii. d. 136.<BR> 4. Proper, right.<BR> 5. True. m. and n.<BR> 1. A malignant spirit, Chr. 37, 2.<BR> 2. A living being, a creature, Man. 1, 50; 95; 2, 159; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0658-b " target="_blank">Page0658-b + 47</a>] Pañc. iii. d. 136. m.<BR> 1. A son, a child.<BR> 2. A demigod of a particular kind.<BR> 3. Śiva. n. An element, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 19; Bhāṣāp. 28; five भूतस् are enumerated: earth, fire, water, air, and æther.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. भवितव्य, What is or ought to be, Chr. 50, 8; 58, 2; used as impersonal pass., Śāk. 22, 17. भवितव्यं त्वया सहायेन मम, You must become my helpmate; अवहित इस् भवद्भिः, You must be attentive, Vikr. 3, 9; अस्माभिस् तथा भवितव्यम्, We will fare thus, Hit. 16, 7, M.M.<BR> II. भव्य.<BR> 1. What is or ought to be, Sāv. 5, 47.<BR> 2. Being.<BR> 3. Good, pleasant, Pañc. 215, 6; Lass. 92, 8; profitable, Pañc. 228, 24; proper, Pañc. 138, 11.<BR> 4. True. m. A tree, Averhoa Carambola, Lass. 52, 12. f. या, A name of Umā. n.<BR> 1. Fruit.<BR> 2. Existence.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. what is or ought not to be, Pañc. 91, 6. 2. unhappy. 3. deceitful.<BR> 4. wicked, Rām. 3, 52, 14.<BR> III. भाव्य,<BR> 1. What must or ought to be, Rām. 3, 49, 13; Bhartṛ. 2, 91; Pañc. 88, 19.<BR> 2. To be investigated (from the Caus.).<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. what is not to be, or not predestined to be, Bhartṛ. 2, 91.<BR> दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be imagined, Mārk. P. 10, 7 (from the Caus.). Desider. बुभूष.<BR> 1. To wish to be or to live, MBh. 4, 678.<BR> 2. To wish to obtain, to choose, MBh. 1, 7068.<BR> --Caus. भावय.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0659-a " target="_blank">Page0659-a + 41</a>] cause to exist, to produce, MBh. 1, 8419.<BR> 2. To support, MBh. 3, 8763.<BR> 3. To make manifest, Man. 8, 60.<BR> 4. (i. 10), To (imagine, to) reflect, to consider, Rām. 2, 67, 20; Pañc. iii. d. 63; Rājat. 5, 125 (भावित-आत्मन्, adj. One who reflects about the universal soul).<BR> 5. (i. 10), To obtain, Rām. 1, 44, 48.<BR> 6. (i. 10), To purify.<BR> 7. (i. 10), † To mix. भावित,<BR> 1. Animated.<BR> 2. Occupied with.<BR> 3. Imagined.<BR> 4. Acknowledged.<BR> 5. Feigned, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 6.<BR> 6. Obtained.<BR> 7. Mixed.<BR> 8. Infused.<BR> 9. Perfumed.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To surpass, MBh. 3, 10731.<BR> --With the noun अ-दर्शन, becoming अदर्शनी अदर्शनी, To become invisible, Pañc. 34, 24; 106, 20.<BR> --With अधर, becoming अधरी अधरी, अधरीभूत, Put down, i. e. admitted, Yājñ. 2, 17 (cf. Roer, transl. n.).<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, अधि-भात, n. The Supreme Being, Bhag. 8, 4.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To be present at (acc.), Nal. 5, 40.<BR> 2. To feel, Man. 12, 17; Vikr. d. 110.<BR> 3. To suffer, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 19.<BR> 4. To enjoy, Pañc. 38, 5.<BR> 5. To learn, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 23.<BR> 6. To perceive, MBh. 3, 2112.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अन्-अनु-भूत, adj. Not perceived, Hit. 47, 18.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु,<BR> 1. To enjoy together, Lass. 6, 4.<BR> 2. To perceive, Ragh. 9, 48.<BR> --With अनु-गुण, becoming अनुगुणी अनुगुणी, To increase in proportion (to the obstacle), Vikr. d. 49 (cf. शतगुणी भू).<BR> --With अन्तर् अन्तर्, To be comprised in, Man. 12, 87.<BR> --With the noun अन्ध, becoming अन्धी अन्धी, To become blind, Pañc. 200, 1.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To attain, Vikr. d. 38.<BR> 2. To assail, Bhag. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0659-b " target="_blank">Page0659-b + 40</a>] 1, 40.<BR> 3. To overpower, Man. 7, 179.<BR> 4. To surpass, Man. 7, 5.<BR> 5. To spread over (acc.), MBh. 3, 10592. अभिभूत,<BR> 1. Overpowered, Pañc. 169, 21; Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 11.<BR> 2. Aggrieved, Pañc. 80, 10.<BR> 3. Perplexed.<BR> --With आ आ, To exist, to live, MBh. 1, 3608.<BR> --With the noun आकुल, becoming आकुली आकुली, To be perplexed, Śāk. 29, 23.<BR> --With the indecl. आविस् आविस्, To become visible. आविर्भूत, Appeared, Utt. Rāmac. 100, 14; become visible, Vikr. d. 8; 78, 20.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To spring up, to arise, Rājat. 5, 216. उद्भूत,<BR> 1. Born, produced.<BR> 2. Proceeded, Ṛt. 1, 24.<BR> 3. Lofty.<BR> 4. Vi-ii-le, present.<BR> 5. Proportionate, Bhāṣāp. 53; 54.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to exist, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 8.<BR> 2. To bring to consciousness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 9.<BR> 3. To apply, Ragh. 2, 62. उद्भावित,<BR> 1. Neglected.<BR> 2. Said.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोद्भूत,<BR> 1. Breaking forth, Lass. 11, 12.<BR> 2. Proceeding, come, Pañc. i. d. 18.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To spring up, to arise, Pañc. 42, 1. समुद्भूत, Born, produced, Pañc. i. d. 392; 42, 1.<BR> --With the numeral एक, becoming एकी एकी, To unite, MBh. 1, 919.<BR> --With एक-छित्त, becoming एकचित्ती एकचित्ती, and एक-मति, becoming एकमती एकमती, To become unanimous, Hit. 27, 3, M.M.; Pañc. 175, 19.<BR> --With कठोर, becoming कठोरी कठोरी, कठोरिभूत, Grown sharp, hot, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 9.<BR> --With कुण्डल, becoming कुण्डली कुण्डली, To ringle, Bhāg. P. 5, 23, 5.<BR> --With क्षपण, becoming क्षपणी क्षपणी, To become a Bauddha mendicant, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 16. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0660-a " target="_blank">Page0660-a + 39</a>]<BR> --With क्किल, becoming खिली खिली, खिलीभूत,<BR> 1. Wasted, impervious, Kumāras. 2, 45.<BR> 2. Vanished, Śāk. d. 149.<BR> --With गुण, becoming गुणी गुणी, गुणीभूत,<BR> 1. Made secondary, MBh. 2, 670.<BR> 2. Become an ornament, Kāvya Prak. 48, 7.<BR> 3. Invested with attributes.<BR> 4. Varied.<BR> 5. Having a certain force or application (as a word) [gunated].<BR> --With गोचर, becoming गोचरी गोचरी, To become visible, Utt. Rāmac. 155, 1.<BR> --With घन, becoming घनी घनी, घनीभूत, Thickened, become thick, Rām. 3, 5, 8.<BR> --With चूर्ण, becoming चूर्णी चूर्णी, To turn into dust, to be pounded, Vikr. d. 4.<BR> --With चौर, becoming चौरी To become a thief, Bhāg. P. 4, 18, 7.<BR> --With जर्जर, becoming जर्जरी जर्जरी, जर्जरीभूत, Decayed, Lass. 7, 9.<BR> --With झणझणा, becoming झणझणी झणझणी, -भूत, Rattling, MBh. 6, 738.<BR> --With तरुणी तरुणी, To become marriageable, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 22.<BR> --With the indecl. तिरस् तिरस्, To disappear, Bhāg. P. 9, 4, 53.<BR> --Caus. To remove, Rām. 1, 44, 9.<BR> --With तीव्र, becoming तीव्री तीव्री,-भूत, Heavy, Rājat. 6, 99.<BR> --With तूष्णीम् तूष्णीम्, To become silent, Pañc. 193, 12. तूष्णींभूत, Silent, MBh. 1, 7951.<BR> --With the noun दूर, becoming दूरी दूरी, To retire, Pañc. 19, 14 (सर्वैर् दूरिभूतम्, All retired).<BR> --With दृढ, becoming दृढी दृढी, To become strong, Pañc. iii. d. 258.<BR> --With द्रव, becoming द्रवी द्रवी, द्रवीभूत,<BR> 1. Become liquid, Mārk. P. 12, 38.<BR> 2. Melted, Utt. Rāmac. 60, 5.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0660-b " target="_blank">Page0660-b + 40</a>] द्वंद्व, becoming द्वंद्वी द्वंद्वी, -भूत, Engaged in close fight, MBh. 7, 3577.<BR> --With द्वैध, becoming द्वधी द्वैधी, To become divided, Śāk. d. 50.<BR> --With नव, becoming नवी नवी, To be renewed, Ragh. 12, 56.<BR> --With निकट, becoming निकटी निकटी, -भूत, Approached, Kathās. 19, 87.<BR> --With निःस्व, i. e. निस्-स्व, becoming निःस्वी निःस्वी, To become poor, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 5.<BR> --With निराश, i. e. निस्- (cf. आशा), becoming निराशी निराशी, To become hopeless, Pañc. 21, 15.<BR> --With the prep. परा परा, To perish, MBh. 1, 4167. पराभूत,<BR> 1. Defeated, Pañc. 151, 11.<BR> 2. Humbled, treated with contempt, Pañc. 82, 7.<BR> --With the noun पराङ्मुख, i. e. पराञ्च्-मुख, becoming पराङ्मुखी पराङ्मुखी,<BR> 1. To turn away, to turn the back, Lass. 24, 20.<BR> 2. To be disinclined, Mālav. 68, 8. पराङ्मुखीभूत, Being adverse, Pañc. 121, 16.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, To despise, MBh. 3, 1025.<BR> 2. To grieve, Pañc. 47, 2.<BR> 3. To injure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2375.<BR> --Caus. To make known, Utt. Rāmac. 177, 6.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, To despise, MBh. 3, 13230.<BR> --With the noun पर्युत्सुक, becoming पर्युत्सुकी पर्युत्सुकी, To become very sad, Śāk. d. 99.<BR> --With पात्र, becoming पात्री पात्री, To become a worthy person, MBh. 4, 1513.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To spring up, Hit. i. d. 26, M.M.; to proceed, Hit. 13, 8; to rise, pr. 47, M.M.<BR> 2. To be brought forth, MBh. 3, 17164.<BR> 3. To appear, Megh. 15.<BR> 4. To become prevalent, Hit. i. d. 86, M.M.; to be powerful, प्र भवति + तराम्, It is most powerful, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0661-a " target="_blank">Page0661-a + 40</a>] Vikr. d. 156; with न, to be powerless, Pañc. 52, 5.<BR> 5. To prevail over, Man. 5, 2; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 814; to be master of (with gen.), Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.<BR> 6. To be able, to serve (with inf. and dat.), Hit. i. d. 96, M.M.; Vikr. d. 9; 55; Ragh. 3, 44. प्रभूत,<BR> 1. Large, Pañc. 47, 25; much, Pañc. 69, 8; long, 4, 17.<BR> 2. Abounding in, distinguished, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 15.<BR> 3. Comparat. Very large, Pañc. 95, 24.<BR> 4. Superl. Highest, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 15.<BR> --With प्रकट, becoming प्रकटी प्रकटी, To become visible, Śiś. 9, 23; known, Pañc. 223, 19.<BR> --With प्रचुर, becoming प्रचुरी प्रचुरी, To increase, Śiś. 9, 20.<BR> --With प्रणयिन्, becoming प्रणयी प्रणयी, To become affectionate or attached to, Suśr. 1, 236, 17.<BR> --With प्रणिधि, becoming प्रणिधी प्रणिधी, To become a spy, Pañc. 172, 6.<BR> --With प्रत्यन्तर (see s. v.), becoming प्रत्यन्तरी प्रत्यन्तरी, To be near, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 5.<BR> --With प्रेमन्-राशि, becoming प्रेमराशी प्रेमराशी, To become a heap, (a great) store of love, Megh. 111.<BR> --With प्रादुस् प्रादुस्, To become manifest or visible, to appear, Pañc. 235, 22.<BR> --With बन्धकी बन्धकी, To become a harlot, Rājat. 5, 466.<BR> --With बहुल, becoming बहुली बहुली, To be multiplied, Pañc. ii. d. 187; बहुली-भूत, Generally known, Śāk. 79, 11.<BR> --With भस्मन्, becoming भस्मी भस्मी, To become mere ashes, Man. 4, 188; Pañc. iii. d. 155. भस्मीभूत, Mere ashes, i. e. wholly worthless, Man. 3, 97.<BR> --With भृत्य, becoming भृत्यी भृत्यी, To become a servant, Rājat. 5, 51. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0661-b " target="_blank">Page0661-b + 40</a>]<BR> --With मन्द, becoming मन्दी मन्दी, -भूत, Become slack or dull, tired, Johns. Sel. 15, 58.<BR> --With मलिन, becoming मलिनी मलिनी, To become soiled, Śāk. d. 176.<BR> --With रहस्, becoming रही रही, रहिभूत, Solitary, alone.<BR> --With राशि, becoming राशी राशी, -भूत, Heaped, Rājat. 5, 190.<BR> --With वश, becoming वशी वशी, -भूत, Subject to another's will.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, Caus.<BR> 1. To trace out, Man. 8, 25.<BR> 2. To observe, Śiś. 9, 81.<BR> 3. To perceive, Vikr. 31, 6; Pañc. 198, 1, v. d. 7; to feel, Vikr. d. 132; to recognise, Vikr. 54, 12; pass. to appear, Pañc. 45, 13.<BR> 4. To prove, Man. 8, 56.<BR> 5. To decide, Pañc. 210, 10. विभावित,<BR> 1. Seen, perceived, Vikr. d. 96 (विभावित-एक-देश, That with whom is seen a part of a stolen object).<BR> 2. Judged.<BR> 3. Conceived.<BR> 4. Established.<BR> 5. Put right, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 14(?).<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, 1. unobserved, Man. 7, 147. 2. not perceived, Śiś. 9, 40.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-विभाव्य, not to be perceived, Śiś. 9, 12.<BR> दुर्व्˚, i. e. दुस्-, difficult to be understood, Rām. 2, 24, 33.<BR> --With वि-फल, becoming विफली विफली, To become fruitless, Pañc. 174, 12.<BR> --With वि-षम, i. e. वि-सम, becoming विषमी विषमी, To stumble, Śāk. d. 90.<BR> --With विषय, becoming विषयी विषयी, To become the province, property, Pañc. 25, 9.<BR> --With वैर, becoming वेरी वैरी, To be changed into hate, Śāk. d. 120.<BR> --With व्यक्त (vb. वि-अञ्ज्), becoming व्यक्ती व्यक्ती, To become visible, Rājat. 5, 240.<BR> --With व्याकुल, becoming व्याकुली व्याकुली, To become [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0662-a " target="_blank">Page0662-a + 42</a>] perplexed, Pañc. 46, 1 (भूत्वा, against gramm.), anxious, Pañc. 142, 3.<BR> --With शत-गुण, becoming शतगुणी शतगुणी, -भूत, Become a hundred times as many, or stronger, Vikr. d. 49, v. r.<BR> --With शिथिल, becoming शिथिली शिथिली, To become loosened, to slacken, Hit. iv. d. 79.<BR> --With शिशिर, becoming शिशिरी शिशिरी, To become cool, Utt. Rāmac. 158, 10.<BR> --With शुच्कि, becoming शुची शुची, To become pure, to purify one's self, Pañc. 221, 7.<BR> --With शूद्र, becoming शुद्री शूद्री, To become a Śūdra, Man. 10, 92.<BR> --With श्याम, becoming श्यामी श्यामी, To become dark blue, Kir. 5, 37.<BR> --With श्रेणी̆, becoming श्रेणी श्रेणि, श्रेणी-भूत, Formed in lines, Megh. 22.<BR> --With सज्ज, becoming सज्जी सज्जी,<BR> 1. To be accoutred, Hit. 59, 9 (सज्जीभूय, in full decoration).<BR> 2. To be ready, Hit. 76, 20.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To be together, MBh. 1, 5658; to unite, Hit. 107, 19.<BR> 2. To be composed, Man. 1, 27.<BR> 3. To accrue, Man. 8, 255; Pañc. 192, 3.<BR> 4. To meet with (instr.), Daśak. in Chr. 201, 6.<BR> 5. To have sexual intercourse with (instr.), MBh. 1, 4398.<BR> 6. To become, Chr. 63, 64.<BR> 7. To spring up, to arise, to proceed, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 17.<BR> 8. To be engendered, Johns. Sel. 1, 2; to be born, Rām. 1, 43, 2.<BR> 9. To take place, Chr. 39, 2; to happen, Hit. 17, 4, M.M.<BR> 10. To be, Hit. 97, 17; to exist, Hit. 130, 12.<BR> 11. To be adequate, Lass. 76, 16.<BR> 12. To be able to exist, Matsyop. 12.<BR> 13. To be able, Śiś. 1, 27.<BR> 14. To be possible, Hit. 99, 6. सम्भूत,<BR> 1. Combined with.<BR> 2. Adequate.<BR> 3. Born.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be with, to meet, MBh. 3, 1982. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0662-b " target="_blank">Page0662-b + 44</a>]<BR> 2. To cause to get, to deliver, Pañc. 84, 17; Ragh. 16, 40.<BR> 3. To confide to, MBh. 1, 2088.<BR> 4. To cause to exist, MBh. 1, 1425.<BR> 5. To cause to recover, Utt. Rāmac. 78, 13.<BR> 6. To nourish, Man. 2, 142.<BR> 7. To preserve, MBh. 1, 1343.<BR> 3. To appoint, Pañc. ii. d. 25.<BR> 9. To make, MBh. 3, 13316.<BR> 10. To manifest, to show, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 12.<BR> 11. To prove, Mālav. 21, 17.<BR> 12. To think, to represent, Śāk. 21, 6; to take for, Pañc. 78, 18.<BR> 13. With अन्यथा, To misunderstand, Śāk. 17, 5.<BR> 14. To consider, Pañc. iii. d. 208; Ragh. 6, 42.<BR> 15. To believe, Pañc. 111, 10.<BR> 16. To honour, Bhartṛ. 2, 27; Utt. Rāmac. 47, 14.<BR> 17. To expect, Pañc. iv. d. 81. सम्भावित,<BR> 1. Adequate, suited.<BR> 2. Possible.<BR> 3. Considered, reflected.<BR> 4. Satisfied.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. सम्भाव्य, Suitable, Pañc. 117, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. impossible, Pañc. 30, 8; v. d. 59.<BR> --With सु-वर्ण, becoming सुवर्णी सुवर्णी, To turn into gold, Pañc. 192, 2.<BR> --With स्तम्भ, becoming स्तम्भी स्तम्भी, To become a post, Hit. i. d. 29, M.M.<BR> --With स्थिर, becoming स्थिरी स्थिरी, To be calm, Lass. 43, 17.<BR> --With स्फार, becoming स्कारी स्प्करी, To become large, to spread, Häberl. Anth. 217, 8; Pañc. v. d. 22; Mṛcch. 49, 6 (to show a hidden property in a magical way, by becoming large, or by throbbing).<BR> --Cf. ϕύω, ϕύλη, ϕώς, ϕωτός (cf. भवन्त्), probably ϕῖτυ, ϕιτύω, perhaps πρές-βυς; Lat. fio, fui, facio (causal), fecundus, fetus, fetare, perhaps femur, femen; O.H.G. pim, pis, etc.; A.S. beón, beó, bist, etc.; Goth. ga-bauan; O.H.G. bûwan, bûan, pu, bûr; A.S. búan, bur; O.H.G. bûari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूत|आत्मभूतः
आत्मभूत आत्मभूत, i. e. आत्मन्-, adj. true to himself, Man. 7, 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्भूत|इत्थंभूत
इत्थम्- + भूत इत्थम्- + भूत, adj. so natured, Pañc. 31, 17 (read as one word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्भूत|एवंभूत
एवम्- + भूत एवम्- + भूत, adj. such, Hit. 10, 7, M.M.; 84, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थभूत
तीर्थ- + भूत तीर्थ- + भूत, adj. hallowed, MBh. 13, 1725.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभूत
दिवा- + भूत दिवा- + भूत, adj. become as clear as the day, MBh. 14, 1757.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

