पानभूमि|पानभूमिः
पान- + भूमि पान- + भूमि, f. a drinking-room, Rām. 5, 14, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लभूमि|मल्लभूमिः
मल्ल- + भूमि मल्ल- + भूमि, f. an arena for athletic contests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यभूमि
बध्य- + भूमि बध्य- + भूमि (vb. वध्), f. place of execution, Hit. 63, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गभूमि|रंगभूमि|रङ्गभूमिः
रङ्ग- + भूमि रङ्ग- + भूमि, f. 1. a field of battle, Pañc. 35, 3. 2. an arena, Johns. Sel. 9, 11. 3. a stage, a place where [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a " target="_blank">Page0664-a + 42</a>] dancing, etc., is exhibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासभूमि
वास- + भूमि वास- + भूमि, f. a dwelling-place, Hit. 38, 2, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासभूमि|विश्वासभूमिः
विश्वास- + भूमि विश्वास- + भूमि, f. a person worthy of confidence, Hit. 18, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतभूमि
संकेत- + भूमि संकेत- + भूमि, f. place of assignation, Lass. 24, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानभूमि
स्थान- + भूमि स्थान- + भूमि, f. dwelling-place, a palace(?), Lass. 28, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभूमि|स्नेहभूमिः
स्नेह- + भूमि स्नेह- + भूमि, f. one worthy of love, Mālat. 83, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धभूमि
सिद्ध- + भूमि सिद्ध- + भूमि, f. the country in which the Siddhas live, Pañc. 242, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिका
भूमिका भूमि + का, f.<BR> 1. Change-of costume in order to represent a different character on the stage.<BR> 2. Decorating images, temples, gateways, etc.<BR> 3. A story; ग्रिहोपरिभूमिकायाम् आरुढः, He mounted to the upper story of the house, Śukas. cod. Petersb. p. 31, b.<BR> 4. A preface to a book.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भूमिक
चतुर्-भूमिक चतुर्-भूमिक, adj. having four stories, Pañc. 228, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तभूमिक
सप्त(न्)- + भूमिक सप्त(न्)- + भूमिक, adj. having seven stories, 44, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिज|भूमिजं|भूमिजः
भूमिज भूमि-ज,<BR> I. adj. Born on the earth.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The planet Mars.<BR> 2. Hell.<BR> III. f. जा, Sītā, the wife of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिष्ठ
भूमिष्ठ भूमिष्ठ, i. e. भूमि-स्थ, adj. Standing or staying on the earth, Chr. 27, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्पृश्
भूमिस्पृश् भूमि-स्पृश्. m.<BR> 1. A man, mankind.<BR> 2. A vaiśya.<BR> 3. A thief, one who creeps along the ground to carry off his plunder.<BR> 4. A blind man.<BR> 5. A cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूय|भूयं|भूयः
भूय भू + य, n. State.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूय|ब्रह्मभूयं
ब्रह्म(न्)- + भूय ब्रह्म(न्)- + भूय, n. identification with Brahman, ultimate happiness, Man. 1, 98, 12, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभूय|राजभूयं
राज(न्)- + भूय राज(न्)- + भूय, n. royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयंस्
भूयंस् भूयंस्, see बहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्त्व|भूयस्त्वं
भूयस्त्व भूयस्त्व, i. e. भूयंस्. + त्व, n. State of being more or greater, Bhāṣāp. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठ|भूयिष्ठं
भूयिष्ठ भूयिष्ठ, see बहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरि|भूरिः
भूरि भूरि (probably बहु-रै, n., i. e. बहु-रि),<BR> I. adj. Much, Pañc. i. d. 23; many, Rājat. 5, 215; Kathās. 22, 96.<BR> II. adv.<BR> 1. Much, exceeding, Pañc. i. d. 213; Bhartṛ. 2, 62.<BR> 2. Frequently, repeatedly, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Brahman.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. A day.<BR> IV. n. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज|भूर्जः|भूर्ज्ज
भूर्ज भूर्ज, m. A kind of birch; its leaf or bark used for writing on, Vikr. 30, 11.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. bircha; A.S. byre, birce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्णि|भूर्णिः
भूर्णि भूर्णि, i. e. भृ + नि, f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्लोक|भूर्लोकः
भूर्लोक भूर्-लोक, i. e. भू + स्-लोक, m. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्
भूष् भूष्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To decorate, to adorn, Man. 3, 55.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, The same, Chr. 296, 4 = Rigv. i. 112, 4; Bhartṛ. 2, 16; Pañc. 256, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषण|भूषणं|भूषणः
भूषण भूषण, i. e. भूष् + अन, n. Ornament, Hit. ii. d. 71; 171.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूषण
पर- + भूषण पर- + भूषण, adj., Hit. iv. d. 121; false reading for परि-, q. cf. मङ्गल-मात्र-, adj., f. णा, only adorned with turmeric, Vikr. d. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषा
भूषा भूष् + आ, f. Adorning, ornament, Rām. 3, 49, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु भूष्णु, i. e. भू + स्नु, adj.<BR> 1. Being.<BR> 2. Being well.<BR> 3. One who desires bliss, Man. 4, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्तृण|भूस्तृणं|भूस्तृणः
भूस्तृण भू + स्-तृण(?), n. A fragrant grass, Andropogon schaenanthus, Man. 6, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ भृ, i. 1, and ii. 3, बिभृ, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To bear, to hold, Vikr. d. 140; Chr. 16, 17.<BR> 2. To wear, Man. 6, 6.<BR> 3. Ātm. To gain, Chr. 291, 13 = Rigv. i. 64, 13.<BR> 4. To possess, MBh. 3, 2583; to have, 2, 57.<BR> 5. To form, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-a " target="_blank">Page0665-a + 43</a>] Rājat. 5, 332.<BR> 6. To nourish, to maintain, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 5.<BR> 7. i. 1, Ātm. To hire, Nal. 15, 4.<BR> 8. To support, Man. 9, 95.<BR> 9. To fill, Hit. 2, 34.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भृत.<BR> 1. Hired.<BR> 2. Having, being possessed of.<BR> 3. Filled. m. A servant.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अतिभृत (rather भृत with अति),<BR> 1. Carefully protected.<BR> 2. Filled, Kir. 5, 20.<BR> --With आ आ, To bring near, to bestow, Lass. 99, 2 = Rigv. v. 9, 7.<BR> --With नि नि, निभृत,<BR> 1. Modest, humble; ˚तम्, humbly, Pañc. 162, 24.<BR> 2. Unmoved, Śāk. d. 8.<BR> 3. Hidden, Pañc. 46, 13; 193, 7.<BR> 4. ˚तम् adv. Hidden, Pañc. 105, 4; secretly, Man. 9, 263.<BR> 5. ˚तम्, adv. with वि-धा, To make hidden, to shut, Pañc. 186, 8.<BR> 6. Lonely, solitary, Megh. 83; ˚तम् with कृ, To dismiss all but one, Hit. 56, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To offer, Chr. 291, 1.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To bring together, Rām. 1, 11, 13.<BR> 2. To accomplish, Vikr. 85, 17; d. 157.<BR> 3. To nourish, Rām. 1, 52, 8. संभृत,<BR> 1. Collected, all, Vikr. d. 38.<BR> 2. Gained, got.<BR> 3. Composed, Hit. iv. d. 68.<BR> 4. Filled.<BR> 5. Nourished, Hit. iii. d. 125 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3272).<BR> 6. Brought, put, Megh. 44.<BR> --Cf. ϕέρω, ϕόρτος, ϕορμός, ϕωριαμός, ϕάρετρα, ϕᾶρος, δί-ϕρος, δι-ϕθέρα; Lat. fero; Goth. bairan; A.S. beran; Goth. barms; A.S. bearm; Goth. barn; A.S. bearn; byrdhen; Goth. briggan; A.S. bringan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत
अ- + भृत अ- + भृत, adj. not paid, Man. 8, 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरभृत
क्षीर- + भृत क्षीर- + भृत, adj. paid with milk, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य भृत्य, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत
अ- + भृत अ- + भृत, adj. immodest, bold, Megh. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृत
सु- + भृत सु- + भृत, adj. very lonely. ˚तम्, adv. 1. secretly, Hit. 86, 6. 2. privately, Hit. 73, 16 (in a very low voice?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृंश्
† भृंश् भृंश्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंश|भृकुंशः
भृकुंश भृकुंश, and भृकुंस भृकुंस, भ्रकुंश and ˚स भ्रकुंश and ˚स, and भ्रुकुंश and ˚स भ्रुकुंश, ˚स, and भ्रूकुंश, ˚स भ्रूकुंश, ˚स, m. A male actor in female apparel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटि|भृकुटिः
भृकुटि भृकुटि, see भ्रूकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृक्ष्
† भृक्ष् भृक्ष्, v. r. of भक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगु|भृगुः
भृगु भृगु, m.<BR> 1. The name of a Muni, Chr. 17, 29.<BR> 2. Jamadagni.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. Śukra.<BR> 5. A cliff, a precipice.<BR> 6. Table-land.<BR> 7. pl. The descendants of Bhṛgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्ग|भृंग|भृङ्गं|भृंगः|भृङ्गः
भृङ्ग भृङ्ग, probably भ्रम्-ग,<BR> I. m., and f. गी (Kathās. 22, 103).<BR> 1. A large bee, Ragh. 8, 52.<BR> 2. A wasp.<BR> 3. The fork-tailed shrike, Lanius cærulescens, Ṛt. 6, 24 (cf. Lass. 52, 18).<BR> 4. A golden vase.<BR> 5. A libertine.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A plant, Woody cassia.<BR> 2. Another, Verbesina prostrata Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गक|भृंगकः|भृङ्गकः
भृङ्गक भृङ्ग + क, m. A bird, a sort of shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गार|भृंगार|भृंगारं|भृङ्गारं|भृंगारः|भृङ्गारः
भृङ्गार भृङ्गार (cf. भृङ्ग),<BR> I. m. A golden vase.<BR> II. n. Gold.<BR> III. f. री, A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्
† भृज् भृज्, i. 1, Ātm. To parch, to fry; cf. भ्रज्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्जन|भृज्जनं|भृज्जनः
भृज्जन भृज्जन, i. e. ब्रज्ज् + अन, n. A frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृड्
† भृड् भृड्, i. 6, Par. To dive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्
ऽभृत् -भृ + त्, latter part of comp. nouns, Bearing, nourishing, protecting; e. g. अ-पात्र-, adj. Supporting unworthy ones, Hit. ii. d. 147. गदा-, m.<BR> 1. A mace-bearer.<BR> 2. A name of Kṛṣṇa, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a " target="_blank">Page0666-a + 44</a>] Bhāg. P. 1, 13, 9. चक्र-, m. Viṣṇu, Rājat. 1, 38. तनु-, m.<BR> 1. A living creature.<BR> 2. A man, mankind, Bhartṛ. 3, 36. तपोभृत्, i. e. तपस्-, m. An ascetic, Hariv. 4849. देह-, m.<BR> 1. A living creature.<BR> 2. A man, mankind. Bhāg. P. 7, 7, 46.<BR> 3. Epithet of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1067. धरणी-, m.<BR> 1. A king.<BR> 2. A mountain. धरा-, m. A mountain, Arj. 7, 27. धर्म-,<BR> 1. m. Supporter of right, an epithet of kings, MBh. 1, 4766.<BR> 2. m. A proper name. नव-शशि(न्)-, Bearing the young moon, epithet of Śiva, Megh. 44. प्राण-, adj. Living, a living creature, Hit. i. d. 111, M.M.; a man, mankind. भू-, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतक|भृतकः
भृतक भृत + क (see भृ),<BR> 1. m. A servant, Man. 6, 45.<BR> 2. (n.) Wages, Man. 3, 156 (or ‘Hired’).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमभृतक|मध्यमभृतकः
मध्यम- + भृतक मध्यम- + भृतक, m. a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृति|भृतिः
भृति भृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Nourishment, Hit. ii. d. 32.<BR> 2. Wages, hire, Man. 8, 231.<BR> 3. Service, Nal. 8, 25.<BR> 4. Capital, principal.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. fors; A.S. beordh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डभृति|पिंडभृति|पिण्डभृतिः
पिण्ड- + भृति पिण्ड- + भृति, f. livelihood, Rām. 2, 26, 37 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभृति|सुधाभृतिः
सुधा- + भृति सुधा- + भृति, m. 1. sacrifice. 2. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृति|हलभृतिः
हल- + भृति हल- + भृति, f. agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य भृत्य,<BR> I. ptcple. fut. pass. of भृ, To be nourished.<BR> II. m. A servant, Pañc. 175, 16; i. d. 325.<BR> III. f. या, Hire.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभृत्य
कु- + भृत्य कु- + भृत्य and किम्-, m. a wicked servant, Pañc. 83, 18; Hit. ii. d. 31 (read किंभृत्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारभृत्या
कुमार-भृत्या कुमार-भृत्या, f. the fostering of a child, Ragh. 3, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कटभृत्य|प्रोत्कटभृत्यः
प्रोत्कट- + भृत्य प्रोत्कट- + भृत्य, m. a favourite, Pañc. 156, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलभृत्य|मूलभृत्यः
मूल- + भृत्य मूल- + भृत्य, m. an old servant, Hit. ii. d. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यता
भृत्यता भृत्य + ता, f., and भृत्यत्व भृत्य + त्व, n. Servitude, service, dependence, Pañc. 24, 11; Hit. ii. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृमि|भृमिः
भृमि भृमि, i. e. भ्रम् + इ, m. A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश्
† भृश् भृश्, i. 4, Par. To fall; cf. भ्रंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश|भृशं
भृश भृश (perhaps akin to भ्रंश्),<BR> I. adj., comparat. भ्रशीयंस्, superl. भ्रशिष्ठ, Much, exceeding.<BR> II. ˚शम्, adv.<BR> 1. Much, Pañc. iii. d. 188.<BR> 2. Exceedingly, violently, Pañc. iii. d. 183.<BR> 3. Superiority, better.<BR> 4. Repeatedly, often, Pañc. iii. d. 13.<BR> 5. Beautifully.<BR> 6. Quickly, Chr. 7, 13; 25, 15.<BR> 7. In the beginning of comp. भृश-, e. g. Chr. 31, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृश|सुभृशं
सु- + भृश सु- + भृश, adj. much, exceeding. ˚शम्, adv. much, excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृशता
भृशता भृश + ता, f. Violence, Ragh. 11, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टि|भृष्टिः
भृष्टि भृष्टि, f., i. e. भ्रज्ज् + ति,<BR> 1. Frying.<BR> 2. A lonely garden.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभृष्टि
सहस्र- + भृष्टि सहस्र- + भृष्टि, adj. having a thousand points (vb. हृष् + ति), Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. i. 85, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भॄ
† भॄ भॄ, ii. 9, भृणा, भृणी, Par.<BR> 1. To blame.<BR> 2. To bear (cf. भृ).<BR> 3. To fry.<BR> 4. To bend, to be crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेक|भेकः
भेक भेक (vb. भी),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A frog, Pañc. 81, 13.<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> II. f. की, The female frog, or a small frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेड|भेडः
भेड भेड, m. A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तृ
भेत्तृ भेत्तृ, i. e. भिद् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what divides, breaks, etc.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One who breaks down, Man. 9, 289.<BR> 2. A separator, divider.<BR> 3. One who wounds, Man. 8, 284.<BR> 4. A traitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद|भेदः
भेद भेद, i. e. भिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Breaking, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 2. Dividing, division, Pañc. 248, 19.<BR> 3. Separating, Pañc. 156, 19; separation, Hit. pr. 9, M.M.<BR> 4. A chasm, a fissure, a cleft, Vikr. 69, 8; a wound, Hit. ii. d. 1. (and betrayal).<BR> 5. Creating divisions [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a " target="_blank">Page0667-a + 42</a>] Man. 7, 198.<BR> 6. Disunion; Pañc. iv. d. 74.<BR> 7. Betrayal, Pañc. 65, 19.<BR> 8. Difference, Pañc. 199, 20.<BR> 9. Kind, Hit. iv. d. 124.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अ- + भेद अ- + भेद, m. undividedness, Hit. iii. d. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यभेद|अन्योन्यभेदः
अन्योन्य- + भेद अन्योन्य- + भेद, m. separation from each other, Hit. 76, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिभेद
गति- + भेद गति- + भेद, m. going with great strides, Śāk. 93, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिभेद|ग्रंथिभेद|ग्रन्थिभेदः
ग्रन्थि- + भेद ग्रन्थि- + भेद, m. a cutpurse, Man. 9, 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भेद
दुर्भेद दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be separated or divided, Pañc. ii. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभेद|स्वरभेदः
स्वर- + भेद स्वर- + भेद, m. difference of voice, Pañc. 37, 25; 199, 20 (different, changed voice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदक|भेदकः
भेदक भेदक, i. e. भिद् + अक, m.<BR> 1. One who breaks, Man. 8, 284 (अस्थि-).<BR> 2. One who breaks open, 9, 280.<BR> 3. One who scratches, 8, 284 (त्वच्-).<BR> 4. One who diverts (watercourses), Man. 3, 163.<BR> 5. A mischief-maker.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डभेदक
गण्ड- + भेदक गण्ड- + भेदक, m. a cutpurse, Śāk. 74, 14 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदतस्
भेदतस् भेद + तस्, adv. According to the difference, Bhag. 18, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदन|भेदनं|भेदनः
भेदन भेदन, i. e. भिद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Dividing.<BR> 2. Piercing, Man. 9, 286.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटभेदन|पुटभेदनं
पुट- + भेदन पुट- + भेदन, n. a town, MBh. 1, 3978.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिन्
भेदिन् भेदिन्, i. e. भिद् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Dividing, breaking, Man. 8, 218.<BR> 2. Wounding, Hit. iv. d. 82.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मभेदिन्|मर्म्मभेदिन्
मर्म(न्)- + भेदिन् मर्म(न्)- + भेदिन्, adj. piercing the vitals, fatal, Chr. 29, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभेदिन्
वृक्ष- + भेदिन् वृक्ष- + भेदिन्, m. 1. a carpenter's chisel. 2. a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरण्ड
भेरण्ड भेरण्ड, see भारण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरि|भेरिः
भेरि and भेरी भेरी̆, f. A kettledrum, Pañc. 20, 7; Bhag. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्ड|भेरुंड|भेरुण्डं|भेरुण्डः
भेरुण्ड भेरुण्ड,<BR> I. (vb. भि), adj. Formidable.<BR> II. m. A form of Śiva.<BR> III. f. डा, One of the Yakṣiṇīs or female attendants on Durgā.<BR> IV. n. (vb. भृ), Conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेल|भेलं|भेलः
भेल भेल, i. e. भी + ल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b " target="_blank">Page0667-b + 41</a>] Timid.<BR> 2. Ignorant.<BR> 3. Tall.<BR> II. m.<BR> I. A raft.<BR> 2. The name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेष्
† भेष् भेष्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To fear (cf. भी, Caus.).<BR> 2. To go(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज|भेषजं
भेषज भेषज, i. e. भिषज् + अ (anomal.), n.<BR> 1. A medicine, a drug, a remedy, Pañc. ii. d. 59; Nal. 9, 30.<BR> 2. Help (against, gen.), Pañc. 184, 19.<BR> 3. A kind of fennel, Nigella indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष|भैक्षं
भैक्ष भैक्ष, and भैक्ष्य भैक्ष्य, i. e. भिक्षा + अ or य, n.<BR> 1. Begging, Man. 2, 48 (क्ष); Lass. 76, 4 (य).<BR> 2. Living by alms, Pañc. i. d. 312 (य).<BR> 3. What is collected by begging, alms, food, Man. 5, 129 (य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमी
भैमी भैमी, i. e. भीम (a proper name), + अ + ई, patronym., f. Damayantī, daughter of Bhīma, Nal. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरव|भैरवं|भैरवः
भैरव भैरव, i. e. भीरु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Formidable, horrid, Rām. 3, 50, 21.<BR> 2. Miserable, Rājat. 5, 408.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva, Rājat. 5, 55.<BR> 2. The name of a river.<BR> 3. A musical mode.<BR> III. f. वी, Durgā.<BR> IV. n. Horror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज|भैषजं|भैषजः
भैषज भैषज, i. e. भिषज् + अ,<BR> I. n. A medicament.<BR> II. m. (? ŚKD. n.), A sort of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज्य|भैषज्यं
भैषज्य भैषज्य, i. e. भिषज् + य,<BR> I. n. A medicament, a drug, Hit. i. d. 110, M.M.; a remedy.<BR> II. m. The descendant of a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भो
भो भो, curtailed भोस्, A vocative particle (properly, Sir!), O! Pañc. 44, 14; Ho! there! Pañc. 161, 17; also repeated, भोभो, Ho! ho! Pañc. 35, 12; 161, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तुकाम
भोक्तुकाम भोक्तुकाम, i. e. भोक्तुम् (vb. 2. भुज्), -काम, adj. Wishing to eat, Hiḍ. 3, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृ
भोक्तृ भोक्तृ, i. e. 2. भुज् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n. One who eats, Hit. i. d. 53, M.M.; or enjoys, Śāk. d. 43; Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 5.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An adverse possessor, Man. 8, 148.<BR> 2. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृत्व|भोक्तृत्वं
भोक्तृत्व भोक्तृ + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Enjoyment, perception, Bhag. 13, 20.<BR> 2. Possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग|भोगः
भोग भोग, i. e. 1. and 2. भुज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A snake's body, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 4.<BR> 2. A snake.<BR> 3. A snake's expanded hood, Pañc. ii. d. 131; feasting, Hit. army in column.<BR> 5. Nourishing, cherishing, food, Bhag. 2, 5.<BR> 6. Pleasure, Rām. 3, 53, 3.<BR> 7. Enjoyment, Bhartṛ. 2, 35; Pañc. ii. d. 131; feasting, Hit. ii. d. 99.<BR> 8. Adverse enjoyment (usufruct), Man. 8, 149.<BR> 9. Possession.<BR> 10. Wealth.<BR> 11. Hire.<BR> 12. The hire of dancing girls.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभोग
काम- + भोग काम- + भोग, m. sensual enjoyment, Rām. 3, 37, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागभोग
नाग- + भोग नाग- + भोग, m. a kind of snake, Rām. 5, 74, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भोग
निर्भोग निर्भ्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. not attached to pleasure, MBh. 12, 2332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगकर
भोगकर भोग-कर, adj., f. री, Affording enjoyment, Bhartṛ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवन्त्|भोगवत्
भोगवन्त् भोग + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Having enjoyment.<BR> 2. Delightful.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. Dancing.<BR> 3. Singing.<BR> III. f. वती,<BR> 1. The capital of the snakes, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 15.<BR> 2. The Gaṅgā of the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्ह
भोगार्ह भोगार्ह, i. e. भोग-अर्ह, n. Wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिक|भोगिकः
भोगिक भोगिक, i. e. भोग + इक, n. A groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
भोगिन् भोगिन्, i. e. भोग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Enjoying.<BR> 2. Abounding in enjoyments, Bhag. 16, 14.<BR> 3. Having enjoyments and an expanded [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b " target="_blank">Page0668-b + 43</a>] hood, Pañc. i. d. 73.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A snake, Bhartṛ. 2, 82.<BR> 2. A king, Hit. iii. d. 58.<BR> 3. The head man of a village.<BR> 4. A barber.<BR> 5. A person who accumulates money for a particular expenditure.<BR> III. f. नी.<BR> 1. The capital of the serpents.<BR> 2. A royal concubine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभोगिन्
कृष्ण- + भोगिन् कृष्ण- + भोगिन्, m. a sort of black snake, Gīt. 6, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज|भोजः
भोज भोज, i. e. भुज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A cowherd.<BR> 2. The name of a country.<BR> 3. The name of a king, Johns. Sel. 19, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजन|भोजनं|भोजनः
भोजन भोजन, i. e. 2. भुज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Enjoying, Pañc. 61, 22.<BR> 2. Eating, Pañc. 245, 22.<BR> 3. Food, Pañc. 138, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजन|अभोजनं
अ- + भोजन अ- + भोजन, n. abstaining from food, Man. 11, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभोजन|अतिभोजनं
अति- + भोजन अति- + भोजन, n. excessive eating, Man. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभोजन
एक- + भोजन एक- + भोजन, n. 1. eating once a day, MBh. 13, 5161. 2. eating in company, MBh. 13, 6238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिभोजन|कृमिभोजनः
कृमि- + भोजन कृमि- + भोजन,<BR> I. adj. one who feeds upon worms, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 18.<BR> II. m. the name of a hell, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजन|म्लेच्छभोजनं|म्लेच्छभोजनः
म्लेच्छ- + भोजन म्लेच्छ- + भोजन,<BR> I. m. wheat.<BR> II. n. halfripe barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभोजन|सहभोजनं
सह- + भोजन सह- + भोजन, n. eating with somebody, Lass. 18, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजस्
भोजस् भोजस्, i. e. 2. भुज् + अस् in विश्व-, adj. Yielding all the enjoyments, Lass. 101, 5 = Rigv. vii. 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजिन्
भोजिन् भोजिन्, i. e. 2. भुज् + इन्, adj. One who eats, Man. 4, 212.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभोजिन्
गृह- + भोजिन् गृह- + भोजिन्, m. a house-mate, Rājat. 5, 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजंगभोजिन्|भुजङ्गभोजिन्
भुजंग- + भोजिन् भुजंग- + भोजिन्, m. the boa constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पभोजिन्
शष्प- + भोजिन् शष्प- + भोजिन्, adj. sbst. a beast feeding on grass, Pañc. 25, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यता
भोज्यता भोज्य + ता (vb. 2. भुज्), f. Condition of being eaten, Pañc. 193, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलि|भोलिः
भोलि भोलि, m. A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोस्
भोस् भोस्, an old voc. sing. of भवन्त्.<BR> 1. A vocative particle, Man. 2, 124; Ho! there! repeated, भोभोस्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a " target="_blank">Page0669-a + 41</a>] O! Hit. 10, 6, M.M.<BR> 2. An interrogative particle, Vikr. 85, 20.<BR> 3. Interj. of grief, Oh! Hit. 71, 3, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजङ्ग|भौजंग
भौजङ्ग भौजङ्ग, i. e. भुजंग + अ, adj., f. गी, Like a snake, Pañc. iii. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत|भौतः
भौत भौत, i. e. भूत + अ (vb. भू),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to spirits, Man. 3, 70.<BR> 2. Demoniac.<BR> 3. Elemental.<BR> 4. Relating to existing beings.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An attendant upon idols.<BR> 2. A worshipper of sprites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिक|भौतिकं|भौतिकः
भौतिक भौतिक, i. e. भूत + इक (vb. भू),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating or appertaining to spirits, Man. 3, 174.<BR> 2. Elemental.<BR> 3. Existing.<BR> II. m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम भौम, i. e. भूमि + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the earth, rising from the ground, Man. 11, 155.<BR> 2. Terrestrial.<BR> 3. Relating to the planet Mars, Lass. 16, 16.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The planet Mars, Pañc. 50, 20.<BR> 2. Hell.<BR> III. f. मी, A name of Sītā.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भौम
अन्तर्- + भौम अन्तर्- + भौम, adj. being or living in the interior of the earth, Rām. 1, 42, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुभौम
बहु- + भौम बहु- + भौम, adj. having many stories.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तभौम
सप्त(न्)- + भौम सप्त(न्)- + भौम, adj. having seven stories, Rām. 5, 10, 11 (? cf. my translation of the Pañc. n. 208. and भूमिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिक|भौरिकः
भौरिक भौरिक, i. e. भूरि + इक, m. The superintendent of gold in a royal treasury (cf. भारिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्यस्
भ्यस् भ्यस्, i. 1, Ātm. To fear, to tremble (cf. भी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश्
भ्रंश् भ्रंश्, and (erroneously) भ्रंस् भ्रंस्, i. 4, भ्रश्य (cf. भ्रश्), भ्रस्य, Par. (also Ātm., e. g. Pañc. iv. d. 39), and † i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To fall, Sund. 1, 15; to fall down, Pañc. i. d. 146.<BR> 2. To be lost, Rām. 3, 54, 20.<BR> 3. To run away, to flee from [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-b " target="_blank">Page0669-b + 43</a>] (abl.), Bhaṭṭ. 14, 105.<BR> 4. To be deprived (with abl.), Man. 7, 111; Pañc. iv. d. 39 (with स् and Ātm.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भ्रष्ट.<BR> 1. Fallen, Hit. i. d. 168 (स्थान-, adj. Having lost their rank).<BR> 2. Lost.<BR> 3. Deprived of, Bhag. 6, 11.<BR> 4. Deviated, Pañc. 228, 14.<BR> 5. Fallen from virtue, wicked.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. भ्रंशय.<BR> 1. To expel, MBh. 3, 8759.<BR> 2. To deprive, MBh. 3, 1571. भ्रंशित, Deprived, Chr. 48, 2.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, अपभ्रष्ट, Corrupted (as speech), Kathās. 17, 41.<BR> --With परि परि, To be deprived (with abl.), Hit. i. d. 128. परिभ्रष्ट,<BR> 1. Fallen, Pañc. 188, 15.<BR> 2. Degraded.<BR> 3. Deprived of (instr.), Pañc. iii. d. 55; Man. 10, 20.<BR> 4. Lost, Nal. 18, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To fall, Ragh. 14, 54 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To be deprived, Mṛcch. 14, 12 (Calc.). प्रभ्रेष्ट,<BR> 1. Fallen, dropping, fallen off.<BR> 2. Broken.<BR> --Caus. To throw down from (abl.), Ragh. 13, 36 (Calc.). प्रभ्रंशित, Expelled, MBh. 3, 601.<BR> --With वि वि, विभ्रष्ट,<BR> 1. Broken off, or from.<BR> 2. Fallen.<BR> 3. Separated.<BR> 4. Deprived, MBh. 3, 3.<BR> 5. Lost.<BR> --Caus. To deprive, Chr. 21, 6.<BR> --Cf. A.S. hreósan and reosan, To fall; Goth. ur-risan; A.S. arisan, To rise; Goth. us-hrisjan and af-hrisjan (Caus.), To cast off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयभ्रष्ट|भयभ्रष्टः
भय- + भ्रष्ट भय- + भ्रष्ट, adj. put to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश|भ्रंशः
भ्रंश भ्रंश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Falling.<BR> 2. Declining from a height, or from propriety, ruin, Bhag. 2, 63.<BR> 3. Falling off, Megh. 2.<BR> 4. Abandoning, dropping, Pañc. iii. d. 246; desertion, Pañc. 145, 10.<BR> 5. Losing, Pañc. 68, 22; loss, Rājat. 5, 307; Hit. iii. d. 5 (स्थान-भ्रंशं ययुः, They did lose their nest).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंश|जातिभ्रंशः
जाति- + भ्रंश जाति- + भ्रंश, m. Loss of caste, Man. 11, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशिन्
भ्रंशिन् भ्रंश् + इन्, भ्रंसिन् भ्रंस् + इन्, adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Falling, Megh. 30; Śāk. 1, 7.<BR> 2. Causing to fall (स्व-अर्थ-, injuring, or detrimental to, our interest), Pañc. 248, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंशिन्
अ- + भ्रंशिन् अ- + भ्रंशिन्, adj. not falling, durable, Pañc. iii. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंस्
भ्रंस् भ्रंस्, भ्रंसिन् भ्रंसिन्, see भ्रंश्, भ्रंशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुंश|भ्रकुंशः
भ्रकुंश and ˚स भ्रकुंश, ˚स, see भृकुंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुटि|भ्रकुटिः
भ्रकुटि भ्रकुटि, see भ्रूकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रक्ष्
† भ्रक्ष् भ्रक्ष्, v. r. of भक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्ज्
भ्रज्ज् भ्रज्ज्, i. 6, भृज्ज, Par. Ātm. To boil or fry, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 86; the base of many forms in भर्ज्.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भृष्ट.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. frigere, frictus, frixus (= भृक्त, see भृज्); ϕρύγω; O.H.G. briuwan; A.S. briwan; and O.N. brugga, To brew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलभृष्ट
तिल- + भृष्ट तिल- + भृष्ट, n. fried grains of sesame, MBh. 13, 5025.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रण्
† भ्रण् भ्रण्, i. 1, Par. To sound (cf. भ्रम् and रण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रभङ्ग|भ्रभंग|भ्रभंगः|भ्रभङ्गः
भ्रभङ्ग भ्रभङ्ग, m. A frown (cf. भ्रू-भङ्ग, s. v. भङ्ग, and भ्रकुंश, भ्रकुटि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम्
भ्रम् भ्रम्, i. 1 and 4, भ्राम्य, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 12228), originally, The flying about and humming of insects.<BR> 1. To turn round, to move circularly, to whirl, Pañc. v. d. 20.<BR> 2. † To be unsteady or unfixed.<BR> 3. To stray, to roam, to wander, Pañc. 43, 4; i. d. 446; to go astray, Pañc. v. d. 68 (Ātm.).<BR> 4. To wander over (acc.), MBh. 1, 5184.<BR> 5. To surround, Rājat. 5, 146.<BR> 6. To mistake.<BR> 7. † To be ignorant.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. भ्रान्त.<BR> 1. Being wandered over (with acc.). Bhartṛ. 3, 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-b " target="_blank">Page0670-b + 43</a>]<BR> 2. Running, Arj. 4, 38; rolling, Chr. 35, 2.<BR> 3. Whirled.<BR> 4. Confused, Rām. 3, 55, 36.<BR> 5. Blundering. n. Roaming, Bhartṛ. 2, 11.<BR> --Caus. भ्रमय (in epic poetry also भ्रामय, also Pañc. 263, 8. or i. 4, Ātm.).<BR> 1. To turn round, Bhag. 18, 61; to whirl, MBh. 2, 762.<BR> 2. To move to and fro (without getting a way of egress), Rām. 1, 44, 12.<BR> 3. To agitate, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 8.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To jump out of (abl.), Draup. 8, 19.<BR> 2. To be beside one's self, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 17 (read उद्भ्रम्य). उद्-भ्रान्त,<BR> 1. Flying upward, Rām. 6, 83, 26.<BR> 2. Whirled on, thrown up, Hit. iii. d. 140.<BR> 3. Whirling on, Utt. Rāmac. 138, 4.<BR> 4. Bewildered, Pañc. 141, 4.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To walk round about, Pañc. 230, 16.<BR> 2. To roam about, Hit. 76, 6, M.M.; Pañc. 21, 1.<BR> 3. To fly round about, Pañc. 148, 10.<BR> --With वि वि, To rove, Nalod. 3, 26.<BR> 2. To wander over, MBh. 3, 2648.<BR> 3. † To play, to wanton. वि-भ्रान्त,<BR> 1. Agitated, Bhag. 16, 16.<BR> 2. Hurried.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With मस् सम्, संभ्रान्त, Agitated, confused, Utt. Rāmac. 50, 3; troubled, Śāk. 12, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. भ्रमर; Lat. fremere; O.H.G. breman; A.S. bremman; O.H.G. bremo, briosa; N.G. brausen; πεμϕρηδών, ϕριμάσσομαι, βρέμω, βροντή, βαϐράζω, βαϐραδών, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम्
अ- + भ्रम् अ- + भ्रम्, adj. not playing (?), unmoved, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम्
अ- + भ्रम् अ- + भ्रम्, adj. fearless, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंभ्रान्त
सु-संभ्रान्त सु-संभ्रान्त, adj. greatly bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम|भ्रमः
भ्रम भ्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Whirling, going round, Rājat. 5, 363.<BR> 2. Straying, roaming.<BR> 3. Error, Bhāṣāp. 133.<BR> 4. A whirlpool.<BR> 5. A watercourse.<BR> 6. A potter's wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमण|भ्रमणं
भ्रमण भ्रमण, i. e. भ्रम् + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a " target="_blank">Page0671-a + 42</a>]<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Whirling, turning round, Bhāṣāp. 6.<BR> 2. Giddiness, Lass. 17, 5.<BR> 3. Wandering, Vikr. 23, 11.<BR> II. f. णी,<BR> A sort of game performed by women for the amusement of a lover or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमर|भ्रमरः
भ्रमर भ्रम् + अर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A (large black) bee, Vikr. 64, 1.<BR> 2. A lover, a gallant.<BR> II. n. Epilepsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमि|भ्रमिः
भ्रमि भ्रम् + इ, f.<BR> 1. Going round, turning about, Utt. Rāmac. 66, 4.<BR> 2. A lathe, Kāśīkh. 17, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रश्
भ्रश् भ्रश्, i. 4, Par. To fall, impersonal pass., Śiś. 9, 73 (it was fallen by the mirror = the mirror fell); cf. भ्रंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टाधिकारत्व
भ्रष्टाधिकारत्व भ्रष्टाधिकारत्व, i. e. भ्रष्ट-अधिकार्च् + त्व (vb. भ्रंश्), n. Loss of office, Pañc. 22, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज्
भ्राज् भ्राज् (probably अभि-राज्), i. 1, Ātm. (in ved. and epic poetry also Par., MBh. 4, 219).<BR> 1. To shine, to beam, Chr. 289, 3 = Rigv. i. 50, 3 (Par.).<BR> --Caus. To illuminate, MBh. 3, 15579.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To shine brilliantly, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4; Rām. 3, 52, 25.<BR> --Cf. भृज्; Lat. flagrare, flamma (for flagma), flamen, fulgur, fulgere, fulmen, fulvus, etc.; Goth. bairhts; A.S. bearht, beorht; O.H.G. beraht, blanch, blich, blichan; ϕλέγω, ϕλόξ; probably also A.S. blác, blaecan, blícan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजदृष्टि
भ्राजदृष्टि भ्राजदृष्टि, i. e. भ्राजन्त्-ऋष्टि, adj. Having shining swords (i. e. lightnings), Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णु|भ्राजिष्णुः
भ्राजिष्णु भ्राज् + इष्णु, adj. Splendid, elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृ
भ्रातृ भ्रातृ, i. e. भृ + आ + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A brother, Chr. 3, 5; du. तरौ, Brother and sister.<BR> 2. A friend, Megh. 10. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b " target="_blank">Page0671-b + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. frater; ϕράτηρ and ϕρατήρ, ϕατρία, etc.; Goth. brothar; A.S. bródhor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भ्रातृ
दुर्भ्रातृ दुर्भ्˚, i. e. दुस्-, m. A wicked brother, MBh. 3, 996.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभ्रातृ|धर्म्मभ्रातृ
धर्म- + भ्रातृ धर्म- + भ्रातृ, m. an associate dwelling in the same religious retreat, Yājñ. 2, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्रातृ
स- + भ्रातृ स- + भ्रातृ or सह-, adj. with a brother, or with brethren, Johns. Sel. 54, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृव्य|भ्रातृव्यः
भ्रातृव्य भ्रातृ + व्य, m.<BR> 1.<BR> A brother's son.<BR> 2. An enemy.<BR> --Cf. Lat. fratrūelis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीय|भ्रात्रीयः
भ्रात्रीय भ्रात्रीय, i. e. भ्रातृ + ईय,<BR> I. adj. Fraternal.<BR> II. m. A brother's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्ति|भ्रांति|भ्रांतिः|भ्रान्तिः
भ्रान्ति भ्रान्ति, i. e. भ्रम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Going round, whirling, rolling, Vikr. d. 4.<BR> 2. Wandering.<BR> 3. Error, Bṛhaspati ap. Cowell, Kusumāñjali, transl. p. 65, n. †; Pañc. 50, 10 (कुमुद-भ्रान्तिं जनयति मत्स्यानाम्, Causes the fishes to mistake him for a lotusflower). चन्दन-, instr. Mistaking (it) for a sandal tree, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामक|भ्रामकः
भ्रामक भ्रामक, i. e. भ्रम्, Caus. + अक,<BR> I. adj. Causing to whirl.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cheat.<BR> 2. A jackal.<BR> 3. The sun-flower.<BR> 4. A sort of loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामर|भ्रामरं|भ्रामरः
भ्रामर भ्रामर, i. e. भ्रमर + अ,<BR> I. m. A sort of loadstone.<BR> II. f. री,<BR> 1. Pārvatī,<BR> 2. A female attendant on Durgā.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Honey.<BR> 2. Whirling round.<BR> 3. Epilepsy.<BR> 4. A kind of dancing.<BR> 5. A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरिन्
भ्रामरिन् भ्रामरिन्, i. e. भ्रामर + इन्, adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Made of honey.<BR> 2. Whirling.<BR> 3. Epileptic, Man. 3, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्
भ्राश् भ्राश्, and † म्रास् भ्रास्, † भ्राश् भ्लाश्, and † भ्रास् भ्लास्, i. 1. and 4, Ātm. To shine; cf. भ्राज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं|भ्राष्ट्रः
भ्राष्ट्र भ्राष्ट्र, i. e. भ्राज् + त्र (cf. भृज्),<BR> I. m. (and n.), A frying-pan, Pañc. i. d. 148.<BR> II. n. Æther.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रास्
भ्रास् भ्रास्, see भ्रश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्री
† भ्री भ्री, ii. 9, Par.<BR> 1. To fear.<BR> 2. To bear, to nourish; cf. भृ and भॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुंश|भ्रुकुंशः
भ्रुकुंश and ˚स भ्रुकुंश and ˚स, see भृकुंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुटि|भ्रुकुटिः
भ्रुकुटि भ्रुकुटि, see भ्रूकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुड्
† भ्रुड् भ्रुड्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To cover.<BR> 2. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुभङ्ग
भ्रुभङ्ग भ्रुभङ्ग = भ्रू-भङ्ग, see भङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुव
ऽभ्रुव -भ्रुव, i. e. भ्रू + अ, a substitute for भ्रू when latter part of comp. adj.; e. g. सु-नासा-अक्षि-भ्रुव, Endowed with handsome noses, eyes, and eyebrows, Nal. 5, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रू
भ्रू भ्रू, f. An eyebrow, Rām. 3, 52, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ὀϕρύς; O.H.G. brâwa; A.S. braew; Lat. frons, frontis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितभ्रू
अ-सित- + भ्रू अ-सित- + भ्रू, adj. having black eyebrows, Śiś. 9, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतभ्रू
नत- + भ्रू नत- + भ्रू (vb. नम्), adj. having arched brows, Vikr. d. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतभ्रू
सम्-हत- + भ्रू सम्-हत- + भ्रू, adj. knitting the brows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभ्रू
सु-भ्रू सु-भ्रू,<BR> I. adj. having fine brows, Vikr. d. 13.<BR> II. and सु-भ्रु, f. a woman, Lass. 90, 15 (ऊ); Sund. 4, 12 (ŭ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुंश|भ्रूकुंशः
भ्रूकुंश and ˚स भ्रूकुंश and ˚स, see भृकुंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुटि|भ्रूकुटिः
भ्रूकुटि and टी भ्रू-कुटी, or भ्रुकुटि, टी भ्रुकुटी̆, or भ्रकुटि भ्रकुटि, and भृकुटि, टी भृकुटी̆, f. A frown, MBh. 1, 4601 (भ्रू-); 7, 762 (भ्रु-); Pañc. 220, 1 (भृ˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण्
† भ्रूण् भ्रूण्, i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. To hope.<BR> 2. To wish.<BR> 3. To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण|भ्रूणः
भ्रूण भ्रूण, m. The embryo (cf. भ्रूणहन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणघ्न
भ्रूणघ्न भ्रूण-घ्न, adj., f. घ्नी, One who occasions or procures abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहन्
भ्रूणहन् भ्रूण-हन्, adj., f. घ्नी, One who occasions or produces abortion, Man. 4, 208; 8, 317 (Jones: At the first place as if he had read ब्रह्मघ्ना, the killer of a priest; at the second, थे किल्लेर् ओफ़् अ प्रिएस्त् or destroyer of an embryo).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेज्
† भ्रेज् भ्रेज्, i. 1, Ātm. To shine; cf. भ्राज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष्
† भ्रेष् भ्रेष्, i. 1, Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To go, to move.<BR> 2. To fear.<BR> 3. To be wrathful (cf. क्रेष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष|भ्रेषः
भ्रेष भ्रेष, m.<BR> 1. Deviation from rectitude (cf. भ्रंश).<BR> 2. Loss.<BR> 3. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लक्ष्
† भ्लक्ष् भ्लक्ष्, v. r. of भक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लाश्
भ्लाश् भ्लाश्, and भ्लास् भ्लास्, see भ्राश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लेष्
† भ्लेष् भ्लेष्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंह्
मंह् मंह्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To increase.<BR> 2. To give (ved.).<BR> --i. 10 and 1, Par. † To speak, to shine. Frequent. ved. मामक्, To grant, Chr. 298, 25 = Rigv. i. 112, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहना
मंहना मंहना, f. Liberality, Lass. 98, 2 (read मंहना) = Rigv. vi. 64, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकर|मकरः
मकर मकर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A marine [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a " target="_blank">Page0673-a + 39</a>] monster confounded usually with the crocodile and shark, but properly a fabulous animal, Johns. Sel. 28, 27; Pañc. 51, 9; iv. d. 1.<BR> 2. One of the signs of the zodiac.<BR> 3. A form of marching an army, Man. 7, 187.<BR> 4. One of Kuvera's treasures.<BR> II. f. री, The wife of the marine monster called मकर, Pañc. 206, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्द|मकरंदः|मकरन्दः
मकरन्द मकरन्द,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The nectar of a flower, Prab. 79, 16.<BR> 2. A kind of jasmine.<BR> II. m. The filament of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुर|मकुरः
मकुर मकुर, मकुल मकुल, see मुकुर, मुकुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठ|मकुष्ठः
मकुष्ठ मकुष्ठ,<BR> I. adj. Going slowly.<BR> II. m. A sort of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्क्
मक्क् मक्क्, see मस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कोल|मक्कोलः
मक्कोल मक्कोल, m. Chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष्
† मक्ष् मक्ष्, see म्रक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष मक्ष, m.<BR> 1. Hypocrisy.<BR> 2. Wrath.<BR> 3. Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षिका
मक्षिका and मक्षीका मक्षी̆का, f. A fly, Rām. 3, 53, 59.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. musca; O.H.G. mucca; A.S. micge; O.N. my; μυῖα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मक्षिक
निर्मक्षिक निर्मक्षिक, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from flies, untroubled, Śāk. 24, 18 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमक्षिका
मधु- + मक्षिका मधु- + मक्षिका, f. a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षु
मक्षु and ˚क्षू मक्षू̆ (properly loc. pl.), adv. Quickly, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख्
† मख् मख्, and मङ्ख् मङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख मख, m.<BR> 1. A warrior, Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR> 2. Sacrifice, oblation, Draup. 2, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μάχομαι, μάχαιρα, μάκελον, μαῖμαξ (from a frequent.), μαιμάκτης, μαιμακτήρια; Lat. macellum, mactare, mucro, maceria; A.S. méce; O.N. moekir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमख
सु- + मख सु- + मख, adj. probably well fighting, a powerful warrior, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. i. 85, 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b " target="_blank">Page0673-b + 39</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ख्
† मङ्ख् मङ्ख्, see मख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध मगध,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a country, Hit. 36, 10, M.M.<BR> 2. An inhabitant of that country.<BR> 3. A bard.<BR> II. f. धा, Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ मघ (cf. मह्),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Power, wealth (ved.).<BR> 2. A kind of flower.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One of the Dvīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR> 2. Pleasure.<BR> III. f. घा (usually pl.), The tenth lunar asterism, Man. 3, 273; Sund. 2, 2.<BR> IV. f. घा or घी, A sort of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवन्
मघवन् मघवन्, a curtailed form of the next.<BR> I. adj., f. घोनी, Wealthy, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR> II. m. Indra, Vikr. 86, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवन्त्|मघवत्
मघवन्त् मघ + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj. Wealthy. m. A sacrificer, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR> II. m. Indra, Vikr. 88, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्|मंक्
मङ्क् मङ्क्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 10.<BR> 2. † To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कुर|मंकुर|मंकुरः|मङ्कुरः
मङ्कुर मङ्कुर, m. A mirror; cf. मुकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तृ
मङ्क्तृ मङ्क्तृ, i. e. मज्ज् + त्रि, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Bathing or drowning.<BR> 2. Cleaning by immersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षु|मंक्षु
मङ्क्षु मङ्क्षु, ind. (= नक्षु),<BR> 1. Quickly, instantly.<BR> 2. Much, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षुण|मंक्षुण|मङ्क्षुणं
मङ्क्षुण मङ्क्षुण, n. Armour for the thighs or legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ग्|मंग्
† मङ्ग् i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ग|मंग|मंगः|मङ्गः
मङ्ग मङ्ग, m. The head of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल|मंगल|मङ्गलं|मङ्गलः
मङ्गल मङ्गल,<BR> I. adj. Lucky, propitious, Man. 2, 34; brave, Pañc. 8, 15.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Prosperity, welfare, Ṛt. 6, 34; bliss, Utt. Rāmac. 89, 4.<BR> 2. Rejoicing, a festival, Pañc. 129, 17; solemnity, Vikr. d. 43 (सन्ध्या-, Evening service).<BR> 3. Blessing, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 10; Sund. 2, 4; prayer, ib. 188, 22.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The planet Mars.<BR> 2. Burnt offering on various occasions of rejoicing.<BR> IV. f. ला.<BR> 1. Umā, the wife of Śiva.<BR> 2. A sort of bent grass, Panicum dactylon.<BR> V. n. Turmeric, Vikr. d. 53 (Sch.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
अ- + मङ्गल अ- + मङ्गल,<BR> I. adj. inauspicious, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 23.<BR> II. n. ill luck, Kumāras. 5, 65; evil omen, Śāk. 63, 13.<BR> III. m. the castor-oil plant, Ricinus communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकमङ्गल|कौतुकमंगल
कौतुक- + मङ्गल कौतुक- + मङ्गल, n. a solemn ceremony, Pañc. 129, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानमङ्गल
पान- + मङ्गल पान- + मङ्गल, n. a banquet, Kathās. 36, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वमङ्गल
सर्व- + मङ्गल सर्व- + मङ्गल, f. ला, Durgā, Hit. 99, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमङ्गल
सु- + मङ्गल सु- + मङ्गल, adj. very fortunate or auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्य|मंगल्य|मङ्गल्यं|मङ्गल्यः
मङ्गल्य मङ्गल्य, i. e. मङ्गल + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Auspicious, conferring happiness, Utt. Rāmac. 99, 1.<BR> 2. Beautiful.<BR> 3. Pious, pure, implying holiness, Man. 2, 31.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The holy fig-tree, Ficus religiosa.<BR> 2. A sort of pulse or lentils.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Sour curds.<BR> 2. Sandal.<BR> 3. Red lead.<BR> 4. Gold.<BR> 5. Water brought from various holy places for the consecration of a king.<BR> IV. f. या. The name of several plants, Agallocum, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गिनी|मंगिनी
मङ्गिनी मङ्गिनी, i. e. मङ्ग + इन् + ई, f. A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्घ्|मंघ्
† मङ्घ् मङ्घ्, i. 1, Par. To adorn.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To begin moving.<BR> 3. To begin.<BR> 4. To move swiftly.<BR> 5. To blame.<BR> 6. To cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्
† मच् मच्, मञ्च् मञ्च्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-b " target="_blank">Page0674-b + 42</a>] मुच् मुच्, and मुञ्च् मुञ्च्,<BR> 1. To cheat, to be wicked.<BR> 2. To boast, to be vain.<BR> 3. To pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचर्चिका|मचर्च्चिका
मचर्चिका मचर्चिका, f. Excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्ज्
मज्ज् मज्ज् (probably मद्-जन्; cf. मद्गु and Lat. mergere; the Indian grammarians write मस्ज्), i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 2, 605). The base of many forms is मञ्ज्.<BR> 1. To dive, Bhartṛ. 2, 91.<BR> 2. To bathe, MBh. 1, 5299.<BR> 3. To sink, Vikr. d. 133; to perish in water, Rām. 1, 1, 89.<BR> 4. To sink into, MBh. 1, 3717 (loc.); Man. 4, 81 (acc.).<BR> 5. To be plunged, Man. 10, 91.<BR> 6. To become disheartened, MBh. 1, 5631.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मग्न,<BR> 1. Plunged, Hit. i. d. 4, M.M.; dived, immersed, Rām. 3, 52, 19.<BR> 2. Sunk, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 6; drowned, Chr. 17, 27.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to plunge, MBh. 1, 3908.<BR> 2. To overwhelm, Rām. 2, 77, 13.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To emerge, Śāk. d. 167.<BR> 2. Pass. impers. To rise, Śiś. 9, 30.<BR> --Caus. To force up, Man. 8, 115.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To bathe, Man. 5, 73.<BR> 2. To submerge, to sink under, Man. 4, 194; Hit. ii. d. 145.<BR> 3. To disappear, MBh. 2, 1504.<BR> 4. To cause to sink (into hell), MBh. 1, 4156. निमग्न,<BR> 1. Plunged in, immersed, Rājat. 5, 85.<BR> 2. Sunk in (not prominent), Vikr. d. 80; Rājat. 5, 74; slender, d. 129.<BR> 3. Covered, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 6.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to dive under water, Man. 8, 114.<BR> 2. To cause to be submerged, MBh. 3, 16612.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्र-मग्न, Immersed, drowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जकृत्
मज्जकृत् मज्जकृत्, i. e. मज्जन्-कृ + त्, n. A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन्
मज्जन् मज्जन् (perhaps for original [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a " target="_blank">Page0675-a + 39</a>] मर्जन्; cf. O.H.G. marag; A.S. mearh, mearg, merg), m.<BR> 1. The marrow of the bones and flesh.<BR> 2. The pith or sap of trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जा
मज्जा मज्जा (cf. the last), f. The marrow of the bones and flesh. Pañc. i. d. 191, cf. my translation, n. 171.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मज्ज
निर्मज्ज निर्मज्ज, i. e. निस्-, adj. marrowless, Hariv. 14533.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन|मज्जनं|मज्जनः
मज्जन मज्ज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Immersion.<BR> 2. Bathing.<BR> 3. Drowning, Pañc. i. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जूषा
मज्जूषा मज्जूषा = मञ्जूषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्मन्
मज्मन् मज्मन्, n. Strength, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. i. 64, 3.<BR> --Cf. Lat. magmentum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च्|मंच्
मञ्च् मञ्च्, i. 1, Ātm. †<BR> 1. To hold.<BR> 2. † To grow high or tall.<BR> 3. † To adore.<BR> 4. † To shine.<BR> --Cf. मच् and म्लुञ्च्.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, To purify, Naiṣ. 7, 43.<BR> --Cf. मृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च|मंच|मंचः|मञ्चः
मञ्च मञ्च, m.<BR> 1. A bedstead.<BR> 2. A scaffold, Johns. Sel. 9, 12.<BR> 3. A chair, Ragh. 6, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्ज्|मंज्
मञ्ज् मञ्ज्, see मार्ज् (Lass. 74, 4. read मज्जत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जर|मंजर|मंजरं|मञ्जरं
मञ्जर मञ्जर, n., and f. री,<BR> 1. A pearl.<BR> 2. A creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरि|मंजरि|मंजरिः|मञ्जरिः
मञ्जरि and मञ्जरी मञ्जरी̆, f.<BR> 1. = मञ्जर, Rām. 6, 15, 7 (pearl).<BR> 2. A shoot, sprout, Vikr. d. 26, 76 (मञ्जरी-चामर, A fan-like sprout).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममञ्जरि
काम-, मदन- + मञ्जरि काम-, मदन- + मञ्जरि, and राग-मञ्जरी, f. proper names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनमञ्जरि
काम-, मदन- + मञ्जरि काम-, मदन- + मञ्जरि, and राग-मञ्जरी, f. proper names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभमञ्जरी
लोभ-मञ्जरी लोभ-मञ्जरी, f. used instead of काममञ्जरी, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 21 (the pearl of covetousness.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरीपिञ्जरित
मञ्जरीपिञ्जरित मञ्जरीपिञ्जरित, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b " target="_blank">Page0675-b + 38</a>] i. e. मञ्जरी-पिञ्जर + इत, adj. Adorned with pearls and gold, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जा|मंजा
मञ्जा मञ्जा, f., मञ्जि मञ्जि, m., and मञ्जी मञ्जी, f. A creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिका|मंजिका
मञ्जिका मञ्जि + का, f. A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठा|मंजिष्ठा
मञ्जिष्ठा मञ्जिष्ठा, properly superl. of मञ्जु, f. Bengal madder, Rubia manjith Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जीर|मंजीर|मंजीरं|मंजीरः|मञ्जीरः
मञ्जीर मञ्जीर,<BR> I. m. and n. An ornament for the feet.<BR> II. m. A post round which passes the string that works the stick of a churn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जु|मंजु
मञ्जु मञ्जु (based on मञ्ज्, a form of मृज्), adj. Beautiful, Vikr. 60, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुल|मंजुल|मञ्जुलं|मञ्जुलः
मञ्जुल मञ्जु + ल,<BR> I. adj. Beautiful.<BR> II. m. A gallinule.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A bower.<BR> 2. A watercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जूषा|मंजूषा
मञ्जूषा मञ्जूषा, f.<BR> 1. A basket, Kathās. 4, 74.<BR> 2. A receptacle, Rām. 1, 67, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ्
† मठ् मठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To inhabit.<BR> 2. To grind.<BR> 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ|मठं|मठः
मठ मठ, m.<BR> 1. A school.<BR> 2. A building inhabited by ascetics, a cloister, a college, Pañc. 116, 18.<BR> 3. A temple.<BR> 4. A carriage.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालमठ
गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ, m. colleges called ‘that of गोपाल’ ‘that of चक्र (-वर्मन्),’ ‘of शूर,’ Rājat. 5, 243; 403; 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमठ
गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ, m. colleges called ‘that of गोपाल’ ‘that of चक्र (-वर्मन्),’ ‘of शूर,’ Rājat. 5, 243; 403; 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमठ
गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ गोपाल-, चक्र-, शूर- + मठ, m. colleges called ‘that of गोपाल’ ‘that of चक्र (-वर्मन्),’ ‘of शूर,’ Rājat. 5, 243; 403; 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठर|मठरः
मठर मठर,<BR> I. adj. Intoxicated.<BR> II. m. The name of a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मडव
मडव मडव, or मडवराज्य मडव-राज्य, n. The name of a district in Kashmir, Rājat. 5, 84; 302; 446.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्डु|मड्डुः
मड्डु मड्डु, m.<BR> A sort of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्
मण् मण्, i. 1, Par. To sound, to murmur.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मणित, Nalod. 2, 60. n. A murmuring sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणि|मणिः
मणि मणि, m. and f., and मणी मणी, f.<BR> 1. A precious stone, a jewel, Vikr. d. 40.<BR> 2. A pearl, Vikr. d. 51.<BR> 3. Fleshy processes hanging from the neck of a goat.<BR> 4. A waterpot.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमणि|इन्दुमणिः
इन्दु- + मणि इन्दु- + मणि and चन्द्र-, m. a fabulous stone, moon-stone, Śiś. 9, 35; Rājat. 6, 296; Utt. Rāmac. 23, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमणि|काचमणिः
काच- + मणि काच- + मणि, m. crystal, Hit. pr. d. 44, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तामणि|चिंतामणि|चिन्तामणिः
चिन्ता- + मणि चिन्ता- + मणि, m. a fabulous gem, the possessor of which may get all he wishes for, Hariv. 8702.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडामणि|चूडामणिः
चूडा- + मणि चूडा- + मणि, m. a jewel worn in a crest or diadem, Hit. i. d. 211, M.M. (चन्द्र-अर्ध-, adj. having the crescent for his crestjewel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुमणि|जतुमणिः
जतु- + मणि जतु- + मणि, m. a mole, Suśr. 1, 92, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिमणि|मसिमणिः
मसि- + मणि मसि- + मणि, m. an inkstand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामणि|लतामणिः
लता- + मणि लता- + मणि, m. coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलमणि|विमलमणिः
वि-मल- + मणि वि-मल- + मणि, m. crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखामणि|शिखामणिः
शिखा- + मणि शिखा- + मणि, m. a jewel worn on the head, Vikr. d. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमणि|शुचिमणिः
शुचि- + मणि शुचि- + मणि, m. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पमणि|सर्पमणिः
सर्प- + मणि सर्प- + मणि, m. the snake-stone, or carbuncle, a jewel said to be found in the head of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमणि
सित- + मणि सित- + मणि, m. crystal, Megh. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यमणि|सूर्यमणिः|सूर्य्यमणि|सूर्य्यमणिः
सूर्य- + मणि सूर्य- + मणि, m. 1. the sun-stone. 2. a tree, Hibiscus phœniceus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणि|स्पर्शमणिः
स्पर्श- + मणि स्पर्श- + मणि, m. the philosopher's stone, converting everything it touches to gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिक|मणिकं|मणिकः
मणिक मणि + क,<BR> I. m. A precious stone, a jewel.<BR> II. n. A small waterpot, Pārask. in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. xxi. n. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकार|मणिकारः
मणिकार मणि-कार, m. A jeweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमय
मणिमय मणि-मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of jewels, Megh. 65.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमणिमय
सित-मणि + मय सित-मणि + मय, adj. made of crystal, Megh. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीचक|मणीचकं|मणीचकः
मणीचक मणीचक, m.<BR> 1. The kingfisher.<BR> 2. The moon-stone, a fabulous stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीवक|मणीवकं
मणीवक मणीवक, n. A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ठ्|मंठ्
† मण्ठ् मण्ठ्, i. 1, Ātm. To remember with regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड्|मंड्
मण्ड् मण्ड् (akin to मद्, मन्द्, probably a denomin. based on a lost signification of मन्द्र), † i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To dress.<BR> 2. To divide.<BR> --† i. 1, Par. To adorn one's self.<BR> --i. 10, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 7572),<BR> 1. To adorn, Pañc. 255, 16.<BR> 2. † To exhilarate.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मण्डित, Adorned, Chr. 29, 31; Pañc. 51, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्डित
अ- + मण्डित अ- + मण्डित, adj. not adorned, Nal. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड|मंडं|मण्डं|मंडः|मण्डः
मण्ड मण्ड् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Ornament.<BR> 2. The castor-oil tree, Palma christi.<BR> II. m. (and n.).<BR> 1. Scum, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 7.<BR> 2. Pith.<BR> 3. The head, Lass. 4, 18.<BR> III. f. डा.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 2. Emblic myrobalan.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिमण्ड|दधिमंड|दधिमण्डः
दधि- + मण्ड दधि- + मण्ड, m. Whey, Bhāg. P. 5, 1, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डक|मंडकः|मण्डकः
मण्डक मण्ड + क, m. A kind of pastry, Pañc. 245, 24 (see my translation, n. 1387).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डन|मंडन|मण्डनं|मण्डनः
मण्डन मण्ड् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Dressing, Pañc. 116, 21 (of the idols).<BR> 2. Ornament, Vikr. d. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डप|मंडपः|मण्डपः
मण्डप मण्ड-प (vb. पा), m. (and n.).<BR> 1. A shed or hall erected on festival occasions, as marriages, and adorned with flowers, Pañc. 129, 17.<BR> 2. An open temple.<BR> 3. A bower, Megh. 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणमण्डप|अधिकरणमण्डपः
अधिकरण- + मण्डप अधिकरण- + मण्डप, a court of justice, Mṛcch. 138, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिमण्डप
केलि- + मण्डप केलि- + मण्डप, m. and n. a pleasure-house, Śāntiś. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भमण्डप|गर्भमंडप|गर्भमण्डपः
गर्भ- + मण्डप गर्भ- + मण्डप, m. the haram, Kathās. 26, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटमण्डप|पटमंडप|पटमण्डपः
पट- + मण्डप पट- + मण्डप, m. and n. a tent, Ragh. 5, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामण्डप|लतामंडप|लतामण्डपः
लता- + मण्डप लता- + मण्डप, m. or n. an arbour, Śāk. 32, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डपिका|मंडपिका
मण्डपिका मण्डपिका, i. e. मण्डप + क, f. A small shop, Hit. 115, 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डयन्त|मंडयंतः|मण्डयन्तः
मण्डयन्त मण्डयन्त् + अ (vb. मण्ड्), m. An ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डल|मंडल|मण्डलं|मण्डलः
मण्डल मण्डल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A sort of sacrifice.<BR> 2. A kind of snake.<BR> 3. A dog.<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. A circle, Utt. Rāmac. 66, 4.<BR> 2. Walking round, Sund. 3, 22; 24.<BR> 3. Bent grass.<BR> 4. A nest, Daśak. 151, 6.<BR> III. n. (and m.).<BR> 1. A circle, Vikr. d. 140; Pañc. 230, 18; a globe, a ball, Pañc. 157, 25.<BR> 2. The disk of the sun or moon, Pañc. 160, 23.<BR> 3. The halo round the sun.<BR> 4. A wheel, Utt. Rāmac. 141, 3.<BR> 5. A heap, a multitude, Pañc. iii. d. 224; Ṛt. 1, 10 (at the end of a comp. adj.); a troop, Rājat. 5, 379.<BR> 6. A district, a province, Rājat. 5, 146; an empire, ib. 155, 262.<BR> 7. Surrounding countries, Man. 7, 154.<BR> 8. A form of array, an army drawn up in a circle, Pañc. 9, 14.<BR> 9. Twelve great empires, into which the whole of India is said to have been divided in old times.<BR> 10. A sort of leprosy with circular spots.<BR> 11. A sort of mystical, diagram, Hit. 59, 22; Lass. 13, 18(?).<BR> 12. A sort of perfume, Lass. 20, 20 (? corr. perhaps मण्डन, cf. मण्डन and गज-मण्डन, s. v. भूति).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शमण्डल|आदर्शमण्डलः
आदर्श- + मण्डल आदर्श- + मण्डल, 1. the reflection of a mirror, Kir. 5, 41. 2. a kind of snake, Suśr. 2, 265, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रममण्डल
आश्रम- + मण्डल आश्रम- + मण्डल, n. the dwelling-place of anchorites, Nal. 12, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मातलमण्डल
क्ष्मा-तल- + मण्डल क्ष्मा-तल- + मण्डल, m. or n. the terrestrial globe, earth, Lass. 68, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमण्डला
त्रि-मण्डला त्रि-मण्डला, f. a poisonous kind of spider, Suśr. 2, 269, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मण्डल|दिङ्मंडल
दिङ्-मण्डल दिङ्-मण्डल, i. e. दिश्-, n.<BR> 1. all the quarters of the world, Bhartṛ. 3, 71. 2. the compass-card.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिमण्डल|प्रकृतिमंडल
प्रकृति- + मण्डल प्रकृति- + मण्डल, n. the whole empire, Ragh. 9, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमण्डल
रङ्ग- + मण्डल रङ्ग- + मण्डल, n. the circuit of an assembled throng.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यमण्डल|सूर्यमंडल|सूर्य्यमण्डल|सूर्य्यमण्डलं
सूर्य- + मण्डल सूर्य- + मण्डल, m. or n. the disk of the sun, Sāv. 7, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमण्डल
स्तन- + मण्डल स्तन- + मण्डल, n. the balls of the female bosom, Ṛt. 1, 8; Lass. 80, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलय
मण्डलय मण्डलय, a denomin. derived from the preceeding; with परि परि, in the ptcple. pf. pass. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b " target="_blank">Page0677-b + 42</a>] परिमण्डलित, Turned round, Kir. 5, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलिन्|मंडलिन्
मण्डलिन् मण्डलिन्, i. e. मण्डल + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूक|मंडूकः|मण्डूकः
मण्डूक मण्डूक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A frog, Pañc. 197, 21.<BR> 2. A flower, Bignonia indica.<BR> II. f. की, A female frog.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपमण्डूक
कूप- + मण्डूक कूप- + मण्डूक, m. a frog in a well, applied to a person of no enterprise, one who never leaves his home, Hit. 82, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूर|मंडूरं|मण्डूरं
मण्डूर मण्डूर, m. and n. Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्
मत् मत्, see 2. मद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतंग|मतङ्ग|मतंगः|मतङ्गः
मतंग मतंग, i. e. मत (vb. मन्), + म्-ग, m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. An elephant. Hiḍ. 1, 13.<BR> 3. A proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 19, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतंगज|मतङ्गज|मतंगजः|मतङ्गजः
मतंगज मतंग-ज, m. An elephant, Mālav. 32, 6; Kir. 5, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतल्लिका
मतल्लिका मतल्लिका, f. Excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मति|मतिः
मति मति, i. e. मन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Mind, Pañc. iii. d. 76.<BR> 2. Understanding, Pañc. 251, 6; intelligence, Hit. pr. d. 42.<BR> 3. Thought, Pañc. iii. d. 258; resolution, Pañc. 216, 14.<BR> 4. Hymn, Chr. 292, 2 = Rigv. i. 86, 2.<BR> 5. Perception, Bhāṣāp. 126.<BR> 6. Opinion, Chr. 13, 13.<BR> 7. Advice.<BR> 8. Wish.<BR> 9. Recollection.<BR> 10. Respect.<BR> 11. A potherb.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mens, mentis, mentio, mentiri, mendax; Goth. ga-munds, môds; A.S. mod, ge-mynd; μῆτις (ved. -माति), μοῦσα, i. e. μαν + τία (= ved. मति, hymn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अ- + मति अ- + मति, f. 1. not knowing (instr. unknowingly), Man. 4, 222. 2. glimmer, image, Chr. 290, 9 = Rigv. i. 64, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमति
एक- + मति एक- + मति,<BR> I. f. direction of the mind on one object, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 21.<BR> II. adj. unanimous, MBh. 12, 12723. See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमति
कृत- + मति कृत- + मति, adj. resolved, MBh. 13, 2211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मति|दुर्म्मति
दुर्मति दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. 1. foolish, Hit. ii. d. 48. 2. wicked, Man. 11, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दितमति
निन्दित- + मति निन्दित- + मति (vb. निन्द्), adj. base-minded, Hit. i. d. 152, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहंमति
निरहंमति निरहंमति, i. e. निस्-अहम्-, adj. free from selfishness, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नमति|प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः
प्रत्युत्-पन्न- + मति प्रत्युत्-पन्न- + मति, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a " target="_blank">Page0678-a + 43</a>] i. e. प्रति-उद्-पन्न (vb. पद्), adj. ready-minded, Śāk. 67, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमति|बहुमतिः
बहु- + मति बहु- + मति, f. estimation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दमति|मंदमति
मन्द- + मति मन्द- + मति, adj. foolish, Pañc. 229, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामति|महामतिः
महा- + मति महा- + मति, adj. highminded, Chr. 6, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथामति
यथा-मति यथा-मति, adv. according to one's understanding or intellect, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
वि- + मति वि- + मति, f. 1. difference of opinion. 2. dislike, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमानमति
विद्यमान- + मति विद्यमान- + मति (vb. विद्), adj. having understanding, Pañc. i. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलमति
विपुल- + मति विपुल- + मति, adj. endowed with great understanding, Pañc. i. d. 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथामति
वृथा- + मति वृथा- + मति, adj. foolish, MBh. 2, 865.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमति|सुमतिः
सु- + मति सु- + मति,<BR> I. f. kindness.<BR> II. adj. very wise, Pañc. 25, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिमन्त्|मतिमत्
मतिमन्त् मति-मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Sensible, intelligent, wise, Pañc. ii. d. 20; Hit. i. d. 127, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्क|मत्कः
मत्क मत्क,<BR> 1. i. e. 2. मद् + क, adj. Mine.<BR> 2. m. A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुण|मत्कुणः
मत्कुण मत्कुण,<BR> 1. A bug (cf. मत्क), Pañc. iii. d. 105.<BR> 2. A flea.<BR> 3. An elephant without tusks.<BR> 4. A beardless man.<BR> 5. A buffalo.<BR> 6. Armour for the thighs or legs.<BR> 6. A cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्य|मत्यं
मत्य मत्य, n. The handle of a sickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर मत्सर, probably 2. मअ-सृ + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Envious, hostile, Utt. Rāmac. 133, 13.<BR> 2. Niggardly.<BR> 3. Wicked.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Envy, Śiś. 9, 63; Man. 3, 231.<BR> 2. Jealousy, Mālav. 55, 8.<BR> 3. Anger, passion.<BR> III. f. रा, A gnat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मत्सर
निर्मत्सर निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्- and वि-. adj. free from envy, passion, Lass. 85, 9 (निस्-); 49, 10 (वि-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतमत्सर
वीत- + मत्सर वीत- + मत्सर, i. e. वि-इत- (vb. इ), adj. free from envy, Indr. 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्सर
स- + मत्सर स- + मत्सर, adj. envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरिन्
मत्सरिन् मत्सरिन्, i. e. मत्सर + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b " target="_blank">Page0678-b + 40</a>] adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Envious, Man. 2, 201.<BR> 2. Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य मत्स्य, i. e. 1. मद् + स्य,<BR> 1. m. A fish, Man. 1, 39.<BR> 2. A particular fish, probably the सफरी.<BR> 3. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR> 4. The name of a country, Man. 2, 19; 7, 193.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकमत्स्य|पाकमत्स्यः
पाक- + मत्स्य पाक- + मत्स्य, m. 1. a particular fish, Suśr. 1, 206, 17. 2. a poisonous kind of insect, ib. 2, 288, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यक
मत्स्यक मत्स्य + क, m. A fish, Matsyop. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डी|मत्स्यंडी
मत्स्यण्डी मत्स्यण्डी, and मत्स्यण्डिका मत्स्यण्डिका, i. e. मत्स्यण्डी + क, f. The juice of the sugar-cane, unrefined, Mālav. 30, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याद
मत्स्याद मत्स्याद, i. e. मत्स्य-अद् + अ, adj. Feeding on fishes, Pañc. 50, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्
मथ् मथ्, † i. 1, Par., मन्थ् मन्थ्, ii. 9, मथ्ना, मथ्नी, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 1120), and † i. 1, Par., and † मान्थ् मान्थ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To churn, Kir. 5, 30.<BR> 2. To produce by churning.<BR> 3. To agitate (mentally), MBh. 1, 3330.<BR> 4. To crush, Pañc. 162, 18; to hurt, to kill.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मथित.<BR> 1. Churned.<BR> 2. Stirred.<BR> 3. Distressed, Megh. 81 (faded).<BR> 4. Agitated, Pañc. i. d. 247.<BR> 5. Destroyed, MBh. 1, 7669.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To agitate, Rām. 2, 26, 2.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To agitate, MBh. 3, 14227.<BR> 2. To cut off, MBh. 3, 10267.<BR> 3. To kill, Pañc. ii. d. 34.<BR> --With नि नि, To annoy, to hurt, Rām. 3, 54, 28.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To churn, to agitate, MBh. 1, 1120.<BR> 2. To shake out, MBh. 1, 6547.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To trample down, to bruise, MBh. 3, 16435.<BR> 2. To annoy, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a " target="_blank">Page0679-a + 44</a>] MBh. 1, 194.<BR> 3. To rob (ved.).<BR> 4. To cut off, MBh. 3, 10267. प्रमथित,<BR> 1. Well churned.<BR> 2. Trampled down.<BR> 3. Pained. n. Butter-milk without water.<BR> --Absolut. प्रमथ्य, Forcibly, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 17.<BR> --Caus. माथय, To annoy, MBh. 3, 8769. प्रमाथित, Ravished, violated, forcibly carried off.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To agitate, MBh. 1, 4876.<BR> --With वि वि, To destroy, MBh. 3, 12258.<BR> --Cf. μάτος, ματεύω, μανθάνω, Προμηθεύς, μόθος, and see मथिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन|मथनं|मथनः
मथन मथ् + अन, n. Churning, Pañc. v. d. 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरमथन|पुरमथनः
पुर- + मथन पुर- + मथन, m. the destroyer of Pura, a name of Śiva, Lass. 67, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमथन|मधुमथनः
मधु- + मथन मधु- + मथन, m. the destroyer of Madhu, a name of Viṣṇu, Lass. 71, 6; Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38 (Burnouf, ‘qui produis le nectar’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिन्
मथिन् मथ् + इन्, the bases of some cases are मन्थन् and मथ्, m.<BR> 1. A churning-stick, MBh. 1, 1124.<BR> 2. The penis.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mentula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरा
मथुरा मथुरा, f.<BR> A district and city now called Muttra, Pañc. 8, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
1. मद् मद्, ved. i. 1, Par.; i. 4, माद्य, Par. (originally, to be wet).<BR> 1. To get drunk (ved.).<BR> 2. To be glad, to rejoice, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1; MBh. 1, 4688.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मत्ल.<BR> 1. Drunk, a drunkard, Man. 9, 78.<BR> 2. Intoxicated, Hit. iv. d. 55; with love, Ṛt. 6, 14; with pride, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 20.<BR> 3. Mad, Rām. 3, 55, 36; furious, Hit. i. d. 34, M.M.; being in rut (as an elephant), Rām. 3, 52, 46.<BR> 4. Pleased. m.<BR> 1. An elephant in rut.<BR> 2. A buffalo.<BR> 3. The Indian cuckoo.<BR> 4. The thorn apple. f. ता, Vinous liquor.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. मादय.<BR> 1. To intoxicate.<BR> 2. To exhilarate, MBh. 3, 10678.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. To rejoice, Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 15. 6.<BR> II. मदय,<BR> 1. To exhilarate. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b " target="_blank">Page0679-b + 43</a>]<BR> 2. To be satisfied, MBh. 1, 4736.<BR> 3. † To doze, to be sluggish.<BR> --With अनु अनु in अनुमत्त, Cured from insanity, again sane, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 14.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To be mad, MBh. 3, 14503. उन्मत्त,<BR> 1. Drunk.<BR> 2. Insane, Rām. 3, 55, 8; furious, Hit. ii. d. 116; Utt. Rāmac. 42, 16; a lunatic, Man. 3, 161; Pañc. iii. d. 67. m. The thorn apple.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. मादय, उन्मादित, Caused to be mad, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 16.<BR> II. मदय, उन्मदित, The same, ib. 191, 18 (read ˚माद्˚).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To stray from (with abl.).<BR> 2. To be negligent, careless, unguarded, Man. 2, 213.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pres. अ-प्रमाद्यन्त्, Being careful, MBh. 12, 3996. प्रमत्त,<BR> 1. Careless, Hit. ii. d. 104.<BR> 2. Intoxicated.<BR> 3. Insane, furious, Chr. 35, 6; being in rut, Pañc. 80, 6.<BR> 4. Addicted to gaming, Man. 9, 78.<BR> 5. Mad with desire, 4, 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. careful, watchful, Pañc. 88, 19.<BR> --With वि वि, विमत्त, Ruttish, Kir. 5, 47.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संमत्त, Intoxicated with love, Sund. 4, 17; cf. 12; see मन्द्.<BR> --Cf. Lat. madidus, madere, manare (for mad + no, denomin.); μαδός, μαδάω, μαδαρός; probably Goth. mats; A.S. maete; Goth. matjan; μασάομαι; Lat. mandere; A.S. maetan, To dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतमत्त|मृतमत्तः
मृत- + मत्त मृत- + मत्त, m. a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
2. मद् मद् (or मत्, probably abl. sing. of अमद्), former part of compounds and base of many derivatives, implying the singular of the pronoun of the first person; cf. e. g. मद्-विध, मदिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद|मदः
मद 1. मद् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Intoxication, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10; Pañc. 202, 25.<BR> 2. Insanity, Pañc. iv. d. 68; rut of an elephant, 87, 16.<BR> 3. Pride, Hit. i. d. 175, M.M.<BR> 4. Joy, Ṛt. 6, 32; sensual enjoyment, Ṛt. 6, 12.<BR> 5. Passion, Rājat. 5, 214; love, Vikr. 59, 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a " target="_blank">Page0680-a + 43</a>]<BR> 6. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 7. The juice that flows from an elephant's temples when in rut, Pañc. i. d. 139.<BR> 8. Semen virile.<BR> 9. Musk.<BR> II. f. दी.<BR> 1. A drinking vessel.<BR> 2. An instrument for making furrows.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मद|दुर्मदः
दुर्मद दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. m. insanity, Bhāg. P. 5, 12, 6.<BR> II. adj. 1. frantic, ib. 8, 2, 25. 2. desiring violently, MBh. 1, 2796; Chr. 23, 38 (युद्ध-, battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमद|धनमदः
धन- + मद धन- + मद, m. pride produced by wealth, Kathās. 18, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मद|निर्म्मद|निर्म्मदः
निर्मद निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from arrogance, MBh. 3, 8683.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामद|महामदः
महा- + मद महा- + मद, m. an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमद|मृगमदः
मृग- + मद मृग- + मद, m. musk, Kathās. 22, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिमदा
रति-मदा रति-मदा, f. an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वमदा
विश्व-मदा विश्व-मदा, f. one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समद
स- + मद स- + मद, adj. 1. intoxicated, Ṛt. 6, 27; delighted, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 10. 2. furious, Bhartṛ. 2, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदामद
सदा- + मद सदा- + मद, adj. ever furious, Pañc. i. d. 48 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1324).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमद
सु- + मद सु- + मद, adj. very drunk, mad, or impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदच्युत्
मदच्युत् मद-च्यु + त्, adj. Yielding intoxication or joy, Chr. 291, 7 = Rigv. i. 85, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदन|मदनः
मदन 1. मद् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Love, Vikr. 22, 8; Kāmadeva, the god of love, Vikr. d. 9.<BR> 2. The season of spring.<BR> 3. Thorn apple, Datura metel.<BR> 4. A bee.<BR> 5. Beeswax.<BR> II. f. न and नी, Spirituous liquor.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदन
उन्-मदन उन्-मदन, i. e. उद्-, adj., f. ना, inflamed with love, Kumāras. 5, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदमुच्
मदमुच् मद-मुच्, adj. Distilling juice, being in rut (viz. an elephant; cf. मद), Utt. Rāmac. 62, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयित्नु|मदयित्नुः
मदयित्नु मदयित्नु, i. e. मद्, Caus., + इत्नु, m.<BR> 1. A drunken man.<BR> 2. A distiller.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR> 4. The god of love.<BR> 5. Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार|मदारः
मदार 1. मद् + आर, m.<BR> 1. An elephant.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> 3. A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिर|मदिरः
मदिर 1. मद् + इर,<BR> I. m. A red species of Khayar, Mimosa catechu.<BR> II. f. रा.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor, Man. 11, 148; wine, nectar, Megh. 76.<BR> 2. The wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिराक्षी
मदिराक्षी मदिराक्षी, i. e. मदिरा-अक्ष + ई, f. A (fascinating) woman, Vikr. d. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरेक्षणी
मदिरेक्षणी मदिरेक्षणी, i. e. मदिरा-ईक्षण + ई, f. A fascinating woman, Vikr. d. 32; Śāk. d. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिष्ठा
मदिष्ठा मदिष्ठा, f. of the superl. of मद + वन्त्, Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदीय|मदीयं
मदीय 2. मद् + ईय, adj. Mine, Pañc. 191, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गु|मद्गुः
मद्गु मद्गु, i. e. मज्ज् + उ (see मज्ज्), m.<BR> 1. An aquatic bird, the diver, Lass. 50, 1.<BR> 2. An outcaste, the son of a Brāhmaṇa by a woman of the bard class.<BR> 3. A ship.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mergus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमद्गु|काकमद्गुः
काक- + मद्गु काक- + मद्गु, m. a kind of fowl, MBh. 13, 5520.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गुर|मद्गुरः
मद्गुर मद्गुर, i. e. मज्ज् + उर (see मज्ज्), m. A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्य|मद्यं
मद्य मद् + य, n. Spirituous liquor, wine, Pañc. 35, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यप|मद्यपः
मद्यप मद्य-प (vb. 1. पा), m. A drinker of intoxicating spirits, Man. 3, 159; a drunkard, Pañc. iv. d. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्र|मद्रः
मद्र मद् + र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Joy.<BR> 2. The name of a country, Sāv. 1, 2.<BR> 3. A sovereign of that country.<BR> II. f. रा, The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वन्
मद्वन् मद् + वन्, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधु|मधुः
मधु मधु,<BR> I. adj. Sweet, Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 6; Megh, 67.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Liquorice.<BR> 2. A tree, Bassia latifolia.<BR> 3. The month Caitra, March--April, Ṛt. 6, 24.<BR> 4. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a " target="_blank">Page0681-a + 40</a>] season of spring, Mālav. d. 26.<BR> 5. The name of a Daitya slain by Viṣṇu; cf. मधुभिद्.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Honey, Hit. i. d. 81, M.M.<BR> 2. The nectar of flowers.<BR> 3. Milk.<BR> 4. Sugar.<BR> 5. Spirituous liquor from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia, or wine, Megh. 93; Ragh. 4, 60.<BR> 6. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μέθυ; O.H.G. medu, mito; A.S. medu, medo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमधु|त्रिमधुः
त्रि- + मधु त्रि- + मधु, adj. one who knows or recites the three verses of the Rigveda, beginning with मधु (Rigv. i. 90, 6--8), Yājñ. 1, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक|मधुकं|मधुकः
मधुक मधु + क,<BR> I. adj. Sweet.<BR> II. m. A bard.<BR> III. m. and n. Liquorice.<BR> IV. n. Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकर|मधुकरः
मधुकर मधु-कर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bee, Vikr. d. 105.<BR> 2. A lover.<BR> II. f. री, A bee, Pañc. ii. d. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकरिका
मधुकरिका मधुकरिका, i. e. मधुकर + क, f. A proper name, Śāk. 77, 16 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकृत्
मधुकृत् मधु-कृ + त्, and मधुद्रु मधु-द्रु, and मधुप मधु-प (vb. 1. पा), m. A bee, Pañc. i. d. 419 (प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुच्युत्
मधुच्युत् मधु-च्यु + त्, adj. Distilling honey, Utt. Rāmac. 69, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्क|मधुपर्कं|मधुपर्कः
मधुपर्क मधु-पर्क, i. e. मधु-पृच् + अ, m. A dish of curds, honey, and clarified butter, Man. 3, 119; Chr. 16, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुभिद्
मधुभिद् मधु-भिद्, m. Viṣṇu (see मधु), Pañc. v. d. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमन्त्|मधुमत्
मधुमन्त् मधु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Sweet, Chr. 296, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमय
मधुमय मधु + मय, adj., f. यी, Sweet, Hit. ii. d. 154; luscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुर|मधुरं|मधुरः
मधुर मधु + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Sweet (figuratively), Pañc. ii. d. 65.<BR> 2. Agreeable, Pañc. 248, 11.<BR> 3. Tender, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b " target="_blank">Page0681-b + 43</a>] Daśak. in Chr. 201, 13.<BR> II. ˚रम्. adv. Sweetly, in an agreeable manner, Chr. 17, 21.<BR> III. m. Sweetness.<BR> IV. f. रा.<BR> 1. Marrow.<BR> 2. The name of a town, Utt. Rāmac. 176, 8.<BR> 3. The name of several plants.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. Treacle.<BR> 2. Poison.<BR> 3. Tin.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मधुर
वाङ्मधुर वाङ्मधुर, i. e. वाच्-, adj. sweet in speech, Hit. 74, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरता
मधुरता मधुर + ता, f. Sweetness, figurat., Pañc. v. d. 83; gracefulness, Pañc. v. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुल|मधुलं
मधुल मधुल (for मधुर), n. Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलिह्
मधुलिह् मधु-लिह्, m. A bee, Vikr. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूक|मधूकं|मधूकः
मधूक मधूक, derived from मधु, m. A tree, Bassia latifolia, Kathās. 7, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूपघ्न|मधूपघ्नं|मधूपघ्नः
मधूपघ्न मधूपघ्न, i. e. मधु-उपघ्न, n. A name of the town Mathurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलक|मधूलकः
मधूलक मधूलक, derived from मधु,<BR> I. adj. Sweet.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Sweetness.<BR> 2. A sort of Bassia latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्य|मध्यं|मध्यः
मध्य म + ध्य (म is an old pronoun),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Middle, Rājat. 5, 313.<BR> 2. Middle-sized, Man. 8, 134; of middle sort, Bhartṛ. 2, 73.<BR> 3. Intermediate; amongst.<BR> 4. Right, proper.<BR> 5. Low.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. The middle, Vikr. d. 6; the centre, abl. amongst, Pañc. 253, 14; at the end of comp. In, Pañc. 10, 5 (नगर-मध्य + म्, in the town).<BR> 2. The waist. Vikr d. 129.<BR> III. m. Cessation, interval.<BR> IV. f. या.<BR> 1. A young woman, a girl arrived at puberty.<BR> 2. The middle finger.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. A horse's flank.<BR> 2. A very large number.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. medius; Goth. midja; A.S. midd, ge-midlian; Goth. -missô, missa-; A.S. mis-; O.H.G. missa, missi, mis-; μέσος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्य
तनु- + मध्य तनु- + मध्य, adj., f. या, having a slender waist, Nal. 3, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजमध्य
भुज- + मध्य भुज- + मध्य, n. the breast, Ragh. 13, 73. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a " target="_blank">Page0682-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग
मध्यग मध्य-ग, adj.<BR> 1. Who or what goes in the centre or amongst.<BR> 2. Existing in, Pañc. iii. d. 205.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमध्यग
बहु- + मध्यग बहु- + मध्यग, adj. belonging to many, Man. 9, 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतस्
मध्यतस् मध्य + तस्, adv. From or in the middle, Hiḍ. 1, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यन्दिन|मध्यंदिन|मध्यन्दिनः
मध्यन्दिन मध्यन्दिन, i. e. मध्य + म्-दिन, n. Noon, Pañc. 82, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमध्यन्दिन|अतिमध्यंदिन
अति- + मध्यन्दिन अति- + मध्यन्दिन, n. time too near the mid-day, Man. 4, 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम|मध्यमं|मध्यमः
मध्यम मध्य + म,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Middle, Vikr. d. 19.<BR> 2. Of middle sort, Hit. ii. d. 69; of moderate strength.<BR> 3. Middle born, neither the oldest nor youngest, Chr. 4, 11.<BR> II. m. and n. The waist, Nal. 1, 10.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The fifth note of the Hindu gamut.<BR> 2. One of the scales.<BR> 3. The middle country (= मध्य-देश).<BR> 4. A sort of deer.<BR> IV. f. मा, A girl arrived at puberty.<BR> 2. The middle finger.<BR> 3. A central blossom.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. medeme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमध्यम
यव- + मध्यम यव- + मध्यम, a kind of penance, Man. 11, 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमध्यम
सु- + मध्यम सु- + मध्यम, adj. having a fine waist, Rām. 3, 52, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थ|मध्यस्थः
मध्यस्थ मध्य-स्थ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Middle.<BR> 2. Living in the midst (of persons), Pañc. 191, 10.<BR> 3. Neutral, Man. 9, 272.<BR> 4. Impartial, Mālav. 9, 2.<BR> 5. Indifferent, Śāk. 63, 19.<BR> II. m. A mediator, a judge, Lass. 92, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्येपृष्ठम्
मध्येपृष्ठम् मध्येपृष्ठम्, i. e. मध्य + इ-पृष्ठ + म्, adv. On the back, Bhartṛ. 2, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वल|मध्वलः
मध्वल मध्वल, i. e. मधु + वल m. Tippling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वासवनिक|मध्वासवनिकः
मध्वासवनिक मध्वासवनिक, i. e. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b " target="_blank">Page0682-b + 45</a>] मधु-आ-सु + अन + इक, m. A distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्विजा
मध्विजा मध्विजा, probably मधु + इ-ज (an anomal. loc.), f. Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्
मन् मन्, i. 4, and ii. 8, Ātm. (in epic poetry, and also elsewhere Par., e. g. Pañc. ii. d. 97).<BR> 1. To think, Chr. 10, 3; 154, 16; Pañc. i. d. 126 (समं विषमम् एव च मन्यते, To consider even and odd, i. e. to make long reflections); with अन्यथा, To doubt, Utt. Rāmac. 104, 2.<BR> 2. To wish, Vikr. 12, 9.<BR> 3. To mind, MBh. 3, 2092; with न, To disregard, Johns. Sel. 53, 125.<BR> 4. To believe, Rājat. 5, 255; Chr. 14, 27.<BR> 5. To understand, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 15.<BR> 6. To know, Lass. 98, 7 = Rigv. v. 9, 1; Daśak. in Chr. 183, 23.<BR> 7. To mention, to declare, Chr. 296, 2 = Rigv. i. 112, 2 (मन्तवे, ved. infin. ‘So many that even a loquacious man cannot reckon them up’).<BR> 8. To take, to value, Pañc. ii. d. 97; i. d. 190; with बहु, To estimate highly, Rājat. 5, 276.<BR> 9. मन्ये is often inserted without syntactic connection.<BR> a. To strengthen an assertion, Lass. 72, 13.<BR> b. In order to give it a modest form, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 15.<BR> c. Ironically, Rām. 3, 51, 25.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मत.<BR> 1. Admitted, Bhāṣāp. 57.<BR> 2. Believed, held, Man. 1, 76.<BR> 3. Understood, known.<BR> 4. Desired, with gen., Chr. 15, 2; Kir. 5, 27.<BR> 5. Respected, regarded. n.<BR> 1. Purpose.<BR> 2. Opinion, Indr. 3, 1.<BR> 3. Doctrine, Pañc. 253, 12.<BR> 4. Knowledge.<BR> 5. Wish.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-मीमांस्य, adj. Not to be questioned, Man. 2, 10.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, मानय,<BR> 1. To estimate highly, to honour, MBh. 8, 2424; also Ātm., Chr. 43, 23.<BR> 2. To love, Rām. 1, 38, 8.<BR> 3. Ātm. †<BR> 1. To be proud.<BR> 2. † To be stupid. Anomal. ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. in the signification of the Par. मानयान, MBh. 3, 13111. मानित, Honoured, Chr. 28, 23. मान्य, माननीय, To be honoured, Bhartṛ. 2, 70; Rājat. 5, 337.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To assent, Man. 9, 97.<BR> 2. To approve, Rām. 2, 2, 13.<BR> 3. With न, To disown, Ragh. 16, 85.<BR> 4. To permit, Rām. 2, 21, 45.<BR> 5. To pardon, Śāk. d. 116. अनुमत,<BR> 1. Assented to, Man. 3, 4.<BR> 2. Concurred with.<BR> 3. Accepted, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 3.<BR> 4. Agreeable.<BR> 5. Beloved. n. Assent, Man. 5, 151; Vikr. d. 58.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to approve, Rām. 2, 2, 8.<BR> 2. To honour, MBh. 3, 278.<BR> 3. To cause to agree, to bring in analogy with, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 1.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To intend, Pañc. 15, 23.<BR> 2. To desire, Man. 10, 95.<BR> 3. To approve, MBh. 2, 1374.<BR> 4. To believe, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 71.<BR> 5. To consider, Pañc. iii. d. 154.<BR> 6. To surpass, MBh. 3, 1388. अभिमत,<BR> 1. Wished.<BR> 2. Assented to.<BR> 3. Agreeable, Megh. 50.<BR> 4. Beloved, Pañc. i. d. 80. n. Wish, Hit. 57, 5, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-अभिमत-, adj. disagreeable, Hit. 15, 2, M.M.<BR> यथा-अभिमत + म्, adv. according to one's wish; how one lists, ad libitum, Pañc. 167, 24.<BR> --With अव अव, To despise, Man. 4, 135; Vikr. d. 30.<BR> 2. To offend, Man. 8, 84.<BR> --Caus. To despise, Man. 2, 50.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, To disdain, Man. 4, 249. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b " target="_blank">Page0683-b + 44</a>]<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. To honour, Rām. 3, 53, 27.<BR> --With वि वि, विमत,<BR> 1. Disliking.<BR> 2. Disagreeing. m. An enemy (rather मत with वि).<BR> --Caus. To disgrace, Śāk. d. 116. विमानित, Dishonoured, Pañc. i. d. 127.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To think, Rām. 3, 52, 2.<BR> 2. To resolve, Rām. 3, 53, 4. संमत;<BR> 1. Assented to, approved; अश्वपृष्ठे संमत, A good horseman, Rām. 1, 19, 19.<BR> 2. Conformable.<BR> 3. Like, resembling, Chr. 32, 23.<BR> 4. Attached to.<BR> 5. Beloved, Man. 3, 39; Pañc. i. d. 65. n. Opinion, Hit. 48, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-, adj. much approved, honoured, Chr. 49, 14.<BR> --Caus. To honour, Rām. 2, 16, 15; Chr. 22, 26.<BR> --Cf. म्ना, मति; μένος, μέμονα, αὐτό-ματος (= मत), μάτην, μάταιος (not real, only imagined), μάντις, μαίνομαι, μῆνις, μαίομαι, μέμαα; Lat. monere, monstrum, monstrare, mentiri (cf. मति), mendax; Goth. munan, muns, munths (cf. मन्त्र); A.S. manian, monian, ge-munan, mudh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमत
बहु- + मत बहु- + मत, adj. 1. thought much of, respected, Bhartṛ. 2, 59. 2. having many different opinions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुमत
साधु- + मत साधु- + मत, adj. praised, Chr. 56, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमत|सुमतः
सु- + मत सु- + मत, adj. kindly disposed. Desider.<BR> I. † मिमनिष and † मिमंस.<BR> II. Anomal. मीमांस, Ātm. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-a " target="_blank">Page0683-a + 44</a>]<BR> 1. To consider, Man. 4, 224.<BR> 2. To learn, MBh. 1, 3878.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनन|मननं
मनन मन् + अन, n. + मत<BR> 1. Minding, considering, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 1; cf. 21.<BR> 2. Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्
मनस् मन् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Mind, Chr. 3, 8; Man. 1, 104; considered as seat of perception (MBh. 14, 668), and passion, the heart, Vikr. d. 19; Bhāg. P. 5, 11, 9.<BR> 2. The intellect, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 24; power of mind, Chr. 27, 7.<BR> 3. Purpose, Chr. 12, 23; Rājat. 5, 251.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μένος, δυσμένης (= दुस्-), εὐμενής (= सु-), and म्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्
अन्य- + मनस् अन्य- + मनस् (cf. अन्यद्), adj. 1. one whose mind is directed to another, Rām. 5, 35, 2.<BR> 2. fickleminded, Hit. i. d. 110, M.M. 3. absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उद्- + मनस् उद्- + मनस्, see s. v. उन्मनस्, and adde, sorry, Vikr. 30, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमनस्
एक- + मनस् एक- + मनस्, adj. one whose mind is directed to one object, intent, Rām. 4, 4, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मनस्|दुर्म्मनस्
दुर्मनस् दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, 1. n. perversity of mind, Rām. 2, 31, 20. 2. adj. disheartened, sad, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 19. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a " target="_blank">Page0684-a + 43</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेषिमनस्
द्वेषिमनस् द्वेषिमनस्, i. e. द्वेषिन्-, adj. hostile, Hit. ii. d. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्र- + मनस् प्र- + मनस्, adj. delighted happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमनस्
प्रीति- + मनस् प्रीति- + मनस्, adj. pleased in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामनस्
महा- + मनस् महा- + मनस्, adj. high-minded, magnanimous, Rām. 3, 55, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुमनस्
वक्तुमनस् वक्तुमनस्, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
वि- + मनस् वि- + मनस्, adj. 1. sad, Utt. Rāmac. 5, 9; heart-broken, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 11. 2. perplexed. 3. changed in mind. 4. averse. 5. absent, thinking of something else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कितमनस्|शंकितमनस्
शङ्कित- + मनस् शङ्कित- + मनस्, adj. timid, Pañc. 104, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनस्
स- + मनस् स- + मनस्, adj. unanimous, Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनस्
सु- + मनस् सु- + मनस्,<BR> I. adj. satisfied, Lass. 54, 20.<BR> II. m. 1. a god. 2. a learned man. 3. a student of the Vedas. 4. wheat. 5. the name of two plants.<BR> II. m. n. and f. (the last only pl.), a flower, Man. 2, 182.<BR> III. f. सी, great flowered jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थितमनस्
सु-स्थित- + मनस् सु-स्थित- + मनस्, adj. content, Hit. ii. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरमनस्
स्थिर- + मनस् स्थिर- + मनस्, adj. having a faithful mind or heart, Pañc. 107, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस
मनस मनस् + अ, A substitute of मनस् as latter part of compounds; e. g. प्रमत्त-, adj. Furious, Chr. 35, 6. प्रवास-उत्सुक-, adj., f. सा, One whose mind is directed to his foreign residence, to the place to which he is about to depart, Vikr. 61, 17. राङ्मनस, i. e. राच्-,<BR> I. n. sing. or du. Word and mind, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 3.<BR> II. f. सा, The goddess of the serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिज|मनसिजः
मनसिज मनस् + इ-ज,<BR> I. adj. Mental.<BR> II. m. The god of love, Vikr. d. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिशय|मनसिशयः
मनसिशय मनसिशय, i. e. मनस् + इ शि + अ, m. Love, Vikr. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विता
मनस्विता मनस्विता, i. e. मनस्विन् + ता, f.<BR> 1. Intelligence.<BR> 2. Hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विन्
मनस्विन् मनस् + विन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Intelligent, Pañc. ii. d. 128; prudent, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b " target="_blank">Page0684-b + 41</a>] Vikr. d. 46.<BR> 2. Attentive.<BR> II. f. नी, A virtuous woman, Rām. 3, 55, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्
मनाक् मनाक्, probably *मन- (for मा + न, ptcple. pf. pass. of मा; cf. μανός and μινυν in μίνυνθα, μινυ in μινύθω; Lat. minu in minuo; Goth. mins, minz, minniza, minnists, which are also derived from मा) -अञ्च्, adv. A little, Hit. ii. d. 138.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनाक्
अ- + मनाक् अ- + मनाक्, adv. much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाका
मनाका मनाका, f. A female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनायु
मनायु मनायु, i. e. *मनाय, a denomin. derived from मनस् with य, + उ, adj. Intelligent, Chr. 294, 9 = Rigv. i. 92, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषा
मनीषा मन् + ईषा, f.<BR> 1. Intellect.<BR> 2. Hymn, Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. i. 112, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमनीष
कु-मनीष कु-मनीष, adj. stupid, Bhāg. P. 1, 3, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषित
मनीषित मनीषित, i. e. मनीषा + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Cherished in mind, Chr. 18, 35.<BR> 2. Aimed at, desired, 12, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिन्
मनीषिन् मनीषिन्, i. e. मनीषा + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Intelligent, wise, Man. 2, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमनीषिन्
कु- + मनीषिन् कु- + मनीषिन्, adj. stupid, Bhāg. P. 4, 31, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनु|मनुः
मनु मनु, curtailed मनुस्, q. cf.<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A man.<BR> 2. Manu, the progenitor of mankind, Man. 1, 1; 36 (Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. i. 112, 16).<BR> II. f. मनावी and मनागि, The wife of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुज|मनुजः
मनुज मनु-ज,<BR> I. m. A man in general, Bhartṛ. 2, 98.<BR> II. f. जा, A woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मनुज
निस्- + मनुज निस्- + मनुज, adj. deserted, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्य|मनुष्यः
मनुष्य मनुष्य, i. e. मनुस् + य,<BR> I. m. Man, a man, Pañc. 255, 17; mankind, Man. 1, 39.<BR> II. f. षी, A woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. mannisco; Goth. mannisks; A.S. mennesc, mennisc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अ- + मनुष्य अ- + मनुष्य,<BR> I. m. one who is not a man, Rām. 2, 93, 21.<BR> II. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a " target="_blank">Page0685-a + 41</a>] deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमनुष्य
अति- + मनुष्य अति- + मनुष्य, adj. superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मनुष्य|दुर्मनुष्यः
दुर्मनुष्य दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, m. a wicked man, MBh. 8, 2117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मनुष्य|निर्म्मनुष्य
निर्म्˚ निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. deserted, Rām. 2, 18, 12 Gorr. 2. without a man (upon its back, viz. an elephant), MBh. 6, 3893.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यत्व|मनुष्यत्वं
मनुष्यत्व मनुष्य + त्व, n. Condition of man, manhood, Man. 12, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुस्
मनुस् मनुस्, for original मन्वन्त् (ptcple. pres. Par. of मन्, ii. 8), m. Man (ved.).<BR> --Cf. मनु; German mannus (Tacit. Germ. 2); Goth. man, manna; A.S. man, mann; Lat. mas, maris; Μίνως.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगत
मनोगत मनोगत, i. e. मनस्-गत (vb. गम्),<BR> I. adj. Seated in the mind.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Thought.<BR> 2. Wish, Chr. 20, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजू
मनोजू मनोजू, i. e. मनस्-जू, adj. Swift as thought, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञ|मनोज्ञं|मनोज्ञः
मनोज्ञ मनोज्ञ, i. e. मनस्-ज्ञ,<BR> I. adj. Beautiful, Ṛt. 6, 25.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. A princess.<BR> 2. Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभव|मनोभवः
मनोभव मनोभव, and मनोभू मनोभू, i. e. मनस्-भू + अ, and मनस्-भू, m. The god of love, Pañc. 128, 5 (भव); Kathās. 3, 62 (भू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरम|मनोरमं
मनोरम मनोरम, i. e. मनस्-रम् + अ, adj. Beautiful, Pañc. 127, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहर|मनोहरं|मनोहरः
मनोहर मनोहर, i. e. मनस्-हृ + अ, adj. Beautiful, charming, Vikr. d. 9; 119.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोहर
सु- + मनोहर सु- + मनोहर, adj. very charming, Pañc. pr. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोह्वा
मनोह्वा मनोह्वा, i. e. मनस्-ह्वे + अ, f. Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तु|मंतु|मंतुः|मन्तुः
मन्तु मन् + तु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A man.<BR> 2. A king.<BR> 3. Offence.<BR> II. f. Intellect.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μαντεύομαι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमन्तु
त्रि- + मन्तु त्रि- + मन्तु, adj. knowing the three [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b " target="_blank">Page0685-b + 41</a>] worlds, i. e. all-wise, Chr. 296, 4 = Rigv. i. 112, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तूय
मन्तूय मन्तूय, a denomin. derived from मन्तु with य, Par. To be offended or jealous, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तृ|मंतृ
मन्तृ मन् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A wise man.<BR> 2. An adviser.<BR> --Cf. Μέντωρ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्र्|मंत्र्
मन्त्र् मन्त्र्, i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from मन्त्र), Ātm. (but often also Par.).<BR> --† i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To take secret council with (with instr. and acc.), Man. 7, 146; Pañc. rec. orn.<BR> 2. To deliberate, Rām. 2, 16, 15.<BR> 3. To resolve, Hit. 129, 13.<BR> 4. To speak, Hit. 64, 6 (Par.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मन्त्रित, Advised.<BR> --Comp.<BR> See कु-.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To accompany with spells or prayers, to consecrate by spells, to charm, Chr. 31, 12; Utt. Rāmac. 39, 10.<BR> 2. To dismiss, MBh. 3, 39.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To consecrate by blessings, Rām. 1, 24, 2; by spells, to charm, Draup. 8, 54.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To address, Rām. 1, 1, 8.<BR> 2. To salute, MBh. 3, 2243.<BR> 3. To invite, Man. 3, 191; Pañc. 26, 20.<BR> 4. To call, Utt. Rāmac. 125, 9.<BR> 5. To ask, MBh. 4, 64.<BR> 6. To take leave (acc.), MBh. 3, 2295.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To address, MBh. 2, 42.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To address, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 10.<BR> 2. To invite, Rām. 1, 46, 12.<BR> 3. To take leave (acc.), Chr. 45, 11.<BR> --With नि नि, To invite, Man. 3, 187; to present with (with instr.) Pañc. iii. d. 139.<BR> --With उपनि उप-नि, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a " target="_blank">Page0686-a + 42</a>]<BR> 1. To invite, Rām. 3, 52, 51.<BR> 2. To consecrate, MBh. 3, 15959.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To invite, MBh. 3, 2112.<BR> --With परि परि, To consecrate, to charm, Arj. 7, 18.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To take council with (instr.), Pañc. 25, 13; Chr. 53, 6.<BR> 2. To deliberate, Man. 7, 216.<BR> 3. To reflect, Pañc. 25, 14.<BR> 4. To salute, MBh. 1, 5454.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. mathljan; see मन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मन्त्रित|दुर्मंत्रित
दुर्मन्त्रित दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. adj. imprudently advised, MBh. 5, 4262.<BR> II. n. a bad advice, ib. 5, 2697.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्त्रित
सु- + मन्त्रित सु- + मन्त्रित,<BR> I. adj. 1. well deliberated, Hit. iii. d. 137. 2. well counselled.<BR> II. n. wise counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्र|मंत्र|मंत्रः|मन्त्रः
मन्त्र मन् + त्र, m.<BR> 1. That part of the Veda which comprises the hymns, Madhusūdana in Weber, Ind. St. i. 14.<BR> 2. A holy text, Vikr. 87, 10; Pañc. 189, 24.<BR> 3. A mystical verse or incantation, charm, Pañc. i. d. 73.<BR> 4. Prayer, Vikr. 32, 16.<BR> 5. A formula sacred to any individual deity.<BR> 6. Advice, Hit. 54, 14; secret consultation, Pañc. i. d. 61 (मन्त्रं सम्-आ-चर्, To intrigue).<BR> 7. A design, Hit. i. d. 128, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. mathl, mathleins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्र|अमंत्र
अ- + मन्त्र अ- + मन्त्र, adj. 1. not accompanied by holy texts, Man. 3, 121. 2. excluded from the use of the Veda, 9, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टिमन्त्र|आकृष्टिमन्त्रः
आकृष्टि- + मन्त्र आकृष्टि- + मन्त्र. m. a charm having the power of attraction, Hit. i. d. 96, M.M. See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मन्त्र|दुर्मंत्र|दुर्मन्त्रः
दुर्मन्त्र दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, m. bad advice, Bhartṛ. 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्त्र
निर्मन्त्र निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. unaccompanied by holy texts, MBh. 1, 2980.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमन्त्र|विषमंत्र|विषमन्त्रः
विष- + मन्त्र विष- + मन्त्र, m. a snakecatcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रज्ञ|मंत्रज्ञ|मन्त्रज्ञः
मन्त्रज्ञ मन्त्र-ज्ञ, m.<BR> 1. A spy.<BR> 2. A priest.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्त्रज्ञ
सु- + मन्त्रज्ञ सु- + मन्त्रज्ञ, adj. well versed in holy texts, Johns. Sel. 10, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रण|मंत्रण|मंत्रणं|मन्त्रणं
मन्त्रण मन्त्रण, i. e. मन्त्र् + अन, n., and f. णा, Advising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतस्
मन्त्रतस् मन्त्र + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. = abl. of मन्त्र, Man. 3, 65.<BR> 2. Advisedly, deliberately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवन्त्|मन्त्रवत्|मंत्रवत्
मन्त्रवन्त् मन्त्र + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Accompanied with holy texts, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b " target="_blank">Page0686-b + 41</a>] Man. 2, 29.<BR> 2. Entitled to use the Vedas.<BR> 3. Initiated.<BR> II. ˚वत्, adv. With holy verses, hallowed by holy texts, Man. 2, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रविद्|मंत्रविद्
मन्त्रविद् मन्त्र-विद्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Conversant with the Vedas, Johns. Sel. 42, 51.<BR> 2. Conversant with charms, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 9.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A spy.<BR> 2. A counsellor, Chr. 55, 6.<BR> 3. A priest.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रविद्
अ- + मन्त्रविद् अ- + मन्त्रविद्, adj. unacquainted with holy texts, unlearned, Man. 3, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिक
मन्त्रिक मन्त्रिक, i. e. मन्त्र + इक, m. One who is conversant with charms, Lass. 17, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिता|मंत्रिता
मन्त्रिता मन्त्रिता, f., and मन्त्रित्व मन्तृत्व, n., i. e. मन्त्रिन् + ता or त्व, The state or office of a counsellor, ministership, Hit. 54, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त्रित्व
स-मन्त्रित्व स-मन्त्रित्व, n. assent, Rājat. 5, 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिन्|मंत्रिन्
मन्त्रिन् मन्त्रिन्, i. e. मन्त्र + इन्, m. A counsellor, Pañc. i. d. 428 (अ-सन्त्-, adj. Having wicked counsellors).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मन्त्रिन्
दुर्मन्त्रिन् दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, m. a bad counsellor, Pañc. iii. d. 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानमन्त्रिन्|प्रधानमंत्रिन्
प्रधान- + मन्त्रिन् प्रधान- + मन्त्रिन्, m. the prime minister, Lass. 35, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामन्त्रिन्|महामंत्रिन्
महा- + मन्त्रिन् महा- + मन्त्रिन्, m. the prime minister, Hit. 97, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिवत्
मन्त्रिवत् मन्त्रिवत्, i. e. मन्त्रिन् + वत्, adv. Like a counsellor, Rājat. 5, 389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ्|मंथ्
मन्थ् मन्थ्, see मथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ|मंथ|मंथः|मन्थः
मन्थ मन्थ, curtailed मन्थन् (see मथिन्), m.<BR> 1. A churning-stick.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. Churning, Utt. Rāmac. 172, 12.<BR> 4. Stirring, Ragh. 3, 10.<BR> 5. Killing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमन्थ|मणिमन्थं
मणि- + मन्थ मणि- + मन्थ, n. rock-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थज|मंथज|मन्थजं
मन्थज मन्थ-ज, n. Butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थन|मंथन|मन्थनं|मंथनः|मन्थनः
मन्थन मन्थ् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Churning, MBh. 1, 1141. Agitating.<BR> II. f. नी, A churn.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमन्थन
अमृत- + मन्थन अमृत- + मन्थन, n. production [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a " target="_blank">Page0687-a + 41</a>] of the Amṛta, the beverage of the gods, by churning, MBh. vol. i. p. 41, l. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थर|मंथर|मन्थरं|मन्थरः
मन्थर मन्थ् + अर,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Slow, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 2.<BR> 2. Torpid, Ragh. 19, 21.<BR> 3. Large.<BR> 4. Crooked.<BR> 5. Stupid.<BR> 6. Low.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A treasure.<BR> 2. Fruit.<BR> 3. An obstacle.<BR> 4. A churning-stick.<BR> 5. A proper name, Hit. 58, 7, M.M.<BR> III. n. Safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थरु|मंथरु|मंथरुः|मन्थरुः
मन्थरु मन्थ् + अरु, m. The wind from a whisk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थान|मंथान|मंथानः|मन्थानः
मन्थान मन्थान (vb. मन्थ्), m. A churning-stick, Rām. 1, 45, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थिन्|मंथिन्
मन्थिन् मन्थ् + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Churning.<BR> 2. Afflicting.<BR> II. f. नी, A churn.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वमन्थिन्
ऊर्ध्व- + मन्थिन् ऊर्ध्व- + मन्थिन्, adj. chaste (cf. मथिन्), Bhāg. P. 5, 3, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्|मंद्
मन्द् मन्द् (from मद्), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. † To get drunk.<BR> 2. To rejoice.<BR> 3. To praise.<BR> 4. To sleep.<BR> 5. † To languish.<BR> 6. † To move slowly.<BR> 7. † To shine.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. mundus; O.H.G. mandjan, to rejoice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द|मंद|मन्दः
मन्द मन्द,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Slow, Śṛṅgārat. 7.<BR> 2. Stupid, Chr. 8, 31.<BR> 3. Unlucky.<BR> 4. Little, Hit. 58, 13.<BR> 5. Low (as a tone), Rām. 3, 55, 36 (adv.); Pañc. 173, 1.<BR> 6. Doubled, मन्दंमन्दम्, adv. Very slowly, Pañc. 90, 21.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Saturn.<BR> 2. A name of Yama.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमन्द|पिचुमंद|पिचुमन्दः
पिचु- + मन्द पिचु- + मन्द, m. a tree, Azadiracta indica A. Juss. (also, but erroneously, पिचुमर्द), Śiś. 5, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगतित्व
मन्दगतित्व मन्द-गति + त्व, n. Property of moving slowly, Pañc. 142, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दत्व|मंदत्वं
मन्दत्व मन्द + त्व, n. Foolishness, Pañc. ii. d. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दन|मंदन|मंदनं|मन्दनं
मन्दन मन्द् + अन, n. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दभाग्यता
मन्दभाग्यता मन्द-भाग्य + ता, f. Misfortune, Pañc. 227, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दर|मंदर|मन्दरः
मन्दर मन्दर (cf. मन्थर, and vb. मन्द्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Slow.<BR> 2. Large<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of a fabulous mountain with which the ocean was churned, MBh. 1, 1112; Kir. 5, 30.<BR> 2. The mandara tree, one of the trees of paradise.<BR> 3. The paradise.<BR> 4. A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दसान|मंदसानः|मन्दसानः
मन्दसान मन्दसान (vb. मन्द्), m.<BR> 1. A name of Agni.<BR> 2. Life.<BR> 3. Sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक|मंदाक|मन्दाकं|मंदाकः|मन्दाकः
मन्दाक मन्दाक, n. A current, a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाकिनी|मंदाकिनी
मन्दाकिनी मन्दाकिनी, i. e. मन्दाक + इन्, f. The Ganges of heaven, Utt. Rāmac. 158, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाय
मन्दाय मन्दाय, a denomin. derived from मन्द with य, Ātm. To go tardily, to delay, Vikr. d. 56; Megh. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दार|मंदार|मंदारः|मन्दारः
मन्दार मन्दार (vb. मन्द्), m.<BR> 1. One of the five trees in Indra's paradise, Vikr. d. 6, 127; Megh. 73.<BR> 2. The coral tree, Erythrina fulgens, Megh. 68.<BR> 3. Swallow-wort, Asclepias gigantea.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमन्दार
कृत- + मन्दार कृत- + मन्दार, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारवती
मन्दारवती मन्दारवती, i. e. मन्दार + वन्त् + ई, f. A proper name, Lass. 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारु|मंदारु|मंदारुः|मन्दारुः
मन्दारु मन्दारु, m. The coral tree, Erythrina fulgens (see मन्दार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिर|मंदिर|मंदिरं|मन्दिरं|मन्दिरः
मन्दिर मन्दिर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The sea.<BR> 2. The back of the knee.<BR> II. f. रा, A stable.<BR> III. f. रा, and n. A house, Hit. ii. d. 126 (n.); a palace, Vikr. 35, 2; Kathās. 26, 283 (f.).<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. A town.<BR> 2. A temple.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करमन्दिर
अवस्कर- + मन्दिर अवस्कर- + मन्दिर, n. the privy, Rājat. 5, 406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिमन्दिर|केलिमंदिर
केलि- + मन्दिर केलि- + मन्दिर, n. A pleasure-house, Caurap. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्रमन्दिर|जलयंत्रमंदिर
जल-यन्त्र- + मन्दिर जल-यन्त्र- + मन्दिर, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a " target="_blank">Page0688-a + 40</a>] n. a summer-house erected in the midst of water or on the bank of a river, Ṛt. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरा|मंदुरा
मन्दुरा मन्दुरा, f. A stable for horses, Weber, Ind. St. iii. 370, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्र|मंद्र|मन्द्रः
मन्द्र मन्द्र, m.<BR> 1. A deep, hollow, or low tone, or sound, Megh. 97 (read मन्द्र-); Vikr. 65, 11 (adj.?).<BR> 2. A sort of drum.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्द्र|आमंद्र|आमन्द्रः
आ- + मन्द्र आ- + मन्द्र, adj. Grumbling, Megh. 35 (read आमन्द्र्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्धातृ|मंधातृ
मन्धातृ मन्धातृ, m. A proper name, Chr. 297, 13 = Rigv. i. 112, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथ|मन्मथः
मन्मथ मन्मथ (frequent. of मन्थ् + अ), m.<BR> 1. A name of the god of love, Pañc. 216, 17.<BR> 2. Love, Ṛt. 1, 27.<BR> 3. The elephant or wood-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मय
मन्मय मन्मय, i. e. 2. मद् + मय, adj. Full of me, attached to me, Bhag. 4, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्य
ऽमन्य -मन् + य, latter part of comp. adj. Thinking one's self; e. g. ज्ञ + म्-मन्य, adj. Thinking one's self a wise man, Rājat. 3, 491.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्या
मन्या मन्या, f. The tendon forming the nape of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यु|मन्युः
मन्यु मन् + यु, m.<BR> 1. Anger, Utt. Rāmac. 83, 11; fury, Pañc. 59, 16.<BR> 2. Sorrow, grief, Chr. 7, 21; Utt. Rāmac. 94, 14.<BR> 3. Distress.<BR> 4. A sacrifice.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μῆνις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यु|अभिमन्युः
अभि- + मन्यु अभि- + मन्यु, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिमन्यु|अहिमन्युः
अहि- + मन्यु अहि- + मन्यु, adj. furious like snakes, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतमन्यु
वीत- + मन्यु वीत- + मन्यु, i. e. वि-इत- (vb. इ), adj. exempt from sorrow or anger, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्यु|समन्युः
स- + मन्यु स- + मन्यु, 1. adj. 1. angry. 2. sorrowful.<BR> II. m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युमन्त्|मन्युमत्
मन्युमन्त् मन्यु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Angry.<BR> 2. Sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वन्तर|मन्वंतर|मन्वन्तरं
मन्वन्तर मन्वन्तर, i. e. मनु-अन्तर,<BR> 1. The period of a Manu, equal [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b " target="_blank">Page0688-b + 39</a>] to seventy-one ages of the gods, Man. 1, 79; Utt. Rāmac. 19, 7; fourteen मन्वन्तरस् constitute a कल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मभ्र्
† मभ्र् मभ्र्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममता
ममता ममता, i. e. मम, gen. sing. of अस्मद्, + ता, f.<BR> 1. Selfishness.<BR> 2. Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममत्व|ममत्वं
ममत्व मम + त्व (cf. the last), n. Arrogance, Lass. 85, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मम्ब्
मम्ब् मम्ब्, see बर्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय्
† मय् मय्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. meare; see मी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय|मयः
मय मय, m.<BR> 1. A camel.<BR> 2. A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयु|मयुः
मयु मयु, m. The name of a class of attendants on Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूख|मयूखः
मयूख मयूख, m.<BR> 1. A ray of light, Pañc. i. d. 92.<BR> 2. Light, splendour, Ṛt. 6, 29.<BR> 3. Beauty.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मयूख
उन्मयूख उन्म्˚, i. e. उद्-, adj. radiant, Ragh. 16, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमयूख|शीतमयूखः
शीत- + मयूख शीत- + मयूख, m. 1. the moon. 2. camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूर|मयूरः
मयूर मयूर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A peacock, Hit. i. d. 178, M.M.<BR> 2. The name of a flower and of a plant.<BR> II. f. री, A peahen, Utt. Rāmac. 55, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयोभू
मयोभू मयोभू, i. e. मयस् (ved. Enjoyment), -भू, adj. Yielding enjoyment, Chr. 295, 18 = Rigv. i. 92, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरक|मरकः
मरक मरक, i. e. मृ + अक, m. Epidemic disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकत|मरकतं
मरकत मरकत, and मरक्त मरक्त, n. An emerald, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 15 (˚कत); Pañc. 9, 5 (˚कत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरण|मरणं
मरण मरण, i. e. मृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Dying, Rām. 3, 48, 1.<BR> 2. Death, Pañc. 128, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणम्
आ-मरण + म् आ-मरण + म्, adv. till death, Hit. i. d. 187, M.M. (आमरण-अन्त, adj. ending only at death). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a " target="_blank">Page0689-a + 39</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमरण|सहमरणं
सह- + मरण सह- + मरण, n. a widow's burning herself with her deceased husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणज
मरणज मरण-ज, adj. Produced by death, Pañc. v. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरत|मरतः
मरत मरत, i. e. मृ + अत, m. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मराल|मरालः
मराल मराल,<BR> I. adj. Soft.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A sort of goose.<BR> 2. A duck.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR> 4. A grove.<BR> 5. Lamp-black used as collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिच|मरिचं|मरिचः
मरिच and मरीच मरी̆च, n. Pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचि|मरीचिः
मरीचि मरीचि (also ˚ची, f., Rām. 1, 56, 18).<BR> I. m. and f. A ray of light, Vikr. d. 47.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One of the Prajāpatis, Man. 1, 58; first of the Pitṛs, 3, 194.<BR> 2. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिका
मरीचिका मरीचि + का, f. The mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिप
मरीचिप मरीचि-प (vb. 1. पा), m. A kind of genius, Sund. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरु|मरुः
मरु मरु, i. e. मृ + उ, m.<BR> 1. A desert, Hit. i. d. 10, M.M.; Bhāg. P. 6, 8, 36.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. The name of a country.<BR> --Cf. probably A.S. mór.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्
मरुत् मरुत् (vb. मृ ?),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. pl. The deities of wind, Vikr. d. 36.<BR> 2. Wind, Pañc. i. d. 353.<BR> 3. Air, Bhāṣāp. 2.<BR> II. n. A sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत|मरुतः
मरुत मरुत् + अ, m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्त|मरुत्तः
मरुत्त मरुत्त, m. The name of a fabulous king, MBh. 14, 226; Viṣṇu P. 352.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्वन्त्|मरुत्वत्
मरुत्वन्त् मरुत् + वन्त्, m.<BR> 1. Indra, Vikr. d. 15.<BR> 2. The monkey Hanumant.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुल|मरुलः
मरुल मरुल. m. A sort of duck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरूक|मरूकः
मरूक मरूक, m. A sort of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरोल
मरोल मरोल, m. A marine monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्क|मर्कः
मर्क मर्क (vb. मृ), m.<BR> 1. A body,<BR> 2. The vital breath which pervades the body.<BR> 3. A monkey.<BR> 4. An imp. Stenzler, in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 531, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कट|मर्कटः
मर्कट मर्क + ट, m.<BR> 1. A monkey, Man. 12, 67; Pañc. 118, 12.<BR> 2. A spider.<BR> 3. A large crane, Ardea argala.<BR> 4. A kind of venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्करा
मर्करा मर्करा, f.<BR> 1. A chasm, a hole.<BR> 2. A vessel.<BR> 3. A barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्च्
मर्च् मर्च्, see मार्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्जू|मर्ज्जू
मर्जू मर्जू, i. e. मृज् + उ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A washerman.<BR> 2. A catamite.<BR> II. f. Cleansing, cleanliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त|मर्तः|मर्त्त|मर्त्तः
मर्त मर्त (old ptcple. pf. pass. of मृ), m. A mortal, a man, Chr. 291, 13 = Rigv. i. 64, 13.<BR> --Cf. μορτός, βροτός; Lat. mortuus, mortalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्य|मर्त्यः
मर्त्य मर्त्य, i. e. मर्त + य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A mortal, a man, Pañc. ii. d. 89.<BR> 2. The earth.<BR> II. f. या, A woman.<BR> III. n. The body, Bhāg. P. 3, 33, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अ- + मर्त्य अ- + मर्त्य, 1. adj. immortal, Ragh. 7, 50. 2. m. a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द|मर्दः
मर्द मर्द, i. e. मृद् + अ, m. Grinding, pounding, MBh. 1, 1121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्दन|मर्द्दन|मर्द्दनं
मर्दन मर्दन, i. e. मृद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rubbing, Pañc. 238, 7.<BR> 2. Touching, Śṛṅgārat. 14.<BR> 3. Grinding, Hit. iii. d. 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमर्दन|अरिमर्द्दन
अरि- + मर्दन अरि- + मर्दन, m. 1. a destroyer of enemies, Draup. 6, 14. 2. a proper name, Hariv. 1917.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वक्षत्रियमर्दन
सर्व-क्षत्रिय- + मर्दन सर्व-क्षत्रिय- + मर्दन, m. the destroyer of all the military class, Johns. Sel. 3, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्दल|मर्दलः|मर्द्दल|मर्द्दलः
मर्दल मर्दल, m. A sort of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्दिन्
मर्दिन् मर्दिन्, i. e. मृद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Grinding; in महिष-मर्दिनि, f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a " target="_blank">Page0690-a + 41</a>] Durgā. लोष्ट-, adj. Who or what breaks clods of earth, Man. 4, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ब्
मर्ब् मर्ब्, see बर्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मज्ञ|मर्मज्ञः|मर्म्मज्ञ|मर्म्मज्ञः
मर्मज्ञ मर्मज्ञ, i. e. मर्मन्-ज्ञ,<BR> I. adj. One who knows another's weak points, Pañc. i. d. 278.<BR> II. m. A learned and intelligent man, Hit. 92, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मन्|मर्म्मन्
मर्मन् मर्मन्, i. e. मृ + मन्, n.<BR> 1. A vital member or organ, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1586.<BR> 2. A joint of a limb, Hit. iv. d. 32.<BR> 3. A weak point, Hit. iii. d. 9.<BR> 4. A secret, Pañc. iii. d. 200.<BR> 5. Design, Hit. iii. d. 19.<BR> 6. Truth.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. membrum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मर्मन्
अन्तर्- + मर्मन् अन्तर्- + मर्मन्, n. the heart, Utt. Rāmac. 128, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमर्मन्|शिरोमर्म्मन्
शिरोमर्मन् शिरोम्˚, i. e. शिरस्-, m. a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ममय
मर्ममय मर्ममय, i. e. मर्मन् + मय, adj., f. यी, Containing (their) secrets, Pañc. 184, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मर|मर्मरः|मर्म्मर|मर्म्मरः
मर्मर मर्मर (a reduplicated form based on an imitative sound), m. The rustling sound of cloth, or dry leaves, Ragh. 6, 57 (at the end of a comp. adj.); of the wind, Rājat. 2, 165 (roaring).<BR> --Cf. Lat. murmurare; O.H.G. murmuron; μόρμορος, μορμύρω, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मरीक|मर्मरीकः|मर्म्मरीक|मर्म्मरीकः
मर्मरीक मर्मरीक, m. A low, a wicked man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मविद्|मर्म्मविद्
मर्मविद् मर्मविद्, and मर्मवेदिन् मर्मवेदिन्, i. e. मर्मन्-विद्, or -वेदिन्, m. A learned and intelligent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्मस्पृश्|मर्म्मस्पृश्
मर्मस्पृश् मर्मस्पृश्, i. e. मर्मन्-स्पृश्, adj. Giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्य|मर्यः
मर्य मर्य, i. e. मृ + य,<BR> I. m. (ved.), A man, a warrior, Chr. 290, 2 = Rigv. i. 61, 2; a husband.<BR> II. f. या, A boundary.<BR> --With<BR> I. cf. perhaps Lat. maritus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्यादा|मर्य्यादा
मर्यादा मर्यादा, i. e. मर्या-द (vb. दा), f.<BR> 1. A landmark, Mān. 9, 201.<BR> 2. A boundary, limit, Pañc. i. d. 65. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b " target="_blank">Page0690-b + 44</a>]<BR> 3. Continuance in the right way, rectitude.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्याद|अमर्य्याद
अ-मर्याद अ-मर्याद, adj. not keeping within the right way, Pañc. i. d. 158; unrestrained, unruly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसाक्षिकमर्याद
अग्नि-साक्षिक- + मर्याद अग्नि-साक्षिक- + मर्याद, adj. one who is married in presence of the sacred fire, Hit. i. d. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्षितमर्याद
अन्-अप-ईक्षित- + मर्याद अन्-अप-ईक्षित- + मर्याद, adj. regardless of the limits (drawn by the holy scriptures), Man. 8, 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मर्याद
दुर्मर्याद दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-मर्याद, adj. wicked, Utt. Rāmac. 113, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मर्याद|निर्मर्य्याद
निर्मर्याद निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-,<BR> I. adj. 1. boundless. 2. unruly. 3. sinful, impious, Pañc. 152, 7. 4. confused, Rām. 3, 69, 19.<BR> II. n. confusion, MBh. 4, 1052; a sort of battle, Hariv. 15978.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमर्याद
भिन्न- + मर्याद भिन्न- + मर्याद (vb. भिद्), adj. unbounded, unrestrained, Utt. Rāmac. 137, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्याद|समर्यादः|समर्य्याद|समर्य्यादः
स- + मर्याद स- + मर्याद, adj. 1. bounded. 2. near. 3. correct in conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्यादिन्
मर्यादिन् मर्यादिन्, i. e. मर्यादा + इन्, adj. not trespassing one's boundary, Lass. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्व्
† मर्व् मर्व्, i. 1, Par. To fill; cf. मार्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ष|मर्षः
मर्ष मर्ष, i. e. मृष् + अ, m. Endurance.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अ- + मर्ष अ- + मर्ष, m. 1. impatience, inability to endure, Utt. Rāmac. 134, 1; indignation, Johns. Sel. 5, 27. 2. passion, wrath, Rām. 6, 100, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरमर्ष
निस्-अ- + मर्ष निस्-अ- + मर्ष, adj. devoid of energy, MBh. 5, 2896.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्ष
सामर्ष सामर्ष, i. e. स-अ-, adj. full of passion, wrathful, Rām. 6, 91, 6. ˚षम्, adv. angrily, Mṛcch. 19, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षण|मर्षणं
मर्षण मर्षण, i. e. म्रिष् + अन, n. Enduring.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अ- + मर्षण अ- + मर्षण, adj. impatient, unable to endure, Nal. 12, 54; wrathful, Hiḍ. 4, 54 (अति-अ-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमर्षण|अघमर्षणं
अघ- + मर्षण अघ- + मर्षण, n. the name of a holy text, Man. 11, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मर्षण|दुर्मर्षणः
दुर्मर्षण दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. adj. difficult to be endured, or to be managed, Rām. 6, 3, 33.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्
† मल् मल्, मल्ल् मल्ल्, i. 1, Ātm., and भल मल्, 1. 10, मलय, or मलापय, Par. To hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल|मलः
मल मल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Dirty.<BR> 2. Niggardly.<BR> II. (m. and) n.<BR> 1. Dirt, filth, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 9.<BR> 2. Sediment, dregs.<BR> 3. Filthy refuse, Man. 11, 93.<BR> 4. Excretion of the body, as fæces, etc., Man. 5, 132.<BR> 5. Sin, Man. 2, 102.<BR> 6. Defilement, Man. 11, 70.<BR> 7. Rust.<BR> 8. Camphor.<BR> 9. Cuttle fishbone.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μέλας (cf. मलिन), μόρον, μάρμαρος, μαρμάιρω; A.S. smere, smerian, smerwian, smyrian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अ- + मल अ- + मल, adj., f. ला, pure, Pañc. ii. d. 182; white, Vikr. d. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यमल
कांस्य- + मल कांस्य- + मल, n. verdigris, Suśr. 2, 237, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मल|निर्म्मल|निर्म्मलं
निर्मल निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ला. 1. stainless, Hit. i. d. 47, M.M. 2. pure, Hit. ii. d. 134; clear, Pañc. 248, 5. 3. bright, Johns. Sel. 12, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमल|बहुमलः
बहु- + मल बहु- + मल, m. lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
वि- + मल वि- + मल,<BR> I. adj. 1. clean, spotless, Chr. 40, 12. 2. pure, Pañc. v. d. 36; Śiś. 9, 13. 3. clear, Pañc. iii. d. 147 = day, Chr. 37, 31. 4. transparent. 5. white. 6. beautiful.<BR> II. n. silvergilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तमल
शान्त- + मल शान्त- + मल, adj. exempt from soil, literally and figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समल|समलं
स- + मल स- + मल,<BR> I. adj. 1. dirty. 2. sinful.<BR> II. n. fæces, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपङ्किन्
मलपङ्किन् मलपङ्किन्, i. e. मल-पङ्क + इन्, adj. Covered with mud and dirt, Chr. 46, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलमल्लक|मलमल्लकः
मलमल्लक मल-मल्ल + क, n. A piece of cloth worn over the privities, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलय|मलयः
मलय मलय, m.<BR> 1. A mountainous range in the Dekhan, Lass. 38, 17; Vikr. d. 25.<BR> 2. The country lying along this range, Malabar.<BR> 3. A garden.<BR> 4. The garden of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयज|मलयजं|मलयजः
मलयज मलय-ज, m. and n. Sandalwood. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322; Vikr. d. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाका
मलाका मलाका, i. e. मल + आक, f.<BR> 1. A lewd woman.<BR> 2. A female messenger.<BR> 3. A female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिन|मलिनं
मलिन मलिन, i. e. मल + इन् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Dirty, Pañc. iii. d. 178; soiled, Hit. ii. d. 39.<BR> 2. Black, Śiś. 9, 18; obscure, ib. 23; obscured, Hit. i. d. 27, M.M.<BR> 3. Sinful.<BR> 4. Bad.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Fault.<BR> 2. Buttermilk.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अ- + मलिन अ- + मलिन, adj. pure, Bhartṛ. 3, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनत्व|मलिनत्वं
मलिनत्व मलिन + त्व, n. Blackness, Cāṇ. 76 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 412.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिम्लुच|मलिम्लुचः
मलिम्लुच मलिम्लुच् + अ (from an anomal. frequent. of म्लुछ्), m.<BR> 1. A thief.<BR> 2. The intercalary lunar month.<BR> 3. Fire.<BR> 4. Wind.<BR> 5. An imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलीमस|मलीमसं|मलीमसः
मलीमस मलीमस (cf. मल), adj.<BR> 1. Dirty, Hit. ii. d. 148; stained, Ragh. 2, 33.<BR> 2. Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल्
मल्ल् मल्ल्, see मल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल|मल्लः
मल्ल मल्ल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Strong.<BR> 2. Excellent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A wrestler; the son of an outcaste Kṣatriya, Man. 10, 22; 12, 45.<BR> 2. A cup.<BR> 3. The hemicranium.<BR> 4. The residue of an oblation.<BR> III. f. ला.<BR> 1. A woman.<BR> 2. Arabian jasmine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमल्ल|हस्तिमल्लः
हस्तिमल्ल हस्तिमल्ल, i. e. हस्तिन्-, m. 1. the elephant of Indra. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेश|गणेशः
गणेश गणेश. 3. a chief of the Nāgas, or serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लक|मल्लकः
मल्लक मल्ल + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A tooth.<BR> 2. A leaf to wrap up something, or a cup, Mṛcch. 126, 9 v. r.; cf. Wilson, Hind. Th. i. 2 ed. 134, n., and Stenzler, n.<BR> II. m., and f. लिका, An oil vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लघटी
मल्लघटी मल्लघटी, f. A kind of dancing, Vikr. 62, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लि|मल्लिः
मल्लि and मल्ली मल्ली̆, f. Arabian jasmine, Jasminum zambac, Lass. 67, 7 (ली).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमल्ली
मधु-मल्ली मधु-मल्ली, f. double jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमल्ली
रङ्ग-मल्ली रङ्ग-मल्ली, f. a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिक|मल्लिकः
मल्लिक मल्लिक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1.<BR> A sort of goose with brown legs and bill, Utt. Rāmac. 20, 4 (rather मल्लिकाख्य) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a " target="_blank">Page0692-a + 39</a>]<BR> 2. A shuttle.<BR> 3. The month Māgha.<BR> II. f. का (i. e. मल्लि + क).<BR> 1. Arabian jasmine, Ṛt. 6, 6.<BR> 2. A goblet.<BR> 3. A river.<BR> 4. See मल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मव्
† मव् मव्, and मव्य् मव्य्, i. 1, Par. To bind, see मू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मश्
† मश् मश्, मिश् मिश्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशक|मशकः
मशक मशक (akin to मक्षिका, q. cf.), m.<BR> 1. A gnat, a musquito, Hit. i. d. 80, M.M.; Pañc. iii. d. 98.<BR> 2. A kind of cutaneous eruption.<BR> 3. A leather water-bag.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशमशक
दंश- + मशक दंश- + मशक, m. a biting gnat, Man. 1, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशहरी
मशहरी मशहरी (मश [= मशक]-हृ + अ + ई), f. Curtains to keep off musquitoes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशुन|मशुनः
मशुन मशुन (perhaps a form of महा-श्वन् + अ), m. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मष्
† मष् मष् (and मुष् मुष्), i. 1, Par. To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मषि|मषिः
मषि m., and मषी f. मषी̆, and मसि m., मसी f. मसि,<BR> 1. Ink, Kathās. 4, 69 (षी); also in Pehlewi मसि, Haug. in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, xix. 305; if it was originally the juice of the cuttle-fish, which the Romans also used for writing, it may be akin to Zend. मश्यो = Sskr. मत्स्ÿअ.<BR> 2. The stalk of the Nyctanthes tristis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मष्क्
मष्क् मष्क्, see मस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्
मस् मस् (cf. मा), i. 4, Par. To mete, to measure.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. मस्त.<BR> --Cf. perhaps μεστός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसार|मसारः
मसार मसार, m. A sapphire, Rām. 3, 48, 12 (? cf. Böhtl. s. v. गल्वर्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसि|मसिः
मसि, मसी मसी̆, see मषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिन|मसिनं
मसिन मसिन, adj. Well ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसुर|मसुरः
मसुर and मसूर मसू̆र,<BR> 1. m., and f. रा, A sort of lentil, Ervum hirsutum, Suśr. 1, 24, 9; 26, 1 (?).<BR> 2. f. रा, A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरिका
मसूरिका मसूरिका, i. e. मसूर + क, f. A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसृण|मसृणं
मसृण मसृण,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Soft, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 14.<BR> 2. Unctuous, shining, ib. 107, 6.<BR> II. f. णा, Linseed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसृणित
मसृणित मसृणित, i. e. मसृण + इत, adj. Polished. Utt. Rāmac. 129, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्क्
† मस्क् मस्क्, मष्क् मष्क्, and मक्क् मक्क्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्कर|मस्करः
मस्कर मस्कर, m. A bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्करिन्
मस्करिन् मस्करिन्, i. e. मस्कर + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A religious mendicant, Lass. 76, 15.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्त|मस्तं
मस्त मस्त (perhaps vb. मन्), n. The head, Lass. 70, 2 (at the end of a comp. adj.); cf. मस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तक|मस्तकं|मस्तकः
मस्तक मस्त + क, m. n.<BR> 1. The head, Pañc. 246, 14.<BR> 2. The top, the summit, Man. 4, 47; Pañc. 262, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमस्तक|मधुमस्तकं
मधु- + मस्तक मधु- + मस्तक, n. a sweetmeat made of flour, honey, oil, and butter (cf. मस्तु),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तिष्क|मस्तिष्कं
मस्तिष्क मस्तिष्क (akin to मस्त), n. The brain, Lass. 4, 17; Hariv. 4740.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तु
मस्तु मस्तु, n. Whey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तुलुङ्ग|मस्तुलुंग|मस्तुलुङ्गः
मस्तुलुङ्ग and मस्तुलुङ्गक मस्तुलुङ्ग and ˚ग + क, m. The brain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह्
मह् मह्, i. 1, and i. 10, Par. To adore, to honour Pañc. ii. d. 72; Kir. 5, 24. The original form was मघ् and the original signification ‘To be great, powerful.’<BR> --Cf. मघ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a " target="_blank">Page0693-a + 45</a>] महन्त्, and Goth. and A.S. magan; Goth. magu, mavi, mahts; A.S. maeht, meaht, miht; Goth. mahteig; O.H.G. magan, great, heavy; A.S. maegn, meagn, strength; Goth. magus, a boy; A.S. mag, maeg, maegen, macian; Goth. magaths; A.S. maegdh; O.H.G. machôn; A.S. macian; μόγος, μόχθος, μόλις (for μόγλοις), μέγαρον (cf. O.H.G. ga-mah; N.G. Gemach), μηχανή, μηχανάομαι; Lat. magnus, mactus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह|महं|महः
मह मह् + अ,<BR> I. adj. f. ही, Great, Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 88, 14.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. A festival.<BR> 3. A sacrifice.<BR> 4. A buffalo.<BR> III. f. हा, A cow.<BR> IV. f. ही.<BR> 1. The earth, Utt. Rāmac. 172, 13 (as deity); Daśak. in Chr. 179, 6; landed property, Pañc. i. d. 322.<BR> 2. A cow.<BR> 3. Name of a river.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. मईअ, मैअ᳓च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मह
धनुर्मह धनुर्मह, i. e. धनुस्-, m. a festival at the consecration of a bow, Hariv. 4391.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्त्व|महत्त्वं
महत्त्व महत्त्व, i. e. महन्त् + त्व, n. Greatness, Pañc. iii. d. 254; finite magnitude (as found in the त्रसरेणु), Bhāṣāp. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महन्त्|महत्
महन्त् महन्त् (properly ptcple. pres. of मह्); the bases of all cases, except the sing. voc. msc., are महान्त् and महत्; ved. महाम् instead of महान्तम्, Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14.<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Great, large, Vikr. 11, 18.<BR> 2. Pre-eminent, Hit. pr. d. 28, M.M.<BR> 3. Much, many.<BR> 4. Excellent, Nal. 2, 25.<BR> II. adv. हत्, Exceedingly, much, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 2.<BR> III. m. The intellectual principle, Sāṅkhyak. 3, 22; Man. 12, 14.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Greatness, infinity, Bhāṣāp. 25.<BR> 2. Kingdom.<BR> V. f. अती, The lute of Nārada.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μέγας, μεγάλου, etc., μείζων, μέγεθος, μεγαίρω, μάλα, μᾶλλον, μῆκος, μακρός, μάκαρες; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b " target="_blank">Page0693-b + 41</a>] Lat. magis, major, majus, maximus, magister, Majus; Goth. mikils; A.S. meagol, micel, micyl, etc.; comparat. Goth. mais; A.S. ma, mae; superl. Goth. maist; A.S. maest, maegeste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमहन्त्|विमहत्
वि- + महन्त् वि- + महन्त्, adj. exceedingly tall, Indr. 1, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहन्त्|सुमहत्
सु- + महन्त् सु- + महन्त्, adj. 1. very great, Chr. 12, 26; very tall, Rām. 3, 55, 1. 2. very important, Nal. 8, 2. 3. abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्
महर् महर्, and महर्लोक महर्-लोक (महर् for महन्, akin to महन्त्, or anomal. for महस्), m. The abode of the saints who survive a destruction of the world; it is said to be situated above the polar star, Weber, Ind. St. ii. 178; cf. 213; Vedāntas. in Chr. 269, 1 (महर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्द्धि
महर्द्धि महर्द्धि, i. e. महा-ऋद्धि, adj. Very perfect, Rājat. 5, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्षि|महर्षिः
महर्षि महर्षि, i. e. महा-ऋषि, m. A sage of a pre-eminent class, Man. 1, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस्
महस् मह् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Light, lustre, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 5; Lass. 97, 6 = Rigv. vi. 64, 2.<BR> 2. A festival.<BR> 3. A sacrifice.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषमहस्
पीयूष- + महस् पीयूष- + महस्, m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रमहस्
मित्र- + महस् मित्र- + महस्, adj. having a friendly light or lustre, Chr. 289, 11 = Rigv. i. 50, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमहस्
वि- + महस् वि- + महस्, adj. very resplendent, Chr. 292, 1 = Rigv. i. 86, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस|महसं
महस महस, n. Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महा
महाऽ महा-, a substitute for महन्त्, when former part of compounds of the Bahuvrīhi and Karmadhāraya classes; e. g. महा-राज, m. A great king, Chr. 3, 4. महा-दुर्ग, adj. Very difficult to be crossed, Pañc. 123, 17. महा-तपस्, adj. Practising great austerities, Chr. 9, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्यागमय
महात्यागमय महा-त्याग + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting in great liberality, Kathās. 23, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानस|महानसं|महानसः
महानस महानस, n. A kitchen, Pañc. 253, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्क|महायशस्कः
महायशस्क महा-यशस् + क, adj. Illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजिक|महाराजिकः
महाराजिक महाराजिक, i. e. महा-राज + इक, m. A kind of demigod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावस|महावसः
महावस महा-वस (vb. वस्), m. The Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहसिकता
महासाहसिकता महा-साहसिक + ता, f. Great boldness, Pañc. 129, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महि|महिः
महि मह् + इ, ved. adj. Great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिका
महिका महिका, f. Frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महित्वन
महित्वन महि + त्वन, ved. n. Greatness, Chr. 291, 7 = Rigv. i. 85, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिमन्
महिमन् महिमन्, i. e. महन्त् + इमन्, m. Greatness, Hit. ii. d. 2; majesty, Vikr. d. 5; exaltation, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतत्यागमहिमन्
अ-कृत-त्याग- + महिमन् अ-कृत-त्याग- + महिमन्, adj. not having practised the greatness (i. e. great virtue) of liberality, Pañc. ii. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघमहिमन्
अ-मोघ- + महिमन् अ-मोघ- + महिमन्, adj. possessing a greatness which is not devoid of effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिला
महिला महिला, f.<BR> 1. A woman, Hit. iv. d. 54.<BR> 2. A plant = प्रियङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिष|महिषः
महिष मह् + इष (cf. मह),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A buffalo, Hit. i. d. 86, M.M.<BR> 2. The emblem and vehicle of Yama.<BR> II. f. षी.<BR> 1. The female buffalo, Pañc. ii. d. 53; 252, 15.<BR> 2. A queen, Utt. Rāmac. 159, 9; Pañc. 27, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रमहिषी
अग्र- + महिषी अग्र- + महिष, f. the first of a king's wives, Rām. 5, 22, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मही
मही मही, see मह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीक्षित्
महीक्षित् मही-क्षि + त्, m. A king, Chr. 3, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीधर|महीधरः
महीधर, महीध्र मही-धर, and महिद्र, i. e. महि-धृ + अ, m. A mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 10 (ध्र).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समहीधर
स-मही-धर स-मही-धर, adj. mountainous, Hit. iii. d. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीप|महीपः
महीप मही-प (vb. 2. पा), m. A king, Pañc. i. d. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभुज्
महीभुज् मही-भुज्, m. A king, Hit. iii. d. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभृत्
महीभृत् मही-भृ + त्, m.<BR> 1. A mountain; in मेरु-, The mountain called Meru, Kir. 5, 1.<BR> 2. A king, Pañc. iii. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीमय|महीमयः
महीमय मही + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of earth, earthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीय
महीय महीय, a denomin. derived from मह, Ātm. (Par., Rām. 6, 82, 44).<BR> 1. To be honoured, Man. 4, 260; pass. महीय्य, The same, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 38.<BR> 2. To be exalted, Śāk. d. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीरुह्
महीरुह् मही-रुह्, and महीरुह मही-रुह् + अ, m. A tree, Kir. 5, 10 (-रुह्); Bhāṣāp. 1 (संसार-महीरुह, The tree-like world).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेला
महेला महेला, f. A woman (cf. महिला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
1. मा मा, ii. 2, Par., ii. 3, मिमा, मिमी, and † i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To mete, to measure, Chr. 289, 7 = Rigv. i. 50, 7.<BR> 2. with न, To surmount, Śiś. 1, 23.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मित.<BR> 1. Moderate, little, Pañc. i. d. 98 (in few words); iii. d. 156.<BR> 2. Scattered.<BR> 3. Known.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. मेय, Measurable.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. immeasurable, Chr. 37, 29.<BR> --Caus. मापय.<BR> 1. To cause to be measured, to get measured, MBh. 1, 2024.<BR> 2. To get prepared, 14, 2521.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To infer, to conclude, MBh. 3, 12470; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 610 (कर्मामनेय, i. e. कर्मन्-, To be found out by one's actions, cf. Hit. iv. d. 100, where कार्यान्˚, to be inferred from the effects); also pass. (मीय), in the signification of the active, MBh. 1, 7043 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-a " target="_blank">Page0695-a + 42</a>] (regularly, Kir. 5, 47).<BR> 2. To reconcile, MBh. 3, 286.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To admeasure, to give, Chr. 294, 7 = Rigv. i. 92, 7.<BR> 2. To compare, Caurap. 43 (anomal. infin. -मितुम्). उपमित, Like, Bhartṛ. 3, 17. उपमेय, Comparable, Megh. 53.<BR> --With नि नि; comp. ptcple. pf. pass. दुस्-निमित, adj. Put down badly, Ragh. 7, 10. निमेय, Measurable, MBh. 13, 2676.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To build, Rām. 1, 5, 6.<BR> 2. To create, Man. 1, 13; Vikr. d. 9.<BR> 3. To cause, Pañc. v. d. 67.<BR> 4. To make, Hit. 48, 2, M.M.; MBh. 1, 2026.<BR> 5. To form, Man. 1, 21; to compose, Hit. i. d. 46, M.M.<BR> --With अभिनिस् अभि-निस्, To create, Kir. 5, 3.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्,<BR> 1. To create, Nal. 17, 7.<BR> 2. To prepare, Rām. 1, 13, 45.<BR> --With परि परि, परिमित,<BR> 1. Limited, Bhartṛ. 3, 50.<BR> 2. Moderate, Rām. 3, 55, 20.<BR> 3. Measured.<BR> 4. Regulated.<BR> 5. Joined. परिमेय, Measurable, few, Rājat. 4, 414.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, immeasurable, MBh. 1, 2455.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To understand, Hit. 74, 7. प्रमित,<BR> 1. Measured.<BR> 2. Known.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-प्रमेय, adj. Unfathomable, Man. 1, 3.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To compare, Rājat. 5, 482.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संमित,<BR> 1. Like, resembling.<BR> 2. Of equal measure, conformable, Sāv. 5, 30.<BR> 3. Reaching to, Man. 2, 46.<BR> 4. Measured.<BR> --Comp.<BR> मृत्यु-, adj. death-like, Chr. 35, 6.<BR> वेद-, adj. made up of the Vedas, Johns. Sel. 94, 53.<BR> --Cf. μάρις, μανός, μέτρον, ἄ-μοτον, μοτόν, μίτος, μῖμος, μιμέομαι, μάτιον, μόδιος, μέδιμνος, μέδομαι, μῆδος; Lat. im-mânis, metior (a denomin. of an old ptcple. pres., cf. mensus), mētare, manus, materia, maturus, imitari, mos, modus, meditari; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b " target="_blank">Page0695-b + 40</a>] O.H.G. mez; O.N. met; Goth. mitan; A.S. metan, maedhian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अ- + मा अ- + मा, adj. immeasurable, measureless, Pañc. iii. d. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
2. मा मा, ii. 3, मिमा, मिमी, Ātm. (ved. Par.). To sound, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
3. मा मा, indecl. A prohibitive particle.<BR> 1. No, with imperat. also with imperf. and aor., which then drop their augment, Vikr. d. 110; in epic poetry it is sometimes retained, Chr. 6, 9; also Utt. Rāmac. 36, 7.<BR> 2. With following स्म, The same, Chr. 41, 4; 42, 10.<BR> 3. Doubled, मामा, In no way, Chr. 26, 66; Vikr. 12, 1.<BR> --Cf. μή; perhaps Lat. ne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस|मांसं|मांसः
मांस मांस, the base of many cases is optionally मांस् मांस्, n. Flesh, Pañc. iii. d. 139; meat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांस|अधिमांसः
अधि- + मांस अधि- + मांस, m. Fleshy excrescences on the eye, Suśr. 2, 310, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमांस|दंतमांस
दन्त- + मांस दन्त- + मांस, n. the gums, Suśr. 1, 125, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मांस
निर्मांस निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. fleshless, Hit. ii. d. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमांस
पूति- + मांस पूति- + मांस, n. dead or decayed flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांस
पृष्ठ- + मांस पृष्ठ- + मांस, n. the flesh of the back; with खाद्, भक्ष्, to assail from behind, Hit. i. d. 80, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामांस|महामांसं
महा- + मांस महा- + मांस, n. man's flesh, Kathās. 20, 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथामांस|वृथामांसं
वृथा- + मांस वृथा- + मांस, n. flesh which has not been sacrificed, Man. 4, 213; 5, 34 (read वृथामांसानि in one word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसज|मांसजं
मांसज मांस-ज, n. Marrow, or serum of the flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसत्व
मांसत्व मांस + त्व, n. The true etymology of मांस, Man. 5, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसमय
मांसमय मांस + मय, adj., f. यी, Of flesh, MBh. 1, 4495.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसल|मांसलं|मांसलः
मांसल मांस + ल, adj. Strong, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसाद
मांसाद मांसाद, i. e. माम्स-अद् + अ, and मांसाशिन् मांसाशिन्, i. e. मांस- 2. अश् + इन्, adj. Feeding on flesh, Pañc. 59, 10; 60, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिक|मांसिकः
मांसिक मांसिक, i. e. माम्स + इक, 1. A vendor of flesh or meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्द|माकंद|माकंदः|माकन्दः
माकन्द माकन्द The name of a town, Johns. Sel. 33, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकरन्द|माकरंद
माकरन्द माकरन्द, i. e. मकरन्द + अ, adj. Consisting of the nectar of flowers, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिक|माक्षिकं|माक्षिकः
माक्षिक माक्षिक, i. e. मक्षिका + अ, n.<BR> 1. Honey.<BR> 2. A peculiar mineral substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकज|माक्षिकजं
माक्षिकज माक्षिक-ज, n. Beeswax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागध|मागधः
मागध मागध, i. e. मगध + अ,<BR> I. adj. Belonging to, or produced in, Magadha, Ragh. 1, 57.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. pl. The inhabitants of Magadha.<BR> 2. A bard, Johns. Sel. 37, 16.<BR> 3. The son of a Vaiśya by a Kṣatriya woman, Man. 10, 11.<BR> 4. Cumin-seed.<BR> III. f. धी.<BR> 1. One of the Prakṛta dialects.<BR> 2. A kind of jasmine, Jasminum auriculatum.<BR> 3. Long pepper.<BR> 4. A sort of cardamoms.<BR> 5. Refined sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ|माघः
माघ माघ, m.<BR> 1. A month, January--February, Pañc. 169, 6.<BR> 2. The name of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघवत
माघवत माघवत, i. e. मघवन्त् + अ, adj. Belonging to Indra, Utt. Rāmac. 124, 11 (-चाप, the rainbow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघवन|माघवनं
माघवन माघवन, i. e. मघवन् + अ, adj., f. नी, Ruled by Indra, Śiś. 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्क्ष्|मांक्ष्
† माङ्क्ष् मान्क्ष्, i. 1, Par. To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलिक|मांगलिक
माङ्गलिक माङ्गलिक, i. e. मङ्गल + इक,<BR> I. adj. Propitious.<BR> II. f. का, A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गल्य|मांगल्य|माङ्गल्यं
माङ्गल्य माङ्गल्य, i. e. मङ्गल + य,<BR> I. adj. Portending good fortune, Śāk. d. 80.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Prosperity.<BR> 2. Festivity, festival, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचल|माचलः
माचल मा-चल् + अ (probably a noun formed from मा चल, ‘Do not stir’), m.<BR> 1. A crocodile.<BR> 2. A robber.<BR> 3. Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिर|माचिरं
माचिर मा-चिर, adj. Short, Cāṇ. 44 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410; ˚रम्, adv. Without delay, quickly, Chr. 19, 5; 57, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठ|मांजिष्ठ|माञ्जिष्ठं
माञ्जिष्ठ माञ्जिष्ठ, i. e. मञ्जिष्ठा + अ,<BR> I. adj. Of a red colour, Rām. 2, 94, 5.<BR> II. n. Red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठिक|मांजिष्ठिक
माञ्जिष्ठिक माञ्जिष्ठिक, i. e. मञ्जिष्ठा + इक, adj. Dyed with Bengal madder, red, Utt. Rāmac. 106, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठर|माठरः
माठर माठर, m.<BR> 1. One of the sun's attendants.<BR> 2. Vyāsa.<BR> 3. A distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठव्य
माठव्य माठव्य, m. A proper name, Śāk. 23, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्
माड् माड्, see माह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव|माणवः
माणव माणव (= मानव. q. cf.), m.<BR> 1. A child.<BR> 2. A man, in a contemptuous sense.<BR> 3. A necklace of sixteen strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवक|माणवकः
माणवक माणव + क, m. A proper name, Vikr. 44, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिका
माणिका माणिका (akin to मणि), f. A weight of eight Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिक्य|माणिक्यं
माणिक्य माणिक्य, i. e. मणि + क + य,<BR> I. n. A ruby, Pañc. 207, 23.<BR> II. f. या, A house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिमन्थ|माणिमंथ|माणिमंथं|माणिमन्थं
माणिमन्थ माणिमन्थ, i. e. मणि-मन्थ + अ, n. Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डलिक|मांडलिक|माण्डलिकः
माण्डलिक माण्डलिक, i. e. मण्डल + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a " target="_blank">Page0697-a + 40</a>] m. The superintendent of a district or province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डव्य
माण्डव्य माण्डव्य, i. e. मण्डु, A proper name, + य, patronym., m. A proper name, Chr. 46, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातङ्ग|मातंग|मातंगः|मातङ्गः
मातङ्ग मातङ्ग, i. e. मतंग + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An outcaste, Rājat. 5, 6.<BR> 2. A barbarian.<BR> 3. An elephant, Hit. ii. d. 63.<BR> 4. The sacred fig-tree, Ficus religiosa.<BR> II. f. गी, Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिश्वन्
मातरिश्वन् मातरिश्वन्, i. e. मातृ + इ-श्वन् (vb. श्वि), m. Air, wind, Chr. 27, 4; Kir. 5, 36; Daśak. in Chr. 200, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलि|मातलिः
मातलि मातलि, m. The charioteer of Indra, Śāk. 94, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातापितृ
मातापितृ माता-पितृ (माता, nom. sing. of मातृ), m. du. Mother and father, Man. 3, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातामह|मातामहः
मातामह माता-मह (माता, nom. sing. of मातृ),<BR> 1. m. A maternal grandfather, Vikr. d. 101.<BR> 2. f. हि, A maternal grandmother, Rājat. 5, 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल|मातुलः
मातुल मातुल, i. e. मतृ + अ,<BR> I. m. A maternal uncle, Rājat. 5, 292; Pañc. 215, 10.<BR> II. f. ला, ली, and लानि, The wife of a maternal uncle.<BR> III. f. लानी, Hemp, Cannabis sativa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलक|मातुलकः
मातुलक मातुल + क, m. Dear uncle, Pañc. 52, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ मा + तृ, f.<BR> 1. A mother, Pañc. ii. d. 190.<BR> 2. A divine mother, the personified energy of a deity, Pañc. pr. d. 1; MBh. 9, 2619 sqq.<BR> 3. The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 4. The earth.<BR> 5. A cow.<BR> 6. Space, æther.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mater; μήτηρ; A.S. móder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमातृ
गो- + मातृ गो- + मातृ, adj. having a cow as mother, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्मातृ
जगन्मातृ जगन्मातृ, i. e. जगत्-, f. epithet of: 1. Durgā, Hariv. 10276; 2. Lakṣmī, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b " target="_blank">Page0697-b + 42</a>] Mārk. P. 18, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमातृ
नाग- + मातृ नाग- + मातृ, f. the mother of the serpents, epithet of Surasā, Rām. 5, 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृ|रंगमातृ
रङ्ग- + मातृ रङ्ग- + मातृ, f. 1. a bawd. 2. lac, the animal dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
वि- + मातृ वि- + मातृ, f. a stepmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमातृ
वेद- + मातृ वेद- + मातृ, f. source of the Veda, epithet of the Gāyatrī, a vedic prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिलीमातृ
शाण्डिली- + मातृ शाण्डिली- + मातृ, f. a matron descended from Śaṇḍila, Pañc. 122, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक मातृ + क,<BR> I. adj. Maternal, Man. 9, 92.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. A mother.<BR> 2. A nurse, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 3.<BR> 3. A goddess.<BR> 4. The alphabet.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृक|देवमातृकः
देव-मातृ + क देव-मातृ + क, adj. deprived of any water but rain. MBh. 2, 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृक
रङ्ग- + मातृक रङ्ग- + मातृक, f. lac, the animal dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृवत्
मातृवत् मातृ + वत्, adv. As a mother, as with a mother, Man. 2, 133; as on a mother, Hit. i. d. 13, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसृ
मातृष्वसृ मातृष्वसृ, i. e. मातृ-स्रसृ, f. A mother's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसेय|मातृष्वसेयः
मातृष्वसेय मातृष्वसेय, and मातृष्वस्रीय मातृष्वस्रीय, i. e. मातृ-ष्वसृ + एय, or ईय,<BR> 1. m. A mother's sister's son.<BR> 2. f. सेयी, स्रीया, A mother's sister's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र मा + त्र,<BR> I. f. त्रा.<BR> 1. Measure, Hit. 121, 5 (distance).<BR> 2. Quantity, Pañc. 32, 24; 226. 14 (द्रव्य-, f. All things of value).<BR> 3. Wealth, substance, Pañc. 34, 13.<BR> 4. Requisite, Pañc. 265, 5 (luggage); material.<BR> 5. A little, a trifle, Pañc. i. d. 46; an atom, Man. 1, 27; an element. Bhag. 2, 14 (also n., Bhāg. P. 5, 11, 9).<BR> 6. A moment.<BR> 7. A short vowel.<BR> 8. Quantity in metre, Pañc. v. d. 43.<BR> 9. An ear-ring.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The totality, the whole, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 17.<BR> 2. As latter part of comp. words (Being limited), alone, only, Cāṇ. 70 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411 (cf. comp.).<BR> 3. As [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-a " target="_blank">Page0698-a + 48</a>] latter part of compounds, often almost without any signification; cf. e. g. अर्थ-मात्र.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μέτρον.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमात्र
अक्ष- + मात्र अक्ष- + मात्र, n. a moment, Arj. 8, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलमात्र
अङ्गुल- + मात्र अङ्गुल- + मात्र, n. only the breadth of a thumb, Pañc. 124, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमात्र|अतिमात्रं
अति- + मात्र अति- + मात्र, adj. excessive, much, overstepping the boundaries, Rām. 2, 12, 108. ˚र + म्, adv. exceedingly, Rām. 2, 93, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थमात्र
अर्थ- + मात्र अर्थ- + मात्र, f. रा, and n. money, Pañc. 132, 25. and 33, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममात्र
आत्म(न्)- + मात्र आत्म(न्)- + मात्र, f. रा, the developments of themselves, Man. 1, 16 (Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतावन्मात्र
एतावन्मात्र एतावन्मात्र, i. e. एतावन्त्-, adj. so great, Pañc. 108, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियन्मात्र|कियन्मात्रः
कियन्मात्र कियन्मात्र, i. e. कियन्त्-, adj. of little importance, Pañc. 47, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशमात्र
क्रोश- + मात्र क्रोश- + मात्र, adj. having the measure of a krośa, ib. i. d. 447.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणमात्रम्
क्षण-मात्र + म् क्षण-मात्र + म्, adv. a moment, Vikr. 7, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमात्र
जात- + मात्र जात- + मात्र, adj., f. रा, just born, immediately after one's birth or beginning, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 18; Pañc. i. d. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमात्र
जाति- + मात्र जाति- + मात्र, n. nothing but birth, Man. 8, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमात्र
जीव- + मात्र जीव- + मात्र, n. germ alone, Pañc. 200, 12 (with न, not even a germ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्र|तन्मात्रं
तन्मात्र तन्मात्र, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालमात्रम्
ताल-मात्र + म् ताल-मात्र + म्, adv. only a moment, Rām. 3, 50, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावन्मात्र
तावन्मात्र तावन्मात्र, i. e. तावन्त्-, adj., f. री, so much, Bhāg. P. 4, 8, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनमात्र
दर्शन- + मात्र दर्शन- + मात्र, n. seeing only, Pañc. 128, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात ध्यात (vb. ध्यै)-, n. only thought of, immediately after having been thought of, Kathās. 5, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगमात्र
नग- + मात्र नग- + मात्र, adj. large as mountains, Arj. 8, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममात्र
नाम(न्)- + मात्र नाम(न्)- + मात्र,<BR> I. n. nothing but the name, only the name, Pañc. iii. d. 78.<BR> II. adj. bearing only the name of something (not being it really), Pañc. i. d. 87; ii. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदातिमात्र
पदाति- + मात्र पदाति- + मात्र, m. a mere foot soldier, Rājat. 5, 424.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापक्षयमात्र
पाप-क्षय- + मात्र पाप-क्षय- + मात्र (n.), entire destruction (or expiation) of sins, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणधारणमात्र
प्राण-धारण- + मात्र प्राण-धारण- + मात्र, adj., f. रा, only sufficing for bare subsistence, Pañc. 236, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमात्र
बलि- + मात्र बलि- + मात्र, n. even the offering called बलि, Pañc. 114, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्र|महामात्रः
महा- + मात्र महा- + मात्र,<BR> I. m. 1. a king's minister. 2. an elephant driver, or breaker, Man. 9, 259. 3. superintendent of the elephants. 4. a man of wealth and consequence.<BR> II. f. त्री. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b " target="_blank">Page0698-b + 43</a>] 1. the wife of an officer of state. 2. the wife of a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तमात्र
मूर्त- + मात्र मूर्त- + मात्र, n. only corporeal, Bhāṣāp. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिमात्र
मूर्ति- + मात्र मूर्ति- + मात्र, f. a minute substantial portion, Man. 1, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगमात्र
युग- + मात्र युग- + मात्र (n. ?), scarcely, Sāv. 4, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षमात्र
वर्ष- + मात्र वर्ष- + मात्र, n. one year only, Pañc. 134, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मात्र
वाङ्मात्र वाङ्मात्र, i. e. वाच्-, n. speech only, Pañc. ii. d. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपमात्र
रूप- + मात्र रूप- + मात्र, n. only beauty, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तामात्र
वार्त्ता- + मात्र वार्त्ता- + मात्र, (n.), a superficial knowledge, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तमात्र
वित्त- + मात्र वित्त- + मात्र, f. रा, wealth, Pañc. 32, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दमात्र
शब्द- + मात्र शब्द- + मात्र, n. mere sound, sound only, Pañc. 20, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरमात्र
शरीर- + मात्र शरीर- + मात्र, n. the mere person, body only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधानमात्र
समाधान- + मात्र समाधान- + मात्र, n. only religious contemplation, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेपमात्र
संक्षेप- + मात्र संक्षेप- + मात्र, n. only an abridgement, Pañc. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतमात्र
स्मृत- + मात्र स्मृत- + मात्र, adj. only remembered, Pañc. 48, 8 (without being called, but only in consequence of being thought of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमात्र
हस्तिमात्र हस्तिमात्र, i. e. हस्तिन्-, adj. as great as an elephant, Pañc. i. d. 373.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रक
ऽमात्रक -मात्र + क, a substitute for मात्र, when latter part of a comp. adj.; e. g. अङ्गुष्ठ-, adj. As long as a thumb, Nal. 14, 9. स्तन्य-त्याग-, adj. In which (viz. age), one is just weaned, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर
मात्सर मात्सर, i. e. मत्सर + अ, adj. Envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर्य|मात्सर्यं|मात्सर्य्य|मात्सर्य्यं
मात्सर्य मात्सर्य, i. e. मत्सर + य, n.<BR> 1. Envy, Hit. i. d. 194, M.M.<BR> 2. Malice.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मात्सर्य
दुस्- + मात्सर्य दुस्- + मात्सर्य, n. wicked envy, Bhartṛ. 3, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यक
मात्स्यक मात्स्यक, i. e. मत्स्य + क, adj. Relating to a fish, Matsyop. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ|माथः
माथ माथ, i. e. मथ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Churning.<BR> 2. A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद|मादः
माद माद, i. e. मद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Intoxication.<BR> 2. Joy.<BR> 3. Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादन|मादनं|मादनः
मादन मादन, i. e. मद्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Delighting.<BR> 2. Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृश्
मादृश् मादृश्, and मादृश मादृश, i. e. 2. मद्-दृश् and दृश् + अ, adj. Like me, Lass. 41, 17 (दृश्); Utt. Rāmac. 42, 15 (श).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्य
माद्य माद्य, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 3. but I prefer correcting मान्द्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रवती
माद्रवती माद्रवती, i. e. मद्र + अ + वन्त् + ई, f. The wife of Paṇḍu, and mother of the two youngest Pāṇḍava princes, Draup. 8, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्री
माद्री माद्री, i. e. मद्र + अ + ई, f. The wife of Paṇḍu, and mother of the two youngest Pāṇḍava princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रेय|माद्रेयः
माद्रेय माद्रेय, i. e. माद्री + एय, m. A son of Mādrī, i. e. Nakula or Sahadeva, Johns. Sel. 27, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव माधव, i. e. मधु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Made of honey.<BR> 2. Belonging to the spring, Vikr. d. 23 (cf. Sch.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu, Pañc. i. d. 238.<BR> 2. The month Vaiśākha.<BR> 3. Spring.<BR> III. f. वी.<BR> 1. Sugar, clayed or candied.<BR> 2. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 3. Durgā.<BR> 4. A large creeper, Gaertnera racemosa, Megh. 76.<BR> 5. A bawd.<BR> IV. n. Sweetness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामाधवी
लता-माधवी लता-माधवी, f. Gaertnera racemosa, Śāk. d. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवसेनाराजन्
माधवसेनाराजन् माधव-सेना-राजन्, m. A proper name. Daśak. in Chr. 191, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुपर्किक
माधुपर्किक माधुपर्किक, i. e. मधुपर्क + इक, adj. Presented as a token of respect to a guest, Man. 9, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमत
माधुमत माधुमत, m. pl. The people of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर|माधुरं
माधुर माधुर, i. e. मधुर + अ,<BR> I. n. Arabian jasmine.<BR> II. f. री, Spirituous liquor; see माधुर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्य|माधुर्यं|माधुर्य्य|माधुर्य्यं
माधुर्य माधुर्य, i. e. मधुर + य, n., and f. री.<BR> 1. Sweetness, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b " target="_blank">Page0699-b + 41</a>] Gracefulness, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूक्षेपालापमाधुर्य
भ्रूक्षेपालाप- + माधुर्य भ्रूक्षेपालाप- + माधुर्य, i. e. भ्रू-क्षेप-आलाप-, n. the gracefulness of the motion of one's brows and speech, Indr. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक माधूक (from मधु and मधूक), adj.<BR> 1. Sweet-voiced, Man. 10, 33.<BR> 2. Made of the Bassia tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य माध्य, i. e. मध्य + अ, adj., f. या, and माध्यम माध्यम, i. e. मध्यम + अ, adj., f. मी, Middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ|माध्यस्थं
माध्यस्थ माध्यस्थ, i. e. मध्यस्थ + अ, n.<BR> 1. Middle state.<BR> 2. Indifference to earthly objects, Man. 4, 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्य|माध्यस्थ्यं
माध्यस्थ्य माध्यस्थ्य, i. e. मध्यस्थ + य, n.<BR> 1. Mediation.<BR> 2. Office of an arbiter, Lass. 92, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वक|माध्वकं
माध्वक माध्वक, i. e. मधु + अ + क (anomal.), n. Spirit distilled from the flowers of the Bassia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वी
माध्वी माध्वी, i. e. मधु + अ + ई (anomal.), f.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the Bassia, Man. 11, 94.<BR> 2. A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीक|माध्वीकं
माध्वीक माध्वी + क, n.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor made from the Bassia.<BR> 2. Wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्
मान् मान्, i. 10 (properly Caus. of मन्, q. cf.), and † i. 1, Par. To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान मान,<BR> I. m., i. e. मान् + अ.<BR> 1. Self-confidence, Pañc. v. d. 3.<BR> 2. Pride, Pañc. iii. d. 13.<BR> 3. Arrogance, Pañc. iii. d. 108; female caprice, indignation, anger, Vikr. 37, 8.<BR> 4. Honour, Pañc. 16, 4; i. d. 251.<BR> 5. Taking.<BR> 6. An agent.<BR> 7. A blockhead.<BR> 8. A barbarian.<BR> II. i. e. मा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Measuring, Bhāṣāp. 108.<BR> 2. Measure in general, Pañc. 7, 16 (कूट-तुला-, With a wrong balance).<BR> 3. A particular measure, the fourth part [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a " target="_blank">Page0700-a + 43</a>] of a खारी.<BR> 4. The computation of the duration of a year.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमान|अतिमानः
अति- + मान अति- + मान, m. arrogance, Cāṇ. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग्नमानम्
अ-भग्न-मान + म् अ-भग्न-मान + म्, adv. without injury to one's honour, Hit. ii. d. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मान
निर्मान निर्म्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from pride, Bhartṛ. 3, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयमान|प्रणयमानः
प्रणय- + मान प्रणय- + मान, m. lover's quarrels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमान|बहुमानः
बहु- + मान बहु- + मान, m. reverence, respect, Vikr. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासमान|मासमानः
मास- + मान मास- + मान, m. a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबहुमानम्
स-बहु-मान + म् स-बहु-मान + म्, adv. with great reverence, Pañc. 130, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानद|मानदः
मानद मान-द (vb. दा), adj.<BR> 1. Inspiring pride; a respectful address, used only in the voc. sing. m., Chr. 38, 15; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानधानिका
मानधानिका मानधानिका, f. A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयितृ
मानयितृ मानयितृ, i. e. मन्, Caus., + तृ, m. One who honours, Indr. 4, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव मानव, i. e. मनु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Human, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 1.<BR> 2. Declared by Manu, Chr. 135, 1. 2.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A man, Pañc. iii. d. 61; mankind, Chr. 8, 33.<BR> 2. A boy.<BR> III. f. वी.<BR> 1. A woman.<BR> 2. A daughter of the first Manu.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटमानव
कपट- + मानव कपट- + मानव, m. under the disguise of a man, Bhāg. P. 1, 1, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डमानव|दण्डमानवः
दण्ड- + मानव दण्ड- + मानव, m. a man bearing a staff, a Brāhmaṇa, Rām. 2, 32, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवन्त्|मानवत्
मानवन्त् मान + वन्त्, adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Proud.<BR> 2. Angry, Śiś. 9, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्य|मानव्यं
मानव्य मानव्य, i. e. मानव + य, n. A multitude of boys (and of men).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस मानस, i. e. मनस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी, Mental, Man. 2, 85; Vikr. d. 30.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The mind, the seat of reasoning and feeling, Pañc. v. 12; Bhāṣāp. 33; Hit. i. d. 140, M.M.; Pañc. iii. d. 45 (भय-संत्रस्त-, adj. Having one's mind terrified by fear); iii. d. 180 (शोक-संतप्त-, burned by grief).<BR> 2. The name of a lake, Vikr. d. 93.<BR> III. f. सी, A goddess of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b " target="_blank">Page0700-b + 45</a>] the Jainas.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमानस
अन्य- + मानस अन्य- + मानस, adj., f. सा, being in love with another, Chr. 14, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यमानस
अन्-अन्य- + मानस अन्-अन्य- + मानस, adj. intent only on one object, Indr. 5, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमानस
पूर्ण- + मानस पूर्ण- + मानस (see vb. पॄ), adj. satisfied, Rām. 3, 75, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टमानस|हृष्टमानसः
हृष्ट- + मानस हृष्ट- + मानस (vb. हृष्). adj. glad, happy, Johns. Sel. 14, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिक
ऽमानिक -मानिक, i. e. मानिन् + क, in पन्डित-, adj. Fancying one's self a learned man, MBh. 12, 6738.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन् मानिन्, i. e. मान + इन्, and मन् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Proud, Ragh. 13, 38.<BR> 2. When latter part of a comp., Who thinks or fancies (cf. comp.).<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A woman, especially one indignant towards her lover, Vikr. d. 118.<BR> 2. A plant, commonly प्रियङ्गु.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अ- + मानिन् अ- + मानिन्, adj. not proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानिन्
अति- + मानिन् अति- + मानिन्, adj. very proud, Rām. 3, 34, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेनमानिन्
अ-स्तेन- + मानिन् अ-स्तेन- + मानिन्, adj. pretending to have committed no theft, Man. 8, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टमानिन्
धृष्ट- + मानिन् धृष्ट- + मानिन्, adj. arrogant, Rām. 2, 96, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमानिन्
पण्डित- + मानिन् पण्डित- + मानिन्, adj. fancying one's self a learned man, MBh. 4, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमानिन्
पुरुष- + मानिन् पुरुष- + मानिन्, adj. fancying one's self a hero, MBh. 5, 6094.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञमानिन्
प्राज्ञ- + मानिन् प्राज्ञ- + मानिन्, adj. fancying one's self a learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमानिन्
शूर- + मानिन् शूर- + मानिन्, adj. one who thinks himself a hero, a boaster, Hit. iv. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभगमानिन्
सु-भग- + मानिन् सु-भग- + मानिन्, adj. fancying one's self fortunate, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष मानुष, i. e. मनुस् (q. cf.), + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. षी.<BR> 1. Human, Rām. 3, 53, 3; 54, 17.<BR> 2. Relating to mankind, Man. 4, 124.<BR> II. m. A man, Pañc. 61, 10.<BR> III. f. षी, A woman, Nal. 13, 55.<BR> IV. n. Human effort, Chr. 56, 16 (दैवं मानुषोपेतम्, Fate combined with human effort).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अ- + मानुष अ- + मानुष,<BR> I. adj., f. षी. 1. not human. 2. inhuman.<BR> II. m. not a man, any other than a man, Man. 9, 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानुष
अति- + मानुष अति- + मानुष, adj. superhuman, Chr. 46, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यमानुष|दिव्यमानुषः
दिव्य- + मानुष दिव्य- + मानुष, m. a demigod, Kathās. 1, 47 (एकान्तसुखिनो देवा मनुष्या नित्यदुःखिनः; दिव्यमानुषचेष्टा [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a " target="_blank">Page0701-a + 40</a>] तु परभागेन हारिणी. विद्याधराणां चरितम् अतस् ते वर्णयाम्य् अहम्; The gods are ever happy, men ever unhappy; [but] the doing of the demigods is charming in the highest degree. Therefore, I shall tell you the adventures of Vidyādharas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्य|मानुष्यं
मानुष्य मानुष्य, i. e. मानुष + य,<BR> I. adj. Human, Nal. 19, 28.<BR> II. n. The state of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यक|मानुष्यकं
मानुष्यक मानुष्य + क, n. A multitude of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रिक|मांत्रिक|मांत्रिकः|मान्त्रिकः
मान्त्रिक मान्त्रिक, i. e. मन्त्र + इक, m. A sorcerer, Rājat. 5, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थ्|मांथ्
† मान्थ् मान्थ् (?), i. 1, Par. To hurt (see मथ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्य|मांद्य|मांद्यं|मान्द्यं
मान्द्य मान्द्य, i. e. मन्द + य, n.<BR> 1. Indisposition, sickness.<BR> 2. Stupidity, torpor, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 17.<BR> 3. Slowness, languishing (and stupidity), Pañc. i. d. 205.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमान्द्य
अ- + मान्द्य अ- + मान्द्य, n. activity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ मान्धातृ, m. A proper name, Pañc. iii. d. 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्मथ
मान्मथ मान्मथ. i. e. मन्मथ + अ, adj. Caused by love, Prab. 41, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्य|मापत्यः
मापत्य मापत्य (probably from the Caus. of मे), m. The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापन|मापनं|मापनः
मापन मापन, i. e. मा, Caus., + अन, n. A balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माम
माम माम, i. e. मम, gen. sing. of अस्मद्, + अ, adj. Mine, Pañc. 98, 13; dear, 50, 12; 16; 51, 13; 23; 52, 4, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक मामक, i. e. मम, gen. sing. of अस्मद्, + क,<BR> I. adj., f. की and मिका, Mine, Bhag. 1, 1.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mother's brother.<BR> 2. A niggard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन मामकीन, i. e. मामक + ईन, adj. Mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय माय, i. e. मन् + य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A juggler.<BR> 2. An Asura.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Understanding.<BR> 2. Fraud, deceit, Man. 7, 104; Hit. i. d. 194, M.M.<BR> 3. Trick in negotiation, diplomacy, Pañc. i. d. 404 (यो मायां कुरुते मूधः प्राणत्यागे धनादिषु, The fool who uses tricks about wealth, etc., his life being in danger).<BR> 4. Wickedness.<BR> 5. Illusion, unreality, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 2.<BR> 6. Magical power, Kathās. 25, 274.<BR> 7. Compassion.<BR> 8. The wife of a juggler.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अ- + माय अ- + माय, f. honesty, truth, Hit. ii. d. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमाय
देव- + माय देव- + माय, f. a phantom created by a god, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमाय
बहु- + माय बहु- + माय, adj. Very wicked, Pañc. i. d. 364.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमाय
सु- + माय सु- + माय, adj. abounding in tricks (?), Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 88, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाद|मायादः
मायाद माया-द (vb. दा), m. A crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाधर
मायाधर माया-धर, adj. Deceitful, disguised, Rām. 3, 49, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामय
मायामय माया + मय, adj., f. यी,<BR> 1. Illusive, Rām. 3, 49, 31.<BR> 2. Magical, Indr. 1, 7; Rām. 3, 55, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावन्त्|मायावत्
मायावन्त् माया + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Deceitful, illusory, unreal.<BR> II. m. A name of Kansa.<BR> III. f. वती, The wife of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायायिन्
मायायिन् मायायिन्, and मायाविन् मायाविन्, i. e. माया + विन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Deceitful, using tricks, Rām. 3, 49, 47 (विन्).<BR> 2. Illusory, unreal.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A juggler.<BR> 2. A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक मायिक, i. e. माया + इक, m. A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन् मायिन्, i. e. माया + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Wise, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7.<BR> 2. Deceptive.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A juggler.<BR> 2. A cheat.<BR> 3. Agni, Viṣṇu, Brahman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिन्
अ- + मायिन् अ- + मायिन्, adj. void of deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मायिन्
दुर्मायिन् दुर्म्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. using tricks, Bhāg. P. 8, 11, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु मायु,<BR> I. m. Bile.<BR> II. i. e. 2. मा + उ, Sounding, crying, at the end of comp. words; ved. गोमायु see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर मायूर, i. e. मयूर + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री.<BR> 1. Belonging to, or coming from, peacocks, Rām. 2, 100, 63 Gorr.; agreeable to peacocks, Mālav. d. 20.<BR> 2. Made of its feathers.<BR> II. n. A flock of peacocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार|मारः
मार मार, i. e. मृ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Dying.<BR> 2. Death.<BR> 3. Killing, Hit. 18, 3, M.M.<BR> 4. Obstruction.<BR> 5. The god of love.<BR> II. f. री.<BR> 1. Plague.<BR> 2. A name of Caṇḍī or Durgā.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार|अमारः
अ- + मार अ- + मार, m. not dying, Rājat. 5, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुमार|धुंधुमारः|धुन्धुमारः
धुन्धु- + मार धुन्धु- + मार, m. a proper name and surname, Rām. 1, 72, 21 Gorr.; MBh. 3, 13486.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुमार
पशु- + मार पशु- + मार, m. the manner of killing a beast, MBh. 3, 370.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामारी
महा-मारी महा-मारी, f. a name of Durgā, Dev. 12, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुमार|शिशुमारः
शिशु- + मार शिशु- + मार, m. 1. the Gangetic porpoise, Pañc. 51, 9. 2. the heavenly porpoise, or collection of the stars and planets; north-west, Johns. Sel. 40, 36. 3. a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक मारक, i. e. मृ, Caus., + अक, m.<BR> 1. A slayer.<BR> 2. A hawk.<BR> 3. Plague.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुमारक
पशु-मार + क पशु-मार + क, adj. accompanied by sacrificing beasts, Bhāg. P. 4, 27, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत मारकत, i. e. मरकत + अ, adj., f. ती, Emerald-like, Hit. pr. d. 41, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारण|मारणं
मारण मारण, i. e. मृ, Caus. + अन, n.<BR> 1. Killing.<BR> 2. Being killed, Man. 5, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारि|मारिः
मारि मारि (vb. मृ), f.<BR> 1. Killing.<BR> 2. Plague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिन्
ऽमारिन् -मारिन्, i. e. मृ + इन् in पूर्व-, adj., f. इनी, Dying before, Man. 5, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिष|मारिषः
मारिष मारिष (for मार्ष, q. cf.), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b " target="_blank">Page0702-b + 42</a>]<BR> I. m. A venerable person (in dramatic language), Vikr. 3, 6.<BR> II. f. षा, The mother of Dakṣa, Lass. 59, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच मारीच, i. e. मरीचि + अ, m. The name of a Muni, Śāk. 100, 8; of a Rākṣasa, Rām. 3, 48, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमारीच
सह- + मारीच सह- + मारीच, adj. With Mārīca, Rām. 3, 48, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत मारुत, i. e. मरुत् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to the Maruts, Chr. 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 87, 6.<BR> 2. Consisting of the Maruts, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Marut.<BR> 2. Wind Pañc. iii. d. 56.<BR> 3. Vital air, Lass. 17, 6 (ऊर्ध्व-, m. Pressing upwards).<BR> III. n. Burnt offering on conception.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमारुत|अतिमारुतः
अति- + मारुत अति- + मारुत, m. strong wind, Yājñ. 1, 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चान्मारुत
पश्चान्मारुत पश्चान्मारुत, i. e. पश्चात्-, m. wind blowing from behind, Ragh. 7, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोमारुत|पुरोमारुतः
पुरोमारुत पुरोमारुत, i. e. पुरस्-, m. wind blowing in front, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुति|मारुतिः
मारुति मारुति, i. e. मरुत् + इ, patronym., m.<BR> 1. Hanumant.<BR> 2. Bhīmasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कंडेयः|मार्कण्डेयः
मार्कण्डेय मार्कण्डेय, m. The name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्
मार्ग् मार्ग् (properly a denomin. derived from मार्ग), i. 1 and 10, Par. (in epic poetry also i. 1, Ātm.).<BR> 1. To trace out, to search, Johns. Sel. 93, 50; Pañc. ii. d. 130.<BR> --i. 10,<BR> 2. † To purify.<BR> 3. † To adorn.<BR> 4. † To go.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि,<BR> 1. To search, MBh. 3, 10975.<BR> 2. To beg for, 14948.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग|मार्गः
मार्ग मार्ग, i. e.<BR> A. मृज् + अ (originally, the tracing out of game by a sporting dog), m.<BR> 1. Search.<BR> 2. Musk.<BR> 3. Trace, Vikr. 57, 12.<BR> 4. A road, Pañc. 122, 6; Vikr. 19, 18; way, Pañc. 98, 22; figuratively, Pañc. 167, 22; use, Lass. 20, 18; title of law, Man. 8, 3; mode. Johns. Sel. 11, 28.<BR> 5. The anus.<BR> B. मृग + अ,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a " target="_blank">Page0703-a + 41</a>] Coming from deer, Rām. 2, 100, 63 Gorr.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of a month, November--December.<BR> 2. The constellation Mṛgaśīrṣa.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरचरमार्ग
अम्बर-चर- + मार्ग अम्बर-चर- + मार्ग, m. the road of the birds, Pañc. i. d. 350.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमार्ग
अर्ध- + मार्ग अर्ध- + मार्ग, m. mid-way, Vikr. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारनिःसरणमार्ग|आहारनिःसरणमार्गः
आहार-निःसरण- + मार्ग आहार-निःसरण- + मार्ग, m. the anus, Pañc. i. d. 458.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मायिन्
उन्मायिन् उन्म्˚, i. e. उद्-, m. wrong way, Hit. 4, 2, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ममार्ग
कर्म(न्)- + मार्ग कर्म(न्)- + मार्ग, m. an opening in walls, etc., serving as a way for thieves, Mṛcch. 64, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलमार्ग|कुलमार्गः
कुल- + मार्ग कुल- + मार्ग, m. the road of honesty, Lass. 40, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमार्ग
कृत- + मार्ग कृत- + मार्ग, adj. made accessible, Vikr. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमार्ग
त्रि- + मार्ग त्रि- + मार्ग,<BR> I. the three worlds, Rām. 1, 45, 40 Gorr.<BR> II. f. गी, three roads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमार्ग|देवमार्गः
देव- + मार्ग देव- + मार्ग, m. the penis and the anus, Rām. 5, 61, 4. 6; Pañc. ed. orn. 55, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रमार्ग
नक्षत्र- + मार्ग नक्षत्र- + मार्ग, m. the road of the stars, Indr. 2, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमार्ग|राजमार्गः
राज(न्)- + मार्ग राज(न्)- + मार्ग, m. a royal or main road, Pañc. 129, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गण|मार्गणं|मार्गणः
मार्गण मार्गण, i. e. मार्ग् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Begging, a beggar.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A solicitor.<BR> 2. An arrow, Chr. 34, 15.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Searching, Hit. iv. d. 71.<BR> 2. Begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गणता
मार्गणता मार्गण + ता, f. The nature of an arrow, Vikr. d. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गव|मार्गवः
मार्गव मार्ग + व, m. The son of a Niṣāda by an Ayogava female, Man. 10, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिर|मार्गशिरः
मार्गशिर मार्गशिर, and मार्गशीर्ष मार्गशीर्ष (cf. मार्ग, and शिरस्, and शीर्ष), m. The name of a month, November--December, Bhag. 10, 35 (-शीर्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिक|मार्गिकः
मार्गिक मार्गिक, i. e. मृग and मार्ग, + इक, m.<BR> 1. A hunter.<BR> 2. A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्
मार्ज् मार्ज् (cf. मृज्), † मञ्ज् मञ्ज्, † मर्च् मर्च्, † मर्व् मर्व्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b " target="_blank">Page0703-b + 38</a>] i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. † To cleanse.<BR> 2. † To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज|मार्जः|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्ज मार्ज, i. e. मृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. A washerman.<BR> 3. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जन|मार्जनः|मार्ज्जन|मार्ज्जनं|मार्ज्जनः
मार्जन मार्जन, i. e. मृज् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. नी.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Rubbing, Man. 5, 116.<BR> 3. Cleaning the person by wiping, bathing, or rubbing it with unguents.<BR> II. f. ना, The sound of a drum, Mālav. d. 20.<BR> III. f. नी, A brush, Pañc. ii. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जार|मार्जारः|मार्ज्जार
मार्जार मार्जार, i. e. मृज् + आर, m., and f. री.<BR> 1. The common cat, Pañc. 110, 23.<BR> 2. The pole-cat.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यमार्जार|अरण्यमार्ज्जार
अरण्य- + मार्जार अरण्य- + मार्जार, m. a wild cat, Pañc 165, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारक|मार्जारकः|मार्ज्जारक
मार्जारक मार्जारक, i. e. मृज् + आर + क, m. A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारीय|मार्जारीयः|मार्ज्जारीय
मार्जारीय मार्जारीय, i. e. मार्जार + ईय, and मार्जालीय मार्जालीय (with ल् for र्), m.<BR> 1. A cat.<BR> 2. A Śūdra.<BR> 3. Cleaning the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्तण्ड|मार्तंड|मार्तंडः|मार्तण्डः|मार्त्तण्ड|मार्त्तण्डः
मार्तण्ड मार्तण्ड, i. e. मृतण्ड + अ, m.<BR> 1. The sun, Utt. Rāmac. 140, 9; Rājat. 5, 153.<BR> 2. A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिक|मार्तिक|मार्त्तिकः
मार्त्तिक मार्त्तिक, i. e. मृत्तिका + अ,<BR> I. adj. Earthen.<BR> II. m. A lid, a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्य
मार्त्य मार्त्य, i. e. मृत + य (adj. or sbst. n.), Mortal, the mortal part, Bhāg. P. 3, 33, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दङ्ग|मार्दंग|मार्दंगः|मार्दङ्गः|मार्द्दङ्ग|मार्द्दङ्गं
मार्दङ्ग मार्दङ्ग, i. e. मृदङ्ग + अ,<BR> I. m. A drummer.<BR> II. n. A town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दव|मार्दवं|मार्द्दव|मार्द्दवं|मार्द्दवः
मार्दव मार्दव, i. e. मृदु + अ, n. Softness, Chr. 57, 24; Bhartṛ. 1, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमार्दव
सु- + मार्दव सु- + मार्दव, n. beautiful softness, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष|मार्षः
मार्ष मार्ष, i. e. मर्ष + अ, m. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a " target="_blank">Page0704-a + 43</a>] venerable man (in dramatic language), Sch. ad Vikr. ed. Bollensen, p. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टि|मार्ष्टिः
मार्ष्टि मार्ष्टि, i. e. मृज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Cleaning the person by bathing, etc.; cf. मार्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल|मालं|मालः
माल माल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A name of a barbarous tribe, Lass. 38, 14.<BR> 2. The name of a country, Megh. 16.<BR> 3. Viṣṇu.<BR> II. i. e. मल + अ, f. ला.<BR> 1. A line.<BR> 2. A garland, a necklace, Hit. i. d. 174, M.M. (धृत-कनक-माल, adj. Bearing a gold necklace).<BR> 3. A chaplet of flowers.<BR> 4. A rosary.<BR> 5. A chain, Pañc. 255, 19.<BR> III. n. A field.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमाल
अक्ष- + माल अक्ष- + माल, f. ला, 1. a rosary, Dev. 2, 23. 2. a name of Arundhatī, the wife of Vaśiṣṭha, Man. 9, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुमाल|केतुमालं|केतुमालः
केतु- + माल केतु- + माल,<BR> I. m. 1. pl. the name of a people, Hariv. 8227. 2. the name of a वर्ष or division of the earth, Bhāg. P. 5, 2, 19.<BR> II. f. ला, the name of a holy place, MBh. 3, 8368.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रमाला
नक्षत्र- + माला नक्षत्र- + माल, f. ला, 1. a group of stars, Rām. 1, 60, 21. 2. all the lunar mansions. 3. a string of twenty-seven pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमाला
नर- + माला नर- + माल, f. ला, a chaplet of human skulls, Dev. 7, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमाला
वन- + माला वन- + माल, f. ला, the chaplet worn by Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमाला|वंदनमाला
वन्दन- + माला वन्दन- + माल, f. ला, the ornamented arc of a gateway (cf. मालक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमाला
वर्ण- + माला वर्ण- + माल, f. ला, the alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसमाला
हंस- + माला हंस- + माल, f. ला, 1. a duck. 2. a flight of wild geese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममाला
हेम- + माला हेम- + माल, f. ला, the wife of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालक|मालकं|मालकः
ऽमालक -माल + क, at the end of comp. adj., f. लिका; e. g. अक्षर-, Consisting of a line of letters, Pañc. ii. d. 183. बद्ध-वन्दन-, adj. Having fastened garlands of salutation, Pañc. 207, 24 (but cf. वन्दन-माला, s. v. माल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालती
मालती मालती, f.<BR> 1. A bud.<BR> 2. A young woman.<BR> 3. Moonlight.<BR> 4. Night.<BR> 5. A river.<BR> 6. Great-flowered jasmine, Jasminum grandiflorum, Megh. 26; Ṛt. 2, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालव|मालवः
मालव मालव, m. The province of Malva, Hit. 113, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकार|मालाकारः
मालाकार माला कार, m., f. री, A flower-seller, a gardener, Pañc. i. d. 394; Lass. 24, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिक|मालिकः
मालिक मालिक, i. e. माला + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a garland.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A flower-gatherer, Pañc. v. d. 55 (cf. Pañc. 156, 20).<BR> 2. A painter.<BR> 3. A sort of bird.<BR> III. f. का.<BR> 1. A garland of flowers, Pañc. 236, 16.<BR> 2. A multitude, Hit. iii. d. 89.<BR> 3. A necklace.<BR> 4. A daughter.<BR> 5. A palace.<BR> 6. A spirituous liquor.<BR> 7. Double jasmine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमालिका|वंदनमालिका
वन्दन- + मालिका वन्दन- + मालिक, f. का, the ornamented arc of a gateway; cf. मालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालित
मालित मालित, i. e. माला + इत, Surrounded, Lass. 4, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन् मालिन्, i. e. माला + इन्,<BR> I. m. A florist.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A female vendor of flowers.<BR> 2. A name of Durgā.<BR> 3. The Ganges of heaven.<BR> 4. A plant, Hedysarum alhagi.<BR> 5. A shrub, Echites caryophyllata.<BR> III. As latter part of compounds, very often adj., f. नी, Wearing a garland or chaplet of, cf. comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमालिन्
अंशु- + मालिन् अंशु- + मालिन्, m. the sun, Ṛt. 1, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमालिन्
अक्ष- + मालिन् अक्ष- + मालिन् (cf. अक्ष-माला), m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 12, 10374.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिमालिन्|ऊर्म्मिमालिन्
ऊर्मि- + मालिन् ऊर्मि- + मालिन्,<BR> I. adj. adorned with a chaplet of waves, Rām. 2, 113, 21.<BR> II. m. the sea, Ragh. 5, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालमालिन्
कपाल- + मालिन् कपाल- + मालिन्, adj. wearing a string of skulls, MBh. 14, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डमालिन्
गण्ड- + मालिन् गण्ड- + मालिन्, adj. sbst. one who has the erysipelas, Man. 3, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकमालिन्
जालक- + मालिन् जालक- + मालिन्, adj., f. नी, adorned with a necklace in the form of a net, Bhāg. P. 8, 20, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरमालिन्
नगर- + मालिन् नगर- + मालिन्, adj. garlanded with cities, Johns. Sel. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्ममालिन्
पद्म- + मालिन् पद्म- + मालिन्, m. the name of a Rākṣasa, Rām. 6, 7, 33. f. epithet of Śrī, MBh. 12, 8353 (adorned with a string of lotus flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरमालिन्
पुर- + मालिन् पुर- + मालिन्, f. नी, the name of a river, MBh. 6, 329. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a " target="_blank">Page0705-a + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिमालिन्
मरीचि- + मालिन् मरीचि- + मालिन्,<BR> I. adj. surrounded by a circle of rays, Hit. 38, 1, M.M.<BR> II. m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमालिन्
वन- + मालिन् वन- + मालिन्, m. Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिमालिन्
वीचि- + मालिन् वीचि- + मालिन्, m. the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममालिन्
हेम- + मालिन् हेम- + मालिन्, adj. adorned with a chaplet of gold, Rām. 3, 50, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्य|मालिन्यं
मालिन्य मालिन्य, i. e. मलिन + य, n. Blackness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1915 (मालिन्यं को दोषः, What an object of blame is the blackness! i. e. the blackness is no object of blame).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूर|मालूरः
मालूर मालूर, m. A fruit-tree, Aegle marmelos, Lass. 86, 6 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्य|माल्यं
माल्य माल्य, i. e. माला + य,<BR> I. adj. Fit for a garland.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A flower, Johns. Sel. 40, 38.<BR> 2. A garland, Pañc. 199, 19.<BR> 3. A chaplet, Man. 2, 177.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमाल्य
गन्ध- + माल्य गन्ध- + माल्य, n. an agreeably smelling wreath, Pañc. 182, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यगुणाय
माल्यगुणाय माल्यगुणाय, a denomin. derived from माल्य-गुण with य, Ātm. To become a garland, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यवन्त्|माल्यवत्
माल्यवन्त् माल्य + वन्त्,<BR> I. m. The name of a mountainous range.<BR> II. f. वती, The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष|माषः
माष माष, m.<BR> 1. A sort of kidney bean, Phaseolus radiatus, Man. 3, 267.<BR> 2. A goldsmith's weight, Man. 8, 134.<BR> 3. A fool.<BR> 4. A cutaneous disease.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाष|महामाषः
महा- + माष महा- + माष, m. a sort of bean, Dolichos catjang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषक|माषकः
माषक माष + क, m. A weight of gold and of silver, Man. 8, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषिक
ऽमाषिक -माषिक, i. e. माष + इक, latter part of comp. adj. Amounting to māṣas; e. g. पञ्च(न्)-, Amounting to five māṣas, Man. 8, 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीण|माषीणं
माषीण माषीण, and माष्य माष्य, i. e. माष + ईन, or य, n. A field of kidney beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास् मास् (= मास, q. cf.), m.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b " target="_blank">Page0705-b + 41</a>] The moon.<BR> 2. A month.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमास्
पुष्प- + मास् पुष्प- + मास्, m. spring (the season), Rām. 3, 79, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास|मासं|मासः
मास मास, (sprung from मान्त्, ptcple. pres. of मा); the base of many cases is optionally मास्, m. A month, Pañc. 169, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. μήν; Lat. monsis; Goth. mêna; A.S. mona; Goth. mênôths; A.S. monadh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमास|अर्धमासः
अर्ध- + मास अर्ध- + मास, m. half a month, a fortnight, Man. 4, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भमास|गर्भमासः
गर्भ- + मास गर्भ- + मास, m. a month of pregnancy, Kathās. 26, 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमास|पुष्पमासः
पुष्प- + मास पुष्प- + मास, m. spring (the season), Rām. 3, 79, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमास|पूर्णमासः
पूर्ण- + मास पूर्ण- + मास, m. 1. the full of the moon. 2. a monthly sacrifice performed on the day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासज्ञ|मासज्ञः
मासज्ञ मास-ज्ञ, m. A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासर|मासरः
मासर मासर, m. The scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासशस्
मासशस् मास + शस्, adv. For months, MBh. 13, 5659.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासानुमासिक
मासानुमासिक मासानुमासिक, i. e. मास-अनु-मास + इक, adj. Performed from month to month, Man. 3, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासावधिक
मासावधिक मासावधिक, i. e. मास-अवधि + क, adj. Having as limit a month, taking place after a month, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिक|मासिकं|मासिकः
मासिक मासिक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Monthly, Man. 3, 123; 5, 140.<BR> 2. Payable in a month.<BR> 3. Hired by the month.<BR> 4. Lasting for a month.<BR> 5. Happening at the end of a month.<BR> II. n. An obsequial sacrifice performed every day of the new moon.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमासिक
अष्टमासिक अष्टमासिक, i. e. अष्टन्-, f. की, lasting eight months, Chr. 47, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मासिक
षण्मासिक षण्मासिक, i. e. षष्-, adj. happening every sixth month, Pañc. 252, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासुरी
मासुरी मासुरी, f. A beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासूर
मासूर मासूर, i. e. मसूर + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a " target="_blank">Page0706-a + 38</a>] adj., f. री, Consisting, made of lentils or pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माह्
† माह् माह् (माड् माड्) i. 1, Par. Ātm. To mete, to measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुल|माहाकुलः
माहाकुल माहाकुल, i. e. महा-कुल + अ, adj. Of a respectable family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्मिक
माहात्मिक माहात्मिक, i. e. महा-आत्मन् + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Majestic, Man. 5, 94.<BR> 2. Of great honour.<BR> 3. Glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्म्य|माहात्म्यं
माहात्म्य माहात्म्य, i. e. महा-आत्मन् + य, n.<BR> 1. Majesty, might, Utt. Rāmac. 96, 3; Pañc. 48, 18; ii. d. 52.<BR> 2. The peculiar efficacy or virtue of a deity or sacred shrine.<BR> 3. A work giving an account of the merits of any holy object, Dev. title.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहित्र
माहित्र माहित्र, (n.), The name of a holy text, Man. 11, 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिर|माहिरः
माहिर माहिर, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष
माहिष माहिष, i. e. महिष + अ, adj., f. षी, Belonging to, or coming from, a buffalo (flesh, milk, etc.), Śārṅg. 82, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषिक|माहिषिकः
माहिषिक माहिषिक, i. e. महिष + इक, m. A keeper of buffaloes, Man. 3, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्य|माहिष्यः
माहिष्य माहिष्य, i. e. महिष + य, m. The offspring of a Kṣatriya father and a Vaiśya mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र माहेन्द्र, i. e. महा-इन्द्र + अ, adj. Relating to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेयी
माहेयी माहेयी, i. e. मही + एय + ई, f. A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि मि, ii. 5, Par. Ātm. To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिछ्|मिच्छ्
† मिछ् मिछ्, पिछ् पिछ्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To inflict pain.<BR> 2. To obstruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिञ्ज्
† मिञ्ज् मिञ्ज् (?), i. 10, Par. To speak. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितद्रु|मितद्रुः
मितद्रु मित-द्रुइ (vb. मा), m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितंपच|मितम्पच|मितम्पचः
मितंपच मितंपच, i. e. मित (vb. मा), + म्-पच् + अ, adj. Niggardly, a niggard, Hit. i. d. 154, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिति|मितिः
मिति मिति, i. e. मा + ति, f.<BR> 1. Measuring.<BR> 2. Determining.<BR> 3. Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्त्र
मित्त्र मित्त्र, commonly written मित्र मित्र, i. e. मिद् + त्र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A vedic deity, Chr. 298, 25 = Rigv. i. 112, 25.<BR> 2. The sun, Pañc. ii. d. 75.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A friend, Rām. 3, 51, 9.<BR> 2. An ally.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्त्र
अ- + मित्त्र अ- + मित्त्र, m., and f. रा, an enemy, Rām. 3, 51, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमित्त्र
कु- + मित्त्र कु- + मित्त्र, n. a treacherous friend, Pañc. iii. d. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरमित्त्र
निस्-अ- + मित्त्र निस्-अ- + मित्त्र, 1. adj. free from enemies, Rām. 2, 18, 7 Gorr. 2. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमित्त्र
धन- + मित्त्र धन- + मित्त्र and पुरु-, m. proper names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्त्र
स- + मित्त्र स- + मित्त्र, adj. with (his) friends, Chr. 54, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्त्र
सु- + मित्त्र सु- + मित्त्र, f. त्रा, one of the wives of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्त्रता
मित्त्रता मित्त्र + ता, f., and मित्त्रत्व मित्त्र + त्व, n. Friendship, Pañc. ii. d. 32; iii. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्त्रयु
मित्त्रयु मित्त्र + यु,<BR> I. adj. Acquiring friends.<BR> II. m. A person acquainted with the ways and manners of mankind (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्त्रवन्त्
मित्त्रवन्त् मित्त्र + वन्त्, adj., f. वती. One who has friends, Pañc. ii. d. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्
मिथ् मिथ्, मिध् मिध् (see मेध्), † मिद् मिद्, † मेद् मेद्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. †<BR> 1. To understand.<BR> 2. To hurt.<BR> 3. To rival (ved.).<BR> --Caus. मेधय, To further, MBh. 13, 7510.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथस्
मिथस् मिथ् + अस्, adv.<BR> 1. Mutually, reciprocally, with each other, Pañc. 125, 10; from each other, Pañc. 42, 22. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a " target="_blank">Page0707-a + 39</a>]<BR> 2. Privately, Man. 8, 195 (Daśak. in Chr. 192, 20. read पार्थिवं मिथो).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिला
मिथिला मिथिला, f. The name of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुन|मिथुनं|मिथुनः
मिथुन मिथ् + उन (for + वन),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A couple, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 8.<BR> 2. Copulation.<BR> 3. Union.<BR> II. m. The sign of the zodiac, Gemini.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिथुन
गो- + मिथुन गो- + मिथुन, n. a bull and a cow, Man. 3, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या मिथ्या (vb. मिथ्), adv. Falsely, Pañc. 7, 16; untruly, feigned, Lass. 9, 11; wrong, Pañc. 206, 11; what does not concern one, Pañc. 9, 24; in vain, Sāv. 6, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद् मिद्, i. 1, Ātm., i. 4, मेद्य, Par., and i. 10, Par., also † मिन्द् मिन्द्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To be unctuous.<BR> 2. † To liquefy.<BR> 3. † To love.<BR> 4. To rejoice (ved.).<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus. प्रमेदित, Made unctuous; greasy. See मिथ्.<BR> --Cf. μειδάω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिध्
† मिध् मिध्, see मिथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्द्|मिंद्
† मिन्द् मिन्द्, see मिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्व्
† मिन्व् मिन्व्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sprinkle.<BR> 2. To gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल्
मिल् मिल् (probably an old denomin. based on a noun derived from मिश्ल (= मिश्र), changed to मिल्ल), i. 6, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To associate, Pañc. 220, 13.<BR> 2. To be connected, 229, 11 (पृष्ठ आगत्य मिलितः, Was the last).<BR> 3. To meet, Hit. 83, 6, M.M.<BR> 4. To assemble, Pañc. 53, 20; Rājat. 5, 465.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. मिलित, Mixed (covered), Pañc. 122, 11.<BR> --With परि परि, परिमिलित, Penetrated, filled, Śiś. 11, 23.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संमिलित, Collected, Pañc. 229, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्
† मिश् मिश्, see मश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र्
मिश्र् मिश्र्, and † मिस्र् मिस्र्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from मिश्र), Par. To mix, Śāk. d. 30. मिश्रित,<BR> 1. Mixed, Pañc. 215, 2.<BR> 2. Respected (i. e. मिश्र + इत, cf. मिश्र).<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To put in disorder, MBh. 1, 3282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र मिश्र, i. e. मिश् (perhaps for मिक्ष्, desider. of मिह्, without red., cf. मिह् with सम्), + र,<BR> I. adj. Mixed, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 187; Pañc. 9, 4; Utt. Rāmac. 42, 11.<BR> II. n. Mixing.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. An elephant.<BR> 2. A respectable person, Sir, Lass. 95, 9; in this sense it is a common affix to nouns, Vikr. 3, 12. and proper names, Lass. 89, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. miscere; O.H.G. miscjan; A.S. miscan; μίσγω, μίγνυμι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्रः|आर्य्यमिश्र|आर्य्यमिश्रः
आर्य- + मिश्र आर्य- + मिश्र, m. pl. a respectable person, Rām. 2, 82, 18; Prab. 25, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रक|मिश्रकं|मिश्रकः
मिश्रक मिश्र + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A mixer.<BR> 2. An adulterator of commodities, a mixer of bad wares with good ones, Man. 11, 50.<BR> II. n. A grove of paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
1. मिष् मिष् (probably for मिक्ष्, and akin to मिह्), i. 1, Par. To sprinkle.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मिष्ट.<BR> 1. Sprinkled.<BR> 2. Sweet, Pañc. 119, 7. n. A fine dish, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1787; sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
2. मिष् मिष्, i. 6, Par. (properly To wink, to contract the eyelids, cf. मील्, क्ष्मील्, श्मील्, स्मील्, and स्मि).<BR> 1. To look at angrily, Chr. 4, 16 (हरामि मिषतां वस्, I shall take [her] while you are looking on angrily, i. e. in spite of you).<BR> 2. † To contend, to resist.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To open one's eyes, Bhag. 5, 9; Kumāras. 5, 25.<BR> 2. To flash, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 16.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, To break forth, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 4.<BR> --With नि नि, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a " target="_blank">Page0708-a + 39</a>] To shut one's eyes, to wink, MBh. 3, 10649.<BR> --Cf. Lat. miser; μῖσος, probably also μύω, cf. ὄμματα, συμ-μεμυκότα, ἀναμεμυκότα; Lat. micare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष|मिषं|मिषः
मिष मिस्ह् + अ,<BR> I. m. Emulation.<BR> II. n. Fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्
† मिस् मिस्, i. 4, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्र्
मिस्र् मिस्र्, see मिश्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह्
मिह् मिह् (for original मिघ्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sprinkle.<BR> 2. To urine, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 6; Man. 4, 52.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. Par. मीढ्वंस् (ved.), also before vowels, मीऌह्˚ for मीढ्˚, One who effuses or gives, Lass. 100, 1 = Rigv. vii. 15, 1.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मीढ.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, प्रमीढ,<BR> 1. Passed, as urine.<BR> 2. Thick.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To sprinkle, to give, Chr. 288, 16 = Rigv. i. 48, 16. (मिमिक्ष्व, imperat. ii. 3, Ātm. or anomal. desider.). Desider. मिमिक्ष, To wish to mix, to unite one's self, Chr. 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 87, 6 (मिमिक्षिरे, anomal. pf. red.).<BR> --Cf. Lat. mingere, mejere; A.S. mígan; Goth. maihstus; A.S. meox, miox, mist; ὁμίχλη, ὀμιχεῖν, μοιχός, μιαίνω, μιαρός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुमीढ
पुरु- + मीढ पुरु- + मीढ, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिर|मिहिरः
मिहिर मिहिर, m.<BR> 1. i. e. मिह् + इर, A cloud.<BR> 2. (borrowed from the Persian language), The sun.<BR> 3. The moon.<BR> 4. Wind.<BR> 5. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिलारोप्य
मिहिलारोप्य मिहिलारोप्य, n. The name of a town, Pañc. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
1. मी मी, ii. 9, मीना, मीनी, and ved. मिना, मिनी, Par. To hurt.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pres. अ-मिनन्त्, Not hurting, Chr. 295, 12 = Rigv. i. 92, 12.<BR> --i. 4, Ātm. To perish.<BR> --With the prep. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b " target="_blank">Page0708-b + 41</a>] आ आ, ii. 9, To hurt, to scrape off, Chr. 295, 10 = Rigv. i. 92, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र, ii. 9,<BR> 1. To diminish, Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR> 2. To surmount, to surpass.<BR> --i. 4, To perish. प्रमीत, Deceased, Man. 3, 245.<BR> --Caus. मापय, To cause to perish, Man. 1, 57; to kill, 8, 295.<BR> --Cf. Lat. prō-mīnere, e-minere, minere, prō-minare, e-minus, co-minus, minari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
† 2. मी मी, i. 1 and 10, Par. To go, see मे.<BR> --Cf. Lat. meare and movere (causal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीन|मीनः
मीन मीन (probably vb. मिह्), m.<BR> 1. A fish, Pañc. ii. d. 3.<BR> 2. The sign of the zodiac, Pisces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीम्
† मीम् मीम्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To sound (cf. 2. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांस
मीमांस मीमांस, see मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसक|मीमांसकः
मीमांसक मीमांसक, i. e. मीमांसा + अक, m. A follower of the PūrvaMīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसा
मीमांसा मीमांसा, i. e. मीमांस + अ, f. Two of the philosophical systems of the Hindus, distinguished as पूर्व and उत्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसाकृत्
मीमांसाकृत् मीमांसा-कृ + त्, m. The author of the Pūrva-Mīmāṃsā philosophy, Jaimini, Pañc. ii. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीर|मीरः
मीर मीर (vb. मिह्), m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मील्
मील् मील् (originally a denomin. based on a noun derived from मिस्ह् by an affix, with initial ल्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To wink, to contract the eyelids, to close the eyes, Gīt. 10, 16.<BR> 2. To be closed of itself (viz. the eyes), Bhaṭṭ. 14, 54.<BR> 3. To be collected, Utt. Rāmac. 126, 5 (with v. r.).<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pf. pass. ईषन्मीलित, i. e. ईषत्- adj. Closed a little, Lass. 13, 7.<BR> --Caus. मीलय, To close (viz. one's [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-a " target="_blank">Page0709-a + 40</a>] eyes), लोचने मीलयित्वा, Like a moment, Megh. 109.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To close (viz. one's eyes), Rājat. 5, 348.<BR> --With आ आ, To close (viz. one's eyes), Daśak. in Chr. 199, 4.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To open one's eyes, MBh. 3, 11155.<BR> 2. To be opened of itself (as one's eyes), Bhaṭṭ. 16, 8.<BR> 3. To open, Gīt. 1, 36; (one's eyes), Vikr. d. 5.<BR> 4. To show, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 23.<BR> 5. To hang down (as curls), Utt. Rāmac. 14, 4.<BR> --Caus. To open (viz. one's eyes), MBh. 2, 2630.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To open one's eyes, Gīt. 4, 19.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To open of itself, to spring up, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To close (viz. one's eyes), Śiś. 9, 11; Vikr. 7, 5; Pañc. 165, 15.<BR> 2. To fall asleep, Man. 1, 52.<BR> 3. To be covered, Rājat. 5, 481.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to shut the eyes, to kill, Pañc. iii. d. 269.<BR> 2. To close, Ṛt. 6, 26.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To close the eyes, Bhaṭṭ. 11, 9.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To close the eyes, Gīt. 4, 19.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To close (viz. the eyes), Ragh. 3, 26 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To close (as flowers), Śāk. 45, 4 Chezy.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to shut the eyes, to make insensible, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 7.<BR> 2. To close, Ragh. 13, 10 (Calc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव्
† मीव् मीव्, i. 1, Par. To grow corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवर|मीवरः
मीवर मीवर (probably from vb. मिह्), adj., f. री, Mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवा
मीवा मीवा (perhaps from vb. मिह्), f. The worm of the intestines, ascarides, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकु|मुकुः
मुकु मुकु (vb. 2. मुच्), m. Liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुट|मुकुटं
मुकुट मुकुट,<BR> I. n. A crest, a diadem, Pañc. 3, 10.<BR> II. (vb. 2. मुच्, cf. मुचुटी), f. टी, Snapping the fingers.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापमुकुट
प्रताप- + मुकुट प्रताप- + मुकुट, m. a proper name, Lass. 5, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्द|मुकुंद|मुकुंदः|मुकुन्दः
मुकुन्द मुकुन्द, m.<BR> 1. A precious gem.<BR> 2. Quicksilver.<BR> 3. One of Kuvera's treasures.<BR> 4. A name of Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 4, 9, 36.<BR> 5. Gum olibanum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुर|मुकुरः
मुकुर मुकुर (also मकुर मकुर), m.<BR> 1. A looking-glass, Śiś. 9, 73 (मु˚).<BR> 2. The stick of a potter's wheel.<BR> 3. A bud.<BR> 4. A tree, Mimusops elengi.<BR> 5. Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुल|मुकुलं|मुकुलः
मुकुल मुकुल (also मकुल मकुल), m. and n.<BR> 1. An opening bud, Ragh. 9, 27 (मु˚); Utt. Rāmac. 14, 5 (दशन-मु˚, bud-like teeth).<BR> 2. The body.<BR> 3. The soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलित
मुकुलित मुकुलित, i. e. मुकुल + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Half closed (as a bud).<BR> 2. Half shut (as the eye), Vikr. 47, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तक|मुक्तकं
मुक्तक मुक्त + क (vb. मुच्क्), n. Any missile weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ता
मुक्ता मुक्ता (f. of the ptcple. pf. pass. of मुच्), f. A pearl, Vikr. d. 153.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खमुक्ता
शङ्ख- + मुक्ता शङ्ख- + मुक्ता, f. Shells and pearls, Rām. 3, 49, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताकण
मुक्ताकण मुक्ता-कण, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताकारता
मुक्ताकारता मुक्ताकारता, i. e. मुक्ता-आकार + ता, The form of a pearl, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ति|मुक्तिः
मुक्ति मुक्ति, i. e. 2. मुच् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Leaving off, Bhartṛ. 2, 52.<BR> 2. Deliverance, release (मुक्तिं प्राप्नुमः, We shall be released), Pañc. 106, 1; ii. d. 44.<BR> 3. The delivery of the soul from the body, and exemption from further transmigration, final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख|मुखं|मुखः
मुख मुख,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. The mouth, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0710-a " target="_blank">Page0710-a + 47</a>] Pañc. 258, 16.<BR> 2. The face, Pañc. 238, 23.<BR> 3. Front, Draup. 8, 8.<BR> 4. Entrance, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 19; the entrance to a house.<BR> 5. An aperture, Śiś. 9, 2.<BR> 6. Commencement, Pañc. 29, 16; Chr. 8, 33.<BR> 7. A means.<BR> 8. Sound.<BR> II. m. The beak of a bird.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुख|अंगुलिमुख
अङ्गुलि- + मुख अङ्गुलि- + मुख, n. the tip of the finger, Śiś. 9, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमुखी
अज-मुखी अज-मुखी, f. the name of a female Rākṣasa, Rām. 5, 25, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुख|अधोमुखः
अधोमुख अधोम्˚, i. e. अधस्-, adj., f. खी. 1. looking downwards, Pañc. 84, 7. 2. turned downwards, Rām. 5, 26, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभि- + मुख अभि- + मुख, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमुख|अयोमुखः
अयोमुख अयोम्˚, i. e. अयस्-, adj. iron-pointed, Rām. 3, 53, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मुख|अवाङ्मुखं|अवाङ्मुखः
अवाङ्मुख अवाङ्म्˚, i. e. अवाञ्च्-, adj. looking downwards, Rām. 4, 32, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुमुख
अश्रु- + मुख अश्रु- + मुख, adj., f. खी, the face covered with tears, Rām. 2, 59, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमुख|अश्वमुखः
अश्व- + मुख अश्व- + मुख, adj., f. खी, having a horse's head, a Kiṃnara, Rām. 4, 44, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदङ्मुख
उदङ्मुख उदङ्मुख, i. e. उदञ्च्-, adj. facing the north, Man. 2, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुख|उन्मुखः
उन्मुख उन्म्˚, i. e. उद्-, adj., f. खी, 1. with the face turned upward, Vikr. 61, 17. 2. directed to, towards, Pañc. 141, 17. 3. desiring, Vikr. d. 26 (भेद-, desiring, or ready (cf. 5.), to break out of its bud). 4. intending, Rājat. 5, 259. 5. near to, Ragh. 3, 12. 6. expecting, Rām. 5, 55, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊल्कामुख
ऊल्का- + मुख ऊल्का- + मुख, m. 1. the name of a goblin, Man. 12, 71. 2. a proper name, Rām. 6, 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वमुख
ऊर्ध्व- + मुख ऊर्ध्व- + मुख, adj. of which the aperture is turned upward; turned upward, Kumāras. 1, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमुख
ऋतु- + मुख ऋतु- + मुख, n. the commencement, or first day of a season, Rām. 2, 105, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमुख
एक- + मुख एक- + मुख, adj. having one as (head) chief, or superintendent, Yājñ. 2, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमुख|कंकमुख|कङ्कमुखः
कङ्क- + मुख कङ्क- + मुख, adj. heron-mouthed, Rām. 6, 79, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथामुख
कथा- + मुख कथा- + मुख, n. introduction to a tale, Pañc. 5, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काला
काला काला, m. 1. a kind of monkey, Rām. 6, 3, 35.<BR> 2. the name of a fabulous people, MBh. 2, 1171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिकामुख
कालिका- + मुख कालिका- + मुख, m. a Rākṣasa Rām. 8, 29, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यमुख
क्रव्य- + मुख क्रव्य- + मुख, m. a proper name, Pañc. 87, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमुख|गोमुखं|गोमुखः
