मुख्य मुख्य, i. e. मुख + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Being in, or belonging to, the face.<BR> 2. Fallen from the mouth, Man. 5, 141.<BR> 3. Chief, principal, Pañc. 158, 2; Hit. 83, 18; Daśak. in Chr. 183, 14; 189, 14.<BR> II. n. A principal rite or ordinance.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजमुख्य
द्वि-ज- + मुख्य द्वि-ज- + मुख्य, and द्वि-जाति-, m. A Brāhmaṇa, MBh. 5, 7279; Man. 3, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारमुख्या
वार-मुख्या वार-मुख्या, f. the head of a set of harlots, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 38; Daśak. in Chr. 183, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यता
मुख्यता मुख्य + ता, f. Pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यशस्
मुख्यशस् मुख्य + शस्, adv. Principally, Nal. 8, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धता
मुग्धता मुग्ध + ता, f., and मुग्धत्व मुग्ध + त्व, n. (vb. मुह्).<BR> 1. Loveliness, charm, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 2. Simplicity.<BR> 3. Stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
† 1. मुच् मुच्, see मच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
2. मुच् मुच्, i. 6, मुञ्च, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To let loose, Pañc. 32, 25; ii. d. 123 (to go); to loosen, Vikr. 13, 10.<BR> 2. To dismiss, Pañc. 128, 25.<BR> 3. To release from (with abl. and instr.), MBh. 1, 5641; Man. 11, 228.<BR> 4. To leave, to abandon, Vikr. 5, 11; Pañc. 57, 10; with देहम्, To die, Hit. iii. d. 31.<BR> 5. To take away, MBh. 3, 2982.<BR> 6. To lose, Rām. 1, 25, 14.<BR> 7. To give up, Man. 8, 150; to sacrifice, Utt. Rāmac. 27, 10.<BR> 8. To cast, Chr. 32, 29; Megh. 85.<BR> 9. To effuse, Ṛt. 6, 28.<BR> 10. To shed, Rām. 2, 37, 15; Chr. 34, 15.<BR> 11. To spit out, Kir. 5, 38.<BR> 12. To void, MBh. 3, 11115.<BR> 13. To utter, Pañc. 57, 14; Kathās. 18, 154; Megh. 55.<BR> 14. To put on, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 95. Pass. (has in epic poetry sometimes the terminations of the Par., e. g. MBh. 3, 1695).<BR> 1. To deliver one's self, to escape, MBh. 1, 656 (with acc., perhaps i. 4).<BR> 2. To deviate from, to abandon (abl.), Pañc. i. d. 302.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मुक्त.<BR> 1. What has been let loose, shot, Pañc. i. d. 219; darted, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.; spit out, Kir. 5, 38; Man. 3, 225; Pañc. 253, 1 (given).<BR> 2. Liberated from corporeal existence, finally happy.<BR> 3. Deprived, Hit. iii. d. 127.<BR> 4. Open, Hit. iii. d. 121 (मुक्त-हस्त, Liberal). n. The spirit released from corporeal existence. मुक्ता, see s. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Absol. मुक्त्वा, Except, Pañc. 44, 11; 73, 19.<BR> --Desider. मुमुक्ष.<BR> 1. To wish to cast, Ragh. 2, 42 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To desire final beatitude, MBh. 3, 167 (cf. मोक्स्ह).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause, or to order, to be liberated, Pañc. 192, 16; Daśak. in Chr. 192, 18.<BR> 2. To cause to shed (tears), Megh. 91.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To let loose, to release, Pañc. in Weber, Ind. St. iii. 373, 6; Hit. 52, 2, M.M.<BR> 2. To redeem from (abl.), Man. 3, 37.<BR> 3. † To delight.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To unyoke, MBh. 3, 2870.<BR> 2. To take off, MBh. 2, 2520.<BR> --With आ आ, To put on, MBh. 1, 4095; Mālav. 37, 19. आमुक्त,<BR> 1. Dressed.<BR> 2. Loosed.<BR> 3. Cast, discharged.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To let loose, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 2; to liberate, Pañc. 38, 21.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, To set free, Pañc. 87, 20.<BR> --With निस् निस्, pass. refl., with acc., To abandon, Rājat. 5, 125. निर्मुक्त,<BR> 1. Let loose, Chr. 34, 12.<BR> 2. Liberated, MBh. 1, 6197.<BR> 3. Separated. m. A snake who has lately cast his skin.<BR> --With अभिनिस् अभि-निस्, अभिनिर्मुक्त, Darted (surprised) by the setting sun (cf. म्लुछ्), Man. 2, 221 (Weber reads अभिनिम्रुक्त, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, xiv. 756).<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, विनिर्मुक्त,<BR> 1. Left, Nal. 13, 21.<BR> 2. Liberated.<BR> 3. Exempt.<BR> 4. Separated, MBh. 3, 2552.<BR> --With परि परि, परिमुक्त, Liberated, MBh. 1, 4659.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To throw, Chr. 44, 4.<BR> 2. To throw out, to vomit, MBh. 1, 7628.<BR> 3. To utter, MBh. 3, 2542.<BR> 4. To produce, Rām. 2, 91, 26.<BR> 5. To remove, MBh. 3, 10819.<BR> 6. To loosen. MBh. 2, 2825.<BR> 7. To release, Man. 4, 181.<BR> 8. To put on, Rām. 2, 9, 39. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-a " target="_blank">Page0713-a + 44</a>]<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To liberate, to release, MBh. 3, 11800. विप्रमुक्त, Liberated from (instr.), MBh. 1, 6771.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To bind, MBh. 2, 2323.<BR> 2. To let loose again, to return, Pañc. iv. d. 1.<BR> 3. To restore, to return, Ragh. 16, 59 (Calc.).<BR> 4. Pass. To be freed from, Man. 10, 118. प्रति-मुक्त,<BR> 1. Clothed, armed.<BR> 2. Thrown mutually, or at one another.<BR> 3. Loosed, or liberated repeatedly.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, To save, MBh. 1, 5812.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To separate, Vikr. d. 129.<BR> 2. To let loose, Śāk. 5, 15.<BR> 3. With गर्भम्, To lay eggs, Pañc. 75, 9.<BR> 4. To set free, Pañc. 41, 22.<BR> 5. Pass. To liberate one's self, to escape from (abl.), MBh. 2, 882.<BR> 6. To take off, MBh. 1, 4095.<BR> 7. To lose, MBh. 3, 315.<BR> 8. Pass. To be released or deprived, Man. 2, 79; Hit. i. d. 65, M.M.<BR> 9. To abandon, Hit. iv. d. 38; MBh. 3, 12381; to leave, Utt. Rāmac. 4, 31; 67, 5.<BR> 10. Pass. To obtain final beatitude, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 15; 216, 13.<BR> 11. To effuse, MBh. 1, 3317.<BR> 12. To shed, Rām. 2, 59, 5.<BR> 13. To throw, MBh. 4, 1866; Utt. Rāmac. 163, 10.<BR> 14. To utter, Chr. 41, 8; Rājat. 5, 408.<BR> 15. To assume, Man. 1, 56. विमुक्त,<BR> 1. Loosed.<BR> 2. Thrown, hurled.<BR> 3. Quitted, lost, i. e. without, Rām. 3, 51, 33.<BR> 4. Issued, let loose from.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10,<BR> 1. To liberate, MBh. 3, 2435.<BR> 2. To relieve, Man. 11, 112.<BR> 3. To avoid, Rām. 5, 42, 11.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To abandon, MBh. 3, 15602.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To shed, MBh. 3, 10236.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mucus, e-mungere; μυκτήρ, ἀπομυκτίζω, μύξα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुच्
अ- + मुच् अ- + मुच्, adj. not lost, Pañc. 174, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्त|जीवन्मुक्तः
जीवन्मुक्त जीवन्म्˚ i. e. जीवन्त्-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-b " target="_blank">Page0712-b + 43</a>] m. one who has obtained final beatitude during his life, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
ऽमुच् -मुच्, adj. Letting loose; e. g. अम्बु-, जल-, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचिर|मुचिरः
मुचिर 2. मुच् + इर, adj. Liberal, a donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुटी
मुचुटी 2. मुच् + उटी, f.<BR> 1. Snapping the fingers.<BR> 2. The fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुछ्
मुछ् मुछ्, v. r. of युछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुज्
† मुज् मुज्, मुञ्ज् मुञ्ज् (others, मृज् मृज्, मृञ्ज् मृञ्ज्), i. 1, Par. To sound. मुज्, मुञ्ज्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To cleanse (cf. मृज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्च्|मुंच्
† मुञ्च् मुञ्च्, see मच् and म्रुञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चक|मुञ्चकः
मुञ्चक मुञ्चक (vb. 2. मुच्), m. The testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज्|मुंज्
† मुञ्ज् मुञ्ज्, see मुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज|मुंज|मुंजः|मुञ्जः
मुञ्ज मुञ्ज, m.<BR> 1. A sort of grass, Saccharum munja, from the fibres of which the string is prepared to form the thread worn by the Brāhmaṇas, Man. 2, 43.<BR> 2. The brahmanical girdle.<BR> 3. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट्
† 1. मुट् मुट् (cf. मृद्), i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To rub, to grind.<BR> 2. To rebuke.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To rub, to grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट्
† 2. मुट् मुट्, मुण्ट् मुण्ट्, मुड् मुड्, मुण्ड् मुण्ड् (cf. मृड् and 1. मुण्ड्), पुड् पुड्, पुण्ड् पुण्ड्, i. 1, Par. To rub, to grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुड्
मुड् मुड्, see पुड् and 2. मुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्
† मुण् मुण्, i. 6, Par. To promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ट्|मुंट्
मुण्ट् मुण्ट्, see 2. मुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ठ्|मुंठ्
† मुण्ठ् मुण्ठ्, i. 1, Ātm. To run away (or to protect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड्|मुंड्
† 1. मुण्ड् मुण्ड्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To shave.<BR> 2. To grind or pound; see 2. मुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड्|मुंड्
† 2. मुण्ड् मुण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To be pure.<BR> 2. To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड|मुंड|मुण्डं|मुण्डः
मुण्ड मुण्ड (probably a form of a noun derived from मृद्, based on the original form मर्द्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Shaved, bald, having no hair on the head, Man. 2, 219.<BR> 2. Low, mean.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. The head, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 6; Hit. iii. d. 89.<BR> 2. The forehead.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A bald-pate.<BR> 2. A barber.<BR> 3. Rāhu.<BR> 4. The name of a Daitya.<BR> IV. f. डा, Bengal madder, Rubia manjith.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिमुण्ड|दण्डिमुण्डः
दण्डिमुण्ड दण्डिमुण्ड, i. e. दण्डिन्-, m. a name of Śiva (bearing a staff and having his head shorn), MBh. 12, 10358.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डय
मुण्डय मुण्डय, a denomin. derived from मुण्ड, Par. To shave, Pañc. 223, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मुण्डित, Shaven, bald, shorn, Pañc. iv. d. 36; 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डिन्|मुंडिन्
मुण्डिन् मुण्डिन्, i. e. मुण्डय + इन्, m. A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
1. मुद् मुद्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Rām. 1, 46, 17), To be delighted, to rejoice, Man. 2, 232.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मुदित, Delighted, Pañc. i. d. 458; Chr. 14, 24. n. Pleasure.<BR> --Caus. To exhilarate (also Ātm.), Bhaṭṭ. 7, 171.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To approve, to permit, MBh. 2, 1787.<BR> 2. To rejoice, MBh. 3, 11535.<BR> --Caus. To celebrate, Chr. 55, 3. अनुमोदित, Agreed, Utt. Rāmac. 38, 18.<BR> --With अभ्यनु अभि-अनु, To dismiss, MBh. 1, 4447.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To be delighted, Rām. 1, 1, 84. प्रमुदित, Pleased, happy, Pañc. 238, 23.<BR> --Caus. To exhilarate, Man. 3, 61. प्रमोदित, Happy. m. A name of Kuvera.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To expect with delight, MBh. 1, 6781.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
2. मुद् मुद्, i. 10, Par. To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
3. मुद् 1. मुद्, f.<BR> 1. Pleasure, joy, Pañc. 159, 20; Kir. 5, 25.<BR> 2. Intoxication.<BR> 3. A wife.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडामुद्
क्रीडा- + मुद् क्रीडा- + मुद्, f. the pleasure of love, Gīt. 9, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदा
मुदा 1. मुद् + आ, f. Joy, pleasure, Chr. 13, 19; 35, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदिर|मुदिरः
मुदिर 1. मुद् + इर, m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. A lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग मुद्ग, m.<BR> 1. A sort of kidney bean, Phaseolus mungo, Lass. 79, 15.<BR> 2. A cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गर|मुद्गरं|मुद्गरः
मुद्गर मुद्गर, m.<BR> 1. A carpenter's hammer.<BR> 2. A mace, Rām. 3, 54, 10; Sund. 2, 3.<BR> 3. A staff armed with iron, used for breaking clods of earth.<BR> 4. A sort of flower.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटमुद्गर
कूट- + मुद्गर कूट- + मुद्गर, m. a hidden mace, MBh. 13, 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रा
मुद्रा मुद्रा, f.<BR> 1. A seal, a signet, Pañc. iv. d. 36 (स्त्री-, woman who is, as it were, the seal, i. e. the order, viz. of the god of love).<BR> 2. A seal-ring.<BR> 3. A stamp, figurat., a form, Utt. Rāmac. 155, 3.<BR> 4. A mode of intertwining the fingers during religious worship, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुद्रा|अंगुलिमुद्रा
अङ्गुलि- + मुद्रा अङ्गुलि- + मुद्रा, f. a seal-ring, Śāk. d. 135, v. r. तर्क-, f. a particular intertwining of the fingers, Bhāg. P. 4, 6, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममुद्रा
नाम(न्)- + मुद्रा नाम(न्)- + मुद्रा, f. a seal-ring with the name of the possessor, Śāk. 17, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमुद्रा
पाद- + मुद्रा पाद- + मुद्रा, f. 1. impression of a footstep, Rājat. 4, 669. 2. trace, ib. 4, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
वि-मुद्र वि-मुद्र, adj. 1. unsealed. 2. blown, budded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र|समुद्रः
स-मुद्र स-मुद्र, adj. sealed, Yājñ. 2, 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रिका
मुद्रिका मुद्रिका, i. e. मुद्रा + क, f. = मुद्रा.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुद्रिका|अंगुलिमुद्रिका
अङ्गुलि- + मुद्रिका अङ्गुलि- + मुद्रिका, f. a seal ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रित|मुद्रितं
मुद्रित मुद्रित, i. e. मुद्रा + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Sealed.<BR> 2. Stamped, marked, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 3; written, Hit. iv. d. 10.<BR> 3. Sealed up, contracted,<BR> 4. Unblown (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुधा
मुधा मुधा, probably from मुह् (cf. the ptcple. pf. pass. मूढ), adv. In vain, Hit. iii. d. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनि|मुनिः
मुनि मुनि, i. e. मन् + इ (उ for अ, by the influence of the preceding labial),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A holy sage, endowed with divine inspiration, Vikr. d. 3.<BR> 2. An ascetic, Pañc. 34, 13.<BR> 3. The saint Agastya, Vyāsa, Kir. 5, 49.<BR> 4. The name of two plants.<BR> II. f. नी̆, A female saint.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामुनि|महामुनिः
महा- + मुनि महा- + मुनि,<BR> I. m. 1. a great Muni, Chr. 15, 29; Rām. 3, 49, 50 (epithet of Agastya.) 2. the saint Agastya. 3. epithet of Paraśurāma, Chr. 19, 12, and of Vyāsa. 4. time.<BR> II. n. Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षु|मुमुक्षुः
मुमुक्षु मुमुक्षु, i. e. मुमुक्ष, desider. of मुच्, + उ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Desiring to dart (viz. arrows), Ragh. 9, 58.<BR> 2. Anxious for liberation from mundane existence or final beatitude, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 22; Vikr. d. 1.<BR> II. m. A sage abstracted from all human passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षुत्व
मुमुक्षुत्व मुमुक्षु + त्व, n. Condition of one who is anxious for final beatitude; wishing for final beatitude, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षा
मुमूर्षा मुमूर्षा, i. e. मुमूर्ष, desider. of मृ, + अ, f. Desire to die, MBh. 1, 1899.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षु|मुमूर्षुः
मुमूर्षु मुमूर्षु, i. e. मुमूर्ष, desider. of मृ, + उ, adj. Being about to die, Hit. 64, 8; Rājat. 5, 218; 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्
† मुर् मुर्, i. 6, To circle, to surround.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. mūrus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर|मुरं|मुरः
मुर मुर, m. The name of a Daitya killed by Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरज|मुरजः
मुरज मुरज,<BR> I. m. A small drum, Mālav. d. 21.<BR> II. f. जा.<BR> 1. A large drum, Kumāras. 6, 40.<BR> 2. The wife of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरला
मुरला मुरला, f. The Narmadā river, Utt. Rāmac. 50, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरली
मुरली मुरली, f. A flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलीधर|मुरलीधरः
मुरलीधर मुरली-धर, m. Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्छ्
मुर्छ् मुर्छ् (akin to मृ and म्लै), i. 1, मूर्छ, Par.<BR> 1. To be faint, to lose consciousness, Rām. 2, 34, 17.<BR> 2. To increase, to grow vehement, Ragh. 12, 57 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To be frequent, Śāk. 66, 4.<BR> 4. To fill, 6, 9 (Calc.).<BR> 5. To be a match for, 2, 34 (Calc.); to be powerful, Śāk. d. 191 (to appear in a looking-glass).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मूर्छित.<BR> 1. Fainted, Vikr. 54, 17; insensible, Rām. 2, 34, 17.<BR> 2. Stupid.<BR> 3. Intoxicated, MBh. 3, 1864.<BR> 4. Infatuated, Chr. 37, 27; bewildered, Lass. 7, 10.<BR> 5. Increased, grown.<BR> 6. Tall.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभिमूर्छित, Intoxicated, infatuated, MBh. 1, 7794.<BR> --With वि वि, विमूर्छित, Wrapped (Stenzler), Yājñ. 3, 75.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To increase, Kir. 5, 41.<BR> 2. To be powerful, Ragh. 16, 64 (Calc.).<BR> --Caus. To cause to faint, Utt. Rāmac. 47, 2.<BR> --Cf. Goth. untila-malsks, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधमूर्च्छित
क्रोध- + मुर्च्छित क्रोध- + मूर्छित, adj. overpowered by wrath, Indr. 5, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मुर|मुर्मुरः
मुर्मुर मुर्मुर, m.<BR> 1. A fire of chaff.<BR> 2. The god of love.<BR> 3. A horse of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्व्
† मुर्व् मुर्व्, i. 1, मूर्व, Par. To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल्
मुल् मुल्, see 2. मूल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशल
मुशल मुशल, मुषल मुष् + अल (see मुस्), and मुसल मुस् + अल,<BR> I. m. n. A pestle, a club, Arj. 10, 5 (ष्).<BR> II. f. लि. A house-lizard.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. मुसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कालमुषल
कङ्काल-मुषल कङ्काल-मुषल, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a " target="_blank">Page0716-a + 40</a>] m. or n. a kind of weapon, Rām. 1, 30, 13 Gorr.; 57, 12 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमुषल|चक्रमुषलः
चक्र-मुषल चक्र-मुषल, adj. performed with the disk and club, Hariv. 5346.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमुषल
दन्त-मुषल दन्त-मुषल, m. or n. a pestle-like tusk, Pañc. 69, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
1. मुष् मुष्, ii. 9, मुष्णा, मुष्णी, and i. 6 (MBh. 3, 13047; Lass. 35, 16), Par. To steal, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 22; to rob, to plunder, Rājat. 5, 268; to captivate, Nal. 5, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मुषित.<BR> 1. Stolen.<BR> 2. Robbed, plundered, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 1.<BR> 3. Deprived of, free from, Hit. 42, 12.<BR> --With परि परि, To rob, to plunder, MBh. 3, 13030.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To rob, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 60. See मष्, मुस्, and मूष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
2. मुष् मुष्,<BR> I. f. Stealing, Rājat. 5, 168 (read मुषे instead of मुखे, ‘Having turned his mind on stealing.’)<BR> II. Latter part of comp. adj. Stealing, robbing; e. g. धृति-, adj. Stealing, destroying constancy, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M. नेत्र-, adj. Captivating the eyes, MBh. 3, 1720. श्री-, Having stolen, i. e. possessed of the beauty, Megh. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल|मुषलः
मुषल मुषल, see मुशल and मुसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल्य|मुषल्यः
मुषल्य मुषल्य, see मुसल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषितक|मुषितकं
मुषितक मुषित + क (vb. मुष्), n. Stolen objects, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्क|मुष्कः
मुष्क मुष्क, m.<BR> 1. i. e. मुष् + क, A thief.<BR> 2. A testicle, the scrotum, Hit. 76, 1, M.M.; 49, 14.<BR> 3. A heap, a multitude.<BR> 4. The name of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कर|मुष्करः
मुष्कर मुष्क + र, m. A man with large testicles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टि|मुष्टिः
मुष्टि मुष्टि, m. and f.<BR> 1. The fist, Rām. 3, 15, 17; Pañc. i. d. 203.<BR> 2. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b " target="_blank">Page0716-b + 39</a>] handful, Pañc. 215, 1.<BR> 3. The handle of a sword.<BR> --Cf. perhaps A.S. fyst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिक|मुष्टिकः
मुष्टिक मुष्टिक, m. A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिता
मुष्टिता मुष्टि + ता, in दृढ- (vb. दृंह्), f. Firmness of grasp, Johns. Sel. 12, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिंधय|मुष्टिन्धय|मुष्टिंधयः|मुष्टिन्धयः
मुष्टिंधय मुष्टिंधय, i. e. मुष्टि + म्-धे + अ, m. A child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्
मुस् मुस्, or मुष् मुष्, i. 4, Par. To break to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल|मुसलं|मुसलः
मुसल मुस् + अल, also मुषल मुष् + अल (see मुस्), n.<BR> 1. A pestle, Man. 3, 88 (स्).<BR> 2. A club.<BR> --Cf. मुशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलिन्
मुसलिन् मुसलिन्, i. e. मुसल + इन्, m. A name of Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल्य|मुसल्यः
मुसल्य मुसल्य, and मुषल्य मुषल्य, i. e. मुसल + य, adj. Deserving death by pounding with a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त्
† मुस्त् मुस्त्, i. 10, Par. To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त|मुस्तं|मुस्तः
मुस्त मुस्त, m., and f. ता, A fragrant grass, Cyperus rotundus, Śāk. d. 39 (ता).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभद्रमुस्त
स-भद्र-मुस्त स-भद्र-मुस्त, adj. full of Cyperus rotundus (cf. भद्र-मुस्तक), Ṛt. i, 17 (but v. r. सु-भद्र-, containing very auspicious Cyperus rotundus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तक|मुस्तकः
मुस्तक मुस्त + क,<BR> I. m. and n. A fragrant grass, Cyperus rotundus.<BR> II. n. A sort of poison.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुस्तक|भद्रमुस्तकः
भद्र- + मुस्तक भद्र- + मुस्तक, n. = मुस्त, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तु|मुस्तुः
मुस्तु मुस्तु, m. The fist (cf. मुष्टि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्र|मुस्रं
मुस्र मुस्र, n. A tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
मुह् मुह्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To be faint, to lose consciousness, Chr. 32, 24.<BR> 2. To be disturbed (in mind), to be perplexed, Bhag. 2, 13.<BR> 3. To fail, Hit. iii. d. 54.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. मूध.<BR> 1. Perplexed, confused, Śiś. 9, 77. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-a " target="_blank">Page0717-a + 44</a>]<BR> 2. Foolish, stupid, Nal. 6, 12; 18, 10.<BR> 3. Deceived.<BR> 4. Ignorant, unlearned, Pañc. 243, 18. m.<BR> 1. A fool, Vikr. 32, 15.<BR> 2. A sluggard.<BR> II. मुग्ध.<BR> 1. Stupid, Pañc. 166, 25.<BR> 2. Being in love, Śāk. d. 36.<BR> 3. Innocent, d. 24.<BR> 4. Simple.<BR> 5. Beautiful, lovely, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. मोहय,<BR> 1. To perplex, MBh. 1, 5457.<BR> 2. To infatuate, Hit. i. d. 179, M.M.; Rām. 3, 55, 22; मोकित, Infatuated, Hit. i. d. 25, M.M.<BR> 3. To stupefy, Man. 11, 96. मोहित,<BR> 1. Puzzled, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 8.<BR> 2. Beguiled, Nal. 8, 16.<BR> --With the prep. व्या वि-आ, Caus. To disturb, to perplex, Pañc. 129, 8. व्यामोहित, Infatuated, Pañc. 199, 1.<BR> --With उद् उद्, उन्-मुग्ध, Disturbed, Siddh. K. 1, 1, 28.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus., Ātm. To perplex, MBh. 1, 3571. परिमूढ, Bewildered, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 7.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> I. प्रमूढ.<BR> 1. Fainted, Utt. Rāmac. 160, 10.<BR> 2. Disturbed, perplexed, Matsyop. 54.<BR> 3. Foolish, stupid, a fool.<BR> II. प्रमुअध. Fainted, Utt. Rāmac. 164, 17.<BR> --Caus. To pérturb, Draup. 6, 21. प्रमोहित, Insensible.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To be disturbed, Bhag. 2, 72.<BR> --Caus. To perplex, MBh. 1, 5978.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> I. विमूढ.<BR> 1. Bewildered, Utt. Rāmac. 101, 1.<BR> 2. Beguiled.<BR> 3. Foolish. m. A kind of divine being (i. e. मूध with वि, Wise), Sund. 3, 5.<BR> II. विमुग्ध, Bewildered, Hit. 91, 9, M.M.; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b " target="_blank">Page0717-b + 40</a>] absorbed.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To disturb, Bhag. 3, 40.<BR> 2. To infatuate, Rājat. 5, 378. विमोहित, Bewitched, Kathās. 25, 274.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To be disturbed, MBh. 3, 10978.<BR> I. संमूढ.<BR> 1. Bewildered.<BR> 2. Stupefied.<BR> 3. Foolish, Hit. iv. d. 71.<BR> 4. Produced rapidly.<BR> 5. Heaped.<BR> 6. Broken.<BR> II. संमुग्ध.<BR> 1. Fascinated.<BR> 2. Stupefied, Utt. Rāmac. 171, 5.<BR> 3. Beautiful.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To perplex, MBh. 2, 1949.<BR> 2. To infatuate, Pañc. i. d. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूढ
अ-मूढ अ-मूढ, adj. 1. not perplexed, bold. 2. wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मूढ
दिङ्मूढ दिङ्मूढ, i. e. दिश्-, adj. one who has lost the points of the compass, and cannot tell the east from the west, Rām. 3, 60, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामूढ
महा-मूढ महा-मूढ, adj. very foolish, a great fool, Pañc. 38, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुग्ध
अति-मुग्ध अति-मुग्ध, being much in love, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 2. Frequent. मोमुह्य, To be much disturbed, MBh. 4, 801.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहिर|मुहिरः
मुहिर मुह् + इर,<BR> I. adj. Foolish.<BR> II. m. Love, the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुर्
मुहुर् मुहुर्, probably मुह् + उ + त्रा, adv.<BR> 1. A moment, Rām. 3, 50, 10 (cf. मुहूर्त and Rām. 3, 50, 6).<BR> 2. Repeatedly, Vikr. d. 6. Doubled, मुहुर्-मुहुर्, adv. Repeatedly, Ṛt. 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्त मुहूर्त, i. e. मुहुर् + त,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A moment, Rām. 3, 50, 6; some time, Vikr. 40, 4 (परं मुहूर्तात्, After some time, not yet).<BR> 2. The thirtieth part of a day and night, or forty-eight minutes.<BR> II. m. An astrologer.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मुहूर्त|दुर्मुहूर्त्त
दुर्मुहूर्त दुर्मुहूर्त, i. e. दुस्-, n. an inauspicious hour, MBh. 12, 6735.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहेर|मुहेरः
मुहेर मुह् + एर, m. A fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
† मू मू, i. 1, Ātm. To bind; see मव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूक|मूकः
मूक मूक,<BR> I. adj. Dumb, Pañc. i. d. 71.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A fish.<BR> 2. A poor man.<BR> 3. A Daitya.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mūtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढता
मूढता मूढ + ता (vb. मुह्), f., and मूढत्व मूढ + त्व, n. Foolishness, Pañc. 123, 13; 228, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढवत्
मूढवत् मूढ + वत् (vb. मुह्), adv. Like a fool, Chr. 8, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र्
मूत्र् मूत्र् (properly a denomin. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a " target="_blank">Page0718-a + 39</a>] derived from मूत्र), i. 10, Par. To urine.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To urine on somebody, Man. 8, 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र|मूत्रं
मूत्र मूत्र (vb. मिह् and aff. त्र), n. Urine, piss, Pañc. 121, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रित|मूत्रितः
मूत्रित मूत्रित, i. e. मूत्र + इत, adj. Soiled with urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख मूर्ख, i. e. मुर्छ् + अ, m. A fool, a blockhead, Vikr. 33, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खता
मूर्खता मूर्ख + ता, f., मूर्खत्व मूर्ख + त्व, n., and मूर्खिमन् मूर्खिमन्, i. e. मूर्ख + इमन्, m. Stupidity, Pañc. iii. d. 246; 127, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छता
मूर्छता मूर्छता, i. e. मुर्छ् + अ + ता, f. Denseness, Vikr. d. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छन
मूर्छन मूर्छन, i. e. मुर्छ् + अन,<BR> I. n. Modulation, Rām. 1, 4, 11.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. A melody, Megh. 84.<BR> 2. A tone as placed in its scale, the seventh part of a scale, Lass. 39, 9; Pañc. iii. d. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छा
मूर्छा मूर्छा, i. e. मूर्छ् + अ, f. Fainting, loss of consciousness, Utt. Rāmac. 58, 7; Pañc. 35, 10 (instr. by fainting, i. e. fainted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छाल|मूर्च्छालः
मूर्छाल मूर्छा + ल, adj. Fainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त|मूर्त्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त मूर्त (akin to मूर्ति), adj., f. ता.<BR> 1. Solid, material, corporeal, Bhāṣāp. 86; 157; Utt. Rāmac. 60, 7.<BR> 2. Embodied, incarnate, Śāk. d. 32; Kathās. 3, 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त्तः
अ- + मूर्त अ- + मूर्त, adj. incorporeal, Bhāṣāp. 87; Kathās. 20, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तत्व|मूर्तत्वं
मूर्तत्व मूर्त + त्व, n. Corporality, Bhāṣāp. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ति|मूर्तिः|मूर्त्ति|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्ति मूर्ति, probably better मूर्त्ति, i. e. मृद् + ति, cf. Man. 12, 120.<BR> 1. Matter, substance, Man. 1, 17; hard substances, Man. 12, 120 (Jones: the terrene parts of the human body).<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b " target="_blank">Page0718-b + 41</a>] Figure, form, Bhartṛ. 2, 1; Pañc. ii. d. 169.<BR> 3. Body, Rājat. 5, 364.<BR> 4. Incarnation, Man. 1, 98.<BR> 5. Image, Man. 2, 225.<BR> 6. Beauty, Pañc. ii. d. 107.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps βρέτας and μορϕή.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्ति|अष्टमूर्तिः|अष्टमूर्त्ति|अष्टमूर्त्तिः
अष्ट(न्)- + मूर्ति अष्ट(न्)- + मूर्ति, m. a name of Śiva, Śiś. 14, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूर्ति|तपोमूर्तिः|तपोमूर्त्ति
तपस्- + मूर्ति तपस्- + मूर्ति,<BR> I. f. incarnation of devotion, Rām. 1, 31, 11.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Bhāg. P. 8, 13, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमूर्ति|तेजोमूर्तिः
तेजस्- + मूर्ति तेजस्- + मूर्ति, adj. consisting entirely of light, Man. 3, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्ति|त्रिमूर्तिः|त्रिमूर्त्ति|त्रिमूर्त्तिः
त्रि- + मूर्ति त्रि- + मूर्ति, adj. having three forms, Kumāras. 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तितस्
मूर्तितस् मूर्ति + तस्, adv. = abl. sing. of मूर्ति, Man. 1, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिमन्त्|मूर्तिमत्|मूर्त्तिमत्
मूर्तिमन्त् मूर्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Having shape or substance, embodied, Utt. Rāmac. 13, 4.<BR> 2. Incarnate, Hit. 100, 2; Śāk. d. 112.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वमूर्तिमन्त्|विश्वमूर्तिमत्
विश्व- + मूर्तिमन्त् विश्व- + मूर्तिमन्त्, adj. taking all forms, omnipresent, Viṣṇu, Johns. Sel. 90, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धज|मूर्द्धजः|मूर्धजः
मूर्धज मूर्धज, i. e. मूर्धन्-ज, m. Hair, the hair of the head, Śāk. d. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्
मूर्धन् मूर्धन्, m. The head, Pañc. 184, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणमूर्धन्
रण- + मूर्धन् रण- + मूर्धन्, m. battle, Chr. 59, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्धन्
त्रि- + मूर्धन् त्रि- + मूर्धन्, m. instead of त्रिशिरस् (see -शिरस्), the name of a Rākṣasa, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्य|मूर्द्धन्यः
मूर्धन्य मूर्धन् + य, adj. Cerebral (rather lingual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध्वन्
मूर्ध्वन् मूर्ध्वन्, m. The head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वा|मूर्व्वा
मूर्वा मूर्वा, f. A sort of creeper, Sanseviera zeylanica, from the fibres of which are made bowstrings and the girdle of the Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
† 1. मूल् मूल् (cf. मूल), i. 1, Par. (and Ātm.), To stand, to be rooted, or firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
2. मूल् मूल्, also † मुल् मुल्. i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a " target="_blank">Page0719-a + 44</a>] मूल), To plant.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To uproot, Hit. ii. d. 84.<BR> 2. To destroy, Vikr. d. 25.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To uproot, Hit. iii. d. 49.<BR> 2. To exterminate, Rājat. 5, 214.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To destroy, Śāntiś. 4, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल|मूलं|मूलः
मूल मूल (vb. मह्),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. The root of a tree, Vikr. d. 41; root (figuratively), Pañc. ii. d. 23.<BR> 2. An eatable root, Utt. Rāmac. 33, 8.<BR> 3. The lowest part, Megh. 77.<BR> 4. Origin.<BR> 5. Cause, Utt. Rāmac. 5, 1.<BR> 6. The vendor, Man. 8, 202.<BR> 7. Commencement; आ मूलात्, From its beginning, Kathās. 22, 98.<BR> 8. Capital, principal.<BR> 9. The original text of any work, as opposed to its comment.<BR> 10. Own.<BR> 11. One's own kingdom, Man. 7, 184.<BR> 12. Near, proximate.<BR> 13. The root of the Arum campanulatum.<BR> II. m. and n. The nineteenth lunar asterism, Lass. 16, 18.<BR> III. f. ली (cf. मुशली, s. v. मुशल), A small house-lizard.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूल
उन्मूल उन्मूल, i. e. उद्-, adj., f. ला, uprooted, Rām. 4, 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूल
ज्येष्ठा- + मूल ज्येष्ठा- + मूल, m. the month Jyaiṣṭha, MBh. 13, 4609.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूल
तपस्- + मूल तपस्- + मूल,<BR> I. adj. having its cause in devotion, Man. 11, 234.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमूल|दंतमूल
दन्त- + मूल दन्त- + मूल, n. the root of a tooth, Suśr. 1, 303, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमूल
धन- + मूल धन- + मूल, adj. rooted, founded, in wealth, Hit. i. d. 121, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममूल|धर्म्ममूल|धर्म्ममूलं
धर्म- + मूल धर्म- + मूल, n. the roots of law, Man. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूल|निर्म्मूल
निर्मूल निर्मूल, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. ला, without any root, MBh. 5, 2747.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमूल|पादमूलं
पाद- + मूल पाद- + मूल, n. 1. the sole of the foot, Pañc. i. d. 161 (पादमूले निपात्यते, the dye is smeared on the sole of the foot, and the lover is caused to fall down before his mistress). 2. the root of the foot, tarsus, Bhāg. P. 2, 1, 26; a polite designation of a person, Rām. 1, 54, 16. 3. the foot of a mountain, Kathās. 1, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध बद्ध (vb. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b " target="_blank">Page0719-b + 42</a>] बन्ध्)-, adj. firmly rooted, Pañc. 232, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयकर्षमूल
विस्मय-कर्ष- + मूल विस्मय-कर्ष- + मूल, adj. caused by astonishment and joy, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूलम्
स-मूल + म् स-मूल + म्, adj. with the root, completely, Pañc. i. d. 339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलक|मूलकं|मूलकः
मूलक मूल + क,<BR> I. m. A sort of poison.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. An esculent root, Man. 8, 341.<BR> 2. The radish, Raphanus sativus.<BR> 3. A sort of yam.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकमूलक
मस्तक- + मूलक मस्तक- + मूलक, n. the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलखानक|मूलखानकः
मूलखानक मूलखानक, i. e. मूल-खन् + अक, m. A digger for roots, Man. 8, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलहरत्व
मूलहरत्व मूलहरत्व, i. e. मूल-हृ + अ + त्व, n. Complete ruin, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिक|मूलिकः
मूलिक मूलिक, i. e. मूल + इक,<BR> I. adj. Radical, primary.<BR> II. m. A devotee.<BR> III. f. का, A multitude of roots (?), Pañc. 157, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्य|मूल्यं
मूल्य मूल्य, i. e. मूल + य,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. The original price, Man. 8, 144.<BR> 2. Price, Pañc. ii. d. 61.<BR> 3. Wages.<BR> 4. An article purchased.<BR> II. adj.<BR> 1. Purchasable.<BR> 2. To be bought for a fair or just price.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूल्य|बहुमूल्यं
बहु- + मूल्य बहु- + मूल्य and महा-, adj. costly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुस्वर्णलक्षमूल्य
बहु-स्वर्ण-लक्ष- + मूल्य बहु-स्वर्ण-लक्ष- + मूल्य, adj. worth many hundred. thousand gold coins, Kathās. 22, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्
† मूष् मूष्, मुष् मुष्, i. 1, Par. To steal (cf. मुष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष|मूषः
मूष मूष,<BR> I. m. A rat, a mouse, Pañc. 190, 21.<BR> II. f. षा and षी.<BR> 1. A female mouse.<BR> 2. A crucible.<BR> --Cf. μῦς; Lat. mus; O.H.G. and A.S. mūs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिक|मूषिकः
मूषिक मूषिक, i. e. मूष + इक,<BR> I. m., f. का, A mouse, a rat, Pañc. 190, 19; 22.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A thief.<BR> 2. A tree, Mimosa śirīsha.<BR> 3. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाञ्चन|मूषिकांचन|मूषिकाञ्चनः
मूषिकाञ्चन मूषिकाञ्चन, i. e. मूषिक-अञ्च् + अन, m. Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृ
मृ मृ, i. 6, म्रिय, Ātm. (properly pass. refl.), in the pf. fut. and condit. Par. (in epic poetry and Cāṇ. 109 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 414, also in other forms, MBh. 1, 6189), To die, Rām. 3, 50, 21.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मृत.<BR> 1. Dead, Chr. 39, 17.<BR> 2. Calcined, reduced (as metals). n.<BR> 1. Death.<BR> 2. Solicited alms, Man. 4, 4. जीवन्मृत, i. e. जीवन्त्-, adj. Living and dead (at the same time), Bhāg. P. 5, 10, 8. Desider. मुमूर्ष, To be about to die, Hariv. 4737; Rājat. 5, 13.<BR> --Caus. मारय, To kill, MBh. 1, 7276 (also Ātm. 13, 1926); Pañc. 229, 22.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To die after, Rām. 2, 12, 84.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रमृत,<BR> 1. Dead.<BR> 2. Concealed. n. Tillage, Man. 4, 4.<BR> --Cf. Lat. morior; A.S. uta-maeran; Goth, maurthr; A.S. mórdher, myrdhra, a-myrdran, mordh, and see मर्त, and अमृत, and मृध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष्
मृक्ष् मृक्ष्, see म्रक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्
मृग् मृग्, † i. 4, Par. i. 10, मृगय (properly a denomin. derived from मृग), Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 1, 5897), To hunt, to search, Vikr. 32, 16; MBh. 1, 3644; with अन्तर्, inwardly, i. e. in the mind, Vikr. d. 1. Anomal. ptcple. pres. मृगयाण, MBh. 3, 2745.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग मृग, i. e. मृज् + अ (cf. मार्ग),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Hunting, Draup. 6, 4.<BR> 2. Investigation.<BR> 3. Asking.<BR> 4. A deer, Hit. pr. d. 36, M.M.; an antelope.<BR> 5. Game, Bhartṛ. 2, 51.<BR> 6. An animal in general, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7.<BR> 7. A kind of elephant.<BR> 8. The fifth lunar constellation.<BR> 9. Musk.<BR> II. f. गी, A female deer of antelope, a doe, Vikr. d. 121.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहामृग|ईहामृगः
ईहा- + मृग ईहा- + मृग, m. a wolf, Rām. 8, 79, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमृग|कृष्णमृगः
कृष्ण- + मृग कृष्ण- + मृग, m. the black antelope, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-b " target="_blank">Page0720-b + 39</a>] Śāk. d. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडामृग|क्रीडामृगः
क्रीडा- + मृग क्रीडा- + मृग, m. a deer for playing with, Rām. 5, 20, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरमृग
गौर- + मृग गौर- + मृग, m. a kind of buffalo, Bos gaurus, Bhāg. P. 8, 10, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रमृग|चित्रमृगः
चित्र- + मृग चित्र- + मृग, m. the spotted antelope, Rām. 5, 20, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारामृग|तारामृगः
तारा- + मृग तारा- + मृग, m. the fifth lunar constellation, Rām. 3, 49, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृग|महामृगः
महा- + मृग महा- + मृग, m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीमृग
मही- + मृग मही- + मृग, m. a terrestrial deer, Rām. 3, 49, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामृग|मायामृगः
माया- + मृग माया- + मृग, m. seeming a deer, not being one really, Rām. 3, 49, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

