मृगेन्द्रता
मृगेन्द्रता मृगेन्द्रता, i. e. मृग-इन्द्र + ता, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-a " target="_blank">Page0721-a + 41</a>] f. Dominion over the beasts, Pañc. i. d. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्
1. मृज् मृज् (akin to मृ), ii. 2, मार्ज्, मृज्, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 4, 722).<BR> 1. To wipe, MBh. 4, 722.<BR> 2. To rub, to stroke, Rām. 1, 64, 7.<BR> 3. To cleanse, MBh. 3, 2577.<BR> 4. To sweep or to cast on somebody, Man. 8, 317.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. मृष्ट.<BR> 1. Rubbed, touched.<BR> 2. Sprinkled.<BR> 3. Cleansed.<BR> 4. Pure, Nal. 12, 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, मार्जय, Par. To wipe away, Bhartṛ. 2, 89. मार्जित, Bright, Rājat. 5, 369.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, To remove, Man. 2, 27.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To sweep away, to destroy, MBh. 1, 5487.<BR> 2. To (rub away, to) wash, to moisten, Utt. Rāmac. 153, 3.<BR> --With आ आ, To wipe, MBh. 2, 2224. आमृष्ट, Rubbed at, Śāk. d. 161.<BR> --With नि नि, To wipe, Man. 4, 216. Desider. मिमृक्ष, To flash down, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4 (ved. red. pf.).<BR> --With निस् निस्, To wipe, Lass. 59, 11.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To wipe, MBh. 3, 584.<BR> 2. To touch, Śāk. 83, 7.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To wipe, Man. 2, 60.<BR> 2. To rub, to stroke, MBh. 3, 1778.<BR> 3. To remove, Ragh. 6, 41; 44.<BR> 4. To destroy, Bhartṛ. 2, 75. प्र-मृष्ट,<BR> 1. Rubbed.<BR> 2. Polished, bright, Mālav. d. 24; clear.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To wipe, Sāv. 5, 96.<BR> 2. To rub, to stroke, MBh. 3, 16849.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To sweep together, Rājat. 5, 74.<BR> 2. To cleanse, Chr. 61, 38.<BR> 3. To purify, MBh. 2, 2186.<BR> --Cf. ἀμέργω, ὀμόργνυμι, ὄμοργμα, ἀμέλγω, γλάγος (for μλάγος by assimilation), γάλα, γάλακτος [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b " target="_blank">Page0721-b + 37</a>] (for original μλακτο, ptcple. of the pf. pass.); Lat. mulgere, mulier, lac (for mlac), margo; Goth. miluks; A.S. meoluc, meolc, melcan; Goth. marka; A.S. mearc, mearcian, ge-mearc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमृष्ट
सु-मृष्ट सु-मृष्ट, adj. very fine, Pañc. 113, 8; very delicate, i. d. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्
2. मृज् मृज्, see मुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज|मृजः
मृज मृज,<BR> I. m. A musical instrument.<BR> II. जा (1. मृज् + अ), f. Cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृञ्ज्
मृञ्ज् मृञ्ज्, see मुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड्
मृड् मृड् (for original मृड्ढ्, i. e. मृष्-धा, cf. Zend. मरेज़्ह्दा and मेरेज़्ह्दिक), i. 6, and ii. 9, मृड्णा, मृड्णी, Par.<BR> 1. To pardon (ved.).<BR> 2. To exhilarate, to delight (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड|मृडः
मृड मृड् + अ, m. Śiva. f. डा, डी, Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडङ्कण|मृडङ्कणः
मृडङ्कण मृडङ्कण, m. A child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्
मृण् मृण् (developed out of मृ + ना, see मॄ), i. 6, Par. To kill.<BR> --Cf. μάρναμαι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणाल|मृणालं|मृणालः
मृणाल मृणाल,<BR> I. m. and n. The stalk of a lotus, Vikr. d. 19.<BR> II. m., and f. ली, A small fibre of a lotus, Vikr. d. 54 (˚ल); Utt. Rāmac. 15, 16 (˚ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालवन्त्|मृणालवत्
मृणालवन्त् मृणाल + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessing fibres, Śāk. 31, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालिन्
मृणालिन् मृणालिन्, i. e. मृणाल + इन्,<BR> I. m. A lotus.<BR> II. f. नी, A place where lotus flowers grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्मय
मृण्मय मृण्मय, and better मृन्मय मृन्मय (Man. 5, 122), i. e. मृद् + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of earth or clay, earthen, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतक|मृतकं|मृतकः
मृतक मृत + क, (vb. मृ), n. A dead body, Lass. 4, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतण्ड|मृतंडः|मृतण्डः
मृतण्ड मृतण्ड, m. The father of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतवत्
मृतवत् मृत + वत् (vb. मृ), adv. Like one dead, Hit. 91, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृति|मृतिः
मृति मृ + ति, f. Death.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mors, mortis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्तिका
मृत्तिका मृत्तिका (derived from मृद्), f.<BR> 1. Earth, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 18; clay (?), Chr. 57, 22.<BR> 2. A fragrant earth.<BR> 3. Fresh earth, Man. 2, 182.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्तिक
पाण्डु-मृत्तिक पाण्डु-मृत्तिक, adj. having a white ground, Rām. 2, 71, 19; chalk-like, ib. 91, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमृत्तिक
पूति-मृत्तिक पूति-मृत्तिक, m. the name of a hell, Man. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्पिण्डतस्
मृत्पिण्डतस् मृत्पिण्डतस्, i. e. मृद्-पिण्ड + तस्, adv. Of a piece of clay, Hit. pr. d. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यु|मृत्युः
मृत्यु मृत्यु (vb. मृ),<BR> 1. m. f. Death, Pañc. iii. d. 14.<BR> 2. m. Yama.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्यु|अपमृत्युः
अप- + मृत्यु अप- + मृत्यु, m. sudden, or unnatural death, Pañc. 186, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्नमृत्यु
प्रत्यासन्न- + मृत्यु प्रत्यासन्न- + मृत्यु (vb. सद्), adj. to whom death was imminent, Pañc. 10, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृत्यु|महामृत्युः
महा- + मृत्यु महा- + मृत्यु, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमृत्यु|विषमृत्युः
विष- + मृत्यु विष- + मृत्यु, m. a kind of pheasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युंजय|मृत्युञ्जय|मृत्युंजयः|मृत्युञ्जयः
मृत्युंजय मृत्युंजय, i. e. म्रित्यु + म्-जि + अ, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युभङ्गुरक|मृत्युभङ्गुरकः
मृत्युभङ्गुरक मृत्यु-भङ्गुर + क, m. A drum beat on funeral occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्सा
मृत्सा मृत्सा, and मृत्स्ना मृत्स्ना (derived from मृद्), f. Good soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्नाभाण्डक|मृत्स्नाभाण्डकः
मृत्स्नाभाण्डक मृत्स्ना-भाण्ड + क, n. An earthen vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
1. मृद् मृद् (akin to मृ), ii. 9, मृद्ना, नी, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 2937, and i. 1, Par., ib. 1, 4979).<BR> 1. To rub, MBh. 3, 2937.<BR> 2. To stroke, MBh. 4, 767.<BR> 3. To grind, to pound, to reduce to dust, MBh. 3, 1349.<BR> 4. To crush, to dash to pieces, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2149.<BR> 5. To batter, Johns. Sel. 25, 5.<BR> 6. To trample on, to tread under foot, Nal. 13, 39. मृदित, Languid, Bhartṛ. 2, 36.<BR> --Caus. मर्दय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-b " target="_blank">Page0722-b + 40</a>]<BR> 1. To rub, Hit. ii. d. 131.<BR> 2. To tread under foot, to kill, MBh. 3, 11106 (anomal. ptcple. pres. Ātm. मर्दयान).<BR> 3. To break to pieces, Rām. 1, 1, 72.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To trample on, MBh. 1, 7750.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To rub, MBh. 4, 468.<BR> 2. To break to pieces, 3, 16346.<BR> 3. To trample on, Rām. 2, 93, 8.<BR> 4. To destroy, MBh. 3, 10203.<BR> --With आ आ, To grind to pieces, Rām. 2, 96, 20.<BR> --With उप उप, To kill, Naiṣ. 5, 110.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To wipe off, Rām. 2, 77, 26.<BR> 2. To surpass (i. 1, Par.), MBh. 1, 4979. परिमृदित, Rubbed, ground, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 16 (trampled upon).<BR> --With प्र प्र, To destroy, MBh. 3, 11676.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To rub to pieces, Rām. 2, 88, 8.<BR> 2. To break, Man. 4, 70.<BR> 3. To destroy, MBh. 1, 5504.<BR> --Caus. To grind, Rām. 2, 88, 2.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To rub, to clean, Pañc. 121, 13.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mordere; A.S. malt; O.H.G. malz; A.S. meltan, miltan; O.H.G. smelzan; A.S. smeortan; O.H.G. smerzan; A.S. smilt, smylt, smolt; ἀμέρδω, ἀμαλδύνω, μέλδω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
2. मृद् मृद्, f.<BR> 1. Earth, Pañc. ii. d. 109; clay, Pañc. ii. d. 36.<BR> 2. A piece of earth, Man. 5, 136.<BR> 3. A fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्ग|मृदंग|मृदंगः|मृदङ्गः
मृदङ्ग मृदङ्ग, probably मृद् + अ + म्-ग, m.<BR> 1. A tabour, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 9; a small drum, Pañc. 20, 8.<BR> 2. A sound.<BR> 3. Bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदर
मृदर मृद् + अर, m.<BR> 1. A hole.<BR> 2. Disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदा
मृदा मृद् + आ, f. Earth, clay.<BR> --Cf. Goth. mulda; A.S. molde; probably Lat. merda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदाकर|मृदाकरः
मृदाकर मृदा-कर, m. The thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदिनी
मृदिनी मृदिनी, i. e. मृद्, or मृदा, + इन् + ई, f. Good soil<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदु|मृदुः
मृदु मृद् + उ, adj., f. द्वी (Rām. 4, 2, 2), comparat. म्रदीयंस्, superl. म्रदिष्ठ.<BR> 1. Soft, Pañc. i. d. 303; iii. d. 253; Johns. Sel. 56, 153 (-पूर्वम्, adv. At first mildly).<BR> 2. Mild, Vikr. d. 85.<BR> 3. Weak, Hit. 81, 22.<BR> 4. Blunt.<BR> 5. Slow, Sāv. 4, 33.<BR> --Cf. Goth. and A.S. mild; Lat. mollis; probably βραδύς; Lat. bardus; ἀϐλαδέως; Lat. blandus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुता
मृदुता मृदु + ता, f. Softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुल|मृदुलं
मृदुल मृदु + ल,<BR> I. adj. Soft.<BR> II. n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुलोमक|मृदुलोमकः
मृदुलोमक मृदुलोमक, i. e. मृदु-लोमन् + क, m. A hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वीका
मृद्वीका मृद्वी + का (मृदु, f.), f. A grape.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुमृद्वीका
पृथु- + मृद्वीका पृथु- + मृद्वीका, f. a broadgrape (?), MBh. 7, 2309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध्
मृध् मृध् (i. e. मृ-धा), i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To kill (ved.).<BR> 2. † To be moist or wet.<BR> --Cf. probably (in spite of the anomal. correspondence), Goth. maurthr; A.S. mórdher, mórdhor; O.H.G. multjan; probably μαλθακός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध|मृधं
मृध मृध् + अ, n. War, battle, Chr. 19, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृन्मय
मृन्मय मृन्मय, see मृण्मय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृन्मरु|मृन्मरुः
मृन्मरु मृन्मरु, i. e. मृद्-मरु, m. A stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश्
मृश् मृश् (often confounded with मृष्), i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 62, 18).<BR> 1. To touch, to stroke.<BR> 2. To think, to consider.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To consider, Rām. 2, 11, 9.<BR> --With अव अव, Caus. To trouble, Bhāg. P. 4, 7, 48. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-b " target="_blank">Page0723-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To touch, Śiś. 9, 34.<BR> 2. To destroy, Ragh. 9, 5 (Calc.).<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pf. pass. अन्-आमृष्ट, Untouched, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 1.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, To overpower, MBh. 4, 164 (with ष् instead of श्).<BR> --With परा परा,<BR> 1. To stroke, Utt. Rāmac. 25, 14.<BR> 2. To touch, Ragh. 3, 68 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To seize, MBh. 4, 46.<BR> 4. To seduce, Chr. 6, 7.<BR> 5. To violate, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 11.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To stroke, Rām. 2, 10, 25.<BR> 2. To seize, Rām. 2, 23, 5 (with ष्).<BR> 3. To consider, Rām. 1, 2, 20.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To stroke, Rām. 2, 20, 32.<BR> 2. To inquire, MBh. 3, 2680 (with ष्).<BR> 3. To examine, Mālav. 11, 23.<BR> 4. To reflect, Hit. 71, 2, M.M.; Bhāg. P. 6, 5, 10; Hit. iv. d. 97 (विमृश्य-कारिन्, One who acts [only] after due reflection). अ-विमृश्य, Without reflecting, Pañc. 238, 25.<BR> 5. To perceive, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 7.<BR> --Caus. To examine, Pañc. i. d. 122.<BR> --With अनुवि अनु-वि, To reflect, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 15.<BR> --Cf. Lat. mulcere, probably, mulcare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
1. मृष् मृष् (often confounded with मृश्), i. 4, and i. 10, and † i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To bear, to endure patiently, Man. 4, 217; Pañc. iii. d. 19; v. d. 67.<BR> 2. To suffer, Utt. Rāmac. 71, 8.<BR> 3. To let, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 10.<BR> 4. To pardon, Man. 8, 313.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-मृष्यन्त्, अ-मर्षयन्त् (Johns. Sel. 54, 135), and अ-मृष्यमाण, Enraged.<BR> --Caus. To suffer, Hit. iii. d. 48.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अ-मर्षित, adj. Impatient, angry, Rām. 4, 9, 13. दुर्मर्षित, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Incited, stirred up, MBh. 14, 2314.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To endure, Pañc. rec. orn.<BR> --With प्रत्यव [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a " target="_blank">Page0724-a + 41</a>] प्रति-अव. To endure reluctantly, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 5.<BR> --With वि वि, To neglect, MBh. 3, 15441.<BR> --Cf. Goth. marzjan (Caus.); O.H.G. marrjan; A.S. myrran.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
† 2. मृष् मृष्, i. 1, Par. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषा
मृषा मृषा (an old instr. sing. of 1. मृष् + अ, properly, ‘With pardon,’ ‘I beg your pardon’), adv.<BR> 1. Falsely, Man. 3, 53.<BR> 2. Uselessly.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृषा
अ- + मृषा अ- + मृषा, adv. truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषार्थक|मृषार्थकं
मृषार्थक मृषार्थक, i. e. मृषा-अर्थ + क, n. An absurdity, an impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषोद्य|मृषोद्यं|मृषोद्यः
मृषोद्य मृषोद्य, i. e. मृषा-वद् + य,<BR> I. adj. and sbst. Lying, a liar.<BR> II. n. Falsehood, Utt. Rāmac. 104, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
मृष्टि मृष्टि, i. e. मृज्, मृश्, and मृष्, + ति, f.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Preparing food, Man. 3, 255.<BR> 3. Touching.<BR> 4. Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मॄ
† मॄ मॄ, ii. 9, मृणा, णी, Par. To kill (see मृण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मे
मे मे, i. 1, Ātm. To barter or to exchange.<BR> --Caus. मापय, To cross over, MBh. 1, 5842 (anomal. ptcple. pres. Ātm. मापयान).<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, To barter, Man. 10, 94.<BR> --Cf. Goth. maithms; A.S. madhm; Goth. maidjan, ga-mains; A.S. maene, mán, gemaene; Lat. mūtuus, communis, munus; μοῖτος, ἀμείϐω (Caus. for ἀ-μεϐίω).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखला
मेखला मेखला, f.<BR> 1. A girdle, Ragh. 8, 63; Utt. Rāmac. 106, 1.<BR> 2. The sacrificial string, see कृ with मेखला.<BR> 3. A sword-belt.<BR> 4. A swordknot.<BR> 5. The slope of a mountain, Megh. 12.<BR> 6. The Narmadā river.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमेखल
मणि-मेखल मणि-मेखल, adj. surrounded by jewels. Ṛt. 6, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिन्
मेखलिन् मेखलिन्, i. e. मेखला + इन्, adj. f. नी, Wearing a girdle, Pañc. iii. d. 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ|मेघः
मेघ मेघ, i. e. मिह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A cloud, Pañc. 169, 6.<BR> 2. A demon.<BR> 3. A fragrant grass.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमेघ|गृहमेघः
गृह- + मेघ गृह- + मेघ, m. a multitude of houses, Rām. 5, 10, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवत्|मेघवन्त्
मेघवत् मेघ + वत्, adv. Like a cloud, Chr. 35, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचक|मेचकं|मेचकः
मेचक मेछक,<BR> I. adj. Black, Utt. Rāmac. 149, 15; dark blue, Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 63; Megh. 60.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Black, or dark blue (the colour).<BR> 2. The eye of a peacock's tail.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR> 4. Smoke.<BR> III. m. and n. Darkness.<BR> IV. n. Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेट्
मेट् मेट्, see म्लेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेठ|मेठः
मेठ मेठ, मेण्ठ मेण्ठ, and मेण्ड मेण्ड, m. An elephant-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेड्
मेड् मेड्, see म्रेड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्र|मेढ्रः
मेढ्र मेढ्र, i. e. मिह् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. The penis, Man. 8, 282.<BR> 2. A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथ्
मेथ् मेथ्, and मेध् मेध्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt (ved.).<BR> 2. To understand.<BR> 3. To associate (ved.).<BR> --Caus. मेधय, To cause to understand, to know, MBh. 13, 7510.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथि|मेथिः
मेथि मेथि, and मेधि मेधि, m. The part of a threshing floor round which the cattle turn to tread out the corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद्
मेद् मेद्, see मिथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद|मेदः
मेद मेद, m.<BR> 1. Adeps, fat.<BR> 2. The son of a Vaideha by a Kārāvara female, Man. 10, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्
मेदस् मेदस्, n.<BR> 1. Marrow, Pañc. i. d. 123.<BR> 2. The serous secretion that spreads amongst the muscular fibres.<BR> 3. Morbid corpulency, Śāk. d. 38.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. medulla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनी
मेदिनी मेदिनी (probably = मृदिनी, and based on its original form मर्दिनी, cf. गेह, वेतन; or perhaps मेद + इन् + ई), f.<BR> 1. The earth, Pañc. iii. d. 41; earth, Johns. Sel. 95, 67.<BR> 2. A country, Cāṇ. 45 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुर|मेदुरः
मेदुर मेदुर (cf. मेदस्), adj.<BR> 1. Unctuous.<BR> 2. Smooth.<BR> 3. Soft.<BR> 4. Thick, Utt. Rāmac. 143, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुरित
मेदुरित मेदुरित, i. e. मेदुर + इत, adj. Unctuous, abounding in water, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्
मेध् मेध्, see मेथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध|मेधः
मेध मेध (i. e. मह् and perhaps धा),<BR> I. m. (and ved., also n., Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3), Sacrifice, 1. 1.<BR> II. f. धा, Understanding, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेध|अश्वमेधः
अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध, m. the sacrifice of a horse, Hit. iv. d. 129; Rām. 6, 104, 7; Ragh. 13, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगमेध|तुरगमेधः
अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध, m. the sacrifice of a horse, Hit. iv. d. 129; Rām. 6, 104, 7; Ragh. 13, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गममेध
अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध अश्व-, तुरग-, तुरङ्गम- + मेध, m. the sacrifice of a horse, Hit. iv. d. 129; Rām. 6, 104, 7; Ragh. 13, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमेध|गृहमेधः
गृह- + मेध गृह- + मेध,<BR> I. m. a domestic sacrifice.<BR> II. adj. referring to the duties of a householder, Bhāg. P. 3, 22, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मेध
दुस्- + मेध दुस्- + मेध, adj., f. ध, stupid, Bhāg. P. 1, 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमेध|नरमेधः
नर- + मेध नर- + मेध, नृ-, पुरुष-, m. the sacrifice of a man, Rām. 1, 63, 6 Gorr. (नर-); Kathās. 26, 238 (पुरुष-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमेध|पितृमेधः
पितृ- + मेध पितृ- + मेध, m. oblation to the Manes, Man. 5, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधस्
ऽमेधस् -मेधस्, a substitute for मेधा, when latter part of a comp. adj.; e. g. अल्प-, Having little understanding, Pañc. ii. d. 92. दुस्-, Stupid, Rām. 1, 25, 11. परम-दुस्-, adj. Most stupid, Pañc. 3, 12. सु-,<BR> I. adj. Intelligent.<BR> II. m. Heart pea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधाविन्
मेधाविन् मेधा + विन्, adj., f. नी, Intelligent, Man. 2, 110; wise, Hit. ii. d. 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मेधाविन्
दुस्- + मेधाविन् दुस्- + मेधाविन्, adj. stupid, MBh. 12, 9486.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधि|मेधिः
मेधि मेधि, see मेथि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधिर|मेधिरः
मेधिर मेधिर, i. e. मेधा + इर, adj. Intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्य|मेध्यं|मेध्यः
मेध्य मेध्य, i. e. मेध + य, adj.<BR> 1. Fit for, belonging to, a sacrifice, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 10.<BR> 2. Pure, Man. 1, 92.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अ- + मेध्य अ- + मेध्य,<BR> I. adj. impure, Man. 4, 53.<BR> II. n. an impure substance, Man. 2, 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनका
मेनका मेनका, i. e. मेना + क, f. One of the courtesans of heaven, and wife to Himālaya, Śiś. 9, 86; Śāk. 14, 23 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेना
मेना मेना, f. One of the courtesans of heaven, and wife to Himālaya, Rām. 1, 37, 15 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाद|मेनादः
मेनाद मे-नाद (मे, an imitative sound), m.<BR> 1. A cat.<BR> 2. A goat.<BR> 3. A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेप्
† मेप् मेप्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेब्
मेब् मेब्, see मेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरु|मेरुः
मेरु मेरु, m. A fabulous mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमेरु|सुमेरुः
सु- + मेरु सु- + मेरु,<BR> I. m. = Meru.<BR> II. adj. excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेल|मेलः
मेल मेल, i. e. मिल् + अ,<BR> I. m., and f. ला, Assemblage, meeting, Pañc. 245, 4 (ला).<BR> II. f. ला, Ink (borrowed from μέλας).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलक|मेलकः
मेलक मेल + क, m. Assemblage, Hit. 72, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेव्
† मेव् मेव्, मेब् मेब्, and म्लेव् म्लेव्, i. 1, Ātm. To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेष|मेषः
मेष मेष (vb. मिह्, probably for मेक्ष),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A ram. Pañc. iii. d. 40.<BR> 2. The sign अरिएस्.<BR> II. f. षी, An ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषिका
मेषिका मेषिका, i. e. मेषी + क, f. An ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेह|मेहः
मेह मेह, i. e. मिह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Making water, Man. 4, 52.<BR> 2. Urine.<BR> 3. A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहतस्
मेहतस् मेह + तस्, adv. By making water, Man. 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहन|मेहनं|मेहनः
मेहन मेहन, i. e. मिह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Membrum virile.<BR> 2. Urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र|मैत्रं|मैत्रः
मैत्र मैत्र, properly मैत्त्र, i. e. मित्त्र + अ (see मित्त्र),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to a friend, friendly, Bhag. 12, 13.<BR> 2. Given by a friend, Man. 9, 206.<BR> 3. m. (viz. संधि), Proceeding from friendship, the name of a kind of alliance, Hit. iv. d. 123.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A friend to all creatures, Man. 2, 87.<BR> 2. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 3. The son of an outcaste Vaiśya, Man. 10, 23.<BR> 4. The anus.<BR> 5. Discharging of excrement, Man. 4, 152.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Friendship, Pañc. ii. d. 47.<BR> 2. The seventeenth lunar asterism.<BR> --Cf. मैत्र्य.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मैत्र
दुर्मैत्र दुर्मैत्र, i. e. दुस्-, adj. hostile, Bhāg. P. 7, 5, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रक|मैत्रकं
मैत्रक मैत्र + क, n. Friendship, Utt. Rāmac. 128, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रता
मैत्रता मैत्र + ता, f. Friendship, Cāṇ. 19 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्राक्षज्योतिक
मैत्राक्षज्योतिक मैत्राक्षज्योतिक, i. e. मैत्र-अक्ष-ज्योति (instead of ज्योतिस्), + क, m. The name of a demon, Man. 12, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुण|मैत्रावरुणः
मैत्रावरुण and मैत्रावरुणि मैत्रावरुण, or ˚णि, i. e. मित्रावरुण (द्वन्द्व comp. of मित्र and वरुण), + अ or इ, patronym., m. A son of Mitra and Varuṇa; a name of Vaśiṣṭha, Utt. Rāmac. 9, 4, and of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेय|मैत्रेयः
मैत्रेय मैत्रेय, i. e. मित्र + एय (cf. मित्त्र).<BR> I. adj. Relating to a friend.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The son of a Vaideha by an Ayogava female.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयक|मैत्रेयकः
मैत्रेयक मैत्रेय + क, m.<BR> 1. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b " target="_blank">Page0726-b + 40</a>] son of a Vaideha by an Ayogava female, Man. 10, 33.<BR> 2. A crier or chaunter of the hours (this being probably the office of a Maitreyaka)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र्य|मैत्र्यं
मैत्र्य मैत्र्य, i. e. मित्र + य (cf. मित्त्र), n., and f. त्री, Friendship, Pañc. iv. d. 70 (n.); 243, 13, and 248, 2 (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिल|मैथिलः
मैथिल मैथिल, i. e. मिथिला + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ली, Born in, referring to, Mithilā, Utt. Rāmac. 110, 13.<BR> II. m. The king of Mithilā, Rām. 3, 53, 2.<BR> III. f. ली, A name of Sītā, ib. 3, 49, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन|मैथुनं
मैथुन मैथुन, i. e. मिथुन + अ,<BR> I. adj. Worn at a time of sexual intercourse, Man. 4, 116.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Sexual intercourse, Hit. pr. d. 25, M.M.<BR> 2. Marriage, holy union, Man. 3, 5 (perhaps adj. Being in accordance with a legitimate marriage).<BR> 3. Matrimony, Pañc. ii. d. 101.<BR> 4. Union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनिन्
मैथुनिन् मैथुनिन्, i. e. मैथुन + इन्, adj. sbst. One who has been connected with a woman, Man. 5, 144.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामैथुनिन्
दिवा- + मैथुनिन् दिवा- + मैथुनिन्, adj. having sexual intercourse by day, Mārk. P. 14, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन्य
मैथुन्य मैथुन्य, i. e. मैथुन + य, adj. Contracted for the purpose of amorous embraces, Man. 3, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाक|मैनाकः
मैनाक मैनाक, i. e. मेना + क + अ, m. The name of a mountain, Rām. 5, 49, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्द|मैंद|मैंदः|मैन्दः
मैन्द मैन्द, m. The name of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्दहन्|मैंदहन्
मैन्दहन् मैन्द-हन्, m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरेय|मैरेयं|मैरेयः
मैरेय मैरेय, n. A spirituous liquor, Rājat. 5, 368.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मो
मो मो, i. e. मा-उ, But not, Chr. 289, 13 = Rigv. i. 50, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तुकाम
मोक्तुकाम मोक्तुकाम, i. e. मोक्तुम्-काम (infin. of मुच्), adj. Desiring to cast, Chr. 41, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष्
मोक्ष् मोक्ष्, i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from मोक्स्ह), and † i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 5301).<BR> 1. To release, to liberate, MBh. 1, 2084.<BR> 2. † To cast.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-मोक्षयन्त्, adj. Neglecting to liberate, Yājñ. 2, 300.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, To release, to liberate, Weber, Ind. St. iii. 371, 4, below.<BR> --With वि वि, To release, to protect, MBh. 1, 7880.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष|मोक्षः
मोक्ष मोक्स्ह् + अ (मोक्स्ह् is an anomal. desider. of मुच्), m.<BR> 1. Untying, Pañc. 109, 9; Megh. 97.<BR> 2. Liberation, Pañc. 109, 11; Chr. 4, 16.<BR> 3. Liberation of the soul from the body and from further transmigration, final beatitude, Man. 1, 114; Pañc. ii. d. 127.<BR> 4. Death.<BR> 5. Acquittance of an obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षक|मोक्षकः
मोक्षक मोक्स्ह् + अक, adj. and sbst., m.<BR> 1. One who sets at liberty, Man. 8, 342.<BR> 2. A deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षण|मोक्षणं
मोक्षण मोक्षण, i. e. मोक्स्ह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Letting go (shedding of blood), Mālav. d. 62.<BR> 2. Liberation, Pañc. 143, 6.<BR> 3. Squandering.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमोक्षण
प्राण- + मोक्षण प्राण- + मोक्षण, n. resigning life, suicide, Pañc. 110, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघ|मोघं|मोघः
मोघ मोघ, i. e. मुह् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Vain, useless, Sāv. 5, 49; Megh. 6; ˚घम्, adv. In vain, Bhag. 3, 16.<BR> 2. Left.<BR> II. m. A fence.<BR> III. f. घा, Trumpet-flower, Bignonia suaveolens.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अ- + मोघ अ- + मोघ,<BR> I. adj., f. घा, not vain, not going astray, unfailing, Vikr. d. 88; attaining one's aim, efficacious, Megh. 72.<BR> II. f. घा. 1. the name of a club, Rām. 1, 29, 12. 2. the name of several plants. 3. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच|मोचं|मोचः
मोच मोछ (vb. मुच् + अ),<BR> I. m. A tree, Hyperanthera morunga.<BR> II. f. चा.<BR> 1. The silk cotton-tree.<BR> 2. The plantain.<BR> III. n. Its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचक|मोचकः
मोचक मोछक, i. e.<BR> A. मोछ + क, m. = मोछ,<BR> I.,<BR> II.<BR> B. मुच् + अक, m.<BR> 1. A devotee, free from worldly passion and desire.<BR> 2. A liberator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचन|मोचनं
मोचन मोछन, i. e. मुच् + अन, n. Liberating, liberation, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 10; Lass. 39, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटन|मोटनं|मोटनः
मोटन मोटन,<BR> I. m. Wind.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Pressing, strangulating, Lass. 43, 1.<BR> 2. Grinding, reducing to dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोण|मोणः
मोण मोण, m.<BR> 1. Dried fruit.<BR> 2. A crocodile.<BR> 3. A fly.<BR> 4. A basket for carrying snakes in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोद|मोदः
मोद मोद, i. e. मुद् + अ, m. Joy, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदक|मोदकः
मोदक मोदक, i. e. मुद् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Delighting.<BR> II. m. and n. A sort of sweetmeat, Pañc. i. d. 303; sweetmeats in general, Vikr. 45, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष|मोषः
मोष मोष, i. e. मुष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Robbing; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 16.<BR> 2. Robbery, Man. 9, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषक|मोषकः
मोषक मोषक, i. e. मुष् + अक, m. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषण|मोषणं
मोषण मोषण, i. e. मुष् + अन, n. Stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोह|मोहं|मोहः
मोह मोह, i. e. मुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Fainting, Vikr. 84, 10; loss of consciousness, Vikr. d. 8.<BR> 2. Bewilderment, distraction, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 13; Ṛt. 6, 26.<BR> 3. Weakness of intellect, Man. 3, 15.<BR> 4. Ignorance, foolishness, infatuation, Pañc. i. d. 250; iii. d. 87.<BR> 5. Error, Matsyop. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहन|मोहनं|मोहनः
मोहन मोहन, i. e. मुह् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Depriving of consciousness or understanding, infatuating, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 13; Kathās. 46, 110 (with विद्या, A magical knowledge).<BR> II. m. One of the arrows of Kāma, Lass. 7, 3.<BR> III. n. Temptation, the overpowering [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a " target="_blank">Page0728-a + 38</a>] of reason by sensual allurements.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटमोहन|कूटमोहनः
कूट- + मोहन कूट- + मोहन, m. epithet of Skanda, MBh. 3, 14632.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिन्
मोहिन् मोहिन्, i. e. मुह् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Bewildering, infatuating, Bhag. 9, 12.<BR> II. f. नी, A kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकुलि|मौकुलिः
मौकुलि मौकुलि, m. A crow, Utt. Rāmac. 48, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिक|मौक्तिकं
मौक्तिक मौक्तिक, i. e. मुक्ता + इक, n. A pearl, Pañc. iv. d. 78.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमौक्तिक
गज- + मौक्तिक गज- + मौक्तिक, n. pearls which are supposed to be in the frontal globes of the elephant, Kir. 12, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्य|मौक्यं
मौक्य मौक्य, i. e. मूक + य, n. Dumbness, Man. 10, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर्य|मौखर्यं|मौखर्य्य|मौखर्य्यं
मौखर्य मौखर्य, i. e. मुखर + य, n., and f. री.<BR> 1. Defamation.<BR> 2. Scurrility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख्य|मौख्यं
मौख्य मौख्य, i. e. मुख + य, n. Pre-eminence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममौख्य
ग्राम- + मौख्य ग्राम- + मौख्य, Hit. 66, 6, probably in erroneous reading for ग्राममुख्य, chief of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौग्ध्य|मौग्ध्यं
मौग्ध्य मौग्ध्य, i. e. मुग्ध (vb. मुह्), + य, n. Charm, beauty, Utt. Rāmac. 107, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्ज|मौंज
मौञ्ज मौञ्ज, i. e. मुञ्ज + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. जि, Made of मुञ्ज, Man. 2, 42.<BR> II. f. जि (and मौञ्जि मौञ्जि, Man. 2, 169, by metrical exigence), The girdle of a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 2, 27; Kumāras. 5, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौढ्य|मौढ्यं
मौढ्य मौढ्य, i. e. मूढ (vb. मुह्), + य, n. Ignorance, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्ड्य|मौंड्यं
मौण्ड्य मौण्ड्य, i. e. मुण्ड + य, n.<BR> 1. Baldness.<BR> 2. Shaving of the head, Man. 8, 370.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलि|मौद्गलिः
मौद्गलि मौद्गलि, m. A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौन|मौनं
मौन मौन, i. e. मुनि + अ, n. Silence, taciturnity, Hit. i. d. 134, M.M.; Pañc. iv. d. 51.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तामौन
चिन्ता- + मौन चिन्ता- + मौन, n. silent thinking, Vikr. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिन्
मौनिन् मौनिन्, i. e. मौन + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Silent, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1677; Rājat. 5, 304.<BR> II. m. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरजिक|मौरजिकः
मौरजिक मौरजिक, i. e. मुरज + इक, m. A drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्ख्य|मौर्ख्यं
मौर्ख्य मौर्ख्य, i. e. मूर्ख + य, n. Stupidity, folly, Rājat. 5, 389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्य|मौर्यः
मौर्य मौर्य, m. The name of an Indian dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्यदत्त
मौर्यदत्त मौर्य-दत्त (vb. दा), m. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व
मौर्व मौर्व, i. e. मूर्व + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. वी, Made of मूर्व, Man. 2, 42.<BR> II. f. वी, A bowstring, Śāk. d. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल|मौलः
मौल मौल, i. e. मूल + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Proceeding from a root.<BR> 2. Of pure blood, Hit. iii. d. 17.<BR> 3. Descended from those who had lived in a village when it was built, Man. 8, 259.<BR> 4. Born in the same district (of the same root), Man. 8, 62.<BR> 5. Hereditary, Man. 7, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि मौलि (akin to मूल), m. and f.<BR> 1. A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR> 2. Hair ornamented and braided round the head.<BR> 3. A crown, diadem, Vikr. d. 60; Pañc. 230, 18.<BR> 4. The head, Lass. 66, 2; Hit. 72, 19 (मौलौ निधाय, Obeying).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धेन्दुमौलि
अर्ध-इन्दु- + मौलि अर्ध-इन्दु- + मौलि, adj. epithet of Śiva (wearing the crescent as diadem), Megh. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमौलि
चक्र- + मौलि चक्र- + मौलि, m. the name of a Rākṣasa, Rām. 6, 69, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाकरकलामौलि
निशाकर-कला- + मौलि निशाकर-कला- + मौलि, adj. (wearing the crescent as diadem), epithet of Śiva, Kathās. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिक|मौलिकः
मौलिक मौलि + क (scarcely मूल + इक), adj. Chief, best, Utt. Rāmac. 61, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिन्
मौलिन् मौलिन्, i. e. मौलि + इन्, adj. Endowed with a diadem, Sund. 1, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौली
मौली मौली (akin to मूल), f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल्य|मौल्यं
मौल्य मौल्य, i. e. मूल + य (cf. मूल्य), n. Price, Lass. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौषल|मौषलं
मौषल मौस्हल, i. e. मुषल + अ, adj. Performed with a club, Hariv. 5648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टा
मौष्टा मौष्टा, i. e. मुष्टि + अ, f. Playing at fisticuffs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्त|मौहूर्तः|मौहूर्त्त|मौहूर्त्तः
मौहूर्त मौहूर्त, and मौहूर्तिक मौहूर्तिक, i. e. मुहूर्त + अ, or इक, m. An astrologer, Hit. 94, 9 (तिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्ना
म्ना म्ना (i. e. मन् + आ), i. 1, मन, Par.<BR> 1. To fix in the memory by frequent repetition.<BR> 2. To remember, to praise (ved.).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To repeat frequently, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 30. आम्नाता, Recorded, Pañc. i. d. 408.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To prescribe, Utt. Rāmac. 92, 6.<BR> --Cf. μιμνήσκω, μνῆμα, μνάομαι; Lat. meminisse.<BR> --Cf. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष्
म्रक्ष् † म्रक्ष्, मृक्ष् मृक्ष् (akin to मृज्), † मक्ष् मक्ष्, i. 1, Par. To accumulate. † म्रक्ष्, मृक्ष्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To smear.<BR> 2. To speak incorrectly.<BR> 3. To accumulate.<BR> 4. To divide, to cut.<BR> --मृक्ष्, with अभि अभि, i. 10, To anoint, MBh. 13, 7426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष|म्रक्षः
म्रक्ष म्रक्ष् + अ, m. Concealment of one's vices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षण|म्रक्षणं
म्रक्षण म्रक्षण, i. e. म्रक्ष् + अन, n. Oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद्
† म्रद् म्रद् (cf. मृद्), i. 1, Ātm. To grind, to reduce to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिष्ठ|म्रदिष्ठः
म्रदिष्ठ म्रदिष्ठ, म्रदीयंस् म्रदीयंस्, see मृदु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुच्
म्रुच् म्रुच्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --With नि नि, and अभिनि अभि-नि, To set (as the sun), ved., Weber, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, xiv. 756, sqq.<BR> --Cf. म्लुछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुञ्च्|म्रुंच्
† म्रुञ्च् म्रुञ्च्, म्लुञ्च् म्लुञ्च्, मञ्च् मञ्च्, मुञ्च् मुञ्च्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेट्
म्रेट् म्रेट्, see म्लेट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेड्
म्रेड् म्रेड्, † म्लेड् म्लेड्, † मेड् मेड्, i. 1, Par. To be mad.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, Caus. To repeat, MBh. 3, 10388.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष्
† म्लक्ष् म्लक्ष् (?), i. 10, Par. To cut, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानता
म्लानता म्लान + ता (vb. म्लै), Languor, Lass. 72, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानि|म्लानिः
म्लानि म्लानि, i. e. म्लै + नि, f.<BR> 1. Fading, decay.<BR> 2. Languor.<BR> 3. Weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच्
म्लुच् म्लुच्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि,<BR> 1. To set (as the sun), Bhāg. P. 5, 21, 9.<BR> 2. With acc. To surprise setting, Man. 2, 220.<BR> --With अभिनि अभि-नि, with acc. To surprise setting, Man. 2, 219.<BR> --Cf. म्रुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च्|म्लुंच्
म्लुञ्च् म्लुञ्च्, see म्रुञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छ म्लेच्छ, m.<BR> 1. A barbarian, Hit. iii. d. 62.<BR> 2. A sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेछ्|म्लेच्छ्
म्लेछ् म्लेछ्, i. 1 and 10, Par.<BR> 1. To speak barbarously, MBh. 2, 2040.<BR> 2. † To speak confusedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेट्
† म्लेट् म्लेट्, म्रेट् म्रेट्, मेट् मेट्, i. 1, Par. To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेव्
† म्लेव् म्लेव्, see मेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लै
म्लै म्लै, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry, ii. 2, e. g. म्लान्ति, MBh. 3, 15683).<BR> 1. To fade, MBh. 3, 15455.<BR> 2. To grow weary, Ragh. 11, 9 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To be faint or languid, MBh. 1, 3391.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. म्लान.<BR> 1. Withered, faded, Pañc. i. d. 88; Utt. Rāmac. 23, 12.<BR> 2. Languid, faint, Bhartṛ. 2, 82; Rājat. 5, 431.<BR> 3. Foul, dirty.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With परि परि, To fade away, to disappear, Pañc. cod. Berol. 144, a. परिम्लान,<BR> 1. Withered, Rām. 2, 59, 8.<BR> 2. Faded, Ragh. 14, 50 (Calc.).<BR> 3. Languid.<BR> 4. Diminished.<BR> 5. Soiled. n.<BR> 1. Change of countenance by grief.<BR> 2. Soil.<BR> --Cf. βλάπτω = Caus. म्लापयामि, μῶλυς, μωλυρός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लान|अम्लानः
अ- + म्लान अ- + म्लान, adj. 1. not faded. 2. clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत् यकृत्, the base of many cases is optionally यकन् यकन्, n. The liver.<BR> --Cf. Lat. jecur; ἧπαρ, ἥπατος, perhaps also A.S. lifer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्
† यक्ष् यक्ष्, i. 10, Ātm. To worship, to honour (cf. यज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष यक्ष (vb. यज्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A kind of demigod, attendant on Kuvera, Chr. 57, 21.<BR> 2. Kuvera.<BR> 3. The palace of Indra.<BR> II. f. क्षी.<BR> 1. A female यक्ष, Rām. 3, 52, 35.<BR> 2. The wife of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षदर
यक्षदर यक्ष-दर, m. The name of a district, Rājat. 5, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिणी
यक्षिणी यक्षिणी, i. e. यक्ष + इन् + ई, f. The wife of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्म|यक्ष्मः
यक्ष्म यक्ष्म, and यक्ष्मन् यक्ष्मन्, i. e. जक्ष् + मन्, m. Pulmonary [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b " target="_blank">Page0730-b + 43</a>] consumption.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयक्ष्मन्
राजयक्ष्मन् राजयक्ष्मन्, i. e. राजन्-, m. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिन्
यक्ष्मिन् यक्ष्मिन्, i. e. यक्ष्मन्, or यक्ष्म, + इन्, adj., f. इणी, and sbst. Phthisical, one who suffers from pulmonary consumption, Man. 3, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यच्छ
यच्छ यच्छ, see यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
यज् यज्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. (ved., also ii. 2, Lass. 101, 13 = Rigv. vii. 16, 5).<BR> 1. To sacrifice, Man. 11, 87; with acc., Rām. 1, 31, 5; with instr., MBh. 1, 2473.<BR> 2. To worship (the deities) by sacrifices, Man. 8, 105.<BR> 3. To worship (the deities), Bhag. 9, 23.<BR> 4. To inaugurate, Rām. 2, 56, 18.<BR> 5. To give, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 49. यजति, see s. v.<BR> --Ptcple. pres. Ātm. यजमान, m. A person who institutes a sacrifice and pays the expense of it, Pañc. 169, 8; 182, 12. Pass. इज्य, in epic poetry ptcple. pres. इज्यन्त्, MBh. 2, 1325. Pf. ptcple. इष्ट.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. याज्य, To be sacrificed. m. A sacrificer, Man. 8, 317. n. Presents for sacrificing.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Infin. यष्टम्, in epic poetry anomal. ईजितुम्, MBh. 2, 1230 (looks like an infin. of the redupl. pf.). Desider. यियक्ष, To wish to sacrifice, MBh. 2, 59.<BR> --Caus. याजय, To perform a sacrifice for another, Man. 3, 151 (also Ātm., MBh. 1, 8123).<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, To worship, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 96.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. (Caus.?), संयाज्य, n. Sacrificing, Man. 11, 59.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-संयाज्य, adj. one with whom nobody is allowed to sacrifice, Man. 9, 238.<BR> --Caus. To perform a sacrifice for another, MBh. 1, 6375.<BR> --Cf. ἅγιος, ἁγίζω, ἁγνός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाज्य
अ- + याज्य अ- + याज्य, m. one for whom it is not allowed to sacrifice, Man. 11, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत|यजतः
यजत यज् + अत, m. An officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजति|यजतिः
यजति यजति, 3. sing. pres. of यज्.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a " target="_blank">Page0731-a + 43</a>] A technical term for those sacrifices which are denoted by the word यजति (cf. जुहोति), Man. 2, 84.<BR> 2. m. A sacrifice (ŚKD.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र यज् + अत्र,<BR> I. adj. Adorable, Lass. 102, 9 = Rigv. vii. 14, 2.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa who keeps a sacrificial fire.<BR> III. n. Maintenance of a sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन|यजनं
यजन यज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sacrificing, Man. 1, 88.<BR> 2. Worshipping.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजन
देव- + यजन देव- + यजन, n. a place of offering to the deities, MBh. 5, 7354; Utt. Rāmac. 10, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजि|यजिः
यजि यज् + इ,<BR> 1. Sacrifice, Man. 10, 79.<BR> 2. A sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस् यज् + उस्, n. The यजुस्, one of the four Vedas, Man. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञ|यज्ञः
यज्ञ यज्ञ, i. e. यज् + न, m. A sacrifice, Man. 1, 22; 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञ|अयज्ञः
अ- + यज्ञ अ- + यज्ञ, m. time when the sacrifice is over, Man. 3, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषियज्ञ|ऋषियज्ञः
ऋषि- + यज्ञ ऋषि- + यज्ञ, m. inaudible muttering of prayers, Man. 4, 21; cf. 3, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयज्ञ|ग्रहयज्ञः
ग्रह- + यज्ञ ग्रह- + यज्ञ, m. a sacrifice offered to the planets, Yājñ. 1, 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपयज्ञ|जपयज्ञः
जप- + यज्ञ जप- + यज्ञ, murmuring prayers, Man. 2, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामयज्ञ
नाम(न्)- + यज्ञ नाम(न्)- + यज्ञ, m. a nominal sacrifice only (not real), Bhag. 16, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चयज्ञ
पञ्च(न्)- + यज्ञ पञ्च(न्)- + यज्ञ, m. (pl.), the five great sacraments, Man. 3, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञ|पाकयज्ञः
पाक- + यज्ञ पाक- + यज्ञ, m. a domestic sacrifice, Man. 2, 86; 11, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावयज्ञ|प्रस्तावयज्ञः
प्रस्ताव- + यज्ञ प्रस्ताव- + यज्ञ, m. sacrificelike treating of a subject, i. e. treating a subject where those who partake of it must propound and prove their views, as at sacrifices every one must give presents, Pañc. ii. d. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायज्ञ|महायज्ञः
महा- + यज्ञ महा- + यज्ञ, m. an essential ceremony, a sacrament, Man. 1, 112; 2, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियज्ञ|विधियज्ञः
विधि- + यज्ञ विधि- + यज्ञ, m. a ceremonial act of worshipping, Man. 2, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवाहस्
यज्ञवाहस् यज्ञवाहस्, i. e. यज्ञ-रह् + अस्, adj. sbst. Carrying away the sacrifices, Chr. 292, 2 = Rigv. i. 86, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसेन|यज्ञसेनः
यज्ञसेन यज्ञ-सेन (cf. सेना), m. A name of Drupada, Chr. 55, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय यज्ञिय, i. e. यज्ञ + इय,<BR> I. adj. Suitable to a sacrifice, Man. 2, 23.<BR> II. m. The द्वापर, or third युग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीतवन्त्|यज्ञोपवीतवत्
यज्ञोपवीतवन्त् यज्ञोपवीतवन्त्, i. e. यज्ञ-उपवीत + वन्त् (vb. व्ये), adj. Invested with the sacred thread, Johns. Sel. 10, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्यु|यज्युः
यज्यु यज्यु (vb. यज्), m. An assistant priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वन्
यज्वन् यज् + वन्, m. A sacrificer, Pañc. i. d. 333.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्वन्
अ- + यज्वन् अ- + यज्वन्, m. one who performs no sacrifices, irreligious, Man. 11, 14; 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्विन्
यज्विन् यज् + विन्, m. A sacrificer, Bhāg. P. 5, 14, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत् यत् (an old denomin. based on a noun derived from यम्, by an aff. with initial त्), i. 1, Ātm. (ved., and in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 3, 2722).<BR> 1. To exert one's self, Pañc. i. d. 284; Chr. 4, 16; to endeavour Man. 11, 6; with infin., MBh. 1, 6360; with dat., Bhag. 7, 3; Vikr. 5, 11 (यतिष्ये सखीप्रत्यानयनाय, I shall endeavour to bring back your friend); Pañc. i. d. 99 (नाशाय, to remove); loc., MBh. 3, 2727; gen., 1, 8085.<BR> 2. With acc. To make, to produce, Rām. 3, 49, 56.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. यतित, Endeavoured, tried, MBh. 1, 6015.<BR> II. यत्त.<BR> 1. Exerting one's self, Chr. 18, 16.<BR> 2. Watchful, Rām. 1, 32, 7.<BR> 3. Resolved.<BR> --Cf. यम्.<BR> --Caus. and i. 10, Par. यातय.<BR> 1. To prepare, to cause to be shown. Mālav. 74, 17.<BR> 2. To distress, to torture, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 31; also Ātm. with आत्मानम्, 5, 26, 18.<BR> 3. Ātm. To be used, Rām. 2, 62, 26 Gorr.<BR> 4. Ātm. To return, to requite, MBh. 3, 1383.<BR> 5. To reprehend, to despise.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To put on, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4.<BR> --With आ आ, आयत्त. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-a " target="_blank">Page0732-a + 40</a>]<BR> 1. Depending on, Man. 7, 65.<BR> 2. Docile, tractable, Hit. 54, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With अत्या अति-आ, To exert one's self excessively, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 6.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, समायत्त, Depending on, MBh. 3, 10484.<BR> --With निस् निस्, Caus., or i. 10,<BR> 1. To give back, to restore, Man. 11, 164.<BR> 2. To requite, MBh. 2, 2660.<BR> 3. To pardon, 1, 3018.<BR> --With प्रतिनिस् प्रति-निस्, Caus., or i. 10, To give back, MBh. 3, 13183.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To endeavour, Man. 7, 198.<BR> 2. To apply to, Rām. 1, 58, 21. प्रयतित, Determined, Johns. Sel. 32, 61.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus., or i. 10, To requite, MBh. 3, 14728.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus., or i. 10, To punish, MBh. 1, 3019.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्
अन्- + यत् अन्- + यत्, adj. independent, Hit. ii. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायत्त|परायत्तं
पर- + आयत्त पर- + आयत्त, adj. 1. depending on another, Pañc. i. d. 295, v. r.<BR> 2. ruled, Kathās. 18, 381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतम|यतमः
यतम यतम, यतर यतर, see यद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतस्
यतस् य + तस् (यद्), adv.<BR> 1. Whence, Rām. 3, 53, 27; from any place, Man. 11, 17; Pañc. i. d. 6 (यतस् ततस्, from wherever, Chr. 19, 5).<BR> 2. Since, Rām. 2, 7, 1.<BR> 3. As, Hit. 127, 10.<BR> 4. Because, Pañc. i. d. 402.<BR> 5. That, Vikr. d. 118.<BR> 6. For, Hit. 7, 2, M.M.; Daśak. in Chr. 194, 4.<BR> 7. Where, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 20.<BR> 8. Doubled, यतोयतस्, Whencesoever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
1. यति यति, i. e. यम् + ति (or perhaps rather a curtailed form of यतिन्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A sage of subdued passions, Hit. ii. d. 171.<BR> 2. A religious mendicant, Rām. 3, 52, 26.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. (i. e. यम् + ति), A pause (in music), Pañc. v. d. 44.<BR> 2. also यती यती, A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
2. यति य + ति (यद्), adj. As many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिन्
यतिन् यतिन्, perhaps यत + इन् (vb. यम्),<BR> I. m. One who has subdued his passions.<BR> II. f. नी, A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्किंचिद
यत्किंचिद यत्किंचिद, i. e. यद्-किम्-चिद् + अ, The name of a holy text, Man. 11, 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्न|यत्नः
यत्न यत् + न, m.<BR> 1. Effort, Pañc. ii. d. 133; 99 (यत्नात्, in spite of every effort), perseverance, energy, Man. 2, 88.<BR> 2. Will, Bhāṣāp. 4.<BR> 3. Diligence, Chr. 51, 1. यत्नेन, Carefully, Pañc. 192, 12.<BR> 4. ˚नात्, Necessarily, Pañc. 176, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्न|अयत्नः
अ- + यत्न अ- + यत्न, m. absence of hardship; instr. and abl. sing. without hardship, Man. 5, 47; easily, Pañc. 201, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयत्न
स- + यत्न स- + यत्न,<BR> I. adj. endeavouring, Hit. 20, 8, M.M.<BR> II. ˚नम्, adv. vigorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्नतस्
यत्नतस् यत्न + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. Vigorously, strenuously, Bhartṛ. 2, 5.<BR> 2. Carefully, Hit. i. d. 128, M.M.; Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नतस्
अ- + यत्नतस् अ- + यत्नतस्, adv. without hardship, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र
यत्र य + त्र (यद्), adv.<BR> 1. = loc. of यद्, Bhag. 8, 23.<BR> 2. Where, in what place.<BR> 3. Doubled, यत्रयत्र, Wherever, Hit. iii. d. 69.<BR> 4. Because, Nal. 12, 7.<BR> 5. That, Nal. 8, 17.<BR> 6. With following कुत्र, In whatever, Hit. iv. d. 84 (cf. v. r. in Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1225).<BR> 7. With following तत्र, Wherever, Chr. 8, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्रत्य
यत्रत्य यत्र + त्य, adj. Where being, whose, Mālat. 144, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथा
यथा य + था (यद्), adv.<BR> 1. In which manner, like, as, Hit. pr. 38, M.M.; Chr. 8, 25; with following तद् एरम्, As--just so, Vikr. 37, 7, 8.<BR> 2. With following तथा, In every way, Hit. ii. d. 138.<BR> 3. As truly as (a form of asseveration), Chr. 7, 16 (literally: ‘As truly I love nobody but thee, so truly I touch my head,’ i. e. ‘As I touch my head, so I [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a " target="_blank">Page0733-a + 42</a>] love nobody but thee’).<BR> 4. In order that, that, Chr. 12, 30.<BR> 5. It is used often as introduction to a direct sentence, Śāk. 7, 1, bel. ज्ञायते यथायम् आभोगस् तपोवनस्येति, ‘One perceives these are the environs of a forest of ascetics.’<BR> 6. Doubled, यथायथा, In what proportion, Man. 4, 20.<BR> 7. Very often it is the former part of comp. adv., of which the latter part has the form of an acc. sing. n.; they may be resolved by supplying ‘is,’ and generally translated by ‘according to that which is implied by the latter part,’ e. g. यथा-काम + म्, literally, ‘as is desire,’ ‘according to one's wish,’ ‘at pleasure, ad libitum,’ Chr. 56, 17. यथा-यथ + म्, adv. Properly, suitably (ŚKD.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्यथा
तद्- + यथा तद्- + यथा, adv. namely, Pañc. 3, 10; 7, 15; for, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाक्रमम्
यथाक्रमम् यथा-क्रम + म्, adv. In order, successively, Vikr. 66, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथादिशम्
यथादिशम् यथा-दिश् + अ + म्, adv. In all directions, MBh. 5, 1753.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाभीष्टदिशम्
यथाभीष्टदिशम् यथाभीष्टदिशम्, i. e. यथा-अभि-इष्ट-दिश् + अ + म् (vb. इष्), adv. In whatever direction one lists, Pañc. 63, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थाक्षर
यथार्थाक्षर यथार्थाक्षर, i. e. यथा-अर्थ-अक्षर, adj. Of which the letters imply the true sense. Vikr. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावकाशम्
यथावकाशम् यथावकाशम्, i. e. यथा-अवकाश + म्, adv. When there is any opportunity, Hit. 102, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हतस्
यथार्हतस् यथार्हतस्, i. e. यथा-अर्ह + तस्, adv. Justly, Man. 7, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावत्
यथावत् यथा + वत्, adv.<BR> 1. Exactly as it was, truly, Chr. 63, 63.<BR> 2. According to law, Man. 2, 89.<BR> 3. Accordingly, suitably, Nal. 6, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेच्छकम्
यथेच्छकम् यथेच्छकम्, i. e. यथा-इच्छ + क + म्, and यथेच्छम् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-b " target="_blank">Page0733-b + 45</a>] यथेच्छम्, i. e. यथा-इच्छ + म् (cf. इच्छा), adv. As one lists, Pañc. 192, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेष्टतस्
यथेष्टतस् यथेष्टतस्, i. e. यथा-%इष्ट (vb. इष्), + तस्, adv. According to will or inclination, Hiḍ. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्
यद् यद्,<BR> I. Relative pronoun; the base of the cases and of most derivatives is य, Who, which, what, Chr. 5, 8.<BR> II. Indefinite pronoun, Any, Chr. 23, 30.<BR> III. Doubled.<BR> 1. In proportion, as each of which, Man. 1, 20.<BR> 2. Whoever, whatever, Hit. pr. d. 34, M.M.<BR> IV. With following interr. pronoun (किम्), Whoever, whatever. Pañc. i. d. 403.<BR> V. Two and more relatives may be combined with one verb; e. g. यद् येन युज्यते, What is fitting for something, Hit. i. d. 53, M.M.; यो ऽत्ति यस्य यदा मांसम्, When one eats the flesh of some (creature), Hit. i. d. 65, M.M.<BR> VI. यद्, acc. sing. n., a particle.<BR> 1. As, since, because, Hit. pr. d. 8, M.M.; wherefore.<BR> 2. That, Hit. 41, 4, M.M.<BR> 3. It is often used as introduction to a direct sentence, Pañc. 175, 13. वदन्ति यद् अस्माकं राजा किं करिष्यति, ‘They say: what will the king do to us?’ 227, 7.<BR> 3. With following वा, Or, Rājat. 5, 441.<BR> 4. With following अपि, Although, Pañc. i. d. 7.<BR> VII. येन, instr. sing. n., adv.<BR> 1. In what manner, Man. 4, 178.<BR> 2. Because, MBh. 3, 10631.<BR> 3. As, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212.<BR> 4. That, Pañc. 84, 17.<BR> VIII. यस्मात्, abl. sing. n., adv. Because, Hit. iv. d. 88; Chr. 16, 11.<BR> --Cf. probably ὅς, ἥ, ὅ, ἵνα, εἵνε-κα (= येन); Goth. ja in jabai.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदा
यदा य + दा (यद्), adv.<BR> 1. When, at what time, Hit. 98, 18.<BR> 2. Doubled, Whenever, Bhag. 4, 7.<BR> 3. With following कदा चिद्--न, Nevermore, Hit. 58, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदि
यदि यदि (probably यद् + य, cf. आदि, आद्य), adv. If, Pañc. 229, 13; with [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a " target="_blank">Page0734-a + 43</a>] following अपि, Although, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2389; with following वा, Or, Pañc. iii. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदु|यदुः
यदु यदु, m.<BR> 1. The name of a king, Śiś. 9, 38.<BR> 2. The name of a country.<BR> 3. pl.<BR> a. The name of a people.<BR> b. The descendants of Yadu, Johns. Sel. 46, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छा
यदृच्छा यद्-ऋच्छ् + आ (see vb. ऋ), f. Following one's own will or fancy; instr. ˚छया, Pañc. iii. d. 2 (without being stopped); by itself, MBh. 12, 6676; as one lists, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 20; by chance, accidentally, Vikr. d. 10; also यदृच्च-, as former part of a comp., by itself, Bhag. 4, 22; Utt. Rāmac. 127, 11 (-संवद, accidental meeting).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्वत्
यद्वत् यद् + वत्, adv. In what manner, as, Pañc. ii. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तृ|यंतृ
यन्तृ यन्तृ, i. e. यम् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n. A person or thing that restrains.<BR> II. m. A charioteer, Man. 2, 88.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहयन्तृ
देह- + यन्तृ देह- + यन्तृ, m. a charioteer, i. e. subduer, of (his) body, i. e. of his senses, Lass. 53, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र्|यंत्र्
यन्त्र् यन्त्र्, † i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from यन्त्र), Par., and † i. 1, Par. To restrain. यन्त्रित,<BR> 1. Checked, restrained, Rām. 1, 40, 17.<BR> 2. Bound, fettered, MBh. 3, 33.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, उपयन्त्रित, Solicited, Man. 11, 177.<BR> --With नि नि, नियन्त्रित,<BR> 1. Fastened, Utt. Rāmac. 106, 1.<BR> 2. Checked.<BR> 3. Squeezed, Śāk. 9, 20 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 4. Ruled, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 17.<BR> 5. Fettered, Pañc. 142, 14.<BR> 6. Embanked, Rājat. 5, 103.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संगन्त्रिट, Stopped, Śāk. 100, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन्त्रित|अयंत्रित|अयन्त्रितः
अ- + यन्त्रित अ- + यन्त्रित, adj. one who does not govern his passions, Man. 2, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयन्त्रित
सु- + यन्त्रित सु- + यन्त्रित, adj. 1. well governed. 2. one who governs his passions completely, Man. 2, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र यन्त्र, i. e. यम् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. An engine or machine in general, any implement, or apparatus, Man. 7, 75; Johns. Sel. 39, 30; Rājat. 5, 104.<BR> 2. A thong, Man. 8, 292.<BR> 3. A sort of vessel, Hit. iii. d. 52.<BR> 4. A mystical diagram, Rāmatap. Up. 1, 13.<BR> 5. Restraining.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डयन्त्र
कोदण्ड- + यन्त्र कोदण्ड- + यन्त्र, n. a bow, Rājat. 5, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटयन्त्र|कूटयंत्र|कूटयन्त्रं
कूट- + यन्त्र कूट- + यन्त्र, n. a trap for deer, birds, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहयन्त्र|गृहयंत्र
गृह- + यन्त्र गृह- + यन्त्र, n. an apparatus for raising flags on a house, Kumāras. 6, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिकायन्त्र
घटिका- + यन्त्र घटिका- + यन्त्र (thus to be corrected, Pañc. 212, 4), and घटी-, n. the rope and bucket of a well, Mārk. P. 12, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्र|जलयंत्र
जल- + यन्त्र जल- + यन्त्र, n. a machine for raising water, Hariv. 8425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालयन्त्र|तालयंत्र
ताल- + यन्त्र ताल- + यन्त्र, n. 1. a small pair of pincers, Suśr. 1, 23, 16. 2. a lock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलयन्त्र|तैलयंत्र
तैल- + यन्त्र तैल- + यन्त्र, n. an oil mill, Bhāg. P. 5, 21, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोययन्त्र|तोययंत्र
तोय- + यन्त्र तोय- + यन्त्र, n. a clepsydra, Sūryas. 13, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारायन्त्र|धारायंत्र
धारा- + यन्त्र धारा- + यन्त्र, n. a water-spout, Prab. 79, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजयन्त्र|ध्वजयंत्र
ध्वज- + यन्त्र ध्वज- + यन्त्र, n. an apparatus for planting the staff of a standard, Rām. 4, 13, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीयन्त्र
नाडी- + यन्त्र नाडी- + यन्त्र, n. any tubelike apparatus, Suśr. 1, 23, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायन्त्र
महा- + यन्त्र महा- + यन्त्र, n. any great mechanical work, Man. 11, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयन्त्र
सु- + यन्त्र सु- + यन्त्र, adj. with machines, Hit. iii. d. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रयन्त्र|सूत्रयंत्र|सूत्रयन्त्रं
सूत्र- + यन्त्र सूत्र- + यन्त्र, n. 1. a loom. 2. a shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीयन्त्र|स्त्रीयंत्र
स्त्री- + यन्त्र स्त्री- + यन्त्र, n. a woman who works like an artificial machine, Pañc. i. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमायायन्त्र
स्व-माया- + यन्त्र स्व-माया- + यन्त्र, adj. formed by his art, Kathās. 29, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रक|यंत्रक|यन्त्रकं|यंत्रकः|यन्त्रकः
यन्त्रक<BR> 1. यन्त्र् + अन, m. An artisan, Rām. 2, 80, 1.<BR> 2. यन्त्र + क, n. A lathe.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्रक
जल- + यन्त्रक जल- + यन्त्रक, n. an engine, Hariv. 8432.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रण|यंत्रण|यंत्रणं|यन्त्रणं
यन्त्रण यन्त्रण, i. e. यन्त्र् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Binding.<BR> 2. Restraining.<BR> 3. Confining.<BR> II. f. णा.<BR> 1. Torturing, pain (ŚKD.), Mālav. 46, 3.<BR> 2. A means of fastening, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 5; Pañc. rec. orn. MS. Berol. 81, a, and Weber, Ind. St. iii. 372, 4, below (read यन्त्रणया instead of यन्त्रया).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यन्त्रण|निर्यंत्रण|निर्यन्त्रणं|निर्य्यन्त्रण
निर्यन्त्रण निर्यन्त्रण, i. e. निस्-, adj. unrestrained, unobstructed, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0735-a " target="_blank">Page0735-a + 43</a>] Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 408. ˚नम्, adv., Ṛt. 1, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखयन्त्रण|मुखयंत्रण|मुखयन्त्रणं
मुख- + यन्त्रण मुख- + यन्त्रण, n. the bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यभ्
† यभ् यभ्, जभ् जभ्, जम्भ् जम्भ्, i. 1, Par. To lie with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्
यम् यम् (akin to दम्), i. 1, यच्छ, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 5704).<BR> 1. To tame, to restrain.<BR> 2. To govern (as horses), MBh. 3, 751.<BR> 3. To give, Man. 2, 55.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. यत, Restrained, governed, Hit. iii. d. 130; in epic poetry also यत्त, MBh. 2, 2011 (maintained by the metre).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, या̆मय.<BR> 1. To restrain.<BR> 2. † To give food.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. यमित, Restrained, Śāk. d. 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. not pared (as nails), Megh. 89.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To give, Chr. 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To stop, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 119.<BR> 2. To suppress, Man. 11, 149.<BR> 3. To draw, to bend (as a bow), Rām. 3, 50, 9; Johns. Sel. 50, 101.<BR> 4. Ātm. To extend, Śāk. 73, 4, C.<BR> 5. Ātm. To possess, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 46. आयत, Long, Pañc. ii. 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> पूर्ण-आयत, adj. completely drawn (as a bow), Hariv. 13413.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अन्-आयम्य, Not to be drawn, unpliant, MBh. 1, 6953.<BR> --With निरा निस्-आ, निरायत, Contracted, Śāk. d. 8.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ,<BR> 1. Ātm. To exert one's power, MBh. 3, 12740.<BR> 2. To fight, Mṛcch. 202, 7; Ātm., Bhaṭṭ. 6, 119.<BR> 3. To open wide one's eyes, Johns. Sel. 47, 76. व्यायत, Long.<BR> 2. Excessive.<BR> 3. Busy.<BR> 4. Hard, firm.<BR> --Caus. यामय, To use exercise, Man. 7, 216.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To rise, Hit. 81, 4 (with infin., in order to kill).<BR> 2. To lift up, Man. 4, 64.<BR> 3. To brandish, Man. 5, 58.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0735-b " target="_blank">Page0735-b + 44</a>] To govern (as horses), Chr. 36, 19.<BR> 5. To offer, MBh. 1, 1853.<BR> 6. To endeavour, MBh. 2, 2357.<BR> 7. To study. उद्यत,<BR> 1. Raised, Chr. 3, 1.<BR> 2. Ready, Hit. 41, 4, M.M.<BR> 3. Intending, Rājat. 5, 237.<BR> 4. Trained.<BR> 5. Active.<BR> --Comp.<BR> समर-, adj. ready for the combat.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्,<BR> 1. To raise, Mṛcch. 171, 20.<BR> 2. To offer, Man. 4, 247. अभ्युद्यत,<BR> 1. Lifted up, Mṛcch. 327, 5 (Calc.).<BR> 2. Rising, proceeding to act, Man. 4, 302.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्,<BR> 1. To lift up. प्रोद्यत, lifted, Pañc. 105, 19.<BR> 2. To cast, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 60.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To incite, to urge (as horses), MBh. 3, 756.<BR> 2. To lift up, 1, 6278.<BR> 3. To endeavour, Rām. 1, 14, 8. समुद्यत, Ready.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. Ātm. To marry, Man. 3, 11 (Par., Man. 11, 172, v. r., see Lois.).<BR> 2. To seize, Ātm., Bhaṭṭ. 1, 16; with भयम्, To fear, Bhaṭṭ. 7, 101.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To stop, to govern, MBh. 4, 1953.<BR> 2. To direct, Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR> 3. To curb, to restrain, Rām. 2, 122, 22, to hold in (the breath), Vikr. d. 1.<BR> 4. To punish, Man. 9, 213.<BR> 5. To bind, Rām. 2, 87, 23.<BR> 6. To attain, Man. 2, 93.<BR> 7. To assume, Man. 10, 93.<BR> 8. To conceal, Man. 10, 59. नियत,<BR> 1. Subdued, self-governed.<BR> 2. Submissive, Sāv. 4, 11.<BR> 3. Abstemious, Chr. 50, 9.<BR> 4. Attentive.<BR> 5. Fixed, Megh. 44.<BR> 6. Certain, destined, Hit. i. d. 43, M.M.; right, i. d. 202, M.M.<BR> 7. Constant, Man. 5, 44.<BR> 8. Inevitable, Man. 8, 419; Utt. Rāmac. 52, 12. ˚तम्, adv.<BR> 1. Forcibly, Ṛt. 6, 20.<BR> 2. Inevitably, Bhartṛ. 2, 41.<BR> 3. Constantly, always.<BR> 4. Surely, Pañc. ii. d. 199. n. Elementary matter.<BR> --Caus. To restrain, Śāk. 92, 19, Chezy. नियमित,<BR> 1. Restrained.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-a " target="_blank">Page0736-a + 42</a>] Confined, Bhartṛ. 2, 93.<BR> 3. Prescribed.<BR> 4. Governed.<BR> --With प्रतिनि प्रति-नि, प्रतिनियत, Determined proportionally (in proportion to the acts done in a preceding existence), Bhartṛ. 2, 92; Daśak. in Chr. 187, 22.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To punish, Man. 9, 249.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To subdue, Man. 2, 93.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To offer, to deliver, Hit. 65, 15; to give, Man. 3, 223; Chr. 288, 15 = Rigv. i. 48, 15 (यच्छतात्, imperat. 2. sing.).<BR> 2. To give in marriage, Man. 9, 89.<BR> 3. To restore, Man. 8, 181; Pañc. 88, 14.<BR> 4. To pay, Man. 8, 158. प्रयत, Well restrained, keeping his organs controlled, Man. 2, 222.<BR> 2. Submissive, Nal. 25, 2.<BR> 3. Careful, Man. 2, 183; intent on his devotion, 11, 158; zealous, Vikr. d. 43.<BR> 4. Pure, Man. 5, 145.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. impure, Man. 5, 142.<BR> --With प्रतिप्र प्रति-प्र, To restore, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 14.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To give, Man. 11, 19.<BR> 2. To give in marriage, MBh. 3, 16661 (= Sāv. 2, 4, v. r. erroneous).<BR> --With वि वि, To give, Chr. 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12 (यन्त, 2. pl. imperat. aor. 1.).<BR> --With सम्<BR> 1. To constrain, Man. 8, 365.<BR> 2. To bind, MBh. 3, 1694.<BR> 3. To subdue, Man. 12, 11.<BR> 4. To govern (as horses), MBh. 3, 12110. संयत, Restrained, subdued, Nal. 1, 4; fettered.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-संयत, adj. well composed, Man. 2, 193 (v. r.).<BR> --Cf. ἥμερος, ζημία, ἡνία, ὄμνυμι; Lat. jejunus, and probably jentare, fræna; Goth. aiths; A.S. adh, adhum; O.H.G. eidum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यत|वाग्यतः
वाग्यत वाग्यत, i. e. वाच्-, adj. silent, taciturn, Man. 3, 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम यम् + अ,<BR> I. adj. sbst. Twin, one of a pair. du. The twins, Draup. 6, 29.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Restraining.<BR> 2. Taming of passion, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 14. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b " target="_blank">Page0736-b + 39</a>]<BR> 3. Moral duty, Man. 4, 204.<BR> 4. Penance.<BR> 5. A festival.<BR> 6. Yama, the judge of the deceased ones, ruler of the infernal regions, Rām. 2, 54, 28; god of death, Pañc. 247, 8.<BR> 7. A crow.<BR> 8. A name of the planet Saturn.<BR> III. f. मी, The Yamunā.<BR> IV. n. A pair.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तकयम
काल-अन्त + क- + यम काल-अन्त + क- + यम, m. Yama, as all-destroying time, Rām. 3, 32, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमक|यमकं|यमकः
यमक यम + क,<BR> I. m. A religious observance.<BR> II. n. A poetical refinement, a species of alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमज|यमजः
यमज यम + ज, m. Twin, Draup. 3, 17; Utt. Rāmac. 112, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमत्व
यमत्व यम + त्व, n. The name Yama, Sāv. 5, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमन|यमनं|यमनः
यमन यम् + अन,<BR> I. m. Yama.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Restraining, Rājat. 5, 114.<BR> 2. Binding.<BR> 3. Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमल|यमलं|यमलः
यमल यम + ल,<BR> I. n. A pair.<BR> II. f. ली, A sort of dress, a body and petticoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुना
यमुना यम् + उना (or rather यम् + वन् + अ), f. The name of a river, Chr. 46, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमेरुका
यमेरुका यम् + एरुका, f. A metal plate or drum used to strike the hours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययाति|ययातिः
ययाति ययाति, m. The name of a king, Śāk. d. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययि|ययिः
ययि ययि (vb. या, red.), A cloud Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 87, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययिन्
ययिन् (vb. या, red., + इन्), ययिन्, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययी
ययी ययी (cf. ययि), m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययु|ययुः
ययु ययु (vb. या, red., + उ), m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. A horse fit for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यर्हि
यर्हि यर्हि, probably यत्र-हि, adv. When.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव यव, m.<BR> 1. Barley, Hordeum hexastichon, Pañc. 224, 4.<BR> 2. The measure of a barleycorn, equal to six mustard seeds.<BR> 3. A natural line across the thumb, supposed to indicate good fortune.<BR> 4. Velocity (vb. जू).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ζεά, ζειά, εἴα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकयव|काकयवः
काक- + यव काक- + यव, m. barren corn, Pañc. ii. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियव
त्रि- + यव त्रि- + यव, adj. weighing three barleycorns, Man. 8, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक|यवकः
यवक यव + क, m. Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्य|यवक्यं
यवक्य यवक्य, i. e. यवक + य, adj. Fit for producing barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवज|यवजः
यवज यव-ज, m. Saltpetre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवन|यवनः
यवन यवन,<BR> I. adj. Swift (vb. जू).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of a country.<BR> 2. The name of a people (originally Greek, Ionian), Man. 10, 44.<BR> 3. (vb. जू), Velocity.<BR> 4. A swift horse.<BR> III. f. नी, A Yavana woman, Vikr. 77, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयवन|कालयवनः
काल- + यवन काल- + यवन, m. the name of a prince of the Yavanas, Hariv. 1961.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनिका
यवनिका यवनिका, i. e. यवन + क, f. A curtain, Bhartṛ. 3, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनेष्ट|यवनेष्टं|यवनेष्टः
यवनेष्ट यवनेष्ट, i. e. यवन-इष्ट (vb. इष्), n. Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमय|यवमयः
यवमय यव + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of or from barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवस|यवसं
यवस यव + स, m. Pasture grass, Pañc. 182, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवागू
यवागू यवागू (from यव, and गु for गो), f. Rice-gruel, Man. 11, 106; 6, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवान|यवानः
यवान यवान (vb. जू), adj. Swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठ|यविष्ठः
यविष्ठ यविष्ठ, यवीयंस् यवीयंस्, see युवन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
यव्य यव्य, i. e. यव + य,<BR> I. adj. Fit for producing barley.<BR> II. m. A month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्
यशस् यशस् (for original दशस् = Lat. decus, from a lost vb. दश्, see below),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Glory, Vikr. 11, 17; fame, Pañc. iii. d. 116 (pl.).<BR> 2. Splendour.<BR> 3. Praise.<BR> II. adj. Renowned, resplendent, Chr. 294, 8 = Rigv. i. 92, 8; superl. यशस्तम, Lass. 101, 9 = Rigv. vii. 16, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. decere, docere; δοκέω, δόξω, δόγμα, δοκεύω, διδάσκω, δάκτυλος; probably A.S. ta, tah; O.H.G. zêha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्
अ- + यशस् अ- + यशस्, n. disgrace, Pañc. ii. d. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियशस्
अति- + यशस् अति- + यशस्, adj. much renowned; archaic acc. (cf. स्रोतस् and ved. forms) -यशाम्, for यशसम्, Nal. 8, 4 (Böhtl., Bopp. v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अप- + यशस् अप- + यशस्, n. disgrace, Bhartṛ. 2, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुयशस्
पृथु- + यशस् पृथु- + यशस्,<BR> I. adj. widely renowned, MBh. 7, 2783.<BR> II. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्
महा- + यशस् महा- + यशस्, adj. illustrious, Rām. 3, 55, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयशस्
सु- + यशस् सु- + यशस्, adj. renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्कर|यशस्करः
यशस्कर यशस्-कर,<BR> I. adj., f. री, Rendering famous, Hit. iii. d. 122.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 472.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्य
यशस्य यशस् + य, adj. Bringing reputation, Man. 3, 106.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्य
अ- + यशस्य अ- + यशस्य, adj. bringing disgrace, Rām. 5, 91, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्वन्त्|यशस्वत्
यशस्वन्त् यशस् + वन्त्, adj., f. वाति, and युअशस्विन् यशस् + विन्, adj., f. विनी, Famous, Chr. 21, 6 (विन्); Lass. 31, 13 (विन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि यष्टि,<BR> I. m. and f. (and यष्टी यष्टी, f.),<BR> 1. A staff, a stick, Pañc. 105, 19; 261, 12; Śiś. 9, 39; a perch, Vikr. d. 43; a stem, d. 44; support, Sāv. 5, 89.<BR> 2. A palisade, Man. 9, 285.<BR> 3. A club, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 4.<BR> 4. A string, Vikr. d. 51.<BR> 5. A necklace.<BR> 6. Any creeping plant, Utt. Rāmac. 81, 5.<BR> 7. Liquorice.<BR> 8. A shrub, Siponanthus indica.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A flagstaff.<BR> 2. The arm and forearm.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुयष्टि|केतुयष्टिः
केतु- + यष्टि केतु- + यष्टि, m. a flag-staff. Ragh. 12, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रयष्टि|गात्रयष्टिः
गात्र- + यष्टि गात्र- + यष्टि, m. a delicate body; when latter part of comp. adj., the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a " target="_blank">Page0738-a + 43</a>] fem. ends in t, Ṛt. 6, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलायष्टि|तुलायष्टिः
तुला- + यष्टि तुला- + यष्टि, the beam of a balance, Pañc. i. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजयष्टि|ध्वजयष्टिः
ध्वज- + यष्टि ध्वज- + यष्टि, f. a flag-staff, Rām. 5, 12, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयष्टि|भारयष्टिः
भार- + यष्टि भार- + यष्टि, f. a yoke or pole for carrying burthens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासयष्टि|वासयष्टिः
वास- + यष्टि वास- + यष्टि, f. a column for a bird to perch on, Megh. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयष्टि|हारयष्टिः
हार- + यष्टि हार- + यष्टि, f. a necklace, Ṛt. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिक|यष्टिकः
यष्टिक यष्टि + क,<BR> I. m. A bird, the lapwing.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. A staff, a club.<BR> 2. A necklace.<BR> 3. A pond.<BR> 4. Liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टुकाम
यष्टुकाम यष्टुकाम, i. e. यष्टुम् (infin. of यज्), -काम, adj. Desiring to sacrifice, Rām. 1, 57, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टृ
यष्टृ यष्टृ, i. e. यज् + तृ, m. A sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्
यस् यस् (akin to यम्, for यंस्), i. 4, and † 1, Par. To make strenuous and persevering exertion, to endeavour.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ,<BR> 1. To endeavour, Rām. 2, 14, 62.<BR> 2. To be afflicted, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 69. आयस्त,<BR> 1. Pained, distressed, Rām. 2, 20, 8.<BR> 2. Vexed, angry.<BR> 3. Managed with difficulty.<BR> 4. Hurt.<BR> 5. Thrown.<BR> 6. Sharpened.<BR> 7. Strained, Pañc. v. d. 28.<BR> --Caus. To torment, Mālav. 32, 7 (Prākṛ.).<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अन्-आयासित, Not practised, Pañc. i. d. 429 (rather अन्-आयास + इत).<BR> --With प्र प्र, To endeavour, Naiṣ. 1, 125. प्रयस्त. Seasoned, dressed with condiments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
या या (akin to इ), ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 1, 33, 6).<BR> 1. To go, Rām. 2, 72, 27; imperat. यातु, Let it go, enough, Hit. 77, 9, M.M.; no matter, Hit. 128, 2.<BR> 2. To go to (with acc.), MBh. 3, 2828; (with dat.), Hit. i. d. 153; (with two acc.), Rām. 3, 55, 48 (सर्वाणि शरनं यामि, All those I approach, or I implore, for help).<BR> 3. To undergo, to obtain, to get, especially with abstract nouns; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-b " target="_blank">Page0738-b + 41</a>] e. g. क्षयम्, To perish, MBh. 3, 8840; रेणु-पदवीम्, To become dust, Vikr. d. 4; संपर्कम्, To be united, Vikr. d. 13; प्रसादम्, To become propitious, inclined to somebody, Pañc. 67, 8; द्वेष्यताम्, To grow odious, Pañc. i. d. 317; विलयम्, To be dissolved, Pañc. i. d. 425.<BR> 4. To pass away, Pañc. iii. d. 97; Bhaṭṭ. 7, 89.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. यात.<BR> 1. Gone, Vikr. d. 72; went.<BR> 2. Escaped, Hit. ii. d. 144.<BR> 3. Obtained, got. n. Driving an elephant with a goad. Desider यियास, To desire to go, MBh. 3, 47.<BR> --Caus. यापय,<BR> 1. To remove, Ragh. 9, 27.<BR> 2. To pass away (time), Pañc. 183, 24.<BR> 3. To induce, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 4 (with dat. in the sense of an infin. ‘Induced to abandon’).<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To pass, Rām. 2, 49, 3.<BR> --With समति सम्-अति, To pass away, Rām. 1, 19, 1.<BR> --With अधि अधि, To escape, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 90.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To follow, Man. 8, 17.<BR> 2. To cut in succession, MBh. 4, 1727. अनुयात,<BR> 1. Followed, accompanied, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 15.<BR> 2. Practised.<BR> --With समनु To follow, MBh. 2, 1608.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To go away, Hit. iv. d. 81; MBh. 3, 15214; Chr. 57, 31 (I propose to read पुरान्, i. e. पुरात्).<BR> 2. To run away, Draup. 8, 35. अपयात, Fallen from, Chr. 35, 3.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप,<BR> 1. To go away, MBh. 3, 789.<BR> 2. To desist from (abl.), Chr. 42, 13.<BR> 3. To pass away, Rām. 2, 49, 2.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To go near (acc.), Rām. 1, 25, 10. अभियात, Approaching, Indr. 2, 8.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To go near at the same time, MBh. 1, 1338.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To approach, Vikr. d. 121, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0739-a " target="_blank">Page0739-a + 41</a>] Pañc. i. d. 213.<BR> 2. To come, Pañc. iii. d. 97; Rājat. 5, 31.<BR> 3. With and without पुनर्, To return, Rām. 1, 1, 75; Chr. 5, 23.<BR> 4. To attain, Lass. 21, 2.<BR> 5. To undergo, to obtain, Rājat. 5, 376; with क्षयम्, To be ruined, Pañc. v. d. 52; with संकोचम्, To be diminished, Pañc. i. d. 105; with हेतुताम्, To become the cause, Hit. i. d. 29, M.M.; with तोषम्, To be satisfied, Hit. ii. d. 149. आयात, Come. n. Excess, Kir. 5, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ, To approach, MBh. 3, 246.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To approach, MBh. 3, 738.<BR> 2. To undergo, to obtain, Rājat. 5, 126. उपायात, n. Arrival, Draup. 4, 24.<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ, To approach, MBh. 4, 280.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To go towards, MBh. 4, 1698.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To meet with, Pañc. 46, 6; 245, 2 (द्वौ पन्थानौ समायातौ, They came to two roads).<BR> 2. To approach, Pañc. 23, 10; Chr. 34, 6.<BR> 3. To obtain, Pañc. i. d. 104.<BR> 4. To come, Hit. 83, 2; to arrive, Hit. 29, 6, M.M.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To rise, Gīt. 4, 19.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, To go to meet (a guest), Rām. 1, 20, 8. प्रत्युद्यात, Saluted, welcomed, Megh. 23.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To go to (acc.), Rām. 2, 50, 15.<BR> 2. To approach, Pañc. i. d. 44; Ragh. 9, 24 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To undergo, to obtain, Man. 12, 69; with प्रीतिम्, To grow agreeable, Pañc. i. d. 317.<BR> 4. To befall, Pañc. iii. d. 244.<BR> --With ओप आ-उप, To come near to (acc.), Lass. 102, 11 = Rigv. vii. 14, 3.<BR> --With उपोप उप-उप, To approach gradually, MBh. 3, 12358. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0739-b " target="_blank">Page0739-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, To return, MBh. 1, 8393.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To go, MBh. 3, 1912.<BR> --With प्रणि प्र-नि, To proceed, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 100.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To go out, or out of (abl.), Rām. 2, 76, 19.<BR> --With अभिनिस् अभि-निस्, To go out, to depart, Rājat. 5, 218.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To go round, to circumambulate (as a token of respect), MBh. 1, 7205.<BR> 2. To protect, Chr. 297, 13 (corr. याथः) = Rigv. i. 112, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To go forth, Hit. 84, 7 (कः प्र याट, Who shall go forth?); to proceed, MBh. 3, 2848.<BR> 2. To proceed to (acc.), MBh. 3, 240.<BR> 3. To rise to (acc.) Bhartṛ. 2, 91.<BR> 4. To attain, Pañc. i. d. 186; to obtain, Pañc. iii. d. 262; with असाध्यताम् (i. e. अ-साध् + य + ता), To become unconquerable, Pañc. i. d. 245; with पराभवम्, To be spoiled, Pañc. i. d. 424.<BR> 5. To proceed from, Rājat. 5, 3745<BR> 6. To depart, Hit. i. d. 189, M.M.; Daśak. iii. in Chr. 187, 15.<BR> 7. To pass away, Kathās. 4, 23.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pres. अ-प्रयान्त्, adj. Not able to move away, Chr. 31, 16. प्रयात,<BR> 1. Gone away.<BR> 2. Gone.<BR> 3. Deceased. m.<BR> 1. A lazy fellow.<BR> 2. A name of Bhṛgu. Desider. To desire to proceed, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 25.<BR> --Caus. प्रयापित, Driven away.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To assail, MBh. 4, 1381.<BR> --With प्रतिप्र प्रति-प्र, To return, MBh. 3, 10287.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To proceed together, MBh. 1, 4645.<BR> 2. To depart to (acc.), MBh. 3, 15082.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To return, Rām. 1, 66, 6.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To pervade (the heavens), and come, Chr. 287, 7 = Rigv. i. 48, 7.<BR> 2. To pierce, to destroy, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 86, 10. वियात, Ill-behaved, impudent.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a " target="_blank">Page0740-a + 39</a>] सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To enter, MBh. 3, 6013.<BR> 2. To come, Lass. 34, 4.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्,<BR> 1. To visit in succession, or one by one, MBh. 3, 10094.<BR> 2. To follow, Rām. 2, 79, 13.<BR> --Cf. perhaps some forms of इ; e. g. ἰέναι; Lat. Janus, janua.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमयायात
क्रम- + आयात क्रम- + आयात, adj. descended from a succession, i. e. a long line of princes, Pañc. i. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याग|यागः
याग याग, i. e. यज् + अ, m. A sacrifice, Bhāṣāp. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्
याच् याच् (akin to या), i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To ask, Vikr. d. 41; to solicit, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 1. With the acc. of the object and of the person, Man. 3, 258; also with the abl. of the person, MBh. 1, 6197.<BR> 2. To offer, to tender.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. याचित.<BR> 1. Importuned, Yājñ. 2, 238.<BR> 2. Requisite, necessary, Pañc. 182, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. याचय, To cause to be asked, Pañc. 25, 15; to be invited, Vikr. 37, 8.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To ask, to beg; with two acc., MBh. 3, 10586.<BR> --With उप उप, उपयाचित,<BR> 1. Requested.<BR> 2. Offered to the deities to render them propitious. n. A vow, Pañc. ii. d. 50; a demand, Kathās. 13, 166.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To beg, to solicit, Chr. 26, 65; with two acc., MBh. 3, 9950.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, The same, 3, 8696.<BR> --With सम् सम्, The same, 3, 8837.<BR> --Cf. αἰτέω, and perhaps ζητέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचित|अयाचितं|अयाचितः
अ- + याचित अ- + याचित, adj. unasked, Man. 4, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियाचित
अति- + याचित अति- + याचित, adj. asked too often, too much assailed with begging, Hit. ii. d. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचक|याचकः
याचक याच् + अक, adj. Asking, a beggar, Pañc. ii. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनक|याचनकः
याचनक याच् + अन + क, adj. Begging importunately, Man. 3, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचना
याचना याच् + अना, Caus., f. Asking, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b " target="_blank">Page0740-b + 39</a>] soliciting, Ragh. 11, 78 (Calc. 77, where the Sch. takes it as n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितक|याचितकं
याचितक याचित + क (vb. याच्), n. A borrowed thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचिष्णुता
याचिष्णुता याच् + इष्णु + ता, f. Habit of soliciting favours, Man. 12, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्ञा
याच्ञा याच्ञा, i. e. याच् + न, f. Begging, Hit. i. d. 97, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज|याजः
याज याज, i. e. यज् + अ, m. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजक|याजकः
याजक याजक, i. e. यज् + अक, m.<BR> 1. A sacrificer, Man. 3, 164.<BR> 2. A royal elephant.<BR> 3. A furious elephant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजक|ग्रामयाजकः
ग्राम- + याजक ग्राम- + याजक, m. one who sacrifices for a village, MBh. 3, 13355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रग्रामयाजक
नक्षत्र-ग्राम- + याजक नक्षत्र-ग्राम- + याजक, adj. one who offers sacrifices to the asterims, MBh. 12, 2874.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजन|याजनं
याजन याजन, i. e. यज्, Caus., + अन, n. Conducting a sacrifice, sacrificing, Man. 3, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजि|याजिः
याजि याजि, i. e. यज् + इ, m. An institutor of sacrifices, Man. 4, 33; 3, 148; anomal. du. याज्यौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजिन्
याजिन् याजिन्, i. e. यज् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Sacrificing.<BR> 2. Worshipping, Bhag. 9, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयाजिन्
आत्म(न्)- + याजिन् आत्म(न्)- + याजिन्, adj. sacrificing one's self, Man. 12, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजिन्
ग्राम- + याजिन् ग्राम- + याजिन्, m. a common sacrificer, Man. 4, 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयाजिन्
सोम- + याजिन् सोम- + याजिन्, m. a sacrificer who drinks the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्याजिन्
हविस्- + याजिन् हविस्- + याजिन्, m. a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्क्य|याज्ञवल्क्यः
याज्ञवल्क्य याज्ञवल्क्य, m. The name of a saint, Utt. Rāmac. 98, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञसेनी
याज्ञसेनी याज्ञसेनी, i. e. यज्ञासेन + अ + ई. f. A name of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक|याज्ञिकः
याज्ञिक याज्ञिक, i. e. यज्ञ + इक, m.<BR> 1. The institutor of a sacrifice.<BR> 2. Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक्य|याज्ञिक्यं
याज्ञिक्य याज्ञिक्य, i. e. याज्ञिक + य, n. A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातना
यातना यातना, i. e. यत्, Caus., + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a " target="_blank">Page0741-a + 44</a>] f.<BR> 1. Pain, torment, Man. 6, 61; Bhāg. P. 7, 1, 41.<BR> 2. Punishment.<BR> 3. Requital, Pañc. 188, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
यातु या + तु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A traveller.<BR> 2. Time.<BR> II. n. A Rākṣasa, or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृ
यातृ यातृ,<BR> I. i. e. या + तृ, m. A driver, Man. 8, 290.<BR> II. Perhaps यम् + तृ, f. A husband's brother's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रा
यात्रा या + त्रा, f.<BR> 1. Going, travelling.<BR> 2. The march of an assailing force, an expedition, Man. 7, 160; 207; Pañc. iii. d. 35.<BR> 3. Going on pilgrimage.<BR> 4. The procession of idols, Hit. i. d. 113, M.M.<BR> 5. A sort of dramatic entertainment.<BR> 6. Passing away time.<BR> 7. Practice, usage, conduct, Man. 9, 25; intercourse, Man. 11, 184.<BR> 8. An expedient, support of life, Man. 4, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थयात्रा
तीर्थ- + यात्रा तीर्थ- + यात्रा, f. pilgrimage to holy places, Pañc. 117, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयात्रा
देव- + यात्रा देव- + यात्रा, f. 1. the procession of idols, Mālav. 69, 13. 2. a sacred festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहयात्रा
देह- + यात्रा देह- + यात्रा, f. 1. death. 2. support of life, Bhāg. P. 4, 23, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयात्रा
प्राण- + यात्रा प्राण- + यात्रा, f. support of life, Pañc. 52, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकयात्रा
लोक- + यात्रा लोक- + यात्रा, f. 1. the way of the world, Mālav. 68, 17. 2. worldly affairs, domestic affairs, Man. 9, 27. 3. traffic, intercourse, Hit. i. d. 104, M.M. 4. the life of the world, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रिक|यात्रिकः
यात्रिक यात्रिक, i. e. यात्रा + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to a march or an enterprise, Man. 7, 184.<BR> 2. Necessary for supporting life, Man. 6, 27.<BR> 3. Usual.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A traveller.<BR> 2. A pilgrim.<BR> III. n. Provision for a march.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धयात्रिक|सिद्धयात्रिकः
सिद्ध- + यात्रिक सिद्ध- + यात्रिक, m. a pilgrim who seeks for the territory of the Siddhas, Pañc. 240, 16; cf. 242, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथातथ्य|याथातथ्यं
याथातथ्य याथातथ्य, i. e. यथा-तथम् (see तथा), + य, n. Truth, Hit. iv. d. 102 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2676).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथात्म्य
याथात्म्य याथात्म्य, i. e. यथा-आत्मन् + य, n. Character, Ragh. 10, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादव|यादवः
यादव यादव, i. e. यदु + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A Yādava, or descendant of Yadu.<BR> 2. Kṛṣṇa.<BR> II. f. वी, Durgā.<BR> III. n. A stock of cattle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यादव
निर्यादव निर्य्˚, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. वा, free from Yādavas, Hariv. 4558.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादस्
यादस् यादस्, n. Any aquatic animal. Kir. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृश्
यादृश् यादृश्, and यादृश् यादृश, i. e. यद्-द्रिश् and -दृश् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Which like, (क़ुअलिस्), Pañc. ii. d. 190.<BR> 2. Which, what, Bhag. 13, 3 (दृश्); Man. 1, 42; Pañc. i. d. 236; Hit. i. d. 205, M.M.<BR> 3. With following तादृश, Whoever, whatever, Pañc. i. d. 435.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान|यानं|यानः
यान यान, i. e. या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going, Man. 4, 72; moving, Pañc. iii. d. 248.<BR> 2. Marching, generally comprising as well: Retreating before an enemy (Pañc. iii. d. 34; cf. 35, and p. 153, 6, 7), as: Attacking an enemy (Pañc. iii. d. 35; Man. 7, 160).<BR> 3. Any vehicle or form of conveyance, a carriage, Man. 2, 202.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशयान
आकाश- + यान आकाश- + यान, n. moving through the sky, Vikr. 22, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रयान
उष्ट्र- + यान उष्ट्र- + यान, n. a vehicle drawn by camels, Man. 11, 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरयान
खर- + यान खर- + यान, n. a vehicle drawn by asses, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयान
गो- + यान गो- + यान, n. a carriage drawn by oxen, Man. 11, 174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयान
जल- + यान जल- + यान, n. a boat, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयान|देवयानं
देव- + यान देव- + यान,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, leading to the gods, MBh. 3, 11000.<BR> II. n. 1. the road leading to the gods, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 55. 2. the vehicle of a god.<BR> III. f. नी, the daughter of Śukra, MBh. 1, 3159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरयान
नर- + यान नर- + यान, n. 1. a carriage drawn by men, MBh. 12, 1383. 2. -याण (with ण्), riding on a man, Pañc. iii. d. 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीयान
नारी- + यान नारी- + यान, n. a carriage for women, Man. 3, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौयान
नौ- + यान नौ- + यान, n. navigation, Rājat. 1, 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयान
पितृ- + यान पितृ- + यान, m. the way of the Manes, leading to the Manes, MBh. 12, 525.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठयान
पृष्ठ- + यान पृष्ठ- + यान, n. 1. going on horseback, riding, Suśr. 1, 258, 5. 2. a horse, Kām. Nītis. 7, 36 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्रयान
शत-सहस्र- + यान शत-सहस्र- + यान, n. a hundred thousand [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a " target="_blank">Page0742-a + 42</a>] roads, Pañc. ii. d. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहयाना
सिंह- + याना सिंह- + यान, f. ना, Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापन|यापनं
यापन यापन, i. e. या, Caus., + अन, n., f. ना (Kām. Nītis. 9, 1).<BR> 1. Spending time.<BR> 2. Staying.<BR> 3. Rejection.<BR> 4. Alleviating.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयापन
काल- + यापन काल- + यापन, n. procrastination, Hit. ii. d. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम|यामः
याम याम,<BR> I. i. e. या + म, m. Going, march, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 87, 3; Chr. 287, 4 = Rigv. i. 48, 4 (approaching, rising).<BR> II. i. e. यम + अ, adj., f. मी.<BR> 1. Relating to Yama.<BR> 2. Inflicted by Yama, Man. 12, 17.<BR> III. i. e. यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Forbearance.<BR> 2. Cessation.<BR> 3. A watch of three hours, Man. 7, 145.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनोददीर्घयाम
अ-विनोद-दीर्घ- + याम अ-विनोद-दीर्घ- + याम, adj., f. मा, endowed with long watches (i. e. seeming long) on account of offering no interesting pursuit, Vikr. d. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियाम
त्रि- + याम त्रि- + याम,<BR> I. adj., f. मा, consisting of three watches, epithet of night, Rām. 2, 10, 7 Gorr.<BR> II. f. मा, night, Vikr. d. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातयाम|यातयामं
यात- + याम यात- + याम, adj. (originally, flat, from having stood a night).<BR> 1. old, spoiled, Bhag. 17, 10. 2. used. 3. rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामन्
यामन् या + मन्, n. Going, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1 (ved. loc. without termination).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामन
यामन यामन, Hiḍ. 1, 38, is a false reading (see MBh. 1, 5912).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामल|यामलं
यामल यामल, i. e. यमल + अ, n. A pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामातृ
यामातृ यामातृ, i. e. यम् + आतृ (cf. जामातृ), and यामातृक यामातृ + क (Lass. 24, 18). m. A daughter's husband.<BR> --Cf. Lat. janitrix; εἰνατέρες; and O.H.G. eidum; A.S. adhum, derived from the same verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामि|यामिः
यामि and यामी यामी̆,<BR> I. i. e. यम् + ई, f.<BR> 1. A sister.<BR> 2. A daughter-in-law, Man. 4, 180 (मी); 183 (मि).<BR> II. i. e. याम + ई, Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिक|यामिकः
यामिक यामिक, i. e. याम + इक,<BR> I. adj. One who announces the watches, Kathās. 3, 63.<BR> II. f. का, Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनी
यामिनी यामिनी, i. e. याम + इन् + ई, f. Night, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 8; Kir. 5, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामी
यामी यामी, see यामि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामेय|यामेयः
यामेय यामेय, i. e. यामि + एय, m. A sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्य|याम्यः
याम्य याम्य, i. e. यम + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या, Relating to Yama, Rām. 3, 54, 10 (with दिश्, The south); propounded by Yama, Man. 8, 173.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Agastya.<BR> 2. Sandal.<BR> III. f. या.<BR> 1. The south.<BR> 2. i. e. याम + य, f. Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायजूक|यायजूकः
यायजूक यायज् + ऊक (frequent. of यज्), m. A performer of frequent sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायिन्
ऽयायिन् -यायिन्, i. e. या + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Going in; e. g. नौ-, adj. sbst. Who or what goes in a boat, Man. 8, 409.<BR> 2. Leading to, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 10 (चित्रकूत-, to the mount of Citrakūta).<BR> 3. सतत-, adj. Taking place continually, Man. 1, 50. समुद्र-, adj. m. A navigator of the ocean, 3, 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव|यावः
याव याव,<BR> I. यव + अ, adj. Relating to barley.<BR> II. m. Lac, the red animal dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावक|यावकं|यावकः
यावक याव + क, m.<BR> 1. Half ripe barley.<BR> 2. Barley-gruel. Man. 11, 125.<BR> 3. Lac.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयावक
स- + यावक स- + यावक, adj., f. विका, painted with lac, Kir. 5, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावज्जीवम्
यावज्जीवम् यवज्जीवम्, i. e. यावन्त्-जीव + म्, adv. All one's life, Pañc. pr. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावतिथ|यावतिथः
यावतिथ यावतिथ (an old superl. of यावन्त्), adj.<BR> 1. That which is as far as.<BR> 2. In how many soever degrees advanced, Man. 1, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावदायुस्
यावदायुस् यावदायुस्, i. e. यावन्त्-आयुस्, adv. All one's life, Vikr. 87, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
यावन यावन, i. e. यवन + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating to the Yavanas.<BR> II. n. Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन्त्|यावत्
यावन्त् यावन्त्, i. e. यद् + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, As much, as many, Hit. iv. d. 69; how much, Rājat. 5, 110; how many, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 12.<BR> II. वत्, acc. sing. n. adv.<BR> 1. As much as, as far as, Johns. Sel. 33, 66.<BR> 2. As many as.<BR> 3. As long as, Pañc. iii. d. 94; with preceding acc. of a word signifying a division of time, During; e. g. सकलां रात्रिं यावत्, During the whole night, Pañc. 117, 8; वर्षम्, During a year, Pañc. ii. d. 66; with following न, Before, Vikr. 61, 10; Pañc. 61, 3.<BR> 4. Meanwhile, Śāk. 18, 22; Vikr. 3, 12.<BR> 5. As far as, unto, until, Rām. 3, 49, 13; with preceding acc., Hit. 111, 18; Pañc. 87, 20; cf. i. d. 132; even, 31, 17.<BR> 6. When. Hit. 85, 9 (with following तावत्, Then), Pañc. 48, 24; if, Pañc. 62, 1.<BR> 7. In order that, Vikr. d. 13; that, Chr. 18, 34.<BR> 8. With a verb it often expresses one's will; e. g. यावत् प्रतिपालयामि, I will wait, Vikr. 38, 5.<BR> 9. Often former part of comp. adverbs; e. g. यावज्जीवम्, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावस|यावसः
यावस यावस, i. e. यवस + अ, m. (n., Hit. iii. d. 53).<BR> 1. A heap of grass.<BR> 2. Provision, Hit. iii. d. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याष्टीक|याष्टीकः
याष्टीक याष्टीक, i. e. यष्टी + क, m. A warrior armed with a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षु
यियक्षु यियक्षु, i. e. यियक्ष, desider. of यज्, + उ, adj. Desirous of sacrificing, Ragh. 13, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियासु
यियासु यियासु, i. e. यियास, desider. of या, + उ, adj. Wishing to go, Kir. 14, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
1. यु यु, ii. 2, Par., and ii. 9, युना, युनि, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To bind.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b " target="_blank">Page0743-b + 43</a>] join, to mix.<BR> 3. To separate (? cf. 2. यु). Ptcple of the pf. pass. युत,<BR> 1. Joined, connected, Rām. 3, 52, 26.<BR> 2. United, Lass. 39, 19.<BR> 3. Attached to.<BR> 4. Endowed, full of, Nal. 12, 2; Chr. 13, 9; Hit. i. d. 152, M.M. (seized).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. व्यति वि-अति, To mix, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 6.- With आ आ, आयुत, Endowed, Nal. 12, 39.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रयुत, Joined. n. A million.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संयुत,<BR> 1. Joined, mixed.<BR> 2. Heaped, Śāk. 69, 15.<BR> 3. Endowed, Sāv. 5, 33; Pañc. iii. d. 48.<BR> 4. Implying, Man. 2, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. juvare, jus (= ved. योस्), jubere (Caus.); ζώννυμι (probably for ζωσνυμι), ζώνη, ζῶστρον.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अ- + युत अ- + युत, m. and n. a myriad, Man. 12, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयुत
गो- + युत गो- + युत, 1. adj., f. ता, full of cattle, Rām. 2, 49, 10. n. a cow-pen, MBh. 14, 1934.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयुत
सु- + युत सु- + युत, adj. well accompanied by, Lass. 50, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
2. यु यु, ii. 3, Par. To keep back.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, Ātm. † To despise.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, ii. 3, To remove, Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तत्व
युक्तत्व युक्त + त्व (vb. युज्), n. Fitness, suitableness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्ति|युक्तिः
युक्ति युक्ति, i. e. युज् + ति. f.<BR> 1. Union, connection.<BR> 2. Propriety, Pañc. iii. d. 163.<BR> 3. Suitable manner, Rājat. 5, 90.<BR> 4. Use, Pañc. 183, 22; Rājat. 5, 165.<BR> 5. Usage, traditionary law.<BR> 6. Inference. argument, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 16; Hit. i. d. 96, M.M.<BR> 7. Probability, Yājñ. 2, 212.<BR> 8. Insertion of circumstances in written evidence, specification of place, time, etc.<BR> 9. Supplying an ellipsis.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयुक्ति
स्व- + युक्ति स्व- + युक्ति, adj. self-harnessed, Chr. 289, 9 = Rigv. i. 50, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तितस्
युक्तितस् युक्ति + तस्, adv. According to justice, Chr. 15, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग युग, i. e. युज् + अ,<BR> I. m. (in epic poetry also n., Chr. 34, 14), A yoke.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A pair, a couple, Śiś. 9, 72; Nal. 14, 25.<BR> 2. Age (ved.), Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR> 3. A lustre of five years.<BR> 4. An age, a period, Man. 1, 71, sqq.; one of the four Indian periods, called सत्य (or कृत), त्रेत, द्वापर, and कलि, Man. 1, 69.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. jugum; Goth. juk; A.S. ioc, iuc, geóc;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरयुग
अम्बर- + युग अम्बर- + युग, n. upper and lower garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतयुग
कृत- + युग कृत- + युग, n. = सत्य-युग, Man. 1, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयुग
गो- + युग गो- + युग, a pair of oxen or beasts in general, Pañc. iii. d. 198; 182, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्युग|चतुर्युगं
चतुर्- + युग चतुर्- + युग,<BR> I. n. the aggregate of the four yugas, Man. 1, 71.<BR> II. adj. containing the four yugas, Ragh. 10, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियुग|त्रियुगः
त्रि- + युग त्रि- + युग, adj. appearing in three yugas, epithet of Kṛṣṇa, Bhāg. P. 3, 24, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयुग
देव- + युग देव- + युग and धर्म-, n. the first age. MBh. 2, 421; Hariv. 761.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चयुग
पञ्च(न्)- + युग पञ्च(न्)- + युग, n. the cycle of five years, MBh. 2, 455.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायुग
महा- + युग महा- + युग, n. the aggregate of the four ages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगंधर|युगन्धर|युगंधरं|युगंधरः|युगन्धरः
युगंधर युगंधर, i. e. युग + म्-धृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. The pole of a carriage.<BR> 2. The name of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपद्
युगपद् युग-पद्, adv.<BR> 1. At one time, Śiś. 9, 41.<BR> 2. Together, Man. 1, 54.<BR> --Cf. perhaps A.S. geoc, rash, praeceps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगल|युगलं
युगल युग + ल, n. A pair, Pañc. 184, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनिवेशितहस्तयुगल
कण्ठ-निवेशित-हस्त- + युगल कण्ठ-निवेशित-हस्त- + युगल (vb. विश्), adj., f. ला, with (both her) hands put to (her) neck, i. e. with her head leaning on her hands, Pañc. 226, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयुगल
वस्त्र- + युगल वस्त्र- + युगल, n. two garments, Pañc. 29, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगांशक|युगांशकः
युगांशक युगांशक, i. e. गुग-अंश + क, m. A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म युग्म, i. e. युज् + म,<BR> I. adj., f. मा, Even, Man. 3, 48.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A pair, a couple, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 4 (-चारिन्, du. Two going together).<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b " target="_blank">Page0744-b + 44</a>] Mixing.<BR> 3. Man. 8, 293, read युग्यम्.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्म
अ- + युग्म अ- + युग्म, adj., f. मा, odd, Man. 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयुग्म
वस्त्र- + युग्म वस्त्र- + युग्म, n. two garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मक
युग्मक युग्म + क, m. A couple, a pair, Lass. 16, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य युग्य, i. e. युज् + य, ptcple. of the fut. pass. of युज्,<BR> I. Fit to be yoked.<BR> II. m. A beast of burthen, Ragh. 5, 49.<BR> III. n. A carriage, Man. 8, 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युङ्ग्
† युङ्ग् युङ्ग्, i. 1, Par. To abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युछ्|युच्छ्
युछ् युछ् (akin to 2. यु), i. 1, Par. To be inattentive or negligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
1. युज् युज् (akin to 1. यु), ii. 7, युनज्, युञ्ज्, Par. Ātm. i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To join, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7 (ved. अयुग्ध्वम्, ii. 2); MBh. 3, 2489.<BR> 2. To connect, Draup. 4, 24.<BR> 3. To endow, Rām. 1, 9, 68.<BR> 4. To put to, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4; MBh. 1, 192.<BR> 5. To direct, to throw, Chr. 41, 2 (anomal. अयुञ्जम्).<BR> 6. To fix one's mind in order to obtain union with the universal spirit, Bhāṣāp. 64.<BR> 7. To meditate, Bhag. 6, 12.<BR> 8. To appoint, MBh. 2, 1290.<BR> 9. To employ, Man. 6, 12.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. युञ्जान, Suitable, MBh. 3, 15633. m.<BR> 1. One who endeavours to obtain union with the universal soul, or one who is engaged in the religious exercise called योग, Bhāṣāp. 64.<BR> 2. A charioteer. Pass., and i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry also with the terminations of the Par.).<BR> 1. To be fit, becoming, Hit. iv. d. 11; Pañc. 61, 4; i. d. 283 (Par.).<BR> 2. To be placed, Hit. iv. d. 76 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3265).<BR> 3. To attach one's self to, Hit. iv. d. 65.<BR> 4. To make one's self ready, Bhag. 2, 38.<BR> 5. To unite one's self with, to attain, Man. 2, 78.<BR> 6. To be obliged, Man. 7, 144.<BR> 7. To meditate, Bhag. 2, 50.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. युक्त.<BR> 1. Joined. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0745-a " target="_blank">Page0745-a + 46</a>]<BR> 2. Fit, Pañc. 69, 10.<BR> 3. Proved.<BR> 4. Endowed with, Hit. iv. d. 33 (कालेन न, Not endowed with, not seizing the right time; cf. Hit. iv. d. 47: अ-लाल-सैन्य-युक्त, Not possessed of an army at the right time).<BR> 5. Employed.<BR> 6. Occupied, Man. 3, 75.<BR> 7. Intent on, 8, 142.<BR> 8. Occupied in the performance of the Yoga.<BR> 9. A student, Man. 2, 223.<BR> 10. ˚तम्, adv. Well, Vikr. 12, 6.<BR> 11. Comparat. युक्ततर, One who is to the utmost on his guard, Man. 7, 186. m. The sage who has acquired union with the universal soul, Bhāṣāp. 64. f. ता, A plant, commonly Eláni. n. A measure of four cubits.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. योग्य.<BR> 1. Fit, Hit. ii. d. 73.<BR> 2. Suitable, Hit. i. d. 62, M.M.<BR> 3. Able, Rājat. 5, 249.<BR> 4. Clever. See s. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अर्थ-, adj. profitable, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 6.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To join, Hit. i. d. 53, M.M.; Rājat. 5, 104; to fix (a snare), Hit. 46, 9, M.M.<BR> 2. To achieve, Rājat. 5, 403.<BR> 3. To treat, Pañc. iv. d. 74.<BR> 4. To bring on, to instigate, Pañc. iv. d. 18.<BR> 5. To entangle, Pañc. ii. d. 125 (Ātm.).<BR> 6. To mix, Man. 7, 218.<BR> 7. To oblige, Chr. 18, 34.<BR> 8. To put to, Rām. 2, 82, 31.<BR> 9. To place, Hit. iii. d. 80.<BR> 10. To appoint, Rājat. 5, 129.<BR> 11. To throw, Chr. 33, 2.<BR> 12. To endow, Man. 1, 26; Vikr. d. 60.<BR> 13. To present with, to give, MBh. 1, 6477.<BR> 14. To return, Daśak. 185, 12.<BR> 15. Pass. To belong, MBh. 3, 12313.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. † To despise.<BR> --With the prep. श्रनु अनु, ii. 7, Ātm.<BR> 1. To examine, Man. 8, 31.<BR> 2. To order, MBh. 4, 105.<BR> 3. To choose a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0745-b " target="_blank">Page0745-b + 43</a>] husband, MBh. 3, 15633.<BR> --With अभि अभि, Ātm.<BR> 1. To prepare for, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 2.<BR> 2. To draw near, to attack, 200, 23. Pass.<BR> 1. To be accused, Man. 8, 183; to be asked (in lawsuit), Vikr. d. 96.<BR> 2. To be rebuked, Man. 8, 50. अभियुक्त,<BR> 1. Diligent, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 4; ever striving, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 8.<BR> 2. Absorbed in meditation, Pañc. i. d. 345.<BR> 3. Attacked, assailed, Hit. iv. d. 24.<BR> 4. Hurt, Rām. 2, 10, 27.<BR> 5. Accused, prosecuted.<BR> --Caus. To appoint, Pañc. 163, 15.<BR> --With आ आ, Ātm. To put, MBh. 1, 7948. आयुक्त, m. Commissioned, an agent, a deputy, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 115.<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ, समुपायुक्त, Surrounded, MBh. 3, 10099.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, समा-युक्त,<BR> 1. Connected, Man. 12, 28; united, Nal. 25, 8.<BR> 2. Surrounded, MBh. 3, 3017.<BR> 3. Gifted, endowed, Pañc. iii. d. 117; Hit. i. d. 174, M.M.<BR> --Caus. To join, MBh. 1, 7200 (to string).<BR> --With उद् उद्, उद्युक्त,<BR> 1. Excited, Rām. 1, 1, 45.<BR> 2. Zealously active, Hit. iii. d. 112; Rājat. 5, 331.<BR> 3. Extended, Lass. 67, 1.<BR> --Caus. To excite, to make ready, MBh. 5, 70.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, Caus. To order to act, Mālav. 9, 16.<BR> --With उप उप, Ātm.<BR> 1. To meddle, MBh. 5, 992.<BR> 2. To employ for one's self, Man. 8, 40.<BR> 3. To enjoy, Megh. 13.<BR> 2. To consume, MBh. 3, 57.<BR> 4. To attach one's self to, MBh. 3, 15633. Pass.<BR> 1. To be suitable, Pañc. 155, 8; to be of use, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1915; to be necessary, Pañc. i. d. 372; अन्-उपयुज्यमान, Unable to be employed, quite weak, Utt. Rāmac. 95, 1.<BR> 2. To employ for one's self, MBh. 3, 12739.<BR> 3. To be worth being regarded, Pañc. i. d. 37. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0746-a " target="_blank">Page0746-a + 46</a>] उपयुक्त,<BR> 1. Suitable, Hit. 98, 14 (किम् उपयुक्तो ऽयम् एतद् वर्तनं गृह्णात्यथानुपयुक्तो वा, Whether he deserves so large a pay or not; literally, whether he receives so large a pay as a suitable person, or as an unsuitable).<BR> 2. Touched by.<BR> 3. Taken.<BR> 4. Eaten.<BR> --Comp.<BR> औ-, adj. unworthy, Śāk. 97, 3.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To consume, MBh. 3, 1538.<BR> --With नि नि, Ātm.<BR> 1. To place; to put to (as horses), Vikr. d. 155; to place at the head, Hit. iii. d. 128; to engage, Johns. Sel. 37, 19; to appoint, Man. 1, 28; Pañc. i. d. 82.<BR> 2. To constrain, Chr. 10, 3; to coerce, Rām. 1, 1, 92; to harass, Man. 8, 186.<BR> 3. To order, Rām. 1, 54, 16.<BR> 4. To commit, Man. 9, 64. नियुक्त,<BR> 1. Connected, Hit. i. d. 158, M.M.<BR> 2. fastened, Rām. 1, 13, 31.<BR> 3. Placed, Hit. 81, 13.<BR> 4. Ascertained.<BR> 5. Engaged in.<BR> 6. Commanded, Rām. 1, 14, 34.<BR> 7. Appointed, Hit. 58, 17.<BR> 8. Authorised, Man. 9, 58.<BR> 9. Offered, Man. 5, 16. m. A functionary, Hit. ii. d. 105.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. नियोज्य.<BR> 1. To be placed, Pañc. i. d. 82.<BR> 2. To be ordered, MBh. 12, 12358. m. A servant, Śāk. d. 163.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-नियोग्य, and अ-नि-योज्य, adj. not suitable to be commanded, Rām. 2, 66, 7; MBh. 1, 3267.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To order to be put. Hit. 46, 13.<BR> 2. To fasten, Pañc. 135, 4; to bring (संदेहे, in danger), Pañc. 8, 21; to accustom, 21, 6.<BR> 3. To endow, Pañc. 4, 25.<BR> 4. To employ, Man. 9, 324; Pañc. i. d. 413; pass. To employ one's self, Pañc. v. d. 68.<BR> 5. To appoint, to charge, Rām. 1, 38, 10.<BR> 6. To direct, Man. 9, 68; to order, to refer (to an ordeal), Pañc. 97, 1.<BR> 7. To coerce, Bhag. 3, 36.<BR> 8. To offer Pañc. 70, 3.<BR> 9. To present with, Pañc. 4, 25.<BR> 10. To perform, Man. 3, 204; to make, Pañc. 24, 5.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि,<BR> 1. To appoint, to charge, MBh. 1, 4152. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0746-b " target="_blank">Page0746-b + 44</a>]<BR> 2. To use, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 10; Lass. 95, 9. विनियुक्त,<BR> 1. Separated, detached, loosed, Johns. Sel. 31, 46.<BR> 2. Parted with.<BR> 3. Appointed.<BR> 4. Applied to.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To appoint, Hit. iii. d. 54.<BR> 2. To intrust, Man. 7, 226.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To appoint, MBh. 1, 2500. संनियुक्त,<BR> 1. Appointed.<BR> 2. Attached to.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To appoint, MBh. 1, 6912.<BR> 2. To allot, Pañc. ii. d. 78.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-न् स्, To throw, Rām. 2, 23, 37.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To put to, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. i. 85, 5.<BR> 2. To put at the head, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 51.<BR> 3. To join, Rām. 1, 17, 11.<BR> 4. To employ, Man. 2, 159; Pañc. i. d. 39.<BR> 5. To direct, Chr. 287, 4 = Rigv. i. 48, 4.<BR> 6. To conduct, Mālav. 45, 9.<BR> 7. To throw, Chr. 31, 11.<BR> 8. To give, Rām. 1, 13, 38.<BR> 9. To lend, Man. 8, 146.<BR> 10. To perform, Man. 2, 248.<BR> 11. To represent, Mālav. 3, 10.<BR> 12. To behove, to be convenient (i. 4, Ātm., or Pass.), Pañc. 224, 24. प्रयुक्त,<BR> 1. Connected with, Rām. 1, 17, 14.<BR> 2. Closely united.<BR> 3. Suitable, MBh. 1, 6845.<BR> 4. Endowed with.<BR> 5. Resulting from, Hit. ii. d. 59.<BR> 6. Appointed, Rām. 3, 51, 27.<BR> 7. Governed, Lass. 53, 10.<BR> 8. Lent, Man. 8, 49.<BR> 9. Done, Śāk. 95, 13.<BR> 10. Lost in meditation. n. Cause.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-, 1. closely connected. 2. well managed.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To throw, Chr. 31, 7.<BR> 2. To cause to be exhibited, Utt. Rāmac. 111, 7.<BR> 3. To show, Man. 3, 112.<BR> 4. To receive, Man. 10, 117.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass, प्रयोज्य.<BR> 1. To be set to work.<BR> 2. To be used. m. A servant n. Capital, principal.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र,<BR> 1. To separate, Rām. 2, 53, 20.<BR> 2. To deprive, MBh. 1, 6735.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To connect, MBh. 1, 4475. संप्रयुक्त,<BR> 1. Joined.<BR> 2. Connected with, holding [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-a " target="_blank">Page0747-a + 43</a>] any intercourse with, Man. 11, 179.<BR> 3. Overtaken, reached.<BR> --Caus. To connect, MBh. 3, 1153.<BR> --With वि वि, Ātm.<BR> 1. To separate, MBh. 3, 10924.<BR> 2. To abandon, Chr. 47, 35 (Par., perhaps it is to be changed to मोक्स्ह्यसि). Pass. To be deprived, Pañc. i. d. 340; to lose, Man. 7, 46; to violate, 5, 91. अ-वि-युक्त, adj. Not separated, Vikr. 78, 20. अ-वियोज्य, Not to be deprived, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 12.<BR> --Caus. To cause to leave, to break off from, Pañc. 31, 6.<BR> 2. To deprive, Pañc. 30, 10; MBh. 3, 2851; to rob, 1, 6225.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To unite, Man. 9, 22.<BR> 2. To endow, MBh. 1, 6289; to endow with, Rām. 1, 1, 21. संयुक्त,<BR> 1. Connected, Chr. 59, 22.<BR> 2. Attached.<BR> 3. Accompanied.<BR> 4. Mixed.<BR> 5. Endowed with, Man. 1, 109.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To join, MBh. 3, 11762.<BR> 2. To endow with, MBh. 1, 6474; Pañc. 244, 5; to present with, Pañc. 30, 12.<BR> 3. To employ, MBh. 3, 816.<BR> 4. Ātm. To meditate, Chr. 38, 13.<BR> --With विसम् वि-सम्, विसंयुक्त, Separated from, neglecting, Man. 2, 80.<BR> --Cf. Lat. jungere; ζεύγνυμι; A.S. geocan, geóce, help.<BR> --Cf. युग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अ- + युज् अ- + युज्, adj. 1. negligent, Rām. 3, 37, 7. 2. not used to, ib. 3, 37, 23. 3. unsuitable, Pañc. 170, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमयुक्तम्
क्षेम-युक्त + म् क्षेम-युक्त + म्, adv. in a prosperous way, Rām. 1, 13, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोयुक्त
तपस्- + युक्त तपस्- + युक्त, adj. devout, Chr. 9, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानयुक्त
विधान- + युक्त विधान- + युक्त, adj. conformable to the sacred precepts, Chr. 51, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
2. युज् युज्,<BR> I. adj. Even, Man. 3, 277.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A joiner.<BR> 2. One who devotes his time to abstract speculation.<BR> III. (n.), A pair.<BR> IV. Latter part of comp. adj. Joined, which are (horses) put to, drawn by, Chr. 27, 7. चतुर्-, adj. Drawn by four horses, MBh. 1, 8005. हरि-, adj. Drawn by (Indra's) horses, Arj. 4, 32.<BR> --Cf. Lat. -jux in conjux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
† युत् युत् (cf. द्युत्), i. 1, Ātm. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युतक|युतकं
युतक युत + क (vb. यु), n.<BR> 1. A pair.<BR> 2. Alliance.<BR> 3. Nuptial presents.<BR> 4. A garment worn by women.<BR> 5. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b " target="_blank">Page0747-b + 41</a>] ends of a cloth.<BR> 6. The edge of a winnowing basket.<BR> 7. Doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धकारित्व
युद्धकारित्व युद्धकारित्व, i. e. युद्ध-कारिन् + त्व (vb. युध्), n. Fighting, Hit. iii. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धमय
युद्धमय युद्ध + मय (see युध्), adj. Warlike, martial, Chr. 24, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
1. युध् युध् (akin to 1. यु), i. 4, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 1, 7119).<BR> 1. To fight, to contend in battle, Man. 7, 89; impersonal pass., Hit. iii. d. 88.<BR> 2. To oppose, Johns. Sel. 55, 145. युद्ध, n.<BR> 1. The use of arms, Man. 3, 162.<BR> 2. War, battle, Pañc. 87, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-योध्य,<BR> I. adj., f. या, not to be warred against, Rām. 6, 112, 47.<BR> II. f. या, the capital of Rāma, the modern Oude, Rām. 1, 5, 1, sqq. Desider. युयुत्स, To desire to fight, MBh. 4, 1252.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to fight, Man. 7, 193.<BR> 2. To defend, MBh. 3, 639.<BR> 3. To oppose, MBh. 2, 2120; to be a match for, Man. 7, 74; Hit. iii. d. 50.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To oppose, MBh. 3, 15645.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. The same, 3, 15054.<BR> 2. To fight with, Utt. Rāmac. 130, 5.<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ, To fight, Śiś. 18, 32.<BR> --With नि नि, नियुद्ध, n. Fighting, particularly boxing, MBh. 1, 5340.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रयुद्ध, n. War, battle. Desider. To desire to fight, MBh. 3, 15646.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To oppose, MBh. 1, 7103.<BR> --Caus. The same, 1, 7116.<BR> --With सम् सम्. The same, 1, 3477 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a " target="_blank">Page0748-a + 39</a>] Caus. The same, 1, 7098.<BR> --Cf. ὑσμίνη, ὑσμίν (cf. युध्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अ- + युद्ध अ- + युद्ध, n. 1. absence of war, Chr. 56, 14 (instr. without war). 2. not fighting, Hit. ii. d. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटयुद्ध
कूट- + युद्ध कूट- + युद्ध,<BR> I. n. 1. a fraudulent manner of fighting. Ragh. 17, 69.<BR> II. adj. fighting fraudulently, Rām. 1, 22, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वयुद्ध|द्वंद्वयुद्ध
द्वन्द्व- + युद्ध द्वन्द्व- + युद्ध, n. single combat, MBh. 7, 582.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
2. युध् युध्,<BR> I. f. War, battle, Pañc. iii. d. 11.<BR> II. m. A warrior, Johns. Sel. 57, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधान|युधानः
युधान युधान (ptcple. pres. of युध्, ii. 2), m. An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिश्रेष्ठ
युधिश्रेष्ठ युध् + इ-श्रेष्ठ, adj. Preeminent in battle, Chr. 49, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिष्ठिर|युधिष्ठिरः
युधिष्ठिर युधिष्ठिर, i. e. युध् + इ-स्थिर, m. The elder of the five Pāṇḍavas, Pañc. ii. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्म|युध्मः
युध्म युध् + म, m.<BR> 1. War, battle.<BR> 2. A bow.<BR> 3. An arrow.<BR> 4. A warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्वन्
ऽयुध्वन् i. e. -युध् + वन् in सह-,<BR> I. adj. Fighting with, or along with.<BR> II. m. A brother in arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युन्थ्
युन्थ् युन्थ्, v. r. of पुन्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युप्
युप् युप्, i. 4, Par. To confuse, to trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयु|युयुः
युयु युयु (probably vb. जू), m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सा
युयुत्सा युयुत्सा, i. e. युयुत्स, desider. of युध्, + अ, f. Eager desire for the combat, Chr. 24, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सु|युयुत्सुः
युयुत्सु युयुत्सु, i. e. युयुत्स, desider. of युध्, + उ,<BR> I. adj. Eager for combat, Johns. Sel. 56, 150; pugnacious, Chr. 63, 66.<BR> II. A proper name, Johns. Sel. 24, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधि
युयुधि युयुध् + इ (red. युध्), adj. Pugnacious, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवति|युवतिः
युवति युवति, see युवन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्
युवन् युवन् (for यवन्, cf. comparat. यवीयंस्, उ by the influence of व्),<BR> I. adj., f. वती and यानि, comparat. यवीयंस्, superl. यविष्ठ, Young, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4.<BR> II. m. A young man, Ṛt. 6, 20.<BR> III. f. वती̆ or यूनी, A young woman. Bhartṛ. 2, 60; Pañc. 158. 3; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b " target="_blank">Page0748-b + 39</a>] Sāv. 2, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. juvenis, junior, Junius, junix, etc.; Goth. juggs; A.S. iong, iung, geong, geogudh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारयुवति
वार-युवति वार-युवति, f. a courtesan, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरयुवति|सुरयुवतिः
सुर-युवति सुर-युवति, f. a celestial woman, Megh. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्
युष्मद् युष्मद्, pronoun of the second person, Thou; the bases of the cases are त्व, तु, युव, यु, युष्म, i. e. यु + स्म, and त, व. Ved. nom. du. युवम्, Chr. 295, 17 = Rigv. i. 92, 17; gen., abl. युवोस्, 296, 2 = Rigv. i. 112, 2.<BR> --Cf. Lat. tu, te, vos; τούν, τύ, σύ, τέ, σέ, σϕῶι, ὔμμες; Goth. thu, jus, izvis; A.S. thu, gyt, eow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मादृश्
युष्मादृश् युष्मादृश्, i. e. युष्मद्-दृश्, adj. Like you, Lass. 76, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यू
यू यू, f. Pease soap (cf. युष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूक|यूकः
यूक यूक, m., and f. का, A louse, Man. 1, 40; Pañc. iii. d. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूति|यूतिः
यूति यूति, i. e. यु + ति, f. Mixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथ|यूथं
यूथ यूथ, i. e. यु + थ,<BR> I. n. A multitude of birds or beasts, a herd, Vikr. d. 110; Pañc. 93, 1.<BR> II. f. थी, A kind of jasmine, Jasminum auriculatum.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यूथ
निर्यूथ निर्यूथ, i. e. निस्-, adj. separated from the herd, Rām. 3, 68, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथप|यूथपः
यूथप यूथ-प (vb. 2. पा), m. The leader of a herd, Pañc. 253, 16; Lass. 46, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथशस्
यूथशस् यूथ + शस्, adv. In flocks, gregariously, Nal. 12, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथिका
यूथिका यूथिका. i. e. युथी (see यूथ), + क, f. A kind of jasmine, Vikr. d. 109; Ṛt. 2, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूप|यूपः
यूप यूप,<BR> I. m. and n. A sacrificial post, MBh. 7, 2266.<BR> II. m. A trophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष्
† यूष् यूष्, i. 1, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष|यूषं|यूषः
यूष यूष, m. and n. Pease soup. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a " target="_blank">Page0749-a + 45</a>] the water in which pulse of various kinds has been boiled.<BR> --Cf. Lat. jus; probably also ζωμός, ζύθος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष्
येष् येष्, see पेष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्र|योक्त्रं
योक्त्र योक्त्र, i. e. युज् + त्र, n. The tie of the yoke of a plough; a halter, Man. 8, 292.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्रय
योक्त्रय योक्त्रय, a denomin. derived from योक्त्र, To enclose, Hiḍ. 4, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग|योगः
योग योग, i. e. युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Junction, Bhāṣāp. 56; joining, union, Vikr. d. 23.<BR> 2. Putting to (horses), Chr. 4, 17.<BR> 3. Putting on armour.<BR> 4. Armour.<BR> 5. Connexion, Hit. i. d. 98, M.M. (कथा-, Conversation).<BR> 6. Result, Hit. iii. d. 140 (पुण्य-, of merit), Man. 1, 41 (तपस्-, force of devotion).<BR> 7. Use, performance, Kir. 5, 52.<BR> 8. Propriety, aptness, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 13.<BR> 9. Mode, Man. 9, 330; Nal. 15, 6.<BR> 10. A rule, a precept.<BR> 11. A means, an expedient, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 19; Hit. i. d. 201, M.M. (अ-दण्ड-, Except by means of punishment: नियत-विषय-वर्ती प्रायशो ऽदण्ड-योगाज् जगतिपर-वशे ऽस्मिन् दुर्लभः साधु-वृत्तः, He who keeps in his appointed sphere (does so) generally by reason of punishment. In this dependent world it is hard to find one who acts of himself virtuously).<BR> 12. A conveyance, a carriage.<BR> 13. Fraud, Man. 8, 165.<BR> 14. Wealth.<BR> 15. Thing.<BR> 16. Lucky conjuncture, Vikr. 38, 12.<BR> 17. Religious and abstract meditation (properly union, viz. with the universal soul), Pañc. 165, 9.<BR> 18. A system of philosophy, Bhag. 2, 39.<BR> 19. The particular practice of devotion, by which union with God is supposed to be obtained.<BR> 20. Magic, or the acquisition of supernatural powers; magical art, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212.<BR> 21. Deathlike state of meditation, Kathās. 4, 111. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-b " target="_blank">Page0749-b + 46</a>]<BR> 22. A spy.<BR> 23. A violator of truth or confidence.<BR> 24. The leading or principal star of a lunar mansion.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अ- + योग अ- + योग, m. unfitness, unsuitableness, impossibility, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियोग|अतियोगः
अति- + योग अति- + योग, m. excess, Suśr. 2, 192, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थयोग
अर्थ- + योग अर्थ- + योग, m. Concurrence of circumstances (as of cause and effect), Hit. ii. p. 2, 13, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथायोग|कथायोगः
कथा- + योग कथा- + योग, m. conversation, MBh. 14, 377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मयोग|कर्मयोगः|कर्म्मयोग|कर्म्मयोगः
कर्म(न्)- + योग कर्म(न्)- + योग, m. business, Man. 10, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयोग|कालयोगः
काल- + योग काल- + योग, m. destiny, MBh. 3, 9919.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमयोग|क्रमयोगः
क्रम- + योग क्रम- + योग, m. order, Man. 1, 42; regular succession, 2, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णयोग|चूर्णयोगः
चूर्ण- + योग चूर्ण- + योग, m. a mixture of fragrant powders, MBh. 12, 2163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयोग
दण्ड- + योग दण्ड- + योग, m. punishment; cf. Hit. i. d. 201, M.M. (supra, 8. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योग|दुर्योगः
दुर्योग दुर्योग, i. e. दुस्-, m. 1. wickedness, Utt. Rāmac. 147, 14. 2. fraud, MBh. 1, 1316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयोग|दैवयोगः
दैव- + योग दैव- + योग, m. contingency, fate, Pañc. i. d. 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानयोग|ध्यानयोगः
ध्यान- + योग ध्यान- + योग, m. meditation, Man. 6, 73; 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रयोग|नक्षत्रयोगः
नक्षत्र- + योग नक्षत्र- + योग, m. the moon's conjunction with the lunar mansions, MBh. 5, 1905.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रायोग
निद्रा- + योग निद्रा- + योग, m. sleep-like absorption in meditation, Hariv. 2217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णयोग
पूर्ण- + योग पूर्ण- + योग (vb. पॄ), m. a sort of fighting, MBh. 2, 910.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तियोग|भक्तियोगः
भक्ति- + योग भक्ति- + योग, m. devotion, as shown by implicit faith in any divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथायोगम्
यथा-योग + म् यथा-योग + म्, adv. in due order, Man. 5, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासयोग|वासयोगः
वास- + योग वास- + योग, m. fragrant powder sprinkled on the cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियोग|विधियोगः
विधि- + योग विधि- + योग, m. 1. combination for any act or rite. 2. the occurrence of predestined events, fate, Hit. i. d. 20, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयोग
सार- + योग सार- + योग, m. possession or application of the essence of any thing, Kir. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्मयोग|स्त्रीधर्म्मयोग
स्त्री-धर्म- + योग स्त्री-धर्म- + योग, m. the laws concerning women, Man. 1, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानयोग|स्थानयोगः
स्थान- + योग स्थान- + योग, m. 1. assignment of suitable places. 2. the best mode of preserving articles, Man. 9, 332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक्षेमकर
योगक्षेमकर योग-क्षेम-कर, adj., f. री, Maintaining and protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगज|योगजं|योगजः
योगज योग-ज, adj. Produced by religious and abstract meditation, Bhāṣāp. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगतस्
योगतस् योग + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. Conjointly. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a " target="_blank">Page0750-a + 43</a>]<BR> 2. Suitably.<BR> 3. Conformably to the law, Man. 6, 9.<BR> 4. Seasonably<BR> 5. Through religious austerities, devotion, Man. 2, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगस्
योगस् योगस्, i. e. युज् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Meditation, religious abstraction.<BR> 2. The half of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिता
योगिता योगिता, i. e. योगिन् + ता, f. Connection, Bhāṣāp. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिन्
योगिन् योगिन्, i. e. योग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Being united, or endowed with, Bhāṣāp. 27.<BR> 2. Who or what joins.<BR> 3. Possessed of superhuman power.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A performer of the religious meditation called Yoga, Bhag. 6, 10.<BR> 2. An ascetic, Pañc. i. d. 333.<BR> 3. One who has acquired supernatural power, Hit. ii. d. 26.<BR> 4. A magician, Pañc. 240, 12; Lass. 4, 9.<BR> III. f. नी, A female fiend.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयोगिन्
काल- + योगिन् काल- + योगिन्, i. e. काल-योग + इन्, m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुयोगिन्
कु- + योगिन् कु- + योगिन्, m. a wicked Yogin, Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रयोगिन्
नक्षत्र- + योगिन् नक्षत्र- + योगिन्, adj. sbst. being connected with the lunar mansions, MBh. 1, 2581; its principal stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्य|योग्यं|योग्यः
योग्य योग्य,<BR> I. See युज्.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A vehicle.<BR> 2. A cake.<BR> 3. A drug, commonly Riddhi.<BR> 4. Sandal.<BR> III. f. या, Military exercise.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतयोग्य
कृत- + योग्य कृत- + योग्य, adj. fighting perfectly, Johns. Sel. 12, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्यता
योग्यता योग्य + ता, f., and योग्यत्व योग्य + त्व, n. Fitness, Pañc. 241, 6; Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 22 (त्व); suitableness, consistency, Bhāṣāp. 81 (ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
योजन योजन, i. e. युज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Joining.<BR> 2. A means for inducing (the gods) to yoke (their horses and to come), Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 88, 5.<BR> 3. A line, row, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3.<BR> 4. The Supreme Being.<BR> 5. A measure of distance of about five or nine miles, Pañc. 226, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजनम्
आ-योजन + म् आ-योजन + म्, adv. the length of a Yojana, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b " target="_blank">Page0750-b + 43</a>] Johns. Sel. 41, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणयोजन
वाण- + योजन वाण- + योजन n. a quiver, Pañc. MS. Berol. 139, b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तयोजनी
सप्तयोजनी सप्तयोजनी, i. e. सप्तन्-योजन + ई, f. an extent of seven Yojanas, Rājat. 5, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजयितृ
योजयितृ योजयितृ, i. e. युज्, Caus., + तृ, m., f. त्री, n.<BR> 1. Who or what joins.<BR> 2. One who enchases, Hit. ii. d. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्र|योत्रं
योत्र योत्र, i. e. यु + त्र, n. = योक्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धृ
योद्धृ योद्धृ, i. e. युध् + तृ, m. A warrior, Pañc. 218, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योध|योधः
योध योध, i. e. युध् + अ, m. A warrior, Man. 7, 97.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तयोध|वसन्तयोधः
वसन्त- + योध वसन्त- + योध, m. the god of love, Ṛt. 6, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतसर्वयोध
हत-सर्व- + योध हत-सर्व- + योध, adj. with all the warriors killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधिन्
योधिन् योधिन्, i. e. युध् + इन्, adj. sbst. Fighting, Hit. iv. d. 48 (काल-, at the right time); a warrior.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रयोधिन्
अग्र- + योधिन् अग्र- + योधिन्, m. a champion, Rām. 4, 21, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटयोधिन्
कूट- + योधिन् कूट- + योधिन्, adj. fighting fraudulently, Rām. 6, 21, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजयोधिन्
गज- + योधिन् गज- + योधिन्, adj. fighting mounted on an elephant, Chr. 4, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वयोधिन्|द्वंद्वयोधिन्
द्वन्द्व- + योधिन् द्वन्द्व- + योधिन्, adj. fighting in single combat, or by pairs, Bhāg. P. 8, 10, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनि|योनिः
योनि योनि, i. e. यु + नि, m. f., and नी, f.<BR> 1. The vulva, Suśr. 2, 397, 10; the womb, Pañc. 188, 5; 6.<BR> 2. Place of birth, Hit. iv. d. 68.<BR> 3. Origin, Man. 2, 25.<BR> 4. A mine.<BR> 5. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनि|अयोनिः
अ- + योनि अ- + योनि,<BR> I. f. any but the natural part (the vulva), Man. 11, 173.<BR> II. adj. without beginning, Kumāras. 2, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्ययोनि|अन्त्ययोनिः
अन्त्य- + योनि अन्त्य- + योनि, adj. of lowest birth, or race, Man. 8, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजयोनि|अम्भोजयोनिः
अम्भोज- + योनि अम्भोज- + योनि, m. Brahman, Prab. 24, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकयोनि
एक- + योनि एक- + योनि, adj. of the same caste, Man. 9, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भयोनि|कुंभयोनि|कुम्भयोनिः
कुम्भ- + योनि कुम्भ- + योनि, m. epithet of Agastya, Ragh. 4, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तयोनि
चित्त- + योनि चित्त- + योनि, m. love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्योनि|जगद्योनिः
जगत्- + योनि जगत्- + योनि, m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 7, 9506.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवयोनि|जीवयोनिः
जीव- + योनि जीव- + योनि, adj. containing life, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग्योनि|तिर्यग्योनिः|तिर्य्यग्योनि
तिर्यग्योनि तिर्यग्योनि, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-, f. the womb of a brute animal, Man. 4, 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योनि
दुर्योनि दुर्य्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. of debased birth, Man. 10, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोनि|देवयोनिः
देव- + योनि देव- + योनि, adj. of divine origin, Dev. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a " target="_blank">Page0751-a + 41</a>] 5, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मयोनि|पद्मयोनिः
पद्म- + योनि पद्म- + योनि, m. epithet of Brahman, MBh. 7, 9427.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापयोनि|पापयोनिः
पाप- + योनि पाप- + योनि, m. wicked, or low, birth, Man. 4, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरायोनि|पुरायोनिः
पुरा- + योनि पुरा- + योनि, adj. of old lineage, MBh. 3, 12705.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनी
वि-योनी वि-योनी, f. the womb of beasts, Man. 12, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीनयोनि
वि-हीन- + योनि वि-हीन- + योनि (vb. हा), adj. base-born, brutish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलसुताचरणरागयोनि
शैल-सुता-चरण-राग- + योनि शैल-सुता-चरण-राग- + योनि, adj. produced by the colour of the feet of Pārvatī, Vikr. d. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पयोनि|सङ्कल्पयोनि|सङ्कल्पयोनिः
संकल्प- + योनि संकल्प- + योनि, m. Kāmadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्व- + योनि स्व- + योनि,<BR> I. adj. related by kin, Man. 2, 134; 206.<BR> II. f. 1. a sister, Man. 11, 170. 2. a near female relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनितस्
योनितस् योनि + तस्, adv. By blood, Man. 2, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषणा
योषणा योषणा, i. e. जुष् + अन् + अ, f. A woman, Lass. 99, 8 = Rigv. iii. 62, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषा
योषा योषा, i. e. जुष् + अ, f. A woman, Chr. 287, 5 = Rigv. i. 48, 5; Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भयोषा
गर्भ- + योषा गर्भ- + योषा, f. a pregnant woman, MBh. 13, 1846 (figurat.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोषा
देव- + योषा देव- + योषा, f. the wife of a god, MBh. 9, 2714.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्
योषित् योषित्, i. e. जुष् + इत् (for जोषन्त्, ptcple. pres.), f. A woman, Vikr. d. 40.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलयोषित्
कुल- + योषित् कुल- + योषित्, f. a virtuous woman, Man. 3, 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ययोषित्
पण्य- + योषित् पण्य- + योषित्, and वार-, f. a harlot, Man. 9, 259 (पण्य-); Daśak. in Chr. 189, 4 (वार-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषिता
योषिता योषित् + आ, f. A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्तिक|यौक्तिकः
यौक्तिक यौक्तिक, i. e. युक्ति + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Connective.<BR> 2. Deducible.<BR> 3. Usual.<BR> 4. Proper, right.<BR> II. m. An associate of one's amusements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगक|यौगकः
यौगक यौगक, i. e. योग + क, adj. Relating to the religious practice called योग (see s. v. योग,<BR> 19.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगंधरायण
यौगंधरायण यौगंधरायण, i. e. युगंधर + आयन, m. A proper name, Kathās. 15, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगपद्य|यौगपद्यं
यौगपद्य यौगपद्य, i. e. युगपद् + य, n. Simultaneousness, Draup. 1, 4 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b " target="_blank">Page0751-b + 41</a>] (at once).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगपद्य|अयौगपद्यं
अ- + यौगपद्य अ- + यौगपद्य, r. non-simultaneousness, Bhāṣāp. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगिक|यौगिकः
यौगिक यौगिक, i. e. योग + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Usual.<BR> 2. Proper.<BR> 3. Relating to the religious practice called योग (see s. v. योग,<BR> 19.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौट्
† यौट् यौट्, यौड् यौड्, i. 1, Par. To join (i. e. जोस्-धा, see यु, and cf. Zend. यओज़्ह्दा and supra मृड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतक|यौतकं
यौतक यौतक, i. e. युतक + अ, n.<BR> 1. Appropriating, Man. 9, 214.<BR> 2. Property, Man. 9, 131 (a nuptial gift, presents made to a bride by her father or friends.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधिष्ठिर|यौधिष्ठिरं
यौधिष्ठिर यौधिष्ठिर, i. e. युधिष्ठिर + अ, adj. Belonging to Yudhiṣṭhira, Johns. Sel. 96, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौन|यौनं
यौन यौन, i. e. योनि + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the womb, uterine.<BR> 2. Connubial, Man. 3, 157; 2, 40.<BR> II. (n.), Contracting affinity, Man. 11, 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवन|यौवनं
यौवन यौवन, i. e. युवन् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Juvenile, Cāṇ. 49 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Youth, Vikr. d. 26; Pañc. 128, 2; manhood.<BR> 2. The age of marriageableness, Chr. 51, 4.<BR> 3. An assemblage of young women.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरयौवन|स्थिरयौवनः
स्थिर- + यौवन स्थिर- + यौवन, adj., f. ना, possessed of eternal youth, Vikr. d. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनवन्त्|यौवनवत्
यौवनवन्त् यौवन + वन्त्, adj., f. वति,<BR> I. Youthful, Hit. 63, 2, M.M.<BR> II. and यौवनस्थ यौवन-स्थ, f. था, Marriageable, Lass. 23, 15; Pañc. 183, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवराज्य|यौवराज्यं
यौवराज्य यौवराज्य, i. e. युवन्-राज + य, n. The dignity of an heir apparent, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 15; Vikr. d. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माक|यौष्माकं
यौष्माक यौष्माक, and यौष्माकीन यौष्माकिन, i. e. युष्मद् + क + अ, or इन, adj. Yours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंह्
1. रंह् रंह् (akin to लङ्घ्, q. cf.), i. 1, Par. and † i. 10, Par. To go, to move, with speed.<BR> --Caus. To impel to speed, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. i. 85, 5.<BR> --Cf. perhaps τρέχω; Goth. thragjan; in this case the Sskr. word has dropped the initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंह्
† 2. रंह् रंह्, वंह् वंह्, i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहस्
रंहस् 1. रंह् + अस्, n. Speed, velocity, Ragh. 2, 34 (Calc.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरंहस्
अति- + रंहस् अति- + रंहस्, adj. of excessive velocity, Śāk. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरंहस्
वात- + रंहस् वात- + रंहस्, adj. swift as the wind, Indr. 1, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्
† रक् † रक्, लक् लक्, रग् रग्, लग् लग्, रघ् रघ्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To taste.<BR> 2. To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्क
रक्क रक्क, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 423.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तक|रक्तकः
रक्तक रक्त + क (see रङ्ज्), m.<BR> 1. Red garments, or cloth.<BR> 2. A man affected with fondness or passion.<BR> 3. A player.<BR> 4. The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तप|रक्तपः
रक्तप रक्त-प (1. पा, cf. रञ्ज्),<BR> I. adj. Who or what drinks blood.<BR> II. m. A Rākṣasa, or demon.<BR> III. f. पा.<BR> 1. A leech.<BR> 2. A female fiend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपायिन्
रक्तपायिन् रक्त-पायिन् (vb. रङ्ज्),<BR> I. m. A bug.<BR> II. f. नी, A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तफेनज|रक्तफेनजः
रक्तफेनज रक्त-फेन-ज, m. A part of the body, apparently intending the lungs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्
रक्ष् रक्ष् (perhaps a desider. of रञ्ज्, without reduplication), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 8836).<BR> 1. To preserve, Man. 7, 213; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b " target="_blank">Page0752-b + 43</a>] Pañc. i. d. 402 (Ātm.).<BR> 2. To spare, Pañc. iii. d. 253.<BR> 3. To guard, to keep, Vikr. 18, 6; Hit. i. d. 194, M.M. (with gen. in the sense of a dat.); to protect from (abl.), MBh. 3, 8762.<BR> 4. To tend, to keep, Man. 9, 328.<BR> 5. To govern, Man. 7, 36.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. सु-रक्षित, Well guarded, Nal. 3, 10. धर्म-रक्षिता, f. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 14.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. दूरक्ष्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Difficult to be guarded, Mṛcch. 65, 17.<BR> --Caus. To protect, Pañc. 70, 13.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To assist, Bhag. 1, 10.<BR> 2. To defend, to protect, MBh. 4, 161; Pañc. i. d. 395.<BR> 3. To guard, MBh. 1, 5616.<BR> 4. To command, Bhag. 1, 10. अभिरक्षित, Cultivated, Pañc. i. d. 254.<BR> --With आ आ, comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. दुस्-आ-रक्ष्य + तम, Most difficult to be protected, Rām. 2, 52, 66.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To preserve, MBh. 1, 6195.<BR> 2. To protect, Pañc. 215, 7; MBh. 3, 14366.<BR> 3. To restrain, Man. 9, 10.<BR> 4. To govern, Man. 7, 142.<BR> 5. To keep, Rām. 2, 96, 38.<BR> 6. To conceal, MBh. 3, 14717.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To save, Pañc. v. d. 89.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To protect, Man. 7, 135; Pañc. iii. d. 9.<BR> 2. To keep off, Rām. 1, 32, 2.<BR> --Cf. probably ἀρκέω, ἀλκτήρ, ἀλαλκτήρ (frequent.), ἄλξις, ἀλέξω; Lat. arx; Goth. ga-rehsns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष|रक्षः
रक्ष रक्ष् + अ,<BR> I. m. One who guards, Lass. 34, 8.<BR> II. m., and f. क्षा.<BR> 1. Preserving, guarding, Pañc. 184, 8; protecting, protection, Pañc. 157, 7.<BR> 2. (i. e. रञ्ज् + त, cf. रक्ता, s. v. रञ्ज्), Lac.<BR> III. f. क्षा.<BR> 1. Ashes.<BR> 2. A sort of bracelet, an amulet, Śāk. 105, 12 (Prākṛ.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्ररक्ष
क्षेत्र- + रक्ष क्षेत्र- + रक्ष, m. a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a " target="_blank">Page0753-a + 43</a>] field-guard, Pañc. 248, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्ष|गोरक्षः
गो- + रक्ष गो- + रक्ष,<BR> I. m. a cowhered.<BR> II. n. keeping cattle, MBh. 2, 525.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ररक्ष
चक्र- + रक्ष चक्र- + रक्ष, m. two men who take care of the wheels of a chariot, MBh. 1, 5467.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगररक्षा
नगर- + रक्षा नगर- + रक्ष, f. government of a town, Mṛcch. 148, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररक्ष|पुररक्षः
पुर- + रक्ष पुर- + रक्ष, m. the watchman of a town, Daśak. 26, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनारक्ष|सेनारक्षः
सेना- + रक्ष सेना- + रक्ष, m. a guard, a sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षक|रक्षकः
रक्षक रक्ष् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who or what protects, who tends, Man. 8, 102.<BR> II. m. A protector, a guardian, Hit. 91, 1, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षक
अ- + रक्षक अ- + रक्षक, adj. imprudent, Pañc. 129, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षक|अङ्गरक्षकः
अङ्ग- + रक्षक अङ्ग- + रक्षक, m. a life-guard, Pañc. 156, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षक
गो- + रक्षक गो- + रक्षक, adj. keeping cattle, Man. 8, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिरक्षक|भूमिरक्षकः
भूमि- + रक्षक भूमि- + रक्षक, m. a swift horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यरक्षक
शस्य- + रक्षक शस्य- + रक्षक, m. a watchman over a field of corn, Hit. 81, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षण|रक्षणं|रक्षणः
रक्षण रक्षण, i. e. रक्ष् + अन, n. Preserving, protecting, Hit. 114, 7; Pañc. iv. d. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षपाल|रक्षपालः
रक्षपाल रक्ष-पाल, m. One who guards, Pañc. 217, 4; 232, 2; probably it is to be changed to रक्षापाल, cf. रक्षापुरुष, Pañc. 229, 6, the name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्
रक्षस् रक्ष् + अस् (perhaps a kind of euphemism, cf. Εὐμενίδες, denoting the Ἐριννύες), n. A Rākṣasa, or evil spirit, Vikr. 54, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिक|रक्षिकः
रक्षिक रक्षिक, i. e. रक्ष + इक (adj. or m.?), A watchman, a policeman, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 18; 199, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितृ
रक्षितृ रक्ष् + इतृ, m. One who protects, Pañc. i. d. 391; a protector, a guard, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षितृ
अ- + रक्षितृ अ- + रक्षितृ, m. one who does not protect, Pañc. iii. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिन्
रक्षिन् रक्ष् + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> I. adj. Who or what guards, Vikr. d. 5.<BR> II. m. A policeman, Śāk. p. 73, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगररक्षिन्
नगर-, नगरी- + रक्षिन् नगर-, नगरी- + रक्षिन्, and पुर-, m. the watchman of a town, a policeman, Mṛcch. 140, 17; MBh. 13, 6216; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b " target="_blank">Page0753-b + 38</a>] Kathās. 13, 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीरक्षिन्
नगर-, नगरी- + रक्षिन् नगर-, नगरी- + रक्षिन्, and पुर-, m. the watchman of a town, a policeman, Mṛcch. 140, 17; MBh. 13, 6216; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b " target="_blank">Page0753-b + 38</a>] Kathās. 13, 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरक्षिन्
पशु- + रक्षिन् पशु- + रक्षिन्, m. a herdsman, Man. 8, 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्ण|रक्ष्णः
रक्ष्ण रक्ष्ण, i. e. रक्ष् + न, m. Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रख्
† रख् रख्, रङ्ख् रङ्ख्, रिख् रिख्, रिङ्ख् रिङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रग्
† रग् रग्, i. 1, Par. To suspect; cf. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघ्
रघ् रघ्, see रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघु|रघुः
रघु रघु, i. e. रङ्घ् + उ,<BR> I. adj. ved. = लघु.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The name of a king, Utt. Rāmac. 96, 3.<BR> 2. pl., and often in comp. words, His descendants, Rām. 3, 49, 57; Megh. 12 (रघु-पति = Rāma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुपत्वन्
रघुपत्वन् रघु-पत् + वन्, adj., f. वरी, Flying swiftly, Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 6.<BR> --With -पत्वन्, cf. Lat. -piter, in acci-piter = ved. आशु-पत्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुष्यद्
रघुष्यद् रघुष्यद्, i. e. रघु-स्यन्द्, adj. Moving quickly, Chr. 290, 7 = Rigv. i. 64, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क|रंक|रङ्कः
रङ्क रङ्क, adj.<BR> 1. Niggardly.<BR> 2. Slow.<BR> 3. Indigent, poor a beggar, Pañc. i. d. 12; 284.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरङ्क|रणरंक|रणरङ्कः
रण- + रङ्क रण- + रङ्क, m. the part of an elephant's face between his tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्कु|रंकु|रंकुः|रङ्कुः
रङ्कु रङ्कु, m. A sort of deer, the spotted axis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ख्
रङ्ख् रङ्ख्, see रख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग्|रंग्
† रङ्ग् रङ्ग्, रिङ्ग् रिङ्ग्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग|रंग|रङ्गं|रंगः|रङ्गः
रङ्ग रङ्ग, i. e. रञ्ज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Colour, paint.<BR> 2. The place where dancing or acting is exhibited, a stage, Śāk. 4, 12; Daśak. in Chr. 190, 10; a place for an assembly, Nal. 5, 3; 8.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a " target="_blank">Page0754-a + 43</a>] A field of battle, Pañc. 35, 3.<BR> 4. Dancing, acting, Śṛṅgārat. 17.<BR> 5. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 353.<BR> II. n. Tin.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिरङ्ग|केलिरङ्गः
केलि- + रङ्ग केलि- + रङ्ग, m. a pleasure-ground, Lass. 87, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वरङ्ग|पूर्वरंग|पूर्वरङ्गः|पूर्व्वरङ्ग|पूर्व्वरङ्गः
पूर्व- + रङ्ग पूर्व- + रङ्ग, m. the prelude to a drama Śiś. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरङ्ग|राजरंग|राजरङ्गं
राज(न्)- + रङ्ग राज(न्)- + रङ्ग, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्ग|सुरंग|सुरङ्गं|सुरंगः|सुरङ्गः
सु- + रङ्ग सु- + रङ्ग,<BR> I. m. 1. bright colour. 2. the orange.<BR> II. f. गा, crystal.<BR> III. n. 1. red sanders. 2. vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गज|रंगज|रङ्गजं
रङ्गज रङ्ग-ज, n. Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गावतारक|रङ्गावतारकः
रङ्गावतारक रङ्गावतारक, i. e. रङ्ग-अव-तॄ + अक, m. A stage player, Man. 4, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्घ्|रंघ्
रङ्घ् रङ्घ्, i. 1, Ātm. To go, to move swiftly (cf. लङ्घ्), Bhaṭṭ. 14, 15.<BR> --† i. 10, To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रच्
रच् रच्, i. 10, रचय, Par.<BR> 1. To make mechanically, Megh. 75.<BR> 2. To make, Rām. 2, 13, 12; Kathās. 3, 66 (गतागतम्, literally a going and returning, i. e. looking on him and turning away her eye).<BR> 3. To arrange, Gīt. 5, 10.<BR> 4. To compose, Pañc. 5, 11.<BR> 5. To adorn, Megh. 67.<BR> 6. To prepare, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR> 7. To string, Pañc. iii. d. 235.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रचित, Written.<BR> --Caus. रचय, To cause to make, Utt. Rāmac. 127, 14 (मम हृदयं तस्नुन्न् अवधानं रचयति, Causes my heart to fix itself only on him, i. e. fills it with love).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, आरचित, Put on, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 6.<BR> --With वि वि, विरचित,<BR> 1. Contrived, arranged, Pañc. 86, 18; Ragh. 5, 76.<BR> 2. Made, Megh. 19.<BR> 3. Ornamented.<BR> 4. Composed, Megh. 84; written, Pañc. 103, 4.<BR> --Cf. Lat. locare; A.S. logian, To place; Lat. locus; A.S. loh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचना
रचना रच् + अना, f.<BR> 1. Making, work, Lass. 83, 4; Kathās. 26, 283 (कनक-, f. Being made, built, of gold.)<BR> 2. Orderly arrangement.<BR> 3. Dressing [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b " target="_blank">Page0754-b + 43</a>] of the hair.<BR> 4. Stringing flowers.<BR> 5. Suspending garlands.<BR> 6. The arrangement of troops, Pañc. 9, 23.<BR> 7. Composition, Rājat. 5, 380; literary composition.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटरचना
कूट- + रचना कूट- + रचना, f. a trap, Pañc. ii. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशरचना
केश- + रचना केश- + रचना, f. dressing of the hair, Ṛt. 4, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षरचना
पक्ष- + रचना पक्ष- + रचना, f. winning friends, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटरचना
पट- + रचना पट- + रचना, f. art of making cloth, Pañc. 132, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनरचना
वचन- + रचना वचन- + रचना, f. eloquence, Pañc. 68, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितदुर्गरचन
विहित-दुर्ग-रचन विहित-दुर्ग-रचन, adj. having ordered the building of a fortress, Pañc. 148, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहरचना
व्यूह- + रचना व्यूह- + रचना, f. arrangement of troops, Pañc. 9, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज|रजं|रजः
रज रज (see रजस्), m.<BR> 1. Dust, Hit. i. d. 152, M.M.<BR> 2. The pollen of flowers.<BR> 3. The menstrual excretion.<BR> 4. The quality of passion.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरज|नीरजं|नीरजः
नीरज नीरज, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. free from dust, MBh. 13, 3822. 2. free from passion, epithet of Śiva, ib. 13, 1261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजक|रजकः
रजक रजक, i. e. रञ्ज् + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A washerman, Hit. 50, 1.<BR> 2. Cloth.<BR> II. f. की.<BR> 1. A washerman's wife.<BR> 2. A woman in her courses at the third day, Lass. 10, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजत|रजतं
रजत रजत (cf. अर्जुन, रञ्ज्, and राज्),<BR> I. adj. White.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. White, the colour.<BR> 2. Silver, Kir. 5, 41; Rājat. 5, 482.<BR> 3. Gold.<BR> 4. Ivory.<BR> 5. Blood.<BR> 6. A necklace.<BR> 7. The name of the mountain Kailāsa.<BR> 8. An asterism.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजत|महारजतं
महा- + रजत महा- + रजत, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजन|रजनं|रजनः
रजन रजन i. e. रञ्ज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Colouring.<BR> 2. Safflower.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजन|महारजनं
महा- + रजन महा- + रजन, n. 1. safflower. 2. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनि|रजनिः
रजनि and रजनी रजनी̆, i. e. रञ्ज् + अनी̆, f.<BR> 1. Night, Pañc. 128, 11; 248, 5 (नी); Śṛṅgārat. 8 (न्ĭ).<BR> 2. The indigo plant.<BR> 3. Lac.<BR> 4. Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिकर|रजनिकरः
रजनिकर and रजनीकर रजनी̆-कर, m. The moon, Śiś. 9, 38 (नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिचर|रजनिचरः
रजनिचर and रजनीचर रजनी̆-चर, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a " target="_blank">Page0755-a + 43</a>]<BR> I. adj. Wandering at night, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2583 (नी).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Rākṣasa, Rām. 3, 53, 61 (नी).<BR> 2. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीकर|रजनीकरः
रजनीकर रजनीकर, and रजनीचर रजनीचर, see s. v. रजनि˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्
रजस् रजस्,<BR> I. i. e. रञ्ज् + अस्, n. (the original signification was probably ‘Dimness;’ cf. रजनि and Goth. riquis).<BR> 1. Sky, Chr. 289, 7 = Rigv. i. 50, 7.<BR> 2. Dust, Man. 11, 110.<BR> 3. The pollen of a flower, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 4. The menses, Man. 4, 41.<BR> II. i. e. perhaps ऋज् + अस् (cf. ὄρεξις), n. The quality of passion, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. riquis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अ- + रजस् अ- + रजस्, adj. free from dust, Nal. 24, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्
नीरजस् नीरजस्, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. free from dust, Rām. 2, 87, 21 Gorr., 2. free from passion, Rām. 4, 44, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोरजस्
परोरजस् परोरजस्, see s. v. परस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
वि- + रजस् वि- + रजस्,<BR> I. adj. free from passion, Chr. 16, 17.<BR> II. f. a woman who has ceased to menstruate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्
स- + रजस् स- + रजस्, f. a woman during menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्क
ऽरजस्क -रजस् + क, a substitute for रजस् when latter part of comp. adj.; e. g. नीरजस्क, i. e. निस्-, adj.<BR> 1. Free from dust, Rām. 4, 44, 86.<BR> 2. Free from passion, Prab. 117, 18, v. r. वि-, adj. Free from dust, Ragh. 10, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्तुर्
रजस्तुर् रजस्-तुर्, adj. Running over the sky (?), Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्वल|रजस्वलः
रजस्वल रजस् + वल,<BR> I. m. A buffalo.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. A woman who has already her courses, Pañc. iii. d. 219.<BR> 2. A woman in her courses, Man. 3, 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजिष्ठ
रजिष्ठ रजिष्ठ, रजीयंस् राजीयंस्, see ऋजु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जु|रज्जुः
रज्जु रज्जु (probably for original स्रज्यु; cf. स्रज् and O.H.G. striech, strie, stracchian; A.S. streccan; Lat. stringere), f. (m., Pañc. i. d. 376 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b " target="_blank">Page0755-b + 45</a>] erroneously, cf. my translation, n. 385).<BR> 1. A rope, Hit. ii. d. 131; a cord, Pañc. 76, 17.<BR> 2. A lock of braided hair.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटकरज्जु|कर्कटकरज्जुः
कर्कटक- + रज्जु कर्कटक- + रज्जु, f. a rope with a hook resembling the claw of a crab, Daśak. 71, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठरज्जु
काष्ठ- + रज्जु काष्ठ- + रज्जु, f. a rope for tying bundles of sticks, Rām. 1, 4, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशरज्जु|पाशरज्जुः
पाश- + रज्जु पाश- + रज्जु, f. fetter, Kathās. 18, 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जुमात्रत्व
रज्जुमात्रत्व रज्जु-मात्र + त्व, n. Condition of being only a rope, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जुवाल
रज्जुवाल रज्जुवाल, m. A particular bird, Man. 5, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्ज्|रंज्
रञ्ज् रञ्ज्. † i. 1, रज, and i. 4, रज्य, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To dye, to colour, Pañc. 132, 24.<BR> 2. To be attached (perhaps originally different and akin to स्रज्, see रज्जु, and लग्).<BR> 3. † To go (cf. ऋज्). The reflexive pass. takes also the terminations of the Par.<BR> 1. To attach one's self to, Pañc. v. d. 8.<BR> 2. To glow, Utt. Rāmac. 138, 2.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रक्त.<BR> 1. Coloured.<BR> 2. Red, Vikr. d. 124; reddened, d. 136.<BR> 3. Agitated by passion, Man. 4, 64.<BR> 4. Fond, affected with love, Pañc. i. d. 155, 159; attached, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 20.<BR> 5. Pure.<BR> 6. Sporting. Comparat. रक्त + तर, Very attached, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 19. रक्त, m. Red, the colour. n.<BR> 1. Blood, Pañc. 60, 25.<BR> 2. Vermilion.<BR> 3. Minium.<BR> 4. Copper.<BR> 5. Saffron. f. ता,<BR> 1. Lac.<BR> 2. The gunjā plant, Abrus precatorius.<BR> 3. Bengal madder.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. रञ्जय.<BR> 1. To colour, Pañc. 132, 24.<BR> 2. To illuminate, Vikr. d. 60; MBh. 1, 6772.<BR> 3. To cause to be attached, to conciliate, Pañc. 113, 24; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-a " target="_blank">Page0756-a + 42</a>] Man. 7, 19.<BR> 4. † To worship.<BR> II. † रजय, To hunt.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, i. 4,<BR> 1. To grow red and fond, Śiś. 9, 7.<BR> 2. To be attached, Bhag. 11, 36; Pañc. i. d. 335.<BR> 3. To love, Rām. 3, 55, 15.<BR> 4. To dally lasciviously with, Man. 3, 173. अनु-रक्त,<BR> 1. Fond, attached, Pañc. 32, 9; loving, Vikr. 59, 21; propitious, Hit. 53, 18.<BR> 2. Pleased.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be in love, to inspire with affection, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 22.<BR> 2. To conciliate, to win, Daśak. 196, 17.<BR> --With अप अप, अपरक्त (rather रक्त with अप), Discoloured, blanched, Śāk. d. 133.<BR> --With अभि अभि, i. 4, To be rejoiced, Rām. 2, 67, 13.<BR> --Caus. To colour, to illuminate, Rām. 1, 38, 21.<BR> --With उप उप, उपरक्त,<BR> 1. Eclipsed, Rām. 1, 55, 9.<BR> 2. Afflicted with pain or calamity. m. Rāhu.<BR> --With वि वि, i. 4, To grow discoloured (viz. the hair), and disinclined (viz. the servants), Pañc. i. d. 94.<BR> 2. To grow alienated, Mṛcch. 23, 5. विरक्त,<BR> 1. Disinclined, Bhartṛ. 2, 2.<BR> 2. Free from worldly passion, Pañc. 33, 16.<BR> 3. Impassioned.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-विरक्त, adj. faithful, Hit. iii. d. 87.<BR> --With सम् सम्, i. 4, To grow red, MBh. 1, 6443. संरक्त,<BR> 1. Red, MBh. 5, 273.<BR> 2. Inflamed.<BR> 3. Impassioned.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्, अनुसंरक्त, Attached, loving, with acc., Rām. 1, 17, 16.<BR> --Cf. ῥέζω, ῥέγος, ῥεγεύς, ῥήσσω, ῥῆγος, λέγνον; probably A.S. ge-regnian, to colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्त
आ- + रक्त आ- + रक्त, adj. 1. reddish, Vikr. 78, 2. red, Pañc. 64, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवरक्त
जीव- + रक्त जीव- + रक्त, n. the blood of the menses, Suśr. 1, 43, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्त|सुरक्तः
सु- + रक्त सु- + रक्त, adj. 1. well dyed. 2. deep red. 3. strongly impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जक|रंजक|रञ्जकं|रञ्जकः
रञ्जक रञ्ज् + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A dyer, Man. 4, 216.<BR> 2. A stimulus, an inciter of affection.<BR> II. n. Red sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जन|रंजन|रञ्जनं|रञ्जनः
रञ्जन रञ्ज् + अन,<BR> I. m. (?), n.<BR> 1. Dyeing, colouring, Rājat. 5, 381.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b " target="_blank">Page0756-b + 40</a>] Conciliating, befriending, Rājat. 5, 436 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 3. Exciting passion, delighting.<BR> II. n. Red sandal.<BR> III. f. नी, The indigo, and several other plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरञ्जन|लोकरंजन
लोक- + रञ्जन लोक- + रञ्जन, n. gaining public confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरञ्जन|स्त्रीरंजन|स्त्रीरञ्जनं
स्त्री- + रञ्जन स्त्री- + रञ्जन, n. pan eaten with the betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रट्
रट् रट्, i. 1, Par. To yell, Mricch. 157, 10; to cry, Kathās. 18, 109.<BR> --i. 10, Par. † To speak (?).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To call to, Śāk. 55, 5 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रठ्
† रठ् रठ्, i. 1, Par. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्
रण् रण् (developed out of रम्-णा, i. e. रम्, ii. 9), i. 4, and i. 1, Par. i. 4,<BR> 1. To shout.<BR> 2. To rejoice, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10.<BR> --i. 1, To sound, Śiś. 1, 10.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रणित, Sounding, Lass. 21, 1. n. Sound.<BR> --† i. 10, रणय, To go.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, i. 4, To rejoice, Chr. 297, 18 = Rigv. i. 112, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण|रणं|रणः
रण रण् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Noise.<BR> 2. The quill or bow of a lute.<BR> II. m. and n. War, battle, Pañc. 218, 16. Doubled, रण-रण,<BR> 1. m. A musquito.<BR> 2. n. Anxiety.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियरण
प्रिय- + रण प्रिय- + रण, adj. delighting in war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारण
महा- + रण महा- + रण, great battle, Chr. 23, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरणक|रणरणकः
रणरणक रण-रण + क, m.<BR> 1. Regret, care, Utt. Rāmac. 25, 11.<BR> 2. Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डक|रंडकः|रण्डकः
रण्डक रण्डक, m. A barren tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डा
रण्डा रण्डा, f.<BR> 1. A widow, Pañc. i. d. 437 (as an abusive word, cf. the last).<BR> 2. A plant, Salvinia cucullata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्व्
† रण्व् रण्व्, रम्ब् रम्ब्, रिण्व् रिण्व्, रिम्ब् रिम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतर्द्धिक
रतर्द्धिक रतर्द्धिक, i. e. रत (vb. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a " target="_blank">Page0757-a + 41</a>] रम्), -ऋद्धि + क, n.<BR> 1. A day.<BR> 2. Bathing for pleasure.<BR> 3. The aggregate of eight auspicious objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रति|रतिः
रति रति, i. e. रम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Pleasure, Śāk. d. 34; joy, Pañc. iii. d. 258; love, Pañc. 226, 1; the goddess of love, Rām. 3, 52, 27; Kathās. 22, 104.<BR> 2. Passion.<BR> 3. Coition, Pañc. ii. d. 154; sexual intercourse, Pañc. iii. d. 116; enjoyment of love, Vikr. d. 85.<BR> 4. A private part.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरति
धर्म- + रति धर्म- + रति, adj. fond of law or virtue, Ragh. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रती
रती रती = रति, Goddess of love, Nal. 16, 12 (on account of the metre).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतू
रतू रतू, f.<BR> 1. The Ganges of heaven.<BR> 2. A woman who speaks the truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्न|रत्नं
रत्न रत्न, i. e. रम् + त्न, n. (m., MBh. 3, 13182).<BR> 1. A jewel, a gem, Rām. 3, 49, 37; figurat., Pañc. ii. d. 194.<BR> 2. A treasure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 985 (विद्या-, Consisting in science).<BR> 3. Anything the best of its kind; e. g. पुंरत्न, i. e. पुंस्-, n. An excellent man, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2706. स्त्री-, An excellent woman, Vikr. d. 110; cf. भस्त्राका.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समौलिरत्न
स-मौलि- + रत्न स-मौलि- + रत्न, adj. with the crown jewel, Vikr. d. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नभाज्
रत्नभाज् रत्नभाज्, i. e. रत्न-भज्, adj. Acquiring jewels, Rām. 3, 49, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नद्रुममय
रत्नद्रुममय रत्न-द्रुम + मय, adj., f. यी, Resembling corals, Arj. 10, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसंघातमय
रत्नसंघातमय रत्न-संघात + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of a heap of jewels, Sund. 3, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नि|रत्निः
रत्नि रत्नि (curtailed अरत्नि),<BR> I. m. (and f.), A cubit measured from the elbow of the end of the closed fist.<BR> II. m. The closed fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ|रथः
रथ रथ (vb. ऋ), m.<BR> 1. A car, Hit. pr. d. 32, M.M.; a war chariot, Chr. 4, 10.<BR> 2. Any vehicle.<BR> 3. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-b " target="_blank">Page0757-b + 45</a>] limb.<BR> 4. A foot.<BR> 5. The body.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rota; A.S. and O.H.G. rad (probably borrowed); probably ῥέθος; Goth. lithus; A.S. lidh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथ|अतिरथः
अति- + रथ अति- + रथ, m. a pre-eminent warrior who fights in a chariot, Rām. 6, 4, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तिरथ
कीर्ति- + रथ कीर्ति- + रथ and कृत्ति-, m. a proper name, Rām. 1, 71, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडारथ|क्रीडारथः
क्रीडा- + रथ क्रीडा- + रथ, m. a carriage serving for excursions, MBh. 13, 2782.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ररथ|चित्ररथः
चित्र- + रथ चित्र- + रथ,<BR> I. adj. having a brilliant chariot, Bhāg. P. 4, 10, 22.<BR> II. m. 1. the sun. 2. a proper name, MBh. 2, 407.<BR> III. f. था, the name of a river, 6, 341.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरथ|दशरथः
दश(न्)- + रथ दश(न्)- + रथ, and दशपूर्व-, i. e. दश(न्)-पूर्व-, m. Daśaratha, the name of Rāma's father, and of others, Rām. 1, 72, 31 Gorr.; Ragh. 8, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररथ|पत्ररथः
पत्र- + रथ पत्र- + रथ, m. a bird, Rām. 3, 25, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परथ|पुष्परथः
पुष्प- + रथ पुष्प- + रथ, or पुष्य-, m. a carriage for pleasure, Rām. 2, 26, 15 (पुष्प-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमरथ|भीमरथः
भीम- + रथ भीम- + रथ,<BR> I. m. an Asura.<BR> II. f. थी. 1. the seventh night in the seventh month of the seventy-seventh year of a man, supposed to be the ordinary period of human life. 2. the name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरथ|मनोरथः
मनोरथ मनोरथ, i. e. मनस्-, m. wish, desire, Vikr. 13, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागममनोरथ
समागम-मनोरथ समागम-मनोरथ, m. desire of union, Vikr. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्रथ|मरुद्रथः
मरुत्- + रथ मरुत्- + रथ, m. 1. a horse. 2. a car in which idols are carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारथ|महारथः
महा- + रथ महा- + रथ, m. 1. a great chariot, Rām. 3, 55, 32. 2. (having a great chariot), a hero, ib. 3, 53, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुरथ|विष्णुरथः
विष्णु- + रथ विष्णु- + रथ, m. Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथ|सरथः
स- + रथ स- + रथ, adj. with the carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसरथ|हंसरथः
हंस- + रथ हंस- + रथ, m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकट्या
रथकट्या रथकट्या, i. e. रथ-कट + य (cf. कट and निकट), f. A multitude of cars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकर|रथकरः
रथकर रथ-कर, m. A carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकार|रथकारः
रथकार रथ-कार, m.<BR> 1. A carpenter, Pañc. 229, 8.<BR> 2. A man sprung from a male of the माहिष्य and a female of the करणी caste, by profession a coach-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकारत्व
रथकारत्व रथकार + त्व, n. The business of a carpenter, Pañc. 228, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथगर्भक|रथगर्भकः
रथगर्भक रथ-गर्भ + क, m. A car or litter borne on men's shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथतुर्
रथतुर् रथ-तुर्, adj. Overpowering, i. e. drawing, the carriage, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 88, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथधूर्गत
रथधूर्गत रथधूर्गत, i. e. रथ-धुर्-गत (vb. गम्), adj. Gone upon the pole of the chariot, Johns. Sel. 15, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारथि
रथारथि रथारथि, i. e. रथ-रथ + इ, adv. In mutual contact of the chariots, i. e. in closest fight, MBh. 4, 1056.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिक|रथिकः
रथिक रथिक, i. e. रथ + इक, m. The owner of, or rider in, a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन्
रथिन् रथिन्, i. e. रथ + ईन्,<BR> I. adj. Mounted on carriages, Rām. 3, 49, 18.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The owner of, or rider in, a car, lord of chariots, Vikr. d. 100.<BR> 2. A warrior who fights in a car, Draup. 2, 12; Utt. Rāmac. 130, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथिन्
अ- + रथिन् अ- + रथिन्, m. one who is not lord of chariots, Johns. Sel. 6, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन|रथिनः
रथिन रथिन, and रथिर रथिर i. e. रथ + इन् + अ, and with र् for न्, m. The owner of, or rider in, a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ्य|रथ्यः
रथ्य रथ्य, i. e. रथ + य,<BR> I. m. A carriage horse.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. A multitude of cars, Rājat. 5, 241 (warriors?).<BR> 2. A high street.<BR> 3. A place where several roads meet.<BR> III. n. A wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्
रद् रद्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To split, to divide.<BR> 2. To dig.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. lêtan; A.S. laetan (cf. the vedic use of रद्); Lat. rādere, rōdere (cf. रद, रदन), perhaps rădius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद|रदः
रद रद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Splitting, Ghaṭ. 1.<BR> 2. A tooth.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरद|द्विरदः
द्वि- + रद द्वि- + रद,<BR> I. adj. having two teeth.<BR> II. m. an elephant, Rām. 4, 9, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्ररद|वज्ररदः
वज्र- + रद वज्र- + रद, m. a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदन|रदनः
रदन रद् + अन, m. A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदिन्
रदिन् रदिन्, i. e. रद + इन्, m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रध्
रध् रध्. i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To perish (ved.).<BR> 2. To be at one's mercy, Chr. 289, 13 = Rigv. i. 50, 13.<BR> 3. To kill, to hurt.<BR> 4. To be completed, finished, matured.<BR> --Caus. रन्धय,<BR> 1. To give in one's power, Chr. 289, 13 = Rigv. i. 50, 13.<BR> 2. To pain, to torment, Rām. 2, 81, 3.<BR> 3. To destroy, Bhāg. P. 8, 21, 2.<BR> --Cf. A.S. rendan, To rend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तिदेव|रंतिदेव|रंतिदेवः|रन्तिदेवः
रन्तिदेव रन्तिदेव, m.<BR> 1. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. The name of a king, Megh. 46 (cf. Viṣṇu P. 481, n. 18).<BR> 3. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तु|रंतुः|रन्तुः
रन्तु रन्तु, f.<BR> 1. A road.<BR> 2. A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धन|रंधन|रंधनं|रन्धनं
रन्धन रन्धन, i. e. रध्, Caus., + अन,<BR> 1. Destroying, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 28.<BR> 2. Cooking, Pāṇ. ii. 1, 36, Sch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्र|रंध्र|रंध्रं
रन्ध्र रन्ध्र, i. e. रध्, Caus., + र, n.<BR> 1. A hole, a fissure, Pañc. ii. d. 42 (cf. also<BR> 3.).<BR> 2. A cavity, Śiś. 4, 61.<BR> 3. A fault, a defect, a weak point, Pañc. 182, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णरन्ध्र
कर्ण- + रन्ध्र कर्ण- + रन्ध्र, m. n. the auditory passage, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरन्ध्र|नीरंध्र|नीरन्ध्रं
नीरन्ध्र नीरन्ध्र, i. e. निस्-, adj. without an interstice, Utt. Rāmac. 143, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्
रप् रप्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To praise (ved.).<BR> --Cf. लप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रफ्
† रफ् रफ्, रम्फ् रम्फ्, रर्फ् रर्फ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ्
रभ् रभ् (originally = ग्रभ्, लभ्), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry and Man. also Par., Man. 7, 59).<BR> 1. † To desire vehemently.<BR> 2. † To act inconsiderately.<BR> 3. To seize, to take (ved.).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To begin, Man. 7, 299. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a " target="_blank">Page0759-a + 42</a>]<BR> 2. To act strenuously, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. आरब्ध.<BR> 1. Began, done; रहस्य् आरब्धा कथा, A secret conversation, Vikr. d. 51.<BR> 2. Having begun, MBh. 1, 7660.<BR> --Absol. आरभ्य, From. Hit. 91, 21.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, To get back, Rām. 2, 64, 60.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ, To begin, MBh. 3, 10724 (Par.).<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ, To begin, Bhag. 18, 15; Pañc. iii. d. 130. प्रारब्ध, n. An attempt, enterprise, Lass. 1, 6.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To begin, Rām. 1, 45, 13, to undertake, Hit. 44, 6, M.M.<BR> 2. To try, MBh. 1, 2238.<BR> 3. To treat, MBh. 3, 16298.<BR> --With परि परि, To embrace, Vikr. d. 147; MBh. 4, 514. Desider. परि रिप्स, To desire to embrace, Ragh. 13, 32 (Calc.).<BR> --With सम् सम्, संरब्ध,<BR> 1. Exasperated, enraged, Rām. 2, 55, 30.<BR> 2. Agitated, overwhelmed, Nal. 13, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, अभिसंरब्ध, Enraged, Rām. 6, 3, 17.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rabies, robur (labor, see लभ्); probably ῥωβίδας, ῥώννυμι; Goth. arbaiths; A.S. earfedh, earfodh; Goth. liban; A.S. leofian, lifian, lybban; O.H.G. laba, labôn; perhaps A.S. a-refian, To bear, a-raefnan, To take away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंरब्ध
सु- + सम्-रब्ध सु- + सम्-रब्ध, adj.<BR> 1. very enraged, Chr. 31, 20. 2. very agitated, Pañc. 238, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस्
रभस् रभ् + अस्, n. ved.<BR> 1. Zeal (in रभस् + वन्त्, zealous, Rigv. i. 9, 6).<BR> 2. Strength, strengthening food, sacrifice, Rigv. i. 145, 3. See रभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस|रभसः
रभस रभस् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Joyful, Kir. 5, 1.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Joy.<BR> 2. Passion, rage, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 8.<BR> 3. Speed, velocity, Śiś. 9, 72; abl. quickly, Rājat. 5, 190.<BR> 4. Precipitation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 315.<BR> 5. Regret, sorrow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरभस|अतिरभसः
अति- + रभस अति- + रभस, m. (or adv. ˚स + म्), excessive [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b " target="_blank">Page0759-b + 46</a>] precipitation, or, with excessive precipitation, Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोविन्दुग्रहणरभस
अम्भस्-विन्दु-ग्रहण- + रभस अम्भस्-विन्दु-ग्रहण- + रभस, adj. running, desirous to get drops of water, Megh. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभसम्
स-रभस + म् स-रभस + म्} adv. 1. quickly Utt. Rāmac. 144, 11. 2. passionate Lass. 24, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्
रम् रम्, i. 1, Ātm. (in poetry also Par., Man. 2, 223), in the Veda also ii. 9, Par.<BR> 1. To rest, Man. 3, 251; to like to stay, Hit. ii. d. 128.<BR> 2. To be delighted, Pañc. i. d. 429; to rejoice, Rām. 2, 34, 50; Vikr. 19, 1 (रंस्यते भवता, impers. pass. You will be glad), 70, 21.<BR> 3. To rejoice at, with loc., Daśak. in Chr. 181, 5 (to be in love); with instr., MBh. 3, 58.<BR> 4. To have sexual intercourse with (instr.), Hit. 66, 7.<BR> 5. To sport, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 15.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रत.<BR> 1. Beloved, Pañc. v. d. 53.<BR> 2. Intent on, Man. 2, 235 (with loc.); occupied, Pañc. 27, 9.<BR> 3. Inclined, Pañc. 203, 2.<BR> 4. Satisfied, Pañc. 228, 10. n.<BR> 1. Coition, copulation, Pañc. i. d. 224.<BR> 2. A private part.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. रन्तव्य, To be rejoiced at, Mṛcch. 62, 22.<BR> II. रमणीय, Pleasing, agreeable, Vikr. 37, 10; Hit. iv. d. 73 (आपात-, in the beginning); beautiful, Vikr. 65, 18 (विशेष-, most beautiful).<BR> III. रम्य.<BR> 1. The same, Ṛt. 6, 2.<BR> 2. m. The champaca, Michelia Champaca.<BR> 3. f. या.<BR> a. Night.<BR> b. The name of a river.<BR> 4. n. Semen virile.<BR> --Comp.<BR> निस्-आतपत्र-, adj. needing no parasol, i. e. cool, and therefore charming, a Karmadhāraya compound, Vikr. d. 73.<BR> --Caus. रमय,<BR> 1. To exhilarate, MBh. 2, 305. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-a " target="_blank">Page0760-a + 41</a>]<BR> 2. To be delighted, to rejoice, MBh. 3, 11379.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनुरत,<BR> 1. Fond of, attached to.<BR> 2. Beloved.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To be delighted, to rejoice, Rām. 2, 27, 18. अभि-रत,<BR> 1. Intent upon, Chr. 14, 26.<BR> 2. Pleased with.<BR> 3. Engaged in, Rām. 3, 49, 39.<BR> 4. Practising.<BR> --With अव अव, अवरत, Stopped, ceased.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. uninterrupted, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 21. ˚तम्, adv. without stopping, Pañc. 93, 15; incessantly, Pañc. 145, 14.<BR> --With आ आ, Par.<BR> 1. To repose, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 38.<BR> 2. To cease, Man. 2, 73.<BR> 3. To take pleasure, Man. 4, 175. अनत, Ceased, Kir. 5, 6.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To repose, MBh. 1, 6035.<BR> 2. To cease, Ragh. 16, 3 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To rejoice, to dally, MBh. 1, 4183.<BR> --With उप उप, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To cease, Chr. 30, 39; with the ptcple. of the pres. in the sense of the infin., Pañc. 53, 19 (मृगशशकादिन् व्यापादयन् नोप रराम, He did not cease killing deer, hares, etc.).<BR> 2. To desist from, with abl., Daśak. in Chr. 181, 12. उपरत,<BR> 1. Stopped, ceased.<BR> 2. Having ceased, Man. 5, 66.<BR> 3. Having desisted from, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 35.<BR> 4. Dead, Pañc. 98, 3 (he breathed out his last).<BR> --With व्युप वि-उप, व्युपरत, Interrupted, stopped, Mṛcch. 1, 2.<BR> --With नि नि, निरत,<BR> 1. Pleased, satisfied, Man. 3, 45.<BR> 2. Attached to (with loc.), loving, Utt. Rāmac. 57, 5; faithful, Rām. 3, 48, 18.<BR> 3. Engaged in, practising, Nal. 6, 10 (अ-हिंसा-, benevolence).<BR> --With परि परि, Par. To be delighted, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 53.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To cease, Utt. Rāmac. 17, 6; with the ptcple. of the pres. in the sense [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b " target="_blank">Page0760-b + 41</a>] of the infin., Pañc. 93, 16.<BR> 2. To desist, Man. 4, 97.<BR> 3. To cease from, desist from (with abl.), Vikr. d. 39; Pañc. 161, 1. विरत, Stopped, ceased, Śiś. 9, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. uninterrupted, Kir. 5, 6. 2. eternal.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To rejoice, Bhaṭṭ. 19, 30.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. râwa, ruowa (i. e. *रम् + वन्, cf. acc. sing. ruouun), râwên (denomin.), resti, rastjan; A.S. rest, restan; ἠρέμα, νω-λεμ + ής.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरत
देव- + रत देव- + रत, adj. devout, Pañc. 118, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माणरत
निर्माण- + रत निर्माण- + रत, m. the name of a class of deities, MBh. 13, 1372.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरत|सुरतं
सु- + रत सु- + रत,<BR> I. adj. 1. playing, playful. 2. compassionate, tender.<BR> II. n. 1. coition, Hit. iii. 27. 2. sexual intercourse, love, Ṛt. 6, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरसुरत
वर-सु- + रत वर-सु- + रत, adj. very wanton, Hit. ii. d. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम रम् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Pleasing, Kir. 5, 20 (at the end of a comp.).<BR> 2. Dear.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A husband, a lover.<BR> 2. The deity of love.<BR> III. f. मा.<BR> 1. A wife or a mistress, Pañc. i. d. 369 (?).<BR> 2. A name of Lakṣmī, Pañc. 46, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरम|मनोरमं
मनस्- + रम मनस्- + रम, see s. v. मनोरम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमक|रमकः
रमक रम् + अक, m. A lover, a gallant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण|रमणं|रमणः
रमण रमण, i. e. रम् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Delighting, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 11.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A husband, Megh. 85.<BR> 2. A lover, Vikr. d. 89; Pañc. i. d. 196; Śiś. 9, 60.<BR> 3. A name of Kāma.<BR> 4. An ass.<BR> III. f. णी, and णा, A wife, a mistress.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Sporting.<BR> 2. Dalliance, love, Megh. 38.<BR> 3. Coition.<BR> 4. The mons veneris.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पररमण|पररमणः
पर- + रमण पर- + रमण, m. a paramour, Pañc. i. d. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीयता
रमणीयता रमणीय + ता (vb. रम्), f. Agreeableness, charm, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 4; Śāk. 82, 2 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीयत्व
रमणीयत्व रमणीय + त्व, n. Agreeableness, charm, Śāk. 80, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमति|रमतिः
रमति रम् + अति, m.<BR> 1. Love.<BR> 2. Paradise.<BR> 3. A crow.<BR> 4. Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्फ्|रंफ्
रम्फ् रम्फ्, see रफ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्ब्
† रम्ब् रम्ब्, i. 1, Ātm. To sound. See रण्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ्|रंभ्
† रम्भ् रम्भ्, लम्भ् लम्भ्, i. 1, Ātm. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ|रंभः|रम्भः
रम्भ रम्भ,<BR> A. i. e. रभ् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bambu.<BR> 2. The name of a monkey.<BR> II. f. भा.<BR> 1. A plantain, Lass. 79, 16.<BR> 2. The name of an Apsaras, Vikr. 87, 10.<BR> 3. A name of Gaurī.<BR> B. (cf. रम्भ्), f. भा, Lowing, as of a cow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरम्भ
गो-रम्भ गो-रम्भ, m. a proper name, Pañc. 26, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय्
† रय् रय्, लय् लय्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय|रयः
रय रय, i. e. री + अ, m.<BR> 1. The stream of a river, Hit. iii. d. 49.<BR> 2. Speed, Megh. 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुरय
आशु- + रय आशु- + रय, adj. impetuous, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरय
शान्त- + रय शान्त- + रय (vb. शम्), adj. slackened in speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयि
रयि रयि, m. Wealth (cf. रै), Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिष्ठ|रयिष्ठः
रयिष्ठ रयिष्ठ, superl. of रय + वन्त्,<BR> 1. Very fleet.<BR> 2. m. A name of Kuvera, Agni or fire, and Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रर्फ्
रर्फ् रर्फ्, see रफ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रल्लक|रल्लकः
रल्लक रल्लक, m.<BR> 1. A blanket.<BR> 2. An eyelash.<BR> 3. A sort of deer, Śiś. 4, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव|रवः
रव रव, i. e. रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sound, Mālat. 79, 19 (at the end of a comp. adj.); cry, Indr. 1, 3; Rājat. 5, 346; 408.<BR> 2. Talk, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1723; Pañc. i. 30 (false r.; cf. my transl. and Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2542).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलरव|कलरवः
कल- + रव कल- + रव, m. 1. a pleasing sound, Bhartṛ. 1, 35. 2. (properly, uttering a pleasing sound), a pigeon. 3. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टारव|घण्टारवः
घण्टा- + रव घण्टा- + रव,<BR> I. m. the sound of a bell, Pañc. 229, 15.<BR> II. f. वा, crotalaria of various species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डरव
चण्ड- + रव चण्ड- + रव, m. the name of a jackal, Pañc. 62, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरव
नीरव नीरव, i. e. निस्-, adj. noiseless, Ragh. 8, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमवेगरव
भीम-वेग- + रव भीम-वेग- + रव, m. a proper name (fearful [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b " target="_blank">Page0761-b + 40</a>] in velocity and noise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनकाकुरव|मदनकाकुरवः
मदन-काकु- + रव मदन-काकु- + रव, m. a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणारवा
वीणा- + रवा वीणा- + रव, f. वा, a proper name, Pañc. 81, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गरव
शार्ङ्ग- + रव शार्ङ्ग- + रव, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवण|रवणं|रवणः
रवण रवण, partly रु + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Sounding, crying.<BR> 2. Sharp, hot.<BR> 3. Unsteady.<BR> 4. Jesting.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The Indian cuckoo.<BR> 2. A camel.<BR> III. n. Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवथ|रवथः
रवथ रवथ, i. e. रु + अथ, m. The Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवि|रविः
रवि रवि, m.<BR> 1. The sun, Pañc. 189, 23; Man. 1, 23.<BR> 2. A proper name, Draup. 2, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशना
रशना रशना, see रसन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मि|रश्मिः
रश्मि रश्मि (i. e. रश् + मि; with रश् cf. probably Lat. laqueus, cf. रसना), m.<BR> 1. A rein, Nal. 19, 22.<BR> 2. A ray of light, Pañc. 162, 11.<BR> 3. An eyelash.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णरश्मि|उष्णरश्मिः
उष्ण- + रश्मि उष्ण- + रश्मि and तिग्म-, m. the sun, Ragh. 5, 4; Śiś. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरश्मि|शीतरश्मिः
शीत- + रश्मि शीत- + रश्मि, m. the moon, Śṛṅgārat. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमरश्मि
स्यूम- + रश्मि स्यूम- + रश्मि, m. a proper name, Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. i. 112, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्
1. रस् रस्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound, Gīt. 10, 6.<BR> 2. To roar, MBh. 3, 14602.<BR> 3. To sing, Śiś. 6, 70.<BR> 4. † To praise.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रसित, Sounded. n.<BR> 1. The rattling of thunder, Ghaṭ. 14.<BR> 2. Sound.<BR> --Cf. s. v.<BR> --Frequent. रारस्, To cry loudly, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 96.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनु-रसित, Accompanied by howling, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 2.<BR> --With आ आ, To lament, Nal. 1, 11. आरसित, n. Cry, Mālav. d. 41.<BR> --With वि वि, To cry, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 42.<BR> --Cf. Goth. razda; O.H.G. rartjan; A.S. reordian; O.H.G. rerjan; A.S. rarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्
2. रस् रस्, i. 10, रसय and रसू-पय [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a " target="_blank">Page0762-a + 47</a>] (rather a denomin. derived from रस), Par.<BR> 1. To taste, Śiś. 10, 27.<BR> 2. † To love. Desider. रिरसयिष, To wish to taste, Śiś. 11, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस|रसं|रसः
रस रस, probably from रम्,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Taste (as sweet, salt), Pañc. 61, 11.<BR> 2. Pleasure, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 1; enjoyment, Śāk. d. 179; Pañc. ii. d. 175; charm, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR> 3. Inclination, Hit. iii. d. 115 (साहस-एकान्त-रस-अनु-वर्तिन्, adj. One who follows only his inclination to inconsiderate haste); love, Utt. Rāmac. 26, 2.<BR> 4. Juice, Man. 2, 77; liquid, 3, 159; Śiś. 9, 46; a dish, Vikr. 19, 1.<BR> 5. Essence, Hit. iv. d. 94 (तद्-, Its best).<BR> 6. Condiment, Hit. iii. d. 56.<BR> 7. Water.<BR> 8. The essential juice of the body, whence blood, etc., are supposed to be engendered.<BR> 9. Semen virile.<BR> 10. Poison.<BR> 11. Gum myrrh.<BR> 12. Quicksilver.<BR> 13. A mineral substance, as sulphur, borax.<BR> 14. Taste, sentiment, emotion, as an object of poetry, as love, terror, etc., Bhartṛ. 2, 21; Rām. 1, 4, 7; Pañc. v. d. 44 (? nine रसस् of music).<BR> 15. Affection of the mind, Utt. Rāmac. 50, 8; passion, Vikr. d. 36; love, Vikr. d. 40.<BR> II. f. सा.<BR> 1. A river of the lower regions, Chr. 297, 12 = Rigv. i. 112, 12.<BR> 2. The tongue.<BR> 3. The earth.<BR> 4. A grape.<BR> 5. The name of several plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अ- + रस अ- + रस, adj. tasteless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरस|अनुरसः
अनु- + रस अनु- + रस, m. a secondary flavour, Suśr. 1, 224, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नरस|अन्नरसः
अन्न- + रस अन्न- + रस, m. the essential properties of food, Nal. 5, 37 (the knowledge of them).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतरस|अमृतरसः
अमृत- + रस अमृत- + रस,<BR> I. m. the amṛta essence, the drink of immortality, Bhartṛ. 3, 77 (काव्य-, poetical works which are like the essence of amṛta).<BR> II. adj., f. सा, having an amṛta-like juice, Pañc. 248, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरस|इक्षुरसः
इक्षु- + रस इक्षु- + रस, m. the juice of the sugar-cane, Pañc. i. d. 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरस|एकरसः
एक- + रस एक- + रस,<BR> I. m. only pleasure, Rām. 1, 9, 8.<BR> II. adj., f. सा. 1. pleased with one object only, ib. 2, 67, 20 (v. r. Gorr.). 2. unchanged, Utt. Rāmac. 102, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकरस|कनकरसः
कनक- + रस कनक- + रस, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b " target="_blank">Page0762-b + 45</a>] m. 1. melted gold, Śāk. 99, 15. 2. yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरस|कामरसः
काम- + रस काम- + रस, m. semination, MBh. 1, 3812.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्ररस|क्षुद्ररसः
क्षुद्र- + रस क्षुद्र- + रस, m. honey, Bhāg. P. 5, 13, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धरस|गन्धरसः
गन्ध- + रस गन्ध- + रस, m. myrrh, MBh. 5, 777.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरस|गोरसः
गो- + रस गो- + रस, m. 1. milk, MBh. 5, 1143. 2. buttermilk. 3. coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरस|नीरसः
नीरस नीरस, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. sapless, vain, Vikr. d. 30. 2. insipid, Bhartṛ. 3, 16. 3. merciless, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 6. 4. charmless, Pañc. iv. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट पिष्ट (vb. पिष्)-, m. water mixed with flour, MBh. 1, 5186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपातरस
प्रणिपात- + रस प्रणिपात- + रस, m. the name of a spell, Rām. 1, 31, 5 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरस|यक्षरसः
यक्ष- + रस यक्ष- + रस, m. spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथारसम्
यथा-रस + म् यथा-रस + म्, adv. according to the sentiments, Mālav. 20, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
वि- + रस वि- + रस,<BR> I. adj. 1. insipid. 2. painful, Utt. Rāmac. 157, 6.<BR> II. m. pain, Utt. Rāmac. 18, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारैकरस
शृङ्गार-एक- + रस शृङ्गार-एक- + रस, adj. only pleased with love, Vikr. d. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
स- + रस स- + रस, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धरस|सिद्धरसः
सिद्ध- + रस सिद्ध- + रस,<BR> I. adj. mineral, metallic.<BR> II. m. 1. quicksilver. 2. an alchymist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरस|सुरसं|सुरसः
सु- + रस सु- + रस,<BR> I. adj. 1. well-flavoured. 2. sweet. 3. elegant.<BR> II. m. a plant, Vitex trifolia.<BR> III. f. सा, and n. 1. holy basil. 2. the name of several plants.<BR> IV. f. सा, Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरस|स्वरसः
स्व- + रस स्व- + रस, m. 1. proper taste. 2. proper flavour. 3. expressed juice. 4. sediment of oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुरस
स्वादु- + रस स्वादु- + रस, f. सा, 1. the hog-plum. 2. a grape. 3. vinous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसक|रसकः
रसक रस + क, m. Stewed or boiled meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज|रसजं|रसजः
रसज रस-ज, m.<BR> 1. Any insect engendered by the fermentation of liquids.<BR> 3. Molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्ञ|रसज्ञः
रसज्ञ रस-ज्ञ,<BR> I. adj. Acquainted with tastes, sentiments, etc.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An alchymist.<BR> 2. A physician.<BR> 3. A poet.<BR> III. f. ज्ञा, The tongue, Bhāṣāp. 52; 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसन|रसनं|रसनः
रसन रस् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sounding, tinkling.<BR> 2. Tasting, Bhāṣāp. 39; Bhag. 15, 9.<BR> II. f. (written also रशना, and perhaps akin to रश्मि, q. cf.).<BR> 1. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a " target="_blank">Page0763-a + 41</a>] woman's girdle, Vikr. d. 115.<BR> 2. The tongue, Bhāṣāp. 100.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरसन
नीरसन नीरसन, i. e. निस्-रसन, adj. without a girdle, Kir. 5, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसमय|रसमयः
रसमय रस + मय, adj., f. यी, Delightful, Utt. Rāmac. 128, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवन्त्|रसवत्
रसवन्त् रस + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Succulent, Bhartṛ. 3, 97.<BR> 2. Agreeable, Vikr. d. 62.<BR> 3. Endowed with the रसस्, love, etc., Utt. Rāmac. 111, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायन|रसायनं|रसायनः
रसायन रसायन, perhaps रस-अयन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Buttermilk.<BR> 2. Poison.<BR> 3. A medicine preventing old age and prolonging life, Pañc. ii. d. 80; elixir, Hit. i. d. 209, M.M. (प्रीति-, Elixir-like joy).<BR> 4. Medicine, a remedy, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 2.<BR> 5. Alchymy, chemistry.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An alchymist.<BR> 2. Garuḍa.<BR> III. f. नी, A vessel conveying nutrition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक रसिक, i. e. रस + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Having taste, flavoured.<BR> 2. Tasteful, as a composition.<BR> 3. Impassioned, inclined, Hit. 103, 3 (साहस-एक-, Inclined only to inconsiderate haste).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. An elephant.<BR> 3. A libertine.<BR> III. f. का (cf. रसन).<BR> 1. A woman's girdle.<BR> 2. The tongue.<BR> 3. Curds with sugar and spice.<BR> 4. Molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिकता
रसिकता रसिक + ता, f. Pleasure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित रसित, probably रस + इत, adj. Gilded, plated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्न|रस्नं
रस्न रस्न, n. A thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य रस्य, i. e. रस + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Savoury, Bhag. 17, 8.<BR> 2. Juicy.<BR> II. n. Blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह्
रह् रह् (for original रध्), i. 1, and i. 10, रहय, Par. To quit, to leave.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रहित.<BR> 1. Abandoned, Rām. 3, 52, 5.<BR> 2. Deprived of, without, Rām. 1, 70, 35. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b " target="_blank">Page0763-b + 44</a>] n. Privacy; loc. sing. Privately, Chr. 37, 2.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि,<BR> 1. To abandon, Rām. 3, 51, 17.<BR> 2. With instr. To separate from, Vikr. d. 114. विरहित,<BR> 1. Abandoned, left, Śiś. 9, 75.<BR> 2. Deprived of, without, Vikr. d. 33; Nal. 10, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. λανθάνω, ἔλαθον, ἀλήθης, probably ἔρημος; Lat. latere (cf. रुधिर); also perhaps λόχος, λέχος (cf. रहस्); Lat. lectum, legere; Goth. ligan, lagjan; A.S. lecgan, licgan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहित
अ- + रहित अ- + रहित, adj. 1. not separated, Vikr. 86, 11.<BR> 2. abounding in, Kir. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
रहस् रह् + अस्,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Secrecy, Pañc. 253, 25; Chr. 5, 6; Vikr. d. 51 (loc., secretly).<BR> 2. A secret, Rājat. 5, 317; a religious or mystic truth.<BR> 3. A place of privacy, a hiding-place, solitude, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 23; Lass. 55, 15.<BR> 4. Copulation, Pañc. i. d. 197 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2366).<BR> 5. A privity.<BR> II. adv. Secretly, privily, Pañc. 192, 23; Chr. 53, 22.<BR> --Cf. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहःस्थ
रहःस्थ रहःस्थ, or रहस्थ रहस्थ, i. e. रहस्-स्थ, adj. Being alone, Pañc. 45, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्य|रहस्यं
रहस्य रहस् + य,<BR> I. adj. Secret, Man. 11, 247; concealed, 4, 144; mysterious.<BR> II. n. A secret, Pañc. 129, 2; a mystery, Lass. 20, 20.<BR> III. f. या, The name of a river.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरहस्य
देव- + रहस्य देव- + रहस्य, n. a secret of the gods, MBh. 15, 964.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरहस्य
स- + रहस्य स- + रहस्य, adj. magical (as weapons), Utt. Rāmac. 11, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रयोगरहस्य
स-प्रयोग- + रहस्य स-प्रयोग- + रहस्य, adj. with the charms or spells for employing (the magic weapons), Johns. Sel. 4, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रही
रही रही, A substitute for रहस् before the derivatives of कृ and भू; cf. भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा रा, ii. 2, Par. (in the ved. also Ātm.), To give, Bhāg. P. 4, 27, 25.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रात.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ved. रातम् अस्तु with Lat. ratum esto and reor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तिरात
कीर्ति- + रात कीर्ति- + रात, and कृति-, m. a proper name, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a " target="_blank">Page0764-a + 45</a>] Rām. 1, 71, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका राका, f.<BR> 1. Full moon, or the day of full moon, Sāh. D. p. 323, 19.<BR> 2. A girl in whom menstruation has commenced.<BR> 3. Itch.<BR> 4. The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस राक्षस, i. e. रक्षस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी.<BR> 1. Belonging to a Rākṣasa, demoniacal, Rām. 3, 48, 11; Lass. 18, 3.<BR> 2. Infested by demons, Man. 3, 280.<BR> 3. (see विधि), A form of marriage, Man. 3, 33.<BR> II. m. An evil spirit, Pañc. 182, 22.<BR> III. f. सी,<BR> 1. A female demon, Hiḍ. 2, 16.<BR> 2. A large tusk.<BR> 3. A sort of perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलराक्षसी
जल-राक्षसी जल-राक्षसी, f. a female demon of the water, MBh. 3, 16255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मराक्षस|ब्रह्मराक्षसः
ब्रह्मराक्षस ब्रह्मराक्षस, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. a demon of the brahmanical class, Man. 12, 60; Pañc. 182, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषराक्षस|मानुषराक्षसः
मानुष- + राक्षस मानुष- + राक्षस, m. a Rākṣasa-like man, a Rākṣasa in the shape of man, Bhartṛ. 2, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेवासुरराक्षस
सदेवासुर- + राक्षस सदेवासुर- + राक्षस, i. e. स-देव-असुर-, adj. with the gods, Asuras, and Rākṣasas, Chr. 41, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राख्
† राख् राख्, लाख् लाख्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To grow dry.<BR> 2. To adorn.<BR> 3. To suffice.<BR> 4. To prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राग|रागः
राग राग, i. e. रञ्ज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Colour, Pañc. 203, 5; Vikr. d. 26 (red colour).<BR> 2. Being subdued by affections, MBh. 13, 12427; Ṛt. 6, 23.<BR> 3. Affection, love, Pañc. iii. d. 266; Daśak. in Chr. 197, 6; desire, sorrow, joy, Rājat. 5, 382.<BR> 4. Wrath, Pañc. 29, 17.<BR> 5. Envy.<BR> 6. Greediness.<BR> 7. Passion, Hit. iv. d. 83 (नि-वृत्त-, adj. Free from passions).<BR> 8. A mode of music, of which six are enumerated, Pañc. 248, 6.<BR> 9. Harmony, Śāk. d. 5.<BR> 10. A king.<BR> II. f. गी, A sort of grain, Eleusine corocana.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराग|अंगराग|अङ्गरागः
अङ्ग- + राग अङ्ग- + राग, m. paint, unguent, powder for smearing and perfuming the body, Ṛt. 6, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग|अपरागः
अप- + राग अप- + राग, m. enmity, Man. 7, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमराग
कृत्रिम- + राग कृत्रिम- + राग, m. an artificial colour, Vikr. d. 40. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b " target="_blank">Page0764-b + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मराग|पद्मरागः
पद्म- + राग पद्म- + राग, m. a ruby, Hit. pr. d. 44, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पराग|पुष्परागः
पुष्प- + राग पुष्प- + राग, m. a topaz, Ragh. 18, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराग|विरागः
वि- + राग वि- + राग, m. 1. disinclination, hatred, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1156. 2. the absence of desire or passion, indifference, disregard of all sensual enjoyment, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतराग|वीतरागः
वीत- + राग वीत- + राग, i. e. वि-इत-,<BR> I. adj. 1. colourless. 2. exempt from passions, Hit. 42, 10, M.M.<BR> II. m. a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
स- + राग स- + राग, adj. 1. coloured. 2. impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राराग|हरिद्रारागः
हरिद्रा- + राग हरिद्रा- + राग, adj. fickle, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागमञ्जरिका
रागमञ्जरिका रागमञ्जरिका, i. e. राग-मञ्जरी + क, f. The wicked Rāgamañjarī, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागारु|रागारुः
रागारु रागारु, adj. One who excites hopes and disappoints them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन् रागिन्, i. e. राग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Coloured.<BR> 2. Red, Pañc. i. d. 225.<BR> 3. Impassioned, agitated by affections, Bhag. 18, 27; given to passions, Hit. iv. d. 83.<BR> 4. Loving, Śiś. 9, 38; being in love, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 23.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A painter.<BR> 2. A lover.<BR> III. f. गिणी.<BR> 1. A shrewd and intriguing woman.<BR> 2. A modification of a musical mode, personified as the wife of the Rāga, Lass. 39, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागिन्
वि- + रागिन् वि- + रागिन् (properly, विराग + इन्, see रग), adj. void of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
† राघ् राघ्, लाघ् लाघ्, i. 1, Ātm. To be able or equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघव|राघवः
राघव राघव, i. e. रघु + अ, patronym., m. (cf. रघु),<BR> 1. A descendant of Raghu; a name of Rāma, Rām. 3, 48, 8.<BR> 2. A sort of fish.<BR> 3. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कव|रांकव|राङ्कवं
राङ्कव राङ्कव, i. e. रङ्क + अ, adj. Made of the hair of the रङ्कु, Rām. 3, 49, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्ग
राङ्ग राङ्ग, A proper name, Lass. 67, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
1. राज् राज्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a " target="_blank">Page0765-a + 43</a>] To shine, Vikr. d. 160; to beam, Rām. 1, 1, 32; Chr. 25, 52 (राजतम्, anomal. instead of राजन्तम्).<BR> 2. ved. To govern (akin to ऋज्, originally रज्).<BR> --Caus. राजय, To illuminate.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. राजित.<BR> 1. Illuminated.<BR> 2. Adorned, Kir. 5, 9.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To shine, MBh. 3, 10960.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus. उपराजित, Illuminated, Pañc. v. d. 12.<BR> --With निस् निस्, नीराजित, Shining, Utt. Rāmac. 150, 12.<BR> --With परि परि, To be very resplendent, Rām. 3, 49, 3.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To shine forth, Pañc. v. d. 2.<BR> 2. To shine, ib. i. d. 373; Rām. 3, 52, 25.<BR> --Caus. To cause to beam, Rām. 2, 26, 2. विराजित,<BR> 1. Illuminated, splendid, Kir. 5, 4; Nal. 5, 3.<BR> 2. Manifested.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, To shine, to beam, Rām. 2, 26, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
2. राज् राज्, latter part of comp. nouns,<BR> I. adj. Shining.<BR> II. curtailed for राजन्, m. A king, Hiḍ. 1, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यराज्
अरण्य- + राज् अरण्य- + राज्, m. king of the forest, epithet of the lion and the tiger, Nal. 12, 13; 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरराज्
असुर- + राज् असुर- + राज्, m. king of the Asuras, epithet of the Asura Baka (see वक), MBh. 1, 6208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुराज्
इन्दु- + राज् इन्दु- + राज् and उडु-, m. the moon, Pañc. i. d. 104; Rām. 4, 5, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकराज्
एक- + राज् एक- + राज्, 1. adj. only shining, Bhāg. P. 3, 5, 24. 2. m. an absolute king, ib. 1, 18, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुराज्
क्रतु- + राज् क्रतु- + राज्, m. the principal sacrifice, Man. 11, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिराज्
गिरि- + राज् गिरि- + राज्, m. the king of the mountains, probably the Himālaya, MBh. 6, 3419.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणराज्
तृण- + राज् तृण- + राज्, m. the palmyra tree, Rām. 6, 91, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज्
देव- + राज् देव- + राज्, m. epithet of Indra and Nahuṣa, Chr. 4, 20; MBh. 13, 4788.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज्|धर्म्मराज्
धर्म- + राज् धर्म- + राज्, m. epithet of Yama, Yudhiṣṭhira, and of a king of the herons, Man. 7, 7; Draup. 8, 13; MBh. 12, 6350.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराज्
नाग- + राज् नाग- + राज्, m. the king of the serpents, Mārk. P. 23, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगराज्
मृग- + राज् मृग- + राज्, m. a lion, Śiś. 9, 18 (पतंग-, m. the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b " target="_blank">Page0765-b + 47</a>] lion-like run).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज्
यक्ष- + राज् यक्ष- + राज्, m. Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वराज्
विश्व- + राज् विश्व- + राज्, and in some cases, विश्वा-, m. an universal sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्
स्व- + राज् स्व- + राज्, m. Brahman or Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज|राजः
ऽराज -राज, a substitute for राजन्, when latter part of comp. words, m. A king.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. reiks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरराज|अमरराजः
अमर- + राज अमर- + राज, m. king of the gods, epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरशत्रुराज
अमर-शत्रु- + राज अमर-शत्रु- + राज, m. epithet of Rāvaṇa, Rām. 6, 35, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिराज|आदिराजः
आदि- + राज आदि- + राज, m. the first or primeval king, epithet of Manu and of a son of Kuru, Rām. 1, 6, 4; MBh. 1, 3741.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षराज|ऋक्षराजः
ऋक्ष- + राज ऋक्ष- + राज, m. 1. the king of the bears, Rām. 6, 6, 12. 2. the king of the stars, epithet of the moon, Vikr. 39, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणराज|तृणराजः
तृण- + राज तृण- + राज, m. the palmyra tree, MBh. 4, 1309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज|देवराजः
देव- + राज देव- + राज, m. Indra, Rām. 6, 34, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजराज|द्विजराजः
द्विज- + राज द्विज- + राज and नक्षत्र-, m. the moon, Ragh. 5, 23; Rām. 5, 18, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज|धर्मराजः|धर्म्मराज|धर्म्मराजः
धर्म- + राज धर्म- + राज, m. epithet of Yama and Yudhiṣṭhira, MBh. 13, 3471; Hariv. 842.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदराज|नदराजः
नद- + राज नद- + राज, the king of the rivers, i. e. the Sindhu, Śiś. 9, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराज|नागराजः
नाग- + राज नाग- + राज, 1. the king of the serpents, Kathās. 22, 209. 2. a great elephant, MBh. 4, 1679.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृराज
पितृ- + राज पितृ- + राज, m. the king of the Manes, i. e. Yama, Sāv. 5, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगराज|भुजगराजः
भुजग- + राज भुजग- + राज, m. the king of the snakes, epithet of Śeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गराज|भृङ्गराजः
भृङ्ग- + राज भृङ्ग- + राज, m. 1. a sort of bird (Lanius malabaricus), Lass. 52, 18. 2. the humble bee. 3. a sort of shrub. 4. a particular sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराज|महाराजः
महा- + राज महा- + राज, m. 1. a sovereign, king, Vikr. 37, 9. 2. a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगराज|मृगराजः
मृग- + राज मृग- + राज, m. a lion, Vikr. 70, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज|यक्षराजः
यक्ष- + राज यक्ष- + राज, m. Kuvera, Chr. 62, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज|युवराजः
युवराज युवराज, i. e. युवन्-, m. a young prince, especially the heir apparent, Pañc. 156, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराज|राजराजः
राजराज राजराज, i. e. राजन्-, m. 1. an universal monarch, Kir. 5, 51. 2. Kuvera. 3. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नराज|विघ्नराजः
विघ्न- + राज विघ्न- + राज, m. Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानराज|विमानराजः
विमान- + राज विमान- + राज, m. the driver of a chariot (of the gods), Utt. Rāmac. 55, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलराज|शैलराजः
शैल- + राज शैल- + राज, m. the king of the mountains, epithet of the Himālaya, Megh. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुराज|सिन्धुराजः
सिन्धु- + राज सिन्धु- + राज, m. Jayadratha, the king of Sindh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखराज
सुख- + राज सुख- + राज, m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरराज
सुर- + राज सुर- + राज, m. Indra, Rājat. 5, 157. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a " target="_blank">Page0766-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभराज
सौभ- + राज सौभ- + राज, m. the king of the Saubhas, Chr. 18, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजक|राजकं|राजकः
राजक राजक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. राज् + अक, Splendid.<BR> 2. राजन् + क, A substitute for राजन् when latter part of comp. adj.; e. g. अ-, adj. Having no king, Man. 7, 3.<BR> II. m. A king.<BR> III. n. An assemblage of kings.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजक|महाराजकः
महा- + राजक महा- + राजक, and महा-राजिक, m. a kind of demigod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराजक
स- + राजक स- + राजक, adj. together with the king, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 519.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकीय|राजकीयः
राजकीय राजकीय, i. e. राजन् + क + ईय, adj. Royal, Lass. 13, 17; 31, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजघ|राजघः
राजघ राजघ, i. e. राजन्-हन्,<BR> I. m. A king killer.<BR> II. adj. Sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत|राजतं
राजत राजत, i. e. रजत + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of silver, Man. 2, 202; Rājat. 5, 12.<BR> II. n. Silver (ŚKD.), Rām. 3, 49, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतस्
राजतस् राजतस्, i. e. राजन् + तस्, From a king, Man. 4, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजता
राजता राजता, i. e. राजन् + ता, f. Royalty, Hit. iii. d. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्
राजन् राज् + अन् (or rather ऋज्, properly रज्, + अन्, cf. Lat. rĕgere),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A king, Chr. 3, 6.<BR> 2. One of the Kṣatriya caste, Man. 2, 32.<BR> 3. A master.<BR> 4. The moon.<BR> 5. Indra.<BR> 6. A Yakṣa.<BR> II. f. राज्ञी.<BR> 1. A queen, Chr. 54, 18; a princess, Chr. 18, 3.<BR> 2. The wife of the sun.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rēgina (for regonia = राज्ञी for राजन् + या), and perhaps Goth. raginon, see 2. राज्, and राज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्
अ- + राजन् अ- + राजन्, m. one who is not a king, Johns. Sel. 32, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिराजन्
काशि- + राजन् काशि- + राजन्, m. the king of Kāśi, Chr. 11, 19 (but -राज, 3, 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराजन्
धर्म-राजन् धर्म-राजन्, m. (cf. राज), Yudhiṣṭhira, MBh. 2, 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराजन्
नाग- + राजन् नाग- + राजन्, m. (cf. राज), Nal. 14, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्य|राजन्यः
राजन्य राजन् + य, m.<BR> 1. A Kṣatriya, a man of the military caste, Utt. Rāmac. 152, 4; Chr. 37, 2.<BR> 2. A name [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b " target="_blank">Page0766-b + 40</a>] of Agni.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्य
अ- + राजन्य अ- + राजन्य, m. one who is not a Kṣatriya, Man. 4, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यक|राजन्यकं
राजन्यक राजन्य + क, n. A multitude of Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्वन्त्|राजन्वत्
राजन्वन्त् राजन् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessing, or ruled by, a good king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजर्षि|राजर्षिः
राजर्षि राजर्षि, see ऋषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवत्|राजवन्त्
राजवत् राजवत्, i. e. राजन् + वत्, adv. As towards the king, Pañc. i. d. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवन्त्|राजवत्
राजवन्त् राजवन्त् = राजन्वन्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस|राजसः
राजस राजस, i. e. रजस् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी.<BR> 1. Belonging to the quality of passion, Man. 12, 32.<BR> 2. Endowed with passion, 12, 40.<BR> II. f. सी, Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूय|राजसूयः
राजसूय राजसूय, i. e. राजन्-सु + य, m. A sacrifice performed by an universal monarch, attended by his tributary princes, Indr. 1, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाय
राजाय राजाय, a denomin. derived from राजन् with य, Ātm. To behave like a king, Hit. ii. d. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजि|राजिः
राजि and राजी राजी̆, i. e. partly probably ऋज् (properly रज्, cf. Lat. di-vigere), + ई̆, f.<BR> 1. A row, a line, Pañc. i. d. 217; a stripe, Vikr. d. 78; a line parting the hair, Rām. 3, 52, 32.<BR> 2. A continuous line.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलराजि|नीलराजिः
नील-राजि नील-राजि, f. a dark line, darkness, Ṛt. 1, 2 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनराजि|वनराजिः
वन-राज् + इ वन-राज् + इ,<BR> I. adj. embellishing a forest.<BR> II. f. a tree, Rām. 3, 52, 23; 55, 45; Draup. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिका
राजिका f.<BR> I. राजि + का, A line.<BR> II. A field.<BR> III. Black mustard, Sinapis racemosa, Pañc. 184, 18.<BR> --Cf. राजक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीव|राजीवं|राजीवः
राजीव राजीव,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An elephant<BR> 2. A kind of deer.<BR> 3. The Indian crane.<BR> 4. A large fish, Cyprinus niloticus Buch., Man. 5, 16.<BR> II. n. A lotus, Chr. 50, 11; Indr. 4, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्ञी
राज्ञी राज्ञी, see राजन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्य|राज्यं
राज्य राज्य, i. e. राजन् + य, n.<BR> 1. A government, Pañc. iii. d. 265.<BR> 2. A kingdom, Rām. 3, 53, 22; Pañc. 202, 19.<BR> 3. Exercise of sovereignty, Rājat. 5, 242.<BR> 4. Administration.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज्य
देव- + राज्य देव- + राज्य, n. the dominion over the gods, Rām. 6, 98, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीराज्य
पृथिवी- + राज्य पृथिवी- + राज्य, n. the sovereignty of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराज्य
महा- + राज्य महा- + राज्य, n. sovereignty, Chr. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज्य
युवराज्य युवराज्य, i. e. युवन्-, n. the dignity of heir apparent, Pañc. 130, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतराज्य
हृत- + राज्य हृत- + राज्य, adj. stripped of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटि|राटिः
राटि राटि, f. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढा
राढा राढा f.<BR> 1. Splendour.<BR> 2. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राति|रातिः
राति रा + ति, f. Gift, present, Lass. 99, 14 = Rigv. iii. 62, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराति|अरातिः
अ- + राति अ- + राति, m. an enemy, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसाराति|वायसारातिः
वायस-अ- + राति वायस-अ- + राति, m. an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र|रात्रं
ऽरात्र -रात्र, a substitute for रातृ, when latter part of comp. words; e. g. अति-, m.<BR> 1. The name of a part of the Jyotiṣṭoma, and of the Sattra sacrifices, Rām. 1, 13, 44; 45.<BR> 2. A proper name, Hariv. 72. अपर-, m. The last watch of the night, Rām. 3, 22, 29. अर्ध-, m. Midnight, Man. 7, 151. एक-,<BR> I. m. A festival of one night's duration, MBh. 13, 4914.<BR> II. n. One night, Man. 3, 102. चिर-, n. A long time, Man. 3, 266. त्रि-, n. sing. Three nights or days, Man. 4, 119; 5, 67. दशरात्र, i. e. दशन्-, m. Ten days, Man. 5, 65. पञ्चर्˚, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Five nights or days, Man. 8, 402; 11, 147.<BR> 2. The sacred scripture of several Vaiṣṇava sects, MBh. 12, 7891.<BR> II. adj. Lasting five nights or days, MBh. 13, 4914. पूर्व-, m. The first part of the night, MBh. 1, 6443. वि-, Deep night, Sāv. 6, 28 (cf. 5, 66). सप्तर्˚, i. e. सप्तन्-, n. A period of seven nights, Man. 2, 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रक|रात्रकं|रात्रकः
रात्रक रात्र + क, n. = पञ्चरात्र, see रात्र.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरात्रक
पञ्च(न्)- + रात्रक पञ्च(न्)- + रात्रक, adj. Lasting five nights, Pañc. ed. orn. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रि|रात्रिः
रात्रि and रात्री रात्री, probably रम् + तृ + ई, f. Night, Hit. pr. d. 24, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरात्रि|कालरात्रिः
काल- + रात्रि काल- + रात्रि, f. 1. the last night of a Kalpa, in which the universe is destroyed by Kāla, Rām. 5, 47, 26. 2. Durgā, Hariv. 3269. 3. = भीम-रथी, see रथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरात्रि|यक्षरात्रिः
यक्ष-रात्रि यक्ष-रात्रि, f. the night of full moon in the month Kārttika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवरात्रि|शिवरात्रिः
शिव-रात्रि शिव-रात्रि, f. a festival in honour of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरात्रि|शेषरात्रिः
शेष-रात्रि शेष-रात्रि, f. the last watch of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिका
रात्रिका रात्रि + का, f. Night, Rājat. 5, 482.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरात्रिका
पञ्च(न्)- + रात्रिका पञ्च(न्)- + रात्रिका, adj. epithet of Viṣṇu (cf. पञ्चन्-रात्र), MBh. 12, 12864 (p. 818, l. 9, bel.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचर|रात्रिचरः
रात्रिचर रात्रि-चर, and रात्रिंत्रर रात्रिंचर, i. e. रात्रि + म्-चर, m. A Rākṣasa. रात्रिचरी, f. A female Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहिण्डक|रात्रिहिण्डकः
रात्रिहिण्डक रात्रि-हिण्ड् + अक, m. A guard of the women's apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् राध् (probably रा-धा), ii. 5, राध्नु, and i. 4, राध्य, Par. ved.<BR> 1. To make merciful or favourable (ii. 5).<BR> 2. To make agreeable (ii. 5).<BR> 3. To accomplish.<BR> 4. To be merciful, or favourable (i. 4).<BR> 5. To be accomplished or finished (i. 4).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. राद्ध.<BR> 1. Accomplished.<BR> 2. Perfect in mysterious or magical power, Bhāg. P. 3, 11, 17.<BR> 3. Cooked. Desider.<BR> 1. विरत्स.<BR> 2. रित्स, To kill, to hurt, to destroy, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 19.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, ii. 5, and i. 4,<BR> 1. To offend against, with gen., MBh. 1, 1389; to injure, Vikr. 5, 8.<BR> 2. To sin, MBh. 4, 1611.<BR> 3. To restrain, MBh. 3, 17005. अपराद्ध,<BR> 1. Sinned, Śāk. d. 57 (न तु ग्रीष्मस्यैवं [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-a " target="_blank">Page0768-a + 43</a>] सुभगम् अपराद्धं युवतिषु, But when heat [sins against, i. e.] injures the girls, it is not so charming).<BR> 2. Sinning, having sinned, guilty, Śāk. 110, 16 (with gen., against).<BR> --With अभि अभि, i. 4, To propitiate, Rām. 2, 30, 33.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To accomplish, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 16 (pass.).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To make favourable, to propitiate, Rām. 1, 17, 31.<BR> 2. To conciliate, Hit. iv. d. 99; to win, Rām. 2, 60, 6.<BR> 3. To worship, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 6.<BR> 4. To serve, Man. 10, 122; Pañc. 125, 12 (किम् अन्च्नाराधितेन, For what purpose serve him?).<BR> 5. To perform, Bhartṛ. 2, 96. आराधित, Pleased, Vikr. 35, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. दुराराध्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be propitiated, or worshipped, or served, Bhartṛ. 3, 78; Bhāg. P. 4, 11, 11.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, Caus. To serve, Man. 10, 121.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, Caus.<BR> 1. To make favourable, to propitiate, MBh. 3, 10344.<BR> 2. To satisfy, to get the approbation of, Utt. Rāmac. 167, 6.<BR> --Cf. ἱλάσκομαι, ῑ̔́ληθι, ἱλάομαι, etc. (for ἰλλαθ, instead of λιλαθ); cf. also ved. इरध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराधित
सु- + राधित सु- + राधित, adj. caused to be very propitious, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2977.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध राध् + अ,<BR> I. m. The month Vaiśākha, April--May.<BR> II. f. धा.<BR> 1. The sixteenth lunar asterism.<BR> 2. The favourite mistress of Kṛṣṇa, Pañc. 45, 2.<BR> 3. The wife of the charioteer of Dhṛtarāṣṭra, by whom Karṇa was fostered.<BR> 4. Lightning.<BR> 5. Emblic myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधन|राधनं
राधन राध् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Completing.<BR> 2. Obtaining.<BR> 3. Pleasure.<BR> II. f. ना, Speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधस्
राधस् राध् + अस्, n. Favour, bliss, wealth, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेय|राधेयः
राधेय राधेय, i. e. राधा + एय [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b " target="_blank">Page0768-b + 40</a>] (see राध), metronym., m. Karṇa, Johns. Sel. 56, 155; Rājat. 5, 379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राभस्य|राभस्यं
राभस्य राभस्य, i. e. रभस + अ, n. The state or condition of velocity, or of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम राम, i. e. रम् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Beautiful.<BR> 2. Black.<BR> 3. White.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A proper name, particularly the hero of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR> 2. A name of Varuṇa.<BR> 3. A horse.<BR> 4. A sort of deer.<BR> III. f. मा, A beautiful female, Vikr. d. 114; Amar. 58.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. राम-चन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुराम|परशुरामः
परशु- + राम परशु- + राम, m. the first of the three renowned Rāmas, the son of Jamadagni, Prab. 5, 5 (cf. Chr. 16, 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलराम|बलरामः
बल- + राम बल- + राम, m. the third Rāma, the half-brother of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 1, 7912.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामज
रामज राम-ज, m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामायण|रामायणं
रामायण रामायण, i. e. राम-अयन (or rather + आयन), n. The name of a renowned epic poem, Utt. Rāmac. 110, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः|राम्भः
राम्भ राम्भ, i. e. रम्भ्ă + अ, m. The bambu staff of a religious student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राल|रालः
राल राल, m. The resinous exudation of the Shorea robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राव|रावः
राव राव, i. e. रु + अ, m. Sound, Hit. 92, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घराव
दीर्घ- + राव दीर्घ- + राव, m. the proper name of a jackal, Hit. 76, 6, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण रावण, m. The king of the Rākṣasas, the ravisher of Sīta, and destroyed by Rāma, Rām. 3, 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणि|रावणिः
रावणि रावणि, i. e. रावण + इ, patronym., m. The eldest son of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश्
राश् राश्, v. r. for रास्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशि|राशिः
राशि राशि, m.<BR> 1. A heap, a quantity, Pañc. 121, 11; 203, 7.<BR> 2. A sign of the zodiac.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निराशि|अग्निराशिः
अग्नि- + राशि अग्नि- + राशि, m. a fireball, Rām. 4, 60, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुराशि|अम्बुराशिः
अम्बु- + राशि अम्बु- + राशि (Ragh. 6, 57), and लवण-अम्बु- (Vikr. d. 18), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a " target="_blank">Page0769-a + 42</a>] जल- (Kathās. 18, 2, but, plenty of water, Kir. 5, 19), पयस्- (Hit. ii. d. 15), and वारि- (Rājat. 5, 15), m. the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मराशि|ब्रह्मराशिः
ब्रह्म(न्)- + राशि ब्रह्म(न्)- + राशि, heap of holiness, Chr. 34, 15 (= Paraśurāma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशोराशि
यशस्- + राशि यशस्- + राशि, m. greatness of glory, i. e. a glorious deed, Vikr. 11, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र राष्ट्र, m. and n.<BR> I. i. e. राज् + त्र,<BR> 1. A realm, empire, kingdom, Pañc. iii. d. 39; v. d. 64 (कुराजान्तानि राष्ट्राणि, Kingdoms find their end [i. e. are ruined] by wicked kings).<BR> 2. An inhabited country, Lass. 76, 18.<BR> II. Any public calamity, as famine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराष्ट्र|सुराष्ट्रः
सु- + राष्ट्र सु- + राष्ट्र, m. the name of a country, सुरत्, Rām. 3, 53, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिक|राष्ट्रिकः
राष्ट्रिक राष्ट्रिक, i. e. राष्ट्र + इक, adj. sbst. Inhabiting, or an inhabitant of, a realm, Man. 10, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय and राष्ट्रीय राष्ट्रीय,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a realm.<BR> II. (राष्त्र्ĭय), m. A king's brother-in-law (in theatrical language), Mṛcch. 66, 23; cf. Böhtl. ad Śāk. 73, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास् रास् (cf. रस्), i. 1, Ātm. (MBh. 8, 1941, Par.), To sound, to cry.<BR> --Cf. राश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास रास, i. e. रस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sound.<BR> 2. Confused noise.<BR> 3. Speech.<BR> 4. A festival among the cowherds, including especially a circular dance.<BR> 5. A chain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरास
दुरास दुरास, i. e. दुस्-, m. disagreeable speech, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ रासभ, i. e. रस् + अ + भ, m. An ass, Pañc. iii. d. 118. f. भी, A she-ass, Pañc. 215, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेरस|रासेरसः
रासेरस रासेरस, m.<BR> I. i. e. रास + इ-रस.<BR> 1. = रास.<BR> 2. Mirth.<BR> 3. A company, a party.<BR> II. (cf. रस), Alchymy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासन
रासन रासन, m. = रस, Pāṇ. Sch. iv. 2, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना रास्ना, f. A sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहु|राहुः
राहु राहु, i. e. रह् + उ, m.<BR> 1. A Daitya to whom the eclipses are ascribed, Hit. i. d. 20, M.M.<BR> 2. The ascending node.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराहु
स- + राहु स- + राहु, adj. seized by Rāhu, i. e. eclipsed, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
1. रि रि, i. 6, रिय, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
2. रि रि, ii. 5, v. r. for ऋ, ii. 5, To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तक|रिक्तकं
रिक्तक रिक्त + क (vb. रिच्), adj.<BR> 1. Void, empty.<BR> 2. Unloaded, unburthened, Man. 8, 404.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थ|रिक्थं
रिक्थ रिक्थ, i. e. रिच् + थ, n.<BR> 1. An inheritance, Man. 9, 104.<BR> 2. Property, Man. 8, 30.<BR> 3. Wealth.<BR> 4. Gold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्ररिक्थ
गोत्र- + रिक्थ गोत्र- + रिक्थ, n. du. family and estate, Man. 9, 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थाद
रिक्थाद रिक्थाद, i. e. रिक्थ-अ-द (vb. दा), m. An heir, a son, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थिन्
रिक्थिन् रिक्थिन्, i. e. रिक्थ + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Wealthy.<BR> II. m. An heir, Man. 9, 162 (एक-, An heir of one man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्षा
रिक्षा रिक्षा, f.<BR> 1. A nit.<BR> 2. A mote in a sunbeam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख्
रिख् रिख्, रिङ्ख् रिङ्ख्, see रख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिच्
रिच् रिच्, ii. 7, रिणच्, रिञ्च्, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To evacuate, to leave, pass., Vikr. d. 8 (being delivered).<BR> 2. To separate, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 36.<BR> --† i. 1, and i. 10,<BR> 1. To join, to mix.<BR> 2. To divide, to separate.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रिक्त,<BR> 1. Empty, Pañc. 89, 2.<BR> 2. Unloaded.<BR> 3. Purged.<BR> 4. Free from, Ragh. 14, 85.<BR> 5. Poor.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of i. 10, or Caus. रेचित,<BR> 1. Freed from.<BR> 2. Purged.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, pass.<BR> 1. To surpass, with abl., Man. 4, 175; with acc., 2, 145; with instr., MBh. 3, 10588.<BR> 2. To prevail, Man. 12, 25; to play the chief part, Hit. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a " target="_blank">Page0770-a + 37</a>] i. d. 161, M.M. अतिरिक्त, Exceeding, Bhāṣāp. 19; excessive.<BR> --With व्यति वि-अति, pass. To surpass, with abl., Ragh. 10, 31. व्यतिरिक्त,<BR> 1. Different, distinct, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 14; 15.<BR> 2. Excepted.<BR> 3. Withdrawn.<BR> --With आ आ; instead of आरेचित (Mixed ?), Daśak. in Chr. 190, 15, I propose to read आरचित (Made). With उद् उद्, pass. To surpass, MBh. 1, 3070. उद्रिक्त,<BR> 1. Distinct.<BR> 2. Increased. adv. Surely, Chr. 20, 19 (perhaps, adj. and, Arrogant).<BR> उद्रेचित, Pre-eminent, Rājat. 5, 365.<BR> --With वि वि, विरिक्त, Purged, Man. 5, 144.<BR> --Cf. Lat. licere, licitare, linquere; λείπω; Goth. af-lifnan; A.S. lyfan, be-lifan, laefan, To leave; also Goth. leihvan; A.S. laen, laenan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्त
अ- + रिक्त अ- + रिक्त, adj. filled, Mālav. 45, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिज्
† रिज् रिज्, i. 1, Par. To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिण्व्
रिण्व् रिण्व्, see रण्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपु|रिपुः
रिपु रिपु, probably लिप् + उ (र् for ल्, or rather the original sound), m. An enemy, Pañc. ii. d. 168.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चरिपु|क्रौञ्चरिपुः
क्रौञ्च- + रिपु क्रौञ्च- + रिपु, m. a name of the god of war, Pañc. i. d. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुता
रिपुता रिपु + ता, f. Enmity, Hit. ii. d. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्र|रिप्रः
रिप्र रिप् + र (probably लिप् + र, cf. रिपु), adj. Vile, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफ्
† रिफ् रिफ् (ऋफ् ऋफ्, and रिह् रिह्), i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To say or to boast.<BR> 2. To fight.<BR> 3. To blame.<BR> 4. To hurt.<BR> 5. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ्|रिंफ्
† रिम्फ् रिम्फ्, i. 6, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्ब्
रिम्ब् रिम्ब्, see रण्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसा
रिरंसा रिरंसा, i. e. रिरंस, desider. of रम्, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wish to sport, Nal. 1, 41. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b " target="_blank">Page0770-b + 38</a>]<BR> 2. Desire of enjoyment, Bhāg. P. 9, 14, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरी
रिरी रिरी, f. Pale brass, prince's metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्
रिश् रिश् (cf. लिश्), i. 6, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिशादस्
रिशादस् रिशादस्, probably रिश् + अ-अद् + अस्, adj. m. A destroyer of those who injure, Chr. 290, 5 = Rigv. i. 64, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्य|रिश्यः
रिश्य रिश् + य, m. A deer, see ऋष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्
रिष् रिष्, i. 1 and 4, Par.<BR> 1. To kill, to hurt, MBh. 3, 13111.<BR> 2. To give offence, Man. 4, 178, Ātm. (Sch., but perhaps pass. To be hurt).<BR> 3. To be hurt (ved.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रिष्ट.<BR> 1. Injured.<BR> 2. Unlucky, n.<BR> 1. Bad luck.<BR> 2. Destruction.<BR> 3. Sin. m.<BR> 1. A sword (cf. ऋष्टि).<BR> 2. The name of a demon.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably ῥαίω, ῥαιστός; Lat. lædo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अ-रिष्ट अ-रिष्ट. see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टि|रिष्टिः
रिष्टि रिष्टि,<BR> I. f. m. A sword (cf. ऋष्टि).<BR> II. रिष् + ति, f. Bad luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्व|रिष्वः
रिष्व रिष् + व, adj. Injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिह्
रिह् रिह्,<BR> 1. See रिफ्.<BR> 2. Ved. = लिह्. Frequent. रेरिह्, ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. रेरिहाण, m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. An Asura or demon.<BR> 3. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
1. री री, ii. 9, रिणा, रिणी. Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To howl.<BR> 3. To hart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
2. री री, i. 4, Ātm. To distil, to ooze, to drop.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To drop after, to follow dropping, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3.<BR> --Cf. Goth. and A.S. rinnan (based on ii. 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढक|रीढकः
रीढक रीढक, m. The backbone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढा
रीढा रीढा, f. Disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीति|रीतिः
रीति री + ति, f.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. Boundary.<BR> 3. Usage, manner, way, Lass. 2. ed. 2, 6.<BR> 4. Natural property.<BR> 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a " target="_blank">Page0771-a + 41</a>] Oozing.<BR> 6. Brass, pale brass.<BR> 7. Calx of brass.<BR> 8. Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीव्
† रीव् रीव्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
1. रु रु, ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To sound, to make a particular sound, as birds, MBh. 1, 5898; bees, etc., to hum, Hit. i. d. 80, M.M.<BR> 2. To bray, MBh. 1, 4508.<BR> 3. To yelp, Man. 4, 113.<BR> 4. To yell, MBh. 4, 1463.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुत, n.<BR> 1. Any cry or noise, humming of bees, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 10.<BR> 2. The cry of birds, Lass. 52, 11.<BR> 3. Song, Śāk. d. 131. Frequent. रोरु and रोरूय, To cry loudly, to yelp loudly, MBh. 1, 6112; 663.<BR> --Caus. रावय, To fill with a roar, MBh. 3, 15928.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभिरुत,<BR> 1. Sounded, filled with the sound of, MBh. 3, 1535.<BR> 2. Sounding.<BR> 3. Humming, Śiś. 9, 34. n. Sound, Rām. 1, 9, 17.<BR> --With आ आ, To cry, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 24.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To sound, Mṛcch. 144, 2.<BR> 2. To yell, Pañc. 64, 4.<BR> 3. To lament, Vikr. d. 102; MBh. 3, 336. विरुत, n. Tone. Śāk. d. 85; singing, Ṛt. 6, 33.<BR> --Caus. To make a braying noise, Man. 4, 64.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To cry, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 71.<BR> --Cf. ὠρύω (frequent.); Lat. raucus, rūmor; A.S. ryn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
† 2. रु रु, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To hurt, or to be angry (?).<BR> 3. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुंश्
† रुंश् रुंश्, i. 10 and 1, Par. To speak, to shine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्म|रुक्मं|रुक्मः
रुक्म रुक्म, i. e. रुच् + म,<BR> I. adj. Clear, bright.<BR> II. n. (ved. m., Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 88, 2).<BR> 1. Gold.<BR> 2. Iron.<BR> III. m. A golden chain, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिन्
रुक्मिन् रुक्मिन्, i. e. रुक्म + इन्,<BR> I. m. The name of a prince, slain by बलराम.<BR> II. f. मिणी, A princess [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-b " target="_blank">Page0771-b + 43</a>] carried off and married by Kṛṣṇa, Mālav. d. 77; cf. Wilson, Hind. Theatr. 2. ed. 183, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष|रुक्षः
रुक्ष and रूक्ष रू̆क्ष, adj.<BR> 1. Rugged, rough, difficult, Vikr. d. 61 (र्ŭ).<BR> 2. Harsh, unkind, Pañc. iv. d. 62 (रू˚); uncouth, Pañc. v. d. 6 (र्ŭ˚, but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 805); Bhartṛ. 2, 59 (र्ŭ˚); cruel, Śāk. d. 191 (रू˚).<BR> 3. Austere, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 8 (र्ŭ).<BR> --Cf. A.S. rug, ruh, ruw; Engl. rough, rugged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष्म
रुक्ष्म रुक्ष्म, Hard, fleshless (?), Rājat. 5, 433 (? perhaps to be changed to रुक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्नता
रुग्नता रुग्न + ता (cf. रुज्), f.<BR> 1. Sickness.<BR> 2. Crookedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
1. रुच् रुच्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 3, 468).<BR> 1. To shine, MBh. 1, 6613; Man. 4, 20.<BR> 2. To please, with dat., MBh. 1, 7550; Hit. ii. d. 49.<BR> 3. To be pleased, to approve, MBh. 1, 7444.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुचित.<BR> 1. Bright.<BR> 2. Sweet.<BR> 3. Pleased, MBh. 1, 7952.<BR> 4. Sharpened (as the appetite).<BR> 5. Digested.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. रुच्य.<BR> 1. Beautiful.<BR> 2. Tonic, stomachic. m. A lover. n. A digestive.<BR> --Caus. रोचय, Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To cause to like.<BR> 2. Ātm. To like, Man. 2, 243.<BR> 3. To choose, Rām. 1, 43, 1.<BR> 4. To resolve, Hariv. 6416.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, To surpass by splendour, MBh. 3, 468.<BR> --With अनु अनु, Caus. To desire, MBh. 3, 12679.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To please (with the dat. of the pers.), Vikr. 21, 11. अभिरुचित,<BR> 1. Pleased.<BR> 2. Delighting, Johns. Sel. 93, 52.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To desire, to like, Rām. 2, 30, 27.<BR> 2. To be ready, Rām. 1, 36, 2.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. Ātm. To like, Rām. 2, 30, 28.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a " target="_blank">Page0772-a + 45</a>] resolve, MBh. 3, 11546 (प्रति belongs perhaps to the noun, not to the vb.).<BR> --With वि वि, To shine, MBh. 3, 1754.<BR> --Cf. लोच्; Lat. lucere, lumen (cf. Goth. lauhmuni; A.S. leóma), luna; Goth. liuhath, liuhtjan; A.S. leoht, lioht, gelihtan, lócian; probably also O.H.G. liuchan, fovere, luchjan, lochon, mulcere; λευκός, λεύσσω, ἀμϕι-λύκη, etc., λύχνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
2. रुच् रुच्, f.<BR> 1. Light, splendour, Kir. 5, 45; Śiś. 9, 23; Kir. 5, 43.<BR> 2. Beauty, Pañc. i. d. 152 (स्मित-पाटल-अधर-, adj. Showing the beauty of smiling पाटल-like lips).<BR> 3. Lightning.<BR> 4. Desire.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. lux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनरुच्
घन- + रुच् घन- + रुच्, adj. of a cloud-like, i. e. dark, colour, Bhāg. P. 4, 5, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणामणिसहस्ररुच्
फणा-मणि-सहस्र- + रुच् फणा-मणि-सहस्र- + रुच्, f. the splendour of the thousand jewels of the serpent's hoods, Śiś. 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारितवर्णसंकररुच्
विस्तारित-वर्ण-संकर- + रुच् विस्तारित-वर्ण-संकर- + रुच्, adj. shining brilliantly by the mixture of colours, and, being very desirous of the mixture of the castes, Rājat. 5, 377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरुच्
शीत- + रुच् शीत- + रुच्, m. the moon, Śiś. 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतरुच्
अ-शीत- + रुच् अ-शीत- + रुच्, m. the sun, Śiś. 9, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचक|रुचकं|रुचकः
रुचक रुच् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Agreeable.<BR> 2. Sharp.<BR> 3. Tonic, stomachic.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ornament of the neck and breast.<BR> 2. A tooth.<BR> 3. A pigeon.<BR> 4. The citron.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Any auspicious or fortunate object.<BR> 2. A garland, a chaplet.<BR> 3. A curl on a horse's neck.<BR> 4. A perfume, commonly रोचना.<BR> 5. Salt.<BR> 6. The fruit of the citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचि|रुचिः
रुचि (and रुची), रुच् + ई, f.<BR> 1. Light, Vikr. d. 48 (च्ĭ); splendour, 19, 9 (ची).<BR> 2. A ray of light.<BR> 3. Beauty, Bhāṣāp. 1, a (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 4. Appearance, Śiś. 9, 19 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 5. Wish, desire, Śiś. 9, 17; pleasure, Pāṇ. 1, 4, 33.<BR> 6. Passion.<BR> 7. Intent application to any object.<BR> 8. Hunger.<BR> 9. Taste, Pañc. iii. d. 259 (च्ĭ); pleasure, Rājat. 5, 1 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b " target="_blank">Page0772-b + 42</a>] (च्ĭ).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णरुचि|उष्णरुचिः
उष्ण- + रुचि उष्ण- + रुचि, m. the sun, Śiś. 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डरुचि
दण्ड-रुचि दण्ड-रुचि, adj. inclined to severity, Pañc. 91, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहरुचि
प्रतिग्रह- + रुचि प्रतिग्रह- + रुचि, adj. eager to take a gift, Man. 4, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसरुचि
मांस- + रुचि मांस- + रुचि, adj. liking flesh, Hit. 42, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविक्रमरुचि
विशेष-विक्रम- + रुचि विशेष-विक्रम- + रुचि, adj. desiring to attack the pre-eminently powerful, Bhartṛ. 2, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गरुचि
संसर्ग- + रुचि संसर्ग- + रुचि, adj. liking intercourse (with), Pañc. iii. d. 259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरितरुचि
स्फुरित- + रुचि स्फुरित- + रुचि, adj. having a trembling (glittering) splendour, Megh. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुचि|स्वरुचिः
स्व- + रुचि स्व- + रुचि, adj. 1. wilful. 2. self-willed, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिता
रुचिता रुचि + ता, f. Interest, interested motives, Man. 12, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिर|रुचिरं
रुचिर रुच् + इर, adj.<BR> 1. Beautiful, Rām. 3, 52, 16; 24; brilliant, Vikr. d. 76.<BR> 2. Agreeable, Pañc. 170, 6.<BR> 3. Sweet.<BR> 4. Stomachic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिष्य|रुचिष्यं
रुचिष्य रुच् + इष्य, adj. Agreeable, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
1. रुज् रुज्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To break, MBh. 3, 678.<BR> 2. To bend.<BR> 3. To pain, to afflict with disease.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुग्ण (MBh. 1, 1.); also wrongly written रुग्न.<BR> 1. Broken.<BR> 2. Bent, crooked.<BR> 3. Injured.<BR> 4. Sick.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, † To hurt, to kill.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To break, MBh. 1, 5884.<BR> --With आ आ, To break, MBh. 3, 423.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To break, MBh. 4, 1082.<BR> --With वि वि, To destroy, Śāk. d. 32, v. r.<BR> --Cf. perhaps ὀρύσσω, διορυγή, probably λυγρός, λευγαλέος, λοιγός, λύγος; Lat. lues (cf. fruor from frug). See रोमन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
2. रुज् रुज्, f.<BR> 1. Pain, Man. 11, 674 Vikr. d. 30.<BR> 2. Sickness, Vikr. d. 51.<BR> 3. Effort, Megh. 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज्
नीरुज् नीरुज्, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. free from pain, Suśr. 1, 289, 2. 2. healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजस्कर
रुजस्कर रुज् + अस्-कर, m. Producing pain, MBh. 3, 14144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजा
रुजा रुज् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Sickness, Sāv. 5, 61; 81.<BR> 2. Destruction.<BR> 3. An ewe.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज|अरुजः
अ-रुज अ-रुज,<BR> I. adj. 1. not breaking, Suśr. 2, 300, 14. 2. healthy, Bhartṛ. 3, 76.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Hariv. 14284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज|नीरुजं|नीरुजः
नीरुज नीरुज, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. जा. 1. free from pain, Suśr. 1, 292, 14. 2. healthy, Hit. i. d. 14, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरुज
स-रुज स-रुज, adj. sick, Sāv. 5, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुज
सु- + रुज सु- + रुज, adj. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजाय
रुजाय रुजाय, a denomin. derived from रुजा with य, Ātm. To be sick, Mālav. 44, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुट्
† रुट् रुट्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To resist.<BR> 2. To suffer pain.<BR> 3. To shine.<BR> --i. 10,<BR> 1. To be angry.<BR> 2. To shine, to speak (cf. रुठ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुठ्
† रुठ् रुठ्, i. 1, Par. To strike, to fell.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To resist.<BR> 2. To suffer pain (cf. रुट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ट्|रुंट्
† रुण्ट् रुण्ट्, रुण्ड् रुण्ड्, i. 1, Par. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ठ्|रुंठ्
† रुण्ठ् रुण्ठ्, लुण्ठ् लुण्ठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To be idle.<BR> 3. To be lame.<BR> 4. To resist.<BR> 5. To steal. See 2. लुठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड्
रुण्ड् रुण्ड्, see रुण्ट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड|रुंड|रुण्डः
रुण्ड रुण्ड, m. A headless body, retaining life and fighting, Utt. Rāmac. 121, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्डिका|रुंडिका
रुण्डिका रुण्डिका (cf. the last), f.<BR> 1. A field of battle.<BR> 2. Superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
रुद् रुद्, ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 52, 19, and i. 1, Chr. 24, 46).<BR> 1. To weep, Vikr. 83, 12; Hit. 99, 3 (read रुदती); to cry, MBh. 2, 2616.<BR> 2. To bewail, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 5.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुदित.<BR> 1. Wept.<BR> 2. Weeping. n. Weeping, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Frequent. रोरुद्, रोरुद्य, To weep, to cry [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b " target="_blank">Page0773-b + 43</a>] excessively, MBh. 3, 10192.<BR> --Caus. रोदय, To cause to weep, Utt. Rāmac. 85, 3.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To weep, Nal. 3, 32.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, To bewail, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 4.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To burst into tears, MBh. 3, 2919.<BR> 2. To weep, to cry, Rām. 1, 17, 22. प्र-रुदित,<BR> 1. Wept.<BR> 2. Weeping, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 21.<BR> 3. Beginning to weep, Vikr. d. 153.<BR> --With वि वि, To weep, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 13. विरुदित, n. Weeping, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 11.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rudere; O.H.G. riuzan; A.S. reotan; probably ὀῤῥωδέω (frequent., cf. रौद्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यरुदित
अरण्य- + रुदित अरण्य- + रुदित, n. complaining of one's griefs to a forest, i. e. without being heard, Amar. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्र|रुद्रः
रुद्र रुद् + र,<BR> I. adj. One who roars, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. i. 64, 3.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Śiva as the god of the tempests, Pañc. pr. d. 1; Bhartṛ. 2, 93.<BR> 2. A class of eleven demigods (personified roaring of the wind), Nal. 10, 24.<BR> III. f. रुद्राणी, Durgā. Pāṇ. iv. 1, 49.<BR> IV. f. द्री, A sort of lute.<BR> --Cf. perhaps λύρα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राणी
रुद्राणी रुद्राणी, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
रुध् रुध्, ii. 7, रुणध्, रुण्ध्, Par. Ātm. (i. 4, see अनु),<BR> 1. To obstruct, MBh. 1, 2367; to check, Rām. 2, 63, 43; to stop, Vikr. d. 121; to obscure, 3, 55, 10.<BR> 2. To keep off, Rām. 1, 28, 22.<BR> 3. To confine, Man. 9, 12; to arrest, Vikr. d. 103.<BR> 4. To bind, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR> 5. To hold, to support Megh. 10.<BR> 6. To besiege, MBh. 3, 638 (anomal. अरुन्धत्).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुद्ध.<BR> 1. Obstructed, stopped, retained, Chr. 33, 33.<BR> 2. Opposed.<BR> 3. Shut, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 14 (separate, रुद्धा दृष्टिः, ‘His eye is shut’).<BR> 4. Besieged.<BR> 5. Surrounded.<BR> 6. Secured, held, Śiś. 9, 75; taken possession of, Pañc. 227, 21. f. धा, A siege.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be besieged, Ragh. 12, 71; epic anomal. रुन्धय, To obstruct, pain, MBh. 3, 999.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-a " target="_blank">Page0774-a + 43</a>] the prep. अनु अनु, To retain, Man. 5, 63.<BR> --i. 4, Ātm. (originally pass.; in epic poetry also with the terminations of the Par., MBh. 4, 492).<BR> 1. (To comply with), to approve, MBh. 3, 13891.<BR> 2. To obey, Utt. Rāmac. 97, 7.<BR> 3. To spare, MBh. 2, 926.<BR> 4. To love, MBh. 3, 16194; Utt. Rāmac. 66, 8; to caress, ib. 71, 1. अनुरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Checked.<BR> 2. Soothed.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To restrain, Rām. 2, 30, 9; to stop, Śāk. d. 35.<BR> 2. To keep in order, Man. 8, 236.<BR> 3. To besiege, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 23. अवरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Checked.<BR> 2. Shut up, secluded, as in a haram. Frequent. रोरुध्, To offend, Rām. 2, 58, 20.<BR> --With आ आ, To keep off, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 49.<BR> --Caus. To obstruct, MBh. 1, 4188.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To obstruct, Man. 8, 348.<BR> 2. To block up, Man. 7, 195.<BR> 3. To molest, Śāk. 24, 8; to trouble, 18, 10.<BR> 4. To obscure, Ragh. 7, 36. उपरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Obstructed.<BR> 2. Covered.<BR> 3. Favoured.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To obstruct, Hit. i. d. 154, M.M.; to stop, Śāk. d. 169.<BR> 2. To restrain, MBh. 3, 13633.<BR> 3. To confine, Man. 11, 176.<BR> 4. To keep off, Bhag. 16, 20. निरुद्ध, Obstructed (not able to work fitly), Pañc. ii. d. 164.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be shut, Rājat. 5, 428.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To confine, Man. 9, 83.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To keep back, MBh. 3, 16830.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To obstruct, MBh. 3, 12114; to stop, Chr. 43, 30.<BR> 2. To make unable to move, Chr. 28, 21.<BR> 3. To interrupt, to make imperfect, Man. 11, 11.<BR> 4. To accuse unjustly, Man. 11, 88. प्रतिरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Impeded.<BR> 2. Surrounded, blockaded.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To withhold, MBh. 2, 227.<BR> 2. To obstruct, Ṛt. 6, 26; to check, Rām. 2, 36, 10.<BR> 3. To combat, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b " target="_blank">Page0774-b + 42</a>] to quarrel with, Pañc. iii. d. 123; iv. d. 82. विरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Opposed, hindered.<BR> 2. Prohibited, Man. 4, 15.<BR> 3. Contrary, opposite, Śiś. 9, 62; Pañc. 131, 11; perverse, Pañc. 199, 4; ˚धम्, Perversely, Pañc. i. d. 64.<BR> 4. Inconsistent, incongruous, Bhāṣāp. 70; Pañc. 130, 1.<BR> 5. Hostile, Rājat. 5, 452; Pañc. 213, 20; disagreeable, Hit. 58, 18.<BR> 6. Surrounded, blockaded, shut up, Pañc. iv. d. 78.<BR> --Comp.<BR> 1.<BR> --Caus. To obstruct, MBh. 3, 360. विरोधित, Fought with, Pañc. iii. d. 1.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To obstruct, MBh. 3, 2541; to check, 2, 226.<BR> 2. To refrain, MBh. 3, 13633.<BR> 3. To fetter, Bhartṛ. 2, 14. संरुद्ध,<BR> 1. Obstructed, Man. 8, 295.<BR> 2. Attacked, 8, 235.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. unimpeded, Rājat. 5, 453.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be embanked, 5, 106.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To keep off, Rām. 2, 14, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुद्ध
अ- + रुद्ध अ- + रुद्ध, adj. unobstructed, without obstacles, Vikr. 49, 16; untroubled, Pañc. i. d. 406. 2. friendly, kind, with gen., Lass. 2. ed. 45, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिरुद्ध
स्मृति- + रुद्ध स्मृति- + रुद्ध, adj. contrary to law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
ऽरुध् -रुध्, adj. Impeding; e. g. कर-, adj. Impeding the hand, or rays, viz. of the sun, Megh. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिर|रुधिरं|रुधिरः
रुधिर रुधिर (from a vb. रुध्, lost in corresponding signification), n.<BR> 1. Blood, Pañc. 123, 14.<BR> 2. Saffron.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. rôt; A.S. reád, roder; ἐρυθρός, ἐρεύθω, ῥούσιος; Lat. rutilus (for old ruthilus), rufus, ruber, robigo, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुप्
† रुप् रुप्, i. 4, Par. To confound (cf. लुप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुमण्वन्त्|रुमण्वत्
रुमण्वन्त् रुमण्वन्त्, i. e. रुमन् (= लवण) + वन्त्, m. The name of a mountain, Pāṇ. 8, 2, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुमा
रुमा रुमा, f.<BR> 1. The wife of a monkey.<BR> 2. The name of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुम्र|रुम्रः
रुम्र रुम्र, adj.<BR> 1. Tawny.<BR> 2. Beautiful (cf. रुमण्वन्त् and लवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरु|रुरुः
रुरु रुरु, m. A sort of deer, Draup. 4, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवथ|रुवथः
रुवथ रुवथ, i. e. रु + अथ, m. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुश्
† रुश् रुश्, i. 6, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशन्त्|रुशत्
रुशन्त् रुशन्त्, adj.<BR> I. Probably originally a ptcple. pres. of रुच्, f. शती, Red, Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13.<BR> II. Probably a ptcple. pres. of रुष्, Cursing, imprecative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
1. रुष् रुष् (akin to रुक्ष् in रुक्ष), † i. 1 and 4, Par. † To hurt.<BR> --† i. 4 and i. 10, Par. To be angry.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रुष्ट (Pañc. 223, 9; Śṛṅgārat. 7), रुषित (Man. 9, 83), and रोषित, Enraged.<BR> --Caus. To irritate, Pañc. 163, 4. रोषित, Irritated, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 16.<BR> --Cf. probably λύσσα, perhaps ἀλυσταίνω, ἀλυκταίνω, ἀλαλύκτημαι; Goth. in-rauhtjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
2. रुष् रुष् (and रुषा रुष् + आ), f. Wrath, anger, Pañc. iv. d. 61; Vikr. d. 80.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरुष्
अति-रुष् अति-रुष्, adj. very furious, Pañc. ii. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरुष्
स-रुष् स-रुष्, adj. angry, Pañc. i. d. 80 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3196).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्
रुह् रुह् (originally रुध्, cf. न्यग्रोध), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm.).<BR> 1. To grow, Man. 9, 36.<BR> 2. To be lost by growing, to cicatrize, to heal, Pañc. iii. d. 112 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2647).<BR> 3. Pass. with the terminat. of the Par. To be mounted, Johns. Sel. 11, 25.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रूढ,<BR> 1. Grown, increased, much, Rājat. 5, 173.<BR> 2. Budded, blown.<BR> 3. Born, produced.<BR> 4. Certain.<BR> 5. Notorious, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 10.<BR> 6. Traditional, conventional, applied especially to words of unknown origin, but of which the employment is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-b " target="_blank">Page0775-b + 42</a>] familiar.<BR> 7. Obscure, Śiś. 10, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. रोहय.<BR> II. रोपय.<BR> 1. To plant, Rām. 2, 80, 7 (रोपय).<BR> 2. To sow, MBh. 3, 13116 (रोहय).<BR> --With the prep. व्यति वि-अति, To obtain, MBh. 3, 13929.<BR> --Caus. रोपय, To cover, MBh. 3, 601.<BR> --With अधि अधि,<BR> 1. To ascend, to mount on, Vikr. d. 14; Rājat. 5, 217.<BR> 2. To fly upward, Rām. 2, 95, 11.<BR> --Caus. रोपय,<BR> 1. To lift, Ragh. 11, 81.<BR> 2. To give, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 21.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप, Caus. रोपय, To deprive, MBh. 3, 1579.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To ascend, to mount, Rām. 1, 44, 5; Chr. 36, 17.<BR> --With अव अव, To descend, Rām. 2, 7, 11.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. रोहय, To order to descend, Ragh. 1, 54.<BR> II. रोपय,<BR> 1. To take down, MBh. 4, 1318.<BR> 2. To root up, Johns. Sel. 53, 123.<BR> 3. To diminish, Man. 1, 82.<BR> 4. Ātm. To alight from, Draup. 3, 8.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव, Caus. रोपय, To deprive, MBh. 4, 536.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To mount, Rām. 3, 48, 5.<BR> 2. To ascend to (with acc.), MBh. 3, 1727. अङ्कम् आरुह्य, Having climbed into one's lap, Hit. ii. d. 166.<BR> 3. With संशयम्, To doubt, Hit. i. d. 6.<BR> 4. With प्रतिज्ञाम्, To promise, MBh. 1, 2015. आरूढ,<BR> 1. Mounted, Man. 4, 120.<BR> 2. Standing, Man. 7, 91.<BR> 3. Elevated, Pañc. i. d. 225.<BR> 4. Having reached, Pañc. 87, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR> हय-, adj. mounted on horseback, Hit. iii. d. 85.<BR> रथ-, adj. mounted on a chariot, Vikr. 5, 4.<BR> लेख्य-, adj. recorded.<BR> --Caus. रोपय,<BR> 1. To cause, to ascend, Chr. 4, 14; Ātm. To try to string, Johns. Sel. 49, 93.<BR> 2. To lift up, Hit. ii. d. 44; on, Chr. 11, 21; to cast, Pañc. i. d. 273; with तुलाम्, To put in a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-a " target="_blank">Page0776-a + 40</a>] balance, i. e. in danger, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR> --Absol. आरुह्य, Having encountered, Hit. i. d. 5, M.M.<BR> 3. To put upon, Pañc. 41, 15.<BR> 4. To draw (a bow), Utt. Rāmac. 118, 1.<BR> 5. To take to, Man. 3, 17.<BR> 6. To cause to grow, to plant, Rājat. 5, 149.<BR> 7. To transfer, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 12.<BR> --With अत्या अति-आ, अत्यारुढ, Risen, Utt. Rāmac. 147, 14.<BR> --With अध्या अधि-आ, To mount, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 16.<BR> --Caus. रोपय,<BR> 1. To cause to ascend, Rām. 2, 55, 15.<BR> 2. To elevate, Pañc. 24, 9.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, To ascend after, MBh. 2, 36.<BR> --With समन्वा सम्-अनु-आ. The same, MBh. 1, 2818.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To ascend, MBh. 2, 37.<BR> 2. To obtain, Ragh. 17, 30 (Calc.).<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ, To ascend. MBh. 3, 10594.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, Caus. To cause to remount, Utt. Rāmac. 133, 4.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To mount on, Pañc. 115, 3; Chr. 45, 12.<BR> 2. To engage, Prab. 116, 9. समारूढ, Mounted, Pañc. 48, 10.<BR> --Caus. रोपय,<BR> 1. To cause to mount, Pañc. 44, 16; to lift up, 52, 2.<BR> 2. To deposit, Man. 6, 38.<BR> --With उप उप, उपरूढ, Undergone, Mālav. 31, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To shoot up, Pañc. iii. d. 55.<BR> 2. To grow, Man. 9, 14.<BR> 3. To heal, Pañc. iii. d. 112. प्ररूढ,<BR> 1. Grown long. Pañc. 182, 10.<BR> 2. Rooted, fastened<BR> 3. Born, produced. m. The belly.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. रोपय, To reestablish, Ragh. 17, 42 (Calc.).<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To grow, Śāk. d. 96.<BR> 2. To spread, Bhag. 15, 3. विरूढ,<BR> 1. Budded, blown.<BR> 2. Born.<BR> --Caus. रोपय, To heal, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 21.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To grow, Bhaṭṭ. 11, 5. संरूढ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b " target="_blank">Page0776-b + 42</a>]<BR> 1. Budded.<BR> 2. Confident, Arj. 11, 1.<BR> --Caus. To plant, to cause to get offspring, Śāk. 138, 1, Chezy.<BR> --Cf. Goth. liugan, jugga-lauths; A.S. leód, liód, probably λαός, βασι-λεύς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरूढ
दूरूढ दूरूढ, i. e. दुस्-, adj. badly cicatrized, Suśr. 1, 297, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूढ
सु- + रूढ सु- + रूढ, adj. prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह|रुहः
रुह रुह् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Growing.<BR> 2. Mounted.<BR> II. f. हा, Bent grass.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीरुह
जगती- + रुह जगती- + रुह, m. a tree, MBh. 7, 8098.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरुह|जलरुहं
जल- + रुह जल- + रुह, n. a lotus, ib. 1, 5005.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूरुह|तनूरुहं|तनूरुहः
तनू- + रुह तनू- + रुह,<BR> I. m. a son, Śātr. 10, 52.<BR> II. n. (and m.). 1. the hair of the body, Arj. 5, 3. 2. the wing of a bird, Varāh. Bṛh. S. 62, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीररुह
तीर- + रुह तीर- + रुह,<BR> I. adj. growing on the bank of a river, Rām. 2, 95, 4.<BR> II. m. a tree growing on the bank of a river, ib. 104, 4 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजकाण्डरुह
वीज-काण्ड- + रुह वीज-काण्ड- + रुह, adj. springing from a seed, or from a slip, Man. 1, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्वन्
रुह्वन् रुह् + वन्, m. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष्
† रूक्ष् रूक्ष्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from रूक्ष), Par. To be harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष|रूक्षं|रूक्षः
रूक्ष रूक्ष, see रुक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढि|रूढिः
रूढि रूढि, i. e. रुह् + ति.<BR> 1. Growing, Rājat. 5, 477.<BR> 2. Birth.<BR> 3. Notoriety.<BR> 4. Traditional meaning of words as opposed to their etymological signification, Pāṇ. i. 2, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्
रूप् रूप्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from रूप), Par.<BR> 1. To form, to represent in pantomime, Vikr. 6, 6; 12, 16; to notify by a gesture, Vikr. 47, 13.<BR> 2. To feign, Vikr. 12, 17.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि,<BR> 1. To perform, Man. 6, 38.<BR> 2. To represent in pantomime, Śāk. 5, 16; Vikr. 29, 8.<BR> 3. To look out, Vikr. 39, 5; to see, 78, 11; to perceive, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 10.<BR> 4. To consider, to ponder, Hit. 10, 3.<BR> 5. To investigate, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 18; to examine, Hit. 99, 1.<BR> 6. To search, Hit. 68, 14.<BR> 7. To select, Pañc. 161, 10.<BR> 8. To appoint, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a " target="_blank">Page0777-a + 46</a>] 8, 24; 184, 8. निरूपित,<BR> 1. Seen.<BR> 2. Discovered.<BR> 3. Considered, Bhāṣāp. 124.<BR> 4. Ascertained, Bhāṣāp. 107.<BR> 5. Resolved, Pañc. 158, 18.<BR> 6. Appointed.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With वि वि, To disfigure, Hit. 65, 1. विरूपित, Deformed, Man. 4, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिरूपित
सु-निरूपित सु-निरूपित, adj. 1. well-considered, Pañc. iii. d. 74. 2. well-searched, Hit. 91, 1. 3. wellascertained, Hit. 98, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप|रूपं
रूप रूप (probably from रूप्, an old form of रोप्, in रोपय, the Caus. of रुह्), n.<BR> 1. Natural state or condition.<BR> 2. State, Pañc. 137, 19.<BR> 3. Form, Vikr. d. 9; figure, Chr. 17, 28; kind, Pañc. 21, 25.<BR> 4. Appearance.<BR> 5. An image.<BR> 6. Beauty, Pañc. iii. d. 239.<BR> 7. Colour, Bhāṣāp. 2. 99.<BR> 8. A play, a dramatic poem.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अ- + रूप अ- + रूप, adj., f. पा, disfigured, Rām. 2, 23, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरूप|अतिरूपः
अति- + रूप अति- + रूप,<BR> I. n. beauty, Lass. 37, 5.<BR> II. adj. beautiful, Rām. 3, 23, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरूप
अन्य- + रूप अन्य- + रूप,<BR> I. n. another shape, Kathās. 13, 172.<BR> II. adj., f. पा, having another shape, Kathās. 12, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकरूप|अनेकरूपः
अन्-एक- + रूप अन्-एक- + रूप, adj., f. पा, having manifold forms, Hit. ii. d. 174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वरूप
अश्व- + रूप अश्व- + रूप, adj. having the shape of a horse, Pañc. 258, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूप|कामरूपः
काम- + रूप काम- + रूप,<BR> I. n. a shape changing as one lists, MBh. 1, 6077.<BR> II. adj., f. पा, taking any or every shape at will, Megh. 6.<BR> III. m. sing. and pl. the name of a country, Ragh. 4, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंरूप
किंरूप किंरूप, i. e. किम्-, adj. of what shape, Pañc. 258, 13. See कु-, जात- (vb. जन्),<BR> I. n. gold, Nal. 1, 19.<BR> II. adj. golden, MBh. 14, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथारूप
तथा- + रूप तथा- + रूप, adj., f. पा, having such a shape, Pañc. 44, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भरूप|गर्भरूपः
गर्भ- + रूप गर्भ- + रूप, adj. child-like, Utt. Rāmac. 168, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशरूप|देशरूपं
देश- + रूप देश- + रूप, n. suitableness, MBh. 12, 3961.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टरूप
नष्ट- + रूप नष्ट- + रूप, adj. disappeared, MBh. 3, 2604.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारूप|नानारूपः
नाना- + रूप नाना- + रूप,<BR> I. n. pl. many shapes, Rām. 3, 1, 21 Gorr.<BR> II. adj. having many shapes, different, Man. 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मरूप
पद्म- + रूप पद्म- + रूप, adj., f. पा, having the colour of a lotus, MBh. 3, 14404.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंरूप
पुंरूप पुंरूप, i. e. पुंस्-, n. the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b " target="_blank">Page0777-b + 45</a>] shape of a man, Kathās. 39, 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वरूप|पूर्व्वरूप|पूर्व्वरूपं
पूर्व- + रूप पूर्व- + रूप,<BR> I. n. symptom of occurring disease, Suśr. 1, 127, 12.<BR> II. adj., f. पा, having its former shape, Lass. 72, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तरूप|प्राप्तरूपः
प्राप्त- + रूप प्राप्त- + रूप, adj. 1. handsome. 2. learned, wise. 3. suitable, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्यरूप
भव्य- + रूप भव्य- + रूप, adj., f. पा, good, Rām. 3, 52, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तरूप
युक्त- + रूप युक्त- + रूप, adj. suitable, Śāk. d. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
वि- + रूप वि- + रूप,<BR> I. adj. 1. deformed, Pañc. i. d. 159. 2. unusual. 3. wicked, Pañc. 213, 23.<BR> II. n. 1. difference of nature. 2. deformity, Cāṇ. 73 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411; monstrous shape.<BR> III. f. पा, the wife of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरूप|विश्वरूपः
विश्व- + रूप विश्व- + रूप,<BR> I. adj. taking all forms, omnipresent.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूप|सरूपः
स- + रूप स- + रूप, adj. like, resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्परूप|सङ्कल्परूप
संकल्प- + रूप संकल्प- + रूप, adj. conformable to one's wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्व- + रूप स्व- + रूप,<BR> I. n. 1. one's own shape, Chr. 62, 51. 2. natural condition, nature, Pañc. 145, 16. 3. natural and obvious purpose. 4. kind.<BR> II. adj. 1. of like character, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 5. 2. like, similar, suitable, Lass. 35, 12. 3. pleasing, Lass. 20, 11. 4. wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मस्वरूप
आत्मस्वरूप आत्मस्वरूप, i. e. आत्मन्-स्व-, adj. true (just as it happened), Pañc. 43, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वरूप
स्त्री-स्व- + रूप स्त्री-स्व- + रूप, adj. having the body of a female, Chr. 61, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टरूप
हृष्ट- + रूप हृष्ट- + रूप, adj., f. पा, having the hair of the body erect with pleasure, Chr. 60, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपक|रूपकं|रूपकः
रूपक रूप + क, n.<BR> 1. Shape.<BR> 2. A drama.<BR> 3. A kind of coin (cf. रूप्य), Pañc. 127, 8; 252, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारूपक|महारूपकं
महा- + रूपक महा- + रूपक, n. a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
वि- + रूपक वि- + रूपक, adj. 1. mis-shaped. 2. frightful, hideous, used as nickname, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपतस्
रूपतस् रूप + तस्, adv. By shape, Nal. 19, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपवन्त्|रूपवत्
रूपवन्त् रूप + वन्त्, adj., f. वति,<BR> 1. Having shape.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Pañc. i. d. 159, Chr.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरूपवन्त्|अधिकरूपवत्
अधिक- + रूपवन्त् अधिक- + रूपवन्त्, adj., f. वती, most beautiful, Hit. 115, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वरूपवन्त्|स्त्रीस्वरूपवत्
स्त्री-स्व- + रूपवन्त् स्त्री-स्व- + रूपवन्त्, adj. having the body of a female. Chr. 61, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिन्
रूपिन् रूपिन्, i. e. रूप + इन्, adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a " target="_blank">Page0778-a + 43</a>] इणी,<BR> 1. Having shape.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Sāv. 1, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR> When latter part of comp. words, रूप generally belongs to the former part, and the aff. इन् to the comp. word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपिन्
अ- + रूपिन् अ- + रूपिन्, adj. without shape, Rām. 1, 23, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरूपिन्
अन्य- + रूपिन् अन्य- + रूपिन्, adj. having another shape, Kathās. 16, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जररूपिन्
कुञ्जर- + रूपिन् कुञ्जर- + रूपिन्, adj. having the shape of an elephant, Sund. 2, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणकरूपिन्
क्षपणक- + रूपिन् क्षपणक- + रूपिन्, adj. wearing the guise of a Bauddha mendicant, Pañc. 235, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथारूपिन्
तथा- + रूपिन् तथा- + रूपिन्, adj. having such a shape, MBh. 12, 7344.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरूपिन्
देव- + रूपिन् देव- + रूपिन्, adj. having a divine shape, Hiḍ. 2, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगरूपिन्
मृग- + रूपिन् मृग- + रूपिन्, adj. having the shape of an antelope, Rām. 3, 49, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनरूपिन्
साधन- + रूपिन् साधन- + रूपिन्, adj. having the form or caracter of expedients, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपिन्
स्व- + रूपिन् स्व- + रूपिन्, adj. endowed with one's own form, Chr. 26, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वरूपिन्
स्त्री-स्व- + रूपिन् स्त्री-स्व- + रूपिन्, adj. having the body of a female, Chr. 63, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्य|रूप्यं
रूप्य रूप्य, i. e. रूप + य,<BR> I. adj. Handsome, Pāṇ. v. 2, 120.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Silver, Man. 4, 230.<BR> 2. Wrought silver, Pāṇ. ib.<BR> 3. Wrought gold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरूप्य|समरूप्यः
सम- + रूप्य सम- + रूप्य, i. e. समरूप + य, adj. of like or same origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्यक
ऽरूप्यक -रूप्य + क, in सुवर्ण-रूप्य + क, adj. Abounding in gold and silver, Rām. 4, 40, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्यमय
रूप्यमय रूप्य + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of silver, Pañc. 241, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूष्
रूष् रूष्, i. 1, Par. † To decorate.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To tremble.<BR> 2. To burst.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. रूषित.<BR> 1. Adorned, Indr. 5, 8.<BR> 2. Inlaid, covered, Rām. 4, 19, 32.<BR> 3. Made rough or rugged.<BR> 4. Pounded, reduced to dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रे
रे रे, A vocative particle, implying contempt or woe, Hit. 81, 21; Bhartṛ. 1, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक्
† रेक् रेक्, i. 1, Ātm. To suspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक रेक,<BR> I. m., and f. का.<BR> 1. Doubt. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b " target="_blank">Page0778-b + 42</a>]<BR> 2. Fear.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Loosening, purging (i. e. रिच् + अ).<BR> 2. An outcaste.<BR> 3. A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक्णस्
रेक्णस् रेक्णस्, i. e. रिच् + नस्, n. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखा
रेखा रेखा, i. e. लिख् + अ, f.<BR> 1. A line, Pañc. ii. d. 183.<BR> 2. Drawing, Śāk. d. 141.<BR> 3. A stripe, Pañc. i. d. 209.<BR> 4. A little, Pañc. ii. d. 148.<BR> 5. Fraud.<BR> 6. Fulness, satisfaction.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. riga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्ररेखा|चंद्ररेखा
चन्द्र- + रेखा चन्द्र- + रेखा, f. खा the crescent, Rām. 5, 20, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररेखा
पत्र- + रेखा पत्र- + रेखा, f. खा, decorating the person by staining it with fragrant pigments of sandal, musk, etc., Ragh. 16, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरेख
सम-रेख सम-रेख, adj. straight, Śāk. d. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचक|रेचकं|रेचकः
रेचक रेचक, i. e. रिच् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Purgative, aperient.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A purgative.<BR> 2. A proper name, Vikr. 76, 2 (but cf. Wilson, Spec. of the Theatre of the Hind. i. 2. ed. p. 260, n.).<BR> III. n. A purge.<BR> IV. m. or n. Exhalation, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 9; a method of suppressing the breath, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचन|रेचनं
रेचन रेचन, i. e. रिच् + अन, n., and f. ना,<BR> 1. Purging, looseness.<BR> 2. Evacuating, Bhāṣāp. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
रेज् रेज्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To shine.<BR> 2. Ved. To tremble.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, To tremble vehemently, Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 87, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेट्
† रेट् रेट्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणु|रेणुः
रेणु रेणु, m. (and f.), Dust, Vikr. d. 4; Pañc. ii. d. 108.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसरेणु|त्रसरेणुः
त्रस- + रेणु त्रस- + रेणु, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तरेणु|रक्तरेणुः
रक्त- + रेणु रक्त- + रेणु, m. 1. red lead. 2. the blossom of the Butea frondosa. 3. a sort of cloth. 4. an angry man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतारेणु
सिकता- + रेणु सिकता- + रेणु, m. a grain of sand, Pañc. ii. d. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेणु
सु- + रेणु सु- + रेणु and हेरोअ-, n. sorts of atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुका
रेणुका रेणु + का, f.<BR> 1. A sort of perfume and medicine.<BR> 2. A sort of pulse, Ervum.<BR> 3. The wife of जमदग्नि and mother of परशु-राम, MBh. 3, 11072.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस्
रेतस् रेतस्, i. e. री + तस्,<BR> 1. Semen virile, MBh. 13, 1160.<BR> 2. Quicksilver.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वरेतस्
ऊर्ध्व- + रेतस् ऊर्ध्व- + रेतस्,<BR> I. adj. chaste, MBh. 2, 470; Hariv. 949.<BR> II. m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भरेतस्
कुम्भ- + रेतस् कुम्भ- + रेतस्,<BR> I. n. semen virile contained in a jar, MBh. 13, 7372.<BR> II. m. a name of Agni, MBh. 3, 14139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुरेतस्
वसु- + रेतस् वसु- + रेतस्, m. fire, MBh. 1, 1021.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निरेतस्
वह्नि- + रेतस् वह्नि- + रेतस्, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरेतस्
विश्व- + रेतस् विश्व- + रेतस्, m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यरेतस्
हिरण्य- + रेतस् हिरण्य- + रेतस्, m. 1. fire, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 14. 2. the sun. 3. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्र|रेत्रं
रेत्र रेत्र, i. e. री + त्र, n.<BR> 1. Semen virile.<BR> 2. Nectar.<BR> 3. Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप्
† रेप् रेप्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप रेप, i. e. लिप् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Low.<BR> 2. Niggardly.<BR> 3. Cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेपस्
रेपस् रेपस्, i. e. लिप् + अस्, n. Wrong or blameable action.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेपस्
वि- + रेपस् वि- + रेपस्, adj. without blemish, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफ|रेफः
रेफ रेफ,<BR> I. adj. Contemptible, bad.<BR> II. m. The letter र्.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरेफ|द्विरेफः
द्वि- + रेफ द्वि- + रेफ, m. A sort of bee (properly containing two र्ऽs in its name भ्रमर), Hariv. 4585.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेब्
रेब् रेब्, see रेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभ्
रेभ् रेभ्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. Ved. Par. To praise.<BR> --Cf. ῥοίϐδην, ῥοῖϐδος, ῥοιϐδέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभण|रेभणं
रेभण रेभण, i. e. रेभ् + अन, n. The lowing of kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेव्
† रेव् रेव्, रेब् रेब्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go by leaps, to flow.<BR> 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्त्|रेवत्
रेवन्त् रेवन्त्, i. e. रयि + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Wealthy, Chr. 295, 14 = [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b " target="_blank">Page0779-b + 40</a>] Rigv. i. 92, 14.<BR> II. f. वती.<BR> 1. A cow.<BR> 2. The last of the lunar asterisms.<BR> 3. One of the मातृस् or energies of the gods.<BR> 4. The wife of बल-राम, Megh. 50, cf. Viṣṇu P. 439.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्त|रेवन्तः
रेवन्त रेवन्त् + अ, m. The fifth Manu of the present Kalpa or period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवा
रेवा रेवा (akin to रेवन्त्), f.<BR> 1. The नर्मदा river, Megh. 19.<BR> 2. The wife of Kāma.<BR> 3. The indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
† रेष् रेष् (for ह्रेष्, q. cf.), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To howl.<BR> 2. To neigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै रै, i. 1, Par. To bark.<BR> --Cf. Lat. latrare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै रै (cf. रयि), m.<BR> 1. Wealth, property, Chr. 287, 1 = Rigv. i. 48, 1.<BR> 2. Gold.<BR> --Cf. Lat. res.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैत्य
रैत्य रैत्य, i. e. रीति + य, adj. Brazen, made of brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत|रैवतः
रैवत रैवत, i. e. रेवन्त् + अ (cf. रेवन्त), m.<BR> 1. The fifth Manu, Man. 1, 62.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva.<BR> 3. A Daitya.<BR> 4. A mountain, the eastern part of the Vindhya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतक|रैवतकं|रैवतकः
रैवतक रैवत + क, m.<BR> 1. The mountain रैवत.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतिक|रैवतिकः
रैवतिक रैवतिक, i. e. रेवती + इक (cf. रेवन्त्), m. A descendant of रेवती, Pāṇ. iv. 1, 146; iv. 3, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोक|रोकं|रोकः
रोक रोक, i. e. रुच् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. Buying with ready money.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A hole.<BR> 2. A boat.<BR> 3. Moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग|रोगः
रोग रोग, i. e. रुज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Disease, Pañc. iii. d. 244.<BR> 2. A sort of Costus, C. speciosus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग|अरोगः
अ- + रोग अ- + रोग,<BR> I. m. health, Hit. i. d. 166, M.M.<BR> II. adj., f. गा, healthy, Man. 1, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रोग
क्षुद्रोग क्षुद्रोग, i. e. क्षुध्-, m. hunger, Pañc. 70, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषारोग
तृषा- + रोग तृषा- + रोग, m. a morbose thirst, MBh. 12, 11268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरोग
नीरोग नीरोग, i. e. निस्-, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a " target="_blank">Page0780-a + 44</a>] healthy, Pañc. i. d. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरोग|पांडुरोग|पाण्डुरोगः
पाण्डु- + रोग पाण्डु- + रोग, m. the jaundice, Suśr. 1, 90, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापरोग|पापरोगः
पाप- + रोग पाप- + रोग, m. a disease considered as a punishment for sin, Man. 5, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोग
स- + रोग स- + रोग, adj. sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्रोग|हृद्रोगः
हृद्- + रोग हृद्- + रोग, m. 1. any disease of the heart. 2. heart-burn. 3. sorrow, Chr. 289, 11 = Rigv. i. 50, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगभाज्
रोगभाज् रोगभाज्, i. e. रोग-भज्, adj. One who suffers from a disease, Pañc. i. d. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिता
रोगिता रोगिता, i. e. रोगिन् + ता, f. in अ-, Health, Hit. pr. d. 19, M.M. स-, f. Sickness, Hit. ii. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिन्
रोगिन् रोगिन्, i. e. रोग + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Sick, Man. 2, 138.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिन्
अ- + रोगिन् अ- + रोगिन्, adj. healthy, Hit. iii. d. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरोगिन्
पाण्डु- + रोगिन् पाण्डु- + रोगिन्, i. e. पाण्डु-रोग + इन्, adj. jaundiced, Suśr. 1, 45, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापरोगिन्
पाप- + रोगिन् पाप- + रोगिन्, i. e. पाप-रोग + इन्, adj. one who suffers from a disease considered as a punishment for sin, Man. 3, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचक|रोचकः
रोचक रोचक, i. e. रुच् + अक,<BR> 1. adj. What pleases, brightens.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Hunger.<BR> 2. A stomachic.<BR> 3. A sort of onion.<BR> 4. Plantain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचक|अरोचकः
अ- + रोचक अ- + रोचक,<BR> I. adj. producing want of appetite, Suśr. 1, 207, 13.<BR> II. m. want of appetite, ib. 1, 169, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचन|रोचनः
रोचन रोचन, i. e. रुच् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Irradiating.<BR> 2. Splendid.<BR> 3. Pleasing.<BR> 4. Sharpening (the appetite).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A stomachic.<BR> 2. The name of several plants.<BR> III. f. ना and नी, A yellow pigment, supposed to be the concrete bile of the cow, or to be found in the head of the animal, Man. 8, 234.<BR> IV. f. ना, An excellent woman.<BR> V. f. नी, Red arsenic, Pāṇ. iv. 2, 2.<BR> VI. n. The æther, Chr. 288, 1 = Rigv. i. 49, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरोचना
गो-रोचना गो-रोचना, f. a yellow pigment, Pañc. i. d. 107 =<BR> III. योग-रोचना, f. a magical रोचना, or unguent, which makes invisible and invulnerable, Mṛcch. 47, 22--24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशरोचना
वंश-रोचना वंश-रोछना, f. Bambu manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिष्णु|रोचिष्णुः
रोचिष्णु रोचिष्णु, i. e. रुच् + इष्णु, adj. Elegantly dressed, Pāṇ. iii. 2, 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिस्
रोचिस् रोचिस्, i. e. रुच् + इस्, n. Light, flame.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुरोचिस्
वसु- + रोचिस् वसु- + रोचिस्, n. a religious ceremony in which the Vasus especially are worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोड्
† रोड् रोड् (cf. रुष्), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be mad.<BR> 2. and रौट् रौट्, रौड् रौड्, i. 1, Par. To despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदन|रोदनं
रोदन रोदन, i. e. रुद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Weeping, Lass. 30, 7.<BR> 2. A tear, tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदस्
रोदस् रोदस्, i. e. रुद् + अस् (the seat of the roaring storm), n. Heaven. du. सी, and as former part of a comp. Heaven and earth, Vikr. d. 1; Chr. 46, 23; Nal. 3, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
रोध रोध, i. e. रुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstruction, Kir. 5, 15.<BR> 2. A bank, a shore.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणरोध|प्राणरोधः
प्राण- + रोध प्राण- + रोध, m. danger of life, Hit. iv. d. 23 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3136).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधन|रोधनः
रोधन रोधन, i. e. रुध् + अन,<BR> I. adj. That which obstructs.<BR> II. m. The planet Mercury.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Obstructing.<BR> 2. Besieging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधस्
रोधस् रोधस्, i. e. रुध् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. A bank, a shore, Vikr. d. 8.<BR> 2. The brink of a well, Bhāg. P. 9, 19, 4.<BR> 3. The flank, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधिन्
ऽरोधिन् -रोधिन्, i. e. रुध् + इन्, adj. Stopping, Rājat. 5, 346; Śāk. d. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्र|रोध्रं|रोध्रः
रोध्र रोध्र, i. e.<BR> I. रुध् + र, n.<BR> 1. Sin.<BR> 2. Offence.<BR> II. Probably akin to रुधिर, m. A tree, the bark of which is used in dyeing, Ragh. 2, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप्
रोप् रोप्, see रुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
रोप रोप,<BR> I. m. probably रुह्, Caus., + अ, An arrow.<BR> II. i. e. रुप् = लुप् + अ, Confusing.<BR> III. n. A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपण|रोपणं|रोपणः
रोपण रोपण, n.<BR> I. i. e. रुह्, Caus., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a " target="_blank">Page0781-a + 41</a>] + अन.<BR> 1. Planting.<BR> 2. Raising.<BR> 3. Placing.<BR> 4. Cicatrizing.<BR> 5. A healing application to sores.<BR> II. i. e. रुप् = लुप् + अन, Confusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपणाका
रोपणाका रोपणाका, f. A bird, Turdus salica, Chr. 289, 12 = Rigv. i. 50, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
रोम रोम, n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्
रोमन् रोमन्, i. e. रुह् + मन्, n. The hair of the body, Pañc. iii. d. 186.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वरोमन्
ऊर्ध्व- + रोमन् ऊर्ध्व- + रोमन्,<BR> I. adj. one whose hairs are erect, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 28.<BR> II. m. the name of a mountain, ib. 5, 20, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनरोमन्
काञ्चन- + रोमन् काञ्चन- + रोमन्, and सुवर्ण-, adj. having gold-like wool, Rām. 3, 49, 4; (Pañc. 35, 1, i. e. a ram).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धरोमन्
स्तब्ध- + रोमन् स्तब्ध- + रोमन् (vb. स्तम्भ्), m. a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थ|रोमंथः|रोमन्थः
रोमन्थ रोमन्थ, probably a noun derived from रुज्, and compounded with मन्थ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Ruminating, Śāk. d. 39.<BR> 2. Chewing, Rājat. 5, 364.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. ita-ruchjan; A.S. roccettan; Lat. rūmen, ruminare (for rug-men), ructare; ἐρεύγομαι (old frequent.), ἐρυγγάνω, ὀρυγγάνω, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थाय
रोमन्थाय रोमन्थाय, a denomin. derived from रोमन्थ with य, Ātm. To ruminate, Pāṇ. iii. 1, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमवन्त्|रोमवत्
रोमवन्त् रोमवन्त्, i. e. रोमन् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Hairy, woolly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमश|रोमशः
रोमश रोमश, i. e. रोमन् + श,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Hairy, Man. 3, 7.<BR> 2. Woolly.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ram.<BR> 2. A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्च|रोमांच|रोमाञ्चः
रोमाञ्च रोमाञ्च, i. e. रोमन्-अञ्च् + अ, m. Horripilation, considered as a sign of rapture, Pañc. ii. d. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्चित|रोमांचित|रोमाञ्चितः
रोमाञ्चित रोमाञ्चित, i. e. रोमाञ्च + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Affected with horripilation, Utt. Rāmac. 81, 4.<BR> 2. Enraptured, Pañc. 128, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष|रोषः
रोष रोष, i. e. रोष् + अ, m. Anger, wrath, Vikr. d. 144; Pañc. 174, 25. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b " target="_blank">Page0781-b + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोष
वि- + रोष वि- + रोष, adj. angry, Draup. 9, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोष
स- + रोष स- + रोष, adj. angry, Śiś. 9, 83. षम्, adv. angrily, Vikr. 55, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषण|रोषणः
रोषण रोषण, i. e. रुष् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Angry.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Quicksilver.<BR> 2. A touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषणता
रोषणता रोषण + ता, f. Wrath, Śāk. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोह|रोहः
रोह रोह, i. e. रुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A bud.<BR> 2. Mounting, Rājat. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहक|रोहकः
रोहक रोहक, i. e. रुह् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Riding, mounted on any vehicle.<BR> II. m. A sort of goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहण|रोहणं|रोहणः
रोहण रोहण, i. e. रुह् + अन,<BR> I. m. A mountain, Adam's peak in Ceylon, Pañc. MS. Berol., cf. Wilson in Trans. of the R.A.S. i. 169.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Growing.<BR> 2. Mountaing.<BR> 3. Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिण|रोहिणं|रोहिणः
रोहिण रोहिण, i. e. रुह् + इन् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The Indian fig-tree.<BR> 2. A fragrant grass.<BR> II. n. A part of the forenoon. See रोहित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित्
रोहित् रोहित्, probably akin to रुधिर, ह् for ध्,<BR> I. m. The sun.<BR> II. f. The female of the black antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित|रोहितं|रोहितः
रोहित रोहित, akin to रुधिर, ह् for ध्,<BR> I. adj., f. ता and इणी.<BR> 1. Red.<BR> 2. Coloured, Man. 1, 38.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Red, the colour.<BR> 2. A (kind of) deer, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 4.<BR> 3. A fish, Cyprinas rohita, Man. 5, 16.<BR> III. f. इणी, also रोहिणि रोहिणि.<BR> 1. The fourth lunar asterism, Vikr. 38, 12 (णी).<BR> 2. The mother of बल-राम.<BR> IV. f. इणी.<BR> 1. Lightning.<BR> 2. A girl at the commencement of the menstruation, Pañc. iii. d. 213.<BR> 3. A woman stained with red pigments.<BR> 4. Inflammatory affection of the throat.<BR> 5. A cow.<BR> 6. Yellow myrobalan.<BR> 7. Bengal madder.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. Blood.<BR> 2. Safflower.<BR> 3. The rainbow appearing in a straight form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिन्
रोहिन् रोहिन्,<BR> I. रुह् + इन्, m.<BR> 1. The Indian fig-tree.<BR> 2. The holy figtree.<BR> II. (cf. रोकित्.) A stag, Rām. 5, 36, 35 (but perhaps is to be read रोहिन्-मांसम्, i. e. रोहित्-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्म
रौक्म रौक्म, i. e. रुक्म + अ, adj. Golden, Man. 4, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्ष्य|रौक्ष्यं
रौक्ष्य रौक्ष्य, i. e. रू̆क्ष + य, n. Roughness, hardness, Ragh. 5, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौचनिक
रौचनिक रौचनिक, i. e. रोचना + इक, adj., f. की, Yellowish, Kir. 5, 45 (cf. also Pāṇ. 4, 2, 2 Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौच्य|रौच्यः
रौच्य रौच्य, m. An ascetic with a staff of Vilva wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौट्
रौट् रौट्, रौड् रौड्, see रोड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्र|रौद्रं|रौद्रः
रौद्र रौद्र, i. e. रुद्र + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. द्री.<BR> 1. Relating to Rudra-Śiva, Arj. 3, 50; cf. 10, 42; descended from Rudra, Johns. Sel. 22, 117.<BR> 2. Formidable, Pañc. i. d. 116.<BR> 3. Irascible.<BR> 4. Acute.<BR> II. m. Heat.<BR> III. f. री, The wife of Śiva.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरौद्र
अति- + रौद्र अति- + रौद्र, adj. exceedingly terrible, Pañc. 216, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमरौद्र
सोम- + रौद्र सोम- + रौद्र, the name of a holy text (perhaps Rigv. vi. 74), Man. 11, 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रता
रौद्रता रौद्र + ता, f. Horribleness, Mālat. 77, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रीभाव
रौद्रीभाव रौद्रीभाव, i. e. रौद्र-भू + अ, m. The character of Śiva, Johns. Sel. 93, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्य|रौप्यं
रौप्य रौप्य, i. e. रूप्य + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Of silver, Man. 8, 135.<BR> 2. Like silver, Rām. 3, 48, 12.<BR> II. n. Silver, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्यमय
रौप्यमय रौप्य + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of silver, Rājat. 5, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौम|रौमं
रौम रौम, and रौमक रौम + क, n. A sort of salt (cf. रुमन्वन्त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरव|रौरवः
रौरव रौरव,<BR> I. i. e. रुरु + अ, adj., f. वी.<BR> 1. Proceeding from the common [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b " target="_blank">Page0782-b + 43</a>] deer (viz. flesh, etc.), Man. 2, 41; 3, 269; Utt. Rāmac. 105, 11.<BR> 2. Unsteady.<BR> II. adj.<BR> 1. Formidable.<BR> 2. Dishonest.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The name of a hell, Man. 4, 88.<BR> 2. A savage.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारौरव|महारौरवः
महा- + रौरव महा- + रौरव, m. the name of a hell, Man. 4, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिण|रौहिणं|रौहिणः
रौहिण रौहिण (cf. रोहित), n. Sandal wood, MBh. 1, 1381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिष|रौहिषं|रौहिषः
रौहिष रौहिष (cf. रोहित्),<BR> I. m. A sort of deer.<BR> II. f. षी.<BR> 1. A doe.<BR> 2. A creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्
लक् लक्, see रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तक|लक्तकः
लक्तक लक्तक, n.<BR> 1. A rag, or rags.<BR> 2. i. e. = रक्त + क (vb. रञ्ज्), Lac, the animal dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्
लक्ष् लक्ष् i. 10 (probably a denomin. derived from लक्ष), Par. and Ātm.<BR> 1. To mark, MBh. 3, 14852.<BR> 2. To see, Vikr. d. 8; to perceive, Śāk. 16, 20. Pass. To appear, Vikr. d. 53; MBh. 3, 2110.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लक्षित, Perceived, evident, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. लक्ष्य.<BR> 1. To be seen, visible, Vikr. d. 37; Daśak. in Chr. 198, 24.<BR> 2. Deserving to be regarded, Hit. iv. d. 14.<BR> 3. To be defined or described, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 10.<BR> 4. Having attributes attached, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 14; 23. n.<BR> 1. A mark.<BR> 2. A butt.<BR> 3. Aim, Utt. Rāmac. 124, 8 (बद्ध, vb. बन्ध्, adj. Having taken his aim); Megh. 72 (कामिन्-, Aim, represented by lovers).<BR> 4. Object, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 22.<BR> 5. A Lac, a hundred thousand, Hit. ii. d. 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. invisible, Kathās. 24, 8. 2. undistinguishable, unimportant, Kumāras. 5, 72.<BR> अभि-लक्ष्य + म्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-a " target="_blank">Page0783-a + 42</a>] adv. to the aim, Rām. 2, 63, 22.<BR> दुर्ल्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be perceived, Bhāg. P. 7, 10, 53.<BR> यूप-, m. a bird.<BR> स्थूल-, adj. 1. = स्थूल-लक्ष (see लक्ष). 2. aiming carelessly.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be seen, to perform, to settle, Chr. 20, 17.<BR> 2. To signify, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 17.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभिलक्षित, Marked.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To see, to perceive, MBh. 2, 2403.<BR> 2. To view, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 12. Pass. To appear, Śāk. d. 133. आलक्ष्य, Śāk. d. 176, is लक्ष्य with आ, adj. Hardly visible.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To direct one's look to, Lass. 2. ed. 66, 17.<BR> 2. To see, MBh. 1, 5249.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To see, to perceive, Vikr. 78, 21; MBh. 3, 2186.<BR> 2. To suspect, Śāk. 15, 15.<BR> 3. To consider, MBh. 3, 12188.<BR> 4. Pass. To be probable, Rām. 2, 61, 11. उपलक्षित, Comprehended, understood.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. not perceived, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 15.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप. To see, to perceive, MBh. 2, 1557.<BR> --With निस् निस्; निर्लक्ष्य, Kathās. 6, 119, is लक्ष्य with निस्, adj. Imperceivable.<BR> --With वि वि, To perceive, Gīt. 2, 19; to see, Pañc. 235, 25. विलक्षित,<BR> 1. Seen.<BR> 2. Affected without a cause.<BR> 3. Disappointed, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 13; Johns. Sel. 52, 115 (rival).<BR> 4. Unmarked (i. e. लक्षित with वि, adj.).<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To perceive, MBh. 3, 16751.<BR> 2. Pass. To appear, Vikr. d. 157. संलक्षित, Distinguished. संलक्ष्य, To be marked.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुःस्˚, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be perceived, Rājat. 6, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षित
अ- + लक्षित अ- + लक्षित, adj. unobserved, Hit. 65, 10, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षित
सु-लक्षित सु-लक्षित, adj. well-ascertained, Man. 8, 403.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष|लक्षं
लक्ष लक्ष, probably from रङ्ज्, and for original रक्त,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A mark, MBh. 3, 14852; Caurap. 15.<BR> 2. Aim, Ragh. 1, 61; Vikr. 54, 4 (? look, perhaps corr. ˚लक्षणः). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b " target="_blank">Page0783-b + 46</a>]<BR> 3. Disguise, fraud.<BR> II. m., and f. क्षा, and n. (Pañc. 255, 23), A Lac, a hundred thousand, Pañc. 255, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
वि- + लक्ष वि- + लक्ष, adj. 1. unmarked. 2. having no characteristic property. 3. having a mark or character contrary to what is usual. 4. surprised. 5. (one who has missed his aim), ashamed, abashed, Pañc. 29, 15; embarrassed, Pañc. 147, 4. 6. with कृ, becoming विलक्षी कृ, to scoff, to insult, Kathās. 6, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष|स्थूललक्षः
स्थूल- + लक्ष स्थूल- + लक्ष, adj. 1. liberal, Indr. 4, 11. 2. wise. 3. remembering both benefits and offences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण|लक्षणं|लक्षणः
लक्षण लक्षण, i. e. लक्ष् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Seeing, sight.<BR> 2. A characteristic mark, Pañc. iii. d. 130; Bhartṛ. 2, 70; a spot.<BR> 3. A holy mark, Hit. 99, 7; a lucky mark, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 11.<BR> 4. Form, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 38.<BR> 5. A name, Pañc. iii. d. 35 (read यात्रालक्षणम्, called यात्रा).<BR> 6. An indication, a definition, Man. 1, 112.<BR> 7. Settlement, 8, 406.<BR> 8. A symptom of actual disease.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The Indian crane.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> III. f. ना.<BR> 1. Metonymy, as distinguished from a word's literal meaning, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 16; Bhāṣāp. 81. Cf. Sāhitya Darp. 11.<BR> 2. The female of the Indian crane.<BR> 3. A goose.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षण|अलक्षणं
अ- + लक्षण अ- + लक्षण,<BR> I. n. a mark of ill fortune, Man. 4, 156.<BR> II. adj., f. णा, 1. without distinguishing marks, Man. 1, 5. 2. inauspicious, Ragh. 14, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहल्लक्षणा
अजहल्लक्षणा अजहल्लक्षणा, i. e. अ-जहत्- (vb. 2. हा), f. using a word in an elliptic meaning, without depriving it of its original signification; e. g. शोण, adj. ‘of a chesnut colour,’ in the sense of ‘a horse of a chesnut colour,’ Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतलक्षण|कृतलक्षणः
कृत- + लक्षण कृत- + लक्षण, adj. brandished, Man. 9, 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्यजुःसामलक्षण
ऋग्यजुःसामलक्षण ऋग्यजुःसामलक्षण, i. e. ऋच्-यजुस्-सामन्-, adj. named Ṛc, Yājus, and Sāman, Man. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलक्षण
ज्ञान- + लक्षण ज्ञान- + लक्षण, adj., f. णा, one of the three transcendental perceptions, Bhāṣāp. 62, cf. 64. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a " target="_blank">Page0784-a + 44</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विलक्षण
द्वि- + लक्षण द्वि- + लक्षण, adj. of two kinds, Man. 7, 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लक्षण|निर्लक्षणः
निर्लक्षण निर्लक्षण, i. e. निस्-, adj. not distinguished, unimportant, Rām. 2, 113, 5 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्षण
राजलक्षण राजलक्षण, i. e. राजन्-, n. 1. royal insignia. 2. any natural mark indicating royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षितलक्षण
लक्षित- + लक्षण लक्षित- + लक्षण, adj., f. णा, in which are evident the marks (of a town), Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
वि- + लक्षण वि- + लक्षण, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषलक्षण
विशेष- + लक्षण विशेष- + लक्षण, n. characteristic mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यलक्षण
सामान्य- + लक्षण सामान्य- + लक्षण, f. णा, one of the three transcendental perceptions, Bhāṣāp. 62. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षण
सु- + लक्षण सु- + लक्षण,<BR> I. adj. having auspicious marks, Rām. 3, 49, 57.<BR> II. n. determining.<BR> III. f. णा, a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षता
लक्षता लक्ष + ता, f. Condition of being the aim, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षितत्व
लक्षितत्व लक्षित + त्व (vb. लक्ष्), n. Condition of being hinted at, of being supplied, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मण|लक्ष्मणं|लक्ष्मणः
लक्ष्मण लक्ष्मण, i. e. लक्ष्मन् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The son of Daśaratha by Sumitrā, Rām. 3, 50, 24.<BR> 2. The Indian crane, Arj. 9, 21.<BR> II. f. णा, The female of the Indian crane.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A mark, a spot, Śiś. 9, 31 (and at the same time Lakṣmaṇa).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहलक्ष्मण
सह- + लक्ष्मण सह- + लक्ष्मण, adj. with Lakṣmaṇa, Rām. 3, 52, 2.<BR> 2. A name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मन्
लक्ष्मन् लक्ष् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. A mark, Ragh. 19, 30; a spot, Śāk. d. 19.<BR> 2. Chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मी
लक्ष्मी लक्ष्मी, i. e. लक्ष्म (i. e. curtailed लक्ष्मन्), + ई, f. (nom. sing. मीस्).<BR> 1. The wife of Viṣṇu, and goddess of prosperity, Rām. 3, 52, 26; Hit. pr. d. 31, M.M.<BR> 2. Prosperity, Bhartṛ. 2, 54.<BR> 3. Wealth, Bhartṛ. 2, 14; Rājat. 5, 18.<BR> 4. Beauty, splendour, Kir. 5, 39; Vikr. d. 23; Śāk. d. 19.<BR> 5. Royal power, Pañc. iii. d. 32; dominion, Rājat. 5, 136.<BR> 6. Superhuman power.<BR> 7. Sīta, the wife of Rāma.<BR> 8. A pearl.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्मी
अ- + लक्ष्मी अ- + लक्ष्मी, f. bad luck, Rām. 3, 72, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृशलक्ष्मी
अ-कृश- + लक्ष्मी अ-कृश- + लक्ष्मी, adj., n. मि [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b " target="_blank">Page0784-b + 43</a>] (nom. sing. m., f. मीस्), endowed with great prosperity, Kir. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयलक्ष्मी
जय- + लक्ष्मी जय- + लक्ष्मी, f. 1. Lakṣmī, as deity of victory, Rājat. 5, 245. 2. a proper name, ib. 7, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालक्ष्मी
महा- + लक्ष्मी महा- + लक्ष्मी, f. Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मी
राजलक्ष्मी राजलक्ष्मी, i. e. राजन्-, f. royal majesty, Vikr. d. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीक
ऽलक्ष्मीक -लक्ष्मी + क, at the end of comp. adj.; e. g. पुत्र-सम्-क्रान्त-, Having transferred the royal power to (their) sons, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीवन्त्|लक्ष्मीवत्
लक्ष्मीवन्त् लक्ष्मी + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Fortunate.<BR> 2. Wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्यता
लक्ष्यता लक्ष्य + ता (see लक्ष्), f. Visibility, Rājat. 5, 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लख्
† लख् लख्, लङ्ख् लङ्ख्, लिङ्ख् लिङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्
1. लग् लग्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To adhere, Pañc. i. d. 340.<BR> 2. To attach one's self, Pañc. 245, 6.<BR> 3. To stick (in the throat), Śiś. 9, 69.<BR> 4. To pass away, to expire, Pañc. 185, 19.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. लग्न.<BR> 1. Attached, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13; impressed, Hit. pr. d. 8, M.M.; joined, Hit. 35, 12; following, Pañc. 106, 13; impending, 50, 18.<BR> 2. Left, Śāk. d. 32.<BR> 3. Intent on, occupied, being about, Pañc. 244, 6.<BR> 4. Auspicious, Hit. 89, 8, M.M. m. A bard. n.<BR> 1. The rising of a sign, its appearance above the horizon, Lass. 24, 8.<BR> 2. Auspicious time, Hit. 97, 13; cf. 94, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनुलग्न, Following, Lass. 30, 10.<BR> --With अव अव, अवलग्न, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a " target="_blank">Page0785-a + 40</a>]<BR> 1. Attached.<BR> 2. m. and n. The waist, Śiś. 9, 49.<BR> --With वि वि, विलग्न,<BR> 1. Joined, attached, Śiś. 9, 20; clinging to, ib. 84; Pañc. 259, 2 (तत्रैव विलग्नः, Took hold of it).<BR> 2. Touching, Pañc. 186, 9.<BR> 3. Tarried, Pañc. 207, 22. n. The waist.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संलग्न, Joined, adhering.<BR> --Cf. perhaps λήγω (but cf. लञ्ज and लङ्गूल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादलग्न
पाद- + लग्न पाद- + लग्न, adj. being in the foot, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 483.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठलग्न
पृष्ठ- + लग्न पृष्ठ- + लग्न, adj. m. one who follows, a partisan, Pañc. 125, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभलग्न|शुभलग्नः
शुभ- + लग्न शुभ- + लग्न, m. (?), an auspicious moment, Hit. 94, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताग्रलग्न
हस्ताग्र- + लग्न हस्ताग्र- + लग्न, i. e. हस्त-अग्र-, adj., f. ना, married, Pañc. 119, 6 (since I have been married to you).<BR> II. लगित.<BR> 1. Connected.<BR> 2. Obtained.<BR> 3. Entered, Hit. 129, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्
2. लग् लग्, see रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगड|लगडं
लगड लगड, adj. Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुड|लगुडः
लगुड लगुड, m.<BR> 1. A stick, a staff, Hit. 51, 6, M.M.<BR> 2. An iron club, a club, Hit. 101, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नक|लग्नकः
लग्नक लग्न + क (vb. लग्), m. A surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघट्
लघट् लघट्, and लघटि लघटि, m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघय
लघय लघय, a denomin. derived from लघु, Par.<BR> 1. To make light, Kir. 5, 4.<BR> 2. To alleviate, to soften, Vikr. d. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिमन्
लघिमन् लघिमन्, i. e. लघु + इमन्, m.<BR> 1. Lightness, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 7.<BR> 2. A supernatural faculty to make one's self as light as one lists, Lass. 3, 18.<BR> 3. Diminutiveness.<BR> 4. Insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघु|लघुः
लघु लघु, i. e. लङ्घ् + उ,<BR> I. adj., f. घु and घ्वी, comparat. लघुतर and लघीयंस्, superl. लघुतम and लघिष्ठ,<BR> 1. Light, Pañc. 76, 18; easy, Pañc. 202, 4; लघीयंस्, Very light, Pañc. i. d. 119.<BR> 2. Insignificant, Pañc. 68, 6; 172, 4 (innoxious).<BR> 3. Quick, Pañc. 55, 11.<BR> 4. Beautiful.<BR> 5. Clean, Man. 2, 70.<BR> 6. Little, Pañc. i. d. 301; small, Pañc. ii. d. 38; narrow, Pañc. 170, 24.<BR> 7. Young, Pañc. 253, 13; younger, Pañc. 220, 3.<BR> 8. Feeble, Man. 7, 209; Pañc. iii. d. 28.<BR> 9. Mean, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b " target="_blank">Page0785-b + 42</a>] low, Cāṇ. 68 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411; living in a low position, Pañc. ii. d. 71.<BR> 10. Vain, frivolous.<BR> 11. Short, as a vowel, Śrut. 3.<BR> 12. A way of flying (of birds), Pañc. ii. d. 57.<BR> II. acc. sing. n. घु, adv. Quickly, Lass. 81, 13 (Prākṛ.).<BR> III. f. घ्वी.<BR> 1. A delicate woman.<BR> 2. A light carriage.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἐλαχύς, ἐλαϕρός, λαγώς; Lat. lepus (for old lephus; cf. formus for old phormus, s. v. घर्म, and रुधिर, and स्कन्ध); Lat. levis; Goth. leihts; O.H.G. lîhti; A.S. lîht.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघु
अ- + लघु अ- + लघु, adj. 1. heavy, Śiś. 9, 78. 2. powerful, ib. 9, 38. 3. long, as a vowel, Śrut. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलघु
परि- + लघु परि- + लघु, adj. 1. very small, Utt. Rāmac. 107, 9. 2. very pure, Megh. 13. 3. very indifferent, Utt. Rāmac. 100, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुता
लघुता लघु + ता, f.<BR> 1. Lightness.<BR> 2. Wantonness, Śiś. 9, 56.<BR> 3. Meanness, insignificance.<BR> 4. Disrespect, Pañc. i. d. 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुत्व|लघुत्वं
लघुत्व लघु + त्व, n. Disregard, Pañc. i. d. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुविवरत्व
लघुविवरत्व लघु-विवर + त्व, n. The opening being narrow. Pañc. 170, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्का|लंका
लङ्का लङ्का, f.<BR> 1. The capital of Ceylon, Lass. 5, 3.<BR> 2. Ceylon, Rām. 3, 53, 35; Pañc. iii. d. 268.<BR> 3. The name of a शाकिनी, or evil spirit.<BR> 4. An unchaste woman.<BR> 5. A branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ख्|लंख्
लङ्ख् लङ्ख्, see लख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग्|लंग्
लङ्ग् लङ्ग्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To go limpingly, to be lame.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, Caus., Pañc. i. d. 369, To stop (? corr. perhaps विलम्बयन्, delaying; cf. विलम्बन and my transl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग|लंग|लंगः|लङ्गः
लङ्ग लङ्ग (vb. लग्), m.<BR> 1. Union.<BR> 2. A lover, a gallant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गक|लंगक|लंगकः|लङ्गकः
लङ्गक लङ्ग + क, m. A lover, a gallant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गिमन्
लङ्गिमन् लङ्गिमन् (vb. लग्), (m.), Union, Lass. 67, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गिममय
लङ्गिममय लङ्गिममय, i. e. लञ्गिमन् + मय, adj., f. यी, Fit to be joined, Lass. 83, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गूल|लंगूल|लंगूलं|लङ्गूलं
लङ्गूल लङ्गूल (vb. लग्), n. The tail of an animal (cf. लाङ्गूल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घ्|लंघ्
लङ्घ् लङ्घ्, i. 1, Par. † To diminish.<BR> --i. 1, Par. Ātm. To ascend, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 32.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm. † To fast.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To jump over, Megh. 55.<BR> 2. To step over, MBh. 3, 11178; Man. 4, 38.<BR> 3. To hinder, Pañc. ii. d. 113.<BR> 4. To surpass, Ragh. 3, 48 (Calc.).<BR> 5. To disregard, Man. 5, 151; Pañc. i. d. 37.<BR> 6. To violate, Man. 8, 371.<BR> 7. † To speak.<BR> 8. † To shine.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> 1. अ-लङ्घनीय, adj. Not to be overtaken, unattainable, Śāk. d. 8.<BR> 2. दुर्लङ्घ्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Difficult to be set aside, Rājat. 5, 395.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, i. 10, To stride over, Man. 4, 54.<BR> --With अव अव, i. 10, To stay, Ghaṭ. 7.<BR> --With उद् उद्, i. 10,<BR> 1. To pursue, Megh. 46.<BR> 2. To neglect, Rājat. 5, 395.<BR> 3. To violate, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 4.<BR> 4. To injure, 191, 21.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अन्-उल्लङ्घनीय, adj. Not to be neglected, Pañc. 247, 19.<BR> --With परि परि, i. 10, To trespass, to leave, Pañc. iv. d. 75.<BR> --With वि वि, i. 10,<BR> 1. To overstep, Kir. 5, 1.<BR> 2. To violate, Ragh. 9 74.<BR> 3. To neglect, Ragh. 3, 4 (Calc.).<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. langên, ga-lingan, ga-langôn; Goth. laggs; A.S. lang, etc.; Lat. longus, languere, etc.; λαγγάζω, λογγάζω, λαγχάνω, λάχος, λόγχη, ἐλέγχω; probably also Goth. laikan, etc. The original signification of this vb. was probably, ‘To overtake by jumping,’ then, ‘To attain.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घन|लंघन|लंघनं|लङ्घनं
लङ्घन लङ्घ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Jumping over.<BR> 2. Passing over, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 1.<BR> 3. Coition, 182, 11.<BR> 4. Exceeding, transgressing, Hit. 87, 1, M.M. (पति-, Injuring one's husband); disregarding, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 34 (of a former husband by marrying another); disdain, Vikr. 34, 4.<BR> 5. Storming, capturing a fort, Hit. iii. d. 136.<BR> 6. Going.<BR> 7. One of a horse's paces, curvetting.<BR> 8. Fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लछ्|लच्छ्
† लछ् लछ् (a form of लक्ष्), and लाञ्छ् लञ्छ्, q. v.<BR> --i. 1, Par. To mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
1. लज् लज्, see लज्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
† 2. लज् लज्, and लञ्ज् लञ्ज्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To fry.<BR> 2. To calumniate, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
† 3. लज् लज्, and लञ्ज् लञ्ज्, i. 10, Par. To appear, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
† 4. लज् लज्, i. 10, Par. To cover (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्ज्
लज्ज् लज्ज् (akin to रञ्ज्, and for original रज्य), and लज् लज् (Bhaṭṭ. 14, 105), i. 6, Ātm. (also Par., Man. 12, 35), To be ashamed, Pañc. ii. d. 106; with the ptcple. pres. in the sense of the infin., Rām. 2, 12, 52; Pañc. 119, 6. (ब्रुवाणो न लज्जसे, You are not ashamed to speak).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लग्न, Ashamed.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To be ashamed, MBh. 3, 2217.<BR> --With सम् सम्, The same, Rām. 2, 55, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जा
लज्जा लज्ज् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Shame, Pañc. v. d. 10.<BR> 2. Bashfulness, Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR> 3. Modesty.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लज्ज
निर्लज्ज निर्लज्ज, i. e. निस्-, and वि-, adj., f. जा, shameless, Pañc. i. d. 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
स- + लज्ज स- + लज्ज, adj., f. जा. 1. ashamed. 2. bashful, Pañc. 45, 8; Daśak. in Chr. 182, 1. 3. modest, Hit. iii. d. 64. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a " target="_blank">Page0787-a + 40</a>] ˚जम्, acc. sing. n. adv. bashfully, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 19; Vikr. 22, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जावन्त्|लज्जावत्
लज्जावन्त् लज्जा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Bashful, modest, Nal. 3, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जित|लज्जितः
लज्जित लज्जित, i. e. लज्जा + इत, adj. Ashamed, bashful, Utt. Rāmac. 158, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज्|लंज्
† लञ्ज् लञ्ज्, लुञ्ज् लुञ्ज्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To be strong.<BR> 2. To injure.<BR> 3. To dwell.<BR> 4. To give.<BR> 5. To speak, to shine. See 2., 3. लज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज|लंज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लञ्ज लञ्ज,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A foot.<BR> 2. The end of the lower garment, tucked into the waistband.<BR> 3. A tail.<BR> II. f. जा.<BR> 1. An adulteress.<BR> 2. Lakṣmī.<BR> 3. Sleep. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्जिका|लंजिका
लञ्जिका लञ्जिका, i. e. लञ्जा + क. f. A harlot.<BR> --Cf. perhaps λάγνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्
† लट् लट् i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be a child.<BR> 2. To cry (cf. रट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटक|लटकः
लटक लटक, m. A bad man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्वा
लट्वा लट्वा, f.<BR> 1. A sparrow.<BR> 2. A musical instrument (?).<BR> 3. A game.<BR> 4. A tree, a species of the करञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्
† 1. लड् and लाड् ला̆ड्, i. 10, ला̆डय, ला̆दापय, Par. To throw up, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्
2. लड् लड्, Caus., or i. 10, Par. लडय,<BR> 1. † To loll (the tongue).<BR> 2. To stir with the tongue, Pañc. 229, 20 (but with ल् instead of ड्).<BR> 3. † To use the tongue.<BR> 4. † To apprise, to show.<BR> 5. † To throw out, to be thrown out.<BR> 6. † To coagulate, to pain.<BR> 7. † To suffer pain. The final ड् seems to stand for ल् (cf. लल्).<BR> --Perhaps cf. λάλος, λαλέω, λῆρος; N.H.G. lallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्
3. लड् लड्, see लल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्डु|लड्डुः
लड्डु लड्डु, A class of sweetmeats, Lass. 2. ed. 59, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्डुक|लड्डुकः
लड्डुक लड्डु + क, m. n. A class of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b " target="_blank">Page0787-b + 43</a>] sweetmeats, Lass. 2. ed. 9, 11; 13; Brahmav. 3, 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड्|लंड्
† लण्ड् लण्ड् (see 1. लड्), उलण्ड् उलण्ड् (i. e. उद्-लण्ड्), and ओलण्ड् ओलण्ड् (i. e. उद्-लण्ड्, or अव-लण्ड्), i. 10, Par. To toss up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लता
लता लता, f.<BR> 1. A creeper, Kathās. 22, 103.<BR> 2. A plant, Pañc. i. d. 253.<BR> 3. A branch, Vikr. d. 13.<BR> 4. Thread.<BR> 5. The name of several plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतलता
अमृत- + लता अमृत- + लता, f. a creeper yielding nectar, Bhartṛ. 1, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पताकभुजलत
उद्-पताक-भुज-लत उद्-पताक-भुज-लत, adj., f. ता, having raised banners instead of creeper-like arms, Kathās. 20, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पलता
कल्प- + लता कल्प- + लता, f. a creeper yielding all wishes (cf. कल्प-तरु), Śāk. d. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागलता
नाग- + लता नाग- + लता, f. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 359.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुलता
बाहु- + लता बाहु- + लता, f. the creeper-like arms, Rājat. 5, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूलता
भ्रू- + लता भ्रू- + लता, f. the creeper-like eyebrow, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलता
भू- + लता भू- + लता, and महि-, f. an earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तालता
मुक्ता- + लता मुक्ता- + लता, f. a pearl necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनलता
मोहन- + लता मोहन- + लता, f. a fascinating plant, Lass. 82, 14 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमलता
रोमलता रोमलता, i. e. रोमन्-, f. a line of hair extending to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडिल्लता
तडिल्लता तडिल्लता, i. e. तडित्-, f. zigzag lightning, Kirāt. 10, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रलता
वेत्र- + लता वेत्र- + लता, f. a stick (of the doorkeeper), Pañc. 16, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यलता|सूर्य्यलता
सूर्य- + लता सूर्य- + लता, f. a plant, Cleome viscosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमलता
सोम- + लता सोम- + लता, f. the Soma plant, Sarcostema viminalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतिका
लतिका लतिका, i. e. लत + क, f. A creeper.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलतिका
अङ्ग- + लतिका अङ्ग- + लतिका, f. a creeper-like body, Utt. Rāmac. 72, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतलतिका
अमृत- + लतिका अमृत- + लतिका, f. a creeper yielding nectar. Śrut. 35 (Brockhaus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलतिका
भू- + लतिका भू- + लतिका, f. creeper-like arms, Śṛṅgārat. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्
लप् लप्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Nal. 21, 16).<BR> 1. To speak, Gīt. 1, 41.<BR> 2. To lament, Nal. 3, 27.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लपिता, n. Voice. Frequent. लालप्, लालप्य, To lament, MBh. 3, 10200. लालप्य, Par., MBh. 1, 968.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, To deny, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0788-a " target="_blank">Page0788-a + 43</a>] Rām. 2, 75, 24.<BR> --With आ आ, To address, MBh. 3, 15604.<BR> --Caus. लापय, To ask, Pañc. i. d. 431; 242, 13.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To prattle, Śāk. 13, 14.<BR> 2. To speak, Pañc. 94, 12; to cry, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 309.<BR> 3. To bewail, Pañc. 75, 25; MBh. 3, 1203.<BR> 4. To invoke, MBh. 2, 2339. प्रलपित, n.<BR> 1. Prattle, Pañc. 146, 1 (वृथा-, Useless words).<BR> 2. Lamentation, Pañc. 224, 16.<BR> --Caus. To incite to speak, Mṛcch. 86, 14.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To wail, Hit. 44, 6, M.M.; MBh. 3, 1203.<BR> 2. To bewail, Rām. 1, 1, 52.<BR> 3. To speak, Johns. Sel. 51, 110.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To converse, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 7.<BR> --Caus. To cause to converse, to address, Hit. i. d. 77, M.M.<BR> --Cf. Lat. loqui; probably ὀλοϕύρομαι (a denomin. based on an old frequent. ὀλοπ and aff. वन्, with ρ for ν).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपन|लपनं
लपन लप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Speaking.<BR> 2. The mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्
लभ् लभ् (in epic poetry also लम्भ् लम्भ्, MBh. 2, 1365, cf. Caus.), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Chr. 21, 8).<BR> 1. To obtain, to get, MBh. 1, 6839; Vikr. d. 42; to acquire, Hit. i. d. 47, M.M.; to enjoy, Vikr. d. 20; Kathās. 26, 283 (अलभत + तराम्, Enjoyed in the highest degree).<BR> 2. With गर्भम्, To become pregnant, Chr. 50, 10.<BR> 3. To approach, MBh. 1, 1756.<BR> 4. To undergo, to perform, Rājat. 5, 154.<BR> 5. Pass. To be contained, Bhāṣāp. 6.<BR> 6. Pass. refl. To take, Rājat. 5, 108.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pres. Ātm. अ-लभमान, adj. Unable to catch, Hit. 121, 15.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लब्ध, Got, obtained, Lass. 20, 7; Rājat. 5, 135. f. धा, A woman whose husband or lover is faithless. Desider. लिप्स. To strive to obtain, Man. 7, 99; 8, 340; to long for, Hit. ii. d. 7.<BR> --Comp. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0788-b " target="_blank">Page0788-b + 41</a>] ptcple. pres. (Par.), अ-लिप्सन्त्, adj. Not desiring, Hit. ii. d. 8.<BR> --Caus. लम्भय, To cause to obtain.<BR> 1. To bestow, MBh. 3, 16068; to give, Vikr. 47, 12.<BR> 2. To find out, Man. 8, 109.<BR> 3. To cause to suffer, MBh. 2, 1529.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लम्भित.<BR> 1. Procured, given.<BR> 2. Adapted.<BR> 3. Addressed.<BR> 4. Heightened, improved.<BR> 5. Cherished.<BR> 6. Gained.<BR> 7. Abused.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, desider. To covet, MBh. 1, 2940.<BR> --With आ आ, To touch, Man. 11, 202; 5, 87; Chr. 7, 16.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To reproach, Vikr. 63, 12; Śiś. 9, 60.<BR> 2. To reprove, Śāk. 59, 15.<BR> --Caus. To blame, Pañc. 134, 24.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To touch, to stroke, Rām. 1, 29, 45.<BR> 2. To rub, Rām. 2, 25, 35.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To obtain, Rājat. 5, 297; to get, Vikr. d. 29.<BR> 2. With गर्भम्, To become pregnant, Rām. 1, 25, 25.<BR> 3. To find, Vikr. 65, 19; Daśak. in Chr. 192, 10.<BR> 4. To perceive, Rām. 2, 65, 13; to feel, Vikr. 67, 4; to be told, Pañc. 172, 21.<BR> 5. To find out, Vikr. 57, 11; to ascertain, Śāk. 11, 16; Man. 7, 57.<BR> 5. To understand, MBh. 2, 769.<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, To recover, Vikr. d. 133.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To deceive, MBh. 3, 2785.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र,<BR> 1. To deceive, Hit. 92, 6; Chr. 53, 23.<BR> 2. To confound, Utt. Rāmac. 155, 10.<BR> 3. To violate, MBh. 3, 223.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To recover, MBh. 1, 7882.<BR> --With वि वि, To occupy, Rājat. 5, 265.<BR> --Cf. λάϕυρον, λαμϐάνω, εἴληϕα, λαῖλαψ (based on a frequent.), probably λέϐης, λίπτω. See रभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभस|लभसः
लभस लभ् + अस, m. A rope for tying a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पट|लंपट|लम्पटः
लम्पट लम्पट (vb. लप्, but cf. also लिम्पट),<BR> I. adj. Covetous, greedy, Pañc. 253, 18.<BR> II. m. A libertine, Lass. 83, 18 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पटत्व
लम्पटत्व लम्पट + त्व, n. Greediness, Bhartṛ. 3, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पाक|लंपाक|लम्पाकः
लम्पाक लम्पाक, m.<BR> 1. A libertine (see the last).<BR> 2. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब्|लंब्
लम्ब् लम्ब्, i. 1, Ātm. (Par., Pañc. 107, 25).<BR> 1. To fall, MBh. 2, 2187.<BR> 2. To set (as the sun), Rām. 1, 33, 20.<BR> 3. To hang downwards, Pañc. v. d. 36.<BR> 4. † To sound.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. लम्बमान.<BR> 1. Depending, Pañc. 259, 7.<BR> 2. Being large or bulky, Pañc. 136, 1.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To fall, MBh. 1, 1035; to descend, Hit. 25, 5, M.M.<BR> 2. To set, MBh. 4, 1040.<BR> 3. To rest upon, Lass. 5, 11.<BR> 4. To lean on, to be supported, MBh. 1, 8443.<BR> 5. To suspend, Pañc. 252, 10.<BR> 6. To support, to hold, Śāk. 86, 21; Vikr. 49, 16.<BR> 7. To take, Śāk. 108, 19. With धैर्यम्,<BR> a. To take courage, Hit. 13, 19.<BR> b. To keep firm, i. e. to yield not, Vikr. 34, 4.<BR> 8. To choose, Śāk. 70, 14. अवलम्बित,<BR> 1. Hanging, Pañc. 116, 23.<BR> 2. Hanging with the head downwards, Lass. 15, 18.<BR> 3. Supported, Vikr. 7, 5.<BR> 4. Depended upon, Hit. i. d. 143, M.M.<BR> --Caus. To support, Mālav. 31, 2; to hold, 42, 6.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, To support, MBh. 3, 10988.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To lean on, to depend upon, Chr. 28, 16.<BR> 2. To support, MBh. 3, 10989.<BR> 3. To keep (स्थैर्यं गृहे, To stay at home), Pañc. 225, 23.<BR> 4. To take, Ghaṭ. 22; to seize, Rājat. 5, 432. With धैर्यम्, To take courage, Pañc. 21, 8. With धृतिम्, To be untroubled, Kathās. 22, 100. आलम्बित,<BR> 1. Hanging, Vikr. d. 140.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b " target="_blank">Page0789-b + 40</a>] Laid on, Vikr. d. 125. नालम्बित, i. e. न-आलम्बित, Unsupported, hopeless, Vikr. d. 38.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To suspend, Pañc. 144, 23.<BR> 2. To maintain, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.<BR> 3. To take, Mṛcch. 55, 19.<BR> 4. To dwell, Hit. i. d. 211, M.M.<BR> --With उद् उद्, उल्लम्बित, Hanging (between heaven and earth), Mṛcch. 33, 19.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुल्लम्बित, Hanging, 34, 2.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रलम्बित, Hanging.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To suspend, Pañc. 98, 4.<BR> --With वि वि, To tarry, Śāk. 18, 21; Pañc. 84, 10. अ-विलम्बित, adj. Without delay, Mālav. 53, 13; Vikr. 79, 13.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To suspend, Pañc. 116, 19.<BR> 2. To delay, iii. d. 232.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, Pañc. 98, 4; erroneous reading, see my transl. n. 480.<BR> --Cf. Lat. labi; A.S. limpian, ge-limp; Engl. To limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब|लंब|लम्बः
लम्ब लम्ब् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Depending, Megh. 82. 88.<BR> 2. Long, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1210; Śāk. 87, 15 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 3. Expanded, large, Hiḍ. 2, 3.<BR> 4. Spacious.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bribe.<BR> 2. Moving a man at a sort of backgammon.<BR> III. f. बा.<BR> 1. Lakṣmī.<BR> 2. Durgā.<BR> 3. A bitter gourd.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगण्डलम्ब
आ-गण्ड- + लम्ब आ-गण्ड- + लम्ब, adj. hanging down to the cheeks, Megh. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बक|लंबक|लंबकः|लम्बकः
लम्बक लम्ब + क, m. A section, Kathās. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बन|लंबन|लम्बनं|लंबनः|लम्बनः
लम्बन लम्ब् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Falling.<BR> 2. A long necklace reaching to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बय
लम्बय लम्बय, a denomin. derived from लम्ब, Par. To extend, Ragh. 6, 75 (Calc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बालकत्व
लम्बालकत्व लम्बालकत्व, i. e. लम्ब-अलक + त्व, n. Hanging down of the curls, Megh. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बिन्
लम्बिन् लम्ब् + इन्, adj. Depending, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a " target="_blank">Page0790-a + 42</a>] Pañc. i. d. 160.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्बिन्
अ- + लम्बिन् अ- + लम्बिन्, adj. unsupported, Lass. 20, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिलम्बिन्
अन्-अति- + लम्बिन् अन्-अति- + लम्बिन्, adj. short, Mālav. d. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वार्धलम्बिन्
पूर्व-अर्ध- + लम्बिन् पूर्व-अर्ध- + लम्बिन्, adj. inclining (his) fore-part, Megh. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बुषा|लंबुषा
लम्बुषा लम्ब् + उषा, f. A necklace of seven strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भ्
लम्भ् लम्भ्, see रम्भ् and लभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भ|लंभ|लंभः|लम्भः
लम्भ लम्भ, i. e. लभ् + अ, m. Gain, Vikr. 49, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भन|लंभन|लंभनं|लम्भनं
लम्भन लम्भन, i. e. लभ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Gaining, getting.<BR> 2. Causing to get, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 12.<BR> 3. Abuse, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय्
लय् लय्, see रय्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय|लयः
लय लय, i. e. ली + अ, m.<BR> 1. Adhering.<BR> 2. A house.<BR> 3. Sport.<BR> 4. Equal time in music and dancing, Pañc. v. d. 43.<BR> 5. Melting; लयं या, To melt away, to vanish, Pañc. v. d. 4.<BR> 6. Dissolution, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 23; 211, 7; destruction.<BR> 7. Loss.<BR> 8. A pause in music, Mālav. 19, 11.<BR> 9. Slackness of mind, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलय|अलयः
अ- + लय अ- + लय,<BR> I. m. nondestruction, duration, Rām. 3, 71, 10.<BR> II. adj. without a fixed abode, Śiś. 4, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लर्ब्
† लर्ब् लर्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्
लल् लल्, and † लड् लड्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry, Ātm., Rām. 1, 9, 19).<BR> 1. To sport, MBh. 3, 1741.<BR> 2. To dally, Rām. 1, 9, 19.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ललित.<BR> 1. Dallying, wanton, Megh. 65.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 6.<BR> 3. Wished. n.<BR> 1. Beauty, Rām. 1, 9, 16.<BR> 2. Love of pleasure, love, Vikr. d. 32.<BR> 3. Softness and delicacy of motion, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 6.<BR> 4. ˚तम्, adv. Sweetly, Dev. 10, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, Par.<BR> A. ललय, † लडय,<BR> 1. To exhilarate, Rām. 2, 43, 5.<BR> 2. To nurse, to foster, to attend, Rām. 2, 47, 6; Pañc. 87, 11.<BR> B. लालय,<BR> 1. To cherish, Pañc. i. d. 397.<BR> 2. To spoil, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2664.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. † लाडय, To desire. लालित,<BR> 1. Desired.<BR> 2. Cherished tenderly, Pañc. iii. d. 126.<BR> 3. Loved, Rājat. 5, 6.<BR> 4. Coaxed, Pañc. 87, 11 (or n. Joy; ˚तेन, Joyfully ?).<BR> 5. Seduced; cf. 2. लड्.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, Caus. लालय,<BR> 1. To court, Mālav. 29, 1.<BR> 2. To fondle, Śāk. 104, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ललित
दुर्ललित दुर्ललित, i. e. दुस्- (cf. Caus.<BR> A.),<BR> I. adj. spoiled, Vikr. d. 27; wayward, Śāk. 103, 4. n. 1. ill habit, Hariv. 8539 (with अति-, excessive). 2. disfavour, Prab. 90, 15. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b " target="_blank">Page0790-b + 43</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुललित
सु- + ललित सु- + ललित, adj. 1. sporting. 2. pleased, very delicate, Hit. 37, 4, M.M. 3. very beautiful, Ṛt. 1, 28; Bhartṛ. 3, 28. ˚तम्, adv. delightedly, easily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललज्जिह्व|ललज्जिह्वः
ललज्जिह्व ललज्जिह्व, i. e. ललन्त्-जिह्व (see 2. लड् and जिह्वा),<BR> I. adj. Fierce, savage.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A camel.<BR> 2. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन|ललनं|ललनः
ललन ललन, i. e. लड्, and लल् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A tree, Shorea robusta.<BR> 2. A boy.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. A wanton woman, Indr. 5, 6.<BR> 2. A woman in general, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 27.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Sport, pleasure.<BR> 2. Lolling the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन्तिका|ललंतिका
ललन्तिका ललन्तिका (akin to लल्), f. A necklace reaching to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाट|ललाटं
ललाट ललाट, n. The forehead, Pañc. ii. d. 183; Vikr. 73, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाललाट
महा- + ललाट महा- + ललाट, adj. with a large forehead, Rām. 3, 55, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटंतप|ललाटन्तप|ललाटंतपः|ललाटन्तपः
ललाटंतप ललाट्ं-तप, i. e. ललाट + म्-तप् + अ, adj. Burning the forehead, Utt. Rāmac. 153, 5; Mālat. 12, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटिका
ललाटिका ललाटिका, i. e. ललाट + क, f.<BR> 1. An ornament worn on the forehead, as a jewel.<BR> 2. A mark made with sandal on the forehead, Pāṇ. iv. 3, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाम|ललामं|ललामः
ललाम ललाम (akin to लल्),<BR> I. n., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a " target="_blank">Page0791-a + 42</a>] also ललामन् ललामन्,<BR> 1. A mark.<BR> 2. A flag.<BR> 3. An ornament, Śāk. 25, 4.<BR> 4. A mane.<BR> 5. A tail.<BR> 6. A line.<BR> 7. Majesty, dignity.<BR> 8. Chief, principal, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 18.<BR> II. f. मी, An ornament worn in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामक|ललामकं
ललामक ललाम + क, n. A chaplet of flowers falling over the forehead, Pāṇ. iv. 4, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितादित्य
ललितादित्य ललितादित्य, i. e. ललित-आदित्य, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्लिय
लल्लिय लल्लिय, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव|लवं|लवः
लव लव, i. e. लू + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Cutting, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 17.<BR> 2. Plucking, Nal. 2, 30.<BR> 3. Reaping.<BR> 4. Smallness, Bhartṛ. 3, 100; Vikr. d. 118 (अपराध-, A very small fault); a little, Hit. iv. d. 76 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3265); a piece, Vikr. d. 125; a drop, Kir. 5, 44.<BR> 5. Hair, Ragh. 15, 32; wool, Man. 8, 151.<BR> 6. A minute, and also a larger division of time.<BR> 7. A kind of quail.<BR> 8. One of Rāma's sons, Utt. Rāmac. 85, 8.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The nutmeg.<BR> 2. Cloves.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलव
ज्ञान- + लव ज्ञान- + लव (m.), a smattering of knowledge, Bhartṛ. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवक|लवकः
लवक लवक, i. e. लू + अक, adj. Who or what cuts, Pāṇ. iii. 1, 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवंग|लवङ्ग|लवङ्गं|लवंगः|लवङ्गः
लवंग लवंग, i. e. लव + म्-ग,<BR> I. m. The clove tree, Myristica caryophyllata, Ragh. 6, 57.<BR> II. n. Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवट
लवट लवट, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवण|लवणं|लवणः
लवण लवण, for original रवण cf. रुमण्वन्त्,<BR> I. n. Salt, Pañc. 184, 9.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Saltness, Hit. iii. d. 56.<BR> 2. The sea of salt water.<BR> 3. The name of a Rākṣasa, Utt. Rāmac. 176, 8.<BR> III. f. णा.<BR> 1. Light, beauty.<BR> 2. The name of a river.<BR> IV. adj.<BR> 1. Salt, saline, Pāṇ. iv. 4, 24.<BR> 2. Charming, beautiful. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b " target="_blank">Page0791-b + 38</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षारलवण|अक्षारलवणं
अ-क्षार-लवण अ-क्षार-लवण. adj. not containing artificial salt, Man. 3, 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन|लवनं
लवन लवन, i. e. लू + अन, n. Cutting, reaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवली
लवली लवली, f. A kind of creeper, Vikr. d. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवशस्
लवशस् लव + शस्, adv. In pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाक|लवाकः
लवाक लवाक, i. e. लू + आक, m. A sickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवि|लविः
लवि लवि, i. e. लू + इ (m. ?), An iron instrument for cutting or cleaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवित्र|लवित्रं
लवित्र लवित्र, i. e. लू + त्र, n. A sickle, Pāṇ. iii. 2, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लश्
लश् लश्, see 2. लस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुन|लशुनं|लशुनः
लशुन लशुन, n. Garlic, Man. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्
लष् लष् (akin to 1. लस्, cf. लालस), i. 1 and 4, Par. To desire; cf. 2. लस्.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To desire, Vikr. 13, 20; to covet, Hit. 69, 5; MBh. 1, 6580.<BR> 2. To take, Vikr. d. 107. अभिलषित, n. Desire, Hit. 95, 4, M.M.<BR> --Cf. λῶ, λῆμα, λαρός, λωΐων, λίαν, λιλαίομαι, λήλαντος, probably λαμία, λάμος, λάρυγξ, λαιμός, λαίτμα, etc.; Lat. lascivus; Goth. luston, lustus; A.S. lust, lyst, lystan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्व|लष्वः
लष्व लष्व, m. A dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्
1. लस् लस्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To embrace.<BR> 2. To sport or play.<BR> 3. To shine, MBh. 3, 15533.<BR> --Caus. लासय, To cause to sport, to move, Vikr. d. 23.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To sport, Pañc. i. d. 152; Bhaṭṭ. 9, 86.<BR> 2. To shine, Śiś. 20, 56.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to shine, Ṛt. 6, 8.<BR> 2. To delight, Hit. 21, 15.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To shine, Śiś. 2, 19.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To break forth, Pañc. ii. d. 193.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a " target="_blank">Page0792-a + 40</a>] shine forth, Śiś. 8, 65.<BR> 3. To sport. समुल्लसित,<BR> 1. Sportive.<BR> 2. Beautiful.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To sport, to dally, Hit. 42, 9; with उपरि in उपरि-वि-लसन्त्, Flashing up, Megh. 48.<BR> 2. To play, to exhibit, Pañc. iii. d. 237.<BR> 3. To shine, Bhartṛ. 3, 23; 36 (to flash); Pañc. i. d. 461 (येन विलसितम्, Who has lived in a brilliant style). विलसित, Sportive, wanton. n.<BR> 1. Wanton pastime.<BR> 2. Splendour. Kir. 5, 46; flashing, Vikr. d. 137.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To break forth, Lass. 24, 14.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. ludo; see लष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विलसित
दुर्विलसित दुर्विलसित, i. e. दुस्-, n. A wicked trick, Prab. 104, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्
† 2. लस् लस्, लष् लष्, लश् लश्, i. 10, Par. To do anything skilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसिका
लसिका लसिका, f. Saliva, spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तक|लस्तकः
लस्तक लस्तक, perhaps लस्त + क (1. लस्, To embrace). m. The middle of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहर
लहर लहर, The name of a district (Lahore), Rājat. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहरि|लहरिः
लहरि and लहरी लहरी, f. A large wave, a wave, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 814.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दलहरि|आनन्दलहरिः
आनन्द- + लहरि आनन्द- + लहरि, f. title of a hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ला
ला ला, ii. 2, Par. To take, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षणिक|लाक्षणिकः
लाक्षणिक लाक्षणिक, i. e. लक्षण + इक, adj., f. की, Characteristic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षा
लाक्षा लाक्षा, i. e. लक्ष = लक्त in लक्तक (q. cf.), + अ, f. Lac, the animal dye, Ṛt. 6, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणलाक्षा
चरण- + लाक्षा चरण- + लाक्षा, f. lac, with which the feet are dyed, Kir. 5, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षिक
लाक्षिक लाक्षिक, adj.<BR> 1. i. e. लाक्षा + इक, Made of lac, dyed with lac, Pāṇ. iv. 2, 2.<BR> 2. i. e. लक्ष + इक, Relating to a large number or a Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाख्
लाख् लाख्, see राख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लागुडिक
लागुडिक लागुडिक, i. e. लगुड + इक, m. One who bears a club, a sentinel, Pañc. 230, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघ्
लाघ् लाघ्, see राघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघव|लाघवं
लाघव लाघव, i. e. लघु + अ, n.<BR> 1. Lightness.<BR> 2. Undervaluing, a cause of undervaluing, Pañc. ii. d. 107; disgrace, iii. d. 113; contempt, Bhag. 2, 35.<BR> 3. Swiftness, Chr. 34, 7.<BR> 4. Readiness, Chr. 5, 23.<BR> 5. Dexterity, Johns. Sel. 11, 25.<BR> 6. Health.<BR> 7. Meanness, Hit. iii. d. 78; insignificance.<BR> 8. Frivolity.<BR> 9. Shortness (of a vowel), Śrut. 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुलाघव
गुरु- + लाघव गुरु- + लाघव, n. the relative weight, Man. 9, 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तलाघव
हस्त- + लाघव हस्त- + लाघव, n. light-handedness, readiness, cleverness, Pañc. 218, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गल|लांगल|लांगलं|लाङ्गलं|लाङ्गलः
लाङ्गल लाङ्गल, vb. लग्, cf. लाङ्गुल,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. The penis.<BR> 2. A plough, Bhartṛ. 2, 98.<BR> 3. The main beam of a house.<BR> 4. The palm tree.<BR> II. f. ली, The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिन्|लांगलिन्
लाङ्गलिन् लाङ्गलिन्, i. e. लाङ्गल + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. A name of बलराम, Megh. 50 (armed with a plough).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुल|लांगुल|लांगुलं|लाङ्गुलं
लाङ्गुल and लाङ्गूल लाङ्गू̆ल (vb. लग्, properly, To hang), n. A tail, Pañc. 259, 7 (ऊ); Hit. i. d. 170, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज्
† लाज् लाज्, लाञ्ज् लाञ्ज्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To fry.<BR> 2. To blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज|लाजं|लाजः
लाज लाज,<BR> I. m. Grain wetted or sprinkled.<BR> II. f. जा, or pl. m. Fried grain, Pañc. 158, 3; Chr. 57, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छ्|लांछ्
लाञ्छ् लाञ्छ् (akin to लक्ष्; cf. लछ्), i. 1, Par. †<BR> 1. To mark.<BR> 2. To dress, Vikr. d. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छन|लांछन|लांछनं|लाञ्छनं|लाञ्छनः
लाञ्छन लाञ्छ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A mark, Pañc. iii. d. 204.<BR> 2. A name, Utt. Rāmac. 2, 4 (श्रि-कण्ठ-पद-, adj. Having as surname the word Śrikaṇṭha.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a " target="_blank">Page0793-a + 40</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगलाञ्छन|मृगलांछन|मृगलाञ्छनः
मृग- + लाञ्छन मृग- + लाञ्छन, m. the moon, Lass. 91, 8 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सलाञ्छन|श्रीवत्सलांछन|श्रीवत्सलाञ्छनः
श्री-वत्स- + लाञ्छन श्री-वत्स- + लाञ्छन, m. a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलाञ्छन|शशलांछन|शशलाञ्छनः
शश- + लाञ्छन शश- + लाञ्छन, m. the moon, Pañc. iii. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्ज्|लांज्
लाञ्ज् लाञ्ज्, see लाज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट|लाटः
लाट लाट, m.<BR> 1. Cloth.<BR> 2. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाड्
लाड् लाड्, see 1. लद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाड
लाड लाड, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाडन
लाडन लाडन, see लालन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ्
† लाभ् लाभ्, i. 10, Par. To throw, to direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ लाभ, i. e. लभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Acquirement, acquisition, Pañc. ii. d. 197.<BR> 2. Gain, Man. 9, 331; Pañc. ii. d. 100.<BR> 3. Enjoying, Pañc. 202, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाभ|अलाभः
अ- + लाभ अ- + लाभ, m. 1. no possibility of getting, Man. 2, 42. 2. loss, Man. 11, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणालाभ
गुण-अ- + लाभ गुण-अ- + लाभ, m. the not taking effect, Suśr. 1, 131, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लाभ
दुर्लाभ दुर्लाभ, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be got, MBh. 12, 11168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणलाभ
द्वि-गुण- + लाभ द्वि-गुण- + लाभ, m. (condition of) receiving something doubled, Pañc. 88, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभालाभ
लाभ-अ- + लाभ लाभ-अ- + लाभ, m. profit and loss, Man. 9, 331.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिलाभ
सिद्धि- + लाभ सिद्धि- + लाभ, m. acquirement of success, i. e. applause, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभिन्
ऽलाभिन् -लाभिन्, i. e. लभ् + इन्, adj. in परीक्षा-क्षण-, adj. Getting the time of proving, Rājat. 5, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालक|लालकः
लालक लालक, i. e. लल्, Caus., + अक, adj., f. लिका. Seducing, Nal. 2, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालन|लालनं|लालनः
लालन लालन, also लाडन, Cāṇ. 84 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 412, i. e. लल्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Coaxing, Rājat. 5, 290.<BR> 2. Spoiling, over-indulging, Pañc. i. d. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालस|लालसः
लालस लालस, i. e. लालस्, frequent. of 1. लस्, but partly in the signification of लष्, + अ, m., and f. सा.<BR> 1. Ardent desire. Bhartṛ. 3, 36 (m.); Pañc. 81, 21 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b " target="_blank">Page0793-b + 41</a>] (at the end of a comp. adj. श्रवण-सुख-, Ardently desiring the pleasure for his ears).<BR> 2. Regret.<BR> 3. Asking.<BR> 4. The longing of a pregnant woman.<BR> 5. Dalliance, MBh. 7, 3383 (?).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनलालस
दर्शन- + लालस दर्शन- + लालस, adj., f. ला, ardently desiring to see, Nal. 12, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिलालस
पति- + लालस पति- + लालस, adj., f. सा, ardently longing for (her) husband, ib. 13, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाला
लाला लाला (akin to ली), f. Saliva, spittle, Bhartṛ. 2, 9; Ṛt. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटिक|लालाटिकः
लालाटिक लालाटिक, i. e. ललाट + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the forehead, worn on it, etc.<BR> 2. Contemplating the forehead.<BR> 3. Relating to fate (which is supposed to be written on one's forehead).<BR> 4. Low.<BR> II. m., and f. की.<BR> 1. An attentive servant.<BR> 2. An idler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाय
लालाय लालाय, a denomin. derived from लाला with य, Ātm. To secrete saliva continually, Pañc. iii. d. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालितक|लालितकः
लालितक लालित + क (see लल्, Caus.), m. A favourite, Rājat. 6, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित्य|लालित्यं
लालित्य लालित्य, i. e. ललित + य (vb. लल्), n. Loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव|लावः
लाव लाव, i. e. लू + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cutting.<BR> 2. Plucking, Ragh. 13, 43.<BR> II. m., and f. वा, A sort of quail, Perdix chinensis, Rām. 3, 53, 57.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलाव|पुष्पलावः
पुष्प- + लाव पुष्प- + लाव, 1. m. a garland-maker, a flower-seller. 2. f. वी, a female flower-gatherer, Megh. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण|लावणं
लावण लावण, i. e. लवण + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to salt.<BR> 2. Salted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावणिक|लावणिकं|लावणिकः
लावणिक लावणिक, i. e. लवण + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to salt.<BR> 2. Salted.<BR> 3. Beautiful.<BR> II. m. A salt merchant.<BR> III. n. A vessel holding salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्य|लावण्यं
लावण्य लावण्य, i. e. लवण + य, n.<BR> 1. Saltness.<BR> 2. Loveliness, charm, Hit. i. d. 136, M.M.; beauty, Lass. 2. ed. 19, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास|लासः
लास लास, i. e. लस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dancing. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a " target="_blank">Page0794-a + 41</a>]<BR> 2. Dalliance.<BR> 3. Pea-water, pulse that has been lightly boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासक|लासकं|लासकः
लासक लासक, i. e. लस् + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A dancer, an actor.<BR> 2. A peacock.<BR> II. f. अका and इका, A dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्य|लास्यं|लास्यः
लास्य लास्य, i. e. लास + य,<BR> I. m. A dancer.<BR> II. f. या, A female dancer.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Dancing.<BR> 2. Union of dance and music, Mārk. P. 68, 26.<BR> 3. The dance of the Indian dancing girls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षा
लिक्षा लिक्षा, f.<BR> 1. A nit, a young louse.<BR> 2. A poppy seed, considered as a measure of weight, Man. 8, 133.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूकालिक्ष
यूका-लिक्ष यूका-लिक्ष, n. lice and nits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्
लिख् लिख्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To scratch, to pick, Hit. 43, 15.<BR> 2. To touch, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 22.<BR> 3. To write, Pañc. 5, 6; Rājat. 5, 396.<BR> 4. To delineate, MBh. 2, 731.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लिखित, Scarified. n.<BR> 1. Writing, scripture.<BR> 2. A book.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To write on, Vikr. 25, 17.<BR> 2. To write, Lass. 91, 5.<BR> 3. To paint, Utt. Rāmac. 9, 13.<BR> --With आ आ, To delineate, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 14; Megh. 103. आलेख्य,<BR> 1. To be written.<BR> 2. To be delineated. n.<BR> 1. Writing.<BR> 2. A painting, picture, Vikr. d. 29.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To pierce, Kir. 5, 30.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To scratch up, MBh. 3, 374.<BR> 2. To polish, Śāk. d. 133.<BR> 3. To peck, Pañc. 146, 14 (see n.).<BR> 4. To slit open, Pañc. 91, 5.<BR> 5. To touch, MBh. 3, 2453.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b " target="_blank">Page0794-b + 41</a>] To strike, Kumāras. 1, 57.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To scratch, to draw lines on (acc.), Man. 4, 55.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To draw furrows on (acc.), Bhartṛ. 2, 98.<BR> 2. To strike, MBh. 3, 11953.<BR> 3. To peck, Hit. 93, 10. M.M.<BR> 4. To delineate, MBh. 3, 16670.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलिख्
चित्र- + लिख् चित्र- + लिख्, adj. painted, Hit. 91, 6, M.M. (-इव, as if painted, i. e. motionless). Ptcple of the fut. pass. लेख्य, n.<BR> 1. A letter.<BR> 2. A written accusation.<BR> 3. A manuscript.<BR> 4. Drawing, Chr. 51, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लेख्य
दुर्-लेख्य दुर्-लेख्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. illegibly written, Yājñ. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखन|लिखनं
लिखन लिख् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Scratching, scarifying.<BR> 2. Writing.<BR> 3. A written document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ख्|लिंख्
लिङ्ख् लिङ्ख्, see लख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिगु|लिगुः
लिगु लिगु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A fool.<BR> 2. A deer.<BR> 3. Part of the earth.<BR> II. n. The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग्|लिंग्
लिङ्ग् लिङ्ग्, i. 1, Par. † To go.<BR> --i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from लिङ्ग), Par. To change a noun according to its gender.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 64, 30), and i. 10. To embrace, Vikr. 71, 118 Mṛcch. 91, 14; Pañc. 187, 6 (i. 10); Kathās. 3, 65 (pf. red. लिलिङ्ग).<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. आलिङ्ग्य, n. A small drum, Rām. 5, 13, 47.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-अ, i. 1, To return an embrace, Mṛcch. 91, 15.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, i. 1,<BR> 1. To embrace, Pañc. 27, 6; Mṛcch. 91, 13.<BR> 2. To hold, Rām. 5, 13, 48; 53.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. and A.S. hring; O.H.G. bringjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग|लिंग|लिंगं|लिङ्गं
लिङ्ग लिङ्ग, n.<BR> 1. A mark, a sign, Nal. 5, 14.<BR> 2. A spot.<BR> 3. A religious mark, Man. 4, 200.<BR> 4. The penis.<BR> 5. The phallus, or Śiva under that emblem.<BR> 6. Nature, as the active power in creation.<BR> 7. The primary body, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 11; cf. 21.<BR> 8. Gender.<BR> 9. The reason, or middle term, Bhāṣāp. 66.<BR> 10. The order of the religious student.<BR> 11. Symptom of disease.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुलिङ्ग|ऋतुलिंग
ऋतु- + लिङ्ग ऋतु- + लिङ्ग, n. the peculiar [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a " target="_blank">Page0795-a + 45</a>] marks of the seasons, Man. 1, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलिङ्ग|त्रिलिंग
त्रि- + लिङ्ग त्रि- + लिङ्ग,<BR> I. adj. 1. possessed of the three qualities, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 13. 2. having three genders (as an adj.).<BR> II. the name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलिङ्ग|देवलिंग
देव- + लिङ्ग देव- + लिङ्ग, n. an idol, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लिङ्ग|निर्लिंग
निर्लिङ्ग निर्लिङ्ग, i. e. निस्-, adj. without distinguishing marks, MBh. 5, 1610.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंलिङ्ग|पुंलिङ्गं
पुंलिङ्ग पुंलिङ्ग, i. e. पुंस्-,<BR> I. n. 1. manhood, MBh. 5, 7489. 2. the masculine gender.<BR> II. adj. having the marks of a male, MBh. 9, 3304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुलिङ्गी
विष्णुलिङ्गी विष्णुलिङ्गी, i. e. विष्णु-लिङ्ग + ई, f. a quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलिङ्ग|स्त्रीलिंग
स्त्री- + लिङ्ग स्त्री- + लिङ्ग, n. 1. the female organs, Chr. 58, 5. 2. the feminine gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गस्थ|लिङ्गस्थः
लिङ्गस्थ लिङ्ग-स्थ, m. A student in theology, Man. 8, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गालिका
लिङ्गालिका लिङ्गालिका, f. A small mouse or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिन्|लिंगिन्
लिङ्गिन् लिङ्गिन्, i. e. लिङ्ग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Having marks, characterised.<BR> 2. One who is entitled to wear religious marks, Man. 4, 200.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ascetic, Pañc. iv. d. 41.<BR> 2. A religious student.<BR> 3. A worshipper of Śiva.<BR> 4. A hypocrite.<BR> 5. An elephant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिङ्गिन्|अलिंगिन्
अ- + लिङ्गिन् अ- + लिङ्गिन्, adj. and m. one who is not entitled to wear religious marks, Man. 4, 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यलिङ्गिन्|आर्य्यलिङ्गिन्
आर्य- + लिङ्गिन् आर्य- + लिङ्गिन्, adj. one who wears the signs of an Ārya, Man. 9, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजलिङ्गिन्|द्विजलिंगिन्
द्विज- + लिङ्गिन् द्विज- + लिङ्गिन्, adj. one who wears the marks of a twice-born (i. e. one of the three first castes), Man. 9, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारलिङ्गिन्
मार्जार- + लिङ्गिन् मार्जार- + लिङ्गिन्, adj. one who has the nature of a cat, Man. 4, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्
लिप् लिप्, i. 6, लिम्प, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To anoint, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 94.<BR> 2. To smear, Hit. 21, 14.<BR> 3. To stain (लिप्यते दोषेण, Incurs sin), Hit. ii. d. 118; to pollute, Man. 4, 201; 10, 104.<BR> 4. To burn, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 22.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लिप्त.<BR> 1. Envenomed.<BR> 2. Embraced.<BR> 3. Defiled.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be decorated, Rām. 2, 9, 40.<BR> --With the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b " target="_blank">Page0795-b + 39</a>] prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To anoint, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 6.<BR> 2. To smear, Śiś. 9, 15. अनुलिप्त,<BR> 1. Smeared, Pañc. iii. d. 32.<BR> 2. Anointed, Hit. 90, 8, M.M.; glistening, Śāk. d. 166.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be anointed, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 7.<BR> --With अव अव, To smear, Lass. 9, 19. अवलिप्त, Proud, arrogant, Man. 4, 79; Pañc. i. d. 341.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To anoint, Utt. Rāmac. 79, 1; Ṛt. 6, 12, v. r.<BR> 2. To smear, Pañc. 171, 11.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To anoint, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 5.<BR> --With उप उप, To pollute, MBh. 2, 2625; Bhag. 13, 32.<BR> --Caus. To let smear, Man. 3, 206.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To anoint, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 20.<BR> 2. To smear, Lass. 9, 12.<BR> 3. To pollute, Hit. 128, 12.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To anoint, MBh. 1, 4950.<BR> --Cf. λίπος, λιπαρής, ἀ-λείϕω, λισσός; Lat. limpidus, lippus; probably also liquidus, liquere, and O.H.G. salba; Goth. salbôn; A.S. sealf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलिप्त
अ-मेध्य-लिप्त अ-मेध्य-लिप्त, adj. defiled (soiled with impurity), Man. 4, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपि|लिपिः
लिपि and लिपी लिप् + ई̆, f.<BR> 1. Anointing, smearing.<BR> 2. Painting.<BR> 3. Writing, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 7; the alphabet, Ragh. 18, 45.<BR> 4. A written paper or book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिकर|लिपिकरः
लिपिकर and लिपिकार लिपि-कार, m.<BR> 1. A scribe.<BR> 2. -कर, A plasterer, whitener, Rām. 1, 12, 6 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तक|लिप्तकः
लिप्तक लिप्त + क (vb. लिप्), m.<BR> A poisoned arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सा
लिप्सा लिप्सा, i. e. लिप्स, desider. of लभ्, + अ, f. Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सु|लिप्सुः
लिप्सु लिप्सु, i. e. लिप्स (see the last), + उ, adj. Desirous, greedy, Pañc. 5, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पट|लिंपट|लिम्पटः
लिम्पट लिम्पट (vb. लिप्, but cf. also लम्पट), m. A lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पाक|लिंपाक|लिम्पाकं|लिंपाकः|लिम्पाकः
लिम्पाक लिम्पाक, m.<BR> 1. The lime tree, Citrus acida.<BR> 2. An ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश्
लिश् लिश्, i. 4, Ātm. To become small.<BR> --† i. 6, Par. To go.<BR> --Cf. क्लिश् and कृश्; ὀλίγος, perhaps λίγδος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्
लिह् लिह्, ii. 2, Par. Ātm. To lick, Hit. i. d. 112, M.M.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लीढ.<BR> 1. Licked, Kir. 5, 38.<BR> 2. Eaten.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. लेह्य, To be licked, Pañc. 61, 12. n. Food, Ragh. 5, 73. Frequent. लेलिह्, लेलिह्य, To lick repeatedly, MBh. 3, 10394. लेलिह्, Ātm., Chr. 39, 5.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. Ātm. लेलिहान, n.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To lick here and there (figurat.), Lass. 2. ed. 79, 79.<BR> 2. To lick up or off; to eat, Śāk. d. 7.<BR> 3. To touch with the tongue, Man. 4, 203. अवलीढ, Devoured, destroyed, Kirātārj. 13, 11. Frequent. To lick repeatedly, MBh. 1, 1181.<BR> --With आ आ, To lick, to touch, Ragh. 10, 46. आलिढ,<BR> 1. Eaten.<BR> 2. Polished, Bhartṛ. 2, 36. n. An attitude in shooting, the right knee advanced, the left leg retracted, Kumāras. 3, 70.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ-प्रत्यालीढ, Eaten. n. An attitude in shooting, etc. = आलीढ, n.<BR> --With परि परि, To lick, to enjoy, Rām. 2, 61, 16. Frequent. To lick repeatedly, Pañc. 55, 7 (see my transl. n. 257).<BR> --With सम् सम्, To lick, MBh. 3, 10653.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, To lick, MBh. 3, 11500.<BR> --Cf. λείχω, λιχανος, λειχήν; Lat. lingere, pol-lex; Goth. bi-laigôn; A.S. liccian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्
ऽलिह् -लिह्, latter part of comp. words, Licking.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनालिह्
रसना- + लिह् रसना- + लिह्, m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली ली (the original signification is ‘To be viscous,’ then ‘To be solvable’), i. 1 and 10, Par. To melt, to liquefy, to dissolve. ii. 9. लिना, लिनी, Par.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-b " target="_blank">Page0796-b + 41</a>] To adhere.<BR> 2. To obtain.<BR> --i. 4, Ātm. (properly pass.),<BR> 1. To be dissolved, to vanish, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 450.<BR> 2. To adhere or cling to.<BR> 3. To dwell, to live, to haunt, MBh. 1, 4310.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लीन.<BR> 1. Melted, dissolved, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 12.<BR> 2. Effaced, wiped away, removed, Kir. 5, 26.<BR> 3. Left.<BR> 4. Embraced.<BR> 5. Staying, Pañc. 187, 5; being situated, resting, Śāk. d. 144.<BR> 6. Entered, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830.<BR> --With the prep. अन्तर् अन्तर्, अन्तर्लीन, Inherent, staying; haunting in the interior, Pañc. 109, 19; i. d. 420; Utt. Rāmac. 56, 10; (not coming out), Pañc. 175, 24. Acc. sing. ˚नम्, adv. Inwardly, Pañc. 185, 3.<BR> --With अप अप, Caus. लापय, Ātm. To deceive, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 44.<BR> --With अभि अभि, अभिलीन, Adhering, Megh. 37.<BR> --With अव अव, To cling to, Nal. 2, 46.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, i. 4, To be dissolved, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 15.<BR> --With आ आ, i. 4, To faint, MBh. 3, 2573.<BR> --With नि नि, i. 4,<BR> 1. To alight, to settle, MBh. 3, 10560.<BR> 2. To lie down, MBh. 3, 12091.<BR> 3. To hide one's self, MBh. 3, 10978. निलीन,<BR> 1. Fused in or into.<BR> 2. Transformed.<BR> 3. Destroyed.<BR> 4. Encompassed.<BR> 5. Full.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, i. 4, To lie down, MBh. 3, 13654.<BR> --With प्र प्र, i. 4,<BR> 1. To be dissolved or absorbed, Man. 1, 54.<BR> 2. To die, Man. 4, 240.<BR> 3. To unite intimately, Man. 12, 17. प्रलीन,<BR> 1. Destroyed.<BR> 2. Unconscious, insensible.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, pass. To be destroyed, Hit. iii. d. 129.<BR> --With वि वि, i. 4,<BR> 1. To alight, Śiś. 1, 12.<BR> 2. To be dissolved, to vanish, Pañc. ii. d. 98; to become ineffectual, iii. d. 74. विलिन,<BR> 1. Liquefied, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a " target="_blank">Page0797-a + 41</a>] melted.<BR> 2. Dissolved, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830; Lass. 11, 15.<BR> 3. Disappeared.<BR> 4. Imagined.<BR> 5. United.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. वि-लायय, -लापय, -ली̆नय (properly a denomin. derived from विलीन), लालय (also a denomin. from लाला with वि), To dissolve. विलायित, Dissolved, Prab. 116, 8.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, i. 4, To be dissolved, to vanish, Bhag. 4, 23.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संलीन,<BR> 1. Joined, put together, Pañc. 163, 6.<BR> 2. Staying, MBh. 1, 7671.<BR> --Cf. Lat. līmus (borrowed O.H.G. lim; A.S. líme, and O.H.G. leim; A.S. lám), po-lîre, linere; λεῖμαξ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अली
अ- + ली अ- + ली, adj. living, Utt. Rāmac. 168, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीनता
लीनता लीन + ता (vb. ली), f. Lying, Śāk. d. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीला
लीला लीला (akin to लस्), f.<BR> 1. Play, sport, pastime, Pañc. 161, 15; लीलया (instr.), Sportively, Pañc. 229, 10; easily, without any effort, Pañc. 211, 12; Hit. 81, 18.<BR> 2. Amorous or wanton sport, Pañc. iii. d. 237.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
स-लील स-लील, adj. wanton, sportive. ˚लम्, adv. affectionately, Kir. 5, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलावती
लीलावती लीलावती, i. e. लीला + वन्त् + ई, f. A wanton woman, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच्
लुच् लुच् (vb. लुञ्च्), f.<BR> 1. Cutting off.<BR> 2. Dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्च्|लुंच्
लुञ्च् लुञ्च्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To pull out, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 3.<BR> 2. To pare, to peel, Pañc. 121, 13.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To pull off, MBh. 3, 10760.<BR> --With वि वि, To pull out, Bhaṭṭ. 18, 38.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. liuhhan; A.S. lyccan, evellere; Lat. runcare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चक
लुञ्चक लुञ्च् + अक, adj. One who pulls out.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशलुञ्चक|केशलुञ्चकः
केश- + लुञ्चक केश- + लुञ्चक, adj. pulling out the hair, Prab. 54, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चन|लुंचन|लुंचनं
लुञ्चन लुञ्च् + अन, n. Pulling out, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्ज्
लुञ्ज् लुञ्ज्, see लञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
1. लुट् लुट्, i. 1 and 4, Par.<BR> 1. To roll upon the ground, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 32 (cf. 3. लुठ्).<BR> 2. † To be connected with (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
† 2. लुट् लुट्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To resist.<BR> 2. To suffer pain.<BR> 3. To shine.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To shine, to speak.<BR> --Cf. रुट् and लुन्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
† 1. लुठ् लुठ्, i. 1, Par. To knock down.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To oppose.<BR> 2. To suffer pain.<BR> 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
2. लुठ् लुठ्, i. 10, Par., and लुण्ठ् लुण्ठ्, † रुण्ठ् रुण्ठ्, i. 1, Par. To rob.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लुण्ठित.<BR> 1. Plundered, robbed, Rājat. 5, 345; 427.<BR> 2. Peeled (?), Pañc. 121, 11 (cf. my transl. n. 790).<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, निर्लोठित, Robbed, Rājat. 5, 159. Cf. लुण्ट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
3. लुठ् लुठ्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To roll upon the ground, to welter, Hit. 123, 18.<BR> 2. To roll down, Rājat. 5, 92.<BR> 3. To move to and fro, Hit. ii. d. 67.<BR> 4. To agitate, to touch, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 18. Ptcple of the pf. pass. लुठित, Rolling on the ground. m. A horse's rolling on the ground.<BR> --With the prep. निस् निस्, निर्लुठित, Rolled down, Rājat. 5, 88.<BR> --With परि परि, To roll about, Daśak. 151, 5.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To roll on the ground, Pañc. 254, 22.<BR> --Caus. प्रलोठित, Rolling, heaving, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठन|लुठनं
लुठन लुठ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR> 2. Rolling on the ground with sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुड्
1. लुड् लुड्, and लुल् लुल्, i. 1, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a " target="_blank">Page0798-a + 39</a>] Par. To agitate, to stir, to disturb.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लुलित.<BR> 1. Agitated, Rām. 1, 42, 29.<BR> 2. Shaken, Utt. Rāmac. 140, 3.<BR> 3. Heaving, panting, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 15; Lass. 20, 20.<BR> 4. Destroyed.<BR> --Caus. लोडय, To agitate, MBh. 1, 2833. Ptcple of the pf. pass.<BR> I. लोडित, Troubled, Rām. 2, 95, 18.<BR> II. लोलित, Agitated, Śiś. 9, 4.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अन्-अभि-लुलित, Without being touched, Śāk. d. 61.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. लोडय,<BR> 1. To trouble, MBh. 1, 7921; with जालैस्, Pañc. 78, 14 (see my transl. n. 374, ‘To fish out,’ cf. वि).<BR> 2. To mix, MBh. 4, 689.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, Caus. लोडय,<BR> 1. To mix, MBh. 3, 11471.<BR> 2. To reflect, Skandap., Kāśīkh. 10, 48.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. लोडय, To agitate, to disturb, MBh. 2, 389.<BR> --With वि वि, विलुलित,<BR> 1. Tremulous.<BR> 2. Falling, shed fast (viz. tears), Utt. Rāmac. 68, 12.<BR> --Caus. लोडय,<BR> 1. To disturb, MBh. 2, 11604.<BR> 2. To fish out, MBh. 12, 4901.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. लोडय, To disturb, MBh. 1, 1477.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुड्
† 2. लुड् लुड्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To adhere, to be attached.<BR> 2. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ट्|लुंट्
लुण्ट् लुण्ट्, i. 1 and 10, Par.<BR> 1. To plunder.<BR> 2. † To disregard.<BR> 3. To peel (cf. my transl. of the Pañc. n. 790).<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, ptcple. of the pf. pass. उल्लुण्टित, Sacked, Pañc. rec. orn. MS. Berol. 121, a. Cf. 2. लुठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठ्|लुंठ्
लुण्ठ् लुण्ठ्, see 2. लुठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ड्|लुंड्
† लुण्ड् लुण्ड्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To plunder<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डीकृत
लुण्डीकृत लुण्डीकृत, i. e. लुण्ड् + अ-कृत, adj. Ragged, Mṛcch. 34, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुन्थ्|लुंथ्
† लुन्थ् लुन्थ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt, to kill.<BR> 2. To afflict.<BR> 3. To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्
लुप् लुप्, i. 1, लुम्प, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To break, to destroy, Hit. iv. d. 12; MBh. 1, 5560.<BR> 2. To spoil, Vikr. 27, 2.<BR> --Pass.<BR> 1. To be violated, Man. 2, 189.<BR> 2. To be lost, Man. 9, 211.<BR> --† i. 4, Par. To disturb, to bewilder.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लुप्त.<BR> 1. Neglected, Bhag. 1, 42.<BR> 2. Disturbed, Śṛṅgārat. 7.<BR> 3. Lost. n. Booty, plunder.<BR> --Caus. लोपय,<BR> 1. To cause to leave, to divert, Ragh. 12, 9 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To let violate, Man. 8, 16.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To break forth, Man. 7, 106.<BR> --With आ आ, Pass. To be troubled, to be clouded, Megh. 103.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To remove, Megh. 71. Pass. To be divided, Lass. 20, 20.<BR> --With परि परि, To disturb, to diminish, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 4.<BR> --With प्र प्र, pass. To be disturbed, MBh. 1, 7750.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र,<BR> 1. To rend in pieces, Man. 3, 225.<BR> 2. To disturb, MBh. 2, 161.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To rend in pieces, Man. 3, 204.<BR> 2. To disturb, Man. 2, 161.<BR> 3. To extinguish, Lass. 2. ed. 97, 54.<BR> 4. To become disfigured, Rām. 2, 60, 15 Gorr. विलुप्त,<BR> 1. Cut off.<BR> 2. Lost, Utt. Rāmac. 72, 12.<BR> 3. Interrupted, Pañc. ii. d. 2.<BR> 4. Seized.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To disturb, MBh. 1, 7752.<BR> 2. To extinguish, MBh. 1, 5233.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, प्रविलुप्त, Lost, removed, fallen.<BR> --Cf. Lat. rumpere; A.S. reaf, reafian; O.H.G. raubôn; very probably also Goth. raupjan, to pull out; λύπη, probably Ὄλυμπος (præruptus, based on a frequent.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुप्त
अ- + लुप्त अ- + लुप्त, adj. undisturbed, Rājat. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धक|लुब्धकः
लुब्धक लुब्ध + क (vb. लुभ्), m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a " target="_blank">Page0799-a + 42</a>]<BR> 1. A covetous or greedy man, Rājat. 5, 345.<BR> 2. A hunter, Pañc. 106, 7.<BR> 3. A libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धता
लुब्धता लुब्ध + ता (vb. लुभ्), f. Greediness, Rājat. 5, 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभ्
लुभ् लुभ्, i. 4, Par. To covet, to desire, Hit. i. d. 27, M.M. (with dat.).<BR> --i. 6, Par. To bewilder, to perplex.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लुब्ध.<BR> 1. Desiring, Hit. 16, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. Covetous, greedy, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 1.<BR> 3. Avaricious, Man. 4, 87. m.<BR> 1. A hunter, Rām. 2, 71, 35.<BR> 2. A lecher.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. लोभनीय, Worthy to be desired, Śāk. d. 20. Superl. लोभनीयतम, Most worthy to be desired, Indr. 5, 14.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to desire, to make greedy, Pañc. 256, 1.<BR> 2. To allure, Rām. 1, 8, 23.<BR> 3. To entice away, Rām. 3, 50, 6.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, Caus. To suffer to be allured, to long after, Rām. 3, 49, 38.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To allure, Mṛcch. 127, 16 (anomal. लोभसे).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To pollute, Man. 9, 20 (Ātm.).<BR> 2. To follow one's carnal desire, Pañc. 262, 9.<BR> --Caus. To allure, MBh. 3, 10044.<BR> --With वि वि, To disturb. विलुभित,<BR> 1. Bewildered.<BR> 2. Shaken (by wind).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To allure, to seduce, Vikr. 8, 16; Daśak. in Chr. 191, 10.<BR> 2. To beguile, Rām. 2, 94, 1.<BR> 3. To enchant, Śāk. 81, 17.<BR> --Cf. Lat. lubet, libet, libido, līber, ‘free’ and ‘son’; ἐλευθερός (based on an old frequent.); Goth. liubs, us-laubjan; A.S. leóf, lyfan, lufian, lóf, leaf, left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलुभ्
अति- + लुभ् अति- + लुभ्, adj. excessively greedy, Hit. ii. 1 (envious).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलुब्ध
गुण- + लुब्ध गुण- + लुब्ध, adj., f. धा, loving excellent qualities, Hit. iv. d. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुम्ब्|लुंब्
† लुम्ब् लुम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To torment.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To torment, or to be invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुल्
लुल् लुल्, see 1. लुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुष्
लुष् लुष्, see 2. लूष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुषभ|लुषभः
लुषभ लुष् + अ + भ (लुष् = vb. रुष्, cf. λύσσα), m. An elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुह्
† लुह् लुह्, i. 1, Par. To covet (cf. लुभ्; भ् is changed to ह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लू
लू लू, ii. 9, लुना, लुनी, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To cut, to clip, MBh. 3, 15644.<BR> 2. To destroy, Śiś. 1, 51.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. लून.<BR> 1. Cut, clipped, Pañc. i. d. 201; cut off.<BR> 2. Wounded, Hit. iv. d. 77.<BR> 3. Injured by biting, Hit. 58, 3.<BR> --With the prep. विप्र वि-प्र, विप्रलून, Severed, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 15.<BR> --Cf. λύω, ἀπο-λαύω; Lat. lucrum, solvo; akin are also Goth. fra-liusan; A.S. leosan, lysan, leás, los.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूता
लूता लूता, f.<BR> 1. A spider, Man. 12, 57; Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 13.<BR> 2. An ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनि|लूनिः
लूनि लू + नि, f. (?), Rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूम|लूमं
लूम लूम, n. A tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष्
† 1. लूष् लूष्, i. 1, Par. To adorn.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष्
† 2. लूष् लूष्, i. 10, and लुष् लुष्, i. 1, Par. To rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख लेख, i. e. लिख् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A letter, Hit. 120, 10.<BR> 2. A god.<BR> II. f. खा.<BR> 1. Writing.<BR> 2. A line, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 3; Bhartṛ. 2, 14; a stripe (of a cloud), Pañc. 203, 5; a stroke, Hit. pr. d. 1, M.M.; flashing (of lightning), Vikr. d. 76.<BR> 3. A mark, Kir. 5, 40.<BR> 4. Delineation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलेखा
इन्दु- + लेखा इन्दु- + लेख, f. खा, the crescent, Kir. 5, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलेख
चन्द्र- + लेख चन्द्र- + लेख,<BR> I. m. the name of a Rākṣasa, Rām. 6, 84, 12.<BR> II. f. खा. 1. the crescent, ib. 5, 19, 21. 2. a proper name, Rājat. 1, 218.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलेखा
चित्र- + लेखा चित्र- + लेख, f. खा, 1. an image, a picture, Gīt. 10, 15. 2. name of an Apsaras, Vikr. 7, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रलेखा
पत्र- + लेखा पत्र- + लेख, f. खा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a " target="_blank">Page0800-a + 42</a>] decorating the person by staining it with fragrant pigments of sandal, musk, etc., Hariv. 7078.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्रलेख
स-पत्र-लेख स-पत्र-लेख, adj. decorated with fragrant pigments, Ṛt. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिलेखा
शशिलेखा शशिलेखा, i. e. शशिन्-, f. 1. a digit of the moon. 2. the name of an Apsaras, Lass. 51, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लेख|हृल्लेखः
हृल्लेख हृल्लेख, i. e. कृद्-, m. 1. reasoning. 2. knowledge. 3. heartache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखक|लेखकः
लेखक लेखक, i. e. लिख् + अक, m. A writer, Pañc. 237, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखन|लेखनं|लेखनः
लेखन लेखन, i. e. लिख् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Scarifying.<BR> 2. Writing, copying, Pañc. 237, 1; scripture.<BR> 3. The bark of the Bhój tree and the leaf of the palm tree, used for writing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनिक|लेखनिकः
लेखनिक लेखनिक, i. e. लेखन + इक, m.<BR> 1. A letter-carrier.<BR> 2. One who signs by proxy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्
† लेप् लेप्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To serve (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप लेप, i. e. लिप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Smearing, plastering, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 748.<BR> 2. Mortar, plaster, MBh. 1, 5724.<BR> 3. Stain, spot.<BR> 4. The wipings of the hand which has offered funeral oblations to three ancestors, these wipings being considered as an oblation to ancestors in the fourth, fifth, and sixth degrees.<BR> 5. Food, Man. 3, 210.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेप|निर्लेपः
निर्लेप निर्लेप, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from spots, Man. 5, 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीलेप|पिंडीलेप
पिण्डी- + लेप पिण्डी- + लेप, m. a kind of ointment, Kathās. 28, 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रलेप|वज्रलेपः
वज्र- + लेप वज्र- + लेप, m. a kind of ointment (?), Pañc. iv. d. 10 (Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2704, pitch); cf. Wilson, Th. of the Hind. 2. ed. ii. p. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपक|लेपकः
लेपक लेपक, i. e. लिप् + अक, m. A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपकर|लेपकरः
लेपकर लेप-कर, m. A writer, Rām. 1, 12, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपन|लेपनं|लेपनः
लेपन लेपन, i. e. लिप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Anointing, Lass. 11, 2.<BR> 2. Smearing. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b " target="_blank">Page0800-b + 40</a>]<BR> 3. Plastering, Chr. 57, 22; Rām. 2, 91, 41 (both at the end of comp. adj. Plastered with).<BR> 4. Mortar, Man. 6, 76.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिलेपन|भूमिलेपनं
भूमि- + लेपन भूमि- + लेपन, n. cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपिन्
ऽलेपिन् -लेपिन्, i. e. लेप + इन्, adj. Having a plastering; in प्रभा-, adj. Covered with splendour, Vikr. d. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यकृत्
लेप्यकृत् लेप्य-कृ + त् (vb. लिप्), m. A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यमयी
लेप्यमयी लेप्यमयी, i. e. लेप्य + मय + ई (vb. लिप्), f. A doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह लेलिह, i. e. लिह्, frequent., + अ, m.<BR> 1. A serpent, MBh. 1, 1318.<BR> 2. A worm breeding in the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश लेश, i. e. लिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Smallness.<BR> 2. When latter part of compound words, often A little bit, little; e. g. Pañc. i. 353; MBh. 3, 1268; Śāk. d. 37.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुलेश
अश्रु- + लेश अश्रु- + लेश, m. drops of tears, Megh. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेयलेश|प्रालेयलेशः
प्रालेय- + लेश प्रालेय- + लेश, m. hailstone, Pañc. i. d. 353.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखलेश
सुख- + लेश सुख- + लेश, m. insignificant pleasure, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38; Pañc. i. d. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलेश
स- + लेश स- + लेश, adj. entire, Kirāt. 14, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टु|लेष्टुः
लेष्टु लेष्टु, perhaps लिश् + तु (but cf. लोष्ट, to which it seems to be akin), m. A clod of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहन|लेहनं
लेहन लेहन, i. e. लिह् + अन, n. Licking, tasting with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैण्
लैण् लैण्, see पैण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक्
लोक् लोक्, i. 1, Ātm., and i. 10, Par. (probably a denomin. derived from लोक),<BR> 1. To see.<BR> 2. i. 10, † To shine, to speak.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, i. 1 and 10,<BR> 1. To see, Hit. 15, 2, M.M.; to look, Hit. 85, 15; to regard, Vikr. 3, 6; to see to, Śāk. 3, 6; to watch, Pañc. 249, 4.<BR> 2. To perceive, Vikr. 21, 3; Lass. 9, 16.<BR> 3. To review (an army), Hit. 94, 8.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, i. 10, To inspect, Śāk. d. 13.<BR> --With आ [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a " target="_blank">Page0801-a + 45</a>] आ, i. 1 and 10,<BR> 1. To look out, MBh. 4, 250.<BR> 2. To regard, Vikr. d. 81; to see, Pañc. i. d. 21; to inspect, to view, MBh. 3, 11024.<BR> 3. To perceive, MBh. 2, 1817.<BR> 4. To consider, Man. 8, 126. सालोकित, n. Look, eye, Mālat. 16, 8.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To look at, MBh. 2, 775.<BR> 2. To acknowledge, Pañc. pr. d. 3.<BR> --With वि वि, i. 10, To see, Vikr. 8, 17; to regard, 12, 20; Utt. Rāmac. 47, 8. विलोक्य,<BR> 1. Regarding, i. e. to, Vikr. 40, 1; to view, Rām. 1, 44, 19.<BR> 2. To take a view of, Pañc. 46, 7.<BR> 3. To look over, Man. 8, 239.<BR> 4. To perceive, 2, 9.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. विलोकित, n. Seeing, Śāk. d. 36.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To look forward, Rām. 1, 9, 59. Cf. रुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक|लोकः
लोक लोक, i. e. लोच्, or रुच्, + अ (with ल् for र्, cf. रुच्), m.<BR> 1. Seeing, sight.<BR> 2. The world, the universe, Chr. 34, 8.<BR> 3. A world, a division of the universe, Vikr. 86, 8 (मध्यम, The middle world, i. e. the earth).<BR> 4. Man, mankind.<BR> 5. Men. people, sing. and pl., Daśak. in Chr. 183, 13; Pañc. i. d. 19; 256, 24; Bhartṛ. 2, 52.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक|अलोकः
अ- + लोक अ- + लोक, m. ceasing of the world, Rām. 1, 37, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलोक
अङ्ग- + लोक अङ्ग- + लोक, m. the name of a country, ib. 4, 43, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोक|अमरलोकः
अमर- + लोक अमर- + लोक, m. the world of the immortals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोक|इन्द्रलोकः
इन्द्र- + लोक इन्द्र- + लोक, m. the world of Indra, Man. 4, 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोक|गोलोकं|गोलोकः
गो- + लोक गो- + लोक, m. Kṛṣṇa's heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहलोक
गृह- + लोक गृह- + लोक, m. the household servants, Hit. 88, 18 (read त्वद्गृह˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनलोक|जनलोकः
जन- + लोक जन- + लोक, m. the name of a world supposed to be situated over the महर्लोक, Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवलोक|जीवलोकः
जीव- + लोक जीव- + लोक, m. 1. the world of living beings, i. e. the earth, Pañc. 226, 6. 2. mankind, people, Pañc. i. d. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोलोक|तपोलोकः
तपोलोक तपोलोक, i. e. तपस्-, m. one of the supposed seven worlds, Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तललोक|तललोकः
तल- + लोक तल- + लोक, m. the lower regions, ib. 2, 6, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोक|त्रिलोकः
त्रि- + लोक त्रि- + लोक,<BR> I. (n.), and f. की, the three worlds, MBh. 13, 1505; Rām. 3, 52, 22; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b " target="_blank">Page0801-b + 42</a>] Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 7.<BR> II. m. ˚क, the inhabitants of the three worlds, ib. 3, 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवीरलोक
नर-वीर- + लोक नर-वीर- + लोक, m. mankind, Hit. iv. d. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोक|परलोकं|परलोकः
पर- + लोक पर- + लोक, m. heaven, paradise, Pañc. 207, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरलोक|पौरलोकः
पौर- + लोक पौर- + लोक, m. pl. citizens, Pañc. 48, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मलोक|ब्रह्मलोकः
ब्रह्मलोक ब्रह्मलोक, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. the supposed eternal residence of the spirits of the pious, Sund. 4, 25; MBh. 12, 3996, in Chr. 94, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकालोक|लोकालोकः
लोकालोक लोकालोक, i. e. लोक-अ-, m. a mountainous belt bounding the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक|विलोकः
वि- + लोक वि- + लोक, adj. solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपाल|लोकपालः
लोकपाल लोक-पाल, m.<BR> 1. A king.<BR> 2. The name of certain divinities, guardians of the world, as Indra, Soma, etc.; cf. a list of them in Wilson's Specimens of the Theatre of the Hindus, i. 2. ed. 219, n. ad Vikr. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायत|लोकायतं|लोकायतः
लोकायत लोकायत, i. e. लोक-आ-यत (vb. यम्?), n. The system of atheistical philosophy, taught by चार्वाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतिक|लोकायतिकः
लोकायतिक लोकायतिक, लोकायत + इक, m. A follower of the Cārvāka system (see the last)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच्
1. लोच् लोच् (= रुच्, the initial र् is changed to ल्, as in the kindred languages, see रुच्), i. 1, Ātm. To see.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, Caus.<BR> 1. To behold, to perceive, MBh. 2, 617.<BR> 2. To regard, Hit. ii. d. 91 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 787).<BR> 3. To consider, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 8; to reflect, Hit. 14, 17.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. अन्-आलोचित, adj. Unconsidered, without due reflection, Pañc. 239, 4.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, To ponder, Lass. 33, 2.<BR> --Cf. λεύσσω s. v. रुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच्
† 2. लोच् लोच्, i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचक|लोचकः
लोचक लोच् + अक, m.<BR> 1. The pupil of the eye.<BR> 2. A wrinkled or contracted eyebrow.<BR> 3. Stibium.<BR> 4. An [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a " target="_blank">Page0802-a + 38</a>] ornament worn by women on the forehead.<BR> 5. An ear-ring.<BR> 6. The rejected slough of the snake.<BR> 7. A lump of flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचन|लोचनं
लोचन लोच् + अन, n. The eye, Vikr. d. 56.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुलोचन|चारुलोचनः
चारु- + लोचन चारु- + लोचन, adj., f. ना, having beautiful eyes, Hariv. 8705.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचन|त्रिलोचनः
त्रि- + लोचन त्रि- + लोचन, adj. having three eyes; epithet and name of Śiva, Ragh. 3, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलोचन
वाम- + लोचन वाम- + लोचन, adj., f. ना, having beautiful eyes, Hit. ii. d. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरलोचन
स्थिर- + लोचन स्थिर- + लोचन, adj. with fixed gaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिलोचन|हरिलोचनः
हरि- + लोचन हरि- + लोचन, m. 1. a crab. 2. an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट्
लोट् लोट्, see लोड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड्
† लोड् लोड्, लौड् लौड्, and लोट् लोट्, i. 1, Par. To be mad; cf. रोड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत|लोतं|लोतः
लोत लोत, m.<BR> 1. A tear.<BR> 2. A mark, a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत्र|लोत्रं
लोत्र लोत्र (a corruption of लोप्त्र), n. Stolen goods, booty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध|लोधः
लोध लोध, and लोध्र लोध्र, m. A tree, the bark of which is used in dyeing, Symplocos racemosa, Śiś. 9, 46; cf. रोध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप|लोपः
लोप लोप, i. e. लुप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Cutting off.<BR> 2. Omission, Man. 3, 63; Lass. 2. ed. 55, 73.<BR> 3. Destruction, disappearance.<BR> 4. Annulling, cancelling.<BR> 5. Elision, Lass. 2. ed. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपक
लोपक लोप + क, m. Violation, MBh. 1, 7772.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपन|लोपनं
लोपन लोपन, i. e. लुप् + अन, n. Violation, Man. 11, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाक|लोपाकः
लोपाक लोपाक, m. A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपापक|लोपापकः
लोपापक लोपापक,<BR> 1. m. A jackal.<BR> 2. f. पिका, A female jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपामुद्रा
लोपामुद्रा लोपामुद्रा, f. The wife of Agastya, Utt. Rāmac. 48, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाशक|लोपाशकः
लोपाशक लोपाशक,<BR> 1. m. A jackal.<BR> 2. f. शिका, A female jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्त्र|लोप्त्रं
लोप्त्र लोप्त्र, i. e. लुप् + त्र, n. Plunder, booty, MBh. 1, 4309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ|लोभः
लोभ लोभ, i. e. लुभ् + अ, m. Covetousness, Man. 2, 178; Pañc. ii. d. 168.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभ|अलोभः
अ- + लोभ अ- + लोभ, m. absence of desire, contentment, Hit. i. d. 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलोभ
अति- + लोभ अति- + लोभ, m. too great covetousness, Pañc. v. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभिन्
लोभिन् लोभिन्, i. e. लुभ् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Desirous, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोम|लोमं|लोमः
ऽलोम -लोम, a substitute for लोमन्, in अति-, adj., f. मा, With too much hair, Man. 3, 8. अनु-,<BR> I. adj. With the hair regular, Rām. 3, 49, 33.<BR> II. f. मा, A wife of a caste inferior to that of the man, Yājñ. 2, 288. प्रति-, see s. v. वि-,<BR> I. adj. (f. मी), Against the grain, reverse, backward, contrary.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Reverse order.<BR> 2. A snake.<BR> 3. A dog.<BR> 4. Varuṇa.<BR> III. n. A water-wheel. सु-, adj., f. मा, Having beautiful hair, Rām. 3, 49, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमन्
लोमन् लोमन्, i. e. रुह् + मन् (cf. रोमन्), n.<BR> 1. The hair of the body, Hit. iii. d. 29.<BR> 2. Feather, Chr. 32, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिलोमन्
असि- + लोमन् असि- + लोमन्, m. the name of a demon, MBh. 1, 2531.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमपाद|लोमपादः
लोमपाद लोमपाद, i. e. लोमन्-पाद, m. The name of a king of Aṅga, Lass. 2. ed. 58, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमश|लोमशः
लोमश लोमश, i. e. लोमन् + श,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Hairy, mixed with hair, Lass. 2. ed. 40, 24.<BR> 2. Woollen.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ram.<BR> 2. The name of a Ṛṣi.<BR> III. f. शा.<BR> 1. A fox.<BR> 2. A female divine being, an attendant on Durgā.<BR> 3. Green vitriol.<BR> 4. The name of several plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोमश|हंसलोमशं
हंस- + लोमश हंस- + लोमश, n. sulphate of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमालिका
लोमालिका लोमालिका, i. e. perhaps लोमन्-आलि + क, f. A fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल|लोलः
लोल लोल, i. e. लुल् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Shaking, tremulous, Hit. i. d. 152, M.M.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a " target="_blank">Page0803-a + 41</a>] trembling, Mālat. 21, 8.<BR> 2. Agitated, Ṛt. 6, 31.<BR> 3. Unsteady, Bhartṛ. 3, 36.<BR> 4. Desiring, Megh. 101; greedy, Rājat. 5, 376.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. The tongue.<BR> 2. Lakṣmī.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोल|आलोलः
आ- + लोल आ- + लोल, adj. trembling a little, Bhartṛ. 3, 48; Kir. 5, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोल|महालोलः
महा- + लोल महा- + लोल, m. a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुप|लोलुपः
लोलुप लोलुप् + अ (frequent. of लुप्), adj.<BR> 1. Desirous, Śāk. d. 98 (Prākṛ.); longing for, covetous, Pañc. iv. d. 12 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2753).<BR> 2. Destroying, MBh. 1, 1970.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुपता
लोलुपता लोलुप + ता, f. Greediness, Bhartṛ. 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुभ|लोलुभः
लोलुभ लोलुभ् + अ (frequent. of लुभ्), adj. Covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट्
† लोष्ट् लोष्ट्, i. 1, Ātm. (cf. लोष्ट), To gather into a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट|लोष्टं|लोष्टः
लोष्ट लोष्ट (for लोष्ट्र, q. v.),<BR> I. m. and n. A clod, a lump of earth, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 3; Man. 11, 263; 4, 49 (potsherd?).<BR> II. n. Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टक|लोष्टकः
लोष्टक लोष्ट + क,<BR> 1. (m. and n.), A clod (of dust), Rām. 3, 37, 18.<BR> 2. (n.), Spot, mark (of stripes), Mṛcch. 34, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टमय
लोष्टमय लोष्ट + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of clay, Man. 8, 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टु|लोष्टुः
लोष्टु लोष्टु (a form of लोष्ट्र, q. cf.; cf. क्रोष्टु = क्रोष्टृ), m. A clod of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट्र
लोष्ट्र लोष्ट्र, n. A clod of earth, Vikr. 54, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोह|लोहं|लोहः
लोह लोह, i. e. लुह्, instead of रुध् (see रुधिर), + अ,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. Iron, Man. 9, 321; Pañc. 100, 23 (cf. my transl.).<BR> 2. Steel.<BR> 3. Any metal, Hit. i. d. 92, M.M.<BR> 4. A weapon.<BR> 5. A fish-hook, Kām. Nītis. 1, 44.<BR> 6. Blood.<BR> 7. Aloe-wood.<BR> II. m. An iron-coloured kid, Man. 3, 272.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलोह|कृष्णलोहं|कृष्णलोहः
कृष्ण- + लोह कृष्ण- + लोह, n. the loadstone, Suśr. 1, 142, 17. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b " target="_blank">Page0803-b + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोह|नीललोहं
नील- + लोह नील- + लोह, n. blue steel, Rām. 3, 53, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोह|पञ्चलोहं
पञ्चलोह पञ्चलोह, i. e. पञ्चन्-, n. a metallic alloy containing five metals, copper, brass, tin, lead, and iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोह|महालोहं
महा- + लोह महा- + लोह, m. the loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविलोह|रविलोहं
रवि- + लोह रवि- + लोह, n. copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारलोह|सारलोहं
सार- + लोह सार- + लोह, n. steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकार|लोहकारः
लोहकार लोह-कार, m. A blacksmith, Pañc. iii. d. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहज|लोहजं
लोहज लोह-ज, n.<BR> 1. Bell-metal.<BR> 2. Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमय|लोहमयं
लोहमय लोह + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of iron.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वलोहमय
सर्व- + लोहमय सर्व- + लोहमय, adj. entirely of iron, Pañc. 122, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहल|लोहलः
लोहल लोहल,<BR> I. adj. Speaking indistinctly.<BR> II. (akin to लोह), m. The principal ring of a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित|लोहितं|लोहितः
लोहित लोहित (= लोहित, q. cf.),<BR> I. adj., f. ता, or इनी, Red, Śāk. d. 29.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Red, the colour.<BR> 2. The planet Mars.<BR> 3. A sort of deer.<BR> 4. A snake.<BR> 5. A form of array.<BR> 6. A sort of fish, Cyprinus rohita.<BR> 7. (m. ?). A kind of mineral, Pañc. i. d. 89.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Blood, Man. 4, 56.<BR> 2. War, battle.<BR> 3. Red sanders.<BR> 4. Saffron.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रलोहित|धूम्रलोहितः
धूम्र- + लोहित धूम्र- + लोहित, adj. of a grey-red colour, MBh. 13, 753.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोहित|नीललोहितः
नील- + लोहित नील- + लोहित,<BR> I. adj. blue-red, purple, of a purple colour, Śāk. d. 194.<BR> II. m. the name of one of the great periods called Kalpas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितक|लोहितकं|लोहितकः
लोहितक लोहित + क,<BR> I. adj. Red.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ruby.<BR> 2. The planet Mars.<BR> III. n. Calx of brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताङ्ग|लोहितांग|लोहिताङ्गः
लोहिताङ्ग लोहिताङ्ग, i. e. लोहित-अङ्ग, m. The planet Mars, Vikr. d. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताय|लोहितायः
लोहिताय लोहिताय, a denomin. derived from लोहित with य, Par. (anomal.), To become red, Lass. 2. ed. 78, 71; 96, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकायतिक|लौकायतिकः
लौकायतिक लौकायतिक, i. e. लोकायत + इक, m. An atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिक|लौकिकः
लौकिक लौकिक, i. e. लोक + इक, adj., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a " target="_blank">Page0804-a + 41</a>] f. की,<BR> 1. Relating to worldly things, Man. 2, 117; mundane (opposed to holy), Utt. Rāmac. 8, 2.<BR> 2. Usual, Man. 11, 184.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौकिक|अलौकिकः
अ- + लौकिक अ- + लौकिक, adj. 1. superhuman, Vikr. 19, 6; transcendental, Bhāṣāp. 62. 2. not common. 3. rare. 4. vedic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवलौकिक
जीव- + लौकिक जीव- + लौकिक, adj. belonging to the human world, MBh. 12, 8495.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौड्
लौड् लौड्, see लोड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौल्य|लौल्यं
लौल्य लौल्य, i. e. लोल + य, n.<BR> 1. Greediness, Pañc. 62, 21; desire, Ragh. 19, 19.<BR> 2. Passion, Pañc. v. d. 61.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौल्य
अ- + लौल्य अ- + लौल्य, adj. free from greediness, MBh. 1, 1506.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलौल्य
अति- + लौल्य अति- + लौल्य, n. excessive greediness, Pañc. 247, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वालौल्य
जिह्वा- + लौल्य जिह्वा- + लौल्य, n. greediness of one's tongue, Pañc. 105, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोलौल्य
मनस्- + लौल्य मनस्- + लौल्य, n. covetousness of mind, Hit. 87, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौह|लौहः
लौह लौह, i. e. लोह,<BR> I. adj. Made of iron, Johns. Sel. 15, 55(?).<BR> II. m. Iron, Rām. 2, 59, 41. (Hit. ii. d. 38, read लोह; cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2771.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित्य|लौहित्यं|लौहित्यः
लौहित्य लौहित्य, i. e. लोहित + य, n. Redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्पी
† ल्पी ल्पी, ल्यी ल्यी, ल्वी ल्वी, ii. 9, Par. To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व व, adv. Like, as (= इव), MBh. 12, 6597; Ragh. 4, 42 (Calc.); Megh. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश|वंशः
वंश वंश,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bambu, Hit. pr. d. 23, M.M.; a staff, Indr. 1, 8.<BR> 2. Lineage, race, Bhartṛ. 2, 24; Vikr. d. 153; bambu (or tree in general), and race, Pañc. ii. d. 189.<BR> 3. Multitude, Draup. 8, 5.<BR> 4. The back-bone.<BR> II. m., and f. शी.<BR> 1. A pipe, a flute, Ragh. 2, 12; Rājat. 5, 362 (m.).<BR> 2. Bambu manna.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंश|अवंशः
अ- + वंश अ- + वंश, m. a low race, Cāṇ. 1. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवंश|आदिवंशः
आदि- + वंश आदि- + वंश, m. a primary, a very old race, MBh. 1, 864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरवंश
जर्जर- + वंश जर्जर- + वंश, m. an old bambu stick, Pañc. 117, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासावंश|नासावंशः
नासा- + वंश नासा- + वंश, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b " target="_blank">Page0804-b + 40</a>] m. the bone of the nose, Pañc. 182, 16 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवंश|पृष्ठवंशः
पृष्ठ- + वंश पृष्ठ- + वंश, m. the back-bone, Suśr. 1, 350, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवंश|रघुवंशः
रघु- + वंश रघु- + वंश, m. the race of Raghu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवंश|सोमवंशः
सोम- + वंश सोम- + वंश, m. 1. the lunar dynasty. 2. a name of Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशज|वंशजः
वंशज वंश-ज, adj.<BR> 1. Caused in (or to) one's tribe, Pañc. v. d. 67 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1323).<BR> 2. Sprung from a good family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिक|वंशिकं
वंशिक वंशिक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a family.<BR> II. n. Aloe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश्य|वंश्यः
वंश्य वंश्य, i. e. वंश + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to a family, of the same family, Rājat. 5, 127.<BR> 2. Of a good family.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son, Man. 1, 61.<BR> 2. A kinsman.<BR> 3. pl. Ancestors, Ragh. 1, 66.<BR> 4. A pupil.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावंश्य
महा- + वंश्य महा- + वंश्य, adj. belonging to a very noble family, Rājat. 5, 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धवंश्य
विशुद्ध- + वंश्य विशुद्ध- + वंश्य, i. e. विशुद्धवंश + य (vb. शुध्), adj. descended from a good family, Rājat. 5, 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंह्
वंह् वंह्, see बंह् and 2. रंह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक
वक वक, m.<BR> 1. A crane, Ardea nivea, Pañc. ii. d. 87.<BR> 2. The name of a demon.<BR> 3. Kuvera.<BR> 4. An apparatus for subliming metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकव्रतिक
वकव्रतिक वकव्रतिक, i. e. वक-व्रत + इक, adj. (acting like cranes), Hypocritic, Man. 4, 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकुल|वकुलः
वकुल वकुल,<BR> I. m. A plant, Mimusops elengi, Ṛt. 2, 25 (बकुल); Mālav. (Weber, n. 73).<BR> II. f. ली, A sort of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकेरुका
वकेरुका वकेरुका, f.<BR> 1. (from वक), A small crane.<BR> 2. (vb. वङ्क्), The branch of a tree, bent by the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकोट
वकोट वकोट (from वक), m. A crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्क्
वक्क् वक्क्, see वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्यता
वक्तव्यता वक्तव्य + ता (vb. वच्), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a " target="_blank">Page0805-a + 43</a>] f.<BR> 1. The nature of what is to be said.<BR> 2. Blame, Man. 8, 230.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुकाम
वक्तुकाम वक्तुकाम, i. e. वक्तुम्-काम (vb. वच्), adj. Desirous of speaking, wishing to say, Vikr. 30, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुमनस्
वक्तुमनस् वक्तुमनस्, i. e. वक्तुम्-मनस् (vb. वच्), adj. Being about to speak, Pañc. 77, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तृ
वक्तृ वक्तृ, i. e. वच् + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. One who speaks, Bhāṣāp. 83; a speaker, Hit. ii. d. 128.<BR> 2. Talkative.<BR> 3. Eloquent, Bhartṛ. 2, 33.<BR> 4. Speaking truth.<BR> 5. Wise.<BR> 6. A teacher.<BR> --Cf. Lat. auctor (see the vedic significations).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्र|वक्त्रं
वक्त्र वक्त्र, i. e. वच् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. The mouth, Pañc. ii. d. 138; 264, 1.<BR> 2. The face, Pañc. 158, 22.<BR> 3. A verse.<BR> 4. A sort of garment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिवक्त्र
दधि- + वक्त्र दधि- + वक्त्र, m. the name of a monkey, Rām. 5, 60, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवक्त्र
दन्त- + वक्त्र दन्त- + वक्त्र, m. a proper name, MBh. 1, 2698.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवक्त्र|दशवक्त्रः
दशवक्त्र दशवक्त्र, i. e. दशन्-, m. a certain spell, Rām. 1, 31, 6 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवक्त्र|पंचवक्त्र|पञ्चवक्त्रः
पञ्चवक्त्र पञ्चवक्त्र, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. adj. having five faces, Rām. 5, 68, 7.<BR> II. m. a name of Śiva, Lass. 66, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावक्त्र
महा- + वक्त्र महा- + वक्त्र, adj. having a large mouth, Hiḍ. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्र|वक्रं|वक्रः
वक्र वक्र, i. e. वङ्क् + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Crooked, Pañc. iii. d. 75; bent, Śāk. d. 9; with पथिन्, a round-about way, Megh. 28.<BR> 2. Indirect, evasive.<BR> 3. Ambiguous, double-meaning, Kathās. 17, 141.<BR> 4. Fraudulent, Pañc. 44, 20; dishonest.<BR> 5. Cruel.<BR> II. m. A name of the planets Saturn and Mars, and of Rudra.<BR> III. n. The bend of a river.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टावक्र|अष्टावक्रः
अष्टा- + वक्र अष्टा- + वक्र, m. a proper name, MBh. 3, 10599.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिम
वक्रिम वक्रिम, i. e. वक्र + इम, adj., f. मा, Bent, Amar. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रोष्ठिका
वक्रोष्ठिका वक्रोष्ठिका, i. e. वक्र-ओष्ठ + क, f. A gentle smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष्
वक्ष् वक्ष्, i. 1, Par. (ved., also [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b " target="_blank">Page0805-b + 40</a>] Ātm.),<BR> 1. To grow, to become tall, Chr. 290, 3 = Rigv. i. 64, 3.<BR> 2. † To be angry.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. उक्षित, Grown up, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2.<BR> --Cf. 2. वज्, of which it is probably an old desider.; Goth. vahsjan; A.S. weaxan; αὔξω, αὐξάνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्
वक्षस् वक्षस्, n. The breast, Hit. iv. d. 130; the bosom, Pañc. 239, 4.<BR> --Probably for original पक्षस्, akin to पक्ष (cf. पिब, पिव, for original पिपा, बणिज्, वणिज्, for पणि-ज्); and cf. Lat. pectus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोज|वक्षोजं|वक्षोजः
वक्षोज वक्षोज, i. e. वक्षस्-ज, n. The female breast, Sāh. Darp. 307, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोरुह्
वक्षोरुह् वक्षोरुह् (Lass. 66, 8), and वक्षोरुह वक्षोरुह, i. e. वक्षस्-रुह् and रुह्, + अ, m. The female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वख्
† वख् वख्, वङ्ख् वङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्नु|वग्नुः
वग्नु वग्नु, i. e. वच् + नु, adj. Talkative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्|वंक्
वङ्क् वङ्क्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go tortuously.<BR> 2. To be crooked.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vacillare, vacare (properly, ‘To give way’), vacuus; O.H.G. waga, cuna, wagôn, moveri, waga; A.S. waeg, etc.; O.H.G. wank, wankôn; A.S. woh, wog, wó, a bending; wancol (perhaps to वङ्ग्), vacillans; probably ὄκνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क|वंक|वंकः|वङ्कः
वङ्क वङ्क् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The bend of a river.<BR> 2. Crookedness.<BR> II. f. का, The pommel of a saddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्रि|वंक्रि|वंक्रिः|वङ्क्रिः
वङ्क्रि वङ्क् + रि,<BR> I. n. A rib.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. The ribs of a building.<BR> 2. A sort of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षण|वंक्षणं|वङ्क्षणः
वङ्क्षण वङ्क्षण, m. The groin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ख्|वंख्
वङ्ख् वङ्ख्, see वख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग्|वंग्
† वङ्ग् वङ्ग्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To limp.<BR> --Cf. वङ्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग|वंग|वङ्गं|वङ्गः
वङ्ग वङ्ग,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Cotton.<BR> 2. The name of a country, Bengal.<BR> 3. Its inhabitants, Ragh. 4, 36.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Lead.<BR> 2. Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गशुल्वज|वंगशुल्वज|वङ्गशुल्वजं
वङ्गशुल्वज वङ्ग-शुल्व-ज, n. Brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्घ्|वंघ्
† वङ्घ् वङ्घ्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To blame.<BR> 3. To begin moving.<BR> 4. To begin.<BR> 5. To move swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्
वच् वच्, ii. 2, Par. (also Ātm.),<BR> 1. To speak, Draup. 6, 24 (अवोचस्, aor. with augment after मा); to say, with the acc. of the object and of the addressed person, Bhag. 2, 1.<BR> 2. To describe, Chr. 34, 7. Pass. उच्य,<BR> 1. To be spoken of (तत् किम् उच्यते, That needs not to be spoken of, i. e. that is of course the best), Pañc. 154, 24.<BR> 2. To be told, Vikr. 81, 5; to be admonished, Pañc. 32, 11.<BR> 3. To be called, Man. 1, 71.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. उक्त, Addressed (परुषाणि, with hard words), Hit. iii. d. 25. n.<BR> 1. A sentence, Pañc. 68, 1.<BR> 2. Speech, Rājat. 5, 205.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. वक्तव्य.<BR> 1. Fit or proper to be said.<BR> 2. Reprehensible.<BR> 3. One of bad fame, Man. 8, 66.<BR> 4. Vile, low.<BR> 5. Dependant, subject. n.<BR> 1. A rule.<BR> 2. Speaking, Pañc. 194, 23.<BR> 3. Speech.<BR> --Comp.<BR> बहु-, adj. much to be praised, Rājat. 5, 67.<BR> II. वचनीय.<BR> 1. To be spoken.<BR> 2. To be noticed, censurable, n. Blame, Utt. Rāmac. 28, 13.<BR> III. वाच्य.<BR> 1. Fit or proper to be spoken, Pañc. 83, 20.<BR> 2. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-b " target="_blank">Page0806-b + 42</a>] be predicated of anything, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 9; 212, 13.<BR> 3. Blameable, Sāv. 1, 32.<BR> 4. Contemptible, vile, outcaste. n.<BR> 1. A predicate.<BR> 2. Blame, Śāk. d. 112.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. not to be spoken of, Rām. 5, 36, 81. 2. not to be addressed, Man. 2, 128.<BR> दुस्-, adj. difficult to be spoken, harsh, Mārk. P. 8, 27. n. evil tidings, Rām. 5, 15, 42.<BR> --Comp. absol. अन्-उक्त्वा, without being ordered, Rājat. 5, 62. Desider. विवक्ष, To desire to speak, to say to, Chr. 57, 26.<BR> --Caus. वाचय.<BR> 1. To order to recite, Rām. 2, 25, 28.<BR> 2. To order to recite blessings, Rām. 2, 6, 7; Chr. 25, 51 (anomal. absol. वाच्य).<BR> 3. To read, Vikr. 26, 7.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To teach, Man. 11, 191. अनूचान, see s. v.<BR> --Caus. To read, Śāk. 17, 4; Vikr. 26, 3.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To address, to say to (with two acc.), MBh. 2, 1998.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To declare, MBh. 3, 1223; to explain, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 11.<BR> 2. To speak, to put properly, Man. 8, 55. निरुक्त, Distinctly declared. n.<BR> 1. Etymological explanation, MBh. 1, 266.<BR> 2. The name of one of the Vedāṅgas (see अङ्ग), ib. 12, 13232.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To begin to speak, Pañc. 77, 1.<BR> 2. To explain, Man. 1, 103; to tell, Pañc. 116, 1.<BR> 3. To say, Pañc. 4, 14; MBh. 2, 503.<BR> 4. To address, Pañc. i. d. 64; Chr. 44, 5. प्रोक्त,<BR> 1. Declared, Hit. iii. d. 74.<BR> 2. Called, Man. 1, 10; Pañc. ii. d. 93. प्रवचनीय,<BR> 1. To be well spoken.<BR> 2. (m.), A good speaker.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To explain comprehensively, Man. 8, 61.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer (with two acc.), Rām. 2, 68, 1. प्रत्युक्त, n. Answer, Megh. 112.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To address, Pañc. 97, 12.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vocare, vox; O.H.G. ga-wahan, memo-rare; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a " target="_blank">Page0807-a + 41</a>] ἔπος; εἶπον (i. e. ἐϝέϝεπον and ϝεϝεπον), θεό-προπος, πέπρωται, ὄψ, ὄσσα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्त
अन्- + उक्त अन्- + उक्त, adj. not uttered, Rām. 3, 14, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोक्त
अर्ध- + उक्त अर्ध- + उक्त, adj. half uttered; ˚तेन, instr. without finishing one's speech, Vikr. 29, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुक्त
दुरुक्त दुरुक्त, i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. adj. 1. harshly spoken to, Pañc. i. d. 100. 2. injurious, MBh. 13, 4987.<BR> II. n. injurious speech, ib. 13, 501.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्त|पुनरुक्तं
पुनर्- + उक्त पुनर्- + उक्त,<BR> I. adj. 1. repeated, MBh. 5, 632. 2. useless, Vikr. 40, 2.<BR> II. n. 1. repetition, Vikr. d. 153 (a second string of pearls). 2. tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलोक्त
प्रतिकूल- + उक्त प्रतिकूल- + उक्त, n. disagreeable speech, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1525.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच|वचः
वच वच् + अ, m. A parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचक्नु|वचक्नुः
वचक्नु वचक्नु (vb. वच्),<BR> I. adj. Talkative, eloquent.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचन|वचनं
वचन वच् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Speaking, Megh. 83 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. ना).<BR> 2. Speech, Pañc. 140, 16.<BR> 3. Word, name, Megh. 29; Vikr. 37, 8; Chr. 12, 26.<BR> 4. Order, Rām. 3, 48, 16.<BR> 5. Sentence, Pañc. 158, 13; 164, 20.<BR> 6. Rule.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन
अ- + वचन अ- + वचन, adj., f. ना, speechless, Śāk. 12, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्यवचन
तथ्य- + वचन तथ्य- + वचन, n. assertion, Pañc. 5, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवचन
प्रिय- + वचन प्रिय- + वचन, n. word of love, Vikr. d. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलवचन
प्रतिकूल- + वचन प्रतिकूल- + वचन, n. refractory speech, Pañc. 37, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषवचन
विशेष- + वचन विशेष- + वचन, n. special or different text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचन|सुवचनं
सु- + वचन सु- + वचन, n. eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनकर|वचनकरः
वचनकर वचन-कर, in अ-, adj. Not regarding advice, Hit. ii. c. 161, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीयता
वचनीयता वचनीय + ता (vb. वच्), f.<BR> 1. Rumour, especially ill report.<BR> 2. Blame, Hit. ii. d. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनेस्थित|वचनेस्थितः
वचनेस्थित वचनेस्थित, i. e. वचन + इ-स्थित (vb. स्था), adj. Compliant, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्
वचस् वच् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Speech, Pañc. iii. d. 113.<BR> 2. Words, a word, Vikr. d. 50.<BR> 3. Order, Chr. 12, 27.<BR> 4. Sentence, Pañc. 167, 7.<BR> 5. Voice, Ṛt. 6, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἔπος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वचस्|दुर्व्वचस्
दुर्वचस् दुर्वचस्, i. e. दुस्-, 1. m. abuse, bad language, Rām. 5, 31, 16. 2. adj. one who uses bad language, ib. 2, 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वचस्
सद्वचस् सद्वचस्, i. e. सन्त् (vb. 1. अस्), n. agreeable speech, Ṛt. 6, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचस्
सु- + वचस् सु- + वचस्, adj. speaking well or much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस
वचस वचस् + अ, adj. Talkative, eloquent, Chr. 296, 2 = Rigv. i. 112, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्कर|वचस्करः
वचस्कर वचस्-कर, adj. Compliant, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्
† 1. वज् वज्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. vagari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्
2. वज् वज्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. (rather Caus. of a lost vb. वज्, probably ‘To increase, to be strong;’ cf. वज्र, उग्र, ओजस्), To strengthen, Lass. 99, 7 = Rigv. iii. 62, 8.<BR> 2. † To prepare the way.<BR> 3. † (rather a denomin. derived from वाज), To trim or feather an arrow.<BR> 4. † To go.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vegere and augere, probably vigor, vigere; ὑγιής; O.H.G. auhôn; A.S. eacan, see वक्ष्; probably also A.S. wacor, cf. Icel. vakr; A.S. wácian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्र|वज्रं|वज्रः
वज्र 2. वज् + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Hard.<BR> 2. Cross, forked.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Indra's thunderbolt, a thunderbolt, Bhartṛ. 2, 32; Hit. ii. d. 158.<BR> 2. A diamond, Johns. Sel. 54, 136; Ragh. 1, 4; Rām. 3, 53, 59(?).<BR> 3. A form of array, Man. 7, 191.<BR> 4. The blossom of the sesamum.<BR> 5. n. Emblic myrobalan, Pañc. iv. d. 10(?).<BR> 6. Sour gruel.<BR> 7. Harsh language.<BR> 8. A child or pupil.<BR> III. f. रा, A plant, Menispermum cordifolium.<BR> IV. f. रा and री, A species of Euphorbia.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. weggi; A.S. waecg, wecg, cuneus, which probably was also the original signification of the Indian sbst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकपाटमन्त्|वज्रकपाटमत्
वज्रकपाटमन्त् वज्र-कपाट + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Having doors of diamond, Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकीलाय
वज्रकीलाय वज्रकीलाय, a denomin. derived from वज्र-कील with य, Ātm. To act like a thunderbolt.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वज्रकीलयित, Struck as by thunderbolts, Utt. Rāmac. 30, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रधर|वज्रधरः
वज्रधर वज्र-धर, and वज्रभृत् वज्र-भृ + त्, m. Indra, Rām. 3, 53, 60; Lass. 2. ed. 76, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रमय
वज्रमय वज्र + मय, adj., f. यी, Hard, adamantine, Utt. Rāmac. 164, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रिन्
वज्रिन् वज्रिन्, i. e. वज्र + इन्, m. Indra, Vikr. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्|वंच्
वञ्च् वञ्च्, i. 1, Par. (Ātm., see with निस्),<BR> 1. To go, to go to, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 74.<BR> 2. To pass over, Bhaṭṭ. 7, 106.<BR> --Caus. (properly, ‘To cause to go astray’),<BR> 1. To avoid.<BR> 2. and i. 10, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 1, 5794), To deceive, Pañc. 169, 1.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. किम् अर्थिनां वञ्चयितव्यम् अस्ति, ‘Why must the poor ones be deceived?’ Hit. i. d. 77, M.M.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To deceive, Chr. 59, 20.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus. To disappoint, Rām. 2, 52, 18.<BR> --With निस् निस्, i. 1, Ātm. To deceive, Śṛṅgārat. 10.<BR> --With परि परि, परिवञ्चित, Deceived, Hit. iv. d. 101.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vafer; probably ἄτη, ἀτάω (cf. विधिना वञ्चित, Kumāras. 4, 10), ἀπᾰ́τη, ἀτάσθαλος, ἀτύζομαι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चक|वंचक|वञ्चकः
वञ्चक वञ्च् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Fraudulent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cheat, Lass. 87, 11; a rogue, Man. 9, 257.<BR> 2. A vile man.<BR> 3. A jackal.<BR> 4. A tame, or house ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चथ|वंचथ|वंचथः|वञ्चथः
वञ्चथ वञ्च् + अथ, m. A rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चन|वंचन|वंचनं|वञ्चनं
वञ्चन वञ्च् + अन, n., and f. ना,<BR> 1. Fraud, Kathās. 3, 54.<BR> 2. Being cheated, Hit. i. d. 127, M.M.<BR> 3. Hallucination of mind, Rām. 2, 34, 37 (ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चुक|वंचुक|वञ्चुकः
वञ्चुक वञ्च् + उक, adj. Crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुल|वंजुल|वञ्जुलः
वञ्जुल वञ्जुल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of several plants, Utt. Rāmac. 46, 1; Sāh. D. 19, 19.<BR> 2. A sort of bird.<BR> II. f. ला, A cow that yields abundance of milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्
† वट् वट् (a form of वृत्, based on the original वर्त्).<BR> --i. 1, Par. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b " target="_blank">Page0808-b + 39</a>] surround.<BR> --i. 10, Par., also बट् बट्, वटय, बटय,<BR> 1. To surround.<BR> 2. To tie.<BR> 3. To partition.<BR> --i. 1, Par. or Caus. वटय, To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट|वटः
वट वट (probably a dialectical form of *वर्त, i. e. वृत् + अ),<BR> I. m., and f. टी, A string, a rope.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The large Indian fig-tree, Ficus indica, Pañc. 104, 17.<BR> 2. A circle.<BR> 3. Equality in shape or dimension.<BR> 4. A small shell, a cowrie.<BR> 5. Pulse ground and fried with oil or butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटक|वटकः
वटक वट + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Pulse ground and fried in oil or butter.<BR> 2. A weight of eight माषस्.<BR> II. f. टिका, A pill, a bolus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटर|वटरः
वटर वटर, m.<BR> 1. A cock.<BR> 2. A thief.<BR> 3. A rogue.<BR> 4. A turban (cf. वट).<BR> 5. i. e. वट, = *वर्त, + क, cf. वट, A churning-stick.<BR> 6. A mat.<BR> 7. A fragrant grass, Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटाकर|वटाकरः
वटाकर वटाकर (probably वट-आकर, but see the next), m. A cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटारक|वटारकः
वटारक वटारक, m. A cord, MBh. 3, 12776 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. का); cf. the last and वराटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटारकमय
वटारकमय वटारक + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of a cord, MBh. 3, 12785.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटि|वटिः
वटि वटि, m. A sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिभ
वटिभ वटि + भ, adj. Having or containing the insects called वटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटु|वटुः
वटु वटु, m.<BR> 1. A young Brāhmaṇa<BR> 2. A pupil, Utt. Rāmac. 104, 9; Prab 22, 3.<BR> 3. A lad, a stripling, Kumāras. 5, 83.<BR> 4. A fool, Śāk. 30, 12.<BR> 5. A flower, Bignonia indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटुक|वटुकः
वटुक वटु + क = वटु,<BR> 1. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठ्
† वठ् वठ्, बठ् बठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be large.<BR> 2. To be able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठर|वठरः
वठर वठर, m. A fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडभि|वडभिः
वडभि and वडभी वडभी̆, or वलभि and वलभी वलभी̆, f.<BR> 1. The wooden frame of a thatch, a roof, Megh. 39 (ड्).<BR> 2. A temporary building on the top of a palace, a turret, Mālav. d. 33 (वलभि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडवा
वडवा वडवा, see बडवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडा
वडा वडा, f. Pulse ground and fried with oil or butter (cf. वट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडिका
वडिका वडिका, i. e. वदा + क, f. Pulse ground and fried, Lass. 79, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडिश
वडिश वडिश. n., and f. शी, A fishhook, Bhartṛ. 1, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड्र|वड्रं
वड्र वड्र, adj. Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्
† वण् वण्, बण् बण्, i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वणिज्
वणिज् वणिज्, see बणिज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट्|वंट्
वण्ट् वण्ट्, i. 1 and 10, To partition, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 985.<BR> --Cf. वण्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट|वंट|वण्टः
वण्ट वण्ट् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A part.<BR> 2. The handle of a sickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टक|वंटक|वंटकः|वण्टकः
वण्टक वण्ट + क, m. A part.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्वण्टक|हृद्वंटक|हृद्वण्टकः
हृद्- + वण्टक हृद्- + वण्टक, m. the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टन|वंटन|वंटनं
वण्टन वण्ट् + अन, n. Dividing, Cāṇ. 5 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, p. 407.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ्|वंठ्
† वण्ठ् वण्ठ्, i. 1, Ātm. To go without a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ|वंठ|वण्ठः
वण्ठ वण्ठ, m.<BR> 1. An unmarried man.<BR> 2. A dwarf.<BR> 3. A javelin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठर|वंठर|वंठरः|वण्ठरः
वण्ठर वण्ठर, m.<BR> 1. A rope for tying a goat.<BR> 2. A dog's tail.<BR> 3. The sheath that envelopes the young bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठाल|वण्ठालः
वण्ठाल वण्ठाल, m.<BR> 1. A mode of conflict, the contest of heroes.<BR> 2. A boat.<BR> 3. A hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड्|वंड्
† वण्ड् वण्ड्, i. 1. Ātm.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b " target="_blank">Page0809-b + 42</a>] divide.<BR> 2. To cover.<BR> --i. 1 and 10, Par. To divide.<BR> --Cf. वण्ट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड|वंड|वण्डः
वण्ड वण्ड,<BR> I. adj. (A person) whose hands have been cut off.<BR> II. f. डा, An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
वत वत (perhaps curtailed अवत, 2. pl. imperat. of अव्; cf. Prākṛ. अविधा, Sch. ad Śāk. 93, 11), indecl. An interjection implying,<BR> 1. Sorrow, woe, Śāk. d. 152; Chr. 3, 37.<BR> 2. Compassion.<BR> 3. Pleasure.<BR> 4. Surprise, Kāvya Prak. 80, 7.<BR> 5. A vocative particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतंस|वतंसः
वतंस वतंस, i. e. अव-तंस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. An ear-ring.<BR> 2. A crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतोका
वतोका वतोका, i. e. अव-तोक, f. A cow miscarrying from accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स वत्स,<BR> I. (vb. 1. वस्), m.<BR> 1. A calf, Hit. i. d. 29, M.M.<BR> 2. i. e. probably *वतस्, = ϝέτος, + अ, A year.<BR> 3. The name of a Ṛṣi, or saint, Man. 8, 116.<BR> 4. pl. The name of a people and their country, Chr. 47, 41; 46, 24.<BR> II. m., and f. सा, Child, Pañc. 169, 25; a term of endearment, Pañc. 130, 4; Vikr. 70, 10; Utt. Rāmac. 8, 9.<BR> III. n. The breast.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. वत्सतर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्स|श्रीवत्सः
श्री- + वत्स श्री- + वत्स, m. 1. Viṣṇu. 2. a mark, usually said to be a curl of hair on the breast of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa, represented by , Johns. Sel. 96, 74. 3. a hole in a wall for felonious purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सतर|वत्सतरः
वत्सतर वत्सत + र,<BR> I. m. A steer.<BR> II. f. री, A heifer, Man. 11, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सर|वत्सरः
वत्सर वत्स + र, m. A year, Pañc. iii. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सल|वत्सलः
वत्सल वत्स + ल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, Affectionate, loving, Pañc. 222, 14; tender, Utt. Rāmac. 48, 1.<BR> II. f. ला, A cow anxious for her calf.<BR> III. n. Fondness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवत्सला
वर- + वत्सला वर- + वत्सल, f. the wife of a father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजवत्सल
सहज- + वत्सल सहज- + वत्सल, adj., f. ला, of inborn fondness, Hit. 87, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सलता
वत्सलता वत्सल + ता, f.<BR> 1. Tenderness, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 8.<BR> 2. Love, Rājat. 5, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सलय
वत्सलय वत्सलय, a denomin. derived from वत्सल, Par. To make tender towards children, Śāk. 102, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सीय|वत्सीयः
वत्सीय वत्सीय, i. e. वत्स + ईय,<BR> I. adj. Fit for a calf.<BR> II. m. A cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्
वद् वद्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To speak, to address (with the acc. of the object and the addressed person), MBh. 3, 1853.<BR> 2. To speak of (with gen.), Pañc. 67, 22.<BR> 3. To sound, to yell, MBh. 3, 15669.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. उदित,<BR> 1. Pronounced, Cāṇ. 1 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 407.<BR> 2. Addressed, Śiś. 9, 61.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. ब्रह्मोद्य, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-उद्य, n. Reciting or explaining the Veda; मृषोद्य, see s. v. सुखोद्य, i. e. सुख-उद्य, adj. To be uttered agreeably, Man. 2, 33.<BR> --Caus. वादय, To cause to sound, Pañc. 229, 13; to play, Man. 4, 64.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. जल-वादित, n. Water music, music performed by water, Hariv. 8426.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. वाद्य, n.<BR> 1. Sound, Ragh. 16, 64.<BR> 2. Any musical instrument, Pañc. 129, 15; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 7 (instrumental music).<BR> --Comp.<BR> जल-, n. a musical instrument sounded by means of water, Hariv. 8427.<BR> पर्ण-, n. a musical instrument made of leaves, Hariv. 3477.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To speak.<BR> 2. To command.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To speak similarly, to imitate another's voice or sound, Ragh. 5, 74 (Calc.).<BR> --With अप अप, To reprove, to insult, Man. 4, 236.<BR> --Caus. To dissuade from, to reprove, MBh. 3, 1036.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To address, Man. 8, 356.<BR> 2. To salute respectfully, MBh. 3, 15668.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To greet respectfully, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-b " target="_blank">Page0810-b + 40</a>] Man. 2, 117; Vikr. 81, 2; with पादयोस्, To greet one by touching his feet, Man. 2, 212.<BR> 2. To play, MBh. 3, 14386.<BR> --With प्रत्यभि प्रति-अभि, Caus. To return a salute, Mṛcch. 34, 7.<BR> --With आ आ, To salute by roaring, Chr. 290, 9 = Rigv. i. 64, 9.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To speak, MBh. 3, 16148.<BR> --With उप उप, Ātm.<BR> 1. To conciliate, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 28.<BR> 2. To beg, Pañc. in Weber, Ind. St. 272, 22 (see my transl. n. 922).<BR> 3. To allure.<BR> --With परि परि, To calumniate, MBh. 1, 3079.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To converse, Pañc. 143, 21.<BR> 2. To explain, Man. 5, 55.<BR> 3. To declare, Hit. ii. d. 160.<BR> 4. To call, Hit. ii. d. 41.<BR> 5. To tell, MBh. 3, 2910.<BR> --Caus. To play, MBh. 1, 5356.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To disagree.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Par. To accord. Ātm. To converse, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 28.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To answer, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 13.<BR> --With वि वि, Ātm. (also Par., Hit. iii. d. 32; Pañc. 183, 6).<BR> 1. To dispute, to wrangle, Man. 3, 159.<BR> 2. To contest, with acc., MBh. 2, 2390.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To converse, Chr. 19, 8; Hit. 88, 13; iii. d. 36.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To play, MBh. 1, 7056.<BR> 2. To declare, Man. 8, 31.<BR> --With विसम् वि-सम्, To break a promise, Man. 8, 219.<BR> --Cf. αὐδή, αὐδάω, perhaps ϕράζω, ϕραδάω; probably Lat. vas, vadis; perhaps O.H.G. far-wâzan; O. Saxon, for-wâtan, recusare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद|वदः
वद वद् + अ, adj. Speaking, speaking well.<BR> --Cf. वशंवद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन|वदनं
वदन वद् + अन, n. The mouth, the face, Pañc. 185, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसपिण्डगृहीतवदन
मांस-पिण्ड-गृहीत- + वदन मांस-पिण्ड-गृहीत- + वदन, adj., f. ना, carrying [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a " target="_blank">Page0811-a + 40</a>] in the mouth a piece of flesh, Pañc. 226, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवदन
सु- + वदन सु- + वदन, adj., f. ना, beautiful, Ṛt. 6, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्य|वदन्यः
वदन्य वदन्य, see वदान्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदरी
वदरी वदरी, f. see बदर, Matsyop. 3, and MBh. 3, 1637; questionable, probably = बदरी-शैल, n. A part of the Himālayarange, and a celebrated place of pilgrimage, cf. Johns. Sel. 90, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदान्य|वदान्यः
वदान्य वदान्य, adj.<BR> I. i. e. अव-दान + य (also वदन्य वदन्य), Munificent, liberal, Man. 4, 224.<BR> II. (from वद्),<BR> 1. Speaking kindly.<BR> 2. Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदाल|वदालः
वदाल वदाल, m. A sheat-fish, Silurus boalis Ham.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदावद|वदावदः
वदावद वदावद (an old frequent. of वद् + अ), adj. Speaking, able to speak well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्
वध् वध्, see हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध|वधः
वध वध् + अ (also बध बध, probably better) m.<BR> 1. Killing, Man. 5, 89; murder, Pañc. i. d. 305.<BR> 2. Death, Man. 8, 104.<BR> 3. Corporal punishment, Man. 9, 291.<BR> 4. A stroke, 11, 100.<BR> 5. A whip, 8, 267.<BR> 6. Hurting, Man. 4, 165.<BR> 7. A killer, a slaughterer, Man. 5, 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध|अवधः
अ- + वध अ- + वध, m. no slaughterer, Man. 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवध|आत्मवधः
आत्मवध आत्मवध, i. e. आत्मन्-, m. suicide, MBh. 1, 6228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवध|गोवधः
गो- + वध गो- + वध, m. slaying a bull or a cow, Man. 11, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपालवध
शिशु-पाल- + वध शिशु-पाल- + वध, m. the destruction of Śiśupāla, title of a poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवध|शुद्धवधः
शुद्ध- + वध शुद्ध- + वध (vb. शुध्), m. simple putting to death, i. e. in any ordinary way, Man. 9, 279 (ब्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधक|वधकः
वधक वध् + अक, also बधक,<BR> I. adj. Destructive, injurious.<BR> II. m. A murderer, Kathās. 3, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधत्र|वधत्रं
वधत्र वध् + अत्र, n. A weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधु|वधुः
वधु वधु (vb. वह्, q. cf.), f.<BR> 1. A wife.<BR> 2. A son's wife (cf. वधू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुटी
वधुटी वधुटी, f. A son's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधू
वधू वधू, also बधू बधू (vb. वह्, q. cf.), f.<BR> 1. A woman, Kirāt. 6, 45.<BR> 2. A wife, Hit. i. d. 192, M.M.; Rām. 3, 51, 14; 55, 29.<BR> 3. A wife recently married.<BR> 4. A son's wife, Sāv. 6, 9.<BR> 5. A female relation, Sund. 4, 16.<BR> 6. The name of several plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलवधू
कुल- + वधू कुल- + वधू, f. a virtuous or respectable wife, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववधू
नव- + वधू नव- + वधू, f. a woman recently married, Ṛt. 6, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवधू
नाग- + वधू नाग- + वधू, f. the female of an elephant, Rām. 2, 65, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्यवधू
प्रेष्य- + वधू प्रेष्य- + वधू, f. a female servant, Draup. 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवधू
वार- + वधू वार- + वधू, f. the head of a set of harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वधू
स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू, and स्वर्गि(न्)-, f. an Apearas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गवधू
स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू, and स्वर्गि(न्)-, f. an Apearas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिवधू
स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू स्वर्-, स्वर्ग- + वधू, and स्वर्गि(न्)-, f. an Apearas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूटी
वधूटी वधूटी, f.<BR> 1. A son's wife.<BR> 2. A young woman, living in her father's house, whether married or unmarried, Bhāṣāp. 1, a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूयु
वधूयु वधूयु, i. e. वधूय, ved., + उ, adj. One who loves his wife, Lass. 99, 8 (where बधूयु) = Rigv. iii. 62, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वध्यता
वध्यता वध्य + ता, or बध्यता बध्य + ता (from वध्, see हन्), f.<BR> 1. Deserving death, Nal. 9, 8.<BR> 2. Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्
† 1. वन् वन्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To serve, to honour.<BR> --Caus. वनय,<BR> 1. To act.<BR> 2. To hurt, to kill. See 3. तन्.<BR> --Cf. perhaps A.S. an-winnan, to fight against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्
2. वन् वन्, ii. 8, Par. Ātm. (in the Vedas also i. 1; ii. 2, etc.).<BR> 1. To ask, to beg.<BR> 2. To accept, Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वनित, Solicited, begged. f. ता,<BR> 1. A beloved woman, a mistress, Bhartṛ. 2, 36.<BR> 2. A woman in general, Vikr. d. 44.<BR> 3. A female bird, Kir. 6, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. 1. वन्, the vedic use, and Lat. Venus, venustas, venerari; O.H.G. wunna; A.S. wyn, ge-wenian; Goth. vêns; A.S. to-wenan; probably ὀνίνημι, ὀνήσω, ὄνειαρ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशवनिता
त्रिदश- + वनिता त्रिदश- + वनित, f. ता, the wife of a deity, Megh 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाकवनित
स-नाक-वनित स-नाक-वनित, adj. endowed with the celestial women (i. e. the Apsarases), Kir. 5, 27. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a " target="_blank">Page0812-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
वन वन,<BR> I. n., and f. नी, A forest, Vikr. d. 79 (न); Pañc. iii. d. 56 (न).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. A cascade or fountain.<BR> 3. A residence, Nal. 3, 22.<BR> 4. A house.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रवन|असिपत्रवनं
असि-पत्र- + वन असि-पत्र- + वन, n. the name of a hell, Man. 4, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवन
चित्र- + वन चित्र- + वन, n. the name of a forest, Hit. 14, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवन
तपोवन तपोवन, i. e. तपस्-, n. a place frequented by ascetics, a sacred grove, Hit. iv. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वण|निर्व्वण
निर्-वण निर्-वण, i. e. निस्-, adj. one who has left a forest, MBh. 5, 863 (˚वन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुवन
परशु- + वन परशु- + वन, n. the name of a hell, MBh. 12, 12075.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवन|पितृवनं
पितृ- + वन पितृ- + वन, n. a cemetery, MBh. 11, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदवन|प्रमदवनं
प्रमद- + वन प्रमद- + वन, n. a royal garden, Vikr. 19, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावन|महावनं
महा- + वन महा- + वन, n. a large forest, Rām. 3, 55, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचर|वनचरः
वनचर वन-चर, m.<BR> 1. A wild beast, Pañc. 255, 17.<BR> 2. A forester, Kirāt. 6, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनज|वनजं|वनजः
वनज वन-ज,<BR> I. adj. Wild.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An elephant.<BR> 2. A fragrant grass, Cyperus rotundus.<BR> III. f. जा, A sort of pulse.<BR> IV. n. A lotus, Ragh. 5, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनद|वनदः
वनद वन-द, and वनमुच् वन-मुच्, m. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनर|वनरः
वनर वनर (from वन), m. A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थ|वनस्थः
वनस्थ वन-स्थ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Being in a forest, Pañc. iii. d. 145.<BR> 2. Living in a forest, Rām. 3, 48, 18.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A deer.<BR> 2. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पति|वनस्पतिः
वनस्पति वनस्पति i. e. वन् (= वन), + अस्-पति, m.<BR> 1. A tree, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 11.<BR> 2. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाटु|वनाटुः
वनाटु वनाटु, i. e. वन-अट् + उ, m. A blue fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायु|वनायुः
वनायु वनायु, m. The name of a country. Ragh. 5, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायुज|वनायुजः
वनायुज वनायु-ज, m. A horse of the Vanāyu breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनार्चक|वनार्चकः|वनार्च्चक|वनार्च्चकः
वनार्चक वनार्चक, i. e. वन-अर्च् + अक, m. A florist, a garland maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाहिर|वनाहिरः
वनाहिर वनाहिर, m. A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनि|वनिः
वनि वन् + इ, m.<BR> 1. Fire or its deity.<BR> 2. Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिन्
वनिन् वनिन्, i. e. वन + इन्, adj. Abounding in water, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीक|वनीकः
वनीक वनीक, and वनीयक वनीयक (vb. वन्), m. A beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचर|वनेचरः
वनेचर वनेचर, i. e. वन + इ-चर,<BR> I. adj. Who or what abides in a forest. Rām. 3, 51, 34.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A forester, Kirāt. 1, 1.<BR> 2. A demon.<BR> 3. A wild beast, Lass. 47, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्|वंद्
वन्द् वन्द् (akin to वद्), i. 1. Ātm.<BR> 1. To salute respectfully, Vikr. 81, 11; MBh. 2, 23.<BR> 2. To praise, Rām. 2, 16, 27.<BR> 3. To venerate, Megh. 12.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. जगद्वन्द्य, i. e. जगत्-, adj. To be praised by mankind, epithet of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 2, 23.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To salute respectfully, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 15.<BR> --With सम् सम्, The same. MBh. 1, 5420.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दन|वंदन|वंदनं|वन्दनं
वन्दन वन्द् + अन,<BR> I. m. A proper name, Chr. 296, 5 = Rigv. i. 112, 5.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Salutation, Man. 2, 216.<BR> 2. The mouth or face.<BR> III. f. ना.<BR> 1. Praise, Chr. 19, 6; praising especially the gods.<BR> 2. Prayer, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 16.<BR> IV. f. नी.<BR> 1. Worship.<BR> 2. Begging, asking.<BR> 3. A drug for restoring the dead to life.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवन्दन|पादवंदन
पाद- + वन्दन पाद- + वन्दन, n. worship, reverence, Yājñ. 1, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारु|वंदारु|वन्दारुः
वन्दारु वन्द् + आरु,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Civil, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a " target="_blank">Page0813-a + 40</a>] polite.<BR> 2. Praising, worshipping, Lass. 67, 6.<BR> II. m. A bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दि|वन्दिः
वन्दि and वन्दी वन्दी̆, f.<BR> 1. A woman in captivity, also a man, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 32; 63; Vikr. d. 3 (वन्दी कृ, To make captive).<BR> 2. A ladder or stairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन् वन्द् + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A praiser, Pañc. 158, 2.<BR> 2. An encomiast, Man. 3, 158; a bard, Vikr. d. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दीकार|वन्दीकारः
वन्दीकार वन्दी-कार, m. A housebreaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्र|वंद्र|वन्द्रं|वंद्रः|वन्द्रः
वन्द्र वन्द् + र, adj. Worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुर|वंधुर
वन्धुर वन्धुर, m. The seat of a chariot, Chr. 290, 9 = Rigv. i. 64, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्य|वन्यं|वन्यः
वन्य वन्य, i. e. वन + य,<BR> I. adj. Produced in, or by, a wood, Pañc. 216, 10; wild, Man. 6, 12.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. A multitude of groves.<BR> 2. A quantity of water, a flood.<BR> III. n. Wild fruit, Rām. 3, 52, 51; 53, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्र|वन्रः
वन्र वन् + र, m.<BR> 1. A co-partner.<BR> 2. A co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्
वप् वप्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> I. (properly Caus. of वी).<BR> 1. To sow, MBh. 3, 1248; figurat., Man. 2, 113.<BR> 2. To cast, MBh. 2, 2033.<BR> 3. † To procreate. Pass. उप्य, Man. 9, 26.<BR> II. (properly a Caus. of वे), To weave.<BR> III. † To shave.<BR> --Caus. वापय, To sow, MBh. 3, 18031.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To put on, Chr. 294, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 4.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To sow, MBh. 3, 17341.<BR> 2. To throw to, MBh. 3, 103.<BR> --Caus. To arrange, to dress, MBh. 1, 819 (cf. with वि).<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, Caus. To cause to be sown, or thrown in, Lass. 2. ed. 12, 9.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To sow, MBh. 3, 17341.<BR> 2. To offer, Man. 3, 216.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To drop. Man. 3, 92.<BR> 2. To sprinkle, Man. 3, 214. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b " target="_blank">Page0813-b + 42</a>]<BR> 3. To offer, Man. 9, 140.<BR> 4. To perform (a sacrifice), Man. 4, 10; 6, 38 (read निरुप्य).<BR> --Caus. To disseminate, Pañc. 85, 20.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To sow, MBh. 3, 15725.<BR> 2. To cast, ib. 3, 1931.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To inlay, to stud, to adorn, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 16. प्रत्युप्त, Shut(?), Utt. Rāmac. 87, 3.<BR> --With वि वि, व्युप्त, Disordered, dishevelled, Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 14.<BR> --Cf. ὀπυίω and ὄιϕω, ὄιϕεω; A.S. wíf; probably also ὅπλον; Goth. vêpn; A.S. waepen. Cf. वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप|वपः
वप वप, i. e.<BR> I. वप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sowing seed.<BR> 2. Shaving.<BR> II. f. पा.<BR> 1. The mucous or glutinous secretion of the flesh or bones, marrow, Rām. 1, 13, 39.<BR> 2. Fat, Man. 12, 63.<BR> 3. Any hole or cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपन|वपनं
वपन वप् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sowing seed.<BR> 2. Semen virile.<BR> 3. Shaving, Man. 5, 140.<BR> II. f. नी, A barber's shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष
ऽवपुष -वपुष, i. e. वपुस् + अ, at the end of comp. instead of वपुस्, in वराह-, n. The body of a hog, Johns. Sel. 94, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्मन्त्|वपुष्मत्
वपुष्मन्त् वपुष्मन्त्, i. e. वपुस् + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Having a body, corporeal, embodied, Kir. 2, 59, Lass. 2. ed. 76, 47.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Sund. 3, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्
वपुस् वपुस् (cf. वपा), n.<BR> 1. The body, Pañc. iii. d. 221.<BR> 2. A handsome form or figure, Śāk. d. 16.<BR> 3. Beauty, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4 (dat. in the sense of the infin. ‘In order to be beautiful’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तृ
वप्तृ वप् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. तॄ, and n.<BR> 1. Who or what sows.<BR> 2. A husbandman, Man. 3, 142.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A progenitor, a father.<BR> 2. A poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्यटदेवी
वप्यटदेवी वप्यट-देवी, f. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 281.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्र|वप्रं|वप्रः
वप्र वप् + र,<BR> I. m. (and n.).<BR> 1. A field, Kir. 5, 36.<BR> 2. Dust, earth.<BR> 3. A mound, Megh. 2; a hillock.<BR> 4. The foundation of any building.<BR> 5. A shore or bank, Kir. 6, 8.<BR> 6. A rampart, MBh. 1, 5810.<BR> 7. The gate of a fortified city.<BR> II. m. A father.<BR> III. f. री, An ant-hill.<BR> IV. n. Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रि|वप्रिः
वप्रि वप् + रि, m.(?), A field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वभ्र्
वभ्र् वभ्र्, see बभ्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्
वम् वम्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To vomit, Man. 4, 121.<BR> 2. To spit out, Rām. 1, 28, 26.<BR> 3. To send forth, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वान्त.<BR> 1. Vomited.<BR> 2. Effused, Megh. 20.<BR> 3. One who has vomited, Man. 5, 144.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. वा̆मय; ptcple. of the pf. pass. वमित, Made to vomit.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To spit out, to vomit, MBh. 3, 15729; figuratively, 3, 1931.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vomere; ἐμέω; Goth. vamm, macula, ana-vammjan; A.S. wemman, maculare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वान्त
दुर्वान्त दुर्वान्त, i. e. दुस्-, adj. one who has been wrongly treated with emetics, Suśr. 2, 191, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम वम् + अ, m., and f. मी, Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथु|वमथुः
वमथु वम् + अथु, m.<BR> 1. Vomiting.<BR> 2. Water ejected from an elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमन|वमनं|वमनः
वमन वम् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Vomiting, Lass. 17, 4; taking, getting. Ragh. 15, 29.<BR> 2. An emetic.<BR> 3. Paining.<BR> II. f. नी, A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमि|वमिः
वमि वम् + इ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> II.<BR> 1. Vomiting, Suśr. 2, 491, 21.<BR> 2. An emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्र|वम्रः
वम्र वम्र,<BR> 1. m. A proper name, Chr. 297, 15 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR> 2. f. रा and री, A small ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्
† वय् वय्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थ|वयःस्थः
वयःस्थ वयःस्थ, and वयस्थ वयस्थ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b " target="_blank">Page0814-b + 40</a>] i. e. वयस्-स्थ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Young.<BR> 2. Mature, middle-aged, from sixteen to seventy.<BR> II. m. A contemporary, a friend.<BR> III. f. स्था.<BR> 1. A woman's female friend.<BR> 2. The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्
वयस् वयस्, n.<BR> 1. Youth, Pañc. i. d. 11.<BR> 2. Age, Vikr. d. 42; time of life, Pañc. iii. d. 221.<BR> 3. A bird, Pañc. i. d. 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवयस्
गत- + वयस् गत- + वयस्, adj. old, Pañc. i. d. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ववयस्
पूर्व- + वयस् पूर्व- + वयस्, adj. Young, MBh. 1, 3196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
स- + वयस् स- + वयस्,<BR> I. adj. contemporary.<BR> II. m. a contemporary, a friend.<BR> III. f. a woman's female friend, Śiś. 9, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्क
वयस्क वयस् + क, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to age.<BR> 2. A substitute for वयस्, as latter part of comp. adj.; e. g. अभिनव-, adj. Young, Hit. 50, 1. समान-, adj. one who is of the same age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्थ|वयस्थः
वयस्थ वयस्थ, see वयःस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्य|वयस्यः
वयस्य वयस् + य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A contemporary, Rām. 1, 12, 22.<BR> 2. A friend, Vikr. 11, 15.<BR> II. f. या, A woman's female friend, Nal. 4, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुन|वयुनं|वयुनः
वयुन वयुन, n.<BR> 1. The faculty of perceiving, consciousness, Chr. 294, 2, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 2; 6.<BR> 2. A temple, Bhāg. P. 3, 4, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोतिग
वयोतिग वयोतिग, i. e. वयस्-अति-ग (vb. गम्), adj. m. A decrepit old man, Man. 7, 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधस्
वयोधस् वयोधस्, i. e. वयस्-धा, m. A young man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्य
वय्य वय्य, m. A proper name, Chr. 296, 6 = Rigv. i. 112, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्
वर् वर्, see वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर वर (erroneously बर बर), i. e. वृ + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Better, Pañc. ii. d. 96.<BR> 2. Best, Indr. 5, 20; excellent, Vikr. d. 119; precious, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M.; beautiful, Rām. 3, 51, 37. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-a " target="_blank">Page0815-a + 46</a>]<BR> 3. Eldest.<BR> II. acc. sing. रम्, adv. Better, preferable, Pañc. pr. d. 4 (अ-जात-मृत-मूर्खेभ्यो मृत-अ-जातौ सुतौ वरम्, If it is to be chosen between having a dead son, or no son, or a stupid one, it is better to have a dead one, or no son at all); with following न, Rather than, Bhartṛ. 2, 11; with following न पुनर्, Better than, Pañc. 138, 19. वरं वा--मा, Rather than, Pañc. pr. d. 6.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Selecting.<BR> 2. Soliciting.<BR> 3. Wish, Rām. 3, 53, 8.<BR> 4. A boon, a blessing, Pañc. 135, 8; Hit. 116, 6; a favour, Rām. 3, 53, 6; a privilege, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 17.<BR> 5. One who solicits a girl for his wife, Sāv. 1, 28; a bridegroom, Pañc. 129, 15.<BR> 6. A son-in-law.<BR> 7. A husband, Lass. 2. ed. 35, 20.<BR> 8. A catamite.<BR> 9. A sparrow.<BR> 10. Surrounding.<BR> IV. f. रा.<BR> 1. A sort of perfume.<BR> 2. The three myrobalans.<BR> 3. A plant, Cissampelos hexandra.<BR> V. f. री.<BR> 1. छाया, the wife of the sun.<BR> 2. Asparagus racemosus.<BR> VI. m. Saffron.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vaila; A.S. wel; O.H.G. wela; A.S. wela, felicitas; ἀρείων, ἄριστος, and see वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवर|कामवरः
काम- + वर काम- + वर, m. choosing what one lists, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तवर
दत्त- + वर दत्त- + वर, adj. 1. one to whom is given the permission to choose a boon, Rām. 1, 1, 22. 2. granted as a boon, ib. 6, 19, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजवर
द्विज- + वर द्विज- + वर, m. a Brāhmaṇa, Kathās. 25, 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकवर
पिक- + वर पिक- + वर, m. an excellent cuckoo (and ascetic), Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवर
पुर- + वर पुर- + वर, n. an excellent town, Rājat. 5, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तवर
प्राप्त- + वर प्राप्त- + वर, adj., f. रा, abounding in blessings, Pañc. 252, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिवर
मुनि- + वर मुनि- + वर, m. the chief of the ascetics, Ṛt. 6, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवर|रघुवरः
रघु- + वर रघु- + वर, m. Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवर
वीर- + वर वीर- + वर, m. a proper name, Lass. 28, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोवर|सरोवरः
सरोवर सरोवर, i. e. सरस्-, m. a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिद्वर
सरित्- + वर सरित्- + वर, f. रा, the Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरट|वरटं|वरटः
वरट वरट,<BR> I. m. A wasp.<BR> II. f. टा, टी, and वरला वरला.<BR> 1. A goose.<BR> 2. A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण|वरणं|वरणः
वरण वरण, i. e. वृ + अन,<BR> I. m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b " target="_blank">Page0815-b + 42</a>]<BR> 1. An enclosure raised on a mound of earth.<BR> 2. A causeway, a bridge.<BR> 3. A camel.<BR> 4. A tree, Capparis trifoliata, Kir. 5, 25.<BR> 5. Any tree.<BR> II. f. The name of a rivulet.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Selecting, choice, Johns. Sel. 53, 127.<BR> 2. Surrounding.<BR> 3. Screening, covering.<BR> 4. Nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्ड|वरंड|वरंडः|वरण्डः
वरण्ड वरण्ड (vb. वृ), m.<BR> 1. A portico.<BR> 2. The string of a fish-hook.<BR> 3. A packet.<BR> 4. A multitude.<BR> 5. A heap of grass.<BR> 6. Pimples on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डक|वरंडक|वरण्डकः
वरण्डक वरण्ड + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Large.<BR> 2. Fearful.<BR> 3. Niggardly.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A canopy on the back of an elephant.<BR> 2. A wall.<BR> 3. A ball.<BR> 4. Pimples on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रा
वरत्रा वरत्रा (vb. वृ), f.<BR> 1. A strap or string of leather, Pañc. 128, 9.<BR> 2. An elephant's or horse's leather girth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरद|वरदः
वरद वर-द,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Conferring a boon, or boons, Chr. 57, 26.<BR> 2. Propitious.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. A girl.<BR> 2. The name of a river, Mālav. d. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रद
वरप्रद वर-प्र-द,<BR> I. adj. Conferring a boon.<BR> II. f. दा, The wife of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितृ
वरयितृ वरयितृ, i. e. वृ, Caus., + तृ, m. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरल|वरलः
वरल वरल, m. A wasp; cf. वरट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराक|वराकः
वराक वराक, i. e. वृ + अक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Poor, Pañc. 108, 13.<BR> 2. Low, vile, impure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 429; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 2; Pañc. 81, 18.<BR> 3. Unhappy, Pañc. 41, 5.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराट|वराटः
वराट वराट, m.<BR> 1. (akin to वरत्रा, probably a dialect. form of it), A cord.<BR> 2. The small shell, called (कपर्द) cowrie, and used as a coin, Pañc. i. d. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटक|वराटकः
वराटक वराट + क, m. f. तिका (and n.),<BR> 1. A rope.<BR> 2. The small shell, called cowrie, and used as a coin, Pañc. 135, 7.<BR> 3. The seed vessel of the lotus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवराटक|किंवराटकः
किम्- + वराटक किम्- + वराटक, adj. despising a cowrie (a farthing), Hit. ii. d. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराण|वराणः
वराण वराण (a ptcple. Ātm. of वृ), m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारक|वरारकं
वरारक वरारक, n. A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराह|वराहः
वराह वराह, m.<BR> 1. A hog, Pañc. 120, 14.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu, who assumed in his third अवतार, or descent, the shape of a boar, Utt. Rāmac. 132, 6.<BR> 3. A form of marching an army, Man. 7, 187.<BR> 4. A mountain.<BR> 5. A sort of measure.<BR> 6. One of the smaller द्वीपस्, or divisions of the world.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. verres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावराह|महावराहः
महा- + वराह महा- + वराह and यज्ञ-, m. Viṣṇu, Johns. Sel. 94, 55 (यज्ञ-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहु|वराहुः
वराहु वराहु, m. A hog, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 88, 5.<BR> --Cf. वराह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिमन्
वरिमन् वरिमन्, i. e. उरु + इमन् (cf. the comparat. of उरु, वरीयंस्), m. Extent, greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्य
वरिवस्य वरिवस्य, denomin. derived from the vedic noun वरिवस् with य, Par. To adore, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्या
वरिवस्या वरिवस्या, i. e. वरिवस्य + आ, f. Worship, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष|वरिषं
वरिष वरिष (for वर्ष), m. n. A year, Lass. 2. ed. 54, 55 (? hypothet. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ वरिष्ठ, and वरीयंस् वरीयंस्, see उरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवर्द|वरीवर्दः|वरीवर्द्द|वरीवर्द्दः
वरीवर्द वरीवर्द = बलीवर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीषु|वरीषुः
वरीषु वरीषु (vb. वृ), m. Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण|वरुणः
वरुण वरुण, i. e. वृ + उन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. In the Veda, the deity of the heavens, Chr. 289, 6 = Rigv. i. 54, 6; in the later [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b " target="_blank">Page0816-b + 42</a>] time, of the waters (originally those of the atmosphere), Rām. 3, 54, 9; the lord of punishment, Man. 9, 245; sovereign of the western quarter, Śiś. 9, 7.<BR> 2. A name of the sun.<BR> 3. Water, or the ocean.<BR> II. f. वरुणानी, The wife of Varuṇa.<BR> --Cf. Οὐρανος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्र|वरुत्रं
वरुत्र वरुत्र, i. e. वृ + त्र, n. An upper garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ|वरूथं|वरूथः
वरूथ वरूथ (vb. वृ),<BR> I. m. A wooden fender round a carriage, to protect it from collision.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Armour.<BR> 2. Leather skin.<BR> 3. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिन्
वरूथिन् वरूथिन्, i. e. वरूथ + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Protected by fenders (cf. the last), Ragh. 9, 11.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. An army, Chr. 54, 14.<BR> 2. The name of an Apsaras, Indr. 2, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य वरेण्य (properly an anomal. ptcple. of the fut. pass. of वृ), adj. Superior, excellent, Lass. 99, 11 = Rigv. iii. 62, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोल|वरोलः
वरोल वरोल, m. A wasp (cf. वरल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कर|वर्करः
वर्कर वर्कर, m.<BR> 1. Any young animal.<BR> 2. A lamb.<BR> 3. A goat.<BR> 4. Sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कराट|वर्कराटः
वर्कराट वर्कराट, m.<BR> 1. A side glance.<BR> 2. The marks of a lover's finger-nails on the bosom of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग|वर्गः|वर्ग्ग
वर्ग वर्ग, i. e. वृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A class (a multitude of similar things), Pañc. 33, 14.<BR> 2. A troop, Pañc. 192, 23.<BR> 3. A chapter.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. vulgus (or = व्रज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवर्ग
आप्त- + वर्ग आप्त- + वर्ग, m. friends, Mālav. 67, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वर्ग|चतुर्वर्गः|चतुर्व्वर्गः
चतुर्- + वर्ग चतुर्- + वर्ग, m. 1. any assemblage of four things, Hit. i. d. 8, M.M. 2. the four objects of human pursuit, viz. wealth, pleasure, virtue, and final beatitude, Rāgh. 10, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्ग|त्रिवर्गः
त्रि- + वर्ग त्रि- + वर्ग, m. any assemblage of three things, e. g. wealth, pleasure, and virtue, Man. 2, 224; Daśak. in Chr. 181, 21; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a " target="_blank">Page0817-a + 42</a>] the three qualities of nature; viz. सत्य, truth; रजस्, passion; and तमस्, darkness; three conditions of a king, loss, gain, equality, MBh. 12, 2664; the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासवर्ग
दास- + वर्ग दास- + वर्ग, m. all the servants, Man. 3, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रवर्ग
पात्र- + वर्ग पात्र- + वर्ग, m. a troop of actors, Vikr. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुवर्ग|बंधुवर्ग|बन्धुवर्गः
बन्धु- + वर्ग बन्धु- + वर्ग, m. relations, Pañc. i. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवर्ग|भृत्यवर्गः
भृत्य- + वर्ग भृत्य- + वर्ग m. servants, ib. (cf. my transl. and Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2542).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिवर्ग|रक्षिवर्गः
रक्षि(न्)- + वर्ग रक्षि(न्)- + वर्ग, m. a sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीण
ऽवर्गीण -वर्गीण, in मद्-वर्ग + ईन, adj. Connected with, or related to, me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीय|वर्गीयः
ऽवर्गीय -वर्गीय, in स्व-, adj. Belonging to (thy) own fraction, Pañc. 212, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग्य|वर्ग्यः
वर्ग्य वर्ग्य, i. e. वर्ग + य, adj. Belonging to a class, Mālat. 4, 6 (a mime).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्|वर्च्च्
† वर्च् वर्च्, i. 1, Ātm. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्|वर्च्चस्
वर्चस् वर्चस्,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Lustre, Rām. 3, 49, 4.<BR> 2. Form, MBh. 1, 1076; Lass. 2. ed. 79, 80.<BR> 3. Excrements.<BR> II. m. The son of Candra.<BR> --Cf. ब्रह्मवर्चस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्क|वर्चस्कः|वर्च्चस्क|वर्च्चस्कः
वर्चस्क वर्चस् + क, m. and n. Ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्विन्|वर्च्चस्विन्
वर्चस्विन् वर्चस् + विन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Bright, Nal. 12, 66.<BR> II. m. The moon.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्चस्विन्|ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्विन्
ब्रह्मन्- + वर्चस्विन् ब्रह्मन्- + वर्चस्विन्, i. e. ब्रह्मवर्चस् + विन्, adj. illumined by the Vedas, Man. 3, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चित
वर्चित वर्चित, Pañc. 3, 10, read चर्चित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्जः|वर्ज्ज
वर्ज वर्ज, i. e. वृज् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Devoid of.<BR> 2. Excepted.<BR> II. ˚जम्, adv. Except, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 10.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Leaving.<BR> 2. Excepting.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृचवर्ज
तृच- + वर्ज तृच- + वर्ज, adj. except three verses, Chr. 294, 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वद्वर्जम्
त्वद्-वर्ज + म् त्वद्-वर्ज + म्, adv. except you, Pañc. 28, 22 (cf. my transl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ववर्जम्
पर्ववर्ज + म् पर्ववर्ज + म्, i. e. पर्वन्-, adj. except the forbidden days of the month, Man. 3, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जन|वर्जनं|वर्ज्जन|वर्ज्जनं
वर्जन वर्जन, i. e. वृज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Abandoning, leaving, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 11.<BR> 2. Desertion, Man. 5, 4.<BR> 3. Avoiding, Man. 5, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्
वर्ण् वर्ण्, 1, 10 (rather a denomin. derived from वर्ण), Par.<BR> 1. To colour, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13.<BR> 2. To depict, to describe, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 145; to explain, Vedāntas. 207, 23.<BR> 3. To praise, MBh. 2, 1226.<BR> 4. † To illuminate.<BR> 5. † To exert one's self.<BR> 6. † To throw, or to grind.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To expose, MBh. 4, 107.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. The same, MBh. 3, 8732.<BR> 2. To tell, Hit. 27, 8.<BR> --With नि नि, To regard, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 12 (probably to be changed to निर्वर्ण्य).<BR> --With निस् निस्, To regard, Śāk. 33, 13; to examine, Vikr. 10, 3.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-निर्वर्णनीय, adj. Not to be looked at, Śāk. 64, 8.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To describe, MBh. 4, 106.<BR> 2. To extol, MBh. 4, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्णः|वर्ण्ण
वर्ण वर्ण, i. e. वृ + न,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Colour, Hit. iii. d. 33.<BR> 2. Staining the body with coloured unguents.<BR> 3. Coloured cloth thrown over the back of an elephant.<BR> 4. Gold.<BR> 5. Beauty.<BR> 6. Theatrical dress or embellishment.<BR> 7. Quality, property.<BR> 8. Fame.<BR> 9. Praise.<BR> 10. A musical mode, Pañc. v. d. 44.<BR> 11. The arrangement of a poem.<BR> 12. A caste, Man. 1, 91; Hit. pr. 46, M.M. (हीन-, adj. One of a low caste); caste and colour at once, Rājat. 5, 377; class, tribe, kind.<BR> 13. Religious observance.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Perfume for the person.<BR> 2. Form, figure.<BR> 3. Sort, kind.<BR> 4. A letter of the alphabet, Bhāṣāp. 163; Vikr. 78, 10.<BR> 5. A syllable, Śrut. 19.<BR> 6. The purity of gold, as ascertained by its streak on the touch-stone.<BR> III. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-a " target="_blank">Page0818-a + 47</a>] n. Saffron.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अ- + वर्ण अ- + वर्ण, m. reproach, blame, Ragh. 14, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्ण|अग्निवर्ण्ण
अग्नि- + वर्ण अग्नि- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. 1. fire-coloured, Rām. 3, 58, 35. 2. boiling hot, Man. 11, 91.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Hariv. 828.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्ण|एकवर्णः
एक- + वर्ण एक- + वर्ण, adj. 1. onecoloured, plain, MBh. 13, 3781. 2. identical, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 29. 3. consisting in one caste only, MBh. 3, 13051.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवर्ण|ज्येष्ठवर्णः
ज्येष्ठ- + वर्ण ज्येष्ठ- + वर्ण, m. a Brāhmaṇa, MBh. 13, 6571.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्ण|दुर्वर्णः|दुर्व्वर्ण|दुर्व्वर्णं
दुर्वर्ण दुर्वर्ण, i. e. दुस्-,<BR> I. adj. of a bad colour, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 45.<BR> II. n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रवर्ण|धूम्रवर्णः
धूम्र- + वर्ण धूम्र- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. grey-coloured, Rām. 4, 39, 28.<BR> II. m. 1. the name of a mountain, Hariv. 12856. 2. a proper name, ib. 1799.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्ण
भिन्न- + वर्ण भिन्न- + वर्ण, adj. discoloured, pale, Megh. 82; cf. Pañc. i. d. 212 (भिन्न-स्वर-मुख-वर्ण, speechless and pale, or, ‘with altered accents and complexion’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवर्ण
मधु- + वर्ण मधु- + वर्ण, adj. sweet, like honey, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 87, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवर्ण
मेघ- + वर्ण मेघ- + वर्ण, adj. cloud-coloured, Indr. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हवर्ण|यथार्हवर्णः
यथार्ह- + वर्ण यथार्ह- + वर्ण, i. e. यथा-अर्ह-, m. a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धवर्ण|लब्धवर्णः
लब्ध- + वर्ण लब्ध- + वर्ण, adj. learned, Ragh. 11, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
वि- + वर्ण वि- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. 1. wanting colour, pale, Nal. 2, 2. 2. bad-coloured. 3. changing colour. 4. low.<BR> II. m. a man of a low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
स- + वर्ण स- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. 1. like, resembling, Megh. 18. 2. of the same caste, kind, MBh. 2, 865.<BR> II. f. णा, Chāyā, the wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्ण|समवर्णः
सम- + वर्ण सम- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. of the same colour, caste, etc.<BR> II. m. community of caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्ण|सुवर्णं|सुवर्णः|सुवर्ण्ण
सु- + वर्ण सु- + वर्ण,<BR> I. adj. 1. of a good colour. 2. brilliant. 3. of a good tribe.<BR> II. n. 1. gold, Pañc. 191, 25. 2. wealth.<BR> III. m. and n. a weight of gold equal to sixteen Māṣas, i. e. about seventy-five grains Troy, Man. 8, 134; a sort of coin, Pañc. 134, 3.<BR> IV. m. 1. a sort of sacrifice. 2. a tree, Cassia fistula.<BR> V. f. णा, the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवर्ण
हिरण्य- + वर्ण हिरण्य- + वर्ण, f. णा, a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक|वर्णकं|वर्णकः|वर्ण्णक
वर्णक वर्ण + क,<BR> I. A substitute for वर्ण, at the end of comp. adj., Daśak. in Chr. 184, 8 (कृपण-, Of a miserable complexion).<BR> II. m., and f. का, A paint, as indigo, orpiment, etc., Bhaṭṭ. 19, 16.<BR> III. m. and n.<BR> 1. Perfume [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b " target="_blank">Page0818-b + 43</a>] for the person.<BR> 2. Sandal.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. A panegyrist.<BR> 2. A circle.<BR> V. f. का, Touch or purity of gold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्णक|त्रिवर्णकं
त्रि- + वर्णक त्रि- + वर्णक, n. the three myrobalans, Suśr. 1, 161, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णन|वर्णनं
वर्णन वर्ण् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Colouring.<BR> 2. Describing, description, Chr. 235, 1. 2; Daśak. in Chr. 185, 22; tale, Pañc. 187, 14.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. Describing, description, Vikr. 19, 9 (प्रति-अवयव-, A detailed description, limb for limb).<BR> 2. Praise, Lass. 2. ed. 81, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाट|वर्णाटः
वर्णाट वर्णाट, m.<BR> 1. A painter.<BR> 2. A singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिक|वर्णिकः
वर्णिक वर्णिक, i. e. वर्ण + इक,<BR> I. m. A scribe.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. A pen.<BR> 2. Ink.<BR> 3. Colour, Śāk. d. 142, v. r.<BR> 4. Attire, Prab. 3, 18, Mālat. 4, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिन्
वर्णिन् वर्णिन्,<BR> I. adj., i. e. वर्ण + इन्, f. नी, Belonging to a caste or tribe.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A painter.<BR> 2. A scribe.<BR> 3. A religious student, Ragh. 5, 19.<BR> 4. A man of either of the four castes.<BR> III. f. नी.<BR> 1. A woman.<BR> 2. Turmeric.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवर्णिनी
वर-वर्णिनी वर-वर्णिनी, f. 1. an excellent woman, Rām. 3, 53, 30. 2. a virtuous woman, Chr. 47, 39. 3. Gaurī. 4. Lakṣmī. 5. Sarasvatī. 6. turmeric. 7. lac. 8. a yellow pigment = रोचना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तक|वर्तकः|वर्त्तक|वर्त्तकं|वर्त्तकः
वर्तक वर्तक, i. e. वृत् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who is, or exists, or abides.<BR> II. m., and f. तका and तिका (Chr. 298, 6 = Rigv. i. 112, 6), A quail, Hit. iii. d. 22; Mālat. 135, 8.<BR> III. m. A horse's hoof.<BR> IV. n. A sort of mixed metal.<BR> --Cf. वर्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तजन्मन्|वर्त्तजन्मन्
वर्तजन्मन् वर्तजन्मन्, i. e. वृत् + अ-जन्मन्, m. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तन|वर्तनः|वर्त्तन|वर्त्तनं|वर्त्तनः
वर्तन वर्तन, i. e. वृत् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Staying.<BR> II. m. A dwarf.<BR> III. f. नी, and n.<BR> 1. Staying, abiding, Utt. Rāmac. 17, 2.<BR> 2. A road.<BR> 3. Grinding.<BR> 4. A ball.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Turning.<BR> 2. A ball of cotton from which the threads are spun.<BR> 3. Occupation, Pañc. i. d. 12. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a " target="_blank">Page0819-a + 45</a>]<BR> 4. Livelihood, Hit. 114, 2.<BR> 5. Appointing, being appointed, Hit. 98, 8.<BR> 6. Wages, Hit. i. d. 45, M.M.<BR> 7. A soldier's pay, Hit. 98, 10; 99, 18.<BR> 8. Colouring, Kir. 10, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तनि|वर्तनिः|वर्त्तनि|वर्त्तनिः
वर्तनि and नी वर्तनी̆, i. e. वृत् + अन + ई, f. A road, Chr. 298, 18 = Rigv. i. 112, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ति|वर्तिः|वर्त्ति|वर्त्तिः
वर्ति and वर्ती वर्ती̆ (vb. वृत्), f.<BR> 1. Perfume for the person.<BR> 2. The wick of a lamp, Bhāg. P. 5, 11, 8 (ति).<BR> 3. A line, a ruled line.<BR> 4. A magic ball, Pañc. 241, 2 (ति), sqq.(?).<BR> 5. The ends of a cloth.<BR> 6. A sort of collyrium, Mālat. 14, 14; Utt. Rāmac. 24, 12 (अमृत-वर्ति, consisting of nectar).<BR> 7. A bougie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिका|वर्त्तिका
वर्तिका वर्ति + का, f.<BR> 1. The wick of a lamp.<BR> 2. Colour, Śāk. d. 142(?).<BR> 3. A pencil, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 13; Ragh. 19, 19; Mālat. 21, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. वर्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवर्तिका|योगवर्त्तिका
योग- + वर्तिका योग- + वर्तिका, f. a magic lamp (see वर्ति), Daśak. in Chr. 186, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिन्|वर्त्तिन्
वर्तिन् वर्तिन्, i. e. वृत् + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Abiding, resting, Pañc. i. d. 224.<BR> 2. Being, Hit. 65, 5, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्रवर्तिन्|उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्
उच्छास्त्र- + वर्तिन् उच्छास्त्र- + वर्तिन्, i. e. उद्-शास्त्र-, adj. one who transgresses the sacred precepts, Man. 4, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गवर्तिन्
उन्मार्ग- + वर्तिन् उन्मार्ग- + वर्तिन्, i. e. उद्-मार्ग-, adj. following evil courses, Rājat. 5, 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवर्तिन्
गुण- + वर्तिन् गुण- + वर्तिन्, adj. pursuing the path of virtue, Rām. 2, 82, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवर्तिन्|गुरुवर्त्तिन्
गुरु- + वर्तिन् गुरु- + वर्तिन्, adj. one who behaves respectfully towards his parents and spiritual teacher, ib. 4, 35, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्तिन्|चक्रवर्त्तिन्
चक्र- + वर्तिन् चक्र- + वर्तिन्, m., f. इनी, 1. a sovereign of the world, MBh. 12, 808. 2. a sovereign, Kathās. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवर्तिन्
दूर- + वर्तिन् दूर- + वर्तिन्, adj. being afar, Megh. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूरवर्तिन्
अति-दूर- + वर्तिन् अति-दूर- + वर्तिन्, adj. being far over, surpassing, Śāk. 146, 8, Chezy. न्याय-, adj. well-behaving, Pañc. i. d. 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्ववर्तिन्
पार्श्व- + वर्तिन् पार्श्व- + वर्तिन्, adj. being at the side, Ragh. 19, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवर्तिन्
पुरोवर्तिन् पुरोवर्तिन्, i. e. पुरस्-, adj. being before one's eyes, in one's presence, Vikr. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलवर्तिन्
प्रतिकूल- + वर्तिन् प्रतिकूल- + वर्तिन्, adj. troubling, Kumāras. 3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशवर्तिन्|वशवर्त्तिन्
वश- + वर्तिन् वश- + वर्तिन्, adj. acting according [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b " target="_blank">Page0819-b + 41</a>] to another's will, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्तिन्|समवर्त्तिन्
सम- + वर्तिन् सम- + वर्तिन्, m. Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवर्तिन्|हस्तवर्त्तिन्
हस्त- + वर्तिन् हस्त- + वर्तिन्, adj. being in one's hand, Hit. iii. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णुः
वर्तिष्णु वर्तिष्णु, i. e. वृत् + इष्णु, adj.<BR> 1. Abiding, being fixed.<BR> 2. Facing an enemy, standing firm in battle.<BR> 3. A circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तिस्
वर्तिस् वर्तिस्, i. e. वृत् + इस्, n. A house, Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्तुल|वर्तुलः|वर्त्तुल|वर्त्तुलं|वर्त्तुलः
वर्तुल वर्तुल (vb. वृत्),<BR> I. adj. Round, circular, Lass. 5, 10.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ball.<BR> 2. A pea.<BR> III. f. ला, A ball at the end of a spindle to assist its rotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मन्
वर्त्मन् वर्त्मन्, i. e. वृत् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. A road, Vikr. 13, 20; way, Hit. i. d. 197, M.M. (पङ्क-, A swamp-way).<BR> 2. An eyelid.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवर्त्मन्
आकाश- + वर्त्मन् आकाश- + वर्त्मन्, n. a way through the air, Hit. 111, 8 (instr. through the air).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवर्त्मन्
कृष्ण- + वर्त्मन् कृष्ण- + वर्त्मन्, m. fire, Man. 2, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवर्त्मन्
घन- + वर्त्मन् घन- + वर्त्मन्, n., नभस्-, n. the sky, Kir. 5, 17; 4, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवर्त्मन्
राजवर्त्मन् राजवर्त्मन्, i. e. राजन्-, n. a royal or main road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध्र
वर्द्ध्र वर्द्ध्र (also वर्ध्र वर्ध्र, Pāṇ. iv. 3, 151),<BR> I. n., and f. री, A leathern thong for securing a saddle.<BR> II. n. Leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्
वर्ध् वर्ध्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. † To cut.<BR> 2. To fill (rather Caus. of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध|वर्द्धं|वर्द्धः|वर्धः
वर्ध वर्ध,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. i. e. वृध् + अ, Increase.<BR> 2. Cutting.<BR> II. n. Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धक|वर्द्धकः|वर्धकः
वर्धक वर्धक (Rām. 1, 12, 7), and वर्धकि वर्धकि (Rām. 2, 63, 2, ed. Seramp.), m. A carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धन|वर्द्धनं|वर्द्धनः|वर्धनः
वर्धन वर्धन, i. e.<BR> A. वृध् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Growing, increasing.<BR> 2. Causing to increase, Nal. 3, 20.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Growing, increasing.<BR> 2. Causing to increase, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 19; Hit. ii. d. 58.<BR> 3. Making powerful, Hit. iii. d. 3.<BR> 4. Elevation, ii. d. 132.<BR> B. n. Cutting.<BR> C. f. नी.<BR> 1. A small water-jar. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a " target="_blank">Page0820-a + 43</a>]<BR> 2. A brush.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलवर्धन
कमल- + वर्धन कमल- + वर्धन, m. the name of a king, Rājat. 5, 446.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलवर्धन
कुल- + वर्धन कुल- + वर्धन, adj. propagating a family, Rām. 1, 15, 46 (Brāhmaṇav. read ˚धनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवर्धन|नन्दिवर्द्धनः|नंदिवर्धन|नन्दिवर्धनः
नन्दि- + वर्धन नन्दि- + वर्धन,<BR> I. adj. causing joy, MBh. 5, 2937.<BR> II. m. 1. a son, Rām. 6, 112, 4. 2. a proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवर्धन
नाभि- + वर्धन नाभि- + वर्धन, n. the section of the navelstring, Man. 2, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यवर्धन
पुण्य- + वर्धन पुण्य- + वर्धन, n. the name of a town, Lass. 21, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुवर्धन
मेरु- + वर्धन मेरु- + वर्धन, m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 366.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवर्धन
रत्न- + वर्धन रत्न- + वर्धन, शंकर-, शम्बु-, m. proper names, Rājat. 5, 40; 268; 300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवर्धन|वंशवर्धनः
वंश- + वर्धन वंश- + वर्धन, m. one by whom his race prospers, Vikr. 87, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षवर्धन
वर्ष- + वर्धन वर्ष- + वर्धन, n. increase of years, or causing increase of years(?), Utt. Rāmac. 85, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धमानक|वर्द्धमानकः|वर्धमानकः
वर्धमानक वर्धमान + क (vb. वृध्), m. A lid, a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धापन|वर्द्धापनं|वर्धापनं
वर्धापन वर्धापन, n.<BR> 1. Cutting, dividing.<BR> 2. i. e. वर्धापय (anomal. Caus. of वृध्), + अन; also ˚नक ˚न + क, A festival on a birthday, Lass. ed. 18, 8; Pañc. ed. orn. 49, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धिन्
वर्धिन् वर्धिन्, i. e. वृध् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Growing, increasing.<BR> 2. Augmenting, Utt. Rāmac. 170, 7; Chr. 51, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्धिष्णु|वर्द्धिष्णुः
वर्धिष्णु वर्धिष्णु, i. e. वृध् + इष्णु, adj.<BR> 1. Growing, increasing.<BR> 2. Enlarging, expanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्पस्
वर्पस् वर्पस्, n. Form, figure.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरवर्पस्
घोर- + वर्पस् घोर- + वर्पस्, adj. having a terrible figure, Chr. 292, 2 = Rigv. i. 64, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मन्|वर्म्मन्
वर्मन् वर्मन्, i. e. वृ + मन्, n. Armour, mail, Rājat. 5, 195.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मन्|वर्म्मन्
वर्मन् वर्मन् may be added after all Kṣatriya names, Colebr. Essays, i. 278; e. g. अपहार-, अवन्ति-, कृत-, गो-पाल-, चक्र-, चण्ड-, चन्द्र-, m. proper names, Daśak. i. in Chr. 179, 3; Rājat. 5, 2; MBh. 1, 562; Rājat. 5, 181; 287; Daśak. in Chr. 200, 23; MBh. 1, 2668.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवर्मन्|धर्म्मवर्म्मन्
धर्म- + वर्मन् धर्म- + वर्मन्, n. the armour or protection of the law, epithet of Kṛṣṇa, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b " target="_blank">Page0820-b + 42</a>] Bhāg. P. 1, 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जितवर्मन्
निर्जित- + वर्मन् निर्जित- + वर्मन्, i. e. निस्-जित, शंकर-, शूर-, m. proper names, Rājat. 5, 251; 128; 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्मित|वर्म्मित|वर्म्मितः
वर्मित वर्मित, i. e. वर्मन् + इत, and वर्मिन् वर्मिन्, i. e. वर्मन् + इन् (MBh. 1, 7765), adj. Armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वर|वर्वरः|वर्व्वर|वर्व्वरं|वर्व्वरः
वर्वर वर्वर,<BR> I. (probably borrowed from βάρϐαρος, cf. बर्बर), m.<BR> 1. A barbarian, an outcaste.<BR> 2. The country inhabited by barbarians.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Woolly or curly hair.<BR> 2. A sort of worm.<BR> 3. The clash of weapons.<BR> 4. A mode of dancing.<BR> III. f. रा and रि, A small bee.<BR> IV. n. Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्वरीक|वर्वरीकः|वर्व्वरीक|वर्व्वरीकः
वर्वरीक वर्वरीक, i. e. वर्वर + ईक, m.<BR> 1. Curly or woolly hair.<BR> 2. A name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्
वर्ष् वर्ष्, see पर्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष वर्ष, i. e. वृष् + अ,<BR> I. adj. at the end of a comp. Raining, Hit. ii. d. 147.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Rain, Megh. 36; figurat., Chr. 39, 3 (a shower of arrows).<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> 3. A year, Rām. 3, 53, 10 (n.); Pañc. 159, 14 (n.).<BR> 4. A division of the known continent, of which there are reckoned nine, Bhāg. P. 8, 9, 22.<BR> 5. India, also called भारत-,<BR> II. f. षा.<BR> 1. pl. The rainy season, Man. 3, 173; Hit. 80, 15.<BR> 2. A sort of gramineous plant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ष|अवर्षः
अ- + वर्ष अ- + वर्ष, m. drought, Rām. 3, 35, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवर्ष
अष्टवर्ष अष्टवर्ष, i. e. अष्टन्-, adj. eight years old, Man. 9, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोवर्ष
तिरोवर्ष तिरोवर्ष, i. e. तिरस्-, adj. protected against rain, MBh. 4, 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशवर्ष
द्वादशवर्ष द्वादशवर्ष, i. e. द्वादशन्-, n. pl. twelve years, Pañc. i. d. 238 (perhaps two words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ष|प्रवर्षः
प्र- + वर्ष प्र- + वर्ष, m. raining fast, Pañc. 93, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवर्ष|शरवर्षः
शर- + वर्ष शर- + वर्ष, m. a shower of arrows, Chr. 4, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षकर|वर्षकरः
वर्षकर वर्ष-कर,<BR> I. adj. Producing rain.<BR> II. m. A cloud.<BR> III. f. री, A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षण|वर्षणं
वर्षण वर्षण, i. e. वृष् + अन, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a " target="_blank">Page0821-a + 40</a>] Raining.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षण|अवर्षणं
अ- + वर्षण अ- + वर्षण, m. drought, Lass. 27, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षधर|वर्षधरः
वर्षधर वर्ष-धर, m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. An eunuch, Pañc. 43, 5; 53, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षवर|वर्षवरः
वर्षवर वर्ष-वर, m. An eunuch, Mālat. 16, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाभू
वर्षाभू वर्षा-भू (see वर्ष),<BR> I. m. A frog.<BR> II. f. भू and भ्वी.<BR> 1. A she-frog.<BR> 2. Hog-weed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिक
वर्षिक वर्षिक, i. e. वर्ष + इक, adj. Raining, rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिन्
वर्षिन् वर्षिन्, i. e. वृष्, and वर्ष, + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Raining, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1183.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रवर्षिन्
अ-पात्र- + वर्षिन् अ-पात्र- + वर्षिन्, adj. raining n (i. e. giving presents to) unworthy persons, Hit. iii. d. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टवर्षिन्
अभीष्ट- + वर्षिन् अभीष्ट- + वर्षिन्, i. e. अभि-इष्ट-वर्ष + इन्, adj. yielding the wished-for rain, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1915.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवर्षिन्
चित्र- + वर्षिन् चित्र- + वर्षिन्, adj. raining in an extraordinary manner, Hariv. 11145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिवर्षिन्
षष्टि- + वर्षिन् षष्टि- + वर्षिन्, adj. sixty years old, Hiḍ. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिष्ठ|वर्षिष्ठः
वर्षिष्ठ वर्षिष्ठ (superl. of वृद्ध),<BR> 1. Oldest.<BR> 2. Very abundant, Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 88, 1. वर्षीयंस् वर्षीयंस् (its comparat.), Very aged, old, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 4 (properly from वर्ष + वन्त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुक|वर्षुकः
वर्षुक वर्षुक (vb. वृष्), adj. Rainy, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षेज|वर्षेजः
वर्षेज वर्षेज, i. e. वर्ष + इ-ज, adj. Produced in the rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्मन्
वर्ष्मन् वर्ष्मन्, n.<BR> 1. The body, Johns. Sel. 94, 54; Hiḍ. 2, 7 (at the end of a comp. adj. Having the body of a mass of clouds, i. e. as black as a big cloud).<BR> 2. Height.<BR> 3. A measure, largeness, Ragh. 4, 76; MBh. 1, 1443.<BR> 4. A handsome form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह्
वर्ह् वर्ह्, बर्ह् बर्ह्, i. 1, Ātm. To be pre-eminent.<BR> --i. 10, To hurt, to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b " target="_blank">Page0821-b + 39</a>] kill.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, i. 10, To destroy, Śiś. 1, 29; cf. बर्ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह|वर्हं
वर्ह वर्ह, see बर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हण|वर्हणं
वर्हण वर्हण, n. A leaf (cf. बर्ह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिण|वर्हिणः
वर्हिण वर्हिण, see बर्हिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिन्
वर्हिन् वर्हिन्, see बर्हिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिषद्
वर्हिषद् वर्हिषद्, वर्हिस् वर्हिस्, see बर्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्
वल् वल् (cf. वृ), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To cover.<BR> 2. To be attached to, Nal. 3, 5.<BR> 3. To hasten, Śiś. 6, 38; Gīt. 6, 3.<BR> 4. To move to and fro, Śiś. 6, 11; Vikr. 59, 20.<BR> 5. To increase, Gīt. 1, 26.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वलित.<BR> 1. Surrounded.<BR> 2. Moved, Rājat. 5, 360; 481; moving, Mālat. 16, 9; turned, 16, 19; Amar. 83.<BR> 3. Constrained.<BR> --Caus. To cause to move, Śiś. 6, 3. Cf. s. v.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अन्-अतिवलित, see s. v. वलित.<BR> --With वि वि, विवलित, Turned away, Amar. 44.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संवलित,<BR> 1. Encompassed, Kir. 5, 48.<BR> 2. United, Mālat. 73, 4.<BR> 3. Mixed Kir. 5, 38.<BR> 4. Possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्ष|वलक्षः
वलक्ष वलक्ष = अव-लक्ष, adj. White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलन|वलनं
वलन वल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Turning, Amar. 19.<BR> 2. Agitation, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलन्तिका
वलन्तिका वलन्तिका, f. A musical mode, Vikr. 59, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलभि|वलभिः
वलभि वलभि, see वडभि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलय|वलयं|वलयः
वलय वलय (Caus., or i. 10), + अ (sometimes बलय),<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A bracelet, Pañc. iii. d. 235.<BR> 2. Circle, circumference, Śiś. 9, 8 (दिश्-, The universe).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An enclosure, Ragh. 13, 21.<BR> 2. Inflammation of the larynx.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षसूत्रवलय
अक्ष-सूत्र- + वलय अक्ष-सूत्र- + वलय, n. a rosary, Utt. Rāmac. 106, 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a " target="_blank">Page0822-a + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलय|कुवलयं
कु- + वलय कु- + वलय, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूवलय
भू- + वलय भू- + वलय, m. n. the terrestrial globe, Mārk. P. 20, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखावलय|लेखावलयः
लेखा- + वलय लेखा- + वलय, an encircling line, Vikr. d. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रततिवलय
व्रतति- + वलय व्रतति- + वलय, a creeper winding round like a bracelet, Śāk. d. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयवन्त्|वलयवत्
वलयवन्त् वलय + वन्त्, adj. Endowed with bracelets, Śāk. 32, 14 (लता-, Endowed with bracelets consisting in creepers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयित|वलयितं
वलयित वलयित, i. e. वलय + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Surrounded, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2245.<BR> 2. Whirling, Mālat. 75, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयिन्
वलयिन् वलयिन्, i. e. वलय + इन्, adj. in ज्योतिस्-लेखा-, Endowed with circles formed by resplendent lines, Megh. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाक|वलाकः
वलाक वलाक,<BR> I. m. A crane.<BR> II. f. का (also बलाका, Man. 5, 14).<BR> 1. The female crane, Megh. 9.<BR> 2. A crane in general, Man. 11, 135.<BR> 3. A flight of cranes.<BR> 4. A mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाहक|वलाहकः
वलाहक वलाहक, and वलि वलि, see बलाहक, बलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलित|वलितः
वलित वलित, i. e. वलि or बलि, + इत, adj., f. ता, and वलिभ वलि + भ, adj. Having wrinkles, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 16 (वलिभ).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. वल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिवलित
अन्-अतिवलित अन्-अतिवलित, adj. almost free from wrinkles (cf. Amar. 47, Sch.), Daśak. in Chr. 198, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिश|वलिशं
वलिश वलिश, see वडिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलीक|वलीकं
वलीक वलीक, n. The edge of a roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूक|वलूकं|वलूकः
वलूक वलूक, m.<BR> 1. A bird.<BR> 2. (n.), The root of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क्
† वल्क् वल्क्, i. 10, Par. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क|वल्कं|वल्कः
वल्क वल्क, i. e. वृ + क,<BR> 1. m. n. The bark of a tree, Kir. 1, 35.<BR> 2. n. The scales of a fish.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवल्क|दंतवल्क
दन्त- + वल्क दन्त- + वल्क, n. the enamel of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 305, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कल|वल्कलं|वल्कलः
वल्कल वल्क + ल, m. and n.<BR> 1. The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b " target="_blank">Page0822-b + 38</a>] bark of a tree, Pañc. 188, 13.<BR> 2. A cloth made of bark, Pañc. v. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ग्
वल्ग् वल्ग्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go by leaps, MBh. 3, 16123.<BR> 2. To bounce, Bhartṛ. 3, 73.<BR> 3. To gallop, Rājat. 5, 342.<BR> 4. To move in different ways, Pañc. i. d. 71.<BR> 5. To fluctuate, MBh. 3, 12080.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वल्गित, n.<BR> 1. Running, Lass. 2. ed. 50, 15.<BR> 2. A horse's gallop.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To run to, MBh. 4, 342.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To gallop, Utt. Rāmac. 119, 4.<BR> --With वि वि, To burst asunder, Mṛcch. 85, 15.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संवल्गित, Overrun, resounding, Mālat. 79, 16.<BR> --Cf. वल्गु and perhaps A.S. wlaence, pompa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गा
वल्गा वल्ग् + आ, f. A bridle, Rājat. 5, 343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गु|वल्गुः
वल्गु वल्ग् + उ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Handsome, Pañc. i. d. 202.<BR> 2. Precious, Hit. iii. d. 70.<BR> II. adv. Beautifully, Pañc. i. d. 71.<BR> III. m. A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुक|वल्गुकं
वल्गुक वल्गु + क,<BR> I. adj. Handsome.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Sandal.<BR> 2. A wood.<BR> 3. Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुल|वल्गुलः
वल्गुल वल्गु + ल,<BR> I. m. The flying fox.<BR> II. f. ला, A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुलिका
वल्गुलिका वल्गुलिका, f. A cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भ्
† वल्भ् वल्भ्, i. 1, Ātm. To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भन|वल्भनं
वल्भन वल्भन, n. Eating, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मिक|वल्मिकः
वल्मिक वल्मिक, m., वल्मिकि वल्मिकि, m., and वल्मीक वल्मीक, m. and n., i. e. वल्मी + क, An ant-hill, Man. 4, 46 (मीक); Pañc. 170, 23 (मीक); Śāk. d. 170 (मीक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मी
वल्मी वल्मी (cf. वम्र), f. An ant, Häberl. Anth. 238, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्युल्
वल्युल् and वल्यूल् वल्यू̆ल्, see पल्पूल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल्
† वल्ल् वल्ल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To be covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लकी
वल्लकी वल्लकी, f. The Indian lute, Ṛt. 1, 8; Śiś. 4, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभ|वल्लभः
वल्लभ वल्लभ,<BR> I. adj., f. भा.<BR> 1. Beloved, Pañc. 169, 25; v. d. 8; superl. ˚भतम, dearest, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR> 2. Superintendent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A lover, a favourite, Pañc. 129, 7; Rājat. 5, 380.<BR> 2. The chief herdsman.<BR> 3. A horse with good marks.<BR> III. f. भा, A mistress, Rājat. 5, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेरवल्लभ
कुवेर- + वल्लभ कुवेर- + वल्लभ, m. a proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवल्लभ|श्रीवल्लभः
श्री- + वल्लभ श्री- + वल्लभ, m. a favourite of fortune, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1912.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभता
वल्लभता वल्लभ + ता, f.<BR> 1. Love, Prab. 10, 8.<BR> 2. State of a favourite, Pañc. ii. d. 75.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवल्लभता
अति- + वल्लभता अति- + वल्लभता, f. excessive love, Pañc. 221, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभत्व
वल्लभत्व वल्लभ + त्व, n. Love, Pañc. 228, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरि|वल्लरिः
वल्लरि and री वल्लरी̆, f.<BR> 1. A creeping plant, Pañc. 229, 16 (रि).<BR> 2. A compound pedicle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकवल्लरि
अलक- + वल्लरि अलक- + वल्लरि, f. pl. creeper-like curls, Amar. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवल्लरी
विष-वल्लरी विष-वल्लरी, f. a poisonous creeper, Bhartṛ. 1, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्लरि|सोमवल्लरिः
सोम- + वल्लरि सोम- + वल्लरि, f. the Soma plant, Sarcostema viminalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लव|वल्लवः
वल्लव वल्लव,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A cook.<BR> 2. A herdsman, Nalod. 1, 2.<BR> 3. A name of Bhīmasena.<BR> II. f. वी, A cowherdess, Kir. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लि|वल्लिः
वल्लि f.<BR> I., and वल्ली वल्ली̆, A creeper, Man. 1, 48 (ली); Pañc. 229, 9; Bhartṛ. 3, 23 (ली).<BR> II. वल्लि, The earth.<BR> III. ली, A plant, Ligusticum ajwaen.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्ली
नाग-वल्ली̆ नाग-वल्ली̆, f. the betel plant, Piper betel, Śiś. 9, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्लि
नाग-वल्ली̆ नाग-वल्ली̆, f. the betel plant, Piper betel, Śiś. 9, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यवल्ली|सूर्य्यवल्ली
सूर्य-वल्ली सूर्य-वल्ली, f. a plant, Cleome viscosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीज|वल्लीजं
वल्लीज वल्ली-ज, n. Pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लुर|वल्लुरं
वल्लुर वल्लुर, n.<BR> 1. A thicket, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b " target="_blank">Page0823-b + 44</a>] wood.<BR> 2. An arbour, a bower.<BR> 3. A place overrun with wild grass, an uncultivated field.<BR> 4. A solitude, a wild.<BR> 5. A place destitute of water, a desert.<BR> 6. A field.<BR> 7. A compound pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लूर|वल्लूरं|वल्लूरः
वल्लूर वल्लूर,<BR> I. (m., f. रा, and) n.<BR> 1. Dried flesh, Man. 5, 13.<BR> 2. Hog's flesh.<BR> II. n. (cf. the last).<BR> 1. A thicket.<BR> 2. A field overrun with grass.<BR> 3. A desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्वज|वल्वजः
वल्वज वल्वज, m. A sort of coarse grass, Man. 2, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्श|वल्शः
वल्श वल्श (m. n. ?), A branch, Bhāg. P. 3, 8, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ह्
† वल्ह् वल्ह्, i. 1, Ātm. To be pre-eminent; cf. बल्ह् and वर्ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्
वश् वश्, ii. 2 (वश्मि, उश्वस्), Par. To desire, to will, Śāk. d. 179; Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 86, 10.<BR> --Cf. ἑκών, ἀέκων, ἕκηλος, εὔκηλος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश|वशं|वशः
वश वश् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Willing.<BR> 2. Tamed, overpowered, Pañc. 208, 13.<BR> 3. Subdued by charms, fascinated.<BR> II. m. and n. Wish, desire.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Will, authority, power, Rām. 3, 55, 18; Pañc. 38, 3.<BR> 2. abl. ˚शात्, at the end of a compound word, By means, Pañc. 32, 24; on account of, Vikr. d. 2; Pañc. 33, 6; 148, 10; 264, 23.<BR> 3. Subjection, Pañc. iii. d. 10; 30; वशे कृ, To overpower, Rām. 3, 55, 7; submission, Pañc. iv. d. 60; वशे भू, To be subjected, to obey, Rām. 3, 55, 18.<BR> 4. Birth.<BR> IV. m.<BR> 1. The residence of harlots.<BR> 2. A proper name, Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. i. 112, 10.<BR> V. f. शा.<BR> 1. A wife.<BR> 2. A daughter.<BR> 3. A husband's sister.<BR> 4. A woman.<BR> 5. A cow.<BR> 6. A female elephant, Vikr. d. 110.<BR> 7. A barren cow.<BR> 8. A barren woman, Man. 8, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अ- + वश अ- + वश, adj., f. शा, 1. having no free will, unwilling, against one's wish, Rām. 2, 59, 4; powerless, Hit. iii. d. 133; without being able to resist, Rām. 4, 6, 12; Man. 5, 33. 2. unsubdued, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a " target="_blank">Page0824-a + 44</a>] Hit. i. d. 17, M.M.<BR> 3. disobedient, Hit. ii. d. 173. ˚शम्, adv. necessarily, Hit. ii. d. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशवश
अङ्कुश- + वश अङ्कुश- + वश, adj. obeying the goad of an elephant, Pañc. i. d. 373.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवश|आत्मवशः
आत्मवश आत्मवश, i. e. आत्मन्-,<BR> I. m. subjection to one's self, Hit. ii. d. 54, M.M.<BR> II. adj. independent, Man. 4, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवश|कर्मवशः|कर्म्मवश
कर्मवश कर्मवश, i. e. कर्मन्-, adj. dependent upon the acts performed in former existences, MBh. 13, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधवश
क्रोध- + वश क्रोध- + वश,<BR> I. (m.), the power of wrath, Man. 2, 214.<BR> II. adj. 1. ruled by wrath, Bhāg. P. 5, 24, 29. 2. the name of several bad spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववश|दैववशः
दैव- + वश दैव- + वश, n. will of fate, Pañc. 160, 17; 174, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रावश
निद्रा- + वश निद्रा- + वश (n.), sleep (literally, power of sleep), Pañc. 37, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश|परवशः
पर- + वश पर- + वश, adj. depending on another, Hit. i. d. 201, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रौषधिवश
मन्त्र-ओषधि- + वश मन्त्र-ओषधि- + वश, adj. to be overcome by charms and herbs, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहवश
मोह- + वश मोह- + वश (n.), unconsciousness (literally, power of unconsciousness), Chr. 36, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
वि- + वश वि- + वश, adj., f. शा (deprived of will). 1. subject, subjected, Rām. 3, 55, 51; Hit. i. d. 171, M.M. (even against their will). 2. independent. 3. uncontrolled, unsubdued. 4. apprehensive of death, Bhartṛ. 2, 29. 5. desirous of death, having the soul free from worldly cares, dead, Ragh. 8, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववश
स्व- + वश स्व- + वश, adj. self-controlled, ruled by one's free will, Hiḍ. 4, 4; independent, Vikr. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशंवदत्व
वशंवदत्व वशं-वद-त्व, i. e. वश + म्-वद् + अ + त्व, n. Speaking compliantly, Ragh. 18, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशग
वशग वश + ग,<BR> 1. adj. Obedient, subject, MBh. 3, 14687; Pañc. i. d. 155; 285.<BR> 2. f. गा, An obedient wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशतस्
वशतस् वश + तस्, adv. In consequence, or on account, of the power of, Bhartṛ. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशता
वशता वश + ता, f. Subjection, Cāṇ. 65 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशि|वशिः
वशि वश् + इ, n. Subduing by magical means, bewitching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिक|वशिकः
वशिक वशिक, adj. Empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिता
वशिता वशि + ता, f. वशित्व वशि + त्व, n., or वशिन् + ता, or त्व,<BR> 1. Subduing by magical means, Lass. 3, 19 (त्व).<BR> 2. Subjugation, dominion, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2977.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिन्
वशिन् वशिन्, i. e. वश + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Subdued.<BR> II. m. One who has subdued his senses, a sage, Śāk. d. 47.<BR> III. f. नी.<BR> 1. A tree, Mimosa Sama Roxb.<BR> 2. A parasite plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिर|वशिरं|वशिरः
वशिर वशिर,<BR> I. m. The name of several plants.<BR> II. n. Sea salt (cf. वसुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिष्ठ|वशिष्ठः
वशिष्ठ वशिष्ठ (in the Vedas वसिष्ठ वसिष्ठ, properly superl. of वसु), m. The name of a Ṛṣi, Man. 1, 35; Chr. 296, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 9 (स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकरण|वशीकरणं
वशीकरण वशीकरण, i. e. वश-कृ + अन,<BR> 1. Subduing in general, Pañc. i. d. 80.<BR> 2. Subduing by magical expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्य|वश्यं|वश्यः
वश्य वश्य, i. e. वश + य,<BR> I. adj., f. या.<BR> 1. Governable, able to be subdued, Pañc. iii. d. 128; subdued, Pañc. 156, 10; 23, 3; being in one's power, 146, 24.<BR> 2. Obedient, ib. 46, 20.<BR> II. m. A dependent, a slave.<BR> III. f. या, An obedient wife.<BR> IV. n. Cloves.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यम्
अ-वश्य + म् अ-वश्य + म्, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवश्य
काम- + वश्य काम- + वश्य, adj. subdued by love, MBh. 3, 11590.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यकता
ऽवश्यकता -वश्यकता, in अ-, i. e. अ-वश्य + क + ता, f. Necessity, Hit. 116, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्
† वष् वष्, बष् बष्, i. 1, Par. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्
वषट् वषट् (probably for वक्षत्, ved. conj. aor. of वह्), ind. An exclamation used on making an oblation to a deity with fire; cf. कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कार|वषट्कारः
वषट्कार वषट्-कार, m. Oblation with fire, Hariv. 11187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कृति
वषट्कृति वषट्-कृति, f. Oblation with fire, Lass. 100, 11 = Rigv. vii. 11, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्क्
† वष्क् वष्क्, विष्क् विष्क्, i. 10, Par. To see; see वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्क
वष्क वष्क, वष्कय वष्कय, and वस्कय वस्कय, i. e. 1. वस् + क, and वस् + क + य, m. A one-year-old calf.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vacca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयणी
वष्कयणी वष्कयणी, वस्कयणी वस्कयणी, and वष्कयिणी वष्कयिणी (i. e. वष्कय + इन् + ई; cf. the last), f. A cow bearing many calves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
1. वस् वस्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 48, 21).<BR> 1. To dwell, MBh. 1, 749; sometimes with वासम्, Man. 2, 242; Chr. 60, 30; to dwell with (with the loc.), Nal. 15, 7.<BR> 2. To pass (the night), Rām. 1, 29, 1.<BR> 3. To live, Hit. 127, 11 (अस्मद्-सेवया, as our servant). Pass. imps. उष्य, Pañc. 30, 24 (उष्यताम्, may it be lived).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. उषित.<BR> 1. Dwelt, having dwelt, Chr. 11, 13.<BR> 2. Remaining in or on.<BR> 3. Stale. Anomal. ptcple. of the fut. pass. वास्तव्य, To be dwelt, Pañc. iii. d. 236. m.<BR> 1. An inhabitant, a citizen, Pañc. 48, 25.<BR> 2. A kinsman, a dependent.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. वासय,<BR> 1. To cause to dwell, MBh. 4, 278; to lodge, Hit. 92, 19.<BR> 2. To people, Hit. iii. d. 95.<BR> 3. To receive hospitably, MBh. 3, 982.<BR> 4. To let abide, MBh. 4, 5600. वासित, Well peopled, Hit. iii. d. 95; see s. v.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. वसय, To dwell.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि,<BR> 1. To inhabit, Rām. 1, 34, 46.<BR> 2. To dwell, Utt. Rāmac. 55, 16.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. समयाध्युषित, see s. v.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To dwell with (with acc.), Rām. 2, 37, 26.<BR> 2. To inhabit, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 75. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-b " target="_blank">Page0825-b + 41</a>]<BR> --With अन्तर् अन्तर् (adv.), To dwell in, Śiś. 3, 9.<BR> --With आ आ<BR> 1. To dwell with (with acc.), Rām. 2, 50, 2.<BR> 2. To inhabit, MBh. 3, 8032.<BR> 3. To have an adulterous connection with (acc.), Man. 8, 374.<BR> 4. To dwell, MBh. 3, 2014.<BR> 5. To undergo, to assume, Man. 3, 2.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To receive, Rām. 2, 12, 101.<BR> 2. To inhabit, MBh. 3, 12188.<BR> --With अध्या अधि-आ, To inhabit, MBh. 1, 5512.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To inhabit, Rām. 2, 54, 41.<BR> --Caus. To pitch, Hit. 84, 11, M.M. (समावासित-कटक, adj. Having pitched his camp).<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus. To expel, Pañc. 47, 6.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To inhabit.<BR> 2. To fast, Man. 2, 220. उपोषित,<BR> 1. Fasted.<BR> 2. Who has fasted, Pañc. 199, 12.<BR> 3. Fasting. n. Fast, Man. 5, 155.<BR> --Caus. To cause to fast, to instruct to fast, Rām. 2, 5, 4.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To dwell, Pañc. 160, 23; Man. 2, 24.<BR> 2. To pass (the night), MBh. 4, 276.<BR> --With अधिनि अधि-नि, To dwell near (with acc.), Bhartṛ. 3, 77.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To dwell, MBh. 3, 16777.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To dwell abroad, MBh. 3, 915(?).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To expel, MBh. 2, 2644; Pañc. iii. d. 270.<BR> 2. To banish, Utt. Rāmac. 112, 6.<BR> --With परि परि, पर्युषित,<BR> 1. One who has passed the night, Pañc. 40, 13.<BR> 2. Stale, not fresh, Man. 4, 211; Pañc. ii. d. 102 (of a flower); Häberl. Anthol. 6, 4.<BR> 3. Insipid, Nal. 12, 13; MBh. 3, 2856.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To dwell abroad, Rām. 2, 36, 8.<BR> 2. To order to dwell abroad, Rām. 2, 41, 6. प्रोषित,<BR> 1. Departed, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 11.<BR> 2. Absent, being on a journey, Megh. 49.<BR> --Caus. To send abroad, to banish, Man. 8, 123.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-a " target="_blank">Page0826-a + 39</a>] To dwell abroad, Man. 2, 132. विप्रोषित, Having been abroad, Rām. 2, 103, 26.<BR> --Caus. To banish, Man. 8, 219.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To dwell near, Hit. 110, 2.<BR> 2. To dwell, Pañc. 32, 23.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To dwell, to pass, Rām. 1, 23, 23.<BR> 2. To pass away, Pañc. 130, 7.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To dismiss, MBh. 3, 8277.<BR> 2. To banish, Man. 8, 123.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To dwell, or to live with (with the acc.), Man. 11, 190.<BR> 2. To cohabit (acc.), Man. 9, 77.<BR> --Cf. Goth. visan; A.S. wesan, ed-wist, werig; O.H.G. wesan and werên, wonên; A.S. wunian; Lat. Vesta, vestibulum, verna; ἄστυ, ἀστός, ἑστία, ὑπερ-ῷον, probably εὐνή, ἰαύω, αὐλή, αὖλις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवास्तव्य
ग्राम- + वास्तव्य ग्राम- + वास्तव्य, m. the inhabitant of a village, MBh. 12, 4803. Anomal. absol. उष्य, Rām. 1, 48, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
2. वस् वस् (the original form of उष्, q. cf.), base of the present, उच्छ, i. 6, Par. To shine, Chr. 287, 3 = Rigv. i. 48, 3 (उच्छात्, conj. imperf. and उवास, pf. red.).<BR> --Infin. वस्तवे, ib. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, व्युष्ट, see separately.<BR> --Cf. Goth. uhtvo, see उषस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
3. वस् वस्, ii. 2, Ātm.<BR> 1. To wear, as clothes, Man. 1, 101; 2, 41.<BR> 2. To put on, Man. 4, 116.<BR> --With नि नि, To put on, Nal. 10, 29.<BR> --Caus. To put on, MBh. 3, 2631.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To put on, Rām. 2, 100, 30.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus. To dress, MBh. 2, 2502.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus. To put on, MBh. 2, 2520.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vasjan (to wear), vasti; A.S. werian; Lat. vestis; ἔννυμι, εἷμα (= ved. वस्मन्, Rigv. iv. 13, 4), ἐσθής.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
† 4. वस् वस्, i. 4, Par. To be unbending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
5. वस् वस्, i. 10, वासय, Par. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b " target="_blank">Page0826-b + 42</a>]<BR> 1. † To love.<BR> 2. To cut.<BR> 3. † To take, or to offer, or to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
6. ऽवस् 3. -वस्, adj. Wearing, Ragh. 11, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसति|वसतिः
वसति and ती वसती̆ (vb. 1. वस्), f.<BR> 1. A dwelling-place, Vikr. d. 137 (ति); Pañc. 123, 16 (ति, at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 2. A house, Nalod. 4, 29.<BR> 3. (perhaps vb. 3. वस्), Night, Sāv. 4, 5; figurat., Chr. 48, 4 (ति).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भवसति|गर्भवसतिः
गर्भ-वसति गर्भ-वसति, f. the womb, Hariv. 3312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वसति|दुर्वसतिः
दुर्वसति दुर्वसति, i. e. दुस्-, f. an uneasy dwelling, Ragh. 8, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणवसति
रमण-वसति रमण-वसति, f. the dwelling-place of the lover, Megh. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन|वसनं
वसन 1. 3. वस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A dwelling.<BR> 2. Covering.<BR> 3. Cloth, Vikr. d. 115.<BR> 4. Also f. ना, An ornament worn by women round the loins.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἑανός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन
सु- + वसन सु- + वसन, adj., f. ना, elegantly attired, Johns. Sel. 41, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्त|वसंत|वसंतः|वसन्तः
वसन्त वसन्त, m.<BR> 1. The season of spring, Pañc. v. d. 4; personified, Lass. 2. ed. 51, 26.<BR> 2. Diarrhœa.<BR> 3. Small-pox.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἔαρ; Lat. ver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन्त|सुवसन्तः
सु- + वसन्त सु- + वसन्त, m. the day of full moon in the month Caitra, a festival in honour of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसा
वसा वसा, f.<BR> 1. Marrow, Nalod. 3, 11; brain (-चटा, the mass of the brain), Kathās. 25, 274.<BR> 2. Fat, adeps, Pañc. 253, 23.<BR> 3. Oily exudation, Man. 5, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसि|वसिः
वसि 3. वस् + इ, (m. f. ?), Clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठ|वसिष्ठः
वसिष्ठ वसिष्ठ, m. The name of a Ṛṣi; cf. वशिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु वसु,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Sweet.<BR> 2. Dry.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A kind of demigod, Rām. 3, 52, 42; MBh. 1, 2582.<BR> 2. A name of Agni.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. Kuvera, Kir. 1, 18.<BR> 5. The sun.<BR> 6. A ray of light, Śiś. 9, 10 (at the end of a comp. adj.; cf. 2. वस्).<BR> 7. A rein.<BR> 8. The tie of a yoke.<BR> 9. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a " target="_blank">Page0827-a + 42</a>] tree.<BR> 10. The name of two plants.<BR> 11. A kind of fish.<BR> 12. A proper name, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 21.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Wealth, Lass. 100, 8 = Rigv. vii. 15, 4 (वस्वस्, ved. abl.); Nal. 5, 48; Daśak. in Chr. 184, 14.<BR> 2. Gold, MBh. 3, 13472.<BR> 3. A gem.<BR> 4. Water.<BR> 5. A sort of salt.<BR> 6. A yellow kind of kidney bean.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἐΰς, ἐάων, cf. वस्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसु|पुनर्वसुः|पुनर्व्वसुः
पुनर्- + वसु पुनर्- + वसु, m. 1. the seventh of the lunar asterisms, Ragh. 11, 36. 2. a name of Viṣṇu and Śiva, MBh. 12, 1511.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावसु|पुरावसुः
पुरा- + वसु पुरा- + वसु, m. a name of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रावसु
मित्रावसु मित्रावसु, i. e. मित्र-, m. a proper name, Śāk. 79, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावसु|विभावसुः
विभा- + वसु विभा- + वसु, m. 1. the sun, Lass. 2. ed. 78, 76. 2. the moon, Śṛṅgārat. 2. 3. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुक|वसुकं|वसुकः
वसुक वसु + क,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A tree, Sesbana grandiflora.<BR> 2. A shrub, Asclepias gigantea.<BR> II. n. Sea salt (cf. वशिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवभू
वसुदेवभू वसु-देव-भू, m. Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधा
वसुधा वसु-धा, f. The earth, Vikr. d. 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रवसुधा
क्षेत्र- + वसुधा क्षेत्र- + वसुधा, f. cultivated land, Rām. 3, 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधाधर
वसुधाधर वसुधा-धर, i. e. वसुधा-धृ + अ, m. A mountain, Vikr. d. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधार
वसुधार वसुधार, i. e. वसु-धृ + अ, adj. Having wealth, Hit. ii. d. 102 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2220).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुंधरा|वसुन्धरा
वसुंधरा वसुंधरा, i. e. वसु + म्-धृ + अ, f. The earth, Pañc. 101, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुमन्त्|वसुमत्
वसुमन्त् वसु + मन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. मती, Wealthy, Johns. Sel. 6, 33.<BR> II. f. मती.<BR> 1. The earth, Vikr. d. 79.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूयु
वसूयु वसूयु, i. e. वसूय, a ved. denomin. derived from वसु, + उ, adj. Desiring wealth, Chr. 289, 4 = Rigv. i. 49, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क्
† वस्क् वस्क्, वष्क् वष्क्, वक्क् वक्क्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क|वस्कः
वस्क वस्क, m. Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कय|वस्कयः
वस्कय वस्कय, and वस्कयणी वस्कयणी, see वष्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्
† वस्त् वस्त्, i. 1, Ātm. To torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त|वस्तं|वस्तः
वस्त वस्त,<BR> I. m. A goat, Man. 11, 138.<BR> II. i. e. 1. वस् + त, n. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्ति|वस्तिः
वस्ति वस्ति, m. and f.<BR> 1. The belly below the navel, Man. 8, 234.<BR> 2. The bladder, Suśr. 2, 201, 12.<BR> 3. A bag made of bladder.<BR> 4. Abiding (vb. 1. वस्).<BR> 5. pl. The skirt of a cloth (vb. 3. वस्).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवस्ति|इन्द्रवस्तिः
इन्द्र- + वस्ति इन्द्र- + वस्ति, the calf (of the leg), Suśr. 1, 348, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तु
वस्तु 1. वस् + तु, n.<BR> 1. Natural disposition.<BR> 2. Essence, the true object, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 10; substance, wealth, Lass. 12, 14.<BR> 3. Object, Bhartṛ. 2, 37; thing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 9, Pañc. 253, 19; means, Hit. i. d. 30, M.M.<BR> 4. The object of love, Megh. 111.<BR> 5. The subject of a poem or play, Vikr. 3, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तु
अ- + वस्तु अ- + वस्तु, n. the unreal, the nothing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 9. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीयवस्तु
अ-द्वितीय- + वस्तु अ-द्वितीय- + वस्तु, n. the substance besides which there is nothing else, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथितवस्तु
ग्रथित- + वस्तु ग्रथित- + वस्तु, adj. composed, Vikr. 3, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुतस्
वस्तुतस् वस्तु + तस्, adv. Essentially, in fact, Siddh. Mukt. 76, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुता
वस्तुता वस्तु + ता, in परिहास-, f. Condition of being the object of derision, Pañc. iii. d. 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्य|वस्त्यं
वस्त्य 1. वस् + त्य, or वस्त + य, n. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्र|वस्त्रं
वस्त्र 3. वस् + त्र, n. m. Cloth, garment, Pañc. 29, 10; bed-linen, 62, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वस्त्र
अन्तर्- + वस्त्र अन्तर्- + वस्त्र, n. a lower garment, Kathās. 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्त्र
वि- + वस्त्र वि- + वस्त्र, adj. deprived of clothes, naked, Lass. 14, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानवस्त्र
स्नान- + वस्त्र स्नान- + वस्त्र, n. a bathing cloth, Hit. ii. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्न|वस्नं|वस्नः
वस्न वस्न,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Price.<BR> 2. Wages.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Wealth.<BR> 2. Abiding [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a " target="_blank">Page0828-a + 45</a>] (vb. 1. वस्).<BR> 3. Substance, thing.<BR> 4. Cloth (vb. 3. वस्).<BR> 5. Skin.<BR> --Cf. ὦνος (for ϝόςνος); Lat. venum (acc.), ven-dere. The vb. which is the base of वस्न is probably also the base of वसु (q. cf.), ἐΰ, and ἐσθλός, ἐσλός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्नसा
वस्नसा वस्नसा, i. e. अव-स्नसा, f. A tendon, a nerve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्निक
वस्निक वस्निक, i. e. वस्न + इक, adj., f. की, Living on, or getting, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्वौकसारा
वस्वौकसारा वस्वौकसारा, i. e. probably वसु-ओक-सार, f.<BR> 1. The capital of Kuvera, Ragh. 16, 10.<BR> 2. That of Indra.<BR> 3. The name of a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्
वह् वह्, i. 1, Par. Ātm. (cf. 2. ऊह्).<BR> 1. To draw, Indr. 1, 7.<BR> 2. To carry, Vikr. d. 24.<BR> 3. To bear, MBh. 1, 5888; 8169; Hit. i. d. 78, M.M.; iv. d. 59 (मूर्ध्ना, on one's head, as token of reverence).<BR> 4. To have, Pañc. 218, 5; to feel, Rājat. 5, 11.<BR> 5. To carry away, Man. 8, 189; Lass. 98, 7 = Rigv. v. 9, 1 (ved. वक्षि, ii. 2).<BR> 6. To bring, Rām. 1, 23, 7.<BR> 7. Pass. To ride, MBh. 1, 5337.<BR> 8. To take in matrimony, MBh. 1, 3377.<BR> 9. To spit out, to vomit, Dev. 8, 45 (corr. perhaps वम्, but cf. उद्).<BR> 10. To proceed, to move, MBh. 3, 2786.<BR> 11. To flow, MBh. 3, 2936.<BR> 12. To breathe, Gīt. 5, 2.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ऊढ, Taken in marriage, Chr. 55, 4. f. ढा, A bride, a wife espoused according to the ritual.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. वाह्य, To be carried. m. A beast of burthen, Man. 8, 151. n. A carriage.<BR> --Comp.<BR> राजवाह्य, i. e. राजन्-, m. a royal elephant.<BR> --Caus. वाहय,<BR> 1. To cause to be brought, Ragh. 5, 32 (Calc.).<BR> 2. Ātm. To cause to be conveyed, MBh. 1, 3153.<BR> 3. Ātm. To travel, Rām. 2, 92, 13.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-b " target="_blank">Page0828-b + 43</a>] Pass. To let one's self be employed as a vehicle, Pañc. 199, 4.<BR> 5. To cause to move, to direct, MBh. 4, 1832.<BR> 6. To cause something (a boat) to carry one's self, to ship in a boat, MBh. 1, 4014.<BR> 7. To cause to take in matrimony, MBh. 1, 4287.<BR> 8. To finish, Megh. 39.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वाहित, n. A heavy burden.<BR> --Comp.<BR> प्रेत-, adj. possessed by a spirit.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, Caus.<BR> 1. To pass (as time), Pañc. 185, 25.<BR> 2. To suffer, Ragh. 13, 28 (Calc.).<BR> --With अधि अधि, अध्यूढ, Superseded by another wife, MBh. 2, 2332.<BR> --With अप अप, To carry away, MBh. 1, 2939. अपोढ, Left, Ragh. 11, 25.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be carried away, Rām. 1, 1, 51.<BR> 2. To cause to retreat, to remove, Pañc. 231, 5.<BR> 3. To cause to be driven away, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 24.<BR> 4. To carry away, Rām. 2, 45, 16.<BR> 5. To ride away, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 19.<BR> --With अभि अभि, अभिवाह्य, see s. v.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To bring near, Chr. 288, 9 = Rigv. i. 48, 9; to bring, Man. 9, 5; Vikr. d. 48.<BR> 2. To bring on, to effect, Vikr. d. 128; to produce, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 14.<BR> 3. To come near, Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be brought, MBh. 2, 2770.<BR> --With उदा उद्-आ,<BR> 1. To convey near, MBh. 3, 15704.<BR> 2. To carry away, Chr. 31, 15.<BR> 3. To marry, MBh. 1, 8830.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To bear on, Chr. 289, 1 = Rigv. i. 50, 1.<BR> 2. To lift up, Rām. 3, 55, 9; Pañc. v. d. 24.<BR> 3. To bounce, Pañc. 141, 4.<BR> 4. To bear, Hit. 127, 1; MBh. 1, 4272.<BR> 5. To feel, Mālat. 96, 4.<BR> 6. To show, Vikr. d. 136.<BR> 7. To carry away, Ragh. 7, 32.<BR> 8. To marry, Man. 3, 8.<BR> 9. To spit out, MBh. 3, 16129.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0829-a " target="_blank">Page0829-a + 43</a>] give in matrimony, Pañc. iii. d. 217.<BR> 2. To ask in marriage, Pañc. 261, 5; to marry, Pañc. 181, 5.<BR> 3. To suffer to be expelled, MBh. 1, 3801.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To lift up, MBh. 2, 718.<BR> 2. To marry, Rām. 2, 107, 3.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To convey near, MBh. 2, 2064.<BR> 2. To bring about, MBh. 2, 2051.<BR> 3. To bear, Rām. 2, 87, 23. उपोढ,<BR> 1. Near.<BR> 2. Collected, Śāk. d. 106; much, Vikr. d. 26; Daśak. in Chr. 194, 6.<BR> 3. Married, Rām. 1, 13, 37.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. Caus. उप-वाह्य, m. A king's elephant.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, समुपोढ, Risen, Utt. Rāmac. 131, 14.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To bring, Chr. 297, 19 = Rigv. i. 112, 19.<BR> 2. To support, Gīt. 1, 16.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To extricate one's self, Lass. 45, 3.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To pass away, Pañc. 219, 14.<BR> 2. To fulfil, Hit. 106, 4.<BR> 3. To settle, Kathās. 13, 86.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Par. To draw, Rām. 2, 52, 43. प्रौढ,<BR> 1. Raised, lifted up.<BR> 2. Forward (as the hand to seize anything).<BR> 3. Confident, bold, Rājat. 5, 457.<BR> 4. Arrogant.<BR> 5. Impudent, Lass. 85, 10.<BR> 6. Fullgrown, Śṛṅgārat. 1; full blowing, Megh. 26 (+ त्व, n. Fertility [of imagination], Mālat. 3, 20).<BR> 7. Thick, heavy, dense (darkness, etc.), large, Rājat. 5, 476.<BR> 8. Old.<BR> 9. Married.<BR> 18. Controverted. f. ढा, A woman from thirty years of age to fifty-five.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. not bold, gentle, Rājat. 5, 458.<BR> अति-, adj. full-blown, Hit. 86, 2, M.M.<BR> अन्-अति-, adj. just shot up, Megh. 77.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, To convey successively, MBh. 3, 13305.<BR> --With वि वि, To marry, MBh. 1, 3884. व्यूढ,<BR> 1. Arrayed, Rājat. 5, 260.<BR> 2. Compact.<BR> 3. Large, Nal. 12, 13.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to marry, to grant sexual intercourse, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0829-b " target="_blank">Page0829-b + 45</a>] Pañc. 129, 9.<BR> 2. To marry, Lass. 23, 11. Comp. ptcple. fut. pass. अ-विवाह्य, adj. Not to be married, Pañc. iii. d. 218.<BR> प्रतिज्ञा-, adj., f. या, To be married according to a vow (under a condition), Hit. 63, 19.<BR> --With निर्वि निस्-वि, To expel, MBh. 1, 6257.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To convey, Rām. 1, 67, 4.<BR> 2. To bring near, MBh. 3, 13188.<BR> --Caus. To agitate, Pañc. v. d. 14.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vehere, via, uxor (originally perhaps ‘one who is about to marry,’ a bride, which was perhaps also the original signification of वधू̆), probably bajulus; Goth. ga-vigan; A.S. wegan; Goth. vigs; A.S. weg; O.H.G. wagan; A.S. waegen; ἄχθος, ὄχος, ὀχέω, αὐχήν (cf. वह), ὀχλεύς; also A.S. weddian, To marry; cf. वधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वह्
अन्- + वह् अन्- + वह्, f. ढा, a concubine, Sāh. Darp. 36, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोढा
नवोढा नवोढा, i. e. नव-, f. a newly-married woman, Hit. i. d. 211, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह|वहः
वह वह,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Bearing, conveying.<BR> 2. Any vehicle, as a horse, a car.<BR> 3. The shoulder of an ox.<BR> 4. A road, a way.<BR> 5. Any male river, a current (? Sāv. 4, 31, at the end of a comp. adj. rather, carrying purity, i. e. clear).<BR> 6. Air, wind.<BR> 7. A measure of four द्रोणस्.<BR> II. f. हा, A river in general.<BR> III. Latter part of comp. words; e. g. पुष्प-गन्ध-, adj. Bringing flowers and perfumes, Indr. 2, 9. सर्व-गन्ध-, adj. Conveying all scents, Man. 1, 76. दुर्वह, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. हा, Difficult to be borne, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 4; or carried, MBh. 12, 3047. वार्त्ता-, m. A chandler, a vendor of grain, oil, etc. श्लाघा-, adj., f. हा, Earning praise, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1155. सु-,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bearing well.<BR> 2. Patient.<BR> 3. Easy to be borne.<BR> II. f. हा.<BR> 1. The Indian lute.<BR> 2. The name of several plants. हुत- (vb. हु), m. Agni or fire, Megh. 44; Ṛt. 1, 27.<BR> --Cf. ὄχος; Lat. via; Goth. vigs; O.H.G. wagan, see वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत|वहतः
वहत वहत, i. e. वहन्त् + अ (vb. वह्), m.<BR> 1. An ox.<BR> 2. A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहति|वहतिः
वहति वह् + अति (cf. the last),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An ox.<BR> 2. A friend.<BR> 3. Air, wind.<BR> II. f. ती, A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहतु|वहतुः
वहतु वहतु (vb. वह्), m. An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन|वहनं
वहन वह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Bearing.<BR> 2. Flowing.<BR> 3. Any vehicle.<BR> 4. A raft, a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन्त|वहंत|वहंतः|वहन्तः
वहन्त वहन्त् + अ (vb. वह्), m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहल|वहलः
वहल वहल,<BR> I. adj. Hard, firm, compact, dense, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 7; Śiś. 9, 16; 8 (-अनुराग, dark-red).<BR> II. n. A raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित्र|वहित्रं
वहित्र वह् + इत्र, n. A boat, a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिश्चर|वहिश्चरः
वहिश्चर वहिश्चर, i. e. वहिस्-चर,<BR> I. adj. Going externally, out of somebody, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 2.<BR> II. m. A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्करण
वहिष्करण वहिष्करण, i. e. वहिस्-करण, n. Expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिस्
वहिस् वहिस्, perhaps from अवधि,<BR> I. adv.<BR> 1. Outwards, Pañc. i. d. 211; out, Hit. 29, 5, M.M.; with भू, to go out, Pañc. 141, 19.<BR> 2. Outside the door, Rājat. 5, 353 (i. e. expecting one's introduction to the king).<BR> 3. In the open air, Rājat. 5, 275.<BR> 4. Apart (from the multitude), Man. 2, 79.<BR> 5. Except (viz. on his hair, Kull.), Man. 4, 72.<BR> II. prep.<BR> 1. With a gen.<BR> a. Besides, Man. 10, 45.<BR> b. Outside, Daśak. 184, 7.<BR> 2. With abl. Outside, Rājat. 5, 329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्नि|वह्निः
वह्नि वह् + नि, m.<BR> 1. A sacrificer, Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.<BR> 2. Fire, Pañc. ii. d. 96; or its deity, Rām. 3, 53, 60.<BR> 3. Digestion, appetite.<BR> 4. Marking-nut plant.<BR> 5. Lead-wort, Plumbago zeylanica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्य|वह्यं
वह्य वह् + य,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A vehicle in general.<BR> 2. A cart.<BR> II. f. या, The wife of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
1. वा वा (originally अव् + आ, cf. ἄημι), ii. 2, Par.<BR> 1. To blow (as the wind), Man. 4, 122; Pañc. i. d. 353.<BR> 2. † To hurt.<BR> --i. 4, वाय (gramm. वै वै, i. 1), Par. To become dry, to dry.<BR> --Ptcple.<BR> 1. वात, Blown.<BR> 2. वान, Dry, dried (cf. both s. v.).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To blow upon (with acc.), Kir. 5, 36.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To cease blowing.<BR> 2. To be extinguished, Śāk. 91, 11, Chezy.<BR> 3. To be refreshed, Śiś. 1, 65.<BR> निर्वात, see under वात.<BR> निर्वाण,<BR> 1. Extinguished, Hariv. 2391.<BR> 2. Liberated from existence, MBh. 13, 2178. n.<BR> 1. Being extinguished, expiring, MBh. 4, 716.<BR> 2. Final beatitude, ib. 14, 543.<BR> 3. Bliss, happiness, ib. 3, 10438, Śāk. 33, 2.<BR> 4. Repose.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. वापय,<BR> 1. To extinguish, MBh. 1, 1608; to cool, Mālat. 128, 15.<BR> 2. To delight, Ragh. 9, 36 (Calc.).<BR> --With परिनिस् परि-निस्, अ-परिनिर्वाण, adj. Not completely finished, Śāk. 39, 20.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To blow vehemently, Pañc. 169, 6.<BR> 2. To blow, Rām. 2, 71, 25.<BR> 3. To smell, to yield a scent, MBh. 1, 6934.<BR> प्रवात, Agitated by the wind, Kumāras. 1, 47.<BR> --Caus. To dry, MBh. 1, 8431.<BR> --With वि वि, To blow, Ṛt. 6, 22.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To blow at the same time, MBh. 4, 1288.<BR> --Cf. ἄημι, ἄελλα, ἀήρ, μετέωρος, ἀείρω (ἀερϳω denomin., cf. ἀέῤῥω), ἄρδην, ἀρτάω, ἀορτήρ, αἰωρέω, αὔρα, probably αὐλός, οὖρος; ἀϋτμήν (= आत्मन्), ἀτμή; probably Lat. vanus, vapor (from the Caus.); Goth. vaian; O.H.G. wadal; see also वात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अ- + वात अ- + वात, adj. not yet calm, still wild, Ragh. 1, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
2. वा वा, A particle of,<BR> 1. Comparison, As, Draup. 7, 15; Rām. 1, 10, 37.<BR> 2. On the one side, Pañc. 43, 14 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a " target="_blank">Page0831-a + 44</a>] (क्षम्यतां यद् वाल्पे किम् अपि प्रणये नातिरेकाद् अयुक्तं तद् अनुष्ठितं तव, What on the one side must be indulged to a very feeble affection, that, done by thee, will not be unsuitable on account of the excess of thy love).<BR> 3. Option, Or; वा--वा, Either--or, Hit. ii. d. 159; Chr. 9, 34; Hit. 73, 22 (किं वा--न वा, Is it--or not).<BR> 4. Doubt, Or if, but if, Pañc. 246, 21.<BR> 5. Opposition, But, Chr. 10, 8; Hiḍ. 4, 2.<BR> 6. Exception, Only.<BR> 7. Asseveration, Indeed, even, Pañc. pr. d. 6.<BR> 8. Conjunction, And.<BR> 9. With preceding अथ (cf. अथ), or also, Hit. iii. d. 95; or, Pañc. 142, 5; or if, Pañc. 137, 20; or rather, Pañc. 82, 17; or, 90, 4; but, Pañc. 27, 1; 38, 17; certainly, Vikr. 70, 21.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ve; ἤ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशिक|वांशिकः
वांशिक वांशिक, i. e. वंश + इक, m. A flute-piper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक|वाकं|वाकः
वाक वाक,<BR> I. i. e. वक + अ,<BR> 1. adj. Relating to a crane.<BR> 2. n. A flight of cranes.<BR> II. i. e. वच् + अ, latter part of comp. words, Sounding, speaking, cf. चक्रवाक, चीरीवाक.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाक
निस्- + वाक निस्- + वाक, m. a proper name, MBh. 12, 8901.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्य|वाक्यं
वाक्य वाक्य, i. e. वच् + य, n.<BR> 1. Speech, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2375; मम वाक्यात्, In my name, Pañc. 142, 24.<BR> 2. A sentence, Pañc. 41, 17.<BR> 3. A rule.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाक्य
निर्वाक्य निर्वाक्य, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. या, speechless, Rām. 6, 98, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावाक्य|महावाक्यं
महा- + वाक्य महा- + वाक्य, n. a principal sentence, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 9; 205, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यतस्
वाक्यतस् वाक्य + तस्, adv. Conformably to the saying, Pañc. i. d. 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागर|वागरः
वागर वागर, m.<BR> 1. A whetstone.<BR> 2. A scholar.<BR> 3. One desirous of final emancipation.<BR> 4. A fearless one.<BR> 5. Certainty.<BR> 6. An obstacle.<BR> 7. Submarine fire.<BR> 8. A wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागारु|वागारुः
वागारु वागारु, adj. One who disappoints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरा
वागुरा वागुरा, f. A net for deer and wild animals, a snare, Hit. ii. d. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरिक|वागुरिकः
वागुरिक वागुरिक, i. e. वागुरा + इक, m. A hunter, Ragh. 9, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुद|वाग्गुदः
वाग्गुद वाग्गुद, m. A sort of bird, Man. 12, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्घस्तवन्त्|वाग्घस्तवत्
वाग्घस्तवन्त् वाग्घस्तवन्त्, i. e. वाच्-हस्त + वन्त्, adj. Possessed of speech and hands, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मित्व
वाग्मित्व वाग्मित्व, i. e. वाग्मिन् + त्व, n. Eloquence, Rājat. 5, 474.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मिन्
वाग्मिन् वाग्मिन्, i. e. वाच् + मिन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Talkative.<BR> 2. Eloquent, Pañc. iii. d. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाघन्त्|वाघत्
वाघन्त् वाघन्त् (probably ptcple. pres. of a lost vb. वाघ् = Lat. vāgire; εὔχομαι) m. Praying, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 88, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क्ष्|वांक्ष्
† वाङ्क्ष् वाङ्क्ष् (perhaps akin to the last), i. 1, Par. To wish.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. wunsc, wunskian; A.S. wiscan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मय|वाङ्मयं
वाङ्मय वाङ्मय, i. e. वाच् + मय,<BR> I. adj., f. यी.<BR> 1. Relating to speech, Bhag. 17, 15.<BR> 2. Endowed with speech, Johns. Sel. 94, 53.<BR> 3. Consisting of words, Ragh. 3, 28.<BR> 4. Eloquent.<BR> II. n. Eloquence.<BR> III. f. यी, Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्
वाच् वाच् (vb. वच्), f.<BR> 1. Speaking, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2647.<BR> 2. Speech, Pañc. iii. d. 112.<BR> 3. A word, Rām. 3, 51, 20 (voice?).<BR> 4. A phrase, a proverb.<BR> 5. Sarasvatī.<BR> 6. Voice, Chr. 44, 36.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवाच्
अन्-ऋत- + वाच् अन्-ऋत- + वाच्, adj. speaking an untruth, lying, Rām. 1, 6, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयवाच्
अ-भय- + वाच् अ-भय- + वाच्, f. promise of safety, Hit. 59, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघवाच्
अ-मोघ- + वाच् अ-मोघ- + वाच्, adj. one whose speech is not idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवाच्
आप्त- + वाच् आप्त- + वाच्, 1. f. the word of a trustworthy person, Ragh. 10, 29. 2. adj. worthy of trust, Śāk. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्|दुर्व्वाच्
दुर्वाच् दुर्वाच्, i. e. दुस्-, f. abuse, MBh. 1, 3076.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टवाच्
दुष्ट- + वाच् दुष्ट- + वाच्, m. a defamer, Man. 8, 386. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a " target="_blank">Page0832-a + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाच्
निर्वाच् निर्वाच्, i. e. निस्-, adj. dumb, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्
प्र- + वाच् प्र- + वाच्, adj. eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवाच्
सत्य- + वाच् सत्य- + वाच्,<BR> I. adj. speaking truth, Rām. 3, 53, 12; Hit. 120, 15.<BR> II. m. 1. a Ṛṣi. 2. a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचंयम|वाचंयमः
वाचंयम वाचंयम, i. e. वाच् + अम्-यम् + अ, m. A sage practising rigid taciturnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक|वाचकः
वाचक वाचक, i. e. वच् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Speaking.<BR> 2. Expressed by words, signifying, Vedāntas. in Chr. 213, 2.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A word, a significant sound.<BR> 2. A speaker.<BR> 3. A messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचन|वाचनं
वाचन वाचन, i. e. वच्, Caus., + अन, n. in स्वस्ति-, n. A preparatory religious rite in which the Brāhmaṇas invoke the blessings of the gods, etc., Vikr. 44, 14; Mālav. 56, 1 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनिक
वाचनिक वाचनिक, i. e. वाचन + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Verbal.<BR> 2. Textual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पति|वाचस्पतिः
वाचस्पति वाच् + अस्-पति, m. Vṛhaspati, preceptor of the gods, Pañc. pr. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पत्य|वाचस्पत्यं
वाचस्पत्य वाचस्पत्य, i. e. वाचस्पति + य, adj. Declared by Vācaspati, Hit. iii. d. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचा
वाचा वाचा, i. e. वाच् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Speech, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 18.<BR> 2. A holy word, Pañc. 221, 7 (oath).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाट|वाचाटः
वाचाट वाचाट, and वाचाल वाचाल (vb. वच्), adj.<BR> 1. Talkative, Man. 3, 8 (ट्).<BR> 2. Boasting, Megh. 92 (ल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिक|वाचिकं|वाचिकः
वाचिक वाचिक, वाच् and वाचा, + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Verbal.<BR> 2. Done by speech, Man. 12, 9.<BR> II. n. News, intelligence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवाचिक
त्रि- + वाचिक त्रि- + वाचिक, adj. given by three holy words (by an oath), Pañc. 222, 16; 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवाचिक
दण्ड- + वाचिक दण्ड- + वाचिक, i. e. दण्डवाच् + इक, adj. performed by deeds or words, Man. 8, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यता
वाच्यता वाच्य + ता (vb. वच्), f.<BR> 1. Blame, Hit. iii. d. 127.<BR> 2. Ill repute.<BR> 3. The quality of being predicable. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b " target="_blank">Page0832-b + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यता
अ- + वाच्यता अ- + वाच्यता, f. blame (cf. अ-वाच्य, s. v. वच्), Kir. 11, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाज|वाजं|वाजः
वाज वाज, i. e. वज् + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. A wing (see comp.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Food, sacrificial food, Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.<BR> 2. Battle, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. i. 85, 5.<BR> 3. Speed.<BR> 4. The feather of an arrow.<BR> 5. Sound.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Clarified butter.<BR> 2. Water.<BR> 3. Rice.<BR> 4. The acidulous mixture of ground meal and water left to ferment.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Engl. wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रवाज
गृध्र- + वाज गृध्र- + वाज, adj. adorned with a vulture's feathers, MBh. 9, 1413.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवाज|चित्रवाजः
चित्र- + वाज चित्र- + वाज, adj. adorned with variegated feathers, Bhāg. P. 4, 10, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवाज
पत्र- + वाज पत्र- + वाज, adj. endowed with feathers, Hariv. 13254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन्
वाजिन् वाजिन्, i. e. वाज + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Swift, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 6.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A sacrificer, Chr. 292, 3 = i. 86, 3.<BR> 2. A horse, Pañc. 218, 7; Rājat. 5, 143.<BR> 3. An arrow.<BR> 4. A bird.<BR> III. f. नी, A mare.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतवाजिन्
श्वेत- + वाजिन् श्वेत- + वाजिन्, m. 1. the moon. 2. Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन|वाजिनं
वाजिन वाजिन i. e. वाज + इन् + अ, n. The scum of curdled milk, Hemac. 3, 495 (= 831, Böhtl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिनीवन्त्|वाजिनीवत्
वाजिनीवन्त् वाजिन् + ई + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessed of sacrifices(?), Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छ्|वांछ्
वाञ्छ् वाञ्छ् (a form of वाङ्क्ष्, with छ् for क्ष्), i. 1, Par. (also Ātm., Hit. i. d. 186, M.M.).<BR> 1. To wish, to desire, Hit. iii. d. 18.<BR> 2. To pursue(?), Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वाञ्छित, n. Wish, Vikr. d. 28; Pañc. iii. d. 42.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To wish, Hit. i. d. 161; Pañc. i. d. 134.<BR> 2. To long after, Hit. i. d. 165, M.M.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To wish, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 53.<BR> --Cf. वाङ्क्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छन|वांछन|वांछनं
वाञ्छन वाञ्छ् + अन, n. Wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छा|वांछा
वाञ्छा वाञ्छ् + आ, f. Wish, desire, Pañc. ii. d. 165.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववाञ्छा
स्व- + वाञ्छा स्व- + वाञ्छा, instr. ad libitum, Hit. ii. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिन्|वांछिन्
वाञ्छिन् वाञ्छ् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Wishing, desirous.<BR> II. f. नी, A libidinous woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट|वाटं|वाटः
वाट वाट, i. e. वट + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of the Indian fig-tree, Man. 2, 45.<BR> II. n., f. ती, and n.<BR> 1. An enclosure, Johns. Sel. 40, 36; a grove(?), Bhāg. P. 1, 6, 11 (टी).<BR> 2. A mud wall.<BR> 3. The groin.<BR> 4. A road.<BR> III. f. ती.<BR> 1. The site of a building.<BR> 2. A house.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवाट
गोवाट गोवाट, m. a cow-pen, Hariv. 3397.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवाटी
पुष्प-वाटी पुष्प-वाटी, f. a flower-garden, Pañc. 221, 10 (erroneously पुष्य-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवाट|यज्ञवाटः
यज्ञ- + वाट यज्ञ- + वाट, m. a place prepared and enclosed for a sacrifice, Johns. Sel. 95, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशवाट
वेश-वाट वेश-वाट, house and court, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवाट|श्मशानवाटः
श्मशान- + वाट श्मशान- + वाट, m. a cemetery, Mālat. 77, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटधान|वाटधानः
वाटधान वाटधान, m. The son of an outcaste Brāhmaṇa by a female Brāhmaṇa, Man. 10, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिका
वाटिका वाटिका, i. e. वाटी + क, f.<BR> 1. The site of a house.<BR> 2. A garden, Pañc. 221, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षवाटिका
वृक्ष- + वाटिका वृक्ष- + वाटिका, f. an orchard, Śāk. 8, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्या
वाट्या वाट्या, f., and वाट्याल वाट्या + ल, m., ली, f. A plant, Sida cordifolia, Lass. Pentap. p. 64, v. 10 (ल); p. 66, v. 33 (या) = MBh. 8, 2034; 2059 (vv. rr.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाड्
वाड् वाड्, see बाड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडव|वाडवं|वाडवः
वाडव वाडव, see बाडव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढ
वाढ वाढ (cf. वहल and बहु),<BR> I. adj., comparat. साधीयंस्, superl. साधिष्ठ.<BR> 1. Hard, firm; साधीयंस्, firmest, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 19.<BR> 2. Much.<BR> II. acc. sing. ढम्, adv.<BR> 1. Much, excessively, Śiś. 9, 77.<BR> 2. Indeed, truly, Rām. 3, 51, 6; Śiś. 9, 51.<BR> 3. Well, very well, Pañc. 24, 11; yes, Daśak. in Chr. 192, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाण|वाणः
वाण वाण (also बाण बाण),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. (perhaps for पर्ण), An arrow, Pañc. 128, 1.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR> 3. The udder of a cow.<BR> 4. A pipe, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10 (with धमन्तस्, playing the pipe, i. e. roaring).<BR> 5. Alone.<BR> 6. The name of an Asura.<BR> II. m., and f. णा.<BR> 1. The feathered part of an arrow.<BR> 2. Blue Barleria, Kir. 4, 28 (णा); 10, 24 (double meaning, also arrow).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवाण
अ-सम-, कुसुम- + वाण अ-सम-, कुसुम- + वाण, and पञ्च(न्)-, m. Kāma (being armed with five arrows), Gīt. 4, 6; Pañc. 128, 1; Megh. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमवाण
अ-सम-, कुसुम- + वाण अ-सम-, कुसुम- + वाण, and पञ्च(न्)-, m. Kāma (being armed with five arrows), Gīt. 4, 6; Pañc. 128, 1; Megh. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिवाण
दृष्टि- + वाण दृष्टि- + वाण, m. an arrow-like look, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवाण|वारवाणः
वार- + वाण वार- + वाण, m. and n. an iron cuirass, or a thick quilted jacket. Ragh. 4, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणमय
वाणमय वाण + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting in arrows, Chr. 34, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणासन|वाणासनं
वाणासन वाणासन, i. e. वाण-असन, n. A bow, Śāk. 20, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणि|वाणिः
वाणि and वाणी वाणी̆ (vb. वे), f.<BR> 1. Weaving.<BR> 2. A weaver's loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज|वाणिजः
वाणिज वाणिज, i. e. वणिज् + अ, m. A merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिजिक|वाणिजिकः
वाणिजिक वाणिजिक, and वाणिज्य वाणिज्य, see बाण्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिन्
वाणिन् वाणिन्, i. e. वाण, and वाणी, + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Having an arrow or arrows, Arj. 5, 25; Rām. 3, 55, 12.<BR> 2. Speaking.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. An intriguing woman.<BR> 2. An intoxicated woman, literally and figuratively.<BR> 3. A dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणी
वाणी वाणी,<BR> 1. Speech, Hit. i. d. 99, M.M.<BR> 2. Voice, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 88, 6; Pañc. 186, 17.<BR> 3. A literary production, Utt. Rāmac. 177, 6.<BR> 4. सरस्वती, the goddess of speech, Brahmav. 2, 78. See वाणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
वात् वात्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from वात), Par.<BR> 1. To fan or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a " target="_blank">Page0834-a + 41</a>] ventilate.<BR> 2. † To give pleasure in travelling.<BR> 3. † To serve.<BR> 4. † To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात वात, i. e. वान्त्, ptcple. pres. of वा + अ, m.<BR> 1. Air, wind, Vikr. d. 25; breeze, 67, 3.<BR> 2. Rheumatism, gout, Śṛṅgārat. 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ventus; Goth. vinds; A.S. wind; O.H.G. wetar; A.S. weder (cf. वातर); ἐτώσιος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अ- + वात अ- + वात, (m. or n.), absence of wind, quiet, Lass. 97, 11 = Rigv. vi. 64, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवात|अनुवातः
अनु- + वात अनु- + वात, m. the windward side; ˚ते, loc. to the windward, Man. 3, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वात|निर्वातः|निर्व्वात|निर्व्वातः
निर्वात निर्वात, i. e. निस्-,<BR> I. adj. 1. not windy, calm. 2. sheltered from the wind, Hit. 80, 20.<BR> II. m. absence of wind, Pañc. iii. d. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवात|पुरोवातः
पुरोवात पुरोवात, i. e. पुरस्-, m. east wind, Vikr. d. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवात|पूतिवातः
पूति- + वात पूति- + वात, m. a fart, Bhāg. P. 5, 5, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवात|प्रतिवातः
प्रति- + वात प्रति- + वात, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकिन्
वातकिन् वात-किन्, i. e. वात + क + इन्, adj. Rheumatic, gouty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातप्रमी
वातप्रमी वात-प्र-मी, m. and f. A swift antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमज|वातमजः
वातमज वात + म्-अज् + अ, m. A swift antelope, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर
वातर वात + र, adj. Windy, stormy.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vintrus; A.S. winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरूष|वातरूषः
वातरूष वात-रूष् + अ (perhaps rather vb. रस्ह्), m.<BR> 1. A gale.<BR> 2. The rainbow.<BR> 3. A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर्द्धि
वातर्द्धि वातर्द्धि, i. e. वात-ऋद्धि, m.<BR> 1. A sort of cup or vessel of wood, with an iron foot.<BR> 2. A club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातल|वातलः
वातल वात + ल (cf. वातर),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Windy, stormy.<BR> 2. Flatulent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Wind.<BR> 2. A sort of pulse, Cicer arietinum.<BR> III. f. ला, A morbid state of the uterus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवातल
अ- + वातल अ- + वातल, adj. not causing flatulence, Suśr. 1, 221, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातापि|वातापिः
वातापि वातापि, m. The name of an Asura devoured by Agastya, Rām. 3, 49, 49, sqq.; MBh. 3, 8619.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायन|वातायनं|वातायनः
वातायन वातायन, i. e. वात-अयन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b " target="_blank">Page0834-b + 43</a>]<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A window, Pañc. 46, 11.<BR> 2. A porch, a pavilion, Utt. Rāmac. 22 13.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. A proper name, Śāk. 81, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाति|वातिः
वाति वाति, m.<BR> 1. (vb. वा), Air, wind.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिक|वातिकः
वातिक वातिक, i. e. वात + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Produced by wind.<BR> 2. Windy.<BR> 3. Rheumatic.<BR> 4. Mad, Sāh. Darp. 286, 14.<BR> II. n. Fever or inflammation, ascribed to a vitiated state of the aerial humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुल|वातुलः
वातुल and वातूल वातू̆ल (from वात),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Gouty.<BR> 2. Mad (cf. the last), Hit. ii. d. 26 (त्ŭ); Rājat. 5, 83 (तू).<BR> II. m. A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्या
वात्या वात्या, i. e. probably वात + य, f. A gale, a whirlwind, Kir. 5, 39; Rājat. 5, 477.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सल्य|वात्सल्यं|वात्सल्यः
वात्सल्य वात्सल्य, i. e. वत्सल + य, n. Tenderness, Pañc. 221, 1; Vikr. d. 147; love, Hit. ii. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्यायन|वात्स्यायनः
वात्स्यायन वात्स्यायन, i. e. वात्स्य, patronym. of वत्स, + आयन, patronym., m. The name of a Muni, Pañc. 45, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद|वादः
वाद वाद, i. e. वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Speaking, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 11.<BR> 2. Sound, Pañc. 248, 11; words, i. d. 475.<BR> 3. Discussion, controversy, Man. 12, 46.<BR> 4. Exposition of holy texts, Man. 6, 50.<BR> 5. Demonstrated conclusion, result.<BR> 6. Accusation.<BR> 7. Report, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवाद|अर्थवादः
अर्थ- + वाद अर्थ- + वाद, m. praise, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वाद|आशीर्वादः|आशीर्व्वादः
आशीर्वाद आशीर्वाद, i. e. आशिस्-, m. a benediction, Pañc. 208, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासवाद|इतिहासवादः
इतिहास- + वाद इतिहास- + वाद, m. a tale, Mālat. 47, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्वाद|उच्चैर्वादः
उच्चैस्- + वाद उच्चैस्- + वाद, m. boasting, Utt. Rāmac. 136, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवाद|धर्मवादः
धर्म- + वाद धर्म- + वाद, m. a conversation concerning law or virtue, Rām. 5, 48, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवाद|पक्षवादः
पक्ष- + वाद पक्ष- + वाद, m. uttering one's opinion, MBh. 7, 6009.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिवाद|पाणिवादः
पाणि- + वाद पाणि- + वाद, n. clapping of the hands, Rām. 2, 65, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलवाद
प्रतिकूल- + वाद प्रतिकूल- + वाद, m. objection, in अ-, adj. not opposing, MBh. 3, 10265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावाद|मिथ्यावादः
मिथ्या- + वाद मिथ्या- + वाद, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a " target="_blank">Page0835-a + 44</a>] adj. speaking untruth, lying, Pañc. iii. d. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाद|लोकवादः
लोक- + वाद लोक- + वाद, m. rumour, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणावाद|वीणावादः
वीणा- + वाद वीणा- + वाद, m. a lutanist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवाद
साम(न्)- + वाद साम(न्)- + वाद, m. pl. words of conciliation, Pañc. iii. d. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवाद|हीनवादः
हीन- + वाद हीन- + वाद (vb. हा), m. contradictory evidence, prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवाद|हेतुवादः
हेतु- + वाद हेतु- + वाद, m. disputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादक|वादकः
वादक वादक, i. e. वद्, Caus., + अक, adj. sbst.<BR> 1. A musician, Johns. Sel. 52, 116.<BR> 2. A speaker.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिवादक|पाणिवादकः
पाणि- + वादक पाणि- + वादक, m. one who makes a clapping of the hands, Rām. 2, 65, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादन|वादनं|वादनः
वादन वादन, i. e. वद्, Caus., + अन, n. Instrumental music, Man. 2, 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादि|वादिः
वादि वादि (vb. वद्), adj.<BR> 1. Speaking.<BR> 2. Wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित्र|वादित्रं
वादित्र वादित्र, i. e. वद्, Caus., + त्र, n.<BR> 1. A musical instrument, Man. 4, 64.<BR> 2. Instrumental music, Indr. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित्व
ऽवादित्व -वादित्व, i. e. वादिन् + त्व, n. in सत्य-, Veracity, Hit. i. d. 98, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिन्
वादिन् वादिन्, i. e. वद् + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Speaking, Vikr. d. 118; Johns. Sel. 57, 164; a speaker, Bhartṛ. 3, 53.<BR> 2. Asserting.<BR> 3. Disputing, Bhartṛ. 3, 47.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An expounder of the law.<BR> 2. A plaintiff, Lass. 92, 2.<BR> 3. Key-note.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवादिन्
अर्थ- + वादिन् अर्थ- + वादिन्, adj. speaking truth, Pañc. 161, 19; cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 467.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंवादिन्
अहंवादिन् अहंवादिन्, i. e. अहम्- (see अस्मद्), adj. self-conceited, Bhag. 18, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवादिन्
उत्तर- + वादिन् उत्तर- + वादिन्, m. the defendant (in an action at law), Yājñ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतवादिन्
ऋत- + वादिन् ऋत- + वादिन्, adj. speaking the truth, MBh. 13, 4402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवादिन्
धर्म- + वादिन् धर्म- + वादिन्, adj. one who likes to speak of law or virtue, Pañc. 166, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितवादिन्
पण्डित- + वादिन् पण्डित- + वादिन्, adj. pretending to be wise, Pañc. i. d. 437.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ववादिन्|पूर्व्ववादिन्
पूर्व- + वादिन् पूर्व- + वादिन्, m. the plaintiff (in an action at law), Yājñ. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलवादिन्
प्रतिकूल- + वादिन् प्रतिकूल- + वादिन्, adj. contradicting, opposing, MBh. 5, 1359.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवादिन्
प्रिय- + वादिन् प्रिय- + वादिन्, adj. speaking agreeably, as one wishes, Pañc. ii. d. 171; Hit. pr. d. 19, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवादिन्
ब्रह्मवादिन् ब्रह्मवादिन्, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. 1. one [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b " target="_blank">Page0835-b + 42</a>] who recites the Vedas, Man. 6, 39. 2. an expounder of the Vedas, Man. 2, 113. 3. a follower of the Vedānta system.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवादिन्
मन्त्र- + वादिन् मन्त्र- + वादिन्, adj. sbst. one who is conversant with charms, Pañc. 210, 17; 43, 10; Lass. 16, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावादिन्
मिथ्या- + वादिन् मिथ्या- + वादिन्, adj., f. नी, lying, a liar, Pañc. 52, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादिन्
सत्य- + वादिन् सत्य- + वादिन्, adj., f. नी, speaking truth, Pañc. 100, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवादिन्
हीन- + वादिन् हीन- + वादिन् (vb. हा), adj. (speaking deficiently), 1. dumb. 2. contradictory. 3. inadmissible (as evidence). 4. cast in law, Pañc. 166, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध्
वाध् वाध्, वाध वाध, see बाध्, बाध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधुक्य|वाधुक्यं
वाधुक्य वाधुक्य, i. e. वधू̆ + क + य, n. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधू
वाधू वाधू (vb. वह्, cf. वधु), f. A boat, a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान<BR> A. i. e. वा + न,<BR> I. adj. Dry, Nalod. 2, 26.<BR> II. m., f. ना, and n. Dry fruit.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Moving.<BR> 2. A heavy sea.<BR> 3. A mat of straw.<BR> 4. Living.<BR> 5. A perfume.<BR> B. n. A hole in the wall of a house.<BR> C. i. e. वन + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a wood, a house.<BR> II. n. A number of woods, Nalod. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानप्रस्थ|वानप्रस्थः
वानप्रस्थ वानप्रस्थ, i. e. वन-प्र-स्थ + अ, m.<BR> 1. The Brāhmaṇa of the third order, who lives in woods, a hermit, Man. 6, 87.<BR> 2. The name of two particular trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानर|वानरः
वानर वानर, i. e. वनर + अ,<BR> I. m., and f. री, A monkey, Pañc. 203, 3; 206, 15.<BR> II. adj., f. री, Belonging to a monkey, MBh. 13, 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानस्पत्य|वानस्पत्यः
वानस्पत्य वानस्पत्य, i. e. वनस्पति + य,<BR> I. adj. Belonging to a tree, Man. 8, 339.<BR> II. m. and n. (Rām. 6, 96, 13), A tree bearing fruits from blossoms, as the mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीर|वानीरः
वानीर वानीर, m. A sort of cane, Calamus rotang, Megh. 42; Ragh. 13, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ताशिन्
वान्ताशिन् वान्ताशिन्, i. e. वान्त (vb. वम्) -अश् + इन्, m. A foul-feeding demon, Man. 3, 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ति|वांति|वान्तिः
वान्ति वान्ति, i. e. वम् + ति, f. Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या वान्या, i. e. वन + य, f. A multitude of groves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप|वापः
वाप वाप, i. e. वप् + अ, m. Shaving, shearing, Man. 11, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापक|वापकः
वापक वापक, see वायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापन|वापनं
वापन वापन, i. e. वप् + अन, n. Shaving, shearing, Man. 11, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापि|वापिः
वापि and वापी वापी̆, f. A pond, Ṛt. 6, 3 (पी); Pañc. iii. d. 91 (पी); an oblong reservoir of water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वापी|स्वर्व्वापी
स्वर्-वापी स्वर्-वापी, f. the Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम वाम,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Left (not right), Rājat. 5, 97; Megh. 94.<BR> 2. Reverse, adverse, Pañc. ii. d. 87; opposite, Śāk. d. 93 (those who act in an opposite way).<BR> 3. Bad, wicked, crooked, Kir. 11, 24.<BR> 4. Short.<BR> 5. Beautiful, Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. Kāma.<BR> 3. An udder.<BR> 4. An animal.<BR> 5. A snake.<BR> III. f. मा.<BR> 1. A woman.<BR> 2. Gaurī.<BR> 3. Lakṣmī.<BR> 4. Sarasvatī.<BR> IV. f. मी.<BR> 1. A mare, Ragh. 5, 32.<BR> 2. A she-ass.<BR> 3. A young female elephant.<BR> 4. The female of a jackal.<BR> V. n. Wealth, Chr. 287, 1 = Rigv. i. 48, 1.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. winistar; A.S. wynstre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामक|वामकः
वामक वाम + क,<BR> I. adj. Left, Mālat. 5, 7.<BR> II. n. A kind of gesture, Vikr. 59, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामत्व
वामत्व वाम + त्व, n. Disfavour, Mālat. 146, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन वामन (from वाम),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Dwarfish, Johns. Sel. 96, 79; a dwarf, Johns. Sel. 95, 63; Bhāg. P. 8, 19, title.<BR> 2. Pressed flat or down, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830 (वामनी-कृत, Pressed down). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b " target="_blank">Page0836-b + 42</a>]<BR> 3. Vile, low.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Viṣṇu (on account of his अवतार in the shape of a dwarf, Bhāg. P. 8, 19).<BR> 2. The elephant that supports the south quarter, Rām. 1, 6, 23.<BR> III. f. ना, The name of an Apsaras, Lass. 2. ed. 50, 23.<BR> IV. f. नी, A female dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूर|वामलूरः
वामलूर वामलूर (cf. वम्र, वल्मी), m. An ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय|वायः
वाय वाय, i. e. वे + अ, m. Weaving.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाय|तंतुवाय|तन्तुवायः
तन्तु-, तन्त्र- + वाय तन्तु-, तन्त्र- + वाय, m. 1. a weaver, Man. 8, 397; Rām. 2, 90, 15 Gorr. 2. a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवाय|तंत्रवाय|तन्त्रवायः
तन्तु-, तन्त्र- + वाय तन्तु-, तन्त्र- + वाय, m. 1. a weaver, Man. 8, 397; Rām. 2, 90, 15 Gorr. 2. a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नवाय|तुन्नवायः
तुन्न- + वाय तुन्न- + वाय (vb. तुद्), m. a tailor, Man. 4, 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायक|वायकः
वायक वायक,<BR> I. m. A multitude.<BR> II. adj. Weaving, a weaver (? in पट्टिका-, A weaver of ribbons, Rām. 2, 90, 21 Gorr.; who has वापक, which Böhtl. changes in वायक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायन|वायनं
वायन वायन, n. Sweetmeats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव वायव, i. e. वायु + अ,<BR> I. adj. Windy.<BR> II. f. वी, The region of the wind, the north-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव्य|वायव्यं
वायव्य वायव्य, i. e. वायु + य, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the wind, Arj. 3, 30.<BR> 2. Coming from, belonging to, its deity, Vikr. d. 18; Utt. Rāmac. 143, 5.<BR> 3. Sacred to the deity of the wind. Chr. 31, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायस|वायसः
वायस वायस (probably वयस् + अ, Long-lived),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A crow, Pañc. 140, 16.<BR> 2. Two plants.<BR> II. f. सी.<BR> 1. A she-crow, Hit. 67, 13.<BR> 2. A species of fig, Ficus oppositifolia.<BR> 3. A vegetable, Solanum indicum.<BR> III. adj.<BR> 1. (वायस + अ). Used by crows(?), Bhāg. P. 1, 5, 10.<BR> 2. (वयस् + अ), f. सी, Consisting of birds, Nalod. 1, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वायस
निस्- + वायस निस्- + वायस, adj. deprived of crows, Pañc. 148, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायु|वायुः
वायु वा + यु, m.<BR> 1. Air, wind, Pañc. 184, 11; its deity, Man. 1, 23.<BR> 2. The air of the body.<BR> 3. Morbid affection [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a " target="_blank">Page0837-a + 42</a>] of the windy humour.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावायु|महावायुः
महा- + वायु महा- + वायु, m. air as clement, Bhāṣāp. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुज
वायुज वायु-ज (literally, Produced by air), Pañc. 44, 15, name of a tree (? cf. my transl. n. 204).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्
वार् वार्, n. Water, Nalod. 3, 51.<BR> --Cf. οὖρον, οὐρέω, οὐρία, perhaps ὑρτήρ, ὔρχη; Lat. urina, urceus, urna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार|वारं|वारः
वार वार,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A multitude, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 23; Rājat. 5, 342; a troop, ib. 453.<BR> 2. A moment.<BR> 3. Opportunity, time, Pañc. 256, 7.<BR> 4. Turn, Hit. 67, 21.<BR> 5. A day of the week, Hit. 48, 3 (भट्टारक-, Sunday).<BR> 6. A gate.<BR> 7. A name of Śiva.<BR> II. acc. रम्, adv. doubled, वारंवारम्, Repeatedly, Hit. 67, 12.<BR> III. instr. रण, adv. Frequently.<BR> IV. n. A vessel for holding spirituous liquor.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἦρα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवारम्
एक-वार + म् एक-वार + म्, adv. 1. once, Pañc. 216, 2. 2. only once, Bhartṛ. 3, 16. 3. at once, Pañc. 174, 23. 4. suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवार|बहुवारः
बहु- + वार बहु- + वार, m. pl. many times, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवार|मधुवारः
मधु- + वार मधु- + वार, m. drinking repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविवार|रविवारः
रवि- + वार रवि- + वार, m. Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणवार|वाणवारः
वाण- + वार वाण- + वार, m. (vb. वृ), 1. a cuirass. 2. armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्ववार
विश्व- + वार विश्व- + वार, adj. (vb. वृ), containing every boon, Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवार|सोमवारः
सोम- + वार सोम- + वार, m. Monday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारक|वारकं|वारकः
वारक वारक, i. e. वृ + अक,<BR> I. adj. Opposing, an agent of resistance.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A horse's paces.<BR> 2. A horse.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. The seat of pain.<BR> 2. A sort of fragrant grass, Brahmav. 2, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकिन्
वारकिन् वारकिन्, i. e. वारक + इन्, m.<BR> 1. An enemy.<BR> 2. The ocean.<BR> 3. A horse with good marks.<BR> 4. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्ग|वारंग|वारंगः|वारङ्गः
वारङ्ग वारङ्ग, m. The narrow end of a sword, sickle, etc., to which the handle is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारटा
वारटा वारटा, i. e. वरट + अ, f. A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारण|वारणं|वारणः
वारण वारण, i. e. वृ + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Armour.<BR> 2. An elephant, Hit. ii. d. 28.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Warding off, Bhartṛ. 2, 14.<BR> 2. Resistance.<BR> 3. Obstacle.<BR> 4. Protecting.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवारण|आतपवारणं
अतप-, उष्ण- + वारण आतप-, उष्ण- + वारण, n. a parasol, Ragh. 3, 70. Kumāras. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवारण|उष्णवारणः
अतप-, उष्ण- + वारण आतप-, उष्ण- + वारण, n. a parasol, Ragh. 3, 70. Kumāras. 5, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वारण|दिग्वारणः
दिग्वारण दिग्वारण, i. e. दिश्-, m. an elephant supposed to support a quarter of the world, MBh. 3, 9929.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवारण|हस्तवारणं
हस्त- + वारण हस्त- + वारण, n. resisting an assault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणावत|वारणावतं|वारणावतः
वारणावत वारणावत, i. e. वारण + वन्त् + अ (m. or n.), A name of Hastināpura, Hiḍ. 1, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला वारला, i. e. वरल + अ, f.<BR> 1. A wasp.<BR> 2. A goose (cf. वरटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसी
वाराणसी वाराणसी, f. The city Benares, Lass. 5, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह|वाराहः
वाराह वाराह, i. e. वरह + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a boar, boarish, Johns. Sel. 93, 52.<BR> II. f. ही.<BR> 1. A sow.<BR> 2. The earth.<BR> 3. One of the divine mothers.<BR> 4. A measure.<BR> 5. An esculent root, Dioscorea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारि|वारिः
वारि वारि,<BR> I. (cf. वार्), n. Water, Pañc. ii. d. 149; fluidity, i. d. 139.<BR> II. f., also वारी वारी,<BR> 1. A water pot.<BR> 2. (vb. वृ), A hole for catching elephants.<BR> 3. (vb. वृ), A rope for fastening elephants.<BR> III. f. रि.<BR> 1. A place where elephants are tied up.<BR> 2. A captive.<BR> 3. Sarasvatī.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशवारि
कुश- + वारि कुश- + वारि, n. water in which कुश grass is boiled, Man. 11, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराम्लोदकवारि
क्षाराम्लोदकवारि क्षाराम्लोदकवारि, i. e. क्षार-अम्ल-उदक-. n. pl. ashes, acids, and water, Man. 5, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनवारि
चन्दन- + वारि चन्दन- + वारि, n. water mixed with sandal, Rām. 3, 53, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रवारि
नेत्र- + वारि नेत्र- + वारि, n. a tear, tears, Rām. 2, 111, 12 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिज|वारिजं|वारिजः
वारिज वारि-ज,<BR> I. adj. Produced in or by water.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A conch-shell.<BR> 2. Any bivalve shell.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A lotus, Bhartṛ. 2, 46.<BR> 2. Salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित्रा
वारित्रा वारि-त्रा, f. An umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिद|वारिदं|वारिदः
वारिद वारि-द (vb. दा),<BR> I. adj. Yielding water.<BR> II. m. A cloud, Utt. Rāmac. 120, 14; Rājat. 5, 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिधर|वारिधरः
वारिधर वारि-धर, m. A cloud, Vikr. d. 73; Rājat. 5, 377.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिधि|वारिधिः
वारिधि वारिधि, i. e. वारि-धा (cf. निधि), m. The ocean, Kir. 1, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरवारिधि|क्षीरवारिधिः
क्षीर- + वारिधि क्षीर- + वारिधि, m. the sea of milk, Kathās. 22, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरुह|वारिरुहं
वारिरुह वारि-रुह् + अ, n. A lotus, Kir. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण|वारुणं|वारुणः
वारुण वारुण, i. e. वरुण + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. णी.<BR> 1. Relating, belonging to Varuṇa, MBh. 1, 1132; Man. 8, 82; 9, 308.<BR> 2. Sacred to Varuṇa, 8, 106.<BR> 3. Epithet of a weapon, Utt. Rāmac. 142, 10; Chr. 31, 12.<BR> II. f. णी.<BR> 1. Any spirituous liquor, Man. 11, 146; Pañc. i. d. 194 (at the same time, The west).<BR> 2. The west, the region of Varuṇa, Pañc. i. d. 194.<BR> 3. The twenty-fifth lunar asterism.<BR> III. n. Water (ŚKD.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण्ड|वारुंड|वारुंडः|वारुण्डः
वारुण्ड वारुण्ड,<BR> I. m. The king of the serpents.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. A vessel for baling water out of a boat.<BR> 2. The rheum of the eyes.<BR> 3. The wax of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्कार्य
वार्कार्य वार्-कार्य (vb. कृ), adj., f. या, Effecting rain, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 88, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष
वार्क्ष वार्क्ष, i. e. वृक्ष + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Made of trees.<BR> 2. Consisting of trees, Man. 7, 70.<BR> II. m. A forest.<BR> III. f. क्षी, A sort of Dryad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्णिक|वार्णिकः
वार्णिक वार्णिक, i. e. वर्ण + इक, m. A scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त|वार्त|वार्त्तं|वार्त्तः
वार्त्त वार्त्त, i. e. वृत्ति + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Well, healthy.<BR> 2. Following any business.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Health.<BR> 2. Chaff.<BR> III. f. ता.<BR> 1. Abiding.<BR> 2. Livelihood, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b " target="_blank">Page0838-b + 41</a>] business, Man. 9, 326; 10, 80.<BR> 3. Agriculture and trade, Ragh. 16, 2.<BR> 4. Rumour, report, Hit. 93, 19.<BR> 5. News, tidings, Utt. Rāmac. 151, 6; Pañc. 231, 21.<BR> 6. The egg-plant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलवार्त्त|गलवार्त
गल- + वार्त्त गल- + वार्त्त, adj. voracious, Pañc. iii. d. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वार्त्ता
दुर्वार्त्ता दुर्वार्त्ता, i. e. दुस्-, f. bad tidings, Sch. ad Ragh. 12, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावार्त्ता|मिथ्यावार्ता
मिथ्या- + वार्त्त्ā मिथ्या- + वार्त्ता, f. false report, Pañc. 51, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धकवार्त्ता
लुब्धक- + वार्त्ता लुब्धक- + वार्त्ता, f. speaking about the hunter, Pañc. 143, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तिक|वार्तिक|वार्त्तिकं|वार्त्तिकः
वार्त्तिक वार्त्तिक, and वार्तिक वार्तिक, i. e. वार्त्ता and वृत्ति, + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to news.<BR> 2. Commentary, explaining (see<BR> IV.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A man of the third caste (i. e. a husbandman or trader).<BR> 2. An envoy.<BR> III. f. (rather वार्तिका वार्तिका), A sort of quail (cf. वर्तक).<BR> IV. n. A critical gloss, e. g. to Pāṇini's Grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्रघ्न|वार्त्त्रघ्नः|वार्त्रघ्नः
वार्त्रघ्न वार्त्रघ्न, i. e. वृत्रघ्न + अ, patronym., m. (a son of Indra), Arjuna, Kir. 15, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्दल|वार्दलः|वार्द्दल|वार्द्दलं|वार्द्दलः
वार्दल वार्-द + ल (vb. दा, cf. वारिद), n. A rainy day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक
वार्द्धक वार्द्धक, i. e. वृद्ध + क + अ, n.<BR> 1. A multitude of old men.<BR> 2. Old age, Pañc. 95, 16 (read वार्धकभावे, but cf. also my transl. n. 466).<BR> 3. Infirmity of old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्य
वार्द्धक्य वार्द्धक्य, i. e. वृद्ध + क + य, n. Old age, Hit. i. d. 113, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्षत्रि
वार्द्धक्षत्रि वार्द्धक्षत्रि, i. e. वृद्ध-क्षत्र + इ, patronym., m. A proper name, Draup. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषि
वार्द्धुषि वार्द्धुषि (probably rather वार्धुषि, i. e. वृध् + उषि, anomal., cf. ved. अश् + उष), m. A usurer, Man. 3, 153; 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिक
वार्द्धुषिक वार्द्धुषि + क (see the last), m. A usurer, Man. 8, 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुष्य
वार्द्धुष्य वार्द्धुष्य, i. e. वार्द्धुषि + य, n. Usury, Man. 11, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध्र
वार्द्ध्र वार्द्ध्र, i. e. वर्द्ध्र + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री, Leathern.<BR> II. n., and f. री, A thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध्रीणस
वार्द्ध्रीणस वार्द्ध्रीणस, i. e. वार्द्ध्री-नस, m.<BR> 1. A long-eared white goat, Man. 3, 271.<BR> 2. A rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्धि|वार्द्धिः|वार्धिः
वार्धि वार्धि, i. e. वार्-धा (cf. निधि), m. The ocean, Pañc. i. d. 420 (वार्धि + वत्, adv. Like the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्मण|वार्मणं|वार्म्मण|वार्म्मणं
वार्मण वार्मण, i. e. वर्मन् + अ, n. A multitude of coats of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिक|वार्षिकं|वार्षिकः
वार्षिक वार्षिक, i. e. वर्ष and वर्षा, + इक, adj. f. की,<BR> 1. Belonging to a year.<BR> 2. Yearly, annual.<BR> 3. Lasting the whole year, Chr. 47, 36 (at the end of a comp. adj. Of which the water does not dry up in the hot season, viz. a river).<BR> 4. Belonging to the rainy season, Man. 9, 304; Draup. 8, 17.<BR> 5. Growing in the rainy season.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवार्षिक
दशवार्षिक दशवार्षिक, i. e. दशन्-, adj., f. की, 1. after the lapse of ten years, Yājñ. 2, 24. 2. having lasted ten years, Pañc. iii. d. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशवार्षिक
द्वादश(न्)- + वार्षिक द्वादश(न्)- + वार्षिक, adj., f. की, 1. twelve years old, Man. 9, 94. 2. lasting twelve years, 3, 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊनद्विवार्षिक
ऊन-द्वि- + वार्षिक ऊन-द्वि- + वार्षिक, adj. under the age of two years, Man. 5, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिला
वार्षिला वार्षिला (vb. वृष्), f. Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष्णेय|वार्ष्णेयः
वार्ष्णेय वार्ष्णेय, i. e. वृष्णि + एय, patronym., m. A proper name, Nal. 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत
वार्हस्पत वार्हस्पत, i. e. वृहस्पति + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Sacred to Vṛhaspati.<BR> 2. Declared by Vṛhaspati, Pañc. 253, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत्य
वार्हस्पत्य वार्हस्पत्य, i. e. वृहस्पति + य, n. Rules of conduct, ethics (Vṛhaspati being supposed to be the author of this science).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालक|वालकः
वालक वालक, i. e. वल् + अक, m. and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b " target="_blank">Page0839-b + 39</a>] n.<BR> 1. A bracelet.<BR> 2. (also f., ŚKD.), A finger-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालवितु
वालवितु वालवितु, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्क|वाल्कं
वाल्क वाल्क, i. e. वल्क + अ, adj. Made of the bark of trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीक|वाल्मीकः
वाल्मीक वाल्मीक, and वाल्मीकि वाल्मीकि, m. A proper name, the poet of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाव
वाव वाव, i. e. probably वा-एव (Weber, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. 2, 4); indecl. used in a question, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूक|वावदूकः
वावदूक वावद् + ऊक (frequent of वद्), adj. Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्
वावृत् वावृत्, वृत् वृत्, i. 4, Ātm. (the first looks rather like an old frequent. of वृत्), To select, to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्
वाश् वाश्, and वास् वास्, i. 4, Ātm. (in epic poetry i. 1, Par. Ātm., MBh. 3, 10493; Nal. 11, 20; 1, 8433; also Mṛcch. 143, 13), To cry, to howl, Ragh. 11, 61.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वाशित, n. The cry of birds or animals. f. ता,<BR> 1. A woman.<BR> 2. A female elephant. Frequent. वावश्य, To cry repeatedly, MBh. 6, 111.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To bewail, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशि|वाशिः
वाशि वाशि, m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशी
वाशी वाश् + ई, f. Roar, prayer(?), Chr. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशीमन्त्|वाशीमत्
वाशीमन्त् वाशी + मन्त्, adj. Roaring, Chr. 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 87, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशुरा
वाशुरा वाशुरा, f. Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्र|वाश्रं|वाश्रः
वाश्र वाश्र,<BR> I. m. A day (cf. वासर).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A dwelling.<BR> 2. A place where four roads meet.<BR> 3. Dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्प|वाष्पं|वाष्पः
वाष्प वाष्प (and वास्प वास्प),<BR> I. m. n.<BR> 1. Vapour, Ragh. 13, 29; steam [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a " target="_blank">Page0840-a + 45</a>] (cf. Pañc. 262, 21).<BR> 2. A tear, Pañc. 160, 5.<BR> 3. n. Iron.<BR> II. f. पी, A drug, commonly हिङ्गुपत्री.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vappa, perhaps vāpor (cf. 1. वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वाष्प
अन्तर्- + वाष्प अन्तर्- + वाष्प, adj. with suppressed tears, Vikr. d. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाष्प
उद्- + वाष्प उद्- + वाष्प, adj. shedding tears, Kathās. 10, 208 (hence उद्वाष्प + त्व, n. shedding tears, Vikr. d. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवाष्पम्
स-वाष्प + म् स-वाष्प + म्, adv. with tears in his eyes, Pañc. 243, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाय
वाष्पाय वाष्पाय, a denomin. derived from वाष्प with य, Ātm. To shed tears, Vikr. d. 147; Mālat. 102, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्
वास् वास्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from वास), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 24), To introduce another quality, to perfume, Gīt. 1, 35.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वासित.<BR> 1. Made fragrant, Utt. Rāmac. 63, 4.<BR> 2. Filled with fragrance, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 551. see s. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To adorn, Vikr. d. 127.<BR> --Cf. वाश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवासित
सु- + वासित सु- + वासित, adj. well perfumed, Ṛt. 1, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास वास, i. e. 1. 3. वस् and वास्, + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Dwelling, Man. 2, 67; resting, Megh. 77; living, Pañc. i. d. 347; Hit. i. d. 113, M.M.; with वस्, to dwell, to live (see s. v. 1. वस्).<BR> 2. A dwellingplace, Vikr. d. 43; a habitation, a house, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 12; Lass. 75, 10.<BR> 3. Cloth, Kathās. 3, 71.<BR> 4. Perfuming, Vikr. d. 38; perfume, Śiś. 9, 52.<BR> II. m., and f. सा, A plant, Justicia ganderusa.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवास|उदवासः
उदवास उदवास, i. e. उदन्-, m. abiding in water, MBh. 13, 354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भवास
गर्भ- + वास गर्भ- + वास, m. the womb, Man. 12, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहवास
गृह- + वास गृह- + वास, m. 1. domestic life. Utt. Rāmac. 27, 3. 2. living as householder, the second order of brahmanical life, MBh. 13, 2181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवास|गोवासः
गो- + वास गो- + वास,<BR> I. m. a cow-pen, ib. 2, 825.<BR> II. adj. covered with the skin of a bull or cow, ib. 8, 3650.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवास|जलवासं|जलवासः
जल- + वास जल- + वास,<BR> I. m. abiding in water, ib. 12, 9281.<BR> II. adj. one who abides in water, ib. 12, 9280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवास|तपोवासः
तपोवास तपोवास, i. e. तपस्-, m. a place where hermits live, Hariv. 5168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवास|पटवासः
पट- + वास पट- + वास, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b " target="_blank">Page0840-b + 45</a>] m. perfumed powder, Gīt. 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवास|भूतवासः
भूत- + वास भूत- + वास, m. Beleric myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटवास|मर्कटवासः
मर्कट- + वास मर्कट- + वास, m. a spider's web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावासम्
यथा-वास + म् यथा-वास + म्, adv. as far as to one's own abode, home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुवास|रेणुवासः
रेणु- + वास रेणु- + वास, m. a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवास|वारिवासः
वारि- + वास वारि- + वास, m. a distiller or dealer in spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीयवास
शयनीय- + वास शयनीय- + वास (vb. शी), m. a sleeping-room, Lass. 2. ed. 19, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवास
स- + वास स- + वास, adj. 1. having a dwelling. 2. scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवास|सुवासः
सु- + वास सु- + वास, m. 1. a pleasant dwelling. 2. an agreeable perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
वासन वासन, i. e. 1. 3. वस् and वास्, + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Abiding, abode.<BR> 2. Any receptacle.<BR> 3. A box, a basket.<BR> 4. A water-jar.<BR> 5. A particular posture.<BR> 6. Knowledge.<BR> 7. Steeping, infusing.<BR> 8. Cloth.<BR> 9. An envelope.<BR> 10. Perfuming.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. An impression remaining unconsciously in the mind from past actions, etc., and, by the resulting merit or demerit, producing pleasure or pain, Bhāṣāp. 162. Cf. Ballantyne, Yoga. ii. 12.<BR> 2. Trust, confidence.<BR> 3. Imagination, fancy, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 1; 219, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवासन
गो- + वासन गो- + वासन,<BR> I. adj. covered with the skin of a bull or cow, MBh. 2, 1825.<BR> II. m. a proper name, ib. 1, 3826.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वासना
दुर्वासना दुर्वासना, i. e. दुस्-, f. a bad inclination, Prab. 109, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासन|निर्वासनं|निर्व्वासन|निर्व्वासनं
निर्वासन निर्वासन, i. e. निस्-, adj. deprived of imagination, Sāh. D. 26, 7; see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासन|वनवासनः
वन- + वासन वन- + वासन, m. a polecat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छिन्नवासन
सम्-उद्-छिन्न- + वासन सम्-उद्-छिन्न- + वासन (vb. छिद्), adj. one in whom ignorance is extirpated, Prab. 50, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासनामयत्व
वासनामयत्व वासना + मय + त्व, n. State of (or consisting in) imagination, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्त|वासंत|वासन्तः
वासन्त वासन्त, i. e. वसन्त + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Vernal, growing in the spring, Man. 6, 11.<BR> 2. Young, in the spring of life.<BR> 3. Diligent in the performance of religious ceremonies.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The Indian cuckoo.<BR> 2. The southern wind.<BR> 3. Any young animal.<BR> 4. A camel.<BR> 5. A catamite.<BR> 6. The name of several [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a " target="_blank">Page0841-a + 42</a>] plants.<BR> III. f. ती.<BR> 1. The name of a deity, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 14; 46, 11.<BR> 2. A festival in honour of Kāma.<BR> 3. The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तक|वासन्तकं
वासन्तक वासन्त + क, adj. Vernal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तिक|वासंतिक|वासन्तिकः
वासन्तिक वासन्तिक, i. e. वसन्त + इक,<BR> I. adj. Vernal, Śāk. 78, 18.<BR> II. m. The buffoon in a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासर|वासरं|वासरः
वासर वासर (vb. 2. वस्),<BR> I. m. and n. A day, Pañc. ii. d. 99; Kathās. 4, 23 (m.); Megh. 104 (n.).<BR> II. m. A kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासव|वासवः
वासव वासव, i. e. वसु + अ,<BR> I. m. Indra, Chr. 22, 23.<BR> II. f. वी, The mother of Vyāsa.<BR> III. adj., f. वी, Belonging to Indra, Megh. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासस्
वासस् वासस्, i. e. 3. वस् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Cloth, clothes, Hit. ii. d. 38.<BR> 2. Curtain, Rām. 1, 13, 29 (read वासोभिः).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवासस्
अधस्- + वासस् अधस्- + वासस्, and अन्तर्-, n. a lower garment, Utt. Rāmac. 106, 1; Kathās. 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवासस्
उत्तर- + वासस् उत्तर- + वासस्, n. an upper garment, Rām. 5, 18, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवासस्
एक- + वासस् एक- + वासस्, adj. wearing only a single cloth, Man. 4, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासस्
कृत्ति- + वासस् कृत्ति- + वासस्, adj. covered with a skin, MBh. 2, 1642.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरवासस्
चीर- + वासस् चीर- + वासस्,<BR> I. adj. 1. covered with a cloth made of bark, Man. 11, 101. 2. covered with rags, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरवल्कलवासस्
चीर-वल्कल- + वासस् चीर-वल्कल- + वासस्, adj. covered with a cloth made of bark, Rām. 3, 55, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवासस्|दंतवासस्
दन्त- + वासस् दन्त- + वासस् (n.), the lip, Kumāras. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वासस्
दिग्वासस् दिग्वासस्, i. e. दिश्-, adj. naked, Man. 11, 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वासस्|दुर्व्वासस्
दुर्वासस् दुर्वासस्, i. e. दुस्-, 1. adj. poorly clothed, MBh. 13, 1176. 2. a proper name, ib. 1, 2768.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवासस्
नील- + वासस् नील- + वासस्, 1. adj. covered with a blue cloth, Bhāg. P. 5, 25, 7. 2. m. the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवासस्
स- + वासस् स- + वासस्, adj. clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासि|वासिः
वासि वासि, f. A carpenter's adze or chisel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
वासित वासित,<BR> I. see वस्, वास्.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Sound.<BR> 2. The cry of birds.<BR> 3. Knowledge.<BR> III. f. ता.<BR> 1. A woman. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b " target="_blank">Page0841-b + 41</a>]<BR> 2. A female elephant, Johns. Sel. 12, 32; Ragh. 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
वासिन् वासिन्, adj., f. नी, i. e.<BR> I. 1. वस् + इन्, Inhabiting, Pañc. 129, 14.<BR> II. वास + इन्, Clothed, Johns. Sel. 59, 184; wearing clothes, Rām. 3, 52, 19; 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवासिन्
काम- + वासिन् काम- + वासिन्, adj. abiding where one lists, Nal. 13, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवासिन्
ग्राम- + वासिन् ग्राम- + वासिन्, adj. 1. dwelling in villages, Man. 7, 118. 2. tame, MBh. 6, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासिन्
वन- + वासिन् वन- + वासिन्,<BR> I. adj. abiding in woods, wild, Hit. 88, 7, M.M.<BR> II. m. a hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तवासिन्
सामन्त- + वासिन् सामन्त- + वासिन्, adj. bordering, neighbouring, Man. 8, 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवासिन्
सु- + वासिन् सु- + वासिन्,<BR> I. adj. dwelling comfortably.<BR> II. f. नी, a bride residing in her father's house, Man. 3, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववासिन्
स्व- + वासिन् स्व- + वासिन्, f. a woman residing in her father's house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ठ|वासिष्ठं|वासिष्ठः
वासिष्ठ वासिष्ठ, i. e. वसिष्ठ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Composed by Vasiṣṭha, Man. 11, 249.<BR> 2. Explained by Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासु|वासुः
वासु वासु, m. Viṣṇu; वासू, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकि|वासुकिः
वासुकि वासुकि, m. The serpent Vāsuki, sovereign of the snakes, Bhag. 10, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुदेव|वासुदेवः
वासुदेव वासुदेव, i. e. वसु-देव + अ, m. Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu, Johns. Sel. 55, 140; Pañc. 44, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुरा
वासुरा वासुरा, f.<BR> I. probably वास् + उ + र.<BR> 1. A woman (cf. the next).<BR> 2. A female elephant.<BR> II. (vb. 1. वस्).<BR> 1. Night.<BR> 2. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासू
वासू वासू, i. e. वास् + उ, f. A young girl, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 24; 187, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त
वास्त वास्त, i. e. वस्त + अ, adj. Made, derived, or coming, from goats, Man. 2, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव|वास्तवं
वास्तव वास्तव, and वास्तविक i. e. वस्तु + अ, or इक, adj.<BR> 1. Being anything in the true sense of the word; real, substantial.<BR> 2. Demonstrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव्य|वास्तव्यः
वास्तव्य वास्तव्य, see 1. वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तिक|वास्तिकं
वास्तिक वास्तिक, i. e. वस्त + इक, n. Goats, Rām. 2, 62, 2, ed. Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तु
वास्तु वास्तु (vb. 1. वस्), m. and n.<BR> 1. The site of a building, a building-place.<BR> 2. Ground, Man. 3, 255.<BR> 3. A house.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवास्तु
पुर- + वास्तु पुर- + वास्तु, n. a ground fit for building a town, Hariv. 6409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवास्तु
पृष्ठ- + वास्तु पृष्ठ- + वास्तु, n. the upper room of a building, Man. 3, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुक|वास्तुकं
वास्तुक and वास्तूक वास्तू̆क, n. A potherb, Lass. 79, 14 (ऊ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तोस्पति
वास्तोस्पति वास्तोस्पति (वास्तोस्, gen. of वास्तु), m. The deity of the house (Man. 3, 89), a name of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त्र|वास्त्रः
वास्त्र वास्त्र, i. e. वस्त्र + अ, adj. Covered with cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्प|वास्पः
वास्प वास्प, see वाष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्
वाह् वाह् (akin to वह्), † बाह् बह्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry, Par., MBh. 1, 6639), To endeavour.<BR> --Caus. वाहय, To employ, Man. 3, 68; 4, 86.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वाहित, Mystified, Pañc. 64, 7.<BR> --With the prep. सम् सम्, To stroke, MBh. 3, 11005.<BR> --Caus. The same, Śāk. d. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह|वाहः
वाह वाह, i. e. वह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Carrying, Hit. 81, 12 (अति-भार-, carrying too heavy burthens).<BR> 2. A vehicle, a conveyance of any kind, a car, Arj. 1, 1.<BR> 3. A horse, Arj. 4, 12.<BR> 4. A carrier of burthens.<BR> 5. The arm.<BR> 6. A bull.<BR> 7. A buffalo.<BR> 8. Air, wind.<BR> 9. A measure of capacity, nearly equal to a ton in freight.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाह|अम्बुवाहः
अम्बु- + वाह अम्बु- + वाह, m. a cloud, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवाह|गंधवाह|गन्धवाहः
गन्ध- + वाह गन्ध- + वाह, m. the wind, Gīt. 1, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवाह|जलवाहः
जल- + वाह जल- + वाह,<BR> I. adj. carrying water, MBh. 2, 301.<BR> II. m. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवाह|पुरुषवाहः
पुरुष- + वाह पुरुष- + वाह, m. Garuḍa, the vehicle of Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 5, 24, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाह|भारवाहः
भार- + वाह भार- + वाह, m. a porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वाह|मरुद्वाहः
मरुद्वाह मरुद्वाह, i. e. मरुत्-, m. smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह|राजवाहः
राजवाह राजवाह, i. e. राजन्-, m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवाह|वायुवाहः
वायु- + वाह वायु- + वाह, m. smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवाह|वारिवाहः
वारि- + वाह वारि- + वाह, m. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवाह|शुकवाहः
शुक- + वाह शुक- + वाह, m. Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाह|साधुवाहः
साधु- + वाह साधु- + वाह, m. a well-trained horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवाह|सार्थवाहः
सार्थ- + वाह सार्थ- + वाह, m. 1. the leader of a caravan, Pañc. 9, 1. 2. a great merchant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-b " target="_blank">Page0842-b + 44</a>] Mṛcch. 2, 3. 3. a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0842-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाह|स्कंधवाह|स्कन्धवाहः
