सु- + विध सु- + विध,<BR> I. adj. 1. of a good kind. 2. in a good or easy way.<BR> II. ˚धम्, adv. easily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0856-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
विधातृ वि-धा + तृ, m., properly, Ruler.<BR> 1. Fate, Pañc. 138, 23.<BR> 2. Brahman, Lass. 91, 13; Bhartṛ. 2, 7. 15 (or fate).<BR> 3. Kāma.<BR> 4. A maker, Mālat. 18, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतविधातृ
अनागत- + विधातृ अनागत- + विधातृ, m. 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a " target="_blank">Page0857-a + 45</a>] a cautious person. 2. the proper name of a fish, Pañc. 77, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0856-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधान|विधानं
विधान विधान, i. e. वि-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sending, ordering, arrangement, creation, Man. 1, 3; Ragh. 6, 11; disposition, Chr. 15, 6; Johns. Sel. 8, 5 (dat. in the sense of the infin.).<BR> 2. Ordinance, Ragh. 8, 40; rule, precept, regulation, Man. 1, 112; 115.<BR> 3. Form, mode, Sund. 1, 22; 26; manner.<BR> 4. Action, especially the performance of religious acts, Chr. 56, 17.<BR> 5. Worship.<BR> 6. Ceremony, Man. 3, 67.<BR> 7. Means, expedient, Pañc. 258, 11.<BR> 8. Gaining.<BR> 9. Wealth.<BR> 10. Act of hostility.<BR> 11. Conflict of opposite feelings.<BR> 12. An elephant's fodder.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविधान
तथा- + विधान तथा- + विधान, adj. following this mode, in this manner, Hit. 101, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवद्विधान
पुंवत्- + विधान पुंवत्- + विधान, n. ceremonies as on the birth of a male, Chr. 51, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायिन्
विधायिन् विधायिन्, i. e. वि-धा + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Establishing a rule or law, Lass. 2. ed. 89, 30.<BR> 2. Placing, Rājat. 5, 295; fixing, securing.<BR> 3. Building, Rājat. 5, 37.<BR> 4. Causing, making, ib. 5, 255.<BR> 5. Delivering, entrusting.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविधायिन्
भय- + विधायिन् भय- + विधायिन्, adj. alarming, fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधि|विधिः
विधि विधि, i. e. वि-धा (cf. निधि), m.<BR> 1. Order, injunction, command, Bhāg. P. 8, 20, 27; Pañc. iii. d. 238 (दैव-, When destiny commands).<BR> 2. Rule, Pañc. 117, 11; precept, Hit. i. d. 167, M.M.; 89, 6 (न विधिः, Is not prescribed, cf. Hit. 94, 3; not just).<BR> 3. A sacred precept.<BR> 4. Ceremony, Man. 2, 67; Pañc. 158, 5.<BR> 5. A text prescribing any particular act.<BR> 6. A sacred work.<BR> 7. Fate, Pañc. ii. d. 20.<BR> 8. Creator, Brahmav. 2, 94; Brahman.<BR> 9. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR> 10. Time.<BR> 11. Kind, sort, manner, Pañc. 138, 15; Vikr. d. 72 (को यं विधिः, How comes that to pass?).<BR> 12. Act, action, Śiś. 9, 78; Pañc. 260, 17; Vikr. d. 9; creation, Kir. 7, 7.<BR> 13. Behaviour, life, Man. 2, 16.<BR> 14. Food [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b " target="_blank">Page0857-b + 43</a>] for horses, elephants, etc.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधि|अविधिः
अ- + विधि अ- + विधि, m. wrong way; instr. unjustly, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मविधि|कर्म्मविधि
कर्मविधि कर्मविधि, i. e. कर्मन्-, m. rule of action, Man. 9, 325.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाविधि|क्रियाविधिः
क्रिया- + विधि क्रिया- + विधि, m. rule of conduct, Man. 12, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मविधि
छद्म-विधि छद्म-विधि, i. e. छद्मन्-, m. disguise, Utt. Rāmac. 17, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विधि
दुस्- + विधि दुस्- + विधि, m. ill fate, Kathās. 21, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवविधि|परिभवविधिः
परिभव- + विधि परिभव- + विधि, m. humiliation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविधि|प्रसाधनविधिः
प्रसाधन- + विधि प्रसाधन- + विधि, m. embellishing, Vikr. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तविधि
प्रायश्चित्त- + विधि प्रायश्चित्त- + विधि, m. rules for penance, Man. 1, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवद्विधि
भवद्विधि भवद्विधि, i. e. भवन्त्-, adj. thy manner (i. e. the same manner in which you are treated), Pañc. 215, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदविधि|भेदविधिः
भेद- + विधि भेद- + विधि, m. separation, Bhartṛ. 2, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलविधि|मंगलविधि|मङ्गलविधिः
मङ्गल- + विधि मङ्गल- + विधि, m. the ceremony of oblations, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाविधि
यथा- + विधि यथा- + विधि, adv. according to rule, Pañc. iii. d. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविधि|विशेषविधिः
विशेष- + विधि विशेष- + विधि, m. 1. special rule or observance. 2. special form, Hit. 117, 19 (of a treaty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारविधि|शृंगारविधि|शृङ्गारविधिः
शृङ्गार- + विधि शृङ्गार- + विधि, m. dress fit for amorous interviews, Pañc. 35, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिज्ञ|विधिज्ञः
विधिज्ञ विधि-ज्ञ, adj. Knowing the rules, Pañc. ii. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधितस्
विधितस् विधि + तस्, adv. According to rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
विधित्सा विधित्सा, i. e. वि-धित्स, desider. of धा, + अ, f. Wish to do, desire, MBh. 12, 6603; design.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विधित्स
निर्-विधित्स निर्-विधित्स, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from desire, MBh. 3, 13953.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सु
विधित्सु विधित्सु, i. e. वि-धित्स (see the last), + उ, adj. Wishing to do or make, Kir. 10, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवत्
विधिवत् विधि + वत्, adv. Agreeably to rule, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 10; Pañc. i. d. 347.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधु|विधुः
विधु विधु, m.<BR> 1. The moon, Man. 3, 127.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu.<BR> 3. Brahman.<BR> 4. A Rākṣasa.<BR> 5. An expiatory oblation.<BR> 6. Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुति|विधुतिः
विधुति वि-धु + ति, f. Shaking, trembling, trepidation, Mālat. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुंतुद|विधुन्तुद|विधुंतुदः|विधुन्तुदः
विधुंतुद विधुंतुद, i. e. विधु + म्-तुद् + अ, m. Rāhu, the personified ascending node, Pañc. i. d. 370.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर विधुर, i. e. व्यध् + उर,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Trembling, Śiś. 9, 77; agitated, Bhartṛ. 1, 37.<BR> 2. Bewildered, Utt. Rāmac. 78, 1.<BR> 3. Adverse, Pañc. 42, 13; i. d. 220.<BR> 4. Separate from a mistress or lover, abandoned, Nalod. 3, 50; Megh. 113; Vikr. d. 102.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Agitation of mind.<BR> 2. Danger, Hit. 50, 8.<BR> 3. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरता
विधुरता विधुर + ता, f. Trembling, agitation, Lass. 72, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवन|विधुवनं
विधुवन विधुवन, i. e. वि-धू + अन, n. Trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूति|विधूतिः
विधूति वि-धू + ति, f.<BR> 1. Shaking.<BR> 2. Agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनन|विधूननं
विधूनन विधूनन, i. e. वि-धू, Caus., + अन, Shaking (rather causing to shake).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयज्ञ
विधेयज्ञ वि-धेय-ज्ञ (vb. धा), adj. One who knows what must be done, Pañc. i. d. 383.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयता
विधेयता वि-धेय + ता (vb. धा), f.<BR> 1. Necessary or proper act or conduct.<BR> 2. Fitness for enactment as a rule.<BR> 3. Submission, Kir. 11, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस|विध्वंसः
विध्वंस वि-ध्वंस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Aversion.<BR> 2. Disrespect.<BR> 3. Offence, Kir. 3, 16.<BR> 4. Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
विध्वंसिन् वि-ध्वंस् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Falling asunder, Hit. i. d. 48, M.M.<BR> 2. Destroying.<BR> 3. Hostile.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविध्वंसिन्
अ- + विध्वंसिन् अ- + विध्वंसिन्, adj. not laying aside, Dev. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद|विनदः
विनद वि-नद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sound, noise.<BR> 2. A tree, Echites scholaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदिन्
विनदिन् वि-नद् + इन्, adj. Roaring, grumbling, Johns. Sel. 91, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय विनय, i. e. वि-नी + अ, m.<BR> 1. Training, discipline, Ragh. 10, 80.<BR> 2. Good behaviour, Pañc. iii. d. 122.<BR> 3. Behaviour, Utt. Rāmac. 109, 6.<BR> 4. Reverence, Lass. 2. ed. 35, 11.<BR> 5. Modesty, Pañc. i. d. 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनय|अविनयः
अ- + विनय अ- + विनय, m. 1. want of modesty or propriety of conduct, Man. 7, 40. 2. wrong behaviour, Hit. ii. d. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विनय|दुर्विनयः
दुस्- + विनय दुस्- + विनय, m. improper conduct, Pañc. 259, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
स- + विनय स- + विनय, adj. well-behaved, modest, Ṛt. 6, 21. ˚यम्-, adv. humbly, modestly, Pañc. 47, 1; Vikr. 86, 10; graciously, Hit. 12, 2, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयन|विनयनं
विनयन विनयन, i. e. वि-नी + अन,<BR> I. adj. Removing, Megh. 53.<BR> II. n. Instruction, accomplishment, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयवन्त्|विनयवत्
विनयवन्त् विनय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Modest, well-behaved.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनयवन्त्
अ- + विनयवन्त् अ- + विनयवन्त्, adj. ill-behaved, Lass. 31, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशन|विनशनं|विनशनः
विनशन वि-नश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Destroying, destruction.<BR> 2. The name of a country, Man. 2, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्वर
विनश्वर वि-नश् + वर, adj. Perishable, Hit. i. d. 46, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना विना (from वि), prep. Without, Pañc. i. d. 131; except (with acc., instr., and abl.), Vikr. d. 10; Hit. pr. d. 32, M.M.; Pañc. 250, 5; iii. d. 34 (न यानं विना प्र शस्यते, Nothing but, i. e. only, marching is recommended).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायक|विनायकः
विनायक विनायक, i. e. वि-नी + अक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A spiritual teacher.<BR> 2. Gaṇeśa, Lass. 1, 1.<BR> 3. Garuḍa.<BR> 4. An obstacle.<BR> II. f. यिका, The wife of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाश|विनाशः
विनाश विनाश, i. e. वि-नश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Perdition, Man. 3, 179; ruin, destruction, Pañc. 162, 12; death, Pañc. 175, 3; 184, 9 (with उप या, To die).<BR> 2. Removal, Pañc. 187, 7; disappearance; with अभि-इ, To disappear, Pañc. v. d. 66.<BR> 3. Loss, Vikr. d. 85; Pañc. 145, 15. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a " target="_blank">Page0859-a + 40</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाश|अविनाशः
अ- + विनाश अ- + विनाश, m. deliverance from ruin, Chr. 56, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशक|विनाशकः
विनाशक विनाशक, i. e. वि-नश्, Caus., + अक, adj. sbst. Destroying, a destroyer, Lass. 4, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशन|विनाशनं|विनाशनः
विनाशन विनाशन, i. e. वि-नश्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. m. A destroyer, Nal. 12, 30 (at the end of a comp.).<BR> II. n. Destruction, Chr. 56, 19; Rām. 4, 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशिन्
विनाशिन् विनाशिन्, i. e. वि-नश् and विनाश, + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Destroying, destructive.<BR> 2. Perishing, Hit. iv. d. 126.<BR> 3. Undergoing transformation, Man. 1, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाशिन्
अ- + विनाशिन् अ- + विनाशिन्, adj. imperishable, Bhag. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाह|विनाहः
विनाह and वीनाह वी̆नाह, i. e. वि-नह् + अ, m. The top or cover of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह|विनिग्रहः
विनिग्रह वि-नि-ग्रह् + अ, m. Restraining, subduing, Bhag. 13, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्रत्व|विनिद्रत्वं
विनिद्रत्व वि-निद्र + त्व (निद्रा), n. Waking, vigilance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपात|विनिपातः
विनिपात विनिपात, i. e. वि-नि-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Falling, Bhartṛ. 2, 10; falling down, Pañc. 203, 2.<BR> 2. Ruin, Śāk. 70, 1.<BR> 3. Calamity, Man. 4, 146.<BR> 4. Death, Man. 8, 185.<BR> 5. Pain.<BR> 6. Disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमय|विनिमयः
विनिमय विनिमय, i. e. वि-नि-मे + अ, m.<BR> 1. Barter, exchange, Mālav. d. 31; instr. alternately, Ragh. 1, 26.<BR> 2. A pledge, a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमेष|विनिमेषः
विनिमेष विनिमेष, i. e. वि-नि-मिष् + अ, m. A wink, sign, Kir. 12, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोग|विनियोगः
विनियोग विनियोग, i. e. वि-नि-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation.<BR> 2. Abandoning, Hit. 99, 13.<BR> 3. Parting with anything in expectation of some advantage.<BR> 4. Appointment to any office.<BR> 5. Application to, or employment in, Hit. 98, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जय|विनिर्जयः
विनिर्जय विनिर्जय, i. e. वि-निस्-जि + अ, m. Victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णय|विनिर्णयः
विनिर्णय विनिर्णय, i. e. वि-निस्-नि + अ,<BR> 1. Ascertainment, Kir. 2, 12.<BR> 2. Settling, Man. 8, 300.<BR> 3. Decision, 1, 114.<BR> 4. A rule, 5, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्बन्ध|विनिर्बंध|विनिर्बंधः|विनिर्बन्धः
विनिर्बन्ध विनिर्बन्ध, i. e. वि-निस्-बन्ध् + अ, m. Pertinacious pursuit, Lass. 2. ed. 77, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्ति|विनिवृत्तिः
विनिवृत्ति वि-नि-वृत् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Stop, stopping, Man. 8, 368.<BR> 2. Abstaining, Pañc. MS. Berol. 149, b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवेश|विनिवेशः
विनिवेश विनिवेश, i. e. वि-नि-विश् + अ, m. An impression, Śāk. d. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चय|विनिश्चयः
विनिश्चय विनिश्चय, i. e. वि-निस्-चि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Decision, Chr. 15, 6; resolution, Sāv. 3, 10.<BR> 2. Certainty, Chr. 17, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापविनिश्चय
पाप- + विनिश्चय पाप- + विनिश्चय, adj. intending evil, Rām. 6, 81, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्मार्थविनिश्चय
स्व-धर्म-अर्थ- + विनिश्चय स्व-धर्म-अर्थ- + विनिश्चय, m. certainty concerning the objects of one's duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतत्व
विनीतत्व वि-नीत + त्व (vb. नी), n. Modesty, Hit. i. d. 118, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
विनेतृ विनेतृ, i. e. वि-नी + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A guide.<BR> 2. A teacher.<BR> 3. A ruler.<BR> 4. A chastiser, Rām. 3, 55, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोद|विनोदः
विनोद विनोद, i. e. वि-नुद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dismissing, removing, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 10; Śāk. 13, 3 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 2. Play, pastime, entertainment, Hit. 13, 7, M.M.; Lass. 5, 15; sport, Pañc. 5, 6 (सरस्वती-, The sport of the goddess of eloquence, i. e. literary practice).<BR> 3. Pleasure, Pañc. 147, 14; happiness, Śāk. 86, 17.<BR> 4. Interest, interesting pursuit, Vikr. d. 45.<BR> 5. Eagerness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विनोद
निस्- + विनोद निस्- + विनोद, adj. without pastime, Megh. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपनविनोद|विलपनविनोदः
विलपन- + विनोद विलपन- + विनोद, m. removing (viz. grief), by lamenting, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदन|विनोदनं
विनोदन विनोदन, i. e. वि-नुद् + अन, n. Play, pastime, enjoyment, Vikr. d. 38; Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदिन्
विनोदिन् विनोदिन्, i. e. वि-नुद् + इन्, adj. Removing, Śāk. d. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दु|विंदु|विन्दुः
विन्दु विन्दु,<BR> I. i. e. विद् + उ, adj.<BR> 1. Intelligent.<BR> 2. Liberal.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A drop of any liquid, Pañc. 123, 14; Vikr. d. 80.<BR> 2. A drop of water, taken as a measure.<BR> 3. A spot.<BR> 4. The bite or mark of a tooth.<BR> 5. A mark of coloured paint on an elephant's face or trunk.<BR> 6. A dot over a letter representing the अनुस्वार.<BR> 7. The part of the forehead between the eyebrows.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णविन्दु
सुवर्ण- + विन्दु सुवर्ण- + विन्दु (m.), Viṣṇu, Mālat. 166, 16; the name of a holy place, Mālat. 145, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यविन्दु
हिरण्य- + विन्दु हिरण्य- + विन्दु, m. fire, MBh. 13, 1697.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्य|विंध्यः|विन्ध्यः
विन्ध्य विन्ध्य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a mountainous range, Hit. 75, 11, M.M.<BR> 2. A hunter.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. Small cardamoms.<BR> 2. A fruit, Annona reticulata.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विन्ध्य
निस्- + विन्ध्य निस्- + विन्ध्य, f. या, the name of a river, Megh. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्नप
विन्नप विन्नप, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यास|विन्यासः
विन्यास विन्यास, i. e. वि-नि-अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Entrusting.<BR> 2. A deposit.<BR> 3. Orderly arrangement, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 38.<BR> 4. Assemblage, collection.<BR> 5. Site, place.<BR> 6. Receptacle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरविन्यास|अक्षरविन्यासः
अक्षर- + विन्यास अक्षर- + विन्यास, m. writing, writ, Vikr. 25, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् विप्, † व्यप् व्यप्, i. 10, Par. To throw.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, To spend, Pañc. MS. Berol. 4, b (प्रवेप्यमानो, v. r. of प्रवेश्यमानो, Kos. ed. orn. 3, 14; cf. Götting. Gel. Anz. 1862, p. 1362).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
विपक्त्रिम विपक्त्रिम, i. e. वि-पच् + तृ + इम, adj.<BR> 1. Ripened, Bhaṭṭ. 1, 10.<BR> 2. Fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षतस्
विपक्षतस् वि-पक्ष + तस्, adv. Inimically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षता
विपक्षता वि-पक्ष + ता, f.<BR> 1. Hostility.<BR> 2. Opposition.<BR> 3. Contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण|विपणः
विपण वि-पण् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sale, Sund. 2, 23.<BR> 2. Low traffic, Man. 3, 152; 10, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणि|विपणिः
विपणि वि-पण् + इ, (m. and) f., and णी, f.<BR> 1. A shop.<BR> 2. A market, Mālav. 24, 21.<BR> 3. The street of a market.<BR> 4. An article for sale.<BR> 5. Traffic, Hariv. 3809.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्ति|विपत्तिः
विपत्ति वि-पत्ति, i. e. वि-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Misfortune, Pañc. iii. d. 77.<BR> 2. Failing, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 263.<BR> 3. Pain.<BR> 4. Death, Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् वि-पद्, and विपदा वि-पद् + आ, f. Calamity, misfortune, Pañc. i. d. 418 (˚पद्); Ragh. 18, 34 (˚पद्, death).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणाम|विपरिणामः
विपरिणाम विपरिणाम, i. e. वि-परि-नम् + अ, m. Change of state or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामिन्
विपरिणामिन् विपरिणामिन्, i. e. वि-परि-नम् + इन्, adj. Undergoing or producing change of state or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तन|विपरिवर्तनं|विपरिवर्त्तन
विपरिवर्तन विपरिवर्तन, i. e. वि-परि-वृत् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Causing to return, Kathās. 46, 121 (with विद्या, a magical knowledge producing that effect).<BR> II. n. Turning back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतता
विपरीतता विपरीतता, i. e. वि-परि-इत + ता, f.<BR> 1. Reverse, that which is contrary, opposite to something, counterpart, Hit. ii. d. 43.<BR> 2. Contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यय|विपर्ययः|विपर्य्यय|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्यय विपर्यय, i. e. वि-परि-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Change, Pañc. 37, 3.<BR> 2. A morbid change, Man. 11, 48; failure of conception, 3, 49; cf. Rām. 1, 47, 3.<BR> 3. Reverse, that which is contrary, opposite to something, Man. 4, 12; Kir. 11, 44; loc. ये, On the contrary, Rām. 2, 26, 34.<BR> 4. Error.<BR> 5. Trespass, Man. 8, 249.<BR> 6. Overthrow, Man. 4, 171.<BR> 7. Opposition, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 12; contrariety.<BR> 8. Perverseness of disposition.<BR> 9. Hostility.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मविपर्यय|कर्म्मविपर्य्यय
कर्मविपर्यय कर्मविपर्यय, i. e. कर्मन्-, m. wrong [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a " target="_blank">Page0861-a + 43</a>] doing, Hit. ii. d. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्यविपर्यय
भाग्य- + विपर्यय भाग्य- + विपर्यय, and विधि-, m. misfortune, Vikr. 63, 19; 69, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यास|विपर्यासः|विपर्य्यास|विपर्य्यासः
विपर्यास विपर्यास, i. e. वि-परि-अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Reverse (cf. the two last), Utt. Rāmac. 96, 15; interchange, ib. 47, 6 (घन-विरल-भावः क्षितिरुहां यातो विपर्यासम्, As for the trees, their state of being close together, or scanty, has interchanged, i. e. where there were before plenty of trees, there are at present few, and vice versā).<BR> 2. Error, mistake, Bhāṣāp. 136; Pañc. 129, 5.<BR> 3. Investing imaginary things with real attributes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित् विपश्चित्, m. A learned man; prudent, wise, Pañc. i. d. 308; Hit. iii. d. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाक|विपाकः
विपाक विपाक, i. e. वि-पच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Cooking.<BR> 2. Ripening, Kir. 4, 26; taking place, Utt. Rāmac. 52, 5.<BR> 3. The consequence of actions, Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR> 4. Unexpected or improbable result.<BR> 5. Distress, Utt. Rāmac. 96, 14.<BR> 6. Change of form or state.<BR> 7. Flavour, taste, MBh. 1, 716.<BR> 8. Digestion.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाकः
कर्मविपाक कर्मविपाक, i. e. कर्मन्-, m. the ripening of actions, retribution, MBh. 4, 1405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविपाक|दशाविपाकः
दशा- + विपाक दशा- + विपाक, m. state, Mālat. 149, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विपाक|दुर्विपाकः
दुस्- + विपाक दुस्- + विपाक, adj. turning out destructive, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदुर्विपाक|दैवदुर्विपाकः
दैव-दुस्- + विपाक दैव-दुस्- + विपाक, m. cruelty (literally, the hard ripening) of fate, Utt. Rāmac. 164, 4; Hit. 18, 7; Utt. Rāmac. 27, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकिन्
विपाकिन् विपाकिन्, i. e. विपाक + इन्, adj. Followed, Mālat. 83, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटन|विपाटनं
विपाटन विपाटन, i. e. वि-पट् + अन, n. Spoliation, Rājat. 5, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठ|विपाठः
विपाठ विपाठ, m. An arrow, MBh. 4, 168; 5, 1865.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका विपादिका (akin to पाद), f.<BR> 1. A blister on the foot.<BR> 2. A riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश् विपाश् (curtailed विपाशा), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b " target="_blank">Page0861-b + 40</a>] and विपाशा विपाशा, i. e. वि-पाश, f. The name of a river, MBh. 1, 6750 (शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिन|विपिनं
विपिन विपिन, n. A thicket, a forest, Lass. 2. ed. 41, 4; a grove, Vikr. 57, 18; Ragh. 4, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविपिन
अति- + विपिन अति- + विपिन, adj. very impenetrable, Kir. 5, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल विपुल (cf. पुल्),<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Large, great, Pañc. i. d. 18; v. d. 5; Bhartṛ. 2, 91. 99; Rām. 3, 54, 28.<BR> 2. Broad.<BR> 3. Deep.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The mountain Meru.<BR> 2. The Himālaya mountain.<BR> 3. A respectable man.<BR> III. f. ला, The earth.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविपुल
सु- + विपुल सु- + विपुल, adj. very spacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलता
विपुलता विपुल + ता, f. Magnitude, Śāk. d. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्र|विप्रः
विप्र विप्र, m.<BR> 1. A poet, or singer of vedic hymns, Chr. 292, 11 and 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 11; 86, 3.<BR> 2. A Brāhmaṇa, a priest, Kathās. 4, 110; Pañc. 158, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकर्ष|विप्रकर्षः
विप्रकर्ष विप्रकर्ष, i. e. वि-प्र-कृष् + अ, m. Distance, Vikr. 66, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकार|विप्रकारः
विप्रकार विप्रकार, i. e. वि-प्र-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Opposition.<BR> 2. Retaliation.<BR> 3. Injury, abuse, Kir. 3, 55.<BR> 4. Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारिन्
विप्रकारिन् विप्रकारिन्, i. e. वि-प्र-कृ + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> 1. Opposing.<BR> 2. Retaliating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृति|विप्रकृतिः
विप्रकृति वि-प्र-कृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Retaliation.<BR> 2. Abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकार|विप्रतिकारः
विप्रतिकार विप्रतिकार, i. e. वि-प्रति-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Opposition.<BR> 2. Reverse.<BR> 3. Contradiction.<BR> 4. Retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्ति|विप्रतिपत्तिः
विप्रतिपत्ति विप्रतिपत्ति, i. e. वि-प्रति-पद् + ति, and वि-प्रतिपत्ति, f.<BR> 1. Mutual connexion with.<BR> 2. Conversancy.<BR> 3. Perplexity.<BR> 4. Various acquirements.<BR> 5. Difference.<BR> 6. Opposition of interests. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a " target="_blank">Page0862-a + 41</a>]<BR> 7. Contest, dispute, Windischmann, Sancara, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसार|विप्रतीसारः
विप्रतीसार विप्रतीसार, i. e. वि-प्रति-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Enmity, hate.<BR> 2. Rage.<BR> 3. Wickedness, evil action.<BR> 4. (also विप्रतिसार विप्रतिसार), Repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोग|विप्रयोगः
विप्रयोग विप्रयोग, i. e. वि-प्र-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation, Man. 9, 1; Pañc. ii. d. 184.<BR> 2. Disunion.<BR> 3. Quarrel.<BR> 4. Deserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलंभः|विप्रलम्भः
विप्रलम्भ विप्रलम्भ, i. e. वि-प्र-लभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Deceiving, deceit, Ragh. 19, 18; Utt. Rāmac. 82, 12; Daśak. in Chr. 182, 14; 185, 9.<BR> 2. Separation, Utt. Rāmac. 82, 7 (अति-भूमि-गत-, adj. Whose separation has reached the highest degree, i. e. who has suffered an exceedingly sorrowful separation).<BR> 3. Disunion.<BR> 4. Quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भन|विप्रलंभनं
विप्रलम्भन विप्रलम्भन, i. e. वि-प्र-लभ् + अन, n. Deception, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भिन्
विप्रलम्भिन् विप्रलम्भिन्, i. e. वि-प्र-लभ् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Deceiving, fallacious, Pañc. 203, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलय|विप्रलयः
विप्रलय विप्रलय, i. e. वि-प्र-ली + अ, m. Dissolution, annihilation, Utt. Rāmac. 143, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलाप|विप्रलापः
विप्रलाप विप्रलाप, i. e. वि-प्र-लप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Idle discourse, prattle.<BR> 2. Quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुम्पक
विप्रलुम्पक विप्रलुम्पक, i. e. वि-प्र-लुप् + अक, adj. Rapacious, Man. 8, 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवास|विप्रवासः
विप्रवास विप्रवास, i. e. वि-प्र-वस् + अ, m. Staying abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासन|विप्रवासनं
विप्रवासन विप्रवासन, i. e. वि-प्र-वस्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Banishment.<BR> 2. Residence abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका विप्रश्निका, i. e. वि-प्रश्न + क, f. A female fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष् वि-प्रुष्, f. A drop (of any fluid), Man. 5, 133; Pañc. 79, 16 (see my transl. n. 383).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्मन्त्|विप्रुष्मत्
विप्रुष्मन्त् विप्रुष् + मन्त् (against grammar), adj., f. मती, Filled with drops, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लव|विप्लवः
विप्लव विप्लव, i. e. वि-प्लु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Spreading; with गम्, To become known, Pañc. iii. d. 258.<BR> 2. Perplexity.<BR> 3. Calamity, disaster, Man. 8, 348.<BR> 4. Tumult, trouble, Hit. i. d. 72, M.M.<BR> 5. Predatory warfare.<BR> 6. Rapine, extortion.<BR> 7. Affray, scuffle, Rājat. 5, 420 (disturbance).<BR> 8. Terrifying an enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR> 9. Sin, wickedness, Rājat. 5, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणविप्लव|प्राणविप्लवः
प्राण- + विप्लव प्राण- + विप्लव, adj. depriving of life, Bhāg. P. 1, 18, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लवतस्
विप्लवतस् विप्लव + तस्, adv. In consequence of the calamity or disturbance; Rājat. 5, 471.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव|विप्लावः
विप्लाव विप्लाव, i. e. वि-प्लु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Inundating.<BR> 2. Devastating.<BR> 3. Causing disturbance.<BR> 4. A horse's gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलता
विफलता वि-फल + ता, f., and विफलत्व वि-फल + त्व, n. Fruitlessness, Śiś. 9, 6 (त्व); Pañc. 244, 8 (˚तां नी, To make fruitless).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्धन
विबन्धन वि-बन्ध् + अन, in परस्पर-, adj. Depending on each other, Pañc. i. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध|विबुधः
विबुध वि-बुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A god, Man. 12, 47.<BR> 2. A learned, a wise man, Pañc. ii. d. 47 (adj.); ii. d. 182.<BR> 3. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्ति|विभक्तिः
विभक्ति विभक्ति, i. e. वि-भज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. A partition, division, Man. 1, 24. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a " target="_blank">Page0863-a + 42</a>]<BR> 2. Part.<BR> 3. Inheritance.<BR> 4. An affix of declension, Pāṇ. i. 4, 104; v. 3, 1, sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभंगः|विभङ्गः
विभङ्ग विभङ्ग, i. e. वि-भञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Breaking.<BR> 2. Fracture.<BR> 3. Stopping, Bhartṛ. 2, 60.<BR> 4. Bending, contracting (especially of the eyebrows).<BR> 5. Expression of features.<BR> 6. Division.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाविभङ्ग
आशा- + विभङ्ग आशा- + विभङ्ग, adj. (with broken hope), hopeless, Hit. i. d. 189, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभव|विभवः
विभव विभव, i. e. वि-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Power, Bhartṛ. 2, 49.<BR> 2. Supreme or superhuman power, Kir. 5, 21.<BR> 3. Wealth, Pañc. iii. d. 96.<BR> 4. Property.<BR> 5. Substance.<BR> 6. Thing, Pañc. iii. d. 167.<BR> 7. Magnanimity.<BR> 8. Emancipation from existence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितविभव
गलित- + विभव गलित- + विभव, adj. one who has spent his fortune (अर्थिषु, on the poor), Bhartṛ. 2, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभवतस्
विभवतस् विभव + तस्, adj. Agreeably to one's power or rank, to the royal majesty, Mālav. 19, 1; Vikr. 30, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा वि-भा, f.<BR> 1. Light.<BR> 2. Lustre, Nalod. 1, 48.<BR> 3. Beauty.<BR> 4. A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाकर|विभाकरः
विभाकर विभा-कर, m.<BR> 1. The sun, Sāh. Darp. p. 312, 2.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाग|विभागः
विभाग विभाग, i. e. वि-भज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dividing, Bhāṣāp. 3; division, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 23; Hit. 119, 18; arrangement, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 15.<BR> 2. Part, Pañc. 243, 20; 241, 7.<BR> 3. Distribution, Rājat. 5, 111.<BR> 4. Partition of inheritance, Man. 1, 115.<BR> 5. The share or portion of inheritance.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभाग
दिग्विभाग दिग्वि˚, i. e. दिश्-, m. a quarter of the compass, direction, Vikr. 5, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागतस्
विभागतस् विभाग + तस्, adv. Proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागशस्
विभागशस् विभाग + शस्, adv. Proportionately, part for part, Man. 12, 17; Bhag. 4, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव|विभावः
विभाव विभाव, i. e. वि-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. An acquaintance.<BR> 2. An excitant of the sentiments of poetical composition, Sāh. Darp. p. 31.<BR> 3. The affections or sentiments, as love, Sch. ad Nalod. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
विभावक विभावक, i. e. वि-भू, Caus., + अक, adj. Discussing, illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन्
विभावन्<BR> I. विभा + वन्, adj., f. वरी, Shining, 287, 1 = Rigv. i. 48, 1; Chr. 295, 14 = Rigv. i. 92, 14.<BR> II. वि-भा + वन्, f. वरी.<BR> 1. Night, Rām. 2, 84, 18.<BR> 2. A harlot.<BR> 3. A bawd.<BR> 4. Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन|विभावनं
विभावन विभावन, i. e. वि-भू + अन, n.<BR> 1. Discussion.<BR> 2. Ascertaining, Vikr. 78, 10 (reading).<BR> 3. Perceiving distinctly, Man. 2, 101.<BR> 4. Conceiving, imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावरी
विभावरी विभावरी, see विभावन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाविन्
विभाविन् विभाविन्, i. e. विभाव + इन्, adj., f. नी, Exciting love, Nalod. 2, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतक|विभीतकं|विभीतकः
विभीतक वि-भीत + क (vb. भी), m., f. (की), A plant, Terminalia belerica, Lass. 52, 15 (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषण|विभीषणः
विभीषण विभीषण, i. e. वि-भी, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj. Terrific, horrible, Hiḍ. 2, 4.<BR> II. m. The brother of Rāvaṇa.<BR> III. f. णा, and n. The property of exciting fear, terrifying, a means of terrifying, Draup. 5, 10 (n.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविभीषण
सु- + विभीषण सु- + विभीषण, adj. very terrible, Rām. 3, 55, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषिका
विभीषिका विभीषिका, i. e. वि-भी, Caus., + अक, f. A means of terrifying, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 1; Pañc. 160, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
विभु विभु, i. e. वि-भू,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Omnipresent.<BR> 2. All-pervading, pervading, Bhāṣāp. 50; 93.<BR> 3. Eternal.<BR> 4. Firm, solid.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A master, a lord, Pañc. 202, 10; Chr. 33, 2; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a " target="_blank">Page0864-a + 41</a>] used particularly in addressing, Indr. 1, 39; Chr. 13, 15; 17, 27.<BR> 2. One who is able (with infin.), Kir. 5, 43.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. Brahman.<BR> 5. Viṣṇu.<BR> 6. The soul.<BR> 7. Time.<BR> 8. Space.<BR> 9. Æther.<BR> 10. A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0863-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुता
विभुता विभु + ता, f., and विभुत्व विभु + त्व, n. Power, Śāk. d. 42 (त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूति|विभूतिः
विभूति वि-भू + ति, f.<BR> 1. Power, dignity, Pañc. 203, 1.<BR> 2. Superhuman power, Hit. iii. d. 115.<BR> 3. Ashes of cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूतिमन्त्|विभूतिमत्
विभूतिमन्त् विभूति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Powerful.<BR> 2. Superhuman, Bhag. 10, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषण|विभूषणं
विभूषण विभूषण, i. e. वि-भूष् + अन, n. Ornament, decoration, Pañc. ii. d. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
विभूषा वि-भूष् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Light, lustre.<BR> 2. Ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेत्तृ
विभेत्तृ विभेत्तृ, i. e. वि-भिद् + तृ, m. A destroyer, Śāk. d. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेद|विभेदः
विभेद विभेद, i. e. वि-भिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dividing, Kir. 13, 1.<BR> 2. Breaking, violating, Hit. iv. d. 124.<BR> 3. Wounding.<BR> 4. Bewildering.<BR> 5. A separation.<BR> 6. Distinction.<BR> 7. Contradiction.<BR> 8. Enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश|विभ्रंशः
विभ्रंश वि-भ्रंश् + अ, m. A precipice, Bhāg. P. 8, 22, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशिन्
विभ्रंशिन् वि-भ्रंश् + इन्, adj. Falling, fallen, Megh. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम|विभ्रमः
विभ्रम वि-भ्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Whirling, Hit. iii. d. 140; going round, Kathās. 20, 226 (agitation); motion, Mālat. 15, 12.<BR> 2. Error, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 3 (हार-, adj. Producing the error of a necklace, i. e. like a necklace); Rājat. 5, 332 (बभ्रुः--सटा-पाटल-विभ्रमम्, Could be mistaken for [i. e. were like] [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b " target="_blank">Page0864-b + 42</a>] a Bignonia-like mane).<BR> 3. Erroneous use, Man. 7, 24.<BR> 4. Doubt.<BR> 5. Play (of the eyes), Śāk. d. 23.<BR> 6. Amorous actions, Pañc. i. d. 151; flurry, confusion, perturbation, Bhag. 2, 63.<BR> 7. Enrapture, Mālat. 155, 7.<BR> 8. Beauty, Pañc. v. d. 3; grace, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविभ्रम|चित्तविभ्रमः
चित्त- + विभ्रम चित्त- + विभ्रम, m. derangement, madness, MBh. 18, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविभ्रम|दृष्टिविभ्रमः
दृष्टि- + विभ्रम दृष्टि- + विभ्रम, m. amorous playing of the eyes, Śāk. d. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभ्रम
स- + विभ्रम स- + विभ्रम, adj. playing, looking amorously, Ṛt. 1, 12; 6, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् वि-भ्राज्, adj.<BR> 1. Shining.<BR> 2. Elegant, richly dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रांतिः|विभ्रान्तिः
विभ्रान्ति विभ्रान्ति, i. e. वि-भ्रम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Whirling, going round.<BR> 2. Hurry, precipitation.<BR> 3. Error.<BR> 4. Confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमतिता
विमतिता वि-मति + ता, f. Stupidity, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
विमनस्क वि-मनस् + क, adj. Sad, etc. = वि-मनस्, see मनस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमय|विमयः
विमय विमय, i. e. वि-मे + अ, m. Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द|विमर्दः|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
विमर्द विमर्द, i. e. वि-मृद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rubbing, Śāk. 105, 14 (rubbing against, or playing with, the young lion); Ṛt. 1, 20.<BR> 2. The trituration of perfumes.<BR> 3. Touch, contact, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 23; conjunction of the sun and moon, eclipse.<BR> 4. Destroying, Hit. 50, 18.<BR> 5. Killing.<BR> 6. War, Vikr. 87, 1; battle, Utt. Rāmac. 138, 5.<BR> 7. Weariness, Chr. 42, 13; tediousness, Mṛcch. 1, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दक|विमर्दकः|विमर्द्दकः
विमर्दक विमर्दक (vb. मृद्), m. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दन|विमर्दनं|विमर्द्दन|विमर्द्दनं
विमर्दन विमर्दन, i. e. वि-मृद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rubbing, grinding.<BR> 2. The trituration of perfumes.<BR> 3. Conjunction of the sun and moon, eclipse.<BR> 4. Destroying, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0864-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दिन्
विमर्दिन् विमर्दिन्, i. e. वि-मृद् + इन्, adj. Destroying, removing, Śāk. d. 69, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्श|विमर्शः
विमर्श विमर्श (erroneously also विमर्ष विमर्ष, e. g. Kathās. 21, 25), i. e. वि-मृश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Investigation.<BR> 2. Reasoning.<BR> 3. Discussion, hesitation, Rām. 1, 20, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विमर्श
निस्- + विमर्श निस्- + विमर्श, adj. devoid of reflection, Kathās. 15, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविमर्शम्
स-विमर्श + म् स-विमर्श + म्, adv. thoughtfully, Śāk. 58, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शन|विमर्शनं
विमर्शन विमर्शन, i. e. वि-मृश् + अन, n. Investigating, discussing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शिन्
विमर्शिन् विमर्शिन्, i. e. वि-मृश् + इन्, adj. Thinking, deliberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्ष|विमर्षः
विमर्ष विमर्ष, i. e. वि-मृष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Irritation, Chr. 60, 28.<BR> 2. Displeasure. Cf. विमर्श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलता
विमलता वि-मल + ता, f. Clearness, Chr. 35, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
विमान वि-मान, m. and n.<BR> 1. A chariot of the gods, Vikr. 4, 1; Rām. 3, 48, 6.<BR> 2. Any vehicle, Rām. 3, 54, 6.<BR> 3. A horse.<BR> 4. A palace, Megh. 64.<BR> 5. (वि-मा + अन), A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानता
विमानता विमान + ता, f. State of a chariot of the gods, Vikr. d. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
विमानना विमानना, i. e. वि-मन्, Caus., + अन, f. Contempt, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 159; Rājat. 5, 339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानस्थ
विमानस्थ विमान-स्थ, adj. Standing on a divine chariot, Pañc. iii. d. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्ग|विमार्गः
विमार्ग m.<BR> I. वि-मार्ग.<BR> 1. A bad road, Lass. 2. ed. 68, 40.<BR> 2. Evil conduct.<BR> II. i. e. वि-मृज् + अ, A broom, a brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गण|विमार्गणं
विमार्गण विमार्गण, i. e. वि-मार्ग् + अण, n. Seeking, Kir. 14, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र
विमिश्र वि-मिश्र, adj. Mixed, MBh. 1, 1139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्ति|विमुक्तिः
विमुक्ति विमुक्ति, i. e. वि-मुच् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Separation.<BR> 2. Liberation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 191; remission, Man. 11, 232.<BR> 3. Saving (one's life), Pañc. ii. d. 174.<BR> 4. Final emancipation from future existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखता
विमुखता वि-मुख + ता, f.<BR> 1. Turning away.<BR> 2. Departure.<BR> 3. Disinclination, opposition, Śāk. 66, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्ष|विमोक्षः
विमोक्ष वि-मोक्ष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Letting loose.<BR> 2. Deliverance (from embarrassment), Chr. 54, 19.<BR> 3. Dismissing unhurt, Man. 8, 316.<BR> 4. Final emancipation, Bhag. 16, 5; Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षण|विमोक्षणं
विमोक्षण विमोक्षण, i. e. वि-मोक्ष् + अन, n., and f. णा,<BR> 1. Untying, Pañc. 107, 24.<BR> 2. Liberation, release, Johns. Sel. 97, 1. 6; Pañc. ii. d. 191.<BR> 3. Abandoning, Man. 2, 243; Pañc. 74, 20 (अण्ड-, Laying eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचन|विमोचनं
विमोचन विमोचन, i. e. वि-मुच् + अन, n. Liberating, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
विमोहन विमोहन, वि-मुह् + अन, n. Seducing, confounding the mind and exciting passions, Rājat. 5, 370.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विंबः|विम्बः
विम्ब विम्ब, विम्बित विम्बित, विम्बोष्ठ विम्बोष्ठ, and विम्बौष्ठ विम्बौष्ठ; see बिम्ब्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् वियत् (perhaps वि-यम् + त्), n. Sky, heaven, Pañc. iii. d. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम|वियमः
वियम and वियाम विया̆म, i. e. वि-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Restraint.<BR> 2. Cessation.<BR> 3. Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोग|वियोगः
वियोग वियोग, i. e. वि-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation, Vikr. 29, 17 (with सह, Pañc. 30, 22).<BR> 2. Disunion.<BR> 3. Loss, Pañc. ii. d. 184; death, Hit. iv. d. 62.<BR> 4. Absence, Megh. 78.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोग|अवियोगः
अ- + वियोग अ- + वियोग, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a " target="_blank">Page0866-a + 42</a>] the not being deprived (with instr.), Daśak. in Chr. 193, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वियोग
सद्वियोग सद्वियोग, i. e. सन्त्- (vb. 1. अस्), separation from the good, Kir. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0865-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन् वियोगिन्, i. e. वियोग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Separated, Nalod. 2, 12.<BR> 2. Absent.<BR> II. m. The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ति|विरक्तिः
विरक्ति विरक्ति, i. e. वि-रञ्ज् + ति, and वि-रक्ति, f.<BR> 1. Absence of affection.<BR> 2. Aversion, Pañc. 114, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचन|विरचनं
विरचन वि-रच् + अन, n., and f. ना,<BR> 1. Making, Vikr. d. 153 (read मुक्तावली-विरचना-पुनर्-उक्तम्; cf. वच् and Böhtl. Roth. s. v. पुनरुक्त).<BR> 2. Composing.<BR> 3. Embellishing.<BR> 4. Embellishment, Mālat. 13, 20 (ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्च|विरंच|विरंचः|विरञ्चः
विरञ्च विरञ्च, and विरञ्चि विरञ्चि (perhaps वि-रच् + अ or इ, but cf. विरिञ्चन), m. Brahman. Śiś. 9, 9; MBh. 1, 1638 has विरिञ्चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरति|विरतिः
विरति विरति, i. e. वि-रम् + ति, and वि-रति, f.<BR> 1. Stop.<BR> 2. Cessation.<BR> 3. End, Bhartṛ. 1, 51.<BR> 4. Indifference, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरप्शिन्
विरप्शिन् विरप्शिन्, adj. Shaking, tossing, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम|विरमः
विरम वि-रम् + अ, m. Cessation, sunset, Śiś. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल विरल (perhaps विल + ल),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fine, delicate, thin.<BR> 2. Little, Śiś. 9, 3; few, Rājat. 5, 56.<BR> 3. Loose, relaxed, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 4.<BR> 4. Separated by an interval, wide.<BR> 5. Remote.<BR> 6. Single, Bhartṛ. 2, 33; rare, Prab. 10, 8; Pañc. i. d. 35; ˚लम्, adv. Rarely, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.<BR> II. n. Sour curds.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरल|अविरलं
अ- + विरल अ- + विरल, adj. 1. coarse. 2. uninterrupted, Utt. Rāmac. 69, 6. 3. close; ˚लम्, adv. closely, Śāk. d. 55; fast, Mālat. 60, 10. 4. dense, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 6; plentiful, Mālat. 14, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरल
प्र- + विरल प्र- + विरल, adj. 1. very rare, very scanty, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b " target="_blank">Page0866-b + 40</a>] Pañc. 182, 16; 214, 22. 2. separate, apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलित
विरलित विरलित, i. e. विरल + इत, in अ-विरलित-कपोल + म्, adv. With closely united cheeks, Utt. Rāmac. 17, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरह|विरहः
विरह वि-रह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation, Megh. 12; Rājat. 5, 373; separation from (with instr.), Man. 5, 149.<BR> 2. Absence, Bhāṣāp. 68; want, Hit. 127, 5.<BR> 3. Cessation, Vikr. d. 130.<BR> 4. Relinquishment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमविरह|प्रथमविरहः
प्रथम- + विरह प्रथम- + विरह, loc. sing. immediately after the separation, Megh. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहज
विरहज विरह-ज, adj. Produced by separation, Vikr. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन् विरहिन्, i. e. विरह + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Separate, Mālat. 144, 3.<BR> 2. Absent from<BR> II. f. इणी.<BR> 1. A woman absent from her husband or lover.<BR> 2. Wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागार्ह|विरागार्हः
विरागार्ह विरागार्ह, i. e. वि-राग-अर्ह (see राग), adj. Fit for freedom from passion, free from passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज् वि-राज्, m.<BR> 1. Splendour.<BR> 2. A man of the military class.<BR> 3. The name of the first progeny of Brahman, Man. 1, 32; 3, 195.<BR> 4. The consciousness which perceives collections or aggregates, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराट|विराटः
विराट विराट, m. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्धृ
विराद्धृ विराद्धृ, i. e. वि-राध् + तृ, m., f. ध्री, and n.<BR> 1. Thwarting, opposing.<BR> 2. Injuring.<BR> 3. Abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध|विराधः
विराध वि-राध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Prevention, opposition.<BR> 2. Vexation.<BR> 3. A Rākṣasa, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधन|विराधनं
विराधन वि-राध् + अन, n. Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराम|विरामः
विराम विराम, i. e. वि-रम् + अ, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a " target="_blank">Page0867-a + 37</a>]<BR> 1. Cessation, rest, Man. 2, 73; ˚मं या, To rest, Bhartṛ. 2, 72.<BR> 2. End, Utt. Rāmac. 63, 5.<BR> 3. Pause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0866-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराव|विरावः
विराव विराव, i. e. वि-रु + अ, m. Sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
विराविन् विराविन्, i. e. विराव + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Shouting.<BR> 2. Resounding, Rām. 1, 19, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चन|विरिंचन|विरिंचनः|विरिञ्चनः
विरिञ्चन विरिञ्चन, m. Brahman (cf. विरञ्च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्ध|विरिब्धः
विरिब्ध विरिब्ध (anomal. ptcple. pf. pass. of वि रेभ्), m. A tone, a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुक्मन्त्|विरुक्मत्
विरुक्मन्त् विरुक्मन्त्, i. e. वि-रुच् + मन्त्, adj. Splendid, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3 (मतः, acc. pl. f. ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धता
विरुद्धता वि-रुद्ध + ता (vb. रुध्), f.<BR> 1. Opposition, contrariety.<BR> 2. Enmity.<BR> 3. Incongruity, abominableness, Pañc. 260, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरुद्धता
अ- + विरुद्धता अ- + विरुद्धता, f. absence of abominableness, Pañc. 261, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपाक्ष|विरूपाक्षः
विरूपाक्ष विरूपाक्ष, i. e. वि-रूप-अक्ष, adj. Having deformed eyes; m. Śiva, Johns. Sel. 89, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेक|विरेकः
विरेक विरेक, i. e. वि-रिच् + अ, m., and विरेचन विरेचन, i. e. वि-रिच् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Purging.<BR> 2. A purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोक|विरोकं|विरोकः
विरोक विरोक, i. e. वि-रुच् + अ,<BR> I. m. A ray of light.<BR> II. n. A chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचन|विरोचनः
विरोचन विरोचन, i. e. वि-रुच् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. The moon.<BR> II. (n. ?), Light, lustre, Rājat. 5, 448.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचिष्णु
विरोचिष्णु विरोचिष्णु, i. e. वि-रुच् + इष्णु, adj.<BR> 1. Shining.<BR> 2. Illuminating, making visible, Man. 1, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध|विरोधः
विरोध विरोध, i. e. वि-रुध् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Hindrance, impediment.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b " target="_blank">Page0867-b + 43</a>] Restraint, check.<BR> 3. Opposition, Pañc. 162, 14; Chr. 56, 16; contradiction, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 18; Kusumāñj. 3, 8; i. d. 147.<BR> 4. Inconsistency (in argument).<BR> 5. Surrounding.<BR> 6. Siege, blockade.<BR> 7. Enmity, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 1; Pañc. 148, 10.<BR> 8. War.<BR> 9. Calamity.<BR> II. f. धी, Fixed rule, institute.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनविरोध|वचनविरोधः
वचन- + विरोध वचन- + विरोध, m. inconsistency of texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरोध|स्मृतिविरोधः
स्मृति- + विरोध स्मृति- + विरोध, m. 1. illegality. 2. disagreement between two or more codes of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधन|विरोधनं
विरोधन विरोधन, i. e. वि-रुध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Hindering.<BR> 2. Opposition.<BR> 3. Incongruity.<BR> 4. Blockading.<BR> 5. Provoking.<BR> 6. Encountering or defying peril.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोधन
अ- + विरोधन अ- + विरोधन, adj. useful, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
विरोधिन् विरोधिन्, i. e. वि-रुध् and विरोध, + इन्,<BR> I. adj. f. नी.<BR> 1. Obstructive.<BR> 2. Preventing, impeding, Man. 4, 17.<BR> 3. Contradictory, inconsistent, Vikr. d. 162.<BR> 4. Exclusive, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 11.<BR> 5. Besieging, blockading.<BR> 6. Quarrelsome.<BR> II. m. An enemy, Lass. 2. ed. 88, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालविरोधिन्
देश-काल- + विरोधिन् देश-काल- + विरोधिन्, adj. acting contrary to place and time, Pañc. iii. d. 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोपण|विरोपणं
विरोपण विरोपण, i. e. वि-रुह्, Caus., + अन, adj. Healing, Śāk. d. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्
† विल् विल्, i. 6, Par. To cover, to conceal.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To throw (cf. पिल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल|विलं|विलः
विल विल, or बिल,<BR> I. m. One of Indra's horses.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A chasm, a hole, Pañc. ii. d. 14; 107, 2 (of a mouse).<BR> 2. A cave, a cavern, Pañc. 193, 15; Rām. 4, 9, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विल
उद्- + विल उद्- + विल, adj. being out of one's hole, Rām. 2, 33, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविल|महाविलं
महा- + विल महा- + विल, n. 1. a cave. 2. sky, heaven. 3. the heart. 4. a water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीविल
स्थाली- + विल स्थाली- + विल, n. the interior or hollow of a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0867-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
विलक्षण विलक्षण, i. e.<BR> A. वि-लक्ष् + अन, n. Seeing.<BR> B. i. e. वि-लक्षण,<BR> I. adj. Different, Bhāṣāp. 113.<BR> II. n. State or condition for which no cause can be assigned, causeless state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षत्व
विलक्षत्व वि-लक्ष + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Absence of mark or aim.<BR> 2. Absence of distinguishing property.<BR> 3. Surprise.<BR> 4. Shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घन|विलंघन|विलंघनं
विलङ्घन वि-लङ्घ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Overstepping.<BR> 2. Striking against, Kir. 5, 29.<BR> 3. Offence, 13, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घिन्
विलङ्घिन् वि-लङ्घ् + इन्, adj. Transgressing, ascending to, Kathās. 14, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपन|विलपनं
विलपन वि-लप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Lamenting, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 10; Hit. 65, 20.<BR> 2. Chattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब|विलंब|विलंबः|विलम्बः
विलम्ब वि-लम्ब् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Falling.<BR> 2. Hanging down.<BR> 3. Slowness.<BR> 4. Delay, Rām. 3, 35, 35; Lass. 75, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्ब|अविलंब|अविलम्बः
अ- + विलम्ब अ- + विलम्ब, and मा-, acc. बम्, adv. without delay, Pañc. 107, 25 (मा-); Vikr. (Lenz.), 84, 12 (अ-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बन|विलंबन|विलंबनं|विलम्बनं
विलम्बन वि-लम्ब् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Depending.<BR> 2. Delaying, delay, Hit. 99, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिन्|विलंबिन्
विलम्बिन् वि-लम्ब् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Hanging down, Śāk. d. 145.<BR> 2. Delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलंभः|विलम्भः
विलम्भ विलम्भ, i. e. वि-लभ् + अ, m. Liberality (cf. ŚKD.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलय|विलयः
विलय विलय, i. e. वि-ली + अ, m.<BR> 1. Liquefaction, Śiś. 9, 17; विलयं गम्, To be dissolved, to end.<BR> 2. Death, Utt. Rāmac. 172, 3.<BR> 3. Destruction, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> 4. Destruction of the world.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविलय
सु- + विलय सु- + विलय, adj. easily fusible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयन|विलयनं
विलयन विलयन, i. e. वि-ली + अन, n.<BR> 1. Liquefying.<BR> 2. Attenuating.<BR> 3. Corroding.<BR> 4. Removing.<BR> 5. Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसन|विलसनं
विलसन वि-लस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sporting, dallying, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 7.<BR> 2. Flashing, Megh. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाप|विलापः
विलाप विलाप, i. e. वि-लप् + अ, m. Lamentation, Lass. 30, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलास|विलासः
विलास विलास, i. e. वि-लस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sport, pastime, dalliance, merriness, Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR> 2. Coquetry, Śāk. d. 35.<BR> 3. Wantonness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1610.<BR> 4. Charm, beauty, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूविलास|भ्रूविलासः
भ्रू- + विलास भ्रू- + विलास, m. amorous motion of the eyebrows, Megh. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
स- + विलास स- + विलास, adj. amorous, wanton, Śiś. 9, 26; ˚सम्, adv. by expressive looks, Mālat. 15, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासन|विलासनं
विलासन विलासन, i. e. वि-लस् + अन, n. Fascination, Indr. 5, 13 (perhaps corr. विलसनैस् with ă).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासवन्त्|विलासवत्
विलासवन्त् विलास + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Sportive,<BR> 2. A dallying, wanton woman, Ṛt. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
विलासिन् विलासिन्, i. e. विलास + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Sportive.<BR> 2. Dallying, wanton, Kir. 10, 41.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu, Śiva, Kṛṣṇa, Kāma.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR> 3. Fire.<BR> 4. A snake.<BR> 5. A sensualist.<BR> III. f. नी.<BR> 1. A woman, Rām. 3, 52, 23.<BR> 2. A harlot, Pañc. iii. d. 122.<BR> 3. The favourite mistress of a king(?), Pañc. 156, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारविलासिनी
वार- + विलासिनी वार- + विलासिनी, f. a harlot, Hit. iv. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरविलासिनी
सुर- + विलासिन्ī सुर- + विलासिनी, f. a courtesan of heaven, Lass. 82, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखन|विलेखनं
विलेखन विलेखन, i. e. वि-लिख् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Digging.<BR> 2. Dividing.<BR> 3. Making furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखिन्
विलेखिन् विलेखिन्, i. e. वि-लिख् + इन्, adj. Scraping, touching, reaching, Johns. Sel. 40, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप|विलेपः
विलेप विलेप, i. e. वि-लिप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Ointment.<BR> 2. Anointing.<BR> 3. Mortar, plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0868-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपन|विलेपनं
विलेपन विलेपन, i. e. वि-लिप् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Anointing the body with fragrant substances, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 8.<BR> 2. Ointment, Hit. i. d. 96, M.M.<BR> 3. Plastering.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A woman adorned with perfumes.<BR> 2. Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनिन्
विलेपनिन् विलेपनिन्, i. e. विलेपन + इन्, in अ-, adj. Deprived of ointments, Rām. 1, 6, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेशय|विलेशयः
विलेशय विलेशय, i. e. विल + इ-शी + अ, m. Any animal living in holes, as a snake, a rat, a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकन|विलोकनं
विलोकन वि-लोक् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Seeing, regarding, Mālat. 68, 5; sight, Kir. 5, 16.<BR> 2. Spying, Hit. iii. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचन|विलोचनं
विलोचन वि-लोच् + अन, n. The eye, Kumāras. 5, 33; Vikr. d. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडन|विलोडनं
विलोडन विलोडन, also विलोलन विलोलन, i. e. वि-लुड् or लुल्, + अन, n.<BR> 1. Agitating, stirring.<BR> 2. Rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोप|विलोपः
विलोप विलोप, i. e. वि-लुप् + अ, m. Seizing, taking away, Hariv. 7267.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपन|विलोपनं
विलोपन विलोपन, i. e. वि-लुप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Destruction.<BR> 2. Deluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ|विलोभः
विलोभ विलोभ, i. e. वि-लुभ् + अ, m. Seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभन|विलोभनं
विलोभन विलोभन, i. e. वि-लुभ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Beguiling, Kir. 10, 17.<BR> 2. Seduction.<BR> 3. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमित
विलोमित विलोमित, i. e. वि-लोम + इत, adj. Made disaffected, i. e. surpassed, and made reversed, Naiṣ. 22, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल विलोल, i. e. वि-लुल् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Shaking, trembling, Ṛt. 1, 14; 19.<BR> 2. Unsteady, fickle.<BR> 3. Rolling (as the eyes).<BR> 4. Tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व विल्व,<BR> I. m. A fruit tree, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b " target="_blank">Page0869-b + 43</a>] Aegle marmelos, Bhartṛ. 2, 68.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Its fruit.<BR> 2. A measure, the same as the Pala.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरविल्व|चिरविल्वः
चिर- + विल्व चिर- + विल्व, m. a tree, Pongamia glabra Vent., Rām. 3, 79, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा विवक्षा, i. e. विवक्ष, desider. of वच्, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wish to speak.<BR> 2. Wish.<BR> 3. A question, MBh. 1, 7197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवध|विवधः
विवध and वीवध वी̆वध, probably वि-वह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A road, Pañc. iii. d. 39 (वि˚).<BR> 2. A yoke for carrying burthens.<BR> 3. A load.<BR> 4. Storing grain or hay, etc.<BR> 5. An ewer.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकविवध
उदक- + विवध उदक- + विवध, and उद(न्)-वीवध-, m. a yoke for carrying water, Pāṇ. 6, 3, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिक|विवधिकः
विवधिक and वीवधिक वी̆वधिक, i. e. वी̆वध + इक, m. A chandler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर|विवरं|विवरः
विवर विवर, i. e. वि-वृ + अ, n.<BR> 1. Separation.<BR> 2. A hole, Hit. 28, 10, M.M.; a chasm, a fissure, Pañc. 10, 12; a breach, Man. 7, 105; an interval, Śāk. d. 166; space, Nalod. 2, 19.<BR> 3. A cave, Pañc. 241, 1.<BR> 4. A vulnerable part, MBh. 9, 3280.<BR> 5. A wound, Ragh. 11, 18.<BR> 6. Fault, defect.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविवर
कर्ण- + विवर कर्ण- + विवर, n. the auditory passage, Bhāg. P. 3, 15, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासाविवर
नासा- + विवर नासा- + विवर, n. the nostril, ib. 3, 15, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरण|विवरणं
विवरण विवरण, i. e. वि-वृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Uncovering.<BR> 2. Explanation.<BR> 3. A sentence, Brahmav. 2, 28.<BR> 4. Detailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त|विवर्तः|विवर्त्त|विवर्त्तः
विवर्त विवर्त, i. e. वि-वृत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going round, Lass. 74, 16; revolving.<BR> 2. Dancing.<BR> 3. Confounding of truth and falsehood, mistaking unreal objects and conceiving them to be what they are not, e. g. mirage for water, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 24.<BR> 4. Object as unreal, opposed to Brahman, the only real essence, Utt. Rāmac. 143, 8.<BR> 5. Modification, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 3; 88, 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a " target="_blank">Page0870-a + 43</a>]<BR> 6. An assemblage, multitude, Mālat. 24, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0869-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तन|विवर्तनं|विवर्त्तन|विवर्त्तनं
विवर्तन विवर्तन, i. e. वि-वृत् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going round, revolving.<BR> 2. Reverential salutation, Kir. 5, 40.<BR> 3. Turning round, overturning, Utt. Rāmac. 102, 4.<BR> 4. Tossing to and fro, Śāk. d. 132.<BR> 5. Returning, Kir. 7, 11.<BR> 6. Passing in succession, Mālat. 23, 14; as various hells, Man. 12, 75.<BR> 7. Being, abiding.<BR> 8. Causing to change, Mālat. 71, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तिन्
विवर्तिन् विवर्तिन्, i. e. वि-वृत् + इन्, adj. Turning back, Śāk. d. 73; Kir. 5, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवर्तिन्
अ- + विवर्तिन् अ- + विवर्तिन्, adj. not showing the heels, Sāv. 7, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वविवर्तिन्
पार्श्व- + विवर्तिन् पार्श्व- + विवर्तिन्, adj. living at the side, Kathās. 19, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धन|विवर्धनं
विवर्धन विवर्धन, i. e. वि-वृध् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Growing, Rām. 3, 49, 41.<BR> 2. Furthering, increasing, Man. 1, 106; Hit. ii. d. 57 (but cf. v. r. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1217).<BR> II. n. Increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वन्त्|विवस्वत्
विवस्वन्त् वि-वस् + वन्त्, (2. वस्)<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Pañc. v. d. 37; Kir. 5, 48.<BR> 2. Aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun.<BR> 3. The seventh Manu (see वैवस्वत).<BR> 4. A god.<BR> II. f. वती, The city of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाक|विवाकः
विवाक विवाक, see प्राड्विवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाद|विवादः
विवाद विवाद, i. e. वि-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Contesting, Śāk. 106, 10; contest, strife, Man. 4, 180; dispute, Pañc. i. d. 68.<BR> 2. Argument, Man. 11, 205.<BR> 3. A lawsuit, Pañc. iii. d. 92.<BR> 4. Sound, Ragh. 18, 42.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाद|अविवादः
अ- + विवाद अ- + विवाद, m. accordance, Man. 8, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवाद
निस्- + विवाद निस्- + विवाद, adj. not contesting, agreeing with each other, MBh. 3, 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तविवाद
शान्त- + विवाद शान्त- + विवाद (vb. शम्), adj. reconciled, appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाविवाद|सीमाविवादः
सीमा- + विवाद सीमा- + विवाद, m. a litigation respecting boundaries, Man. 8, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन् विवादिन्, i. e. विवाद + इन्, adj. and sbst.<BR> 1. Contending.<BR> 2. A party in a lawsuit, Man. 8, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास|विवासः
विवास विवास, i. e.<BR> I. वि- 1. वस्, Caus., + अ, m. Banishment, Nal. 19, 6.<BR> II. वि-वास, adj. Without clothes, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासन|विवासनं
विवासन विवासन, i. e. वि- 1. वस्, Caus., + अन, n. Banishment, banishing, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह|विवाहः
विवाह विवाह, i. e. वि-वह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Marriage, Pañc. 188, 22.<BR> 2. Nuptial form, Man. 3, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR> see कु-, दुस्-, m. a bad form of marriage, Man. 3, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहिन्
ऽविवाहिन् -विवाहिन्, i. e. विवाह + इन्, in अ-, adj. Such one who is forbidden to be allied by marriage, Man. 9, 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविंशति
विविंशति विविंशति, m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तता
विविक्तता वि-विक्त + ता (vb. विच्), f. A free or empty space, Rājat. 5, 354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षु
विविक्षु विविक्षु, i. e. विविक्ष, desider. of विश्, + उ, adj. Desiring to enter, Vikr. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीत|विवीतः
विवीत वि-वीत (vb. वी, substitute for अज्), n. A pasture ground, Yājñ. 2, 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृति|विवृतिः
विवृति वि-वृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Discovery, manifestation, Kir. 10, 19.<BR> 2. Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्ति|विवृत्तिः
विवृत्ति वि-वृत् + ति, f. Turning round, rolling, whirling, tumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धि|विवृद्धिः
विवृद्धि विवृद्धि, i. e. वि-वृध् + ति, f. Growth, increase. Man. 1, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक|विवेकः
विवेक विवेक, i. e. वि-विच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Discrimination, Man. 1, 26; Pañc. i. d. 294.<BR> 2. Judgment, Bhartṛ. 2, 10.<BR> 3. Discussion, investigation.<BR> 4. True knowledge, Bhartṛ. 1, 89.<BR> 5. A reservoir.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेक|अविवेकः
अ- + विवेक अ- + विवेक,<BR> I. m. absence of discrimination or judgment, Hit. iv. d. 97. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a " target="_blank">Page0871-a + 41</a>]<BR> II. adj. wanting discrimination, stupid, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0870-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकज्ञ
विवेकज्ञ विवेक-ज्ञ, adj. Intelligent, Pañc. i. d. 431.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकता
विवेकता विवेक + ता, in अ-, f. Want of judgment, Hit. pr. d. 11, M.M. निस्-विवेकत्व, see s. v. निर्वि˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन् विवेकिन्, i. e. विवेक + इन्, adj. Judicious, discriminative, prudent, Pañc. 131, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकिन्
अ- + विवेकिन् अ- + विवेकिन्, adj. defective in judgment, unable to discriminate, Kathās. 24, 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तृ
विवेक्तृ विवेक्तृ, i. e. वि-विच् + तृ, m. A wise man, Rājat. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचन|विवेचनं
विवेचन विवेचन, i. e. वि-रिच् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Discrimination.<BR> 2. Decision, Man. 8, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ विवोढृ, i. e. वि-वह् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A husband.<BR> 2. A bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक विव्वोक, m. Affectation of indifference, one of the feminine actions, tending to excite love, Sāh. Darp. 284, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
1. विश् विश्, i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 43, 6),<BR> 1. To enter, Hit. ii. d. 48.<BR> 2. To enter in (with acc.), Bhag. 11, 29.<BR> 3. To pierce, Rājat. 5, 217.<BR> 4. To begin, Rām. 1, 11, 20.<BR> 5. To sit down, Rām. 2, 82, 2.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. विष्ट, Penetrated, pervaded.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. वेश्य,<BR> I. f. या, A harlot, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M.<BR> II. n. The habitation of harlots.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To enter after somebody, MBh. 1, 796.<BR> 2. To enter, Pañc. 187, 25.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To approach, Hit. i. d. 2, M.M.<BR> 2. To enter, Man. i, 29.<BR> 3. To occupy, Chr. 35, 5.<BR> 4. To proceed, Man. 1, 18. आविष्ट,<BR> 1. Pierced, wounded, Rām. 3, 52, 20.<BR> 2. Overpowered, affected with, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-b " target="_blank">Page0871-b + 42</a>] Lass. 2. ed. 45, 18; possessed (by a demon, or by any sentiment), Pañc. 40, 18; Chr. 31, 15; 7, 21.<BR> 3. Covered, Pañc. i. d. 73 (कञ्चुक-, by a coat of mail and by a snake's hide).<BR> 4. Full of, Hit. 126, 17.<BR> --Caus. वेशय, To cause to enter, Bhag. 8, 10.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, To enter, MBh. 1, 5389.<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ,<BR> 1. To enter, Rām. 2, 85, 15.<BR> 2. To begin, Rām. 1, 62, 22.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To enter at once, Man. 1, 56.<BR> 2. To enter, MBh. 1, 7272.<BR> 3. To approach, Bhartṛ. 2, 81.<BR> 4. To sit on, Man. 2, 119; Pañc. ii. d. 63. समाविष्ट, Endowed, Lass. 2, 2.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To put on, MBh. 3, 9913.<BR> 2. To commit, Pañc. i. d. 106.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To sit down, Vikr. 15, 5; Chr. 11, 17.<BR> 2. To encamp, MBh. 3, 659.<BR> 3. To enter, to occupy, MBh. 1, 5389. उपविष्ट,<BR> 1. Seated, Pañc. 68, 21; sitting, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 10; sitting quietly, Pañc. 53, 23; sitting down for performing, Pañc. 224, 15.<BR> 2. Arrived, entered, Lass. 2. ed. 44, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> बल-, adj. endowed with, or possessed of, strength.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to sit down, Vikr. 28, 18 (corr. वेशयति); to place, Man. 3, 208.<BR> 2. To sit down, Pañc. 147, 6 (probably to be read, उपविश्य).<BR> --With उपोप उप-उप,<BR> 1. To sit near, (with the acc.), MBh. 3, 11777.<BR> 2. To sit down, MBh. 1, 4914. उपोपविष्ट,<BR> 1. Surrounded, Rām. 1, 4, 26.<BR> 2. Sitting, MBh. 1, 6959.<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, To sit down opposite to, MBh. 2, 1156 (perhaps प्रति is to be separated, and preposition belonging to the preceding word).<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To sit down, Vikr. 81, 4; MBh. 1, 8479.<BR> --Caus. To cause to sit down, Hit. 69, 5.<BR> --With नि नि, Ātm. (in epic [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0872-a " target="_blank">Page0872-a + 43</a>] poetry also Par., MBh. 1, 6960).<BR> 1. To enter, MBh. 1, 7566.<BR> 2. To descend, MBh. 1, 7308.<BR> 3. To sit down, Śiś. 1, 19.<BR> 4. To lie down, Pañc. 205, 8.<BR> 5. To marry, MBh. 1, 1852.<BR> 6. To be intent on, Man. 2, 8.<BR> 7. To return, MBh. 3, 1426 (probably is to be read निर्वेश्य). निविष्ट,<BR> 1. Situated on, Rām. 3, 53, 35.<BR> 2. Arranged, Man. 9, 252.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to enter, Man. 4, 171.<BR> 2. To place, Rām. 1, 18, 21.<BR> 3. To lay the foundation of, Hariv. 6521.<BR> 4. With मनस्, To apply one's mind to, Man. 6, 35.<BR> 5. To draw, Śāk. d. 42.<BR> 6. To cause to lie down, to encamp, Śāk. 18, 23.<BR> 7. To cause to marry, MBh. 1, 7138; to unite to a match, Śāk. d. 95.<BR> --With अभिनि अभि-नि,<BR> 1. To sit down, to settle in (with acc.), Pāṇ. 1, 4, 47; figurat., Bhaṭṭ. 8, 80.<BR> 2. To be very set upon, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 21. अभिनिविष्ट,<BR> 1. Endowed with, Ragh. 2, 75 (Calc.).<BR> 2. Fixed, Mālat. 19, 2.<BR> 3. Determined.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To place, Śiś. 1, 15.<BR> 2. To build, Ragh. 15, 29.<BR> 3. To cause to be very set upon, Mālav. 28, 8.<BR> --With प्रत्यभिनि प्रति-अभि-नि, प्रत्यभिनिविष्ट, Pursuing pertinaciously, Mālat. 88, 22.<BR> --With प्रतिनि प्रति-नि, प्रतिनिविष्ट, Obstinate, Bhartṛ. 2, 4.<BR> --With वि-नि वि-नि, Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to enter, Rājat. 5, 318.<BR> 2. To join(?), Rājat. 5, 39.<BR> 3. To place, Rājat. 5, 445.<BR> 4. To suspend, Pañc. i. d. 160.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, संनिविष्ट, Entered, seated, Bhag. 15, 15.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to enter, Man. 11, 202 (read संनिवेश्य).<BR> 2. To cause to lie down, MBh. 3, 665.<BR> 3. To unite, to join, Man. 1, 16.<BR> 4. To place, Vikr. 73, 8; Ragh. 12, 58 (Calc.).<BR> 5. To put on, Ṛt. 1, 7.<BR> 6. To contemplate, Man. 12, 120.<BR> --With निस् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0872-b " target="_blank">Page0872-b + 42</a>] निस्,<BR> 1. To enjoy, Megh. 109.<BR> 2. To return, to reward, MBh. 5, 4943.<BR> 3. To embellish, Hariv. 7858.<BR> --With परि परि, see 2. विष् with परि.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To enter, Chr. 24, 50.<BR> 2. To appear, Vikr. 71, 11.<BR> 3. To begin, Rām. 1, 31, 28. प्रविष्ट,<BR> 1. Entered, pass. and act., Śāk. d. 7; Rājat. 5, 13; 58.<BR> 2. Entered upon, engaged in. Desider. विविक्ष, To wish to enter, MBh. 3, 10836.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to enter, Pañc. 256, 1; to let enter, 16, 2.<BR> 2. To introduce (with two acc.), MBh. 1, 4427; as one's wife, Chr. 6, 8.<BR> 3. To lay up, Man. 8, 38. प्रव्च्शित, Called, or sent in.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र,<BR> 1. To enter after somebody, MBh. 1, 7800.<BR> 2. To enter, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 13.<BR> 3. To go through, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 10.<BR> 4. To follow, to accommodate one's self to, Pañc. i. d. 78 (cf. Hit. ii. d. 50).<BR> 5. To cohabit with. MBh. 1, 4275.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To enter, MBh. 1, 3303.<BR> 2. To cohabit with, Man. 9, 8.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To enter, MBh. 1, 6741.<BR> 2. To lie down, MBh. 3, 13149; to go to rest, Man. 4, 55.<BR> 3. To cohabit with, Man. 3, 48.<BR> --Caus. To place, MBh. 1, 4274.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्, To lie down after somebody, Ragh. 2, 24 (Calc.).<BR> --Cf. ἵκω, ἱκνέομαι; see 2. विश् and वेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वेश्या|स्वर्व्वेश्या
स्वर्-वेश्या स्वर्-वेश्या, f. an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0871-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
2. विश् विश्,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A man of the mercantile caste, Chr. 4, 19 (the king may be called lord of the Vaiśyas, because the Brāhmaṇas are theoretically his superiors, the Kṣatriyas his equals, and the Śūdras too base for being meant; but perhaps it has the following signification).<BR> 2. A man in general.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Family, tribe, Chr. 289, 5 = Rigv. i. 50, 5; Chr. 296, 3 = Rigv. i. 112, 3 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a " target="_blank">Page0873-a + 41</a>].<BR> 2. Entrance.<BR> 3. A daughter.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vaihts; A.S. with; O.H.G. ni-with, eo-wiht, neo-wiht.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0872-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश|विशं
विश विश, see विस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क|विशंक|विशङ्कः
विशङ्क<BR> I. वि-शङ्क (cf. शङ्का), adj. Fearless; acc. कम्, adv., Daśak. in Chr. 196, 3.<BR> II. वि-शङ्क् + आ, f. Suspicion, Nal. 24, 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्क|अविशंक
अ- + विशङ्क अ- + विशङ्क, adj. free from suspicion, fearless, Nal. 4, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशङ्क|निर्विशंक|निर्व्विशङ्क
निस्- + विशङ्क निस्- + विशङ्क, adj. fearless, Man. 7, 176 (Pañc. 123, 18 read also निर्व्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कट|विशंकट|विशङ्कटः
विशङ्कट विशङ्कट (Pāṇ. 5, 2, 28, nevertheless for original वि-संकट), adj. Great, large, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 50; Mālat. 78, 2 (with स्); acc. टम्, adv. Vehemently, Pañc. 46, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
विशद विशद,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Of a white colour, Megh. 41; Śiś. 9, 26; Kir. 5, 12.<BR> 2. Clear, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322.<BR> 3. Pure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2680; spotless, Śāk. d. 97.<BR> 4. Evident.<BR> 5. Beautiful.<BR> II. m. White, the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशय|विशयः
विशय विशय, i. e. वि-शी + अ, m. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयिन्
विशयिन् विशयिन्, i. e. विशय + इन्, adj. Dubious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशर|विशरः
विशर विशर, i. e. वि-शॄ + अ, m. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसन|विशसनं|विशसनः
विशसन वि-शस् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Dissecting.<BR> 2. Killing, ruin, Utt. Rāmac. 96, 5.<BR> II. m. A crooked sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसितृ
विशसितृ वि-शस् + इतृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Who or what dissects, Man. 5, 51.<BR> 2. Who or what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाख|विशाखः
विशाख<BR> I. वि-शाख (cf. शाखा), adj. Branchless.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Kārttikeya.<BR> 2. An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR> 3. A solicitor, a beggar.<BR> 4. A spindle.<BR> III. f. खा, The sixteenth lunar asterism, Lass. 16, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातन|विशातनं|विशातनः
विशातन विशातन, i. e. वि-शातय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b " target="_blank">Page0873-b + 40</a>] (Caus. of शद्), + अन, adj., f. नी, Causing to fall asunder, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाय|विशायः
विशाय विशाय, i. e. वि-शी + अ, m. Sleeping and watching alternately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारण|विशारणं
विशारण विशारण, i. e. वि-शॄ + अन, n. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद विशारद,<BR> 1. Learned, wise.<BR> 2. Skilled, conversant with, Pañc. ii. d. 14; Chr. 5, 5.<BR> 3. Famous.<BR> 4. Bold, presuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल विशाल (perhaps vb. श्रि),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Great, large, Hit. 14, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. Broad.<BR> 3. Eminent, illustrious, Hit. pr. d. 39. M.M.<BR> II. m. A sort of deer.<BR> III. f. ला.<BR> 1. The city Ougein, Megh. 31, and another town.<BR> 2. Bitter apple, Cucumis colocynthis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालता
विशालता विशाल + ता, f.<BR> 1. Magnitude.<BR> 2. Breadth.<BR> 3. Distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख वि-शिख (probably from शिखा),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An arrow, Chr. 34, 13; Rājat. 5, 221 (उत्खायमान-, adj. While the arrow was drawn out).<BR> 2. An iron crow.<BR> II. f. खा.<BR> 1. A sort of needle.<BR> 2. A spade.<BR> 3. A highway.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाक्षविशिख
कटाक्ष- + विशिख कटाक्ष- + विशिख, m. an arrow-like amorous look, Bhartṛ. 2, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिप|विशिपं
विशिप विशिप, n. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टता
विशिष्टता वि-शिष्ट + ता (vb. शिष्), f.<BR> 1. Excellence, distinction, Hit. pr. d. 42, M.M.<BR> 2. Individuality, having distinguishing properties.<BR> 3. Peculiarity, as of duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धि|विशुद्धिः
विशुद्धि विशुद्धि, i. e. वि-शुध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Purity, Man. 5, 67; 9, 9.<BR> 2. Correctness.<BR> 3. Purifying, purification, Bhag. 6, 12; Utt. Rāmac. 9, 17.<BR> 4. Sameness.<BR> 5. Removal of doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
विशेष विशेष, i. e. वि-शिष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-a " target="_blank">Page0874-a + 46</a>] Difference, Pañc. 219, 14; at the end of comp. words, Different, e. g. गति-, m. Different ways, Pañc. 247, 11. पुरुष-, This or that man, Pañc. i. d. 124.<BR> 2. Special property, Hit. pr. d. 25, M.M.<BR> 3. A change for the better, Mālav. 46, 9.<BR> 4. Sort, kind, manner, Megh. 65; Hit. ii. d. 149; Pañc. 114, 25; a different object, Megh. 58.<BR> 5. Excellence, superiority; विशेषेण, Particularly, Pañc. 142, 15; 162, 9; at the end of comp. words, Excellent; e. g. भक्ष-, m. Excellent food, Pañc. 113, 9; 117, 2, cf. my transl. n. 767; Vikr. d. 142.<BR> 6. A limb.<BR> 7. A mark on the forehead with sandal.<BR> 8. Speciality, characteristic marks, Lass. 13, 4 (तपस्विन्-, of an ascetic).<BR> 9. Abl. विशेषात्, Especially, Pañc. ii. d. 100; even more, just for that, Pañc. 109, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषम्
अ-विशेष + म् अ-विशेष + म्, adv. without choosing, Arj. 3, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोविशेष|तपोविशेषः
तपोविशेष तपोविशेष, i. e. तपस्-, m. pl. various modes of devotion, Man. 2, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविशेष
दशा- + विशेष दशा- + विशेष, m. a special condition, Hit. 78, 8, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेष|निर्विशेषः|निर्व्विशेष
निस्- + विशेष निस्- + विशेष,<BR> I. m. want of difference, Hit. 113, 11.<BR> II. adj. 1. having no discrimination, Hit. ii. d. 68. 2. not different. 3. equal. 4. acc. षम्, adv.<BR> a. without difference, Hit. 84, 5, M.M.<BR> b. alike, Hit. 128, 10.<BR> c. exceedingly, Utt. Rāmac. 99, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविशेष|प्रसाधनविशेषः
प्रसाधन- + विशेष प्रसाधन- + विशेष, m. highest accomplishment, Vikr. d. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसविशेष
रस- + विशेष रस- + विशेष, m. a more excellent juice, Pañc. ii. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
स- + विशेष स- + विशेष, adj. 1. having discrimination, Hit. 55, 13. 2. having characteristic qualities. 3. extraordinary, Hit. 60, 6, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
विशेषक विशेषक, i. e. वि-शिष् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Discriminative, distinguishing.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. An attribute, a predicate.<BR> 2. A mark on the forehead made with sandal, etc., and worn either as an ornament, Mālav. d. 40; Daśak. in Chr. 199, 4, or sectarial [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b " target="_blank">Page0874-b + 42</a>] distinction.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रविशेषक|पत्रविशेषकः
पत्र- + विशेषक पत्र- + विशेषक, strokes and lines drawn on the face with fragrant pigments of sandal, musk, etc., Ragh. 3, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रनष्टविशेषक
वि-प्र-नष्ट- + विशेषक वि-प्र-नष्ट- + विशेषक (vb. नश्), adj., f. का, one whose discriminative faculty or perception has disappeared, Rām. 3, 55, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषक
स- + विशेषक स- + विशेषक, adj. discriminated, having distinguishing properties, Bhāṣāp. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषज्ञ
विशेषज्ञ विशेष-ज्ञ, adj.<BR> 1. Deeply learned, Hit. 129, 9; iv. d. 98.<BR> 2. Wise, intelligent.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषज्ञ
अ- + विशेषज्ञ अ- + विशेषज्ञ, adj. having no judgment, Hit. iii. d. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
विशेषण विशेषण, i. e. वि-शिष् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Discriminative.<BR> 2. Distinctive.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Distinguishing, discriminating.<BR> 2. An attribute, epithet, Vikr. 20, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेषण
निस्- + विशेषण निस्- + विशेषण, adj. without attributes, Bhāg. P. 2, 10, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषण
स- + विशेषण स- + विशेषण, adj. distinguished, characterised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणता
विशेषणता विशेषण + ता, f. The state of being a distinguishing mark, Bhāṣāp. 60; cf. Kusumāñj. transl. pp. 13, 55, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणवन्त्|विशेषणवत्
विशेषणवन्त् विशेषण + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having a distinguishing attribute, Bhāṣāp. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषतस्
विशेषतस् विशेष + तस्, adv. Especially, Hit. 80, 1, M.M.; particularly, Vikr. d. 62.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषतस्
स- + विशेषतस् स- + विशेषतस्, adv. particularly, excellently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषवन्त्|विशेषवत्
विशेषवन्त् विशेष + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Peculiar.<BR> 2. Excellent.<BR> 3. Superior, better, Johns. Sel. 17, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्यक
विशेष्यक विशेष्य + क (vb. शिष्), latter part of a comp. adj. in तद्वद्-विशेष्यक, i. e. तद्वन्त्-, Relating to an object possessing such an attribute, Bhāṣāp. 134; cf. Kusumāñj. transl. 61, 1-6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधन|विशोधनं
विशोधन विशोधन, i. e. वि-शुध् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Purifying, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a " target="_blank">Page0875-a + 40</a>] Rām. 1, 26, 19.<BR> 3. Expiation, Man. 11, 143; 156.<BR> II. f. नी, The capital of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित्व
विशोधित्व विशोधित्व, i. e. विशोधिन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Purifying.<BR> 3. Freeing from obstructions, clearing, Hit. iii. d. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधिन्
विशोधिन् विशोधिन्, i. e. वि-शुध् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Purifying.<BR> 3. Clearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषण|विशोषणं
विशोषण विशोषण, i. e. वि-शुष् + अन,<BR> I. adj.(?), Drying, Arj. 8, 8; the name of a weapon.<BR> II. n. Drying.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुविशोषण
तालु- + विशोषण तालु- + विशोषण, n. the growing dry of the palate (by much speaking), MBh. 8, 4760.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्न|विश्नः
विश्न विश्न, i. e. 2. विछ् + न, m. Splendour, Pāṇ. iii. 3, 90; vi. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्पति
विश्पति विश्-पति, m. Lord of the house, Lass. 100, 13 = Rigv. vii. 15, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्पला
विश्पला विश्पला, f. A proper name, Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. i. 112, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रणन|विश्रणनं
विश्रणन and विश्राणन विश्रा̆णन, i. e. वि-श्रण् + अन, n. Gift, donation, Ragh. 2, 54 (आ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम|विश्रमः
विश्रम वि-श्रम् + अ, m. Rest, repose, quiet, Vikr. d. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भ|विश्रंभ|विश्रंभः|विश्रम्भः
विश्रम्भ वि-श्रम्भ् + अ (also विस्रम्भ विस्रम्भ), m.<BR> 1. Trust, confidence, Pañc. i. d. 306; ii. d. 190.<BR> 2. Affection, Hit. 46, 1, M.M. (-आलाप, Affectionate talk).<BR> 3. Sportive noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भिन्|विश्रंभिन्
विश्रम्भिन् विश्रम्भिन्, i. e. वि-श्रम्भ्, and विश्रम्भ, + इन्, also विस्रम्भिन् विस्रम्भिन्, adj.<BR> 1. Trusting, confiding in.<BR> 2. Trustworthy, MBh. 1, 5845 (स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रय|विश्रयः
विश्रय विश्रय, i. e. वि-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abode, asylum.<BR> 2. Dependence upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रयिन्
विश्रयिन् विश्रयिन्, adj.<BR> 1. Living or dwelling in.<BR> 2. Depending on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रवस्
विश्रवस् वि-श्रवस्, m. A proper name, Rām. 3, 53, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणन|विश्राणनं
विश्राणन विश्राणन, see विश्रणन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्ति|विश्रांति|विश्रांतिः|विश्रान्तिः
विश्रान्ति विश्रान्ति, i. e. वि-श्रम् + ति, f. Rest, repose, Vikr. d. 20; Kathās. 22, 104 (रतेस्--वासवेश्मेव विश्रान्त्यै--आवयोर् अभवत्, literally, It was for us like the sleeping-room of the goddess of love for reposing in).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राम|विश्रामः
विश्राम विश्राम, i. e. वि-श्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rest, repose, Pañc. 145, 9; Hit. i. d. 138, M.M.<BR> 2. Stop, pause, Utt. Rāmac. 103, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राव|विश्रावः
विश्राव विश्राव, i. e. वि-श्रु + अ, m., and विश्रुति वि-श्रु + ति, f. Fame, celebrity, notoriety.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुति|लोकविश्रुतिः
लोक-विश्रुति लोक-विश्रुति, f. 1. fame. 2. unfounded rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
विश्लथ वि-श्लथ् + अ, adj. Relaxed, Ragh. 6, 73; languid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेष|विश्लेषः
विश्लेष विश्लेष, i. e. वि-श्लिष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation, Pañc. 225, 18 (with सह); disunion.<BR> 2. A chasm, Kathās. 2, 49.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविश्लेष|चित्तविश्लेषः
चित्त- + विश्लेष चित्त- + विश्लेष, m. separation of the hearts, loss of friendship, Pañc. 225, 17 (with instr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषिन्
विश्लेषिन् विश्लेषिन्, i. e. वि-श्लिष् + इन्, adj. Falling, Ragh. 16, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व विश्व, probably वि-श्वि (cf. the aor. of श्वि, अ-श्वम्, and शश्वन्त्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. All, every, Lass. 97, 2 = Rigv. vi. 64, 1; every one, Lass. 101, 4 = Rigv. vii. 16, 1; particularly former part of comp. words, cf. विश्व-कर्मन्, विश्वकृत्, etc.<BR> 2. Whole.<BR> 3. Universal.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A term of the Vedāntra philosophy, the faculty perceiving singleness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 13.<BR> 2. pl. (विश्वे), A class of deities, Indr. 2, 13.<BR> III. n. The world, Śāk. d. 1.<BR> IV. (n. and) f. वा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a " target="_blank">Page0876-a + 40</a>] Dry ginger.<BR> V. f. वा, A tree, a plant, Aconitum ferox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकद्रु|विश्वकद्रुः
विश्वकद्रु विश्व + क-द्रु,<BR> I. adj. Wicked.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A dog trained for the chase.<BR> 2. Sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकृत्
विश्वकृत् विश्व-कृ + त्, m.<BR> 1. The creator.<BR> 2. A son of Brahman, the artist of the gods (= विश्व-कर्मन्), Sund. 3, 13, cf. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजनीन
विश्वजनीन विश्वजनीन, विश्वजनीय विश्वजनीय, and विश्वजन्य विश्वजन्य, i. e. विश्व-जन + ईन, or ईय, or य, adj. Good for all men, universally salutary, Man. 9, 31 (-जन्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजित्
विश्वजित् विश्व-जि + त्,<BR> I. adj. All-subduing.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A particular sacrifice, Man. 11, 74.<BR> 2. The noose of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वञ्च्
विश्वञ्च् विश्वञ्च्, A false writing for विष्वञ्च्, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतस्
विश्वतस् विश्व + तस्, adv. Everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतुर्
विश्वतुर् विश्व-तुर्, adj. All-subduing, Chr. 288, 16 = Rigv. i. 48, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वद्र्यञ्च्
विश्वद्र्यञ्च् विश्वद्र्यञ्च्, i. e. विश्व + त्र-अञ्च् (with द् for त्; cf. also तिर्यञ्च्), adj., f. द्रीची, Moving everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वप्सन्
विश्वप्सन् विश्वप्सन्, i. e. विश्व-भस् + अन् (properly the curtailed ptcple. of the pres.), m.<BR> 1. A god.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR> 3. The sun.<BR> 4. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वंभर|विश्वम्भर|विश्वंभरः|विश्वम्भरः
विश्वंभर विश्वंभर, i. e. विश्व + म्-भृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. All-sustaining.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Indra.<BR> III. f. रा, The earth, Utt. Rāmac. 7, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसन
विश्वसन वि-श्वस् + अन, n. Trusting, confiding in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसनीयता
विश्वसनीयता i. e. वि-श्वसनीय + ता (vb. श्वस्), f. Inspiring confidence, Śāk. 27, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसह
विश्वसह विश्व-सह् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Allenduring.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. The earth.<BR> 2. One of the tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसुविद्
विश्वसुविद् विश्व-सु-विद्, adj. Giving everything well, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसृज्
विश्वसृज् विश्व-सृज् (nom. sing. -सृट् and सृक्, MBh. 14, 7367), m.<BR> 1. The creator of the universe, MBh. 1, 1.; Śiś. 9, 80.<BR> 2. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाची
विश्वाची विश्वाची, i. e. विश्व-अञ्च् + ई, f. The name of an Apsaras, Lass. 2. ed. 50, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामित्र|विश्वामित्रः
विश्वामित्र विश्वामित्र, i. e. विश्व-मित्र, m. The name of a Muni, Johns. Sel. 23, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वावसु|विश्वावसुः
विश्वावसु विश्वावसु, i. e. विश्व-वसु, m.<BR> 1. One of the Manus.<BR> 2. One of the Gandharvas, Indr. 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास|विश्वासः
विश्वास विश्वास, i. e. वि-श्वस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Confidence, trust, Pañc. ii. d. 23.<BR> 2. Faith, Vikr. 71, 13.<BR> 3. Secret, Hit. 73, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वास|अविश्वासः
अ- + विश्वास अ- + विश्वास, m. 1. want of confidence, distrust, Pañc. i. d. 295. 2. treachery(?), Rām. 3, 52, 48. ˚शम्, adv. without confiding, distrustfully, Pañc. iii. d. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासन|विश्वासनं
विश्वासन (or ना?), विश्वासन (or ना), i. e. वि-श्वस्, Caus., + अन, n. (or f.), Producing confidence, Pañc. 165, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासिन्
विश्वासिन् विश्वासिन्, i. e. वि-श्वस्, and विश्वास, + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Trusting.<BR> 2. Trusty, honest.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासिन्
अ- + विश्वासिन् अ- + विश्वासिन्, adj. mistrustful, Megh. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासैकसार
विश्वासैकसार विश्वासैकसार, i. e. विश्वास-एक-सार, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेभोजस्
विश्वेभोजस् विश्वेभोजस् (i. e. विश्व and भोजस्), m. A name of Indra, Matsyapurāṇa, see Aufrecht, Ujjvalad. p. 250, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0876-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
† 1. विष् विष्, i. 1, Par. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
2. विष् विष्, ii. 3, वेविष्, Par. Ātm. To pervade, to embrace, etc. (ved.).<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, Caus.<BR> 1. To present, to offer, Man. 3, 228; to offer food, MBh. 1, 7182 (where it is written with श् instead of ष्).<BR> 2. To wait on, Rām. 1, 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
† 3. विष् ii. 9, विष्णा, विष्णी, Par. To separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
4. विष् विष्, f. Excrement, Man. 4, 48.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविष्|कर्ण्णविष्
कर्ण- + विष् कर्ण- + विष्, f. ear-wax, Man. 5, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष|विषं|विषः
विष विष,<BR> I. m. and n. Poison, Pañc. iii. d. 83 (n.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. See विस.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. virus; ἰός, ἴον; Lat. viola (poison is connected with blue, cf. विष-पुष्प, and Śiva's neck growing blue, by swallowing the poison churned out of the sea).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविष
कर्ण- + विष कर्ण- + विष, n. poison sprinkled in one's ears (treacherous speech), Pañc. i. d. 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीविष|दूषीविषं
दूषी- + विष दूषी- + विष, n. vegetable poison that has become old and diminished in strength, Suśr. 2, 254, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविष|दृष्टिविषः
दृष्टि- + विष दृष्टि- + विष, m. a snake, Kir. 14, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष
निस्- + विष निस्- + विष, adj., f. षा, deprived of poison, Pañc. iii. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रविष
नेत्र- + विष नेत्र- + विष, adj. having poison in one's eyes, MBh. 2, 2140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविष|महाविषः
महा- + विष महा- + विष, m. a small venomous snake, Rām. 3, 53, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाविष|लालाविषः
लाला- + विष लाला- + विष, m. an insect whose spittle is poison, as a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषङ्ग
विषङ्ग विषङ्ग, i. e. वि-सञ्ज् + अ, m. Attachment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषङ्ग
निस्- + विषङ्ग निस्- + विषङ्ग, adj. indifferent, Bhāg. P. 4, 22, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्णता
विषण्णता विषण्ण + ता (vb. सद्), f. Dejection, want of energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषता
विषता विष + ता, f. State of poison, Śiś. 9, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषद|विषदं|विषदः
विषद विष-द,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Giving [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b " target="_blank">Page0877-b + 43</a>] poison.<BR> 2. Shedding water.<BR> II. m. A cloud.<BR> III. n. Green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदर्शनमृत्युक|विषदर्शनमृत्युकः
विषदर्शनमृत्युक विष-दर्शन-मृत्यु + क, m. A kind of pheasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधर|विषधरः
विषधर विषधर, i. e. विष-धृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Venomous.<BR> II. m. A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषम|विषमं|विषमः
विषम विषम, i. e. वि-सम,<BR> I. adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Unequal, different, Kir. 5, 40.<BR> 2. Inconstant, Hit. ii. d. 104.<BR> 3. Odd (in numbers), figurat., Pañc. i. d. 126.<BR> 4. Unhappy, Hit. iv. d. 3.<BR> 5. Unparalleled, unequalled, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 1.<BR> 6. Uneven, Pañc. ii. d. 188; sloping, Vikr. 10, 9.<BR> 7. Rough, Vikr. d. 49; Pañc. 188, 9.<BR> 8. Difficult, painful, Bhartṛ. 2, 54; disagreeable, Pañc. i. d. 12.<BR> 9. Frightful, Hit. iii. d. 133.<BR> 10. Dishonest, wicked, Hiḍ. 1, 39; Hit. ii. d. 111.<BR> 11. Partial, Man. 7, 27.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Inequality.<BR> 2. Oddness.<BR> 3. Unevenness, Man. 1, 24 (uneven valleys, Jones).<BR> 4. An inaccessible place, a precipice, Rām. 3, 51, 40; Pañc. 142, 6; a thicket, a pit, Man. 8, 232.<BR> 5. Difficulty, pain, Pañc. v. d. 65; misfortune, Bhartṛ. 2, 95.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यवज्रविषम
वाक्य-वज्र- + विषम वाक्य-वज्र- + विषम, adj. rough, coarse, by (using) thunderbolt-like words, Pañc. iii. d. 236 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2928).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमय
विषमय विष + मय, adj., f. यी (Pañc. i. d. 211, या, but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 119, read विषमय्यो), Poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमस्थ|विषमस्थः
विषमस्थ विषम-स्थ, adj.<BR> 1. Standing unevenly.<BR> 2. Being in difficulty or misfortune, Nal. 10, 1.<BR> 3. Inaccessible, Pañc. i. d. 195.<BR> 4. Safely posted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित विषमित, i. e. विषम + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Made crooked, Kir. 10, 56.<BR> 2. Made difficult to be walked on, Kir. 12, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0877-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषय|विषयः
विषय विषय (probably वि-क्षि + अ), m.<BR> 1. A collection of villages.<BR> 2. A country, Rājat. 5, 51; Pañc. 129, 14; a kingdom, Bhartṛ. 2, 12; Rām. 3, 54, 28 (यम-, The lower regions, death); a place, Śāk. 104, 14; Kir. 5, 38.<BR> 3. Anything indigenous or peculiar to a province.<BR> 4. Home, province, department, sphere, Vikr. 39, 14; Pañc. 4, 17 (जीवितव्य-, Duration of life); Pañc. 227, 22 (application); element, that which is peculiarly known to those who occupy themselves with it or live therein.<BR> 5. Horizon, sight, a place which may be looked over by somebody, reach, Man. 8, 148; Hit. 28, 3, M.M.; Megh. 35; 101.<BR> 6. Anything perceivable by the senses, an object of sense, Man. 1, 15; Vikr. d. 9.<BR> 7. An object in general, Bhāṣāp. 36; अत्र विषये, Concerning this object, Pañc. 114, 20; धनविषये, Concerning wealth, Pañc. 139, 3; स्त्रीणां विषये, Concerning women, 27, 18; an object of art, Mālav. d. 29.<BR> 8. Worldly object, affair, business, enjoyment, etc., Pañc. iii. d. 244; sensual enjoyment, Hit. iii. d. 116.<BR> 9. Aim, Śiś. 9, 40.<BR> 10. A religious observance.<BR> 11. Refuge, asylum.<BR> 12. A lover, a husband.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषय|अविषयः
अ- + विषय अ- + विषय,<BR> I. adj. unacquainted with worldly objects, Śāk. 55, 20.<BR> II. m. 1. not being an object, Mālat. 17, 2. 2. invisibility, Hit. ii. d. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यविषय
अन्-अन्य- + विषय अन्-अन्य- + विषय, adj. having, or referring to, no other object, Vikr. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशविषय
अवकाश- + विषय अवकाश- + विषय, adj., f. या, literally, having as its sphere space, room, i. e. demanding a place (which it cannot get because the heart is filled with pride, etc.), Pañc. iii. d. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुर्विषय|चक्षुर्विषयः
चक्षुर्विषय चक्षुर्विषय, i. e. चक्षुस्-, m. sight, Man. 2, 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्षुर्विषय
अ-चक्षुस्- + विषय अ-चक्षुस्- + विषय, adj. not distinguishable by one's eye, Man. 4, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसमुदयावाप्तिविषय
गुण-समुदय-अवाप्ति- + विषय गुण-समुदय-अवाप्ति- + विषय, adj., f. या, having as its object the acquirement of a multitude of good qualities, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b " target="_blank">Page0878-b + 43</a>] Hit. i. d. 174, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषय|निर्व्विषय
निस्- + विषय निस्- + विषय,<BR> I. m. no home, not being a dwelling-place, Hariv. 3654.<BR> II. adj. 1. having no home banished, Rām. 3, 79, 47. 2. not attached to worldly objects, Bhāg. P. 2, 1, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिविषय|नीतिविषयः
नीति- + विषय नीति- + विषय, m. sphere of prudent conduct, Pañc. 112, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायनविषय
पलायन- + विषय पलायन- + विषय, adj., f. या, having flight as its object, i. e. advising flight, Pañc. 247, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रविषय|मित्रविषयः
मित्र- + विषय मित्र- + विषय, m. friendship, Pañc. 131, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवतिविषय
युवति- + विषय युवति- + विषय, m. a woman, Megh. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविषय|श्रुतिविषयः
श्रुति- + विषय श्रुति- + विषय, m. 1. an object of hearing, i. e. sound, Śāk. d. 1. 2. an object of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वविषय|स्वविषयः
स्व- + विषय स्व- + विषय, m. one's own country, Hit. i. d. 170, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन् विषयायिन्, i. e. विषय + यिन् (for विन्), m.<BR> 1. A king.<BR> 2. An organ of sense.<BR> 3. Kāma.<BR> 4. A sensualist.<BR> 5. A materialist.<BR> 6. A man of business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन् विषयिन्, i. e. विषय + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. णी.<BR> 1. Attached to sensual objects, carnal, sensual, Hit. ii. d. 144; voluptuary, Śāk. 68, 14.<BR> 2. Conversant with worldly occupations, Hit. 13, 7, M.M.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A king.<BR> 2. Kāma.<BR> 3. A sensualist.<BR> 4. A materialist.<BR> 5. A man of business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषहर|विषहरः
विषहर विषहर, i. e. विष-हृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Removing venom.<BR> II. f. रा and री, The goddess of the serpent race, the sister of Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा विष् + आ,<BR> I. f. Excrement, Amarak.<BR> II. ind. Intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाण|विषाणं|विषाणः
विषाण विषाण, i. e. वि-सो + अन, m. (f. णी), and n.<BR> 1. The horn of an animal, Bhartṛ. 2, 5; Pañc. i. d. 311.<BR> 2. The tusks of an elephant or boar, Lass. 2. ed. 46, 24; Draup. 8, 21.<BR> II. f. णी, The name of two plants.<BR> III. n. Costus speciosus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषाण
निस्- + विषाण निस्- + विषाण, adj. without tusks, MBh. 6, 4677.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशविषाण
शश- + विषाण शश- + विषाण, and शशक-, n. the horn of a hare; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a " target="_blank">Page0879-a + 42</a>] anything improbable or extraordinary, Bhartṛ. 2, 5; 3, 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0878-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन् विषाणिन्, i. e. विषाण + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Having horns, MBh. 6, 71.<BR> 2. Having huge tusks, Rām. 2, 52, 18, Seramp.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Any animal with horns.<BR> 2. A bull.<BR> 3. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाद|विषादः
विषाद विषाद, i. e. वि-सद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Lassitude, dejection, lowness of spirits, want of energy, fear, Draup. 8, 3; Chr. 40, 20; weakness, Mālat. 35, 9.<BR> 2. Distress, affliction, sorrow, Vikr. 5, 11; Pañc. 221, 5.<BR> 3. Disappointment, despair, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषाद
अ- + विषाद अ- + विषाद, adj. unwearied, Johns. Sel. 57, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविषादम्
स-विषाद + म् स-विषाद + म्, adv. afflicted, Pañc. 107, 19; sorrowful, Vikr. 30, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादिन्
विषादिन् विषादिन्, i. e. विषाद + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Dejected, Bhag. 18, 23.<BR> 2. Sorrowful, Man. 6, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाय
विषाय विषाय, a denomin. derived from विष with य, Ātm. To turn into poison, Bhartṛ. 1, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषु
विषु विषु (probably a loc. pl. of द्वि, cf. वि), adv.<BR> 1. Equally, same, alike.<BR> 2. Many, various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुव|विषुवं
विषुव विषुव, विषुवत् विषुवत्, i. e. विषु + वन्त्, n. (व, by dropping the final त्), The equinox, Hit. 114, 22 (व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्क्
विष्क् विष्क्, see वष्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ|विष्कंभ|विष्कंभः|विष्कम्भः
विष्कम्भ विष्कम्भ, i. e. वि-स्कम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstacle, hindrance, resistance.<BR> 2. The bolt of a door.<BR> 3. A post, the roof-tree of a house.<BR> 4. Spreading.<BR> 5. A posture of the devotees, called योगिन्.<BR> 6. Act, doing anything.<BR> 7. The first of the twenty-seven astronomical periods called योगस्.<BR> 8. A prelude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भक|विष्कंभक
विष्कम्भक विष्कम्भ + क, m. A prelude, Vikr. 36, 14; Śāk. 31, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भिन्|विष्कंभिन्
विष्कम्भिन् विष्कम्भिन्, i. e. वि-स्कम्भ् + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Obstructive, impeding.<BR> II. m. The bolt of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्किर|विष्किरः
विष्किर विष्किर, i. e. वि-कॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A bird, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 13.<BR> 2. Tearing to pieces.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखविष्किर|नखविष्किरः
नख- + विष्किर नख- + विष्किर, m. a bird wounding with strong talons, a bird of prey, Man. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरविष्किर|स्मेरविष्किरः
स्मेर- + विष्किर स्मेर- + विष्किर, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप|विष्टपं|विष्टपः
विष्टप विष्टप (cf. पिष्टप, and पिव् for पि-पा, s. v. 1. पा), m. and n. A world, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3288.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टप|त्रिविष्टपं
त्रि- + विष्टप त्रि- + विष्टप, n. the world of Indra, Yājñ. 3, 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ|विष्टंभ|विष्टंभः|विष्टम्भः
विष्टम्भ विष्टम्भ, i. e. वि-स्तम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstacle.<BR> 2. Stopping.<BR> 3. Placing in or upon, planting (one's feet), Kir. 13, 16.<BR> 4. Paralysis, loss of motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भिन्|विष्टंभिन्
विष्टम्भिन् विष्टम्भिन्, i. e. वि-स्तम्भ् + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Stopping.<BR> 2. Checking.<BR> 3. Making motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टर|विष्टरः
विष्टर विष्टर, i. e. वि-स्तॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A handful of Kuśa or sacred grass, MBh. 3, 1881.<BR> 2. A seat made of twenty-five straws of Kuśa grass tied up in a sheaf.<BR> 3. A layer, MBh. 15, 739; a bed.<BR> 4. A couch, a seat, Vikr. 86, 15.<BR> 5. The seat of a Brahman, either real or in effigy, as presiding at a sacrifice.<BR> 6. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टा
विष्टा विष्टा, (Pañc. 192, 16), and विष्ठा विष्ठा (Man. 3, 180; 4, 220; 10, 91), f. Fæces, ordure (cf. 4. विष्).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविष्ठा
गो-विष्ठा गो-विष्ठा, f. cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखविष्ठा
मुख-विष्ठा मुख-विष्ठा, f. a cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
विष्टि विष्टि, i. e. 2. विष् + टि,<BR> I. adj. and sbst. Working, a workman.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Occupation, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3; act, action.<BR> 2. Unpaid labour.<BR> 3. Hire, Rām. 2, 63, 55, Seramp.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a " target="_blank">Page0880-a + 37</a>] Sending, dispatching.<BR> 5. Sending to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0879-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठल|विष्ठलं
विष्ठल विष्ठल, i. e. वि-स्थल, n. A place situated remote or apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा विष्ठा, see विष्टा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णु|विष्णुः
विष्णु विष्णु, i. e. 2. विष् + नु, m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu, one of the three principal Indian deities, Chr. 291, 7 = Rigv. i. 85, 7; Pañc. 44, 16.<BR> 2. Agni.<BR> 3. One of the Vasus.<BR> 4. The name of an ancient law-giver.<BR> 5. A pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुमय
विष्णुमय विष्णु + मय, adj., f. यी, Emanated from Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पन्द|विष्पंद|विष्पंदः|विष्पन्दः
विष्पन्द विष्पन्द, i. e. वि-स्पन्द् + अ, m. Throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फार|विष्फारः
विष्फार विष्फार, i. e. वि-स्फर् + अ, m. The twang of a bow (cf. विस्फार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्य|विष्यः
विष्य विष्य, i. e. विष + य, adj. Deserving death by poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्द|विष्यंदः|विष्यन्दः
विष्यन्द विष्यन्द, i. e. वि-स्यन्द् + अ, m. Flowing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्षेण
विष्वक्षेण विष्वक्षेण, and विष्वक्सेन विष्वक्सेन, i. e. विष्वञ्च्-सेन (see सेना), m. Viṣṇu, Bhāg. P. 8, 13, 24 (स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वञ्च्|विष्वंच्
विष्वञ्च् विष्वञ्च्, i. e. विषु-अञ्च्,<BR> I. adj., f. षूची, Going everywhere, all-pervading, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 20.<BR> II. acc. वक्, adv.<BR> 1. Every way, everywhere, Pañc. ii. d. 2.<BR> 2. All about, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वणन|विष्वणनं
विष्वणन विष्वणन, n., and विष्वाण विष्वाण, m., i. e. वि-स्वन् + अन, or अ, Eating, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्
† विस् विस्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस|विसं
विस विस (also विश and विष), probably curtailed विसर, or विसल (cf. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b " target="_blank">Page0880-b + 42</a>] both), i. e. वि-सृ + अ, n. The film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily, Śāk. d. 66; Vikr. d. 94; MBh. 13, 4509; 12, 7877 (all with स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयोग|विसंयोगः
विसंयोग विसंयोग, i. e. वि-सम्-युज् + अ, m. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवाद|विसंवादः
विसंवाद विसंवाद, i. e. वि-सम्-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Contradiction, disagreement, Pañc. iii. d. 261; Mālav. d. 23.<BR> 2. Disappointing, deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवादिन्
विसंवादिन् विसंवादिन्, i. e. वि-सम्-वद्, and विसंवाद, + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Contradicting, disagreeing, Rājat. 5, 193.<BR> 2. Disputing.<BR> 3. Crafty, cunning.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसंवादिन्
अ- + विसंवादिन् अ- + विसंवादिन्, adj. incontestible, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंष्ठुल
विसंष्ठुल विसंष्ठुल (वि, सम्, and vb. स्था), adj. Unsteady, agitated, Kāvya Prak. 105, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर|विसरः
विसर विसर, i. e. वि-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Spreading, Kāvya Prak. 79, 9.<BR> 2. A multitude, Mālat. 23, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ग|विसर्गः
विसर्ग विसर्ग, i. e. वि-सृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abandoning.<BR> 2. Final emancipation.<BR> 3. Departure.<BR> 4. Relinquishment.<BR> 5. Dismission, Chr. 9, 38.<BR> 6. Creation, Bhag. 8, 3.<BR> 7. Evacuation of excrement, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 20.<BR> 8. Separation.<BR> 9. Donation.<BR> 10. Light, lustre.<BR> 11. The southern course of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जन|विसर्जनं|विसर्ज्जनं
विसर्जन विसर्जन, i. e. वि-सृज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Relinquishing, Nal. 10, 15.<BR> 2. Sending away, dismissing, Chr. 9, 38.<BR> 3. Sending.<BR> 4. Donation, Lass. 80, 3 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 5. Throwing the image of a deity in holy water, as the concluding rite of a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्प|विसर्पः
विसर्प विसर्प, i. e. वि-सृप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Spreading, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 6.<BR> 2. Flying, gliding.<BR> 3. Going.<BR> 4. Unwished consequence of any act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पण|विसर्पणं
विसर्पण विसर्पण, i. e. वि-सृप् + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a " target="_blank">Page0881-a + 40</a>] n.<BR> 1. Spreading.<BR> 2. Flying.<BR> 3. Going gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0880-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पिन्
विसर्पिन् विसर्पिन्, i. e. वि-सृप् + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> 1. Spreading, Śiś. 9, 36; Vikr. d. 16 (वसुधाधर-कन्दरा-, Spreading through the clefts of the mountains, viz. the echo); 67, 1.<BR> 2. Gliding, going gently.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दविसर्पिन्
मन्द- + विसर्पिन् मन्द- + विसर्पिन्, adj. moving slowly, Pañc. i. d. 282 (a louse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसल|विसलं
विसल विसल, probably वि-सृ + अ (with ल् for र्), m. A shoot, a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसार|विसारः
विसार विसार, i. e. वि-सृ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Going smoothly, gliding.<BR> 2. Expansion, Nalod. 1, 19.<BR> 3. A fish.<BR> II. n. A wood.<BR> III. f. री, The region of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारिन्
विसारिन् विसारिन्, i. e. वि-सृ + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Gliding, flowing.<BR> 2. Spreading, Kir. 10, 11.<BR> II. m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसिनी
विसिनी विसिनी, i. e. विस + इन् + ई (see विश), f.<BR> 1. A lotus flower, Bhartṛ. 3, 7.<BR> 2. An assemblage of lotus flowers, Mālat. 51, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूचिका
विसूचिका विसूचिका (akin to सूचि), f.<BR> 1. Spasmodic cholera, Pañc. 138, 8.<BR> 2. Symptoms of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरण|विसूरणं
विसूरण विसूरण, i. e. वि-† सूर् + अन, n., and f. णा, Sorrow, Vikr. d. 82 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरित|विसूरितं
विसूरित वि-† सूर् + इत,<BR> I. n. Repentance.<BR> II. f. ता, A fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत्वर|विसृत्वरः
विसृत्वर वि-सृ + त्वर, adj. Going smoothly, gliding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृमर|विसृमरः
विसृमर वि-सृ + मर, adj. Gliding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्टि|विसृष्टिः
विसृष्टि विसृष्टि, i. e. वि-सृज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Quitting.<BR> 2. Leaving.<BR> 3. Dismissing.<BR> 4. Giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्त|विस्तः
विस्त विस्त, m. A weight of gold, about half an ounce Troy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तर|विस्तरः
विस्तर विस्तर, i. e. वि-स्तॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Spreading.<BR> 2. Prolixity, Pañc. iii. d. 103.<BR> 3. Detail; instr. ˚रेण, Fully, at length, Chr. 9, 37; Sund. 1, 1.<BR> 4. Abundance, Man. 6, 55; multitude, Hit. iii. d. 12.<BR> 5. Assemblage, a large company, Man. 3, 125.<BR> 6. A bed.<BR> 7. A seat, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविस्तर|अतिविस्तरः
अति- + विस्तर अति- + विस्तर, m. excessive prolixity, Vikr. 3, 6 (अलम्, with instr., enough).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्तर
स- + विस्तर स- + विस्तर, adj. with (its) detail, complete, Pañc. 114, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तरम्
सु-विस्तर + म् सु-विस्तर + म्, adv. at large, Hit. 73, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरतस्
विस्तरतस् विस्तर + तस्, adv. Fully, at length, Pañc. 181, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरता
विस्तरता विस्तर + ता, f. Spreading, Kir. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरशस्
विस्तरशस् विस्तर + शस्, adv. Fully, at length, Man. 9, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तार|विस्तारः
विस्तार विस्तार, i. e. वि-स्तॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Spreading, extension, Megh. 18.<BR> 2. Vastness.<BR> 3. Length, Rām. 1, 40, 15.<BR> 4. Detail, Yājñ. 3, 95.<BR> 5. Breadth, amplitude.<BR> 6. Amplification.<BR> 7. The diameter of a circle.<BR> 8. The branch of a tree with its new shoots.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविस्तार
अति- + विस्तार अति- + विस्तार, m. excessive extension, Pañc. 245, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारिन्
विस्तारिन् विस्तारिन्, i. e. विस्तार + इन्, adj., f. ऋणी,<BR> 1. Extending, Utt. Rāmac. 157, 16; large, Mālat. 131, 10.<BR> 2. Powerful, Mālat. 81, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्णता
विस्तीर्णता वि-स्तीर्ण + ता (vb. स्तॄ), f.<BR> 1. Extension, Hit. iii. d. 53.<BR> 2. Vastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृति|विस्तृतिः
विस्तृति वि-स्तृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR> 2. Breadth.<BR> 3. The diameter of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पष्ट|विस्पष्टः
विस्पष्ट वि-स्पष्ट (properly ptcple. of the pf. pass. of स्पश्, see दृश्), adj.<BR> 1. Apparent, evident.<BR> 2. Plain, intelligible.<BR> 3. ˚टम्, adv. Evidently, Indr. 5, 39. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a " target="_blank">Page0882-a + 41</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्ट|अविस्पष्टं
अ- + विस्पष्ट अ- + विस्पष्ट, 1. adj. not clear, obscure. 2. acc. टम्, adv. without pronouncing well letters and accents, Man. 4, 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0881-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार|विस्फारः
विस्फार विस्फार, i. e. वि-स्फर् + अ, m. The twang of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलिङ्ग|विस्फुलिंग|विस्फुलिंगः|विस्फुलिङ्गः
विस्फुलिङ्ग वि-स्फुलिङ्ग, m.<BR> 1. A spark of fire, MBh. 1, 1431.<BR> 2. A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फूर्जथु|विस्फूर्जथुः
विस्फूर्जथु वि-स्फूर्जथु, m.<BR> 1. Rolling, Ragh. 13, 12.<BR> 2. Thunder, ib. 14, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फोट|विस्फोटः
विस्फोट विस्फोट, i. e. वि-स्फुट् + अ, m., and f. टा,<BR> 1. Boil, pustule, Śāk. Sch. ad 20, 10.<BR> 2. Small-pox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मय|विस्मयः
विस्मय विस्मय, i. e. वि-स्मि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Surprise, Vikr. 78, 5; wonder, Pañc. i. d. 459 (बालके को त्र विस्मयः, literally, What wonder concerning a little boy, i. e. how much more a little boy).<BR> 2. Pride, Man. 4, 237.<BR> 3. Doubt, uncertainty, Hit. 13, 19; perplexity, Hit. ii. d. 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मय|सविस्मयः
स-विस्मय स-विस्मय, adj., f. या, 1. surprised, Pañc. 44, 24. 2. doubtful, Hit. 54, 18. 3. ˚यम्, adv. surprised, Pañc. 76, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयंगम
विस्मयंगम विस्मयंगम, i. e. विस्मय + म्-गम् + अ, adj. Astonishing (with acc. आत्मानम्, thyself), Johns. Sel. 17, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयिन्
विस्मयिन् विस्मयिन्, i. e. विस्मय + इन्, adj., f. नि, Astonished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरण|विस्मरणं
विस्मरण विस्मरण, i. e. वि-स्मृ + अन, n. Forgetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मापन|विस्मापनः
विस्मापन विस्मापन, i. e. वि-स्मि, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Causing surprise, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 5.<BR> 2. Illusion, deceit.<BR> 3. Kāma.<BR> 4. A magical or enchanted city, a city of the Gandharvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृति|विस्मृतिः
विस्मृति वि-स्मृ + ति, f. Forgetting. Utt. Rāmac. 122, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्यन्द
विस्यन्द वि-स्यन्द् + अ, m. Flowing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्र|विस्रं
विस्र विस्र, n. A smell like that of raw meant, Śāk. 74, 10 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंस|विस्रंसः
विस्रंस वि-स्रंस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Relaxation.<BR> 2. Decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंसन
विस्रंसन वि-स्रंस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Loosening, untying, Sāh. D. 113, 16.<BR> 2. Falling.<BR> 3. Flowing, dropping.<BR> 4. A laxative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भ|विस्रंभ|विस्रम्भः
विस्रम्भ विस्रम्भ, and विस्रम्भिन् विस्रम्भिन्, see विश्र्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रसा
विस्रसा विस्रसा, i. e. वि-स्रंस् + अ, f. Decrepitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावण|विस्रावणं
विस्रावण विस्रावण, i. e. वि-स्रु, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Causing to flow.<BR> 2. Bleeding.<BR> 3. Distilling.<BR> 4. A spirit distilled from molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहग|विहगः
विहग विह-ग (cf. विहा), m.<BR> 1. A bird, Pañc. ii. d. 21.<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> 3. An arrow.<BR> 4. The sun.<BR> 5. The moon.<BR> 6. A planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंग|विहङ्ग|विहंगः|विहङ्गः
विहंग विहंग, i. e. विह + म्-ग (see the last),<BR> I. adj. Flying, going swiftly.<BR> II. m. A bird, Pañc. 157, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विहंग
निस्- + विहंग निस्- + विहंग, adj. without birds, Hariv. 3489.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगम|विहङ्गम|विहंगमः|विहङ्गमः
विहंगम विहंगम, i. e. विह + म्-गम् + अ (see the last),<BR> I. m. A bird, Pañc. ii. d. 20.<BR> II. f. मा, A pole or yoke for carrying burthens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगिका|विहङ्गिका
विहंगिका विहंगिका, i. e. विहंग, in the signification of विहंगमा, + क, f. A pole or yoke for carrying burthens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहति|विहतिः
विहति विहति, i. e.<BR> I. वि-हन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Striking, killing.<BR> 2. Defeat, Nalod. 1, 10; Kir. 10, 63.<BR> II. वि-हति, m. A friend.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविहति|प्रणयविहतिः
प्रणय- + विहति प्रणय- + विहति, f. denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहनन|विहननं
विहनन वि-हन् + अन, m.<BR> 1. Impediment.<BR> 2. Killing, injuring.<BR> 3. A<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0882-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर|विहरः
विहर विहर, i. e. वि-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separation.<BR> 2. Absence.<BR> 3. Exchanging, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 920.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरण|विहरणं
विहरण विहरण, i. e. वि-हृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Taking off or away.<BR> 2. Going about for pleasure or exercise, Pañc. 25, 10; roaming, Bhartṛ. 3, 92.<BR> 3. Relaxation, pastime, pleasure, Pañc. 236, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्तृ|विहर्त्तृ
विहर्तृ विहर्तृ, i. e. वि-हृ + तृ, m. One who robs, Draup. 8, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसन|विहसनं
विहसन वि-हस् + अन, n. Laughing gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा वि-हा, indecl. Heaven, paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस्
विहायस् विहायस्, i. e. वि-हा + यस् (for वस्),<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. The sky.<BR> 2. The open air, Man. 2, 186.<BR> II. instr. सा, adv. Through the air, Rām. 3, 54, 6.<BR> III. m. A bird.<BR> --Cf. χάος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहार|विहारः
विहार विहार, i. e. वि-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Wandering, going about, walking for pleasure, Rām. 3, 51, 20; Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 1.<BR> 2. Sporting, Hit. 83, 4, M.M.; pleasure, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 9; relaxation, Rām. 3, 49, 39.<BR> 3. A Bauddha or Jaina convent, Pañc. 236, 8.<BR> 4. A temple, Hit. 19, 10 (cf. वीहार).<BR> 5. A palace, Mālat. 8, 4.<BR> 6. The shoulder.<BR> 7. A sort of bird.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयेन्द्रविहार
जयेन्द्र- + विहार जयेन्द्र- + विहार, i. e. जय-इन्द्र-, m. a convent built by Jayendra, a king of Cashmere, Rājat. 5, 427.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विहार
निस्- + विहार निस्- + विहार, adj. deprived of pleasure, Hariv. 11150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाविहार
हिंसा- + विहार हिंसा- + विहार, m. roaming with the intention to do mischief, Rām. 3, 51, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारक
विहारक विहार + क (or विहारिक विहार + इक?), adj., f. रिका, Belonging to a Bauddha convent, Mālat. 104, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारवन्त्|विहारवत्
विहारवन्त् विहार + वन्त्, adj. Taking pleasure, liking, Man. 10, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिन्
विहारिन् विहारिन्, i. e. वि-हृ and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b " target="_blank">Page0883-b + 40</a>] विहार, + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> 1. Walking about, wandering, Hit. i. d. 20, M.M.<BR> 2. Taking pleasure or relaxation, rejoicing one's self, Śāk. 17, 21; Pañc. 30, 25; ii. d. 21.<BR> 3. Beautiful, Bhartṛ. 1, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहास|विहासः
विहास विहास, i. e. वि-हस् + अ, m. A gentle laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिंसक
विहिंसक वि-हिंस् + अक, adj. Injuring, Pañc. iii. d. 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित्रिम
विहित्रिम विहित्रिम, i. e. वि-हित + रिम (vb. धा), adj. Done according to rule, Bhaṭṭ. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीनता
विहीनता वि-हीन + ता (vb. हा), f. Abandoning, Pañc. ii. d. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृति|विहृतिः
विहृति वि-हृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Opening.<BR> 2. Pastime, pleasure, Nalod. 2, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठक|विहेठकः
विहेठक वि-हेठ् + अक, m. An injurer, a reviler, MBh. 1, 3076.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठन|विहेठनं
विहेठन वि-हेठ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Hurting, killing.<BR> 2. Rubbing, grinding.<BR> 3. Afflicting.<BR> 4. Affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल|विह्वलः
विह्वल वि-ह्वल् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Agitated, Rām. 2, 48, 2; overcome with fear or agitation, Chr. 34, 8.<BR> 2. Distressed, afflicted, Chr. 32, 28 (perhaps rather सविह्वल, in one word, full of emotion).<BR> 3. Fused, liquid.<BR> 4. Languishing, Lass. 2. ed. 60, 25.<BR> 5. Desponding, Mālat. 142, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्वल
अ- + विह्वल अ- + विह्वल, adj. strong, Chr. 30, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविह्वल
परि- + विह्वल परि- + विह्वल, adj. very agitated, Rām. 2, 84, 6 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलता
विह्वलता विह्वल + ता, f. Agitation, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
1. वी वी, ii. 2, Par. (ved.),<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To approach.<BR> 3. To pervade, to obtain.<BR> 4. To conceive, to grow pregnant.<BR> 5. To desire, to love, Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR> 6. To eat, to enjoy.<BR> 7. It is used as substitute for [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a " target="_blank">Page0884-a + 39</a>] the vb. अज्, To drive, to move.<BR> 8. To throw.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वित, Tranquil, quiet, tame.<BR> --Caus. वायय and वापय, To cause to conceive (see वप्).<BR> --Cf. οἴσω, οἴαξ, οἰήϊον; Lat. in-vîtus (Not liking), in-vitare, To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0883-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
2. वी वी, f. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक|वीकः
वीक वीक, i. e. वि + क, m.<BR> 1. A bird.<BR> 2. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीकाश|वीकाशः
वीकाश वीकाश, i. e. वि-काश् + अ, m. Æther, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष|वीक्षं|वीक्षः
वीक्ष वीक्ष, i. e. वि-ईक्ष् + अ,<BR> I. m., and f. क्षा, Sight, seeing, investigation, Pañc. 62, 12 (f.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Surprise.<BR> 2. A visible object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षण|वीक्षणं
वीक्षण वीक्षण, i. e. वि-ईक्ष् + अन, n. Sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्खा|वींखा
वीङ्खा वीङ्खा, i. e. वि-ईङ्ख् + अ, f.<BR> 1. Moving.<BR> 2. Dancing.<BR> 3. One of a horse's paces.<BR> 4. Cowach, Carpopogon pruriens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचयन
वीचयन वीचयन, i. e. वि-चि + अन, n. Research, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचि|वीचिः
वीचि वीचि (m. and) f., also वीची वीची, f.<BR> 1. A wave, Hit. iii. d. 140 (इ); Pañc. i. d. 209 (ई).<BR> 2. A ray of light.<BR> 3. Small, little.<BR> 4. Leisure.<BR> 5. Pleasure.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचि|अवीचिः
अ- + वीचि अ- + वीचि,<BR> I. adj. waveless.<BR> II. m. a hell, Yājñ. 3, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीचि|महावीचिः
महा- + वीचि महा- + वीचि, m. a hell, Man. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्
वीज् वीज्, † i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR> --i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from व्यज), Par. To fan, Mālat. 63, 9; Chr. 25, 56.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, i. 10, To fan, MBh. 3, 1764.<BR> --With उद् उद्, i. 10, To fan, MBh. 3, 1757.<BR> --With उप उप, i. 10, To fan, Śāk. 33, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज वीज, also बीज बीज, i. e. probably [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b " target="_blank">Page0884-b + 44</a>] वि-ज (vb. जन्), n.<BR> 1. Seed, germ, Śāk. 91, 14; Pañc. 51, 11; 200, 12.<BR> 2. Semen virile.<BR> 3. Receptacle, place of deposit.<BR> 4. Marrow.<BR> 5. Origin.<BR> 6. Divine truth as the cause of being.<BR> 7. The origin of the business of a drama.<BR> 8. The mystical syllable which forms the essential part of the मन्त्र of any deity.<BR> 9. Algebra.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीज|अवीजः
अ- + वीज अ- + वीज,<BR> I. n. bad grain, Man. 9, 291.<BR> II. adj. without manly strength, Man. 9, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवीज|अग्निवीजं
अग्नि- + वीज अग्नि- + वीज, n. gold, Man. 5, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तवीज
उप्त- + वीज उप्त- + वीज (vb. वप्), adj., f. जा, sown, Śāk. 91, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीरवीज
उशीर- + वीज उशीर- + वीज, m. the name of a mountain, Rām. 6, 3, 32; also उषीर-, with ष् instead of श्, 4, 41, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिवीज
नीति- + वीज नीति- + वीज, n. a germ of intrigue, Pañc. 85, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिवीज|मणिवीजः
मणि- + वीज मणि- + वीज, m. the pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवीज|मंत्रवीज
मन्त्र- + वीज मन्त्र- + वीज, n. seed-like deliberation, Hit. ii. d. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गवीज
रङ्ग- + वीज रङ्ग- + वीज, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववीज
स्व- + वीज स्व- + वीज, m. the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवीज
हर- + वीज हर- + वीज, n. quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवीज|हरिवीजं
हरि- + वीज हरि- + वीज, n. yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजक|वीजकः
वीजक वीज + क,<BR> 1. m. The common citron, Rām. 2, 69, 8, ed. Seramp.<BR> 2. A substitute for वीज, as latter part of a comp. adj., e. g. अ-, adj. Not sown, Man. 10, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजन|वीजनं|वीजनः
वीजन<BR> I. n. विज् + अन.<BR> 1. Fanning, being fanned, Rājat. 5, 386.<BR> 2. A fan.<BR> II. n. Thing.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A sort of pheasant.<BR> 2. The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवत्|वीजवन्त्
वीजवत् वीज + वत्, adv. Like seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवन्त्|वीजवत्
वीजवन्त् वीज + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Who or what has seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिन्
वीजिन् वीजिन्, i. e. वीज + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Having seed.<BR> 2. Having sown seed, Man. 9, 51; 52.<BR> II. m. A father, a progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्य|वीज्यः
वीज्य वीज्य, i. e. वीज + य, adj.<BR> 1. Sprung from seed.<BR> 2. Sprung from some family.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीज्य|महावीज्यं
महा- + वीज्य महा- + वीज्य, n. the septum of the scrotum, and part of the perinæum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0884-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटिका
वीटिका वीटिका, f.<BR> 1. The betel plant.<BR> 2. The preparation of the Areca nut with spices, and enveloped in the leaf of the betel plant, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 17.<BR> 3. A tie, a fastening, Amar. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणा
वीणा वीणा, f. The Indian lute, Hit. ii. d. 73.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवीणा|दंतवीणा
दन्त- + वीणा दन्त- + वीणा, f. chattering of the teeth, Pañc. 94, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रवीणा
सूत्र- + वीणा सूत्र- + वीणा, f. a sort of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणिन्
वीणिन् वीणिन्, i. e. वीणा + इन्, adj. Furnished with lutes, Megh. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतंस|वीतंसः
वीतंस वीतंस, see वितंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतहव्य
वीतहव्य वीत-हव्य (vb. वी and हु), m. A proper name, MBh. 13, 1943.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीति|वीतिः
वीति वी + ति,<BR> I. f.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. Engendering.<BR> 3. Eating, Lass. 101, 9 = Rigv. vii. 16, 4.<BR> 4. Cleaning.<BR> 5. Light, lustre.<BR> II. m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथि|वीथिः
वीथि and वीथी वीथी̆, probably वि-इ + थ + ई, f.<BR> 1. A line, MBh. 13, 5261.<BR> 2. A road, Pañc. i. d. 189; Indr. 2, 12.<BR> 3. A stall, a shop, Śiś. 9, 32.<BR> 4. A terrace in front of a house.<BR> 5. A sort of drama.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजवीथी
अज-वीथी अज-वीथी, f. the name of a part of the orbit of the moon, Yājñ. 3, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवीथि|घनवीथिः
घन-वीथि घन-वीथि, f. the road of the clouds, as if they were shops, Śiś. 9, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रवीथी
नक्षत्र-वीथी नक्षत्र-वीथी, f. the orbit of the stars, MBh. 13, 521.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोवीथी
नभोवीथी नभोवीथी, i. e. नभस्-, f. the orbit of the sun, Bhāg. P. 5, 22, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीथी
नाग-वीथी नाग-वीथी, f. 1. a line formed by snakes, MBh. 13, 5261. 2. the name of a part of the orbit of the moon, Yājñ. 3, 187. 3. a proper name, Hariv. 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरवीथी
सुर-वीथी सुर-वीथी, f. the road of the gods, Indr. 2, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथिका
वीथिका वीथि + का, f. A hall, Utt. Rāmac. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथी
वीथी वीथी, see वीथि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्र|वीध्रं|वीध्रः
वीध्र वीध्र, i. e. वि-इन्ध् + र, adj. Clear, clean, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाह|वीनाहः
वीनाह वीनाह, see विनाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीपा
वीपा वीपा, f. Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीप्सा
वीप्सा वीप्सा, i. e. वि-ईप्स, desider. of आप्, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Successive order, Pāṇ. viii. 1, 4.<BR> 2. Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्
वीर् वीर्, i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from वीर), Ātm.<BR> 1. To be valiant.<BR> 2. To show one's heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर वीर, i. e. वृ + अ (probably for original वार),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Heroic.<BR> 2. Strong.<BR> 3. Powerful.<BR> 4. Eminent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A hero, Chr. 5, 1.<BR> 2. A brave man, Hit. i. d. 169, M.M.<BR> 3. A soldier, Rājat. 5, 134.<BR> 4. Heroism, as a रस or poetical sentiment.<BR> 5. Fire.<BR> 6. Sacrificial fire (see विरहन्, वीरोज्झ, and वीरोपजीविक).<BR> 7. An actor.<BR> III. f. रा.<BR> 1. A matron, a wife and mother.<BR> 2. The plantain tree.<BR> 3. The name of several plants.<BR> 4. Spirituous liquor, or a particular kind of it.<BR> IV. n. The name of several plants. वीरतर, see s. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vir; Goth. vair; A.S. wer; probably ἥρως, Ἥρα, Ἡρακλῆς, εἰρήν.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर|अवीरः
अ- + वीर अ- + वीर, and निस्-, f. रा, a woman who has neither husband nor son, Man. 4, 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवीर|एकवीरः
एक- + वीर एक- + वीर, m. an unparalleled hero, MBh. 4, 1912.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर|महावीरः
महा- + वीर महा- + वीर, m. 1. a hero. 2. a lion. 3. a white horse. 4. a sort of hawk. 5. Garuḍa. 6. Indra's thunderbolt. 7. Viṣṇu. 8. Agni. 9. sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीर
सु- + वीर सु- + वीर,<BR> I. adj. abounding in heroes.<BR> II. m. pl. the name of a people, Draup. 8, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरजयन्तिका|वीरजयंतिका
वीरजयन्तिका वीरजयन्तिका, i. e. probably विर-जयन्त + क, f.<BR> 1. A war-dance.<BR> 2. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरण|वीरणं
वीरण वीरण,<BR> I. n. A fragrant grass, Andropogon muricatum, Rām. 2, 80, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a " target="_blank">Page0886-a + 40</a>]<BR> II. f. णी.<BR> 1. A side-glance.<BR> 2. A deep place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0885-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतर|वीरतरं|वीरतरः
वीरतर वीर + तर, m.<BR> 1. A distinguished hero, Lass. 48, 11.<BR> 2. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरता
वीरता वीर + ता, f. Heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवन्त्|वीरवत्
वीरवन्त् वीर + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Abounding in heroes, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR> 2. Having a hero.<BR> II. f. वती, A wife whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहन्
वीरहन् वीर-हन्, m. A Brāhmaṇa who has suffered the sacred domestic fire to become extinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरानक
वीरानक वीरानक, The name of a town, Rājat. 5, 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराय
वीराय वीराय, a denomin. derived from वीर with य, To show one's heroism, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरिणी
वीरिणी वीरिणी, f. The name of a river, Matsyop. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुध्
वीरुध् वीरुध्, i. e. वि-रुह्, f.<BR> 1. A creeper.<BR> 2. A plant which grows again when being cut, Man. 11, 142.<BR> 3. A plant in general, Pañc. iii. d. 50; Vikr. d. 38.<BR> 4. A branch and shoot, Utt. Rāmac. 44, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीरुध्
निस्- + वीरुध् निस्- + वीरुध्, adj. deprived of plants, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोज्झ|वीरोज्झः
वीरोज्झ वीरोज्झ, i. e. वीर-उज्झ् + अ, m. A Brahman who omits offering burnt offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोपजीविक|वीरोपजीविकः
वीरोपजीविक वीरोपजीविक, i. e. वीर-उप-जीव + इक, m. A Brāhmaṇa who claims presents on the merit of having preserved his sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य|वीर्यं|वीर्य्य|वीर्य्यं
वीर्य वीर्य, i. e. वीर + य, n.<BR> 1. Strength, power, Chr. 23, 33; Vikr. d. 16.<BR> 2. Fortitude, Chr. 4, 14.<BR> 3. Heroism.<BR> 4. Dignity.<BR> 5. Splendour. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b " target="_blank">Page0886-b + 43</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघवीर्य
अ-मोघ- + वीर्य अ-मोघ- + वीर्य, adj. 1. of unfailing virility. 2. of unfailing power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर्य|निर्वीर्य्य|निर्व्वीर्य्य
निस्- + वीर्य निस्- + वीर्य, adj. powerless, Hit. ii. d. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर्य|महावीर्यः|महावीर्य्य|महावीर्य्यः
महा- + वीर्य महा- + वीर्य,<BR> I. adj. very strong, Rām. 3, 53, 12.<BR> II. m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रवीर्य|विचित्रवीर्यः|विचित्रवीर्य्य|विचित्रवीर्य्यः
वि-चित्र- + वीर्य वि-चित्र- + वीर्य, m. a proper name, Chr. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवीर्य
सम- + वीर्य सम- + वीर्य, adj. having equal strength, Hit. iv. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीर्य|सुवीर्य्य|सुवीर्य्यं
सु- + वीर्य सु- + वीर्य, n. 1. great vigour. 2. abundance in heroes, Chr. 288, 12 = Rigv. i. 48, 12 (cf. i. 40, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यवन्त्|वीर्यवत्|वीर्य्यवत्
वीर्यवन्त् वीर्य + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Strong, Man. 2, 114.<BR> 2. Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवध|वीवधः
वीवध वीवध, and वीवधिक वीवधिक, see विवध, विवधिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीहार|वीहारः
वीहार वीहार, i. e. वि-हृ + अ (cf. विहार), m. A Bauddha or Jaina convent, a sanctuary, a temple, a holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुङ्ग्|वुंग्
† वुङ्ग् वुङ्ग्, बुङ्ग् बुङ्ग्, i. 1, Par. To abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुण्ट्|वुंट्
वुण्ट् वुण्ट्, see विण्ट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ वृ, and वॄ वृ, i. 1. ii. 5, वृणु, and ii. 9, वृणा, वृणी, Par. Ātm (this verb comprehends perhaps two verbs which were originally different; the original signification of the one seems to be, ‘To guard by covering,’ that of the other, ‘To coose’).<BR> 1. To screen, to cover, MBh. 3, 10970.<BR> 2. To conceal (ved.).<BR> 3. To surround, MBh. 5, 164.<BR> 4. To resist (ved.).<BR> 5. To select, to choose, Rām. 2, 9, 25.<BR> 6. To woo, MBh. 3, 16647.<BR> 7. ii. 9, Ātm. To select for one's self, Ragh. 3, 6; to beg, Dev. 11, 36.<BR> 8. To prefer, Rām. 2, 70, 12.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वृत.<BR> 1. Agreed or assented to.<BR> 2. Served.<BR> 3. Affected by.<BR> 4. Vitiated, spoiled.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. वर्य,<BR> 1. To be applied to for aid.<BR> 2. To be yielded to or indulged. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0887-a " target="_blank">Page0887-a + 46</a>]<BR> 3. Chief, principal (rather वर + य), Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 41; Kir. 7, 20. m. Kāma. f. या, A girl choosing her own husband (rather वर + य).<BR> --Comp.<BR> अर्य-, m. a respectable man of the third caste, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 17.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10,<BR> I. वरय, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To select, to choose, Hit. 116, 7; Rām. 1, 43, 17; in marriage, Chr. 52, 10.<BR> 2. To beg (with two acc.), Rām. 1, 36, 16.<BR> 3. To fall to one's share (acc.), Rām. 1, 65, 21.<BR> II. वारय, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To stop, Man. 8, 239.<BR> 2. To hinder, Nal. 3, 24.<BR> 3. To keep off.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वारित, Prevented.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुस्-, adj. kept off badly, MBh. 13, 267.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass.<BR> I. वार्य, Excellent. n. Sacrifice, Lass. 101, 13 = Rigv. vii. 16, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुस्-, adj. 1. difficult to be kept off, irresistible, MBh. 12, 3661. 2. dangerous to be troubled, cf. MBh. 1, 1917 (+ ता, f. state of such one).<BR> II. वारणिय.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुस्-, adj. irresistible, MBh. 8, 3629.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप,<BR> 1. To open (ved.)<BR> 2. To show, Ragh. 10, 7 (Calc.).<BR> --Caus. अपवारित, Screened, Mālat. 93, 14.<BR> --Absol. अपवार्य (in theatrical language), Aside, apart, Śāk. 28, 17.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 1, 1296.<BR> 2. To conceal, Ragh. 17, 61.<BR> 3. To fill, Man. 2, 144.<BR> 4. To comprehend, Bhag. 13, 13.<BR> 5. To obstruct, Rām. 1, 26, 28.<BR> 6. To choose, MBh. 1, 4738.<BR> 7. To beg. आवृत,<BR> 1. Enclosed, surrounded, Man. 4, 73.<BR> 2. Invested.<BR> 3. Overspread.<BR> 4. Covered, Hit. 80, 15.<BR> 5. Filled, Chr. 293, 4 = Rigv. i. 87, 4.<BR> 6. Occupied, Rājat. 5, 235. m. A man of mixed origin, the son of a Brāhmaṇa by an Ugra woman, Man. 10, 15.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10,<BR> 1. To cover, Rām. 1, 32, 11.<BR> 2. To conceal, MBh. 3, 2370.<BR> 3. To keep off, MBh. 2, 2431.<BR> --With अपा अप-आ, To uncover, MBh. 1, 1341; to open, Bhag. 2, 32.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, पर्यावृत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0887-b " target="_blank">Page0887-b + 42</a>] Covered, Mālat. 90, 7.<BR> --With प्रा प्र-आ, To put on, MBh. 1, 2033. प्रावृत, Covered, enclosed, encompassed. m., f. ता, and n. A wrapper, a cloak, a veil.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To stop, MBh. 3, 363.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To cover, MBh. 3, 2310.<BR> 2. To shut, MBh. 1, 8343.<BR> 3. To stop, MBh. 3, 10329. समावृत,<BR> 1. Surrounded, encompassed, Rām. 3, 54, 15.<BR> 2. Enclosed.<BR> 3. Concealed, Chr. 32, 32.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus., or i. 10, वरय, To ask, Rām. 2, 11, 9.<BR> --With नि नि, To surround, Chr. 296, 3 = Rigv. i. 112, 3. निवृत, m., f. ता, and n. A wrapper, a cloak, a veil.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To surround, MBh. 1, 4961.<BR> 2. To protect, Chr. 42, 15.<BR> 3. To stop, to hinder, MBh. 1, 8172.<BR> 4. To draw back from (abl.), Bhartṛ. 2, 64.<BR> 5. To with hold, Hit. iii. d. 10.<BR> 6. To interdict, Pañc. 28, 19; Daśak. in Chr. 181, 7.<BR> 7. To exclude, Man. 9, 221. निवारित,<BR> 1. Opposed, Pañc. 247, 20.<BR> 2. Stopped, Lass. 18, 1. अ-निवार्य, adj. Irresistible, Chr. 45, 7. दुर्निवार्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. Difficult to be kept off, MBh. 12, 3770.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To keep off, MBh. 1, 1756.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, To obstruct, Mālat. 11, 16.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निर्-वृत,<BR> 1. Free from cares, Hit. 50, 6.<BR> 2. Happy, satisfied, Man. 1, 54.<BR> 3. Enraptured, Vikr. 71, 12. n. A house.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-निर्वृत + म्, adv. cheerlessly, Hit. ii. d. 143.<BR> --With परि परि, To surround, Vikr. d. 44; MBh. 1, 3. अ-परिवृत, adj. Unenclosed, Man. 8, 238.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10,<BR> 1. To surround, Pañc. ii. d. 23; Chr. 42, 9.<BR> 2. To cover, Chr. 4, 20.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, Caus. To surround, MBh. 3, 10234.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To cover, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 25.<BR> 2. To put [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-a " target="_blank">Page0888-a + 45</a>] on, MBh. 3, 2977.<BR> 3. To choose, MBh. 3, 17186.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To guard, MBh. 3, 10474.<BR> 2. To expose for choice, Chr. 8, 31.<BR> 3. To prefer, MBh. 3, 10810.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus., or i. 10,<BR> 1. To keep off, MBh. 4, 1896.<BR> 2. To oppose, Rām. 3, 49, 22. अ-प्रतिवारित, adj. Not prohibited, Man. 8, 360.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To open, Chr. 294, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 4 (ved. आवर्, aor.); MBh. 1, 6275.<BR> 2. To disclose, Rājat. 5, 185; to reveal, MBh. 2, 6925.<BR> 3. To woo, MBh. 1, 4413. वि-वृत,<BR> 1. Opened, Hit. 76, 6.<BR> 2. Naked, MBh. 1, 2924.<BR> 3. Expanded.<BR> 4. Displayed, Man. 7, 102.<BR> 5. Exposed, discovered.<BR> 6. Explained, expounded.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. without showing a weak side, MBh. 1, 5559.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To cover, Vikr. 47, 12; MBh. 2, 2623; to hide, Vikr. 43, 5.<BR> 2. To secure, Man. 7, 102.<BR> 3. To restrain, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 27. संवृत,<BR> 1. Covered, Hit. ii. d. 139.<BR> 2. Concealed, Ragh. 7, 27.<BR> 3. Surrounded, MBh. 3, 571.<BR> 4. Closed.<BR> 5. Compressed.<BR> 6. Secured, Pañc. 91, 2.<BR> 7. Attended, Johns. Sel. 59, 178.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, (m. or n.), the name of a hell, Man. 4, 81.<BR> स-, adj. decently dressed, Man. 2, 193 (v. r.).<BR> --Caus. To keep off, MBh. 3, 14994.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To cover, Chr. 36, 23 (imperf. without augment).<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. wara; A.S. ware, heed; O.H.G. wâr, verus; Goth. varjan; A.S. wreon, To cover; warian, werian, arcere; O.H.G. wari, depulsio; werna; A.S. wearne, obstaculum; O.H.G. warnôn; A.S. warnian, wearnian, cavere, prohibere; Goth. viljan; A.S. willan, velle; Goth. valjan; O.H.G. weljan, eligere; Lat. perhaps aperio, operio; probably velum, velare; verus, valeo, valor; velle; ἐρύω, ἀρνέομαι, ὄρομαι, ὤρα, εὑρίσκω, ἀρά, ἀρείων, ἄριστος, ἦρα, βούλομαι, βουλή, βελτίων, βέλτιστος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्ववृत
ऊर्ध्व- + वृत ऊर्ध्व- + वृत, adj. worn over the shoulder, Man. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवृत
स्वयम्- + वृत स्वयम्- + वृत, adj. chosen by one's self, Vikr. d. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0886-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंह्
1. वृंह् वृंह्, बृंह् बृंह्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To grow, to increase.<BR> 2. To roar, Śiś. 17, 31 (Ātm.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वृंहित.<BR> 1. Increased.<BR> 2. Cerished, MBh. 2, 2589.<BR> 3. Nourished. n. The roar of elephants, Kir. 7, 39.<BR> --Caus. To augment, MBh. 3, 11334.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, Caus. To augment, Dev. 8, 8. उपवृंहित,<BR> 1. Collected from.<BR> 2. Possessed of, endowed with, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 6.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To augment, MBh. 1, 260.<BR> --Cf. वृह्; βράχω, βράζω, βράγχος, βρόγχος, βρόχθος, probably also βράσσω, and βρυχάομαι; ῥόχθος, ὀρεχθέω, ῥαχία, ῥέγχω, ῥόγχος, and probably ῥύγχος, ῥυζέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंह्
† 2. वृंह् वृंह्, बृंह् बृंह्, i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहण|वृंहणः
वृंहण वृंहण, i. e. 1. वृंह् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Nourishing.<BR> II. m. A kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्
† वृक् वृक्, i. 1. Ātm. To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक|वृकः
वृक वृक, perhaps akin to व्रश्च्,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A wolf, Pañc. 19, 13.<BR> 2. A crow.<BR> 3. A jackal.<BR> 4. Turpentine.<BR> 5. Compounded perfume.<BR> 6. A tree. Sesbana grandiflora.<BR> II. f. का, A plant, Cissampelos hexandra.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vulfs; A.S. wulf; λύκος; Lat. lupus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृक
अ- + वृक अ- + वृक, adj. secure, Chr. 288, 15 = Rigv. i. 48, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालावृक|शालावृकः
शाला- + वृक शाला- + वृक, m. 1. a jackal, Draup. 6, 8. 2. a monkey. 3. a cat. 4. a dog. 5. a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकोदर|वृकोदरः
वृकोदर वृकोदर, i. e. वृक-उदर, m. A name of Bhīma, Johns. Sel. 12, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्कक
वृक्कक वृक्कक, m. The kidney, Yājñ. 3, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष्
† वृक्ष् वृक्ष्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To select.<BR> 2. To cover.<BR> 3. To keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष|वृक्षः
वृक्ष वृक्ष, probably akin to वृह्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0889-a " target="_blank">Page0889-a + 44</a>] m. A tree, Man. 1, 47; Pañc. iii. d. 107.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रवृक्ष
असि-पत्र- + वृक्ष असि-पत्र- + वृक्ष, m. a fabulous tree in hell, Ragh. 14, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पवृक्ष|कल्पवृक्षः
कल्प- + वृक्ष कल्प- + वृक्ष, m. a tree yielding all wishes (cf. कल्पतरु), Megh. 63; Vikr. d. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरवृक्ष|क्षीरवृक्षः
क्षीर- + वृक्ष क्षीर- + वृक्ष, m. the glomerous fig-tree, Ficus glomerata, Śāk. 54, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यवृक्ष|चैत्यवृक्षः
चैत्य- + वृक्ष चैत्य- + वृक्ष, m. a fig-tree growing in a holy place, Man. 9, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपवृक्ष|दीपवृक्षः
दीप- + वृक्ष दीप- + वृक्ष, m. the stand of a lamp, Rām. 2, 5, 18 Gorr.; a lamp on a stand, a lantern, MBh. 12, 7402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृक्ष
निस्- + वृक्ष निस्- + वृक्ष, adj. deprived of trees, MBh. 5, 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0888-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षक|वृक्षकः
वृक्षक वृक्ष + क, m.<BR> 1. A tree.<BR> 2. A particular tree, Wrightea antidysenterica.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0889-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृक्षक
अ- + वृक्षक अ- + वृक्षक, adj. deprived of trees, Rām. 4, 44, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0889-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभिद्
वृक्षभिद् वृक्ष-भिद्, f. An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0889-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमय
