अ-व्याप्य- + वृत्ति अ-व्याप्य- + वृत्ति, f. (in logic) limited in space, as the special qualities of soul and æther, sc. knowledge, etc., and sound, Bhāṣāp. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छवृत्ति
उञ्छ- + वृत्ति उञ्छ- + वृत्ति, m. a gleaner, Man. 8, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंवृत्ति
एवम्- + वृत्ति एवम्- + वृत्ति, adj. so conditioned, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 212 = Pañc. i. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ववृत्ति
गर्व- + वृत्ति गर्व- + वृत्ति, f. state of pride, female arrogance, Vikr. d. 53 (व्रत-अपदेश-उज्झित-गर्व-वृत्ति, adj. having abandoned her pride under the pretext of a vow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवृत्ति|चित्तवृत्तिः
चित्त- + वृत्ति चित्त- + वृत्ति, f. 1. feeling, sentiments, Śāk. 4, 11; Ṛt. 6, 26. 2. thinking, thought, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवृत्ति|ज्येष्ठवृत्तिः
ज्येष्ठ- + वृत्ति ज्येष्ठ- + वृत्ति, adj. acting as an elder brother ought to act, Man. 9, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्येष्ठवृत्ति|अज्येष्ठवृत्तिः
अ-ज्येष्ठ- + वृत्ति अ-ज्येष्ठ- + वृत्ति, adj. not acting as an elder brother ought, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वृत्ति
तद्-वृत्ति तद्-वृत्ति, adj. abiding in that, i. e. as शब्दत्व in शब्द, Bhāṣāp. 60, cf. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोवृत्ति
तमस्- + वृत्ति तमस्- + वृत्ति, f. darkness, Vikr. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वृत्ति|दुर्वृत्तिः
दुस्- + वृत्ति दुस्- + वृत्ति, f. 1. a bad action, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 799. 2. distress, MBh. 13, 2389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवृत्ति|द्यूतवृत्तिः
द्यूत- + वृत्ति द्यूत- + वृत्ति, m. the keeper of a gaming house, Man. 3, 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यवृत्ति|धैर्यवृत्तिः
धैर्य- + वृत्ति धैर्य- + वृत्ति, adj. constant, Hit. ii. d. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गवृत्ति|पतंगवृत्ति
पतङ्ग- + वृत्ति पतङ्ग- + वृत्ति, adj. acting like a grasshopper (flying into a flame), Pañc. iii. d. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीनवृत्ति
पर-अधीन- + वृत्ति पर-अधीन- + वृत्ति, adj. dependent on another, Megh. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षवृत्ति|परोक्षवृत्तिः
परोक्ष- + वृत्ति परोक्ष- + वृत्ति,<BR> I. f. unseen, unwitnessed behaviour, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 610.<BR> II. adj. one whose behaviour is not witnessed by anybody, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलवृत्ति
प्रतिकूल- + वृत्ति प्रतिकूल- + वृत्ति, adj. opposing, Bhāg. P. 3, 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्यवृत्ति
भाग्य- + वृत्ति भाग्य- + वृत्ति, f. state of fortune, fortune, Rājat. 5, 261. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a " target="_blank">Page0895-a + 43</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकवृत्ति|वकवृत्तिः
वक- + वृत्ति वक- + वृत्ति, adj. living like cranes, a hypocritical devotee, Man. 4, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरावृत्ति|वागुरावृत्तिः
वागुरा- + वृत्ति वागुरा- + वृत्ति, m. one who subsists by catching wild animals, Man. 10, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यवृत्ति
वैश्य- + वृत्ति वैश्य- + वृत्ति, f. agriculture or trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्ति|शीलवृत्तिः
शील- + वृत्ति शील- + वृत्ति, f. virtue, Pañc. ii. d. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववृत्ति|श्ववृत्तिः
श्ववृत्ति श्ववृत्ति, i. e. श्वन्-, f. 1. life of a dog, Pañc. i. d. 300 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3292). 2. servitude, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवृत्ति|समवृत्तिः
सम- + वृत्ति सम- + वृत्ति, adj. equable, moderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्ति|साधुवृत्तिः
साधु- + वृत्ति साधु- + वृत्ति,<BR> I. f. the institutes or moral and ritual observances of the Hindus.<BR> II. adj. virtuous, Bhartṛ. 2, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववृत्ति
स्व- + वृत्ति स्व- + वृत्ति, adj. subsisting by one's own exertion, Cāṇ. 23 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0894-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिता
वृत्तिता वृत्ति + ता, f., and वृत्तित्व वृत्ति + त्व, n.<BR> 1. State of residing or being contained in, as the हेतु in the पक्ष, Bhāṣāp. 67 (त्व).<BR> 2. Profession, subsistence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्तवृत्तिता
अन्-आयत्त-वृत्तिता अन्-आयत्त-वृत्तिता (vb. यत्), f. independence, Hit. ii. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिमन्त्|वृत्तिमत्
वृत्तिमन्त् वृत्ति + मन्त्, adj. Thinking, Lass. 2. ed. 88, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्र|वृत्रः
वृत्र वृत्र, m.<BR> 1. The name of a demon slain by Indra, Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. i. 85, 9; Chr. 18, 41.<BR> 2. An enemy.<BR> 3. Darkness.<BR> 4. A cloud.<BR> 5. A mountain.<BR> 6. Sound.<BR> 7. A wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रहन्
वृत्रहन् वृत्र-हन्, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथा
वृथा वृथा, i. e. वर + था, adv.<BR> 1. Without pain (to one's own pleasure), Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 88, 6.<BR> 2. Without necessity, Man. 11, 144 (वृथा-आलम्भ, m. Cutting or plucking unnecessarily).<BR> 3. In vain, Man. 4, 63; vain, Pañc. i. d. 62.<BR> 4. Useless, fruitless, Pañc. iii. d. 31.<BR> 5. Foolishly, Vikr. 55, 20.<BR> 6. Wrongly, incorrectly, Śṛṅgārat. 21.<BR> 7. Without being sacrificed, Man. 5, 34; 4, 213.<BR> --Cf. ῥεῖα, βρᾶ, ῥᾷ, ῥάϊστος, ῥᾷδιος, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथासंकरजात
वृथासंकरजात वृथा-संकर-जात (vb. जन्), adj. Born in vain (i. e. one who [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b " target="_blank">Page0895-b + 44</a>] discharges not his duties), or by the mixture of different castes, Man. 5, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसान|वृधसानः
वृधसान वृधसान (vb. वृध्), m. A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध|वृद्धं|वृद्धः
वृद्ध वृद्ध,<BR> I. ptcple. of the pr. pass. of वृध्.<BR> 1. Old, ancient, aged, Vikr. d. 43. Comparat. ज्यायंस्, and वर्षीयंस्; superl. ज्येष्ठ, and वर्षिष्ठो, see s. v.<BR> 2. Wise, learned.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An old man.<BR> 2. A sage, a respectable man, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 7.<BR> III. n. Benzoin.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. वृध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलवृद्ध|कुलवृद्धः
कुल- + वृद्ध कुल- + वृद्ध, m. the senior of a tribe, Bhāg. P. 4, 9, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोवृद्ध
वयस्- + वृद्ध वयस्- + वृद्ध, adj. very old, Chr. 13, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यावयोवृद्ध
विद्या-वयस्- + वृद्ध विद्या-वयस्- + वृद्ध, adj. high in science and age, Hit. 41, 3, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबालवृद्ध
स-बाल- + वृद्ध स-बाल- + वृद्ध, adj. with children and old men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धत्व|वृद्धत्वं
वृद्धत्व वृद्ध + त्व, m. Old age, Pañc. 226, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धि|वृद्धिः
वृद्धि वृद्धि, i. e. वृध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Increase, Pañc. 187, 7; augmentation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 438.<BR> 2. Prosperity, Bhartṛ. 2, 82; Pañc. i. d. 382.<BR> 3. Wealth.<BR> 4. Interest, Man. 8, 143; Pañc. 88, 14 (द्वि-गुण-, Consisting in doubling the lent amount); usury.<BR> 5. Profit, gain, Man. 8, 401.<BR> 6. Extension of power or revenue, Pañc. i. d. 264.<BR> 7. A heap, a quantity, a multitude.<BR> 8. Rise, ascending.<BR> 9. The increase of the digits of the sun or moon.<BR> 10. The eleventh of the astronomical योगस्, or the principal star of the eleventh lunar mansion.<BR> 11. Cutting off.<BR> 12. (In law), Forfeiture.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृद्धि|कालवृद्धिः
काल- + वृद्धि काल- + वृद्धि, f. periodical, monthly interest, Man. 8, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदवृद्धि|कुसीदवृद्धिः
कुसीद- + वृद्धि कुसीद- + वृद्धि, f. interest on money, Man. 8, 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवृद्धि|चक्रवृद्धिः
चक्र- + वृद्धि चक्र- + वृद्धि, f. 1. interest agreed on the risk of safe carriage, Man. 8, 156. 2. interest upon interest, Man. 8, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिमन्त्|वृद्धिमत्
वृद्धिमन्त् वृद्धि + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Augmented, increased, increasing, Pañc. ii. d. 38; Bhartṛ. 2, 50.<BR> 2. Wealthy.<BR> 3. Prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0895-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्
वृध् वृध् (i. e. वि-ऋध्), i. 1, Ātm.; in the aor., fut., and condit., also Par. (in epic poetry also in the remaining forms, MBh. 1, 7864),<BR> 1. To grow, to increase, MBh. 1, 4865; Pañc. i. d. 408; iv. d. 66 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 781).<BR> 2. To prosper, Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. i. 112, 24 (वृधे, ved. infin.); MBh. 3, 12268; with दिष्ट्या, properly, to prosper by fortune: it is used as a mode of giving joy; दिष्ट्या वर्धसे, I give you joy, Vikr. 8, 2; with the instr. of the object of gratulation, Vikr. 11, 11, I give you joy on account of.<BR> 3. To last, Rājat. 5, 461.<BR> 4. To augment, MBh. 1, 5540.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. वर्धामान, m.<BR> 1. A shallow earthen platter, used also as top to water-jars, a lid.<BR> 2. A sort of riddle.<BR> 3. A mystical figure.<BR> 4. Viṣṇu.<BR> 5. The name of a district and city, Burdwan, Pañc. 134, 2 (f. ना, Lass. 28, 9).<BR> 6. The castor-oil tree.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वृद्ध (see also s. v.).<BR> 1. Grown up, Vikr. d. 148.<BR> 2. Full-grown.<BR> 3. Heaped.<BR> 4. Large.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. वर्धय,<BR> 1. To augment, Man. 6, 23; Hit. ii. d. 88 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3228).<BR> 2. To make powerful, Hit. iii. d. 3.<BR> 3. To exalt, Man. 9, 109. वर्धित, Filled, full, Man. 3, 224.<BR> --i. 10, † To speak, to shine.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To increase, Man. 2, 94.<BR> 2. To abound, Man. 3, 259.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To grow up, Pañc. i. d. 228.<BR> 2. To increase, Rājat. 5, 194.<BR> --Caus. To rear, Śāk. 100, 15.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To increase, Man. 4, 42. प्रवृद्ध,<BR> 1. Grown up, Rājat. 5, 8; full-grown.<BR> 2. Expanded.<BR> 3. Large, Rām. 3, 53, 15.<BR> 4. Swollen.<BR> 5. Deep.<BR> 6. Violent, Ṛt. 1, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-,<BR> I. adj. fullgrown.<BR> II. m. a proper name.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b " target="_blank">Page0896-b + 42</a>] अतिप्र अति-प्र, अतिप्रवृद्ध (rather प्रवृद्ध with अति), One who behaves too arrogantly, Man. 9, 320.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, Caus. To cause to prosper, MBh. 1, 4350.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To increase too much, Pañc. i. d. 201.<BR> 2. To increase, MBh. 1, 2992; to grow, Pañc. i. d. 47.<BR> 3. To prosper, MBh. 3, 16881. विवृद्ध, Very large, Pañc. i. d. 6.<BR> --With संवि सम्-वि, To increase, MBh. 1, 4977.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To grow up, Sāv. 2, 10. संवृद्ध, Increased, Rājat. 5, 382.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to grow, to plant, Pañc. i. d. 275.<BR> 2. To augment, Vikr. d. 158; MBh. 2, 1601.<BR> 3. To cherish, Rām. 1, 39, 18; to bring up, Pañc. 182, 13.<BR> 4. To nourish, Hit. 58, 10, M.M. संवर्धित, Cherished, brought up, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 4.<BR> --Cf. Goth. valdan; A.S. waldan, and at least as akin, Goth. vaurts; O.H.G. uurza; βραδινός, ῥαδινός, ῥίζα, βλαστός, βλασταίνω, βλωθρός (βλωθ = ved. व्राध् in व्राधन्त्); A.S. weald; ἄλσος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवृद्ध
तपोवृद्ध तपोव्˚, i. e. तपस्-, adj. abounding in austerities, pious, Chr. 48, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधु
वृधु वृधु, m. A proper name, Man. 10, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्त|वृंत|वृंतं|वृन्तं
वृन्त वृन्त, n.<BR> 1. The nipple.<BR> 2. The foot, stalk of a leaf or fruit, Mālat. 16, 20.<BR> 3. The stand of a water-jar.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवृन्त|तालवृंत|तालवृन्तं
ताल- + वृन्त ताल- + वृन्त, n. a fan (properly a leaf of the palm-tree), Rām. 5, 20, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवृन्त|दीर्घवृन्तः
दीर्घ- + वृन्त दीर्घ- + वृन्त, m. a tree, Calosanthes indica Bl. Suśr. 2, 13, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनवृन्त|स्तनवृंत|स्तनवृन्तः
स्तन- + वृन्त स्तन- + वृन्त, m. a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्तिका|वृंतिका
वृन्तिका वृन्तिका, i. e. वृन्त + क, f. A small stalk, MBh. 1, 1443.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्द|वृंद|वृन्दं|वृन्दः
वृन्द वृन्द,<BR> I. adj. Many, all.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A heap, Chr. 25, 62.<BR> 2. A multitude, Pañc. 222, 23; Bhartṛ. 3, 47.<BR> III. f. दा, Holy basil, Ocymum sanctum.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवृन्द
एक- + वृन्द एक- + वृन्द, m. a disease of the throat, Suśr. 1, 306, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0896-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दार|वृंदार|वृन्दारः
वृन्दार वृन्दार, i. e. वृन्द + आर (cf. the next), adj. Comparat. वृन्दीयंस्; superl. वृन्दिष्ठ.<BR> 1. Eminent.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Lass. 2. ed. 88, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दारक|वृंदारक|वृन्दारकः
वृन्दारक वृन्दार + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Much, great.<BR> 2. Excellent, chief, venerable, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 45.<BR> 3. Handsome.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The head of a crowd or herd.<BR> 2. A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिन्
ऽवृन्दिन् -वृन्दिन्, in अश्व-, i. e. -वृन्द + इन्, adj. Consisting in a multitude of horses, MBh. 5, 5703.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिष्ठ|वृंदिष्ठ|वृन्दिष्ठः
वृन्दिष्ठ वृन्दिष्ठ, वृन्दीयंस् वृन्दीयंस्, see वृन्दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्
† वृश् वृश्, i. 4, Par. To choose, to select (cf. वृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिक|वृश्चिकः
वृश्चिक वृश्चिक (vb. व्रश्च्), m.<BR> 1. A scorpion, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 27.<BR> 2. The sign Scorpio.<BR> 3. A caterpillar.<BR> 4. A crab.<BR> 5. A centipede.<BR> 6. A sort of beetle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवृश्चिक
पत्र- + वृश्चिक पत्र- + वृश्चिक, m. a certain poisonous animal, Suśr. 2, 287, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्
वृष् वृष् (probably वि-ऋष्, q. cf.), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 5464),<BR> 1. To rain, Rām. 1, 9, 56.<BR> 2. To shed, MBh. 1, 1419.<BR> 3. To moisten, Dev. 3, 2.<BR> 4. † To hurt.<BR> 5. † To weary.<BR> 6. † To give.<BR> 7. † To engender.<BR> 8. † To have supreme power.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. वर्षन्त्, Rain, Man. 4, 38.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pf. pass. अ-वृष्ट, adj. Not having rained, Pañc. 51, 16.<BR> --Caus. To induce to rain, MBh. 3, 9991.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. †<BR> 1. To be possessed of generative power.<BR> 2. To be powerful.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To shower on, Rām. 2, 67, 8; Vikr. 54, 6.<BR> 2. To rain, MBh. 1, 4062; figuratively, Man. 9, 304. अभिवृष्ट, Rained on, extinguished by rain, Vikr. d. 125.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निर्वृष्ट, Having done raining, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b " target="_blank">Page0897-b + 41</a>] Ragh. 4, 15 (Calc.).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To begin to rain, Pañc. 169, 7.<BR> 2. To rain, Naiṣ. 22, 41. प्रवृष्त, One who has caused to rain, Utt. Rāmac. 158, 6.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To rain fast, Man. 9, 304.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To assail, Chr. 34, 15.<BR> --With वि वि, To deluge with rain.<BR> --Cf. ἀπο-έρσει, etc.; ἕρση; akin is βρέχω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष|वृषं|वृषः
वृष वृष् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bull, Hit. 58, 16.<BR> 2. The sign Taurus.<BR> 3. A rat (as in वृष-दंशक, m. A cat, Sāh. D. 303, 6).<BR> 4. As latter part of comp. nouns, Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR> II. f. षी, The seat of the religious student, made of Kuśa grass (cf. Rām. 3, 49, 23). MBh. 13, 462.<BR> III. n. A peacock's tail.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मावृष|क्ष्मावृषः
क्ष्मा- + वृष क्ष्मा- + वृष, m. a lord of the earth, Rājat. 5, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृष|गोवृषः
गो- + वृष गो- + वृष, m. 1. the bull kept for impregnating cows, Man. 9, 150. 2. a bull, Pañc. i. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृष
निस्- + वृष निस्- + वृष, adj. deprived of bulls, Hariv. 4108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषक
वृषक वृष + क, m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषखादि
वृषखादि वृषखादि, i. e. वृषन्-खादि, adj. Adorned or endowed with rain, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण|वृषणः
वृषण वृषण, i. e. वृष् + अन, m. The testicles or scrotum, Man. 8, 283; Pañc. 10, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. as akin, ὄρχις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णवृषण
तीक्ष्ण- + वृषण तीक्ष्ण- + वृषण, m. a proper name, Pañc. 135, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषध्वज|वृषध्वजः
वृषध्वज वृष-ध्वज,<BR> I. adj. Having as emblem a bull.<BR> II. m. Śiva, Johns. Sel. 89, 25; Kir. 13, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषन्
वृषन् वृष् + अन्, m.<BR> I. adj. Raining, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. i. 64, 1.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The dropping beverage, called Soma, Chr. 291, 7 = Rigv. i. 85, 7.<BR> 2. A bull.<BR> 3. A horse.<BR> 4. A name of Indra, Ragh. 10, 53.<BR> 5. Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0897-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभ|वृषभः
वृषभ वृष-भ (vb. भा),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bull, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M. (दुष्ट-, A malicious bull).<BR> 2. The orifice of the ear.<BR> 3. An elephant's ear.<BR> 4. As latter part of comp. words, Preeminent, excellent.<BR> II. f. भी, A widow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृषभ|गोवृषभः
गो- + वृषभ गो- + वृषभ, m. a bull, MBh. 1, 3935.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवरवृषभ
नर-वर- + वृषभ नर-वर- + वृषभ, m. a most preeminent man, Pañc. i. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषय|वृषयः
वृषय वृषय, m. Refuge, shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषल|वृषलः
वृषल वृषल (from वृष्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. A Śūdra, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 1, cf. 4.<BR> 3. A man of the three first classes who, by neglecting his religious duties, has lost his caste.<BR> 4. A sinner, Lass. Pentap. p. 70, v. 73.<BR> 5. Garlic.<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. A Śūdra woman, Man. 3, 19; Pañc. iii. d. 218 (but cf. Kāśīkh. 40, 93).<BR> 2. A woman during menstruation.<BR> 3. A barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलक|वृषलकः
वृषलक वृषल + क, m. A poor Śūdra, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्य
वृषस्य वृषस्य, a denomin. derived from वृष with स्य, Par. To be warm, to long for sexual intercourse, Ragh. 12, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपि|वृषाकपिः
वृषाकपि वृषाकपि (probably वृषन्-कपि),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. Agni.<BR> II. f. पायी.<BR> 1. Lakṣmī.<BR> 2. Gaurī.<BR> 3. Swāhā, the wife of Agni.<BR> 4. Śaci, the wife of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टि|वृष्टिः
वृष्टि वृष्टि, i. e. वृष् + ति, f. Rain, Vikr. d. 154.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृष्टि|अवृष्टिः
अ- + वृष्टि अ- + वृष्टि, f. drought, Pañc. 50, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्यवृष्टि
प्राज्य- + वृष्टि प्राज्य- + वृष्टि, adj. sending plenty of rain, Śāk. d. 193.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलावृष्टि|शिलावृष्टिः
शिला- + वृष्टि शिला- + वृष्टि, f. hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णि|वृष्णिः
वृष्णि वृष्णि, i. e. वृष् + नि,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Passionate, angry.<BR> 2. Heretical.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ram.<BR> 2. Indra.<BR> 3. Agni.<BR> 4. Viṣṇu.<BR> 5. One of the descendants of Yadu, Bhag. 10, 37.<BR> 6. The name of a class of Kṣatriyas and Vaiśyas, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b " target="_blank">Page0898-b + 40</a>] Pañc. iii. d. 268.<BR> 7. Air, wind.<BR> 8. A ray of light.<BR> --Cf. ἀρν in ἀρνός, ἀρνειός, ῥήν, ἕρσαι, ἔριϕος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
1. वृह् वृह्, बृह् बृह्, i. 6, Par. To make any effort, to raise.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To raise, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 9.<BR> 2. To pull out, MBh. 1, 7307.<BR> 3. To draw forth, Man. 1, 14. परि-वृढ, see separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
† 2. वृह् वृह्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To increase; cf. वृध्.<BR> 2. To roar; cf. वृंह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतिका
वृहतिका वृहतिका, i. e. वृहन्त् + ई + क, f.<BR> 1. An upper garment, a mantle, a wrapper, Kir. 5, 45.<BR> 2. A small sort of egg plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहन्त्|वृहत्
वृहन्त् वृहन्त्, see बृहन्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पति|वृहस्पतिः
वृहस्पति वृहस्पति, see बृहस्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वॄ
वॄ वॄ, † बॄ बॄ, ii. 9, Par. Ātm. see वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वे
वे वे, i. 1, Par. Ātm. To weave, MBh. 1, 806.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To warp, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 7.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To work in the woof, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 7 (‘Who is the warp and the weft of the universe’).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्रोत, i. e. प्र-उत.<BR> 1. Sewn or stitched.<BR> 2. Joined.<BR> 3. Tied, strung.<BR> 4. Set, inlaid.<BR> 5. Pierced, Ragh. 9, 75.<BR> 6. Put on (a spit), MBh. 1, 4316; impaled. n. Cloth.<BR> --Cf. ἤτριον, ὀθόνη; O.H.G. wât; A.S. waed, vestimentum; O.H.G. weban; A.S. wefan (= the regular Sskr. Caus., which would have been वापय or व्ăपय), waefels, weft; probably also ὀπέας, ἠπητής; akin at least is also ὑϕή, ὑϕαίνω; Lat. viere, vimen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेक्ष्
† वेक्ष् वेक्ष्, व्लेक्ष् व्लेक्ष्, i. 10, Par. To see (cf. अव-ईक्ष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेग|वेगः
वेग वेग, i. e. विज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Speed, Vikr. 6, 6; Pañc. ii. d. 174; 258, 21 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a " target="_blank">Page0899-a + 41</a>] (वेगाद् वेगं गम्, To increase one's speed more and more).<BR> 2. The flight of an arrow, Kir. 13, 24.<BR> 3. Impetus, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 11; breeze, Mālat. 127, 12.<BR> 4. Stream, Hit. iv. d. 59.<BR> 5. Sudden impulse, inconsiderate haste, Pañc. i. d. 122.<BR> 6. Energy.<BR> 7. Strength, Rām. 5, 3, 42.<BR> 8. Pleasure.<BR> 9. Love.<BR> 10. External indication of any internal effect, proceeding from passion, medicine, poison, etc., as convulsion, sweat, etc., Daśak. in Chr. 187, 16.<BR> 11. Evacuation of natural excretions.<BR> 12. Semen virile.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डवेग
चण्ड- + वेग चण्ड- + वेग, adj. possessed of violent speed or movement, Rām. 5, 74, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेग
निस्- + वेग निस्- + वेग, adj. quiet, Rām. 1, 56, 9 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावेग|महावेगः
महा- + वेग महा- + वेग,<BR> I. adj. very swift, Chr. 29, 33.<BR> II. m. a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवेग|विषवेगः
विष- + वेग विष- + वेग, m. absorption of venom, as shown by some bodily changes, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेगम्
स-वेग + म् स-वेग + म्, adv. hastily, Pañc. 89, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0898-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगतस्
वेगतस् वेग + तस्, adv. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवन्त्|वेगवत्
वेगवन्त् वेग + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Swift, Rām. 3, 50, 5.<BR> 2. Impetuous, Lass. 2. ed. 79, 77; 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगित|वेगितः
वेगित वेगित, i. e. वेग + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Quickened.<BR> 2. Swift, MBh. 8, 3048.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिता
वेगिता वेगिता, i. e. वेगिन् + ता, f. Speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिन्
वेगिन् वेगिन्, i. e. वेग + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Swift, Kir. 8, 39.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A courier.<BR> 2. A hawk.<BR> III. f. नी, A river, Rām. 2, 55, 6, ed. Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेडा
वेडा वेडा, f. A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण्
वेण् वेण्, see वेन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण|वेणः
वेण वेण, m.<BR> 1. The son of a Vaideha by an Ambaṣṭha woman, Man. 10, 19.<BR> 2. A proper name, 7, 41.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवेणा
कृष्ण- + वेणा कृष्ण- + वेणा and तुङ्ग-वेणा, f. names of rivers, MBh. 3, 8180; 14233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणि|वेणिः
वेणि<BR> I. and वेणी वेणी̆ (vb. व्ê),<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b " target="_blank">Page0899-b + 43</a>] Weaving.<BR> 2. Unornamented and braided hair, as worn by widows and women whose husbands are absent, viz. twisted together in a single braid, Megh. 97 (णि); 18 (णी).<BR> 3. A braid of hair in general, Rājat. 5, 449 (as royal ornament?).<BR> 4. Assemblage of water, as the conflux of rivers.<BR> II. वेणी वेणी, f.<BR> 1. An ewe.<BR> 2. Stream.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवेणी
एक-वेṇई̆ एक-वेणी̆, f. a single braid (as a token of mourning), Śāk. 106, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवेणि
एक-वेṇई̆ एक-वेणी̆, f. a single braid (as a token of mourning), Śāk. 106, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवेणी
पुष्प-वेणी पुष्प-वेणी, f. 1. a chaplet, Rām. 3, 68, 41. 2. the name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्र-वेणी̆ प्र-वेणी̆, f. 1. unornamented hair, as worn by widows or women in absence of their husbands, Ragh. 15, 30. 2. a coloured woollen cover, MBh. 15, 727.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणि|प्रवेणिः
प्र-वेणी̆ प्र-वेणी̆, f. 1. unornamented hair, as worn by widows or women in absence of their husbands, Ragh. 15, 30. 2. a coloured woollen cover, MBh. 15, 727.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणु|वेणुः
वेणु वेणु, m.<BR> 1. A bambu, Hit. iv. d. 26; reed, Pañc. iii. d. 57.<BR> 2. A flute, a pipe, Brahmav. 2, 50.<BR> 3. The name of a king.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणु|त्रिवेणुः
त्रि- + वेणु त्रि- + वेणु,<BR> I. adj. epithet of a chariot, ornamented with three flags(?), Bhāg. P. 4, 26, 1.<BR> II. m. a part of a chariot, MBh. 7, 1626.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुक|वेणुकं|वेणुकः
वेणुक वेणु + क, n. A pike used for driving an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुध्म|वेणुध्मः
वेणुध्म वेणु-ध्म (vb. ध्मा), m. The player on a flute or pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतन|वेतनं
वेतन वेतन (probably a form of वर्तन, q. cf.), n.<BR> 1. Hire, wages, Pañc. 22, 10; Nal. 15, 6.<BR> 2. Livelihood, Hit. 88, 17.<BR> 3. Silver.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयवेतन
उभय- + वेतन उभय- + वेतन, adj. 1. accepting wages from his master and his master's enemy, Pañc. 22, 10. 2. living in two elements (water and land), Hit. 88, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेतन|कृतवेतनः
कृत- + वेतन कृत- + वेतन, adj. hired, Yājñ. 2, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेतन
निस्- + वेतन निस्- + वेतन, adj. receiving no wages, Rājat. 5, 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनिन्
ऽवेतनिन् -वेतनिन्, i. e. वेतन + इन्, adj. Receiving wages, in कुप्य-वेतन + इन्, Receiving a very small pay, MBh. 3, 657.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस|वेतसः
वेतस वे + तस् + अ, m. The ratan, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a " target="_blank">Page0900-a + 42</a>] Calamus rotang, Nal. 12, 112; Vāmanap. ap. Aufrecht, Ujjvalad. 251, n.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. wîda; A.S. widhig; Lat. vitex, vitis; ἰτέα, οἶσος, οἶνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0899-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस्वन्त्|वेतस्वत्
वेतस्वन्त् वे + तस् + वन्त् (cf. the last), adj., f. वती, Reedy, abounding in reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेताल|वेतालः
वेताल वेताल, m.<BR> 1. i. e. अव-इत-आलय, A sprite haunting cemeteries and animating dead bodies, Lass. 5, 13; Hit. 65, 12.<BR> 2. (for वेत्र + आल, cf. वेत्रधर), A door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्तृ
वेत्तृ वेत्तृ, i. e. विद् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Knowing, understanding, acquainted with, Rām. 3, 53, 41.<BR> 2. Who obtains or acquires.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A sage.<BR> 2. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्र|वेत्रः
वेत्र वे + त्र,<BR> I. m. A reed, a cane, the ratan, Nal. 12, 5.<BR> II. n. A staff, Pañc. 16, 1; the staff of a door-keeper, Ragh. 6, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रधर|वेत्रधरः
वेत्रधर वेत्रधर, i. e. वेत्र + धृ + अ,<BR> 1. m., f. रा, A door-keeper, Ragh. 6, 82 (रा).<BR> 2. m. A mace-bearer, a staffbearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रवती
वेत्रवती वेत्रवती, i. e. वेत्र + वन्त् + ई, f.<BR> 1. The name of a river, Megh. 25.<BR> 2. A proper name, Śāk. 61, 15 (or, a female door-keeper, cf. 16 and वेत्रिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रिन्
वेत्रिन् वेत्रिन्, i. e. वेत्र + इन्, m. A door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेथ्
वेथ् वेथ्, see विथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद|वेदः
वेद वेद, i. e. विद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Knowledge.<BR> 2. The generic name for the sacred writings of the Hindus, especially for the four collections called ऋग्वेद, i. e. ऋच्-, यजुर्वेद, i. e. यजुस्-, सामवेद, i. e. सामन्-, and अथर्ववेद, i. e. अथर्वन्-, Man. 1, 21; Pañc. iii. d. 64; 205 (pl.); MBh. in Chr. 94, 2 (three Vedas, i. e. the three first).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद|अवेदः
अ- + वेद अ- + वेद, m. oblivion, Man. 5, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेद|आयुर्वेदः|आयुर्व्वेदः
आयुर्वेद आयुर्वेद, i. e. आयुस्-, m. 1. the science [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b " target="_blank">Page0900-b + 45</a>] of medicine, Suśr. 1, 1, 12. 2. the writings of authority on medicine, Hariv. 1539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रवेद|क्षत्रवेदः
क्षत्र- + वेद क्षत्र- + वेद, m. the Veda of the second caste (science of government, politics), Rām. 1, 65, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ववेद|गंधर्ववेद|गन्धर्ववेदः|गन्धर्व्ववेद|गन्धर्व्ववेदः
गन्धर्व- + वेद गन्धर्व- + वेद, m. the science of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वेद|चतुर्वेदः
चतुर्- + वेद चतुर्- + वेद,<BR> I. m. pl. 1. the four Vedas Hariv. 14074. 2. a kind of Manes, MBh. 2, 463.<BR> II. adj. 1. containing the four Vedas, ib. 3, 13560. 2. conversant with the four Vedas, Hariv. 7993.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेद|त्रिवेदः
त्रि- + वेद त्रि- + वेद, adj. conversant with the three (first) Vedas (i. e. the Ṛc, Yajus, and Sāman), Man. 2, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वेद
दुस्- + वेद दुस्- + वेद, adj. 1. Difficult to be known, Rām. 4, 46, 2. 2. unlearned, MBh. 3, 13437.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वेद|धनुर्वेदः|धनुर्व्वेदः
धनुर्वेद धनुर्वेद, i. e. धनुस्-, m. the knowledge of the bow, of archery, the title of a sacred work, Rām. 5, 32, 9; Johns. Sel. 57, 161 (with साक्षात्, the embodied Dhanurveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेद|परिवेदः
परि- + वेद परि- + वेद, m. complete knowledge, MBh. 3, 13462.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदन|वेदनं
वेदन वेदन, i. e. विद् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. ना.<BR> 1. Perception, knowledge conveyed by the senses.<BR> 2. Knowledge.<BR> 3. Pain, Pañc. 146, 23 (ना); agony, Pañc. 44, 2 (ना).<BR> 4. Presenting.<BR> 5. The ceremony of holding the ends of a mantle, to be observed by a Śūdra female on her marriage with a man of either of the three first classes.<BR> II. n. Marrying, Man. 10, 24; marriage, 9, 65.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसववेदना
प्रसव- + वेदना प्रसव- + वेदना, f. pains in labour, Pañc. 228, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्
वेदविद् वेद-विद्, adj. and sbst. Versed in the Vedas, Chr. 27, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस्
वेदस् वेदस्, i. e. विद् + अस्,<BR> I. m. The Vedas collectively.<BR> II. n. Wealth, Lass. 100, 5 = Rigv. vii. 15, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्ववेदस्
विश्व- + वेदस् विश्व- + वेदस्, adj. and sbst. one who knows all things, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8; a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ववेदस्|सर्व्ववेदस्
सर्व- + वेदस् सर्व- + वेदस्, m. a man who, at the conclusion of the विश्वजित् sacrifice, divides all his property amongst the priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0900-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस
ऽवेदस -वेदस् + अ, at the end of a comp. for वेदस्, in सर्व-,<BR> I. n. All one's property, Man. 6, 38.<BR> II. adj. One who has given all his property at a sacred rite, Man. 11, 1, Calc. (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाङ्ग|वेदांग|वेदाङ्गं
वेदाङ्ग वेदाङ्ग, i. e. वेद-अङ्ग, m. A sacred science connected with the Vedas; six sciences come under this denomination, viz. pronunciation, grammar, prosody, explanation of obscure terms, description of religious rites, and astronomy, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 10; Lass. 49, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्त|वेदांत|वेदान्तः
वेदान्त वेदान्त, i. e. वेद-अन्त, m.<BR> 1. The complete Veda, Man. 2, 160.<BR> 2. A philosophical system based particularly on the Upaniṣads, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, sqq.; 203, 24.<BR> 3. pl. Works concerning this philosophy, Vikr. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तग|वेदांतग
वेदान्तग वेदान्त-ग (vb. गम्), वेदान्तज्ञ वेदान्त-ज्ञ (vb. ज्ञा), and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तिन्|वेदांतिन्
वेदान्तिन् वेदान्तिन्, i. e. वेदान्त + इन्, m. A follower of the वेदान्त philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदि|वेदिः
वेदि<BR> I. and वेदी वेदी̆, f.<BR> 1. Ground prepared for sacrifice, an altar, Śāk. 31, 6; Nal. 1, 9; Rām. 1, 21, 5.<BR> 2. A quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or palace, usually furnished with a raised floor or seat, and covered with a roof supported by pillars, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 16.<BR> 3. A bench, ib. 3, 23, 17.<BR> 4. A seal-ring.<BR> II. वेदि वेदि,<BR> 1. m. A teacher.<BR> 2. f. Sarasvatī.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवेदि|उत्तरवेदिः
उत्तर-वेदि उत्तर-वेदि, f. the northern fire-place, MBh. 3, 7078.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेदि
उद्-वेदि उद्-वेदि, adj. furnished with an elevated altar, Ragh. 17, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्वेदि
वहिस्-वेदि वहिस्-वेदि, adv. on the outside of the sacred hearth, Man. 11, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिका
वेदिका वेदि + का, f.<BR> 1. Ground [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b " target="_blank">Page0901-b + 42</a>] prepared for sacrificial ceremonies, a rude altar, Mālav. 60, 3.<BR> 2. A quadrangular open shed in the middle of a court-yard, erected for various purposes, and furnished with a seat, Pañc. 129, 17.<BR> 3. A seat, Rām. 6, 75, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिजा
वेदिजा वेदिजा, i. e. वेदि-ज (vb. जन्), f. Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिन्
वेदिन् वेदिन्, i. e. विद् and वेद, + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Knowing, acquainted with, Man. 1, 97.<BR> 2. Marrying, Man. 3, 16.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Brahman.<BR> 2. A learned Brāhmaṇa, a teacher.<BR> III. m. A plant, Cissampelos hexandra.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यावेदिन्
कन्या- + वेदिन् कन्या- + वेदिन्, m. a son-in-law, Yājñ. 1, 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणवेदिन्
करुण- + वेदिन् करुण- + वेदिन्, adj. compassionate, Rām. 3, 69, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरवेदिन्|गंभीरवेदिन्
गम्भीर- + वेदिन् गम्भीर- + वेदिन्, m. a restive elephant, Ragh. 4, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिवेदिन्
नीति- + वेदिन् नीति- + वेदिन्, adj. knowing the rules of policy, Hit. 31, 8, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषान्तरवेदिन्
पुरुष-अन्तर- + वेदिन् पुरुष-अन्तर- + वेदिन्, adj. knowing the heart of mankind, Vikr. 36, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्धृ
वेद्धृ वेद्धृ, see व्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध|वेधः
वेध वेध, i. e. व्यध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Piercing, breaking through, Rājat. 5, 95.<BR> 2. Perforation.<BR> 3. Depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधक|वेधकं|वेधकः
वेधक वेधक, i. e. व्यध् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Piercing, sharp.<BR> 2. A perforator (of gems), Rām. 2, 64, 12, ed. Seramp.<BR> II. m. Camphor.<BR> III. n. Grain, rice in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधन|वेधनं
वेधन वेधन, i. e. व्यध् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Piercing.<BR> 2. Perforation.<BR> 3. Depth.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. An instrument used to pierce gems.<BR> 2. An instrument for piercing an elephant's car.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढवेधन
दृढ- + वेधन दृढ- + वेधन, n. hitting with an arrow which remains in the wound, MBh. 7, 2635.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्
वेधस् वेधस्,<BR> I. adj. sbst. m. Creating, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. i. 64, 1.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The creator, Mālat. 14, 4; Brahman, Bhartṛ. 3, 98.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a " target="_blank">Page0902-a + 40</a>]<BR> 3. Śiva, Arj. 10, 50.<BR> 4. The sun.<BR> 5. A wise man, Śṛṅgārat. 21 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0901-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिन्
वेधिन् i. e. व्यध् + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Piercing, hitting, Lass. 36, 19.<BR> II. f. नी, A leech.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिवेधिन्
कोटि- + वेधिन् कोटि- + वेधिन्, adj. piercing the top, i. e. able to perform the most difficult task, Rājat. 1, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवेधिन्
शब्द- + वेधिन् शब्द- + वेधिन्,<BR> I. adj. an archer who is able to hit an object not seen but only heard, Rām. 2, 63, 10; ˚धित्व, n. its abstract, Rām. 1, 28, 22.<BR> II. m. a name of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रवेधिन्
शीघ्र- + वेधिन् शीघ्र- + वेधिन्, m. a good archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्
वेन् वेन्, † वेण् वेण्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. † To go.<BR> 2. † To know.<BR> 3. † To reflect.<BR> 4. † To discern.<BR> 5. † To hold or take a musical instrument.<BR> 6. † To play on a musical instrument.<BR> 7. † To take.<BR> 8. To praise (ved.).<BR> 9. To love, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 86, 8.<BR> --Cf. αἰνέω, αἴνη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन वेन् + अ, m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेप्
वेप् वेप् (akin to वी, its old Caus.), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Indr. 5, 48), To shake, to tremble, Pañc. 94, 4; Daśak. in Chr. 201, 13.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, To tremble, Nal. 9, 26.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To tremble, Rām. 2, 8, 8.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vibrare; O.H.G. weibôn, fluitare; weibjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथु|वेपथुः
वेपथु वेप् + अथु, m. Trembling, Vikr. d. 147; Pañc. iii. d. 227; tremor.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेपथु
अति- + वेपथु अति- + वेपथु, adj. trembling vehemently, Lass. 59, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथुभृत्
वेपथुभृत् वेपथु-भृ + त्, adj. Trembling, Śiś. 9, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथुमन्त्|वेपथुमत्
वेपथुमन्त् वेपथु + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Trembling, Śāk. d. 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेपथुमन्त्|अतिवेपथुमत्
अति- + वेपथुमन्त् अति- + वेपथुमन्त्, adj. trembling vehemently, Śiś. 9, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपन|वेपनं
वेपन वेपन, i. e. विप् and वेप्, + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b " target="_blank">Page0902-b + 41</a>] n.<BR> 1. Trembling (ŚKD.).<BR> 2. The shooting off of a bow, Rām. 1, 67, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपस्
वेपस् वेप् + अस्, n. Trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेम|वेमः
वेम वे + म, m., and वेमन् वे + मन्, m. and n. A loom.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेम
सु-वेम सु-वेम, m. a good loom, MBh. 1, 806.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेर|वेरं|वेरः
वेर वेर (m. and) n.<BR> 1. The body.<BR> 2. Saffron.<BR> 3. The egg-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्
1. वेल् वेल्, see वेल्ल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्
2. वेल् वेल्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from वेला), Par. To declare the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल|वेलं|वेलः
वेल वेल,<BR> I. n. A grove.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. Time, Pañc. 55, 6; 163, 20; loc. लायाम्, Seasonably.<BR> 2. Tide, Pañc. 75, 24; flow, current.<BR> 3. Sea-shore, Śiś. 9, 38 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 4. Boundary, Pañc. iii. d. 269.<BR> 5. Leisure, interval, opportunity.<BR> 6. Sudden death.<BR> 7. Sickness.<BR> 8. The gums.<BR> 9. Speech.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेलम्
अति-वेल + म् अति-वेल + म्, adv. unseasonably, MBh. 2, 2187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेलम्
अनु-वेल + म् अनु-वेल + म्, adv. continually, Ragh. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेल|उद्वेलः
उद्-वेल उद्-वेल, adj. breaking out of its shore, Kathās. 18, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयवेला
तोय-वेला तोय-वेला, f. a bank, a shore, Hariv. 12014.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावेल
महा-वेल महा-वेल, adj. of high tides, surgy, Johns. Sel. 13, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल्
वेल्ल् वेल्ल्, वेल् वेल्, † वेह्ल् वेह्ल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To go.<BR> 2. वेल्ल्, To shake, to tremble, Utt. Rāmac. 121, 6.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वेल्लित.<BR> 1. Shaking.<BR> 2. Crooked, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 19.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनुवेल्लित, Lying crooked under, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 18. n. A bandage used in surgery, Suśr. 1, 65, 17.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. वेल्ल्, To abscond, Utt. Rāmac. 48, 12.<BR> 2. वेल्, To struggle, Mālat. 140, 3.<BR> --With वि वि, वेल्ल्, To struggle, to tremble, Kathās. 18, 174.<BR>//Probably akin to Lat. volvo; εἴλω, ἐλύω, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a " target="_blank">Page0903-a + 43</a>] etc.; O.H.G. wuoljan; Goth. valvjan; A.S. willian, waeltan, etc. (cf. the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0902-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लन|वेल्लनं
वेल्लन वेल्ल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rolling on the ground (as a horse).<BR> 2. A sort of rolling-pin with which cakes, etc., are prepared.<BR> 3. Going.<BR> 4. Shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेवी
वेवी वेवी (properly a frequent. of वी, q. cf.), ii. 2, Ātm. (ved. also Par., Rigv. iii. 55, 9),<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To pervade.<BR> 3. To conceive or become pregnant.<BR> 4. To desire.<BR> 5. To throw.<BR> 6. To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश वेश, m.<BR> 1. i. e. विश् + अ.<BR> 1. Entrance.<BR> 2. A house.<BR> 3. A house of prostitutes, Man. 4, 84; Daśak. in Chr. 193, 13.<BR> II. also वेष वेष.<BR> 1. Dress, apparel, Man. 4, 18, and 200 (ष्); Pañc. 129, 17 (ष्).<BR> 2. Ornament, decoration.<BR> 3. Disguise.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. οἶκος; Lat. vicus; Goth. veihs; A.S. wie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवेश|अग्निवेशः
अग्नि- + वेश अग्नि- + वेश, m. a proper name, Johns. Sel. 1, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरणवेश
अभिसरण- + वेश अभिसरण- + वेश, adj., f. शा, dressed in a garb fit for meeting one's lover, Vikr. 40, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवेश|आर्य्यवेश
आर्य- + वेश आर्य- + वेश, adj. dressed like an Ārya, or a respectable man, Rām. 1, 7, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटयुवतिवेश
कपट-युवति- + वेश कपट-युवति- + वेश, adj. under the disguise of a girl, Bhāg. P. 8, 12, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेश
कृत- + वेश कृत- + वेश, adj. dressed, Gīt. 11, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवेश
पुंवेश पुंवेश, i. e. पुंस्-, adj. dressed like a man, Kathās. 29, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारवेश|शृंगारवेश|शृङ्गारवेशः
शृङ्गार- + वेश शृङ्गार- + वेश, adj. dressed suitably for amorous enterprises, MBh. 5, 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेश|सवेशः
स- + वेश स- + वेश, adj. 1. near. 2. dressed, ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशक|वेशकः
वेशक वेशक, i. e. विश् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Who or what enters.<BR> II. m. A house.<BR> III. f. शिका, Entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन्त|वेशंत|वेशंतः|वेशन्तः
वेशन्त वेशन्त (vb. विश्), m.<BR> 1. A small pond.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशिन्
वेशिन् वेशिन्, i. e. वेश + इन्, adj. Assuming a particular dress or form.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ववेशिन्|सर्व्ववेशिन्
सर्व- + वेशिन् सर्व- + वेशिन्, i. e. सर्ववेश + इन्, m. an actor, a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मन्
वेश्मन् वेश्मन्, i. e. विश् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. A house, Pañc. iii. d. 172; 218; an abode.<BR> 2. A temple, Rājat. 5, 167.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडावेश्मन्
क्रीडा- + वेश्मन् क्रीडा- + वेश्मन्, n. a house for amusement, Vikr. d. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुवेश्मन्
जतु- + वेश्मन् जतु- + वेश्मन्, m. a house, constructed of shell-lac, Johns. Sel. 55, 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायुक्षालनवेश्मन्
पायु-क्षालन- + वेश्मन् पायु-क्षालन- + वेश्मन्, n. a privy, Rājat. 4, 572.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनवेश्मन्|बंधनवेश्मन्
बन्धन- + वेश्मन् बन्धन- + वेश्मन्, n. a prison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासवेश्मन्
वास- + वेश्मन् वास- + वेश्मन्, n. the inner part of a house, a sleeping-room, Kathās. 22, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवेश्मन्
श्मशान- + वेश्मन् श्मशान- + वेश्मन्, m. 1. Śiva. 2. a ghost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्या
वेश्या वेश्या, see under विश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष|वेषः
वेष वेष, see वेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट्
वेष्ट् वेष्ट्, i. 1, Ātm. To surround, to encompass, to twist about, MBh. 1, 1800. वेष्टित,<BR> 1. Dressed, Hit. pr. d. 40, M.M.<BR> 2. Stopped, Hit. 106, 17.<BR> 3. Secured from access.<BR> 4. Enveloped, wrapped up, Man. 1, 49.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To surround, MBh. 12, 12449.<BR> 2. To twist about, MBh. 1, 1801.<BR> 3. To invest, to blockade, Ragh. 11, 51; 52 (Calc.).<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To twist, Pañc. i. d. 376.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To untwist, Megh. 89; MBh. 7, 3168 उद्वेष्टन्ति is to be changed to उच्चेष्टन्ति.<BR> --Caus. To open, Mālav. 70, 17.<BR> --With उप उप, उपवेष्टित, Twined, Mṛcch. 115, 13.<BR> --With परि परि, To surround, Pañc. 97, 25. परि-वेष्टित,<BR> 1. Tied, Hit. ii. d. 131.<BR> 2. Covered, veiled.<BR> --Caus. To embrace, Pañc. i. d. 41.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्र-वेष्टित, Covered, MBh. 3, 10047.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To surround one's self, to be surrounded, MBh. 12, 12449.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To surround, to encompass, MBh. 3, 10264.<BR> 2. To cover, MBh. 3, 12889.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट वेष्ट् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Surrounding.<BR> 2. An enclosure, a fence.<BR> 3. A turban. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a " target="_blank">Page0904-a + 40</a>]<BR> 4. Resin.<BR> 5. Turpentine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्ट|कर्णवेष्टः|कर्ण्णवेष्ट
कर्ण- + वेष्ट कर्ण- + वेष्ट, m. 1. an ear-ring, Rām. 5, 19, 12. 2. a proper name, MBh. 1, 2696.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवेष्ट|दन्तवेष्टः
दन्त- + वेष्ट दन्त- + वेष्ट, m. 1. the gum, the jaw, Yājñ. 3, 96. 2. a disease of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 93, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवेष्ट|पत्रवेष्टः
पत्र- + वेष्ट पत्र- + वेष्ट, m. a kind of ear-ring, Ragh. 16, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0903-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टक|वेष्टकं|वेष्टकः
वेष्टक वेष्ट् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Surrounding, a surrounder.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A wall, a fence.<BR> 2. A pumpkin gourd.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A turban.<BR> 2. Resin.<BR> 3. Turpentine.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवेष्टक
दन्त- + वेष्टक दन्त- + वेष्टक, m. a disease of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 303, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टन|वेष्टनं
वेष्टन वेष्ट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Surrounding, being worn, Rājat. 5, 343 (see उल्लासन).<BR> 2. An envelope, Pañc. 147, 2.<BR> 3. A wall, a fence.<BR> 4. A turban, a diadem, Ragh. 1, 42 (cf. Sch. Calc. 43).<BR> 5. The outer ear, or the meatus auditorius and the concha.<BR> 6. An attitude in dancing, a particular disposition of the hands, also a crossing of the feet.<BR> 7. Bdellium.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टन
उद्- + वेष्टन उद्- + वेष्टन,<BR> I. n. pressure, a pressing pain, Suśr. 1, 332, 2.<BR> II. adj. of which the band is loosened (as hair), Ragh. 7, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्प|वेष्पः
वेष्प वेष्प, m. Water (cf. वाष्प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेस्
† वेस् वेस्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसर|वेसरः
वेसर वेसर, m. A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसवार|वेसवारः
वेसवार वेसवार, m. A condiment, as pepper, spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्
† वेह् वेह्, बेह् बेह्, i. 1, Ātm. To endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहत्
वेहत् वेहत्, probably वि-हन् + त्, f. A cow miscarrying from taking the bull unseasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्ल्
वेह्ल् वेह्ल्, see वेल्ल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
1. वै वै, see 1. वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
2. वै वै, a particle,<BR> 1. So indeed, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b " target="_blank">Page0904-b + 41</a>] Pañc. ii. d. 26.<BR> 2. Just, Nal. 26, 5.<BR> 3. Although, Chr. 6, 6.<BR> 4. Granted, if, Hit. ii. d. 21 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 572).<BR> 5. Preceded by तु, But just, Man. 2, 22.<BR> 6. Preceded by न, Perhaps not, Lass. 27, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्ष|वैकक्षं
वैकक्ष वैकक्ष, i. e. वि-कक्ष + अ, n.<BR> 1. A garland worn over one shoulder and under the other.<BR> 2. An upper garment, a wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्षक|वैकक्षकं
वैकक्षक वैकक्ष + क, n. = वैकक्ष,<BR> 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्तन|वैकर्तनः|वैकर्त्तन
वैकर्तन वैकर्तन, i. e. विकर्तन (The sun), + अ, patronym. Son of the sun, i. e. Karṇa, Johns. Sel. 56, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्प|वैकल्पं
वैकल्प वैकल्प, i. e. विकल्प + अ, n. in अर्थ-, n. Perversion or disguise of fact, Man. 8, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्पिक|वैकल्पिकः
वैकल्पिक वैकल्पिक, i. e. विकल्प + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Alternative.<BR> 2. Doubtful, indeterminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्य|वैकल्यं
वैकल्य वैकल्य i. e. विकल + य, n.<BR> 1. Lameness, imbecility, Pañc. i. d. 193: Hit. 121, 14; Pañc. 254, 9 (बुद्ढि-, of understanding).<BR> 2. Deficiency, defect, want, Man. 10, 85; Pañc. i. d. 119.<BR> 3. Insufficiency, Pañc. 166, 16.<BR> 4. Non-existence.<BR> 5. Agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकारिक|वैकारिकः
वैकारिक वैकारिक, i. e. विकार + इक,<BR> I. adj. Modified, Bhāg. P. 2, 5, 30.<BR> II. m. A class of deities, ib.; MBh. 12, 13626.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकालिक
वैकालिक वैकालिक, i. e. विकाल + इक, adj. Occurring in, or belonging to, the afternoon, Lass. 24, 18 (कम्, adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकुण्ठ|वैकुंठ|वैकुंठः|वैकुण्ठः
वैकुण्ठ वैकुण्ठ (partly properly patronym. from विकुण्ठा, The mother of Viṣṇu, + अ),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu, Padmap. 2, 5.<BR> 2. Indra.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The paradise of Viṣṇu, Pañc. 48, 3.<BR> 2. Talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत|वैकृतं|वैकृतः
वैकृत वैकृत, i. e. विकृति + अ,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a " target="_blank">Page0905-a + 42</a>] Changed.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Change, Rām. 1, 9, 45; Rājat. 5, 314.<BR> 2. Aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0904-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्लव्य|वैक्लव्यं
वैक्लव्य वैक्लव्य, i. e. विक्लव + य, n. Confusion, commotion, affliction, Nal. 23, 23; Śāk. d. 81; 111, 3 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. या); despair, Mālat. 142, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैक्लव्यम्
स-वैक्लव्य + म् स-वैक्लव्य + म्, adv. despairingly, 164, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखानस|वैखानसः
वैखानस वैखानस, i. e. विखानस (a proper name), + अ,<BR> I. adj. Instituted by Vaikhānasa (with व्रत, the life of an anchoret), Śāk. d. 26.<BR> II. m. An anchoret, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 5; cf. 93, 5.<BR> III. f. सी, A vessel used for frying meat to be offered in sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैगुण्य|वैगुण्यं
वैगुण्य वैगुण्य, i. e. वि-गुण + य, n.<BR> 1. Absence of qualities.<BR> 2. Contrariety of qualities.<BR> 3. Inferiority, badness, baseness, Man. 10, 68.<BR> 4. Unskilfulness, Man. 8, 293.<BR> 5. Fault, defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचक्षण्य|वैचक्षण्यं
वैचक्षण्य वैचक्षण्य, i. e. विचक्षण + य, n. Skill, cleverness, proficiency.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवैचक्षण्य
अति- + वैचक्षण्य अति- + वैचक्षण्य, n. excessive proficiency, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्र्य|वैचित्र्यं
वैचित्र्य वैचित्र्य, i. e. वि-चित्र + य, n.<BR> 1. Variety, Hit. pr. d. 2, M.M.<BR> 2. Surprisingness, Mālat. 16, 2; surprise, 36, 9.<BR> 3. Sorrow, Mālat. 46, 12; despair, 66, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजनन|वैजननं|वैजननः
वैजनन वैजनन, i. e. विजनन + अ, m. The last month of uterine gestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्त|वैजयंत|वैजयंतः|वैजयन्तः
वैजयन्त वैजयन्त, i. e. विजयन्त + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The banner of Indra, Indr. 1, 8.<BR> 2. A banner in general, Rām. 2, 97, 25 Gorr.<BR> 3. The palace of Indra.<BR> II. f. ती.<BR> 1. A flag, a banner, Hit. 63, 1, M.M.<BR> 2. A kind of garland.<BR> 3. The name of two trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्तिक|वैजयंतिक|वैजयंतिकः|वैजयन्तिकः
वैजयन्तिक वैजयन्तिक,<BR> I. i. e. वैजयन्त + इक, adj. Bearing a flag, a flagbearer.<BR> II. f. का, i. e. वैजयन्ती + क, f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b " target="_blank">Page0905-b + 41</a>]<BR> 1. A flag, Mālat. 13, 19.<BR> 2. A string of pearls, Vikr. 12, 17 (Prākṛ.; cf. Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजात्य|वैजात्यं
वैजात्य वैजात्य, i. e. वि-जाति + य, n.<BR> 1. Difference or deviation from ordinary conduct.<BR> 2. Looseness, wantonness.<BR> 3. Difference of species or caste.<BR> 4. Exclusion from caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजिक|वैजिकं|वैजिकः
वैजिक वैजिक, i. e. वीज + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Seminal, relating to seed, to conception, Man. 2, 27.<BR> 2. Relating to sexual union, Man. 5, 63.<BR> II. m. A young shoot.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Origin, cause.<BR> 2. Soul, spirit.<BR> 3. Oil prepared from the Morunga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैडालव्रतिक|वैडालव्रतिकः
वैडालव्रतिक वैडालव्रतिक, i. e. विडाल-व्रत + इक, adj. and sbst. Acting like a cat, hypocritical, Man. 4, 192; a hypocrite, 4, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण|वैणः
वैण वैण, i. e. वेनु + अ (anomal.), m. A cutter of bambu, a worker in bambuwork, Man. 4, 215 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणव|वैणवं|वैणवः
वैणव वैणव, i. e. वेणु + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. वी, Made of bambu, Man. 4, 36.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A bambu-staff.<BR> 2. A worker in bambu or wicker-work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणविक|वैणविकः
वैणविक वैणविक, i. e. वेणु + इक, m. A player on a flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणिक|वैणिकः
वैणिक वैणिक, i. e. वीणा + इक, m. A lutist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुक|वैणुकं|वैणुकः
वैणुक वैणुक, i. e. वेणु + क, n. A bambu pike, headed with iron, used to drive an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण्य|वैण्यः
वैण्य वैण्य, i. e. वेण + य, patronym., m. The son of Veṇa, Pañc. iii. d. 269.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतंसिक|वैतंसिकः
वैतंसिक वैतंसिक, i. e. वी̆तंस + इक, m. A vendor of the flesh of beasts or birds, Govardhana, Āryā Sapt. 154, b.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवैतंसिक
द्यूत- + वैतंसिक द्यूत- + वैतंसिक, m. vendors of beasts and birds for playing with, Rām. 2, 90, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतनिक|वैतनिकः
वैतनिक वैतनिक, i. e. वेतन + इक, adj., f. की, sbst.<BR> 1. Living on wages. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a " target="_blank">Page0906-a + 42</a>]<BR> 2. A hireling, a labourer.<BR> 3. A stipendiary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0905-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतरणि|वैतरणिः
वैतरणि and णी वैतरणी, i. e. वितरण + ई, f.<BR> 1. The river of hell, MBh. 18, 84 (णी).<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतस|वैतसः
वैतस वैतस, i. e. वेतस + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. सी, Reed-like, Pañc. iii. d. 18.<BR> II. m. A sort of cane, Calamus fasciculatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतान
वैतान वैतान, i. e. वितान + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Taken from the holy hearth, Śāk. d. 83.<BR> 2. Sacrificial, sacred, Śāk. 43, 11, Chezy. (v. r.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Oblation with fire.<BR> 2. The sacred ordinances, Man. 11, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानिक|वैतानिकः
वैतानिक वैतानिक, i. e. वितान + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Performed with the three sacred fires, Man. 6, 9; 7, 78.<BR> 2. Sacrificial, sacred, Śāk. 31, 11.<BR> II. n. Burnt offering, especially of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालिक|वैतालिकः
वैतालिक वैतालिक, m.<BR> I. i. e. विताल + इक, A bard, whose principal duty is to awaken a chief at dawn with music and song, a singer, Śāk. 62, 1; MBh. 1, 6940.<BR> II. i. e. वेताल + इक, One who has a Vetāla for a familiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतृष्ण्य
वैतृष्ण्य वैतृष्ण्य, i. e. वि-तृष्ण (see तृष्णा), + य, n. Quenching of the thirst, Man. 5, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध|वैदग्धं
वैदग्ध वैदग्ध, n., वैदग्ध्य वैदग्ध्य, n., and f. धी, i. e. वि-दग्ध (vb. दह्), + अ or य,<BR> 1. Cleverness, skill, Bhartṛ. 2, 15 (ध); Lass. 91, 13 (धी); Mālat. 3, 20; 18, 7; 9 (ध्य).<BR> 2. Acuteness, intelligence, Mālat. 129, 7.<BR> 3. Cunning, craft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदर्भ|वैदर्भं|वैदर्भः
वैदर्भ वैदर्भ,<BR> A. i. e. विदर्भ + अ,<BR> I. m. The sovereign of Vidarbha, the father of Damayantī.<BR> II. f. भी.<BR> 1. Damayantī, Nal. 24, 50.<BR> 2. Rukmiṇī.<BR> 3. The wife of Agastya.<BR> 4. The law [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b " target="_blank">Page0906-b + 43</a>] of Vidarbha, by which cousins-german were allowed to intermarry in that country.<BR> B. i. e. वि-दृभ् + अ + अ, n. Crafty or indirect speech.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवैदर्भ|दंतवैदर्भ|दन्तवैदर्भः
दन्त- + वैदर्भ दन्त- + वैदर्भ, m. the loosening of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 31, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदल|वैदलं|वैदलः
वैदल वैदल,<BR> I. i. e. विदल + अ, adj. Made of cane, Man. 5, 119.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A flat unleavened cake.<BR> 2. Any leguminous vegetable or grain.<BR> III. n. A vessel of wicker-work, a basket made of reeds, Man. 6, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिक|वैदिकः
वैदिक वैदिक, i. e. वेद + इक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Relating to the Vedas, Man. 2, 117.<BR> 2. Scriptural, 2, 15.<BR> 3. Recommended, ordained in the Vedas, 2, 2; 84; 8, 190.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa well versed in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुष्य|वैदुष्यं
वैदुष्य वैदुष्य, i. e. विद्वंस् (vb. विद्), + य, n. Science, Rājat. 6, 290.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदूर्य|वैदूर्य्य|वैदूर्य्यं
वैदूर्य वैदूर्य, i. e. विदूर + य,<BR> I. adj. Brought from Vidūra.<BR> II. n. A gem of a dark-blue colour, the lapis lazuli, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 15; Rām. 3, 49, 2; 53, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदूर्यमय
वैदूर्यमय वैदूर्य + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of lapis lazuli, Bhartṛ. 2, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेशिक|वैदेशिकः
वैदेशिक वैदेशिक, i. e. वि-देश + इक, adj. Foreigner, a foreigner, Pañc. 184, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेह|वैदेहः
वैदेह वैदेह, i. e. विदेह + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The king of Videhā, father of Sītā, Utt. Rāmac. 93, 12.<BR> 2. A trader by profession.<BR> 3. The son of a Vaiśya by a Brāhmaṇa woman, Man. 10, 11.<BR> 4. pl. Descendants of mixed castes, Lass. Pentap. 66, 31.<BR> 5. An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR> II. f. ही.<BR> 1. The wife of a trader.<BR> 2. Sītā (the daughter of the king of Videhā), Rām. 3, 49, 12; Utt. Rāmac. 14, 9.<BR> 3. Long pepper.<BR> 4. A sort of pigment, called Rocanā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0906-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेहक|वैदेहकः
वैदेहक वैदेह + क, m. = वैदेह,<BR> I., cf. Man. 10, 13 (= वैदेह,<BR> 1. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्य|वैद्यः
वैद्य वैद्य, i. e. वेद + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the Vedas, Lass. Pentap. 67, 43.<BR> 2. Relating to medicine, medical.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A follower of the Vedas, or one conversant with the Vedas.<BR> 2. A learned man, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 1.<BR> 3. A physician, Pañc. iii. d. 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवैद्य|विषवैद्यः
विष- + वैद्य विष- + वैद्य, m. a dealer in antidotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वैद्य|स्वर्वैद्यः
स्वर्- + वैद्य स्वर्- + वैद्य, m. either of the Aśvins, the physicians of the heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यक|वैद्यकं|वैद्यकः
वैद्यक वैद्य + क, m. A physician, Śṛṅgārat. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्याधर
वैद्याधर वैद्याधर, i. e. विद्याधर + अ, adj. Belonging to the Vidyādharas, Kathās. 26, 241.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्युत
वैद्युत वैद्युत, i. e. विद्युत् + अ, adj. Proceeded from lightning, Vikr. d. 154 (अग्निः, A flash of lightning); Utt. Rāmac. 125, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध|वैधः
वैध वैध, i. e. विधि + अ, adj. According to rule, ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधर्म्य|वैधर्म्यं
वैधर्म्य वैधर्म्य, i. e. वि-धर्म + य, n.<BR> 1. Irreligion, impropriety.<BR> 2. Difference of duty.<BR> 3. Difference, Bhāṣāp. 28; Kusumāñj. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधव|वैधवः
वैधव वैधव, i. e. विधु + अ, patronym., m. The son of the moon, i. e. Budha, Vikr. d. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधवेय|वैधवेयः
वैधवेय वैधवेय, i. e. विधवा + एय, m. The son of a widow, Śāk. 23, 14 (but read वैधेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधव्य|वैधव्यं
वैधव्य वैधव्य, i. e. विधवा + य, n. Widowhood, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 450.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैधव्य
अ- + वैधव्य अ- + वैधव्य, adj., f. या, relating to non-widowhood, not to become a widow, Sāv. 4, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवैधव्य
बाल- + वैधव्य बाल- + वैधव्य, n. state of one who has become a widow already when a child, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 450.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधात्र|वैधात्रः
वैधात्र वैधात्र, i. e. विधातृ + अ. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b " target="_blank">Page0907-b + 40</a>] patronym., m. Sanatkumāra, the son of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधेय|वैधेयः
वैधेय वैधेय (perhaps धेय [vb. धा], compounded with वि and aff. अ), adj. Foolish, a fool, Vikr. 30, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध्यत|वैध्यतः
वैध्यत वैध्यत, m. Yama's doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतेय|वैनतेयः
वैनतेय वैनतेय, i. e. वि-नता, A proper name, the wife of Kāśyapa (vb. नम्), + एय, metronym., m. Garuḍa, Vikr. 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनयिक|वैनयिकः
वैनयिक वैनयिक, i. e. विनय + इक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Relating to morals or behaviour.<BR> 2. Enforcing proper conduct.<BR> 3. Magisterial, performed by the officers of criminal justice, Man. 7, 65.<BR> II. m. A war carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनायक
वैनायक वैनायक, i. e. विनायक + अ, adj., f. की, Referring to, or made by, Gaṇeśa, Mālat. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनाशिक|वैनाशिकं|वैनाशिकः
वैनाशिक वैनाशिक, i. e. विनाश + इक, m.<BR> 1. A dependent, a subject, a slave.<BR> 2. An astrologer.<BR> 3. A spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनीतक|वैनीतकः
वैनीतक वैनीतक, i. e. वि-नीत (vb. नी), + क, m. and n. A mediate conveyance, as a porter carrying a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैन्य|वैन्यः
वैन्य वैन्य, i. e. वेन + य, patronym., m.<BR> 1. The king Pṛthu, the son of Vena (ŚKD.).<BR> 2. The name of a deity(?), Rājat. 5, 97; 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपरीत्य|वैपरीत्यं
वैपरीत्य वैपरीत्य, i. e. वि-परि-इत (vb. इ), + य, n.<BR> 1. Contrariety, opposition, reverse, Sāh. Darp. 12, 17.<BR> 2. Counterpart, Hit. ii. d. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैफल्य|वैफल्यं
वैफल्य वैफल्य, i. e. वि-फल + य, n. Uselessness, MBh. 13, 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभव|वैभवं
वैभव वैभव, i. e. विभव + अ, n. Power, greatness, Kir. 12, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्राज|वैभ्राजं
वैभ्राज वैभ्राज, i. e. वि-भ्राज् + अ + अ, n. A garden of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमत्य|वैमत्यं
वैमत्य वैमत्य, i. e. वि-मति + य, n. Dissension, Rājat. 5, 462.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमनस्य|वैमनस्यं
वैमनस्य वैमनस्य, i. e. वि-मनस् + य, n. Sadness, heart-break, Śāk. 79, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमल्य
वैमल्य वैमल्य, i. e. वि-मल + य, n. Purity, cleanness, Rājat. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्र|वैमात्रः
वैमात्र वैमात्र, i. e. वि-मातृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Born of a step-mother, Rām. 3, 53, 19.<BR> II. m. A step-mother's son.<BR> III. f. त्री, A step-mother's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्रेय|वैमात्रेयः
वैमात्रेय वैमात्रेय, i. e. वि-मातृ + एय,<BR> I. m. A step-mother's son.<BR> II. f. यी, A half-sister, or one by a different mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमानिक|वैमानिकः
वैमानिक वैमानिक, i. e. विमान + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to a heavenly car.<BR> 2. Borne in chariots of the gods, Man. 12, 48.<BR> 3. A god, Rājat. 5, 370.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमूल्यतस्
वैमूल्यतस् वैमूल्यतस्, i. e. वि-मूल + य + तस्, adv. By overcharging the price(?), Man. 9, 287 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमेय|वैमेयः
वैमेय वैमेय, i. e. वि-मेय (vb. मे), + अ, m. Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयग्र्य|वैयग्र्यं
वैयग्र्य वैयग्र्य, i. e. व्यग्र + य, n. Being engaged, Lass. 2. ed. 37, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयर्थ्य|वैयर्थ्यं
वैयर्थ्य वैयर्थ्य, i. e. वि-अर्थ + य, n. Uselessness, Vikr. 29, 18; unprofitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाकरण|वैयाकरणः
वैयाकरण वैयाकरण, i. e. व्याकरण + अ,<BR> I. adj. Grammatical.<BR> II. m. A grammarian.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवैयाकरण|प्रथमवैयाकरणः
प्रथम- + वैयाकरण प्रथम- + वैयाकरण, a first-rate grammarian, Pāṇ. 6, 2, 56, Sch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र|वैयाघ्रः
वैयाघ्र वैयाघ्र, i. e. व्याघ्र + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Consisting of a tiger-skin, Chr. 25, 52.<BR> 2. Covered with a tiger-skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयात्य|वैयात्यं
वैयात्य वैयात्य, i. e. वि-यात (vb. या), + य, n.<BR> 1. Lasciviousness, Hit. iii. d. 7; Rājat. 5, 384.<BR> 2. Boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयासकि|वैयासकिः
वैयासकि वैयासकि, i. e. व्यास + अक् + इ [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b " target="_blank">Page0908-b + 40</a>] (or rather + क + इ), patronym., m. A son of Vyāsa, Bhāg. P. 2, 3, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैर|वैरं
वैर वैर, i. e. वीर + अ, n.<BR> 1. Heroism, prowess.<BR> 2. Enmity, Pañc. 66, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वैर
निस्- + वैर निस्- + वैर,<BR> I. n. peaceableness, Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 45.<BR> II. adj. peaceable, MBh. 15, 882.<BR> III. रम्, adv. being no enmity, Rām. 4, 20, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरकृत्
वैरकृत् वैर-कृ + त्, m. An enemy, Pañc. ii. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरङ्गिक|वैरंगिकः|वैरङ्गिकः
वैरङ्गिक वैरङ्गिक, i. e. वि-रङ्ग + इक, m. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिक|वैरागिकः
वैरागिक वैरागिक, and वैरागिन् वैरागिन्, i. e. वि-राग + इक, and इन्, m. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्य|वैराग्यं
वैराग्य वैराग्य, i. e. वि-राग + य, n.<BR> 1. Absence of worldly desire, Bhag. 6, 35 (devotion); Pañc. 50, 16.<BR> 2. Disaffection, Hit. iii. d. 90.<BR> 3. Sorrow, Pañc. 82, 13; 116, 11.<BR> 4. Despondency, 235, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैराग्यम्
स-वैराग्य + म् स-वैराग्य + म्, adv. sorrowfully, Pañc. 66, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्यता
वैराग्यता वैराग्य + ता, f. Absence of worldly desire, Pañc. 50, 15 (devotion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराज|वैराजः
वैराज वैराज, i. e. विराज् + अ, adj. or m. (viz. लोक), The name of certain worlds, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराय
वैराय वैराय, a denomin. derived from वैर with य, Ātm. To fight, to behave inimically, Bhartṛ. 2, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिता
वैरिता वैरिता, i. e. वैरिन् + ता, f. Enmity, Pañc. iii. d. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन् वैरिन्, i. e. वैर + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Heroic, Bhartṛ. 2, 32 (? Böhtl., as on an enemy).<BR> 2. Hostile, Megh. 100.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A hero.<BR> 2. An enemy, Pañc. ii. d. 121.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढवैरिन्
दृढ- + वैरिन् दृढ- + वैरिन् (vb. दृंह्), m. a relentless foe, Johns. Sel. 60, 189. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a " target="_blank">Page0909-a + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ववैरिन्
पूर्व- + वैरिन् पूर्व- + वैरिन्, adj. one who has first commenced hostilities, MBh. 6, 3745.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0908-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्य|वैरूप्यं
वैरूप्य वैरूप्य, i. e. वि-रूप + य, n.<BR> 1. Deformity, Pañc. i. d. 466; Ragh. 12, 40.<BR> 2. Difference of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्यता
वैरूप्यता वैरूप्य + ता, f. Deformity, Nal. 19, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचन|वैरोचनः
वैरोचन वैरोचन, i. e. विरोचन + अ,<BR> I. adj. Proceeding from the sun, Kir. 5, 46.<BR> II. patronym.<BR> 1. The son of Agni.<BR> 2. The son of the sun.<BR> 3. Bali, son of Virocana, Johns. Sel. 30, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनि|वैरोचनिः
वैरोचनि वैरोचनि, i. e. विरोचन + इ, patronym., m.<BR> 1. The son of the sun.<BR> 2. Bali, the son of Virocana, Arj. 8, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्ष्य|वैलक्ष्यं
वैलक्ष्य वैलक्ष्य, i. e. वि-लक्ष + य, n.<BR> 1. Absence of any characteristic.<BR> 2. Contrariety, reverse.<BR> 3. Contrary course to that which is usual or natural.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैलक्ष्य
स- + वैलक्ष्य स- + वैलक्ष्य, adj. abashed, embarrassed, Rājat. 5, 60. ˚यम्, adv. embarrassed, Vikr. 32, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्व|वैल्वं
वैल्व वैल्व, i. e. विल्व + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the विल्व tree.<BR> 2. Made of its wood, Man. 2, 45.<BR> II. n. The fruit of the विल्व tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवधिक|वैवधिकः
वैवधिक वैवधिक, i. e. विवध + इक, m. A chandler, a vendor of grain, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्य|वैवर्ण्यं
वैवर्ण्य वैवर्ण्य, i. e. वि-वर्ण + य, n.<BR> 1. Change of colour, Pañc. i. d. 213.<BR> 2. Deviation from tribe or caste.<BR> 3. Difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वत|वैवस्वतः
वैवस्वत वैवस्वत, i. e. विवस्वन्त् + अ, patronym., m.<BR> 1. Yama.<BR> 2. The seventh Manu, Matsyop. 9 (cf. Man. 1, 62).<BR> 3. One of the Rudras.<BR> 4. The planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक वैवाहिक, i. e. विवाह + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to marriage, nuptial, Man. 2, 67.<BR> II. m. (or perhaps, तं तु is to be changed to तत् तु; then it would be n.), Wedding, Chr. 14, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशंपायनः|वैशम्पायनः
वैशम्पायन वैशम्पायन, m. The name of a Muni or sage, MBh. 1, 97; 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस|वैशसं
वैशस वैशस, i. e. वि-शस् + अ + अ, n.<BR> 1. Rending in pieces, Bhāg. P. 3, 30, 27.<BR> 2. Slaughter, Utt. Rāmac. 113, 6; Pañc. ed. orn. 36, 22; Bhāg. P. 4, 11, 10.<BR> 3. Distress, Utt. Rāmac. 160, 5.<BR> 4. Hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्र|वैशस्त्रं
वैशस्त्र वैशस्त्र, i. e. वि-शस्त्र + अ, n. The state of being defenceless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाख|वैशाखं|वैशाखः
वैशाख वैशाख i. e. विशाखा + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a month, April--May, Rājat. 5, 260.<BR> 2. A churningstick.<BR> II. f. खी, The day of full moon in the month वैशाख.<BR> III. n. An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक वैशिक, i. e. probably वेश्या + इक, anomal., n. Arts of a courtesan, Lass. 2. ed. 59, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट्य|वैशिष्ट्यं
वैशिष्ट्य वैशिष्ट्य, i. e. वि-शिष्ट (vb. शिष्), + य, n.<BR> 1. Endowment with.<BR> 2. Distinction, difference, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक वैशेषिक, i. e. विशेष + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Characteristic, Bhāṣāp. 43.<BR> 2. Belonging to the Vaiśeṣika doctrine (cf.<BR> II.), Bhāṣāp. 104; 140.<BR> II. n. A peculiar philosophical system, the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR> III. m. A follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine, Kusumāñj. 3, 8 (p. 29, 13, ed. Cowell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्य|वैशेष्यं
वैशेष्य वैशेष्य, i. e. विशेष + य, n.<BR> 1. Specific or generic distinction.<BR> 2. Superiority, Man. 9, 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्य|वैश्यः
वैश्य वैश्य, i. e. विश् + य,<BR> I. m. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a " target="_blank">Page0910-a + 41</a>] man of the third caste, Man. 1, 116; Hit. iv. d. 21.<BR> II. f. या, A woman of the Vaiśya caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0909-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवण|वैश्रवणः
वैश्रवण वैश्रवण, m. Kuvera, Hit. ii. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव वैश्वदेव, i. e. विश्व-देव + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the Viśvadevas, Man. 4, 183; dedicated or sacred to them.<BR> 2. Relating to all divinities.<BR> II. n. Offering or sacrifice to all the divinities, Man. 3, 83, 84; Pañc. iv. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानर|वैश्वानरः
वैश्वानर वैश्वानर,<BR> I. i. e. विश्व-नर + अ, adj. Relating to, fit for, etc., all men.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Agni, fire, Utt. Rāmac. 174, 3; Pañc. 224, 21.<BR> 2. The general consciousness, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 11.<BR> III. f. री, A particular sacrifice, Man. 11, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वासिक
वैश्वासिक वैश्वासिक, i. e. विश्वास + इक, adj. Trustworthy, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वी
वैश्वी वैश्वी, i. e. विश्व + अ + ई, f. The name of the twenty-first lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषम्य|वैषम्यं
वैषम्य वैषम्य, i. e. विषम + य, n.<BR> 1. Inequality, unevenness.<BR> 2. Solitariness.<BR> 3. Difficulty.<BR> 4. Misery, distress, Nal. 9, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवैषम्य
अति- + वैषम्य अति- + वैषम्य, n. situation in a place of very difficult access, Hit. iii. d. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्टुत|वैष्टुतं
वैष्टुत वैष्टुत, i. e. वि-स्तुत (vb. स्तु), + अ, n. The ashes of a burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्ट्र|वैष्ट्रं|वैष्ट्रः
वैष्ट्र वैष्ट्र, n. The world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णव|वैष्णवं|वैष्णवः
वैष्णव वैष्णव, i. e. विष्णु + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. वी, Relating or belonging to Viṣṇu, Johns. Sel. 95, 70; Rājat. 5, 125; Arj. 4, 30.<BR> II. m. A follower of Viṣṇu, Rājat. 5, 43.<BR> III. f. वी.<BR> 1. One of the मातृस्, the personified [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b " target="_blank">Page0910-b + 38</a>] energy of Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Durgā.<BR> 3. A flower, Clitoria ternatea.<BR> 4. Sacred basil, Ocymum sanctum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णवत्व
वैष्णवत्व वैष्णव + त्व, n. Faith in Viṣṇu, Rājat. 5, 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसारिण|वैसारिणः
वैसारिण वैसारिण, i. e. विसारिन् + अ, m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहायस|वैहायसं
वैहायस वैहायस, i. e. विहायस् + अ, adj. Being in the air, aërial, Pāraskara Gṛ. S. ii. 2 in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 533, 23; suspended in the air, Johns. Sel. 39, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहासिक|वैहासिकः
वैहासिक वैहासिक, i. e. विहास + इक, m. A comic actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोटा
वोटा वोटा, f. A female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्र|वोड्रः
वोड्र वोड्र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The boa-constrictor.<BR> 2. A sort of fish.<BR> II. f. री, The fourth part of a पण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढृ
वोढृ वोढृ, i. e. वह् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A porter, one who carries or draws, Pañc. 8, 16.<BR> 2. A charioteer.<BR> 3. A bull.<BR> 4. A guide, a leader, Lass. 97, 10 = Rigv. vi. 64, 3 (ved. वोल्हा, nom. sing.).<BR> 5. A bridegroom, Man. 8, 204.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वोढृ
धूर्वोढृ धूर्वोढृ, i. e. धुर्-, m. a beast of burthen, Pañc. ed. orn. 4, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरुखान|वोरुखानः
वोरुखान वोरुखान, m. A horse described as of red and white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लासक
वोल्लासक वोल्लासक, The name of a city, Rājat. 5, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लाह|वोल्लाहः
वोल्लाह वोल्लाह, m. A horse with light mane and tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोहित्थ|वोहित्थं|वोहित्थः
वोहित्थ वोहित्थ, n. A vessel, a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौषट्
वौषट् वौषट् (= वषट्, q. cf.; वषट् has first become वोषट् by the influence of the व्, as in वोढृ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a " target="_blank">Page0911-a + 42</a>] from वह्, and then, as in Zend., वओषट् = वौषट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0910-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसक|व्यंसकः
व्यंसक व्यंसक, i. e. वि-अंस् + अक, m. A cheat, a rogue, a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ति|व्यक्तिः
व्यक्ति व्यक्ति, i. e. वि-अञ्ज् + ती, f.<BR> 1. Distinctness, Śāk. d. 167.<BR> 2. Individuality.<BR> 3. An individual (opp. to जाति), Siddh. Mukt. 82, 10.<BR> 4. Appearance, manifestation Bhag. 7, 23; 10, 14; Megh. 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकलव्यक्ति
अ-सकल- + व्यक्ति अ-सकल- + व्यक्ति, adj. not being visible completely, Megh. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्र|व्यग्रः
व्यग्र व्यग्र, i. e. वि-अग्र, adj., f. रा,<BR> 1. Bewildered, Hit. iii. d. 108 (भोजन-, by the care for provisions).<BR> 2. Distracted.<BR> 3. Agitated, Pañc. 200, 8.<BR> 4. Engaged in, Vikr. 77, 4; occupied, Pañc. 121, 14; zealously occupied, Pañc. iii. d. 236; zealous, eager, Rājat. 5, 144.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्र
अ- + व्यग्र अ- + व्यग्र, adj. 1. not distracted, Utt. Rāmac. 52, 13; careful, Chr. 16, 19. 2. not disturbed, Lass. 2. ed. 39, 9; peaceable, Nal. 26, 20. 3. cool, deliberate, Draup. 9, 1; रम्, adv. reckless. Mālat. 78, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्रता
व्यग्रता व्यग्र + ता, f. Zealous occupation, Pañc. 252, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्रत्व
व्यग्रत्व व्यग्र + त्व, n. Perplexedness, confusion, Pañc. iii. d. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग|व्यंग|व्यङ्गः
व्यङ्ग व्यङ्ग, i. e. वि-अङ्ग,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Deformed, mutilated, MBh. 1, 1089.<BR> 2. Lamed.<BR> 3. Bodiless.<BR> 4. Ill-arranged.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cripple.<BR> 2. A frog.<BR> 3. Discoloration of the face, dark spots on the cheek.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्ग|अव्यंग|अव्यङ्गः
अ- + व्यङ्ग अ- + व्यङ्ग, adj. having no defect, Man. 3, 10; sound, Pañc. 184, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गता
व्यङ्गता व्यङ्ग + ता, f. Mutilation, Pañc. i. d. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गय
व्यङ्गय व्यङ्गय, a denomin. derived from व्यङ्ग, Par. To mutilate, Pañc. 38, 13; 40, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गार
व्यङ्गार व्यङ्गार, i. e. वि-अङ्गार, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b " target="_blank">Page0911-b + 44</a>] Without charcoal. n. loc. रे, At the time when the burning charcoal is extinguished, Man. 6, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्
व्यच् व्यच् (i. e. वि-अञ्च्), i. 6, विच, Par.<BR> 1. To surround, to encompass (ved.).<BR> 2. † To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यज|व्यजः
व्यज व्यज, i. e. वि-अज् + अ, m. A fan, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजन|व्यजनं
व्यजन व्यजन, i. e. वि-अज् + अन, n. A fan, Hit. ii. d. 155; Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालव्यजन|बालव्यजनं
बाल- + व्यजन बाल- + व्यजन, n. a fly-flapper used as an emblem of princely rank (made of the bushy tail of the Bos grunniens), Johns. Sel. 21, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जक|व्यंजक|व्यञ्जकः
व्यञ्जक व्यञ्जक, i. e. वि-अञ्ज् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Clearly showing, Man. 2, 68.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mark.<BR> 2. External indication of passion or feeling.<BR> 3. Feeling, Mālat. 154, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जन|व्यंजन|व्यंजनं|व्यञ्जनं
व्यञ्जन व्यञ्जन, i. e. वि-अञ्ज् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A mark, a sign, Hit. iii. d. 36; the marks of puberty (hairs of the body), Pañc. iii. d. 214 (pl.).<BR> 2. Paraphernalia, insignia.<BR> 3. A beard, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 28.<BR> 4. A privy part, either male or female.<BR> 5. Sauce, Rām. 1, 13, 15; condiment, Pañc. 52, 1.<BR> 6. A consonant, Sāv. 5, 25.<BR> II. n., and f. ना, Irony, sarcasm.<BR> III. f. ना, The third power of a word, suggestion, Sāh. Darp. 16, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यञ्जन|अव्यंजन|अव्यञ्जनः
अ- + व्यञ्जन अ- + व्यञ्जन, adj. ना, without the marks of puberty, Pañc. iii. d. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातव्यञ्जन|अजातव्यंजन
अ-जात- + व्यञ्जन अ-जात- + व्यञ्जन (vb. जन्), adj. beardless, Rām. 3, 42, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यञ्जन|निर्व्यंजन
निस्- + व्यञ्जन निस्- + व्यञ्जन, adj. without condiment, MBh. 12, 3189. loc. ने, downrightly, Pañc. 218, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
व्यतिकर व्यतिकर, i. e. वि-अति-कृ + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Reciprocal, or acting one with another.<BR> 2. Pervading.<BR> 3. Contiguous to.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Reciprocity, exchange, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 16; interchange, Mālat. 34, 11; reciprocal action, ib. 199, 16; relation, alternation, Utt. Rāmac. 125, 11.<BR> 2. Action in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a " target="_blank">Page0912-a + 43</a>] general, Pañc. 30, 8; 237, 22; 130,<BR> 3. Contact, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 429; contiguity.<BR> 4. Opportunity, Pañc. 40, 18.<BR> 5. Mixture, Megh. 15; union, Utt. Rāmac. 84, 2 (at the end of a comp. adj. ‘united’); conflux, Ragh. 8, 94.<BR> 6. Misfortune, calamity, Pañc. 42, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टव्यतिकर
दृष्ट- + व्यतिकर दृष्ट- + व्यतिकर, adj. one whose misfortune is evident, Hit. 110, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताव्यतिकर|वार्त्ताव्यतिकर|वार्त्ताव्यतिकरः
वार्ता- + व्यतिकर वार्ता- + व्यतिकर, m. a report's going from one to another, i. e. a report going from one to another, Pañc. 130, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0911-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकरित
व्यतिकरित व्यतिकरित, i. e. व्यतिकर + इत, adj. Pervaded, Mālat. 40, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम|व्यतिक्रमः
व्यतिक्रम व्यतिक्रम, i. e. वि-अति-क्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Inverted or retrograde order, reverse, Kir. 11, 76.<BR> 2. Contrariety.<BR> 3. Misfortune.<BR> 4. Passing over or beyond, transgression, Man. 8, 244; Pañc. 46, 20.<BR> 5. Fault, Man. 8, 229; sin, Rām. 1, 8, 12.<BR> 6. Non-performance (as of contracts), 8, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक|व्यतिरेकः
व्यतिरेक व्यतिरेक, i. e. वि-अति-रिच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Separateness.<BR> 2. Negative inference, Bhāṣāp. 141.<BR> 3. Interception, Mālat. 140, 20.<BR> 4. Difference.<BR> 5. Dissimilitude of things compared in some respects to each other.<BR> 6. Exclusion, exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिलङ्घिन्
व्यतिलङ्घिन् व्यतिलङ्घिन्, i. e. वि-अति-लङ्घ् + अ + इन्, adj. Removed, Ragh. 6, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्ग|व्यतिषंग|व्यतिषंगः|व्यतिषङ्गः
व्यतिषङ्ग व्यतिषङ्ग, i. e. वि-अति-सञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Mutual or reciprocal junction.<BR> 2. Fastening, tying together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहार|व्यतिहारः
व्यतिहार and व्यतीहार व्यती̆हार, i. e. वि-अति-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Barter, exchange.<BR> 2. Exchange of blows or abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीपात|व्यतीपातः
व्यतीपात व्यतीपात, i. e. वि-अति-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Disrespect.<BR> 2. A portent indicating calamity.<BR> 3. Great calamity.<BR> 4. Day of new moon, falling on a Sunday, and the moon being in certain [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b " target="_blank">Page0912-b + 42</a>] mansions.<BR> 5. The seventeenth of the astrological Yogas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहार|व्यतीहारः
व्यतीहार व्यतीहार, see व्यतिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यय|व्यत्ययः
व्यत्यय व्यत्यय, i. e. वि-अति-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Inverted or retrograde order.<BR> 2. Contrariety, reverse.<BR> 3. Interchange, Pāṇ. iii. 1, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यास|व्यत्यासः
व्यत्यास व्यत्यास, i. e. वि-अति- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Inverted or retrograde order.<BR> 2. Reversed position.<BR> 3. Contrariety, reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्
व्यथ् व्यथ्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 4, 1453),<BR> 1. To tremble, MBh. 8, 4693.<BR> 2. To be disquieted or afflicted, MBh. 2, 1801.<BR> 3. To fear, MBh. 3, 717.<BR> 4. To suffer pain, ib. 3, 2675.<BR> 5. To dry (Sch.), Man. 7, 84.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. व्यथित.<BR> 1. Alarmed, frightened, Rām. 3, 53, 61.<BR> 2. Afflicted, Ṛt. 6, 18.<BR> 3. Disturbed, Kir. 5, 11; Daśak. in Chr. 193, 1 (changed).<BR> 4. Pained, Pañc. 69, 2.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To make uneasy, Bhag. 2, 15; to afflict, Pañc. ii. d. 103.<BR> 2. To frighten, MBh. 3, 16418.<BR> 3. To lead away from, Bhaṭṭ. 10, 36.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To be afflicted, Rām. 2, 18, 41.<BR> 2. To be frightened, Bhag. 11, 20; to fear (or to tremble), with gen., MBh. 5, 4564. प्रव्यथित, Very anxious, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 7.<BR> --With संप्र सम्प्र, संप्रव्यथित, Frightened, Rām. 1, 38, 16.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vithon, To shake; probably ὄθη, ὄθομαι, ὠθέω, ἐνοσί-χθων, ἔννοσις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथक|व्यथकः
व्यथक व्यथ् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Inflicting pain.<BR> 2. Distressing, afflicting, Kir. 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथा
व्यथा व्यथ् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Alarm, fear, Utt. Rāmac. 9, 6.<BR> 2. Distress, Pañc. 215, 19.<BR> 3. Pain, Pañc. iv. d. 19; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-a " target="_blank">Page0913-a + 44</a>] disease, Pañc. v. d. 66.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ|अव्यथः
अ-व्यथ अ-व्यथ, adj. without pain, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुव्यथ
गुरु- + व्यथ गुरु- + व्यथ, adj. afflicted by heavy pains, Vikr. d. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथ
निर्व्यथ निर्व्यथ, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. quiet, MBh. 3, 13065. 2. free from pain, Rājat. 5, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यथ
स- + व्यथ स- + व्यथ, Adj. 1. suffering pain, with distress, Hit. 113, 13. 2. sorrowful, Śiś. 9, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0912-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्
व्यध् व्यध्, i. 4, विध्य, Par.<BR> 1. To pierce, Chr. 292, 9 = Rigv. i. 86, 9 (ved. विध्यता, with lengthened final).<BR> 2. To hit, Johns. Sel. 39, 31 (वेद्धा, anomal. first fut.).<BR> 3. To wave in triumph, Johns. Sel. 52, 115 (anomal. red. pf. विव्यधुस्).<BR> 4. To pick, Pañc. 62, 9; to wound, Man. 8, 12.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. विद्ध.<BR> 1. Wounded, Chr. 31, 16.<BR> 2. Thrown, Man. 9, 43.<BR> 3. Beaten, whipped.<BR> 4. Opposed, impeded.<BR> 5. Resembling, like. n. A wound, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2647.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, अति-विद्ध, Pierced, transfixed, Rām. 2, 9, 51.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To throw after (another), Man. 9, 43. अनुविद्ध,<BR> 1. Wounded, Ṛt. 1, 13.<BR> 2. Obstructed, Śāk. d. 19; checked.<BR> 3. Mixed, Mālat. 15, 13.<BR> 4. Ornamented, Megh. 66; variegated.<BR> 5. Set (as a jewel).<BR> 6. Full of, abounding.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To throw away, MBh. 3, 15686.<BR> 2. To omit, to neglect, Man. 11, 4. अप-विद्ध,<BR> 1. Thrown away, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 21.<BR> 2. Discarded, Kir. 5, 30 (by churning).<BR> 3. (viz. पुत्र, A son), who having been disowned by his parents, is adopted by another, Man. 9, 159.<BR> 4. Contemptible.<BR> 5. Disabled, broken, literally and figuratively.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप, व्यपविद्ध, Rejected, MBh. 3, 15763.<BR> --With आ आ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b " target="_blank">Page0913-b + 39</a>] To throw, MBh. 3, 11511. आविद्ध,<BR> 1. Thrown, Man. 9, 43.<BR> 2. Pierced, wounded.<BR> 3. Crooked, Vikr. d. 115.<BR> 4. Disappointed.<BR> 5. Stupid.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, To vibrate, MBh. 3, 677. व्याविद्ध, Dishevelled, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 1.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To vibrate, Ragh. 26, 78 (Calc.).<BR> --With उद् उद्, उद्विद्ध, Lofty, Lass. 2. ed. 72, 5.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निर्विद्ध, Wounded, Rām. 3, 50, 19.<BR> --With परि परि, To wound, MBh. 1, 4102.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To throw away, Rām. 2, 63, 34.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To strike, Ragh. 14, 54.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To wound, MBh. 3, 11960.<BR> --Cf. perhaps ϝεθ in ἄεθλος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद्ध
सु- + विद्ध सु- + विद्ध, adj. deeply wounded, Ṛt. 6, 28. Anomal. infin. वेद्धुम् (from विध्, for व्यध्, based on विध्य), MBh. 1, 5286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविद्ध
अन्- + आविद्ध अन्- + आविद्ध, adj. 1. not bored, Śāk. d. 45. 2. unhurt, Suśr. 2, 32, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्व|व्यध्वः
व्यध्व व्यध्व, i. e. वि-अध्वन्, m. A bad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध|व्यधः
व्यध व्यध् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Piercing, Kāvya Prak. 100, 9.<BR> 2. Striking.<BR> II. f. धा, Bleeding, Suśr. 1, 362, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यन्तर|व्यंतरः|व्यन्तरः
व्यन्तर व्यन्तर, i. e. वि-अन्तर, m. A deity (haunting in a tree), Pañc. 250, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यप्
व्यप् व्यप्, see विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रप
व्यपत्रप व्यपत्रप, i. e. वि-अप-त्रप, adj. Shameless, Rām. 2, 68, 17, ed. Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेश|व्यपदेशः
व्यपदेश व्यपदेश, i. e. वि-अप-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Information.<BR> 2. Name, appellation, Bhāṣāp. 46.<BR> 3. Race, Śāk. 104, 6.<BR> 4. Renown, Man. 7, 168.<BR> 5. Pretext, Pañc. iii. d. 79 (महताम्, Pretending [the authority of] powerful men).<BR> 6. Hint.<BR> 7. Craft.<BR> 8. Stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपण|व्यपरोपणं
व्यपरोपण व्यपरोपण, i. e. वि-अप-रुह्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Extirpating, expelling.<BR> 2. Cutting, Ragh. 3, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0913-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृति|व्यपाकृतिः
व्यपाकृति व्यपाकृति, i. e. वि-अप-आ-कृ + ति, n. Repelling, denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाय|व्यपायः
व्यपाय व्यपाय, i. e. वि-अप-इ + अ, m. End, Ragh. 3, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रय|व्यपाश्रयः
व्यपाश्रय व्यपाश्रय, i. e. वि-अप-आ-शृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Taking refuge with, Bhag. 18, 56; relying upon.<BR> 2. Expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षा
व्यपेक्षा व्यपेक्षा, i. e. वि-अप-ईक्ष् + अ, f.<BR> 1. Mutual connexion.<BR> 2. Regard, Chr. 43, 24 (corr. thus); expectation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यपेक्ष
निर्व्यपेक्ष निर्व्यपेक्ष, i. e. निस्-, adj. indifferent, Ragh. 14, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यपेक्षा
स- + व्यपेक्षा स- + व्यपेक्षा, adj. connected, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचार|व्यभिचारः
व्यभिचार व्यभिचार, i. e. वि-अभि-चार् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going astray, erring (literally and figurat.)<BR> 2. The presence of the हेतु without the साध्य, Bhāṣāp. 136.<BR> 3. Following improper courses.<BR> 4. Crime, vice, sin, Hit. iii. d. 16; MBh. 1, 912.<BR> 5. Infidelity of a wife, Man. 10, 164.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचार|सव्यभिचारः
स- + व्यभिचार स- + व्यभिचार, m. a too general middle term (as fire to prove smoke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारतस्
व्यभिचारतस् व्यभिचार + तस्, adv. From the व्यभिचार, involved in the other supposition, Bhāṣāp. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिता
व्यभिचारिता व्यभिचारिता, i. e. व्यभिचारिन् + ता, f. Error, Bhāṣāp. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारित्व
व्यभिचारित्व व्यभिचारित्व, i. e. व्यभिचारिन् + त्व, n. Doubt.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वव्यभिचारित्व
स्वत्व- + व्यभिचारित्व स्वत्व- + व्यभिचारित्व, n. doubt or uncertainty of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिन्
व्यभिचारिन् व्यभिचारिन्, i. e. वि-अभि-चर् and र्यभिचार + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Going astray, wanton, Hit. pr. d. 21, M.M.<BR> 2. Doing what is improper.<BR> II. f. इणी, A wanton woman, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 507.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारिन्
अ- + व्यभिचारिन् अ- + व्यभिचारिन्, adj. never failing, Śāk. 81, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभ्र
व्यभ्र व्यभ्र, i. e. वि-अभ्र, adj. Cloudless, Nal. 17, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय्
व्यय् व्यय्, i. 1, Ātm. (a denomin. from व्यय), To squander away, Hit. ii. d. 91.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. व्ययित,<BR> 1. Expended, Hit. 98, 17.<BR> 2. Dissipated, Hit. 60, 10.<BR> 3. Fallen to decay.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय व्यय, i. e. वि-इ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Mutable, Man. 1, 19.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Disappearance, loss, Lass. 59, 1; Pañc. i. d. 179; Mālat. 70, 14 (risk).<BR> 2. Destruction, Ragh. 5, 5; Daśak. in Chr. 181, 5 (detriment).<BR> 3. Expenditure, expense, Man. 8, 287; Pañc. 138, 4.<BR> 4. Squandering away, Lass. 75, 13.<BR> 5. Misfortune, decline.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यय|अव्ययं|अव्ययः
अ- + व्यय अ- + व्यय, adj. 1. immutable, Man. 1, 19. 2. eternal, Johns. Sel. 23, 118; Rājat. 5, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यय
अति- + व्यय अति- + व्यय, m. spending too much, Hit. ii. d. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनव्यय|भोजनव्ययः
भोजन- + व्यय भोजन- + व्यय, m. expense for food, Hit. 98, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्यय|स्वल्पव्ययः
सु-अल्प- + व्यय सु-अल्प- + व्यय,<BR> I. adj. suffering small expenses, Hit. 46, 8.<BR> II. m. a very small expense, Hit. iii. d. 130 (read कोषस्वल्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययिन्
ऽव्ययिन् -व्ययिन्, i. e. व्यय + इन्, adj. in उदय-, Mounting and falling, Hit. iii. d. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थ|व्यर्थं
व्यर्थ व्यर्थ, i. e. वि-अर्थ, adj.<BR> 1. Useless, unprofitable, Pañc. i. d. 445; Hit. i. d. 129, M.M.; Pañc. 134, 14.<BR> 2. Unmeaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थता
व्यर्थता व्यर्थ + ता, f.<BR> 1. Uselessness, with या or गम्, To become useless, Pañc. 128, 1. 215, 22.<BR> 2. Inoffensiveness, Pañc. 169, 14.<BR> 3. Nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीक|व्यलीकं|व्यलीकः
व्यलीक व्यलीक (cf. अलीक),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Disagreeable, offensive.<BR> 2. Improper.<BR> 3. Painful.<BR> 4. Strange.<BR> II. m. A catamite.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Any displeasing or improper act.<BR> 2. Disagreeableness.<BR> 3. Pain, grief, Śāk. d. 183; Pañc. i. d. 272.<BR> 4. Fault, transgression, Śiś. 9, 85; Hit. ii. d. 125.<BR> 5. Cheating, falsehood, Pañc. i. d. 136 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3208).<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a " target="_blank">Page0915-a + 42</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यलीक
निस्- + व्यलीक निस्- + व्यलीक, adj. 1. not offending, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 49. 2. without pain, pleased, Rām. 2, 18, 53 Gorr.; (given) with pleasure, MBh. 13, 5994. 3. ˚कम्, adv. sincerely, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 42; cf. ˚क + तस्, adv. the same, 3, 24, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0914-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवक्रोशन|व्यवक्रोशनं
व्यवक्रोशन व्यवक्रोशन, i. e. वि-अव-क्रुश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Altercation.<BR> 2. Abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छेद|व्यवच्छेदः|व्यवछेद
व्यवच्छेद व्यवच्छेद, i. e. वि-अव-छिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dividing.<BR> 2. A division.<BR> 3. Discrimination.<BR> 4. Distinction, contrast.<BR> 5. Letting fly an arrow, shooting.<BR> 6. Cutting in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा व्यवधा, i. e. वि-अव-धा, f.<BR> 1. A covering, a screen.<BR> 2. Being covered, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधान|व्यवधानं
व्यवधान व्यवधान, i. e. वि-अव-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Intervening, Ragh. 13, 44.<BR> 2. Separation, Śiś. 9, 51.<BR> 3. Covering, a cover, Śāk. 92, 13 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 4. Being covered, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधायक|व्यवधायकः
व्यवधायक व्यवधायक, i. e. वि-अव-धा + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Intervening.<BR> 2. Separating.<BR> 3. Screening, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधि|व्यवधिः
व्यवधि व्यवधि, i. e. वि-अव-धा (cf. निधि), m. Covering, or a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसाय|व्यवसायः
व्यवसाय व्यवसाय, i. e. वि-अव-सो + अ, m.<BR> 1. Perseverance, Pañc. iii. d. 264; eagerness.<BR> 2. Exertion, effort, Pañc. 215, 22; energy, Pañc. 134, 10; cf. 138, 7; i. d. 195 (येषां व्यवसायनिश्चयः, Who are resolved to endeavour).<BR> 3. Following any business or profession.<BR> 4. Resolve, determination, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 32.<BR> 5. Obstinacy, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 412.<BR> 6. Plan, device, trick, Hit. ii. d. 113 (or, perseverance).<BR> 7. Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायिन्
व्यवसायिन् व्यवसायिन्, i. e. व्यवसाय + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Persevering.<BR> 2. Active, energetic, Hit. ii. d. 11; willing, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b " target="_blank">Page0915-b + 43</a>] Pañc. 134, 10; cf. 138, 7; undertaking, resolute, Pañc. i. d. 278.<BR> 3. Engaged in business.<BR> 4. Performing one's duty, Man. 12, 103.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायिन्
अ- + व्यवसायिन् अ- + व्यवसायिन्, adj. not energetic, Hit. ii. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था व्यवस्था, i. e. वि-अव-स्था, f.<BR> 1. Separating, placing remote or apart.<BR> 2. Placing.<BR> 3. Staying.<BR> 4. State, course, Rājat. 5, 80.<BR> 5. A decree, a written declaration of the law, decision, Rājat. 5, 461.<BR> 6. An engagement, a contract.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थ
अ-व्यवस्थ अ-व्यवस्थ, adj. undecided, Ragh. 7, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापक
व्यवस्थापक व्यवस्थापक, i. e. वि-अव-स्था, Caus., + अक, adj. Deciding, Rājat. 6, 54 (दुस्-, adj. Deciding wrongly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापन|व्यवस्थापनं
व्यवस्थापन व्यवस्थापन, i. e. वि-अव-स्था, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Placing apart.<BR> 2. Placing.<BR> 3. Fixing.<BR> 4. Appointing.<BR> 5. Deciding.<BR> 6. Declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थिति|व्यवस्थितिः
व्यवस्थिति व्यवस्थिति, i. e. वि-अव-स्था + ति, f.<BR> 1. Constancy, perseverance, Bhag. 16, 1.<BR> 2. Determining.<BR> 3. Rule, Man. 10, 70.<BR> 4. Extracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्तृ|व्यवहर्त्तृ
व्यवहर्तृ व्यवहर्तृ, i. e. वि-अव-हृ + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Transacting business, engaged in affairs.<BR> 2. Observing established usages.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A judge.<BR> 2. A litigant, a plaintiff.<BR> 3. Partaker, associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार|व्यवहारः
व्यवहार व्यवहार, i. e. वि-अव-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Doing, performing, Bhāṣāp. 105 (गणन-, Numbering); Lass. 76, 9; occupation, Śāk. 104, 23; action, Mālat. 70, 6.<BR> 2. Affair, Utt. Rāmac. 127, 3 (नास्य व्यवहारो स्त्रेस्हु, He has nothing with weapons); Man. 8, 420.<BR> 3. Profession, business, Pañc. i. d. 91.<BR> 4. Pecuniary transaction, Man. 3, 64; usury, Pañc. i. d. 12.<BR> 5. Petty traffic, Man. 7, 137; trade, Pañc. 7, 17.<BR> 6. Usage, custom, Hit. 58, 18.<BR> 7. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a " target="_blank">Page0916-a + 41</a>] Conduct, Hit. i. d. 57; 70, M.M.<BR> 8. Practice of the courts, or civil and criminal law, Man. 8, 148; judicial proceeding, Man. 8, 1.<BR> 9. Administration of justice, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 528.<BR> 10. Any acts cognisable in courts.<BR> 11. An occurrence which must be inquired, an important affair, Pañc. 45, 13.<BR> 12. Lawsuit, Pañc. 165, 4.<BR> 13. A contract.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाव्यवहारम्
यथा-व्यवहार + म् यथा-व्यवहार + म्, adv. conformably to custom, Hit. 87, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0915-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारक|व्यवहारकः
व्यवहारक व्यवहारक i. e. वि-अव-हृ + अक,<BR> I. m. A trader, Pañc. 138, 15.<BR> II. f. रिका.<BR> 1. Usage.<BR> 2. A brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारज्ञ|व्यवहारज्ञः
व्यवहारज्ञ व्यवहार-ज्ञ, m. A young man of age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारवन्त्|व्यवहारवत्
व्यवहारवन्त् व्यवहार + वन्त्, adj. Occupied, working with, Man. 10, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक व्यवहारिक, i. e. व्यवहार + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Customary.<BR> 2. Relating to legal process.<BR> 3. Litigant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवाय|व्यवायं|व्यवायः
व्यवाय व्यवाय, i. e. वि-अव-इ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Copulation, Rājat. 5, 280.<BR> 2. Intervening, interval.<BR> 3. Covering, disappearance.<BR> II. n. Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायिन्
व्यवायिन् व्यवायिन्, i. e. व्यवाय + इन्, adj. sbst. Lecherous, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्व
व्यश्व व्यश्व, i. e. वि-अश्व, adj. Having no horse, Chr. 297, 15 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यष्टि
व्यष्टि व्यष्टि, i. e. वि-अक्ष् + ति, f. Singleness, individuality, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसन|व्यसनं
व्यसन व्यसन, i. e. वि-अस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Calamity, misfortune, Vikr. 59, 1; Pañc. ii. d. 13; destruction, Mālat. 154, 13; loss, Kir. 13, 15.<BR> 2. Fate.<BR> 3. Ill luck.<BR> 4. Fruitless effort, Bhartṛ. 2, 96 (pl.).<BR> 5. Inability, incompetence (see the next).<BR> 6. Fault, vice, Man. 7, 45; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b " target="_blank">Page0916-b + 44</a>] Hit. pr. d. 48, M.M.; crime.<BR> 7. Sin, Śāk. d. 38.<BR> 8. Intent application or attachment to an object, Pañc. i. d. 314; diligence, Hit. i. d. 31, M.M.<BR> 9. Individuality.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधव्यसन
आयुध- + व्यसन आयुध- + व्यसन, n. destruction of weapons, Man. 7, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौव्यसन
नौ- + व्यसन नौ- + व्यसन, n. shipwreck, Śāk. 90, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलव्यसन
बल- + व्यसन बल- + व्यसन, n. defeat or rout of an army, Hit. iv. d. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलव्यसन
मूल- + व्यसन मूल- + व्यसन, n. execution for a crime (Sch.), Man. 10, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिता
व्यसनिता व्यसनिता, f., and व्यसनित्व व्यसनित्व, n., i. e. व्यसनिन् + ता, or त्व,<BR> 1. Wickedness, Rājat. 5, 255 (त्व); Hit. 94, 3 (ता, instr. Wrongly).<BR> 2. Calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिन्
व्यसनिन् व्यसनिन्, i. e. व्यसन + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Wicked, Pañc. v. d. 17; vicious, Man. 7, 53; Pañc. 163, 14; ruled by passions, Kathās. 26, 199.<BR> 2. Unfortunate, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 814; being in distress, Hit. iii. d. 34; afflicted, Hit. iv. d. 44 (दुर्भिक्ष-, by the calamity of famine).<BR> 3. Intent on, Bhartṛ. 2, 100.<BR> 4. Occupied, Pañc. 192, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसनिन्
अ- + व्यसनिन् अ- + व्यसनिन्, adj. not attached to wicked inclinations, Hit. iii. d. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोत्सेकपराक्रमव्यसनिन्
मानोत्सेकपराक्रम- + व्यसनिन् मानोत्सेकपराक्रम- + व्यसनिन्, i. e. मान-उत्सेक-पराक्रम-व्यसन + इन्, adj. endowed with pride, loftiness, prowess, and intent application, Pañc. iii. d. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतव्यसनिन्
सूत- + व्यसनिन् सूत- + व्यसनिन्, i. e. सूतव्यसन + इन्, adj. being distressed by the incompetence of the charioteer, Chr. 35, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसु
व्यसु व्यसु, i. e. वि-असु, adj. Lifeless, Rājat. 5, 241.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरण|व्याकरणं
व्याकरण व्याकरण, i. e. वि-आ-कृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Explaining.<BR> 2. Grammar, Pañc. 4, 14; ii. d. 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भव्याकरण
गर्भ- + व्याकरण गर्भ- + व्याकरण, n. the development of the embryo, Suśr. 1, 325, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणीव्याकरण
गर्भिणी- + व्याकरण गर्भिणी- + व्याकरण, n. the development of pregnancy, Suśr. 1, 366, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुल|व्याकुलः
व्याकुल व्याकुल, i. e. वि-आकुल, adj.<BR> 1. Confounded, bewildered, Pañc. 9, 13; 144, 4; Hit. iii. d. 110.<BR> 2. Trembling, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a " target="_blank">Page0917-a + 39</a>] Utt. Rāmac. 83, 5.<BR> 3. Dimmed, Chr. 17, 25.<BR> 4. Occupied, Megh. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0916-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलता
व्याकुलता व्याकुल + ता, f., and व्याकुलत्व व्याकुल + त्व, n. Perplexity, Pañc. 143, 4 (ता); agitation, 58, 3 (ता); fear, ib. 76, 12 (त्व).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याकुलता
निर्व्याकुलता निर्व्याकुलता, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलय
व्याकुलय व्याकुलय, a denomin. derived from व्याकुल, Par. To frighten, Pañc. 89, 14.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. व्याकुलित (or व्याकुल + इत), Agitated, alarmed, Pañc. 222, 8; perplexed, Pañc. 142, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृति|व्याकृतिः
व्याकृति व्याकृति, i. e. वि-आ-कृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Explaining.<BR> 2. Grammar.<BR> 3. Change of form, development, Suśr. 1, 9, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोश|व्याकोशः
व्याकोश व्याकोश, and व्याकोष व्याकोष, i. e. वि-आ-कोश, adj. Budded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षेप|व्याक्षेपः
व्याक्षेप व्याक्षेप, i. e. वि-आ-क्षिप् + अ, m. Delay; in अ-, m. Absence of delay, Ragh. 10, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या व्याख्या, i. e. वि-आ-ख्या, f. Exposition, comment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यातृ
व्याख्यातृ व्याख्यातृ, i. e. वि-आ-ख्या + तृ, m. An expounder, Rājat. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यान|व्याख्यानं
व्याख्यान व्याख्यान, i. e. वि-आ-ख्या + अन, n. Explaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टन|व्याघट्टनं
व्याघट्टन व्याघट्टन, i. e. वि-आ-घट्ट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rubbing.<BR> 2. Churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघात|व्याघातः
व्याघात व्याघात, i. e. वि-आ-हन्, Caus., + अ, m.<BR> 1. Obstacle, Hit. ii. d. 4.<BR> 2. Striking.<BR> 3. Wounding, Indr. 5, 11.<BR> 4. Destroying.<BR> 5. The thirteenth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्र|व्याघ्रः
व्याघ्र व्याघ्र, i. e. वि-आ-घ्रा,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A tiger, Pañc. 157, 25.<BR> 2. As latter part of comp. words, Best, preeminent, e. g. पुरुष-, m. An eminent [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b " target="_blank">Page0917-b + 41</a>] man (literally, A tiger-like man), Rām. 3, 53, 19.<BR> II. f. घ्री, The female of a tiger, Bhartṛ. 3, 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याघ्र
निस्- + व्याघ्र निस्- + व्याघ्र, adj. tigerless, Pañc. 231, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याज|व्याजः
व्याज व्याज, i. e. वि-अञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Deceit, fraud, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396; Pañc. 147, 15.<BR> 2. Disguise either of purpose or person.<BR> 3. Appearance, Pañc. iii. d. 125; pretence, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 2.<BR> 4. Means, Pañc. 75, 24; 118, 3.<BR> 5. Wickedness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याज
निस्- + व्याज निस्- + व्याज, adj. upright, honest, Kathās. 22, 146. ˚जम्, adv.<BR> 1. honestly, Amar. 79. 2. exactly, Rājat. 4, 343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याज
स-व्याज स-व्याज, adj. 1. cunning, pretending. 2. fraudulent. ˚जम्, adv. cunningly, under a pretext, Śāk. 18, 21; Vikr. 12, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याड|व्याडः
व्याड व्याड, m.<BR> 1. A snake.<BR> 2. A beast of prey.<BR> 3. A rogue.<BR> 4. Indra (cf. व्याल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडि|व्याडिः
व्याडि व्याडि, m. The name of a grammarian, Kathās. 4, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादान|व्यादानं
व्यादान व्यादान, i. e. वि-आ-दा + अन, n. Opening, setting ajar, Hit. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादित
व्यादित व्यादित, see दा with वि-आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादीर्घ
व्यादीर्घ व्यादीर्घ, i. e. वि-आ-दीर्घ, adj. Long, Bhartṛ. 1, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध|व्याधं|व्याधः
व्याध व्याध, i. e. व्यध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A hunter, Pañc. 147, 11.<BR> 2. A low or wicked man.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मव्याध|धर्म्मव्याधः
धर्म- + व्याध धर्म- + व्याध, m. the pious hunter, epithet of a Brāhmaṇa re-born as hunter in consequence of a curse, MBh. 3, 13710.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगव्याध|मृगव्याधः
मृग- + व्याध मृग- + व्याध, m. a hunter, Rājat. 5, 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाम|व्याधामः
व्याधाम व्याधाम, i. e. वि-आ-धमा + अ (from धम्), m. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाय
व्याधाय व्याधाय, a denomin. derived from व्याध with य, Ātm. To become a hunter, Śṛṅgārat. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0917-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधि|व्याधिः
व्याधि व्याधि, i. e. व्यध् + इ, m.<BR> 1. Pain, Mālat. 69, 5.<BR> 2. Sickness, Hit. i. d. 3, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याधि
निस्- + व्याधि निस्- + व्याधि, adj. healthy, MBh. 9, 2322.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधित|व्याधितः
व्याधित व्याधित, i. e. व्याधि + इत, adj. Afflicted with disease, Man. 4, 157; 8, 395; sick, Hit. i. d. 201, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिन्
व्याधिन् व्याधिन्, i. e. व्याध + इन्, adj. Frequented by hunters, Nalod. 3, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यान|व्यानः
व्यान व्यान, i. e. वि-अन् + अ, m. One of the five vital airs, that which is diffused throughout the body, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापक|व्यापकः
व्यापक व्यापक, i. e. वि-आप् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Diffusive.<BR> 2. Extensive.<BR> II. m. A pervading attribute, one always found where some other is found, Bhāṣāp. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापकत्व
व्यापकत्व व्यापक + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Diffusion, pervadence.<BR> 2. State of being more extensive, Bhāṣāp. 9, cf. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापत्ति|व्यापत्तिः
व्यापत्ति व्यापत्ति, i. e. वि-आ-पद् + ति, f. Ruin, Pañc. i. d. 316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद् व्यापद्, i. e. वि-आ-पद्, f.<BR> 1. Calamity, Hit. 95, 1, M.M. (at the end of a comp. adj. त्यक्त-, vb. त्यज्, Free from calamity).<BR> 2. Derangement.<BR> 3. Disease.<BR> 4. Death, Megh. 111.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहव्यापद्
विरह- + व्यापद् विरह- + व्यापद्, adj. (dying), vanishing by separation, Megh. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापाद|व्यापादः
व्यापाद व्यापाद, i. e. वि-आ-पद् + अ, m. The wish or project to injure another person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादन|व्यापादनं
व्यापादन व्यापादन, i. e. वि-आ-पद्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Killing, Pañc. 265, 16 (सर्प-, Being killed by the snake).<BR> 2. Wishing to injure another person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादनीयता
व्यापादनीयता व्यापादनीय + ता [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b " target="_blank">Page0918-b + 44</a>] (vb. पद्), f. Necessity of being killed, Pañc. 143, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापार|व्यापारः
व्यापार व्यापार, i. e. वि-आ- 2. पृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Occupation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 18; doing, Pañc. 162, 8; business, 262, 7; Vikr. d. 58 (व्यापारं व्रजसि शरीरे, You have to do with my body, i. e. you command over my body).<BR> 2. Work, Śāk. d. 26; Bhāṣāp. 58; 79.<BR> 3. Affair, Pañc. 57, 8.<BR> 4. Trade (cf. व्रज्), profession.<BR> 5. Exercise, practice, exertion, Hit. pr. d. 43, M.M.; activity, Mālat. 10, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापार|अव्यापारः
अ- + व्यापार अ- + व्यापार and मिथ्या-, m. occupation with things in which one is not concerned, Pañc. 9, 24 (मिथ्या-), and i. d. 26 (अ-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंव्यापार
किम्- + व्यापार किम्- + व्यापार, adj. with what occupied, Śāk. Chezy., 150, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्व्यापार
दृग्व्यापार दृग्व्यापार, i. e. दृश्-, m. play of the eyes, Rājat. 5, 366 (pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यापार
निस्- + व्यापार निस्- + व्यापार,<BR> I. m. absence of occupation, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 13.<BR> II. adj. not occupied, Ragh. 15, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्यापार|वाग्व्यापारः
वाग्व्यापार वाग्व्य्˚, i. e. वाच्-, m. conversation, Hit. 85, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापित्व
व्यापित्व व्यापित्व, i. e. व्यापिन् + त्व, n. The state of pervading, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापिन्
व्यापिन् व्यापिन्, i. e. वि-आप् + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Diffusive.<BR> 2. Comprehensive.<BR> 3. Pervading, Bhāṣāp. 42.<BR> 4. Filling, Kir. 5, 18.<BR> 5. Extending to, Śāk. d. 170.<BR> II. m. The pervading property or power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्ति|व्याप्तिः
व्याप्ति व्याप्ति, i. e. वि-आप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Pervading, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 18.<BR> 2. Universal permeation, omnipresence.<BR> 3. Inherence, the inherent and essential presence of any thing or property in another, as heat in fire, oil in the sesamum seed.<BR> 4. The relation of a subject (व्याप्त, व्याप्य) to a predicate (व्यापक) in an universal proposition, Bhāṣāp. 65; 67; 68; 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिमन्त्|व्याप्तिमत्
व्याप्तिमन्त् व्याप्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a " target="_blank">Page0919-a + 41</a>] मती,<BR> 1. Pervading, diffusive.<BR> 2. Pervaded, attended by, Man. 12, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0918-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्व|व्याप्यत्वं
व्याप्यत्व व्याप्य + त्व (vb. आप् with वि), n.<BR> 1. Capacity of being pervaded, or of obtaining, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 15.<BR> 2. State of being less extensive, Bhāṣāp. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याम|व्यामः
व्याम व्याम, i. e. वि-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A fathom, or the space between the tips of the fingers of either hand when the arms are extended, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 17; MBh. 3, 10207.<BR> 2. Smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्ष|व्यामर्षः
व्यामर्ष व्यामर्ष, i. e. वि-आ-मृष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Erasure (vb. मृश्?).<BR> 2. Impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिश्र|व्यामिश्रं
व्यामिश्र व्यामिश्र, i. e. वि-आ-मिश्र (q. cf.), adj. Mixed, blended, confounded, Bhag. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोह|व्यामोहः
व्यामोह व्यामोह, i. e. वि-आ-मुह् + अ, m. Error, foolishness, Prab. 76, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायतत्व|व्यायतत्वं
व्यायतत्व व्यायतत्व, i. e. वि-आ-यत (vb. यम्), + त्व, n. Firmness, Śāk. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम|व्यायामः
व्यायाम व्यायाम, i. e. वि-आ-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Athletic exercise.<BR> 2. Exertion, fighting, Arj. 3, 40.<BR> 3. Manhood, manliness, MBh. 13, 542.<BR> 4. Occupation, business.<BR> 5. A difficulty.<BR> 6. Fatigue, labour, Sāv. 5, 2.<BR> 7. A fathom (see व्याम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिन्
व्यायामिन् व्यायामिन्, i. e. व्यायाम + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Athletic.<BR> 2. Active.<BR> 3. Undergoing fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याल|व्यालः
व्याल व्याल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Wicked, Kir. 17, 25.<BR> 2. Cruel.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A snake, Hit. iii. d. 30.<BR> 2. A beast of prey, Pañc. i. d. 420.<BR> 3. A vicious elephant, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR> 4. A rogue.<BR> 5. A king.<BR> III. f. ली, A female snake, Chr. 22, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालग्राहिन्
व्यालग्राहिन् व्याल-ग्राहिन्, m. A serpent-catcher, Hit. iii. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोल
व्यालोल व्यालोल, i. e. वि-आ-लुल् + अ, adj. Tremulous, shaking, Rājat. 5, 372. Cf. the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोलकुन्तलकलापवन्त्|व्यालोलकुन्तलकलापवत्
व्यालोलकुन्तलकलापवन्त् व्यालोल-कुन्तल-कलाप + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, With dishevelled hair, Caur. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावक्रोशी
व्यावक्रोशी व्यावक्रोशी, i. e. वि-आ-अव-क्रुश् + अ + ई, f. Mutual imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावभाषी
व्यावभाषी व्यावभाषी, i. e. वि-आ-अव-भाष् + अ + ई, f. Mutual abuse or imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त|व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त्तः
व्यावर्त व्यावर्त, i. e. वि-वा-वृत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Going round, revolving.<BR> 2. Encompassing.<BR> 3. Choosing, appointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तकता
व्यावर्तकता व्यावर्तकता, i. e. वि-आ-वृत् + अक + ता, f. Excluding, Vedāntas. in Chr. 213, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तन|व्यावर्तनं|व्यावर्त्तन
व्यावर्तन व्यावर्तन, i. e. वि-आ-वृत् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rolling round.<BR> 2. A volute, Kir. 5, 30.<BR> 3. A band.<BR> 4. Encompassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारिक|व्यावहारिकः
व्यावहारिक व्यावहारिक, i. e. व्यवहार + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Active, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 6.<BR> 2. Usual, customary.<BR> 3. Judicial, relating to trials, Man. 8, 78.<BR> II. m. A counseller, Rām. 2, 51, 13, ed. Seramp. (thus to be read).<BR> III. n. Use, Man. 8, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृति|व्यावृतिः
व्यावृति व्यावृति, i. e. वि-आ-वृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Covering, screening.<BR> 2. Exclusion, exception (? see the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्ति|व्यावृत्तिः
व्यावृत्ति व्यावृत्ति, i. e. वि-आ-वृत् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Rolling back.<BR> 2. Surrounding, screening.<BR> 3. Rejection, exclusion, exception, Kumāras. 2, 27.<BR> 4. Choice.<BR> 5. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यास|व्यासः
व्यास व्यास, i. e. वि- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Extension, diffusion.<BR> 2. Distinction, detail.<BR> 3. A sage, the supposed compiler [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a " target="_blank">Page0920-a + 39</a>] of the Vedas and Purāṇas, Lass. 49, 2; Chr. 45, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0919-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासङ्ग|व्यासंग|व्यासंगः|व्यासङ्गः
व्यासङ्ग व्यासङ्ग, i. e. वि-आ-सञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Addition.<BR> 2. Attachment, Bhartṛ. 1, 66; sitting on, Mālat. 153, 4.<BR> 3. Separation, detachment.<BR> 4. Perplexity, confusion, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहार|व्याहारः
व्याहार व्याहार, i. e. वि-आ-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Voice, a word, speech, Utt. Rāmac. 104, 5.<BR> 2. Humorous speech, jest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृति|व्याहृतिः
व्याहृति व्याहृति, i. e. वि-आ-हृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Voice, speech.<BR> 2. A word.<BR> 3. A mystical word, as ॐ, स्वर्, Man. 2, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छेत्तृ
व्युच्छेत्तृ व्युच्छेत्तृ, i. e. वि-उद्-छिद् + तृ, m. f. त्री, and n. Who or what destroys.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्युच्छेत्तृ
अ- + व्युच्छेत्तृ अ- + व्युच्छेत्तृ, m. a protector, MBh. 12, 2901.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युति|व्युतिः
व्युति व्युति, i. e. वि-वे + ति, f.<BR> 1. Weaving.<BR> 2. Sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम|व्युत्क्रमं|व्युत्क्रमः
व्युत्क्रम व्युत्क्रम, i. e. वि-उद्-क्रम् + अ, Inverted order, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थान|व्युत्थानं
व्युत्थान व्युत्थान, i. e. वि-उद्-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Completion of religious meditation, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 16.<BR> 2. Independence.<BR> 3. Obstruction, hindering.<BR> 4. Opposition, doing that which is prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पत्ति|व्युत्पत्तिः
व्युत्पत्ति व्युत्पत्ति, i. e. वि-उद्-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Conversancy with literature or science.<BR> 2. Etymology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदास|व्युदासः
व्युदास व्युदास, i. e. वि-उद्- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Throwing away, Nalod. 4, 14 (loss).<BR> 2. Indifference to, disregard for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपदेश|व्युपदेशः
व्युपदेश व्युपदेश, i. e. वि-उप-दिश् + अ, m. Pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरम|व्युपरमः
व्युपरम व्युपरम, i. e. वि-उप-रम् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b " target="_blank">Page0920-b + 39</a>] m. Cessation, Utt. Rāmac. 159, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपशम|व्युपशमः
व्युपशम व्युपशम, i. e. वि-उपशम, m. Not ceasing (at the end of a comp. adj.), Mālat. 86, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
† 1. व्युष् व्युष्, or प्युष् प्युष्, i. 4, Par. To burn (cf. उष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
† 2. व्युष् व्युष्, or प्युष् प्युष्, प्युस् प्युस्, पुष् पुष्, व्युस् ब्युस्, or बुस् बुस्, i. 4, Par. To divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
† 3. व्युष् व्युष्, or प्युष् प्युष्, पुस् पुस्, i. 10, Par. To reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
व्युष्ट व्युष्ट, i. e. the ptcple. of the pf. pass. of वि- 2. वस्,<BR> I. Dawned.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Dawn.<BR> 2. Day.<BR> 3. Fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्टि|व्युष्टिः
व्युष्टि व्युष्टि, i. e. वि- 2. वस् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Dawn, Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR> 2. Fruit, consequence.<BR> 3. Increase.<BR> 4. Praise, Brāhmaṇav. 2, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह|व्यूहः
व्यूह व्यूह, i. e. वि-ऊह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Military array, Man. 7, 187.<BR> 2. An army, Ragh. 7, 51; squadron, Man. 7, 188.<BR> 3. A flock, a multitude, Nal. 12, 30.<BR> 4. Logic.<BR> 5. Making.<BR> 6. The body.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भव्यूह
गर्भ- + व्यूह गर्भ- + व्यूह, m. a kind of array, MBh. 6, 3850; 3851.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रव्यूह|चक्रव्यूहः
चक्र- + व्यूह चक्र- + व्यूह, m. the array in a circle, ib. 7, 1441.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डव्यूह|दंडव्यूह|दण्डव्यूहः
दण्ड- + व्यूह दण्ड- + व्यूह, m. the array in line, Man. 7, 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलव्यूह
मण्डल- + व्यूह मण्डल- + व्यूह, m. the array in a circle, cf. Pañc. 9, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहन|व्यूहनं
व्यूहन व्यूहन, i. e. वि-ऊह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Arraying.<BR> 2. Structure of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ये
व्ये व्ये (i. e. वि-इ), i. 1, Par. Ātm. To cover.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. वित, placed, bound, Vikr. d. 157.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a " target="_blank">Page0921-a + 42</a>] the prep. आ आ, आवीत, Enveloped, Bhāg. P. 3, 31, 4.<BR> --With उप उप, उपवीत, n. The cord worn by the three first classes of the Hindus over the left and under the right shoulder, Man. 2, 44.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With नि नि, निवीत, n. The brahmanical thread suspended round the neck, in which manner it is worn on some occasions.<BR> --With परि परि, परिवीत,<BR> 1. Surrounded, Kir. 5, 42; invested.<BR> 2. Covered, clothed, Ragh. 15, 77 (Calc.).<BR> 3. Overspread, pervaded. n. The bow of Brahman.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संवीत,<BR> 1. Surrounded.<BR> 2. Covered, Rām. 3, 50, 12.<BR> 3. Clothed, Rām. 3, 52, 9.<BR> 4. Adorned, Rām. 3, 52, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἱ in ἱμάτιον.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवीत
यज्ञ- + वीत यज्ञ- + वीत, n. the sacrificial cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीत
सु- + वीत सु- + वीत, adj. well covered, Chr. 27, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0920-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योकार|व्योकारः
व्योकार व्यो-कार (व्यो is perhaps an imitative sound), m. A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमन्
व्योमन् व्योमन्, n.<BR> 1. The sky, atmosphere, heaven, Pañc. ii. d. 21; Vikr. d. 20.<BR> 2. Æther, Bhāṣāp. 2.<BR> 3. Water.<BR> 4. A temple sacred to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योष|व्योषं
व्योष व्योष, i. e. वि-उष् + अ, n. The aggregate of three spices, black pepper, long pepper, and dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्
व्रज् व्रज्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 2263),<BR> 1. To go, Man. 2, 56; Pañc. i. d. 129 (विश्वासे, To trust).<BR> 2. To proceed, Hit. iv. d. 75.<BR> 3. To pass away (as time), Pañc. 117, 9; Megh. 104.<BR> 4. To go to (with acc.), Pañc. i. d. 325; to approach, Bhag. 18, 66; to visit for adultery, Man. 8, 383.<BR> 5. To obtain, Pañc. i. d. 246.<BR> 6. To undergo; with abstracts, to become that which the corresponding concrete noun signifies, e. g. Pañc. 33, 7, छात्रताम्, to become a pupil; cf. Man. 3, 179; Śāk. d. 9; निर्-वृतिम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-b " target="_blank">Page0921-b + 42</a>] To grow happy, Vikr. d. 28.<BR> 7. With व्यापारम् and loc. To rule over, Vikr. d. 58.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. व्रजित, Going. n. Roaming.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To send.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. † To prepare, to adorn.<BR> 2. † To go.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To follow, Man. 11, 111; to pursue, Pañc. i. d. 314 (सङ्गम्, To attach one's self).<BR> 2. To visit in successive order, MBh. 3, 8266.<BR> 3. To perform, Man. 2, 241.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To follow, MBh. 2, 1606.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To approach, Man. 2, 196.<BR> 2. With पुनर्, To return, MBh. 3, 10273.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To go to meet, Ragh. 1, 90.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To wander about as a mendicant, Man. 6, 33.<BR> 2. To walk, MBh. 12, 5098. परिव्रज्या, see s. v.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To go away (from home), Man. 6, 39; cf. 34.<BR> 2. To go in exile, Rām. 3, 53, 16. प्रव्रजित, Gone away, Hit. 64, 4. m. A mendicant. f. ता, A female devotee, Man. 8, 363. n. Wandering about as a mendicant, Chr. 10, 5. प्रव्रज्या, see s. v.<BR> --Caus. To banish, MBh. 2, 2674.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To go near, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 96.<BR> --With उपसम् उप-सम्, To go near, Man. 6, 51.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vrikan, persequi; A.S. wrecan; O.H.G. rehhan, wreh, exul; A.S. wraecca; probably Lat. ulciscor (or to रक्ष्?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्रजित
दुस्- + व्रजित दुस्- + व्रजित, n. a bad manner of going, MBh. 3, 14669. व्रज्या, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज व्रज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A road.<BR> 2. A flock, a herd, Chr. 292, 3 = Rigv. i. 86, 3; a multitude, MBh. 6, 5441.<BR> 3. A cow-pen, Chr. 294, 4 = Rigv. i. 92, 4.<BR> 4. The name of a district about अग्र and मथुरा.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Lat. vulgus (or = वर्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोव्रज|गोव्रजः
गो- + व्रज गो- + व्रज, m. 1. pasture ground for cattle, Man. 4, 52. 2. a proper name, MBh. 9, 2568.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रव्रज
नेत्र- + व्रज नेत्र- + व्रज, m. (pl.), all the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a " target="_blank">Page0922-a + 42</a>] eyes, Ragh. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0921-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजन|व्रजनं
व्रजन व्रज् + अन, n. Going, roaming, Pañc. 116, 24; exile, Pañc. iii. d. 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या<BR> I. व्रज् + या, f.<BR> 1. March.<BR> 2. Attack.<BR> 3. Wandering about as a mendicant.<BR> II. व्रज + य, f.<BR> 1. A flock, a class, a tribe.<BR> 2. A theatre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रञ्ज्
† व्रञ्ज् व्रञ्ज् (?), i. 1, Par. To go (cf. व्रज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् व्रण्, † i. 1, Par. To sound.<BR> --i. 10 (cf. the next), Par. To wound, व्रणित (rather व्रण + इत), Wounded, Utt. Rāmac. 94, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण|व्रणं|व्रणः
व्रण व्रण, n.<BR> 1. A wound, Pañc. 170, 25.<BR> 2. A fracture, Man. 2, 47.<BR> 3. A boil, a tumour, Hit. ii. d. 101.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. vulnus; οὐλή (i. e. ϝολνη), ἄπ-ελος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रण
अ- + व्रण अ- + व्रण, adj. 1. without any fracture, Man. 2, 47. 2. without a wound or perceivable injury, Suśr. 2, 311, 13(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतव्रण|अकृतव्रणः
अ-कृत- + व्रण अ-कृत- + व्रण, m. a proper name, Chr. 13, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्रण
निस्- + व्रण निस्- + व्रण, adj. 1. unwounded, MBh. 7, 2742. 2. without a fracture, Man. 6, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तारितबहुव्रण
वि-स्तारित-बहु- + व्रण वि-स्तारित-बहु- + व्रण, (vb. स्तृ), adj., f. णा, having made many wounds, Pañc. 171, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणिन्
व्रणिन् व्रणिन्, i. e. व्रण + इन्, adj. Having boils, sores, Bhartṛ. 1, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रत|व्रतं|व्रतः
व्रत व्रत (an old ptcple. of the pf. pass. of वृ), n.<BR> 1. A (self-chosen) voluntary act, Chr. 43, 24; rule, Rām. 3, 53, 18; Bhartṛ. 2, 69.<BR> 2. Action, doing, Man. 9, 304.<BR> 3. Work, Chr. 295, 12 = Rigv. i. 92, 12.<BR> 4. A devout act, Man. 2, 173; as fasting, continence, a vowed observance, a vow, Vikr. 37, 7; Pañc. 260, 13.<BR> 5. Eating (cf. पयस्-व्रत).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably ἑορτή.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत
अ- + व्रत अ- + व्रत, adj. one who does not observe the rules of his order, Man. 3, 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कव्रत|अर्कव्रतं|अर्कव्रतः
अर्क- + व्रत अर्क- + व्रत, n. levying taxes, drawing the wealth of the people, as the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-b " target="_blank">Page0922-b + 47</a>] sun evaporates water, Man. 9, 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधाराव्रत
असि-धारा- + व्रत असि-धारा- + व्रत, n. a vow to stand on the edge of a sword, Pañc. 196, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यव्रत|आर्य्यव्रत
आर्य- + व्रत आर्य- + व्रत, adj. one who observes the rules of the Āryas, or respectable men, MBh. 1, 7424.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुव्रत|इन्दुव्रतं
इन्दु- + व्रत इन्दु- + व्रत, n. a kind of vow, MBh. 13, 1797.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रव्रत
इन्द्र- + व्रत इन्द्र- + व्रत, n. the duty of the king to distribute gratifications, Man. 9, 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोव्रत
गो- + व्रत गो- + व्रत, adj. continent, MBh. 5, 3560.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीव्रत
गौरी- + व्रत गौरी- + व्रत, n. lasciviousness, Hit. 42, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डव्रत
दण्ड- + व्रत दण्ड- + व्रत, n. judicial power, Bhāg. P. 4, 13, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढव्रत
दृढ- + व्रत दृढ- + व्रत, adj. 1. one who observes his vows, Man. 11, 81. 2. persevering in observing one's vow, Sund. 1, 10. 3. persisting in, Rām. 3, 52, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रत|देवव्रतः
देव- + व्रत देव- + व्रत, adj. attached to the deities, pious, Bhāg. P. 1, 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतव्रत|धृतव्रतः
धृत- + व्रत धृत- + व्रत, adj. attached, faithful, Rām. 3, 2, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमव्रत
नियम- + व्रत नियम- + व्रत, n. vow of penance, Pañc. 165, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्रत
निस्- + व्रत निस्- + व्रत, adj. one who does not observe the religious precepts, MBh. 12, 1335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिव्रत
पति- + व्रत पति- + व्रत,<BR> I. n. fidelity to one's husband, ib. 13, 165; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 741.<BR> II. f. ता, a faithful or virtuous woman, Pañc. iii. d. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोव्रत|पयोव्रतः
पयोव्रत पयोव्रत, i. e. पयस्-,<BR> I. n. the vow of living only on milk, Bhāg. P. 8, 16, 58.<BR> II. adj., f. ता, nourished by milk alone, Man. 11, 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मव्रत
ब्रह्मव्रत ब्रह्मव्रत, i. e. ब्रह्मन्- (n.), chastity, Pañc. 187, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुव्रत|मधुव्रतः
मधु- + व्रत मधु- + व्रत, m. a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रत|महाव्रतं
महा- + व्रत महा- + व्रत, adj., f. ता, one who has undergone great austerities, Chr. 17, 27; 40, 15 (read महा-व्रतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतव्रत|मारुतव्रतं
मारुत- + व्रत मारुत- + व्रत, n. the duty of a king to trace out everything by means of spies, cf. Man. 9, 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनव्रत
मौन- + व्रत मौन- + व्रत, adj., f. ता, holding one's tongue, Pañc. 94, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतव्रत
यत- + व्रत यत- + व्रत (vb. यम्), adj. firm to an engagement or vow, Johns. Sel. 36, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमव्रत|यमव्रतं
यम- + व्रत यम- + व्रत, n. the duty of a king to punish offences without partiality, cf. Man. 9, 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यव्रत
रहस्य- + व्रत रहस्य- + व्रत, n. the command of that mysterious power by which mystical weapons may be wielded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलव्रत
विपुल- + व्रत विपुल- + व्रत, adj. of great devotion, Johns. Sel. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशितव्रत
सम्-शित- + व्रत सम्-शित- + व्रत (vb. शि), adj. 1. one who has accomplished [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a " target="_blank">Page0923-a + 43</a>] his vow, Man. 1, 104 (read संशित instead of शंसित). 2. faithful to a vow or obligation, Johns. Sel. 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यव्रत|सत्यव्रतः
सत्य- + व्रत सत्य- + व्रत,<BR> I. adj. veracious, honest, Rām. 3, 55, 38.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Pañc. iii. d. 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्रत|सुव्रतः
सु- + व्रत सु- + व्रत,<BR> I. adj. rigidly observing any religious vow or obligation, virtuous, Chr. 58, 6.<BR> II. f. ता. 1. a virtuous wife. 2. a cow easily milked. 3. a proper name, Śāk. 102, 22 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिव्रत|स्तुतिव्रतः
स्तुति- + व्रत स्तुति- + व्रत, m. a bard, a herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0922-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतति|व्रततिः
व्रतति and ती व्रतती̆ (vb. वृत्). f.<BR> 1. Spreading.<BR> 2. A creeper, Śāk. d. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्थ|व्रतस्थः
व्रतस्थ व्रत-स्थ, adj., f. था, Engaged in religious austerities, Chr. 47, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिक
ऽव्रतिक -व्रतिक, i. e. व्रत + इक in वक-, adj. Acting like a crane, hypocritic, Man. 4, 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिन् व्रतिन्, i. e. व्रत + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Engaged in a religious vow or obligation, pious, Pañc. i. d. 467.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An employer of priests.<BR> 2. An ascetic.<BR> 3. A religious student, Man. 2, 189; 4, 91; 11, 121.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोव्रतिन्
गो- + व्रतिन् गो- + व्रतिन्, m. the name of a sort of anchorite, MBh. 5, 3559 (cf. गो-व्रत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रतिन्
देव- + व्रतिन् देव- + व्रतिन्, adj. worshipping the deities, MBh. 13, 3534 (cf. देव-व्रत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रतिन्
महा- + व्रतिन् महा- + व्रतिन्, m. 1. a devotee, an ascetic (cf. महा-व्रत). 2. a name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकव्रतिन्
वक- + व्रतिन् वक- + व्रतिन्, adj. acting like a crane, hypocritic, Man. 4, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन व्रातीन, i. e. व्रत + ईन, m. A hired labourer, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च्
व्रश्च् व्रश्च्, i. 6, वृश्च, Par.<BR> 1. To tear.<BR> 2. To cut, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 41.<BR> 3. To wound.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वृक्ण, Broken, Bhaṭṭ. 12, 75.<BR> --Cf. ἕλκος, ῥάκος, λακίς, λακερός; Lat. lacerare, ulcus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं|व्रश्चनः
व्रश्चन व्रश्च् + अन,<BR> I. m. A small saw or chisel.<BR> II. n. Cutting, wounding, Man. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजि|व्राजिः
व्राजि व्राजि, i. e. व्रज् + इ, f. (?), A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात|व्रातः
व्रात व्रात, probably व्रत + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The company and attendants at a marriage feast.<BR> 2. An assemblage, a multitude, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 19; Chr. 4, 19.<BR> 3. The son of an outcaste.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Bodily labour.<BR> 2. Day labour.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषव्रात
वृषव्रात वृषव्रात, i. e. वृषन्-, adj. abounding in drops of rain, Chr. 291, 4 = Rigv. i. 85, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्य|व्रात्यः
व्रात्य व्रात्य, i. e. व्रात + य,<BR> I. m. An outcaste, Man. 2, 39.<BR> II. f. या, The daughter of an outcaste, Man. 8, 373.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यता
व्रात्यता व्रात्य + ता, f. The state of an outcaste, Man. 11, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
† व्री व्री, ii. 9, व्री̆णा, व्री̆णी, Par. To choose.<BR> --i. 4, Ātm. To be chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् व्रीड्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To be, or grow bashful, Vikr. 8, 17.<BR> 2. † To throw.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वृडित (perhaps rather वॄडा + इत), Ashamed, modest, Chr. 56, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड व्रीड (m. and) f. डा,<BR> 1. Shame, Rājat. 5, 338.<BR> 2. Bashfulness, Bhartṛ. 2, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रीड
स- + व्रीड स- + व्रीड, adj., f. डा, 1. ashamed, Chr. 61, 42. 2. bashful, Chr. 5, 4; Vikr. 10, 12. 3. modest. ˚डम्, adv. 1. with shame, ashamed, Pañc. 208, 13. 2. bashfully, Vikr. 28, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् व्रीस्, see व्रूस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि व्रीहि (probably derived from वृध्), m. Rice, Pañc. 167, 1 (pl. grains of rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
† व्रुड् व्रुड्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To cover.<BR> 2. To heap.<BR> 3. To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूष्
व्रूष् व्रूष्, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
† व्रूस् व्रूस्, or व्रूष् व्रूष्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a " target="_blank">Page0924-a + 39</a>] कष् कष्, व्रीस् व्रीस्, i. 10, Par. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0923-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय व्रैहेय, i. e. व्रीहि + एय, adj. Fit for, or sown with, rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली व्ली, see ब्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् व्लेक्ष्, see वेक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु शंयु, i. e. शम् + यु, adj. Happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव शंव, i. e. शम् + व,<BR> I. adj. Prosperous, happy, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 18.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR> 2. The iron head of a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर शंवर, n. Water (see शम्बर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस् शंस्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 7687),<BR> 1. To praise, MBh. 2, 2298; pass. शस्य, Chr. 292, 4 = Rigv. i. 86, 4.<BR> 2. To report, Man. 7, 116; Rām. 3, 55, 16.<BR> 3. To say, Vikr. d. 105; MBh. 3, 2584.<BR> 4. † To be unhappy.<BR> 5. † To hurt.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. शस्त.<BR> 1. Best, excellent.<BR> 2. Right, happy. n.<BR> 1. Happiness.<BR> 2. The body.<BR> II. शंसित.<BR> 1. Praised, Pañc. i. d. 195.<BR> 2. Said.<BR> 3. Wished.<BR> 4. Calumniated.<BR> 5. Certain. Man. 1, 104, read संशित.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. शस्य.<BR> 1. Praiseworthy, Pañc. i. d. 248; excellent.<BR> 2. Desirable. n.<BR> 1. Good quality, merit.<BR> 2. Fruit (cf. सस्य), Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 650.<BR> 3. Corn, Hit. 46, 6, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR> नव-, n. new grain, Man. 4, 26.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, अभिशस्त,<BR> 1. Accused, Man. 8, 373.<BR> 2. Defamed, Man. 4, 211. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b " target="_blank">Page0924-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> I. Par.<BR> 1. To report, Ragh. 1, 86.<BR> 2. To conciliate, Draup. 5, 12.<BR> II. Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 2, 1904).<BR> 1. To wish, MBh. 3, 17171.<BR> 2. To hope, Śāk. d. 48.<BR> 3. To fear, Bhāg. P. 1, 13, 31.<BR> 4. To believe, Rām. 2, 51, 14. आशंसित, Desired, Kir. 5, 52.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To desire, MBh. 1, 6920.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To praise, Man. 3, 230; anomal. प्रशंसीयात्, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 975 = Cāṇ. 37 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 409; absol. प्रशस्य, Pañc. 98, 4.<BR> 2. To recommend, Man. 5, 127.<BR> 3. With न, To disapprove, to blame, Chr. 7, 12.<BR> 4. To esteem, Man. 7, 209.<BR> 5. To declare, Lass. 12, 18. प्रशस्त, Good, Hit. iii. d. 74.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-प्रशस्त, bad, inferior, Nalod. 20, 41. n. dirt, Man. 11, 255.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. प्रशस्य, Good. Comparat. ज्यायंस् and श्रेयांस्, superl. ज्येष्ठ and श्रेष्ठ, see s. v. v.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To praise, MBh. 3, 11908.<BR> --Cf. Lat. censere, canere, Casmena, carmen, con-cinn + us; Goth. hazjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त
अ-शस्त अ-शस्त, adj. 1. not praiseworthy, Rājat. 5, 13. 2. inauspicious, Lass. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा शंस् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Praise, Pañc. i. d. 80.<BR> 2. Speech.<BR> 3. Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
ऽशंसिन् -शंस् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Announcing, Vikr. 60, 14; 65, 11.<BR> 2. Showing, Śiś. 9, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्त्
शंस्त् शंस्त्, see सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ शंस् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A panegyrist.<BR> 2. A flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् शक्, ii. 9, शक्नु, Par., and i. 4, शक्य, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To endure, MBh. 3, 11277.<BR> 2. To be able, Rām. 1, 42, 21; with the infin., Man. 7, 6; with the ptcple. in the signification of the infin., अपूर्यां पूरयन्न् इच्छाम्...न शक्नुयात्, He is not able to satisfy the insatiable desire, MBh. 12, 514. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-a " target="_blank">Page0925-a + 47</a>]<BR> 3. Impers. pass. To be fit to be done, MBh. 1, 6678.<BR> 4. The pass. transfers its pass. signification to the infin. which it governs, e. g. न शक्यन्ते नियन्तुम्, Man. 2, 96 (They cannot be restrained); Hit. 11, 6, M.M. (नीतिं ग्राहयितुं शक्यन्ते, They are able to be taught good behaviour); with a ptcple. of the pass. of the Caus. instead of the infin., न शक्यते निवर्त्यमाना, Chr. 46, 23 (She cannot be induced to return).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. शक्त.<BR> 1. Powerful, capable, Man. 2, 109.<BR> 2. Able, Vikr. d. 72; with the infin., Man. 9, 10; with the loc. in the sense of an infin., MBh. 3, 2263; Pañc. iv. d. 28.<BR> 3. Clever, Hit. ii. d. 74.<BR> 4. Diligent, attentive, intent.<BR> 5. Speaking civilly (cf. शच्).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. शक्य.<BR> 1. Easy to be overpowered, Pañc. iii. d. 53.<BR> 2. Practicable, possible, Rām. 3, 53, 27; Chr. 8, 27.<BR> 3. Transfers its pass. signification to the infin. which it governs, e. g. शक्या रक्षितुम्, Man. 9, 10 (They can be guarded).<BR> 4. Superl. शक्यतम, Most possible, Hit. iii. d. 115 (न शक्यतमाः समीहितुम्, Are not at all to be aspired to).<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. impossible, Hit. i. d. 89, M.M.; Chr. 57, 25. Anomal. desider. शिक्ष, Par. Ātm. To learn, Man. 2, 20. शिक्षित,<BR> 1. Instructed, Pañc. 94, 20.<BR> 2. Learned, Hit. ii. d. 154.<BR> 3. Disciplined.<BR> 4. Trained (as an animal).<BR> 5. Docile.<BR> 6. Modest, diffident.<BR> 7. Skilful, clever, conversant.<BR> --Caus. of the desider. शिक्षय, To teach, M.M. 2, 69.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनु-शिक्षित, Learned (by imitation), Utt. Rāmac. 63, 2.<BR> --Caus. of the desider. To instruct, MBh. 1, 5761.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b " target="_blank">Page0925-b + 41</a>] अव अव, अवशक्य, Possible, Caurap. 43.<BR> --With अभि अभि, Caus. of the desider. To instruct, MBh. 1, 8033.<BR> --With आ आ, desider. To impart, to grant, Chr. 297, 19 = Rigv. i. 112, 19.<BR> --With उप उप, desider. To learn, MBh. 3, 1790.<BR> --Cf. Lat. queo (for quecjo), ne-queo (nequinont, for ne-quic + nont), conari; O.N. hagr, dexter, hagna, prodesse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्त|अशक्तं
अ- + शक्त अ- + शक्त, adj. powerless, Pañc. i. d. 362.<BR> II. शकित, Able, i. e. could; transfers its pass. signification to the infin. which it governs, e. g. न शकिता नेतुम्, Rām. 1, 44, 53 (She could not be led).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक शक,<BR> 1. m. pl. The name of a people, Man. 10, 44.<BR> 2. A particular caste.<BR> 3. An era, especially that of Śālivāhana, commencing seventy-six or seventy-eight years after the Christian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकच
शकच शकच, Rājat. 5, 176 (? perhaps to be corrected to शकज, A man of Śaka, i. e. Scythic extraction, or a proper name).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट शकट, probably for शक् + अत्र,<BR> I. m., f. टी, and n. A cart, Hit. i. d. 89, M.M. (n.); Pañc. 8, 15 (ता); Rām. 1, 33, 18 (टी); with प्राजापत्य, name of an asterism, Pañc. i. d. 239 (टा).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cart-load.<BR> 2. A Daitya slain by Kṛṣṇa.<BR> III. m. or n.<BR> 1. An implement for preparing grain, Man. 5, 117.<BR> 2. A form of marching an army, 7, 187.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीशकट|रोहिणीशकटः
रोहिणी- + शकट रोहिणी- + शकट, m. or n. an asterism, probably αϐγδε Tauri, Pañc. 50, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटार
शकटार शकटार, m.<BR> 1. A bird of prey (a vulture?), Hit. ii. d. 97.<BR> 2. and शकटाल शकटाल, A proper name, Kathās. 4, 104 (ल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका शकटिका, i. e. शकटी + क, f. A small cart.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृच्छकटिका
मृच्छकटिका मृच्छकटिका, i. e. मृद्-, f. the cart made of clay, the toy-cart, title of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् शकन्, see शकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल शकल (a form of शर्कर by [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a " target="_blank">Page0926-a + 42</a>] intermediate *शक्कर, and with ल् for र्, cf. शर्करा),<BR> I. m. and n. A part, a portion, a piece, Utt. Rāmac. 46, 19; Pañc. iii. d. 193 (194); 262, 25; a potsherd, Man. 6, 28.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Skin.<BR> 2. Bark.<BR> 3. The scales of a fish.<BR> 4. A kind of (black) pigment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0925-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् शकलिन्, i. e. शकल + इन्, m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार शकार, m. A silly brother-in-law of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन शक् + उन (or rather शक् + वन् + अ, cf. शकुन्त),<BR> I. m. A bird, Nal. 9, 12.<BR> II. n. An omen;<BR> a. auspicious, Lass. 43, 5;<BR> b. inauspicious, Pañc. 52, 11 (किं शकुनकारनं किं चित् संजातम्, Has something come to pass caused by a bird, or by an inauspicious omen, i. e. has there happened a misfortune?).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुन|अशकुनं|अशकुनः
अ- + शकुन अ- + शकुन, n. an inauspicious omen, Śiś. 9, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
शकुनि शक् + उनि (see the last),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bird, Pañc. iii. d. 140.<BR> 2. The Indian kite, Falco cheela.<BR> 3. A surname of the Aśvins, MBh. 1, 723.<BR> 4. A proper name. Indr. 3, 9.<BR> II. f. नी, A hensparrow.<BR> --Probably akin to O.N. haukr; Danish, hog; O.H.G. habuh; A.S. hafoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः|शकुन्तः
शकुन्त शक् + उन्त (or rather शक् + वन्त् + अ, cf. शकुन), m.<BR> 1. A bird, Pañc. i. d. 155.<BR> 2. The Indian vulture.<BR> 3. The blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुंतकः|शकुन्तकः
शकुन्तक शकुन्त + क, m., f. तिका, A bird, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला शकुन्त + ला, f. A proper name, Śāk. 3, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानशकुन्तला
अभिज्ञान- + शकुन्तला अभिज्ञान- + शकुन्तला, n. (suppl. नाटक, a drama), having as subject Śakuntalā, recognised by a token of remembrance, Śāk. 3, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः|शकुन्तिः
शकुन्ति शकुन्ति (cf. शकुन्त), m. A bird, Utt. Rāmac. 69, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुल|शकुलः
शकुल शकुल, m. A fish (cf. शकलिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्
शकृत् शकृत्, and सकृत् सकृत् (for original स्कृत्, from the old form of the vb. कॄ), n., the base of some cases is शकन्, Fæces, excrement, Man. 2, 182.<BR> --Cf. σκώρ, σκατός, σκέρ-βολος; A.S. scearn; perhaps Lat. stercus and cerda in su-cerda (rather to शृध्?), etc.; and Goth. spai-skuldrs, Spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्कर|शक्करः
शक्कर शक्कर, and शक्वर शक्वर, i. e. शक् + वन् + अ (with र् for न्),<BR> I. m. A bull.<BR> II. f. री,<BR> 1. A zone, a girdle.<BR> 2. A woman of impure caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति शक् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Strength, Pañc. i. d. 265; with loc., Bhartṛ. 2, 60 (आत्मदमने, in restraining or ruling one's self).<BR> 2. Power. Hit. pr. d. 31, M.M.<BR> 3. The active power of a deity personified as his wife (as गौरि of शिव, etc.), Kathās. 3, 62 (of the god of love); eight particular goddesses, ब्राह्मी, etc. cf. Wilson, Hind. Th. 2. ed. ii. 52, n. ad Mālat. 74, 5.<BR> 4. Signification, Bhāṣāp. 79.<BR> 5. Allaying opposition.<BR> 6. An iron spear or dart, MBh. 5, 5259; a sword, Mālat. 82, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्ति|अशक्तिः
अ- + शक्ति अ- + शक्ति, f. want of strength, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशक्ति
अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति, बहु-, m. proper names, Pañc. 3, 11. 12; 183, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरशक्ति
अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति, बहु-, m. proper names, Pañc. 3, 11. 12; 183, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रशक्ति
अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति, बहु-, m. proper names, Pañc. 3, 11. 12; 183, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशक्ति
अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति अनन्त-, अमर-, उग्र-, देव- + शक्ति, बहु-, m. proper names, Pañc. 3, 11. 12; 183, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशक्ति|आत्मशक्तिः
आत्मशक्ति आत्मशक्ति, i. e. आत्मन्-, f. one's own strength or power, Hit. pr. d. 31, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशक्ति
यथा- + शक्ति यथा- + शक्ति, adv. to the utmost of one's power, Hit. ii. d. 51; Lass. 59, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिशक्ति|रतिशक्तिः
रति- + शक्ति रति- + शक्ति, f. the faculty of enjoying love, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2077.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवशक्ति
शिव- + शक्ति शिव- + शक्ति, m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तितस्
शक्तितस् शक्ति + तस्, adv. According to power or ability, Pañc. 161, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिता
ऽशक्तिता -शक्ति + ता, in भोजन-, f. The faculty of enjoying food, Cāṇ. 40 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0926-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिधर|शक्तिधरः
शक्तिधर शक्ति-धर, m. A name of Skanda, the god of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिमन्त्|शक्तिमत्
शक्तिमन्त् शक्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Powerful, mighty, Pañc. iii. d. 14.<BR> 2. Able, ib. iii. d. 169.<BR> 3. Having gained a fortune or a competence, Man. 10, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तु|शक्तुः
शक्तु शक्तु, and सक्तु सक्तु, m. and n., according to some authorities only m. pl. (Pañc. 252, 10, with स्), The flour of barley and other grain first fried and then ground, Hit. 114, 22 (श्).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसक्तु
दधि- + सक्तु दधि- + सक्तु, pl. fried meal mixed with curds, MBh. 13, 5049.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नु|शक्नुः
शक्नु शक् + नु (cf. शच्), adj. Speaking civilly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्र|शक्रः
शक्र शक् + र, m.<BR> 1. Indra, Rām. 3, 54, 8.<BR> 2. A king(?), Rām. 3, 49, 41 (cf. Gorr. n.).<BR> 3. The name of two trees, Pentaptera arjuna and Nerium antidysentericum.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्र
अति- + शक्र अति- + शक्र, adj. exceeding Indra, Arj. 4, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ल|शक्लः
शक्ल शक् + ल (cf. शच्), adj. Affable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन् शक् + वन्,<BR> I. m. An elephant.<BR> II. f. वरी, A river. Cf. शक्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वर|शक्वरः
शक्वर शक्वर (cf. शक्कर),<BR> I. m. A bull.<BR> II. f. री.<BR> 1. A finger-ring.<BR> 2. A zone. Cf. the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क्|शंक्
शङ्क् शङ्क्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Rām. 2, 90, 15),<BR> 1. To hesitate, to be uncertain, Rām. 3, 49, 16.<BR> 2. To doubt, MBh. 3, 16512.<BR> 3. To think probable, to believe, MBh. 4, 97; to think, Vikr. d. 55.<BR> 4. To distrust, to suspect, MBh. 3, 2327.<BR> 5. To fear, Vikr. 66, 10; MBh. 3, 2274.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शङ्कित.<BR> 1. Suspicious, Pañc. 187, 4; alarmed, frightened, Rām. 3, 52, 48.<BR> 2. Being fearful of (with gen. and abl.), Pañc. 100, 9.<BR> 3. Doubtful, uncertain.<BR> 4. Weak. unsteady.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b " target="_blank">Page0927-b + 41</a>]<BR> --Caus. To frighten, Mālav. 44, 13.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति,<BR> 1. To suspect, Rām. 2, 52, 57.<BR> 2. To fear, Rām. 2, 22, 30.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To be uncertain, Man. 8, 96.<BR> 2. To doubt, Matsyop. 34. अभिशङ्कित,<BR> 1. Suspecting, Chr. 14, 26.<BR> 2. Afraid, Mālat. 143, 3.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To hesitate, Pañc. i. d. 437 (with ptcple. in the sense of an infin.).<BR> 2. To doubt. Śāk. 66, 19.<BR> 3. To think probable, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 2.<BR> 4. To suspect, to apprehend, Mālat. 69, 19; Man. 7, 183.<BR> 5. To fear, Utt. Rāmac. 62, 4.<BR> --With निस् निस्, निःशङ्कित (rather शङ्कित with निस्),<BR> 1. Not hesitating, Pañc. 217, 12.<BR> 2. Careless, ib. 161, 16.<BR> --With परि परि, To suspect, MBh. 3, 10356; with दोषेण, a crime or sin, Nal. 24, 26. परिशङ्कित,<BR> 1. Suspected, Chr. 54, 15.<BR> 2. Suspecting, Chr. 18, 36.<BR> 3. Fearful, Lass. 2. ed. 61, 32.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To doubt, MBh. 1, 2966.<BR> 2. To suspect, Śāk. d. 114.<BR> 3. To fear, Mālat. 70, 13; Pañc. ii. d. 178. अ-विशङ्कित, adj. Fearless, Vikr. 81, 11.<BR> --With निर्वि निस्-वि, निर्विशङ्कित (rather वि-शङ्कित with निस्), acc. ˚तम्, adv. Without hesitation, Hariv. 7335.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To suspect, MBh. 4, 568.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cunc + tari; A.S. hangian; Goth. and O.H.G. hugjan; Goth. hugs; A.S. hige, hyge, hogu, hygian, hyggan, hiegan, hogian; O.H.G. hugu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशङ्कित|नित्यशंकित
नित्य- + शङ्कित नित्य- + शङ्कित, adj. constantly suspicious, Hit. i. d. 24, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकर|शङ्कर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शंकर शंकर, i. e. शम्-कृ + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Causing happiness, Padmap. 2, 6.<BR> 2. Auspicious.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva, Hariv. 15408; Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 20.<BR> 2. A proper name, Lass. 2. ed. 87, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्का|शंका
शङ्का शङ्क् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Doubt, uncertainty, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a " target="_blank">Page0928-a + 44</a>] Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 13; Kir. 5, 42 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. का); error, 5, 38.<BR> 2. Presumption, Nal. 24, 3.<BR> 3. Hope, Bhartṛ. 3, 5.<BR> 4. Fear, Pañc. 238, 21; apprehension, Hit. i. d. 23, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्क|अशंक
अ-शङ्क अ-शङ्क, adj. without fear, regard, Hit. i. d. 80, M.M. ˚कम्, adv. courageously, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्क
निस्-शङ्क निस्-शङ्क, adj. 1. without hesitation, Pañc. 24, 13 (regardless). 2. fearless, Pañc. 123, 25. ˚कम्-, adv. without fear, Hit. ii. d. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशङ्क
वीत- + शङ्क वीत- + शङ्क, i. e. वि-इत-, adj. fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशङ्क
स- + शङ्क स- + शङ्क, adj. fearful, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0927-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्किन्|शंकिन्
शङ्किन् शङ्किन्, i. e. शङ्क्, and शङ्का, + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Fearful of, Rājat. 5, 144.<BR> 2. Suspecting, Hit. iv. d. 101.<BR> 3. Full of danger, Pañc. i. d. 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कु|शंकु|शंकुः|शङ्कुः
शङ्कु शङ्क् + उ, (partly शक् + उ, cf. शक्ति), m.<BR> 1. Fear.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. Kāma.<BR> 4. A demon.<BR> 5. Poison.<BR> 6. Sin.<BR> 7. A pin, Hit. iv. d. 69; a pale, a style, Man. 8, 271; a stake.<BR> 8. The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR> 9. A dart, Utt. Rāmac. 75, 12; a javelin, Pañc. 87, 12 (cf. Hiḍ. 2, 4); a weapon in general.<BR> 10. A goose.<BR> 11. An ant-hill.<BR> 12. A skate.<BR> 13. A number, ten billions.<BR> 14. A tree, Shorea robusta.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कु|त्रिशंकु|त्रिशङ्कुः
त्रि- + शङ्कु त्रि- + शङ्कु, m. the name of a king, Hariv. 730.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशङ्कु|दन्तशङ्कुः
दन्त- + शङ्कु दन्त- + शङ्कु, n. an instrument for drawing out teeth, Suśr. 1, 26, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहशङ्कु|लोहशंकु|लोहशङ्कुः
लोह- + शङ्कु लोह- + शङ्कु, m. 1. an iron pike. 2. a hell, Man. 4, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुर|शंकुर|शङ्कुरः
शङ्कुर शङ्क् + उर, adj. Formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुला|शंकुला
शङ्कुला शङ्कु + ला, f. A pair of scissors (cf. दन्त-शङ्कु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्ख|शंख|शंखं|शंखः|शङ्खः
शङ्ख शङ्ख,<BR> I. m. and n. The conch-shell used as a vessel for offering libations, and for blowing as a horn, Pañc. 20, 8.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A shell, Pañc. iv. d. 76; 158, 4.<BR> 2. A military drum.<BR> 3. The temple or temporal bone, Lass. 2. ed. 13, 13.<BR> 4. An elephant's cheek.<BR> 5. A large number, ten or a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b " target="_blank">Page0928-b + 41</a>] hundred billions.<BR> 6. One of Kuvera's treasures, Pañc. ii. d. 12.<BR> 7. A particular perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κόγχη, κόλχος, κόχλος, κάλχη.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशङ्ख|महाशंख|महाशङ्खः
महा- + शङ्ख महा- + शङ्ख, m. 1. the forehead. 2. a thousand millions. 3. one of Kuvera's treasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशङ्ख
स- + शङ्ख स- + शङ्ख, adj. with a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्याशङ्ख
संध्या- + शङ्ख संध्या- + शङ्ख, m. the conch proclaiming (by its sounding) the evening hour, Mālat. 41, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशङ्खा|स्थूलशंखा
स्थूल- + शङ्खा स्थूल- + शङ्ख, adj., f. खा, having a large vulva, Lass. Pentap. 65, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशङ्ख|हेमशंख|हेमशङ्खः
हेम- + शङ्ख हेम- + शङ्ख, m. Viṣṇu (cf. Pañc. 44, 15, sqq.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खक|शंखक|शंखकं|शङ्खकं|शंखकः|शङ्खकः
शङ्खक शङ्ख + क,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. The conch-shell.<BR> 2. The temples, Yājñ. 3, 93.<BR> 3. Pain in the temples and forehead.<BR> II. n. A bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खध्म|शंखध्म|शङ्खध्मः
शङ्खध्म शङ्ख-ध्म (vb. ध्मा), m. A shell-blower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिन्|शंखिन्
शङ्खिन् शङ्खिन्, i. e. शङ्ख + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Having a shell or shells.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The ocean.<BR> 2. A shell-blower.<BR> 3. A worker in shells.<BR> 4. Viṣṇu (cf. हेम-शङ्ख).<BR> III. f. इनी.<BR> 1. One of the four classes into which females are divided.<BR> 2. A female spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच्
† शच् शच्, i. 1, Ātm. To speak (cf. शक्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचि|शचिः
शचि and शची शच्की̆ (vb. शक्, cf. शक्र), f.<BR> 1. The wife of Indra, Rām. 3, 54, 26 (ई).<BR> 2. ची, Strength, Chr. 296, 8 = Rigv. i. 112, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शञ्च्|शंच्
शञ्च् शञ्च्, see श्वञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्
† शट् शट्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be diseased.<BR> 2. To divide.<BR> 3. To be dissolved.<BR> 4. To be low-spirited.<BR> 5. To go.<BR> --Cf. 2. शठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटा
शटा शटा, see सटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
† 1. शठ् शठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To deceive.<BR> 2. To kill or hurt.<BR> 3. To suffer pain.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To be lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
† 2. शठ् शठ्, शट् शट्, शल् शल्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a " target="_blank">Page0929-a + 41</a>] i. 10, Ātm. To praise, to flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0928-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
† 3. शठ् शठ्, श्वठ् श्वठ्, i. 10, शथय, श्वठय, Par.<BR> 1. To speak ill.<BR> 2. To speak well.<BR> 3. To be true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
† 4. शठ् शठ्, श्वठ् श्वठ्, श्वण्ठ् श्वण्ठ्, सठ् सठ्, स्वठ् स्वठ्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To finish, to adorn.<BR> 2. To leave unfinished or unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ शठ, probably akin to शत्रु, cf. शतेर, perhaps a form of *शत्र,<BR> I. adj. Wicked, dishonest, perfidious, Lass. 31, 17; Hit. ii. d. 115.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A rogue, a knave, Man. 7, 123.<BR> 2. A false husband or lover, Lass. 45, 5; Śṛṅgārat. 10; Mālav. d. 55 (read शठ).<BR> 3. An idler.<BR> 4. A blockhead.<BR> 5. A mediator.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशठ
अ- + शठ अ- + शठ, adj. honest, Man. 3, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशठ|दंतशठ|दन्तशठः
दन्त- + शठ दन्त- + शठ, m. common lime, Ferronia elephantum Corr., and Averrhoa carambola Lin., Suśr. 1, 157, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्
† शण् शण्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To give (cf. श्रण्).<BR> 2. To move(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
शण शण, n.<BR> 1. Hemp, MBh. 3, 16350.<BR> 2. Bengal San, a plant from which a kind of hemp is prepared, Crotalaria juncea.<BR> 3. (for *शर्ण, i. e. शॄ + न), An arrow.<BR> --Cf. κάνναϐις; O.H.G. hanaf; A.S. haenep (borrowed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणसूत्रमय
शणसूत्रमय शण-सूत्र + मय, adj., f. यी, Consisting of शण-threads, Man. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ठ|शंठः
शण्ठ शण्ठ, m. An eunuch (cf. शण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड्|शंड्
† शण्ड् शण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To disease.<BR> 2. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड|शंड|शण्डं|शंडः|शण्डः
शण्ड शण्ड,<BR> I. m. n. A collection of lotus flowers.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An eunuch. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b " target="_blank">Page0929-b + 45</a>]<BR> 2. An impotent man.<BR> 3. A bull at liberty (cf. शण्ठ and शण्ढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ढ|शंढ|शंढः|शण्ढः
शण्ढ शण्ढ, m.<BR> 1. An eunuch.<BR> 2. An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR> 3. A bull at liberty (cf. the last, षण्ड, and षण्ढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत|शतं
शत शत, numeral, n. (also m., Nal. 15, 6, शतं शतास्, ten thousand), A hundred, Chr. 28, 20 (pl.); nom. in the sense of an instr. (i. e. indecl.), Chr. 287, 7 = Rigv. i. 48, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. centum; ἑ-κατόν (ἑν-κατόν); Goth. and A.S. hund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्धशत
अध्यर्ध- + शत अध्यर्ध- + शत, i. e. अधि-अर्ध-,<BR> I. n. a hundred and fifty.<BR> II. adj. consisting of a hundred and fifty, MBh. 1, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धशत
अर्ध- + शत अर्ध- + शत, n. a hundred and fifty, Man. 8, 331.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टशत
अष्टशत अष्टशत, i. e. अष्टन्-, n. eight hundred, Yājñ. 1, 302.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशत
एक- + शत एक- + शत, n. a hundred and one; with गवाम्, a hundred cows and one bull, Man. 11, 129 (cf. 127).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावच्छत
तावच्छत तावच्छत, i. e. तावन्त्-, adj., f. ती, containing so many hundreds, Man. 1, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशत
त्रि- + शत त्रि- + शत,<BR> I. n. three hundred, Rām. 1, 13, 31 Gorr.<BR> II. adj. three hundredth, MBh. 3, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशत
दशशत दशशत, i. e. दशन्-, n., and f. ती, a thousand, MBh. 3, 2658 (त); Rājat. 5, 71 (ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरश्मिशत
दश-रश्मि- + शत दश-रश्मि- + शत, i. e. दशन्-, adj. (having a thousand rays), epithet of the sun, Ragh. 8, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशत
द्वि- + शत द्वि- + शत,<BR> I. n. 1. two hundred. 2. hundred and two.<BR> II. adj. 1. amounting to two hundred, Man. 8, 257. 2. two hundredth, MBh. i. adhy. 200, sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशत|पंचशत
पञ्चशत पञ्चशत, i. e. पञ्चन्-,<BR> I. n., and f. ती, five hundred, Man. 8, 384 (त); Kathās. 44, 77 (ती).<BR> II. adj. 1. five hundred, MBh. 3, 15723. 2. amounting to five hundred, Yājñ. 2, 301. 3. paying an amercement of five hundred, Man. 8, 376.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परःशत परःशत, i. e. परस्-, adj., f. ता, more than a hundred, MBh. 6, 4267.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक|शतकः
शतक शत + क,<BR> I. adj. Hundred.<BR> II. (m.?), n. A century, a collection of a hundred stanzas, Bhartṛ. title.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0929-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतखण्डमय
शतखण्डमय शत-खण्ड + मय, adj. Consisting of a hundred pieces, Bhartṛ. 3, 16 (cf. खण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतघ्नी
शतघ्नी शतघ्नी, i. e. शत-हन् + ई, f.<BR> 1. A kind of weapon, Arj. 6, 16.<BR> 2. A female scorpion.<BR> 3. A disease of the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततम|शततमः
शततम शत + तम, ord. num., f. मी, Hundredth, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशततम
द्वि- + शततम द्वि- + शततम, adj. two hundredth, Hariv. adhy. 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशततम
त्रि- + शततम त्रि- + शततम, adj. 1. three hundredth, Hariv. adhy. 300. 2. hundred and third, Rām. ii. adhy. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःशततम
चतुःशततम चतुःशततम, i. e. चतुर्-, adj. hundred and fourth, Rām. ii. adhy. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशततम
पञ्चशततम पञ्चशततम, i. e. पञ्चन्-, adj. hundred and fifth, Rām. ii. adhy. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशततम
नवशततम नवशततम, i. e. नवन्-, adj. hundred and ninth, Rām. vi. adhy. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाविंशतिशततम
द्वाविंशति- + शततम द्वाविंशति- + शततम, i. e. द्वि-विंशति-, adj. hundred and twenty-second, Rām. ii. adhy. 122 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतद्रु|शतद्रुः
शतद्रु शत-द्रु, f. The name of a river, the Setlej, MBh. 1, 6753.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधा
शतधा शत + धा, adv.<BR> 1. In a hundred ways, hundred-fold, Man. 12, 115.<BR> 2. In a hundred pieces, Pañc. 94, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभिषज्
शतभिषज् शत-भिषज्, and शतभिषा शतभिषा (a mutilation of भिषज्), f. A lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमान|शतमानः
शतमान शत-मान, m. and n.<BR> 1. A पल of silver, Man. 8, 137 (m.).<BR> 2. A measure so termed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतयोजनवत्
शतयोजनवत् शत-योजन + वत्, adv. As if a hundred योजनस् large, Pañc. i. d. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशस्
शतशस् शत + शस्, adv. By hundreds, a hundred-fold, Chr. 30, 8; 36, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशाखत्व
शतशाखत्व शत-शाख + त्व (cf. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b " target="_blank">Page0930-b + 41</a>] शाखा), n. Condition of having many branches, of being much increased, Rājat. 5, 376.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसंघशस्
शतसंघशस् शत-संघ + शस्, adv. By hundreds, Arj. 10, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिन्
शतिन् शतिन्, i. e. शत + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Consisting of hundreds, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR> II. m. One who is possessed of a hundred, Pañc. v. d. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेर|शतेरः
शतेर शतेर (cf. शत्रु), m.<BR> 1. An enemy.<BR> 2. Injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्त्रि
शत्त्रि शत्त्रि, m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रु|शत्रुः
शत्रु शत्रु (rather शत्त्रु शत्त्रु, i. e. probably शद् or शत्, for शातय, Caus. of शद्, + त्रु, cf. Goth. hats; A.S. hate, héte; perhaps Lat. hod in odisse, hestis, and below), m. An enemy, a foe, Pañc. i. d. 131.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἔχθος, ἐχθρός, ὀχθέω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशत्रु|इन्द्रशत्रुः
इन्द्र- + शत्रु इन्द्र- + शत्रु, m. Prahlāda, Ragh. 7, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चशत्रु
क्रौञ्च- + शत्रु क्रौञ्च- + शत्रु, m. the god of war, Mṛcch. 173, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशत्रु|देवशत्रुः
देव- + शत्रु देव- + शत्रु, m. 1. an Asura, MBh. 7, 6296. 2. a Rākṣasa, Rām. 6, 36, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशत्रु|बहुशत्रुः
बहु- + शत्रु बहु- + शत्रु, adj. having many enemies, Kathās. 4, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधशत्रु|विबुधशत्रुः
विबुध- + शत्रु विबुध- + शत्रु, m. a demon, Vikr. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रशत्रु
वृत्र- + शत्रु वृत्र- + शत्रु, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुंसह
शत्रुंसह शत्रुंसह, i. e. शत्रु + म्-सह् + अ, adj. Bearing, or patient with an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघ्न|शत्रुघ्नः
शत्रुघ्न शत्रु-घ्न,<BR> I. adj. Killing a foe.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 31, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुंजय|शत्रुञ्जय|शत्रुंजयः|शत्रुञ्जयः
शत्रुंजय शत्रुंजय, i. e. शत्रु + म्-जि + अ,<BR> I. adj. Subduing an enemy.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A proper name, Draup. 2, 11.<BR> 2. An elephant.<BR> 3. The name of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुतस्
शत्रुतस् शत्रु + तस्, adv. From any enemy, Nal. 14, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुता
शत्रुता शत्रु + ता, f., and शत्रुत्व [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a " target="_blank">Page0931-a + 41</a>] शत्रु + त्व, n. Enmity, hostility, Pañc. ii. d. 32; Cāṇ. 19 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0930-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्वरी
शत्वरी शत्वरी, i. e. शम् + त्वन् + ई (cf. शमनी, s. v. शमन, र् for न्), f. The night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्
शद् शद् substitutes in the pres., imperf. imperat. and potent. the pass. of शी, viz. शीय; in the remaining forms, Par. To fall, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 77 (शीय).<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. शातय (probably a denomin., perhaps from an anomal. ptcple. of the pf. pass. शात for शत्त, cf. the substitution of a vowel long by nature for one long by position, and vice versā in the Prākṛ. languages), To fell, to throw down, Rām. 1, 66, 10. शातित, Cut off, Rām. 1, 66, 12, Seramp.<BR> II. शादय, To drive, Pāṇ. vii. 3, 42.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र, Caus. शातय, To break off, MBh. 1, 5561.<BR> --With वि वि, Caus. शातय, To break to pieces, MBh. 3, 11971.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. शातय, The same, MBh. 3, 865.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cadere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद|शदः
शद शद् + अ, also (but wrongly) सद सद, m. Any edible vegetable product, as fruits, Man. 8, 151; 241 (with स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रि|शद्रिः
शद्रि शद् + रि,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. An elephant.<BR> 3. Arjuna.<BR> II. f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस् शनकैस्, i. e. शन + क, instr. pl. (cf. शनैस्), adv.<BR> 1. By degrees, gradually, Man. 7, 172.<BR> 2. In every case that arises, Man. 7, 116.<BR> 3. Mildly, Śiś. 9, 26; Chr. 41, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनि|शनिः
शनि शनि (cf. शनैस्), and शनैश्चर शनैश्चर, i. e. शनैस्-चर, m. The planet Saturn, Pañc. 50, 19 (शनैश्चर); Rām. 2, 52, 15 (शनैश्चर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस् शनैस् (probably for शम्नैस्, instr. pl. of an old ptcple. pf. pass. of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b " target="_blank">Page0931-b + 42</a>] शम्), adv. (properly ‘With intervals of quiet’).<BR> 1. Hesitating, slowly, Vikr. 71, 18; stealthily, Vikr. d. 56.<BR> 2. Mildly, Chr. 32, 27.<BR> 3. Successively, by little and little, Rājat. 5, 470; at will, independently.<BR> 4. Doubled, शनैः-शनैस्, adv. By little and little, Man. 3, 233; successively, Pañc. 212, 1; step by step, 35, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंताति
शंताति शंताति, i. e. शम् + ताटि, f. Happiness, yielding bliss, Chr. 297, 20 = Rigv. i. 112, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् शप्, i. 1 and 4, Par. Ātm. (the original signification was probably ‘To cry aloud’),<BR> 1. To execrate, to curse. Man. 3, 58.<BR> 2. With the dat., To revile, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 33.<BR> 3. To swear, Man. 8, 110.<BR> 4. To assure by an oath, Rām. 2, 11, 8.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to swear, Man. 8, 113 (with the instr. of the object by which one is sworn).<BR> 2. To conjure; शपितासि जीवितेन, You are conjured by the life of, Mālat. 129, 10.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To execrate, Rām. 2, 41, 3.<BR> --With परि परि, The same, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 33.<BR> --Cf. probably κόμπος; cf. the frequent. शंशप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप|शपः
शप शप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. An imprecation.<BR> 2. An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथ|शपथः
शपथ शप् + अथ, m.<BR> 1. An imprecation, curse, Pañc. 62, 2; cursing.<BR> 2. An oath, asseveration by oath or ordeal, Man. 8, 109; 190; Pañc. i. d. 130.<BR> 3. Conjuration, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपन|शपनं
शपन शप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A curse.<BR> 2. An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफ|शफं|शफः
शफ शफ, m. and n.<BR> 1. A hoof in general, Man. 10, 89.<BR> 2. A horse's hoof.<BR> 3. The root of a tree.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. huof; A.S. hóf, The hoof of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशफ|एकशफः
एक- + शफ एक- + शफ, adj. and sbst. any animal whose hoof is not cloven, Man. 10, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशफ|द्विशफः
द्वि- + शफ द्वि- + शफ, adj. and sbst. any cloven-footed animal, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a " target="_blank">Page0932-a + 42</a>] Man. 11, 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशफ|मुखशफः
मुख- + शफ मुख- + शफ, adj. foulmouthed, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0931-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफर|शफरः
शफर शफ + र, and सफर सफर, m., and f. री, A small fish, Cyprinus Sophore, Pañc. ii. d. 87 (र); Bhartṛ. 3, 94 (री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबल|शबलः
शबल शबल = शवल, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द्
शब्द् शब्द्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from शब्द), शब्दय and शब्दापय, Par.<BR> 1. To sound, Śiś. 11, 47; to bray, Pañc. 224, 9.<BR> 2. To call, MBh. 3, 14400.<BR> 3. To address, Rām. 2, 59, 7 (शब्दापय).<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. शब्दित, n. Braying (of an ass), Pañc. 249, 6.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To declare, Man. 6, 82.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To say, MBh. 1, 3215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द शब्द, i. e. शप्-द (vb. दा), m.<BR> 1. Sound, Pañc. 129, 15; noise, Pañc. 123, 24.<BR> 2. A word, Vikr. d. 1.<BR> 3. Grammar, Pañc. 4, 17; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशब्द|जयशब्दः
जय- + शब्द जय- + शब्द, m. 1. a shout of victory. 2. the exclamation जय, victory, Vikr. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालशब्द
ताल- + शब्द ताल- + शब्द, m. 1. noise produced by falling cocoanuts, Hariv. 3715. 2. noise produced by clapping the hands, applause, ib. 4111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्द|निःशब्दः
निःशब्द निःशब्द, i. e. निस्-, adj.<BR> I. adj. soundless, noiseless, Megh. 112 (without speaking); Rām. 5, 3, 47.<BR> II. n. silence, Rām. 4, 59, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशब्द
स-शब्द स-शब्द, adj. proclaimed, Rājat. 5, 361. ˚दम्, adv. with loud noise, Bhartṛ. 2, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशब्द
साधु- + शब्द साधु- + शब्द, m. a cry of ‘Good.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दज
शब्दज शब्द-ज, adj. Produced by words, by verbal communication, Bhāṣāp. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन शब्द् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Sounding, sonorous.<BR> II. n. Uttering sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाय
शब्दाय शब्दाय, a denomin. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-b " target="_blank">Page0932-b + 45</a>] derived from शब्द with य, Ātm. To sound, to cry, Pañc. 254, 21; to bray, Pañc. 249, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
1. शम् शम्, i. 4, शाम्य, Par. (the original signification is ‘To get tired’),<BR> 1. To cease, Man. 2, 94.<BR> 2. To grow calm, to be appeased, MBh. 2, 1936; to grow satisfied and pacified, Rājat. 5, 400.<BR> 3. To be calm, undisturbed, MBh. 1, 6362.<BR> 4. To sacrifice, Chr. 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12; Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 86, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शान्त.<BR> 1. Hushed, stilled (as wind).<BR> 2. Ceased, Hit. 80, 21; extinguished, Kir. 17, 16.<BR> 3. Allayed, alleviated.<BR> 4. Calm, undisturbed, Utt. Rāmac. 7, 7; tranquil, pacified, free from passions, Pañc. i. d. 181; content, Hit. i. d. 142, M.M.<BR> 5. Meek, humble, Chr. 48, 10.<BR> 6. Purified, cleansed.<BR> 7. Repelled, MBh. 1, 212.<BR> 8. ˚तम्, adv.<BR> a. Enough, Utt. Rāmac. 71, 2.<BR> b. A prohibitive word, implying negation, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 1 (it must not befall), aversion, disgust, fie, for shame, heaven forbid, Śāk. 67, 13; Daśak. in Chr. 200, 13; hush, Utt. Rāmac. 10, 1.<BR> 9. Killed, MBh. 1, 7523. m. An ascetic. n. Appeasing, pacifying. f. ता, A proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 103, 3; 173, 9.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10,<BR> I. शमय.<BR> 1. To cause to cease, to extinguish, Megh. 54; Hit. i. d. 87, M.M.<BR> 2. To tame, Vikr. d. 156; to appease, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 6.<BR> 3. To remove. MBh. 5, 238; to avert, Śāk. 7, 16.<BR> 4. To subdue, MBh. 3, 14620.<BR> 5. To desist, Johns. Sel. 48, 84.<BR> II. शामय, Ātm. To look at or inspect.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप,<BR> 1. To cease, MBh. 4, 1775.<BR> 2. To grow quiet, MBh. 3, 1008.<BR> --Caus. शामय,<BR> 1. To allay, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 16; 17.<BR> 2. To kill, MBh. 3, 8541.<BR> --With अभ्युप अभि-उप, अभ्युपशान्त, Appeased, Ṛt. 1, 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-a " target="_blank">Page0933-a + 42</a>]<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To see, MBh. 2, 1740.<BR> 2. To hear, Rām. 2, 44, 25. निशान्त, Quiet, patient. n. A house, a dwelling, Ragh. 16, 40.<BR> --Caus. शामय,<BR> 1. To see, Rām. 1, 2, 6.<BR> 2. To hear, 2, 57, 21.<BR> --With अभिनि अभि-नि, Caus. शामय, To perceive, Daśak. 201, 14.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To hear, MBh. 3, 1878.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To hear, MBh. 2, 1658.<BR> --Caus. शामय, To summon, Chr. 52, 10.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. शमय, To allay, Gīt. 7, 20.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To cease, Rām. 2, 40, 33; to fade, Man. 4, 186.<BR> 2. To be restrained, Pañc. i. d. 357; to become extinguished, Pañc. iii. d. 54.<BR> 3. To be appeased, soothed, Chr. 22, 14; Pañc. i. d. 315.<BR> 4. To grow calm, MBh. 2, 1941.<BR> 5. To heal, Pañc. 253, 23. प्रशान्त,<BR> 1. Ceased, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 16 (withdrawn).<BR> 2. Dead, Rājat. 5, 21.<BR> 3. Calmed, tranquillised, Nal. 26, 35; Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 21.<BR> 4. Tamed, Lass. 53, 15.<BR> 5. Relieved.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. शमय.<BR> 1. To allay, MBh. 2, 12978; to soothe, Man. 8, 391.<BR> 2. To extinguish, MBh. 1, 8156.<BR> 3. To kill, MBh. 2, 2031.<BR> II. शामय, To conquer, MBh. 3, 12196.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संशान्त, Extinguished, Rām. 2, 66, 1.<BR> --Caus. शमय, To allay, Rām. 2, 98, 1; to settle, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR> --Cf. κάμνω (cf. ved. शम्, ii. 9, शम्ना), σιδηρο-κμής, κημός (cf. शम्या); O.H.G. chamo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0932-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
2. शम् शम्,<BR> I. (sbst.), Work, Chr. 293, 5 = Rigv. i. 87, 5.<BR> II. indecl.<BR> 1. Happy, happily, auspiciously.<BR> 2. Hail, happiness, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 34; 8, 3, 23; Nalod. 3, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम|शमः
शम शम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rest, quiet, Śāk. d. 96; tranquillity.<BR> 2. Disregarding [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b " target="_blank">Page0933-b + 40</a>] the objects of sense, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 19.<BR> 3. Quiet of mind, the absence of passion, Pañc. i. d. 181.<BR> 4. Final happiness.<BR> 5. Cure, Utt. Rāmac. 144, 13; convalescence.<BR> 6. The hand.<BR> 7. Abuse, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमक|शमकः
शमक शम् + अक, adj. sbst. Pacifying, a pacifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथ|शमथः
शमथ शम् + अथ, m.<BR> 1. Quiet, tranquillity of mind, absence of passion.<BR> 2. A counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन शम् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Calmness.<BR> 2. End; with या, To be destroyed, Pañc. iii. 31, v. r. (cf. my translation and Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1868).<BR> 3. Immolation.<BR> 4. Hurt, injury.<BR> 5. Abuse, malediction.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An antelope,<BR> 2. Yama.<BR> III. f. नी, The night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमल|शमलं
शमल शमल, n. Impurity, Bhāg. P. 2, 8, 5; calamity, 1, 13, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमि|शमिः
शमि and मी शमी̆, f.<BR> I. A legume or pod.<BR> II. मी.<BR> 1. A tree, Acacia Suma Roxb., Pañc. 94, 1; Ragh. 3, 9.<BR> 2. A shrub, Serratula anthelmintica.<BR> III. A large stick, Man. 8, 237 (Sch.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशमी
महा-शमी महा-शमी, f. a large Acacia Suma, Pañc. 97, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन् शमिन्, i. e. शम + इन्, adj. Tranquil, tranquillised, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पा|शंपा
शम्पा शम्पा, f. Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब्|शंब्
शम्ब् शम्ब्, see शर्ब् and सम्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शम्बर शम्बर, and सम्बर सम्बर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a demon, Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. A sort of deer.<BR> 4. A fish.<BR> 5. War.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. A religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलं|शंबलः|शम्बलः
शम्बल शम्बल,<BR> I. (m. and) n.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a " target="_blank">Page0934-a + 41</a>] Stock for travelling expenses.<BR> 2. A bank, a shore.<BR> 3. Envy.<BR> II. f. ली, A procuress (cf. सम्बल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0933-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बु|शंबु|शंबुः|शम्बुः
शम्बु शम्बु (cf. the next), m. A bivalve shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बूक|शंबूक|शंबूकः|शम्बूकः
शम्बूक शम्बूक (borrowed from σαμϐύκη),<BR> I. m. (and f. का), A bivalve shell.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A conch-shell.<BR> 2. A snail.<BR> 3. The edge of the frontal protuberance of an elephant.<BR> 4. The name of a Daitya.<BR> 5. A proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भु|शंभु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शम्भु शम्-भु (vb. भू), m.<BR> 1. Śiva, Pañc. i. d. 175.<BR> 2. Brahman.<BR> 3. A sage man.<BR> 4. A सिद्ध, a demi-divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्या
शम्या शम् + या, f.<BR> 1. The pin of a yoke, Kātyāyana S. in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. xxxvii.<BR> 2. A sacrificial vessel, ib.<BR> 3. A staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्व
शम्व शम्व, n. The iron end of a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय|शयः
शय शय, i. e. शी + अ,<BR> I. adj. Asleep, sleeping.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Sleep.<BR> 2. A couch.<BR> 3. A snake, boa-constrictor.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ὀρέσ-κοιος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहाशय|गुहाशयः
गुहा- + शय गुहा- + शय,<BR> I. adj. 1. reposing in the heart, Bhāg. P. 3, 28, 19. 2. haunting caves, Suśr. 1, 200, 7.<BR> II. m. 1. a tiger. 2. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाशय
दिवा- + शय दिवा- + शय, adj. sleeping by day, Ragh. 19, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशय
नित्य- + शय नित्य- + शय, adj. sleeping always, MBh. 3, 10415.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयथ|शयथः
शयथ शयथ, i. e. शी + अथ,<BR> I. adj. Sleepy.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Death.<BR> 2. A snake, boa-constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयन|शयनं
शयन शयन, i. e. शी + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sleeping, reposing, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 1; sleep, Hit. pr. d. 28, M.M.<BR> 2. A bed, a couch, Vikr. d. 51 (कुसुम-, of flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयानक|शयानकः
शयानक शयान + क (vb. शी), m. The boa-constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयालु|शयालुः
शयालु शयालु, शय + आलु,<BR> I. adj. Sleepy.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A snake, boa-constrictor.<BR> 2. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयिन्
ऽशयिन् -शयिन्, i. e. शी + इन्, adj. Reposing, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयु|शयुः
शयु शयु, i. e. शी + उ, m.<BR> 1. A snake, boa-constrictor.<BR> 2. A proper name, Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. i. 112, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुन|शयुनः
शयुन शयुन (see the last), m. The boa-constrictor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्या
शय्या शय्या, i. e. शी + या, f. A bed, a couch, Pañc. 138, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःशय्य
अ-धःशय्य अ-धःशय्य, i. e. अधस्-,<BR> I. adj. sleeping on the ground, Rām. 5, 66, 13.<BR> II. f. या, sleeping on a low bed, Man. 2, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भशय्या
गर्भ- + शय्या गर्भ- + शय्या, f. the womb, MBh. 12, 6758.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्शय्या
पृथक्- + शय्या पृथक्- + शय्या, f. sleeping apart, Hit. ii. d. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशय्या
भू- + शय्या भू- + शय्या, f. lying on the ground, Pañc. i. d. 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय्या
महा- + शय्या महा- + शय्या, f. a throne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरशय्या
वीर- + शय्या वीर- + शय्या, f. a certain posture, Lass. 2. ed. 70, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्यापालत्व
शय्यापालत्व शय्या-पाल + त्व, n. The office of guarding the bed (of a king), Pañc. 63, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर|शरं|शरः
शर शर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A sort of reed, Saccharum sara, Man. 8, 247; a reed, Pañc. 140, 25.<BR> 2. An arrow (i. e. शॄ + अ), Pañc. 224, 11.<BR> 3. The cream of slightly curdled milk, Mālav. d. 43 (cream, cf. सर).<BR> II. n. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्मशर|अयुग्मशरः
अ-युग्म- + शर अ-युग्म- + शर (having an odd number of arrows), m. Kāmadeva, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमशर|कुसुमशरः
कुसुम- + शर कुसुम- + शर (having flowers instead of arrows), m. epithet of Kāma, Kathās. 26, 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशर|पंचशर|पञ्चशरः
पञ्चशर पञ्चशर, i. e. पञ्चन्- (having five arrows), m. Kāma, Prab. 72, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशर|पुष्पशरः
पुष्प- + शर पुष्प- + शर, m. Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशर
स- + शर स- + शर, adj. furnished with arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिशर|हरिशरः
हरि- + शर हरि- + शर, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरज|शरजं|शरजः
शरज शर-ज, n. Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरट|शरटः
शरट शरट, see सरट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण|शरणं
शरण शरण, n.<BR> I. (akin to श्रि),<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a " target="_blank">Page0935-a + 41</a>] A house, Pañc. i. d. 69; habitation, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 26.<BR> 2. Refuge, Hit. i. d. 189, M.M.; protection, Pañc. 90, 5; 141, 11; 175, 12; help, Vikr. 19, 17; a protector.<BR> II. (vb. श्री + अन), Killing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरण
अ- + शरण अ- + शरण, adj. without a refuge, helpless, Utt. Rāmac. 74, 10; Hit. 90, 1, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरणीकृत
अशरणी-कृत अशरणी-कृत, made helpless, Pañc. i. d. 241.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशरण
अग्नि- + शरण अग्नि- + शरण, n. the sanctuary where the sacred fire is kept, Vikr. 35, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0934-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणि|शरणिः
शरणि शरणि (akin to श्रि), f.<BR> 1. A row, a line.<BR> 2. A road, a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
शरण्य शरण्य, i. e. शरण + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Needing protection, Lass. 2. ed. 90, 50; helpless, poor, miserable.<BR> 2. Yielding protection, helping, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 3; Sāv. 1, 2; Chr. 17, 25.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A house.<BR> 2. Refuge, protection, a protector.<BR> 3. (i. e. शॄ + अन + य), Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्
शरद् शरद्, and शरदा शरदा (probably from शॄ), f.<BR> 1. The autumn, Pañc. v. d. 42 (रद्).<BR> 2. A year, Utt. Rāmac. 11, 8 (रद्).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतशरद्
परिणत-शरद् परिणत-शरद्, i. e. परि-नत- (vb. नम्), f. the latter part of autumn, Megh. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदिज|शरदिजं
शरदिज शरद् + इ-ज, adj. Produced in autumn, Utt. Rāmac. 3, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्वन्त्|शरद्वत्
शरद्वन्त् शरद् + वन्त्, m. A proper name, Johns. Sel. 59, 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरधि|शरधिः
शरधि शरधि, i. e. शर-धा (cf. निधि), m. A quiver, Vikr. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरन्मेघवत्
शरन्मेघवत् शरन्मेघवत्, i. e. शरद्-मेघ + वत्, adv. Like clouds of autumn, Hit. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभ|शरभः
शरभ शरभ (cf. करभ), m.<BR> 1. A fabulous animal with eight legs, stronger than a lion, Megh. 55.<BR> 2. A young elephant.<BR> 3. A camel.<BR> 4. A grasshopper (cf. शलभ).<BR> 5. A locust, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b " target="_blank">Page0935-b + 37</a>] Ṛt. 1, 23.<BR> --Cf. perhaps κάραϐος; A.S. crabba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरमय|शरमयं
शरमय शर + मय, adj., f. यी, Made or consisting of शर grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयु|शरयुः
शरयु and यू शर + यू̆ (better सरयू̆, q. cf.), f. The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरल|शरलः
शरल शरल (cf. सरल),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Upright, Pañc. iii. d. 69.<BR> 2. Fraudulent(?).<BR> II. m. A sort of pine, Rām. 5, 17, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवणोद्भव|शरवणोद्भवः
शरवणोद्भव शरवणोद्भव, and शरवणभव शरवणभव, i. e. शर-वन-उद्-भू + अ, or -वन-भव, m. A name of the god of war, Megh. 46 (˚वणभ्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवाणि|शरवाणिः
शरवाणि शरवाणि, m.<BR> 1. The head of an arrow.<BR> 2. The maker of arrows.<BR> 3. A foot-soldier (probably an anomal. derivation from शर + वन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्य|शरव्यं
शरव्य शर + व्य (or शरु + य?), n. A butt, a mark for arrows, Śāk. d. 156; aim, Ragh. 11, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराटि|शराटिः
शराटि शराटि, शराडि शराडि, शराति शराति, शरारि शरारि, and शरालि शरालि, f. A bird, Turdus ginginianus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराय
शराय शराय, a denomin. derived from शर with य, Ātm. To become an arrow, Śṛṅgārat. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारि|शरारिः
शरारि शरारि, शरालि शरालि, see शराटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु शरारु (vb. शॄ), adj. Hurtful, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराव|शरावं|शरावः
शराव शराव, m. and n. (ŚKD.),<BR> 1. A lid, a cover.<BR> 2. A shallow cup or dish, Hit. 114, 22; Pañc. 174, 14; Man. 6, 56; a tray, Vikr. 45, 13; a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a " target="_blank">Page0936-a + 43</a>] vessel (figurat. निष्ठीवन-, A spitting box), Bhartṛ. 1, 91.<BR> 3. A measure equal to two कुडवस्.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुशराव
शक्तु- + शराव सक्तु- + शराव, m. a pot full of flour of barley, Hit. 115, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0935-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरासन|शरासनं
शरासन शरासन, i. e. शर-असन, n.<BR> 1. Shooting arrows.<BR> 2. A bow, Vikr. d. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरि
शरि शरि, i. e. शॄ + ई, adj. Hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरिमन्
शरिमन् and शरीमन् शरी̆मन्, m. Bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीर|शरीरं
शरीर शरीर (vb. शॄ), n.<BR> 1. The body, Pañc. iii. d. 96.<BR> 2. Life, Hit. iii. d. 103.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. perhaps A.S. hold, cadaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीर|अशरीरः
अ- + शरीर अ- + शरीर, m. Kāma, Śiś. 9, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गशरीर|लिंगशरीर
लिङ्ग- + शरीर लिङ्ग- + शरीर, n. the primary body, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषशरीर
शेष- + शरीर शेष- + शरीर, n. the remaining body, i. e. all the other parts of the body, Pañc. 38, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशरीर
सूक्ष्म- + शरीर सूक्ष्म- + शरीर, n. atom-like body, a Vedāntic term, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरज|शरीरजः
शरीरज शरीर-ज,<BR> I. adj. Produced by the body.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son.<BR> 2. Disease.<BR> 3. Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरिन्
शरीरिन् शरीरिन्, i. e. शरीर + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. रिणी.<BR> 1. Embodied, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 12.<BR> 2. Living, Chr. 20, 20 (नहि वाणा मयोत्सृष्टाः सज्जन्ति शरीरिणां कायेषु, For the arrows which I have shot do not stick in the bodies of living beings, i. e. all<BR> I. hit with my arrows must die).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A sentient being, Rājat. 5, 20; Pañc. iii. d. 90; a man, Pañc. ii. d. 107.<BR> 2. An embodied spirit, Man. 1, 53; 6, 64.<BR> 3. The soul, Bhag. 2, 18; Bhāṣāp. 26.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरिन्
अ- + शरीरिन् अ- + शरीरिन्, adj. incorporeal, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरु|शरुः
शरु शरु, i. e. शॄ + उ (or rather शर् + वन्, cf. κεραυν + ός), m.<BR> 1. An arrow.<BR> 2. The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR> 3. Any weapon.<BR> 4. Passion, anger.<BR> --Cf. Goth. hairus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करा
शर्करा शर्करा (probably from vb. शॄ, but cf. कर्कर), f.<BR> 1. A potsherd.<BR> 2. Gravel.<BR> 3. Stone, Rājat. 5, 432.<BR> 4. A part.<BR> 5. A soil abounding in stony fragments.<BR> 6. Clayed or candied sugar, Pañc. i. d. 423; 185, 21; Lass. 79, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. calculus, calx; κρόκη, κροκάλη, κάχληξ, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडशर्करा|गुडशर्क्करा
गुड- + शर्करा गुड- + शर्करा, f. sugar, Suśr. 2, 457, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशर्कर
निःशर्कर निःशर्कर, i. e. निस्-, adj. free from stones, Rām. 1, 2, 6 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिशङ्खशर्कर
मणि-शङ्ख-शर्कर मणि-शङ्ख-शर्कर, adj. having shells and gravel consisting of jewels, Rām. 2, 63, 36, ed. Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्तुहिनशर्कर
वृहत्-तुहिनशर्कर वृहत्-तुहिनशर्कर, i. e. वृहन्त्-तुहिन-, adj. full of great pieces of ice, Rājat. 3, 362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करावन्त्|शर्करावत्
शर्करावन्त् शर्करा + वन्त्, and शर्करिल शर्करिल, i. e. शर्करा + इल, adj., f. वती, ला, Full of stony particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ध|शर्द्धः|शर्धः
शर्ध शर्ध, i. e. शृध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A fart.<BR> 2. A troop, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. 2, 64, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्धंजह|शर्धञ्जह|शर्द्धंजहः|शर्धंजहः
शर्धंजह शर्धंजह, i. e. शर्ध + म्-जह (the latter is a mutilation of जहत्, the ptcple. pres. of हा), m. Any leguminous pulse (causing flatulence), as beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ब्|शर्ब्ब्
† शर्ब् शर्ब्, i. 1, Par.<BR> I. To kill.<BR> II. and शम्ब् शम्ब्, To go (cf. शर्व्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मन्|शर्म्मन्
शर्मन् शर्मन् (vb. श्रि, cf. शरण), n.<BR> 1. Blessing, Chr. 292, 12 = Rigv. i. 85, 12 (ved. शर्म for शर्माणि).<BR> 2. Happiness, delight, Indr. 3, 9; Draup. 8, 23.<BR> --Comp.<BR> A. शर्मन् may be added at the end of all Brāhmaṇa names, as देव-, विष्णु-, m., MBh. 1, 2049; Hit. 11, 4, M.M.<BR> B. अ-, n. misery, Kir. 12, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मवन्त्|शर्मवत्|शर्म्मवत्
शर्मवन्त् शर्मवन्त्, i. e. शर्मन् + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Happy, auspicious, Man. 2, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0936-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्मिष्ठा
शर्मिष्ठा शर्मिष्ठा, i. e. superl. of the last, f. A proper name, the wife of Yayāti, Śāk. d. 82; Mālav. 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्या|शर्य्या
शर्या शर्या, i. e. शॄ + या, f. Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्यात
शर्यात शर्यात, m. A proper name, Chr. 297, 17 = Rigv. i. 112, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्|शर्व्व्
† शर्व् शर्व्, सर्व् सर्व्, i. 1, Par. To kill (cf. शॄ and the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व|शर्वः|शर्व्व|शर्व्वः
शर्व शर्व, i. e. शॄ + व (cf. शरु),<BR> I. m. A name of Śiva, Pañc. ii. d. 169; Hariv. 15408.<BR> II. f. शर्वाणी, Śiva's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वट
शर्वट शर्वट, m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 413.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वरी|शर्व्वरी
शर्वरी शर्वरी, i. e. शॄ + वन् + ई, (with र् for न्, cf. शरु), f.<BR> 1. Night, Man. 1, 66.<BR> 2. A woman.<BR> 3. Turmeric.<BR> --Cf. probably as akin, Κέρϐερος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्वरीक|शर्व्वरीक
शर्वरीक शर्वरी + क, adj. Hurtful, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्
शल् शल्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To shake, to tremble (cf. चल्).<BR> 2. To cover.<BR> --i. 1, Par. To go, to run. Cf. श्वल् and शठ्.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, i. 1, Par. To start up, Śiś. 3, 37.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. उच्छलित.<BR> 1. Starting up, bubbling up, Pañc. i. d. 148.<BR> 2. Uncovered, Vikr. 57, 19.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, To spurt out, Śiś. 2, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल|शलं|शलः
शल शल, probably शॄ + अ (with ल् for र्),<BR> I. m. and n. The quill of a porcupine.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A dart.<BR> 2. A kind of field.<BR> 3. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलक|शलकः
शलक शलक, m. A spider; Pañc. iii. d. 179, read शलाकां.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलभ|शलभः
शलभ शलभ (cf. शरभ), m.<BR> 1. A grasshopper, Pañc. i. d. 369; iv. d. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b " target="_blank">Page0937-b + 43</a>] 58 (cf. पतङ्ग).<BR> 2. A locust, Arj. 7, 24; Chr. 34, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलल|शललं
शलल शलल (cf. शल), n., and f. ली, The quill of a porcupine, Pāraskara Gṛ. S. ii. 1, in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 532 (ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाका
शलाका शलाका (cf. शल), f.<BR> 1. A javelin.<BR> 2. An arrow.<BR> 3. A small stake, rod, the bar of a cage, Pañc. iii. d. 179; a rib of an umbrella, etc.<BR> 4. A fibrous stick used as a brush or pencil, Suśr. 1, 33, 18; a pencil, Ragh. 7, 8.<BR> 5. A porcupine.<BR> 6. A piece of ivory used in particular games, a domino, MBh. 5, 1225 (read ˚का-धूर्तान्, Sharpers).<BR> 7. A bone.<BR> 8. A bird, Turdus gosalica.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कान्तशलाका
अयस्-कान्त- + शलाका अयस्-कान्त- + शलाका, f. a magnetised needle, Mālat. 14, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाक|निःशलाकः
निःशलाक निःशलाक, i. e. निस्-. adj. (properly, free from the birds called Turdus gosalica), lonely, Man. 7, 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशशलाका
वंश- + शलाका वंश- + शलाका, f. 1. the bambu pipe that forms the body of the lute. 2. any small bambu pin or stake, as the bar of a cage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाटु|शलाटुः
शलाटु शलाटु, adj. Unripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्क|शल्कं
शल्क शल्क, probably शॄ + क (with ल् for र्), n.<BR> 1. A part.<BR> 2. The bark of a tree.<BR> 3. The scale of a fish.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशल्क|महाशल्कः
महा- + शल्क महा- + शल्क, m. a prawn or shrimp, Man. 3, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्क|सशल्कः
स- + शल्क स- + शल्क, adj. scaly, Man. 5, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्भ्
† शल्भ् शल्भ्, i. 1, Ātm. To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्य|शल्यं|शल्यः
शल्य शल्य, i. e. शल + य,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A dart, a javelin.<BR> 2. An arrow, Utt. Rāmac. 46, 14; Chr. 30, 1 (m.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A peg, a pin.<BR> 2. A porcupine.<BR> 3. A thorny shrub, Vangueria spinosa.<BR> 4. A boundary.<BR> 5. The name of a king, Johns. Sel. 50, 98.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Any stake or thorn, Bhartṛ. 2, 97.<BR> 2. An iron crow.<BR> 3. Any extraneous substance which has lodged in the body, as an arrow or thorn.<BR> 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a " target="_blank">Page0938-a + 42</a>] Difficulty.<BR> 5. Poison.<BR> 6. Sin.<BR> 7. Abuse.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κῆλα, pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशल्य
निस्- + शल्य निस्- + शल्य, adj. free from an arrow, MBh. 6, 3375. ˚यम्, adv. free from pain or care, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
वि- + शल्य वि- + शल्य, adj. 1. free from thorns or spikes, Rām. 6, 71, 24. 2. free from pain or care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्य
स- + शल्य स- + शल्य, adj. 1. pierced by a thorn or dart. 2. pierced, Vikr. d. 29. 3. troublesome, difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0937-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक|शल्यकः
शल्यक शल्य + क, m.<BR> 1. A thron, a stake.<BR> 2. A dart, a pike.<BR> 3. A hedgehog, Man. 12, 65.<BR> 4. A porcupine, ib. 5, 18; Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यवन्त्|शल्यवत्
शल्यवन्त् शल्य + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Shooting arrows, one who has shot an arrow, Man. 9, 44.<BR> 2. Set with stakes.<BR> 3. Harassed with difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लक|शल्लकं|शल्लकः
शल्लक शल्लक (cf. शल्क and शल्य),<BR> I. m. A plant, Bignonia indica.<BR> II. f. की,<BR> 1. A porcupine.<BR> 2. The gum olibanum tree, Boswellia thurifera, Vikr. d. 107.<BR> III. n. Bark, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्व|शल्वः
शल्व शल्व, m. The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव्
शव् शव्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To alter, to change, to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव|शवं|शवः
शव शव,<BR> I. m. and n. A dead body, Man. 4, 108; Pañc. v. d. 24 (m.); Kathās. 4, 107 (m.).<BR> II. n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवर|शवरः
शवर शवर, m.<BR> 1. A barbarian tribe, a Śavara, Nalod. 3, 37.<BR> 2. f. री, A female of that tribe, Utt. Rāmac. 19, 14.<BR> 3. Śiva.<BR> 4. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरशवर
स्मर- + शवर स्मर- + शवर, m. the शवर- like (i. e. cruel) god of love, Bhartṛ. 1, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शवल शवल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Variegated, of a variegated colour, Mālat. 145, 12; grown or yellow, Vikr. d. 109 (cf. Wilson, Spec. of the Theatre of the Hind. 2. ed. i. 250, n.).<BR> 2. Imitative.<BR> 3. Articulated, Rājat. 5, 68 (divided, viz. by rivers).<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. A brindled cow. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b " target="_blank">Page0938-b + 40</a>]<BR> 2. The cow of plenty, Vaśiṣṭha's cow, Rām. 1, 52, 21.<BR> III. n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवलत्व
शवलत्व शवल + त्व, n. Alternation, Mālat. 161, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवस्
शवस् शवस्, i. e. शु (= श्वि) + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Power, strength, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR> 2. A corpse.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यशवस्
सत्य- + शवस् सत्य- + शवस्, adj. possessed of real strength, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 86, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्
† शश् शश् (originally शस्, cf. शश and N.G. hast; Eng. to hasten, श् for स् by assimilation), i. 1, Par. To jump, to move by leaping. Pres. ptcple. शशन्त्, Kir. 15, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश|शशः
शश शश् + अ (originally शस, cf. O.H.G. haso; A.S. hara), m.<BR> 1. A hare, Pañc. ii. d. 79; or rabbit.<BR> 2. The spots on the moon, supposed to resemble the figure of a hare (cf. शशधर, sqq.).<BR> 3. Gum myrrh.<BR> 4. A tree, Symplocos racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशक|शशकः
शशक शश + क, m. A hare, Hit. ii. d. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशधर|शशधरः
शशधर शश-धर, शशभृत् शश-भृ + त्, शशाङ्क शशाङ्क, i. e. शश-अङ्क, and शशिन् शशिन्, i. e. शश + इन्, m. The moon, Bhartṛ. 1, 40 (धर); Pañc. i. d. 107 (शशाङ्क); Vikr. d. 8 (शशिन्); 109 (शशिन्); see शश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वन्त्|शश्वत्
शश्वन्त् शश्वन्त् (for original स-श्वन्त्, vb. श्वि; cf. ἅπας and विश्व, शाश्वत), acc. n. वत्, adv.<BR> 1. Perpetually, Megh. 56; Hit. i. d. 211, M.M.<BR> 2. Again and again.<BR> --Cf. πᾶς, i. e. mutilated ἅπας.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्
† शष् शष्, i. 1, Par. To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुल|शष्कुलः
शष्कुल शष्कुल,<BR> I. m. A plant, Galedupa arborea Roxb.<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. The outer ear, Yājñ. 3, 96.<BR> 2. Rice or barley water.<BR> 3. A sort of pie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0938-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्प|शष्पं|शष्पः
शष्प शष्प, and शस्प शस्प, Pañc. 9, 6 (probably from vb. शस्; cf. वि-शस् and शस्त्र, properly, grass which may be cut), n.<BR> 1. Young grass, Ragh. 2, 26; Vikr. d. 120 (read शष्प instead of शष्य, Boll., and शस्य, Calc.).<BR> 2. Loss of intellect.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cespes, i. e. cespo + vit = शस्प + वन्त्, Endowed with young grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पभुज्
शष्पभुज् शष्प-भुज्, adj. sbst. A beast feeding on grass, Pañc. 102, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् शस् (akin to शम्, cf. e. g. यस् and यम्), i. 1, Par. To hurt, to kill, MBh. 3, 1638; cf. सस्.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To hurt, Rām. 2, 11, 16 (figurat. To overpower by deceit); अभिशस्त, Hurt, Man. 11, 112.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रशस्त, Destroyed, removed, MBh. 12, 5067.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To dissect, Rām. 1, 13, 35.<BR> 2. To sacrifice, MBh. 3, 10495.<BR> 3. To kill, Nal. 11, 28. विशस्त्च्,<BR> 1. Cut, dissected.<BR> 2. Hurt, killed.<BR> --Cf. Lat. hostia; Goth. hunsl; A.S. husel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसन|शसनं
शसन शस् + अन, n. Immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्र|शस्त्रं|शस्त्रः
शस्त्र शस् + त्र,<BR> I. n. A sword, a scimitar, Pañc. 34, 15; Chr. 18, 33; 2.<BR> II. f. त्री, A knife, Bhartṛ. 1, 89.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A weapon in general, Vikr. 87, 2; Pañc. 263, 6; Nal. 11, 28 (an arrow).<BR> 2. Iron.<BR> 3. Steel.<BR> 4. A hymn.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. castrare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशस्त्र
अति- + शस्त्र अति- + शस्त्र, adj. surpassing weapons, Ragh. 12, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशस्त्र
निस्- + शस्त्र निस्- + शस्त्र, adj. disarmed, unarmed, Rājat. 5, 406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तशस्त्र|न्यस्तशस्त्रः
न्यस्त- + शस्त्र न्यस्त- + शस्त्र, i. e. नि-अस्त-, adj. one who has laid down his weapons, epithet of the Manes, Man. 3, 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशस्त्र
महा- + शस्त्र महा- + शस्त्र, n. an excellent weapon, Chr. 25, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
वि- + शस्त्र वि- + शस्त्र, adj. disarmed, unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रधर|शस्त्रधरः
शस्त्रधर शस्त्र-धर, and शस्त्रभृत् ऽअस्त्र-भृ + त्, m. A warrior, Chr. 13, 5 (-भृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व
शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व, i. e. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b " target="_blank">Page0939-b + 41</a>] शस्त्र-अस्त्र-भृ + त् + त्व, n. Bearing arms for striking and throwing, Man. 10, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिक
ऽशस्त्रिक -शस्त्रिक, substituted for शस्त्र, as latter part of a comp. adj., Daśak. in Chr. 189, 6 in कण्ठ-न्यस्त-, Having put a knife to (his) throat, and 201, 10, अ-लक्ष्य- (my) sword not being noticed (properly against grammar, which prescribes शस्त्रक with अ, but perhaps for शस्त्रिन् + क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन् शस्त्रिन्, i. e. शस्त्र + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Armed, Rājat. 5, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्प|शस्पं|शस्पः
शस्प शस्प, see शष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य शस्य, see शंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक|शाकं|शाकः
शाक शाक, partly शक् + अ,<BR> I. (m. and) n. A potherb, any vegetable, Man. 2, 246; Hit. i. d. 67, M.M.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Power.<BR> 2. One of the seven द्वीपस्.<BR> 3. An era, especially that of Śālivāhana, beginning seventy-six or seventyeight years after the Christian.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलशाक
उत्पल- + शाक उत्पल- + शाक, m. the name of a plant, Rājat. 5, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशाक
काल- + शाक काल- + शाक, n. Ocimum sanctum, Man. 3, 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तशाक|तिक्तशाकः
तिक्त- + शाक तिक्त- + शाक, m. 1. a bitter vegetable, Rājat. 5, 49(?). 2. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रशाक|पत्रशाकः
पत्र- + शाक पत्र- + शाक, m. a potherb, Man. 12, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकट|शाकटं|शाकटः
शाकट शाकट, i. e. शकट + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a cart.<BR> II. m. A draught ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटीन|शाकटीनः
शाकटीन शाकटीन, i. e. शकट + ईन,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a cart.<BR> II. m. A cart-load as a measure of weight or value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल|शाकलः
शाकल शाकल, adj. Epithet of a kind of sacrifice, Man. 11, 200; cf. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलहोमीय
शाकलहोमीय शाकलहोमीय, i. e. शाकल-होम + ईय, adj. Belonging to the शाकलहोम, Man. 11, 256 (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0939-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकट|शाकशाकटं
शाकशाकट शाकशाकट, and शाकशाकिन शाकशाकिन (cf. शाक), n. A field of vegetables, a kitchen garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिनी
शाकिनी शाकिनी, i. e. शाक + इन् + ई, f. A female divinity of an inferior class, Pañc. 241, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन|शाकुनः
शाकुन शाकुन, i. e. शकुन + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Of or relating to birds. Man. 3, 268.<BR> 2. Portentous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिक|शाकुनिकः
शाकुनिक शाकुनिक, i. e. शकुन + इक,<BR> I. adj. Of or relating to birds.<BR> II. m. A fowler, Man. 8, 260; Pañc. iii. d. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त|शाक्तः
शाक्त शाक्त, and शाक्त्य शाक्त्य, i. e. शक्ति + अ or य, m. A worshipper of the female principle, Lass. 2. ed. 87, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तीक|शाक्तीकः
शाक्तीक शाक्तीक, i. e. शक्ति + ईक, m. A spearman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त्य|शाक्त्यः
शाक्त्य शाक्त्य, see शाक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्य|शाक्यः
शाक्य शाक्य, m. Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha faith, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्
† शाख् शाख्, i. 1, Par. To pervade, to embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखा
शाखा शाखा, f.<BR> 1. The branch of a tree, Pañc. 148, 5.<BR> 2. An arm.<BR> 3. Any part of an animal devoid of sensibility, as a horn.<BR> 4. A division, a sect.<BR> 5. A subdivision of the Vedas, according to the different schools and redactions of the holy writings, Windischmann, Sankara, 112.<BR> 6. A part, Mālav. d. 29.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशाख
त्रि-शाख त्रि-शाख, adj., f. खी, consisting of three wrinkles (viz. a frown), MBh. 8, 4336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशाखा|स्कंधशाखा
स्कन्ध- + शाखा स्कन्ध- + शाखा, f. the principal branch of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाभृत्
शाखाभृत् शाखा-भृ + त्, m. A tree, Kir. 5, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखिन्
शाखिन् शाखिन्, i. e. शाखा + इन्,<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b " target="_blank">Page0940-b + 42</a>] adj., f. नी, Having branches, branched, literally and figuratively.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A tree, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 187.<BR> 2. A Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खिक|शांखिक|शांखिकः|शाङ्खिकः
शाङ्खिक शाङ्खिक, i. e. शङ्ख + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a conch-shell.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A shell-cutter.<BR> 2. A shellblower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट|शाटः
शाट शाट, m., and f. टी, and शाटक शाटक, m. and n.<BR> 1. A petticoat, Pañc. i. d. 160 (टक); Rām. 2, 32, 21 (टी); a gown, Mṛcch. 49, 11.<BR> 2. (टी), Cloth, Bhāg. P. 9, 9, 7.<BR> 3. (ट), A garment, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1210.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशाटि|स्थूलशाटिः
स्थूल-शाटि स्थूल-शाटि, or -शाटक, m., and टका, टिका, f. coarse cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाठ्य|शाठ्यं
शाठ्य शाठ्य, i. e. शठ + य, n.<BR> 1. Deceit, Hit. i. d. 99, M.M.<BR> 2. Wickedness.<BR> 3. Perfidy, hatred, Bhartṛ. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्
† शाड् शाड्, or शाल् शाल्, i. 1, Ātm. To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण शाण,<BR> A. i. e. शण + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of Bengal San, Man. 2, 41.<BR> II. f. णी.<BR> 1. Ragged garment.<BR> 2. A new unseamed and single breadth of cloth, given to the religious student at his investiture.<BR> III. n. Coarse cloth, canvass.<BR> B. (from vb. शो, cf. शान), m., and f. णी.<BR> 1. A whet or grindstone, Bhartṛ. 2, 36 (read शाणो˚).<BR> 2. A touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शांडिल्यः|शाण्डिल्यः
शाण्डिल्य शाण्डिल्य, i. e. शण्डिल, a proper name, + य, patronym., f. ली (Pañc. 122, 1), Descended from Śaṇḍila, Pañc. ii. d. 83. m. The name of a Muni, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भ|शातकुंभ|शातकुंभं|शातकुम्भं|शातकुम्भः
शातकुम्भ शातकुम्भ, i. e. शत-कुम्भ + अ, n. Gold, Śiś. 9, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भमय
शातकुम्भमय शातकुम्भ + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Arj. 9, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
शातन शातन,<BR> I. n. Withering, becoming thin (cf. शात, s. v. शो).<BR> II. i. e. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a " target="_blank">Page0941-a + 41</a>] शातय, Caus. of शद्, + अन, at the end of a comp. adj. Cutting off, Ragh. 3, 42 (v. r., cf. शातिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0940-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभिष
शातभिष शातभिष, or शातभिषज शातभिषज, i. e. शतभिषा, or शतभिषज्, + अ, m. One who is born during the lunar mansion called शतभिषा or शतभिषज्, Vārt. 2, ad Pāṇ. iv. 2, 8; cf. iv. 3, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमन्यव
शातमन्यव शातमन्यव, i. e. शत-मन्यु, a name of Indra, + अ, adj. Belonging to Indra, Kir. 13, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातिन्
शातिन् शातिन्, i. e. शातय, Caus. of शद्, + इन्, adj. Cutting off, Ragh. 3, 42 (v. r., cf. शातन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव शात्रव, i. e. शत्रु + अ,<BR> I. m. An enemy, MBh. 8, 1523.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Enmity.<BR> 2. A multitude of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद|शादः
शाद शाद, i. e. शद + अ, m.<BR> 1. Young grass.<BR> 2. Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल शाद्वल, i. e. शाद + वल,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Covered with young grass, Vikr. 57, 18; Rām. 3, 50, 14.<BR> 2. Green, Kāśīkh. 32, 50, and Aufrecht, Ujjvalad. 255, n.<BR> II. sbst. (n.) A place covered with grass, Kir. 7, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्
† शान् शान् (properly a denomin. derived from शान), used only in the anomal. desider. शीशांस, Par. Ātm. To whet, to sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान|शानः
शान शान, i. e. शो + न, m.<BR> 1. A grindstone.<BR> 2. A touchstone.<BR> --Cf. A.S. haenan, lapidare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानैश्चर
शानैश्चर शानैश्चर, i. e. शन्दिश्चर + अ, adj. Falling on a Saturday, Lass. 16, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनव|शांतनव|शांतनवः|शान्तनवः
शान्तनव शान्तनव, i. e. चन्तन + अ, patronym., m. The son of Śāntanu, i. e. Bhīṣma, Chr. 4, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनु|शांतनु|शान्तनुः
शान्तनु शान्तनु, m. The name of a king, Chr. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ति|शांति|शांतिः|शान्तिः
शान्ति शान्ति, i. e. शम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Quiet, the absence of passion, and indifference to objects of pleasure or pain, Hit. 78, 8, M.M.; iii. d. 4.<BR> 2. Felicity, Lass. 96, 12.<BR> 3. Rest, repose, Mālat. 87, 6.<BR> 4. Ceasing, Hit. iii. d. 88.<BR> 5. Causing to cease, Mālat. 128, 3; remission, alleviation, soothing, Śṛṅgārat. 14; Śāk. 31, 11; Vikr. d. 24.<BR> 6. Appeasing (the stomach), Bhartṛ. 2, 23.<BR> 7. Expiatory rites to avert evil Rām. 1, 11, 14.<BR> 8. Preservation, Pañc. 89, 5; 90, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व्|शांत्व्
शान्त्व् शान्त्व्, and (worse, although very frequent), सान्त्व् सान्त्व्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 2, 2428),<BR> 1. To pacify, Man. 7, 172 (with स्).<BR> 2. To comfort, to console, Mālat. 146, 3 (with स्); MBh. 4, 436 (with स्).<BR> 3. To address mildly, Man. 8, 79 (with स्); Chr. 38, 7 (with श्).<BR> 4. To conciliate, Rām. 1, 38, 5 (with स्).<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To comfort, Rām. 2, 32, 39 (with श्).<BR> --With उप उप, To comfort, MBh. 3, 14330 (with स्).<BR> --With परि परि, To console, Rām. 2, 23, 42 (with श्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व शान्त्व, and सान्त्व सान्त्व (Man. 8, 391), i. e. शम् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Conciliation.<BR> 2. Comforting, consoling.<BR> 3. Mildness, Man. 8, 391 (स्); Chr. 42, 9 (श्).<BR> 4. Mild speech, Rām. 2, 35, 23; MBh. 5, 2650 (सान्त्व).<BR> 5. Peaceable way, Pañc. iii. d. 26 (सान्त्व); Lass. 45, 14 (श्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाप|शापः
शाप शाप, i. e. शप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abuse.<BR> 2. Oath.<BR> 3. Curse, Pañc. 186, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द शाब्द, i. e. शब्द + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Sonorous, sounding.<BR> 2. Relating to or derived from words, Bhāṣāp. 80.<BR> 3. Nominal.<BR> II. f. दि, Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0941-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक शाब्दिक, i. e. शब्द + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to sounds or words.<BR> II. m. A grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन् शामन् (vb. शम्, cf. सामन्), n. Conciliation, appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन|शामनं|शामनः
शामन शामन, i. e. शम्, anomal. Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Killing.<BR> 2. Tranquillity.<BR> 3. End; with या, To be destroyed, Pañc. iii. 31 (but cf. my transl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्र|शामित्रं
शामित्र शामित्र, शम् + त्र (see the last), n.<BR> 1. A deadly blow, Mṛcch. 161, 11.<BR> 2. Sacrificing.<BR> 3. Tieing cattle.<BR> 4. A sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बूक|शांबूक|शांबूकः|शाम्बूकः
शाम्बूक शाम्बूक = शम्बूक, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शाम्भव शाम्भव, i. e. शम्भु + अ,<BR> I. adj. Belonging to Śiva, Pañc. i. d. 175.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. A worshipper of Śiva.<BR> 3. A sort of poison.<BR> III. f. वी, Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
शायक शायक, see सायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन् शायिन्, i. e. शी + इन्, adj., f. नी, Lying down, lying, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 15; living, Hit. i. d. 138, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वशायिन्
ऊर्ध्व- + शायिन् ऊर्ध्व- + शायिन्, m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशायिन्
एक- + शायिन् एक- + शायिन्, adj. resting ever on the same seat, Lass. 2. ed. 70, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादशायिन्
प्रासाद- + शायिन् प्रासाद- + शायिन्, adj., f. नी, one who had slept in a palace, Hiḍ. 1, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगशायिन्
योग- + शायिन् योग- + शायिन्, adj. absorbed in meditation, Rājat. 5, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलशायिन्|स्थंडिलशायिन्
स्थण्डिल- + शायिन् स्थण्डिल- + शायिन्, m. a devotee who sleeps on ground prepared for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्
† शार् शार्, सार् सार्, i. 10, Par. To be weak (cf. शॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार शार,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Variegated (in colour), Daśak. in Chr. 180, 1 (of hair, mixed with grey and white).<BR> 2. Yellow.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Hurting (vb. शॄ).<BR> 2. A mixture of blue and yellow, a green.<BR> 3. Variegating.<BR> 4. Air, wind (cf. सार).<BR> 5. A piece or man at chess, backgammon, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b " target="_blank">Page0942-b + 44</a>] Daśak. in Chr. 185, 24 (cf. सार).<BR> III. f. री.<BR> 1. An arrow (vb. शॄ, cf. शर), Chr. 297, 16 = Rigv. i. 112, 16.<BR> 2. Kuśa grass.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशार|कृष्णशारः
कृष्ण- + शार कृष्ण- + शार, adj. blue-black, Megh. 48, read -शार (Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारंगः|शारङ्गः
शारङ्ग शारङ्ग (cf. the last and सारङ्ग),<BR> I. adj. Variegated, spotted.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A deer.<BR> 2. An elephant.<BR> 3. The चातक, Cuculus melanoleucus.<BR> 4. A peacock.<BR> 5. A large bee.<BR> III. f. गी.<BR> 1. A sort of fiddle.<BR> 2. The wife of Mandapāla, Man. 9, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद शारद, i. e. शरद् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. दी.<BR> 1. Autumnal, Nal. 13, 44; Lass. 91, 15.<BR> 2. Produced or growing in the autumn, Man. 6, 11.<BR> 3. New.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Grain or rice ripening in the autumn.<BR> 2. A sort of kidney bean.<BR> 3. Autumnal sickness.<BR> 4. Autumnal sunshine.<BR> 5. A year.<BR> III. f. दा.<BR> 1. Sarasvatī, Lass. 38, 7.<BR> 2. A title of Durgā.<BR> 3. A sort of guitar.<BR> IV. f. दी, The day of full moon in the month कार्त्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्वत|शारद्वतः
शारद्वत शारद्वत, i. e. शरद्वन्त् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Descended from Śaradvant, Johns. Sel. 20, 94.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Śāk. 63, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारि|शारिः
शारि शारि (cf. शार),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A piece or man at chess, draughts, etc.<BR> 2. An elephant's housings.<BR> 3. Fraud.<BR> II. m., f. रि or री, A bird, Gracula religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका शारिका, i. e. शारि + क, f.<BR> 1. A bird, Gracula religiosa and Turdus salica, Lass. 20, 1 (cf. सारिका).<BR> 2. A bow or stick for playing any stringed musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर शारीर, i. e. शरीर + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Corporeal, Bhag. 17, 14; relating to animal bodies, Man. 5, 110.<BR> 2. Spiritual, incorporate.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Excrement, Man. 11, 202.<BR> 2. The soul whilst incorporate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0942-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक शारीर + क, and शारीरिक शारीरिक, i. e. शरीर + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Corporeal.<BR> 2. Incorporate; cf. शारीरक-सूत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कक|शार्ककः
शार्कक शार्कक (cf. शर्करा), m.<BR> 1. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR> 2. Cream, the froth of milk.<BR> 3. A lump of meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कर|शार्करः
शार्कर शार्कर, i. e. शर्करा + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Stony.<BR> 2. Sugary.<BR> II. m. The froth of milk, cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्गाल
शार्गाल शार्गाल, i. e. शृगाल + अ, adj., f. ली, Belonging to a jackal, MBh. 13, 411.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्ग|शार्ंग|शार्ङ्गं|शार्ङ्गः
शार्ङ्ग शार्ङ्ग, i. e. शृङ्ग + अ,<BR> I. adj. Horny, made of horn, etc.<BR> II. m. (n.?),<BR> 1. A bow, Śāk. 94, 2.<BR> 2. The bow of Viṣṇu.<BR> 3. The name of a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गिन्|शार्ंगिन्
शार्ङ्गिन् शार्ङ्गिन्, i. e. शार्ङ्ग + इन्, m.<BR> 1. An archer.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu, Megh. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूल|शार्दूलः|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूल शार्दूल, m.<BR> 1. A tiger, Nal. 12, 129.<BR> 2. A Rākṣasa.<BR> 3. A sort of bird.<BR> 4. (as latter part of comp. words), Best, pre-eminent; e. g. मुनि-, m. A pre-eminent sage, Lass. 49, 15; राजशर्दूल, i. e. राजन्-, m. A pre-eminent king, Rām. 3, 49, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्व
शार्व शार्व, i. e. शर्व + अ, adj. Belonging to Śiva, Bhartṛ. 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वर|शार्व्वरं
शार्वर शार्वर, i. e. शर्वरी + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Nocturnal.<BR> 2. Mischievous, pernicious.<BR> II. m. Darkness.<BR> III. f. री Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्
† शाल् शाल्, see शाड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल|शालः
शाल शाल (cf. साल),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A tree, Shorea robusta (ŚKD.), MBh. 9, 3239; 14, 2521.<BR> 2. A fish, Ophiocephalus wrahl Ham., Hiḍ. 2, 18.<BR> 3. Śālivāhana.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. A large [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b " target="_blank">Page0943-b + 43</a>] branch of a tree.<BR> 2. A hall.<BR> 3. A stable, Hit. i. d. 135, M.M.<BR> 4. A house.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. heal, A hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपशाला
अपूप- + शाला अपूप- + शाला, f. a bakehouse, Man. 9, 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशाला
अश्व- + शाला अश्व- + शाला, f. a stable, Nal. 19, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वचलनशाला
अश्व-चलन- + शाला अश्व-चलन- + शाला, f. a stable for riding horses, Pañc. 252, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वशाला|गांधर्वशाला
गान्धर्व- + शाला गान्धर्व- + शाला, f. a music-room, Kathās. 12, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःशाल|चतुःशालं
चतुःशाल चतुःशाल, i. e. चतुर्-,<BR> I. adj. possessing four halls, Pañc. 252, 17.<BR> II. n. a square formed by four houses, Rām. 3, 23, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशाला|चंद्रशाला
चन्द्र- + शाला चन्द्र- + शाला, f. an apartment on the house-top, Ragh. 13, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशाला
चित्र- + शाला चित्र- + शाल, f. a hall adorned with pictures, a picture-gallery, Rām. 3, 61, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तनशाला|नर्त्तनशाला
नर्तन- + शाला नर्तन- + शाला, f. a dancing-room, MBh. 4, 696.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीशाला
पत्नी- + शाला पत्नी- + शाला, f. a room erected near the place of a sacrifice for the women and sacrificial implements, MBh. 12, 3648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णशाला
पर्ण- + शाला पर्ण- + शाला, f. 1. an arbour, Rām. 3, 6, 15. 2. the name of a district inhabited by anchorites, MBh. 13, 3398.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशाला
पाक- + शाला पाक- + शाला, f. the kitchen, Lass. 81, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गशाला|रंगशाला
रङ्ग- + शाला रङ्ग- + शाला, f. a hall for public exhibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथशाला
रथ- + शाला रथ- + शाला, f. a coach-house, Nal. 21, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पशाला
शिल्प- + शाला शिल्प- + शाला, n., and f. ला, a workshop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदशाला
सूद- + शाला सूद- + शाला, f. a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालभञ्जी|शालभंजी
शालभञ्जी शालभञ्जी, and शालभञ्जिका शालभञ्जिका, i. e. शाल-भञ्ज् + अ + ई, and + क, f.<BR> 1. A doll.<BR> 2. A kind of play in the east of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाजिर|शालाजिरः
शालाजिर शालाजिर, m. and n. A hollow earthen cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालार|शालारं
शालार शालार, n.<BR> 1. A ladder.<BR> 2. The claw of an elephant.<BR> 3. A bird-cage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालि|शालिः
शालि शालि, m.<BR> 1. Rice, Pañc. 163, 23.<BR> 2. The civet or polecat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिक|शालिकः
शालिक शालिक, i. e. शाला̆ + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating or belonging to the Shorea robusta, a hall, etc.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A weaver.<BR> 2. A village of artificers.<BR> 3. A tax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0943-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिता
शालिता शालिता, i. e. शालिन् + ता, f.<BR> 1. Possessing.<BR> 2. Confidence in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन् शालिन्, i. e. शाला + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Belonging to a house, domestic.<BR> 2. Endowed with, Kathās. 46, 107; Kir. 5, 32; possessed of, having, Pañc. v. d. 12.<BR> 3. Shining or resplendent with.<BR> II. f. नी, A proper name, Lass. 39, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानशालिन्
अभिमान- + शालिन् अभिमान- + शालिन्, adj. proud. जल-ज-, adj. full of fishes, MBh. 2, 1813.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयशालिन्
नय- + शालिन् नय- + शालिन्, adj. conversant with politics, Kir. 5, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुशालिन्
बाहु- + शालिन् बाहु- + शालिन्, m. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यशालिन्
वीर्य- + शालिन् वीर्य- + शालिन्, adj. strong, heroic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्र|शालिहोत्रः
शालिहोत्र शालिहोत्र, m.<BR> 1. The name of a writer on veterinary medicine, Nal. 19, 28; Pañc. 253, 22; 255, 4.<BR> 2. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्रज्ञ
शालिहोत्रज्ञ शालिहोत्र-ज्ञ, adj. Knowing (the precepts of) Śālihotra, Pañc. 255, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन शालीन, i. e. शाला + ईन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Ashamed, bashful, humble, Nalod. 2, 3; Ragh. 6, 81; Mālav. 51, 7 (cf. शाल्त्नीकरण, Humbling, Pāṇ. 1, 3, 70).<BR> 2. Like.<BR> II. m. An opulent householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालु|शालुः
शालु शालु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A frog.<BR> 2. An astringent substance.<BR> 3. A sort of perfume.<BR> II. n. The root of the water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूक|शालूकं|शालूकः
शालूक शालूक (cf. the last), n. The root of the esculent water lily.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठशालूक
कण्ठ- + शालूक कण्ठ- + शालूक, n. a swelling in the throat, Suśr. 1, 306, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूर|शालूरः
शालूर शालूर (cf. शालु), m. A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेय|शालेयं|शालेयः
शालेय शालेय, i. e. शालि + एय, adj. Fit for rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलि|शाल्मलिः
शाल्मलि and ली शाल्मली̆, f.<BR> 1. The silk cotton tree, Bombax heptaphyllum, Man. 8, 246.<BR> 2. One of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b " target="_blank">Page0944-b + 42</a>] seven द्वीपस्.<BR> 3. ली, A hell, Man. 4, 90.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशाल्मलि|कूटशाल्मलिः
कूट- + शाल्मलि कूट- + शाल्मलि, f. a fabulous thorny rod of the cotton tree for torturing the wicked in hell, MBh. 18, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्व|शाल्वः
शाल्व शाल्व, i. e. शल्व + अ, m.<BR> 1. pl. The inhabitants of Śalva, Sāv. 2, 7; Chr. 5, 6; 18, 34; 35.<BR> 2. The king of the Śālvas, ib. 14, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वेय
शाल्वेय शाल्वेय, i. e. शल्व + एय, m. pl. The inhabitants of Śalva, Draup. 1, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव शाव,<BR> I. i. e. शव + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to, or produced by, a dead body, Man. 5, 59.<BR> 2. Dead, Sāv. 5, 61.<BR> II. (akin to श्वि, cf. शिशु), m. The young of any animal, Utt. Rāmac. 122, 12 (सिंह-, A lion's cub).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावक|शावकः
शावक शाव + क, m. The young of any animal Hit. 39, 4, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर शावर, i. e. शवर + अ,<BR> I. adj. Low, vile.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Fault.<BR> 2. Sin, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत शाश्वत, i. e. शश्वन्त् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती,<BR> 1. All, Utt. Rāmac. 36, 7; MBh. 12, 9192.<BR> 2. Eternal, Hit. ii. d. 60; perpetual, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 101 (with न, perishable); ˚तम्, adv. Constantly, Mālat. 3, 5.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Vyāsa.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. The sun.<BR> III. f. ती, The earth.<BR> IV. n. Heaven.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाश्वत
अ- + शाश्वत अ- + शाश्वत, adj. short, Pañc. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशाश्वत
परि- + शाश्वत परि- + शाश्वत, adj. eternal, MBh. 5, 4574.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल शाष्कुल (anomal. for शौष्कुल, q. cf.), adj. Eating flesh or fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् शास् (for शशस्, i. e. शंस्, ii. 3); the base of many formations is शिष् for शिस् (or rather शिशस्, i. e. शंस्, ii. 3, with इ in the reduplication), ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 4993),<BR> 1. To teach, Bhag. 2, 7; pass. शिष्य, To learn, Pañc. 4, 20; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a " target="_blank">Page0945-a + 44</a>] 94, 10.<BR> 2. To report, to proclaim, Man. 11, 82.<BR> 3. To command, Ragh. 15, 79 (Calc.).<BR> 4. To govern, Man. 7, 18.<BR> 5. To punish, Man. 4, 175; 8, 314.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शिष्ट.<BR> 1. Disciplined.<BR> 2. Docile.<BR> 3. Good, MBh. 1, 6845.<BR> 4. Learned, Man. 3, 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. शिष्य, m. A pupil, Vikr. 35, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. indocile, Pañc. i. d. 433.<BR> उप-, m. a pupil of a pupil, Prab. 28, 3.<BR> --Caus. To punish, Hit. 65, 18 (शासित). शासित, Governed.<BR> --Comp.<BR> मातृ-, m. a fool.<BR> सु-, adj. well-governed, Hit. i. d. 21, M.M.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To teach, Rājat. 5, 400; to instruct, Śāk. 55, 18.<BR> 2. To speak to, to address, MBh. 4, 98.<BR> 3. To order, Man. 9, 233; Vikr. 70, 13; 86, 19 (acc. of the pers.).<BR> 4. To govern, MBh. 1, 4124.<BR> 5. To punish, Man. 11, 99.<BR> --With समनु सम्-अनु, To govern, Nal. 12, 49.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> I. Par.<BR> 1. To report, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 27.<BR> 2. To command, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 4.<BR> II. Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Arj. 5, 19).<BR> 1. To pray for benefits to (dat.), Man. 3, 80.<BR> 2. To pray, Bhaṭṭ. 5, 16.<BR> 3. To wish, Utt. Rāmac. 7, 15; MBh. 3, 12430.<BR> 4. To hope, Śāk. 112, 3.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. आशास्य, Desirable. n. Wish, blessing, Ragh. 5, 34.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. not to be desired, Ragh. 4, 44.<BR> --With उप उप, see शिष्य above.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To command, MBh. 2, 2433.<BR> 2. To govern, Man. 9, 66.<BR> 3. To punish. Chr. 16, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ट
अ- + शिष्ट अ- + शिष्ट, adj. wicked, MBh. 1, 6845.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0944-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन शास् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Governing, chastisement, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 873.<BR> 2. An order, Rām. 3, 51, 8; Vikr. d. 155; precept, Nal. 26, 9; edict, Nal. 2, 10.<BR> 3. A royal grant of land or privileges, Pañc. 4, 25.<BR> 4. A deed, a written [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b " target="_blank">Page0945-b + 44</a>] contract.<BR> 5. A शास्त्र or scripture.<BR> 6. The government of the passions.<BR> 7. Instruction, Johns. Sel. 57, 165.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशासन
कूट- + शासन कूट- + शासन, n. a forged royal edict, Man. 9, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रशासन
ताम्र- + शासन ताम्र- + शासन, n. an edict engraved on a copper plate, Daśak. 20, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशासन|दुःशासनः
दुस्- + शासन दुस्- + शासन, m. a proper name, MBh. 1, 2447.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशासन|धर्म्मशासन
धर्म- + शासन धर्म- + शासन, n. a code of law, MBh. 1, 2950.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशासन
पर- + शासन पर- + शासन, n. the order of another, Pañc. i. d. 300 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3292).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरशासन|पुरशासनः
पुर- + शासन पुर- + शासन, m. (the chastiser of Pura), epithet of Śiva, Kumāras. 7, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमशासन|भीमशासनः
भीम- + शासन भीम- + शासन, m. Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशासन
महा- + शासन महा- + शासन, a minister, Lass. 67, 10 (? cf. n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ शास् + इतृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what orders, commands; a governor, a king Śāk. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्ति|शास्तिः
शास्ति शास् + ति, f. Punishment inflicted by royal command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ शास् + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Who or what orders, a ruler.<BR> 2. A teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र शास् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. An order.<BR> 2. A precept, Pañc. 141, 13.<BR> 3. Scripture, institutes of religion, law, science, learning in general, Hit. pr. d. 10, M.M.; Bhartṛ. 2, 12; Chr. 5, 5.<BR> 4. A work of religious or scientific caracter, Man. 1, 58; Hit. pr. d. 6, M.M.; a collection, a treatise, a book, Pañc. pr. d. 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलच्छास्त्र
चलच्छास्त्र चलच्छास्त्र, i. e. चलन्त्- (vb. चल्), adj. one whose governing is staggering, unsteady, Lass. 53, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानशास्त्र
ज्ञान- + शास्त्र ज्ञान- + शास्त्र, n. a work on soothsaying, Lass. 36, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कशास्त्र
तर्क- + शास्त्र तर्क- + शास्त्र, n. logic, MBh. 12, 9678.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशास्त्र|धर्म्मशास्त्र|धर्म्मशास्त्रं
धर्म- + शास्त्र धर्म- + शास्त्र, n. 1. a book treating of duty, Hit. 19, 8, M.M. 2. the body of law, Man. title, 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयशास्त्र
नय- + शास्त्र नय- + शास्त्र and नीति-, n. 1. the science of political conduct, Rām. 3, 56, 18; MBh. 1, 5567. 2. works on polity, Pañc. pr. d. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशास्त्रम्
यथा-शास्त्र + म् यथा-शास्त्र + म्, adv. as the law ordains, Man. 2, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशास्त्र
शब्द- + शास्त्र शब्द- + शास्त्र, n. rules of grammar, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a " target="_blank">Page0946-a + 40</a>] Pañc. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशास्त्र
हय- + शास्त्र हय- + शास्त्र, n. art of training or treating horses, Chr. 25, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुशास्त्र
हेतु- + शास्त्र हेतु- + शास्त्र, n. a philosophical (= heretical) book, Man. 2, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0945-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्रकृत् शास्त्र + कृ + त्, m.<BR> 1. An author of a शास्त्र, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 17.<BR> 2. An author in general.<BR> 3. A Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञ|शास्त्रज्ञः
शास्त्रज्ञ शास्त्र-ज्ञ, adj.<BR> 1. Knowing the institutes of religion, etc., Pañc. i. d. 385.<BR> 2. Knowing by books, a theorist, Hit. iii. d. 54 (कर्मस्व् अदृष्टकर्मा यः शास्त्रज्ञो पि स मुह्यति, He who has not tested his skill by works, although knowing it by books, makes mistakes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतस्
शास्त्रतस् शास्त्र + तस्, n. According to the sacred authorities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवत्|शास्त्रवन्त्
शास्त्रवत् शास्त्र + वत्, adv. Like the holy writings, Hit. iii. d. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवन्त्|शास्त्रवत्
शास्त्रवन्त् शास्त्र + वन्त्, adj. Skilled in the holy writings, Pañc. iii. d. 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाहि
शाहि शाहि m. The name of a dynasty, Rājat. 5, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि शि, † ii. 5, Par. Ātm. To sharpen (cf. शो).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा शिंशपा, (शिंशिपा शिंशिपा, Lass. 4, 10; 14; 5, 6), f. Two trees, Dalbergia Siśu and the Aśoka tree, Pañc. 249, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्य|शिक्यं
शिक्य, शिक्य, n., and f. या,<BR> 1. The string suspended from either end of a pole to receive a burthen.<BR> 2. The burthen so carried.<BR> 3. The strings of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् शिक्ष्, see शक्, desider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा शिक्षा, i. e. शिक्ष, desider. of शक्, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Learning, Johns. Sel. 8, 3; Rājat. 5, 318; study.<BR> 2. One of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b " target="_blank">Page0946-b + 43</a>] the six Vedāṅgas, treating of pronunciation, Madhusūdana in Weber, Ind. St. i. 16.<BR> 3. Modesty.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिक्षा
उप- + शिक्षा उप- + शिक्षा, f. desire of learning, Mṛcch. 17, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजशिक्षा
गज- + शिक्षा गज- + शिक्षा, f. training of elephants, MBh. 1, 4355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखंडः|शिखण्डः
शिखण्ड शिखण्ड (cf. शिखा), m.<BR> 1. The tail of a peacock, Vikr. d. 81.<BR> 2. Locks of hair left at the time of tonsure, hair, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 15; 180, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखंडकः|शिखण्डकः
शिखण्डक शिखण्ड + क, m.<BR> 1. The tail of a peacock.<BR> 2. The lock of hair, or crest, left on the crown of the head, Utt. Rāmac. 105, 5; Śāk. 59, 17 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखंडिकः|शिखण्डिकः
शिखण्डिक शिखण्डिक,<BR> I. i. e. शिखण्डिन् + क, m. A cock.<BR> II. i. e. शिखण्ड + क, f. का, A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिन्|शिखंडिन्
शिखण्डिन् शिखण्डिन्, i. e. शिखण्ड + इन्,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A peacock, Utt. Rāmac. 65, 9.<BR> 2. A peacock's tail.<BR> 3. A cock.<BR> 4. An arrow.<BR> 5. A Ṛṣi.<BR> 6. The son of Drupada, who had been before a girl, Chr. 3, 1.<BR> II. f. नी, The daughter of Drupada, who was metamorphosed into a man, Chr. 52, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिन्|चित्रशिखंडिन्
चित्र- + शिखण्डिन् चित्र- + शिखण्डिन्, m. pl. the seven Ṛṣis, MBh. 12, 12722.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशिखण्डिन्
स- + शिखण्डिन् स- + शिखण्डिन्, adj. with Śikhaṇḍin, Chr. 54, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखर|शिखरं|शिखरः
शिखर शिखर (cf. शिखा), m. and n.<BR> 1. Summit, Pañc. 9, 7; end.<BR> 2. The summit of a mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 91; Vikr. 10, 6.<BR> 3. The top of a tree.<BR> 4. The edge or a point of a sword.<BR> 5. Horripilation.<BR> 6. The armpit.<BR> 7. A gem of a bright red colour; the bud of the Arabian jasmine, Megh. 80 (Sch.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिखर
त्रि- + शिखर त्रि- + शिखर, adj. having three summits, the name of a mountain, Rām. 4, 44, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन् शिखरिन्, i. e. शिखर + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a " target="_blank">Page0947-a + 44</a>]<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Crested, peaked, pointed.<BR> 2. Resembling the buds of the Arabian jasmine, Rām. 3, 52, 27.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mountain, Rām. 3, 55, 44.<BR> 2. A tree.<BR> 3. A stronghold.<BR> 4. The lapwing.<BR> II. f. इणी,<BR> 1. A line of hair extending across the navel.<BR> 2. An excellent woman.<BR> 3. A dish of curds and sugar with spices. Vikr. 42, 7 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 4. Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0946-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा शिखा, f.<BR> 1. Point, top, Rām. 3, 49, 34; end. Śāk. d. 14; Ragh. 16, 48 (at the end of a comp. adj.; Sch. filaments).<BR> 2. A crest, Rām. 3, 53, 60.<BR> 3. A peacock's crest.<BR> 4. A lock of hair on the crown of the head, Vikr. d. 124 (head).<BR> 5. Flame, Pañc. i. d. 319.<BR> 6. A ray of light.<BR> 7. Chief.<BR> 8. A branch.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशिख|अग्निशिखं|अग्निशिखः
अग्नि-शिख अग्नि-शिख,<BR> I. adj. as hot as fire, Rām. 6, 30, 27.<BR> II. f. खा, flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिख
उच्छिख उच्छिख, i. e. उद्-शिख, adj. blazing upwards or brightly, Utt. Rāmac. 65, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिख|त्रिशिखं|त्रिशिखः
त्रि-शिख त्रि-शिख, adj., f. खा, having the shape of a trident, Pañc. 220, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशिखा
दीप- + शिखा दीप- + शिखा, f. the flame of a lamp, Kathās. 18, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तशिख
दीप्त-शिख दीप्त-शिख, adj. blazing, Rām. 3, 53, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनशिखा
स्तन- + शिखा स्तन- + शिखा, f. a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावत्|शिखावन्त्
शिखावत् शिखा + वत्, adv. Like a crest, Pañc. 121, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावन्त्|शिखावत्
शिखावन्त् शिखा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावल|शिखावलः
शिखावल शिखा + वल,<BR> I. adj., f. लि.<BR> 1. Crested.<BR> 2. Burnt, Śṛṅgārat. 16.<BR> II. m. A peacock, Lass. 2. ed. 91 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिन्
शिखिन् शिखिन्, i. e. शिखा + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Crested, MBh. 6, 71.<BR> 2. Having a lock of hair on the top of the head, Rām. 3, 52, 9.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cock.<BR> 2. A peacock, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> 3. A religious mendicant.<BR> 4. A mountain. Rājat. 5, 15.<BR> 5. An arrow.<BR> 6. A bull.<BR> 7. A horse.<BR> 8. Fire, Rām. 3, 55, 11; Pañc. iv. d. 76 (but cf. also Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 125).<BR> 9. A lamp.<BR> 10. Ketu, the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b " target="_blank">Page0947-b + 38</a>] personified descending node, Pañc. i. d. 240 (see my transl.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रशिखिन्
शस्त्र- + शिखिन् शस्त्र- + शिखिन्, adj. proud of (the practice of) weapons, Utt. Rāmac. 149, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रु|शिग्रुः
शिग्रु शिग्रु, m.<BR> 1. A tree, Morunga guilandina.<BR> 2. A potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुक
शिग्रुक शिग्रु + क, m. A particular plant (cf. the last), Man. 6, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्ख्|शिंख्
† शिङ्ख् शिङ्ख्, i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घ्|शिंघ्
शिङ्घ् शिङ्घ्, i. 1, Par. To smell.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, To kiss, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाण|शिंघाण|शिङ्घाणं|शिंघाणः|शिङ्घाणः
शिङ्घाण शिङ्घाण,<BR> I. m. Froth, foam.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The mucus of the nose.<BR> 2. Rust of iron.<BR> 3. A glass vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकं|शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणकः
शिङ्घाणक शिङ्घाण + क, m. Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज्|शिंज्
शिञ्ज् शिञ्ज्, ii. 2, Ātm. To tinkle, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 4; Megh. 77 (Par.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शिञ्जित, Tinkling, Rām. 1, 9, 17. n. Tinkling, Ragh. 4, 56; of metallic ornaments worn as chains, rings, etc., Vikr. d. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज|शिंज|शिंजः|शिञ्जः
शिञ्ज शिञ्ज् + अ,<BR> I. m. Tinkling.<BR> II. f. जा, A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जिन्
शिञ्जिन् शिञ्ज् + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Tinkling.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A bow-string.<BR> 2. Metallic rings worn round the toes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिट्
† शिट् शिट्, सिट् सिट्, i. 1, Par. To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितता
शितता शित + ता (see शो), f. Sharpness, Śiś. 9, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिताभ्र
शिताभ्र शिताभ्र, see सिताभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति शिति,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Black, dark blue, Vikr. d. 151; Bhāg. P. 4, 4, 18.<BR> 2. White.<BR> II. m. The भूर्ज or birch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल शिथिल (cf. श्लथ्), adj.<BR> 1. Loose, Vikr. d. 115; Pañc. ii. d. 143; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a " target="_blank">Page0948-a + 42</a>] loosened, Megh. 69.<BR> 2. Flaccid, faded, Śāk. d. 41.<BR> 3. Feeble, languid, Bhartṛ. 2, 22.<BR> 4. Ineffective.<BR> 5. Relaxed, dissolved, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 5.<BR> 6. Not very careful, Pañc. ii. d. 82.<BR> 7. Not rigidly observed.<BR> 8. Loosely retained.<BR> 9. Abandoned, Ragh. 2, 41 (˚ली कृ, To abandon).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिथिल
अ- + शिथिल अ- + शिथिल, adj. tight, close, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0947-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलता
शिथिलता शिथिल + ता, f.<BR> 1. Looseness, state of dissolution, Pañc. 30, 11.<BR> 2. Relaxedness, relaxation.<BR> 3. Want of energy, Pañc. iv. d. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलय
शिथिलय शिथिलय, a denomin. derived from शिथिल, Par. To loosen, to make loose, Śāk. 9, 21.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शिथिलित (or शिथिल + इत).<BR> 1. Loosened, loosed, loose, Śāk. d. 57.<BR> 2. Relaxed, dissolved, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनि|शिनिः
शिनि शिनि, m. pl. The name of a class of Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफा
शिफा शिफा, f.<BR> 1. A fibrous root.<BR> 2. A lash with a whip, Man. 8, 369; 9, 230.<BR> 3. A river.<BR> 4. A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बि|शिम्बिः
शिम्बि and वी शिम्बी, f. A legume, a pod, Mālat. 145, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर|शिरं|शिरः
शिर शिर,<BR> I. i. e. curtailed शिरस्, n.<BR> 1. The head.<BR> 2. The root of the pepper plant.<BR> II. f. रा (cf. सिरा), Any vessel of the body, really, or supposed to be of a tubular form, as a nerve, Rām. 5, 32, 11; a vein.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिर
त्रि- + शिर त्रि- + शिर,<BR> I. adj. having three points, MBh. 13, 7379.<BR> II. m. the name of a Rākṣasa, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःस्थ|शिरःस्थः
शिरःस्थ शिरःस्थ, i. e. शिरस्-स्थ, adj. Borne on the head, Pañc. v. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस् शिरस् (for original शरस्, cf. Zend. शर, and शीर्ष), n. (the base of some cases is optionally शीर्षन्, i. e. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-b " target="_blank">Page0948-b + 43</a>] शिरस् + अन्),<BR> 1. The head, Pañc. iii. d. 193; शिरसा प्र-णि-पत्, To reverence by inclining one's head, Vikr. 3, 12; शिरसा कृ, To bear on one's head, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1847.<BR> 2. The top of a mountain, Kir. 5, 17; of a tree.<BR> 3. Chief, principal.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κάρα, κάρηνον, κρανίον; Lat. cere- in cerebrum, and cer- in cervix, (vix fron vincire, cf. शिरोधरा); A.S. haernes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्
अ- + शिरस् अ- + शिरस्, adj. headless, Man. 9, 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रशिरस्
अभ्र- + शिरस् अभ्र- + शिरस्, n. a head represented by the sky, Śiś. 9, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशिरस्
अश्व- + शिरस् अश्व- + शिरस्,<BR> I. n. the head of a horse, MBh. 3, 3083.<BR> II. adj. having the head of a horse, ib. 12, 13100.<BR> III. m. a proper name, ib. 1, 2531.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःशिरस्
उच्चैःशिरस् उच्चैःशिरस्, i. e. उच्चैस्-, adj. m. a man of high rank. Kumāras. 1, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालशिरस्
कपाल- + शिरस् कपाल- + शिरस्, Rām. 2, 54, 30 (= 2, 54, 32 Gorr., where कलाप-) ? perhaps a name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्चशिरस्|कूर्च्चशिरस्
कूर्च- + शिरस् कूर्च- + शिरस्, n. the upper part of the palm and ball of the foot, Suśr. 1, 345, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिरस्
त्रि- + शिरस् त्रि- + शिरस्,<BR> I. adj. having three heads, MBh. 5, 229.<BR> II. m. the name of an Asura and a Rākṣasa, ib. 9, 1755; Rām. 3, 29, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशिरस्
द्वि- + शिरस् द्वि- + शिरस्, adj. having two heads, Pañc. 251, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजशिरस्
भुज- + शिरस् भुज- + शिरस्, n. the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशिरस्
मृग- + शिरस् मृग- + शिरस्, n. the fifth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुमारशिरस्
शिशु-मार- + शिरस् शिशु-मार- + शिरस्, n. a part of the heaven studded with stars, the north-east point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिज|शिरसिजः
शिरसिज शिरस् + इ-ज, and शिरसिरुह् शिरस् + इ-रुह्, m. The hair of the head, Kir. 10, 52 (-ज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्क|शिरस्कं
शिरस्क शिरस् + क,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A helmet.<BR> 2. A turban, a cap.<BR> II. f. का, A palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्त्र|शिरस्त्रं
शिरस्त्र शिरस्-त्र (vb. त्रा), and शिरस्त्राण शिरस्-त्राण, n.<BR> 1. A helmet, Rājat. 5, 342; Ragh. 4, 64.<BR> 2. A turban, a cap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिराल|शिरालं
शिराल शिरा + ल (see शिर),<BR> I. adj., f. ला.<BR> 1. Veiny, showing the veins, Kāśīkh. 37, 14; Bhaṭṭ. 2, 30.<BR> 2. Showing [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a " target="_blank">Page0949-a + 42</a>] the tendons.<BR> II. n. An acid fruit, Averrhoa carambola.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0948-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरि|शिरिः
शिरि शिरि, i. e. शॄ + इ, m.<BR> 1. A sword.<BR> 2. An arrow.<BR> 3. A murderer.<BR> 4. A locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरीष|शिरीषः
शिरीष शिरीष (akin to the last),<BR> I. m. A tree, Acacia sirisa, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR> II. n. Its flower, Śāk. d. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधरा
शिरोधरा शिरोधरा, i. e. शिरस्-धृ + अ, f. The neck, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 23 (read ˚शिरोधरोद्देश˚).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकायशिरोधर
महा-काय-शिरोधर महा-काय-शिरोधर, adj. having a great body and neck, Rām. 3, 55, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधि|शिरोधिः
शिरोधि शिरोधि, i. e. शिरस्-धा (cf. निधि), f. The neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुह्
शिरोरुह् शिरोरुह्, i. e. शिरस्-रुह्, and शिरोरुह शिरोरुह, i. e. शिरस्-रुह् + अ, m. Hair, Pañc. iii. d. 193 (ह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्
† शिल् शिल्, सिल् सिल्, i. 6, Par. To glean (cf. the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल|शिलं|शिलः
शिल शिल,<BR> A. n. Gleaning ears of corn, Man. 3, 100; 10, 112.<BR> B. i. e. probably शो + ल,<BR> I. f. ला.<BR> 1. A stone, Pañc. 100, 18; a rock, Vikr. d. 49.<BR> 2. A flat stone on which condiments are ground.<BR> 3. Arsenic.<BR> II. f. ला and ली.<BR> 1. A stone or beam placed across a post or pillar.<BR> 2. The timber of a door frame.<BR> III. f. ली.<BR> 1. A dart, an arrow, Ragh. 7, 62.<BR> 2. An earth-worm.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डशिला|गंडशिला
गण्ड-शिला गण्ड-शिला, f. a large rock, Bhāg. P. 3, 13, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूपशिल
जात-रूप-शिल जात-रूप-शिल, m. the name of a (golden) mountain, Rām. 4, 14, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थशिला
तीर्थ-शिला तीर्थ-शिला, f. stone steps leading to a bathing-place, Śṛṅgārat. 1 (read ˚लम्, at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यशिला
बध्य- + शिला बध्य- + शिला, f. ला, rock of execution, Pañc. 52, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिल|मनःशिलः
मनःशिल मनःशिल, i. e. मनस्-, m., and f. ला, red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पशिला
स्वल्प-शिला स्वल्प-शिला, i. e. सु-अल्प-, f. a very small stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाटक|शिलाटकः
शिलाटक शिलाटक, m.<BR> 1. A room on the top of a house.<BR> 2. A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलि|शिलिः
शिलि and ली शिली̆ (cf. शिली, under शिल), f. The lower timber of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्र|शिलींध्र|शिलीन्ध्रं|शिलींध्रः|शिलीन्ध्रः
शिलीन्ध्र शिलीन्ध्र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A sort of tree.<BR> 2. A kind of fish.<BR> II. f. री.<BR> 1. Clay, earth.<BR> 2. A small earthworm (cf. शिली, under शिल).<BR> 3. A sort of bird.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Hail (cf. शिला).<BR> 2. A mushroom, Megh. 11.<BR> 3. The flower of the plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीपद|शिलीपदः
शिलीपद शिलीपद (a dialect. form of श्लीपद, q. cf.), m. A morbid enlargement of the leg, Lass. 94, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्प|शिल्पं
शिल्प शिल्प, n.<BR> 1. Proficiency in any manual or mechanical art, or profession; art, Pañc. i. d. 4, 446; Bhāg. P. 3, 23, 17; Chr. 51, 1; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 12.<BR> 2. A sort of spoon used at sacrifices to throw the butter into the fire.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशिल्प
कृत- + शिल्प कृत- + शिल्प, adj. one who has attained a knowledge of his art, Yājñ. 2, 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिक
शिल्पिक शिल्पिक, i. e. शिल्प + इक,<BR> I. adj. Manual, mechanic.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Handicraft.<BR> 2. (and शिस्पक शिल्प + क), A sort of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिन्
शिल्पिन् शिल्पिन्, i. e. शिल्प + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Belonging or relating to a mechanical profession or art.<BR> II. m., f. नी, and n. An artificer, a mechanic, Pañc. 10, 6; Johns. Sel. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिव|शिवं|शिवः
शिव शिव (probably akin to शवस्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Prosperous, Hit. 68, 17; auspicious, Mālat. 6, 12; happy.<BR> 2. Right, Nal. 20, 17.<BR> 3. 17.<BR> 3. Comparat. शिवतर, Very complacent, Utt. Rāmac. 145, 2.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva, a deity of the Hindu triad, Kir. 5, 21; dual, Śiva and his wife, ib. 5, 40.<BR> 2. The phallic emblem of Śiva.<BR> 3. An auspicious planetary conjunction.<BR> 4. The Vedas.<BR> 5. One of the astronomical periods termed योगस्.<BR> 6. A pillar to which cattle are tied.<BR> 7. A sort of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a " target="_blank">Page0950-a + 42</a>] perfume.<BR> III. f. वा.<BR> 1. Durgā, the wife of Śiva.<BR> 2. The female jackal, Sāv. 5, 75.<BR> 3. The name of several plants.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Happiness, Arj. 5, 19; bliss, Mālat. 160, 14.<BR> 2. Wellbeing, Pañc. 16, 5.<BR> 3. Final emancipation from separate existence.<BR> 4. Water.<BR> 5. Sea or fossile salt.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिव|अशिवः
अ- + शिव अ- + शिव,<BR> I. adj. inauspicious, Rām. 3, 29, 11.<BR> II. n. ill-luck, ib. 3, 30, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाशिव|सदाशिवः
सदा- + शिव सदा- + शिव, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0949-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवंकर|शिवङ्कर|शिवङ्करः
शिवंकर शिवंकर, i. e. शिव + म्-कृ + अ, adj. Auspicious, conferring happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवताति|शिवतातिः
शिवताति शिव + ताति, f. Benevolence, Mālat. 160, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवि|शिविः
शिवि शिवि, m.<BR> 1. A beast of prey.<BR> 2. The name of a king, Sāv. 2, 17; MBh. 13, 2046, sqq.; pl. his descendants, Draup. 8, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिविका शिविका, f.<BR> 1. A palanquin, a litter, Rām. 2, 60, 76, Seramp.<BR> 2. A tent, Johns. Sel. 9, 12; a marquee.<BR> 3. A proper name, MBh. 3, 13155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविर|शिविरं
शिविर शिविर,<BR> I. m. The name of a tribe(?), Rājat. 5, 176.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A camp.<BR> 2. A royal camp or residence.<BR> 3. A guard or defence for the soldiers.<BR> 4. A sort of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिर|शिशिरः
शिशिर शिशिर (akin to शो, cf. the ved. inflection of this vb.),<BR> I. adj. Cold, cool, Vikr. d. 41; comparat. Very cool, refreshing, Pañc. 9, 4.<BR> II. (m. and) n.<BR> 1. Cold, frost, Megh. 81.<BR> 2. Coolness, Vikr. 19, 17 (of a wood).<BR> 3. The cold season, Pañc. v. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशु|शिशुः
शिशु शिशु, i. e. reduplic. श्वि, m.<BR> 1. The young of man or any animal, Vikr. d. 121; Pañc. 160, 4; a child, Pañc. i. d. 241; a calf, Pañc. 182, 12; a pup, etc.<BR> 2. A boy.<BR> 3. A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक|शिशुकः
शिशुक शिशु + क, m.<BR> 1. A child, Pañc ii. d. 200.<BR> 2. A porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुता
शिशुता शिशु + ता, f., शिशुत्व शिशु + त्व, n. Childhood, Utt. Rāmac. 107, 6; Pañc. 220, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्न|शिश्नं|शिश्नः
शिश्न शिश्न, m. The penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
† 1. शिष् शिष्, i. 1, Par. To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
2. शिष् शिष्, ii. 7, शिनष्, शिंष्, Par. To leave; pass. To be left, MBh. 2, 1964.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शिष्ट.<BR> 1. Left, remaining.<BR> 2. Also sbst. Chief, Hit. 100, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. शेषय, To leave, to spare, MBh. 3, 14760.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, pass. To be left, MBh. 3, 2276. अवशिष्ट, Remaining, Hit. 61, 4, M.M.; remainder, Man. 3, 116; Hit. 103, 14 (अव-शिष्ट-बल, adj. With the rest of [my] army).<BR> --Caus. अवशेषित (perhaps अव-शेष + इत), Left, spared, MBh. 1, 5129.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, Caus. pass. समवशेषित, Left, spared, MBh. 1, 6337.<BR> --With उद् उद्, उच्छिष्ट,<BR> 1. Left, remainder, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 8.<BR> 2. Left behind, Rājat. 5, 11.<BR> 3. One who has a remnant of food in his mouth, Man. 2, 56; 4, 75. n. Remains, remainder of food, Man. 5, 140.<BR> --With निस् निस्, Caus. निःशेषित (perhaps rather निःशेष, i. e. निस्-शेष, + इत),<BR> 1. Used up entirely (without leaving any part), Rām. 1, 65, 6.<BR> 2. Exterminated, Pañc. 201, 22 (cf. my translation, n. 1210).<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To leave, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 93; with न, To destroy, Ragh. 12, 79.<BR> --With वि वि, To distinguish, to make distinguished, to augment, Mālat. 71, 8. Pass.<BR> 1. To be distinguished, Ragh. 17, 62.<BR> 2. To prefer, with abl. and instr., MBh. 3, 14735. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-a " target="_blank">Page0951-a + 44</a>] Pass.<BR> a. To be better than, Man. 2, 83; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1678 (मूर्ख-सहस्रेण प्राज्ञे एक वि शिष्यते, One wise man is better than a thousand fools); to be of more weight, Rām. 2, 35, 8.<BR> b. To be most preferable, best, Hit. iii. d. 50; to be pre-eminent, Man. 9, 297. विशिष्ट,<BR> 1. Having distinctive and exclusive properties, Bhāṣāp. 132.<BR> 2. Especial.<BR> 3. Endowed with, possessed of.<BR> 4. Distinguished, Hit. pr. 42, M.M.; superior, pre-eminent, Chr. 28, 15; best, Bhag. 1, 7.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. विशेष्य.<BR> 1. What is determinable or to be distinguished, Bhāṣāp. 131.<BR> 2. Principal, primary, chief. m. A substantive. n. The subject of a predicate.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To distinguish, MBh. 3, 16449.<BR> 2. To surpass, Chr. 44, 2.<BR> 3. To adorn, Mṛcch. 59, 14. विशेषित,<BR> 1. Distinguished, separated.<BR> 2. Excellent.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To increase, Utt. Rāmac. 102, 5.<BR> --With प्रतिवि प्रति-वि, प्रतिविशिष्ट, Better than (with abl.), MBh. 1, 4684.<BR> --Cf. Lat. quæso, quæro, quæstor, perhaps cura; Goth. qvisteins, qvistjan, fra-qvisteins, fra-qvistjan, fra-qvistnan, us-qvistjan, based on a noun qvist = *शिष् + ति, Leaving, abandoning; also us-haista, Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशिष्ट
विषम- + शिष्ट विषम- + शिष्ट, adj. unfair (division).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0950-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टि|शिष्टिः
शिष्टि शिष्टि, i. e. शास् + ति, f. An order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्यता
शिष्यता शिष्य + ता (see शास्), f. The state of a pupil, Pañc. 34, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी शी (cf. शद्), ii. 2, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 5, 63),<BR> 1. To lie (as on the ground), Daśak. in Chr. 187, 11.<BR> 2. To lie down, 187, 6.<BR> 3. To repose, MBh. 1, 5033.<BR> 4. To sleep, Man. 2, 163.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शयित, Lying, Śiś. 9, 39.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. शयनीय, Fit for sleeping, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-b " target="_blank">Page0951-b + 41</a>] lying on, Utt. Rāmac. 67, 3. n. A couch.<BR> --Caus. शायय,<BR> 1. To cause to lie, to throw, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 22.<BR> 2. To put, Rām. 2, 66, 16.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति,<BR> 1. To surpass, Ragh. 5, 14 (Calc.).<BR> 2. To sleep longer than (acc.), MBh. 3, 14686.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अन्-अति-शयरीय, adj. Not to be surpassed, Kir. 5, 52.<BR> --With अधि अधि,<BR> 1. To lie down on (acc.), Rām. 2, 88, 12.<BR> 2. To sleep on, Ragh. 5, 28 (Calc.).<BR> 3. To sleep, Pañc. 26, 25.<BR> 4. To inhabit, Bhaṭṭ. 10, 35.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To lie down, to sleep, near, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 4.<BR> --With आ आ, To sleep on, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> --With उप उप, To lie near (with acc.), Lass. 2. ed. 70, 51.<BR> --With निस् निस्, in निःशयान (rather शयान with निस्, adj.), Not sleeping, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 10.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To sleep opposite to (acc.), MBh. 3, 16300.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संशयान, and संशयित, Dubious, Chr. 31, 32 (Hit. iv. d. 19, read संशयितम्).<BR> --Cf. κεῖμαι, κεῖται (= शेते), κοίτη, κοιμάω, κῶμα, κώμη; Lat. quies, quiesco, civis; O.H.G. hîwî, matrimonium; A.S. hiwa, familia; O.H.G. hîwo, m. hîwa, f. conjux; hîwjan, hîjan, nubere; Goth. hêthjô (= κοίτη), haithi, campus, haims; O.H.G. haim; A.S. ham, haeman (cf. κοιμάω).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
1. शीक् शीक् or सीक् सीक् (probably better, cf. सिच्), i. 1, Ātm. To sprinkle, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
† 2. शीक् शीक्, सीक् सीक्, i. 1, Ātm. To go, to move.<BR> --i. 1, and 10, Par.<BR> 1. To be angry.<BR> 2. To endure patiently.<BR> 3. To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
† 3. शीक् शीक्, i. 10, Par. To speak, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0951-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकर|शीकरं|शीकरः
शीकर शीकर (cf. 1. शीक्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A drop of water, Ragh. 16, 62; of rain, Śāk. d. 166.<BR> 2. Thin rain, Ṛt. 1, 15; Kir. 5, 15 (also सीकर, MBh. 14, 2201).<BR> 3. Spray, Mālat. 147, 14.<BR> II. n. A sort of pine, or its resin.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशीकर|करशीकरः
कर- + शीकर कर- + शीकर and करिन्-, m. water expelled by an elephant's trunk, Kir. 16, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकरिन्
शीकरिन् शीकरिन्, i. e. शीकर + इन्, adj. Sprinkling, Utt. Rāmac. 63, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र|शीघ्रं
शीघ्र शीघ्र, adj.<BR> 1. Quick, speedy, Vikr. d. 140 (मण्डल-शीघ्र-चार, Turning round quickly).<BR> 2. Violent, Pañc. iii. d. 52.<BR> 3. ˚रम्, adv. Swiftly, Pañc. 128, 4. Comparat. ˚रतर + म्, adv. As quickly as possible, Pañc. 88, 6.<BR> --Cf. A.S. higian, To make haste; κιχάνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्
शीत् शीत्, An imitative sound expressing pleasure, Bhartṛ. 1, 49 (cf. सीत्), and trembling, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 738.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत शीत (probably an old ptcple. pf. pass. of शो),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cold, Hit. i. d. 79, M.M.; chilly.<BR> 2. A pathetic.<BR> 3. Idle.<BR> 4. Stupid.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Coldness, Pañc. 169, 14.<BR> 2. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अ- + शीत अ- + शीत, adj. hot, Bhāṣāp. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतता
शीतता शीत + ता, f. Coldness, Pañc. i. d. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतल|शीतलं|शीतलः
शीतल शीत + ल,<BR> I. adj. Cold, cool, Pañc. ii. d. 58; figurat., Vikr. d. 90. Comparat. ˚लतर, Cooler, Śiś. 9, 4.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The moon.<BR> 2. A sort of camphor.<BR> III. m., f. ला, and ली, and n. The name of several plants.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Coldness.<BR> 2. A pearl.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतल
अ- + शीतल अ- + शीतल, adj. hot, Śiś. 9, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशीतल
अति- + शीतल अति- + शीतल, adj. very cool, Hit. iii. d. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीतल|सुशीतलं
सु- + शीतल सु- + शीतल, adj. very cool, Hit. i. d. 96, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशीतल
हिम- + शीतल हिम- + शीतल, adj. very cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्कार|शीत्कारः
शीत्कार शीत्-कार, m.<BR> 1. Making the sound शित्, sighing on account of pleasure.<BR> 2. A frown. Amar. 31 (Sch.). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b " target="_blank">Page0952-b + 40</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशीत्कारम्
स-शीत्कार + म् स-शीत्कार + म्, adv. with sighs, Vikr. d. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु शीधु, m. and n. Rum distilled from molasses, intoxicating spirits, Śiś. 9, 87; wine, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322 (cf. सीधु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन शीन, see श्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्
† शीभ् शीभ्, i. 1, Ātm. To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर|शीरः
शीर शी + र, m. A snake, boa-constrictor, Pañc. 203, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णता
शीर्णता शीर्ण + ता, f., and शीर्णत्व शीर्ण + त्व, n. (vb. शॄ), Emaciation, withering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्वि|शीर्व्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्वि शीर्वि, i. e. शॄ + वि, adj. Hurtful, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ष|शीर्षं
शीर्ष शीर्ष, i. e. curtailed शीर्षन् (cf. शिरस्), n. The head, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 2 (-छेद्य, adj. One who must be beheaded), Bhartṛ. 2, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. and A.S. hals; Lat. collum; see शिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशीर्ष|गोशीर्षं|गोशीर्षः
गो- + शीर्ष गो- + शीर्ष,<BR> I. adj. shaped like a cow's head, MBh. 7, 8097.<BR> II. n. a kind of sandal, Rām. 4, 41, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्ष|त्रिशीर्षः
त्रि- + शीर्ष त्रि- + शीर्ष, adj. having three heads, MBh. 1, 2162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशीर्ष
दशशीर्ष दशशीर्ष, i. e. दशन्-, m. 1. a name of Rāvaṇa, Rām. 4, 10, 22. 2. a spell, ib. 1, 30, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशीर्ष
पञ्च- + शीर्ष पञ्च- + शीर्ष, adj. having five heads, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वशीर्ष
पूर्व- + शीर्ष पूर्व- + शीर्ष, adj. f. षा, with the head turned to the east, MBh. 13, 463.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशीर्ष|मृगशीर्षं|मृगशीर्षः
मृग- + शीर्ष मृग- + शीर्ष, m. the fifth lunar mansion, Lass. 16, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षक|शीर्षकं|शीर्षकः
शीर्षक शीर्ष + क,<BR> I. m. Rāhu.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The skull.<BR> 2. A helmet.<BR> 3. Judgment, sentence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशीर्षिका
स्थूल-शीर्षिका स्थूल-शीर्षिका, f. a small ant with a large head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्य|शीर्षण्यः
शीर्षण्य शीर्षण्य, i. e. शीर्षन् + य,<BR> I. m. Clean and unentangled hair.<BR> II. n. A helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षन्
शीर्षन् शीर्षन् (see शिरस्), A substitute [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a " target="_blank">Page0953-a + 46</a>] for शिरस्, as latter part of some comp. words, and in some derivatives; e. g. सहस्र-, adj. Thousand-headed, Johns. Sel. 91, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0952-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील्
शील् शील् (probably a denomin. derived from the next), i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To meditate.<BR> 2. To adore, to worship.<BR> --Caus., and i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To make, Gīt. 9, 6.<BR> 2. To practise, Mṛcch. 34, 19.<BR> 3. To visit, Gīt. 7, 4.<BR> 4. To worship, MBh. 1, 3207.<BR> 5. To put on, to dress, Gīt. 5, 11.<BR> 6. † To repeat.<BR> 7. † To surpass.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शीलित, Skilled, conversant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील शील, i. e.<BR> A. शिष् + ल (m. and) n.<BR> 1. Nature, quality. MBh. 1, 4054.<BR> 2. Disposition, inclination, character, Pañc. i. d. 282; a good character, Pañc. v. d. 2.<BR> 3. Moral practice, Man. 2, 6.<BR> 4. Good conduct, Johns. Sel. 13, 45.<BR> 5. Virtue, Bhartṛ. 2, 77.<BR> 6. Beauty.<BR> B. शी + ल, m. A large snake.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशील
अ- + शील अ- + शील, adj. wicked, Kir. 11, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादनशील
अभि-वादन- + शील अभि-वादन- + शील, adj. one who habitually salutes, Man. 2, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणशील
गुण- + शील गुण- + शील, adj. virtuous, Hit. i. d. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशील|दानशीलः
दान- + शील दान- + शील, adj. liberal, Yājñ. 3, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्शील
दुस्- + शील दुस्- + शील, adj. wicked, Rām. 3, 2, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखशील
दुःख- + शील दुःख- + शील, adj. austere, MBh. 4, 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशील|धर्म्मशील|धर्म्मशीलः
धर्म- + शील धर्म- + शील, adj. just, virtuous, Indr. 1, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशील
पुण्य- + शील पुण्य- + शील, adj. virtuous, MBh. 5, 6011.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसशील
मांस- + शील मांस- + शील, adj. fleshy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगयाशील
मृगया- + शील मृगया- + शील, adj. attached to hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशील
यज्ञ- + शील यज्ञ- + शील, adj. sbst. a sacrificer, Man. 11, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
वि- + शील वि- + शील, adj. not observing approved usages, Man. 5, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशील
विषम- + शील विषम- + शील, adj. uneven, difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिशील
शान्ति- + शील शान्ति- + शील, m. a proper name, Lass. 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशील
साधु- + शील साधु- + शील, adj. virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशील|सुशीलः
सु- + शील सु- + शील,<BR> I. adj. 1. well disposed, of good disposition. 2. well made, Pañc. ii. d. 74.<BR> II. f. ला, the wife of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानशील
स्नान- + शील स्नान- + शील, adj. bathing, observing ablations, Hit. 18, 7, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलतस्
शीलतस् शील + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. By natural disposition, Pañc. i. d. 288.<BR> 2. Concerning the character, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलता
ऽशीलता -शील + ता, f. in त्याग-, Generosity, Hit. i. d. 104, M.M. शालीन-, f. Bashfulness, Utt. Rāmac. 173, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवन्त्|शीलवत्
शीलवन्त् शील + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Of a good disposition, Ragh. 10, 71.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिशीलवन्त्|श्रुतिशीलवत्
श्रुति- + शीलवन्त् श्रुति- + शीलवन्त्, adj. one who is learned in the Vedas, Man. 3, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन् शी + वन्,<BR> I. m. The boaconstrictor.<BR> II. f. वरी, An iguana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु शु, see स्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्
† शुक् शुक्, i. 1. Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक|शुकं|शुकः
शुक शुक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A parrot, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR> II. m. and n. The name of several plants.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A turban.<BR> 2. The hem of a cloth.<BR> 3. Cloth.<BR> 4. A sort of perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहशुक|गृहशुकः
गृह- + शुक गृह- + शुक, m. 1. a parrot kept in a house, Amar. 13. 2. a poet maintained by a prince, Rājat. 5, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त शुक्त,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Sour, acid.<BR> 2. Harsh.<BR> 3. i. e. 2. शुच् + त, Clean, pure.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A preparation which has become acid by undergoing fermentation, as vinegar, etc., Man. 2, 177; 4, 211; 11, 153.<BR> 2. Sour gruel.<BR> 3. Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तक|शुक्तकं
शुक्तक शुक्त + क (n.), Sour eructation, Man. 4, 121 (Lois.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ति|शुक्तिः
शुक्ति शुक्ति, i. e. 2. शुच् + ति, f.<BR> 1. A pearl oyster, Pañc. i. d. 280.<BR> 2. A conch.<BR> 3. A small shell.<BR> 4. A portion of the skull used as a cup.<BR> 5. A curl or feather on a horse's neck or breast.<BR> 6. A disease of the cornea.<BR> 7. A sort of perfume.<BR> 8. A weight of two कर्षस्.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ति|महाशुक्तिः
महा- + शुक्ति महा- + शुक्ति, f. the pearl oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिज|शुक्तिजं
शुक्तिज शुक्ति-ज (vb. जन्), n. A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्र|शुक्रं|शुक्रः
शुक्र शुक्र, i. e. 2. शुच् + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Resplendent, Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 48, 14.<BR> 2. Pure, Windischmann, Sankara, 68.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A name of Agni.<BR> 2. The planet Venus, Pañc. pr. d. 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a " target="_blank">Page0954-a + 43</a>]<BR> 3. The month Jyeṣṭhā (May--June), Hiḍ. 1, 10.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Semen virile, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 13; MBh. 1, 2434; male and female strength, Man. 3, 49.<BR> 2. A morbid affection of the iris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0953-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रल
शुक्रल शुक्र + ल, adj. Spermatic, augmenting the seminal secretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ल|शुक्लं|शुक्लः
शुक्ल शुक्ल, i. e. 2. शुच् + ल,<BR> I. adj. White, Pañc. i. d. 39; bright, i. d. 104; Man. 1, 66 (with पक्ष, the fortnight of the month in which the moon increases).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. One of the astronomical योगस्.<BR> 3. The light half of the month from new to full moon. Bhag. 8, 24; Rājat. 5, 412.<BR> III. f. ला, A name of Sarasvatī.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Silver.<BR> 2. Fresh butter.<BR> 3. A disease of the cornea.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशुक्ल
पञ्चशुक्ल पञ्चशुक्ल, i. e. पञ्चन्-, m. a certain poisonous insect, Suśr. 2, 288, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ला
महा-शुक्ला महा-शुक्ला, f. Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लाभिजातीय
शुक्लाभिजातीय शुक्लाभिजातीय, i. e. शुक्ल-अभि-जन् + ति + ईय, adj. Of a pure race, Rām. 6, 10, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्षि|शुक्षिः
शुक्षि शुक्षि, m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्ग|शुंग|शुंगः|शुङ्गः
शुङ्ग शुङ्ग,<BR> I. m. The Indian figtree, Windischmann, Sankara, 179.<BR> II. f. गा, The sheath of a young bud (cf. Atharv.-Ved. viii. 7, 4, at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
1. शुच् शुच्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 4, 488),<BR> 1. To be afflicted, to grieve, Man. 3, 57.<BR> 2. To grieve for, to bewail, Pañc. i. d. 379.<BR> 3. To regret, to repent, Pañc. 118, 6.<BR> 4. To be absorbed in deep meditation, Lass. 2. ed. 42, 11, cf. 9.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शुचित, Sad, lamenting.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. अ-शोच्य, adj. Not to be grieved for, Pañc. i. d. 379; 475.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To afflict. MBh. 4, 581.<BR> 2. To bewail, MBh. 1, 5649.<BR> --With the prep. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b " target="_blank">Page0954-b + 43</a>] अनु अनु, To bewail, Bhag. 2, 11; Pañc. i. d. 475.<BR> --Caus. The same, MBh. 2, 2594.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To be much afflicted, MBh. 1, 4025.<BR> 2. To bewail, MBh. 3, 13656.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, To bewail, MBh. 1, 3229.<BR> --Cf. Goth. hiufan, queri; A.S. heaf, heofian; O.H.G. huvo, ulula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
2. शुच् शुच्, i. 4, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To shine, to be pure (ved.).<BR> 2. † To be wet.<BR> 3. † To be fetid. Ptcple of the fut. pass. शोच्य.<BR> 1. To be purified.<BR> 2. Wicked, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To make pure, Kathās. 19, 84, दूषितं तृणतोयादि प्रतियोगैर् अशोचयत्, He made pure (i. e. he restored to their former state), by antidotes, food, water, etc., which were spoiled (i. e. poisoned).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुच्
अ- + शुच् अ- + शुच्, adj. innocent, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
3. शुच् 1. शुच्, f.<BR> 1. Sorrow, Hit. i. d. 133, M.M.; grief, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 14.<BR> 2. Calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचन्ति
शुचन्ति शुचन्ति, m. A proper name, Chr. 296, 7 = Rigv. i. 112, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि 2. शुच् + इ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. White, resplendent, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322.<BR> 2. Clear (as a jewel), Utt. Rāmac. 35, 18.<BR> 3. Gentle (cf. शुचि-स्मित, s. v. स्मि).<BR> 4. Clean, Bhartṛ. 2, 17; purified.<BR> 5. Pure, Man. 1, 76; pious.<BR> 6. Exempt from passion.<BR> 7. Honest, upright, Rām. 3, 53, 12; Pañc. 191, 13.<BR> 8. Free from fault, Pañc. i. d. 215.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. Purity, virtue, correctness.<BR> 3. Purification by ablution.<BR> 4. Judicial acquittal.<BR> 5. A faithful and tried minister.<BR> 6. The month Jyeṣṭha (May--June), and Āṣāḍha (June--July), i. e. the hot season, Ragh. 3, 3; Rājat. 5, 477; Hiḍ. 1, 10.<BR> 7. The sun.<BR> 8. The moon.<BR> 9. Fire.<BR> 10. The planet Venus.<BR> 11. Śiva.<BR> 12. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 13. Oblation [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a " target="_blank">Page0955-a + 40</a>] to fire at the first feeding of an infant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचि|अशुचिः
अ- + शुचि अ- + शुचि, adj. impure, Hit. ii. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाशुचि
उपधा- + शुचि उपधा- + शुचि, adj. free from deceit, Hit. iii. d. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0954-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित्व
शुचित्व शुचि + त्व, n. Purity, Hit. i. d. 95, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य्
† शुच्य् शुच्य्, चुच्य् चुच्य्, i. 1, Par. To express or squeeze out. शुक्त, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीरता
शुटीरता *शुटीर + ता, and शुटीर्य शुतीर्य, i. e. *शुटीर + य, n. Heroism, prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ्
† शुठ् शुठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be lame.<BR> 2. To prevent.<BR> --i. 10, Par. To be lazy (cf. 1. शठ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्|शुंठ्
† शुण्ठ् शुण्ठ्, i. 1, Par. To be lame.<BR> --i. 1. and 10, Par. To be dried or desiccated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुंठिः|शुण्ठिः
शुण्ठि, ठी शुण्ठी̆, f., and शुण्ठ्य शुण्ठ्य, n. Dry ginger, Pañc. 262, 13 (य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड्|शुंड्
† शुण्ड् शुण्ड्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To break.<BR> 2. To vex, to torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड|शुंड|शुंडः|शुण्डः
शुण्ड शुण्ड,<BR> I. m. The exudation from an elephant's temples.<BR> II. f. डा.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 2. A tavern.<BR> 3. An elephant's trunk, Pañc. 165, 1.<BR> 4. The stalk of the lotus.<BR> 5. A whore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुंडकः|शुण्डकः
शुण्डक शुण्डक (cf. the last), m. A distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुंडारः|शुण्डारः
शुण्डार शुण्डार (cf. शुण्ड), m.<BR> 1. A distiller.<BR> 2. An elephant's trunk, Mahāvīrac. 17, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिका|शुंडिका
शुण्डिका शुण्डिका, f. The soft palate.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डिका|गलशुंडिका
गल- + शुण्डिका गल- + शुण्डिका, f. 1. the uvula or the soft palate, Yājñ. 3, 98. 2. swelling of the kernels of the throat, Suśr. 1, 90, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डी
शुण्डी शुण्डी in कण्ठ्-, f. Swelling of the kernels of the throat, Suśr. 1, 306, 5 (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धता
शुद्धता शुद्ध + ता (vb. शुध्), f. Purity, Pañc. iv. d. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्त|शुद्धांत|शुद्धान्तः
शुद्धान्त शुद्धान्त, i. e. शुद्ध-अन्त, m.<BR> 1. The private or women's apartments, Vikr. d. 43; Utt. Rāmac. 25, 4 (-चारिन्, m., add. s. v. चारिन्, A servant of the private apartments).<BR> 2. The king's wife or concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धि|शुद्धिः
शुद्धि शुद्धि, i. e. शुध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Cleaning, cleansing.<BR> 2. Purity, purification, Pañc. iii. d. 119.<BR> 3. Correctness, truth, Mālat. 50, 14; certainty, Lass. 22, 11.<BR> 4. Acquittal.<BR> 5. Covering (of expenses), Pañc. 251, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशुद्धि
अग्नि- + शुद्धि अग्नि- + शुद्धि, f. purification by fire, passing the fiery ordeal, Utt. Rāmac. 5, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यशुद्धि|द्रव्यशुद्धिः
द्रव्य- + शुद्धि द्रव्य- + शुद्धि, f. purification of inanimate things, Man. 5, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरशुद्धि|वैरशुद्धिः
वैर- + शुद्धि वैर- + शुद्धि, f. revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध्
शुध् शुध् (probably for original श्वध्), i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To be purified, Man. 3, 132; Pañc. i. d. 307.<BR> 2. To become pure, Man. 5, 63.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शुद्ध.<BR> 1. Pure, Hit. d. 78, M.M.<BR> 2. White.<BR> 3. Faultless, genuine, Mālav. d. 30.<BR> 4. Innocent.<BR> 5. Acquitted.<BR> 6. Authorised.<BR> 7. Alone, Megh. 88; only, mere, simple.<BR> 8. Whetted. n.<BR> 1. Pure spirit.<BR> 2. Rock-salt.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. act. शुद्धवन्त्, f. वती; nom. pl. वत्जस्, Man. 11, 249, designates a holy text beginning शुद्धवत्यस्.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To purify, Man. 9, 282.<BR> 2. To explain, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 4.<BR> 3. To examine, to investigate, Pañc. 42, 11. शोधित, Purified, excused, Man. 8, 202.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, Caus.<BR> 1. To clean, to secure, Rām. 2, 31, 25.<BR> 2. To solve, to explain, Gīt. 12, 28.<BR> --With वि वि, To be purified, Man. 5, 66. विशुद्ध,<BR> 1. Pure, Pañc. pr. d. 9.<BR> 2. Faultless, Mālav. 21, 8; Hit. pr. d. 23, M.M. (वंश-, regarding, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a " target="_blank">Page0956-a + 40</a>] the bambu, of which it is made, viz. a bow).<BR> 3. White, Ṛt. 6, 34.<BR> 4. Corrected.<BR> 5. Pious, virtuous.<BR> 6. Humble, modest.<BR> 7. Settled, Man. 8, 201.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. wicked, Rājat. 5, 315.<BR> --Caus. To purify, MBh. 3, 15979.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संश्व्द्ध,<BR> 1. Purified, expiated, Bhag. 6, 45.<BR> 2. Clean.<BR> 3. Refined.<BR> 4. Acquitted (as a debt, or of a crime).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To purify, Rājat. 5, 89.<BR> 2. To secure, Man. 7, 185.<BR> 3. To cover (as expenses), MBh. 2, 204.<BR> 4. To examine, Man. 7, 219.<BR> --Cf. शुन्ध्; καθαρός; probably Lat. castus; O.H.G. haitar, screnus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्ध|अशुद्धं
अ- + शुद्ध अ- + शुद्ध, adj. impure, wicked, Pañc. i. d. 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशुद्ध
अति- + शुद्ध अति- + शुद्ध, very pure, Hit. i. d. 198, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0955-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्
† शुन् शुन्, i. 6, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन|शुनः
शुन शुन, i. e. श्वन् + अ, m. A dog. शुनी, see s. v. श्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनक|शुनकः
शुनक शुन + क, m. A dog, a young dog, Rām. 1, 61, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनःशेप|शुनःशेपः
शुनःशेप शुनःशेप (ved.), and शुनःशेफ शुनःशेफ (Rām. 1, 61, 19), i. e. श्वन् + अस्-शेप, or -शेफ, m. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनाशीर|शुनाशीरः
शुनाशीर शुनाशीर, and शुनासीर शुनासीर (so in the Vedas), m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनि|शुनिः
शुनि शुनि, i. e. श्वन् + इ, m. A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्|शुंध्
शुन्ध् शुन्ध् (cf. शुध्), i. 1, Par. To purify. Ātm. To be purified.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्यु|शुंध्युः|शुन्ध्युः
शुन्ध्यु शुन्ध् + यु,<BR> I. adj. Purifying, Chr. 289, 9 = Rigv. i. 50, 9.<BR> II. m. A name of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
1. शुभ् शुभ् (probably for original श्वभ्, cf. शुध्; see also शुम्भ्, s. v. 2. शुभ्), i. 1, Ātm., i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To shine, Chr. 40, 9.<BR> 2. To be splendid, Rām. 2, 47, 17.<BR> 3. To be beautiful, MBh. 4, 49.<BR> 4. To be gay or happy, Pañc. iii. d. 226.<BR> 5. † To hurt, to kill Ved. infin. शुभे, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b " target="_blank">Page0956-b + 42</a>] Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4.<BR> --Caus. शोभय, To cause to shine, to adorn, Rām. 2, 96, 31.<BR> --Ved. Caus. शुभय, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3.<BR> शोभित, Trimmed, Hit. iii. d. 27.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, To shine, Pañc. i. d. 85.<BR> --Caus. To adorn, Rām. 1, 5, 16; Pañc. 159, 20.<BR> --With वि वि, To shine, Hit. ii. d. 71.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus. To adorn, Ṛt. 6, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
† 2. शुभ् शुभ्, शुम्भ् शुम्भ्, सुभ् सुभ्, सुम्भ् सुम्भ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To speak, to shine.<BR> 2. To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ शुभ् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. भा.<BR> 1. Splendid, Lass. 2. ed. 72, 5; beautiful, Pañc. iii. d. 185. Comparat. शुभतर, Very beautiful, Pañc. 226, 5.<BR> 2. Distinguished, Lass. 2. ed. 59, 10.<BR> 3. Learned.<BR> 4. Happy, Hit. i. d. 5, M.M.; good, Pañc. iii. d. 106; virtuous, i. d. 150.<BR> II. m. One of the astrological Yogas.<BR> III. f. भा.<BR> 1. A female friend of the goddess Umā, Rām. 3, 52, 26.<BR> 2. Bambu manna.<BR> 3. Bent grass.<BR> IV. n. Happiness, hail, Hit. 54, 17.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभ|अशुभं
अ- + शुभ अ- + शुभ, adj. 1. wicked, Pañc. i. d. 403. 2. inauspicious, Lass. 16, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाशुभ
शुभाशुभ शुभाशुभ, i. e. शुभ-अ-शुभ, adj. good or wicked, Pañc. ii. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंभावुक
शुभंभावुक शुभंभावुक, i. e. शुभ + म्-भू + उक, adj. Resplendent, Lass. 67, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु शुभंयु, i. e. शुभ + म् + यु, adj. Happy, prosperous, Ragh. 8, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र शुभ् + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. White, Megh. 53; Lass. 4, 17.<BR> 2. Shining, bright, Chr. 291, 3 = Rigv. i. 85, 3; Pañc. i. d. 252.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. Sandal, Padmap. 3, 4.<BR> III. f. रा.<BR> 1. The Ganges.<BR> 2. Crystal. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a " target="_blank">Page0957-a + 39</a>]<BR> 3. Bambu manna.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Silver.<BR> 2. Talc.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुभ्र|महाशुभ्रं
महा- + शुभ्र महा- + शुभ्र, n. silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0956-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रत्व
शुभ्रत्व शुभ्र + त्व, n. Whiteness, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1915.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रि|शुभ्रिः
शुभ्रि शुभ् + रि, m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ्|शुंभ्
शुम्भ् शुम्भ् (cf. 2. शुभ्), i. 6, Par. (ved. also Ātm.) To shine.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Ātm. To assume as ornament, to adorn one's self with (acc.), Chr. 295, 10 = Rigv. i. 92, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Ātm. To adorn one's self carefully, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1.<BR> --Cf. probably, A.S. camb: O.H.G. kamp; κομψός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क्
† शुल्क् शुल्क्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To create.<BR> 2. To gain.<BR> 3. To abandon.<BR> 4. To speak (cf. श्वल्क्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क|शुल्कं|शुल्कः
शुल्क शुल्क, m. and n.<BR> 1. Toll, tax, duty, Man. 10, 120.<BR> 2. Money given at the purchase of anything, to ratify the bargain.<BR> 3. Money given to the parents of the bride, originally as purchase-price, cf. MBh. 13, 2422, sqq. and 4530; Man. 3, 51.<BR> 4. A nuptial present, Man. 9, 93.<BR> 5. The profits of household labour, care of milch cattle, etc., when considered as the legal property of the wife.<BR> 6. Price, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणशुल्क
गुण-, धन- + शुल्क गुण-, धन- + शुल्क, विर्य-, adj., f. का, having as its price, i. e. to be purchase by, good qualities, money, prowess, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 24; 191, 1, and Chr. 4, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनशुल्क
गुण-, धन- + शुल्क गुण-, धन- + शुल्क, विर्य-, adj., f. का, having as its price, i. e. to be purchase by, good qualities, money, prowess, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 24; 191, 1, and Chr. 4, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व|शुल्वं
शुल्व शुल्व, n.<BR> 1. Copper.<BR> 2. A rope.<BR> 3. Institute, law.<BR> 4. A sacrificial observance.<BR> 5. A quantity of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्वारि|शुल्वारिः
शुल्वारि शुल्वारि, m. Sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषक|शुश्रूषकः
शुश्रूषक शुश्रूषक, i. e. शुश्रूष, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b " target="_blank">Page0957-b + 42</a>] desider. of श्रु, + अक,<BR> I. adj. Obedient, Lass. 41, 14.<BR> II. m. A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषण|शुश्रूषणं
शुश्रूषण शुश्रूषण, i. e. चुश्रूष, see the last, + अन, n. Obedience, MBh. 1, 741.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषा
शुश्रूषा शुश्रूषा, i. e. शुश्रूष, see the last, + अ, f.<BR> 1. Wishing to hear.<BR> 2. Obedience, Lass. 41, 7.<BR> 3. Service, Man. 1, 91; 2, 112; Pañc. 214, 19; reverence, Man. 2, 229.<BR> 4. Speaking.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशुश्रूषा
अग्नि- + शुश्रूषा अग्नि- + शुश्रूषा, f. attention to the sacred fires, Man. 2, 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणशुश्रूषा
चरण- + शुश्रूषा चरण- + शुश्रूषा, f. prostration, Rām. 3, 14, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशुश्रूषा
परि- + शुश्रूषा परि- + शुश्रूषा, f. complete obedience, Lass. 41, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशुश्रूषा
पाद- + शुश्रूषा पाद- + शुश्रूषा, f. obedience, Hariv. 12585.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषु
शुश्रूषु शुश्रूषु, i. e. शुश्रूष, see the last, + उ, adj. Obedient, attentive, Man. 2, 109; MBh. 1, 740.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्
शुष् शुष् (for सुष्, and that for original सुस्; श् for स्, by the assimilating influence of ष्), i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 96, 34),<BR> 1. To become dry, literally and figuratively, Rām. 2, 69, 19; MBh. 2, 1685; 3, 591.<BR> 2. To be withered, to be afflicted, Draup. 6, 11.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शुष्क.<BR> 1. Dried up, Pañc. 51, 5; dry, Pañc. ii. d. 96.<BR> 2. Causeless, Pañc. 172, 1.<BR> 3. Unprofitable.<BR> 4. Offensive, Man. 11, 35.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To dry up, Pañc. i. d. 117; MBh. 3, 189.<BR> 2. To emaciate, Man. 6, 24.<BR> 3. To destroy, Gīt. 12, 5.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To dry up, Rām. 2, 64, 65.<BR> 2. To emaciate, Chr. 57, 23.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To become dried up, Bhaṭṭ. 16, 17.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus.<BR> 1. To dry up, MBh. 3, 12874.<BR> 2. To emaciate, MBh. 1, 4624.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To become dried up and withered, Rām. 2, 30, 25.<BR> 2. To be afflicted, Chr. 12, 25. परि-शुष्क, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a " target="_blank">Page0958-a + 39</a>]<BR> 1. Completely dry, Rām. 2, 59, 9.<BR> 2. Withered.<BR> 3. Emaciated, Rām. 4, 16, 35.<BR> --Caus. To emaciate, Pañc. 182, 11.<BR> --With वि वि, विशुष्क,<BR> 1. Very dry, thirsty, Ṛt. 1, 15<BR> 2. Withered, Mālat. 78, 4.<BR> --Caus. To dry up, MBh. 3, 10767.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To be dried up, MBh. 1, 8230. संशुष्क, Completely dry, Ṛt. 1, 22.<BR> --Caus. To dry up, Ragh. 6, 36.<BR> --Cf. σαυσαρός, σαυκός (= शुष्क for सुस् + क), σαυχμός, αὐχμός, σαχνός, αὔω, αὖος, αὐστηρός; Lat. siccus (= शुष्क for सुस् + क); Goth. siuk; A.S. seoc, seac, sioc, sic; O.H.G. siuh, siuchî, siuhjan; Goth. sauht; A.S. and O.H.G. suht.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0957-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष|शुषः
शुष शुष् + अ, m., and शुषि or षी शुष् + ई̆,<BR> 1. Drying.<BR> 2. A hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिर|शुषिरं|शुषिरः
शुषिर शुष् + इर,<BR> I. adj. Perforated (cf. शुष).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. A rat.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A hole.<BR> 2. A wind instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिल|शुषिलः
शुषिल शुष् + इल, m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्क|शुष्कः
शुष्क शुष्क, see शुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कल|शुष्कलं|शुष्कलः
शुष्कल शुष्क + ल, m., f. ला, and ली, and n. Dry flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्ण|शुष्णः
शुष्ण शुष्ण, i. e. शुष् + न, m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्म|शुष्मं|शुष्मः
शुष्म शुष् + म,<BR> I. adj. Strong, Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. Fire.<BR> 3. Wind.<BR> III. n. Light.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशुष्म
अन्-अन्त- + शुष्म अन्-अन्त- + शुष्म, adj. always roaring, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मन्
शुष्मन् शुष् + मन्,<BR> I. m. Fire.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Light, lustre.<BR> 2. Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मिन्
शुष्मिन् शुष्मिन्, i. e. शुष्म + इन्, adj. Strong, Hiḍ. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक|शूकं|शूकः
शूक शूक, m. and n.<BR> 1. The awn [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b " target="_blank">Page0958-b + 42</a>] of barley.<BR> 2. A bristle, a spicula.<BR> 3. Compassion.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यशूक|शस्यशूकं
शस्य- + शूक शस्य- + शूक, n. the beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित शित (or सित-), m. 1. barley. 2. wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकर|शूकरः
शूकर शूकर, m. A hog, Hit. 57, 12, M.M. f. री, A sow. Cf. सूकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्र|शूद्रः
शूद्र शूद्र,<BR> I. m.A man of the fourth caste, Man. 1, 31; 116; Hit. iv. d. 21.<BR> II. f. रा, A woman of that caste.<BR> III. f. री, or राणी, The wife of a Śūdra.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशूद्र|महाशूद्रः
महा- + शूद्र महा- + शूद्र, m. a cowherd. f. री, a milk-woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रक|शूद्रकः
शूद्रक शूद्र + क, m. A proper name, Lass. 28, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रता
शूद्रता शूद्र + ता, f., and शूद्रत्व शूद्र + त्व, n. The nature or condition of a Śūdra, Man. 2, 168 (त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून शून,<BR> I. see श्वि.<BR> II. (cf. सुन), f. ना.<BR> 1. A slaughter-house, Man. 4, 85; Mālav. 25, 2; cf. the next.<BR> 2. The soft palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूनाचक्रध्वजवन्त्
शूनाचक्रध्वजवन्त् शूना-चक्र-ध्वज + वन्त्, adj. One who has a slaughter-house, or an oil-press, or a vintner's flag, Man. 4, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूनास्थ
शूनास्थ शूना-स्थ, adj. Being in, brought from, a slaughter-house, Man. 11, 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्य|शून्यं|शून्यः
शून्य शून्य (probably for original श्वन्य, vb. श्वि),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Empty, void, Vikr. 66, 1; vacant, Mālat. 11, 8; ruined, Rām. 2, 13, 16.<BR> 2. Deprived of, with instr., Bhāṣāp. 69 (read शून्या सिद्धिर्); Vikr. d. 130 (as former part of a comp. Without, Pañc. 208, 22; figurat., Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 249).<BR> 3. Unsuspicious, Rām. 3, 50, 24.<BR> 4. Unmeaning, indifferent, Pañc. 117, 14.<BR> 5. Lonely, Pañc. 231, 18 (शून्ये, secretly); desert, Rām. 3, 51, 17 (n. in the lonely place).<BR> II. f. या, A hollow reed.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A vacuum.<BR> 2. Heaven.<BR> 3. A dot. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a " target="_blank">Page0959-a + 42</a>]<BR> 4. A cypher.<BR> 5. Absolute vacuity or rather nonentity, a principle of the Bauddha metaphysics, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κενεός, κεννός, κενός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्य
अ- + शून्य अ- + शून्य, adj. full, performed, Śāk. 24, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धिशून्य
अन्यथा-सिद्धि- + शून्य अन्यथा-सिद्धि- + शून्य, adj. free from superfluous determination (as a cause), Bhāṣāp. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशून्य
परि- + शून्य परि- + शून्य, adj. completely empty, or void of, Ragh. 8, 65; 19, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वशून्य
सर्व- + शून्य सर्व- + शून्य, adj. completely empty, Hit. i. d. 125, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0958-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यता
शून्यता शून्य + ता, f., and शून्यत्व शून्य + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Emptiness, Lass. 72, 10 (ता).<BR> 2. Unreality.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृशून्यता
मातृ- + शून्यता मातृ- + शून्यता, f. condition of having no mother, Cāṇ. 49 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यवत्
शून्यवत् शून्य + वत्, adv. Like a cypher, annihilated, Daśak. in. Chr. 183, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्
† शूर् शूर्, सूर् सूर्, i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To hurt or kill.<BR> 2. To be firm.<BR> --i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Ātm.<BR> 1. To be valiant.<BR> 2. To make great exertion. विसूरित, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर शूर, i. e. *शवन् (for शवस्), + अ (with र् for न्), m.<BR> 1. A hero, Hit. i. d. 71, M.M.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. A lion.<BR> 4. A boar.<BR> 5. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 32; 46.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κοῦρος, κόρος, probably κῦρος, κοίρανος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीशूर|पिंडीशूर|पिण्डीशूरः
पिण्डी- + शूर पिण्डी- + शूर (see पिण्ड), m. a hero at dinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावशूर
स्व-भाव- + शूर स्व-भाव- + शूर, adj. containing men who are naturally heroes, Hit. iii. d. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरता
शूरता शूर + ता, f. Prowess, heroism, Hit. iii. d. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरसेनक
शूरसेनक शूरसेन + क (see सेना), m. pl. A people and country about Mathurā, Man. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरसेनज
शूरसेनज शूरसेन-ज (see सेना), m. An inhabitant of Śūrasena. Man. 7, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्
† शूर्प् शूर्प्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्पः|शूर्प्प
शूर्प शूर्प (and probably better सूर्प सूर्प, q. cf.),<BR> I. m. and n. A winnowing basket, Man. 5, 117.<BR> II. m. A measure of two द्रोणस्.<BR> III. f. पी.<BR> 1. A small winnowing basket, a toy for children.<BR> 2. A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पक|शूर्पकः|शूर्प्पक
शूर्पक शूर्पक, m. A demon, the enemy of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्
† शूल् शूल्, i. 1 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par.<BR> 1. To be sick.<BR> 2. To make a loud noise.<BR> 3. To impale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल|शूलं|शूलः
शूल शूल (cf. शो),<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. A pike, a dart, a weapon, Sund. 1, 24; Rām. 5, 53, 53.<BR> 2. An iron pin or spit.<BR> 3. A banner.<BR> 4. Sharp pain, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 19; Lass. 31, 18; especially in the belly, as colic, Rājat. 5, 53.<BR> 5. Death.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. A stake for impaling criminals, Pañc. 238, 1.<BR> 2. A whore.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डशूल
अ-काण्ड- + शूल अ-काण्ड- + शूल (m. n.), sudden colic, Rājat. 5, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशूल|कर्णशूलः|कर्ण्णशूल
कर्ण- + शूल कर्ण- + शूल, m. and n. earache, Suśr. 1, 55, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिशूल|कुक्षिशूलः
कुक्षि- + शूल कुक्षि- + शूल, m. colic, ib. 1, 219, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूल|त्रिशूलं
त्रि- + शूल त्रि- + शूल,<BR> I. n. a trident, Rām. 5, 37, 38.<BR> II. m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशूल|दंतशूल|दन्तशूलः
दन्त- + शूल दन्त- + शूल (m. and n.), toothache, MBh. 12, 11267.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलक|शूलकः
शूलक शूल + क, m. A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिक|शूलिकं|शूलिकः
शूलिक शूलिक, i. e. शूल + इक,<BR> I. adj. Roasted on a spit (ŚKD.).<BR> II. m. A hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन्
शूलिन् शूलिन्, i. e. शूल + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Suffering sharp pain.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A spearman.<BR> 2. A stake-bearer.<BR> 3. Śiva, Bhartṛ. 2, 52.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूलिन्
त्रि- + शूलिन् त्रि- + शूलिन्,<BR> I. n. Śiva.<BR> II. f. नी, Durgā, Hariv. 9428.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्य|शूल्यं
शूल्य शूल्य, i. e. शूला̆ + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Roasted on a spit, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 9.<BR> 2. Deserving impalement.<BR> II. n. Roasted meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष्
शूष् शूष्, see सूष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगाल|शृगालः
शृगाल शृगाल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A jackal, Hit. 52, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> 3. A coward.<BR> 4. A demon.<BR> 5. Kṛṣṇa.<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. A she-jackal, Pañc. 220, 9.<BR> 2. A fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालिका
शृगालिका शृगालिका, i. e. शृगाली + क, f.<BR> 1. A female jackal, Pañc. 226, 20.<BR> 2. A fox.<BR> 3. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलं|शृंखलः|शृङ्खलः
शृङ्खल शृङ्खल, m., f. ला, and n.<BR> 1. A chain, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 12 (ला).<BR> 2. A belt worn round a man's body.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृङ्खल|उच्छृंखल|उच्छृङ्खलं
उच्छृङ्खल उच्छृङ्खल, i. e. उद्-, adj. ungovernable, Hit. iii. d. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नशृङ्खल
छिन्न- + शृङ्खल छिन्न- + शृङ्खल, adj. (vb. छिद्), having broken (his) chain (viz. an elephant), Daśak. in Chr. 190, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशृङ्खल|विशृंखल|विशृङ्खलः
वि- + शृङ्खल वि- + शृङ्खल, adj. unfettered, unrestrained, dissolute, Bhartṛ. 2, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्ग|शृंग|शृंगं|शृङ्गं|शृङ्गः
शृङ्ग शृङ्ग, probably शर + म्-ग (cf. शॄ),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A horn, Pañc. 9, 7; a horn-like vessel, Ragh. 16, 70.<BR> 2. The top of a mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 77; Daśak. in Chr. 188, 21 (उदय-अचल-इन्द्र-पद्मराग-शृङ्ग-कल्पा, As if it [viz. the sun] was the ruby top of the mountain उदय); summit of a building, Pañc. 10, 8.<BR> 3. Height, dignity.<BR> 4. Sovereignty.<BR> 5. A mark.<BR> 6. A lotus.<BR> 7. An artificial fountain.<BR> II. f. गी.<BR> 1. A fish, a sort of silurus.<BR> 2. A sort of drug.<BR> 3. A sort of gold used for making trinkets.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. as akin, κέρας; Lat. cornu; Goth. haurn; A.S. horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशृङ्ग
अ- + शृङ्ग अ- + शृङ्ग, adj. having no horns, Rājat. 5, 460.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्सामशृङ्ग
ऋक्सामशृङ्ग ऋक्सामशृङ्ग, i. e. ऋच्-सामन्-, m. a name of Viṣṇu, Rām. 6, 102, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशृङ्ग|एकशृंग|एकशृङ्गः
एक- + शृङ्ग एक- + शृङ्ग,<BR> I. m. 1. epithet of Viṣṇu, Rām. 6, 102, 13. 2. pl. a class of Manes, MBh. 2, 463.<BR> II. f. गा, a proper name, Hariv. 987.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःशृङ्ग
चतुःशृङ्ग चतुःशृ˚, i. e. चतुर्-, m. the name of a mountain, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालमणिशृङ्ग
प्रबाल-मणि- + शृङ्ग प्रबाल-मणि- + शृङ्ग, adj. having horns of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b " target="_blank">Page0960-b + 42</a>] coral and jewels, Rām. 3, 49, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशृङ्ग
स- + शृङ्ग स- + शृङ्ग, adj. possessed of a horn, Chr. 40, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गवेर|शृंगवेर
शृङ्गवेर शृङ्गवेर,<BR> I. n. Ginger.<BR> II. Name of a town, Utt. Rāmac. 14, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाट|शृंगाट|शृङ्गाटं|शृंगाटः|शृङ्गाटः
शृङ्गाट शृङ्गाट, and शृङ्गाटक शृङ्गाट + क, n. A place where four roads meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृंगारः|शृङ्गारः
शृङ्गार शृङ्गार (from शृङ्ग, cf. the next),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Copulation, coition, Pañc. i. d. 191.<BR> 2. Love, Vikr. d. 9; as an object of poetical description.<BR> 3. (m. or n.?), Elegant dress (properly, a dress for amorous purposes), Pañc. 36, 18 (cf. my transl. n. 173).<BR> 4. Marks made with red lead on an elephant's head and trunk.<BR> 5. Mark in general, Lass. 69, 5 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Red lead.<BR> 2. Cloves.<BR> 3. Fragrant powder for the dress or person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृंगारकः|शृङ्गारकः
शृङ्गारक शृङ्गार + क, adj. Horned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृंगिणः|शृङ्गिणः
शृङ्गिण शृङ्गिण, i. e. शृङ्गिन् + अ, m. A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिन्|शृंगिन्
शृङ्गिन् शृङ्गिन्, i. e. शृङ्ग + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Horned, Hit. i. d. 18, M.M.<BR> 2. Crested, peaked.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mountain.<BR> 2. A tree.<BR> 3. An elephant.<BR> III. f. इणी, A cow.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालमणिशृङ्गिन्
प्रबाल-मणि- + शृङ्गिन् प्रबाल-मणि- + शृङ्गिन्, i. e. प्रबालमणिशृङ्ग + इन्, adj. having horns of coral and jewels, Rām. 3, 49, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणि|शृणिः
शृणि शृणि (vb. शॄ), f. The hook for goading an elephant, Hit. ii. d. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्
शृध् शृध्, i. 1, Ātm., and in the aor., fut., and condit. also Par. To fart.<BR> --i. 1, Par. Ātm. † To wet, to moisten.<BR> --i. 10, To insult (by breaking wind against, or by defiling with excrements).<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To break wind against somebody, Man. 8, 282.<BR> --Cf. शकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधू
शृधू शृध् + ऊ, f. The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ शॄ, ii. 9, शृणा, णी, Par.<BR> 1. To hurt, to wound, Kir. 14, 13.<BR> 2. Pass. To be broken, to split in pieces, MBh. 3, 591 (with the termination of the Par.).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शीर्ण.<BR> I. Broken; Pañc. i. d. 387; MBh. i. d. 267.<BR> 2. Withered, Megh. 30.<BR> 3. Wasted, decayed, Mālat. 79, 18 (अन्तर्-, Mouldering in it, viz. its water).<BR> 4. Slender, thin.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, pass. To be dissolved, to spread, Rām. 1, 31, 44, Seramp. (Schlegel, 1, 38, 14, v. r.).<BR> --With परि परि, pass. To be broken, to split, MBh. 3, 11141.<BR> --With वि वि, pass.<BR> 1. To be broken, Man. 8, 408.<BR> 2. To be destroyed, MBh. 1, 3726.<BR> 3. To go asunder, to slip away, Man. 2, 74.<BR> 4. To fade away, Bhartṛ. 2, 25; Hit. iv. d. 42. विशीर्ण,<BR> 1. Broken, Pañc. 80, 9.<BR> 2. Divided, Megh. 19.<BR> 3. Withered, decayed.<BR> 4. Wasted, dispersed, Nal. 13, 17.<BR> --Cf. A.S. hyrt; κέρας; Lat. cornu; Goth. haurn; A.S. horn; κεραός; Lat. cervus; A.S. heorot, heort; κλάω, κλῆρος, κολοϐός, probably κορύνη; Goth. hairus, A sword; perhaps O.H.G. bi-hal, bipennis; Lat. clava, quiris, probably in-columis; cf. शरु, शृङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखर|शेखरं|शेखरः
शेखर शेखर (from शिखर, with aff. अ, for regular शैखर), m.<BR> 1. A crest, a diadem, Mālat. 145, 8; Lass. 13, 6 (at the end of a comp. adj.); chief, Caurap. 45 (read शेखर).<BR> 2. A garland of flowers worn on the crown of the head, Ṛt. 1, 6.<BR> 3. A proper name, Lass. n. ad 67, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुशेखर|इन्दुशेखरः
इन्दु-, चन्द्र- + शेखर इन्दु-, चन्द्र- + शेखर, and शशिशेखर, i. e. शशिन्-, m. Śiva (having the moon as crest, wearing the moon on his head), Kathās. 4, 22 (इन्दु-); Hit. 116, 6 (चन्द्र-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशेखर|चंद्रशेखर|चन्द्रशेखरः
इन्दु-, चन्द्र- + शेखर इन्दु-, चन्द्र- + शेखर, and शशिशेखर, i. e. शशिन्-, m. Śiva (having the moon as crest, wearing the moon on his head), Kathās. 4, 22 (इन्दु-); Hit. 116, 6 (चन्द्र-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेप|शेपः
शेप शेप, शेफ शेफ, and सेफ सेफ, m. The penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपस्
शेपस् शेपस्, and शेफस् शेफस्, n.<BR> 1. The penis.<BR> 2. A testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपाल|शेपालः
शेपाल शेपाल = शेवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेमुषी
शेमुषी शेमुषी (properly fem. of the ptcple. of the red. pf. of शम्) f. Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेल्
शेल् शेल्, see सेल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलु|शेलुः
शेलु शेलु, m.<BR> 1. A small tree, Cord myxa.<BR> 2. A kind of fruit, Man. 5, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव्
† शेव् शेव्, i. 1, Ātm. To worship (cf. सेव्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव|शेवः
शेव शेव,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A snake (vb. शी)<BR> 2. Happiness.<BR> II. acc. वम्, indecl. Hail, homage, an exclamation or salutation addressed to the deities.<BR> III. n., and f. वा, The penis (cf. शेप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवधि|शेवधिः
शेवधि शेवधि i. e. शेव-धा (cf. निधि), m. A treasure, Mālat. 103, 10; also सेवधि, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाल|शेवालं
शेवाल शेवाल, शैवल and शैवाल शैवा̆ल, m. n. The green moss-like substance growing on the surface of water, duck-weed (Vallisneria? cf. शेपाल and शैव), Pañc. 188, 12 (शैवल); Śāk. d. 19 (शैवल); Rām. 2, 46, 32, Seramp. (शैवाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष|शेषं|शेषः
शेष शेष, i. e. शिष् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Remaining, Man. 1, 102; 3, 47; Megh. 31; other, Pañc. 123, 13; all the other, Vikr. d. 52.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. Remainder, residue, Pañc. iii. d. 256; 51, 11 (वीज-शेष-मात्र, Even a residue of seed), Daśak. in Chr. 184, 24 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 2. What is omitted, Man. 8, 320; 322 (शेषे, for less).<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Killing, destroying, finishing.<BR> 2. End, Pañc. 55, 6.<BR> 3. The king of the serpent race, at once the conch and canopy of Viṣṇu, and the upholder of the world, Bhartṛ. 2, 28.<BR> 4. A name of Baladeva.<BR> IV. f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-a " target="_blank">Page0962-a + 44</a>] षा, Flowers and other things that have been offered to an idol (and are then distributed amongst the worshippers), Sāv. 1, 27.<BR> --Comp.<BR> A. as former part of comp. words, often: remaining, cf. शेष-शरीर, शेष-भाग.<BR> B. अ-, adj., f. षा, entire, all, every, Mālat. 2, 3; Ragh. 3, 65; Pañc. 163, 7. acc. षम्, instr. षेण, and adv. ष + तस्, entirely, Kumāras. 5, 82; Bhag. 10, 16; Man. 1, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यशेष|आलेख्यशेषः
आलेख्य- + शेष आलेख्य- + शेष, adj. (of whom is left only a likeness), dead, Ragh. 14, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्यशेष|कार्यशेषः|कार्य्यशेष
कार्य- + शेष कार्य- + शेष, n. the completion of a business, or affair begun, Man. 3, 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवशेष
जीव- + शेष जीव- + शेष, adj. having saved only the bare life, Pañc. 160, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशेष
देव- + शेष देव- + शेष, n. the remainder of an offering to a deity, MBh. 13, 2019.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामशेष|नामशेषः
नाम-शेष नाम-शेष, i. e. नामन्-, adj., f. षा, 1. one of whom only the name is left, Utt. Rāmac. 37, 18. 2. dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निः-शेष निः-शेष, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. षा, 1. without leaving a residue, without sparing anybody or anything, completely destroyed, Pañc. iii. d. 256; MBh. 2, 1531. 2. all, whole, Pañc. i. d. 21. ˚षम्, ष + तस्, adv. completely, Kathās. 24, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलमल्लकशेष
मलमल्लक- + शेष मलमल्लक- + शेष, adj. one to whom is left nothing but a small piece of cloth to cover his privities. Daśak. in Chr. 184, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःशेष|यशःशेषः
यशस्- + शेष यशस्- + शेष, adj. dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यशेष|वाक्यशेषः
वाक्य- + शेष वाक्य- + शेष, m. the remainder of one's speech, Vikr. 35, 8 (i. e. you will say).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशेष
स्मृति- + शेष स्मृति- + शेष, adj. f. षा, that of which is left nothing but remembrance, Rājat. 5, 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतशेष
हत- + शेष हत- + शेष, adj. the remainder of the killed, i. e. those who had avoided being killed, Pañc. 122, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शै
शै शै, see श्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्य|शैक्यः
शैक्य शैक्य, i. e. शिक्य + अ, adj. Placed between the ropes of a porter's yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष्य|शैक्ष्यं
शैक्ष्य शैक्ष्य, i. e. शिक्षा + य, n. Learning, skill, Johns. Sel. 48, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख|शैखः
शैख शैख, m. The offspring of an outcaste Brāhmaṇa, Man. 10, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखावत्य
शैखावत्य शैखावत्य, m. A proper name, Chr. 9, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्य|शैत्यं
शैत्य शैत्य, i. e. शीत + य, n. Coldness, Pañc. ii. d. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिल्य|शैथिल्यं
शैथिल्य शैथिल्य, i. e. शिथिल + य, n.<BR> 1. Looseness, laxity, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 11.<BR> 2. Flaccidity.<BR> 3. Weakness, Śāk. 110, 15; cowardice, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 11.<BR> 4. Smallness, Hit. 62, 22.<BR> 5. Relaxation of rule or connexion.<BR> 6. Inattention, Pañc. 118, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैनेय|शैनेयः
शैनेय शैनेय, probably शिनि + एय, m. Satyaki, the charioteer of Kṛṣṇa, MBh. 7, 7242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल|शैलं|शैलः
शैल शैल, i. e. शिला + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Stony, Arj. 8, 10; rocky.<BR> 2. Mountainous, mountaineer.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A mountain, Man. 1, 27; Vikr. 10, 6.<BR> 2. A dike, Pañc. i. d. 115.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Bitumen.<BR> 2. Storax.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडा
क्रीडा क्रीडा, m. a pleasure mountain, Megh. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यशैल|तार्क्ष्यशैलं
तार्क्ष्य- + शैल तार्क्ष्य- + शैल, n. a kind of collyrium, Suśr. 2, 66, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनशैल|तुहिनशैलः
तुहिन- + शैल तुहिन- + शैल, m. the Himālaya, Kathās. 22, 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशैल
पञ्चशैल पञ्चशैल, i. e. पञ्श्हन्-, m. the name of a mountain, Mārk. P. 55, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीशैल|बदरीशैलः
बदरी- + शैल बदरी- + शैल (see वदरी), n. a part of the Himālaya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थशैल|मंथशैल|मन्थशैलः
मन्थ- + शैल मन्थ- + शैल, m. the mount Mandara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशैल
महा- + शैल महा- + शैल, m. a great mountain, Bhartṛ. 2, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलज|शैलजं
शैलज शैल-ज, adj. Produced in or on mountains.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशैलज
हिम- + शैलज हिम- + शैलज, f. जा, Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलमय
शैलमय शैल + मय, adj., f. यी, Rocky, consisting of stones, Rājat. 5, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाट|शैलाटः
शैलाट शैलाट, i. e. शैल-अट् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A mountaineer, a barbarian.<BR> 2. A lion.<BR> 3. Crystal.<BR> 4. An idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालिन्
शैलालिन् शैलालिन्, i. e. *शैलाल + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a " target="_blank">Page0963-a + 41</a>] from शिलालिन् (a proper name), m. (properly a follower of the art taught by Śilālin), An actor, a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0962-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूष|शैलूषः
शैलूष शैलूष, i. e. शिलूष (a proper name), + अ, m.<BR> 1. An actor, a public dancer, Man. 4, 214.<BR> 2. The master of the band, or one who beats time.<BR> 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR> 4. a tree, Aegle marmelos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेय|शैलेयं|शैलेयः
शैलेय शैलेय, i. e. शैल + एय,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Produced in the mountains.<BR> 2. Mountainous, mountaineer.<BR> II. m. A bee, Ṛt. 6, 25.<BR> III. f. यी, Pārvatī.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Rock-salt.<BR> 2. Benzoin or storax.<BR> 3. A kind of vegetable perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल्य|शैल्यं
शैल्य शैल्य, i. e. शिला + य, n. Stoniness, hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव|शैवं|शैवः
शैव शैव, i. e. शिव + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating, belonging, to Śiva, Rām. 1, 66, 19.<BR> II. m. A worshipper of Śiva.<BR> III. n. A plant, Vallisneria octandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवता
शैवता शैव + ता, f. Worship of Śiva, Rājat. 5, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवल|शैवलं|शैवलः
शैवल and शैवाल शैवा̆ल, see शेवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवालक
शैवालक शैवाल + क, A substitute for शैवाल, at the end of a Bhvr. comp., Śṛṅgārat. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव्य|शैव्यः
शैव्य शैव्य,<BR> I. i. e. शिव + य, adj. Relating to Śiva.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. One of the horses of Kṛṣṇa.<BR> 2. i. e. शिवि + य, A tribe of the Śivis.<BR> 3. A proper name.<BR> III. f. या, A proper name, Sāv. 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशव|शैशवं
शैशव शैशव, i. e. शिशु + अ, n. Childhood, Man. 8, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिर|शैशिरः
शैशिर शैशिर, i. e. शिशिर + अ,<BR> I. adj. Belonging to the cold season, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 738.<BR> II. m. The name of a mountain, Arj. 3, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शो
शो शो, † i. 4, श्य (the original form was अश् + य; cf. Lat. acies, acus, acer, acidus; ἀκή, ἀκμή, ἄκρος, ἀκόνη, ἄκων; Goth. aqvizi; A.S. acas; Sskr. अश्र, अश्रि, अश्रु, अश्मन्, अश्व, अष्ट्र, etc.), Par.; ved. ii. 3, शिशा, शिशी, Par. Ātm. To sharpen, Lass. 98, 15 = Rigv. v. 9, 5 (cf. शि).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. शात.<BR> 1. Sharpened, sharp, Rājat. 5, 407.<BR> 2. Handsome.<BR> 3. Happy.<BR> 4. Thin, Ragh. 10, 70; feeble. n. Joy, happiness.<BR> II. शित.<BR> 1. Sharpened, sharp, Chr. 29, 35.<BR> 2. Thin, emaciated.<BR> 3. Feeble.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, ii. 3, To incite, Lass. 101, 15 = Rigv. vii. 16, 6.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> I. निशात, Sharpened, sharp, Bhāg. P. 3, 19, 14; polished, burnished.<BR> II. निशित, Sharpened, sharp, Chr. 29, 27; figurat., Pañc. i. d. 201. n. Iron.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संशित,<BR> 1. Certain, certified, established.<BR> 2. Completed, finished, Chr. 9, 38; 45, 16 (cf. संशित-व्रत).<BR> 3. Completing, attentive in completing, Johns. Sel. 1, 1.<BR> --Cf. also (see above), ἀκωκή, ἀκρέμων, ἀκριϐής, ὄκρις, ἄκανος, ἄκανθα, ἄκορνα, ὀξύς (i. e. ὀκ + τυ), ὄξος, ἄχωρ, (i. e. ἀκ + ϝαν), ἄχυρον, ἄχερδος, αἰχμή; Lat. aculeus, cătus (= शात), tri-que + trus, cos, cautes, citus (= शित), probably ciere, cio, cieo (= श्यामि); Goth. ahana, probably O.H.G. hvezjan; A.S. hwettan (a denomin.); Goth. hvôtjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिशित
सु-निशित सु-निशित, adj. very sharp, Chr. 29, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोक|शोकः
शोक शोक, i. e. 1. शुच् + अ, m. Sorrow, grief, Pañc. 103, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोक|अशोकं|अशोकः
अ- + शोक अ- + शोक, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशोक|त्रिशोकः
त्रि- + शोक त्रि- + शोक, m. the name of a Ṛṣi, Chr. 297, 13 = Rigv. i. 112, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोक
निःशोक निःश्˚, i. e. निस्- and वि-, adj. free front sorrow, Hariv. 14227 (निस्-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशोक|वीतशोकः
वीत- + शोक वीत- + शोक, i. e. वि-इत-,<BR> I. adj. free from sorrow.<BR> II. m. the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशोक
स- + शोक स- + शोक, adj. sorrowful. Hit. 77, 1; sad, Ṛt. 6, 16. ˚कम्, adv. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a " target="_blank">Page0964-a + 42</a>] sorrowfully, Vikr. 52, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृच्छोक|हृच्छोकः
हृच्छोक हृच्छोक, i. e. हृद्-, and हृदय-, m. heartache, a pang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0963-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकवन्त्|शोकवत्
शोकवन्त् शोक + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Sorrowful, Chr. 17, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचन|शोचनं
शोचन शोचन, i. e. 1. शुच् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Sorrowing.<BR> II. n. Sorrow, grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिष्केश|शोचिष्केशः
शोचिष्केश शोचिष्केश, i. e. शोचिस्-केश,<BR> I. adj. Having (rays of) light as hair, epithet of the sun, Chr. 289, 8 = Rigv. i. 50, 8.<BR> II. m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिस्
शोचिस् शोचिस्, i. e. 2. शुच् + इस्, n. Light, splendour, Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 88, 14; Kāvya Prak. 70, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रशोचिस्
शुक्र- + शोचिस् शुक्र- + शोचिस्, adj. possessed of a resplendent lustre, Lass. 102, 7 = Rigv. vii. 14, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ शोठ (perhaps a form of a lost शुष् + त), adj. (ŚKD.), sbst.<BR> 1. Foolish, a blockhead.<BR> 2. Idle, an idler.<BR> 3. A rogue.<BR> 4. A low man.<BR> 5. A sinner, a criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण्
† शोण् शोण्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To become red (rather a denomin. derived from the next).<BR> 2. To go, to move. शोणित, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण शोण, i. e. probably (although already in the Vedas). स-वर्ण,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Crimson, of a crimson colour, of chesnut colour, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 11.<BR> 2. Red in the face, from passion, etc.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Crimson, the colour of the red lotus.<BR> 2. A horse of a reddish or bright chesnut colour, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 10.<BR> 3. Fire.<BR> 4. A red sort of sugar-cane.<BR> 5. The name of a river.<BR> 6. A flower, Bignonia indica.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Blood.<BR> 2. Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणित|शोणितं
शोणित शोणित, i. e. शोण + इत,<BR> I. adj. Red, crimson, Ragh. 2, 39.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Blood, Pañc. iii. d. 32.<BR> 2. Saffron.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवशोणित
जीव- + शोणित जीव- + शोणित, n. living, i. e. sound blood. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b " target="_blank">Page0964-b + 42</a>] Suśr. 2, 193, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयशोणित
पूय- + शोणित पूय- + शोणित, n. purulent blood, Man. 3, 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिमन्
शोणिमन् शोणिमन्, i. e. चोण + इमन्, m. Redness, Gīt. 12, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथ|शोथः
शोथ शोथ, i. e. शू (for श्वि), + थ, m. Swelling from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधन|शोधनं|शोधनः
शोधन शोधन, i. e. शुध् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Cleaning, purifying.<BR> II. m. The lime.<BR> III. f. नी, A broom.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Cleaning, removing what may be prejudicial, Hit. 97, 15; purifying.<BR> 2. Expiation, Man. 11, 125.<BR> 3. Punishment, Man. 1, 115.<BR> 4. Correcting from faults.<BR> 5. Rooting up, Man. 9, 253.<BR> 6. Precise determination, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 11.<BR> 7. The refining of metals.<BR> 8. Payment, acquittal.<BR> 9. Fæces, ordure.<BR> 10. Green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधिन्
ऽशोधिन् -शोधिन्, i. e. शुध् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Requiting, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोफ|शोफः
शोफ शोफ (vb. श्वि, cf. शोथ), m. Intumescence.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशोफ|दंतशोफ|दन्तशोफः
दन्त- + शोफ दन्त- + शोफ, m. swelling of the gum, Suśr. 1, 116, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभ
शोभ शोभ, i. e. शुभ् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bright.<BR> 2. Handsome.<BR> II. f. भा.<BR> 1. Splendour, Megh. 60; Daśak. in Chr. 183, 4 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. भा).<BR> 2. Light.<BR> 3. Beauty, Hit. ii. d. 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभन|शोभनं|शोभनः
शोभन शोभन, i. e. शुभ् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. ना.<BR> 1. Splendid.<BR> 2. Beautiful, Rām. 4, 44, 38; ironically, Pañc. 216, 8.<BR> 3. Propitious, Pañc. 143, 23; 153, 21 (n. with न, Misfortune, Pañc. 175, 18).<BR> 4. Virtuous.<BR> 5. Good, Pañc. 126, 20.<BR> 6. Richly dressed.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A planet.<BR> 2. Burnt offering for auspicious results.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Shining, being splendid.<BR> 2. A lotus.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनशोभन|वनशोभनं
वन- + शोभन वन- + शोभन, n. a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभिन्
ऽशोभिन् -शोभिन्, i. e. शुभ् and शोभ, + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a " target="_blank">Page0965-a + 41</a>] adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Shining, Vikr. d. 137; Rājat. 5, 358; Megh. 58.<BR> 2. Exceeding, Rājat. 5, 384.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितशोभिन्
स्मित- + शोभिन् स्मित- + शोभिन् (vb. स्मि), adj., f. नी, smiling beautifully, Lass. 2. ed. 55, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0964-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोष|शोषः
शोष शोष, i. e. शुष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Drying up, Pañc. 51, 5; 159, 15.<BR> 2. Exsiccation, ib. 76, 11.<BR> 3. Pulmonary consumption.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुशोष
तालु- + शोष तालु- + शोष, m. morbid dryness of the palate, Suśr. 1, 306, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशोष
दुस्- + शोष दुस्- + शोष, adj. difficult to be dried up, MBh. 8, 656.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशोष|परिशोषः
परि- + शोष परि- + शोष, m. complete drying up or shrivelling, Rām. 4, 15, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषण|शोषणं|शोषणः
शोषण शोषण, i. e. शुष् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Drying up, causing to fade, Śāk. d. 58.<BR> II. m. One of the arrows of Kāma, Lass. 7, 3.<BR> III. n. Drying up, Lass. 2. ed. 91, 61; Pañc. 27, 1 (वृथा-शरीर-, Useless mortifying one's self).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषिन्
ऽशोषिन् -शोषिन्, i. e. शुष् + इन्, Drying up, in हृदय-कुसुम-, adj. Causing (her) flower-like heart to fade, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक|शौकं
शौक शौक, i. e. शुक + अ, n. A flock of parrots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तेय|शौक्तेयं
शौक्तेय शौक्तेय, i. e. शुक्ति + एय, n. A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्ल्य|शौक्ल्यं
शौक्ल्य शौक्ल्य, i. e. शुक्ल + य, n. Whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौङ्गेय|शौङ्गेयः
शौङ्गेय शौङ्गेय, m. Garuḍa, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 12 (cf. Wilson, Daśak. p. 93, n. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौच|शौचं
शौच शौच, i. e. शुचि + अ, n.<BR> 1. Purity, Rājat. 5, 11; cleanness, Pañc. iii. d. 112.<BR> 2. Honesty, Pañc. v. d. 2.<BR> 3. Purification, Man. 2, 69; cleaning (of vessels), Pañc. ii. d. 109, cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3029.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौच|अशौचं
अ- + शौच अ- + शौच, n. 1. impurity. Man. 11, 183. 2. perfidy, Lass. 21, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशौच
अर्थ- + शौच अर्थ- + शौच, n. purity in acquiring wealth, honesty, Man. 5, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचत्व
शौचत्व शौच + त्व, n., in अ-, Impurity, Hit. i. d. 194, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेय|शौचेयः
शौचेय शौचेय, i. e. शुचि + एय, m. A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौट्
† शौट् शौट्, शौड् शौड्, i. 1, Par. To be proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर|शौटीरः
शौटीर शौटीर (i. e. *शुटीर + अ, cf. शुटीरता), adj. Proud. m.<BR> 1. A hero, Rām. 3, 48, 4.<BR> 2. An ascetic who has given up worldly pursuits.<BR> 3. An upstart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर्य|शौटीर्यं|शौटीर्य्य|शौटीर्य्यं
शौटीर्य शौटीर्य, i. e. शौटीर (or *शुटीर, see the last), + य, n.<BR> 1. Pride.<BR> 2. Heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड्
शौड् शौड्, see शौट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्ड|शौंड|शौण्डः
शौण्ड शौण्ड, i. e. शुण्ड + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Drunk, intoxicated.<BR> 2. Addicted to liquor, Draup. 6, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशौण्ड|दानशौंड|दानशौण्डः
दान- + शौण्ड दान- + शौण्ड, adj. exceedingly liberal, Rājat. 6, 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिक|शौंडिक|शौंडिकः|शौण्डिकः
शौण्डिक शौण्डिक, i. e. शुण्ड + इक,<BR> I. m. A distiller and vendor of spirituous liquors, Man. 4, 216.<BR> II. f. की. A female keeper of a tavern, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिकेय|शौंडिकेय|शौंडिकेयः|शौण्डिकेयः
शौण्डिकेय शौण्डिकेय, i. e. शौण्डिक + एय, m. A demon, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 531, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौन|शौनं
शौन शौन, i. e. शूना + अ (n.), Meat kept at a slaughter-house, Man. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनक|शौनकः
शौनक शौनक, m. A proper name, Man. 3, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनिक|शौनिकः
शौनिक शौनिक, i. e. शूना + इक, m.<BR> 1. A butcher, Man. 4, 86.<BR> 2. A poulterer, a vendor of flesh of birds.<BR> 3. Chase, hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य|शौर्यं|शौर्य्य|शौर्य्यं
शौर्य शौर्य, i. e. शूर + य, n. Prowess, heroism, Pañc. iii. d. 53; 238, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किक|शौल्किकः
शौल्किक शौल्किक, i. e. शुल्क + इक, m. Superintendent of tolls or customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्विक|शौल्विकः
शौल्विक शौल्विक, i. e. शुल्व + इक, m. A coppersmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिक|शौवस्तिकं
शौवस्तिक शौवस्तिक, i. e. श्वस्त्य + इक, adj. Of, or belonging to, tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौष्कल|शौष्कलः
शौष्कल शौष्कल, i. e. शुष्कल + अ,<BR> I. adj. Eating flesh.<BR> II. m. A vendor of flesh (ŚKD.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत्
श्चुत् श्चुत्, and 1. श्च्युत् श्च्युत् (derived from a noun based on श्च्यु, cf. च्यु), i. 1, Par. To ooze, to drop, Kir. 5, 29 (श्च्युत्); to distill, Mālat. 81, 13 (श्चुत्).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. श्च्युतित.<BR> 1. Shed, sprinkled.<BR> 2. Dropping, flowing.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, To drop, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 87, 2 (श्चुत्).<BR> --With नि नि, श्चुत्, To drop down, Mālat. 128, 5.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To distill, Mālat. 24, 3; Bhaṭṭ. 14, 79 (श्चुत्).<BR> --Cf. Goth. skevjan (= श्चु); skura; A.S. scur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युत्
2. ऽश्च्युत् -श्च्युत्, latter part of comp. words, adj. Shedding, जल- (water), Kir. 5, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नथ्
श्नथ् श्नथ्, i. 1, Par. To hurt, to kill, to destroy.<BR> --Cf. Goth. snithan; A.S. snidhan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशान|श्मशानं
श्मशान श्मशान, i. e. probably श्मन् (for शम् + अन्, cf. κμης in σιδηρο-κμής), -शयन, n. A cemetery, Pañc. v. d. 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेश्मशानम्
पारेश्मशानम् पारेश्मशानम्, i. e. पार + इ-श्मशान + म्, adv. beyond the cemetery, Mālat. 79, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रु
श्मश्रु श्मश्रु, n. The beard, Pañc. 182, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तश्मश्रु
रक्त- + श्मश्रु रक्त- + श्मश्रु (vb. रञ्ज्), adj. having a red beard, Hiḍ. 3, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्मश्रु|सश्मश्रुः
स- + श्मश्रु स- + श्मश्रु, f. a woman with a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितश्मश्रु
सित- + श्मश्रु सित- + श्मश्रु, adj. silvery-bearded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुल
श्मश्रुल श्मश्रु + ल, adj. Having a beard, Ragh. 4, 63; one who lets grow his beard, Man. 11, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मील्
† श्मील् श्मील्, स्मील् स्मील् (cf. मील्), i. 1, Par. To wink, to contract the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान श्यान, see श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याम|श्यामः
श्याम श्याम (probably from श्वि, cf. श्येत),<BR> I. adj., f. मा.<BR> 1. Green.<BR> 2. Dark-blue, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 3. Black, Bhartṛ. 2, 14; 36 (dry ?); shady, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 8.<BR> 4. Brown, Hiḍ. 2, 25; Nal. 12, 50; 18, 11.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Green, black (the colour).<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> 3. The कोकिल or Indian cuckoo.<BR> 4. A sacred fig-tree at प्रयाग, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 11; cf. Wilson, Hind. Theat. 2. ed. i. 302, n. †.<BR> 5. Thorn-apple.<BR> III. m., and f. मा, A sort of grain, Panicum frumentaceum.<BR> IV. f. मा.<BR> 1. Night.<BR> 2. Shade, shadow.<BR> 3. The female of the Indian cuckoo, Pañc. 157, 4.<BR> 4. A cow.<BR> 5. Durgā.<BR> 6. A married woman before she has borne children.<BR> 7. A plant, commonly Priyaṅgn, Megh. 102; and name of several others.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. Pepper.<BR> 2. Sea salt.<BR> --Cf. κύανος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामल|श्यामलः
श्यामल श्याम + ल,<BR> I. adj., f. ला, Of a dark-blue or black colour, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 13; blackish, Mālat. 145, 10.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Black (the colour).<BR> 2. Pepper.<BR> 3. The religious fig-tree.<BR> 4. A large bee.<BR> III. f. ला, Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाक|श्यामाकः
श्यामाक श्यामाक (cf. श्याम), m. A sort of grain, Panicum frumentaceum, Śāk. d. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाय
श्यामाय श्यामाय, a denomin. derived from श्याम with य, Ātm. To become black, to prove impure (as gold, cf. the next), Mālav. d. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामिका
श्यामिका श्यामिका, i. e. श्याम + क, f. Impurity (of gold), Ragh. 1, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामित
श्यामित श्यामित, i. e. श्याम + इत, adj. Blackened, discoloured, Kir. 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याल|श्यालः
श्याल श्याल, see स्याल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालक|श्यालकः
श्यालक श्याल + क, m. A miserable brother-in-law, Cāṇ. 80 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 412.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव श्याव (akin to श्याम), adj. Of a brown colour, livid, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत श्येत (probably from श्वि in श्वित्, cf. श्वेत and Zend. श्पि in श्पि + तम, श्पि + ति),<BR> I. adj., f. ता and श्येनी, White, Kir. 5, 31.<BR> II. m. White (the colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येन|श्येनः
श्येन श्येन (akin to the last),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. A hawk, Pañc. 188, 15.<BR> II. f. नी. A female hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै श्यै, i. 1, Ātm. † To go.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. श्यान, Thick, viscous, adhesive.<BR> II. शीन, Thick. congealed.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, To dry up, Ragh. 17, 37. आश्यान,<BR> 1. Dry, Ragh. 4, 24.<BR> 2. A little dry (i. e. श्यान, with आ), Kumāras. 7, 9.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रतिशीन, Melted, fluid, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनंपाता|श्यैनम्पाता
श्यैनंपाता श्यैनंपाता, i. e. श्येन + म्-पत् + अ + अ, f. Hawking, hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्क्|श्रंक्
† श्रङ्क् श्रङ्क्, स्रङ्क् स्रङ्क्, श्लङ्क् श्रङ्क्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्ग्|श्रंग्
† श्रङ्ग् श्रङ्ग्, श्लङ्ग् श्लङ्ग्, श्वङ्ग् श्वङ्ग्, स्वङ्ग् स्वङ्ग्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण्
श्रण् श्रण्, i. 1 and 10, Par. To give, to present.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, i. 10, To distribute, to give, Ragh. 14, 15. विश्राणित, Given away, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत् श्रत्, perhaps properly श्रथ्, a prefix combined and compounded with धा, and in the Vedas with कृ, and their derivatives, and implying faith.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cred in credo, for cred-do; see धा, p. 437.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्
श्रथ् श्रथ्, i. 1 and 10, Par., and श्रन्थ् ii. 9, श्रथ्ना, नी, and i. 1 and 10, Par.<BR> 1. To tie (ved. ii. 9).<BR> 2. To untie, to loosen (ved. ii. 9).<BR> 3. † To kill. श्रन्थ्, i. 1, Ātm. To be loose. श्रथ्, i. 10, Par.<BR> I. † श्राथय,<BR> 1. To apply diligently.<BR> 2. To delight frequently.<BR> II. श्रथय, † To be loose.<BR> --Cf. κλώθω, κάλαθος; Lat. crates, rete, restis; Goth. af-hlathan; O.H.G. and A.S. hládan; O.H.G. hlast; A.S. hlaest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथन|श्रथनं
श्रथन श्रथ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Tieing.<BR> 2. Untieing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधानता
श्रद्दधानता श्रद्दधान + ता (ptcple. pres. of श्रत्-धा), f. Faith, Man. 7, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध श्रद्ध, i. e. श्रत्-धा, n., and f. धा.<BR> 1. Faith, Man. 3, 202 (f.); Bhag. 6, 37 (f.).<BR> 2. Trust, intimacy, Rājat. 5, 285.<BR> 3. Respect, reverence, Pañc. 265, 15 (f.).<BR> 4. Purity.<BR> 5. Wish, hope, Bhartṛ. 1, 89.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धा
अ-श्रद्धा अ-श्रद्धा, f. want of faith, Man. 4, 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाश्रद्धम्
यथा-श्रद्ध + म् यथा-श्रद्ध + म्, adv. confidently, without reserve, Nal. 4, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धामय
श्रद्धामय श्रद्धा + मय, adj., f. यी, Full of faith, Bhag. 17, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु श्रद्धा + लु,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Faithful.<BR> 2. Wishing, desirous.<BR> II. f. A pregnant woman longing for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धावन्त्|श्रद्धावत्
श्रद्धावन्त् श्रद्धा + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Believing, having faith, Bhag. 3, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धेयत्व
श्रद्धेयत्व श्रद्धेय + त्व (ptcple. of the fut. pass. of श्रत्-धा), n. Trustworthiness, Pañc. 162, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ्|श्रंथ्
श्रन्थ् श्रन्थ्, see श्रथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः|श्रन्थः
श्रन्थ श्रन्थ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Tieing.<BR> 2. Untieing.<BR> 3. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थन|श्रंथन|श्रंथनं|श्रन्थनं
श्रन्थन श्रन्थ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Tieing.<BR> 2. Stringing flowers.<BR> 3. Loosening.<BR> 4. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम् श्रम्, i. 4, श्राम्य, Par.<BR> 1. To exert one's self, Lass. 2. ed. 66, 18.<BR> 2. To perform acts of religious austerity, to undergo mortification or penance.<BR> 3. To be wearied, Megh. 97.<BR> 4. † To be distressed.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. श्रान्त.<BR> 1. Wearied, fatigued, tired, Vikr. 67, 2.<BR> 2. Calmed. m. An ascetic.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, परिश्रान्त,<BR> 1. Having performed acts of religious austerity, MBh. 3, 10002.<BR> 2. Fatigued, Man. 4, 99.<BR> 3. Exhausted, MBh. 1, 7626.<BR> 4. Overcome with distress, Mālat. 154, 10.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To repose, Hit. iv. d. 67; Rām. 1, 62, 1.<BR> 2. To go to rest, Vikr. 40, 2.<BR> 3. To cease, Pañc. 220, 25 (with ptcple. in the signification of an infin.). विश्रान्त,<BR> 1. Reposed, Hit. 77, 1; reposing, Pañc. 222, 1; having reposed, Hit. 99, 5.<BR> 2. Ceased, Vikr. d. 130; desisting from.<BR> 3. Calm, composed, Utt. Rāmac. 3, 1.<BR> --Caus. श्रमय (and in epic poetry श्रामय), To let repose, MBh. 3, 11004.<BR> --Cf. perhaps A.S. hearm, grief, and O.H.G. râmen, râmjan, intendere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रान्तम्
अ-श्रान्त + म् अ-श्रान्त + म्, adv. indefatigably, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्रान्त
अति- + श्रान्त अति- + श्रान्त, adj. very fatigued, Pañc. 52, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम श्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Exertion, Pañc. 226, 25; labour, toil, Pañc. 134, 14; taking pains, Chr. 22, 20; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-b " target="_blank">Page0968-b + 44</a>] with कृ, to study, Man. 2, 168.<BR> 2. Military exercise.<BR> 3. Fatigue, weariness, Hiḍ. 1, 19; Kir. 5, 28; Utt. Rāmac. 158, 10 (-अम्बु, Perspiration).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रम|अश्रमः
अ- + श्रम अ- + श्रम, m. absence of weariness, Ragh. 2, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्रम
अति- + श्रम अति- + श्रम, m. great fatigue, Śāk. d. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्रम|कृतश्रमः
कृत- + श्रम कृत- + श्रम, adj. tired, Hit. iii. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यातव्याकरणश्रम
ख्यात-व्याकरण- + श्रम ख्यात-व्याकरण- + श्रम, m. renowned for his study of grammar, Rājat. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितश्रम
जित- + श्रम जित- + श्रम, adj. not suffering from fatigue, Hit. iii. d. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तेभकुम्भविदलनकृतश्रम
मत्त-इभ-कुम्भ-विदलन-कृत- + श्रम मत्त-इभ-कुम्भ-विदलन-कृत- + श्रम, adj. one who has ever endeavoured to tear to pieces the frontal globes of furious elephants, Pañc. i. d. 351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाश्रम
वृथा- + श्रम वृथा- + श्रम, m. vain exertion, Pañc. 116, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रम
स- + श्रम स- + श्रम, adj. wearied fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण श्रमण, i. e. श्रम् + अन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Following a low business.<BR> 2. Base.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An ascetic, a Bauddha friar, Rājat. 5, 427.<BR> 2. A religious mendicant, Rām. 1, 13, 13.<BR> III. f. णा.<BR> 1. A female mendicant; also णी, Rām. 2, 38, 5.<BR> 2. A woman of low caste or business.<BR> 3. A handsome woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणाय
श्रमणाय श्रमणाय, a denomin. derived from the last with य, Ātm. To become a beggar, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 787.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन् श्रम् + इन्, and श्रम + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Laborious, diligent.<BR> 2. Wearying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्भ्|श्रंभ्
श्रम्भ् श्रम्भ्, स्रम्भ् स्रम्भ्, i. 1, Ātm. † To be careless.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To entrust, to confide.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. विश्रब्ध.<BR> 1. Confided, entrusted, MBh. 3, 2161.<BR> 2. Confided in.<BR> 3. Confident, fearless, Pañc. 75, 9.<BR> 4. Firm, Chr. 32, 30.<BR> 5. Tranquil, patient.<BR> 6. Lowlyminded. Acc. ˚धम्, adv.<BR> 1. Without hesitation, Man. 8, 417.<BR> 2. Without fear, Rām. 3, 49, 33.<BR> 3. Quietly, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयण|श्रयणं
श्रयण श्रयण, i. e. श्रि + अन, n. Refuge, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
श्रव श्रव, m., i. e.<BR> 1. श्रु + अ, The ear.<BR> 2. (Wrongly for स्रव), Oozing, dripping.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णश्रव|कर्ण्णश्रव
कर्ण- + श्रव कर्ण- + श्रव, adj. perceivable by the ear, Man. 4, 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुःश्रव
सु-दुस्- + श्रव सु-दुस्- + श्रव, m. very ill fame, Utt. Rāmac. 166, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवण|श्रवणं|श्रवणः
श्रवण श्रवण, i. e. श्रु + अन,<BR> I. m. and n. The ear, Hit. i. d. 193, M.M.<BR> II. m., and f. णा, The twenty-third lunar asterism.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Hearing, Pañc. 188, 10.<BR> 2. Study, Vedāntas. in Chr. 216, 2; learning, Mālat. 6, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रश्रवण
उग्र- + श्रवण उग्र- + श्रवण, adj. dreadful to hear, Johns. Sel. 96, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस् श्रवस्, i. e. श्रु + अस्, n.<BR> 1. The ear.<BR> 2. Renown, wealth, Chr. 294, 8 = Rigv. i. 92, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κλέος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःश्रवस्
उच्चैःश्रवस् उच्चैःश्रवस्, i. e. उच्चैस्-, m. a fabulous horse, MBh. 1, 366.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुःश्रवस्
चक्षुःश्रवस् चक्षुःश्रवस्, i. e. चक्षुस्-, m. a snake, MBh. 12, 13803.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घश्रवस्
दीर्घ- + श्रवस् दीर्घ- + श्रवस्, adj. widely renowned, Chr. 297, 11 = Rigv. i. 112, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रवस्
देव- + श्रवस् देव- + श्रवस्, m. a proper name, Hariv. 1461 (Θεοκλῆς).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुश्रवस्
पृथु- + श्रवस् पृथु- + श्रवस्,<BR> I. adj. widely renowned, Bhāg. P. 4, 15, 4.<BR> II. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरश्रवस्
विष्टर- + श्रवस् विष्टर- + श्रवस्, m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धश्रवस्
वृद्ध- + श्रवस् वृद्ध- + श्रवस् (vb. वृध्), m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्रवस्
सु- + श्रवस् सु- + श्रवस्, adj. famous, Chr. 288, 2 = Rigv. i. 49, 2 (cf. εὐκλεής).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यु
श्रवस्यु श्रवस् + यु, adj. Desirous of renown or wealth, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाय्य|श्रवाय्यः
श्रवाय्य श्रवाय्य, m. An animal destined for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठा
श्रविष्ठा श्रविष्ठा (f. of a superl. based on श्रवस्, in the signification ‘wealth’), f. A lunar asterism (= धनिष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रा
श्रा श्रा, † ii. 2, Par., श्रै श्रै [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b " target="_blank">Page0969-b + 42</a>] († स्रै स्रै, † शै शै), † i. 1, श्राय, Par.<BR> 1. To boil, to cook, to mature, to ripen.<BR> 2. † To sweat; cf. श्री.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. श्राण.<BR> 1. Boiled, dressed.<BR> 2. Moist, wet. f. णा, Rice-gruel.<BR> II. श्रित, Cooked, ved. and Rām. 2, 56, 24, Schlegel (but Gorr. 2, 56, 26, शृत).<BR> III. शृत, Boiled, Man. 11, 147.<BR> --Caus. श्रपय and † श्रापय, To cook, MBh. 3, 5038.<BR> --Cf. κρίϐανος, κρίϐανον, κλίϐανος, κριϐάνη, κράμϐος, καρτός, κάρϕω, κάρδοπος, probably κραῦρος, perhaps κέραμος, κέρνον; Lat. cremare, carbo, probably calere, cinis; Goth. hauri, hlaibs; A.S. heordh, hláf, haerefaest, haerfest, Ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्ध|श्राद्धं
श्राद्ध श्राद्ध, i. e. श्रद्धा + अ,<BR> I. adj. Faithful.<BR> II. n.<BR> I. A funeral ceremony and worship of the Manes, consisting of offerings to the gods and Manes, and gifts and food to the relations and assisting Brāhmaṇas, Man. 1, 112; 3, 81; 82; 204; Pañc. ii. d. 101.<BR> 2. Gifts given at the श्राद्ध, Lass. 89, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिश्राद्ध|वृद्धिश्राद्धं
वृद्धि- + श्राद्ध वृद्धि- + श्राद्ध, n. a sacrifice to progenitors on any prosperous occasion, as a birth of a son, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक श्राद्धिक, i. e. श्राद्ध + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to an obsequial offering.<BR> 2. n. A present given at a श्राद्ध, Man. 4, 116.<BR> II. m., f. कि, n. The object, receiver, or enjoyer of an obsequial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रांतिः|श्रान्तिः
श्रान्ति श्रान्ति, i. e. श्रम् + ति. f. Weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम्
श्राम् श्राम्, v. r. of ग्राम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम श्राम, i. e. श्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A temporary shed.<BR> 2. Time.<BR> 3. A month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राय|श्रायः
श्राय श्राय,<BR> I. श्रि + अ, m. Refuge, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a " target="_blank">Page0970-a + 42</a>] protection.<BR> II. श्री + अ, adj. Sacred, or belonging, to the goddess श्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावक|श्रावकः
श्रावक श्रावक, i. e. श्रु, Caus., + अक, m.<BR> 1. The name of a class of the Bauddha votaries; a lay votary of the Bauddha religion, Pañc. 236, 19.<BR> 2. A pupil, Mālat. 174, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण श्रावण, i. e.<BR> A. श्रवण + अ,<BR> I. adj. Born or produced under the asterism श्रवना̆.<BR> II. m. The name of a month (July--August).<BR> III. f. णी.<BR> 1. The day of full moon in the month Śrāvaṇa, Man. 4, 95.<BR> 2. The name of one of the domestic sacrifices (पाक-यज्ञ), Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 527.<BR> B. श्रु, Caus., + अन, n. Causing to hear.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यश्रावण
सत्य- + श्रावण सत्य- + श्रावण, n. taking an oath, Pañc. 97, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक श्रावणिक, i. e. श्रावण + इक, m. The month श्रावण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि श्रि, i. 1, Par. Ātm. (the original signification is probably ‘To cling to’’ ‘To lean’),<BR> 1. To go to, Ragh. 3, 70 (Calc.); to come, Vikr. d. 112.<BR> 2. To enter, MBh. 5, 1741.<BR> 3. To obtain, Chr. 294, 2 = Rigv. i. 92, 2.<BR> 4. To undergo, Rājat. 5, 132 (with the abstract आनुकूल्यम्, ‘To become inclined,’ read अशिश्रियन्).<BR> 5. To serve (ved.). Ptcple of the pf. pass. श्रित.<BR> 1. Cherished, protected, fied for refuge.<BR> 2. Served, worshipped.<BR> 3. Joined with, contiguous to.<BR> 4. Sitting on, Lass. 2. ed. 89, 37.<BR> 5. Covered.<BR> 6. Having.<BR> --With the prep. अधि अधि, To ascend; with शयनम्, To go to rest, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 20. अधिश्रित,<BR> 1. Trespassing, being out of, Pañc. 291, 11 (v. r.).<BR> 2. Placed.<BR> 3. Received.<BR> 4. Included.<BR> --With समधि सम्-अधि, To approach, Nal. 23, 12.<BR> --With अभि [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-b " target="_blank">Page0970-b + 45</a>] अभि, To have recourse to, MBh. 1, 8274.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To go to, Pañc. 188, 18; Chr. 46, 19; to retire in (acc.), Vikr. d. 155.<BR> 2. With a word implying, ‘Ground, earth,’ To fall to, Chr. 32, 25.<BR> 3. To enter, Rām. 2, 67, 5; with रथम्, To mount, MBh. 1, 8187.<BR> 4. To undergo, Hit. 75, 17; Rājat. 5, 130; मित्रभावम् आश्रित्य, Having become friends, Pañc. 141, 19; to take, Utt. Rāmac. 88, 2.<BR> 5. To have recourse to, MBh. 3, 13069; absol. आश्रित्य, By help, by means of, Śāk. 4, 12.<BR> 6. To use, Lass. 85, 7.<BR> 7. To seek, Hit. ii. d. 127.<BR> 8. To choose, Hit. 75, 10.<BR> 9. To obtain, Pañc. 94, 24.<BR> 10. To follow, Bhartṛ. 2, 33.<BR> 11. To inhabit, Man. 7, 72.<BR> 12. To depend upon, Man. 1, 17.<BR> 13. To assist, MBh. 1, 5916. आश्रित,<BR> 1. Having recourse to; with अहंकारम्, Having grown presumptuous, Pañc. 76, 20; using, Johns. Sel. 38, 27.<BR> 2. Having attained, Pañc. 76, 8.<BR> 3. Having assumed, Johns. Sel. 94, 56.<BR> 4. Following, Man. 5, 90; practising.<BR> 5. Inhabiting.<BR> 6. Being, Rām. 3, 49, 33.<BR> 7. Receiving anything as an inherent or integral part.<BR> 8. Inherent, Bhāṣāp. 85.<BR> 9. Taking one's station, Rājat. 5, 286.<BR> 10. A dependent, Hit. 30, 10, M.M.; Kumāras. 3, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, To go to, Rām. 2, 84, 7.<BR> --With अपा अप-आ, To resort to, to have recourse to, MBh. 1, 651 (अन्-अपाश्रित्य, without the help of).<BR> --With व्यपा वि-अप-आ, To have recourse to, Bhag. 9, 32.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To go to, MBh. 1, 5918.<BR> 2. To have recourse to, Bhag. 4, 10. उपाश्रित्य, By aid, Man. 9, 316.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. उपाश्रित.<BR> 1. Supporting.<BR> 2. Relying upon.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. not relied upon, used as support, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 7. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-a " target="_blank">Page0971-a + 42</a>]<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ, To have recourse to, MBh. 2, 618. समुपाश्रित, Having resorted to, Rājat. 5, 141.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To go to, MBh. 1, 5927; to approach; with आसनम्, to sit down, Pañc. i. d. 283.<BR> 2. To enter, Man. 6, 2.<BR> 3. To occupy, Pañc. 136, 8; to obtain, i. d. 417.<BR> 4. To have recourse to, Pañc. 154, 15; समाश्रित्य, by aid, Man. 3, 77.<BR> 5. To confide in, Man. 7, 70. समाश्रित,<BR> 1. Fled for refuge, protected.<BR> 2. Having assumed, Chr. 29, 25.<BR> 3. Joined, Rājat. 5, 248.<BR> 4. Depending on, Pañc. iii. d. 62.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. Ātm. To rise, MBh. 4, 1018.<BR> 2. Par. To raise, Rām. 2, 66, 17. उच्छ्रित,<BR> 1. Produced.<BR> 2. Lifted up. Hit. ii. d. 154.<BR> 3. High, Kir. 5, 1.<BR> 4. Rising, MBh. 3, 2437.<BR> 5. Increased in size or bulk.<BR> 6. Prosperous.<BR> 7. Left, abandoned.<BR> 8. Deprived, Pañc. v. d. 11 (फल-, Will not be fulfilled).<BR> --Comp.<BR> अति-, excessively elevated, Hit. ii. d. 120.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, अभ्युच्छ्रित, Raised, Draup. 8, 20.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोच्छ्रित, High, Mṛcch. 76, 21.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुच्छ्रित,<BR> 1. Raised, MBh. 3, 8064.<BR> 2. Lofty, Hit. ii. d. 84.<BR> --With उप उप, To come to, to hit, MBh. 3, 10456.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, To come out, Sāv. 6, 14.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रश्रित, Modest, humble, well-behaved, Indr. 1, 10.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, संप्रश्रित, The same, Rām. 2, 70, 11.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To unite, Mālat. 15, 2 (Ātm.).<BR> 2. To go to, MBh. 3, 13053.<BR> 3. To attain, to get, Man. 10, 60.<BR> 4. To have recourse to, MBh. 2, 128; Pañc. 155, 21; to flee to, Hit. iii. d. 147.<BR> 5. To seek, Rām. 1, 1, 6.<BR> 6. To depend upon, Rām. 2, 60, 20. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b " target="_blank">Page0971-b + 42</a>]<BR> 7. To inhabit, Man. 2, 24. संश्रित,<BR> 1. Having gone for refuge to (acc.), Pañc. iii. d. 129.<BR> 2. Come for refuge, Śāk. d. 104.<BR> 3. Protected, supported.<BR> 4. Joined, Rājat. 5, 335. m. An attendant, Man. 4, 179.<BR> --With अभि-सम् अभि-सम्, अभिसंश्रित, Having gone to, Lass. 2. ed. 76, 54 (went to).<BR> --Cf. शरण, and Goth. hulth; A.S. hold; perhaps Goth. hail; A.S. hál; perhaps Lat. clemens; to the original signification seem to belong, κλίνω, κλισία, κλιτύς; Lat. in-clinare, clivus; Goth. hlains, hleithra, hlija; A.S. hlynian, hlidh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकश्रित
अन्-एक- + श्रित अन्-एक- + श्रित, adj. inherent in many, Bhāṣāp. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्रित
पर- + श्रित पर- + श्रित, adj. dependent, Hit. ii. d. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित्
ऽश्रित् -श्रि + त्, latter part of comp. adj. Reaching, rising to; cf. नभःश्रित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियपुत्र
श्रियपुत्र श्रियपुत्र, crroneously for प्रियपत्र, m. A kind of bird, Lass. 52, 20, see 2. ed. p. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियस्
श्रियस् श्रियस्, probably श्रि + अस् (cf. 2 श्री and ved. भियस्, n.), Happiness, Chr. 293, 6 = Rigv. i. 87, 6 (cf. 293, 3 = Rigv. i. 88, 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
† श्रिष् श्रिष्, श्लिष् श्लिष्, i. 1, Par. To burn (cf. श्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
1. श्री श्री (cf. श्रा), ii. 9, श्रीणा, णी, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To cook, to burn.<BR> 2. To mix.<BR> --Cf. probably κίρνημι, κεράω, κεράννυμι, κικράω, etc.; Lat. pin-cerna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
2. श्री श्री (either from श्रा, To ripen, cf. Lat. Ceres, or from श्रि-, To approach for protection), f.<BR> 1. The deity of plenty and prosperity, the wife of Viṣṇu, Rām. 3, 52, 22.<BR> 2. Fortune, Vikr. d. 161; 162; success, happiness, prosperity, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12; highest dignity, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2 (pl.); royal bliss, power, Vikr. d. 76; Pañc. i. d. 271; well-being, Pañc. i. d. 292; favour, Chr. 294, 6 = [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a " target="_blank">Page0972-a + 44</a>] Rigv. i. 92, 6.<BR> 3. Wealth, property, Kir. 14, 13.<BR> 4. Beauty, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 5. Light, splendour, Pañc. v. d. 4.<BR> 6. Glory, Pañc. iii. d. 259.<BR> 7. Intellect.<BR> 8. Decoration.<BR> 9. A name of Sarasvatī.<BR> 10. A tree, Pinus longifolia.<BR> 11. Cloves.<BR> 12. A prefix to the names of deities, and revered persons, and books, implying, Holy, illustrious, famous; e. g. श्री-विष्णु, The holy deity, Viṣṇu; श्रि-राम; श्री-भागवत-पुराण, The holy Bhāgavata-Purāṇa, cf. Rājat. 5, 30; 426; Lass. 45, 12; 66, 16; 67, 4; Bhartṛ. p. 21, 1. 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्री
अप- + श्री अप- + श्री, adj. deprived of beauty, Śiś. 11, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयश्री
जय- + श्री जय- + श्री, f. the goddess of victory, Rājat. 2, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्री
महा- + श्री महा- + श्री, f. epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीक
ऽश्रीक -श्री + क, a substitute for श्री at the end of comp. adj.; e. g. निःश्रीक, i. e. निस्-, adj.<BR> 1. Unfortunate, MBh. 5, 533.<BR> 2. Deprived of beauty, light, ib. 14, 476. पुण्य-, Endowed with a pure royal majesty, Utt. Rāmac. 105, 5. वि-गत-, adj. Unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमन्त्|श्रीमत्
श्रीमन्त् श्री + मन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. मती.<BR> 1. Fortunate, Hit. 54, 20.<BR> 2. Wealthy.<BR> 3. Famous, Pañc. iii. d. 238.<BR> 4. Beautiful, Mālat. 148, 8; Chr. 27, 6.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील श्री + ल, adj.<BR> 1. Fortunate.<BR> 2. Wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सकिन्
श्रीवत्सकिन् श्रीवत्सकिन्, i. e. श्री-वत्स + ह + इन्, m. A horse having a curl of hair on his breast and face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
1. श्रु श्रु, ii. 5, शृणु, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 386),<BR> 1. To hear, Man. 5, 75; Chr. 292, 2 = Rigv. i. 86, 2 (ved. शृणुता); Chr. 288, 10 = Rigv. i. 48, 10 (श्रुधि, imperat. aor.).<BR> 2. To be attentive, Man. 1, 4.<BR> 3. To be obedient, Bhag. 13, 58. श्रुत,<BR> 1. Understood.<BR> 2. Called, Lass. 2. ed. 61, 28. n.<BR> 1. The object of hearing, that which is heard.<BR> 2. Sacred learning, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-b " target="_blank">Page0972-b + 42</a>] Man. 2, 149; Bhartṛ. 2, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शुश्रूषित, Served, Pañc. 118, 24.<BR> --Caus. श्रावय,<BR> 1. To cause to hear, i. e. to speak, to say, Rām. 2, 3, 31.<BR> 2. To propound, Man. 1, 59.<BR> 3. To inform, Rām. 1, 17, 18.<BR> 4. To report, MBh. 1, 6518.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, To hear, Man. 9, 100; pass. To be told, Pañc. 3, 10. Desider. To obey, Rām. 2, 8, 18.<BR> --With आ आ, To hear, Chr. 292, 5 = Rigv. i. 86, 5 (श्रोषन्तु, imperat. of the aor.).<BR> --Caus. To report, MBh. 3, 15260.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To promise, Rām. 2, 76, 3, Seramp.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To be attentive, Chr. 11, 18.<BR> 2. To hear, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 3; MBh. 2, 1244; with abl. To hear from, Vikr. 11, 15.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To hear, MBh. 1, 384.<BR> --With परि परि, To hear, MBh. 1, 3754.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To promise, Rām. 1, 16, 8.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, Caus. To remind one of his promise, Rām. 2, 107, 5.<BR> --With वि वि, pass.<BR> 1. To be heard round about, Rām. 1, 13, 13.<BR> 2. To become famous, Hit. pr. d. 20, M.M. विश्रुत,<BR> 1. Told round about, celebrated, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 12.<BR> 2. Heard, attended to, Amar. 15.<BR> 3. Known.<BR> 4. Famous, Rām. 3, 53, 32.<BR> 5. Pleased, happy.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cry aloud, MBh. 1, 6287.<BR> 2. To fill with noise, to pervade, MBh. 3, 16556. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a " target="_blank">Page0973-a + 42</a>]<BR> 3. To report, MBh. 3, 12266.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, अभिविश्रुत, Celebrated, MBh. 1, 2718.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To hear, MBh. 1, 1627.<BR> 2. Ātm. To promise, MBh. 3, 2143.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to be heard, to cry, Pañc. 172, 25.<BR> 2. To report, MBh. 5, 560.<BR> --Cf. κλύω, κλυτός (= श्रुत), κλέος (= श्रवस्), ἀ-κροάομαι; Lat. clutus, cliens, probably aus-cultare, laudo (for claus-do, cf. श्रवस्); Goth. hrôtheigs, hliuma; A.S. hlúd, hlyd, hlowan (Causal), hlyn, hlyrian(?), hliosa, hlyst, hlystan; O.H.G. hliumunt (= ved. श्रोमन्त), hlôsên.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश्रुत
कु- + श्रुत कु- + श्रुत and दुस्-, adj. imperfectly heard, Pañc. v. d. 1 (कु-); Rām. 3, 41, 10. (दुस्-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुश्रुत
बहु- + श्रुत बहु- + श्रुत, adj. having learned much, Hit. i. d. 25, M.M. Desider. शुश्रूष, Ātm.<BR> 1. To wish to hear, MBh. 3, 13248; to wish to learn, Bhāg. P. 2, 9, 40.<BR> 2. To obey, Indr. 5, 34.<BR> 3. To attend dutifully, Man. 4, 244.<BR> 4. To serve, Man. 10, 100.<BR> 5. To worship, Rām. 1, 8, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
2. श्रु श्रु, see स्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्य
श्रुतर्य श्रुतर्य, m. A proper name, Chr. 296, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतवन्त्|श्रुतवत्
श्रुतवन्त् श्रुत + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Instructed in sacred learning, Bhartṛ. 2, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुति|श्रुतिः
श्रुति श्रु + ति, f.<BR> 1. Hearing, Indr. 2, 5.<BR> 2. An ear, Vikr. d. 56.<BR> 3. Report, Johns. Sel. 53, 127.<BR> 4. The Vedas, the revealed law, Hit. i. d. 31, M.M.; Pañc. 167, 1.<BR> 5. A holy text, Man. 2, 15; 11; 33; Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुति|अश्रुतिः
अ- + श्रुति अ- + श्रुति, f. 1. not hearing, Utt. Rāmac. 69, 11. 2. oblivion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुःश्रुति
चक्षुःश्रुति छक्षुःश्रुति, i. e. चक्षुस्-, m. a snake, Rājat. 5, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णश्रुति
पूर्ण- + श्रुति पूर्ण- + श्रुति (vb. पॄ), adj. having the ears filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाश्रुति
यथा- + श्रुति यथा- + श्रुति, adv. conformable to the precepts of the Vedas, Śāk. d. 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमन्त्|श्रुतिमत्
श्रुतिमन्त् श्रुति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Hearing, Bhag. 13, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुती
श्रुती श्रुती, Rām. 3, 55, 34, for श्रुति, on account of the metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुव|श्रुवः
श्रुव श्रुव, incorrectly for स्रुव, m.<BR> 1. A sacrificial ladle to pour घृत on the fire of a sacrifice, Rām. 6, 96, 12.<BR> 2. Sacrifice, Rām. 2, 62, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रूयमाणत्व
श्रूयमाणत्व श्रूयमाण + त्व (ptcple. pres. pass. of श्रु), + त्व, n. Condition of being heard, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेक्
श्रेक् श्रेक्, see स्रेक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणि|श्रेणिः
श्रेणि श्रेणि, i. e. श्रि + नि, m., f., and णी, f.<BR> 1. A line, a row, Lass. 67, 10; 69, 8.<BR> 2. A troop, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 6; Chr. 34, 13 (णी); Bhartṛ. 2, 28 (णी; भुवन-, all the worlds); ib. 71 (णि; उपकार-, plenty of benefits); Rājat. 5, 331 (शिरस्-श्रेणि, a great quantity of heads).<BR> 3. A company of artisans following the same business, Bhāg. P. 9, 10, 38.<BR> 4. A corporation, Man. 8, 41.<BR> 5. A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदश्रेणि
पद- + श्रेणि पद- + श्रेणि, f. footsteps, Kathās. 33, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयंस्
श्रेयंस् श्रेयंस्, akin to श्री,<BR> I. Comparat. of प्रशस्य (see शंस्).<BR> 1. Better, Hit. iii. d. 3.<BR> 2. Best, Pañc. iii. d. 55; excellent, most beloved, Hit. iii. d. 34. acc. n. यस्, adv. Well, most excellent; with न, Rather--than, Rām. 3, 48, 16.<BR> II. f. यसि, The name of several plants.<BR> III. n. यस्.<BR> 1. Prosperity, Pañc. 182, 1; fortune, Vikr. 68, 7 (pl.); happiness, Pañc. i. d. 344; Kir. 5, 49 (pl.).<BR> 2. Final happiness.<BR> 3. Virtue.<BR> 4. An act leading to the chief temporal good, Man. 3, 223, 224.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेयंस्
अ- + श्रेयंस् अ- + श्रेयंस्, n. evil, Chr. 23, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस
ऽश्रेयस -श्रेयस् + अ, in निस्-, n. Final beatitude, Man. 1, 117; 12, 83; 104. 2. श्वस्-,<BR> I. adj. Happy.<BR> II. ˚सम्, adv. Well.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Happiness.<BR> 2. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्कर
श्रेयस्कर श्रेयस्कर, i. e. श्रेयंस्-कृ + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Effecting happiness, Pañc. 73, 19.<BR> 2. Ensuring felicity, Man. 7, 88.<BR> 3. Making better.<BR> 4. Propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्त्व
श्रेयस्त्व श्रेयस्त्व, i. e. श्रेयंस् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Superiority, Man. 10, 66.<BR> 2. Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठ|श्रेष्ठं|श्रेष्ठः
श्रेष्ठ श्रेष्ठ,<BR> I. Superl. of श्रेयंस्. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a " target="_blank">Page0974-a + 42</a>]<BR> 1. Best, excellent, Lass. 40, 6; of a higher rank, Pañc. iii. d. 219.<BR> 2. Oldest, senior.<BR> 3. Superl. श्रेष्ठ + तम, The very best, Hit. iii. d. 87.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A king.<BR> 2. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 3. Kuvera.<BR> III. n. Cow's milk.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुश्रेष्ठ
कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ, m. an excellent descendant of Kuru, Bharata, Bhṛgu, Chr. 17, 32; 41, 6; 26, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतश्रेष्ठ|भरतश्रेष्ठः
कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ, m. an excellent descendant of Kuru, Bharata, Bhṛgu, Chr. 17, 32; 41, 6; 26, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुश्रेष्ठ|भृगुश्रेष्ठः
कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ कुरु-, भरत-, भृगु- + श्रेष्ठ, m. an excellent descendant of Kuru, Bharata, Bhṛgu, Chr. 17, 32; 41, 6; 26, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिश्रेष्ठ
मुनि- + श्रेष्ठ मुनि- + श्रेष्ठ, m. an excellent sage, Lass. 48, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णश्रेष्ठ|वर्णश्रेष्ठः
वर्ण- + श्रेष्ठ वर्ण- + श्रेष्ठ, adj. being of the best caste, Hit. iv. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठता
श्रेष्ठता श्रेष्ठ + ता, f. Superiority, eminence, Man. 4, 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठिन्
श्रेष्ठिन् श्रेष्ठिन्, i. e. श्रेष्ठ + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Best.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An artist eminent by birth.<BR> 2. The head of a body of persons following the same business, Pañc. 234, 6; i. d. 14, read ˚ठी; Daśak. in Chr. 184, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रै
श्रै श्रै, see श्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रैष्ठ्य|श्रैष्ठ्यं
श्रैष्ठ्य श्रैष्ठ्य, i. e. श्रेष्ठ + य, n. Superiority, Man. 1, 100; 12, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण्
† श्रोण् श्रोण्, श्लोण् श्लोण्, i. 1, Par. To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण श्रोण, adj. Lame, Chr. 296, 8 = Rigv. i. 112, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणि|श्रोणिः
श्रोणि श्रोणि, m., f., and नी, f.<BR> 1. The hips and loins, buttocks, Vikr. d. 100 (णि); Megh. 80 (णी).<BR> 2. A road, a way.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. clunis; κλόνις.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुश्रोणी
पृथु-श्रोणी पृथु-श्रोणी, adj., f. having large buttocks, Indr. 5, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकटितटश्रोणी
महा-कटि-तट-श्रोणी महा-कटि-तट-श्रोणी, adj. having large hips and buttocks, Indr. 2, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्रोणी
सु-श्रोणी सु-श्रोणी, adj., f. καλλίπυγος, Lass. 52, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
श्रोतस् श्रोतस्, i. e. श्रु + तस्, n.<BR> 1. The ear.<BR> 2. An organ of sense; the trunk of an elephant as his special organ, Megh. 43 (Sch.).<BR> 3. Erroneously for स्रोतस्.<BR> 4. श्रोतम्, Padmap. 8, 11, must be changed to श्रौतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ श्रोतृ, i. e. श्रु + तृ, m., f. त्रि, and n. Hearing, a hearer, Hit. ii. d. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्र|श्रोत्रं
श्रोत्र श्रोत्र, i. e. श्रु + त्र, n. The ear, Pañc. v. d. 15.<BR> --Cf. A.S. hleodhor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय श्रोत्रिय, i. e. श्रोत्र + इय,<BR> I. adj. Modest, well-behaved.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Brāhmaṇa conversant with the Vedas, Man. 2, 134 (cf. Sch. ad Śāk. d. 128).<BR> 2. One who observes the religious precepts, Pañc. 110, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रोत्रिय
अ- + श्रोत्रिय अ- + श्रोत्रिय, adj. without learned Brāhmaṇas, Pañc. ii. d. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिश्रोत्रिय|मंत्रिश्रोत्रिय|मन्त्रिश्रोत्रियः
मन्त्रिश्रोत्रिय मन्त्रिश्रोत्रिय, i. e. मन्त्रिन्-, m. a श्रोत्रिय- like minister, Pañc. 25, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत|श्रौतं|श्रौतः
श्रौत श्रौत, i. e. श्रुत + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the ear, hearing.<BR> 2. Relating to sacred learning, on the Vedas, Padmap. 8, 11 (see श्रोतस्).<BR> 3. Prescribed by the Vedas, Śāk. 61, 12.<BR> II. n. Any observance ordained by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट् श्रौषट्, anomal. old conjunct. of the aor. of श्रु (cf. वषट्), indecl. An exclamation used in making an offering to the Manes or gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण श्लक्ष्ण, adj.<BR> 1. Small, slender, thin, Lass. 2. ed. 60, 19.<BR> 2. Smooth, even, soft, Nal. 5, 5; Man. 8, 396; polished, Rām. 1, 13, 32, Seramp.<BR> 3. Mild, amiable, Nal. 8, 12.<BR> 4. Honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णय
श्लक्ष्णय श्लक्ष्णय, a denomin. derived from श्लक्ष्ण, Par. To make thin or small, Pāṇ. iii. 1, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्क्|श्लंक्
श्लङ्क् श्लङ्क्, see श्रङ्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्ग्|श्लंग्
श्लङ्ग् श्लङ्ग्, see श्रङ्ग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ्
श्लथ् श्लथ्, i. 1, and † 10, Par.<BR> 1. To be relaxed, to open, Bhāg. P. 8, 12, 21.<BR> 2. To be weak (cf. श्रथ्). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a " target="_blank">Page0975-a + 42</a>]<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To be relaxed, Bhāg. P. 6, 1, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ श्लथ् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Untied.<BR> 2. Relaxed, Bhartṛ. 1, 25; loose, Vikr. d. 146; flaccid, Ṛt. 6, 8.<BR> 3. Dishevelled (hair).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिश्लथम्
अ-परि-श्लथ + म् अ-परि-श्लथ + म्, adv. very tightly, Utt. Rāmac. 147, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख्
† श्लाख् श्लाख्, i. 1, Par. To pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्
श्लाघ् श्लाघ्, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 3, 13306),<BR> 1. To flatter, Bhaṭṭ. 8, 72.<BR> 2. To praise, MBh. 1, 1; श्लाघ्य, Praiseworthy, Rām. 3, 55, 16.<BR> 3. To boast, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 20. श्लाघ्य, Honourable, ib. 186, 21.<BR> --Caus. To approve, Hit. 61, 6.<BR> --Cf. κρήγυον, probably κόλαξ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा श्लाघ् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Flattery.<BR> 2. Praise, Pañc. iii. d. 33; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1155.<BR> 3. Boasting, Vikr. 56, 15.<BR> 4. Service.<BR> 5. Wish, desire.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्लाघम्
स-श्लाघ + म् स-श्लाघ + म्, adv. praising, Vikr. 52, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघिन्
ऽश्लाघिन् -श्लाघ् + इन्, adj., in रण-, Chr. 20, 19, Praising, desiring combat (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकु|श्लिकुः
श्लिकु श्लिकु,<BR> I. m. A servant.<BR> II. n.(?), Astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
1. श्लिष् श्लिष्, i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 3040); the original signification seems to have been, To adhere (cf. श्रि).<BR> 1. To embrace, Gīt. 1, 44.<BR> 2. To tie, Hit. i. d. 83.<BR> 3. To join, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 19. श्लिष्ट, Touched by, clung or adhered to, leaning on, Rām. 2, 68, 22, Seramp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. To unite.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ,<BR> 1. To embrace, Rām. 2, 96, 22.<BR> 2. To approach, Arj. 6, 12.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, उपाश्लिष्ट, Having [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b " target="_blank">Page0975-b + 39</a>] embraced, Lass. 2. ed. 73, 23.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To embrace, MBh. 3, 10043.<BR> 2. To bring near, Arj. 6, 8.<BR> --With स्वा सु-आ, To embrace tightly, Man. 11, 103.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To embrace, MBh. 4, 515.<BR> 2. With उरसा, To press against one's breast, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 6.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To hold near, Vikr. 78, 11.<BR> 2. To stop, Vikr. 10, 16.<BR> --With वि वि, To burst, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 67. विश्लिष्ट, Separated, disunited.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To separate, Megh. 7.<BR> 2. To disunite, Pañc. 42, 7.<BR> --With सम् सम्, with उरसा, To press against one's breast, Rām. 1, 10, 28. संश्लिष्ट,<BR> 1. Close together, adjoining, touching.<BR> 2. United, joined, Pañc. ii. d. 136.<BR> 3. Endowed, Pañc. 143, 8.<BR> 4. Embraced.<BR> --Caus. To join, MBh. 2, 735.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्लिष्ट
सु- + श्लिष्ट सु- + श्लिष्ट, adj. 1. well fastened, Hit. i. d. 87, M.M. 2. well strung, Mālat. 18, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
2. श्लिष् श्लिष्, see श्रिष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपद|श्लीपदं
श्लीपद श्लीपद, i. e. probably श्लिष्-पद, n. Morbid enlargement of the legs (cf. शिलीपद and the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदिन्
श्लीपदिन् श्लीपदिन्, i. e. श्लीपद + इन्, adj. Club-footed, Man. 3, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील श्लील, i. e. श्री + ल (cf. श्रील), adj. Prosperous.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लील
अ- + श्लील अ- + श्लील, adj. 1. coarse, vulgar. 2. abusive. n. 1. rustic language. 2. untruth. 3. low abuse, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष|श्लेषः
श्लेष श्लेष, i. e. श्लिष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Embracing, an embrace, Utt. Rāmac. 153, 4.<BR> 2. Union.<BR> 3. Association.<BR> 4. Paronomasia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मक|श्लेष्मकः
श्लेष्मक श्लेष्मक, i. e. श्लेष्मन् + क, m. Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण श्लेष्मण, i. e. श्लेष्मन् + अ, adj. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन् श्लेष्मन्, i. e. श्लिष् + मन्, m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a " target="_blank">Page0976-a + 36</a>] The phlegmatic humour, mucus, Man. 4, 132; Pañc. iii. d. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मल|श्लेष्मलः
श्लेष्मल श्लेष्मल, i. e. श्लेष्मन् + अ (with ल् for न्), adj. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मात|श्लेष्मातः
श्लेष्मात श्लेष्मात (akin to the last), m. A small tree, Cordia latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातक|श्लेष्मातकः
श्लेष्मातक श्लेष्मात + क (m.), A tree, Cordia myxa, Man. 6, 14; cf. Rām. 1, 13, 28 (˚कमय क + मय, adj. Made of श्लेष्मातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्
† श्लोक् श्लोक् (rather a denomin. derived from the next), i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To compose verses.<BR> 2. To be composed.<BR> 3. To acquire.<BR> 4. To abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक|श्लोकः
श्लोक श्लोक, i. e. श्रु + क, m.<BR> 1. Fame.<BR> 2. A verse, Pañc. 106, 8; a saying, Chr. 22, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोक|पुण्यश्लोकः
पुण्य- + श्लोक पुण्य- + श्लोक,<BR> I. adj. well-famed, Bhāg. P. 1, 12, 18.<BR> II. m. 1. a name of Nala, Nal. 7, 18. 2. epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira and Viṣṇu.<BR> III. f. का, a name of Damayantī and Sītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण्
श्लोण् श्लोण्, see श्रोण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक्रीडिन्
श्वक्रीडिन् श्वक्रीडिन्, i. e. श्वन्-क्रीडा + इन्, m. A breeder of sporting dogs, Man. 3, 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वघ्निन्
श्वघ्निन् श्वघ्निन् (? nom. sing. घ्नी), m. A gamester, Chr. 295, 10 = Rigv. i. 92, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वङ्क्|श्वंक्
† श्वङ्क् श्वङ्क्, or स्वङ्क् स्वङ्क्, i. 1, Ātm. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वङ्ग्
श्वङ्ग् श्वङ्ग्, see श्रङ्ग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच्
श्वच् श्वच्, see श्वञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज्
श्वज् श्वज्, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वञ्च्|श्वंच्
श्वञ्च् श्वञ्च् (ved.), † श्वच् श्वच्, † शञ्च् शञ्च्, † श्वज् श्वज्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b " target="_blank">Page0976-b + 39</a>] † श्वञ्च् श्वञ्ज्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वञ्ज्
श्वञ्ज् श्वञ्ज्, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् श्वठ्, and श्वण्ठ् श्वण्ठ्, see 4. शठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन् श्वन् (probably from श्वि),<BR> I. m. A dog, Hit. i. d. 112, M.M.<BR> II. f. शुनी, A bitch.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. κύων, ἁλ-κυών; Lat. canis, catulus (based on श्वन्त्, the original form of श्वन्); Goth. hunds (based on श्वन्त्); A.S. hund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशुनी
देव-शुनी देव-शुनी, f. the bitch of the gods, सरमा, MBh. 1, 671.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनश्वन्
वन-श्वन् वन-श्वन्, m. 1. A jackal. 2. a tiger. 3. a civet or polecat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वनर|श्वनरः
श्वनर श्वनर, i. e. श्वन्-नर, m. A base fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपच्
श्वपच् श्वपच्, i. e. श्वन्-पच्, m. and f. A dog-feeder, Man. 3, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपच|श्वपचः
श्वपच श्वपच, i. e. श्वन्-पच् + अ, m., and f. चा,<BR> 1. A dog-feeder.<BR> 2. A man or woman of a low caste, Rājat. 5, 390; 404.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपाक|श्वपाकः
श्वपाक श्वपाक, i. e. श्वन्-पच् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A man of a low and outcaste tribe, Rājat. 5, 217; 382.<BR> 2. The son of a क्षत्तृ by an उग्रा woman, Man. 10, 19.<BR> II. f. की, A woman of a low or outcaste tribe, Rājat. 5, 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र्
† श्वभ्र् श्वभ्र्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To live in distress.<BR> 3. To make a hole, to pierce (cf. the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र|श्वभ्रं
श्वभ्र श्वभ्र, n. A hole, Vikr. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथु|श्वयथुः
श्वयथु श्वयथु, i. e. श्वि + अथु, m. Swelling, intumescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयीची
श्वयीची श्वयीची, i. e. probably श्वि + अ-अञ्च्, f.(?), A disease (tumefaction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वर्त्|श्वर्त्त्
† श्वर्त् श्वर्त्, or स्वर्त् स्वर्त्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To live in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्
† श्वल् श्वल्, श्वल्ल् श्वल्ल्, i. 1, Par. To run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्क्
† श्वल्क् श्वल्क्, i. 10, Par. To speak; cf. शुल्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्ल्
श्वल्ल् श्वल्ल्, see श्वल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववन्त्|श्ववत्
श्ववन्त् श्ववन्त्, i. e. श्वन् + वन्त्, m. A dog-feeder, Man. 4, 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर|श्वशुरः
श्वशुर श्वशुर (for original स्व-शुर; श् for स् by the assimilating influence of the following श्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A father-in-law, a wife's or husband's father, Rām. 3, 53, 5.<BR> 2. du. A father and mother-in-law.<BR> II. f. श्वश्रू, A mother-in-law, Sāv. 3, 20; Rājat. 5, 245.<BR> --Cf. Lat. socer, socrus; Goth. svaihra; A.S. sweger, sweor; ἑκυρός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुरक|श्वशुरकः
श्वशुरक श्वशुर + क, m. A father-in-law, Pañc. 130, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर्य|श्वशुर्यः|श्वशुर्य्य|श्वशुर्य्यः
श्वशुर्य श्वशुर्य, i. e. श्वशुर + य, m. A brother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रू
श्वश्रू श्वश्रू, see श्वशुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
1. श्वस् श्वस्, ii. 2 (but potent. very often, according to i. 1, श्वसेत्), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 690); the original signification seems to have been ‘To pant.’<BR> 1. To breathe, Hit. i. d. 150.<BR> 2. To sigh, Rām. 2, 22, 1.<BR> 3. To hiss, MBh. 4, 2040.<BR> 4. † To kill.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. श्वसित.<BR> 1. Breathing.<BR> 2. Sighing. n.<BR> 1. Breathing.<BR> 2. Breath.<BR> 3. Sighing, Śiś. 9, 65; sigh, Mālat. 11, 9.<BR> --Caus. To (cause to breathe easily, i. e. to) re-create, Rām. 2, 84, 18.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ,<BR> 1. To fetch breath, to revive, MBh. 2, 17.<BR> 2. To recover, Mālat. 64, 4.<BR> 3. To take courage, MBh. 3, 690.<BR> 4. To sigh, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-b " target="_blank">Page0977-b + 42</a>] Bhaṭṭ. 9, 56.<BR> I. आश्वसित, Encouraged, cheered, consoled.<BR> II. आश्वस्त, Recreated, MBh. 3, 13150.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to fetch breath, to cause to recover, MBh. 1, 5406; to refresh, Pañc. 104, 7.<BR> 2. To inspire with courage, Bhag. 11, 30; with hope, Vikr. d. 50.<BR> 3. To console, Rām. 2, 75, 39.<BR> 4. To soothe, to reconcile, Hit. 57, 7. आश्वासित, Blessed, Vikr. d. 154.<BR> --With पर्या परि-आ, Caus. To console, MBh. 3, 11006.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ,<BR> 1. To respire, Rām. 2, 51, 2.<BR> 2. To take courage again, Ragh. 7, 74. प्रत्याश्वस्त, Recollected, Rām. 1, 67, 20; re-created, Megh. 96.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To recover, Vikr. 7, 6.<BR> 2. To calm one's self, Nal. 11, 73.<BR> 3. To take courage, Hit. 103, 18.<BR> 4. To take confidence, Mālat. 20, 10; to confide in, MBh. 3, 16098. समाश्वस्त, Full of confidence, Man. 7, 59.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To encourage, Rām. 1, 17, 29.<BR> 2. To console, MBh. 3, 2679.<BR> 3. To calm, Hit. 90, 21.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To exhale, Mālat. 12, 15.<BR> 2. To breathe, Man. 3, 72.<BR> 3. To pant, MBh. 3, 15690.<BR> 4. To expand, to open (as a flower), Vikr. d. 57; Mālav. d. 31.<BR> 5. To sigh, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 120.<BR> 6. To heave, to rise, Vikr. d. 6. उच्छ्वसित,<BR> 1. Swollen (figurat.), Megh. 98.<BR> 2. n. Loosening, Megh. 69.<BR> 3. n. Breath, Śāk. 31, 10.<BR> --Caus. To refresh, Ṛt. 6, 8, v. r. उच्छ्वासित,<BR> 1. Made loose, Megh. 59.<BR> 2. Fatigued, ib. 71.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To sigh, MBh. 3, 2376.<BR> 2. To hiss, Rām. 3, 53, 55.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To sigh heavily, Pañc. iv. d. 5.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To sigh, Vikr. 21, 14; Rām. 2, 57, 11.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, To sigh heavily, Rām. 2, 85, 19.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a " target="_blank">Page0978-a + 41</a>] confide, Mṛcch. 63, 24.<BR> 2. To put one's trust in, with gen. and loc., Hit. i. d. 85.<BR> 3. To be fearless, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 25.<BR> I. विश्वसित and विश्वस्त, Trusted, confided in.<BR> II. विश्वस्त,<BR> 1. Confided, deserving confidence, Hit. iii. d. 128.<BR> 2. Faithful.<BR> 3. Bold, Rājat. 5, 405.<BR> 4. Full of confidence, fearless, Hiḍ. 2, 25; without any suspicion, Pañc. 33, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To inspire with confidence, Pañc. 33, 7.<BR> --With अभिवि अभि-वि, Caus. To inspire with confidence, MBh. 3, 10021.<BR> --With परिवि परि-वि, To confide completely, to be fearless, MBh. 3, 11451.<BR> --Caus. To console, Rām. 2, 30, 26.<BR> --Cf. Lat. queri, ques + tus; A.S. hweosan, difficulter respirare, and perhaps hysian, hyst, gist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविश्वस्त
सु- + विश्वस्त सु- + विश्वस्त, adj. 1. confidential. 2. without any suspicion, Pañc. 34, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
2. श्वस् श्वस्, probably from श्वि in श्वित्, adv.<BR> 1. To-morrow, Hit. iv. d. 126.<BR> 2. Future, e. g. as former part in श्वस्-श्रेयस, and श्वस् + तन, and cf. श्वोवसीय.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. cras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वस्
परश्वस् परश्वस्, incorrectly for परःश्वस्, i. e. परस्-, adv. The day after to-morrow, Pañc. ed. orn. 41, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसन|श्वसनं|श्वसनः
श्वसन 1. श्वस् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Air, wind, breath, Śiś. 9, 52; Kir. 10, 34.<BR> 2. A plant, Vangueria spinosa.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Breathing, MBh. 8, 4205.<BR> 2. Sighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्तन|श्वस्तनं
श्वस्तन 2. श्वस् + तन, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. What will be to-morrow.<BR> 2. Future.<BR> --Cf. Lat. crastinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्त्य|श्वस्त्यं
श्वस्त्य 2. श्वस् + त्य, adj. What will be to-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान|श्वानः
श्वान श्वान, i. e. श्वन् + अ,<BR> I. m. A dog, Pañc. iii. d. 118.<BR> II. f. नी, A bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वापद|श्वापदः
श्वापद श्वापद, i. e. श्वन्-पद + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b " target="_blank">Page0978-b + 41</a>]<BR> I. adj. Ferocious, relating to a beast of prey.<BR> II. m. A beast of prey, Pañc. ii. d. 124; Lass. 53, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाविध्
श्वाविध् श्वाविध्, i. e. श्वन्-व्यध् m. A porcupine, Man. 5, 18; 12, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वास|श्वासः
श्वास श्वास, i. e. 1. श्वस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Breathing, Pañc. ii. d. 173.<BR> 2. Breath, Rājat. 5, 183.<BR> 3. Air, wind.<BR> 4. Sighing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नश्वास|छिन्नश्वासः
छिन्न- + श्वास छिन्न- + श्वास (vb. छिद्),<BR> I. adj. one who breathes at irregular intervals, Suśr. 1, 115, 17.<BR> II. m. a kind of asthma, ib. 2, 294, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वि
श्वि श्वि, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To swell, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 19.<BR> 2. To increase; ved. शूशुवंस्, anomal. ptcple. of the red. pf. Large, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 92, 15.<BR> 3. † To go.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. शून.<BR> 1. Swelled, swollen, Suśr. 2, 134, 3.<BR> 2. Increased.<BR> 3. Morbidly swollen.<BR> --With the prep. उद् उद्, उच्-छून,<BR> 1. Swollen, Megh. 82; Rājat. 5, 271; turgid.<BR> 2. Lofty, high.<BR> 3. Fat, bulky.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, प्रोच्-छून, Swelled, swollen.<BR> --Cf. κίων, κίω, κινέω; κύω, κῦμα, ἐγ-κισσάω, κίσσα, κύαμος, κοῖλος, κύλα, κύτος, κυτίς, κύαθος, κῶνος, κηκίς and κίκυς (based on the frequent.); Lat. cuneus, cumulus, super-cilia, crescere; Goth. us-hulon; A.S. hol; see शून्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्
श्वित् श्वित् (an old denomin. based on a vb. श्वि, cf. Zend. श्पि-तम, etc.), i. 1, Ātm. (ved. also Par.), To be white.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, To shine, Chr. 295, 12 = Rigv. i. 92, 12 (अश्वैत्, ved. aor.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्र|श्वित्रं
श्वित्र श्वित्र (perhaps better श्वित्त्र, i. e. श्वित् + त्र, or from the lost vb. श्वि [cf. श्वित्], with त्र, as चि + त्र from चि), n. White leprosy (Atharva-V. iii. 27, 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रिन्
श्वित्रिन् श्वित्रिन्, i. e. श्वित्र + इन्, adj., f. इणी, Subject to leprosy, Man. 3, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विन्द्|श्विंद्
श्विन्द् श्विन्द् (akin to श्वि in श्वित्), † i. 1, Ātm. To be white.<BR> --Ptcple. of the red. pf. शिश्विदान.<BR> 1. Innocent.<BR> 2. Guilty.<BR> --Cf. probably κυδνός, κυδρός, κῦδος; Goth. hveits; A.S. hvít; O.H.G. hwîz; Goth. hvaitei; A.S. hvaete; O.H.G. hwaizi, hiza, haiz; A.S. hat; (O.H.G. hei, perhaps from श्वि without the final न्द्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत|श्वेतं|श्वेतः
श्वेत श्वेत (i. e. श्वित् + अ, or from श्वि in श्वित्, श्विन्द्),<BR> I. adj., f. ता and नी, White, Pañc. 60, 24; wearing a white dress, Pañc. iii. d. 73.<BR> II. m., and f. ता, A small white shell used as a coin.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. A white cloud.<BR> 3. The planet Venus.<BR> 4. A fabulous range of mountains.<BR> 5. One of the द्वीपस्, or divisions of the world.<BR> 6. A conch.<BR> 7. Cumin seed.<BR> IV. f. ता.<BR> 1. Crystal.<BR> 2. Candied sugar.<BR> 3. The name of several plants.<BR> V. n. Silver.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्वेत
महा- + श्वेत महा- + श्वेत, f. ता, 1. Sarasvatī. 2. candied sugar. 3. the name of two plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्र्य|श्वैत्र्यं
श्वैत्र्य श्वैत्र्य, i. e. श्वित्र + य, n. Leprosy, Man. 11, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वोवसीय
श्वोवसीय श्वोवसीय, and श्वोवसीयस श्वोवसियस, i. e. curtailed from श्वस्-वसीयस् (comparat. of वसु), or with aff. अ,<BR> I. adj. Fortunate, auspicious.<BR> II. -वसीय, n. Happiness, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ऽष -ष, see पञ्चष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्क|षट्कः
षट्क षट्क, i. e. षष् + क,<BR> I. adj. Six, sixfold.<BR> II. n. An aggregate of six, Pañc. 5, 12; Bhāṣāp. 31.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b " target="_blank">Page0979-b + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिषट्क
ऊर्मि- + षट्क ऊर्मि- + षट्क, n. the six waves (human infirmities), which obstruct the course of quiet life, viz. grief, ignorance, old age, death, hunger, and thirst, Lass. 58, 9 (where thus to be corrected).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चरण|षट्चरणः
षट्चरण षट्चरण, i. e. षष्-चरण, m. A bee, Śāk. d. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पद|षट्पदः
षट्पद षट्पद, i. e. षष्-पद, m. A bee, Man. 7, 129; Vikr. d. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदज्य
षट्पदज्य षट्पद-ज्य (see ज्या), adj. The string of which consists of bees, epithet of the bow of Kāma, Megh. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्घ्रि|षडंघ्रि|षडङ्घ्रिः
षडङ्घ्रि षडङ्घ्रि, i. e. षष्-अङ्घ्रि, m. A bee, Bhartṛ. 1, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ज|षड्जः
षड्ज षड्ज, i. e. षष्-ज, m. The fourth note of the Hindu gamut, Ragh. 1, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्धा
षड्धा षड्धा (?), i. e. षष् + धा, adv. In six ways (see षोढा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ड|षंड|षंडः|षण्डः
षण्ड षण्ड,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A bull at liberty.<BR> 2. An eunuch.<BR> 3. A wood, a thicket, Megh. 20.<BR> 4. A multitude.<BR> II. m. and n. A quantity of lotuses.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलषण्ड
कमल- + षण्ड कमल- + षण्ड, n. a multitude of lotuses, Lass. 2. ed. 46, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुषण्ड|तरुषंड|तरुषण्डः
तरु- + षण्ड तरु- + षण्ड and द्रुम-, n. a group of trees, Pañc. 10, 4; Rām. 4, 13, 13 (तरु-); 4, 13, 12. (द्रुम-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मषण्ड|पद्मषंड
पद्म- + षण्ड पद्म- + षण्ड, n. a quantity of lotuses, ib. 3, 76, 15 (cf. शण्ड, शण्ढ, षण्ढ, and खण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्डक|षंडक|षंडकः|षण्डकः
षण्डक षण्ड + क, m. An eunuch. MBh. 4, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ढ|षंढ|षंढः|षण्ढः
षण्ढ षण्ढ, m. An eunuch, Man. 2, 158 (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्
षष् षष्, for original स्वक्ष्, numeral adj. Six, Man. 1, 16; cf. षष्-भाग.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sex; ἕξ, ϝέξ; Goth. saihs; A.S. seox, six, sex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषष्
द्वि- + षष् द्वि- + षष्, twelve Bhāg. P. 4, 1, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ट
ऽषष्ट -षष्ट, i. e. षष्टि + अ, ord. num. Sixtieth.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकषष्ट
एक- + षष्ट एक- + षष्ट, sixtyfirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकोनषष्ट
एकोन- + षष्ट एकोन- + षष्ट, i. e. एक-ऊन-, fifty-ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाषष्ट
द्वा- + षष्ट द्वा- + षष्ट and द्वि-, sixty-second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषष्ट
त्रि- + षष्ट त्रि- + षष्ट, sixty-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःषष्ट
चतुःष्ट चतुःष्˚ i. e. चतुर्-, sixty-fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चषष्ट|पंचषष्ट
पञ्चष्ट पञ्चष्˚, i. e. पञ्चन्-, sixty-fifth, etc., MBh. xii. adhy. 61, sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टि|षष्टिः
षष्टि षष्टि, i. e. षष् + ति, numeral, f. Sixty, Chr. 28, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकषष्टि|एकषष्टिः
एक- + षष्टि एक- + षष्टि, f. sixty-one, Bhāg. P. 6, 6, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाषष्टि
द्वा- + षष्टि द्वा- + षष्टि and द्वि-, f. sixty-two, MBh. xii. 162; i. adhy. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःषष्टि|चतुःषष्टिः
चतुःषष्टि चतुःष्˚, i. e. चतुर्-, f. sixty-four, Man. 8, 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चषष्टि|पंचषष्टि|पञ्चषष्टिः
पञ्चषष्टि पञ्चष्˚, i. e. पञ्चन्-, f. sixty-five, MBh. xii. adhy. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक|षष्टिकः
षष्टिक षष्टि + क,<BR> I. adj. Bought with sixty.<BR> II. m., and f. का, A kind of rice of quick growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक्य|षष्टिक्यं
षष्टिक्य षष्टिक्य, i. e. षष्टिक + य, adj. Fit for the rice called षष्टिक (see the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टितम|षष्टितमः
षष्टितम षष्टि + तम, ord. num., f. मी, Sixtieth, Rām. v. sarg. 60.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकषष्टितम
एक- + षष्टितम एक- + षष्टितम, sixty-first, Rām. v. sarg. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाषष्टितम
द्वा- + षष्टितम द्वा- + षष्टितम and द्वि-, sixty-second, Rām. iv. sarg. 62; v. adhy. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषष्टितम
त्रि- + षष्टितम त्रि- + षष्टितम, sixtythird, MBh. i. adhy. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःषष्टितम
चतुःषष्टितम चतुःष्˚, i. e. चतुर्-, sixty-fourth, Rām. vi. sarg. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चषष्टितम
पञ्चषष्टितम पञ्चष्˚, i. e. पन्चन्-, sixty-fifth, MBh. ii. adhy. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवषष्टितम
नवषष्टित्म नवष्˚, i. e. नवन्-, sixty-ninth, Rām. vi. sarg. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिधा
षष्टिधा षष्टि + धा, adv. In sixty ways.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषष्टिधा
त्रि- + षष्टिधा त्रि- + षष्टिधा, adv. in sixty-three parts, Suśr. 1, 153, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठ|षष्ठः
षष्ठ षष्ठ, i. e. षष् + थ,<BR> I. ord. num., f. ठी, Sixth, Vikr. d. 20.<BR> II. f. ठा.<BR> 1. Durgā.<BR> 2. The sixth day of the lunar fortnight.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sextus; Goth. saihsta; A.S. sixta; ἕκτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृषष्ठ
मातृ- + षष्ठ मातृ- + षष्ठ, adj. six, inclusively of the mother, Hiḍ. 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठक|षष्ठकः
षष्ठक षष्ठ + क, adj. Sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नकालता
षष्ठान्नकालता षष्ठान्नकालता, i. e. षष्ठ-अन्न-काल + ता, f. Eating only at the time of the sixth meal, i. e. on the evening of every third day, Man. 11, 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडव|षाडवः
षाडव षाडव (derived anomal. from the nom. of षष्), m.<BR> 1. Sentiment.<BR> 2. Music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्य|षाड्गुण्यं
षाड्गुण्य षाड्गुण्य, i. e. षष्-गुण + य, n. An aggregate of six, six articles, Man. 7, 58; six measures, 7, 167; six kinds of behaving against an enemy, Pañc. 154, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मासिक
षाण्मासिक षाण्मासिक, i. e. षष्-मास + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to six months, come to pass six months ago, Bṛhaspati ap. Cowell, Kusumāñjali transl. p. 65, n. †.<BR> 2. Half-yearly, Man. 7, 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिड्ग|षिड्गः
षिड्ग षिड्ग, m. An inconstant lover, a gallant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुक्क्
षुक्क् षुक्क्, see ष्वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडन्त्|षोडत्
षोडन्त् षोडन्त्, i. e. षष्-दन्त्, m. A young ox, or one with six teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडश|षोडशः
षोडश षोडश, i. e. षोडशन् + अ, or curtailed, ord. num., f. शी, Sixteenth, Pañc. ii. d. 58.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषोडश
परि- + षोडश परि- + षोडश, full sixteen, Nal. 26, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभषोडश
वृषभ- + षोडश वृषभ- + षोडश (having a bull as sixteenth, i. e.) fifteen cows and a bull, Man. 9, 124, v. r. (cf. Lois.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशक
षोडशक षोडशक, i. e. षोडशन् + क, adj. Consisting of sixteen, Hit. iv. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशन्
षोडशन् षोडशन्, i. e. षष्-दशन्, numeral adj. Sixteen, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 3; 182, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोढा
षोढा षोढा, i. e. षष् + धा, adv. In six ways, sixfold, Yājñ. 3, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टम्भ्
ष्टम्भ् ष्टम्भ्, see स्तम्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ट्यै
ष्ट्यै ष्ट्यै, see स्त्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठिव्
ष्ठिव् † ष्ठिव्, i. 1, ष्ठीव, and i. 4, ष्ठीव्य, and ष्ठीव् ष्ठीव्, i. 1, Par. To spit, Bhaṭṭ. 12, 18.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ष्ठ्यूत, Ejected, as saliva.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, To spit, Man. 5, 145. निष्ठ्यूत, Spit out, Rājat. 5, 462 (कूर्च-आभाषण-, spit out, i. e. uttered, with boasting words); ejected, ib. 96. n. Saliva, Man. 4, 132.<BR> --With अवनि अव-नि, To spit on, Man. 8, 282.<BR> --With निस् निस्, To sketch, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 18. निःष्ठ्यूत, Distilled, Śāk. d. 80.<BR> --Cf. probably σίαλον, σίαλος, στυγέω, στύξ, etc., σπῖλος, σπιλόω, ψύττω, πτύω, ἐπι-ϕθύζω; Lat. spuere; Goth. speivan; A.S. spíwan; O.H.G. spîchilla; cf. क्षिव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवन|ष्ठीवनं
ष्ठीवन ष्ठीव् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Spitting.<BR> 2. Spittle, Man. 4, 156; 5, 123.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्चष्ठीवन
कूर्च- + ष्ठीवन कूर्च- + ष्ठीवन, n. boasting speech, Rājat. 5, 462 (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वस्क्
† ष्वस्क् ष्वस्क्, स्वष्क् ष्वष्क्, ष्वक्क् ष्वक्क्, षुक्क् षुक्क्, स्वस्क् स्वस्क्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स स, originally ‘One.’<BR> I. See तद्; in the Vedas appears also the loc. सस्मिन्.<BR> II. As former part of comp. nouns.<BR> 1. With; see स-कमल, adj. With lotus flowers.<BR> 2. The same, like, equal; see स-धर्मन्, adj. Of the same caste, etc.<BR> --Cf. σ in σήμερον, ὁ, ἡ, οἱ, αἱ, ἑ in ἕεις, εἷς (e. g. in ἑ-ϝενς), ἁ- (e. g. in ἁ-πλοῦς), ἀ- (e. g. in ἀδελϕός), ὀ- (e. g. in ὄ-πατρος); Lat. sum = eum, sam = eam, -sum, sem- in semper, sim- in simplex; Goth. sa, so; A.S. se, seo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्|संयन्त्
संयत् संयत्, i. e. सम्-यम् + त्, m. and f. War, battle, Chr. 36, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयन्तृ|संयंतृ
संयन्तृ संयन्तृ, i. e. सम्-यम् + तृ, m. f. त्री, and n. Constraining, a constrainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयम|संयमः
संयम संयम, i. e. सम्-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Restraining, Man. 2, 88.<BR> 2. Restraint, forbearance.<BR> 3. Abstaining, Bhartṛ. 2, 60.<BR> 4. Avoiding the infliction of pain on others, compassionateness, Śāk. d. 177.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्संयम|वाक्संयमः
वाक्संयम वाक्संयम, i. e. वाच्-, m. modesty, Bhartṛ. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमन|संयमनं|संयमनः
संयमन संयमन, i. e. सम्-यम् + अन,<BR> I. m. A ruler, Sāv. 5, 65.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Restraining, Sāv. 3, 20.<BR> 2. Selfdenial or control, forbearance.<BR> 3. A religious vow or obligation.<BR> 4. Holding, detaining.<BR> 5. Drawing in, Śāk. 5, 12.<BR> 6. A cluster of four houses.<BR> III. f. नी, The capital of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमिन्
संयमिन् संयमिन्, i. e.<BR> I. सम्-यम् + इन्, adj. Who or what restrains, subdues; abstaining, Bhag. 2, 69.<BR> II. संयम + इन्, m. One who subdues his passions, a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयात्रा
संयात्रा संयात्रा, i. e. सम्-या + त्र, f. Travelling into another island or continent, voyaging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयान|संयानं|संयानः
संयान संयान, i. e. सम्-या + अन, n. Going together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाम|संयामः
संयाम संयाम, i. e. सम्-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Restraint.<BR> 2. Self-control, forbearance.<BR> 3. Abstaining from giving pain to others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाव|संयावः
संयाव संयाव, i. e. सम्-यु + अ, m. A thin cake of unleavened bread fried with melted butter, Man. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुग|संयुगः
संयुग संयुग, i. e. सम्-युज् + अ, m. War, battle, Chr. 33, 4; Rājat. 5, 424.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुज्
संयुज् संयुज्, i. e. सम्-युज्, adj.<BR> 1. Joined.<BR> 2. Endowed with good qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोग|संयोगः
संयोग संयोग, i. e. सम्-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Connexion, Man. 3, 157; Rām. 3, 49, 20; Chr. 38, 15 (संयोगम् एनसा न प्राप्स्यसे, You will not incur guilt).<BR> 2. Junction, Bhāṣāp. 3; adherence, accession, Pañc. ii. d. 146.<BR> 3. A kind of alliance where both parties unite only for one object, but attack with united power, Hit. iv. d. 115.<BR> 4. Union, being, living, with, Megh. 85; 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजन|संयोजनं
संयोजन संयोजन, i. e. सम्-युज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Joining, uniting, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 20; Daśak. in Chr. 281, 2.<BR> 2. Copulation, coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षण|संरक्षणं
संरक्षण संरक्षण, i. e. सम्-रक्ष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Protecting, guarding, Pañc. 129, 2; protection, Johns. Sel. 95, 71.<BR> 2. Saving, Man. 6, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भ|संरंभ|संरंभः|संरम्भः
संरम्भ संरम्भ, i. e. सम्-रभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Beginning, Vikr. d. 61.<BR> 2. Wrath, Vikr. d. 115; rage, anger, Vikr. d. 39.<BR> 3. Pride, arrogance.<BR> 4. Agitation, Rājat. 5, 334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भिन्|संरंभिन्
संरम्भिन् संरम्भिन्, i. e. संरम्भ + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Angry.<BR> 2. Proud.<BR> 3. Agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधन|संराधनं
संराधन संराधन, i. e. सम्-रध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Propitiation.<BR> 2. Perfect meditation, Windischmann, Sankara, 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराव|संरावः
संराव संराव, i. e. सम्-रु + अ, m. Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरोध|संरोधः
संरोध संरोध, i. e. सम्-रुध् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hindering, stopping, Pañc. 162, 11; Mālat. 79, 18.<BR> 2. Impediment.<BR> 3. Check, curb.<BR> 4. Fetter.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंरोध|कालसंरोधः
काल- + संरोध काल- + संरोध, m. expiry of the time (for which something has been pledged), Man. 8, 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलय|संलयः
संलय संलय, i. e. सम्-ली + अ, m. Sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलाप|संलापः
संलाप संलाप, i. e. सम्-लप् + अ, m. Conversation, Hit. i. d. 38, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलोडन|संलोडनं
संलोडन संलोडन, i. e. सम्-लोड् + अन, n. Making mad, MBh. 1, 1397.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्|संवन्त्
संवत् संवत्, probably सम्-*वत् (cf. परुत्), indecl.<BR> 1. A year.<BR> 2. A year of विक्रमादित्यऽस् era.<BR> --Cf. ἔτος, ἐνιαυτός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्सर|संवत्सरः
संवत्सर संवत्सर, i. e. सम्-वत्सर, m. A year, Rām. 3, 55, 19; Pañc. 186, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसंवत्सर|परिसंवत्सरः
परि- + संवत्सर परि- + संवत्सर, m. a full year, Man. 3, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवदन|संवदनं
संवदन संवदन, i. e. सम्-वद् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. ना (cf. the next).<BR> 1. Subduing by charms or magical drugs.<BR> 2. A charm.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Communication of tidings.<BR> 2. Sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवनन|संवननं
संवनन संवनन, i. e. सम्-वन् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Subduing by charms or magical drugs; a means of securing, Ragh. 16, 74.<BR> 2. Fascination, charming, Rājat. 5, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवरण|संवरणं
संवरण संवरण, i. e. सम्-वृ + अन, n. Concealing, Vikr. 79, 5; secret, Mālat. 174, 7; pretext, Mālat. 7, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त|संवर्तः|संवर्त्त|संवर्त्तः
संवर्त संवर्त, i. e. सम्-वृत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Destruction of the universe, Johns. Sel. 91, 35.<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> 3. Multitude, Mālat. 166, 12.<BR> 4. Being.<BR> 5. Beleric myrobalan.<BR> 6. The name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तक|संवर्तकः|संवर्त्तक|संवर्त्तकः
संवर्तक संवर्त + क, m.<BR> 1. Submarine fire, Bhartṛ. 2, 68.<BR> 2. Baladeva.<BR> 3. The plough of Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्ति|संवर्तिः|संवर्त्ति|संवर्त्तिः
संवर्ति संवर्ति, and संवर्तिका संवर्तिका (vb. वृत्), f. The new leaf of a water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धक|संवर्द्धकः
संवर्धक संवर्धक, i. e. सम्-वृध् + अक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a " target="_blank">Page0983-a + 40</a>] adj. Augmenting, augmentative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धन|संवर्द्धनं|संवर्धनं
संवर्धन संवर्धन, i. e. सम्-वृध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Increasing, thriving, increase, Vikr. 49, 16; happiness, Vikr. 57, 2.<BR> 2. Bearing up, nourishing and developing, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्षण
संवर्षण संवर्षण, i. e. सम्-वृष् + अन, or rather सम्-वर्षन, n. Abundance of rain, Lass. 27, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवलन|संवलनं
संवलन संवलन, i. e. सम्-वल् + अन, n. Mixture, Mālat. 167, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवसथ|संवसथः
संवसथ संवसथ, i. e. सम्- 1. वस् + अथ, m. A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाद|संवादः
संवाद संवाद, i. e. सम्-वद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Conversation, Pañc. 118, 25.<BR> 2. Communication of intelligence, information, Mālat. 80, 5.<BR> 3. Assent, agreement, Mālav. 72, 8.<BR> 4. Conformity, correspondence, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवादिन्
संवादिन् संवादिन्, i. e. सम्-वद् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Corresponding, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवास|संवासः
संवास संवास, i. e. सम्- 1. वस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Dwelling together, Pañc. 196, 15.<BR> 2. Society, union, Hit. iv. d. 65.<BR> 3. A house.<BR> 4. An open space within or without a town for the meeting of the townsmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाह|संवाहः
संवाह संवाह, m., i. e. सम्-वाह् + अ,<BR> 1. Rubbing the body.<BR> 2. An attendant employed to rub and knead the body.<BR> 3. Extortion, Rājat. 5, 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहक|संवाहकः
संवाहक संवाहक, i. e. सम्-वाह् + अक, m. An attendant employed to rub and knead the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहन|संवाहनं
संवाहन संवाहन, i. e. सम्-वा̆ह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Bearing, carrying, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 15.<BR> 2. Rubbing and kneading the body, Megh. 94; stroking, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b " target="_blank">Page0983-b + 41</a>] touching, Mālat. 150, 10.<BR> 3. Extortion, Rājat. 5, 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविज्ञान
संविज्ञान संविज्ञान, i. e. सम्-वि-ज्ञा + अन, n. Knowledge, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवित्ति|संवित्तिः
संवित्ति संवित्ति, i. e. सम्-विद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Perception, knowledge, Kir. 11, 34; 16, 32.<BR> 2. Recollection of a thing or person previously known.<BR> 3. Reconciliation, accommodation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्
संविद् संविद्, i. e. सम्-विद्, f.<BR> 1. Contract, agreement, Man. 8, 5; Pañc. ii. d. 60.<BR> 2. Promise, MBh. 1, 1223.<BR> 3. Intellect.<BR> 4. Knowledge, Mālat. 100, 10; Kir. 18, 42.<BR> 5. Name, appellation.<BR> 6. Sign, signal.<BR> 7. A watch-word, a battle-cry.<BR> 8. Battle.<BR> 9. Institute.<BR> 10. Pleasing.<BR> 11. Hemp.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसंविद्
न- + संविद् न- + संविद्, f. want of consciousness, Bhartṛ. 1, 27, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधा
संविधा संविधा, i. e. सम्-वि-धा, f.<BR> 1. Arrangement, food, Ragh. 14, 17.<BR> 2. Kind of living, Ragh. 1, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधान|संविधानं
संविधान संविधान, i. e. सम्-वि-धा + अन, n. Mode, Mālat. 34, 11; rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधानक|संविधानकं
संविधानक संविधान + क, n. Strange, surprising occurrence, Utt. Rāmac. 87, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभाग|संविभागः
संविभाग संविभाग, i. e. सम्-वि-भज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Distributing, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 22.<BR> 2. Apportioning, giving a portion, Man. 4, 32; Pañc. ii. d. 25.<BR> 3. Communication, Mālat. 128, 12.<BR> 4. Part, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभागिन्
संविभागिन् संविभागिन्, i. e. संविभाग + इन्, adj. Partaking, Pañc. 243, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीक्षण|संवीक्षणं
संवीक्षण संवीक्षण, i. e. सम्-वि-इक्ष् + अन, n. Search, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृति|संवृतिः
संवृति संवृति, i. e. सम्-वृ + ति, f. Concealment, Kir. 10, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेग|संवेगः
संवेग संवेग, i. e. सम्-विज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Haste proceeding from fear, Utt. Rāmac. 51, 14.<BR> 2. Speed, Utt. Rāmac. 26, 12 (तीव्र-, adj. Wounding quickly).<BR> 3. Vehemence, Utt. Rāmac. 95, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेद|संवेदः
संवेद संवेद, i. e. सम्-विद् + अ, m. Perception, consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेदन|संवेदनं
संवेदन संवेदन, i. e. सम्-विद् + अन, n. Perceiving, suffering, Utt. Rāmac. 30, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेश|संवेशः
संवेश संवेश, i. e. सम्-विश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Copulation.<BR> 2. A chair.<BR> 3. Sleeping, sleep.<BR> 4. Dreaming, a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेशक
संवेशक संवेशक, see गृहसंव्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यवहार|संव्यवहारः
संव्यवहार संव्यवहार, i. e. सम्-वि-अव-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Relation to each other, Pañc. i. d. 316.<BR> 2. Business, Man. 8, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यान|संव्यानं
संव्यान संव्यान, i. e. सम्-व्ये + अन, n.<BR> 1. Cloth, vesture.<BR> 2. Covering.<BR> 3. An upper garment, Kir. 4, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशप्तक|संशप्तकः
संशप्तक संशप्तक, i. e. सम्-शप्त + क (vb. शप्), m.<BR> 1. A soldier sworn never to recede, and stationed to prevent the flight of the rest.<BR> 2. A brother in arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशमन
संशमन संशमन, i. e. सम्-शम् + अन, in पाप-, adj. Removing sin, Rām. 2, 56, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय|संशयः
संशय संशय, i. e. सम्-शी + अ, m.<BR> 1. Doubt, Hit. pr. d. 10, M.M.; uncertainty; very often with न, to be sure, Pañc. i. d. 256.<BR> 2. Possibility, Hit. ii. d. 160.<BR> 3. Danger, Rām. 3, 51, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
अ- + संशय अ- + संशय, 1. m. absence of doubt, to be sure, Rām. 5, 23, 25. 2. ˚यम्, adv. undoubtedly, Pañc. i. d. 406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंशय
अर्थ- + संशय अर्थ- + संशय, adj. one whose solvency is doubtful, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंशय
निस्- + संशय निस्- + संशय, adj. 1. doubtless, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b " target="_blank">Page0984-b + 42</a>] Brāhmaṇav. 2, 30. 2. resolute, MBh. 5, 7080. 3. ˚यम्, adv. undoubtedly, certainly, MBh. 3, 1243.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसंशय|प्राणसंशयः
प्राण- + संशय प्राण- + संशय, m. danger of life, Pañc. 130, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंशयम्
वि-संशय + म् वि-संशय + म्, adv. undoubtedly, Pañc. ii. d. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंशय
स- + संशय स- + संशय, adj. doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयालु|संशयालुः
संशयालु संशयालु, i. e. संशय + आलु, adj. Dubious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयितृ
संशयितृ संशयितृ, i. e. सम्-शी + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Dubious, sceptical, a sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्धि|संशुद्धिः
संशुद्धि संशुद्धि, i. e. सम्-शुध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Cleaning the body.<BR> 2. Purification, Bhag. 16, 1.<BR> 3. Correction.<BR> 4. Acquittal of debt.<BR> 5. Acquittance of charge or crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधन|संशोधनं
संशोधन संशोधन, i. e. सम्-शुध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Cleaning.<BR> 2. Purifying.<BR> 3. Correcting.<BR> 4. Refining.<BR> 5. Discharging, paying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चत्
संश्चत् संश्चत्, i. e. सम्-चत्, m. A juggler, a conjuror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चाय
संश्चाय संश्चाय, a denomin. derived from संश्चत्, Ātm. To conjure, to juggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रय|संश्रयः
संश्रय संश्रय, i. e. सम्-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Refuge, a dwelling-place, Pañc. 155, 23; having become the dwellingplace, being possessed by, Nal. 20, 41.<BR> 2. Asylum.<BR> 3. Protection, Śāk. d. 177.<BR> 4. Seeking protection (Man. 7, 160), or the alliance of a powerful prince, Pañc. 154, 10.<BR> 5. Alliance, Pañc. 154, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यसंश्रय|अन्योन्यसंश्रयः
अन्योन्य- + संश्रय अन्योन्य- + संश्रय, m. supporting each other, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसंश्रय
एक- + संश्रय एक- + संश्रय, m.<BR> I. union, Pañc. iii. d. 52.<BR> II. adj. united, Pañc. iii. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टसंश्रय
कष्ट- + संश्रय कष्ट- + संश्रय, adj. accompanied by pains, Pañc. i. d. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजसंश्रय
भुज- + संश्रय भुज- + संश्रय, m. taking refuge to one's arms, help of arms, Lass. 2. ed. 68. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रव|संश्रवः
संश्रव संश्रव, i. e. सम्-श्रु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hearing, Mālat. 48, 17.<BR> 2. Agreement. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a " target="_blank">Page0985-a + 41</a>]<BR> 3. Promise.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
अ- + संश्रव अ- + संश्रव, m. the not being audible; loc. वे, out of hearing, Man. 2, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रवण|संश्रवणं
संश्रवण संश्रवण, i. e. सम्-श्रु + अन, n. The ear, Rām. 6, 23, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेष|संश्लेषः
संश्लेष संश्लेष, i. e. सम्-श्लिष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Embracing, embrace, Śāk. d. 124.<BR> 2. Union, Windischmann, Sankara, 152; contact, association, Lass. 24, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघटितसंश्लेष
अ-घटित- + संश्लेष अ-घटित- + संश्लेष, adj., f. षा, impossible to be closely joined, Pañc. 203, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषण|संश्लेषणं
संश्लेषण संश्लेषण, i. e. सम्-श्लिष् + अन, n. Means of binding together, Utt. Rāmac. 65, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्ति|संसक्तिः
संसक्ति संसक्ति, i. e. सम्-सञ्ज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Tieing, fastening.<BR> 2. Union.<BR> 3. Proximity.<BR> 4. Intimacy, acquaintance.<BR> 5. Addiction to, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद् संसद्, i. e. सम्-सद्, f.<BR> 1. An assembly, Pañc. 19, 14.<BR> 2. Court of justice, Man. 8, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरण|संसरणं
संसरण संसरण, i. e. सम्-सृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going, proceeding.<BR> 2. Going unobstructedly.<BR> 3. The unresisted march of troops.<BR> 4. The beginning of war or battle.<BR> 5. A highway.<BR> 6. A resting-place for passengers near the gates of a city.<BR> 7. Birth, the production of living beings.<BR> 8. The world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ग|संसर्गः
संसर्ग संसर्ग, i. e. सम्-सृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Mixture, Hit. i. d. 5, M.M.<BR> 2. Touching, contact, Śāk. d. 3; Pañc. i. d. 280.<BR> 3. Union, Hit. pr. d. 41, M.M.<BR> 4. Acquaintance, familiarity, intercourse, Pañc. iii. d. 234; Daśak. in Chr. 196, 3.<BR> 5. Sensual attachment, Man. 6, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गतस्
संसर्गतस् संसर्ग + तस्, adv. By union and intercourse, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गिन्
संसर्गिन् संसर्गिन्, i. e. संसर्ग + इन्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b " target="_blank">Page0985-b + 41</a>] adj. f. इणी, adj.<BR> 1. In contact with, united, connected, Cāṇ. 106 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 413.<BR> 2. Familiar, acquainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्जन|संसर्जनं|संसर्ज्जन
संसर्जन संसर्जन, i. e. सम्-सृज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Abandoning, leaving.<BR> 2. Voiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्प|संसर्पः
संसर्प संसर्प, i. e. सम्-सृप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Creeping.<BR> 2. Gliding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसार|संसारः
संसार संसार, i. e. सम्-सृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Transmigration, Man. 12, 40.<BR> 2. Mundane existence, Pañc. 165, 17.<BR> 3. The world, Hit. pr. d. 14, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसार
आ- + संसार आ- + संसार, adj. always changing, Kathās. 5, 103. ˚रम्, adv. till the end of the world, Rājat. 5, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारिन्
संसारिन् संसारिन्, i. e. संसार + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी, Mundane, worldly.<BR> II. m. An animal or sentient being, a man, Mālat. 140, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्धि|संसिद्धिः
संसिद्धि संसिद्धि, i. e. सम्-सिध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Perfection, Bhag. 3, 20; Pañc. 4, 21.<BR> 2. Obtaining, Kathās. 13, 166.<BR> 3. Natural disposition, nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृति|संसृतिः
संसृति संसृति, i. e. सम्-सृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Current, stream.<BR> 2. Course, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 9.<BR> 3. Transmigration, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 14.<BR> 4. The world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टत्व|संसृष्टत्वं
संसृष्टत्व संसृष्ट + त्व (vb. सृज्), n.<BR> 1. Union.<BR> 2. (In law), The voluntary co-residence of father and son, or brothers, after partition of property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टि|संसृष्टिः
संसृष्टि संसृष्टि, i. e. सम्-सृज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Uniting.<BR> 2. Collecting.<BR> 3. Living together in one family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेक|संसेकः
संसेक संसेक, i. e. सम्-सिच् + अ, m. Moistening, Rājat. 5, 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवन
संसेवन संसेवन, i. e. सम्-सेव् + अन, n. Waiting on, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवा
संसेवा संसेवा, i. e. सम्-सेव् + अ, f. Service, Rājat. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कर्तृ|संस्कर्त्तृ
संस्कर्तृ संस्कर्तृ, i. e. सम्-कृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what completes, initiates, Utt. Rāmac. 170, 8; dresses (as meat), Man. 5, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कार|संस्कारः
संस्कार संस्कार, i. e. सम्-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Completing.<BR> 2. Perfecting, perfection, Utt. Rāmac. 135, 6.<BR> 3. Embellishment, decoration, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 19; Pañc. 185, 25; ornament, Mālat. 126, 9.<BR> 4. Institution and education, Man. 1, 111.<BR> 5. Purification.<BR> 6. A purificatory rite, Man. 2, 26; 27; Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 13.<BR> 7. Ceremony in general, Man. 3, 43.<BR> 8. The investiture with the holy cord, Man. 11, 150.<BR> 9. Consecration (of a king), Man. 7, 2.<BR> 10. Obsequies, Lass. 17, 11.<BR> 11. Purity.<BR> 12. Preparing as an article of medicine or food.<BR> 13. Impression, form, mould, Śāk. d. 133 (Sch. a polishing stone).<BR> 14. The power of memory, Kathās. 7, 19.<BR> 15. Apprehension, conception, Rājat. 5, 228; resolution, Hit. 112, 5 (वि-स्मृत-पूर्व-, adj. Forgetting his former resolution).<BR> 16. The selfreproductive quality (Ballantyne, i. e. vitality, elasticity, and mental impression), Bhāṣāp. 29; 156.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसंस्कार|अग्निसंस्कारः
अग्नि- + संस्कार अग्नि- + संस्कार, m. 1. consecration of fire. 2. burning of the dead body, Man. 5, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंस्कार
दुस्- + संस्कार दुस्- + संस्कार, m. bad inclination, Rājat. 5, 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशसंस्कार
केश- + संस्कार केश- + संस्कार, m. dressing the hair, Megh. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंस्कार|पात्रसंस्कारः
पात्र- + संस्कार पात्र- + संस्कार, m. cleaning a vessel that has been used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंस्कार|पुनःसंस्कारः
पुनःसंस्कार पुनःसंस्कार, i. e. पुनर्-, m. renewed investiture, Man. 11, 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरसंस्कार|शरीरसंस्कारः
शरीर- + संस्कार शरीर- + संस्कार, m. 1. adorning the person. 2. purification of the body by various ceremonies, initiation, etc., Man. 2, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्क्रिया
संस्क्रिया संस्क्रिया, i. e. सम्-कृ + या, f.<BR> 1. Any purificatory rite.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b " target="_blank">Page0986-b + 41</a>] Funeral ceremonies, as burning the dead body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्
संस्त् संस्त्, see सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भ|संस्तंभ|संस्तंभः|संस्तम्भः
संस्तम्भ संस्तम्भ, i. e. सम्-स्तम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Fixing, making firm (as a post).<BR> 2. Confirming.<BR> 3. Stop.<BR> 4. Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तर|संस्तरः
संस्तर संस्तर, i. e. सम्-स्तृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A couch, a bed, Pañc. 117, 12; a layer, MBh. 1, 4708.<BR> 2. Sacrifice, Rām. 1, 13, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तरण
संस्तरण संस्तरण, i. e. सम्-स्तृ + अन, n. Strewing, Śāk. 31, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तव|संस्तवः
संस्तव संस्तव, i. e. सम्-स्तु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Praise, Pañc. iv. d. 60.<BR> 2. Acquaintance, Kir. 4, 22. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्ताव|संस्तावः
संस्ताव संस्ताव, i. e. सम्-स्तु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hymning in chorus, the repetition of the verses of the Veda by a number of Brāhmaṇas.<BR> 2. The place occupied at a sacrifice by the singing Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुति|संस्तुतिः
संस्तुति संस्तुति, i. e. सम्-स्तु + ति, f. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्याय|संस्त्यायः
संस्त्याय संस्त्याय, i. e. सम्-स्त्यै + अ, m.<BR> 1. Assemblage, heap.<BR> 2. Vicinity.<BR> 3. Spreading, diffusion.<BR> 4. A house, Mālat. 23, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थ|संस्थः
संस्थ संस्थ,<BR> A. i. e. सम्-स्थ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Standing, being, Pañc. i. d. 231 (मण्दल-, in the disc, viz. of the sun); ii. d. 157.<BR> 2. Staying with, associated.<BR> 3. Stationary, fixed.<BR> 4. Living, Pañc. 94, 2; iii. d. 226.<BR> 5. Lasting, Lass. 42, 15.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An inhabitant.<BR> 2. A countryman.<BR> 3. A spy.<BR> B. i. e. सम्-स्था, f.<BR> 1. An assembly.<BR> 2. Condition of being, situation, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 38.<BR> 3. Appearance.<BR> 4. Form.<BR> 5. Occupation, Man. 1, 21.<BR> 6. Continuance in the right way, correct conduct.<BR> 7. A sort [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a " target="_blank">Page0987-a + 44</a>] of sacrifice.<BR> 8. Stay, step.<BR> 9. A royal ordinance.<BR> 10. End.<BR> 11. Death.<BR> 12. Destruction.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरसंस्थ
दूर- + संस्थ दूर- + संस्थ, adj. distant, Megh. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरसंस्थ
धर- + संस्थ धर- + संस्थ, adj. having the form of a mountain, Kir. 15, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसंस्थ
फल- + संस्थ फल- + संस्थ, adj. bearing fruit, Brāhmaṇav. 3, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणसंस्थ
ब्राह्मण- + संस्थ ब्राह्मण- + संस्थ, adj. belonging to Brāhmaṇas, Man. 8, 325.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंस्थ
स्व- + संस्थ स्व- + संस्थ, f. absorption in one's own self, Bhāg. P. 6, 4, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थान|संस्थानं
संस्थान संस्थान, i. e. सम्-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. A heap, a quantity.<BR> 2. The aggregation of the primitive atoms.<BR> 3. Position, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 17; form, figure, shape, Śāk. d. 126.<BR> 4. Fabrication, construction.<BR> 5. A vicinity.<BR> 6. Standing, being, Hit. ii. d. 90 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 59).<BR> 7. A common place of abode.<BR> 8. A place where four roads meet, an open place(?), Rām. 2, 65, 32, Seramp.<BR> 9. Any place, Man. 8, 371; a station, 9, 261.<BR> 10. A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR> 11. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापन|संस्थापनं
संस्थापन संस्थापन, i. e. सम्-स्था, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Collecting.<BR> 2. Placing.<BR> 3. Establishing, Bhag. 4, 8; fixing, Lass. 2. ed. 87 14.<BR> 4. A regulation, Man. 8, 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थास्नु
संस्थास्नु संस्थास्नु, i. e. सम्-स्था + स्नु, adj. Immovable, MBh. 7, 372.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थिति|संस्थितिः
संस्थिति संस्थिति, i. e. सम्-स्था + ति, f.<BR> 1. Staying together, Hit. i. d. 38, M.M.<BR> 2. Accumulation, heap.<BR> 3. Contiguity.<BR> 4. Abiding, Hit. i. d. 104, M.M.; abode, Man. 6, 90.<BR> 5. State of life.<BR> 6. Duration, Hit. i. d. 42, M.M.<BR> 7. Restraint, Man. 9, 14.<BR> 8. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्श|संस्पर्शः
संस्पर्श संस्पर्श, i. e. सम्-स्पृश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Touching, Rām. 3, 49, 44; contact, Pañc. 198, 13; mixture, 250, 4.<BR> 2. Being touched, being affected, Pañc. 93, 1.<BR> 3. Perception, sense.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंस्पर्श
दुःख- + संस्पर्श दुःख- + संस्पर्श, adj. of whom or of which the touch causes pain, MBh. 5, 2046.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृश्
संस्पृश् संस्पृश्, i. e. सम्-स्पृश्, ad Touching, Amar. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोट|संस्फोटः
संस्फोट संस्फोट, i. e. सम्-स्फुट, m. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरण|संस्मरणं
संस्मरण संस्मरण, i. e. सम्-स्मृ + अन, n. Remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृति|संस्मृतिः
संस्मृति संस्मृति, i. e. सम्-स्मृ + ति f. Remembrance, Kir. 18, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्राव|संस्रावः
संस्राव संस्राव, i. e. सम्-स्रु + अ, m. Flowing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसंस्राव|कर्णसंस्रावः|कर्ण्णसंस्राव
कर्ण- + संस्राव कर्ण- + संस्राव, m. suppuration of the ear, Suśr. 2, 362, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतजानुक|संहतजानुकः
संहतजानुक संहत-जानु + क (vb. हन्), adj. Knock-kneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतता
संहतता संहत + ता, f., and संहतत्व संहत + त्व, n. (vb. हन्),<BR> 1. Close approximation, contact, Śiś. 9, 44. (ता, and agreement).<BR> 2. Compactness.<BR> 3. Combination.<BR> 4. Union, Hit. iv. d. 26 (त्व); agreement (see<BR> 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहति|संहतिः
संहति संहति, i. e. सम्-हन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Combination, Hit. i. d. 34. M.M.; union, agreement, Rājat. 5, 247 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 2. Assemblage, heap, multitude, Kir. 5, 4; bulk, 12, 10.<BR> 3. Compactness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिसंहति
अरि- + संहति अरि- + संहति, f. multitude of enemies, Nalod. 4, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नसंहति
भिन्न- + संहति भिन्न- + संहति (vb. भिद्), adj. disunited, Rājat. 5, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसंहति|शस्त्रसंहतिः
शस्त्र- + संहति शस्त्र- + संहति, f. an arsenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमसंहति|हिमसंहतिः
हिम- + संहति हिम- + संहति, f. ice and snow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहनन|संहननं
संहनन संहनन, i. e. सम्-हन् + अन,<BR> I. m. A destroyer, a conqueror, MBh. 3, 13300.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Rubbing the body.<BR> 2. Compactness, inflexibility, MBh. 1, 7022.<BR> 3. Strength.<BR> 4. Body, Utt. Rāmac. 152, 12.<BR> 5. Agreement, MBh. 12, 2420.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहसंहनन|सिंहसंहननः
सिंह- + संहनन सिंह- + संहनन, adj. 1. of lion strength. 2. handsome and well shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरण|संहरणं
संहरण संहरण, i. e. सम्-हृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Collecting.<BR> 2. Restraining.<BR> 3. Destroying, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 17 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a " target="_blank">Page0988-a + 41</a>] (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 4. Taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्तृ
संहर्तृ संहर्तृ, i. e. सम्-हृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. A destroyer, Vikr. d. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्ष|संहर्षः
संहर्ष संहर्ष, m., i. e.<BR> I. सम्-हृष् + अ.<BR> 1. Pleasure, joy.<BR> 2. Erection of the hair of the body.<BR> II. for संघर्ष.<BR> 1. Rubbing.<BR> 2. Envy.<BR> 3. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहात|संहातः
संहात संहात (probably for संघात, q. cf., which is also a v. r.), m. One of the hells, Man. 4, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार|संहारः
संहार संहार, i. e. सम्-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Collection, comprehensive description, in ऋतु-, of the (six) seasons, title of a poem, Lass. 60, 1.<BR> 2. Abridgment.<BR> 3. Restraining.<BR> 4. Destruction (of the world), Man. 1, 80.<BR> 5. Practice, Rām. 1, 30, 2; skill.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंहार
स- + संहार स- + संहार, adj. with charms for restraining (magical weapons), Johns. Sel. 4, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूति|संहूतिः
संहूति संहूति, i. e. सम्-ह्वे + ति, f. Clamour, tumultuous exclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलवर्ण
सकलवर्ण स-क-ल-वर्ण, adj. Endowed with the letters क and ल (viz. कलह), i. e. Quarrelling, Nalod. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाकोल|सकाकोलः
सकाकोल स-काकोल, m. One of the hells, Man. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाश|सकाशः
सकाश सकाश, probably स-*काश (vb. काश्), m. Vicinity, presence, Nal. 1, 21; Pañc. 66, 10; acc. and loc. To, Pañc. 23, 1; Chr. 6, 6; Pañc. 55, 19. Abl. From, Pañc. 220, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथपतिसकाशम्
यूथ-पति-सकाश + म् यूथ-पति-सकाश + म्, acc. To the chief of the herd, Pañc. 160, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत् स-कृ + त्, adv.<BR> 1. Once, Vikr. d. 10.<BR> 2. At once, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 5.<BR> 3. With, together. Cf. शकृत्.<BR>--Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
अ- + सकृत् अ- + सकृत्, adv. repeatedly, Pañc. iii. d. 116; Chr. 30, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्ति|सक्तिः
सक्ति सक्ति, i. e. सञ्ज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Contact.<BR> 2. Junction, Kir. 5, 46.<BR> 3. Addiction to, attachment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसक्ति|अतिसक्तिः
अति- + सक्ति अति- + सक्ति, f. closest union, Śiś. 9, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तिमन्त्|सक्तिमत्
सक्तिमन्त् सक्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Attached.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसक्तिमन्त्|अतिसक्तिमत्
अति- + सक्तिमन्त् अति- + सक्तिमन्त्, adj. too much attached, Hit. iv. d. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तु|सक्तुः
सक्तु सक्तु, see शक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुल
सक्तुल सक्तु + ल, adj. Containing flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थन्
सक्थन् सक्थन्, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थि
सक्थि सक्थि, probably सञ्ज् + थन्, n.; the base of some cases is सक्थन्,<BR> 1. The thigh.<BR> 2. A bone.<BR> 3. The frame of a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख
ऽसख -सख, a substitute for सखि at the end of comp. words; e. g. नर-, m. Friend of Nārāyana, Vikr. d. 3. प्रिय-,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A dear friend, Chr. 13, 12.<BR> 2. A tree, Mimosa catechu.<BR> II. f. खी, A female friend, Utt. Rāmac. 61, 13. बलभिद्-, m. Friend of Indra, Śāk. 27, 23. मदिरा-, m. The mango, Mangifera Indica. मधु-, m. Kāma. मरुत्-, m.<BR> 1. Indra.<BR> 2. Fire, Ragh. 2, 10. वसन्त-, m.<BR> 1. Friend of spring, Vikr. 31, 18.<BR> 2. Kāma. वायु-, m. Fire. स्मर-, m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखि
सखि सखि, i. e. probably स- 1. क्षि,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An associate, Pañc. iii. d. 56; a companion, 265, 3.<BR> 2. A friend, Vikr. 12, 1.<BR> II. f. खी, A female friend, Vikr. 8, 2; Pañc. 258, 9.<BR> --Cf. Lat. socius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखित्व|सखित्वं
सखित्व सखि + त्व, n. Friendship, Pañc. 60, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख्य|सख्यं|सख्यः
सख्य सख्य, i. e. सखि + य, n.<BR> 1. Friendship, Hit. 38, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. Equality, Man. 2, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्
† सग् सग्, i. 1, Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर|सगरः
सगर स-गर,<BR> 1. adj. Poisonous.<BR> 2. The name of a king, whose greatgrandson brought the Ganges from heaven to the earth, Pañc. iii. d. 269; Rām. 1, 40, sqq. Gorr.; Daśak. in Chr. 197, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ्य|सगर्भ्यः
सगर्भ्य सगर्भ्य, i. e. स-गर्भ + य, m. A brother by the same father and mother; cf. गर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुडशृङ्गक
सगुडशृङ्गक स-गुड-शृङ्ग + क, adj., f. गिका, Endowed with cupolas, MBh. 3, 643.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघ्
सघ् सघ्, ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. † To hurt, to kill.<BR> 2. To bear (cf. सह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकर|सङ्कर|संकरः|सङ्करः
संकर संकर, i. e. सम्-कॄ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Mixing, blending, Rājat. 5, 377.<BR> 2. The union of a man with a woman of a higher caste, Man. 5, 89; culpable mixture, Rām. 1, 6, 17.<BR> 3. A mixed or degraded caste.<BR> 4. Dust, sweepings.<BR> 5. The crackling of flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकरिन्
संकरिन् संकरिन्, i. e. सम्-कॄ + इन्, adj. Produced by culpable mixture of castes, Lass. Pentap. 66, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकरीकरण|सङ्करीकरण|सङ्करीकरणं
संकरीकरण संकरीकरण, i. e. संकर-कृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Mixing, blending.<BR> 2. Causing loss of caste, Man. 11, 68.<BR> 3. Confusion either in kind, number, or arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकर्षण|सङ्कर्षण|संकर्षणं|सङ्कर्षणं|संकर्षणः|सङ्कर्षणः
संकर्षण संकर्षण, i. e. सम्-कृष् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Attracting.<BR> 2. Ploughing.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Baladeva, brother of Kṛṣṇa, Johns. Sel. 55, 140; Rājat. 5, 112.<BR> 2. Name of another man, Lass. 2. ed. 88, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकलन|सङ्कलन|संकलनं|सङ्कलनं
संकलन संकलन, i. e. सम्-कल् + अन,<BR> I. n., and f. ना.<BR> 1. Heaping.<BR> 2. Junction, collision, Kir. 18, 8.<BR> 3. Blending, intermixture.<BR> II. n. Addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्प|सङ्कल्प|संकल्पः|सङ्कल्पः
संकल्प संकल्प, i. e. सम्-कॢप् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b " target="_blank">Page0989-b + 43</a>] m.<BR> 1. Will, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 1; Hit. 54, 8, M.M.<BR> 2. Wish, Megh. 100; desire, Mālat. 125, 4.<BR> 3. Mind, Nal. 24, 50.<BR> 4. A solemn vow, Chr. 48, 5.<BR> 5. Expectation of advantage from a holy work, Man. 2, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतसंकल्प
धृत- + संकल्प धृत- + संकल्प, adj., f. पा, resolved (to, with loc.), Chr. 45, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापसंकल्प
पाप- + संकल्प पाप- + संकल्प, adj. illintentioned, Rām. 2, 74, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवसंकल्प
शिव- + संकल्प शिव- + संकल्प (m.), the name of a hymn, Man. 11, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसंकल्प
सिद्ध- + संकल्प सिद्ध- + संकल्प, adj. one who has obtained his wishes, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टसंकल्प
हृष्ट- + संकल्प हृष्ट- + संकल्प, adj. contented, glad, Nal. 24, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पज|सङ्कल्पज|संकल्पजः
संकल्पज संकल्प-ज,<BR> I. adj. Proceeding from hope of advantage.<BR> II. m. Kāma, Johns. Sel. 45, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकसुक|सङ्कसुक
संकसुक संकसुक, i. e. सम्-कस् + उक, adj.<BR> 1. Unsteady, fickle.<BR> 2. Uncertain, doubtful.<BR> 3. Feeble, weak.<BR> 4. Wicked.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकसुक|असङ्कसुक
अ- + संकसुक अ- + संकसुक, adj. firm, steady (in mind), Man. 6, 43, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकार|सङ्कार|संकारः|सङ्कारः
संकार संकार, i. e. सम्-कॄ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Dust, sweepings.<BR> 2. The crackling of flame.<BR> II. f. री, A girl recently deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकाश|सङ्काश|संकाशः|सङ्काशः
ऽसंकाश -संकाश, i. e. सम्-काश् + अ, latter part of comp. adj. Like, similar; e. g. गज-, adj. Resembling elephants, Chr. 4, 18. मृत्यु-, adj. death-like, ib. 39, 8. अद्भुत-, adj. well-nigh marvellous, Johns. Sel. 36, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकीर्तन
संकीर्तन संकीर्तन, i. e. सम्-कॄत् + अन, n., and f. ना,<BR> 1. Praising.<BR> 2. Glorification.<BR> 3. Honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकुल|सङ्कुल|सङ्कुलं
संकुल संकुल (cf. कुल), adj., f. ला,<BR> 1. Crowded, Pañc. 43, 4.<BR> 2. Filled with, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 14; full, 1, 9, 41.<BR> 3. Mixed, Nal. 13, 13.<BR> 4. Perplexed, Hit. iii. d. 107.<BR> 5. n. Throng, Mālat. 19, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेत्
संकेत् संकेत् (cf. कित्), i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a " target="_blank">Page0990-a + 43</a>] next), Par.<BR> 1. To invite.<BR> 2. † To advise.<BR> 3. To fix or appoint a time.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pf. pass. (or rather संकेत + इत), अ-संकेतित, adj. Without agreement, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेत|सङ्केत|संकेतः|सङ्केतः
संकेत संकेत, i. e. सम्-कित् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sign, Lass. 2. ed. 5, 20.<BR> 2. Gesture, gesticulation.<BR> 3. Appointment, agreement, convention, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 24; Pañc. 26, 3.<BR> 4. Condition, the circumstances under which anything is effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतक
संकेतक संकेत + क (m.), and संकेतन संकेतन, i. e. सम्-कित् + अन, n. Appointment, a rendezvous, Kathās. 4, 37 (क); Pañc. 129, 1 (क); Lass. 2. ed. 20, 14 (न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकोच|सङ्कोच|सङ्कोचं|संकोचः|सङ्कोचः
संकोच संकोच, i. e. सम्-कुच् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Contracting, contraction, Pañc. iii. d. 20 (कौर्मं संकोचम् आस्थाय, Contracting himself like a tortoise).<BR> 2. Diminution, Pañc. i. d. 105.<BR> 3. Fear, Rājat. 5, 14.<BR> 4. Shutting, closing (as a flower), Naiṣ. 22, 43 (Sch.).<BR> 5. Tieing, binding.<BR> 6. A fish, Raia Sancara Ham.<BR> II. n. Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रन्दन|सङ्क्रन्दन|संक्रंदन|संक्रंदनः|संक्रन्दनः|सङ्क्रन्दनः
संक्रन्दन संक्रन्दन, i. e. सम्-क्रन्द् + अन, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रम|सङ्क्रम|संक्रमः|सङ्क्रमः
संक्रम and संक्राम संक्रा̆म, i. e. सम्-क्रम् + अ,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. Difficult progress, making way through almost impervious passes.<BR> 2. The means of effecting such a passage, a causeway, a bridge, Man. 9, 285 (र्ă).<BR> 3. Means of attaining, Pañc. iv. d. 2 (र्ă).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Concurrence.<BR> 2. Going.<BR> 3. Traversing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यसंक्रम
सूर्य-संक्रम सूर्य-संक्रम, m. the passage of the sun from one sign to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रमण|सङ्क्रमण|संक्रमणं|सङ्क्रमणं
संक्रमण संक्रमण, i. e. सम्-क्रम् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Concurrence.<BR> 2. Passing from one point to another, transition from one body into another, Pañc. 48, 16; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b " target="_blank">Page0990-b + 42</a>] Lass. 26, 4.<BR> 3. The day at which begins the sun's progress to the north of the equator, the summer solstice.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भसंक्रमण
गर्भ- + संक्रमण गर्भ- + संक्रमण, n. entering in a womb, MBh. 14, 472.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रान्ति|सङ्क्रान्ति|संक्रांति|संक्रांतिः|संक्रान्तिः|सङ्क्रान्तिः
संक्रान्ति संक्रान्ति, i. e. सम्-क्रम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Union, Mālat. 153, 17; Utt. Rāmac. 63, 4 (imbibing).<BR> 2. Passage from one point to another.<BR> 3. The passage of the sun or planetary bodies from one sign of the zodiac to another.<BR> 4. Proceeding, Mālav. d. 15; 18.<BR> 5. Imitation.<BR> 6. Reflection.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरायणसंक्रान्ति
उत्तरायण- + संक्रान्ति उत्तरायण- + संक्रान्ति, i. e. उत्तर-अयन-, f. the sun's entrance into its northern journey, Pañc. 119, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यसंक्रान्ति
सूर्य- + संक्रान्ति सूर्य- + संक्रान्ति, f. the sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्राम|सङ्क्राम|संक्रामः|सङ्क्रामः
संक्राम संक्राम, see संक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्लेद|सङ्क्लेद|संक्लेदः|सङ्क्लेदः
संक्लेद संक्लेद, i. e. सम्-क्लिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Moisture, wet, damp.<BR> 2. The rudiment of the fœtus, its form in the first month after conception, Yājñ. 3, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षय|सङ्क्षय|संक्षयः
संक्षय संक्षय, i. e. सम्-क्षि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Complete consumption, Pañc. 47, 10.<BR> 2. Loss, Rājat. 5, 385.<BR> 3. Destroying, Pañc. i. d. 256; destruction, Pañc. 104, 18; iii. d. 13.<BR> 4. The destruction of the world, Chr. 34, 8.<BR> 5. End, Chr. 30, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षिप्ति|सङ्क्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्तिः
संक्षिप्ति संक्षिप्ति, i. e. सम्-क्षिप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Abridgment.<BR> 2. Throwing.<BR> 3. Sending.<BR> 4. Ambuscade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेप|सङ्क्षेप|संक्षेपः
संक्षेप संक्षेप, i. e. सम्-क्षिप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Throwing together; instr. एण, In all, Man. 7, 157.<BR> 2. Abridgment, MBh. 1, 102; Pañc. 4, 17; iii. d. 103 (पात्, in a few words).<BR> 3. Conciseness.<BR> 4. Throwing.<BR> 5. Sending.<BR> 6. Taking away.<BR> 7. Assisting in another's duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेपतस्
संक्षेपतस् संक्षेप + तस्, adv. Concisely, Arj. 1, 13; Sāv. 2, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षोभ|सङ्क्षोभ|संक्षोभः
संक्षोभ संक्षोभ, i. e. सम्-क्षुभ् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a " target="_blank">Page0991-a + 43</a>] m.<BR> 1. Shaking, Vikr. d. 12.<BR> 2. Trembling, Indr. 5, 9.<BR> 3. Agitation.<BR> 4. Overturning.<BR> 5. Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्य|सङ्ख्य|संख्यं|सङ्ख्यं
संख्य संख्य, i. e. सम्-ख्या,<BR> I. n. War, battle, Rām. 3, 54, 28.<BR> II. f. या,<BR> 1. Number in general, Pañc. 156, 6; संख्यया परिवर्जित, Without number, innumerable, Pañc. ii. d. 62.<BR> 2. A numeral.<BR> 3. Reflection, deliberation.<BR> 4. Intellect.<BR> 5. Manner, Rājat. 5, 172.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्य|असङ्ख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
अ- + संख्य अ- + संख्य, adj., f. या, innumerable, Pañc. 122, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसंख्य
कुल- + संख्य कुल- + संख्य, f. being numbered among, belonging to eminent families, Man. 3, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसंख्य
गो- + संख्य गो- + संख्य, m. a cowherd, MBh. 4, 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्धसंख्य
दशार्ध- + संख्य दशार्ध- + संख्य, i. e. दशन्-अर्ध-, adj. five, Johns. Sel. 52, 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसंख्य
शत-संख्य शत-संख्य, adj. numbering a hundred, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 911.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रसंख्य
सहस्र- + संख्य सहस्र- + संख्य, f. a thousand, Kir. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यता|सङ्ख्यता
संख्यता संख्य + ता, f.<BR> 1. Number.<BR> 2. Numeration, counting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यातस्
संख्यातस् संख्या + तस्, adv. = abl. sing. of संख्या, Bhāṣāp. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यान|सङ्ख्यान|संख्यानं|सङ्ख्यानं
संख्यान संख्यान, i. e. सम्-ख्या + अन, n.<BR> 1. Numbering, enumeration, Man. 8, 400.<BR> 2. Reckoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यावन्त्|सङ्ख्यावत्|संख्यावत्
संख्यावन्त् संख्या + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Having number, numbered.<BR> 2. Intelligent.<BR> II. m. A learned Brāhmaṇa, a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
सङ्ग सङ्ग, i. e. सम्-ग (vb. गम्), and सञ्ज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Joining, uniting, Pañc. 187, 6.<BR> 2. Meeting, Utt. Rāmac. 33, 6.<BR> 3. Confluence of rivers.<BR> 4. Touch, Mālat. 170, 3.<BR> 5. Association, Hit. i. d. 202, M.M.; Pañc. i. d. 224; keeping company, Bhartṛ. 2, 34; intercourse, friendship, love (कान्ता-, of one's wife), Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR> 6. Attaching, Ragh. 2, 42 (an arrow, i. e. throwing).<BR> 7. Attachment, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 600; Pañc. i. d. 194; wordly attachment, Bhag. 2, 48.<BR> 8. Desire, cupidity, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b " target="_blank">Page0991-b + 44</a>] Indr. 4, 3; Daśak. in Chr. 181, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ग|असंग|असंगः
अ- + सङ्ग अ- + सङ्ग,<BR> I. m. 1. non-attachment, not being attached to, Man. 6, 75. 2. a proper name, Hariv. 9207.<BR> II. adj. 1. unfastened, MBh. 2, 944. 2. unimpeded, Ragh. 3, 63 (Mallin., ed. Calc. v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसङ्ग
दुस्- + सङ्ग दुस्- + सङ्ग, m. bad inclination, Bhāg. P. 1, 10, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्ग|निःसंग|निःसंगः|निःसङ्गः
निस्- + सङ्ग निस्- + सङ्ग,<BR> I. adj. 1. unimpeded, MBh. 5, 2371. 2. disinterested, free from desire, self-interest, Hit. i. d. 187, M.M.; indifferent, Prab. 110, 16.<BR> II. ˚गम्, adv. without hesitation, Rām. 2, 21, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तसङ्ग|मुक्तसंग|मुक्तसंगः
मुक्त- + सङ्ग मुक्त- + सङ्ग (vb. मुच्), adj. disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथासङ्गम्
यथा-सङ्ग + म् यथा-सङ्ग + म्, adv. so as to be adapted. Nal. 23, 9 (the door lifts itself as much as is necessary far his entering it without bowing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सङ्ग|सत्संग|सत्संगः
सत्सङ्ग सत्सङ्ग, i. e. सन्त्- (vb. 1. अस्),<BR> I. m. association with the good.<BR> II. adj. good, pious, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगति|सङ्गति|संगतिः|सङ्गतिः
संगति संगति, i. e. सम्-गम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Meeting, Pañc. iv. d. 20.<BR> 2. Chance, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 2.<BR> 3. Union. Johns. Sel. 37, 19; association, Pañc. iii. d. 55.<BR> 4. Intercourse, Pañc. 60, 9; sexual intercourse, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 13.<BR> 5. Frequenting.<BR> 6. Questioning for further information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगम|सङ्गम|संगमः|सङ्गमः
संगम संगम, i. e. सम्-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Meeting, Pañc. iii. d. 127; acquiring, Pañc. ii. d. 197.<BR> 2. Confluence of rivers, Utt. Rāmac. 49, 5.<BR> 3. Association, attendance, Hit. i. d. 113, M.M.; union, Vikr. d. 33; Pañc. ii. d. 184; company, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212.<BR> 4. Touch, Hit. iii. d. 20; mixture.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्संगम
त्वद्- + संगम त्वद्- + संगम, m. union with thee, Vikr. d. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगमन
संगमन संगमन, i. e. सम्-गम् + अन, n. Meeting, Utt. Rāmac. 144, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगमनीय
संगमनीय संगमनीय, i. e. संगमन + ईय, adj. Causing reunion, Vikr. d. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगर|सङ्गर|सङ्गरं|संगरः|सङ्गरः
संगर संगर, i. e. सम्-गॄ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Agreement.<BR> 2. Promise, Indr. 4, 12. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a " target="_blank">Page0992-a + 43</a>]<BR> 3. A transaction of sale.<BR> 4. War, battle, Man. 4, 121; Bhartṛ. 2, 85.<BR> 5. Misfortune.<BR> 6. Poison (cf. गर).<BR> II. n. The fruit of the Śamī tree.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंगर|सत्यसङ्गर|सत्यसंगरः|सत्यसङ्गरः
सत्य- + संगर सत्य- + संगर and स्थिर-, adj. true, veracious, Indr. 4, 12 (स्थिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगाद
संगाद संगाद, i. e. सम्-गद् + अ, m. Conversation, Mārk. P. 35, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिन्|संगिन्
सङ्गिन् सङ्गिन्, i. e. सङ्ग + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Uniting with.<BR> 2. Attached, devoted to, Bhag. 3, 26.<BR> 3. Lustful, libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीतक
संगीतक संगीतक, i. e. सम्-गीत (vb. गै), (cf. गीतक, n.), A public entertainment consisting of songs, dancing, and music, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 8; Lass. 68, 4 (a drama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीति|सङ्गीति|संगीतिः|सङ्गीतिः
संगीति संगीति, i. e. सम्-गै + ति, f.<BR> 1. The science of music and dancing.<BR> 2. Discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगोपन|सङ्गोपन|सङ्गोपनं
संगोपन संगोपन, i. e. सम्-गुप् + अन, n. Hiding, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रह|सङ्ग्रह|संग्रहः|सङ्ग्रहः
संग्रह संग्रह, i. e. सम्-ग्रह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Collection, Pañc. ii. d. 176; conjunction, Bhāṣāp. 133; totality, Bhag. 18, 18.<BR> 2. A place where anything is kept.<BR> 3. Quantity.<BR> 4. A compilation, an abridgment, Bhag. 8, 11.<BR> 5. A catalogue.<BR> 6. Clenching the fist, clenching, grasp, Hit. iv. d. 13.<BR> 7. Effort.<BR> 8. Restraining, Lass. 2, 1.<BR> 9. Governing, Man. 7, 113.<BR> 10. Protecting, protection, Man. 8, 311.<BR> 11. Propitiating, attaching, Pañc. i. d. 330 (कुर्वन्ति संग्रहम्, Attach to themselves); Rājat. 5, 295; encouraging, Man. 3, 138.<BR> 12. Assent, promise.<BR> 13. Taking, seizing, Rājat. 5, 274; mentioning, Hit. ii. d. 57.<BR> 14. Elevation, loftiness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारसंग्रह|दारसङ्ग्रह|दारसंग्रहः
दार- + संग्रह दार- + संग्रह, m. marrying, Chr. 51, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसंग्रह
धर्म- + संग्रह धर्म- + संग्रह, m. a collection of merit, of good actions, Pañc. iii. d. 96 (हर्तव्यः, one must do many good actions); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b " target="_blank">Page0992-b + 42</a>] Chr. 28, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसंग्रह
मध्यम- + संग्रह मध्यम- + संग्रह, m. intriguing with another man's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसंग्रह
सार- + संग्रह सार- + संग्रह, adj. containing the essence, Cāṇ. 2 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, p. 407.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रहण|सङ्ग्रहण|संग्रहणं
संग्रहण संग्रहण, i. e. सम्-ग्रह् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Collecting, compiling.<BR> 2. Enchasing, Hit. ii. d. 71.<BR> 3. Sexual intercourse.<BR> 4. Adultery, Man. 8, 72; cf. 6, 356, sqq.<BR> 5. Taking.<BR> 6. Accepting.<BR> 7. Hope.<BR> II. f. णी, Dysentery.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिसंग्रहण
पाणि- + संग्रहण पाणि- + संग्रहण, n. shaking hands as a token of promise, Rām. 4, 34, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंग्रहण
स्त्री- + संग्रहण स्त्री- + संग्रहण, n. adultery, Man. 8, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राम्
† संग्राम् संग्राम्, i. 10 (or rather a denomin. derived from the next), Ātm. (Par.), To fight, to make war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राम|सङ्ग्राम|संग्रामः|सङ्ग्रामः
संग्राम संग्राम, i. e. सम्-ग्रह् + म, m.<BR> 1. War, battle, Hit. 75, 17; fighting, Pañc. 238, 22.<BR> 2. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 305; 423.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राह|सङ्ग्राह|संग्राहः|सङ्ग्राहः
संग्राह संग्राह, i. e. सम्-ग्रह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Clenching the fist.<BR> 2. The fist.<BR> 3. The gripe of a shield.<BR> 4. Seizing forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघ|सङ्घ|संघः|सङ्घः
संघ संघ, i. e. सम्-हन्, m.<BR> 1. Multitude, Indr. 1, 36.<BR> 2. Flock, Hariv. 8788.<BR> 3. Quantity.<BR> 4. Inhabitants, Man. 8, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्ट|सङ्घट्ट|संघट्टः|सङ्घट्टः
संघट्ट संघट्ट, i. e. सम्-घट्ट् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Friction, Megh. 54; rubbing.<BR> 2. Embracing.<BR> 3. Clashing together, Mālat. 74, 13; collision, Pañc. 35, 5; shock, Mālat. 144, 11.<BR> 4. Meeting, encounter.<BR> II. f. टा, A large creeper.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंघट्ट
अ- + संघट्ट अ- + संघट्ट, m. having no rival, Ragh. 14, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्टन|सङ्घट्टन|संघट्टनं|सङ्घट्टनं
संघट्टन संघट्टन, i. e. सम्-घट्ट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rubbing together.<BR> 2. Collision, Pañc. 165, 8.<BR> 3. Close contact.<BR> 4. The intertwining of wrestlers.<BR> 5. Union, Lass. 24, 8 (erroneously, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a " target="_blank">Page0993-a + 41</a>] ˚घड्डन); cohesion.<BR> 6. Collecting, Rājat. 5, 340.<BR> 7. Meeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघड्डन
संघड्डन संघड्डन, Lass. 24, 8, read संघट्टन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघर्ष|सङ्घर्ष|संघर्षः|सङ्घर्षः
संघर्ष संघर्ष, i. e. सम्-घृष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Trituration, rubbing, grinding, friction, MBh. 1, 1134; Rājat. 5, 477.<BR> 2. Collision, Rām. 1, 26, 10.<BR> 3. Emulation, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 19; envy.<BR> 4. Going gently, gliding.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तसंघर्ष
दन्त- + संघर्ष दन्त- + संघर्ष, m. gnashing the teeth, Mārk. P. 34, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघर्षिन्
संघर्षिन् संघर्षिन्, i. e. सम्-घृष् or संघर्ष, + इन्, adj. Emulating, Mālav. 13, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघशस्|सङ्घशस्
संघशस् संघ + शस्, adj.<BR> 1. By troops.<BR> 2. Collectively.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसंघशस्
शत- + संघशस् शत- + संघशस्, adv. by troops of hundreds, Indr. 1, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघाटिका|सङ्घाटिका
संघाटिका संघाटिका, i. e. संघाटी + क, f.<BR> 1. A couple.<BR> 2. A procuress.<BR> 3. Smell.<BR> 4. A plant, Trapa bispinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघाटी
संघाटी संघाटी (सम् and vb. हन्), f., in the comp. भिक्षु-, f. The garb of a mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघात|सङ्घात|संघातः|सङ्घातः
संघात संघात, i. e. सम्-हन्, Caus., + अ, m.<BR> 1. Association, connexion, Bhartṛ. 2, 56 (शिला-, properly, of a stone, i. e. its strong structure, a hard stone).<BR> 2. Assemblage, multitude, Pañc. 157, 24; Rājat. 5, 260; cluster, Mālat. 153, 8.<BR> 3. Killing, striking.<BR> 4. A division of Tartarus.<BR> 5. Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघातवन्त्|सङ्घातवत्|संघातवत्
संघातवन्त् संघात + वन्त्, adj. Having, or connected with, many, Pañc. iii. d. 57.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृसंघातवन्त्|भ्रातृसङ्घातवत्
भ्रातृ- + संघातवन्त् भ्रातृ- + संघातवन्त्, i. e. भ्रातृसंघात + चन्त्, m. having many brothers, Pañc. iii. d. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्
सच् सच्, i. 1, Ātm., and Par. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b " target="_blank">Page0993-b + 41</a>] Ātm.; ved. ii. 3, सिषच् and सश्च् (i. e. ससच्),<BR> 1. To follow.<BR> 2. To obey.<BR> 3. To favour.<BR> 4. To honour, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR> 5. To cause to flow, Chr. 296, 9 = Rigv. i. 112, 9.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the pres. अ-सश्चन्त् and अ-सश्चत् (Not obeying, not ceding), not ceasing, inexhaustible, Chr. 296, 2 = Rigv. i. 112, 2.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sequi, secundus, secus, sequior, sacer; ἕπομαι, ἕσπετο (for σεσπ = ved. सश्च्), ὁπλότερος, ἑκάς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचि|सचिः
सचि सच् + इ, m. Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिव|सचिवः
सचिव सचि + व, m.<BR> 1. A friend, a companion, Rājat. 5, 341.<BR> 2. A minister, a counsellor, Rām. 3, 53, 4; Kām. Nītis. 4, 28, sqq.; Pañc. 155, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> See कु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसचिव|धीसचिवः
धी- + सचिव धी- + सचिव, m. a counsellor, Rājat. 2, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मसचिव|नर्मसचिवः|नर्म्मसचिव
नर्मसचिव नर्मसचिव, i. e. नर्मन्-, m. a princes's companion, whose business it is to amuse him by jokes, Kām. Nītis. 5, 20; a favourite, Mālat. 37, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिवता
सचिवता सचिव + ता, f. The office of a minister, Rājat. 5, 389.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदानन्द|सच्चिदानंद|सच्चिदानन्दः
सच्चिदानन्द सच्चिदानन्द, i. e. सन्त् (vb. 1. अस्), -चित्-आनन्द, n. Brahman, or the Supreme Spirit, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजुस्
सजुस् सजुस्, i. e. स-जुष्,<BR> I. adj. sbst. Associated, a companion.<BR> II. सजूस्, adv. With, together with (with the instr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ज्
1. सज्ज् सज्ज्, see सञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ज्
† 2. सज्ज् सज्ज्, सञ्च् सञ्च् (सञ्ज् सञ्ज्), i. 1, Par. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ज|सज्जः
सज्ज 1. सज्ज् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Armed.<BR> 2. Fortified.<BR> 3. Got ready, Chr. 30, 3; 31, 18; prepared, Pañc. ii. d. 200 (cf. my transl.).<BR> 4. Ornamented.<BR> 5. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a " target="_blank">Page0994-a + 41</a>] Dressed.<BR> II. f. जा.<BR> 1. Armour.<BR> 2. Dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जता
सज्जता सज्ज + ता, f. Readiness, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जन|सज्जनं|सज्जनः
सज्जन सज्जन, i. e.<BR> A. सन्त् (vb. 1. अस्), -जन, adj.<BR> 1. Respectable.<BR> 2. Good, virtuous, Bhartṛ. 2, 46; 50.<BR> B. 1. सज्ज् + अन,<BR> I. (m., f. ना), n.<BR> 1. Fastening, Man. 2, 63.<BR> 2. Arming.<BR> 3. Dressing.<BR> 4. Preparing.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A guard.<BR> 2. A ferry.<BR> III. f. ना, Caparisoning an elephant, Govardh. Āryā Sapt. 370, d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जित|सज्जितः
सज्जित सज्जित, i. e. सज्ज + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Prepared, Pañc. i. d. 173; 197, 25.<BR> 2. Armed.<BR> 3. Dressed, ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्य
सज्य स-ज्य (see ज्या), adj. Strung (as a bow), Johns. Sel. 39, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्च्
सञ्च् सञ्च्, see 2. सज्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चक|संचकः
सञ्चक सञ्चक (m.?), Stamp, and disc (of the moon), Naiṣ. 22, 47; 48 (Sch. ad 47).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचय|सञ्चय|संचयः|सञ्चयः
संचय संचय, i. e. सम्-चि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Collection, Man. 4, 3.<BR> 2. Heaping up, accumulation, Pañc. ii. d. 158; Hit. i. d. 159, M.M.<BR> 3. Being constructed, built, Pañc. 33, 6.<BR> 4. Heap, Pañc. 175, 2 (काष्ठ-, pl. A funeral pile).<BR> 5. Multitude, Mālat. 14, 6; quantity, Pañc. ii. d. 142.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंचय|अतिसञ्चय
अति- + संचय अति- + संचय, m. excessive accumulation, Hit. i. d. 159, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचयन|सञ्चयन|संचयनं|सञ्चयनं
संचयन संचयन, i. e. सम्-चि + अन, n.<BR> 1. Gathering up, Man. 5, 59; putting together, Pañc. 244, 2.<BR> 2. Collecting the ashes and bones of a body which has been burned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचयिक
ऽसंचयिक -संचयिक in मास-, i. e. मास-संचयिन् + क, adj. One who gathers enough for a month, Man. 6, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचयिन्|सञ्चयिन्
संचयिन् संचयिन्, i. e. सम्-चि + इन्, adj., f. नी, Who or what collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचर|सञ्चर|संचरः|सञ्चरः
संचर संचर, i. e. सम्-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A defile, any narrow or difficult pass, a road along the edge of a mountain, or a bridge, etc.<BR> 2. Difficult passage.<BR> 3. A road.<BR> 4. The body.<BR> 5. Killing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिसंचर
मूर्ति- + संचर मूर्ति- + संचर, adj. embodied, Utt. Rāmac. 145, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचरण
संचरण संचरण, i. e. सम्-चर् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Going, Mālat. 15, 12.<BR> 2. Setting in motion, use, Pañc. 44, 17 (perhaps it must be changed to संचारण, q. cf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचलन|सञ्चलन|संचलनं|सञ्चलनं
संचलन संचलन, i. e. सम्-चल् + अन, n., and f. ना, Trembling, shaking, Mālat. 147, 12; Kir. 18, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचलनाडि
संचलनाडि संचलनाडि, i. e. सम्-चल् + अ-नाडि, f. Artery, pulse, Rām. 2, 50, 13, Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचार|सञ्चार|संचारः|सञ्चारः
संचार संचार, i. e. सम्-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Difficult progress.<BR> 2. Difficulty, distress.<BR> 3. Going, Rām. 3, 52, 34; motion, Bhartṛ. 1, 11.<BR> 4. Course, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 16 (of life).<BR> 5. Contagion.<BR> 6. Setting in motion, Bhāṣāp. 151.<BR> 7. Leading.<BR> 8. Inciting.<BR> 9. A gem supposed to be in the head of a serpent.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंचार
दुःख- + संचार दुःख- + संचार, adj. passing in a disagreeable manner, Rām. 3, 22, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंचार
दुस्- + संचार दुस्- + संचार, adj., f. रा, difficult to be passed, Pañc. i. d. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंचार
निस्- + संचार निस्- + संचार, adj. 1. not walking, staying at home, Rājat. 6, 125. 2. motionless, quiet, Mālat. 126, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंचार
पात्र- + संचार पात्र- + संचार, m. perhaps, arranging the vessels after dinner, MBh. 12, 9975 (perhaps to be corrected to पात्रसंस्कार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंचार|भूतसञ्चार|भूतसंचारः|भूतसञ्चारः
भूत- + संचार भूत- + संचार,<BR> 1. m. possession by evil spirits.<BR> II. f. री, fire in a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचारक|सञ्चारक|संचारकः
संचारक संचारक, i. e. सम्-चर्, Caus., + अक,<BR> I. m. A leader, Hit. ii. d. 123.<BR> II. f. रिका.<BR> 1. A female messenger, a bawd.<BR> 2. A pair.<BR> 3. Smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचारण|सञ्चारण|संचारणं
संचारण संचारण, i. e. सम्-चर्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Setting in motion (cf. संचरण).<BR> 2. Impelling.<BR> 3. Leading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संचारिन्|सञ्चारिन्
संचारिन् संचारिन्, i. e. सम्-चर्, and संचार, + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Moving, Kumāras. 3, 54.<BR> 2. Fickle, unsteady, changeable.<BR> 3. Difficult.<BR> 4. Putting in motion.<BR> 5. Contagious.<BR> 6. Hereditary (as disease).<BR> II. m. Incense.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंचारिणी
भूत-संचारिणी भूत-संचारिणी, f. fire in a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्|संज्
1. सञ्ज् सञ्ज्, i. 1, सज, Par. The pass. सज्य has become very often सज्ज, which in epic poetry appears with the terminations of the Par. (MBh. 1, 7694), whence सज्ज् has begun to be considered as a radical vb., To adhere, Ragh. 4, 47; Chr. 20, 20; नहि वाणा मयोत्सृष्टाः सज्जन्तीह शरीरिणां कायेषु, literally, ‘For the arrows cast by me do not stick to the bodies of living men,’ i. e. ‘all those who are hit by my arrows will die.’ Pass.<BR> 1. To be attached, MBh. 3, 63.<BR> 2. To become attached, Man. 6, 55.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सक्त.<BR> 1. Attached, Man. 7, 30.<BR> 2. Devoted.<BR> 3. Diligent, intent on.<BR> 4. Impending, Pañc. 186, 24.<BR> 5. Belonging, Pañc. 222, 13; related, 89, 18.<BR> 6. Concerning, Pañc. 221, 14.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To pimp, Man. 8, 362 (सज्जय).<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, षञ्ज्; अति-सक्त (i. e. सक्त with अति), Exceedingly attached, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 21.<BR> --With व्यति वि-अति,<BR> 1. Par. To connect mutually, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 8.<BR> 2. Ātm. To change, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 3. व्यतिषक्त, Intermarrying, Man. 10, 25.<BR> --With अनु अनु, षञ्ज्, To cling, to cleave, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 15. Pass. To be attached to, Bhag. 6, 4. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-b " target="_blank">Page0995-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With अभि अभि, षञ्ज्, To humiliate, MBh. 3, 1090.<BR> --With अव अव, To suspend, Rām. 3, 53, 52. अवसक्त.<BR> 1. Hanging, MBh. 1, 1692.<BR> 2. Taken hold of, and pervaded, Śiś. 9, 7.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To fix, to put on, MBh. 3, 16125.<BR> 2. To entrust, MBh. 1, 1955. Pass. To be attached or fettered, Śāk. d. 74. आसक्त,<BR> 1. Attached, Rām. 3, 50, 9.<BR> 2. Intent on, occupied, Pañc. 27, 9; zealously following.<BR> 3. Trusting to.<BR> 4. Eternal.<BR> 5. ˚तम्, adv. Eternally.<BR> --Caus. सञ्जय, To cause to be attached, Ragh. 6, 83.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ, व्यासक्त, Occupied, Vikr. 60, 6.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To attach, MBh. 1, 4418.<BR> 2. To entrust, to resign to, Man. 4, 257. समासक्त,<BR> 1. Attached, Rām. 2, 64, 9.<BR> 2. Joined.<BR> 3. Combined.<BR> 4. Marked, affected by.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To attach, Mālat. 172, 13. उत्सक्त, Attached, Rājat. 5, 127.<BR> --With नि नि, निषक्त, Fixed, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 3.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To attach one's self, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 3. Pass.<BR> 1. To be strongly addicted, Man. 4, 16.<BR> 2. To be relevant, to apply, Bhāṣāp. 61. प्रसक्त,<BR> 1. Attached to, Pañc. ii. d. 3.<BR> 2. Fettered, Pañc. i. d. 208.<BR> 3. Engaged in, Pañc. 197, 25.<BR> 4. Connected with.<BR> 5. Obtained.<BR> 6. Employed.<BR> 7. Continual, Mālat. 70, 19; eternal.<BR> 8. Opened, expanded, Utt. Rāmac. 118, 5.<BR> 9. ˚तम्, adv. Continually.<BR> --With अतिप्र अति-प्र in अतिप्रसक्त, i. e. प्रसक्त with अति, Too much attached, Pañc. i. d. 201.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, अनुप्रसक्त, Attached, Śiś. 9, 63.<BR> --With वि वि, विषक्त,<BR> 1. Hung up, Śāk. d. 31.<BR> 2. Adhering closely, firmly rooted, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 23; Utt. Rāmac. 94, 12.<BR> 3. In contact with.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a " target="_blank">Page0996-a + 41</a>] सम् सम्, pass.<BR> 1. To adhere, MBh. 3, 17228.<BR> 2. To be entwined, MBh. 2, 917.<BR> 3. To be connected, Rām. 2, 25, 37. संसक्त,<BR> 1. Attached to, Pañc. i. d. 192; attached, Mālat. 145, 11.<BR> 2. Tied, connected, Rājat. 5, 366.<BR> 3. Restrained, Nal. 13, 21.<BR> 4. Endowed with.<BR> 5. Joined, linked together.<BR> 6. Contiguous.<BR> --Cf. σάττω (for σαγyω), σαγή, σάγμα, σακτός, σάκτωρ, probably σάκκος, σάκτας.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
अ- + सक्त अ- + सक्त, adj. not attached, Pañc. ii. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्|संज्
2. सञ्ज् सञ्ज्, see 2. सज्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज|संज|संजः|सञ्जः
सञ्ज सञ्ज, m.<BR> 1. Brahman<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जतर
सञ्जतर सञ्जतर, n. The name of a city, Pañc. 118, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संजनन|सञ्जनन
संजनन संजनन, i. e. सम्-जन् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Begetting.<BR> 2. Producing, Lass. 2. ed. 60, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संजीव
संजीव संजीव, i. e. सम्-जीव् + अ, adj. Living, Rām. 6, 26, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संजीवक
संजीवक संजीवक, i. e. सम्-जीव् + अक, m. A proper name, Hit. 58, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संजीवन|सञ्जीवन|संजीवनं|सञ्जीवनं
संजीवन संजीवन, i. e. सम्-जीव् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Animating, bringing to life, Pañc. 244, 4; reanimating, Utt. Rāmac. 51, 9; life-restoring, Mālat. 167, 4.<BR> 2. A hell, Man. 4, 89.<BR> 3. A cluster of four houses.<BR> II. f. नी, A kind of elixir, Lass. 79, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संजीविन्
संजीविन् संजीविन्, i. e. सम्-जीव् + इन्, f. नी, reanimating, Lass. 18, 13 (perhaps to be changed into संजिवनी, cf. जीवन and the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञ
संज्ञ संज्ञ, i. e. सम्-जानु, adj. Knock-kneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञक
ऽसंज्ञक -संज्ञ + क, a substitute for संज्ना, at the end of comp. adj., or sbst. based on them; e. g. आसन-, adj. Called आसन, Pañc. 154, 8. रवि-, n. Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञा
संज्ञा संज्ञा, i. e. सम्-ज्ञा, f.<BR> 1. Consciousness, Vikr. 71, 20; Chr. 31, 18.<BR> 2. Intellect, mind, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 1.<BR> 3. Thought.<BR> 4. Knowledge, Bhag. 1, 7.<BR> 5. Sign, Vikr. 47, 12; gesticulation.<BR> 6. Name, appellation, Hit. iv. d. 88.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसंज्ञ|अन्तःसञ्ज्ञ
अन्तःसंज्ञ अन्तःसंज्ञ, i. e. अन्तर्-, adj. possessed of internal consciousness, Man. 1, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंज्ञ
कृत- + संज्ञ कृत- + संज्ञ, adj. 1. ready-minded. 2. distinguished by appropriate marks, Man. 7, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतसंज्ञ
अ-कृत- + संज्ञ अ-कृत- + संज्ञ, adj. irresolute, MBh. 14, 588.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसंज्ञ
गत- + संज्ञ गत- + संज्ञ, adj. bereft of sense, Indr. 5, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसंज्ञ
जीव- + संज्ञ जीव- + संज्ञ, adj. called life, Man. 12, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंज्ञ
निस्- + संज्ञ निस्- + संज्ञ, adj. deprived of consciousness, Rām. 3, 62, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंज्ञ
वि- + संज्ञ वि- + संज्ञ, adj. 1. lifeless, 2. bereft of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यसंज्ञ
सूर्य-संज्ञ सूर्य-संज्ञ, n. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसंज्ञ
सोम- + संज्ञ सोम- + संज्ञ, n. camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञावन्त्|सञ्ज्ञावत्
संज्ञावन्त् संज्ञा + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Recovered after insensibility.<BR> 2. Having a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञित
संज्ञित संज्ञित, i. e. संज्ञा + इत, adj. Called, Rām. 1, 39, 4; Lass. 16, 16 (at the end of a comp.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करसंज्ञित
कर- + संज्ञित कर- + संज्ञित, adj. called tax, Man. 7, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञु
संज्ञु संज्ञु, i. e. सम्-जानु, adj. Knock-kneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्वर|सञ्ज्वर|संज्वरः|सञ्ज्वरः
संज्वर संज्वर, i. e. सम्-ज्वर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Fever.<BR> 2. Heat, burning, scorching, a burn.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्वर
अ- + संज्वर अ- + संज्वर, adj. without indignation, Man. 4, 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्वरवन्त्|सञ्ज्वरवत्
संज्वरवन्त् संज्वर + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Hot, Mālat. 154, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्
† सट् सट्, i. 1, Par. To be a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट|सटं
सट सट (cf. जट), m., f. टा (also शटा शटा, Padmap. 16, 97), and n.<BR> 1. An ascetic's clotted hair, Bhāg. P. 7, 8, 32 (टा).<BR> 2. A braid of hair, Draup. 9, 9 (टा); a mane, Śiś. 1, 47; bristles (of a boar), Ragh. 9, 60.<BR> 3. A crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्ट्
† सट्ट् सट्ट्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To kill, to injure.<BR> 2. To be strong.<BR> 3. To give.<BR> 4. To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सठ्
सठ् सठ्, see 4. शठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत|सततं
सतत स-तत (vb. तन्),<BR> I. adj. Continual, eternal.<BR> II. ˚तम्, adv. Continually, eternally, always, Pañc. 182, 9; Hit. i. d. 41, M.M. When former part of a comp. the final म् is dropped; e. g. सतत-यायिन्, Taking place continually, Man. 1, 50; Bhartṛ. 2, 46 (सतत-दुर्गत, i. e. -दुस्-गत, Ever poor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततग|सततगः
सततग सतत-ग, m. Wind, Hiḍ. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सति|सतिः
सति सति, i. e. सन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Gift, giving.<BR> 2. End, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीत्व|सतीत्वं
सतीत्व सतीत्व, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), + ई + त्व, n. Virtuousness or purity in a wife, chastity, Pañc. iii. d. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीन|सतीनः
सतीन सतीन, and सतीनक सतीन + क, m. Peas, or a particular kind of pulse (cf. सतील).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ्य|सतीर्थ्यः
सतीर्थ्य सतीर्थ्य, i. e. स-तीर्थ + य, m. A fellow student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतील|सतीलः
सतील सतील,<BR> 1. m. A bambu.<BR> 2. Air, wind.<BR> II. m., and f. ला, Peas, or a particular kind of pulse (cf. सतीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलक|सतीलकः
सतीलक सतील + क, m. Pulse in general, or of a particular kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कर्मन्|सत्कर्म्मन्
सत्कर्मन् सत्कर्मन्, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), -कर्मन्, n.<BR> 1. A good act.<BR> 2. Virtue.<BR> 3. Hospitality.<BR> 4. Funeral obsequies.<BR> 5. Expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कार|सत्कारः
सत्कार सत्कार, i. e. सन्त् (see the last), -कार, m.<BR> 1. Reverence, Sāv. 3, 20, b; attention, Pañc. i. d. 84.<BR> 2. Hospitality, hospitable reception, Hit. 60, 1, M.M.<BR> 3. A meal, a festival, Man. 3, 59. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b " target="_blank">Page0997-b + 44</a>]<BR> 4. Care, Sāv. 3, 20, a.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कार|असत्कारः
अ- + सत्कार अ- + सत्कार, m. injury, MBh. 1, 6355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिसत्कार|अतिथिसत्कारः
अतिथि- + सत्कार अतिथि- + सत्कार, m. hospitable treatment, Śāk. 7, 15 (corr. ˚का˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्क्रिया
सत्क्रिया सत्क्रिया, i. e. सन्त्-क्रिया (see सत्कर्मन्) f.<BR> 1. Good action, Bhartṛ. 2, 96.<BR> 2. Doing good, charity, virtue, Śāk. d. 112.<BR> 3. Worship.<BR> 4. Respectful treatment, Kir. 1, 12.<BR> 5. Hospitality, Man. 3, 126.<BR> 6. Funeral or obsequial ceremonies.<BR> 7. Any purificatory ceremony.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तसत्क्रिया
अन्त- + सत्क्रिया अन्त- + सत्क्रिया, f. funeral ceremonies, Rājat. 5, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ता
सत्ता सत्ता, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple pres. of 1. अस्), + ता, f.<BR> 1. Existence, being, reality, Bhāṣāp. 7.<BR> 2. Goodness, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तावन्त्|सत्तावत्
सत्तावन्त् सत्ता + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessing reality, Bhāṣāp. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्र
सत्त्र सत्त्र, and सत्र सत्र, n., i. e.<BR> I. सद् + त्र.<BR> 1. A sacrifice, Utt. Rāmac. 4, 1.<BR> 2. Liberality, munificence.<BR> II. perhaps स-त्रा.<BR> 1. Covering, concealing, a hiding-place, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 10 (तद्-दृष्टि-विभ्रम-उत्पल-वन-सत्त्र-अपाश्रय, adj. Concealed in the play of her looks, which seemed as it were the covert of a wood of lotuses).<BR> 2. Fraud, cheating.<BR> 3. A house.<BR> 4. Wealth.<BR> 5. A wood, a forest, Kir. 13, 9.<BR> 6. A tank.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसत्त्र
दीर्घ- + सत्त्र दीर्घ- + सत्त्र, n. 1. a Soma sacrifice of long continuance, MBh. 3, 5051. 2. the name of a place of pilgrimage, ib. 5050.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसत्त्र
देव- + सत्त्र देव- + सत्त्र, n. a longlasting sacrifice in honour of the gods, MBh. 3, 8188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसत्त्र
पञ्चसत्त्र पञ्चसत्त्र, i. e. पञ्चन्-, n. the name of a locality, Rājat. 5, 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसत्त्र
ब्रह्मसत्त्र ब्रह्मसत्त्र, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, n. 1. what must be read constantly, Man. 2, 106. 2. teaching the Veda, Man. 4, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिन्
सत्त्रिन् सत्त्रिन्, i. e. सत्त्र + इन्, m.<BR> 1. One constantly performing sacrifice, occupied with a sacrifice, Man. 5, 93. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a " target="_blank">Page0998-a + 46</a>]<BR> 2. A priest superintending a sacrifice.<BR> 3. A liberal housekeeper,<BR> 4. An ambassador.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसत्त्रिन्
दीर्घ- + सत्त्रिन् दीर्घ- + सत्त्रिन्, i. e. दीर्घसत्त्र + इन्, adj. one who performs a long sacrifice, Bhāg. P. 1, 4, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्व|सत्त्वं|सत्त्वः
सत्त्व सत्त्व, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), + त्व,<BR> I. m. and n.<BR> 1. An animal, Pañc. 69, 5 (n.); Hit. 56, 20; Lass. 2. ed. 44, 3 (m.); a beast, Ragh. 15, 15; a monster, Rām. 1, 40, 20.<BR> 2. A being, Pañc. 165, 9; Rām. 3, 55, 48 (n.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Being, existence.<BR> 2. Life, Śāk. d. 42.<BR> 3. Nature, natural property, Hit. ii. d. 39; character, 100, 6.<BR> 4. Essence, true essence, Bhag. 2, 45; 10, 36.<BR> 5. Certainty, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 17.<BR> 6. Breath.<BR> 7. Mind, Draup. 7, 15.<BR> 8. Strength, power, Hit. 67, 5, M.M.; courage, Hit. ii. d. 78.<BR> 9. Self-possession, Arj. 6, 20.<BR> 10. A demon, a goblin.<BR> 11. The quality of goodness, Man. 3, 40; virtue, Lass. 2. ed. 44, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्त्व
अ- + सत्त्व अ- + सत्त्व,<BR> I. n. non-existence.<BR> II. adj. without energy, Rām. 6, 89, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीनसत्त्व
अ-दीन- + सत्त्व अ-दीन- + सत्त्व, adj. happy, Draup. 2, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्नसत्त्व
आपन्न- + सत्त्व आपन्न- + सत्त्व (vb. पद्), adj. f. वा, pregnant, Śāk. 65, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसत्त्व
गत- + सत्त्व गत- + सत्त्व (vb. गम्), adj. lifeless, Nal. 16, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसत्त्व
देव- + सत्त्व देव- + सत्त्व, adj. having the nature of a deity, Rām. 2, 1, 29 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्त्व
निस्- + सत्त्व निस्- + सत्त्व, adj. 1. deprived of living beings, Pañc. 55, 8. 2. deprived of strength, Hit. i. d. 133, M.M. (निः-सत्त्व + ता, f. misery, Mālat. 79, 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिसत्त्व|बोधिसत्त्वं|बोधिसत्त्वः
बोधि- + सत्त्व बोधि- + सत्त्व, m. a Bauddha saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबोधिसत्त्व
अति-बोधि-सत्त्व अति-बोधि-सत्त्व, adj. surpassing a bodhisattva, Mālat. 171, 9 (corr. धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासत्त्व|महासत्त्वः
महा- + सत्त्व महा- + सत्त्व, adj. good, virtuous, Hit. 100, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढसत्त्व
मूढ- + सत्त्व मूढ- + सत्त्व (vb. मुह्), adj. insane, silly, Draup. 7, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्त्व
स- + सत्त्व स- + सत्त्व, f. वा, pregnant, a pregnant woman, Ragh. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्ववन्त्|सत्त्ववत्
सत्त्ववन्त् सत्त्व + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, and sbst.<BR> 1. Living, a living being, Rām. 1, 41, 8.<BR> 2. Endowed with, possessed of, the true essence, Bhag. 10, 36.<BR> 3. Endowed with strength, magnanimous, Bhartṛ. 2, 31.<BR> 4. Natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वस्थ|सत्त्वस्थः
सत्त्वस्थ सत्त्व-स्थ (vb. स्था), adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b " target="_blank">Page0998-b + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Existing in the nature of things.<BR> 2. Animate.<BR> 3. Inherent in animals.<BR> 4. Good, excellent.<BR> 5. Performing well, Mālav. 20, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वोत्साहवन्त्|सत्त्वोत्साहवत्
सत्त्वोत्साहवन्त् सत्त्वोत्साहवन्त्, i. e. सत्त्व-उत्साह + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with courage and energy, Pañc. iii. d. 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रतिपक्षिता
सत्प्रतिपक्षिता सत्प्रतिपक्षिता, i. e. सन्त्-प्रतिपक्ष + इन् + ता (cf. सत्प्रतिपक्ष, under प्रतिपक्ष), f. Condition of containing two opposite sets of premises, Bhāṣāp. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्य|सत्यं|सत्यः
सत्य सत्य, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. True, Kathās. 4, 104; superl. सत्यतम, Quite true, Hit. 87, 7, M.M.; realised, Chr. 48, 11; सत्यं कृ, To fulfil, Rām. 3, 53, 8.<BR> 2. Sincere, Lass. 2. ed. 29, 19; honest.<BR> II. ˚यम्, adv.<BR> 1. Truly, Vikr. 71, 18; indeed, Rājat. 5, 86; yes, Man. 11, 196.<BR> 2. A particle of interrogation.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Rāmacandra.<BR> 2. The uppermost of the seven worlds, the abode of Brahman.<BR> IV. f. या.<BR> 1. Veracity.<BR> 2. Sītā.<BR> V. n.<BR> 1. Truth, Rām. 3, 53, 20.<BR> 2. An oath, Chr. 58, 3; Pañc. 97, 17.<BR> 3. Demonstrated conclusion.<BR> 4. The first Yuga, the golden age.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἐτεός; A.S. for-sodh, Forsooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
अ- + सत्य अ- + सत्य,<BR> I. adj. untrue, false, MBh. 3, 14133.<BR> II. n. untruth, Man. 11, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक|सत्यकं
सत्यक सत्य + क,<BR> I. adj. True, veracious.<BR> II. n. Ratification of a bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यंकार|सत्यङ्कार|सत्यंकारः|सत्यङ्कारः
सत्यंकार सत्यंकार, i. e. सत्य + म्-हृ + अ, m. Ratification of a bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यजित्
सत्यजित् सत्य-जि + त्, m. A proper name, Johns. Sel. 29, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यता
सत्यता सत्य + ता, f.<BR> 1. Truth, trueness, Rājat. 5, 27 (they ascended living to the truly highest abode of Hara).<BR> 2. Veracity, Hit. i. d. 95, M.M.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a " target="_blank">Page0999-a + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्यता
निस्- + सत्यता निस्- + सत्यता, f. want of veracity, Hit. i. d. 97, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवन्त्|सत्यवत्
सत्यवन्त् सत्य + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, True, practising truth.<BR> II. m. A proper name.<BR> III. f. वति, A proper name, Chr. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापन|सत्यापनं
सत्यापन सत्यापन, i. e. सत्यापय (a denomin. derived from सत्य), + अन, n., and f. ना, Ratification of a bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र्
† सत्र् सत्र्, i. 10, Ātm.<BR> 1. To accomplish, or to extend.<BR> 2. To connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र सत्र, see सत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रा
सत्रा स + त्रा, prep. (with instr.), With, together with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रिन्
सत्रिन् सत्रिन्, सत्व सत्व, see सत्त्रिन्, सत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वन्
सत्वन् सत्वन्, m. A warrior, Chr. 290, 2 = Rigv. i. 64, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कार|सथूत्कारः
सथूत्कार स-थूत्-कार, i. e. स-थूत् (an-imitative sound), -कार, n. Sputtering in speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
1. सद् सद्, i. 1 and 6, सीद (for सिसद), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 5184),<BR> 1. To sink down, to lie, Rām. 3, 74, 31.<BR> 2. To sit down (ved.).<BR> 3. To become helpless, Man. 4, 191; to be in distress, Pañc. ii. d. 24.<BR> 4. To be impeded, Man. 9, 94.<BR> 5. To be low-spirited, dejected, MBh. 1, 2061; Hit. iii. d. 6.<BR> 6. To decay, to perish, Man. 4, 34; Hit. ii. d. 75.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सन्न.<BR> 1. Lying motionless, Man. 6, 56; still.<BR> 2. Shrunk, diminished.<BR> 3. Gone, lost, Kir. 3, 38.<BR> 4. Dispirited.<BR> 5. Oppressed, Kumāras. 7, 85.<BR> 6. Spoiled, Ragh. 19, 19.<BR> --Caus. सादय,<BR> 1. To throw down, Draup. 8, 29.<BR> 2. To afflict, MBh. 3, 50.<BR> 3. To destroy, Vikr. d. 42. सादित,<BR> 1. Exterminated.<BR> 2. Exhausted.<BR> 3. Decayed.<BR> 4. Broken. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-b " target="_blank">Page0999-b + 43</a>]<BR> 5. Distressed, Kir. 14, 57.<BR> 6. Drawn.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To wither, to perish gradually, MBh. 3, 2674; to perish, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 10.<BR> 2. To be exhausted, to pine, Man. 4, 187.<BR> 3. To be afflicted, Sāv. 5, 47. अवसन्न,<BR> 1. Ended, Hit. 14, 6, M.M.<BR> 2. Languid, weak, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 12.<BR> 3. Dispirited, unhappy, Cāṇ. 65 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411.<BR> 4. Bent.<BR> 5. Separated.<BR> 6. Nonsuited.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To destroy, Bhag. 6, 5.<BR> 2. To mitigate, Śāk. d. 103.<BR> --Comp. absol. अन्-अवसाद्य, Without desponding, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 9.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To sink down, MBh. 3, 713.<BR> 2. To perish, MBh. 3, 823.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, समवसन्न, Sorrowful, MBh. 2, 956.<BR> --With आ आ, To sit down, Chr. 291, 6 = Rigv. i. 85, 6.<BR> --i. 1 and 10, सादय,<BR> 1. To approach, Rām. 2, 56, 33; to come to, Pañc. 127, 17; 247, 8 (रात्रिम् आसाद्य, at night); to reach, Hit. pr. d. 47, M.M.; to overtake, Vikr. 6, 7.<BR> 2. To attack, Rām. 1, 21, 12.<BR> 3. To find, Man. 4, 227.<BR> 4. To obtain, Vikr. 73, 4; MBh. 3, 10472; with गर्रम्, To become proud. Pañc. 26, 3. आसन्न, Near, Hit. 84, 7, M.M.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Absol. आसाआय,<BR> 1. Having found. Hit. iv. d. 60 (कार्यम्, a motive. i. e. if it is one's interest).<BR> 2. Agreeably to, Man. 8, 324.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ,<BR> 1. To step on, Kir. 5, 52.<BR> 2. To obtain, MBh. 3, 17101.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To be near, Kir. 11, 36. प्रत्यासन्न, Near, Pañc. 10, 9; imminent, Hit. 115, 15.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To approach, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-a " target="_blank">Page1000-a + 43</a>] Chr. 58, 10.<BR> 2. To encounter, to meet with, Pañc. 120, 9; MBh. 2, 553.<BR> 3. To attach, MBh. 1, 5453.<BR> 4. To find, Pañc. 87, 7; MBh. 1, 2346.<BR> 5. To obtain (चेतनाम्, To recover), Pañc. 58, 19. समासादित,<BR> 1. Attained.<BR> 2. Obtained, Pañc. 69, 16.<BR> 3. Finished, performed.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To perish, Bhag. 3, 24.<BR> 2. † To ascend.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To destroy, Rām. 5, 3, 21.<BR> 2. To draw forth, Man. 9, 267.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To destroy, to remove, MBh. 2, 235.<BR> 2. To draw forth, Man. 9, 261.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, Caus. To destroy, MBh. 3, 8832.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To approach.<BR> 2. To worship, Lass. 100, 1 = Rigv. vii. 15, 1.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To sit down, Rām. 1, 20, 14; Pañc. 8, 18 (to fall down); to plunge, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> 2. To be afflicted, MBh. 3, 333.<BR> नि-षण्ण,<BR> 1. Sitting, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 7.<BR> 2. Placed in.<BR> 3. Reciined, supported, Vikr. 64, 12.<BR> 4. Gone to.<BR> --Caus. To cause to sit down, to kneel, Mālat. 91, 9.<BR> --With सनि सम्-नि,<BR> 1. To sink down, Chr. 31, 15.<BR> 2. To sit down, MBh. 1, 8077 (संनिषिदतुः, corr. ˚षेदतुः).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To be propitious, gracious, Vikr. d. 39 (for the transition to this signification, cf. inclined, Lat. propensus; Germ. geneigt); to favour, MBh. 1, 1259.<BR> 2. To be soothed, Vikr. 72, 5; Hit. ii. d. 150.<BR> 3. To be calm, Man. 2, 54; to be glad, Mālat. 46, 12.<BR> 4. To become clear, Man. 6, 67. प्रसन्न,<BR> 1. Favourable, soothed, Pañc. 223, 9; kind, Vikr. d. 53; propitious, Chr. 39, 5.<BR> 2. Quiet, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 6.<BR> 3. Pleased.<BR> 4. Clear, Nal. 12, 112.<BR> 5. True, Mālat. 20, 3. f. ना, Spirituous liquor.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To propitiate, Vikr. d. 54; Rām. 1, 66, 24. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b " target="_blank">Page1000-b + 43</a>]<BR> 2. To soothe, Man. 11, 205.<BR> 3. To solicit. to beg, Rām. 1, 45, 9 Gorr.; to beg pardon, Pañc. 223, 11. प्रसादित,<BR> 1. Worshipped.<BR> 2. Reconciled, Chr. 42, 15.<BR> 3. Cleansed, purified.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, Caus. To soothe, MBh. 3, 14063.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To be soothed, Rām. 2, 26, 34.<BR> --Caus. To propitiate, MBh. 3, 14039.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To be exhausted, MBh. 3, 448.<BR> 2. To be afflicted. Bhag. 1, 28.<BR> 3. To be sorrowful, MBh. 3, 3075.<BR> 4. To despair, Hit. 82, 18. विषण्ण, Dejected, Vikr. 43, 2; sad, Rām. 1, 40, 24; desponding, spiritless.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-, adj. very sad, Rām. 3, 50, 28.<BR> --Caus. To afflict, Rām. 2, 53, 31.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To be in distress, Pañc. ii. d. 24; to pine, Man. 4, 33.<BR> --Cf. ὁδός, probably, Goth. sinths; A.S. in-sidhian, To enter (= सादय ?); οὖδος, ἔδεθλον; Lat. solum; ἕδος, ἕζομαι; Lat. sedeo; Goth. sitan; A.S. on-settan, sittan; ἵζω (= सिद् + यामि); Lat. sidere, probably de-sidero, sella (i. e. sed + la); Goth. sitls; O.H.G. sezal; A.S. sadl, sadel; O.H.G. satul; ἱδρύω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासन्न|महासन्नः
महा- + सन्न महा- + सन्न, m. Kuvera. आसादित,<BR> 1. Gone to, reached.<BR> 2. Obtained, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 5.<BR> 3. Spread.<BR> 4. Effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादित
अन्-आसादित अन्-आसादित, adj. not tested, Hit. iii. d. 41 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3202).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
2. ऽसद् -सद्, latter part of comp. words, Sitting, dwelling; e. g. अरण्य-, adj. Living in forests, Utt. Rāmac. 133, 6. आश्रम-, m. An anchorite, Śāk. 28, 11. गगण-, m. An inhabitant of the air, Śiś. 4, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद|सदः
सद सद, see शद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन|सदनं
सदन सद् + अन, n.<BR> 1. A house, Pañc. ii. d. 64; a palace, Pañc. i. d. 352.<BR> 2. Decaying, perishing.<BR> 3. Exhaustion.<BR> 4. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसदन|राजसदनं
राजसदन राजसदन, i. e. राजन्-, m. a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्
सदस् सद् + अस्, n.<BR> 1. Seat, abode, Chr. 291, 2 = Rigv. i. 85, 2.<BR> 2. (and m.), Assembly, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.<BR> --Cf. ἕδος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1000-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसदात्मक
सदसदात्मक सदसदात्मक, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), -अ सन्त्-आत्मन् + क, adj. Being both existent and not existent, Man. 1, 11; 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्य|सदस्यः
सदस्य सदस् + य, m.<BR> 1. An assistant at a sacrifice, Śāk. 32, 11.<BR> 2. Any person present or belonging to an assembly, Rām. 1, 13, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदा
सदा स + दा, adv. Always, Pañc. i. d. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातन|सदातनः
सदातन सदा + तन,<BR> I. adj. Eternal.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन्द|सदानंद|सदानन्दः
सदानन्द सदानन्द, i. e. सदा-आनन्द,<BR> I. adj. Always happy.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Vedāntas. in Chr. 219, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्ष|सदृक्षः
सदृक्ष सदृक्ष, i. e. स-दृश् + स, and सदृश् स-दृश्, adj. Like, similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश|सदृशः
सदृश स-दृश् + अ, adj., f. शी,<BR> 1. Like, Vikr. 36, 10; similar, Pañc. 165, 18; of the same rank, Pañc. iii. d. 219.<BR> 2. Conformable, Śāk. 7, 4; fit, Hit. ii. d. 47; proper, right, suitable, Utt. Rāmac. 166, 6.<BR> 3. Worthy, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
अ- + सदृश अ- + सदृश, adj. unbecoming, Rām. 3, 49, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यसदृश
अन्-अन्य- + सदृश अन्-अन्य- + सदृश, adj. not having their like, surpassing all others, Pañc. 4, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन् सद् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. A house, a dwelling, Kir. 5, 30.<BR> 2. A temple, Rājat. 5, 158 (read शूर-सद्म्˚).<BR> 3. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसद्मन्
देव- + सद्मन् देव- + सद्मन्, n. the seat of the gods, MBh. 1, 3687.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगसद्मन्
भोग- + सद्मन् भोग- + सद्मन्, n. the zenana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसद्मन्
सुर- + सद्मन् सुर- + सद्मन्, n. heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्
सद्यस् सद्यस्, i. e. स-दिव् + अस् (abl.-gen. of दिव्), adv.<BR> 1. To-day, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 7.<BR> 2. Instantly, Pañc. 175, 1; in an instant, on a sudden, Vikr. d. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्क|सद्यस्कः
सद्यस्क सद्यस् + क, adj. New, recent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु सद् + रु, adj.<BR> 1. Resting, staying.<BR> 2. Going.<BR> --Cf. probably ἱδρυ in ἱδρύνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वंद्व
सद्वंद्व स-द्वंद्व, adj. Litigating, disunited, Hit. iii. d. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वसथ|सद्वसथः
सद्वसथ सद्वसथ, i. e. सन्त् (ptcple. pres. of 1. अस्), -वस् + अथ, m. A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिस्
सधिस् सधिस्, m. An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्र्यञ्च्|सध्र्यंच्
सध्र्यञ्च् सध्र्यञ्च्, i. e. स + त्रा-अञ्च् (त् changed to ध्, by the influence of र्, and आ̆ to ई, in analogy with the change of final आ̆ before अस्, कृ, भू),<BR> I. adj., f. रीची, Accompanying, a companion.<BR> II. f. रीची, A woman's female friend.<BR> III. ˚यक्, adv. Together with, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 48 (united with themselves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्
सन् सन्, i. 1, Par., ii. 8, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. † To honour.<BR> 2. To obtain.<BR> 3. To give. Desider. सिषास, To wish to obtain (aid), Chr. 296, 5. = Rigv. i. 112, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
सनत् सनत्, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनद्
सनद् स + न + द् (properly acc. sing. n. of स + न), adj. ved. Old, eternal (see सनातन), adv. Always.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sins; ἕνη; Goth. sineigs; Lat. senex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सना
सना स + ना (properly an old instr. sing. of सन; cf. सनद्). adv. Always, perpetually.<BR> --Cf. A.S. sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनात्
सनात् सनात् (abl. sing. of सन, see the last), adv. Always, perpetually, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातन|सनातनः
सनातन सना + तन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Perpetual, eternal, Man. 1, 7; Pañc. ii. d. 112.<BR> 2. Firm, permanent.<BR> 3. Primeval, Man. 1, 22 (ordained from the beginning); 3, 284.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu, Bhaṭṭ. 1, 1; Śiva, Brahman.<BR> III. f. नी, Lakṣmī, Durgā, Sarasvatī.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sinteins, sinteino.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथता
सनाथता स-नाथ + ता, f. State of having a protector, Pañc. iii. d. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनि|सनिः
सनि सन् + इ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Worship, service.<BR> 2. Giving, donation.<BR> II. m., f., and नी, f. A respectful solicitation.<BR> III. f. नी̆, A quarter or point of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठेव|सनिष्ठेवं
सनिष्ठेव सनिष्ठेव, i. e. स-नि-ष्ठिव् + अ, n. Speech uttered with saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुतर्
सनुतर् सनुतर्, probably सानु + तर्, adv. In a concealing manner, Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्|सत्|संत्
सन्त् सन्त्, see 1. अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतक्षण
संतक्षण संतक्षण, i. e. सम्-तक्ष् + अन, n. Sarcastic language, scoff, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतति|सन्तति|संततिः|सन्ततिः
संतति संतति, i. e. सम्-तन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Continuity, Mālat. 14, 16.<BR> 2. Continuous line, line, Pañc. 182, 17.<BR> 3. Extent, multitude, Kir. 5, 17.<BR> 4. Race, lincage.<BR> 5. Offspring, Utt. Rāmac. 166, 8; Hit. 67, 9; a son, a daughter.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसंतति|कुलसन्तति|कुलसंततिः
कुल- + संतति कुल- + संतति, f. propagation of family, Man. 5, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतर्पण|सन्तर्पण|संतर्पणं|सन्तर्पणं
संतर्पण संतर्पण, i. e. सम्-तृप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Satiating.<BR> 2. Satisfying.<BR> 3. Gratifying, delighting, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 13; Mālat. 95, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतान|सन्तान|संतानं|संतानः|सन्तानः
संतान संतान, i. e. सम्-तन् + अ, m. (n., Draup. 5, 88),<BR> 1. Spreading, Utt. Rāmac. 50, 10; Hit. i. d. 206, M.M. (extending their influence from one existence to another); extension, Śāk. d. 167.<BR> 2. Being spread, having grown, Utt. Rāmac. 97, 13 (-वाहिन्, old).<BR> 3. Family, race, lincage, Draup. 5, 88.<BR> 4. Progeny, Man. 3, 15.<BR> 5. A son, a daughter, Hit. iv. d. 109.<BR> 6. One of the trees of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानिका
संतानिका संतानिका, i. e. संतान + क, f.<BR> 1. Froth.<BR> 2. Cream.<BR> 3. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b " target="_blank">Page1002-b + 41</a>] cobweb.<BR> 4. The blade of a knife of sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संताप|सन्ताप|संतापः|सन्तापः
संताप संताप, i. e. सम्-तप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Heat, Mālat. 17, 9 (figurat.); fire, Utt. Rāmac. 141, 10; Pañc. i. d. 392.<BR> 2. Affliction, Pañc. ii. d. 59.<BR> 3. Pain, Vikr. 55, 20; distress.<BR> 4. Passion.<BR> 5. Repentance, Pañc. v. d. 16.<BR> 6. Penance, Kir. 5, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापन|सन्तापन|संतापनः|सन्तापनः
संतापन संतापन, i. e. सम्-तप्, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. adj. Burning.<BR> II. m. One of the arrows of Kāmadeva.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Burning.<BR> 2. Paining, afflicting.<BR> 3. Exciting passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ति|संति|संतिः|सन्तिः
सन्ति सन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. End, destruction.<BR> 2. Gift, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतोष|सन्तोष|संतोषः|सन्तोषः
संतोष संतोष, i. e. सम्-तुष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Contentedness, Pañc. ii. d. 163; satisfaction; with कृ, To be satisfied, Pañc. 136, 12; to be content, Pañc. 139, 17.<BR> 2. Joy.<BR> 3. Thumb and forefinger.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतोष|असन्तोष|असंतोषः
अ- + संतोष अ- + संतोष, m. pain, Mālat. 94, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतोषण|सन्तोषण|संतोषणं
संतोषण संतोषण, i. e. सम्-तुष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Pleasing.<BR> 2. Comforting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतोषवन्त्|सन्तोषवत्
संतोषवन्त् संतोष + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Content.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतोषवन्त्|असन्तोषवत्
अ- + संतोषवन्त् अ- + संतोषवन्त्, adj. not content, Pañc. ii. d. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्रास|सन्त्रास|संत्रासः
संत्रास संत्रास, i. e. सम्-त्रस् + अ, m. Fear, Johns. Sel. 27, 16; Rājat. 5, 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंश|सन्दंश|संदंशः|सन्दंशः
संदंश संदंश, i. e. सम्-दंश् + अ, m. A pair of tongs, Pañc. 52, 8 (स्व-दशन-, His claws which are like a pair of nippers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंशक|सन्दंशक|संदंशकः
संदंशक संदंश + क,<BR> I. m. A pair of tongs, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 10.<BR> II. f. शिका.<BR> 1. A pair of nippers, or small shears or tongs.<BR> 2. A vice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदर्भ|सन्दर्भ|संदर्भः|सन्दर्भः
संदर्भ संदर्भ, i. e. सम्-दृभ् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a " target="_blank">Page1003-a + 40</a>] m.<BR> 1. Weaving garlands.<BR> 2. Stringing, collecting.<BR> 3. Uniting, mixture, Utt. Rāmac. 170, 2.<BR> 4. Work, Utt. Rāmac. 111, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदर्शन|सन्दर्शन|संदर्शनं|सन्दर्शनं
संदर्शन संदर्शन, i. e. सम्-दृश् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Seeing each other, meeting, Pañc. 109, 22; 161, 14.<BR> 2. Looking, sight, presence, Chr. 25, 60.<BR> 3. Consideration, Hit. 129, 10.<BR> 4. Appearance, Vikr. 78, 19; संदर्शनं गम्, To appear, Pañc. 235, 10.<BR> 5. Vision, Megh. 105.<BR> 6. Showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदान|सन्दान|संदानं|सन्दानं|संदानः|सन्दानः
संदान संदान, i. e.<BR> I. सम्- 3. दा + अन, n. A rope, a cord (especially for tying cattle).<BR> II. सम्-दान, m. The elephant's temples, or part whence the ichorous fluid issues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानित|सन्दानित|सन्दानितः
संदानित संदानित, i. e. संदान + इत, adj. Bound, Mālav. 41, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानिनी|सन्दानिनी
संदानिनी संदानिनी, i. e. संदान + इन् + ई, f. A cow-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदाव|सन्दाव|संदावः|सन्दावः
संदाव संदाव (cf. दूत, दूर; but probably it is rather a Prākṛt form of संद्राव), m. Flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदीपन
संदीपन संदीपन, i. e. सम्-दीप् + अन,<BR> I. n. Inflaming, Ṛt. 1, 12; inflammation (of wrath), Utt. Rāmac. 116, 10.<BR> II. m. One of Kāmadeva's arrows, Lass. 7, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदूषण
संदूषण संदूषण, i. e. सम्-दुष्, Caus., + अन, n. A vice which causes infamy, Man. 9, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेश|सन्देश|संदेशः|सन्देशः
संदेश संदेश, i. e. सम्-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Information, news, tidings, Pañc. 162, 3; Kathās. 17, 161.<BR> 2. Commission, Megh. 97.<BR> 3. Command, Vikr. 86, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशक
संदेशक संदेश + क (m.), n. Information, Pañc. 51, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशहर|सन्देशहर|संदेशहरः|सन्देशहरः
संदेशहर संदेशहर, and संदेशहारक [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b " target="_blank">Page1003-b + 43</a>] संदेशहारक, i. e. संदेश-हृ + अ, and -हृ, Caus., + अक, m. A messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेह|सन्देह|संदेहः|सन्देहः
संदेह संदेह, i. e. सम्-दिह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Doubt, Pañc. iv. d. 25; uncertainty.<BR> 2. Danger, Pañc. i. d. 192.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंदेह
निस्- + संदेह निस्- + संदेह,<BR> I. adj. doubtless.<BR> II. ˚हम्, adv. undoubtedly, Somad. Nal. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेहदोलास्थ
संदेहदोलास्थ संदेह-दोला-स्थ, adj. Moved by doubt, as by a swing, Hit. iv. d. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदोह|सन्दोह|संदोहः|सन्दोहः
संदोह संदोह, i. e. सम्-दुह् + अ, m. Assemblage, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संद्राव|सन्द्राव|संद्रावः|सन्द्रावः
संद्राव संद्राव, i. e. सम्-द्रु + अ, m. Flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधा
संधा संधा, i. e. सम्-धा, f.<BR> 1. Agreement, promise, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 19.<BR> 2. Intimate union.<BR> 3. State, condition.<BR> 4. Stipulation, Lass. 2. ed. 91, 54.<BR> 5. Steadiness, fixedness.<BR> 6. Twilight.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसंध
जल-संध जल-संध, m. a proper name, Johns. Sel. 24, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासंध|जरासन्ध|जरासन्धः
जरा-संध जरा-संध, m. a proper name, ib. 49, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंध|सत्यसन्ध|सत्यसंधः|सत्यसन्धः
सत्य-संध सत्य-संध,<BR> I. adj. 1. veracious, adhering to truth, Chr. 12, 1. 2. faithful to his promise, Man. 7, 31.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Bharata. 2. Janamejaya.<BR> III. f. धा, Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसंध|असत्यसन्ध
अ-सत्य-संध अ-सत्य-संध, adj. treacherous, Hit. i. d. 78, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधान|सन्धान|संधानं|सन्धानं
संधान संधान, i. e. संधा + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Uniting, Hit. iii. d. 119 (भिन्न- [vb. भिद्], Uniting what is disunited); joining.<BR> 2. Fixing (the arrow to the bow), Śāk. d. 52.<BR> 3. Tieing, binding.<BR> 4. Peace, alliance.<BR> 5. Association, union, Pañc. iii. d. 10; Śāk. d. 9.<BR> 6. Company.<BR> 7. Mixing.<BR> 8. A relish, something eaten to excite thirst.<BR> 9. Pickles.<BR> 10. Sour rice-gruel.<BR> 11. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 12. Supporting.<BR> 13. Receiving.<BR> 14. Contracting [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a " target="_blank">Page1004-a + 46</a>] the skin, etc., by astringent applications.<BR> II. n., and f. नी, Distillation.<BR> III. f. नी, A foundry.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंधान|अतिसन्धान|अतिसंधानं
अति- + संधान अति- + संधान, n. deceit (v. r. अभि-, better), Śāk. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधान|अभिसन्धान|अभिसंधानं|अभिसन्धानं
अभि- + संधान अभि- + संधान, n. 1. speech, Rām. 5, 51, 21. 2. deceit, Ragh. 17, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंधान|दुःसन्धान
दुस्- + संधान दुस्- + संधान, adj. difficult to be united, Hit. i. d. 91, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानित|सन्धानित|सन्धानितः
संधानित संधानित, i. e. संधान + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Strung together.<BR> 2. Bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधि|सन्धि|संधिः|सन्धिः
संधि संधि, i. e. सम्-धा (cf. निधि), m.<BR> 1. Union, junction, Pañc. 210, 13; Megh. 59 (joint, structure of a mountain).<BR> 2. Alliance, Man. 7, 163.<BR> 3. Peace, Man. 7, 56.<BR> 4. Making peace, a treaty, Hit. i. d. 87, M.M.<BR> 5. A joint, an articulation of the body, Ṛt. 1, 7; Hit. iv. d. 63 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1842).<BR> 6. A fold, Pañc. 62, 13.<BR> 7. The euphonic union of the final and initial letters of words or parts of a comp.<BR> 8. An interval, a pause or rest.<BR> 9. A period at the expiration of each Yuga or age, MBh. 12, 12953.<BR> 10. A hole, a chasm, especially in a wall, for felonious purposes, a breach, Man. 9, 276; Daśak. in Chr. 186, 12.<BR> 11. Breaking, dividing, division, Lass. 87, 5.<BR> 12. The vulva.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालसंधि|कपालसन्धि|कपालसंधिः
कपाल- + संधि कपाल- + संधि, m. a peace on equal terms, Hit. iv. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवसंधि
ध्रुव- + संधि ध्रुव- + संधि, m. a proper name, Rām. 1, 70, 26 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदसंधि
पद- + संधि पद- + संधि, m. = 7. Rām. 1, 3, 60 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वसंधि
पर्वसंधि पर्वसंधि, i. e. पर्वन्-, m. the time of the periodic change of the moon, MBh. 3, 11647.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगतसंधि
सम्-गत- + संधि सम्-गत- + संधि (vb. गम्), m. a peace concluded after having before made friendship, Hit. iv. d. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानसंधि|सन्तानसन्धि|संतानसंधिः
संतान- + संधि संतान- + संधि, m. a peace concluded after having given one's daughter (in marriage), Hit. iv. d. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसंधि|समसन्धि|समसंधिः
सम- + संधि सम- + संधि, f. alliance or peace on equal terms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकरसंधि
सु-कर- + संधि सु-कर- + संधि, adj. easy to be joined or united, Pañc. ii. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधित|सन्धित|सन्धितः
संधित संधित, i. e. संधा and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b " target="_blank">Page1004-b + 44</a>] संधि, + इत,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Tied, bound, Man. 8, 342.<BR> 2. United, Pañc. i. d. 130; reconciled.<BR> 3. Pickled.<BR> II. n. Pickles.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंधित|असन्धित
अ- + संधित अ- + संधित, adj. unbound, Man. 8, 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंधित|अतिसन्धित
अति- + संधित अति- + संधित, see under धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसंधित|समसन्धित
सम- + संधित सम- + संधित, adj. 1. allied on equal terms (cf. the last). 2. bound equally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंधित
सु- + संधित सु- + संधित, adj. well reconciled, Pañc. iii. d. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधितस्
ऽसंधितस् संधि + तस्, in सम-, adv. From an alliance on equal terms, Hit. iv. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिनी|सन्धिनी
संधिनी संधिनी, i. e. संध + इन् + ई, f.<BR> 1. A cow with calf, or one which has taken a bull, Man. 5, 8.<BR> 2. One who is milked unseasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधुक्षण
संधुक्षण संधुक्षण, i. e. सम्-धुक्ष् + अन, n. Inflaming, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्या|सन्ध्या
संध्या संध्या, f., i. e.<BR> I. संधि + य,<BR> 1. Twilight, either morning or evening, Man. 2, 101; Rām. 3, 51, 5; Pañc. i. d. 198; evening, Mālat. 41, 16.<BR> 2. The period between the expiration of one Yuga, or age, and the commencement of another, Man. 1, 69.<BR> 3. Holy rites of morning, noon, and evening, Man. 2, 69.<BR> 4. Evening prayer, Vikr. 37, 9; MBh. 1, 1890.<BR> 5. Promise, agreement.<BR> 6. Joining, union.<BR> 7. Boundary.<BR> 8. A particular flower.<BR> 9. The name of a river.<BR> II. सम्-ध्यै, Reflection.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसंध्या|अग्रसन्ध्या
अग्र- + संध्या अग्र- + संध्या, f. dawn, Śāk. d. 78 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंध्यम्|उपसन्ध्यम्
उप-संध्य + म् उप-संध्य + म्, adv. near twilight, Śiś. 9, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसंध्य|त्रिसन्ध्य|त्रिसन्ध्यं
त्रि-संध्य त्रि-संध्य, n. morning, noon, and evening, MBh. 3, 4063.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंध्य
स-संध्य स-संध्य, adj. 1. vespertine. 2. with the period following the end of a Yuga (see<BR> 2.), Man. 1, 70 (see the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्यांश|सन्ध्यांश|संध्यांशः|सन्ध्यांशः
संध्यांश संध्यांश, i. e. संध्या-अंश, m.<BR> 1. Twilight.<BR> 2. The period at the end of each Yuga, Man. 1, 70 (सम्ध्यांश is perhaps especially the twilight following the expiring Yuga, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a " target="_blank">Page1005-a + 40</a>] and संध्या that which precedes the commencing Yuga).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्यातृ
संध्यातृ संध्यातृ, Man. 8, 342, m. One who binds, v. r. संदातृ, better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्यात्व
संध्यात्व संध्या + त्व, n. The time of twilight and devotion, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनति|सन्नति|संनतिः|सन्नतिः
संनति संनति, i. e. सम्-नम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Reverence, reverential salutation.<BR> 2. Humility, Rām. 1, 46, 9.<BR> 3. Sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनय|सन्नय|संनयः|सन्नयः
संनय संनय, i. e. सम्-नी + अ, m.<BR> 1. Multitude, Johns. Sel. 53, 126; number, quantity.<BR> 2. Rear, rearguard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनहन
संनहन संनहन, i. e. सम्-नह् + अन, n. Arming, preparing, making one's self ready, Rām. 4, 15, 20.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसंनहन
सर्व- + संनहन सर्व- + संनहन, n. assembling a complete army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनाम
संनाम संनाम, i. e. सम्-नम् + अ, m. Worship, Nalod. 1, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनाह|सन्नाह|संनाहः|सन्नाहः
संनाह संनाह, i. e. सम्-नह् + अ, m. Armour, mail, Johns. Sel. 26, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंनाह
वि- + संनाह वि- + संनाह, adj. without a coat of mail, Man. 7, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसंनाह
सर्व- + संनाह सर्व- + संनाह, 1. arming or assembling a complete army. 2. the Universal Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनाह्य|सन्नाह्य|संनाह्यः|सन्नाह्यः
संनाह्य संनाह्य, i. e. संनाह + य, m. A war elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिकर्ष|सन्निकर्ष|संनिकर्षः|सन्निकर्षः
संनिकर्ष संनिकर्ष, i. e. सम्-नि-कृष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Connection, relation, Bhāṣāp. 62. 131.<BR> 2. Nearness, proximity, Utt. Rāmac. 151, 11; Pañc. i. d. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिकर्षण|सन्निकर्षण|संनिकर्षणं|सन्निकर्षणं
संनिकर्षण संनिकर्षण, i. e. सम्-नि-कृष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Approximation, approaching.<BR> 2. Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधातृ|सन्निधातृ
संनिधातृ संनिधातृ, i. e. सम्-नि-धा + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A receiver of stolen goods, Man. 9, 278.<BR> 2. One who places [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b " target="_blank">Page1005-b + 42</a>] near, who introduces, the name of a court officer, Pañc. 156, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधान|सन्निधान|संनिधानं|सन्निधानं
संनिधान संनिधान, i. e. सम्-नि-धा + अन, n., and संनिधि संनिधि, i. e. सम्-निधा (cf. निधि), m.<BR> 1. Proximity, Hit. pr. d. 41, M.M. (धान); Pañc. v. d. 42 (धि).<BR> 2. Perceptibility, appearance, presence, Vikr. 19, 1. (धान); Hit. i. d. 113, M.M. (धि); Bhartṛ. 2, 99 (संनिधि-रत्न-पूर्ण, Full of jewels in close neighbourhood, i. e. round about himself, easily to be caught).<BR> 3. Placing, depositing, a receptacle, Pañc. i. d. 204 (धान).<BR> 4. Receiving, taking charge of.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसंनिधि|कुलसन्निधि|कुलसन्निधिः
कुल-संनिधि कुल-संनिधि, m. the presence of a company, Man. 8, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिपात|सन्निपात|संनिपातः|सन्निपातः
संनिपात संनिपात, i. e. सम्-नि-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Contact, collision, Bhāṣāp. 116; Kir. 5, 36.<BR> 2. Assemblage, multitude.<BR> 3. Morbid state of the three humours, Pañc. i. d. 193.<BR> 4. Alighting, descending.<BR> 5. Arrival.<BR> 6. Union, junction.<BR> 7. Mixture, Megh. 5; miscellaneous collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिबन्धन|सन्निबन्धन|सन्निबन्धनं
संनिबन्धन संनिबन्धन, i. e. सम्-नि-बन्ध् + अन, n. Tieing fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिभ|सन्निभ|सन्निभः
संनिभ संनिभ, i. e. सम्-नि-भा, adj. Like, similar, Pañc. i. d. 374; iii. d. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनियन्तृ
संनियन्तृ संनियन्तृ, i. e. सम्-नि-यम् + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what chastises, Man. 9, 320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवृत्ति|सन्निवृत्ति|संनिवृत्तिः|सन्निवृत्तिः
संनिवृत्ति संनिवृत्ति, i. e. सम्-नि-वृत् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Return, Śāk. d. 137.<BR> 2. Restraint, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवेश|सन्निवेश|संनिवेशः|सन्निवेशः
संनिवेश संनिवेश, i. e. सम्-नि-विश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. An open place, either in a town or its vicinity, where the people take exercise; place, Ragh. 6, 19.<BR> 2. Assemblage, multitude, Ragh. 16, 11 (? v. r.).<BR> 3. Vicinity.<BR> 4. Junction, union, Mālat. 18, 5.<BR> 5. Causing to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a " target="_blank">Page1006-a + 42</a>] enter, putting in.<BR> 6. Construction, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 13 (कन्या-पुर-, of the gynæceum); fabrication, Mālat. 151, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसंनिवेश
भूमि- + संनिवेश भूमि- + संनिवेश, m. the shape, face of a region, Utt. Rāmac. 47, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजसंनिवेश
समाज- + संनिवेश समाज- + संनिवेश, m. a building for an assembly, Utt. Rāmac. 161, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यसन|सन्न्यसन|संन्यसनं
संन्यसन संन्यसन, i. e. सम्-नि -2. अस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Abandonment of all worldly affections and possessions, Bhag. 3, 4.<BR> 2. Entrusting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यास|सन्न्यास|संन्यासः|सन्न्यासः
संन्यास संन्यास, i. e. सम्-नि- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abandonment.<BR> 2. Abandonment of all worldly affections and possessions, and fixing one's mind only on the Supreme Spirit, Man. 1, 114; 5, 108.<BR> 3. Deposit, trust.<BR> 4. Stake (in game), Nal. 26, 5.<BR> 5. Sudden death.<BR> 6. Indian spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यासिक
ऽसंन्यासिक -संन्यासिक, i. e. संन्यासिन् + क, in वेद-, m. An ascetic according to the Veda, Man. 6, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यासिन्|सन्न्यासिन्
संन्यासिन् संन्यासिन्, i. e. संन्यास + इन्, m.<BR> 1. One who has abandoned all worldly affections, etc. (see संन्यास), Bhag. 5, 3; Lass. 48, 15.<BR> 2. The Brāhmaṇa of the fourth order, the religious mendicant.<BR> 3. An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मातुर|सन्मातुरः
सन्मातुर सन्मातुर, i. e. सन्त्-मातृ + अ, m. The son of a virtuous mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मान|सन्मानः
सन्मान सन्मान, i. e. सन्त्-मान, m. Respect for the good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्
सप् सप्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To connect.<BR> 2. To worship.<BR> --Cf. σέϐομαι, σέϐας, σεμνός, perhaps ἅπτω (doubtful on account of ἐάϕθη, ἄαπτος).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्न|सपत्नः
सपत्न सपत्न, i. e. स-पत्नी + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ना, Hostile, Pañc. i. d. 318.<BR> II. m. A foe, Man. 4, 14; cf. पत्नी.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्न
अ- + सपत्न अ- + सपत्न, and निस्-, adj. 1. without a rival, Vikr. d. 85 (निस्-). 2. uncontested, MBh. 3, 4093 (अ-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकरण|सपत्त्राकरणं|सपत्राकरणं
सपत्राकरण सपत्रा-करण, i. e. सपत्रा-कृ + अन, n., and सपत्राकृति सपत्रा-कृ + ति. f. (cf. सपत्रा-कृ, p. 209), Affliction, excessive agony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपदि
सपदि स-पद् + इ, adv.<BR> 1. Instantly, Pañc. 198, 3.<BR> 2. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्य
सपर्य सपर्य, a denomin. derived from a lost noun सपस् = σέϐας, in the form *सपन् (with र् for न्), with य, Par. To worship (ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्या|सपर्य्या
सपर्या सपर्या, i. e. सपर्य + अ, f. Worship, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डता
सपिण्डता स-पिण्ड + ता, f. The condition of being a सपिण्ड, Man. 5, 60 (see स-पिण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तक|सप्तकः
सप्तक सप्तक, i. e. सप्तन् + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Containing seven, Man. 11, 52.<BR> 2. Seven.<BR> 3. Seventh.<BR> II. n. A collection of seven verses, Man. 11, 255.<BR> III. f. की, A woman's girdle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्तक
सप्तसप्तक सप्तसप्तक, i. e. सप्तन्-, n. fortynine (winds), Rām. 3, 53, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तत
ऽसप्तत -सप्तत, i. e. सप्तति + अ, ord. num., f. ती, Seventieth; e. g. एक-, Seventy-first, MBh. xii. adhy. 71. द्वा- or द्वि-, Seventy-second, MBh. xii. adhy. 72 (द्वा); i. adhy. 72 (द्वि). त्रि-, Seventy-third, ib. xii. adhy. 73.<BR> चतुःसप्तत, i. e. चतुर्-, Seventyfourth, MBh. xii. adhy. 74.<BR> पञ्चसप्तत, i. e. पञ्चन्-, Seventy-fifth, ib. i. adhy. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तति|सप्ततिः
सप्तति सप्तति, i. e. सप्तन् + ति, numeral, f. Seventy, Man. 1, 79.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसप्तति|एकसप्ततिः
एक- + सप्तति एक- + सप्तति, f. seventy-one, Man. 1, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वासप्तति|द्वासप्ततिः
द्वा- + सप्तति द्वा- + सप्तति or द्वि-, f. seventy-two, MBh. xii. adhy. 172 (द्वा); Man. 7, 157 (द्वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसप्तति|पंचसप्तति|पञ्चसप्ततिः
पञ्चसप्तति पञ्चस्˚, i. e. पञ्चन्-, f. seventy-five, MBh. xii. adhy. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्तति
सप्तसप्तति सप्तस्˚, i. e. सप्तन्-, f. seventy-seven, Rājat. 5, 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकसप्तति|शुकसप्ततिः
शुक- + सप्तति शुक- + सप्तति, f. seventy tales of a parrot, title of a work, Lass. 38, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ततितम|सप्ततितमः
सप्ततितम सप्तति + तम, ord. num., f. मी, Seventieth, MBh. xii. adhy. 70.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसप्ततितम
द्वि- + सप्ततितम द्वि- + सप्ततितम, seventy-second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसप्ततितम
त्रि- + सप्ततितम त्रि- + सप्ततितम, seventy-third, MBh. ii. adhy. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःसप्ततितम
चतुःसप्ततितम चतुःस्˚, i. e. चतुर्-, seventy-fourth, Rām. vi. sarga 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवसप्ततितम
नवसप्ततितम नवस्˚, i. e. नवन्-, seventy-ninth, Rām. vi. sarga 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदश|सप्तदशः
सप्तदश सप्तदश, i. e. सप्तदशन् + अ, or curtailed, ord. num., f. शी, Seventeenth, MBh. iv. adhy. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदशन्
सप्तदशन् सप्तदशन्. i. e. सप्तन्-दशन्, numeral adj. Seventeen, MBh. v. adhy. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधा
सप्तधा सप्तधा, i. e. सप्तन् + धा, adv. In seven ways, sevenfold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसप्तधा
द्वि- + सप्तधा द्वि- + सप्तधा, adv. in fourteen parts, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तन्
सप्तन् सप्तन्, numeral adj. Seven, Man. 1, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἑπτά; Lat. septem; Goth. sibun; A.S. seofon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसप्तन्
त्रि- + सप्तन् त्रि- + सप्तन्, adj. twentyone, MBh. 9, 664.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसप्तन्
पञ्चसप्तन् पञ्चसप्तन्, i. e. पञ्चन्-, adj. thirty-five, Mārk. P. 76, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्तन्
सप्तसप्तन् सप्तसप्तन्, i. e. सप्तन्-, adj. seven and seven (seven ancestors and seven descendants), Man. 1, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तम|सप्तमः
सप्तम सप्तम. i. e. सप्तन् + म,<BR> I. ord. num., f. मी, Seventh, MBh. iv. adhy. 7; Lass. 2. ed. 13, 12 (the seventh lunar mansion).<BR> II. f. मी, The seventh day of the fortnight, Rājat. 5, 221.<BR> --Cf. Lat. septimus; ἕϐδομος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तर्षि
सप्तर्षि सप्तर्षि, i. e. सप्तन्-ऋषि, m. pl.<BR> 1. The seven Ṛṣis or great saints, मरीचि, अत्रि, etc.<BR> 2. The constellation Ursa major.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तला
सप्तला सप्तला, f. The name of several plants, e. g. the trumpet-flower, Bignonia suaveolens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ति|सप्तिः
सप्ति सप् + ति, m.<BR> 1. A span (of horses), united like a span, Chr. 291, 1 = Rigv. i. 85, 1<BR> 2. A horse.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b " target="_blank">Page1007-b + 41</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्ति|सप्तसप्तिः
सप्तसप्ति सप्तसप्ति, i. e. सप्तन्-, m. the sun (properly, drawn by seven horses), Kir. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसप्ति|सितसप्तिः
सित- + सप्ति सित- + सप्ति, m. Arjuna, Kir. 13, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफर|सफरः
सफर सफर, see शप्कर; सफल सफल, see स-फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध्
सबाध् स-बाध्, adj. Striking with fear, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभक्तिकम्
सभक्तिकम् स-भक्ति + क + म्, adv. Respectfully, Lass. 41, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभा
सभा सभा, f.<BR> 1. An assembly, Man. 8, 11; council, Rām. 2, 63, 36, Seramp.<BR> 2. A much frequented place, Man. 9, 264.<BR> 3. A court of justice, Man. 8, 12; Pañc. iii. d. 109.<BR> 4. A house.<BR> 5. A palace, Johns. Sel. 94, 57; Rājat. 5, 391.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसभा
राजसभा राजसभा, i. e. राजन्-, f. a royal assembly, a court, Lass. 2, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसभ
स्त्री-सभ स्त्री-सभ, n. an assembly of females.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वसभा
ह्रस्व-सभा ह्रस्व-सभा, f. a small hall; cf. सभ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाज्
सभाज् सभाज्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from a noun, *सभाज्, i. e. स-भज्), Par.<BR> 1. To serve, to worship, Rām. 5, 8, 20.<BR> 2. To honour, to beautify, Utt. Rāmac. 105, 5.<BR> 3. † To exhilarate.<BR> 4. † To show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजन|सभाजनं
सभाजन सभाज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Courtesy, politeness.<BR> 2. Honour, Mālav. 74, 10 (thanks).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभासद्
सभासद् सभा-सद्, and सभासद सभा-सद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. An assistant at an assembly, Rām. 2, 5, 24 (सद्); Pañc. i. d. 336 (सद).<BR> 2. A judge, Man. 8, 12 (सद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभास्तार|सभास्तारः
सभास्तार सभास्तार, i. e. सभा-आ-स्तृ + अ, m. An assistant at an assembly, MBh. 2, 1787.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभिक|सभिकः
सभिक सभिक, i. e. सभा + इक, m. The keeper of a gaming-house, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 20; Mṛcch. 33, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्य|सभ्यः
सभ्य सभ्य, i. e. सभा + य,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a " target="_blank">Page1008-a + 44</a>]<BR> 1. Relating to an assembly, fit for it, Ragh. 1, 55; polite, Pañc. i. d. 294 (cf. Bhartṛ. 3, 57; सभ्य-इतर, vulgar).<BR> 2. Trusted, faithful.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An assistant at an assembly of scholars, Rājat. 5, 32; of courtiers, 86; of judges, Pañc. 40, 23.<BR> 2. A person of honourable parentage, Bhaṭṭ. 1, 13.<BR> 3. The keeper of a gaming-house.<BR> 4. The servant of a keeper of a gaminghouse (?), Daśak. in Chr. 186, 4.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. sibba; A.S. sib, sibbe, ge-sib; Goth. trasti-sibja, adoptatio, ga-sibjôn, reconciliare, un-sibja, iniqua; O.H.G. sibbi, sibbo, ga-sibbo, ga-sibbôt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1007-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यता
सभ्यता सभ्य + ता, f. Politeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
† 1. सम् सम्, स्तम् स्तम्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To be unconfused.<BR> 2. To be confused.<BR> --i. 10, समय, स्तमय, Par. To be confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
2. सम् स + म् (acc. sing. n. of स),<BR> 1. prep. With, only in the Veda, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR> 2. Combined and compounded with verbs and their derivatives, and compounded with nouns, With, together, much, very, wholly, beautifully. When followed by a prefix, it is generally without a special signification; e. g. सम्-उद्-क्षिप्, Pañc. 43, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम स + म,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Even, plain, Śāk. 5, 14; Pañc. ii. d. 188.<BR> 2. Same, Hit. 116, 18.<BR> 3. Equal, MBh. 10, 622; समं कृ, To balaṇce, to pay, Man. 8, 177.<BR> 4. Convenient, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1880; Nalod. 4, 8 (voice, neither too low nor too loud).<BR> 5. Straight, Śāk. d. 9.<BR> 6. Looking on unmoved, (with gen. and loc.), MBh. 1, 1061; 1942.<BR> 7. Impartial, indifferent, Lass. 6, 16.<BR> 8. Mean, common, Man. 7, 85; Hit. pr. d. 42, M.M. (not pre-eminent).<BR> 9. Like, similar, Chr. 8, 27 (मया, Like myself).<BR> 10. Good, Chr. 12, 28; virtuous. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b " target="_blank">Page1008-b + 43</a>]<BR> 11. A purchaser at a fair price, Man. 9, 287.<BR> 12. Full, complete.<BR> 13. All, whole, entire (follows the pronominal declension).<BR> II. ˚मम्,<BR> A. adv.<BR> 1. With (with instr.), Rājat. 5, 216; together, Śiś. 9, 24; Vikr. 88, 17.<BR> 2. Equally, Hit. iii. d. 49; Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 18.<BR> 3. Like, Johns. Sel. 15, 55 (with loc. ?).<BR> 4. In the same way, Śiś. 9, 44.<BR> 5. Conformable to, Pañc. 25, 14.<BR> 6. Entirely, ib. 63, 1.<BR> B. prep. (with instr.), With, Hit. i. d. 79, M.M.; together with, Pañc. ii. d. 200.<BR> III. f. मा, A year, Man. 4, 26.<BR> IV. n. Level plain, Man. 1, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sama, and sama-, e. g. in sama-frathjis; A.S. same, sam-; Goth. samana; A.S. somne, samne; Goth. samath; A.S. sámod; Goth. sums, and A.S. sum, quidam; Lat. similis, simul, semel, sem-per, singuli; ὁμός, ὁμοῖος, ὅμοιος, ὁμαλός, ἁμᾷ, ἅμα, μία, μέν (cf. स).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
अ- + सम अ- + सम, 1. uneven, Kir. 5, 7. 2. unequal, Man. 10, 73. 3. incomparable, Kathās. 23, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःसम
चतुःसम चतुःसम, i. e. चतुर्-, adj. having four even or smooth (members of the body), Rām. 5, 32, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्षम्
समक्षम् सम्-अक्ष + म्, adv. Eye to eye, in presence of, Śāk. 97, 10; Hit. 99, 10; Mālat. 47, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समग्र|समग्रः
समग्र सम्-अग्र, adj.<BR> 1. Entire, complete, Megh. 57; full, Hiḍ. 3, 13.<BR> 2. All, Rām. 3, 49, 37.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
अ- + समग्र अ- + समग्र, adj. not full-grown, Vikr. d. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचित्तत्व
समचित्तत्व सम-चित्त + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Equanimity.<BR> 2. Indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज|समजं|समजः
समज सम्-अज् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A multitude of beasts.<BR> 2. A number of blockheads.<BR> II. n. A forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्ञा
समज्ञा सम-ज्ञा, f. Fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्या
समज्या सम्-अज् + या, f. An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समञ्जस|समंजस|समञ्जसं|समञ्जसः
समञ्जस समञ्जस, i. e. सम्-अञ्जस् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a " target="_blank">Page1009-a + 42</a>] (cf. अञ्जसा), + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Proper, right, fit, Johns. Sel. 5, 28 (न-अति-, Not very proper, f. सा; MBh. 1, 5832, f. सी).<BR> 2. Correct, true.<BR> 3. Virtuous, good, Kir. 14, 12.<BR> 4. Experienced.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Propriety.<BR> 2. Correct evidence, Man. 8, 256.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जस|असमंजस|असमञ्जसं
अ- + समञ्जस अ- + समञ्जस,<BR> I. adj. unfit, unskilled, Utt. Rāmac. 95, 12; incorrect, Mālat. 162, 10.<BR> II. सम्, adv. unbecomingly, MBh. 2, 2100.<BR> III. n. impropriety, an abominable act, Pañc. in Weber, Ind. St. iii. 371, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समता
समता सम + ता, f.<BR> 1. Sameness, similarity.<BR> 2. Equality, Pañc. ii. d. 90 (स्व-जाति-समतां गत, Grown equal to his kind).<BR> 3. State of a common (not pre-eminent) person, Hit. pr. d. 42, M.M.<BR> 4. Equanimity, Man. 6, 44.<BR> 5. Right decision, Man. 8, 178.<BR> 6. Perfectness, Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम|समतिक्रमः
समतिक्रम सम्-अति-क्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Transgressing.<BR> 2. Omission, Man. 11, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्व|समत्वं
समत्व सम + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Equality, Bhag. 2, 48.<BR> 2. Identity, Pañc. i. d. 468.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिक|समधिकः
समधिक सम्-अधिक, adj.<BR> 1. Exceeding, Megh. 100.<BR> 2. Abundant, plentiful, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन
समन समन, probably सम्-अन् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Zeal.<BR> 2. A diligent man, Chr. 287, 6 = Rigv. i. 48, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञान|समनुज्ञानं
समनुज्ञान समनुज्ञान, i. e. सम्-अनु-ज्ञा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Assent.<BR> 2. Permission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुव्रत
समनुव्रत सम्-अनु-व्रत, adj. Entirely devoted to, Nal. 13, 55 (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त|समंत|समन्तः
समन्त सम्-अन्त,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. From every part, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1446; entire.<BR> 2. All.<BR> II. Abl. तात्, adv.<BR> 1. From every part, Pañc. 51, 18.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b " target="_blank">Page1009-b + 43</a>] All round, on every side, Mālat. 158, 4; Pañc. 230, 16; Chr. 4, 20.<BR> 3. Completely, Pañc. 148, 12.<BR> III. m. Limit, boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्ततस्
समन्ततस् समन्त + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. All round, on every side, Hit. ii. d. 158.<BR> 2. Wholly, Man. 3, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वय|समन्वयः
समन्वय समन्वय, i. e. सम्-अनु-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Natural succession.<BR> 2. Connected sequence, consequence, Lass. 2. ed. 46, 31.<BR> 3. Conjunction with each other, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिसरण|समभिसरणं
समभिसरण समभिसरण, i. e. सम्-अभि-सृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Approaching.<BR> 2. Seeking.<BR> 3. Endeavouring to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहार|समभिहारः
समभिहार समभिहार, i. e. सम्-अभि-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Repetition.<BR> 2. Excess, surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममय
सममय सम + मय, adj., f. यी, Proceeding from the same cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समय|समयः
समय समय, i. e. सम्-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Agreement, Pañc. 193, 13; treaty, Pañc. 24, 25; contract, bargain.<BR> 2. Engagement, Chr. 58, 2; appointment.<BR> 3. Religious obligation, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 304.<BR> 4. Established moral or ceremonial custom, Chr. 19, 4.<BR> 5. Rule, Man. 9, 273; law, Hit. ii. d. 45, M.M.<BR> 6. Condition, Nal. 13, 67.<BR> 7. Order, instruction.<BR> 8. Oath, Sāv. 4, 17.<BR> 9. Sign, hint, indication.<BR> 10. Proper time for anything, season, Kir. 2, 28.<BR> 11. Opportunity, leisure.<BR> 12. Time, Vikr. 56, 1; Pañc. 229, 10.<BR> 13. Same time, Chr. 7, 15.<BR> 14. Limit, boundary.<BR> 15. Demonstrated conclusion, and conclusion in general, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसमय|ऋतुसमयः
ऋतु- + समय ऋतु- + समय, m. season proper for conception, Pañc. 74, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथासमयम्
यथा-समय + म् यथा-समय + म्, adv. according to established custom, Johns. Sel. 10, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नसमय|लग्नसमयः
लग्न- + समय लग्न- + समय, m. auspicious time, Pañc. 129, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया समया, adv. and prep. with [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a " target="_blank">Page1010-a + 41</a>] acc.,<BR> I. (old instr. of सम).<BR> 1. Within, midst.<BR> 2. Near, Vārt. ad Pāṇ. ii. 3, 2; Nalod. 4, 8.<BR> II. (old instr. of समय).<BR> 1. At a fixed time.<BR> 2. Seasonably, in due time.<BR> --Cf. ἁμᾷ, ἅμα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयाध्युषित
समयाध्युषित समयाध्युषित, i. e. समय-अध्युषित (vb. 1. वस्, with अधि), n. A time at which neither stars nor sun are visible, Man. 2, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर|समरं|समरः
समर समर, i. e. सम्-ऋ + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. War, battle, Hit. 106, 10.<BR> II. m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थ|समर्थः
समर्थ सम्-अर्थ,<BR> I. adj., f. था.<BR> 1. Proper, fit, Pañc. 169, 10.<BR> 2. Allowed, Man. 4, 186.<BR> 3. Made proper, prepared, Pañc. 121, 24.<BR> 4. Able, Hit. 31, 3, M.M.; adequate to.<BR> 5. Strong, powerful, Pañc. iii. d. 54.<BR> 6. Connected in sense.<BR> II. m. The construction of words.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
अ- + समर्थ अ- + समर्थ, adj. 1. not adequate, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 11. 2. unable, Hit. 32, 4, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसमर्थ
अति- + समर्थ अति- + समर्थ, adj. very strong, Hit. 83, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थता
समर्थता समर्थ + ता, f.<BR> 1. Adequacy.<BR> 2. Ability.<BR> 3. Strength, power.<BR> 4. Signification of terms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थन|समर्थनं
समर्थन सम्-अर्थ् + अन, m.<BR> 1. Reconciling differences, allaying a dispute.<BR> 2. Perseverance in an arduous undertaking.<BR> 3. Deliberation, deciding on the propriety or impropriety of anything.<BR> 4. Objecting, objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्धक|समर्द्धकः
समर्धक समर्धक, i. e. सम्-ऋध् + अक, adj. Granting a boon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पण|समर्पणं|समर्प्पण
समर्पण समर्पण, i. e. सम्-ऋ, Caus., + अन, n. Delivering, consigning, handing over, Kathās. 4, 109; Rājat. 5, 299.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवतार|समवतारः
समवतार समवतार, i. e. सम्-अव-तॄ + अ, m. A place of pilgrimage at a sacred stream, Kir. 5, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
समवस्था सम्-अव-स्था, f. State, Śāk. 39, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाय|समवायः
समवाय समवाय, i. e. सम्-अव-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Multitude, Pañc. 130, 7; aggregate; meeting, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 14.<BR> 2. Assembly, Man. 4, 108.<BR> 3. Intimate and constant relation, Bhāṣāp. 1. 58; as of yarn and the cloth made of it, the individual and its species, etc.<BR> 4. Intimate union, Śāk. 108, 10; union, Pañc. i. d. 376.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिन्
समवायिन् समवायिन्, i. e. समवाय + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Aggregated.<BR> 2. Connected intimately, Bhāṣāp. 16; 17.<BR> II. n. Intimate and inseparable cause, as thread of cloth.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
अ- + समवायिन् अ- + समवायिन्, adj. the non-intimate cause, as the conjunction of two halves for a jar, Sch. ad Bhāṣāp. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्टि|समष्टिः
समष्टि समष्टि, i. e. सम्-अक्ष् + ति, f. Totality, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन|समसनं
समसन सम्-अस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Combination.<BR> 2. Formation of compound terms.<BR> 3. Contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थ|समस्थः
समस्थ सम-स्थ, adj.<BR> 1. Even.<BR> 2. Like, similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्या
समस्या सम्-अस् + या (fem. of the ptcple. fut. pass. of सम्- 2. अस्), f.<BR> 1. The part of a stanza given to another person to complete it.<BR> 2. The giving to another person part of a stanza, and requiring him to complete it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांश|समांशः
समांश समांश, i. e. सम-अंश,<BR> I. m. An equal part.<BR> II. adj. Entitled to an equal share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांशिन्
समांशिन् समांशिन्. i. e. समांश + इन्, adj. sbst. A co-heir, entitled to an equal share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांसमीना
समांसमीना समांसमीना, i. e. सम + म्-समा + म् + ईन (see सम), f. A cow bearing a calf every year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्षिन्
समाकर्षिन् समाकर्षिन्, i. e. सम्-आ-कृष् + अ + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Possessing a diffusive fragrance.<BR> II. m., f. णी, n. A scent spreading afar, Amarakoṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकार
समाकार समाकार, i. e. सम-आकार, adj. Like in appearance. Pañc. i. d. 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुलत्व
समाकुलत्व सम्-आकुल + त्व, n. Agitation, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या सम्-आ-ख्या, f.<BR> 1. Fame.<BR> 2. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागति|समागतिः
समागति समागति, i. e. सम्-आ-गम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Arrival.<BR> 2. Union.<BR> 3. Meeting.<BR> 4. (i. e. सम-आगति), Similar progress or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम|समागमः
समागम सम्-आ-गम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Arrival, Vikr. 10, 21 (return); approach.<BR> 2. Union, Vikr. d. 29; junction, Pañc. 128, 3; assembly, Pañc. 196, 16.<BR> 3. Association, intercourse, Hit. pr. d. 42, M.M.<BR> 4. Encountering, meeting, Pañc. 161, 12.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तसमागम
धूर्त- + समागम धूर्त- + समागम, m. the assemblage of rogues, title of a drama, Lass. 66, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघात|समाघातः
समाघात समाघात, i. e. सम्-आ-हन्, Caus., + अ, m.<BR> 1. War, battle.<BR> 2. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचार|समाचारः
समाचार समाचार, i. e.<BR> I. सम्-आ-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Proper practice or conduct, MBh. 5, 2688; Pañc. 24, 10.<BR> 2. Proceeding, conduct, Draup. 9, 17.<BR> 3. Going, way, Pañc. 109, 11.<BR> 4. Information, report.<BR> II. सम-आचार, adj. Equal in virtuous conduct, Pañc. iii. d. 140.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षक्रियासमाचार
मोक्ष-क्रिया- + समाचार मोक्ष-क्रिया- + समाचार, adj. affording a way for liberating, Pañc. 109, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाकुलसमाचार
वृथा-कुल- + समाचार वृथा-कुल- + समाचार, adj. descended from a low family and ill-behaved, Johns. Sel. 20, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुसमाचार
साधु- + समाचार साधु- + समाचार, adj. wellbehaved, Pañc. 41, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज|समाजः
समाज समाज, i. e. सम्-अज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A multitude, MBh. 1, 5698; a number.<BR> 2. An assembly, Pañc. 158, 7. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b " target="_blank">Page1011-b + 42</a>]<BR> 3. A convivial meeting.<BR> 4. An elephant.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतसमाज|द्यूतसमाजः
द्यूत- + समाज द्यूत- + समाज, m. an assembly of gamesters, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षासमाज|प्रेक्षासमाजः
प्रेक्षा- + समाज प्रेक्षा- + समाज, m. the crowd at theatres, Man. 9, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजिक|समाजिकः
समाजिक समाजिक, i. e. समाज + इक, m. A spectator, Mālat. 4, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादान|समादानं
समादान समादान, i. e. सम्-आ-दा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Receiving suitable donations.<BR> 2. Taking.<BR> 3. The daily observances of the जैन sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेश|समादेशः
समादेश समादेश, i. e. सम्-आ-दिश् + अ, m. Advice, Pañc. i. d. 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधान|समाधानं
समाधान समाधान, i. e. सम्-आ-धा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Restraining the senses and confining the mind to contemplation on the true nature of spirit, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 13, cf. 18; contemplation, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 5.<BR> 2. Promising, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधि|समाधिः
समाधि समाधि, i. e. सम्-आ-धा (cf. निधि), m.<BR> 1. Composing or reconciling differences.<BR> 2. Storing corn.<BR> 3. The joint of the neck, Kir. 16, 21.<BR> 4. A tomb.<BR> 5. Agreement, promise.<BR> 6. Requital.<BR> 7. Restraining the senses and confining the mind to contemplation on the true nature of spirit, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 18; 216, 1, cf. 217, 21; contemplation, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 1; devotion, Pañc. 162, 24.<BR> 8. A religious vow or obligation, Kumāras. 3, 24.<BR> 9. Silence.<BR> 10. Demonstrated conclusion.<BR> 11. Attempting impossibilities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिन्
समाधिन् समाधिन्, i. e. समाधि + इन्, adj. Absorbed in contemplation, meditating, Bhag. 4, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिस्थ|समाधिस्थः
समाधिस्थ समाधि-स्थ, adj. Devoted to meditation, Pañc. 162, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
समान<BR> A. i. e. स-मान,<BR> I. adj., f. ना and नी.<BR> 1. Like, similar, equal, Vikr. d. 110; Pañc. ii. d. 26.<BR> 2. Same, Chr. 295, 10 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a " target="_blank">Page1012-a + 42</a>] = Rigv. i. 92, 10; Man. 7, 163; Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 21; one, uniform.<BR> 3. Good, virtuous.<BR> 4. Honoured, Lass. 1, 12.<BR> II. अम्, adv. Equally (with instr.), Kir. 18, 4.<BR> III. m. A friend, Nalod. 2, 16.<BR> B. i. e. सम्-अन् + अ, m. One of the vital airs, that which is essential to digestion, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानता
समानता समान + ता, f.<BR> 1. Sameness, equality.<BR> 2. Community of kind or quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानोदर्य|समानोदर्यः|समानोदर्य्य|समानोदर्य्यः
समानोदर्य समानोदर्य, i. e. समान-उदर + य, m. A brother of whole blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापक|समापकः
समापक सम्-आप् + अक, adj.<BR> 1. Finishing, completing.<BR> 2. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन|समापनं
समापन सम्-आप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Conclusion, completion, Man. 5, 88.<BR> 2. A section, a chapter.<BR> 3. Profound meditation.<BR> 4. Acquisition.<BR> 5. Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापिपयिषु
समापिपयिषु समापिपयिषु, i. e. सम्-आपिपयिष (desider. of the Caus. of आप्), + ऊ, adj. Wishing to complete, MBh. 1, 6872.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्ति|समाप्तिः
समाप्ति सम्-आप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. End, Man. 2, 244.<BR> 2. Perfection, accomplishment, Rām. 2, 43, 31; Bhartṛ. 3, 98.<BR> 3. Reconciling differences, putting an end to disputes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिक|समाप्तिकः
समाप्तिक समाप्ति + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Completing, final.<BR> 2. One who has finished the whole, Man. 3, 145.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A finisher.<BR> 2. One who has completed a whole course of holy study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नाय|समाम्नायः
समाम्नाय समाम्नाय, i. e. सम्-आ-म्ना + अ, m. Enumeration, Prātiś. ed. Regnier, Journ. As. 1856, p. 187.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुसमाम्नाय|पशुसमाम्नायः
पशु- + समाम्नाय पशु- + समाम्नाय, m. works on animal sacrifices, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाय|समायः
समाय समाय, i. e. सम्-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A visit.<BR> 2. Arrival, Mālat. 170, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायोग|समायोगः
समायोग समायोग, i. e. सम्-आ-युज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Union, Lass. 2. ed. 65, 6; junction, connection.<BR> 2. Aiming with (a bow), Rām. 1, 67, 10.<BR> 3. Heap, multitude.<BR> 4. Cause, motive, object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भ|समारंभ|समारंभः|समारम्भः
समारम्भ समारम्भ, i. e. सम्-आ-रभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Commencement, beginning, Pañc. ii. d. 196.<BR> 2. Undertaking, Chr. 7, 14; Pañc. 183, 2.<BR> 3. Using, Pañc. ii. d. 146.<BR> 4. An unguent, Sch. Śāk. ap. Böhtl. 211, ad 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भण
समारम्भण समारम्भण, i. e. सम्-आ-रभ् + अन, n. = समालम्भन, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराधन|समाराधनं
समाराधन सम्-आ-राध् + अन, n. Winning, gratifying, Ragh. 18, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपण|समारोपणं
समारोपण समारोपण, i. e. सम्-आ-रुह्, Caus., + अन, n. Placing or fixing in or on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोह|समारोहः
समारोह समारोह, i. e. सम्-आ-रुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Ascending.<BR> 2. Riding upon.<BR> 3. Agreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बन|समालंबनं
समालम्बन सम्-आ-लम्ब् + अन, n. Resting upon, being supported by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भ|समालंभ|समालंभः|समालम्भः
समालम्भ समालम्भ, m., and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भन|समालंभन|समालंभनं|समालम्भनं
समालम्भन समालम्भन, n., i. e. सम्-आ-लभ् + अ, or अन,<BR> 1. Smearing the body with coloured perfumes, cf. Böhtl. ad Śāk. 48, 18.<BR> 2. समालम्भ, Seizing (for a sacrifice), MBh. 2, 864.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्तन|समावर्तनं|समावर्त्तन|समावर्त्तनं
समावर्तन समावर्तन, i. e. सम्-आ-वृत् + अन, n. A pupil's return home after having finished his religious studies, Man. 2, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावाय|समावायः
समावाय समावाय, i. e. सम्-आ-अव-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Integral aggregation, totality, Bhāg. P. 2, 8, 14.<BR> 2. Association.<BR> 3. A multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावास|समावासः
समावास समावास, i. e. सम्-आ- १. वस् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a " target="_blank">Page1013-a + 40</a>] m. A dwelling-place, Pañc. 160, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेश|समावेशः
समावेश समावेश, i. e. सम्-आ-विश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Entrance.<BR> 2. Possession by evil spirits.<BR> 3. Affection, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रय|समाश्रयः
समाश्रय समाश्रय, i. e. सम्-आ-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Refuge.<BR> 2. Seeking protection.<BR> 3. Protection.<BR> 4. A dwelling-place, Pañc. 126, 2; iii. d. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लेष|समाश्लेषः
समाश्लेष समाश्लेष, i. e. सम्-आ-श्लिष् + अ, m. Embrace, Mālat. 158, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वास|समाश्वासः
समाश्वास समाश्वास, i. e. सम्-आ-श्वस् + अ, m. Trust, belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासन|समाश्वासनं
समाश्वासन समाश्वासन, i. e. सम्-आ-श्वस्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Recreating, recreation, Pañc. 162, 18.<BR> 2. Consolation, Vikr. 26, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास|समासः
समास समास, i. e. सम्- 2. अस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Aggregation.<BR> 2. Composition of words, Pāṇ. ii. 1, 3.<BR> 3. Composition of differences.<BR> 4. Contraction, conciseness; ˚सेन, instr. Succinctly, Man. 2, 25; Lass. 2. ed. 49, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्ति|समासक्तिः
समासक्ति समासक्ति, i. e. सम्-आ-सञ्ज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Union.<BR> 2. Comprehension.<BR> 3. Affection, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासज्जन
समासज्जन समासज्जन, i. e. सम्-आ-सञ्ज् + अन, n. Joining, uniting, union, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासतस्
समासतस् समास + तस्, adv. Succinctly, Man. 1, 68; Vikr. 19, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासवन्त्|समासवत्
समासवन्त् समास + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती.<BR> 1. Compounded.<BR> 2. Abridged.<BR> II. m. A tree, Cedrela Tunna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्थ
समास्थ समास्थ, i. e. सम-आ-स्थ (cf. आस्था), adj. Being happy, Chr. 10, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरण|समाहरणं
समाहरण समाहरण, i. e. सम्-आ-हृ + अन, n. Uniting, collecting, composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहर्तृ
समाहर्तृ समाहर्तृ, i. e. सम्-आ-कृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Habituated to acquire, Man. 7, 60.<BR> 2. A collector (of taxes or duties ?), Pañc. 156, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहार|समाहारः
समाहार समाहार, i. e. सम्-आ-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Collection, aggregation, Mālat. 155, 8.<BR> 2. Contraction, abridgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृति|समाहृतिः
समाहृति सम्-आ-हृ + ति, f. Abridgment, compilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वय|समाह्वयः
समाह्वय समाह्वय, i. e. सम्-आ-ह्वे + अ, m.<BR> 1. Calling out.<BR> 2. War, battle.<BR> 3. The conflict of animals or birds for sport, cockfighting, etc., Man. 9, 223; 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वान|समाह्वानं
समाह्वान समाह्वान, i. e. सम्-आ-ह्वे + अन, n.<BR> 1. Calling, Pañc. 193, 17.<BR> 2. Challenge, Nal. 7, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्
समित् सम्-इ + त्, f. War, battle, Kāvya Prak. p. 67, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिता
समिता समिता, f. Wheat, flour.<BR> --Cf. समीद and σεμίδαλις; Lat. simila, similago; it appears also in the Coptic samit and Arab. samîd, and is probably borrowed from the Greek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिति|समितिः
समिति i. e.<BR> I. सम्-इ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Meeting, union.<BR> 2. Assembly, Nal. 5, 7; company,<BR> 3. Likeness, equality.<BR> 4. War, battle.<BR> II. सम्-इति, indecl. A holy verse beginning with सम्, Man. 11, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समितिंजय
समितिंजय समितिंजय, i. e. समिति + म्-जि + अ, adj. Conquering, i. e. eminent in, the assembly, Rām. 2, 71, 29, Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्
समिध् समिध्, i. e. सम्-इन्ध्, f. Fuel, wood, Śāk. 7, 9; grass, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 6 (कुश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धन|समिंधनं|समिन्धनं
समिन्धन सम्-इन्ध् + अन, n. Fuel, Bhaṭṭ. 2, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिर|समिरः
समिर समिर, see समीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1013-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक|समीकं
समीक समीक, probably सम्यञ्च् + अ, n. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकरण|समीकरणं
समीकरण समीकरण, i. e. सम-कृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Equalising.<BR> 2. Assimilation, digestion, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष|समीक्षं|समीक्षः
समीक्ष सम्-ईक्ष् + अ,<BR> I. f. क्षा.<BR> 1. Investigation, search.<BR> 2. Looking, inspection, sight.<BR> 3. Understanding, intellect.<BR> 4. Nature, essential nature.<BR> II. n. The साङ्ख्य system of philosophy (cf. Śiś. 2, 59, where समीक्ष्य).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्षम्
अ-समीक्ष + म् अ-समीक्ष + म्, adv. inconsiderately, Hit. 43, 22 (former part of a compound, without the final म्, but v. r. अ-समीक्ष्य-कारिन्, probably to be preferred, Acting without due deliberation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीच|समीचः
समीच समीच, i. e. सम्यञ्च् + अ,<BR> I. m. The ocean.<BR> II. f. ची, A doe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचीन|समीचीनं
समीचीन समीचीन, i. e. सम्यञ्च् + ईन,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Right, correct.<BR> 2. True.<BR> 3. Fit, proper, Pañc. 229, 1.<BR> II. n. Truth, Bhāg. P. 2, 4, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीद|समीदः
समीद समीद, m. Fine wheat flour; cf. समिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीन|समीनः
समीन समीन, i. e. समा + ईन (see सम), adj.<BR> 1. Yearly, annual.<BR> 2. Hired for a year.<BR> 3. A year hence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीप|समीपः
समीप समीप, i. e. सम्-आप् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Near, at hand.<BR> II. n. Proximity, vicinity, Pañc. 81, 17; 167, 7; loc. पे, To, Pañc. 83, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपतस्
समीपतस् समीप + तस्, adv. Before, near.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मत्समीपतस्
अस्मद्- + समीपतस् अस्मद्- + समीपतस्, i. e. अस्मत्समीप + तस्, adv. in our presence, Nal. 6, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराजसमीपतस्
देव-राज- + समीपतस् देव-राज- + समीपतस्, adv. in the presence of the king of the gods, Arj. 2, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपस्थ
समीपस्थ समीप-स्थ, adj. Placed, or situated, or living near, Lass. 2. ed. 44, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर|समीरः
समीर and समिर समी̆र, i. e. सम्-ईर् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b " target="_blank">Page1014-b + 41</a>] m. Air, wind, Bhāg. P. 8, 24, 36; Prab. 80, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरण|समीरणः
समीरण समीरण, i. e. सम्-ईर् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Air, Mālat. 148, 20; wind, Arj. 4, 7.<BR> 2. A traveller.<BR> 3. A plant, commonly Maruvaka.<BR> II. n. Throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्षण|समुक्षणं
समुक्षण समुक्षण, i. e. सम्-उक्ष् + अन, n. Shedding, Mālat. 48, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चय|समुच्चयः
समुच्चय समुच्चय, i. e. सम्-उद्-चि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Collection, Cāṇ. 2 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 407.<BR> 2. Conjunction of words or sentences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छेद|समुच्छेदः
समुच्छेद समुच्छेद, i. e. सम्-उद्-छिद् + अ, m. Destroying, destruction, Kir. 11, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रय|समुच्छ्रयः
समुच्छ्रय समुच्छ्रय, i. e. सम्-उद्-श्रि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Height, elevation.<BR> 2. Opposition, enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्राय|समुच्छ्रायः
समुच्छ्राय समुच्छ्राय, i. e. सम्-उद्-श्रि + अ, m. Height, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्कर्ष|समुत्कर्षः
समुत्कर्ष समुत्कर्ष, i. e. सम्-उद्-कृष् + अ, m. Boasting one's self as being of a high tribe, Man. 11, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रम|समुत्क्रमः
समुत्क्रम समुत्क्रम, i. e. सम्-उद्-क्रम् + अ, m. Rise, assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रोश|समुत्क्रोशः
समुत्क्रोश समुत्क्रोश, i. e. सम्-उद्-क्रुश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Crying aloud.<BR> 2. An osprey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थ|समुत्थः
समुत्थ समुत्थ, i. e. सम्-उद्-स्थ, adj.<BR> 1. Rising, Chr. 33, 34; getting up.<BR> 2. Born, produced, Man. 8, 353.<BR> 3. Occasioned, occurring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थान|समुत्थानं
समुत्थान समुत्थान, i. e. सम्-उद्-स्था + अन, n.<BR> 1. Rising, getting up.<BR> 2. Increase (as of size or wealth), Rām. 3, 49, 49.<BR> 3. Healing a wound, perfect cure, Man. 8, 287.<BR> 4. Symptom of disease.<BR> 5. Performance of work, occupation.<BR> 6. With संभूय, Partnership, Man. 8, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पत्ति|समुत्पत्तिः
समुत्पत्ति समुत्पत्ति, i. e. सम्-उद्-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Origin, Man. 1, 111; production, birth.<BR> 2. Formation, Man. 5, 49.<BR> 3. Occurrence, existence. Man. 6, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिञ्ज|समुत्पिंज|समुत्पिञ्जः
समुत्पिञ्ज समुत्पिञ्ज, i. e. सम्-उद्-पिञ्ज् + अ, and समुत्पिञ्जल समुत्पिञ्ज + ल,<BR> I. adj. Excessively confused.<BR> II. m. An army in great disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिञ्जलक|समुत्पिञ्जलकः
समुत्पिञ्जलक समुत्पिञ्जल + क, m. Excessive confusion, Johns. Sel. 13, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पीडन
समुत्पीडन समुत्पीडन, i. e. सम्-उद्-पीड् + अन, n. Pressing, Lass. 87, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सर्ग|समुत्सर्गः
समुत्सर्ग समुत्सर्ग, i. e. सम्-उद्-सृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abandoning.<BR> 2. Giving.<BR> 3. Voiding of excrements, Man. 4, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सारण|समुत्सारणं
समुत्सारण समुत्सारण, i. e. सम्-उद्-सृ, Caus., + अन, n. Pursuing, hunting, Śāk. 22, 1 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुक|समुत्सुकः
समुत्सुक सम्-उत्सुक, adj.<BR> 1. Regretting, sorrowful, longing, Vikr. d. 10; 13.<BR> 2. Agitated, Lass. 2. ed. 62, 42.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमुत्सुक
परि- + समुत्सुक परि- + समुत्सुक, adj. very agitated, Rām. 2, 65, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुकत्व
समुत्सुकत्व समुत्सुक + त्व, n. Longing, desire, Ṛt. 6, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुकय
समुत्सुकय समुत्सुकय, denomin. of सम्-उत्सुक, Par. To cause to long for, Kir. 11, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सेध|समुत्सेधः
समुत्सेध समुत्सेध, i. e. सम्-उद्-सिध् + अ, m. Height, elevation, Rām. 6, 2, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमचित्रसमुत्सेध
हैम-चित्र- + समुत्सेध हैम-चित्र- + समुत्सेध, adj., f. धा, enchased with golden pictures, Draup. 8, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदय|समुदयं|समुदयः
समुदय and समुदाय समुदा̆य, i. e. सम्-उद्-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Rising (as of the sun), rise.<BR> 2. A day.<BR> 3. Effort.<BR> 4. Revenue, Man. 7, 56 (ă).<BR> 5. Multitude, Pañc. 82, 5 (आ); number, heap, Utt. Rāmac. 145, 8; Chr. 53, 5 (समुदयं} [पगे१०१५-ब् + ४१] {बलानां कृत्वा, Having collected his armies).<BR> 6. War, battle.<BR> 7. The rear or reserve of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागम|समुदागमः
समुदागम सम्-उद्-आ-गम् + अ, m. Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाचार|समुदाचारः
समुदाचार समुदाचार, i. e. सम्-उद्-आ-चर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Intention, purpose, design.<BR> 2. Proper, or right usage (address), Śāk. 67, 9 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाय|समुदायः
समुदाय समुदाय, see समुदय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरण|समुदीरणं
समुदीरण समुदीरण, i. e. सम्-उद्-ईर् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Declaring, speaking, pronouncing, Dev. 4, 7.<BR> 2. Repeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग|समुद्गः
समुद्ग समुद्ग, i. e.<BR> I. सम्-उद्-ग, adj.<BR> 1. Who or what rises.<BR> 2. Who or what pervades.<BR> II. स-मुद्ग, m. A covered box, a casket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गक|समुद्गकः
समुद्गक समुद्ग + क, m. A covered box, a casket, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्देश|समुद्देशः
समुद्देश समुद्देश, i. e. सम्-उद्-दिश् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Pointing out.<BR> 2. Describing.<BR> 3. Particularising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धरण|समुद्धरणं
समुद्धरण समुद्धरण, i. e. सम्-उद्-हृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Taking out.<BR> 2. Eradicating.<BR> 3. Drawing up.<BR> 4. Food vomited or thrown up.<BR> 5. Extricating, lifting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धर्तृ|समुद्धर्त्तृ
समुद्धर्तृ समुद्धर्तृ, i. e. सम्-उद्-हृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n.<BR> 1. Who or what takes out, pulls out, etc.<BR> 2. A deliverer, a redeemer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्भव|समुद्भवः
समुद्भव समुद्भव, i. e. सम्-उद्-भू + अ, m. Origin, Man. 6, 61.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसमुद्भव
कुल- + समुद्भव कुल- + समुद्भव, adj. descended from a high family, Hit. 7, 21 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जसमुद्भव|मज्जसमुद्भवं|मज्जसमुद्भवः
मज्ज-समुद्भव मज्ज-समुद्भव, i. e. मज्जन्-, n. semen genitale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्बन्धनसमुद्भव
मद्-बन्धन- + समुद्भव मद्-बन्धन- + समुद्भव, adj. caused by (the binding of me, i. e.) my bondage, Pañc. iii. d. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निदाहसमुद्भव
वह्नि-दाह- + समुद्भव वह्नि-दाह- + समुद्भव, adj., f. वा, produced by burning, Pañc. v. d. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थभ्रंशसमुद्भव
सार्थ-भ्रंश- + समुद्भव सार्थ-भ्रंश- + समुद्भव, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a " target="_blank">Page1016-a + 39</a>] adj. beginning with the loss of the caravan, Pañc. 68, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यम|समुद्यमः
समुद्यम सम्-उद्-यम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Lifting up, Chr. 29, 25.<BR> 2. Effort, exertion, Bhag. 1, 22.<BR> 3. Commencing, onset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र|समुद्रः
समुद्र समुद्र, i. e.<BR> I. सम्-उन्द् + र, m. A sea, the ocean, Pañc. 157, 25; Vikr. 68, 6.<BR> II. स-मुद्र (cf. मुद्रा), adj. Sealed, Man. 8, 188.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारसमुद्र|क्षारसमुद्रः
क्षार- + समुद्र क्षार- + समुद्र, m. the sea of salt, Bhāg. P. 5, 17, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरसमुद्र|क्षीरसमुद्रः
क्षीर- + समुद्र क्षीर- + समुद्र, m. the sea of milk, Pañc. 44, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारसमुद्र
संसार- + समुद्र संसार- + समुद्र, m. the ocean-like world, ib. 33, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रग|समुद्रगः
समुद्रग समुद्र-ग,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A trader by sea.<BR> 2. A seaman.<BR> II. f. गा, A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रज
समुद्रज समुद्र-ज, adj. Born from the sea, Pañc. i. d. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रारु|समुद्रारुः
समुद्रारु समुद्रारु (from समुद्र), m.<BR> 1. A shark.<BR> 2. A large fabulous fish.<BR> 3. Rāma's bridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वाह|समुद्वाहः
समुद्वाह समुद्वाह, i. e. सम्-उद्-वह् + अ, m. Nuptials, Sāv. 3, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वेग|समुद्वेगः
समुद्वेग समुद्वेग, i. e. सम्-उद्-विज् + अ, m. Fear, Rām. 3, 55, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्दन|समुंदन|समुंदनं|समुन्दनं
समुन्दन सम्-उन्द् + अन, n. Wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नति|समुन्नतिः
समुन्नति समुन्नति, i. e. सम्-उद्-नम् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Height, elevation, Hit. pr. d. 14, M.M.<BR> 2. Rank, dignity.<BR> 3. Pride.<BR> 4. Increase, prosperity, Kir. 2, 21.<BR> 5. Lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्मूलन|समुन्मूलनं
समुन्मूलन समुन्मूलन, i. e. सम्-उद्-मूल् + अन, n. Unrooting, destruction, Utt. Rāmac. 31, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपजोषम्
समुपजोषम् समुपजोषम्, i. e. सम्-उप-जुष् + अ + म्, adv. Happily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेशन|समुपवेशनं
समुपवेशन समुपवेशन, i. e. सम्-उप-विश् + अन, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b " target="_blank">Page1016-b + 41</a>] n. A building, Utt. Rāmac. 161, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपार्जन|समुपार्जनं
समुपार्जन समुपार्जन, i. e. सम्-उप-अर्ज् + अन, n. Reconciliation, Man. 7, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूर|समूरः
समूर समूर, and समूरु समूरु, m. A kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूह|समूहः
समूह समूह, i. e. सम्-ऊह्, or वह्, + अ, m. Assemblage, multitude, Śāk. d. 31; Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायादसमूह
दायाद- + समूह दायाद- + समूह, m. all the kinsmen, Pañc. 222, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसमूह
शस्त्र- + समूह शस्त्र- + समूह, n. (?), an arsenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहन|समूहनं
समूहन समूहन, i. e. सम्-ऊह्, or वह्, + अन,<BR> I. n. Collection, plenty, Man. 4, 102.<BR> II. f. नी, A broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धि|समृद्धिः
समृद्धि समृद्धि, i. e. सम्-ऋध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Thriving, increase, Ragh. 8, 13 (at the end of a comp. adj.); gain, Pañc. 134, 8.<BR> 2. Prosperity, Hit. i. d. 209, M.M.; well-being, Bhartṛ. 2, 34.<BR> 3. Supremacy, power.<BR> 4. Wealth, Pañc. ii. d. 71.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्धि|असमृद्धिः
अ- + समृद्धि अ- + समृद्धि, f. misfortune, Man. 4, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धिन्
ऽसमृद्धिन् समृद्धिन्, i. e. सम्-ऋद्ध + इन् (vb. ऋध्), adj., f. नी, Possessing plenty (of), Rām. 5, 53, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समोकस्
समोकस् सम्-ओकस्, adj. Endowed, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समोदक|समोदकं
समोदक समोदक, i. e. सम-उदक, n. A mixture of half butter-milk and half water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपत्ति|सम्पत्ति|संपत्तिः|सम्पत्तिः
संपत्ति संपत्ति, i. e. सम्-पद् + ति, f. Prosperity, Hit. i. d. 141, M.M.; success, Lass. 3, 20; power.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपत्ति|असम्पत्ति|असंपत्तिः
अ- + संपत्ति अ- + संपत्ति, f. non-succeeding, Man. 12, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसंपत्ति|धनसम्पत्ति
धन- + संपत्ति धन- + संपत्ति, f. wealth, Hit. pr. d. 11, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपसंपत्ति
रूप- + संपत्ति रूप- + संपत्ति, f. beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपद्|सम्पद्
संपद् संपद्, i. e. सम्-पद्, f.<BR> 1. Success, Hit. i. d. 183, M.M.; prosperity, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.<BR> 2. Blessing, Śāk. d. 189.<BR> 3. Wealth, Śāk. 91, 13; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a " target="_blank">Page1017-a + 42</a>] power, Megh. 54.<BR> 4. Accomplishment, Mālat. 104, 17; perfection, excellence, Hit. iii. d. 53; Śiś. 9, 1 (अभि-ताप-, Most violent heat, excess of heat).<BR> 5. Advancement in good qualities, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 7.<BR> 6. Adornment, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 18.<BR> 7. Fate, Bhag. 16, 3; 4.<BR> 8. A necklace of pearls.<BR> 9. A treasure, Man. 3, 255; Rājat. 5, 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपराय|सम्पराय|संपरायः|सम्परायः
संपराय संपराय, i. e. सम्-परा-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. War, battle, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 2.<BR> 2. Calamity.<BR> 3. Futurity.<BR> 4. A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपरिशोषण|सम्परिशोषण
संपरिशोषण संपरिशोषण, i. e. सम्-परि-शुष् + अन, n. Emaciation, Rām. 2, 10, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपर्क|सम्पर्क|सम्पर्कं|संपर्कः|सम्पर्कः
संपर्क संपर्क, i. e. सम्-पृच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Mixture.<BR> 2. Copulation.<BR> 3. Union, Vikr. d. 13; Pañc. iii. d. 58.<BR> 4. Contact, Megh. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपर्किन्
संपर्किन् संपर्किन्, i. e. संपर्क + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> 1. Blended, mixed.<BR> 2. United with.<BR> 3. In contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपर्कीय|सम्पर्कीय|सम्पर्कीयः|सम्पर्क्कीय
संपर्कीय संपर्कीय, i. e. संपर्क + ईय, adj. Liable to come in contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपाक|सम्पाक|संपाकः|सम्पाकः
संपाक संपाक, i. e. सम्-पच् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Reasoning, a reasoner.<BR> 2. Impudent.<BR> 3. Lecherous, libertine.<BR> 4. Small, little.<BR> II. m. A tree, Cassia fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपात|सम्पात|संपातः|सम्पातः
संपात संपात, i. e. सम्-पत् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Concurrence, falling against each other, Johns. Sel. 58, 170; butting together, Pañc. 35, 7.<BR> 2. Meeting, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 15.<BR> 3. Descending, falling down, Bhartṛ. 2, 29; Vikr. 85, 20 (flashing); Daśak. in Chr. 186, 15 (flashing).<BR> 4. Alighting (as a bird), flying (of arrows), Bhag. 1, 20.<BR> 5. A special mode of flight (of birds), Pañc. ii. d. 57.<BR> 6. Going, moving, Utt. Rāmac. 22, 8. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b " target="_blank">Page1017-b + 40</a>]<BR> 7. Being removed, Man. 6, 56.<BR> 8. The son of Garuda, a fabulous bird.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासंपात|धारासम्पात|धारासंपातः|धारासम्पातः
धारा- + संपात धारा- + संपात, m. a shower of rain, Prab. 87, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंपात|निःसम्पात|निःसंपातः|निःसम्पातः
निस्- + संपात निस्- + संपात, adj. impassable, Hariv. 4286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिसंपात
वृष्टि- + संपात वृष्टि- + संपात, m. a shower of rain, Rājat. 5, 275.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपाति|सम्पाति|संपातिः|सम्पातिः
संपाति संपाति, i. e. सम्-पत् + इ, m. A fabulous bird, Mahāvīrac. 74, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपातिन्
संपातिन् संपातिन्, i. e. सम्-पत् + इन्, adj., f. नी, Falling together, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपादन|सम्पादन|संपादनं|सम्पादनं
संपादन संपादन, i. e. सम्-पद्, Caus. + अन, n.<BR> 1. Accomplishing, Vikr. 37, 7 (व्रत-, The completion of a vow); effecting, making, Pañc. 133, 1.<BR> 2. Cleansing, Man. 3, 255.<BR> 3. Attaining.<BR> 4. Acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपीड|सम्पीड|संपीडः
संपीड संपीड, i. e. सम्-पीड् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Pain, torture.<BR> 2. Agitating, Kir. 7, 12.<BR> 3. Sending.<BR> II. f. डा, Torment, Man. 12, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपीडन|सम्पीडन|संपीडनं|सम्पीडनं
संपीडन संपीडन, i. e. सम्-पीड् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Pressing.<BR> 2. Castigation, punishment.<BR> 3. Sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपीति|सम्पीति|संपीतिः|सम्पीतिः
संपीति संपीति, i. e. सम्-पा + ति, f. Drinking in company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपुट|सम्पुट|संपुटः|सम्पुटः
संपुट संपुट (cf. पुट), m.<BR> 1. Cavity, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 2; Ṛt. 1, 21.<BR> 2. A covered box.<BR> 3. A flower, commonly Kuruvaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपुटक|सम्पुटक|सम्पुटकः
संपुटक संपुट + क,<BR> I. m. A casket.<BR> II. f. टिका, A box filled with ornaments, Pañc. ii. d. 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संपूजन|सम्पूजन|संपूजनं
संपूजन संपूजन, i. e. सम्-पूज् + अन, n. Treating with respect, reverence, Man. 3, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रक्षालन
संप्रक्षालन संप्रक्षालन, i. e. सम्-प्र-क्षल्, Caus., + अन, n. Inundation, Matsyop. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रणेतृ|सम्प्रणेतृ
संप्रणेतृ संप्रणेतृ, i. e. सम्-प्र-नी + तृ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a " target="_blank">Page1018-a + 40</a>] m.<BR> 1. A judge, Man. 7, 26.<BR> 2. A ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रतापन|सम्प्रतापन|संप्रतापनं
संप्रतापन संप्रतापन, i. e. सम्-प्र-तप्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Heating, burning.<BR> 2. Afflicting.<BR> 3. One of the hells, Man. 4, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रति|सम्प्रति|सम्प्रतिः
संप्रति संप्रति, i. e. सम्-प्रति, adv. Now, at this time, Pañc. 172, 9; Vikr. d. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रतिपत्ति|सम्प्रतिपत्ति|संप्रतिपत्तिः|सम्प्रतिपत्तिः
संप्रतिपत्ति संप्रतिपत्ति, i. e. सम्-प्रति-पद् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Agreement.<BR> 2. Admission.<BR> 3. Co-operation.<BR> 4. Presence, company.<BR> 5. Assault.<BR> 6. Doing, performing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रतिरोधक|सम्प्रतिरोधक|संप्रतिरोधकं|सम्प्रतिरोधकं|संप्रतिरोधकः
संप्रतिरोधक संप्रतिरोधक, i. e. सम्-प्रति-रुध् + अक, n. Durance, actual confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रतीति|सम्प्रतीति|संप्रतीतिः|सम्प्रतीतिः
संप्रतीति संप्रतीति, i. e. सम्-प्रति-इ + ति, f. Fame, notoriety, Kir. 3, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रदातृ
संप्रदातृ संप्रदातृ, i. e. सम्-प्र-दा + तृ, m. A giver, Man. 9, 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रदान|सम्प्रदान|संप्रदानं|सम्प्रदानं
संप्रदान संप्रदान, i. e. सम्-प्र-दा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Giving, gift, Hit. iv. d. 108.<BR> 2. Bestowing in marriage, Man. 7, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रदाय|सम्प्रदाय|संप्रदायः|सम्प्रदायः
संप्रदाय संप्रदाय, i. e. सम्-प्र-दा + अ, m.<BR> 1. Traditional doctrine, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 12 (दत्त-दिव्य-अस्त्र-, adj. Possessed of the traditional knowledge of the celestial arms); Rājat. 5, 139.<BR> 2. A peculiar doctrine and exclusive worship of one divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रधारणा|सम्प्रधारणा
संप्रधारणा संप्रधारणा, i. e. सम्-प्र-धृ, Caus., + अन, f. Deliberation, determining the propriety or impropriety of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रमोष|सम्प्रमोष|संप्रमोषः
संप्रमोष संप्रमोष, i. e. सम्-प्र-मुष् + अ, m. Suppression, Bhāg. P. 6, 4, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रयोग|सम्प्रयोग|संप्रयोगः|सम्प्रयोगः
संप्रयोग संप्रयोग, i. e. सम्-प्र-युज् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b " target="_blank">Page1018-b + 39</a>] m.<BR> 1. Union, Mālat. 36, 8; copulation, connexion.<BR> 2. Mutual relation, proportion.<BR> 3. Order, natural series.<BR> 4. Magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रयोगिन्|सम्प्रयोगिन्
संप्रयोगिन् संप्रयोगिन्, i. e. संप्रयोग + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A joiner.<BR> 2. A libertine.<BR> 3. A catamite.<BR> 4. A conjuror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रवेश
संप्रवेश संप्रवेश, i. e. सम्-प्र-विश् + अ, m. Entrance, Rājat. 5, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रश्न|सम्प्रश्न|संप्रश्नः
संप्रश्न संप्रश्न, i. e. सम्-प्रछ् + न, m. Asking, question, Hit. ii. d. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रसाद|सम्प्रसाद|संप्रसादः
संप्रसाद संप्रसाद, i. e. सम्-प्र-सद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Favour, grace, Utt. Rāmac. 42, 5.<BR> 2. Serenity, Windischmann, Sankara, 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रहार|सम्प्रहार|संप्रहारः|सम्प्रहारः
संप्रहार संप्रहार, i. e. सम्-प्र-हृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Striking, wounding.<BR> 2. War, battle, Śāk. 98, 14.<BR> 3. Going, motion.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वंद्वसंप्रहार
द्वंद्व- + संप्रहार द्वंद्व- + संप्रहार, m. a single combat, Utt. Rāmac. 121, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्राप्ति|सम्प्राप्ति|संप्राप्तिः|सम्प्राप्तिः
संप्राप्ति संप्राप्ति, i. e. सम्-प्र-आप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Obtaining, Pañc. 5, 10; acquisition, ib. 104, 1.<BR> 2. Gaining, Man. 7, 208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रीति|सम्प्रीति|संप्रीतिः
संप्रीति संप्रीति, i. e. सम्-प्री + ति,<BR> 1. Attachment, affection, Man. 3, 113.<BR> 2. Friendly assent, 8, 146.<BR> 3. Delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रेषण
संप्रेषण संप्रेषण, i. e. सम्-प्र -1. इष् + अन, n. Sending, Man. 7, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्लव|सम्प्लव|संप्लवः
संप्लव संप्लव, i. e. सम्-प्लु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Surge, Rām. 1, 32, 17.<BR> 2. Submerging, submersion, Hariv. 12375; inundation.<BR> 3. Falling on all sides, Man. 4, 103; ruin, Hit. i. d. 72, M.M. (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 458).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संफाल|सम्फाल|संफालः|सम्फालः
संफाल संफाल, i. e. सम्-स्फल् + अ, m. A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब्|संब्
† सम्ब् सम्ब्, शम्ब् शम्ब्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a " target="_blank">Page1019-a + 43</a>] साम्ब् साम्ब्, i. 10, Par. To connect.<BR> --Cf. सर्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबन्ध|सम्बन्ध|संबंध|संबन्धः|सम्बन्धः
संबन्ध संबन्ध, i. e. सम्-बन्ध् + अ,<BR> 1. Connexion, union, Man. 3, 157; Utt. Rāmac. 27, 15 (मद्-, with me); Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 9 (of intimately united subjects, cf. 204, 1; 212, 19; 21).<BR> 2. Relationship, Pañc. ii. d. 106; relation, Hit. i. d. 157, M.M. (अस्येदम् इति सम्बन्धो हानौ दुःखेन गम्यते, The proprietary connection between them is ascertained only by his grief in losing it).<BR> 3. Fitness, propriety.<BR> 4. Success, prosperity.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ततिसंबन्ध
सप्तति- + संबन्ध सप्तति- + संबन्ध, m. a collection of seventy tales, Lass. 40, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंबन्ध
सु- + संबन्ध सु- + संबन्ध, adj. well joined, Pañc. ii. d. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंबन्ध|स्त्रीसम्बन्ध|स्त्रीसंबंध|स्त्रीसंबन्धः
स्त्री- + संबन्ध स्त्री- + संबन्ध, m. marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबन्धक|सम्बन्धक|संबंधक|संबन्धकः
संबन्धक संबन्ध + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating, concerning.<BR> 2. Fit, suitable, Chr. 55, 7.<BR> 3. m. (viz. संधि), Proceeding from relationship, name of a kind of alliance, Hit. iv. d. 123.<BR> II. m. A friend, Rām. 1, 12, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबन्धिन्|सम्बन्धिन्|संबंधिन्
संबन्धिन् संबन्धिन्, i. e. संबन्ध + इन्, adj. and sbst., f. नी,<BR> 1. Connected with, Pañc. iii. d. 141; inherent, Vedāntas. in Chr. 214, 2; referring to, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 22.<BR> 2. Related, Man. 2, 132; 4, 179; a relation by marriage, Utt. Rāmac. 12, 4; 98, 3.<BR> 3. Belonging to, Pañc. 121, 25.<BR> 4. Possessing good qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बर|संबर|सम्बरं|संबरः|सम्बरः
सम्बर सम्बर, see शम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बल|संबल|संबलं|संबलः
सम्बल सम्बल,<BR> I. (m.), n. Stock for travelling expenses.<BR> II. n. Water (cf. शम्बल, शम्बर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबाध|सम्बाध|संबाधः|सम्बाधः
संबाध संबाध, i. e. सम्-बाध् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Being thronged, Hariv. 2677.<BR> 2. Pressing on, pressure, Johns. Sel. 60, 185.<BR> 3. Difficulty, Mārk. P. 21, 1.<BR> 4. The road to Tartarus.<BR> 5. The vulva.<BR> 6. Fear.<BR> II. adj., f. धा (Rām. 1, 40, 22, Schlegel; 2, 65, 33, Seramp.; Śakuntalop. ap. Chezy., ii. 29). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b " target="_blank">Page1019-b + 43</a>]<BR> 1. Narrow.<BR> 2. Crowded, Ragh. 12, 67.<BR> 3. Blocked up, Pañc. i. d. 427 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1446); impassable.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबाध|असम्बाध
अ- + संबाध अ- + संबाध, adj. 1. large, MBh. 2, 345. 2. lonely, Kir. 3, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबाध|अभिसम्बाध
अभि- + संबाध अभि- + संबाध, adj., f. धा, very narrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंबाध
आ- + संबाध आ- + संबाध, adj. crowded, full of, Rām. 5, 23, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंबाध
निस्- + संबाध निस्- + संबाध, adj. 1. large, Suśr. 1, 241, 7. 2. shortest (properly, without any obstruction), Daśak. in Chr. 186, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरसंबाध
शर- + संबाध शर- + संबाध, adj., f. धा, covered with arrows, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्यश्वरथसंबाध
हस्त्यश्वरथ- + संबाध हस्त्यश्वरथ- + संबाध, i. e. हस्तिन्-अश्व-रथ-, adj., f. धा, crowded by elephants, horses, and carriages, Rām. 3, 54, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबाधन|सम्बाधन|संबाधनं|सम्बाधनं
संबाधन संबाधन, i. e. सम्-बाध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Obstructing, Pañc. i. d. 427 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1446).<BR> 2. A barrier, a gate.<BR> 3. A door-keeper.<BR> 4. The point of a stake or spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबुद्धि|सम्बुद्धि|संबुद्धिः|सम्बुद्धिः
संबुद्धि संबुद्धि, i. e. सम्-बुध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Calling, or calling to.<BR> 2. (In grammar), The vocative case, Pāṇ. 2, 3, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबोध|सम्बोध|संबोधः|सम्बोधः
संबोध संबोध, i. e. सम्-बुध् + अ, m. Instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबोधन|सम्बोधन|संबोधनं|सम्बोधनं
संबोधन संबोधन, i. e. सम्-बुध् + अन,<BR> 1. Calling.<BR> 2. Addressing, Chr. 38, 16.<BR> 3. (In grammar), The vocative case (see संबुद्धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभव|सम्भव|संभवः|सम्भवः
संभव संभव, i. e. सम्-भू + अ, m.<BR> 1. Mixing, union.<BR> 2. Adaptation, appropriateness.<BR> 3. Adequacy, ability.<BR> 4. Possibility.<BR> 5. Compatibility, consistency.<BR> 6. Agreement.<BR> 7. Acquaintance.<BR> 8. Destruction, loss.<BR> 9. Springing up, Hit. iv. d. 72; origin, Man. 1, 116; birth, Mālat. 156, 6; Pañc. 263, 23; production, Hit. 16, 5, M.M.<BR> 10. Producing and rearing, Man. 2, 227.<BR> 11. Cause, motive, Pañc. i. d. 328 (ग्रहण-, of taking, viz. the life of a dependent).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव|असम्भव|असंभवः
अ- + संभव अ- + संभव,<BR> I. m. 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-a " target="_blank">Page1020-a + 46</a>] non-existence, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 872; impossibility, Pañc. ii. d. 4. 2. omission, Man. 11, 27.<BR> II. adj. impossible, Hit. i. d. 27, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनःसम्भव|अपुनःसंभव
अपुनःसम्भव अपुनःसम्भव, i. e. अ-पुनर्-, adj., f. वा, not rising again, Rājat. 1, 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंभव
अस्थि- + संभव अस्थि- + संभव,<BR> I. adj. produced by the bones, MBh. 1, 1514.<BR> II. m. the marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसम्भव|आत्मसंभव|आत्मसंभवः
आत्मसम्भव आत्मसम्भव-, i. e. आत्मन्-,<BR> I. m. a son, Rām. 5, 18, 27.<BR> II. f. वा, a daughter, ib. 3, 20, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुसंभव
ऊरु- + संभव ऊरु- + संभव, adj., f. वा, produced from the thigh, Vikr. 8, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भसंभव|कुम्भसम्भव|कुंभसंभव|कुम्भसम्भवः
कुम्भ- + संभव कुम्भ- + संभव, adj., m. epithet of Agastya, Bhāg. P. 6, 3, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भसंभव
गर्भ- + संभव गर्भ- + संभव, m. the production of an embryo, pregnancy, Yājñ. 1, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसंभव
दधि- + संभव दधि- + संभव, adj. prepared of milk, Man. 5, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजनसंभव
देव-यजन- + संभव देव-यजन- + संभव, adj., f. वा, sprung up from a place prepared for a sacrifice, Utt. Rāmac. 10, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मसंभव
पद्म- + संभव पद्म- + संभव, adj., m. epithet of Brahman, Hariv. 3233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोमीसंभव
पौलोमी- + संभव पौलोमी- + संभव, adj. born from Paulomī, Vikr. d. 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषसंभव
मानुष- + संभव मानुष- + संभव, adj. coming from a man, Pañc. 141, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालकुलसंभव
विशाल-कुल- + संभव विशाल-कुल- + संभव, adj. sprung from an illustrious race, Hit. pr. d. 39, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरारिसंभव
सुर-अरि- + संभव सुर-अरि- + संभव, adj. caused by an enemy of the gods, Vikr. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभार|सम्भार|संभारः|सम्भारः
संभार संभार, i. e. सम्-भृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Maintaining, supporting.<BR> 2. Apparatus, things required for any act or affair, Rām. 1, 11, 13; Pañc. 157, 22.<BR> 3. Provision, getting everything ready.<BR> 4. Completion, Mālat. 171, 5.<BR> 5. Fullness, wealth, Nal. 26, 24.<BR> 6. Multitude, heap, quantity, Utt. Rāmac. 141, 8; Pañc. i. d. 35; Rājat. 5, 273.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभावन|सम्भावन|संभावनं|सम्भावनं
संभावन संभावन, i. e. सम्-भू, Caus., + अन, n., and f. ना,<BR> 1. Adequacy, ability.<BR> 2. Fitness.<BR> 3. Possibility.<BR> 4. Doubt.<BR> 5. Considering, Ragh. 5, 28 (f.); reflecting.<BR> 6. Review, Pañc. 218, 6 (f.).<BR> 7. Thought, Mālav. 38, 15 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 8. Worship, Pañc. 264, 4; honour, Rājat. 5, 328.<BR> 9. Love, Śāk. d. 163 (f.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पत्वसंभावना
सर्पत्व- + संभावना सर्पत्व- + संभावना, f. imagination [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b " target="_blank">Page1020-b + 42</a>] of being a snake, mistaking for a snake, Vedāntas. in Chr. 206, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाष
संभाष संभाष, i. e. सम्-भाष् + अ,<BR> I. m. Conversation, Man. 2, 195; in स्नेह-, Kind conversation, Pañc. 51, 23.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Greeting, Hit. i. d. 38, M.M.<BR> 2. A criminal connexion, Man. 8, 363.<BR> 3. Contract, agreement.<BR> 4. War-cry, watch-word.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरसंभाष
मधुर-संभाष मधुर-संभाष, adj. discoursing agreeably, Chr. 53, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाषण|सम्भाषण|संभाषणं|सम्भाषणं
संभाषण संभाषण, i. e. सम्-भाष् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Conversation, Lass. 41, 17.<BR> 2. Sexual intercourse, Lass. 10, 20.<BR> 3. War-cry, watchword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभूति|सम्भूति|संभूतिः
संभूति संभूति, i. e. सम्-भू + ति, f.<BR> 1. Combination.<BR> 2. Birth, Man. 2, 147.<BR> 3. Origin, Rājat. 5, 73; production.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भसंभूति
गर्भ- + संभूति गर्भ- + संभूति, f. pregnancy, Kathās. 5, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभृति|सम्भृति|संभृतिः|सम्भृतिः
संभृति संभृति, i. e. सम्-भृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Support, nourishment.<BR> 2. Preparation, provision.<BR> 3. Plenitude, fullness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभेद|सम्भेद|संभेदः|सम्भेदः
संभेद संभेद, i. e. सम्-भिद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Breaking, splitting.<BR> 2. Union, mixture, Mālat. 167, 4.<BR> 3. The confluence of two rivers, Man. 8, 356, or the junction of a river with the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोग|सम्भोग|संभोगः|सम्भोगः
संभोग संभोग, i. e. सम्-भुज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Enjoyment, Pañc. ii. d. 67; sensual enjoyment, Rājat. 5, 230.<BR> 2. Coition, Megh. 94; copulation.<BR> 3. A catamite.<BR> 4. Use, occupation, Man. 8, 200.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभोग|असम्भोग
अ- + संभोग अ- + संभोग, m. non-enjoyment, Hit. i. d. 156, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोजन|सम्भोजन|संभोजनं
संभोजन संभोजन, i. e. सम्-भुज् + अन,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Convivial, Man. 8, 141.<BR> II. n. A meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभ्रम|सम्भ्रम|संभ्रमः|सम्भ्रमः
संभ्रम संभ्रम, i. e. सम्-भ्रम् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Turning round, revolving.<BR> 2. Haste, MBh. 1, 764.<BR> 3. Confusion [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a " target="_blank">Page1021-a + 43</a>] arising from fear, joy, haste, etc.; cheerful quickness, Bhartṛ. 2, 54; zeal, Rājat. 5, 306.<BR> 4. Fear, alarm, Man. 4, 118; Pañc. 52, 16.<BR> 5. Error, ignorance.<BR> 6. Reverence, Hit. iv. d. 103 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3337).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रम|असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रमः
अ- + संभ्रम अ- + संभ्रम and निस्-, adj. unembarrassed, Rājat. 5, 82; 4, 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससम्भ्रमम्|ससंभ्रमम्
स-सम्भ्रम + म् स-सम्भ्रम + म्, adv. 1. hastily, Śāk. 6, 15; Pañc. 198, 9. 2. in confusion, Śāk. 40, 18; perplexed, Pañc. 140, 24. 3. in fear, Vikr. 25, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंभ्रम
सु- + संभ्रम सु- + संभ्रम, m. great haste, Hit. pr. d. 15, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभ्रमभृत्
संभ्रमभृत् संभ्रम-भृ + त्, adj. Embarrassed, Śiś. 9, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमति|सम्मति|संमतिः|सम्मतिः
संमति संमति, i. e. सम्-मन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Agreement.<BR> 2. Approbation, Pañc. 229, 1.<BR> 3. Regard, respect, Kir. 10, 36.<BR> 4. Real knowledge.<BR> 5. Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमद|सम्मद|संमदः|सम्मदः
संमद संमद, i. e. सम्-मद् + अ, m. Joy, Mālat. 77, 11; happiness, Govardh. Āryā Saptaśatī, 275, d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमर्द
संमर्द संमर्द, i. e. सम्-मृद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Friction, rubbing.<BR> 2. War, battle, Kathās. 3, 66.<BR> 3. Trampling on, treading on, Rājat. 5, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमाद|सम्माद|संमादः|सम्मादः
संमाद संमाद, i. e. सम्-मद् + अ, m. Intoxication, frenzy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमान|सम्मान|संमानः|सम्मानः
संमान संमान, i. e.<BR> I. सम्-मन् + अ, n. (Wils. and thus Hit. ii. d. 132, but Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2755 corrects ˚नः, m.; the n. is against the general rule), Respect, honour, Man. 2, 162.<BR> II. संमा + अन, n. Measure.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमान|असम्मान|असम्मानं|असंमानः
अ- + संमान अ- + संमान, m. no honour, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमार्जक|सम्मार्जक|संमार्जकः|सम्मार्ज्जकः
संमार्जक संमार्जक, i. e. सम्-मृज् + अक, m. A sweeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमार्जन|सम्मार्जन|संमार्जनं|सम्मार्ज्जनं
संमार्जन संमार्जन, i. e. सम्-मृज् + अन,<BR> I. n. Cleaning, purifying, sweeping, Pañc. 27, 5; 26, 22.<BR> II. f. नी, A broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्र|सम्मिश्र|सम्मिश्रः
संमिश्र संमिश्र, i. e. सम्-मिश्र, adj. Mixed, blended, joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्ल
संमिश्ल संमिश्ल (= the last, with ल् for र्), adj. Endowed, Chr. 290, 10 = Rigv. i. 64, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुखीन|सम्मुखीन|सम्मुखीनः
संमुखीन संमुखीन, i. e. सम्-मुख + ईन, adj. Before, in front of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमूर्छन|सम्मूर्छन|सम्मूर्च्छनं|संमूर्छनं
संमूर्छन संमूर्छन, i. e. सम्-मुर्छ् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Uniform, or universal expansion, or permeation.<BR> 2. Increasing.<BR> 3. Height.<BR> 4. Fainting, insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमेलन
संमेलन संमेलन, i. e. सम्-मिल् + अन, n. Union, Utt. Rāmac. 177, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमोद|सम्मोद|संमोदः|सम्मोदः
संमोद संमोद, i. e. सम्-मुद् + अ, m. Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमोह|सम्मोह|संमोहः
संमोह संमोह, i. e. सम्-मुह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Beguilement, fascination.<BR> 2. Stupefaction, Utt. Rāmac. 107, 8.<BR> 3. Folly.<BR> 4. Illusion of mind, Man. 7, 12.<BR> 5. Ignorance.<BR> 6. Fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यञ्च्|सम्यंच्
सम्यञ्च् सम्यञ्च्, i. e. सम-अञ्च् (the final अ of सम is changed to ई, as before अस्, कृ, भू),<BR> I. adj., f. मीची.<BR> 1. Going with, accompanying.<BR> 2. Same, common, uniform.<BR> 3. Accurate, correct.<BR> 4. Right, true.<BR> 5. Pleasant, agreeable.<BR> II. acc. sing. n. यक्, adv.<BR> 1. Properly, fitly, rightly, Man. 2, 14; well, Pañc. 134, 7; Vikr. 39, 7.<BR> 2. Duly, Man. 3, 76; Pañc. 128, 17.<BR> 3. By honourable means, Man. 7, 60.<BR> 4. Distinctly, Man. 2, 101; Pañc. 167, 6.<BR> 5. Wholly, completely, Pañc. 72, 17.<BR> 6. Comprehensively, Man. 2, 89.<BR> 7. With, Nal. 9, 8.<BR> 8. Together, Lass. 98, 14 = Rigv. v. 9, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्
सम्राज् सम्-राज्, m. A paramount sovereign, one who rules over other princes, and has performed the Rājasūya sacrifice; a sovereign, Rājat. 5, 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सय्
† सय् सय्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर सर, i. e. सृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Who or what goes.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. An arrow (? see शर).<BR> 3. The coagulum of curds or milk.<BR> 4. Salt, saltness.<BR> III. m., and f. रा or री, A waterfall.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. A pond, a lake, Pañc. 131, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. serum; ὀρρός, ὀρός; Lat. sal; Goth. salt; A.S. sealt; ἅλς; Lat. salum, insula; ἔναλος; A.S. siringie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिसर|मणिसरः
मणि- + सर मणि- + सर, m. a necklace, Utt. Rāmac. 18, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकसर|मौक्तिकसरः
मौक्तिक- + सर मौक्तिक- + सर, m. a string of pearls, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरक|सरकं|सरकः
सरक सरक, i. e. सृ + अक,<BR> I. adj. Going, moving.<BR> II. m. and n.<BR> 1. A continuous line of road.<BR> 2. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 3. Drinking spirits.<BR> 4. A drinking vessel.<BR> 5. Distribution of spirits.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. A lake.<BR> 3. Heaven.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसरक
त्रि- + सरक त्रि- + सरक, n. a mixture of three spirituous liquors, Śiś. 10, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरघा
सरघा सरघा, f. A bee, Ragh. 4, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरज|सरजं
सरज सर-ज, n. Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट्
सरट् सरट्, m.<BR> 1. Air, wind.<BR> 2. A cloud.<BR> 3. A lizard.<BR> 4. (ved.), A bee, Chr. 297, 21 = Rigv. i. 112, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट|सरटः
सरट सरट, and शरट शरट, m. The gecko, Lacerta gecko, Man. 12, 57 (with स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटि|सरटिः
सरटि सरटि, m.<BR> 1. Wind.<BR> 2. A cloud (cf. सरट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण सरण, i. e. सृ + अन,<BR> I. adj. Who or what goes.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Going.<BR> 2. Oxidised iron.<BR> III. f. णा and णि, A plant, Pæderia fetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणि|सरणिः
सरणि and णी सरणी̆, i. e. सृ + अन + ई, f.<BR> 1. A path, a road.<BR> 2. A straight or continuous line.<BR> 3. A disease of the throat. Cf. the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्ड|सरंड|सरंडः|सरण्डः
सरण्ड सरण्ड, m.<BR> 1. A bird.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> 3. A sort of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यु|सरण्युः
सरण्यु सरण्यु (vb. सृ + अण + य + उ), m.<BR> 1. Air, wind.<BR> 2. Water.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR> --Cf. Ἐριννύς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा सरमा, f.<BR> 1. The bitch of the gods, MBh. 1, 671.<BR> 2. The daughter of Dakṣa, Viṣṇu P. 122, n. 19.<BR> 3. The wife of Rāvaṇa's brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयु|सरयुः
सरयु सरयु (vb. सृ),<BR> I. m. Air, wind.<BR> II. f., also यू यू, The name of a river, Rām. 2, 49, 15 (यू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल सरल (vb. सृ),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Straight, Pañc. ii. d. 189.<BR> 2. Upright, honest, Mālat. 38, 1.<BR> II. m. A sort of pine, Pinus longifolia Roxb., Megh. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस् सरस्, i. e. सृ + अस् (cf. सर),<BR> I. n., and f. सी.<BR> 1. A large pond, Pañc. 159, 14 (रस्); Kir. 12, 51 (रसी).<BR> 2. A piece of water in which the lotus grows.<BR> II. n. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.N. sir, saer, sior (sea); A.S. sirendae.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरविन्दुसरस्
कर्पूर-, तृण-विन्दु- + सरस् कर्पूर-, तृण-विन्दु- + सरस्, n. names of lakes, Hit. 84, 13, M.M. (कर्पूर-); MBh. 3, 15365 (तृणविन्दु-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणविन्दुसरस्
कर्पूर-, तृण-विन्दु- + सरस् कर्पूर-, तृण-विन्दु- + सरस्, n. names of lakes, Hit. 84, 13, M.M. (कर्पूर-); MBh. 3, 15365 (तृणविन्दु-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसरस्
नभस्- + सरस् नभस्- + सरस्, n. clouds, sky, Rām. 5, 55, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमसरस्
हिम- + सरस् हिम- + सरस्, n. cold water, Mālat. 17, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस सरस, i. e. सरस् + अ, and स-रस,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. A pond.<BR> 2. (or m. ?), Alchemy, Rājat. 4, 247.<BR> 3. A substitute for सरस् at the end of some comp. words.<BR> II. adj.<BR> 1. Tasty, juicy, Megh. 14.<BR> 2. Beautiful, charming, Mālat. 51, 5; Bhartṛ. 1, 6; agreeable, Ṛt. 1, 2.<BR> 3. New, Śiś. 9, 85.<BR> 4. Impassioned.<BR> 5. ˚सम्, adv. Enraptured, Vikr. 57, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिज|सरसिजं
सरसिज सरस् + इ-ज, n. A lotus, Kir. 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीरुह|सरसीरुहं|सरसीरुहः
सरसीरुह सरसी-रुह् + अ (see सरस्), n. A lotus, Mālat. 169, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वन्त्|सरस्वत्
सरस्वन्त् सरस् + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Juicy, sapid.<BR> 2. Elegant.<BR> 3. Sentimental.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The ocean.<BR> 2. A male river.<BR> 3. A buffalo.<BR> III. f. वती.<BR> 1. The wife of Brahman, the goddess of speech and eloquence, Rājat. 5, 415; of wisdom, Vikr. d. 162.<BR> 2. The wife of a Muni.<BR> 3. An excellent woman.<BR> 4. Speech, Hit. 116, 8; Ragh. 15, 46, ed. Calc.; Rām. 1, 2, 34 (? modulation); the faculty or its exercise.<BR> 5. A river.<BR> 6. The name of a river, Chr. 20, 24.<BR> 7. A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरागता
सरागता स-राग + ता, f. State of being coloured or red, Pañc. i. d. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरि|सरिः
सरि सरि, i. e. सृ + इ, f. A waterfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित् सरित्, i. e. सृ + इत् (for सरन्त्, ptcple. pres.), f.<BR> 1. A river, Man. 1, 24; Vikr. 68, 5 (परमार्थ-, Indeed a river).<BR> 2. Thread.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसरित्
कु- + सरित् कु- + सरित्, f. a rivulet, Pañc. ii. d. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युसरित्
द्यु- + सरित् द्यु- + सरित्, f. the celestial Gaṅgā, Bhartṛ. 3, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिमन्
सरिमन् and सरीमन् सरी̆मन् (vb. सृ), m. Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीसृप|सरीसृपः
सरीसृप सरीसृप, i. e. सरीसृप् (frequent. of सृप्), + अ, m. A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोगिता
सरोगिता सरोगिता, i. e. स-रोग + इन् + ता, f. Sickliness, Hit. ii. d. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोज|सरोजं|सरोजः
सरोज सरोज, i. e. सरस्-ज, n. A lotus, Śiś. 9, 30; 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजिन्
सरोजिन् सरोजिन्, i. e. सरोज + इन्,<BR> I. m. Brahman.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A lotus, Bhartṛ. 1, 100.<BR> 2. A multitude of lotuses.<BR> 3. A pond abounding in lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुह्
सरोरुह् सरोरुह्, and सरोरुह सरोरुह, n., and -रुहिणि -रुहिणी, f., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b " target="_blank">Page1023-b + 42</a>] i. e. सरस्-रुह्, and -रुह् + अ, and + इन् + ई, A lotus, Lass. 73, 15 (ह); Utt. Rāmac. 24, 1 (ह); Kir. 4, 34 (हिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ग|सर्गः
सर्ग सर्ग, i. e. सृज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Abandoning, letting go.<BR> 2. Creation, Man. 1, 27.<BR> 3. Natural property, nature, Bhag. 5, 19.<BR> 4. Certainty,<BR> 5. Tendency of a thing.<BR> 6. Assent, agreement.<BR> 7. Effort, will, Ragh. 3, 51.<BR> 8. A chapter, Rām. i. sarga 1, sqq.; a book, Śiś. 1, sqq.<BR> 9. Voiding, as of excrement.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिसर्ग|आदिसर्गः
आदि- + सर्ग आदि- + सर्ग, m. first creation, MBh. 14, 1095.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसर्ग|त्रिसर्गः
त्रि- + सर्ग त्रि- + सर्ग, m. the threefold production (of qualities), Bhāg. P. 1, 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्|सर्ज्ज्
† सर्ज् सर्ज्, i. 1, Par. To gain (cf. अर्ज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज|सर्जः|सर्ज्ज|सर्ज्जः
सर्ज सर्ज, m.<BR> 1. A tree, Shorea robusta, Mālat. 148, 14.<BR> 2. Another tree, Pentaptera arjuna.<BR> 3. The resinous exudation of the Shorea robusts, MBh. 1, 5723.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जन|सर्जनं|सर्ज्जन|सर्ज्जनं
सर्जन सर्जन, i. e. सृज् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Abandoning.<BR> 2. Creating.<BR> 3. Voiding.<BR> 4. The rear or reserve of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जू|सर्ज्जू
सर्जू सर्जू, i. e. सृज् + ऊ,<BR> I. m. A merchant.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. Lightning.<BR> 2. A necklace.<BR> 3. Going, following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प|सर्पः
सर्प सर्प, i. e. सृप् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Sliding motion.<BR> 2. A snake, Man. 1, 37; Pañc. iii. d. 46.<BR> II. f. पी, The female of the snake.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. serpens; ἑρπετός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसर्प|कालसर्पः
काल- + सर्प काल- + सर्प, and कृष्ण-, m. a particular snake, Coluber Naga, Lass. 16, 11; Pañc. i. d. 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पण|सर्पणं|सर्प्पण
सर्पण सर्पण, i. e. सृप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Gliding, going.<BR> 2. The slow flight of an arrow nearly parallel to the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पभुज्
सर्पभुज् सर्प-भुज्, m.<BR> 1. A peacock.<BR> 2. A crane.<BR> 3. A large snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिन्
सर्पिन् सर्पिन्, i. e. सृप् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a " target="_blank">Page1024-a + 38</a>] इणी.<BR> 1. Gliding, creeping.<BR> 2. Moving, Kir. 5, 35.<BR> II. f. इणी.<BR> 1. A female serpent, Pañc. 210, 12.<BR> 2. A small medicinal shrub.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठसर्पिन्
पीठ- + सर्पिन् पीठ- + सर्पिन्, m. a cripple, Man. 8, 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिष्मन्त्|सर्पिष्मत्
सर्पिष्मन्त् सर्पिष्मन्त्, i. e. सर्पिस् + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Seasoned with clarified butter, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्
सर्पिस् सर्पिस्, i. e. सृप् + इस्, n. Clarified butter, Pañc. iii. d. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्|सर्ब्ब्
† सर्ब् सर्ब्, सम्ब् सम्ब्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्म|सर्मः|सर्म्म
सर्म सर्म, i. e. सृ + म, m. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्|सर्व्व्
सर्व् सर्व्, see शर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व|सर्वः|सर्व्व|सर्व्वः
सर्व सर्व, probably स + त्र + व,<BR> I. adj., f. वा.<BR> 1. All, Nal. 17, 50.<BR> 2. Every, Megh. 20; 91.<BR> 3. Whole, entire, Pañc. 53, 24.<BR> II. m. Viṣṇu, Śiva.<BR> --Cf. ὅλος; Lat. soll-ennis, soll-ers, salvus, salus (= ved. सर्व + ताति, ὁλότης).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंसह|सर्व्वंसह
सर्वंसह सर्वंसह, i. e. सर्व + म्-सह् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. All-sustaining.<BR> 2. Patient, enduring.<BR> II. f. हा, The earth, Govardh. Āryā Saptaśatī, 163, d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वक|सर्व्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्वक सर्व + क, adj. All, every.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वकर्मीण|सर्व्वकर्म्मीण|सर्व्वकर्म्मीणः
सर्वकर्मीण सर्वकर्मीण, i. e. सर्व-कर्मन् + ईन, adj. Performing, or conversant with, every business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वग|सर्वगः|सर्व्वग|सर्व्वगं|सर्व्वगः
सर्वग सर्व-ग,<BR> I. adj. All-pervading.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Brahman.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. Soul, spirit.<BR> III. n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वगतत्व
सर्वगतत्व सर्व-गत + त्व (vb. गम्), n. Omnipresence, Bhāṣāp. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वगुह्यमय
सर्वगुह्यमय सर्व-गुह्य + मय (vb. गुह्), adj. Made up of all mystery, Johns. Sel. 23, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंकष
सर्वंकष सर्वंकष, i. e. सर्व + म् -कष् + अ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b " target="_blank">Page1024-b + 41</a>]<BR> I. adj. All-pervading, allsubduing, Mālat. 14, 19.<BR> II. m. A rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वजित्|सर्व्वजित्
सर्वजित् सर्व-जि + त्, adj.<BR> 1. Allsubduing, irresistible.<BR> 2. All-surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वज्ञ|सर्व्वज्ञ|सर्व्वज्ञः
सर्वज्ञ सर्व-ज्ञ,<BR> I. adj. Omniscient, Hit. 129, 9; Bhartṛ. 2, 8.<BR> II. m. Śiva.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असर्वज्ञ
अ- + सर्वज्ञ अ- + सर्वज्ञ, adj. not omniscient, Rājat. 5, 317.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वज्ञानमय
सर्वज्ञानमय सर्व-ज्ञान + मय, adj., f. य्त्, Containing every knowledge, Man. 2, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतस्|सर्व्वतस्
सर्वतस् सर्व + तस्, adv., and prep. with the acc., Siddh. K. 36, a.<BR> 1. From every quarter, Man. 2, 240; from every part, Pañc. iii. d. 51; from everybody, i. d. 156 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1031).<BR> 2. In every direction, Nal. 1, 25.<BR> 3. Round about, Chr. 4, 19.<BR> 4. Wholly, entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतेजोमय|सर्व्वतेजोमय
सर्वतेजोमय सर्वतेजोमय, i. e. सर्व-तेजस् + मय, adj., f. यी, Containing every splendour, Man. 7, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोदिक्क
सर्वतोदिक्क सर्वतोदिक्क, i. e. सर्वतस्-दिश् + क, adj. Diffused over all quarters, Rājat. 5, 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोदिशम्
सर्वतोदिशम् सर्वतोदिशम्, i. e. सर्वतस्-दिश् + अ + म्, adv. To every quarter (of the world), Nal. 16, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्र|सर्व्वत्र
सर्वत्र सर्व + त्र,<BR> I. = loc. of सर्व, Cāṇ. 48 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410.<BR> II. adv.<BR> 1. In all places, everywhere, Pañc. ii. d. 125.<BR> 2. At all times, always, Vikr. 30, 14; 39, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वथा|सर्व्वथा
सर्वथा सर्व + था, adv.<BR> 1. In all ways, by all means, Pañc. 161, 13; with न, Not at all, Mālat. 154, 13.<BR> 2. At every time, Man. 2, 15.<BR> 3. Certainly, Vikr. 32, 8.<BR> 4. Exceeding, mostly, completely, Hit. 81, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदा|सर्व्वदा
सर्वदा सर्व + दा, adv. At all times, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a " target="_blank">Page1025-a + 39</a>] always, Rām. 6, 10, 23; Pañc. ii. d. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदेवमय|सर्वदेवमयः|सर्व्वदेवमय
सर्वदेवमय सर्व-देव + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of, or comprising all, the gods, Pañc. i. d. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वधुरावह|सर्व्वधुरावह|सर्व्वधुरावहः
सर्वधुरावह सर्व-धुरा-वह् + अ, and सर्वधुरीण सर्व-धुरीण, m. An ox fit for any carriage or draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंदम
सर्वंदम सर्वंदम, i. e. सर्व + म्-दम् + अ, m. A name of Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभूतकृत्|सर्व्वभूतकृत्
सर्वभूतकृत् सर्व-भूत-कृ + त्, adj. Who or what causes all that exists, Man. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभूतमय|सर्व्वभूतमय
सर्वभूतमय सर्व-भूत + मय, adj.<BR> I. Comprising all beings, Man. 1, 7.<BR> II. m. The supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वभूतात्मन्|सर्व्वभूतात्मन्
सर्वभूतात्मन् सर्वभूतात्मन्, i. e. सर्व-भूत-आत्मन्, m. The universal all-pervading Spirit, Man. 1, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वमय|सर्व्वमय|सर्व्वमयः
सर्वमय सर्व + मय, adj., f. यी, General, universal, comprehensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वमेध्यत्व
सर्वमेध्यत्व सर्व-मेध्य + त्व, n. Perfect purity, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3296 = Pañc. iii. d. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वर्तुक
सर्वर्तुक सर्वर्तुक, i. e. सर्व-ऋतु + क, adj. Fit for, or inhabitable in, every season, Man. 7, 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वशस्|सर्व्वशस्
सर्वशस् सर्व + शस्, adv.<BR> 1. Universally, everywhere, Johns. Sel. 29, 34.<BR> 2. All together, Chr. 37, 1; Nal. 2, 22; 12, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसिद्धार्थ|सर्व्वसिद्धार्थ
सर्वसिद्धार्थ सर्वसिद्धार्थ, i. e. सर्व-सिद्ध (vb. सिध्), -अर्थ, adj. Having every wish attained, Man. 1, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वाङ्गीण|सर्वांगीण|सर्व्वाङ्गीण|सर्व्वाङ्गीणः
सर्वाङ्गीण सर्वाङ्गीण, i. e. सर्व-अङ्ग + ईन, adj.<BR> 1. Spreading through the whole body, spread over all the limbs, Vikr. d. 51; thrilling through [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b " target="_blank">Page1025-b + 42</a>] the whole body, d. 149.<BR> 2. Relating to the Aṅgas or parts of science collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वान्नीन|सर्व्वान्नीन|सर्व्वान्नीनः
सर्वान्नीन सर्वान्नीन, i. e. सर्व-अन्न + ईन, adj. Eating all sorts of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षप|सर्षपः
सर्षप सर्षप,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. sort of mustard, Sinapis dichotoma, Windischmann, Sankara, 165.<BR> 2. A small measure of weight, a mustard seed so considered.<BR> 3. A sort of poison.<BR> II. f. पी, A small bird.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरसर्षप|गौरसर्षपः
गौर- + सर्षप गौर- + सर्षप, m. 1. white mustard, Sinapis glauca, Man. 5, 120; Suśr. 1, 16, 10. 2. a measure of weight, Man. 8, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्षप|राजसर्षपः
राजसर्षप राजसर्षप, i. e. राजन्-, m. 1. mustard. 2. a measure of weight, Man. 8, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्
† सल् सल्, i. 1, Par. To go (cf. सृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिल|सलिलं
सलिल सलिल (vb. सृ, cf. सर), n. Water, Pañc. 165, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसलिल
अन्तःसलिल अन्तःसलिल, i. e. अन्तर्-, adj., f. ला, containing water, Ragh. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधसलिल
अ-गाध- + सलिल अ-गाध- + सलिल, adj. having bottomless water, Pañc. ii. d. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनसलिल
नयन- + सलिल नयन- + सलिल, n. tears, Megh. 40; 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसलिल
निःसलिल निःसलिल, i. e. निस्-, adj. deprived of water. Rājat. 1, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलपूरवत्
सलिलपूरवत् सलिल-पूर + वत्, adv. Like a large quantity of water, Pañc. ii. d. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलस्थलचर
सलिलस्थलचर सलिल-स्थल-चर, adj. sbst. Living in water and on the land, Pañc. 131, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलेशय
सलिलेशय सलिलेशय, i. e. सलिल + इ + शी + अ, adj. Lying in water, Lass. 50, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलोकता
सलोकता स-लोक + ता, f. Condition of dwelling in the same world as, Man. 11, 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव|सवं|सवः
सव सव, i. e. सु, and सू, + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Sacrifice.<BR> 2. Offspring.<BR> 3. The sun.<BR> 4. The moon.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Sprinkling [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a " target="_blank">Page1026-a + 40</a>] the Soma, or juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR> 2. The juice of flowers.<BR> 3. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसव|गोसवः
गो- + सव गो- + सव, m. a kind of sacrifice, Man. 11, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवन|सवनं
सवन सवन, i. e. सु, and सू, + अन,<BR> I. m. The moon.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Extracting and drinking the Soma, or juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR> 2. A sacrifice, Rām. 1, 13, 5.<BR> 3. Bearing children, bringing forth young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ सवितृ, i. e. सू + तृ,<BR> I. m. The sun, Vikr. d. 20.<BR> II. f. त्री, A mother.<BR> III. adj. Causing, Kir. 3, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृद्धिक
सवृद्धिक स-वृद्धि + क, adj. Bearing interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य सव्य, adj.<BR> 1. Left, left hand, Pañc. i. d. 86.<BR> 2. Southern, south.<BR> 3. Backward, reverse, contrary.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. σκαιός; Lat. scævus, probably also sinister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अप- + सव्य अप- + सव्य,<BR> I. adj. right (not left), Man. 3, 214; अपसव्यं कृ, to keep the right side towards one, ib.<BR> II. अपसव्यम्, adv. from the left to the right, Man. 3, 279.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यतस्
सव्यतस् सव्य + तस्, adv. On one's left hand, Chr. 31, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यसाचिन्
सव्यसाचिन् सव्यसाचिन्, perhaps सव्य-स-अञ्च् + इन् (cf. साचि), m. (Drawing the bow with his left hand), a name of Arjuna, Pañc. iii. d. 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठृ
सव्येष्ठृ सव्येष्ठृ, i. e. सव्य + इ-स्थार् (स्थार् for स्थान्, with र् for न्, and स्थान् for स्थान्त्, old ptcple. pres. of स्था), m. A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्च्
सश्च् सश्च्, see सच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्
सस् सस्, † शस् शस्, † संस्त् संस्त्, † शंस्त् शंस्त्, ii. 2, Par. To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्य|सस्यं
सस्य सस्य, n.<BR> 1. Fruit, Nal. 24, 52 (at the end of a comp. adj., f. या).<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-b " target="_blank">Page1026-b + 44</a>] Corn, grain, Man. 4, 26 (cf. शस्य, under शंस्).<BR> 3. A weapon (cf. शस्).<BR> 4. A quality, an excellence (cf. शंस्).<BR> --Cf. perhaps εἴα, ἤϊον.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
सस्यक सस्य + क,<BR> I. adj. Possessed of all good qualities.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A sort of precious stone.<BR> 2. A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
1. सह् सह् (probably a combination of two originally different verbs, viz. सह्, ‘to conquer,’ cf. सहस्, and स-वह्, ‘to bear,’ cf. infin. सोढुम् = स-वोढुम्, ptcple. of the pf. pass. सोढ = स-ऊढ), i. 1, Ātm. (also Par.), and † i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To bear, Vikr. d. 135; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 997 (Par.); to undergo, Man. 2, 227.<BR> 2. To endure, Bhartṛ. 2, 30.<BR> 3. To allow, Pañc. 135, 7 (Par.).<BR> 4. To forbear (with gen.), Bhag. 11, 44.<BR> 5. To be patient, to wait, Ragh. 5, 25.<BR> 6. To be able to resist, to oppose, to conquer, Rām. 1, 22, 21.<BR> 7. To stop, Rām. 2, 24, 27.<BR> 8. To be able (with infin.), Hit. ii. d. 139.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --ptcple. of the pres. अ-सहमान, adj. Not able to endure, Pañc. 221, 1.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सोढ.<BR> 1. Borne, endured.<BR> 2. Patient, enduring. सहित, see s. v.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. सह्य.<BR> 1. Equal or adequate to, Pañc. ii. d. 200 (but cf. my transl. n. 907).<BR> 2. Sweet, agreeable; see also s. v.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-सह्य, adj. 1. insupportable, Ṛt. 1, 10. 2. unconquerable, Ragh. 18, 24.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, absol. अभिषह्य, Forcibly, Man. 8, 367.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To make an effort or exertion, Bhaṭṭ. 19, 16.<BR> 2. To dare, Pañc. 22, 1; with acc., To dare to pursue, Nal. 4, 16.<BR> 3. To be able (with infin. and dat. of an abstract noun), Rām. 3, 51, 17; MBh. 3, 16543 (परिभोगाय, To enjoy).<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To be able, to wish, Ragh. 5, 22.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a " target="_blank">Page1027-a + 42</a>] Caus. To incite, to instigate, Rām. 2, 9, 46.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, Caus. To incite, MBh. 2, 1412.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To make an effort, Pañc. iii. d. 51.<BR> 2. To endure, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 5; absolut. प्रसह्य, Violently, Man. 8, 235.<BR> 3. To overpower, Rām. 2, 5, 7.<BR> 4. To be able (with infin.), MBh. 1, 4842.<BR> --With अभिप्र अभि-प्र, To be able, Kir. 12, 18.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To sustain, Rām. 1, 37, 8.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To sustain, Ragh. 4, 49.<BR> 2. To suffer, Rām. 2, 61, 4.<BR> 3. To endure, Rām. 2, 12, 106.<BR> 4. To be able to resist, MBh. 5, 2021.<BR> 5. To determine.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. विषह्य, Possible, Arj. 5, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. not being able to be determined or ascertained, Man. 8, 265.<BR> दुर्विषह्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj., f. या, difficult to be sustained.<BR> --Cf. ἔχω, ἕξω, ἔσχον, ἐχυρός, σχέσις, ἰσχάνω, ὑπισχνέομαι, σχολή; see सहस् and सह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
† 2. सह् सह्, i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To bear.<BR> 2. To satisfy.<BR> 3. To delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
1. सह सह् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bearing, Bhartṛ. 2, 68.<BR> 2. Suffering.<BR> 3. Enduring, Pañc. iii. d. 178 (शीत-वात-आतप-, Enduring coldness, wind, and heat).<BR> 4. Patient.<BR> 5. Able, Vikr. 78, 10; Śiś. 9, 51.<BR> II. m. and n. Strength, power.<BR> III. m. The month Mārgaśīrṣa (November--December).<BR> IV. f. हा.<BR> 1. The earth.<BR> 2. The name of several plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह
अ- + सह अ- + सह, adj. 1. not able to support, Kathās. 9, 37. 2. impatient, 6, 114. 3. unable, Hit. ii. d. 120 (भरस्य, to bear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालसह
अ-काल- + सह अ-काल- + सह, adj. unable to be maintained a long time, Hit. iii. d. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निःसह निःसह, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. unable to bear, Kathās. 17, 9. 2. powerless, Gīt. 2, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासह|महासहः
महा- + सह महा- + सह,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b " target="_blank">Page1027-b + 41</a>] much-enduring.<BR> II. f. हा, the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुसह
शत्रु- + सह शत्रु- + सह, adj. enduring an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसह|सर्वसहः|सर्व्वसह|सर्व्वसहः
सर्व- + सह सर्व- + सह, adj. enduring everything, very patient, Hit. i. d. 63, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकार्यसह
स्व-कार्य- + सह स्व-कार्य- + सह, adj. able to do one's duty, Vikr. d. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
2. सह सह, i. e. स + धा (with ह् for ध् as often, and the final shortened, cf. त्र for त्रा, सध, ved.),<BR> 1. adv. as former part of comp. words, With, united, common, like, complete (e. g. सहकारिन्).<BR> 2. prep. With (with instr., Rām. 3, 55, 41; epic also with dat., Chr. 13, 15; with abl., Cāṇ. 105 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 413).<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. sŏdā + lis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहक
सहक सह् + अक, adj. Enduring, Nalod. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकार|सहकारः
सहकार i. e.<BR> I. स-ह-कार, adj. Endowed with the letter ह, i. e. the vocative particle, i. e. calling, Nalod. 2, 14.<BR> II. 2. सह-कार, m. A fragrant sort of mango, Vikr. d. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिता
सहकारिता सहकारिता, i. e. सहकारिन् + ता, f. Co-operation, assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिन्
सहकारिन् सह-कारिन्, adj., f. इणी, Co-operating, assisting, Bhāṣāp. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्
सहकृत् सह-कृ + त्, and सहकृत्वन् सह-कृ + त्वन्, adj. sbst. Assisting, an assister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचर|सहचरः
सहचर सह-चर् + अ,<BR> I. m. A companion, Pañc. 243, 3; a friend, 43, 4.<BR> II. f. री, A companion, a wife, Vikr. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचार|सहचारः
सहचार सहचार, i. e. सह-चर् + अ, m. The accompaniment of the middle term by the major, Bhāṣāp. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचारिन्
सहचारिन् सह-चारिन्, m. A companion, a friend, Pañc. 43, 1 (परस्परम् अतीव, Very dear to each other).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहज|सहजः
सहज सह-ज,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Born or produced with, together, Johns. Sel. 16, 66.<BR> 2. Innate, Indr. 4, 7.<BR> 3. Natural, Hit. 87, 12; Pañc. 110, 15.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A brother of whole blood.<BR> 2. The natural state or disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजन्या
सहजन्या सह-जन्या (see जन्य), f. The name of an Apsaras, Vikr. 51, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदेव|सहदेवः
सहदेव सह-देव,<BR> I. m. The youngest of the five Pāṇḍava princes.<BR> II. f. वा and वी, The name of several plants, Pañc. 157, 23 (वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्म|सहधर्मः|सहधर्म्म
सहधर्म सह-धर्म, m. Community of duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्मचारिन्
सहधर्मचारिन् सहधर्म-चारिन्,<BR> I. m. A husband, Śāk. 111, 12.<BR> II. f. इणी, A legitimate wife, ib. 5; Utt. Rāmac. 85, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्मिन्|सहधर्म्मिन्
सहधर्मिन् सहधर्मिन्, i. e. सहधर्म + इन्,<BR> I. adj.; f. इणी.<BR> 1. Following the same law.<BR> 2. Having same or like properties.<BR> II. f. इणी, A woman married according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन सह् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Enduring.<BR> II. n. Bearing, enduring.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहन|असहनः
अ- + सहन अ- + सहन, adj., f. ना, 1. unable to bear or endure, Kathās. 15, 87. 2. jealous, Vikr. d. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपांसुकिल
सहपांसुकिल सह-पांसु-किल (किल, Play, Hemac.), and सहपासुक्रीडन सह-पांसु-क्रीडन, adj. sbst. m. (properly, One who has played with another in the sand, i. e. in his childhood), a friend from childhood, Mālat. 151, 17 (-क्रीडन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस् सह् + अस्,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The month Mārgaśīrṣa (Nov.--Dec.).<BR> 2. The winter season.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. ved. Victory, strength, Lass. 101, 10 = Rigv. vii. 16, 4; power.<BR> 2. instr. सा, adv.<BR> a. Without consideration, precipitately, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b " target="_blank">Page1028-b + 41</a>] Hit. iv. d. 97; quickly, Rām. 3, 54, 9.<BR> b. On a sudden, Pañc. 222, 23; Śāk. d. 9; at once, Pañc. 182, 14; with (?), Johns. Sel. 46, 1 (perhaps corr. सह चाप्स्˚).<BR> 3. Light.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sigis; A.S. sigor, sige.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्य|सहस्यः
सहस्य सहस् + य, m. The month Pauṣa (Dec.--Jan.), Pāṇ. iv. 4, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्र|सहस्रं
सहस्र सहस्र, numeral, n. A thousand, Pañc. 130, 16.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परःसहस्र परःसहस्र, i. e. परस्-, adj., f. रा, more than a thousand, Utt. Rāmac. 11, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकृत्वस्
सहस्रकृत्वस् सहस्र-कृत्वस्, adv.<BR> 1. A thousand times, Man. 2, 79.<BR> 2. Repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रतय
सहस्रतय सहस्र + तय,<BR> I. adj. Thousandfold.<BR> II. n. A thousand, Śiś. 9, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधा
सहस्रधा सहस्र + धा, adv. In a thousand ways, thousandfold, Kir. 5, 17; in a thousand pieces, Pañc. 190, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रमीळ्ह
सहस्रमीळ्ह सहस्र-मीऌह (ved. for मीढ, vb. मिह्), adj. Yielding a thousand treasures, Chr. 296, 10 = Rigv. i. 112, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशस्
सहस्रशस् सहस्र + शस्, adv. By a thousand, or thousands, Pañc. i. d. 262; thousandfold.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्रशस्
शत- + सहस्रशस् शत- + सहस्रशस्, adv. by hundreds of thousands, by myriads, Johns. Sel. 11, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रिन्
सहस्रिन् सहस्रिन्, i. e. सहस्र + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Having a thousand, Pañc. v. d. 69.<BR> 2. Consisting of thousands, Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15.<BR> 3. (A fine) amounting to a thousand. Man. 8, 276.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A body of a thousand men.<BR> 2. Commander or prefect of a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्वन्त्|सहस्वत्
सहस्वन्त् सहस् + वन्त्, adj., f. वति. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a " target="_blank">Page1029-a + 42</a>] Powerful, Lass. 99, 2 = Rigv. v. 9, 7 (ved. voc. ˚वस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाय|सहायः
सहाय सहाय, probably सह-इ + अ, m.<BR> 1. A companion, Pañc. 221, 22.<BR> 2. An adherent.<BR> 3. A helper, Lass. 52, 1.<BR> 4. An ally, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 1.<BR> 5. The ruddy goose, Anas casarca.<BR> 6. A sort of drug and perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहाय
अ- + सहाय अ- + सहाय, adj. one who has no assistant, Man. 7, 30; no allies, Pañc. iii. d. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिणीसहाय
करिणी- + सहाय करिणी- + सहाय, adj. with his female elephant, Vikr. 64, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसहाय
दुस्- + सहाय दुस्- + सहाय, adj. abandoned, MBh. 5, 1861.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसहाय|धर्मसहायः
धर्म- + सहाय धर्म- + सहाय, m. a companion for fulfilling religious duties, Sāh. D. 37, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसहाय|मधुसहायः
मधु- + सहाय मधु- + सहाय, m. Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनसहाय|वचनसहायः
वचन- + सहाय वचन- + सहाय, m. a companion for conversation, Pañc. 221, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायक
ऽसहायक -सहाय + क, instead of सहाय, at the end of a comp. adj., in नारयण-, Accompanied by Nārāyaṇa, Johns. Sel. 90, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायता
सहायता सहाय + ता, f., and सहायत्व सहाय + त्व, n.<BR> 1. A multitude of companions.<BR> 2. Companionship, union, Pañc. 59, 10 (त्व).<BR> 3. Help, Pañc. 154, 17 (त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायवन्त्|सहायवत्
सहायवन्त् सहाय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Having a companion, Pañc. i. d. 97; Hit. iv. d. 18 (‘in the true sense of the word’).<BR> 2. Assisted, befriended.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहायवन्त्|असहायवत्
अ- + सहायवन्त् अ- + सहायवन्त्, adj. alone, Man. 6, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
सहित सहित, i. e. 2. सह + इत, adj.<BR> 1. Accompanied by; at the end of comp. words, With, Hit. 61, 4.<BR> 2. With (with instr.), Chr. 23, 32.<BR> 3. Associated, Chr. 62, 52. pl. All, Lass. 2. ed. 61, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसहित
कर्ण- + सहित कर्ण- + सहित, adj. with the ears, Pañc. 217, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु सह् + इष्णु, adj.<BR> 1. Able to support, Śāk. d. 37.<BR> 2. Patient, Kir. 2, 50; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b " target="_blank">Page1029-b + 42</a>] resigned.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णु
अ- + सहिष्णु अ- + सहिष्णु, adj. 1. unable to bear, Mālat. 144, 4. 2. unable, Hit. 126, 17. 3. envious, Hit. 85, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुता
सहिष्णुता सहिष्णु + ता, f.<BR> 1. Ability to support, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 17.<BR> 2. Patience, resignation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णुता
अ- + सहिष्णुता अ- + सहिष्णुता, f. envy, Bhartṛ. 2, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरि|सहुरिः
सहुरि सह् + उरि,<BR> I. m. The sun.<BR> II. f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढ|सहोढः
सहोढ सहोढ, i. e. सह-ऊढ (vb. वह्), m.<BR> 1. The son of a pregnant bride, Man. 9, 160.<BR> 2. A thief caught with stolen property upon him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर सहोर, i. e. probably सह + वन् + अ, with र् for न्, adj. Good, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य सह्य,<BR> A. See सह्.<BR> B. i. e. सह + य,<BR> I. adj. Powerful, strong.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Health, convalescence.<BR> 2. Assistance, Rām. 6, 3, 26.<BR> C. m. The name of a range of mountains, Kir. 18, 5.<BR> --Cf. perhaps σαο and σω in σαώτερος, σῶος, σωτήρ, σώζω, σῶκος; Lat. sanus, but questionable on account of A.S. sund; O.H.G. ga-sunt (perhaps = सह + वन्त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिक|सांयात्रिकः
सांयात्रिक सांयात्रिक, i. e. संयात्रा + इक, m. A merchant who trades by sea, Pañc. i. d. 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन सांयुगीन, i. e. संयुग + ईन,<BR> I. adj. Skilled in war, Vikr. 87, 2; warlike, Ragh. 11, 30.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A soldier skilled in war.<BR> 2. An able leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविण|सांराविणं
सांराविण सांराविण, i. e. सम्-रु + इन् + अ, n. Shout, Mālat. 77, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर सांवत्सर, i. e. संवत्सर + अ,<BR> I. adj. Annual, perennial.<BR> II. m. An almanac-maker, an astrologer, Kām. Nītis. 4, 33; Pañc. iii. d. 67.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसांवत्सर
अति- + सांवत्सर अति- + सांवत्सर, adj., f. री, going beyond a year, Man. 8, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिक|सांवत्सरिकः
सांवत्सरिक सांवत्सरिक, i. e. संवत्सर + इक,<BR> I. adj. Yearly, Man. 7, 80.<BR> II. m. An astrologer, Pañc. 156, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक सांवादिक, i. e. संवाद + इक, m. A logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवृत्तिक
सांवृत्तिक सांवृत्तिक, संवृत्ति + इक, Phenomenal, illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक सांशयिक, i. e. संशय + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Dubious, Pañc. iii. d. 11.<BR> 2. Irresolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक सांसारिक, i. e. संसार + इक, adj. Worldly, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक सांसिद्धिक, i. e. संसिद्धि + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to a thing's nature, innate, Bhāṣāp. 38.<BR> 2. Effected naturally, spontaneous, Sāṅkhya Aph. iii. 20.<BR> 3. Effected by supernatural means, as spells, etc. ib. v. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिक|सांस्थानिकः
सांस्थानिक सांस्थानिक, i. e. संस्थान + इक, m. An inhabitant or native of the same place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् साकम्, i. e. स-अञ्च् + अ + म् (cf. साचि),<BR> I. adv. At the same time, together, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4.<BR> II. prep. With (with instr.), Kāvya Prak. 103, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्य|साकल्यं
साकल्य साकल्य, i. e. स-कल (see कला), + य, n.<BR> 1. Totality, Nalod. 3, 19; instr. येन, Completely, Man. 12, 25.<BR> 2. The whole, all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेत|साकेतं
साकेत साकेत, n. A name of Ayodhya, Ragh. 13, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतक|साकेतकः
साकेतक साकेत + क, m. An inhabitant of Sāketa, Śāk. 90, 23 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुक|साक्तुकं|साक्तुकः
साक्तुक साक्तुक, i. e. सक्तु + क,<BR> I. m. Barley.<BR> II. n. A quantity of fried grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षतम्
साक्षतम् साक्षतम्, i. e. स-अ-क्षत [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b " target="_blank">Page1030-b + 40</a>] (vb. क्षण्), + म्, adv. Uninterruptedly, Lass. 66, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात् साक्षात्, abl. sing. of स-अक्ष, adv.<BR> 1. In presence, Nal. 24, 13 (in their presence, being present); before, eye to eye, Indr. 2, 16.<BR> 2. From (cf. सकाशात्, s. v. सकाश), Arj. 1, 12.<BR> 3. Manifestly, evidently, visibly, Man. 2, 237; Pañc. 46, 6; Nal. 1, 4 (सक्षाद्-इव मनुः, like an embodied Manu); with one's own eyes, Pañc. 197, 12.<BR> 4. Openly, Mālat. 6, 13.<BR> 5. As, like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्कार|साक्षात्कारः
साक्षात्कार साक्षात्-कार, m. Perception, Vedāntas. in Chr. 215, 24; Bhāṣāp. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिक
ऽसाक्षिक साक्षिक, i. e. साक्षिन् + क, a substitute for साक्षिन्, when latter part of comp. adj.; e. g. अ-, adj. Where there was no witness, Man. 8, 109. अग्नि-, adj. Having fire or Agni as witness, Rām. 4, 7, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिता
साक्षिता साक्षिता, i. e. साक्षिन् + ता, f. Testimony, evidence, Man. 8, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन् साक्षिन्, i. e. स-अक्ष + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी.<BR> 1. Witnessing, having witnessed, Hit. iv. d. 62.<BR> 2. Attesting.<BR> II. m. A witness, Pañc. iii. d. 93; with gen. and loc., Pāṇ. ii. 3, 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटसाक्षिन्
कूट- + साक्षिन् कूट- + साक्षिन् and दुस्-, m. a false witness, Yājñ. 2, 77 (कूट-); Rām. 3, 18, 34 (दुस्-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिमन्त्|साक्षिमत्
साक्षिमन्त् साक्षिमन्त्, i. e. साक्षिन् + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Having or requiring witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्य|साक्ष्यं
साक्ष्य साक्ष्य, i. e. साक्षिन् + य, n.<BR> 1. Evidence, Man. 8, 82.<BR> 2. Giving evidence, 8, 62; testimony, MBh. 5, 1225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखेय|साखेयः
साखेय साखेय, i. e. सखि + एय, adj. Friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागर|सागरः
सागर सागर (cf. सगर), m.<BR> 1. The ocean, Pañc. i. d. 240.<BR> 2. A kind of deer.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरसागर|क्षीरसागरः
क्षीर- + सागर क्षीर- + सागर, m. the sea of milk, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वसागर|पूर्वसागरः
पूर्व- + सागर पूर्व- + सागर, m. the eastern sea, Ragh. 4, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिसागर
बुद्धि- + सागर बुद्धि- + सागर, m. a proper name, or rather, plenty of wisdom, or having plenty of wisdom, Lass. 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरग
सागरग सागर-ग (vb. गम्), f. The Gaṅgā or Ganges, Chr. 47, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्र
साग्र साग्र, i. e. स-अग्र (अग्र, adj. Excessive, Gramm.), adj. With a surplus, more than, Rām. 5, 7, 28; 4, 8, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कर्य|सांकर्य|सांकर्यं|साङ्कर्य्य
साङ्कर्य साङ्कर्य, i. e. संकर + य, n.<BR> 1. Mixture.<BR> 2. The concurrence of various properties in one subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्काश्या|सांकाश्या
साङ्काश्या साङ्काश्या, i. e. संकाश + य, f. Name of a town, Rām. 1, 70, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्क्षेपिक|सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
साङ्क्षेपिक साङ्क्षेपिक, i. e. संक्षेप + इक, adj. Short, summary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
साङ्ख्य साङ्ख्य, i. e. संख्य + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Numeral, relating to number.<BR> 2. Deliberating, reasoning, Bhag. 3, 3.<BR> 3. Rational, discriminative.<BR> II. m. The Sāṅkhya system of philosophy, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 33; Bhag. 2, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग|सांग
साङ्ग साङ्ग, i. e. स-अङ्ग, adj.<BR> 1. With the members, divisions.<BR> 2. Complete, finished, Utt. Rāmac. 166, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गतिक|सांगतिक|सांगतिकः
साङ्गतिक साङ्गतिक, i. e. संगति + इक,<BR> I. adj. Associating.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A visitor.<BR> 2. One who comes on business, Man. 3, 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
साङ्ग्रामिक साङ्ग्रामिक, i. e. संग्राम + इक, adj., f. का, Relating to war, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 6; Pañc. i. d. 103; warlike, martial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि साचि, i. e. loc. sing. of स-अञ्च्, adv. Crookedly, awry, Kir. 10, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्य|साचिव्यं
साचिव्य साचिव्य, i. e. सचिव + य, n.<BR> 1. Friendship.<BR> 2. Ministership, Pañc. 13, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साजात्य|साजात्यं
साजात्य साजात्य, i. e. स-जाति + य, n. Community of genus, Bhāṣāp. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्
† साट् साट्, i. 10, Par. To make manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
साति साति, i. e. सन् + ति and सो + ति, f.<BR> 1. Gaining, acquisition, Chr. 297, 22 = Rigv. i. 112, 15.<BR> 2. Gift, giving.<BR> 3. End, conclusion.<BR> 4. Destruction.<BR> 5. Sharp pain.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसाति
वाज- + साति वाज- + साति, f. gain of food, Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. i. 112, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विक|सात्त्विकः
सात्त्विक सात्त्विक, i. e. सत्त्व + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Endowed with the quality सत्त्व, i. e. the best of qualities, Man. 3, 263.<BR> 2. Endowed with goodness, Man. 12, 40.<BR> 3. Relating, belonging to, or proceeding from, that quality, Bhag. 7, 12; Man. 12, 31.<BR> 4. Good, honest, true, Hit. i. d. 15, M.M.; sincere, Mālat. 16, 3.<BR> II. m. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकि|सात्यकिः
सात्यकि सात्यकि, m. The charioteer of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवत|सात्यवतः
सात्यवत सात्यवत, i. e. सत्यवती (see सत्यवन्त्), + अ, metronym., m. The son of Satyavatī, i. e. Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत|सात्वतः
सात्वत सात्वत, i. e. probably सात्वन्त् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Baladeva.<BR> 3. The son of an outcaste Vaiśya, Man. 10, 23.<BR> 4. pl. The name of a people.<BR> II. f. ती, A proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वन्त्|सात्वत्
सात्वन्त् सात्वन्त्, m.<BR> 1. A follower, a worshipper.<BR> 2. A man of the Yādava tribe, Bhāg. P. 8, 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद साद, m., i. e.<BR> A. सद् + अ,<BR> 1. Perishing, decay, Nalod. 2, 26; 3, 24; Vikr. d. 44 (अ-पक्ष-, Not being deprived of its wings).<BR> 2. Weariness, exhaustion, Ragh. 8, 57; Śiś. 9, 77.<BR> 3. Pain, Nalod. 2, 26.<BR> B. Purity, Padmap. 8, 20; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a " target="_blank">Page1032-a + 43</a>] cleanness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करसाद|करसादः
कर- + साद कर- + साद, m. sinking down of one's arms, and setting or disappearing of the sun's rays, Pañc. i. d. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन|सादनं
सादन सादन, i. e. सद्, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Dispelling.<BR> 2. Destroying.<BR> 3. Wearying.<BR> 4. Exhaustion.<BR> 5. A house, a dwelling, Hiḍ. 4, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसादन
यम- + सादन यम- + सादन, n. the palace of Yama i. e. Tartarus, Lass. 17, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादि|सादिः
सादि सादि, i. e. सद् + इ, m. A carioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् सादिन्, i. e. सद्-इन्,<BR> I. adj. Destroying, Rām. 2, 34, 37.<BR> II. m. One who rides on a horse or elephant, or is mounted in a car, Johns. Sel. 26, 8; Rājat. 5, 451.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसादिन्
अश्व- + सादिन् अश्व- + सादिन्, m. a horseman, Ragh. 7, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्य|सादृश्यं
सादृश्य सादृश्य, i. e. सदृश + य, n.<BR> 1. Resemblance, similarity, Kir. 5, 26; Bhāṣāp. 78.<BR> 2. A likeness, Megh. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क साद्यस्क, i. e. सद्यस् + क, adj. Quick, instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् साध् (i. e. probably सो-धा), ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. To finish, to accomplish.<BR> 2. To conquer, Hit. iii. d. 40.<BR> --† i. 4, Par. To be completed or accomplished (cf. सिध्).<BR> --Caus. (also of सिध्, q. cf.),<BR> 1. To bring to a conclusion, to accomplish, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 24; Hit. i. d. 1.<BR> 2. To prepare for heaven, Man. 2, 248.<BR> 3. To secure, Man. 7, 173.<BR> 4. To effect, to perform, MBh. 5, 117.<BR> 5. To overcome, Hit. 59, 21; to conquer, MBh. 1, 7435; to kill, Pañc. 211, 12.<BR> 6. To obtain, Man. 6, 75.<BR> 7. To recover a debt, Man. 8, 176.<BR> 8. To learn, Ragh. 10, 29.<BR> 9. To set out, to go away, Śāk. 7, 19; to fly, Mālat. 126, 5; to proceed, Vikr. 60, 13.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. साधित.<BR> 1. Accomplished, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 24.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-b " target="_blank">Page1032-b + 44</a>] Mastered, Kathās. 46, 118; obtained, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 11.<BR> 3. Successful, Lass. 3, 16.<BR> 4. Recovered (as a debt).<BR> 5. Fulfilled, discharged.<BR> 6. Punished, Pañc. 257, 4; punished by fine.<BR> 7. Awarded (as the thing or fine).<BR> 8. Awarded to or in favour of (as the person to whom the fine is to be paid).<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. साध्य.<BR> 1. What must or will be accomplished, Hit. pr. d. 1.<BR> 2. Practicable, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 23.<BR> 3. Conquerable, Pañc. i. d. 244.<BR> 4. To be mastered, Pañc. i. d. 73; Śiś. 5, 49.<BR> 5. Able to be destroyed, Pañc. 194, 19.<BR> 6. To be inferred or concluded, Bhāṣāp. 137.<BR> 7. To be cured, curable. m. A class of inferior deity, Man. 3, 195. n.<BR> 1. Accomplishment, perfection.<BR> 2. (In logic), The major term in a syllogism, Siddh. Mukt. 62, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. उप उप, उपसाधित, Subdued, Pañc. iii. d. 249.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To settle, Man. 8, 187.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus.<BR> 1. To further, Pañc. i. d. 407.<BR> 2. To accomplish, Pañc. i. d. 140.<BR> 3. To dress, Śāk. 49, 21.<BR> 4. To acquire, Pañc. i. d. 2.<BR> 5. To subdue, Man. 7, 103. प्रसाधित,<BR> 1. Accomplished, done.<BR> 2. Ornamented, decorated, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 10. प्रसाध्य,<BR> 1. What may be done.<BR> 2. To be destroyed, defeated.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Caus. To settle, Hit. iv. d. 117. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a " target="_blank">Page1033-a + 45</a>]<BR> --With सम् सम्, Caus.<BR> 1. Ātm. To be successful, MBh. 3, 1478.<BR> 2. To endow with, Rām. 2, 36, 9.<BR> 3. To destroy, MBh. 3, 1683.<BR> 4. To extinguish, MBh. 1, 2841.<BR> 5. To obtain, Man. 2, 100.<BR> 6. To cause to be paid, 8, 213.<BR> 7. To regain, 8, 50.<BR> --Cf. probably Goth. sandjan; A.S. sendan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्य|असाध्यं
अ- + साध्य अ- + साध्य, adj. 1. unattainable, Pañc. i. d. 223. 2. intractable, Hit. ii. d. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाससाध्य
आयास- + साध्य आयास- + साध्य, adj. scarcely to be settled, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाध्य|दुःसाध्यः
दुःसाध्य दुःसाध्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj.<BR> 1. difficult to be accomplished, Pañc. ii. d. 26. 2. difficult to be conquered, Pañc. 56, 10. 3. difficult to be cured, Hariv. 16132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसाध्य
दुष्प्रसाध्य दुष्प्रसाध्य, i. e. दुस्-, adj. difficult to be defeated, Kām. Nītis. 10, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक साध् + अक,<BR> I. adj., f. धिका,<BR> 1. Accomplishing.<BR> 2. Helping, Indr. 5, 56.<BR> 3. Magical, Pañc. 241, 2; an adept, Mālat. 74, 6; 9, 7 (Prākṛ.).<BR> II. f. इका, Deep sleep (= सुषुप्ति, a vedantic term).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाधक|उत्तरसाधकः
उत्तर- + साधक उत्तर- + साधक, m. one who accomplishes what remains, an assistant, Lass. 3, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्यसाधक|कार्य्यसाधक
कार्य- + साधक कार्य- + साधक, adj., f. धिका, accomplishing one's aim, Hit. i. d. 34, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन साध् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Accomplishing, Hit. iv. d. 98 (साध्य-, What must be accomplished, i. e. one's aim).<BR> 2. Advancement, Man. 4, 196.<BR> 3. A means of accomplishing, Pañc. i. d. 8.<BR> 4. Wealth.<BR> 5. A part of an army, Utt. Rāmac. 39, 12.<BR> 6. Instrument.<BR> 7. Cause, efficient cause, Man. 11, 237; source of prosperity, Man. 12, 100.<BR> 8. Subduing by charms, Pañc. 241, 2.<BR> 9. Killing, destroying, Kir. 14, 17.<BR> 10. Obsequies.<BR> 11. Authority.<BR> 12. Proof, substantiation.<BR> 13. The हेतु or middle term in an inference.<BR> 14. Enforcement of the delivery of anything, of payment, especially juridically, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 20; 185, 21.<BR> 15. Medicament, drug.<BR> 16. Matter, materials, that of which anything is composed.<BR> 17. Substance, thing.<BR> 18. The penis, Sāh. D. 212, 19.<BR> 19. Going.<BR> 20. Following, profit, Pañc. 86, 24.<BR> 21. Good works, Windischmann, Sankara, 97.<BR> 22. Friendship.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधन
अ- + साधन अ- + साधन, adj. having no means, Hit. i. d. 1, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसाधन
त्रि- + साधन त्रि- + साधन, adj., f. ना, having a threefold origin, Ragh. 3, 13 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b " target="_blank">Page1033-b + 40</a>] (viz. majesty, perseverance, and counsel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसाधन|मंत्रसाधन
मन्त्र- + साधन मन्त्र- + साधन, n. a magical performance, Lass. 3, 16 (घोर-, dele' before घोर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनसाधन
लेखन- + साधन लेखन- + साधन, n. writing materials, Śāk. 37, 9 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसाधन
साध्य- + साधन साध्य- + साधन, n. effecting what is to be done, Hit. iv. d. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधन|सिद्धसाधनं|सिद्धसाधनः
सिद्ध- + साधन सिद्ध- + साधन,<BR> I. m. white mustard.<BR> II. n. 1. the performance of magical rites. 2. the materials employed in magical or alchemical processes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनता
साधनता साधन + ता, f., and साधनत्व साधन + त्व, n. State or condition of being a means to a desired end, Bhāṣāp. 146 (त्व); 147 (ता).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसाधनता
बहु-साधनता बहु-साधनता, f. possessing many expedients, Śiś. 9, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन्त|साधंत|साधंतः|साधन्तः
साधन्त साधन्त् + अ (vb. साध्), m. A beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्य|साधर्म्यं
साधर्म्य साधर्म्य, i. e. स-धर्म + य,<BR> 1. Community, equality, of duty, Vikr. 65, 12.<BR> 2. Community of properties, common character, Bhāṣāp. 12. 28; likeness, Kusumāñj. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण साधारण, i. e. स-धारण + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging to many, common, Bhāṣāp. 71; equal, Vikr. d. 34.<BR> 2. Like, similar, Lass. 85, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारण|असाधारणं|असाधारणः
अ- + साधारण अ- + साधारण, adj. 1. not common, Bhāṣāp. 72. 2. unparalleled, Hit. 32, 8, M.M. 3. excessive, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणत्व|साधारणत्वं
साधारणत्व साधारण + त्व, and साधारण्य साधारण्य, i. e. साधारण + य, n. Community, universality, general law, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. xxxix. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिमन्
साधिमन् साधिमन्, i. e. साधु + इमन्, m. Goodness, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ साधिष्ठ, साधीयंस् साधियंस्, see वाढ and the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु साध् + उ,<BR> I. adj., f. धु and ध्वी, comparat. साधीयंस्, superl. साधिष्ठ,<BR> 1. Perfect, Śāk. d. 2.<BR> 2. Fit, proper, right.<BR> 3. Good, Hit. i. d. 11, M.M.; kind, Pañc. iv. d. 72; virtuous, pure.<BR> 4. Excellent.<BR> 5. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR> II. acc. sing. धु, adv.<BR> 1. Well, Śāk. d. 11; Vikr. 6, 6.<BR> 2. Indeed, Vikr. 20, 9.<BR> 3. With instr., prohibiting, Enough, away with, Pañc. v. d. 40.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A Muni or sage.<BR> 2. An honest man, Pañc. 67, 6.<BR> 3. A usurer, Hit. 111, 1; a merchant, Hit. 65, 9.<BR> IV. f. धु and ध्वी, A chaste, virtuous woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधु
अ- + साधु अ- + साधु, adj. wicked, Kir. 14, 12; 21; unpleasant, Kir. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसाधु
सर्व- + साधु सर्व- + साधु, adv. quite well, Hit. 127, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुता
साधुता साधु + ता, f., and साधुत्व साधु + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Correctness, Utt. Rāmac. 4, 10 (त्व).<BR> 2. Goodness, Pañc. i. d. 277 (त्व); Daśak. in Chr. 187, 23 (ता).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुत्व
अ-साधुत्व अ-साधुत्व, n. wickedness, Hit. iii. d. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुंमन्य|साधुम्मन्य
साधुंमन्य साधुंमन्य, i. e. साधु + म्-मन् + य, adj. Thinking one's self virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशीलत्व
साधुशीलत्व साधु-शील + त्व, n. Virtuous disposition, Hit. i. d. 85, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य साध्य,<BR> 1. See साध्.<BR> 2. i. e. साध्य + अ, adj. Belonging to the Sādhyas, a class of inferior deity, Arj. 4, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यता
साध्यता साध्य + ता, f. in अ-, State of not being able to be overcome, Pañc. i. d. 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यवन्त्|साध्यवत्
साध्यवन्त् साध्य + वन्त् (vb. साध्),<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Comprehending that which is to be proved.<BR> II. m. (In law), The party on whom rest the onus probandi.<BR> III. n. That in which the साध्य or major term resides (i. e. the पक्ष and its सपक्षऽस्), Bhāṣāp. 67; 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वस|साध्वसं
साध्वस साध्वस, probably स-ध्वंस् + अ + अ, n.<BR> 1. Fear, terror, Vikr. d. 56; Mālav. 20, 9; 53, 21; Śāk. 12, 21.<BR> 2. Perturbation, Bhāg. P. 1, 11, 19.<BR> 3. Torpor, Utt. Rāmac. 80, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाध्वस
अति- + साध्वस अति- + साध्वस, m. too great fear, Hit. iii. d. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसाध्वस
निःसाध्वस निःसाध्वस, i. e. निस्-, adj. 1. fearless, Hariv. 8709. 2. bold, Rām. 1, 64, 16 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
स- + साध्वस स- + साध्वस, adj., f. सा, alarmed, frightened, timid, Vikr. 28, 10. ˚सम्, adv., 28, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसि|सानसिः
सानसि सानसि, m. (?), f. (?), Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु सानु, probably सो + नु, m. and n.<BR> 1. End, point, the top of a mountain, Mālat. 145, 10.<BR> 2. Level ground on the top or edge of a mountain, tableland, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 13.<BR> 3. A forest.<BR> 4. A shoot, a sprout.<BR> 5. A road.<BR> 6. A gale of wind.<BR> 7. A learned man, a sage.<BR> 8. The sun.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसानु
अन्तःसानु अन्तःसानु, i. e. अन्तर्-, adv. on a table-land, Kir. 5, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमन्त्|सानुमत्
सानुमन्त् सानु + मन्त्,<BR> I. m. A mountain, Vikr. d. 76.<BR> II. f. मती, The name of an Apsaras, Śāk. 77, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तपन|सांतपन|सांतपनं|सान्तपनं
सान्तपन सान्तपन, i. e. सम्-तप् + अन + अ, n. A sort of penance, Man. 11, 212; 5, 20; 11, 129.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासान्तपन|महासांतपन|महासान्तपनं|महासांतपनः
महा- + सान्तपन महा- + सान्तपन, n. a severer sort of penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिक|सांतानिक|सान्तानिकः
सान्तानिक सान्तानिक, i. e. संतान + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Expansive.<BR> 2. Relating to posterity.<BR> 3. Belonging to the heavenly tree. संतान, Kir. 18, 20.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa intending to marry for the sake of issue, Man. 11, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व्|सांत्व्
सान्त्व् सान्त्व्, and सान्त्व सान्त्व see शान्त्व्, शान्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वन|सांत्वन|सांत्वनं|सान्त्वनं
सान्त्वन सान्त्व् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Conciliation, reconcilement.<BR> 2. Appeasing, Rājat. 5, 345 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> II. n., and f. ना.<BR> 1. Speaking kindly and in a conciliatory manner.<BR> 2. Mildness, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 21 (n.); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a " target="_blank">Page1035-a + 42</a>] kind or deceiving words, Pañc. iv. d. 1 (n. pl.).<BR> 3. Friendly salutation and enquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सान्दृष्टिक सान्दृष्टिक, i. e. सम्-दृश् + ति + इक, m. Immediate consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्र|सांद्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सान्द्र सान्द्र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Thick, coarse, gross, Caurap. 12; Ṛt. 1, 20; intense, Śiś. 9, 15; 22.<BR> 2. Stout, robust.<BR> 3. Much, abundant, Mālat. 60, 13.<BR> 4. Vehement, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 830; Daśak. in Chr. 190, 8; Ragh. 7, 11; सान्द्रतर, Increased, Śiś. 9, 37.<BR> 5. Clustering, collected.<BR> 6. Compact, but having interstices.<BR> 7. Unctuous, oily, Kāvya Prak. 62, 11.<BR> 8. Soft, bland.<BR> 9. Pleasing, agreeable, Mālat. 127, 12; Megh. 97 (v. r.).<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A thicket, a wood.<BR> 2. A heap, a cluster.<BR> --Cf. probably ἁδρός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिकः
सान्धिविग्रहिक सान्धिविग्रहिक, i. e. संधि-विग्रह + इक, m. Prime minister (who decides peace and war), Lass. 2. ed. 16, 9; Sāh. D. 7, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्ध्य|सांध्य|सान्ध्यः
सान्ध्य सान्ध्य, i. e. संध्या + अ, adj. Relating to twilight or the evening, Kir. 5, 8; Śiś. 9, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सान्नहनिक सान्नहनिक, i. e. संनहन + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Bearing or putting on armour.<BR> 2. Calling to arms.<BR> II. m. An armour-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं|सांनाय्यः
सान्नाय्य सान्नाय्य, i. e. probably सम्-नाय्य (ptcple. of the fut. pass. of the Caus. of नी), + अ, n. The thing to be offered with fire, Pāṇ. iii. 1, 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्य|सांनिध्य|सांनिध्यं|सान्निध्यं
सान्निध्य सान्निध्य, i. e. संनिधि + य, n.<BR> 1. Vicinity, Pañc. 258, 7.<BR> 2. Presence, Man. 8, 87; attendance, Hit. 53, 12.<BR> 3. ˚यम्, adv. Near, Indr. 5, 24.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असान्निध्य|असांनिध्य
अ- + सान्निध्य अ- + सान्निध्य, n. absence, Rām. 3, 55, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्यतस्|सांनिध्यतस्
सान्निध्यतस् सान्निध्य + तस्, adv. From the proximity, Mālat. 48, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निपातिक|सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सान्निपातिक सान्निपातिक, i. e. संनिपात + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Complicated (as disease), relating to the morbid state of the three humours collectively, Hit. iii. d. 119.<BR> 2. Miscellaneous, promiscuous, collective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिकः
सान्न्यासिक सान्न्यासिक, i. e. संन्यास + इक, m. A beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न
सापत्न सापत्न, i. e. स-पत्नी + अ, adj. Born from another wife, Rām. 3, 53, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यं|सापत्न्यः
सापत्न्य सापत्न्य, i. e.<BR> A. सपत्न + य,<BR> I. m. An enemy.<BR> II. n. Ambition, Rām. 1, 45, 16.<BR> B. स-पत्नी + य, n. Plurality of wives, or the condition of the wife of one who has other wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिण्ड्य|सापिंड्य|सापिंड्यं|सापिण्ड्यं
सापिण्ड्य सापिण्ड्य, i. e. स-पिण्ड + य, n. Kindred, connexion, by presenting offerings to the same Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपद
साप्तपद साप्तपद, i. e. सप्तन्-पद + अ, adj. Produced by seven steps (walked together), Pañc. ii. d. 47; Sāv. 5, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीन|साप्तपदीनं
साप्तपदीन साप्तपदीन, i. e. साप्त-पद + ईन, n. Friendship, Kumāras. 5, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष साप्तपौरुष, i. e. सप्तन्-पुरुष + अ, adj., f. षी, Comprising seven generations, Man. 3, 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्य|साफल्यं
साफल्य साफल्य, i. e. स-फल + य, n.<BR> 1. Productiveness, fruitfulness, Hit. ii. d. 21.<BR> 2. Advantage, Man. 12, 93.<BR> 3. State of earning the fruit, Mālat. 72, 9 (at the end of a Bahuvr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्
† साम् साम्, i. 10 (rather a dénomin. derived from सामन्), Par. To conciliate, to appease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्य|सामग्र्यं
सामग्र्य सामग्र्य, i. e. समग्र + य, n., and f. ग्री,<BR> 1. Entireness, wholeness, the whole, Bhāṣāp. 63 (ग्री); Rām. 2, 70, 45, Seramp. (read प्राणसामग्र्यम्), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a " target="_blank">Page1036-a + 43</a>]<BR> 2. Perfection, Pañc. 109, 10 (ग्री).<BR> 3. Stock, Hit. 130, 1 (ग्री); effects.<BR> 4. Implements, apparatus, Pañc. iii. d. 129 (ग्री); utensils, 250, 5 (ग्री).<BR> 5. Train, retinue, Hit. 98, 11 (य्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामज|सामजः
सामज सामज,<BR> I. i. e. सामन् + ज, adj. Producing from or produced by the Sāma-Veda.<BR> II. m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामञ्जस्य|सामंजस्य|सामंजस्यं|सामञ्जस्यं
सामञ्जस्य सामञ्जस्य, i. e. समञ्जस + य, n. Fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् सामन्, probably for शामन् (cf. शान्त्व, सान्त्वन), i. e. शम् + मन्, n.<BR> 1. Calming, Nalod. 1, 41.<BR> 2. Conciliation.<BR> 3. Speaking kindly, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1847.<BR> 4. Mildness, Man. 8, 187; instr. म्ना, Willingly, voluntarily, Pañc. iv. d. 27.<BR> 5. Negotiation, Man. 7, 107.<BR> 6. Peaceable way, Pañc. i. d. 421; Chr. 20, 17.<BR> 7. The name of the third Veda, the Sāma- Veda, Man. 1, 23.<BR> 8. Song, Bhag. 10, 35; Indr. 2, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठसामन्
ज्येष्ठ- + सामन् ज्येष्ठ- + सामन्,<BR> I. n. the name of a particular song (of the Sāma- Veda), Man. 3, 185.<BR> II. m. one who sings this song, Yājñ. 1, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसामन्
त्रि- + सामन् त्रि- + सामन्, adj. one who sings three verses (of the SāmaVeda), or the song called त्रिःसामन् (?), MBh. 12, 3638.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसामन्
सु- + सामन् सु- + सामन्, n. good negotiation, Pañc. iii. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्त|सामंत|सामन्तः
सामन्त सामन्त, i. e. समन्त + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Limitative.<BR> 2. Bordering, neighbouring, Man. 8, 259.<BR> 3. Universal, Ragh. 5, 28 (Sch.).<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A neighbour, Man. 7, 69; Pañc. iii. d. 91.<BR> 2. The chief of a district, a (tributary) king, Mālat. 102, 6; Rājat. 5, 223; Vikr. d. 60.<BR> 3. A leader, a general, Rām. 1, 20, 12; a champion, Rājat. 5, 249.<BR> III. n. Neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक सामयिक, i. e. समय + इक. adj.<BR> 1. According to agreement, exact.<BR> 2. Conventional, customary. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b " target="_blank">Page1036-b + 43</a>]<BR> 3. Seasonable.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामयिक
अ- + सामयिक अ- + सामयिक, unseasonable, Kir. 2, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्य|सामर्थ्यं
सामर्थ्य सामर्थ्य, i. e. समर्थ + य, n.<BR> 1. Fitness, Rājat. 5, 308.<BR> 2. Adequacy, Pañc. i. d. 215 (that which is adequate, but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1873, v. r.); being entitled, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3027.<BR> 3. Profit, Rām. 2, 61, 44, Seramp.<BR> 4. Ability, Pañc. 263, 7.<BR> 5. Strength, Rājat. 5, 384; power, Hit. ii. d. 140; fortitude, Bhag. 2, 36.<BR> 6. Mutual relation of words.<BR> 7. Sense of words.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामर्थ्य
अ- + सामर्थ्य अ- + सामर्थ्य, n. weakness, Pañc. 69, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसामर्थ्य
निःसामर्थ्य निःसामर्थ्य, i. e. निस्-, adj. unfit, MBh. 5, 4587.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनदर्शनसामर्थ्य
हीन-दर्शन- + सामर्थ्य हीन-दर्शन- + सामर्थ्य (vb. का), adj. blind, Rājat. 5, 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्षता
सामर्षता सामर्षता, i. e. स-अ-मर्ष + ता, f. Wrath, Ragh. 7, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक सामवायिक, i. e. समवाय + इक, m.<BR> 1. The chief of a company or corporation.<BR> 2. A principal minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक सामाजिक, i. e. समाज + अ, m. An assistant or spectator at an assembly, Mālav. 17, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्य|सामानाधिकरण्यं
सामानाधिकरण्य सामानाधिकरण्य, i. e. समान-अधिकरण + य, n.<BR> 1. Common office.<BR> 2. The condition of relating to the same object, Vedāntas. in Chr. 212, 21.<BR> 3. The residing in the same substratum or subject, Kusumāñj. 14, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य सामान्य, i. e. समान + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Common, Hit. i. d. 157, M.M.; Nal. 13, 17; in common, Pañc. 264, 2; base, Rājat. 5, 197; सामान्यतर, Very insignificant, not dexterous, Pañc. 133, 1.<BR> 2. Equal, Śāk. d. 92.<BR> 3. Generic.<BR> 4. General, universal, whole.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Totality.<BR> 2. Public affairs, Man. 7, 56.<BR> 3. Equanimity, Hit. i. d. 95, M.M.<BR> 4. Common property, Hit. pr. d. 25, M.M.<BR> 5. Kind, genus, or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a " target="_blank">Page1037-a + 42</a>] species, Bhāṣāp. 1; 7, 63.<BR> 6. Identity, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 11.<BR> III. f. या, A whore.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्य
अ- + सामान्य अ- + सामान्य and निस्-, adj. uncommon, extraordinary, Pañc. 115, 7; Rājat. 4, 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यनारीसामान्य
अन्-अन्य-नारी- + सामान्य अन्-अन्य-नारी- + सामान्य, adj. having no intercourse with other women, Vikr. d. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकसामान्य
अ-लोक- + सामान्य अ-लोक- + सामान्य, adj. uncommon, Mālat. 6, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसामान्य
सर्व- + सामान्य सर्व- + सामान्य, adj. common to all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक सामासिक, i. e. समास + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Compounded, Bhag. 10, 33; composite.<BR> 2. Comprehensive, comprising the whole, Man. 7, 180; 10, 63.<BR> 3. Summary, brief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि सामि, i. e. a form of the old instr. *साम्या of साम्य (cf. आदि for आद्य), adv.<BR> 1. Half.<BR> 2. Blameably.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. sâmi-; A.S. sâm-, e. g. in O.H.G. sâmi-quek; A.S. sâm-cuce; Lat. semi-; ἡμι, ἥμισυς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेन्य
सामिधेन्य सामिधेन्य, i. e. सम्-इधेन्य (an old ptcple. of the fut. pass. of इन्ध्), + अ,<BR> I. m. A mantra or mystical prayer.<BR> II. f. नी,<BR> 1. Fuel.<BR> 2. A prayer used on adding fuel to the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्य|सामीप्यं|सामीप्यः
सामीप्य सामीप्य i. e. समीप + य,<BR> I. m. A neighbour, Sāv. 2, 8.<BR> II. n. Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र सामुद्र, i. e. समुद्र + अ,<BR> I. adj. Marine, sea-born.<BR> II. m. A mariner, a voyager.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Seasalt.<BR> 2. Cuttle-fish bone.<BR> 3. (i. e. स-मुद्र + अ, see मुद्रा), A spot or mark on the body (cf. the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
सामुद्रिक सामुद्रिक, i. e. स + मुद्र (cf. मुद्रा), + इक,<BR> I. adj. Relating to spots on the body, or the good or ill fortune supposed to be indicated by them.<BR> II. m. An interpreter of spots on the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्पराय|सांपराय|सांपरायः
साम्पराय साम्पराय, i. e. संपराय + अ<BR> I. adj. Warlike (?). MBh. 1, 723. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b " target="_blank">Page1037-b + 41</a>]<BR> II. (n.),<BR> 1. Future, MBh. 1, 1921.<BR> 2. Future life, Bhāg. P. 8, 19, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्परायिक|सांपरायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
साम्परायिक साम्परायिक, i. e. संपराय + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to war, military, Man. 7, 185; warlike, Ragh. 17, 62.<BR> 2. Calamitous.<BR> 3. Future, relating to a future state, Man. 11, 30.<BR> II. n. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतम्|सांप्रतम्
साम्प्रतम् साम्प्रतम्, i. e. संप्रति + अ + म्, adv.<BR> 1. Now, at this time, Pañc. 161, 18.<BR> 2. Seasonably, fitly, properly.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्प्रत|असांप्रत|असाम्प्रतं
अ-साम्प्रत अ-साम्प्रत, adj. unbecoming, Pañc. i. d. 275. ˚तम्, adv. unbecomingly, Hit. iii. d. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतिक|सांप्रतिक
साम्प्रतिक साम्प्रतिक, i. e. सम्प्रति + इक, adj. Suitable, Utt. Rāmac. 73, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रदायिक|सांप्रदायिक
साम्प्रदायिक साम्प्रदायिक, i. e. संप्रदाय + इक, adj. Belonging to traditional doctrine, transferred by traditional doctrine, Utt. Rāmac. 155, 8 (अ-, with नहि, Their tradition will not die out, they are hereditary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ब्
साम्ब् साम्ब्, see सम्ब्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बवती
साम्बवती साम्बवती, A proper name, Rājat. 5, 295.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्य|साम्यं
साम्य साम्य, i. e. सम + य, n.<BR> 1. Equality, Man. 11, 195.<BR> 2. Equability, Bhag. 6, 33.<BR> 3. Harmony, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 4.<BR> 4. Likeness, similarity, Kir. 17, 51.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसाम्य
त्रि- + साम्य त्रि- + साम्य, n. equality of the three fundamental qualities, Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्य|साम्राज्यं
साम्राज्य साम्राज्य, i. e. सम्राज् + य, n. Imperial rule, Man. 8, 387; sovereignty, Pañc. 42, 14; Rājat. 5, 49; 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्यकृत्
साम्राज्यकृत् साम्राज्य-कृ + त्, adj. One who gains imperial rule, Man. 8, 387.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साय|सायं|सायः
साय साय,<BR> A. i. e. से + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. End.<BR> 2. Evening, Vikr. 77, 12.<BR> B. m. An arrow.<BR> II. acc. यम्, adv. Evening, in the evening, Pañc. iii. d. 159.<BR> III. loc. ये, adv. In the evening.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sērus, sērum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसायम्
अति-सायम् अति-सायम्, adv. too late, Man. 4, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायक|सायकः
सायक साय + क (and शायक शायक), m.<BR> 1. An arrow, Pañc. 120, 10.<BR> 2. A sword.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमसायक|असमसायकः
अ-सम- + सायक अ-सम- + सायक and पुष्प-, m. Kāma, the god of love, Kathās. 15, 2; Lass. 66, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकमय
सायकमय सायक + मय, adj. Consisting in arrows, MBh. 4, 1853.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन्तन|सायंतन|सायन्तनः
सायन्तन सायन्तन, i. e. साय + म् + तन, adj., f. नी, Belonging to the evening, vespertine, Pañc. 229, 10; Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्य|सायुज्यं
सायुज्य सायुज्य, i. e. स-युज् + य, n.<BR> 1. Intimate union, identification.<BR> 2. Similarity, likeness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसायुज्य|राजसायुज्यं
राज-सायुज्य राज-सायुज्य, i. e. राजन्-, n. royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्
सार् सार्, see शार्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार सार, perhaps सृ + अ, with ‘cream,’<BR> II.<BR> 9. as first signification,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Essential, Hit. iv. d. 71.<BR> 2. Excellent, best, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 22; Pañc. i. d. 284; Hit. iii. d. 89.<BR> 3. Hard, Śāk. d. 10.<BR> 4. Irrefragable (as an argument), proved, Man. 9, 262.<BR> II. m. (and n.).<BR> 1. The pith or sap of trees.<BR> 2. The essence of anything, the essential or vital part of it, Hit. ii. d. 126; Pañc. 49, 4.<BR> 3. Nectar, Bhāg. P. 7, 6, 25.<BR> 4. The substance or material part (of a book, speech, etc.), Pañc. pr. d. 3; 10 (n.).<BR> 5. Marrow, Ragh. 10, 10.<BR> 6. Strength, vigour, Hit. 104, 7; affluence, Hit. i. d. 90, M.M. (अर्थ-, of wealth, cf.<BR> IV.<BR> 2.).<BR> 7. Prowess, heroism.<BR> 8. Firmness, hardness.<BR> 9. The coagulum of curds, cream.<BR> 10. Fresh butter.<BR> 11. Air, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-b " target="_blank">Page1038-b + 47</a>] wind (cf. शार).<BR> 12. Disease, pus, Hit. ii. d. 101 (and wealth).<BR> III. m., and f. री, A man at chess, backgammon (cf. शार).<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Water.<BR> 2. Wealth, Man. 8, 126; Daśak. in Chr. 189, 3 (at the end of a comp. adj.).<BR> 3. Fitness.<BR> 4. Steel.<BR> 5. (In rhetoric), Climax.<BR> V. f. रा, Kuśa grass.<BR> VI. f. री, Turdus Salica Buch.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. सर; Goth. sêls; A.S. sel, sael.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असार|असारं|असारः
अ- + सार अ- + सार, adj. 1. sapless, Hit. iv. d. 87. 2. insipid, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 2; vain, Pañc. 165, 17. 3. weak, Pañc. i. d. 376. 4. bad, Man. 8, 202. 5. poor, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासार
सार-अ- + सार सार-अ- + सार, m. 1. strength and weakness, Hit. 104, 7. 2. excellence or defect, Man. 9, 331. 3. substance and emptiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसारा
अग्र- + सारा अग्र- + सारा, f. रा, a method of numbering, by which one may sum up the sand of a hundred Koṭis of Gaṅgā rivers, Lalit. 141 (cf. Archimedes' method).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसार|अद्रिसारः
अद्रि- + सार अद्रि- + सार, m. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसार|अन्तःसारः
अन्तःसार अन्तःसार, i. e. अन्तर्-,<BR> I. m. and n. 1. the inward pus and wealth, Hit. ii. d. 101. 2. own worth, Cāṇ. 69 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411.<BR> II. adj. 1. having inward essence, full of strength, Pañc. i. d. 142. 2. heavy, ponderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसार|अर्थसारः
अर्थ- + सार अर्थ- + सार, m. important motive, Pañc. ii. d. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मसार|अश्मसारः
अश्मसार अश्मसार, i. e. अश्मन्-, m. iron, Suśr. 2, 531, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसार
एक- + सार एक- + सार, m. only essence, Bhartṛ. 2, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसार|कृष्णसारः
कृष्ण- + सार कृष्ण- + सार (cf. शार),<BR> I. adj. of a blue-black colour, Rām. 5, 32, 47.<BR> II. m. 1. the black-pied antelope, Man. 2, 23; Vikr. d. 120. 2. the name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसार|गिरिसारः
गिरि- + सार गिरि- + सार, m. 1. iron. 2. tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसार|घनसारः
घन- + सार घन- + सार, m. camphor, Lass. 92, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनसार|चंदनसार|चन्दनसारः
चन्दन- + सार चन्दन- + सार, m. the best sandal, Rām. 2, 20, 43 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्सार|त्वक्सारः
त्वक्सार त्वक्सार, i. e. त्वच्-, m. reed, Man. 10, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टसार
दृष्ट- + सार दृष्ट- + सार, adj. one of whom the strength is tested, Kām. Nītis. 8, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिभवसार
निस्-अभिभव- + सार निस्-अभिभव- + सार, adj. having the highest excellence, i. e. than which there is nothing better, Bhartṛ. 2, 54 (but cf. also Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1859).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
निःसार निःसार, i. e. निस्-, adj., f. रा, 1. sapless, Suśr. 1, 20, 16; Cāṇ. 66 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 411. 2. powerless, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a " target="_blank">Page1039-a + 44</a>] insignificant, Pañc. i. d. 421.<BR> 3. insipid.<BR> 4. vain, perishable, Hit. iv. d. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसार
प्राण- + सार प्राण- + सार, adj. having the marrow of life, Śāk. d. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रसार
वज्र- + सार वज्र- + सार,<BR> I. adj. having the vigour of a thunderbolt, Pañc. 58, 10.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तसार
वेदान्त- + सार वेदान्त- + सार, m. the essence of the Vedānta philosophy, Vedāntas. title, in Chr. 202, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलासार|शिलासारं
शिला- + सार शिला- + सार, m. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलसार
शैल- + सार शैल- + सार, adj. firm as a rock, Kir. 10, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकलार्थशास्त्रसार
स-कल-अर्थ-शास्त्र- + सार स-कल-अर्थ-शास्त्र- + सार, adj. containing the essence of precepts about all things, Pañc. pr. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसार|सत्त्वसारः
सत्त्व- + सार सत्त्व- + सार, m. excellence of strength, i. e. the most powerful, Utt. Rāmac. 151, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसार|सुसारः
सु- + सार सु- + सार, m. 1. a kind of jewel or crystal (?), MBh. 7, 672. 2. Mimosa catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभूत्येकसार
स्व-अनुभूति-एक-सार स्व-अनुभूति-एक-सार, adj. whose only essence consists in enjoying himself, Bhartṛ. 2, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्ग|सारंग|सारङ्गः
सारङ्ग सारङ्ग (cf. शारङ्ग),<BR> I. adj. Variegated, spotted.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Variegated colour.<BR> 2. A lion.<BR> 3. An elephant.<BR> 4. A deer, Vikr. 63, 9; Śāk. 5, 5.<BR> 5. The Cātaka, Cuculus melanoleucus, Megh. 21.<BR> 6. The Indian cuckoo.<BR> 7. A kind of crane.<BR> 8. A peacock.<BR> 9. A large bee, Nalod. 1, 44.<BR> 10. A cloud.<BR> 11. A tree.<BR> 12. A parasol.<BR> 13. A garment.<BR> 14. Hair.<BR> 15. A lotus.<BR> 16. A flower.<BR> 17. A conch-shell.<BR> 18. A jewel.<BR> 19. Gold.<BR> 20. A bow.<BR> 21. Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR> 22. Sandal.<BR> 23. Camphor.<BR> III. f. गी, A sort of fiddle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसारङ्ग|कृष्णसारङ्गः
कृष्ण- + सारङ्ग कृष्ण- + सारङ्ग,<BR> I. adj. blackpied.<BR> II. m. the black-pied antelope, Śāk. 61, 14 (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण सारण, i. e. सृ, Caus., + अन, m. Dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणि|सारणिः
सारणि and णी सारणी̆ i. e. सृ + अन + ई, f. A canal, a water-conduit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतस्
सारतस् सार + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. Essentially.<BR> 2. Vigorously.<BR> 3. Concerning (their) wealth, fortune, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 8; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b " target="_blank">Page1039-b + 41</a>] in proportion to the value, Man. 8, 405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारता
सारता सार + ता, f.<BR> 1. Essence, Pañc. ii. d. 84.<BR> 2. Substance.<BR> 3. Strength.<BR> 4. Highest degree, Rājat. 5, 400.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असारता
अ- + सारता अ- + सारता, f. fragility, Ragh. 8, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासारता
सार-अ- + सारता सार-अ- + सारता, f. strong and weak points, Pañc. 53, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथि|सारथिः
सारथि सारथि, i. e. स-रथ + इ, m. A charioteer, Bhāṣāp. 49.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसारथि
कु- + सारथि कु- + सारथि, m. a bad charioteer. Lass. 53, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसारथि
धर्म- + सारथि धर्म- + सारथि, a proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 17, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिसारथि|पार्ष्णिसारथिः
पार्ष्णि- + सारथि पार्ष्णि- + सारथि, m. du. the two carioteers who govern the outer horses attached to the extremities of the axletree, MBh. 1, 5490.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसारथि|मधुसारथिः
मधु- + सारथि मधु- + सारथि, m. Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथ्य|सारथ्यं
सारथ्य सारथ्य, i. e. सारथि + य, n. Charioteership, charioteering, Chr. 27, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसारथ्य
अश्व- + सारथ्य अश्व- + सारथ्य, n. management of horses and cars, Man. 10, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारफल्गुत्व
सारफल्गुत्व सार-फल्गु + त्व, n. Importance and non-importance, the proportional importance, Man. 9, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारमेय|सारमेयः
सारमेय सारमेय, i. e. सरमा + एय,<BR> I. m. A dog, Pañc. 110, 23.<BR> II. f. यी, A bitch.<BR> --Cf. probably Ἑρμείας.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवत्ता
सारवत्ता सारवत्ता, i. e. सारवन्त् + ता, f. Hardness, Ragh. 3, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवन्त्|सारवत्
सारवन्त् सार + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Substantial, having pith, substance.<BR> 2. Fertile, Hit. iv. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस|सारसं|सारसः
सारस सारस, i. e. सरस् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating or belonging to a lake, Nalod. 2, 40.<BR> II. m., and f. सी, The Indian crane, male and female, Ardea sibirica, Rām. 3, 53, 58; Pañc. 82, 6; ii. d. 103 (cf. my transl.); a bird in general, Nalod. 2, 10.<BR> III. m. The moon.<BR> IV. n. A lotus, Caurap. 44.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसारस|राजसारसः
राज-सारस राज-सारस, i. e. राजन्-, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसन|सारसनं
सारसन सारसन, i. e. स-रसन + अ, n. A girdle, Kir. 18, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत|सारस्वतः
सारस्वत सारस्वत, i. e. सरस्वन्त् + ई + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती,<BR> 1. Relating to the goddess Sarasvatī,<BR> 2. Relating or belonging to the river Sarasvatī, Megh. 50.<BR> 3. Eloquent.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A staff of the Vilva tree.<BR> 2. The name of a country; pl. its people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारापराधतस्
सारापराधतस् सारापराधतस्, i. e. सार-स्पराध + तस्, adv. Conformably to the proved crimes, Man. 9, 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिका
सारिका सारिका, f. A bird, Turdus Salica and Gracula religiosa (cf. शारिका), Pañc. iv. d. 51; Megh. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिन्
ऽसारिन् -सारिन्, i. e.<BR> I. सृ + इन्, adj. Going; पार्व-, Going in front, being the first, MBh. 5, 142.<BR> II. सार + इन्, adj. Having the essence or substance of, Nal. 12, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्य|सारूप्यं
सारूप्य सारूप्य, i. e. स-रूप + य, n.<BR> 1. Identity of form.<BR> 2. Conformity, Man. 4, 18.<BR> 3. Close resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्यतस्
सारूप्यतस् सारूप्य + तस्, adv. In consequence of the identity. Mālat. 76, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थ|सार्थः
सार्थ सार्थ, i. e. स-अर्थ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Opulent.<BR> 2. Of like meaning.<BR> 3. Significant.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A caravan, Pañc. 3, 21.<BR> 2. A troop, Rājat. 5, 374.<BR> 3. A multitude in general, Lass. 66, 17; Śāk. 32, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसार्थम्
एक-सार्थ + म् एक-सार्थ + म्, together, Johns. Sel. 36, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गसार्थ|भंगसार्थ|भङ्गसार्थः
भङ्ग- + सार्थ भङ्ग- + सार्थ, adj. fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थिक|सार्थिकः
सार्थिक सार्थिक, i. e. सार्थ + इक, m. A merchant, Pañc. 8, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्धम्
सार्धम् सार्धम्, i. e. स-अर्ध + म्, prep. (with instr.), With, Man. 1, 27; Pañc. i. d. 61; iii. d. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष सार्पिष, and सार्पिष्क सार्पिष्क, i. e. सर्पिस् + अ, or क, adj. Dressed with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पी
सार्पी सार्पी, see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प्य|सार्प्यः
सार्प्य सार्प्य, i. e. सर्प + य,<BR> I. adj. Relating to a snake.<BR> II. f. पी, The ninth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकामिक|सार्व्वकामिक
सार्वकामिक सार्वकामिक, i. e. सर्व-काम + इक, adj. Satisfying every wish, Kir. 18, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकालिक|सार्व्वकालिक
सार्वकालिक सार्वकालिक, i. e. सर्व-काल + इक, adj., f. की, Of all times or seasons, everlasting, MBh. 1, 7648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्वजनिक सार्वजनिक, and सार्वजनीन सार्वजनीन, i. e. सर्व-जन + इक, or ईन, adj. Relating, or belonging, or suited, to all men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वदैवत्य|सार्व्वदैवत्य
सार्वदैवत्य सार्वदैवत्य, i. e. सर्व-देवत + य, adj. Presided over by, or sacred to, all the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौतिक|सार्व्वभौतिक
सार्वभौतिक सार्वभौतिक, i. e. सर्व-भूत + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Belonging or relating to all elements, beings.<BR> 2. Comprising all animated beings, Man. 12, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौम|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्वभौम सार्वभौम, i. e. सर्व-भूमि + अ,<BR> I. adj. Relating to, or consisting of, the whole earth.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An universal monarch.<BR> 2. The elephant of the northern quarter.<BR> 3. A proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 22, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्वलौकिक सार्वलौकिक, i. e. सर्व-लोक + इक, adj. Prevailing through the universe, Mālat. 7, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववर्णिक|सार्व्ववर्णिक
सार्ववर्णिक सार्ववर्णिक, i. e. सर्व-वर्ण + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Of every kind, Man. 2, 244.<BR> 2. Belonging to every tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेदस|सार्ववेदसः|सार्व्ववेदस
सार्ववेदस सार्ववेदस, i. e. सर्व-वेदस् + अ, m. One who gives away all his wealth at a sacred rite, Man. 11, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्यः
सार्ववेद्य सार्ववेद्य, i. e. सर्व-वेद + य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a " target="_blank">Page1041-a + 41</a>] m. A Brāhmaṇa conversant with all the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप सार्षप, i. e. सर्षप + अ,<BR> I. adj. Made of or from mustard.<BR> II. n. Mustard oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टिता
सार्ष्टिता सार्ष्टिता, perhaps स-ऋष् + ति + ता, f. Equality, Man. 4, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल|सालः
साल साल (cf. शाल),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A wall surrounding a building, a wall in general, Daśak. in Chr. 201, 1.<BR> 2. A tree, Shorea robusta, Man. 8, 246.<BR> 3. A tree in general.<BR> 4. A fish, Ophiocephalus Wrahl.<BR> II. f. ला, A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालभञ्जिका|सालभंजिका
सालभञ्जिका साल-भञ्ज् + इका, f. A doll, a puppet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्य|सालोक्यं
सालोक्य सालोक्य, i. e. स-लोक + य, n. Habitation with, Man. 4, 231; MBh. 3, 11184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्व|साल्वः
साल्व साल्व, m.<BR> 1. = शाल्व.<BR> 2. The name of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वहन्
साल्वहन् साल्व-हन्, m. Viṣṇu (the slayer of Sālva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधानता
सावधानता सावधानता, i. e. स-अवधान + ता, f. Carefulness, Pañc. 34, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन सावन, i. e. सु, Caus., + अन, m.<BR> 1. An employer of priests for a sacrifice.<BR> 2. The ceremonies by which a sacrifice is terminated.<BR> 3. Varuṇa.<BR> 4. A month of thirty solar days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णि|सावर्णिः
सावर्णि सावर्णि, i. e. स-वर्ण + इ, m. The eighth Manu, Bhāg. P. 8, 13, 11.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसावर्णि|इन्द्रसावर्णिः
इन्द्र- + सावर्णि इन्द्र- + सावर्णि, the fourteenth Manu, ib. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसावर्णि|दक्षसावर्णिः
दक्ष- + सावर्णि दक्ष- + सावर्णि, m. the ninth Manu, ib. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसावर्णि|देवसावर्णिः
देव- + सावर्णि देव- + सावर्णि, m. the thirteenth Manu, ib. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसावर्णि|धर्म्मसावर्णि|धर्म्मसावर्णिः
धर्म- + सावर्णि धर्म- + सावर्णि, m. the eleventh Manu, ib. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसावर्णि|ब्रह्मसावर्णिः
ब्रह्मन्- + सावर्णि ब्रह्मन्- + सावर्णि, m. the tenth Manu, ib. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रसावर्णि|रुद्रसावर्णिः
रुद्र- + सावर्णि रुद्र- + सावर्णि, m. the twelfth Manu, ib. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्य|सावर्ण्यं
सावर्ण्य सावर्ण्य, i. e. स-वर्न + य, n. Identity of caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र सावित्र, i. e. सवितृ + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Descended from the sun, Utt. Rāmac. 132, 3.<BR> 2. Belonging to the dynasty descended from the sun, ib. 27, 13.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> 3. A Vasu or demigod so called.<BR> 4. Karṇa, child of the sun.<BR> 5. One of the Nakṣatras, or lunar asterisms, Johns. Sel. 15, 62.<BR> III. f. त्री.<BR> 1. A beam of light, a cluster of solar rays.<BR> 2. Umā, the wife of Śiva, Sāv. 1, 7.<BR> 3. A proper name, Sāv. 1, 21.<BR> 4. The name of the most holy verse of the Rigv. (iii. 62, 11), Man. 2, 77; 11, 191.<BR> 5. The ceremony of investiture with the sacrificial string, Man. 2, 38.<BR> IV. n. The sacrificial string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साष्टाङ्गम्|साष्टांगम्
साष्टाङ्गम् साष्टाङ्गम्, i. e. स-अष्टन्-अङ्ग + म्, adv. With a humble prostration (touching the earth with eight parts of the body, viz. the forehead, breast, both shoulders, hands, and feet), Pañc. 33, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना सास्ना, f. The dewlap of an ox, Sāh. D. 10, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्य|साहचर्यं|साहचर्य्य|साहचर्य्यं
साहचर्य साहचर्य, i. e. सह-चर + य, n. Company, association, congregation, Mālat. 6, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस|साहसं|साहसः
साहस साहस, i. e. सहस् + अ, n. (and m., Man. 8, 138),<BR> 1. Violence, Man. 8, 345.<BR> 2. Oppression, cruelty, Śiś. 8, 59.<BR> 3. Punishment, Man. 8, 120.<BR> 4. Rape, ravishment.<BR> 5. Hatred.<BR> 6. Boldness, daring, Hit. ii. d. 3; Pañc. 135, 8; courage, Mālat. 75, 12.<BR> 7. Rashness, Hit. iii. d. 115; Hit. 100, 3.<BR> 8. Suicide, Pañc. 135, 6; Daśak. in Chr. 189, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमसाहस
विषम- + साहस विषम- + साहस, n. temerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक|साहसिकः
साहसिक साहसिक, adj., i. e. साहस + इक,<BR> I. adj., f. की.<BR> 1. Using force or violence, Man. 3, 344.<BR> 2. Rapacious.<BR> 3. Cruel, Mālat. 9, 5.<BR> 4. Inflicted as punishment.<BR> 5. Perpetrated by violence.<BR> 6. Bold, daring.<BR> 7. Rash, Mālat. 64, 4; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a " target="_blank">Page1042-a + 42</a>] impetuous.<BR> II. m. A robber, Pañc. i. d. 390.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसिक
अ- + साहसिक अ- + साहसिक, adj., f. की, being of a mild disposition, Śiś. 9, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाहसिक
अति- + साहसिक अति- + साहसिक, adj. very bold, daring, Pañc. 241, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमसाहसिक
अ-सम- + साहसिक अ-सम- + साहसिक, adj. who has not his match in boldness, Lass. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहसिक|महासाहसिकः
महा- + साहसिक महा- + साहसिक, m. 1. an assaulter. 2. a robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिकता
साहसिकता साहसिक + ता, f. in महा-, Great boldness, Pañc. 129, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र साहस्र, i. e. सहस्र + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating or belonging to a thousand.<BR> 2. Bought with a thousand.<BR> 3. Paid per thousand, as interest, duty.<BR> 4. A thousandfold, a thousand times better, Man. 2, 85.<BR> II. m. An army or detachment, a thousand strong.<BR> III. n. An aggregate of many thousands.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशसाहस्र
दशसाहस्र दशसाहस्र, i. e. दशन्-,<BR> I. adj. consisting of ten thousand, MBh. 4, 289.<BR> II. n. ten thousand, Hariv. 13900.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशसाहस्र
द्वादशसाहस्र द्वादशसाहस्र, i. e. द्वादशन्-, adj. consisting of twelve thousand, Man. 1, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसाहस्र
शत- + साहस्र शत- + साहस्र, adj. consisting of a hundred thousand, a hundred thousandfold, Man. 7, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहायक|साहायकं
साहायक साहायक, i. e. सहाय + क (? perhaps it is to be read साकाय्यक), n. Assistance, Rājat. 5, 307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्य|साहाय्यं
साहाय्य साहाय्य, i. e. सहाय + य, n.<BR> 1. Friendship.<BR> 2. Alliance.<BR> 3. Help. Pañc. ii. d. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्य|साहित्यं
साहित्य साहित्य, i. e. सहित + य,<BR> I. n., and f. हिति, Society, connexion, combination.<BR> II. n. Poetry, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वय|साह्वयः
साह्वय साह्वय, i. e. स-आह्वय, m. Fighting animals for sport or money.<BR> --Cf. आह्वय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सि
सि सि, ii. 5 and 9, Par. Ātm. To bind.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सित, Bound, surrounded, Chr. 296, 5 = Rigv. i. 112, 5; cf. s. v. सित.<BR> --With the prep. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b " target="_blank">Page1042-b + 39</a>] प्र प्र, प्रसित,<BR> 1. Bound.<BR> 2. Attached to.<BR> 3. Diligent, attentive.<BR> --Cf. सीमन्; σειρά; O.H.G. sail; A.S. sal, laqueus, sael, saelan, sieran, syrwan; Goth. in-sailjan, illaqueare; O.H.G. saito; A.S. sad, laqueus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंह|सिंहः
सिंह सिंह,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A lion, Pañc. 218, 22.<BR> 2. The sign Leo.<BR> 3. As latter part of comp. words, Preeminent; e. g. पुरुष-, m. (properly, a lion-like man), A hero, Hit. pr. d. 31, M.M. राजसिंह, i. e. राजन्-, m. A great king, Hit. iii. d. 121.<BR> II. f. ही, A lioness, Rām. 3, 53, 46; Pañc. 218, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहल|सिंहलं|सिंहलः
सिंहल सिंह + ल,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Tin.<BR> 2. Brass.<BR> 3. Cassia bark.<BR> II. n., and f. ला, Ceylon, Hit. 63, 10 (ल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहान|सिंहानं
सिंहान सिंहान, n.<BR> 1. Rust of iron.<BR> 2. The mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाय
सिंहाय सिंहाय, a denomin. derived from सिंह with य, Ātm. To behave like a lion, Hit. iii. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासनस्थ
सिंहासनस्थ सिंहासनस्थ, i. e. सिंह-आसन-स्थ, adj. Sitting on the throne, Pañc. 195, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका सिंहिका, i. e. सिंहि + क, f. The mother of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकत
सिकत सिकत,<BR> I. m. pl. Sand.<BR> II. f. ता.<BR> 1. Sandy soil.<BR> 2. Sand, Vikr. d. 79 (pl.); Pañc. ii. d. 62.<BR> 3. Gravel or stone (the disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतामय|सिकतामयं
सिकतामय सिकता + मय, adj., f. यी, सिकतावन्त् सिकता + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, and सिकतिल सिकतिल, i. e. सिकता + इल, adj. Sandy, Bhartṛ. 3, 49 (तिल, see Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2721).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थ|सिक्थं|सिक्थः
सिक्थ सिक्थ, i. e. सिच् + थ.<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Boiled rice.<BR> 2. A lump or ball of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-a " target="_blank">Page1043-a + 40</a>] boiled rice, Skanda P., Kāśīkh. 81, 38.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Beeswax.<BR> 2. Indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थक|सिक्थकं
सिक्थक सिक्थ + क, n. Beeswax.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसिक्थक|मधुसिक्थकः
मधु- + सिक्थक मधु- + सिक्थक, n. a sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
सिच् सिच्, i. 6, सिञ्च, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To sprinkle, MBh. 1, 8153.<BR> 2. To discharge, Man. 11, 170; with शुक्रम्, To lose semen, 2, 181.<BR> 3. To pour in, Bhartṛ. 2, 20.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, षिच्,<BR> 1. To besprinkle, Rām. 1, 38, 14; to wet, Pañc. 50, 9.<BR> 2. To pour upon, Megh. 49.<BR> 3. To inaugurate by sprinkling with sacred water, to initiate, Rām. 1, 1, 79; Vikr. d. 161. Ātm. To be inaugurated, MBh. 3, 14423.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be inaugurated, MBh. 1, 3117.<BR> --With अव अव, अव-सिक्त, Sprinkled, MBh. 1, 7730.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. To order to be dropped in, Man. 8, 272.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To make haughty, Ragh. 17, 43. उत्सिक्त,<BR> 1. Sprinkled.<BR> 2. Overflowing, abounding, Rām. 1, 21, 13.<BR> 3. Haughty, Kathās. 18, 86.<BR> 4. Mad, Man. 8, 71.<BR> --With नि नि, षिच्, To sprinkle, Vikr. d. 23; Ragh. 3, 26.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be sprinkled, Rām. 2, 63, 9.<BR> --With परि परि, षिच्,<BR> 1. To sprinkle round about, Pañc. iii. d. 26.<BR> 2. To sprinkle, MBh. 1, 4500.<BR> --With प्र प्र, i. 4, To flow away, MBh. 3, 14767. प्रसिक्त, Sprinkled, Utt. Rāmac. 58, 4.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संसिक्त,<BR> 1. Sprinkled, Rām. 1, 5, 8.<BR> 2. Moistened, Pañc. iii. d. 33.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. sîhan, colare, seihjan, mingere, probably Goth. saivs; O.H.G. seo, gi-sich; Lat. stilla (for stic-la; cf. strau in O.H.G. straum = Sskr. स्रो, vb. स्रु); στίλη, probably ἰκμάς, σίκυς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिचय|सिचयः
सिचय सिचय, m. Cloth, Vikr. d. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिट्
सिट् सिट्, see शिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित सित,<BR> I. (cf. सि and सो), adj. White, Vikr. d. 53; Pañc. 158, 3.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. White (the colour).<BR> 2. The light half of the month from new to full moon, Rājat. 5, 327.<BR> 3. The planet Venus.<BR> 4. An arrow.<BR> III. f. ता.<BR> 1. Candied sugar.<BR> 2. Moonlight.<BR> 3. A handsome woman.<BR> 4. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 5. The name of several plants.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Silver.<BR> 2. Sandal.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
अ- + सित अ- + सित, adj., f. ता and असिक्नी,<BR> I. adj. 1. black, Rām. 2, 96, 19. 2. the black half of the month from full to new moon, Pañc. ed. orn. i. d. 139..<BR> II. m. 1. black (the colour). 2. a proper name, MBh. 1, 106.<BR> III. f. ता, a proper name, Hariv. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितासित|सितासितः
सित-अ- + सित सित-अ- + सित,<BR> I. adj. white and black.<BR> II. m. a name of Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताभ्र|सिताभ्रः
सिताभ्र सिताभ्र, i. e. सित-अभ्र, m and n. (also सिताभ सिताभ, a dialect. form, m., and सिताभ्रक सिताभ्र + क, n.), Camphor (Indr. 1, 6, सिताभ्र, White clouds; MBh. 13, 836, शिताभ्र, White-clouded).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिमन्
सितिमन् सितिमन्, i. e. सित + इमन्, m. Whiteness, Śiś. 1, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्त|सिद्धांत|सिद्धान्तः
सिद्धान्त सिद्धान्त, i. e. सिद्ध-अन्त, m. Demonstrated conclusion, established truth, reliable doctrine; doctrine, Lass. 2. ed. 90, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थ|सिद्धार्थः
सिद्धार्थ सिद्धार्थ, i. e. सिद्ध-अर्थ,<BR> I. adj. One who has obtained his aim, Chr. 62, 60; successful.<BR> II. m. White mustard, Pañc. 158, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धार्थ
अ- + सिद्धार्थ अ- + सिद्धार्थ, adj. unfortunate, Rām. 3, 55, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धि|सिद्धिः
सिद्धि सिद्धि, i. e. सिध् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Accomplishment, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 4; Hit. ii. d. 13; fulfilment, Vikr. d. 28 (read अभिमुखिष्विव, in the ed. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a " target="_blank">Page1044-a + 46</a>] of Bollens).<BR> 2. Success, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3255; prosperity, well-being, Pañc. i. d. 432.<BR> 3. Use, Pañc. ii. d. 93 (न सिद्ध्यै, useless).<BR> 4. Final emancipation, supreme felicity, Man. 2, 93.<BR> 5. The fruit of the adoration of the gods or of ascetic austerities.<BR> 6. The acquisition of supernatural powers by magical means, magical power, Pañc. 241, 3.<BR> 7. A magical shoe, which is supposed to convey the bearer wherever he likes.<BR> 8. A medicinal root.<BR> 9. Indisputable conclusion, decision, Pañc. iii. d. 91.<BR> 10. Validity.<BR> 11. Knowledge, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 8; understanding, intellect, Rām. 5, 18, 13.<BR> 12. Acquittance, discharge (of debt).<BR> 13. Concealment.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धि|असिद्धिः
अ- + सिद्धि अ- + सिद्धि, f. 1. imperfect accomplishment, failure, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3255. 2. want of proof, conclusion not warranted by the premises, Bhāṣāp. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयासिद्धि|आश्रयासिद्धिः
आश्रय-अ- + सिद्धि आश्रय-अ- + सिद्धि, स्वरूप-अ-, व्याप्यत्व-अ-, f. forms of असिद्धि, or fallacious inference, Bhāṣāp. 74-76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसिद्धि
अति- + सिद्धि अति- + सिद्धि, f. excessive accomplishment, Rām. 4, 57, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धि|अन्यथासिद्धिः
अन्-यथा- + सिद्धि अन्-यथा- + सिद्धि, f. establishing wrongly, especially assigning superfluous causes, Bhāṣāp. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासिद्धि|महासिद्धिः
महा- + सिद्धि महा- + सिद्धि, f. magical power, Lass. 3, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसिद्धि|यज्ञसिद्धिः
यज्ञ- + सिद्धि यज्ञ- + सिद्धि, f. due performance of sacrifice, Man. 1, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्धि|रससिद्धिः
रस- + सिद्धि रस- + सिद्धि, f. knowledge of alchemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातसिद्धि|विघातसिद्धिः
वि-घात- + सिद्धि वि-घात- + सिद्धि, and विघ्न-, f. removing obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धि|साध्यसिद्धिः
साध्य- + सिद्धि साध्य- + सिद्धि, f. 1. completion. 2. establishing what is to be proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामसिद्धि
सामसिद्धि सामसिद्धि, i. e. सामन्-, f. the art of accomplishing something in a peaceable way, Pañc. 91, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
1. सिध् सिध् (i. e. probably सो-धा, cf. साध्), i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 12025),<BR> 1. To be accomplished, Pañc. i. d. 2.<BR> 2. To reach, Śāk. d. 38 (with loc.).<BR> 3. To attain one's aim, Pañc. i. d. 131.<BR> 4. To succeed, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 3.<BR> 5. To be established, Hit. 84, 17; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-b " target="_blank">Page1044-b + 47</a>] to be valid, Man. 8, 74; 163.<BR> 6. Pass. To be concluded, Bhāṣāp. 77.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सिद्ध.<BR> 1. Accomplished, Hit. i. d. 31, M.M. (प्रकृति-, by nature, i. e. natural; n. true nature, Bhartṛ. 2, 42); effected, settled, Pañc. i. d. 424.<BR> 2. Succeeded, Pañc. 44, 10; successful, Pañc. v. d. 77.<BR> 3. Liberated, emancipated.<BR> 4. Endowed with supernatural powers.<BR> 5. Prepared, compounded (in medicine).<BR> 6. Ready (as money), Hit. ii. d. 92.<BR> 7. Cooked, dressed, Man. 3, 84; Pañc. 116, 22.<BR> 8. Subdued, acquired, by magical power, Lass. 2. ed. 3, 3; Kathās. 18, 177; gained, Pañc. 250, 12.<BR> 9. Demonstrated, proved.<BR> 10. Judged, decided, Utt. Rāmac. 10, 8.<BR> 11. Valid, deemed right, Mālat. 160, 5.<BR> 12. Celebrated, famous.<BR> 13. Shining, splendid.<BR> 14. Eternal.<BR> 15. Initiated in alchemy or magic, magical, Pañc. 241, 6.<BR> 16. Discharged, settled (as a debt). m.<BR> 1. A sort of demigod, Pañc. 242, 5.<BR> 2. A wise man, Hit. ii. d. 98.<BR> 3. An ascetic who has attained one or all of his purposes.<BR> 4. A magician, Pañc. 242, 21. n. Sea salt.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. सेधय and साधय, see साध्.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To be acquired, Man. 11, 237.<BR> 2. To succeed, Bhag. 3, 8.<BR> 3. To be known, Man. 12, 97. प्रसिद्ध,<BR> 1. Celebrated, famous, Pañc. 127, 20; Lass. 49, 17.<BR> 2. Known, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 11.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a " target="_blank">Page1045-a + 40</a>] Adorned.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To attain beatitude, Man. 2, 87. संसिद्ध, One who has attained beatitude, Lass. 49, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
अ- + सिद्ध अ- + सिद्ध, adj. 1. unaccomplished. 2. imperfect. 3. unproven. 4. unripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्ध
अन्यथा- + सिद्ध अन्यथा- + सिद्ध, adj. wrongly established, especially used of superfluous causes, Bhāṣāp. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्ध
रस- + सिद्ध रस- + सिद्ध,<BR> I. adj. accomplished in poetry, Bhartṛ. 2, 21.<BR> II. m. an alchemist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहितसिद्ध
अ-वि-हित- + सिद्ध अ-वि-हित- + सिद्ध (vb. ध), adj. not artificial, innate, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पसिद्ध
संकल्प- + सिद्ध संकल्प- + सिद्ध, adj. endowed with supernatural powers by energy, Chr. 58, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णसिद्ध|सुवर्णसिद्धः
सुवर्ण- + सिद्ध सुवर्ण- + सिद्ध, m. an adept who has acquired gold (by magical means), Pañc. 243, 1, sqq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
2. सिध् सिध्, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 15643),<BR> 1. To command.<BR> 2. To restrain, Lass. 101, 1 = Rigv. vii. 15, 10.<BR> 3. To ordain.<BR> 4. † To do an auspicious act.<BR> 5. † To go. सिद्ध, see s. v. 1. सिध्.<BR> --With the prep. अप अप, To remove, Man. 11, 198.<BR> --With नि नि, षिध्,<BR> 1. To remove, Rājat. 5, 56.<BR> 2. To prohibit, MBh. 1, 279.<BR> 3. To forbid, Man. 8, 361; Pañc. 160, 25.<BR> --Caus. To prohibit, Pañc. 160, 25.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, षिध्,<BR> 1. To prevent, Pañc. 171, 25.<BR> 2. To restrain, Man. 2, 206.<BR> 3. To forbid, Man. 8, 361.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To restrain, MBh. 1, 1594.<BR> 2. To keep off, Chr. 31, 9.<BR> --With विप्रति वि-प्रति, विप्रतिषिद्ध, Contradicted, containing contradiction, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्म|सिध्मं
सिध्म सिध्म, and सिध्मन् सिध्मन्, n. Leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल सिध्म + ल, and सिध्मवन्त् सिध्म + वन्त्, adj. Affected with leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्य|सिध्यः
सिध्य सिध्य, m. The asterism Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र सिध् + र, adj. Perfect, good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रकावण|सिध्रकावणं
सिध्रकावण सिध्रकावण, i. e. सिध्र + क-वन, n. One of the celestial gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनीवाली
सिनीवाली सिनीवाली, f. A name of the day of new moon, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. lviii. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुक|सिंदुक|सिंदुकः|सिन्दुकः
सिन्दुक सिन्दुक (probably vb. स्यन्द्), m. A small tree,. Vitex negundo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुवार|सिंदुवार|सिंदुवारः|सिन्दुवारः
सिन्दुवार सिन्दुवार (cf. सिन्दुक), m. A small tree, Vitex negundo, Pañc. 105, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूर|सिंदूर|सिन्दूरं|सिंदूरः|सिन्दूरः
सिन्दूर सिन्दूर (vb. स्यन्द् ?),<BR> I. m. A sort of tree.<BR> II. f. री.<BR> 1. Red clothes.<BR> 2. The name of two plants.<BR> III. n. Red lead, minium, Ṛt. 1, 24; Kathās. 23, 78 (red colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धु|सिंधु|सिंधुः|सिन्धुः
सिन्धु सिन्धु (probably from vb. स्यन्द्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The Indus, Rājat. 5, 215.<BR> 2. The ocean, Pañc. i. d. 117.<BR> 3. The country along the Indus; m. pl. Its inhabitants, Draup. 1, 6.<BR> 4. The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples.<BR> 5. An elephant.<BR> II. f. A river in general, Śāk. d. 117; Rājat. 5, 112.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युसिन्धु
द्यु- + सिन्धु द्यु- + सिन्धु, f. the Gaṅgā, Kathās. 4, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिन्धु|सोमसिंधु|सोमसिन्धुः
सोम- + सिन्धु सोम- + सिन्धु, m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुज|सिंधुज|सिन्धुजं|सिन्धुजः
सिन्धुज सिन्धु-ज,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. River or sea-born.<BR> 2. Born in Sindhu.<BR> II. n. Rock-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुर|सिंधुर|सिंधुरः|सिन्धुरः
सिन्धुर सिन्धु + र, m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्व्
सिन्व् सिन्व्, see निन्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिप्र|सिप्रं|सिप्रः
सिप्र सिप्र,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Perspiration, sweat.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR> II. f. रा.<BR> 1. A woman's zone.<BR> 2. A female buffalo.<BR> 3. A river near Oujein, Pañc. 240, 11; Megh. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिभ्
सिभ् सिभ्, see सृभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम|सिमः
सिम सिम (akin to सम), adj. Every, all, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्भ्
सिम्भ् सिम्भ्, see सृम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिर|सिरः
सिर सिर (vb. सि ?),<BR> I. m. The root of long pepper.<BR> II. f. रा.<BR> 1. Any tubular vessel of the body, as a vein, a nerve, Suśr. 1, 267, 13.<BR> 2. A bucket a baling vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिल्
सिल् सिल्, see शिल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिव्
सिव् सिव्, i. 4, सीव्य, Par.<BR> 1. To sew.<BR> 2. To unite, Utt. Rāmac. 128, 5.<BR> --Ptcple. cf. the pf. pass. स्यूत.<BR> 1. Sewn, Mālat. 77, 4; stitched, joined, made, Prab. 116, 8.<BR> 2. Pierced by a fishing-book.<BR> --With the prep. अनु अनु, अनुस्यूत,<BR> 1. Sewn on (cf. अनुस्यूतत्व).<BR> 2. Closely attached to.<BR> 3. Uninterrupted.<BR> --Cf. सि; Goth. siujan; A.S. siwian; O.H.G. siut, suila, saum; A.S. seam, limbus; O.N. saumr, sutura; Lat. suere, Con-sus, Con-sualia; κασ-σύω, probably ὑμήν and Ὑμήν (cf. सीवनी, s. v. सीवन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषा
सिषाधयिषा सिषाधयिषा, i. e. सिस्काधयिष, desider. of the causal of साध् and सिध्, + अ, f. Wish or purpose to effect, to prove, Bhāṣāp. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षा
सिसृक्षा सिसृक्षा, i. e. सिसृक्ष, desider. of सृज्, + अ, f. Wish or purpose to create, Man. 1, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षु
सिसृक्षु सिसृक्षु, i. e. सिसृक्ष, desider. of सृज्, + उ, adj. Wishing or purposing to create, Man. 1, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्
सीक् सीक्, see 1. 2. शीक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीकर|सीकरः
सीकर सीकर, see शीकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीता
सीता सीता (vb. सि), f.<BR> 1. A furrow, the track of the ploughshare.<BR> 2. Husbandry, Man. 9, 293.<BR> 3. Name of a goddess, wife of Indra, presiding over fruits, etc., Pāraskara Gṛ. S. in Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 538, 17.<BR> 4. The wife of Rāma, Rām. 5, 48, 19.<BR> 5. Lakṣmī.<BR> 6. Umā.<BR> 7. One of the fabulous branches of the Gaṅgā.<BR> 8. Spirituous liquor.<BR> --Cf. सीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्
सीत् सीत् (cf. शीत्), an imitative sound, expressing sighing, shivering with cold, murmuring, Rājat. 1, 213; cf. Nalod. 2, 62, Sch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्य|सीत्यं
सीत्य सीत्य, i. e. सीत + य,<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b " target="_blank">Page1046-b + 40</a>] Tilled, ploughed.<BR> II. n. Corn, grain.<BR> --Cf. probably σῖτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीद
सीद सीद, see 1. सद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधु|सीधुः
सीधु सीधु, m. Spirit distilled from molasses, Ṛt. 6, 33; Indr. 5, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्
सीमन् सीमन्, i. e. सि or सिव् + मन्, and सीमा सीमा, f.<BR> 1. A boundary, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 461; a limit, a landmark, Man. 8, 149; 255; Pañc. i. d. 104 (मन् and मा); skirt, Utt. Rāmac. 43, 6 (मन्).<BR> 2. Observance of due bounds in morals, Bhaṭṭ. 1, 6; Nalod. 3, 28.<BR> 3. A field.<BR> 4. The nape of the neck.<BR> 5. The scrotum.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἵμας; O.S. sîmo, laqueus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसीमन्
निःसीमन् निःसीमन्, i. e. निस्-, adj. boundless, Bhartṛ. 2, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त|सीमंत|सीमंतः|सीमन्तः
सीमन्त सीमन्त, i. e. *सीमन्त्, the original form of सीमन्, + अ,<BR> I. m. A separation of the hair on each side, so as to leave a distinct line on the top of the head, Megh. 66.<BR> II. m. and n. The head.<BR> III. m. or n. A landmark (?), Lass. 41, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तित|सीमंतित
सीमन्तित सीमन्तित, i. e. ptcple. pf. pass. of a denomin. सीमन्तय, derived from सीमन्त, Marked by a line, Kir. 4, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तिनी|सीमंतिनी
सीमन्तिनी सीमन्तिनी, i. e. सीमन्त + इन् + ई, f. A woman, Hit. ii. d. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमा
सीमा सीमा, see सीमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर|सीरः
सीर सीर (vb. सि, cf. सीता), m.<BR> 1. A plough, Megh. 16.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरिन्
सीरिन् सीरिन्, i. e. सीर + इन्, m. Baladeva, Śiś. 2, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धसीरिन्
अर्ध- + सीरिन् अर्ध- + सीरिन्, i. e. अर्धसीर + इन्, m. A cultivator who takes half the crop for his labour, Yājñ. 1, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीवन|सीवनं
सीवन सीवन, i. e. सिव् + अन,<BR> I. n. Sewing, stitching.<BR> II. f. नी, The frenum of the prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीस|सीसं
सीस सीस, सीसक सीस + क, and सीसपत्रक सीस-पत्र + क, n. Lead, Man. 5, 114 (सक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
1. सु सु, i. 1, and ii. 2, Par., and सू सू, ii. 4, सुय (properly pass. refl. of सु), and ii. 2, Ātm.<BR> 1. To beget, Man. 10, 32.<BR> 2. To bear, to bring forth, Man. 10, 39; Pañc. pr. d. 5. ii. 5, सुनु, Par. Ātm. (the act of expressing the Soma juice being compared to the act of generating, cf. Rigv. i. 28), To express the Soma juice, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. सुत,<BR> 1. m. A son, Pañc. i. d. 185.<BR> 2. f. ता, A daughter, Chr. 3, 9.<BR> 3. m. pl. Children, Man. 2, 28.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, षु,<BR> 1. To express the Soma juice, Rām. 1, 13, 5 (cf. Schlegel's translation).<BR> 2. To extract juice, Man. 5, 10.<BR> 3. To sprinkle, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 90.<BR> --With उद् उद्, ii. 5, To agitate, Bhāg. P. 3, 20, 35 (cf. 2. सू).<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To beget, Man. 10, 30. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-b " target="_blank">Page1047-b + 44</a>]<BR> 2. To bring forth, Man. 4, 44.<BR> 3. Pass. To be brought forth, Man. 10, 36; with the termination of the Par. (i. 4, Par.), MBh. 12, 5687. प्रसूत,<BR> 1. Engendered, Hit. pr. d. 23, M.M.<BR> 2. Born, Pañc. 45, 2.<BR> 3. Produced, Chr. 294, 8 = Rigv. i. 92, 8.<BR> 4. Engendering, Man. 3, 19.<BR> 5. Having brought forth, delivered, Hit. 72, 14; Utt. Rāmac. 52, 1 (she has brought forth).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र,<BR> 1. To beget, Man. 10, 33.<BR> 2. Pass. To be brought forth, MBh. 3, 12978 (with the termination of the Par.).<BR> --Cf. ὕω, υἱός, ὑστέρα; Goth. sunus; A.S. sunu (cf. सूनु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसुता
गिरि- + सुता गिरि- + सुत, f. ता, Pārvatī, Pañc. i. d. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नुसुता
जह्नु- + सुता जह्नु- + सुत, f. ता, the Gaṅgā, MBh. 1, 3913.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसुत
जीव- + सुत जीव- + सुत, adj. one who has living children, Bhāg. P. 6, 19, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारसुत
दार- + सुत दार- + सुत, m. wife and son, Yājñ. 2, 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीसुत|दासीसुतः
दासी- + सुत दासी- + सुत, m. a base man, Rājat. 5, 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसुत|धर्म्मसुत|धर्म्मसुतः
धर्म- + सुत धर्म- + सुत, m. (the son of the god Dharma), epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुत|भूसुतः
भू- + सुत भू- + सुत and मही-, m. the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुसुत|भृगुसुतः
भृगु- + सुत भृगु- + सुत, m. 1. Śukra or Venus. 2. Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधासुत|राधासुतः
राधा- + सुत राधा- + सुत, m. Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलसुता
शैल- + सुता शैल- + सुत, f. ता, Pārvatī, Vikr. d. 128.<BR> II. सूल,<BR> 1. Engendered.<BR> 2. Born. f. ता,<BR> 1. A daughter, Pañc. 181, 5.<BR> 2. A woman lying in; see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरसुत|सूरसुतः
सूर- + सुत सूर- + सुत, m. Aruṇa, the dawn.<BR> III. सून,<BR> 1. Born, produced.<BR> 2. Blown, budded (as a flower). m. A son, Pañc. 198, 2. f. ना, A daughter. n.<BR> 1. Bringing forth, parturition.<BR> 2. A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
अ- + सुत अ- + सुत, adj. one who has not brought forth, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 809.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसुत
कुल- + सुत कुल- + सुत, adj. descended from a respectable family, Pañc. pr. d. 6. प्रसून, Born, produced. n.<BR> 1. A bud, a blossom, Utt. Rāmac. 129, 12; flower, Mālat. 57, 13.<BR> 2. Fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विससुत
विस- + सुत विस- + सुत, n. a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
2. सु सु, i. 1, and ii. 2, Par. † To possess power or supremacy (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
3. सु सु, i. 1, Par. Ātm. † To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
4. सु सु (for original वसु, cf. εὖ, ἐΰς; ἐάων = Zend. वङ्ह्व्ãम् = Sskr. *वस्वाम्),<BR> I. adv. ved. Beautifully, Chr. 296, 1 = Rigv. i. 112, 1.<BR> II. Very seldom combined and compounded with a verbum finitum; e. g. Pañc. i. d. 205, but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 647; but very often with nouns,<BR> 1. Good, well, Rām. 3, 53, 6; Ṛt. 6, 2; Lass. 15, 5.<BR> 2. Beautiful, beautifully, Rām. 3, 52, 35.<BR> 3. Much, very, Chr. 4, 12.<BR> 4. Easily, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 2. Comparat. सुतराम्,<BR> 1. Better.<BR> 2. With न, Very badly, Pañc. 199, 24; with मा, In no way, Megh. 108.<BR> 3. More, Śiś. 9, 67; Pañc. 163, 3.<BR> 4. Exceedingly, Śiś. 9, 55.<BR> 5. Consequently, of course.<BR> --Cf. εὖ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकालिन्
सुकालिन् सुकालिन्, probably सु -2. काल + इन्, m. pl. The Manes of the Śūdras, Man. 3, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृत्
सुकृत् सु-कृ + त्, adj.<BR> 1. Virtuous, pious, Chr. 294, 3 = Rigv. i. 92, 3; Pañc. ii. d. 170.<BR> 2. Fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्
सुख् सुख्, i. 10, सुखय (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To make happy, to comfort, Megh. 86; to delight, Vikr. d. 61; MBh. 3, 181; Hit. i. d. 96, M.M. सुखित (ptcple. pf. pass., or सुख + इत), Pleased, Vikr. 59, 1; happy, Śāk. d. 99. n. Happiness, Mālav. 33, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख सु-ख,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Happy.<BR> 2. Joyful, Ṛt. 6, 2.<BR> 3. Agreeable, sweet, Chr. 16, 15; Rām. 3, 55, 45.<BR> 4. Virtuous, pious.<BR> 5. Easy, Pañc. 211, 10.<BR> II. खम्, adv.<BR> 1. And सुखेन, Joyfully, Nal. 17, 18; Pañc. 53, 7; iii. d. 79; well, Pañc. iii. d. 164; Vikr. 65, 17 (सुखम् आस्तां भवान्, Farewell).<BR> 2. Placidly, Man. 1, 54.<BR> 3. Willingly, Bhartṛ. 2, 49; Indr. 4, 18; with following न पुनर्, Rather...than, Bhartṛ. 2, 100 (तेजस्विनः सुखम् असून् अपि संत्यजन्ति...न पुनः प्रतिज्ञाम्, The virtuous renounce even life rather than break a promise).<BR> 4. And सुखेन, Easily, Bhartṛ. 2, 3; Pañc. 52, 20; 48, 2.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. Happiness, Pañc. 184, 2.<BR> 2. Joy, MBh. 12, 12427.<BR> 3. Pleasure, Vikr. d. 49; Pañc. 216, 10; alleviation, Pañc. iv. d. 19.<BR> 4. Easiness, see<BR> II.<BR> 4. 5. Paradise.<BR> 6. Water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
अ- + सुख अ- + सुख,<BR> I. adj. 1. unhappy, MBh. 1, 3984. 2. difficult, Kir. 5, 49.<BR> II. n. distress, Pañc. ii. d. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश्यसुख
अ-निर्देश्य- + सुख अ-निर्देश्य- + सुख (vb. दिश्), adj. having inexpressible pleasure, Vikr. d. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसुख
अन्तःसुख अन्तःसुख, i. e. अन्तर्-, adj. one who derives his happiness from his soul, Bhag. 5, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसुख
ग्राम- + सुख ग्राम- + सुख and ग्राम्य-, n. pleasure of common people, sexual intercourse, MBh. 5, 3225; 3226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसुख
निस्- + सुख निस्- + सुख, adj. sad, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b " target="_blank">Page1048-b + 39</a>] MBh. 5, 2379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथासुखम्
यथा-सुख + म् यथा-सुख + म्, adv. 1. happily, Hit. 95, 1, M.M. 2. willingly, Nal. 23, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखद|सुखदं|सुखदः
सुखद सुख-द,<BR> I. adj. Affording pleasure, Pañc. ii. d. 2.<BR> II. f. दा, A courtesan of Indra's heaven.<BR> III. n. The seat of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखमय
सुखमय सुख + मय, adj., f. यी, Full, or consisting of happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखस्थ
सुखस्थ सुख-स्थ (vb. स्था), adj. Happy, Pañc. i. d. 406.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिन्
सुखिन् सुखिन्, i. e. सुख + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Happy, Pañc. 262, 10.<BR> 2. Glad, Hit. 78, 3.<BR> 3. Pleasant.<BR> 4. Comfortable (corpulent), Hit. 106, 16.<BR> II. m. A religious ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोद्य
सुखोद्य सुखोद्य, i. e. सुख-उद्य (ptcple. of the fut. pass. of वद्), adj. To be uttered agreeably, Man. 2, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग|सुगं|सुगः
सुग सु-ग,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Going well.<BR> 2. Graceful.<BR> 3. Well rid of.<BR> 4. Plain, intelligible.<BR> 5. Easy of access, Pañc. ii. d. 151.<BR> II. n. Fæces, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगोपा
सुगोपा सु-गोपा (गोपा, ved. = गोप), adj. Having a good protector, Chr. 292, 1 = Rigv. i. 86, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्म्य
सुग्म्य सुग्म्य, i. e. सु-गम् + अ + य, adj. Yielding happiness, Chr. 288, 13 = Rigv. i. 48, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचेलक|सुचेलकः
सुचेलक सु-चेल + क, m. Cloth or fine cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनता
सुजनता सु-जन + ता, f., सुजनत्व सु-जन + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Goodness, Bhartṛ. 2, 99 (उप याति सुजनताम्, becomes a good person, a friend).<BR> 2. Benevolence, Bhartṛ. 2, 80 (ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुट्ट्
† सुट्ट् सुट्ट्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To disregard.<BR> 2. To be small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवन्त्|सुतवत्
सुतवन्त् सुत + वन्त् (vb. 1. सु),<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a " target="_blank">Page1049-a + 41</a>] adj. Having children.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The father of a son.<BR> 2. A drinker of the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिन्
सुतिन् सुतिन्, i. e. सुत + इन् (vb. 1. सु),<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Having a child or children, Pañc. pr. d. 7.<BR> II. m. A father.<BR> III. f. नी, A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्वन्
सुत्वन् सु + त्वन्, m.<BR> 1. An offerer or drinker of the Soma juice, Bhaṭṭ. 4, 12, Sch.<BR> 2. A student who has performed his ablutions subsequent or preparatory to a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदानु
सुदानु सु-दा + नु, adj. Munificent, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदामन्
सुदामन् सु-दा + मन्, m.<BR> 1. A cloud.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. The sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदास्
सुदास् सुदास्, and (but wrongly) सुदास सुदास, m. The name of a king, Chr. 297, 19 = Rigv. i. 112, 19; Man. 7, 41 (cf. Lois.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्तर|सुदुस्तरः
सुदुस्तर सुदुस्तर, i. e. सु-दुस्-तॄ + अ, adj. Very difficult to be crossed, Hit. i. d. 4, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधा
सुधा सु-धा, and -धे + अ, f.<BR> 1. Plaster, mortar, Rām. 2, 80, 13; Daśak. in Chr. 199, 18.<BR> 2. A brick, Chr. 57, 22.<BR> 3. The beverage of the gods, nectar, Pañc. v. d. 42.<BR> 4. The nectar of flowers.<BR> 5. Juice.<BR> 6. Water.<BR> 7. Lightning.<BR> 8. The name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाद्रव|सुधाद्रवः
सुधाद्रव सुधाद्रव, a denomin. derived from सुधा-द्रव, Par. To flow like nectar, Lass. 67, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामय|सुधामयः
सुधामय सुधा + मय,<BR> I. adj., f. यी,<BR> 1. Made of plaster.<BR> 2. Consisting of nectar.<BR> II. m. A palace, a mansion, a brick or stone building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहर|सुधाहरः
सुधाहर सुधा-हर, and सुधाहृत् सुधा-हृ + त्, m. Garuḍa, a fabulous bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाशीर|सुनाशीरः
सुनाशीर सुनाशीर, and सुनासीर सुनासीर, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्द|सुंदः|सुन्दः
सुन्द सुन्द, m. A proper name, Rām. 3, 48, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दर|सुंदर|सुन्दरं|सुन्दरः
सुन्दर सुन्दर,<BR> I. adj., f. री, Handsome, Pañc. 184, 14; Draup. 1, 15; charming, Kathās. 22, 103; right, Pañc. 130, 4; 164, 11. Comparat. ˚रतर + म्, adv. Very well, Pañc. 88, 15.<BR> II. m. Kāma, the god of love.<BR> III. f. री.<BR> 1. A handsome woman, Rām. 3, 52, 29.<BR> 2. Turmeric.<BR> 3. A small timber tree, Heritiera minor.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्दर
अ- + सुन्दर अ- + सुन्दर, adj. disagreeable, Hit. ii. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसुन्दर
अति- + सुन्दर अति- + सुन्दर, adj., f. री, very beautiful, Draup. 1, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसुन्दरी|सुरसुंदरी
सुर- + सुन्दरी सुर- + सुन्दर, f. री, an Apsaras or courtesan of heaven, Kir. 5, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरलोकसुन्दरी
सुर-लोक- + सुन्दरी सुर-लोक- + सुन्दर, f. री, 1. a celestial woman, Vikr. d. 21. 2. a name of Durgā, Rājat. 5, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दरक
सुन्दरक सुन्दर + क, m. A proper name, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दरंमन्य
सुन्दरंमन्य सुन्दरंमन्य, i. e. सुन्दर + म्-मन् + य, adj. Thinking himself handsome, Daśak. in Chr. 195, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपिश्
सुपिश् सु-पिश्, adj. Graceful, Chr. 290, 8 = Rigv. i. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्ति|सुप्तिः
सुप्ति सुप्ति, i. e. स्वप् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Sleeping, sleep.<BR> 2. Drowsiness.<BR> 3. Numbness, insensibility.<BR> 4. Confidence, trust.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसुप्ति|समसुप्तिः
सम- + सुप्ति सम- + सुप्ति, f. universal sleep, the end of a Kalpa, and destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभ्
सुभ् सुभ्, sec 2. शुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाषितमय
सुभाषितमय सु-भाषित + मय, i. e. (vb. भाष्), + मय, adj. Consisting in fine speeches, Pañc. ii. d. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभ्रु|सुभ्रुः
सुभ्रु सुभ्रु, see भ्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम|सुमं|सुमः
सुम सुम, probably 1. सु + म (cf. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a " target="_blank">Page1050-a + 40</a>] सून, प्रसून, s. v. 1. सु), n. A flower, Cāṇ. 24 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमर
सुमर सुमर, i. e. सु-मृ + अ, adj. Easy to die, Rām. 2, 57, 20 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्न|सुम्नं
सुम्न 4. सु + म्न, n. A hymn.<BR> --Cf. ὕμνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्नयु|सुम्नयुः
सुम्नयु सुम्नयु, i. e. सुम्न + य, a ved. denomin., + उ, m. A chanter of hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्भ्
सुम्भ् सुम्भ्, see 2. शुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयन्त्रितत्व
सुयन्त्रितत्व सु-यन्त्रित + त्व (vb. यन्त्र्), n. State of being well bound, Pañc. 146, 25 (cf. my transl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयोधन|सुयोधनः
सुयोधन सुयोधन, i. e. सु-युध् + अन, m. A name of Duryodhana (easy to be fought), Hiḍ. 4, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुय्य
सुय्य सुय्य,<BR> I. m. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 72.<BR> II. f. या, A proper name, ib. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर्
† सुर् सुर्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To possess superhuman power.<BR> 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर|सुरः
सुर सुर, i. e. 2. स्वर् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Pañc. iii. d. 69.<BR> 2. A god, Pañc. iii. d. 211; Vikr. d. 48.<BR> 3. A sage.<BR> II. f. रा and री.<BR> 1. Spirituous liquor, Pañc. i. d. 338 (रा).<BR> 2. A drinking vessel.<BR> 3. A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्विष्
सुरद्विष् सुर-द्विष्, m. An Asura or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभि|सुरभिः
सुरभि सु-रभ् + इ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fragrant, Vikr. d. 105; sweet-smelling.<BR> 2. Pleasing.<BR> 3. Handsome.<BR> 4. Friendly.<BR> 5. Good.<BR> 6. Wise.<BR> 7. Celebrated.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A fragrance, a perfume.<BR> 2. Spring, Kir. 10, 30.<BR> 3. The month Caitra (March--April).<BR> 4. Resin.<BR> 5. The Michelia Champaca.<BR> 6. Nutmeg.<BR> III. f. भी̆.<BR> 1. The earth.<BR> 2. The cow of plenty, Lass. 2. ed. 89, 36 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b " target="_blank">Page1050-b + 41</a>] (ĭ); Megh. 46.<BR> 3. A cow.<BR> 4. Spirituous liquor.<BR> 5. The name of several plants.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Gold.<BR> 2. Sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिकन्दर
सुरभिकन्दर सुरभि-कन्दर, m. Name of a mountain, Vikr. 65, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभित
सुरभित सुरभित, i. e. सुरभि + इत, adj. Perfumed, Megh. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराप|सुरापः
सुराप सुरा-प (vb. 1. पा), adj., f. पी, Drinking spirits, one who habitually drinks spirits, Man. 5, 90; Pañc. iv. d. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरासव|सुरासवः
सुरासव सुरासव, i. e. सुरा-आसव, n. Spirituous liquor, MBh. 13, 4737.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुङ्गा|सुरुंगा
सुरुङ्गा सुरुङ्गा (borrowed from σύριγξ), f. A hole made underground, or through the walls of a building, a mine, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुच्
सुरुच् सु-रुच्, adj. Very shining, Chr. 296, 1 = Rigv. i. 112, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्रवती
सुरेन्द्रवती सुरेन्द्रवती, i. e. सुर-इन्द्र + वन्त् + ई, f. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलभ|सुलभः
सुलभ सु-लभ् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Of easy acquisition, easy to be found, Pañc. ii. d. 171; easy to be got, Pañc. iii. d. 262; easy to be perceived, Vikr. d. 26.<BR> 2. Easy to be effected.<BR> 3. Easy.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
अ- + सुलभ अ- + सुलभ, adj. not easy to be obtained, Vikr. 19, 2; Hit. i. d. 184, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्चल
सुवर्चल सु-वर्च् + अल,<BR> I. m. A country so named.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. The wife of the sun.<BR> 2. Linseed.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसुवर्चला|ब्रह्मसुवर्च्चला
ब्रह्मसुवर्चला ब्रह्मसुवर्चला, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, f. a plant, an infusion of which is used as an expiatory means, Man. 11, 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्चस|सुवर्चसः
सुवर्चस सु-वर्चस् + अ, adj. Shining brightly, Sāv. 5, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णमय
सुवर्णमय सु-वर्ण + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Pañc. 192, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद|सुविदः
सुविद सु-विद् + अ, m. A guard or attendant on the womens' apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदत्र
सुविदत्र सु-विद् + अत्र, n. A household.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदल्ल|सुविदल्लं|सुविदल्लः
सुविदल्ल सुविदल्ल,<BR> I. n. A haram.<BR> II. f. ला, A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवृक्ति|सुवृक्तिः
सुवृक्ति सुवृक्ति, i. e. सु-वृज् + ति, f. A hymn, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. i. 64, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशंस
सुशंस सु-शंस् + अ, adj. Well-praising, a good praiser, Lass. 101, 15 = Rigv. vii. 16, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशमी
सुशमी सु-शम् + ई (?), m. A good acquirer (?), Lass. 101, 6 (so to be read instead of सुशर्मा) = Rigv. vii. 16, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीम|सुशीमः
सुशीम सुशीम, see सुषीम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषंसद्
सुषंसद् सुषंसद्, i. e. सु-संसद्, adj. Endowed with a comfortable house, Chr. 296, 7 = Rigv. i. 112, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषम|सुषमः
सुषम सुषम, i. e. सु-सम,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Same, even.<BR> 2. Beautiful.<BR> 3. All.<BR> II. f. मा, Exquisite beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषि|सुषिः
सुषि सुषि, सुषिर सुषिर = शुषि, शुषिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषीम|सुषीमः
सुषीम सुषीम, also (better, cf. शीत),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीम|सुशीमः
सुशीम सुशीम,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cold.<BR> 2. Pleasant.<BR> 3. Intense, Daśak. 106, 6, cf. Wils., n.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Cold.<BR> 2. The moon gem.<BR> 3. A sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्त|सुषुप्तं
सुषुप्त सुषुप्त, i. e. सु-सुप्त (vb. स्वप्), adj. Fast asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्ति|सुषुप्तिः
सुषुप्ति सुषुप्ति, i. e. सु-सुप्ति, f. Deep sleep, insensibility, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुम्णा
सुषुम्णा सुषुम्णा, f. An artery, Bhāg. P. 2, 2, 24 (Sch.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्टुति
सुष्टुति सुष्टुति, i. e. सु-स्तुति. f. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b " target="_blank">Page1051-b + 41</a>] beautiful hymn, Lass. 99, 5 = Rigv. iii. 62, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्ठु
सुष्ठु सुष्ठु, i. e. सु-स्था + उ, adv.<BR> 1. Well, Hit. 73, 21; Vikr. 60, 6; excellently.<BR> 2. Much, very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थ|सुस्थः
सुस्थ सु-स्थ (vb. स्था), adj.<BR> 1. Being well, healthy, Hit. iii. d. 119; Man. 4, 142.<BR> 2. Happy, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुह्
† सुह् सुह्, (in signification 1, 2, for सुख्, q. cf.), i. 4, Par.<BR> 1. To satisfy, to delight.<BR> 2. To be pleased.<BR> 3. To bear, to endure (cf. सह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृत्ता
सुहृत्ता सुहृत्ता, i. e. सु-हृद् + ता, f. Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुह्म
सुह्म सुह्म, m. pl. Name of a people, Ragh. 4, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
1. सू सू, see 1. सु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
2. सू सू, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To cast, to send.<BR> 2. To incite, to impel.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सूत.<BR> 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR> 2. Gone, departed, Pañc. 176, 4; see s. v.; see 1. सु with उद्.<BR> --Cf. perhaps σεύω, σοῦμαι; Lat. sævus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
3. सू सू,<BR> A. (1. सू),<BR> I. f. Birth.<BR> II. As latter part of comp. words,<BR> 1. Bringing forth, yielding; e. g. काम-, adj. Yielding wishes, Ragh. 5, 33.<BR> 2. A father. कुमार-, m. A name of Agni, father of Kumāra, the god of war, MBh. 2, 1148.<BR> 3. One who has brought forth. जीव-, adj. f. One who has borne a living child, MBh. 1, 7353. f. A mother. विचित्रवीर्य-, f. The mother of Vicitravīrya.<BR> B. (2. सू), in स-असु-, adj. Having arrows, Kir. 15, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक|सूकः
सूक 2. सू + क, m.<BR> 1. An arrow.<BR> 2. Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूकर|सूकरः
सूकर सू-कर,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A hog (see शूकर).<BR> 2. The hog-deer.<BR> 3. A potter.<BR> II. f. री, A sort of moss, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a " target="_blank">Page1052-a + 42</a>] Lycopodium imbricatum.<BR> --With the first part cf. Lat. sus; σῦς, ὗς, σύαινα; O.H.G. sû; A.S. sugu; Goth. svein; A.S. swin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्त|सूक्तं
सूक्त सूक्त, i. e. सु-उक्त (vb. वच्),<BR> I. adj. Well or properly said.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A hymn.<BR> 2. A sentence, Pañc. 266, 5.<BR> 3. pl. Seducing words, MBh. 8, 2037.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ति|सूक्तिः
सूक्ति सूक्ति, i. e. सु-उक्ति, f. Kind speech, Rājat. 5, 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्म|सूक्ष्मं|सूक्ष्मः
सूक्ष्म सूक्ष्म, i. e. perhaps सु-क्षाम (but cf. also सूच्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Little, small, Pañc. i. d. 254; Bhartṛ. 2, 90.<BR> 2. Atomic, atom-like, Man. 1, 7; 22.<BR> 3. Fine, delicate, tender, Rām. 3, 49, 3; 52, 9; Pañc. i. d. 395.<BR> 4. Subtle, exact, Pañc. 62, 12. ˚मम्, adv. Attentively, Utt. Rāmac. 154, 10.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An atom.<BR> 2. Clearingnut plant, Strychnos potatorum.<BR> III. f. मा.<BR> 1. A kind of jasmine.<BR> 2. Small cardamoms.<BR> 3. A sort of perfume.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Fine thread.<BR> 2. The supreme soul.<BR> 3. Subtlety, craft.<BR> 4. Fraud.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसूक्ष्म
सु- + सूक्ष्म सु- + सूक्ष्म, adj. very small, Pañc. ii. d. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मता
सूक्ष्मता सूक्ष्म + ता, f. Subtlety, the subtle essence, Man. 6, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मत्व
सूक्ष्मत्व सूक्ष्म + त्व, n. Fineness, subtilty, Bhag. 13, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदर्शिता
सूक्ष्मदर्शिता सूक्ष्मदर्शिता, i. e. सूक्ष्म-दर्शिन् + ता, f. Acuteness, wisdom, Mālav. 21, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्
सूच् सूच्, i. 10 (properly a denomin. derived from सूचि, and signifying originally ‘To point out’), Par.<BR> 1. To indicate, to show (by a gesture), Śāk. 8, 17; Vikr. 7, 4.<BR> 2. To prove, MBh. 3, 2706.<BR> 3. To betray, Ragh. 17, 50.<BR> 4. To espy, to see, Śāk. d. 14; to trace out, Vikr. 57, 5.<BR> 5. To hear, Śāk. 52, 11. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b " target="_blank">Page1052-b + 41</a>]<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, To indicate, Nal. 23, 18.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To indicate, Pañc. 158, 7.<BR> 2. To prove, Hit. iv. d. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच|सूचः
सूच सूच (akin to सूचि),<BR> I. m. The shoot of Kuśa grass.<BR> II. f. चा.<BR> 1. Piercing.<BR> 2. (cf. सूच्), Gesticulation.<BR> 3. Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचक|सूचकः
सूचक सूच् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Indicative, Johns. Sel. 15, 59.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A spy, an informer.<BR> 2. A teacher.<BR> 3. A dog.<BR> 4. A crow.<BR> 5. A cat.<BR> 6. A detracter, Man. 4, 71; 11, 50.<BR> 7. A scoundrel.<BR> 8. An imp.<BR> 9. The manager or chief actor of a company.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसूचक|विषसूचकः
विष- + सूचक विष- + सूचक, m. the Greek partridge, Perdix rufa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचन|सूचनं
सूचन सूच् + अन,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Informing, information.<BR> 2. Teaching, describing.<BR> II. f. ना.<BR> 1. Piercing (cf. सूचि).<BR> 2. Conveying any intimation by signs, gesticulation.<BR> 3. Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचि|सूचिः
सूचि and सूची सूची (probably akin to सिव्, cf. सूत्र), f.<BR> 1. Piercing.<BR> 2. A needle, Rām. 3, 53, 50; Megh. 24 (चि); Hit. 98, 22 (ची).<BR> 3. (cf. सूच्), Indication of a feeling by signs.<BR> 4. A mode of dancing, MBh. 7, 3383 (?).<BR> 5. A mode of array, a sharp file or column.<BR> 6. A cone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिक|सूचिकः
सूचिक सूचि + क,<BR> I. m. A tailor.<BR> II. f. का.<BR> 1. A needle.<BR> 2. An elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिता
सूचिता सूचि + ता, f. Needle-work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
सूत सूत,<BR> I. cf. 1. सु and 2. सू.<BR> II. m.<BR> A. i. e. probably 2. सू + तृ (cf. नापित).<BR> 1. A charioteer, Vikr. 5, 4.<BR> 2. The son of a Kṣattriya by a Brāhmaṇī wife, Man. 10, 10.<BR> 3. A bard, Johns. Sel. 37, 16.<BR> B.<BR> 1. A carpenter.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> III. m. and n. Quicksilver. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a " target="_blank">Page1053-a + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससूत
स- + सूत स- + सूत, adj. with the charioteer, Chr. 34, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतक|सूतकं|सूतकः
सूतक सूत + क (see vb. 1. सु),<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Birth, Man. 4, 112; 5, 58; cf. 4, 110 (birth of Rāhu = causing an eclipse).<BR> 2. Impurity from child-birth, Lass. 76, 7.<BR> II. m. and n. Quicksilver.<BR> III. f. का and तिका, A woman recently delivered, Man. 4, 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतत्व
सूतत्व सूत + त्व, n. The art of a charioteer, Nal. 22, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
सूति<BR> A. सू + ती, (see vb. 1. सु), f.<BR> 1. Birth, production.<BR> 2. Offspring.<BR> 3. Source, Kir. 2, 56.<BR> B. i. e. सिव् + ति, f. Sewing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युसूति|मृत्युसूतिः
मृत्यु- + सूति मृत्यु- + सूति, f. a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्या
सूत्या 1. सू + त्या, f.<BR> 1. Drinking the Soma juice.<BR> 2. Religious ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र्
सूत्र् सूत्र्, i. 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par.<BR> 1. To bind, to string.<BR> 2. † To unbind, to loosen.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सूतित.<BR> 1. Strung.<BR> 2. Arranged in the form of सूत्रस्, Lass. 2. ed. 89, 34.<BR> 3. Arranged.<BR> 4. Ruled, prescribed (in the Sūtras), Rājat. 5, 477.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, आसूत्रित, Attached, Rājat. 5, 482.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र सूत्र, i. e. सिव् + त्र, n.<BR> 1. A thread, Hit. 65, 13.<BR> 2. Fibre, Vikr. d. 19.<BR> 3. A string, Vikr. d. 140; the holy string, d. 157.<BR> 4. A rule in morals or science, a short aphorism, e. g. the rules of Pāṇini.<BR> 5. An opinion or decree in law.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिसूत्र|कटिसूत्रं
कटि- + सूत्र कटि- + सूत्र, n. a zone, Bhāg. P. 5, 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठसूत्र|कंठसूत्र
कण्ठ- + सूत्र कण्ठ- + सूत्र, n. a kind of embracing, Ragh. 19, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पसूत्र
कल्प- + सूत्र कल्प- + सूत्र, n. a सूत्र or rule concerning ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसूत्र|कालसूत्रं
काल- + सूत्र काल- + सूत्र, n. the name of a hell, Man. 3, 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्र|दीर्घसूत्रः
दीर्घ- + सूत्र दीर्घ- + सूत्र, adj. irresolute, Pañc. 245, 23. (दिर्घ-सूत्र + ता, f. procrastination, Rām. 2, 72, 96, Seramp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घसूत्र
अ-दीर्घ- + सूत्र अ-दीर्घ- + सूत्र, adj. resolute. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b " target="_blank">Page1053-b + 40</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसूत्र|धर्म्मसूत्र
धर्म- + सूत्र धर्म- + सूत्र,<BR> I. n. a work on law, Utt. Rāmac. 71, 12.<BR> II. m. a proper name, Bhāg. P. 9, 22, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूत्र|ब्रह्मसूत्रं
ब्रह्म-सूत्र ब्रह्म-सूत्र, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, n. title of a vedantic work, Lass. 2. ed. 87, 14 (see शारीरक-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसूत्र|मानसूत्रं
मान- + सूत्र मान- + सूत्र, n. 1. a chain of gold or silver worn round the loins. 2. a thread for measuring, Daśak. in Chr. 186, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलसूत्र
मूल- + सूत्र मूल- + सूत्र, n. a principal precept, Cāṇ. 3 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, p. 407.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसूत्र|यज्ञसूत्रं
यज्ञ- + सूत्र यज्ञ- + सूत्र, n. the sacrificial cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकसूत्र
शारीरक- + सूत्र शारीरक- + सूत्र, n. statement concerning the embodied spirit, i. e. the ब्रह्मसूत्रस् of Bādarāyaṇa, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीसूत्र|सावित्रीसूत्रं
सावित्री- + सूत्र सावित्री- + सूत्र, n. the sacrificial cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तसूत्र
हस्त- + सूत्र हस्त- + सूत्र, n. a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रकार|सूत्रकारः
सूत्रकार सूत्र-कार, m. An author of a work containing rules, precepts, Utt. Rāmac. 92, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्यत्रिकसूत्रकार
तौर्य-त्रिक- + सूत्रकार तौर्य-त्रिक- + सूत्रकार, m. author of the rules concerning vocal and instrumental music and dancing, ib. 111, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रण|सूत्रणं
सूत्रण सूत्रण, i. e. सूत्र् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Stringing.<BR> 2. Arranging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रधार|सूत्रधारः
सूत्रधार सूत्र-धार, m.<BR> 1. A carpenter, Hit. 49, 12.<BR> 2. The manager or principal actor of a company Vikr. 3, 12.<BR> 3. The author of a set of rules.<BR> 4. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रभिद्
सूत्रभिद् सूत्र-भिद्, m. A tailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रमध्यभू
सूत्रमध्यभू सूत्र-मध्य-भू, m. Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रला
सूत्रला सूत्र + ला, f. A spindle or distaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रामन्
सूत्रामन् सूत्रामन्, i. e. सु-त्रामन्, m. Indra (cf. त्रामन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिका
सूत्रिका सूत्रिका, i. e. सूत्र + क. f. A kind of dish (or cake), Pañc. 245, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिन्
सूत्रिन् सूत्रिन्, i. e. सूत्र + इन्,<BR> I. adj., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a " target="_blank">Page1054-a + 39</a>] f. इण्त्, Having threads, rules.<BR> II. m. A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद्
सूद् सूद्, † i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To kill, to hurt.<BR> 2. To distill.<BR> 3. To eject.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To incite (ved.).<BR> 2. To kill, MBh. 1, 2833; Pañc. 48, 3; ii. d. 39.<BR> 3. † To distill.<BR> 4. † To eject.<BR> 5. † To promise.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, Caus. To kill, Rām. 1, 27, 19.<BR> --With नि नि, Caus. To kill, MBh. 1, 1339.<BR> --With विनि वि-नि, To kill, MBh. 3, 8814.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, To kill, MBh. 3, 8742.<BR> --Cf. συδ in παν-συδίῃ, πασ-συδί (see 2. सू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद|सूदः
सूद सूद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A cook, Rām. 3, 28, 27.<BR> 2. Seasoning.<BR> 3. Anything seasoned.<BR> 4. Split peas.<BR> 5. Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदन|सूदनं
सूदन सूद् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Destructive, a destroyer, Johns. Sel. 16, 67; 22, 116.<BR> II. n. Destroying, Nal. 12, 126.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चसूदन|क्रौंचसूदन|क्रौञ्चसूदनः
क्रौञ्च- + सूदन क्रौञ्च- + सूदन, m. a name of the god of war, Suśr. 2, 386, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसूदन|बलसूदनः
बल- + सूदन बल- + सूदन, m. a name of Indra, Lass. 50, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसूदन|मधुसूदनः
मधु- + सूदन मधु- + सूदन, m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून|सूनं|सूनः
सून सून,<BR> I. See 1. सु.<BR> II. adj. Empty (wrongly for शून, see श्वि).<BR> III. f. ना (cf. शून).<BR> 1. A shambles or slaughter-house, a place or utensil of slaughter, Man. 3, 68.<BR> 2. Hurting, killing, Bhāg. P. 1, 17, 38.<BR> 3. The uvula.<BR> 4. A zone.<BR> 5. A river.<BR> 6. The mumps.<BR> 7. A ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनरी
सूनरी सूनरी, i. e. सु-नर + ई, adj. f. A respectable woman, Chr. 287, 5 = Rigv. i. 48, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनिन्
सूनिन् सूनिन्, i. e. सूना + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A butcher.<BR> 2. A hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनु|सूनुः
सूनु सू + नु (see vb. 1. सु),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A son, Vikr. d. 145.<BR> 2. A younger. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b " target="_blank">Page1054-b + 39</a>] brother.<BR> 3. The sun.<BR> II. f. नू, A daughter.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sunus; A.S. sunu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनृत|सूनृतं
सूनृत सूनृत, probably based on सु-नृ + ता,<BR> I. f. ता, Excellent song, Chr. 287, 2 = Rigv. i. 48, 2; Chr. 294, 7 = Rigv. i. 92, 7.<BR> II. adj. त, f. ता,<BR> 1. True and agreeable, Utt. Rāmac. 135, 4.<BR> 2. Auspicious.<BR> 3. Gentle, Hit. i. d. 59, M.M.; kind, Śāk. 13, 1.<BR> 4. Dear to.<BR> III. n. Agreeable and true discourse or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनृतावन्त्|सूनृतावत्
सूनृतावन्त् सूनृतावन्त्, i. e. सूनृत + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in excellent songs, Chr. 295, 14 = Rigv. i. 92, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्मद|सून्मदः
सून्मद and सून्माद i. e. सु-उन्माद, adj. Mad, crazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूप|सूपः
सूप सूप, m.<BR> 1. Broth, Man. 3, 226; soup.<BR> 2. Sauce.<BR> 3. A cook.<BR> 4. A vessel.<BR> 5. An arrow.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. suf; O.N. sup; A.S. supan; O.H.G. sûfan, saufjan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपकार|सूपकारः
सूपकार सूप-कार, m. A cook, Pañc. 253, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूम|सूमं|सूमः
सूम सू + म (see vb. 1. सु), m.<BR> 1. Milk.<BR> 2. Water.<BR> 3. Sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्
सूर् सूर्, see शूर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर|सूरः
सूर सूर, i. e. 2. स्वर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. The sun, Chr. 289, 2, 9 = Rigv. i. 50, 2; 9.<BR> 2. A wise man, Chr. 292, 5 = Rigv. i. 86, 5.<BR> 3. A teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरण|सूरणः
सूरण सूरण, m. An esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरत|सूरतः
सूरत सूरत, i. e. सु-रत (see रम्), adj.<BR> 1. Compassionate, tender.<BR> 2. Calm, tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरि|सूरिः
सूरि सूरि, i. e. 2. स्वर् + इ (or rather curtailed सूरिन्), m.<BR> 1. The sun.<BR> 2. A wise man, Chr. 287, 4 = Rigv. i. 48, 4; Pañc. i. d. 71.<BR> 3. A teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरिन्
सूरिन् सूरिन्, i. e. सूर + इन्,<BR> I. adj. Wise.<BR> II. m. A learned man, a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्
† सूर्क्ष् सूर्क्ष्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To respect.<BR> 2. To disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्षण|सूर्क्षणं
सूर्क्षण सूर्क्षण, i. e. सूर्क्ष् + अन, n. Disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य्
† सूर्क्ष्य् सूर्क्ष्य्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To envy.<BR> 2. To disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य|सूर्क्ष्यः
सूर्क्ष्य सूर्क्ष्य, m. A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्प|सूर्पः|सूर्प्प
सूर्प सूर्प (cf. शूर्प), m. A winnowing basket, Yājñ. 1, 285; Pañc. 121, 19.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. swarb, gurges; N.N.L. zwerven, vagari; Goth. svairban; O.H.G. swerban (To dry something, originally, by swinging it in the open air).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्मि|सूर्मिः|सूर्म्मि
सूर्मि and सूर्मी सूर्मी̆, f.<BR> 1. An iron image (of a woman), Man. 11, 103.<BR> 2. The pillar of a house.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तसूर्मि|तप्तसूर्मिः
तप्त-सूर्मि तप्त-सूर्मि, f. the name of a hell, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य|सूर्यः|सूर्य्य|सूर्य्यः
सूर्य सूर्य, i. e. 2. स्वर्, or rather *सवर् (for original *सवन्), + य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The sun, Pañc. 37, 20.<BR> 2. Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR> 3. The sen of Bali.<BR> II. f. या.<BR> 1. The wife of the sun.<BR> 2. A new bride.<BR> 3. A bitter gourd.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ἀϐέλιος (for ἀϝέλιος = *सवर् + य), ἠέλιος, ἥλιος; Goth. sauil; Lat. sol; Goth. sunna (= *सवन् + य), sunno; A.S. sunna, sunne, sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्यम्
प्रति-सूर्य + म् प्रति-सूर्य + म्, adv. opposite to the sun; प्रतिसूर्य, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यज|सूर्यजः|सूर्य्यज|सूर्य्यजः
सूर्यज सूर्य-ज,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Karṇa.<BR> 2. Sugrīva.<BR> II. f. जा, The Yamunā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्यभक्तक|सूर्य्यभक्तक|सूर्य्यभक्तकः
सूर्यभक्तक सूर्य-भक्त + क (see भज्), m.<BR> 1. A worshipper of the sun.<BR> 2. A flower, Pentapetes phœnicea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्योढ|सूर्योढः|सूर्य्योढ|सूर्य्योढः
सूर्योढ सूर्योढ, i. e. सूर्य-आढ (vb. वह्),<BR> I. adj. One who comes after sunset, Pañc. 35, 16; i. d. 136.<BR> II. m. An evening guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष्
† सूष् सूष् (cf. 1. सु), शूष् शूष्, i. 1, Par. To bring forth, to bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृ
सृ सृ, i. 1, and ii. 3, सिसृ, Par.<BR> 1. To flow, to flow to, Chr. 292, 5 = Rigv. i. 86, 5 (सस्रुषीस्, ved. for सस्रुष्यस्).<BR> 2. To blow, Megh. 54.<BR> 3. To go, MBh. 1, 1696; to go to, 3, 2728.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To extend.<BR> 2. To move, to touch, Megh. 84.<BR> 3. To remove, Megh. 89.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, Caus. To extend, MBh. 3, 665.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To follow, Man. 11, 77; to pursue, Pañc. 227, 23.<BR> 2. To go to, Megh. 31.<BR> 3. To return to, Pañc. 137, 12. अनुसृत, Accompanied, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 9.<BR> --Caus. To pursue, MBh. 1, 4309.<BR> --With अप अप, To retire, Pañc. iii. d. 40; 220, 13; to withdraw, Hit. 13, 18.<BR> --Caus. To order to withdraw, Man. 7, 149; to remove, Pañc. 15, 25.<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To go to, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 1; to approach, MBh. 1, 3002.<BR> 2. To attack, MBh. 1, 1175.<BR> --Caus. To meet, Mṛcch. 121, 14.<BR> --With अत्यभि अति-अभि, To pass, MBh. 1, 3854.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to go out, to call out, Chr. 53, 22.<BR> 2. To expel, MBh. 3, 14872; to drive away, Bhartṛ. 1, 18.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्, Caus.<BR> 1. To offer, Hit. ii. d. 154.<BR> 2. To urge on, to incite, MBh. 3, 10620.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, Caus. To give, Prab. 116, 7.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To approach, Śāk. 12, 14; Vikr. 11, 11; with आसनम्, To sit down, Vikr. 46, 20.<BR> 2. To visit, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-a " target="_blank">Page1056-a + 42</a>] Vikr. d. 3; Daśak. in Chr. 192, 16.<BR> --With नि नि, निसृत,<BR> 1. (= निःसृत), Gone forth, disappeared, Rājat. 4, 566.<BR> 2. f. ता, A plant, Ipomœa Turpethum.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To slip or to go forth or out, Hit. 29, 5, M.M.; 44, 7, M.M.<BR> 2. To depart, Man. 6, 4. अ-निःसरन्त्, adj. Not being able to withdraw, Pañc. 195, 8. निःसृत,<BR> 1. Gone out, having left (abl.), Hit. iii. d. 133.<BR> 2. Broken forth, Śiś. 9, 25.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to go out, MBh. 3, 12995.<BR> 2. To drive away, to expel, Pañc. 227, 9.<BR> --With विनिस् वि-निस्, विनिःसृत, Gone forth or out, issued forth, Man. 4, 165; Vikr. d. 43.<BR> --With परि परि, To flow round, MBh. 3, 10983.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To proceed, Rām. 2, 59, 10; to pass, Vikr. d. 63.<BR> 2. To spring up, Pañc. iii. d. 258.<BR> 3. To break forth, Mālat. 24, 17.<BR> 4. To increase, Pañc. iii. d. 2.<BR> 5. To extend, Ṛt. 1, 25. प्रसृत,<BR> 1. Gone.<BR> 2. Spread.<BR> 3. Stretched.<BR> 4. Long.<BR> 5. Swift.<BR> 6. Modest, Rām. 3, 52, 21.<BR> 7. Attached to, occupied.<BR> 8. Appointed. m. The palm of the hand. f. ता, The leg. n. A measure of two पलस्. Comparat. प्रसृततर, Excessive, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 15.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To stretch forward or out, MBh. 3, 345; Pañc. 53, 6.<BR> 2. To spread, Pañc. 105, 1; 157, 25; 174, 11.<BR> 3. To open wide, Mṛcch. 35, 17.<BR> 4. To expose for sale, Man. 5, 129.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, To spread, Ragh. 16, 3.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, Caus.<BR> 1. To replace, Śāk. d. 61.<BR> 2. To remove, Vikr. d. 47. प्रतिसारित,<BR> 1. Repelled.<BR> 2. Dressed (as a wound).<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To spread, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b " target="_blank">Page1056-b + 41</a>] Śiś. 9, 19.<BR> 2. To return, Śiś. 9, 37. विसृत,<BR> 1. Spread.<BR> 2. Drawn (as a bowstring), Kir. 10, 53.<BR> 3. Uttered, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 22.<BR> --Caus. To extend, Rām. 1, 42, 6. विसारित,<BR> 1. Set on foot.<BR> 2. Effected.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To obtain, Man. 12, 70.<BR> --Caus. To cause to revolve, Man. 12, 124.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्, Caus. To dismiss, MBh. 3, 11552.<BR> --Cf. ὁρμή, ὁρμάω, etc., σάλος, σάλα, σαλεύω; Lat. salio, saltare (A.S. saltian, borrowed); ἅλλομαι, also ἰάλλω (rather than to ऋ, p. 136), probably also Lat. serere; ἁρμός, ὅρμος, ἕρμα; A.S. serian, to set in order (Caus., cf. also Lat. serere).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविन्दुप्रसृत
पञ्चविन्दुप्रसृत पञ्चविन्दुप्रसृत, i. e. पन्चन्-विन्दु-, n. a kind of dancing motion, Daśak. 145, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक|सृकः
सृक सृ + क, m.<BR> 1. A lotus.<BR> 2. Air, wind.<BR> 3. An arrow (cf. सृग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कन्
सृक्कन् सृक्कन्, सृक्क सृक्क, सृक्वन् सृक्वन्, सृक्व सृक्व, i. e. सृज् + वन् (anomal.), n. The corner of the mouth, Pañc. 55, 7 (क्कन्); 262, 20 (cf. my transl.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसृक्कन्
विष- + सृक्कन् विष- + सृक्कन्, m. a wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृग|सृगः
सृग सृग, i. e. probably सृज् + अ, m. A short arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
सृज् सृज् (akin to सृ), i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 1, 16, 6), and † i. 4, Ātm.<BR> 1. To let flow, to let loose, Rām. 1, 44, 38.<BR> 2. To effuse, to shed (ved.).<BR> 3. To create, Man. 1, 25; 41; with gen. in the sense of the dat., Hit. pr. d. 27, M.M. (to destinate).<BR> 4. To beget, Rām. 1, 16, 9.<BR> 5. To cast, Chr. 32, 23.<BR> 6. To put on, to place, Nal. 5, 28.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सृष्ट.<BR> 1. Abandoned.<BR> 2. Connected.<BR> 3. Adorned.<BR> 4. Much, many.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति,<BR> 1. To leave, MBh. 3, 431.<BR> 2. To give (with gen.), Rām. 2, 18, 23; Vikr. d. 15. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-a " target="_blank">Page1057-a + 41</a>]<BR> 3. To remit.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप, To abandon, MBh. 3, 16104.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To give, Rām. 1, 9, 63.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To let loose, Man. 1, 8; Matsyop. 23.<BR> 2. To cast, MBh. 1, 1973.<BR> 3. To give (one his life), Nal. 26, 23.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To throw, MBh. 3, 14253.<BR> 2. To put down, MBh. 3, 10438.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव,<BR> 1. To abandon, MBh. 1, 6749.<BR> 2. To throw, MBh. 3, 1586.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To place on, MBh. 1, 1703.<BR> 2. To commit, Man. 9, 323.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To shed, Chr. 12, 28.<BR> 2. To let loose, Chr. 36, 21; Pañc. 224, 4.<BR> 3. To abandon, Man. 6, 16; Vikr. 37, 8; Daśak. in Chr. 194, 23.<BR> 4. To shoot, figurat., Pañc. i. d. 219 (cf. my transl.); to cast, Chr. 20, 20.<BR> 5. To throw away, Vikr. d. 94; 70, 8.<BR> 6. To dismiss, MBh. 3, 2093.<BR> 7. To give up, Man. 8, 144.<BR> 8. To decline, Man. 8, 170.<BR> 9. To repudiate, Pañc. iii. d. 210; 170, 25.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To shed, Rām. 2, 44, 21.<BR> 2. To let loose, to leave, Pañc. 226, 23.<BR> 3. To cast, Man. 4, 56.<BR> 4. To put off, Chr. 30, 4.<BR> 5. To place, Man. 3, 244.<BR> 6. To dismiss (without punishment), Man. 8, 347.<BR> 7. To lose, MBh. 3, 8750.<BR> --With उप उप, उपसृष्ट,<BR> 1. Connected to.<BR> 2. Swarming, Man. 4, 61.<BR> 3. Seized by, possessed by (evil demons), Rām. 2, 47, 1, Seramp.<BR> 4. Assailed, Bhāg. P. 4, 12, 16.<BR> 5. Eclipsed, Man. 4, 37. n. Coition.<BR> --With नि नि, निसृष्ट,<BR> 1. Delivered.<BR> 2. Emancipated, Man. 8, 419.<BR> 3. Centrical.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With संनि सम्-नि, संनिसृष्ट, Committed, MBh. 1, 7134.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To abandon, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-b " target="_blank">Page1057-b + 42</a>] MBh. 3, 1080.<BR> 2. To injure, MBh. 2, 856.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रतिसृष्ट,<BR> 1. Sent.<BR> 2. Given.<BR> 3. Celebrated.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To shed, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 7.<BR> 2. To let loose, Rām. 1, 44, 13; to abandon, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38.<BR> 3. To create, to produce, Man. 1, 11.<BR> 4. To drop, Man. 9, 282.<BR> 5. To send, Chr. 54, 12.<BR> 6. To let fall, Utt. Rāmac. 41, 3; to cast, MBh. 4, 1856; to throw away, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2876.<BR> 7. To repudiate, Pañc. 200, 4.<BR> 8. To utter, to sound, Rām. 3, 51, 20.<BR> 9. To give, Rām. 2, 36, 8 (with gen. instead of dat.); Utt. Rāmac. 111, 5. विसृष्ट,<BR> 1. Abandoned, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 14.<BR> 2. Given away.<BR> 3. Dismissed.<BR> 4. Expelled.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To shed, Ṛt. 6, 12, v. r.<BR> 2. To dismiss, Pañc. 214, 3; Chr. 14, 25.<BR> 3. To spare, MBh. 1, 8362.<BR> 4. To repudiate, MBh. 3, 1860.<BR> 5. To put off, Chr. 42, 14. विसर्जित,<BR> 1. Abandoned, Hit. ii. d. 17.<BR> 2. Given away.<BR> --With सम् सम्, pass.<BR> 1. To mix, Ragh. 5, 69.<BR> 2. To meet with (instr.), Ragh. 13, 73.<BR> 3. To converse with one, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 6. संसृष्ट,<BR> 1. United, composed, Man. 1, 56.<BR> 2. Reunited, Man. 9, 212.<BR> 3. Connected as partners.<BR> 4. Dressed in clean clothes.<BR> 5. Involved in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
अ- + सृज् अ- + सृज्, adj. uninterrupted, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
अ- + सृज् अ- + सृज्, adj. not allowed, Man. 2, 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृञ्जय|सृंजय
सृञ्जय सृञ्जय, m.<BR> 1. A people, Johns. Sel. 29, 34.<BR> 2. A proper name, Chr. 13, 7; 15, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणि|सृणिः
सृणि सृणि,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An enemy.<BR> 2. The moon.<BR> II. m., f., and णी, f. A hook to drive an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणीका
सृणीका सृणीका, f. Saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृति|सृतिः
सृति सृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Gliding, Man. 6, 63.<BR> 2. Going, proceeding.<BR> 3. A road, Bhag. 8, 27.<BR> 4. Hurting. See कु-.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वन्
सृत्वन् सृत्वन्, m. The creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदाकु|सृदाकुः
सृदाकु सृदाकु,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. Wind.<BR> 3. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR> 4. The disc of the sun.<BR> II. f. A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्
सृप् सृप् (akin to सृ), i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 96, 9),<BR> 1. To creep, Rām. 2, 59, 10.<BR> 2. To go, to move, Hit. 30, 3.<BR> --With the prep. व्यति वि-अति, To move to and fro, MBh. 4, 1042.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To approach, MBh. 1, 6201.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To go away, MBh. 3, 14112.<BR> 2. To run away, Rām. 2, 29, 4.<BR> 3. To deviate from, Pañc. iii. d. 241 (अप-सर्प्य, anomal., or erroneously for अपसृप्य).<BR> 4. To espy, Utt. Rāmac. 25, 5 (पौर-जानपदान्, the inhabitants of the town and district).<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप, To run away, MBh. 4, 1899.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To rise, Nal. 23, 9 (cf. यथासंगम्, under सङ्ग).<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, To rise, Ragh. 6, 8.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To go near, to approach, Chr. 61, 40.<BR> 2. To undergo, Hit. ii. d. 175.<BR> 3. To go forth, Pañc. 159, 23; Man. 9, 269.<BR> 4. To move, Hit. iv. d. 27.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To approach, MBh. 1, 6450.<BR> --With परि परि, To go to and fro. Rām. 3, 52, 48.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To proceed, Pañc. 120, 9. प्रसृप्त, Come forth, Utt. Rāmac. 27, 6.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To sneak about, Pañc. ii. d. 48; to fly about, Hit. 16, 3, M.M.<BR> 2. To spread, Mālat. 32, 4.<BR> 3. To disperse, Nal. 1, 25.<BR> 4. To flow to and fro on (acc.), Utt. Rāmac. 18, 7.<BR> 5. To wind, to meander, Rām. 1, 44, 17.<BR> 6. To run away, MBh. 1, 8286.<BR> --With सम् सम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b " target="_blank">Page1058-b + 36</a>]<BR> 1. To flow, Megh. 29.<BR> 2. To glide, to move, Megh. 52.<BR> --Cf. Lat. serpere; ἔρπω; A.S. slipan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाट|सृपाटः
सृपाट सृपाट, m., and f. टि, A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाटिका
सृपाटिका सृपाटिका, f. The beak of a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्र|सृप्रः
सृप्र सृप् + र, m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृभ्
† सृभ् सृभ्, सृम्भ् सृम्भ्, सिभ् सिभ्, सिम्भ् सिम्भ्, स्रिभ् स्रिभ्, स्रिम्भ् स्रिम्भ्, i. 1, Par. To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमर|सृमरः
सृमर सृ + मर,<BR> I. adj. Going.<BR> II. m. A young deer, Rām. 3, 49, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृम्भ्|सृंभ्
सृम्भ् सृम्भ्, see सृभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टि|सृष्टिः
सृष्टि सृष्टि, i. e. सृज् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Creation, Vikr. 8, 18; Man. 1, 25; with आद्या, Śāk. d. 1, The first creation, i. e. water.<BR> 2. Nature.<BR> 3. A liberal gift, Man. 3, 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सॄ
सॄ सॄ, see स्वॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्
सेक् सेक्, see स्रेक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक सेक, i. e. सिच् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sprinkling, Hit. ii. d. 132; Kir. 5, 26; a drop (? of fire), Pañc. i. d. 416.<BR> 2. Seminal fluid.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसेक
अमृत- + सेक अमृत- + सेक, m. sprinkling with the beverage of the gods, Hit. ii. d. 132 (फलन्त्य् अमृतसेके ऽपि पथ्यानि विषद्रुमाः, ‘Poisonous trees, although sprinkled with nectar, do not bear healthy fruits’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकिम|सेकिमं
सेकिम सेकिम (vb. सिच्), n. A radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तृ
सेक्तृ सेक्तृ, i. e. सिच् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what sprinkles.<BR> II. m. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्त्र|सेक्त्रं
सेक्त्र सेक्त्र, i. e. सिच् + त्र, n. A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक सेचक, i. e. सिच् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Sprinkling.<BR> II. m. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचन|सेचनं
सेचन सेचन, i. e. सिच् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sprinkling, watering, Śāk. 8, 23.<BR> 2. Dripping.<BR> II. n., and f. नी, A bucket.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसेचन
अग्नि- + सेचन अग्नि- + सेचन, n. spirituous liquor (?), Pañc. ii. d. 165 ( Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2772 reads सेवनैः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेटु|सेटुः
सेटु सेटु, m.<BR> 1. The water melon.<BR> 2. A kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु सेतु, i. e. सि + तु, m.<BR> 1. A mound, a bank, a dike, Rājat. 5, 91; figurat. Means of protecting (the law and institutes), Bhāg. P. 3, 1, 36; 3, 21, 54.<BR> 2. A high causeway in fields.<BR> 3. A landmark, Man. 8, 245.<BR> 4. A pass, a defile.<BR> 5. Figurat. Law, Bhāg. P. 3, 9, 19.<BR> 6. A bridge, Pañc. i. d. 115 (cf. my transl.).<BR> 7. The islands between India and Ceylon (cf. नल-सेतु), Lass. 2. ed. 92, 66.<BR> 3. A tree, Tapia cratæva.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसेतु|धर्मसेतुः
धर्म- + सेतु धर्म- + सेतु, m. a dike for the protection of right, Hariv. 11315.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाषण्डधर्मसेतु
अ-पाषण्ड-धर्म-सेतु अ-पाषण्ड-धर्म-सेतु, m. a dike for the protection of right free from heresy, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलसेतु
नल- + सेतु नल- + सेतु, m. the bridge constructed by the monkey Nala, name of the islands between India and Ceylon, Rām. 6, 108, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेत्र|सेत्रं
सेत्र सेत्र, i. e. सि + त्र, n. A ligament or fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना सेना, i. e. स + न, f. 1. An army, Vikr. 11, 16.<BR> 2. The wife of Kārttikeya, the god of war.<BR> --Comp.<BR> I. At the end of Tatpuruṣa comp. it may become n.; e. g. ब्राण्मण-सेना, f., or -सेन, n., Pāṇ. ii. 4, 25.<BR> II. इन्द्र- and चित्र-सेन, m. proper names, Draup. 8, 15; Indr. 3, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसेना
चित्र-सेना चित्र-सेना, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b " target="_blank">Page1059-b + 42</a>] f. a proper name, Indr. 2, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेना
देव- + सेना देव- + सेना,<BR> I. f. an army of celestials, MBh. 3, 14245.<BR> II. m. देव-सेन, a proper name, Kathās. 15, 63.<BR> III. f. ना, a proper name, MBh. 3, 14257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासेना
महा- + सेना महा- + सेना,<BR> I. adj. having a great army, Chr. 52, 12.<BR> II. m. 1. a general.<BR> 2. Kārttikeya, the god of war, Vikr. d. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसेन|यज्ञसेनः
यज्ञ- + सेन यज्ञ- + सेन, m. a proper name, Johns. Sel. 26, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपसेन
रूप-सेन रूप-सेन, m. a proper name, Lass. 19, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेन|वीरसेनं|वीरसेनः
वीर-सेन वीर-सेन, m. the father of Nala, Nal. 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरसेन|शूरसेनः
शूर-सेन शूर-सेन, m. 1. a country about Mathura, Man. 7, 193. 2. a proper name. 3. pl. m., and also ˚नकाः ˚नकाः, the inhabitants, Man. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानी
सेनानी सेना-नी, m.<BR> 1. A general, Hit. iii. d. 69.<BR> 2. Kārttikeya, the god of war, Kir. 15, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफ|सेफः
सेफ सेफ, see शेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराह|सेराहः
सेराह सेराह, m. A horse of a milk-white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् सेल्, † शेल् शेल्, i. 1, Par. To go or move.<BR> --With the prep. अति अति, Caus. To oblige to make excessive marches, Hit. iii. d. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्
सेव् सेव् (akin to सप्), i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To follow, to apply one's self to, Man. 6, 35.<BR> 2. To study, MBh. 3, 27.<BR> 3. To practise, Man. 6, 29; to do, Ragh. 17, 49.<BR> 4. To enjoy, Hit. i. d. 172, M.M. (cherish); Pañc. v. d. 24; carnally, Man. 8, 365; to love, Hit. 87, 1.<BR> 5. To inhabit, MBh. 3, 2402.<BR> 6. To tarry somewhere (with acc.), Man. 4, 131.<BR> 7. To frequent, Pañc. i. d. 9; Lass. 39, 7; to search, Vikr. d. 41.<BR> 8. To stand at, to guard, Hit. 98, 18.<BR> 9. To serve, to gratify, Ragh. 11, 11.<BR> 10. To honour, Man. 7, 38; to worship, Hit. ii. d. 27. सेवित,<BR> 1. Pursued, used.<BR> 2. Protected.<BR> 3. Frequented, Hit. i. d. 150, M.M.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-a " target="_blank">Page1060-a + 42</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To worship, Hit. ii. d. 33.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ,<BR> 1. To practise, Mṛcch. 35, 6.<BR> 2. To employ for smearing with, Ṛt. 6, 12 (v. r.).<BR> 3. To enjoy, Vikr. 67, 3; MBh. 3, 16564.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To practise, Man. 11, 174. समासेरित, Served.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To apply one's self to, to practise, MBh. 2, 159.<BR> 2. To perform, MBh. 13, 7567.<BR> 3. To enjoy, MBh. 3, 15382.<BR> 4. To serve, to honour, Man. 4, 133.<BR> 5. To haunt, Pañc. i. d. 279. उपसेवित, Smeared, Rām. 2, 100, 33.<BR> --With अभ्युप अभि-उप, To observe, MBh. 3, 13432.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To enjoy, Rām. 1, 35, 23.<BR> --With नि नि, षेव्,<BR> 1. To pursue, to attach one's self to, Hit. i. d. 209, M.M.<BR> 2. To practise, Man. 4, 155.<BR> 3. To employ, Śiś. 9, 68.<BR> 4. To enjoy, MBh. 3, 11877.<BR> 5. To inhabit, Pañc. 31, 1; Rām. 1, 31, 21.<BR> 6. To observe, Śāk. d. 26.<BR> 7. To attend, Man. 9, 300.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To worship, Kir. 18, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
अ- + सेवित अ- + सेवित, adj. not frequented, Hit. i. d. 144, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसेवित
सु- + सेवित सु- + सेवित, adj. well served, Hit. i. d. 21, M.M. सेव्य,<BR> 1. To be taken care of.<BR> 2. Venerable; with जन, Master, Vikr. d. 39. m., f. या, and n. Names of plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेव्य
अ- + सेव्य अ- + सेव्य, adj. 1. not deserving to be served, Pañc. i. d. 286. 2. not deserving to be visitéd, Pañc. 31, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसेव्य
दुस्- + सेव्य दुस्- + सेव्य, adj. difficult to be treated, MBh. 13, 2225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक<BR> A. सेव् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Servile, dependent,<BR> II. m. A servant, Pañc. 217, 25; Rājat. 5, 51 (read देव सेवकः, ‘O king, a servant of the minister Śūra, hold by him like a son...’).<BR> B. i. e. सिव् + अक, A sack.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसेवक|कुलसेवकः
कुल- + सेवक कुल- + सेवक, m. an excellent servant, Pañc. i. d. 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि सेवधि, also शेवधि, q. cf., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b " target="_blank">Page1060-b + 43</a>] m.<BR> 1. A divine treasure owned by Kuvera, the god of wealth.<BR> 2. A treasure, Man. 2, 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
सेवन सेवन, i. e. सिव् and सेव् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Sewing, stitching.<BR> 2. A sack.<BR> 3. Following, being addicted to, haunting, Pañc. 241, 1; practising, Hit. ii. d. 32; using, 217, 23.<BR> 4. Enjoying, dallying with, Man. 11, 178.<BR> 5. Service, Rājat. 5, 368.<BR> II. f. नी, A needle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसेवन
काम- + सेवन काम- + सेवन, n. wantonness, Lass. 40, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिसेवन
कृषि- + सेवन कृषि- + सेवन, n. husbandry, Bhartṛ. 2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नसेवनी
तुन्न- + सेवनी तुन्न- + सेवन (vb. तुद्), f. नी, the suture of a wound, Suśr. 1, 93, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा सेव् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Service, Man. 4, 5; Vikr. d. 42.<BR> 2. Servitude, Hit. i. d. 136, M.M.<BR> 3. Practice, Rājat. 5, 280.<BR> 4. Worship, Bhag. 4, 34.<BR> 5. Homage, Rājat. 5, 154.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवा
अ- + सेवा अ- + सेवा, f. avoiding to serve, Man. 2, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारसेवा
वार- + सेवा वार- + सेवा, f. 1. harlotry. 2. a set of courtesans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसेवा
स्त्री- + सेवा स्त्री- + सेवा, f. libertinism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसेवा
हीन- + सेवा हीन- + सेवा (vb. हा), f. serving a low person, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित्व
सेवित्व सेवित्व, i. e. सेविन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Staying, inhabiting, Bhag. 13, 10.<BR> 2. Serving, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविन्
सेविन् सेव् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Pursuing, practising.<BR> 2. Serving.<BR> 3. Honouring, Man. 7, 38.<BR> 4. Dwelling, Vikr. 64, 1.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विट्सेविन्
द्विट्सेविन् द्विट्सेविन्, i. e. द्विष्-, m. a traitor, Man. 9, 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यता
सेव्यता सेव्य + ता (vb. सेव्), f.<BR> 1. State of being honoured, Ṛt. 1, 2; Hit. ii. d. 89 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1304).<BR> 2. Rank, eminence, worth, Mālat. 46, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सै
† सै सै, i. 1, Par. To waste or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंह|सैंहः
सैंह सैंह, i. e. सिंह + अ, adj., f. ही,<BR> 1. Inherent in a lion, Hit. i. d. 174. M.M.<BR> 2. Lion-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिक|सैंहिकः
सैंहिक सैंहिक,<BR> I. i. e. सिंह + इक, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a " target="_blank">Page1061-a + 40</a>] adj. Lion-like.<BR> II. i. e. सिंहिका + अ, metronym., m. Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकेय|सैंहिकेयः
सैंहिकेय सैंहिकेय, i. e. सिंहिका + एय, metronym., m. Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकत|सैकतं|सैकतः
सैकत सैकत, i. e. सिकता + अ,<BR> I. adj. Sandy.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A sand-bank, Śāk. d. 144.<BR> 2. A bank, a shore, Ragh. 5, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिक|सैकतिकं|सैकतिकः
सैकतिक सैकतिक, i. e. सिकता + इक,<BR> I. adj. Living in doubt and error.<BR> II. m. A religious mendicant.<BR> III. n. A thread worn to secure good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैद्धान्तिक|सैद्धांतिक|सैद्धान्तिकः
सैद्धान्तिक सैद्धान्तिक, i. e. सिद्धान्त + इक, adj. Relating to a demonstrated truth, knowing the truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनापत्य|सैनापत्यं
सैनापत्य सैनापत्य, i. e. सेना-पति + य, n. The command of an army, Man. 12, 100; generalship, Vikr. d. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनिक|सैनिकः
सैनिक सैनिक, i. e. सेना + इक,<BR> I. adj. Belonging or relating to an army.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A soldier, Hit. ii. d. 82; Rājat. 5, 430.<BR> 2. A guard, a picket.<BR> 3. A body of forces in array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धव|सैंधव|सैन्धवं|सैन्धवः
सैन्धव सैन्धव, i. e. सिन्धु + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Marine.<BR> 2. Produced or born in Sindh, Johns. Sel. 96, 73.<BR> II. m. and n. Rock-salt.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A horse.<BR> 2. pl. The people of the country along the Indus, Draup. 6, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवक|सैंधवक|सैन्धवकः
सैन्धवक सैन्धव + क, adj. Relating to the Saindhavas (see the last); with नृप, their king, Draup. 8, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्य|सैन्यं|सैन्यः
सैन्य सैन्य, i. e. सेना + य,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A soldier, Rājat. 5, 216.<BR> 2. A guard.<BR> II. n. An army, Hit. iii. d. 79.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससैन्य
स- + सैन्य स- + सैन्य, adj. with the army, Rājat. 5, 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरन्ध्री|सैरंध्री
सैरन्ध्री सैरन्ध्री, i. e. सीर + म्-धृ + अ + अ, f.<BR> 1. A female artist, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b " target="_blank">Page1061-b + 41</a>] female servant, Nal. 13, 55; Pañc. iii. d. 240.<BR> 2. Epithet and name of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिक|सैरिकः
सैरिक सैरिक, i. e. सीर + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to a plough.<BR> 2. Having furrows.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A ploughman.<BR> 2. A plough-ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्र|सैरिंध्र|सैरिंध्रः|सैरिन्ध्रः
सैरिन्ध्र सैरिन्ध्र, for सैरन्ध्र, see सैरन्ध्री and cf. सौदामिनी,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A menial servant.<BR> 2. The son of a Dasyu by an Ayogava female, Man. 10, 32.<BR> II. f. ध्री (cf. सैरन्ध्री), 1. A female servant.<BR> 2. Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिभ|सैरिभः
सैरिभ सैरिभ (akin to सीर, cf. सैरिक), m.<BR> 1. A buffalo.<BR> 2. Indra's heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैसक
सैसक सैसक, i. e. सीसक + अ, adj. Leaden, Man. 11, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सो
सो सो, i. 4, स्य (probably akin to 2. अस्, of which the base of the present is अस्य), Par. To destroy.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सित, Finished, completed, destroyed; see s. v.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव,<BR> 1. To let fly, Rigv. i. 104, 1.<BR> 2. To fail, Kir. 16, 17. अवसित, Completed, Śāk. 3, 6; finished, Vikr. 37, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. सायय, To cause to be completed, Ragh. 5, 76.<BR> --With अध्यव अधि-अव,<BR> 1. To practise, Hit. 42, 10, M.M.<BR> 2. To be able, Śiś. 9, 76.<BR> 3. To determine, MBh. 3, 16254.<BR> 4. To reflect, Śāk. d. 115, v. r.<BR> --With पर्यव परि-अव, To endeavour, Naiṣ. 6, 23. पर्यवसित,<BR> 1. Finished, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 10.<BR> 2. Resolved, Mālat. 75, 3.<BR> 3. Perished, lost Mālat. 149, 6.<BR> 4. With लोकान्तरम् Gone in another world, Utt. Rāmac. 172, 4.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव, प्रत्यवसित, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a " target="_blank">Page1062-a + 41</a>] Eaten.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To effectuate, to be able, Megh. 29.<BR> 2. To establish, Man. 12, 113.<BR> 3. To determine, Megh. 112.<BR> 4. To reflect, Śāk. d. 115.<BR> 5. To believe, Rām. 2, 12, 71.<BR> 6. To wish, Śāk. d. 17. Anomal. pres. सामि, MBh. 3, 16808; potent. सेयम्, 1, 4163; fut. सिष्यामि, 1, 6118; absol. व्यवस्य, 1, 5926. व्यवसित,<BR> 1. Resolved, Mālat. 21, 10.<BR> 2. Energetic, persevering, Vikr. 57, 2; endeavouring, Vikr. d. 125.<BR> 3. Tricked, cheated. n. Certainty.<BR> --Caus. सायय, To embolden, Kir. 1, 28.<BR> --With संव्यव सम्-वि-अव, To decree, Man. 7, 13.<BR> --With वि वि, To distill, Chr. 291, 5 = Rigv. i. 85, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवसित
दुस्- + अवसित दुस्- + अवसित, adj. difficult to be comprehended, Bhāg. P. 6, 16, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढृ
सोढृ सोढृ, i. e. सह् + तृ, m., f. ढ्री, and n.<BR> 1. Enduring, patient.<BR> 2. Powerful, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्साहता
सोत्साहता सोत्साहता, i. e. स-उत्साह + ता, f. Energy, Kathās. 25, 296 (read सेत्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदर्य|सोदर्यः|सोदर्य्य|सोदर्य्यः
सोदर्य सोदर्य, i. e. स-उदर + य, m. A brother of whole blood, Man. 9, 212; Pañc. iv. d. 6 (cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 542).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोनह|सोनहः
सोनह सोनह, m. Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाक|सोपाकः
सोपाक सोपाक, perhaps an anomal. form of श्वपाक, m. The son of a Caṇḍāla by a Pukkasī female, Man. 10, 38.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुसोपाक|पांडुसोपाक|पाण्डुसोपाकः
पाण्डु- + सोपाक पाण्डु- + सोपाक, m. the son of a Caṇḍāla by a Vaidehī female, Man. 10, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाधिक
सोपाधिक सोपाधिक, i. e. स-उपाधि + क, adj. Special, limited by a condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपान|सोपानं
सोपान सोपान, n. Stairs, steps, Kathās. 26, 283; a ladder, Vikr. 39, 4; MBh. 5, 1017.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखारोहणसोपान
सुखारोहण- + सोपान सुखारोहण- + सोपान, i. e. सुख-आरोहण-, adj. having stairs easy ascent, MBh. 2, 1281.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपानत्क
सोपानत्क सोपानत्क, i. e. स-उपानह् + क, adj. With sandals, Man. 3, 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम|सोमं|सोमः
सोम सोम, i. e. 1. सु + म,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The acid juice of the Sarcostema viminalis, Chr. 292, 10 = Rigv. i. 85, 10; Bhag. 9, 20.<BR> 2. Sarcostema viminalis, MBh. 14, 274; Pañc. i. d. 346; personified, Pañc. iii. d. 111; 112.<BR> 3. Nectar, the beverage of the immortals.<BR> 4. Water.<BR> 5. The moon, Chr. 27, 8.<BR> 6. Kuvera, the god of wealth; Yama, the god of death; Śiva.<BR> 7. Air, wind,<BR> 8. Camphor.<BR> 9. A mountainous range.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Rice-gruel.<BR> 2. Sky.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसोम|नृसोमः
नृ- + सोम नृ- + सोम, m. a distinguished man (properly, a moon-like man), Ragh. 5, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमक
सोमक सोम + क, m.<BR> 1. Grandfather of Drupada.<BR> 2. pl. Name of the whole family, Johns. Sel. 42, 51; Chr. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमज|सोमजं|सोमजः
सोमज सोम-ज, n. Milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमन्
सोमन् सोमन् (cf. सोम), m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमप|सोमपः
सोमप and सोमपा सोम-पा̆, m.<BR> 1. One that drinks the juice of the moonplant; the performer of a sacrifice.<BR> 2. The Manes of the Brāhmaṇas, Man. 3, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपीतिन्
सोमपीतिन् सोमपीतिन्, i. e. सोम-पीति + इन्, m. A drinker of the Somajuice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमभू
सोमभू सोम-भू, m. The son of Soma, Budha, the regent of Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवन्त्|सोमवत्
सोमवन्त् सोम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessing Soma (with दिश्, the region of the Himālaya, cf. Sch. ad Kumāras. 1, 17), Rām. 1, 41, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसद्
सोमसद् सोम-सद्, m. The name of the Manes of the Sādhyas, Man. 3, 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाल|सोमालः
सोमाल सोमाल, properly a Prākṛ. word for Sskr. सुकूमार, Vararuci, ii. 30, ed. Cowell, adj. Soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमिन्
सोमिन् सोमिन्, i. e. सोम + इन्, m. A performer of a Soma sacrifice, Chr. 288, 1 = Rigv. i. 49, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठ|सोल्लुंठ|सोल्लुंठः|सोल्लुण्ठः
सोल्लुण्ठ सोल्लुण्ठ, m., and सोल्लुण्ठन सोल्लुण्ठन, n., i. e. स-उद्-लुण्ठ् + अ, or अन, Irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर|सौकरः
सौकर सौकर, i. e. सूकर + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Relating to a hog, Kir. 12, 53.<BR> 2. Hoggish, swinish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्य|सौकर्यं|सौकर्य्य|सौकर्य्यं
सौकर्य सौकर्य, i. e. सु-कर and सूकर + य, n.<BR> 1. Ease of effecting anything.<BR> 2. Easy and extempore preparation of food or medicine.<BR> 3. Hoggishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकुमार्य|सौकुमार्यं|सौकुमार्य्य
सौकुमार्य सौकुमार्य, i. e. सु-कुमार + य, n.<BR> 1. Youthfulness, Rām. 3, 52, 36.<BR> 2. Tenderness, Mālat. 57, 11.<BR> 3. Delicacy, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्म्य|सौक्ष्म्यं
सौक्ष्म्य सौक्ष्म्य, i. e. सूक्ष्म + य, n.<BR> 1. Minuteness.<BR> 2. Subtilty, Bhag. 13, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायिक|सौखशायिकः
सौखशायिक सौखशायिक, i. e. सुख-शायिन् + इक, and सौखशायनिक सौखशायनिक, i. e. सुख-शयन + इक, adj. Asking if one has slept well, Rām. 2, 12, 36 Gorr.; Ragh. 10, 14 (cf. Siddh. K. 83, b. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखसुप्तिक|सौखसुप्तिकः
सौखसुप्तिक सौखसुप्तिक, i. e. सुख-सुप्ति + इक, m. A bard who wakes a prince in the morning with music and song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौख्य|सौख्यं
सौख्य सौख्य, i. e. सुख + य, n. Pleasure, Pañc. 3, 15; happiness, Pañc. ii. d. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगत|सौगतः
सौगत सौगत, i. e. सु-गत + अ (vb. गम्), m.<BR> 1. A follower of the Bauddha faith, Lass. 2. ed. 88, 28; Śiś. 2, 28.<BR> 2. A heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं|सौगन्धः
सौगन्ध सौगन्ध, i. e. सु-गन्ध + अ, n.<BR> 1. A fragrant grass.<BR> 2. Fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं|सौगन्धिकः
सौगन्धिक सौगन्धिक, i. e. सौगन्ध + इक,<BR> I. adj. Fragrant, Nal. 13, 2.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A dealer in perfumes.<BR> 2. Sulphur.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. The white water lily, Indr. 2, 2.<BR> 2. A fragrant grass.<BR> 3. A ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध्य|सौगंध्य|सौगंध्यं|सौगन्ध्यं
सौगन्ध्य सौगन्ध्य, i. e. सु-गन्ध + य, n. Fragrance.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसौगन्ध्य
त्रि- + सौगन्ध्य त्रि- + सौगन्ध्य, n. three spices, Suśr. 1, 162, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचि|सौचिः
सौचि सौचि, and सौचिक सौचिक, i. e. सूचि + इ (?), or इक, m. A tailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजन्य|सौजन्यं
सौजन्य सौजन्य, i. e. सु-जन + य, n.<BR> 1. Goodness, Utt. Rāmac. 60, 4; magnanimousness, Rājat. 5, 192; generosity, Mālat. 66, 2.<BR> 2. Kindness, compassion, benevolence, Bhartṛ. 2, 45; clemency, Mālat. 140, 10.<BR> 3. Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौति|सौतिः
सौति सौति, i. e. सूत + इ, m. A proper name, Lass. 2. ed. 71, 1. 3, bel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्य|सौत्यं
सौत्य सौत्य, i. e. सूत + य, n. Carioteership, Nalod. 4, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्र|सौत्रः
सौत्र सौत्र, i. e. सूत्र + अ,<BR> I. adj. According to rule or precept.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 2. A radical which is no verbal root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रामणी
सौत्रामणी सौत्रामणी, i. e. सू̆-त्रामन् + अ, f. A kind of sacrifice, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, vii. 527.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदर्य|सौदर्यं
सौदर्य सौदर्य, i. e. स + उदर + य, adj. Entered into fraternity with, Daśak. in Chr. 189, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामनी
सौदामनी सौदामनी, and सौदामिनी सौदामिनी, i. e. सुदामन् + अ (in सौदामिनी, अ is irregularly changed to इ, as in सैरिन्ध्र), f.<BR> 1. Lightning, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 8 (मिनि).<BR> 2. One of the Apsaras.<BR> 3. A proper name, Mālat. 144, 1 (मिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदाम्नी
सौदाम्नी सौदाम्नी, i. e. सुदामन् + अ, f. Lightning (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिक|सौदायिकं
सौदायिक सौदायिक, i. e. सु-दाय + इक, adj. Received, by a woman as a nuptial gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदास|सौदासः
सौदास सौदास, i. e. सुदास् + अ, patronym., m. The son of Sudās, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौध|सौधः
सौध सौध, i. e. सुधा + अ, n.<BR> 1. A mansion, a palace, Pañc. 128, 8.<BR> 2. Silver.<BR> 3. Opal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधातकि
सौधातकि सौधातकि, i. e. सु-धातृ + अक + इ (cf. Pāṇ. iv. 1, 97), m. A proper name, Utt. Rāmac. 90, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन|सौनः
सौन सौन, i. e. सूना + अ,<BR> I. Relating to a slaughter-house.<BR> II. n. Butchers' meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनधर्म्य
सौनधर्म्य सौनधर्म्य, i. e. सौन-धर्म + य, n. Bloody hatred, MBh. 5, 715.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्द|सौनंद|सौनंदं|सौनन्दं
सौनन्द सौनन्द, i. e. सु-नन्द + अ, n. The club of Baladeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनिक|सौनिकः
सौनिक सौनिक, i. e. सूना + इक, m.<BR> 1. A butcher, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 31.<BR> 2. A vendor of the flesh of beasts or birds, Utt. Rāmac. 29, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन्दर्य|सौंदर्य|सौंदर्यं|सौन्दर्य्य|सौन्दर्य्यं
सौन्दर्य सौन्दर्य, i. e. सुन्दर + य, n. Beauty, loveliness, Mālat. 155, 17; Hit. ii. d. 148; Rājat. 5, 148; 381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्ण|सौपर्णं
सौपर्ण सौपर्ण, i. e. सु-पर्ण + अ,<BR> I. adj. Belonging or relating to Garuḍa, Utt. Rāmac. 132, 9.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The emerald.<BR> 2. Dry ginger.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौपर्ण
अति- + सौपर्ण अति- + सौपर्ण, adj. surpassing that (viz. the power) of Garuḍa, Rām. 4, 58, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णेय|सौपर्णेयः
सौपर्णेय सौपर्णेय, i. e. सुपर्णा. (see पर्ण), + एय, m. Garuḍa, a fabulous bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिक|सौप्तिकं
सौप्तिक सौप्तिक, i. e. सुप्ति + इक,<BR> I. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b " target="_blank">Page1064-b + 40</a>] adj. Somnolent, somniferous.<BR> II. n. Nocturnal combat, MBh. 10, title.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबल|सौबलः
सौबल सौबल, i. e. सु-बल + अ (patronym., MBh. 1, 5655), m. A proper name, Indr. 3, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ|सौभं
सौभ सौभ,<BR> I. m. The name of a people, Chr. 14, 24; 18, 35.<BR> II. n. The city of Hariścandra, suspended in mid-air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभग|सौभगं
सौभग सौभग, i. e. सु-भग + अ, n.<BR> 1. A gift of fortune, riches, Chr. 288, 9; 295, 15 = Rigv. i. 48, 9; 92, 15.<BR> 2. Welfare, MBh. 1, 724.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्र|सौभद्रः
सौभद्र सौभद्र, i. e. सु-भद्रा (a proper name, f.), + अ, metronym., m. The son of Subhadrā, MBh. 1, 1947; cf. Wils. Viṣṇu P. 460.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेय|सौभागिनेयः
सौभागिनेय सौभागिनेय, from सुभगा + इन् + ई + एय (see भग), m. The son of an auspicious mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्य|सौभाग्यं
सौभाग्य सौभाग्य, i. e. सु-भग + य, n.<BR> 1. Good fortune, auspiciousness, Megh. 30; Nal. 1, 10; Rājat. 5, 230; 282.<BR> 2. Beauty, charm, Ṛt. 6, 3; Utt. Rāmac. 155, 4.<BR> 3. Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्र|सौभ्रात्रं
सौभ्रात्र सौभ्रात्र, i. e. सु-भ्रातृ + अ, n. Brotherly affection, fraternity, MBh. 3, 355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस सौमनस, i. e. सु-मनस् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Pleasing.<BR> 2. Flowery.<BR> II. n. Pleasure, satisfaction, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 92, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्य|सौमनस्यं
सौमनस्य सौमनस्य, i. e. सु-मनस् + य, n. Enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक सौमिक, i. e. सोम + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Performed with the Soma juice, Man. 4, 26; relating to it.<BR> 2. Lunar.<BR> II. f. की, A sacrifice performed on the day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्र|सौमित्रः
सौमित्र and सौमित्रि सौमित्र, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a " target="_blank">Page1065-a + 41</a>] and त्रि, i. e. सुमित्रा (see मित्र), + अ, or इ, metronym., m. Lakṣmaṇa, Rām. 3, 49, 11 (त्रि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिक|सौमेधिकः
सौमेधिक सौमेधिक, i. e. सु-मेधा + इक, m. A sage, a seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुक|सौमेरुकं
सौमेरुक सौमेरुक, i. e. सु-मेरु + क, n. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य सौम्य, i. e. सोम + य,<BR> I. adj., f. मी.<BR> 1. Handsome, Sāv. 1, 14; pleasing, excellent, Man. 2, 125; used in addressing, Dear, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 11; Draup. 1, 14; Megh. 50; 84.<BR> 2. Strong, Pañc. 169, 6.<BR> 3. Placid, mild, Rām. 3, 52, 51; 55, 3.<BR> 4. Sacred to the moon.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Budha, regent of Mercury.<BR> 2. One of the Khaṇḍas, or divisions of the continent.<BR> 3. A class of Pitṛs or Manes, Man. 3, 199.<BR> 4. pl. Five stars in Orion's head.<BR> III. f. या, The Soma plant, Sarcostema viminalis, and several others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यता
सौम्यता सौम्य + ता, f., and सौम्यत्व सौम्य + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Beauty.<BR> 2. Gentleness, Indr. 5, 7 (ता).<BR> 3. Benevolence, Bhag. 17, 16 (त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर सौर, i. e. सूर्य, and सुरा, + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. री.<BR> 1. Solar, Pañc. iii. d. 187.<BR> 2. Sacred to Sūrya, i. e. the sun, Man. 5, 86.<BR> 3. Celestial.<BR> 4. Spirituous,<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A solar month.<BR> 2. A solar day.<BR> 3. The planet Saturn.<BR> III. f. री, The wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरथ|सौरथः
सौरथ सौरथ, i. e. सु-रथ + अ, m. A hero, MBh. 3, 13300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ सौरभ, i. e. सु-रभी̆ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Fragrant.<BR> II. f. भी, A cow, Brāhmaṇav. 1, 12.<BR> III. n. Fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय सौरभेय, i. e. सुरभी̆ + एय,<BR> I. m. An ox.<BR> II. f. यी, A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यं|सौरभ्यः
सौरभ्य सौरभ्य, i. e. सुरभि + य,<BR> I. m. Kuvera, the god of wealth.<BR> II. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b " target="_blank">Page1065-b + 40</a>] n.<BR> 1. Fragrance, Lass. 92, 8.<BR> 2. Pleasingness, beauty.<BR> 3. Fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैन्धव सौरसैन्धव, i. e. सुर-सिन्धु + अ, adj. Relating to the Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं|सौराष्ट्रकः
सौराष्ट्रक सौराष्ट्रक, i. e. सुराष्ट्र + क (see राष्ट्र), n. A sort of white or bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरि|सौरिः
सौरि सौरि, i. e. सूर्य + इ, m. Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिक|सौरिकः
सौरिक सौरिक, i. e. सुरा̆ + इक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Celestial.<BR> 2. Spirituous.<BR> 3. Due for liquors, Man. 8, 159.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Heaven.<BR> 2. A vendor of spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्चल|सौवर्च्चल|सौवर्च्चलं
सौवर्चल सौवर्चल, i. e. सुवर्चल + अ, n.<BR> 1. सोचल् salt.<BR> 2. Natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्ण|सौवर्णं|सौवर्णः
सौवर्ण सौवर्ण, i. e. सु-वर्ण + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Golden, Pañc. 174, 22.<BR> 2. Weighing a सुवर्ण (see सुवर्ण under वर्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्णिक|सौवर्णिकः
ऽसौवर्णिक -सौवर्णिक, i. e. सु-वर्ण (see वर्ण), + इक, in चतुःसौवर्णिक, i. e. चतुर्-, adj. Weighing four सुवर्णस् (see the last), Man. 8, 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवस्तिक|सौवस्तिकः
सौवस्तिक सौवस्तिक, i. e. स्वस्ति + इक,<BR> I. adj. Benedictory.<BR> II. m. A family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविद|सौविदः
सौविद सौविद, i. e. सुविद + अ, and सौविदल्ल सौविदल्ल, i. e. सुविदल्ल + अ, m. A guard or attendant on the womens' apartment, Sāh. D. 281, 1 (-दल्ल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर|सौवीरं|सौवीरः
सौवीर सौवीर, i. e. सु-वीर + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The name of a country.<BR> 2. pl. Its inhabitants, Draup. 4, 12; 8, 27.<BR> 3. The king of the Sauvīras, ib. 4, 7.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The fruit of the jujube.<BR> 2. Antimony.<BR> 3. Sour gruel.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुसौवीर
सिन्धु- + सौवीर सिन्धु- + सौवीर, m. pl. name of a people, Rām. 1, 12, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीरक|सौवीरकं|सौवीरकः
सौवीरक सौवीर + क, m. An inhabitant of Sauvīra, Rām. 3, 53, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौष्ठव|सौष्ठवं
सौष्ठव सौष्ठव, i. e. सुष्ठु + अ, n.<BR> 1. Excellence, beauty, Mālav. 20, 3.<BR> 2. Excess.<BR> 3. Fleetness, MBh. 1, 5368 (read सौष्ठवेन); lightness, suppleness, Mālav. 14, 9.<BR> 4. A part of a drama.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठव|असौष्ठवं
अ- + सौष्ठव अ- + सौष्ठव, adj. disarrayed, Mālat. 11, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससौष्ठव
स- + सौष्ठव स- + सौष्ठव, adj. 1. excellent. 2. quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द|सौहार्दः|सौहार्द्द|सौहार्द्दं|सौहार्द्दः
सौहार्द सौहार्द, and सौहार्द्य सौहार्द्य, i. e. सु-हृद् + अ or य, n.<BR> 1. Affection, Mālat. 2, 18 (द).<BR> 2. Friendship, Hit. i. d. 99, M.M. (द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहित्य|सौहित्यं
सौहित्य सौहित्य, i. e. सु-हित + य (vb. धा), n.<BR> 1. Satiety, satisfaction.<BR> 2. Fullness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौहित्य|अतिसौहित्यं
अति- + सौहित्य अति- + सौहित्य, n. excessive satiety, Man. 4, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद|सौहृदं
सौहृद सौहृद, and सौहृद्य सौहृद्य, i. e. सु-हृद् + अ or य, n. Friendship, Vikr. d. 10 (द); Pañc. ii. d. 130 (द). (Pañc. v. d. 19, सौहृद, A friend, --perhaps a misreading.)<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसौहृद
दृढ-सौहृद दृढ-सौहृद, adj. having true friendship, Pañc. 239, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्नेहसौहृद
विगत-स्नेह-सौहृद विगत-स्नेह-सौहृद (vb. गम्), adj. abandoning love and friendship, Sund. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
1. स्कन्द् स्कन्द्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To jump.<BR> 2. To jump upwards, to ascend.<BR> 3. To burst out, MBh. 1, 5105.<BR> 4. To jump downward, to drop, to fall, Bhaṭṭ. 22, 11.<BR> 5. To perish, Man. 7, 84.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्कन्न.<BR> 1. Trickled down, Rām. 1, 38, 27.<BR> 2. Sprinkled, MBh. 1, 2434.<BR> 3. Fallen.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To emit (the seminal fluid), Man. 2, 180; 9, 150.<BR> 2. To neglect. Man. 6, 9.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To assail, to besiege, Śiś. 1, 51.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, To jump out, MBh. 4, 810.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, Caus. To assail, Man. 7, 196.<BR> --With आ आ, To assail, Mālat. 151, 9; Bhaṭṭ. 17, 11.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To assail, Bhaṭṭ. 16, 10. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b " target="_blank">Page1066-b + 42</a>]<BR> --With परि परि, स्कन्द् and ष्कन्द्, To spring about, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 75.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To spring forward, MBh. 1, 134; to spring down, 3, 15587.<BR> 2. To burst forth, MBh. 1, 2380. प्रस्कन्न, Fallen. m. A sinner, one who has violated the usages of his caste.<BR> --Caus. To cross (a river), MBh. 4, 1971.<BR> --Cf. Lat. scandere; σκάνδαλον, σχαστήο (χ for κ by the influence of σ), probably σκάζω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
† 2. स्कन्द् स्कन्द्, स्कन्ध् स्कन्ध्, i. 10, Par. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
3. स्कन्द् स्कन्द्, see स्कुन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कंदः|स्कन्दः
स्कन्द 1. स्कन्द् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Skanda or Kārttikeya, the god of war, Megh. 44.<BR> 2. A king.<BR> 3. The body.<BR> 4. The bank of a river.<BR> 5. A clever man (cf. स्कन्ध).<BR> 6. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 417 (or घ्राणस्कन्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दक|स्कंदक|स्कंदकः|स्कन्दकः
स्कन्दक स्कन्द + क, m. A soldier, Rājat. 5, 174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दन|स्कंदन|स्कंदनं|स्कन्दनं
स्कन्दन स्कन्द् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Effusion.<BR> 2. Purging.<BR> 3. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध्|स्कंध्
स्कन्ध् स्कन्ध्, see 2. स्कन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध|स्कंध|स्कंधः|स्कन्धः
स्कन्ध स्कन्ध,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The shoulder, Pañc. 144, 23.<BR> 2. The body, Mālat. 84, 17.<BR> 3. The trunk of a tree, Pañc. iii. d. 149.<BR> 4. A branch, Pañc. 134, 5.<BR> 5. A branch of human knowledge.<BR> 6. A book, Bhāg. P. i. ii., etc.<BR> 7. The five objects of sense.<BR> 8. The five forms of mundane consciousness, in the Bauddha philosophy, Śiś. 2, 26; cf. Burnouf, Introd. à l'Hist. du Buddh. 475.<BR> 9. A road.<BR> 10. Part of an army.<BR> 11. War.<BR> 12. A multitude.<BR> 13. An agreement.<BR> 14. A king.<BR> 15. A wise or learned man.<BR> 16. A heron.<BR> II. f. धा.<BR> 1. A branch.<BR> 2. A creeper.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. sculdor, sculder; O.H.G. scultarra; probably σπάθη; Lat. scapula (for old scaphula, cf. rufus, s. v. रुधिर, and rutilus, ib. for old ruthilus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालस्कन्ध|कालस्कंध|कालस्कन्धः
काल- + स्कन्ध काल- + स्कन्ध, m. the name of several plants, e. g. Diospyros embryopteris Pers., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a " target="_blank">Page1067-a + 42</a>] Suśr. 1, 138, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापृष्ठगलस्कन्ध
महा-पृष्ठ-गल- + स्कन्ध महा-पृष्ठ-गल- + स्कन्ध, adj. having a large back, neck, and shoulders, Hiḍ. 2, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्कन्ध|राजस्कन्धः
राजस्कन्ध राजस्कन्ध, i. e. राजन्-, m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणोन्नामितस्कन्ध
विषाण-उद्-नामित- + स्कन्ध विषाण-उद्-नामित- + स्कन्ध (vb. नम्), adj. whose shoulders reach to his horns, Hit. iii. d. 144 (but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 932).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणोल्लिखितस्कन्ध
विषाण-उद्-लिखित- + स्कन्ध विषाण-उद्-लिखित- + स्कन्ध, adj. whose shoulders are slit up by horns, i. e. brave, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 932.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्कन्ध
वृष- + स्कन्ध वृष- + स्कन्ध, adj. having the shoulders of a bull, Rām. 3, 55, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्कन्ध|स्कंधस्कंध|स्कन्धस्कन्धः
स्कन्ध- + स्कन्ध स्कन्ध- + स्कन्ध (repeated), m. every shoulder, Kām. Nītis. 9, 19 (where the visarga must be erased), Hit. iv. d. 122, v. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्|स्कंधस्
स्कन्धस् स्कन्धस्, n.<BR> 1. The shoulder.<BR> 2. The trunk of a tree (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धावार|स्कंधावार|स्कन्धावारः
स्कन्धावार स्कन्धावार, i. e. स्कन्ध-आ-वृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. An army, or division of it attached to the king.<BR> 2. A royal residence.<BR> 3. A camp, Hit. 107, 21; MBh. 1, 6950.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कंधिकः|स्कन्धिकः
स्कन्धिक स्कन्धिक, i. e. स्कन्ध + इक, m. An ox of burthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिन्|स्कंधिन्
स्कन्धिन् स्कन्धिन्, i. e. स्कन्ध + इन्, m. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धोपनेय
स्कन्धोपनेय स्कन्धोपनेय, i. e. स्कन्ध-उप-नेय (vb. नी), adj. m. (viz. संधि), A form of peace-offering in which fruit or grain is presented as token of submission, Hit. iv. d. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भ्|स्कंभ्
स्कम्भ् स्कम्भ्, i. 1, Ātm., ii. 5, स्कभ्नु and 9, स्कभ्ना, नी, Par.<BR> 1. To make firm (to create), Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 40.<BR> 2. To support (ved.).<BR> 3. To stop, to obstruct, to impede.<BR> --With the prep. वि वि, Caus. विष्कम्भित,<BR> 1. Impeded, shown away, Pañc. 29, 6.<BR> 2. Obstructed, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b " target="_blank">Page1067-b + 43</a>] precluded, Pañc. 56, 10.<BR> --Cf. स्तम्भ् and स्तम्ब; Lat. scabellum, scamnum; Goth. ga-skapjan, ga-skafts; A.S. scapen, sceápan, sceaft; O.H.G. scafan, scafôn, scoppôn, to stop; probably σκῆπτρον, σκήπτω, σκίμπτω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु स्कु, ii. 5, स्कुनु, and 2, स्कुना, नी, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. † To go by leaps.<BR> 2. To cover, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 82.<BR> 3. † To lift.<BR> 4. † To approach.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, To cover in one's turn, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 82.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ob-scurus, scutum, corium, cavere, cautus, causa; probably A.S. scuva, umbra; Goth. skôh; A.S. scoh, sceo; O.H.G. scur, tugurium; A.S. scúnian; O.H.G. skiuhan also A.S. scawian, sceawian, to see (concerning the signification, cf. वृ, ὁράω); ἐπι-σκύνιον, σκῦτος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुन्द्|स्कुंद्
† स्कुन्द् स्कुन्द्, स्कन्द् स्कन्द्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To jump or go by leaps.<BR> 2. To raise (cf. 1. स्कन्द्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुम्भ्|स्कुंभ्
† स्कुम्भ् स्कुम्भ्, ii. 5, स्कुभ्नु, and 9, स्कुभ्ना, नी, Par.<BR> 1. To stop or hinder.<BR> 2. To hold; cf. स्कम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद्
स्खद् स्खद्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To cut.<BR> 2. To hurt or kill.<BR> 3. To discomfit. to defeat.<BR> 4. To fatigue, to exhaust.<BR> 5. To destroy.<BR> 6. To make firm.<BR> --Cf. क्षद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् स्खल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To stumble, to tumble, Hit. iii. d. 132.<BR> 2. To fall, Mālat. 73, 2.<BR> 3. To stutter, Mālat. 162, 10; to hesitate, Hit. ii. d. 63.<BR> 4. To err, to fail, Rām. 1, 13, 10.<BR> 5. To disappear, Śṛṅgārat. 7. स्खलित,<BR> 1. Shaken, Mālat. 148, 15.<BR> 2. Shaking, wavering.<BR> 3. Staggering, Śiś. 9, 78; interrupted, faltering, Utt. Rāmac. 70, 6; stammering, ib. 95, 12.<BR> 4. Fluctuating, Pañc. 188, 10.<BR> 5. Drunk.<BR> 6. Hesitating.<BR> 7. Slipped, fallen.<BR> 8. Stopped, Śāk. d. 131; obstructed, Vikr. d. 49. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a " target="_blank">Page1068-a + 43</a>]<BR> 9. Confounded, Śāk. d. 132; Śiś. 9, 83. n.<BR> 1. Tumbling, Pañc. i. d. 316; ii. d. 188; falling.<BR> 2. Deviating from virtue, fault, Vikr. d. 89; sin, d. 115.<BR> 3. Stratagem.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To stagger, Arj. 8, 14.<BR> 2. To tumble, Pañc. 36, 16.<BR> --Cf. छल; Lat. scelus, culpa; Goth. skula, skulan; A.S. sceal, sculan, scyld; cf. also स्फर्, स्फुर्, स्फल्, स्फुल्, which may be originally identical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अ- + स्खलित अ- + स्खलित, adj. not stumbled, Pañc. ii. d. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन|स्खलनं
स्खलन स्खल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Stumbling.<BR> 2. Falling, Caurap. 13; Utt. Rāmac. 44, 13 (flowing through).<BR> 3. Falling from virtue.<BR> 4. Tripping in speech.<BR> 5. Falling together.<BR> 6. Rubbing, Śiś. 9, 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खुड्
† स्खुड् स्खुड्, i. 6, Par. To cover (v. r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तक्
† स्तक् स्तक्, i. 1, Par. To resist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्
स्तन् स्तन्, i. 1, Par. To sound, to sigh.<BR> --i. 10, To thunder, Chr. 290, 6 = Rigv. i. 64, 6. स्तनित, n.<BR> 1. Thunder, Man. 4, 103.<BR> 2. The noise of clapping the hands.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. नि नि, ष्टन्,<BR> 1. To sigh, MBh. 3, 14060.<BR> 2. To bewail, Rām. 2, 77, 8.<BR> --Cf. στένω; Icel. stynja; N.H.G. stöhnen; Lat. tonare (cf. ved. तन् + यतु = स्तनयित्नु, thunder), tonitru; A.S. thunor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविद्युत्स्तनित
स-विद्युत्- + स्तनित स-विद्युत्- + स्तनित, adj. with lightning and thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन|स्तनः
स्तन स्तन, m. The nipple, the female breast, Vikr. d. 7; Pañc. ii. d. 98.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलस्तन
गल- + स्तन गल- + स्तन,<BR> I. m. a small fleshy process resembling nipples, hanging from the throat of some species of the Bengal goat, Pañc. iii. d. 265.<BR> II. f. नी, a she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्तन
त्रि- + स्तन त्रि- + स्तन, adj., f. नी, having three breasts, Pañc. v. d. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुतस्तन
प्रस्नुत- + स्तन प्रस्नुत- + स्तन, adj., f. नी, from whose breast [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b " target="_blank">Page1068-b + 40</a>] drops milk, Rājat. 5, 76; Utt. Rāmac. 64, 10 (a token of maternal love, cf. Arji Bordschi, in the German Journal, Ausland, 1858, p. 823; Stan. Julien, Mém. sur les Contrées Occident., par Hiouen Thsang. ii. 152).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतस्तन
संहत- + स्तन संहत- + स्तन (vb. हन्), adj., f. नी, whose breasts are very contiguous to each other, Rām. 3, 52, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनन|स्तननं
स्तनन स्तन् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sound.<BR> 2. Groaning.<BR> 3. The grumbling of clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनंधय|स्तनन्धय|स्तनंधयः|स्तनन्धयः
स्तनंधय स्तनंधय, i. e. स्तन + म्-धे + अ,<BR> I. adj. Suckling, Mālat. 164, 11 (read दृष्टस् तनयः स्त्˚).<BR> II. m., and f. या and यी, An infant, Ragh. 14, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नु|स्तनयित्नुः
स्तनयित्नु स्तनयित्नु, i. e. स्तन्, i. 10, + इत्नु, m.<BR> 1. Thunder, Utt. Rāmac. 122, 12.<BR> 2. Lightning, Utt. Rāmac. 55, 8.<BR> 3. A cloud.<BR> 4. Sickness.<BR> 5. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्य|स्तन्यं
स्तन्य स्तन्य, i. e. स्तन + य, n. Milk, Pañc. 238, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धता
स्तब्धता स्तब्ध + ता (vb. स्तम्भ्), f. Stubbornness, MBh. 5, 1536.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धत्व|स्तब्धत्वं
स्तब्धत्व स्तब्ध + त्व, n. in अ-, Unsteadiness, Hit. i. d. 98, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीकरण
स्तब्धीकरण स्तब्धीकरण, i. e. स्तब्ध-कृ + अन, n. Making rigid, paralysing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीभाव
स्तब्धीभाव स्तब्धीभाव, i. e. स्तब्ध-भू + अ, m. Growing stiff, torpidity, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्
स्तम् स्तम्, see सम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तंबः|स्तम्बः
स्तम्ब स्तम्ब (cf. स्तम्भ्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A post to which an elephant is tied.<BR> 2. A mountain.<BR> 3. A shrub.<BR> 4. A clump of grass, a cluster, Pañc. 140, 25.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. A post.<BR> 2. Stupidity [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a " target="_blank">Page1069-a + 44</a>] insensibility.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. stapel, a prop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशस्तम्ब
कुश- + स्तम्ब कुश- + स्तम्ब, m. 1. a cluster of Kuśa grass, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 13. 2. the name of a place of pilgrimage, MBh. 13, 1714.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्तम्ब|ब्रह्मस्तम्बः
ब्रह्मस्तम्ब ब्रह्मस्तम्ब, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. the world, Mahāvīrac. 51, 4; 86, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरस्तम्ब|शरस्तंब|शरस्तम्बः
शर- + स्तम्ब शर- + स्तम्ब, m. a clump of reeds, Pañc. 140, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरि|स्तंबकरि|स्तम्बकरिः
स्तम्बकरि स्तम्बकरि, m. Corn or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघ्न|स्तंबघ्न|स्तम्बघ्नः
स्तम्बघ्न स्तम्बघ्न, i. e. स्तम्ब-हन् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Turf-destroying.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A hoe.<BR> 2. A sickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बेरम|स्तंबेरम|स्तंबेरमः|स्तम्बेरमः
स्तम्बेरम स्तम्बेरम, i. e. स्तम्ब + इ-रम् + अ, m. An elephant, Ragh. 5, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ्|स्तंभ्
स्तम्भ् स्तम्भ्, ii. 5, स्तभ्नु, and 9, स्तभ्ना, नी, Par.<BR> 1. To make firm (to create), ved.<BR> 2. To stop, to make immovable, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 45.<BR> 3. To oppose, to hurtle, Arj. 6, 13.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm. To become immovable, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 55.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्तब्ध,<BR> 1. Stopped, blocked up.<BR> 2. Immovable, MBh. 3, 2214.<BR> 3. Firm, Utt. Rāmac. 76, 1; hard, Pañc. 190, 17; rigid, Daśak. in Chr. 187, 13; stiff, Hit. 51, 8, M.M.<BR> 4. Hard-hearted, Hit. iv. d. 102.<BR> 5. Stubborn, Bhag. 18, 28.<BR> 6. Coarse, Bhāg. P. 4, 2, 8.<BR> 7. Stupid, Śṛṅgārat. 21.<BR> 8. Insensible.<BR> 9. Indifferent, Hit. ii. d. 104.<BR> 10. Paralysed.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To support, MBh. 3, 827.<BR> 2. To make immovable, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 10; to stop, MBh. 3, 10378. स्तम्भित,<BR> 1. Stopped, contained, Megh. 61; constrained, Mālat. 140, 4.<BR> 2. Stupified, paralysed, Rām. 1, 75, 17; insensible, Utt. Rāmac. 159, 3.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, after which the initial स्त् becomes ष्ट्,<BR> 1. To bind, Böhtl. Chr. 229, verse 178.<BR> 2. To rest on, Mahāvīrac. 74, 5.<BR> 3. To rely on, Bhag. 9, 8. अवष्टब्ध,<BR> 1. Supported.<BR> 2. Stopped.<BR> 3. Paralysed.<BR> 4. Opposed.<BR> 5. Near, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 72.<BR> 6. Hanging from. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b " target="_blank">Page1069-b + 42</a>]<BR> 7. Surpassed, overcome.<BR> 8. Bound.<BR> 9. Wrapped up.<BR> --With पर्यव परि-अव,<BR> 1. To surround, Mālat. 86, 4; 8.<BR> 2. To surround and oppose, Utt. Rāmac. 122, 18.<BR> --With समव सम्-अव, To encourage, Chr. 29, 34.<BR> --With उद् उद्, Caus. उत्तम्भय, To cherish, support, Kir. 2, 48. उत्तम्भिल,<BR> 1. Supported, upheld.<BR> 2. Erect, Utt. Rāmac. 60, 3.<BR> 3. Stopped.<BR> --With नि नि, निस्तब्ध, Stopped.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> I. प्रतिस्तब्ध, Stopped.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With वि वि, ष्टम्भ्,<BR> 1. To fix (to create), MBh. 1, 6694; with पादौ, to stand immovable, Hit. ii. d. 120.<BR> 2. To stop, MBh. 3, 2123; to restrain, Chr. 29, 36. विष्टब्ध,<BR> 1. Fixed, well supported, Man. 9, 296.<BR> 2. Placed in or upon.<BR> 3. Hindered.<BR> 4. Made motionless.<BR> --Caus. To stop, to restrain, MBh. 3, 10314. विष्टम्भित, Stopped, Śāk. d. 106.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To support, Bhag. 3, 43.<BR> 2. To corroborate, Rām. 2, 14, 13.<BR> 3. To stop, Rām. 2, 63, 47.<BR> 4. To hurtle, Pañc. 190, 15. संस्तब्ध,<BR> 1. Made firm.<BR> 2. Corroborated.<BR> 3. Stopped.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To corroborate, Rām. 2, 34, 53.<BR> 2. To make immovable, MBh. 1, 7291.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To corroborate, Rām. 2, 64, 11.<BR> --Cf. στέμϕυλον, στέμϐω (cf. स्तम्ब); O.H.G. stamphôn; O.N. stôfn; O.H.G. stam; A.S. stemn (based on स्तम्भ् + न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अ- + स्तब्ध अ- + स्तब्ध, adj. unconquered, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अ- + स्तब्ध अ- + स्तब्ध, adj. unconquered, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 82.<BR> II. प्रतिष्टब्ध, Stopped, obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तम्भ स्तम्भ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A post, a pillar, Hit. 49, 11; Pañc. i. d. 142.<BR> 2. A stem, Hit. iv. d. 71 (कदली-, adj. Having the stem of a कदली, i. e. faintly supported).<BR> 3. Obstruction. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a " target="_blank">Page1070-a + 41</a>]<BR> 4. Stupefaction, Kir. 12, 28.<BR> 5. Stupidity.<BR> 6. Insensibility, Bhartṛ. 3, 6.<BR> 7. Coldness, Mālat. 80, 7.<BR> 8. Paralysis, Mālat. 21, 7.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. steb, a trunk (of a tree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्तम्भ
निःस्तम्भ निःस्तम्भ, i. e. निस्-, adj. without pillars, Kām. Nītis. 11, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रस्तम्भ|नेत्रस्तंभ|नेत्रस्तम्भः
नेत्र- + स्तम्भ नेत्र- + स्तम्भ, m. rigidity of the eyes, Suśr. 2, 232, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवाष्पस्तम्भम्
स-वाष्प-स्तम्भ + म् स-वाष्प-स्तम्भ + म्, adv. suppressing tears, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्तम्भ|स्मरस्तम्भः
स्मर- + स्तम्भ स्मर- + स्तम्भ, m. the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भक
स्तम्भक स्तम्भ् + अक, adj. Restraining, Rām. 1, 30, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकर|स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तम्भकर स्तम्भ-कर, m. A fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तम्भन स्तम्भ् + अन,<BR> I. m. One of Kāma's arrows.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Supporting, holding upright, Pañc. i. d. 405.<BR> 2. Stopping.<BR> 3. Suppressing the use of the faculties by magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिन्|स्तंभिन्
ऽस्तम्भिन् -स्तम्भ् + इन्, adj. Restraining, Nalod. 1, 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर स्तर, i. e. स्तॄ + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A layer.<BR> 2. A bed.<BR> II. f. री, Smoke.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्तर
स- + स्तर स- + स्तर, m. a bed of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरिमन्
स्तरिमन् and स्तरीमन् स्तरी̆मन्, i. e. स्तृ + ई̆मन्, m. A bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तव|स्तवः
स्तव स्तव, i. e. स्तु + अ, m.<BR> 1. Praising, MBh. 13, 7662.<BR> 2. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक स्तवक i. e. स्तु + अक, m.<BR> 1. Praise.<BR> 2. A panegyrist.<BR> 3. A cluster of blossoms, Pañc. iii. d. 155; Vikr. d. 125; a designation of chapters in the Kusumāñjali.<BR> 4. A multitude.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमस्तवक|कुसुमस्तवकः
कुसुम- + स्तवक कुसुम- + स्तवक, m. a nosegay, Bhartṛ. 2, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकित
स्तवकित स्तवकित, i. e. स्तवक + इत, adj. Full of blossoms.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवकुसुमस्तवकित
अभिनव-कुसुम-स्तवक + इत अभिनव-कुसुम-स्तवक + इत, adj. having clusters of fresh blossoms, Vikr. d. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीदृङ्नीरजस्तवकित
नारी-दृश्-नीरज- + स्तवकित नारी-दृश्-नीरज- + स्तवकित, adj. having as (i. e. instead of) clusters of blossoms the lotus-like eyes of the women, Rājat. 5, 480.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवन|स्तवनं
स्तवन स्तवन, i. e. स्तु + अन, n. Praising, a hymn, Brahmav. 2, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिघ्
† स्तिघ् स्तिघ्, ii. 5, Ātm.<BR> 1. To ascend.<BR> 2. To assail.<BR> --Cf. Goth. steigan; A.S. stígan, staeger, a stair; O.H.G. steigal; A.S. sticol; στείχω, στίχη, στοῖχος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिप्
† स्तिप् स्तिप्, स्तेप् स्तेप्, i. 1, Ātm. To ooze, to drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिभि|स्तिभिः
स्तिभि स्तिभि, m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्
स्तिम् स्तिम्, † स्तीम् स्तीम्, i. 4, Par. To be wet. स्तिमित,<BR> 1. Wet, Mālat. 16, 5; Rājat. 5, 481.<BR> 2. Immovable, Ragh. 1, 73; Rām. 3, 52, 12 (adv.); steady, fixed (of the eye), Megh. 37 (Sch.): benumbed, Mālat. 12, 2.<BR> 3. Soft, Śāk. d. 192.<BR> 4. Unsteady, tossing, Mālat. 50, 13; trembling, Mālav. d. 27 (? rather, immovable; वामं संधि-स्तिमित-वलयम्, The left hand, of which the bracelet is immovable, on account of the contact or support of the hip). n. Moisture, Pañc. i. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितत्व|स्तिमितत्वं
स्तिमितत्व स्तिमित + त्व (see the last), n. Absence of motion, absorption, Mālat. 47, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्वि स्तीर्वि, i. e. स्तॄ + वि, m. An officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तु
स्तु स्तु, ii. 2, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To praise, Rām. 2, 65, 53; ved. Ātm. To be praised, Chr. 294, 7 = Rigv. i. 92, 7 (स्तवे instead of स्तवते, i. 1).<BR> 2. To worship by hymns, MBh. 1, 721.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि, ष्टु, To praise, Pañc. 172, 14.<BR> --With समभि सम्-अभि, To praise, Rām. 1, 14, 26.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To praise, Mālat. 76, 13.<BR> 2. To begin, Utt. Rāmac. 162, 10; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a " target="_blank">Page1071-a + 41</a>] Mālav. 13, 21.<BR> 3. To say, to report, Hit. 100, 16. प्रस्तुत,<BR> 1. Praised.<BR> 2. Declared, Mālat. 16, 15; vowed, Hit. 120, 21.<BR> 3. Approached.<BR> 4. Desired, expected.<BR> 5. Prepared, ready, being at hand, Hit. 87, 21.<BR> 6. Done.<BR> 7. Made of.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. To cause to begin, MBh. 1, 6. प्रस्तावित, Caused to be told, Mālat. 47, 1.<BR> --With वि वि, ष्टु, To praise, MBh. 1, 7056.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To praise, Indr. 2, 9. संस्तवान, Eloquent. संस्तुत,<BR> 1. Praised, Rājat. 5, 9.<BR> 2. Known, Utt. Rāmac. 76, 2.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, 1. disagreeing, Śāk. d. 33. 2. unfit, Pañc. i. d. 41 (but cf. v. r., Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 404).<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To praise, MBh. 3, 12709.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, To praise, MBh. 1, 2122.<BR> --Cf. perhaps Æol. στύμα, στόμα (questionable, on account of Zend. श्तमन्, the muzzle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अ- + स्तु अ- + स्तु, adj. 1. extraneous. 2. unsuitable, Pañc. 36, 23; cf. i. d. 193.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाप्रस्तुतम्
यथा-प्रस्तुत + म् यथा-प्रस्तुत + म्, adv. conformably to the circumstances, Mālat. 146, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुच्
† स्तुच् स्तुच्, i. 1, Ātm. To be clear, to be propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्
ऽस्तुत् -स्तु + त्, latter part of comp. words, Praising; e. g. छन्दस्-, adj. Praising by hymns, Bhāg. P. 5, 20, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुति|स्तुतिः
स्तुति स्तु + ति, f. Praise, Sund. 2, 4; Utt. Rāmac. 136, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्तुति
निस्- + स्तुति निस्- + स्तुति, adj. without praising (anything,) MBh. 12, 8832.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनक|स्तुनकः
स्तुनक स्तुनक, m. A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्
स्तुभ् स्तुभ्,<BR> 1. (i. e. स्तु-भा), i. 1, Par. To praise.<BR> 2. † i. 1, Ātm. To stupify, to be stupified; cf. स्तुम्भ्.<BR> --Caus. ved. To praise, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 88, 6.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, ष्टुभ्, ved. To praise, ib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ|स्तुभः
स्तुभ स्तुभ, m. A he-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुम्भ्|स्तुंभ्
† स्तुम्भ् स्तुम्भ्, ii. 5, स्तुभ्नु, and 9, स्तुभ्ना, नी (cf. स्तम्भ्), Par.<BR> 1. To stop (cf. Rigv. v. 54, 1).<BR> 2. To stupify.<BR> 3. To expel.<BR> --Cf. στῡ́ϕω, στῦϕελός, στυμνός, στυϕεδανός, and τυϕεδανός, probably τυϕλός, τυϕώδης; perhaps O.H.G. stumph, stumbal; A.S. stypel; Goth. and A.S. dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप्
† स्तूप् स्तूप्, i. 4 and 10, Par. To heap, to pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप|स्तूपः
स्तूप स्तूप, m.<BR> 1. A heap, a pile, a Bauddha construction for keeping holy relics.<BR> 2. A funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
1. स्तृ स्तृ, ii. 5, स्तृणु, and स्तॄ स्तॄ, ii. 9, स्तृणा, णी, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. To spread, to expand.<BR> 2. To cover, Ragh. 7, 55.<BR> --Caus. To cover, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 48.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, To cover, to fill, Kir. 14, 29.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To spread, MBh. 3, 15142.<BR> 2. To cover, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 15. आस्तरणीय, n. A cover, a carpet, Rām. 5, 11, 19.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ, To cover (fire with water, i. e. to extinguish), MBh. 1, 1495.<BR> --With उप उप, ptcple. pf. pass. उपस्तीर्ण, Arranged, MBh. 2, 2033.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To spread, Rām. 3, 49, 9.<BR> 2. To arrange, MBh. 1, 6975.<BR> 3. To cover, Śiś. 9, 18.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रस्तृत, Disappeared.<BR> --With वि वि, To spread, Man. 1, 51; 7, 33. विस्तृत.<BR> 1. Diffused.<BR> 2. Diffuse.<BR> 3. Wide opened, MBh. 3, 12905.<BR> 4. Broad, Matsyop. 13; ample, Nalod. 3, 14. विस्तीर्ण, Large, great, Pañc. 51, 20; iii. d. 264.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to spread, Pañc. 171, 3.<BR> 2. To extend, Man. 7, 188. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a " target="_blank">Page1072-a + 39</a>]<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To spread, MBh. 1, 7163.<BR> 2. To cover, MBh. 2, 1774.<BR> --Cf. στόρνυμι, στορεύς, στρώννυμι, στλεγγίς; Lat. sternere, strages, struere, stringo; O.H.G. sturm; A.S. stearm, storm; strene, lectus; Goth. straujan; A.S. streowian, sternere; A.S. strion, thesaurus, strionan; O.H.G. sterbjan (old Caus.), interficere, sterban; A.S. stearfian, steorfan, mori; strec; O.H.G. strac; A.S. streccan, a-stregdan, a-strican, probably stregan, stredan; ge-strangian, To strengthen, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तीर्ण
सु-विस्तीर्ण सु-विस्तीर्ण, adj. very large, Hit. 79, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
2. स्तृ स्तृ, see स्पृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
3. स्तृ स्तृ, probably 2. अस् + तृ, A star, Chr. 293, 1 = Rigv. i. 87, 1.<BR> --Cf. ἀστήρ, τεῖρος; Æol. τέῤῥος; Goth. stairno; A.S. steorra; Lat. stella (see तार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष्
स्तृक्ष् स्तृक्ष्, i. 1. Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह्
† स्तृह् स्तृह्, स्तॄह् स्तृह्, i. 6, Par. To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ स्तॄ, see स्तृ; स्तॄह् स्तॄह्, see स्तृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन्
स्तेन् स्तेन्, 1, 10 (rather a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To steal, Man. 4, 256; 8, 333.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन|स्तेनं|स्तेनः
स्तेन स्तेन, m. A thief, Man. 8, 197.<BR> --Cf. prebably στερέω; Goth. stilan; A.S. stelan, stal, stalian, stalu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप्
† स्तेप् स्तेप्, i. 10, Par. To throw; see स्तिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेम|स्तेमः
स्तेम स्तेम, i. e. स्तिम् + अ, m. Wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेय|स्तेयं
स्तेय स्तेय, perhaps anomal. स्तेन + य, n. Theft, robbery, Man. 2, 116; Vikr. d. 139.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेय|अस्तेयं
अ- + स्तेय अ- + स्तेय, n. not stealing, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन् स्तेयिन्, i. e. स्तेय + इन्, m. A thief, Man. 9, 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तै
स्तै स्तै, see स्नै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन|स्तैनं
स्तैन स्तैन, and स्तैन्य स्तैन्य, i. e. स्तेन + अ, or य, n. Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक स्तोक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Little, Pañc. 263, 25; short, Pañc. 245, 13; small, few, Pañc. 31, 5.<BR> 2. Low, Bhartṛ. 2, 10.<BR> II. ˚कम्, adv.<BR> 1. A little, Pañc. 170, 6.<BR> 2. Cf. बहुतरम्, see बहु.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The Cātaka, Cuculus melanoleucus.<BR> 2. A drop of water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तोक
अ- + स्तोक अ- + स्तोक, adj. much, Mālat. 161, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकक|स्तोककः
स्तोकक स्तोक + क, m. The Cātaka, Cuculus melanoleucus, Man. 12, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ स्तोतृ, i. e. स्तु + तृ, m., f. त्री, n. Praising, a praiser, Chr. 297, 11 = Rigv. i. 112, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्र|स्तोत्रं
स्तोत्र स्तोत्र, i. e. स्तु + त्र, n. Praise, Lass. 53, 17; Rājat. 5, 351.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथास्तोत्र
अन्यथा- + स्तोत्र अन्यथा- + स्तोत्र, n. ironical praise, Yājñ. 2, 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभ|स्तोभं|स्तोभः
स्तोभ स्तोभ, i. e. स्तुम्भ्, and स्तुभ् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Stopping.<BR> 2. Contumely.<BR> 3. Latter part of the name of some verses of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्
† स्तोम् स्तोम्, i. 10 (a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम स्तोम, i. e. partly स्तु + म,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Praise, Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 48, 14.<BR> 2. Sacrifice.<BR> 3. A heap, a quantity, multitude, Utt. Rāmac. 31, 7.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. The head.<BR> 2. Wealth.<BR> 3. Grain.<BR> 4. A stick bound with iron.<BR> III. adj. Crooked.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोम|व्रात्यस्तोमः
व्रात्य- + स्तोम व्रात्य- + स्तोम, m. a sacrifice to recover the rights forfeited by an improper delay of the investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्येन|स्त्येनः
स्त्येन स्त्येन (cf. स्तेन), m.<BR> 1. A thief.<BR> 2. Nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै स्त्यै, ष्ट्यै ष्ट्यै, i. 1, Par. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a " target="_blank">Page1073-a + 42</a>]<BR> 1. To be collected or joined.<BR> 2. Pass. To increase, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 3 (to spread round about).<BR> 3. To sound.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्त्यान,<BR> 1. Thick, gross, bulky.<BR> 2. Soft, bland. n.<BR> 1. Thickness.<BR> 2. Idleness.<BR> 3. Echo, Utt. Rāmac. 45, 2.<BR> --With प्र प्र, ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्रस्तीत and प्रस्तीम.<BR> 1. Crowded, clustering.<BR> 2. Sounded.<BR> --Cf. probably στενός; Lat. stipare (Caus.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री स्त्री, probably 1. सू + तृ + ई, f.<BR> 1. A woman, Pañc. iii. d. 61.<BR> 2. A female in general, Draup. 4, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरस्त्री
अमर- + स्त्री अमर- + स्त्री, f. an Apsaras, Kir. 10, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलस्त्री
कुल- + स्त्री कुल- + स्त्री, f. a respectable or chaste woman, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 277; Daśak. in Chr. 191, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुलस्त्री
सु-कुल- + स्त्री सु-कुल- + स्त्री, f. a respect able woman, Cāṇ. 36 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणस्त्री
पण- + स्त्री पण- + स्त्री and पण्य-, f. a courtesan, Mṛcch. 127, 20; Pañc. iii. d. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्त्री
सु- + स्त्री सु- + स्त्री, f. a brave wife, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरस्त्री
सुर- + स्त्री सुर- + स्त्री, f. an Apsaras, a nymph, Vikr. d. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीक
ऽस्त्रीक -स्त्री + क, a substitute for स्त्री, at the end of a comp. adj.; e. g. स-, adj. With women, Śāk. 61, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीता
स्त्रीता स्त्री + ता, f., and स्त्रीत्व स्त्री + त्व, n. Womanhood, Chr. 52, 19 (त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंस
स्त्रीपुंस स्त्री-पुंस् + अ, m. Wife and husband, Man. 1, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपूर्विन्
स्त्रीपूर्विन् स्त्रीपूर्विन्, i. e. स्त्री-पूर्व + इन्, adj. One who has been at first a female, Chr. 63, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमन्त्|स्त्रीमत्
स्त्रीमन्त् स्त्री + मन्त्, m. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण स्त्रैण, i. e. स्त्री + न,<BR> I. adj. Female, Feminine.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Womanhood, Utt. Rāmac. 100, 8.<BR> 2. The female sex, Bhartṛ. suppl. 24 (Sch., children).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठद्विजबालवृद्धविकलस्त्रैण
भूयिष्ठ-द्विज-बाल-वृद्ध-विकल-स्त्रैण भूयिष्ठ-द्विज-बाल-वृद्ध-विकल-स्त्रैण, adj. consisting [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b " target="_blank">Page1073-b + 42</a>] for the greatest part of Brāhmaṇas, children, old and sick persons, and women, Utt. Rāmac. 114, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ स्थ (vb. स्था), adj. Staying, abiding; e. g. गर्भ-, Being in the womb, Hit. pr. d. 27, M.M. जन-, adj. Living amongst men, Bhāg. P. 7, 15, 56. जल-, adj. Existing in water, Rām. 4, 13, 10. तट-, adj.<BR> 1. Standing on the shore.<BR> 2. Indifferent, Utt. Rāmac. 60, 2. दूर-, adj. Standing aloof, Man. 2, 202. भू-तल-, adj. Standing, being on the surface of the earth, Pañc. 106, 6. यौवन-, adj., f. था, Marriageable, Sāv. 1, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग्
स्थग् स्थग्, i. 1, Par. To cover, Śiś. 9, 21. स्थगित, Hidden, covered, Kir. 14, 31; Rājat. 5, 415 (सरस्वती स्थगिता, ‘Sarasvatī has hidden herself,’ i. e. I can scarcely find words).<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cover, Mālat. 7, 8; to veil, Mālat. 149, 15.<BR> 2. To cause inability of perceiving anything, Utt. Rāmac. 78, 2.<BR> --Cf. στέγω, στέγη, τέγη; Lat. tegere; O.H.G. dakjan; A.S. theccan, thaca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग स्थग् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cheating, a rogue.<BR> 2. Shameless.<BR> II. f. गी, A betel box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगन|स्थगनं
स्थगन स्थग् + अन, n. Covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगिका
स्थगिका स्थगिका, i. e. स्थग + का, f.<BR> 1. A courtesan, Śukas. Narr. 7, MS.<BR> 2. The office of the betel-bearer, Pañc. v. r. of the MSS. H., I., and K., ad Kos. 63, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगु|स्थगुः
स्थगु स्थगु, m. A hump on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिल|स्थंडिल|स्थंडिलं|स्थण्डिलं
स्थण्डिल स्थण्डिल, n.<BR> 1. A square place prepared for a sacrifice, MBh. 13, 6550; Rājat. 6, 87.<BR> 2. A barren field.<BR> 3. A heap of clods, Man. 10, 71.<BR> 4. A boundary, a landmark, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलसितक|स्थंडिलसितक|स्थण्डिलसितकं
स्थण्डिलसितक स्थण्डिलसितक (cf. स्थण्डिल), n. An altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलेशय|स्थंडिलेशय|स्थण्डिलेशयः
स्थण्डिलेशय स्थण्डिलेशय, i. e. स्थण्डिल + इ-शय, m. A devotee sleeping on a place prepared for a sacrifice, Lass. 2. ed. 49, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति स्थपति, i. e. स्था, Caus., + अति, and perhaps स्थ-पति,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An architect, Pañc. 10, 4.<BR> 2. A carpenter, a wheelwright, Rām. 2, 63, 2, Seramp.<BR> 3. The performer of the Vṛhaspati sacrifice, MBh. 1, 2029.<BR> 4. A carioteer.<BR> 5. A king or chief.<BR> 6. A guard or attendant of the womens' apartment.<BR> II. adj. Chief, best.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करस्थपति|पुष्करस्थपतिः
पुष्कर- + स्थपति पुष्कर- + स्थपति, m. a name of Śiva, MBh. 13, 1207 (erroneously written पुस्कर-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट स्थपुट, adj.<BR> 1. Distressed.<BR> 2. Bent with pain, Mālat. 78, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल्
† स्थल् स्थल् (akin to स्था, cf. the next), i. 1, Par. To stand or be firm.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. stallan, stellan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल|स्थलं
स्थल स्थल् + अ, or rather स्था + ल,<BR> I. n., and f. ली.<BR> 1. Firm or dry ground, Hit. i. d. 89, M.M. (ल).<BR> 2. Place, Vikr. d. 79 (लि); Pañc. 161, 15 (ल).<BR> II. n., and f. ला, A spot drained and raised.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A mound, a terrace, Megh. 67.<BR> 2. A tent.<BR> 3. Point, topic.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. stal, stall; A.S. stal, stael; O.H.G. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b " target="_blank">Page1074-b + 42</a>] stullan; Goth. ga-stalds; O.H.G. stelza, stolz; also A.S. stillan, stille.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकृतस्थली
अद्रि-कृत- + स्थली अद्रि-कृत- + स्थल, f. ली, an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशस्थल|कुशस्थलं
कुश- + स्थल कुश- + स्थल, n., and f. ली, names of towns, MBh. 2, 614 (ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तहर्म्यस्थल
कॢप्त-हर्म्य-स्थल कॢप्त-हर्म्य-स्थल, adj., f. ली, of which the ground of the palaces was made, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डस्थल|गंडस्थल
गण्ड- + स्थल गण्ड- + स्थल, n., and f. ली, 1. the cheek, Śṛṅgārat. 7 (ल); Daśak. in Chr. 199, 2 (ली). 2. an elephant's temple, Pañc. i. d. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनस्थली
जघन-स्थली जघन-स्थली, f. the buttocks, Śiś. 9, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थली
प्रसव- + स्थली प्रसव- + स्थल, f. ली, a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुस्थल
मरु- + स्थल मरु- + स्थल, n. a desert, Hit. i. d. 10, M.M.; 80, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्थल
महा- + स्थल महा- + स्थल, f. ली, the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्स्थल
वक्षस्- + स्थल वक्षस्- + स्थल, n. breast, Hit. iv. d. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलकमल|स्थलकमलं|स्थलकमलः
स्थलकमल स्थल-कमल, n., and -कमलिनी, f. A shrub, Hibiscus mutabilis, Megh. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलज
स्थलज स्थल-ज, adj.<BR> 1. Growing on earth, Man. 6, 13.<BR> 2. Terrestrial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलता
स्थलता स्थल + ता, in शुष्क-स्थल + ता, f. Dryness, Pañc. 84, 19; 79, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशय|स्थलेशयः
स्थलेशय स्थलेशय, i. e. स्थल + इ-शय, m. An amphibious animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवि|स्थविः
स्थवि स्थवि, probably vb. स्था (see the next), m. A weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर स्थविर, probably for स्थावर, cf. स्थाविर,<BR> I. adj., f. रा.<BR> 1. Fixed, firm.<BR> 2. Old, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 12.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An old man.<BR> 2. A beggar.<BR> 3. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ स्थविष्ठ, स्थवीयंस् स्थवीयंस्, see स्थूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्था
स्था स्था, i. 1, तिष्ठ, Par., and in some significations only Ātm., but in epic poetry Ātm. as well as Par., against the rules of the Gramm.<BR> 1. To stand, Hit. i. d. 97; with जानुभ्याम्, To kneel, Vikr. 63, 6; with शासने, To obey, Vikr. d. 155.<BR> 2. To cease to move, to stand still, to stop, Vikr. d. 20; Rām. 1, 60, 19; to wait, Vikr. 88, 17; to be restrained, Man. 7, 108.<BR> 3. To stay, MBh. 2, 732; to abide, Man. 7, 37 (शासने, He may abide by their decision).<BR> --Impers. pass., Hit. 46, 2, M.M.; Lass. 56, 2, स्थीयताम्, It may be abided, viz. by you, i. e. you may abide.<BR> 4. With instr. To practise, to use what the instrumental expresses, Pañc. 31, 18 (सामादिभिस्, To use conciliatory speech, etc.); 76, 20 (मौनव्रतेन, To be silent).<BR> 5. To be, Man. 8, 158; to exist, Man. 7, 8.<BR> 6. To remain, Lass. 51, 25; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1075-a " target="_blank">Page1075-a + 47</a>] Man. 4, 111; to stand at one's side, Hit. i. d. 72, M.M.<BR> 7. With an absol. it implies duration of the action expressed by the absol.; e. g. या स्थिता व्याप्य, Which ever fills, Śāk. d. 1; Vikr. 14, 5 (परिक्रम्योपविश्य स्थित, After having walked up and down, he sits down and remains sitting).<BR> 8. To be at hand, Man. 5, 104; Hit. 50, 21.<BR> 9. Ātm. To stand firm, MBh. 1, 5558.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्थित.<BR> 1. Got up, risen.<BR> 2. Standing, Chr. 17, 24.<BR> 3. Steady, firm, immovable.<BR> 4. Upright, virtuous.<BR> 5. Stayed, stopped.<BR> 6. Desisted, Pañc. v. d. 40 (from singing).<BR> 7. Having lived (सुखे, happily), Pañc. ii. d. 95; कथं स्थितासि, How did you do ? Vikr. 72, 6; living, Rām. 3, 53, 59.<BR> 8. Being, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 11; Pañc. 149, 13 (एवं स्थिते, The matter being thus); Pañc. 136, 3 (लम्बमानौ यथा स्थितौ, How they hang down).<BR> 9. Established, determined, Chr. 28, 17.<BR> 10. Agreed, promised.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. fut. pass. स्थेय,<BR> 1. To be fixed or determined.<BR> 2. To be placed. m.<BR> 1. A judge, an arbitrator, Hit. iv. d. 1.<BR> 2. A domestic priest.<BR> --Comp.<BR> उच्चैःस्थेय, i. e. उच्चैस्-, n. standing upright, Bhartṛ. 2, 61.<BR> दुस्-, n. difficult standing, MBh. 12, 11090.<BR> --Caus. स्थापय,<BR> 1. To place, Vikr. 78, 7; Hit. i. d. 112.<BR> 2. To establish, Rām. 3, 54, 19.<BR> 3. To restrain, to stop, Śāk. 6, 16; Vikr. 10, 19.<BR> 4. To keep, Man. 7, 44.<BR> 5. To cause to exist, to found, Man. 1, 62.<BR> 6. To cause to be durable, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 21.<BR> 7. To let live, Hit. 121, 14.<BR> 8. To give in marriage, MBh. 1, 2576.<BR> --With the prep. अधि [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1075-b " target="_blank">Page1075-b + 46</a>] अधि, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm.),<BR> 1. To stand on, Man. 4, 78; MBh. 2, 2541, शिरः पादेनाधि स्थास्यामि, I shall put my foot on his head.<BR> 2. To be supported, to rest on, Rām. 1, 34, 34.<BR> 3. To stay, MBh. 1, 3572.<BR> 4. To remain, Chr. 32, 31, शरा अन्तराधिष्ठिताः, The arrows remained in the sky.<BR> 5. To inhabit, MBh. 3, 12198.<BR> 6. To stand, MBh. 1, 8325.<BR> 7. To be, MBh. 1, 2867.<BR> 8. To command, Man. 7, 114; to govern, Rām. 2, 1, 25; to lead, Utt. Rāmac. 91, 8.<BR> 9. To pass over, Rām. 1, 31, 19.<BR> 10. To surpass, MBh. 3, 14652; to overcome, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 72.<BR> 11. To ascend to, Chr. 288, 2 = Rigv. i. 49, 2.<BR> 12. To do; with प्रसादम्, To show favour, Mālat. 140, 11. अधिष्ठित (and धिष्ठित),<BR> 1. Guided, Utt. Rāmac. 3, 7.<BR> 2. Fixed, established, Pañc. 29, 7.<BR> 3. Occupied, Hit. 56, 20.<BR> 4. Overpowered, Pañc. 30, 5.<BR> 5. Guarded, Utt. Rāmac. 38, 13.<BR> 6. Presiding, Pañc. 97, 1.<BR> 7. Standing, MBh. 13, 835.<BR> --Comp.<BR> दुस्-, adj. wrongly performed, MBh. 7, 3314. n. remaining unbecomingly in some place, MBh. 12, 3084.<BR> --With समधि सम्-अधि, To administer, MBh. 2, 199.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To stand near, Man. 11, 111.<BR> 2. To follow, to obey, Man. 2, 9.<BR> 3. To remain, Lass. 56, 10.<BR> 4. To execute, to perform, Rām. 1, 12, 3; to do, Pañc. 192, 10; to act, Vikr. 24, 7; to practise, Daśak. in Chr. 182, 6.<BR> 5. To govern, Draup. 4, 12. अनुष्ठित,<BR> 1. Agreed to, done accordingly.<BR> 2. Done, Rām. 1, 51, 6; तथा-अनुष्ठिते, Afterwards, thereupon, Pañc. 43, 14; 42, 2; 37, 22. n. Action, Pañc. 43, 15. Desider. तिष्ठास, To wish to imitate, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 6.<BR> --With अव अव, Ātm.<BR> 1. To withdraw, Hit. 47, 22.<BR> 2. To stand firm, Vedāntas. in Chr. 218, 5; to keep ground, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 70 (= Hit. ii. d. 120, v. r.); to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1076-a " target="_blank">Page1076-a + 45</a>] stand ready, Pañc. 91, 6 (with dat., for).<BR> 3. To be decided, Śāk. 23, 11.<BR> 4. To remain, Man. 8, 145; Pañc. 127, 17.<BR> 5. To be present, MBh. 1, 4826.<BR> 6. To stay; किम् अत्रावस्थाय मया कर्तव्यम्, What shall<BR> I. do here ? Hit. 59, 1, M.M.; with instr. To practise, Pañc. 50, 13 (cf. the simple vb.) अव-स्थित,<BR> 1. Standing, Vikr. d. 160; Rājat. 5, 49.<BR> 2. Abiding, remaining firm, Rām. 3, 50, 15.<BR> 3. Steady, Man. 7, 60.<BR> 4. Being, Pañc. 180, 20 (एवम् अवस्थिते, Matters being in this state). यथावस्थित, As it was, Pañc. 196, 18. ˚तम्, adv. Truly (as it happened), Pañc. 237, 19.<BR> 5. Engaged in, prosecuting.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. 1. unsteady, changed, Utt. Rāmac. 47, 4. 2. fickle, unchaste, Rām. 5, 51, 10; Man. 11, 138.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to stand, to place, Hit. 61, 4, M.M.<BR> 2. To cause to stay, to leave, Vikr. 35, 3.<BR> --With पर्यव परि-अव, Ātm.<BR> 1. To rely on, MBh. 1, 4029.<BR> 2. To exist everywhere, Bhag. 2, 65.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव, To stand opposite, Sund. 3, 24.<BR> --Caus. To collect; with आत्मानम्, To recover, Vikr. 8, 1.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव, व्यव-स्थित,<BR> 1. Separated, going away, Pañc. 57, 9, अग्रे, He took the head.<BR> 2. Extracted.<BR> 3. Constant, Lass. 2. ed. 39, 10.<BR> 4. Declared.<BR> 5. Appointed.<BR> 6. Fixed, Man. 10, 68; based, Mālat. 70, 7.<BR> 7. Depending on, Hit. iv. d. 98.<BR> 8. Staying, having rested at the same place, Chr. 20, 1.<BR> 9. Restrained, Utt. Rāmac. 135, 8 (-विषय, Of which the sphere is restrained to one alone).<BR> 10. Standing, Chr. 27, 1; Pañc. 229, 21 (अग्रे, Was standing in front of him).<BR> 11. With वाक्ये, Obeying, Rām. 3, 51, 35.<BR> 12. Existing, Pañc. 76, 23.<BR> 13. One who has agreed, Man. 8, 156.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To establish, Daśak. in Chr. 184, 19.<BR> 2. To perform, Ragh. 14, 53.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1076-b " target="_blank">Page1076-b + 44</a>] समव सम्-अव, समवस्थित,<BR> 1. Ready, MBh. 3, 633.<BR> 2. Standing immovable, Vikr. d. 4.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To stop (a chariot), MBh. 3, 887.<BR> 2. To found, (a tribe), MBh. 1, 4365.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To be near at hand, Man. 9, 87.<BR> 2. To stand on, Chr. 290, 9 = Rigv. i. 64, 9; to sit on, MBh. 3, 11776.<BR> 3. To stay, to remain, Hit. 95, 1, M.M.<BR> 4. To walk toward, Man. 11, 104.<BR> 5. To turn to; अपयानम् आस्थित, Turning to withdraw, i. e. being about to withdraw, Śiś. 9, 84; कां बुद्धिम् आस्थाय, What did you think (when...)? Chr. 21, 5.<BR> 6. To ascend, MBh. 1, 3677 (a chariot).<BR> 7. To assume, Pañc. iii. d. 20; Rām. 3, 50, 26 (a shape).<BR> 8. To apply, MBh. 3, 11964 (a weapon); Man. 2, 88 (care).<BR> 9. To observe, Man. 7, 226; with वृत्तिम्, To behave, Man. 2, 133.<BR> 10. To perform, Man. 2, 103; MBh. 3, 8514 (religious austerities).<BR> 11. To act, to behave, Nal. 9, 8. आस्थित,<BR> 1. Standing on (with acc.), Chr. 36, 16.<BR> 2. Stayed.<BR> 3. Occupied.<BR> 4. Applied to, having recourse to, having assumed, Rām. 3, 50, 26.<BR> 5. Undergone, Lass. 2. ed. 90, 49.<BR> 6. Spread.<BR> 7. Observing, following, Man. 5, 36.<BR> 8. Practising, exhibiting, Lass. 53, 17; with acc., Vikr. d. 130 (absorbed in).<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, Ātm. To approach carnally, MBh. 3, 10754.<BR> --With समुपा सम्-उप-आ, To observe (a law). MBh. 1, 7452.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To undergo, Chr. 49, 4 (समास्थितस् तपो घोरम्, He performed great austerities).<BR> 2. To apply, MBh. 3, 11967; with वृत्तिम्, To act, Man. 4, 2; with योगम्, To exert one's self, Man. 7, 44.<BR> 3. To perform, Rām. 1, 56, 24. समास्थित, Seated.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To get up, to rise, Rām. 2, 72, 24; Vikr. 31, 18; उत्तिष्ठमान, Being about to rise, Pañc. i. d. 408. उत्थाय-उत्थाय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1077-a " target="_blank">Page1077-a + 44</a>] Whenever one rises, Hit. i. d. 3, M.M.<BR> 2. To rouse one's self, Bhag. 2, 3.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. उत्थित.<BR> 1. Rising, Lass. 2. ed. 46, 23.<BR> 2. Arising (as revenue), Hit. iv. d. 121.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To lead away (one's wife from her father's house), Lass. 22, 1 (cf. 24, 9).<BR> 2. To lift, Hit. 91, 13, M.M.; to raise, Rām. 2, 72, 23 (a fallen person); to lift out, Hit. 21, 7, M.M.<BR> 3. To arouse, MBh. 1, 1887.<BR> 4. To reanimate, MBh. 1, 3297.<BR> --With अनूद् अनु-उद्, To rise after one, Ragh. 2, 24.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्,<BR> 1. To rise, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 14.<BR> 2. To rise to (with acc.), Utt. Rāmac. 83, 5.<BR> --With प्रत्युद् प्रति-उद्, To rise to salute, Man. 2, 119.<BR> --With व्युद् वि-उद्, To incite, MBh. 1, 7404.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To rise together, Chr. 13, 7.<BR> 2. To rise, Sāv. 1, 8.<BR> 3. To return to life, MBh. 3, 16574. समुत्थित,<BR> 1. Swollen up, Rām. 3, 49, 51.<BR> 2. Arisen, produced, Pañc. 57, 15.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To raise, MBh. 1, 6588.<BR> 2. To reanimate, Rām. 1, 1, 85.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To stand near, Rām. 1, 13, 38; to be imminent, Pañc. 86, 25.<BR> 2. To stand opposite, Man. 2, 48.<BR> 3. To be at hand, MBh. 3, 11671.<BR> 4. To serve, Rām. 1, 16, 28; to wait on, Śāk. 3, 12; Vikr. 3, 8 (Ātm.); to salute, Mālat. 2, 3 (Ātm.).<BR> 5. To oblige (by presents), Ragh. 18, 21.<BR> 6. To adore, MBh. 1, 4405.<BR> 7. To embrace, MBh. 3, 10754.<BR> 8. To approach, Rām. 1, 25, 4; to arrive at, Man. 3, 76.<BR> 9. To fall to one's share, Pañc. 194, 5; MBh. 3, 3043. उपस्थित,<BR> 1. Arrived, come, Man. 3, 103.<BR> 2. Staying, standing by or near, Hit. 47, 2, M.M.<BR> 3. Near, Rām. 2, 51, 18; impending, Hit. i. d. 3, M.M.<BR> 4. Caused.<BR> 5. Got.<BR> 6. Felt.<BR> 7. Cleansed.<BR> 8. Done.<BR> 9. Known.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To bring near, Śāk. 28, 9; to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1077-b " target="_blank">Page1077-b + 40</a>] order to be brought, Utt. Rāmac. 22, 8.<BR> 2. To supply, Rām. 1, 26, 2 (a ship).<BR> 3. To place, Rām. 2, 3, 18.<BR> --With अभ्युप अभि-उप, To adore, Bhāg. P. 5, 7, 12. अभ्युपस्थित, Accompanied, MBh. 3, 16132.<BR> --With पर्युप परि-उप,<BR> 1. To surround, Rām. 2, 64, 1.<BR> 2. To wait on, Rām. 2, 32, 15. पर्युपस्थित, Imminent, MBh. 3, 13027.<BR> --With प्रत्युप प्रति-उप, प्रत्युपस्थित,<BR> 1. Imminent, MBh. 3, 1920.<BR> 2. Present, Utt. Rāmac. 156, 14.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप,<BR> 1. To approach, Chr. 7, 17; Pañc. ii. d. 13.<BR> 2. To fall in the way, Hit. 76, 8, M.M.<BR> 3. To send, Śāk. d. 43. समुपस्थित, Imminent, Chr. 5, 4.<BR> --With नि नि, निष्ठित,<BR> 1. Firm, fixed.<BR> 2. Certain.<BR> 3. Staying in, Bhag. 13, 17.<BR> 4. Versed in, Rām. 1, 12, 20.<BR> 5. Engaged in.<BR> --With परिनि परि-नि, परिनिष्ठित, Very skilled in, Rām. 1, 9, 8.<BR> --Caus. परिनिष्ठापित, Taught, Utt. Rāmac. 35, 10.<BR> --With परि परि, To stand round about, to surround, Pañc. 51, 19. परिष्ठित, Standing, Lass. 23, 6.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.),<BR> 1. To set out, Vikr. 12, 10; to depart (with the acc., to), MBh. 3, 2401.<BR> 2. To come, Vikr. 37, 17. प्रस्थित, Set out, Śāk. 7, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR> पूर्व-, adj. set out before, Vikr. 6, 6.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To push on, Rājat. 5, 415.<BR> 2. To induce to retire, Hit. 130, 10.<BR> 3. To send away, Rām. 2, 9, 2; to despatch, Hit. 88, 8, M.M.; to dismiss, MBh. 3, 2716.<BR> --With प्रत्यभिप्र प्रति-अभि-प्र, Ātm. To depart, MBh. 1, 683.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, Ātm.<BR> 1. To depart, MBh. 1, 8140.<BR> 2. To spread, MBh. 1, 3709.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, Ātm. To depart, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-a " target="_blank">Page1078-a + 45</a>] MBh. 2, 1198. सम्प्रस्थित,<BR> 1. Departed, MBh. 3, 8540.<BR> 2. Being about to set off, Rām. 2, 38, 13.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To stand firm, to be supported, Pañc. i. d. 93.<BR> 2. To depend upon, MBh. 1, 6190.<BR> 3. To stay, MBh. 3, 11855. प्रतिष्ठित,<BR> 1. Fixed, Pañc. i. d. 93; staying, Pañc. iii. d. 214.<BR> 2. Secured, acquired.<BR> 3. Supported, Man. 8, 163.<BR> 4. Placed.<BR> 5. Married.<BR> 6. Comprised.<BR> 7. Infixed, present, Bhag. 3, 15.<BR> 8. Applied, Man. 8, 226.<BR> 9. Applicable.<BR> 10. Completed, done, Pañc. 86, 20.<BR> 11. Consecrated.<BR> 12. Famous (rather प्रतिष्ठा + इत), Nal. 22, 12.<BR> 13. Valued.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-, 1. well rooted, Pañc. iii. d. 51. 2. well set up, well consecrated, Hit. pr. d. 45, M.M. 3. celebrated.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To set up, to erect, Rājat. 5, 38.<BR> 2. To place, Chr. 12, 28.<BR> 3. To offer, Man. 3, 135. प्रतिष्ठापित, Appointed, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 20.<BR> --With संप्रति सम्-प्रति, To rest on, MBh. 1, 8359.<BR> --With वि वि, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.),<BR> 1. To spread, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 92, 5.<BR> 2. To stand apart, to stand, MBh. 1, 6559. विष्ठित, Stopping, Rām. 3, 52, 11.<BR> --With सम् सम्, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par.),<BR> 1. To stand close together, MBh. 3, 15716.<BR> 2. To stand on, to be on, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR> 3. To agree, to conform to, Mṛcch. 15, 12.<BR> 4. To be completed, Man. 5, 98.<BR> 5. To exist, to live, Pañc. 96, 13.<BR> 6. To perish, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 9. संस्थित,<BR> 1. Heaped, covered (painted ?), Rām. 5, 10, 4.<BR> 2. Frequented, Man. 8, 371.<BR> 3. Contiguous.<BR> 4. Like.<BR> 5. Placed in or on, Pañc. i. d. 105 (नियोग-, Being in office).<BR> 6. Residing, Pañc. 60, 24.<BR> 7. Lying, Hit. iv. d. 130.<BR> 8. Abiding, Lass. 53, 9.<BR> 9. Fixed.<BR> 10. Stopped, MBh. 3, 1763.<BR> 11. Concluded.<BR> 12. Dead, Man. 3, 247.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-, 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-b " target="_blank">Page1078-b + 43</a>] very contiguous (to each other), Rām. 3, 52, 28. 2. well situated. 3. being well. 4. well defined, circumscribed.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To collect, to compose, Vikr. 29, 15 (one's self.)<BR> 2. To place, Pañc. 174, 21.<BR> 3. To subject, Man. 9, 2.<BR> 4. To restrain, to stop.<BR> 5. To kill, MBh. 1, 4610. संस्थापित,<BR> 1. Accumulated.<BR> 2. Restrained.<BR> 3. Fixed, established.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, परिसंस्थित, Standing together round about, MBh. 1, 4827.<BR> --Cf. ἵστημι, ἔστην, σταμίν, στῆμα, στήμων, στάμνος, ἱστός, ἐπίσταμαι, στήλη, σταθερός, σταθμός, στῆθος, σθένος, τόπος (from the Caus.); Lat. stare, sistere, stamen, stupere (Caus.), stupidus; cf. स्थूल; O.H.G. stân, stên; Goth. and A.S. standan (frequent.); O.H.G. standa; A.S. stidh, stand, cupellus; stadhelian; O.H.G. stat, locus; stat, stad, ripa; tur-studil; A.S. studu, postis; O.H.G. stunt; A.S. stund; A.S. staef (based on the Caus.), stif, stifian (or to स्त्यै ?). On nouns like स्थवि, etc., are based σταυρός, στύω, στῦλος, στόα; Goth. staujan, stôjan; O.H.G. stauuan; cf. also A.S. stow, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंस्थ
