असुस्थ|असुस्थः
अ-सु- + स्थ अ-सु- + स्थ, adj. not being well, dejected, Hit. iii. d. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु स्थाणु (vb. स्था),<BR> I. adj. Firm, steady, fixed, immovable, Chr. 46, 20; MBh. 1, 7291.<BR> II. m. and n. The trunk of a tree, Man. 9, 44; Bhāṣāp. 128.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. A stake, a post, Pañc. i. d. 55.<BR> 2. A spear.<BR> 3. A nest of white ants.<BR> 4. Śiva, Vikr. d. 1; Rām. 3, 53, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुवत्
स्थाणुवत् स्थाणु + वत्, adv. Like a post, Pañc. i. d. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थांडिलः|स्थाण्डिलः
स्थाण्डिल स्थाण्डिल, i. e. स्थण्डिल + अ, m.<BR> 1. An ascetic who sleeps on the place prepared for a sacrifice.<BR> 2. A religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ स्था + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Who or what stands.<BR> --Cf. Lat. stator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थान|स्थानं
स्थान स्थान, i. e. स्था + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Staying, Lass. 28, 10; stay, state, Utt. Rāmac. 51, 5; Man. 7, 56 (forces); position, Hit. i. d. 51, M.M.<BR> 2. Middle state, as neither loss nor gain (equality), calmness, Rām. 3, 52, 2 (corr. नहि मे जीवितं स्थाने, My life, i. e. my whole being, is disquieted).<BR> 3. Firmness of troops.<BR> 4. Keeping in array.<BR> 5. Halt.<BR> 6. Place, Pañc. 133, 5; 37, 8; a holy place, Chr. 46, 26; the right place, Hit. ii. d. 70.<BR> 7. Country, Hit. i. d. 169, M.M.<BR> 8. An altar, Vikr. d. 43.<BR> 9. An open place in a town.<BR> 10. A dwelling-place, Hit. iii. d. 5; house, Chr. 60, 37; Śṛṅgārat. 11.<BR> 11. A town.<BR> 12. Office, Rājat. 5, 297.<BR> 13. The part of an actor, Vikr. 3, 9.<BR> 14. Degree, rank, Hit. i. d. 168, M.M.<BR> 15. Object, Man. 2, 136; Pañc. 82, 12.<BR> 16. Likeness.<BR> 17. Intimation (cf. स्थानक), Lass. 7, 5.<BR> 18. Interval.<BR> II. loc. ने, adv.<BR> 1. Fitly, properly, justly, Vikr. 8, 16; in the right moment, Śāk. 37, 34.<BR> 2. Sometimes, MBh. 1, 6845.<BR> 3. Because.<BR> 4. Instead, Pañc. 37, 21.<BR> 5. Like, as, Pañc. 52, 1; 55, 22.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. δύστηνος (i. e. δυσ-στηνος), ἄ-στηνος, ἀ-στήν, ἀσταίνω, δυσταίνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अ-स्थान अ-स्थान, n. unsuitable, wrong place, Pañc. 10, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचितस्थान
अन्-उचित- + स्थान अन्-उचित- + स्थान, n. the same, Pañc. 64, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मत्स्थान
अस्मद्- + स्थान अस्मद्- + स्थान, n. our place; loc. ने, instead of us (me), Pañc. 83, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःस्थान
उच्चैस्- + स्थान उच्चैस्- + स्थान, n. elevation in rank, Man. 7, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकस्थान
एक- + स्थान एक- + स्थान, n. same place; loc. ने, together, Pañc. 85, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मस्थान|कर्म्मस्थान
कर्मस्थान कर्मस्थान, i. e. कर्मन्-, n. a government building, Rājat. 5, 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपस्थान
कोप- + स्थान कोप- + स्थान, n. an object of wrath, i. e. easy to be injured, Lass. 41, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्थान|जनस्थानं
जन- + स्थान जन- + स्थान, n. the name of a wood, Utt. Rāmac. 17, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मस्थान
जन्मस्थान जन्मस्थान, i. e. जन्मन्-, n. birthplace, home, Pañc. 247, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीयस्थान
तदीय- + स्थान तदीय- + स्थान, n. its place, Vikr. 71, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्थान
धन- + स्थान धन- + स्थान, n. treasury, Rājat. 4, 621.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणस्थान
धर्म-अधिकरण- + स्थान धर्म-अधिकरण- + स्थान, n. court of justice, Pañc. 40, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थान
प्रसव- + स्थान प्रसव- + स्थान, n. a nest, Pañc. 74, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यस्थान
बध्य- + स्थान बध्य- + स्थान, or वध्य- (vb. वध्), n. place of execution, Pañc. 41, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनस्थान|बंधनस्थान
बन्धन- + स्थान बन्धन- + स्थान, n. a stable, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b " target="_blank">Page1079-b + 44</a>] Pañc. 224, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षस्थान
भक्ष- + स्थान भक्ष- + स्थान, n. state of being (one's) food, Pañc. 131, 2 (भक्षस्थाने स्थितम् अपि, although you are destined to be his food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्थानम्
यथा-स्थान + म् यथा-स्थान + म्, adv. instantly, Pañc. in Weber, Ind. St. iii. 373, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषिकास्थान
विभीषिका- + स्थान विभीषिका- + स्थान, n. object, or means, of frightening, Pañc. 160, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासस्थान
विश्वास- + स्थान विश्वास- + स्थान,<BR> I. n. an object or person of trust.<BR> II. विश्वासस्थाने, adv. as hostage, Pañc. 55, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरस्थान
वीर- + स्थान वीर- + स्थान, n. a certain posture, Lass. 2. ed. 70, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जनस्थाने
व्यञ्जन-स्थाने व्यञ्जन-स्थाने, loc. as condiment (करोमि, I shall use), Pañc. 52, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कस्थान
शुल्क- + स्थान शुल्क- + स्थान, n. any object of toll or duty, Man. 8, 398.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतस्थान|सङ्केतस्थान
संकेत- + स्थान संकेत- + स्थान, n. 1. place of assignation. 2. a sign, an intimation. Lass. 7, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरस्थान
सुर- + स्थान सुर- + स्थान, n. a temple, Hit. iii. d. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिस्थान|सिद्धिस्थानं
सिद्धि- + स्थान सिद्धि- + स्थान, n. name of a country, Lass. 40, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयस्थान|हृदयस्थानं
हृदय- + स्थान हृदय- + स्थान, n. the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानक|स्थानकं
स्थानक स्थान + क, n.<BR> 1. A town.<BR> 2. A basin of water at the root of a tree,<BR> 3. A bubble on spirits or wine.<BR> 4. A kind of speaking (addressing ?), Vikr. 64, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकास्थानक
पताका- + स्थानक पताका- + स्थानक, n. intimation of an episode in a drama, Daśar. 1, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानासनविहारवन्त्|स्थानासनविहारवत्
स्थानासनविहारवन्त् स्थानासनविहारवन्त्, adj. स्थान-आसन-विहार + वन्त्, adj. Occupying the station, seat, and place of religious exercises (of his preceptor), Man. 2, 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक स्थानिक, i. e. स्थान + इक,<BR> I. adj. Local.<BR> II. m. The governor of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन् स्थानिन्, i. e. स्थान + इन्, adj. Having a place or situation, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय स्थानीय, i. e. स्थान + ईय,<BR> I. adj. Relating or suitable to any place.<BR> II. n. A city.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसस्थानीय
अवतंस- + स्थानीय अवतंस- + स्थानीय, adj., f. या, taking the place of a crest, i. e. being, as it were, the ornament, Daśak. in Chr. 179, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठस्थानीय
कण्ठ- + स्थानीय कण्ठ- + स्थानीय, adj. having [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a " target="_blank">Page1080-a + 42</a>] its place in the throat, Vedāntas. in Chr. 207, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक स्थापक, i. e. स्था, Caus., + अक,<BR> I. adj. Causing to stand, placing, fixing, ordering.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A stage manager.<BR> 2. The founder of a temple.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिस्थापक|स्थितिस्थापकः
स्थिति- + स्थापक स्थिति- + स्थापक,<BR> I. adj. who or what fixes (cf. स्थिति).<BR> II. m. (n., Wils.), elasticity, Bhāṣāp. 95; 156 (cf. स्थिति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्य|स्थापत्यः
स्थापत्य स्थापत्य, i. e. स्थपति + य,<BR> I. m. A guard of the womens' apartments.<BR> II. n. Architecture, building, erecting, Rām. 1, 12, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापन|स्थापनं
स्थापन स्थापन, i. e. स्था, Caus., + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Placing, Naiṣ. 22, 45, Sch.; fixing, erecting, founding.<BR> 2. Concentrating one's thoughts upon the object of meditation.<BR> 3. Ordering.<BR> 4. A habitation.<BR> 5. A ceremony performed when the mother perceives the first signs of living conception.<BR> II. f. ना, Stage management.<BR> III. f. नी, A plant, Cissampelos hexandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन् स्था + मन्, n. Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन् स्थायिन्, i. e. स्था + इन्, adj., f. नी,<BR> 1. Staying, lasting, Hit. i. d. 48, M.M.<BR> 2. Firm, steady, unchangeable, Pañc. i. d. 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अ- + स्थायिन् अ- + स्थायिन्, adj. not permanent, Bhartṛ. 2, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःस्थायिन्
पुरस्- + स्थायिन् पुरस्- + स्थायिन्, adj. standing before one's eyes, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थायिन्
वन- + स्थायिन् वन- + स्थायिन्,<BR> I. adj. abiding in a wood.<BR> II. m. a hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक स्थायुक, i. e. स्था + उक,<BR> I. adj. Steady, stationary.<BR> II. m. The overseer of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाल|स्थालं
स्थाल स्था + ल,<BR> I. n. A plate, a dish, Rājat. 5, 46.<BR> II. f. ली, A pot, Pañc. 262, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर स्था + वर (i. e. वन् + अ, with र् for न्).<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Fixed, stable, immovable, Man. 1, 40; 41; 5, 28.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b " target="_blank">Page1080-b + 43</a>] Stationary (guards), Man. 9, 266.<BR> 3. Established, regular.<BR> II. m. A mountain, Bhag. 10, 25.<BR> III. n.<BR> 1. A bowstring.<BR> 2. Real estate.<BR> 3. A heirloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरता
स्थावरता स्थावर + ता, f. Immobility, Man. 12, 9 (a vegetable or mineral form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर स्थाविर, i. e. स्था + वन् + अ, with इ for अ, and र् for न्, n. Old age, Man. 9, 3 (adj. Old, Hit. i. d. 119, M.M.; but cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1774).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासक|स्थासकः
स्थासक स्थासक (vb. स्था), m.<BR> 1. A bubble of any fluid (cf. स्थानक).<BR> 2. Smearing the body with fragrant unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु स्थासु, vb. स्था, n. Bodily strength or capability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु स्था + स्नु, adj.<BR> 1. Firm, immovable, Man. 1, 56.<BR> 2. Durable, eternal, Kir. 2, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिक|स्थिकः
स्थिक स्थिक, i. e. स्थ + क, m. A buttock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिति|स्थितिः
स्थिति स्थिति, i. e. स्था + ति, f.<BR> 1. Standing, Mālat. 160, 6; staying, stay, Man. 11, 237.<BR> 2. Living, doing well, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1125.<BR> 3. Residence, Utt. Rāmac. 5, 1.<BR> 4. Remaining, Pañc. pr. d. 8 (गर्भे, in the womb, i. e. not being brought forth).<BR> 5. Keeping, i. d. 159 (but cf. v. r. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1561).<BR> 6. Being fixed, duration, Vikr. d. 153; a firm position, Pañc. i. d. 220.<BR> 7. State, Cāṇ. 90 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 412; condition, Pañc. 124, 4; natural state (cf. -स्थापक, Bhāṣāp. 95, properly ‘restoring the natural state’).<BR> 8. Correctness of conduct, Kir. 11, 54.<BR> 9. Honour, Mālat. 152, 20; dignity, Nal. 12, 10.<BR> 10. Stop, cessation.<BR> 11. Limit, boundary.<BR> 12. A sure decision, Man. 2, 225; a settled rule, 3, 120; a maxim, Hit. 50, 9, M.M.<BR> 13. Order, decree. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a " target="_blank">Page1081-a + 44</a>]<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्नस्थिति
अ-भिन्न- + स्थिति अ-भिन्न- + स्थिति (vb. भिद्), adj. not swerving from the right path, Śāk. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्स्थिति|पृथक्स्थितिः
पृथक्- + स्थिति पृथक्- + स्थिति, f. separation, Vikr. d. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठस्थिति
मठ- + स्थिति मठ- + स्थिति, f. staying in a college of priests, Pañc. ii. d. 66 (read मठस्थित्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यस्थिति|राज्यस्थितिः
राज्य- + स्थिति राज्य- + स्थिति, f. staying in government, being a king, Pañc. 251, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थिति|सुस्थितिः
सु- + स्थिति सु- + स्थिति, f. 1. welfare. 2. health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमन्त्|स्थितिमत्
स्थितिमन्त् स्थिति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Firm, stable, Vikr. d. 160.<BR> 2. Virtuous, Man. 9, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर स्थिर, i. e. स्था + र,<BR> I. adj., comparat. स्थेयंस्, superl. स्थेष्ठ.<BR> 1. Firm, Vikr. d. 1; fixed, immovable, Bhag. 6, 33 (स्थिरी कृ, To stop, Pañc. 258, 20).<BR> 2. Permanent, Vikr. d. 109; Chr. 291, 15 = Rigv. i. 64, 15; eternal, Megh. 56.<BR> 3. Hard, Utt. Rāmac. 30, 2; solid, strong, Indr. 1, 18.<BR> 4. Steady, Mālat. 175, 6; free from passion, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR> 5. Cool, collected, Lass. 43, 17.<BR> 6. Convinced, sure, Chr. 53, 25.<BR> 7. Constant, determined, Chr. 43, 28.<BR> 8. Faithful, Pañc. 107, 11.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A deity.<BR> 2. Final emancipation.<BR> 3. A mountain.<BR> 4. A tree.<BR> 5. A bull.<BR> 6. Kārttikeya, the god of war.<BR> 7. Saturn.<BR> III. f. रा.<BR> 1. The earth.<BR> 2. Silk-cotton tree, and two other plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. στηρίζω, στερεός, στεῤῥός, στελεόν; Lat. stolidus, stultus; O.H.G. starên; A.S. starian; O.H.G. storrên, stornên, starh; A.S. starc; O.H.G. ga-starkên, starhjan, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अ-स्थिर अ-स्थिर, adj. 1. inconstant, Hit. iii. d. 106. 2. weak, Man. 8, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरता
स्थिरता स्थिर + ता, f.<BR> 1. Firmness, Śāk. d. 90; stability; स्थिरतां नी, To secure, Pañc. 97, 14.<BR> 2. Moral firmness.<BR> 3. Fortitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरत्व|स्थिरत्वं
स्थिरत्व स्थिर + त्व, n. Firmness, steadiness, Johns. Sel. 12, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिरत्व
अ- + स्थिरत्व अ- + स्थिरत्व, n. inconstancy, Man. 8, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुड्
† स्थुड् स्थुड्, i. 6, To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूणा
स्थूणा स्थूणा (vb. स्था, based on [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b " target="_blank">Page1081-b + 43</a>] स्था + व˚, cf. the next), f.<BR> 1. A pillar, a post, Pañc. 37, 6.<BR> 2. An iron image,<BR> 3. An anvil.<BR> 4. A disease.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मस्थूणा
वेश्मस्थूणा वेश्मस्थूणा, i. e. वेश्मन्-, f. the main post of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूर|स्थूरः
स्थूर स्थूर, i. e. स्था + वर (cf. the next), m. A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिन्
स्थूरिन् स्थूरिन्, i. e. स्थूर (in the signification of *स्थव in स्थवीयंस्, cf. स्थूल and स्थूलिन्), + इन्, m. A packhorse.<BR> --Cf. Zend. श्तओर (= स्थूर, or rather स्थौर, cf. स्थौरिन्), A beast of burden; Goth. stiurs; A.S. steor; ταῦρος, cf. also स्थूल, and O.H.G. stiuri, fortis; A.S. stor; O.H.G. stur, magnus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल्
† स्थूल् स्थूल्, i. 10 (a denomin. derived from the next), Par. To become big or bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल स्थूल = स्थूर (with ल् for र्), but in the original signification of its base, स्था + वर,<BR> I. adj., comparat. स्थूलतर and स्थवीयंस्, superl. स्थूलतम and स्थविष्ठ.<BR> 1. Great, large, Rājat. 5, 12; Megh. 47; Pañc. i. d. 373; स्थूलतर, Very large, Pañc. 134, 5.<BR> 2. Bulky, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 22; fat.<BR> 3. Powerful, Pañc. 168, 25.<BR> 4. Clumsy.<BR> 5. Coarse, Pañc. 133, 1.<BR> 6. Stupid.<BR> II. m. The jack tree.<BR> III. f. ला.<BR> 1. A sort of pepper.<BR> 2. A pumpkin gourd.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. A heap.<BR> 2. A tent.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्थूल
अति- + स्थूल अति- + स्थूल, adj. 1. very big, Rām. 5, 10, 17. 2. too clumsy, Suśr. 1, 25, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तास्थूल
मुक्ता- + स्थूल मुक्ता- + स्थूल, adj. as large as pearls, Megh. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलता
स्थूलता स्थूल + ता, f.<BR> 1. Coarseness, bulkiness, Pañc. i. d. 205.<BR> 2. Stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलिन्
स्थूलिन् स्थूलिन् (cf. स्थूरिन्), m. A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेयंस्
स्थेयंस् स्थेयंस्, स्थेष्ठ स्थेष्ठ, see स्थिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्य|स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्य स्थैर्य, i. e. स्थित + य, n.<BR> 1. Firmness, stability, staying continually, Pañc. 225, 22.<BR> 2. Constancy, Pañc. iii. d. 102.<BR> 3. Patience, Pañc. iii. d. 238.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अ- + स्थैर्य अ- + स्थैर्य, n. perishableness, Rājat. 5, 381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौर|स्थौरं
स्थौर स्थौर, i. e. स्थूर (but in the signification of स्थूल and स्थूरिन्, q. cf.), + अ, n.<BR> 1. Strength, power.<BR> 2. A load for a horse or ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरिन्
स्थौरिन् स्थौरिन्, i. e. स्थौर + इन् (cf. स्थूरिन्), m.<BR> 1. A pack-horse.<BR> 2. A strong horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौललक्ष्य
स्थौललक्ष्य स्थौललक्ष्य, i. e. स्थूल-लक्ष + य, n. Incessant liberality, Man. 7, 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौलशीर्ष|स्थौलशीर्षं
स्थौलशीर्ष स्थौलशीर्ष, i. e. स्थूल-शीर्ष + अ, adj. Large-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल्य|स्थौल्यं
स्थौल्य स्थौल्य, i. e. स्थूल + य, n. Largeness, bulk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन स्नपन, i. e. स्ना, Caus., + अन, n.<BR> 1. Washing.<BR> 2. Bathing, ablution, Śiś. 8, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नव|स्नवः
स्नव स्नव, i. e. स्नु + अ, m. Oozing, dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नस्
† स्नस् स्नस्, i. 1 and 4, Par.<BR> 1. To eject.<BR> 2. To eat (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नसा
स्नसा स्नसा, f. A tendon, a muscle.<BR> --Cf. perhaps O.H.G. snôr, snuor, see स्नाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ना
स्ना स्ना, ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 7072),<BR> 1. To bathe, Man. 4, 82; anomal. potent. स्नायीत, MBh. 3, 7072.<BR> 2. To perform the ceremony of bathing when leaving the house of one's spiritual preceptor, Man. 2, 245. स्नात,<BR> 1. Bathed, having bathed, Rājat. 5, 391; Daśak. in Chr. 188, 20.<BR> 2. Purified, Mahāv. 77, 2; pure. m. (One whose spiritual instruction is finished, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b " target="_blank">Page1082-b + 45</a>] see<BR> 2.), an initiated householder.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. स्ना̆पय,<BR> 1. To wash, to cleanse, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 7 (आ); Megh. 44 (ă).<BR> 2. To weep for (?), Utt. Rāmac. 69, 1 (ă). स्नपित,<BR> 1. Bathed, Mālat. 60, 10.<BR> 2. Moistened, Kir. 5, 44; 47.<BR> --With अप अप, अपस्नात, Bathed after mourning, Rām. 2, 42, 22.<BR> --With नि नि, निष्णात,<BR> 1. Perfect, superior.<BR> 2. Learned, MBh. 1, 3988; skilful, conversant, Śāk. 65, 18.<BR> 3. Given to, Mālat. 37, 3.<BR> 4. (In law), Agreed upon, Mālat. 174, 13. अति-निष्णात, Very conversant, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 19.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. प्रतिस्नात, Bathed.<BR> 2. प्रतिष्णात, Pure.<BR> --Comp.<BR> सु-प्रतिष्णात, adj. certain.<BR> --Cf. ναρός, νᾶμα, νοτίς, νῆσος, νίπτω; Lat. nare; Goth. nadr; A.S. naeddre, nedre; O.H.G. nacho; see नौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नात|मृतस्नातः
मृत- + स्नात मृत- + स्नात, adj. 1. bathed after mourning. 2. dying immediately after ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्ना
सु- + स्ना सु- + स्ना,<BR> I. adj. very clean, Lass. 24, 4.<BR> II. m. a student who has performed his ablutions preparatory or subsequent to a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातक|स्नातकः
स्नातक स्नात + क (vb. स्ना), m. A Brāhmaṇa just returned from the mansion of his preceptor, Man. 2, 138 (cf. स्ना); an initiated householder, Lass. 71, 1; a Brāhmaṇa in his second आश्रम (order of life), Man. 1, 113; Hit. 123, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यास्नातक|विद्यास्नातकः
विद्या-, विद्या-व्रत- + स्नातक विद्या-, विद्या-व्रत- + स्नातक, and व्रत-, m. a Brāhmaṇa who has completed his studentship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याव्रतस्नातक|विद्याव्रतस्नातकः
विद्या-, विद्या-व्रत- + स्नातक विद्या-, विद्या-व्रत- + स्नातक, and व्रत-, m. a Brāhmaṇa who has completed his studentship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नान|स्नानं
स्नान स्नान, i. e. स्ना + अन, n.<BR> 1. Bathing, Pañc. 100, 8.<BR> 2. Purification by bathing, Man. 1, 111; Pañc. iii. d. 120.<BR> 3. Anything used in it, as water, perfumed powder, etc., Ṛt. 1, 4; Megh. 34, Sch.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिःस्नान
त्रिस्- + स्नान त्रिस्- + स्नान, n. bathing three times a day, Kām. Nītis. 2, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्नान
दुस्- + स्नान दुस्- + स्नान, n. inauspicious bathing, Hariv. 3413.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नान|मृतस्नानं
मृत- + स्नान मृत- + स्नान, n. funeral ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानीय|स्नानीयं
स्नानीय स्नानीय, adj. Ablutionary, fit for bathing in, or to be used in bathing, Mālav. d. 87; Ragh. 16, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापक|स्नापकः
स्नापक स्नापक, i. e. स्ना, Caus., + अक, m. A servant who supplies or applies bathing water, Rām. 2, 64, 12, Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापन|स्नापनं
स्नापन स्नापन, i. e. स्ना, Caus., + अन, Bathing, Man. 2, 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायिन्
स्नायिन् स्नायिन्, i. e. स्ना + इन्, adj., f. नी, Bathing, Man. 11, 214.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यस्नायिन्
नित्य- + स्नायिन् नित्य- + स्नायिन्, adj. constantly bathing, Hit. 40, 10. M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायु|स्नायुः
स्नायु स्नायु (probably a form of स्नाव, for स्नाउ), f.<BR> 1. A tendon, Man. 8, 234; Pañc. 182, 17; a muscle, Bhartṛ. 2, 23.<BR> 2. The string of a bow, Pañc. 121, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायुमय
स्नायुमय स्नायु + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of tendons, Pañc. 144, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाव|स्नावः
स्नाव स्नाव, m. A tendon, a muscle.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. senwa; A.S. sinu, sinw, senw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धता
स्निग्धता स्निग्ध + ता (vb. स्निह्), f.<BR> 1. Affection.<BR> 2. Unctuousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निट्
स्निट् स्निट्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To love (cf. स्निह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निह्
स्निह् स्निह्, i. 4, Par. (properly, To be viscous, easy to be attached to), To bear affection to, Śāk. 102, 6 (to this boy).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्निग्ध.<BR> 1. Oily, unctuous, smooth, Rājat. 5, 319.<BR> 2. Wet, Megh. 16 (Sch.),<BR> 3. Resplendent, Vikr. d. 70 (कनक-निकष-, like a streak of pure gold).<BR> 4. Agreeable, Megh. 65.<BR> 5. Coarse.<BR> 6. Thick, dense, Megh. 1.<BR> 7. Cooling, emollient.<BR> 8. Attached, Hit. ii. d. 151; kind, well affected, Man. 7, 32; 120; loving, Pañc. i. d. 317. m.<BR> 1. A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b " target="_blank">Page1083-b + 40</a>] friend, Pañc. ii. d. 178.<BR> 2. Two kinds of pine. f. धा, Marrow. n.<BR> 1. Oil, Megh. 60.<BR> 2. Beeswax.<BR> 3. Light.<BR> 4. Thickness.<BR> --† i. 10, Par. To be unctuous.<BR> --With अति अति, अतिस्निग्ध, Very smooth, Rām. 3, 49, 36.<BR> --With उप उप, Caus. To cause to love, to fascinate, Utt. Rāmac. 34, 18.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रस्निग्ध, Very oily, Śāk. d. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
1. स्नु स्नु, ii. 2, Par. To distill, to flow.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To pour forth, Rām. 2, 64, 55, Seramp. प्रस्नुत, Dropping, Rājat. 5, 76 (cf. s. v. स्तन).<BR> --Cf. Æol. ναύω, νάω; Goth. snivan; A.S. sniwan; O.H.G. sniutan; A.S. snytan; probably also Goth. sniumjan, sniumundo; O.H.G. sniumi; A.S. sneome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
2. स्नु, स्नु, probably सो + नु (cf. सानु), m. and n. Table-land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुतस्
स्नुतस् स्नुतस् (for स्नायु + तस्), adv. From the muscles, Bhāg. P. 3, 12, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा स्नुषा, f.<BR> 1. A daughter-in-law, Utt. Rāmac. 15, 8.<BR> 2. The milkhedge plant.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. snur; A.S. snóru; Lat. nurus; νυός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुस्
† स्नुस् स्नुस्, i. 4, Par. To eat, or to be invisible, or to take (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
† स्नुह् स्नुह्. i. 4, Par. To vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेह|स्नेहः
स्नेह स्नेह, i. e. स्निह् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Oil, Ragh. 4, 75; unguent, grease, Megh. 93; Rām. 2, 64, 68.<BR> 2. Moisture, the corporeal fluids, Man. 12, 120.<BR> 3. Oiliness, viscidity, Bhāṣāp. 4; 86.<BR> 4. Affection, love, Pañc. ii. d. 178; Megh. 111 (plur., read स्नेहान् आहुः).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्स्नेह
निस्- + स्नेह निस्- + स्नेह, adj., f. हा, 1. not oily, Man. 5, 87. 2. void of affection, Pañc. iv. d. 47. 3. free from desire, MBh. 13, 1658. 4. not. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a " target="_blank">Page1084-a + 39</a>] treated affectionately, Pañc. i. d. 94. 5. abhorred, Somad. Nal. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकस्नेह|मस्तकस्नेहः
मस्तक- + स्नेह मस्तक- + स्नेह, m. the brain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्नेह
वि-गत- + स्नेह वि-गत- + स्नेह (vb गम्), adj. void of affection, Sund. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्नेह
स-स्नेह स-स्नेह, adj. affectionate, Hit. iv. d. 74. ˚हम्, adv. affectionately, Pañc. 187, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन्
स्नेहन् स्नेहन् (vb. स्निह्), m. A sort of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन|स्नेहनं
स्नेहन स्नेहन, i. e. स्निह् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Anointing.<BR> 2. Unctuousness.<BR> 3. An unguent, an emollient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभू
स्नेहभू स्नेह-भू, m. The phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहवन्त्|स्नेहवत्
स्नेहवन्त् स्नेह वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Possessed of affection.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेहवन्त्|अस्नेहवत्
अ- + स्नेहवन्त् अ- + स्नेहवन्त्, deprived of affection, Pañc. i. d. 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित|स्नेहितः
स्नेहित स्नेहित, i. e. स्नेह + इत,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Kind, affectionate.<BR> 2. Beloved.<BR> II. m. A friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिन्
स्नेहिन् स्नेहिन्, i. e. स्नेह + इन्,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Affectionate.<BR> 2. Oily.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A friend.<BR> 2. A painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नै
स्नै स्नै, † स्तै स्तै, i. 1, Par. To dress, to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध्य|स्नैग्ध्यं
स्नैग्ध्य स्नैग्ध्य, i. e. स्निग्ध + य (vb. स्निह्), n.<BR> 1. Affectionateness.<BR> 2. Oiliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्द्|स्पंद्
स्पन्द् स्पन्द्, i. 1, Ātm. To tremble, Mṛcch. 105, 12. स्पन्दित,<BR> 1. Throbbing, Vikr. d. 50; beating.<BR> 2. Gone. n. Pulsation.<BR> --With the prep. परि परि, To tremble, Rām. 2, 14, 12.<BR> --With वि वि, To struggle, MBh. 3, 445.<BR> --Cf. σϕενδόνη, σϕεδανός, σϕοδρός, σϕόδρα (ϕ by the influence of σ); Lat. funda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्द|स्पंद|स्पंदः|स्पन्दः
स्पन्द स्पन्द् + अ, m. Trembling, motion, Bhāṣāp. 158.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पन्द|अस्पंद
अ- + स्पन्द अ- + स्पन्द, adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b " target="_blank">Page1084-b + 42</a>] immovable, Utt. Rāmac. 125, 13; Rājat. 5, 364.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शस्पन्द|स्पर्शस्पंद|स्पर्शस्पन्दः
स्पर्श- + स्पन्द स्पर्श- + स्पन्द, m. a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दन|स्पंदन|स्पंदनं|स्पन्दनं
स्पन्दन स्पन्द् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Quivering, trembling (Bhāṣāp. 6, read स्पन्दनो˚).<BR> 2. Throbbing, Mālat. 5, 3.<BR> 3. Quickening of the child in the womb.<BR> 4. Going.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भास्पन्दन
गर्भ-अ- + स्पन्दन गर्भ-अ- + स्पन्दन, n. immobility of the child in the womb, Suśr. 1, 49, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दिन्
स्पन्दिन् स्पन्द् + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Quivering, Rājat. 5, 1.<BR> 2. Palpitating (as an eye), Megh. 93 (with उपरि-, above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परितृ
स्परितृ स्परितृ, i. e. स्पृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. The active cause of pain, an enemy, a disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध्
स्पर्ध् स्पर्ध् (i. e. स्पृ-धा), i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., MBh. 5, 170),<BR> 1. To contend with, to contest, MBh. 1, 205.<BR> 2. To emulate, to vie, Pañc. v. d. 50; to envy, Rām. 2, 60, 65, Seramp.<BR> 3. To be equal, MBh. 1, 4991. स्पर्धित, Contended with, envied, defied.<BR> --With बि वि, To vie, MBh. 1, 1088.<BR> --Cf. Goth. spaurds; A.S. spyrd; O.H.G. spurt, stadium (originally certamen); probably also A.S. flit, ge-flit, strife; see स्पृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध
स्पर्ध स्पर्ध् + अ,<BR> I. adj. Emulous, envious.<BR> II. f. धा.<BR> 1. Emulation, envy, jealousy, Johns. Sel. 45, 68; Rājat. 5, 285.<BR> 2. Successive elevation.<BR> 3. Sameness.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्धा
वि-स्पर्धा वि-स्पर्धा, f. absence of envy, MBh. 5, 1602.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धिन्
स्पर्धिन् स्पर्धिन्, i. e. स्पर्धा + इन्, adj.<BR> 1. Rivalling, Pañc. ed. orn. 3, 5.<BR> 2. Emulating, Ragh. 13, 13.<BR> 3. Envious.<BR> 4. Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श्
† स्पर्श् स्पर्श्, स्पश् स्पश्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To take.<BR> 2. To embrace (cf. स्पृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श स्पर्श, i. e. स्पृश् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Touch, Vikr. 47, 12; feeling, Man. 1, 76; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a " target="_blank">Page1085-a + 41</a>] Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 23; Bhāṣāp. 3; touching, Śāk. d. 27; Mālav. 29, 13; contact, Bhag. 2, 14.<BR> 2. Sexual intercourse, Rājat. 5, 401.<BR> 3. Gift, donation.<BR> 4. The thing touching.<BR> 5. Air, wind, Arj. 5, 14.<BR> 6. The agent of pain, as sickness (Daśak. in Chr. 190, 19, शिरस्-शूल-, headache, or literally, ‘the perceiving as of a sharp spear in my head’).<BR> 7. Morbid heat.<BR> II. f. शा, A wanton woman.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्पर्श|दुःस्पर्शः
दुस्- + स्पर्श दुस्- + स्पर्श, adj. 1. of difficult or disagreeable touch, MBh. 13, 2109. 2. affecting disagreeably, Bhāg. P. 3, 17, 5 (of wind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्पर्श
सम- + स्पर्श सम- + स्पर्श, adj. literally, having the same contact, i. e. 1. wounding like, Chr. 39, 5. 2. the touching of which has the same effect, viz. to defile, Pañc. iii. d. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शक|स्पर्शकः
स्पर्शक स्पर्शक, i. e. स्पृश् + अक, adj. Touching, a toucher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शता
स्पर्शता स्पर्श + ता, f. Touching, Śāk. d. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शन|स्पर्शनं|स्पर्शनः
स्पर्शन स्पर्शन, i. e. स्पृश् + अन,<BR> I. m. Wind.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Touching, Pañc. 163, 5.<BR> 2. Sensation, Man. 12, 120.<BR> 3. Gift, donation.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शन|अस्पर्शनं
अ- + स्पर्शन अ- + स्पर्शन, n. not touching, Pañc. ii. d. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शवन्त्|स्पर्शवत्
स्पर्शवन्त् स्पर्श + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Palpable, Bhāṣāp. 25.<BR> 2. Smooth, soft, Kumāras. 1, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्
स्पर्ष् स्पर्ष्, see पर्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टृ
स्पर्ष्टृ स्पर्ष्टृ, i. e. स्पृश् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. The agent of pain.<BR> 2. Morbid heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
1. स्पश् स्पश्, † पश् पश्, † पष् पष्, † पस् पस्, i. 1, Par. Ātm.<BR> 1. † To obstruct.<BR> 2. To string together.<BR> 3. To begin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
2. स्पश् स्पश्, see स्पर्श्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश|स्पशः
स्पश स्पश् + अ (see दृश्), m.<BR> 1. A spy, Man. 8, 116 (v. r. see Lois.; read in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b " target="_blank">Page1085-b + 44</a>] Kull. commentary चारभूत, and cf. the vedic designation of Agni as दूत, messenger); Pañc. 156, 21.<BR> 2. A secret agent,<BR> 3. War.<BR> 4. Fighting with a dangerous animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट स्पष्ट, i. e. the ptcple. pf. pass. of स्पश् (see दृश्),<BR> 1. Evident, Vedāntas. in Chr. 211, 18.<BR> 2. Clear, able to see (not blind), Pañc. 262, 24.<BR> 3. Intelligible.<BR> 4. टम्, adv. a Distinctly, Lass. 2. ed. 34, 20. b. Looking in the face, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. con-spectus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अ- + स्पष्ट अ- + स्पष्ट, adj. indistinct, Vedāntas. in Chr. 205, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पष्ट|विस्पष्टः
वि- + स्पष्ट वि- + स्पष्ट, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पार्ह
स्पार्ह स्पार्ह, i. e. स्पृहा + अ, adj. Desirable, Lass. 100, 9 = Rigv. vii. 15, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृ
स्पृ स्पृ, † स्तृ स्तृ, † स्मृ स्मृ, ii. 5, Par.<BR> 1. † To gratify.<BR> 2. To protect.<BR> 3. † To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
1. स्पृश् स्पृश्, i. 6, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm.),<BR> 1. To touch, Rām. 2, 42, 6; 3, 53, 47; with अद्भिस्, To sprinkle with water, Man. 2, 60; with हस्तम् अन्योन्यम्, To shake hands with each other, Vikr. 11, 14.<BR> 2. To reach, to attain, Lass. 2. ed. 78, 72.<BR> 3. Pass. To be seized, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 5 (by inebriation or frenzy).<BR> 4. To obtain, to undergo, MBh. 3, 318. स्पृष्ट,<BR> 1. Touched, Bhartṛ. 2, 36.<BR> 2. Felt.<BR> 3. Defiled, Lass. 2. ed. 67, 31.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut pass. अ-स्पृश्य, not to be touched, Rājat. 5, 401.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To order to touch, Man. 8, 114.<BR> 2. To give, Man. 11, 135.<BR> --With अप अप, in अपो पस्पृश्य, MBh. 1, 764, To touch water for ablution, i. e. to rinse one's mouth, is probably preserved as an archaism for अप उपस्पृश्य, see उप-स्पृश्.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a " target="_blank">Page1086-a + 40</a>] couch, Chr. 36, 14; दन्तईस् दन्तान्, To gnash the teeth, Nal. 7, 3; with and without अद्भिस्, To sprinkle with water, Man. 4, 143; 5, 138.<BR> 2. To rinse one's mouth (as ablution), Man. 2, 53.<BR> 3. To bathe, Man. 5, 62.<BR> --With पर्युप परि-उप, To touch or to use for ablution, MBh. 3, 165.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप,<BR> 1. The same, MBh. 3, 8022.<BR> 2. To bathe, MBh. 3, 10530.<BR> --With परि परि, To touch, Rām. 1, 9, 38.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To touch, Man. 3, 178; with अद्भिस्, To sprinkle with water, Man. 2, 53.<BR> 2. To perceive, Rājat. 5, 375. संस्पृष्ट, Touched, Hit. ii. d. 16.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To bathe, MBh. 3, 8080.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, To touch, to stroke, MBh. 3, 1457.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्पृष्ट
श्वस्पृष्ट श्वस्पृष्ट, i. e. श्वन्-, adj. touched by a dog, defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
2. स्पृश् स्पृश्, adj. Who or what touches, touching, Rājat. 5, 343; 475 (having).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस्पृश्
दिव- + स्पृश् दिव- + स्पृश्, and नभस्-, adj. touching or reaching to the heavens, MBh. 1, 2854; 11, 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयस्पृश्
प्रणय- + स्पृश् प्रणय- + स्पृश्, adj. affectionate, Mālat. 76, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश|स्पृशः
स्पृश स्पृश् + अ, erroneous reading, Man. 8, 116 (see स्पश).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्पृश
दुस्- + स्पृश दुस्- + स्पृश, adj. of disagreeable touch, Hariv. 3654.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्पृश
नभस्- + स्पृश नभस्- + स्पृश, adj. touching the heavens, Bhag. 11, 24 (may belong also to नभः-स्पृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टि|स्पृष्टिः
स्पृष्टि स्पृष्टि, i. e. स्पृश् + ति, f. Touch, feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टिन्
स्पृष्टिन् स्पृष्टिन्, i. e. स्पृष्ट (vb. स्पृश्), + इन्, adj. One who has touched, Man. 5, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्
स्पृह् स्पृह्, i. 10, स्पृहय (old Caus. of स्पर्ध्, with ह् for ध्, and ऋ for अर्), Par., with dat. and gen.<BR> 1. To envy, Pañc. 137, 16.<BR> 2. To desire, to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b " target="_blank">Page1086-b + 40</a>] long for, Rām. 3, 53, 39; Śāk. 103, 4.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. spero, spes; O.H.G. spulgen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीयता
स्पृहणीयता स्पृहणीय + ता (vb. स्पृह्), f. Condition of being worthy to be desired, Utt. Rāmac. 160, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीयत्व
स्पृहणीयत्व स्पृहणीय + त्व (vb. स्पृह्), n. Enviableness, Rājat. 5, 336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयाय्य
स्पृहयाय्य स्पृहयाय्य (vb. स्पृह्), adj. Desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहा
स्पृहा स्पृह् + आ, f. Wish, desire, Hit. ii. d. 121; Pañc. 131, 19 (read स्पृहां).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगतस्पृह
अ-गत- + स्पृह अ-गत- + स्पृह, adj., f. हा, not having attained one's desire, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गतस्पृह
निस्-, वि-गत- + स्पृह निस्-, वि-गत- + स्पृहा (vb. गम्), and वीत-, i. e. वि-इत-, adj., f. हा, free from wish or desire, Pañc. iii. d. 84 (निस्-); Kir. 3, 12 (वीत-), स-, adj., f. हा, desirous, Kir. 14, 36. ˚हम्, adv. passionately longing, Śāk. 11, 19; Vikr. 13, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्पृह
निस्-, वि-गत- + स्पृह निस्-, वि-गत- + स्पृहा (vb. गम्), and वीत-, i. e. वि-इत-, adj., f. हा, free from wish or desire, Pañc. iii. d. 84 (निस्-); Kir. 3, 12 (वीत-), स-, adj., f. हा, desirous, Kir. 14, 36. ˚हम्, adv. passionately longing, Śāk. 11, 19; Vikr. 13, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पॄ
† स्पॄ स्पॄ, ii. 9, स्पृणा, णी, Par. To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ स्प्रष्टृ, i. e. स्पृश् + तृ,<BR> I. m., f. ट्री, n. Who or what touches.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The agent of pain, as a disease.<BR> 2. Morbid heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट्
स्फट् स्फट्, see स्फुट्, स्फिट्ट्, स्फुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट|स्फटः
स्फट स्फट (cf. स्फुट्),<BR> I. m., and f. टा, A snake's expanded hood.<BR> II. f. टी, Alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिक|स्फटिकः
स्फटिक स्फटिक, probably for स्पष्टिक, i. e. स्पष्ट + इक, (properly, transparent), m. Crystal, Hit. ii. d. 157; Kir. 5, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकमय
स्फटिकमय स्फटिक + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फण्ट्|स्फंट्
स्फण्ट् स्फण्ट्, see स्फण्ड्, स्फुट्, स्फिट्ट्, स्फुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फण्ड्|स्फंड्
† स्फण्ड् स्फण्ड्, स्फुण्ड् स्फुण्ड्, स्फण्ट् स्फण्ट्, स्फुण्ड् स्फुण्ट्, i. 10, Par. To jest or joke with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फर्
स्फर् स्फर्, see स्फुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फरण|स्फरणं
स्फरण स्फरण, i. e. स्फर् + अन, n. Trembling, throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फल्
स्फल् स्फल्, see स्फुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिक|स्फाटिकं
स्फाटिक स्फाटिक, i. e. स्फटिक + अ, adj. Crystalline, Rām. 5, 9, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाति|स्फातिः
स्फाति स्फाति, i. e. स्फाय् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Swelling, intumescence.<BR> 2. Increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाय्
स्फाय् स्फाय्, i. 1, Ātm. (properly pass. of a lost vb. स्पन्, फ् for प्, by the influence of स्), To swell, to become bulky, to increase, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 109.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. स्फात, Swollen, enlarged.<BR> II. स्फीत,<BR> 1. Swollen, enlarged, large, Nal. 24, 37; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 11; thick, Mālat. 75, 21.<BR> 2. Abounding, Lass. 1, 8 (abounding in taste, i. e. elegant); much, many.<BR> 3. Successful, risen in rank.<BR> 4. Affected by hereditary disease.<BR> --Caus. स्फावय (for original स्फापय), To augment, Bhaṭṭ. 12, 76.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. spannan (originally, To draw); O.H.G. and A.S. spanan; Goth. and A.S. spinnan; σπάω, ἀ-σπάζομαι, ἀγαπάω (i. e. ἀγαν-σπαω); Lat. spatium, patere (a denomin. derived from *pă-to, old ptcple. pf. pass.); probably also A.S. spówan (cf. Caus.); spédan; Goth. spêd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
स्फार स्फार, i. e. स्फाय् + र and स्फर् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Large, Mālat. 81, 14; great, Kathās. 7, 19; Pañc. v. d. 22; spreading, Bhartṛ. 3, 85 (cf. स्फारी-भू).<BR> 2. Loud.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Quivering, throbbing.<BR> 2. Twanging, as of a bowstring.<BR> 3. A bubble or flaw in gold.<BR> --Cf. σϕαῖρα (i. e. σϕαρια).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारण|स्फारणं
स्फारण स्फारण, i. e. स्फुर्, Caus., + अन, n., and स्फाल स्फाल, i. e. स्फुल् + अ, m. Trembling, throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालन|स्फालनं
स्फालन स्फालन, i. e. स्फल्, Caus. + अन, n.<BR> 1. Quivering, shaking.<BR> 2. Rubbing, friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिच्
स्फिच् स्फिच्, f. A buttock, Man. 8, 281.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. spec; A.S. spic (the buttocks being the fattest parts of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहत्स्फिच्
बृहत्स्फिच् बृहत्स्फिच्, i. e. बृहन्त्-, m. a proper name, Pañc. 117, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बस्फिच्|लंबस्फिच्
लम्ब- + स्फिच् लम्ब- + स्फिच्, adj. having large buttocks, Hiḍ. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्
† स्फिट् स्फिट्, i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To despise.<BR> 2. To love.<BR> 3. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्ट्
† स्फिट्ट् स्फिट्ट्, स्फिट् स्फिट्, स्फट् स्फट्, i. 10, Par. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर स्फिर, i. e. स्फाय् + र (cf. स्फार), adj., comparat. स्फेयंस्, superl. स्फेष्ठ,<BR> 1. Large.<BR> 2. Much, many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीति|स्फीतिः
स्फीति स्फीति, i. e. स्फाय् + ति, Increase, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्
स्फुट् स्फुट् (akin to स्फुर्, स्फुल्; probably for original *स्पर्त्; O.H.G. spaltan; Engl. split), i. 6, Par., and † i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. (also † i. 1, Par., and † स्फुण्ट् स्फुण्ट्, स्फट् स्फट्, † स्फण्ट् स्फण्ट्, i. 1, Par.), To burst, Utt. Rāmac. 77, 15; MBh. 1, 3023.<BR> 2. To open, to expand (as a flower), Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> 3. To disperse, to run away, Bhaṭṭ. 10, 8. स्फुटित,<BR> 1. Burst, broken, destroyed, Pañc. 98, 1; 254, 23 (cf. 42, 10).<BR> 2. Splay (as feet), Pañc. 104, 15.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10,<BR> 1. स्फोटय, To break, to divide, to tear open, Pañc. 87, 7; to destroy, Pañc. 42, 10.<BR> 2. † स्फुटय, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a " target="_blank">Page1088-a + 41</a>] To burst, to appear.<BR> 3. स्फाटय, स्फाटित, Cleft, Hit. 49, 11.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus., or i. 10, स्फोटय,<BR> 1. To cause to sound, MBh. 3, 11139.<BR> 2. To strike, Lass. 30, 18; especially one's own arm with the hand (perhaps rather, to snap the fingers, cf. स्फोटन), Man. 4, 64.<BR> 3. To pat, MBh. 3, 1780.<BR> --With प्र प्र, Caus., or i. 10, To pierce, MBh. 4, 2100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट स्फुट् + अ, and perhaps at the same time a form of स्पष्ट, with उ, by the influence of the labial, फ् by that of स्, cf. स्फटिक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Broken, rent.<BR> 2. Opened, expanded (as a flower), Utt. Rāmac. 81, 5.<BR> 3. Spread.<BR> 4. Loud, Rām. 6, 8, 45.<BR> 5. Manifest, evident, Kir. 11, 44.<BR> 6. Plain, distinct, Pañc. iii. d. 109, i. d. 180 (without duplicity).<BR> 7. White, bright, Bhartṛ. 3, 23.<BR> 8. Known.<BR> II. टम्, adv. Distinctly, Pañc. 167, 15; evidently, Hit. iii. d. 89; certainly, Nalod. 2, 41.<BR> III. f. टा, A snake's expanded hood, Pañc. iii. 135.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपरिस्फुट
अति-परि- + स्फुट अति-परि- + स्फुट, adj. very distinct; with न, half concealed, Śāk. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटता
स्फुटता स्फुट + ता, f. Perspicuity, Kir. 2, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटन|स्फुटनं
स्फुटन स्फुट् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Tearing, rending.<BR> 2. Opening, expanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटार्थ
स्फुटार्थ स्फुटार्थ, i. e. स्फुट-अर्थ, adj. Intelligible, obvious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटि|स्फुटिः
स्फुटि and स्फुटी स्फुट् + ई̆, f.<BR> 1. Kibe, swelling of the feet.<BR> 2. A sort of melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटिका
स्फुटिका स्फुटिका, i. e. स्फुट् + अक, f. A small piece (?), Daśak. in Chr. 199, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्ट्
† स्फुट्ट् स्फुट्ट्, i. 10, Par. To slight, to despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुड्
† स्फुड् स्फुड्, i. 6, Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुण्ट्|स्फुंट्
स्फुण्ट् स्फुण्ट्, see स्फण्ड्, स्फुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुण्ड्|स्फुंड्
† स्फुण्ड् स्फुण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm. To open, to expand (cf. स्फुट्); see स्फण्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्कार|स्फुत्कारः
स्फुत्कार स्फुत्-कार (स्फुत्, an imitative sound), m. Crackling, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्
स्फुर् स्फुर्, also स्फर् स्फर्, (which appears only in the Caus. and derivative nouns; nevertheless, it is the original form, its अ being changed to उ by the combined influence of the preceding labial and the accent of the sixth conj. cl.), i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To tremble, MBh. 3, 1867; to palpitate, Mṛcch. 143, 14; to throb, Mālat. 5, 5.<BR> 2. To struggle, Pañc. iii. d. 123; to rebound, Johns. Sel. 48, 83.<BR> 3. To break forth, Gīt. 11, 1; Hit. ii. d. 59 (पुरः स्फुरन्त्, Springing up before one's eyes).<BR> 4. To flash, to shine, to sparkle, Gīt. 10, 6; Hit. ii. d. 52; Pañc. i. d. 33; Vikr. d. 136.<BR> 5. To destroy (ved.). स्फुरित,<BR> 1. Shaken.<BR> 2. Trembling, Pañc. 64, 15; throbbing.<BR> 3. Glittering, Megh. 15; shining, Mālat. 40, 10.<BR> 4. Swollen. n.<BR> 1. Trembling, motion, MBh. 1, 1258.<BR> 2. Throbbing of the eyelids, the quivering of the lip, Kumāras. 7, 18.<BR> --Caus. स्फारय, and † स्फोरय, To cast, Lass. 66, 8. स्फारित,<BR> 1. Throbbing, Mālat. 60, 12.<BR> 2. Spread, large, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 552.<BR> --With अभि अभि, अभि-स्फुरित,<BR> 1. Expanded, in full bloom.<BR> 2. Known.<BR> --With परि परि, परिस्फुरित,<BR> 1. Glanced.<BR> 2. Glancing.<BR> 3. Expanded, Utt. Rāmac. 72, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To tremble, MBh. 3, 11498. प्रस्फुरित,<BR> 1. Trembling, Johns. Sel. 22, 112.<BR> 2. Swollen, Pañc. 220, 1.<BR> 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a " target="_blank">Page1089-a + 41</a>] Budded.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To tremble, MBh. 3, 15639.<BR> 2. To struggle, MBh. 1, 6001.<BR> 3. To glitter, Kathās. 26, 283. विस्फुरित,<BR> 1. Tremulous, shaken, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 10.<BR> 2. Swollen, enlarged.<BR> --Caus. स्फारय,<BR> 1. To draw (a bow), Rām. 3, 30, 28; Kir. 17, 24.<BR> 2. To cause to flash, MBh. 3, 404. विस्फारित,<BR> 1. Trembling.<BR> 2. Flashing, Rām. 1, 54, 19.<BR> 3. Twanged or drawn, as a bowstring, Kir. 14, 31.<BR> 4. Evident.<BR> --Cf. σπαίρω (i. e. σπαρ + ϳω; the Sskr. फ् is produced by the influence of स्), ἀ-σπαίρω, probably σπείρω, σπέρμα, σποράς; the ved. use shows that hither belong also A.S. spurnan; σϕυρόν; A.S. spura; probably Lat. sperno. Cf. स्खल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर|स्फुरः
स्फुर स्फुर् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Trembling, Pañc. iii. d. 237; throbbing.<BR> 2. Swelling.<BR> 3. A shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरण|स्फुरणं
स्फुरण स्फुरण, i. e. स्फुर् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Trembling, Bhāg. P. 3, 26, 29 (trembling appearance).<BR> 2. Quivering of the lips, throbbing of the eyes.<BR> 3. Expansion of the mind, Pañc. 42, 6.<BR> 4. Breaking forth, flashing, Megh. 28; glittering, Mālat. 143, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्छ्
† स्फुर्छ् स्फुर्छ् (i. e. स्फुर् + छ्), स्वुर्छ् स्वुर्छ्, i. 1, स्फूर्च्छ, स्वूर्च्छ, Par.<BR> 1. To expand.<BR> 2. To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्
स्फुर्ज् स्फुर्ज् (i. e. स्फुर् + ज्), i. 1, स्फूर्ज, Par. To thunder, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 41.<BR> --With वि वि, विस्फूर्जित, Resounding (as arrows), Bhāg. P. 2, 7, 25. n.<BR> 1. Roar (of the wind), Arj. 8, 6 (read स्फूर्ज्˚).<BR> 2. Increase, Ragh. 13, 12, Calc. Sch.<BR> --Cf. Lat. spargo; A.S. sprecan; spraencan, sprengan, sprincan, springan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल्
स्फुल् स्फुल् (originally = स्फुर्), also स्फल् स्फल्, which, like स्फर्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b " target="_blank">Page1089-b + 39</a>] appears only in the Caus. and derivative nouns, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. † To tremble, to throb.<BR> 2. † To appear.<BR> 3. † To collect.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. स्फालय,<BR> 1. To strike, Utt. Rāmac. 123, 4; Ragh. 16, 13; to touch, Utt. Rāmac. 150, 8 (?).<BR> 2. To crush, Pañc. 93, 17.<BR> --With वि वि, To move cheerfully, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 76.<BR> --Cf. σϕάλλω (Caus.); O.H.G. fallan; A.S. feallan; Lat. fallere. Cf. स्खल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल|स्फुलं
स्फुल स्फुल् + अ, n. A tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलन|स्फुलनं
स्फुलन स्फुल् + अन, n. Trembling, throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिङ्ग स्फुलिङ्ग, probably स्फुल् + अ + म्-ग, m., f. गा, n. A spark of fire, Vikr. d. 125.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलिङ्ग|विस्फुलिंग|विस्फुलिंगः|विस्फुलिङ्गः
वि- + स्फुलिङ्ग वि- + स्फुलिङ्ग, m. 1. the same. 2. a sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्गिन्
स्फुलिङ्गिन् स्फुलिङ्गिन्, adj., f. नी, Having sparks of fire, Mārk. P. 99, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्जः|स्फूर्ज्ज
स्फूर्ज स्फूर्ज, i. e. स्फुरिज् + अ, m.<BR> 1. The sound of thunder.<BR> 2. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जथु|स्फूर्जथुः|स्फूर्ज्जथु
स्फूर्जथु स्फूर्जथु, i. e. स्फुर्ज् + अथु, m. A thunderclap, Mahāvīrac. 124, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्ति स्फूर्ति, i. e. स्फुर् + ति, f. Shaking, Bhartṛ. 3, 34; throbbing, Windischmann, Sankara, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्तिमन्त्|स्फूर्तिमत्|स्फूर्त्तिमत्
स्फूर्तिमन्त् स्फूर्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Tremulous.<BR> 2. Kind-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयंस्
स्फेयंस् स्फेयंस्, स्फेष्ठ स्फेष्ठ, see स्फिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोट|स्फोटः
स्फोट स्फोट, i. e. स्फुट् + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Bursting, breaking.<BR> 2. A tumour, a boil, Suśr. 2, 383, 10.<BR> 3. The eternal sound, in the Pūrva Mīmāṃsā.<BR> II. f. टा, The hood of the snake.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तास्फोट|मुक्तास्फोटः
मुक्ता- + स्फोट मुक्ता- + स्फोट, m. a pearl-oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन स्फोटन, i. e. स्फुट् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Breaking, Pañc. 81, 8; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a " target="_blank">Page1090-a + 42</a>] tearing.<BR> 2. Fidgeting with the hand, snapping the fingers.<BR> II. f. नी, A gimblet, an auger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्य|स्फ्यं
स्फ्य स्फ्य, n. An implement used in sacrifices, shaped like a spit, Man. 5, 117; cf. Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. xxxvi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बॄ
स्बॄ स्बॄ, see स्वॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म स्म, an old case (probably the instr. sing. n.) of सम; a particle.<BR> 1. A present and ptcple. of the pres. followed by it have generally a past sense; e. g. प्रति वसतः, स्म, They dwelt, Pañc. 43, 1; कथयन्तौ स्म...आसाताम्, Chr. 16, 20, They were sitting and told.<BR> 2. Preceded by मा, sometimes after a present, and in the Ved., after particles, it has no distinct signification; मा स्म कार्षीस्, Do not, Chr. 41, 4; चरन्ति स्म, They go, Indr. 1, 23; अध स्म, Lass. 98, 14 = Rigv. v. 9, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मय|स्मयः
स्मय स्मय, i. e. स्मि + अ, m.<BR> 1. Surprise, astonishment.<BR> 2. Arrogance, pride, Bhartṛ. 3, 2; Rājat. 5, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर|स्मरः
स्मर स्मर, i. e. स्मृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Recollection.<BR> 2. Love, Hit. 86, 4, M.M.<BR> 3. Kāma, the god of love, Pañc. 226, 1; Śāk. d. 119 (and at the same time, perhaps, Remembrance).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मर
जाति- + स्मर जाति- + स्मर, adj., f. रा, one who remembers or knows his former existences, MBh. 3, 8180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्मर
दुस्- + स्मर दुस्- + स्मर, adj. disagreeable to be remembered, Utt. Rāmac. 157, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरण|स्मरणं
स्मरण स्मरण, i. e. स्मृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Remembering, Hit. ii. d. 56; remembrance, Pañc. 208, 14.<BR> 2. Memory,<BR> 3. Regretting.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मरण
जाति- + स्मरण जाति- + स्मरण, n. Remembering one's former existences, MBh. 12, 6256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवीथिका
स्मरवीथिका स्मर-वीथि + का, f. A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्तृ
स्मर्तृ स्मर्तृ, i. e. स्मृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, n. Who or what remembers, Bhāg. P. 1, 15, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारण|स्मारणं
स्मारण स्मारण, i. e. स्मृ, Caus., + अन, n. Calling to mind, causing to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त स्मार्त, i. e. स्मृति + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Memorial, relating to memory.<BR> 2. Within memory.<BR> 3. Recorded in the स्मृतिस्, or codes of law, Man. 1, 108.<BR> 4. Following or professing the law books.<BR> II. m. A Brāhmaṇa following the revealed law; one who knows the traditional law, Pañc. i. d. 283.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि स्मि, i. 1, Ātm. (in epic poetry also Par., Chr. 27, 1), To smile, Chr. 27, 3. स्मित,<BR> 1. Smiling, Pañc. i. d. 152.<BR> 2. Blown (as a flower), Pañc. i. d. 152. n. A smile, Vikr. 13, 4.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --† i. 10, Ātm. To despise. Frequent. सेष्मीय, To suffer from convulsions, to tremble, Mālav. 47, 5.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To smile, MBh. 3, 8237.<BR> --With उद् उद्, To smile, MBh. 1, 7059. उत्स्मायित्वा (Rām. 1, 1, 63), is an anomalous form either for उत्स्माययित्वा, Caus. ‘To make a mock of, to insult.’ or for उत्स्मित्वा, and then to be changed to उत्स्मयित्वा, ‘To burst into laughter.’<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To smile, Chr. 44, 35.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To be surprised, Rām. 3, 49, 3.<BR> 2. To admire.<BR> 3. To be proud, Man. 4, 236. विस्मित, Astonished, perplexed, Hit. 56, 18.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. स्मापय, To cause to be surprised, Ragh. 2, 33.<BR> --Cf. स्मेर and O.H.G. smielan; A.S. smaerc, smirk; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-a " target="_blank">Page1091-a + 41</a>] Lat. mirari; probably σμοιός, μέμϕομαι (Caus.), μῶμος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्मित
शुचि- + स्मित शुचि- + स्मित, adj. smiled, smiling sweetly, Rām. 3, 49, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
स- + स्मित स- + स्मित, adj. smiling; ˚तम्, adv., Vikr. 28, 12; Rām. 3, 49, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मित
सु- + स्मित सु- + स्मित, adj. smiling. f. ता, a woman with a smiling countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्मित
सु- + विस्मित सु- + विस्मित, adj. much surprised, Pañc. 41, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट्
† स्मिट् स्मिट् (akin to स्मि), i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To despise.<BR> 2. To love.<BR> 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील्
स्मील् स्मील्, see च्मील्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
1. स्मृ स्मृ, i. 1, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 1, 3005),<BR> 1. To remember (with acc. and gen.), Vikr. 29, 16; Chr. 20, 17; with the second fut. in the sense of past time, Śiś. 1, 68, स्मरति--हनिष्यति, You remember having killed.<BR> 2. To desire, to long for (with gen.), MBh. 3, 12281.<BR> 3. To record, to declare, Pañc. i. d. 36. स्मृत,<BR> 1. Recollected.<BR> 2. Recorded, Chr. 52, 11.<BR> 3. Said (according to traditional doctrine), Man. 1, 20.<BR> 4. Allowed (according to tradition), Man. 3, 13.<BR> 5. Called, Man. 1, 10.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. of the fut. pass. स्मर-स्मर्य, m. An ass.<BR> --Caus.<BR> I. स्मारय,<BR> 1. To cause to remember, MBh. 2, 2484; with gen., Kir. 6, 13 (स्म्ăरय.).<BR> 2. To give in formation, Mālat. 8, 9.<BR> II. स्म्ăरय, To cause to remember with grief, Vikr. d. 78.<BR> --With अनु अनु,<BR> 1. To call to mind, Man. 2, 217; to remember, Bhāg. P. 4, 30, 28 (pass.)<BR> 2. To invoke, Pañc. 258, 25.<BR> --Caus. स्मारय, To cause to remember with sorrow, Kir. 5, 14.<BR> --With अप अप, To forget, Mālat. 161, 2.<BR> --With वि वि, To forget, MBh. 3, 15705; Śāk. 37, 4.<BR> --Caus. स्मारय, To cause to forget, Vikr. d. 59.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To remember, Man. 4, 149.<BR> --Caus. स्मारय, To cause to remember, MBh. 2, 2537.<BR> --With अनुसम् अनु-सम्,<BR> 1. To remember, MBh. 1, 6911.<BR> 2. To long for, MBh. 4, 149.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b " target="_blank">Page1091-b + 42</a>] remember, MBh. 3, 15758.<BR> --Cf. μάρτυρ, μέριμνα, μέρμερος; Lat. memor; O.H.G. mâri; Goth. mêrjan, meritha; A.S. maelan, mal, ge-maered, maerdh, a-maerian, maersian, meldian; Goth. maurnan; A.S. murnan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
2. स्मृ स्मृ, see स्पृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृति|स्मृतिः
स्मृति स्मृ + ति, f.<BR> 1. Recollection, remembrance, memory, Hit. iv. d. 96; Bhag. 2, 63; Bhāṣāp. 47; Rājat. 5, 5; Utt. Rāmac. 100, 14.<BR> 2. The body of law, as delivered originally by tradition; tradition, Man. 2, 6; Pañc. 164, 20.<BR> 3. A law book.<BR> 4. A passage concerning law, Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 2.<BR> 5. Understanding.<BR> 6. Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिमन्त्|स्मृतिमत्
स्मृतिमन्त् स्मृति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती,<BR> 1. Remembering, having recovered one's recollection, Śāk. 112, 16.<BR> 2. Having a good memory, Man. 7, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर स्मेर, i. e. स्मि + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Smiling, Kāvya Prak. 121, 5; Ratnāv. p. 35, 10 (2. ed.).<BR> 2. Blown (as a flower), blooming, Bhartṛ. 1, 35; opened, Mālat. 16, 10.<BR> 3. Evident.<BR> II. m. Evidence, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद|स्यदः
स्यद स्यद, i. e. स्यन्द् + अ, m. Speed, Nalod. 4, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द्|स्यंद्
स्यन्द् स्यन्द्, i. 1, Ātm., and in the aor., fut., and condit., Par.<BR> 1. To drop, to distill, Lass. 59, 5.<BR> 2. To flow, MBh. 1, 3990.<BR> 3. To run, Nal. 13, 10.<BR> --With the prep. अभि अभि (ष्यन्द् and स्यन्द्), To rain on, Utt. Rāmac. 16, 10; 133, 9 (हृदयं स्नेहेन, To flow, to melt with love).<BR> --With नि नि (ष्यन्द् and स्यन्द्), To flow, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यन्दन स्यन्द् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Quick, Kir. 15, 16.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A war chariot, Hit. iii. d. 81.<BR> 2. Air.<BR> 3. A tree, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a " target="_blank">Page1092-a + 39</a>] Dalbergia ougeinensis, Nal. 12, 3.<BR> II. f. नी, Saliva.<BR> IV. n.<BR> 1. Oozing, Bhāṣāp. 6; 155.<BR> 2. Water.<BR> 3. Going swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनिका|स्यंदनिका
स्यन्दनिका स्यन्दनिका, i. e. स्यन्दनी + क, f. A drop of saliva, Rām. 3, 53, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिन्|स्यंदिन्
स्यन्दिन् स्यन्द् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Oozing, trickling, Utt. Rāmac. 23, 3.<BR> 2. Going.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. Saliva.<BR> 2. A cow bearing twins.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्यन्दिन्|सुधास्यंदिन्
सुधा- + स्यन्दिन् सुधा- + स्यन्दिन्, adj. flowing with nectar, Bhartṛ. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम्
† स्यम् स्यम्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To go.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm. To consider, to think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमन्तक स्यमन्तक, m. The gem worn by Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीक|स्यमीकः
स्यमीक स्यमीक,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. An anthill.<BR> 2. A particular tree.<BR> 3. Time.<BR> 4. Cloud.<BR> II. f. का, Indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याल|स्यालः
स्याल स्याल, and श्याल श्याल,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A wife's brother, Bhag. 1, 34 (श्).<BR> 2. The favourite of a king, Rājat. 5, 451 (? श्).<BR> II. f. ली, A wife's sister.<BR> --Cf. ἀέλιοι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूति|स्यूतिः
स्यूति स्यूति, i. e. सिव् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Sewing, needle-work.<BR> 2. A sack.<BR> 3. Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यून|स्यूनः
स्यून स्यून, i. e. सिव् + न, m.<BR> 1. A ray of light.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूम|स्यूमं|स्यूमः
स्यूम स्यूम, i. e. सिव् + म, m. A ray of light; cf. स्यूम-रश्मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योत|स्योतः
स्योत स्योत, vb. सिव्, m. A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन स्योन,<BR> A. adj. Handsome, pleasing.<BR> B. (vb. सिव्),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A ray of light.<BR> 2. The sun.<BR> 3. A sack.<BR> II. n. Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंश्
स्रंश् स्रंश्, v. r. of the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
1. स्रंस् स्रंस्, i. 1, Ātm. To fall [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b " target="_blank">Page1092-b + 40</a>] down. Bhag. 1, 30; to fall asunder, Utt. Rāmac. 77, 15.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. स्रस्त.<BR> 1. Fallen, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 20.<BR> 2. Hanging down, Śāk. d. 29.<BR> 3. Loosened.<BR> 4. Separated.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to fall from, Bhartṛ. 1, 49.<BR> 2. To move, Ragh. 6, 75.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. स्रंसित, Caused to be loosened, Utt. Rāmac. 40, 12.<BR> --With the prep. आ आ, आस्रस्त, Fallen off, MBh. 4, 777.<BR> --With वि वि, विस्रस्त, The same, Arj. 10, 64.<BR> --Caus. To cause to drop, Mahāvīrac. 73, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
2. स्रंस् स्रंस्, v. r. of श्रम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन् स्रंस् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Falling, Mālat. 79, 3; being loosened, Śāk. d. 29.<BR> 2. Hanging down, pendulous.<BR> II. m. A tree, commonly पीलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंह्
† स्रंह् स्रंह्, i. 1, Ātm. To confide (cf. श्रम्भ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्विन्
स्रग्विन् स्रग्विन्, i. e. स्रज् + विन्, adj., f. नी, Bearing a chaplet, Man. 2, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रङ्क्
स्रङ्क् स्रङ्क्, see श्रङ्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज् स्रज्, vb. सृज्, f. A chaplet, a wreath of flowers, a garland, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3322; Vedāntas. in Chr. 203, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रम्भ्|स्रंभ्
स्रम्भ् स्रम्भ्, see श्रम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रव|स्रवः
स्रव स्रव, i. e. स्रु + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Oozing, trickling, flowing, Lass. 2. ed. 59, 5.<BR> 2. A drop, Hiḍ. 2, 9.<BR> 3. A fountain.<BR> II. f. वा, A plant, Sanseviera zeylanica.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. ῥόος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिस्रव
गिरि- + स्रव गिरि- + स्रव, f. वा, a mountain stream, MBh. 13, 6362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवण|स्रवणं
स्रवण स्रवण, i. e. स्रु + अन, n.<BR> 1. Oozing, flowing.<BR> 2. Sweat.<BR> 3. Urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवन्त
स्रवन्त स्रवन्त, i. e. स्रवन्त्, ptcple. pres. of स्रु, + अ, adj. Dropping, Pañc. i. d. 346.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ स्रष्टृ, i. e. सृज् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A creator, Man. 1, 33; MBh. 7, 2864; Vikr. d. 159.<BR> 2. A maker, author, Rājat. 4, 655.<BR> 3. Brahman.<BR> 4. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तर|स्रस्तरः
स्रस्तर स्रस्तर, i. e. probably स्रंस् + तृ + अ, or + त्र, n. A bed, Kāvya Prak. 68, 4 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक् स्राक्, vb. सृ, probably सर-अञ्च्, cf. द्राक्, acc. sing. n., adv. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राव|स्रावः
स्राव स्राव, i. e. स्रु + अ, m. Oozing, flowing.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्राव|गर्भस्रावः
गर्भ- + स्राव गर्भ- + स्राव, m. miscarriage, abortment, Pañc. pr. d. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासास्राव|नासास्रावः
नासा- + स्राव नासा- + स्राव, m. catarrh, Suśr. 2, 371, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालास्राव|लालास्रावः
लाला- + स्राव लाला- + स्राव, m. a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
स्रिध् स्रिध्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To injure, to assail (ved.).<BR> 2. To be injured (ved.).<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. stritan, strit; A.S. stridh; Lat. stlis, lis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
स्रिध् स्रिध्, An enemy, Chr. 87, 8 = Rigv. i. 48, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ्
स्रिभ् स्रिभ्, स्रिम्भ् स्रिम्भ्, see सृभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव्
† स्रिव् स्रिव्, i. 4, स्रीव्य, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु स्रु (cf. सृ), श्रु श्रु (bad), † शु शु, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To flow, Rām. 2, 63, 18; Man. 4, 122.<BR> 2. To slip away, Man. 4, 74; to perish, MBh. 2, 932.<BR> 3. To be divulged, to transpire, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 3.<BR> 4. To let flow, Rām. 2, 91, 15; to shed, MBh. 1, 1485. स्रुत, Flowing, dropping, Śiś. 9, 15.<BR> --Caus. स्रावय, To cause to flow, Man. 4, 169.<BR> --With निस् निस्, Caus. To cause to flow off, to empty, MBh. 3, 13164.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To flow round about, Mālat. 169, 3.<BR> 2. To flow, MBh. 3, 2966. परिस्रुत, Oozed, trickled. f. ता, Vinous or distilled liquor.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b " target="_blank">Page1093-b + 40</a>] प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To flow forth, MBh. 3, 8127.<BR> 2. To let flow, Rām. 2, 48, 13; Hit. i. d. 177, M.M. (to yield, viz. milk). प्रस्रुत,<BR> 1. Oozed, dropped.<BR> 2. Dropping, Kir. 4, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With वि वि, To shed, MBh. 3, 825. विस्रुत,<BR> 1. Flowing, Rām. 1, 34, 9.<BR> 2. Dropped.<BR> 3. Spread.<BR> --Caus. विस्रावित,<BR> 1. Caused to flow.<BR> 2. Bled.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. straum; A.S. streám; O.H.G. sliumo, slunic, slunigên; ῥέω, ῥυθμός, Στρύμων.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रुत
त्रि- + स्रुत त्रि- + स्रुत, m. (an elephant in rut), of whom the juice breaks forth at three places of his forehead, Rām. 2, 26, 18 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुग्घ्नी
स्रुग्घ्नी स्रुग्घ्नी, probably स्रुच्-हन् + अ, f. Natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् स्रुच्, i. e. स्रु-अञ्च्, f. A sort of ladle to pour clarified butter on a sacrificial fire, Draup. 6, 20; Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. xli. 4; 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत्
ऽस्रुत् -स्रु + त्, adj. Flowing, distilling; e. g. अमृत-, adj. Distilling nectar, Śiś. 9, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुति|स्रुतिः
स्रुति स्रु + ति, f.<BR> 1. Oozing, distilling; Kir. 5, 44.<BR> 2. Exudation, resin, Megh. 106.<BR> 3. Stream, Rājat. 5, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुव|स्रुवः
स्रुव स्रुव, i. e. स्रु + अ (cf. श्रुव),<BR> I. m., and f. वा, A sacrificial ladle to pour घृत on a sacrificial fire, Journ. of the German Oriental Society, ix. viii.<BR> II. f. वा, The name of two plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू स्रू (vb. स्रु), f.<BR> 1. A sacrificial ladle, Rām. 1, 60, 12.<BR> 2. A cascade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
† स्रेक् स्रेक्, सेक् सेक्, श्रेक् श्रेक्, स्वेक् स्वेक्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै स्रै, see श्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत|स्रोतं|स्रोतः
स्रोत स्रोत, i. e. curtailed स्रोतस्, n. A rapid stream.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कस्रोत
शुष्क- + स्रोत शुष्क- + स्रोत, adj., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a " target="_blank">Page1094-a + 44</a>] f. ता, of whom the water is dried up, Nal. 16, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस् स्रोतस्, i. e. स्रु + तस्, n.<BR> 1. A current, stream, Vikr. d. 24.<BR> 2. The course of water, Mālat. 79, 18.<BR> 3. A torrent, Mālat. 60, 11; a river.<BR> 4. A wave, Śāk. d. 50.<BR> 5. A spring.<BR> 6. Water.<BR> 7. An organ of sense (? cf. श्रोतस् and Mallinātha ad Megh. 43), MBh. 1, 814.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्रोतस्
उद्- + स्रोतस् उद्- + स्रोतस्, and ऊर्ध्व-, adj. the course (of life) of which is going upwards, Bhāg. P. 3, 10, 18; MBh. 14, 1054.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गस्रोतस्
गर्ग- + स्रोतस् गर्ग- + स्रोतस्, n. the name of a place of pilgrimage, MBh. 9, 2132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यक्स्रोतस्|तिर्य्यक्स्रोतस्
तिर्यक्स्रोतस् तिर्यक्स्रोतस्, i. e. तिर्यञ्च्-, m. the course (of life) of which is going athwart, the animals, Mārk. P. 47, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रोतस्
त्रि- + स्रोतस् त्रि- + स्रोतस्, adj. having three courses, epithet of the Gaṅgā, Śāk. d. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलस्रोतस्
मूल- + स्रोतस् मूल- + स्रोतस्, n. principal current, Rājat. 5, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्य|स्रोतस्यः
स्रोतस्य स्रोतस् + य, m.<BR> 1. Śiva.<BR> 2. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती स्रोतस्वती, and स्रोतस्विनी स्रोतस्विनी, i. e. स्रोतस् + वन्त्, or विन्, + ई, f. A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोवह्
स्रोतोवह् स्रोतोवह्, and स्रोतोवहा स्रोतोवहा, i. e. स्रोतस्-वह्, or वह्, + अ, f. A river, Śāk. d. 50 (वह्); 143 (वहा); Vikr. 67, 4 (वहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व स्व,<BR> I. pron. refl. One's own self, Vedāntas. in Chr. 210, 13; Man. 8, 85; especially as former part of comp. words, e. g. स्व-गत, adj. Kept to one's self, apart; adv. स्वगतम्,<BR> 1. Speaking to himself, Pañc. 27, 11.<BR> 2. Aside (in theatrical language), Vikr. 30, 8.<BR> II. adj., f. स्वा.<BR> 1. Own, Pañc. i. d. 369; 226, 14 (my); Vikr. 27, 3 (thy); Hit. i. d. 16, M.M. (his).<BR> 2. Of one's own tribe, Man. 3, 13.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Soul, Nalod. 3, 30.<BR> 2. A kinsman, Man. 2, 109.<BR> IV. n. Property, wealth, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 13; Hit. 65, 17 (हृत-सर्व-, adj. Robbed of all his property).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. se, suns; Goth. sve, sik, seina; A.S. sín; σϕέ, ἕ, εἷο, ἑός; A.S. swa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवस्व|देवस्वं
देव- + स्व देव- + स्व, n. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b " target="_blank">Page1094-b + 39</a>] property of the gods, Man. 11, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्स्व
निस्- + स्व निस्- + स्व, adj. 1. deprived of property, Man. 9, 231. 2. poor, Pañc. ii. d. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्व
पर- + स्व पर- + स्व, n. another person's property, Man. 7, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्वम्
यथा-स्व + म् यथा-स्व + म्, adv. 1. properly. 2. individually, Kir. 14, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वस्व|सर्व्वस्व|सर्व्वस्वं
सर्व- + स्व सर्व- + स्व, n. 1. the whole property, Pañc. iii. d. 132. 2. the whole essence of anything, Pañc. 111, 6; iii. d. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक स्व + क, adj., f. का, Own, Pañc. iii. d. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय स्वकीय, i. e. स्वक + ईय, adj.<BR> 1. Own, Pañc. 187, 12; his, ib. 42, 2.<BR> 2. Of one's own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्ग्|स्वंग्
स्वङ्ग् स्वङ्ग्, see श्रङ्ग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छक
स्वच्छक स्वच्छक, i. e. सु-अच्छ + क, adj. White, beautiful, Pañc. i. d. 225 (pure = harmless ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्वज स्व-ज,<BR> I. adj. Self-born or produced.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A son.<BR> 2. Perspiration.<BR> III. f. जा, A daughter.<BR> IV. n. Blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजनाय
स्वजनाय स्वजनाय, a denomin. derived from स्व-जन with य, Ātm. To become a relation, Pañc. i. d. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्ज्|स्वंज्
स्वञ्ज् स्वञ्ज्, (probably from स्व), i. 1, स्वज, Ātm. (also Par., MBh. 4, 513), To embrace, MBh. 3, 2999.<BR> --With परि परि, ष्वञ्ज्, To embrace, Vikr. 11, 3.<BR> --With अभिपरि अभि-परि, To embrace, Rām. 2, 44, 10.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, To embrace, MBh. 1, 3307.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To embrace, Chr. 32, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् स्वठ्, see 3. 4. शठ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्र|स्वतंत्र|स्वतन्त्रः
स्वतन्त्र स्व-तन्त्र, see तन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रता
स्वतन्त्रता स्व-तन्त्र + ता, f.<BR> 1. Independence, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a " target="_blank">Page1095-a + 41</a>] Man. 5, 148.<BR> 2. Wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतस्
स्वतस् स्व + तस्, adv.<BR> 1. By one's own self, MBh. 3, 10054; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 15.<BR> 2. Of itself, Bhāṣāp. 135.<BR> 3. Out of one's own property, Man. 8, 166; 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वता
स्वता स्व + ता, f. Relation to one's own self, Śāk. d. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्र|स्वत्रः
स्वत्र स्व-त्र (vb. त्रा),<BR> I. adj. Selfpreserving.<BR> II. m. A blind man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्व|स्वत्वं
स्वत्व स्व + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Self-existence.<BR> 2. Independence.<BR> 3. Ownership, proprietary right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् स्वद्, i. e. probably सु-अद्,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्
स्वाद् स्वाद्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To taste, to eat, MBh. 1, 3362.<BR> 2. To please, to be liked, Śiś. 10, 23. स्वादनीय, Savoury, Indr. 1, 26.<BR> --i. 10, Par.<BR> 1. To taste, Bhaṭṭ. 7, 40.<BR> 2. † To cut.<BR> --With आं आ, To taste, to eat, Rām. 1, 9, 36.<BR> --Comp. ptcple. pf. pass., अन्-आस्वादित, adj. Not tasted, not touched, Śāk. d. 43. आस्वाद्य, Savoury, Hit. pr. d. 47, M.M. n.Cookery, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 7 (?).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --i. 10,<BR> 1. To taste, Pañc. 35, 3.<BR> 2. To eat, Pañc. 214, 22.<BR> --Cf. A.S. swaesend, Food; ἁνδάνω, εὔαδε, ἕαδα, ἑδανός, and ἡδονή (and see स्वादु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्वाद्य
निस्- + आस्वाद्य निस्- + आस्वाद्य, adj. yielding no enjoy ment, Rām. 2, 36, 12. आस्वादनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतास्वादनीय
अ-मृत- + आस्वादनीय अ-मृत- + आस्वाद्नीय, adj. as pleasant to the taste as nectar, MBh. 3, 1740.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदन|स्वदनं
स्वदन स्वद् + अन, n. Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्वधा स्व-धा,<BR> I. f.<BR> 1. Spontaneity, Chr. 290, 4 = Rigv. i. 64, 4 (they are produced without an external cause).<BR> 2. Self-will, strength, Chr. 294, 6 = Rigv. i. 88, 6.<BR> 3. A personification of Māya, or worldly illusion.<BR> 4. The food offered to deceased ancestors, Man. 9, 127. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b " target="_blank">Page1095-b + 41</a>]<BR> 5. A nymph, the food of the Manes personified.<BR> II. Indecl. An exclamation or blessing used on presenting an oblation to the Manes, Man. 3, 252.<BR> --Cf. Lat. suetus; Goth. sidus; A.S. sidu, siodo; ἔθος, ἦθος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाभुज्
स्वधाभुज् स्वधा-भुज्, m.<BR> 1. A deified ancestor.<BR> 2. A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिति|स्वधितिः
स्वधिति स्वधिति, m. and f., also ती ती, An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितीवन्त्|स्वधितीवत्
स्वधितीवन्त् स्वधिती + वन्त्, adj. Armed with an axe, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 88, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् स्वन्, i. 1, Par. To sound, e. g. to sing, Rām. 2, 65, 5.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. स्वनित, Sounding. n. The noise of thunder.<BR> II. स्वान्त, Sounded.<BR> --Caus. स्व्ăनय, †<BR> 1. To cause to sound.<BR> 2. † To sound.<BR> 3. and स्वानय, † To adorn.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव, or वि वि, To make a noise when eating; in this signification the vb. is changed to ष्वण्.<BR> --With नि नि, निस्वनित, n. Noise, MBh. 7, 324.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sonare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन स्वन् + अ, m. Sound, Nal. 25, 5.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sonus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करस्वन|करस्वनः
कर- + स्वन कर- + स्वन, m. the sound produced by clapping the hands, Rām. 5, 83, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्वन
दुस्- + स्वन दुस्- + स्वन, adj. sounding disagreeably, MBh. 5, 7241.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुस्वन|मंजुस्वन
मञ्जु- + स्वन मञ्जु- + स्वन, adj., f. ना, sweetsounding, Vikr. 60, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्वन|महास्वनः
महा- + स्वन महा- + स्वन,<BR> I. adj. loud-sounding, Nal. 21, 5.<BR> II. m. 1. a loud sound. 2. a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामेघस्वन
महा-मेघ- + स्वन महा-मेघ- + स्वन, adj. having the sound of a large cloud, Indr. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनि|स्वनिः
स्वनि स्वन् + इ, m. Sound, Mahāv. 132, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
ऽस्वनिक -स्वनिक in पाणि-, i. e. पाणि-स्वन + इक, m. One who claps the hands, MBh. 12, 1899.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्
स्वप् स्वप्, ii. 2 (i. 1, Man. 4, 99), Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 3, 15993),<BR> 1. To sleep, Man. 1, 25.<BR> 2. To fall asleep, MBh. 2, 2027.<BR> 3. To lie down to sleep, to go to bed, Man. 4, 99.<BR> 4. To lie down, to extend one's self, Man. 11, 103.<BR> 5. To lie, MBh. 4, 1674.<BR> 6. To be dead, Bhaṭṭ. 18, 11.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. सुप्त.<BR> 1. Having slept, Sāv. 5, 64.<BR> 2. Sleeping, Vikr. d. 135.<BR> 3. Senseless. n. Sleep.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With the prep. अव अव. To sleep, Rām. 2, 56, 1.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To fall asleep, Hit. 50, 2. प्रसुप्त,<BR> 1. Beginning to sleep, Pañc. 134, 6; gone to bed, Pañc. 117, 12.<BR> 2. Fallen asleep, Chr. 38, 6.<BR> 3. Slept, Sāv. 5, 65.<BR> 4. Sleeping, Daśak. in Chr. 199, 6.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To sleep, MBh. 1, 955.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To sleep, MBh. 1, 5967.<BR> --Cf. Lat. sopire (Caus.); A.S. swefian; O.H.G. suabjan, suebjan; ὕπαρ; see स्वप्न, also with ल् for व् (cf. श्वस्); Goth. slêpan; A.S. slápan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वप्न|दिवास्वप्नः
दिवा- + स्वप्न दिवा- + स्वप्न, adj. sleeping at day, Hit. iii. d. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपन|स्वपनं
स्वपन स्वप् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Sleeping, Hit. iii. d. 75.<BR> 2. Sleep.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वपन
दिवा- + स्वपन दिवा- + स्वपन, n. sleeping by day, Suśr. 1, 330, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्तुकाम
स्वप्तुकाम स्वप्तुकाम, i. e. स्वप्तुम्-काम (vb. स्वप्), adj. Wishing to sleep, Johns. Sel. 91, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न|स्वप्नः
स्वप्न स्वप् + न, m.<BR> 1. Sleep, Vedāntas. in Chr. 208, 6.<BR> 2. Indolence, Man. 12, 33.<BR> 3. Dreaming.<BR> 4. A dream, Vikr. d. 29; Pañc. 134, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. swefn; Lat. somnus; ὕπνος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रत्स्वप्न
जाग्रत्स्वप्न जाग्रत्स्वप्न, i. e. जाग्रन्त्-, m. waking and sleeping, Man. 1, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वप्न|दिवास्वप्नः
दिवा- + स्वप्न दिवा- + स्वप्न, m. sleeping by day, Man. 7, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्वप्न|दुःस्वप्नः
दुस्- + स्वप्न दुस्- + स्वप्न, m. an inauspicious dream, Rām. 2, 71, 23 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्वप्न
सु- + स्वप्न सु- + स्वप्न, m. a lucky dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज् स्वप्न-ज् (ज्, from vb. जन्), adj. Sleeping, asleep, MBh. 3, 10648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज
स्वप्नज स्वप्न-ज, adj. Produced by a dream, Megh. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावज
स्वभावज स्व-भाव-ज, adj.<BR> 1. Become by one's own nature, Hit. i. d. 205, M.M.<BR> 2. Innate, Hit. i. d. 194, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावतस्
स्वभावतस् स्व-भाव + तस्, adv. By one's own nature, Pañc. 166, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभू
स्वभू स्व-भू, m.<BR> 1. Viṣṇu.<BR> 2. Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवर|स्वयंवरः
स्वयंवर स्वयंवर, i. e. स्वयम्-वर,<BR> I. m. The public choice of a husband by a princess, Nal. 2, 8.<BR> II. f. रा, A girl choosing her husband, Man. 9, 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् स्वयम् (from स्व), indecl.<BR> 1. Reflective pronoun of the three persons; Self, myself, Pañc. 163, 19; himself, Pañc. iii. d. 114; one's self, Hit. ii. d. 23; by himself, Mālat. 70, 5.<BR> 2. Spontaneously, Bhartṛ. 2, 82; Pañc. 230, 15.<BR> 3. Of one's own accord, Pañc. v. d. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंभू|स्वयम्भू
स्वयंभू स्वयंभू, i. e. स्वयम्-भू- (existing by himself, not created), m.<BR> 1. Brahman, Man. 1, 3; 94; Viṣṇu, Śiva, Pañc. i. d. 422 (?).<BR> 2. Time.<BR> 3. Love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
† 1. स्वर् स्वर् (सुर् सुर्), i. 10, स्वरय (सुरय), To blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
2. स्वर् स्वर्, i. e. सू + अन् (with र् for न्),<BR> I. n. (Rigv. i. 105, 3), The sun, Chr. 289, 5 = Rigv. i. 50, 5.<BR> II. indecl.<BR> 1. Splendour.<BR> 2. Heaven, Bhag. 9, 20; Rājat. 5, 8.<BR> 3. Paradise.<BR> 4. A mystical word, signifying the space between the sun and polar star, Man. 2, 76; Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर स्वर, i. e. स्वृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sound, Pañc. 82, 17; voice, Pañc. v. d. 83. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a " target="_blank">Page1097-a + 40</a>]<BR> 2. Snoring.<BR> 3. A note in music, Pañc. v. d. 43.<BR> 4. A vowel.<BR> 5. Accent, Sāv. 5, 25.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अ- + स्वर अ- + स्वर, adj. low, indistinct, Rām. 2, 42, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारस्वर
तार- + स्वर तार- + स्वर, m. loud sound or voice, Pañc. 97, 19; 107, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नस्वर
भिन्न- + स्वर भिन्न- + स्वर (vb. भिद्), adj. 1. faltering in speech. 2. hoarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्वर
महा- + स्वर महा- + स्वर, adj. crying aloud, Rām. 3, 55, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वर|विस्वरः
वि- + स्वर वि- + स्वर, adj. discordant, inharmonious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्वर
सु- + स्वर सु- + स्वर, adj. loud, Chr. 12, 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित स्वरित, i. e. स्वर + इत,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Articulated.<BR> 2. Sounded as a note.<BR> 3. Accented.<BR> II. m. The circumflex accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरु|स्वरुः
स्वरु स्वरु, m., i. e.<BR> I. स्वृ + उ,<BR> 1. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR> 2. An arrow.<BR> II.<BR> 1. Sunshine.<BR> 2. A sacrifice.<BR> 3. A kind of scorpion.<BR> 4. Shavings of the sacrificial post.<BR> 5. The sacrificial post, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 92, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपता
स्वरूपता स्व-रूप + ता, f.<BR> 1. Natural state.<BR> 2. Handsomeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग|स्वर्गः
स्वर्ग स्वर्-ग, m. Heaven, Indra's paradise, Bhartṛ. 2, 85; Vikr. d. 59; Pañc. i. d. 248.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वर्ग|भूस्वर्गः
भू- + स्वर्ग भू- + स्वर्ग, m. the mountain Sumeru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गजित्
स्वर्गजित् स्वर्ग-जि + त्, adj. Obtaining or ensuring paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गद
स्वर्गद स्वर्ग-द (vb. दा), adj. Procuring paradise, Pañc. i. d. 283.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिन्
स्वर्गिन् स्वर्गिन्, i. e. स्वर्ग + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A deity, Śāk. d. 193; Megh. 31.<BR> 2. (In law), Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीय
स्वर्गीय स्वर्गीय, i. e. स्वर्ग + ईय, adj. Heavenly, divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग्य|स्वर्ग्यः
स्वर्ग्य स्वर्ग्य, i. e. स्वर्ग + य, adj.<BR> 1. Heavenly.<BR> 2. Procuring a place in heaven, Man. 3, 106.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अ- + स्वर्ग्य अ- + स्वर्ग्य, adj. prejudicial to heavenly beatitude, Man. 2, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्जित्
स्वर्जित् स्वर्-जि + त् (m.), A peculiar sacrifice, Man. 11, 74 (cf. स्वर्गजित्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ण|स्वर्णं
स्वर्ण स्वर्ण, i. e. सु-वर्ण, n. Gold, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 14; a gold coin, Kathās. 22, 97.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटस्वर्ण
कूट- + स्वर्ण कूट- + स्वर्ण, n. counterfeit gold, Yājñ. 2, 297.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक
स्वर्णक स्वर्ण + क, adj. Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकृत्
स्वर्णकृत् स्वर्ण-कृ + त्, m. A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णज|स्वर्णजं
स्वर्णज स्वर्ण-ज, n. Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदी
स्वर्णदी स्वर्णदी, i. e. स्वर्-नदी, f. The Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्त्|स्वर्त्त्
स्वर्त् स्वर्त्, see श्वर्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्द्|स्वर्द्द्
† स्वर्द् स्वर्द्, i. 1, Ātm. To taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्
† स्वल् स्वल्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पक
स्वल्पक स्वल्पक, i. e. सु-अल्प + क, adj.<BR> 1. Little.<BR> 2. Few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पशिलाय
स्वल्पशिलाय स्वल्पशिलाय, a denomin. derived from सु-अल्प-शिला, with य, Ātm. To become a little stone, Bhartṛ. 2, 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववीर्यतस्
स्ववीर्यतस् स्व-वीर्य + तस्, adv. Conformably to one's power, Pañc. i. d. 460.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृ
स्वसृ स्वसृ, i. e. probably स्व-स्त्री, f. A sister, Hiḍ. 1, 31; Chr. 295, 11 = Rigv. i. 92, 11 (the night).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. svistar; A.S. sweoster, swuster, syster; Lat. soror, con-sobrinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमस्वसृ
यम- + स्वसृ यम- + स्वसृ, f. the Yamunā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृत्
स्वसृत् स्व-सृ + त्, adj. Going or moving at one's own will, Chr. 294, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्क्
स्वस्क् स्वस्क्, see ष्वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्ति
स्वस्ति स्वस्ति, i. e. सु- 1. अस् + ति,<BR> I. f. Welfare, blessing, Lass. 102, 12 = Rigv. vii. 14, 3. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a " target="_blank">Page1098-a + 44</a>]<BR> II. indecl.<BR> 1. A particle of benediction, bliss, hail! happiness, in the sense of a nomin., Chr. 36, 16; Vikr. 87, 19; Rām. 3, 51, 37; or acc., Nal. 12, 120.<BR> 2. A term of sanction or approbation, so be it!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिक|स्वस्तिकः
स्वस्तिक स्वस्ति + क,<BR> I. m. and n. A temple of a particular form, with a portico in front.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Any auspicious object.<BR> 2. The meeting of four roads.<BR> 3. A palace having a portico on three sides.<BR> 4. A mystical mark, Mālat. 73, 13 (at the end of a Bahuvr. comp. f. का); a cross.<BR> 5. The crossing of the arms.<BR> 6. A particular kind of posture, Vedāntas. in Chr. 217, 17.<BR> 7. A kind of cake.<BR> 8. A libertine.<BR> 9. Garlic.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मस्वस्तिक
पद्म- + स्वस्तिक पद्म- + स्वस्तिक, m. or n. a mystical mark consisting of lotus flowers, Rām. 5, 10, 4 (Sch. a fourcornered sort of painting).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमन्त्|स्वस्तिमत्
स्वस्तिमन्त् स्वस्ति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्त्ययन
स्वस्त्ययन स्वस्त्ययन, i. e. स्वस्ति-अयन,<BR> I. adj. Auspicious, producing happiness, Man. 1, 106.<BR> II. n. The recitation of holy texts for the averting of evil, Man. 5, 152; benediction, Chr. 25, 51 (कृत-स्वस्त्ययन, adj. After having received benedictions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थ|स्वस्थः
स्वस्थ स्व-स्थ, adj., f. था,<BR> 1. Relying upon one's self, resolute, Pañc. 106, 22; firm, Pañc. ii. d. 88.<BR> 2. Content, Pañc. 56, 2.<BR> 3. Well, safe, Mālat. 63, 12; healthy, Man. 7, 226.<BR> 4. Selfsufficient, independent, Nal. 2, 1. (दमयन्ती न स्वस्था बभूव नलं प्रति, Damayantī was dependent with regard to Nala, i. e. she was in love with Nala).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अ- + स्वस्थ अ- + स्वस्थ, adj., f. था, 1. not firm, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 936. 2. ill, suffering, Śāk. 31, 9. 3. dependent, enamoured, Nal. 2, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थता
स्वस्थता स्वस्थ + ता, f. Well-being, health, Pañc. 159, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीय|स्वस्रीयः
स्वस्रीय स्वस्रीय, i. e. स्वसृ + ईय,<BR> I. m. A sister's son, Man. 3, 148.<BR> II. f. या, A sister's daughter, Man. 11, 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्तिका
स्वहस्तिका स्वहस्तिका (v. r. सुह्˚), i. e. स्व- (or सु), -हस्त + क, f. An axe (?), Pañc. 122, 10; 123, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाच्छन्द्य|स्वाच्छंद्य|स्वाच्छंद्यं|स्वाच्छन्द्यं|स्वाछन्द्य
स्वाच्छन्द्य स्वाच्छन्द्य, i. e. स्व-छन्द + य, n. Independence, wilfulness; abl. Voluntarily, Man. 3, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वातन्त्र्य|स्वातंत्र्य|स्वातंत्र्यं|स्वातन्त्र्यं
स्वातन्त्र्य स्वातन्त्र्य, i. e. स्व-तन्त्र + य, n.<BR> 1. Independence, Man. 9, 3; Bhartṛ. 3, 92.<BR> 2. Wilfulness, Man. 5, 147 (mere pleasure, Jones).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाति|स्वातिः
स्वाति or स्वाती स्वाती̆, f.<BR> 1. One of the wives of the sun.<BR> 2. The star Arcturus, or fifteenth lunar asterism.<BR> 3. An auspicious constellation, Bhartṛ. 2, 57.<BR> 4. A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्
स्वाद् स्वाद्, see स्वद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद|स्वादः
स्वाद स्वाद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Tasting, eating, Pañc. 253, 18; drinking.<BR> 2. Taste.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वाद
वि- + स्वाद वि- + स्वाद, adj. insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिन्
स्वादिन् स्वाद् + इन्, adj. Tasting, drinking, Nalod. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिमन्
स्वादिमन् स्वादिमन्, i. e. स्वादु + इमन्, m. Sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादु|स्वादुः
स्वादु स्वाद् + उ,<BR> I. adj., comparat. स्वादीयंस्, superl. स्रादिष्ठ,<BR> 1. Grateful to the palate.<BR> 2. Sweet, Pañc. v. d. 88; स्वादिष्ठ, with abl. Sweeter, Bhartṛ. 3, 97.<BR> 3. Agreeable.<BR> 4. Handsome.<BR> II. दु, adv. Sweetly.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. Sweetness, Megh. 25 (? n.).<BR> 2. Molasses.<BR> 3. A medicinal root.<BR> IV. f. दु, or द्वी, A grape.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. swét, swaes; Goth. suts; O.H.G. suozi; Lat. suavis (i. e. svādu + i), suadere; ἡδύς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वादु
निस्- + स्वादु निस्- + स्वादु, adj. unsweet, Hit. 77, 1, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनता
स्वाधीनता स्वाधीनता, i. e. स्व-अधीन + ता, f. Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायवन्त्|स्वाध्यायवत्
स्वाध्यायवन्त् स्वाध्यायवन्त्, i. e. स्व-अध्याय + वन्त्, m. A student of the Vedas, Johns. Sel. 36, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायिन्
स्वाध्यायिन् स्वाध्यायिन्, i. e. स्व-अध्याय + इन्,<BR> 1. A student of the Vedas.<BR> 2. A tradesman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान|स्वानः
स्वान स्वान, i. e. स्वन् + अ, m. Sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान्त|स्वांत|स्वान्तं
स्वान्त स्वान्त,<BR> I. See स्वन्.<BR> II. i. e. स्व-अन्त, n.<BR> 1. The mind, Vedāntas. in Chr. 202, 12; Bhartṛ. 3, 92.<BR> 2. A cavern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाप|स्वापः
स्वाप स्वाप, i. e. स्वप् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Sleeping, Utt. Rāmac. 24, 7; sleep.<BR> 2. Sleepiness.<BR> 3. Loss of sensation.<BR> 4. The sleep of a limb.<BR> 5. Ignorance.<BR> 6. Dream.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वाप|दिवास्वापः
दिवा- + स्वाप दिवा- + स्वाप, m. sleeping by day, Suśr. 1, 330, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापतेय|स्वापतेयं
स्वापतेय स्वापतेय, i. e. स्व-पति + एय, n. Wealth, MBh. 1, 1781; Pañc. ii. d. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविक|स्वाभाविकः
स्वाभाविक स्वाभाविक, i. e. स्व-भाव + इक, adj. Being by one's own nature, inherent, natural, Man. 3, 46; Pañc. 66, 10; 110, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिक
ऽस्वामिक -स्वामिक, i. e. स्वामिन् + क, a substitute for स्वामिन्, when latter part of a comp. adj.; e. g. प्रनष्ट- (so to be read instead of प्रणष्ट, Man. 8, 30), adj. That of which it is not known whether its owner is alive or dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामित्व|स्वामित्वं
स्वामित्व स्वामित्व, i. e. स्वामिन् + त्व, n.<BR> 1. Ownership.<BR> 2. Sovereignty, Pañc. 163, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् स्वामिन्, i. e. स्व + मिन्, m.<BR> 1. A proprietor.<BR> 2. A master, Pañc. i. d. 328.<BR> 3. A sovereign, Hit. 3, 4, M.M. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b " target="_blank">Page1099-b + 44</a>]<BR> 4. A husband, Hit. 87, 9, M.M.; a lover.<BR> 5. A spiritual preceptor.<BR> 6. A learned Brāhmaṇa.<BR> 7. Viṣṇu, Śiva, Kārttikeya, the god of war, Garuḍa, a fabulous bird.<BR> 8. In comp. it signifies often a sanctuary built by, or in honour of those who are denoted in the former part of the comp.; e. g. अवन्ति-, m. a sanctuary built by Avantivarman, Rājat. 5, 45. अभिमन्यु-, m. A sanctuary built in commemoration of Abhimanyu, Rājat. 6, 299. धर्म-, m. A sanctuary built by Dharma, Rājat. 4, 696. विष्णु-, A sanctuary built in honour of Viṣṇu, Rājat. 5, 99.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अ- + स्वामिन् अ- + स्वामिन्, m. one who is not owner, Man. 8, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्वामिन्
कु- + स्वामिन् कु- + स्वामिन्, m. a wicked master, Pañc. 73, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्वामिन्
गो- + स्वामिन् गो- + स्वामिन्, m. 1. the owner of cattle, Man. 8, 231. 2. a holy man, used after proper names, as a honorary title.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्स्वामिन्
जगत्- + स्वामिन् जगत्- + स्वामिन्, m. the lord of the universe, Prab. 99, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयस्वामिन्
जय- + स्वामिन् जय- + स्वामिन्, m. the lord of victory, epithet of Śiva, Rājat. 5, 448.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणस्वामिन्
रण- + स्वामिन् रण- + स्वामिन्, m. the lord of battles, epithet of Śiva, Rājat. 5, 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवस्वामिन्
शिव- + स्वामिन् शिव- + स्वामिन्, m. a proper name, Rājat. 5, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्य|स्वाम्यं
स्वाम्य स्वाम्य, i. e. स्वामिन् + य, n.<BR> 1. Ownership.<BR> 2. Mastership.<BR> 3. Supremacy, Hit. 84, 7; dominion, Dev. 1, 8.<BR> 4. Marital dominion, Man. 5, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुव|स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायम्भुव स्वायम्भुव, i. e. स्वयंभू + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to Brahman.<BR> 2. Descended from Brahman.<BR> II. m. The son of Brahman, Śāk. d. 168; epithet of the first Manu, Man. 1, 61; 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायुज्
स्वायुज् स्वायुज्, i. e. सु, or स्व, -आ-युज्, adj. Easily yoked, or putting themselves spontaneously to the chariot, Chr. 294, 2 = Rigv. i. 92, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्
स्वाराज् स्वाराज्, i. e. स्वर्-राज्, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्य|स्वाराज्यं|स्वाराज्यः
स्वाराज्य स्वाराज्य, n., i. e.<BR> I. स्व-राज् + य, The state of Brahman, union [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a " target="_blank">Page1100-a + 43</a>] with Brahman, final felicity, Man. 12, 91.<BR> II. स्वाराज् + य, Indra's heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिष|स्वारोचिषः
स्वारोचिष स्वारोचिष, i. e. स्व-रोचिस् + अ, m. The second Manu, Man. 1, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थिक
स्वार्थिक स्वार्थिक, i. e. स्व-अर्थ + इक, adj.<BR> 1. Done with one's own property.<BR> 2. Having one's own object.<BR> 3. Having its literal meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्य|स्वास्थ्यं
स्वास्थ्य स्वास्थ्य, i. e. स्वस्थ + य, n.<BR> 1. Health, Pañc. 183, 22.<BR> 2. Content.<BR> 3. Happiness, Pañc. ii. d. 165.<BR> 4. Self-reliance, firmness, Pañc. ii. d. 170 (with व्रज्, To recover).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा स्वाहा,<BR> I. indecl. An exclamation on offering to the gods.<BR> II. f. A personification of the preceding as the wife of fire, Ragh. 1, 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
1. स्विद् स्विद्, i. 4, Par. To perspire, to sweat, Gīt. 10, 16.<BR> --i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. † To be greasy or unctuous.<BR> 2. † To be disturbed.<BR> 3. † To shed.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. स्विदित,<BR> 1. Sweated, melted.<BR> 2. Perspiring.<BR> II. स्विन्न, Sweating, Lass. 59, 6.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to perspire; स्वेद्य, What must be treated by sudorific means, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 890.<BR> 2. To warm, Hit. ii. d. 131. स्वेदित, Sweated, heated.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रस्विन्न, and प्रस्वेदिन्द्,<BR> 1. Perspiring, covered with perspiration, Rām. 2, 100, 35 (स्विन्न).<BR> 2. Heated; प्रस्वेदित (also<BR> 3.), Hot, causing perspiration.<BR> --Cf. Goth. sveitan; A.S. swaetan; O.H.G. svizzan, sueizjan (Caus.); ιδρώς, σίδηρος; Lat. sudor, sudare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
2. स्विद् स्विद्, i. e. सु-इद्,<BR> 1. A particle used in an interrogation, Perhaps, Kir. 12, 15; 14, 60; after किम्, MBh. 3, 10648; after उत and उताहो (see उत), Or, Pañc. 41, 1; 142, 5.<BR> 2. An exclamation of doubt or surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विष्टकृत्
स्विष्टकृत् स्विष्टकृत्, i. e. सु-इष्ट (vb. यज्), -कृ + त्, The name of a divinity, the fire of the good sacrifice, Man. 3, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरण|स्वीकरणं
स्वीकरण स्वीकरण, i. e. स्व-कृ + अन, n.<BR> 1. Assenting.<BR> 2. Promising.<BR> 3. Marriage, Śāk. 66, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार|स्वीकारः
स्वीकार स्वीकार, i. e. स्व-कृ + अ, m.<BR> 1. Assent.<BR> 2. Promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय स्वीय, i. e. स्व + ईय,<BR> I. adj. Own, Pañc. ii. d. 80.<BR> II. f. या, A faithful. wife.<BR> --Cf. ἑός, σϕέος, σϕός.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वुर्छ्
स्वुर्छ् स्वुर्छ्, see स्फुर्छ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ स्वृ, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To sound.<BR> 2. To praise (ved.).<BR> 3. To be pained.<BR> 4. † To go.<BR> --Caus. To sing, Chr. 294, 5 = Rigv. i. 88, 5 (सस्वर्, ved. aor.).<BR> --With सम् सम्, Ātm. To pain, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 28.<BR> --Cf. Lat. susurro, absurdus, surdus (properly, Suffering from humming in the ears), sorex; σύριγξ, ὕραξ, ὕρον; probably Goth. svaran; A.S. swaran, swerian, and-swar, answer; probably Lat. sorbere; ῥοϕέω (from the sound of drinking; cf. Zend. क़र् = Sskr. स्वर्, properly, To smack; cf. अव and वि, with स्वन्, also विष्वणन, विष्वाण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वॄ
† स्वॄ स्वॄ, स्वॄ स्बॄ, सॄ सॄ, ii. 9, स्वृणा, स्बृणा, सृणा, णी, Par. To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेक्
स्वेक् स्वेक्, see स्रेक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छातस्
स्वेच्छातस् स्वेच्छातस्, i. e. स्व-इच्छा + तस्, adv. Conformably to one's wish, Hit. 69, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेद|स्वेदः
स्वेद स्वेद, i. e. स्विद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Perspiration, sweat, Vikr. 27, 2.<BR> 2. Hot moisture, Vedāntas. in Chr. 209, 5.<BR> 3. Warmth.<BR> 4. Hot work, labour, Chr. 292, 8 = Rigv. i. 86, 8.<BR> 5. Vapour.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. sueiz; A.S. swát.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
स- + स्वेद स- + स्वेद,<BR> I. adj. perspiring, exuding, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a " target="_blank">Page1101-a + 41</a>] Rājat. 5, 343.<BR> II. f. दा, a virgin deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदन|स्वेदनं
स्वेदन स्वेदन, i. e. स्विद् + अन,<BR> I. n.<BR> 1. Perspiration.<BR> 2. Causing to perspire, warming, Hit. ii. d. 130.<BR> 3. A sudorific.<BR> II. f. नी, An iron plate used for cooking and frying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनिक
स्वेदनिक स्वेदनिक, i. e. स्वेदनी + क, f. An iron plate for cooking and frying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर स्वैर (from स्व and ईर्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Self-willed, Pañc. 31, 3; of one's own accord, Rām. 3, 52, 27 (without the permission of her husband); unrestrained.<BR> 2. Slow, or refractory, Nal. 21, 13; Sāv. 5, 98.<BR> 3. Dependent on one's will, unimportant, MBh. 1, 1726; 1921; 3, 13573.<BR> II. रम्, adv.<BR> 1. With one's own will, assent, Rām. 3, 52, 27; Utt. Rāmac. 29, 6; Kathās. 22, 99.<BR> 2. Of one's own accord, Rājat. 5, 411.<BR> III. n. Wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैरता स्वैर + ता, and स्वैरिता स्वैरिता, i. e. स्वैरिन् + ता, f. Wilfulness, Lass. 2. ed. 19, 18 (र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन् स्वैरिन्, i. e. स्वैर + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. इणी, Self-willed, wanton, Lass. 42, 13.<BR> II. f. इणी, An unchaste woman, Pañc. 129, 1; Rājat. 5, 316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
1. ह ह,<BR> 1. = ved. घ, Lass. 98, 2 = Rigv. vi. 64, 5.<BR> 2. A particle laying a stress on the preceding word (as γέ), or without a distinct signification, Man. 9, 28; Chr. 12, 2; 25, 62; न ह, Not indeed, Man. 9, 270; used very often after the red. pf. (Rām. 3, 52, 53), and imperf. Pāṇ. iii. 2, 116.<BR> 3. A vocative particle, Ho! holloa!<BR> 4. A particle of reproach.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ha, ho, hi, in hic, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b " target="_blank">Page1101-b + 42</a>] hæc, hoc; Goth. prefix, ga-; A.S. ge-; see घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
2. ऽह -ह (vb. हन्), at the end of comp. adj. Killing, Pāṇ. iii. 2, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंस्
हंस् हंस्, a denomin. derived from the next, Par. To behave like a swan, Lass. 67, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंस|हंसः
हंस हंस,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A goose, a gander, a swan, a phœnicopteros, Vikr. d. 95; Man. 3, 10; it is the vehicle of Brahman.<BR> 2. A sort of horse.<BR> 3. The sun.<BR> 4. A devotee.<BR> 5. A liberal prince.<BR> 6. One of the vital breaths.<BR> 7. Brahman, Viṣṇu, Śiva, Kāma, the god of love.<BR> 8. (In composition), Best, excellent.<BR> II. f. सी.<BR> 1. A goose.<BR> 2. A proper name, Rājat. 5, 359.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. gans; A.S. gós, gandra; Lat. anser; χήν.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परहंस
पर- + हंस पर- + हंस, and परम-, m. an ascetic who has subdued all his senses, MBh. 13, 6478 (परम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहंस|राजहंसः
राजहंस राजहंस, i. e. राजन्-, m. 1. an excellent king. 2. m., f. सी, a white goose with red legs and bill, Vikr. d. 19; a flamingo, Hit. 79, 7. 3. a drake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसक|हंसकः
हंसक हंस + क, m.<BR> 1. The flamingo.<BR> 2. An ornament for the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकाकीय
हंसकाकीय हंसकाकीय, i. e. हंस-काक + ईय, adj. Relating to the goose and the crow (a fable), MBh. 1, 543.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपदिका
हंसपदिका हंसपदिका, i. e. हंस-पद + ई + क, f. A proper name, Śāk. 59, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका हंसिका, i. e. हंसी + क, f. A goose, Nalod. 2, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो हंहो,<BR> 1. An interjection of calling, Caurap. 22; Ho! holloa! Pañc. 192, 12; Vikr. 61, 12.<BR> 2. A particle of contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जा|हंजा
हञ्जा हञ्जा, and हञ्जे हञ्जे, A vocative particle used in addressing a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a " target="_blank">Page1102-a + 37</a>] female attendant (in theatrical language), Sāh. D. 172, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्
† हट् हट्, i. 1, Par. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्ट|हट्टः
हट्ट हट्ट,<BR> I. m. A market, a fair, Pañc. 262, 15.<BR> II. f टी, A petty market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ्
† हठ् हठ्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To jump.<BR> 2. To treat with violence.<BR> 3. To bind to a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ हठ, perhaps a dialect. form of हस्त,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Violence, Rām. 5, 35, 11; abl. ठात्, By force, Pañc. 138, 1.<BR> 2. Rapine.<BR> II. m., f. ठी, A plant, Pistia stratiotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिक|हडिकः
हडिक हडिक, and हड्डक हड्डक, m. A sweeper, a servant of the lowest caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्ड|हड्डं
हड्ड हड्ड, n. A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डक|हड्डकः
हड्डक हड्डक, see हडिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डज|हड्डजं
हड्डज हड्ड-ज, n. Marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डे|हंडे
हण्डे हण्डे, used like हञ्जा, q. cf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतक|हतकः
हतक हत + क (vb. हन्),<BR> I. adj. Miserable (?), Mālat. 87, 3.<BR> II. m. A coward, Utt. Rāmac. 30, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश|हताशः
हताश हताश, i. e. हत-आश, (see हन् and आशा), m.<BR> 1. Hopeless, desponding.<BR> 2. Weak.<BR> 3. Barren.<BR> 4. Cruel, merciless.<BR> 5. Vile, wicked, Vikr. 8, 9 (Prākṛ.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हति|हतिः
हति हति, i. e. हन् + ति, f.<BR> 1. Striking; in कल-, f. Ploughing.<BR> 2. Destroying, removing, Bhartṛ. 3, 100.<BR> --Cf. A.S. dynt; see हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्नु|हत्नुः
हत्नु हत्नु, i. e. हन् + त्नु, m.<BR> 1. A weapon.<BR> 2. Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्य
हत्य हत्य, i. e. हन् + त्य, n., and f. या, Killing, Chr. 297, 14 = Rigv. i. 112, 14 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b " target="_blank">Page1102-b + 44</a>] (n.); Pañc. i. d. 306 (I read तस्य हत्या तदुत्थाना, The murder of that man has its origin in this person, i. e. his death is caused by that person, by trusting to whom he has found it; but cf. also Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2850); 221, 14 (f.).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहत्या
गो- + हत्या गो- + हत्या, f. killing a cow, Man. 11, 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महत्या
ब्रह्महत्या ब्रह्महत्या, i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, f. killing a Brāhmaṇa, Hit. i. d. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहत्या
भ्रूण- + हत्या भ्रूण- + हत्या, f. murder of an unborn child, Rām. 2, 47, 41, Seramp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहत्या
वीर- + हत्या वीर- + हत्या, f. the slaughter of a man (Jones, ‘a son’), Man. 11, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहत्या
स्त्री- + हत्या स्त्री- + हत्या, f. the crime of having killed a woman, Pañc. 216, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हथ|हथः
हथ हथ, i. e. हन् + थ, m. A man in despondency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद्
हद् हद्, i. 1, Ātm. To evacuate, as fæces.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. हन्न, Passed, as ordure.<BR> --Cf. χέζω, χόδος; probably O.H.G. scîzan; A.S. scitan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
हन् हन्, probably for original धन्, ii. 2, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 1, 45, 49), ved., i. 1, जिघ्न; some verbal forms are derived also, or only, from बध् बध्, or वध् वध्,<BR> 1. To strike, MBh. 1, 6706; to peck, Hit. 81, 21.<BR> 2. To wound, to hurt, Man. 10, 84; to injure, Pañc. iii. d. 50 (बध्यन्ते, pass.), to overturn (right), Man. 8, 15.<BR> 3. To kill, Rām. 2, 78, 22; pass. बध्, with the termination of the Par., MBh. 2, 8765.<BR> 4. To destroy, Man. 8, 14; मा कतो ऽबधित्, 8, 15 (blot out the').<BR> 5. To remove (darkness), Hit. pr. d. 17, M.M.; (impurity), Man. 2, 102.<BR> 6. To impede, Rājat. 5, 253.<BR> 7. † To go.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. हत.<BR> 1. Killed, Chr. 62, 51.<BR> 2. Utterly ruined, Śāk. d. 22.<BR> 3. Ended.<BR> 4. Lost, Chr. 32, 28.<BR> 5. Deprived of, without, especially when former part of comp. adj.; e. g. हत-साध्वस, adj. Fearless, cf. also Kir. 5, 49; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1103-a " target="_blank">Page1103-a + 45</a>] Sāv. 5, 17.<BR> 6. Disappointed.<BR> 7. Worthless, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 809.<BR> 8. (In arithmetic), Multiplied. n.<BR> 1. Hurting, killing.<BR> 2. Multiplication.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. बध्य.<BR> 1. Deserving death, Vikr. d. 144.<BR> 2. Condemned to death.<BR> --Comp.<BR> आत्मवध्या, i. e. आत्मन्-, f. suicide, MBh. 1, 6227.<BR> --Frequent. जंघन्, To strike repeatedly, Chr. 293, 2 = Rigv. i. 88, 2.<BR> --Desider. जिघांस, To wish or to be inclined to kill, Man. 5, 3; Johns. Sel. 54, 135 (Ātm.).<BR> --Caus. घातय, properly a denomin. derived from घात, To cause to be killed, Bhag. 2, 21 (कं घातयति हन्ति कम्, Whom will he kill by means of others or by his own hand?). घातव्य (anomal. for घातयितव्य, or हन्तव्य?), Deserving death, Mālav. 9, 9. घात्य, To be killed, Pañc. 194, 6 (सुख-, Easy to be killed).<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To remove (sin), Man. 6, 96.<BR> 2. To take away, Bhartṛ. 2, 15 (probably is to be read अपहर्तुम्).<BR> --With अभि अभि,<BR> 1. To assail, Daśak. in Chr. 194, 11.<BR> 2. To strike, Man. 11, 206; anomal. अभ्य् अघ्नम्, Arj. 7, 6.<BR> 3. To cast on, Utt. Rāmac. 117, 3.<BR> 4. To kill, MBh. 3, 12108. अभिहत,<BR> 1. Struck, Chr. 40, 9.<BR> 2. Subdued.<BR> 3. (In medicine), Obstructed.<BR> 4. (In arithmetic), Multiplied.<BR> --With अव अव, To kick (अन्योन्यं जानुभिस्, each other with the knees, in wrestling), MBh. 2, 915.<BR> --With आ आ, Ātm., when without object, or the object being a member,<BR> 1. To strike, Dev. 9, 27; Rām. 3, 50, 20.<BR> 2. To beat (a kettle-drum), Megh. 67.<BR> 3. Ātm. To kill one's self, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1103-b " target="_blank">Page1103-b + 43</a>] Daśak. in Chr. 199, 12. आहत,<BR> 1. Struck, Pañc. v. d. 4; injured, killed.<BR> 2. Understood, known.<BR> 3. Uttered falsely.<BR> 4. Multiplied. m. A drum. n.<BR> 1. Old cloth.<BR> 2. Assertion of an impossibility.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. without being beaten (as drums), Chr. 37, 25.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ,<BR> 1. To strike, MBh. 1, 8223.<BR> 2. To wound, Chr. 43, 25. अभ्याहत,<BR> 1. Killed.<BR> 2. Obstructed, impeded.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ, To drive back, Chr. 31, 11 (Ātm.).<BR> --With व्या वि-आ,<BR> 1. To obstruct, to impede, Rām. 2, 10, 32.<BR> 2. To delay, Ragh. 9, 54. अ-व्याहत, Unimpeded, Pañc. 16, 1.<BR> --Caus. To obstruct, MBh. 1, 8109.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To join, Arj. 3, 40.<BR> 2. To strike, Pañc. i. d. 339; MBh. 1, 6291.<BR> 3. To beat (a kettle-drum), MBh. 1, 7941.<BR> 4. To kill, Rām. 1, 32, 17. समाहत,<BR> 1. Struck, Hit. iii. d. 147 (नीति-मन्त्र-पवनैः, Struck by the counsels of good policy as by storms).<BR> 2. Wounded.<BR> --With उद् उद्, ved. जिघ्न, To throw up, Chr. 290, 11 = Rigv. i. 64, 11. उद्धत,<BR> 1. Thrown up (as dust), Śāk. d. 8; (as the sea), Johns. Sel. 28, 27.<BR> 2. Raised, Ṛt. 1, 10; moved, Pañc. 21, 2.<BR> 3. Intense, Pañc. 93, 2.<BR> 4. Puffed up, haughty, Utt. Rāmac. 151, 2; Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2375.<BR> 5. Ill-behaved, rude.<BR> 6. Rām. 2, 53, 32, read उद्धृतौ, with Gorr. 39.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. not proud, Rām. 2, 6, 22.<BR> मद-, adj. drunk, mad, Pañc. 254, 8.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्, समुद्धत,<BR> 1. Risen, Utt. Rāmac. 124, 10.<BR> 2. Proud, Śiś. 2, 117; Kir. 5, 15.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To scratch, MBh. 2, 2123 (you scratch as a cat its nourisher).<BR> 2. To touch, Man. 9, 208.<BR> 3. To strike, Mālat. 160, 18.<BR> 4. To kill, Kathās. 26, 140; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1104-a " target="_blank">Page1104-a + 43</a>] Utt. Rāmac. 176, 8. उपहत,<BR> 1. Injured, spoiled, Vikr. d. 127.<BR> 2. Assailed, Śṛṅgārat. 12.<BR> 3. Pained, afflicted, Ṛt. 1, 15; दारिद्र-, adj. Afflicted by poverty, Pañc. 119, 5; अपाय-उपहत-अन्तर्-आत्मन्, adj. One whose heart is discouraged by misfortune, Hit. iii. d. 115.<BR> 4. Struck by lightning, etc., by the rays of the sun, Kir. 5, 48.<BR> 5. Destroyed.<BR> 6. Infected, polluted, tarnished, Śāk. d. 191.<BR> 7. Impure.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अन्-, adj. approved, Bhartṛ. 2, 60.<BR> --With नि नि,<BR> 1. To strike, MBh. 3, 11953.<BR> 2. To kill, Hit. iii. d. 116.<BR> 3. To destroy, Hit. i. d. 42, M.M.<BR> 4. To disregard, Hit. pr. d. 31, M.M. निहत,<BR> 1. Struck down, Lass. 2. ed. 78, 70.<BR> 2. Killed, Kir. 14, 14.<BR> 3. Infixed, attached, Rām. 2, 82, 16.<BR> --With परिणि परि-नि, To strike, MBh. 3, 12261 (has नि).<BR> --With विनि वि-नि,<BR> 1. To pat, Rām. 1, 9, 16.<BR> 2. To kill, Pañc. i. d. 347.<BR> 3. To destroy, Hit. iv. d. 37; to remove (darkness), MBh. 1, 85.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To drag out (of one's house), Rājat. 5, 432.<BR> 2. To remove, Suśr. 1, 100, 16.<BR> --With परा परा, To push on, MBh. 3, 1288 (the clouds were pushed on by the violence of the wind). पराहत,<BR> 1. Struck.<BR> 2. Assailed. n. Strike, Mālat. 140, 15.<BR> --With परि परि, परिहत, Lost, Gīt. 5, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. not avoided, Śāk. 69, 2 (v. r. probably is to be read अपरिकृत).<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रहत,<BR> 1. Struck, wounded.<BR> 2. Beaten (as a drum), Megh. 65.<BR> 3. Killed.<BR> 4. Repelled.<BR> 5. Overcome.<BR> 6. Spread, expanded.<BR> 7. Contiguous.<BR> 8. Learned, accomplished.<BR> --Absol. प्रबध्य, Being killed, Pañc. iii. d. 269.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, अ-विप्रहत, adj. Not distant, Rām. 1, 26, 12.<BR> --With [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1104-b " target="_blank">Page1104-b + 45</a>] प्रति प्रति,<BR> 1. To return a blow, MBh. 3, 1091.<BR> 2. To drive back, Śāk. d. 50; to remove, Vikr. d. 20.<BR> 3. To disown, Śāk. d. 191.<BR> 4. To keep off, Śāk. d. 13; to prevent, Mālat. 174, 6.<BR> 5. To oppose, to resist, Arj. 10, 20. प्रतिहत,<BR> 1. Obstructed, Mālat. 156, 9.<BR> 2. Repulsed, Arj. 8, 11; averted, Śāk. 91, 15.<BR> 3. Hated.<BR> 4. Struck.<BR> 5. Disappointed.<BR> 6. Sent, dispatched.<BR> 7. Overthrown, fallen.<BR> 8. Tied, bound.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. 1. uninjured, Hit. i. d. 126, M.M. 2. unfailing, Mālat. 86, 3.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To strike, Arj. 10, 23.<BR> 2. To afflict, MBh. 2, 151; Rām. 3, 79, 28.<BR> 3. To kill, Pañc. 86, 23; MBh. 3, 11117.<BR> 4. To destroy, Man. 7, 27.<BR> 5. To interrupt, Mālav. d. 38.<BR> 6. To separate, Mālat. 163, 3.<BR> 7. To obstruct, to impede, Pañc. iii. d. 232; Bhartṛ. 2, 73.<BR> 8. To deny, to refuse, Ragh. 11, 2. विहत, Opposed, resisted.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. irresistible, Megh. 10.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be destroyed, Hit. iii. d. 109.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To put together, to close (one's hands), Man. 2, 71. संहत,<BR> 1. Joined, combined, Hit. i. d. 36, M.M.<BR> 2. Collected, Indr. 1, 6; keeping together, Hit. iii. d. 125.<BR> 3. Closely allied, Man. 7, 66.<BR> 4. Closed, shut.<BR> 5. Compact, Rām. 3, 52, 25.<BR> 6. Strong-knit, Draup. 7, 9 (the forehead by frowning); well-limbed.<BR> 7. Combining, acting together.<BR> 8. Struck, wounded, killed.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. disagreeing, Pañc. v. d. 86.<BR> सु-, adj. well-compacted, well-knit.<BR> --With अभिसम् अभि-सम्, To unite, MBh. 2, 800.<BR> --Cf. θάνατος, θείνω, θνήσκω; Goth. dauths, dauthus; A.S. deád, deadh; dydan, to kill; Lat. fen-d in offendere, infestus, probably fessus, fatigare (cf. rutilus, s. v. रुधिर, latere, s. v. रह्, etc.); with बध्, cf. πάθος, πάσχω; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a " target="_blank">Page1105-a + 42</a>] Lat. patior; perhaps A.S. beado, battle; bytl, a hammer; also Goth. du-ginnan; A.S. a-ginnan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अ- + हन् अ- + हन्, adj. 1. not beaten (as a drum). 2. unwashed, MBh. 2, 99. 3. new, Rām. 2, 3, 10. n. new cloth (properly, ‘not yet washed’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहत|मनोहतः
मनोहत मनोहत, i. e. मनस्-, adj. disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
ऽहन् -हन्, latter part of comp. words, f. घ्नी, Killing, having killed, etc.; e. g. चक्षुर्हन्, i. e. चक्षुस्-, adj. Killing by a glance of his eye, MBh. 13, 2156. पितृ-, m. A parricide, Rājat. 5, 447. ब्रह्महन्. i. e. ब्रह्मन्-, m. The slayer of a Brāhmaṇa, Man. 11, 101; 128 (anomal. gen. -हणस् instead of घ्नस्). यज्ञ-, adj. Sacrifice-destroying, a name of Śiva, Johns. Sel. 96, 78. वीरहन् and वृत्रहन्, see s. vv. हय-ग्रीव- (see ग्रीवा), m. Viṣnu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन|हनः
हन हन् + अ,<BR> I. m. A killer.<BR> II. Latter part of comp. words, Killing; e. g. क्षत्रिय-हण, m. A destroyer of the Kṣatriyas, MBh. 5, 7116. वीर-हण, adj., f. णी, Hero-killing, MBh. 9, 3238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनन|हननं|हननः
हनन हन् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Striking, Mālat. 85, 7.<BR> 2. Injuring.<BR> 3. Killing.<BR> 4. Multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनु|हनुः
हनु<BR> I. हनु (vb. 1. हा? cf. A.S. goma, the jaws), m., f. also नू नू (and n.), The jaw.<BR> II. हन् + उ, f.<BR> 1. A weapon.<BR> 2. Sickness.<BR> 3. Death.<BR> 4. A sort of vegetable perfume.<BR> --Cf. γένυς; Lat. gena; Goth. kinnus; A.S. cinn, cyn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमन्त्|हनुमत्
हनुमन्त् and हनूमन्त् हनू̆ + मन्त्,<BR> I. adj. Having large jaws.<BR> II. m. The monkey chief, Hanumant, Utt. Rāmac. 20, 8 (ऊ); Mahāv. 114, 17 (ŭ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूष|हनूषः
हनूष हनूष (derived from हनु), m. A Rākṣasa or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त|हंत
हन्त हन्त,<BR> I. An inceptive particle, Lass. 2. ed. 69, 44.<BR> II. An interjection.<BR> 1. Of grief, pity, Alas! [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b " target="_blank">Page1105-b + 40</a>] Mālat. 24, 6; Utt. Rāmac. 13, 17.<BR> 2. Of pleasure, Vikr. 10, 9; Utt. Rāmac. 37, 5; joy, ib. 39, 15.<BR> 3. Of hurry, Śṛṅgārat. 14.<BR> 4. Of surprise, Utt. Rāmac. 142, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तकार|हंतकार|हन्तकारः
हन्तकार हन्त-कार, m. Rice to be given to a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तु|हंतुः|हन्तुः
हन्तु हन् + तु, m.<BR> 1. Death.<BR> 2. A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तृ|हंतृ
हन्तृ हन् + तृ, m.<BR> 1. A murderer, Man. 5, 34.<BR> 2. A theif, a robber.<BR> 3. One who injures, Hit. i. d. 76, M.M. (कार्य-, another's interest).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्महन्तृ
धर्म- + हन्तृ धर्म- + हन्तृ, f. त्री, one who overturns the law, MBh. 1, 2440.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नहन्तृ
विघ्न- + हन्तृ विघ्न- + हन्तृ, m. a destroyer of obstacles, Cāṇ. 97 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 413.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
हम् हम्, An interjection of wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भा|हंभा
हम्भा हम्भा (an imitative sound), f. The lowing of kine, Rām. 1, 54, 18; 55, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्म्
† हम्म् हम्म्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय्
† हय् हय्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To worship.<BR> 3. To sound.<BR> 4. To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय हय, i. e. हि + अ,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. A horse, Vikr. d. 4.<BR> 2. A man of a particular class.<BR> 3. Indra.<BR> II. f. यी, A mare.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहय|हरिहयः
हरि- + हय हरि- + हय, m. 1. Indra, Johns. Sel. 19, 88.<BR> 2. the sun.<BR> 3. Skanda, the god of war.<BR> 4. Ganeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयंकष|हयङ्कष|हयंकषः|हयङ्कषः
हयंकष हयंकष, i. e. हय + म्-कष् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A charioteer.<BR> 2. Indra's charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयन|हयनं|हयनः
हयन हयन, i. e. हि + अन,<BR> I. m. A year.<BR> II. n. A covered carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर हर, i. e. हृ + अ,<BR> I. adj. Taking, Pañc. i. d. 278; seizing, carrying, Kir. 5, 50; depriving of (विभ्रम-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a " target="_blank">Page1106-a + 45</a>] surpassing the beauty), Bhartṛ. 1, 5.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Śiva, Vikr. d. 48.<BR> 2. Agni.<BR> 3. An ass (cf. खर).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहर
अंश- + हर अंश- + हर, m. a co-heir, Yājñ. 2, 132; 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलहर|मूलहरः
मूल- + हर मूल- + हर, adj. uprooting (viz. happiness), Man. 8, 353.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थहर
रिक्थ- + हर रिक्थ- + हर, m. an heir, ib. 9, 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वपापहर
सर्व-पाप- + हर सर्व-पाप- + हर, adj. removing, or the remover of, all sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरहर|स्मरहरः
स्मर- + हर स्मर- + हर, m. Śiva, Kāvya Prak. 103, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरक|हरकः
हरक हरक, i. e. हृ + अक, m.<BR> 1. A taker.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> 3. A person of reflection.<BR> 4. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरण|हरणं
हरण हरण, i. e. हृ + अन,<BR> I. m. The hand.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Taking, seizing, Pañc. iv. d. 28; carrying away, Pañc. ii. d. 111; 112; removing, Hit. ii. d. 155; stealing, Man. 8, 323.<BR> 2. Withholding, Hit. iii. d. 90.<BR> 3. Annulling. disregarding, Rājat. 5, 180.<BR> 4. The arm.<BR> 5. Accepting.<BR> 6. A special gift, as a nuptial present.<BR> 7. Semen virile.<BR> 8. Gold.<BR> 9. Boiling water.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालहरण
काल- + हरण काल- + हरण, n. delaying, Utt. Rāmac. 125, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहरण
गो- + हरण गो- + हरण, n. stealing cattle, Pañc. i. d. 281.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहरण
स्त्री- + हरण स्त्री- + हरण, n. carrying off a woman, ravishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि हरि (curtailed हरित्),<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Green.<BR> 2. Tawny.<BR> 3. Yellow, Indr. 1, 7; Arj. 4, 12.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Green, tawny, yellow, the colour.<BR> 2. Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa, Hit. pr. d. 28, M.M.; Pañc. pr. d. 1.<BR> 3. Indra, Śāk. d. 156.<BR> 4. Śiva.<BR> 5. Yama.<BR> 6. The sun, Mālat. 149, 1.<BR> 7. The moon.<BR> 8. A ray of light.<BR> 9. Fire.<BR> 10. Wind.<BR> 11. A horse (of Indra; cf. the ved. use of हरित्, and Śāk. 6, 5); Arj. 4, 32.<BR> 12. A lion, Vikr. d. 16.<BR> 13. A parrot.<BR> 14. The Indian cuckoo.<BR> 15. A peacock.<BR> 16. A goose.<BR> 17. An ape, Utt. Rāmac. 84, 9.<BR> 18. A frog.<BR> 19. A snake.<BR> 20. One of the वर्षस्, or divisions, into which the continent is divided.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. A.S. growan; O.H.G. grôen, grôni; A.S. groen, grene; also geal, gealla; Lat. gilvus; χολή, and probably χλόα; cf. हरित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरहरि|नरहरिः
नर- + हरि नर- + हरि, and नृ-, m. Viṣṇu, in his fourth avatāra, as a lionheaded man, Bhāg. P. 5, 18, 7; 7, 8, 27. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b " target="_blank">Page1106-b + 43</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिक|हरिकः
हरिक हरि + क, m. A horse of a yellowish-blue tint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण (akin to हरित्, cf. हरि),<BR> I. adj., f. णी, Yellowish-white, MBh. 13, 5893; Rājat. 5, 482.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Yellowish-white (the colour).<BR> 2. White.<BR> 3. A deer, an antelope, Pañc. 140, 23.<BR> 4. A goose.<BR> 5. Viṣṇu, Śiva.<BR> 6. A minor division of the world.<BR> III. f. णी.<BR> 1. A doe, Megh. 80; 102.<BR> 2. Yellow jasmine.<BR> 3. A beautiful woman.<BR> 4. A golden image, Rājat. 5, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणक|हरिणकः
हरिणक हरिण + क, m. A deer, Śāk. d. 10; Utt. Rāmac. 67, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाय
हरिणाय हरिणाय, a denomin. derived from हरिण, with य, Ātm. To become a deer, Śṛṅgārat. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित् हरित् (for original हरन्त्, cf. हिरण),<BR> I. adj. Green.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Green, the colour.<BR> 2. A horse of the sun (properly, his rays), Chr. 287, 8 = Rigv. i. 50, 8.<BR> 3. A lion.<BR> 4. The sun, Śāk. 6, 5.<BR> 5. Viṣṇu.<BR> 6. Kidney bean.<BR> III. m. and n. Grass.<BR> IV. f.<BR> 1. A quarter, or point of the compass, Śiś. 9, 28.<BR> 2. Turmeric.<BR> --Cf. χάριτες; Goth. gulth; A.S. gold (see हरि, Yellow, and हिरण); akin is also Goth. glitmunjan, To shine; cf. also χόρτος; Goth. gras; A.S. graes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित हरित,<BR> I. adj., f. ता, or इणी (cf. हरिण),<BR> 1. Green, Megh. 21; Hit. i. d. 178, M.M. (in हरिती-कृत, adj. Made green)<BR> 2. Dark blue, Kir. 5, 38.<BR> 3. Grassy.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Green, the colour.<BR> 2. A lion.<BR> III. f. ता.<BR> 1. Bent grass.<BR> 2. Turmeric.<BR> 3. A brown grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल हरिताल, i. e. हरित + आल,<BR> I. n. Yellow orpiment.<BR> II. f. ली.<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a " target="_blank">Page1107-a + 39</a>] Bent grass.<BR> 2. A line in the sky.<BR> 3. A sort of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालक|हरितालकं|हरितालकः
हरितालक हरिताल + क,<BR> I. m. The green pigeon.<BR> II. f. लिका.<BR> 1. A sort of grass.<BR> 2. The fourth lunar day of the month Bhadra.<BR> III. n. Theatrical decoration of the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदश्व|हरिदश्वः
हरिदश्व हरिदश्व, i. e. हरित्-अश्व, m. The sun, Kir. 2, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा हरिद्रा, f. Turmeric, Sch. ad Vikr. d. 53; MBh. 3, 12880; Rājat. 5, 381.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिन्मणि|हरिन्मणिः
हरिन्मणि हरिन्मणि, i. e. हरित्-मणि, m. An emerald, Kir. 6, 23; 14, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभुज्
हरिभुज् हरि-भुज्, m. A snake (properly, eating frogs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
हरिमन् हरिमन्, m.<BR> I. i. e. हरि + इमन्, Paleness, Chr. 289, 11 = Rigv. i. 50, 11.<BR> II. i. e. हृ + इमन्, Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिय|हरियः
हरिय हरिय (derived from हरि), m. A horse of yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिले
हरिले हरिले, A term of calling a female slave (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवन्त्|हरिवत्
हरिवन्त् हरि + वन्त्, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्र|हरिश्चंद्रः|हरिश्चन्द्रः
हरिश्चन्द्र हरि-श्चन्द् + र (see चन्द्), m. The name of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहेतिहूति
हरिहेतिहूति हरि-हेति-हूति (हरि-हेति, The weapon of Viṣṇu, i. e. चक्र, the discus, and हूति = वाक), m. = चक्र-वाक, A kind of duck, Śiś. 9, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतक
हरीतक हरीतक (derived from हरित्), m., f. की, Yellow or chebulic myrobalan, Terminalia Chebula, Lass. 2. ed. 51, 33 (क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणु|हरेणुः
हरेणु हरेणु,<BR> I. m. Peas, pulse.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. A sort of drug and perfume.<BR> 2. A reputable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तृ|हर्त्तृ
हर्तृ हर्तृ, i. e. हृ + तृ, m., f. त्री, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b " target="_blank">Page1107-b + 41</a>] and n.<BR> 1. One who takes, seizes, a robber, Man. 8, 342.<BR> 2. One who brings, Mālat. 150, 10.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहर्तृ
भय- + हर्तृ भय- + हर्तृ, m. a remover of fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यहर्तृ
शल्य- + हर्तृ शल्य- + हर्तृ, m. a weeder, Rām. 5, 28, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मन्|हर्म्मन्
हर्मन् हर्मन्, n. Yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मित|हर्म्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्मित हर्मित, adj.<BR> 1. Thrown.<BR> 2. Burned (cf. घर्म).<BR> 3. Yawned (cf. the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्य|हर्म्म्यं|हर्म्यं
हर्म्य हर्म्य, n. A palace, Vikr. d. 56; a mansion, a house, Pañc. ii. d. 63.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिहर्म्य
मणि- + हर्म्य मणि- + हर्म्य, n. a pavilion of gems, Vikr. 38, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्|हर्य्य्
हर्य् हर्य्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To take, ved., cf. हृ.<BR> 2. † To go.<BR> 3. † To desire.<BR> 4. † To be weary.<BR> --Cf. χαίρω, γέλως, γελάω; Goth. gailjan, gôljan; A.S. gal, gagol; see हृ, and cf. हृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यत|हर्यतः|हर्य्यत|हर्य्यतः
हर्यत हर्यत, m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यश्व|हर्यश्वः|हर्य्यश्व|हर्य्यश्वः
हर्यश्व हर्यश्व, i. e. हरि-अश्व, m. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष हर्ष, i. e. हृष् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. षा, Delighted, happy, Mālav. 60, 5.<BR> II. m. Joy, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 12; exultation, Hit. i. d. 32, M.M.; happiness, Pañc. iii. d. 188.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तहर्ष
उपात्त- + हर्ष उपात्त- + हर्ष, i. e. उप-आ-दत्त- (vb. दा), adj. joyful, Ṛt. 6, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तहर्ष|दंतहर्ष|दन्तहर्षः
दन्त- + हर्ष दन्त- + हर्ष, m. 1. a morbid affection of the teeth, Suśr. 1, 305, 3. 2. chattering of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्ष|रोमहर्षः
रोमहर्ष रोमहर्ष, i. e. रोमन्-, m. horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्षम्
स-हर्ष + म् स-हर्ष + म्, adv. cheerfully, Vikr. 6, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नहर्ष
सन्न- + हर्ष सन्न- + हर्ष (vb. सद्), adj. destitute of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक हर्षक, i. e. हृष् + अक,<BR> I. adj. Delighting.<BR> II. m. The name of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण हर्षण, i. e. हृष् + अन,<BR> I. adj. Delighting.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A cause of pleasure.<BR> 2. A morbid affection of the eyes.<BR> III. n. Rejoicing.<BR> --Comp.[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a " target="_blank">Page1108-a + 39</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्षण|रोमहर्षणं|रोमहर्षणः
रोमहर्षण रोमहर्षण, i. e. रोमन्-,<BR> I. adj. causing the hair to stand erect, terrible, Rām. 1, 30, 17.<BR> II. n. horripilation, caused by pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमहर्षण|लोमहर्षणं|लोमहर्षणः
लोमहर्षण लोमहर्षण, i. e. लोमन्-,<BR> I. adj. causing horripilation or delight, Chr. 39, 2; Utt. Rāmac. 42, 18.<BR> II. n. horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोमहर्षण
अ-लोमन्- + हर्षण अ-लोमन्- + हर्षण, adj. causing displeasure, Rām. 3, 51, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु हर्षयित्नु, i. e. हृष्, Caus., + त्नु,<BR> I. adj. Delighting.<BR> II. m. A child.<BR> III. (m. ?), Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुल|हर्षुलः
हर्षुल हर्षुल, i. e. हृष् + उल,<BR> I. adj. Delighted, Rājat. 5, 473.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A lover.<BR> 2. A deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
† हल् हल्, i. 1, Par. To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल हल,<BR> I. m. A plough, Gīt. 1, 12.<BR> II. f. ला.<BR> 1. The earth.<BR> 2. Vinous liquor.<BR> 3. Water. See हला, s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृत्
हलभृत् हल-भृ + त्,<BR> I. adj. Having a plough.<BR> II. m. Balarāma, Megh. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहलाशब्द
हलहलाशब्द हलहला-शब्द (हलहला, imitative sound), m.<BR> 1. Shout, Rām. 2, 60, 68, Seramp.; 2, 13, 29 Gorr.<BR> 2. Tumult, noise, Chr. 41, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हला
हला हला, a vocative particle, addressed to a female friend (in theatrical language), Śāk. 9, 7 (Prākṛ.); cf. हल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाह|हलाहः
हलाह हलाह, m. A horse of mixed colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाहल|हलाहलं|हलाहलः
हलाहल हलाहल, m. and n. A sort of poison, Pañc. 105, 6. Cf. हालहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलि|हलिः
हलि हलि, m.(?),<BR> 1. A furrow.<BR> 2. Agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिन्
हलिन् हलिन्, i. e. हल + इन्, m.<BR> 1. A ploughman.<BR> 2. Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीमक|हलीमकः
हलीमक हलीमक, i. e. हरिमन् + क, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b " target="_blank">Page1108-b + 40</a>] with ल् for र्, and इ lengthened, n. A sort of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्य|हल्यं
हल्य हल्य, i. e. हल + य,<BR> I. adj. Ploughed.<BR> II. f. या, A multitude of ploughs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीष|हल्लीषं
हल्लीष हल्लीष, and हल्लीस हल्लीस, n.<BR> 1. A dance performed by women in a circle.<BR> 2. A minor dramatic entertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव हव, m.,<BR> I. हु + अ, m. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR> II. ह्वे (q. cf.), + अ,<BR> 1. Calling, Chr. 288, 10 = Rigv. i. 48, 10; 292, 2 = Rigv. i. 86, 2.<BR> 2. Challenging.<BR> 3. Order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवन|हवनं|हवनः
हवन हवन, i. e. हु + अन,<BR> I. n. Sacrifice.<BR> II. f. नी, A hole in the ground for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवस्
हवस् हवस्, i. e. ह्वे + अस्, n. Praise, Chr. 291, 12 = Rigv. i. 64, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवित्री
हवित्री हवित्री, i. e. हु + त्र, f. A hole in the ground for keeping the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्भुज्
हविर्भुज् हविर्भुज्, i. e. हविस्-भुज्, m.<BR> 1. Fire, Śiś. 1, 2.<BR> 2. The name of the Manes of the Kṣatriyas, Man. 3, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्मन्त्|हविष्मत्
हविष्मन्त् हविष्मन्त्, i. e. हविस् + मन्त्, adj. With oblations, Lass. 98, 6 = Rigv. v. 9, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्य|हविष्यं
हविष्य हविष्य, i. e. हविस् + य, n.<BR> 1. Clarified butter.<BR> 2. The same with rice.<BR> 3. An oblation, Man. 3, 256.<BR> 4. Wild grains, Man. 11, 77; 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यन्तीय
हविष्यन्तीय हविष्यन्तीय, The name of a holy text, Man. 11, 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यभुज्
हविष्यभुज् हविष्य-भुज्, m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविस्
हविस् हविस्, i. e. हु + इस्, n.<BR> 1. Clarified butter, Bhag. 4, 24.<BR> 2. An oblation, sacrifice, Lass. 100, 1 = Rigv. vii. 15, 1; Śāk. d. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यवाह|हव्यवाहः
हव्यवाह हव्य-वाह, हव्यवाहन हव्य-वाहन, हव्याश हव्याश, i. e. हव्य-अश् + अ, and हव्याशन हव्याशन, i. e. हव्य-अशन, m. Fire, Draup. 2, 10 (वाह); Rām. 3, 51, 29 (वाहन); Rājat. 5, 416 (आश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्
हस् हस्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To laugh, Daśak. in Chr. 185, 24; to smile, Lass. 2. ed. 53, 48.<BR> 2. To laugh at (with acc.), Śiś. 1, 71. हसित,<BR> 1. Smiling.<BR> 2. Blown (as a flower). n.<BR> 1. Laughter, jesting, Kir. 13, 47.<BR> 2. Smiling, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 396.<BR> 3. The bow of Kāma, the god of love. कास्य, Laughable, ridiculous, Pañc. i. d. 356. n.<BR> 1. Laughter, mirth.<BR> 2. Amusement, Man. 9, 227.<BR> 3. Jest, Pañc. 209, 16; Rām. 2, 69, 5.<BR> 4. Ridicule, Hit. pr. d. 7, M.M. Frequent. जाहस्, जाहस्य, To smile very much, MBh. 3, 14650.<BR> --Caus. हासय, To cause to laugh, Kumāras. 7, 95.<BR> --With व्यति वि-अति, Par. To laugh at each other.<BR> --With अप अप, To laugh at, Rām. 2, 35, 21.<BR> --Caus. To ridicule, 1, 34, 17.<BR> --With अव अव,<BR> 1. To laugh, Pañc. 191, 3; to smile, Lass. 2. ed. 55, 74.<BR> 2. To laugh at, ridicule, MBh. 3, 11181. अवहास्य, Ridiculous, Rām. 4, 14, 31.<BR> --With उप उप, To mock, Mṛcch. 49, 10.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To laugh, Pañc. 216, 10; Rām. 1, 2, 23.<BR> 2. To mock, Nal. 12, 117. प्रहसित, Laughing, cheerful, Pañc. 36, 2. n. Laughter, mirth.<BR> --Caus. प्रहासित, Caused to laugh, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 24.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To laugh, MBh. 1, 3431.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To laugh, Vikr. 12, 20; Lass. 73, 9; Pañc. 74, 15 (विहस्यमान, perhaps corr. ˚हसमान, but also irreg.).<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b " target="_blank">Page1109-b + 43</a>] To smile, Śāk. 17, 8.<BR> 3. To laugh at, MBh. 1, 4762. विहसित, n. A gentle laugh.<BR> --With संवि सम्-वि, To laugh, Mṛcch. 85, 14.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. histrio; perhaps τεθεία, τωθάζω, frequentative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस हस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Laughter.<BR> 2. Derision, Padmap. 16, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन|हसनं
हसन हस् + अन,<BR> I. n. Laughter.<BR> II. f. नी, A fire-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन्तिका|हसंतिका
हसन्तिका हसन्तिका, i. e. हसन्ती + क, f. A fire-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन्ती|हसंती
हसन्ती हसन्ती (ptcple. pres. f. of हस्), f. A fire-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त|हस्तं|हस्तः
हस्त हस्त,<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. The hand, Vikr. 27, 3.<BR> 2. An elephant's trunk, Megh. 14; Hiḍ. 3, 9.<BR> 3. A multitude, after words signifying ‘hair.’<BR> 4. A cubit, or measure extending from the elbow to the little finger, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3348.<BR> II. m., f. ता, The thirteenth lunar asterism.<BR> III. n. A bellows.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. handu; A.S. hand; Lat. pre-hendere; χανδάνω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्त
अ- + हस्त अ- + हस्त, adj. without hands, Man. 5, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहस्त|अग्रहस्तः
अग्र- + हस्त अग्र- + हस्त, m. 1. the tip of the extended hand, Rām. 2, 23, 4. 2. the tip of an elephant's trunk, Vikr. d. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्त|अपहस्तः
अप- + हस्त अप- + हस्त, n. It taking away. 2. stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतहस्त|कपोतहस्तः
कपोत- + हस्त कपोत- + हस्त, m. a mode of joining the hands, as token of reverence, Śāk. 78, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्त|कृतहस्तः
कृत- + हस्त कृत- + हस्त, adj. 1. skilled in archery, MBh. 4, 1843. 2. dexterous, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशहस्त|केशहस्तः
केश- + हस्त केश- + हस्त, m. a tuft of hair, MBh. 3, 1822.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गहस्त
खड्ग- + हस्त खड्ग- + हस्त, adj. bearing a sword, Lass. 26, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्त|गलहस्तः
गल- + हस्त गल- + हस्त, m. throttling, Kathās. 4, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालहस्त
जाल- + हस्त जाल- + हस्त, adj. with a net or nets in (his or their) hands, Pañc. 104, 14; 246, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डहस्त|दंडहस्त|दण्डहस्तं|दण्डहस्तः
दण्ड- + हस्त दण्ड- + हस्त,<BR> I. adj. bearing a staff, MBh. 6, 4959.<BR> II. m. 1. a staffbearer. 2. a door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्व्यग्रहस्त
धनुस्-व्यग्र- + हस्त धनुस्-व्यग्र- + हस्त, adj., f. ता, holding a bow in one's hand, Vikr. 77, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशहस्त|पाशहस्तः
पाश- + हस्त पाश- + हस्त, adj. bearing a noose in his hand, Rām. 3, 54, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तहस्त
मुक्त- + हस्त मुक्त- + हस्त (vb. मुच्), adj. liberal, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a " target="_blank">Page1110-a + 42</a>] Hit. iii. d. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तहस्त
अ-मुक्त- + हस्त अ-मुक्त- + हस्त, adj., f. ता, economical, Man. 5, 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुहस्त|लघुहस्तः
लघु- + हस्त लघु- + हस्त,<BR> I. adj. ready, or light-handed.<BR> II. m. a good archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्त|विहस्तः
वि- + हस्त वि- + हस्त, adj. confounded, bewildered, Ragh. 5, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलहस्त|शूलहस्तः
शूल- + हस्त शूल- + हस्त, adj. armed with a lance, Sund. 1, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलमुद्गरहस्त
शूल-मुद्गर- + हस्त शूल-मुद्गर- + हस्त, adj. armed with clubs and lances, Sund. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलहस्त|स्थूलहस्तः
स्थूल- + हस्त स्थूल- + हस्त, m. the fore part of an elephant's trunk, Megh. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तहस्त
स्रस्त- + हस्त स्रस्त- + हस्त (vb. स्रंस्), adj. relaxing one's hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्त|स्वहस्तः
स्व- + हस्त स्व- + हस्त, m. own hand, handwriting, letter, Vikr. d. 38 (दयिता-स्नेह-, a love-letter of one's mistress).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवन्त्|हस्तवत्
हस्तवन्त् हस्त + वन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Endowed with hands, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1106.<BR> 2. Dexterous, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तस्थ
हस्तस्थ हस्त-स्थ, adj. Being in one's hand, Hit. ii. d. 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिन्
हस्तिन् हस्तिन्, i. e. हस्त + इन्,<BR> I. m. An elephant, Hit. i. d. 17, M.M.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. A female elephant.<BR> 2. A class of women.<BR> 3. A drug and perfume.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धहस्तिन्|गंधहस्तिन्
गन्ध- + हस्तिन् गन्ध- + हस्तिन्, m. a kind of elephant (in rut?), Rām. 5, 73, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलहस्तिन्
जल- + हस्तिन् जल- + हस्तिन्, m. a large aquatic animal (the crocodile ?), Pañc. 51, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुर|हस्तिनापुरं
हस्तिनापुर हस्तिनापुर, हस्तिनीपुर हस्तिनीपुर (from हस्तिन्, with पुर), n. Ancient Delhi, Hit. 81, 11 (ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिप|हस्तिपः
हस्तिप हस्तिप, and हस्तिपक हस्तिपक, i. e. हस्तिन्-प, and -प + क, m.<BR> 1. An elephant-driver, Hit. ii. d. 83 (पक).<BR> 2. An elephant-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य हस्त्य, i. e. हस्त + य, adj.<BR> 1. Given with the hand.<BR> 2. Done with the hand.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहस्त्य
सु- + हस्त्य सु- + हस्त्य, adj. clever, skilful, Chr. 290, 1 = Rigv. i. 64, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र हस् + र, m. A fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा हहा, m. A Gandharva, MBh. 13, 7639.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
1. हा हा, ii. 3, जिहा, Ātm.<BR> 1. To give way (ved.).<BR> 2. To go, Kir. 13, 23.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To rise, Daśak. in Chr. 183, 13 (Rām. 2, 71, 12, Schl. read उर्जिहान्˚, with Gorr. 2, 73, 10).<BR> 2. To raise, Bhaṭṭ. 3, 47.<BR> 3. To leave, Mālat. 163, 11.<BR> --With उप उप, To descend, Śiś. 1, 37.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To obtain, Nalod. 1, 54.<BR> --Cf. χήμη, χάσις, χαίνω, χαλάω; Lat. in-hiare, hiscere; O.H.G. gîên, ginên, geinôn; A.S. ginan, cinan, geonan, gynian, ganian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
2. हा हा (akin to the last), ii. 3, जहा, Par.<BR> 1. To abandon, to leave, MBh. 3, 12339; to forsake, Man. 6, 42.<BR> 2. To avoid, Pañc. iii. d. 71.<BR> 3. To remove, MBh. 1, 2301.<BR> 4. To resign, Bhag. 2, 50.<BR> 5. To let fall, Hit. ii. d. 120.<BR> 6. To lose, Rām. 2, 63, 50. Pass. हीय,<BR> 1. To be forsaken, Man. 6, 42.<BR> 2. To be lost, Pañc. ii. d. 6.<BR> 3. To be deprived, Man. 3, 17; 5, 161.<BR> 4. To be omitted, MBh. 1, 6424.<BR> 5. To become weary or weak, MBh. 1, 6291.<BR> 6. To be lowered, Hit. pr. 42.<BR> 7. To fail (in a lawsuit), Man. 8, 56; cf. Pañc. 166, 18.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. हीन.<BR> 1. Deprived, Man. 8, 232; Rām. 3, 51, 40.<BR> 2. Free from.<BR> 3. Wasted, decayed, feeble, Pañc. iii. d. 133.<BR> 4. Dencient, defective.<BR> 5. Lower, less, Man. 2, 194.<BR> 6. Blameable, vile, bad, low, Man. 3, 107. m. An objectionable witness.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Absol. हित्वा, Neglecting, without regarding, Hit. iv. d. 17. Desider. जिहास, To wish to leave, Daśak. in Chr. 188, 8.<BR> --Caus. हापय,<BR> 1. To cause to want, to refuse, MBh. 3, 1463.<BR> 2. To omit, Man. 3, 71.<BR> --With अप अप, To leave, Vikr. 33, 13; Nal. 24, 11.<BR> --Absol. अपहाय, Besides, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-a " target="_blank">Page1111-a + 42</a>] Ragh. 6, 19 (whom did Lakṣmī worship besides him?).<BR> --With अव अव, pass. To be left, MBh. 3, 11558.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव, To abandon, MBh. 3, 13661.<BR> --With अपा अप-आ,<BR> 1. To leave, MBh. 1, 4946.<BR> 2. To pass by, MBh. 3, 2963 (= Nal. 24, 13, Bopp., अपहाय, against the metre).<BR> --Absol. अपाहाय, Except (except immortality, speak what you wish for), MBh. 3, 11982 (= Arj. 3, 47, Bopp., अपहाय, against the metre).<BR> --With नि नि, निहीन, Low, vile.<BR> --With परि परि, pass.<BR> 1. To decrease, MBh. 3, 12858; with अङ्गैस्, Śāk. 34, 12 (Prākṛ. Thy limbs become thinner).<BR> 2. To be wanting, Rām. 1, 2, 16 (act so that nothing may be wanting); to be unacquainted with, Mālat. 69, 18.<BR> 3. To be deprived, Man. 9, 254.<BR> 4. To be lost, Hit. ii. d. 68.<BR> 5. To be avoided, Hit. ii. d. 54.<BR> 6. To be omitted, to be snipped, MBh. 2, 2460 (with the termination of the Par.). परिहीन,<BR> 1. Deprived, Bhāṣāp. 14.<BR> 2. Waned, decayed.<BR> --Caus. To abandon, Man. 8, 206.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To leave, MBh. 1, 4620.<BR> 2. Pass. To be lost, to perish, Man. 4, 41; to be relinquished, Kir. 14, 13.<BR> --With विप्र वि-प्र, विप्रहीण,<BR> 1. Abandoned, Chr. 8, 27 (read णा).<BR> 2. Deprived, MBh. 1, 8142.<BR> --With वि वि, To abandon, Lass. 2. ed. 77, 65; to leave, Śāk. d. 67; Vikr. d. 41. विहीन,<BR> 1. Deprived, void of, without, Bhartṛ. 2, 17; Rām. 2, 52, 37; Pañc. iii. d. 24.<BR> 2. Free from, Ragh. 18, 13.<BR> --Comp.<BR> पृच्छा-, adj. one who has not asked, Pañc. i. d. 438.<BR> --Caus. विहापित,<BR> 1. Given.<BR> 2. Extorted. n. Gift.<BR> --With प्रवि प्र-वि, To neglect, to disdain, Pañc. iv. d. 36.<BR> --Cf. χῆρος, χωρίς, χῆτος, χατέω; Goth. gaidv, giban; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b " target="_blank">Page1111-b + 41</a>] A.S. gifan (= हापय, cf. विहापित), gafol, gaefel, gif; Engl. if; Lat. habere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहीनात्
पाद-हीनात् पाद-हीनात्, abl., adv. on a sudden, Suśr. 2, 145, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलहीन
फल- + हीन फल- + हीन, adj. yielding no profit, Pañc. i. d. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
3. हा हा, an interj.<BR> 1. Of pain, weariness, grief, Ah! Mālat. 153, 21; Rām. 3, 50, 22; 55, 35; sorrow, Woe! Vikr. 61, 7.<BR> 2. Of joy.<BR> 3. Of reproach, Rām. 3, 51, 25.<BR> 4. Of wrath, Mālat. 82, 5. Repeated, हाहा हा-हा, interjection of,<BR> 1. Surprise.<BR> 2. Grief, Pañc. 35, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक हाटक,<BR> I. adj. Golden, Rām. 3, 49, 8.<BR> II. n. Gold, Pañc. 184, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकमय|हाटकमयं
हाटकमय हाटक + मय, adj., f. यी, Made of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्र|हात्रं|हात्रः
हात्र हा + त्र (vb.?), n. Wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान हान, i. e. 2. हा + अन, n.<BR> 1. Relinquishing.<BR> 2. Prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानि|हानिः
हानि 2. हा + नि, f.<BR> 1. Abandonment, Bhag. 2, 65.<BR> 2. Privation, absence, Pañc. v. d. 83.<BR> 3. Diminution, neglecting, Utt. Rāmac. 86, 10.<BR> 4. Loss, Hit. i. d. 157, M.M.<BR> 5. Want, Rājat. 5, 179.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोहानि
तेजस्- + हानि तेजस्- + हानि, f. loss of splendour and of power, Pañc. i. d. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यहानि|वीर्य्यहानि
वीर्य- + हानि वीर्य- + हानि, f. 1. loss of vigour or courage. 2. impotence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहानि|स्वत्वहानिः
स्वत्व- + हानि स्वत्व- + हानि, f. forfeiture of proprietary right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानिकर
हानिकर हानिकर, i. e. हानि-कृ + अ, adj. Prejudicial, Pañc. i. d. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्त्र|हांत्रः|हान्त्रः
हान्त्र हान्त्र (हान्द्र हान्द्र), i. e. probably हन् + त्र, n. Dying, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायन|हायनं|हायनः
हायन हायन, i. e. हयन + अ,<BR> I. m. and n. A year, Man. 2, 154.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A flame.<BR> 2. A sort of rice<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकहायन
एक- + हायन एक- + हायन, adj. one year old, Man. 11, 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहायण
त्रि-हायण त्रि-हायण, adj., f. णी, three years old, MBh. 3, 14854.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिहायन|षष्टिहायनः
षष्टि- + हायन षष्टि- + हायन,<BR> I. adj. sixty years old, Hiḍ. 4, 23.<BR> II. m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्
हार् हार्, a denomin. derived from the next, Par. To behave or be like a string of pearls, Lass. 67, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
हार हार, i. e. partly ह्रि + अ,<BR> I. adj. Who or what takes.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Taking.<BR> 2. A porter.<BR> 3. A string of pearls, Pañc. 52, 22; 53, 1.<BR> 4. War, battle.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलहार
जल- + हार जल- + हार, m., f. री, one who carries water, Hariv. 3400.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतहार|प्रेतहारः
प्रेत- + हार प्रेत- + हार, i. e. प्र-इत-, m. one who carries a corpse, a near kinsman, Man. 5, 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वस्वहार
सर्व-स्व- + हार सर्व-स्व- + हार, m. seizure or confiscation of all one's property, Man. 9, 242; 8, 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारक|हारकः
हारक हारक, i. e. हृ + अक,<BR> I. adj. Taking, drawing upon one's self, Man. 8, 308.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A thief, a plunderer, Rājat. 5, 451.<BR> 2. A rogue.<BR> 3. i. e. कार + क, A string of pearls, Pañc. 176, 3.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डहारक|मण्डहारकः
मण्ड- + हारक मण्ड- + हारक, m. a distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूर|हारहूरः
हारहूर हारहूर,<BR> I. m. Vinous liquor.<BR> II. f. रा, A grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि हारि,<BR> I. i. e. हृ + इ, adj. Handsome.<BR> II. f.<BR> 1. A caravan.<BR> 2. Defeat in war or gambling.<BR> III. f. री, A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिकण्ठ|हारिकंठ|हारिकण्ठः
हारिकण्ठ हारिकण्ठ, cf. हारी, s. v. हारि, and कण्ठ,<BR> I. adj. Wearing a necklace.<BR> II. m. The Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण हारिण, i. e. हरिण + अ, adj. Relating to deer. Man. 3, 268 (venison).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिक|हारिणिकः
हारिणिक हारिणिक, i. e. हरिण + इक, m. A hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित हारित, i. e. हरित् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Green, the colour.<BR> 2. The green pigeon, Lass. 2. ed. 52, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्र|हारिद्रः
हारिद्र हारिद्र, i. e. हरिद्रा + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Stained with turmeric.<BR> 2. Yellow.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Yellow, the colour.<BR> 2. The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्रव
हारिद्रव हारिद्रव, m. A tree, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b " target="_blank">Page1112-b + 40</a>] Curcuma zanthorizon, Chr. 289, 12 = Rigv. i. 50, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
हारिन् हारिन्, i. e. हृ + इन्, adj., f. इणी,<BR> 1. Taking, Man. 8, 308.<BR> 2. Robbing, Pañc. i. d. 31.<BR> 3. Agitating (with gen.), Man. 12, 28.<BR> 4. Captivating, Śāk. d. 5; charming, Pañc. i. d. 303; Daśak. in Chr. 196, 19; delighting, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 3288.<BR> 5. Pleasant, Kathās. 22, 103.<BR> 6. Bringing, Śāk. 61, 9.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थहारिन्
रिक्थ- + हारिन् रिक्थ- + हारिन्,<BR> I. adj. taking or inheriting property.<BR> II. m. 1. an heir. 2. a maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहारिन्
रोग- + हारिन् रोग- + हारिन्, m. a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहारिन्
स्त्री- + हारिन् स्त्री- + हारिन्, m. one who carries off a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीत|हारीतः
हारीत हारीत (cf. हारित), m.<BR> 1. The green pigeon, Ragh. 4, 46.<BR> 2. A Muni, author of a law book.<BR> 3. A rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीतक|हारीतकः
हारीतक हारीत + क, m. The green pigeon (ŚKD.), Pañc. 158, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्द|हार्दं|हार्द्द|हार्द्दं
हार्द हार्द, i. e. हृद् + अ, n.<BR> 1. Affection, love, Vikr. d. 148; kindness.<BR> 2. Will, Bhāg. P. 1, 7, 55.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्द|सहार्द्द|सहार्द्दः
स- + हार्द स- + हार्द, adj. affectionate, tender, Śiś. 9, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाल|हालः
हाल हाल,<BR> I. i. e. हल + अ, m.<BR> 1. A plough.<BR> 2. Balarāma, Śālivāhana.<BR> II. f. ला, Spirituous liquor, Pañc. i. d. 62.<BR> III. f. ली, A wife's younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहल|हालहलं
हालहल, हालहाल, हालाहल, हाला̆हा̆ल, n. A sort of poison, Pañc. i. d. 62 (हालाहल, cf. Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1261). Cf. हलाहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिक|हालिकः
हालिक हालिक, i. e. हल + इक, adj. Belonging or relating to a plough, as a cultivator, a peasant, Pañc. 225, 22; cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी हालिनी, f. A sort of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालु|हालुः
हालु हालु, m. A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाव|हावः
हाव हाव, i. e. ह्वे + अ, m.<BR> 1. Calling. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a " target="_blank">Page1113-a + 40</a>]<BR> 2. Coquetry, dalliance, Indr. 2, 32; cf. Bharata, ap. Sch. ad Nalod. 2, 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास|हासः
हास हास, i. e. हस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Laughing, Hit. ii. d. 56.<BR> 2. Joy, Nalod. 1, 31.<BR> 3. Derision, Rām. 1, 3, 19.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हास|अन्तर्हासः
अन्तर्- + हास अन्तर्- + हास, m. an inward or suppressed laugh, Pañc. 187, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहास|महाहासः
महा- + हास महा- + हास, m. a horse-laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पहास|पुष्पहासः
पुष्प- + हास पुष्प- + हास, m. 1. a flowergarden (?), Hariv. 12395.<BR> 2. a name of Viṣṇu. 3. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसहासा
मांस- + हासा मंस- + हास, f. सा, skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहास
स- + हास स- + हास, adj. smiling, Lass. 66, 5; ˚सम्, adv. scornfully, Utt. Rāmac. 136, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासक|हासकः
हासक हासक, i. e. हस्, Caus., + अक,<BR> I. m. A buffoon.<BR> II. f. सिका, Laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिन्
हासिन् हासिन्, i. e. हस् + इन्, and हास + इन्, adj., f. नी, Laughing, smiling, Rājat. 5, 449; Rām. 3, 52, 31 (चारु-, sweetly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्त
हास्त हास्त, i. e. हस्त + अ, adj. Formed by the hands (with मुकुल = अञ्जलि, humble salutation), Nalod. 1, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिक|हास्तिकं|हास्तिकः
हास्तिक हास्तिक, i. e. हस्तिन् + क,<BR> I. m. A rider on an elephant.<BR> II. n. A herd of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिन|हास्तिनं
हास्तिन हास्तिन, i. e. हस्तिन् + अ,<BR> I. adj. As big as an elephant.<BR> II. n. Hastināpura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिनपुर|हास्तिनपुरं
हास्तिनपुर हास्तिन-पुर, n. Ancient Delhi, Chr. 5, 23. Cf. हस्तिनापुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यता
हास्यता हास्य + ता (vb. हस्), f. Condition of being ridiculous, Pañc. ii. d. 29; Rājat. 5, 144; Pañc. v. d. 33 (˚तां या, To grow ridiculous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस् हाहस्, and हाहा हाहा, m. A gandharva (cf. हहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाकार|हाहाकारः
हाहाकार हा-हा-कार, m.<BR> 1. Lamentation.<BR> 2. The uproar of battle, Lass. 2. ed. 78, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
1. हि हि, ii. 5, हिनु, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To send.<BR> 3. To discharge, as an arrow from a bow, to throw, Bhaṭṭ. 14, 36.<BR> --With प्र प्र, हिणु,<BR> 1. To send, Pañc. 161, 19; Daśak. in Chr. 184, 19.<BR> 2. To discharge, to throw, Chr. 40, 12 (anomal. ˚हिण्वम्). प्रहित,<BR> 1. Dispatched, Hit. 92, 20.<BR> 2. Stretched out, extended.<BR> --With अनुप्र अनु-प्र, अनुप्रहित, Dispatched after (something), Utt. Rāmac. 39, 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
2. हि हि,<BR> I. A particle,<BR> 1. Because, Utt. Rāmac. 167, 8; for, Chr. 4, 16; on account of; with preceding तथा, Namely, to wit, Śāk. d. 31; Pañc. 221, 6.<BR> 2. Assuredly (assertion), Matsyop. 22; Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.<BR> 3. Indeed (interrogation), Hiḍ. 3, 17.<BR> 4. But, Chr. 10, 2; Daśak. in Chr. 180, 20.<BR> II. An interjection,<BR> 1. Of grief, Ah! alas!<BR> 2. Of envy and hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्
हिंस् हिंस् (an anomal. desider. of हन्), i. 1, and ii. 7, हिनस्, हिंस्, Par.<BR> 1. To strike, Bhaṭṭ. 17, 13.<BR> 2. To hurt, Man. 7, 73.<BR> 3. To kill, Man. 5, 42.<BR> 4. To destroy, Vikr. d. 16; Pañc. i. d. 342.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. हिंसित, n. Injury, Pañc. v. d. 70.<BR> --Caus., or i. 10, Par. To kill, MBh. 3, 13030.<BR> --With आ आ, To kill, Man. 7, 20, v. r.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To hurt, Man. 7, 73.<BR> 2. To injure, Man. 11, 26.<BR> --With प्रति प्रति, प्रतिहिंसित, n. Requital of an injury, Pañc. v. d. 70.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To injure, Rām. 2, 56, 39, Seramp.<BR> 2. To damage (grain), Man. 8, 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक हिंस् + अक,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Mischievous, injurious, noxious, Pañc. iii. d. 106.<BR> 2. One who has injured, Pañc. i. d. 342.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A beast of prey.<BR> 2. An enemy.<BR> 3. A Brāhmaṇa skilled [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a " target="_blank">Page1114-a + 39</a>] in the Atharva-Veda (cf. हिंसा).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अ- + हिंसक अ- + हिंसक, adj. innoxious, harmless, Man. 5, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसन|हिंसनं
हिंसन हिंस् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Slaying, Man. 10, 78<BR> 2. Injury, ib. 2, 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा हिंस् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Injuring, Man. 8, 255; injury, mischief, Rām. 3, 51, 20.<BR> 2. Spoiling, Man. 11, 63.<BR> 3. Incantation; in हिंसा-कर्मन्, Employment of mystical texts for malevolent purposes.<BR> 4. Killing, murder, Bhāg. P. 2, 6, 8; Pañc. 60, 6.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अ- + हिंसा अ- + हिंसा, f. 1. not hurt, Man. 5, 44. 2. not injuring, 6, 75.<BR> 3. not giving pain, Man. 2, 159. 4. benevolence, Hit. 43, 1, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारु|हिंसारुः
हिंसारु हिंसा + रु, m. A tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु हिंसा + लु, adj. Mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालुक|हिंसालुकः
हिंसालुक हिंसालु + क,<BR> I. adj. Mischievous.<BR> II. m. A mischievous dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीर|हिंसीरः
हिंसीर हिंसीर (vb. हिंस्), m.<BR> 1. A tiger.<BR> 2. A villain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र हिंस् + र,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. One who delights in mischief, Man. 3, 164; mischievous, destroying, Man. 9, 310.<BR> 2. Terrible.<BR> 3. Cruel, Hit. ii. d. 174.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A beast of prey, Ragh. 2, 62.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR> III. f. रा.<BR> 1. A vein.<BR> 2. The name of three plants.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अ- + हिंस्र अ- + हिंस्र, adj. not injuring (any living being), Man. 4, 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्राहिंस्र
हिंस्र-अ- + हिंस्र हिंस्र-अ- + हिंस्र, n. noxious and innocent, Man. 1, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्क्
† हिक्क् हिक्क्, i. 1, Par. To hiccough.<BR> --i. 10, Ātm., v. r. of किष्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्का
हिक्का हिक्का, f. Hiccough, Lass. 17, 4; Rām. 6, 28, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गु|हिंगु
हिङ्गु हिङ्गु, m. Assafœtida<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिञ्जीर|हिंजीर|हिंजीरः|हिञ्जीरः
हिञ्जीर हिञ्जीर, m. A rope for an elephant's feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिट्
हिट् हिट्, see बिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्ब|हिडिंब|हिडिंबः|हिडिम्बः
हिडिम्ब हिडिम्ब,<BR> I. m. The name of a Rākṣasa, Hiḍ. 2, 1 (read हिड्˚).<BR> II. f. बा, His sister, ib. 15 (read हिड्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्ड्|हिंड्
हिण्ड् हिण्ड्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To disregard.<BR> --With आ आ, To ramble, Śāk. 20, 5 (Prākṛ.).<BR> --With परि परि, Daśak. 151, 6 (anomal. पर्यहिण्डत, which Wilson translates, ‘They were deserted’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डक|हिंडक
हिण्डक हिण्ड् + अक, see रात्रिहिण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डन|हिंडन|हिंडनं|हिण्डनं
हिण्डन हिण्ड् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Wandering.<BR> 2. Copulation.<BR> 3. Writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डिक|हिंडिकः|हिण्डिकः
हिण्डिक हिण्डिक, m. An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डी|हिंडी
हिण्डी हिण्डी, f. Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीर|हिंडीर|हिंडीरः|हिण्डीरः
हिण्डीर हिण्डीर,<BR> I. m. Cuttle-fish bone, Sāh. D. 287, 16.<BR> II. n. A pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
हित हित,<BR> I.<BR> --Ptcple. pf. pass. of धा and हि (q. cf.).<BR> II. f. ता, A causeway, a dike, Man. 9, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकर|हितकरः
हितकर हित-कर,<BR> I. adj. Kind, favourable.<BR> II. m. A benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकृत्
हितकृत् हित-कृ +त्, adj. Useful, Pañc. i. d. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रणी
हितप्रणी हितप्रणी, i. e. हित-प्र-नी, m. A spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवन्त्|हितवत्
हितवन्त् हित + वन्त्, adj., f. वती,<BR> 1. Friendly.<BR> 2. Useful, Hit. iii. d. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोल|हिंदोल|हिंदोलः|हिन्दोलः
हिन्दोल हिन्दोल, and हिन्दोलक हिन्दोल + क, m. A swing (cf. दुल्, अन्दोलय), Śṛṅgārat. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलय
† हिन्दोलय हिन्दोलय (a denomin. derived from हिन्दोल), Par. To swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्व्
† हिन्व् हिन्व्, i. 1, Par. To satisfy or please (cf. धिन्व्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम|हिमं|हिमः
हिम हिम (i. e. lost ह्यम् + अ),<BR> I. adj. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a " target="_blank">Page1115-a + 40</a>] Cold, Bhāg. P. 4, 25, 18.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Frost, show, Pañc. 169, 14.<BR> 2. Cold, Pañc. iii. d. 165; coolness, Mālat. 100, 4.<BR> 3. Fresh butter.<BR> 4. Tin.<BR> 5. A pearl.<BR> 6. A lotus.<BR> 7. Sandal-wood.<BR> III. m.<BR> 1. The moon.<BR> 2. The Himālaya mountain.<BR> 3. Sandal.<BR> 4. Camphor.<BR> IV. f. मा.<BR> 1. Winter (a year), Chr. 291, 14 = Rigv. i. 64, 14.<BR> 2. Small cardamoms.<BR> 3. A fragrant grass, Cyperus.<BR> 4. A perfume.<BR> --Cf. Lat. hiems, hibernus (for himernus); χιών.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमकर|हिमकरः
हिमकर हिम-कर,<BR> I. adj. Frigorific, cold.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. The moon, Lass. 92, 7.<BR> 2. Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमज|हिमजः
हिमज हिम-ज,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Produced by cold.<BR> 2. Produced in the Himālaya.<BR> II. f. जा, Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवन्त्|हिमवत्
हिमवन्त् हिम + वन्त्,<BR> I. adj., f. वती, Cold.<BR> II. m. Himālaya, Vikr. d. 160; Rājat. 5, 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानी
हिमानी हिमानी, i. e. हिम + ई, f. Great frost, a mass of snow, Nalod. 2, 5; Kir. 4, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमालय|हिमालयः
हिमालय हिमालय, i. e. हिम-आलय, m. The Himālaya range of mountains, Kumāras. 1, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमिका
हिमिका हिमिका, i. e. हिम + क, f. Hoar-frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम्य|हिम्यः
हिम्य हिम्य, i. e. हिम + य, adj. Frozen, snowy, cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण|हिरणं
हिरण हिरण (i. e. *हरन् + अ, cf. हरित्), n.<BR> 1. Gold.<BR> 2. A cowry (a small coin).<BR> 3. Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्मय|हिरण्मयं|हिरण्मयः
हिरण्मय हिरण्मय, probably हिरण + मय,<BR> I. adj., f. यी, Golden, MBh. 7, 2266; Utt. Rāmac. 39, 6.<BR> II. m. Brahman.<BR> III. n. One of the divisions of the continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्य|हिरण्यं
हिरण्य हिरण्य, probably हिरण + य, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b " target="_blank">Page1115-b + 38</a>] n.<BR> 1. Gold, Pañc. iii. d. 15; Man. 2, 29 (a golden spoon).<BR> 2. Silver.<BR> 3. Wealth.<BR> 4. A cowry (a small coin).<BR> 5. Substance.<BR> 6. Imperishable matter<BR> 7. Semen virile.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहिरण्य
गो- + हिरण्य गो- + हिरण्य, n. kine and gold, MBh. 2, 1833.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यक|हिरण्यकः
हिरण्यक हिरण्य + क, m. A proper name, Hit. 28, 8, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपुहन्
हिरण्यकशिपुहन् हिरण्य-कशिपु-हन्, m. Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यबाहु|हिरण्यबाहुः
हिरण्यबाहु हिरण्य-बाहु, and हिरण्यवाह हिरण्य-वाह, m.<BR> 1. The river Sone.<BR> 2. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवन्त्|हिरण्यवत्
हिरण्यवन्त् हिरण्य + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Abounding in gold, Chr. 295, 16 = Rigv. i. 92, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरुक्
हिरुक् हिरुक्, indecl.<BR> 1. Without, except.<BR> 2. Amongst.<BR> 3. Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्
† हिल् हिल्, i. 6, Par. To express (amorous) inclination, to dally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्लोलय
हिल्लोलय हिल्लोलय (v. r. of हिन्दोलय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिष्क्
हिष्क् हिष्क्, v. r. of किष्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिहि
हिहि हिहि, an interj. of surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनक
ऽहीनक -हीन + क (vb. 2. हा), in करपादैक-, i. e. कर-पाद-एक-, adj. Losing a hand and a foot, Yājñ. 2, 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनत्व
ऽहीनत्व -हीन + त्व (vb. 2. हा), in उत्साह-शक्ति-, n. Want of the power of exertion, Hit. iv. d. 36. पुत्र-, n. Condition of having no son, Cāṇ. 49 in Berl. Monatsb. 1864, 410. बुद्धि-, n. Want of understanding. Hit. ii. d. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीर|हीरं|हीरः
हीर हीर (partly for हार, q. cf.),<BR> I. m.<BR> 1. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR> 2. A necklace.<BR> 3. A lion.<BR> 4. A snake.<BR> 5. Śiva.<BR> II. f. रा.<BR> 1. Lakṣmī.<BR> 2. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a " target="_blank">Page1116-a + 42</a>] An ant.<BR> 3. A cockroach.<BR> III. n. A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुक|हीलुकं
हीलुक हीलुक, n. Rum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही हीही, indecl.<BR> 1. An interjection of laughter, Hee! hee!<BR> 2. Of surprise, Ah!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु हु, ii. 3, जुहु, Par.<BR> 1. To sacrifice, Man. 4, 206.<BR> 2. To worship by oblations, Man. 2, 156. हुत,<BR> 1. Sacrificed, Bhartṛ. 2, 67.<BR> 2. One to whom is sacrificed, Sāv. 1, 21. n. Oblation.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. हव्य, Fit to be offered. n.<BR> 1. An offering to the gods, Man. 1, 94; 95.<BR> 2. Clarified butter, Kir. 1, 22.<BR> --Caus. To cause to worship, Rām. 2, 25, 25.<BR> --With आ आ, आहुत, Worshipped by sacrifices, Lass. 100, 14 = Rigv. vii. 15, 7. आहवनीय, m. (viz. अग्नि), The sacrificial fire, Man. 2, 231.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To worship by sacrifices, Ragh. 1, 53.<BR> --With प्र प्र, प्रहुत, m. (viz. यज्ञ), Sacrificial food offered to spirits, Man. 3, 73. n. Offering to spirits.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-प्रहुत, adj. not sacrificed before, Bhāg. P. 5, 26, 18.<BR> --Cf. χέω; Goth. giutan; A.S. geotan; Lat. fundere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहुत|अहुतः
अ-हुत अ-हुत, adj. not sacrificed (= जप), divine study, Man. 3, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुंकार|हुङ्कार|हुङ्कारः
हुंकार हुंकार, i. e. हुम् (an imitative sound), -कार, m.<BR> 1. Uttering a menacing sound, Rājat. 5, 345.<BR> 2. Roaring, bellowing, Pañc. 162, 25 (of an elephant).<BR> 3. Twang (of a bow), Śāk. d. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्कृत
हुंकृत हुंकृत, i. e. हुम्-कृत (vb. कृ),<BR> I. adj. Uttered as an incantation.<BR> II. n.<BR> 1. Incantation.<BR> 2. Roar (of the thunder), Mālat. 151, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्
† हुड् हुड्, i. 6, Par.<BR> 1. To collect,<BR> 2. To dive.<BR> 3. See हूड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड|हुडः
हुड हुड, and हुडु हुडु, m. A ram, MBh. 3, 640 (ड ?); Pañc. i. d. 216 (डु).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुड
स-हुड स-हुड, adj., f. डा, MBh. 3, 640, with rams (for fighting ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्क|हुडुक्कः
हुडुक्क हुडुक्क, m.<BR> 1. A gallinule.<BR> 2. A drunken man.<BR> 3. A kind of drum.<BR> 4. A stick bound with iron.<BR> 5. The bar of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड्|हुंड्
† हुण्ड् हुण्ड्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To collect.<BR> 2. To select.<BR> 3. See भुण्ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड|हुंड|हुंडः|हुण्डः
हुण्ड हुण्ड, m.<BR> 1. A tiger.<BR> 2. A ram.<BR> 3. A village hog.<BR> 4. An imp.<BR> 5. A blockhead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डिका
हुण्डिका हुण्डिका, f. Assignment, order (given for the maintenance of soldiers), Rājat. 5, 265 (cf. Troyer and हुण्ड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुज्
हुतभुज् हुत-भुज् (vb. हु), m. Agni, or fire, Vikr. d. 8; Utt. Rāmac. 123, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतवह|हुतवहः
हुतवह हुत-वह् + अ (vb. हु), m. Fire, Pañc. 182, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताश|हुताशः
हुताश हुताश, i. e. हुत- 2. अश् + अ, m. Fire, Johns. Sel. 22, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशनवन्त्|हुताशनवत्
हुताशनवन्त् हुताशनवन्त्, i. e. हुत-अशन + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Endowed with the sacred fire, Śāk. d. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम् हुम्, an interj.<BR> 1. Of remembering, Ah! Utt. Rāmac. 136, 14.<BR> 2. Of repulse, Away!<BR> 3. Of interrogation, Hey?<BR> 4. Of assent, Yes.<BR> 5. Of doubt.<BR> 6. A mystical syllable used in incantations (cf. हुंकार, हुंकृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्छ्
† हुर्छ् हुर्छ् (properly, ह्वृ + छ्; cf. ऋ + छ्, s. v. ऋ, गछ्, s. v. गम्, etc.), i. 1, Par. To be crooked, to go crookedly.<BR> --Cf. Goth. vraiqs; probably Lat. quercus, ob-liquus; λοξός (old ptcple. pf. pass.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल्
† हुल् हुल्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. To go.<BR> 2. To cover.<BR> 3. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलहुली
हुलहुली हुलहुली, f. Inarticulate sounds of pleasure made by women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुष्कपुर
हुष्कपुर हुष्क-पुर, i. e. (probably the name of a Scythian tribe), -पुर, n., Rājat. 5, 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु and हुहू हुहू̆ (probably from an anomal. frequent. of ह्वे), m. A Gandharva, Indr. 2, 14 (हु); MBh. 13, 7639 (हू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू हू, an interjection of calling, of contempt, of pride, and of weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूंकार|हूङ्कार|हूङ्कारः
हूंकार हूंकार, i. e. हूम्-कार,<BR> 1. Uttering the sound हूम्, Dev. 6, 9; as injury, Man. 11, 204.<BR> 2. Roaring, Kathās. 4, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूंकृति
हूंकृति हूंकृति, i. e. हूम्-कृति (cf. the last), f.<BR> 1. Making हूम्, sound of a sleeping person, Kathās. 3, 64, at the end of a comp. adj.<BR> 2. Injury, Nalod. 2, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड्
† हूड् हूड्, होड् होड्, हुड् हुत् हौड् हौड्, ह्रूड् ह्रूड्, ह्रुड् ह्रुड्, ह्रौड् ह्रौड्, i. 1, Par. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूति|हूतिः
हूति हूति, i. e. ह्वे + ति, f.<BR> 1. Calling.<BR> 2. Challenging.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवहूति|देवहूतिः
देव- + हूति देव- + हूति, f. 1. invocation of the gods, Lass. 102, 7 = Rigv. vii. 14, 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवहूती
देव-हूती देव-हूती, the name of a spell, Bhāg. P. 9, 24, 31. 3. a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुरुहूति
सु-पुरु- + हूति सु-पुरु- + हूति, adj. very much invoked, Bhāg. P. 6, 9, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वहूति
पूर्व- + हूति पूर्व- + हूति, f. former invocation, Lass. 98, 2 = Rigv. vi. 64, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम् हूम्, an interj. (cf. हुम्),<BR> 1. Of doubt, Humph! ha!<BR> 2. Of interrogation, Hey?<BR> 3. Of assent, Yes.<BR> 4. Of anger, fear.<BR> 5. Of laughing, Lass. 80, 1 (Prākṛ.).<BR> 6. Of reproach, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-b " target="_blank">Page1117-b + 44</a>] contempt, Lass. 2. ed. 48, 47; equivalent to ‘Be silent,’ Tush!<BR> 7. Of aversion.<BR> 8. A mystical syllable, Cf. हूंकार, हूंकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरव|हूरवः
हूरव हू + रव (हू, an imitative sound), m. A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ हृ (for original भृ, which still appears in the signification of हृ in the Vedas; cf. भृ. The original signification, ‘to bring,’ becomes, on the one side, ‘to carry to,’ on the other, ‘to carry away’).<BR> --i. 1, Par. Ātm. † ii. 3, जिहृ, Par.<BR> 1. To convey, Megh. 7.<BR> 2. To offer, Man. 3, 121.<BR> 3. To direct or discharge (an arrow), Chr. 37, 29.<BR> 4. To take, to fetch, Sāv. 5, 103.<BR> 5. To retain, Hit. 90, 9.<BR> 6. To seize, to carry away, Vikr. d. 38; Bhag. 2, 67 (his understanding is carried away, as a ship by the wind).<BR> 7. To cut off (the head), MBh. 3, 10184.<BR> 8. To steal, to rob, Rām. 1, 1, 51; to charm, Vikr. d. 85.<BR> 9. To acquire, Bhartṛ. 3, 97; to gain, Hit. iv. d. 133.<BR> 10. To put off, Man. 4, 74.<BR> 11. To accept, to inherit, Man. 9, 131.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. कृत, Captivated, Śāk. d. 5.<BR> --Ptcple. of the fut. pass. हार्य (Lass. 98, 12, read ह्वार्य).<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Caus. हारय,<BR> 1. To cause to take, i. e. to give, Pañc. iv. d. 47; to give away, i. d. 296; to cause to drink, Rājat. 5, 368.<BR> 2. To send, Megh. 4. हारित,<BR> 1. Lost, Lass. 21, 19.<BR> 2. Fascinated, Rājat. 5, 367.<BR> --With अनु अनु, To imitate. Gīt. 8, 4.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To take [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1118-a " target="_blank">Page1118-a + 42</a>] away, Pañc. i. d. 352; to rob, Ragh. 9, 7; Vikr. 11, 5.<BR> 2. To captivate, Lass. 69, 10.<BR> 3. To take off, Man. 4, 55.<BR> 4. To remove, MBh. 3, 719. अपकृत, Seized (by sleep), Nal. 10, 7.<BR> --Caus. अपहारित, Caused or ordered to be robbed, Rām. 1, 42, 2.<BR> --With व्यप वि-अप,<BR> 1. To remove, MBh. 3, 870.<BR> 2. To cut off, MBh. 2, 1584.<BR> --With अभि अभि, To remove, to cut off, MBh. 3, 14610.<BR> --Caus. To attack, Draup. 8, 5.<BR> --With अव अव, To put off, MBh. 4, 1304. अवहृत,<BR> 1. Taken off, back, or away, seized, stolen.<BR> 2. Fined. अवहार्य,<BR> 1. Recoverable, to be restored, Man. 8, 145.<BR> 2. To be fined, Man. 8, 198.<BR> --With अभ्यव अभि-अव, To eat, Bhāg. P. 5, 9, 12. अभ्यवहार्य, see s. v.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to eat, Daśak. in Chr. 200, 8.<BR> 2. To cause to resist, MBh. 3, 16369.<BR> --With प्रत्यव प्रति-अव, Caus. To suspend or to interrupt again, Chr. 37, 30.<BR> --With व्यव वि-अव,<BR> 1. To waste away, Mālat. 153, 21.<BR> 2. To distinguish, to name, Vedāntas. in Chr. 204, 13.<BR> 3. To act, Hit. 62, 9; MBh. 3, 12861; to behave, Mālat. 7, 7.<BR> 4. To litigate, Daśak. in Chr. 190, 2.<BR> 5. To fight, MBh. 4, 1870.<BR> 6. To obtain, MBh. 3, 1462 (satisfaction). व्यवहार्य,<BR> 1. To be observed as a duty.<BR> 2. Subject to legal process.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> 1. To carry, Man. 2, 182.<BR> 2. To offer (a sacrifice), Rām. 6, 113, 10; Man. 6, 10.<BR> 3. To give, Man. 2, 245.<BR> 4. To fetch, Nal. 20, 5.<BR> 5. To rob, Nal. 26, 7.<BR> 6. To get, Man. 9, 190 (to bring forth a son).<BR> 7. To enjoy, Lass. 70, 14.<BR> 8. To eat, MBh. 3, 54; 57.<BR> 9. To destroy, Mālat. 153, 12. आहृत,<BR> 1. Brought, Hit. iii. d. 6.<BR> 2. Collected, Pañc. 263, 22.<BR> 3. Made captive, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1118-b " target="_blank">Page1118-b + 43</a>] Man. 8, 415 (ध्वज-, under a standard, or in battle, a kind of slave). आहार्य,<BR> 1. Producible (अन्-, Not producible, Man. 8, 202).<BR> 2. Removable. Desider. To wish to recover, MBh. 1, 6247.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To cause to hold, Man. 8, 114.<BR> 2. To cause to be paid, MBh. 2, 987; to collect (duties), Man. 7, 80.<BR> 3. To apply, Hiḍ. 4, 48.<BR> 4. To show (as anger), Rām. 1, 60, 19; (joy), Chr. 58, 11.<BR> 5. To eat, Lass. 29, 14.<BR> --With अन्वा अनु-आ, अन्वाहार्य, see s. v.<BR> --With अभ्या अभि-आ, To offer, MBh. 1, 3733.<BR> --With उदा उद्-आ,<BR> 1. To utter, Man. 11, 96; to pronounce, 2, 199; to call, Vikr. d. 88.<BR> 2. To tell, MBh. 3, 2190.<BR> 3. To require, Mālat. 2, 15. उदाहृत,<BR> 1. Called, named, Kir. 11, 72.<BR> 2. Said, Chr. 42, 12.<BR> 3. Illustrated.<BR> 4. Predicated, Bhāṣāp. 14.<BR> --With प्रत्युदा प्रति-उद्-आ, To answer, Rām. 1, 52, 10.<BR> --With समुदा सम्-उद्-आ, समुदाहृत,<BR> 1. Uttered, Rām. 1, 14, 23.<BR> 2. Declared.<BR> 3. Illustrated, recorded, Man. 1, 50.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ,<BR> 1. To offer, MBh. 1, 758 (cf. Man. 2, 245).<BR> 2. To employ, MBh. 3, 1353. उपाहृत,<BR> 1. Taken, got, Rājat. 5, 444.<BR> 2. Prepared, cultivated (?), Rājat. 5, 110.<BR> --With प्रत्या प्रति-आ,<BR> 1. To recover, MBh. 3, 8655.<BR> 2. To utter, MBh. 3, 2177 (a speech).<BR> 3. To cry, Draup. 6, 7.<BR> 4. To report, Chr. 45, 14. प्रत्याहृत,<BR> 1. Resumed.<BR> 2. Restrained.<BR> 3. Withheld.<BR> --With व्या वि-आ,<BR> 1. To explain, declare, MBh. 3, 12466; Vikr. 55, 21.<BR> 2. To report, Pañc. 30, 8.<BR> 3. To tell, Rām. 2, 53, 5.<BR> 4. To speak, Rām. 1, 48, 1; to address (acc.), Pañc. 109, 18.<BR> 5. To utter, to pronounce, Bhag. 8, 13.<BR> 6. To answer, Rām. 2, 93, 8.<BR> --With अभिव्या अभि-वि-आ, Caus. To pronounce, Man. 2, 172.<BR> --With प्रव्या [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1119-a " target="_blank">Page1119-a + 44</a>] प्र-वि-आ,<BR> 1. To foretell, MBh. 1, 7240.<BR> 2. To roar, MBh. 3, 15673.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To restore (to its former condition), Man. 8, 319.<BR> 2. To collect, to assemble, MBh. 1, 6951.<BR> 3. To offer, Rām. 1, 58, 4.<BR> 4. To destroy, Bhag. 11, 32. समाहृत,<BR> 1. Accepted.<BR> 2. Compiled.<BR> 3. Much, Pañc. 171, 11.<BR> --With उद् उद्,<BR> 1. To take out, Ragh. 2, 30 (an arrow out of the quiver); to draw out of (abl.), Hit. iii. d. 30; from, Hit. 39, 2, M.M.<BR> 2. To lift up, MBh. 1, 3299.<BR> 3. To pluck up, Man. 7, 110.<BR> 4. To pull out, MBh. 3, 11186; to exterminate, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 483; to destroy, MBh. 3, 221.<BR> 5. To hold out, to extend, Man. 4, 58.<BR> 6. To raise, to extol, MBh. 1, 4923.<BR> 7. To corroborate, Bhag. 6, 5 (cf. Daśak. in Chr. 189, 9).<BR> 8. To deliver from (abl.), Vikr. d. 94; to save, MBh. 2, 2293; Pañc. i. d. 403. उद्-धृत,<BR> 1. Thrown up.<BR> 2. Vomited.<BR> 3. Separated.<BR> 4. Divided.<BR> 5. Recovered.<BR> 6. Uncovered.<BR> 7. Dispersed.<BR> 8. Extracted, Man. 4, 62. In the Pañcatantra occurs उद्धरित instead of उद्धृत, Saved, Pañc. 114, 7; 141, 10; cf. my translation, n. 753. Desider. To wish to relieve, Man. 4, 251.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To order to pull out, Ragh. 9, 78.<BR> 2. To lift up, MBh. 3, 10946.<BR> --With अभ्युद् अभि-उद्, To further, Pañc. iii. d. 246. अभ्युद्धृत,<BR> 1. Taken out.<BR> 2. Destined, Mṛcch. 61, 3.<BR> --Caus. To snatch away, MBh. 3, 13326.<BR> --With प्रोद् प्र-उद्,<BR> 1. To lift up, Rām. 2, 110, 4.<BR> 2. To fetch (water), Ṛt. 1, 23.<BR> 3. To save, Lass. 2. ed. 88. 21.<BR> --With समुद् सम्-उद्,<BR> 1. To take out, Sāv. 5, 17.<BR> 2. To pick up, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 2262.<BR> 3. To lift up, MBh. 3, 10946.<BR> 4. To extol, MBh. 1, 4271.<BR> 5. To favour, Pañc. 188, 1.<BR> 6. To destroy, Ṛt. 1, 20; MBh. 1, 3821 समुद्धृत,<BR> 1. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1119-b " target="_blank">Page1119-b + 43</a>] Thrown up (as food).<BR> 2. Extricated, lifted out.<BR> 3. Divided, set apart, deducted, Man. 9, 116.<BR> 4. Seized.<BR> --With उप उप,<BR> 1. To bring, Daśak. in Chr. 196, 18.<BR> 2. To offer, Śāk. 113, 4; with पूजाम्, To honour, Rām. 1, 51, 5.<BR> 3. To sacrifice, Mālat. 75, 6.<BR> 4. To destroy, MBh. 2, 861. Desider. To wish to offer, MBh. 2, 862.<BR> --Caus. To cause to be offered, Rām. 1, 20, 9.<BR> --With समुप सम्-उप, To offer, to perform (a sacrifice), Rām. 1, 40, 2.<BR> --With निस् निस्,<BR> 1. To draw from, Man. 7, 4.<BR> 2. To export (wares), Man. 8, 399.<BR> 3. To carry out (a corpse), Man. 5, 91; 10, 55.<BR> 4. To pull out, MBh. 3, 6033.<BR> 5. To mix (the clothes of one person with those of another), Man. 8, 396. निर्हृत, Extracted.<BR> --With परि परि,<BR> 1. To pass by (a place for paying custom), Man. 8, 400.<BR> 2. To shun, Hit. i. d. 75.<BR> 3. To avoid, Pañc. 261, 5; Megh. 14.<BR> 4. To conceal, Mṛcch. 14, 3.<BR> 5. To leave, to spare, Rām. 2, 48, 10 (Gorr. v. r. 2, 45, 26). परिहृत, Quitted, Rājat. 5, 190. परिहार्य, To be separated, Kathās. 39, 32.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. unavoidable, Bhag. 2, 27.<BR> --With प्र प्र,<BR> 1. To direct, Śāk. d. 11.<BR> 2. To strike, Man. 8, 300.<BR> 3. To assail (with dat.), Chr. 28, 24; (with gen.), 25 (read प्र हरे); to attack, Pañc. 149, 1.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pres. प्रहरन्त्, m. A warrior, Chr. 35, 2. प्रहृत, Seized. n. Striking, killing.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, To fight, MBh. 3, 15167.<BR> --With वि वि,<BR> 1. To remove, to wipe off (a tear), Śāk. 49, 19.<BR> 2. To change, Johns. Sel. 5, 31.<BR> 3. To alternate (between standing and sitting), Man. 6, 22.<BR> 4. To ramble for pleasure, Megh. 61; to ramble, Pañc. 197, 22.<BR> 5. To divert one's self, Man. 7, 221. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-a " target="_blank">Page1120-a + 43</a>]<BR> 6. To pass (as time), Man. 6, 33.<BR> 7. To live, MBh. 4, 27. व्थृत,<BR> 1. Expanded.<BR> 2. Sported. n. Reluctance (in a female) to avow her feelings to her lover.<BR> --With सम् सम्,<BR> 1. To contract, Bhag. 2, 58 (as the tortoise contracts its limbs).<BR> 2. To clench (the fist), MBh. 3, 11517.<BR> 3. To abridge, Ragh. 10, 33.<BR> 4. To seize, MBh. 3, 18.<BR> 5. To draw away (the curtain of a theatre), Mālav. d. 22.<BR> 6. To take back, Śāk. d. 131; to put aside, Utt. Rāmac. 148, 12.<BR> 7. To withhold, Hit. i. d. 60, M.M.<BR> 8. To destroy, MBh. 1, 241.<BR> 9. To restrain (as wrath), Nal. 6, 14; (fear), Mālat. 125, 1.<BR> 10. To take, Man. 9, 113; 8, 188; 189.<BR> 11. To conciliate, MBh. 1, 5996. संहृत, Scattered.<BR> --Comp.<BR> अ-, adj. unrestrained, perpetual, Utt. Rāmac. 2, 9.<BR> --With उपसम् उप-सम्,<BR> 1. To take back, Śāk. 94, 20.<BR> 2. To withhold, Hit. i. d. 58, M.M.<BR> 3. To collect, MBh. 1, 7206.<BR> --With समुपसम् सम्-उप-सम्, To stop, Utt. Rāmac. 144, 4.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्,<BR> 1. To take back, Ragh. 9, 57; to draw back, Śāk. d. 11.<BR> 2. To retract, Rām. 2, 22, 10. प्रति-संहृत,<BR> 1. Compressed.<BR> 2. Checked, Śiś. 2, 15.<BR> 3. Comprehended, included.<BR> --Caus. To retract, Rām. 2, 22, 26.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. co-hors; heres; χείρ, χράομαι, κίχρημι (cf. जिहर्मि); Goth. geiro, gairôn, gairnjan; A.S. georn, avidus, geornian, to yearn; Engl. yare; cf. हर्य्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्य|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अ-हार्य अ-हार्य, 1. not to be seized or confiscated, Man. 9, 189. 2. not to be brought back, Daśak. in Chr. 181, 8 (सा चेद् अहार्यनिश्चया, ‘if she cannot be induced to change her mind’).<BR> 3. not to be gained (by bribes), incapable of perfidy, Man. 7, 217. Desider. जिहीर्ष, To wish to rob, MBh. 1, 7480.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृच्छय|हृच्छयः
हृच्छय हृच्छय, i. e. हृद्-शि + अ, m. Kāma, the god of love, and love, Indr. 5, 44; Nal. 1, 17; Bhāg. P. 3, 14, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीय
हृणीय हृणीय, (properly a denomin. derived from a lost noun, *हृण, akin to हरित्, हिरण, with य), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b " target="_blank">Page1120-b + 43</a>] Ātm.<BR> 1. To be angry.<BR> 2. To be ashamed.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. galla; A.S. gealla; χολή; Lat. fel, bilis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीया
हृणीया हृणीया, i. e. हृणीय + अ, f.<BR> 1. Censure, reproach.<BR> 2. Bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृति|हृतिः
हृति हृ + ति, f. Robbing, Rājat. 5, 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्
हृद् हृद्, n.<BR> 1. The heart, Hit. 77, 3, M.M.; Pañc. i. d. 151 (former part of a comp.).<BR> 2. The mind.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. Goth. hairto; A.S. heorte; Lat. cor, cordis; κέαρ, κήρ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृद्
दुस्- + हृद् दुस्- + हृद्,<BR> I. adj. wicked, MBh. 3, 17300.<BR> II. m. an enemy, MBh. 4, 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्
सु- + हृद् सु- + हृद्,<BR> I. adj. loving, Pañc. i. d. 294; superl. सुहृत्तम, very fond (of each other), Hit. i. d. 1, M.M.<BR> II. m. 1. a friend, Vikr. 11, 13. 2. an ally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
अ-सु- + हृद् अ-सु- + हृद्, adj. hostile, Rājat. 5, 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंसुहृद्
किम्-सु- + हृद् किम्-सु- + हृद्, m. a bad friend, Hit. ii. d. 31 (read किंसुहृद्); cf. Kir. 1, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखासुहृद्
मखासु- + हृद् मखासु- + हृद्, i. e. मख-अ-सु-, m. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसुहृद्
मधु-सु- + हृद् मधु-सु- + हृद्, m. Kāmadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदय|हृदयं
हृदय हृदय, n. (cf. the last),<BR> 1. The heart, Vikr. d. 7.<BR> 2. The mind, Pañc. i. d. 198.<BR> 3. Knowledge, Nal. 14, 21.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --Cf. καρδία.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्णहृदय
अ-कर्ण- + हृदय अ-कर्ण- + हृदय, adj. deprived of ears and heart, Pañc. iv. d. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहृदय
अयस्- + हृदय अयस्- + हृदय, adj. iron-hearted, Ragh. 9, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुहृदय|भीरुहृदयः
भीरु- + हृदय भीरु- + हृदय, m. a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तीकृतहृदय
रिक्ती-कृत- + हृदय रिक्ती-कृत- + हृदय (vb. रिच्), adj. deprived of (its) heart, Pañc. 89, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यहृदय
शून्य- + हृदय शून्य- + हृदय, adj. unsuspecting, unsuspicious, Pañc. 208, 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदय|सहृदयः
स- + हृदय स- + हृदय,<BR> I. adj. 1. along with the heart, Vikr. 71, 13. 2. compassionate, Rām. 2, 13, 16.<BR> II. m. a wise man, Böhtl. Ind. Spr. 1265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृदय|सुहृदयः
सु- + हृदय सु- + हृदय, adj. good-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणहृदय|हरिणहृदयः
हरिण- + हृदय हरिण- + हृदय, adj. fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयंगम|हृदयङ्गम|हृदयङ्गमं
हृदयंगम हृदयंगम, i. e. हृदय + म्-गम् + अ, adj.<BR> 1. Affecting.<BR> 2. Touching the heart, sweet, Ragh. 19, 13.<BR> 3. Dear, Utt. Rāmac. 103, 5; Rājat. 5, 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयच्छिद्
हृदयच्छिद् हृदयच्छिद्, i. e. हृदय-छिद्, adj. Heart-piercing, Chr. 36, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयवन्त्|हृदयवत्
हृदयवन्त् हृदय + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, and हृदयालु हृदयालु, i. e. हृदय + आलु, adj. Good-hearted, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयविध्
हृदयविध् हृदयविध्, i. e. हृदय-व्यध्, adj. Heart-piercing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयस्थ
हृदयस्थ हृदय-स्थ, adj. Cerished in the heart. Pañc. 46, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिक|हृदयिकः
हृदयिक हृदयिक, i. e. हृदयिन् + क, adj., and हृदयिन् हृदयिन्, i. e. हृदय + इन्, adj., f. नी, Good-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिस्पृश्
हृदिस्पृश् हृद् + इ-स्पृश्, adj. Beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्य|हृद्यं|हृद्यः
हृद्य हृद् + य,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Produced in or from the heart.<BR> 2. Dear, Bhag. 17, 8.<BR> 3. Affectionate.<BR> 4. Pleasant, Rām. 3, 52, 25; Kathās. 26, 283.<BR> 5. Savoury, Man. 3, 227.<BR> II. m. A Mantra or verse for effecting fascination.<BR> III. f. या, A medicinal root.<BR> IV. n. Cassia bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लास|हृल्लासः
हृल्लास हृल्लास, i. e. हृद्-लस् + अ, m.<BR> 1. Hiccough.<BR> 2. Heart-ache, Mālat. 57, 9 (Sch. = हृदय-शोचक and हृदय-अवसाद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्
हृष् हृष् (originally भृष्), i. 4, Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., MBh. 2, 1219),<BR> 1. To bristle, to be erect (as hair, especially of the body, a token of fear, or, more commonly, of pleasure), MBh. 2, 1757; Rām. 3, 50, 27.<BR> 2. To be glad, Daśak. in Chr. 197, 6.<BR> --† i. 1, Par. To lie, to affirm falsely.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass.<BR> I. हृषित and हृष्ट.<BR> 1. Having the hair of the body erect with pleasure, Rām. 3, 50, 27 (हृष्ट); MBh. 4, 1245 (हृषित); with fear, Rām. 2, 9, 34 Gorr.<BR> 2. Standing erect (of flowers), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-b " target="_blank">Page1121-b + 40</a>] Nal. 23, 17 (हृषित).<BR> 3. Pleased, Vikr. 75, 1 (हृष्ट).<BR> 4. Astonished<BR> 5. Disappointed, deceived.<BR> II. हृष्ट, Smiling.<BR> --Caus.<BR> 1. To delight, Chr. 27 10.<BR> 2. To be glad, Man. 6, 57. हर्षित, Delighted, Pañc. 146, 22.<BR> --With नि नि, निहृष्ट, Pleased, Daśak. in Chr. 198, 4.<BR> --With परि परि, Caus. To delight much, MBh. 3, 887.<BR> --With संपरि सम्-परि, Caus. To delight completely, or much, MBh. 3, 17470.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To be very glad, Bhag. 5, 20; प्रहृष्ट, Very glad, Pañc. 241, 23.<BR> --Caus. To delight, Hit. iv. d. 9; प्रहर्षित, Very delighted, Pañc. 241, 16.<BR> --With संप्र सम्-प्र, संप्रहृष्ट,<BR> 1. Erect (viz. the hair of the body), MBh. 3, 3061.<BR> 2. Pleased, MBh. 1, 3107.<BR> --Caus. संप्रहर्षित, Much delighted, MBh. 3, 11829.<BR> --With सम् सम्, To be glad, MBh. 2, 941. संहृष्ट-रोमाङ्ग, i. e. -रोमन्-अङ्ग, adj. literally, ‘Having a body, the hair of which stood erect,’ Rām. 3, 55, 5.<BR> --With अतिसम् अति-सम्, अतिसंहृष्ट, Very glad, Lass. 2. ed. 47, 40.<BR> --With परिसम् परि-सम्, परिसंहृष्ट, Very pleased, Rām. 3, 49, 11.<BR> --With प्रतिसम् प्रति-सम्, To be glad, Rām. 3, 49, 11.<BR> --Cf. ϕρίσσω, ϕρίξ; O.H.G. burst; A.S. byrst, bristl, forst, frost, gelu; frysan; a-grísan, gerst, gryre; Lat. horrere, Hersilia; probably χέρσος, χήρ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीक|हृषीकं
हृषीक हृष् + ईक, n. Any organ of sense.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृषीक
दुस्- + हृषीक दुस्- + हृषीक, adj. having defective organs of sense, MBh. 3, 13951.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीकेश|हृषीकेशः
हृषीकेश हृषीकेश, i. e. हृषीक-ईश, m. Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu, Rām. 1, 45, 30; Rājat. 5, 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टवत्
हृष्टवत् हृष्टवत्, i. e. हृष्ट + वन्त्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a " target="_blank">Page1122-a + 40</a>] acc. sing. n., adv. Cheerfully, Johns. Sel. 59, 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टि|हृष्टिः
हृष्टि हृष्टि i. e. हृष् + ति, f. Joy, Mālat. 82, 4; delight, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे हे,<BR> 1. A vocative particle, Lass. 8, 18.<BR> 2. An interjection expressing envy or malice, He! Pañc. 37, 23; disapprobation, Bhartṛ. 2, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का हेक्का, f. Hiccough (cf. हिक्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेट्
† हेट् हेट् (?), हेठ् हेठ्, i. 1, Ātm. and Par.<BR> 1. To be wicked.<BR> 2. To vex or harass, to hurt; see हेढ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ|हेठः
हेठ हेठ, m.<BR> 1. Hindering, obstructing.<BR> 2. Hurting, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड्
हेड् हेड् (हेल् हेल्), i. 1, Ātm. To disregard; अ-हेडमान, adj. Careful, Rām. 2, 68, 22.<BR> --† i. 1, Par. To surround, to attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडज|हेडजः
हेडज हेड् + अ-ज, m. Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेढ्
† हेढ् हेढ्, हेठ् हेठ्, ii. 9, हेढ्णा, हेठ्णा, णी, Par.<BR> 1. To be born again.<BR> 2. To produce happiness or purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेति|हेतिः
हेति हेति, i. e. नि + ति, f.<BR> 1. A weapon, Pañc. i. d. 236.<BR> 2. A ray of the sun.<BR> 3. Flame.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासहेति|श्वासहेतिः
श्वास- + हेति श्वास- + हेति, f. sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतिक
ऽहेतिक -हेति + क, a substitute for हेति, when latter part of comp. words; e. g. शक्ति-, m. A spearman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतिमन्त्|हेतिमत्
हेतिमन्त् हेति + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, in हरि-, Illuminated by the sun, Mālat. 149, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतु|हेतुः
हेतु हेतु, perhaps हि + तु (properly, Impulse, Chr. 18, 2),<BR> 1. Motive; abl., on account of, Rām. 3, 49, 39; in order to, Hit. i. d. 173, M.M.; dat. मृत्यु-हेतवे, In order to kill, Bhāg. P. 7, 1, 41.<BR> 2. Origin.<BR> 3. Cause, Hit. i. d. 42, M.M.; reason, Pañc. i. d. 417; proof, Lass. 2. ed. 65, 2.<BR> 4. Means, Hit. 114, 7; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b " target="_blank">Page1122-b + 43</a>] Rājat. 5, 310; prize, 5, 71.<BR> 5. Condition, Draup. 9, 10; law, Hit. ii. d. 10.<BR> 6. The reason or middle term in an inference, Bhāṣāp. 68.<BR> 7. हेतौ, loc. By reason of.<BR> 8. Logic, Daśak. in Chr. 180, 8.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हेतु
निस्- + हेतु निस्- + हेतु, adj. having no cause, MBh. 12, 3277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक हेतु + क,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Relating to the cause.<BR> 2. Causal, instrumental<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. An active cause, an instrument, Hit. 55, 5.<BR> 2. A logician, Man. 12, 111.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहेतुक
भय- + हेतुक भय- + हेतुक, adj. dangerous, Hit. 85, 1, M.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेतुक
स- + हेतुक स- + हेतुक, adj. 1. produced by a cause, Bhāṣāp. 100. 2. with the motive, Rājat. 5, 54 (Śūra knowing that he had retired, and also his motive for it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुता
हेतुता हेतु + ता, f., and हेतुत्व हेतु + त्व, n. Causation, the state of being a cause, Hit. i. d. 29, M.M. (ता); Rājat. 5, 292; 388 (ता); Bhāṣāp. 146, 147 (त्व).<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तहेतुत्व
निमित्त-हेतु + त्व निमित्त-हेतु + त्व, n. the being an instrumental cause, Bhāṣāp. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुमन्त्|हेतुमत्
हेतुमन्त् हेतु + मन्त्, adj.<BR> 1. Having a cause; that in which the reason or middle term resides (i. e. the पक्ष), Bhāṣāp. 68.<BR> 2. Accompanied by arguments, Rām. 3, 53, 20.<BR> 3. Attacked by arguments, MBh. 12, 597 (perhaps it is to be read हि instead of ऽपि, then it would be, Skilled in logic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम|हेमं|हेमः
हेम हेम,<BR> I. m. A horse of dark colour.<BR> II. n. Gold (cf. हेमन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमक|हेमकं
हेमक हेम + क (n.), Gold, Rām. 3, 49, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकार|हेमकारः
हेमकार हेम-कार, m. A goldsmith, Man. 9, 292.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन् हेमन्,<BR> I. m. Winter (ŚKD.).<BR> II. n. Gold, Ragh. 1, 10, Naiṣ. 22, 52; Vikr. d. 140 (or हेम).<BR> --Cf. χειμών; with ρ for ν, χειμέρ + ιος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमन्त हेमन्त (i. e. *हेमन्त्, original [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a " target="_blank">Page1123-a + 37</a>] form of हेमन्, + अ), m. (and n.), The cold season, winter, about November--December, Pañc. 94, 2.<BR> --Cf. χεῖμα.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममय
हेममय हेम + मय, adj., f. यी, Golden, Rām. 3, 49, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमल|हेमलः
हेमल हेम + ल, m.<BR> 1. A goldsmith.<BR> 2. A touchstone.<BR> 3. A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवन्त्|हेमवत्
हेमवन्त् हेम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Golden, Rām. 3, 50, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल हेमवल (probably from हेम), n. A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्ब|हेरंब|हेरंबः|हेरम्बः
हेरम्ब हेरम्ब, m.<BR> 1. Gaṇeśa, Mālat. 144, 21.<BR> 2. A buffalo.<BR> 3. A proud hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरिक|हेरिकः
हेरिक हेरिक, m. A spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरुक|हेरुकः
हेरुक हेरुक, m. An attendant on Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेल्
हेल् हेल्, see हेड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलन|हेलनं
हेलन हेल् + अन, n.<BR> 1. Disregard, Bhāg. P. 1, 19, 2.<BR> 2. Dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेला
हेला हेल् + आ, f.<BR> 1. Sport, Ratnāv. 2. ed. 17, 11.<BR> 2. Contempt, Śiś. 2, 48.<BR> 3. Dallying, lascivious endearment, delight, Mālat. 157, 19.<BR> 4. Manner, Neriosengh, see Gött. Gel. Anz. 1861, p. 1837.<BR> 5. instr. लया (properly, Sportively, easily; cf. लीला), At once, Pañc. ii. d. 80; 106, 1; 134, 13; 168, 6; Rājat. 5, 84.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकहेला
एक- + हेला एक- + हेला, f. instr. at once, Pañc. 256, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेला
स- + हेला स- + हेला, adj. sportive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलि|हेलिः
हेलि हेल् + इ, m.<BR> 1. The sun (borrowed from ἥλιος), Bhaviṣyap., see Aufrecht, Ujjvalad. 267, n.<BR> 2. Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलुदिण्ण
हेलुदिण्ण हेलु-दिण्ण (हेलु, The name of a village, and दिण्ण, the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b " target="_blank">Page1123-b + 40</a>] Prākṛt. form for दत्त), adj. Presented with the village हेलु, Rājat. 5, 397.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष्
हेष् हेष्, i. 1, Ātm. To neigh as a horse, Pañc. iv. d. 49.<BR> हेषित, m. Neighing, Episod. MBh. de Śakuntala, ed. Chezy., 1, 16.<BR> --Cf. probably Lat. hinnire, hinnulus; γίννος; but cf. also ह्रेष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषा
हेषा हेष् + आ, f. Neighing (as a horse, or braying, as an ass), Kir. 16, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषाय
हेषाय हेषाय, a denomin. derived from हेषा with य, Ātm. To neigh, Pañc. 254, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषिन्
हेषिन् हेष् + इन्, m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

है
है है, A vocative particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक|हैतुकः
हैतुक हैतुक, i. e. हेतुक + अ,<BR> I. adj. Causal, causative.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. A follower of the Mīmāṃsā doctrines.<BR> 2. A sceptic, a sophist, Man. 4, 30.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामहैतुक
काम- + हैतुक काम- + हैतुक, adj. caused by arbitrariness, i. e. by accident, Bhag. 16, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक्य
हैतुक्य हैतुक्य, i. e. हैतुक + य, in the comp. अ-, n. Want of selfish motives, Bhāg. P. 3, 29, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम हैम, i. e. हेमन् + अ,<BR> I. adj.<BR> 1. Cold.<BR> 2. Golden, Vikr. d. 157.<BR> II. n. Hoar-frost.<BR> III. f. मी, Yellow jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
हैमन हैमन, i. e. हेमन् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Winterly, MBh. 2, 2669; Kir. 17, 12.<BR> II. m. The month Mā Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR> III. n. Winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्त|हैमन्तं
हैमन्त हैमन्त, and हैमन्तिक हैमन्तिक, i. e. हेमन्त + अ, or इक,<BR> I. adj. Wintry.<BR> II. n. Winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमल|हैमलः
हैमल हैम + ल, n. Winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवत|हैमवतं|हैमवतः
हैमवत हैमवत, i. e. हिमवन्त् + अ,<BR> I. adj., f. ती, Belonging to the Himālaya mountain, Draup. 5, 5.<BR> II. m. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a " target="_blank">Page1124-a + 37</a>] A sort of poison.<BR> III. f. ती.<BR> 1. Pārvatī.<BR> 2. Several plants.<BR> IV. n. India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैयंगवीन|हैयङ्गवीन|हैयंगवीनं|हैयङ्गवीनं
हैयंगवीन हैयंगवीन, i. e. ष्यस् + अ + म्-गो + ईन, n. Fresh butter (prepared a day before it is used), Ragh. 1, 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यगर्भ
हैरण्यगर्भ हैरण्यगर्भ, i. e. हिरण्य-गर्भ + अ, patronym., m. A son of Brahman, Man. 3, 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यवासस्
हैरण्यवासस् हैरण्यवासस्, i. e. हिरण्य + अ-वासस्, m. An arrow. MBh. 4, 2071.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरिक|हैरिकः
हैरिक हैरिक, m. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहय|हैहयः
हैहय हैहय, m.<BR> 1. The name of a people, Chr. 34, 12.<BR> 2. A prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हो
हो हो, A vocative particle, Kir. 15, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड्
† होड् होड्, i. 1, Ātm. To disregard; see हूद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड|होडः
होड होड, m. A raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडृ
होडृ होडृ, m. A robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढ|होढं
होढ होढ,<BR> I. adj. Stolen.<BR> II. n. Stolen goods, Man. 9, 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृ
होतृ होतृ, i. e.<BR> I. हु + तृ, m., f. त्री, and n. Sacrificing, a sacrificer, Śāk. d. 1; Bhartṛ. 2, 47.<BR> II. हु, or ह्वे + तृ (cf. ह्वे), m. A priest who, at sacrifice, recites the hymns of the Rigveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्र|होत्रं
होत्र होत्र, i. e. हु + त्र, n.<BR> 1. A burnt-offering.<BR> 2. An oblation of clarified butter.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निहोत्र|अग्निहोत्रं|अग्निहोत्रः
अग्नि- + होत्र अग्नि- + होत्र, n. 1. a ceremony consisting in oblations to consecrated fire, Man. 4, 25. 2. the consecrated fire, Man. 5, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिहोत्र|वीतिहोत्रः
वीति- + होत्र वीति- + होत्र, m. 1. Agni. 2. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्र|शालिहोत्रः
शालि- + होत्र शालि- + होत्र, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रीय|होत्रीयं|होत्रीयः
होत्रीय होत्रीय, i. e. होत्र + ईय,<BR> I. m. A priest offering an oblation.<BR> II. n. A place where oblations are offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम|होमः
होम होम, i. e. हु + म, m. An oblation of clarified butter, a sacrifice, Chr. 60, 36 (corr. दत्त-); Pañc. i. d. 347.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपहोम|जपहोमः
जप- + होम जप- + होम, m. the oblation consisting in prayers, Man. 10, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वी|दर्व्वी
दर्वी̆ दर्वी̆, m. oblation with a spoon, MBh. 2, 537 (वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वी|दर्व्वी
दर्वी̆ दर्वी̆, m. oblation with a spoon, MBh. 2, 537 (वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतहोम|हुतहोमः
हुत- + होम हुत- + होम (vb. हु), m. a Brāhmaṇa who has offered an oblation. (n.), an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमन्
होमन् होमन्, i. e. हु + मन्, n. An oblation of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमवन्त्|होमवत्
होमवन्त् होम + वन्त्, adj., f. वती, Having performed sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमि|होमिः
होमि होमि, i. e. हु + मि, m.<BR> 1. Fire.<BR> 2. Clarified butter.<BR> 3. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिन्
होमिन् होमिन्, i. e. होम + इन्, m. A priest who makes an oblation of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरा
होरा होरा (borrowed from ὥρα), f.<BR> 1. The rising of a sign of the zodiac.<BR> 2. An hour.<BR> 3. A line.<BR> 4. A work on astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होहौ
होहौ होहौ, and हौ हौ, interj. of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौड्
हौड् हौड्, see हूड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक हौतृक, i. e. होतृ + क, adj. Relating to the priest called होतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्य|हौम्यं
हौम्य हौम्य, i. e. होम + य, n. Clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नु
ह्नु ह्नु, ii. 2, Ātm.<BR> 1. To take away, Bhaṭṭ. 15, 88.<BR> 2. To conceal one's self, Pāṇ. i. 4, 34.<BR> --With अप अप,<BR> 1. To conceal, Naiṣ. 1, 49.<BR> 2. To deny, to disclaim, Man. 8, 53. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a " target="_blank">Page1125-a + 38</a>]<BR> --With नि नि, To deny, Man. 8, 59.<BR> --With अतिनि अति-नि, To deny strongly, Daśak. in Chr. 193, 9.<BR> --With अपनि अप-नि, To conceal, Mālat. 16, 14.<BR> --Cf. Lat. ab-nuere, nutare, gnavus, navare, i-gnavus, se-gnis, niti, nictare, con-nivere; Goth. hneivan, hnaivs; A.S. hnigan; ἀνα-νεύω, νεύω, νυστάζω, νυθός, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्मल्
† ह्मल् ह्मल्, i. 1, Par. To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्
ह्यस् ह्यस्, i. e. perhaps ह-द्यस् (cf. सद्यस्), adv. Yesterday.<BR> --Cf. Lat. hes + ternus, heri; Goth. gis + tra; A.S. gyrstan; χθές.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्तन|ह्यस्तनं
ह्यस्तन ह्यस् + तन, adj., f. नी, and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्त्य|ह्यस्त्यः
ह्यस्त्य ह्यस् + त्य, adj. Of yesterday, Chr. 39, 4 (तन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रग्
† ह्रग् ह्रग्, ह्रग् ह्लग्, i. 1, Par. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद|ह्रदः
ह्रद ह्रद, probably ह्राद् + अ, m.<BR> 1. A large piece of water, Utt. Rāmac. 53, 9; a deep lake, Pañc. 159, 14.<BR> 2. A ray of light.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाह्रद|गंगाह्रद|गङ्गाह्रदः
गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद, m. names of holy ponds, MBh. 3, 7047 (गङ्गा-); 13, 7645 (तीर्थमहा-); Chr. 46, 28. (राम-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थह्रद
गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद, m. names of holy ponds, MBh. 3, 7047 (गङ्गा-); 13, 7645 (तीर्थमहा-); Chr. 46, 28. (राम-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामह्रद
गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद गङ्गा-, तीर्थ-महा-, राम- + ह्रद, m. names of holy ponds, MBh. 3, 7047 (गङ्गा-); 13, 7645 (तीर्थमहा-); Chr. 46, 28. (राम-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतह्रद
शत- + ह्रद शत- + ह्रद, f. दा, 1. lightning, Vikr. 66, 1. 2. the thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदिनी
ह्रदिनी ह्रदिनी, i. e. ह्रद + इन् + ई, f.<BR> 1. A river, Bhāg. P. 6, 4, 41.<BR> 2. Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रप्
ह्रप् ह्रप्, see ह्लप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्
ह्रस् ह्रस्, i. 1, Par.<BR> 1. † To sound (cf. रस्).<BR> 2. To become small, to be lessened, Man. 1, 83.<BR> --Caus. ह्रासय, To diminish, Man. 11, 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिमन्
ह्रसिमन् ह्रसिमन्, i. e. ह्रस्व + इमन्, m. Shortness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्व|ह्रस्वं|ह्रस्वः
ह्रस्व ह्रस् + व,<BR> I. adj., comparat. ह्रसीयंस्, superl. ह्रसिष्ठ,<BR> 1. Short, Johns. Sel. 15, 53; Bhāṣāp. 109.<BR> 2. Small, Johns. Sel. 51, 107.<BR> 3. Low Nal. 23, 9.<BR> II. m. A dwarf.<BR> --Cf. χέρνϊ, χερείων, χείρων, χείριστος; perhaps Lat. brevis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वक
ह्रस्वक ह्रस्व + क, adj. Small, Rām. 2, 117, 13 Gorr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद्
ह्राद् ह्राद्, i. 1, Ātm. To sound inarticulately (as a drum), Bhaṭṭ. 14, 4; to roar (as thunder), Kāśinātha apud Wilkins.<BR> --Cf. χλάζω, κέχλαδα (see ह्लाद्), probably χάλαζα; Lat. grando; perhaps χέραδος, etc.; Goth. grêtan; A.S. graetan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद|ह्रादः
ह्राद ह्राद् + अ, m. Noise, Kir. 16, 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिन्
ह्रादिन् ह्राद् + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी, Sounding.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. Lightning.<BR> 2. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR> 3. A river.<BR> 4. The olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रास|ह्रासः
ह्रास ह्रास, i. e. ह्रस् + अ, m. Sound.<BR> 2. Decrease, Man. 1, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री ह्री (cf. हृणीय), ii. 3, जिह्री, Par. To be ashamed, Ragh. 15, 44.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. ह्रीण, and ह्रीत, Ashamed, bashful, modest, Nal. 13, 30 (ह्रीत).<BR> --Caus. ह्रेपय, To put to blush, to confound, Kir. 11, 64.<BR> --With सम् सम्, संह्रीण, Ashamed.<BR> --Cf. probably O.H.G. hriuwan; A.S. hreówan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री ह्री, f. Shame, Hit. i. d. 133, M.M.; bashfulness, Pañc. i. d. 185; personified, Rām. 3, 52, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीका
ह्रीका ह्री + का, f.<BR> 1. Bashfulness, modesty.<BR> 2. Fear.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रीक
निस्- + ह्रीक निस्- + ह्रीक, adj. bold, MBh. 7, 4806.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीकु|ह्रीकुः
ह्रीकु ह्री + कु, adj. Bashful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीछ्|ह्रीच्छ्
† ह्रीछ् ह्रीछ् (i. e. ह्री + छ्; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a " target="_blank">Page1126-a + 36</a>] cf. हुर्छ्), i. 1, Par. To be ashamed or modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीमन्त्|ह्रीमत्
ह्रीमन्त् ह्री + मन्त्, adj., f. मती, Bashful, modest, Bhartṛ. 2, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुड्
ह्रुड्, ह्रूड् ह्रू̆द्, see हूड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेप्
† ह्रेप् ह्रेप्, i. 1, Ātm. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपण|ह्रेपणं
ह्रेपण ह्रेपण, i. e. ह्री, Caus., + अन, n. Putting to shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेष्
ह्रेष् ह्रेष्, i. 1, Ātm.<BR> 1. To neigh as a horse, MBh.<BR> 2. † To go. ह्रेषित, n. Neighing, MBh. 3, 11764.<BR> --Caus. To neigh, MBh. 3, 11764.<BR> --Cf. रस्; O.H.G. hros; A.S. hors; χρόμη, χρεμίζω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषा
ह्रेषा ह्रेष् + आ, f. Neighing as a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषुक|ह्रेषुकः
ह्रेषुक ह्रेषुक, MBh. 3, 8871, An instrument for digging with (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रौड्
ह्रौड् ह्रौड्, see हूड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लग्
ह्लग् ह्लग्, see ह्रग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लप्
† ह्लप् ह्लप्, ह्रप् ह्रप्, i. 10, Par. To speak (cf. क्लप् and लप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लस्
† ह्लस् ह्लस्, i. 1, Par. To sound (cf. ह्रस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद्
ह्लाद् ह्लाद्, i. 1, Ātm. To be glad or delighted, MBh. 1, 3036.<BR> --Caus. To delight, Rām. 2, 44, 10.<BR> --With आ आ, Caus. To delight, Nal. 21, 8.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To be delighted, Kir. 11, 8.<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. प्रह्लन्न, Pleased, glad.<BR> --Caus. To delight, Rām. 1, 9, 56; Pañc. ii. d. 63; Vikr. d. 149 (Ātm.). प्रह्लादित, Rejoiced.<BR> --Cf. κέχλαδα, καχλάζω; A.S. glaed, glad, gladian; O.H.G. glat, splendens (cf. ह्रा̆दिनी, ह्लादिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद|ह्लादः
ह्लाद ह्लाद् + अ, m. Pleasure, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिन्
ह्लादिन् ह्लादिन्, i. e. ह्लाद् + इन्, and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b " target="_blank">Page1126-b + 40</a>] ह्लाद + इन्,<BR> I. adj., f. नी.<BR> 1. Delighting, Ṛt. 6, 29.<BR> 2. Happy, glad.<BR> II. f. नी.<BR> 1. Lightning.<BR> 2. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीका
ह्लीका ह्लीका = ह्रीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीकु|ह्लीकुः
ह्लीकु ह्लीकु,<BR> I. (= ह्रीकु), adj. Bashful, modest.<BR> II. m.<BR> 1. Tin.<BR> 2. Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वल्
ह्वल् ह्वल् (cf. ह्वृ), i. 1, Par. To move, to shake, to tremble, Bhaṭṭ. 9, 8.<BR> --Caus. To cause to tremble, Bhaṭṭ. 6, 45.<BR> --With वि वि, To stagger, to be agitated, Rām. 2, 13, 4. विह्वलित, Staggering, Rām. 1, 9, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वान|ह्वानं
ह्वान ह्वान, i. e. ह्वे + अन, n. Cry.<BR> --Comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह्वान
कु- + ह्वान कु- + ह्वान, n. disagreeable cry, Bhāg. P. 1, 14, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृ
ह्वृ ह्वृ (originally ध्वृ, q. cf.), ह्वॄ ह्वॄ, i. 1, and ii. 9, ह्वृणा, णी, Par. To be crooked.<BR> --Cf. Lat. curvus, varus; κυρτός, κύρβεις; Goth. hvairban; A.S. hwearfian (Caus.), hwerfa, hweorfan; hwealf, hwealfa; ἐρέϕω.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वे
ह्वे ह्वे, i. 1, Par. Ātm. (in the Vedas also हू हू),<BR> 1. To call, Rām. 2, 34, 11; Chr. 289, 4 = Rigv. i. 49, 4 (अहूषत, ved. aor.); Chr. 288, 14 = Rigv. i. 48, 14 (जुहूरे, ved. red. pf.).<BR> 2. To name, Kumāras. 1, 26.<BR> 3. To invoke, MBh. 1, 4944.<BR> 4. To challenge, to vie with (with acc.), MBh. 3, 1823 (शशिनं ह्वयन्ती, Vying with the moon).<BR> --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. हूत, Summoned, invited.<BR> --Comp.<BR> --With आ आ,<BR> I. Par. (in epic poetry also Ātm., Rām. 2, 91, 12).<BR> 1. To call, Rām. 2, 58, 1.<BR> 2. To invoke, Rām. 2, 91, 12; Lass. 101, 3 = Rigv. vii. 16, 1 (आ हुवे, ved. pres.); Lass. 101, 7 = Rigv. vii. 16, 3 (आ जुह्वान, ptcple. pf. pass.).<BR> 3. To invite, Man. 3, 27. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1127-a " target="_blank">Page1127-a + 11</a>]<BR> 4. To convoke, Hit. 82, 16.<BR> II. Ātm.<BR> 1. To challenge, MBh. 2, 879; Chr. 26, 74 (आह्वयाम् आस, anomal. pf.), 37, 10 (आह्वयान, anomal. ptcple. pres.).<BR> 2. To emulate.<BR> --Caus. ह्वायय, To order to call, Rām. 2, 89, 3.<BR> --With उपा उप-आ, Ātm. To challenge, MBh. 2, 1785.<BR> --With समा सम्-आ,<BR> 1. To convoke, Pañc. 82, 6; Rām. 1, 8, 18.<BR> 2. To call, Pañc. 210, 10; MBh. 3, 8549.<BR> 3. To challenge, MBh. 2, 1518. समाहूत, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1127-b " target="_blank">Page1127-b + 11</a>] Convoked, Daśak. in Chr. 191, 19.<BR> --With नि नि, To call down (from heaven), Chr. 298, 24 = Rigv. i. 112, 24.<BR> --With प्र प्र, To call, Utt. Rāmac. 146, 2.<BR> --Cf. O.H.G. hweion; Goth. vôpjan (probably the regular Caus.); A.S. hweóp (cry, called out), and wepan; probably also cygan (3. conj., cl. जुहू); βοή, βοάω, probably ἀΰω and ἰωή; Lat. re-boare, and perhaps vovere, vōtum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूत|पुरुहूतः
पुरु- + हूत पुरु- + हूत, adj. invoked by many, or much invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BEN&page=1126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ben" target="_blank">Correction</a>

